मोढ
मोढ मोढ, अस्, m., N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोढक
मोढक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोण|मोणः
मोण मोण, अस्, m. dried fruit; a kind of<BR>fly (= नक्र-मक्षिका); a basket in which snakes<BR>are carried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोणक
मोणक, a word used to explain डिम्बिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोतीराम
मोतीराम मोतीराम, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kānada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोद|मोदः
मोद मोद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मुद्), pleasure,<BR>delight, gladness, joyousness, joyfulness; fragrance,<BR>perfume [cf. आ-मोद]; N. of a Muni; (आ), f. =<BR>अज-मोदा, q. v.<BR>—मोद-कर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Muni.<BR>—मोद-मोदिनी, f. ‘delighting by fragrance,’<BR>Eugenia Jambolana (= जम्बु).<BR>—मोदाख्य (˚द-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, m. the mango tree.<BR>—मोदा-गिरि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a country.<BR>—मोदाढ्या (˚द-आढ्˚), f.<BR>= अज-मोदा, q. v.<BR>—मोदा-पुर, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदक|मोदकः
मोदक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, delighting, rejoicing,<BR>pleasing, gladdening, exhilarating, causing happiness<BR>or delight; glad, cheerful; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a small<BR>round sweetmeat or a sweetmeat in general; (in<BR>medicine) a sort of pill; (अस्), m. a particular mixed<BR>caste (the son of a Kṣatriya by a Śūdra mother);<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of metre, four times ¯˘˘¯˘˘¯<BR>˘˘¯˘˘¯; (ई), f., N. of a particular mythical club<BR>or weapon.<BR>—मोदक-कार, अस्, m. a sweetmeat-<BR>maker, confectioner.<BR>—मोदक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>composed of sweetmeats.<BR>—मोदक-शराव, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a dish of sweetmeats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदकिका
मोदकिका, f. (at the end of a comp. after nu-<BR>merals), a sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदन|मोदनं
मोदन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Caus.), giving joy,<BR>gratifying, gladdening, delighting, (generally at the<BR>end of a comp., e. g. क्रव्याद-गण-मोदन,<BR>giving joy to numbers of beasts of prey, Mahā-bh.<BR>Droṇa-p. 1576); (अम्), n. the act of pleasing or<BR>affording pleasure; joy, pleasure; = उच्छिष्ट-मो-<BR>दन, wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदनीय
मोदनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be rejoiced at, to be<BR>delighted in, delightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदमान
मोदमान, अस्, आ, अम्, rejoicing, being glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदयत्
मोदयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, rejoicing, delighting;<BR>(अन्ती), f. a sort of wild lovage, Ptychotis Ajowan;<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदयन्तिका|मोदयंतिका
मोदयन्तिका, f. = मोदयन्ती, Ptychotis Ajowan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदाकिन्
मोदाकिन्, ई, m. (probably) N. of a hill (Mahā-bh.<BR>Bhīṣma-p. 427).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदायनि
मोदायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Moda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदित|मोदितः
मोदित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, gratified, delighted;<BR>(अम्), n. pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदिन्
मोदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, rejoicing, glad, pleased, cheerful,<BR>merry, happy; making glad, gladdening, gratifying,<BR>delighting, (often at the end of comps., cf. गीत-म्˚);<BR>(इनी), f., N. of various plants (= अज-मोदा, मल्-<BR>लिका, यूथिका, वृत्त-मल्लिका); musk; an intoxi-<BR>cating beverage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदोष
मोदोष, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोमुघ
मोमुघ मोमुघ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of<BR>rt. 1. मुह्), very much perplexed, greatly embar-<BR>rassed; mad, insane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरट|मोरटं|मोरटः
मोरट मोरट, अस्, m. a species of plant<BR>with sweet juice (= क्षीर-मोरट); the milk of a<BR>cow recently calved, biestings, (according to lexico-<BR>graphers, अम्, n.); (आ), f. = मूर्वा, hemp used for<BR>bow-strings, Sanseviera Roxburghiana; (अम्), n. the<BR>root of the sugar-cane; the flower of Alangium<BR>Hexapetalum; the root of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरटक|मोरटकं
मोरटक, अम्, n. the root of the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोराक
मोराक मोराक, अस्, m., N. of king Pravara-<BR>sena's minister (founder of the temple called after<BR>him मोराक-भवन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरिका
मोरिका मोरिका, f., N. of a female poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरी
मोरी, N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोर्वणीकर
मोर्वणीकर मोर्वणी-कर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोष|मोषः
मोष मोष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मुष्), a<BR>robber, thief, plunderer; robbery, theft, stealing;<BR>plundering, sacking, (नगर-मोष, plundering a<BR>city); anything robbed or stolen, stolen property.<BR>—मोष-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, one who practises theft, a<BR>thief.<BR>—मोषाभिदर्शन (˚ष-अभ्˚), अम्, n.<BR>seeing or witnessing a robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषक|मोषकः
मोषक, अस्, m. a thief, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषण|मोषणं
मोषण, अस्, ई, अम्, robbing, plundering, carry-<BR>ing off; (अम्), n. the act of robbing, plundering,<BR>stealing, defrauding, embezzling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषयित्नु|मोषयित्नुः
मोषयित्नु, उस्, m. (fr. the Caus.), a Brāhman;<BR>the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषा
मोषा, f. robbery, theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोष्टृ
मोष्टृ, टा, m. a robber, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोह|मोहं|मोहः
मोह मोह, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. मुह्), uncon-<BR>sciousness, loss of consciousness, fainting, a swoon;<BR>delusion, bewilderment, perplexity, distraction,<BR>phrenzy; weakness of intellect, ignorance, folly,<BR>foolishness, infatuation; error, mistake, going astray;<BR>pain, affliction; wonder, amazement, astonishment;<BR>Infatuation (personified as the offspring of Brahmā);<BR>(in phil.) darkness or delusion of mind preventing<BR>the discernment of truth (leading men to believe in<BR>the reality of worldly objects and to addict themselves<BR>to mundane or sensual enjoyment); a magical art<BR>employed to bewilder an enemy (= मोहन); मो-<BR>हात्, ind. through ignorance, from folly or infatuation.<BR>—मोह-कलिल, अम्, n. a thicket or snare of illu-<BR>sion.<BR>—मोह-चूडोत्तर (˚ड-उत्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—मोह-जाल, अम्, n. the net of delusion,<BR>the snare or fetters of illusory objects, the fascination<BR>of the world.<BR>—मोह-निद्रा, f. ‘sleep of infatua-<BR>tion,’ thoughtless assurance, overweening confidence.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">Page0798-c+ 79</a>]<BR>—मोह-पाश, अस्, m. the snare of (wordly) illu-<BR>sion.<BR>—मोह-मन्त्र, अस्, m. an infatuating spell,<BR>deluding charm.<BR>—मोह-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consist-<BR>ing of infatuation, leading to delusion, perplexing.<BR>—मोह-मुद्गर, अस्, m. ‘hammer of ignorance<BR>or infatuation,’ N. of a metrical exposition of the<BR>Vedānta philosophy; of another work.<BR>—मोह-<BR>रात्रि, इस्, f. ‘night of bewilderment,’ the night when<BR>the world is to be destroyed.<BR>—मोह-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, possessed of infatuation, infatuated, foolish, igno-<BR>rant.<BR>—मोह-शास्त्र, अम्, n. erroneous or false<BR>teaching, false doctrine.<BR>—मोह-शूलोत्तर (˚ल-उत्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—मोहोपमा (˚ह-उप्˚), f.<BR>‘error-comparison,’ a rhetorical figure in which there<BR>is a confusion of the subject and object of a comparison<BR>(e. g. ‘regarding thy face, O dear one, as the moon,<BR>I run after the moon as if it were thy face’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहक
मोहक, अस्, इका, अम्, bewildering, confusing,<BR>infatuating, causing ignorance or folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहन|मोहनं|मोहनः
मोहन, अस्, ई, अम्, stupefying, depriving of con-<BR>sciousness or sensation, bewildering, perplexing,<BR>puzzling, confusing, deceiving, deluding, leading<BR>astray, infatuating, fascinating; (अस्), m. the thorn-<BR>apple; epithet of Śiva; N. of one of the five arrows<BR>of Kāma-deva, the god of love; (आ), f. the flower<BR>of a sort of jasmine; a sort of grass, Trigonella Cor-<BR>niculata; (ई), f. Basella Cordifolia; a term for a<BR>particular magical formula or incantation; N. of a<BR>female demon (daughter of Garbha-hantṛ); of an<BR>Apsaras; (अम्), n. the act of stupefying, bewildering,<BR>perplexing, deluding, puzzling, deceiving, fascinating;<BR>stupor, loss of sensation, unconsciousness, the being<BR>deluded or infatuated, delusion, infatuation, decep-<BR>tion, embarrassment, mistake; temptation, seduction;<BR>sexual intercourse; a magical charm or incantation<BR>used to bewilder an enemy; the formula used in<BR>that process (especially certain magical hymns of<BR>the Atharva-veda); any means employed for per-<BR>plexing or deluding others; N. of a town.<BR>—मो-<BR>हन-चन्द, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मोहन-दास<BR>or मोहन-दास-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of a commentary on the Mahā-nāṭaka or Hanūman-<BR>nāṭaka.<BR>—मोहन-प्रकृति, इस्, m., N. of a pupil<BR>of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—मोहन-भोग, अस्, m. a parti-<BR>cular kind of sweetmeat.<BR>—मोहन-लता, f. a plant<BR>which has the power of fascinating.<BR>—मोहन-वल्-<BR>लिका or मोहन-वल्ली, f. a species of plant.<BR>—मो-<BR>हनास्त्र (˚न-अस्˚), अम्, n. a weapon charmed to<BR>fascinate or bewitch the person against whom it is<BR>directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनक|मोहनकः
मोहनक, अस्, m. an epithet of the month<BR>Caitra, (also written मोहनिक); (इका), f. a<BR>species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनीय
मोहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to delusion, de-<BR>pending on illusion or error, resulting from infatua-<BR>tion, producing delusion; perplexing, puzzling, con-<BR>fusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहयत्
मोहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. the Caus.) stupefying,<BR>bewildering, depriving of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहयितृ
मोहयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who perplexes or<BR>deludes, a perplexer, infatuator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहित
मोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied, perplexed, bewil-<BR>dered, infatuated, deluded, beguiled, fascinated, (often<BR>in comps., e. g. काम-मोहित, infatuated by love.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिन्
मोहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, stupefying, confusing, puzzling,<BR>perplexing, illusive, fallacious, beguiling, alluring,<BR>fascinating; (इनी), f. a fascinating woman; N. of an<BR>Apsaras; the flower of a species of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहुक
मोहुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being deluded, falling<BR>into error or confusion, going astray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक
मौक मौक, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Mūka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकलि|मौकलिः
मौकलि मौकलि or मौकुलि, इस्, m. a crow,<BR>raven; [cf. मौद्गलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकुन्द
मौकुन्द मौकुन्द, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>Mukunda, i. e. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिक|मौक्तिकं
मौक्तिक मौक्तिक, अम्, n. (fr. मुक्ता), a<BR>pearl (properly ‘a collection of pearls’).<BR>—मौक्तिक-<BR>गुम्फिका, f. a female stringer of pearls.<BR>—मौक्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">Page0799-a+ 76</a>]<BR>तिक-तण्डुल, अस्, m. a kind of white Yāvanāla.<BR>—मौक्तिक-दामन्, अ, n. a string of pearls; a<BR>kind of metre, four times ˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘.<BR>—मौक्तिक-प्रसवा, f. a pearl muscle; [cf.<BR>मुक्ता-प्रसू.]<BR>—मौक्तिक-मारण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a subject treated of in the Dhātu-ratna-mālā.<BR>—मौक्तिक-माला, f. an ornament of pearls, a pearl<BR>necklace; a species of metre, four times ¯˘˘¯¯, ˘˘<BR>˘˘¯¯.<BR>—मौक्तिक-रत्न, अम्, n. a pearl gem,<BR>pearl; [cf. मुक्ता-रत्न.]<BR>—मौक्तिकरत्न-ता, f.<BR>the state or condition of a pearl.<BR>—मौक्तिक-शुक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. a pearl oyster; [cf. मुक्ता-शुक्ति.]<BR>—मौक्तिक-<BR>सर, अस्, m. a string of pearls.<BR>—मौक्तिकाभ<BR>(˚क-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, resembling pearls.<BR>—मौक्-<BR>तिकावली (˚क-आव्˚), f. a string of pearls; [cf. मुक्-<BR>तावली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्य|मौक्यं
मौक्य मौक्य, अम्, n. (fr. मूक), the state<BR>of being dumb, dumbness, speechlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्ष
मौक्ष मौक्ष, अम्, n. (fr. मोक्ष), N. of<BR>a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्षिक
मौक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (in astronomy) relating to<BR>the release of a planet (from an eclipse), relating to<BR>the end of an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौख|मौखं
मौख मौख, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मुख), relat-<BR>ing or belonging to the mouth or face, frontal; (अम्),<BR>n. a fault or defect connected with the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखिक|मौखिकं
मौखिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = मौख above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौख्य|मौख्यं
मौख्य, अम्, n. precedence, pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखर
मौखर मौखर (fr. मुखर), epithet of<BR>a family or race (‘talkative?’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखरि|मौखरिः
मौखरि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखरी
मौखरी, f. = मौखर्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखर्य|मौखर्यं|मौखर्य्य|मौखर्य्यं
मौखर्य, अम्, n. talkativeness, garrulity, lo-<BR>quaciousness; scurrility, defamation, abusiveness,<BR>abuse, calumny, vilification; (आ), the feminine form<BR>of Maukhari above, (according to Scholiast on Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 79.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौग्ध्य|मौग्ध्यं
मौग्ध्य मौग्ध्य, अम्, n. (fr. मुग्ध),<BR>simplicity, innocence, inexperience, silliness; a femi-<BR>nine grace (asking a lover to tell what is already<BR>known); charm, beauty; (also incorrectly written<BR>मौग्ध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौघ्य|मौघ्यं
मौघ्य मौघ्य, अम्, n. (fr. मोघ), vain-<BR>ness, uselessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौच|मौचं
मौच मौच, अम्, n. (fr. मोच), the fruit of<BR>the banana or plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौजवत
मौजवत मौजवत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मूज-वत्),<BR>Ved. coming from or produced on the mountain<BR>Mūja-vat; (अस्), m. a patronymic of Akṣa (author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 34; also read मौजवत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्ज|मौंज
मौञ्ज मौञ्ज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मुञ्ज), made<BR>of Muñja grass or its fibres; resembling Muñja grass;<BR>(अस्), m. a blade of Muñja grass; (ई), f., scil. मे-<BR>खला, a Brāhman's girdle or cord made of a triple<BR>string of Muñja grass; any girdle.<BR>—मौञ्जी-तृणा-<BR>ख्य (˚ण-आख्˚), अस्, m. Muñja grass.<BR>—मौञ्जी-<BR>धर, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing or carrying Muñja grass.<BR>—मौञ्जी-निबन्धन, अम्, n. the binding on of<BR>the girdle of Muñja grass, ligation of the sacrificial<BR>cord (Manu II. 27).<BR>—मौञ्जी-पत्त्रा, f. Eleusine<BR>Indica.<BR>—मौञ्जी-बन्धन, अम्, n. the ligation or<BR>binding on of the Muñja grass girdle, investiture<BR>with the sacred thread, (in Manu 11. 169. shortened<BR>on account of the metre to मौञ्जि-बन्धन.)<BR>—मौञ्जीबन्धन-चिह्नित, अस्, आ, अम्, distin-<BR>guished by the ligation of the Muñja zone (Manu<BR>II. 170).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जक
मौञ्जक, अस्, m. a blade of Muñja grass; (also<BR>read मुञ्जक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जकायन
मौञ्जकायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जवत
मौञ्जवत, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. coming from the<BR>mountain Muñja-vat; (also read मौजवत, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जायन
मौञ्जायन, अस्, m. (fr. मुञ्ज), a patronymic;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a warlike family; (ई), f. a princess<BR>of the Mauñjāyanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जायनीय
मौञ्जायनीय, अस्, m. a king of the Mauñjāyanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जिन्
मौञ्जिन्, ई, इनी, इ, girt with or wearing a girdle<BR>of Muñja grass, (नाग-मौञ्जिन्, wearing a snake<BR>for a girdle.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जीय
मौञ्जीय, अस्, आ, अम्, made of Muñja grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौढ्य|मौढ्यं
मौढ्य मौढ्य, अस्, m. (fr. मूढ), a patro-<BR>nymic; (अम्), n. stupidity, want of understanding,<BR>folly, fatuity, ignorance, simplicity; spiritual folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौण्डिनिकाय
मौण्डिनिकाय मौण्डि-निकाय, अस्, m. (मौण्डि<BR>fr. मुण्ड), a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौण्ड्य|मौंड्यं
मौण्ड्य मौण्ड्य, अम्, n. (fr. मुण्ड),<BR>shaving of the head, the having the head shaved,<BR>tonsure; baldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौत्र|मौत्रं
मौत्र मौत्र, अम्, n. (fr. मूत्र), a quantity<BR>of urine, chamber-lye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद
मौद मौद, आस्, m. pl. (probably fr. मोद),<BR>N. of a school; (अस्), m. a pupil of this school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदहायन
मौदहायन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदक
मौदक मौदक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मोदक),<BR>relating to sweetmeats; dealing or trading in sweet-<BR>meats; (अम्), n. a particular version of a sacred text<BR>by Mauda, (in this sense connected with मौद<BR>above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदकिक|मौदकिकः
मौदकिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मोदक), consisting<BR>or composed of sweetmeats; (अस्), m. a seller of<BR>sweetmeats, confectioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदनिक
मौदनिक (fr. मोदन), see Gaṇa Kāśyādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदनेयक
मौदनेयक, see Gaṇa Kattryādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदमानिक
मौदमानिक (fr. मोदमान), see Gaṇa Kāś-<BR>yādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदाकिन्
मौदाकिन्, a various reading for मोदाकिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्ग
मौद्ग मौद्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मुद्ग), relating<BR>to a bean; (अस्), m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गिक
मौद्गिक, अस्, ई, अम्, purchased with beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गीन|मौद्गीनं
मौद्गीन, अस्, ई, अम्, sown with beans, fit for<BR>being sown with kidney-beans, bearing beans (said<BR>of a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गलि|मौद्गलिः
मौद्गलि मौद्गलि, इस्, m. (fr. मुद्गल), a<BR>crow [cf. मौकलि].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गल्य|मौद्गल्यः
मौद्गल्य, descended or sprung from Mudgala;<BR>(अस्), m. a proper N.; patronymic of Nāka; of<BR>Śata-balākṣa; of Lāṅgalāyana; a particular mixed<BR>caste; मौद्गलास्, m. pl., see Gaṇa Kaṇvādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 2, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गल्यायन
मौद्गल्यायन, अस्, m. (patronymic fr. मौद्-<BR>गल्य), N. of a pupil of Śākya-muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गल्यीय
मौद्गल्यीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Maudgalya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गिक
मौद्गिक मौद्गिक, मौद्गीन. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौन|मौनं
मौन मौन, अस्, m. (fr. मुनि), a patro-<BR>nymic; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a dynasty; (ई), f., N.<BR>of the fifteenth day in the dark half of the month<BR>Phālguna, when a ceremony of bathing in silence is<BR>performed; (अम्), n. the office or position of a<BR>Muni or holy sage; silence, taciturnity.<BR>—मौन-<BR>भट्ट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मौन-मन्त्राव-<BR>बोध (˚र-अव्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work by Sundara-<BR>śukla.<BR>—मौन-मुद्रा, f. the Mudrā or attitude<BR>of silence.<BR>—मौन-व्रत, अम्, n. a vow of silence;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), observing a vow of silence, holding<BR>one's tongue; [cf. मुनि-व्रत.]<BR>—मौनव्रत-<BR>धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or मौन-व्रतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ob-<BR>serving a vow of silence.<BR>—मौन-सम्मति, इस्, f.<BR>silent assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिक
मौनिक, अस्, ई, अम्, resembling a Muni or<BR>inspired sage, like a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिचिति
मौनिचिति (fr. मुनि-चित), see Gaṇa Sutaṅga-<BR>mādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिन्
मौनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, silent, observing silence, taci-<BR>turn, reserved, not speaking; (ई), m. = मुनि, an<BR>ascetic, hermit, holy sage, one who has overcome his<BR>passions and retired from the world; (sometimes at<BR>the end of proper names, e. g. गोपीनाथ-म्˚, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">Page0799-c+ 77</a>]<BR>Muni Gopīnātha.)<BR>—मौनि-त्व, अम्, n. silence,<BR>taciturnity, reticence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिस्थलिक
मौनिस्थलिक (fr. मुनि-स्थल), see Gaṇa<BR>Kumudādi 2. to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनेय|मौनेयः
मौनेय, आस्, m. pl. (fr. मुनि), N. of a school;<BR>(आस्), m. f. pl. epithet of a class of Gandharvas and<BR>Apsarasas; (अम्), n. the position or office of a<BR>Muni (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौन्द
मौन्द मौन्द, अस्, m. a proper N.; (also<BR>read मौद्ग, मोद.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौरजिक|मौरजिकः
मौरजिक मौरजिक, अस्, m. (fr. मुरज), a<BR>drum-beater, drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौरव
मौरव मौरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मुरु), coming<BR>from or relating to the Daitya Muru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्व
1. मौर्व, अस्, ई, अम्, made from the iron called<BR>मुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्ख्य|मौर्ख्यं
मौर्ख्य मौर्ख्य, अम्, n. (fr. मूर्ख), stu-<BR>pidity, folly, fatuity, (sometimes less correctly read<BR>मौर्ख.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्य|मौर्यः
मौर्य मौर्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Mura; a metronymic from Murā; N. of a dynasty<BR>beginning with Candra-gupta.<BR>—मौर्य-दत्त, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—मौर्य-पुत्र, अस्, m. (with<BR>Jainas), N. of one of the eleven Gaṇādhipas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्व
मौर्व 2. मौर्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मूर्वा), made<BR>of the Sanseviera Roxburghiana, coming from or<BR>relating to मूर्वा or bow-string hemp; (ई), f. a<BR>string or girdle made of मूर्वा, the string of inves-<BR>titure for a Kṣatriya (Manu II. 42); a bow-string;<BR>(in geometry) the chord of an arc.<BR>—मौर्वी-मेख-<BR>लिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing a girdle made of मूर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्विका
मौर्विका, f. (in geometry) the chord of an arc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्वीक
मौर्वीक (at the end of an adj. comp.) = मौर्वी,<BR>a bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल|मौलः
मौल मौल, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, (fr. मूल), pro-<BR>ceeding from a root, radical, original; handed down<BR>from antiquity (as an old custom, &c.); ancient, of<BR>old standing; living from olden times or for genera-<BR>tions in any country, indigenous; of pure or good<BR>extraction, nobly born, of a good family; holding<BR>an office from ancient times, brought up in a king's<BR>service for generations, (मौलो मन्त्री or मौलः<BR>सचिवः, an old minister, one born in the country or<BR>one whose forefathers have held the same office, see<BR>Manu VII. 54, where, according to Kullūka, मौलः<BR>= पितृ-पितामह-क्रमेण सेवकः); hereditary,<BR>(मौलः पार्थिवः, an hereditary prince.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलभारिक
मौलभारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मूल-भार), car-<BR>rying a load of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलि|मौलिः
मौलि, इस्, m. (probably fr. मूल), the head, the<BR>top of anything; the plant Jonesia Asoka; a patro-<BR>nymic; (अयस्), m. pl., N. of a tribe; (इस्), m. f. a<BR>diadem [cf. मुकुट], crown, crest; a tuft or lock<BR>of hair left on the crown of the head after tonsure,<BR>a top-knot (= चूडा); hair ornamented and braided<BR>round the head, = धम्मिल; (इस्), f. the earth, (in<BR>this sense according to some मौली, f.)<BR>—मौलि-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. f. a crest gem, jewel worn in a diadem.<BR>—मौलि-मण्डन, अम्, n. an ornament for the<BR>head.<BR>—मौलि-माला or मौलि-मालिका, f. a wreath<BR>or crown worn on the head.<BR>—मौलि-मालिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, having a wreath or crown on the top of the head;<BR>उदयाचल-मौलिमालिन्, having the eastern moun-<BR>tain for its crest (said of the sun).<BR>—मौलि-मुकुट,<BR>अम्, n. a diadem for the head, tiara; [cf. मुकुट.]<BR>—मौलि-रत्न, अम्, n. a crest jewel, crown jewel,<BR>head jewel.<BR>—मौल्य्-आभरण, अम्, n. a head<BR>ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिक|मौलिकः
मौलिक, अस्, ई, अम्, producing roots, &c.; coming<BR>from or belonging to the root, radical, original [cf.<BR>मूलिक]; chief, principal, being of low origin, (op-<BR>posed to कुलीन); inferior; (अस्), m. a digger of roots,<BR>a dealer in roots; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिक्य
मौलिक्य, अम्, n. an abstract noun from मूलिक,<BR>see Gaṇa Purohitādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिन्
मौलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a diadem or crown,<BR>diademed, crested; having at the top, (sometimes at<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">Page0800-a+ 75</a>]<BR>the end of a comp., e. g. चक्र-मौली शकटः, a<BR>cart having the wheels uppermost.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0799-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलेय
मौलेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल्य|मौल्यं
मौल्य, अस्, -ली, अम्, being at the root; (अम्),<BR>n. price, (for मूल्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलि|मौलिः
मौलि मौलि. See p. 799, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौशल
मौशल मौशल, मौषल, &c., incorrectly<BR>for मौसल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौषिकि
मौषिकि मौषिकि, इस्, m. a metronymic<BR>from Mūṣikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौषिकीपुत्र
मौषिकी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टा
मौष्टा मौष्टा, f. (fr. मुष्टि), a combat with<BR>fists, boxing match, sparring, playing at fisticuffs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टिक|मौष्टिकः
मौष्टिक, अस्, m. a cheat, impostor, rogue,<BR>sharper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौसल|मौसलः
मौसल मौसल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मुसल),<BR>club-shaped, club-formed; relating to the battle with<BR>clubs, (मौसलम् पर्व = मौसल-पर्वन् be-<BR>low); fought with clubs (as a battle); an epithet of<BR>a Madhu-parka (composed of ghee and spirituous<BR>liquor); (आस्), m. pl. of मौसल्य below.<BR>—मौ-<BR>सल-पर्वन्, अ, n. ‘Musala-section,’ N. of the six-<BR>teenth book of the Mahā-bhārata (in which is de-<BR>scribed the death of Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma and the<BR>self-destruction of Kṛṣṇa's family through the curse<BR>of some Brāhmans; it is narrated that in consequence<BR>of this curse, the Andhakas and Yādavas indulged<BR>in intoxicating liquors which led to a general quarrel<BR>in which the infuriated relatives, having no weapons,<BR>plucked the rushes [एरका], and with these, turned<BR>to clubs by the working of the curse, slaughtered<BR>each other).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौसल्य
मौसल्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Musala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौसुल
मौसुल मौसुल, अस्, m. a Moslim, Mussul-<BR>mān, Muhammedan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्त|मौहूर्तः|मौहूर्त्त|मौहूर्त्तः
मौहूर्त मौहूर्त, अस्, m. (fr. मुहूर्त), an<BR>astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्तिक|मौहूर्तिकः|मौहूर्त्तिक|मौहूर्त्तिकः
मौहूर्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, lasting for a moment or<BR>instant, momentary; relating to a particular time;<BR>(अस्), m. an astrologer; N. of a class of celestial<BR>beings (children of Muhūrtā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्न
म्न म्न in चर्म-म्न, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्ना
म्ना म्ना (connected with rt. मन्, with<BR>which म्ना was originally identical), cl. 1.<BR>P. मनति, मम्नौ, म्नास्यति, अम्नासीत्, म्ना-<BR>यात् or म्नेयात्, म्नातुम्, to bind or fix in the<BR>mind, repeat over in the mind, fix in the memory<BR>by frequent repetition, repeat; to study or learn<BR>diligently; to remember; to celebrate, praise (Ved.):<BR>Pass. म्नायते: Caus. म्नापयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अमिम्नपत्: Desid. मिम्नासति: Intens. माम्ना-<BR>यते, माम्नाति, माम्नेति; [for comparisons see<BR>under rt. मन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्नात
म्नात, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed in the mind, repeated,<BR>learnt, remembered; [cf. आ-म्˚, समा-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्यक्ष्
म्यक्ष् म्यक्ष् (a Vedic verb, of which the<BR>following forms are found, म्यक्षति, मिम्यक्ष,<BR>मिमिक्षतुस्, मिमिक्षुस्, मिमिक्षिरे, अम्यक्,<BR>मिमिक्षत्), to be fixed in or on; to be in any<BR>place or state; to be near, to be present, to be at<BR>hand; to go to, reach; to be associated or united;<BR>(Sāy. = प्राप्नोति, सङ्गच्छते, संहतो भ-<BR>वति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष्
म्रक्ष् म्रक्ष् or मृक्ष् (connected with<BR>rts. 1. मृज्, मक्ष्), cl. 1. P. म्रक्-<BR>षति, मृक्षति, &c., to accumulate, collect, as-<BR>semble; to rub; cl. 10. P. म्रक्षयति, मृक्ष-<BR>यति, &c., to accumulate, collect; to combine, mix;<BR>to rub, smear, anoint; to speak indistinctly or incor-<BR>rectly; (according to some) to divide, cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष|म्रक्षः
म्रक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbing, destroying, (in<BR>तुवि-म्˚, q. v.); (अस्), m. concealment of one's vices<BR>or failings, hypocrisy, slyness.<BR>—म्रक्ष-कृत्वन्,<BR>आ, अरी, अ, Ved. rubbing to pieces, destroying (said of<BR>Indra; Sāy. = वध-कर्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्षण|म्रक्षणं
म्रक्षण, अम्, n. the act of rubbing in or on,<BR>anointing, smearing the body with unguents; any-<BR>thing to be rubbed on, ointment, oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रद्
म्रद् म्रद् (another form of rt. 1. मृद्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. A. म्रदते, मम्रदे, म्र-<BR>दितुम्, to rub; to grind, pound, reduce to powder;<BR>to tread or trample on: Caus. म्रदयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अमम्रदत्: Desid. मिम्रदिषते: Intens.<BR>माम्रद्यते, माम्रत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रद
म्रद, म्रदस्, in ऊर्ण-म्रद, ऊर्ण-म्र-<BR>दस्, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदय
म्रदय म्रदय (fr. मृदु), Nom. P. म्र-<BR>दयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to make soft or smooth; to<BR>polish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिमन्
म्रदिमन्, आ, m. softness, tenderness, mildness,<BR>gentleness.<BR>—म्रदिमान्वित (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>endowed with softness, soft, mild, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिष्ठ|म्रदिष्ठः
म्रदिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of मृदु), very<BR>soft, exceedingly mild, softest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदीयस्
म्रदीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of मृदु),<BR>softer, milder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रातन|म्रातनं
म्रातन म्रातन, अम्, n. Cyperus Rotundus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रित्
म्रित् म्रित् [cf. rt. मृ], cl. 4. P. म्रित्यति,<BR>Ved. to decay, moulder away, be dissolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रियमाण
म्रियमाण म्रियमाण. See p. 790, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुच्
म्रुच् म्रुच् [cf. rts. म्रुञ्च्, म्लुच्], cl. 1.<BR>P. म्रोचति, Aor. अम्रुचत् or अम्रोचीत्,<BR>&c., to go, move: Desid. मुम्रुचिषति, मुम्रो-<BR>चिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रोक
म्रोक, अस्, m., N. of a destructive Agni (men-<BR>tioned in Atharva-veda V. 31, 9); of a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुञ्च्|म्रुंच्
म्रुञ्च् म्रुञ्च्, cl. 1. P. म्रुञ्चति, &c., =<BR>rt. म्रुच् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेट्
म्रेट् म्रेट् or म्रेड् (= rts. मेट्, म्लेट्), cl.<BR>1. P. म्रेटति, म्रेडति, to be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लक्त|म्लक्तं
म्लक्त म्लक्त (?), अस्, आ, अम्, stolen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लक्ष्
म्लक्ष् म्लक्ष्, cl. 10. P. म्लक्षयति,<BR>to cut, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लात
म्लात म्लात, म्लान, म्लायिन्, म्लास्नु. See<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लिष्ट|म्लिष्टं|म्लिष्टः
म्लिष्ट म्लिष्ट, &c. See under rt. म्लेछ्<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुच्
म्लुच् म्लुच् [cf. rt. म्रुच्], cl. 1. P.<BR>म्लोचति, Aor. अम्लुचत् or अम्लोचीत्,<BR>&c., to go; to go down: Desid. मुम्लुचिषति,<BR>मुम्लोचिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुक्त
म्लुक्त in अप-म्लुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. retired,<BR>withdrawn, concealed, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुञ्च्|म्लुंच्
म्लुञ्च् म्लुञ्च्, cl. 1. P. म्लुञ्चति, &c.,<BR>= rt. म्लुच् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुप्
म्लुप् म्लुप्, another form of rt. म्लुच्<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुप्त
म्लुप्त in उप-म्लुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, retired, with-<BR>drawn, concealed, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेछ्|म्लेच्छ्
म्लेछ् म्लेछ्, cl. 1. P. म्लेच्छति, मिम्लेच्-<BR>छ, म्लेच्छितुम्, cl. 10. P. म्लेच्छ-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to speak confusedly or barbarously;<BR>to talk an unintelligible or foreign language, to speak<BR>a provincial or barbarous dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लिष्ट|म्लिष्टं|म्लिष्टः
म्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. Pāṇ. VII. 2, 18], spoken<BR>barbarously or indistinctly, indistinct (as speech),<BR>foreign, barbarous; = म्लान, withered, faded, faint;<BR>(अम्), n. indistinct speech, a foreign language.<BR>—म्लिष्टोक्ति (˚ट-उक्˚), इस्, f. indistinct or bar-<BR>barous speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ|म्लेच्छं|म्लेच्छः|म्लेछ
म्लेच्छ, अस्, m. a foreigner, barbarian, non-Arian,<BR>man of an outcast race, (a generic term for a person<BR>speaking any language but Sanskrit and not conform-<BR>ing to the usual Hindū institutions); a wicked or<BR>bad man, sinner; foreign or barbarous speech, igno-<BR>rance of the language of the country; (अम्), n. copper.<BR>—म्लेच्छ-कन्द, अस्, m. ‘foreign-root,’ Allium<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">Page0800-c+ 79</a>]<BR>Ascalonicum, garlic.<BR>—म्लेच्छ-जाति, इस्, m. a man<BR>belonging to one of the Mleccha or barbarian races,<BR>a barbarian, savage, mountaineer (as a Kirāta, Śa-<BR>vara, Pulinda).<BR>—म्लेच्छ-देश, अस्, m. a foreign<BR>or barbarous country, any country inhabited by<BR>people of a language and institutions different from<BR>the Hindūs.<BR>—म्लेच्छ-निवह, अस्, m. a host or<BR>swarm of barbarians.<BR>—म्लेच्छ-भाषा, f. a foreign<BR>or barbarous language.<BR>—म्लेच्छ-भोजन, अस्, m.<BR>‘food of foreigners or barbarians,’ wheat; (अम्), n.<BR>= यावक, half-ripe barley.<BR>—म्लेच्छ-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. the country of the Mlecchas or barbarians.<BR>—म्लेच्छ-मुख, अम्, n. ‘foreign countenance,’<BR>copper (see म्लेच्छास्य).<BR>—म्लेच्छ-वाच्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>speaking a barbarous or foreign language, speaking<BR>the language of the Mlecchas, (opposed to आर्य-वाच्,<BR>speaking the language of the Āryas, Manu X. 45.)<BR>—म्लेच्छाख्य (˚छ-आख्˚), अम्, n. ‘called Mlec-<BR>cha,’ copper.<BR>—म्लेच्छाश (˚छ-आश˚), अस्, m. ‘food<BR>of barbarians,’ wheat; [cf. म्लेच्छ-भोजन.]<BR>—म्लेच्छास्य (˚छ-आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘barbarian-face,’<BR>copper, (so named because the complexion of the<BR>Greek and Muhammedan invaders of India was sup-<BR>posed to be copper-coloured; cf. म्लेच्छाख्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छन|म्लेच्छनं
म्लेच्छन, अम्, n. the act of speaking unintel-<BR>ligibly or confusedly; speaking in a foreign or bar-<BR>barous tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छित|म्लेच्छितं
म्लेच्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken barbarously or un-<BR>intelligibly, foreign, barbarian; (अम्), n. a foreign<BR>tongue, ungrammatical speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छितक|म्लेच्छितकं
म्लेच्छितक, अम्, n. the speaking in a language<BR>unintelligible to others, foreign speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेट्
म्लेट् म्लेट् or म्लेड् (= rt. म्रेट्), cl. 1.<BR>P. म्लेटति, म्लेडति, &c., to be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेव्
म्लेव् म्लेव् [cf. rt. मेव्], cl. 1. A. म्ले-<BR>वते, &c., to serve, worship, gratify by<BR>service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लै
म्लै म्लै, cl. 1. P. म्लायति (ep. also A.<BR>म्लायते, and cl. 2. P. म्लाति, म्लान्ति),<BR>मम्लौ (मम्ले), म्लास्यति, अम्लासीत्, म्लायात् or<BR>म्लेयात्, म्लातुम्, to wither, fade, decay; to be<BR>faint or languid, grow weary, languish; to become<BR>weak or feeble; to become thin or emaciated; to<BR>be dispirited or downcast; to be sad: Caus. म्लाप-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to wither or fade; to enfeeble,<BR>make languid or dispirited, emaciate; [cf. Gr. βλάπτω<BR>= Caus. म्लापयति, μῶλυς, μωλυρύς.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लात
म्लात, अस्, आ, अम्, faded, withered; made white<BR>by tanning (said of leather).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लान|म्लानं
म्लान, अस्, आ, अम्, withered, faded; wearied,<BR>weary, wan; languid, languishing; enfeebled, ema-<BR>ciated, faint, feeble, weak; dispirited, dejected, sad,<BR>downcast, melancholy; foul, dirty [cf. मल]; black,<BR>dark-coloured; (अम्), n. a withered or faded state,<BR>withering, fading; absence of brightness or lustre.<BR>—म्लान-क्षीण, अस्, आ, अम्, withered and lan-<BR>guishing.<BR>—म्लान-ता, f. witheredness, the state of<BR>being faded; the being out of spirits; lassitude,<BR>languor.<BR>—म्लान-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, depressed in<BR>mind, dispirited.<BR>—म्लान-वक्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing a downcast countenance.<BR>—म्लान-स्रज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>having a withered or faded garland.<BR>—म्लानाङ्ग<BR>(˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having enfeebled limbs, weak-<BR>bodied; (ई), f. a woman during the menses.<BR>—म्ला-<BR>नेन्द्रिय (˚न-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having enfeebled<BR>senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानि|म्लानिः
म्लानि, इस्, f. withering, fading, decay; languor,<BR>faintness, lassitude, weariness, emaciation; growing<BR>thin; dejection, sadness; foulness, filth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लायत्
म्लायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, fading, withering; lan-<BR>guishing.<BR>—म्लायद्-वक्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>haggard or sorrowful face, having an emaciated<BR>appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लायमान
म्लायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, fading, withering, lan-<BR>guishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लायिन्
म्लायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, becoming faded or withered;<BR>growing thin or emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लास्नु
म्लास्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, becoming faded or withered;<BR>growing thin or emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0800-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य 1. य, the twenty-sixth consonant of<BR>the Nāgarī alphabet, being the semivowel of the<BR>vowels इ, ई, and allied to the soft palatal consonant ज्,<BR>and having the sound of the English य्, (in Bengal<BR>it is usually pronounced ज्.)<BR>—य-कार, अस्, m. the<BR>letter or sound य.<BR>—यकारादि-पद (˚र-आद्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a word beginning with the letter or sound<BR>य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य 2. य, (in prosody) a bacchic or foot<BR>consisting of a short syllable followed by two long<BR>ones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य 3. य, the actual base of the relative<BR>pronoun in declension, though यद्, q. v., is used as<BR>the base in comps. and in the derivative यदीय, (the<BR>declension follows that of the demonstrative pronoun<BR>तद्, q. v., य् being substituted for the initial letter of<BR>that pronoun throughout.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य 4. य, अस्, m. (in some senses fr. rt. 1.<BR>या), one who goes or moves, a goer, mover; air,<BR>wind; a carriage; union, joining; restraining; fame,<BR>celebrity; barley; light, lustre; abandoning; N. of<BR>Yama; (आ), f. going, proceeding; a car, carriage;<BR>restraining, checking; religious meditation; getting,<BR>obtaining; N. of Lakṣmī; pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्
यक् यक्, (in grammar) a term for the<BR>syllable य, which is the sign of the Passive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकन्
यकन् यकन्, a defective word optionally<BR>substituted for यकृत् in certain cases. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्
यकृत् यकृत्, त्, n. (all the cases except the<BR>Nom. Voc. sing. du. pl., Acc. sing. du. are optionally<BR>formed from a base यकन्, hence Acc. pl. यकृन्ति<BR>or यकानि, Inst. sing. du. pl. यकृता or यक्ना, य-<BR>कृद्भ्याम् or यकभ्याम्, यकृद्भिस् or यक-<BR>भिस्, see Pāṇ. VI. 1, 63, Vopa-deva III. 39, III. 165,<BR>Gram. 144), the liver; [cf. Gr. ἧπαρ; Lat. jecur;<BR>(perhaps) Angl. Sax. lifer; Lett. ak-ni-s; Bohem.<BR>jatra, ‘the liver.’]<BR>—यकृत्-कोश, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>the cyst or membrane enveloping the liver.<BR>—य-<BR>कृद्-आत्मिका, f. a kind of cockroach.<BR>—यकृद्-<BR>उदर or यकृद्-दाल्य or यकृद्-दाल्य्-उदर,<BR>अम्, n. an enlargement of the liver.<BR>—यकृद्-वर्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, liver-coloured, of the colour of liver.<BR>—यकृद्-वैरिन्, ई, m. Andersonia Rohitaka.<BR>—यकृन्-मेदस्, अस्, n. liver and fat.<BR>—यकृल्-<BR>लोम, आस्, or यकृल्-लोमन्, आनस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्
यक्ष् यक्ष् (connected with rt. 1. यज्),<BR>cl. 1. P. यक्षति, (according to some<BR>originally) to move, stir (as a living being); to<BR>honour; cl. 10. A. यक्षयते, अययक्षत, &c.,<BR>to worship, honour; (according to Sāy. प्र-यक्-<BR>षन्त in Ṛg-veda 1. 132, 5 = प्रकर्षेण<BR>यजन्ते, they diligently worship.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष|यक्षः
यक्ष, अम्, n. (the neut. form is found only in<BR>Ved.), a living supernatural being (or a being deserv-<BR>ing of worship, cf. rt. 1. यज्), an unsubstantial or<BR>spiritual apparition, a ghost, spirit; (according to<BR>Sāy.) worship, adoration (= पूजा); sacrifice (=<BR>यज्ञ); anything honoured or revered; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of certain mythical beings or demigods who,<BR>like the Guhyakas, are attendants on Kuvera, the<BR>god of wealth, and employed in the care of his<BR>garden and treasures, (they are variously described<BR>as sons of Pulastya, of Pulaha, of Krodhā, of Kaś-<BR>yapa; or in Hari-vaṃśa 11794. as sprung from the<BR>feet of Brahmā; according to the Vāyu-Purāṇa they<BR>were descended from Khasā or Khaśā, who had two<BR>sons, Yakṣa and Rakṣas, severally the progenitors<BR>of the Yakṣas and Rākṣasas; the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa<BR>1. 5. narrates that they were produced by Brahmā as<BR>beings emaciate with hunger, of hideous aspect, and<BR>with long beards, and that crying out ‘let us eat,’<BR>they were denominated Yakṣas, [fr. जक्ष्, to eat];<BR>in the Brahma-Purāṇa thirteen Yakṣas are appointed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-b" target="_blank">Page0801-b+ 81</a>]<BR>by Viṣṇu as guardians of a particular city; though<BR>generally regarded as beings of a benevolent and<BR>inoffensive disposition, like the Yakṣa described in<BR>Kālidāsa's Megha-dūta, they are nevertheless occa-<BR>sionally classed with Piśācas and other malignant<BR>spirits; the Buddhists give them a prominent posi-<BR>tion, describing them in some of their legends as<BR>cruel demons who feast on human flesh and have<BR>the power of raising storms; in others, as harmless<BR>beings who delight in songs, dances, &c.); a sub-<BR>division of a Vyantara (with Jainas); N. of Kuvera;<BR>of a Muni; of the palace of Indra; (ई), f. a female<BR>Yakṣa; N. of Kuvera's wife; (अस्, आ, अम्), a Vedic<BR>word said to be formed fr. the Aor. of rt. 1. यज्,<BR>and used at the end of a comp.<BR>—यक्ष-कर्-<BR>दम, अस्, m. an ointment or perfumed paste con-<BR>sisting of camphor, agallochum, musk, and kakkola,<BR>or, according to some, saffron, in equal proportions;<BR>(according to others the ointment also contains<BR>sandal-wood.)<BR>—यक्ष-कूप, अस्, m. ‘Yakṣa-<BR>tank,’ N. of a place.<BR>—यक्ष-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>being possessed by Yakṣas,’ N. of a particular kind<BR>of insanity.<BR>—यक्षग्रह-परिपीडित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>afflicted with the preceding insanity.<BR>—यक्ष-तरु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘Yakṣa-tree, ’ the Indian fig-tree.<BR>—यक्ष-<BR>ता, f. or यक्ष-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition<BR>of a Yakṣa, the being a Yakṣa.<BR>—यक्ष-दर,<BR>N. of a district.<BR>—यक्ष-दासी, f., N. of a wife of<BR>Śūdraka.<BR>—यक्ष-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. having the<BR>look or appearance of a Yakṣa, having a living or<BR>visible appearance, bodily, corporeal, (but according<BR>to Sāy. = उत्सवस्य द्रष्टा, a gazer or spectator<BR>at a festival.)<BR>—यक्ष-धूप, अस्, m. the resin of<BR>Shorea Robusta; resin in general; incense.<BR>—यक्-<BR>ष-नायक, अस्, m., N. of the servant of the fourth<BR>Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR>—यक्ष-पति,<BR>इस्, m. a king of the Yakṣas; N. of Kuvera.<BR>—यक्ष-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—यक्ष-<BR>बलि, इस्, m. an oblation to the Yakṣas.<BR>—यक्ष-<BR>भृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. ‘Yakṣa-bearing,’ nourishing or<BR>supporting the Yakṣas; receiving worship, receiving<BR>that which is honoured; (Sāy. = पूजितं हविर्-<BR>आदिकं दधानः.)<BR>—यक्ष-मल्ल, अस्, m. (with<BR>Buddhists) N. of one of the five Lokeśvaras.<BR>—यक्-<BR>ष-रस, अस्, m. a kind of intoxicating drink.<BR>—यक्ष-राज्, ट्, m. ‘king of the Yakṣas,’ N. of<BR>Kuvera; of Maṇi-bhadra; a palæstrum or place pre-<BR>pared for wrestling and boxing.<BR>—यक्ष-राज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Yakṣa-king,’ N. of Kuvera.<BR>—यक्षराट्-पुरी,<BR>f., N. of Alakā, the capital of Kuvera (supposed to<BR>be situated on mount Kailāsa).<BR>—यक्ष-रात्रि, इस्,<BR>f. ‘the night of the Yakṣas,’ N. of a Hindū festival<BR>(= दीपाली, q. v.).<BR>—यक्ष-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of<BR>a commentator on Śākaṭāyana.<BR>—यक्ष-वित्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one whose property is like that of the Yakṣas,<BR>one who has merely the guardianship of property<BR>and does not make use of it himself.<BR>—यक्ष-<BR>सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—यक्ष-स्थल, अस्,<BR>m. (?), N. of a place.<BR>—यक्षाङ्गना (˚ष-अङ्˚),<BR>f. a Yakṣa woman.<BR>—यक्षाङ्गी (˚ष-अङ्˚), f.,<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—यक्षाधिप (˚ष-अध्˚), अस् or<BR>यक्षाधिपति (˚ष-अध्˚), इस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>Yakṣas,’ N. of Vaiśravaṇa or Kuvera.<BR>—यक्षा-<BR>मलक (˚ष-आम्˚), अम्, n. the fruit of a species<BR>of date called Piṇḍa-kharjūra.<BR>—यक्षावास (˚ष-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘the abode or residence of the Yakṣas,’<BR>the Indian fig-tree.<BR>—यक्षी-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>or condition of a female Yakṣa, the being a Yakṣī.<BR>—यक्षेन्द्र (˚ष-इन्˚), अस्, m. a king of the<BR>Yakṣas; N. of Kuvera.<BR>—यक्षेश् (˚ष-ईश्), ट्,<BR>m., N. of the servants of the eleventh and eighteenth<BR>Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR>—यक्षेश (˚ष-<BR>ईश) or यक्षेश्वर (˚ष-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a king of<BR>the Yakṣas; N. of Kuvera.<BR>—यक्षोडुम्बरक<BR>(˚ष-उड्˚), अम्, n. the fruit of the Ficus Religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षक
यक्षक, अस्, m. = यक्ष, N. of certain mythi-<BR>cal beings attending on Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षण
यक्षण, अम्, n. probably for जक्षण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षन्
यक्षन्, probably for यक्ष्मन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षिन्
यक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having life, living, really exist-<BR>ing (said of Varuṇa); adorable, (Sāy. = यजनीय);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">Page0801-c+ 78</a>]<BR>(इणी), f. = यक्षी, a female Yakṣa; N. of Kuvera's<BR>wife; a sort of female fiend attached to the service<BR>of Durgā and frequently, like a sylph or fairy, main-<BR>taining intercourse with mortals.<BR>—यक्षिणी-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the state or condition of a female Yakṣa,<BR>the being a Yakṣī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षु
यक्षु, उस्, m., अवस्, m. pl., N. of a family or<BR>race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्म|यक्ष्मः
यक्ष्म, अस्, m. sickness, disease in general or<BR>N. of a large class of diseases (probably of a con-<BR>sumptive nature); pulmonary disease, consumption.<BR>—यक्ष्म-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. destroying<BR>or removing sickness; (अस्), m. the reputed author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 161, (having the patro-<BR>nymic Prājāpatya.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मन्
यक्ष्मन्, आ, m. pulmonary consumption, con-<BR>sumption, decline (= शोष, क्षय).<BR>—यक्ष्म-<BR>गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, seized with consumption, afflicted<BR>with or suffering from consumption.<BR>—यक्ष्म-<BR>ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, attacked by consumption.<BR>—य-<BR>क्ष्म-ग्रह, अस्, m. a consumptive seizure, attack<BR>of consumption.<BR>—यक्ष्म-घ्नी, f. ‘destroying<BR>consumption,’ grapes, raisins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मिन्
यक्ष्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, consumptive, phthisical;<BR>(ई), m. one who suffers from pulmonary consump-<BR>tion (Manu III. 154).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मोधा
यक्ष्मोधा, f. a kind of sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्य
यक्ष्य यक्ष्य, यक्ष्यमाण. See under<BR>rt. 1. यज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्
यङ् यङ्, (in grammar) a term for the<BR>syllable य, which is the sign of the Intensive.<BR>—यङ्-अन्त, अस्, m. (in grammar) the Ātmane-<BR>pada Intensive formed by reduplication and the<BR>addition of the syllable य.<BR>—यङ्-लुक्, the dropping<BR>or omission of य (i. e. according to the theory of<BR>grammarians a blank substituted for the य of the<BR>Intensive).<BR>—यङ्लुग्-अन्त, अस्, m. the Parasmai-<BR>pada Intensive formed without य.<BR>—यङ्लुग्-अन्त-<BR>शिरोमणि, N. of a treatise on the Intensive without<BR>य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यच्छत्
यच्छत् यच्छत्, यच्छमान. See under<BR>rt. यम्, p. 809, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यच्छन्दस्
यच्छन्दस् यच्-छन्दस्. See under यद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्
यज् 1. यज्, cl. 1. P. A. यजति, -ते,<BR>Impv. यजतु, यजताम् (2nd sing. P.,<BR>Ved. यक्षि, A. यक्ष्व, 2nd pl. यजध्व for<BR>यजध्वम्), Perf. इयाज (2nd sing. इयजिथ or<BR>इयष्ठ or येजिथ, 3rd du. ईजतुस्, 3rd pl. ईजुस्),<BR>ईजे (3rd pl. ईजिरे, part. ईजान, cf. Manu XI. 87),<BR>1st Fut. यष्टा, 2nd Fut. यक्ष्यति, -ते, Aor.<BR>अयाक्षीत् (1st du. अयाक्ष्व, 1st pl. अयाक्ष्म,<BR>3rd sing., Ved. अयाट्, 2nd sing. अयास्; other Vedic<BR>forms यक्षत्, यक्षतस्, यक्षताम्), अयष्ट<BR>(1st sing. अयक्षि, 1st du. अयक्ष्वहि, 1st pl.<BR>अयक्ष्महि, 3rd pl. अयक्षत), Prec. इज्यात् (3rd<BR>du. इज्यास्ताम्, 3rd pl. इज्यासुस्), यक्षीष्ट (2nd<BR>pl. यक्षीध्वम्), Cond. अयक्ष्यत्, अयक्ष्-<BR>यत, Indec. part. इष्ट्वा (इष्ट्वीनम्, Pāṇ. VII.<BR>1, 48), Inf. यष्टुम् (ep. ईजितुम्, Ved. यष्टवे,<BR>यजध्यै), to worship with sacrifices or oblations,<BR>make an offering or oblation, sacrifice, (in Ved.<BR>generally A. if the sacrificer makes the offering on<BR>his own account, in the later language properly P.<BR>when used with reference to the sacrificing priest,<BR>and A. when referring to the person who provides<BR>the sacrifice, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. I. 3, 72, and<BR>Vopa-deva XXIII. 58); to sacrifice or make an<BR>oblation to a particular deity (with acc. of the deity<BR>to whom the sacrifice or offering is made, and inst.<BR>of the means by which the sacrifice or oblation is<BR>performed, e. g. हविषा यक्षि देवान्, worship<BR>the gods with an oblation; and dat. of the thing for<BR>which the offering is made, e. g. यक्ष्वा सौम-<BR>नसाय रुद्रम्, worship Rudra for a sound under-<BR>standing; also with dat. or even loc. of the person<BR>to whom the offering is made, or with प्रति after<BR>the acc.; rarely with acc. of the thing for which<BR>the offering is made, e. g. यजन्ते अस्य सख्यम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">Page0802-a+ 81</a>]<BR>they sacrifice for his friendship); to worship, adore,<BR>honour, venerate, revere, respect; to consecrate,<BR>dedicate, inaugurate; to invite to a sacrifice (Ved.);<BR>to honour with one's presence, come to, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 75, 5. यक्षि = सङ्गच्छ-<BR>स्व): Pass. इज्यते, Impf. ऐज्यत (Pres. part. Pass.<BR>इज्यमान, ep. इज्यत्), to be sacrificed, to be wor-<BR>shipped, &c.: Caus. याजयति, -यते, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अयीयजत्, to cause to sacrifice or worship, &c.; to<BR>assist at a sacrifice; to perform the office of the<BR>sacrificing priest: Desid. यियक्षति, -ते, to desire<BR>to sacrifice or worship, wish to make an offering:<BR>Intens. यायज्यते, यायजीति, यायष्टि; [cf. Zend<BR>yaz, ‘to honour, worship;’ Gr. ἅζ-ο-μαι, ἅγ-ιο-ς,<BR>ἅγ-νό-ς, ἅγίζω, ἕναγίζω, ἅγ-ος..]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0801-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्य
यक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be sacrificed or wor-<BR>shipped, &c., (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>60, 3 = यष्टव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्यमाण
यक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, about to perform a<BR>sacrifice, wishing to make a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्
2. यज्, ट्, ट्, ट् [cf. Pāṇ. VIII. 2, 36], sacrificing,<BR>worshipping, a sacrificer, (at the end of a comp., cf.<BR>दिवि-य्˚, देव-य्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज|यजः
यज, अस्, m. a sacrifice, &c. (at the end of a<BR>comp.); = अग्नि, fire.<BR>—यज-प्रैष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having a Praiṣa or invitation with the word<BR>यज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्
यजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sacrificing, worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत|यजतः
यजत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worthy of worship, (Sāy.<BR>= यजनीय, यष्टव्य); adorable, holy, godly,<BR>divine (said of Agni, Indra, and other gods, also of<BR>the chariot of the Aśvins); august, sublime, dignified,<BR>awe-inspiring, awful; (अस्), m. an officiating priest<BR>at a sacrifice (= ऋत्व्-इज्); the moon; N. of Śiva; of<BR>a Ṛṣi with the patronymic Ātreya (author of the<BR>hymns Ṛg-veda V. 67, 68; cf. Zend yazata).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजति|यजतिः
यजति, इस्, m. a technical term for those sacrificial<BR>ceremonies to which the verb यजति is applied (as<BR>distinguished from जुहोति, q. v.), a solemn sacrifice,<BR>(according to Kullūka, जुहोति-यजति-क्रियाः =<BR>होम-यागादि-रूपाः क्रियाः, oblations to fire and<BR>solemn sacrifices, Manu II. 84.)<BR>—यजति-देश, अस्,<BR>m. or यजति-स्थान, अम्, n. the place or position<BR>south of the Vedi or sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्र|यजत्रः
यजत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worthy of worship<BR>(Sāy. = यजनीय, यष्टव्य), deserving of adora-<BR>tion, adorable, worthy of sacrifice (said of Agni, of<BR>Varuṇa, and the Ādityas, and of heaven and earth);<BR>(अस्), m. = अग्नि = होत्रिन्, a Brāhman who has main-<BR>tained his consecrated fire; (अम्), n. = अग्नि-होत्र,<BR>the maintenance of the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजथ
यजथ, Ved. (only found in the dat. यजथाय,<BR>often = the inf. यष्टुम्), worship of the gods,<BR>sacrifice, (Sāy. = यज्ञ, यजन); an adorer, wor-<BR>shipper, (Sāy. = यष्टृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन|यजनं
यजन, अम्, n. the act of sacrificing, sacrifice, wor-<BR>shipping; a place of sacrifice; N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजनीय
यजनीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. यजन), relating to<BR>sacrifice or worship; (अम्), n., scil. अहन्, the day<BR>of sacrifice or consecration, i. e. the first day of the<BR>month, [cf. माघी-पक्ष-य्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन्त|यजन्तः
यजन्त, अस्, m. a sacrificer, worshipper (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमान|यजमानः
यजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, worshipping, sacrificing,<BR>&c.; (अस्), m. a person who institutes or performs<BR>a regular sacrifice and pays the expences of it, a<BR>person who employs a priest or priests to perform<BR>a sacrifice or any fixed or occasional religious cere-<BR>monies, any person who intends performing or is<BR>able to bear the cost of a regular sacrifice; a patron,<BR>host, rich man, householder, respectable person,<BR>gentleman, (as the person who employs priests to<BR>sacrifice is generally a householder, the title Yajamāna<BR>has come to signify in modern times ‘the head of a<BR>family,’ ‘chief of a caste or tribe,’ ‘head man of<BR>a community;’ the family priest employed by a<BR>Yajamāna is sometimes an hereditary functionary,<BR>and cannot be dismissed as long as he performs his<BR>functions efficiently); (ई), f. the wife of a Yajamāna.<BR>—यजमान-त्व, अम्, n. the rank or position of a<BR>Yajamāna.<BR>—यजमान-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>the Brāhmaṇa of the Yajamāna.<BR>—यजमान-लोक,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">Page0802-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. the world or heaven of sacrificers.<BR>—यज-<BR>मान-शिष्य, अस्, m. the pupil of a Brāhman who<BR>defrays the expences of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमानक|यजमानकः
यजमानक, अस्, m. = यजमान, the person<BR>paying the cost of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजस्
यजस्, अस्, n., Ved. honour, worship, sacrifice,<BR>(Sāy. = याग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजा
यजा, f., N. of a female tutelary being (mentioned<BR>in connection with Sītā, Śamā, and Bhūti).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजाक|यजाकः
यजाक, अस्, आ, अम्, making offerings or presents,<BR>liberal, munificent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजि|यजिः
यजि, इस्, m. one who institutes or performs a<BR>sacrifice, a sacrificer; sacrificing, honouring, worship-<BR>ping, (at the end of a comp., cf. देव-य्˚); a sacri-<BR>fice, (in this sense the gender is doubtful); the root<BR>यज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजिन्
यजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, a worshipper, sacrificer, offerer of<BR>oblations; worshipping, honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजिष्ठ
यजिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worshipping very<BR>much, worshipping or honouring in the highest<BR>degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजिष्णु
यजिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, worshipping or adoring the<BR>gods with sacrifices, making sacrifices to the deities,<BR>sacrificing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजीयस्
यजीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. honouring more, mak-<BR>ing better offerings or sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजु|यजुः
यजु, उस्, m., N. of one of the ten horses of<BR>the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुष
यजुष in ऋग्-यजुष, अम्, n. the Ṛg and the<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुष्क
यजुष्क in अ-यजुष्क, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुष्य
यजुष्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. यजुस्), Ved. relating<BR>to ceremonial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुस्
यजुस्, उस्, n. religious reverence, veneration, wor-<BR>ship, oblation, sacrifice (Ved.); that by which a<BR>sacrifice is effected, a sacrificial prayer or formula; a<BR>text of the Yajur-veda or rather a technical term for<BR>certain words or Mantras muttered in a peculiar<BR>manner at a sacrifice, (these Mantras were properly<BR>in prose as distinguished from the metrical ऋच् which<BR>was recited, and the metrical सामन् which was<BR>sung, see मन्त्र, 2. ऋच्; although, however, the<BR>prose Yajus is a distinctive feature of the Yajur-veda,<BR>this Veda is in real fact chiefly composed of verses<BR>taken from the Ṛg-veda, which may then also be<BR>called Yajus, cf. यजुर्-वेद below); N. of the<BR>Yajur-veda, q. v., (in this sense also frequently य-<BR>जूंषि, n. pl.); (उस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—यजुः-<BR>शाखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, familiar with a Śākhā of the<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR>—यजुर्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of<BR>verses of the Yajur-veda; [cf. ऋङ्-मय.]<BR>—यजुर्-<BR>लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f., N. of a particular formula.<BR>—यजुर्-<BR>विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing the Yajus, conversant with<BR>sacrificial formulas, one who is familiar with the<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR>—यजुर्-विधान, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—यजुर्-वेद, अस्, m. ‘the sacrificial Veda,’ the<BR>collective body of sacred Mantras or texts which con-<BR>stitute the Yajur-veda, (these Mantras, though often<BR>consisting of the prose Yajus, are frequently identical<BR>with the Mantras of the Ṛg-veda, the Yajur-veda<BR>being only a collection of liturgical forms or rather a<BR>sort of sacrificial prayer-book for the Adhvaryu priests<BR>formed out of the Ṛg-veda, which had to be dissected<BR>and re-arranged with additional texts for sacrificial<BR>purposes; to serve these purposes, the hymns of the<BR>Ṛg-veda are scattered about piecemeal, verses of the<BR>same hymn being often transposed, verses from dif-<BR>ferent hymns combined, and even those of different<BR>poets brought together into one and the same hymn;<BR>in fact the compilation of the Yajur-veda resulted<BR>from the gradual growth of a complicated ritual in<BR>connection with those sacrifices without which the<BR>Hindū believed it was impossible to secure the favour<BR>of his gods, and for the performance of which the<BR>unsystematic collection of hymns in the Ṛg-veda<BR>was unsuited: the great characteristic feature of the<BR>Yajur-veda is its division into two distinct collections<BR>of texts, the one called Taittirīya-saṃhitā or Kṛṣṇa,<BR>i. e. ‘Black’ [because in it the Saṃhitā or simple<BR>collection of texts and Brāhmaṇa or explanation of<BR>the rites in which the texts were employed is con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-c" target="_blank">Page0802-c+ 80</a>]<BR>fused]; the other called Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā or Śukla,<BR>i. e. ‘White’ [because in this, which is thought to be<BR>the more recent of the two recensions, the Saṃhitā is<BR>cleared from confusion with its Brāhmaṇa, and there-<BR>fore looks white and orderly]: the order of sacrifices,<BR>however, of both divisions of the Yajur-veda is simi-<BR>lar, two of the principal being the Darśa-pūrṇa-māsa<BR>or sacrifice to be performed at new and full moon, and<BR>the Aśva-medha or horse-sacrifice; cf. तैत्तिरीय-<BR>संहिता, वाजसनेयि-संहिता.)<BR>—यजुर्वेद-<BR>श्राद्ध, N. of a work (treating of the prayers and<BR>rites to be used at the anniversaries of the death of<BR>parents according to the school of the Yajur-veda).<BR>—यजुर्-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, familiar with the Yajur-<BR>veda.<BR>—यजुर्वेदि-वृषोत्सर्ग-तत्त्व (˚ष-उत्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of part of the Smṛti-tattva by Raghu-<BR>nandana on the release of a bull according to the<BR>teaching of the Yajur-veda.<BR>—यजुर्वेदि-श्राद्ध-<BR>तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of certain verses by Raghu-<BR>nandana on the anniversaries of the death of parents<BR>according to the school of the Yajur-veda.<BR>—य-<BR>जुष्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. performed with a<BR>Yajus, consecrated or dedicated with a sacrificial<BR>formula.<BR>—यजुष्-कृत्ति, इस्, f., Ved. consecration or<BR>dedication with a sacrificial formula.<BR>—यजुष्-क्रिया,<BR>f., Ved. a rite or ceremony accompanied with a<BR>Yajus.<BR>—यजुष्-टम, Ved. superl. of यजुस्.<BR>—यजुष्-टर, Ved. compar. of यजुस्.<BR>—यजुष्-<BR>टस्, ind., Ved. from a Yajus; in relation to a Yajus;<BR>on the authority of the Yajur-veda.<BR>—यजुष्-टा, f.<BR>or यजुष्-ट्व, अम्, n., Ved. the state of a Yajus.<BR>—यजुष्-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the Yajus,’ N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—यजुष्-पात्र, अम्, n., see Gaṇa Kaskādi<BR>to Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 48.<BR>—यजुष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. any rite accompanied with a sacrificial formula,<BR>(यजुष्मत्य इष्टकास्,) a term for certain bricks<BR>used in building the sacrificial altar.)<BR>—यजुस्-सात्,<BR>ind. to the state of a Yajus.<BR>—यजूदर (यजुस् +<BR>उदर), अस्, m., Ved. ‘Yajus-bellied, having the Yajus<BR>for a belly,’ epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञ|यज्ञः
यज्ञ, अस्, m. prayer, devotion, homage, praise,<BR>(used in the older language with these meanings;<BR>cf. Zend यश्न); worship of a deity, respect or<BR>reverence for a deity, act of worship or devotional<BR>act in general, (the five most important acts of de-<BR>votion which ought to be performed daily by every<BR>twice-born man are भूत-य्˚, मनुष्य-य्˚, पितृ-<BR>य्˚, देव-य्˚, ब्रह्म-य्˚, q. q. v. v.; cf. महा-य्˚);<BR>a sacrifice (this is the most common sense of the<BR>word), any offering or oblation, (चिन्ता-यज्ञ, a<BR>sacrifice in thought, mental offering); Sacrifice (per-<BR>sonified); a form of Viṣṇu; N. of a son of Ruci<BR>by Ākūti; of Indra under Manu Svāyambhuva;<BR>(according to native authorities also) N. of Agni; =<BR>आत्मन्; यज्ञ प्राजापत्य, N. of the reputed<BR>author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 130.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. a sacrificial act, sacrificial rite or<BR>ceremony; (आ, आ, अ), occupied or engaged in a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, resembling or<BR>like a sacrifice, of the form or nature of an offering.<BR>—यज्ञ-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘sacrifice-loving,’<BR>desiring sacrifice, eager for worship.<BR>—यज्ञ-कार,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, occupied or engaged in a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-काल, अस्, m. ‘sacrifice-time,’ a season for<BR>sacrifice; N. of the last lunar day in each half of a<BR>month.<BR>—यज्ञ-कीलक, अस्, m. ‘sacrifice-post,’ the<BR>post to which the victim is fastened.<BR>—यज्ञ-कुण्ड,<BR>अम्, n. a hole in the ground for receiving the sacri-<BR>ficial fire.<BR>—यज्ञ-कृत्, त्,त्,त्, ‘sacrifice-doing,’ wor-<BR>shipping, performing or arranging a sacrifice, em-<BR>ployed or occupied in a sacrifice; causing or occa-<BR>sioning sacrifices; (त्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; a<BR>priest conducting a sacrifice; N. of a king.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>कृन्तत्र, अम्, n. a fragment or portion of a sacri-<BR>fice.<BR>—यज्ञ-केतु, उस्, m., Ved. (perhaps) one who<BR>is conversant with sacrifice; having the sacrifice for<BR>a mark or sign, the announcer of a sacrifice, (Sāy.<BR>= यज्ञः प्रज्ञापको यस्य); N. of a Rākṣasa<BR>(in Rāmāyaṇa VI. 18, 14).<BR>—यज्ञ-कोप, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—यज्ञ-क्रतु, उस्, m. a sacri-<BR>ficial rite or ceremony in honour of the gods; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0803-a" target="_blank">Page0803-a+ 81</a>]<BR>complete rite or chief ceremony; a personification<BR>of Viṣṇu; (अवस्), m. pl. the Yajña and Kratu<BR>sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञ-क्रिया, f. sacrificial act, any sacri-<BR>ficial rite or ceremony.<BR>—यज्ञ-गाथा, f. a sacrificial<BR>verse or any memorial verse connected with the<BR>ritual of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—यज्ञ-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘sacrifice-<BR>destroying,’ interrupting sacrifices; (अस्), m. a demon<BR>who interrupts sacrifices, a malicious or evil-omened<BR>demon.<BR>—यज्ञ-छाग, अस्, m. a goat for sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘sacrifice-knowing,’ con-<BR>versant with sacrifices, understanding the worship of<BR>the gods.<BR>—यज्ञ-तति, इस्, f., Ved. a sacrificial offer-<BR>ing, performance of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-तनू, ऊस्,<BR>f. a form of worship; epithet of certain Vyāhṛtis;<BR>of certain sacrificial bricks (इष्टका).<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>तन्त्र-सुधा-निधि, इस्, m., N. of a work on<BR>Vedic ritual by Sāyaṇācārya.<BR>—यज्ञ-तन्त्र-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Sūtra work.<BR>—यज्ञ-त्रातृ, ता, m.<BR>‘sacrifice-protector,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-दक्षि-<BR>णा, f. a sacrificial gift or present, a fee or donation<BR>given to the priests engaged in the performance<BR>of a ceremony.<BR>—यज्ञ-दत्त, अस्, m. ‘sacrifice-<BR>given,’ a proper N. (commonly used in examples).<BR>—यज्ञदत्तक, अस्, m. (a diminutive), dear little<BR>Yajña-datta.<BR>—यज्ञदत्त-वध, अस्, m. ‘Yajña-<BR>datta's death,’ N. of an episode of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—यज्ञदत्त-शर्मन्, आ, m. a proper N. (often<BR>used in examples).<BR>—यज्ञ-दीक्षा, f. initiation into<BR>sacrifices, admission to sacrificial rites, due perform-<BR>ance of the sacrifice (see Manu II. 169).<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>देव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यज्ञ-द्रव्य, अम्, n.<BR>any sacrificial utensil, anything used for sacrifice, a<BR>sacrificial vessel.<BR>—यज्ञ-द्रुह्, -ध्रुक् or -ध्रुट्,<BR>m. an enemy of sacrifices, a Rākṣasa.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>धर, अस्, आ, अम्, bringing the sacrifice, bearing an<BR>offering; (अस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-धीर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. experienced in or conversant with<BR>the worship of the gods; constant in sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-नारायण, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>नारायण-दीक्षित, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—यज्ञ-निर्वाह, अस्, m. the accomplishment or<BR>carrying out of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-निर्वृत्ति, इस्, f.<BR>completion or reward of a sacrifice, fruit of a sacri-<BR>ficial offering.<BR>—यज्ञ-निष्कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. arrang-<BR>ing the sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-नी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. conduct-<BR>ing worship, directing the sacrifice; (ईस्), m. a par-<BR>taker of the sacrifice, (Sāy. = यज्ञस्य निर्वाह-<BR>कः.)<BR>—यज्ञ-नेमि, इस्, m. ‘surrounded by sacri-<BR>fices,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यज्ञ-पति, इस्, m. lord<BR>of the sacrifice, (applied to the person who institutes<BR>and bears the expence of a sacrificial ceremony); N.<BR>of Soma and of Viṣṇu (as gods in whose honour<BR>an offering is made); of an author.<BR>—यज्ञ-पत्नी,<BR>f. the wife of the person who institutes a sacrifice,<BR>(as taking part in the ceremony.)<BR>—यज्ञ-पथ,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. path of worship, way of sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-पद् or यज्ञ-पाद्, Ved. (perhaps) walk-<BR>ing on sacrifices, (a feminine form यज्ञ-पदी is<BR>given.)<BR>—यज्ञ-परिभाषा, f., N. of a Sūtra work<BR>by Āpastambha.<BR>—यज्ञ-परुस्, उस्, n., Ved. a joint<BR>or part of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-पशु, उस्, m. an<BR>animal for sacrifice, victim; a horse.<BR>—यज्ञ-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. a sacrificial vessel.<BR>—यज्ञपात्रीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, proper or suitable for a sacrificial vessel.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>पार्श्व, अम्, n., N. of a work; (अस्), m., N. of an<BR>author (according to some).<BR>—यज्ञ-पुंस् पुमान्,<BR>m. ‘soul of sacrifice,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-पुच्-<BR>छ, अम्, n., Ved. the tail, i. e. the last part or con-<BR>clusion of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-पुरश्-चरण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—यज्ञ-पुरुष or यज्ञ-पू-<BR>रुष, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-प्रयाण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of the eighty-fifth chapter of the Uttara-<BR>kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—यज्ञ-प्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved.<BR>taking pleasure in sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञ-फल-द, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, yielding the fruit of sacrifices; (अस्), m.<BR>‘recompensing or rewarding for sacrifice,’ an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-बन्धु, उस्, m., Ved. com-<BR>panion of sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-बाहु, उस्, m. ‘arm of<BR>sacrifice,’ N. of Agni; of Priya-vrata.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>भङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of the Fifth Act of Vaidya-nātha's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0803-b" target="_blank">Page0803-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Citra-yajña-nāṭaka.<BR>—यज्ञ-भाग, अस्, m. a part<BR>or portion of a sacrifice; (अस्, आ, अम्), having a<BR>share in a sacrifice, partaking of an offering; (अस्),<BR>m. a god, deity.<BR>—यज्ञभाग-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, en-<BR>joying a share in a sacrifice; (क्), m. a god, deity.<BR>—यज्ञभागेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of Indra.<BR>—यज्ञ-भाजन or यज्ञ-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a<BR>sacrificial vessel or utensil.<BR>—यज्ञ-भावन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, causing or promoting sacrifice; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-भावित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>honoured with sacrifices (said of the gods).<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>भुज्, क्, क्, क्, enjoying sacrifice, taking pleasure in<BR>offerings; (क्), m. a god, deity (especially Viṣṇu).<BR>—यज्ञ-भूमि, इस्, f. ‘sacrifice-ground,’ a place<BR>for sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-भूषण, अस्, m. ‘sacrifice-<BR>ornament,’ white Darbha grass.<BR>—यज्ञ-भृत्, त्, m.<BR>‘sacrifice-bearer,’ an arranger or institutor of a sacri-<BR>fice, one who institutes or bears the expence of a<BR>sacrifice; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-भोक्तृ,<BR>ता, m. ‘enjoyer of sacrifice,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>मण्डल, अम्, n. a sacrificial ring or circle, place<BR>for sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the<BR>mind or attention set on sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञ-मन्-<BR>मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. intent on sacrifices, delighting<BR>in sacrifice, (Sāy. = यज्ञार्थम् मतिमत्, यज्वन्.)<BR>—यज्ञ-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of sacrifices,<BR>containing sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-महोत्सव (˚हा-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a great sacrificial feast or ceremony.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>मालि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यज्ञ-मुख, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. an introduction to a sacrifice, commencement<BR>of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-मुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, ‘sacrifice-steal-<BR>ing,’ robbing a sacrifice; (ट्), m. a demon who lies<BR>in wait and carries off a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-मूर्ति,<BR>इस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यज्ञ-मेनि, Ved. = आयुध<BR>(according to the commentator).<BR>—यज्ञ-यशस,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. the beauty or splendor of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, suited or proper for a<BR>sacrifice; (अस्), m. Ficus Glomerata.<BR>—यज्ञ-रस,<BR>अस्, m. ‘juice or fluid of sacrifice,’ the Soma.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>राज्, ट्, m. ‘king of the sacrifice,’ the moon, (per-<BR>haps for यज्व-राज्; cf. यज्वनाम् पतिः under<BR>यज्वन्.)<BR>—यज्ञ-रुचि, इस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—यज्ञ-रेतस्, अस्, n. ‘seed of sacrifice,’ the Soma.<BR>—यज्ञर्त (˚न-ऋत), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. suitable or<BR>proper for sacrifice (?); set apart for sacrifice (?).<BR>—यज्ञ-लिङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘having sacrifice for his<BR>attribute,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यज्ञ-वचस्, अस्, n.,<BR>Ved. a sacrificial word or speech; (आस्), m., N. of a<BR>preceptor (having Rājastambāyana as his patronymic).<BR>—यज्ञ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having or possessing<BR>sacrifice, worshipping.<BR>—यज्ञ-वनस्, Ved. loving<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-वराह, अस्, m. Viṣṇu in the<BR>boar-incarnation; [cf. यज्ञ-सूकर.]<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. increasing or promoting<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king.<BR>—यज्ञ-वल्क, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यज्ञ-वल्ली,<BR>f. = सोम-वल्ली, Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—यज्ञ-वाट,<BR>अस्, m. ‘sacrifice-enclosure,’ a place prepared and<BR>enclosed for a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-वाम, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—यज्ञ-वास्तु, उ, n., Ved. a place for<BR>worship or sacrifice, sacrificial ground.<BR>—यज्ञ-वाह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, conducting or accompanying the sacrifice,<BR>conveying the sacrifice to the gods; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>one of Skanda's attendants.<BR>—यज्ञ-वाहन, अस्, m.<BR>the conductor of a sacrifice, a Brāhman; ‘having<BR>sacrifice for a vehicle,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; of Śiva.<BR>—यज्ञ-वाहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. bringing or offer-<BR>ing sacrifice, a worshipper, offerer of sacrifice; re-<BR>ceiving sacrifice (said of the gods and of the Maruts).<BR>—यज्ञ-वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, conducting or accompany-<BR>ing the sacrifice, conveying the sacrifice to the gods.<BR>—यज्ञ-विद्, त्, त्, त्, ‘sacrifice-knowing,’ skilled in<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-विद्या, f. knowledge of sacrifice,<BR>skill in sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-विभ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. one whose sacrifice has failed or is profitless.<BR>—यज्ञ-वीर्य, अस्, m. ‘whose might is sacrifice,’<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञ-वृक्ष, अस्, m. ‘sacri-<BR>fice-tree,’ the banian or Indian fig-tree.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. exalted with sacrifices,<BR>delighted with offerings (said of Indra).<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>वृध्, Ved. pleased with sacrifices or abounding in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0803-c" target="_blank">Page0803-c+ 81</a>]<BR>sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञ-वेदि, इस्, or यज्ञ-वेदी, f. an<BR>altar for sacrifice, a place prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-वेशस, अम्, n., Ved. interruption of wor-<BR>ship or sacrifice, desecration or profanation of sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-वोढवे (वोढवे, dat. c. of वोढु, used<BR>as an inf. of rt. वह्), Ved. to accompany or attend<BR>the sacrifice, to convey the offering to the gods.<BR>—यज्ञ-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. observing the<BR>sacrifice, conforming to the ritual or observance of<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-शत्रु, उस्, m. an enemy of sacri-<BR>fices; N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—यज्ञ-शरण, अम्, n.<BR>‘sacrifice-shed,’ a building or temporary structure<BR>under which sacrifices are performed.<BR>—यज्ञ-शाला,<BR>f. a sacrificial hall; = अग्नि-शरण, a house or place<BR>for keeping the sacrificial fire.<BR>—यज्ञ-शास्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. the science of sacrifice, ordinances or rules relating<BR>to sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञशास्त्र-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing<BR>the rules or ordinances for sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञ-शिष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, (anything) left from a sacrifice or oblation.<BR>—यज्ञ-शिष्टाशन (˚ट-अश्˚), अम्, n. the eating<BR>of the remains of a sacrifice, a repast on the remnants<BR>of a sacrifice (Manu III. 118).<BR>—यज्ञ-शील, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, accustomed to perform sacrifices, frequently per-<BR>forming sacrifices; (अस्), m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—यज्ञ-शेष, अस्, अम्, m. n. the remains or<BR>residue of a sacrifice (Manu III. 285).<BR>—यज्ञ-श्री,<BR>ईस्, ईस्, इ, promoting or favourable to sacrifice, (Sāy.<BR>= यज्ञस्य सम्पद्-रूपः); (ईस्), m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—यज्ञ-श्रेष्ठा, f. Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—यज्ञ-संशित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. excited by<BR>offerings or sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञ-संस्था, f., Ved. the<BR>constitution or basis of a sacrifice, form of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-सदन, अम्, n. a sacrificial hall.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>सदस्, अस्, n. an assembly or number of people at<BR>a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-समृद्धि, इस्, f., N. of the<BR>eighty-sixth chapter of the Uttara-kāṇḍa of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—यज्ञ-सम्भार, अस्, m. apparatus or<BR>materials for a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-साध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>‘sacrifice-effecting,’ accomplishing sacrifices.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>साधन, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘sacrifice-effecting,’ accomplish-<BR>ing sacrifices; occasioning or causing sacrifices, (used<BR>as an epithet of Viṣṇu.)<BR>—यज्ञ-सार, अस्, m.<BR>‘essence of sacrifice,’ N. of Viṣṇu; Ficus Glome-<BR>rata.<BR>—यज्ञ-सारथि, N. of a Sāman.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>सिद्धि, इस्, f. the completion or accomplishment of<BR>a sacrifice, the due performance of a sacrificial cere-<BR>mony; obtaining the objects of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>सूकर, अस्, m. Viṣṇu in his incarnation as a boar<BR>(= यज्ञ-वराह).<BR>—यज्ञ-सूत्र, अम्, n. a sacred<BR>cord worn over the left shoulder and under the right<BR>arm at sacrifices, the sacrificial thread or cord, (see<BR>यज्ञोपवीत.) — यज्ञ-सेन, अस्, m., N. of Dru-<BR>pada; of a king of Vidarbha; of a Dānava; of<BR>Viṣṇu; of various men.<BR>—यज्ञ-सोम, अस्, m., N.<BR>of several Brāhmans.<BR>—यज्ञ-स्थल, अम्, n. a place<BR>for sacrifice; N. of an Agra-hāra; of a Grāma; of<BR>a town.<BR>—यज्ञ-स्थाणु, उस्, m. a sacrificial post or<BR>stake.<BR>—यज्ञ-स्थान, अम्, n. a place for sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—यज्ञ-<BR>हन्, आ, -घ्नी, अ, destroying sacrifice, injuring or<BR>vitiating sacrifice, interrupting worship; (आ), m., N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—यज्ञ-हन, अस्, आ, अम्, = यज्ञ-हन्<BR>above; (अस्), m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—यज्ञ-हृ-<BR>दय, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘whose heart is sacrifice,’ liking<BR>sacrifice above everything else, loving sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञ-होतृ, ता, m. an offerer at a sacrifice;<BR>invoker of the (gods who are) worthy of worship,<BR>(Sāy. = यष्टव्यानां देवानाम् आह्वातृ); N. of<BR>a son of Manu Uttama.<BR>—यज्ञांश (˚ञ-अं˚), अस्,<BR>m. a part or share of a sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञांश-भुज्,<BR>क्, m. ‘enjoying a share in sacrifices,’ a god, deity.<BR>—यज्ञागार (˚ञ-अग्˚ or -आग्˚), अम्, n. a shed for<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञाङ्ग (˚ञ-अङ्˚), अम्, n. ‘sacrifice-<BR>limb,’ a part of a sacrifice, any means or instrument<BR>or implement of a sacrifice; (अस्), m. the glomerous<BR>fig-tree, Ficus Glomerata; Acacia Catechu; Clero-<BR>dendrum Siphonanthus; N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa;<BR>of Śiva; (आ), f. Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—यज्ञात्मन्<BR>(˚ञ-आत्˚), आ, m. ‘soul of sacrifice,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञात्म-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Pārthasārathi-miśra.<BR>—यज्ञानुकाशिन् (˚ञ-अन्˚), ई,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">Page0804-a+ 81</a>]<BR>इनी, इ, Ved. looking at or inspecting sacrifices, (accord-<BR>ing to a commentator = यज्ञ-तत्त्व-प्रकाशन-<BR>समर्थ.) — यज्ञान्त (˚ञ-अन्˚), अस्, m. the con-<BR>clusion or termination of a sacrifice; a supplementary<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञान्त-कृत्, त्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञायतन (˚ञ-आय्˚), अम्, n. a place for sacri-<BR>fice.<BR>—यज्ञायुध (˚ञ-आय्˚), अम्, n., Ved. ‘sacri-<BR>fice-instrument,’ any vessel or utensil employed at a<BR>sacrifice, (ten are usually enumerated.)<BR>—यज्ञायु-<BR>धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having or furnished with sacri-<BR>ficial utensils.<BR>—यज्ञारि (˚ञ-अरि), इस्, m. ‘foe of<BR>sacrifices,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—यज्ञार्थ (˚ञ-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, serving for a sacrifice; (अम्), ind. for<BR>the sake of sacrifice.<BR>—यज्ञार्ह (˚ञ-अर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, deserving sacrifice; suitable or fit for sacrifice;<BR>(औ), m. du. epithet of the two Aśvins.<BR>—यज्ञाव-<BR>यव (˚ञ-अव्˚), अस्, m. ‘whose limbs consist of<BR>sacrifices,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यज्ञावसान (˚ञ-<BR>अव्˚), अम्, n., N. of the ninety-third chapter of the<BR>Uttara-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—यज्ञाशन (˚ञ-<BR>अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘consumer of sacrifices,’ a god, deity.<BR>—यज्ञा-साह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. mighty in sacrifice;<BR>bearing the sacrifice, (Sāy. = यज्ञस्य वोढृ or<BR>धारयितृ.) — यज्ञेश (˚ञ-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>worship or of sacrifice,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; of the sun.<BR>—यज्ञेश्वर (˚ञ-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of worship or<BR>of sacrifice,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of an author;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a particular magical incantation.<BR>—यज्ञेश्वरार्य (˚र-आर्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यज्ञेषु (˚ञ-इषु), उस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यज्-<BR>ञेष्ट (˚ञ-इष्˚), अम्, n. a species of fragrant grass<BR>(= दीर्घ-रोहिषक).<BR>—यज्ञोडुम्बर (˚ञ-<BR>उड्˚), अस्, m. = उडुम्बर, Ficus Glomerata.<BR>—यज्-<BR>ञोपकरण (˚ञ-उप्˚), अम्, n. ‘sacrifice-instrument,’<BR>any utensil or implement useful or necessary for sacri-<BR>fice.<BR>—यज्ञोपवीत (˚ञ-उप्˚), अम्, n. the solemn<BR>investiture of youths of the first three castes, Brāh-<BR>mans, Kṣatriyas, and Vaiśyas, with a peculiar thread<BR>or cord worn over the left shoulder and hanging<BR>down diagonally across the body to the right hip, by<BR>which they are considered regenerated and admitted<BR>to the twice-born classes, see उप-नय; (in the<BR>later language) the sacred thread itself, (originally, it<BR>appears, worn at sacrifices and restricted to the first<BR>three tribes, as explained above; in modern times<BR>assumed by other mixed castes in various parts of<BR>India, as by the Vaidyas or medical caste in Bengal;<BR>according to Manu II. 44, a Brāhman's thread should<BR>be of cotton, a Kṣatriya's of flax or hemp, a Vaiśya's<BR>of woollen thread, and the youths should be invested<BR>at particular ages, see उप-नय and cf. यज्ञ-<BR>सूत्र; this thread is commonly called Janeo, which<BR>is probably corrupted fr. यज्ञोप्˚.)<BR>—यज्ञोपवीत-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, or यज्ञोपवीतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, invested<BR>with the sacred thread; [cf. उपवीतिन्.]<BR>—यज्ञोपा-<BR>सक (˚ञ-उप्˚), अस्, m. an honourer of sacrifices,<BR>one who performs a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0802-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञक
यज्ञक = याजक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञाय
यज्ञाय (fr. यज्ञ), Nom. P. यज्ञायति, -यितुम्,<BR>Ved. to perform a sacrifice or be diligent in sacri-<BR>ficing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञायज्ञिय
यज्ञायज्ञिय, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman, (so called<BR>from the verse Ṛg-veda I. 168, 1, which begins with<BR>यज्ञा-यज्ञा; it is also called Agniṣṭoma-sāman,<BR>from coming at the end of the Agni-ṣṭoma.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञायत्
यज्ञायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. one who performs<BR>a sacrifice or is eager to make offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञारङ्गेशपुरी
यज्ञारङ्गेश-पुरी, f., N. of a town, (perhaps<BR>for यज्ञ-रङ्गेश-पुरी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिक|यज्ञिकः
यज्ञिक, अस्, m. Butea Frondosa; = यज्ञदत्तक,<BR>(see Scholiast on Pāṇ. V. 3, 78; cf. देविक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिन्
यज्ञिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having sacrifices, abounding in<BR>sacrifices [cf. दाक्षायणयज्ञिन्]; (ई), m. epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिय|यज्ञियं|यज्ञियः
यज्ञिय, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of worship or sacrifice,<BR>sharing in sacrifice; sacred, godly, divine, adorable,<BR>(applied to gods and to anything belonging to them,<BR>e. g. the chariot of the Aśvins; also to rivers, &c.);<BR>active or eager in the worship of the gods, skilful in<BR>sacrifice, having a capacity for sacrifice; pious, de-<BR>voted, holy; belonging to worship, relating to a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">Page0804-b+ 79</a>]<BR>sacrifice, suitable or fit for sacrifice, sacrificial; (अस्),<BR>m. a god, deity; N. of the Dvāpara or third Yuga.<BR>—यज्ञिय-देश, अस्, m. ‘sacrificial country,’ the<BR>country of the Hindūs, Hindūstān or that region<BR>in which sacrificial ceremonies can be duly performed,<BR>the country in which the black antelope is native,<BR>see Manu II. 23.<BR>—यज्ञिय-शाला, f. a hall for sacri-<BR>fice, sacrificial hall; a temple, shrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञियत्
यज्ञियत्, Ved. a word used in Śatapatha-Br. IX.<BR>2, 3, 10. to explain अध्वर्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञीय|यज्ञीयः
यज्ञीय, अस्, आ, अम्, suitable or fit for sacrifice,<BR>proper for the performance of a sacrifice, sacrificial;<BR>(अस्), m. the glomerous fig-tree, Ficus Glomerata.<BR>—यज्ञीय-ब्रह्म-पादप, अस्, m. a species of<BR>plant (= विकङ्कत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्य
यज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be worshipped, adorable; to<BR>be sacrificed, &c.; (अम्, आ), n. f. worshipping, sacri-<BR>ficing, in देव-य्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्यमान
यज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, = इज्यमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्यु|यज्युः
यज्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, worshipping, adoring, honour-<BR>ing; devout, pious, godly; taking part in a sacrifice,<BR>an assistant priest at a sacrifice; (उस्), m. an Adhvaryu<BR>priest or one conversant with the Yajur-veda; = य-<BR>जमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्वन्
यज्वन्, आ, अरी, अ (a feminine form in अनी is said<BR>to exist), worshipping, sacrificing; a worshipper,<BR>adorer, honourer; a sacrificer, one who performs<BR>sacrifices in due form or agreeably to the ritual of the<BR>Veda, sacrificial, effective of sacrifices, (Sāy. = याग-<BR>निष्पादक); यज्वनाम् पतिः, N. of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्विन्
यज्विन्, ई, इनी, इ, = यज्वन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टव्य
यष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be worshipped, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टि|यष्टिः
1. यष्टि, इस्, f. (for 2. यष्टि see s.v.), sacrificing,<BR>(perhaps incorrect for 3. इष्टि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टुकाम
यष्टु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring to worship,<BR>wishing or intending to sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टृ
यष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, one who worships or sacri-<BR>fices, a worshipper, sacrificer (= यजमान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यण्व
यण्व यण्व, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यण्वापत्य
यण्वापत्य and यण्वापत्योत्तर, अम्, n., N.<BR>of two Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्|यन्त्
यत् 1. यत्, यन्, यती, यत् (fr. rt. 5. इ),<BR>going, passing, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्|यन्त्
यत् 2. यत् (connected with rt. यम्), cl.<BR>1. A. (Ved. and ep. also P.) यतते (-ति),<BR>येते (3rd pl. येतिरे), यतिष्यते, अयतिष्ट, यति-<BR>तुम्, to join, connect, unite (Ved. P.); to excite,<BR>arouse (Ved. P., according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>36, 2. यतति = यातयति, प्रवर्तयति, he arouses,<BR>animates to exertion); to join or attach one's self to,<BR>unite one's self with, associate with (Ved. A.); to<BR>come together or be arranged in order (Ved. A.);<BR>to proceed, go (Ved.); to try to join one's self with<BR>(with loc.); to endeavour to reach (Ved. A.); to<BR>strive or endeavour after, struggle after, be eager or<BR>anxious for (with loc. or dat. or even acc., or with<BR>one of the following prepositional words, अर्थे,<BR>अर्थाय, अर्थम्, हेतोस्, प्रति, or with the inf.);<BR>to exert one's self, endeavour, take pains, make<BR>effort, persevere, observe caution, be watchful; to<BR>strive against, be engaged in mutual contest, contend<BR>together (Ved.): Caus. यातयति, -यते, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अयीयतत्, to join, connect, associate, unite<BR>(Ved. P.); to join or attach one's self to (Ved. A.);<BR>to join or unite to (Ved. P.); to requite, recompense,<BR>repay, restore, return, give up; to cause to be repaid<BR>or requited or restored; to receive in requital (A.);<BR>to cause to strive or make effort, animate, encourage,<BR>instigate; to cause to contend (Ved.); to pain,<BR>harass, distress, torture, vex, annoy; to reprehend,<BR>despise: Desid. यियतिषते: Intens. यायत्यते,<BR>यायत्ति; [cf. according to some Gr. ζητέω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतत्
यतत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, exerting one's self, striving<BR>after, &c., (in Ṛg-veda V. 48, 5. यतत् = उद्ध-<BR>रत्, extirpating.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतन|यतनं
यतन, अम्, n. the act of making effort or exertion,<BR>an effort, endeavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतनीय
यतनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be exerted or persevered<BR>or striven after; (the neut. may be used impersonally,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">Page0804-c+ 79</a>]<BR>e. g. सदा यतनीयम् मुक्तौ, one must always<BR>strive after final emancipation.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतमान
यतमान, अस्, आ, अम्, striving, endeavouring,<BR>struggling, persevering, making effort, taking pains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतव्य
यतव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. an unused यतु), Ved. =<BR>प्रयत्न-वत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतान
यतान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. uniting or coming to-<BR>gether (in regular order), ranging; proceeding, (Sāy.<BR>= प्रवर्तमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतित
यतित, अस्, आ, अम्, striven, endeavoured, attempted,<BR>tried, striven after, (sometimes with inf. used pas-<BR>sively, e. g. एष त्वया हन्तुं यतितः, he was<BR>attempted to be killed by thee); endeavouring, tak-<BR>ing pains; (the neut. may be used impersonally,<BR>e. g. यतितम् मया गन्तुम्, it was attempted by<BR>me to go, it was my intention to go.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतितव्य
यतितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be strived for or after,<BR>to be endeavoured; (the neut. is used impersonally<BR>with loc., e. g. अर्थार्जने यतितव्यम्, one must<BR>strive for the acquisition of money.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतुन
यतुन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. going, moving, (Sāy. =<BR>गन्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्त
1. यत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see under rt. यम्),<BR>endeavoured, making effort or exertion, taking care,<BR>watchful; prepared, ready; ready for (e. g. रणे<BR>यत्तः, ready for battle, or with an inf.); resolved;<BR>cared for, attended to (as a chariot, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्न|यत्नः
यत्न, अस्, m. effort, endeavour, exertion, energy,<BR>diligence, perseverance, zeal; labour, work, trouble,<BR>pains, difficulty; effort for, endeavour after (with<BR>loc., e. g. परोपकृतौ यत्नः, an effort for the<BR>benefit of another); यत्नं कृ, to make effort,<BR>use exertion, take pains, strive; (एन), ind. with<BR>effort, diligently, vigorously, eagerly, with all one's<BR>might; carefully; (आत्), ind. from effort, with effort,<BR>after great exertions; in spite of every effort; neces-<BR>sarily.<BR>—यत्न-तस्, ind. from effort, diligently, vigo-<BR>rously, eagerly, zealously; carefully.<BR>—यत्न-प्रति-<BR>पाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be explained with difficulty,<BR>difficult, not easy.<BR>—यत्न-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessing energy, making or using effort, energetic,<BR>using exertion, strenuous, laborious, assiduous, perse-<BR>vering, diligent; striving after, taking pains about<BR>(with loc.).<BR>—यत्नवत्-त्व, अम्, n. the state or<BR>condition of making effort, diligence, zealousness.<BR>—यत्नाक्षेप (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m. (in rhetoric) the<BR>making an objection notwithstanding an effort to<BR>repress it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्य
यत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be strived for or after, to<BR>be exerted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत|यतः
यत यत. See under rt. यम्, p. 809.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतम|यतमः
यतम यतम, अस्, आ, अत् (superl. of 3. य or<BR>यद्; see Gram. 236), who or which (of many).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतमथा
यतमथा, ind., Ved. in which of many ways,<BR>(यतमथा कतमथा, in the same way, as<BR>always.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतर|यतरः
यतर, अस्, आ, अत् (compar. of 3. य), who or<BR>which (of two).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतरथा
यतरथा, ind. in which of two ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतस्
यतस् यतस्, ind. (fr. the pronom. base<BR>3. य; correlative of ततस्, q. v., and often used<BR>for the ablative or even instrumental cases यस्मात्,<BR>येभ्यस्, यस्यास्, येन, &c. of the relative pronoun<BR>यद्, but oftener as an adverb or conjunction), from<BR>which, from what, whence; in consequence of<BR>which, for which reason, wherefore; because, since,<BR>whereas, as, for; from which place, wherefrom,<BR>from any place; where, whither, in which direction;<BR>from which time, from which time forward, ever<BR>since, (यतो जाता, from her birth up to the present<BR>time, ever since her birth); that, so that, on con-<BR>dition that; यतो-यतस्, from whichever, from<BR>whatever, from whatever place, from wherever,<BR>whencesoever, wherever, whithersoever; यतस्-ततस्,<BR>from whichever, from which place soever, from this<BR>or that person or place, from any one whatever,<BR>from any place whatsoever, any whither, any where-<BR>soever; यत एव कुतश् च, from this or that place,<BR>from any place whatever; यतः-प्रभृति, whence-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">Page0805-a+ 76</a>]<BR>forward, from which time forward, from what time;<BR>[cf. Gr. ὅ-θε-ν; Slav. jundu-se.]<BR>—यतो-जा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, or यतोद्भव (˚तस्-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>produced from which.<BR>—यतो-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, ori-<BR>ginating in or from which.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0804-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यति|यतिः
यति 1. यति (fr. the pronom. base 3. य;<BR>correlative of तति, q. v.; declined in plur. only, all<BR>the cases except the nom. voc. acc. taking termina-<BR>tions, e. g. inst. यतिभिस्, dat. and abl. यतिभ्यस्,<BR>gen. यतीनाम्, loc. यतिषु, see Gram. 227. a),<BR>as many (= Lat. quot); as often; how many; how<BR>often. (For 2. यति see p. 809, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिथ
यतिथ, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘as maniest, the as manieth;’<BR>[cf. ततिथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिधा
यतिधा, ind., Ved. in as many parts, in as many<BR>ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतीयस
यतीयस यतीयस (?), अम्, n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतुका
यतुका यतुका or यतूका, f. a species of<BR>plant (= रजनी, जननी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतुन
यतुन यतुन. See p. 804, col.3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्कर
यत्कर यत्-कर, यत्-काम, यत्-कारणम्,<BR>यत्-क्रतु, &c. See p. 808, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्न|यत्नः
यत्न यत्न, यत्य, &c. See p. 804, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्र
यत्र यत्र, ind. (fr. the pronom. base 3.<BR>य; correlative of तत्र, q. v., often used for the<BR>loc. cases यस्मिन्, यस्याम्, येषु, &c., but oftener<BR>as an adverb or conjunction), in which place, where,<BR>wherein, wherever, whither; when; whereas, be-<BR>cause, since; that, so that; यत्र यत्र, wherever,<BR>wheresoever, whithersoever, whensoever; यत्र-<BR>तत्र, in any place whatever, anywhere, (यत्र-<BR>तत्र दिने, on any day whatever, on whatever day<BR>you like); यत्र-कुत्र, in any place whatever;<BR>everywhere, in every part; यत्र-कुत्रचित् or यत्र-<BR>कुत्रापि, in whatever place, in some place or other,<BR>in any place whatever, anywhere, in whichever (e. g.<BR>यत्र-कुत्रापि जन्मनि, in whichever birth); य-<BR>त्र-क्वचन or यत्र-क्वापि or यत्र-क्व च or<BR>यत्र-क्व वा, wherever, whithersoever, anywhere,<BR>anywhither; whenever, as often as, every time; at<BR>any time; hither and thither.<BR>—यत्र-कामम्, ind.<BR>wherever it pleases, according to pleasure or wish.<BR>—यत्र-कामावसाय (˚म-अव्˚), अस्, m. the super-<BR>natural power of taking up an abode or transporting<BR>one's self anywhere one likes, (this power is said to<BR>belong to some Yogins.)<BR>—यत्रकामावसायि-ता,<BR>f. or यत्रकामावसायि-त्व, अम्, n. = यत्र-कामा-<BR>वसाय above.<BR>—यत्रकामावसायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>having the power of taking up a residence or trans-<BR>porting one's self anywhere one wishes.<BR>—यत्र-<BR>तत्र-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, lying down anywhere, sleep-<BR>ing anywhere.<BR>—यत्र-सायङ्-गृह or यत्र-सा-<BR>यम्-प्रतिश्रय, अस्, आ, अम्, having or taking up<BR>an abode wherever the evening finds one, spending<BR>the night anywhere where one happens to be.<BR>—य-<BR>त्र-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, where staying, in which place<BR>abiding.<BR>—यत्राकूत (˚र-आक्˚), अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>aim or object in view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्रत्य
यत्रत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, where being, dwelling in<BR>which place, relating to which place, of which place,<BR>whose (used relatively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथऋषि
यथऋषि यथ-ऋषि, यथर्चम्, &c. See<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथा
यथा यथा, ind. (fr. the pronom. base<BR>3. य; correlative of तथा, q. v.), in which manner,<BR>in which way, as, like as, like, (sometimes redun-<BR>dantly connected with इव); as, for example; as truly<BR>as, (in asseverations, followed by तथा or तेन<BR>सत्येन, so truly); that, so that, in order that (with<BR>pot. or not unfrequently with pres. impf. perf. fut.<BR>or aor.; in the earlier language यथा in this sense<BR>is often found after the first word of a sentence);<BR>that, whether, (often used as an introduction to a<BR>direct sentence after verbs of knowing, believing,<BR>hearing, doubting, &c., either with or without इति,<BR>e. g. ज्ञायते यथा राजा तत् करिष्यति, it is known<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-b" target="_blank">Page0805-b+ 81</a>]<BR>that the king will do that; विद्धि यथा सा पुनर्<BR>एष्यतीति, know that she will return); whereas,<BR>since, because; when, as when, as if; as soon as; as<BR>is right or proper (= यथा-वत्); how! (as an<BR>exclamation); यथा — तथा, as — so; as — just so,<BR>(instead of तथा, the other similar correlatives एवम्,<BR>एव, तद्वत्, तद् एवम् are often found in the cor-<BR>responding clause); यथा यथा — तथा तथा, in<BR>whatever manner — in that manner; according as — so;<BR>in whatever degree or proportion — in that degree or<BR>proportion; by how much the more — by so much<BR>the more; यथा-तथा, in whatever manner, in<BR>any manner or way, in every way, as always, as ever;<BR>यथा-कथञ्चित्, in any way, in any manner, any<BR>wise, somehow or other, anyhow; तद् यथा, as<BR>here follows, that is to say, namely, as for example;<BR>यथा-कथा, as much as; यथा-कथा च, now<BR>and then, rarely, unfrequently; यथैव (यथा<BR>एव), just as.<BR>—यथ-ऋषि, ind., Ved. according<BR>to the Ṛṣi (see Gram. 38. h).<BR>—यथर्चम्<BR>(˚था-ऋच्˚), ind. according to the Ṛc.<BR>—यथर्तु<BR>(˚था-ऋतु), ind. according to the season; in accord-<BR>ance with a fixed time, corresponding to the right<BR>season.<BR>—यथर्तुक (˚था-ऋत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, cor-<BR>responding to the season of the year.<BR>—यथर्तु-<BR>पुष्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing flowers or blossoms at<BR>the right season.<BR>—यथर्षि (˚था-ऋषि), ind. =<BR>यथ-ऋषि above.<BR>—यथांश-तस् (˚था-अं˚), ind.<BR>according to shares or portions, in due proportion,<BR>proportionably.<BR>—यथा-कनिष्ठम्, ind. accord-<BR>ing to the youngest, from the youngest to the oldest;<BR>[cf. यथा-ज्येष्ठम्.]<BR>—यथा-कर्तब्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, as proper to be done; (अम्), n. what is right<BR>or proper to be done (under any particular circum-<BR>stances).<BR>—यथा-कर्म, ind. in accordance with<BR>(any) action, according to actions, in accordance with<BR>duties; according to circumstances.<BR>—यथा-कर्म-<BR>गुणम्, ind. in accordance with actions and qualities.<BR>—यथ-कल्पम्, ind. in conformity with ritual<BR>or ceremonial, according to rule or rubric.<BR>—यथा-<BR>काण्डम्, ind. according to Kāṇḍas or chapters.<BR>—यथा-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, conformable to desire,<BR>(acting) according to wish; (अम्), ind. according to<BR>wish, as one likes, at pleasure, agreeably, easily,<BR>comfortably.<BR>—यथाकामार्चितार्थिन् (˚म-अर्˚,<BR>˚त-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, honouring suppliants by conform-<BR>ing to their desires.<BR>—यथा-कामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, acting<BR>according to will or pleasure, independent, wilful,<BR>uncontrolled.<BR>—यथाकाम्य, अम्, n. (probably in-<BR>correct for याथाकाम्य), will, inclination, pleasure.<BR>—यथा-कायम्, ind., Ved. ‘according to body or<BR>form,’ according to the dimensions (of anything).<BR>—यथा-कारम्, ind. according to which way, in<BR>which manner.<BR>—यथा-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, as acting,<BR>acting in which way.<BR>—यथा-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>यथा-कर्तव्य.<BR>—यथा-काल, अस्, m. the proper<BR>time (for anything), a suitable moment, auspicious<BR>time; (अम्), ind. according to time, in due time, at<BR>the proper moment, at the right time.<BR>—यथाकाल-<BR>प्रबोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, watchful in proper seasons,<BR>waking at the right time.<BR>—यथा-कुलधर्मम्,<BR>ind. according to family usage, in conformity with<BR>family customs.<BR>—यथा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, as has<BR>been done, as agreed, made or done according to<BR>rule, done according to custom or agreement, usual,<BR>customary, conventional; (अम्), ind. as happened,<BR>according to usual practice, in the way agreed upon.<BR>—यथा-कृष्टम्, ind., Ved. according to furrows,<BR>furrow. after furrow.<BR>—यथा-कॢप्ति, ind. in a suit-<BR>able or fitting way.<BR>—यथा-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>conforming to a plan or design, forming which plan.<BR>—यथा-क्रमम् or यथा-क्रमेण, ind. accord-<BR>ing to order, in regular order or series, in due suc-<BR>cession, regularly, methodically, successively, in a row,<BR>respectively, in due form, properly.<BR>—यथा-क्रोशम्,<BR>ind., Ved. according to Krośas.<BR>—यथा-क्षमम्,<BR>ind. according to power or ability, as much as pos-<BR>sible.<BR>—यथा-क्षेमेण, ind. with all due safety or<BR>security, safely, comfortably, peaceably.<BR>—यथा-<BR>खातम्, ind., Ved. as dug or excavated.<BR>—यथा-<BR>ख्यम् (˚था-आख्˚), ind. according to names, as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-c" target="_blank">Page0805-c+ 81</a>]<BR>named.<BR>—यथाख्यात (˚था-आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as<BR>previously described or mentioned, before mentioned.<BR>—यथाख्यानम् (˚था-आख्˚), ind. in accordance<BR>with any narrative or statement, according to the cir-<BR>cumstances narrated, as stated.<BR>—यथा-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, as gone, as previously gone; यथागत (˚था-<BR>आग्˚), as come, as one came; as one came (into the<BR>world), without sense, stupid [cf. यथा-जात]; यथा-<BR>गतम् or यथागतेन, ind. by the way one came.<BR>—यथागमम् (˚था-आग्˚), ind. according to tra-<BR>dition, as handed down.<BR>—यथा-गात्रम्, ind., Ved.<BR>according to limbs, limb after limb.<BR>—यथा-गु-<BR>णम्, ind. according to Guṇas or qualities.<BR>—यथा-<BR>गृहम्, ind. according to houses or habitations,<BR>(यान्ति यथा-गृहम्, they go to their respective<BR>homes.)<BR>—यथा-गृहीतम्, ind., Ved. as taken, just<BR>as laid hold of, as, come to hand, in regular order or<BR>succession.<BR>—यथा-गोत्र-कुल-कल्पम्, ind. ac-<BR>cording to the usages of a family or race.<BR>—यथाग्नि<BR>(˚था-अग्˚), ind., Ved. according to (the size of)<BR>the fire.<BR>—यथा-ग्रहणम्, ind., Ved. according<BR>to any statement, conformably to what was men-<BR>tioned.<BR>—यथाङ्गम् (˚था-अङ्˚), ind., Ved. accord-<BR>ing to limbs or members, limb after limb.<BR>—यथा-<BR>चमसम्, ind., Ved. Camasa after Camasa.<BR>—य-<BR>थाचारम् (˚था-आच्˚), ind. according to custom, as<BR>usual, as customary.<BR>—यथा-चारिन् or यथाचारिन्<BR>(˚था-आच्˚), ई, इणी, इ, Ved. as proceeding, as acting.<BR>—यथा-चिन्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, as thought of or con-<BR>sidered, previously considered.<BR>—यथा-चोदितम्,<BR>ind., Ved. according to precept, in conformity with<BR>injunction.<BR>—यथा-छन्दसम्, ind., Ved. accord-<BR>ing to metre, one metre after another.<BR>—यथा-जात,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, just as born; senseless, stupid, foolish, a<BR>natural; barbarous, outcast; (अम्), ind. according to<BR>race or family, family by family.<BR>—यथा-जाति, ind.,<BR>Ved. according to birth, according to kind or class, sort<BR>by sort.<BR>—यथा-जोषम्, ind., Ved. according to<BR>will or pleasure, according to one's satisfaction, (also<BR>read यथा-योषम्.)<BR>—यथाज्ञप्त (˚था-आज्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, as previously enjoined, before directed.<BR>—य-<BR>था-ज्ञानम्, ind. according to knowledge, to the<BR>best of one's knowledge or judgment.<BR>—यथा-<BR>ज्येष्ठम्, ind. according to the oldest, by seni-<BR>ority, according to rank, from the oldest to the<BR>youngest.<BR>—यथा-तत्त्वम्, ind. in accordance with<BR>truth, as the case really is, according to actual fact,<BR>exactly, precisely, strictly, accurately.<BR>—यथा-तथ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, conformable to truth or the exact state<BR>of the case, right, true, accurate; (अम्), ind. in con-<BR>formity with truth or reality; precisely, exactly; as<BR>is becoming or proper, fitly, duly, in a suitable<BR>manner; (अम्), n. a detailed account of events, nar-<BR>rative of particulars.<BR>—यथा-तथ्यम् or यथा-<BR>तथ्येन, ind. in accordance with the truth, really,<BR>truly.<BR>—यथा-तृप्ति, ind. to the heart's content, to<BR>full satisfaction of one's desire.<BR>—यथात्मक (˚था-<BR>आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, according to nature or character,<BR>having which nature.<BR>—यथा-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, as<BR>given.<BR>—यथा-दर्शनम्, ind. according to every<BR>occurrence, in every single case.<BR>—यथा-दायम्,<BR>ind. according to shares or portions.<BR>—यथा-दिक् or<BR>यथा-दिशम्, ind. according to the various quarters<BR>of the sky; in all directions.<BR>—यथादिष्ट (˚था-<BR>आद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as enjoined or directed, correspond-<BR>ing to what has been enjoined, conformable to a<BR>direction; (अम्), ind. in accordance with a direction<BR>or injunction.<BR>—यथा-दीक्षम्, ind. in accordance<BR>with religious observances.<BR>—यथा-दृष्टम् or<BR>यथा-दृष्टि, ind. as seen or observed.<BR>—यथा-<BR>देवतम्, ind., Ved. deity after deity, divinity by<BR>divinity.<BR>—यथा-देश-काल-देहावस्थान-विशे-<BR>षम् (˚ह-अव्˚), ind. according to differences of<BR>place, time, and bodily constitution.<BR>—१. यथा-<BR>देशम्, ind. according to places.<BR>—२. यथादेशम्<BR>(˚था-आद्˚), ind. according to direction or injunction.<BR>—यथा-द्रव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, according to property,<BR>proportioned or conformable to wealth.<BR>—यथा-<BR>धर्मम्, ind. according to duty or right, in proper<BR>form or order.<BR>—यथाधिकारम् (˚था-अध्˚), अम्,<BR>ind. according to authority.<BR>—यथा-धिष्ण्यम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0806-a" target="_blank">Page0806-a+ 81</a>]<BR>ind., Ved. according to the position or arrangement<BR>of the Dhiṣṇya.<BR>—यथाधीत (˚था-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, as read, conformable to the text; (अम्), ind.<BR>according to the text.<BR>—यथाध्यापकम् (˚था-<BR>अध्˚), ind. according to the teacher, agreeably to<BR>the instructions of a teacher.<BR>—यथा-नाम, ind.,<BR>Ved. according to name, name by name.<BR>—यथा-<BR>नारद-भाषित, अस्, आ, अम्, exactly as Nārada<BR>announced, being just as Nārada stated.<BR>—यथा-<BR>निःसृप्तम्, ind., Ved. as gone forth or out.<BR>—य-<BR>था-निरुप्तम्, ind., Ved. as presented or offered.<BR>—यथा-निर्दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, as directed or en-<BR>joined, before mentioned or described, previously<BR>directed.<BR>—यथा-निलयम्, ind. each in its own<BR>resting-place or lair (said of animals).<BR>—यथा-नि-<BR>वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wherever dwelling or abiding.<BR>—यथानीकम् (˚था-अन्˚), ind. according to the<BR>extent of the army, as far as the host extended.<BR>—यथानुपूर्वम् (˚था-अन्˚) or यथानुपूर्-<BR>व्यम् or यथानुपूर्व्या (˚था-आन्˚), ind. according<BR>to a regular series, in regular order or succession,<BR>successively.<BR>—यथानुभूतम् (˚था-अन्˚), ind. ac-<BR>cording to experience, by previous experience.<BR>—य-<BR>थानुरूपम् (˚था-अन्˚), ind. according to form or<BR>rule, in exact conformity, orderly, properly.<BR>—य-<BR>था-न्यस्तम्, ind. as thrown down, as deposited.<BR>—यथा-न्यायम्, ind. according to rule, according<BR>to justice, justly, rightly, fitly, as is fitting or suitable,<BR>properly.<BR>—यथा-न्युप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, as presented<BR>or offered, in the order presented.<BR>—यथा-पण्यम्,<BR>ind. according to the (value of the) wares or com-<BR>modities.<BR>—यथा-पदम्, ind., Ved. according to<BR>the Pada or word.<BR>—यथापराध-दण्ड, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, inflicting punishment in proportion to the crime.<BR>—यथापराधम् (˚था-अप्˚), ind. according to<BR>the offence or error.<BR>—यथा-परु, ind., Ved. ac-<BR>cording to joints, joint after joint, limb by limb.<BR>—यथा-पुरम्, ind. as before, as on previous<BR>occasions.<BR>—यथा-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, being as<BR>before, previous, former; (अम्), ind. as before, as<BR>previously; in succession, one after another.<BR>—य-<BR>था-प्रज्ञम्, ind. according to knowledge.<BR>—य-<BR>था-प्रतिगुणम्, ind. according to qualities, to the<BR>best of one's abilities.<BR>—यथा-प्रतिज्ञम्, ind. ac-<BR>cording to agreement, as settled or arranged.<BR>—य-<BR>था-प्रतिरूपम्, ind., Ved. as is suitable or fitting.<BR>—यथा-प्रत्यर्हम्, ind. according to merit.<BR>—यथा-प्रदिष्टम्, ind. according to direction<BR>or precept, as is suitable or proper.<BR>—यथा-प्र-<BR>देशम्, ind. according to direction or precept, in a<BR>suitable or proper manner; according to place, in<BR>a suitable or proper place, at proper places, on all<BR>sides.<BR>—यथा-प्रधानतस् or यथा-प्रधा-<BR>नम्, ind. according to precedence or superiority,<BR>by rank.<BR>—यथा-प्रयोगम्, ind. according to<BR>usage or practice.<BR>—यथा-प्रश्नम्, ind. in accord-<BR>ance with the question.<BR>—यथा-प्रस्तुतम्, ind.<BR>conformably to the circumstances.<BR>—यथा-प्राणम्,<BR>ind. according to one's whole soul, with all one's<BR>might.<BR>—यथा-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, as obtained or<BR>arrived, in conformity with a particular state or con-<BR>dition, suitable or conformable to circumstances;<BR>(अम्), ind. in conformity with rule, regularly, pro-<BR>perly.<BR>—यथाप्राप्त-स्वर, अस्, m. an accent ac-<BR>cording to rule.<BR>—यथा-प्रार्थितम्, ind. according<BR>to wish, by request.<BR>—यथा-प्रीति, इस्, इस्, इ, in<BR>accordance with love or affection, affectionate, loving.<BR>—यथा-फलम्, ind. according to fruit, when<BR>bearing fruit.<BR>—यथा-बलम्, ind. according to<BR>power, with all one's might, to the best of one's<BR>ability; according to the (condition of the) army,<BR>according to the (number of) forces.<BR>—यथा-बीजम्<BR>= यथा-वीजम्, q. v.<BR>—यथा-बुद्धि, ind. accord-<BR>ing to knowledge, to the best of one's judgment.<BR>—यथा-भक्त्या (भक्त्या, inst. c. of भक्ति),<BR>ind. with full or entire devotion.<BR>—यथा-भक्षि-<BR>तम्, ind. as eaten.<BR>—यथा-भवनम्, ind. ac-<BR>cording to houses, house by house.<BR>—यथा-भा-<BR>गम्, ind. according to shares or portions, according<BR>to the share of each, proportionably; each in his<BR>respective place, in the proper place.<BR>—यथा-भा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0806-b" target="_blank">Page0806-b+ 81</a>]<BR>जनम्, ind., Ved. each in his proper place or posi-<BR>tion.<BR>—यथा-भाव, अस्, m. conformity to any<BR>destined state, destiny; (अस्, आ, अम्,) having which<BR>nature or condition, being of which nature.<BR>—यथा-<BR>भिकामम् (˚था-अभ्˚), ind. according to wish or<BR>desire.<BR>—यथाभिज्ञायम् (˚था-अभ्˚), ind., Ved.<BR>as one has perceived or ascertained.<BR>—यथाभि-<BR>प्रेत (˚था-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as wished or intended;<BR>desired; (अम्), ind. according to one's desire or wish,<BR>agreeably, pleasantly.<BR>—यथाभिमत (˚था-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, as wished, desired, approved; (अम्), ind.<BR>according to wish or will, at pleasure. at will, wher-<BR>ever desire leads one, (सर्वे यथाभिमत-देशं<BR>गताः, they all went to the place that each wished.)<BR>—यथाभिरामम् (˚था-अभ्˚), ind. according to<BR>loveliness, according to the degree of charmingness<BR>(belonging to each).<BR>—यथाभिरुचित (˚था-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, accordant with taste or liking, pleasurable,<BR>agreeable, pleasant, pleasing.<BR>—यथाभिरूपम्<BR>(˚था-अभ्˚), ind. according to Scholiast on Pāṇ. II.<BR>1, 7 = अभि-रूपस्य योग्यम्, according to beauty<BR>of form (?).<BR>—यथाभिलषित (˚था-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, as wished, desired.<BR>—यथाभिलिखित (˚था-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. painted in the manner stated.<BR>—यथाभिवृष्टम् (˚था-अभ्˚), ind., Ved. ac-<BR>cording to the quantity of rain that has fallen.<BR>—य-<BR>थाभिहितम् (˚था-अभ्˚), ind. as spoken.<BR>—यथा-<BR>भीष्ट (˚था-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as wished, liked,<BR>desired, (यथाभीष्ट-दिशं जग्मुह्, they went<BR>to the quarter that each wished.)<BR>—यथा-भूतम्,<BR>ind. in accordance with fact, according to what has<BR>happened; according to the truth.<BR>—यथा-भू-<BR>यसो-वाद (भूयसस्, gen. c. of भूयस्), अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a general rule.<BR>—यथाभ्यर्थित (˚था-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as already requested, previously<BR>asked for.<BR>—यथा-मङ्गलम्, ind., Ved. according<BR>to custom.<BR>—यथा-मति, ind. according to opinion;<BR>to the best of one's judgment.<BR>—यथा-मनीषितम्,<BR>ind. according to wish, by desire or request.<BR>—यथा-<BR>मात्रम्, ind. according to measure or quantity.<BR>—यथा-मानम्, ind. according to measure or<BR>dimensions, according to the circumference.<BR>—य-<BR>था-मुखम्, ind. according to face or appearance,<BR>from face to face.<BR>—यथामुखीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>looking straight at (with gen.).<BR>—यथा-मुख्यम्,<BR>ind. according to the chief (persons), as regards the<BR>chiefs; (एन), ind. by way of precedence or prefer-<BR>ence, before all.<BR>—यथाम्नातम् (˚था-आम्˚) or य-<BR>थाम्नायम् (˚था-आम्˚), ind. in accordance with<BR>sacred tradition; according to the tenour of a sacred<BR>text.<BR>—यथा-यजुस्, ind. according to the Yajus.<BR>—यथायतनम् (˚था-आय्˚), ind., Ved. each in<BR>his own place or abode.<BR>—यथा-यथम्, ind. (fr.<BR>यथा + यथा), in a proper manner, as is fit or proper,<BR>rightly, properly, suitably, fitly; in regular order,<BR>severally, by degrees, gradually.<BR>—यथा-युक्तम् or<BR>यथा-युक्ति or यथायुक्ति-तस्, ind. as is fitting,<BR>in a proper manner, fitly, rightly, suitably, according<BR>to circumstances.<BR>—यथा-यूथम्, ind. according<BR>to herds, by flocks.<BR>—यथा-योगम् or यथा-यो-<BR>गेन, ind. as is fit, in a suitable manner, according<BR>to circumstances, according to requirements; in due<BR>order.<BR>—यथा-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, accordant with<BR>propriety; (अम्), ind. as is fitting or proper, suitably,<BR>properly, fitly.<BR>—यथा-योनि, ind. according to the<BR>womb, according to birth.<BR>—यथारब्ध (˚था-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as begun or commenced, previously<BR>commenced.<BR>—यथारम्भम् (˚था-आर्˚), ind. ac-<BR>cording to the commencement, in regular order or<BR>succession.<BR>—यथा-रसम्, ind. according to the<BR>sentiments.<BR>—यथा-रुचम् or यथा-रुचि, ind. ac-<BR>cording to taste, according to pleasure or liking.<BR>—यथा-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, accordant with (beauty<BR>of) form, having a handsome form, suitable; (अम्),<BR>ind. according to the form or appearance; in a<BR>suitable way, properly, duly; of the same shape or<BR>appearance.<BR>—यथार्थ (˚था-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>accordant with reality, conformable to truth or the<BR>true meaning, agreeing with fact, true, actual, real,<BR>genuine, right, fit, suitable; (अम्), ind. according to<BR>the meaning, conformably to the sense, according to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0806-c" target="_blank">Page0806-c+ 81</a>]<BR>the aim or object, according to truth or fact, suitably,<BR>fitly, truly, really.<BR>—यथार्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>यथार्थ, having a suitable meaning, right, true,<BR>real.<BR>—यथार्थ-तत्त्वम् (i. e. यथा + अर्थ-<BR>त्˚), ind. ‘according to the reality of the matter,’<BR>in accordance with the truth, truly, really.<BR>—य-<BR>थार्थ-तस्, ind. in accordance with the truth,<BR>truly, rightly, fitly.<BR>—यथार्थ-ता, f. suitableness,<BR>fitness, rectitude, propriety, genuineness, the state of<BR>appearing to the greatest advantage (Kirātārj. VIII.<BR>49).<BR>—यथार्थ-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking fitly<BR>or truly.<BR>—यथार्थ-वर्ण, अस्, m. ‘having a true<BR>colour or appearance,’ a spy, secret emissary; [cf.<BR>यथार्ह-वर्ण]<BR>—यथार्थाक्षर (˚थ-अक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, significant in every syllable, of which<BR>the letters or syllables express the true sense.<BR>—य-<BR>थार्थित (˚था-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as asked, pre-<BR>viously asked.<BR>—यथार्थित्वम् (˚था-अर्˚), ind.<BR>according to design or purpose.<BR>—यथार्पित (˚था-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as delivered.<BR>—यथार्ह (˚था-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as deserving, according to merit,<BR>corresponding to desert, as is fit or right, appropriate,<BR>suitable, just, adequate; (अम्), ind. according to<BR>merit or worth, agreeably to propriety, suitably, fitly.<BR>—यथार्हणम् (˚था-अर्˚), ind. according to<BR>merit or worth; according to propriety.<BR>—यथार्ह-<BR>तस्, ind. according to worth or merit, according to<BR>propriety, as is proper or suitable, justly.<BR>—यथार्ह-<BR>वर्ण, अस्, m. ‘having a suitable appearance,’ a spy,<BR>secret agent.<BR>—यथा-लब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, as ob-<BR>tained or met with, as found at first, previously<BR>found.<BR>—यथा-लाभम्, ind. according to what one<BR>finds, just as it happens to occur; according to gain<BR>or profit.<BR>—यथा-लिङ्गम्, ind., Ved. according to<BR>characteristic marks or tokens.<BR>—यथा-लोकम्, ind.,<BR>Ved. according to room or place.<BR>—यथावकाशम्<BR>(˚था-अव्˚), ind. according to room or space; in the<BR>proper place; according to opportunity or leisure, on<BR>the first opportunity, as occasion or leisure may<BR>occur.<BR>—यथा-वत्, ind. according to propriety, as<BR>is fitting, duly, becomingly, properly, rightly, suitably,<BR>precisely, exactly, truly; according to law; as (=<BR>यथा).<BR>—यथावद्-ग्रहण, अम्, n. right com-<BR>prehension.<BR>—यथा-वयस् or यथा-वयसम्, ind.<BR>according to age, of the same age.<BR>—यथा-वर्णम्,<BR>ind. according to caste, by caste.<BR>—यथा-वर्ण-<BR>विधानम्, ind. according to the rules or laws of<BR>caste.<BR>—यथा-वशम्, ind., Ved. according to<BR>pleasure or inclination.<BR>—यथावसरम् (˚था-अव्˚),<BR>ind. according to opportunity, as occasion may re-<BR>quire, on every occasion.<BR>—यथा-वस्तु, ind. accord-<BR>ing to the state of the matter, precisely, exactly,<BR>accurately, strictly.<BR>—यथावस्थम् (˚था-अव्˚), ind.<BR>according to state or condition; according to circum-<BR>stances, each according to his own circumstances.<BR>—यथावासम् (˚था-आव्˚), ind. according to dwell-<BR>ings, each to his own abode.<BR>—यथा-वास्तु, ind.<BR>in accordance with the site or ground.<BR>—यथा-<BR>वित्तम्, ind. by virtue of (the right of) property<BR>(Ved.); according to possession, in proportion to<BR>power or substance.<BR>—यथा-विद्यम्, ind. according<BR>to knowledge.<BR>—यथा-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of which<BR>kind or sort (= Lat. qualis); of such a kind or<BR>sort, such as.<BR>—यथा-विधानम् or यथा-विधा-<BR>नेन, ind. according to prescription or rule, by<BR>order.<BR>—यथा-विधि, ind. according to direction<BR>or precept, according to rule, duly, fitly, suitably,<BR>(in Hari-vaṃśa 7138. यथा-विधिम् occurs on ac-<BR>count of the metre.)<BR>—यथा-विभवम्, ind. accord-<BR>ing to power or ability, in proportion to property or<BR>resources.<BR>—यथा-वीजम्, ind. according to the seed<BR>or germ.<BR>—यथा-वीर्यम्, ind. according to strength<BR>or vigour, in respect of manliness or courage.<BR>—य-<BR>था-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, as happened or occurred, as<BR>ensued; as done, as acted; (अम्), n. a previous occur-<BR>rence or event; the circumstances or details of an<BR>event, (अवेदयद् यथा-वृत्तम्, he related the<BR>details of the occurrence, he told exactly how it<BR>happened); (अम्), ind. according to the occurrence<BR>or event, according to all the circumstances, circum-<BR>stantially, truly; according to the metre.<BR>—यथा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0807-a" target="_blank">Page0807-a+ 81</a>]<BR>वृत्तान्त (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. an event or<BR>adventure just as it occurred.<BR>—यथा-वृत्ति, ind.<BR>according to way or mode of life.<BR>—यथा-वृद्-<BR>धम्, ind. according to age or seniority.<BR>—यथा-<BR>वृद्धि, ind. according to increase, in accordance<BR>with the waxing (of the moon, &c.).<BR>—यथा-व्य-<BR>वहारम्, ind. conformably to custom, according to<BR>usage.<BR>—यथा-व्याधि, ind. according to the (nature<BR>of a) disease or sickness.<BR>—यथा-व्युत्पत्ति, ind.<BR>according to the view propounded; according to the<BR>etymology.<BR>—यथा-शक्ति or यथा-शक्त्या, ind.<BR>according to power or ability, to the utmost of one's<BR>power, as far as possible.<BR>—यथाशयम् (˚था-आश्˚),<BR>ind. according to intention or wish; according to<BR>stipulation.<BR>—यथा-शरीरम्, ind. according to<BR>body, body by body.<BR>—यथा-शास्त्रम्, ind. accord-<BR>ing to the Śāstras or sacred codes of law, according<BR>to the precepts of science, as the law ordains.<BR>—य-<BR>थाशास्त्रानुसारिन् (˚र-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, observing<BR>the Śāstras or scriptures, following the precepts of<BR>the sacred codes of law.<BR>—यथा-शीलम्, ind. in con-<BR>formity with character, agreeably to disposition.<BR>—यथा-श्रद्धम्, ind. according to inclination<BR>(Ved.); according to faith, in all faith, in all fidelity,<BR>confidently, confidingly.<BR>—यथाश्रमम् (˚था-आश्˚),<BR>ind. according to the Āśrama or period of life, (see<BR>आश्रम.)<BR>—यथाश्रयम् (˚था-आश्˚), ind. accord-<BR>ing to the connection or dependance (of anything),<BR>according to the mode of connection (of one thing<BR>with another).<BR>—यथा-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, corres-<BR>ponding to (what has been) heard, agreeing with a<BR>report; (अम्), n. a corresponding or suitable tra-<BR>dition; (अम्), ind. as heard, as reported, according<BR>to report; according to sacred precept or injunction,<BR>according to Vedic precept.<BR>—यथा-श्रुति, ind. ac-<BR>cording to revealed precept, in accordance with the<BR>injunctions of sacred books, conformably to the pre-<BR>cepts of the Veda.<BR>—यथा-श्रेष्ठम्, ind. in order<BR>of merit (so that the best is placed first); in order of<BR>precedence.<BR>—यथा-संस्थम्, ind. according to<BR>circumstances.<BR>—यथा-संहितम्, ind. in accord-<BR>ance with the Saṃhitā.<BR>—यथा-सख्यम्, ind. ac-<BR>cording to friendship.<BR>—यथा-सङ्कल्पित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, corresponding to wish, in accordance with (a<BR>proposed) plan, answering expectations.<BR>—यथा-<BR>सङ्ख्य, ‘Relative order,’ a figure in rhetoric which<BR>separating each verb from its immediate subject so<BR>arranges verbs with verbs and subjects with subjects<BR>that each may answer to each; (अम्, एन), ind. ac-<BR>cording to number, number for number (so that in<BR>two rows composed of similar numbers the several<BR>terms of one row correspond with those of the other).<BR>—यथा-सङ्गम्, ind. according to need or exi-<BR>gence, as required, suitably, so as to adapt (itself),<BR>opportunely.<BR>—यथा-सत्यम्, ind. in accordance<BR>with truth, agreeably to the reality.<BR>—यथासनम्<BR>(˚था-आस्˚), ind., Ved. each in proper place or seat,<BR>according to proper position.<BR>—यथा-सन्दिष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, as agreed or directed; (अम्), ind. accord-<BR>ing to direction or order.<BR>—यथा-सन्धि, ind., Ved.<BR>according to Sandhi.<BR>—यथा-समयम्, ind. ac-<BR>cording to agreement, according to established cus-<BR>tom; according to time, at the proper time.<BR>—य-<BR>था-समाम्नातम्, ind. as repeated, according to<BR>what has been mentioned.<BR>—यथा-सम्पद्, ind.,<BR>Ved. according to the event, as may happen.<BR>—य-<BR>था-सम्प्रत्ययम्, ind. according to agreement.<BR>—यथा-सम्प्रदायम्, ind. according to tra-<BR>dition, in accordance with traditional teaching or<BR>usage.<BR>—यथा-सम्बन्धम्, ind. according to<BR>relationship.<BR>—यथा-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, accord-<BR>ant with possibility, possible; (अम्), ind. compatibly,<BR>according to the previous order, successively.<BR>—यथा-<BR>सम्भविन्, ई, इनी, इ, or यथा-सम्भावित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, compatible, corresponding, suitable, appropriate.<BR>—यथा-सवनम्, ind. according to the order of<BR>the Savana (Ved.); according to the time, at the<BR>proper season.<BR>—यथा-साम, ind., Ved. according to<BR>the order of the Sāman.<BR>—यथा-सामर्थ्यम्, ind.<BR>according to ability or power.<BR>—यथा-सारम्, ind.<BR>according to quality or goodness.<BR>—यथा-सिद्ध,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0807-b" target="_blank">Page0807-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, as effected; just as prepared, just as<BR>cooked (said of food).<BR>—यथा-सुखम्, ind. ac-<BR>cording to ease or pleasure, at ease, at will or pleasure,<BR>comfortably, agreeably, pleasantly, happily.<BR>—य-<BR>थासुख-मुख, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having the face<BR>turned in any direction one pleases.<BR>—यथा-स्तुत्,<BR>ind., Ved. according to the order of the Stut, Stut by<BR>Stut.<BR>—यथा-स्तुतम् or यथा-स्तोमम्, ind., Ved.<BR>according to the order of the Stoma.<BR>—यथा-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. the right or proper place; (अस्, आ, अम्), each<BR>in proper place, arranged in order; (अम्, ए), ind.<BR>according to place, each according to the right place,<BR>all in regular order, according to rank, in order,<BR>properly, suitably; instantly.<BR>—यथा-स्थाम, ind.,<BR>Ved. in the proper place, in regular order (= यथा-<BR>स्थानम्).<BR>—यथा-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, accordant<BR>with circumstances, standing properly; right, proper,<BR>fit, true; (अम्), ind. according to place or circum-<BR>stances; in statu quo; properly, truly, certainly,<BR>assuredly.<BR>—यथा-स्थिति, ind. in accordance with<BR>usage or custom, as usual, as on previous occasions.<BR>—यथा-स्मृति, ind. according to recollection, ac-<BR>cording to the precepts of the law-books.<BR>—यथा-<BR>स्मृति-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, as remembered, as fixed in<BR>the memory.<BR>—यथा-स्व, अस्, आ, अम्, each accord-<BR>ing to (his, her, their) own, every one his own;<BR>(अम्), ind. each on (his, her, their) own account,<BR>each for himself or in his own way, individually,<BR>properly.<BR>—यथा-स्वैरम्, ind. according to incli-<BR>nation or wish, at pleasure, freely, independently.<BR>—यथाहार (˚था-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having suit-<BR>able food, eating anything that comes in the way.<BR>—यथेक्षितम् (˚था-ईक्˚), ind. according to what<BR>was actually seen, as beheld with one's own eyes.<BR>—यथेच्छ (˚था-इच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, agreeable to<BR>wish or desire; (आ), f. a suitable wish or desire;<BR>यथेच्छया, inst. c. according to wish, at will or<BR>pleasure; (अम्), ind. according to wish or desire, at<BR>pleasure, ad libitum, agreeably, pleasantly.<BR>—यथेच्-<BR>छकम्, ind. = यथेच्छम् above.<BR>—यथेतम्<BR>(˚था-एत्˚), ind., Ved. as happened, as it turned out,<BR>(also written यथैतम्.)<BR>—यथेपसया (˚था-ईप्˚),<BR>ind. according to wish or inclination, at pleasure.<BR>—यथेप्सित (˚था-ईप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as wished,<BR>agreeable to wish or expectation, wished for, desired;<BR>(अम्), ind. according to wish or desire, agreeably to<BR>fancy, agreeably, pleasantly, spontaneously, ad libitum,<BR>wantonly.<BR>—यथेष्ट (˚था-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as<BR>wished or desired, agreeable to wish, accordant with<BR>desire, wished for, desired, loved, dear; (अम्), ind.<BR>according to wish or inclination, at pleasure, plea-<BR>santly, agreeably; carelessly; according to sacrifice<BR>(Ved.; in this sense fr. 2. इष्ट).<BR>—यथेष्ट-गति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, or यथेष्ट-चारिन् or यथेष्ट-सञ्चारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, going according to will or inclination, going<BR>where one wishes, independent, free; (ई), m. a bird.<BR>—यथेष्ट-तस्, ind. according to inclination or<BR>wish, at pleasure, independently.<BR>—यथेष्टाचार<BR>(˚ट-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, doing what one likes, unre-<BR>strained, licentious.<BR>—यथेष्टासन (˚ट-आस्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, sitting down as one likes.<BR>—यथैतम् =<BR>यथेतम् above.<BR>—यथोक्त (˚था-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>as said or spoken, as told or directed, previously told<BR>or prescribed, enumerated before, above mentioned;<BR>(अम्), ind. according to what has been stated, as<BR>mentioned before, as previously described or related;<BR>यथोक्तेन, in the above mentioned way.<BR>—य-<BR>थोक्त-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking as told, reporting<BR>accurately what has been said.<BR>—यथोचित (˚था-<BR>उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, accordant with propriety or equity,<BR>proper, fit, suitable, becoming; (अम्), ind. suitably, fitly,<BR>properly.<BR>—यथोत्तर (˚था-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, follow-<BR>ing in regular order or succession, succeeding one an-<BR>other; (अम्), ind. in regular order or succession, one after<BR>another.<BR>—यथोत्साहम् (˚था-उत्˚), ind. according to<BR>power or ability, with all one's might.<BR>—यथोदय<BR>(˚था-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. next following; (अम्),<BR>ind. according to means or circumstances, in propor-<BR>tion to one's income.<BR>—यथोदित (˚था-उद्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, as said or spoken, previously told, before stated,<BR>above mentioned; (अम्), ind. as mentioned before<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0807-c" target="_blank">Page0807-c+ 80</a>]<BR>or above, according to a previous statement.<BR>—य-<BR>थोद्गत (˚था-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as arisen; as one<BR>came (into the world), without sense, childlike,<BR>stupid; [cf. यथागत.]<BR>—यथोद्दिष्ट (˚था-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as indicated or described, before<BR>mentioned; (अम्), ind. in the manner stated, in the<BR>above mentioned way.<BR>—यथोद्देशम् (˚था-उद्˚),<BR>ind. according to direction, in the manner pointed<BR>out.<BR>—यथोद्भवम् (˚था-उद्˚), ind. according to<BR>rise or origin.<BR>—यथोपजोषम् (˚था-उप्˚), ind.<BR>according to inclination or pleasure, according to<BR>desire.<BR>—यथोपदिष्ट (˚था-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as<BR>specified or indicated, as stated, before mentioned;<BR>(अम्), ind. in the manner above mentioned or pre-<BR>viously described.<BR>—यथोपदेशम् (˚था-उप्˚), ind.<BR>according to advice or suggestion, according to in-<BR>structions or orders.<BR>—यथोपपत्ति (˚था-उप्˚), ind.<BR>according to the event or occasion, as may happen.<BR>—यथोपपन्न (˚था-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as happened,<BR>occurring naturally, unconstrained, natural.<BR>—यथो-<BR>पपादम् (˚था-उप्˚), ind., Ved. as may occur or<BR>happen.<BR>—यथोपमा (˚था-उप्˚), f. (in rhetoric)<BR>a comparison expressed by यथा.<BR>—यथोपयोगम्<BR>(˚था-उप्˚), ind. according to use or need, according<BR>to requirements or circumstances.<BR>—यथोपस्मारम्<BR>(˚था-उप्˚), ind., Ved. according to recollection, as<BR>one may happen to remember.<BR>—यथोपाधि (˚था-<BR>उप्˚), ind. according to the condition or limitation,<BR>according to the supposition.<BR>—यथोप्त (˚था-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, as sown, in proportion to the seed sown.<BR>—यथौकसम् (˚था-ओक्˚), ind., Ved. each accord-<BR>ing to (his) abode.<BR>—यथौचित्य (˚था-औच्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a corresponding or suitable way; यथौचित्यात्,<BR>in a suitable manner, fitly, suitably; (अम्), ind. accord-<BR>ing to propriety, properly, fitly, duly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्
यद् यद्, यस्, या, यद् (the actual base of<BR>this relative pronoun is य, except in compounds<BR>and in the derivative यदीय; its proper correlative<BR>is तद्, q. v., but other demonstrative pronouns and<BR>pronominals, such as एतद्, इदम्, अदस्, तादृश,<BR>ईदृश, सर्व, often occur in the correlative clauses;<BR>see 3. य), who, which, what, that, whoever, which-<BR>ever, whatever, any. The relative यद् often pre-<BR>cedes the noun to which it refers, this noun being<BR>either put in the same case with the relative or<BR>joined with the demonstrative (e. g. यस्य नरस्य<BR>बुद्धिः स बलवान् or यस्य बुद्धिः स नरो<BR>बलवान्, of whatever man there is intellect he is<BR>strong); sometimes the relative stands alone, an<BR>antecedent noun or pronoun being understood from<BR>which it takes its gender and number (e. g. ध-<BR>नेन किं यो न ददाति, what is the use of wealth<BR>[to him] who does not give?); or the relative itself<BR>may be dropped (e. g. न करोत्य् अ-कार्यं तम्<BR>आर्यम् आहुः, they call him honourable [who] does<BR>nothing improper to be done). Sometimes the rela-<BR>tive यद्, with or without its demonstrative, appears<BR>to be used redundantly to eke out the metre, or<BR>perhaps to give force to the noun with which it is<BR>connected, even the neut. sing. being occasionally<BR>thus used in connection with words of a different<BR>gender and number, and the relative being itself<BR>almost untranslatable (e. g. यन् मरणं सो ऽस्य<BR>विश्रामः, that very death is his rest; अन्धो जडः<BR>पीठ-सर्पी सप्तत्या स्थविरश्-च यः, a blind<BR>man, an idiot, a cripple, and a man seventy years<BR>old; यत् क्षान्तिः समये श्रुतिः शिव शिवेत्य्-<BR>उक्तिर् मनो-निर्वृतिर् असौ मुक्ति-मार्गे स्थितिः,<BR>forbearance, obedience to ordinances, saying ‘Śiva,<BR>Śiva,’ contentment of mind, this is continuance on the<BR>road of emancipation); and sometimes this redundant<BR>or emphatic use of यद् causes a sudden change of<BR>construction from accusative to nominative (e. g.<BR>अपोहेत रसान् अश्मनो लवणं चैव पशवो<BR>ये च, he should avoid liquids, stones, and salt, and<BR>all cattle). The relative यद् is often repeated to<BR>express ‘whoever,’ ‘whatever,’ ‘whichever,’ &c. (e. g.<BR>यो यः, whatever man; या या, whatever woman;<BR>यद् यद्, whatever thing; यो यो यावतिथः,<BR>whichever [is] how many soever degrees, i. e. in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-a" target="_blank">Page0808-a+ 81</a>]<BR>proportion as each of which is advanced in the series);<BR>or the repetition of यद् may be caused by a kind of<BR>attraction, the second relative being equivalent to<BR>an indefinite pronoun (e. g. यो यस्य भावः स्यात्,<BR>whatever may be the disposition of any one; यद्<BR>रोचते यस्मै, whatever is pleasing to any one);<BR>or the relative may be used to express similar inde-<BR>finite meanings when joined with कश्चित्, कश्चन,<BR>को ऽपि, कश्च, को वा (e. g. यः कश्चित् or यः-<BR>कश्चन, whosoever; यत् किञ्चित् or यत् किञ्च,<BR>whatsoever; येन केनाप्य् उपायेन, by any means<BR>whatsoever; यानि कानि च मित्राणि, any friends<BR>whatsoever; यस्मै कस्मै च, to any one what-<BR>ever; यस्मिन् कस्मिन् वा देशे, in any country<BR>whatever); or even with a demonstrative pronoun<BR>(e. g. यस्मै तस्मै, to any one whatever; यस्-<BR>मात् तस्मात्, from any one, from this or that per-<BR>son; येन तेन कर्मणा, by any act whatever);<BR>or sometimes the relative यद् is used alone with the<BR>indefinite sense ‘any one,’ &c. (e. g. स्त्रियं स्पृ-<BR>शेद् यः सङ्ग्रहणं स्मृतम्, should any one<BR>touch a woman it is called an adulterous act; याम्<BR>अजां वृको हन्यात् पाले तत् किल्विषम् भवेत्,<BR>if a wolf kill any she-goat the blame must be on the<BR>keeper). यद् is also connected in a peculiar manner<BR>with the personal pronouns, which, when placed<BR>immediately after the relative, appear to derive force<BR>or emphasis from this juxtaposition (e. g. यो ऽहम्,<BR>I that very person who; यस् त्वम्, thou that very<BR>one who, &c.). यद् in the neut. sing. is used as<BR>an adverbial conjunction equivalent to ‘for which<BR>reason,’ ‘on which account,’ ‘wherefore,’ ‘since,’<BR>‘as,’ ‘because,’ ‘when,’ ‘while,’ ‘if,’ ‘with regard<BR>to,’ ‘as to,’ &c.; or still oftener as a simple con-<BR>junction meaning ‘that,’ especially after the verbs of<BR>saying, hearing, &c., or such words as काम, युक्त,<BR>आश्चर्य, &c. (e. g. धीवरैर् उक्तं यत् — , it was<BR>said by the fishermen that — ; श्रुतं त्वया यत् — ,<BR>it has been heard by thee that — ; आश्चर्यं यत् — ,<BR>it is a wonder that — ); frequently followed by a verb<BR>in the indicative (e. g. अयं नूतनो न्यायो यद्<BR>अरातिं हत्वा सन्तापः क्रियते, this is a new<BR>doctrine that having killed an enemy remorse is expe-<BR>rienced); less frequently in the potential (e. g. एष<BR>मे कामो यत् स राज्यम् आप्नुयात्, this is my desire<BR>that he may obtain the kingdom); यद् अपि, although;<BR>यच्-च, that (according to Pāṇ. III. 3, 148, with<BR>potential, after expressions of impossibility, disbelief,<BR>hope, disregard, reproach, and wonder, e. g. न<BR>श्रद्-दधे यच्-च तत्र-भवान् वृषलं या-<BR>जयेत्, I do not believe that your Highness will allow<BR>a Śūdra to sacrifice); यद् वा, or, or else, whether,<BR>(in the writings of commentators यद् वा generally<BR>occurs when an alternative reading or meaning is<BR>proposed, and may commonly be translated by ‘or,’<BR>‘or else’): in philosophical writings यः is said to<BR>be used as a synonymn for पुरुषः: [cf. Zend<BR>ya: Gr. ὅ-ς, ἥ, ὅ, ἵνα, ὡς: Goth. ja-bai, ‘if;’ jau,<BR>‘whether:’ Lith. ji-s, ‘he;’ ji, ‘she;’ ju, ‘it:’<BR>Slav. i, ja, je.]<BR>—यच्-छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having<BR>which metre.<BR>—यच्-छील, अस्, आ, अम् (यद् + शील),<BR>having which disposition.<BR>—यत्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>which doing or undertaking.<BR>—यत्-काम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. which desiring, wishing which.<BR>—यत्-<BR>काम्या, ind., Ved. with which view or design.<BR>—यत्-कारणम् or यत्-कारणात्, ind. for which<BR>cause or reason, on which account, in consequence<BR>of which; since, because, as, while.<BR>—यत्-कारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, which doing or undertaking.<BR>—यत्-किञ्चे-<BR>दम् (˚च-इदम्), the commencement of the sacred<BR>text Ṛg-veda VII. 89, 5, (incorrectly read यत्-<BR>किञ्चिदम्.)<BR>—यत्-कृते, ind. on account of which,<BR>for which reason, wherefore, why.<BR>—यत्-क्रतु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. having which resolution, forming which<BR>plan.<BR>—यद्-अभावे, ind. in the absence of which,<BR>for want of which, in default of which.<BR>—यद्-<BR>अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, having which object in view, hav-<BR>ing which intention; (अम्, ए), ind. on which account,<BR>for which purpose, for the sake of which, wherefore,<BR>why, &c.; as, since, when, because, whereas.<BR>—यद्-<BR>आत्मक, अस्, इका, अम्, having which being or exist-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-b" target="_blank">Page0808-b+ 81</a>]<BR>ence.<BR>—यद्-ऋच्छा, f. acting as one lists, following<BR>one's own inclination, self-will, spontaneity, wilful-<BR>ness, independence, (according to native lexicogra-<BR>phers = स्वैरिता, स्वेच्छा, स्वाच्छन्द्य, निर्नि-<BR>मित्त); accident, an accidental occurence or event,<BR>chance, contingence, (यद्-ऋच्छया, as one likes,<BR>of one's own accord, spontaneously, by accident,<BR>accidentally, incidentally, by chance, unexpectedly);<BR>(in grammar) a noun which is neither a generic nor<BR>specific term nor noun of agency, one either not<BR>derived from authority or not possessing meaning.<BR>—यदृच्छा-तस्, ind. spontaneously, by accident,<BR>&c. (= यद्-ऋच्छया above).<BR>—यदृच्छाभिज्ञ<BR>(˚छा-अभ्˚), अस्, m. a voluntary or self-offered<BR>witness.<BR>—यदृच्छा-लाभ-तुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>satisfied with obtaining what comes spontaneously,<BR>easily satisfied.<BR>—यदृच्छा-संवाद, अस्, m. acci-<BR>dental or spontaneous conversation, incidental inter-<BR>course.<BR>—यदृच्छिक, अस्, m., scil. पुत्र, a son<BR>who offers himself for adoption.<BR>—यद्-देवत or<BR>यद्-देवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having which god-<BR>head or divinity.<BR>—यद्-द्वन्द्व, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR>—यद्-धेतोस्, ind. (धेतोस् for हेतोस्, abl. c.<BR>of हेतु), from which reason or cause, on which<BR>account.<BR>—यद्-भविष्य, अस्, m. one who says<BR>‘what will be,’ or ‘what must be must be,’ one who<BR>believes in the power of fate; a fatalist; N. of a fish<BR>(in the Hitopadeśa).<BR>—यद्रियञ्च् or यद्र्यञ्च्,<BR>अङ्, द्रीची, अक् (fr. यद् with अद्रि substituted for अद्<BR>and rt. अञ्च्; cf. मद्र्यञ्च्), Ved. moving or turn-<BR>ing in which direction, extending to which point,<BR>reaching whither or to what place or in which di-<BR>rection, (incorrectly written यद्रञ्च्, यद्द्रञ्च्.)<BR>—यद्-वत्, ind. in which way, as, (used as a corre-<BR>lative of तद्-वत् and एवम्.)<BR>—यद्-वद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, talking anything, talking nonsense, saying no<BR>matter what.<BR>—यद्वाहिष्ठीय, अम्, n. (fr. यद्<BR>वाहिष्ठम्, the first two words of Ṛg-veda V.<BR>25, 7), N. of a Sāman.<BR>—यद्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>which sort (= Lat. qualis).<BR>—यद्-वृत्त, अम्, n.<BR>anything which has occurred, an adventure; any form<BR>of यद्.<BR>—यन्-निमित्तम्, ind. on which account,<BR>for which reason, in consequence of which, through<BR>which.<BR>—यन्मंहिष्ठीय, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—यन्-मध्ये, ind. in the centre of which.<BR>—यन्-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed or consisting of which.<BR>—यन्-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having which measure,<BR>of which dimensions or circumference, &c.<BR>—यन्-<BR>मूर्धन्, आ, m. the head of whom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0807-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद
यद = यद् above, (occurring only in the form<BR>यदम् at the end of an adverbial comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदा
यदा, ind. at what time, when, whenever, (gene-<BR>rally followed in the correlative clause by तदा or<BR>ततस् or तर्हि or in Ved. by आद् इत्); whereas,<BR>since, as; if; यदा यदा, whenever; यदा तदा,<BR>at any time whatsoever; यदा यदा — तदा तदा,<BR>as often as — so often; यदैव — तदैव, when<BR>indeed — then indeed; यदा प्रभृति — तदा प्र-<BR>भृति, from whatever time — from that time forward;<BR>यदा-कदा-च, Ved. as often as, whenever; यदा-<BR>कदा-चित्, at any time; न यदा-कदा-चित्, never<BR>at any time; यदा is sometimes joined in the same<BR>sentence with other relatives used indefinitely (e. g.<BR>यो ऽत्ति यस्य यदा मांसम्, when any one eats<BR>the flesh of any one).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदि
यदि, ind. (in Ved. sometimes lengthened to यदी),<BR>if, in case that; whether; if haply, if perchance; pro-<BR>vided that, when. As a conjunction meaning ‘if,’<BR>यदि is sometimes joined with the present indicative<BR>(e. g. यदि जीवति भद्राणि पश्यति, if he live he<BR>will behold prosperity); sometimes with the poten-<BR>tial (e. g. यदि राजा दण्डं न प्रणयेत्, if the<BR>king were not to inflict punishment; or with omis-<BR>sion of यदि, e. g. वृको हन्याद् अजाम्, if a wolf<BR>should kill a goat); sometimes with the future (e. g.<BR>यदि न करिष्यन्ति तत्, if they will not do that);<BR>sometimes with the aorist or even imperfect or perfect<BR>(e. g. यदि प्रजा-पतिर् न वपुर् अस्राक्षीत्, if<BR>the Creator had not created the body; यद्य् एतन्<BR>न मे ऽकथयत्, if he were not to tell me that;<BR>यद्य् आह, if he had said); sometimes with the con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">Page0808-c+ 75</a>]<BR>ditional (e. g. यद्य् अनुज्ञाम् अदास्यत्, if he should<BR>give permission); sometimes यदि may be translated<BR>by ‘that’ (e. g. नाशंसे यदि जीवन्ति, I do not<BR>expect that they are alive); rarely यदि is joined<BR>redundantly with चेद् (e. g. यदि चेत् स्यात्, if it<BR>should be); or with पुरा (e. g. पुरा यदि पश्यामि,<BR>before that I see); यद्य्-अपि, even if, although,<BR>(followed by तथापि, q. v., or तदपि in the corre-<BR>lative clause); यदि वा, or if, or whether; or else, or;<BR>or rather (= अथ वा); यदि — यदि वा, यदि वा —<BR>यदि वा, यदि वा — वा, if — or if, whether — or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदीय|यदीयं
यदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to whom, whose,<BR>belonging to which or what, (यदीय-करुणात्,<BR>from whose favour.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदावाजदावर्य
यदावाजदावर्य यदावाजदावर्य, N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदु|यदुः
यदु यदु, उस्, m., N. of an ancient hero<BR>(often mentioned in the Veda together with Turvaśa<BR>or Turvasu, and described as preserved by Indra during<BR>an inundation, see Ṛg-veda I. 174, 9); N. of a son<BR>of Yayāti, (in the later mythology Yadu and Puru<BR>are both sons of Yayāti, the fifth monarch of the<BR>lunar dynasty, Kṛṣṇa being descended from Yadu<BR>[cf. यदु-नाथ below], and both Bharata and<BR>Kuru, the ancestor of the Pāṇḍu princes, being<BR>descended from Puru; Yadu is also described as a<BR>brother of Turvasu); N. of a son of Vasu (king of<BR>Cedi); of a son of Hary-aśva; (according to some)<BR>N. of a country on the west of the Jumna river,<BR>about Mathurā and Vṛndā-vana, over which Yadu<BR>ruled, (according to other authorities the kingdom<BR>of Yadu is the Dakṣiṇa or peninsula of India);<BR>(अवस्), m. pl. the family and descendants of Yadu<BR>[cf. यादव]; = दशार्हाः, q. v.<BR>—यदु-कुलोद्वह<BR>(˚ल-उद्˚) or यदूद्वह, अस्, m. ‘supporter of the<BR>family of Yadu,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यदु-ध्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—यदु-नाथ, अस्, or यदु-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the Yadus,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यदु-पुङ्गव, अस्, m. a chief of the Yadus.<BR>—यदु-वंश, अस्, m. the family of Yadu.<BR>—य-<BR>दु-वीर-मुख्य, अस्, m. ‘leader of the heroes of<BR>Yadu,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यदु-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m.<BR>‘best of the Yadus,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदृच्छा
यदृच्छा यद्-ऋच्छा, यद्-धेतोस्, यद्-वत्,<BR>&c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्यपि
यद्यपि यद्य्-अपि. See under यदि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्रियञ्च्
यद्रियञ्च् यद्रियञ्च्, यद्र्यञ्च्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्वा
यद्वा यद्वा, f. = बुद्धि, perception, mind,<BR>intelligence (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्तव्य
यन्तव्य यन्तव्य, यन्ति, यन्तृ, &c. See<BR>p. 809, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र्|यंत्र्
यन्त्र् यन्त्र् (more properly regarded as<BR>a Nom. fr. यन्त्र, p. 809, col. 2, cf.<BR>यन्त्रय), cl. 1. 10. P. यन्त्रति, यन्त्रयति,<BR>&c., to restrain, curb, check, bind, fasten, confine;<BR>to strain; to force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रण|यंत्रण|यंत्रणं|यन्त्रणं
यन्त्रण, अम्, n. the act of restraining, control-<BR>ling, curbing, checking, binding, fastening, confining;<BR>restraint, restriction, limitation, (आहार-यन्त्रण,<BR>restriction in diet); a means of fastening, bond,<BR>bandage; the application of a bandage (also आ, f.);<BR>constraint, compulsion, force, torturing, pain, anguish,<BR>(in these senses also आ, f.); guarding, protecting,<BR>protection; (ई), f. a wife's younger sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रित|यंत्रित|यन्त्रितः
यन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, restrained, curbed, checked;<BR>bound, fastened, fettered, confined; bound by, sub-<BR>ject to; one who strains every nerve, one who<BR>makes exertions or takes pains.<BR>—यन्त्रित-कथ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, restrained in speech, constrained to be<BR>silent.<BR>—यन्त्रित-सायक, अस्, m. one who has fixed<BR>an arrow (in a kind of self-acting bow or machine<BR>which discharges itself when touched).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र|यंत्र|यंत्रं|यन्त्रं
यन्त्र यन्त्र, यन्त्रय, यन्त्रिन्, &c. See<BR>p. 809, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्मय
यन्मय यन्-मय, यन्-मात्र. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0808-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यभ्
यभ् यभ्, cl. 1. P. यभति, ययाभ,<BR>यप्स्यति, अयाप्सीत्, यब्धुम्, to know<BR>carnally, have sexual intercourse with, lie with:<BR>Desid. A. यियप्सते, to desire sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यभन|यभनं
यभन, अम्, n. copulation, sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यभ्य
यभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be carnally known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियप्स्यमान
यियप्स्यमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Desi.), desir-<BR>ing to be carnally known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम्
यम् यम् (connected with rt. 2. यत्),<BR>cl. 1. P. यच्छति (Ved. and ep. also A.<BR>यच्छते, Ved. also यमति, -ते), ययाम (2nd<BR>sing. ययन्थ or येमिथ, 3rd pl. P. येमुस्, 3rd<BR>sing. A. येमे, 3rd pl. येमिरे, Part. A. येमान),<BR>यंस्यति, अयंसीत् (Vedic forms are यमत्, यंसि,<BR>यमुस्, यन्धि, यन्त, यन्तम्, यंसत्, यंसन्,<BR>अयांसम्, अयान्, अयांसि, यंसते, अयंसत), यन्-<BR>तुम्, यमितुम् (Ved. यमम्, यन्तवे, यमि-<BR>तवै), to sustain, support, hold up, maintain (Ved.);<BR>to support one's self (A., Ved.); to raise, hold up,<BR>lift up (Ved.); to raise (a sound, &c., Ved.); to<BR>stretch out, extend, spread (Ved.); to keep in, hold<BR>back, restrain, check, stop, rein, curb, tame, govern,<BR>control, regulate, suppress; to offer, present, grant,<BR>bestow, confer, give to any one (with loc. or dat.); to<BR>present with anything (inst., Ved.); to offer or resign<BR>one's self, give one's self up to (A., Ved.); to dis-<BR>play, exhibit (Ved.); to go, approach (Ved.): Pass.<BR>यम्यते, अयामि, to be raised or lifted up, &c.<BR>(Ved.); to be held back or restrained, &c.; to be<BR>offered, &c.: Caus. यमयति, (or according to<BR>others) यामयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अयीयमत्, to cause<BR>to hold back or restrain, &c.; to restrain, hold in,<BR>check, keep in order, control; to offer, give, present,<BR>serve with (food, &c.); Desid. यियंसति: Intens.<BR>यंयम्यते, यंयमीति, यंयन्ति; [cf. Gr. ζημία,<BR>ἡνία, ἥμερος: Lat. jejunus, frœna, emo (for<BR>sumo), sub-imo, demo (for de-imo): Lith. immu,<BR>‘to take:’ Slav. imami: Russ. imaju: Hib. iomai-<BR>nim, ‘I drive, force, compel;’ iomain, ‘a driving.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यच्छत्
यच्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, restraining, controlling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यच्छमान
यच्छमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. stretching out,<BR>extending; distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत|यतः
यत, अस्, आ, अम्, restrained, held in, curbed,<BR>kept in check, governed, &c.; limited, moderate,<BR>temperate; (अम्), n. the spurring or guiding of an<BR>elephant by means of the rider's feet.<BR>—यत-गिर्,<BR>ईर्, ईर्, ईर्, one who restrains speech, keeping silence;<BR>[cf. यत-वाच्.]<BR>—यतङ्-कर, अस्, m., Ved. one<BR>who regulates, a regulator, (Sāy. = यमन-कर्तृ.)<BR>—यत-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one who controls the<BR>thoughts or restrains the feelings, subdued in mind.<BR>—यतचित्तात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, one who con-<BR>trols the soul and spirit, of subdued or well-governed<BR>mind.<BR>—यत-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, restraining or con-<BR>trolling anger.<BR>—यत-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, = यत-<BR>चित्त above.<BR>—यत-मैथुन, अस्, आ, अम्, abstain-<BR>ing from sexual intercourse or restraining all desire<BR>for it.<BR>—यत-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having well<BR>held or guided reins.<BR>—यतवाक्-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being restrained in speech, reticence.<BR>—यत-<BR>वाच्, क्, क्, क्, restraining speech, observing silence,<BR>reticent.<BR>—यत-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, observing vows,<BR>keeping to engagements, holding to any promised<BR>observance.<BR>—यत-स्रुच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. raising or<BR>lifting up the sacrificial ladle, stretching out or extend-<BR>ing the ladle; [cf. उद्यत-स्रुच्.]<BR>—यतात्मन् (˚त-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, self-restrained, restraining or curbing<BR>the soul, governing one's self.<BR>—यतात्म-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having a subdued mind, self-restrained.<BR>—य-<BR>ताहार (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, abstaining from food,<BR>temperate in eating, abstemious.<BR>—यतेन्द्रिय (˚त-<BR>इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the organs of sense restrained,<BR>of subdued passions, chaste, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यति|यतिः
2. यति, इस्, f. (for 1. see p. 805, col. 1), restraint,<BR>control, check; guidance; stopping, ceasing, rest,<BR>term; a pause (in music); cæsura (in prosody); a<BR>widow, (in this sense also यती; cf. यतिनी); (इस्),<BR>m. an ascetic, devotee, one who has restrained his<BR>passions and abandoned the world; N. of a mythical<BR>race of ascetics (connected with the Bhṛgus and,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">Page0809-b+ 81</a>]<BR>according to one legend, said to have taken part in<BR>the creation of the world); N. of a son of Brahmā;<BR>of a son of Nahuṣa; of a son of Viśvāmitra; (with<BR>Jainas) N. of a class of ascetics; N. of Śiva; =<BR>निकार.<BR>—यति-चान्द्रायण, अम्, n., N. of a par-<BR>ticular kind of penance (Manu XI. 218).<BR>—यति-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of a Yati or ascetic.<BR>—यति-<BR>धर्म, अस्, m. the duty of an ascetic or devotee.<BR>—यति-धर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a son of Śva-phalka.<BR>—यतिधर्म-समुच्चय, अस्, m., N. of a work<BR>on the duties of ascetics.<BR>—यति-पञ्चक, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of five stanzas on the subject of ascetics.<BR>—यति-<BR>पात्र, अम्, n. an ascetic's vessel, a wooden vessel<BR>for collecting alms, (sometimes a hollow bamboo or<BR>an earthen bowl or a gourd is used for that purpose.)<BR>—यति-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, wanting the cæsura<BR>(in grammar or prosody).<BR>—यति-मैथुन, अम्, n.<BR>the copulation or cohabitation of devotees, the un-<BR>chaste life of ascetics.<BR>—यति-वर्य, अस्, m., N.<BR>of the author of a commentary on Śiro-maṇi's<BR>Dīdhiti.<BR>—यति-विलास, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यति-<BR>सान्तपन, अम्, n., N. of a particular kind of<BR>penance, (a पञ्च-गव्य lasting for three days.)<BR>—यत्य्-अनुष्ठान-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a trea-<BR>tise on the duties of ascetics by Śaṅkara Ānanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिन्
यतिन्, ई, m. = 2. यति, an ascetic; (इनी), f. a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यती
यती. See under 2. यति, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्त
2. यत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 804, col. 3), =<BR>यत, col. 1, (occurring rarely in ep. poetry, and only<BR>when required by the exigency of metre.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्वा
यत्वा, ind. having restrained, having curbed or<BR>controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्तव्य
यन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be held in or restrained; to<BR>be checked or controlled, to be guided or managed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्ति
यन्ति, इस्, f., see Pāṇ. VI. 4, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्तुरम्
यन्तुरम्, acc. sing. m., in Ṛg-veda III. 27, II,<BR>VIII. 19, 2. explained by Sāy. as an irregularity for<BR>यन्तारम्, and used as an epithet of Agni (= सर्-<BR>वस्य नियन्तारम्, regulator of all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्तृ|यंतृ
यन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, restraining, controlling; guid-<BR>ing, directing, &c.; one who restrains, a governor,<BR>ruler, director, manager, a guider, driver (of a chariot,<BR>waggon, &c.); an elephant driver or rider; fixing,<BR>one who fixes or makes fast (Ved.); giving, a giver<BR>(Ved.); in Naighaṇṭuka III. 19. यन्तारस् is enu-<BR>merated among the याच्ञाकर्माणस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र|यंत्र|यंत्रं|यन्त्रं
यन्त्र, अम्, n. a means or instrument for holding<BR>or restraining or fastening anything, a prop, support,<BR>stay, fence, barrier; a fetter, band, fastening, tie,<BR>thong, cord, rein, trace, harness; a surgical instru-<BR>ment (especially any blunt instrument, such as<BR>tweezers, a vice, &c., opposed to शस्त्र); any<BR>instrument, machine, engine, implement, apparatus,<BR>vessel, appliance, (कूप-यन्त्र, a machine for draw-<BR>ing water from a well; cf. जल-य्˚, तैल-य्˚, गोल-<BR>य्˚); a lock, bolt, &c.; restraining, restraint, con-<BR>straint, force, (यन्त्रेण, forcibly, violently); an<BR>amulet, a diagram of a mystical nature or astrological<BR>character used as an amulet.<BR>—यन्त्र-करण्डिका,<BR>f. a kind of magical basket.<BR>—यन्त्रकर्म-कृत्,<BR>त्, m. a person who makes instruments or machines,<BR>a machinist, artisan.<BR>—यन्त्र-गरुड, अस्, m. an<BR>image of Garuḍa mechanically contrived to move by<BR>itself.<BR>—यन्त्र-गृह, अम्, n. an oil-mill; a manu-<BR>factory.<BR>—यन्त्र-गोल, अस्, m. a kind of pea.<BR>—यन्त्र-चेष्टित, अम्, n. any magical work or<BR>operation, enchantment.<BR>—यन्त्र-तक्षन्, आ, m.<BR>a constructer of machines, maker of instruments; a<BR>preparer of charms or spells.<BR>—यन्त्र-दृढ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, secured by a lock or bolt (as a door).<BR>—यन्-<BR>त्र-धारा-गृह, अम्, n. a room fitted up with a<BR>kind of shower-bath, a bath-room with flowing water;<BR>[cf. धारा-गृह.]<BR>—यन्त्र-नाल, अम्, n. a me-<BR>chanical pipe or tube, the pipe of a well.<BR>—यन्त्र-<BR>पुत्रक, अस्, इका, m. f. a mechanical doll or puppet<BR>fitted with strings or any contrivance for moving the<BR>limbs.<BR>—यन्त्र-पेषणी, f. a hand-mill.<BR>—यन्त्र-<BR>प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a work (attributed to<BR>Madana-pāla).<BR>—यन्त्र-प्रवाह, अस्, m. an arti-<BR>ficial stream of water, machine for watering.<BR>—यन्-<BR>त्र-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of a machine, arti-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-c" target="_blank">Page0809-c+ 79</a>]<BR>ficially made or constructed.<BR>—यन्त्र-मातृका, f.,<BR>N. of one of the sixty-four Kalās.<BR>—यन्त्र-मार्ग,<BR>अस्, m. an aqueduct, canal.<BR>—यन्त्र-मुक्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, thrown by any kind of machine (said of wea-<BR>pons).<BR>—यन्त्र-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with<BR>(all necessary) implements or apparatus, (यन्त्र-<BR>युक्ता नौः, a boat fitted out with oars, sails, &c.)<BR>—यन्त्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing or furnished<BR>with a machine.<BR>—यन्त्र-शर, अस्, m. a missile<BR>shot off by machinery.<BR>—यन्त्र-सूत्र, अम्, n. the<BR>cord attached to a jointed doll or puppet.<BR>—यन्त्रा-<BR>कार (˚र-आक्˚) and यन्त्रोद्धर (˚र-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of two works.<BR>—यन्त्रारूढ (˚र-आर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fixed or mounted on the revolving engine<BR>(of the universe).<BR>—यन्त्रालय (˚र-आल्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a printing-office, press.<BR>—यन्त्रोत्क्षिप्तोपल (˚र-<BR>उत्˚, ˚त-उप्˚), अस्, m. a stone shot off by a machine<BR>(sling, ballista, &c.).<BR>—यन्त्रोपल (˚र-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a mill-stone, mill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रक|यंत्रक|यन्त्रकं|यंत्रकः|यन्त्रकः
यन्त्रक, अस्, इका, अम्, restraining, a restrainer,<BR>tamer, subduer; (अस्), m. one acquainted with instru-<BR>ments or machinery, a maker of instruments or<BR>machines, machinist, artisan; (अम्), n. a bandage<BR>(in medicine); a turner's wheel, lathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रय
यन्त्रय, Nom. P. यन्त्रयति, -यितुम्, to bind,<BR>confine, restrain, (see rt. यन्त्र्); to put on bandages,<BR>&c.; to place in splints, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रिन्|यंत्रिन्
यन्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having or furnished with har-<BR>ness or trappings (said of a horse); furnished with an<BR>amulet; tormenting, a tormentor, harasser, painer;<BR>(इणी), f. a wife's younger sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम|यमः
यम, अस्, m. a rein, curb, bridle (Ved.); a<BR>driver, charioteer (Ved.); restraining, controlling,<BR>taming, keeping in check, restraint, (वाचां यमः,<BR>restraint of words, silence); self-control, any great<BR>moral duty or observance, (as opposed to नियम,<BR>a minor duty or observance, see Manu IV. 204;<BR>some of the Yamas are as follow, ‘restraining the<BR>organs of sense,’ ‘chastity, and the control of all<BR>sensual desires,’ ‘refraining from violence or injury,’<BR>‘patience,’ ‘truthfulness,’ ‘honesty’); a twin, one of<BR>a pair or couple, a fellow, (यमौ, ‘the twins,’ an<BR>epithet of the Aśvins and of their twin children by<BR>Mādrī, called Nakula and Sahadeva); a symbolical<BR>expression for the number two; N. of the god who<BR>presides over the Pitṛs, q. v., and rules the spirits of<BR>the dead, (he is regarded in Post-vedic mythology<BR>as the appointed Judge and ‘Restrainer’ or Punisher<BR>of the dead, in which capacity he corresponds to the<BR>Greek Pluto and to Minos; he is one of the eight<BR>guardians of the world as regent of the South quarter,<BR>in which direction in some region of the lower<BR>world is his abode, called Yama-pura; thither a soul,<BR>when it leaves the body, is said to repair, and there,<BR>after the recorder, Citra-gupta, has read an account<BR>of its actions kept in a book called Agra-sandhānī,<BR>it receives a just sentence, either ascending to heaven<BR>or to the world of the Pitṛs or being driven down<BR>to one of the twenty-one hells [called the awful<BR>provinces of the kingdom of Yama] to be born<BR>again, after undergoing its appointed recompense<BR>of bliss or pain, in higher or lower forms of being;<BR>in unison with these functions Yama is sometimes<BR>called ‘king of Justice’ or simply ‘Justice’ [see<BR>धर्म-राज, धर्म], sometimes ‘Rod-bearer’<BR>or ‘Noose-bearer’ [see दण्ड-धर, पाशिन्], some-<BR>times ‘lord of the Pitṛs or Manes’ [see पितृ-पति],<BR>sometimes ‘king of Death’ or simply ‘Death’ [see<BR>मृत्यु-राज्, मृत्यु, काल, अन्तक], sometimes<BR>‘god of the Śrāddha’ [see श्राद्ध-देव]: in the<BR>Vana-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata, 1. 16754, where<BR>there is a story of his appearing to a dying man, he<BR>is described as dressed in blood-red garments, with<BR>a glittering form, a crown on his head, glowing<BR>eyes, and, like Varuṇa, holding a noose, with which<BR>he binds the spirit after drawing it from the body,<BR>in size about the measure of a man's thumb: he is<BR>otherwise represented as grim in aspect, green in<BR>colour, clothed in red, riding on a buffalo, and<BR>holding a club in one hand and noose in the other:<BR>he is said to possess two four-eyed watch-dogs, called<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-a" target="_blank">Page0810-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Karbura [= Cerberus?], ‘spotted,’ and Śyāma,<BR>‘dark,’ which guard the road to his abode: in the<BR>later mythology he is always represented as a terrible<BR>deity inflicting tortures, called यातना, on departed<BR>souls: according to some the earlier legends point<BR>to the original meanings of his name being ‘twin,’<BR>and make him a kind of first man, Yama and his<BR>twin sister Yamī being the first pair of beings<BR>born from Vivasvat, ‘the Sun,’ and his wife Sa-<BR>raṇyū; the seventh Manu, another form of the first<BR>man, being also born from the Sun, and so regarded<BR>as a brother of Yama, [see especially Ṛg-veda X. 10,<BR>part of which is ascribed to the authorship of Yama<BR>Vaivasvata, and cf. वैवस्वत]; Yama is, how-<BR>ever, described as resisting sexual alliance with his<BR>sister; Yama is also regarded as the regent of<BR>the Nakṣatra Apabharaṇī or Bharaṇī, see यम-<BR>देवता); N. of the author of a hymn to Viṣṇu;<BR>of the author of a Dharma-śāstra; of the planet<BR>Saturn, (Saturn being regarded as the son of Vivasvat<BR>and Chāyā); of one of Skanda's attendants (men-<BR>tioned together with Ati-yama); a crow [cf. यम-<BR>दूतक]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of deities with<BR>Buddhists; (ई), f., N. of Yama's twin sister, who is<BR>identified in Post-vedic mythology with the river<BR>goddess Yamunā; (अम्), n. a pair, brace, couple;<BR>(in gram.) the twin letter of any consonant, (when a<BR>nasal consonant follows immediately after one of the<BR>four other consonants in each class, the consonant<BR>preceding the nasal may be doubled, and the inter-<BR>posed letter is then called its यम or twin, thus in<BR>क्क्ङ्, the interposed क् is a यम; but this inter-<BR>posed letter is generally understood, and not written<BR>in practice); pitch of the voice, tone of utterance,<BR>key; (अस्, आ or ई, अम्), twin-born, twin, double,<BR>coupled, paired.<BR>—यम-कालिन्दी, f., N. of Sañjñā<BR>(wife of the Sun and, according to one account,<BR>mother of Yama).<BR>—यम-किङ्कर, अस्, m. Yama's<BR>servant, a messenger of death.<BR>—यम-कीट, अस्, m.<BR>a wood-louse; an earth-worm.<BR>—यम-कील, अस्,<BR>m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यम-केतु, उस्, m. Yama's<BR>ensign or mark; a sign of death.<BR>—यम-कोटि, इस्,<BR>or यम-कोटी, f., N. of a mythical town (fabled<BR>by astronomers to be situated 90° or 1235 Yojanas<BR>east of Laṅkā).<BR>—यम-क्षय, अस्, m. Yama's<BR>abode.<BR>—यम-गाथा, f. a verse or hymn treating<BR>of Yama.<BR>—यम-गीत, अम्, n. ‘the hymn of Yama<BR>(in praise of Viṣṇu),’ N. of the seventh chapter of<BR>the third book of the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa, in which Yama<BR>instructs his ministers to keep clear of the worshippers<BR>of Viṣṇu, that god's votaries being admitted by him<BR>to be exempt from his authority.<BR>—यम-घाण्ट,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an astronomical Yoga.<BR>—यम-घ्न,<BR>अस्, m. ‘destroying Yama or death,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—यम-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, twin-born; (अस्),<BR>m. a twin; (औ), m. du. twins.<BR>—यम-जात or<BR>यम-जातक, अस्, आ, अम्, = यम-ज above.<BR>—य-<BR>म-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of Yama,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—यम-जिह्वा, f. ‘Yama's tongue,’ N. of a pro-<BR>curess (in Kathā-sarit-s. LVII. 59).<BR>—यम-तर्-<BR>पण, अम्, n. presenting libations to Yama on the<BR>fourteenth day of the dark half of the month Āśvina.<BR>—यम-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—यम-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the being Yama, the name Yama.<BR>—यम-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m., N. of an Asura; of a<BR>Rākṣasa; of a warrior on the side of the gods;<BR>(आ), f. Yama's tooth, (यमदंष्ट्रान्तरं ग-<BR>तः, one who has fallen into the jaws of Yama or<BR>Death); (आस्), f. pl. the last eight days of the month<BR>Āśvina and the whole of Kārttika considered as a<BR>period of general sickness.<BR>—यम-दण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>Yama's rod.<BR>—यम-दूत, अस्, m. Yama's messenger<BR>or minister (employed to bring the souls of the dead<BR>to Yama's judgment-seat, and thence conduct them<BR>to their final destination); a crow (as boding evil<BR>or death); (ई), f., N. of one of the nine Samidhs.<BR>—यम-दूतक, अस्, m. Yama's messenger or<BR>minister; a crow; (इका), f. Indian tamarind.<BR>—य-<BR>म-देवता, f., N. of the lunar asterism Bharaṇī<BR>as presided over by Yama, (also अम्, n.)<BR>—यम-<BR>दैवत, अस्, आ, अम्, having Yama for lord or ruler.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-b" target="_blank">Page0810-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—यम-द्रुम, अस्, m. ‘Yama's tree,’ Bombax<BR>Heptaphyllum.<BR>—यम-द्वितीया, f., N. of the second<BR>day in the light half of the month Kārttika (when<BR>brothers and sisters dress up and exchange gifts^1 and<BR>compliments in allusion to the attachment of Yama<BR>and his sister Yamī; cf. भ्रातृ-द्वितीया).<BR>—यम-<BR>द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of an island.<BR>—यम-धानी, f.<BR>Yama's dwelling or abode.<BR>—यम-धार, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of double-edged weapon.<BR>—यम-नक्षत्र,<BR>अम्, n. Yama's asterism or lunar mansion, (see above<BR>under यम.)<BR>—यम-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing Yama as a guide or leader.<BR>—यम-पाश, अस्,<BR>m. the snare or noose of Yama.<BR>—यम-पुर, अम्,<BR>n. the city or abode of Yama, (see above under<BR>यम.)<BR>—यम-पुरुष, अस्, m. Yama's servant or<BR>minister.<BR>—यम-प्रस्थ-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town, where Yama was especially worshipped.<BR>—य-<BR>म-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, dear to Yama, beloved by<BR>Yama; (अस्), m. the Indian fig-tree, Ficus Indica.<BR>—यम-भगिनी, f. ‘Yama's sister,’ the river Ya-<BR>munā or Jumna.<BR>—यम-मार्ग, अस्, m. Yama's<BR>road or path.<BR>—यममार्ग-गमन, अम्, n. the<BR>going or entering on Yama's road, receiving the<BR>recompense for one's actions.<BR>—यम-यातना, f.<BR>the torment or torture inflicted by Yama.<BR>—यम-<BR>रथ, अस्, m. ‘Yama's vehicle,’ i. e. a buffalo.<BR>—य-<BR>म-राज्, ट्, m. king Yama.<BR>—यम-राज, अस्, m.<BR>king Yama; N. of a physician.<BR>—यम-राजन्, आ,<BR>m. king Yama; (आ, आ, अ), Ved. having Yama as<BR>king, subject to Yama.<BR>—यम-राज्य or यम-<BR>राष्ट्र, अम्, n. Yama's kingdom, the dominion of<BR>Yama.<BR>—यमर्क्ष (˚म-ऋक्˚), अम्, n., Ved. a<BR>lunar mansion or asterism supposed to be under<BR>Yama or Saturn.<BR>—यम-लोक, अस्, m. Yama's world,<BR>the region of Yama.<BR>—यम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessing restraint, one who governs himself or keeps<BR>the passions in subjection, self-restrained, temperate,<BR>moderate.<BR>—यम-वत्सा, f., Ved. a cow bearing<BR>twin calves.<BR>—यम-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘Yama's vehi-<BR>cle,’ i. e. a buffalo.<BR>—यम-विषय, अस्, m. Yama's<BR>realm or empire.<BR>—यम-व्रत, अम्, n. a religious<BR>observance or vow made to Yama; Yama's method<BR>or manner (i. e. punishing offences without regard<BR>to persons or without partiality, as one of the duties<BR>of kings, see Manu IX. 307); N. of a Sāman.<BR>—यम-शिख, अस्, m., N. of a Vetāla.<BR>—यम-<BR>श्राय, अस्, m. the residence or place of resort of Yama,<BR>the Southern quarter.<BR>—यम-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>among whom Yama is the chief or takes precedence<BR>(said of the Pitṛs).<BR>—यम-श्व, अस्, m. Yama's<BR>dog, (see under यम.)<BR>—यम-सदन, अम्, n.<BR>Yama's seat or abode.<BR>—यम-सभ, अस्, आ, m.<BR>f. Yama's council or court of justice, the tribunal<BR>of Yama.<BR>—यमसभीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to<BR>Yama's court of justice.<BR>—यम-सात्, ind. to the<BR>power of Yama; यमसात् कृ, to make over to<BR>Yama, deliver over to the god of death; यमसात्<BR>कृत, made over to or devoted to Yama, sent to<BR>Yama.<BR>—यम-सादन, अम्, n. Yama's seat or<BR>abode (= यम-सदन).<BR>—यम-सू, ऊस्, f. bring-<BR>ing forth twins; (ऊस्), m. Yama's father, the Sun.<BR>—यम-सूक्त, अम्, n., Ved. a hymn in honour<BR>of Yama.<BR>—यम-सूर्य, अम्, n. a building with<BR>two halls or porches, one with a western, the other<BR>with a northern aspect.<BR>—यम-स्तोम, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an Ekāha.<BR>—यम-स्वसृ, सा, f. ‘Yama's sister,’<BR>N. of the river Yamunā (commonly called Jumna); N.<BR>of Durgā.<BR>—यम-हार्दिका, f., N. of one of Devī's<BR>female attendants.<BR>—यम-हासेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚स-<BR>ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—यमातिरात्र (˚म-<BR>अत्˚), अस्, m., Ved., N. of a Sattra of forty-nine days<BR>duration.<BR>—यमादर्शन-त्रयोदशी (˚म-अद्˚),<BR>f., N. of a particular thirteenth lunar day.<BR>—यमा-<BR>दर्शनत्रयोदशी-व्रत, अम्, n. a religious observ-<BR>ance on the above day, (those who perform this are<BR>said to be exempted from seeing Yama.)<BR>—यमा-<BR>दित्य (˚म-आद्˚), अस्, m. a particular form of the<BR>sun.<BR>—यमानुग (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, following<BR>Yama, being in attendance on Yama.<BR>—यमानु-<BR>चर (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. a servant or attendant of<BR>Yama.<BR>—यमान्तक (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. Yama (re-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">Page0810-c+ 81</a>]<BR>garded) as the destroyer or god of death [cf. कालान्-<BR>तक]; ‘Yama's destroyer,’ N. of Śiva; (औ), m.<BR>du. Yama and the god of death.<BR>—यमारि (˚म-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. ‘Yama's enemy,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—य-<BR>मालय (˚म-आल्˚), अस्, m. Yama's abode.<BR>—यमेश<BR>(˚म-ईश), अस्, आ, अम्, having Yama as lord or<BR>chief; (अम्), n. the Nakṣatra Bharaṇī.<BR>—यमे-<BR>श्वर (˚म-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0809-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमक|यमकं|यमकः
यमक, अस्, m. restraint, check, &c., = यम,<BR>(in this sense, according to some, अम्, n.); = व्रत,<BR>a religious obligation or observance; a twin, one of<BR>a pair or couple, a fellow; scil. स्नेह, two similar<BR>greasy substances, oil and ghee; (अम्), n. (in medi-<BR>cine) a double band or bandage; (in artificial poetry)<BR>the repeating or setting in opposition in the same<BR>stanza of words or syllables different in meaning but<BR>similar in sound, a kind of play on words or parono-<BR>masia, (the following kinds are enumerated, युक्-<BR>पाद-यमक, अ-युक्-पाद-य्˚, आद्यन्त-य्˚, पा-<BR>दादि-य्˚, पाद-मध्य-य्˚, पादान्त-य्˚, पादादि-<BR>मध्य-य्˚, पादाद्यन्त-य्˚, मध्यान्त-य्˚, काञ्-<BR>ची-य्˚, गर्भ-य्˚, चक्रवाल-य्˚, पुष्प-य्˚, महा-<BR>य्˚, मिथुन-य्˚, वृत्त-य्˚, विपथ-य्˚, समुद्ग-<BR>य्˚, सर्व-य्˚, यमकावली-य्˚); N. of a kind of<BR>metre, four times ˘˘˘˘˘; a couple of similar<BR>substances (as serum and marrow, oil and ghee); (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), twin, twin-born, fellow, doubled, twofold.<BR>—यमक-काव्य, अम्, n., N. of an artificial poem<BR>ascribed to Ghaṭa-karpara.<BR>—यमक-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being a Yamaka, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमन|यमनं|यमनः
यमन, अस्, ई, अम्, restraining, curbing, taming,<BR>governing, managing; (अस्), m. the god Yama;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of restraining or holding, curbing;<BR>binding; the being restrained, stopping, ceasing,<BR>term, cessation, rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमल|यमलं|यमलः
यमल, अस्, आ, अम्, twin, one of a pair or couple,<BR>paired, doubled; (अस्), m. a term for the number<BR>two; (औ), m. du. twins, a pair, couple, brace; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of hiccough; N. of a Tantra deity; of a<BR>river; (ई), f. a pair; a sort of dress consisting of<BR>two pieces (body and petticoat); (अम्), n. a pair.<BR>—यमल-शान्ति, इस्, f. a purificatory ceremony<BR>after the birth of twins.<BR>—यमलार्जुन (˚ल-अर्˚),<BR>औ, m. du. two Arjuna trees which obstructed the<BR>path of Kṛṣṇa, when a child, and were uprooted<BR>by him, (according to Hari-vaṃśa 3449, his foster-<BR>mother Yaśo-dā had tied him to an उलूखल or<BR>large wooden mortar, but such was the strength of<BR>the child that he not only dragged away the mortar<BR>but the twin Arjuna trees with which it came in<BR>contact; these trees were afterwards personified as<BR>the enemies of Kṛṣṇa, and in the later mythology<BR>they are regarded as metamorphoses of Nala-kūbara<BR>and Maṇi-grīva, two sons of Kuvera.)<BR>—यमलार्-<BR>जुनक (˚ल-अर्˚), औ, m. du. = यमलार्जुन.<BR>—यमलार्जुन-भञ्जन, अस्, m. or यमलार्-<BR>जुन-हन्, आ, m. epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—यमलोद्भव (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, m. the birth of<BR>twins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसान
यमसान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. champing the bit,<BR>holding the reins or bridle; (Sāy. = तृणादिकं<BR>नियच्छत्, holding or champing grass, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमानिका
यमानिका or यमानी, f. Ptychotis Ajowan; [cf.<BR>क्षेत्र-य्˚, यवानिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमाय
यमाय, Nom. A. यमायते, -यितुम्, to repre-<BR>sent or be like Yama, the god of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमिक
यमिक, अम्, n., with अगस्त्यस्य, N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमित
यमित, अस्, आ, अम्, restrained, checked, curbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमिन्
यमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, restraining, curbing, controlling;<BR>(ई), m. one who restrains himself, a sage who has sub-<BR>dued his senses; (इनी), f., Ved. bringing forth twins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमिष्ठ
यमिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. guiding or managing<BR>best, most skilful in restraining or guiding (horses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुना
यमुना, f., N. of a river, commonly called<BR>the Jumna (personified as Yamī, the twin sister of<BR>Yama, q. v., and hence regarded as daughter of the<BR>Sun as well as sister of the seventh Manu or Manu<BR>Vaivasvata; this celebrated river rises in the Himā-<BR>laya mountains among the Jumnotri peaks at an<BR>elevation of 10, 849 feet, and flows for 860 miles<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">Page0811-a+ 74</a>]<BR>before it joins the Ganges at Allahabad, its water<BR>being there clear as crystal, while that of the Ganges<BR>is yellow; the confluence is a very sacred spot with<BR>the Hindūs, and the river Sarasvatī being supposed<BR>to join the other two rivers underground, the place<BR>is called त्रि-वेणी, q. v.); N. of a daughter of the<BR>Muni Mataṅga.<BR>—यमुना-जनक, अस्, m. the<BR>father of Yamunā; N. of the god of the Sun.<BR>—यमुना-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—य-<BR>मुना-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of a district.<BR>—यमुना-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of Yamunā,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—यमुना-प्रभव, अस्, m. the source of the<BR>river Yamunā (celebrated as a place of pilgrimage).<BR>—यमुना-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, living on the Yamunā.<BR>—यमुना-भिद्, त्, m., N. of Bala-deva (so called<BR>from his having divided the river into two parts with<BR>his ploughshare).<BR>—यमुना-भ्रातृ, ता, m. the<BR>brother of Yamunā, i. e. Yama.<BR>—यमुनाष्टक<BR>(˚ना-अष्˚), अम्, n., N. of a short poem (consisting<BR>of eight stanzas) on the glories of the river Yamunā.<BR>—यमुनाष्ट-पदी (˚ना-अष्˚), f., N. of a short<BR>poem on the Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0810-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम्य
1. यम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, restrainable, to be curbed<BR>or controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम्य
2. यम्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. यम), Ved. being a<BR>twin, (Sāy. = यम-रूप, मिथुन-भूत); twin-<BR>like, belonging to twins; (आ), f. night, (according<BR>to Naighaṇṭuka 1. 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदग्नि|यमदग्निः
यमदग्नि यमदग्नि, an incorrect reading<BR>for जमद्-अग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमन्वन्
यमन्वन् यमन्वन्, आ, m. or यमन्वा, f. a<BR>term for a form increased by Vṛddhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमया
यमया यमया, N. of the sixth astrono-<BR>mical Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमयिष्णु
यमयिष्णु यमयिष्णु, in Sāma-veda I. 5,<BR>1, 2, 3 = नमयिष्णु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमल|यमलं|यमलः
यमल यमल. See p. 810, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुन्द
यमुन्द यमुन्द, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुषदेव
यमुषदेव यमुषदेव, N. of a kind of<BR>woven cloth mentioned in Rāja-taraṅgiṇi 1. 299.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमेरुका
यमेरुका यमेरुका, f. a kind of drum or<BR>gong on which the hours are struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययाति|ययातिः
ययाति ययाति, m., N. of a celebrated<BR>monarch of the lunar race (son of king Nahuṣa,<BR>whom he succeeded; he first married the daughter<BR>of Uśanas or Śukra, Devayānī, who had been thrown<BR>into a well by Śarmiṣṭhā, daughter of Vṛṣa-parvan;<BR>Yayāti having found her and wedded her, she de-<BR>manded that Śarmiṣṭhā, who had ill-treated her,<BR>should become her handmaid; this was granted, but<BR>Yayāti then fell in love with the handmaid and<BR>secretly married her, for which the father of Deva-<BR>yānī inflicted on him premature decay; from the<BR>two wives of Yayāti came the two lines of the lunar<BR>race, Yadu being the son of Devayānī, and Puru of<BR>Śarmiṣṭhā; Yayāti Nāhuṣa is represented as the<BR>author of Ṛg-veda IX. 101, 4-6).<BR>—ययाति-चरित,<BR>अम्, n. the history of Yayāti; N. of a drama in seven<BR>acts by Rudra-deva (celebrating the amours of Yayāti<BR>and Śarmiṣṭhā).<BR>—ययाति-पतन, अम्, n. ‘fall of<BR>Yayāti,’ N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—ययाति-<BR>विजय, अस्, m. ‘Yayāti's victory,’ N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययावर|ययावरः
ययावर ययावर for यायावर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययि|ययिः
ययि ययि, इस्, इस्, इ, or ययी, ईस्, ईस्, इ (fr. rt.<BR>1. या), Ved. going, moving, hastening, swift, quick;<BR>(ईस्), m. a horse; a road; Śiva; a cloud, (in this<BR>sense the gender is doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययिन्
ययिन्, ई, m., N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययिवस्
ययिवस्, वान्, युषी, वत्, who or what has gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययु|ययुः
ययु, उस्, उस्, उ, going, moving, hastening, quick,<BR>swift; (उस्), m. a horse fit for sacrifice (‘one running<BR>about wild’); a horse (generally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यर्हि
यर्हि यर्हि (fr. the pronom. base 3. य;<BR>its proper correlative is तर्हि or एतर्हि, but it may<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-b" target="_blank">Page0811-b+ 79</a>]<BR>be followed by तदा, तत्र, अथ, &c.), when, at<BR>what time, whenever, while, whereas, since, as,<BR>because; (यर्हि is found in construction with either<BR>pres. or pot.; also with impf. or perf. or aor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव|यवः
यव 1. यव, अस्, m. Ved. the first half of<BR>a month, (generally in the pl.; according to the<BR>commentators = पूर्व-पक्षाः; also written याव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवन्
यवन्, आ, m. = 1. यव above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव्य|यव्यं|यव्यः
1. यव्य, अस्, m. (for 2. see col. 3), a month<BR>(as containing a यव, see above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव|यवः
यव 2. यव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. यु), Ved.<BR>warding off, keeping off, averting, preventing, re-<BR>moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवयावन्
यवयावन्, आ, m., Ved. one who keeps off or<BR>averts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव|यवः
यव 3. यव, अस्, m. (perhaps connected<BR>with rt. 2. यु), barley, (in the earliest times pro-<BR>bably any grain or corn yielding flour or meal); a<BR>barely-corn; (as a measure of length) a barley-corn<BR>= (1/6) or (according to others) (1/8) of an अङ्गुल; (as a<BR>weight) a barley-corn = 6 grains of white mustard<BR>seed or (according to others) = 12 mustard seeds =<BR>(1/2) गुञ्ज; (in palmistry) a figure or mark on the<BR>hand resembling a barley-corn, a natural line across<BR>the thumb at the second joint compared to a grain<BR>of barley and supposed to indicate good fortune; N.<BR>of a particular astronomical Yoga, (viz. when the<BR>favourable planets are situated in the fourth and<BR>tenth mansions and the unfavourable ones in the first<BR>and seventh); speed, velocity (?); a double convex<BR>lens (?); [cf. Zend yava; Gr. ζεά; Lith. jawa-s.]<BR>—यव-क्री, ईस्, m. a buyer or purchaser of barley;<BR>a proper N.; [cf. यव-क्रीत.]<BR>—यव-क्रीत, अस्,<BR>m. ‘purchased with barley,’ N. of a son of Bharad-<BR>vāja.<BR>—यव-क्षार, अस्, m. an alkali prepared<BR>from the ashes of burnt barley-straw, saltpetre, nitre,<BR>nitrate of potash.<BR>—यव-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. a field of<BR>barley.<BR>—यव-क्षोद, अस्, m. barley-meal.<BR>—यव-<BR>खद, see Gaṇa Vrīhy-ādi to Pāṇ. V. 2, 116.<BR>—यव-गोधूम-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced from<BR>barley and wheat, prepared with barley and wheat.<BR>—यव-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘barley-necked,’<BR>whose neck is like a grain of barley (said of a fowl;<BR>called also यव-शिरस्, q. v.).<BR>—यव-चतुर्थी, f. a<BR>sort of game played on the fourth day in the light<BR>half of the month Vaiśākha (when people throw<BR>barley-meal over one another).<BR>—यव-चूर्ण, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. barley-meal.<BR>—यव-ज, अस्, m. = यव-<BR>क्षार; Ptychotis Ajowan (= यवानी).<BR>—यव-<BR>तिक्ता, f. a species of plant (= शङ्खिनी).<BR>—यव-<BR>द्वीप, अस्, m. the island Yava, (also written जल-<BR>द्वीप.)<BR>—यव-नाल, अस्, m. a sort of grass or<BR>grain, Andropogon Bicolor; barley-straw (?) .<BR>—य-<BR>वनाल-ज, अस्, m. an alkali made from the ashes<BR>of the above plant, nitre; [cf. यव-क्षार.]<BR>—य-<BR>व-पिष्ट, अम्, n. barely-meal.<BR>—यव-प्रख्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, resembling barley-meal; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>particular eruption or small tumor like a barely-corn.<BR>—यव-प्ररोह, अस्, m. a shoot or ear of barley.<BR>—यव-फल, अस्, m. the bamboo cane; Indian<BR>spikenard, Nardostachys Jatamansi; Wrightia Anti-<BR>dysenterica; the tree Ficus Infectoria; an onion.<BR>—यव-बुस, अम्, n. the husk or chaff of barley.<BR>—यवबुसक, अस्, आ, अम्, (to be paid) at the time<BR>of the production of barley-husk (as a debt; cf.<BR>Pāṇini IV. 3, 48).<BR>—यव-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessing or abounding in barley; containing barley,<BR>mixed with barley; (आन्), m., N. of a Gandharva;<BR>of the author of a Vedic hymn; (अती), f. a kind of<BR>metre, twice ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘, ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘<BR>¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ¯; (अत्), n. abundance of grain (Ved.).<BR>—यव-मध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having the middle<BR>like a barely-corn, i. e. stout or broad in the centre<BR>and thin or tapering at the ends; (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of drum; (आ), f. a kind of metre; (अम्), n. a kind<BR>of penance (= यव-मध्यम, q. v.); a particular<BR>measure of length.<BR>—यव-मध्यम, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of lunar penance, (see चान्द्रायण.)<BR>—यव-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of barley, made of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">Page0811-c+ 80</a>]<BR>barley.<BR>—यव-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, measuring a barley-<BR>corn, as large as a grain of barley.<BR>—यव-मुष्टि,<BR>इस्, m. f. a handful of barley.<BR>—यव-लास, अस्, m.<BR>nitre, saltpetre.<BR>—यव-वक्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a head or point like a grain of barley.<BR>—यव-शिरस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, having a head shaped like a grain of<BR>barley, (see यव-ग्रीव.)<BR>—यव-शूक or यव-<BR>शूक-ज, अस्, m. = यव-क्षार, a kind of alkaline<BR>salt prepared from the ashes of burnt barley-straw.<BR>—यव-सुर, अम्, n. malt-liquor, an intoxicating<BR>drink prepared from barley, beer.<BR>—यवाकार (˚व-<BR>आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, barley-shaped, shaped like a barley-<BR>corn.<BR>—यवाग्र-ज (˚व-अग्˚), अस्, m. = यव-<BR>क्षार, N. of a plant, Ptychotis Ajowan (= य-<BR>वानी).<BR>—यवाग्रयण (˚व-आग्˚), अम्, n. the first-<BR>lings or first-fruits of barley.<BR>—यवाङ्कुर (˚व-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a shoot or blade of barley.<BR>—यवाचित (˚व-<BR>आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, laden with barley.<BR>—यवाद् (˚व-<BR>अद्), त्, त्, त्, eating barley, living on barley.<BR>—य-<BR>वान्न (˚व-अन्˚), अम्, n. barley-food, boiled barley.<BR>—यवापत्य (˚व-अप्˚), अम्, n. = यव-क्षार.<BR>—यवाम्ल-ज (˚व-अम्˚), अम्, n. sour barley-<BR>gruel.<BR>—यवाशिर् (˚व-आश्˚), ईर्, ईर्, ईर्, mixed or<BR>malted with barley.<BR>—यवाहार (˚व-आह्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having barley for food, living on barley.<BR>—य-<BR>वाह्व (˚व-आह्˚), अस्, m. = यव-क्षार.<BR>—यवोत्-<BR>थ (˚व-उत्˚), अम्, n. = यवाम्ल-ज.<BR>—यवोदर<BR>(˚व-उद्˚), अम्, n. the body or thick part of a grain of<BR>barley used as a measure of length.<BR>—यवोर्वरा (˚व-<BR>उर्˚), f., Ved. a filed sown with barley, barley-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक|यवकः
यवक, अस्, m. barley; = यव-प्रकार, a sort<BR>of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्य|यवक्यं
यवक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, producing barley, sown with<BR>barley, fit for barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्षा
यवक्षा, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवयु
यवयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desiring barley or corn,<BR>(Sāy. = यवेच्छु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवस|यवसं
यवस, अम्, n. (according to some also अस्, m.),<BR>grass, fodder, food, pasturage, pasture, meadow grass.<BR>—यवस-प्रथम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. beginning<BR>with or depending on good pasturage, well-nurtured;<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-s. XXI. 43.<BR>first or best of all kinds of food.)<BR>—यवसाद् (˚स-<BR>अद्), त्, त्, त्, Ved. eating or consuming grass, grazing,<BR>pasturing, feeding.<BR>—यवसान्नोदकेन्धन (˚स-<BR>अन्न-उद्˚, ˚क-इन्˚), अम्, n. grass, corn, water, and<BR>fuel.<BR>—यवसोदक (˚स-उद्˚), ए, n. du. grass and<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवागू
यवागू, ऊस्, f. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 81. said to come<BR>fr. rt. 2. यु), sour gruel, rice-gruel (made from rice<BR>boiled with water and said to be composed of six<BR>measures of water to one of rice); any thin decoction<BR>of other kinds of grain, &c., (according to some, a<BR>decoction in which four measures of grain are steeped<BR>in sixty-four measures of water and the whole boiled<BR>down to half the original quantity.)<BR>—यवागू-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of Yavāgū.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवानिका
यवानिका, f. Ptychotis Ajowan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवानी
यवानी, f. a kind of bad barley; Ptychotis Ajowan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवास|यवासः
यवास, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 2. यु), = यास,<BR>Alhagi Maurorum; a species of Khadira; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of grass (= गुण्डासिनी).<BR>—यवास-शर्करा, f.<BR>a kind of sugar made from Yavāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवासक|यवासकः
यवासक, अस्, m. Alhagi Maurorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवासिनी
यवासिनी, f. a district abounding in Yavāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविक
यविक or यविल, अस्, आ, अम्, having or producing<BR>barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविन्
यविन्, ई, इनी, इ, = यविक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव्य|यव्यं|यव्यः
2. यव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. यव्य see col. 2),<BR>suitable or fit for barley; sown with or consisting of<BR>barley; (अस्), m., Ved. a stock of barley or fruit;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a family of Ṛṣis; (अम्), n. a<BR>field of barley; (Ved.) epithet of certain Homa-<BR>mantras; (आ), f., Ved. a river, stream (in Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 98, 8).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव्यावती
यव्या-वती, f., Ved., N. of a river (in Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 27, 6, identified by Sāy. with Hariyūpīyā, which<BR>he describes as the N. of a river or of a city); N. of<BR>a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्षार|यवक्षारः
यवक्षार यव-क्षार. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0811-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवगण्ड|यवगण्डः
यवगण्ड यवगण्ड, अस्, m. = युव-गण्ड,<BR>a kind of eruption on the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवन|यवनः
यवन यवन, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. or 2. यु,<BR>or connected with rt. जु = 1. जू), one who keeps<BR>back; one who mixes, &c., see Gaṇa Nandyādi to<BR>Pāṇ. III. 1, 134; a fast horse, courser, (in this sense<BR>fr. rt. 1. जू and connected with जवन, for which it<BR>is sometimes a false reading); speed, velocity, (con-<BR>nected with rt. 1. जू); an Ionian, Greek, (in Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 74. said to be fr. rt. 2. यु); a king of the<BR>Greeks; a Muhammadan, (sometimes applied to<BR>both the Muhammadan and European invaders of<BR>India as coming from the same quarter); any<BR>foreigner; a barbarian generally (Manu X. 44);<BR>the country of the Yavanas (sometimes applied to<BR>Bactria, Ionia, Greece, and more recently to Arabia);<BR>a carrot; olibanum; (आस्), m. pl. the Ionians or<BR>Greeks; the Greek astrologers; N. of a dynasty;<BR>(ई), f. a Greek or Muhammadan woman; the wife<BR>of a Yavana; = जवनी, a curtain.<BR>—यवन-देश,<BR>अस्, m. the country of the Yavanas.<BR>—यवनदेश-<BR>ज, ‘growing in the country of the Yavanas,’ styrax<BR>or benzoin.<BR>—यवन-द्विष्ट, अस्, m. ‘hated or<BR>disliked by Yavanas,’ bdellium.<BR>—यवन-पुर,<BR>अम्, n. the city of the Yavanas, (probably) Alex-<BR>andria.<BR>—यवन-प्रिय, अम्, n. ‘dear to Yavanas,’<BR>pepper.<BR>—यवन-मुण्ड, अस्, m. a bald Yavana,<BR>one with a shaved head.<BR>—यवन-सेन, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—यवनाचार्य (˚न-आच्˚), अस्, m. an<BR>astronomical writer (frequently quoted by Varāha-<BR>mihira and other ancient Hindū astronomers, perhaps<BR>any Greek astronomer).<BR>—यवनारि (˚न-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. ‘enemy of the Yavanas,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa or<BR>Viṣṇu; of a king of Vārāṇasī.<BR>—यवनेश्वर<BR>(˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author of the Mīna-<BR>rāja-jātaka.<BR>—यवनेष्ट (˚न-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>liked by the Yavanas; (अस्), m. a kind of onion or<BR>garlic; Azadirachta Indica; (आ), f. the wild date<BR>tree; (अम्), n. lead; an onion, garlic; pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनक
यवनक, अस्, m. a particular kind of grain;<BR>(इका), f. = यवनी, a Yavana woman; = जवनिका,<BR>a curtain or screen, an outer tent, a screen of cloth<BR>surrounding a tent; a veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनानी
यवनानी, f. the writing of the Yavanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनाल|यवनालः
यवनाल यव-नाल. See p. 811, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवय
यवय यवय (fr. युवन्), Nom. P. यव-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to make young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवयस
यवयस यवयस, अम्, n., N. of a Varṣa<BR>in Plaksha-dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवस|यवसं
यवस यवस. See p. 811, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवागू
यवागू यवागू. See p. 811, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवान|यवानः
यवान यवान, अस्, आ, अम्, quick, swift,<BR>rash, (incorrectly for जवान, part. fr. rt. 1. जू.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवानिका
यवानिका यवानिका. See p. 811, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवाष
यवाष यवाष = येवाष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवाषिक
यवाषिक, see Gaṇa 1. Kumudādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवाषिन्
यवाषिन्, see Gaṇa Prekṣādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविष्ठ|यविष्ठः
यविष्ठ यविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of<BR>युवन्), youngest, very young, last-born; (अस्), m.<BR>a younger brother; N. of Agni (called ‘the youngest’<BR>or ‘last-born’ of the gods, either as produced from<BR>wood or as placed on the altar after everything else);<BR>N. of a Brāhman; (आस्), m. pl. his descendants;<BR>अग्नि यविष्ठ, N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-<BR>veda VIII. 91; [cf. Old Germ. jungisto.] — 1. य-<BR>विष्ठ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing the word य-<BR>विष्ठ.<BR>—२. यविष्ठ-वत्, ind. like a youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविष्ठ्य
यविष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. youngest, = य-<BR>विष्ठ, (Sāy. = युवतम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवीयस्
यवीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of युवन्),<BR>younger; (आन्), m. a younger brother; a Śūdra (as<BR>opposed to one of the three higher castes); (असी), f.<BR>a younger sister; [cf. Goth. juhisa.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवीयस
यवीयस, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवीनर
यवीनर यवीनर, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Ajamīḍha; of a son of Dvimīḍha and of Bharmyāśva<BR>and of Vāhyāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवीयुध्
यवीयुध् यवीयुध्, त्, त्, त् (fr. Intens. of rt.<BR>1. युध्), Ved. eager to fight, fond of war, warlike,<BR>(also written यव्युध्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव्य|यव्यं|यव्यः
यव्य 1.2. यव्य. See p. 811, cols. 2,3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यश|यशः
यश यश. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशद|यशदं
यशद यशद, अम्, n. a species of mineral<BR>(commonly called दस्ता, which according to some<BR>is zinc or pewter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्
यशस् यशस्, अस्, n. (in Uṇādi-s. IV. 190.<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. अश्; according to some for ori-<BR>ginal दशस् = Lat. decus, fr. a lost rt. दश्), beautiful<BR>or handsome appearance, beauty, splendor, magnifi-<BR>cence, worth, excellence (Ved.); honour, glory,<BR>praise, renown, fame, reputation, distinction, cele-<BR>brity; Fame (personified as the son of Kāma and<BR>Rati or of Dharma and Kīrtti); an object of honour<BR>or respect, a person of respectability; favour, parti-<BR>ality (Ved.); = उदक, water (Ved.); अन्न, food<BR>(Ved.); = धन, wealth (Ved.); N. of a Sāman;<BR>(आस्), m. a proper N.; (आस्, आस्, अस्), Ved. beautiful,<BR>handsome, splendid, resplendent; worthy, excellent;<BR>renowned, honoured, respected, venerated; pleasant,<BR>pleasing, agreeable, estimable; [cf. Gr. δοκ-έ-ω,<BR>δόξα, δόγμα, δοκεύω, διδάσκω, δάκτυλος; Lat.<BR>dec-et, decus, dignu-s, doceo; probably Angl. Sax.<BR>ta, tah; Old Germ. zeha.]<BR>—यशः-कर्ण, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—यशः-काय, अस्, m. a body consisting<BR>of fame or glory, i. e. glory, reputation.<BR>—यशः-<BR>केतु, उस्, m., N. of various kings.<BR>—यशः-पटह,<BR>अस्, m. a drum, a double drum.<BR>—यशः-पाल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—यशः-प्रख्यापन, अम्, n.<BR>spreading abroad or proclaiming the glory (of any<BR>one).<BR>—यशः-शरीर, अम्, n. = यशः-काय above.<BR>—यशः-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, having nothing left but<BR>glory or fame, i. e. dead; (अस्), m. death, dying.<BR>—यशश्-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—यशस्-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing renown, conferring fame<BR>or distinction, famous, glorious; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>various men.<BR>—यशस्कर-स्वामिन्, N. of a temple<BR>founded by a certain Yaśas-kara.<BR>—यशस्-काम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, honour-loving, desirous or eager for fame,<BR>ambitious.<BR>—यशस्-काम्य, Nom. P. -काम्यति,<BR>&c., to desire honour or fame, be eager for renown.<BR>—यशस्-काम्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, desiring fame, de-<BR>sirous of glory.<BR>—यशस्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing honour,<BR>conferring dignity or renown.<BR>—यशस्-तम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. most renowned or resplendent.<BR>—य-<BR>शस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing honour or glory,<BR>full of honour, honourable, glorious, famous; pleasant,<BR>pleasing, excellent, handsome; agreeable, estimable;<BR>(अती), f., N. of a woman.<BR>—यशस्वि-तम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, most famous or renowned.<BR>—यशस्-विन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, possessing honour or glory, renowned, famous, cele-<BR>brated, glorious; excellent, handsome; (इनी), f. epithet<BR>of a particular artery; N. of several plants, wild cotton<BR>(= वन-कार्पासी, यव-तिक्ता, महा-ज्योतिष्मती);<BR>N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—यशो-<BR>गोपि, इस्, m., N. of a commentator on the Śrauta-<BR>sūtras of Kātyāyana.<BR>—यशो-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, de-<BR>stroying the appearance or beauty (Ved.); destroying<BR>fame or reputation.<BR>—यशो-द, अस्, आ, अम्, glory-<BR>giving, bestowing distinction, conferring fame or<BR>renown; (अस्), m. quicksilver; (आ), f., N. of the<BR>wife of the cowherd Nanda, (she resided at Go-kula,<BR>and was the foster-mother of Kṛṣṇa, who immedi-<BR>ately after his birth as son of Devakī and Vasu-deva<BR>was entrusted to her care, that he might be protected<BR>from the enmity of Kaṃsa); N. of the wife of<BR>Mahā-vīra and daughter of Samara-vīra; N. of the<BR>daughter of a class of Manes.<BR>—यशो-दत्त, अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—यशो-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. glory-<BR>giving, conferring beauty, (for यशो-दा, f. of यशो-<BR>द, see above.)<BR>—यशोदा-गर्भ-सम्भूता, f.<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—यशोदा-नन्द, अस्, m. Yaśo-<BR>dā's son, i. e. Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यशो-देव, अस्, m., N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-c" target="_blank">Page0812-c+ 79</a>]<BR>a Buddhist mendicant; of a son of Rāma-candra;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a daughter of Vainateya and wife of<BR>Bṛhan-manas.<BR>—यशो-धन, अम्, n. a fund or<BR>stock of fame; (अस्, आ, अम्), whose wealth consists<BR>of fame, rich in renown, renowned, famous (said of<BR>persons); (अस्), m., N. of a king.<BR>—यशो-धर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, maintaining or preserving glory, uphold-<BR>ing renown; (अस्), m., N. of the fifth day of the<BR>civil month (कर्म-मास); of the eighteenth<BR>Arhat of the preceding and of the nineteenth of the<BR>future Utsarpiṇī; of a son of Kṛṣṇa by Rukmiṇī,<BR>(also read यशो-वर); of various other men; (आ),<BR>f., N. of the fourth night of the civil month; of the<BR>mother of Rāhula; of several other women.<BR>—यशो-<BR>धा, आस्, आस्, अम्, conferring splendor or fame.<BR>—यशो-धामन्, अ, n. site or abode of glory.<BR>—यशो-नन्दि, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—यशो-भ-<BR>गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. possessing fame, rich in glory,<BR>famous, renowned.<BR>—यशो-भगीन, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>यशो-भग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., see Pāṇ. IV. 4, 131.<BR>—यशो-भद्र, अस्, m. (with Jainas) N. of one of<BR>the six Śruta-kevalins.<BR>—यशो-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, bearing<BR>fame, possessing renown, famous, renowned; bring-<BR>ing glory.<BR>—यशो-मती, f., N. of the third lunar<BR>night.<BR>—यशो-मत्य, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—यशो-माधव, अस्, m. a form of Viṣṇu.<BR>—य-<BR>शो-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist author.<BR>—यशो-<BR>राज, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—यशो-राशि, इस्, m. a<BR>heap or mass of glory, a glorious deed.<BR>—यशो-<BR>लेखा f., N. of a princess.<BR>—यशो-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessing fame or glory; (अती), f., N. of various<BR>women; of a district (originally of a stream; some-<BR>times abbreviated into यशो-वति); of a mythical<BR>town on mount Meru.<BR>—यशो-वर, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a son of Kṛṣṇa by Rukmiṇī, (see यशो-धर.)<BR>—यशो-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. the path of glory, road to<BR>fame.<BR>—यशो-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a poet; of<BR>several other men, (यशो-वर्मक is found at the<BR>end of an adj. comp.)<BR>—यशो-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, de-<BR>stroying fame or reputation.<BR>—यशो-हर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, taking away fame, depriving of reputation,<BR>dishonouring; N. of a place, (gender doubtful.)<BR>—यशोहर-जित्, त्, m., N. of Kacu-rāya.<BR>—यशो-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, shorn of fame or glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यश|यशः
यश at the end of a comp. = यशस्, cf. अति-य्˚;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस
यशस at the end of a comp. = यशस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्य
यशस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, famous, glorious, renowned,<BR>celebrated, honoured; bestowing glory or distinction,<BR>producing fame, creditable; (आ), f., N. of a plant (=<BR>जीवन्ती); of another plant (= ऋद्धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्यु
यशस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. seeking favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टव्य
यष्टव्य यष्टव्य, यष्टृ. See p. 804,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टि|यष्टिः
यष्टि 2. यष्टि, इस्, f. (rarely m.), or यष्टी,<BR>f. (probably fr. rt. यम्; for 1. यष्टि see p. 804,<BR>col. 2), a staff, stick, wand; a staff armed with iron,<BR>mace, club; a pole, column, pillar; a perch; a stem, sup-<BR>port; a palisade; a flag-staff [cf. ध्वज-य्˚]; a stalk,<BR>stem, blade; a reed; a branch; the arm (= भुज-<BR>दण्ड); anything thin or slender (e. g. अङ्ग-<BR>यष्टि, a slender or delicate form; असि-यष्टि, a<BR>sword-blade; cf. गात्र-य्˚, शरीर-य्˚, भुज-य्˚); a<BR>string, thread (= तन्तु), string of pearls, necklace<BR>[cf. हार-य्˚]; a particular kind of pearl necklace;<BR>liquorice (= यष्टी-मधुक, मधुका); sugar-<BR>cane (= मधु-यष्टि); Clerodendrum Siphonan-<BR>thus (= भार्गी); any creeping plant.<BR>—यष्टि-<BR>गृह, अम्, n., N. of a district.<BR>—यष्टि-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, carrying a stick or staff; (अस्), m. a club-<BR>bearer, mace-bearer, staff-bearer.<BR>—यष्टि-निवास,<BR>अस्, m. a pole serving as a perch (for peacocks,<BR>Raghu-v. XVI. 14); a pigeon-house standing on<BR>upright poles; [cf. वास-यष्टि.]<BR>—यष्टि-प्राण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one whose strength or power is as slender<BR>as a stalk or reed, powerless or feeble as a reed<BR>(= यष्टिर् वेणु-दण्ड एव प्राणः शक्तिर् यस्य<BR>सः); out of breath.<BR>—यष्टि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having a stick or staff, furnished with a flag-staff.<BR>—यष्टि-मधु, उ, n. or यष्टि-मधुका, f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">Page0813-a+ 77</a>]<BR>liquorice.<BR>—यष्टि-यन्त्र, अम्, n. a particular<BR>astronomical instrument.<BR>—यष्टी-पुष्प, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a plant, Putranjiva Roxburghii; [cf. पुत्र-<BR>जीव.]<BR>—यष्टी-मधु, उ, or यष्टी-मधुक,<BR>अम्, n. = यष्टि-मधु.<BR>—यष्ट्य्-आघात, अस्, m.<BR>a blow with a stick, a cudgeling, beating.<BR>—यष्ट्य्-<BR>आह्व or यष्ट्य्-आह्वय, अस्, m. liquorice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0812-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिक|यष्टिकः
यष्टिक, अस्, m. a species of water-fowl (= जल-<BR>कुक्कुट; cf. को-यष्टि); a bird, the lapwing;<BR>(आ), f. a staff, stick, club; a particular pearl ornament<BR>or necklace (especially of one string); an oblong<BR>pond or tank; liquorice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टी
यष्टी. See under 2. यष्टि, p. 812, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टीक|यष्टीकं
यष्टीक, अम्, n. liquorice (= यष्टि-मधु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्ट्रस्क
यष्ट्रस्क यष्ट्रस्क (?), आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्
यस् यस् (probably connected with rt.<BR>यम्), cl. 4. 1. P. यस्यति, यसति, य-<BR>यास, यसितुम्, to froth up, foam (Ved.; but ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 104, 2, ययस्तु<BR>= आयासम् प्राप्नोतु = उपक्षीयताम्), to make<BR>great effort or exertion, strive, endeavour, labour,<BR>preserve, trouble one's self; to strive after (with<BR>dat.); [cf. Gr. ζέ-ω, (ζέν-νυμι, ἔ-ζεσ-μαι, ζέσ-σε-ν),<BR>ζέα-μα, ζέ-μα, ζέ-σι-ς, ζεσ-τό-ς, ζῆ-λο-ς; Old<BR>Germ. jes-an, ger-ja-n.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यसित्वा
यसित्वा or यस्त्वा, ind. making effort, endeavour-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्क|यस्कः
यस्क, अस्, m. a proper N.; (आस्), m. pl. the de-<BR>scendants of Yaska; यस्का गैरिक्षिताः, N. of a<BR>school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्य
यस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be endeavoured, to be done<BR>with energy or perseverance; (according to a com-<BR>mentator) = वध्य, to be killed, fit or ready for<BR>slaughter.<BR>—यस्य-त्व, अम्, n. effort, energy; fit-<BR>ness for slaughter; death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्मात्
यस्मात् यस्मात्, ind. (abl. of 3. य or यद्;<BR>correlative of तस्मात्, q. v.), from which, from which<BR>cause, since, as, because; that, in order that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यह
यह यह, अस्, m. or यहस्, अस्, n., Ved.<BR>water; strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यहु|यहुः
यहु यहु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. = महत्, great;<BR>(उस्), m. = अपत्य, offspring, a child, (in Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 60, 13, Agni is called सहसो यहुः, Sāy. =<BR>सहसः पुत्रः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यह्व|यह्वः
यह्व, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. = महत्, great, mighty,<BR>powerful, &c.; (perhaps) being in continual motion<BR>or activity, restless, active; continual, perpetual (said<BR>of Agni, Rudra, and Soma); continually moving or<BR>flowing; (व्यस्), f. pl., Ved. flowing or running<BR>water, a river, (सप्त यह्वीः, the seven great rivers);<BR>(वी), f. du. epithet of heaven and earth, of night<BR>and day, of evening and morning, (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 142, 7, यह्वी means ‘the two<BR>children,’ according to some it may mean ‘the two<BR>hands’); (अस्), m. = यजमान, a sacrificer (accord-<BR>ing to Uṇādi-s. 1. 154).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यह्वत्|यह्वन्त्
यह्वत् (fem. अती), Ved. = यह्व above; (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. यह्वती = महती, great.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

या
या 1. या, cl. 2. P. (ep. also A.) याति (-ते),<BR>Impf. अयात् (3rd pl. अयान् or अयुस्), Pot.<BR>यायात्, Impv. यातु (2nd sing. याहि), ययौ (2nd<BR>sing. ययाथ or ययिथ, 1st pl. ययिम, Part.<BR>ययिवस्), यास्यति, अयासीत् (Vedic forms अयासुस्,<BR>यासत्, यासिष्ठम्, यासीष्ट), यातुम् (Ved. यातवे,<BR>यातवै), to go, proceed, move, set out, march, travel,<BR>journey; to go away, withdraw, retire; to pass<BR>away, pass by, elapse (said of time); to extend, last<BR>(said of time, e. g. मासं याति, it lasts for a month);<BR>to take place, come to pass, prosper, succeed; to<BR>proceed, behave, act; to go or come to, travel or<BR>journey towards, approach, arrive at, reach (with acc.<BR>or even dat. or loc. or with प्रति after an acc.);<BR>to go or march against; to go to any state or con-<BR>dition, to become, be (with acc. and especially acc.<BR>of an abstract noun, e. g. विनाशं याति, he goes to<BR>destruction, i. e. he is destroyed; काठिन्यं याति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">Page0813-b+ 81</a>]<BR>it goes to hardness, i. e. becomes hard); to under-<BR>take, obtain, get (with acc.); to go in to, have carnal<BR>intercourse with (with acc.); to go to for any object,<BR>request, implore, solicit (with double acc., e. g. यामि<BR>वो द्रविणम्, I go to you for money, I solicit<BR>wealth of you; त्वां शरणं यामि, I go to thee<BR>for help); to find out, discover, perceive. The<BR>meanings of या may be variously extended by com-<BR>bining it with other words and phrases, e. g. प-<BR>लाय्य या, to run away; बहिर् या, to go out;<BR>अधो या, to go down, sink; क्षेमेण या, to<BR>escape safely; खण्डशो या, to fall to pieces; शत-<BR>धा या, to fall into a hundred pieces; यात्रां<BR>या, to undertake a journey; मृगयां या, to go<BR>out hunting; शिरसा महीं या, to bow down to<BR>the ground with the head; अगोचरं नयनयोर्<BR>या, to become invisible; द्वेष्यतां या, to become<BR>hated; विलयं या, to be dissolved; कर्णौ या,<BR>to come to the ears, be heard; करे या, to come to<BR>hand, be obtained; वशं या, to be subject to<BR>(with gen.); प्रकृतिं या, to return to one's<BR>natural state; निद्रां या, to fall asleep; निधनं<BR>या, to die; दर्शनं या, to become visible, be<BR>seen; उदयं या, to rise (said of stars, &c.): Pass.<BR>यायते, to be gone, &c.: Caus. यापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अयीयपत्, to make or cause to go or proceed,<BR>cause to set off or march, command to go away,<BR>drive away, remove, cure (a disease); to cause to<BR>pass by or elapse, pass or spend (as time, night, &c.);<BR>to cause to subsist, support; to cause to arrive at or<BR>obtain (with a double acc., e. g. तं श्रियं या-<BR>पयति, he causes him to obtain fortune); to induce:<BR>Desid. यियासति, to wish or intend to go, to desire<BR>to proceed, &c.: Intens. यायायते, यायेति, यायाति,<BR>to go frequently, &c.; [cf. Gr. ἰάπτω (= Caus. या-<BR>पयामि), ἵημι, ἥ-σω (= यास्यामि), perhaps also some<BR>forms like ἰέναι: Lat. jacio; Janus, janua.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

या
2. या, आस्, आस्, अम् [cf. 4. य, p. 801, col. 1],<BR>going, proceeding, moving, &c. (at the end of a<BR>comp., see एव-या, तुर-या, देव-या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्
1. यात्, यान्, याती or यान्ती, यात् (for 2. यात् see<BR>s.v.), going, proceeding, moving; that which moves<BR>(e. g. Ṛg-veda I. 32, 15, इन्द्रो यातो ऽवसितस्य राजा,<BR>Indra the sovereign of all that is movable and im-<BR>movable).<BR>—यात्-सत्त्र, अम्, n., Ved. ‘continuing<BR>sacrifice,’ N. of certain solemn ceremonies which go<BR>on for a long period, (also called Sārasvata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात|यातं|यातः
यात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, proceeded, marched,<BR>passed, &c.; gone to, attained, obtained (with acc.);<BR>passed by or away, elapsed, escaped; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of going, going, march, proceeding; motion,<BR>(often confounded with यान, q. v.); the past time<BR>(e. g. यातम् अनागतं च, the past and the<BR>future); the guiding or driving of an elephant with<BR>a goad.<BR>—यात-याम, अस्, आ, अम्, or यात-यामन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, that which has completed its course or (ac-<BR>cording to others) that which has stood for a night<BR>(and so become flat and stale), used, spoiled, im-<BR>paired, useless, rejected; raw, half ripe; who or<BR>what has run out or completed a course, exhausted,<BR>old, aged.<BR>—यातयाम-त्व, अम्, n. uselessness,<BR>unprofitableness; old age.<BR>—यातानुयात (˚त-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the going and following.<BR>—यातायात (˚त-<BR>आय्˚) or यातोपयात (˚त-उप्˚), अम्, n. a going and<BR>coming; intercourse.<BR>—यातोपयातिक, see Gaṇa<BR>Akṣa-dyūtādi to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातव्य
1. यातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone or set out, to<BR>be marched; to be gone against, to be assailed or<BR>attacked, (the neuter is used impersonally.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातव्य
2. यातव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. यातु below), service-<BR>able against witchcraft, keeping off Rākṣasas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याति
याति, इस्, f. (said to be fr. the Intens.), see Pāṇ. I.<BR>1, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातिक|यातिकः
यातिक, अस्, m. a traveller, (probably incorrect for<BR>यात्रिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातु|यातुः
1. यातु, 3rd sing. Impv. of rt. 1. या above (often<BR>used as an interjection), let it go, let it pass, be it so,<BR>no matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातु|यातुः
2. यातु, उस्, उस्, उ, a goer, one who goes or<BR>moves; (उस्), m. a traveller, wayfarer; wind; time;<BR>(perhaps) sorcery, witchcraft, (but according to Sāy.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">Page0813-c+ 81</a>]<BR>यातु means either कर्मणां हिंसा, injury of rites,<BR>or पीडा, pain, torture); a kind of evil spirit, Rākṣasa,<BR>demon; (उ), n. a weapon, (according to Sāy. as<BR>inflicting यातना, pain); a Rākṣasa, evil spirit,<BR>demon.<BR>—यातु-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying Yātus;<BR>(अस्), m. bdellium.<BR>—यातु-चातन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>‘Yātu-removing,’ driving away Rākṣasas.<BR>—यातु-<BR>जम्भन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. ‘Yātu-destroying,’ de-<BR>stroying Rākṣasas or demons.<BR>—यातु-जू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ,<BR>Ved. incited by Yātus, impelled by Rākṣasas; (Sāy.)<BR>pressing forwards or eager to torment (said of demons).<BR>—यातु-धान, अस्, m. an evil spirit, Rākṣasa,<BR>demon; (ई), f. a female Rākṣasa.<BR>—यातु-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. practising witchcraft or sorcery, evil-<BR>disposed, injurious, malignant; composed of demons<BR>or Rākṣasas, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 133,<BR>2, यातु-मत् means either ‘possessing injury,’ ‘in-<BR>flicting injury,’ or ‘possessing injurious weapons,’ or<BR>‘possessing demons.’)<BR>—यातु-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. skil-<BR>ful in sorcery or witchcraft, learned in the practices<BR>of Rākṣasas.<BR>—यातु-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, Ved. destroy-<BR>ing witchcraft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातुमावत्|यातुमावन्त्
यातु-मावत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. (according to the<BR>Pada text of the Ṛg-veda and Atharva-veda Prāti-<BR>śākhya IV. 8. this word is divided यातु-मावत्, not<BR>यातुमा-वत् as might be expected), = यातु-मत्,<BR>‘practising sorcery, &c.,’ (but according to Sāy. यातु<BR>= यातना, ‘torment,’ and मा = व्यापार, ‘practice,’<BR>as if fr. 2. यातु with rt. 3. मा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातृ
1. यातृ, ता, त्री, तृ (for 2. see p. 815, col. 2),<BR>going, proceeding, &c., being on a journey or march;<BR>(ता), m. a goer, traveller; a driver, charioteer, coach-<BR>man; a destroyer, slayer, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 32, 14 = हन्तृ; according to modern<BR>scholars the meaning may be ‘an avenger,’ as if fr.<BR>rt. 2. यत्; cf. 3. यात्, ऋण-या.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातृक|यातृकः
यातृक, अस्, m. a wayfarer, traveller, (wrongly<BR>for यात्रिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रा
यात्रा, f. going, setting off, journey, travel, march,<BR>the march of an army, expedition, (यात्रां या or<BR>दा, to undertake an expedition or campaign, take<BR>the field); going on a pilgrimage; a company of<BR>pilgrims; a festive train, procession, the procession<BR>of idols; a feast, festival (= उत्सव); a sort of<BR>dramatic entertainment; a road; support of life,<BR>livelihood, subsistence, provisions; passing away time;<BR>going to and fro; intercourse, (लौकिकी यात्रा or<BR>जगद्-यात्रा, worldly intercourse); way, means, ex-<BR>pedient; practice, usage, custom; N. of a particular<BR>kind of astrological work (especially of one by Varāha-<BR>mihira, the full title of which is Yoga-yātrā).<BR>—या-<BR>त्रा-करण, अम्, n. the setting forth on a journey,<BR>a march.<BR>—यात्रा-कार, अस्, m. the author of a work<BR>of the Yātrā class.<BR>—यात्रा-गमन, अम्, n. the<BR>going on a journey or expedition.<BR>—यात्रा-प्रसङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. engaging in or performing a pilgrimage.<BR>—यात्रा-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of an expedition,<BR>success of a campaign.<BR>—यात्रा-महोत्सव (˚हा-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, m. a great festive procession.<BR>—यात्रार्-<BR>थम् (˚रा-अर्˚), ind. for the sake of marching.<BR>—या-<BR>त्रोत्सव (˚रा-उत्˚), अस्, m. a festive procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रिक|यात्रिकः
यात्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to a march, relating<BR>to an expedition or campaign, marching, journeying,<BR>performing a pilgrimage; relating to the support of<BR>life, requisite for subsistence; customary, usual; (अस्),<BR>m. a traveller; a pilgrim; (अम्), n. a march, expe-<BR>dition, campaign; provisions for a march, supplies,<BR>&c.; N. of a particular class of astrological works;<BR>[cf. यात्रा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रिन्
यात्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, being on a march, being in a<BR>procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यान|यानं|यानः
यान, अस्, अम्, m. n. way, road, path (Ved.);<BR>(अम्), n. the act of going, moving, riding; marching<BR>or proceeding (against an enemy), attacking; re-<BR>treating, retreat; a journey; a procession; a con-<BR>veyance or vehicle of any kind, carriage, waggon,<BR>chariot, car; a litter, palanquin; (with Buddhists) the<BR>vehicle or means of arriving at knowledge, the<BR>means of release from repeated births; (ई), f., see<BR>Gaṇa Gaurādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 41; [cf. Lat. janua.]<BR>—यान-कर, अस्, m. ‘carriage-maker,’ a wheel-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">Page0814-a+ 81</a>]<BR>wright, carpenter.<BR>—यान-पात्र or यान-पात्रक,<BR>अम्, n. ‘going-vessel,’ a ship, boat.<BR>—यानपात्रिका,<BR>f. a small vessel, boat.<BR>—यान-भङ्ग, अस्, m. the<BR>fracture of a vessel or boat, shipwreck.<BR>—यान-<BR>मुख, अम्, n. the fore part of a waggon or chariot,<BR>the pole or part where the yoke is fixed.<BR>—यान-<BR>यान, अम्, n. riding in a carriage, driving in a<BR>chariot, a drive.<BR>—यान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a<BR>carriage or vehicle; travelling in a carriage.<BR>—यान-<BR>शाला, f. a coach-house, cart-shed.<BR>—यान-स्वामिन्,<BR>ई, m. the owner of a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0813-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानक|यानकं
यानक, अस्, m. a vehicle, carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप
याप, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus.), the causing to go;<BR>[cf. काल-य्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापक
यापक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.), causing to<BR>go or come, causing to pass away or spend, bringing,<BR>granting, bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापन|यापनं
यापन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to go or pass away,<BR>bringing to an end; mitigating, alleviating, curing;<BR>prolonging or supporting life; (आ, अम्), f. n. the<BR>causing to go, act of driving away or expelling, ex-<BR>pulsion, removal, rejection; the cure or alleviation<BR>(of a malady); the causing (time) to pass away,<BR>spending time, wasting time, delay, procrastination;<BR>loitering, staying; maintenance, support (= वर्तन,<BR>यात्रा); exercise, practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापनीय
यापनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be caused to go, to be<BR>passed or spent (as time); to be removed or cured,<BR>to be expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापयत्
यापयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to go or pass,<BR>spending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापित
यापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to go; spent (as time);<BR>expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्ता
याप्ता, f. twisted or plaited hair (= जटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्य|याप्यः
याप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be passed or spent (as time);<BR>to be removed or cured; to be expelled or rejected;<BR>low, vile, contemptible, little, trifling, unimportant.<BR>—याप्य-त्व, अम्, n. curability.<BR>—याप्य-यान,<BR>अम्, n. a palanquin, litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम|यामः
1. याम, अस्, m. (for 2. याम see p. 816, col. 1),<BR>motion, course, going, proceeding, coming; a road,<BR>way, path (Ved.); progress (Ved.); a carriage,<BR>chariot (Ved.); a night-watch, period or watch of<BR>three hours, the eighth part of a day; a wandering<BR>star, planet (?); यामस्य अर्कः, N. of a Sāman;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of gods; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa (wife of Dharma or Manu;<BR>sometimes written Yāmi); N. of an Apsaras; night.<BR>—याम-कोश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. covering up or<BR>obstructing the way, (Sāy. = मार्ग-प्रतिबन्-<BR>धक.)<BR>—याम-घोष, अस्, m. ‘sounding the<BR>watches,’ a cock; a metal plate on which the night-<BR>watches or hours are struck, a drum or gong used<BR>for a similar purpose, (in this sense said to be also<BR>आ, f.)<BR>—याम-तूर्य, अम्, n. or याम-दुन्दुभि,<BR>इस्, m. or याम-नाली, f. a kind of drum or metal<BR>plate on which the night-watches or hours are struck,<BR>a clock.<BR>—याम-मात्र, अम्, n. a mere watch,<BR>only three hours.<BR>—याम-यम, अस्, m. a regular<BR>or stated occupation for every hour.<BR>—याम-वती, f.<BR>‘possessing watches,’ night.<BR>—याम-वृत्ति, इस्, f.<BR>the being on watch, standing on guard.<BR>—याम-<BR>श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, renowned for going or speed,<BR>(Sāy. = शिघ्र-गमनेन विश्रुत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामन्
1. यामन्, अ, n. (for 2. see p. 816, col. 1), Ved.<BR>going, motion, course; flight, flying; coming, arrival;<BR>a march, expedition; the act of approaching or<BR>addressing (with prayers, entreaties, &c.), invocation,<BR>supplication; offering, oblation, sacrifice, (यामन्<BR>is used in some passages as a Ved. loc. without ter-<BR>mination); पुनर्-यामन्, आ, आ, अ, coming into<BR>use again; [cf. यात-यामन्.]<BR>—याम-हू, ऊस्, ऊस्,<BR>उ, Ved. one who allows himself to be invoked by<BR>prayers or offerings, ready or inclined to assist;<BR>(Sāy.) to be invoked to come or to be invoked at<BR>the right time (= गमनार्थम् आह्वातव्य or<BR>काले ह्वातव्य).<BR>—याम-हूति, इस्, f., Ved. invo-<BR>cation for assistance; (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 8, 18, याम-हूतिषु = देवानाम् आह्वानं<BR>येषु यागेषु, in sacrifices at which there is an<BR>invocation of the gods.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामि|यामिः
1. यामि = यामी under 1. याम. (For 2. यामि<BR>see p. 816, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिक|यामिकः
यामिक, अस्, आ, अम्, being on watch or guard;<BR>(अस्), m. a night-watcher, watchman, one who an-<BR>nounces the watches, one on guard or duty at night;<BR>(इका), f. = यामिनी, night.<BR>—यामिक-भट, अस्, m.<BR>a night-watcher, watchman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनय
यामिनय (fr. यामिनी), Nom. P. यामिनयति,<BR>यितुम्, to appear like night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनी
यामिनी, f. (fr. 1. याम), night (as possessing<BR>watches); N. of a daughter of Prahlāda; of the wife<BR>of Tārkṣa (mother of Śalabha).<BR>—यामिनी-पति, इस्,<BR>m. the husband or lord of night, the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामीर|यामीरः
यामीर, अस्, m. the moon; (आ), f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामेय|यामेयः
1. यामेय, अस्, m. (fr. 1. यामि), a metronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्या
याम्या, f. (fr. 1. याम), = यामिनी, night, (for या-<BR>म्या, the south, see under याम्य, p. 816, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायावर|यायावरः
यायावर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.), going<BR>repeatedly; wandering in all directions, having no<BR>fixed or permanent abode; (अस्), m. a vagrant men-<BR>dicant, saint; a horse selected for the horse sacrifice<BR>(‘wandering at large’); a Brāhman who has pre-<BR>served his household fire (?); N. of Jarat-kāru;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a family of Brāhmans (to which<BR>Jarat-kāru belonged); (अम्), n. the life of a wan-<BR>dering beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायिन्
यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going, moving, travelling, jour-<BR>neying, marching, running, riding, driving, flying;<BR>a traveller, passenger; riding or going in or on,<BR>(generally at the end of comps., e. g. गज-यायिन्,<BR>riding on an elephant; cf. नौ-य्˚); going to, jour-<BR>neying towards; going on an expedition, taking the<BR>field, going to war; opposing each other (said of<BR>planets; cf. ग्रह-युद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन्
1. यावन्, आ, m. (for 2. see p. 817, col. 1), Ved.<BR>a rider, horseman, horse-soldier; an invader, aggres-<BR>sor, enemy, (Sāy. = अभिगन्तृ); going, driving,<BR>riding (at the end of a comp.; cf. अग्र-य्˚, पूर्व-<BR>य्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास्यत्
यास्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to go, about<BR>to proceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियासु
यियासु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid.), wishing to go,<BR>intending to set off or depart, desirous of taking the<BR>field or entering on an expedition; intending to fly<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

या
या 3. या, fem. of the relative pronoun<BR>यद्. See p. 807, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याकृत्क
याकृत्क याकृत्क (fr. यकृत्), see Pāṇ. VII.<BR>3, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याक्ष
याक्ष याक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यक्ष), be-<BR>longing or peculiar to the Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याग|यागः
याग याग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. यज्), an offer-<BR>ing, oblation, sacrifice; any ceremony in which<BR>offerings and oblations are presented.<BR>—याग-कर्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. a sacrificial rite or ceremony.<BR>—याग-<BR>काल, अस्, m. time of sacrifice.<BR>—याग-मण्डप,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a hall for sacrifices, a temple.<BR>—याग-<BR>सन्तान, अस्, m., N. of Jayanta (son of Indra).<BR>—याग-सूत्र, अम्, n. the sacrificial cord, sacred<BR>thread, (see यज्ञ-सूत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्
याच् याच्, cl. 1. P.A. याचति, -ते, य-<BR>याच, ययाचे, याचिष्यति, -ते, अयाचीत्,<BR>अयाचिष्ट, याचितुम्, to ask, beg, solicit, pray, re-<BR>quest, desire, entreat, require, implore, supplicate,<BR>importune (with double acc., e. g. देवं वरं<BR>याचते, he solicits a boon from the god; also with<BR>abl. and rarely with gen. of person, e. g. अन्नम्<BR>परात् or परस्य याचते he begs food from an-<BR>other; or the thing asked may be compounded with<BR>अर्थे or अर्थम्, e. g. मोक्षार्थम् याचते, he<BR>asks for deliverance; or may be in acc. with<BR>प्रति, e. g. सुतम् प्रति ययाचे, he asked for<BR>a son; or in dat., e. g. तं ययाचे ऽभ्यव-<BR>हाराय, he asked him for food); to offer any-<BR>thing (acc.) to any one (dat.), tender (e. g. याचति<BR>वित्तं गुरवे, he offers property to the Guru); to<BR>promise (?); कन्यां याच्, to be a suitor for a girl,<BR>to ask a girl in marriage from any one (abl. or rarely<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">Page0814-c+ 79</a>]<BR>acc.): Pass. याच्यते: Caus. याचयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अययाचत्, to cause to ask, &c.: Desid. यियाचिषति,<BR>-ते, (in Ṛg-veda VIII. 67, 1, याचिषामहे = या-<BR>चामहे): Intens. यायाच्यते, यायाक्ति (1st sing.<BR>यायाच्मि), to ask repeatedly, importune; [cf. Gr.<BR>αἰτέω, which however may be connected with rt.<BR>अर्थ्; cf. also, according to some, ζητέω.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचक|याचकः
याचक, अस्, ई, अम्, asking, one who asks or<BR>solicits, a petitioner, asker, beggar; (ई), f. a female<BR>beggar or petitioner.<BR>—याचक-वृत्ति, इस्, f. the<BR>occupation or profession of a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचन|याचनं
याचन, अम्, n. the act of asking, begging, re-<BR>questing; asking in marriage, (दुहितृ-याचन, the<BR>being a suitor for a daughter); (आ), f. asking, solicit-<BR>ing, requesting, entreating, petitioning; a request,<BR>petition, entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचनक|याचनकः
याचनक, अस्, m. an asker, petitioner, an impor-<BR>tunate man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचनीय
याचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be asked, to be desired<BR>or requested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचमान|याचमानः
याचमान, अस्, आ, अम्, asking, begging, re-<BR>questing, soliciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचित|याचितं
याचित, अस्, आ, अम्, asked, prayed for, begged,<BR>requested, solicited, entreated, importuned (with acc.,<BR>e. g. दशरथो रामं याचितः, Daśaratha was<BR>asked for Rāma); requisite, necessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचितक|याचितकं
याचितक, अम्, n. anything borrowed, any article<BR>borrowed for use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचितव्य
याचितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be asked or solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचितृ
याचितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who begs or solicits, an<BR>asker, petitioner; a suitor, wooer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचित्वा
याचित्वा, ind. having asked, having solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचिन्
याचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, asking, desiring, requesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचिष्णु
याचिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, disposed to ask, habitually<BR>asking or begging, soliciting favours, importuning,<BR>an importunate person.<BR>—याचिष्णु-ता, f. the habit<BR>of soliciting favours, importunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्ञा
याच्ञा, f. the act of asking, requesting, begging,<BR>solicitation, asking alms, mendicancy, mendicity; a<BR>petition, request, prayer, entreaty; the being a<BR>suitor, making an offer of marriage.<BR>—याच्ञा-जीवन,<BR>अम्, n. subsisting by begging or mendicancy.<BR>—याच्-<BR>ञा-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, obtained by begging or<BR>asking.<BR>—याच्ञा-भङ्ग, अस्, m. failure of request,<BR>an unsuccessful entreaty, useless request.<BR>—याच्ञा-<BR>वचस्, अस्, n. words used in begging or entreating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्ञ्य
याच्ञ्य, अस्, m. or याच्ञ्या, f., Ved. = याच्ञा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्य|याच्यं
याच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be asked or solicited, to be<BR>importuned, to be asked for alms, to be desired or<BR>requested; to be required; (अम्), n. the making a<BR>request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्यमान
याच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being asked or solicited,<BR>being prayed for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्छ्रेष्ठ
याच्छ्रेष्ठ याच्-छ्रेष्ठ. See under 2. यात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्
याज् याज्, ट्, ट्, ट् (fr. rt. 1. यज्), one who<BR>sacrifices or offers oblations, an offerer, sacrificer;<BR>[cf. हयमेध-याज्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज|याजः
याज, अस्, m. a sacrificer (in अति-य्˚, q. v.); boiled or<BR>cooked rice; food in general; N. of a Brahmarṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजक|याजकः
याजक, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus.), a sacrificer, sacri-<BR>ficing priest, one who offers sacrifices or oblations, a<BR>priest officiating at a sacrifice, (often at the end of<BR>a comp., cf. ग्राम-य्˚, नक्षत्र-य्˚; sometimes<BR>compounded with the person who institutes the sacri-<BR>fice, e. g. क्षत्रिय-याजक, the sacrificer for a<BR>Kṣatriya; cf. शूद्र-य्˚); a royal elephant; a furious<BR>elephant or one in rut.<BR>—याजक-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>condition or office of a sacrificing priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजन|याजनं
याजन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), the act of con-<BR>ducting a sacrifice or causing it to be performed,<BR>superintending or assisting at the sacrifices of others,<BR>(sometimes with gen., e. g. व्रात्यानां याजनं<BR>कृत्वा, having officiated at a sacrifice for outcasts,<BR>Manu XI. 197; अयाज्य-याजन, sacrificing for those<BR>who have no right to sacrifice, Manu III. 65.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजनीय
याजनीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), to be made<BR>or allowed to sacrifice, to be assisted at a sacrifice,<BR>one for whom it is allowable to officiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजमान|याजमानं
याजमान, अम्, n. (fr. यजमान), the part of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">Page0815-a+ 79</a>]<BR>sacrificial ceremony performed by the Yajamāna or<BR>institutor of the sacrifice himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0814-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजमानिक
याजमानिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the Yaja-<BR>māna, belonging to the institutor of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजयितृ
याजयितृ, ता, m. (fr. the Caus.), one who con-<BR>ducts a sacrifice or causes it to be performed, the<BR>officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजि|याजिः
याजि, इस्, f. a sacrifice, oblation; (इस्), m. accord-<BR>ing to Ujjvala-datta on Uṇādi-s. IV. 124 = यष्टृ,<BR>a sacrificer, the institutor of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजिका
याजिका, f. a sacrifice, oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजिन्
याजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sacrificing, conducting a sacrifice,<BR>one who officiates at a sacrifice, a sacrificer, (usually<BR>at the end of comps.; cf. देव-य्˚, बहु-य्˚); wor-<BR>shipping, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजुक|याजुकः
याजुक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of comps.) habi-<BR>tually sacrificing or making offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञ
याज्ञ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यज्ञ), belonging to sacri-<BR>fice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञतुर
याज्ञतुर, अस्, m. (fr. यज्ञ-तुर), a patro-<BR>nymic of Ṛṣabha; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञदत्तक
याज्ञदत्तक (fr. यज्ञ-दत्त), see Gaṇa Arī-<BR>haṇādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञदत्ति
याज्ञदत्ति, इस्, m. a patronymic from Yajña-<BR>datta; Kuvera (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञदेव
याज्ञदेव, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञपत
याज्ञपत (fr. यज्ञ-पति), see Gaṇa Aśva-<BR>patyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञवल्क
याज्ञवल्क, अस्, ई, अम्, composed by or derived<BR>from Yājñavalkya; (आस्), m. pl. of याज्ञवल्क्य, see<BR>Gaṇa Kaṇvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, III.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञवल्कीय
याज्ञवल्कीय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Yājñaval-<BR>kya, composed by or descended from Yājñavalkya;<BR>(अम्), n., scil. धर्म-शास्त्र, the code of Yājña-<BR>valkya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञवल्क्य|याज्ञवल्क्यः
याज्ञवल्क्य, अस्, m. (fr. यज्ञ-वल्क्य), N. of an<BR>ancient sage frequently quoted as an authority in the<BR>Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa, (the first reputed teacher of<BR>the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā or White Yajur-veda, revealed<BR>to him by the Sun, cf. तैत्तिरीय-संहिता, वाज-<BR>सनेयि-संहिता); N. of the author of a celebrated<BR>code of laws (by some identified with the preceding<BR>sage; this code is only second in importance to that<BR>of Manu, and with its most celebrated commentary,<BR>the Mitākṣara, is the leading authority of the<BR>Mithilā school; it is much later than Manu, and<BR>probably in its present form dates from about the<BR>first century of our era); the family of Yājñavalkya;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of an Upaniṣad; (अस्, की, अम्), relating<BR>to Yājñavalkya, composed by or derived from Yājña-<BR>valkya.<BR>—याज्ञवल्क्य-गीता, f., N. of a poem in<BR>commendation of the practice of Yoga attributed to<BR>Yājñavalkya.<BR>—याज्ञवल्क्य-टीका, f., N. of several<BR>commentaries on the code of Yājñavalkya (besides<BR>the Mitākṣara by Vijñāneśvara, there are other<BR>commentaries by Deva-bodha, Dharmeśvara, Bhāruci,<BR>Viśva-rūpa, and Śūla-pāṇi).<BR>—याज्ञवल्क्य-धर्-<BR>म-शास्त्र, अम्, n. Yājñavalkya's code of laws.<BR>—याज्ञवल्क्य-शिक्षा, f., N. of a treatise.<BR>—याज्-<BR>ञवल्क्य-स्मृति, इस्, f. the body of law as delivered<BR>by Yājñavalkya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञसेन|याज्ञसेनः
याज्ञसेन, अस्, or याज्ञसेनि, इस्, m. (fr. यज्ञ-<BR>सेन), a patronymic of Śikhaṇḍin; (ई), f. a patro-<BR>nymic of Draupadī (as daughter of Yajñasena).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञायनि
याज्ञायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Yajña.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक|याज्ञिकः
याज्ञिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>sacrifice, &c.; (अस्), m. a sacrificer or the officiating<BR>priest at a sacrificial ceremony, the institutor of a<BR>sacrifice, one skilled in sacrificial rites, a Ritualist;<BR>N. of various kinds of plants &c. used at a sacrifice;<BR>of Kuśa grass; of a red-flowering Khadira; the<BR>sacred fig-tree; Butea Frondosa.<BR>—याज्ञिक-देव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentator on Kātyāyana's Śrauta-<BR>sūtra.<BR>—याज्ञिक-वल्लभा, f., N. of a work.<BR>—याज्-<BR>ञिकानन्त (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—याज्ञिकाश्रय (˚क-आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक्य|याज्ञिक्यं
याज्ञिक्य, अम्, n. (fr. याज्ञिक), the laws or ob-<BR>servances relating to sacrificial rites; sacrificial cere-<BR>monies in general, a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिय|याज्ञियः
याज्ञिय, अस्, ई, अम्, = यज्ञिय, sacrificial, belong-<BR>ing to sacrifices; fit or suitable for sacrifice; (अस्),<BR>m. one skilled in sacrificial rites, (in this sense a<BR>various reading for याज्ञिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञीय
याज्ञीय probably incorrect for यज्ञीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्य|याज्यं|याज्यः
याज्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), to be made or<BR>allowed to sacrifice, one on whose behalf a sacrifice is<BR>made; to be sacrificed; sacrificial; (अस्), m. a sacrificer,<BR>performer of a sacrifice for others; the person for<BR>whom a sacrifice is performed, the master or insti-<BR>tutor of a sacrifice; (आ), f., scil. ऋच्, the sacred text<BR>uttered at the moment of making the offering, the<BR>words of consecration used at a sacrifice; (अम्), n.<BR>property or presents obtained by officiating at sacri-<BR>fices.<BR>—याज्य-ता, f. or याज्य-त्व, अम्, n. the rank<BR>or position of a sacrificer or of one for whom a<BR>sacrifice is performed.<BR>—याज्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>having the Yājyā or consecrating text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्वन|याज्वनः
याज्वन, अस्, m. (fr. यज्वन्), the son of a sacri-<BR>ficer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजुर्वैदिक
याजुर्वैदिक याजुर्वैदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>यजुर्-वेद), belonging or relating to the Yajur-<BR>veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजुष|याजुषं|याजुषः
याजुष, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the Yajus, belong-<BR>ing to the Yajur-veda; (अस्), m. an observer of reli-<BR>gious ceremonies as prescribed in the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजुष्मती
याजुष्मती, f., scil. इष्टका, a kind of brick used<BR>for the sacrificial altar; [cf. यजुष्-मत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञ
याज्ञ याज्ञ, याज्य. See col. 1. and above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्
यात् 2. यात्, ind. (properly obsolete abl. fr.<BR>the pronom. base 3. य, cf. तात्; for 1. यात् see p. 813,<BR>col. 2, for 3. यात् see below), inasmuch as, so far as,<BR>so long as, since, (but according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>1. 80, 15, यात् = यान्तम्, pervading; VII. 88, 4, यात्<BR>= यातः = गच्छतः, passing; VI. 21, 6, यात् =<BR>यानि [कर्माणि], which [actions]; according to<BR>some यात् is an interjection of pleasure; of alarm; of<BR>restlessness.)<BR>—याच्-छ्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (i. e. यात्<BR>+ श्रेष्ठ), Ved. the best possible; [cf. यावच्-<BR>छ्रेष्ठ; but according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III.<BR>53, 21, यात् is a separate word, and means ‘an<BR>enemy,’ as if fr. rt. 2. यत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्
यात् 3. यात् (fr. rt. 2. यत्), in ऋण-यात्, Ved.<BR>the avenger of guilt or debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात|यातं|यातः
यात यात, &c. See p. 813, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातन|यातनं
यातन यातन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus. of rt.<BR>2. यत्), the act of requiting, requital, retaliation,<BR>recompense, reward, return; वैरस्य यातनम्,<BR>requital of hostile acts, revenge, vengeance; (आ), f.<BR>requital, (यातनाम् दा, to make requital, revenge);<BR>recompense, retaliation, reward [cf. वैर-य्˚]; acute<BR>pain, torment, anguish, agony, (especially) punish-<BR>ment inflicted by Yama, the pains of hell; personified<BR>as the daughter of Fear (भय) and Death (मृत्यु).<BR>—यातनार्थीय (˚ना-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, fit for tor-<BR>ment, capable of suffering, susceptible of the pains of<BR>hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातयत्
यातयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, joining, connecting, uniting<BR>(Ved.); existing, animating (Ved.); requiting, re-<BR>compensing, &c.<BR>—यातयज्-जन, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>uniting or bringing men together; animating man-<BR>kind, impelling men to exertion (said of Mitra,<BR>Varuṇa, and Aryaman; according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda 1. 136, 3, the meaning as applied to Aryaman<BR>may be ‘tormenting [irreligious] men in hell’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातलराय
यातलराय यातल-राय, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातव्य
यातव्य यातव्य. See p. 813, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातस्रुच
यातस्रुच यातस्रुच, अम्, n. (fr. यत-स्रुच्),<BR>= यौक्तस्रुच, N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातानप्रस्थ
यातानप्रस्थ यातानप्रस्थ, N. of a place.<BR>यातानप्रस्थक, relating to the above place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातु|यातुः
यातु यातु, यातु-घ्न, &c. See p. 813.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातृ
यातृ 2. यातृ, ता, f. (acc. यातरम्, nom.<BR>acc. du. यातरौ, nom. pl. यातरस्; said in Uṇādi-s.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">Page0815-c+ 74</a>]<BR>II. 98. to be fr. rt. 2. यत्), a husband's brother's<BR>wife. (For 1. यातृ see p. 813, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्निक
यात्निक यात्निक, आस्, m. pl. (fr. यत्न), N.<BR>of a Buddhist school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्य|यात्यं|यात्यः
यात्य यात्य, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus. of rt.<BR>2. यत्), ‘to be tormented, subject to the torments of<BR>hell,’ an inhabitant of hell, a condemned spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रा
यात्रा यात्रा, यात्रिक, &c. See p. 813,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्सत्त्र
यात्सत्त्र यात्-सत्त्र. See p. 813, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथ
याथ याथ (fr. rt. 1 या), in दीर्घ-याथ,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथाकथाच|याथाकथाचं
याथाकथाच याथाकथाच, अम्, n. (fr. यथा<BR>कथा च), anything which occurs now and then;<BR>that which happens under any circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथाकामी
याथाकामी, f. or याथाकाम्य, अम्, n. (fr. यथा-<BR>काम), the acting according to will or desire, doing<BR>as one thinks fit or proper, conformity to one's<BR>wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथातथ्य|याथातथ्यं
याथातथ्य, अम्, n. (fr. यथा-तथम्), a<BR>proper state or condition, proper way or course,<BR>reality, rectitude, propriety, truth; (अम्, एन), ind.<BR>according to truth, in reality, as is proper.<BR>—याथा-<BR>तथ्य-तस्, ind. from the truth, according to truth,<BR>in reality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथात्म्य
याथात्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. यथात्मन्), real nature<BR>or essence, true character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथार्थिक
याथार्थिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यथार्थ), con-<BR>formable to truth or reality, just, true, right, real.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथार्थ्य|याथार्थ्यं
याथार्थ्य, अम्, n. conformity with truth or<BR>fact, consistency with reality, the true or real mean-<BR>ing; suitableness, justness, rightness, application, use,<BR>accomplishment, attainment of an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथासंस्तरिक
याथासंस्तरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यथा-सम्-<BR>स्तर), letting the covering lie according (to the<BR>original position).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादईश|यादईशः
यादईश याद-ईश, यादः-पति. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादमान
यादमान यादमान, अस्, आ, अम् (Pres. part.<BR>A. fr. an old form याद्, which, according to Sāy., is<BR>a substitute for rt. याच्), Ved. closely connected with,<BR>seeking connection or association with, wishing to<BR>mix, (Sāy. = सङ्गतिं याचमान, but in Ṛg-veda<BR>VII. 69, 3 = गच्छत् or गमयत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादव|यादवः
यादव यादव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यदु), relating<BR>to Yadu, descended or coming from Yadu; (अस्), m.<BR>a descendant of Yadu; N. of Kṛṣṇa; of a lexi-<BR>cographer; of an astronomer; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>descendants of Yadu; = माधवः, वृष्णयाः;<BR>(ई), f. a Yādava female; N. of Durgā; (अम्), n. a<BR>stock of cattle.<BR>—यादव-गिरि, N. of a country.<BR>—यादव-पण्डित, अस्, m. = यादव-व्यास.<BR>—या-<BR>दव-राय, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—यादव-व्यास,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the Siddhānta-saṅgraha<BR>and of a commentary on the Nyāya-siddhānta-mañ-<BR>jarī.<BR>—यादव-शार्दूल, अस्, m. ‘Yādava-tiger,<BR>chief of the Yādavas,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—यादवा-<BR>चार्य (˚व-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR>—याद-<BR>वाभ्युदय (˚व-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—यादवेन्द्र (˚व-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>of an author.<BR>—यादवोदय (˚व-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘rise<BR>of the Yādavas,’ N. of a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादवक
यादवक, आस्, m. pl. the descendants of Yadu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याद्व
याद्व, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. belonging to the family<BR>of Yadu; (अस्), m. a son or descendant of Yadu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादस्
यादस् यादस्, अस्, n. a fluid, water; a river;<BR>semen; desire, lust (Ved. originally ‘close carnal<BR>connection;’ cf. यादमान); any animal living in<BR>water, any large aquatic animal, a monster of the<BR>deep, sea monster; यादसां नाथः or यादसाम्<BR>प्रभुः or यादसाम् पतिः, ‘lord of sea ani-<BR>mals,’ N. of Varuṇa; the ocean.<BR>—याद-ईश, अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of marine animals,’ the sea.<BR>—यादः-पति,<BR>इस्, m. ‘lord of sea animals,’ the ocean, sea; N.<BR>of Varuṇa.<BR>—यादो-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of sea<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">Page0816-a+ 75</a>]<BR>monsters,’ N. of Varuṇa.<BR>—यादो-निवास, अस्, m.<BR>‘abode of sea animals,’ the ocean, sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0815-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादु|यादुः
यादु, उस्, m. a fluid, liquid, water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादुर
यादुर, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. embracing sensually or<BR>voluptuously, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I, 126,<BR>6, यादुरी = बहु-रेतो-युक्ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृक्ष|यादृक्षः
यादृक्ष या-दृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. य +<BR>दृक्ष, fr. rt. 1. दृश्), looking or appearing like<BR>which, what like, which like, as like, of which sort<BR>or nature, (used correlatively to तादृक्ष, q. v.: cf.<BR>Gr. ἥλιξ, ἡλίκος; Lat. qualis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृश्
यादृश्, क्, क्, क् (Ved. nom. यादृङ्), or यादृश,<BR>अस्, ई, अम् (see 2. दृश्, दृश), which like, what<BR>like, as like, of whatever kind or nature, whoever,<BR>whichever, whatever, which, what, (used correlatively<BR>to तादृश् and तादृश); यादृश, तादृश, any<BR>one whatever, anybody whatsoever.<BR>—यादृग्-गुण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of whatever qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृच्छिक|यादृच्छिकः
यादृच्छिक यादृच्छिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यद्-<BR>ऋच्छा), voluntary, spontaneous, independent; acci-<BR>dental, casual, unexpected; (अस्), m. an officiating<BR>priest who does as he pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याद्राध्य
याद्राध्य याद्-राध्य, अस्, आ, अम् (i. e. 1. यात्<BR>+ राध्य), obtainable by moving or living creatures,<BR>(according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda II. 38, 8 = गच्-<BR>छतां राध्य; or according to modern scholars,<BR>the word may be used adverbially, as if fr. 2. यात् +<BR>राध्यम्, ‘as far as is practicable,’ ‘as well or as<BR>quickly as possible,’ cf. याच्-छ्रेष्ठ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याद्व
याद्व याद्व. See p. 815, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यान|यानं|यानः
यान यान, &c. See p. 813, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यान्त्रिक|यांत्रिक
यान्त्रिक यान्त्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यन्त्र),<BR>belonging to instruments or implements, relating to<BR>blunt surgical instruments, (see यन्त्र); artificially<BR>or mechanically refined (said of sugar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापक
यापक यापक, यापन, याप्ता. See p. 814,<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याभ|याभः
याभ याभ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. यभ्), sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>—याभ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याभिस्
याभिस् याभिस्, ind. (inst. pl. fem. fr. the<BR>pronom. base 3. य, see यद्), Ved. whereby, that,<BR>in order that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम|यामः
याम 2. याम, अस्, m. (fr. rt. यम्; for<BR>1. याम see p. 814, col. 1), restraint, forbearance,<BR>&c., = याम; (अस्, ई, अम्), relating to Yama, (in<BR>this sense fr. यम); coming or derived from Yama,<BR>done or ordered by Yama; (अम्), n., N. of several<BR>Sāmans.<BR>—यामोत्तर (˚म-उत्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामक|यामकः
यामक, औ, m. du., N. of the Nakṣatra Punar-<BR>vasū; (ई), f. the voc. यामकि is used as a term of<BR>abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामन्
2. यामन् = यामिन् in अन्तर्-यामन्. (For 1. see<BR>p. 814, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिन्
यामिन् in अन्तर्-यामिन्, q. v. (For यामिनी see<BR>p. 814, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्य|याम्यः
याम्य, अस्, -मी, अम्, relating or belonging to Yama,<BR>like or resembling Yama, &c., (याम्य ऋक्ष, the<BR>Nakṣatra Bharaṇī presided over by Yama); southern,<BR>southerly, (याम्ये or याम्येन, in the south, in<BR>a southerly direction); (अस्), m., scil. नर or पु-<BR>रुष or दूत, a servant of Yama; N. of Agastya;<BR>of Śiva; of Viṣṇu; sandal-wood; (आ), f. the lunar<BR>asterism Bharaṇī; scil. दिश् or आशा, the southern<BR>quarter, south, (for याम्या, night, see p. 814, col. 2.)<BR>—याम्य-तस्, ind. from the south.<BR>—याम्य-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—याम्य-पाश, अस्,<BR>m. the noose or fetter of Yama.<BR>—याम्यायन<BR>(˚य-आय्˚), अम्, n. the sun's progress south of the<BR>equator, the winter solstice (= दक्षिणायन).<BR>—याम्योत्तर (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, southern and<BR>northern, going from south to north.<BR>—याम्योत्तर-<BR>वृत्त, अम्, n. south and north circle, the solstitial<BR>colure.<BR>—याम्योद्भूत (˚या-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, aris-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">Page0816-b+ 69</a>]<BR>ing or growing in the south; (अस्), m. a species of<BR>tree (= श्री-ताल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामकिनी
यामकिनी यामकिनी, f. = 2. यामि below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामदूत
यामदूत यामदूत, आस्, m. pl. (fr. यम-<BR>दूत), N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामरथ
यामरथ, अम्, n. (fr. यम-रथ), scil. व्रत,<BR>N. of a particular religious observance relating to<BR>Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामनेमि|यामनेमिः
यामनेमि यामनेमि, इस्, m., N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामल|यामलं
यामल यामल, अम्, n. = यमल, a pair;<BR>N. of a class of Tantra works, (often wrongly written<BR>जामल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामलायन
यामलायन (fr. यमल), see Gaṇa Pakṣādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामलीय
यामलीय, अम्, n. (fr. यामल), N. of a work<BR>or of a class of works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामातृ
यामातृ यामातृ, ता, or यामातृक, अस्, m.<BR>= जामातृ, a daughter's husband, son-in-law; [cf.<BR>Gr. εἰνάτερ-ες; Lat. janitr-i-c-es; Old Germ.<BR>eidum; Angl. Sax. adhum.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामायन
यामायन यामायन, अस्, m. (fr. यम), a<BR>patronymic of various authors of Vedic hymns; of<BR>Ūrdhva-kṛśana; of Kumāra; of Damana; of Deva-<BR>śravas; of Mathita; of Śaṅkha; of Saṅkasuka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामि|यामिः
यामि 2. यामि, इस्, or यामी, f. (for 1. यामि<BR>see p. 814, col. 2), = जामि, स्वसृ, a sister, female<BR>relation; a daughter-in-law; a woman of rank or<BR>respectability (= कुल-स्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामेय|यामेयः
2. यामेय, अस्, m. (for 1. see p. 814, col. 2), a<BR>sister's son, nephew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिक|यामिकः
यामिक यामिक. See p. 814, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामित्र|यामित्रं
यामित्र यामित्र, अस्, m. = जामित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनी
यामिनी यामिनी, यामीर. See. p. 814, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामी
यामी यामी. See under 1. याम, p. 814,<BR>col. 1, and 2. यामि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुन|यामुनं
यामुन यामुन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यमुना), be-<BR>longing or relating to the river Yamunā (commonly<BR>called Jumna), coming from it, growing in it, &c.;<BR>(अस्), m. a metronymic; N. of a mountain; of an<BR>author; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (अम्), n.,<BR>scil. आञ्जन, antimony, collyrium; N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—यामुनाचार्य (˚न-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a pre-<BR>ceptor (author of the Stotra-ratna).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुनेष्टक|यामुनेष्टकं
यामुनेष्टक यामुनेष्टक, अम्, n. lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुन्दायनि
यामुन्दायनि यामुन्दायनि, इस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Yamunda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुन्दायनिक
यामुन्दायनिक or यामुन्दायनीय, अस्, m.<BR>patronymics from Yamunda, (used contemptuously,<BR>cf. Pāṇ. IV. 1, 149.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्य|याम्यः
याम्य याम्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायजूक|यायजूकः
यायजूक यायजूक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. 1. यज्), frequently sacrificing, constantly mak-<BR>ing offerings, devout; (अस्), m. a performer of fre-<BR>quent sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायात
यायात यायात, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Ya-<BR>yāti, belonging to Yayāti, &c.; (अम्), n., N. of the<BR>eighteenth chapter of the ninth book of the Bhāga-<BR>vata-Purāṇa (containing an account of Yayāti).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायावर|यायावरः
यायावर यायावर, यायिन्. See p. 814,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यार्कायण
यार्कायण यार्कायण, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव|यावः
याव 1. याव = 1. यव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव|यावः
याव 2. याव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. यव), relat-<BR>ing to barley, consisting of barley, made or prepared<BR>from barely, = यावक; (अस्), m. a kind of food<BR>prepared from barley; lac or the red dye prepared<BR>from the cochineal insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावक|यावकं|यावकः
यावक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind of food prepared<BR>from barley, barley-gruel; half ripe barley; awnless<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-c" target="_blank">Page0816-c+ 80</a>]<BR>barley; forced rice; a sort of kidney-bean; a kind<BR>of pulse, Dolichos Biflorus; a kind of pulse said to<BR>be peculiar to Kaśmīra; lac, the red dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावक्रीतिक
यावक्रीतिक, अस्, m. (fr. यव-क्रीत), one con-<BR>versant with the history of Yava-krīta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावत्|यावन्त्
यावत् यावत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. the pronom.<BR>base 3. य; correlative of तावत्, q. v.), as great, as<BR>large, as much, as many (= Lat. quot), as often, as<BR>far, as long, how much, how many, of what sort<BR>or kind, (for examples see तावत्); यावत्-तावत्,<BR>‘quantum-tantum,’ an expression used in algebra<BR>for the relation of the first unknown quantity and<BR>its co-efficient); यावन्तः कियन्तः, as many as.<BR>यावत्, ind. (i. e. acc. sing. neut. used adverbially),<BR>as greatly, as much as, as many as, as often as; as far<BR>as, as long as, while, whilst, during; meanwhile, in the<BR>mean time; as soon as, the moment that; till, until,<BR>until such a time as (with pres. or pot. or fut. or aor.<BR>or impf.); that, in order that; when (followed by<BR>the correlative तावत्, meaning ‘then’); even, just.<BR>यावत् meaning ‘during,’ ‘for,’ ‘until,’ ‘up to,’ ‘as<BR>far as,’ &c. is often used like a preposition with an<BR>acc. (e. g. वर्षं यावत्, for a year; मासम्<BR>एकं यावत्, during one month; यावद् वर्षाणि<BR>द्वादश, for twelve years; शतं जन्मानि यावत्,<BR>for a hundred births; सूर्योदयं यावत्, until<BR>sunrise; सर्प-विवरं यावत्, up to the serpent's<BR>hole); or with indeclinable words like अद्य (e. g.<BR>अद्य यावत्, up to to-day); or sometimes with a<BR>nominative followed by इति (e. g. अन्त इति यावत्, as<BR>far as the end; त्रिंशद् इति यावत्, as many as thirty,<BR>up to thirty; पञ्च यावद् इति, up to five); यावद्-आ<BR>and sometimes even यावत् alone may be used with<BR>a following abl. to express ‘up to,’ ‘as far as,’<BR>‘until,’ &c. (e. g. यावद्-आ समापनात् or simply<BR>यावत् समापनात्, until the completion); यावन्<BR>न, as long as not, before that, until that; न<BR>परम् or न केवलम् — यावत्, not only — but also;<BR>यावता, ind. (i. e. inst. c. used adverbially), as far as,<BR>as long as; up to, until; as soon as, the moment<BR>that; यावति, ind. (i. e. loc. c. used adverbially),<BR>as far as, as long as, &c.; [cf. Gr. ἧμος; Lat. quan-<BR>tus?].<BR>—यावच्-छक्यम्, ind. (i. e. यावत् + शक्-<BR>यम्), as far as possible, according to ability.<BR>—या-<BR>वच्-छस्, ind. (i. e. यावत् + शस्), Ved. as often as,<BR>as many times as, in as many ways as.<BR>—यावच्-<BR>छस्त्रम्, ind. (i. e. यावत् + श्˚), Ved. as far as<BR>the Śastra extends.<BR>—यावच्-छेषम्, ind. (i. e.<BR>यावत् + श्˚), Ved. as much as is left, as many as<BR>remain.<BR>—यावच्-छ्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (i. e. यावत्<BR>+ श्˚), Ved. the best possible.<BR>—यावच्-छ्लोकम्,<BR>ind. (i. e. यावत् + श्˚), according to the number<BR>of the Ślokas.<BR>—यावज्-जन्म, ind. throughout<BR>life, all one's life long.<BR>—यावज्-जीवम् or यावज्-<BR>जीवेन, ind. throughout life, during the whole<BR>of life, for life, for the rest of life.<BR>—यावज्जीविक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. life-long, as long as life, lasting for<BR>life.<BR>—यावज्जीविक-ता, f. the lasting for life.<BR>—या-<BR>वत्-कपालम्, ind., Ved. according to the circum-<BR>ference of the cup or bowl.<BR>—यावत्-कामम्, ind.,<BR>Ved. as much as one likes, according to desire,<BR>—यावत्-कालम्, ind. for the whole period, as long<BR>as (anything may last).<BR>—यावत्-कृत्वस्, ind., Ved.<BR>as often as, as many times as.<BR>—यावत्-तरसम्,<BR>ind., Ved. according to power or ability (= यावद्-<BR>बलम्, यथा-शक्ति).<BR>—यावत्-त्मूत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. as far as soaked with fat.<BR>—यावत्-प्रमाण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, as great, as big, as large.<BR>—यावत्-सं-<BR>सारम्, ind. as long as the world lasts.<BR>—यावत्-<BR>सत्त्वम्, ind. as far as ability goes, to the best of<BR>one's understanding.<BR>—यावत्-सबन्धु, ind., Ved.<BR>as far as relationship extends, inclusive of all relations.<BR>—यावत्-समस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, as many as form the<BR>whole, large as it is.<BR>—यावत्-स्वम्, ind., Ved. as<BR>much as one possesses, according to one's property.<BR>—यावद्-अङ्गीन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. forming as large<BR>a member or limb.<BR>—यावद्-अन्तम् or यावद्-अन्-<BR>ताय, ind. as far as the end, to the last.<BR>—यावद्-<BR>अभीक्ष्णम्, ind. for a moment's duration, for an<BR>instant.<BR>—यावद्-अमत्रम्, ind. corresponding to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">Page0817-a+ 71</a>]<BR>the number of the vessels, as many drinking-vessels<BR>as (there may be).<BR>—यावद्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, as<BR>many as necessary, corresponding to requirement;<BR>(अम्), ind. as much as may be useful, according to<BR>need.<BR>—यावद्-अह, अम्, n., Ved. the corresponding<BR>day (‘the how-manieth day’).<BR>—यावद्-आ-भूत-<BR>सम्प्लवम्, ind. up to the dissolution of the crea-<BR>tion, to the end of the world.<BR>—यावदायुः-प्र-<BR>माण, अस्, आ, अम्, measured by the duration of life,<BR>lasting for life.<BR>—यावद्-आयुषम्, ind., Ved. as<BR>long as life lasts, all through life, for the whole of<BR>life.<BR>—यावद्-आयुस्, ind. as long as life lasts, all<BR>through life, for life.<BR>—यावद्-इत्थम्, ind. as much<BR>as necessary.<BR>—यावद्-ईप्सितम्, ind. as far as agree-<BR>able, as much as desired.<BR>—यावद्-उक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. as far as stated, as much as stated.<BR>—यावद्-<BR>उत्तमम्, ind. up to the furthest limit or boundary.<BR>—यावद्-गमम्, ind. as fast as one can go, as<BR>quickly as possible.<BR>—यावद्-बलम्, ind. as far as<BR>strength goes, as long as strength lasts, to the best of<BR>one's ability, with all one's might or strength.<BR>—या-<BR>वद्-भाषित, अस्, आ, अम्, as far as has been said, as<BR>much as said.<BR>—यावद्-राज्यम्, ind. for the whole<BR>reign.<BR>—यावद्-वेदम्, ind. as much as gained or<BR>obtained.<BR>—यावद्-व्याप्ति, ind. to the utmost reach<BR>or extent.<BR>—यावन्-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having which<BR>measure, of which size, as large, extending as far;<BR>moderate, insignificant, unimportant, diminutive,<BR>little; (अम्), ind. in some measure or degree, a<BR>little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0816-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावतिथ|यावतिथः
यावतिथ, अस्, ई, अम् (a kind of ordinal of यावत्<BR>or, according to some, an old superl.), ‘the how-<BR>manieth,’ ‘as-manieth,’ in how many soever degrees<BR>advanced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन्
यावन् 2. यावन् = 1. यव. (For 1. यावन्<BR>see p. 814, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन्
यावन् 3. यावन् (fr. rt. 1. यु) in ऋण-यावन्,<BR>q. v.; [cf. 2. यव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन|यावनः
यावन 1. यावन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यवन;<BR>for 2. see col. 2, for 3. see col. 3), born or produced<BR>in the land of the Yavanas; (अस्), m. incense (as<BR>coming from the country of the Yavanas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावनाल|यावनालः
यावनाल यावनाल, अस्, m. = यव-नाल,<BR>q. v.; (ई), f. sugar extracted from Yava-nāla.<BR>—या-<BR>वनाल-निभ or यावनाल-शर, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of cane or reed resembling the Yāvanāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावयत्
यावयत् यावयत्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावशूक|यावशूकः
यावशूक यावशूक, अस्, m. (fr. यव-शूक)<BR>= यव-क्षार, a kind of alkaline salt prepared<BR>from the ashes of burnt barley-straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावस|यावसः
यावस यावस, अस्, m. (fr. यवस), a heap<BR>or quantity of grass; fodder, provender, provisions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावास
यावास यावास (fr. यवास), see Gaṇa Pa-<BR>lāśādi to Pāṇ. IV. 3, 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव्य|याव्यं
याव्य याव्य. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याशु
याशु याशु, n. (perhaps connected with rt.<BR>यस्), embracing, embrace, sexual union, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 126, 6. याशूनि = प्रजनन-<BR>सम्बन्धीनि कर्माणि = भोगाः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याशोधरेय|याशोधरेयः
याशोधरेय याशोधरेय (fr. यशो-धरा),<BR>अस्, m. a metronymic of Rāhula (the son of Śākya-<BR>muni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याशोभद्र
याशोभद्र याशोभद्र (fr. यशो-भद्र), अस्,<BR>m., N. of the fourth day of the civil month (कर्म-<BR>मास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याष्टीक|याष्टीकः
याष्टीक याष्टीक (fr. 2. यष्टि), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>armed with a stick or club, having a staff of office;<BR>(अस्), m. a warrior armed with a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास|यासः
यास यास, अस्, m. = यवास, Alhagi Mau-<BR>rorum; (आ), f. a species of thrush, Turdus Salica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास्क|यास्कः
यास्क यास्क, अस्, m. (fr. यस्क), a patro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">Page0817-b+ 78</a>]<BR>nymic, N. of the author of the Nirukta or commen-<BR>tary on the difficult Vedic words contained in the<BR>lists called Nighaṇṭus, (these consist of three divisions,<BR>1. the Naighaṇṭuka or a list of synonymous words,<BR>2. the Naigama or words usually occurring in the<BR>Veda only, 3. the Daivata or words relating to deities<BR>and sacrificial acts; according to some, these three<BR>lists were drawn up by Yāska himself, and then com-<BR>mented on in his Nirukta, which quotes Vedic pas-<BR>sages in illustration of the words, and is the oldest<BR>Vedic commentary extant; Yāska is supposed to<BR>have lived before Pāṇini); (आस्), m. pl. the pupils of<BR>Yaska.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास्कायनि
यास्कायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Yāska.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास्कायनीय
यास्कायनीय or यास्कीय, आस्, m. pl. the pupils<BR>of Yāskāyani.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यित्थ
यित्थ यित्थ, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियक्षत्
यियक्षत् यियक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or यिय-<BR>क्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Desid. of rt. 1. यज्),<BR>purposing to sacrifice, wishing to worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियक्षु
यियक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing or intending to<BR>sacrifice, desirous of worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियविषु
यियविषु यियविषु. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियासु
यियासु यियासु. See p. 814, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
यु 1. यु (said in Dhātu-pāṭha XXIV. 23.<BR>to be अ-मिश्रणे, i. e. the opposite in meaning<BR>to rt. 2. यु below, which is मिश्रणे, but rt. 1. यु is<BR>entirely Vedic), cl. 3. P. युयोति, (युयुधि according<BR>to Pāṇ. III. 4, 88); Impv. 2nd sing. युयोधि; the<BR>other forms are Vedic, e. g. युयोत, युयवत्, यु-<BR>वन्त, अयावि, यावीस्, यूषम्, योषत्, योषति,<BR>यौषुस्, यौष्टम्, यौस्, Inf. योतवे, योतवै,<BR>योतोस्, Ved. to separate, remove, exclude, ward off;<BR>to protect from (with abl.); to keep off (with acc.);<BR>to drive away, scatter, (Sāy. = पृथक्-कृ); to keep<BR>apart, to be or remain separate, (Sāy. = पृथग्-<BR>भू); cl. 10. A. यावयते, &c., to despise (?):<BR>Caus. यवयति, यावयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>separate or remove or keep off, &c.: Intens. योयू-<BR>यते, योयवीति, to be violently separated or rent<BR>asunder, (Sāy. = अत्यर्थम् पृथग्-भू.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन|यावनः
2. यावन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.; for 1. यावन<BR>see col. 1, for 3. see col. 3), the act of removing or<BR>keeping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावयत्
यावयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. the Caus.), causing to<BR>keep off, warding off, protecting.<BR>—यावयत्-सख,<BR>अस्, m. a protecting friend or companion.<BR>—याव-<BR>यद्-द्वेषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. driving away hostile<BR>beings (said of Uṣas, who is supposed to make the<BR>Rākṣasas and other malignant spirits vanish at her<BR>approach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत्
1. युत्, त्, त्, त् (for rt. 2. युत् see s.v.), keeping off,<BR>preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत|युतं|युतः
1. युत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see col. 3), separated,<BR>separate.<BR>—युत-द्वेषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. delivered<BR>from enemies, relieved from foes, (Sāy. = पृथग्-<BR>भूत-शत्रुक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
यु 2. यु (allied to rt. 1. युज्), cl. 2. P.,<BR>cl. 9. P.A. यौति (3rd pl. युवन्ति), युनाति,<BR>युनीते, युयाव (2nd sing. युयविथ, 3rd pl. यु-<BR>युवुस्), युयुवे, यविष्यति, -ते, अयावीत्, अय-<BR>विष्ट, यवितुम्, (these forms are rarely found in<BR>classical Sanskrit, but the following are found in the<BR>older language, यौमि, युवते, युवासे, युवस्व,<BR>अयुवत, युते, युवते, युताम्, (नि) युयोतम्, यु-<BR>यवत्, युयुवे, युविता, (नि)यूय), to attach, har-<BR>ness, bind, fasten; to join, unite, connect; to mix,<BR>combine; to gain possession of (Ved.); to bestow,<BR>confer (Ved.); to worship, honour (according to<BR>Naigh. III. 14): Pass. यूयते, 1st Fut. याविता, 2nd<BR>Fut. याविष्यते, Aor. अयावि, Prec. याविषीष्ट,<BR>to be joined or mixed: Caus. यावयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अयीयवत्: Desid. of Caus. यियावयिषति:<BR>Desid. यियविषति, युयूषति, to wish to unite or<BR>join; to yoke: Intens. योयूयते, योयवीति, योयोति,<BR>to unite very closely; [cf. Gr. ζώ-ννυ-μι (perhaps<BR>for ζωσνυμι), ζώ-νη, ζῶστρον; Lat. juvare, jus,<BR>juro, jubere.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन|यावनः
3. यावन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.; for 1. see<BR>col. 1, for 2. see col. 2), the act of uniting or join-<BR>ing, mixing, mingling, blending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव्य|याव्यं
याव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be joined or mixed, to be<BR>united or mingled; miscible; = याप्य, unimportant,<BR>insignificant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियविषा
यियविषा, f. (fr. the Desid.), the wish to mix<BR>or blend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियविषु
यियविषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to mix or blend;<BR>wishing to fill or cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत|युतं|युतः
2. युत, अस्, आ, अम् (often at the end of comps.),<BR>fastened to or on, attached to [cf. वडिश-य्˚]; added,<BR>joined, united; connected or joined with, accom-<BR>panied, attended by, furnished with, endowed with,<BR>possessed of, filled with, covered with; (अम्), n. a<BR>particular measure of length = 4 Hastas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युतक|युतकं
युतक, अस्, आ, अम्, attached, connected, joined,<BR>united; (अम्), n. a pair, couple; union, alliance,<BR>friendship, forming friendship; a nuptial gift or<BR>present (= यौतक); a sort of cloth or dress; a sort<BR>of dress worn by women; the edge of a garment,<BR>border of a woman's dress; the edge of a winnow-<BR>ing basket; suspicion, doubt, uncertainty (= सं-<BR>शय); an asylum, refuge (= सं-श्रय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युति|युतिः
युति, इस्, f. uniting, joining, junction, union; the<BR>being furnished with (with inst.); the obtaining pos-<BR>session of; the sum, total number; (in arithmetic)<BR>addition; (in astronomy) conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
यु 3. यु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. 1. या), Ved.<BR>going, moving, (Sāy. = गच्छत्); coming to<BR>misfortune, incurring evil, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>18, 13 = यातृ, अपगमन-शील or दुःखं<BR>गच्छत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
यु 4. यु, the actual base of the dual and<BR>plural numbers of the second personal pro-<BR>noun, (see युष्मद्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्
युक् युक् (?) or युत् (?), ind. badly, ill;<BR>(these appear to be wrong forms.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्त|युक्तं|युक्तः
युक्त युक्त, युक्ति, &c. See p. 818.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग युग, युग्म, युग्य, &c. See p. 818,<BR>col. 2, and p. 819, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगत्
युगत् युगत्, in Naigh. II. 15. a various<BR>reading for द्यु-गत्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युङ्ग्
युङ्ग् युङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. युङ्गति, युयुङ्ग,<BR>युङ्गितुम्, to desert, relinquish, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युङ्ग
युङ्ग युङ्ग in अ-युङ्ग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युङ्गिन्
युङ्गिन् युङ्गिन्, ई, m., N. of a particular<BR>mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युछ्|युच्छ्
युछ् युछ् (connected with rt. 1. यु), cl.<BR>1. P. युच्छति, युयुच्छ, युच्छितुम्,<BR>to leave, quit, go away, depart (Ved.); to err, be<BR>negligent or inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् 1. युज् (connected with rt. 2. यु),<BR>cl. 7. P. A. युनक्ति, युङ्क्ते (said to be<BR>also cl. 1. P. योजति), युयोज, युयुजे (Ved. 3rd pl.<BR>युयुज्रे), योक्ष्यति, -ते, अयुजत् or अयौक्षीत्,<BR>अयुक्त (epic forms (अनु)युञ्जसे, 3rd sing. युञ्जते,<BR>अयुञ्जम्, युञ्जत; Vedic forms युजे, युनजते,<BR>योज, योजम्, योजते, युयोजते, अयुजि, अयुज्रन्,<BR>युजन्त, अयुक्षत), योक्तुम् (Ved. Inf. युजे),<BR>to yoke, join, attach, join together, unite, fasten,<BR>connect, add; to harness, put to (horses, &c.); to<BR>join one's self to, come into union or conjunction<BR>with (e. g. रोहिणीं शशी युनक्ति, the moon unites<BR>with Rohiṇī); to adhere, cleave to (A.); to apply,<BR>fit, fix; to use, employ, make use of; to make<BR>ready, prepare, fit out, arrange; to appoint, institute;<BR>to enjoin, charge; to put on, place on, fix on, fasten<BR>on (as an arrow on a bow-string); to put in, infix,<BR>insert, inject; to fix the mind (मनस्, चित्तम्, &c.)<BR>on anything (loc.); to direct, turn, bend the thoughts<BR>(चिन्ताम्, &c.) towards any object (loc.); to concen-<BR>trate or fix the mind (in order to obtain union with<BR>the Universal Spirit); to be absorbed or deeply en-<BR>gaged in meditation, meditate, think upon; to join<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0818-a" target="_blank">Page0818-a+ 81</a>]<BR>or connect with (with inst.), bring into the posses-<BR>sion of, furnish or endow with (with inst.), bestow<BR>anything (acc.) upon any one (loc. or gen.), grant,<BR>confer: Pass. युज्यते (ep. also युज्यति), Aor. अयोजि,<BR>to be yoked or joined; to be fastened or united; to<BR>be harnessed; to be put to; to join or connect one's<BR>self with, be in conjunction with, to adhere, cleave<BR>to; to be applied; to be fit or proper, to be adapted<BR>or suitable, to be right; to be made ready or pre-<BR>pared; to be placed or fixed on, to be directed<BR>towards; to be absorbed or immersed in; to medi-<BR>tate; to be joined or endowed with or possessed of<BR>(with inst.); to participate in, attain to, possess,<BR>obtain (with inst.): Caus. योजयति, -यते, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अयूयुजत्, to cause to join or unite; to cause<BR>union or conjunction; to yoke, harness, put to; to<BR>join, unite, fasten, connect, add; to apply, fix, fit,<BR>place, lay; to use, make use of; to prepare, arrange,<BR>equip, undertake, execute; to appoint, employ, com-<BR>mission, appoint to (with loc.); to fix on, place on<BR>or in; to fix the mind (मनस् or आत्मानम्) on,<BR>direct the thoughts &c. to (with loc.); to concen-<BR>trate the attention on, be immersed or engrossed in<BR>(with loc.); to furnish or endow with (with inst.);<BR>to make to possess or partake of (with inst.), cause<BR>to share in, present with, bestow upon; to urge or<BR>incite any one (acc.) to anything (dat.), to excite,<BR>instigate; to surround; to think little of, esteem<BR>lightly, despise (A.): Desid. युयुक्षति, -ते, to<BR>wish to join or unite, to desire to appoint, to desire<BR>to place in any employment or occupation; to wish<BR>to fix or place; to be about to place or put on; to<BR>intend to fix (the mind) on; to wish to be absorbed<BR>in: Intens. योयुज्यते, योयुजीति, योयोक्ति; [cf. Gr.<BR>ζεύγ-νυ-μι (ἐ-ζύγ-η-ν), ζεῦγ-μα, ζεῦγ-ος, ὁμό-ζυξ,<BR>σύ-ζυξ, ζυγ-ό-ς, ζυγ-ό-ν; Lat. ju-n-g-o, ju-men-<BR>tu-m, con-jux, jug-u-m, jugeru-m, juxta; Goth.<BR>juk, ga-juk; Old Germ. joh, joch; Angl. Sax. geo-<BR>can, geoce; Slav. ig-o; Lith. junga-s, jung-iu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0817-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्त|युक्तं|युक्तः
युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, yoked, joined, united, con-<BR>nected, attached, fastened, harnessed; used, em-<BR>ployed, prepared, fitted out, arranged, ready, arranged<BR>in regular order, adapted, fitted, fit, suitable, just,<BR>proper, right, moderate, due, (युक्तः कालेन यः,<BR>one who makes use of the right opportunity; आयति-<BR>युक्त, suitable or profitable for the future); ap-<BR>pointed, engaged, occupied; fixed on, intent on<BR>(with loc. or at the end of a comp.); occupied with,<BR>immersed in, engaged in, absorbed in, attentive,<BR>attached to, given up or devoted to, absorbed in<BR>abstract meditation or in the religious exercise called<BR>Yoga; exercised in, skilled in, experienced, skilful,<BR>clever; active, energetic; joined with, furnished<BR>with, endowed with, filled with, possessed of, having,<BR>possessing (with inst. or at the end of a comp.);<BR>connected with, relating to; proved, inferred, de-<BR>duced by argument; (in gram.) primitive, i. e. not<BR>derivative; (अम्), ind. collectively, in troops (Ved.);<BR>suitably, properly, rightly, fitly, duly, well; (अस्), m.<BR>a sage or saint who has become united with the<BR>Universal Soul, one who is so absorbed in meditating<BR>on the Supreme Spirit as to be free from all feeling<BR>and passion; N. of a son of Manu Raivata; of one<BR>of the seven Ṛṣis under Manu Bhautya; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a plant (commonly called Elāni, cf. युक्त-<BR>रसा); (अम्), n. a team, yoke; a measure of four<BR>cubits, (incorrectly for 2. युत.)<BR>—युक्त-कर्मन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, invested with any office or function, ap-<BR>pointed to any work.<BR>—युक्त-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or<BR>युक्त-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, doing properly or suitably, acting<BR>fitly.<BR>—युक्त-ग्रावन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having the<BR>stone (for bruising the Soma) prepared, (Sāy. =<BR>उद्यत-ग्रावन्.)<BR>—युक्त-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most<BR>fit; most absorbed in or intent on, very much<BR>devoted to.<BR>—युक्त-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more fit, very<BR>intent on or attentive, very much on one's guard<BR>(Manu VII. 186).<BR>—युक्त-त्व, अम्, n. application,<BR>use, employment; suitableness, fitness, propriety.<BR>—युक्त-दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, employing or applying<BR>punishment; punishing justly.<BR>—युक्तदण्ड-ता, f.<BR>the inflicting of just punishment.<BR>—युक्त-मनस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0818-b" target="_blank">Page0818-b+ 81</a>]<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, ready-minded, fixing the mind, attentive.<BR>—युक्त-मांसल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. properly stout or<BR>fleshy.<BR>—युक्त-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a particular kind<BR>of cleansing clyster; of a sort of elixir.<BR>—युक्त-रसा,<BR>f. a species of plant (= युक्ता).<BR>—युक्त-रूप, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, suitably formed, symmetrical, suitable, proper,<BR>fit, moderate; fit for, corresponding to (with loc. or<BR>gen.); (अम्), ind. suitably.<BR>—युक्त-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. containing the verb युज्.<BR>—युक्त-शीतोष्ण<BR>(˚त-उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of moderate cold and heat.<BR>—युक्त-सेन, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose army is ready<BR>(for marching).<BR>—युक्तसेनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating<BR>to one whose army is ready for marching.<BR>—युक्ता-<BR>यस् (˚त-अय्˚), अस्, n. ‘bound with iron,’ a sort of<BR>spade or shovel.<BR>—युक्तायुक्त (˚त-अय्˚), अम्, n.<BR>the proper and improper, right and wrong.<BR>—युक्-<BR>तारोहिन् (˚त-आर्˚), ई, इणी, इ, see Pāṇ. VI. 2, 81.<BR>—युक्तार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having mean-<BR>ing, filled with significance, sensible, rational, signi-<BR>ficant.<BR>—युक्ताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing yoked horses; consisting of horses, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda V. 41, 5 = अश्व-सहित, ac-<BR>companied with horses.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्ति|युक्तिः
युक्ति, इस्, f. yoking, joining, junction, juncture,<BR>union, connection, combination; putting to, harness-<BR>ing; application, use, employment, practice, usage;<BR>appliance, means, plan, scheme, expedient, (द्रव्य-<BR>युक्तिभिस्, by the appliances of money); trick, con-<BR>trivance, device, stratagem; charm, spell; suitableness,<BR>adaptedness, adjustment, fitness, aptness, propriety,<BR>correctness; skill, dexterity, ingenuity, art; reasoning,<BR>argument, argumentation, inference, induction, deduc-<BR>tion from circumstances; probability, provableness;<BR>reason, ground, motive; (in the drama) connection<BR>of events in the plot, concatenation of incidents, in-<BR>telligent weighing of the circumstances; (in gram.)<BR>connection of words, a sentence; (in law) enumera-<BR>tion of circumstances, specification of place, time,<BR>&c.; (in rhetoric) emblematic or mystical expression<BR>of purpose; supplying an ellipsis; sum, total; mix-<BR>ture or alloying of metals; conjunction (in astro-<BR>nomy); युक्त्या, inst. c. by means of, by virtue of<BR>(at the end of a comp.); by device or stratagem,<BR>cunningly, craftily, cleverly, artfully, skilfully, under<BR>pretext or pretence; properly, suitably, fitly, duly;<BR>युक्तिं कृ, to make arrangements, take measures;<BR>to find a means, discover a remedy; to employ<BR>stratagem.<BR>—युक्ति-कथन, अम्, n. statement of<BR>argument, giving reasons.<BR>—युक्ति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>causing fitness, suitable, proper, fit; established,<BR>proved.<BR>—युक्ति-कल्प-तरु, उस्, m. [cf. कल्प-<BR>तरु], ‘Kalpa tree of prosperity,’ N. of a work<BR>ascribed to king Bhoja (describing the virtues and<BR>good qualities that ought to be found in a king's<BR>ministers, army, &c.).<BR>—युक्ति-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing the proper application, knowing the means<BR>or remedy; skilled in mixing (substances).<BR>—युक्ति-<BR>तस्, ind. by means of, by virtue of (at the end of a<BR>comp.); by stratagem or craft, craftily, cleverly,<BR>artfully, under some pretence or pretext; in a suitable<BR>manner, properly, fitly, duly, according to propriety<BR>or justice.<BR>—युक्ति-भाषा, f., N. of a work.<BR>—युक्-<BR>ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, joined, united, tied; possessing<BR>fitness, full of contrivances or plans, fertile in expe-<BR>dients, ingenious, clever, inventive, able, competent;<BR>furnished with arguments, based on argument, proved.<BR>—युक्तिमत्-त्व, अम्, n. the being based on argu-<BR>ment, the being proved.<BR>—युक्ति-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing fitness or aptness, experienced, expert,<BR>skilful; possessing fitness or reason, suitable, proper,<BR>fit; established, proved.<BR>—युक्ति-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the<BR>science of what is suitable or proper.<BR>—युक्ति-स्नेह-<BR>प्रपूरणी, f., N. of a commentary on the Śāstra-<BR>dīpikā by Rāma-kṛṣṇa Bhaṭṭa, (the work is also<BR>called Siddhānta-candrikā.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्त्वा
युक्त्वा, ind. having yoked, having joined, having<BR>harnessed; having equipped or furnished; (a form<BR>युङ्क्त्वा is also found.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग, अस्, अम्, m. n. a yoke; (अम्), n. a pair,<BR>couple, brace; a double Śloka or two Ślokas so con-<BR>nected that the sense is only completed by the two<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0818-c" target="_blank">Page0818-c+ 81</a>]<BR>together; a race or generation of men, (generally in<BR>Ved. with मानुष or मनुष्य); a period or<BR>astronomical cycle of five years, a lustrum, (especially<BR>such a period in the cycle of Jupiter); an age of the<BR>world, long mundane period of years, (of which there<BR>are four, each preceded by a period called सन्ध्या,<BR>‘twilight,’ and followed by a period called सन्ध्यांश,<BR>‘portion of twilight;’ viz. 1. Kṛta or Satya, 2. Tretā,<BR>3. Dvāpara, 4. Kali, of which the first three have<BR>already elapsed, while the Kali is that in which we<BR>are supposed to live; the first consists of 4000 divine<BR>years with 400 for each of its twilights, the second<BR>of 3000 with 300 for each twilight, the third of<BR>2000 with 200 for each twilight, the fourth or Kali<BR>of 1000 with 100 for each twilight; but since a divine<BR>year equals 360 years of men, the four Yugas com-<BR>prise severally 1, 728, 000, 1,296,000, 864,000,<BR>and 432, 000 years, the aggregate 4,320, 000 con-<BR>stituting ‘a great Yuga,’ or महा-युग, q. v.: the<BR>regularly descending numbers in the above series<BR>represent a corresponding physical and moral deteri-<BR>oration in those who live during each age, the present<BR>or Kali-yuga being the worst; this last Yuga is sup-<BR>posed to have commenced 3101 or 3102 years B.C.);<BR>a measure of length (= 4 Hastas or cubits); a sym-<BR>bolical expression for the number 4 and sometimes<BR>for the number 12; N. of a particular position or<BR>configuration of the moon; of a particular Nābhasa<BR>constellation (of the class called Saṅkhyā-yoga, when<BR>all the planets are situated in two houses); a species<BR>of drug or medicinal plant (= वृद्धि); [cf. Gr.<BR>ζυγόν; Lat. jugum; Angl. Sax. ioc, iuc, geoc.]<BR>—युग-कीलक, अस्, m. the pin of a yoke.<BR>—युग-<BR>क्षय, अस्, m. the end of a Yuga, destruction of<BR>the world.<BR>—युग-दीर्घ, अस्, आ, अम्, long as a<BR>chariot yoke.<BR>—युगन्-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, holding<BR>or bearing the yoke; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the pole of a<BR>carriage or wood to which the yoke is fixed; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a particular magical formula spoken over<BR>weapons; of a king; of a mountain; of a forest;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—युग-प, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Gandharva.<BR>—युग-पत्त्र or युग-पत्त्रक,<BR>अस्, m. mountain ebony, the plant Bauhinia Varie-<BR>gata.<BR>—युग-पत्त्रिका, f. the plant Dalbergia Sissoo.<BR>—युगपत्-प्राप्ति, इस्, f. simultaneous arrival, arriv-<BR>ing all together.<BR>—युग-पद्, ind. ‘being in the<BR>same yoke or by the side of each other,’ together,<BR>at one time, at the same time, simultaneously, at<BR>once, all at once, all together.<BR>—युग-पार्श्वक or<BR>युग-पार्श्व-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going at the side of<BR>the yoke (said of a young ox in training).<BR>—युग-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a section of the Garga-saṃ-<BR>hitā.<BR>—युग-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, ‘yoke-armed,’ having<BR>arms like a yoke, long armed.<BR>—युग-भङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. the breaking of a yoke.<BR>—युग-मात्र, अम्,<BR>n. the length of a yoke; (अस्, ई, अम्), as large as a<BR>yoke.<BR>—युग-वरत्र or युग-वरत्रा, see Gaṇa<BR>Khaṇḍikādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 45.<BR>—युग-व्यायत-<BR>बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, having arms long as a yoke; long<BR>armed.<BR>—युगांशक (˚ग-अं˚), अस्, m. ‘part of a<BR>Yuga or lustrum,’ a year, (also युगांसक.)<BR>—यु-<BR>गादि (˚ग-आदि), इस्, m. the commencement of a<BR>Yuga, the beginning of the world.<BR>—युगादि-कृत्,<BR>त्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—युगादि-जिन, अस्, m. the first<BR>Jina of a Yuga.<BR>—युगादिजिन-श्री, ईस्, m., N. of<BR>Ṛṣabha.<BR>—युगादीश (˚दि-ईश), अस्, m. ‘first lord<BR>of a Yuga,’ N. of Ṛṣabha.<BR>—युगाद्या (˚ग-आद्˚),<BR>f. the first day of a Yuga or age of the world; the<BR>anniversary of it.<BR>—युगाध्यक्ष (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘superintendent of a Yuga,’ epithet of Prajāpati;<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—युगान्त (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of<BR>the yoke; the meridian, midday, noon; the end<BR>of a generation; the end of an age or Yuga, destruc-<BR>tion of the world.<BR>—युगान्तक, अस्, m. the end of<BR>an age, end of the world.<BR>—युगान्त-बन्धु, उस्,<BR>m. a real and constant friend.<BR>—युगान्तर (˚ग-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. a kind of yoke, a peculiar yoke; the<BR>second half of the arc cutting the meridian described<BR>by the sun; another generation, a succeeding age.<BR>—युगान्ताग्नि (˚त-अग्˚), इस्, m. the fire at the end<BR>of the world.<BR>—युगेश (˚ग-ईश), अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">Page0819-a+ 81</a>]<BR>lord or ruler of a lustrum.<BR>—युगोरस्य (˚ग-उर्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a particular array of troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगल|युगलं
युगल, अम्, n. a pair, couple, brace, (उपानद्-<BR>युगलम्, a pair of shoes; कण्ठ-निवेशित-हस्त-<BR>युगला, having both her hands applied to her neck);<BR>‘double prayer,’ N. of a prayer offered up to<BR>Lakṣmī and Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—युगल-भक्त, आस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of a subdivision of the Caitanya Vaiṣṇavas.<BR>—युगलाख्य (˚ल-आख्˚), अस्, m. a species of<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगलक|युगलकं
युगलक, अम्, n. a pair, couple, brace; a couple<BR>of Ślokas or two verses so connected that the sense is<BR>only completed by the two together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगलाय
युगलाय, Nom. A. युगलायते, &c., to be like<BR>or represent a pair (of anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगलायित
युगलायित, अस्, आ, अम्, representing or like a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगाय
युगाय, Nom. A. युगायते, &c., to appear as<BR>long as a Yuga, to seem like eternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगिन्
युगिन् in वस्त्रयुगिन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्म|युग्मं
युग्म, अस्, आ, अम्, even [cf. अ-य्˚]; (अम्), n. a<BR>pair, couple, brace; twins; the sign of the zodiac<BR>Gemini; a couple of Ślokas or two verses so con-<BR>nected that the sense is only completed by the two<BR>together; junction, union, mixing, uniting; conflu-<BR>ence (of two streams).<BR>—युग्म-ज, औ, m. du.<BR>twins.<BR>—युग्म-पत्त्र, अस्, m. mountain ebony,<BR>Bauhinia Variegata (= युग-पत्त्र).<BR>—युग्म-<BR>पत्त्रिका, f. Dalbergia Sissoo (= युग-पत्त्रिका).<BR>—युग्म-पर्ण, अस्, m. Bauhinia Variegata; Al-<BR>stonia Scholaris.<BR>—युग्म-फला, f., N. of various<BR>plants (= इन्द्र-चिर्बिटी, वृश्चिकाली, गन्धिका).<BR>—युग्म-फलोत्तम (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, m. Asclepias<BR>Rosea.<BR>—युग्म-विपुला, f. a species of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मक
युग्मक, अस्, आ, अम्, even; (अम्), n. a pair,<BR>couple, brace; a couple of Ślokas or verses connected<BR>by the construction of the sentence (the sense being<BR>completed only by the two together).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मन्
युग्मन्, आ, आ, अ, or युग्मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>even.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मिन्
युग्मिन्, ई, इनी, इ, an adj. fr. युग्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्य|युग्यं|युग्यः
युग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or proper to be yoked or<BR>harnessed; belonging to a yoke; yoked, harnessed;<BR>drawn by (e. g. अश्व-युग्य, drawn by horses); any<BR>yoked or draught animal; (अम्), n. a vehicle, car-<BR>riage, car, chariot; जमदग्नेर् व्रतं युग्यम्,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR>—युग्य-वाह, अस्, m. a coachman,<BR>driver.<BR>—युग्य-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a car-<BR>riage, a person in a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
2. युज्, क्, क्, क् (often at the end of comps.;<BR>when uncompounded the strong cases ought to<BR>have a nasal inserted, e. g. युङ्, युञ्जौ, युञ्जस्,<BR>युञ्जम्, युञ्जौ), yoked, joined, connected, joined<BR>to, harnessed, drawn by, (चतुर्-युज्, drawn by four<BR>horses; अश्व-सहस्र-युज्, drawn by a thousand<BR>horses; हयोत्तम-युज्, drawn by the best horses);<BR>yoked or joined together, any one who is joined<BR>or yoked, a yoke-fellow, yoke-mate, companion;<BR>furnished or provided with, filled with, affected by,<BR>possessed of, possessing (e. g. प्रीति-युज्, possessing<BR>pleasure, pleased; काम-युज्, possessing, i. e. grant-<BR>ing desires, cf. धर्म-युज्); exciting, an exciter,<BR>(युङ् भियः, exciter of fear); in couples or pairs,<BR>even, not odd, not single, not separate [cf. अ-युज्];<BR>(क् or ङ्), m. a pair, couple, the number two; a<BR>joiner, one who joins or unites; one who devotes<BR>his time to abstract contemplation, a sage; a measure<BR>of 300 poles (?); युजौ, m. du. the sign of the<BR>zodiac Gemini; the two Aśvins; [cf. Lat. con-jux,<BR>con-jug-is.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज
युज = 2. युज्, ‘even,’ ‘not odd,’ in a few comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्य|युज्यः
युज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. connected, united, friendly;<BR>related, allied; suitable, fit, fitting, proper; of the same<BR>kind, homogeneous; a kinsman; (अम्), n. union,<BR>connection, relationship; जमदग्नेर् व्रतं युज्-<BR>यम्, N. of a Sāman, (also read युग्यम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्यमान
युज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being united or joined<BR>or connected with (with inst.); being furnished or<BR>provided with, possessing (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जक
युञ्जक, अस्, आ, अम्, applying, performing, exer-<BR>cising, practising, (ध्यान-युञ्जक, practising<BR>devotion.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जत्
युञ्जत्, अन्, अती, अत्, uniting, joining; uniting spi-<BR>ritually, practising devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जान|युंजान|युञ्जानः
युञ्जान, अस्, आ, अम्, uniting, combining, joining<BR>with; suitable, fitting, proper; successful, prosperous;<BR>(अस्), m. a driver, coachman, charioteer; a Brāhman,<BR>one who by the religious exercise called Yoga endea-<BR>vours to obtain union with the Supreme Soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जानक
युञ्जानक, अस्, आ, अम्, containing the word<BR>युञ्जान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुक्षमाण
युयुक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Desid.), wish-<BR>ing to join or unite; wishing to effect spiritual union<BR>(with the divine essence), devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुजान
युयुजान, अस्, आ, अम् (Perf. Part. A.), one who<BR>has yoked or joined.<BR>—युयुजान-सप्ति, ई, m. du.,<BR>Ved. having harnessed or yoked their horses (said of<BR>the two Aśvins; Sāy. = रथे युज्यमानाश्वौ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्तव्य
योक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be yoked or joined or<BR>united, to be united (spiritually); to be applied or<BR>made use of, applicable, practicable; to be appointed<BR>to (any office), to be charged with (with loc., e. g.<BR>कर्मणि योक्तव्यः, to be charged with a business);<BR>to be fixed on or directed to (as the mind); to be<BR>furnished or endowed with, to be made to be pos-<BR>sessed of (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्तृ
योक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who yokes or harnesses,<BR>a harnesser, driver, coachman; an exciter, rouser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्त्र|योक्त्रं
योक्त्र, अम्, n. any instrument for tying or fas-<BR>tening, a tie, fastening, band, cord, halter, rope,<BR>thong, girth; the tie of the yoke of a plough; the<BR>thongs by which an animal is attached to the pole<BR>of a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्त्रक
योक्त्रक, अम्, n. = योक्त्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्त्रय
योक्त्रय (fr. योक्त्र), Nom. P. योक्त्रयति, &c.,<BR>to tie, bind, fasten, wind round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग|योगः
योग, योग्य, &c. See p. 821, col. 2, and<BR>p. 823, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजन|योजनं
योजन, योजयितृ, योजितृ, योज्य, &c. See<BR>p. 823, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जन्द
युञ्जन्द युञ्जन्द, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत्
युत् 2. युत् (allied to rts. जुत्, ज्युत्, द्युत्;<BR>for 1. युत् see p. 817, col. 2), cl. 1. A.<BR>योतते, &c., to shine; [cf. Hib. iudh, ‘a day;’<BR>an-iudh, ‘to-day;’ iodhna, ‘brightness, purity;’<BR>‘clean, pure.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत|युतं|युतः
युत युत, युतक. See under rts. 1. and 2.<BR>यु, p. 817.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युति|युतिः
युति युति. See p. 817, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत्कार
युत्कार युत्-कार, युद्-भू. See under 2.<BR>युध्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्ध|युद्धं
युद्ध युद्ध. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्
युध् 1. युध्, cl. 4. A. P. (in Post-Vedic<BR>literature usually A. except where the metre<BR>requires P.) युध्यते (-ति), युयुधे (3rd pl. P.<BR>युयुधुः), योत्स्यते (योत्स्यति), अयुद्ध (अयो-<BR>धीत्), योद्धुम् (Ved. Inf. युधये), to fight,<BR>combat, oppose in battle (with acc.); to overcome<BR>in battle, conquer, vanquish (with acc.); to fight or<BR>contend with (with inst. or inst. with सह, e. g.<BR>शत्रुभिः or शत्रुभिः सह युध्यते, he fights<BR>with enemies); to fight for or about (with loc.,<BR>Ved.); to wage war, fight, engage in battle or war;<BR>(according to Naigh. II. 14) to go (P.): Pass. यु-<BR>ध्यते, to be fought: Caus. P. योधयति (rarely<BR>A. -ते), -यितुम्, Aor. अयूयुधत्, to cause to fight,<BR>make to fight with (with inst.); to order to fight;<BR>to make war upon, attack, fight against, oppose; to<BR>overcome in battle, vanquish, conquer; to defend:<BR>Pass. of Caus. योध्यते, to be made to fight, &c.:<BR>Desid. युयुत्सति, -ते (in ep. often P. on account<BR>of the metre), to be desirous or anxious to fight; to<BR>wish to conquer; to prepare to fight: Caus. of<BR>Desid. युयुत्सयति, to make desirous of fighting,<BR>make eager for battle: Intens. योयुध्यते, योयोद्-<BR>धि; [cf. Zend yud: Gr. ὑσ-μλιην, ὑσ-μίν: Hib.<BR>iodhna, ‘spears, arms’ (= आ-युध); iodnach,<BR>‘valiant;’ iodhlan, ‘a hero:’ (perhaps also) Angl.<BR>Sax. gudh: (perhaps) Old Germ. gund, ‘battle.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्ध|युद्धं
युद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fought, encountered; over-<BR>come, subdued, conquered; (अम्), n. war, battle,<BR>conflict, fight, combat, struggle, contest, strife, en-<BR>gagement; (in astronomy) opposition, conflict of the<BR>planets.<BR>—युद्ध-काण्ड, अम्, n. ‘battle-section,’<BR>N. of the sixth book of Vālmīki's Rāmāyaṇa; of<BR>the sixth book of the Adhyātma-rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—युद्-<BR>धकारि-त्व, अम्, n. making war, fighting.<BR>—युद्-<BR>ध-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, making war, fighting, con-<BR>tending, struggling, engaging in battle.<BR>—युद्ध-<BR>कीर्त्ति, इस्, m., N. of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—युद्ध-गान्धर्व, अम्, n. a battle like the<BR>dance of the Gandharvas.<BR>—युद्ध-जयार्णव<BR>(˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a section of the Jyotiḥ-<BR>śāstra.<BR>—युद्ध-जयोपाय (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—युद्ध-जित्, त्, त्, त्, victorious in battle.<BR>—युद्ध-द्यूत, अम्, n. the game of war, luck<BR>of battle, chance of war, (see द्यूत.)<BR>—युद्ध-<BR>धर्म, अस्, m. the law of war.<BR>—युद्ध-पराङ्-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, averse from fighting.<BR>—युद्ध-<BR>पुरी, f., N. of a town.<BR>—युद्ध-भू, ऊस्, or<BR>युद्ध-भूमि, इस्, f. battle-ground, a field of battle.<BR>—युद्ध-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of war, re-<BR>sulting from battle, relating to war, warlike, martial.<BR>—युद्ध-मार्ग, अस्, m. a mode of fighting,<BR>stratagem, manœuvre.<BR>—युद्ध-मुष्टि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Ugra-sena.<BR>—युद्ध-मेदिनी, f.<BR>battle-ground, a field of battle.<BR>—युद्ध-योजक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, preparing for war, eager for battle.<BR>—युद्ध-रङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘battle-arena,’ field of<BR>battle; (अस्, आ, अम्), whose arena is battle; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Kārttikeya.<BR>—युद्ध-वस्तु, उ, n. an<BR>implement of war.<BR>—युद्ध-विद्या, f. the science<BR>of war, military art.<BR>—युद्ध-वीर, अस्, m. ‘battle-<BR>hero,’ a valiant man, warrior, hero, champion; he-<BR>roism, bravery (as one of the Rasas).<BR>—युद्ध-<BR>शक्ति, इस्, f. warlike vigour or prowess.<BR>—युद्ध-<BR>शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, warlike, courageous, valiant, bold.<BR>—युद्ध-सार, अस्, m. ‘battle-goer,’ a horse.<BR>—युद्धाचार्य (˚ध-आच्˚), अस्, m. ‘war-pre-<BR>ceptor,’ a military instructor, one who teaches the<BR>use of arms.<BR>—युद्धाजि (˚ध-आजि), इस्, m., N. of<BR>a descendant of Aṅgiras.<BR>—युद्धाध्वन् (˚ध-<BR>अध्˚), आ, आ, अ, going or resorting to battle.<BR>—युद्-<BR>धार्थिन् (˚ध-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, desirous of war,<BR>seeking war.<BR>—युद्धावसान (˚ध-अव्˚), अम्, n.<BR>cessation of war, truce.<BR>—युद्धोद्यम (˚ध-<BR>उद्˚), or युद्धोद्योग (˚ध-उद्˚), अस्, m. pre-<BR>paring for battle, vigorous and active preparation for<BR>war.<BR>—युद्धोन्मत्त (˚ध-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘battle-mad,’ fierce or frantic in battle; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—युद्धोपकरण (˚ध-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a war implement, accoutrements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धक
युद्धक, अम्, n. = युद्ध, war, battle, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धिन्
युद्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, relating to war or battle, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्
2. युध्, त्, त्, त्, warring, fighting; a fighter, war-<BR>rior, soldier, hero, champion; (त्), f. war, fight,<BR>battle, combat, conflict, struggle, contest.<BR>—युत्-<BR>कार, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. making war, waging war,<BR>fighting, contending.<BR>—युद्-भू, ऊस्, f. battle-ground,<BR>a field of battle.<BR>—युधा-जित्, त्, त्, त् (युधा, inst. c.),<BR>conquering or vanquishing by means of war; (त्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Kroṣṭu by a woman called<BR>Mādrī; of a son of Kekaya (uncle of Bharata); of<BR>a son of Vṛṣṇi; of a king of Ujjayinī.<BR>—युधा-<BR>मन्यु, उस्, m. (युधा, inst. c.), N. of a warrior<BR>on the side of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—युधि-श्रेष्ठ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, pre-eminent in battle.<BR>—युधि-ष्ठिर, अस्,<BR>m. (युधि, loc. c. + स्थिर), ‘firm or steady in<BR>battle,’ N. of the eldest of the five reputed sons<BR>of Pāṇḍu, (though nominally the son of Pāṇḍu, he<BR>was really the child of Pṛthā or Kuntī, Pāṇḍu's wife,<BR>by the god Dharma or Yama, whence he is often<BR>called Dharma-putra or Dharma-rāja; as the eldest<BR>of the five Pāṇḍavas, he ultimately succeeded Pāṇḍu<BR>as king, first reigning over Indra-prastha, and after-<BR>wards, when the Kuru princes or sons of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra were defeated, at Hāstina-pura); N. of a son<BR>of Kṛṣṇa; of two kings of Kaśmīra; of a potter<BR>(in Pañca-tantra, p. 217); of a preceptor; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the descendants of Yudhi-ṣṭhira, son of Pāṇḍu.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">Page0820-a+ 80</a>]<BR>—युधिष्ठिर-पुरोगम, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>Yudhi-ṣṭhira as leader, led on by Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0819-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधांश्रौष्टि
युधांश्रौष्टि, इस्, m., Ved. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधाजि
युधाजि, cf. यौधाजय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधाजित्
युधा-जित्, युधा-मन्यु. See under 2. युध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधाजीव
युधाजीव, अस्, m. a proper N., (perhaps for<BR>युद्धाजीव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधान|युधानः
युधान, अस्, m. a man of the second or military<BR>order, a warrior; an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधासुर
युधासुर, अस्, m., N. of king Nanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधि
युधि, Ved. fighting, contending, battle, (usually<BR>occurring in the dat. युधये used as a Ved. Inf.<BR>in the sense ‘to fight.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिक|युधिकः
युधिक, अस्, आ, अम्, fighting, contending, (per-<BR>haps an incorrect form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिङ्गम|युधिंगम
युधिङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम् (युधिम्, acc. c.),<BR>Ved. going to battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिष्ठिर|युधिष्ठिरः
युधि-ष्ठिर. See under 2. युध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधेन्य
युधेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be fought with,<BR>to be overcome in battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्म|युध्मः
युध्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. warlike, material; (अस्),<BR>m. a warrior, champion, soldier, (Sāy. = योद्धृ);<BR>a battle, fight; an arrow; a bow; (according to<BR>some) = शेष-सङ्ग्राम; = शरभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्य
युध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be fought with; to be<BR>conquered or subdued, conquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्यमान
युध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, fighting, making war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्यामधि
युध्यामधि, इस्, m., Ved. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्वन्
युध्वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. warlike, martial, a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सत्
युयुत्सत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing to fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सा
युयुत्सा, f. (fr. the Desid.), the wishing to fight,<BR>desire for war, eagerness for battle, pugnacity, enmity.<BR>—युयुत्सा-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, without wish or in-<BR>tention to fight, cowardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सु|युयुत्सुः
युयुत्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to fight, desiring<BR>war, eager for battle; anxious to fight with (with<BR>inst. or with सह, सार्धम्, &c. with inst.); pug-<BR>nacious, hostile, ambitious; (उस्), m. a combatant;<BR>N. of one of the sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुधन्
युयुधन्, आ, m., N. of a king of Mithilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुधान|युयुधानः
युयुधान, अस्, m., N. of a son of Satyaka, (he<BR>was one of the allies of the Pāṇḍavas); a Kṣatriya,<BR>warrior; epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुधि
युयुधि or यूयुधि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. warlike,<BR>martial, pugnacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्स्यमान
योत्स्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, about to fight, ready to<BR>fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धव्य
योद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be fought or contended,<BR>to be overcome in battle, (the neuter may be used<BR>impersonally, e. g. कैर् मया सह योद्धव्यम्,<BR>by whom is it to be fought with me.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धुकाम
योद्धु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to fight,<BR>anxious for battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धृ
योद्धृ, धा, m. a fighter, warrior, champion,<BR>combatant, soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योध|योधः
योध, अस्, m. a fighter, warrior, champion, com-<BR>batant, soldier; battle, war (in दुर्-य्˚, मिथो-य्˚,<BR>q. q. v. v.); a kind of metre, four times ¯˘¯¯˘¯.<BR>—योध-धर्म, अस्, m. the law of soldiers,<BR>military law, duty of the Kṣatriya caste.<BR>—योध-<BR>मुख्य, अस्, m. a chief warrior, leader.<BR>—योध-<BR>वीर, अस्, m. a hero, warrior.<BR>—योध-संराव,<BR>अस्, m. challenging to battle, mutual defiance of<BR>combatants.<BR>—योध-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying<BR>warriors.<BR>—योधागार (˚ध-आग्˚), अस्, m. a soldier's<BR>dwelling, barrack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधक
योधक, अस्, m. = योध, a fighter, warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधन|योधनं|योधनः
योधन, अम्, n. the act of fighting, battle, war,<BR>strife.<BR>—योधन-पुर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधनीपुर
योधनी-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधयत्
योधयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, fighting, making war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधिक
योधिक, epithet of a particular mode of fighting;<BR>[cf. यौधिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधिन्
योधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fighting, contending, waging<BR>war, (at the end of comps., e. g. दिव्यास्त्र-योधिन्,<BR>fighting with divine weapons; cf. हय-य्˚); con-<BR>quering, subduing, a conqueror (e. g. दानव-<BR>योधिन्, conquering the Dānavas); (ई), m. a warrior.<BR>—योधि-वन, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधीयस्
योधीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of योध), more<BR>warlike or martial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधेय|योधेयः
योधेय, अस्, m. = योध, a warrior, combatant;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योध्य
योध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be fought, to be overcome<BR>in battle, to be conquered or subdued, conquerable;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युन्थ्
युन्थ् युन्थ् = rt. पुन्थ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युप्
युप् युप्, cl. 4. P. युप्यति, युयोप, अयु-<BR>पत्, &c., to confuse, trouble, perplex; to<BR>efface, destroy, obliterate; to make level or smooth;<BR>to be concealed, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>104, 4. युयोप = गूढम् आसीत्): Caus. योपयति,<BR>यितुम्, to efface, obliterate, destroy: Intens. यो-<BR>युप्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योपन|योपनं
योपन, अम्, n. the act of effacing (foot-prints<BR>or traces, &c.) or anything used for effacing or obli-<BR>terating; the act of oppressing, obstructing, molest-<BR>ing, perplexing, confusing, destroying, effacing, obli-<BR>terating (sometimes at the end of comps.; cf. पद-य्˚,<BR>जन-य्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योपयत्
योपयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, effacing, obliterating,<BR>obstructing, perplexing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयु|युयुः
युयु युयु, उस्, m. a horse, (probably incor-<BR>rect for ययु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुक्खुर|युयुक्खुरः
युयुक्खुर युयुक्-खुर, अस्, m. a hyena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सा
युयुत्सा युयुत्सा, युयुत्सु, युयुधान, &c.<BR>See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुवि
युयुवि युयुवि. See यूयुवि, p. 821, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युव
युव युव, the actual base of the dual of the<BR>second personal pronoun, (युवाम्, nom. acc. you two;<BR>युवाभ्याम्, inst. dat. abl.; युवयोस्, gen. loc.;<BR>Ved. forms युवम्, युवभ्याम्, युवोस्.)<BR>—युव-<BR>द्रिक्, ind., Ved. directed towards both of you.<BR>—युव-धित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. placed or arranged<BR>for you both; beneficial to you both, (Sāy. युवा-<BR>भ्यां विहित.)<BR>—युवा-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>given by both of you.<BR>—युवा-नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>brought by both of you.<BR>—युवा-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>yoked for you both, harnessed by you both.<BR>—युवा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. belonging to both of you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवत्|युवन्त्
1. युवत् (for 2. युवत् see col. 3), Ved. abl. du.<BR>of the 2nd personal pronoun, (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 109, 1. युवत् = युवाभ्याम्.)<BR>—युवद्-<BR>देवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having (each of) you for<BR>a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवयु
युवयु or युवायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. longing for<BR>both of you, (Sāy. युवयु = युवां कामयमा-<BR>न); intended for you both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवाकु
युवाकु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. belonging to both of you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवक|युवकः
युवक युवक. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवन्
युवन् युवन्, आ, युवति or युवती or यूनी, अ<BR>(said to be fr. rt. 2. यु, but according to some for<BR>द्युवन्, fr. 3. द्यु or rt. 2. दिव्, ‘to shine;’ com-<BR>par. यवीयस्, q. v.; superl. यविष्ठ, q. v.), young,<BR>youthful, juvenile, adult, arrived at puberty (applied<BR>to men or animals); endowed with native or natural<BR>strength, strong, excellent, good, healthy; (आ), m. a<BR>youth, young man, a young animal; (in the Veda<BR>युवन् is also applied to Indra, Agni, and various<BR>other gods); the younger descendant of any one (an<BR>elder descendant being still alive); N. of the ninth<BR>year in Jupiter's cycle of sixty years; (युवति, इस्),<BR>f. a girl, young woman, any youthful female, any<BR>young female animal, (इभ-युवति, a young female<BR>elephant; the term युवति is also applied in the<BR>Veda to Uṣas, Night and Morning, Heaven and<BR>Earth); turmeric; (युवती), f. = युवति, a young<BR>woman; the sign of the zodiac Virgo; [cf. Lat.<BR>juveni-s, jun-ior, Junius, junix: Goth. juggs:<BR>Angl. Sax. iong, iung, geong, geogudh: Lith.<BR>jauna-s: Slav. junu, ‘a youth;’ junosti, ‘youth.’]<BR>—युव-खलति, इस्, इस्, इ, bald in youth; युव-<BR>खलती, f. bald in girlhood.<BR>—युव-गण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>an eruption on the face of young people.<BR>—युव-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">Page0820-c+ 75</a>]<BR>जरत्, अन्, अती, अत्, appearing old in youth, becoming<BR>old at an early age.<BR>—युव-जानि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>having a young wife.<BR>—युव-ता, f. or युव-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. youthfulness, youth.<BR>—युवति-जन or यु-<BR>वती-जन, अस्, m. a young woman.<BR>—युवतीष्टा<BR>(˚ति-इष्˚), f. yellow jasmine (= स्वर्ण-यूथिका).<BR>—युव-पलित, अस्, आ (?), अम्, grey-haired in youth.<BR>—युव-प्रत्यय, अस्, m. a suffix forming the so-<BR>called Yuvan patronymics.<BR>—युव-मारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>Ved. dying in youth.<BR>—युव-राज, अस्, m. ‘young<BR>king,’ an heir-apparent associated with the reigning<BR>sovereign in the government, a crown prince; epithet<BR>of Maitreya the future Buddha; one of the Jaina<BR>Pontiffs.<BR>—युवराज-त्व or युव-राज्य, अम्, n.<BR>the rank or position of an heir-apparent to a throne.<BR>—युव-राजन्, आ, m. = युव-राज above.<BR>—युव-<BR>राज-शब्द-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, possessing the title of<BR>heir-apparent.<BR>—युव-वलिन, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>wrinkles in youth or at an early age.<BR>—युवी-भू,<BR>cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to become young.<BR>—युवी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवक|युवकः
युवक, अस्, m. = युवन्, a youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवत्|युवन्त्
2. युवत्, Ved. = युवन्, youthful, Ṛg-veda X.<BR>39, 8. (For 1. युवत् see col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवति|युवतिः
युवति or युवती. See under युवन्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवन्यु
युवन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. youthful, juvenile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवश
युवश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. young, youthful, juvenile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवन
युवन युवन (?), अस्, m. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवनाश्व|युवनाश्वः
युवनाश्व युवनाश्व, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>father of Māndhātṛ; of various persons.<BR>—युव-<BR>नाश्व-ज, अस्, m. the son of Yuvanāśva, i. e. Mān-<BR>dhātṛ (an early sovereign of the solar dynasty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवन्यु
युवन्यु युवन्यु, युव-राज, &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवा
युवा युवा, f., Ved., N. of one of Agni's<BR>arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवादत्त
युवादत्त युवा-दत्त, युवायु, &c. See<BR>under युव, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवाम
युवाम युवाम, N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्टग्राम
युष्टग्राम युष्ट-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मद्
युष्मद् युष्मद्, a form derived from युष्-<BR>मत्, abl. pl. of the pronominal base 4. यु, and<BR>serving for the base of the 2nd personal pronoun in<BR>the plural number and at the beginning of some<BR>compounds; the actual base, however, in most of<BR>the plural cases is युष्म, which is also found in a<BR>few compounds, cf. युष्मा-दत्त below; the fol-<BR>lowing forms are found, यूयम्, nom. pl. you;<BR>युष्मान्, acc. you; युष्माभिस्, inst. by you;<BR>युष्मभ्यम्, dat. to you; युष्मत् or युष्मत्-<BR>तस्, abl. from you; युष्माकम्, gen. of you, (in<BR>Ved. the final nasal may be dropped, e. g. युष्मा-<BR>कैक for युष्माकम् एक); युष्मासु (Ved. also<BR>युष्मे), loc. in you, cf. Ṛg-veda VIII. 47, 8;<BR>[cf. Zend yūs; Gr. ὑμεῖς, Æol. ὔμμες (fr. ὔσμες);<BR>Goth. and Lith. ju-s.]<BR>—युष्मद्-अर्थम्, ind.<BR>for you, on your account.<BR>—युष्मद्-आयत्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, dependent upon you, at your disposal.<BR>—युष्मद्-वाच्य, अम्, n. (in gram.) the second<BR>person.<BR>—युष्मद्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of your kind<BR>or sort, like you.<BR>—युष्मा-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>given or bestowed by you; [cf. युवा-दत्त.]<BR>—युष्मा-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, or युष्मा-दृश, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, like you, similar to you, resembling you, one<BR>such as you; [cf. मादृश्, त्वा-दृश्.]<BR>—युष्मा-<BR>नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. led or accompanied by you.<BR>—युष्मा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. belonging to you.<BR>—युष्मेषित (˚मा-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. excited<BR>or instigated by you.<BR>—युष्मोत (˚मा-ऊत), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. protected or loved by you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मदीय|युष्मदीयः
युष्मदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, your, yours, your own,<BR>belonging to you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मयत्|युष्मयन्त्
युष्मयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. seeking you,<BR>addressed to you, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda II.<BR>39, 7 = युवाम् इच्छत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0820-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्माक
युष्माक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. your, yours; [cf.<BR>युष्माक under युष्मद्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यू
यू यू, ऊस्, m. (according to some f.), soup,<BR>pease-soup, broth (= यूष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूक|यूकः
यूक यूक, अस्, आ, m. f. (said to be fr. rt. 2.<BR>यु), a louse.<BR>—यूक-देवी, f., N. of a princess.<BR>—यूका-लिक्ष, अम्, n. lice and nits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूकर
यूकर यूकर, see Gaṇa Kṛśāśvādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूति|यूतिः
यूति यूति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 2. यु), joining,<BR>mixing, mixture, junction, connection, union, addi-<BR>tion; [cf. युति, वहिर्-यूति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथ|यूथं
यूथ यूथ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (usually अम्, n.;<BR>fr. rt. 2. यु), a flock, herd (of birds, animals, &c.);<BR>a bevy, troop, band; a multitude, number, large<BR>quantity; (ई), f. a kind of jasmine (= यूथिका).<BR>—यूथ-ग, अस्, m., N. of a class of gods under<BR>Manu Cākṣuṣa.<BR>—यूथ-नाथ, अस्, m. the lord<BR>of a band, leader of a troop, head of a flock or herd;<BR>a large elephant.<BR>—यूथ-प, अस्, or यूथ-पति,<BR>इस्, m. a keeper or protector of a troop, lord or<BR>captain of a band; the leader of a herd (especially<BR>of elephants), a large elephant.<BR>—यूथपति-सका-<BR>शम्, ind. to the chief of the herd.<BR>—यूथ-परि-<BR>भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen out or strayed from the<BR>herd.<BR>—यूथ-पशु, उस्, m., N. of a particular tax<BR>or tithe.<BR>—यूथ-पाल, अस्, m. = यूथ-प.<BR>—यू-<BR>थ-भ्रष्ट or यूथ-विभ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>यूथ-परिभ्रष्ट above.<BR>—यूथ-मुख्य, अस्,<BR>m. the chief or captain of a troop.<BR>—यूथ-शस्, ind.<BR>in troops or bands, in flocks or herds, gregariously.<BR>—यूथ-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, = यूथ-परिभ्रष्ट.<BR>—यूथाग्रणी (˚थ-अग्˚), ईस्, m. a leader of a band<BR>or troop.<BR>—यूथी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to<BR>make or form into a herd, to unite in a flock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथक
यूथक at the end of an adj. comp. = यूथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथर
यूथर, an adj. fr. यूथ, see Gaṇa Aśmādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथिका
यूथिका, f. a kind of jasmine, Jasminum Auricu-<BR>latum; globe-amaranth; Clypea Hernandifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथ्य
यूथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to a herd or<BR>flock; being at the head of the herd; belonging to<BR>a troop or herd of (at the end of a comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यून
यून यून, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 2. यु), a band,<BR>cord, string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूनि|यूनिः
यूनि, इस्, f. joining, connection, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूनर्वन्
यूनर्वन् यूनर्वन्, a Vedic word of which<BR>the sense is doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूनी
यूनी यूनी, f. of युवन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूप|यूपः
यूप यूप, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 27. fr. rt. 2. यु, ‘to bind;’ but according to<BR>some, more probably fr. rt. युप्), a smooth post or<BR>stake to which the sacrificial victim is fastened, any<BR>sacrificial post, (usually made of bamboos or Khadira<BR>wood; in Rāmāyaṇa I. 13, 24, 25, where the horse<BR>sacrifice is described, twenty-one of these posts are<BR>set up, six made of Vilva, six of Khadira, six of<BR>Palāśa, one of Uḍumbara, one of Śleṣmātaka, and<BR>one of Deva-dāru); a column erected in honour of<BR>a victory, a trophy (= जय-स्तम्भ); N. of a par-<BR>ticular conjunction of the class आकृति-योग (i. e.<BR>when all the planets are situated in the first, second,<BR>third, and fourth houses).<BR>—यूप-कटक, अस्, m. a<BR>wooden ring at the top of the sacrificial post; (ac-<BR>cording to some) an iron ring at its base.<BR>—यूप-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m. the part of a sacrificial post which is<BR>sprinkled with ghee.<BR>—यूप-केतु, उस्, m., N. of<BR>Bhūri-śravas.<BR>—यूप-च्छेदन, अम्, n. the cutting<BR>of the sacrificial post.<BR>—यूप-दारु, n. the wood<BR>for the sacrificial post.<BR>—यूप-द्रु, उस्, m. Acacia<BR>Catechu (the wood of this tree being especially suit-<BR>able for the sacrificial post).<BR>—यूप-द्रुम, अस्, m.<BR>= यूप-द्रु above; = रक्त-खदिर.<BR>—यूप-<BR>ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘having the sacrificial post as an<BR>emblem,’ epithet of the sacrifice (personified).<BR>—यू-<BR>प-लक्षण, अम्, n., N. of a Pariśiṣṭa of Kātyā-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">Page0821-b+ 72</a>]<BR>yana.<BR>—यूप-लक्ष्य, अस्, m. a bird (said to be so<BR>called as ‘having a post [round which a snare is<BR>tied] for its aim’).<BR>—यूप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>a sacrificial post.<BR>—यूप-वाह, अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>carrier or bearer of the sacrificial post.<BR>—यूप-<BR>व्रस्क, अस्, m. the cutter of the sacrificial post.<BR>—यूपाक्ष (˚प-अक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Rākṣasa,<BR>(also read यूपाख्य.)<BR>—यूपाग्र (˚प-अग्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the top of the sacrificial post.<BR>—यूपाहुति (˚प-<BR>आह्˚), इस्, f. an offering at the erection of the sacri-<BR>ficial post.<BR>—यूपोच्छ्रय (˚प-उच्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>ceremony of erecting the sacrificial post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपीय
यूपीय or यूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or suitable for<BR>a sacrificial post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूयम्
यूयम् यूयम्. See युष्मद्, p. 820, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूयुधि
यूयुधि यूयुधि = युयुधि, p. 820, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूयुवि
यूयुवि यूयुवि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. 1. यु; ac-<BR>cording to the Pada-pāṭha युयुवि), Ved. setting<BR>aside, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष्
यूष् यूष् [cf. rt. जूष्], cl. 1. P. यूषति,<BR>&c., to injure, hurt, wound; to kill; [cf.<BR>Slav. juchŭ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष|यूषं|यूषः
यूष यूष, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be con-<BR>nected with rt. यूष् above; cf. जूष), soup, broth,<BR>pease-soup, the water in which pulse of various kinds<BR>has been boiled; (अस्), m. the Indian mulberry tree;<BR>[cf. probably Gr. ζωμός, ζύθος; Lat. jus; Slav.<BR>jucha.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूषन्
यूषन्, a form optionally substituted for यूष<BR>in all the cases except Nom. Voc. sing. du. pl., Acc.<BR>sing. du. (e. g. Acc. pl. यूषान् or यूष्णः, Inst.<BR>sing. यूषेण or यूष्णा, du. यूषाभ्याम् or यू-<BR>षभ्याम्, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूस्
यूस् = यूष above; [cf. यू.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येन
येन येन, ind. (inst. of 3. य or यद्), by<BR>which, by means of which, by which way, in which<BR>manner, in whatever way or manner, in which direc-<BR>tion, whither, where, in whatever direction, where-<BR>soever; on which account, in consequence of which,<BR>wherefore; because, since, as; that, so that, in order<BR>that (with pot. or pres. or fut.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येमन
येमन येमन, अम्, n. = जेमन, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येयजामह
येयजामह येयजामह, अस्, m. a term for<BR>the expression ये यजामहे, which immediately<BR>precedes the Yājyā or formula of consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येयायेय
येयायेय येयायेय (˚य-अय्˚), अम्, n. (fr. rt.<BR>1. या), that which is to be gone after and not to be<BR>gone after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येवाष
येवाष येवाष, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>noxious insect, (also read यवाष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येष्
येष् येष्, cl. 1. P. येषति, &c., Ved. to<BR>boil up, bubble; to flow, leak; cl. 1. A.<BR>येषते, &c., to exert one's self, endeavour, perse-<BR>vere, = rt. पेष्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येषत्
येषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, boiling up, bubbling; flow-<BR>ing, leaking; (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 53, 22 = स्र-<BR>वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येष्टिह
येष्टिह येष्टिह, Ved. epithet of a Muhūrta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येष्ठ
येष्ठ येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. fr. rt. 1. या),<BR>going very quickly, moving with the greatest rapidity,<BR>(Sāy. Ṛg-veda VII. 56, 6 = यातृतम, अतिशयेन<BR>गन्तृ, but Ṛg-veda V. 41, 3 = यन्तृतम, re-<BR>straining greatly, as if fr. rt. यम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्
योक् योक्, ind. = ज्योक्, for a long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्तव्य
योक्तव्य योक्तव्य, योक्तृ, योक्त्र, &c. See<BR>p. 819, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग|योगः
योग योग, अस्, m. (in one or two excep-<BR>tional cases अम्, n.; fr. rt. 1. युज्), the act of yoking,<BR>joining, junction, conjunction, uniting, union, con-<BR>tact; the harnessing or putting to (of horses); a yoke,<BR>team, (षड्-योग, having a team of six); convey-<BR>ance; the arraying or equipping (of an army),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-c" target="_blank">Page0821-c+ 81</a>]<BR>arrangement, disposition; applying, fixing, application,<BR>use, employment, appointment, institution; the put-<BR>ting on armour; armour; the fixing (of an arrow or<BR>other weapon); application of a remedy or medicine,<BR>remedy, cure; mode, manner, method, means, (यो-<BR>गेन or योगात् at the end of comps. = ‘by means<BR>of,’ ‘by reason of,’ ‘through’); an expedient, artifice,<BR>plan, device, (योगेन, artfully, craftily); a super-<BR>natural means, charm, incantation, spell, magic,<BR>magical art; fraud, deceit [cf. योग-नन्द]; side,<BR>part, argument; occasion, opportunity; fitness, pro-<BR>priety, suitability, aptness, congruity, (योगेन, suit-<BR>ably, fitly, in accordance with, conformably to); the<BR>performance or execution (of anything); undertaking,<BR>occupation, work, business; gaining, acquiring, ac-<BR>quisition [cf. योग-क्षेम]; accession of property,<BR>substance, wealth, thing; connection, consequence,<BR>result, (योगात् at the end of comps. = ‘in consequence<BR>of,’ e. g. कर्म-योगात्, in consequence of actions,<BR>i. e. of destiny); combination or mixing of various<BR>materials, association, mixture; contact, (with Jainas)<BR>contact or mixing with the outer world; (in the<BR>Sāṅkhya phil.) one of the ten Mūlikārthas; con-<BR>nection with, the partaking or possessing of (with<BR>inst.); conjunction (in astronomy, cf. नक्षत्र-<BR>योग), lucky conjuncture; (in arithmetic) addition,<BR>sum, total; the being connected together, depend-<BR>ance, relation, regular order or series, (कथा-योग,<BR>conversation); a period of time, (काल-योगेन, after<BR>the lapse of some time; नव-योग, nine times);<BR>a combination or configuration of stars, a constella-<BR>tion, asterism, (these with the moon are called in<BR>astronomical works चान्द्र-योगाः, and are thirteen<BR>in number; without the moon they are called ख-<BR>योगाः or नाभस-योगाः, and are divided into<BR>आकृति-योगाः, सङ्ख्या-योगाः, आश्रय-योगाः, and<BR>दल-योगाः; two others are added, called द्विग्रह-<BR>योगाः); (in astronomy) N. of a particular division<BR>of time or astronomical period, (a period of variable<BR>length during which the joint motion in longitude<BR>of the sun and moon amounts to 30° 204; the term<BR>योग in this sense is a mere mode of indicating the<BR>sum of the longitude of the sun and moon; twenty-<BR>seven such Yogas are enumerated, beginning with<BR>1. Viṣkambha, and ending with 27. Vaidhṛti, or<BR>according to some authorities twenty-eight); the<BR>leading or principal star of a lunar mansion; etymo-<BR>logy, derivation of the meaning of a word from its<BR>root; the etymological meaning of a word (opposed<BR>to रूढि); (in gram.) the connection of words<BR>together, dependence of one word upon another,<BR>construction; a rule, aphorism, precept [cf. योग-<BR>विभाग]; application of effort, endeavour, diligence,<BR>assiduity, zeal, attention, (पूर्णेन योगेन or जल-<BR>पूर्णेन योगेन, with all one's powers, with over-<BR>flowing zeal); application or concentration of the<BR>thoughts, fixing the mind on a particular point and<BR>keeping the body in a fixed posture, abstract con-<BR>templation, meditation; the systematic practice of<BR>the above abstract contemplation or meditation; the<BR>Yoga system of philosophy as established by Patañjali,<BR>(the Yoga is the name of the second of the two<BR>divisions of the Sāṅkhya system, its chief aim being<BR>to teach the means by which the human soul may<BR>attain complete union with Īśvara or the Supreme<BR>Being, whose existence it establishes, while the origi-<BR>nal system or Sāṅkhya proper, without acknowledging<BR>a Supreme Being, teaches the successive development<BR>of the Tattvas or principles of creation from an origi-<BR>nal Tattva, called Prakṛti or Pradhāna; according to<BR>Patañjali, the author of the second system, Yoga is<BR>defined to be ‘the preventing of the modifications<BR>of चित्त or the thinking principle [which modifica-<BR>tions arise through the three Pramāṇas, perception,<BR>inference, and verbal testimony, as well as through<BR>incorrect ascertainment, fancy, sleep, and recollection]<BR>by अभ्यास or the constant practice of keeping the<BR>mind in its unmodified state [clear as crystal when<BR>uncoloured by contact with other substances], and by<BR>वैराग्य or dispassion;’ this dispassion being ob-<BR>tained by प्रणिधान or devotedness to Īśvara,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0822-a" target="_blank">Page0822-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the Supreme, who is defined as a particular Puruṣa<BR>or spirit unaffected by afflictions, works, &c., and<BR>having the appellation Praṇava or Om, which mono-<BR>syllable is to be muttered and its meaning reflected<BR>on in order to attain knowledge of the Supreme and<BR>the prevention of the obstacles to Yoga: the eight<BR>means or stages of Yoga or mental concentration<BR>are, 1. यम, forbearance; 2. नियम, religious ob-<BR>servances; 3. आसन, postures; 4. प्राणायाम, regu-<BR>lation of the breath; 5. प्रत्याहार, restraint of the<BR>senses; 6. धारणा, steadying of the mind; 7. ध्या-<BR>न, contemplation; 8. समाधि, profound medita-<BR>tion, which, according to the Bhagavad-gītā VI. 13,<BR>is to be practised by fixing the eyes on the tip of<BR>the nose: true liberation is the cessation of all idea<BR>of self and the separation of matter and spirit or<BR>कैवल्य, isolation: the self-mortification and asce-<BR>ticism of the Yoga connects it closely with Buddhism);<BR>the union of the individual soul with the universal<BR>soul, devotion, pious seeking after God; any single<BR>act or rite conducive to Yoga or abstract contem-<BR>plation; (personified as) the son of Dharma and<BR>Kriyā; a follower of the Yoga system of philosophy;<BR>a traitor, violator of confidence, spy; N. of a com-<BR>mentator on the Paramārtha-sāra; (आ), f., N. of<BR>Pīvarī (daughter of the Pitṛs called Barhiṣads); of<BR>a Śakti.<BR>—योग-कक्षा, f. = योग-पट्ट.<BR>—योग-<BR>कन्या, f., N. of the infant daughter of Yaśo-dā<BR>(substituted as the child of Devakī for the infant<BR>Kṛṣṇa and therefore killed by Kaṃsa, but imme-<BR>diately raised to heaven as a beautiful girl; as she<BR>ascended she warned Kaṃsa of his doom, see Hari-<BR>vaṃśa 3340).<BR>—योग-करण्डक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>minister of Brahma-datta; (इका), f., N. of a female<BR>ascetic (प्रव्राजिका).<BR>—योग-कुण्डलिनी, f., N. of<BR>an Upaniṣad.<BR>—योग-क्षेम, अस्, m. the security<BR>or secure possession of what has been acquired, the<BR>keeping safe of property; the charge for securing<BR>property (from accidents), insurance, (in Manu IX.<BR>219. the term योग-क्षेम is applied to counsel-<BR>lors, family priests, &c. as the cause of security);<BR>property, substance, profit, gain; security, well-being,<BR>welfare, prosperity; (अम्), n. or (औ), m. du. gain<BR>and security, maintenance and protection, the acqui-<BR>sition and preservation of property, making fresh<BR>gains as well as keeping what has been acquired, (in<BR>these senses the word must be regarded as a Dvandva<BR>comp.)<BR>—योगक्षेम-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing<BR>gain and security, causing protection of what is<BR>acquired, one who takes charge of property, a<BR>keeper.<BR>—योग-गति, इस्, f. state of union, original<BR>state, primitive condition.<BR>—योग-चक्षुस्, उस्, m.<BR>‘contemplation-eyed,’ one whose eye is meditation,<BR>epithet of a Brāhman.<BR>—योग-चर, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Hanumat.<BR>—योग-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m., N. of a philosophical<BR>treatise in four chapters by Śivānanda Sarasvatī.<BR>—योग-चूर्ण, अस्, अम्, m. n. magical powder.<BR>—योग-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by or arising from<BR>Yoga or meditation; (अम्), n. agallochum.<BR>—योग-<BR>तत्त्व, अम्, n. the principle of Yoga; N. of an<BR>Upaniṣad.<BR>—योग-तत्त्व-प्रकाश or योग-तत्त्व-<BR>प्रकाशक, N. of a work.<BR>—योग-तन्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>a book treating of the Yoga system of philosophy;<BR>(with Buddhists) N. of a class of writings.<BR>—योग-<BR>तरङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-तल्प, अम्,<BR>n. ‘Yoga-couch,’ = योग-निद्रा.<BR>—योग-तस्, ind.<BR>conjointly; suitably, properly; conformably to, in<BR>accordance with; seasonably, in due season; through<BR>devotion, by the power of magic, &c.; by means of,<BR>in consequence of, (often at the end of comps.)<BR>—योग-तारका or योग-तारा, f. the chief star in a<BR>Nakṣatra.<BR>—योग-तारावली, f., N. of a work.<BR>—यो-<BR>ग-त्व, अम्, n. the state of Yoga.<BR>—योग-दान,<BR>अम्, n. gift of the Yoga, communicating the Yoga<BR>doctrine; a fraudulent gift.<BR>—योग-दीपिका, f., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—योग-देव, अस्, m., N. of a Jaina<BR>author.<BR>—योग-धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, doing homage<BR>to the Yoga.<BR>—योग-धारणा, f. continuance or<BR>perseverance in devotion.<BR>—योग-नन्द, अस्, m.<BR>the false Nanda, (opposed to सत्य-नन्द.)<BR>—योग-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0822-b" target="_blank">Page0822-b+ 81</a>]<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. ‘Yoga-lord,’ N. of Śiva; of Datta.<BR>—योग-नाविक, अस्, m. a kind of fish (= गर्गाट).<BR>—योग-निद्रा, f. ‘contemplation-sleep,’ a state of<BR>half contemplation, half sleep, or a state between<BR>sleep and wakefulness which admits of the full exer-<BR>cise of the mental powers (supposed to be peculiar<BR>to devotees), light sleep; (especially) the sleep of<BR>Viṣṇu at the end of a Yuga; Viṣṇu's Sleep per-<BR>sonified as a goddess and said to be a form of Durgā;<BR>(according to others) the great sleep of Brahmā,<BR>during the period between the annihilation and re-<BR>production of the universe.<BR>—योग-निद्रालु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—योग-निलय, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—योगन्-धर, अस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>formula recited over weapons; N. of a minister of<BR>Śatānīka; of Piṇḍola.<BR>—योग-पट्ट or योग-पट्-<BR>टक, अम्, n. the cloth thrown over the back and<BR>knees of an ascetic during meditation.<BR>—योग-पति,<BR>इस्, m. ‘Yoga-lord,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—योग-पत्नी, f.<BR>‘wife of Yoga,’ N. of Pīvarī, (called also योगा and<BR>योग-मातृ.)<BR>—योग-पथ, अस्, m. the road lead-<BR>ing to Yoga.<BR>—योग-पद, अम्, n. the state or con-<BR>dition of contemplation.<BR>—योग-पदक, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a particular garment worn during contempla-<BR>tion.<BR>—योग-पातञ्जल, अस्, m. a follower or dis-<BR>ciple of Patañjali as teacher of the Yoga doctrine.<BR>—योग-पादुका, f. a magical shoe (supposed to<BR>carry the wearer wherever he wishes).<BR>—योग-पा-<BR>रङ्-ग, अस्, m. ‘conversant with Yoga,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—योग-पीठ, अम्, n. a particular posture during<BR>religious contemplation.<BR>—योग-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>obtained through abstract meditation.<BR>—योग-बल,<BR>अम्, n. the force of devotion, the power of magic,<BR>supernatural power.<BR>—योग-बीज, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—योग-भावना, f. (in algebra) composition<BR>of numbers by the sum of the products.<BR>—योग-<BR>भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a commentary by Vyāsa.<BR>—योग-भास्कर, N. of a work.<BR>—योग-भ्रष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has fallen from the practice of<BR>Yoga.<BR>—योग-मणि-प्रभा, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary on the Yoga-sūtra.<BR>—योग-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>coming or resulting from Yoga or contemplation;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—योगमय-ज्ञान, अम्,<BR>n. knowledge derived from contemplation.<BR>—योग-<BR>महिमन्, आ, m., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-मातृ, ता,<BR>f. mother of Yoga; epithet of Pīvarī.<BR>—योग-माया,<BR>f. the Māyā or magical power of the Yoga.<BR>—योग-<BR>मार्तण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-माला, f.<BR>‘garland of magic &c.,’ N. of a work on magic.<BR>—योग-मुक्तावली (˚त-आव्˚), f., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-मूर्ति-धर, आस्, m. pl. ‘bearing the form<BR>of the Yoga,’ epithet of a class of Manes.<BR>—योग-<BR>याज्ञवल्क्य, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-यात्रा,<BR>f. the road or way to union with the Supreme Spirit,<BR>the way of profound meditation; N. of a work by<BR>Varāha-mihira.<BR>—योग-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, or योग-<BR>योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, immersed in deep meditation, ab-<BR>sorbed in the Yoga.<BR>—योग-युज्, क्, क्, क्, possessing<BR>Yoga.<BR>—योग-रङ्ग, अस्, m. the orange tree (=<BR>नारङ्ग).<BR>—योग-रत्न, अम्, n. a magical jewel;<BR>‘jewel of remedies,’ N. of a work on medicine.<BR>—योग-रत्न-माला, f. ‘string of jewels of spells,’<BR>N. of a work on sorcery and various magical arts<BR>ascribed to Nāgārjuna, (it is also called Āścarya-<BR>ratna-mālā, and is probably an epitome of a much<BR>larger work.)<BR>—योग-रत्न-समुच्चय, अस्, m.<BR>‘collection of jewels of remedies,’ N. of a medical<BR>work by Candraṭa.<BR>—योग-रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘mine of jewels of charms or remedies,’ N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—योग-रत्नावली (˚न-आव्˚), f. ‘string<BR>of jewels of charms,’ N. of a work.<BR>—योग-रथ,<BR>अस्, m. the Yoga as a chariot.<BR>—योग-रसायन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘Yoga-elixir,’ N. of certain verses or a com-<BR>position ascribed to Śiva.<BR>—योग-रहस्य, अम्, n.<BR>‘Yoga-secret,’ N. of a work.<BR>—योग-राज, अस्, m.<BR>‘king of medicines,’ N. of a particular medicinal<BR>preparation; a king or master in the Yoga.<BR>—योग-<BR>राजोपनिषद् (˚ज-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—योग-रूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a special as well<BR>as an etymological and general meaning, (said of<BR>certain words, e. g. पङ्क-ज means ‘growing in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0822-c" target="_blank">Page0822-c+ 81</a>]<BR>mud’ and ‘a lotus-flower;’ the English word parasol<BR>is an example of a similar kind.)<BR>—योग-रोचना,<BR>f., N. of a kind of magical ointment (having the<BR>power of making invisible or invulnerable).<BR>—योग-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, connected, united, joined; one<BR>who applies himself to or practises the Yoga.<BR>—योग-वर्तिका, f. a magical lamp, magic-lantern.<BR>—योग-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, bringing about, causing,<BR>promoting, furthering.<BR>—योग-वाचस्पत्य, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—योग-वार्त्तिक, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>commentary on the Pātañjala-bhāṣya by Vijñāna-<BR>bhikṣu, (also called Pātañjala-bhāṣya-vārttika.)<BR>—योग-वासिष्ठ, अम्, n., N. of a work by an<BR>unknown author treating of the way of obtaining<BR>final happiness and reckoned among Vedānta treatises,<BR>(it is in the form of a dialogue between Vasiṣṭha<BR>and his pupil, the youthful Rāma, and is considered<BR>as an appendage to the Rāmāyaṇa of Vālmīki, to<BR>whom it is attributed; it is also called Vāsiṣṭha-<BR>rāmāyaṇa.)<BR>—योगवासिष्ठ-तात्पर्य-प्रकाश,<BR>N. of a commentary on the preceding work.<BR>—यो-<BR>गवासिष्ठ-सार, अस्, m., N. of an abridgement<BR>or abstract of the Yoga-vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—योगवासिष्ठ-<BR>सार-चन्द्रिका, f. and योगवासिष्ठसार-विवृति,<BR>इस्, f., N. of two commentaries on the preced-<BR>ing abridgement.<BR>—योगवासिष्ठीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to the Yoga-vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—योग-वाह, अस्,<BR>m. a term for the sounds Visarjanīya, Jihvāmūlīya,<BR>Upadhmānīya, and Nāsikya; (ई), f. alkali; honey;<BR>quicksilver.<BR>—योग-वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, contriving<BR>artifices (?), plotting, scheming; (इ), n. a menstruum<BR>or medium for mixing medicines.<BR>—योग-विक्रय,<BR>अस्, m. a fraudulent sale.<BR>—योग-विद्, त्, त्, त्, know-<BR>ing the (right) means, understanding the proper way<BR>or method, skilful; conversant with the Yoga; (त्),<BR>m., N. of Śiva; a follower of the Yoga doctrines;<BR>a practiser of devotional exercises; a magician; a<BR>compounder of medicines.<BR>—योग-विभाग, अस्, m.<BR>the disuniting or separation of that which is usually<BR>combined together into one, the separation of one<BR>rule into two, making two rules of what might be<BR>propounded as one.<BR>—योग-वृत्ति-सङ्ग्रह, अस्,<BR>m., N. of certain selected annotations by Udayakara<BR>Pāṭhaka on the Yoga-sūtras.<BR>—योग-शत, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a medical work.<BR>—योग-शतकाख्यान (˚क-<BR>आख्˚), अम्, n., N. of a work by Sanātana.<BR>—योग-<BR>शब्द, अस्, m. the word Yoga; a word the meaning<BR>of which is plain from the etymology.<BR>—योग-शरी-<BR>रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, ‘Yoga-bodied,’ whose body is Yoga.<BR>—योग-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, half asleep and half ab-<BR>sorbed in religious meditation.<BR>—योग-शास्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. the Śāstra relating to the Yoga system (especially<BR>that of Patañjali); the Yoga philosophy, Yoga<BR>doctrine.<BR>—योग-शिक्षा, f., N. of an Upaniṣad,<BR>(for योग-शिखा?).<BR>—योग-शिखा, f., N. of an Upa-<BR>niṣad.<BR>—योग-संसिद्धि, इस्, f. perfection in<BR>Yoga.<BR>—योग-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-समाधि, इस्, m. the absorption of the<BR>soul in profound meditation peculiar to the Yoga<BR>system.<BR>—योग-सार, a universal remedy, panacea;<BR>N. of a work on the Yoga system.<BR>—योग-सार-<BR>सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a short treatise on the<BR>doctrines of the Yoga system by Vijñāna-bhikṣu.<BR>—योग-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, perfected by means of<BR>the Yoga or profound abstraction; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>sister of Vācas-pati.<BR>—योग-सिद्धान्त-चन्द्रिका<BR>and योग-सिद्धि-प्रक्रिया, f., N. of two philoso-<BR>phical works.<BR>—योग-सिद्धि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, ex-<BR>perienced or skilful in the art of magic.<BR>—योग-<BR>सुधा-निधि, इस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—योग-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n. the aphorisms on the Yoga system of philo-<BR>sophy ascribed to Patañjali, (these consist of four<BR>Pādas or chapters; the oldest commentary on them<BR>is said to be by Vyāsa, and there are other commen-<BR>taries on that by Vācaspati-miśra, Vijñāna-bhikṣu,<BR>Bhoja-deva, Nāgoji-bhaṭṭa, &c.)<BR>—योग-सेवा, f. the<BR>practice or cultivation of religious abstraction.<BR>—योग-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, remaining engrossed in<BR>Yoga.<BR>—योग-हृदय, अम्, n. ‘heart of the Yoga,’<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—योगाग्नि-मय (˚ग-अग्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, Ved. filled with the fire of the Yoga, attained<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-a" target="_blank">Page0823-a+ 81</a>]<BR>through the ardour of devotion.<BR>—योगाङ्ग (˚ग-<BR>अङ्˚), अम्, n. a means of attaining Yoga, (eight<BR>such Aṅgas are enumerated, viz. यम, नियम,<BR>आसन, प्राणायाम, प्रत्याहार, धारणा, ध्या-<BR>न, and समाधि, or according to another authority<BR>six, viz. आसन, प्राण-संरोध, with the last<BR>four as enumerated above; see under योग.)<BR>—यो-<BR>गाचार (˚ग-आच्˚), अस्, m. the observance or practice<BR>of the Yoga; N. of a Yoga work; a disciple or<BR>follower of a particular Buddhist sect or school;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a particular sect or school of<BR>Buddhists, (they maintain the eternal existence of<BR>conscious sense or intelligence [विज्ञान] alone.)<BR>—योगाचार्य (˚ग-आच्˚), अस्, m. a teacher of the<BR>art of magic; a teacher of the Yoga system of phi-<BR>losophy.<BR>—योगाञ्जन (˚ग-अञ्˚), अम्, n. a healing<BR>ointment; the Yoga as a salve.<BR>—योगात्मन् (˚ग-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, whose soul or essence is Yoga; one<BR>who fixes the mind on the Yoga system.<BR>—योगा-<BR>धमन (˚ग-आध्˚), अम्, n. a fraudulent pledge.<BR>—योगानन्द (˚ग-आन्˚), अस्, m. the delight or joy<BR>of the Yoga.<BR>—योगानुशासन (˚ग-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘Yoga-instruction,’ the doctrine of the Yoga, the<BR>system or precepts of Patañjali.<BR>—योगानुशासन-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n. = योग-सूत्र.<BR>—योगान्त (˚ग-अन्˚)<BR>or योगान्तिका (scil. गति), N. of the seven divisions into<BR>which, according to Parāśara, the orbit of Mercury is<BR>divided.<BR>—योगापत्ति (˚ग-आप्˚), इस्, f., Ved. modi-<BR>fication of usage or custom.<BR>—योगाम्बर (˚ग-<BR>अम्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist deity.<BR>—योगारङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. = योग-रङ्ग.<BR>—योगारूढ (˚ग-आर्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, engaged in profound meditation or devotion.<BR>—योगासन (˚ग-आस्˚), अम्, n. the posture or mode<BR>of sitting proper for profound and abstract meditation,<BR>a way of sitting similar to that of the Yoga.<BR>—यो-<BR>गेन्द्र (˚ग-इन्˚), अस्, m. a master or adept in the<BR>Yoga.<BR>—योगेश (˚ग-ईश), अस्, m. a master of the<BR>Yoga, any principal sage or Yogin, epithet of Yājña-<BR>valkya; of Śiva; N. of the city of Brahmā.<BR>—यो-<BR>गेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a master or adept in the<BR>Yoga, any principal sage or Yogin; one who has<BR>obtained superhuman faculties, a magician; a deity,<BR>the object of devout contemplation; epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; a Vetāla (as perfectly skilled in magical<BR>arts); an epithet of Yājñavalkya [cf. योगेश]; N.<BR>of a son of Deva-hotra; of a Brahma-rākṣasa; (ई),<BR>f. a mistress of the Yoga; a fairy; N. of a goddess;<BR>of a Vidyā-dharī; a species of plant (= बन्ध्या-<BR>कर्कोटकी).<BR>—योगेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—योगेश्वर-त्व or योगैश्वर्य (˚ग-<BR>ऐश्˚), अम्, n. perfect mastery of the Yoga.<BR>—यो-<BR>गेष्ट (˚ग-इष्˚), अम्, n. tin; lead.<BR>—योगोपनि-<BR>षद् (˚ग-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगक
योगक, अस्, m., N. of Agni (as the nuptial fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगस्
योगस्, अस्, n. meditation, religious abstraction;<BR>the half of a lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगाय
योगाय, Nom. A. योगायते, &c., to become<BR>Yoga, to be changed into religious contemplation or<BR>devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगि
योगि = योगिन् (occasionally occurring in ep. where<BR>the metre requires योगीनाम् for योगिनाम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगित
योगित, अस्, आ, अम्, bewitched, enchanted, under the<BR>influence of charms or sorcery, mad, crazy, wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगिन्
योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, who or what joins or effects<BR>junction, being in conjunction with (at the end of a<BR>comp., e. g. चन्द्र-योगिन्, being in conjunction<BR>with the moon; cf. सोम-य्˚); connected with,<BR>endowed or provided with, possessed of, relating to<BR>(at the end of a comp., e. g. काल-य्˚, connected<BR>with fate; cf. स्वादु-य्˚); possessed of magical<BR>powers; practising or following the Yoga philo-<BR>sophy; (ई), m. a follower of the Yoga system, a<BR>Yogin or contemplative saint, a devotee, ascetic in<BR>general; a religious or devout man, a magician,<BR>conjurer, one supposed to have obtained supernatural<BR>powers; N. of Yājñavalkya; of Arjuna; of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Śiva; of a Buddha; of a particular mixed caste;<BR>(इनी), f. a female demon or being endowed with<BR>magical power, a fairy, witch, sorceress (represented<BR>as an attendant of Śiva or Durgā; eight Yoginīs<BR>are enumerated as created by and attendant on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-b" target="_blank">Page0823-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Durgā); epithet of a particular Tantrika Śakti;<BR>(with Buddhists) a woman representing any goddess<BR>who is the object of adoration; N. of Durgā.<BR>—योगि-<BR>ता, f. or योगि-त्व, अम्, n. the being connected<BR>with, the having reference or relation to (at the end<BR>of a comp.), connection, relationship, the state or<BR>condition of a Yogin.<BR>—योगि-दण्ड, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of reed or cane (= वेत्र).<BR>—योगि-निद्रा, f. ‘a<BR>Yogin's sleep,’ light sleep, wakefulness.<BR>—योगिनी-<BR>जाल-शम्बर, अम्, n. and योगिनी-ज्ञानार्णव (˚न-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m. and योगिनी-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of three<BR>Tantra works.<BR>—योगिनी-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—योगिनी-भैरव and योगिनी-हृदय, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of two Tantra works.<BR>—योगि-पत्नी, f. a Yogin's<BR>wife.<BR>—योगि-मातृ, ता, m. a Yogin's mother.<BR>—यो-<BR>गि-राज्, ट्, m. a king among Yogins.<BR>—योगीन्द्र<BR>(˚गि-इन्˚) or योगीश (˚गि-ईश), अस्, m. a chief or lord<BR>among contemplative saints; N. of Yājñavalkya.<BR>—योगीश्वर (˚गि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. = योगीश; (ई), f.,<BR>N. of a goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगीय
योगीय (fr. योग), Nom. A. योगीयते, &c., to<BR>regard as Yoga, treat as Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्य|योग्यं|योग्यः
योग्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. योग and fr. rt. 1. युज्),<BR>fit for the yoke (Ved.); belonging to a particular<BR>remedy (Ved.); useful, serviceable, fit, becoming,<BR>suitable, proper, appropriate, fit for, qualified for,<BR>capable of, able to (with dat., loc. or even gen. or<BR>at the end of a comp. or with active or passive<BR>inf., e. g. स तत्-साधनाय योग्यः, he is fit for<BR>accomplishing that; नेयं वनस्य योग्या, she is<BR>not fit for a forest; कर्म-योग्य, fit for work;<BR>इमे योग्या राक्षसैर् योद्धुम्, they are able to<BR>fight with the Rākṣasas; छेत्तुं योग्यं तत्,<BR>that is fit to be cut); fit for Yoga, proper for reli-<BR>gious meditation; (अस्), m. a calculator of expedients;<BR>the asterism Puṣya; (आ), f. preparation, contrivance<BR>(Ved. Sāy. Ṛg-veda III. 6, 6, ‘materials or appliance<BR>for harnessing’); exercise, practice, (especially) bodily<BR>exercise, gymnastics, warlike or martial exercise,<BR>drill; N. of the wife of Sūrya; (अम्), n. a species<BR>of plant (= ऋद्धि); sandal-wood; a vehicle, con-<BR>veyance, carriage; a cake; milk.<BR>—योग्य-ता, f. or<BR>योग्य-त्व, अम्, n. suitableness, propriety, fitness,<BR>consistency, appropriateness; ability, capability.<BR>—योग्यता-वाद, अस्, m., N. of certain verses by<BR>an unknown author.<BR>—योग्या-रथ, अस्, m. a car-<BR>riage employed in military exercises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजक
योजक, अस्, इका, अम्, uniting, joining; one who<BR>yokes or harnesses, a harnesser, groom; an arranger,<BR>preparer, contriver, effecter; [cf. युद्ध-य्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजन|योजनं
योजन, अम्, n. the act of joining, junction, har-<BR>nessing, yoking; that which is yoked or harnessed<BR>(as ‘a yoke of oxen,’ ‘pair or team of horses,’ ‘a<BR>vehicle or its trappings;’ so explained by some in<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 62, 6, &c., but in Ṛg-veda I. 88, 5.<BR>योजनम् is explained to mean ‘a means for inducing<BR>the gods to yoke their horses,’ i. e. a hymn); a stage<BR>or distance gone in one harnessing or without un-<BR>yoking; a particular measure of distance sometimes<BR>regarded as about equal to an European league (i. e.<BR>4 or 5 English miles, but more correctly = 4 Krośas<BR>or about 9 miles; according to other calculations =<BR>2(1/2) English miles, and according to some = 8 Krośas);<BR>a way, course, road (Ved.); a line, row (Ved.?);<BR>the act of applying, application, fixing, arranging,<BR>preparing, preparation, (आहार-य्˚, preparation of<BR>food); erecting, constructing, (in these senses some-<BR>times आ, f.); application of the sense of a passage,<BR>the putting together of the sense, construction (in<BR>gram.); application of effort, exertion (Ved., Sāy. =<BR>उद्योग); the act of inciting or exciting, instigation;<BR>application of the thoughts, concentration of the<BR>mind, abstraction, directing the thoughts to one<BR>point (= योग); the Supreme Being or Soul of the<BR>Universe; (आ), f. union, connection; grammatical<BR>construction.<BR>—योजन-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, whose<BR>scent or fragrance extends for a Yojana, diffusing<BR>perfume to the distance of a Yojana; (आ), f. musk;<BR>epithet of Satya-vatī the mother of Vyāsa; of Sītā.<BR>—योजन-गन्धिका, f. epithet of Satya-vatī.<BR>—यो-<BR>जन-पर्णी, f. Bengal madder, Rubia Munjista (=<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">Page0823-c+ 77</a>]<BR>मञ्जिष्ठा).<BR>—योजन-वल्लिका or योजन-वल्ली,<BR>f. = योजन-पर्णी, col. 2.<BR>—योजन-शत, अम्, n.<BR>a hundred Yojanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनिक
योजनिक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp. after a numeral) so many Yojanas long, mea-<BR>suring so many Yojanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनीय
योजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be joined or united; to<BR>be applied; to be added; to be made use of or<BR>employed, serviceable, useful; to be connected with<BR>(with inst.); to be set to work; to be grammati-<BR>cally connected or arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजन्य
योजन्य at the end of an adj. comp., e. g.<BR>षष्टि-य्˚, sixty Yojanas distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजयितव्य
योजयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus. of rt.<BR>1. युज्), to be joined or applied; to be used or<BR>employed; to be chosen or selected; to be endowed<BR>or furnished with (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजयितृ
योजयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. the Caus.), who or<BR>what joins^1 or unites; joining, combining, one who<BR>applies or sets, a setter (of precious stones), one who<BR>enchases, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजित|योजितं
योजित, अस्, आ, अम्, joined, united, mixed; applied,<BR>arranged, concerted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजितृ
योजितृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. rt. 1. युज्), one who<BR>unites or joins, a joiner, uniter, connecter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योज्य
योज्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. युज्), to be joined;<BR>to be applied or directed to; to be appointed or<BR>arranged; to be made use of or employed, to be<BR>brought in use; to be added to (with loc.); to be<BR>endowed or furnished with (with inst.); to be shared<BR>in; one on whom the mind is to be fixed or concen-<BR>trated, an object of Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योटक|योटकः
योटक योटक, अस्, m. a combination of<BR>stars, &c., constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योतु|योतुः
योतु योतु, उस्, m. (probably fr. rt. 2. यु),<BR>= परि-माण, measure in general; cleaning; puri-<BR>fying, separating (?fr. rt. 1. यु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्र|योत्रं
योत्र योत्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 2. यु), = योक्त्र,<BR>a fastening, tie, band, cord, rope, line; the tie or<BR>cord that fastens the yoke of the plough to the neck<BR>of the ox.<BR>—योत्र-प्रमाद, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्स्यमान
योत्स्यमान योत्स्यमान. See p. 820, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धव्य
योद्धव्य योद्धव्य, योद्धृ, योध, योधिन्,<BR>&c. See p. 820, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनल|योनलः
योनल योनल, अस्, m. = यव-नाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनि|योनिः
योनि योनि, इस्, m. f. (rarely fem. in the<BR>older language; sometimes also योनी, f.; said to<BR>be fr. rt. 2. यु), the womb, uterus, matrix, vulva,<BR>vagina, female organs of generation; site of birth or<BR>production, any place of birth or origin, native place;<BR>a home, abode, site, lair, nest; birth, origin, source<BR>[cf. जगद्-य्˚, कर्म-य्˚], spring, fountain, (at the<BR>end of an adj. comp. = ‘originating in,’ ‘arising or<BR>proceeding from,’ ‘sprung from,’ ‘produced by,’ e. g.<BR>अगुरु-योनिर् धूपः, aromatic vapour proceeding<BR>from aloe wood); a repository, receptacle, seat; a<BR>mine; family, race, stock, caste, the form of exist-<BR>ence or station fixed by birth, a class or particular<BR>nature of created existence (e. g. that of a man,<BR>Brāhman, animal, &c.); the regent of the Nakṣatra<BR>Pūrva-phalgunī; water; a mystical term for the<BR>sound ए.<BR>—योनि-कुण्ड, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>mystical diagram.<BR>—योनि-गुण, अस्, m. the property<BR>of a womb, quality of a place of origin.<BR>—योनि-<BR>ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. = छन्दस्, q. v.<BR>—योनि-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, born or produced from the womb, viviparous,<BR>(opposed to अ-य्˚, q. v.)<BR>—योनि-तस्, ind. from birth,<BR>by blood.<BR>—योनि-त्व, अम्, n. the being an origin<BR>or source; the arising from or being based on.<BR>—योनि-देवता, f. the Nakṣatra Pūrva-phalgunī.<BR>—योनि-देश, अस्, m. the region of the womb or<BR>the generative organs.<BR>—योनि-द्वार, अम्, n. the<BR>orifice of the womb; N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—योनि-नासा, f. the upper part of the female organ,<BR>the point of union of the labiæ.<BR>—योनि-भ्रंश,<BR>अस्, m. fall of the womb, prolapsus uteri.<BR>—योनि-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. connected with the womb<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">Page0824-a+ 76</a>]<BR>or with the mother.<BR>—योनि-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. released from birth or from being born again.<BR>—योनि-मुख, अम्, n. the orifice of the uterus.<BR>—योनि-मुद्रा, f., N. of a particular position of<BR>the fingers.<BR>—योनि-रञ्जन, अम्, n. the menstrual<BR>excretion.<BR>—योनि-रोग, अस्, m. disease of the female<BR>organs of generation.<BR>—योनि-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. the<BR>clitoris.<BR>—योनि-संवृत्ति, इस्, f. contraction or<BR>closure of the vagina.<BR>—योनि-सङ्कर, अस्, m.<BR>‘confusion of births,’ mixture of caste by unlawful<BR>intermarriage, misalliance.<BR>—योनि-सम्बन्ध, अस्,<BR>m. relation by marriage, affinity.<BR>—योनि-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, = योनि-ज.<BR>—योन्य्-अर्शस्, अस्, n. a fleshy<BR>excrescence in the female organ (= कन्द), pro-<BR>lapsus uteri (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0823-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिन्
योनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, = योनि, at the end of an adj.<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योन्य
योन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. forming a womb or<BR>receptacle (for the waters; Sāy. = उदक-निर्ग-<BR>मन-द्वार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योपन|योपनं
योपन योपन. See under rt. युप्, p. 820.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषणा
योषणा योषणा, f. (probably fr. rt. 2. यु,<BR>cf. युवन्; according to others connected with rt.<BR>1. जुष्), a girl, maiden, young woman, wife; (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda V. 52, 14) a hymn,<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषन्
योषन्, अणस्, f. pl. (apparently only used in<BR>plur.), Ved. women, young women, maidens; epi-<BR>thet of the ten fingers (in Ṛg-veda IX 1, 7, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषा
योषा, f. a girl, young woman, woman, female,<BR>wife; epithet of the early dawn (Ved., but according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 123, 9. योषा = मिश्रयन्ती,<BR>blending); the female of an animal, a mare (Ved.);<BR>speech, (Sāy. = माध्यमिका वाक्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषित्
योषित्, त्, f. a woman, female, wife; the female<BR>(of an animal, e. g. अलि-योषित्, a female bee).<BR>—योषित्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done by a woman,<BR>contracted by a female.<BR>—योषित्-प्रतियातना, f.<BR>the image or statue of a woman.<BR>—योषित्-सर्प,<BR>अस्, m. a serpent of a woman, a woman like a ser-<BR>pent.<BR>—योषिद्-रत्न, अम्, n. a jewel of a woman,<BR>a most excellent woman.<BR>—योषिन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>formed like a woman, representing a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषिता
योषिता, f. a woman, female, wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषित्वा
योषित्वा, ind. (said to be a kind of ind. part.<BR>derived fr. योषित्), having made into a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योस्
योस् योस्, ind. welfare, happiness, (gene-<BR>rally used in Ved. after शम्; according to Sāy.<BR>योः = यावनम्, ‘the warding off of dangers,’ as if<BR>fr. rt. 1. यु, or सुखस्य मिश्रयिता, ‘the mixer<BR>or causer of happiness,’ as if fr. rt. 2. यु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योहुल
योहुल योहुल, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौकरीय
यौकरीय यौकरीय (fr. यूकर), see Gaṇa<BR>Kṛśāśvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौक्तस्रुच
यौक्तस्रुच युक्तस्रुच, अम्, n. (fr. युक्त +<BR>स्रुच्), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौक्ताश्व
यौक्ताश्व, अम्, n. (fr. युक्ताश्व), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौक्ताश्वाद्य
यौक्ताश्वाद्य and यौक्ताश्वोत्तर, अम्, n., N.<BR>of two Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौक्तिक|यौक्तिकः
यौक्तिक यौक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. युक्ति), any-<BR>thing which connects or binds, suitable, proper, fit;<BR>founded on reasoning, logical; inferrible, deducible;<BR>usual, customary; (अस्), m. a king's companion or<BR>associate (= नर्म-सचिव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौग|यौगः
यौग यौग, अस्, m. (fr. योग), a follower<BR>of the Yoga system of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगक|यौगकः
यौगक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the religious<BR>exercise called Yoga; [cf. यौगिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगन्धर|यौगंधर
यौगन्धर or यौगन्धरक, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. युगन्-धर), relating to Yugan-dhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगन्धरायण
यौगन्धरायण, अस्, m. (fr. युगन्-धर<BR>and योगन्-धर), a patronymic; N. of a minister<BR>of Udayana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगन्धरायणीय|यौगंधरायणीय
यौगन्धरायणीय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or<BR>belonging to Yaugandharāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगन्धरि|यौगंधरि
यौगन्धरि, इस्, m. a king of the Yugan-dharas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगपद
यौगपद, अम्, n. = यौगपद्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगपद्य|यौगपद्यं
यौगपद्य, अम्, n. (fr. युग-पद्), simulta-<BR>neousness, contemporaneousness; यौगपद्येन =<BR>युग-पद्, simultaneously, together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगवरत्र
यौगवरत्र, अम्, n. = युग-वरत्राणां स-<BR>मूह, see Gaṇa Khaṇḍikādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगिक|यौगिकः
यौगिक, अस्, ई, अम्, useful, applicable; proper,<BR>customary, usual; belonging to a remedy, remedial;<BR>derivative, suiting the derivation, agreeing with the<BR>etymology, derived from the etymology, (यौगिकी<BR>सञ्ज्ञा, a word retaining that signification which<BR>belongs to it according to its etymology; यौगिक-<BR>रूढ, a word which has both an etymological and<BR>special meaning, cf. योग-रूढ); relating to the<BR>Yoga, proceeding or derived from the Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौजनशतिक|यौजनशतिकः
यौजनशतिक यौजनशतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>योजन + शत), one who goes a hundred Yojanas;<BR>one who deserves to be approached from a distance<BR>of a hundred Yojanas; [cf. क्रौशशतिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौजनिक|यौजनिकः
यौजनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. योजन), going or<BR>extending a Yojana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौट्
यौट् यौट् or यौड्, cl. 1. P. यौटति,<BR>यौडति, &c., Caus. Aor. अयुयौटत्,<BR>&c., to join or fasten together; [cf. योटक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतक|यौतकं
यौतक यौतक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. युतक),<BR>anything which rightfully belongs to or is the pro-<BR>perty of any one; (अम्), n. private property, (espe-<BR>cially) property given at marriage, a woman's dowry,<BR>nuptial gift, presents made to a bride at her marriage<BR>by her father or friends; (according to some also) a<BR>gift to the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतकि
यौतकि, इस्, m. a patronymic; यौतक्या, f., see<BR>Gaṇa Krauḍy-ādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतुक|यौतुकं
यौतुक, अम्, n. = यौतक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतव|यौतवं
यौतव यौतव, अम्, n. measure in general<BR>(= पौतव, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौथिक|यौथिकः
यौथिक यौथिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यूथ), be-<BR>longing to a band or troop, belonging to a flock or<BR>herd; (अस्), m. one belonging to the same flock or<BR>company, a companion, comrade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौथ्य
यौथ्य, see Gaṇa Saṅkāśādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौध|यौधः
यौध यौध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. योध), warlike,<BR>martial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधाजय
यौधाजय, अम्, n., N. of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधिक
यौधिक, epithet of a particular mode of fighting<BR>(Hari-vaṃśa 15980; also read योधिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधिष्ठिर|यौधिष्ठिरं
यौधिष्ठिर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. युधि-ष्ठिर),<BR>relating or belonging to Yudhi-ṣṭhira; (अस्), m. a<BR>descendant of Yudhi-ṣṭhira; (ई), f. a female de-<BR>scendant of Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधिष्ठिरि
यौधिष्ठिरि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Yudhi-<BR>ṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधेय|यौधेयः
यौधेय, अस्, m. a king of the Yaudheyas; N.<BR>of a son of Yudhi-ṣṭhira; = योद्धृ, a warrior;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a warlike race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधेयक
यौधेयक = यौधेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौन|यौनं
यौन 1. यौन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. योनि), relating<BR>to the womb or place of birth, uterine; concerning<BR>or relating to marriage or to affinity; resulting<BR>through marriage; connected by the mother's side,<BR>connubial; (अम्), n. matrimonial connection, con-<BR>jugal alliance, marriage, relationship by marriage;<BR>(at the end of an adj. comp.) proceeding from,<BR>arising from (e. g. अग्नि-यौन, proceeding from<BR>fire).<BR>—यौन-सम्बन्ध, अस्, m. relationship by<BR>marriage, affinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौन|यौनं
यौन 2. यौन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people,<BR>(probably contracted for Yavana.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौप
यौप यौप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. यूप), relating<BR>to the sacrificial post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौप्य
यौप्य, see Gaṇa Saṅkāśādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौयुधानि
यौयुधानि यौयुधानि, इस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Yuyudhāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवत|यौवतं
यौवत यौवत, अम्, n. (fr. युवति), a num-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">Page0824-c+ 74</a>]<BR>ber of girls, assemblage of young women; = यौ-<BR>तव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवतेय|यौवतेयः
यौवतेय, अस्, m. the son of a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवन|यौवनं
यौवन यौवन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. युवन्), ju-<BR>venile; (अम्), n. youth, youthfulness, the prime of<BR>life, bloom of youth, puberty, manhood, (at the end<BR>of an adj. comp. the fem. ends in आ, cf. प्राप्त-य्˚);<BR>a number of young people (especially of young<BR>women); any youthful act or juvenile indiscretion;<BR>N. of the third grade or degree in the mysteries of<BR>the Śāktas.<BR>—यौवन-कण्टक, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>an eruption common in youth, pimples &c. on the<BR>face of young people.<BR>—यौवन-दर्प, अस्, m.<BR>the pride of youth, rashness, juvenile indiscretion or<BR>conceit.<BR>—यौवन-दशा, f. the period of youth.<BR>—यौवन-पिडका, f. = यौवन-कण्टक.<BR>—यौवन-प्रान्त, अस्, अम्, m. n. the extreme<BR>verge or end of youth.<BR>—यौवन-भिन्न-शैशव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, whose childhood is divided by youth,<BR>passing from childhood to manhood.<BR>—यौवन-<BR>मत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, intoxicated by (the pride of)<BR>youth; (आ), f. a species of metre, four times ¯˘˘¯¯,<BR>¯¯¯¯¯¯¯˘˘¯¯.<BR>—यौवन-लक्षण, अम्,<BR>n. a sign or characteristic of youth; charm, loveli-<BR>ness, grace; the female breast.<BR>—यौवन-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessing youth, being in youth, young,<BR>youthful.<BR>—यौवन-श्री, ईस्, f. the beauty of youth-<BR>fulness.<BR>—यौवन-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘being in the<BR>bloom of youth,’ arrived at puberty, youthful, mar-<BR>riageable.<BR>—यौवनावस्था (˚न-अव्˚), f. the state<BR>of youth, youthfulness, puberty.<BR>—यौवनोद्भेद<BR>(˚न-उद्˚), अस्, m. the ardour of youthful passion,<BR>sexual love or inclination; Kāma-deva, the god of<BR>love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनक|यौवनकं
यौवनक, अम्, n. = यौवन, youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनाश्व|यौवनाश्वः
यौवनाश्व, अस्, m. (fr. युवनाश्व), a patro-<BR>nymic of Māndhātṛ; a patronymic of a grandson<BR>of Māndhātṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनाश्वक|यौवनाश्वकः
यौवनाश्वक, अस्, or यौवनाश्वि, इस्, m. a<BR>patronymic of Māndhātṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनिक
यौवनिक, अस्, m. (?), = यौवन, youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनिन्
यौवनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, youthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवराजिक
यौवराजिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. युव-राज), see<BR>Gaṇa Kāśyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवराज्य|यौवराज्यं
यौवराज्य, अम्, n. (fr. युव-राज), the rank or<BR>office of a Yuva-rāja or heir-apparent associated in<BR>the kingdom; the rights and privileges of heir-<BR>apparent, right of succession to the kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौषिण्य|यौषिण्यं
यौषिण्य यौषिण्य, अम्, n. womanhood;<BR>[cf. योषन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौष्माक|यौष्माकं
यौष्माक यौष्माक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. युष्म),<BR>your, yours, belonging to you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौष्माकीण
यौष्माकीण, अस्, ई, अम्, your, yours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

र|रं|रः
र 1. र, the twenty-seventh consonant of<BR>the Nāgarī alphabet, being the semivowel of the<BR>vowels ऋ, ॠ, and having the sound of the English r<BR>in real.<BR>—र-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

र|रं|रः
र 2. र, अस्, m. fire; heat, warmth; burn-<BR>ing, scorching; love, desire; speed; (आ), f. = वि-<BR>भ्रम; giving, = दान; gold, = काञ्चन; (ई),<BR>f. going, motion, = गति; (अम्), n. = तेजस्, bright-<BR>ness, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

र|रं|रः
र 3. र, (in prosody) a cretic or a short<BR>between two long syllables.<BR>—र-विपुला, f. ‘abound-<BR>ing in cretics,’ N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंसु
रंसु रंसु, उस्, उस्, उ (said by some to be<BR>fr. rt. रण्, but according to Nirukta VI. 17. and<BR>Sāy. fr. rt. रम्), Ved. cheerful, joyful, delightful;<BR>(उ), ind. cheerfully, delightfully, (Sāy. = रमणी-<BR>येषु, i. e. आज्यादि-हविःषु, in oblations, &c.)<BR>—रंसु-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a pleasing<BR>tongue or voice, (Sāy. = रमणीय-ज्वालोपेत, pos-<BR>sessing a pleasing tongue of flame.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0824-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंह्
रंह् रंह् (connected with rt. लङ्घ्; cf.<BR>rt. रङ्घ्), cl. 1. P. रंहति (also Ved. A.<BR>रंहते), ररंह, रंहितुम्, to go, move with<BR>speed, hasten; to make to run or go rapidly, cause<BR>to flow; to flow: Caus. रंहयति (according to<BR>some also रंहापयति), to cause to move rapidly,<BR>urge on; to cause to flow; to go; to speak; to<BR>shine, (in the last two senses a various reading for<BR>rt. वंह्); [cf. perhaps Gr. τρέχ-ω; Goth. thrag-<BR>ja.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंह|रंहः
रंह = रंहस् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहण|रंहणं
रंहण, अम्, n. going swiftly, hastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहति|रंहतिः
रंहति, इस्, f. (?), speed, velocity; the speed of<BR>a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहमाण
रंहमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, moving or flowing<BR>rapidly, (Sāy. = वेगं कुर्वाण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहस्
रंहस्, अस्, n. speed, quickness, velocity; eager-<BR>ness, vehemence, violence, impetuosity; N. of Śiva,<BR>(Vehemence personified); of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहस
रंहस at the end of an adj. comp. = रंहस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहि|रंहिः
रंहि, इस्, f., Ved. the act of running or flowing,<BR>a running stream; the making to run, pursuing,<BR>hunting; speed, haste, flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रारहाण
रारहाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens.; in Pada-pāṭha<BR>ररहाण), Ved. going quickly, hastening, swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्
रक् रक् (connected with rts. रग्, रघ्,<BR>लक्, लग्), cl. 10. P. राकयति, &c., to taste,<BR>relish; to obtain, get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक|रकः
रक, अस्, m. the sun gem; crystal; a hard<BR>shower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रकसा
रकसा रकसा, f. a mild form of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्क
रक्क रक्क, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रक्क-<BR>जया, f., N. of a statue of Śrī erected by Rakka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्त|रक्तं|रक्तः
रक्त रक्त, रक्तक, रक्त-कङ्गु, &c. See<BR>p. 826, col. 3, and p. 828, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ति|रक्तिः
रक्ति रक्ति, &c. See p. 828, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्
रक्ष् 1. रक्ष् (thought by some to be<BR>connected with rt. रञ्ज् as a kind of Desid.<BR>form of that rt.), cl. 1. P. रक्षति (Ved. and ep. also A.<BR>रक्षते), ररक्ष, रक्षिष्यति, अरक्षीत् (an<BR>earlier form अराक्षीत् is also given, Ved. Leṭ. रक्-<BR>षिषत्), रक्षितुम्, to guard, watch, take care of,<BR>protect, preserve, save, keep, (रहस्यं रक्ष्,<BR>to keep a secret), hold, maintain, tend, (पशून्<BR>रक्ष्, to tend cattle); to govern, rule over, (क्षि-<BR>तिम् or वसुधां रक्ष्, to govern the earth); to<BR>spare, save; to protect or save from (with abl.); to<BR>take care, beware of, be on one's guard against;<BR>to take refuge or shelter (A.): Caus. रक्षयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अररक्षत्, to guard, watch, protect:<BR>Desid. रिरक्षिषति, to wish to guard, intend to pro-<BR>tect from (with abl.): Intens. रारक्ष्यते, राराष्टि,<BR>to protect very carefully; [cf. probably Gr. ἀρκ-έ-ω,<BR>ἄρκιο-ς, ἀλκτήρ, ἀλαλκτήρ, ἀλκή, ἀλέξω; Lat.<BR>arc-e-o, arx; Goth. ga-rehsns.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्
2. रक्ष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, guarding, watching, protecting,<BR>tending, &c. (at the end of a comp., cf. गो-रक्ष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष|रक्षः
रक्ष, अस्, ई, m. f. a guard, guardian, protector,<BR>keeper; protecting, preserving, watching, keeping,<BR>&c. (often at the end of a comp., cf. गो-र्˚); (आ), f.<BR>the act of protecting or guarding, protection, care,<BR>preservation, security; a guard, watch; any preser-<BR>vative, any act or right performed for protection or<BR>preservation, a sort of bracelet or amulet, any mys-<BR>tical token used as a charm; a tutelary divinity [cf.<BR>महा-र्˚]; ashes (used as a preservative); (आ or ई),<BR>f. a piece of thread or silk bound round the wrist on<BR>particular occasions (especially on the full moon of<BR>Śrāvaṇa, either as an amulet and preservative against<BR>misfortune, or as a symbol of mutual dependence,<BR>or as a mark of respect; among the Rājputs it is<BR>sometimes sent by a lady of rank or family to a<BR>person of influence whose protection she is desirous<BR>of securing and whom she thus adopts, as it were, as a<BR>male relative or brother).<BR>—रक्ष-पाल or रक्ष-<BR>पालक, अस्, m. a protector, guard.<BR>—रक्ष-भ-<BR>गवती, f. = प्रज्ञा-पारमिता.<BR>—रक्षा-करण्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">Page0825-b+ 80</a>]<BR>डक, अम्, n. an amulet in the shape of a small<BR>basket.<BR>—रक्षा-गृह, अम्, n. ‘watch-room,’ a<BR>lying-in chamber, room appropriated to a lying-in<BR>woman.<BR>—रक्षाधिकृत (˚षा-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>entrusted with the protection or superintendence (of<BR>a country, &c.), placed over the government; (अस्),<BR>m. a superintendent or governor (of a province),<BR>magistrate, superintendent of police.<BR>—रक्षाधि-<BR>पति (˚षा-अध्˚) or रक्षा-पति, इस्, m. one placed<BR>over for protection, a superintendent of police.<BR>—रक्षा-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a kind of birch tree (=<BR>भूर्ज).<BR>—रक्षा-पुरुष, अस्, m. a watchman,<BR>guard, protector.<BR>—रक्षापेक्षक (˚षा-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a doorkeeper, porter; a guard of the women's<BR>apartments; a catamite; an actor, mime.<BR>—रक्षा-<BR>प्रदीप, अस्, m. a light kept burning for protection<BR>(against evil spirits, &c.).<BR>—रक्षा-भूषण, अम्,<BR>n. an ornament or amulet worn for protection (against<BR>evil spirits, &c.).<BR>—रक्षाभ्यधिकृत (˚षा-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, and अस्, m. = रक्षाधिकृत.<BR>—रक्षा-मङ्गल, अम्, n. a ceremony performed<BR>for protection (against evil spirits, &c.).<BR>—रक्षा-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. a jewel worn as a preservative (against<BR>evil spirits, &c.).<BR>—रक्षा-मल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—रक्षा-महौषधि, इस्, f. a sovereign<BR>remedy serving as a preservative (against evil spirits,<BR>&c.).<BR>—रक्षा-रत्न, अम्, n. = रक्षा-मणि.<BR>—रक्षा-रत्न-प्रदीप, अस्, m. a lamp shining<BR>or brilliant with gems used as a preservative (against<BR>evil spirits, &c.; cf. रत्न-प्रदीप).<BR>—रक्षार्-<BR>थम् (˚षा-अर्˚), ind. for the sake of guarding, for<BR>guarding.<BR>—रक्षा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having or en-<BR>joying protection, protected, guarded.<BR>—रक्षा-सर्-<BR>षप, अस्, m. mustard as a preservative (against evil<BR>spirits).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षक|रक्षकः
रक्षक, अस्, इका, अम्, who or what protects or<BR>guards or tends [cf. गो-र्˚]; guarding, protecting;<BR>(अस्), m. a guardian, protector; a guard, watch;<BR>(इका), f. a female guardian or protector; an amulet,<BR>charm, anything worn as a preservative (= रक्षा).<BR>—रक्षकाम्बा (˚क-अम्˚), f., N. of the wife of<BR>Rāmānuja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षण|रक्षणं|रक्षणः
रक्षण, अस्, m. a protector, defender, guardian;<BR>N. of Viṣṇu; (आ), f. the act of protecting or guard-<BR>ing, watching over, protection; (ई), f. a rein, bridle;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of guarding, watching, protecting,<BR>tending, caring for, preserving, protection, (पशू-<BR>नां रक्षणम्, the tending of cattle); a ceremony<BR>performed for protection or preservation.<BR>—रक्ष-<BR>णार्थम् (˚ण-अर्˚), ind. for the sake of guarding or<BR>protecting.<BR>—रक्षणोपाय (˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>means of safety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणारक|रक्षणारकः
रक्षणारक or रक्षणीरक, अस्, m. (pro-<BR>bably connected with rt. 1. रक्ष्), morbid retention<BR>of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणि|रक्षणिः
रक्षणि, इस्, f. a species of plant (= त्रायमाणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणीय
रक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be guarded or pre-<BR>served, to be protected; to be watched or guarded<BR>against, defensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षत्
रक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, guarding, protecting, pre-<BR>serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षमाण
रक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, protecting, guarding,<BR>being on one's guard, watching against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्
1. रक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (for 2. see col. 2), protecting<BR>(at the end of a comp., e. g. पथि-र्˚, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षा
रक्षा, f. guard, protection, &c.; see रक्ष,<BR>col. 1; (for रक्षा = राक्षा, lac, see राक्षा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षि
रक्षि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. guarding, protecting (at the<BR>end of a comp., e. g. पथि-र्˚, पशु-र्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिक|रक्षिकः
रक्षिक, अस्, m. (fr. रक्षा), a guard, protector,<BR>policeman.<BR>—रक्षिक-पुरुष, अस्, m. a watch-<BR>man, policeman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षित|रक्षितं
रक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, guarded, protected, taken<BR>care of, preserved, maintained, kept; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a teacher of medicine; of a grammarian; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—रक्षित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, con-<BR>taining the idea of रक्ष् or ‘protecting, &c.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितक
रक्षितक in दार-रक्षितक, relating to the<BR>guarding or protection of wives; (इका), f. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितव्य
रक्षितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be guarded, to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">Page0825-c+ 79</a>]<BR>protected or taken care of, to be guarded against or<BR>kept off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितृ
रक्षितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who guards or protects,<BR>a guardian, guard, protector, watch, sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिन्
रक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, a guardian, protector, defender,<BR>guard, sentinel; guarding, protecting, protecting<BR>from (often at the end of comps., e. g. अमृत-<BR>रक्षिन्, guarding the nectar; cf. रिपु-र्˚, सर्व-<BR>र्˚).<BR>—रक्षि-वर्ग, अस्, m. an assemblage of guards<BR>or sentinels, body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्ण|रक्ष्णः
रक्ष्ण, अस्, m. protection (= त्राण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्य
रक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be guarded or protected,<BR>to be taken care of; to be watched against; to be<BR>concerned about, to be on one's guard against (with<BR>abl.).<BR>—रक्ष्य-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, to be protected<BR>most carefully, requiring the greatest watching, most<BR>worthy of protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्यमाण
रक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being guarded or<BR>protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ररक्षाण
ररक्षाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. excessively pro-<BR>tecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्
रक्ष् 3. रक्ष् (probably a form of rt.<BR>ऋक्ष् = rts. रिश्, 1. रिष्, q. q. v. v.), Ved.<BR>to hurt, injure, destroy, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्
2. रक्षस्, अस्, n. hurt, injury, damage (Ved.,<BR>but according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 104, 23.<BR>रक्षस् = राक्षस-जाति, ‘the race of Rākṣasas,’<BR>and in I. 36, 20. रक्षस् = बलम्, ‘strength’);<BR>‘the injurer,’ (according to some a kind of euphe-<BR>mism fr. rt. 1. रक्ष्, like Εὐμενίδες); an evil<BR>being or demon, an ogre, malignant spirit, a<BR>Rākṣasa, (these beings play an important part in<BR>the Hindū religious and mythological system; see<BR>their description under राक्षस); (आस्), m., Ved.<BR>an evil and malignant being, a nocturnal fiend or<BR>Rākṣasa, (see राक्षस.)<BR>—रक्ष-ईश, अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of the Rākṣasas,’ N. of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—रक्षः-<BR>सभ, अम्, n. an assemblage or multitude of Rāk-<BR>ṣasas.<BR>—रक्षस्-त्व, अम्, n. the nature of a<BR>Rākṣasa, demoniacal nature or disposition, fiend-<BR>ishness, malignity, malice.<BR>—रक्षस्-पाश, अस्, m.<BR>a contemptible Rākṣasa, despicable demon; [cf.<BR>पाश.]<BR>—रक्षस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having or<BR>attended by Rākṣasas, demoniacal, evil-disposed,<BR>malignant; (Sāy.) powerful, strong (= बल-वत्).<BR>—रक्षो-गण, अस्, m. a class or company of<BR>demons.<BR>—रक्षो-गण-भोजन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>hell where human beings are eaten by Rākṣasas.<BR>—रक्षो-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, driving back or repel-<BR>ling Rākṣasas, killing or destroying Rākṣasas;<BR>(अस्), m. Semecarpus Anacardium; white mustard;<BR>(ई), f. Acorus Calamus; (अम्), n. sour rice-gruel.<BR>—रक्षो-जननी, f. ‘producing Rākṣasas,’ night.<BR>—रक्षो-ऽधिदेवता, f. the chief goddess of the<BR>Rākṣasas.<BR>—रक्षो-भाष्, ट्, Ved. barking or mak-<BR>ing a noise like a Rākṣasa, (see 2. भाष्.)<BR>—रक्-<BR>षो-मुख, अस्, m. ‘Rākṣasa-faced,’ N. of a man;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. his descendants.<BR>—रक्षो-युज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>Ved. associated with Rākṣasas.<BR>—रक्षो-वाह,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a race.<BR>—रक्षो-विक्षोभिणी, f.<BR>‘agitating or exciting the Rākṣasas,’ N. of a god-<BR>dess.<BR>—रक्षो-हण, अस्, आ, अम्, = रक्षो-हन्.<BR>—रक्षोहणक, containing the word रक्षो-<BR>हण.<BR>—रक्षो-हत्य, अम्, n., Ved. the killing or<BR>destruction of Rākṣasas.<BR>—रक्षो-हन्, हा, घ्नी,<BR>ह, Ved. destroying or killing Rākṣasas; (हा),<BR>m., N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 162;<BR>bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्य
रक्षस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, useful for (keeping off)<BR>Rākṣasas, anti-demoniacal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रख्
रख् रख् or रङ्ख् (connected with rts.<BR>रिख्, रिङ्ख्), cl. 1. P. रखति, रङ्खति,<BR>&c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रग्
रग् रग्, cl. 1. P. रगति, रराग, अरगीत्,<BR>&c., to doubt, suspect; cl. 10. P. रागयति<BR>= rt. रक्, to taste, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघ्
रघ् रघ् (= rt. रक्), cl. 10. P. राघयति,<BR>to taste, relish; to obtain; cl. 1. A. रङ्घते,<BR>&c., to go, (see rt. रङ्घ्); [cf. Lith. ragauja.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0825-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघु|रघुः
रघु रघु, उस्, घ्वी, उ (fr. rt. रंह् or<BR>रङ्घ्), Ved. fleet, rapid, rushing, (Sāy. = शीघ्र-<BR>गामिन्); eager; light (= लघु), fickle; (उस्), m.<BR>a racer, fleet courser (Ved.); N. of an ancient king<BR>and ancestor of Rāma, (in the Raghu-vaṃśa he is<BR>described as the son of Dilīpa and Su-dakṣiṇā, and<BR>in III. 21. the name Raghu is said to have been<BR>given to him as ‘going’ to the end of the Śāstras<BR>and to the destruction of his enemies; he was the<BR>father of Aja, the father of Daśa-ratha, and was<BR>therefore great-grandfather of Rāma; but different<BR>accounts are given of Rāma's genealogy, and in<BR>Rāmāyaṇa II. 110, 28. Raghu is said to be son of<BR>Kakutstha; in the Hari-vaṃśa two Raghus are men-<BR>tioned among the ancestors of Rāma); N. of a son<BR>of Śākya-muni; of the author of the Kavi-darpaṇa;<BR>an abbreviation for Raghu-vaṃśa, q. v.; (अवस्), m.<BR>pl. the Raghus or descendants of Raghu; [cf. रा-<BR>घव.]<BR>—रघु-कार, अस्, m., N. of Kālidāsa the<BR>author of the Raghu-vaṃśa.<BR>—रघु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. produced from a fleet courser or racer.<BR>—र-<BR>घु-टिप्पणी, f., N. of a commentary on the Raghu-<BR>vaṃśa.<BR>—रघु-तनय, अस्, m. son of Raghu, N.<BR>of Rāma.<BR>—रघु-देव, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Virudāvalī; (ई), f., N. of a commentary on<BR>the Tattva-cintāmaṇi by Raghu-deva.<BR>—रघु-द्रु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. going or running quickly, running<BR>like a race-horse.<BR>—रघु-नन्दन, अस्, m. a<BR>descendant or son of Raghu, N. of Rāma; N. of an<BR>author of several treatises on religion and law.<BR>—र-<BR>घु-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of Rāma; of various persons;<BR>of the author of the Rasika-ramaṇa.<BR>—रघु-पति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of Rāma; of the father of the lexicogra-<BR>pher Jaṭā-dhara.<BR>—रघु-पत्म-जंहस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. light-winged, (Sāy.) having a light-falling<BR>foot (= लघु-पतन-समर्थ-पाद).<BR>—रघु-<BR>पत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. lightly flying, going or<BR>moving quickly; [cf. Lat. acci-piter = Sansk. आशु-<BR>पत्वन्.]<BR>—रघु-प्रतिनिधि, इस्, m. image or<BR>counterpart of Raghu.<BR>—रघु-प्रवर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of Rāma.<BR>—रघु-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>having light or little wrath, mild-tempered, (Sāy. =<BR>लघु-क्रोध); full of eagerness or zeal.<BR>—रघु-<BR>यामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. going quickly, moving lightly.<BR>—रघु-राम, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रघु-<BR>वंश, अस्, m. the race or family of Raghu; N.<BR>of Kālidāsa's celebrated poem in honour of the race<BR>of Raghu, (it consists of nineteen chapters or books;<BR>cf. महा-काव्य.)<BR>—रघुवंश-तिलक, अस्, m.<BR>‘ornament of the race of Raghu,’ epithet of Rāma.<BR>—रघुवंश-सञ्जीवनी, f., N. of Mallinātha's<BR>commentary on the Raghu-vaṃśa.<BR>—रघु-वर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of Rāma.<BR>—रघु-वर्तनि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. lightly rolling or turning (said of a chariot and<BR>of a horse).<BR>—रघु-वीर, अस्, m., N. of Rāma;<BR>of an author (= Raghu-deva).<BR>—रघु-ष्यद्, त्, त्,<BR>त् (i. e. रघु + स्यद्), Ved. moving quickly, hasty,<BR>speedy, rapid, (Sāy. = शीघ्र-गमन, शीघ्रं<BR>स्यन्दमान.)<BR>—रघूत्तम (˚घु-उत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘best of the Raghus,’ N. of Rāma.<BR>—रघूद्वह<BR>(˚घु-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘offspring of Raghu,’ N. of<BR>Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघीयस्
रघीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of रघु), Ved.<BR>more rapid or fleet, very swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुयत्|रघुयन्त्
रघुयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (Part. fr. an unused Nom.<BR>रघुय), moving fleetly or rapidly, (Sāy. = शीघ्रं<BR>गच्छत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुया
रघुया, ind. (fr. रघु), Ved. quickly, swiftly,<BR>lightly, (Sāy. = शीघ्र-गामिन्, as if रघु-या.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघूयत्|रघूयन्त्
रघूयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. = रघुयत् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्क|रंक|रङ्कः
रङ्क रङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, niggardly, mean,<BR>indigent, poor, miserable, hungry, (कङ्क-रङ्क,<BR>a hungry or half-starved crane; cf. जल-र्˚, मत्स्य-<BR>र्˚); slow; (अस्), m. a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्कु|रंकु|रंकुः|रङ्कुः
रङ्कु रङ्कु, उस्, m. a species of deer or<BR>antelope; N. of a place.<BR>—रङ्कु-मालिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a Vidyā-dhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्क्तृ
रङ्क्तृ रङ्क्तृ. See रक्तृ, p. 828, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्क्षु
रङ्क्षु रङ्क्षु, N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ख्
रङ्ख् रङ्ख् = rt. रख्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ग्|रंग्
रङ्ग् रङ्ग् (= rt. रिङ्ग्), cl. 1. P. रङ्गति,<BR>&c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ग|रंग|रङ्गं|रंगः|रङ्गः
रङ्ग रङ्ग, रङ्गिन्, &c. See p. 828.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गोजि
रङ्गोजि रङ्गोजि, इस्, or रङ्गोजि-भट्ट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the father of Koṇḍabhaṭṭa and brother of<BR>Bhaṭṭoji.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्घ्|रंघ्
रङ्घ् रङ्घ् [cf. rt. रंह्], cl. 1. A. रङ्-<BR>घते, ररङ्घे, रङ्घितुम्, to go, hasten,<BR>run; cl. 10. P. or Caus. रङ्घयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>speak; to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्घस्|रंघस्
रङ्घस्, अस्, n. = रंहस्, haste, speed, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रच्
रच् रच्, cl. 10. P. रचयति, रचयाम्-<BR>आस, रचयितुम्, to make, form, fabricate,<BR>create, produce; to prepare, get ready, contrive,<BR>plan, arrange, dispose; to complete, effect; to com-<BR>pose, write (a book or any literary work); to string<BR>together; to adorn, decorate; to place in or on<BR>(with loc.), fix on; to direct (the thoughts &c.)<BR>towards: Caus. रचयति, to cause to make or do<BR>(with two acc.); to cause to move, put in motion;<BR>[cf. Lat. locare, locus: Angl. Sax. logian, ‘to<BR>place;’ loh.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचन|रचनं
रचन, अम्, n. the act of making, forming, form-<BR>ation, creation, arranging, putting in order, managing,<BR>directing, preparing; (आ, अम्), f. n. arrangement,<BR>disposition, management, preparation, performance,<BR>accomplishment, fabrication; a literary production,<BR>work, composition; dressing of the hair; stringing<BR>flowers or garlands, the arrangement of troops, array;<BR>a creation of the mind, artificial image, (अर्थ-<BR>रचना, striving after or accomplishing an object;<BR>गीति-रचना, a musical or vocal composition; निवास-<BR>रचना, a building); according to native lexicogra-<BR>phers रचना = परि-स्पन्द or परि-स्यन्द, प्र-<BR>ति-यत्न, ग्रन्थन, गुम्फ, व्यूह, निवेश,<BR>स्थिति; also = पाश, भार, पक्ष, उच्चय,<BR>‘abundance,’ ‘quantity,’ when compounded with a<BR>word meaning ‘hair’ (e. g. केश-रचना, abundance<BR>of hair); (आ), f., N. of the wife of Tvaṣṭṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचयत्
रचयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, making, forming, com-<BR>posing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचयितृ
रचयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who makes or com-<BR>poses, a composer, author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचयित्वा
रचयित्वा, ind. having made or formed, having<BR>arranged, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचित|रचितः
रचित, अस्, आ, अम्, made, formed, fabricated, pro-<BR>duced, prepared, made ready, concerted, contrived,<BR>planned, arranged, completed, effected, composed,<BR>written; strung together; decorated, adorned; fas-<BR>tened, placed in or on (with loc.); directed towards;<BR>furnished or equipped with, provided with (with<BR>inst. or at the end of a comp.); (अस्), m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—रचित-त्व, अम्, n. the being composed or<BR>written.<BR>—रचित-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, having the mind<BR>directed to (with loc.), intent on.<BR>—रचित-पङ्क्ति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, forming a line.<BR>—रचित-शिखर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the summit adorned.<BR>—रचितार्थ (˚त-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has obtained his object<BR>(= कृतार्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्
रज् रज्. See rt. रञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज|रजं|रजः
रज, रजक, रजनि, रजस्, &c. See p. 828,<BR>cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजि|रजिः
रजि रजि, इस्, m., N. of a demon or king<BR>subdued by Indra, (according to Sāy., Ṛg-veda VI.<BR>26, 6, रजि means ‘a maiden or a kingdom called<BR>Raji;’ and X. 105, 2, ‘heaven and earth’ or ‘the<BR>sun and moon,’ but the meaning is obscure); N. of a<BR>son of Āyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजिष्ठ
रजिष्ठ रजिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of ऋजु),<BR>Ved. = ऋजिष्ठ, most honest or upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजीयस्
रजीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of ऋजु), Ved. more<BR>honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजीकृ
रजीकृ रजी-कृ, रजो-गात्र, &c. See p. 829,<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जु|रज्जुः
रज्जु रज्जु, उस्, f. (at the end of a comp.<BR>sometimes उस्, m.; in the older language also रज्जू,<BR>Ved. acc. रज्ज्वम्, gen. रज्ज्वास् [Manu XI. 168]<BR>and रज्जोस्; said in Uṇādi-s. I. 16. to be fr. rt. सृज्;<BR>according to some, perhaps for original स्रज्यु, cf.<BR>स्रज्), a rope, cord, string, line, (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp. the fem. may be रज्जुका); N. of certain<BR>sinews or tendons proceeding from the vertebral<BR>column (in anatomy); a lock of braided hair, braid<BR>(= वेणी); N. of a particular constellation; [cf. Lat.<BR>ligare, stringere; Old Germ. stricch, stric, strac-<BR>chian; Angl. Sax. streccan.]<BR>—रज्जु-कण्ठ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—रज्जु-दाल, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>a species of tree.<BR>—रज्जु-दालक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>wild-fowl.<BR>—रज्जु-पेडा, f. a rope basket.<BR>—रज्जु-<BR>भार, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—रज्जु-मात्र-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the condition of being only a rope.<BR>—रज्जु-वाल, अस्, m. = रज्जु-दालक, a wild-fowl.<BR>—रज्जु-शारद, अस्, आ, अम्, newly drawn up by a<BR>rope (said of water; Pāṇini VI. 2, 9).<BR>—रज्जु-<BR>सर्ज, अस्, m., Ved. a rope-maker.<BR>—रज्जूद्धृत<BR>(˚जु-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, drawn up by means of a rope.<BR>—रज्ज्व्-अवलम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hanging by a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जव्य
रज्जव्य, अम्, n., Ved. material for a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्छ्
रञ्छ् रञ्छ्. See नि-रञ्छन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्ज्|रंज्
रञ्ज् रञ्ज् or रज्, cl. 1. 4. P. A. रजति,<BR>-ते (ep. also रञ्जति), रज्यति, -ते, र-<BR>रञ्ज (3rd pl. ररजतुस् or ररञ्जतुस्), ररञ्जे,<BR>रङ्क्ष्यति, -ते, अराङ्क्षीत्, अरङ्क्त, रज्यात्,<BR>रङ्क्षीष्ट, रङ्क्तुम्, to be dyed or coloured, to<BR>redden, grow red, glow; to dye, tinge, colour; to<BR>be affected or moved, to have the passions or feelings<BR>roused, to be excited; to be pleased or delighted<BR>with (with inst.); to attach one's self to, be attached<BR>or devoted to, (perhaps in this sense connected with<BR>rt. लग्); fall in love with, be enamoured of (usually<BR>with loc.); to go, (in this sense cl. 1. P. according<BR>to Naighaṇṭuka II. 14): Caus. रञ्जयति, -यते,<BR>-यितुम्, to dye, colour, paint, make red, redden,<BR>illuminate; to rejoice, gratify, exhilarate, charm; to<BR>cause to be attached, to conciliate; (according to<BR>Naighaṇṭuka III. 14) = rt. अर्च्, to worship, (also<BR>रजयति); to hunt, (in this sense only रजयति):<BR>Desid. रिरङ्क्षति, -ते: Intens. रारज्यते, रा-<BR>रङ्क्ति, to be greatly affected or excited; to be<BR>intensely attached or devoted; [cf. Gr. ῥέζ-ω, ῥαγ-εύ-ς,<BR>ῥηγ-εύ-ς, ῥεγ-εύ-ς, ῥέγ-ος, ῥέγ-μα, ῥήσσω,<BR>ῥῆγ-ος, λέγ-νον: probably Angl. Sax. ge-regnian,<BR>‘to colour.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्त|रक्तं|रक्तः
रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, coloured, dyed, painted, tinged,<BR>stained; reddened, red, crimson, of a red colour; nasal-<BR>ized (said of a vowel, cf. रङ्ग); affected by passion,<BR>excited, incited, impassioned, passionately fond of,<BR>attached, affected with love or interest towards; lov-<BR>ing, dear, beloved; lovely, pleasant, agreeable, sweet,<BR>charming; fond of play, engaging in pastime, sport-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. red colour; safflower; Barringtonia<BR>Acutangula; epithet of Śiva; (आ), f. lac (= लाक्षा);<BR>Abrus Precatorious; Bengal madder, Rubia Munjista;<BR>= उष्ट्र-काण्डी; N. of one of the seven tongues<BR>of fire; the female personification of a particular<BR>musical mode; (अम्), n. blood; copper; saffron;<BR>the fruit of the Flacourtia Cataphracta; vermilion;<BR>cinnabar; = पद्मक; [cf. Gr. ῥόδον; Hib. rot.]<BR>—रक्त-कङ्गु, उस्, m. Panicum Italicum.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>कण्ट, अस्, m. a species of Celastrus.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, ई, अम्, or रक्त-कण्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>sweet-voiced, having an impassioned voice or note;<BR>(अस्), m. = कोकिल, the Indian cuckoo.<BR>—रक्तकण्-<BR>ठ-खग, अस्, m. a sweet-voiced bird.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>कदम्ब, अस्, m. a red-flowering Kadamba.<BR>—रक्-<BR>त-कदली, f. a species of Musa or plantain.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>कन्द, अस्, m. coral; N. of two bulbous plants (=<BR>रक्तालु, राज-पलाण्डु).<BR>—रक्त-कन्दल, अस्, m.<BR>coral.<BR>—रक्त-कमल or रक्त-कम्बल, अम्, n.<BR>a red lotus-flower.<BR>—रक्त-करवीर or रक्त-<BR>करवीरक, अस्, m. a red-flowering Oleander,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0827-a" target="_blank">Page0827-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Nerium Odorum Rubro-simplex.<BR>—रक्त-कञ्चन,<BR>अस्, m. Bauhinia Variegata.<BR>—रक्त-काण्डा, f. a<BR>red-flowering Punarnavā.<BR>—रक्त-काष्ठ, अम्, n.<BR>Cæsalpina Sappan.<BR>—रक्त-कुमुद, अम्, n. the<BR>flower of Nymphæa Rubra, red lotus.<BR>—रक्त-कृ-<BR>मिजा, f. red lac.<BR>—रक्त-केशर, अस्, m. Rottleria<BR>Tinctoria; the coral tree.<BR>—रक्त-कैरव or रक्त-<BR>कोकनद, अम्, n. the flower of Nymphæa Rubra,<BR>a red lotus-flower.<BR>—रक्त-कोशतकी, f. a species of<BR>plant (= महा-जाली).<BR>—रक्त-खदिर, अस्, m. a<BR>red-flowering Khadira.<BR>—रक्त-खाडव, अस्, m.<BR>a species of foreign date.<BR>—रक्त-गन्धक, अम्,<BR>n. myrrh.<BR>—रक्त-गर्भा, f. Lawsonia Alba.<BR>—रक्-<BR>त-गुल्म, अस्, m. a particular form of the disease<BR>called गुल्म.<BR>—रक्त-गुल्मिनी, f. a female suffering<BR>from the above-mentioned disease.<BR>—रक्त-गैरिक,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of ochre.<BR>—रक्त-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. a<BR>kind of Mimosa.<BR>—रक्त-ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘red-<BR>necked,’ a kind of pigeon; a Rākṣasa.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, blood-destroying, corrupting the<BR>blood; (अस्), m. Andersonia Rohitaka; (ई), f. a kind<BR>of Dūrvā grass.<BR>—रक्त-चन्दन, अम्, n. red<BR>sandal; Cæsalpina Sappan; saffron.<BR>—रक्त-चित्र-<BR>क, अस्, m. a species of shrub.<BR>—रक्त-चिल्लिका, f.<BR>a kind of Chenopodium.<BR>—रक्त-चूर्ण, अम्, n.<BR>vermilion.<BR>—रक्त-च्छर्दि, इस्, f. vomiting or<BR>spitting blood.<BR>—रक्त-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>from blood.<BR>—रक्त-जन्तुक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>worm, an earth-worm.<BR>—रक्त-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>red-tongued; (अस्), m. a lion.<BR>—रक्त-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, more red; more attached, very attached; (अम्),<BR>n. = रक्त-गैरिक.<BR>—रक्त-ता, f. redness; the<BR>nature of blood; the being affected by passion.<BR>—रक्त-तुण्ड, अस्, m. ‘red-beaked,’ a parrot.<BR>—रक्त-तुण्डक, अस्, m. a kind of worm.<BR>—रक्-<BR>त-तृणा, f. a species of grass (= गो-मूत्रिका).<BR>—रक्त-तेजस्, अस्, n. flesh.<BR>—रक्त-त्रिवृत्, त्, f. a<BR>red-flowering Trivṛt.<BR>—रक्त-त्व, अम्, n. redness;<BR>the being affected by passion, affection.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>दन्तिका or रक्त-दन्ती, f. ‘red-toothed,’ N. of<BR>Durgā or Pārvatī.<BR>—रक्त-दला, f., N. of two<BR>plants (= चिविल्लिका, नलिका).<BR>—रक्त-दूषण,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, corrupting or vitiating the blood.<BR>—रक्-<BR>त-दृश्, क्, m. ‘red-eyed,’ a pigeon.<BR>—रक्त-धातु,<BR>उस्, m. red chalk or orpiment, earth, ruddle; copper.<BR>—रक्त-नयन, अस्, ई, अम्, red-eyed, having red<BR>eyes; (अस्), m. a kind of partridge, Perdix Rufa.<BR>—रक्त-नाडी, f. a fistulous ulcer on the gum caused<BR>by a bad state of the blood.<BR>—रक्त-नाल = जीवन्ती,<BR>a kind of lotus.<BR>—रक्त-नासिक, अस्, m. ‘red-<BR>beaked,’ an owl.<BR>—रक्त-नेत्र, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>red-eyed.<BR>—रक्तनेत्र-ता, f. or रक्तनेत्र-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the state of having red or blood-shot eyes.<BR>—रक्त-प, अस्, आ, अम्, blood-drinking, blood-<BR>sucking; (अस्), m. a Rākṣasa; (आ), f. a blood-<BR>sucker, leech; a Ḍākinī or female fiend.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>पक्ष, अस्, m. ‘red-winged,’ epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—रक्त-पट, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a red cloth or<BR>garment; (अस्), m. a kind of mendicant (= साङ्ख्य-<BR>भिक्षु).<BR>—रक्तपटी-कृत, अस्, m. changed into<BR>a रक्त-पट mendicant.<BR>—रक्त-पत्त्रा, f. Bœr-<BR>havia Erecta Rosea.<BR>—रक्त-पत्त्राङ्ग, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of red sandal.<BR>—रक्त-पत्त्रिका, f., N. of two<BR>plants (= नाकुली, रक्त-पुनर्नवा).<BR>—रक्त-<BR>पदी, f. a species of plant.<BR>—रक्त-पद्म, अम्,<BR>n. a red lotus-flower, large red water-lily.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>पर्ण = रक्त-पुनर्नवा.<BR>—रक्त-पल्लव, अस्,<BR>m. Jonesia Asoka.<BR>—रक्त-पाकी, f. the egg-plant.<BR>—रक्त-पात, अस्, m. bloodshed, spilling of blood.<BR>—रक्त-पाता, f. a leech.<BR>—रक्त-पाद, अस्, आ or<BR>ई, अम्, red-footed; (अस्), m. a bird with red feet, a<BR>parrot; an elephant; a war-chariot; (ई), f. Mimosa<BR>Pudica.<BR>—रक्त-पायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, blood-drinking;<BR>(ई), m. a bug; (इनी), f. a blood-sucker, leech.<BR>—रक्त-पारद, अम्, अस्, n. m. cinnabar.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>पिटिका, f. a red boil or ulcer.<BR>—रक्त-पिण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. Hibiscus Rosa Sinensis; (अम्), n. the flower of<BR>this plant; a spontaneous discharge of blood from<BR>the nose and mouth; a red pimple or boil; a species<BR>of climbing plant, Ventilago Madraspatana.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>पिण्डक, अस्, m. = रक्तालु.<BR>—रक्त-पित्त, अम्, n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0827-b" target="_blank">Page0827-b+ 81</a>]<BR>‘blood-bile,’ a peculiar disturbance of the blood<BR>caused by bile, plethora, spontaneous hemorrhages<BR>from the mouth, nose, &c. (accompanied with fever,<BR>head-ache, vomiting, purging, &c.).<BR>—रक्तपित्त-<BR>कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing the above disease.<BR>—रक्तपित्त-हा, f. ‘removing रक्त-पित्त,’ a<BR>kind of Dūrvā grass.<BR>—रक्त-पित्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sub-<BR>ject to or suffering from रक्त-पित्त.<BR>—रक्त-पुच्-<BR>छक, अस्, इका, अम्, red-tailed; (इका), f. a kind of<BR>lizard.<BR>—रक्त-पुनर्नवा, f. a red-flowering Punar-<BR>navā.<BR>—रक्त-पुष्प, अम्, n. a red flower; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), red-flowered, bearing red flowers; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of various plants, Bauhinia Variegata Purpuras-<BR>cens; = कर-वीर; = दाडिम; = वक; = बन्धू-<BR>क; = पुन्-नाग; (आ), f. Bombax Heptaphyllum;<BR>(ई), f., N. of various plants, Grislea Tomentosa; =<BR>पाटलि; = जवा; = आवर्तकी; = नाग-दमनी; =<BR>करुणी; = उष्ट्र-काण्डी.<BR>—रक्त-पुष्पक, अस्,<BR>m., N. of various plants. = पलाश; = पर्पत; =<BR>शाल्मलि; (इका), f. Mimosa Pudica; = रक्त-पु-<BR>नर्नवा; = भू-पाटली.<BR>—रक्त-पूय, N. of a<BR>hell.<BR>—रक्त-पूरक, अम्, n. the dried peel or<BR>integument of the mangosteen^1.<BR>—रक्त-पूर्ण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, full of blood.<BR>—रक्तपूर्ण-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being full of blood, fulness of blood.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>पैत्त or रक्त-पैत्तिक, adjectives from रक्त-<BR>पित्त.<BR>—रक्त-प्रदर, अस्, m., Ved. a flow of<BR>blood from the womb.<BR>—रक्त-प्रमेह, अस्, m. a<BR>disease of the bladder, the passing of blood in the<BR>urine.<BR>—रक्त-प्रवाह, अस्, m. a stream of blood.<BR>—रक्त-प्रसव, अस्, m., N. of two plants (=<BR>रक्त-करवीर, रक्ताम्लान).<BR>—रक्त-फल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having or bearing red fruit; (अस्), m. the<BR>Indian fig-tree; (आ), f. Momordica Monadelpha; =<BR>स्वर्ण-वल्ली.<BR>—रक्त-फेन-ज, अस्, m. a part of<BR>the body, (probably) the lungs.<BR>—रक्त-बिन्दु,<BR>रक्त-बीज, &c., see रक्त-विन्दु, &c.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>भव, अम्, n. ‘blood-produced,’ flesh.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, being in love, amorous, ena-<BR>moured.<BR>—रक्त-मञ्जर, अस्, m. Barringtonia<BR>Acutangula.<BR>—रक्त-मण्डल, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a red disk (said of the moon); having devoted<BR>subjects; (अस्), m. a species of red-spotted or red-<BR>ringed snake; (आ), f. a particular venomous animal;<BR>(अम्), n. a red lotus-flower.<BR>—रक्त-मण्डल-ता, f.,<BR>Ved. the appearance of red spots on the body caused<BR>by a bad state of the blood.<BR>—रक्त-मत्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, drunk or satiated with blood (said of a leech).<BR>—रक्त-मत्स्य, अस्, m. a species of red fish.<BR>—रक्त-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of blood, full<BR>of blood, bloody.<BR>—रक्त-मस्तक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>red-headed; (अस्), m. a species of heron, Ardea<BR>Sibirica.<BR>—रक्त-माद्री, f. a particular disease pe-<BR>culiar to women.<BR>—रक्त-मुख, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्,<BR>red-faced, having a red mouth; (अस्), m., N. of an<BR>ape.<BR>—रक्त-मूत्र-ता, f. the voiding of blood with<BR>urine.<BR>—रक्त-मूलक, अस्, m. a kind of mustard.<BR>—रक्त-मूला, f. Mimosa Pudica.<BR>—रक्त-मेह,<BR>अस्, m. the voiding of blood with urine.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>मोक्ष, अस्, m. or रक्त-मोक्षण, अम्, n. blood-<BR>letting, bleeding, venesection, &c.<BR>—रक्त-यष्टि,<BR>इस्, or रक्त-यष्टिका, f. Rubia Munjista.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>यावनाल, अस्, m. = तुवर-यावनाल.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>राजि, इस्, m. a particular venomous insect; a peculiar<BR>disease of the eye.<BR>—रक्त-राजी, f. a particular<BR>venomous insect; cress, Lepidium Sativum.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>रेणु, उस्, m. vermilion; a bud of Butea Frondosa;<BR>Rottleria Tinctoria; a sort of cloth; an angry man.<BR>—रक्त-रेणुका, f. a bud of Butea Frondosa.<BR>—रक्त-रैवतक, अम्, n. a species of fruit tree<BR>(= महा-पारेवत).<BR>—रक्त-लशुन, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of garlic.<BR>—रक्त-लोचन, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्,<BR>red-eyed; (अस्), m. a pigeon.<BR>—रक्त-वटी or<BR>रक्त-वरटी, f. small-pox.<BR>—रक्त-वर्ग, अस्, m.<BR>lac; N. of various plants, the pomegranate tree;<BR>Butea Frondosa; Pentapetes Phœnicea; Rubia Mun-<BR>jista; two kinds of saffron; safflower.<BR>—रक्त-वर्-<BR>ण, अस्, m. red colour; the colour of blood; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), red-coloured; (अस्), m. the cochineal insect,<BR>= इन्द्र-गोप; (अम्), n. gold.<BR>—रक्त-वर्ध-<BR>न, अस्, ई, अम्, increasing or promoting the formation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0827-c" target="_blank">Page0827-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of blood; (अस्), m. Solanum Melongena.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>वर्षाभू, ऊस्, f. = रक्त-पुनर्नवा.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>वसन, अस्, आ, अम्, red-clad, clad in red garments,<BR>clothed in red; (अस्), m. a Brāhman in the fourth<BR>order or stage of life as a religious mendicant.<BR>—रक्त-वात, अस्, m. a particular disease.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>वालुक, अम्, आ, n. f. vermilion.<BR>—रक्त-वासस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, or रक्त-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing red gar-<BR>ments, clad in red.<BR>—रक्त-विकार, अस्, m. altera-<BR>tion or deterioration of blood.<BR>—रक्त-विद्रधि,<BR>इस्, m. a blood-red boil, a boil or ulcer filled with<BR>blood.<BR>—रक्त-विन्दु, उस्, m. a red spot forming a<BR>flaw in a jewel; a drop of blood.<BR>—रक्त-वीज, अस्,<BR>m. the pomegranate tree; N. of an Asura.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>वीजका, f. a species of plant (= तरदी).<BR>—रक्त-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m. a kind of tree.<BR>—रक्त-वृत्ता, f.<BR>Nyctanthes Arbor Tristis.<BR>—रक्त-शालि, इस्, m. red<BR>rice, Oryza Sativa.<BR>—रक्त-शासन, अम्, n. ver-<BR>milion.<BR>—रक्त-शिग्रु, उस्, m. red-flowering Śigru.<BR>—रक्त-शीर्षक, अस्, m. a kind of heron; Pinus<BR>Longifolia; the resin of Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>शुक्र-ता, f. bloody condition of the semen.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>शृङ्गिक, अम्, n. poison, venom.<BR>—रक्त-श्मश्रु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, having a red beard.<BR>—रक्त-श्मश्रु-<BR>शिरोरुह, अस्, आ, अम्, having a red beard and hair.<BR>—रक्त-श्याम, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-red.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>ष्ठीवन-ता or रक्त-ष्ठीवी, f. the spitting of<BR>blood.<BR>—रक्त-सङ्कोच, अस्, m. safflower.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>सङ्कोचक, अम्, n. a red lotus-flower.<BR>—रक्त-<BR>सञ्ज्ञ, अम्, n. saffron.<BR>—रक्त-सन्दंशिका, f. a<BR>blood-sucker, leech.<BR>—रक्त-सन्ध्यक, अम्, n.<BR>the flower of Nymphæa Rubra.<BR>—रक्त-सरोरुह,<BR>अम्, n. a red lotus-flower.<BR>—रक्त-सर्षप, अस्, m.<BR>Sinapis Ramosa.<BR>—रक्त-सहा, f. the red globe-<BR>amaranth.<BR>—रक्त-सार, अस्, आ, अम्, whose essence<BR>or predominating quality is blood, of a sanguinary<BR>disposition; (अस्), m. a species of plant, = अम्ल-<BR>वेतस, रक्त-खदिर; (अम्), n. red sandal;<BR>Cæsalpina Sappan.<BR>—रक्त-सूर्यमणि, इस्, m. a<BR>beautiful red-flowering shrub (Hibiscus Phœniceus).<BR>—रक्त-सूर्याय, Nom. A. -सूर्यायते, &c., to<BR>represent or be like a red sun.<BR>—रक्त-सौगन्-<BR>धिक, अम्, n. a red lotus-flower.<BR>—रक्त-स्रग्-<BR>अनुलेपिन्, ई, m. (probably) ‘wearing a red garland<BR>and being anointed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—रक्त-स्राव,<BR>अस्, m. a flow of blood, hemorrhage (Ved.); a kind<BR>of sour sorrel or dock.<BR>—रक्त-हंसा, f., N. of a<BR>Rāgiṇī.<BR>—रक्त-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, bloodless, cold-<BR>blooded.<BR>—रक्ताकार (˚त-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘having a<BR>red appearance,’ coral.<BR>—रक्ताक्त (˚त-आक्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dyed red; sprinkled or besmeared with blood;<BR>(अम्), n. red sandal or Cæsalpina Sappan.<BR>—रक्ता-<BR>क्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, red-eyed, having red or<BR>blood-shot eyes; fearful, dreadful, = क्रूर; (अस्), m.<BR>a buffalo; Perdix Rufa; a pigeon; the Indian crane;<BR>N. of a sorcerer; (अम्), n., N. of the fifty-eighth<BR>year in a Jupiter's cycle of sixty years.<BR>—रक्ताक्षि<BR>(˚त-अक्˚), इस्, or रक्ताक्षिन्, ई, m., N. of the fifty-<BR>eighth year in a Jupiter's cycle of sixty years.<BR>—रक्-<BR>ताङ्क (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, m. coral.<BR>—रक्ताङ्ग (˚त-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘red-bodied,’ a species of bird; a bug;<BR>a species of plant (= काम्पिल्ल, कम्पिल्ल); the<BR>planet Mars; the disk of the sun or moon; N. of a<BR>serpent-demon; (आ, ई), f. a species of plant, = जी-<BR>वन्ती; (ई), f. Rubia Munjista; coral; (अम्), n.<BR>coral; saffron; a species of plant (= कम्पिल्ल).<BR>—रक्तातिसार or रक्तातीसार (˚त-अत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘blood-diarrhœa,’ dysentery, bloody flux.<BR>—रक्ता-<BR>धरा (˚त-अध्˚), f. a Kinnarī.<BR>—रक्ताधार<BR>(˚त-आध्˚), अस्, m. ‘blood-receptacle,’ the skin.<BR>—रक्ताधिमन्थ (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, m. inflamma-<BR>tion of the eyes, ophthalmia with discharge of blood.<BR>—रक्तान्त (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having red ex-<BR>tremities, having the corners (of the eyes) inflamed.<BR>—रक्तापह (˚त-अप्˚), अम्, n. myrrh.<BR>—रक्ता-<BR>पामार्ग (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, m. red-flowering Apā-<BR>mārga.<BR>—रक्ताभ (˚त-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, red-<BR>looking, having a red appearance.<BR>—रक्ताभिष्-<BR>यन्द (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ophthalmia brought on by<BR>the state of the blood, redness of the vessels of the<BR>eye with a watery discharge.<BR>—रक्तामिषाद (˚त-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">Page0828-a+ 81</a>]<BR>आमिष-अद), अस्, आ, अम्, eating blood and flesh.<BR>—रक्ताम्बर (˚त-अम्˚), अम्, n. a red garment;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), wearing a red cloth, clad in red gar-<BR>ments; (अस्), m. any vagrant devotee wearing red<BR>garments; (आ), f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—रक्ताम्बर-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the wearing of red garments (with<BR>Buddhist monks).<BR>—रक्ताम्बर-धर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, wearing red garments.<BR>—रक्ताम्बु-पूर (˚त-<BR>अम्˚), अस्, m. a stream or flood of blood.<BR>—रक्-<BR>ताम्बु-रुह (˚त-अम्˚), अम्, n. a red lotus-flower.<BR>—रक्ताम्र (˚त-आम्˚), अस्, m. a species of plant<BR>(= कोशाम्र).<BR>—रक्तारुण (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>blood-red, red as blood.<BR>—रक्तार्बुद (˚त-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a bloody tumour.<BR>—रक्तार्मन् (˚त-अर्˚), अ, n.<BR>a particular disease of the eyes.<BR>—रक्तार्शस् (˚त-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, n. a form of hemorrhoids.<BR>—रक्तालु (˚त-आलु),<BR>उस्, or रक्तालुक, अस्, m. a species of red yam,<BR>Dioscorea Purpurea.<BR>—रक्ताशय (˚त-आश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘blood-receptacle,’ any viscus containing or secreting<BR>blood (as the heart, liver, spleen).<BR>—रक्ताशोक (˚त-<BR>अश्˚), अस्, m. red-flowering Aśoka.<BR>—रक्तेक्षु<BR>(˚त-इक्˚), उस्, m. red sugar-cane.<BR>—रक्तैरण्ड<BR>(˚त-एर्˚), अस्, m. the red Ricinus or castor-oil plant.<BR>—रक्तैर्वारु (˚त-एर्˚), उस्, m. a kind of cucum-<BR>ber (= इन्द्र-वारुणी).<BR>—रक्तोत्क्लिष्ट (˚त-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a particular disease of the eyes.<BR>—रक्तोत्पल<BR>(˚त-उत्˚), अस्, m. Bombax Heptaphyllum; (अम्), n.<BR>a red lotus, the flower of Nymphæa Rubra.<BR>—रक्-<BR>तोत्पलाभ (˚ल-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, being like the<BR>colour of Nymphæa Rubra, resembling the red lotus.<BR>—रक्तोपल (˚त-उप्˚), अम्, n. red chalk, red<BR>earth, red ochre or orpiment, indurated ochre or<BR>clay iron-stone.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0826-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तक|रक्तकः
रक्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, red; passionately attached<BR>to, fond of, enamoured; pleasing, entertaining,<BR>amusing; bloody, containing blood; (अस्), m. a red<BR>garment; an amorous or impassioned man; a sporter,<BR>player; N. of various plants bearing red flowers,<BR>Pentapetes Phœnicea; the globe-amaranth; = रक्त-<BR>शिग्रु; = रक्तैरण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तला
रक्तला, f. = काक-तुण्डी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ति|रक्तिः
रक्ति, इस्, f. pleasingness, attractiveness, charming-<BR>ness, loveliness; the being attached, affection, attach-<BR>ment, devotion, loyalty; = रक्तिका, the seed of Abrus<BR>Precatorius.<BR>—रक्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>charms, charming, lovely, attractive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तिका
रक्तिका, f. Abrus Precatorius; the seed or grain<BR>of this plant used as a weight = (1/6) or (1/7) or (2/15) of a<BR>Māṣaka; (according to some, the seed weighs about<BR>1(5/16) of a grain troy, the artificial Ratti or Raktikā<BR>should be double that weight, but in common use it<BR>averages nearly 2(1/4) grains.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तिमन्
रक्तिमन्, आ, m. redness, red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तृ
रक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who colours or dyes, a<BR>colourist, painter, (more correctly रङ्क्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्त्वा
रक्त्वा or रङ्क्त्वा, ind. having dyed; having<BR>attached one's self to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ग|रंग|रङ्गं|रंगः|रङ्गः
रङ्ग, अस्, m. colour, paint, pigment, dye, hue;<BR>the nasal modification or nasalizing of a vowel; a<BR>place of public amusement or for dramatic exhibi-<BR>tions, theatre, play-house, amphitheatre, stage, arena,<BR>place of public contest, place for athletic exercises or<BR>feats, sports, &c.; a place of assembly; an assembly or<BR>assemblage of spectators; a field of battle; dancing,<BR>singing, acting, diversion, mirth; borax; an extract<BR>obtained from Acacia Catechu; a proper N.; (अम्),<BR>n. tin (= वङ्ग; in this sense also अस्, m.).<BR>—रङ्ग-<BR>कार or रङ्ग-कारक, अस्, m. ‘a colour-maker,’<BR>painter, colourist.<BR>—रङ्ग-काष्ठ, अम्, n. Cæsal-<BR>pina Sappan.<BR>—रङ्ग-क्षेत्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—रङ्ग-चर, अस्, m. ‘a stage-goer,’ stage-<BR>player, actor, player, performer, &c.; a gladiator.<BR>—रङ्ग-ज, अम्, n. red lead, vermilion.<BR>—रङ्ग-<BR>जीवक, अस्, m. ‘living by colours,’ a painter, an<BR>actor, performer.<BR>—रङ्ग-द, अस्, m. borax; an<BR>extract from Acacia Catechu; a particular white<BR>paint (= स्फटी, दृढ-रङ्गा).<BR>—रङ्ग-दत्त,<BR>(probably) अम्, n., N. of a drama.<BR>—रङ्ग-दायक,<BR>अम्, n. a particular kind of earth (= कङ्कुष्ठ).<BR>—रङ्ग-दृढा, f. a sort of white paint (=<BR>दृढ-रङ्गा).<BR>—रङ्ग-देवता, f. a goddess sup-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-b" target="_blank">Page0828-b+ 81</a>]<BR>posed to preside over sports and diversions, the god-<BR>dess or genius of pleasure.<BR>—रङ्ग-द्वार्, र्, f. a stage-<BR>door, the door or entrance of a theatre.<BR>—रङ्ग-द्वार,<BR>अम्, n. a stage-entrance, stage-door; the prologue of<BR>a play.<BR>—रङ्ग-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of various men;<BR>of the author of a commentary on the Vikramorvaśī-<BR>(A.D. 1656); of a commentator on the Sūrya-<BR>siddhānta.<BR>—रङ्ग-पताका, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—रङ्ग-पत्त्री or रङ्ग-पुष्पी, f. the indigo<BR>plant.<BR>—रङ्ग-पीठ, अम्, n. a place for dancing.<BR>—रङ्ग-प्रवेश, अस्, m. entering on the stage,<BR>engaging in theatrical performances.<BR>—रङ्ग-भूति,<BR>इस्, f. the night of full moon in the month Āśvina.<BR>—रङ्ग-भूमि, इस्, f. a place for acting, stage,<BR>theatre, arena; a battle-field,<BR>—रङ्ग-मङ्गल,<BR>अम्, n. a stage-festival, rejoicing or festive ceremony<BR>on the stage.<BR>—रङ्ग-मण्डप, अस्, अम्, m. n. a<BR>play-house, theatre.<BR>—रङ्ग-मण्डल, अम्, n. the<BR>circuit of an arena or assembly.<BR>—रङ्ग-मध्य,<BR>अम्, n. the middle of an arena.<BR>—रङ्ग-मल्ल,<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.; (ई), f. the Indian lute.<BR>—रङ्ग-<BR>माणिक्य, अम्, n. a ruby (= माणिक्य).<BR>—रङ्ग-<BR>मातृ, ता, f. lac or the insect which forms the red<BR>dye; a bawd; = त्रुटि.<BR>—रङ्ग-मातृका, f. lac.<BR>—रङ्ग-राज, अस्, m., N. of a king; of a learned<BR>man, (also called Raṅgarāja-dīkṣita, &c.)<BR>—रङ्ग-<BR>लासिनी, f. Nyctanthes Arbor Tristis.<BR>—रङ्ग-वती,<BR>f., N. of a woman (who killed her husband Ranti-<BR>deva).<BR>—रङ्ग-वल्लिका or रङ्ग-वल्ली, f., N. of<BR>a kind of plant used at sacrifices.<BR>—रङ्ग-वस्तु, उ,<BR>n. any colouring substance, paint.<BR>—रङ्ग-वाट,<BR>a place or arena enclosed for contests, plays, dancing,<BR>&c.<BR>—रङ्ग-वाराङ्गना (˚र-अङ्˚), f. a kind of<BR>dancing girl.<BR>—रङ्ग-विद्या-धर, अस्, m. a pro-<BR>ficient in or teacher of the art of acting.<BR>—रङ्ग-<BR>वीज, अम्, n. silver.<BR>—रङ्ग-शाला, f. a play-house,<BR>theatre, dancing-hall, dancing-room.<BR>—रङ्ग-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, standing in an arena.<BR>—रङ्गाङ्गण<BR>(˚ग-अङ्˚), अम्, n. the area of an amphitheatre or<BR>arena, an arena or place of public contest.<BR>—रङ्-<BR>गाङ्गा (˚ग-अङ्˚), f. a particular white substance<BR>(= स्फटी).<BR>—रङ्गाजीव (˚ग-आज्˚), अस्, m. ‘living<BR>by colours,’ a painter; one who lives by the stage,<BR>an actor, performer.<BR>—रङ्गारि (˚ग-अरि), इस्, m. a<BR>fragrant Oleander.<BR>—रङ्गावतरण (˚ग-अव्˚),<BR>अम्, n. entering on the stage, engaging in theatrical<BR>performances; the profession of an actor.<BR>—रङ्गा-<BR>वतारक (˚ग-अव्˚), अस्, or रङ्गावतारिन्, ई, m.<BR>one who enters the stage or engages in theatrical<BR>performances, a stage-player, actor.<BR>—रङ्गेश (˚ग-<BR>ईश), अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रङ्गेश्वरी (˚ग-ईश्˚),<BR>f. (probably) N. of the wife of Raṅgeśa.<BR>—रङ्-<BR>गेष्ठालुक (˚ठ-आल्˚), अम्, n. a kind of bulbous<BR>root or onion, (also रङ्गेष्ठालु.)<BR>—रङ्गोप-<BR>जीविन् (˚ग-उप्˚), ई, or रङ्गोपजीव्य, अस्, m. one<BR>who lives by the stage, a stage-player, actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गण|रंगणं
रङ्गण, अम्, n. (probably) dancing, merry-<BR>making, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गिन्|रंगिन्
रङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, colouring, dyeing, painting;<BR>passionate, impassioned; attached to, devoted to,<BR>finding enjoyment in; acting or exhibiting on a<BR>stage, being an actor; (इणी), f. Asparagus Race-<BR>mosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज|रजं|रजः
रज, अस्, m. = रजस्, dust [cf. नी-र्˚]; the pollen<BR>of flowers; the menstrual excretion, (in this sense<BR>also अम्, n.); the quality of passion, (see रजस्);<BR>emotion, affection; N. of one of Skanda's attendants;<BR>of a king (a son of Vi-raja).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजक|रजकः
रजक, अस्, m. a washerman (so called from his<BR>being occupied in the cleaning or whitening of<BR>clothes; the washermen are regarded as a degraded<BR>caste of Hindūs); a parrot; N. of a king; (ई), f. a<BR>washerman's wife, washerwoman; epithet of a woman<BR>on the third day of the menses; (इका), f. a washer-<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजत|रजतं
रजत, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. rt. 2. अर्ज्], white, whitish,<BR>silver-coloured, silvery, (रजतं हिरण्यम्, white<BR>gold, i. e. silver); silver, made of silver, like silver;<BR>(अम्), n. silver [cf. अर्जुन]; gold; a pearl-ornament<BR>or necklace; blood; ivory; N. of a particular moun-<BR>tain (perhaps of Kailāsa); of a particular lake; an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">Page0828-c+ 81</a>]<BR>asterism, constellation; [cf. Gr. ἀργό-ς, ἀργ-ή-ς,<BR>ἄργυ-ρο-ς; Lat. arg-entu-m; Hib. airgiod.]<BR>—रजत-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a silver jar.<BR>—रजत-<BR>कूट, N. of a peak on the Malaya mountains.<BR>—रजत-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vajra-<BR>daṃṣṭra (a king of the Vidyā-dharas).<BR>—रजत-<BR>द्युति, इस्, m., N. of Hanumat.<BR>—रजत-नाभ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a particular fabulous being.<BR>—रजत-<BR>नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a white navel; (इस्), m., N.<BR>of a descendant of Kuvera.<BR>—रजत-पर्वत, अस्,<BR>m. a silver mountain; N. of a particular mountain.<BR>—रजत-पात्र or रजत-भाजन, अम्, n. a<BR>silver cup, silver vessel of any kind.<BR>—रजत-प्रस्-<BR>थ, अस्, m., N. of Kailāsa.<BR>—रजत-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, made of silver, silver.<BR>—रजत-वाह, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. his descendants.<BR>—रज-<BR>ताद्रि (˚त-अद्˚), इस्, m. ‘silver-mountain,’ N. of<BR>Kailāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजताकर
रजताकर, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजन|रजनं|रजनः
रजन, अस्, m., N. of a person with the patro-<BR>nymic Kauṇeya; a ray, beam; (अम्), n. colouring,<BR>dyeing; safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनक
रजनक, अस्, m. a proper N. (= रजन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनि|रजनिः
रजनि, इस्, or रजनी, f. (the latter is the more<BR>common; said to be fr. rt. रञ्ज् in the sense ‘to<BR>colour,’ cf. रजस्), night; N. of Durgā; a species<BR>of plant (= जनी, जतूका, जतु-कृत्); Curcuma<BR>Longa, (all words meaning ‘night’ appear to be<BR>used for this plant); Curcuma Aromatica; the indigo<BR>plant; N. of a river; [cf. Hib. reag, ‘night.’]<BR>—रजनि-कर, अस्, m. ‘the night-maker,’ the<BR>moon.<BR>—रजनि-चर, अस्, m. ‘night-rover,’ a Rāk-<BR>ṣasa; [cf. रजनी-चर.]<BR>—रजनिम्-मन्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, passing for or looking like night.<BR>—रजनि-<BR>राक्षसी, f. night regarded as a Rākṣasī.<BR>—रजनी-<BR>कर, अस्, m. ‘the night-maker,’ the moon.<BR>—र-<BR>जनी-गन्ध, अस्, m. Polianthes Tuberosa; (आ), f. a<BR>species of plant bearing white flowers.<BR>—रजनी-<BR>चर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, wandering in the night,<BR>moving about by night; (अस्), m. epithet of the<BR>moon; a Rākṣasa, an evil spirit; a night-watcher;<BR>a thief.<BR>—रजनीचर-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord or pro-<BR>tector of night-wanderers,’ epithet of the moon,<BR>(wrongly read रजनी-चय-नाथ.) — रजनी-जल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘night-dew,’ rime, hoar-frost.<BR>—रजनी-द्वन्-<BR>द्व, अम्, n. a period of two nights with the inter-<BR>mediate day.<BR>—रजनी-पति, इस्, m. ‘the lord or hus-<BR>band of night,’ the moon.<BR>—रजनी-मुख, अम्, n.<BR>‘front or beginning of night,’ evening, nightfall.<BR>—रजनी-रमण, अस्, m. ‘the husband of night,’<BR>the moon.<BR>—रजनी-हासा, f. Nyctanthes Arbor<BR>Tristis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीय
रजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be enjoyed, enjoyable,<BR>charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजयित्री
रजयित्री, f. (fr. the Caus.), Ved. a female painter<BR>or colourist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्
रजस्, अस्, n. (said to be fr. rt. रञ्ज् in the sense<BR>‘to colour,’ cf. rt. 2. अर्ज्; according to some the<BR>original meaning may have been ‘dimness,’ cf. र-<BR>जनि and Goth. riquis), the sphere of vapour or<BR>mist, region of clouds, atmosphere, air, firmament<BR>(Ved.; sometimes represented as the expanse of<BR>heaven or sky in general); any sphere or world or<BR>division of the world (so used in Ved. according to<BR>Yāska and Sāy.; the dual रजसी = ‘heaven and earth,’<BR>or perhaps ‘the lower and higher atmospheres’ im-<BR>mediately above the earth; त्रीणि रजांसि = ‘the<BR>three worlds’ or earth, atmosphere, and sky; some-<BR>times even six such spheres are enumerated); vapour,<BR>mist, clouds, rain-water, water (according to Nirukta<BR>IV. 19); gloom, gloominess, dimness, darkness; im-<BR>purity, dirt, dust, powder, speck of dust, any small<BR>particle of matter, (गो-रजस्, a speck of dust on a<BR>cow's hair; a mote in a sun-beam; एडक-रजस्,<BR>a speck of dust on a sheep's fleece); the dust or<BR>pollen of flowers; cultivated or ploughed land (as<BR>‘dusty’), arable land, fields; the ‘darkening’ quality,<BR>passion, foulness, impurity; (in philosophy) the<BR>second of the three Guṇas or qualities, (the three are<BR>called सत्त्व, goodness, रजस्, passion, and तमस्,<BR>darkness; cf. गुण; of these रजस् is sometimes<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">Page0829-a+ 81</a>]<BR>identified with तेजस्, energy or activity: it is said to<BR>predominate in air, and to be active, urgent, and<BR>variable); passion, emotion, feeling, affection; the<BR>menstrual excretion; tin; (according to Nirukta IV.<BR>19) = ज्योतिस्, अहन्; (आस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi, son of<BR>Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—रज-उद्वास, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one<BR>who has put off soiled clothes; [cf. मलोद्वासस्.]<BR>—रजः-पटल, अम्, n. a coating of dust.<BR>—र-<BR>जः-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of passion (a term<BR>applied to a person when the object is to mark<BR>his being of no particular note; cf. रजस्-तोक).<BR>—रजः-प्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, filled with (the quality<BR>of) passion.<BR>—रजः-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. silver,<BR>made of silver.<BR>—रजः-शुद्धि, इस्, f. a pure or<BR>right condition of the menses.<BR>—रजः-स्पृश्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, touching the dust or the ground, touching the<BR>earth.<BR>—रजस्-तमस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, being under<BR>the influence of the two qualities रजस् and त-<BR>मस्, (see above.)<BR>—रजस्-तमो-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made up or consisting of the qualities रजस् and<BR>तमस्.<BR>—रजस्-तुर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, Ved. hastening<BR>through the sky or atmosphere, (Sāy.) dust-scattering<BR>(= पांसोस् त्वरयितृ) or water-scattering (= उद-<BR>कस्य प्रेरक).<BR>—रजस्-तोक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>child or offspring of passion; avarice, greediness.<BR>—रजस्-वल, अस्, आ, अम्, having water (Ved. =<BR>उदक-वत्); covered with dust, dusty; full of the<BR>quality रजस्, full of passion; (अस्), m. a buffalo;<BR>(आ), f. a menstruating woman, a female during the<BR>menses; a marriageable woman.<BR>—रजस्-विन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, dusty, full of dust or pollen; full of the<BR>quality रजस्.<BR>—रजी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to<BR>change or turn into dust.<BR>—रजेषित (fr. रज for<BR>रजस् + इषित), according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>46, 28. रजस् = उष्ट्र or गर्दभ, इषित =<BR>प्रापित.<BR>—रजो-गात्र, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—रजो-गुण, अस्, m. the quality रजस्<BR>or passion, (see under रजस्.)<BR>—रजोगुण-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of or having the quality रजस्.<BR>—रजो-ग्रहि, इस्, इस्, इ, see Vopa-deva XXVI. 48.<BR>—रजो-दर्शन, अम्, n. the (first) appearance of<BR>the menstrual excretion.<BR>—रजो-निमीलित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, blinded by passion or desire.<BR>—रजो-बन्ध,<BR>अस्, m. suppression of menstruation.<BR>—रजो-बल,<BR>अम्, n. darkness, (perhaps more correctly रजो-वल.)<BR>—रजो-मेघ, अस्, m. a cloud of dust.<BR>—रजो-रस,<BR>अस्, m. darkness.<BR>—रजो-हर, अस्, m. ‘remover of<BR>impurity,’ a washerman.<BR>—रजो-हरण-धारिन्<BR>(according to Halāyudha II. 189) = व्रतिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0828-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस
रजस (at the end of an adj. comp.) = रजस्<BR>(e. g. अ-प्राप्त-रजसा, not yet having menstruated);<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), obscure, dark, dim, Ved.; (perhaps)<BR>dirty, unclean, impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजसानु|रजसानुः
रजसानु, उस्, m. a cloud; soul, heart (= चित्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्क
रजस्क (at the end of an adj. comp.) = रजस्<BR>in नी-र्˚, वि-र्˚, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्य
1. रजस्य, Nom. P. रजस्यति, &c., to become<BR>dust, to be scattered as dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्य
2. रजस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the quality<BR>रजस्; dusty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजित
रजित, अस्, आ, अम् (for रञ्जित), affected, moved, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्ज
रञ्ज in जल-रञ्ज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जक|रंजक|रञ्जकं|रञ्जकः
रञ्जक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.), = रञ्जन,<BR>colouring, dyeing; causing affection or passion, ex-<BR>citing love or pleasure, gladdening, rejoicing, pleas-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. a colourist, dyer, painter; an inciter<BR>of affection &c., stimulus; a species of plant (=<BR>कम्पिल्लक); biliary humor on which vision de-<BR>pends; (अकी), f. a female colourer or dyer; (अम्),<BR>n. red sandal; vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जन|रंजन|रञ्जनं|रञ्जनः
रञ्जन, अस्, ई, अम्, colouring, dyeing, (केश-<BR>रञ्जन, dyeing the hair); exciting passion or love;<BR>gratifying, exhilarating, delighting, rejoicing, (जन-<BR>रञ्जनी, ‘men-rejoicing,’ N. of a particular formula);<BR>conciliating, befriending; (अस्), m. Saccharum Munja,<BR>= मुञ्ज; (ई), f. the female personification of a<BR>particular musical mode; (probably) friendly saluta-<BR>tion; N. of various plants, the indigo plant; Nyc-<BR>tanthes Arbor Tristis; saffron; a kind of fragrant<BR>perfume; (अम्), n. the act of colouring, dyeing;<BR>colour, dye; the act of pleasing, delighting, concili-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">Page0829-b+ 78</a>]<BR>ating, rejoicing, giving pleasure; nasalizing (in<BR>gram.); red sandal-wood.<BR>—रञ्जन-द्रु, उस्, m. a<BR>kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जनक|रञ्जनकः
रञ्जनक, अस्, m. a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जनीय
रञ्जनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be coloured or dyed;<BR>to be rejoiced or pleased; anything which may be<BR>rejoiced at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जित|रंजित
रञ्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, dyed, coloured, tinted; affected,<BR>moved; highly delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जिनी
रञ्जिनी, f., N. of various plants, the indigo plant;<BR>Rubia Munjista; [cf. रञ्जनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रट्
रट् रट्, cl. 1. P. रटति, रराट, &c., to<BR>shout, howl, yell, cry, scream, roar, bellow;<BR>to call out, proclaim aloud; to shout with joy,<BR>applaud: Caus. रटयति, &c., to shout, &c.; to<BR>speak [cf. rt. रठ्]: Intens. रारटीति, to scream<BR>aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटन|रटनं
रटन, अम्, n. the act of shouting, &c.; cry or<BR>shout of applause, approbation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटन्ती|रटंती
रटन्ती, f., N. of the fourteenth day in the dark<BR>half of the month Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटित|रटितं
रटित, अस्, आ, अम्, screamed, shouted, &c.; (अम्),<BR>n. a roar, yell, scream, cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रट्टा
रट्टा रट्टा, f., N. of a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रठ्
रठ् रठ् [cf. rt. रट्], cl. 1. P. रठति,<BR>&c., to speak; [cf. Old Germ. rediôn, re-<BR>dinôn; Old Sax. rethjôn, rethinôn, ‘to speak;’<BR>perhaps Goth. rasda.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रड्ड
रड्ड रड्ड, अस्, m. a proper N.; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्
रण् रण् (thought by some to be deve-<BR>loped out of a base रम्णा, fr. rt. रम्),<BR>cl. 1. P. (Ved. also cl. 4. P.) रणति (रण्यति),<BR>रराण, अराणीत् (Ved. forms रारण or in Pada-<BR>pāṭha ररण, रणिष्टन्), रणितुम्, to rejoice,<BR>exult; to take pleasure in (with loc., rarely with acc.,<BR>Ved.); to delight (Ved.); to sound, ring, rattle,<BR>jingle; to shout: Caus. P. A. रणयति, रणयते,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अरीरणत् or अरराणत् (Ved. forms<BR>रारणत्, अरारणुस्, रारन्धि, रारन्तु, ररा-<BR>णत), to cause to rejoice; cause to be pleased,<BR>delight; to rejoice or be pleased at, delight in (with<BR>loc., Ved.); to make to sound, cause to sound forth;<BR>to praise; to go (P.): Desid. रिरणिषति: Intens.<BR>रंरण्यते, रंरण्टि; [cf. Hib. ran, ‘a squeal,<BR>roar;’ ranach, ‘a roaring.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण|रणं|रणः
रण, अस्, m. joy, delight, gratification, pleasure<BR>(Ved.); sound, noise; the quill or bow of a lute;<BR>going, motion; (अस्, अम्), m. n. battle, war, combat,<BR>fight, conflict.<BR>—रण-कर्मन्, अ, n. ‘war-busi-<BR>ness,’ war, battle, combat, fighting.<BR>—रण-कामिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, desirous of war, wishing to fight.<BR>—रण-<BR>काम्य, Nom. P. -काम्यति, &c., to wish for battle.<BR>—रण-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. causing battle or<BR>strife.<BR>—रण-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing joy, gratifying,<BR>delighting (Ved.); fighting, a fighter, combatant,<BR>warrior.<BR>—रण-क्षित्ति, इस्, f. or रण-क्षेत्र, अम्,<BR>n. or रण-क्षोणि, इस्, f. place of battle, battle-field.<BR>—रण-गोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, engaged in war, fight-<BR>ing.<BR>—रण-जय, अस्, m. victory in battle.<BR>—र-<BR>णञ्-जय, अस्, m. (रणम्, acc. c.), N. of a king.<BR>—रण-तूर्य, अम्, n. a war-drum, military drum.<BR>—रण-दर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रण-दुन्-<BR>दुभि, इस्, m. a military drum.<BR>—रण-दुर्गाधा-<BR>रण-यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a particular amulet.<BR>—रण-पण्डित, अस्, m. ‘skilled in battle,’ a<BR>warrior.<BR>—रण-पुर-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>certain statue of Sūrya.<BR>—रण-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>battle-loving, fond of war or battle, warlike; (अस्),<BR>m. a falcon; (अम्), n. the fragrant root of Andro-<BR>pogon Muricatus.<BR>—रण-भट, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—रण-भू, ऊस्, or रण-भूमि, इस्, f. a battle-<BR>ground, field of battle.<BR>—रण-मत्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>furious in battle; (अस्), m. an elephant.<BR>—रण-<BR>मार्ग-कोविद, अस्, आ, अम्, experienced in the art<BR>or ways of war.<BR>—रण-मुख, अम्, n. the front<BR>or van of battle; the van of an army.<BR>—रण-<BR>मुष्टि, इस्, m. a species of plant (= विष-मुष्टि).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">Page0829-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—रण-मूर्धन्, आ, m. the front or van of a<BR>fight.<BR>—रण-रङ्क, अस्, m. the space between the<BR>tusks of an elephant.<BR>—रण-रङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘battle-<BR>stage,’ a place or field of battle.<BR>—रणरङ्ग-<BR>मल्ल, अस्, m. = भोज-राज, q. v.<BR>—रण-रण,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the buzzer,’ a gnat, musquito; (अम्), n. a<BR>longing, anxious desire; regret (for a lost object).<BR>—रण-रणक, अस्, अम्, m. n. anxiety, anxious<BR>regret for some beloved object; desire, love; (अस्),<BR>m. the god of love.<BR>—रण-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. the<BR>fortune of war; the goddess of battle.<BR>—रण-<BR>वन्य, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रण-वाद्य, अम्,<BR>n. a military instrument of music, martial music.<BR>—रण-विशारद, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in war.<BR>—रण-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, having war or battle for a<BR>profession.<BR>—रण-शिक्षा, f. the art or science of<BR>war.<BR>—रण-शिरस्, अस्, n. the head or front of a<BR>battle.<BR>—रण-शूर, अस्, m. a hero in war, warrior.<BR>—रण-संरम्भ, अस्, m. the fury of battle.<BR>—रण-सङ्कुल, अम्, n. the confusion or noise of<BR>battle, a melée, mixed or tumultuary combat.<BR>—र-<BR>ण-सज्जा, f. military accoutrement.<BR>—रण-सत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. war or battle regarded as a sacrifice.<BR>—रण-<BR>सहाय, अस्, m. ‘war-helper,’ an ally.<BR>—रण-स्तम्-<BR>भ, अस्, m. ‘battle-pillar,’ a monument of war or<BR>battle, trophy, column; N. of a country (Chitore?).<BR>—रण-स्थान, अम्, n. a battle-place, field of<BR>battle.<BR>—रण-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a statue of<BR>Śiva as lord of battle.<BR>—रणाग्नि (˚ण-अग्˚), इस्, m.<BR>the fire of battle, battle regarded as fire.<BR>—रणाग्र<BR>(˚ण-अग्˚), अम्, n. the head or front of a battle.<BR>—रणाङ्ग (˚ण-अङ्˚), अम्, n. ‘war-implement,’<BR>weapon of war or battle, any weapon, a sword.<BR>—रणाङ्गन (˚ण-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a battle-place,<BR>field of battle, (also रणाङ्गण.)<BR>—रणाजि (˚ण-<BR>आजि), इस्, m., N. of a Sādhya.<BR>—रणाजिर (˚ण-अज्˚),<BR>अम्, n. area or arena for fighting, battle-field.<BR>—र-<BR>णातोद्य (˚ण-आत्˚), अम्, n. a battle-drum, military<BR>drum.<BR>—रणादित्य (˚ण-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king<BR>of Kaśmīra; of another person.<BR>—रणान्त-कृत्<BR>(˚ण-अन्˚), त्, m. ‘making an end of battle,’ N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—रणापेत (˚ण-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, flying<BR>away from battle (Kirāt. XV. 33).<BR>—रणाभियोग<BR>(˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्, m. engaging in battle, warlike en-<BR>counter.<BR>—रणारम्भा (˚ण-आर्˚), f., N. of the<BR>wife of Raṇāditya.<BR>—रणारम्भा-स्वामि-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a statue erected by Raṇārambhā.<BR>—र-<BR>णालङ्करण (˚ण-अल्˚), अस्, m. a heron (= कङ्क).<BR>—रणावनि (˚ण-अव्˚), इस्, f. battle-ground, a field<BR>of battle.<BR>—रणाश्व (˚ण-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—रणे-चर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, going or mov-<BR>ing about in the field of battle (said of Viṣṇu).<BR>—रणेश (˚ण-ईश) or रणेश्वर (˚ण-ईश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. = रण-स्वामिन्.<BR>—रणे-स्वच्छ, अस्, m. a cock.<BR>—रणैषिन् (˚ण-एस्˚), ई, इणी, इ, eager for battle.<BR>—रणोत्कट (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, furious or mad<BR>in battle; (अस्), m., N. of one of Skanda's attendants;<BR>of a Daitya.<BR>—रणोत्साह (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, m. prowess<BR>in battle.<BR>—रणोद्दाम (˚ण-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>eager for battle.<BR>—रणोद्देश (˚ण-उद्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>field of battle; a part or quarter of a battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणक
रणक, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणत्
रणत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sounding, rattling; going.<BR>—रणत्-कार, अस्, m. a rattling or clanking sound;<BR>any sound; humming (of bees).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणित|रणितं
रणित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, sounding, rattling;<BR>(अम्), n. sound, any ringing or rattling sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणितृ
रणितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. rejoicing in, delighting<BR>in, (Sāy. = रमण-शील.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्य
रण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. agreeable, enjoyable,<BR>delightful, pleasant; fit for fighting, warlike; (अम्),<BR>n., Ved. joy, pleasure; war, battle.<BR>—रण्य-जित्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, Ved. conquering in battle, victorious in war.<BR>—रण्य-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. speaking agreeably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्व
रण्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pleasant, delightful, agree-<BR>able, lovely; joyous, gay; sounding; to be praised,<BR>worthy of praise.<BR>—रण्व-सन्दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>looking lovely, appearing beautiful, (Sāy. = रम-<BR>णीय-दर्शन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्वन्
रण्वन्, in Ṛg-veda V. 44, 10, according to Sāy.<BR>= रमणीय, agreeable, pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0829-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्ड|रंड|रण्डः
रण्ड रण्ड, अस्, आ, अम् (in Uṇādi-s. I. 113.<BR>said to be fr. rt. रम्), mutilated, maimed, crippled,<BR>(incorrect for वण्ड, q. v.); faithless (in शाखा-<BR>रण्ड, q. v.); (अस्), m. a man who dies without<BR>male issue; a barren tree; (आ), f. a term of abuse<BR>in addressing women, a slut; a widow, (बाल-रण्डा,<BR>a young widow); Salvinia Cucullata; N. of a species<BR>of metre.<BR>—रण्डाश्रमिन् (˚ड-आश्˚), ई, m. one who<BR>loses a wife after the forty-eighth year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्डक|रंडकः|रण्डकः
रण्डक, अस्, m. a barren tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्य
रण्य रण्य, रण्व, &c. See p. 829, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्व्
रण्व् रण्व् (= rts. रम्ब्, रिण्व्, रिम्ब्), cl.<BR>1. P. रण्वति, to go; (a form रण्व् for<BR>rt. रण् occurs in Taittrīya-s. I. 2, 5, 1, where, accord-<BR>ing to the commentator, रण्वतु = रमयतु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्वित
रण्वित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. रण्व् for rt. रण्), in<BR>Ṛg-veda II. 3, 6. according to Sāy. = शब्दित,<BR>स्तुत, sounded, praised, or गच्छत्, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत|रतं
रत रत, रति, &c. See p. 833, cols. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतान्ध्री
रतान्ध्री रतान्ध्री, f. a fog, mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रताम्बुक
रताम्बुक रताम्बुक, ए, n. du. the two<BR>cavities immediately above the hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतू
रतू रतू, ऊस्, f. (said to be fr. a Sautra rt.<BR>ऋत्), the river of heaven, the celestial Ganges; a<BR>true speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्न|रत्नं
रत्न रत्न, अम्, n. (rarely अस्, m.; according<BR>to Uṇādi-s. III. 14. fr. rt. रम्), a gift, present<BR>(Ved., in this sense perhaps connected with rt. 1. रा);<BR>property, goods, riches, possessions (Ved.); a jewel,<BR>gem, treasure, precious stone, pearl; anything valu-<BR>able or desirable, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 41,<BR>6, &c. रत्नम् = रमणीयम्); any precious thing,<BR>anything excellent or best of its kind (e. g. पुत्र-<BR>रत्न, an excellent son; गो-रत्नानि, excellent<BR>cows; cf. पुं-र्˚, स्त्री-र्˚); a magnet, loadstone<BR>[cf. मणि]; = रत्न-हविस् (Ved.); (अस्), m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रत्न-कन्दल, अस्, m. coral.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>कर, अस्, m., N. of Kuvera.<BR>—रत्न-करण्डक,<BR>N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—रत्न-कलश, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रत्न-कला, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—रत्न-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>कूट, अस्, m., N. of a mountain; of a Bodhi-sattva;<BR>of an island.<BR>—रत्नकूट-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Buddhist Sūtra work.<BR>—रत्न-केतु, उस्, m., N. of<BR>a Buddha; of a Bodhi-sattva; (said to be a name<BR>common to 2000 future Buddhas.)<BR>—रत्न-कोटि,<BR>N. of a Samādhi.<BR>—रत्न-कोश or रत्न-कोष,<BR>अस्, m. ‘repository of jewels,’ N. of various works.<BR>—रत्न-क्षेत्र-कूट-सन्दर्शन, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Bodhi-sattva, (also written रत्न-च्छत्त्र-कूट-<BR>सन्दर्शन.)<BR>—रत्न-खचित, अस्, आ, अम्, set or<BR>studded with gems.<BR>—रत्न-खानि, इस्, f. a jewel-<BR>mine, mine for precious stones.<BR>—रत्न-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, holding precious stones, filled with jewels,<BR>containing jewels; (अस्), m. the sea; N. of Kuvera;<BR>of a Bodhi-sattva; of a commentator on the Viṣṇu-<BR>Purāṇa; (आ), f. the earth.<BR>—रत्न-ग्रीव-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—रत्न-चन्-<BR>द्र, अस्, m., N. of a god (said to be the guardian<BR>deity of a jewel-mine); of a Bodhi-sattva; of a son<BR>of Vimbisāra.<BR>—रत्न-चन्द्रामति, इस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—रत्न-चूड, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva; of<BR>a mythical king.<BR>—रत्न-चूडा-परिपृच्छा, f., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—रत्न-च्छत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘jewel-um-<BR>brella,’ an umbrella (adorned) with precious stones.<BR>—रत्नच्छत्त्र-कूट-सन्दर्शन, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—रत्नच्छत्त्राभ्युद्गताव-<BR>भास (˚र-अभ्˚, ˚त-अव्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—रत्न-तेजो-ऽभ्युद्गत-राज, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Buddha.<BR>—रत्न-त्रय, अम्, n. (with Jainas)<BR>‘jewel-triad,’ three jewels or excellent things (viz.<BR>सम्यग्-दर्शन, सम्यग्-ज्ञान, and सम्यक्-<BR>चारित्र).<BR>—रत्नत्रय-परीक्षा, f., N. of a<BR>treatise on the Vedānta by Apya-dīkṣita.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m., N. of various persons.<BR>—रत्न-दर्-<BR>पण, अस्, m. ‘jewel-mirror,’ a looking-glass (orna-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-b" target="_blank">Page0830-b+ 81</a>]<BR>mented) with jewels; N. of a commentary on the<BR>Sarasvatī-kaṇṭhābharaṇa.<BR>—रत्न-दीप, अस्, m.<BR>‘jewel-lamp,’ a lamp in which jewels give out light,<BR>a gem serving as a light, (such gems are fabled to<BR>be in Pātāla.)<BR>—रत्न-दीपिका, f., N. of a work.<BR>—रत्न-द्रुम, (probably) coral; [cf. रत्न-<BR>वृक्ष.]<BR>—रत्नद्रुम-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made<BR>or composed of coral, resembling coral.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>द्वीप, ‘jewel-island, pearl-island,’ N. of a particular<BR>island.<BR>—रत्न-धर, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Jagad-dhara.<BR>—रत्न-धा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. getting<BR>or possessing wealth, possessed of riches or precious<BR>things, (रत्नधा-तम, superl. possessing great<BR>riches.)<BR>—रत्न-धेनु, उस्, f. an offering of jewels<BR>(properly in the shape of a cow, see धेनु).<BR>—रत्-<BR>न-धेय, अम्, n., Ved. the giving away or distri-<BR>bution of wealth, (according to Sāy. also = दातव्यं<BR>रत्नम्, treasure that ought to be given, and र-<BR>मणीय-धनस्य दातृ, giver of precious wealth.)<BR>—रत्न-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—रत्न-नदी, f. ‘jewel-river,’ N. of a river.<BR>—रत्न-नाभ, अस्, m. ‘having a jewel on the<BR>navel,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—रत्न-निचय, अस्, m. a<BR>heap or collection of jewels, &c.<BR>—रत्न-निधि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘receptacle of pearls, mine of jewels,’ epithet of<BR>the sea; of Meru; N. of Viṣṇu; a wagtail (in<BR>this sense probably for रत-निधि).<BR>—रत्न-प-<BR>रीक्षा, f. ‘jewel-testing,’ N. of a work.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>पर्वत, अस्, m. ‘jewel-mountain,’ a mountain con-<BR>taining jewels; N. of Meru.<BR>—रत्न-पाणि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva; of a grammarian.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>पाल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रत्न-पुर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—रत्न-प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>dictionary.<BR>—रत्न-प्रदीप, अस्, m. = रत्न-दीप.<BR>—रत्न-प्रभ, अस्, m., N. of a particular class of<BR>deities; of a king; (आ), f. epithet of the earth; N.<BR>of a hell (with Jainas); of various women; of a<BR>Nāgī; of the seventh Lambaka of the Kathā-sarit-<BR>sāgara.<BR>—रत्न-बाहु, उस्, m. ‘jewel-armed,’ N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—रत्न-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, distributing gifts or<BR>wealth (Ved.); acquiring or possessing jewels, pos-<BR>sessing treasures.<BR>—रत्न-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>a gem or jewel.<BR>—रत्न-मञ्जरी, f., N.of a Vidyā-<BR>dharī; of a woman in the Hitopadeśa.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>मति, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रत्न-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made or consisting of jewels, abundantly studded<BR>with precious stones.<BR>—रत्न-माला, f. a jewel<BR>necklace, pearl necklace, &c.; N. of various works;<BR>of a lexicon; of a Dharma-śāstra; of a work by<BR>Śrī-pati (= ज्योतिष-र्˚); = न्याय-रत्नमाला.<BR>—रत्नमाला-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a necklace<BR>of jewels or pearls; (अती), f., N. of one of Rādhā's<BR>female attendants.<BR>—रत्नमालिका, f. (diminutive<BR>fr. रत्न-माला), a little jewel necklace.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, adorned with a necklace of jewels.<BR>—रत्न-मुकुट, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—रत्न-मुख्य, अम्, n. ‘chief of jewels,’ a<BR>diamond.<BR>—रत्न-मुद्रा, f., N. of a Samādhi.<BR>—रत्न-मुद्रा-हस्त, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—रत्न-मेघ-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist<BR>Sūtra work.<BR>—रत्न-यष्टि, इस्, m., N. of a Bud-<BR>dha.<BR>—रत्न-युग्म-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—रत्न-रक्षित, अस्, m., N. of one of the two<BR>translators of the Karaṇḍa-vyūha into Tibetan.<BR>—रत्-<BR>न-राज्, ट्, m. ‘jewel-king,’ a ruby.<BR>—रत्न-राजि,<BR>इस्, f. a string of pearls.<BR>—रत्न-राशि, इस्, m. a heap<BR>of precious stones, collection of jewels; the sea,<BR>ocean.<BR>—रत्न-रेखा, f., N. of a princess.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>लिङ्गेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्, m. (with Buddhists)<BR>Svayam-bhū in his visible form.<BR>—रत्न-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, accompanied with gifts (Ved.); possessing<BR>wealth or treasure, abounding in precious stones,<BR>decorated with jewels; (आन्), m., N. of a mountain;<BR>(अती), f. the earth; N. of various women.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>वर्धन, अस्, m., N. of a person (who erected a<BR>statue of Śiva called after him रत्नवर्धनेश).<BR>—रत्न-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a merchant.<BR>—रत्-<BR>न-वर्ष, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Yakṣas.<BR>—रत्न-वर्षुक, अम्, n., N. of the mythical<BR>car Puṣpaka (supposed to rain or pour forth jewels;<BR>see पुष्पक).<BR>—रत्न-विशुद्ध, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-c" target="_blank">Page0830-c+ 79</a>]<BR>world.<BR>—रत्न-वृक्ष, (probably) coral.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>शलाका, f. a sprout or sprig of jewels<BR>—रत्न-शास्त्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work by Agastya.<BR>—रत्न-शिखर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—रत्न-शिखिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a Buddha.<BR>—रत्न-शेखर, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of the Guṇa-sthāna-prakaraṇa.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>षष्ठी, f. the sixth day of a particular fortnight.<BR>—रत्न-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a work on law.<BR>—रत्न-सङ्घात, अस्, m. a number or collection<BR>of jewels.<BR>—रत्नसङ्घात-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made or consisting of a number of jewels.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>समुद्गल, N. of a Samādhi.<BR>—रत्न-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Dhyāni-buddha; of a Buddha; of a<BR>Bodhi-sattva; of the place where the Buddha Śaśi-<BR>ketu is to appear.<BR>—रत्न-सागर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—रत्न-सानु, उस्, m., N. of the mountain<BR>Meru.<BR>—रत्न-सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, producing jewels;<BR>(ऊस्), f. the earth.<BR>—रत्न-सूति, इस्, f. the earth.<BR>—रत्न-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रत्न-स्व-<BR>मिन्, N. of a temple founded by Ratna.<BR>—रत्न-<BR>हविस्, इस्, n., Ved. N. of a particular oblation in<BR>the Rāja-sūya having reference to whatever may be<BR>reckoned among a king's most valuable treasures.<BR>—रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m. a jewel-mine; the<BR>sea, ocean; N. of a Buddha; of a Bodhi-sattva; of<BR>a poet; of the author of the Vrata-kalpa-druma; of<BR>various other persons; of a horse descended from<BR>Uccaiḥ-śravas; of various works; of a Dharma-<BR>śāstra; of a work on music; of a work on rhetoric;<BR>of a town, (in this sense probably अम्, n.)<BR>—रत्ना-<BR>कर-निघण्ट, अस्, m., N. of a dictionary.<BR>—रत्-<BR>नाङ्क (˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu's car.<BR>—रत्नाङ्गुरीयक (˚न-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a finger-<BR>ring (set) with precious stones, (also written रत्-<BR>नाङ्गुलीयक.)<BR>—रत्नाढ्य (˚न-आढ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, abounding in jewels.<BR>—रत्ना-देवी, f., N. of<BR>a princess.<BR>—रत्नाद्रि (˚न-अद्˚), इस्, m., N. of a<BR>mythical mountain.<BR>—रत्नाधिपति (˚न-अध्˚),<BR>इस्, m. a superintendent of treasures or valuables; N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—रत्ना-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—रत्नाभरण (˚न-आभ्˚), अम्, n. an ornament<BR>made of jewels.<BR>—रत्नार्चिस् (˚न-अर्˚), इस्, m., N.<BR>of a Buddha.<BR>—रत्नालोक (˚न-आल्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>lustre or brilliance of a gem.<BR>—रत्ना-वती, f., N.<BR>of a town.<BR>—रत्नावभास (˚न-अव्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Kalpa.<BR>—रत्नावली (˚न-आव्˚), f. a string of<BR>pearls, row of jewels, pearl necklace; N. of a parti-<BR>cular rhetorical figure; of various women; of a cele-<BR>brated comedy by Harṣa-deva; of a Tantra work;<BR>of various other works.<BR>—रत्नावली-निबन्ध, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a work.<BR>—रत्नासन (˚न-आस्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a throne ornamented with jewels.<BR>—रत्नेन्द्र (˚न-<BR>इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘jewel-chief,’ a very precious jewel.<BR>—रत्नेश्वर (˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of various<BR>persons; (अम्), n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—रत्नोत्तमा<BR>(˚न-उत्˚), f., N. of a Tantra deity.<BR>—रत्नोद्भव<BR>(˚न-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist saint.<BR>—रत्-<BR>नोल्का (˚न-उल्˚), f., N. of a Tantra deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नक
रत्नक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्निन्
रत्निन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having gifts, receiving<BR>presents or offerings, possessing treasures, having<BR>precious things, (Sāy. = रमणीय-धन-वत् or<BR>रमणीय-फल-वत्, having valuable riches or<BR>rewards); epithet of certain persons in whose dwell-<BR>ing the Ratna-havis (q. v.) is offered by a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नि|रत्निः
रत्नि रत्नि, इस्, m. f. (a corrupted form of<BR>अरत्नि), the elbow; a measure of length (= the dis-<BR>tance from the elbow to the end of the closed fist, a<BR>cubit); (इस्), m. the closed fist.<BR>—रत्नि-पृष्ठक,<BR>अम्, n. the elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्यङ्ग|रत्यंग|रत्यङ्गं
रत्यङ्ग रत्य्-अङ्ग. See under रति, p. 833.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ|रथः
रथ रथ, अस्, m. (according to some fr.<BR>rt. 4. ऋ, according to Uṇādi-s. II. 2. fr. rt. रम्,<BR>according to Nirukta IX. 11. fr. rt. रंह्), a two-<BR>wheeled vehicle, carriage, car, chariot, war-chariot;<BR>a vehicle or equipage in general, (applied also to the<BR>vehicles of the gods; in Ved. applied sometimes to<BR>the driver as well as the vehicle, but according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda V. 63, 7. रथ = रंहण-स्व-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-a" target="_blank">Page0831-a+ 81</a>]<BR>भाव, of a swift nature, going swiftly); a warrior,<BR>hero, champion; the body; the foot; a limb, mem-<BR>ber, part; Calamus Rotang; Dalbergia Ougeinensis;<BR>= पौरुष; pleasure, delight, desire [cf. मनो-<BR>रथ, रथ-जित्]; (ई), f. a small carriage; [cf.<BR>probably Gr. ῤέθος; Lat. rota; Old Germ. rad;<BR>Angl. Sax. rad, lidh; Goth. lithus; Lith. ratas;<BR>Hib. roth.]<BR>—रथ-कट्या or रथ-कड्या, f. a<BR>quantity of chariots, assemblage of cars.<BR>—रथ-<BR>कर, अस्, m. = रथ-कार below.<BR>—रथ-कल्-<BR>पक, अस्, m. an officer who has charge of a king's<BR>chariots, the arranger or superintendent of a great<BR>man's equipages.<BR>—रथ-काम्य, Nom. P. -काम्-<BR>यति, &c., to long for a chariot, wish to be yoked<BR>(said of a horse, &c.).<BR>—रथ-काय, अम्, n. the<BR>whole body or collection of chariots (constituting one<BR>division of an army).<BR>—रथ-कार or रथ-का-<BR>रक, अस्, m. a chariot-maker, coach-builder, wheel-<BR>wright, carpenter (regarded as the son of a Māhiṣya<BR>by a Karaṇī).<BR>—रथकार-त्व, अम्, n. the trade<BR>or business of a carriage-builder.<BR>—रथ-कुटुम्-<BR>बिक, अस्, or रथ-कुटुम्बिन्, ई, m. a carriage-<BR>driver, charioteer, coachman.<BR>—रथ-कूबर, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a chariot-shaft, pole of a carriage.<BR>—र-<BR>थ-कृत्, त्, m. a carriage or chariot-maker, wheel-<BR>wright (regarded as the son of a Māhiṣya by a<BR>Karaṇī); N. of a Yakṣa.<BR>—रथ-केतु, उस्, m. the<BR>flag or banner of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-क्रान्त, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a particular time (in music).<BR>—रथ-<BR>क्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. purchased for the price of a<BR>chariot.<BR>—रथ-क्षय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. abiding<BR>or remaining in a chariot.<BR>—रथ-क्षोभ, अस्,<BR>m. the shaking about of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-गणक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘car-numberer,’ (probably) an officer who<BR>numbers or counts a great man's chariots.<BR>—रथ-<BR>गर्भक, अस्, m. ‘an embryo-carriage,’ i. e. a litter,<BR>sedan-chair, palanquin.<BR>—रथ-गुप्ति, इस्, f. ‘car-<BR>preservative,’ a fence of wood or iron protecting a<BR>war-chariot from collisions, &c.<BR>—रथ-गृत्स, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. a clever or skilful charioteer.<BR>—रथ-गो-<BR>पन, अम्, n. = रथ-गुप्ति.<BR>—रथ-ग्रन्थि, इस्,<BR>m. the knot or fastening of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-घो-<BR>ष, अस्, m. the sound or rattling noise of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-चक्र, अम्, n. a chariot-wheel.<BR>—रथ-<BR>चक्र-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. arranged in the form of a<BR>chariot-wheel.<BR>—रथ-चरण, अस्, m. ‘chariot-<BR>foot,’ a chariot-wheel; the ruddy goose.<BR>—रथ-<BR>चर्या, f. chariot-course, chariot-exercise, chariot-race,<BR>travelling or going by carriage, (frequently in pl.)<BR>—रथ-चर्षण, Ved. a particular part of a<BR>chariot, the middle part where people sit, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 5, 19. रथ-चर्षणे<BR>= रथस्य द्रष्टव्ये मध्ये देशे.)<BR>—रथ-<BR>चित्रा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—रथ-जङ्घा, f. a par-<BR>ticular part of a carriage, the hinder part.<BR>—रथ-<BR>जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. conquering chariots, obtaining<BR>chariots by conquest; gaining desire, winning affec-<BR>tion, (see रथ.)<BR>—रथ-जूति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>rushing along in a chariot; (इस्), m. (perhaps) a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रथ-ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of<BR>chariots, skill in driving.<BR>—रथ-ज्ञानिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>skilled in managing a chariot, skilful in driving a<BR>carriage.<BR>—रथ-ज्वर, अस्, m. a crow.<BR>—रथ-<BR>तुर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, Ved. urging a chariot, drawing a<BR>carriage, (Sāy. Ṛg-veda I. 88, 2 = रथस्य-प्रे-<BR>रयितृ.)<BR>—रथ-दारु, उ, n. wood suitable for<BR>carriage building.<BR>—रथ-द्रु, उस्, or रथ-द्रु-<BR>म, अस्, m. Dalbergia Ougeinensis.<BR>—रथ-धुर्,<BR>ऊर्, f. the pole of a chariot, shaft of a carriage.<BR>—रथ-धूर्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone or standing<BR>upon the fore-part of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-नाभि, इस्,<BR>f. the nave of a chariot-wheel.<BR>—रथ-निर्घोष<BR>or रथ-निर्ह्राद, अस्, m. the sound or rattling of<BR>a chariot.<BR>—रथ-निस्वन, अस्, m. sound of a<BR>chariot.<BR>—रथ-नीड, अस्, m. the seat or inner<BR>part of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-नेमि, इस्, f. the rim or<BR>circumference of a chariot-wheel.<BR>—रथन्-तर,<BR>अम्, n. (रथम्, acc. c.), N. of various Sāmans;<BR>(अस्), m. a form of Agni (regarded as a son of<BR>Tapas); (ई), f., N. of a wife of Taṃsu.<BR>—रथ-<BR>पथ, अस्, m. a carriage road.<BR>—रथ-पर्याय,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-b" target="_blank">Page0831-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. Calamus Rotang.<BR>—रथ-पाद, अस्, m.<BR>‘carriage-foot,’ a carriage or chariot-wheel.<BR>—रथ-<BR>पुङ्गव, अस्, m. chief of warriors.<BR>—रथ-प्रष्-<BR>ठ, अस्, m. any one who goes before or leads a<BR>chariot.<BR>—रथ-प्रा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. (according<BR>to Sāy.) = रथस्य पूरयितृ, filling a chariot<BR>(with riches, said of Vāyu); (आस्), f., N. of a river.<BR>—रथ-प्रोत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fixed or fastened<BR>in a car.<BR>—रथ-प्रोष्ठ, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रथ-प्सा, आस्, f., N. of a river.<BR>—रथ-बन्-<BR>ध, अस्, m. ‘carriage-fastening,’ the fastenings or<BR>harness of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-मण्डल, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. a number of chariots.<BR>—रथ-मध्य-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, standing in the centre of a car.<BR>—रथ-<BR>महोत्सव, अस्, m. a great car-festival, the solemn<BR>procession of an idol on a car.<BR>—रथ-मुख, अम्,<BR>n. the front or fore-part of a carriage.<BR>—रथ-<BR>यात्रा, f. ‘car-procession,’ the festive procession of<BR>an idol on a car (especially the procession of the<BR>car of Jagan-nātha).<BR>—रथ-यान, अम्, n. the<BR>going by carriage or in a chariot.<BR>—रथ-यावन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. going by carriage or in a chariot.<BR>—रथ-युग, अस्, m. a chariot yoke.<BR>—रथ-<BR>युज्, क्, क्, क्, yoking carriage, harnessed to chariots<BR>(Ved.); (क्), m. a charioteer.<BR>—रथ-युद्ध,<BR>अम्, n. a chariot fight, a battle (between combatants<BR>mounted) on chariots.<BR>—रथ-यूथ, अस्, अम्, m.<BR>n. a quantity or number of chariots.<BR>—रथ-यो-<BR>जक, अस्, m. the yoker or harnesser of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-योध, अस्, m. one who fights from a<BR>chariot.<BR>—रथ-राज, अस्, m. ‘chariot-king,’ N. of<BR>an ancestor of Śākya-muni.<BR>—रथ-वंश, अस्, m.<BR>a number of carriages.<BR>—रथ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having or possessing carriages, accompanied with<BR>chariots; containing the word रथ.<BR>—रथ-वर,<BR>अस्, m. an excellent chariot; excellent warrior.<BR>—र-<BR>थ-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. a carriage-road, highway, street.<BR>—रथ-वाह, अस्, ई, अम्, drawing a carriage or<BR>chariot; (अस्), m. a carriage-horse, a horse yoked in<BR>a carriage; a coachman, charioteer.<BR>—रथ-वा-<BR>हक, अस्, m. a coachman, charioteer.<BR>—रथ-वा-<BR>हन, अस्, m. a proper N.; (अम्), n. a movable<BR>platform or stand on which carriages may be placed.<BR>—रथ-विज्ञान, अस्, m. or रथ-विद्या, f. skill<BR>in managing chariots, the art of driving cars.<BR>—र-<BR>थ-विमोचन, अम्, n. the unyoking of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-विमोचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the<BR>unyoking of chariots.<BR>—रथ-वीति, इस्, m., Ved. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रथ-वीथी, f. a carriage way, high-<BR>road, street.<BR>—रथ-वेग, अस्, m. the speed or<BR>velocity of a chariot.<BR>—रथ-व्रज or रथ-<BR>व्रात, अस्, m. = रथ-वंश.<BR>—रथ-शक्ति, इस्,<BR>f. the staff which supports the banner of a war-<BR>chariot.<BR>—रथ-शाला, f. a coach-house, carriage-<BR>shed.<BR>—रथ-शिक्षा, f. the art of driving a chariot,<BR>coachmanship.<BR>—रथ-शिरस्, अस्, or रथ-शीर्ष,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. = रथ-मुख.<BR>—रथ-श्रेणि, इस्,<BR>f. a row of carriages, line of chariots.<BR>—रथ-<BR>सङ्ग, अस्, m. a hostile encounter of chariots.<BR>—र-<BR>थ-सत्तम, अस्, m. a most excellent chariot; the<BR>best of warriors.<BR>—रथ-सप्तमी, f., N. of the<BR>seventh day in the light half of the month Māgha<BR>(so called as the beginning of a Manvantara when a<BR>new Sun ascended his car).<BR>—रथ-सारथि, इस्, m.<BR>a charioteer, coachman.<BR>—रथ-सूत्र, अम्, n. rules<BR>or directions about carriage building.<BR>—रथ-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being on a chariot, mounted on a car;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—रथस्-पति, इस्, m. (रथस्<BR>probably a form of the genitive; cf. वनस्-पति),<BR>Ved. the deity presiding over pleasure (or over war-<BR>chariots).<BR>—रथ-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. touching the<BR>chariot.<BR>—रथ-स्वन, अस्, m. the sound or rattling<BR>of chariots; (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. having the sound of<BR>a chariot (?), having a sounding chariot; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Yakṣa.<BR>—रथाक्ष (˚थ-अक्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>carriage axle; a measure of length, = 104 Aṅgulas;<BR>N. of one of Skanda's attendants.<BR>—रथाग्र्य (˚थ-<BR>अग्˚), अस्, m. the best warrior, (sometimes incorrectly<BR>written रथाग्र.)<BR>—रथाङ्ग (˚थ-अङ्˚), अम्, n.<BR>any part of a carriage, (in this sense also अस्, m.); a<BR>carriage-wheel, chariot-wheel; a discus (especially<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">Page0831-c+ 81</a>]<BR>that of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu); a potter's wheel or<BR>lathe; (अस्), m. the ruddy goose, Anas Casarca, =<BR>चक्र-वाक; (ई), f. a species of plant, = ऋद्धि;<BR>(आ), f., see रथाह्वा.<BR>—रथाङ्ग-तुल्याह्वयन<BR>(˚य-आह्˚), अस्, m. ‘(a bird) having the same name<BR>as the wheel of a carriage,’ i. e. the Anas Casarca<BR>or ruddy goose (= चक्र-वाक).<BR>—रथाङ्ग-ना-<BR>मक, अस्, or रथाङ्ग-नामन्, आ, or रथाङ्ग-<BR>सञ्ज्ञ, or रथाङ्ग-साह्व, or रथाङ्गाह्व (˚ग-<BR>आह्˚), or रथाङ्गाह्वय (˚ग-आह्˚), अस्, m. = र-<BR>थाङ्ग-तुल्याह्वयन above.<BR>—रथाङ्ग-नेमि,<BR>इस्, f. the circumference or felly of a chariot-wheel.<BR>—रथाङ्ग-पाणि, इस्, m. ‘having a wheel, i. e. a<BR>discus in hand,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—रथाङ्ग-श्रोणि-<BR>विम्बा, f. having buttocks like a wheel, i. e. semi-<BR>circular.<BR>—रथानीक (˚थ-अन्˚), अम्, n. an array<BR>or army of war-chariots.<BR>—रथान्तर (˚थ-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a preceptor, (for रथीतर); N. of a<BR>Kalpa.<BR>—रथाभ्र (˚थ-अभ्˚) or रथाभ्र-<BR>पुष्प, अस्, m. Calamus Rotang.<BR>—रथा-रथि,<BR>ind. (fr. रथ + रथ), carriage to carriage, chariot<BR>against chariot, in closest fight; [cf. नखा-नखि.]<BR>—रथारूढ (˚थ-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mounted on<BR>a chariot.<BR>—रथारोह (˚थ-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sit-<BR>ting or mounted on a chariot, one who fights from<BR>a chariot; (अस्), m. the mounting or ascending a<BR>chariot, entering a carriage.<BR>—रथारोहिन् (˚थ-<BR>आर्˚), ई, इणी, इ, mounting a car, one who rides on or<BR>fights from a chariot.<BR>—रथार्भक (˚थ-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a small carriage.<BR>—रथा-वट्ट, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रथावयव (˚थ-अव्˚), अस्, m. any<BR>part or portion of a carriage.<BR>—रथावर्त (˚थ-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—र-<BR>थाश्व (˚थ-अश्˚), अस्, m. a carriage or chariot-<BR>horse; (अम्), n. a carriage and horse.<BR>—रथा-सह्,<BR>औ, m. du., Ved. able or fit to draw a chariot (said<BR>of the two horses of Vāyu).<BR>—रथाहर् (˚थ-अह्˚)<BR>or रथाह्न (˚थ-अह्˚) or रथाह्न्य, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. a day by carriage or chariot, a day's journey by<BR>carriage.<BR>—रथाह्वा (˚थ-आह्˚), f., N. of a river,<BR>(also read रथाङ्का, रथाङ्गा.)<BR>—रथे-चित्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. variegated or glittering on a<BR>chariot.<BR>—रथेश (˚थ-ईश), अस्, m. the owner or<BR>master of a carriage, a warrior or combatant fighting<BR>from a chariot; (आ), f. the pole of a carriage, (for<BR>the next.)<BR>—रथेषा (˚थ-ईषा), f. the pole or<BR>shaft of a carriage, chariot-pole.<BR>—रथेषु (˚थ-<BR>इषु), उस्, m., N. of a kind of arrow.<BR>—रथे-<BR>ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. standing on a car or chariot,<BR>moving or going by carriage, a warrior or combatant<BR>fighting from a chariot; [cf. Zend rathœstā.]<BR>—रथोढ (˚थ-ऊढ) or रथोऌह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. carried on a chariot or carriage.<BR>—रथोत्तम<BR>(˚थ-उत्˚), अस्, m. an excellent chariot or carriage.<BR>—रथोत्सव (˚थ-उत्˚), अस्, m. the car-festival, a<BR>solemn procession of an idol mounted on a car.<BR>—रथोद्धत (˚थ-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>haughty on his car; (आ), f., N. of a kind of metre,<BR>four times ¯˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯; N. of a work.<BR>—रथोद्वह (˚थ-उद्˚) or रथोपस्थ (˚थ-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, m. the seat of a chariot, seat for driving,<BR>driving-box (as lower than the main body of the car),<BR>the hinder part of a car.<BR>—रथोरग (˚थ-उर्˚), आस्,<BR>m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—रथोष्मा (˚थ-उष्˚),<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR>—रथौघ (˚थ-ओघ), अस्, m.<BR>a number of carriages or chariots.<BR>—रथौजस्<BR>(˚थ-ओज्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having the strength of a<BR>chariot, as strong as a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0830-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथक|रथकः
रथक, अस्, m. a particular part of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथया
रथया, f., Ved. desire for carriages or chariots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथयु
रथयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desiring or wishing for<BR>carriages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथर्य
रथर्य, Nom. P. रथर्यति, &c., Ved. to go<BR>or travel by carriage or chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथर्वी
रथर्वी, f., Ved. epithet of a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथस्या
रथस्या, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिक|रथिकः
रथिक, अस्, ई, अम्, going by carriage or chariot,<BR>any one who travels or rides in a carriage, the owner<BR>of a car or carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथित
रथित, अस्, आ, अम्, equipped or furnished with a<BR>chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0831-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन्
रथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having or possessing a chariot<BR>or carriage, going in a car, travelling or riding in<BR>a carriage; consisting of chariots; accustomed to<BR>chariots (said of horses, Ved.); belonging to car-<BR>riages; (ई), m. an owner of a carriage, lord of<BR>chariots; a warrior who fights from a chariot; (इनी),<BR>f. a number of carriages or chariots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन|रथिनः
रथिन, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing a carriage, riding<BR>in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिर|रथिरः
रथिर, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing a carriage or<BR>chariot, going in a carriage; hastening, quick,<BR>speedy; (अस्), m. a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिराय
रथिराय, Nom. P. रथिरायति, &c., Ved. to<BR>go quickly, hasten; (Sāy.) to possess a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिरायत्
रथिरायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. hastening; having<BR>chariots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथी
रथी (a Vedic word formed fr. रथ, and used<BR>as both adj. and subst.; रथ्यम् acc. sing., रथ्यस्<BR>acc. pl.), one going by chariot, one who is furnished<BR>with a chariot or carriage; forming a cart-load, as<BR>much as a cart will carry, carried on a waggon, be-<BR>longing to a chariot; a carriage-driver, coachman,<BR>charioteer, a warrior who fights from a chariot; a<BR>guide, leader, master, lord.<BR>—रथी-तम, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. chief or best of charioteers, (Sāy. = अतिशयेन<BR>रथिन् or अतिशयेन रंहितृ.)<BR>—रथी-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, a better or superior charioteer; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a preceptor; (आस्), m. pl. his descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथीकर
रथीकर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथीय
रथीय, Nom. P. रथीयति, &c., to desire a<BR>chariot; to go or travel in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथीयत्
रथीयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. desiring a chariot;<BR>going in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ्य|रथ्यः
रथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>carriage or chariot, accustomed to a carriage; delight-<BR>ing in roads (?); (अस्), m. a carriage or chariot-horse,<BR>(also आ, f.); a part of a chariot; (आ), f. a road for<BR>carriages, high-road, main road, a place where several<BR>roads meet; a number of carriages or chariots, assem-<BR>blage of cars; (अम्), n., Ved. carriage equipments<BR>or harness, chariot trappings, a wheel or any part<BR>of a carriage; (perhaps) a chariot-race or contest<BR>with chariots; a conveyance, carriage (?).<BR>—रथ्य-<BR>चर्या, f. = रथ-चर्या, q. v.<BR>—रथ्यावसर्पण<BR>(˚या-अव्˚), अम्, n. walking down a road.<BR>—रथ्यो-<BR>पसर्पण (˚या-उप्˚), अम्, n. walking to a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्
रद् रद्, cl. 1. P. रदति, रराद, रदितुम्,<BR>to scratch, scrape; to split, chop, divide,<BR>tear, break, rend; to gnaw; to dig; to open (a<BR>road &c., Ved.); to guide, lead, conduct (Ved.); to<BR>convey anything to any one, give, dispense (Ved.);<BR>[cf. Lat. rad-o, rod-o, ros-trum, perhaps radius;<BR>probably Goth. letan; Angl. Sax. lœtan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद|रदः
रद, अस्, आ, अम्, scratching, scraping, splitting,<BR>rending, tearing, gnawing; (अस्), m. the act of<BR>scratching or gnawing, &c.; a tooth; an elephant's<BR>tusk; a symbolical expression for the number thirty-<BR>two.<BR>—रद-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘tooth-covering,’ a<BR>lip; [cf. दन्त-च्छद.]<BR>—रदाङ्कुर (˚द-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the point of a tooth.<BR>—रदा-वसु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. dispensing wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदन|रदनः
रदन, अस्, m. a tooth, tusk; an elephant's tusk;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of splitting, tearing, rending, gnawing.<BR>—रदन-च्छद, अस्, m. = रद-च्छद, a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदनिका
रदनिका, f. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदनिन्
रदनिन्, ई, m. ‘tusked,’ an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदिन्
रदिन्, ई, m. ‘tusked,’ an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्द|रद्दः
रद्द रद्द, अस्, m., N. of the eleventh Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्ध
रद्ध रद्ध, रद्धृ. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्य्
रद्य् रद्य्, cl. 1. P. रद्यति, &c., to be<BR>firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रध्
रध् रध् or रन्ध्, cl. 4. P. रध्यति,<BR>ररन्ध (1st pl. ररन्धिम or रे-<BR>ध्म), रधिष्यति or रत्स्यति, अरधत् or<BR>अरन्धत् (Vedic forms रारधुस्, रधम्, र-<BR>धाम, रन्धि, रन्धीस्), Inf. रद्धुम्, रधि-<BR>तुम्, रन्धितुम्, to become subject to any one<BR>(dat.), to be subdued (Ved.); to be destroyed,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">Page0832-b+ 75</a>]<BR>perish (Ved.); to be completed or matured [cf.<BR>rt. राध्]; to bring into subjection, subdue; to op-<BR>press, injure, hurt, torment, kill: Caus. P. रन्ध-<BR>यति (Ved. also A. -ते), -यितुम्, Aor. अररन्धत्<BR>(Ved. रीरधत्), to make subject, subdue; to pain,<BR>torment, oppress, hurt, injure, destroy, bring to<BR>nothing; to cook, prepare food: Desid. रिरधि-<BR>षति or रिरत्सति: Intens. रारध्यते, रारद्धि,<BR>to give into the power of, hand over to; [cf. Lat.<BR>lœdo; Angl. Sax. rendan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्ध
रद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, subdued, hurt, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्धृ
रद्धृ, धा, m. one who subdues or oppresses,<BR>a subduer, conqueror, oppressor, tormentor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रधित
रधित, अस्, आ, अम्, injured, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रधितृ
रधितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, injurious, hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रध्र
रध्र, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. रध्, but<BR>in the first sense perhaps fr. a form रध् = rt. ऋध्<BR>or राध्, q. v.; cf. Zend अरेद्र), Ved. prosperous,<BR>happy, rich, wealthy, liberal; worshipping or gaining<BR>the favour of the gods; injuring, (Sāy. = समृद्ध<BR>or राधक or आराधक or हिंसक.)<BR>—रध्र-<BR>चोद or रध्र-चोदन, अस्, m., Ved. bestowing<BR>wealth, assisting or encouraging the prosperous;<BR>driver or impeller of enemies, (Sāy. = समृद्धा-<BR>नाम् प्रेरक or हिंसकानां चोदक.)<BR>—र-<BR>ध्र-तुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to some) =<BR>रध्र-चोद above, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda VI. 18, 4. रध्र-तुरः is gen. c. of रध्र-<BR>तुर्, a subduer, injurer, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धक
रन्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, subduing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धन|रंधन|रंधनं|रन्धनं
रन्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, one who destroys, a de-<BR>stroyer; (अम्), n. the act of destroying or annihilat-<BR>ing; the act of cooking, preparation or dressing of<BR>food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धनाय
रन्धनाय, Nom. P. रन्धनायति, &c., Ved.<BR>to make subject, deliver into the power of, (Sāy. =<BR>वशी-कृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धस्
रन्धस्, आस्, or रन्धस, अस्, m., N. of a man<BR>belonging to the family of Andhaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धि|रंधि|रंधिः|रन्धिः
रन्धि, इस्, f. subjection, subjugation (Ved.); the<BR>being prepared or cooked; cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धित|रंधित|रन्धितं
रन्धित, अस्, आ, अम्, subdued; destroyed; cooked,<BR>dressed (as food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धिष
रन्धिष, अस्, m., Ved. = हन्तृ, a destroyer<BR>(Vājasaneyi-s. VIII. 55).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्
रन् 1. रन् = rt. रण्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ति
1. रन्ति, इस्, m., Ved. (according to some) a<BR>fighter, warrior, (but according to Sāy. रन्ति = र-<BR>ममाण, रमण-शील, delighting, taking pleasure,<BR>as if fr. rt. रम्, see 2. रन्ति at p. 833, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्त्य
रन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to some)<BR>agreeable, pleasant, (perhaps to be connected with rt.<BR>रम्, but in Ṛg-veda X. 29, 3. another reading has<BR>रंह्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्
रन् 2. रन् in Ṛg-veda I. 120, 7, according<BR>to Sāy. = रातारौ = दातारौ, ‘givers,’ as if pres. part.<BR>of rt. 1. रा, the sing. being substituted for the dual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तव्य
रन्तव्य रन्तव्य, रन्ति, रन्तृ. See p. 833.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तु|रंतुः|रन्तुः
रन्तु रन्तु, उस्, f. a way, road; a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्त्य
रन्त्य रन्त्य. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्दला
रन्दला रन्दला, f., N. of Sañjñā (wife of<BR>the Sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्|रंध्
रन्ध् रन्ध् = rt. रध्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धक
रन्धक, रन्धन, &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्र|रंध्र|रंध्रं
रन्ध्र रन्ध्र, अम्, n. (rarely also अस्, m.;<BR>said to be fr. rt. रध्, probably connected with rt.<BR>रद्), a slit, split, opening, fissure, aperture, hole,<BR>chasm, vent, cavity, (nine openings are usually<BR>reckoned in the human body, viz. two in the nose,<BR>eyes, and ears respectively, one in the mouth, urethra,<BR>and anus, and there is an imaginary tenth opening<BR>in the skull); a symbolical expression for the number<BR>nine; N. of a particular part of a horse's head; a<BR>defect, fault, flaw, imperfection, weak part, assailable<BR>point; N. of the eighth astrological mansion.<BR>—रन्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">Page0832-c+ 77</a>]<BR>ध्र-कण्ट, अस्, m. a species of plant (= जाल-<BR>वर्वूरक).<BR>—रन्ध्र-प्रहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, attack-<BR>ing the weak places (of an enemy).<BR>—रन्ध्र-<BR>बभ्रु, उस्, m. a rat.<BR>—रन्ध्र-वंश, अस्, m. a<BR>hollow bamboo.<BR>—रन्ध्रागत (˚र-आग्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a disease which attacks the throat of horses.<BR>—रन्-<BR>ध्रानुसारिन् (˚र-अन्˚) or रन्ध्रान्वेषिन् (˚र-<BR>अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, looking out for flaws, picking holes,<BR>seeking for weak or assailable points; [cf. छिद्रान्-<BR>वेषिन्.]<BR>—रन्ध्रान्वेषण (˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>the act of seeking for weak places, picking holes,<BR>searching for flaws.<BR>—रन्ध्रापेक्षिन् (˚र-अप्˚), ई,<BR>इणी, इ, watching for weak or assailable places, spying<BR>out holes, looking out for an assailable point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप्
रप् रप् [cf. rt. लप्], cl. 1. P. रपति,<BR>रराप, &c., Ved. to talk (frivolously),<BR>chatter; to murmur; to praise, (Sāy. अरपत् =<BR>अस्तौत्): Intens., Ved. रारपीति, to make a loud<BR>crackling noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राप्य|राप्यः
राप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be said or spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रपस्
रपस् रपस्, अस्, n. [cf. रेपस्], defect, fault,<BR>sin; hurt, injury, (Sāy. = पाप, but Ṛg-veda I. 69,<BR>4. रपांसि = बाधकानि राक्षसादीनि, disturbing<BR>or injurious Rākṣasas, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप्श्
रप्श् रप्श्, a Vedic root, only occurring<BR>in the pres. part. below and with the<BR>preps. प्र and वि; [cf. वि-रप्श्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप्शदूधन्
रप्शद्-ऊधन्, आ, आ or ध्नी, अ, Ved. having a<BR>full or distended udder, (Sāy. = महोधस्क.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप्सु
रप्सु रप्सु (according to Mahī-dhara) =<BR>रूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप्सुदा
रप्सुदा, du., in Ṛg-veda VIII. 72, 12 (the<BR>meaning is obscure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रफ्
रफ् रफ् or रम्फ्, cl. 1. P. रफति,<BR>रम्फति, &c., to go [cf. rt. रर्फ्]; to<BR>injure, hurt, kill; [cf. rts. रिफ्, ऋफ्; cf. also Lat.<BR>rep-o, serp-o.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रफित
रफित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. injured, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब्धृ
रब्धृ रब्धृ. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ्
रभ् रभ् (originally connected with rts.<BR>ग्रभ्, लभ्), cl. 1. A. (in poetry also P.)<BR>रभते (-ति), रेभे, रप्स्यते, अरब्ध, रब्धुम्,<BR>to seize, take (Ved.); to take hold of, clasp, embrace;<BR>to desire vehemently, regret; to act rashly: Pass.<BR>रभ्यते, अरम्भि: Caus. रम्भयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अररम्भत्: Desid. रिप्सते: Intens. रार-<BR>भ्यते, रारम्भीति, रारब्धि; [cf. Gr. ῥώννυμι,<BR>λαμβάνω: Lat. rabies, robur: Goth. arbaiths, li-<BR>ban: Angl. Sax. earfedh, earfodh, leofian, lifian,<BR>lybban, (perhaps also) a-refian, ‘to bear;’ a-rœfnan,<BR>‘to take away:’ Old Germ. laba, labôn.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब्धृ
रब्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, seizing, taking hold of;<BR>beginning [cf. आ-रभ्]; who or what seizes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ
रभ, अस्, m., N. of an ape (in Rāmāyaṇa IV.<BR>33, 14).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस्
रभस्, अस्, n. violence, impetuosity, (रभसा,<BR>with impetuosity, violently), zeal; force, energy,<BR>power, strength, strengthening food, oblation (Ved.).<BR>—रभस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing impe-<BR>tuosity, violent, impetuous, zealous.<BR>—रभो-दा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, Ved. bestowing strength or force, (Sāy. =<BR>बलस्य दातृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस|रभसः
रभस, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. रभस् above), impe-<BR>tuous, violent, rapid, fierce, wild; eager; powerful,<BR>strong, energetic; strengthening, invigorating (Ved.);<BR>joyful; (अस्), m. violence, impetuosity, vehemence,<BR>haste, speed, velocity, precipitation, (रभसात् or<BR>रभसेन, with violence, impetuously, in great<BR>haste, quickly); passion, anger, ill temper, rage;<BR>passionate fondness; joy, pleasure; regret, sorrow;<BR>N. of a magical incantation recited over weapons;<BR>of a Dānava; of a king (son of Rambha); of a<BR>lexicographer; of a Rākṣasa; of an ape (in Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa IV. 39,7).<BR>—रभस-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभसान
रभसान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = रभस, impe-<BR>tuous, violent, rapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0832-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभि
रभि, इस्, f., Ved. (according to some) a particu-<BR>lar part of a car or chariot, (but according to Sāy.,<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 5, 29, रभि is an adj. = आरम्भ-<BR>णीय or आलम्भन-भूत, ‘supporting.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभिष्ठ
रभिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most violent or<BR>impetuous, very strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभीयस्
रभीयस् or रभ्यस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. more<BR>impetuous, very strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भ|रंभः|रम्भः
1. रम्भ, अस्, m. (for 2. see p. 834, col. 1), a<BR>prop, support, staff, stick; a bamboo; N. of the<BR>fifth Kalpa; of a son of Āyu; of a son of Viviṃśati;<BR>of a king of Vajra-rātra; of the father of the Asura<BR>Mahiṣa and brother of Karambha; of an ape (in<BR>Rāmāyaṇa IV. 39, 20, &c.); (आ), f. the plantain,<BR>Musa Sapientum; a sort of rice; a kind of metre,<BR>four times ˘˘˘˘¯¯¯¯; N. of Gaurī or of Dāk-<BR>ṣāyaṇī in the Malaya mountains; N. of a celebrated<BR>Apsaras (wife of Nala-kūbara and carried off by<BR>Rāvaṇa; Rambhā is best known as a beautiful<BR>nymph of Indra's paradise; she is sometimes regarded<BR>as a form of Lakṣmī, when she sprang with thirteen<BR>other precious things from the froth of the churned<BR>ocean; she takes her place in Hindū mythology as<BR>a kind of popular Venus or type of female beauty);<BR>a harlot.<BR>—रम्भा-तृतीया, f., N. of the third day<BR>of the first half of the month Jyaiṣṭha (so called<BR>because Hindū women on this day imitate the<BR>beautiful nymph Rambhā, who bathed on the same<BR>day with particular ceremonies).<BR>—रम्भाभिसार<BR>(˚भा-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘the meeting or assaulting of<BR>Rambhā,’ N. of a drama.<BR>—रम्भा-व्रत, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a particular ceremony, (see above.)<BR>—रम्-<BR>भोरु (˚भ-ऊरु), उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ, having beautiful<BR>thighs, (see ऊरु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भक
रम्भक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भिन्
रम्भिन्, ई, m., Ved. ‘carrying a stick,’ an old<BR>man; (Sāy.) a door-keeper, porter; (इणी), f., Ved.<BR>(probably) a particular vessel or ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्सु
रिप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid), wishing to seize<BR>or take hold of, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभिनेय
रभिनेय रभिनेय (?), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभेणक
रभेणक रभेणक, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-<BR>demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्
रम् रम्, cl. 1. A. (in poetry also P.)<BR>रमते (-ति), रेमे, रंस्यते, अरंस्त (in<BR>the Veda also cl. 9. P. रम्णाति, &c.) रन्तुम्, (and<BR>with a preposition sometimes) रमितुम्, to stop,<BR>stay, calm, tranquillize, (in these senses cl. 9. P.,<BR>Ved.); to rest, repose, remain quiet, take one's ease<BR>(cl. 1. A.); to remain, stay, pause; to like to stay or<BR>remain; to make happy, rejoice, please (cl. 1. P.<BR>and A.); to be pleased or delighted, to rejoice (cl. 1.<BR>A.); to be pleased with or rejoice at, take delight in<BR>(with loc. or inst. or with सह and inst.); to play<BR>or sport with, dally with (with inst. or with सह<BR>and inst., or with सार्धम् &c. and inst.); to have<BR>sexual intercourse with (with inst.), know carnally<BR>(with acc.); to couple (said of deer): Caus. रम-<BR>यति (according to some also रामयति), -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अरीरमत् (Ved. रमयामकः, Pāṇ. III. 1,<BR>42), to cause to stay, stop (Ved.); to calm, tranquil-<BR>lize (Ved.); to delight, gratify, please, rejoice, amuse,<BR>give pleasure, cause (sexual) enjoyment; to cause to<BR>couple (said of deer); to be pleased or delighted, to<BR>rejoice: Desid. रिरंसते: Intens. रंरम्यते,<BR>रंरन्ति, रंरमीति (Ved. रारन्धि, according to<BR>Sāy. = रमस्व, cf. Pāṇ. VI. 4, 103); [cf. Zend<BR>ram, rām-a, airi-ma; Gr. ἠρέμα, ἠρεμα-ῖο-ς,<BR>ἠρεμ-ία, ἡρεμ-έ-ω, ἠρεμίζω, ἔρη-μο-ς, ἐρημ-ία,<BR>ἐρημ-ό-ω, νω-λεμ-ές; Goth. rim-is; Old Germ.<BR>rawa, ruowa, rawen, resti, rastjan; Angl. Sax.<BR>rest, restan; Lith. ram-a-s, rom-u-s, rim-ti,<BR>ram-dy-ti; Hib. reamhain, ‘pleasure.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत|रतं
रत, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, delighted, amused,<BR>gratified, satisfied, happy; enamoured of, fondly<BR>attached to; delighted with, taking pleasure in,<BR>pleased with (with inst.); intent on, addicted to;<BR>devoted to, occupied in, engaged in (with loc.); in-<BR>clined to, disposed; loved, beloved; (आ), f., N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-b" target="_blank">Page0833-b+ 81</a>]<BR>the mother of Day (in Mahā-bh. Ādi-p. 2584);<BR>(अम्), n. pleasure, enjoyment, enjoyment of love,<BR>sexual union, coition, copulation; the private parts<BR>(= गुह्य).<BR>—रत-कील, अस्, m. a dog.<BR>—रत-<BR>कूजित, अम्, n. lascivious murmur.<BR>—रत-गुरु,<BR>उस्, m. a husband.<BR>—रत-ज्वर, अस्, m. a crow.<BR>—रत-तालिन्, ई, m. a libertine, voluptuary.<BR>—रत-<BR>ताली, f. a procuress, bawd.<BR>—रत-नाराच, अस्, m.<BR>(according to some) = रत-नारीच, अस्, (except in the<BR>first meaning).<BR>—रत-नारीच, अस्, m. a voluptuary;<BR>a dog; N. of Kāma-deva, the god of love; lasci-<BR>vious murmur.<BR>—रत-निधि, इस्, m. a species of<BR>bird (the wagtail).<BR>—रत-बन्ध, अस्, m. sexual<BR>union.<BR>—रतर्द्धिक (˚त-ऋद्˚), अम्, n. a day;<BR>bathing for pleasure; the aggregate of eight auspi-<BR>cious objects.<BR>—रत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. con-<BR>taining a form of the rt. रम्.<BR>—रत-व्रण, अस्,<BR>m. a dog.<BR>—रत-शायिन्, ई, m. a dog.<BR>—रत-<BR>हिण्डक, अस्, m. a ravisher or seducer of women; a<BR>libertine.<BR>—रतान्दुक (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. a dog.<BR>—रतामर्द (˚त-आम्˚), अस्, m. a dog.<BR>—रता-<BR>यनी (˚त-अय्˚), f. a prostitute, harlot.<BR>—रतार्थिन्<BR>(˚त-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, wishing for sexual enjoyment,<BR>amorous, lascivious; (इनी), f. a wanton woman.<BR>—रतोत्सव (˚त-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘love-festival,’ feast<BR>of sexual enjoyment.<BR>—रतोद्वह (˚त-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रति|रतिः
रति, इस्, f. rest, repose (Ved.); pleasure, enjoy-<BR>ment, delight, joy, amusement; love, affection, fond-<BR>ness; fondness for, pleasure in, attachment or addic-<BR>tion to (with loc.); the pleasure of love, sexual<BR>passion, sexual intercourse; the pudenda; = रति-<BR>गृह, q. v.; the goddess of Love or Sexual Passion<BR>personified as the wife of Kāma-deva; N. of the<BR>sixth Kalā of the moon; of an Apsaras; of the wife<BR>of Vibhu (mother of Pṛthu-ṣeṇa); of a magical<BR>incantation recited over weapons; a mystical term<BR>for the letter न्; N. of a metre, four times ¯˘.<BR>—रति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, pleasure-causing, joy-<BR>making, preparing love or happiness; being in love,<BR>enamoured, = कामिन्; (अस्), m. epithet of a Samādhi.<BR>—रति-कर्मन्, अ, n. sexual intercourse.<BR>—रति-<BR>कान्त-तर्क-वाग्-ईश, अस्, m., N. of a commentator<BR>on the Mugdha-bodha.<BR>—रति-कुहर, अम्, n. pu-<BR>dendum muliebre.<BR>—रति-क्रिया, f. sexual inter-<BR>course.<BR>—रति-खेद-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping<BR>after the fatigue of sexual enjoyment.<BR>—रति-गुण,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Deva-gandharva.<BR>—रति-गृह, अस्,<BR>m. ‘pleasure-house,’ a brothel; pudendum muliebre.<BR>—रति-चरण-समन्त-स्वर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king of the Gandharvas.<BR>—रति-जनक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—रति-जह, अस्, m., N. of a Samādhi.<BR>—रति-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in the art of love.<BR>—रति-तस्कर, अस्, m. a ravisher, seducer.<BR>—रति-<BR>नाग, अस्, m. a sort of coitus.<BR>—रति-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘Rati's husband,’ i. e. Kāma-deva, the god of love.<BR>—रति-पाश, अस्, m. a sort of coitus.<BR>—रति-प्र-<BR>पूर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a particular Kalpa or age.<BR>—रति-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘beloved by Rati,’ i. e. Kāma-<BR>deva; (आ), f. a N. of Dākṣāyaṇī, (also read रवि-<BR>प्रिया.)<BR>—रति-भवन, अम्, n. ‘pleasure-abode,’<BR>a house for prostitution, brothel.<BR>—रति-मञ्जरी,<BR>f., N. of an erotic work.<BR>—रति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having enjoyment or pleasure, gay, cheerful, pleased,<BR>gratified.<BR>—रति-मदा, f. an Apsaras.<BR>—रति-मन्-<BR>दिर, अम्, n. ‘pleasure-house,’ a pleasure-room,<BR>pleasure-temple; Love's dwelling; pudendum muli-<BR>ebre.<BR>—रति-मित्र, अस्, m. a sort of coitus.<BR>—रति-<BR>रण-धीर, अस्, आ, अम्, bold or energetic in Love's<BR>contests.<BR>—रति-रमण, अस्, m. Rati's lover or<BR>husband, i. e. Kāma-deva.<BR>—रति-रस, अस्, m. the<BR>taste or pleasure of love, sexual enjoyment; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), having the flavour or taste of love, as sweet as<BR>love.<BR>—रति-रस-ग्लानि, इस्, f. lassitude after sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>—रति-रहस्य, अम्, n. ‘secrets or<BR>mysteries of love,’ N. of an erotic work by Kokkvoka.<BR>—रति-लक्ष, अम्, n. sexual intercourse.<BR>—रति-<BR>लम्पट, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of sexual enjoyment,<BR>lascivious, lustful.<BR>—रति-लोल, अस्, m., N. of a demon.<BR>—रति-वर, अस्, m. Rati's husband, Kāma-deva;<BR>a gift or offering vowed to Rati.<BR>—रति-वर्धन,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">Page0833-c+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, increasing love.<BR>—रति-वल्ली, f. love<BR>regarded as a creeper.<BR>—रति-शक्ति, इस्, f. the faculty<BR>of sexual enjoyment, virile power.<BR>—रति-शूर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘love-hero,’ a man of great procreative power.<BR>—रति-संयोग, अस्, m. sexual union.<BR>—रति-<BR>संहित, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied with love, abound-<BR>ing in affection.<BR>—रति-सत्वरा, f. Trigonella Cor-<BR>niculata.<BR>—रति-सर्वस्व, अम्, n. ‘the whole essence<BR>of love,’ N. of a work on erotic subjects.<BR>—रति-<BR>सुन्दर, अस्, m. a sort of coitus.<BR>—रति-सेन, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of the Colas.<BR>—रत्य्-अङ्ग, अम्,<BR>n. pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिका
रतिका, f. a particular musical mode (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रती
रती, f. = रति, the wife of Kāma and goddess of<BR>love, (lengthened on account of the metre.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्वा
रत्वा, ind. having sported or dallied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तव्य
रन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be rejoiced at, to be<BR>loved, lovable, lovely, amiable; (अम्), n. pleasure,<BR>enjoyment, play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ति
2. रन्ति, इस्, f. (for 1. see p. 832, col. 2), amuse-<BR>ment, pleasure, delight (? Ved., if रन्ति has this<BR>sense, it may equally be referred to rt. 1. रन्; it is<BR>said also to be used as a term of endearment for a<BR>cow); (इस्), m., N. of a lexicographer (= रन्ति-देव).<BR>—रन्ति-देव, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu; of a king<BR>(son of Saṅkṛti); of a lexicographer; a dog.<BR>—रन्ति-<BR>नार or रन्ति-भार, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तुमनस्
रन्तु-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (रन्तु for रन्तुम्,<BR>inf. of rt. रम्), inclined to take pleasure, wishing<BR>to enjoy sexual pleasures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तृ
रन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. liking to remain, de-<BR>lighting in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम|रमः
रम, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing, delighting, rejoicing,<BR>gratifying, giving pleasure, delightful [cf. मनो-<BR>रम]; dear, beloved; (अस्), m. joy; a lover, hus-<BR>band, spouse; the god of love, Kāma-deva; the red-<BR>flowering Aśoka; (आ), f. a wife, mistress; N. of<BR>Lakṣmī, the goddess of fortune; good luck, fortune,<BR>riches, opulence; splendor, pomp; N. of the eleventh<BR>day in the dark half of the month Kārttika; of a<BR>daughter of Śaśi-dhvaja and wife of Kalki.<BR>—रमा-<BR>कान्त, अस्, m. ‘lover of Ramā,’ Viṣṇu.<BR>—रमा-<BR>धव, अस्, m. ‘husband of Ramā,’ Viṣṇu.<BR>—र-<BR>माधिप (˚मा-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of Ramā,’<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—रमा-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of Ramā,’<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; N. of a poet; of a commentator<BR>on the Amara-kośa.<BR>—रमा-पति, इस्, m. ‘husband<BR>of Ramā,’ Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—रमा-प्रिय, अम्,<BR>n. ‘dear to Ramā,’ a lotus.<BR>—रमा-वेष्ट, अस्, m.<BR>turpentine.<BR>—रमाश्रय (˚मा-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘Ra-<BR>mā's refuge or protection, ’ Viṣṇu.<BR>—रमेश (˚मा-<BR>ईश) or रमेश्वर (˚मा-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘Ramā's lord,’<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमक|रमकः
रमक, अस्, आ, अम्, sporting, playing, dallying,<BR>jesting; (अस्), m. a lover, wooer, suitor.<BR>—रमक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण|रमणं|रमणः
रमण, अस्, ई, अम्, causing pleasure, pleasing,<BR>gratifying, delighting, rejoicing, agreeable, delightful,<BR>charming; (अस्), m. a lover, wooer, spouse, husband,<BR>(क्षपा-रमण, the husband of night, the moon);<BR>the god of love or Kāma-deva; an ass; a testicle; a<BR>species of tree (= महा-रिष्ट); N. of a mythical<BR>son of Mano-harā; of Aruṇa or the charioteer of the<BR>sun; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f. a charming<BR>woman, a wife, mistress; a kind of metre, four times<BR>˘˘¯; N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in Rāma-tīrtha; (ई), f. a<BR>beautiful young woman, a mistress, wife; Aloe Indica<BR>(= बाला); a kind of metre, four times ˘˘¯ or four<BR>times ˘˘¯˘˘¯; N. of a female serpent-demon;<BR>(अम्), n. sporting, playing, dalliance, amorous sport,<BR>love, sexual pleasure or intercourse; joy or pleasure<BR>in general; the hinder parts, the hip and loins, the<BR>pudenda (= जघन); the root of Trichosanthes<BR>Diœca; N. of a forest.<BR>—रमण-वसति, इस्, f.<BR>the dwelling-place of a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणक|रमणकं
रमणक, अस्, m., N. of a Varṣa; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of the regent of this Varṣa, (he was a son of<BR>Yajña-bāhu); of Dvīpa; of a son of Vīti-hotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीय|रमणीयं
1. रमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be enjoyed, pleasant,<BR>agreeable, delightful, beautiful, lovely, charming,<BR>handsome.<BR>—रमणीय-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">Page0834-a+ 75</a>]<BR>charming.<BR>—रमणीय-ता, f. or रमणीय-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. pleasantness, agreeableness, delightfulness,<BR>beauty, charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0833-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीय|रमणीयं
2. रमणीय (fr. रमणी), Nom. A. रमणी-<BR>यते, &c., to represent or take the place of a wife,<BR>to be the mistress of any one (gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीयक
रमणीयक, अम्, n. pleasantness, beauty, (for<BR>रामणीयक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण्य|रमण्यं
रमण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) = 1. रमणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमति|रमतिः
रमति, इस्, f., Ved. a place of pleasant resort; (इस्,<BR>इस्, इ), liking to remain in one place, not straying (Ved.,<BR>said of a cow); (इस्), m. a lover; paradise, heaven;<BR>a crow; time; the god of love, Kāma-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमाण
रमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, playing, sporting, disporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमयत्
रमयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. the Caus.), causing<BR>delight, giving pleasure; enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्य|रम्यः
रम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be enjoyed, enjoyable,<BR>pleasing, pleasant, delightful, agreeable, beautiful,<BR>handsome; (अस्), m. Michelia Champaka (= चम्-<BR>पक); = वक-वृक्ष; N. of a son of Āgnīdhra;<BR>(आ), f. night [cf. राम्या]; Hibiscus Mutabilis; N.<BR>of a female personification of a particular musical<BR>mode; of a daughter of Meru (wife of Ramya); of<BR>a river; (अम्), n. the root of Trichosanthes Diœca;<BR>semen virile.<BR>—रम्य-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>village.<BR>—रम्य-ता, f. or रम्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>pleasantness, enjoyableness, agreeableness, pleasure,<BR>beauty.<BR>—रम्य-पुष्प, अस्, m. Bombax Hepta-<BR>phyllum.<BR>—रम्य-फल, अस्, m. a species of plant<BR>(= कारस्कर).<BR>—रम्य-श्री, ईस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—रम्य-सानु, उस्, उस्, उ, having pleasant peaks<BR>or summits (said of a mountain).<BR>—रम्याक्षि (˚य-<BR>अक्˚), इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्यक|रम्यकं
रम्यक, अस्, m. Melia Sempervirens; the root<BR>of Trichosanthes Diœca; N. of a son of Āgnīdhra;<BR>(आ), f., scil. सिद्धि, N. of one of the eight perfec-<BR>tions in the Sāṅkhya system, (in this sense also अम्,<BR>n.); (अम्), n., N. of a Varṣa called after Āgnīdhra's<BR>son Ramyaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्र|रम्रः
रम्र, अस्, m., N. of Aruṇa, the charioteer of<BR>the sun [cf. रमण]; beauty, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमठ|रमठं
रमठ रमठ, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>in the west of India, (also read रमट, रामठ);<BR>(अम्), n. = रामठ, Asa Fœtida.<BR>—रमठ-<BR>ध्वनि, इस्, m. Asa Fœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमितङ्गम|रमितंगम
रमितङ्गम रमितङ्गम, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्फ्|रंफ्
रम्फ् रम्फ्. See rt. रफ्, p. 832.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्ब्
रम्ब् रम्ब् [cf. rt. रम्भ् below], cl. 1.<BR>A. रम्बते, ररम्बे, &c., to sound; to<BR>go (cl. 1. P. रम्बति, cf. rt. रण्व्); to hang down,<BR>hang loosely (= rt. लम्ब्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भ्|रंभ्
रम्भ् रम्भ् [cf. rts. रम्ब्, लम्भ्], cl. 1.<BR>A. रम्भते, &c., to sound, roar, bellow,<BR>low (as cows), &c., make a noise; (for रम्भ्, as a<BR>form of rt. रभ्, see rt. रभ् at p. 832.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भ|रंभः|रम्भः
2. रम्भ, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 833, col. 1),<BR>sounding, roaring, lowing, &c.; (आ), f. a sounding,<BR>roaring; the lowing (of cattle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भमाण
रम्भमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding, roaring,<BR>bellowing, lowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्य|रम्यः
रम्य रम्य, रम्र, &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय्
रय् रय् [cf. rt. लय्], cl. 1. A. रयते, रेये,<BR>&c., रयितुम्, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय|रयः
रय रय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. री), the stream of<BR>a river, current; rapid flow, quick motion, velocity,<BR>speed, swiftness, (रयात् or रयेण quickly, imme-<BR>diately, straightway); course [cf. संवत्सर-र्˚];<BR>impetuosity, vehemence, violence, ardour, zeal, im-<BR>petuous onset; N. of a son of Purū-ravas; of a king.<BR>—रय-प्रश्न-सूत्र-सिद्धान्त or राय-प्˚, N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—रय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing a<BR>rapid current or course, swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयिष्ठ|रयिष्ठः
रयिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, very swift or fleet, very<BR>vehement; (अस्), m., N. of Agni; of Kuvera; of<BR>Brahman; (अम्), n., N. of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयक
रयक रयक, अस्, m. = रवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयि
रयि रयि, इस्, m. (sometimes also इस्, f.; fr. rt.<BR>1. रा; the following forms occur in the Veda, रयिम्,<BR>रयिभिस्, रयीणाम्, रय्या, रय्यै, रय्याम्; cf. 2.<BR>रै), Ved. property, goods, possessions, treasure, wealth;<BR>stuff, materials; (रयेर् आङ्गिरसस्य प्रस्तोभः,<BR>N. of a Sāman.)<BR>—रयि-द, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving<BR>property, a bestower of wealth.<BR>—रयि-पति, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a lord of property or wealth.<BR>—रयि-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. possessing property, well off, rich;<BR>containing the word रयि.<BR>—रयि-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>obtaining or possessing property or wealth.<BR>—रयि-<BR>वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. abounding in riches, (Sāy. =<BR>रय्या or धनेन वृद्ध.)<BR>—रयि-षाच्, क्, क्, क्<BR>(i. e. रयि + साच्), Ved. sharing or possessing pro-<BR>perty, (Sāy. = धन-समवायिन्.)<BR>—रयि-षाह्, ट्,<BR>ट्, ट् (i. e. रयि + साह्), Ved. ruling over property,<BR>(Sāy. = रयीणाम् अभिभवितृ.)<BR>—रयि-ष्ठा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम् (i. e. रयि + स्था) or रयि-स्थान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. being a receptacle of riches, possessing<BR>wealth or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयिक्व
रयिक्व, अस्, m. = रैक्व, a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयिन्तम
रयिन्-तम, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of an unused<BR>form रयिन्; cf. Pāṇ. VIII. 2. 17), Ved. possessing<BR>much property, very wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयीयत्|रयीयन्त्
रयीयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (pres. part. fr. a Nom. fr.<BR>रयि), Ved. wishing for property, desiring riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयीषिन्
रयीषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. desiring treasures, (appa-<BR>rently an incorrect form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय्यावट्ट
रय्यावट्ट रय्यावट्ट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रराट|रराटं
रराट रराट, अम्, n. (an earlier form of<BR>ललाट, q. v.), the forehead, brow; (ई), f. the fore-<BR>head; twisted grass used in a particular manner for<BR>the Havir-dhāna (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रराट्य
रराट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to the<BR>forehead; (आ), f. twisted grass, (see रराटी above);<BR>the horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ररावन्
ररावन् ररावन्, आ, आ, अ (fr. rt. 1. रा),<BR>liberal, bountiful, (Sāy. = हविः, प्रयच्छत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रर्फ्
रर्फ् रर्फ् [cf. rt. रफ्], cl. 1. P. रर्-<BR>फति, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रलमानाथ
रलमानाथ रलमा-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>poet; [cf. रमा-नाथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रला
रला रला, f. a species of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रल्लक|रल्लकः
रल्लक रल्लक, अस्, m. a woollen cloth,<BR>woollen coverlet, blanket; a species of stag or deer;<BR>an eyelash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रव|रवः
रव रव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. रु), a cry, shriek,<BR>bray, yell, howl, roar (of animals, wild beasts, &c.);<BR>song, singing (of birds &c.); hum, humming; clamour,<BR>outcry; talk; thunder; sound, noise (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवण|रवणं|रवणः
रवण, अस्, आ, अम्, crying, screaming, roaring,<BR>shrieking, singing, making an outcry or noise of<BR>any kind, sounding, sonorous (= शब्दन); jesting,<BR>a jester (= भण्डक); sharp, hot (= तीक्ष्ण);<BR>unsteady, fickle, changing, = चञ्चल; (अस्), m. a<BR>camel; the Koil or Indian cuckoo; N. of a man; of<BR>a serpent-king; (अम्), n. brass, bell metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवत्
रवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (for रुवत्, q. v., pres. part. P.<BR>of rt. 1. रु), crying^1 out, raising a cry, bellowing.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवथ|रवथः
रवथ, अस्, m. = रव (Ved.); the Koil or<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवमाण
रवमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (anomalous pres. part. A.<BR>of rt. 1. रु), crying, roaring, raising a cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवस्
रवस् in पुरू-रवस्, बृहद्-रवस्, q.q. v.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवाण
रवाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = रवमाण above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवितृ
रवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who cries or calls<BR>out, crier, screamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवक
रवक रवक, अस्, m., N. of a Dharaṇa or<BR>particular weight of pearls (thirty making the Dha-<BR>raṇa; also read रयक, रिवक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवणक|रवणकः
रवणक रवणक, a filter made of cane or<BR>bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवि|रविः
रवि रवि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. रु),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">Page0834-c+ 77</a>]<BR>a particular form of the sun (sometimes regarded as<BR>one of the twelve Ādityas); the sun (in general) or<BR>the god of the sun; a mountain; N. of a Sauvīraka;<BR>of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; the right canal for the<BR>passage of the vital air (?).<BR>—रवि-कर, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a commentator.<BR>—रवि-कान्त, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>crystal (= सूर्य-कान्त).<BR>—रवि-गुप्त, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a poet.<BR>—रवि-चक्र, अम्, n. a particular astro-<BR>nomical diagram (the sun represented as a man car-<BR>rying the stars on the various parts of his body).<BR>—रवि-ज, अस्, m. ‘child of the sun,’ N. of a parti-<BR>cular Ketu; the planet Saturn.<BR>—रवि-तनय, अस्,<BR>m. the son of the sun, the planet Saturn.<BR>—रवि-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—रवि-तेजस्, अस्,<BR>n. the radiance of the sun.<BR>—रवि-दत्त, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a priest; of a poet.<BR>—रवि-दिन, अम्, n. the<BR>day of the sun, Sunday.<BR>—रवि-दीप्त, अस्, sun-<BR>lighted, sun-illuminated.<BR>—रवि-देव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a poet.<BR>—रवि-नन्दन, अस्, m. ‘son of the<BR>sun,’ Manu Vaivasvata; the ape Sugrīva.<BR>—रवि-<BR>पत्त्र, अस्, m. a sort of shrub.<BR>—रवि-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>m. the son of the sun, the planet Saturn.<BR>—रवि-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m., N. of various plants, = लकुच; =<BR>आदित्य-पत्त्र; = रक्त-करवीर; (आ), f., N. of<BR>Dākṣāyaṇī in Gaṅgā-dvāra; (अम्), n. a red lotus-<BR>flower; copper.<BR>—रवि-बिम्ब, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>sun's disk.<BR>—रवि-मण्डल, अम्, n. the sun's<BR>orb or disk.<BR>—रवि-रत्न, अम्, n. = रवि-कान्त.<BR>—रवि-रत्नक, अम्, n. ‘sun-jewel,’ a ruby.<BR>—रवि-लोचन, अस्, m. ‘sun-eyed,’ N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—रवि-लोह, अम्, n. copper.<BR>—रवि-वार,<BR>अस्, m. or रवि-वासर, अस्, अम्, m. n. the day of<BR>the sun, Sunday.<BR>—रवि-सङ्क्रान्ति, इस्, f. the sun's<BR>entrance into a sign of the zodiac.<BR>—रवि-सञ्ज्ञक,<BR>अम्, n. copper (‘called after the sun’).<BR>—रवि-सम-<BR>प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, radiant as the sun.<BR>—रवि-सा-<BR>रथि, इस्, m. the sun's charioteer, i. e. Aruṇa or the<BR>Dawn.<BR>—रवि-सुत, अस्, m. son of the sun, the planet<BR>Saturn; the ape Sugrīva.<BR>—रवि-सुन्दर-रस, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a particular elixir.<BR>—रवि-सूनु, उस्, m.<BR>son of the sun, the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवितृ
रवितृ रवितृ. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविन्द
रविन्द रविन्द, अम्, n. = अरविन्द, a lotus,<BR>lotus-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविपुला
रविपुला र-विपुला. See under 3. र, p. 824.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवीषु|रवीषुः
रवीषु रवीषु, उस्, m. the god of love,<BR>Kāma-deva, (also read वरीषु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रशना
रशना रशना, f. (connected with रश्मि<BR>below), a rope, cord, line; a rein, bridle; a girth,<BR>girdle, zone, woman's zone or girdle, (in this and<BR>the previous senses often incorrectly written रसना);<BR>the tongue, (in this sense incorrect for रसना); a<BR>finger (according to Naigh. II. 5).<BR>—रशन-सम्-<BR>मित, अस्, आ, अम् (रशन for रशना), Ved. as<BR>long as the rope on the sacrificial post.<BR>—रशना-<BR>कलाप, अस्, m. a woman's girdle formed out of<BR>several strings or threads; [cf. कलाप, रश्मि-<BR>कलाप.]<BR>—रशनाकृत (˚ना-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>guided by a cord, managed with a bridle.<BR>—रशना-<BR>गुण, अस्, m. the cord of a girdle.<BR>—रशनागुणा-<BR>स्पद (˚ण-आस्˚), अम्, n. the place for the girdle,<BR>waist.<BR>—रशनोपमा (˚ना-उप्˚), f. ‘string of com-<BR>parisons,’ a form of simile (when the object to which<BR>anything is compared is made the subject of another<BR>comparision, which again leads to a third and so on).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रशनाय
रशनाय, Nom. A. रशनायते, &c., to be<BR>guided by a rein or bridle (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रशनायमान
रशनायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being guided<BR>by a rein.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मि|रश्मिः
रश्मि रश्मि, इस्, m. (in one passage इस्, f.;<BR>connected with रशना above; in Uṇādi-s. IV. 46.<BR>said to be fr. रश्, substituted for rt. 1. अश्, to per-<BR>vade; perhaps connected with rt. 1. लस्, to shine), a<BR>string, rope, cord; a bridle, rein, leash; a measuring<BR>cord or rope; a goad, whip; a finger (Ved.); a ray<BR>of light, beam [cf. अंशु]; an eyelash (= पक्ष्-<BR>मन्); (in Vājasaneyi-s. XV. 6. said to) = अन्न;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">Page0835-a+ 80</a>]<BR>[cf. probably Lat. laqueus.]<BR>—रश्मि-कलाप, अस्,<BR>m. a pearl-necklace &c. consisting of fifty-four (or<BR>according to others fifty-six) threads.<BR>—रश्मि-केतु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘beam-bannered,’ epithet of a Rākṣasa; of<BR>a particular comet (Ved.).<BR>—रश्मि-क्रीड, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—रश्मि-पति, इस्, m. a species of<BR>plant (= रवि-पत्त्र).<BR>—रश्मि-पवित्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. purified by rays or beams.<BR>—रश्मि-प्र-<BR>भास, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—रश्मि-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. a circle or garland of rays.<BR>—रश्मि-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having rays or beams, radiant; (आन्), m. the<BR>sun; a proper N.<BR>—रश्मि-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed<BR>of beams, consisting of rays.<BR>—रश्मि-मालिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, encircled or garlanded with rays.<BR>—रश्मि-मुच,<BR>अस्, m. ‘ray-emitting,’ the sun.<BR>—रश्मि-राज, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—रश्मि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>rays, radiant; (आन्), m. the sun, (also रश्मी-वत्.)<BR>—रश्मि-शत-शहस्र-परिपूर्ण-ध्वज, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0834-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मन्
रश्मन्, only found in inst. c. m. रश्मा = रश्-<BR>मिना, by a rein (Ṛg-veda VI. 67, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मिन्
रश्मिन् at the end of an adj. comp. = रश्मि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मिस
रश्मिस, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्
रस् 1. रस् [cf. rt. 1. रास्], cl. 1. P. (some-<BR>times also A.) रसति (-ते), ररास, र-<BR>सिष्यति, अरासीत् or अरसीत्, रसितुम्, to roar, howl,<BR>bellow, neigh, yell, cry, scream, cry out, sound, make<BR>any sound or noise; to sing; to resound, reverberate;<BR>(according to Naigh. III. 14) to praise: Caus. रास-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरीरसत्: Desid. रिरसिषति:<BR>Intens. रारस्यते, रारस्ति, to cry out loudly, scream<BR>aloud; [cf. Goth. razda; Old Germ. rartjan,<BR>rerjan; Angl. Sax. reordian, rarian.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसत्
रसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, crying, sounding, making<BR>any sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसन|रसनं|रसनः
1. रसन, अम्, n. the act of roaring or screaming,<BR>crying, tinkling, sounding, &c., the shaking or rum-<BR>bling (of the earth), croaking (of frogs); sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
1. रसित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, uttering inarticulate<BR>sounds; (अम्), n. a roar, scream, cry, noise, sound;<BR>the rattling of thunder.<BR>—रसिताशिन् (˚त-आश्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, consuming or destroying by mere noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितृ
1. रसितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who roars or bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रारस्यमान
रारस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.), crying<BR>out or howling very loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्
रस् 2. रस् (perhaps to be regarded as a<BR>Nominal fr. रस below), cl. 1. 4. 10. P.<BR>रसति, रस्यति, रसयति (also रसापयति; in<BR>Ved. occasionally A. रसयते), to taste, relish; to<BR>feel, perceive, be sensible of; to love: Pass. रस्यते:<BR>Desid. रिरसयिषति, to desire to taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस|रसं|रसः
रस, अस्, m. (perhaps connected with rt. रम्),<BR>the sap or juice of plants, juice of fruit; juice of the<BR>sugar-cane, syrup; (metaphorically) the best or finest<BR>or prime part of anything, essence, marrow; any<BR>liquid or fluid, (गवां रसः, milk), water, liquor,<BR>drink; milk; melted butter; any mixture, draught,<BR>elixir, potion; nectar; poison, poisonous drink;<BR>soup, broth; a constituent fluid or essential juice of<BR>the body, serum, (especially) the primary juice called<BR>chyle (formed from the food and changed by the<BR>bile into blood); mercury, quicksilver (sometimes<BR>regarded in philosophical works as a kind of quint-<BR>essence of the human body or as possessing some<BR>supernatural power over its juices; elsewhere regarded<BR>as the seminal fluid of Śiva); semen virile; taste,<BR>savour, flavour, relish, (the six principal tastes are said<BR>to be मधुर, अम्ल, लवण, कटुक, तिक्त, and<BR>कषाय, q.q. v.v.); a symbolical expression for the<BR>number six; anything used to give relish, a condi-<BR>ment, sauce, spice, seasoning; the organ or instrument<BR>of taste, the tongue; taste or inclination for anything,<BR>appetite, enjoyment of anything, love, affection,<BR>desire; anything that stimulates enjoyment, pleasure,<BR>charm, grace, elegance, beauty, sweetness, spirit, wit;<BR>taste, style, character (of a work); taste, sentiment,<BR>feeling, emotion, pathos, affection, passion, dispo-<BR>sition, (in dramatic composition ten Rasas are enu-<BR>merated, viz. शृङ्गार, love; वीर, heroism; बी-<BR>भत्स, disgust; रौद्र, anger or fury; हास्य,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-b" target="_blank">Page0835-b+ 81</a>]<BR>mirth; भयानक, terror; करुण, pity; अद्भुत,<BR>wonder; शान्त, tranquillity or contentment; वात्-<BR>सल्य, paternal fondness: according to some only<BR>nine or eight are enumerated, the last or last two<BR>being omitted); myrrh; any mineral or metallic salt<BR>(as sulphur, borax, green vitriol, &c.); a metal or<BR>mineral in a state of fusion; gold; a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four times seventy syllables; = शब्द?;<BR>(आ), f. moisture, humidity (Ved.); N. of a river<BR>(Ved.); a mythical stream supposed to flow round<BR>the earth and the atmosphere (Ved.); the lower<BR>world, hell [cf. रसा-तल]; the earth, ground, soil;<BR>the tongue; N. of various plants, Clypea Hernandi-<BR>folia; Boswellia Thurifera; Panicum Italicuml; a<BR>vine or grape; = काकोली; (अम्), n. myrrh; milk;<BR>taste; [cf. according to some, Gr. δρόσος; Lat. ros,<BR>ror-is (for ros-is); Lith. rassa; Russ. rosa.]<BR>—रस-कर्पूर, अम्, n. sublimate or muriate of<BR>mercury (made with sulphur, mercury, and common<BR>salt; the crystals formed in the first operation are<BR>sublimed a second time).<BR>—रस-कर्मन्, अ, n. or<BR>रस-कल्पना, f. preparation of quicksilver, any<BR>process undergone by quicksilver.<BR>—रस-कल्या-<BR>णिनी-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular ceremony;<BR>of the twenty-second chapter of the Bhaviṣyottara-<BR>Purāṇa; of the sixty-second chapter of the Matsya-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—रस-कुल्या, f., N. of a river in Kuśa-<BR>dvīpa.<BR>—रस-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—रस-<BR>केसर, अम्, n. camphor.<BR>—रस-कोमल, अम्, n.<BR>a particular mineral.<BR>—रस-क्रिया, f. application of<BR>fluid remedies or fomentations.<BR>—रस-गन्ध, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. gum-myrrh.<BR>—रस-गन्धक, अस्, m.<BR>myrrh; brimstone, sulphur.<BR>—रस-गर्भ, अम्,<BR>n. a collyrium made from the juice of the Curcuma<BR>Xanthorrhiza; a mineral preparation, vermilion.<BR>—रस-ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, apprehending or per-<BR>ceiving flavours, having a taste for enjoyments, ap-<BR>preciating pleasures; (अस्), m. the organ of taste.<BR>—रस-ग्राहक, अस्, इका, अम्, apprehending or<BR>perceiving flavours, sensible of flavour.<BR>—रस-घ-<BR>न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. full of juice, consisting entirely<BR>of juice.<BR>—रस-घ्न, अस्, m. borax.<BR>—रस-चन्-<BR>द्रिका, f., N. of Śaṅkara's commentary on the<BR>Abhijñāna-śakuntala.<BR>—रस-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a medical work.<BR>—रस-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, originating<BR>in fluids, produced from liquids; proceeding from<BR>chyle; born in passion; (अस्), m. sugar, molasses;<BR>any insect engendered by the fermentation of liquids;<BR>(अम्), n. blood.<BR>—रस-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing<BR>tastes, discriminating or appreciating flavour or excel-<BR>lence, knowing what gives real enjoyment, knowing<BR>the true essence of things, capable of discerning the<BR>spirit or beauty of anything, well versed in any know-<BR>ledge; (अस्), m. a poet or man of discrimination,<BR>any writer who understands the Rasas; an alchemist<BR>who understands the magical properties of mercury;<BR>a physician; a preparer of mercurial and chemical<BR>compounds; (आ, अम्), f. n. the tongue.<BR>—रसज्ञ-<BR>ता, f. or रसज्ञ-त्व, अम्, n. knowledge of flavours;<BR>acquaintance with the true essence of things, poetical<BR>skill or taste; alchemy; discrimination, skill, expe-<BR>rience.<BR>—रस-ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of tastes<BR>(a branch of medical science).<BR>—रस-ज्येष्ठ, अस्,<BR>m. the first or best taste, sweet taste, sweetness; the<BR>sentiment of love.<BR>—रस-तन्मात्र, अम्, n. the<BR>subtile element or rudiment of taste.<BR>—रस-तम,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. the juice of all juices, best juice, essence<BR>of essences.<BR>—रस-तरङ्गिनी, f., N. of a treatise<BR>on poetical sentiment or pathos by Bhānu-datta; of<BR>another work.<BR>—रस-तस्, ind. according to taste or<BR>flavour.<BR>—रस-ता, f. or रस-त्व, अम्, n. fluidity,<BR>juiciness, the being chyle, state of chyle.<BR>—रस-<BR>तेजस्, अस्, n. ‘strength of the chyle,’ blood.<BR>—रस-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, emitting juice or sap, emitting resin;<BR>(अस्), m. ‘giver of fluids or mixtures,’ a physician.<BR>—रस-दर्पण, अस्, m. ‘mirror of the Rasas,’<BR>N. of a medical work.<BR>—रस-दालिका, f. a kind of<BR>sugar-cane.<BR>—रस-दीपिका, f. ‘lamp of the Rasas,’<BR>N. of a medical work.<BR>—रस-द्राविन्, ई, m. a kind<BR>of citron (= मधुर-जम्बीर).<BR>—रस-धातु,<BR>उ, n. ‘fluid-metal,’ quicksilver.<BR>—रस-नाथ, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-c" target="_blank">Page0835-c+ 81</a>]<BR>m. ‘chief of fluids,’ quicksilver, mercury.<BR>—रस-<BR>नायक, अस्, m. ‘leader or lord of quicksilver,’ N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—रस-निवृत्ति, इस्, f. cessation or loss of<BR>taste, &c.<BR>—रस-नेत्रिका, f. realgar, red arsenic.<BR>—रसन्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = रस-तम.<BR>—रस-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a medical work.<BR>—रस-पाक-ज, अस्, m. ‘produced by the cooking<BR>of juices,’ sugar.<BR>—रस-पाचक, अस्, m. ‘cooker of<BR>sauces or flavours,’ a cook.<BR>—रस-पारिजात, अस्, m.<BR>‘the Pārijāta tree of Rasas,’ N. of a work on medi-<BR>cine.<BR>—रस-पुष्प, अम्, n. a particular preparation<BR>of mercury, a kind of muriate formed by subliming<BR>in close vessels a mixture of sulphur, mercury, and<BR>common salt.<BR>—रस-प्रदीप, अस्, m. ‘lamp of<BR>the Rasas,’ N. of a work on medicine; of a work<BR>on rhetoric.<BR>—रस-प्रबन्ध, अस्, m. ‘connection<BR>of Rasas,’ any poetical composition, (especially) a<BR>drama.<BR>—रस-फल, अस्, m. a cocoa-nut tree (the<BR>fruit of which contains a fluid).<BR>—रस-बन्धन,<BR>अम्, n. (probably) a particular part of the intestines.<BR>—रस-बोध, अस्, m. knowledge of taste (especially<BR>in poetic composition).<BR>—रस-भङ्ग, अस्, m. in-<BR>terruption or cessation of passion or sentiment.<BR>—रस-भव, अम्, n. ‘produced from chyle,’<BR>blood.<BR>—रस-भस्मन्, अ, n. calx or oxide of<BR>mercury.<BR>—रस-भेद, अस्, m. a particular prepa-<BR>ration of quicksilver.<BR>—रस-भेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dis-<BR>charging juice (said of fruits which burst with ripe-<BR>ness).<BR>—रस-भोजन, अस्, आ, अम्, feeding on<BR>liquids or fluids; (अम्), n. an entertainment given to<BR>Brāhmans in which they are feasted with the juice<BR>of mangoes.<BR>—रस-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a treatise by<BR>Bhānu-datta on the Rasas, (describing the various<BR>kinds of heroes and heroines, their feelings, passions,<BR>and peculiarities.)<BR>—रस-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed<BR>of juice or sap, consisting of fluid, juicy, liquid;<BR>savoury; consisting of quicksilver; full of taste,<BR>delightful, of great beauty, charming.<BR>—रस-मल,<BR>अम्, n. the refuse of the juices (of the body), impure<BR>excretions.<BR>—रस-महार्णव, अस्, m. ‘ocean of<BR>Rasas,’ N. of a work.<BR>—रस-मतृका, f. ‘mother<BR>of taste,’ the tongue.<BR>—रस-मात्र, अम्, n. =<BR>रस-तन्मात्र.<BR>—रस-मूला, f., N. of a Prākṛt<BR>metre consisting of four times twenty-four instants.<BR>—रस-यामल, अम्, n., N. of a medical work.<BR>—रस-योग, आस्, m. pl. scientifically mixed juices<BR>or prepared mixtures.<BR>—रस-रत्न, अम्, n. ‘jewel<BR>of Rasas,’ N. of a medical work.<BR>—रस-रत्न-<BR>दीपिका, f. and रस-रत्न-प्रदीप, अस्, m. and<BR>रस-रत्न-हार, अस्, m. and रस-रत्नाकर<BR>(˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m. and रस-रत्नावली (˚न-आव्˚),<BR>f. and रस-रहस्य, अम्, n., N. of various works<BR>treating of the Rasas and of medicine.<BR>—रस-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘king of fluids,’ quicksilver; = रसाञ्-<BR>जन.<BR>—रस-राज-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. and रस-राज-<BR>शङ्कर, and रस-राजहंस, अस्, m., N. of three<BR>medical works.<BR>—रस-लेह, अस्, m. quicksilver.<BR>—रस-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having juice or sap, full of<BR>juice, juicy, succulent; tasteful, sapid, savoury, luscious,<BR>well-seasoned, well-flavoured, strong; containing the<BR>essence (of anything); moist, well-watered; tasty,<BR>charming, elegant, graceful, beautiful; possessing<BR>love and the other Rasas; impassioned, full of feel-<BR>ing (in rhetoric applied to the poetical description of<BR>inanimate objects as affected by emotions of love and<BR>jealousy); spirited, witty; (अती), f. a kitchen; N.<BR>of an erotic poem; of a supplement to the Saṅ-<BR>kṣipta-sāra by Jūmara-nandin.<BR>—रसवत्-ता, f.<BR>juiciness, savouriness, sapidity; tastefulness; elegance,<BR>beauty, gracefulness.<BR>—रस-वर्ज, अस्, m. avoidance<BR>of tastes or flavours.<BR>—रस-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, bring-<BR>ing or producing juice.<BR>—रस-विक्रय, अस्, m. the<BR>sale of stimulating juices or liquors.<BR>—रस-विक्र-<BR>यिन्, ई, m. syrup-seller, liquor-seller, a dealer in<BR>essences or spices.<BR>—रस-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing<BR>tastes, knowing or appreciating flavours, having good<BR>taste, discriminating.<BR>—रस-विशेष, अस्, m. a more<BR>excellent juice or flavour.<BR>—रस-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the<BR>science of Rasas, alchemy.<BR>—रस-शोधन, अस्, m.<BR>borax; (अम्), n. purification of quicksilver.<BR>—रस-<BR>सङ्ग्रह-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m., N. of a medical work.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-a" target="_blank">Page0836-a+ 80</a>]<BR>—रस-सागर, अस्, m. ‘ocean of Rasas,’ N. of a<BR>work on medicine; of a work on rhetoric.<BR>—रस-<BR>सार, N. of a commentary on the second book of<BR>the Kiraṇāvalī.<BR>—रस-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, brought<BR>to perfection by means of quicksilver; skilled in<BR>alchemy; well versed in or conversant with the<BR>poetical Rasas, accomplished in poetry.<BR>—रस-सिद्-<BR>धान्त-सागर and रस-सिन्धु and रस-सुधा-<BR>कर and रस-सुधाम्भोधि (˚धा-अम्˚) and<BR>रसाकर (˚स-आक्˚), N. of various works on medi-<BR>cine or on the Rasas.<BR>—रस-सिद्धि, इस्, f. per-<BR>fection attained by means of quicksilver, knowledge<BR>of the art of performing various chemical operations<BR>with mercury which with certain mystical rites secure<BR>health and wealth to the adept; skill in alchemy.<BR>—रस-सिन्दूर, अम्, n. a sort of factitious cin-<BR>nabar made with zinc, mercury, blue vitriol, and<BR>nitre fused together.<BR>—रस-स्थान, अम्, n. cin-<BR>nabar or vermilion.<BR>—रस-हृदय, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a work on alchemy.<BR>—रसा-खन, अस्, m. ‘digging<BR>or scratching in the soil,’ a cock.<BR>—रसाग्रज (˚स-<BR>अग्˚), अम्, n. = रसाञ्जन.<BR>—रसाञ्जन (˚स-अञ्˚),<BR>अम्, n. vitriol of copper or a sort of collyrium pre-<BR>pared from it with the addition of Curcuma or<BR>(according to some) from the calx of brass with<BR>Amomum Anthorrhiza or (according to others) from<BR>lead-ore.<BR>—रसाढ्य (˚स-आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abounding in juice or sap, abounding in moisture;<BR>(अस्), m. Spondias Mangifera.<BR>—रसा-तल, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of one of the seven hells or regions under the<BR>earth, (see पाताल); the lower world or hell in general,<BR>(not to be confounded with Naraka or the place of<BR>punishment); N. of the fourth astrological mansion.<BR>—रसात्मक (˚स-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, having juice<BR>or sap for its essence, consisting of nectar; having<BR>the nature of liquid or fluid; characterized by sapi-<BR>dity or savour; having taste or flavour; having grace<BR>or elegance for its essence, elegant, beautiful.<BR>—र-<BR>सादान (˚स-आद्˚), अम्, n. the taking or drawing<BR>up of moisture, drying up or absorption of fluid,<BR>sucking, suction.<BR>—रसाधार (˚स-आध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘receptacle of fluids or moisture,’ the sun.<BR>—रसा-<BR>धारण (˚स-आध्˚), अम्, n., Ved. retention of<BR>moisture (by the sun's rays).<BR>—रसाधिक (˚स-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, full of taste, tasty, elegant,<BR>abounding in enjoyments; (अस्), m. borax; (आ), f. a<BR>species of plant.<BR>—रसाधिपत्य (˚सा-आध्˚), अम्,<BR>n. dominion over the lower world.<BR>—रसाध्यक्ष<BR>(˚स-अध्˚), अस्, m. a superintendent of liquors or<BR>fluids.<BR>—रसानुप्रदान (˚स-अन्˚), अम्, n., Ved.<BR>the bestowing of moisture, (according to Yāska one<BR>of the functions of Indra.)<BR>—रसान्तर (˚स-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. another taste or flavour; another pleasure or<BR>enjoyment; different passion or emotion, change of<BR>feeling or sentiment.<BR>—रसा-पायिन्, ई, m. ‘drinking<BR>with the tongue,’ a dog.<BR>—रसाभास (˚स-आभ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the semblance or mere appearance of senti-<BR>ment, a sentiment attributed to an inanimate object;<BR>the unsuitable manifestation of a sentiment.<BR>—रसा-<BR>भिनिवेश (˚स-अभ्˚), अस्, m. accession of sentiment,<BR>intentness of feeling or passion.<BR>—रसाभिव्यञ्जिका<BR>(˚स-अभ्˚), f., N. of a commentary.<BR>—रसाभ्यन्-<BR>तर (˚स-अभ्˚), अम्, n. inside the waters.<BR>—र-<BR>सामृत (˚स-अम्˚) and रसामृत-सिन्धु and<BR>रसाम्भोधि and रसाम्भो-निधि (˚स-अम्˚), N.<BR>of various medical works.<BR>—रसाम्ल (˚स-अम्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a kind of sorrel (= अमल-वेतस); vinegar made<BR>from fruit; sour sauce, (especially) tamarind sauce;<BR>= वृक्षामल, चुक्र.<BR>—रसायन (˚स-अय्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a particular drug used as a vermifuge (= विडङ्ग);<BR>an alchemist; N. of Garuḍa; (ई), f. a canal or chan-<BR>nel for the fluids (of the body), a vessel conveying<BR>chyle, a lacteal or absorbent vessel; N. of various<BR>plants, = गुडूची, काक-माची, महा-करञ्ज, गो-<BR>रक्ष-दुग्धा, मांस-च्छदा; (अम्), n. a medi-<BR>cine supposed to prevent old age and prolong life,<BR>an elixir, elixir vitæ; any medicine or medicinal<BR>compound; alchemy, chemistry, the employment<BR>of mercury as a remedy or for magical purposes;<BR>(according to native lexicographers also) buttermilk;<BR>poison; long pepper (?).<BR>—रसायन-फला, f. Ter-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">Page0836-b+ 81</a>]<BR>minalia Chebula or Citrina.<BR>—रसायन-श्रेष्ठ,<BR>अस्, m. ‘best of elixirs,’ mercury.<BR>—रसार्णव (˚स-<BR>अर्˚) and रसालङ्कार (˚स-अल्˚), अस्, m. two works<BR>on medicine.<BR>—रसालय (˚स-आल्˚), अस्, m. the seat<BR>or abode of the Rasas; the seat of enjoyments; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—रसावतार (˚स-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a medical work.<BR>—रसाश (˚स-आश),<BR>अस्, m. the drinking or consuming of liquors.<BR>—र-<BR>साशिन् (˚स-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, drinking or enjoying<BR>liquids.<BR>—रसाशिर् (˚स-आश्˚), ईर्, ईर्, ईर्, Ved. mixed<BR>with juice or liquid, (Sāy.) mixed with milk.<BR>—र-<BR>साश्वासा (˚स-आश्˚), f. a kind of creeper (= पलाशी).<BR>—रसास्वाद (˚स-आस्˚), अस्, m. the sipping of juices.<BR>or liquids; the perception of enjoyment, sense of<BR>joy or pleasure.<BR>—रसास्वादिन् (˚स-आस्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>tasting juice, perceiving or apprehending flavours;<BR>(ई), m. ‘juice-sipper,’ a bee.<BR>—रसाह्व (˚स-आह्˚),<BR>अस्, m. turpentine, the resin of Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—रसेन्द्र (˚स-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘chief of fluids or<BR>metals,’ quicksilver, mercury; the philosopher's stone<BR>(the touch of which turns iron to gold).<BR>—रसेन्द्र-<BR>कल्प-द्रुम, अस्, m., N. of a work by Rāma-<BR>kṛṣṇa treating of the preparation of mercury and<BR>minerals or metals for medicinal uses.<BR>—रसेन्द्र-<BR>चिन्ता-मणि, इस्, m., N. of a similar work to the<BR>above by Rāma-candra.<BR>—रसेश्वर (˚स-ईश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of fluids or metals,’ mercury, quicksilver;<BR>[cf. रसेन्द्र.]<BR>—रसेश्वर-दर्शन, अम्, n. the<BR>science of the application of mercury to various che-<BR>mical and magical operations, the doctrine of alchemy.<BR>—रसेश्वर-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m., N. of a work<BR>establishing the efficacy of mercury in alchemy.<BR>—रसोत्तम (˚स-उत्˚), अस्, m. Phaseolus Mungo,<BR>= मुद्ग; (अम्), n. (?), ‘best of liquids,’ milk.<BR>—रसोत्पत्ति (˚स-उत्˚), इस्, f. production of taste<BR>or flavour; development of passion or sentiment;<BR>generation of the vital fluids.<BR>—रसोदधि (˚स-उद्˚),<BR>इस्, m. ‘ocean of Rasas,’ N. of a rhetorical treatise on<BR>the Rasas.<BR>—रसोद्भव (˚स-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘pro-<BR>duced in water,’ a pearl.<BR>—रसोपल (˚स-उप्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘water-stone,’ a pearl.<BR>—रसोल्लास (˚स-उल्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘the spontaneous evolution of the fluids (or juices<BR>of the body, without nutriment from without),’ N.<BR>of one of the eight Siddhis or states of perfection,<BR>(also written रसोल्लासा); springing up of desire,<BR>increase of longing (for anything).<BR>—रसौकस् (˚सा-<BR>ओक्˚), आंसि, n. pl. the habitations of the lower world;<BR>(आस्, आस्, अस्), inhabiting the lower regions; (आस्), m.<BR>an inhabitant of the lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसक|रसकः
रसक, अस्, m. stewed or boiled meat, broth,<BR>soup made from meat, (also अम्, n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसत्
रसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, tasting, perceiving flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसन|रसनं|रसनः
2. रसन, अस्, m. (for 1. रसन see p. 835,<BR>col. 1), phlegm (regarded as the cause of taste to the<BR>tongue); (आ), f. the tongue; N. of two plants, =<BR>रास्ना; = गन्ध-भद्रा; (incorrectly) = रशना;<BR>(अम्), n. tasting, taste, flavour, savour; the organ of<BR>taste; the being sensible of (anything), perception,<BR>apprehension, sense.<BR>—रसना-रद, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>the tongue for teeth,’ a bird.<BR>—रसना-लिह्, ट्, m.<BR>‘licking with the tongue,’ a dog.<BR>—रसनेन्द्रिय<BR>(˚न-इन्˚), अम्, n. the organ of taste, the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसयति|रसयतिः
रसयति, इस्, f. (fr. a Nom. base रसय), taste,<BR>flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसयितव्य
रसयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be tasted, tasty,<BR>palatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसयितृ
रसयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who tastes, a taster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसयित्वा
रसयित्वा, ind. having tasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायक|रसायकः
रसायक, अस्, m. a kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाय्य
रसाय्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. a Nom. रसाय), Ved.<BR>to be made savoury or tasteful; juicy, tasteful,<BR>savoury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाल|रसालं|रसालः
रसाल, अस्, m., N. of various plants and trees,<BR>the mango tree; the sugar-cane; a kind of sugar-<BR>cane (= पुण्ड्रक); the olibanum tree; the bread-<BR>fruit tree; wheat; a kind of grain; a kind of mouse;<BR>(आ), f. curds mixed with sugar and spices; the<BR>tongue; Dūrvā grass; Desmodium Gangeticum; a<BR>vine or grape; (ई), f. a kind of sugar-cane; (अम्),<BR>n. frankincense; gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालसा
रसालसा, f. any tubular vessel of the body (espe-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">Page0836-c+ 78</a>]<BR>cially one conveying the fluids), a vein, artery; a<BR>nerve, tendon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालिहा
रसालिहा, f. Hemionitis Cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिक|रसिकः
रसिक, अस्, आ, अम्, = स-रस, tasty, savoury,<BR>flavoured, well-tasted, sapid, tasteful (as a dish, com-<BR>position, &c.), full of feeling or passion, impassioned,<BR>graceful, elegant, beautiful; spirited, witty, facetious,<BR>humourous; having a discriminating taste, apprehend-<BR>ing or appreciating flavour or excellence, appreciative;<BR>having a liking or passion for, taking pleasure in,<BR>delighting in (sometimes with loc. or at the end of<BR>a comp.); fanciful; lustful; (अस्), m. a man full of<BR>feeling or passion; a libertine; Ardea Sibirica (=<BR>सारस); a horse; an elephant; (आ), f. the juice of<BR>the sugar-cane, molasses; curds with sugar and spice;<BR>the tongue [cf. रसना]; a woman's girdle [cf.<BR>रशना].<BR>—रसिक-ता, f. tastefulness, savouriness,<BR>sapidity; taste, feeling, the having a taste for; taking<BR>pleasure in.<BR>—रसिक-रञ्जनी, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary.<BR>—रसिक-रमण, अम्, n., N. of a poem by<BR>Raghu-nātha, (it consists of eighteen chapters, and<BR>contains the life and adventures of Dur-vāsas, a<BR>Vaiṣṇava preceptor and ascetic.)<BR>—रसिका-भार्य,<BR>अस्, m. a man who has a passionate wife or one full of<BR>feeling.<BR>—रसिकेश्वर, अस्, m. (probably fr. रसिका,<BR>a passionate woman, + ईश्वर), N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
2. रसित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 835, col. 1),<BR>tasted; having taste or flavour or sentiment; covered<BR>or overlaid with gold, gilded, plated, (in this sense fr.<BR>रस, gold, + इत); (अम्), n. vinous liquor, wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितवत्
रसित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has tasted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितृ
2. रसितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, = रसयितृ, a taster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिन्
रसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having juice or sap, juicy, liquid;<BR>tasteful, spirited, full of feeling, impassioned; having<BR>good taste, having a taste for the beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्य|रस्यं
रस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, juicy, tasty, savoury, palatable;<BR>(आ), f., N. of two plants, = रास्ना; = पाठा; (अम्),<BR>n. blood (supposed to be produced from chyle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्यमान
रस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being tasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसुन|रसुनः
रसुन रसुन, अस्, m. = रसोन, लशुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोन|रसोनः
रसोन or रसोनक, अस्, m. a kind of garlic,<BR>shalote, Allium Ascalonicum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्न|रस्नं
रस्न रस्न, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 1. रस्),<BR>a thing, object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह्
रह् रह् (perhaps originally रध्), cl. 1. P.<BR>रहति, रराह, रहितुम्, cl. 10. P. रह-<BR>यति, अररहत् or अरीरहत् (?), रहयितुम्, to<BR>leave, quit, relinquish, abandon, desert, give up,<BR>surrender, resign; [cf. Gr. λανθάνω, ἔλαθον, λάθρα,<BR>ἀλήθης; (probably) ἔρημος; perhaps also λόχος,<BR>λέχος: Lat. lates; lectum, lego: Goth. ligan,<BR>lagjan: Angl. Sax. lecgan, licgan: Lith. leidmi,<BR>leidziu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह|रहः
रह, अस्, m. = 1. रहस् below.<BR>—रह-रूढ-<BR>भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, withdrawn into privacy, being<BR>private or in secret.<BR>—रह-सू, ऊस्, f., Ved. a woman<BR>bringing forth (a child) in secret, a bad woman who<BR>conceals the birth of her child.<BR>—रह-स्थ, see<BR>under 1. रहस् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहण|रहणं
रहण, अम्, n. the act of quitting, desertion,<BR>abandonment; separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहयत्
रहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, quitting, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्
1. रहस्, अस्, n. (for 2. see p. 837, col. 1), loneliness,<BR>solitariness, solitude, privacy, secrecy, retirement, (र-<BR>हसि, in secret, secretly, privily; रहस्सु, privately, in<BR>private, secretly); a lonely or deserted place, private<BR>or solitary abode, hiding-place; a secret, mystery,<BR>mystical truth; sexual intercourse, copulation; a<BR>privity; (अस्), ind. in a solitary place, in secret,<BR>secretly, clandestinely, privately, privily, (opposed to<BR>प्र-काशम्.)<BR>—रहः-स्थ or रह-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, standing or being in a lonely place or in private,<BR>being apart, being alone; being in the enjoyment of<BR>love.<BR>—रहस्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, executing a secret<BR>commission.<BR>—रही-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., or<BR>रही-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to withdraw to<BR>a solitary place, retire apart.<BR>—रही-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, withdrawn to a lonely place, retired.<BR>—रहो-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">Page0837-a+ 79</a>]<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a lonely place, being alone;<BR>secret, clandestine, concealed, private.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0836-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस
रहस in अनु-र्˚, &c. = 1. रहस्, p. 836, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहसनन्दिन्
रहसनन्दिन् or रहसानन्दिन् (?), ई, m., N.<BR>of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्य|रहस्यं
रहस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, secret, private, clandestine,<BR>concealed; mysterious; fit to be concealed; (अम्),<BR>n. a secret, any secret doctrine or mystery, anything<BR>hidden or recondite, mystical or esoteric teaching;<BR>an Upaniṣad (Manu II. 165); (अम्), ind. in secret,<BR>secretly, privately; (आ), f., N. of a river; of two<BR>plants, = रास्ना; = पाठा.<BR>—रहस्य-त्रय-सार,<BR>‘essence of the three mystical doctrines,’ N. of a<BR>treatise by Veṅkata Ācārya (being a short exposition<BR>in verse of the doctrines of the Vedānta according to<BR>Rāmānuja).<BR>—रहस्य-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, secret-<BR>possessing, being in possession of a secret or mystery,<BR>initiated into a secret rite or mystery.<BR>—रहस्य-<BR>भेद, अस्, m. or रहस्य-भेदन, अम्, n. or<BR>रहस्य-विभेद, अस्, m. revealing a secret, dis-<BR>closure of a secret or mystery.<BR>—रहस्य-व्रत, अम्,<BR>n. ‘mystical-vow,’ the mystic science of obtaining<BR>command over magical weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यु
रहस्यु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहाट|रहाटः
रहाट, अस्, m. (perhaps for रहो-ऽट), a coun-<BR>sellor, minister; a ghost, spirit; a spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहाय
रहाय (fr. रहस्), Nom. A. रहायते, &c., to<BR>be lonely or private, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहित|रहितं
रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, left, quitted, forsaken, aban-<BR>doned, deserted; lonely, solitary; deserted by, sepa-<BR>rated from, free from, deprived of, void or destitute<BR>of, without (with inst. or at the end of comps. or<BR>sometimes at the beginning, e. g. भर्त्रा-रहिता, a<BR>woman separated from her husband; रत्न-रहित<BR>or रहित-रत्न, destitute of gems); (अम्), n. pri-<BR>vacy, secrecy, (रहिते, loc. c. in secret, in privacy,<BR>secretly, privately.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहीकृ
रही-कृ, रही-भू. See under 1. रहस्, p. 836.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्
रहस् 2. रहस्, अस्, n. = रंहस्, swiftness,<BR>rapidity. (For 1. रहस् see p. 836, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहूगण
रहूगण रहूगण, आस्, m. pl., N. of a family<BR>belonging to the race of Aṅgiras; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>the author of the hymns Ṛg-veda IX. 37, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रा
रा 1. रा, cl. 2. P. (Ved. also A.) राति (-ते),<BR>ररौ, &c. (Vedic forms रासते, अरासत,<BR>रासन्, रासत् [see 2. रास्], रास्व, ररते, ररा-<BR>थाम्, ररास्व, ररीध्वम्, रिरीहि, ररे, रराथे,<BR>ररिम, ररिवस्, रासीय, Inf. रातवे), to grant,<BR>give, bestow, impart, give up, surrender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रराण
रराण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving, bountiful, (see<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 117, 24.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रा
2. रा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) grant-<BR>ing, bestowing, giving; (for रा, fem. of 2. र, see<BR>p. 824, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राका
राका, f. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 40. fr. rt.<BR>1. रा above), the goddess presiding over the actual<BR>day of full moon (or regarded as the Full Moon's<BR>consort; Anu-mati is supposed to preside over the<BR>previous day); the day of full moon, full moon; N.<BR>of a daughter of Aṅgiras and Smṛti; of a daughter<BR>of Aṅgiras and Śraddhā; of the wife of Dhātṛ and<BR>mother of Prātṛ; of a Rākṣasī, mother of Khara<BR>and Śūrpa-ṇakhā; of a daughter of Su-mālin; of a<BR>river; itch, scab; a girl in whom menstruation has<BR>just commenced.<BR>—राका-चन्द्र, अस्, m. full moon.<BR>—राका-निशा, f. the night of full moon.<BR>—राका-<BR>पति, इस्, or राका-रमण, अस्, m. ‘husband of<BR>Rākā,’ full moon.<BR>—राका-विभावरी, f. the night<BR>of full moon.<BR>—राकाविभावरी-जानि, इस्, m. ‘the<BR>consort of the night of Rākā,’ full moon.<BR>—राका-<BR>शशाङ्क, अस्, or राका-शशिन्, ई, m. full moon.<BR>—राकेन्दीवर-बन्धु (˚का-इन्˚), उस्, m. full<BR>moon.<BR>—राकेश (˚का-ईश), अस्, m. full moon; N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात
रात, अस्, आ, अम्, given (Ved. रातम् अस्तु, ‘let<BR>it be given;’ cf. Lat. ratum esto), presented, be-<BR>stowed (often at the end of comps.; cf. अस्मद्-र्˚,<BR>कीर्त्ति-र्˚, देव-र्˚, ब्रह्म-र्˚); (अस्), m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—रात-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having a ready<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">Page0837-b+ 78</a>]<BR>or willing mind, ready, willing.<BR>—रात-हविस्, इस्,<BR>इस्, इस्, Ved. one who offers oblations.<BR>—रात-हव्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who willingly presents offerings,<BR>a liberal offerer or worshipper (of the gods), one to<BR>whom the offering is presented, one who receives<BR>the oblation; (अस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi with the<BR>patronymic Ātreya (author of Ṛg-veda V. 65,<BR>66).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राति|रातिः
राति, इस्, इस् or ई, इ, Ved. ready or willing to give,<BR>generous, favourable; ready, willing; (इस्), m. a<BR>friend, (opposed to अ-राति); (इस्), f. the act of giving<BR>or granting, bestowal, presentation, favour; a gift,<BR>present, offering, oblation; इन्द्रस्य रातिः, N. of<BR>a Sāman.<BR>—राति-षाच्, क्, क्, क् (षाच् for साच्), Ved.<BR>granting favours, dispensing gifts, liberal, bountiful,<BR>generous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावन्
रावन्, आ, m., Ved. a giver, bestower; [cf. अ-र्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राउल
राउल राüल, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राकिणी
राकिणी राकिणी, f., N. of a Tantra goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्य
राक्य राक्य, अस्, &c., coming or descended<BR>from Raka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस राक्षस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. रक्षस्,<BR>q. v.), of or belonging to a Rakṣas or evil demon,<BR>like a Rakṣas, demoniacal, infested by demons;<BR>(scil. विवाह or विधि) one of the eight forms of<BR>marriage (the violent seizure and rape of a girl after<BR>the defeat or destruction of her relatives, see Manu<BR>III. 33); (अस्), m. an evil being or demon, an evil<BR>or malignant spirit, a Rakṣas, (the Rākṣasas are<BR>sometimes regarded as produced from Brahmā's<BR>foot, sometimes with Rāvaṇa as descendants of<BR>Pulastya; elsewhere they are styled children of<BR>Khasā or Su-rasā; according to some they are dis-<BR>tinguishable into three classes, one sort being of a<BR>semi-divine nature and ranking with Yakṣas &c.,<BR>another corresponding to Titans or relentless enemies<BR>of the gods, and a third answering more to demons,<BR>imps, fiends, goblins, going about at night, haunting<BR>cemeteries, disturbing sacrifices and devout men,<BR>animating dead bodies, ensnaring and even devouring<BR>human beings, and generally hostile to the human<BR>race; this last class is the one most commonly de-<BR>noted by the term Rakṣas or Rākṣasa; their place<BR>of abode, according to the Rāmāyaṇa, was Laṅkā in<BR>Ceylon, where resided their chief, Rāvaṇa, q. v.; in<BR>Rāmāyaṇa V. 10, 17, &c. they are fully described;<BR>some have long arms, some are fat, others thin, some<BR>dwarfish, others enormously tall and humpbacked,<BR>some have only one eye, others only one ear, some<BR>enormous paunches, others projecting teeth and<BR>crooked thighs, while others can assume noble forms<BR>and are beautiful to look upon; they are further<BR>described as biped, triped, quadruped, with heads of<BR>serpents, donkeys, horses, elephants, and every ima-<BR>ginable deformity; cf. 2. रक्षस्); a king of the<BR>Rākṣasas; (with Jainas) one of the eight classes of<BR>Vyantaras; epithet of the thirtieth Muhūrtha; one<BR>of the astronomical Yogas or divisions of the moon's<BR>path; N. of a minister of Nanda; of a poet; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. epithet of the forty-ninth year in the<BR>Jupiter cycle of sixty years; (ई), f. a Rākṣasa<BR>female, Rākṣasī or female demon; the island of<BR>the Rākṣasas, i. e. Laṅkā or Ceylon; epithet of<BR>a malignant spirit supposed to haunt one of the<BR>four corners of a house; night; a kind of perfume<BR>(= चण्डा); a large tooth, tusk.<BR>—राक्षस-काव्य,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a poem.<BR>—राक्षस-ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>‘Rākṣasa-demon,’ epithet of a particular kind of<BR>insanity or seizure (produced by evil spirits).<BR>—राक्-<BR>षस-ता, f. or राक्षस-त्व, अम्, n. fiendishness,<BR>the state or condition of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—राक्षसा-<BR>लय (˚स-आल्˚), अस्, m. abode of the Rākṣasas.<BR>—राक्षसी-करण, अस्, m. the act of changing<BR>into a Rākṣasa.<BR>—राक्षसी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>become or changed into a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षा
राक्षा राक्षा, f. (sometimes written रक्षा),<BR>= लाक्षा, lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षोघ्न
राक्षोघ्न राक्षोघ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, treating of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-c" target="_blank">Page0837-c+ 80</a>]<BR>or relating to the slayer of a Rakṣas; अगस्त्यस्य<BR>राक्षोघ्नम् and अग्ने राक्षोघ्नम्, N. of two<BR>Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षोसुर
राक्षोऽसुर, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or treating<BR>of a Rakṣas and Asura; containing the words रक्-<BR>षस् and असुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राख्
राख् राख् [cf. rt. लाख्], cl. 1. P. राखति,<BR>&c., Caus. Aor. अरराखत्, to be arid or<BR>dry; to adorn; to suffice, be able or competent; to<BR>impede, prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राग|रागः
राग राग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. रञ्ज्), the act of<BR>colouring or dyeing, tinting [cf. मूर्धज-र्˚];<BR>colour, hue, tint, dye, red colour, (sometimes at the<BR>end of an adj. comp., e. g. कृमि-राग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>red as cochineal, dyed with cochineal); affection,<BR>emotion, passion, feeling; a musical mode, (six pri-<BR>mary modes or orders of sounds are enumerated,<BR>viz. भैरव, कौशिक, हिन्दोल, दीपक, श्री-<BR>राग, and मेघ; or श्री-राग, वसन्त, पञ्-<BR>चम, भैरव, मेघ, and नत-नारायण;<BR>or मालव, मल्लार, श्री-राग, वसन्त, हिल्-<BR>लोल, and कर्णाट: these six Rāgas or modes are<BR>supposed to have been originally connected with the<BR>six Ṛtus or seasons, each mode, like the several<BR>seasons, moving some Rāga or affection of the mind;<BR>they are personified, and each of the six is wedded to<BR>five consorts, called Rāgiṇīs, and is the father of eight<BR>sons; sometimes six Rāgiṇīs are assigned to each<BR>Rāga); a musical note, harmony, music; the quality<BR>Rajas, q. v.; feeling or mental affection in general,<BR>love, sympathy, interest in anything, joy, pleasure;<BR>vehement longing or desire; regret, sorrow; greedi-<BR>ness, envy; anger, wrath; loveliness, beauty, charm,<BR>attraction; nasalization; N. of a particular process in<BR>the preparation of quicksilver; a king, prince; the<BR>sun; the moon; (आ), f. Eleusine Coracana, a sort of<BR>grain (commonly called Rāggy, much cultivated in<BR>the south of India); N. of the second daughter of<BR>Aṅgiras; [cf. according to some, Gr. ὀργή, perhaps<BR>for ῥογή.]<BR>—राग-खाडव, see राग-षाडव.<BR>—राग-खाण्डव, अम्, n. a kind of sweetmeat;<BR>[cf. राग-षाडव.]<BR>—राग-खाण्डविक, अस्, m. a<BR>maker of the above sort of sweetmeat.<BR>—राग-<BR>चूर्ण, अस्, m. Acacia Catechu (a tree yielding an<BR>astringent resin, the wood of which is used in dye-<BR>ing); a red powder (which the Hindūs throw over<BR>each other at the vernal festival called Holi; cf.<BR>होलाका); red lead; lac; Kāma-deva, the god of<BR>love.<BR>—राग-च्छन्न, अस्, m. the god of love or<BR>Kāma-deva; N. of Rāma.<BR>—राग-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>colour-giving, colouring, passion-inspiring; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of shrub, = तैरणी; (आ), f. ‘producing<BR>various colours,’ crystal.<BR>—राग-द्रव्य, अम्, n.<BR>‘colour-substance,’ paint, dye.<BR>—राग-पट्ट, a kind<BR>of precious stone.<BR>—राग-पुष्प, अस्, m. Penta-<BR>petes Phœnicea; the red globe-amaranth; (ई), f.<BR>the Chinese rose.<BR>—राग-प्रसव, अस्, m. Penta-<BR>petes Phœnicea; the red globe-amaranth.<BR>—राग-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. the connection of the Rāgas, ex-<BR>pression or manifestation of affection, affection,<BR>passion.<BR>—राग-बन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, exciting or<BR>inflaming the passions.<BR>—राग-भञ्जन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Vidyā-dhara.<BR>—राग-मञ्जरिका, f. a dimi-<BR>nutive from राग-मञ्जरी below (‘wicked Rāga-<BR>mañjarī’).<BR>—राग-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—राग-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘consisting of colour or<BR>of red colour,’ red-coloured, red; dear, beloved.<BR>—राग-माला, f. ‘string or series of musical Rāgas,’<BR>a chapter on the subject of musical Rāgas; N. of a<BR>work on the musical Rāgas by Kṣema-karṇa.<BR>—राग-युज्, क्, m. a ruby.<BR>—राग-रज्जु, उस्, m.<BR>Kāma-deva, the god of love.<BR>—राग-लता, f. ‘Pas-<BR>sion-creeper, Passion-flower,’ N. of Rati (wife of<BR>Kāma-deva).<BR>—राग-लेखा, f. a streak or line of<BR>paint, stroke, the mark of dye.<BR>—राग-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having colour, coloured, red; impassioned.<BR>—रा-<BR>ग-विबोध, अस्, m., N. of a celebrated treatise on<BR>the musical Rāgas and theory of music.<BR>—राग-<BR>वृन्त, अस्, m. ‘Passion-stalk,’ N. of Kāma-deva,<BR>the god of love.<BR>—राग-षाडव, अस्, m. a sweet-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-a" target="_blank">Page0838-a+ 79</a>]<BR>meat made from grapes and pomegranates together<BR>with a kind of broth made from Phaseolus Mungo;<BR>(according to others) half ripe mango fruit made<BR>into syrup with ginger, cardamoms, oil, butter, &c.,<BR>(also written राग-खाडव, राग-षाढव; cf.<BR>राग-खाण्डव.)<BR>—राग-सूत्र, अम्, n. any<BR>coloured thread or string; a silk thread; the string<BR>of a balance.<BR>—रागाङ्गी (˚ग-अङ्˚) or रागाढ्या<BR>(˚ग-आढ्˚), f. Rubia Munjista (= मञ्जिष्ठा).<BR>—रागात्मक (˚ग-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, composed<BR>of or characterized by passion, impassioned.<BR>—रागा-<BR>नुगाविवृति (˚ग-अन्˚), इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—रा-<BR>गान्ध (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blind with passion<BR>or desire.<BR>—रागान्वित (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>colour or dye, coloured; affected by passion or<BR>desire.<BR>—रागायात (˚ग-आय्˚), अम्, n. excess of<BR>passion, the coming on or uprising of excessive<BR>passion.<BR>—रागार्णव (˚ग-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work on the musical Rāgas.<BR>—रागार्ह (˚ग-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of affection, any suitable object<BR>of affection.<BR>—रागाशनि (˚ग-अश्˚), इस्, m. a Bud-<BR>dha; a Jina.<BR>—रागोद्रेक (˚ग-उद्˚), अस्, m. excess<BR>of passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0837-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागदालि|रागदालिः
रागदालि, इस्, m. a kind of lentil (= मसूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागारु|रागारुः
रागारु, उस्, उस्, उ, one who raises hopes of a gift<BR>which he afterwards disappoints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिन्
रागिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. rt. रञ्ज् and fr. राग),<BR>coloured, dyed, painted, having a particular colour<BR>(applied to a kind of Amaurosis or blindness when<BR>it affects the second membrane of the eye, as opposed<BR>to अ-रागिन्, which affects the first); red, of a red<BR>colour; full of passion or feeling; impassioned,<BR>labouring under emotion, given up to passion; full<BR>of love, loving, affectionate, warm, susceptible, in<BR>love; passionately fond of, devotedly attached to,<BR>taking great pleasure in (with loc. or at the end of<BR>a comp.), eagerly desirous of, having great taste or<BR>relish for (anything); colouring, painting, dyeing;<BR>rejoicing, delighting, gladdening, exhilarating; (ई),<BR>m. a painter; a lover; a lustful man, libertine; a<BR>sort of grain (= बहुतर-कणिश); (इणी), f. a<BR>modification of the musical mode called Rāga, (thirty<BR>or thirty-six Ragiṇīs are enumerated, either five or<BR>six being assigned to each Rāga and personified as<BR>his wives); a wanton and intriguing woman; N. of<BR>the eldest daughter of Menakā; a form of Lakṣmī.<BR>—रागि-ता, f. the state of being coloured or impas-<BR>sioned, affectionateness, tenderness, fondness for,<BR>longing after, eager desire for (with loc. or at the<BR>end of comps.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघ्
राघ् 1. राघ् [cf. rt. लाघ्], cl. 1. A. रा-<BR>घते, रराघे, राघितुम्, to be able or<BR>competent: Caus. राघयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अर-<BR>राघत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघ्
2. राघ्, राक्, m. an able or efficient person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघव|राघवः
राघव राघव, अस्, m. (fr. रघु), a de-<BR>scendant of Raghu; a patronymic of Aja; of Daśa-<BR>ratha; (especially) of Rāma-candra; of a more<BR>recent king (author of the Hasta-ratnāvalī); of the<BR>author of the Gaṇeśa-stuti hymn; of a serpent-<BR>demon; sea, ocean; a species of large fish; (औ),<BR>m. du. the two Rāghavas, i. e. Rāma and Lakṣ-<BR>maṇa.<BR>—राघव-चैतन्य, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—राघव-देव, अस्, m., N. of a poet; of the<BR>father of Dāmodara and grandfather of Śārṅgadhara;<BR>of the author of the Laghu-cintana.<BR>—राघव-<BR>पाण्डवीय, अम्, n., N. of an artificial poem by<BR>Kavi-rāja giving a narrative of the acts of both<BR>Rāghavas and Pāṇḍavas in such a way that it may<BR>be interpreted either as a history of one or the other<BR>family.<BR>—राघव-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—रा-<BR>घवानन्द (˚व-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Hari-nanda; of the author of the Nyāyāvalī-dīdhiti;<BR>of the author of a commentary on the Mānava-<BR>dharma-śāstra.<BR>—राघवानुज-ग (˚व-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, referring to the younger brother of Rāma.<BR>—राघवाभ्युदय (˚व-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘rise of<BR>Rāma,’ N. of a drama.<BR>—राघवायण (˚व-<BR>अय्˚), अम्, n. Rāma's history, i. e. the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">Page0838-b+ 78</a>]<BR>—राघवेन्द्र (˚व-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘Rāghava-chief,’<BR>N. of several persons.<BR>—राघवेश्वर (˚व-ईश्˚),<BR>‘Rāghava-lord,’ N. of one of Śiva's Liṅgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघवीय
राघवीय, अम्, n. the work composed by Rā-<BR>ghava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कल|रांकलः|राङ्कलः
राङ्कल राङ्कल, अस्, m. a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कव|रांकव|राङ्कवं
राङ्कव राङ्कव, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the<BR>Raṅku species of deer; made from the hair of the<BR>Raṅku deer, woollen; coming from Raṅku (said of<BR>animals, see Pāṇ. IV. 2, 100); (अम्), n. woollen<BR>cloth made of deer's hair, a woollen cover or gar-<BR>ment; a rug, blanket.<BR>—राङ्कवाजिन (˚व-अज्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a woollen skin.<BR>—राङ्कवास्तरण (˚व-<BR>आस्˚), अम्, n. a woollen coverlet.<BR>—राङ्कवास्तृत<BR>(˚व-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, covered with a woollen rug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कवक
राङ्कवक, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from Raṅku<BR>(said of men, see Pāṇ. IV. 2, 100).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कवायण
राङ्कवायण, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from Raṅku<BR>(said of animals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्ग
राङ्ग राङ्ग, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्गण|राङ्गणं
राङ्गण राङ्गण, अम्, n. a kind of flower<BR>(commonly called Raṅgan).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राचित
राचित राचित, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Racita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राचितायन
राचितायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Rācita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
राज् 1. राज् (perhaps connected with rt.<BR>ऋज्, originally रज्), cl. 1. P. A. (in Ved.<BR>only P.) राजति, -ते (Ved. also cl. 2. राष्टि, अराड्),<BR>रराज (2nd sing. रराजिथ or रेजिथ, 3rd pl.<BR>रराजुः or रेजुः), रराजे or रेजे, राजितुम् (Ved.<BR>राजसे), to reign, rule, exercise sovereignty, to be a<BR>king or sovereign, to be the first or chief (of any-<BR>thing); to rule over (with gen.); to govern, direct<BR>(with acc.); to be illustrious or eminent; to shine,<BR>glitter, glisten, be radiant or splendid; to appear as:<BR>Caus. राजयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरराजत्, to reign,<BR>rule; to illuminate, make radiant: Desid. रिराजि-<BR>षति, -ते: Intens. राराज्यते, रारष्टि; [cf. Lat.<BR>rego, di-rigo, rex; Goth. ragino, reikja (=<BR>राज्य), reik-s, ‘a chief;’ Old Germ. rîchi.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
2. राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, shining, radiant (at the end of<BR>comps.); (ट्), m. = राजन्, a king, sovereign, chief;<BR>any principal object or anything the best of its kind<BR>[cf. शङ्ख-राज्]; N. of an Ekāha; a metre of<BR>four times twenty-two syllables; (ट्), f., Ved., N. of<BR>a goddess; (according to Mahī-dhara) = राज्य, a<BR>kingdom; [cf. Lat. rex; Goth. reiks.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज|राजः
राज, अस्, m. (at the end of a comp.) = राजन्, a<BR>king, prince, sovereign, chief; any principal object<BR>or anything the best of its kind; [cf. व्यूह-र्˚; at<BR>the end of an adj. comp. the fem. ends in आ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजक|राजकं|राजकः
राजक, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminating, irradiating,<BR>splendid; (अस्), m. a little king, petty prince; =<BR>राजन् (often at the end of an adj. comp.); N.<BR>of various persons; (अम्), n. a number of kings or<BR>sovereigns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकीय|राजकीयः
राजकीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. राजक), of or belonging<BR>to a king, kingly, princely, royal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत्
राजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, ruling; shining, (an ano-<BR>malous form राजतम् for राजन्तम् is given.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्
राजन्, आ, m. (for fem. राज्ञी see p. 840, col. 3), a<BR>king, sovereign, prince, ruler, chief, governor, (at the<BR>end of an adj. comp. the fem. may be formed in<BR>three ways, viz. either like the masc. or fr. राज, and<BR>declined like the fem. of शिव, or with राज्ञी de-<BR>clined like नदी, e. g. बहु-राजन्, having many<BR>kings, makes its fem. sing. du. either बहु-राजा,<BR>राजानौ or बहु-राजा, -राजे or बहु-राज्ञी, -रा-<BR>ज्ञ्यौ, see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 28; sometimes राजन् is found at<BR>the end of a comp. where राज would be more correct;<BR>cf. नाग-राजन्, काशि-र्˚); a man of the military<BR>caste, Kṣatriya, a man of the royal tribe (= राज-<BR>न्य); N. of Yudhi-ṣṭhira; a master; the moon;<BR>Indra; a Yakṣa; N. of one of the eighteen attend-<BR>ants on Sūrya (identified with a form of Guha);<BR>government, guidance, (this is said to be the sense<BR>in only one passage, Ṛg-veda X. 49, 4; according<BR>to Sāy. राजनि = राजनार्थम्.)<BR>—राज-ऋषि =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-c" target="_blank">Page0838-c+ 80</a>]<BR>राजर्षि.<BR>—राज-कथा, f. a history of kings, royal<BR>history.<BR>—राज-कदम्ब, अस्, m. ‘royal Kadamba,’<BR>a sort of Kadamba.<BR>—राज-कन्दर्प, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—राज-कन्यका or राज-कन्या, f. a<BR>king's daughter, princess.<BR>—राज-कर, अस्, m.<BR>king's tax, tribute paid to a king, royal tribute or<BR>taxes.<BR>—राज-कर्कटी, f. a kind of cucumber (=<BR>चीनाकर्कटी.).<BR>—राज-कर्ण, अस्, m. an elephant's<BR>tusk.<BR>—राज-कर्तृ, ता, m. ‘king-maker,’ one who<BR>assists at the coronation of a king; (तारस्), m. pl.<BR>those who place the king on the throne.<BR>—राज-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. the business or duty of a king; any<BR>service performed for a king, royal service; the<BR>Soma ceremony; (आणि), n. pl. royal or state affairs.<BR>—राज-कलश, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राज-कला,<BR>f. the sixteenth part of the moon's disk, a crescent<BR>of the moon.<BR>—राज-कलि, इस्, m. a bad king who<BR>does not protect his subjects.<BR>—राज-कशेरु, उस्, m.<BR>a fragrant grass, Cyperus Rotundus; (उ), n. the root<BR>of Cyperus Pertenuis.<BR>—राज-कार्य, अम्, n. a<BR>king's duty or business, state affairs.<BR>—राज-कुञ्-<BR>जर, अस्, m. ‘an elephant among kings,’ a great or<BR>powerful monarch.<BR>—राज-कुमार, अस्, m. a king's<BR>son, prince.<BR>—राज-कुमारिका, f. a king's daughter,<BR>princess.<BR>—राज-कुल, अम्, n. a king's family, royal<BR>family; the court of a king; a court of justice; a<BR>royal palace.<BR>—राजकुल-भट्ट, अस्, m. any learned<BR>man attached to a royal household.<BR>—राज-कुल्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of royal race, of regal descent.<BR>—राज-कुष्-<BR>माण्ड, अस्, m. Solanum Melongena.<BR>—राज-कृत्,<BR>त्, m. = राज-कर्तृ.<BR>—राज-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>or performed by a king.<BR>—राज-कृत-प्रतिज्ञ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has fulfilled the king's conditions.<BR>—राज-कृत्य, अम्, n. king's duty or business,<BR>state affairs.<BR>—राज-कृत्वन् = राज-कर्तृ (followed<BR>by an acc., Bhaṭṭi-k. VI. 130).<BR>—राज-कोशातक,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of fruit.<BR>—राज-क्रय, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>purchase of Soma.<BR>—राज-क्रिया, f. the business of<BR>a king, royal or state affairs.<BR>—राज-क्षवक, अस्<BR>m. a kind of mustard.<BR>—राज-खर्जूरी, f. a kind<BR>of date tree (= नृप-प्रिया).<BR>—राज-गण, अस्, m.<BR>a host of kings.<BR>—राज-गवी, f. Bos Grunniens.<BR>—राज-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going to the king or<BR>ruler, devolving or escheating to the sovereign (as<BR>property &c. to which there are no heirs).<BR>—राज-<BR>गिरि, इस्, m. ‘king's hill,’ N. of a place; a species of<BR>vegetable (= राजाद्रि).<BR>—राज-गुरु, उस्, m. a king's<BR>minister, royal counsellor.<BR>—राज-गुह्य, अम्, n. a<BR>royal mystery.<BR>—राज-गृह, अस्, m. a king's house,<BR>royal dwelling, palace; N. of the chief city in Ma-<BR>gadha (said to be nine Yojanas distant from Pāṭali-<BR>putra); (अस्, आ, अम्), belonging to the city Rāja-gṛha.<BR>—राज-गृहक, अस्, आ, अम्, of or belonging to the<BR>city Rāja-gṛha.<BR>—राज-गेह, अस्, m. = राज-गृह,<BR>a palace.<BR>—राज-ग्रीव, अस्, m. a species of fish.<BR>—रा-<BR>ज-घ, अस्, m. a king-killer, regicide; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>sharp, hot.<BR>—राज-चिह्न, अम्, n. a mark or sign of<BR>royalty, insignia of royalty, regalia.<BR>—राज-चिह्नक,<BR>अम्, n. the organs of generation (= उप-स्थ).<BR>—राज-जक्ष्मन् for राज-यक्ष्मन्, q. v.<BR>—रा-<BR>ज-जम्बू, ऊस्, f. a species of Jambū; a species of<BR>date tree.<BR>—राज-तनय, अस्, m. a king's son,<BR>prince; (आ), f. a king's daughter, princess.<BR>—राज-<BR>तरङ्गिणी, f. ‘stream or current history of kings,’<BR>N. of a celebrated history of the kings of Kaśmīra<BR>or Cashmere by Kalhaṇa (written A.D. 1148).<BR>—राज-तरु, उस्, m. Cathartocarpus or Cassia Fis-<BR>tula; Pterospermum Acerifolium.<BR>—राज-तरुणी,<BR>f., N. of a plant, the globe-amaranth.<BR>—राज-तस्,<BR>ind. from a king.<BR>—राज-ता, f. or राज-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>kingship, royalty, the rank or function of a king,<BR>sovereignty, princedom, kingly dignity or authority,<BR>government.<BR>—राज-ताल, अस्, m. or राज-ताली, f. a<BR>betel-nut tree; (अस्), m., N. of a particular measure<BR>or time in music.<BR>—राज-तिमिष, अस्, m. Cucumis<BR>Sativus.<BR>—राज-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—राज-तुङ्ग, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राज-तेमि-<BR>ष, अस्, m. = राज-तिमिष. — राज-दण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>a king's sceptre, kingly authority, punishment in-<BR>flicted by a king; fine payable to a king.<BR>—राज-<BR>दत्ता, f. a proper N.<BR>—राज-दन्त, अस्, m. a prin-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0839-a" target="_blank">Page0839-a+ 81</a>]<BR>cipal tooth, front tooth; a proper N.<BR>—राजदन्ति,<BR>इस्, m. a patronymic from Rāja-danta.<BR>—राज-दर्-<BR>शन, अम्, n. the act of seeing or appearing before<BR>a king, a royal audience; N. of a kind of artificial<BR>composition.<BR>—राज-दार, आस्, m. pl. a king's wife,<BR>royal consort; the wives of a king.<BR>—राज-दुहितृ,<BR>ता, f. a king's daughter, princess.<BR>—राज-दूत, अस्,<BR>m. a king's ambassador.<BR>—राज-दूर्वा, f. a kind of<BR>high-growing Dūrvā grass.<BR>—राज-दृषद्, त्, f.,<BR>N. of the larger or lower mill-stone.<BR>—राज-देव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a lexicographer (= भोज-राज-देव).<BR>—राज-द्रुम, अस्, m. = राज-वृक्ष.<BR>—राज-<BR>द्रोह, अस्, m. ‘the act of injuring a king,’ high trea-<BR>son, rebellion.<BR>—राज-द्रोहिन्, ई, m. ‘king-injurer,’<BR>a traitor, rebel.<BR>—राज-द्वार्, र्, f. or राज-द्वार,<BR>अम्, n. the king's gate, gate of a royal palace.<BR>—राज-द्वारिक, अस्, m. a royal porter or gate-<BR>keeper.<BR>—राज-धत्तूर or राज-धत्तूरक, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of thorn-apple.<BR>—राज-धर्म, अस्, m.<BR>a king's duty; (आस्), m. pl. royal duties, rules or<BR>laws relating to kings.<BR>—राजधर्म-कौस्तुभ,<BR>N. of a part of the Smṛti-kaustubha.<BR>—राज-धर्-<BR>मन्, आ, m., N. of the king of the cranes or herons<BR>(a son of Kaśyapa, Mahā-bh. Śānti-p. 6337).<BR>—रा-<BR>जधर्मानुशासन (˚म-अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘instruc-<BR>tion in the duties of kings,’ N. of the first section of<BR>the Śānti-p. of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—राज-धान or<BR>राज-धानक, अम्, n. or राज-धानिका, or राज-<BR>धानी, f. a royal city, metropolis, capital, a king's<BR>residence, palace.<BR>—राज-धान्य, अम्, n. ‘royal<BR>grain,’ Panicum Frumentaceum; a kind of rice.<BR>—राज-धामन्, अ, n. a king's residence, royal<BR>palace.<BR>—राज-धीर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राज-<BR>धुर, अस्, m. or राज-धुरा, f. ‘king's yoke,’ the<BR>burden of government.<BR>—राज-धुस्तूरक or राज-<BR>धूर्त, अस्, m. a species of large Datura or thorn-<BR>apple.<BR>—राज-नगरी, f. a royal city.<BR>—राज-नन्-<BR>दन, अस्, m. a king's son, prince.<BR>—राज-नय,<BR>अस्, m. royal conduct or policy, the administration<BR>of government, politics.<BR>—राज-नापित, अस्, m. a<BR>royal barber, a first-rate barber.<BR>—राज-नामन्, आ,<BR>m. Trichosanthes Diœca.<BR>—राज-निघण्टु, उस्, or<BR>राज-निघण्ट, अस्, m., N. of a dictionary of materia<BR>medica (including many herbs and plants) by Hara-<BR>hari-paṇḍita, (also written राज-निर्घण्ट.)<BR>—राज-<BR>निर्धूत-दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has under-<BR>gone punishment from a king.<BR>—राज-निवेशन,<BR>अम्, n. a king's abode, palace.<BR>—राज-नीति, इस्, f.<BR>royal conduct or policy, the administration of govern-<BR>ment, statesmanship, politics.<BR>—राज-नील, अम्, n.<BR>an emerald.<BR>—राजन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (anomalous for<BR>राज-वत्, see Pāṇ. VIII. 2, 14), having a good<BR>king, governed by a just monarch (Raghu-v. VI.<BR>22).<BR>—राज-पटोल or राज-पटोलक, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of cucumber, Trichosanthes Diœca; (ई), f. =<BR>मधुर-पटोली (?).<BR>—राज-पट्ट, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of precious stone, a diamond of inferior quality (said<BR>to be brought from Virāṭa-deśa in the north-west of<BR>India); a royal fillet or tiara.<BR>—राज-पट्टिका, f. =<BR>चातक-पक्षिन्.<BR>—राज-पति, इस्, m. a lord of<BR>kings.<BR>—राज-पत्नी, f. a king's wife, royal consort,<BR>queen.<BR>—राज-पथ, अस्, m. the king's highway, a<BR>main road, public road, principal street.<BR>—राज-प-<BR>थाय, Nom. A. -पथायते, &c., to represent or<BR>be like a main road.<BR>—राज-पद, अम्, n. the rank<BR>of a king, kingship.<BR>—राज-पद्धति, इस्, f. a main<BR>road, principal street.<BR>—राज-पर्णी, f. Pæderia<BR>Fœtida.<BR>—राज-पलाण्डु, उस्, m. a particular kind<BR>of onion.<BR>—राज-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a king; of a<BR>royal family.<BR>—राज-पितृ, ता, m. a king's father.<BR>—राज-पीलु, उस्, m. a species of tree (= महा-<BR>पीलु).<BR>—राज-पुत्र, अस्, m. a king's son, prince;<BR>a Kṣatriya or man of the military tribe (in the<BR>Hindū caste system); the son of a Vaiśya by an<BR>Ambaṣṭhā or the son of a Kṣatriya by a Karaṇī;<BR>a Rājpoot (the name of a class of persons who claim<BR>descent from the ancient Kṣatriyas); the planet<BR>Mercury (regarded as the son of the moon); a kind<BR>of mango; (ई), f. a king's daughter, princess; a<BR>female of the Rājpoot tribe; N. of several plants, a<BR>bitter gourd (= काटु-तुम्बी); a kind of jasmine<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0839-b" target="_blank">Page0839-b+ 81</a>]<BR>(= जाती, मालती); a kind of perfume (= रेणुका);<BR>a kind of metal (= राज-रीति); a musk-rat; (आ), f.,<BR>Ved. ‘having kings for sons,’ a mother of kings.<BR>—राज-पुत्रक, अम्, n. a number of king's sons,<BR>assemblage of princes.<BR>—राज-पुत्रिका, f. a kings<BR>daughter, princess; a species of bird (= शरारि).<BR>—राज-पुत्रीय, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—राज-पुर,<BR>अम्, n. a royal city, the residence of a king; N. of a<BR>city; (ई), f., N. of a city.<BR>—राज-पुरुष, अस्, m. a<BR>royal servant or attendant; a king's minister.<BR>—राज-<BR>पुष्प, अस्, m. Mesua Roxburghii; (ई), f. a species<BR>of plant (= करुणी).<BR>—राज-पूग, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of Areca or betel-nut palm.<BR>—राज-पूरुष, अस्, m.<BR>= राज-पुरुष above.<BR>—राज-पौरुषिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, being in a king's service.<BR>—राज-पौरुष्य,<BR>अम्, n. (fr. राज-पुरुष), the state of a royal<BR>servant, the being a king's minister.<BR>—राज-प्र-<BR>कृति, इस्, f. a king's minister.<BR>—राज-प्रदेय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, to be given or presented to a king.<BR>—राज-<BR>प्रसाद, अस्, m. royal favour.<BR>—राज-प्रिय, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of onion; (आ), f. a species of plant (=<BR>करुणी).<BR>—राज-प्रेष्य, अस्, m. a king's servant;<BR>(अम्), n. royal service, service of kings, (more cor-<BR>rectly राज-प्रैष्य.)<BR>—राज-फणिज्झक, अस्,<BR>m. an orange tree.<BR>—राज-फल, अम्, n. ‘royal<BR>fruit,’ the fruit of Trichosanthes Diœca; (अस्), m.<BR>‘bearing royal fruit,’ a species of tree, = राजादनी;<BR>(आ), f. Eugenia Jambolana.<BR>—राज-बदर, अस्, m.<BR>a species of jujube tree; (अम्), n. a sort of Justicia<BR>plant; salt.<BR>—राज-बन्ध, अस्, m. imprisonment by<BR>the king.<BR>—राज-बला, f. Pæderia Fœtida.<BR>—राज-<BR>बान्धव, अस्, m. a relation of a king, royal rela-<BR>tion; (ई), f. a female relation of a king.<BR>—राज-<BR>भट, अस्, m. a king's soldier, soldier of the royal<BR>army.<BR>—राज-भट्टिका, f. a species of water-fowl.<BR>—राज-भद्रक, अस्, m. Costus Speciosus or Ara-<BR>bicus; Azadirachta Indica.<BR>—राज-भय, अम्, n.<BR>king's risk, danger from a king, fear of a king.<BR>—राज-भवन, अम्, n. a king's abode, royal<BR>palace.<BR>—राज-भार्या, f. a king's wife, queen.<BR>—राज-भूय, अम्, n. = राज-ता, royalty, &c.<BR>—राज-भृत्, see Gaṇa Saṅkalādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2,<BR>75.<BR>—राज-भृत, अस्, आ, अम्, hired by the king,<BR>being in the king's service; (अस्), m. a king's soldier.<BR>—राज-भृत्य, अस्, m. a servant of a king, royal<BR>servant or minister, courtier, any public officer.<BR>—रा-<BR>ज-भोग, अस्, m. a king's meal, royal repast.<BR>—राज-<BR>भोगीन, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for a king's enjoyment,<BR>suitable for a king's use.<BR>—राज-भोग्य, अस्, m.<BR>Buchanalia Latifolia; (अम्), n. nutmeg.<BR>—राज-भो-<BR>जन, अस्, आ, अम्, eaten by kings.<BR>—राज-भौत,<BR>अस्, m. a king's fool or jester.<BR>—राज-भ्रातृ, ता,<BR>m. a king's brother.<BR>—राज-मणि, इस्, m. ‘royal<BR>gem,’ a kind of precious stone.<BR>—राज-मण्डूक,<BR>अस्, m. a species of large frog.<BR>—राज-मन्त्र-धर,<BR>अस्, m. a king's counsellor, royal minister.<BR>—राज-<BR>मन्त्रिन्, ई, m. a minister of state.<BR>—राज-मन्-<BR>दिर, अम्, n. the palace of a king, a royal mansion;<BR>N. of the chief town of Kaliṅga.<BR>—राज-मल्ल,<BR>अस्, m. a royal wrestler.<BR>—राज-महिल, N. of a<BR>town.<BR>—राज-महेन्द्र-तीर्थ (˚हा-इन्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—राज-मातृ, ता, f. a king's mother.<BR>—राज-मात्र, अम्, n., Ved. every one claiming<BR>the name of Rājan.<BR>—राज-मानुष, अस्, m. a<BR>royal officer or minister, any public officer.<BR>—राज-<BR>मार्ग, अस्, m. the king's highway, a royal or main<BR>road, high road, high street, principal street (one<BR>passable for horses and elephants); the way or<BR>method of kings, procedure of kings (as warfare<BR>&c.).<BR>—राज-मार्तण्ड, N. of a commentary by<BR>Bhoja-deva on Patañjali's Yoga-sūtras.<BR>—राज-मा-<BR>ष, अस्, m. a kind of bean, Dolichos Catjang.<BR>—राज-माष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, suited to the cultiva-<BR>tion of Rāja-māṣa, consisting of or sown with this<BR>plant (as a field &c.).<BR>—राज-मुद्ग, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of bean.<BR>—राज-मुद्रा, f. a royal signet or seal.<BR>—राज-मुनि, इस्, m. = राजर्षि.<BR>—राज-मृ-<BR>गाङ्क (˚ग-अङ्˚), N. of a particular medicinal com-<BR>pound; of an astronomical work.<BR>—राज-यक्ष्म,<BR>अस्, or (in later authors) राज-यक्ष्मन्, आ, m. a<BR>particular kind of dangerous disease; (in the later<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0839-c" target="_blank">Page0839-c+ 81</a>]<BR>language) pulmonary consumption, atrophy.<BR>—राज-<BR>यक्ष्म-नामन्, आ, m., Ved., N. of a particular<BR>mythical being (said to be connected with the build-<BR>ing or foundation of a house).<BR>—राज-यक्ष्मिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, suffering from consumption, consumptive.<BR>—राज-यज्ञ, अस्, m. a king's sacrifice, royal offer-<BR>ing.<BR>—राज-यान, अम्, n. a royal vehicle, palanquin.<BR>—राज-युध्वन्, आ, m. a king's soldier, royal<BR>warrior; one who makes war against a king.<BR>—राज-<BR>योग, अस्, m. a constellation under which princes are<BR>born or a configuration of planets &c. at the birth of<BR>any person indicating him to be destined for kingship;<BR>a particular stage in abstract meditation, an easy mode<BR>of meditation as distinguished from the more rigo-<BR>rous; [cf. योग.]<BR>—राज-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, befit-<BR>ting a king, suitable for royalty, princely.<BR>—राज-<BR>योषित्, त्, f. a king's wife, queen.<BR>—राज-रङ्ग,<BR>अम्, n. ‘royal tin,’ silver.<BR>—राज-रथ, अस्, m. a<BR>royal carriage.<BR>—राज-राक्षस, अस्, m. ‘a Rāk-<BR>ṣasa of a king,’ a bad king.<BR>—राज-राज्, ट्, m. a<BR>king of kings, supreme sovereign; N. of the moon.<BR>—राज-राज, अस्, m. a king of kings, supreme<BR>sovereign, emperor; N. of Kuvera; of the moon;<BR>of a man.<BR>—राजराज-ता, f. or राजराज-त्व or<BR>राज-राज्य, अम्, n. the rank of a supreme sovereign<BR>or emperor, dominion over all princes, universal<BR>sovereignty.<BR>—राज-राम-नगर, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a town.<BR>—राज-रीति, इस्, f. a kind of brass or bell-<BR>metal.<BR>—राजर्षभ (˚ज-ऋष्˚), अस्, m. the chief<BR>of kings.<BR>—राजर्षि (˚ज-ऋषि), इस्, m. a royal<BR>Ṛṣi or saint, Ṛṣi of royal descent, that holy and<BR>superhuman personage which a king or man of the<BR>military class may become by the performance of<BR>great austerities (e. g. Purū-ravas, Viśvā-mitra, &c.;<BR>see ऋषि, विश्वा-मित्र).<BR>—राजर्षिन्, ई, m. = रा-<BR>जर्षि above.<BR>—राज-लक्षण, अम्, n. a royal<BR>sign or token, any mark on the body &c. indicating<BR>a future king; royal insignia, regalia.<BR>—राज-लक्ष्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. a royal token, sign of royalty; (आ), m.<BR>‘having the marks of royalty,’ N. of Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR>—राज-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. the Fortune or Prosperity<BR>of a king (personified as a goddess), a king's good<BR>genius, the good fortune or glory of a king, royal<BR>majesty or sovereignty; N. of a princess.<BR>—राज-<BR>लिङ्ग, अम्, n. a kingly mark, royal token.<BR>—राज-<BR>लीला-नामन्, आनि, n. pl., N. of a collection of epithets<BR>borne by Kṛṣṇa having reference to 118 of his di-<BR>versions when he had attained to regal rank.<BR>—राज-<BR>लेख, अस्, m. ‘king's writing,’ a royal letter or<BR>edict.<BR>—राज-लोक, अस्, m. a company of kings.<BR>—राज-वंश, अस्, m. a family of kings, royal<BR>family, dynasty.<BR>—राजवंशावली (˚श-आव्˚), f. the<BR>genealogy of kings, royal pedigree.<BR>—राजवंशीय<BR>or राजवंश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a royal<BR>family, of regal race or descent.<BR>—१. राज-वत्, ind.<BR>like a king; as towards a king.<BR>—२. राज-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having a king, possessing kings; (आन्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Dyutimat; (अती), f., N. of the wife<BR>of the Gandharva Deva-prabha.<BR>—राज-वदन, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—राज-वध, अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>king's weapon.<BR>—राज-वन्दिन्, ई, m. a proper N.<BR>—राज-वर्चस्, अस्, n. kingly rank or dignity,<BR>majesty.<BR>—राज-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. a king's high road,<BR>principal street.<BR>—राज-वर्धन, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—राज-वल्लभ, अस्, m. a king's favourite; N.<BR>of various plants (= राज-बदर, राजादनी, रा-<BR>जाम्र); N. of a kind of incense; of a work.<BR>—राज-वल्ली, f. Momordica Charantia.<BR>—राज-<BR>वशीभूत, अस्, आ, अम्, subject to a king, loyal.<BR>—राजवशीभूत-ता, f. loyalty, allegiance.<BR>—राज-<BR>वसति, इस्, f. dwelling in a king's court; a royal<BR>residence, palace.<BR>—राज-वार्त्तिक, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Sāṅkhya work.<BR>—राज-वाह, अस्, m. a horse.<BR>—राज-<BR>वाहन, अस्, m., N. of a son of king Rāja-haṃsa.<BR>—राज-वाह्य, अस्, m. a royal elephant.<BR>—राज-वि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘royal bird,’ the blue jay.<BR>—राज-विद्या, f.<BR>royal science, kingcraft, state policy, statesmanship,<BR>administration of government, political economy.<BR>—राज-विनोद-ताल, अस्, m. a kind of time or<BR>measure in music.<BR>—राज-विहार, अस्, m. a royal<BR>convent.<BR>—राज-वीजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sprung from a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-a" target="_blank">Page0840-a+ 81</a>]<BR>royal progenitor, of royal parentage or descent.<BR>—राज-वीथी, f. a principal street, high street, main<BR>road.<BR>—राज-वीर्य, अम्, n. the power of a king,<BR>regal power.<BR>—राज-वृक्ष, अस्, m. ‘royal tree,’<BR>Cathartocarpus Fistula; Buchanania Latifolia (or the<BR>Piyāl tree); Euphorbia Tirucalli.<BR>—राज-वृत्त, अम्,<BR>n. the conduct of a king, the duty or occupation of<BR>a sovereign.<BR>—राज-वेश्मन्, अ, n. a king's abode,<BR>palace.<BR>—राज-वेष, अस्, m. a royal garment.<BR>—रा-<BR>ज-शण, अस्, m. a plant from the fibres of which a<BR>coarse cordage and canvas are prepared, Corchorus<BR>Olitorius.<BR>—राज-शफर, अस्, m. a species of fish<BR>(the Hilsa fish).<BR>—राज-शय्या, f. a king's couch,<BR>royal couch, royal seat or throne.<BR>—राज-शाक, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of pot-herb (= वास्तूक).<BR>—राज-शाक-<BR>निका or राज-शाकिनी, f. a kind of vegetable (= राज-<BR>गिरि).<BR>—राज-शार्दूल, अस्, m. ‘a tiger of a king,’<BR>great king.<BR>—राज-शासन, अम्, n. a royal edict or<BR>order.<BR>—राज-शास्त्र, अम्, n. royal science, king-<BR>craft, state policy, statesmanship, political economy.<BR>—राज-शुक, अस्, m. a kind of parrot (= प्राज्ञ).<BR>—राज-शृङ्ग, अस्, m. a species of fish, Macropte-<BR>ronatus Magar; a sort of sheat fish; (अम्), n. a<BR>royal Chattar or umbrella with a golden handle.<BR>—राज-शेखर, अस्, m., N. of a king of Kerala<BR>(the author of several dramas).<BR>—राज-शैल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—राज-श्यामलोपासक (˚ल-<BR>उप्˚), आस्, m. pl., N. of a sect.<BR>—राज-श्यामाक, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of grain.<BR>—राज-श्री, ईस्, f. the Fortune<BR>or Prosperity of a king (personified; cf. राज-<BR>लक्ष्मी), the good fortune or glory of a king,<BR>royal sovereignty or majesty.<BR>—राज-संश्रय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having kings for a refuge or protection, de-<BR>pendent on kings.<BR>—राज-संसद्, त्, f. a king's<BR>assembly or court, court of justice.<BR>—राज-सत्तम,<BR>अस्, m. a most excellent king.<BR>—राज-सत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a king's sacrifice, any sacrifice instituted by a king.<BR>—राज-सदन, अम्, or राज-सद्मन्, अ, n. a<BR>royal dwelling, palace.<BR>—राज-सन्निधान, अम्, n.<BR>the royal presence.<BR>—राज-सभा, f. a royal assembly<BR>or court, court of justice, royal council, privy council.<BR>—राजसभा-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being at a king's<BR>court, a courtier.<BR>—राज-सर्प, अस्, m. a species of<BR>large serpent.<BR>—राज-सर्षप, अस्, m. black mus-<BR>tard, Sinapis Ramosa; a seed of the above used as<BR>a weight (= 3 Likṣās = (1/3) of a Gaura-sarṣapa).<BR>—राज-सात्, ind. to the state of a king, to the<BR>power of a king.<BR>—राजसात्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>&c., to give over to the power of a king, make de-<BR>pendent on a king.<BR>—राज-सायुज्य, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>state of close union with royalty,’ sovereignty.<BR>—राज-<BR>सारस, अस्, m. ‘royal crane,’ a peacock.<BR>—राज-<BR>सिंह, अस्, m. ‘a lion of a king,’ an illustrious king;<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—राज-सुख, अम्, n. a sovereign's<BR>happiness or welfare.<BR>—राज-सुत, अस्, m. a king's<BR>son, prince; (आ), f. a king's daughter, princess.<BR>—राज-सुन्दर-गणि, इस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—राज-सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. creating or making a<BR>king.<BR>—राज-सूनु, उस्, m. a king's son, prince.<BR>—राज-सूय, अस्, अम्, m. n. a great sacrifice or<BR>religious ceremony performed at the coronation of a<BR>supreme sovereign or universal monarch by the king<BR>himself and his tributary princes, (such a sacrifice at<BR>the inauguration of Yudhi-ṣṭhira is described in the<BR>Sabhā-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata); a lotus; a<BR>kind of rice; a mountain; राजसूयो मन्त्रः, a<BR>Mantra recited at the Rāja-sūya ceremony.<BR>—राज-<BR>सूय-याजिन्, ई, m. a priest who officiates at a Rāja-<BR>sūya sacrifice.<BR>—राजसूयारम्भ-पर्वन् (˚य-<BR>आर्˚), अ, n., N. of section 12-18 in the Sabhā-<BR>parvan of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—राजसूयिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, relating to the Rāja-sūya sacrifice.<BR>—राज-सू-<BR>येष्टि (˚य-इष्˚), इस्, f. the Rāja-sūya sacrifice.<BR>—राज-सेवक, अस्, m. a king's servant.<BR>—राज-<BR>सेवा, f. king's service, royal service.<BR>—राज-सेविन्,<BR>ई, m. a king's servant.<BR>—राज-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>horse.<BR>—राज-स्तम्ब, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राज-<BR>स्तम्बायन, अस्, and राजस्तम्बि, इस्, m. patro-<BR>nymics from Rāja-stamba.<BR>—राज-स्त्री, f. a king's<BR>wife, queen.<BR>—राजस्थलक, see Gaṇa Dhūmādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 127.<BR>—राज-स्थली, f., N. of a place.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-b" target="_blank">Page0840-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—राज-स्व, अम्, n. the property of a king, royal<BR>possessions; revenue, tribute.<BR>—राज-स्वर्ण, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of thorn-apple.<BR>—राज-स्वामिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘lord of kings,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—राज-हंस, अस्,<BR>m. ‘king goose,’ a flamingo (a sort of white goose<BR>with red legs and bill); an illustrious king; N. of a<BR>king of Magadha; of an author; (ई), f. the female<BR>flamingo.<BR>—राज-हत्या, f. assassination of a king,<BR>regicide.<BR>—राज-हर्म्य, अम्, n. a king's palace,<BR>royal palace.<BR>—राज-हर्षण, अम्, n. ‘king's de-<BR>light,’ the flower of Tabernæmontana Coronaria.<BR>—राज-हस्तिन्, ई, m. a royal elephant, a handsome<BR>elephant.<BR>—राज-हार, अस्, m., Ved. a bearer or<BR>bringer of Soma.<BR>—राज-हासक, अस्, m. a species<BR>of fish, Cyprinus Catla.<BR>—राजाग्नि (˚ज-अग्˚), इस्, m.<BR>the fire of a king, i. e. wrath of a king.<BR>—राजाङ्गण<BR>(˚ज-अङ्˚), अम्, n. royal court, the court-yard of a<BR>palace.<BR>—राजाज्ञा (˚ज-आज्˚), f. a king's edict, royal<BR>decree or command, ordinance.<BR>—राजातन (˚ज-<BR>आत्˚), अस्, m. Buchanania Latifolia; Butea Frondosa;<BR>Mimusops Kauki.<BR>—राजात्मक-स्तव (˚ज-आत्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a panegyric of Rāma.<BR>—राजात्यावर्-<BR>तक (˚ज-अत्˚), अस्, m. = राजावर्त.<BR>—राजादन<BR>(˚ज-अद्˚), अस्, m. Buchanania Latifolia; Mimusops<BR>Kauki or Hexandra; Butea Frondosa [cf. राजातन];<BR>(ई), f. a species of tree, = कपीष्ट, भूपेष्ट, &c.;<BR>(अम्), n. the nut of Buchanania Latifolia; the fruit<BR>of the Mimusops.<BR>—राजादेश (˚ज-आद्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>king's command.<BR>—राजाद्रि (˚ज-अद्˚), इस्, m. a<BR>species of vegetable.<BR>—राजाधिकारिन् (˚ज-अध्˚), ई,<BR>m. ‘royal official,’ a judge.<BR>—राजाधिकृत (˚ज-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. a judge (placed over [judicial affairs]<BR>by a king).<BR>—राजाधिदेव (˚ज-अध्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of Śūra; (ई), f., N. of a daughter of Śūra.<BR>—राजा-<BR>धिराज (˚ज-अध्˚), अस्, m. a king of kings, supreme<BR>king, paramount sovereign, mighty potentate.<BR>—रा-<BR>जाधिष्ठान (˚ज-अध्˚), अम्, n. ‘royal city, royal<BR>capital,’ a town in which a king has built a palace.<BR>—राजाध्वन् (˚ज-अध्˚), आ, m. a royal road, prin-<BR>cipal street.<BR>—राजानक (˚ज-अन्˚), अस्, m. an in-<BR>ferior king, petty prince.<BR>—राजानुजीविन् (˚ज-अन्˚),<BR>ई, m. the dependent of a king, a king's servant.<BR>—राजान्त-करण (˚ज-अन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, causing<BR>the destruction of kings.<BR>—राजान्न (˚ज-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. food obtained from a king or great personage; a<BR>kind of rice of a superior quality (grown in Andhra).<BR>—राजान्य-त्व (˚ज-अन्˚), अम्, n., Ved. a change<BR>of kings.<BR>—राजापसद (˚ज-अप्˚), अस्, m. a de-<BR>graded or outcast king.<BR>—राजाभरण (˚ज-आभ्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a king's ornament, regalia.<BR>—राजाभिषेक<BR>(˚ज-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the consecration or coronation of<BR>a king, royal inauguration or installation.<BR>—राजाम्र<BR>(˚ज-आम्˚), अस्, m. a superior kind of mango.<BR>—रा-<BR>जाम्ल (˚ज-अम्˚), अस्, m. = अम्ल-वेतस.<BR>—राजार्क<BR>(˚ज-अर्˚), अस्, m. Calotropis Gigantea.<BR>—राजार्ह<BR>(˚ज-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, fit or suitable for a king,<BR>worthy of a prince, royal, noble; (आ), f. Eugenia<BR>Jambolana; (अम्), n. aloe wood, Agallochum; a<BR>kind of rice (= राजान्न).<BR>—राजार्हण (˚ज-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a royal gift or offering of honour.<BR>—राजा-<BR>लाबू (˚ज-अल्˚), ऊस्, f. a species of cucumber, (also<BR>राजालाबु.)<BR>—राजालुक (˚ज-आल्˚), अस्, m. a species<BR>of tuberous plant or yam (= महा-कन्द).<BR>—रा-<BR>जावरत (˚ज-आव्˚), अस्, m. a kind of diamond or<BR>other gem (of an inferior quality, said to come from<BR>the country Virāṭa, and regarded as a lucky possession<BR>though not esteemed as an ornament; in the Rasa-<BR>rāja-lakṣmī enumerated among the Rasas or metallic<BR>substances).<BR>—राजावलि, इस्, or राजावली (˚ज-आव्˚),<BR>f. a line of kings, a royal dynasty or genealogy; N.<BR>of the history or chronicles of a particular line of<BR>kings.<BR>—राजावली-पताका, f., N. of a history of the<BR>kings of Kaśmīra by Prājya-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—राजावली-पा-<BR>टक, N. of the history or chronicles of a particular<BR>line of kings.<BR>—राजाश्व (˚ज-अश्˚), अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>large or powerful stallion.<BR>—राजासन (˚ज-आस्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a royal seat, throne.<BR>—राजासन्दी (˚ज-आस्˚),<BR>f., Ved. a stool or stand on which the Soma is placed.<BR>—राजाहि (˚ज-अहि), इस्, m. a kind of large snake.<BR>—राजेन्द्र (˚ज-इन्˚), अस्, m. a lord of kings, king<BR>of kings, supreme sovereign, emperor; N. of a poet;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">Page0840-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of a son of Kāśī-nātha.<BR>—राजेन्द्र-गिर्, ईर्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—राजेश्वर (˚ज-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a king of<BR>kings, supreme sovereign; a proper N.<BR>—राजेष्ट<BR>(˚ज-इष्˚), अस्, m. ‘liked by kings,’ a kind of onion,<BR>= राज-पलाण्डु; (अम्), n. a kind of rice (= रा-<BR>जान्न).<BR>—राजोद्वेजन-सञ्ज्ञक (˚ज-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a species of plant.<BR>—राजोपकरण (˚ज-उप्˚),<BR>आनि, n. pl. the paraphernalia of a king, ensigns of<BR>royalty.<BR>—राजोपजीविन् (˚ज-उप्˚), इनस्, m. pl. the<BR>subjects of a king.<BR>—राजोपसेवा (˚ज-उप्˚), f. a<BR>king's service, royal service.<BR>—राजोपसेविन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, serving a king; (ई), m. a king's servant, royal<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन
राजन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to a royal family,<BR>of regal descent (but not belonging to the warrior<BR>caste); (ई), f., N. of a river; (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्य|राजन्यः
राजन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. राजन्), kingly, princely,<BR>royal; (अस्), m. a royal personage, one of princely<BR>rank, a nobleman; a man of the military or regal<BR>tribe, a Kṣatriya, (the title Rājanya was the more<BR>ancient designation of the second or Kṣatriya caste);<BR>N. of Agni or Fire; a kind of date tree, = क्षीरिका;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. epithet of a particular family of warriors;<BR>(आ), f. a lady of royal rank.<BR>—राजन्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being a warrior or belonging to the military caste.<BR>—राजन्य-बन्धु, उस्, m. the friend or connec-<BR>tion of a prince (generally used in contempt); a<BR>Kṣatriya.<BR>—राजन्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. con-<BR>nected with one of royal rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यक|राजन्यकं
राजन्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabited by warriors;<BR>(अम्), n. a number of Kṣatriyas, assemblage of<BR>warriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमान
राजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, glittering, radiant.<BR>—राजमान-त्व, अम्, n. splendor, radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजान
राजान (fr. राजन्), Nom. P. राजानति, &c., to<BR>become a king (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाय
राजाय, Nom. A. राजायते, to act or behave like<BR>a king, to consider one's self a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिक
राजिक, अस्, आ, अम्, in षोडश-र्˚, q. v., (for रा-<BR>जिका, a streak, field, &c., see p. 841, col. 2.); (अस्),<BR>m. a lord, chief, noble person; N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजित
राजित, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminated, irradiated; adorned,<BR>embellished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीय
राजीय (fr. राजन्), Nom. P. राजीयति, &c., to<BR>wish or long for a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीव|राजीवं|राजीवः
1. राजीव, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 841, col. 2),<BR>living at a king's expense (= राजोपजीविन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्ञी
राज्ञी, f. (fem. of राजन्), a queen, princess, the<BR>wife of a king; epithet of the western quarter of the<BR>Soul of the Universe (see Chāndogya-Upaniṣad III.<BR>15, 2); N. of the wife of the Sun; deep-coloured<BR>or yellowish red brass (consisting of three parts of<BR>copper to one of zinc or tin); [cf. Lat. regina;<BR>perhaps Goth. raginon.]<BR>—राज्ञी-पद, अम्, n. the<BR>rank or dignity of a queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्य|राज्यं
राज्य, अस्, &c., Ved. of or belonging to a king,<BR>kingly, princely, royal; (अम्), n. kingship, royalty,<BR>sovereignty, reign; a kingdom, country, principality,<BR>empire, monarchy, government; administration or<BR>exercise of government, (ब्राह्मण-र्˚, a country<BR>governed by Brāhmans; cf. सुर-र्˚.)<BR>—राज्य-कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, exercising government, ruling; (अस्), m.<BR>the tribute paid by tributary princes, (in this sense<BR>fr. 2. कर.)<BR>—राज्य-कर्तृ, ता, m. an adminis-<BR>trator or officer of government; a king.<BR>—राज्य-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, exercising government or sovereignty,<BR>ruling.<BR>—राज्य-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from<BR>sovereignty; (अस्), m. a king who has lost his king-<BR>dom, a deposed or dethroned monarch.<BR>—राज्य-<BR>च्युति, इस्, f. loss of sovereignty, deposal, dethrone-<BR>ment.<BR>—राज्य-तन्त्र, अम्, n. (also आणि, n. pl.),<BR>the science or rules of government, theory or system<BR>of administration, rule, government.<BR>—राज्य-देवी,<BR>f., N. of the mother of Vāṇa.<BR>—राज्य-द्रव्य,<BR>अम्, n. a requisite of sovereignty, any object neces-<BR>sary for the consecration of a king.<BR>—राज्यद्रव्य-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of or belonging to the<BR>requisites of royalty.<BR>—राज्य-धर, अस्, m. ‘exer-<BR>cising rule,’ a proper N.<BR>—राज्य-धुरा, f. burden of<BR>government, administration.<BR>—राज्य-परिभ्रष्ट,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">Page0841-a+ 77</a>]<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from or deprived of a kingdom.<BR>—राज्य-पाल, अस्, m. ‘kingdom-protector,’ N. of<BR>a king.<BR>—राज्य-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, giving or con-<BR>ferring a kingdom.<BR>—राज्य-भङ्ग, अस्, m. sub-<BR>version of sovereignty.<BR>—राज्य-भाज्, क्, m. the<BR>possessor of a kingdom, a king.<BR>—राज्य-भार, अस्,<BR>m. the weight of (the duties of) government.<BR>—राज्य-<BR>भेद-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing division or discord<BR>in a government.<BR>—राज्य-भोग, अस्, m. the pos-<BR>session of sovereignty, government of a kingdom.<BR>—राज्य-भ्रंश, अस्, m. ‘falling from sovereignty,’<BR>deposition from a kingdom.<BR>—राज्य-भ्रष्ट, अस्,<BR>m. one fallen from royalty, a deposed sovereign.<BR>—राज्य-रक्षा, f. protection or defence of a king-<BR>dom.<BR>—राज्य-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. the good fortune of<BR>a kingdom, glory of sovereignty.<BR>—राज्य-लीला, f.<BR>‘king-play,’ pretending to be a king.<BR>—राज्यलीलाय,<BR>Nom. A. राज्यलीलायते, &c., to play the king, pre-<BR>tend to be a king.<BR>—राज्यलीलायित, अम्, n. the<BR>playing at kings.<BR>—राज्य-लोभ, अस्, m. desire for<BR>royalty, lust of dominion, ambition.<BR>—राज्य-वर्-<BR>धन, अस्, m., N. of a king (son of Dama); of<BR>another (son of Pratāpa-śīla or Prabhākara-vardhana).<BR>—राज्य-व्यवहार, अस्, m. government business.<BR>—राज्य-श्री, ईस्, f., N. of a daughter of Pratāpa-<BR>śīla.<BR>—राज्य-सुख, अम्, n. the pleasure or sweets<BR>of royalty, enjoyment of a kingdom.<BR>—राज्य-सेन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king of Nandī-pura.<BR>—राज्य-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or राज्य-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being in a<BR>kingly office, bearing sway, ruling, governing.<BR>—रा-<BR>ज्य-स्थिति, इस्, f. the being in a royal office, being a<BR>king, bearing rule.<BR>—राज्य-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, spoiling<BR>a kingdom, the spoiler of an empire.<BR>—राज्याङ्ग<BR>(˚य-अङ्˚), अम्, n. ‘limb of royalty,’ a requisite of<BR>regal administration (variously enumerated as seven,<BR>eight, or nine, viz. the monarch, the prime minister,<BR>a friend or ally, treasure, territory, a stronghold, an<BR>army, the companies of citizens, and the Puro-hita<BR>or spiritual adviser).<BR>—राज्याधिकार (˚य-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. authority over a kingdom; right or title to<BR>a sovereignty.<BR>—राज्यापहरण (˚य-अप्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the taking away or deprivation of a kingdom,<BR>usurpation.<BR>—राज्यापहारक (˚य-अप्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>usurper.<BR>—राज्याभिषिक्त (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>inaugurated to an empire, crowned.<BR>—राज्याभि-<BR>षेक (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, m. inauguration to a king-<BR>dom, coronation.<BR>—राज्याश्रम-मुनि (˚य-आश्˚),<BR>इस्, m. ‘the monk of a royal hermitage,’ a king.<BR>—राज्यैकशेषेण (˚य-एक्˚), ind. with the single<BR>exception of the kingdom.<BR>—राज्योपकरण (˚य-<BR>उप्˚), आनि, n. pl. the instruments or paraphernalia<BR>of government, insignia of sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0840-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्र|राष्ट्रं|राष्ट्रः
राष्ट्र. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकिनेय
राजकिनेय राजकिनेय, अस्, m. (fr. रजकी),<BR>a metronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत|राजतं
राजत राजत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रजत), silvery,<BR>made of silver, silver; (अम्), n. silver.<BR>—राजतान्-<BR>वित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered or overlaid with silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनि
राजनि राजनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Rajana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस|राजसः
राजस राजस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रजस्), belong-<BR>ing or relating to the quality रजस्, attendant on<BR>the quality of passion, endowed with or influenced<BR>by the quality of passion, passionate; (ई), f., N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—राजस-त्व, अम्, n. the state or predo-<BR>minance of the quality of passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसिक
राजसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = राजस above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसाइ
राजसाइ राजसाई, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजासलखण
राजासलखण राजासलखण, अस्, m. a pro-<BR>per N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजि|राजिः
राजि राजि, इस्, or राजी, f. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 124. fr. rt. राज्, but probably fr. रज्,<BR>for rt. ऋज्), a streak, stripe, line, row, rank; a con-<BR>tinuous or unbroken line; a line parting the hair;<BR>black mustard (= राजिका; in this sense generally<BR>राजी); (इस्), m., N. of a son of Āyu, (also read रजि.)<BR>—राजि-चित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated with stripes<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">Page0841-b+ 71</a>]<BR>(said of a species of snake).<BR>—राजि-फला, f. ‘having<BR>striped fruit,’ a kind of cucumber (= चीनाकर्कटी).<BR>—राजि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing stripes, striped;<BR>epithet of a species of snake.<BR>—राजी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, formed into lines, striped.<BR>—राजी-फल, अस्,<BR>m. Trichosanthes Diœca.<BR>—राजी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>= राजि-मत् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिका
राजिका, f. (for राजिक see p. 840, col. 3), a stripe,<BR>streak, line, row, range; a field; black mustard,<BR>Sinapis Ramosa; a grain of mustard, mustard-seed<BR>(as a weight = (1/3) of a Sarṣapa); a particular eruption<BR>(enumerated among the Kṣudra-rogas).<BR>—राजिका-<BR>फल, अस्, m. white mustard, Sinapis Glauca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिल|राजिलः
राजिल, अस्, आ, अम्, striped; (अस्), m. epithet of a<BR>species of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजी
राजी. See under राजि, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीव|राजीवं|राजीवः
2. राजीव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. राजी; for 1. see p. 840,<BR>col. 3), streaked, striped; (अस्), m. a species of fish<BR>(its spawn is said to be poisonous); a kind of deer;<BR>the Indian crane; an elephant; N. of the pupil of<BR>Viśva-nātha; (अम्), n. a blue lotus-flower.<BR>—राजीव-<BR>नेत्र or राजीव-लोचन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, lotus-eyed,<BR>blue-eyed.<BR>—राजीव-पृश्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having<BR>lotus-coloured spots or streaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीविनी
राजीविनी, f. the plant Nelumbium Speciosum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीक
राजीक राजीक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेय
राजेय राजेय, अस्, ई, अम्, coming or derived<BR>from Raji.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेयु
राजेयु राजेयु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्जुकण्ठिन्
राज्जुकण्ठिन् राज्जुकण्ठिन्, इनस्, m. pl. (fr.<BR>रज्जु-कण्ठ), the school of Rajju-kaṇṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्जुदाल
राज्जुदाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रज्जु-दाल), coming<BR>from the Rajju-dāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्जुभारिन्
राज्जुभारिन्, इणस्, m. pl. (fr. रज्जु-भार), the<BR>school of Rajju-bhāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्ञी
राज्ञी राज्ञी, राज्य, &c. See p. 840, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राटि|राटिः
राटि राटि, इस्, f. (fr. rt. रट्), war, battle;<BR>= शरारि, (probably a mistake for आटि, see राडि<BR>below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राटिका
राटिका, f. in मृग-र्˚, q. v., (perhaps) ‘causing<BR>the deer to scream.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राटु
राटु, उस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राडि|राडिः
राडि राडि, said to = शरारि, (apparently a<BR>mistake for आडि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राढा
राढा राढा, f. (sometimes written रारा),<BR>beauty, splendor, light, lustre; N. of a district in the<BR>west of Bengal (= सुह्म); of the capital of this<BR>district.<BR>—राढा-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राढीय|राढीयः
राढीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the district or<BR>town Rāḍhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राण|राणं
राण राण, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. रण्),<BR>a leaf; a peacock's tail; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणक
राणक राणक, N. of a commentary by<BR>Someśvara Bhaṭṭa on the Tantra-vārttika; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of an author; (इका), f. a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणड्य
राणड्य राणड्य, अस्, m., N. of Dāmodara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणाक
राणाक राणाक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणायन
राणायन राणायन, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Raṇa.<BR>—राणायनी-पुत्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणायनीय|राणायनीयः
राणायनीय, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the school of Rāṇāyana; (अम्), n. the Sūtras<BR>of Rāṇāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणायनीयि
राणायनीयि, इस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणि
राणि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Rāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणिग
राणिग राणिग, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Jayāditya and uncle of Keśavārka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राण्ड्य
राण्ड्य राण्ड्य or रान्द्र्य (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI. 23, 6) = रमणीय, agreeable,<BR>gratifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात
रात रात, राति, &c. See p. 837, cols. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रातन्ती|रातंती
रातन्ती रातन्ती (?), a festival on the four-<BR>teenth day of the second half of the month Pauṣa<BR>(when people bathe at the first appearance of dawn.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रातुल
रातुल रातुल, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śud-<BR>dhodana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र|रात्रं
रात्र रात्र, रात्रक. See p. 842, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रि|रात्रिः
रात्रि रात्रि, इस्, or रात्री, f. (in the older<BR>language generally रात्री; probably fr. rt. रम्),<BR>night, the darkness or stillness of night [cf. राम];<BR>Night personified, (रात्रौ, at night, by night; रा-<BR>त्रौ शयनम्, a festival on the eleventh day of the<BR>first half of the month Āṣāḍha, regarded as the<BR>night of the gods beginning with the summer solstice,<BR>when Viṣṇu reposes for four months on the serpent<BR>Śeṣa); = अति-रात्र; = रात्रि-पर्याय; = रात्रि-<BR>सामन्; one of the four bodies of Brahmā, (in this<BR>and the following senses only रात्रि); = हरिद्रा,<BR>turmeric; रात्रि भारद्वाजी, f., N. of the authoress<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 127.<BR>—रात्रि-कर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘night-maker,’ the moon.<BR>—रात्रि-काल, अस्, m.<BR>night-time.<BR>—रात्रि-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, night-wander-<BR>ing, prowling or roaming at night; (अस्), m. a night-<BR>rover, night-prowler, thief, robber; a night-watcher,<BR>watchman, guard, patrol; a Rākṣasa; a goblin,<BR>ghost, fiend, evil spirit; (ई), f. a Rākṣasa female.<BR>—रात्रि-चर्या, f. night-roving, roaming about at<BR>night; a nightly act or ceremony.<BR>—रात्रि-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced at night, appearing by night, noc-<BR>turnal; (अम्), n. a star, constellation.<BR>—रात्रि-जल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘night-water,’ dew, mist, fog.<BR>—रात्रि-जा-<BR>गर, अस्, m. night-watching, wakefulness at night;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), watching at night, sitting up at night;<BR>(अस्), m. a dog.<BR>—रात्रि-जागरण, अम्, n. the act<BR>of sitting up all night.<BR>—रात्रिजागर-द, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, causing waking or wakefulness at night, keeping<BR>awake at night; (अस्), m. a gnat, musquito.<BR>—रा-<BR>त्रिञ्-चर = रात्रि-चर above.<BR>—रात्रि-तरा, f. (com-<BR>par. of रात्रि), the depth or dead of night.<BR>—रात्रि-<BR>तिथि, इस्, f. a lunar night.<BR>—रात्रि-दिवम् = रात्रिन्-<BR>दिवम् below.<BR>—रात्रि-नाशन, अस्, m. ‘night-<BR>destroyer,’ the sun.<BR>—रात्रिन्-दिव, अम्, n. a night<BR>and day, day and night; (अम्, आ), ind. by night<BR>and day.<BR>—रात्रि-पद-विचार, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—रात्रि-परिशिष्ट, अम्, n. = रात्रि-सूक्त.<BR>—रात्रि-पर्याय, अस्, m., Ved. the three recurring<BR>sentences in the recitation of the Ati-rātra.<BR>—रात्रि-<BR>पुष्प, अम्, n. ‘night-flower,’ a lotus-flower which<BR>opens during the night.<BR>—रात्रि-पूजा, f. night-wor-<BR>ship, the nocturnal worship of a deity.<BR>—रात्रि-बल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, powerful by night, manifesting power at<BR>night; (अस्), m. a Rākṣasa.<BR>—रात्रि-भोजन, अम्,<BR>n. night-eating, the act of taking food at night.<BR>—रात्रिभोजन-निषेध, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—रात्रिम्-अट, अस्, m. = रात्र्य्-अट.<BR>—रात्रि-मणि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘night-jewel,’ the moon.<BR>—रात्रि-मारण,<BR>अम्, n. night-killing, a murder committed in the<BR>night.<BR>—रात्रिम्-मन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, thinking it<BR>night; being regarded as night, appearing like night.<BR>—रात्रि-योग, अस्, m. night-fall, the coming on of<BR>night.<BR>—रात्रि-रक्षक, अस्, m. a night-guard,<BR>watchman, night-watcher.<BR>—रात्रि-राग, अस्, m.<BR>‘the colour of night,’ darkness, obscurity.<BR>—रात्रि-<BR>लग्न-निरूपण, अम्, n., N. of a treatise ascribed<BR>to Kālidāsa.<BR>—रात्रि-वासस्, अस्, n. a night-garment,<BR>night-dress; the garment of night, i. e. darkness,<BR>obscurity.<BR>—रात्रि-विगम, अस्, m. departure of<BR>night, break of day, dawn, day-light.<BR>—रात्रि-विश्ले-<BR>ष-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going apart at night, separating<BR>at night; (ई), m. the ruddy goose, Anas Casarca.<BR>—रात्रि-वेद, अस्, or रात्रि-वेदिन्, ई, m. ‘night-<BR>knower,’ a cock.<BR>—रात्रि-षामन् or रात्रि-सामन्,<BR>अ, n. a Sāman belonging to the Ati-rātra.<BR>—रात्रि-<BR>सत्त्र, अम्, n., Ved. a night sacrifice, night cere-<BR>mony.<BR>—रात्रि-सूक्त or रात्री-सूक्त, अम्, n. epithet<BR>of certain hymns on Night appended to Ṛg-veda X.<BR>127.<BR>—रात्रि-हास, अस्, m. ‘laughing, i. e. opening<BR>in the night,’ the white lotus.<BR>—रात्रि-हिण्डक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘moving about at night,’ a guard of the women's<BR>apartments.<BR>—रात्री-दैवोदास or रात्री-हव-दै-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">Page0842-a+ 79</a>]<BR>वोदास, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—रात्र्य्-अट, अस्,<BR>m. ‘night-moving,’ a Rākṣasa, goblin; a ghost; a<BR>night-walker; a thief.<BR>—रात्र्य्-अन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>night-blind, unable to see by night.<BR>—रात्र्यन्ध-<BR>ता, f. night-blindness.<BR>—रात्र्य्-अहनी, n. du. night<BR>and day.<BR>—रात्र्य्-आगम, अस्, m. the coming on<BR>or approach of night; [cf. अहर्-आगम.]<BR>—रात्र्य्-<BR>आन्ध्य, अम्, n. night-blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0841-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र|रात्रं
रात्र, अम्, n. (at the end of comps.) = रात्रि,<BR>night; [cf. त्रि-र्˚, पञ्च-र्˚, दिवा-र्˚; also used alone<BR>in त्रीणि रात्राणि, Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 6230.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रक|रात्रकं|रात्रकः
रात्रक, अस्, इका, अम्, nocturnal, nightly, lasting<BR>a night [cf. पञ्च-र्˚]; (अस्), m. a man who takes<BR>up his abode in a harlot's house for one year; (अम्),<BR>n. = पञ्च-रात्र, a general term for the sacred<BR>books of various Vaiṣṇava sects; (according to<BR>others) a period of five nights collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिक
रात्रिक (at the end of a comp. after a numeral),<BR>lasting a certain number of nights or days (e. g.<BR>पञ्च-रात्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, lasting five nights); suf-<BR>ficient for or completed in a certain number of<BR>nights or days [cf. एक-र्˚]; (आ), f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रीण
रात्रीण, अस्, आ, अम्, lasting a certain number of<BR>nights, completed &c. in a certain number of nights,<BR>(एक-रात्रीण, completed in one night; cf. द्वि-र्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्याकूपार
रात्र्याकूपार, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथकारिक
राथकारिक राथकारिक (fr. रथ-कार),<BR>see Gaṇa Kumudādi 2. to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथकार्य
राथकार्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Ratha-<BR>kāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथगणक
राथगणक, अम्, n. the occupation or office of<BR>a Ratha-gaṇaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथजितेयी
राथजितेयी, f. (fr. रथ-जित्), epithet of certain<BR>Apsarases (Atharva-veda VI. 130, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथन्तर|राथंतर
राथन्तर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रथन्-तर), Ved.<BR>relating to the Rathantara Sāman; (अस्), m. a patro-<BR>nymic; (ई), f., N. of a female teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथन्तरायण|राथंतरायण
राथन्तरायण, अस्, m. (fr. रथन्-तर), a<BR>patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथप्रोष्ठ
राथप्रोष्ठ, अस्, m. a patronymic of Asamāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथितर
राथितर, अस्, m. (fr. रथी-तर), Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic of Satya-vacas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथीतरीपुत्र
राथीतरी-पुत्र, अस्, m. son of Rāthītarī, N. of<BR>a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राथ्य
राथ्य, अस्, आ (?), अम्, belonging to a chariot, fit<BR>for a chariot, useful for a carriage; = रथ्य (of which<BR>it is a lengthened form, Ṛg-veda I. 157, 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्ध|राद्धं
राद्ध राद्ध, राद्धान्त, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्
राध् राध् (connected with rts. ऋध्, 1. रा),<BR>cl. 5. 4. P. राध्नोति, राध्यति (some-<BR>times A. राध्यते), रराध (2nd sing. रराधि-<BR>थ or रेधिथ, 3rd du. रराधतुस् or रेधतुस्,<BR>3rd pl. रराधुस् or रेधुस्, but according to Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 4, 123. the contracted forms are only used in<BR>the sense ‘to injure, kill;’ see also Vopa-deva VIII.<BR>52), रात्स्यति, अरात्सीत् (1st pl. अरात्स्म, 3rd pl.<BR>अरात्सुस्), अराधिष्ट (Vedic forms राधति, अरा-<BR>धत्, राधत्), राद्धुम्, (without prep. this verb<BR>is generally Ved.), to make favourable or kind, pro-<BR>pitiate, conciliate, make agreeable (cl. 5); to be<BR>favourable or merciful (cl. 4); to accomplish, per-<BR>form, effect, finish, perfect, complete, make ready,<BR>prepare, carry out, (generally cl. 5. or Ved. cl. I.<BR>राधति); to attain; to be accomplished or finished<BR>(cl. 4); to succeed, prosper, be successful (cl. 4);<BR>to be prepared or ready (cl. 4); to be ready for<BR>(with dat. or loc.); to fall to the share of any one<BR>(dat.); to put an end to, destroy, injure, exterminate:<BR>Pass. राध्यते, Aor. अराधि, to be conciliated or<BR>made favourable &c., to be appeased; to be accom-<BR>plished, to be successful &c.: Caus. राधयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अरीरधत्, to make favourable, conci-<BR>liate, propitiate, satisfy, appease; to accomplish,<BR>perform, complete, bring to a successful issue, cause<BR>to succeed; to make ready or prepared for (with<BR>dat.): Desid. रिरात्सति, to wish to conciliate or pro-<BR>pitiate; रित्सति, to wish to injure, destroy, hurt<BR>(Pāṇ. VII. 4, 54, Vārt.): Intens. राराध्यते, रा-<BR>राधि; [cf. according to some, Gr. ἱλάσκομαι,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-b" target="_blank">Page0842-b+ 81</a>]<BR>ἵληθι, ἱλάομαι, &c.; according to others, ἔρδω<BR>Goth. rêda, ga-rêda, und-rêda.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्ध|राद्धं
राद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, propitiated, conciliated; ac-<BR>complished, perfected, completed, finished, performed,<BR>done; prepared, ready; cooked, dressed; perfected<BR>(as a religious vow), observed (as a fast); perfect in<BR>mysterious or magical power, adept, initiated; ob-<BR>tained, attained; appeared; successful, prosperous,<BR>fortunate, happy; fallen to the share or lot of any<BR>one.<BR>—राद्धान्त (˚ध-अन्˚), अस्, m. = सिद्धान्त,<BR>an established end or result, demonstrated conclusion,<BR>a proved or established fact, demonstrated truth,<BR>dogma; the conclusion of an argument.<BR>—राद्धान्-<BR>तित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the preceding), logically demon-<BR>strated, proved, established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धि|राद्धिः
राद्धि, इस्, f. accomplishment, perfection, com-<BR>pletion; success, prosperity, good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध|राधः
राध, अस्, अम्, m. n. = राधस्, favour, good-<BR>will; a gift, affluence, &c.; (अस्), m., N. of the<BR>month Vaiśākha (= April-May; in this sense fr.<BR>राधा below); a proper N.; (आ), f. prosperity,<BR>success; N. of the twenty-first Nakṣatra Vi-śākhā<BR>(containing four stars in the shape of a festoon; the<BR>stars are supposed to be α, ι, ν Libræ, and γ Scor-<BR>pionis, cf. नक्षत्र); a later form for अनु-राधा;<BR>lightning; a particular attitude in shooting (standing<BR>with the feet a span apart; cf. राधा-भेदिन्); Em-<BR>blic Myrobalan; the plant Clitoria Ternatea; N.<BR>of the foster-mother of Karṇa, (she was the wife of<BR>Adhiratha, who was the Sūta or charioteer of king Śūra,<BR>and who found Karṇa, the illegitimate child of Pṛthā<BR>or Kuntī by the Sun, when exposed by his mother on<BR>the banks of the Jumna, and brought him up as his<BR>own son); N. of a celebrated cowherdess or Gopī<BR>(the favourite mistress and consort of Kṛṣṇa, q. v.,<BR>during his residence in Vṛndā-vana amongst the cow-<BR>herds, and a principal personage in Jayadeva's cele-<BR>brated lyrical poem, the Gīta-govinda, q. v.; she is<BR>sometimes supposed to typify the human soul, attracted<BR>towards Kṛṣṇa as the divine goodness, sometimes the<BR>divine or mystical love to which Kṛṣṇa returns at<BR>the end of his more worldly amours; at a later<BR>period she was worshipped as a goddess, and is occa-<BR>sionally regarded as an Avatāra of Lakṣmī as Kṛṣṇa<BR>is of Viṣṇu; she is also, under other aspects, iden-<BR>tified with Dākṣāyaṇī); N. of a female slave.<BR>—राध-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a minister of<BR>Aśoka.<BR>—राध-रङ्क, अस्, m. a plough; thin<BR>rain; hail.<BR>—राध-रङ्कु, उस्, m. = सार, शीकर,<BR>जलदोपल.<BR>—राधस्-पति, इस्, m. [cf. रथस्-<BR>पति], Ved. a lord of gifts or wealth.<BR>—राधा-<BR>कान्त, अस्, m. ‘lover of Rādhā,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—राधा-कृष्ण, अस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>the Dhātu-ratnāvalī.<BR>—राधा-जन्माष्टमी (˚म-<BR>अष्˚), f., N. of the eighth day of a particular fort-<BR>night (commemorating the birthday of Rādhā; cf.<BR>कृष्ण-ज्˚).<BR>—राधा-तनय, अस्, m. son of Rā-<BR>dhā, i. e. Karṇa.<BR>—राधा-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra.<BR>—राधा-दामोदर, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of an elementary treatise on the Vedānta.<BR>—राधा-नगरी, f., N. of a town in the neigh-<BR>bourhood of Ujjayinī.<BR>—राधानुराधीय (˚धा-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the Nakṣatras Rādhā<BR>and Anurādhā.<BR>—राधा-भेदिन्, ई, m., N. of Ar-<BR>juna, (according to some this name has reference<BR>to a particular attitude in shooting, see राधा above<BR>and cf. राधा-वेधिन्; according to others it was<BR>given to Arjuna as having prevailed on Kṛṣṇa to<BR>abandon Rādhā.)<BR>—राधा-माधव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR>—राधा-मोहन-शर्मन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the Mitākṣarā-siddhānta-saṅ-<BR>graha.<BR>—राधा-रमण, अस्, m., N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—राधा-रस-सुधा-निधि or राधा-सुधा-नि-<BR>धि, इस्, m., N. of a poem by Hari-vaṃśa Go-svāmin<BR>celebrating the praises of Rādhā as worshipped in<BR>Vṛndā-vana (supposed to have been written at the<BR>end of the sixteenth century).<BR>—राधा-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessed of prosperity or wealth, rich.<BR>—राधा-वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘the beloved of Rādhā,’<BR>N. of Kṛṣṇa; epithet of various persons.<BR>—राधा-<BR>विनोद, अस्, m., N. of a poem.<BR>—राधा-वेधिन्, ई,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">Page0842-c+ 77</a>]<BR>m., N. of Arjuna; [cf. राधा-भेदिन्.]<BR>—राधा-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. son of Rādhā, i. e. Karṇa.<BR>—राधेश<BR>or राधेश्वर (˚धा-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of Rādhā,’<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधक
राधक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. liberal, bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधन|राधनं
राधन, अम्, n. the act of pleasing, satisfying,<BR>conciliating; pleasure, satisfaction; the act of accom-<BR>plishing, effecting, completing, succeeding; obtain-<BR>ing, acquisition; the means or instrument of accom-<BR>plishing anything; (आ), f. speaking, speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधस्
राधस्, अस्, n., Ved. favour, good-will, kindness,<BR>a gift of affection, a gift or present in general; bene-<BR>ficence, liberality, munificence; accomplishment of<BR>one's wishes, success, (अल्प-राधस्, one who has<BR>obtained but little success, unfortunate); striving to<BR>accomplish or gain, (अनन्य-राधस्, striving after<BR>nothing else); opulence, wealth, riches, affluence,<BR>might, power.<BR>—राधस्-पति, see under राध.<BR>—राधो-गूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. agreeable through<BR>kindness (according to Mahī-dhara); giving or be-<BR>stowing wealth.<BR>—राधो-देय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pre-<BR>sented with gifts or offerings; (अम्), n., Ved. the giving<BR>of presents, bestowing wealth, showing favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधि
राधि, राधी, see Gaṇa Bahvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1,<BR>45; [cf. कृष्ट-राधि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधिक
राधिक, अस्, m., N. of a king (son of Jaya-<BR>sena); (आ), f. a diminutive of the name Rādhā<BR>(expressive of endearment).<BR>—राधिका-विनोद, अस्,<BR>m. = राधा-विनोद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधेय|राधेयः
राधेय, अस्, m. (fr. राधा), a metronymic of<BR>Karṇa (as passing for the child of his foster-mother<BR>Rādhā, see राधा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्य
राध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be conciliated or<BR>propitiated, to be appeased or satisfied; to be accom-<BR>plished or performed, achievable; to be completed;<BR>to be obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्रेवकि
राध्रेवकि राध्रेवकि (?), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रान्द्र्य
रान्द्र्य रान्द्र्य, various reading for राण्ड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रान्धस
रान्धस रान्धस, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राप्य|राप्यः
राप्य राप्य. See rt. रप्, p. 832, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राभस्य|राभस्यं
राभस्य राभस्य, अम्, n. (fr. रभस), velo-<BR>city, impetuosity; eagerness, delight, joy, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम|रामं|रामः
राम राम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. रम्), pleasing,<BR>delighting, rejoicing; lovely, beautiful, charming,<BR>pleasant; obscure, dark-coloured, dark, black [cf.<BR>रात्रि]; white; (अस्), m. joy, pleasure; ‘the pleasing<BR>or beautiful one,’ N. of three celebrated mytholo-<BR>gical personages, commonly called Paraśu-rāma,<BR>Rāma-candra, and Bala-rāma, (of these the first two<BR>are always regarded as Avatāras of Viṣṇu, one born<BR>at the beginning, the other at the end of the second<BR>age: the first or Paraśu-rāma, ‘Rāma with the<BR>axe,’ forms the sixth Avatāra; he is sometimes called<BR>Jāmadagnya, as son of the sage Jamad-agni by<BR>Reṇukā, and sometimes Bhārgava, as descended from<BR>Bhṛgu, and he is the type of Brāhmanism arrayed in<BR>opposition to the military caste, see परशु-राम:<BR>the second, Rāma-candra, forms Viṣṇu's seventh<BR>Avatāra, and is the hero of the great epic poem<BR>called Rāmāyaṇa; his wife, Sītā, is sometimes re-<BR>garded as an Avatāra of Lakṣmī; he has the patro-<BR>nymic Dāśarathi, as son of Daśa-ratha, a king of the<BR>solar dynasty, and Rāghava, as descended from Raghu<BR>[see Raghu], and he typifies the conquering Kṣa-<BR>triyas advancing southwards and subjugating the bar-<BR>barous aborigines represented by the demon Rāvaṇa<BR>and his followers, the Rākṣasas: the third, Bala-<BR>rāma, ‘the strong Rāma,’ born in the third age, is<BR>a kind of Hindū Hercules, the seventh son of Vasu-<BR>deva and elder brother of Kṛṣṇa, both being de-<BR>scended from Yadu [who with Puru formed the<BR>two branches of the lunar dynasty]; he is sometimes<BR>called Halāyudha, ‘armed with a plough,’ sometimes<BR>Musalin, ‘club-armed,’ and although occasionally<BR>regarded as Viṣṇu's eighth Avatāra, is more properly<BR>an incarnation of the great serpent Śeṣa, see बल-<BR>देव, बल-राम: according to Jainas, a Rāma is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0843-a" target="_blank">Page0843-a+ 81</a>]<BR>enumerated among the nine white Balas [see बल]:<BR>in Viṣṇu-Purāṇa III. 2. a Rāma is mentioned<BR>among the seven Ṛṣis of the eighth Manvantara<BR>presided over by Manu Sāvarṇi, cf. Hari-vaṃśa 453);<BR>N. of the author of Ṛg-veda X. 110 (with the pa-<BR>tronymic Jāmadagnya belonging to Paraśu-rāma);<BR>N. of Varuṇa; of a person with the patronymic<BR>Mārgaveya; of various others persons or teachers;<BR>of a king of Malla-pura; of a king of Śṛṅga-vera;<BR>a lover; a kind of deer; a horse; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people; (आ), f. a beautiful female, handsome<BR>woman, a young and charming woman, a woman in<BR>general; a woman of low origin; N. of various<BR>plants (= श्वेत-कण्टकारी, गृह-कन्या, आराम-<BR>शीतला, अशोक); Asa Fœtida (= हिङ्गु); vermilion<BR>(= हिङ्गुल); a kind of pigment (= गो-रोचना);<BR>ruddle; a river; a kind of metre, ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘<BR>¯¯, ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯, ¯¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯, ¯<BR>¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯; N. of an Apsaras; of a daughter<BR>of Kumbhāṇḍa; of the mother of the ninth Arhat<BR>of the present Ava-sarpiṇī; (ई), f., Ved. darkness,<BR>night [cf. रात्रि]; (अम्), n. darkness; Chenopodium<BR>Album; = कुष्ठ; = तमाल-पत्त्र.<BR>—राम-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—राम-करी, f.<BR>‘joy-causing,’ N. of one of the Rāgiṇīs or female<BR>personifications of the musical modes.<BR>—राम-कर्-<BR>पूर or राम-कर्पूरक, अस्, m. a species of<BR>fragrant grass.<BR>—राम-कल्पद्रुम, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a work on law.<BR>—राम-कवच, अम्, n. ‘Rāma's<BR>breast-plate or charm,’ N. of part of the Brahma-<BR>yāmala-tantra (in which Śiva narrates to Pārvatī the<BR>most efficacious rites in the worship of Rāma).<BR>—रा-<BR>म-कान्त, अस्, m. a kind of sugar-cane; N. of a<BR>Scholiast.<BR>—राम-किरी or राम-कीरी (according to<BR>some) = राम-करी.<BR>—राम-किल्विष, अम्, n. an<BR>offence against Rāma.<BR>—राम-कुतूहल, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—राम-कुमार, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राम-कृष्ण, अस्, m., N. of various persons.<BR>—राम-कृष्ण-काव्य or राम-कृष्ण-विलोम-<BR>काव्य, अम्, n., N. of an artificial poem by the<BR>astronomer Sūrya celebrating the praises of Rāma<BR>and Kṛṣṇa (read either backwards or forwards; cf.<BR>विलोमाक्षर-काव्य).<BR>—राम-कृष्ण-पद्धति,<BR>इस्, f., N. of work.<BR>—राम-केली, f., N. of a Rāgiṇī<BR>or musical mode.<BR>—राम-केशव-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—राम-कौतुक, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—राम-क्षेत्र, अम्, n., N. of a district.<BR>—राम-गङ्गा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—राम-गायत्री,<BR>f., N. of a particular hymn on Rāma.<BR>—राम-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘Rāma's mountain,’ N. of several mountains<BR>(especially, according to some, of Citra-kūṭa in Bun-<BR>delkund and of another hill near Nagpore, now called<BR>Ramtek).<BR>—राम-गीत-गोविन्द, N. of a poem.<BR>—राम-गीता, f., N. of a poem partly extracted<BR>from the Adhyātma-rāmāyaṇa (in which spiritual<BR>knowledge is shown to be better than ritualistic<BR>observances; also आस्, f. pl.).<BR>—राम-गोविन्द-तीर्थ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—राम-ग्राम, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a kingdom.<BR>—राम-चक्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>particular mystical circle.<BR>—राम-चन्द्र, अस्, m.<BR>‘Rāma-moon’ or ‘moon-like Rāma,’ N. of Rāma<BR>the son of Daśa-ratha, the hero of the Rāmāyaṇa (see<BR>under राम, p. 842; although his name is connected<BR>with the moon, he is not of the lunar race, like<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Bala-rāma, but of the solar race of kings<BR>beginning with Vivasvat or ‘the Sun,’ whose son<BR>was Manu Vaivasvata or the Manu of the present<BR>period, and whose son again was Ikṣvāku, from<BR>whom sprang the two branches of the solar dynasty,<BR>the chief of which or that of Ayodhyā may be said<BR>to have commenced in Kakutstha, the ancestor of<BR>Rāma-candra); N. of various kings, authors, pre-<BR>ceptors &c. of later times.<BR>—रामचन्द्र-चम्पू,<BR>ऊस्, f., N. of a work by Kavi-candra (see चम्पू).<BR>—रामचन्द्र-चरित्र-सार, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>short poem by Agniveśa narrating the exploits of<BR>Rāma-candra.<BR>—रामचन्द्र-स्तव-राज, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an extract from the Sanat-kumāra-saṃhitā (in<BR>which Rāma-candra is represented as endowed with<BR>the divine nature of Kṛṣṇa).<BR>—रामचन्द्राश्रम<BR>(˚र-आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a commentator on the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0843-b" target="_blank">Page0843-b+ 80</a>]<BR>Sarasvatī-sūtra; (अम्), n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—राम-<BR>चन्द्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘rise of Rāma-<BR>candra,’ N. of a work by Puruṣottama.<BR>—राम-<BR>चर, अस्, m., N. of Bala-rāma.<BR>—राम-चरण,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the Rāma-vilāsa and of<BR>a commentary on the Sāhitya-darpaṇa.<BR>—राम-च-<BR>रित, अम्, n. the exploits of Rāma-candra the son of<BR>Daśa-ratha.<BR>—राम-च्छर्दनक, अस्, m. a species<BR>of plant.<BR>—राम-ज, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राम-<BR>जननी, f. the mother of Rāma (applicable to the<BR>mother of any one of the three Rāmas).<BR>—राम-<BR>जन्मन्, अ, n. the birth or birthday of Rāma.<BR>—राम-जीवन, अस्, m., N. of a son of Rudra-<BR>rāya.<BR>—राम-तपन, N. of an Upaniṣad; [cf.<BR>तपन.]<BR>—राम-तरुणी, f. a species of tree.<BR>—राम-तर्क-वाग्-ईश, अस्, m., N. of a gram-<BR>marian.<BR>—राम-तापनीय, अम्, n., N. of a well<BR>known Upaniṣad (belonging to the Atharva-veda).<BR>—राम-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of various persons.<BR>—राम-त्व, अम्, n. the being<BR>Rāma.<BR>—राम-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—राम-दर्शनादितस् (˚न-आद्˚), ind. after having<BR>seen Rāma.<BR>—राम-दास, अस्, m., N. of various<BR>persons.<BR>—राम-दूत, अस्, m. ‘Rāma's messenger,’<BR>N. of Hanumat; a monkey; (ई), f. a kind of basil.<BR>—राम-देव, अस्, m., N. of Rāma the son of<BR>Daśa-ratha; of various persons.<BR>—राम-द्वादशी,<BR>f., N. of the twelfth day in one of the halves of the<BR>month Jyaiṣṭha.<BR>—राम-धर, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—राम-नगर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—राम-<BR>नवमी, f., N. of the ninth day in the light half of<BR>the month Caitra, being the birthday of Rāma-<BR>candra.<BR>—राम-नवमी-निर्णय, अस्, m., N. of<BR>certain verses on the fast and feast to be observed on<BR>the above day.<BR>—राम-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of Rāma<BR>the son of Daśa-ratha; of various persons.<BR>—राम-<BR>नाम-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular religious<BR>observance.<BR>—राम-नारायण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>grammarian.<BR>—राम-नारायण-जीव, अस्, and रा-<BR>म-नृपति, इस्, m., N. of two kings.<BR>—राम-<BR>न्यायालङ्कार (˚य-अल्˚) and राम-पण्डित and<BR>राम-पाल, अस्, m., N. of various persons.<BR>—राम-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a village.<BR>—राम-पूग, अस्,<BR>m. a species of small Areca or betel-nut tree, Areca<BR>Triandra.<BR>—राम-पूजा-शरणी, f., N. of a work.<BR>—राम-पूर्व-तापनीय, अम्, n. the first part of<BR>the Rāma-tāpanīya, q. v.<BR>—राम-प्रकाश, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a commentary.<BR>—राम-प्रसाद-तर्क-वाग्-<BR>ईश and राम-प्रसाद-तर्कालङ्कार, अस्, m., N.<BR>of two Paṇḍits.<BR>—राम-बाण = राम-वाण, q. v.<BR>—राम-भक्त, अस्, m. a worshipper of Rāma; a<BR>proper N.<BR>—राम-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of various<BR>persons.<BR>—राम-भद्र, अस्, m., N. of Rāma the<BR>son of Daśa-ratha; of various persons.<BR>—राम-<BR>मन्त्र, अस्, m. a Mantra addressed to Rāma.<BR>—राममन्त्र-पटल, अम्, n. a collection of<BR>Mantras addressed to Rāma.<BR>—राम-मिश्र and<BR>राम-मोहन, अस्, m., N. of two persons.<BR>—राम-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. a particular diagram.<BR>—राम-र-<BR>हस्य, अम्, n., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—राम-राज,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—राम-राम, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a preceptor.<BR>—राम-रुद्र-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of<BR>an author; (ई), f., N. of his commentary on Dina-kara's<BR>treatise relating to invocations.<BR>—राम-लवण, अम्,<BR>n. a kind of salt.<BR>—राम-लिङ्ग-कृति, इस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR>—राम-लेखा, f., N. of a princess.<BR>—राम-वर्धन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राम-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a commentator on the Rāma-<BR>gītā.<BR>—राम-वल्लभ, अम्, n. Cassia bark.<BR>—रा-<BR>म-वाजपेयिन्, ई, m., N. of an author.<BR>—राम-<BR>वाण, अस्, m. ‘Rāma's arrow,’ a kind of sugar-cane;<BR>a particular medicinal preparation.<BR>—राम-विलास,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a poem by Rāma-caraṇa.<BR>—राम-<BR>विलास-काव्य, अम्, n., N. of a poem in four chapters<BR>by Hari-nātha (describing the amours of Rāma and<BR>Sītā).<BR>—राम-वीणा, f. ‘Rāma's lute,’ a kind of<BR>lute, (said to be also applicable ironically to the horn<BR>blown by Bala-rāma.)<BR>—राम-व्याकरण, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a grammatical work by Vopa-deva.<BR>—राम-<BR>व्रतिन्, इनस्, m. pl. ‘devoted to Rāma,’ N. of a<BR>sect.<BR>—राम-शर, अस्, m. a kind of sugar-cane.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0843-c" target="_blank">Page0843-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—राम-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Uṇādi-koṣa (a metrical work on words formed with<BR>Uṇādi suffixes).<BR>—राम-शीतला, f. = आराम-शीतला,<BR>a fragrant plant.<BR>—राम-श्री-पाद, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>preceptor.<BR>—राम-षड्-अक्षर-मन्त्र-राज, अस्,<BR>m. a particular Mantra or prayer of six syllables<BR>addressed to Rāma.<BR>—राम-संयमिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of the author of certain Vedānta precepts in verse.<BR>—राम-सख, अस्, m. ‘Rāma's friend,’ N. of<BR>Sugrīva.<BR>—राम-सरस्, अस्, n., N. of a sacred lake.<BR>—राम-सहस्र-नाम-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. ‘praise of<BR>Rāma's thousand names,’ N. of a section of the Brahma-<BR>yāmala-tantra.<BR>—राम-साहि, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—राम-सिंह, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राम-सूक्त,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a hymn.<BR>—राम-सेतु, उस्, m. ‘Rā-<BR>ma's bridge,’ a ridge of sand now called Adam's<BR>bridge.<BR>—राम-सेनक, अस्, m. Gentiana Cherayta.<BR>—राम-सेवक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—राम-<BR>स्तुति, इस्, f. and राम-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. ‘Rāma's praise,’<BR>N. of two works.<BR>—राम-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>statue of Rāma.<BR>—राम-हृदय, अम्, n. ‘Rāma's<BR>heart,’ N. of a part of the Adhyātma-rāmāyaṇa re-<BR>vealing the supposed mystical essence of Rāma.<BR>—राम-ह्रद, अस्, m. ‘Rāma's lake,’ N. of a<BR>sacred bathing-place.<BR>—रामाचक्र, probably for<BR>राम-चक्र.<BR>—रामाचार्य (˚म-आच्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of various religious teachers.<BR>—रामा-च्छर्दनक,<BR>various reading for राम-च्छर्दनक.<BR>—रामात्-<BR>मैक्य-प्रकाशिका (˚म-आत्˚), f., N. of a treatise<BR>by Satya-jñānānanda-tīrtha Yati setting forth Rāma's<BR>identity with the Supreme Soul.<BR>—रामा-देवी, f., N.<BR>of the mother of Jaya-deva.<BR>—रामाधिकरण<BR>(˚म-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Rāma.<BR>—रा-<BR>मानन्द (˚म-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a disciple of<BR>Rāmānuja and founder of a subdivision of the Vaiṣ-<BR>ṇava sect.<BR>—रामानन्द-स्वामिन्, ई, m. the author<BR>of the Vaidya-bhūṣaṇa.<BR>—रामानुज (˚म-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘younger brother of Rāma,’ (this title would<BR>be applicable to Kṛṣṇa as born after Bala-rāma of<BR>the same father); N. of a celebrated reformer, author<BR>of several Vedānta treatises, (he belonged to the sect<BR>of the Vaiṣṇavas, was regarded as an incarnation of<BR>Śeṣa, and flourished in the twelfth century in<BR>the south of India, where he combated the Śaivas);<BR>रामानुजम् मतम्, the sect of Rāmānuja.<BR>—रा-<BR>मानुष्टुभ् (˚म-अन्˚), प्, f., N. of a particular<BR>prayer addressed to Rāma.<BR>—रामाभिनन्द (˚म-<BR>अभ्˚) or रामाभ्युदय (˚म-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a drama.<BR>—रामायण (˚म-अयन), अम्, n.<BR>‘Rāma's goings or adventures,’ N. of Vālmīki's<BR>famous epic poem describing the adventures of Rāma-<BR>candra, (it contains about 24000 verses in seven<BR>books, called Kāṇḍas, viz. 1. Bāla-kāṇḍa or Ādi-k˚,<BR>2. Ayodhyā-k˚, 3. Araṇya-k˚, 4. Kiṣkindhyā-k˚,<BR>5. Sundara-k˚, 6. Yuddha-k˚, 7. Uttara-k˚; the<BR>seventh is thought to be a comparatively modern<BR>addition, and gives the history of Rāma and Sītā after<BR>their reunion and installation as king and queen of<BR>Ayodhyā, afterwards dramatized by Bhava-bhūti in<BR>the Uttara-rāma-caritra; Rāma's character, as de-<BR>scribed in the Rāmāyaṇa, is that of a perfect man,<BR>born to suffering and self-denial, which he bears<BR>with more than human patience; the author, Vālmīki,<BR>was probably a real person, and although there are<BR>two recensions of the poem, of which the purest<BR>belongs to the north-west of India, six books at least<BR>are thought to be the work of one man, and not,<BR>like the Mahā-bhārata, the production of different<BR>epochs and minds); (अस्, ई, अम्), relating to the<BR>history of Rāma; a descendant of Rāma, (see<BR>Atharva-veda VI. 83, 3.)<BR>—रामायणीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating or belonging to the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—रामार्-<BR>चन-चन्द्रिका (˚म-अर्˚), f., N. of a work.<BR>—रा-<BR>मार्य (˚म-आर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—रा-<BR>मालिङ्गन-काम (˚मा-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, longing for<BR>the embrace of a handsome person; (अस्), m. epithet<BR>of the red-flowering globe-amaranth.<BR>—रामा-वक्-<BR>षोजोपम (˚ज-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, resembling the<BR>breasts of a beautiful woman; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>the Anas Casarca or ruddy goose.<BR>—रामाश्रम<BR>(˚म-आश्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रामाश्वमेध<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">Page0844-a+ 75</a>]<BR>(˚म-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘Rāma's horse-sacrifice,’ N. of a<BR>part of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—रामाश्वमेधिक, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, relating to Rāma's horse-sacrifice.<BR>—रामेन्-<BR>द्र-यति (˚म-इन्˚), इस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>a Vedānta treatise called the Viveka-sāra.<BR>—रामेन्-<BR>द्र-वन, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—रामेश<BR>(˚म-ईश), अस्, m. a proper N.; (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>Liṅga.<BR>—रामेश्वर (˚म-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>various persons; (अम्), n., N. of a Liṅga; of a<BR>Tīrtha or sacred bathing-place.<BR>—रामेषु (˚म-<BR>इषु), उस्, m. ‘Rāma's arrow,’ epithet of a species<BR>of sugar-cane; a proper N.<BR>—रामोत्तर-तापनीय<BR>(˚म-उत्˚), अम्, n. the second part of the Rāma-<BR>tāpanīya; [cf. राम-पूर्व-त्˚.]<BR>—रामोद (˚म-<BR>उद), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रामोदायन, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. the preceding), a patronymic.<BR>—रामोपनिषद्<BR>(˚म-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of one of the more recent<BR>Upaniṣads of the Atharva-veda.<BR>—रामोपाध्याय<BR>(˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—रामोपा-<BR>सक (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m. a worshipper of Rāma-<BR>candra the son of Daśa-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0842-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामक|रामकः
रामक, अस्, &c. (fr. the Caus. of rt. रम्), one<BR>who delights or gratifies, delighting; = रमक,<BR>q. v.; (अस्), m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामठ|रामठं|रामठः
रामठ, अस्, अम्, m. n. Asa Fœtida; (अस्),<BR>m. Alangium Hexapetalum; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (ई), f. = नाडी-हिङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामण|रामणः
रामण, अस्, m., N. of two plants, Diospyros Embry-<BR>opteris; = गिरि-निम्ब; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामणि
रामणि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामणीयक|रामणीयकं
रामणीयक, अम्, n. (fr. 1. रमणीय), loveli-<BR>ness, agreeableness, charmingness, delightfulness,<BR>beauty; N. of a Dvīpa; (अस्, ई, अम्), lovely, agree-<BR>able, beautiful, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामल
रामल, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामाण्डार
रामाण्डार, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामि
रामि, इस्, m. (fr. राम), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामिन्
रामिन्, ई, इणी, इ, delighting sexually, in क्षण-<BR>र्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामिल|रामिलः
रामिल, अस्, m. a lover, husband; the god of<BR>love, Kāma-deva; N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामी
रामी, f. See under राम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम्या
राम्या, f., Ved. night; [cf. रात्रि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामुष
रामुष रामुष, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम्भ|रांभ|रांभः|राम्भः
राम्भ राम्भ, अस्, m. (fr. 1. रम्भ), the<BR>bamboo staff of a religious student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राय|रायः
राय राय, अस्, m. a king, prince, (at the<BR>beginning or end of a proper N. used as a title of<BR>honour, = राजन्, of which it is a corruption.)<BR>—रा-<BR>य-मुकुट, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Pada-<BR>candrikā, a commentary on the Amara-koṣa; of<BR>the author of a work on law.<BR>—राय-राघव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the Hasta-ratnāvalī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायण|रायणं
रायण रायण, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. रै), sounding, crying, making a noise; pain<BR>(= पीडा).<BR>—रायणेन्द्र-सरस्वती (˚ण-इन्˚), m.,<BR>N. of a commentator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायभाटी
रायभाटी रायभाटी, f. the stream of a<BR>river; [cf. रय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायस्काम
रायस्काम रायस्-काम, रायस्-पोष, रायो-<BR>वाज, &c. See under 3. रै, p. 853, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायाणनीय
रायाणनीय रायाणनीय, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायान
रायान रायान or रायन (?), अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रारा
रारा रारा. See राढा, p. 841, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राल|रालः
राल राल or रालक, अस्, m. the resin of<BR>Shorea Robusta (= अराल).<BR>—राल-कार्य, अस्, m.<BR>Shorea Robusta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राव|रावः
राव राव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. रु), a cry,<BR>shriek, roar, scream, yell, roaring, bellowing, vocife-<BR>ration, the cry of any animal; a sound, noise in<BR>general; [cf. रव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावण|रावणः
रावण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Caus.), screaming, roar-<BR>ing, crying, bellowing, bewailing, making lamentation;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">Page0844-b+ 77</a>]<BR>(अस्), m. ‘the Vociferator,’ N. of the ruler of Laṅkā<BR>or Ceylon and the famous chief of the Rākṣasas or<BR>demons whose subjugation and destruction by Rāma-<BR>candra, the seventh incarnation of Viṣṇu, form the<BR>subject of the Rāmāyaṇa, (as son of Viśravas, he was<BR>younger brother of Kuvera, but by a different mother,<BR>Ilavilā being the mother of Kuvera, and Keśinī of<BR>the three other brothers, Rāvaṇa, Vibhīṣaṇa, and<BR>Kumbha-karṇa; both Rāvaṇa and Kuvera, the god<BR>of wealth, are often called Paulastya, as grandchildren<BR>of the Ṛṣi Pulastya, one of the seven or ten mind-<BR>born sons of Brahmā, and as Kuvera is king of the<BR>Yakṣas, so is Rāvaṇa of the Rākṣasas, the latter,<BR>however, are always malignant beings [see राक्षस],<BR>and Rāvaṇa himself is one of the worst of the many<BR>impersonations of evil common in Hindū mythology;<BR>he is the Satan of the Rāmāyaṇa as Duryodhana is<BR>of the Mahā-bhārata; he has ten heads [whence his<BR>names Daśa-grīva, Daśānana, &c.] and twenty arms,<BR>symbolizing strength; his power is described as so<BR>great, that where he is ‘there the sun does not give<BR>out its heat, the winds through fear of him do not<BR>blow, the fire ceases to burn, and the ocean becomes<BR>motionless;’ he even, by his power, defeated his own<BR>brother Vaiśravaṇa or Kuvera, and carried off his self-<BR>moving car, called Puṣpaka, the wonders of which<BR>are described in the Rāmāyaṇa; this potency was,<BR>as usual, acquired by self-inflicted austerities, which<BR>had obtained from Brahmā a boon, in virtue of which<BR>Rāvaṇa was invulnerable by gods and divine beings<BR>of all kinds, though not by men or a god in human<BR>form; as Viṣṇu became incarnate in Rāma-candra<BR>to destroy Rāvaṇa, so other gods produced innume-<BR>rable monkeys, bears, and various semi-divine animals<BR>to do battle with the legions of demons, his subjects,<BR>under Khara, Dūṣaṇa, and his other generals; see<BR>हनु-मत्); a patronymic from Ravaṇa; N. of the<BR>author of a commentary on the Sāma-veda; of one<BR>on the Ṛg-veda; of the author of the Arka-cikitsā;<BR>of a king of Kaśmīra (mentioned together with Indra-<BR>jit and Vibhīṣaṇa); (अम्), n. the act of screaming,<BR>&c.; N. of a Muhūrta.<BR>—रावण-गङ्गा, f. ‘Rā-<BR>vaṇa's Ganges,’ N. of a river in Laṅkā (called after<BR>the Rākṣasa Rāvaṇa).<BR>—रावण-हस्र, a parti-<BR>cular stringed instrument.<BR>—रावण-ह्रद, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a lake (from which the Śata-dru or Sutlej<BR>takes its rise).<BR>—रावणारि (˚ण-अरि), इस्, m. Rā-<BR>vaṇa's enemy, i. e. Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणि|रावणिः
रावणि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Rāvaṇa, N. of<BR>Indra-jit (eldest son of the demon Rāvaṇa) or of<BR>any son of Rāvaṇa; of the author of a Bāla-tantra;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl. the sons of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राविन्
राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, screaming, crying, roaring, bel-<BR>lowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावन्
रावन् रावन्. See p. 837, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावौट
रावौट रावौट, N. of a royal race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राश्
राश् राश्, various reading for rt. रास्,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशभ
राशभ राशभ, incorrect for रासभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशि|राशिः
राशि राशि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 132. fr. rt. 1. अश्), a heap, mass, pile, accumu-<BR>lation, congeries, group, multitude, quantity, number;<BR>the figure or figures put down for an arithmetical<BR>operation (such as multiplying, dividing, &c.); a<BR>measure of quantity (Ved. = द्रोण); a sign of the<BR>zodiac (as being a certain sum or quantity of de-<BR>grees), one twelfth part of the ecliptic, an astrolo-<BR>gical house; N. of an Ekāha (Ved.).<BR>—राशि-गत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, placed in a heap, heaped, piled up,<BR>accumulated; computed, summed up.<BR>—राशि-चक्र,<BR>अम्, n. the zodiacal circle, zodiac; epithet of a par-<BR>ticular mystical circle.<BR>—राशि-त्रय, अम्, n. ‘triad<BR>of numbers,’ the rule of three.<BR>—राशि-नामन्, अ,<BR>n. a name given to a child taken from the Rāśi<BR>under which he is born.<BR>—राशि-प, अस्, m. the regent<BR>of an astrological house.<BR>—राशि-प्रविभाग, अस्, m.<BR>a division or distribution of the twelve signs of the<BR>zodiac (under the twenty-eight Nakṣatras); N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-c" target="_blank">Page0844-c+ 80</a>]<BR>the 102nd Adhyāya of Varāha-mihira's Vṛhat-saṃ-<BR>hitā.<BR>—राशि-भाग, अस्, m. a fraction.<BR>—राशिभा-<BR>गानुबन्ध (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, m. the addition of a<BR>fraction.<BR>—राशिभागापवाह (˚ग-अप्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>subtraction of a fraction.<BR>—राशि-भेद, अस्, m. a<BR>portion or division of a zodiacal sign or astrological<BR>house.<BR>—राशि-भोग, अस्, m. the passage of the sun<BR>or moon or any planet through a sign of the zodiac.<BR>—राशि-व्यवहार, अस्, m. (in arithmetic) the<BR>method for finding the quantity contained in a heap.<BR>—राशि-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or being in a<BR>heap, heaped up, accumulated.<BR>—राशी-करण, अम्,<BR>n. the making into a heap, heaping up, piling to-<BR>gether.<BR>—राशी-करण-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work of the Pāśupatas.<BR>—राशी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -क-<BR>रोति, -कुरुते, &c., to make or form into a heap,<BR>heap together, pile up, accumulate.<BR>—राशी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, made into a heap, heaped up, accumu-<BR>lated.<BR>—राशी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to be-<BR>come a heap, be piled up or accumulated.<BR>—राशी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become a heap, accumulated, piled,<BR>heaped.<BR>—राश्य्-अंश = नवांश, q. v.<BR>—राश्य्-अधि-<BR>प, अस्, m. the regent of an astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्र|राष्ट्रं|राष्ट्रः
राष्ट्र राष्ट्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. राज्; also<BR>अस्, m. in Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 3050), a kingdom,<BR>realm, empire, dominion, sovereignty; a district,<BR>country, region, territory, inhabited country; a people,<BR>nation, subjects; (अस्, अम्), m. n. any public calamity<BR>(as famine, plague, &c.), affliction; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a king (a son of Kāśi).<BR>—राष्ट्र-कर्षण, अम्,<BR>n. distressing or oppressing a kingdom.<BR>—राष्ट्र-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring a kingdom.<BR>—राष्ट्र-<BR>कूट, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race.<BR>—राष्ट्र-गुप्ति, इस्,<BR>f. protection of a kingdom.<BR>—राष्ट्र-गोप, अस्, m.<BR>a guardian or protector of a kingdom.<BR>—राष्ट्र-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n. system of government, government.<BR>—राष्ट्र-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. giving dominion.<BR>—राष्ट्र-दिप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (see दिप्सु), Ved.<BR>intending to injure a country or people, menacing a<BR>country.<BR>—राष्ट्र-देवी, f., N. of the wife of Citra-<BR>bhānu.<BR>—राष्ट्र-पति, इस्, m. the lord of a kingdom,<BR>king, sovereign, (राष्ट्रपत is given as an adj.<BR>from this word.)<BR>—राष्ट्र-पाल, अस्, m. a protector<BR>or guardian of a kingdom, king, sovereign; N. of a<BR>son of Ugra-sena; (ई), f., N. of a daughter of Ugra-<BR>sena.<BR>—राष्ट्र-पालिका, f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Ugra-sena.<BR>—राष्ट्र-भङ्ग, अस्, m. breaking up<BR>or dissolution of a kingdom.<BR>—राष्ट्र-भय, अम्,<BR>n. fear for a kingdom, danger threatening a country.<BR>—राष्ट्र-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, supporting a kingdom,<BR>taking care of the sovereignty; (त्), m., N. of a son<BR>of Bharata; (तस्), m. pl. the subjects of a kingdom;<BR>epithet of dice (in Atharva-veda VII. 109, 6); of<BR>certain prayers and oblations; (त्), f., N. of an<BR>Apsaras.<BR>—राष्ट्र-भृति, इस्, f. or राष्ट्र-<BR>भृत्य, अम्, n., Ved. maintenance of government,<BR>support of authority.<BR>—राष्ट्र-भेद, अस्, m. divi-<BR>sion of a kingdom.<BR>—राष्ट्र-वर्धन, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, increasing the kingdom, exalting or extending<BR>dominion; (अस्), m., N. of a minister of Daśa-ratha<BR>and Rāma.<BR>—राष्ट्र-वासिन्, ई, m. an inhabitant of<BR>a kingdom, subject.<BR>—राष्ट्रान्त-पाल (˚र-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the protector of the borders of a country.<BR>—राष्ट्राभिवृद्धि (˚र-अभ्˚), इस्, f. the increase<BR>of a kingdom, exaltation of a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रक|राष्ट्रकः
राष्ट्रक at the end of an adj. comp. = राष्ट्र,<BR>a kingdom, &c.; (अस्, इका, अम्), dwelling in a<BR>kingdom or country; (इका), f. a kind of Solanum<BR>(= बृहती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रि|राष्ट्रिः
राष्ट्रि, इस्, f. = राष्ट्री, a female ruler, pro-<BR>prietress, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिक|राष्ट्रिकः
राष्ट्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to or inhabiting<BR>a kingdom; (अस्), m. an inhabitant of a kingdom,<BR>subject; the ruler of a kingdom, governor; [cf.<BR>राष्ट्रक above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिन्
राष्ट्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. possessing or occupying<BR>a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिय|राष्ट्रियः
राष्ट्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a kingdom<BR>or country; born in a kingdom; (अस्), m. a king's<BR>brother-in-law (in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0844-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्री
राष्ट्री, f., Ved. a female ruler or sovereign or<BR>proprietress; (Sāy.) = राजन-शीला; a form राष्ट्री,<BR>m., is found in Ṛg-veda VI. 4, 5 (according to Sāy.)<BR>= राज्य-वत्, possessing a kingdom, a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रीय|राष्ट्रीयः
राष्ट्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a country or<BR>kingdom; (अस्), m. a king's brother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्
रास् 1. रास् (connected with rt. 1. रस्),<BR>cl. 1. A. रासते, ररासे, रासितुम्, to<BR>scream, cry, yell, howl (said of animals); to sound,<BR>make any cry or noise: Intens. रारास्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रारास्यमान
रारास्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, crying aloud, uttering<BR>loud lamentations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास|रासः
रास, अस्, m. uproar, confused noise, din; noise,<BR>sound in general; N. of a particular rustic dance (in<BR>this sense probably connected with लास, लास्य, q. v.),<BR>a kind of circular dance practised by cowherds, (especi-<BR>ally) that in which Kṛṣṇa and the Gopīs engaged;<BR>any sportive game or festive amusement, amorous<BR>pastime, play in general; (according to some also)<BR>speech; a chain.<BR>—रास-क्रीडा, f. a sportive dance,<BR>the circular dance of Kṛṣṇa and the cowherdesses.<BR>—रास-मण्डल, अम्, n. Kṛṣṇa's circular dance<BR>or dancing-ground.<BR>—रास-यात्रा, f. a festival in<BR>honour of Kṛṣṇa and his dances with the Gopīs on<BR>the full moon of the month Kārttika.<BR>—रासे-रस,<BR>अस्, m. (रासे, loc. c.), the dance described above;<BR>pastime, sport, festive mirth; a company, assembly,<BR>party; love, desire, sentiment; the sixth night after<BR>delivery when the family sit up all night (?); alchemy;<BR>[cf. रस.]<BR>—रासोत्सव (˚स-उत्˚), अस्, m. the Rāsa<BR>festival or festive dances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासक|रासकं
रासक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind of drama or<BR>dramatic entertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभ|रासभः
रासभ, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding, braying; neighing<BR>(applied in Ṛg-veda III. 53, 5. to the horse of<BR>Indra); (अस्), m. an ass, jackass, donkey, (in Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 34, 9, I. 116, 2. the chariot of the Aśvins is<BR>said to be drawn by a single ass, and other authorities<BR>mention two asses, but in other places their car is<BR>described as drawn by golden-winged, falcon-like,<BR>swan-like horses); (ई), f. a she-ass.<BR>—रासभ-<BR>धूसर, अस्, आ, अम्, ass-grey, grey as an ass, light<BR>brown.<BR>—रासभ-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, yoked with<BR>asses, drawn by asses.<BR>—रासभ-वन्दिनी, f. Arabian<BR>jasmine.<BR>—रासभ-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रासभाराव (˚भ-आर्˚), अस्, m. the braying of<BR>asses.<BR>—रासभारुण (˚भ-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, brown<BR>as an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्य
रास्य in गो-रास्य, अस्, m., N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्
रास् 2. रास्, a form of rt. 1. रा, to give,<BR>(to which forms like रासते, अरासत,<BR>रासन्, रासत् are sometimes referred; see Naigh.<BR>III. 20.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासन
रासन रासन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रसना), relating<BR>to the tongue, perceptible by the tongue, pertaining to<BR>the sense or organ of taste, savoury, palatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभ|रासभः
रासभ रासभ. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासायन
रासायन रासायन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रसायन),<BR>relating to an elixir, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्ना
रास्ना रास्ना, f. (according to Uṇādi-S. III.<BR>15. fr. rt. 1. रस्), a girdle (Ved.; cf. रशना); N.<BR>of two plants, Mimosa Octandra, a thorny shrub;<BR>the ichneumon plant; a sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्नाका
रास्नाका, f., Ved. a small girdle or band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्नाव
रास्नाव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a girdle, girdled,<BR>girt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्प
रास्प रास्प, Ved. (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda V. 43, 14) a sacrificial ladle (= 2. जुहू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्पिर
रास्पिर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to Sāy.)<BR>holding the sacrificial ladles, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्पिन
रास्पिन रास्पिन, अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Sāy. either fr. rt. 1. रस् or rt. रप्), Ved. sounding<BR>forth praise, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहक्षति
राहक्षति राहक्षति, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहित्य|राहित्यं
राहित्य राहित्य, अम्, n. (fr. रहित), the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">Page0845-b+ 78</a>]<BR>being without anything, the being destitute of, free-<BR>dom from anything, destitution, destituteness (at the<BR>end of a comp., e. g. कृपा-राहित्य, the being<BR>without compassion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहिल
राहिल राहिल, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहु|राहुः
राहु राहु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. रह्;<BR>probably connected with rts. रभ्, ग्रभ्), ‘the<BR>looser’ or ‘the seizer,’ N. of a Daitya or demon who<BR>is supposed to seize the sun and moon and thus<BR>cause eclipses, (according to the common myth<BR>he was a son of Vipra-citti and Sinhikā, and had<BR>four arms, his lower part ending in a tail; he was the<BR>instigator of all mischief among the Daityas, and<BR>when the gods had produced the Amṛta or nectar<BR>from the churned ocean, he disguised himself like<BR>one of them and drank a portion of it, but the Sun<BR>and Moon having detected his fraud and informed<BR>Viṣṇu, the latter severed his head and two of his<BR>arms from the rest of his body; the portion of nectar<BR>he had swallowed having secured his immortality,<BR>the head and tail were transferred to the stellar<BR>sphere, the head wreaking its vengeance on the Sun<BR>and Moon by occasionally swallowing them for a<BR>time, while the tail, under the name of Ketu, gave<BR>birth to a numerous progeny of comets and fiery<BR>meteors: in astronomy Rāhu is variously regarded<BR>as a dragon's head, as the ascending node of the<BR>moon, or as one of the planets); an eclipse or<BR>(rather) the moment of occultation or obscuration;<BR>the regent of the south-west quarter.<BR>—राहु-गत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘gone to Rāhu,’ darkened, ob-<BR>scured, eclipsed.<BR>—राहु-ग्रसन or राहु-ग्र-<BR>हण, अम्, n. ‘seizure or swallowing by Rāhu,’ an<BR>eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>—राहु-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘swallowed by Rāhu,’ eclipsed.<BR>—राहु-ग्रास<BR>or राहु-ग्राह, अस्, m. an eclipse of the sun or<BR>moon, the immersion at an eclipse.<BR>—राहु-च्छत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. green ginger.<BR>—राहु-दर्शन, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. ‘appearance of Rāhu,’ an eclipse.<BR>—राहु-पर्-<BR>वन्, अ, n. the day or period of an eclipse.<BR>—राहु-<BR>पीडा, f. ‘oppression by Rāhu,’ an eclipse.<BR>—राहु-<BR>पूजा, f. the worship of Rāhu.<BR>—राहु-भेदिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘severing Rāhu,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—राहु-<BR>मूर्ध-भिद्, त्, or राहु-मूर्ध-हर, अस्, m.<BR>‘decapitator of Rāhu,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—राहु-<BR>रत्न, अम्, n. Rāhu's jewel, N. of a kind of jewel.<BR>—राहु-संस्पर्श, अस्, m. contact with Rāhu,<BR>i. e. an eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>—राहु-सूतक,<BR>अम्, n. the birth or appearance of Rāhu, an eclipse<BR>of the sun or moon.<BR>—राहूच्छिष्ट (˚हु-उच्˚) or<BR>राहूत्सृष्ट (˚हु-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘left or despised by<BR>Rāhu,’ a shalote, Allium Ascalonicum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहवि
राहवि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुल
राहुल, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śākya-muni; of<BR>a son of Śuddhodana; of a minister of Hiouen-<BR>thsang.<BR>—राहुल-सू, ऊस्, m. father of Rāhula, i. e.<BR>Śākya-muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुलक
राहुलक, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुलत
राहुलत (?), अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist patriarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूगण
राहूगण राहूगण, अस्, m. (fr. रहूगण),<BR>Ved. a patronymic of Gotama; (आस्), m. pl. of the<BR>following word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूगण्य
राहूगण्य, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
रि 1. रि (connected with rts. 1. री, 4. ऋ),<BR>cl. 6. P. रियति, रिराय, रेष्यति, अरैषीत्,<BR>रेतुम्, to go, move; cl. 5. P. रिणोति, &c., to hurt<BR>[cf. rt. 4. ऋ]; cl. 9. P. A. रिणाति, रिणीते, &c., to<BR>go, move; to draw out, drive out, set free, expel;<BR>to separate, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 60,<BR>2. अरिणीत = योजनात् प्रापितवन्तः); to emit; to<BR>bestow, grant; to hurt, injure, kill; to be injured<BR>(A.); to howl, &c. [cf. rt. 1. री]: Caus. राययति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अरीरयत्: Desid. रिरीषति: Intens.<BR>रेरीयते, रेरयीति, रेरेति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिणत्
रिणत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. injuring, hurting; setting<BR>free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
रि 2. रि, at the end of adj. comps.; [cf.<BR>अति-रि, बृहद्-रि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
रि 3. रि (a contraction of ऋषभ), the<BR>second note of the Hindū gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिःफ
रिःफ रिःफ, अम्, n. (fr. Gr. ῥιφή), Ved.<BR>epithet of the twelfth astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्त|रिक्तं
रिक्त रिक्त, रिक्थ, &c. See below and<BR>p. 846, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्वन्
रिक्वन् रिक्वन्, आ, m., Ved. = स्तेन, a thief<BR>(according to Naigh. III. 24).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्षा
रिक्षा रिक्षा, f. a nit (= लिक्षा); a mote<BR>in a sun-beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिख्
रिख् रिख् (connected with rts. रिङ्ख्,<BR>रिङ्ग्, रख्, रङ्ख्), cl. 1. P. रेखति,<BR>&c., to go, move (so given by Vopa-deva, but by<BR>other grammarians identified in this sense with rt.<BR>रिङ्ख् below); cl. 6. P. (not in use, but apparently<BR>the original form of rt. लिख्, cl. 6. लिखति, q. v.),<BR>to scratch, scrape, write; [cf. रेखा; cf. also Gr.<BR>ἐρείκω, ἐρέχθω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्ख्|रिंख्
रिङ्ख् रिङ्ख् (connected with rts. रिख्,<BR>रख्, रङ्ख्, रिङ्ग्, रङ्ग्), cl. 1. P.<BR>रिङ्खति, &c., to go, move, creep, crawl (said of<BR>young children); to go slowly; to slip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्ख|रिङ्खः
रिङ्ख, अस्, m. See under रिङ्खा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्खण|रिंखण|रिंखणं|रिङ्खणं
रिङ्खण, अम्, n. the act of crawling, creeping<BR>(said of children who creep on all fours).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्खा|रिंखा
रिङ्खा, f. creeping, sliding; dancing; one of a<BR>horse's paces; a horse's hoof; deceiving, disappoint-<BR>ing, (according to some also अस्, m. in the previous<BR>senses); the plant Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्ग्|रिंग्
रिङ्ग् रिङ्ग् (connected with rts. रङ्ग्,<BR>रिङ्ख्, &c., see above), cl. 1. P. रिङ्गति,<BR>&c., to go, move, creep, crawl (said of young children),<BR>to move slowly or with difficulty; to slip: Caus.<BR>रिङ्गयति, &c., to cause to creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गण|रिंगण|रिंगणं|रिङ्गणं
रिङ्गण, अम्, n. the act of moving, creeping,<BR>crawling (= रिङ्खण); slipping, sliding; deviating<BR>(from rectitude, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गत्
रिङ्गत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, creeping, crawling, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गमाण
रिङ्गमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, creeping, crawling,<BR>slipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गि|रिंगिः|रिङ्गिः
रिङ्गि, इस्, f. going, moving, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गित|रिंगितं
रिङ्गित, अम्, n. motion, surging (of waves).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गिन्
रिङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, creeping, crawling (said of young<BR>children).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिच्
रिच् रिच्, cl. 7. P. A. रिणक्ति, रिङ्क्ते,<BR>रिरेच, रिरिचे, रेक्ष्यति, -ते, अरिचत् or<BR>अरैक्षीत् (Vedic forms अरिरेचीत्, अरैक्), अरिक्त<BR>(1st sing. अरिक्षि), रेक्तुम्, to empty, make empty,<BR>evacuate, clear, purge, remove, separate, divide; to<BR>resign, give up, deliver up, part with, sell, (but ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 24, 9. ‘to recover,<BR>get back’); to leave, leave behind, bequeath; cl. 10.<BR>1. P. रेचयति, रेचति, &c., to divide, separate; to<BR>disconnect, disjoin; to leave, abandon; to join, mix:<BR>Pass. रिच्यते, Aor. अरेचि, to be emptied, &c.; to be<BR>deprived of, lose, be freed from; to be destroyed,<BR>perish: Caus. रेचयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरीरिचत्, to<BR>cause to empty, make empty; to discharge, emit (as<BR>breath); to abandon, give up: Desid. रिरिक्षति,<BR>-ते: Intens. रेरिच्यते, रेरेक्ति; [cf. Zend ric; Gr.<BR>λείπ-ω, λιμπάν-ω, λεῖμμα, λείψανο-ν, λοιπός; Lat.<BR>linqu-o, re-linqu-o, re-liqu-u-s, lic-e-t (Osc. lik-i-<BR>tud = lice-to), lic-e-o-r; Goth. laib-a, bi-laib-jan,<BR>af-lif-nan, leihvan; Old Germ. bi-lib-an; Mod.<BR>Germ. bleibe; Angl. Sax. lyfan, be-lijan, lafan,<BR>lœn, lœnan; Lith. lek-u, lik-ti, lek-as, pa-<BR>laiki-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक
रिक (?), अम्, n. the heart, mind; law, litigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्त|रिक्तं
रिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, emptied, cleared, purged;<BR>empty, void; unloaded, unburdened; hollow, hol-<BR>lowed (as the hands); having nothing, poor, indi-<BR>gent; vain, worthless, valueless; epithet of one of<BR>the four wagtails (employed in augury); free from,<BR>devoid of, deprived of, destitute of, without; (आ), f.,<BR>scil. तिथि, epithet of the fourth, ninth, or fourteenth<BR>days of the lunar fortnight; (अम्), n. an empty<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">Page0846-a+ 76</a>]<BR>place, empty space, vacuum, void, vacuity; a desert,<BR>wilderness, wood, forest.<BR>—रिक्त-कुम्भ, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. (the sound of) an empty vessel, a hollow<BR>sound, empty or senseless language.<BR>—रिक्त-कृत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. making empty, emptying; causing a<BR>vacuum.<BR>—रिक्त-गुरु, see Pāṇ. VI. 2, 42.<BR>—रिक्त-<BR>ता, f. emptiness, vacuity, void, empty space or space<BR>in general.<BR>—रिक्त-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, empty-handed,<BR>bringing no present.<BR>—रिक्त-भाण्ड, अम्, n. an<BR>empty vessel; (अस्, आ, अम्), having no vessels or<BR>effects.<BR>—रिक्त-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, empty-minded,<BR>thinking of nothing<BR>—रिक्त-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>empty-handed, having empty hands, bringing no<BR>present; carrying away no present.<BR>—रिक्तार्क (˚त-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m. a Sunday falling on one of the Riktā<BR>days.<BR>—रिक्ती-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make<BR>empty or void, remove, take away; to steal; to<BR>get back, recover.<BR>—रिक्तीकृत-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>emptied or deprived of heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0845-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तक|रिक्तकं
रिक्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, empty, void; unladen, un-<BR>burdened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थ|रिक्थं
रिक्थ, अम्, n. (frequently written ऋक्थ), pro-<BR>perty left at death, inheritance, portion, bequest;<BR>property in general, possessions, substance, wealth;<BR>gold.<BR>—रिक्थ-ग्राह, अस्, आ, अम्, receiving an in-<BR>heritance, inheriting property; (अस्), m. an inheritor,<BR>heir.<BR>—रिक्थ-जात, अम्, n. the aggregate of a<BR>property, collected estate (of a deceased person).<BR>—रिक्थ-भागिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or रिक्थ-भाज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, inheriting or sharing property, dividing the pro-<BR>perty (of a deceased person), an inheritor, heir.<BR>—रिक्थ-विभाग, अस्, m. the division or sharing<BR>of (a deceased person's) property, partition of inherit-<BR>ance; a share in an inheritance.<BR>—रिक्थ-हर or<BR>रिक्थ-हार, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, receiving an inherit-<BR>ance, inheriting property; (अस्), m. an heir.<BR>—रिक्-<BR>थ-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, receiving or inheriting pro-<BR>perty; (ई), m. an heir, one who succeeds to property;<BR>a maternal uncle; the seed of the Indian fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थाद
रिक्थाद (˚थ-आद), अस्, आ, अम्, receiving an<BR>inheritance; (अस्), m. an heir, son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थिन्
रिक्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, inheriting property; possessing<BR>property, wealthy; (ई), m. an heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थीय
रिक्थीय in अ-रिक्थीय, अस्, आ, अम्, incapable of<BR>inheriting property, having no claim to inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिच्यमान
रिच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being emptied, being<BR>purged, being left clear, being freed from, being<BR>delivered from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरिक्वस्
रिरिक्वस्, वान्, m., Ved. one who has emaciated<BR>or attenuated (his body by austerities, Ṛg-veda IV.<BR>24, 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक|रेकः
रेक, रेच, रेचित, &c. See p. 852, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिज्
रिज् रिज् (connected with rt. ऋञ्ज्), cl. 1.<BR>A. रेजते, &c., to fry; to parch; [cf. rt.<BR>भृज्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिटि|रिटिः
रिटि रिटि, इस्, f. the crackling or roaring<BR>of flame; a musical instrument; black salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिणीनगर
रिणीनगर रिणी-नगर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिण्व्
रिण्व् रिण्व् or रिम्ब् (= rt. रण्व्), cl. 1.<BR>P. रिण्वति, रिम्बति, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रित्
रित् रित्, त्, त्, त् (fr. rt. 1. रि), Ved. (per-<BR>haps) moving, flowing, (Sāy. = गन्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रितक्वन्
रितक्वन् रितक्वन्, आ, m., Ved. a thief,<BR>(various reading for तक्वन्, Naigh. III. 24.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिद्ध
रिद्ध रिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (probably for ऋद्ध,<BR>q. v.), ripe (said of grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिधम|रिधमः
रिधम रिधम, अस्, m. (perhaps connected<BR>with रिद्ध above), spring; love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्
रिप् 1. रिप् (the old form of rt. लिप्, q. v.;<BR>in Ṛg-veda V. 85,8. the form रिरिपुः<BR>= लेपयन्ति = पापम् आरोपयन्ति), Ved. to smear,<BR>smear or cover over; to defile, spoil; to deceive,<BR>cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्
2. रिप्, प्, f., Ved. injury, fraud, deceit, trick,<BR>guile, (Sāy. = हिंसा, माया); the earth, (Sāy. =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">Page0846-b+ 79</a>]<BR>भूमि); (प्, प्, प्), injuring, an injurer, enemy,<BR>deceiver, cheat, (Sāy. = रिपु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपु|रिपुः
रिपु, उस्, उस्, उ (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 27. fr.<BR>rt. रप्; according to others, connected with rt. 1. रि<BR>or with Caus. of rt. 1. री; cf. rt. रिफ्), injuring,<BR>cheating, deceiving, fraudulent, treacherous, false<BR>(Ved.); (उस्), m. a deceiver, cheat, rogue, thief<BR>(Ved.); an enemy, adversary, foe; (in astrology) a<BR>hostile planet; epithet of the sixth astrological house;<BR>N. of a son of Śliṣṭi.<BR>—रिपु-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>slaying an enemy, killing foes; (इनी), f. a species of<BR>creeper; Abrus Precatorius.<BR>—रिपु-घ्न, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, killing an enemy.<BR>—रिपुञ्-जय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>conquering a foe, vanquishing enemies; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of several kings; of a son of Śliṣṭi; of a son<BR>of Suvīra; of a son of Viśva-jit.<BR>—रिपु-ता, f. en-<BR>mity, hostility.<BR>—रिपु-निपातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, causing<BR>an enemy to fall, destroying a foe.<BR>—रिपु-बल,<BR>अम्, n. an enemy's army.<BR>—रिपु-भय, अम्, n.<BR>fear or danger from an enemy.<BR>—रिपु-भवन,<BR>अम्, n. or रिपु-भाव, अस्, m. epithet of the sixth<BR>astrological house.<BR>—रिपु-मल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—रिपु-रक्त, अम्, n. an enemy's blood.<BR>—रिपु-रक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, preserving from an<BR>enemy.<BR>—रिपु-राक्षस, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>elephant.<BR>—रिपु-वर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>an enemy.<BR>—रिपु-वश, अस्, आ, अम्, subject to an<BR>enemy.<BR>—रिपुवश-त्व, अम्, n. subjection to an<BR>enemy.<BR>—रिपु-सूदन, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying ene-<BR>mies.<BR>—रिपु-स्थान, अम्, n. epithet of the sixth<BR>astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्त
रिप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (= लिप्त), Ved. anointed,<BR>smeared, (अपि-रिप्त in Ṛg-veda I. 118, 7 = पट-<BR>लेन पिहित-दृष्टि, i. e. blinded.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्र|रिप्रः
रिप्र, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. V. 55. fr.<BR>rt. 1. री), dirt, impurity (Ved.); sin, (Sāy. = पाप;<BR>cf. Nirukta IV. 21); (अस्, आ, अम्), vile, bad; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Śliṣṭi.<BR>—रिप्र-वाह, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. carrying off or removing impurity or sin,<BR>(Sāy. = पापस्य वोढृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप|रेपः
रेप, अस्, आ, अम्, low, vile, inferior, contemptible;<BR>cruel, savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेपस्
रेपस्, अस्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 189. fr.<BR>rt. रप्; cf. रपस्), a spot, stain; a wrong or<BR>blamable action, fault, sin; (आस्, आस्, अस्), low, vile,<BR>contemptible; miserly, niggardly; wicked, aban-<BR>doned, cruel, savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्सु
रिप्सु रिप्सु. See p. 833, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिफ्
रिफ् रिफ् [cf. rt. रिह्], cl. 6. P. रिफति,<BR>रिरेफ, &c., to utter a murmuring gut-<BR>tural sound, to utter a rough or grating or burring<BR>sound, to pronounce the letter र् [cf. रेफ below];<BR>to murmur or snarl at, revile, find fault with, blame,<BR>despise; (according to lexicographers also capable of<BR>the following senses), to speak, say, relate; to boast,<BR>(कत्थने being a various reading for कथने);<BR>to give; to fight; to hurl, kill, (in this sense = rts.<BR>ऋफ्, रिम्फ्): Pass. रिफ्यते, to be murmured or<BR>spoken in a grating or burring manner, to have or<BR>take the pronunciation of the letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिफत्
रिफत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, murmuring, uttering<BR>a burring sound, pronouncing the letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिफित
रिफित, अस्, आ, अम्, uttered in a burring or<BR>grating manner, pronounced with the sound of the<BR>letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफ|रेफः
रेफ, अस्, m. a burr, burring or grating sound, the<BR>letter र्; a cretic (see 3. र); passion, affection of<BR>the mind; (अस्, आ, अम्), low, vile, contemptible;<BR>[cf. रेप above.]<BR>—रेफ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>containing a burring sound, having the sound of र्.<BR>—रेफ-विपुला = र-विपुला, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफस्
रेफस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, low, vile, contemptible;<BR>wicked, abandoned; miserly, niggardly; cruel, savage;<BR>[cf. रेपस् above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफित्वा
रेफित्वा, ind. having uttered a burring or grating<BR>sound, having pronounced with the sound of the<BR>letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफिन्
रेफिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. containing a burring sound,<BR>containing the letter र्, having the nature of र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिभ्
रिभ् रिभ् or रेभ्, cl. 1. A. रेभते (Ved.<BR>also P. रेभति), रिरेभे, रेभितुम्, to<BR>crackle, creak; to murmur (as a stream &c.); to<BR>sound in general; to chatter, babble, clatter; to talk<BR>or speak aloud, shout with joy, rejoice [cf. rt. रिह्];<BR>to praise, glorify, worship (Ved. P.): Pass. रिभ्यते,<BR>to be praised or glorified; [cf. Gr. ῥοίβδην, ῥοῖβδος,<BR>ῥοιβδέω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिभ्वन्
रिभ्वन्, आ, m., Ved. (according to Naigh. III.<BR>24) a thief; [cf. रिह्वन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभ|रेभः
रेभ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. crackling; sounding<BR>loudly; (अस्), m. a praiser, reciter of praises, panegyrist,<BR>celebrator; a talker, prattler, chatterer; N. of a<BR>Ṛṣi (who was cast into a well by the Asuras, and<BR>rescued by the Aśvins after having lain there for ten<BR>nights and nine days, see Ṛg-veda I. 112, 5. 116,<BR>24, &c.); N. of the author of Ṛg-veda VIII. 97<BR>(having the patronymic Kāśyapa).<BR>—रेभ-सूनू,<BR>m. du. two sons of Rebha, the authors of the hymns<BR>Ṛg-veda IX. 99, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभण|रेभणं
रेभण, अम्, n. the lowing of kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभत्
रेभत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. crackling, sounding;<BR>praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभिल
रेभिल and रेभिलक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिमेद|रिमेदः
रिमेद रिमेद, अस्, m. = अरि-मेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्फ्|रिंफ्
रिम्फ् रिम्फ् (connected with rt. ऋफ्;<BR>cf. rt. रिफ्), cl. 6. P. रिम्फति, to<BR>hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्फ|रिंफ
रिम्फ, अम्, n. the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्ब्
रिम्ब् रिम्ब् = rt. रिण्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरंसा
रिरंसा रिरंसा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. रम्),<BR>the desire to rejoice or be pleased, wish to sport;<BR>desire of pleasure or sexual enjoyment, lasciviousness,<BR>lustfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरंसु
रिरंसु, उस्, उस्, उ, desiring to rejoice, wishing to<BR>sport, wishing for sexual pleasures, lustful, wanton,<BR>lascivious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरमयिषु
रिरमयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of Caus.),<BR>wishing to cause or give pleasure (especially sexual<BR>pleasure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरक्षिषा
रिरक्षिषा रिरक्षिषा, f. (fr. the Desid. of<BR>rt. 1. रक्ष्), the desire to watch or keep guard,<BR>wish to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरक्षा
रिरक्षा, f. less correct for the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरक्षिषु
रिरक्षिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, desiring to watch or keep<BR>guard, wishing to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरक्षु
रिरक्षु, less correct for रिरक्षिषु above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरिक्षु
रिरिक्षु रिरिक्षु. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरी
रिरी रिरी, f. yellow brass, pale brass,<BR>prince's metal; [cf. रीरी, रीति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिल्हण
रिल्हण रिल्हण or रिह्लण, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिवक
रिवक रिवक, अस्, m. = रवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश्
रिश् रिश् (according to some an older<BR>form of rt. 1. लिश्, q. v.; closely connected<BR>with rt. 1. रिष्, from which, in some forms and<BR>meanings, it is not distinguishable; cf. also rts. रुश्,<BR>1. रुष्), cl. 6. P. रिशति, रिरेश, रेक्ष्यति, अरि-<BR>क्षत्, रेष्टुम्, Ved. to tear, rend, tear off, break<BR>off, pluck off, injure, hurt; to feed on, graze: Caus.<BR>रेशयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरीरिशत्: Desid. रिरिक्षति,<BR>to wish to injure: Intens. रेरिश्यते, रेरेष्टि; [cf.<BR>Slav. resati, ‘to cut.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरिक्षत्
रिरिक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. wishing to injure,<BR>&c.; (अन्), m. an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरिक्षु
रिरिक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to injure or harm,<BR>(this form is sometimes referred to rt. 1. रिष्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश|रिशः
रिश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. tearing, tearing off, injur-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. an injurer, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिशत्
रिशत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, Ved. tearing, injuring,<BR>hurting; feeding or grazing upon, consuming, (Sāy.<BR>= भक्षणार्थं हिंसत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिशादस्
रिशादस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (a word of doubtful derivation<BR>and meaning; said to be fr. रिश, an enemy, + अद<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">Page0847-a+ 77</a>]<BR>fr. rt. अद्), Ved. destroying those who injure, de-<BR>stroying enemies, epithet of the Maruts, &c.; [cf.<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 39, 4.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0846-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्ट|रिष्टं|रिष्टः
1. रिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. रिष्ट see below),<BR>Ved. torn, torn off, broken, injured; wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश्य|रिश्यः
रिश्य रिश्य, अस्, m. = ऋश्य, an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्
रिष् 1. रिष् (closely connected with rt.<BR>रिश्, from which, in some forms and mean-<BR>ings, it is not distinguishable; cf. also rts. रुश्,<BR>1. रुष्), cl. 1. 4. P. रेषति, रिष्यति (in ep. and<BR>later authors also A. रिष्यते), रिरेष, रेषिष्यति,<BR>अरेषीत् or अरिषत् (Vedic forms रिषत्, रिषाम,<BR>रिषाथन, रेषत्, रीषत), रेषितुम् or रेष्टुम्<BR>(Ved. inf. रिषे), to injure, hurt, harm; to kill,<BR>destroy, ruin; to give offence; to be injured or<BR>destroyed, suffer wrong, perish (cl.4); to fail, mis-<BR>carry, meet with misfortune or disaster (cl. 4): Caus.<BR>रेषयति, -यते, -यितुम्, Aor. अरीरिषत्, अरीरि-<BR>षत, to cause to be injured, injure, hurt, harm; to<BR>cause to miscarry, make to fail; to fail, miscarry,<BR>meet with misfortune or disaster (A.): Desid. रिरि-<BR>षिषति, रिरेषिषति, (according to some also रि-<BR>रिक्षति): Intens. रेरिष्यते, रेरेष्टि; [cf. pro-<BR>bably Gr. ῥαίω, ῥαιστός; Lat. lœdo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्
2. रिष्, ट्, f. injury; (ट्, ट्, ट्), injuring, an injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष
रिष, अस्, आ, अम्, injuring, destroying, &c.; [cf.<BR>नघा-रिष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिषण्य
रिषण्य, Nom. P. रिषण्यति, &c. (Pāṇ. VII.<BR>4, 36), Ved. to injure, harm, be hurtful; to reject<BR>(a petition); to fail, miscarry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिषण्यु
रिषण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. injurious, hurtful, ma-<BR>levolent, (Sāy. = हिंसक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिषीक
रिषीक, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) destroying, destruc-<BR>tive, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्ट|रिष्टं|रिष्टः
2. रिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see above), injured,<BR>hurt, wounded; unlucky; (according to some also)<BR>lucky; (अम्), n. mischief, harm; misfortune, bad luck<BR>(= अरिष्ट); destruction, loss; sin; (according to<BR>some also) good luck, prosperity; (अस्), m. a sword;<BR>the soap plant, Sapindus Detergens; N. of a king;<BR>of a Daitya or demon (destroyed by Viṣṇu); of a<BR>son of a Manu; (आ), f., N. of the mother of the<BR>Apsarases.<BR>—रिष्ट-ताति, इस्, इस्, इ, causing prosperity,<BR>propitious; auspicious; [cf. शिव-ताति.]<BR>—रिष्ट-<BR>देह, अस्, आ, अम्, wounded in body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टक|रिष्टकः
रिष्टक, अस्, m. Sapindus Detergens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टि|रिष्टिः
रिष्टि, इस्, f. injury, hurt, damage; failure, mis-<BR>carriage, misfortune, bad luck; (according to some)<BR>good luck; इषु-रिष्टि, ‘the going astray or swerv-<BR>ing of an arrow,’ N. of a Sāman; (इस्), m. = ऋष्टि,<BR>a sword, (according to some also इस्, f.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टीय
रिष्टीय, Nom. P. रिष्टीयति, &c. = रिषण्य<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्व|रिष्वः
रिष्व, अस्, आ, अम्, injurious, hurtful, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिषि|रिषिः
रिषि रिषि, इस्, m. = ऋषि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्फ
रिष्फ रिष्फ, अम्, n. = रिःफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्य|रिष्यः
रिष्य रिष्य, अस्, m. = ऋष्य, ऋश्य.<BR>—रिष्य-मूक, अस्, m. = ऋष्य-मूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिह्
रिह् रिह् (a Vedic form of rt. लिह्), the<BR>following forms of this rt. are found, रेऌहि,<BR>रिहति (3rd pl. रिहन्ति, A. रिहते), to lick, taste;<BR>to caress, kiss; (also regarded as another form of rt.<BR>रिफ्, and therefore said to be capable of the follow-<BR>ing meanings) to praise, worship; to say, speak; to<BR>boast; to give [cf. rt. 1. रा]; to blame; to fight;<BR>to hurt, injure; to kill, (in this sense said to be also<BR>रेहति): Intens. रेरिह्यते, to lick again and again;<BR>to caress, kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिहत्
रिहत्, अन्, अती, अत्, licking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिहाण
रिहाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. licking, caressing, wish-<BR>ing to caress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिहायस्
रिहायस्, आस्, m., Ved. a thief, robber (Naigh.<BR>III. 24).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिह्वन्
रिह्वन्, आ, m. a thief; [cf. रिभ्वन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेरिहाण|रेरिहाणः
रेरिहाण. See s.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिहम्
रिहम् रिहम्, ind., Ved. various reading<BR>for ऋहत्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

री
री 1. री (connected with rt. 1. रि), cl.<BR>9. P. A. रिणाति, रिणीते, रिराय (3rd du.<BR>रिर्यतुस्), रिर्ये, रेष्यति, रेष्यते, अरैषीत्,<BR>अरेष्ट, रेतुम्, to go, move; to hurt, injure, kill,<BR>(see rt. 1. रि); to howl [cf. rt. 1. रु]; cl. 4. A.<BR>रीयते, &c., to melt, become fluid, distil, drip,<BR>trickle, ooze, drop, flow [cf. rt. 1. ली]: Caus. रेप-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरीरिपत्: Desid. रिरीषति,<BR>-ते: Intens. रेरीयते, रेरयीति; [cf. Goth. and<BR>Angl. Sax. rinnan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीण|रीणं
रीण, अस्, आ, अम्, dropping, trickling, oozing,<BR>distilling, flowing, leaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीति|रीतिः
रीति, इस्, f. going, motion, moving, flowing, trick-<BR>ling; a stream, river; a course; a line, streak; a<BR>limit, boundary (= सीमन्); general course or way,<BR>method, mode, manner, fashion; usage, observance,<BR>custom, practice, natural property or disposition;<BR>style, diction, (three styles of diction or composition<BR>are enumerated, viz. वैदर्भी, गौडी, पाञ्चालि, to<BR>which a fourth is sometimes added, viz. लाटिका, and<BR>even a fifth and sixth, viz. आवन्तिका and मागधी);<BR>bell-metal, brass, pale brass; calx of brass; rust of<BR>iron; scoria of any metal or the oxide formed on<BR>the surface of metals by their exposure to heat and<BR>air.<BR>—रीति-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, acquainted with estab-<BR>lished usages or customs.<BR>—रीति-पुष्प, अम्, n.<BR>‘brass-efflorescence,’ calx of brass.<BR>—रीति-प्रष्ठ,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a Praṣṭha weight of brass.<BR>—रीति-<BR>बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, brass-bound, studded or inlaid<BR>with brass.<BR>—रीती-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a row,<BR>standing in a line.<BR>—रीत्य्-अप्, प्, प्, प्, Ved. stream-<BR>ing with rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीतिक|रीतिकं
रीतिक, अम्, n. calx of brass; (आ), f. bell-metal,<BR>brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

री
री 2. री = रै in ऋधद्-री, (for री, fem.<BR>of 2. र, see under 2. र, p. 824.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीज्या
रीज्या रीज्या, f. reproach, censure [cf.<BR>रीढा]; shame, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीठा
रीठा रीठा, f. or रीठा-करञ्ज, अस्, m. a<BR>species of Karañja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढक|रीढकः
रीढक रीढक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>रिह्), the back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढा
रीढा रीढा, f. (probably fr. rt. रिह्), dis-<BR>respect. disregard, contempt, irreverence; [cf. अव-<BR>लीढा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीर
रीर रीर, अस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीरी
रीरी रीरी, f. = रिरी, yellow brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीव्
रीव् रीव्, cl. 1. P. A. रीवति, -ते, &c., to<BR>take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
रु 1. रु, cl. 2. P. रौति, रवीति (Ved. also<BR>रुवति, and in some forms also A.), Impf.<BR>अरौत् or अरवीत् (1st du. अरुव or अरुवीव, 3rd<BR>pl. अरुवन्), रुराव (1st du. रुरुविव, 3rd pl. A.<BR>रुरुविरे), रविता or (according to Vopa-deva IX.<BR>53) रोता, रविष्यति, अरावीत् (A. अराविष्ट, 3rd<BR>pl. अराविषुस्, Ved. अरवन्त), रवितुम्, and (ac-<BR>cording to Vopa-deva) रोतुम्, to cry or make any<BR>particular sound or noise, bellow, roar, howl, yelp,<BR>yell, bray, shout, shriek; to hum (as bees); to sound<BR>in general; to cry aloud, to fill with noise or cries;<BR>to praise (according to Naigh. III. 14): Pass. रू-<BR>यते: Caus. रावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरीरवत्<BR>(anomalous form 3rd pl. अरूरुवन्), to cause to<BR>bellow or roar, &c., to cause an uproar; to fill with<BR>shrieks, clamour, &c.: Desid. of Caus. रिरावयि-<BR>षति: Desid. रुरूषति: Intens. रोरूयते, -ति,<BR>रोरवीति, रोरोति, to cry out loudly, bellow or roar<BR>loudly, yelp loudly, scream aloud, to vociferate; [cf.<BR>Gr. ὠρύ-ω, ὠρυ-θ-μό-ς, ὀρυ-μαγδό-ς; Lat. rû-mor,<BR>rûm-i-to, râvi-s, rau-cu-s; Angl. Sax. ryn; Slav.<BR>rev-a, rju-ti, ‘to roar.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
2. रु, उस्, m. sound, noise; fear, alarm; war,<BR>battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुत|रुतं
1. रुत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see col. 3), sounded,<BR>filled with the cry (of animals), made to resound,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">Page0847-c+ 75</a>]<BR>rendered vocal; (अम्), n. any cry or noise, yell,<BR>roar, humming (of bees), the note of birds; song.<BR>—रुत-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, understanding the cries (of<BR>animals); (अस्), m. an augur.<BR>—रुत-व्याज, अस्, m.<BR>simulated cry or sound; mimicry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुतायत
रुतायत (?), अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. रुत), rendered<BR>vocal (by the sound of birds, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवण्य
रुवण्य (fr. an unused form रुवण), Nom. P. रु-<BR>वण्यति, &c., Ved. to cry, utter harsh or loud cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवण्यु
रुवण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. sounding, clamouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवत्
रुवत्, अन्, अती, अत्, crying out, bellowing, howling,<BR>crying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवथ|रुवथः
रुवथ, अस्, m. the bellowing of a bull (Ved.);<BR>a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरवण
रोरवण, अम्, n. (fr. the Intens.), Ved. a loud<BR>cry or roaring, violent bellowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुवत्
रोरुवत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. sounding or shouting<BR>loudly, (referred by some to rt. 3. रु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुवाण
रोरुवाण, अस्, आ, अम्, crying loudly, making a<BR>loud cry or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरूय
रोरूय, अस्, m. crying much, &c. (Vopa-deva<BR>XXVI. 29).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरूयमाण
रोरूयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, crying loudly, making<BR>a loud cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
रु 3. रु, cl. 1. A. रवते, रुरुवे, &c.,<BR>Ved. to break to pieces, dash to pieces; to<BR>kill, hurt (?); to be angry (?); to go; to speak:<BR>Caus. रावयति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
4. रु, उस्, m. cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुत|रुतं
2. रुत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see col. 2), broken to<BR>pieces, divided, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुंश्
रुंश् रुंश्, cl. 1. 10. P. रुंशति, रुंश-<BR>यति, &c., to speak; to shine (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक|रुकः
रुक रुक, अस्, आ, अम्, liberal, bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्काम
रुक्काम रुक्-काम. See under 2. रुच्, p. 848.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्प्रतिक्रिया
रुक्प्रतिक्रिया रुक्-प्रतिक्रिया. See under<BR>2. रुज्, p. 848, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्म|रुक्मं|रुक्मः
रुक्म रुक्म, रुक्मिन्, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मत्|रुक्मन्त्
रुक्मत् रुक्-मत्, रुङ्-मत्. See under 2. रुच्,<BR>p. 848, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्ष|रुक्षः
रुक्ष 1. रुक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see p. 848,<BR>col. 1), rough, harsh, &c. = रूक्ष, q. v.; [cf. Angl.<BR>Sax. rug, ruh, ruw; Eng. rough, rugged.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्सद्मन्
रुक्सद्मन् रुक्-सद्मन्, रुग्-अन्वित, &c.<BR>See under 2. रुज्, p. 848, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुग्ण
रुग्ण रुग्ण, रुग्न. See p. 848, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्
रुच् 1. रुच् (connected with rt. लोच्, q. v.),<BR>cl. 1. A. (sometimes P. on account of the<BR>metre), रोचते (-ति), रुरुचे, रोचिष्यते, अरुचत्,<BR>अरोचिष्ट, रोचितुम् (Ved. Inf. रुचे), to shine, be<BR>bright or resplendent (said of the sun, fire, stars,<BR>&c.); to make bright or resplendent (Ved. P.); to<BR>shine beautifully, appear beautiful, appear good; to<BR>please, be agreeable; to please any one (dat. or gen.);<BR>to be pleased, find pleasure in, approve, desire (some-<BR>times with acc. or dat.); Pass. रुच्यते, Aor. अरोचि, to<BR>be bright or radiant: Caus. रोचयति, -यते, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अरूरुचत्, to cause to shine; to enlighten, illu-<BR>minate, irradiate, make bright; to make pleasant<BR>or agreeable; to please (A.), be pleasant to any one<BR>(dat.); to cause to like; to cause any one (acc.) to<BR>long for anything (dat.); to cause to appear beautiful<BR>or good, to find pleasure in, like, approve, choose (A.);<BR>to resolve: Pass. of Caus. रोच्यते, to be agreeable:<BR>Desid. रुरुचिषते, रुरोचिषते; [cf. Gr. ἀμφι-λύκ-η,<BR>λύχ-νο-ς, λευκό-ς, λοῦσσο-ν:]; Lat. luc-eo,<BR>lux, lu-men, lucidu-s, lu-na, Leucesius, di-luc-<BR>ulu-m: Goth. liuh-ath, ‘light;’ lauhmoni, ‘light-<BR>ning;’ liuhtjan: Old Germ. lichan, luchjan,<BR>lochon: Angl. Sax. leoht, lioht, gelihtan, locian:<BR>Slav. luca, ‘a ray;’ luna, ‘the moon:’ Lith.<BR>lauka-s, lauki-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्म|रुक्मं|रुक्मः
रुक्म, अस्, आ, अम्, bright, radiant, clear; (अस्),<BR>m. an ornament of gold, golden chain, (perhaps<BR>also) an ornament of precious stones (Ved.); the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-a" target="_blank">Page0848-a+ 81</a>]<BR>plant Mesua Roxburghii; the thorn-apple; N. of a<BR>son of Rucaka; (अम्), n. gold; iron.<BR>—रुक्म-<BR>कवच, अस्, m., N. of a grandson of Uśanas.<BR>—रुक्म-कारक, अस्, m. a worker in gold, gold-<BR>smith.<BR>—रुक्म-केश, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Bhīṣmaka.<BR>—रुक्म-पाश, अस्, m., Ved. a string<BR>on which golden ornaments are worn.<BR>—रुक्म-पुर,<BR>अम्, n. ‘city of gold,’ N. of the city inhabited by<BR>Garuḍa.<BR>—रुक्म-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>gold surface, coated or overlaid with gold, gold-<BR>plated, gilded.<BR>—रुक्म-प्रस्तरण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having an outer garment decorated with gold.<BR>—रुक्म-बाहु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Bhīṣmaka.<BR>—रुक्म-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of gold, golden.<BR>—रुक्म-मालिन्, ई, m., N. of a son of Bhīṣmaka.<BR>—रुक्म-रथ, अस्, m. a golden car or chariot; the<BR>chariot of Rukma-ratha, i. e. of Droṇa; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having a golden chariot; (अस्), m., N. of Droṇa; of<BR>a son of Śalya; of a son of Mahat; of a son of<BR>Bhīṣmaka.<BR>—रुक्म-वक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>golden-breasted, having golden ornaments on the<BR>breast (said of the Maruts).<BR>—रुक्म-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, possessing gold, golden, ornamented with gold;<BR>(आन्), m. a proper N., = रुक्मिन्; (अती), f. a parti-<BR>cular metre, four times ¯˘˘¯¯¯˘˘¯¯; N. of<BR>a granddaughter of Rukmin and wife of Aniruddha.<BR>—रुक्म-वाहन, अस्, आ, अम्, golden-carred, hav-<BR>ing a golden chariot; (अस्), m., N. of Droṇa.<BR>—रुक्म-स्तेय, अम्, n. stealing gold.<BR>—रुक्माङ्-<BR>गद (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a golden<BR>bracelet on the upper arm; (अस्), m., N. of various<BR>kings.<BR>—रुक्माभ (˚म-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, shining<BR>like gold, bright as the purest gold.<BR>—रुक्मेषु<BR>(˚म-इषु), उस्, m. ‘golden-arrowed,’ N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0847-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मि
रुक्मि, इस्, m. a proper N. (= रुक्मिन्; in one<BR>or two passages रुक्मिम् is used for रुक्मिणम् on<BR>account of the metre).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिन्
रुक्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wearing golden ornaments,<BR>decorated with golden ornaments (Ved.), gilded,<BR>gilt; (ई), m., N. of the eldest son of Bhīṣmaka<BR>and adversary of Kṛṣṇa (who carried off his sister<BR>Rukmiṇī; he was slain by Bala-deva); N. of a<BR>mountain; (इणी), f., N. of a daughter of Bhīṣmaka<BR>carried off and espoused by Kṛṣṇa, (she is repre-<BR>sented as the mother of Pra-dyumna, and in the<BR>later mythology = ) the goddess Lakṣmī; N. of<BR>Dākṣāyaṇī in Dvāravatī; of a daughter of Śreṣ-<BR>thin Sulocana.<BR>—रुक्मि-दर्प, अस्, m., N. of Bala-<BR>deva (so called as proud of having overcome Rukmin).<BR>—रुक्मि-दारिन्, ई, or रुक्मि-दारण, अस्, or<BR>रुक्मि-भिद्, त्, m. ‘destroyer of Rukmin,’ N. of<BR>Bala-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्ष|रुक्षः
2. रुक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 847, col. 3),<BR>Ved. shining, brilliant, radiant, glittering, (Sāy. =<BR>दीप्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्
2. रुच्, क्, f. light, lustre, brightness; lightning;<BR>splendor, beauty, loveliness; colour; appearance,<BR>(sometimes at the end of a comp., e. g. जनाः, सुर-<BR>रुचः, god-like men); pleasure, delight, liking,<BR>wish, desire; [cf. Lat. lux.]<BR>—रुक्-काम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. desiring splendor, eager for lustre.<BR>—रुक्-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of brightness, shin-<BR>ing; (आन्), m., N. of Agni.<BR>—रुङ्-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. containing the word रुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच
रुच, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bright, radiant, brilliant;<BR>(आ), f. light, lustre, beauty; pleasure, delight, desire,<BR>liking; the note of the parrot or Maina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचक|रुचकं|रुचकः
रुचक, अस्, आ, अम्, agreeable, pleasing; sharp,<BR>acrid; tonic, stomachic; (अस्), m. epithet of a kind<BR>of four-sided column; epithet of one of the five<BR>great personages born under particular constellations;<BR>the citron, Citrus Medica; a pigeon; N. of a moun-<BR>tain; of a son of Uśanas; (अम्), n. one of the five<BR>kinds of bone in the human body (that of the teeth),<BR>a tooth, (said to be also अस्, m.); a kind of golden<BR>ornament, an ornament for the neck, a ring, an<BR>ornament for a horse, (according to some अस्, m.); a<BR>curl on a horse's neck; any object or substance sup-<BR>posed to bring good luck, (also अस्, m.); epithet of<BR>a sort of building or temple having terraces on three<BR>sides and closed only on the north side; a stomachic,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">Page0848-b+ 81</a>]<BR>tonic; (according to native authorities also) Ricinus<BR>Communis; a garland, wreath, crown; sochal salt;<BR>natron, alkali; the perfume Rocanā; an anthel-<BR>minthic medicine commonly called Viḍaṅga; = प्रोत्-<BR>कट; = उत्कट; = स्वाद्यरस (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचि|रुचिः
रुचि, इस्, f. light, lustre, brightness, splendor, beauty;<BR>a ray of light; colour; appearance; liking, taste, re-<BR>lish, zest, appetite, hunger; wish, desire, pleasure,<BR>(रुच्या, with pleasure, willingly); passion; inclina-<BR>tion, taste for, liking for, (at the end of comps. in<BR>the sense ‘having a taste or liking for,’ cf. मांस-<BR>र्˚, हिंसा-र्˚); intent application to any object; (in<BR>erotic works) epithet of a particular kind of lover's<BR>embrace; a kind of yellow pigment (= गो-रोचना);<BR>N. of an Apsaras; of the wife of Deva-śarman; (इस्),<BR>m., N. of a Prajā-pati, the husband of Ākūti and<BR>father of Yajña or Su-yajña and of Manu Raucya;<BR>of a son of Viśvā-mitra; of a king; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>pleasing, pleasant, agreeable (= रुचिर).<BR>—रुचि-<BR>कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing pleasure, entertaining,<BR>diverting, amusing, exciting desire; causing an appe-<BR>tite or relish, tasteful, savoury, sapid, appetizing,<BR>stomachic; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Keśava.<BR>—रुचि-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing a relish, relishing.<BR>—रुचि-ता, f.<BR>or रुचि-त्व, अम्, n. the having a taste or liking for,<BR>taking pleasure in (at the end of comps., cf. स-<BR>मान-रुचि-ता, हिंसा-रुचि-त्व); desire, interest,<BR>(आरम्भ-रुचि-ता, engaging in enterprises from<BR>mere liking or from interested motives, having a<BR>taste for new enterprises.)<BR>—रुचि-दत्त, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a commentator on the Tattva-cintā-maṇi-<BR>prakāśa.<BR>—रुचि-देव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रुचि-<BR>धामन्, आ, आ, अ, having light for an abode; (अ),<BR>n. the abode of light (epithet of the sun).<BR>—रुचि-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—रुचि-पति, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a commentator on the Anarghya-rāghava.<BR>—रुचि-पर्वन्, आ, m. a proper N.<BR>—रुचि-प्रद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, giving an appetite, appetizing.<BR>—रुचि-<BR>प्रभ, अस्, m., N. of a Daitya.<BR>—रुचि-फल, अम्,<BR>n. a kind of fruit (= अमृताह्व).<BR>—रुचि-भर्तृ,<BR>ता, m. ‘lord or bearer of light,’ the sun; ‘lord or<BR>cherisher of pleasure,’ a husband.<BR>—रुचि-रुचि in<BR>रुचि-रुचे रोचनम्, N. of a Sāman.<BR>—रुचि-वह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bringing light.<BR>—रुचि-सम्प्रकॢप्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, prepared with good taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचित|रुचितं
रुचित, अस्, आ, अम्, brightened, bright, shining;<BR>pleased; sweet, delicate, dainty; sharpened (said of<BR>the appetite); digested.<BR>—रुचित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. containing the meaning of रुचित or of rt.<BR>1. रुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचित्वा
रुचित्वा or रोचित्वा, having shone, &c. (Pāṇ. I.<BR>2,26).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिर|रुचिरं
रुचिर, अस्, आ, अम्, bright, brilliant, radiant, light,<BR>shining, glittering, beautiful; pleasing, agreeable, charm-<BR>ing, pleasant; sweet, dainty, nice; stomachic, cordial,<BR>restorative; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Sena-jit; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of yellow pigment (= गो-रोचना); N. of<BR>a metre, four times thirty instants; of another, four<BR>times ˘¯˘¯, ˘˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯; N. of a river;<BR>(अम्), n. saffron; a radish; cloves.<BR>—रुचिर-केतु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—रुचिर-दन्तौष्-<BR>ठ (˚त-ओष्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having beautiful teeth<BR>and lips.<BR>—रुचिर-देव, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रुचिर-धी, ईस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रुचिर-<BR>प्रभास-सम्भव, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-<BR>demon.<BR>—रुचिर-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>pleasing or beautiful countenance.<BR>—रुचिर-वाच्, क्,<BR>क्, क्, having pleasant speech, eloquent.<BR>—रुचिर-<BR>श्री-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—रुचिराञ्-<BR>जन (˚र-अञ्˚), अस्, m. = शोभाञ्जन, Hyperanthera<BR>Moringa.<BR>—रुचिरानन (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>handsome-faced, beautiful.<BR>—रुचिरापाङ्गी (˚र-<BR>अप्˚), f. ‘having beautiful corners of the eyes,’ a<BR>woman with beautiful eyes.<BR>—रुचिराश्व (˚र-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Sena-jit.<BR>—रुचिरा-सुत, अस्,<BR>m. a metronymic of Pālakāpya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिष्य|रुचिष्यं
रुचिष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing, pleasant, agree-<BR>able, liked; giving an appetite, tonic, stomachic;<BR>dainty, nice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुची
रुची, f. = रुचि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्य|रुच्यं|रुच्यः
रुच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, bright, radiant, beautiful,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">Page0848-c+ 77</a>]<BR>handsome, pleasing, agreeable, delightful; palatable,<BR>delicious, giving an appetite, stomachic, tonic; (अस्),<BR>m. a lover, husband; N. of various plants, Strychnos<BR>Potatorum; rice; Ægle Marmelos; (अम्), n. a<BR>digestive, tonic; = सौवर्चल.<BR>—रुच्य-कन्द, अस्,<BR>m. Arum Campanulatum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज्
रुज् 1. रुज्, cl. 6. P. रुजति (rarely A. -ते),<BR>रुरोज, रोक्ष्यति, अरौक्षीत् (in Vāja-<BR>saneyi-s. XVI. 47. मा रोक् = भङ्गम् मा कार्षीः),<BR>रोक्तुम्, to break, break open, break to pieces, break<BR>down, destroy; to bend; to pain, cause pain, afflict<BR>with disease, disorder, injure: Pass. रुज्यते, to be<BR>broken, &c.: Caus. रोजयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरूरु-<BR>जत्, to cause to break, to injure, hurt, kill: Desid.<BR>रुरुक्षति: Intens. रोरुज्यते, रोरोक्ति; [cf. Gr.<BR>λυγ-ρό-ς, λευγαλέο-ς, λοιγό-ς, λοίγιο-ς, perhaps<BR>ὀ-ρύσσω, ὄ-ρυγμα, ὀ-ρυκτή, ὀ-ρυχή; Lat. lug-e-o,<BR>lug-u-bri-s, luc-tu-s, lu-e-s; Lith. luz-ti, ‘to<BR>break.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुग्ण
रुग्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (sometimes incorrectly written<BR>रुग्न), broken, broken to pieces; thwarted, checked;<BR>bent, crooked, curved; injured; diseased, sick, in-<BR>firm.<BR>—रुग्ण-ता, f. or रुग्ण-त्व, अम्, n. broken-<BR>ness, crookedness; infirmity, sickness, disease.<BR>—रुग्-<BR>ण-रय, अस्, आ, अम्, checked in an onset, foiled<BR>in an attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज्
2. रुज्, क्, क्, क्, breaking, breaking or dashing to<BR>pieces; (क्), f. fracture; pain, sickness, illness, disease,<BR>(अक्षि-रुज्, a disease of the eye); toil, fatigue,<BR>weariness, effort, trouble.<BR>—रुक्-प्रतिक्रिया, f.<BR>counteraction of disease, treatment of sickness, prac-<BR>tice of medicine, curing, remedying.<BR>—रुक्-सद्मन्,<BR>अ, n. ‘seat of pain,’ excrement, feces.<BR>—रुग्-अन्-<BR>वित, अस्, आ, अम्, attended with pain, painful.<BR>—रुग्-<BR>दाह, अस्, m. a kind of fever.<BR>—रुग्-भय, अम्,<BR>n. fear of disease.<BR>—रुग्-भेषज, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>‘disease-medicine,’ any medicine or drug.<BR>—रुग्-<BR>विनिश्चय, अस्, m. ‘determination of disease,’ N. of<BR>a work by Mādhava (treating of the causes and<BR>diagnosis of eighty kinds of disease).<BR>—रुजस्-कर,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम् (रुजस्, acc. pl. + कर), causing or<BR>producing pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज
रुज, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking, breaking to pieces,<BR>destroying (at the end of comps., cf. वलं-र्˚); (अस्),<BR>m. a word of doubtful meaning in Atharva-veda XVI.<BR>3, 2; (आ), f. breaking, fracture, rupture, destruction,<BR>overthrow; pain, sickness, disease, illness, disorder;<BR>Costus Speciosus or Arabicus (= कुष्ठ); an ewe.<BR>—रुजा-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing pain, making<BR>sick or ill, sickening; (अस्), m. sickness, disease;<BR>sickness induced by passion or love (said to be one<BR>of the Bhāvas or sentiments); (अम्), n. the acid<BR>fruit of Averrhoa Carambola.<BR>—रुजापह (˚जा-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, keeping off pain, removing sickness or dis-<BR>ease.<BR>—रुजा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having pain or disease,<BR>painful, diseased.<BR>—रुजा-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. painful.<BR>—रुजा-सह, अस्, m. a species of fruit tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजाय
रुजाय, Nom. A. रुजायते, &c., to be sick or ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुक्षणि
रुरुक्षणि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. the Desid.), Ved. wish-<BR>ing or able to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुट्
रुट् रुट्, cl. 1. A. रोटते, &c., to strike<BR>against, resist, oppose; to suffer pain; to<BR>shine; cl. 10. P. रोटयति, &c., to be angry [cf.<BR>rt. 1. रुष्]; to shine; to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुठ्
रुठ् रुठ्, cl. 1. P. रोठति, &c., to strike,<BR>strike down, fell; cl. 1.A. रोठते, &c., to<BR>strike against, resist, oppose; to torment, pain; to<BR>suffer pain; [cf. rt. रुट्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोठमान
रोठमान, अस्, आ, अम्, paining; suffering pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुणस्करा
रुणस्करा रुणस्करा, f. a cow easily milked,<BR>a gentle cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुणा
रुणा रुणा, f., N. of a river flowing into<BR>the Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ट्|रुंट्
रुण्ट् रुण्ट्, cl. 1. P. रुण्टति, &c., to steal,<BR>rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ठ्|रुंठ्
रुण्ठ् रुण्ठ् (= rt. लुण्ठ्), cl. 1. P. रुण्-<BR>ठति, &c., to go; to be lame; to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">Page0849-a+ 79</a>]<BR>idle; to strike against, resist; to steal, (in this sense<BR>a various reading for rt. रुण्ट्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0848-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ड्
रुण्ड् रुण्ड्, cl. 1. P. रुण्डति, &c. = rt.<BR>रुण्ट्, p. 848, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ड|रुंड|रुण्डः
रुण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, maimed, mutilated; (अस्), m.<BR>according to some also (अम्), n. a headless body,<BR>mere trunk (retaining life and continuing to mix in<BR>battle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्डिका|रुंडिका
रुण्डिका, f. a field of battle; a female messenger<BR>or go-between; the threshold of a door; superhuman<BR>power (= वि-भूति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुत|रुतं
रुत रुत, &c. See under rt. 1. रु, p. 847,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुथ
रुथ रुथ, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्
रुद् 1. रुद् [cf. rt. 1. रु], cl. 2. P. रोदिति<BR>(Ved. also cl. 6. रुदति, ep. also A. रुदते),<BR>Impf. अरोदीत् or अरोदत् (Pāṇ. VII. 3, 98, 99; 1st<BR>sing. अरोदम्, 3rd pl. अरुदन्), Impv. रोदितु (2nd<BR>sing. रुदिहि), Perf. रुरोद (ep. रुरुदे), 2nd Fut.<BR>रोदिष्यति (Ved. रोत्स्यति), Aor. अरोदीत् (3rd pl.<BR>अरोदिषुस्) or अरुदत्, रोदितुम्, to weep, cry, shed<BR>tears, wail, lament; to bewail, deplore; to roar, howl:<BR>Pass. रुद्यते, Aor. अरोदि: Caus. रोदयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अरूरुदत्, to cause to weep or lament:<BR>Desid. रुरुदिषति: Intens. रोरुद्यते, रोरोत्ति, to<BR>weep very much; [cf. perhaps Gr. ὀῤῥωδέω; Lat.<BR>rud-o; Old Germ. riuzan; Angl. Sax. reotan;<BR>Lith. raudoju; Slav. rudajun.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्
2. रुद्, त्, त्, त्, weeping, crying, lamenting [cf.<BR>अघ-र्˚]; (त्), f. cry, wail, lamentation; sound,<BR>noise; grief; pain, affliction; disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदत्
रुदत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, weeping, crying,<BR>wailing, bewailing; (अन्ती), f. a species of small shrub<BR>(= रुदन्तिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदथ|रुदथः
रुदथ, अस्, m. a child, a pupil, scholar; a dog;<BR>a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदन|रुदनं
रुदन, अम्, n. the act of crying, weeping,<BR>lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदन्तिका
रुदन्तिका, f. ‘the weeper,’ epithet of a species<BR>of small succulent shrub (= अमृत-स्रवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदमान
रुदमान, अस्, आ, अम्, weeping, wailing, lament-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदित|रुदितं
रुदित, अस्, आ, अम्, wept, lamented, deplored;<BR>weeping, crying, lamenting; wet with tears; (अम्),<BR>n. a weeping, wailing, crying, lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदित्वा
रुदित्वा, ind. having wept, having lamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्यमान
रुद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being bewailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्र|रुद्रः
रुद्र, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s. II. 22.<BR>fr. rt. 1. रुद् above; according to others fr. rt. 1. रु<BR>+ द्र fr. rt. 2. द्रु, to run; connected with रोदस्,<BR>q. v., and perhaps with रुधिर), crying, howling,<BR>roaring, one who cries or roars, dreadful, horrible,<BR>terrific, awful; great, large; (according to the fanciful<BR>etymologies of native writers, the following meanings<BR>are also assigned to this word), driving away evil;<BR>running about and roaring; praiseworthy, to be<BR>praised, (according to Naigh. III. 16) = स्तोतृ, a<BR>praiser, panegyrist, worshipper; (अस्), m. ‘the Roarer’<BR>or ‘Howler,’ N. of the god of tempests and father<BR>of the Rudras or Maruts, (originally perhaps the<BR>mere personified roaring of the storms, but as the<BR>crackling or raging of fire may resemble the sound<BR>of wind, so in the Veda the god of storms is some-<BR>times identified with the god of fire; though gene-<BR>rally represented as a destroying deity whose terrible<BR>shafts bring death or disease on men and cattle, he<BR>is also addressed as benevolent and auspicious [शिव],<BR>and is even supposed to have a healing efficacy from<BR>his chasing away vapours and purifying the atmo-<BR>sphere; hence he has various epithets in the Veda,<BR>such as ‘multiform,’ ‘terrible as a wild beast,’ ‘tawny-<BR>coloured,’ ‘wearing braided hair’ [कपर्दिन्], ‘ce-<BR>lestial boar,’ ‘armed with a strong bow and fleet<BR>arrows,’ ‘cause of prosperity to man and beast,’ ‘pos-<BR>sessor of healing remedies,’ ‘greatest of physicians,’<BR>&c.; he is of course ruler of the Rudras, who are<BR>the same as the storm winds, more usually called<BR>Maruts, and who are often associated with Indra [see<BR>मरुत्]: in the later mythology the epithet शिव,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-b" target="_blank">Page0849-b+ 81</a>]<BR>‘propitious,’ which does not occur as a name in the<BR>Veda, was employed as the real name of the destroy-<BR>ing deity, being at first applied as an euphemism to<BR>propitiate him: moreover the character of the deity<BR>lost its special connection with storms, and developed<BR>into a personification of the destroying principle<BR>generally, though even the Epic and Purānic Śiva<BR>was regarded as the generator as well as destroyer:<BR>moreover a new class of beings, described as eleven<BR>in number, though still called Rudras, took the<BR>place of the original Rudras or Maruts: in the Veda<BR>only three groupings of deities into classes appear to<BR>be recognised, Indra belonging to the Vasus, Varuṇa<BR>to the Ādityas, and Rudra to the Rudras or Maruts;<BR>but in Manu XI. 221. the Maruts are enumerated<BR>as a fourth group, being there distinguished from<BR>the eleven Rudras: in Viṣṇu-Purāṇa I. 7. Rudra<BR>is said to have sprung from Brahmā's forehead, and<BR>to have afterwards separated himself into a figure<BR>half male and half female, the former portion sepa-<BR>rating again into the eleven Rudras, who were so<BR>called because they ‘ran about crying aloud’ [रुद-<BR>नाद् द्रावणाच्-च, cf. rts. 1. रुद्, 2. द्रु]; hence<BR>these later Rudras are sometimes regarded as inferior<BR>manifestations of Śiva, and most of their names are<BR>also names of Śiva; these names are variously given<BR>in the different Purāṇas; those of the Vāyu are<BR>Ajaikapād, Ahvi-bradhna, Hara, Nir-ṛta, Īśvara,<BR>Bhuvana, Aṅgāraka, Ardha-ketu, Mṛtyu, Sarpa,<BR>Kapālin: according to other accounts the Rudras are<BR>represented as children of Kaśyapa and Surabhī or of<BR>Brahmā and Surabhī or of Bhūta and Su-rūpā); a<BR>form or manifestation or N. of Śiva (in the later<BR>mythology, as explained above; according to the<BR>Viṣṇu-Purāṇa I. 8. Rudra is one of the eight forms<BR>of Śiva; he is elsewhere reckoned among the Dik-<BR>pālas as regent of the north-east quarter); a symbo-<BR>lical expression for the number eleven (from the<BR>eleven Rudras, see above); a mystical epithet of<BR>the letter ए; Calotropis Gigantea; N. of various<BR>persons; of a lexicographer; of a poet; of a king;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the Rudras (described above); an<BR>abbreviated expression for the texts or hymns ad-<BR>dressed to the Rudras [cf. रुद्र-जप]; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a wife of Vasu-deva; of a daughter of Rau-<BR>drāśva; = रुद्र-जटा; (ई), f. a kind of lute or<BR>guitar; [cf. रुद्र-वीणा; cf. perhaps also Gr. λύρα.]<BR>—रुद्र-कलश, अम्, n. ‘Rudra's vessel,’ a parti-<BR>cular kind of pot or vessel used in making oblations<BR>to the planets.<BR>—रुद्र-कवीन्द्र (˚वि-इन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a proper N. (= रुद्र-भट्ट).<BR>—रुद्र-काली, f. a<BR>form of Durgā.<BR>—रुद्र-कोटि, इस्, f., N. of a place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR>—रुद्र-कोष, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>lexicon by Rudra.<BR>—रुद्र-गण, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>‘Rudra-class,’ the troop of beings called Rudras,<BR>(see under रुद्र.)<BR>—रुद्र-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘Ru-<BR>dra's offspring,’ N. of Agni.<BR>—रुद्र-गीत, अम्, आ,<BR>n. f. the song of Rudra (in which Agastya repeats<BR>a dialogue between himself and Rudra).<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>चण्डिक, epithet of a particular text or formula.<BR>—रुद्र-चण्डी, f. a form of Durgā; N. of a<BR>section in the Rudra-yāmala.<BR>—रुद्र-चन्द्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—रुद्र-च्छत्त्र, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रुद्र-ज, अस्, m. (according to some)<BR>अम्, n. ‘produced from Rudra or Śiva,’ quicksilver<BR>(supposed to be the semen of Śiva).<BR>—रुद्र-जटा,<BR>f. ‘Rudra's hair,’ N. of a species of creeper.<BR>—रु-<BR>द्र-जप, अस्, m., N. of a particular prayer or<BR>hymn addressed to Rudra.<BR>—रुद्र-जपन, अम्,<BR>n. the recitation of the Rudra-japa in a low tone.<BR>—रुद्र-जापक, अस्, इका, अम्, or रुद्र-जापिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, one who recites the Rudra-japa in a low<BR>tone.<BR>—रुद्र-जाप्य, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>hymn or prayer extracted from the Vājasaneyi-saṃ-<BR>hitā and addressed to Rudra.<BR>—रुद्र-तनय, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Rudra's son,’ N. of the third black Vāsudeva;<BR>of Punishment; epithet of a sword.<BR>—रुद्र-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the being Rudra.<BR>—रुद्र-दत्त, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author; of a work on medicine.<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>दामन्, आ, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रुद्र-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of various persons; of the author of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-c" target="_blank">Page0849-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Yayāti-carita; of the author of a commentary on<BR>the Prabodha-candrodaya.<BR>—रुद्र-धर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author.<BR>—रुद्र-न्याय-वाचस्पति-भट्-<BR>टाचार्य (˚त-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author (=<BR>रुद्र-भट्टाचार्य).<BR>—रुद्र-पण्डित, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author (= रुद्र-सूरि).<BR>—रुद्र-पत्नी,<BR>f. Rudra's wife, the goddess Durgā; linseed, Linum<BR>Usitatissimum.<BR>—रुद्र-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of<BR>a work by Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—रुद्र-पाल, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रुद्र-पुत्र, अस्, m. Rudra's son, a<BR>patronymic of the twelfth Manu; [cf. रुद्र-सा-<BR>वर्णि.]<BR>—रुद्र-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a province.<BR>—रुद्र-पूजन, अम्, n. or रुद्र-पूजा, f. ‘wor-<BR>ship of Rudra,’ N. of a work.<BR>—रुद्र-प्रताप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king (= प्रताप-रुद्र).<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>प्रयाग, अस्, m., N. of the sacred place where the<BR>river Mandākinī joins the Ganges.<BR>—रुद्र-प्रिया,<BR>f. ‘dear to Rudra,’ epithet of Terminalia Chebula;<BR>the goddess Pārvatī.<BR>—रुद्र-बलि, इस्, m. an oblation<BR>of meat &c. presented to the Rudras.<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Śṛṅgāra-<BR>tilaka (= रुद्रट); of the author of a commentary<BR>on the Vaidya-jīvana; = रुद्र-कवीन्द्र.<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>भट्टाचार्य (˚ट-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author<BR>and commentator.<BR>—रुद्र-भाष्य, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a work by Ahobala.<BR>—रुद्र-भू, ऊस्, or रुद्र-<BR>भूमि, इस्, f. ‘Rudra's ground,’ a cemetery.<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>भूति, इस्, m., N. of a preceptor (having the patro-<BR>nymic Drāhyāyaṇi).<BR>—रुद्र-भैरवी, f. a form<BR>of Durgā.<BR>—रुद्र-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of<BR>Rudra, having the essence of Rudra.<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>महा-देवी, f., N. of the wife of king Govinda-<BR>canda.<BR>—रुद्र-यज्ञ, अस्, m. an oblation or sacri-<BR>fice offered to Rudra.<BR>—रुद्र-यामल, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tantra work in the form of a dialogue<BR>between Bhairava and Bhairavī.<BR>—रुद्र-राय, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—रुद्र-राशि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रुद्र-रोदन, अम्, n. ‘Rudra's tears,’ i. e. gold.<BR>—रुद्र-रोमन्, आ, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending upon Skanda.<BR>—रुद्र-लटा, f. = रुद्र-<BR>जटा.<BR>—रुद्र-लोक, अस्, m. Rudra's world.<BR>—रु-<BR>द्र-वट, N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—रुद्र-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. having Rudra or the Rudras.<BR>—रुद्रवद्-<BR>गण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. surrounded by the Rudra<BR>troop.<BR>—रुद्र-वर्तनि, ई, m. du. ‘proceeding on<BR>terrible roads,’ N. of the Aśvins, (Sāy. = रोदन-<BR>शील-मार्गौ or स्तूयमान-मार्गौ.)<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>विंशति, इस्, f. epithet of the last twenty years in the<BR>Jupiter cycle of sixty years.<BR>—रुद्र-विधान, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—रुद्र-वीणा, f. epithet of a<BR>particular religious observance.<BR>—रुद्र-शर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—रुद्र-सम्प्रदायिन्, इनस्,<BR>m. pl., N. of a sect.<BR>—रुद्र-सरस्, अस्, n., N. of a<BR>lake.<BR>—रुद्र-सर्ग, अस्, m. Rudra's creation; the<BR>creation of the eleven Rudras.<BR>—रुद्र-सामन्, अ,<BR>n., N. of a particular Sāman.<BR>—रुद्र-सावर्णि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of the twelfth Manu; [cf. रुद्र-पुत्र,<BR>मनु.]<BR>—रुद्रसावर्णिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging<BR>or relating to Rudra-sāvarṇi, being under Rudra-<BR>sāvarṇi.<BR>—रुद्र-सिंह, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रु-<BR>द्र-सुन्दरी, f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—रुद्र-सू, ऊस्,<BR>f. a mother of eleven children.<BR>—रुद्र-सूक्त, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a particular hymn.<BR>—रुद्र-सूरि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author.<BR>—रुद्र-सृष्टि, इस्, f. Rudra's<BR>creation; the creation of the eleven Rudras; [cf.<BR>रुद्र-सर्ग.]<BR>—रुद्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>warrior.<BR>—रुद्र-सोम, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—रुद्र-स्कन्द, अस्, m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—रुद्र-स्वर्ग, अस्, m. Rudra's heaven.<BR>—रुद्र-<BR>स्वामिन्, ई, m. a proper N.<BR>—रुद्र-हिमालय, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a peak of the Himālaya mountains.<BR>—रुद्र-हूति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (according to Mahī-<BR>dhara on Vājasaneyi-s. XXXVIII. 16) being invoked<BR>by praisers or worshippers.<BR>—रुद्र-हृदय, अम्,<BR>n., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—रुद्राक्रीड (˚र-आक्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘Rudra's play-ground,’ a cemetery, place<BR>where dead bodies are burnt or buried (Rudra being<BR>supposed to dance and sport in such places at evening<BR>twilight).<BR>—रुद्राक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘Rudra-<BR>eyed,’ a kind of tree, Elæocarpus Ganitrus; (अम्),<BR>n. the berry of this tree (used for rosaries); a rosary;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">Page0850-a+ 79</a>]<BR>N. of an Upaniṣad, (the gender here and in the preced-<BR>ing sense is doubtful.)<BR>—रुद्राक्ष-माला, f. a rosary<BR>made of Rudrākṣa berries.<BR>—रुद्राचार्य (˚र-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रुद्राध्याय (˚र-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. epithet of particular prayers addressed to Rudra.<BR>—रुद्राध्यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who recites or<BR>repeats the above prayers.<BR>—रुद्रायण (˚र-अय्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king of Roruka.<BR>—रुद्रारि (˚र-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. Rudra's enemy; N. of Kāma-deva;<BR>(इस्, इस्, इ), having Rudra for an enemy, hostile to<BR>Rudra.<BR>—रुद्रावर्त (˚र-आव्˚), N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—रुद्रावसृष्ट (˚र-अव्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. let go or hurled by Rudra.<BR>—रुद्रावास<BR>(˚र-आव्˚), अस्, m. Rudra's abode, i. e. Kāśi or Be-<BR>nares.<BR>—रुद्रैकादशिनी (˚र-एक्˚), f. the eleven<BR>Rudra hymns.<BR>—रुद्रोपनिषद् (˚र-उप्˚), त्, f., N.<BR>of two Upaniṣads.<BR>—रुद्रोपस्थ (˚र-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘Rudra's generative organ,’ N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रक
रुद्रक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रट|रुद्रटः
रुद्रट, अस्, m. an abbreviated form of Rudra-<BR>bhaṭṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राणी
रुद्राणी, f. Rudra's wife, the goddess Durgā;<BR>epithet of a girl eleven years of age, in whom men-<BR>struation has not yet commenced, representing the<BR>goddess Durgā at the Durgā festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रिय
रुद्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging or relating<BR>to Rudra [cf. शत-रुद्रिय], coming from Rudra;<BR>relating to the Rudras, coming from them, &c.;<BR>terrific, fearful, awful, impetuous; (according to Sāy.<BR>also) uttering praise or giving pleasure; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the Maruts; (अम्), n. Rudra's majesty or power;<BR>(Sāy.) pleasure, delight (= सुख).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुदिषु
रुरुदिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid.), wishing or<BR>intending to weep, inclined to cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोद|रोदः
रोद, अस्, m., Ved. weeping, wailing, lamenting,<BR>lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदन|रोदनं
रोदन, अम्, n. the act of weeping or wailing,<BR>bewailing, lamentation; weeping, a tear, tears; (ई),<BR>f. Alhagi Maurorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदमान
रोदमान, अस्, आ, अम्, for रुदमान, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदस्
रोदस्, अस्, n. heaven, &c. See p. 855, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदितव्य
रोदितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bewailed or lamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदित्वा
रोदित्वा, ind. = रुदित्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुदत्
रोरुदत्, अन्, अती, अत्, weeping or wailing bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुदा
रोरुदा, f. violent weeping, excessive lamentation.<BR>—रोरुदा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, full of excessive lamen-<BR>tation, weeping violently or intensely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुद्यमान
रोरुद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, weeping or crying<BR>bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्ध|रुद्धं
रुद्ध रुद्ध. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्र|रुद्रः
रुद्र रुद्र. See p. 849, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्
रुध् 1. रुध् (= rt. 1. रुह्), cl. 1. P. रो-<BR>धति, &c., Ved. to sprout, shoot, grow,<BR>germinate; [cf. न्यग्-रोध, 2. अव-रोध.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध|रोधः
1. रोध, अस्, m. sprouting, growing, &c.; [cf.<BR>2. अव-र्˚, न्यग्-र्˚.]<BR>—रोधावरोध (˚ध-अव्˚),<BR>probably ‘moving up and down.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्
रुध् 2. रुध्, cl. 7. P. A. रुणद्धि,<BR>रुन्द्धे (ep. also रुन्धति, रुन्धते,<BR>रोधति, Impf. अरुन्धत्), रुरोध, रुरुधे,<BR>रोत्स्यति, -ते, अरुधत् or अरौत्सीत्, अरुद्ध (Ved.<BR>forms अरौत्, रुध्मस्, अरौत्सि), रोद्धुम् (ep.<BR>also रोधितुम्), to stop, check, arrest, restrain,<BR>hinder, impede, prevent, obstruct, suppress, oppose;<BR>to hold, withhold, retain, keep; to avert, keep off,<BR>keep back; to shut, close, lock, shut up, lock up,<BR>block up, close up, stop up, fill up; to besiege,<BR>blockade, lay siege to, invest; to shut in, enclose,<BR>surround, confine (with loc. of the place of confine-<BR>ment or with double acc. according to Vopa-deva V.<BR>6); to bind; to cover, cover up, cover over, obscure;<BR>to oppress, torment, harass: Pass. रुध्यते, Aor.<BR>अरोधि: Caus. रोधयति, -ते (ep. also रुन्ध-<BR>यति), -यितुम्, Aor. अरूरुधत्, to cause to stop;<BR>to restrain, impede, obstruct; to cause to be con-<BR>fined; cause to be besieged; to fetter, enchain; to<BR>oppress, torment, harass: Desid. रुरुत्सति, -ते:<BR>Intens. रोरुध्यते, रोरोद्धि; [cf. perhaps Hib.<BR>rundha, ‘secret, mysterious;’ rundhachd, ‘secrecy;’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">Page0850-b+ 80</a>]<BR>ruindiamhar, ‘a mystery;’ ruine, ‘secrecy:’ Goth.<BR>runa, ‘a mystery:’ Old Germ. runen, runazjan,<BR>which may be related to rt. 1. रु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्ध|रुद्धं
रुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, stopped, checked, impeded,<BR>restrained, obstructed, suppressed, opposed; held,<BR>withheld; kept, kept back; shut, closed, shut up,<BR>secured; invested, besieged, blockaded; shut in,<BR>enclosed, confined, surrounded, begirt, fenced in;<BR>covered, covered up; (अस्), m., N. of a town; (आ),<BR>f. a siege.<BR>—रुद्ध-गिर्, ईर्, ईर्, ईर्, having the<BR>utterance choked or impeded.<BR>—रुद्ध-प्रवाह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the stream obstructed.<BR>—रुद्ध-<BR>मूत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having the urine suppressed;<BR>suffering from retention of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्धक
रुद्धक, अम्, n. citron, (perhaps for रुचक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्ध्वा
रुद्ध्वा, ind. having stopped or checked, having<BR>restrained or obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्
3. रुध्, त्, त्, त्, stopping, restraining, impeding,<BR>holding; [cf. कर-र्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध
रुध, अस्, आ, अम्, stopping, restraining, hinder-<BR>ing, repelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुधिक्रा
रुधि-क्रा, m., Ved., N. of an Asura or demon<BR>conquered by Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुन्धत्
रुन्धत्, अन्, अती, अत्, stopping, hindering, op-<BR>posing, impeding; resisting, refusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुत्सु
रुरुत्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to obstruct or oppose;<BR>wishing to bind or tie up (as the hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोद्धव्य
रोद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be closed or shut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोद्धृ
रोद्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, one who stops or<BR>obstructs, one who shuts in, a besieger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध|रोधः
2. रोध, अस्, m. (for 1. रोध see col. 1), the<BR>act of stopping, checking, arresting, restraining,<BR>hindering, impeding, preventing, &c.; restraint,<BR>stoppage, obstruction, suppression, prevention, pro-<BR>hibition; shutting up, confining; closing, blocking<BR>up; siege, blockade (of a town); attacking, making<BR>war upon; a dam, bank, shore [cf. रोधस् below];<BR>a proper N.; N. of a hell.<BR>—रोध-कृत्, त्, m. epi-<BR>thet of the forty-fifth year in the Jupiter cycle of sixty<BR>years.<BR>—रोध-चक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (rivers) forming<BR>eddies on the bank, (Sāy. = रोधन-शीलानि चक्राणि<BR>यासु.)<BR>—रोध-वक्रा, f. = रोधो-वक्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधक
रोधक, अस्, इका, अम्, stopping, checking, re-<BR>straining, confining, shutting up, besieging, block-<BR>ading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधन|रोधनः
रोधन, अस्, ई, अम्, obstructing, impeding, being<BR>an obstacle or hindrance; (अस्), m. the planet Mer-<BR>cury; (आ), f. = रोधस्; (अम्), n. the act of stop-<BR>ping, checking, restraining, preventing, impeding,<BR>oppressing; the act of confining, confinement, re-<BR>straint; besieging, blockading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधस्
रोधस्, अस्, n. a bank, embankment, dam, ob-<BR>struction; a mound, high bank, wall, a shore; the<BR>brink of a well; a flank, epithet of a woman's hips;<BR>[cf. तट.]<BR>—रोधः-पतन-कलुष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(rendered) muddy by the falling in of a bank.<BR>—रो-<BR>धस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having high banks<BR>(said of rivers; Ved.); (अती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—रोधो-वक्रा, f. ‘winding along its banks,’ a<BR>river.<BR>—रोधो-वती, f. ‘having banks,’ a river.<BR>—रोधो-वप्र, अस्, m. a rapid river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधिन्
रोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, stopping, checking, restraining,<BR>hindering, preventing, prohibiting; shutting up,<BR>closing; destroying; a species of plant, (gender<BR>doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध्य
रोध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stopped or checked,<BR>to be restrained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुधिर|रुधिरं|रुधिरः
रुधिर रुधिर, अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. I. 52. fr. rt. 2. रुध्; according to some<BR>fr. a lost rt. रुध्; according to others connected<BR>with rts. 1. रुध् and 1. रुह्; cf. रोहित), red,<BR>blood-red, bloody (Ved.); (अस्), m. the blood-red<BR>planet, i. e. Mars; a kind of precious stone [cf. रु-<BR>धिराख्य]; (अम्), n. blood; saffron; N. of a<BR>town; [cf. शोणित-पुर: cf. also Gr. ἐρεύθ-ω,<BR>ἐρυθ-ρός, ἔρευθ-ος, ἐρυθρ-ιά-ω, ἐρυσίβη, ῥούσιος:]<BR>Lat. ruber, rufu-s, rutilu-s (for old ruthilus),<BR>rob-igo: Old Norse riod-r, ‘ruddy;’ rioda: Goth.<BR>ga-riud-jo: Old Germ. rot, rost: Angl. Sax. read,<BR>roder: Slav. rud-e-ti, ruzd-a: Lith. raud-a, rud-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">Page0850-c+ 74</a>]<BR>a-s, rūdi-s: Hib. ruadh, ruaid, ‘red, reddish;’<BR>ruaidhim, ‘I redden.’]<BR>—रुधिर-ताम्राक्ष, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having blood-red eyes.<BR>—रुधिर-पायिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘drinking blood,’ a Rākṣasa or demon.<BR>—रु-<BR>धिर-प्रदिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, besmeared with<BR>blood.<BR>—रुधिर-प्लावित, अस्, आ, अम्, swimming<BR>with blood, soaked in blood.<BR>—रुधिर-रूषित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, covered with blood.<BR>—रुधिर-लेप, अस्, m.<BR>blood-stain, smear of blood.<BR>—रुधिर-विन्दु, उस्, m.<BR>a drop of blood.<BR>—रुधिराक्ष (˚र-अक्˚) = रुधि-<BR>राख्य below (according to some).<BR>—रुधिराख्य<BR>(˚र-आख्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘blood-named, red as blood,’<BR>epithet of a particular precious stone.<BR>—रुधिराध्या-<BR>य (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Kālikā-<BR>Purāṇa treating of the sacrifice of animals.<BR>—रुधि-<BR>रानन (˚र-आन्˚), अम्, n. epithet of one of the five<BR>retrograding motions of Mars.<BR>—रुधिरान्ध<BR>(˚र-अन्˚), ‘whose waters are blood,’ N. of a hell.<BR>—रुधिरामय (˚र-आम्˚), अस्, m. ‘blood-disease,’<BR>hemorrhage (= रक्त-पित्त).<BR>—रुधिराविल (˚र-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blood-stained, soiled with blood.<BR>—रुधिराशन (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, feeding on<BR>blood (said of Rākṣasas &c.).<BR>—रुधिरोद्गारिन्<BR>(˚र-उद्˚), ई, इणी, इ, spitting blood, vomiting blood;<BR>(ई), m. epithet of the fifty-seventh year in the Jupiter<BR>cycle of sixty years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुप्
रुप् 1. रुप् (an older form of rt. 1. लुप्),<BR>cl. 4. P. रुप्यति, रुरोप, अरुपत्, &c.,<BR>to suffer violent or racking pain (Ved.); to violate,<BR>confound, disturb: Caus. रोपयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अरूरुपत्, to cause acute pain; to break off; [cf.<BR>Lat. rumpo, rupi, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप|रोपः
1. रोप, 1. रोपित, &c. See p. 855, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुप्
रुप् 2. रुप् (connected with rt. 1. रुह्),<BR>Ved. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुभेटि
रुभेटि रुभेटि, इस्, f. fog, vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुम
रुम रुम, अस्, m. a proper N. (Ved.); (आ),<BR>f., N. of a salt-mine or salt-lake (in the district of<BR>Sambhar in Ajmere); of a wife of the ape Su-grīva.<BR>—रुमा-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, obtained from the<BR>Rumā salt-mines; [cf. रौमक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुमण्वत्|रुमण्वन्त्
रुमण्वत्, आन्, m. a proper N.; N. of a moun-<BR>tain (‘possessing salt’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुम्र|रुम्रः
रुम्र रुम्र, अस्, आ, अम् (in Uṇādi-s. II. 14.<BR>said to be fr. rt. रम्) = अरुण, tawny; the dawn,<BR>&c.; = शोबन, bright, beautiful, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरु|रुरुः
रुरु रुरु, उस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. IV. 103.<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. रु), a kind of deer; a species of<BR>rapacious animal, a dog; a species of fruit tree; N.<BR>of a son of the Ṛṣi Pramati by the Apsaras Ghṛ-<BR>tācī; of a divine being enumerated among the Viśve<BR>Devāḥ; of one of the seven Ṛṣis under Manu<BR>Sāvarṇi (his patronymic is Kāśyapa); of a Dānava<BR>or Daitya (said to have been slain by Durgā); of a<BR>form of Bhairava, (sometimes called रुरु-भैरव.)<BR>—रुरु-मुण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a mountain, (also<BR>read उरु-मुण्ड.)<BR>—रुरु-शीर्षन्, आ, -ष्णी, अ,<BR>Ved. ‘deer-headed,’ having a deer's horn or having<BR>a destructive point (said of an arrow; Sāy. = शृङ्ग-<BR>शीर्षन् or हन्तृ-शिरस्क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुक
रुरुक, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुक्षणि
रुरुक्षणि रुरुक्षणि. See p. 848, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुत्सु
रुरुत्सु रुरुत्सु. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुदिषु
रुरुदिषु रुरुदिषु. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवण्य
रुवण्य रुवण्य, रुवथ. See p. 847, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवु|रुवुः
रुवु रुवु, उस्, m. [cf. उरुवु], the castor-<BR>oil tree, Ricinus Communis (= रक्तैरण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवुक|रुवुकः
रुवुक or रुवूक, अस्, m. Ricinus Communis;<BR>[cf. उरुवुक, रूवुक, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुश्
रुश् रुश् (connected with and in some<BR>forms and meanings identified with rt.<BR>1. रुष्), cl. 6. P. रुशति, रुरोश, रोक्ष्यति,<BR>अरुक्षत्, रोष्टुम्, to hurt, injure, kill; to vex,<BR>displease, annoy: Caus. रोशयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">Page0851-a+ 77</a>]<BR>अरूरुशत्: Desid. रुरुक्षति: Intens. रोरुश्यते,<BR>रोरोष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0850-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशत्|रुशन्त्
1. रुशत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, hurting, injuring,<BR>vexing, displeasing; cursing, imprecating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशङ्गु
रुशङ्गु रुशङ्गु, उस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशत्|रुशन्त्
रुशत् 2. रुशत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत् (probably<BR>to be regarded as a participle connected with rt.<BR>1. रुच्), Ved. brilliant, bright, light-coloured, white;<BR>[cf. Gr. λευκός]<BR>—रुशत्-पशु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having<BR>white cattle; (Sāy.) having brilliant rays or blazing<BR>with the oblation (= रुशद्-रश्मि or प्रकाशित-<BR>हविस्).<BR>—रुशद्-ऊर्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having glis-<BR>tening waves, having bright flames (said of Fire;<BR>Sāy. = दीप्त-ज्वाल).<BR>—रुशद्-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>having white or bright cattle; bright-rayed, (Sāy.<BR>= रोचमान-रश्मि); (उस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—रु-<BR>शद्-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a light-coloured<BR>carriage; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—रुशद्-वत्स, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having a bright or white calf or offspring,<BR>(the Dawn is so called as parent of the Sun.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशना
रुशना रुशना, f., N. of one of the wives<BR>of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशम
रुशम रुशम, अस्, m. a proper N.; (आ), f.<BR>a proper N., (Ruśamā is said to have contended<BR>with Indra as to which of the two would run fastest<BR>round the earth, and to have won by the artifice of<BR>only going round Kurukṣetra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशेकु
रुशेकु रुशेकु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्
रुष् 1. रुष् (connected with and in<BR>some forms and meanings identified with<BR>rt. रुश्; allied also to रुक्ष् in 1. रुक्ष), cl.<BR>1. P. रोषति, रुरोष, रोषिष्यति, अरोषीत् or<BR>अरुषत्, रोषितुम् or रोष्टुम्, to hurt, injure, kill;<BR>to vex, annoy, displease, make angry, disgust; to<BR>take ill, be offended (Ved.); cl. 4. रुष्यति, to be<BR>vexed or annoyed; to be offended; to be cross or<BR>angry; to injure, &c.: cl. 10. or Caus. रोषयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अरूरुषत्, to vex, annoy, displease, irritate;<BR>to enrage, exasperate: Desid. रुरुषिषति, रुरोषि-<BR>षति: Intens. रोरुष्यते, रोरोष्टि; [cf. probably<BR>Gr. λύσσα, λυσσάω, λυσσαίνω, (perhaps also) ἀλυσταίνω,<BR>ἀλυκταίνω, ἀλαλὐκτημαι; Goth. in-rauht-<BR>jan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्
2. रुष्, ट्, f. anger, wrath, rage, fury, passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुषङ्गु|रुषंगु
रुषङ्गु, उस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुषत्
रुषत्, अन्, अन्ती or अती (as if fr. rt. रुश्), अत्,<BR>hurting, injuring, vexing, displeasing.<BR>—रुषद्-गु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुषा
रुषा, f. = 2. रुष्, anger, wrath, rage, fury.<BR>—रुषान्वित (˚षा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, filled with<BR>anger, full of wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुषित|रुषितः
रुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, injured; enraged, irritated,<BR>&c., = रुष्ट below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्ट|रुष्टः
रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, enraged, irritated, offended,<BR>angry, furious; (अस्), m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्टि|रुष्टिः
रुष्टि, इस्, f. anger, wrath, rage, fury, passion.<BR>—रुष्टि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, angry, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्य
1. रुष्य, रुष्य-मत्, see Gaṇa Madhvādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्य
2. रुष्य, ind. having irritated or enraged, &c.<BR>(Rāmāyaṇa II. 98, 12).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्यत्
रुष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being angry or offended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष्
रोष्, ट्, m. one who hurts or injures, an injurer;<BR>one who irritates or enrages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष|रोषः
रोष, अस्, m. anger, rage, wrath, passion, fury.<BR>—रोष-ताम्राक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, having eyes red<BR>with anger.<BR>—रोष-परीत, अस्, आ, अम्, filled with<BR>wrath.<BR>—रोष-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of anger,<BR>proceeding from fury.<BR>—रोष-वाहण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘being a vehicle of anger,’ bearing or feeling wrath<BR>(= आरूढ-क्रोध).<BR>—रोषाक्षेप (˚ष-आक्˚),<BR>अस्, m. (in rhetoric) angry expression of dissent, angry<BR>reproach, ironical taunt.<BR>—रोषावरोह (˚ष-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a warrior on the side of the gods in<BR>the war against the Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषण|रोषणः
रोषण, अस्, ई, अम्, angry, wrathful, passionate,<BR>easily enraged; enraged at or against, (क्षत्रिय-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">Page0851-b+ 80</a>]<BR>रोषण, exasperated at the Kṣatriyas); (अस्), m. a<BR>touch-stone; quicksilver; an arid or desert soil con-<BR>taining salt; Grewia Asiatica.<BR>—रोषण-ता, f. the<BR>state of being easily enraged, proneness to anger,<BR>irritability, wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषित
रोषित, अस्, आ, अम्, enraged, exasperated, irritated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषिन्
रोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, angry, wrathful, irritable, furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष्टृ
रोष्टृ, टा, टॄ, an injurer; one who is vexed<BR>or angry, wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्
रुह् 1. रुह् (originally written रुध्; cf.<BR>rt. 1. रुध्), cl. 1. P. रोहति (ep. also A.<BR>रोहते), रुरोह, रोक्ष्यति, अरुक्षत् (Ved. and<BR>ep. अरुहत्), रोढुम् (ep. रोहितुम्, Ved. रोहिष्यै,<BR>Pāṇ. III. 4, 10), to rise, mount upwards, ascend,<BR>climb; to spring up, shoot forth, sprout, germinate,<BR>to be produced or born; to grow, grow up, be<BR>developed or formed, grow larger, increase, increase<BR>in size; to grow together, grow over, cicatrize,<BR>heal; to reach to, attain: Caus. रोहयति or (in the<BR>later language) रोपयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरूरुहत्<BR>or अरूरुपत्, to cause to ascend, raise up, elevate;<BR>to place in or on, fix, fasten; to deliver over, com-<BR>mit, entrust; to plant, sow, put in the ground; to<BR>cause to grow, cause to grow over or heal: Desid.<BR>रुरुक्षति: Intens. रोरुह्यते, रोरोढि; [cf. per-<BR>haps Gr. λαό-ς, βασι-λεύ-ς: perhaps Lat. rus, rur-<BR>is: Goth. liugan, jugga-lauths; liudith, ‘it<BR>grows;’ lauths, ‘a man’ (gen. laudi-s): Old<BR>Germ. liut, ‘a people;’ liuti (= Mod. Germ.<BR>Leute), sumarlota, ‘a twig;’ ruota, ‘a set, twig:’<BR>Old Sax. ruoda: Angl. Sax. rod: Slav. rod-i-ti,<BR>‘to bring forth;’ na-rodu, ‘a people:’ Lith. liu-<BR>dinu, ‘to produce;’ rudu, ‘autumn:’ Celt. rho-<BR>dara, ‘a kind of plant;’ rod-ra, ‘a tree:’ Scot.<BR>ros, ‘seed;’ rosach, ‘full of seed:’ Hib. rosan, ‘a<BR>shrub;’ rud, ‘a wood, forest;’ ruadh, ‘strength,<BR>value; strong;’ romho, ‘very much, great;’ rom-<BR>hoide, ‘greatness;’ ruidh, ‘running, a race;’ roid,<BR>‘a race;’ ruaidhneach, ‘hair;’ laidir, ‘strong,<BR>stout;’ laidireacht, laidireas, ‘strength.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्
2. रुह्, ट्, f. rising, ascending, ascent, sprouting,<BR>germinating, growth; (at the end of a comp.) shoot-<BR>ing up, germinating, growing, increasing; [cf. अम्-<BR>भो-र्˚, क्षिति-र˚, भूमी-र˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह|रुहः
रुह, अस्, आ, अम्, rising, mounting, springing up,<BR>germinating, growing, springing from, growing on,<BR>produced on (at the end of a comp., cf. पङ्क-र्˚,<BR>भूमी-र˚, मही-र˚); mounted, ascended upon; (आ),<BR>f. bent grass, Panicum Dactylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुहक|रुहकं
रुहक, अम्, n. a hole, vacuity, cave, chasm;<BR>[cf. 1. रोप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुहाण
रुहाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. attaining, gaining; gain-<BR>ing over, delighting, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 32, 8. मनो रुहाण = चित्ताम् आरोहत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्वन्
रुह्वन्, आ, m. a plant, tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढ|रूढं|रूढः
रूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, mounted, risen, ascended;<BR>sprung up, born, produced; grown, grown up, in-<BR>creased; budded, blown; large, bulky, great, much;<BR>grown or spread about, diffused, commonly known,<BR>notorious; certain, ascertained; traditional, generally<BR>received, popular, customary, conventional, not to be<BR>etymologically resolved; having a special meaning<BR>or one not depending directly on the etymology<BR>(said of words); obscure.<BR>—रूढ-प्रणय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, whose love or affection has grown strong.<BR>—रू-<BR>ढ-योग, अस्, आ, अम्, whose Yoga or devotion has<BR>increased.<BR>—रूढ-यौवन, अस्, m. one who has<BR>attained to youth or adolescence.<BR>—रूढ-वञ्श,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of a high family.<BR>—रूढ-वचन, अम्,<BR>n. = रूढि-शब्द below.<BR>—रूढ-सौहृद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, whose friendship is grown or increased, firm<BR>in friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढि|रूढिः
रूढि, इस्, f. ascending, rising, rise, ascent;<BR>springing up, germination, birth, origin; growth,<BR>increase; fame, renown, notoriety; tradition, cus-<BR>tom, traditional or customary usage, common cur-<BR>rency, general prevalence, popular or conventional<BR>acceptation of words (as opposed to their direct ety-<BR>mological meaning); the employment of a word in<BR>a sense not borne out by its etymology.<BR>—रूढि-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">Page0851-c+ 78</a>]<BR>शब्द, अस्, m. a word not etymologically derived, a<BR>word used in a conventional sense (as opposed to the<BR>etymological, thus शत्रु as a Rūḍhi-śabda means<BR>‘enemy,’ but in its etymological sense ‘a destroyer’).<BR>—रूढिशब्द-ता, f. the state of being used in a<BR>conventional sense (said of a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढ्वा
रूढ्वा, ind. having ascended, having grown, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोढृ
रोढृ, 2. रोप, रोह, &c. See pp. 854, 855.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुहिरुहिका
रुहिरुहिका रुहिरुहिका, f. = उत्कण्ठा; [cf.<BR>रण-रणक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष्
रूक्ष् रूक्ष् (more properly regarded as<BR>a Nom. fr. रूक्ष below; cf. rts. 1. रुष्,<BR>रूष्, रूषित), cl. 10. P. रूक्षयति (according<BR>to Vopa-deva also रूक्षापयति), -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अरुरूक्षत्, to be rough or harsh; to make dry or<BR>emaciated (Ved.); to soil, smear (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष|रूक्षं|रूक्षः
रूक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps fr. rt. 1. रुष्, q. v.,<BR>but according to Uṇādi-s. III. 66. fr. rt. 1. रुह्;<BR>and according to others connected with rt. रूष् and<BR>रूषित; sometimes written रुक्ष, see 1. रुक्ष),<BR>rough, harsh (to the touch), not smooth or soft;<BR>rough to the taste, astringent, not bland; rough,<BR>rugged, uneven, difficult; harsh, cruel, unkind, un-<BR>couth, austere; firm, dry, arid, parched, emaciated;<BR>(अस्), m. a species of grass (= वरक); a tree [cf.<BR>रुह्वन्, according to some for Prākṛt rukkha =<BR>वृक्ष]; (आ), f. Croton Polyandrum or Croton<BR>Tiglium.<BR>—रूक्ष-गन्धक, अस्, m. bdellium.<BR>—रूक्ष-ता, f. or रूक्ष-त्व, अम्, n. roughness,<BR>harshness, dryness, aridity, emaciation; harshness,<BR>unkindness, unfriendliness.<BR>—रूक्ष-दर्भ, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of grass.<BR>—रूक्ष-पत्त्र, अस्, m. Tro-<BR>phis Aspera (= शाखोट).<BR>—रूक्ष-पेषम्, ind.,<BR>with rt. पिष्, to pound dry, i. e. without adding<BR>butter or any liquid (Pāṇ. III. 4, 35).<BR>—रूक्ष-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m. = ऋषभौषध.<BR>—रूक्ष-<BR>स्वादु-फल, अस्, m. a species of fruit tree.<BR>—रू-<BR>क्षी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make rough or<BR>dry.<BR>—रूक्षी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made rough, soiled,<BR>besmeared, covered with, (पांसु-रूक्षीकृत, soiled<BR>or covered with dust; cf. रूषित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्षण|रूक्षणं
रूक्षण, अस्, ई, अम्, making dry or thin, attenu-<BR>ating (Ved.); (अम्), n. the act of making dry or<BR>thin; (in medicine) treatment for reducing fat or<BR>corpulence.<BR>—रूक्षणात्मिका (˚ण-आत्˚), f. a species<BR>of grain (= लङ्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्षित
रूक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, made rough, rough; soiled,<BR>smeared; [cf. अ-रूक्षित, रूषित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूखर
रूखर रूखर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Śaiva<BR>sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूचक
रूचक रूचक, incorrect for रुचक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढ|रूढं|रूढः
रूढ रूढ, रूढि. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्
रूप् रूप् (more properly regarded as<BR>a Nom. fr. रूप below), cl. 10. P. रूप-<BR>यति, &c., to form, mould, model, figure, represent,<BR>to represent on the stage, exhibit in pantomime or<BR>by gesture, act; to feign; to view, inspect, contem-<BR>plate; (probably) to appear, (in this sense only A.<BR>रूपयते, see Vopa-deva XXII. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप|रूपं
रूप, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 28. fr.<BR>rt. 1. रु, but probably fr. a base रूप् for रोप्, Caus.<BR>of rt. 1. रुह्; at the end of an adj. comp. the fem.<BR>ends in आ), any outward appearance or phenomenon,<BR>form, figure, shape, (रूपं कृ, to assume a form);<BR>any object of vision or visible object (as colour &c.);<BR>reflected form, image, representation, similitude, re-<BR>semblance, semblance; the form of a noun or verb<BR>&c. (in grammar), an inflected form by declension<BR>or conjugation; a beautiful appearance, handsome form,<BR>mien, or figure, shapeliness, beauty, elegance, grace;<BR>natural state or condition, natural disposition, nature,<BR>essence, property, character, characteristic, peculiarity,<BR>feature, sign, symptom; kind, sort, species; mode,<BR>manner; a single specimen, type, copy, pattern,<BR>original, exemplar; discrete quantity, the number<BR>one, the arithmetical unit; integer number, (in this<BR>sense said to be plur.); known or absolute number,<BR>a known quantity (expressed in algebra by the first<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-a" target="_blank">Page0852-a+ 81</a>]<BR>syllable रू); a particular coin, (probably) a rupee [cf.<BR>रूपक, रूप्य]; a drama, play, dramatic compo-<BR>sition; (according to native lexicographers रूप has<BR>also the following meanings), cattle, a herd of cattle;<BR>= मृग, a beast; = शब्द, sound, word; a Śloka,<BR>verse; = ग्रन्थावृत्ति, acquiring familiarity with<BR>any book by frequent recitation or learning by heart;<BR>(अस्), m. a proper N.; (अस् or अम्), m. n. (?) , N. of<BR>a place; (आ), f., N. of a river. रूप is frequently<BR>used in compounds in the sense ‘formed of,’ ‘com-<BR>posed of,’ ‘consisting of,’ ‘having the figure or<BR>appearance of,’ ‘in the form of,’ ‘having the same<BR>form or colour as,’ ‘like to’ (especially at the end of<BR>adj. comps., e. g. मनोज्ञ-रूपा स्त्री, a beautifully-<BR>formed woman; अन्-आचार-रूप, of an unusual ap-<BR>pearance; अशोक-रूप, having the colour of the<BR>Aśoka, Aśoka-coloured; sometimes used almost re-<BR>dundantly, cf. घोर-र्˚).<BR>—रूप-कर्तृ, ता, m.<BR>‘maker of forms or figures,’ N. of Viśva-kṛt.<BR>—रू-<BR>प-कार, अस्, m. a maker of images, sculptor.<BR>—रू-<BR>प-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, making forms or figures; (त्), m.<BR>epithet of Tvaṣṭṛ (Ved.); a sculptor.<BR>—रूप-गो-<BR>स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of an author.<BR>—रूप-ग्रह, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, apprehending forms, perceiving colours; (अस्),<BR>m. the eye.<BR>—रूप-चिन्ता-मणि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—रूप-जीव for रूपाजीव, q. v.<BR>—रूप-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing forms, perceiving or recog-<BR>nising shapes, distinguishing or discriminating visible<BR>objects (as colours &c.).<BR>—रूप-तत्त्व, अम्, n.<BR>‘reality of form,’ inherent property, natural dispo-<BR>sition, nature, essence.<BR>—रूप-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having most form or colour.<BR>—रूप-तस्, ind.<BR>according to form, by shape, in form.<BR>—रूप-ता,<BR>f. or रूप-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being formed<BR>or composed of (often at the end of comps., e. g.<BR>दुःख-रूप-ता, the consisting of pain).<BR>—रूप-<BR>धर, अस्, आ, अम्, having the form or shape of,<BR>being of the colour of (at the end of a comp., e. g.<BR>गो-रूप-धर, cow-shaped; cf. काम-र्˚); (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—रूप-धातु, उस्, m. the element<BR>of form, original seat or region of form (with Bud-<BR>dhists; the other two elements being काम-ध्˚,<BR>q. v., and अरूप-ध्˚, ‘the element of formlessness’).<BR>—रूपधारि-त्व, अम्, n. the power of assuming<BR>any form or shape.<BR>—रूप-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, bear-<BR>ing a form, assuming a shape; endowed with a good<BR>figure, possessed of beauty.<BR>—रूप-धृक् or रूप-<BR>धृत्, त्, त्, त् (see धृक्, p. 459), having the form<BR>or shape of, resembling (at the end of a comp.,<BR>e. g. कपि-रूप-धृत्, monkey-shaped; cf. विवि-<BR>ध-र्˚).<BR>—रूप-धेय, अम्, n., Ved. form, external<BR>appearance; [cf. नाम-धेय.]<BR>—रूप-नयन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—रूप-नारायण,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—रूप-नाशन, अस्, m.<BR>‘form-destroying,’ an owl.<BR>—रूप-प, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people.<BR>—रूप-पति, इस्, m., Ved. ‘lord of<BR>forms,’ epithet of Tvaṣṭṛ.<BR>—रूप-पुर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—रूप-भागानुबन्ध (˚ग-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the addition of a fraction to a unit.<BR>—रूप-<BR>भागापवाह (˚ग-अप्˚), अस्, m. the deduction of a<BR>fraction from a unit.<BR>—रूप-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, having<BR>form or beauty.<BR>—रूप-भेद, अस्, m. diversity of<BR>form, variety of manifestations; (अम्), n., N. of a Tantra<BR>work.<BR>—रूप-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a woman; of a<BR>work on medicine.<BR>—रूप-मात्र, अम्, n. only<BR>beauty.<BR>—रूप-माला, f., N. of a grammatical work;<BR>(ई), ? f., N. of a metre, four times — -.<BR>—रूप-यौवन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing beauty<BR>and youth.<BR>—रूप-रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—रूप-लता, f., N. of a princess.<BR>—रूप-लावण्य, अम्, n. beauty of form, elegance,<BR>loveliness.<BR>—रूप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having form or<BR>colour, possessing shape or figure, possessed of body,<BR>formed, embodied, bodily, corporeal; having a beauti-<BR>ful form or figure, handsomely formed, handsome,<BR>beautiful, lovely, graceful; having the form or ap-<BR>pearance of (at the end of comps.); (अती), f. a<BR>handsome or beautiful woman; N. of various women;<BR>of a river.<BR>—रूप-वाहिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people,<BR>(also read रूप-वासिक.)<BR>—रूप-विपर्यय, अस्,<BR>m. a morbid change of bodily form.<BR>—रूप-विभा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">Page0852-b+ 81</a>]<BR>ग, अस्, m. the portioning of an integer number.<BR>—रूप-शस्, ind., Ved. in various forms, according<BR>to different formations.<BR>—रूप-शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, pos-<BR>sessing form or figure, possessed of beauty, hand-<BR>some, beautiful.<BR>—रूप-शिखा, f., N. of a daughter<BR>of the Rākṣasa Agni-śikha.<BR>—रूप-समृद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. perfect in form; perfectly beautiful.<BR>—रूप-समृद्धि, इस्, f. perfection of form, a<BR>suitable form.<BR>—रूप-सम्पत्ति, इस्, or रूप-सम्-<BR>पद्, त्, f. perfection or excellence of form, beauty,<BR>handsomeness, elegance.<BR>—रूप-सिद्धि, इस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—रूप-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a Vidyā-<BR>dhara; of a king.<BR>—रूप-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘being<BR>in form,’ having form or figure.<BR>—रूप-हानि, इस्,<BR>f. loss of form, (in the Nyāya one of the seven pre-<BR>ventives of classification.)<BR>—रूपाजीव (˚प-आज्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, making a living by beauty of form, living<BR>by prostitution; (आ), f. a harlot, prostitute.<BR>—रू-<BR>पाधिबोध (˚प-अध्˚), अस्, m. the perception of<BR>form or of any visible object (by the senses).<BR>—रूपा-<BR>वचर (˚प-अव्˚), आस्, m. pl., N. of a class of gods<BR>(with Buddhists); [cf. कामावचर.]<BR>—रूपावली<BR>(˚प-आव्˚), f. a string of inflections, series of varia-<BR>tions of form through declension and conjugation,<BR>&c.<BR>—रूपाश्रय (˚प-आश्˚), अस्, m. a reposi-<BR>tory or receptacle of beauty, an exceedingly hand-<BR>some person.<BR>—रूपास्त्र (˚प-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>beauty for a weapon,’ Kāma-deva, the god of love.<BR>—रूपेन्द्रिय (˚प-इन्˚), अम्, n. the organ of form,<BR>the organ which perceives form and colour, the eye.<BR>—रूपेश्वर (˚प-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>god; (ई), f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—रूपोपजीवन (˚प-<BR>उप्˚), अम्, n. the gaining a livelihood by a handsome<BR>figure.<BR>—रूपोपजीविन् (˚प-उप्˚), ई, इनी, इ, gaining<BR>a livelihood by means of a handsome form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0851-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपक|रूपकं|रूपकः
रूपक, अस्, आ, अम्, appearing in an assumed form<BR>(Ved.); illustrating by metaphor, describing by figu-<BR>rative language, figurative; (अस्), m. a particular coin,<BR>(probably) a rupee [cf. रूप्य]; (इका), f. swallow-<BR>wort, Asclepias Lactifera: (अम्), n. form, figure,<BR>shape, image (often at the end of a comp. in the<BR>sense of ‘having the form of,’ ‘composed of,’ ‘con-<BR>sisting in’); any manifestation or representation;<BR>feature, sign, symptom; kind, species; (in rhetoric)<BR>a metaphor, comparison, simile, the description of<BR>one object under the form of another which it is<BR>poetically supposed to resemble (especially a simile<BR>or comparison when इव, वत्, &c. are omitted: there<BR>are three or four varieties of the figure Rūpaka,<BR>e. g. the खण्ड-रूपक or ‘imperfect metaphor,’<BR>the अर्ध-रूपक or ‘partial metaphor,’ and the<BR>ललामक-रूपक or ‘flowery metaphor;’ and they<BR>differ from the Upamā or comparison chiefly in the<BR>omission of the particles denoting resemblance,<BR>such as इव, यथा, सह, or the Taddhita affix वत्;<BR>when this last is added the simile is called Taddhito-<BR>pamā); a drama, play, theatrical performance, (one<BR>of the two classes of dramatic composition divided<BR>into ten species including the Nāṭaka or principal<BR>play and the Prahasana or farce; see also प्र-क-<BR>रण, भाण, &c.; cf. उप-रूपक); a particular<BR>weight (= 3 Guñjās); = मूर्त (मूर्ति?); = धूर्त.<BR>—रूपक-ताल, अस्, m. a particular time in music.<BR>—रूपक-वाक्य, अम्, n. or रूपक-शब्द, अस्,<BR>m. a figurative expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपण|रूपणं
रूपण, अम्, n. figurative illustration, metaphorical<BR>description; examination, investigation, proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपयत्
रूपयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, figuring, describing, repre-<BR>senting, acting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपयित्वा
रूपयित्वा, ind. having represented or acted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपस्विन्
रूपस्विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. handsome, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपिक|रूपिकः
रूपिक, coined gold or silver, money.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपिणिका
रूपिणिका, f. (dimin. fr. रूपिणी), a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपित
रूपित, अस्, आ, अम्, formed, represented, exhibited,<BR>imagined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपिन्
रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having form or figure, possessed<BR>of body, formed, embodied, corporeal; having a<BR>beautiful form or figure, well-shaped, handsome,<BR>beautiful; having the form or appearance of, having<BR>the character of, characterized by, appearing as, like<BR>(at the end of a comp., e. g. काल-रूपिन्, ई, m. ‘having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">Page0852-c+ 76</a>]<BR>the form of Death,’ an epithet of Śiva; cf. देव-र्˚);<BR>(ई), m., N. of a son of Aja-mīḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्य|रूप्यं
रूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having a beautiful form or<BR>appearance, well-shaped, handsome, beautiful; bear-<BR>ing a stamp, stamped, impressed; to be denoted<BR>figuratively or metaphorically; formerly in the pos-<BR>session of or possessed by (as an affix or at the end<BR>of a comp., see Pāṇ. V. 3, 54, Vopa-deva VII. 67;<BR>cf. also Pāṇ. IV. 3, 81); (अस्), m. a proper N.; N.<BR>of a mountain; (अम्), n. silver; wrought silver,<BR>silver or gold bearing a stamp or impression, stamped<BR>coin; wrought gold.<BR>—रूप्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made or consisting of silver, containing silver.<BR>—रू-<BR>प्य-माक्षिक, अम्, n. silver Mākṣika, Hepatic<BR>pyrites of iron.<BR>—रूप्याचल (˚य-अच्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘silver-mountain,’ N. of the mountain Kailāsa.<BR>—रू-<BR>प्याध्यक्ष (˚य-अध्˚), अस्, m. a superintendent<BR>of silver or of silver coinage, master of the mint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्यक
रूप्यक in सुवर्ण-रूप्यक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूम
रूम रूम, N. of a place, (also read रूप.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूर
रूर रूर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hot, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूवुक|रूवुकः
रूवुक रूवुक, अस्, m. the castor-oil tree,<BR>Ricinus Communis; [cf. रुवुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूष्
रूष् रूष्, cl. 1. P. रूषति, &c., to<BR>adorn, decorate; to cover, smear [cf. rt.<BR>रूक्ष्, रूक्षित]; cl. 10. P. रूषयति, &c., to<BR>tremble; to burst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूषक|रूषकः
रूषक, अस्, m. a plant, Gendarussa Vulgaris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूषण|रूषणं
रूषण, अम्, n. the act of adorning, decoration;<BR>covering, strewing, smearing, soiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूषित|रूषितं
रूषित, अस्, आ, अम् (sometimes confounded with<BR>रुषित, q. v.), adorned, decorated; perfumed; in-<BR>laid; covered (with dust &c.), strewed, overspread,<BR>soiled, besmeared, smeared [cf. rt. रूक्ष्, रूक्षित,<BR>रुधिर-र्˚]; made rough or rugged [cf. रूक्ष];<BR>pounded, (perhaps for रुषित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रे
रे रे, ind. a vocative particle (generally<BR>used contemptuously or to express disrespect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेउइ
रेउइ रेüइ, N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक्
रेक् रेक्, cl. 1. A. रेकते, रिरेके, रेकितुम्,<BR>to suspect, doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक|रेकः
1. रेक, अस्, m. suspicion, doubt, fear, care, anxiety,<BR>concern; a man of a low caste, outcast; a frog; [cf.<BR>भेक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक|रेकः
रेक 2. रेक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. रिच्), emptying,<BR>loosening, looseness, purging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेकु
रेकु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. empty, void, deserted,<BR>solitary, lonely, secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक्णस्
रेक्णस्, अस्, n., Ved. (in Uṇādi-s. IV. 198. the form<BR>given is रिक्णस्), any property left (by a deceased<BR>person), inherited possession, property, any valuable<BR>object or possession, gold, (by some written रेक्नस्.)<BR>—रेक्णस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of valu-<BR>able property, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेच
रेच, अस्, m. the emptying of the lungs (in the<BR>practice of Yoga), emission of breath; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>plant (= कम्पिल्लक); of another (= अङ्कोठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचक|रेचकं|रेचकः
रेचक, अस्, इका, अम्, emptying, purging, purga-<BR>tive, aperient, cathartic; emptying the lungs, emitting<BR>the breath; (अस्), m. the act of breathing out or exha-<BR>lation, expiration or emission of breath, (especially)<BR>expelling the breath out of one of the nostrils (in<BR>the practice of Yoga); a syringe; N. of various<BR>aperient medicines; the purging-nut plant, Croton<BR>Jamalgota; nitre, saltpetre; N. of a forester in the<BR>Vikramorvaśī; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (अम्),<BR>n. a purge, cathartic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचन|रेचनं
रेचन, अस्, ई, अम्, purging, purgative, cathartic,<BR>aperient; (ई), f., N. of various plants (= त्रि-वृत्,<BR>दन्ती, गुन्द्रा, रोचनिका, काम्पिल्ल, कालाञ्जनी);<BR>(अम्, आ), n. f. the act of emptying, making empty<BR>or void, lessening, diminishing; emitting the breath;<BR>purging, looseness; evacuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचनक|रेचनकः
रेचनक, अस्, m. = कम्पिल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचित
रेचित, अस्, आ, अम्, left void or empty, freed from,<BR>cleared; purged; (अम्), n., N. of one of a horse's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">Page0853-a+ 77</a>]<BR>paces, cantering [cf. rt. 1. रेज्]; a particular position<BR>of the hands in dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0852-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेच्य|रेच्यः
रेच्य, अस्, m. = रेच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेख
रेख रेख, अस्, m. (fr. रिख् = rt. लिख्), a<BR>line, &c. (= रेखा below); a proper N.; (आ). f. a<BR>line; a streak, stripe; a row, series [cf. लेखा];<BR>a continuous line; drawing; the first or prime me-<BR>ridian (considered to be a line drawn from Laṅkā<BR>to Meru, i. e. from Ceylon supposed to lie on the<BR>equator to the North-pole); = आभोग, fulness, satis-<BR>faction; = छद्मन्, deceit, fraud; a small quantity,<BR>little portion; [cf. probably Old Germ. riga.]<BR>—रे-<BR>खांश (˚खा-अं˚), अस्, m. a degree of longitude.<BR>—रेखाकार (˚खा-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, formed in<BR>lines, striped.<BR>—रेखा-गणित, अम्, n. ‘line-reckon-<BR>ing,’ geometry.<BR>—रेखान्तर (˚खा-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>geographical longitude, distance east or west from<BR>the first meridian, (see रेखा above.)<BR>—रेखा-न्यास,<BR>अस्, m. the marking down of lines or lineaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखक
रेखक in विन्दु-रेखक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखाय
रेखाय, Nom. A. रेखायते, &c., to praise,<BR>flatter; to vex, distress, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखायनि
रेखायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखिन्
रेखिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having lines (on the hand &c.),<BR>lined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेच
रेच रेच. See p. 852, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेज्
रेज् 1. रेज् [cf. rt. 1. राज्], cl. 1. A. रेजते<BR>(Ved. also P. रेजति), &c., to shine; to<BR>shake, tremble, quiver, flicker (Ved.); to cause to<BR>tremble or shake (Ved. P.); (according to Naigh. II.<BR>14) to go (P.): Caus. रेजयति, &c., to cause to<BR>tremble or quake, to shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेज्
2. रेज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, shining; shaking, a shaker; (ट्),<BR>m., N. of Agni or fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेजमान
रेजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. quaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेट्
रेट् रेट्, cl. 1. P. A. रेटति, -ते, रिरेट,<BR>रिरेटे, रेटितुम्, to speak; to ask, seek,<BR>request: Caus. रेटयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अरिरेटत्:<BR>Desid. रिरेटिषति, -ते: Intens. रेरेट्यते, रेरेट्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेड्
रेड् रेड् or रेऌ (a Vedic rt. probably con-<BR>nected with rt. 1. रिष्), to be angry, &c.,<BR>(according to Naigh. II. 12. रेऌअते = क्रुध्यति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणु|रेणुः
रेणु रेणु, उस्, m. (according to some also<BR>उस्, उ, f. n.; according to Uṇādi-s. III. 38. fr. rt.<BR>1. री), dust, a grain or atom of dust, sand, &c.; the<BR>pollen of a flower; N. of a particular medicinal drug<BR>(= रेणुका, पर्पट); N. of the author of the<BR>hymns Ṛg-veda IX. 70, X. 89, (his patronymic is<BR>Vaiśvāmitra); of a son of Vikukṣi; (उस्), f., N. of<BR>a wife of Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—रेणु-ककाट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. furrowing through or tossing up the dust; (Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda VI. 28, 4 = रजस उद्भेदकः.)<BR>—रेणु-कारिका, f., N. of a Kārikā.<BR>—रेणु-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, m. ‘sand-vessel,’ (probably) a kind of hour glass<BR>(used for astronomical purposes).<BR>—रेणु-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the state or condition of dust, the being dust, dustiness.<BR>—रेणु-दीक्षित, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—रेणु-<BR>प, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—रेणु-पदवी, f.<BR>a path of dust.<BR>—रेणु-पालक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—रेणु-मत्, आन्, m., N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra<BR>by Reṇu.<BR>—रेणु-रूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with<BR>dust, dusty; (अस्), m. an ass.<BR>—रेणु-वास, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dwelling in dust, covered with the pollen of<BR>flowers; (अस्), m. a bee.<BR>—रेणु-शस्, ind. to dust,<BR>into dust, (रेणुशः कृ, to make into dust, turn to<BR>dust.)<BR>—रेणु-सार or रेणु-सारक, अस्, m. ‘essence<BR>of dust, ‘camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुक|रेणुकः
रेणुक, अस्, m., N. of a Yakṣa; of a mythical<BR>elephant; of a particular formula recited over weapons;<BR>(आ), f. a particular drug or medicinal substance (said<BR>to be fragrant, but bitter and slightly pungent in<BR>taste, and of a greyish colour; it is procured in grains<BR>about the size of pepper-corns); a sort of pulse; N.<BR>of the wife of Jamad-agni and mother of Paraśu-<BR>rāma, (she was the daughter of Reṇu and of king<BR>Prasena-jit); N. of a Kārikā composed by Hari-hara.<BR>—रेणुकाचार्य (˚क-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">Page0853-b+ 72</a>]<BR>—रेणुका-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of Reṇukā,’ i. e. Pa-<BR>raśu-rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत|रेतं|रेतः
रेत रेत, रेतः-कुल्या, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतस्
रेतस् रेतस्, अस्, n. (fr. rt. 1. री), a flow, flood,<BR>stream, current, flow of water or rain (Ved.); flow of<BR>semen, seminal fluid, semen, sperm, virile energy;<BR>seed, offspring, progeny, posterity, descendants (Ved.);<BR>quicksilver (regarded as ‘Śiva's semen’); sin, (Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda IV. 3, 7 = पाप.)<BR>—रेतः-कुल्या, f.<BR>a stream or river of semen virile (in a particular hell).<BR>—रेतः-सिच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. discharging semen; an<BR>epithet of particular Iṣṭakās.<BR>—रेतः-सिच्य, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. discharge of semen.<BR>—रेतस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. possessed of seed, abounding in seed, impregnat-<BR>ing, prolific, productive; (आन्), m. epithet of Agni.<BR>—रेतस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. abounding in seed, pro-<BR>lific, productive.<BR>—रेतो-धा, आस्, f., Ved. the act of<BR>impregnating, impregnation; (आस्, आस्, अम्), impreg-<BR>nating, fertilizing; (आस्), m. a father.<BR>—रेतो-धेय,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. impregnation.<BR>—रेतो-मार्ग, अस्, m.<BR>the seminal duct or canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत|रेतं|रेतः
रेत = रेतस्, semen virile.<BR>—रेत-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>born or produced from seed; any beloved offspring<BR>or child; (आ), f. sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतन|रेतनं
रेतन, अम्, n. semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतस
रेतस at the end of a comp. = रेतस्; [cf. अग्नि-<BR>र्˚, कपोत-र्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतस्य
रेतस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. conveying seed, (the first<BR>verse of the Bahiṣpavamāna Stotra is so called.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतिन्
रेतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. abounding in seed; impreg-<BR>nating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत्य|रेत्यं
रेत्य, अम्, n. = रीति, bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत्र|रेत्रं
रेत्र, अम्, n. semen virile; quicksilver; nectar,<BR>ambrosia; perfumed or aromatic powder; (these<BR>meanings are sometimes given to वेत्र, which is<BR>confounded with रेत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेधक
रेधक रेधक, अस्, m. a proper N., (also<BR>read रेचक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप्
रेप् रेप्, cl. 1. A. रेपते, &c., to go,<BR>move; to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप|रेपः
रेप रेप, रेपस्. See p. 846, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफ|रेफः
रेफ रेफ, रेफस्, रेफिन्. See p. 846,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेब्
रेब् रेब् = rt. रेव्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभ्
रेभ् रेभ्. See rt. रिभ्, p. 846, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेमि
रेमि रेमि, a Vedic adjective fr. rt. रम्,<BR>see Pāṇ. III. 2, 171, Vārtt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेरिवन्
रेरिवन् रेरिवन्, आ, m., Ved. = प्रेरयितृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेरिह
रेरिह रेरिह, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens. of rt.<BR>रिह्, q. v.), Ved. continually or repeatedly licking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेरिहत्
रेरिहत्, अत्, अती, अत्, Ved. excessively licking, lick-<BR>ing up, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेरिहाण|रेरिहाणः
रेरिहाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. repeatedly licking or<BR>caressing; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva; a thief; an Asura;<BR>= अम्बर; = वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेव्
रेव् रेव् or रेब्, cl. 1. A. रेवते, रेबते,<BR>&c., to go, move, flow; to leap, jump, go<BR>by leaps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेव
रेव, अस्, m., N. of a son of Ānarta and father of<BR>Raivata; (आ), f., N. of the Narma-dā river (which<BR>rises in one of the Vindhya mountains called Āmra-<BR>kūṭa or more commonly Amarakantak in the province<BR>of Gondwana, and after a westerly course of about<BR>800 miles falls into the sea below Broach); the<BR>indigo plant; N. of Rati (the wife of Kāma-deva);<BR>(अम्), n., N. of various Sāmans.<BR>—रेवोत्तरस् (˚वा-<BR>उत्˚), आस्, m., Ved. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवट|रेवटं|रेवटः
रेवट, अस्, m. a boar; a bamboo cane; a whirl-<BR>wind; a kind of poison; oil of the Morunga tree;<BR>the fruit of the plantain; (अम्), n. a muscle or conch-<BR>shell with its windings or spiral lines going from<BR>right to left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवण
रेवण, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवत्|रेवन्त्
रेवत् रे-वत्, रे-वती. See below and p. 854.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवत|रेवतः
रेवत रेवत, अस्, m. the citron tree; Ca-<BR>thartocarpus Fistula; N. of various persons; of a son<BR>of Andhaka or of Ānarta; of the father of Revatī<BR>and father-in-law of Bala-rāma; of a Varṣa (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवतक|रेवतकं
रेवतक, अस्, m. a proper N.; (अम्), n. a species<BR>of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवति|रेवतिः
रेवति, इस्, f., N. of Rati (wife of Kāma-deva);<BR>= रे-वती, the wife of Bala-rāma.<BR>—रेवति-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. (रेवति for रेवती), the son of Revatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेशयदारिन्
रेशयदारिन् रेशय-दारिन् (रेशय = हिंसत्),<BR>Ved. destroying those who injure, (used in Nirukta<BR>VI. 14. to explain रिशादस्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेशी
रेशी रेशी, f., Ved. epithet of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्
रेष् 1. रेष्, cl. 1. A. रेषते, रिरेषे, रे-<BR>षितुम्, to howl, roar, yell (as wolves); to<BR>neigh, whinny (as a horse; cf. rt. ह्रेष्); to utter<BR>any inarticulate sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्
2. रेष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, one who howls or neighs, howling,<BR>neighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषण|रेषणं
1. रेषण, अम्, n. the howl of a wolf, howling,<BR>yelling, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषा
रेषा, f. howling, yelling (of wolves); neighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषित
रेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, yelled, sounded; (अम्), n.<BR>neighing, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्
रेष् 3. रेष्, ट् (fr. rt. 1. रिष्), in Vājasa-<BR>neyi-s. VI. 18. according to Mahī-dhara = रिष्टा or<BR>हिंसिता, (perhaps referrible to rt. रिश्, to injure.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष
रेष, अस्, m., Ved. injury, hurt, receiving injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषण|रेषणं
2. रेषण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. injuring, hurting;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of injuring, injury, hurt, damage;<BR>failure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषिन्
रेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, injuring, hurting; [cf. पुरु-<BR>ष-र्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्टृ
रेष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, one who injures or hurts,<BR>an injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्मन्
रेष्मन्, आ, m., Ved. a storm, whirlwind, storm-<BR>cloud, (according to Mahī-dhara) the dissolution or<BR>destruction of the world.<BR>—रेष्म-च्छिन्न or<BR>रेष्म-मथित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rent or broken<BR>by a storm, torn up by a tempest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्म्य
रेष्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in or exposed to<BR>a storm, involved in destruction (at the dissolution<BR>of the world).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेहत्
रेहत् रेहत्, see Gaṇa Bhṛśādi to Pāṇ. III.<BR>1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेहाय
रेहाय, Nom. A. रेहायते, &c., see Gaṇa Bhṛ-<BR>śādi to Pāṇ. III. 1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै 1. रै, cl. 1. P. रायति, ररौ, रातुम्, to<BR>bark, bark at (with acc.); to sound; [cf. Lat.<BR>latrare.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
2. रै, आस् (?) , m. barking, sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै 3. रै, रास्, m. rarely f. (connected with<BR>रयि, q. v., fr. rt. 1. रा; acc. रायम्, Ved. राम् =<BR>Lat. rem; for other cases see Gram. 132), property,<BR>possessions, goods, wealth, gold; costliness; (रै),<BR>ind., see Gaṇa Cādi to Pāṇ. I. 4. 57; [cf. Lat. res.]<BR>—रायस्-काम, अस्, आ, अम् (रायस्, gen. c.), Ved.<BR>desirous of property, anxious to become rich.<BR>—रा-<BR>यस्-पोष, अस्, m., Ved. increase of property or<BR>riches, the possession of wealth, increase of pros-<BR>perity; (अस्, आ, अम्), increasing riches (said of Kṛṣṇa).<BR>—रायस्-पोषक, अस्, इका, अम्, increasing riches.<BR>—रायस्-पोष-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, or रायस्पोष-<BR>दावन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. granting increase of wealth,<BR>bestowing increase of prosperity.<BR>—रायस्-पोष-<BR>वनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. procuring increase of riches<BR>(धन-पुष्टेः सम्पादयितृ).<BR>—रायो-वाज, अस्,<BR>m. (रायस्, gen. c.), Ved. a proper N.<BR>—रायो-<BR>वाजीय, अम्, n. (fr. the preceding), N. of a Sāman.<BR>—रै-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to transform<BR>into property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवत्|रेवन्त्
रे-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (रे contracted fr. रयि + वत्),<BR>having prosperity or wealth, rich, wealthy, opulent,<BR>prosperous; grand in external appearance, shining,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">Page0854-a+ 78</a>]<BR>glittering, beautiful, illustrious; (अत्), ind., Ved. ra-<BR>diantly, beautifully; (अती), f., N. of the fifth Nak-<BR>ṣatra, (see नक्षत्र; sometimes also अत्यस्, f.<BR>pl.); the day of Revatī; N. of the evil genius or<BR>goddess presiding over a particular sickness, (some-<BR>times identified with Durgā, sometimes with Aditi);<BR>N. of the wife of Mitra; of a daughter of the Lustre<BR>(कान्ति) of the Nakṣatra Revatī and mother of<BR>Manu Raivata; of the wife of Bala-rāma (daughter<BR>of Kakudmin); of a wife of Amṛtodana; (अत्यस्)<BR>f. pl. ‘the wealthy ones, the shining ones,’ epithet<BR>of cows (Ved.); waters, water, a quantity of water<BR>(Ved.); epithet of the verse Ṛg-veda I. 30, 13 (so<BR>called from रेवती being the first word; the Raivata<BR>Sāman is formed from this verse; according to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 3, 34, Vārtt. 1. रेवती = one born under the<BR>Nakṣatra Revatī); रेवद् याज्ञतुरम्, N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR>—रेवती-भव, अस्, m. ‘son of Revatī,’<BR>the planet Saturn.<BR>—रेवती-रमण, अस्, m. the<BR>husband of Revatī, i. e. Bala-rāma; N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—रेवतीश (˚ती-ईश), अस्, m. lord or husband of<BR>Revatī, i. e. Bala-rāma.<BR>—रेवती-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of Revatī,’ a N. of Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0853-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवत्य
रेवत्य (a Vedic adjective fr. रेवती, Pāṇ. IV. 4,<BR>122), illustrious, beautiful, &c. (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवन्त|रेवन्तः
रेवन्त, अस्, m., N. of a son of Sūrya and chief<BR>of the Guhyakas; the fifth Manu of the present<BR>Kalpa; [cf. रैवत.]<BR>—रेवन्त-मनु-सू, ऊस्, f.<BR>mother of Manu Revanta, epithet of Sañjñā (wife of<BR>Sūrya).<BR>—रेवन्तोत्तर (˚त-उत्˚), N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैक्व
रैक्व, अस्, m., Ved. a proper N.; [cf. रयिक्व.]<BR>—रैक्व-पर्ण, आस्, m. pl., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैय
रैय, Nom. P. रैयति, &c., to desire riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवत|रैवतः
रैवत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रे-वत्), coming or de-<BR>scended from a wealthy family, rich, opulent, wealthy;<BR>relating to Manu Raivata; belonging to or connected<BR>with the Raivata Sāman (said of Indra, Savitṛ;<BR>Ved.); (अस्), m. a cloud (Ved.); a kind of Soma;<BR>a sort of vegetable; N. of a demon presiding over<BR>a particular child's disease; N. of one of the eleven<BR>Rudras; of Śiva; of the fifth Manu; of a Daitya;<BR>of a Ṛṣi; of a Brahmarṣi; of a king; a patro-<BR>nymic of Kakudmin (the ruler of Ānarta; in this<BR>sense fr. रेवत); a metronymic of a son of Amṛ-<BR>todana by Revatī; N. of a mountain near Kuśa-<BR>sthalī, the capital of the country Ānarta; (ई), f. in<BR>Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 6236, according to the com-<BR>mentator = रैवत above; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—रैवत-मदनिका, f., N. of a Goṣṭhī drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवतक|रैवतकं|रैवतकः
रैवतक, see Gaṇa Arīhaṇādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2,<BR>80; (अस्), m., N. of a mountain (= रैवत); N.<BR>of a porter (in the Śakuntalā); (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>the inhabitants of the mountain Raivataka; (अम्),<BR>n. a species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवतिक|रैवतिकः
रैवतिक, अस्, m. a metronymic from Revatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवतिकीय
रैवतिकीय, adj. fr. रैवतिक (Pāṇ. IV. 3,<BR>131).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवत्य
रैवत्य, अम्, n. (fr. रेवत्), riches, wealth;<BR>रैवत्य ऋषभः, N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैख
रैख रैख, अस्, m. (fr. रेख), a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैणव
रैणव रैणव, अस्, m. (fr. रेणु), a patro-<BR>nymic; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैणुकेय
रैणुकेय, अस्, m. (fr. रेणुका), a metronymic<BR>of Paraśu-rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैतस
रैतस रैतस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रेतस्), Ved. be-<BR>longing to seed or semen, seminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैतिक
रैतिक रैतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रीति), of or<BR>belonging to brass, brazen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैत्य
रैत्य, अस्, &c., made of brass, brazen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैभ
रैभ रैभ, अस्, m. (fr. रेभ), a patronymic;<BR>(ई), f., Ved., scil. ऋच्, epithet of particular ritualistic<BR>verses; N. of the three verses, Atharva-veda XX.<BR>127, 4-6 (so called from the word रेभ occurring<BR>several times).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैभ्य
रैभ्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Rebha, N. of<BR>a son of Sumati and father of Dushyanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवत|रैवतः
रैवत रैवत. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैष्णायन
रैष्णायन रैष्णायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोक|रोकं|रोकः
रोक रोक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. रुच्), light,<BR>lustre, brightness, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI.<BR>66, 6 = दीप्ति, ‘light,’ or बाधक, ‘obstructing’);<BR>buying with ready money; (अम्), n. a hole, cavity; a<BR>boat, ship; moving, shaking; = कृपण-भेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोकस्
रोकस्, अस्, n., Ved. light or any phenomenon of<BR>light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोग|रोगः
रोग रोग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. रुज्), ‘breaking<BR>up of strength,’ infirmity, weakness, sickness, disease,<BR>malady, (क्षुद्-रोग, disease from hunger; क्षे-<BR>त्रिय-रोग, an incurable disease, see क्षेत्रिय);<BR>Disease regarded as an evil genius or demon; Costus<BR>Speciosus or Arabicus.<BR>—रोग-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>seized with sickness, sick, diseased.<BR>—रोग-घ्न,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, removing sickness, curative, remedial,<BR>medicinal; (अम्), n. medicine.<BR>—रोग-ज्ञान, अम्,<BR>n. knowledge of diseases.<BR>—रोग-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>giving or causing sickness.<BR>—रोग-नाशन, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, Ved. destroying sickness, removing disease.<BR>—रोग-निग्रहण, अम्, n. suppression of disease.<BR>—रोग-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, causing disease.<BR>—रोग-<BR>भय, अम्, n. fear of disease.<BR>—रोग-भाज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>possessing sickness, one who suffers from disease, ill,<BR>sick.<BR>—रोग-भू, ऊस्, f. the place or seat of sickness,<BR>the body.<BR>—रोग-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>sickness, recovered from illness.<BR>—रोग-मुरारि<BR>(˚र-अरि), इस्, m., N. of a work on medicine.<BR>—रोग-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘king of sicknesses,’ consumption.<BR>—रोग-लक्षण, अम्, n. the sign or symptoms<BR>of a disease.<BR>—रोग-शान्तक, अस्, m. a curer of<BR>disease, a physician.<BR>—रोग-शान्ति, इस्, f. cure or<BR>alleviation of disease.<BR>—रोग-शिला, f. realgar, red<BR>arsenic.<BR>—रोग-शिल्पिन्, ई, m. a species of plant (com-<BR>monly called Śaralu), Cassia Fistula.<BR>—रोग-श्रेष्-<BR>ठ, अस्, m. ‘the chief of sicknesses,’ fever.<BR>—रोग-<BR>ह, अम्, n. ‘destroying disease,’ a drug, medicament.<BR>—रोग-हन्, हा, m. ‘remover of disease,’ a phy-<BR>sician.<BR>—रोग-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, taking away disease,<BR>remedial, curative, medicinal; (अम्), n. medicine.<BR>—रोग-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking away disease, curing,<BR>curative; (ई), m. a physician.<BR>—रोग-हृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>curing disease; (त्), m. a physician.<BR>—रोगान्तक<BR>(˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, ‘disease-destroying,’ curative,<BR>medicinal; (अस्), m. a physician.<BR>—रोगान्वित (˚ग-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of sickness, sick, diseased.<BR>—रोगायतन (˚ग-आय्˚), अम्, n. the abode of<BR>disease, seat of malady, the body.<BR>—रोगार्त (˚ग-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, suffering from sickness or disease,<BR>afflicted with any disease.<BR>—रोगोन्मादित (˚ग-<BR>उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, maddened with disease, mad (said<BR>of a dog).<BR>—रोगोपशम (˚ग-उप्˚), अस्, m. cure or<BR>alleviation of disease.<BR>—रोगोल्बण-ता (˚ग-उल्˚), f.,<BR>Ved. the spreading or raging of diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगित
रोगित, अस्, आ, अम्, diseased, suffering from sick-<BR>ness; mad (said of a dog).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिन्
रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, sick, sickly, diseased, ill, (मन्द-<BR>रोगिन्, seldom ill.)<BR>—रोगि-तरु, उस्, m. ‘tree of<BR>the sick, ‘epithet of the Aśoka tree.<BR>—रोगि-ता, f.<BR>sickness, illness, a diseased state.<BR>—रोगि-वल्लभ,<BR>अम्, n. ‘friend of the sick,’ medicine, a drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिष्ठ
रोगिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of रोगिन्), one who<BR>is always sickly or ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोग्य|रोग्यं
रोग्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. रोग), related to or con-<BR>nected with disease, producing sickness, unwhole-<BR>some, unhealthy; (रोग्य may also be a fut. part.<BR>pass. fr. rt. 1. रुज्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोच
रोच रोच, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. रुच्), en-<BR>lightening, illuminating, one who lightens or makes<BR>bright; (अस्), m., N. of a king; [cf. गो-र्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचक|रोचकः
रोचक, अस्, आ, अम्, brightening, enlightening,<BR>&c. (= रोचन); giving an appetite, (अ-रोचक,<BR>taking away appetite, depriving of appetite); pleas-<BR>ing, agreeable; (अस्), m. hunger, appetite; a sto-<BR>machic, stimulant, any medicine, fruit, &c. supposed<BR>to strengthen the tone of the stomach and restore<BR>lost appetite; N. of various plants, the plantain; a<BR>kind of onion; a worker in glass or artificial orna-<BR>ments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचकिन्
रोचकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having desire or appetite;<BR>अ-रोचकिन्, free from desire or appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचन|रोचनः
रोचन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, enlightening, making<BR>bright, illuminating, irradiating, lightening, light,<BR>bright, splendid, beautiful; causing or exciting de-<BR>sire, giving pleasure or satisfaction, pleasing, agree-<BR>able, pleasant, charming, lovely; sharpening or giving<BR>an appetite, stomachic; (अस्), m. a stomachic; a<BR>variety of the cotton tree; = पलाण्डु, आरग्-बध,<BR>करञ्ज, अङ्कोठ, दाडिम; epithet of a demon<BR>presiding over a particular disease; N. of one of the<BR>five arrows of the god of love (‘exciter of pleasures’);<BR>N. of a son of Viṣṇu by Dakṣiṇā; N. of Indra<BR>under Manu Svārociṣa; of a mountain; (आ), f. the<BR>bright sky, firmament, (see रोचनम् below); a<BR>handsome woman; a particular yellow pigment (com-<BR>monly called गो-रोचना, q. v.); a red lotus-flower;<BR>dark Śālmali (= Marāṭhī kāḷī sāmvarī) = वंश-<BR>रोचना, bamboo manna or Tabāṣīr; N. of a wife<BR>of Vasu-deva; (ई), f., N. of various plants, Convol-<BR>vulus Turpethum; = काम्पिल्ल; = दन्ति; = आम-<BR>लकी; red arsenic, realgar; a particular yellow pig-<BR>ment, = रोचना; (अम्), n. light, brightness (Ved.),<BR>the bright sky, firmament, luminous sphere (of which<BR>there are said to be three, see Ṛg-veda I. 102, 8;<BR>in this sense sometimes आ, f.); a luminary (Ved.);<BR>the raising a desire for; देवानां रोचनम्, N. of<BR>a Sāman.<BR>—रोचन-फल, अस्, m. the citron tree;<BR>(आ), f. a species of cucumber.<BR>—रोचन-स्था, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, Ved. abiding in light, dwelling in the firma-<BR>ment.<BR>—रोचना-कृ, see Gaṇa Sākṣādādi to Pāṇ.<BR>I. 4, 74.<BR>—रोचना-मुख, अस्, m., N. of a Daitya.<BR>—रोचना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing light,<BR>shining, light, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचनक|रोचनकः
रोचनक, अस्, m. the citron tree; (इका), f. a<BR>species of plant (= शुण्डा-रोचनी, काम्पिल्लिका); =<BR>वंश-रोचना, bamboo manna or Tabāṣīr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचमान|रोचमानः
रोचमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, glittering, bright,<BR>splendid, resplendent; pleasing, gratifying, charming,<BR>pleasant, agreeable, (अ-रोचमान, not agreeable,<BR>unpleasant); (अस्), m. a tuft or curl of hair on a<BR>horse's neck; N. of a king; of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending upon Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचस्
रोचस् in स्व-रोचस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचि|रोचिः
रोचि, light, a beam, ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिन्
रोचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, light, bright, (see मित-र्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिष
रोचिष, अस्, m. (fr. रोचिस्), N. of a son of Vibhā-<BR>vasu by Uṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिष्णु|रोचिष्णुः
रोचिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, shining, giving light, bright,<BR>splendid, brilliant, beautiful, gaily adorned, elegantly<BR>dressed, gay, blooming; giving an appetite.<BR>—रो-<BR>चिष्णु-मुख, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having a bright<BR>countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिस्
रोचिस्, इस्, n. light, splendor, brightness, brilliancy,<BR>flame.<BR>—रोचिष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing light,<BR>giving light; (आन्), m., N. of a son of Manu Svāro-<BR>cisha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोची
रोची, f. a pot-herb, Hingtsha Repens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोच्य|रोच्यं
रोच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be illuminated or enlight-<BR>ened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोट
रोट रोट in पूग-रोट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोटकव्रत
रोटक-व्रत, अम्, n. epithet of a particular reli-<BR>gious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोटिका
रोटिका, f. bread or a kind of bread, wheaten cakes<BR>toasted on an earthen or iron dish (= Hindūstānī<BR>रोटी); यव-रोटिका, barley bread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोटी
रोटी, f. bread, in फिरङ्ग-र्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोड्
रोड् रोड्, cl. 1. P. रोडति, &c., to be mad<BR>(= rt. लोड्); to despise, disrespect, (in this<BR>sense = rts. रौड्, रौट्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोड|रोडः
रोड रोड, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied, contented;<BR>(अस्), m. crushing, pounding (= क्षोद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोढृ
रोढृ रोढृ, ढा, ढ्री, ढृ (fr. rt. 1. रुह्),<BR>one who ascends or grows, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोणीक
रोणीक रोणीक, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोणीकीय
रोणीकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Roṇīka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोद|रोदः
रोद रोद, रोदन, &c. See p. 850, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0854-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदस्
रोदस् रोदस्, अस्, n. (fr. rt. 1. रुद्; in Ni-<BR>rukta VI. 1. रोदस् is connected with रोधस् as if<BR>fr. rt. 2. रुध्), the seat of the roaring winds, heaven;<BR>(असी), n. du. heaven and earth, the upper and lower<BR>world, (in Ṛg-veda IX. 22, 5. रोदसोः, gen. du. =<BR>द्यावा-पृथिव्योः.)<BR>—रोदः-कुहर, अम्, n. the<BR>canopy of heaven.<BR>—रोदस्-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. a word<BR>used in explaining the etymology of रोदसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदसी
रोदसी, f. heaven; N. of the wife of Rudra and<BR>mother of the Maruts; (Sāy. also) mother of the<BR>Maruts or lightning; (अस्यौ or असी), f. du. heaven<BR>and earth, the upper and lower world, (in Ṛg-veda I.<BR>33, 5. रोदस्योः, gen. du. = द्यावा-पृथिव्योः; the<BR>form रोदसी for nom. acc. du. is also referred to रोदस्<BR>above.)<BR>—रोदसि-प्रा, आस्, आस्, अम् (रोदसि for रो-<BR>दसी), Ved. filling heaven and earth (= द्यावा-<BR>पृथिव्योः पूरयितृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोद्धव्य
रोद्धव्य रोद्धव्य, रोद्धृ. See p. 850,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध|रोधः
रोध 1. रोध. See p. 850, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध|रोधः
रोध 2. रोध, रोधस्, रोधिन्, &c. See<BR>p. 850, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध्र|रोध्रं|रोध्रः
रोध्र रोध्र, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rt. 1. रुध् and रुधिर), the tree Symplocos<BR>Racemosa (having yellow leaves; the red powder<BR>thrown over persons during the Holī festival is pre-<BR>pared from the bark of this tree); (अम्), n. sin, (in<BR>this sense also अस्, m.); offence, injury, (in these<BR>two senses probably connected with rt. 2. रुध्.)<BR>—रोध्र-पुष्प, अस्, m. Bassia Latifolia; a species<BR>of ringed snake.<BR>—रोध्र-पुष्पक, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of grain (said to be a sort of शालि); a species<BR>of ringed snake.<BR>—रोध्र-पुष्पिणी, f. Grislea To-<BR>mentosa.<BR>—रोध्र-शूक, अस्, m. a kind of rice<BR>(the ears of which are similar in colour to the flowers<BR>of the Rodhra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप|रोपः
रोप 1. रोप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. रुप् = rt.<BR>1. लुप्), confusing, disturbing; (अम्), n. a fissure,<BR>chasm, hole, cavity, (in this sense possibly connected<BR>with rt. 1. रुह्, cf. रुहक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपण|रोपणं|रोपणः
1. रोपण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. causing bodily pain,<BR>causing racking or griping pain; (अम्), n. according<BR>to the commentator on Taittirīya-Brāhmaṇa III.<BR>476, 9 = विमोहन or उपद्रव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपि
रोपि, इस्, f., Ved. acute or racking pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपित
1. रोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, bewildered, perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपुषी
रोपुषी, f., Ved., according to some = रोपि; ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 191, 13. ‘destroying,’<BR>रोपुषीणाम् = लोपयित्रीणाम् = छेत्त्रीणाम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप|रोपः
रोप 2. रोप, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus. of rt.<BR>1. रुह्), the act of raising or setting up, &c. (=<BR>2. रोपण); the planting (of trees); an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपक|रोपकः
रोपक, अस्, m. a planter [cf. वृक्ष-र्˚]; a<BR>weight of metal or a coin ((1/70) of a Suvarṇa; cf.<BR>रूपक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपण|रोपणं|रोपणः
2. रोपण, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to grow, causing<BR>to grow over or cicatrize, healing; putting or placing<BR>on, (अम्), n. the act of setting up or erecting, raising;<BR>the act of planting, setting, &c.; healing, cicatrizing;<BR>a healing application (used for sores).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपणीय
रोपणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be set up or erected or<BR>raised; to be planted; useful for healing or cicatrizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपयितृ
रोपयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who sets up or erects,<BR>an erecter; a planter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपित
2. रोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to grow; raised,<BR>erected, elevated; set, planted, placed in or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपिन्
रोपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, raising, erecting, setting, planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप्य
रोप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be raised or erected; to be<BR>planted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपणाका
रोपणाका रोपणाका, f., Ved. a kind of<BR>bird, (Sāy.) a thrush (= शारिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोम|रोमं|रोमः
रोम 1. and 2. रोम, 1. and 2. रोमक, &c.<BR>See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्
रोमन् रोमन्, अ, n. (probably fr. rt. 1. रुह्;<BR>cf. लोमन्; according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 150. fr. rt.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-b" target="_blank">Page0855-b+ 81</a>]<BR>1. रु), the hair on the body of men and animals,<BR>(especially) short hair, bristles, wool, down, nap, &c.,<BR>(less properly applicable to the long hair on the head<BR>and beard of men, and to that on the mane and tail<BR>of animals); the feathers of a bird; (आणस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people; [cf. Hib. romach, ‘hairy;’ ro-<BR>machad, ‘hairiness;’ roinfaith, ‘hair-cloth;’ roin,<BR>roine, ‘hair, fur;’ roineach, ‘hairy.’]<BR>—रोम-<BR>कन्द, अस्, m. a kind of bulbous root or vegetable<BR>(= पिण्डालु).<BR>—रोम-कर्णक, अस्, m. ‘hair-eared,’<BR>a hare.<BR>—रोम-कूप, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘hair-hole,’ a<BR>pore of the skin; [cf. रोम-रन्ध्र.]<BR>—रोम-<BR>केसर, अम्, n. the tail of the Bos Grunniens<BR>used as a Chowri, a whisk; (also written रोम-<BR>केशर.)<BR>—रोम-गर्त, अस्, m. = रोम-कूप.<BR>—रोम-गुच्छ, अस्, m. or रोम-गुत्स, अम्,<BR>n. the tail of the Bos Grunniens used as a<BR>Chowri.<BR>—रोमण्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. = रो-<BR>म-वत्, covered with hair, hairy.<BR>—रोम-त्यज्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, Ved. losing the hair (said of a horse).<BR>—रोम-पाद, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—रोम-<BR>पुलक, अस्, m. the bristling of the hairs of the<BR>body, a thrill of joy or fear (= रोम-हर्ष).<BR>—रोम-फला, f. = रोमश-फल.<BR>—रोम-<BR>बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘hair-bound,’ made or fastened<BR>with the hair of animals, woven with hair.<BR>—रोम-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. hair-texture.<BR>—रोम-भूमि, इस्,<BR>f. the place of the hair, i. e. the skin.<BR>—रोम-<BR>मूर्धन्, आ, आ or ध्नी, अ, having short hairs on<BR>the head, covered with hair or down on the head<BR>(said of insects).<BR>—रोम-रतासार, अस्, m. the<BR>belly, (apparently a wrong form.)<BR>—रोम-रन्ध्र,<BR>अम्, n. a hole through which a hair shoots out, a<BR>pore of the skin.<BR>—रोम-राजि, इस्, or रोम-राजी, f.<BR>a row or line of hair, a streak of hair (on the abdo-<BR>men of men and especially of women just above the<BR>navel, said to be a sign of puberty).<BR>—रोम-राजि-<BR>पथ, अस्, m. the line of the hair above the navel,<BR>(in तनु-र्˚ = ‘the waist.’)<BR>—रोम-लता or रोम-<BR>लतिका, f. the winding line of hair above the navel<BR>(of women).<BR>—रोम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of<BR>hair, covered with hair, hairy, woolly.<BR>—रोम-वाहिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, cutting off hair, sharp enough to cut a hair.<BR>—रोम-विकार, अस्, m. or रोम-विक्रिया, f. change<BR>of the hair of the body, bristling or erection of the<BR>hair of the body, horripilation.<BR>—रोम-विध्वंस,<BR>अस्, m. ‘hair-destroying,’ a louse.<BR>—रोम-विवर,<BR>अम्, n. = रोम-कूप.<BR>—रोम-वेध, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR>—रोम-शुक, अम्, n. a kind of per-<BR>fume.<BR>—रोम-हर्ष, अस्, m. the bristling of the<BR>hair of the body, a thrill or shudder (caused by joy,<BR>fear, cold, &c.).<BR>—रोम-हर्षण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>causing the hair to bristle or stand erect, causing<BR>excessive joy, causing a shudder or horror, awe-<BR>inspiring, thrilling; (अस्), m. Terminalia Belerica<BR>(the nuts of which are used as dice); N. of Sūta<BR>(the pupil of Vyāsa and supposed narrator of the<BR>events in the Purāṇas); N. of the father of Sūta;<BR>(अम्), n. = रोम-हर्ष.<BR>—रोम-हर्षित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, thrilled with delight, having the hair of the<BR>body bristling or erect with joy or horror.<BR>—१. रो-<BR>माञ्च (˚म-अञ्˚), अस्, m. ‘curling or erection of<BR>the hair of the body,’ a thrill of rapture (= रोम-<BR>हर्ष); thrill of horror, horripilation.<BR>—२. रो-<BR>माञ्च (fr. the preceding), Nom. P. रोमाञ्चति,<BR>&c., to have the hair erect from excessive rapture,<BR>to feel a thrill of joy or horror.<BR>—रोमाञ्च-कञ्चुक,<BR>अस्, m. a coat of mail consisting (as it were) of the<BR>down of the body erect through delight.<BR>—रोमाञ्-<BR>चकिन्, ई, m., N. of a serpent-demon.<BR>—रोमाञ्चिका,<BR>f. a species of plant (= रुदन्ती).<BR>—रोमाञ्चित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the hair of the body erect or thrilled<BR>with joy or horror, enraptured.<BR>—रोमान्त (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. the hairy side, i. e. the upper side of<BR>the hand.<BR>—रोमाली (˚म-आली), f. a row or line of<BR>hair (above the navel; cf. रोम-राजि); = वयः-<BR>सन्धि, (probably) puberty.<BR>—रोमालु (˚म-आलु),<BR>उस्, m. a sort of vegetable (= पिण्डालु).<BR>—रोमालु-<BR>विटपिन्, ई, m. a species of plant (= कुम्भी).<BR>—रो-<BR>मावली (˚म-आव्˚), f. a row or line of hair (above<BR>the navel; cf. रोमाली).<BR>—रोमाश्रय-फला (˚म-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">Page0855-c+ 74</a>]<BR>आश्˚), f. a species of shrub.<BR>—रोमोद्गति (˚म-उद्˚),<BR>इस्, f. or रोमोद्गम (˚म-उद्˚) or रोमोद्भेद<BR>(˚म-उद्˚), अस्, m. erection of the hair (= रोम-<BR>हर्ष, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोम|रोमं|रोमः
1. रोम = रोमन् (at the end of an adj. comp., e. g.<BR>अ-रोम, having no hair, hairless; cf. स-र्˚); (अस्),<BR>m. a hole, cavity [cf. 1. रोप]; (अम्), n. water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमक|रोमकं|रोमकः
1. रोमक = रोमन् (at the end of an adj. comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमश|रोमशः
रोमश, अस्, आ, अम्, having thick hair, having<BR>thick wool or bristles, hairy, woolly; (अस्), m. a<BR>sheep, ram; a hog, boar; a sort of vegetable (=<BR>पिण्डालु, कुम्भी); N. of a Ṛṣi; of an astro-<BR>nomer [cf. 2. रोमक]; (आ), f. Cucumis Utilissi-<BR>mus; N. of the reputed authoress of Ṛg-veda 1.<BR>126, 7; (अम्), n. the pudenda (Ved.).<BR>—रोमश-<BR>फल, अस्, m. a species of plant (= टिण्डिश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोम|रोमं|रोमः
रोम 2. रोम, the city Rome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमक|रोमकं|रोमकः
2. रोमक, अस्, m. Rome; ‘the Roman’ as epi-<BR>thet of a particular astronomer; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people (mentioned in Mahā-bh. Sabhā-p. 1837;<BR>cf. रोमाणस् under रोमन्); the people of the<BR>Roman empire, the Romans; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>saline earth and the salt extracted from it; a kind<BR>of magnet.<BR>—रोमक-पत्तन, अम्, n. the city of<BR>Rome.<BR>—रोमक-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m., N. of one<BR>of the five chief Siddhāntas in the age of Varāha-<BR>mihira.<BR>—रोमकाचार्य (˚क-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>teacher of astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकायण
रोमकायण, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्थ|रोमंथः|रोमन्थः
रोमन्थ रोमन्थ, अस्, m. (according to<BR>some fr. रुज् + मन्थ), ruminating, chewing the<BR>cud, (गगण-रोमन्थ, अस्, m. ‘ruminating on<BR>the sky, ‘nonsense, absurdity); chewing; frequent<BR>repetition; [cf. Gr. ἐρεύγομαι, ἐρυγγάνω,<BR>ὀρυγγἀνω; Lat. rūmen (for rug-men), ruminare,<BR>ructare; Old Germ. ita-ruchjan; Angl. Sax. roc-<BR>cettan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्थाय
रोमन्थाय, Nom. A. रोमन्थायते, &c., to<BR>ruminate, chew the cud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्थायमान
रोमन्थायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, ruminating, chew-<BR>ing the cud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाञ्च|रोमांच|रोमाञ्चः
रोमाञ्च 1. and 2. रोमाञ्च. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरवण
रोरवण रोरवण, रोरुवत्, रोरूय. See<BR>p. 847, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुक
रोरुक रोरुक, N. of a country or of a<BR>town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुदा
रोरुदा रोरुदा. See p. 850, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोल|रोलः
रोल रोल, अस्, m. Flacourtia Cataphracta;<BR>green ginger; (आ), f. a particular metre (= लोला).<BR>—रोल-देव, अस्, m., N. of a painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोलम्ब|रोलंबः|रोलम्बः
रोलम्ब रोलम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, distrustful,<BR>unbelieving (?); (अस्), m. a bee; dry or arid soil (?).<BR>—रोलम्ब-कदम्ब, अम्, n. a swarm of bees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोलिचन्द्रू
रोलिचन्द्रू रोलिचन्द्रू, ऊस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोशंसा
रोशंसा रोशंसा (?), f. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष्
रोष् रोष्, रोष, &c. See p. 851, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोह|रोहः
रोह रोह, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. रुह्), rising,<BR>mounting upwards, ascending, springing up, growing<BR>[cf. रोह-शिखिन्]; riding on, (अश्व-रोह, riding<BR>on a horse); (अस्), m. rising, height, altitude; the<BR>raising or increasing of anything (as of a number<BR>from a smaller to a higher denomination); the<BR>growing, growth; a bud, blossom, shoot, sprout.<BR>—रोह-ग, अस्, m., N. of a mountain (= रोहण).<BR>—रोह-शिखिन्, ई, m. fire which mounts upwards,<BR>ascending flame.<BR>—रोह-सेन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहक|रोहकः
रोहक, अस्, &c. = रोढृ; riding on [cf. कटि-<BR>र्˚], a rider; growing on [cf. ग्राव-र्˚]; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of a kind of spirit or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहण|रोहणं|रोहणः
रोहण, अस्, m., N. of a mountain (Adam's peak<BR>in Ceylon); (ई), f. a medicine for healing or cica-<BR>trizing (a wound; Ved.); (अम्), n. a rising or<BR>ascending; a means of ascending (Ved.); the act of<BR>mounting up, riding on, sitting on, standing on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">Page0856-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(ज्या-रोहण, the putting or fastening on of a bow-<BR>string); the growing over, healing; the proceeding<BR>from, consisting of; semen virile.<BR>—रोहण-द्रुम,<BR>अस्, m. the sandal tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0855-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहत्
रोहत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, rising, mounting, ascending,<BR>growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहन्त|रोहंतः|रोहन्तः
रोहन्त, अस्, m. a particular tree; a tree in<BR>general; (ई), f. a particular creeper; a creeper in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहस्
रोहस्, अस्, n., Ved. height, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहाय
रोहाय (fr. रोहत् above), Nom. A. रोहायते,<BR>&c., see Gaṇa Bhṛśādi to Pāṇ. III. 1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहि|रोहिः
रोहि, इस्, m. a kind of deer; a seed; a tree; a pious<BR>or religious man, one observing a vow (= व्रतिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिण|रोहिणं|रोहिणः
रोहिण, अस्, आ, अम्, born under the asterism<BR>Rohiṇī; (अस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu; of a man; of<BR>various plants, = भू-तृण, वट, रोहितक; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the descendants of Rohiṇa; (अम्), n. epithet<BR>of the ninth Muhūrta (a part of the forenoon,<BR>extending to midday, in which Śrāddhas are espe-<BR>cially to be observed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणि|रोहिणिः
रोहिणि, इस्, f. = रोहिणी, the Nakṣatra.<BR>—रोहिणि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n., Ved. = रोहिणी-त्व.<BR>—रोहिणि-नन्दन,<BR>अस्, m. the son of Rohiṇī, i. e. Bala-rāma.<BR>—रोहिणि-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son of Rohiṇī,’ a proper N.<BR>—रो-<BR>हिणि-षेण or रोहिणि-सेन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणिका
रोहिणिका, f. a woman with a red face (either<BR>from anger or from being coloured with pigments);<BR>inflammation of the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणी
रोहिणी, f. (fem. of रोहित, col. 2; see also the fem.<BR>of रोहिन्, col. 2), a red cow, (in the Veda perhaps also)<BR>a red mare; a cow in general, (in Hindū mythology<BR>Rohiṇī is represented as a daughter of Surabhi and<BR>mother of cattle; she is also said to be the mother<BR>of Kāma-dhenu, the cow of plenty); N. of the<BR>ninth Nakṣatra or lunar asterism (personified as a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa, and the favourite wife of the<BR>Moon, called ‘the Red one,’ from the colour of the<BR>star Aldebaran or principal star in the constellation;<BR>the Nakṣatra contains five stars, probably α, β, γ, δ, ε,<BR>Tauri, and according to Hindū notions is figured by<BR>a wheeled carriage or sometimes by a temple or a<BR>fish); N. of the lunar day belonging to the above<BR>Nakṣatra; lightning; a young girl, one in whom<BR>menstruation has just commenced, a girl nine years<BR>of age; inflammation of the throat (of various kinds);<BR>N. of various plants, a kind of vegetable (= कटु-<BR>रोहिणी, सोम-वल्क, काश्मरी, हरीतकी, मञ्जिष्-<BR>ठा); N. of a wife of Vasu-deva and mother of<BR>Bala-rāma; of a wife of Kṛṣṇa; of the wife of<BR>Mahā-deva; of a daughter of Hiraṇya-kaśipu; of<BR>one of the sixteen Vidyā-devīs; (according to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 4, 34, Vārtt. 1, there is an adj. रोहिणी, meaning<BR>‘born under the Nakṣatra Rohiṇī.’)<BR>—रोहिणी-<BR>कान्त, अस्, m. ‘the lover of Rohiṇī,’ epithet of the<BR>Moon.<BR>—रोहिणी-चन्द्र-व्रत and रोहिणी-चन्द्र-<BR>शयन, अम्, n., N. of two religious observances.<BR>—रोहिणी-तनय, अस्, m. the son of Rohiṇī, i. e.<BR>Bala-rāma.<BR>—रोहिणी-तपस्, N. of a work.<BR>—रो-<BR>हिणी-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—रोहिणी-त्व,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. the state or condition of the Nakṣatra<BR>Rohiṇī.<BR>—रोहिणी-पति, इस्, m. the husband of Ro-<BR>hiṇī, i. e. the Moon.<BR>—रोहिणी-प्रिय, अस्, m. the<BR>lover of Rohiṇī, i. e. the Moon.<BR>—रोहिणी-भव,<BR>अस्, m. the son of Rohiṇī, i. e. the planet Mercury.<BR>—रोहिणी-योग, अस्, m. the conjunction of the moon<BR>with the Nakṣatra Rohiṇī.<BR>—रोहिणी-रमण, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the lover of the cow,’ a bull; the lover or<BR>husband of Rohiṇī, i. e. the Moon.<BR>—रोहिणी-वल्-<BR>लभ, अस्, m. the lover of Rohiṇī, i. e. the Moon.<BR>—रोहिणी-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular reli-<BR>gious observance.<BR>—रोहिणीश (˚नी-ईश), अस्, m. the<BR>lord or husband of Rohiṇī, i. e. the Moon.<BR>—रोहिणी-<BR>शकट, अस्, अम्, m. n. an asterism, probably α, β,<BR>γ, δ, ε, Tauri.<BR>—रोहिणी-षेण, अस्, m. a proper N.;<BR>[cf. रोहिणि-षेण.]<BR>—रोहिणी-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of<BR>Rohiṇī, ‘the planet Mercury.<BR>—रोहिण्य्-अष्टमी, f.<BR>the eighth day in the dark half of the month Bhādra<BR>when the moon is in conjunction with the Nakṣatra<BR>Rohiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित्
रोहित्, त्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 99. fr. rt.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">Page0856-b+ 78</a>]<BR>1. रुह्), the sun; a species of fish, = रोहित; (त्),<BR>f. a red mare (Ved.); the female of a deer, doe; a<BR>sort of creeper; (तस्), f. pl. epithet of rivers (ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. I. 13); the fingers (according to<BR>Naigh. II. 5); (त्, त्, त्), red, of a red colour.<BR>—रो-<BR>हिद्-अश्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having red mares (said<BR>of Agni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित|रोहितं|रोहितः
रोहित, अस्, आ or (more commonly) रोहिणी, अम्<BR>[cf. लोहित], red, of a red colour [cf. रुधिर];<BR>coloured; (अस्), m. red (the colour), a red horse; a<BR>fox; a form of Fire or the Sun (Ved.); another deity<BR>in Atharva-veda XIII. 1; N. of the hymns of the<BR>above Veda in which the god Rohita is mentioned;<BR>a kind of deer; a species of fish, Cyprinus Ro-<BR>hita; a kind of tree, Andersonia Rohitaka; a sort of<BR>ornament made of precious stones; a particular form<BR>of rainbow, (see रोहितम् below); N. of a son of<BR>Hari-ścandra; of a Manu; of a son of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>of a son of Vapuṣ-mat (king of Śālmala); of a<BR>river; (आस्), m. pl. epithet of a class of Gandharvas;<BR>of a class of gods under the twelfth Manu; (इणी), f.,<BR>see col. 1; (अम्), n. a kind of rainbow appearing in<BR>a straight form, Indra's bow unbent and invisible to<BR>mortals; blood; saffron.<BR>—रोहित-कूल, N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—रोहित-कूलीय and रोहित-कूलीयाद्य and<BR>रोहित-कूलीयोत्तर, अम्, n., N. of Sāmans.<BR>—रो-<BR>हित-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—रोहित-<BR>गिरीय, आस्, m. pl. the inhabitants of the mountain<BR>Rohita-giri.<BR>—रोहित-पुर, अम्, n., N. of the town<BR>founded by Rohitaka the son of Hari-ścandra.<BR>—रो-<BR>हित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a red horse.<BR>—रोहित-वस्तु, N. of a place.<BR>—रोहिताक्ष (˚त-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, red-eyed, having red eyes.<BR>—रो-<BR>हिताञ्जि (˚त-अञ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. marked with red.<BR>—रोहिताश्व, अस्, आ, अम्, having red horses; (अस्),<BR>m. the god of fire, Agni; N. of a son of Hari-<BR>ścandra.<BR>—रोहितैत (˚त-एत), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>variegated with red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितक|रोहितकः
रोहितक, अस्, m., N. of a tree, Andersonia Ro-<BR>hitaka; N. of a river; of a Stūpa; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people; (इका), f. a woman whose face is stained<BR>with red pigments or red with rage.<BR>—रोहितका-<BR>रण्य (˚क-अर्˚), अम्, n. ‘Rohitaka-wood,’ N. of<BR>a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितायन
रोहितायन, अस्, m. a patronymic, (probably for<BR>रौहितायन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितेय|रोहितेयः
रोहितेय, अस्, m. Andersonia Rohitaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिन्
रोहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, rising, mounting upwards, grow-<BR>ing, increasing; grown, shot up, long, tall; (ई), m.,<BR>N. of various trees, Andersonia Rohitaka; the sacred<BR>fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa; the Indian fig-tree, Ficus<BR>Indica; (इणी), f., N. of various plants, [cf. रोहिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिष्
रोहिष्, ट्, f. = रोहित्, a doe; = रौहिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिष|रोहिषः
रोहिष, अस्, m. a kind of fragrant grass; a species<BR>of fish; a kind of deer.<BR>—रोहिष-तृण = भूति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिष्यै
रोहिष्यै, dat. of an unused form रोहिषी or<BR>रोहिषि, used as a Ved. inf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोही
रोही, f. = रोहित्, a doe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहीतक|रोहीतकः
रोहीतक, अस्, m. = रोहितक, Andersonia Rohi-<BR>taka; N. of a place or of a mountain, (according to<BR>some a stronghold on the borders of Multan is so<BR>called.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्म
रौक्म रौक्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रुक्म), golden,<BR>adorned with gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्मिणेय|रौक्मिणेयः
रौक्मिणेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Ruk-<BR>miṇī, epithet of Pradyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्षक
रौक्षक रौक्षक, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्षायण
रौक्षायण, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्ष्य|रौक्ष्यं
रौक्ष्य रौक्ष्य, अम्, n. (fr. रूक्ष), rough-<BR>ness, hardness, dryness, aridity, emaciation; rough-<BR>ness, harshness, cruelty, uncouthness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौचनिक
रौचनिक रौचनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रोचना),<BR>coloured with Rocanā, Rocanā-coloured, yellowish;<BR>(अम्), n. the tartar of the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौच्य|रौच्यः
रौच्य, अस्, m. (fr. रुच्य = बिल्व), a staff of<BR>Bilva wood; (according to some) an ascetic with<BR>a staff of Bilva wood, a patronymic of the thir-<BR>teenth Manu; of the ninth Manu, (in these senses<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">Page0856-c+ 76</a>]<BR>fr. रुचि); (अस्, &c.), of or belonging to the thirteenth<BR>Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौट्
रौट् रौट् or रौड् (see rt. रोड्), cl. 1. P.<BR>रौटति, रौडति, to despise, treat with<BR>disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौढीय
रौढीय रौढीय, आस्, m. pl. (probably fr.<BR>रूढि), N. of a grammatical school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्र|रौद्रं|रौद्रः
रौद्र रौद्र, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. रुद्र), of<BR>or belonging to Rudra or to the Rudras, &c., Rudra-<BR>like, violent, impetuous, wrathful, irascible, savage,<BR>wild, fearful, terrible, formidable; acute; addressed<BR>to Rudra (said of a hymn); called after Rudra (said<BR>of a river); bringing or betokening misfortune;<BR>(अम्), ind. fearfully, horribly; (अस्), m. a patronymic<BR>of a descendant of Rudra; a worshipper of Rudra;<BR>heat, warmth, ardor, passion, wrath, rage, (also अम्,<BR>n.); the cold season of the year, winter; N. of<BR>Yama; of the fifty-fourth year of the Jupiter cycle<BR>of sixty years; N. of a particular Ketu (Ved.); (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a class of evil spirits; N. of a people;<BR>(ई), f., N. of Gaurī; a species of plant (= रुद्र-<BR>जटा); N. of a commentary on the Siddhānta-muk-<BR>tāvalī by Rudra-bhaṭṭācārya; (अम्), n. formidable-<BR>ness, dreadfulness, fierceness, savageness; heat, warmth,<BR>solar heat, sunshine; wrath, rage; N. of the Nak-<BR>ṣatra Ārdrā when situated under Rudra; N. of<BR>a Liṅga; of a Sāman.<BR>—रौद्र-कर्मन्, अ, n. a<BR>terrible magic rite or one performed for some dread-<BR>ful purpose; (आ, आ, अ), doing dreadful acts, perform-<BR>ing horrors; (आ), m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—रौद्र-कर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, doing dreadful acts,<BR>performing fearful things.<BR>—रौद्र-ता, f. wild or<BR>savage state, fierceness, fearful condition, horribleness,<BR>formidableness, dreadfulness.<BR>—रौद्र-दर्शन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of dreadful appearance, formidable, ter-<BR>rific.<BR>—रौद्र-पाद, (apparently) N. of a Nak-<BR>ṣatra (= रौद्र = आर्द्रा).<BR>—रौद्र-मनस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, Ved. savage-minded, fierce.<BR>—रौद्राश्व<BR>(˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son or more distant<BR>descendant of Puru.<BR>—रौद्री-भाव, अस्, m. the<BR>character of Rudra or Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रक
रौद्रक = रुद्रेण कृतम्, see Gaṇa Kulālādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 3, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्राग्न
रौद्राग्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रुद्र + अग्नि), Ved.<BR>relating to Rudra and Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्राणी
रौद्राणी in रौद्राणी-स्तोत्र, probably for रु-<BR>द्राणी-स्तोत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रायण
रौद्रायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रि
रौद्रि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौध
रौध रौध, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Rodha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौधादिक
रौधादिक रौधादिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रु-<BR>धादि), belonging to the class of roots beginning<BR>with रुध्, i. e. the seventh class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौधिर
रौधिर रौधिर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रुधिर),<BR>bloody, consisting of blood, caused by blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौप्य|रौप्यं
रौप्य रौप्य, अस्, &c. (fr. रूप्य), made of<BR>silver, silver; like silver, silvery; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>place; (अम्), n. silver.<BR>—रौप्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of silver, made of silver, silver.<BR>—रौप्य-<BR>माषक, अस्, m. a Māṣaka weight of silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौप्यायण
रौप्यायण, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौप्यायणि
रौप्यायणि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Rūpya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौम|रौमं
रौम रौम, अस्, m. a proper N.; (अम्), n.<BR>a kind of salt (= रौमक below).<BR>—रौम-ल-<BR>वण, अम्, n. salt from the Rumā district, (see<BR>below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमक|रौमकं
रौमक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. रोमक), Roman,<BR>spoken by the inhabitants of the Roman empire;<BR>derived or coming from the astronomer Romaka;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of salt procured from a salt-lake near<BR>Sambhar in Ajmere, (in this sense fr. रुमा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमकीय
रौमकीय (fr. रोमक), see Gaṇa Kṛśāvādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमण्य
रौमण्य रौमण्य (fr. रोमन्), see Gaṇa<BR>Saṅkāśādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0856-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमशीय
रौमशीय (fr. रोमश), see Gaṇa Kṛśāśvādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमहर्षणक
रौमहर्षणक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. रोमहर्-<BR>षण), made or composed by Roma-harṣaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमायण
रौमायण (fr. रोमन्), see Gaṇa Pakṣādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौम्य
रौम्य रौम्य, आस्, m. pl., N. of particular<BR>evil spirits in the service of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौरव|रौरवः
रौरव रौरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रुरु), made<BR>of the hide of the deer called रुरु; fearful, dread-<BR>ful, terrible; unsteady, cheating, fraudulent, dishonest;<BR>(अस्), m. a savage; N. of one of the hells (Manu<BR>IV. 88); of the fifth Kalpa; (अम्), n. the fruit of<BR>the Ruru tree; N. of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौरवक
रौरवक = रुरुणा कृतम्, see Gaṇa Kulālādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 3, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौरुकिन्
रौरुकिन्, इनस्, m. pl. (fr. रुरुक), the school<BR>of Ruruka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौशर्मन्
रौशर्मन् रौशर्मन्, आ, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिक
रौहिक रौहिक = रुह इव, see Gaṇa<BR>Aṅgulyādi to Pāṇ. V. 3, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिण|रौहिणं|रौहिणः
रौहिण रौहिण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रोहिणी), born<BR>under the Nakṣatra Rohiṇī; (अस्), m. the sandal<BR>tree; the Indian fig-tree; N. of Agni; of a demon<BR>vanquished by Indra; a proper N. (according to<BR>Naigh. I. 10) = मेघ, a cloud; N. of a gramma-<BR>tical school; (अम्), n. sandal-wood; N. of the ninth<BR>Muhūrta of the day; इन्द्रस्य राजन-रौहिणे<BR>and धातू रौहिणम्, N. of particular Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिणक
रौहिणक, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिणायन
रौहिणायन, अस्, m. (fr. रोहिण), a patronymic<BR>of Priya-vrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिणि
रौहिणि, इस्, m. a patronymic; रौहिणेर् एकर्-<BR>षे राजनम्, N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिणेय|रौहिणेयं|रौहिणेयः
रौहिणेय, अस्, m. (fr. रोहिणी), a metronymic;<BR>a calf, (also ई, f.); N. of Bala-rāma; the planet<BR>Mercury; (अम्), n. an emerald.<BR>—रौहिणेश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ (˚ण-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिण्य
रौहिण्य, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहित
रौहित, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रोहित), coming from the<BR>animal or fish called रोहित; relating to Manu Ro-<BR>hita; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहितक
रौहितक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रोहितक), Ved. made<BR>from the wood of the Andersonia Rohitaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहित्यायनि
रौहित्यायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिदश्व
रौहिदश्व, अस्, m. (fr. रोहिद्-अश्व), a patro-<BR>nymic of Vasu-manas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिष्
रौहिष्, ट्, m. = रौहिष, a kind of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिष|रौहिषं|रौहिषः
रौहिष, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 48.<BR>fr. rt. 1. रुह्; cf. रोहित्, रोहित, रोहिष), a kind<BR>of deer; a species of fish, = रोहित; (ई), f. a doe of<BR>the Rauhiṣa species; a creeper (= लता); = दूर्वा;<BR>a sort of grass (= कत्-तृण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौही
रौही, f. the female of a particular kind of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहीतक
रौहीतक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. रोहीतक), coming<BR>from the Andersonia Rohitaka, made of Andersonia<BR>Rohitaka wood; coming from the district Rauhīta;<BR>(अस्), m. = रोहीतक, Andesonia Rohitaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहीतदेश
रौहीत-देश, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहेय
रौहेय (fr. रोह), see Gaṇa Sakhyādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल 1. ल, the twenty-eighth consonant of<BR>the Nāgarī alphabet, being the semivowel of the<BR>vowels ऌ, ॡ, and having the sound of the English<BR>ल्.<BR>—ल-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ल.<BR>—ल-<BR>कार-वाद, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल 2. ल, Pāṇini's general or technical term<BR>for all the tenses and moods or verbal terminations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल 3. ल, अस्, m., N. of Indra; cutting (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल 4. ल (for लघु), a short syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्
लक् लक् (= rt. रक्), cl. 10. P. लाकयति,<BR>&c., to taste; to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक|लकः
लक, अम्, n. the forehead; an ear or spike of<BR>wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकच|लकचः
लकच or (more generally) लकुच, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of bread-fruit tree, Artocarpus Lacucha (a tree<BR>containing a large quantity of sticky milky juice);<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकुट|लकुटः
लकुट लकुट, अस्, m. = लगुड, a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकुटिन्
लकुटिन्, ई, इनी, इ, carrying a club, armed with<BR>a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकुल
लकुल लकुल, लकुल्य, see Gaṇa Balādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकुलिन्
लकुलिन्, ई, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्कक
लक्कक लक्कक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्त
लक्त लक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, = रक्त, red; [cf.<BR>गूथ-लक्त.]<BR>—लक्त-कर्मन्, आ, m. a red variety<BR>of the Lodh tree (used in dyeing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्तक|लक्तकः
लक्तक, अस्, m. lac, the red dye (= अलक्तक);<BR>a dirty and tattered cloth, a rag, (in this sense =<BR>नक्तक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्वनचन्द्र
लक्वनचन्द्र लक्वन-चन्द्र, अस्, m. a pro-<BR>per N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्
लक्ष् लक्ष्, cl. 1. A. लक्षते, to per-<BR>ceive, apprehend, observe, see, view,<BR>contemplate; cl. 10. P. A. (more properly regarded<BR>as a Nom. fr. लक्ष below), लक्षयति, -ते, अल-<BR>लक्षत्, अललक्षत, लक्षयितुम्, to mark,<BR>sign, betoken, distinguish, denote, characterize, indi-<BR>cate; to define or describe accurately; to signify,<BR>express (especially indirectly); to aim at (a mark or<BR>object); to consider, regard, think, call, name; to<BR>observe, enquire into, examine; to notice (any par-<BR>ticular marks), apprehend, recognise, know; to re-<BR>mark, observe, perceive, see: Pass. लक्ष्यते, to be<BR>marked; to be aimed at; to be meant or intended;<BR>to be perceived or observed; to appear, seem: Caus.<BR>लक्षयति, &c., to cause to be seen or exhibited,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष|लक्षं
लक्ष, अम्, n. (according to some for original<BR>रक्त, fr. rt. रञ्ज्; according to others fr. rt. लग्,<BR>cf. लक्ष्मन्, लक्ष्मी), a mark, sign, token; a<BR>mark to aim or shoot at, target, butt, aim, object,<BR>prey, prize (= लक्ष्यम्; cf. लब्ध-ल्˚); appear-<BR>ance, show, pretence, disguise, fraud; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. a lac, one hundred thousand, (said to be also आ,<BR>f.)<BR>—लक्ष-ता, f. the condition of being a mark<BR>or aim.<BR>—लक्ष-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—लक्ष-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—लक्ष-<BR>शस्, ind. by hundreds of thousands, by lacs.<BR>—लक्-<BR>ष-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, pretending to be asleep,<BR>appearing asleep.<BR>—लक्ष-होम, अस्, m. ‘lac-<BR>oblation,’ N. of a particular offering to the planets.<BR>—लक्षाधीश (˚ष-अध्˚), अस्, m. a person<BR>possessed of a lac (or of a hundred thousand rupees).<BR>—लक्षान्त-पुरी (˚ष-अन्˚), f., N. of a town.<BR>—लक्षी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, &c.,<BR>to make a mark or object, to aim at, point at, look<BR>at.<BR>—लक्षी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made a mark, aimed<BR>at, directed towards.<BR>—लक्षीकृत-घ्राण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, looking at the nose, fixing the gaze on the tip<BR>of the nose.<BR>—लक्षी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c.,<BR>to become a mark or aim or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षक|लक्षकं
लक्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, marking or indicating<BR>(especially indirectly, i. e. not by name); hinting at,<BR>expressing elliptically or by metonymy; a proper N.;<BR>(अम्), n. a lac, one hundred thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षण|लक्षणं|लक्षणः
लक्षण, अम्, n. a mark, distinctive mark, sign,<BR>symbol, token, indication, characteristic (often at the<BR>end of comps., e. g. पुरुष-ल्˚, the mark or organ<BR>of virility; at the end of adj. comps. the fem. is in<BR>आ and rarely in ई); character, attribute, quality;<BR>stroke, line, spot; a lucky mark, favourable sign;<BR>a symptom or indication of disease; an accurate<BR>mark, accurate description, definition; settled rate,<BR>fixed tariff (Manu VIII. 406); a designation, appel-<BR>lation, name, (sometimes at the end of comps.,<BR>e. g. ऋग्-यजुः-साम-लक्षण, named Ṛg, Yajur,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">Page0857-c+ 81</a>]<BR>and Sāma); aiming at, aim, intention, scope, object,<BR>signification; form, kind; subject, head, term, pro-<BR>vince; effect, operation influence; cause, occasion;<BR>observation, sight, seeing; (अस्), m. the Indian<BR>crane, Ardea Sibirica; a proper N.; = लक्ष्मण,<BR>the brother of Rāma; (आ), f. aim, object, view; an<BR>indirect indication or hint, elliptical mode of expres-<BR>sion, ellipsis, a word or phrase understood though<BR>not expressed, metonymy; indirect application of a<BR>word (as distinguished from its literal meaning); =<BR>लक्ष्मणा, the female of the Ardea Sibirica; a<BR>goose; N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—लक्षण-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, sign-knowing, understanding marks (especially<BR>those on the body), able to interpret or explain<BR>them.<BR>—लक्षण-त्व, अम्, n. the being a mark<BR>or definition.<BR>—लक्षण-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>deprived of good marks, fallen into misfortune, un-<BR>lucky.<BR>—लक्षण-लक्षणा, f., N. of a particular<BR>mode of expression by ellipsis or by metonymy.<BR>—लक्षण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing marks or<BR>signs, marked, distinguished, characterized, (त्रिंशल्-<BR>लक्षण-वत्, having thirty marks or character-<BR>istics.)<BR>—लक्षण-वाद-रहस्य, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a short philosophical treatise.<BR>—लक्षण-सङ्ग्र-<BR>ह, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—लक्षण-सन्निपात,<BR>अस्, m. the impressing or fixing of a mark, branding,<BR>stigmatizing.<BR>—लक्षण-समुच्चय, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—लक्षणान्वित (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>endowed with good marks, lucky.<BR>—लक्षणोरु<BR>(˚ण-ऊरु), उस्, ऊस्, उ, having good marks on the<BR>thighs? (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 70).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षणक
लक्षणक, अस्, इका, अम्, having marks or tokens<BR>&c. (at the end of an adj. comp. = लक्षण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षणिन्
लक्षणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing marks, &c.; =<BR>लक्षण-ज्ञ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षणीय
लक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be perceived or re-<BR>garded as, perceptible, to be expressed by ellipsis,<BR>expressible by metonymy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षण्य|लक्षण्यः
लक्षण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. लक्षण), serving as<BR>a mark or token, having good marks or signs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षयत्
लक्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, marking, observing,<BR>perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षयित्वा
लक्षयित्वा, ind. having perceived or observed,<BR>having noticed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षित|लक्षितः
लक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, marked, denoted, character-<BR>ized; characterized or recognisable by; defined;<BR>expressed (indirectly), hinted at; aimed at; re-<BR>marked, observed, perceived, discerned, discovered,<BR>beheld, seen, evident; considered, regarded; enquired<BR>into, examined.<BR>—लक्षित-त्व, अम्, n. the state of<BR>being marked or expressed indirectly.<BR>—लक्षित-<BR>लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having the marks (of any-<BR>thing) perceived or evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षितव्य
लक्षितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be marked or defined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षिन्
लक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having good marks or signs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्म
लक्ष्म = लक्ष्मन् at the end of an adj. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मक
लक्ष्मक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मण|लक्ष्मणं|लक्ष्मणः
लक्ष्मण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. लक्ष्मन्), having<BR>marks or signs, furnished with tokens or character-<BR>istics; possessed of lucky signs or marks, lucky,<BR>fortunate, prosperous, thriving; (अस्), m. the Indian<BR>crane, Ardea Sibirica; N. of a Vāsiṣṭha; of a son of<BR>Daśa-ratha by his wife Su-mitrā, (he was younger<BR>brother and companion of Rāma during his travels<BR>and adventures; Lakṣmaṇa and Śatru-ghna were<BR>both sons of Su-mitrā, but Lakṣmaṇa alone is usually<BR>called Saumitri; he so attached himself to Rāma as<BR>to be called Rāma's second self; whereas Śatru-<BR>ghna attached himself to Bharata); N. of various<BR>other persons; (आ), f. the female of the Ardea<BR>Sibirica; a goose; N. of various plants (= ओषधि,<BR>पृश्नि-पर्णी, पुत्र-कन्दा, श्वेत-कण्टकारी);<BR>N. of a wife of Kṛṣṇa; of a daughter of Duryo-<BR>dhana (carried off by Śāmba, son of Kṛṣṇa); of<BR>an Apsaras; of the mother of the eighth Arhat of<BR>the present Avasarpiṇī; (अम्), n. = लक्षण, a<BR>mark, sign, token, spot; a name.<BR>—लक्ष्मण-<BR>कवच, अम्, n., N. of a hymn in praise of Lakṣ-<BR>maṇa.<BR>—लक्ष्मण-कुण्डक, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—लक्ष्मण-खण्ड-प्रशस्ति, इस्, f., N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—लक्ष्मण-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-a" target="_blank">Page0858-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—लक्ष्मण-देव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—लक्ष्-<BR>मण-प्रसू, ऊस्, f. the mother of Lakṣmaṇa,<BR>i. e. Su-mitrā, one of three wives of Daśa-ratha,<BR>(she was also the mother of Śatru-ghna.)<BR>—लक्ष्-<BR>मण-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Gīta-govinda-ṭīkā.<BR>—लक्ष्मण-राज-देव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—लक्ष्मण-सेन, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—लक्ष्मण-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a statue of<BR>Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—लक्ष्मणा-कन्द = पुत्र-कन्दा.<BR>—लक्ष्मणाचार्य (˚ण-आच्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—लक्ष्मणानुचर (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—लक्ष्मणोरु (˚ण-ऊरु),<BR>उस्, ऊस्, उ, see लक्षणोरु (Vopa-deva IV. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मण्य
लक्ष्मण्य, अस्, m. a proper N., (according to<BR>Sāy.) a son of Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मन्
लक्ष्मन्, अ, n. (according to some fr. rt. लग्),<BR>a mark, spot, sign, token, characteristic; definition;<BR>= प्रधान, the chief, principal, most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मि
लक्ष्मि = लक्ष्मी, (shortened on account of<BR>the metre.)<BR>—लक्ष्मि-वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, in-<BR>creasing good fortune.<BR>—लक्ष्मि-सम्पन्न, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, possessed of good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मी
लक्ष्मी, ईस् (rarely ई), f. (according to some fr.<BR>rt. लग्; according to others connected with rt. लञ्ज्,<BR>to shine), a mark, sign, indication, token (Ved.;<BR>sometimes even ‘a bad sign’ in Ved., but in this<BR>sense usually with पापी); a good sign, (in Ved.<BR>usually with पुण्या); good fortune, good luck, for-<BR>tune, prosperity, wealth, success, happiness; beauty,<BR>grace, loveliness, charm, splendor; N. of the god-<BR>dess of fortune and beauty, (frequently in the later<BR>mythology identified with Śrī and regarded as the<BR>wife of Viṣṇu or Nārāyaṇa; according to the legend<BR>narrated in Rāmāyaṇa I. 45, 40-43, she sprang<BR>with other precious things from the froth of the<BR>ocean when churned by the gods and demons for<BR>the recovery of the Amṛta [see मन्दर]; she<BR>appeared with a lotus in her hand, whence she is<BR>also called Padmā; she is, moreover, connected in<BR>other ways with the lotus, and according to another<BR>legend is said to have appeared at the creation<BR>floating over the water on the expanded petals of a<BR>lotus-flower; Lakṣmī is also variously regarded as<BR>a wife of Sūrya, as a wife of Prajā-pati, as a wife of<BR>Dharma and mother of Kāma, as sister [or mother]<BR>of Dhātṛ and Vidhātṛ, as wife of Dattātreya); the<BR>Good Genius or Fortune of a king personified; royal<BR>power, dominion; superhuman power; N. of Dāk-<BR>ṣāyaṇī in Bharatāśrama; of Sītā the wife of Rāma,<BR>and of other women; the wife of a hero; N. of tur-<BR>meric and various other auspicious plants (= ऋद्धि,<BR>वृद्धि, प्रियङ्गु, फलिनी, स्थल-पद्मिनी,<BR>शमी); N. of the eleventh Kalā of the moon; of<BR>a metre, four times ¯¯˘¯˘˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯; of<BR>another, four times ¯¯¯˘˘¯¯¯˘¯˘˘¯¯; =<BR>द्रव्य; = मुक्ता, a pearl; [cf. Lith. Laime, ‘the<BR>goddess of happiness.’]<BR>—लक्ष्मी-कान्त, अस्, m.<BR>‘the beloved of Lakṣmī,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; कल्-<BR>लालेशो लक्ष्मी-कान्तः, N. of a deity.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-<BR>कुल-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-<BR>कुलार्णव (˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-गृह, अम्, n. ‘abode of Lakṣmī,’<BR>epithet of the red lotus-flower.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-चरित्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-जनार्दन, अम्,<BR>n. Lakṣmī and Janārdana.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-ताल, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of palm (= श्री-ताल); epithet of a particular<BR>time in music.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-त्व, अम्, n. the being<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-दास, अस्, m., N. of a com-<BR>mentator on Bhāskara's astronomy.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-<BR>देवी, f., N. of the authoress of a commentary on<BR>the Mitākṣarā-vyākhyāna.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-धर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a poet; of various other persons; (probably<BR>अम्), n. a particular metre, four times ¯˘¯¯˘<BR>¯¯˘¯¯˘¯.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>Lakṣmī, N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-नारायण, औ,<BR>m. du., अम्, n. sing. Lakṣmī and नारायण.<BR>—लक्-<BR>ष्मी-नारायण-यति, इस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-निवास, अस्, m. the abode of the god-<BR>dess of fortune.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-निवासाभिधान (˚स-<BR>अभ्˚), N. of a work.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-नृसिंह, अम्, n.<BR>Lakṣmī and ‘the man-lion;’ (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-b" target="_blank">Page0858-b+ 81</a>]<BR>king.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-पति, इस्, m. the husband or lord<BR>of Lakṣmī or Fortune; N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa;<BR>a king or prince (as husband of Lakṣmī, who is<BR>often regarded as the consort of a king); the betel-<BR>nut tree; the clove tree.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>m. the son of Lakṣmī; N. of Kāma; a horse;<BR>epithet of Kuśa and Lava (the sons of Rāma and<BR>Sītā).<BR>—लक्ष्मी-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘Lakṣmī's flower,’ a<BR>ruby.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-पूजन, अम्, n. the ceremony of<BR>worshipping Lakṣmī performed by a bridegroom<BR>in company with his bride (at the conclusion of the<BR>marriage after the bride has been brought to her<BR>husband's house).<BR>—लक्ष्मी-पूजा, f. ‘the worship<BR>of Lakṣmī,’ N. of a festival on the fifteenth day in<BR>the dark half of the month Āśvina (said to be cele-<BR>brated in modern times by bankers and traders to<BR>propitiate Fortune).<BR>—लक्ष्मी-प्रणयिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, dear to Lakṣmī, a favourite of fortune.<BR>—लक्ष्-<BR>मी-फल, अस्, m. Ægle Marmelos.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-<BR>यजुस्, उस्, n., N. of a particular sacred text.<BR>—लक्-<BR>ष्मी-रमण, अस्, m. the husband of Lakṣmī,<BR>i. e. Viṣṇu.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed<BR>of fortune or good luck, lucky, prosperous, fortunate,<BR>wealthy, rich, thriving; handsome, beautiful; the<BR>bread-fruit tree, Artocarpus Integrifolia; another<BR>tree (= श्वेत-रोहित).<BR>—लक्ष्मी-वर्म-देव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-वल्लभ, अस्, m.<BR>‘favourite of Lakṣmī,’ N. of an author.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-<BR>वसति, इस्, f. ‘abode of Lakṣmī,’ epithet of the<BR>lotus-flower (Nelumbium Speciosum).<BR>—लक्ष्मी-<BR>वहिष्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, excluded from fortune,<BR>destitute of wealth.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-वार, अस्, m. ‘Lak-<BR>ṣmī's day, ‘Thursday.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-वेष्ट, अस्, m.<BR>turpentine (= श्री-वेष्ट, q. v.).<BR>—लक्ष्मीश (˚मी-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. the lord of Lakṣmī, i. e. Viṣṇu; a<BR>prosperous man; the mango tree.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-सख,<BR>अस्, m. a friend of the goddess of fortune, a favourite<BR>of Lakṣmī.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-सनाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, en-<BR>dowed with beauty or fortune.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-समा-<BR>ह्वया, f. ‘having the name of Lakṣmī,’ N. of<BR>Sītā.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-सह-ज, अस्, m. ‘produced together<BR>with Lakṣmī,’ the moon (supposed to have arisen<BR>together with Lakṣmī from the ocean when churned<BR>by the gods and Asuras, see लक्ष्मी, col. 1).<BR>—लक्-<BR>ष्मी-सूक्त, अम्, n. a particular hymn addressed to<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-सेन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—लक्ष्मी-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. ‘praise of Lakṣmī,’ N.<BR>of a particular hymn ascribed to Agastya.<BR>—लक्ष्म्य्-<BR>आराम, अस्, m. the garden of Lakṣmī; N. of a<BR>forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीक
लक्ष्मीक = लक्ष्मी at the end of an adj.<BR>comp. (e. g. पुत्र-सङ्क्रान्त-लक्ष्मीक, one<BR>whose fortune has been transferred to a son; अलक्-<BR>ष्मीक-तम, most unfortunate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्य|लक्ष्यं|लक्ष्यः
लक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be marked, to be defined<BR>or described; having marks or attributes, to be ex-<BR>pressed indirectly; to be aimed at; to be regarded<BR>as, deserving to be regarded; to be looked at or<BR>observed, observable, perceptible, visible; to be re-<BR>cognised or known, recognisable by (with inst. or at<BR>the end of a comp.); (अस्), m. epithet of a magical<BR>formula or charm recited over weapons; (अम्), n.<BR>an aim, object, mark to be aimed at, butt, target,<BR>prize; a lac or one hundred thousand; mere appear-<BR>ance, sham, pretence [cf. लक्ष्य-सुप्त]; a sign,<BR>token (for लक्ष्मन्); an example, illustration (?).<BR>—लक्ष्य-क्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, having an indirectly<BR>perceptible method (said of that which is suggested<BR>by poetry but not expressed).<BR>—लक्ष्य-ज्ञ-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. knowledge of a mark or aim; knowledge<BR>of examples.<BR>—लक्ष्य-ता, f. or लक्ष्य-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the being indirectly expressed; the being<BR>an aim or object, (लक्ष्यतां या, to become<BR>an aim or object); perceptibility, visibility, (लक्ष्-<BR>यतां नी, to make visible.)<BR>—लक्ष्य-भेद,<BR>अस्, m. the cleaving of a mark.<BR>—लक्ष्य-वीथी,<BR>f. the visible or universally recognisable road, (ac-<BR>cording to a commentator = ब्रह्म-लोक-मार्ग.)<BR>—लक्ष्य-वेधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, piercing or hitting<BR>a mark.<BR>—लक्ष्य-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, pretending<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">Page0858-c+ 79</a>]<BR>to be asleep, shamming sleep.<BR>—लक्ष्य-हन्, हा,<BR>घ्नी, ह, hitting the mark; (हा), m. an arrow.<BR>—लक्ष्याभिहरण (˚य-अभ्˚), अम्, n. the carry-<BR>ing off of a prize.<BR>—लक्ष्यी-कृ, लक्ष्यी-कृत, = लक्-<BR>षी-कृ, लक्षी-कृत, see under लक्ष.<BR>—लक्ष्यी-<BR>भू = लक्षी-भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लख्
लख् लख् or लङ्ख् (= rt. लिङ्ख्), cl. 1.<BR>P. लखति, लङ्खति, &c., to go, move,<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लखिमादेवी
लखिमादेवी लखिमा-देवी, f., N. of a prin-<BR>cess, (a corruption fr. लक्ष्मी-देवी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्
लग् लग् (this rt. is most extensively<BR>and variously applied in spoken languages<BR>allied to Sanskrit), cl. 1. P. लगति, ललाग, अलगीत्,<BR>&c., to adhere, stick; to attach or fasten one's self<BR>to, cling to, clasp; to touch, join, become united;<BR>to meet, come in contact, intersect, cut (as lines); to<BR>approach near, follow closely (on any event), ensue<BR>or happen immediately; cl. 10. P. लागयति, &c.,<BR>to taste; to obtain, (in these senses = rts. लक्, रक्):<BR>Caus. लगयति, &c., to cause to adhere, &c.; [cf.<BR>perhaps Gr. λήγω and, according to some, possibly<BR>Lat. ligare.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगनीय
लगनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be attached, to be<BR>clung to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगित|लगितं
लगित, अस्, आ, अम्, attached to, adhered, con-<BR>nected with; obtained, got; entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगित्वा
लगित्वा, ind. having adhered, having clasped, hav-<BR>ing closely approached so as to touch or join, (तस्य<BR>पादयोर् लगित्वा, having clung to his feet.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्न|लग्नं|लग्नः
1. लग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see p. 860, col. 2),<BR>attached, adhered, stuck, held fast; attached to, joined<BR>to, connected with; coming in contact, meeting,<BR>intersecting, cutting (said of lines); adhering or<BR>clinging to, sticking to or upon, remaining on, im-<BR>pressed upon, fastened in, sticking in; fastened on,<BR>directed towards; followed or following closely, im-<BR>mediately ensuing; intent on, closely occupied about;<BR>auspicious; (अस्), m. a bard or minstrel (who awakes<BR>the king in the morning); a furious elephant or one<BR>in rut; (अम्), n. the point of contact or intersection<BR>(of two lines), the point where the horizon and the<BR>ecliptic or path of the planets meet; the point or arc<BR>of the equator which corresponds to a given point<BR>or arc of the ecliptic; the division of the equator<BR>which rises in succession with each sign in an oblique<BR>sphere; the point of the ecliptic which at a given<BR>time is upon the meridian or at the horizon, (क्षि-<BR>तिजे लग्नम्, horizon Lagna; मध्य-लग्न, me-<BR>ridian Lagna); the moment of the sun's entrance into<BR>a zodiacal sign; the rising of the sun or of the<BR>planets; (in astrology) a scheme or figure of the<BR>twelve houses or zodiacal signs (used as a horoscope);<BR>the whole of the first astrological house; an auspicious<BR>moment, a particular time fixed upon as lucky for<BR>the performance of anything, (rarely अस्, m.); the<BR>decisive moment, time for action, decisive measure,<BR>(also अस्, m.)<BR>—लग्न-काल, अस्, m. the moment or<BR>time pointed out by astrologers as favourable for any<BR>undertaking, an auspicious moment or time.<BR>—लग्-<BR>न-ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, insisting firmly on anything,<BR>persisting steadfastly in, important, obtrusive.<BR>—लग्-<BR>न-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of an astronomical work.<BR>—लग्न-दिन, अम्, n. or लग्न-दिवस, अस्, m.<BR>an auspicious day, a day fixed upon or chosen as<BR>favourable for any undertaking.<BR>—लग्न-देवी, f.,<BR>N. of a fabulous cow of stone.<BR>—लग्न-नक्षत्र,<BR>अम्, n. any auspicious constellation of the moon's<BR>path.<BR>—लग्न-पत्त्रिका, f. a paper on which the<BR>auspicious moment for a marriage &c. is noted down.<BR>—लग्न-भुज, अस्, m. (in astronomy) ascensional<BR>difference.<BR>—लग्न-मण्डल, अम्, n. the circle of<BR>signs, the zodiac.<BR>—लग्न-मास, अस्, m. an auspi-<BR>cious month.<BR>—लग्न-मुहूर्त, अम्, n. the auspi-<BR>cious moment or period for a marriage, &c.<BR>—लग्-<BR>न-वेला, f. or लग्न-समय, अस्, m. = लग्न-काल.<BR>—लग्न-शुद्धि, इस्, f. auspiciousness of the signs<BR>&c. for the commencement of any contemplated<BR>work.<BR>—लग्नासु (˚न-असु), अवस्, m. pl. (in astro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">Page0859-a+ 76</a>]<BR>nomy) ascensional equivalents in respirations.<BR>—लग्-<BR>नाह (˚न-अह), अस्, m. = लग्न-दिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नक|लग्नकः
लग्नक, अस्, m. a (fixed) surety or security, one<BR>who is responsible; a bondsman, bail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्निका
लग्निका, f. incorrect for नग्निका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग
लग लग, (in prosody) an iambus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगालिका
लगालिका, f. a kind of metre, four times ˘¯˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगड|लगडं
लगड लगड, अस्, आ, अम्, beautiful, hand-<BR>some; [cf. लडह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगत
लगत लगत or लगध, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of a work on astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुड|लगुडः
लगुड लगुड, अस्, m. (perhaps connected<BR>with rt. लग्), a stick, staff; a club, iron club.<BR>—ल-<BR>गुड-हस्त, अस्, m. ‘staff-in-hand,’ a man armed<BR>with a stick or mace, a staff-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुर|लगुरः
लगुर, अस्, m. = लगुड above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्न|लग्नं|लग्नः
लग्न लग्न, &c. See p. 858, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघट्
लघट् लघट्, ट्, or लघटि, इस्, m. (accord-<BR>ing to Uṇādi-s. I. 134. fr. rt. लङ्घ्), air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघन्ती
लघन्ती, f., N. of a river, (also read लङ्घती.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघय
लघय लघय, लघिमन्. See p. 860.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघु|लघुः
लघु लघु, उस्, -घ्वी or उस्, उ (a later form<BR>of रघु, q. v.; according to Uṇādi-s. I. 30. fr. rt.<BR>लङ्घ्), quick, swift, fleet, rapid, light, nimble,<BR>active; epithet of a particular mode of flying (pe-<BR>culiar to birds); epithet of the Nakṣatras Hasta,<BR>Aśvinī, and Puṣya; light, easy, not difficult or<BR>heavy; easy of digestion; (in prosody) short or<BR>light (i. e. a light vowel as opposed to a गुरु<BR>or heavy, the proper term for a short vowel being<BR>ह्रस्व); lightly pronounced (said of the pronunci-<BR>ation of व, as opposed to मध्यम and गुरु);<BR>little, small, narrow, diminutive, slight, unimportant,<BR>trivial, insignificant, trifling, of little worth or esti-<BR>mation; weak, feeble, wretched, low, lowly, humble,<BR>mean, contemptible, vain, frivolous; sapless, pithless;<BR>young, younger; soft, low, gentle (as sound; op-<BR>posed to अ-लघु, loud); pleasing, agreeable, plea-<BR>sant, handsome, beautiful; clean, pure; (उ), ind.<BR>quickly, rapidly, swiftly; lightly, easily, &c.; con-<BR>temptibly, (लघु मन्, to think lightly of, despise);<BR>(उस्), f. Trigonella Corniculata; (घ्वी), f. a slender<BR>or delicate woman; a light carriage; Trigonella Cor-<BR>niculata; (उ), n. a particular measure of time (= 15<BR>Kāṣṭhās = (1/15) Nāḍikā); Agallochum, a particular<BR>kind of Agallochum; the root of Andropogon Muri-<BR>catus; [cf. Gr. ἐλαχύ-ς, ἐλαφρός, λαγώς: Lat. lev-<BR>i-s, levi-ta-s, levare, lepus (for old lephus): Goth.<BR>leihts: Old Germ. lîhti: Angl. Sax. lîght: Slav.<BR>lig-u-ku: Lith. lengva-s: Hib. lag, ‘weak, feeble,<BR>faint;’ lagudhadh, ‘diminution, weakening;’ la-<BR>guighthe, ‘weakened, lessened;’ laghad, ‘fewness,<BR>weakness;’ lagaighim, ‘I weaken;’ laigidh, laigse,<BR>laigsinn, ‘weakness, infirmity;’ lugh, ‘little, swift,<BR>active;’ lughad, ‘littleness.]’<BR>—लघु-कङ्कोल, अस्,<BR>m. Pimenta Acris.<BR>—लघु-कण्टका, f. Mimosa<BR>Pudica.<BR>—लघु-कर्कन्धु, उस्, m. f. a small<BR>kind of Zizyphus.<BR>—लघु-कर्णी, f. a species of<BR>plant (= Marāṭhī मोरवेल).<BR>—लघु-काय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, light-bodied; (अस्), m. a goat.<BR>—लघु-<BR>काश्मर्य, अस्, m. a kind of tree.<BR>—लघु-कोष्ठ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a light stomach, having little in<BR>the stomach.<BR>—लघु-कौमुदी, f. ‘the short Kau-<BR>mudī, ‘N. of an epitome of the Siddhānta-kaumudī<BR>by Varada-rāja.<BR>—लघु-क्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a quick or rapid step, going quickly, hastening;<BR>(अम्), ind. with quick step, quickly, hastily.<BR>—ल-<BR>घु-क्रिया, f. a small event, trifle.<BR>—लघु-ख-<BR>ट्विका, f. a small bedstead or couch, easy chair.<BR>—लघु-खर्तर, N. of a family.<BR>—लघु-<BR>गङ्गाधर, अस्, m. a particular powder or medi-<BR>cine (used in diarrhœa).<BR>—लघु-गर्ग, अस्, m. a<BR>species of fish (probably a variety of the Pimelodus).<BR>—लघु-गोधूम, अस्, m. a small kind of wheat.<BR>—लघु-ग्रह-मञ्जरि, इस्, f., N. of an astrolo-<BR>gical work.<BR>—लघु-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a com-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-b" target="_blank">Page0859-b+ 81</a>]<BR>mentary by Brahmānanda-sarasvatī on the Advaita-<BR>siddhi (described as a refutation of the Nyāya theory<BR>from the point of view of the Vedānta).<BR>—लघु-<BR>चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, light-minded, little-minded, having<BR>little thought, thoughtless, frivolous, fickle, unsteady.<BR>—लघुचित्त-ता, f. light-mindedness, thoughtless-<BR>ness, fickleness.<BR>—लघु-चित्र-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>light and ready-handed.<BR>—लघु-चिन्तन, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of an epitome of the Mīmāṃsā Sūtras by Rāghava-<BR>deva.<BR>—लघु-चिन्तामणि-रस, अस्, m. epithet of<BR>a particular fluid mixture.<BR>—लघु-चिर्भिटा, f. co-<BR>locynth.<BR>—लघु-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, little-minded,<BR>low-minded, frivolous.<BR>—लघु-च्छदा, f. a kind<BR>of asparagus.<BR>—लघु-च्छेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to<BR>be cut, easy to be extirpated, easily annihilated or<BR>destroyed.<BR>—लघु-जङ्गल, अस्, m. a sort of quail<BR>(= लाबक).<BR>—लघु-जातक, अम्, n., N. of a short<BR>work by Varāha-mihira on horoscopes.<BR>—लघु-<BR>जातिविवेक, अस्, m. ‘the short Jāti-viveka,’ N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—लघु-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more quick, lighter,<BR>easier, &c. (= लघीयस्).<BR>—लघु-ता, f. or लघु-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. quickness, rapidity, agility, activity;<BR>lightness, levity, ease, facility; shortness; smallness,<BR>littleness, lowness, meanness, insignificance, unim-<BR>portance, thoughtlessness, levity, frivolity; wanton-<BR>ness; want of rank or dignity, humbleness of origin;<BR>disregard, disrespect.<BR>—लघु-दन्ती, f. a small kind<BR>of Croton.<BR>—लघु-दीपिका, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary.<BR>—लघु-दुन्दुभि, इस्, m. a small drum.<BR>—लघु-द्राक्षा, f. a small stoneless grape (com-<BR>monly called Kishmish).<BR>—लघु-द्राविन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>fusing or liquefying easily, flowing rapidly (said of<BR>quicksilver).<BR>—लघु-द्वारवती, f. the young or<BR>recent Dvāra-vatī, i. e. the more modern part of the<BR>town.<BR>—लघु-नाभ-मण्डल, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>particular mystical circle.<BR>—लघु-नामन्, अ, n.<BR>Agallochum.<BR>—लघु-नारदीय, अम्, n. the short<BR>Nāradīya.<BR>—लघु-न्याय-सुधा, f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on the Śata-ślokī.<BR>—लघु-न्यास, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a grammatical treatise.<BR>—लघु-पञ्चमूल,<BR>अम्, n. the smaller Pañca-mula, q. v.<BR>—लघु-पण्-<BR>डित, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—लघु-पतनक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘quickly flying, lightly falling,’ N. of a crow<BR>(in the Hitopadeśa).<BR>—लघु-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of plant (= रोचनी).<BR>—लघु-पत्त्र-फला,<BR>f. = लघूदुम्बरिका.<BR>—लघु-पत्त्री, f. a species<BR>of plant.<BR>—लघु-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—लघु-पराशर, अस्, m. the shorter Parāśara.<BR>—लघु-परिभाषा-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a short<BR>commentary on the grammatical Paribhāṣās.<BR>—ल-<BR>घु-पर्णी, f. = लघु-कर्णी.<BR>—लघु-पाक, अस्,<BR>m. easy digestion, digestibility; (अस्, आ, अम्), easy<BR>of digestion, easily digested.<BR>—लघु-पाकिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, easily digested.<BR>—लघु-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>quickly flying, lightly falling or alighting; (ई), m.,<BR>N. of a crow.<BR>—लघु-पिच्छिल, अस्, m. Cordia<BR>Myxa.<BR>—लघु-पुलस्त्य, अस्, m. the shorter or<BR>lesser Pulastya.<BR>—लघु-पुष्प, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>Kadamba.<BR>—लघु-प्रयत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, using<BR>little effort, indolent, impotent; pronounced with<BR>slight articulation.<BR>—लघु-बदर, अस्, ई, m. f. a<BR>kind of jujube tree.<BR>—लघु-बुद्ध-पुराण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of an epitome of the Lalita-vistara.<BR>—लघु-<BR>बोध, अस्, m. ‘easily understood,’ N. of a grammar.<BR>—लघु-ब्रह्मवैवर्त, अम्, n., N. of an epi-<BR>tome of the Brahma-vaivarta.<BR>—लघु-ब्राह्मी, f.<BR>a species of plant.<BR>—लघु-भव, अस्, m. a low<BR>station, humble birth.<BR>—लघु-भागवत, अम्, n.<BR>the short Bhāgavata.<BR>—लघु-भाव, अस्, m. light<BR>state, lightness, ease, facility.<BR>—लघु-भुज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>eating little.<BR>—लघु-भूषण-कान्ति, इस्, f., N. of<BR>a commentary.<BR>—लघु-भोजन, अम्, n. a light<BR>repast, slight refreshment.<BR>—लघु-मञ्जूषा, f.,<BR>N. of a commentary.<BR>—लघु-मन्थ, अस्, m. =<BR>क्षुद्राग्निमन्थ, Premna Spinosa.<BR>—लघु-<BR>मांस, अस्, m. ‘having light (i. e. easily digested)<BR>flesh, ‘a kind of partridge; (ई), f. a kind of Valeriana.<BR>—लघु-मानस, N. of an astronomical work.<BR>—लघु-मित्र, अम्, n. a slight or weak friend, an<BR>ally of little power or value.<BR>—लघु-मूल, अम्, n.<BR>(in algebra) the lesser root of an equation, the least<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-c" target="_blank">Page0859-c+ 81</a>]<BR>root with reference to the additive quantities; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), having a small root or beginning, easily<BR>commenced.<BR>—लघु-मूलक, अम्, n. a radish.<BR>—लघु-यम, अस्, m. ‘the short Yama,’ N. of a<BR>particular recension of Yama's law-book.<BR>—लघु-<BR>राशि, इस्, इस्, इ, (in arithmetic) composed of fewer terms<BR>(as a side in an equation; opposed to बहु-राशि,<BR>q. v.).<BR>—लघु-लय, अम्, n. the root of a fragrant<BR>Andropogon Muricatus.<BR>—लघु-ललित-विस्तर,<BR>N. of an extract from the Lalita-vistara.<BR>—लघु-<BR>वसिष्ठ-सिद्धान्त or लघु-वासिष्ठ-सिद्धान्-<BR>त, अस्, m., N. of an epitome of the Vasiṣṭha-sid-<BR>dhānta.<BR>—लघु-वाक्य-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of certain<BR>Vedānta precepts by Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—लघु-वार्त्-<BR>तिक, अम्, n., N. of the last eight books of the<BR>Tantra-vārttika; of a metrical epitome of the Mī-<BR>māṃsā Sūtras by Kumārila.<BR>—लघु-वासस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, thinly or lightly dressed; wearing clean or pure<BR>clothing.<BR>—लघु-विक्रम, अस्, m. a quick step;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), having a quick step, quick-footed,<BR>with hasty step, hastening.<BR>—लघु-विवर-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the state of having a narrow opening.<BR>—लघु-विष्णु, उस्, m. ‘the short Viṣṇu,’ N. of<BR>a particular recension of Viṣṇu's law-book.<BR>—ल-<BR>घु-वृत्ति, इस्, f. a short commentary; N. of a par-<BR>ticular commentary; (इस्, इस्, इ), badly behaved, ill-<BR>conducted, ill-conditioned, of low practices, low, vile;<BR>ill-done, mismanaged; having a light nature, light.<BR>—लघुवृत्ति-ता, f. insignificance, meanness; bad<BR>conduct, mismanagement.<BR>—लघु-वेधिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, easily piercing, cleverly hitting.<BR>—लघु-वैया-<BR>करण-सिद्धान्त-मञ्जूषा, f., N. of an epitome<BR>of the Vaiyākaraṇa-siddhānta-mañjūṣa.<BR>—लघु-<BR>शब्दरत्न, अम्, n., N. of an epitome of the<BR>Śabda-ratna.<BR>—लघु-शब्देन्दु-शेखर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a commentary on the Siddhānta-kaumudī<BR>(being an epitome of the Śabdendu-śekhara).<BR>—ल-<BR>घु-शमी, f. a kind of Acacia.<BR>—लघु-शान्ति-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n. an epitome of the Śānti-purāṇa.<BR>—लघु-शिखर-ताल, अस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>time in music.<BR>—लघु-शिवपुराण, अम्, n. the<BR>short Śiva-purāṇa.<BR>—लघु-शौनकी, f. ‘the shorter<BR>Śaunakī, ‘N. of a work.<BR>—लघु-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>and लघु-सङ्ग्रहिणी-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of two<BR>works.<BR>—लघु-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘weak-natured,’<BR>having a weak or fickle character, having an easy<BR>disposition.<BR>—लघुसत्त्व-ता, f. weakness of cha-<BR>racter, fickleness.<BR>—लघु-साङ्ख्य-वृत्ति or ल-<BR>घु-साङ्ख्य-सूत्र-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of an epitome<BR>of the Sāṅkhya-pravacana-bhāṣya.<BR>—लघु-सार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of little importance, insignificant, unim-<BR>portant, worthless.<BR>—लघु-सिद्धान्त-कौमुदी,<BR>f. = लघु-कौमुदी, q. v.<BR>—लघु-सिद्धान्त-<BR>चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a commentary.<BR>—लघु-सुदर्-<BR>शन, अम्, n. a particular medicinal powder.<BR>—ल-<BR>घु-स्यद, अस्, आ, अम्, = रघु-ष्यद्, going quickly.<BR>—लघु-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, light-handed, ready-<BR>handed, active, nimble, expert, clever; (अस्), m. a<BR>good archer.<BR>—लघुहस्त-ता, f. or लघुहस्त-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. ready-handedness, activity, expertness.<BR>—लघुहस्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, = लघु-हस्त.<BR>—लघु-हारित, अस्, m. ‘the short Hārīta,’ N. of<BR>a particular recension of Hārīta's law-book.<BR>—लघु-<BR>हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, light-hearted, fickle.<BR>—लघु-<BR>हेम-दुग्धा, f. Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR>—लघू-क-<BR>रण, अम्, n. the act of making light, making less,<BR>lessening, diminishing, diminution; thinking little<BR>of, contemning.<BR>—लघू-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>light, reduced in weight, made easier or shorter,<BR>abbreviated; lessened, reduced in importance, made<BR>insignificant; thought lightly of.<BR>—लघूक्ति (˚घु-<BR>उक्˚), इस्, f. a brief mode of expression.<BR>—लघूत्-<BR>थान (˚घु-उत्˚) or लघु-समुत्थान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, making active efforts, doing work rapidly.<BR>—ल-<BR>घूदुम्बरिका (˚घु-उद्˚), f. Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR>—लघु-अञ्जीर, अम्, n. a small fig.<BR>—लघु-अत्रि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘the short Atri,’ N. of a particular recension<BR>of Atri's law-book.<BR>—लघ्व्-आद्य्-उडुम्बराह्वा<BR>(˚र-आह्˚), f. = लघूदुम्बरिका.<BR>—लघ्व्-आर्य-<BR>सिद्धान्त, अस्, m. an abbreviation of the Ārya-<BR>siddhānta.<BR>—लघु-आशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or लघु-आहार,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">Page0860-a+ 76</a>]<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, eating little, making a light repast,<BR>moderate in diet, moderate, abstemious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघय
लघय, Nom. P. लघयति, &c., to make light,<BR>lighten, lessen, diminish, alleviate, mitigate, soften.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघिमन्
लघिमन्, आ, m. lightness, levity, absence of<BR>weight; a kind of सिद्धि or supernatural faculty of<BR>assuming excessive lightness at will; smallness, dimi-<BR>nutiveness, insignificance; frivolousness, fickleness;<BR>meanness, lowness, diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघिष्ठ|लघिष्ठः
लघिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of लघु), most<BR>quick, very swift; lightest, very light; very small, &c.;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἐλάχιστο-ς.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघीयस्
लघीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of लघु), more<BR>quick, very swift; lighter, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघूय
लघूय, Nom. P. लघूयति, &c., Ved. to<BR>think lightly of, despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ्वी
लघ्वी, f. a delicate woman, &c. See under<BR>लघु, p. 859, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्
लङ् लङ्, a technical term or symbol in<BR>grammar for the terminations of the Imperfect or<BR>First Preterite or for that tense itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्क
लङ्क लङ्क, अस्, m. a proper N.; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of the chief town in Ceylon or of the whole<BR>island (renowned as the capital and habitation of the<BR>great Rākṣasa Rāvaṇa and his hosts of demons,<BR>whose conquest by Rāma-candra, q. v., after the car-<BR>rying off of his wife Sītā by Rāvaṇa, forms the subject<BR>of the Rāmāyaṇa; according to some accounts<BR>Laṅkā was much larger than the island of Ceylon is<BR>at present or even distinct from Ceylon, the first<BR>meridian of longitude which passed through Ujjayinī<BR>being supposed to pass through Laṅkā also); = रा-<BR>वण-ह्रद; N. of a Śākinī or evil spirit; an<BR>unchaste woman; a branch; a kind of grain.<BR>—लङ्क-टङ्कटा, f., N. of a daughter of Sandhyā<BR>(wife of Vidyut-keśa and mother of Su-keśa).<BR>—लङ्-<BR>का-दाहिन्, ई, m. the burner of Laṅkā, i. e. Hanu-mat<BR>(as having set fire to the city with his burning tail).<BR>—लङ्काधिपति (˚का-अध्˚), इस्, or लङ्का-नाथ,<BR>अस्, or लङ्का-पति, इस्, m. lord of Laṅkā, i. e.<BR>Rāvaṇa.<BR>—लङ्कारि (˚का-अरि), इस्, m. the enemy<BR>of Laṅkā, i. e. Rāma.<BR>—लङ्कावतार (˚का-अव्˚)<BR>N. of a Buddhist Sūtra work, (abbreviated from<BR>सद्धर्म-ल्˚; it is one of the chief religious works<BR>of the Buddhists, treating of their law and of many<BR>abstruse philosophical problems.)<BR>—लङ्का-स्थायिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, residing or being in Laṅkā; (ई), m. a<BR>plant.<BR>—लङ्केश or लङ्केश्वर (˚का-ईश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the lord of Laṅkā, i. e. Rāvaṇa.<BR>—लङ्केश-वनारि-<BR>केतु (˚न-अर्˚), उस्, m. ‘having the enemy of the<BR>grove of Ravāṇa (i. e. the monkey Hanu-mat) for<BR>an ensign, ‘N. of Arjuna.<BR>—लङ्कोदय (˚का-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. or लङ्कोदयासु, अवस्, m. pl. (in astronomy)<BR>the equivalents of the signs in right ascension (lite-<BR>rally ‘ascension at Laṅkā’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कापिका
लङ्कापिका or लङ्कायिका or लङ्कारिका or लङ्-<BR>कोपिका or लङ्कोयिका, f. the plant Trigonella Cor-<BR>niculata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ख्|लंख्
लङ्ख् लङ्ख्. See rt. लख्, p. 858, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्खनी|लंखनी
लङ्खनी लङ्खनी, f. the bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ग्|लंग्
लङ्ग् लङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. लङ्गति, &c., to go;<BR>to go lame, limp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ग|लंग|लंगः|लङ्गः
1. लङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, lame, limping; (अस्), m.<BR>limping, lameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ग|लंग|लंगः|लङ्गः
लङ्ग 2. लङ्ग, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rt. लग्), union, association, connection; a lover,<BR>paramour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गक|लंगक|लंगकः|लङ्गकः
लङ्गक, अस्, m. a lover, paramour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गल|लंगल|लंगलं
लङ्गल, अम्, n. = लाङ्गल, a plough; N. of a<BR>kingdom, (also written लाङ्गल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गिम
लङ्गिम or लङ्गिमन् (?), union.<BR>—लङ्गिम-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, fit to be joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गूल|लंगूल|लंगूलं|लङ्गूलं
लङ्गूल, अम्, n. = लाङ्गूल, the tail of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घ्|लंघ्
लङ्घ् लङ्घ्, cl. 1. P. A. लङ्घति, -ते,<BR>ललङ्घ, ललङ्घे, लङ्घितुम्, to<BR>leap, spring, go by leaps; to ascend, mount upon;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">Page0860-b+ 78</a>]<BR>to diminish, lessen, weaken, (in this sense connected<BR>with लघु); to dry, dry up (P.); to fast, abstain<BR>from food (A.); cl. 10. P. or Caus. लङ्घयति,<BR>&c., to jump or spring over, leap or step over, over-<BR>step, go beyond (with acc.); to pass over, traverse;<BR>to ascend, mount, cross over; to transgress, trample<BR>upon, violate, disregard, disrespect, disdain, insult,<BR>offend, displease, injure, prevent, hinder, oppose; to<BR>go beyond, excel, surpass, outshine, outstrip; to cause<BR>any one to go beyond his meal-time, cause to fast<BR>[cf. सु-लङ्घित]; to speak; to shine: Desid. of<BR>Caus. लिलङ्घयिषति, to intend to step over; [cf.<BR>according to some, Gr. λαγγάζω, λογγάζω, λαγχόνω,<BR>λάχος, λόγχν, ἐλέγχω; Lat. longus, lan-<BR>guere; Old Germ. langên, ga-lingan, ga-langon;<BR>Goth. laggs; Angl. Sax. lang, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घक|लंघक
लङ्घक, अस्, m., Ved. one who leaps over or<BR>transgresses, one who insults or displeases, an offender,<BR>transgressor, violator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घती
लङ्घती, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घन|लंघन|लंघनं|लङ्घनं
लङ्घन, अम्, n. the act of leaping or jumping,<BR>going by leaps or jumps, springing, leaping over,<BR>overstepping, stepping across; one of a horse's paces,<BR>curvetting, bounding; ascending, mounting, attain-<BR>ing; the act of assaulting or storming, capturing a<BR>fort, capture, conquest; the act of jumping over,<BR>passing over, overstepping, exceeding, going beyond<BR>bounds, transgressing, violation; transgressing pro-<BR>priety; despising, disregarding, disdain, contempt;<BR>the act of offending or displeasing, injury, harm,<BR>offence, affront; fasting, abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घनीय|लंघनीय
लङ्घनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be lept over, to be<BR>stepped or passed over, to be passed, passable, attain-<BR>able; transgressible, to be violated; to be disregarded;<BR>to be injured or wronged; to be fasted.<BR>—लङ्घ-<BR>नीय-ता, f. or लङ्घनीय-त्व, अम्, n. capability of<BR>being lept or stepped over or transgressed; attain-<BR>ability; capability of being injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घित|लंघित
लङ्घित, अस्, आ, अम्, lept over, overstepped,<BR>passed beyond, passed over, traversed, transgressed,<BR>violated, disregarded, insulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घितव्य
लङ्घितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = लङ्घनीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घ्य|लंघ्य
लङ्घ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be jumped or stepped<BR>over; to be traversed or passed, attainable; capable<BR>of being transgressed or violated; to be neglected or<BR>disregarded; capable of being injured or wronged;<BR>to be made to fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लछ्|लच्छ्
लछ् लछ् (= rt. लाञ्छ्; connected with<BR>rt. लक्ष्), cl. 1. P. लच्छति, ललच्छ,<BR>&c., to mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
लज् 1. लज् (= rt. लज्ज्, q. v.), cl. 6. A.<BR>लजते, लेजे, लजितुम्, to be ashamed:<BR>Caus. लाजयति: Desid. लिलजिषते: Intens. लालज्-<BR>यते, लालक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लजकारिका
लज-कारिका, f. (लज for लज्जा), the sensitive<BR>plant, Mimosa Pudica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
लज् 2. लज् (= rt. 1. लञ्ज्), cl. 1. P. ल-<BR>जति, &c., to fry, roast; to calumniate,<BR>blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
लज् 3. लज् (= rt. 2. लञ्ज्), cl. 10. P.<BR>लजयति, &c., to appear, seem, shine;<BR>to cover, (in this sense another reading for rt. जल्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्ज्
लज्ज् लज्ज् (perhaps connected with a<BR>base रज्य fr. rt. रञ्ज्; cf. rt. 1. लज्),<BR>cl. 6. A. लज्जते (sometimes also P. लज्जति), ललज्जे,<BR>लज्जिष्यते, अलज्जिष्ट, लज्जितुम्, to be ashamed,<BR>blush: Caus. लज्जयति: Desid. लिलज्जिषते: Intens.<BR>लालज्ज्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्न|लग्नं|लग्नः
2. लग्न, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 858, col. 3),<BR>ashamed; (this part. is also referrible to rt. 1. लज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्ज
लज्ज, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. his<BR>descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जका
लज्जका, f. the wild cotton-tree, Gossypium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जत्
लज्जत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, being ashamed,<BR>blushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जमान
लज्जमान, अस्, आ, अम्, blushing, feeling shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जरी
लज्जरी, f. a white sensitive plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जा
लज्जा, f. shame, modesty, bashfulness; Shame<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">Page0860-c+ 75</a>]<BR>(personified as the wife of Dharma and as the<BR>mother of Vinaya); the sensitive plant, Mimosa<BR>Pudica.<BR>—लज्जा-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, or लज्जा-<BR>कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, causing or occasioning shame,<BR>shameful.<BR>—लज्जाकृति (˚जा-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, feigning<BR>modesty.<BR>—लज्जान्वित (˚जा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessed of shame, ashamed, modest, bashful.<BR>—लज्जा-<BR>रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, void of shame, shameless, im-<BR>modest.<BR>—लज्जा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of shame,<BR>full of shame, ashamed, bashful, modest; embar-<BR>rassed, perplexed.<BR>—लज्जावत्-त्व, अम्, n. bashful-<BR>ness, modesty.<BR>—लज्जा-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a modest<BR>disposition, bashful, modest.<BR>—लज्जा-शून्य or लज्जा-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of shame, void of modesty,<BR>shameless, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाय
लज्जाय, Nom. (probably A.) लज्जायते, &c., to<BR>be ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जायित
लज्जायित, अस्, आ, अम्, ashamed, abashed, embar-<BR>rassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जालु|लज्जालुः
लज्जालु, उस्, उस्, उ, bashful, modest, shameful;<BR>(उस्), m. f. the sensitive plant, Mimosa Pudica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जित|लज्जितः
लज्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, ashamed, abashed, modest,<BR>bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जिरी
लज्जिरी, f. = लज्जालु, Mimosa Pudica; [cf. लज्-<BR>जरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्या
लज्या, f. = लज्जा, shame, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्चा|लंचा
लञ्चा लञ्चा, f. a present, bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्छन
लञ्छन लञ्छन, Eleusine Coracana (a<BR>kind of grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज्|लंज्
लञ्ज् 1. लञ्ज् (= rt. 2. लज्), cl. 1. P. लञ्-<BR>जति, &c., to fry, roast; to calumniate,<BR>blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज्|लंज्
लञ्ज् 2. लञ्ज् (also read लुञ्ज्), cl. 10. P.<BR>लञ्जयति, &c., to be strong; to strike,<BR>injure; to dwell; to give; to speak; to shine; to<BR>be manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज|लंज|लंजः|लञ्जः
लञ्ज लञ्ज, अस्, m. a foot; the end of the<BR>lower garment tucked into the waist-band; a tail;<BR>= पङ्गु; (आ), f. an adulteress; sleep; a current;<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्जिका|लंजिका
लञ्जिका, f. a harlot, prostitute; [cf. perhaps Gr.<BR>λαγ-αρό-ς,λάγ-νο-ς, Lat. langu-e-o,<BR>langu-i-du-s, langu-or, laxus, lac-tes.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्
लट् 1. लट्, cl. 1. P. लटति, &c., to be a<BR>child, act or talk like a child, be childish;<BR>to cry; [cf. rt. रट्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट|लटः
लट, अस्, m. one who speaks like a child, a block-<BR>head, fool; a fault, defect; a thief.<BR>—लट-पर्ण,<BR>अम्, n. = त्वच, large cinnamon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटक|लटकः
लटक, अस्, m. a bad man, contemptible person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्ट|लट्टः
लट्ट, अस्, m. = लटक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्य
लट्य, Nom. P. लट्यति, &c., to speak foolishly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्व|लट्वः
लट्व, अस्, m. a horse; a particular caste (said to<BR>be a tribe of mountaineers); a dancing boy; a par-<BR>ticular Rāga or scale in music; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>bird (said to be a kind of sparrow); safflower; a<BR>kind of Karañja; the fruit of a kind of Karañja;<BR>fruit in general; a curl on the forehead, &c. (=<BR>भ्रमरक); a game, gambling (= द्यूत); a<BR>bad or unchaste woman; a sweetmeat (?) ; = अवद्य;<BR>= शिली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्वाका
लट्वाका, f. = लट्वा, a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्
लट् 2. लट्, a technical term or symbol<BR>in grammar for the terminations of the Present or<BR>for that tense itself.<BR>—लड्-अर्थ-वाद, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a treatise on the meaning of the Present tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटकन
लटकन लटकन or लटकन-मिश्र, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्
लड् लड्, cl. 1. P. लडति, &c., to play,<BR>sport, frolic, dally (= rt. लल्, q. v.); cl.<BR>10. P. लडयति, लडापयति, &c., to throw, toss;<BR>to blame, (in this sense = rt. लाड्); cl. 10. P. or<BR>Caus. लडयति, to loll the tongue, use or put out<BR>the tongue, stir with the tongue, lick [cf. rt. लल्];<BR>to caress, foster, cherish (= ललयति, लालयति, see<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">Page0861-a+ 76</a>]<BR>rt. लल्); to stir, coagulate; to harass, annoy; to be<BR>harassed or pained (?); to throw up or out (?) ; to<BR>apprise (?); [cf. perhaps Gr. λάλος, λαλέω, λῆρος;<BR>Mod. Germ. lallen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लडित
लडित = ललित, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लडक
लडक लडक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लडह|लडहः
लडह लडह, अस्, आ, अम्, handsome, pleasing,<BR>beautiful, charming; (अस्), m., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्ड|लड्डः
लड्ड लड्ड, अस्, m. a wretch, villain, bad<BR>man; [cf. लट्ट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्डु|लड्डुः
लड्डु लड्डु or लड्डुक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind<BR>of sweetmeat (made of coarsely ground gram or<BR>other pulse, or of corn-flour, mixed up with sugar<BR>and spices, and fried in ghee or oil; there are several<BR>varieties of this sweetmeat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्वा
लड्वा लड्वा, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लण्ड्|लंड्
लण्ड् लण्ड् [cf. rt. ओलण्ड्], cl. 10. P. लण्-<BR>डयति, &c., to cast upwards, throw or<BR>toss up; to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लण्ड|लंड|लंडं|लण्डं
लण्ड लण्ड, अम्, n. excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लण्ड्र|लंड्र|लंड्रः|लण्ड्रः
लण्ड्र लण्ड्र (probably fr. the French<BR>लोन्द्रेस्), London.<BR>—लण्ड्र-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born<BR>or produced in London.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लता
लता लता, f. (said to be fr. a Sautra rt.<BR>लत्), a creeper, creeping plant, winding plant in<BR>general, (the brows, arms, curls, lightning, &c. are<BR>frequently metaphorically compared to the form of<BR>a creeper; cf. भ्रू-ल्˚, बाहु-ल्˚, तडिल्-ल्˚, &c.); a<BR>plant of any kind; a branch; musk-creeper, = कस्तू-<BR>रिका [cf. लता-कस्तूरिका below]; N. of various<BR>plants, Panicum Italicum; Trigonella Corniculata;<BR>Cardiospermum Halicacabum; Gærtnera Racemosa;<BR>Panicum Dactylon; = कैवर्तिका; = सारिवा; the<BR>thong or lash of a whip, a whip; a string or thread<BR>of pearls; a slender or graceful woman; a woman<BR>in general; N. of a metre, four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘<BR>¯˘¯¯, ˘¯¯˘¯¯˘¯; N. of an Apsaras; of a<BR>daughter of Meru and wife of llāvṛta.<BR>—लता-कर,<BR>अस्, m. a particular position of the hands in dancing.<BR>—लता-करञ्ज, अस्, m. Guilandina Bonduc.<BR>—लता-<BR>कस्तूरिका or लता-कस्तूरी, f. musk-creeper, a kind<BR>of aromatic medicinal plant or substance (said to<BR>grow in the Dekhan).<BR>—लता-गृह, अस्, अम्, m.<BR>n. ‘creeper-house,’ a house or bower built or sur-<BR>rounded with creepers, an arbour.<BR>—लताङ्गी (˚ता-<BR>अङ्˚), f. a kind of plant (= कर्कट-शृङ्गी).<BR>—ल-<BR>ताङ्गुलि (˚ता-अङ्˚), इस्, f. ‘creeper-finger,’ a branch<BR>serving as a finger.<BR>—लता-जिह्व, अस्, m. ‘creeper-<BR>tongued,’ a snake.<BR>—लता-तरु, उस्, m., N. of various<BR>trees, Shorea Robusta; Borassus Flabelliformis; the<BR>orange tree.<BR>—लता-द्रुम, अस्, m. Shorea Robusta.<BR>—लतानन (˚ता-आन्˚), अस्, m. a particular position<BR>of the hands in dancing.<BR>—लतान्त (˚ता-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘the end of a creeper,’ a flower.<BR>—लता-पनस,<BR>अस्, m. the water-melon.<BR>—लता-पर्ण, अस्, m., N.<BR>of Viṣṇu; (ई), f. Curculigo Orchioides; Trigonella<BR>Fœnum Græcum.<BR>—लता-पृक्का, f. Trigonella Cor-<BR>niculata.<BR>—लता-प्रतान, अस्, m. the tendril of a<BR>creeper.<BR>—लता-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of Tricho-<BR>santhes Diœca.<BR>—लता-भद्रा, f. Pæderia Fœtida.<BR>—लता-भवन, अम्, n. an arbour (= लता-गृह).<BR>—लता-मणि, इस्, m. ‘creeper-jewel,’ coral.<BR>—लता-<BR>मण्डप, अस्, m. ‘creeper-pavilion,’ an arbour,<BR>bower.<BR>—लता-मरुत्, त्, f. Trigonella Corniculata.<BR>—लता-माधवी, f. the Mādhavī creeper, Gærtnera<BR>Racemosa.<BR>—लता-मृग, अस्, m. an ape, monkey.<BR>—लताम्बुज (˚ता-अम्˚), अम्, n. a kind of cucum-<BR>ber.<BR>—लता-यष्टि, इस्, f. Bengal madder, Rubia<BR>Munjista.<BR>—लता-यावक, अम्, n. a shoot, sprout,<BR>young or tender pasturage.<BR>—लता-रसन, अस्, m.<BR>‘creeper-tongued,’ a snake.<BR>—लतार्क (˚ता-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a green onion.<BR>—लतालक (˚ता-अल्), अस्, m. an<BR>elephant.<BR>—लतालय (˚ता-आल्˚), अस्, m. an abode or<BR>dwelling made of creepers.<BR>—लता-वलय, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. = लता-गृह, an arbour.<BR>—लतावलय-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of bowers or having bracelet-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">Page0861-b+ 73</a>]<BR>like creepers.<BR>—लता-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the cocoa-nut<BR>tree; Shorea Robusta.<BR>—लता-वेष्ट, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a mountain; a kind of coitus.<BR>—लता-वेष्टन<BR>or लता-वेष्टितक, अम्, n. ‘creeper-embrace,’ an<BR>embrace or kind of embrace.<BR>—लता-वेष्टित, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—लता-शङ्ख, अस्, m.<BR>Shorea Robusta.<BR>—लतोद्गम (˚ता-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the upward climbing of a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतिका
लतिका, f. a small creeper or winding plant; a<BR>string of pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतु
लतु लतु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लत्तिका
लत्तिका लत्तिका, f. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 147. fr. a Sautra rt. लत्, to hurt), a kind of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लदनी
लदनी लदनी, f., N. of a female poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लद्ध
लद्ध लद्ध (?) , अस्, m. a particular animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लद्धनदेव
लद्धनदेव लद्धन-देव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप्
लप् 1. लप्, cl. 1. P. लपति (sometimes<BR>also A. लपते when required by the<BR>metre), ललाप, लपितुम्, to chatter, prate, speak,<BR>talk; to whisper; to wail, lament, weep: Caus. ला-<BR>पयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलीलपत् or अललापत्, to<BR>cause to talk: Desid. लिलपिषति: Intens. लालप्-<BR>यते, लालप्ति, to talk incessantly or excessively,<BR>chatter senselessly, prattle; to bewail, lament; [cf.<BR>Gr. ἔ-λακ-ο-ν, λέ-λακ-α, λά-σκ-ω, λακ-ε-ρό-ς, λα-<BR>κέρυζα, (probably also) ὀλοφύρομαι, according to<BR>some also λάλος, λαλέω (through reduplication, the<BR>final letter of rt. लप् being rejected): Lat. loqu-o-r,<BR>loquax, loquela, Ajus Locu-ti-us, la-mentum;<BR>labium, labrum, lambo: Slav. reka: Lith. su-<BR>rik-ti, rek-iu: Hib. labhraim, ‘I speak;’ labh-<BR>radh, ‘speech, discourse.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप्
2. लप्, speaking, talking. See अभीलाप-लप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपन|लपनं
लपन, अम्, n. the act of speaking, talking;<BR>the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपित|लपितं
लपित, अस्, आ, अम्, chattered, spoken, said; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a Śārṅgikā or particular bird (with which<BR>Manda-pāla is said to have allied himself); (अम्),<BR>n. voice, speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाप|लापः
लाप, अस्, m. chattering, speaking, talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लापिका
लापिका in अन्तर्-लापिका, f. a sort of riddle or<BR>enigma; [cf. वहिर्-ल्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लापिन्
लापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking, saying, declaring; be-<BR>wailing, lamenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाप्य|लाप्यं
लाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken, &c.; to be<BR>lamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालप्यमान
लालप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking incessantly;<BR>wailing or bewailing greatly, supplicating much, (a<BR>form लालप्यत् is also found.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपेटिका
लपेटिका लपेटिका, f., N. of a place of pil-<BR>grimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपेत
लपेत लपेत, अस्, m., N. of a demon pre-<BR>siding over a particular disease of children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप्सिका
लप्सिका लप्सिका, N. of a kind of prepared<BR>food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप्सुद
लप्सुद लप्सुद, अम्, n., Ved. = कूर्च, the<BR>beard (of a goat &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप्सुदिन्
लप्सुदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having a beard, bearded<BR>(said of a goat &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब|लबः
लब लब, अस्, m., Ved. a quail [cf. लव];<BR>N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 119,<BR>(his patronymic is Aindra.)<BR>—लब-सूक्त, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध|लब्धः
लब्ध लब्ध, लब्धक, &c. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ्
लभ् लभ् (probably a later form of rt.<BR>रभ्), cl. 1. A. लभते (ep. also P. ल-<BR>भति; a nasal is also sometimes inserted, e. g.<BR>लम्भते, अलम्भत, as if fr. a rt. लम्भ्), लेभे,<BR>लप्स्यते, अलब्ध, लब्धुम्, to take, seize, take<BR>hold of, catch, catch hold of; to receive, (गर्भं<BR>लभ्, to receive an embryo, conceive, become preg-<BR>nant), obtain, get, acquire, enjoy; to meet with,<BR>find, gain possession of, have, possess; to recover,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-c" target="_blank">Page0861-c+ 81</a>]<BR>regain; to gain the power of doing anything, be<BR>able, be permitted (with infinitive, e. g. लभते<BR>द्रष्टुम्, he is able or is allowed to see); to per-<BR>ceive, know, understand, learn: Pass. लभ्यते,<BR>Aor. अलाभि or अलम्भि (with prep. only अलम्भि),<BR>to be taken or received, to be gained or obtained,<BR>&c.; to be found; to be contained; to take (Passive<BR>reflexive): Caus. लम्भयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अल-<BR>लम्भत्, to cause to take or receive, cause to obtain,<BR>&c. (generally with a double acc.; rarely with acc.<BR>and inst.); to give, bestow; to obtain, receive; to<BR>find out, discover; to cause to suffer: Desid. लिप्सते<BR>(sometimes P. when required by the metre; Ved.<BR>also लीप्सते), to wish to seize or take hold of, to<BR>strive to obtain, desire to receive or obtain, long for:<BR>Intens. लालभ्यते, लालम्भीति, लालब्धि; [cf. Gr.<BR>λάφυρον, λαμβάνω, εἴληφα, λαῖλαψ, probably<BR>λέβης, λίπτω: Old Pruss. labba-s, ‘goods, posses-<BR>sions;’ lab-s, ‘good:’ Lith. laba-s, ‘good,’ lobis,<BR>‘possessions, goods:’ Slav. lov-i-ti: Hib. lamh, ‘a<BR>hand.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध|लब्धः
लब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, taken, seized, taken hold of,<BR>obtained, received, got, gained, won, acquired; per-<BR>ceived, apprehended, known, obtained (as a quotient<BR>by division &c.; cf. लब्धि); (आ), f. a woman<BR>whose husband or lover is faithless; epithet of a<BR>particular heroine.<BR>—लब्ध-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has gained his wishes.<BR>—लब्ध-कीर्त्ति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, one who has won fame or glory.<BR>—लब्ध-चेतस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, one who has recovered his right mind,<BR>restored to sense, recovered.<BR>—लब्ध-जन्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, one who has obtained birth, born.<BR>—लब्ध-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m. ‘restoring what one has received,’ a<BR>proper N.<BR>—लब्ध-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has acquired wealth, wealthy.<BR>—लब्ध-नामन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, one who has gained a name, well spoken of,<BR>famous, celebrated.<BR>—लब्ध-नाश, अस्, m. the loss<BR>of what has been acquired.<BR>—लब्ध-प्रणाश, अस्,<BR>m. the loss of anything acquired; N. of the fourth<BR>book of the Pañca-tantra.<BR>—लब्ध-प्रतिष्ठ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has acquired fame or renown.<BR>—लब्ध-प्रशमन, अम्, n. the securing of<BR>what has been acquired, keeping acquisitions in<BR>safety; (according to Kullūka on Manu VII. 56)<BR>bestowing acquisitions on a proper recipient.<BR>—लब्-<BR>धप्रशमन-स्वस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, at ease by<BR>(reason of) the securing or secure possession of<BR>acquisitions.<BR>—लब्ध-लक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has hit the mark, one who has obtained the prize;<BR>skilled in the use of missiles; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—लब्ध-लक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = लब्ध-लक्ष.<BR>—लब्ध-वर, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has obtained<BR>a boon or favour; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—लब्ध-<BR>वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has learnt his letters,<BR>lettered, learned, sage, skilful, clever.<BR>—लब्धवर्-<BR>ण-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, honouring the learned.<BR>—लब्ध-<BR>विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has acquired knowledge<BR>or wisdom, learned, educated.<BR>—लब्ध-शब्द, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, = लब्ध-नामन्.<BR>—लब्ध-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who has recovered his senses, restored to<BR>consciousness.<BR>—लब्ध-सिद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, one who<BR>has attained perfection.<BR>—लब्धानुज्ञ (˚ध-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has obtained leave of absence.<BR>—लब्धान्तर (˚ध-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has found an opportunity.<BR>—लब्धावकाश (˚ध-<BR>अव्˚) or लब्धावसर (˚ध-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has found an opportunity or gained scope, one<BR>who has obtained leisure.<BR>—लब्धोदय (˚ध-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has received birth or<BR>production (Kumāra-s. I. 25); one who has attained<BR>prosperity, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धक
लब्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, obtained, received, got,<BR>attained; [cf. दुःख-लब्धिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धवत्|लब्धवन्त्
लब्धवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has obtained or<BR>gained or received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धव्य
लब्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be obtained or received,<BR>to be gained or attained, obtainable, &c. See लभ्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धि|लब्धिः
लब्धि, इस्, f. obtaining, gaining, acquisition,<BR>acquirement, attainment; anything gained or ob-<BR>tained, gain, advantage, profit; the quotient (in<BR>arithmetic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धृ
लब्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, one who obtains or<BR>receives, a receiver, gainer, recipient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध्रिम
लब्ध्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, obtained, received, attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध्वा
लब्ध्वा, ind. having obtained or gained, having<BR>got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ
लभ in इषल्-ल्˚, दुर्-ल्˚, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभन|लभनं
लभन, अम्, n. the act of obtaining or getting,<BR>the meeting with, gaining possession of; the act of<BR>conceiving, conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभस|लभसः
लभस, अस्, m. a horse's foot-rope, a rope for<BR>tying a horse (= वाजि-बन्धन); wealth, riches;<BR>one who asks or solicits, a solicitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ्य|लभ्यं
लभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be found or met with,<BR>capable of being acquired, acquirable, obtainable,<BR>attainable, procurable, to be reached (see प्रांशु-ल्˚);<BR>to be understood or known, intelligible; suitable,<BR>proper, fit; to be furnished or provided with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ्यमान
लभ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being obtained, being<BR>acquired. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भ|लंभ|लंभः|लम्भः
लम्भ, अस्, m. the obtaining or attaining, attain-<BR>ment, acquirement; finding, meeting with, recovery;<BR>gain; (आ), f. a sort of fence or enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भक
लम्भक, अस्, m. one who obtains, an obtainer,<BR>one who finds, a finder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भन|लंभन|लंभनं|लम्भनं
लम्भन, अम्, n. the act of obtaining or re-<BR>ceiving, attainment, recovery; the act of procuring,<BR>causing to get; abuse, reviling (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भनीय
लम्भनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be obtained or re-<BR>ceived, to be attained, attainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भम्
लम्भम्, ind. having taken or obtained, (लम्-<BR>भं लम्भम् repeatedly taking, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भयत्
लम्भयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to obtain,<BR>procuring, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भित|लंभित
लम्भित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), caused to<BR>obtain or receive, given, procured, gained; height-<BR>ened, improved; cherished; applied, employed,<BR>adapted; addressed, spoken to; abused (?).<BR>—लम्-<BR>भित-कान्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, one who has acquired lustre<BR>or beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भुक
लम्भुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who is accus-<BR>tomed to receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ|लाभः
लाभ, अस्, m. obtaining, receiving, gaining, get-<BR>ting, meeting with, finding, acquirement, acquisition;<BR>gain, advantage, profit; capture, conquest; appre-<BR>hension, comprehension, perception, knowledge; en-<BR>joying; = प्राप्ति, N. of the eleventh astrological<BR>house or lunar mansion; [cf. Slav. lovu.]<BR>—लाभ-<BR>कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, or लाभ-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing<BR>gain, making or procuring profit, gainful, profitable.<BR>—लाभ-लिप्सा, f. greediness of gain, avarice, covet-<BR>ousness.<BR>—लाभ-लिप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of gain<BR>or profit, covetous, grasping.<BR>—लाभ-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having gain or profit; being in possession of.<BR>—लाभालाभ (˚भ-अल्˚), औ, m. du. profit and loss,<BR>advantage and disadvantage, gain and detriment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभक|लाभकः
लाभक, अस्, m. gain, profit, advantage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभम्
लाभम्, ind. = लम्भम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभिन्
लाभिन्, ई, इनी, इ, obtaining, gaining, meeting<BR>with, finding, receiving, acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ्य|लाभ्यं
लाभ्य, अम्, n. = लाभ (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सा
लिप्सा, f. (fr. the Desid.), the desire to gain, wish<BR>to acquire or obtain, desire for possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सित
लिप्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished to be obtained,<BR>coveted, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सितव्य
लिप्सितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, desirable to be obtained,<BR>to be wished for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सु|लिप्सुः
लिप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to gain or obtain, de-<BR>siring to become possessed of (with acc.), eager for,<BR>desirous of, covetous.<BR>—लिप्सु-ता, f. the state of<BR>wishing to obtain, covetousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्स्य
लिप्स्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be wished to be obtained,<BR>desirable to be acquired, eligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीप्सितव्य
लीप्सितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worthy of being<BR>acquired, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्
लम् लम् (a later form of rt. रम्), cl.<BR>1. P. लमति (= रमति), ललाम (=<BR>रराम), &c., to delight in, sport, enjoy (sexually).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लमक|लमकः
लमक, अस्, m. = रमक, a lover, wooer, para-<BR>mour, (according to Ujjvala-datta, Uṇādi-s. II. 33,<BR>= तीर्थ-शोधक); a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्न
लम्न लम्न, आस्, m. pl., N. of a particular<BR>tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पक
लम्पक लम्पक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Jaina<BR>sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पट|लंपट|लम्पटः
लम्पट लम्पट, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps con-<BR>nected with rt. लप्; cf. लिम्पट), covetous, greedy,<BR>desirous, lustful; hankering after, addicted to (licen-<BR>tious pleasures), lascivious, dissolute; (अस्), m. a<BR>libertine, lecher, dissolute person.<BR>—लम्पट-ता, f.<BR>or लम्पट-त्व, अम्, n. eagerness, greediness; liber-<BR>tinism, lasciviousness, dissoluteness, lewdness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पाक|लंपाक|लम्पाकः
लम्पाक, अस्, आ, अम्, = लम्पट; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a country (= मुरण्ड; according to some the<BR>district of Lamghan in Cabul).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पा
लम्पा लम्पा, f., N. of a town; of a king-<BR>dom.<BR>—लम्पा-पटह, अस्, m. a kind of drum (=<BR>प्रतिपत्ति-पटह, टट्टरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्फ|लंफ|लंफः|लम्फः
लम्फ लम्फ, अस्, m. a leap, spring, jump;<BR>[cf. झम्प.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्फन|लंफन|लंफनं
लम्फन, अम्, n. leaping, springing, jumping,<BR>(a form उल्-लम्फन, ‘jumping up,’ is given.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्ब्|लंब्
लम्ब् लम्ब् (a later form of rt. रम्ब्), cl.<BR>1. A. लम्बते (sometimes also P. लम्-<BR>बति), ललम्बे, लम्बिष्यते, अलम्बिष्ट, लम्-<BR>बितुम्, to hang down, depend, dangle, hang from,<BR>hang on or upon, depend on or from; to sink, sink<BR>down, go down, decline, fall, set (as the sun); to be<BR>fastened to, be attached to, hold on to, rest on; to<BR>fall behind, stay behind, lag behind, be retarded; to<BR>delay, tarry; to sound (fr. rt. रम्ब्; cf. rt. लम्भ्):<BR>Caus. लम्बयति, &c., to cause to hang down or<BR>depend, let down; to hang up, suspend; to cause to<BR>be fastened or attached, join; to stretch out, extend;<BR>to depress, (perhaps) discourage; [cf. Lat. labi;<BR>Lith. rambus; Angl. Sax. limpian, ge-limp; Eng.<BR>limp.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्ब|लंब|लम्बः
लम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, hanging down, depending,<BR>pendulous, pendent, dangling; hanging on or upon,<BR>attached to; long, tall; expanded, great, large;<BR>spacious, capacious; (अस्), m. a perpendicular (in<BR>geometry); complement of latitude, co-latitude (in<BR>astronomy), the arc between the pole of any place<BR>and the zenith; epithet of a particular throw or<BR>move (at a kind of chess or a game like backgam-<BR>mon or draughts); N. of a Muni; of a Daitya; a<BR>present, bribe (?) , = नर्तक, अङ्ग, कान्त; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of bitter gourd or cucumber; N. of one of<BR>the Mātṛs attending upon Skanda; N. of Durgā or<BR>Gaurī; of Lakṣmī; of a daughter of Dakṣa and<BR>wife of Dharma or Manu; of a Rākṣasī.<BR>—लम्ब-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having pendulous ears, long-<BR>eared; (अस्), m. a he-goat, goat; an elephant; a<BR>hawk, falcon; a Rākṣasa; Alangium Hexapetalum;<BR>N. of one of Śiva's attendants; of an ass (in one of<BR>the stories of the Pañca-tantra); of a hare (in the<BR>Pañca-tantra).<BR>—लम्ब-केश, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, hav-<BR>ing hanging or flowing hair.<BR>—लम्ब-केशक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘long-haired,’ N. of a Muni.<BR>—लम्ब-गुण,<BR>अस्, m. the sine of the co-latitude (in astronomy).<BR>—लम्ब-जठर, अस्, आ, अम्, big-bellied.<BR>—लम्-<BR>ब-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, letting the tongue hang out;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—लम्ब-ज्या or लम्ब-<BR>ज्यका, f. the sine of the co-latitude (in astronomy).<BR>—लम्ब-दन्ता, f. a kind of plant (= सैंहली).<BR>—लम्ब-पयोधरा, f. a woman with large or<BR>pendent breasts; N. of one of the Mātṛs attending<BR>upon Skanda.<BR>—लम्ब-रेखा, f. the complement<BR>of latitude, co-latitude (in astronomy).<BR>—लम्ब-<BR>वीजा, f. = लम्ब-दन्ता.<BR>—लम्ब-स्फिच्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>having large or protuberant buttocks.<BR>—लम्बाक्ष<BR>(˚ब-अक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—लम्बालक<BR>(˚ब-अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having pendulous curls or<BR>ringlets.<BR>—लम्बालक-त्व, अम्, n. pendulosity of<BR>ringlets.<BR>—लम्बोदर (˚ब-उद्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>a large or protuberant belly, pot-bellied; (अस्), m. a<BR>voracious person, glutton; N. of Gaṇeśa; of a king;<BR>of a Muni; (ई), f., N. of a female demon.<BR>—लम्-<BR>बोष्ठ (˚ब-ओष्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having a large<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">Page0862-c+ 76</a>]<BR>or prominent under-lip; (अस्), m. a camel, (also<BR>written लम्बौष्ठ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बक|लंबक|लंबकः|लम्बकः
लम्बक, अस्, m. a perpendicular (in geometry);<BR>the complement of latitude, co-latitude (in astro-<BR>nomy); N. of a particular implement or vessel; N.<BR>of the fifteenth astronomical Yoga; N. of the larger<BR>sections or books of the Kathā-sarit-sāgara (of which<BR>there are eighteen, containing in all 124 Taraṅgas<BR>or chapters); (इका), f. the uvula or soft palate.<BR>—लम्बिका-कोकिला, f., N. of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बन|लंबन|लम्बनं|लंबनः|लम्बनः
लम्बन, अस्, आ, अम्, hanging down, depending,<BR>pendulous; causing to hang down; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>Śiva; phlegm, the phlegmatic humor; (अम्), n.<BR>hanging down, depending, descending, falling; fringe;<BR>a long necklace (depending from the neck to the<BR>navel); the parallax in longitude (of the moon), the<BR>interval of the lines between the earth's centre and<BR>surface; epithet of a particular mode of fighting;<BR>N. of a Varṣa in Kuśa-dvīpa.<BR>—लम्बन-विधि,<BR>इस्, m. the rule for calculating the above parallax (in<BR>astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बमान|लम्बमानं
लम्बमान, अस्, आ, अम्, hanging down, depend-<BR>ing, descending, dangling, falling, going down;<BR>being large or bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बिका|लंबिका
लम्बिका, f. See under लम्बक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बित|लंबित|लम्बितः
लम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, hanging down, pendent;<BR>suspended; sunk, gone down, set; laying hold of,<BR>attached to, supported or resting on; = वि-लम्बित,<BR>slow (of time in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बिन्
लम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hanging down, depending, pen-<BR>dent, hanging down as far as, hanging on or upon;<BR>(इनी), f. one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बुक
लम्बुक, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-demon; N. of<BR>the fifteenth astronomical Yoga, (for लम्बक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बुषा|लंबुषा
