लल्
लल् लल् (= rt. लड्), cl. 1. P. A. ललति,<BR>ललते, &c., to play, sport, frolic, dally;<BR>to play (with the tongue); cl. 10. P. ललयति, &c.,<BR>to loll the tongue, &c. (see rt. लड्): Caus. P. लाल-<BR>यति, &c. (according to some also ललयति), to cause<BR>to sport or dally; to caress, fondle, coax, cherish,<BR>nurse, love; A. लालयते, &c., to desire, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल
लल, अस्, आ, अम्, sporting, frolicking, playful;<BR>lolling, wagging; wishing, desirous.<BR>—लल-जिह्व =<BR>ललज्-जिह्व below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललत्
ललत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, playing, sporting, dallying;<BR>playing with the tongue, &c.<BR>—ललज्-जिह्व, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, playing with the tongue, lolling the tongue,<BR>moving the tongue hither and thither; fierce, savage;<BR>(अस्), m. a camel; a dog.<BR>—ललद्-अम्बु, उस्, m. a<BR>particular plant (= लिम्पाक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन|ललनं|ललनः
ललन, अस्, आ, अम्, playing, coruscating (said of<BR>light, colour, &c.); sporting; (अस्), m., N. of various<BR>plants, = साल, प्रियाल; (आ), f. a wanton woman;<BR>a woman (in general), a wife; the tongue; N. of<BR>several metres, four times ¯˘˘¯¯, ¯˘˘¯˘˘¯;<BR>four times ¯˘˘¯¯, ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯; a particular<BR>kind of Gāthā; N. of a mythical being; (अम्), n.<BR>play, sport, pleasure, dalliance; the playing or mov-<BR>ing to and fro of the tongue; lolling the tongue.<BR>—ललना-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, dear to women, liked<BR>by females; (अस्), m. Nauclea Cadamba; (अम्), n.<BR>= ह्री-वेर, a kind of drug.<BR>—ललना-वरूथिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, surrounded by a troop of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललनिका
ललनिका, f. a little woman, a miserable woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन्तिका|ललंतिका
ललन्तिका, f. (fr. ललन्ती, fem. of ललत्), a long<BR>pendulous necklace; a lizard, chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललमान
ललमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sporting, playing, dallying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाक|ललाकः
ललाक, अस्, m. the penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललित|ललितं|ललितः
ललित, अस्, आ, अम्, sported, played, playing, sport-<BR>ing, dallying, wanton, frolicsome, amorous, volup-<BR>tuous; lovely, handsome, beautiful, graceful, elegant,<BR>naive, simple, artless, gay, cheerful; soft, gentle;<BR>pleasing, charming, pleasant, agreeable, wished for,<BR>desired, loved; trembling, tremulous, shaken; = च-<BR>लित; (अम्), ind. sweetly, agreeably, gracefully;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of a particular position of the hands<BR>in dancing; N. of a particular musical scale or Rāga,<BR>(according to some ललिता, f.); (आ), f. a wanton<BR>woman, a woman in general; musk; N. of a god-<BR>dess; of a form of Durgā or Pārvatī; of a Gopī<BR>(identified with Durgā and Rādhikā); of a river;<BR>of various metres, 30 + 32 instants; four times<BR>˘˘˘˘˘˘¯¯¯¯˘¯; four times ¯¯˘¯˘˘˘¯<BR>˘¯˘¯; four times ¯˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯;<BR>four times ¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯;<BR>twice ¯˘¯˘˘¯˘¯, ˘˘¯˘˘˘˘¯˘¯; (अम्), n.<BR>sport, dalliance, amorous gesture, love; grace, beauty,<BR>charm, charmingness, gracefulness of gait, softness<BR>and delicacy of motion, languid gestures in a woman<BR>(expressive of amorous sentiment, ‘lolling,’ ‘lan-<BR>guishing, ‘&c.); any natural and artless act (as that<BR>of a child); simplicity, innocency, ingenuousness; N.<BR>of two metres, four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯;<BR>four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯¯¯¯˘¯; N. of a town.<BR>—ललित-चैत्य, अस्, m., N. of a particular Caitya.<BR>—ललित-ताल, अस्, m., N. of a particular time (in<BR>music).<BR>—ललित-पद, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of<BR>amorous words; elegantly composed; a kind of<BR>metre, four times ˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯¯.<BR>—ललित-<BR>पद-बन्धन, अम्, n. an amorous composition<BR>in verse, a metrical composition treating of love.<BR>—ललित-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—ललित-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n. = ललित-विस्तर-पुराण.<BR>—ल-<BR>लित-प्रहार, अस्, m. a soft or gentle blow.<BR>—ल-<BR>लित-माधव, अम्, n., N. of a drama by Rūpa.<BR>—ललित-ललित, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively beautiful,<BR>very handsome.<BR>—ललित-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, beauti-<BR>ful-eyed; (आ), f., N. of the daughter of a Vidyā-dhara<BR>Vāma-datta.<BR>—ललित-वनिता, f. a lovely woman.<BR>—ललित-विस्तर, अस्, m. or ललित-विस्तर-पुरा-<BR>ण, अम्, n., N. of a Sūtra work giving a detailed<BR>record of the simple and natural acts in the life of<BR>Buddha or Śākya-muni.<BR>—ललित-व्यूह, अस्, m.<BR>epithet of a particular kind of Samādhi or meditation<BR>(with Buddhists); N. of a Deva-putra; of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR>—ललिता-तृतीया, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra<BR>work.<BR>—ललिता-तृतीय, f. epithet of a particular<BR>third day.<BR>—ललितादित्य (˚त-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a king of Kaśmīra.<BR>—ललितादित्य-पुर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a town founded by Lalitāditya.<BR>—ललिता-पञ्-<BR>चमी, f. the fifth day of the moon's increase in<BR>the month Āśvina on which the worship of the<BR>goddess Lalitā or Pārvatī is celebrated.<BR>—ललितापीड<BR>(˚त-आप्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king of Kaśmīra.<BR>—ल-<BR>लिताभिनय (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, m. erotic performance,<BR>representation of love scenes.<BR>—ललिता-माधव =<BR>ललित-माधव.<BR>—ललिताचन-चन्द्रिका (˚ता-<BR>अर्˚), f., N. of a work on the worship of Lalitā.<BR>—ललितार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having an<BR>amorous meaning.<BR>—ललितार्थ-बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>composed in words of love or in words having an<BR>amorous meaning.<BR>—ललिता-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>particular religious observance.<BR>—ललिता-षष्ठी,<BR>f. epithet of a particular sixth day.<BR>—ललिता-सप्-<BR>तमी, f. epithet of the seventh day in the light half<BR>of the month Bhādra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

