ललीतिका
ललीतिका, f., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाल
लाल, अस्, m., N. of an astronomer; (आ), f. saliva,<BR>spittle, slaver.<BR>—लाल-चन्द्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—लाल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (लाल for लाला), causing<BR>saliva to flow.<BR>—लाल-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of an astro-<BR>nomer.<BR>—लाला-भक्ष, अस्, m. ‘having saliva for<BR>food, ‘N. of the hell appropriated to those who eat<BR>their meals without first offering food to the gods,<BR>to the Manes, or to guests.<BR>—लाला-मेह, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">Page0863-b+ 79</a>]<BR>passing mucous urine.<BR>—लाला-विष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whose saliva is poison (said of venomous insects).<BR>—लाला-स्रव, अस्, m. ‘distilling saliva,’ a spider.<BR>—लाला-स्राव, अस्, m. a flow of saliva or spittle;<BR>‘emitting saliva,’ a spider.<BR>—लाला-स्राविन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>causing a flow of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालक|लालकः
लालक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus. of rt. लल्),<BR>caressing, fondling, coaxing, seducing; (इका), f. a<BR>jesting or evasive reply, equivoque.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालन|लालनं|लालनः
लालन, अस्, ई, अम्, caressing, fondling, coaxing;<BR>(अस्), m. a particular venomous animal, a sort of<BR>mouse; (अम्), n. the act of caressing, fondling,<BR>coaxing, dandling; spoiling, indulging, over-indulg-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालनीय
लालनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be caressed or fondled or<BR>coaxed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालयत्
लालयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, caressing, coaxing; stroking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालयितव्य
लालयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = लालनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाय
लालाय, Nom. A. लालायते, &c., to emit saliva,<BR>slaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालायित|लालायितः
लालायित, अस्, आ, अम्, emitting or discharging<BR>saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालिक|लालिकः
लालिक, अस्, m. a buffalo; [cf. लाविक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालित
लालित, अस्, आ, अम्, caressed, tenderly cherished,<BR>fondled, nursed, coaxed, indulged, seduced; loved,<BR>desired; (अम्), n. pleasure, joy, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालितक|लालितकः
लालितक, अस्, m. a fondling, darling, little favourite,<BR>pet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालित्य|लालित्यं
लालित्य, अम्, n. (fr. ललित), loveliness, grace,<BR>beauty, pleasingness, pleasantness, sweetness, loveli-<BR>ness, charm, grace, beauty; gaiety; amorous or lan-<BR>guid gestures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालिन्
लालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, caressing, fondling, coaxing; (ई),<BR>m. a seducer; (इनी), f. a wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालील
लालील, अस्, m., Ved., N. of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाल्य
लाल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = लालनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललल्ल
ललल्ल ललल्ल, an onomatopoetic word<BR>representing a lisping sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाट|ललाटं
ललाट ललाट, अम्, n. (a later form of र-<BR>राट, q. v.), the forehead, brow, (ललाटे, ‘on the<BR>forehead, in front;’ the destiny of every individual<BR>is conceived by the Hindūs to be written on the<BR>forehead.)<BR>—ललाट-तट, अम्, n. the slope of the<BR>forehead, the forehead.<BR>—ललाटन्-तप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>burning the forehead (as the sun).<BR>—ललाट-पट्ट,<BR>अम्, n. or ललाट-पट्टिका, f. ‘the plate’ or flat surface<BR>of the forehead, the forehead; a tiara, fillet.<BR>—ल-<BR>लाट-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—ललाट-फ-<BR>लक, अम्, n. the flat surface of the forehead.<BR>—ल-<BR>लाट-रेखा, f. a line on the forehead supposed to<BR>indicate long life; a wrinkled or corrugated brow;<BR>a coloured sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR>—लला-<BR>टाक्ष (˚ट-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having an eye in the<BR>forehead; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटक|ललाटकं
ललाटक, अम्, n. a beautiful forehead; the fore-<BR>head, brow; (इका), f. an ornament worn on the fore-<BR>head; a mark made with sandal on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटिकाय
ललाटिकाय, Nom. A. ललाटिकायते, &c., to re-<BR>present or be like a mark on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटिकायमान
ललाटिकायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, representing a mark<BR>on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटूल
ललाटूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a high or handsome<BR>forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाट्य
ललाट्य, अस्, &c. = रराट्य, of or belonging to<BR>the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाम|ललामं|ललामः
ललाम ललाम, अम्, n. (probably connected<BR>with rt. लल्; cf. ललाट), a mark or spot on the<BR>forehead, mark or spot in general; an ornament<BR>for the forehead, ornament, decoration, embellish-<BR>ment in general, (in this sense also अस्, m.); a<BR>coloured mark on the forehead of a horse or bull,<BR>&c.; a sign, symbol, token, mark of caste, &c.; a<BR>banner, flag, ensign; a line, row; any one who is<BR>the ornament of his class, any eminent or principal<BR>person, (in this sense even अम्, n.); anything the<BR>best of its kind, any grand or beautiful object; emi-<BR>nence, beauty, dignity; a tail; a mane; a horn (?) ;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), having a mark or spot on the forehead,<BR>marked with a blaze (said of cattle); beautiful, agree-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">Page0863-c+ 77</a>]<BR>able, charming; (अस्), m. a horse; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>female demon (Ved.); a kind of ornament for the<BR>ears.<BR>—ललाम-गु, उस्, m., Ved. a facetious term for<BR>the penis.<BR>—ललाम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a mark<BR>or spot; having an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललामक|ललामकं
ललामक, अम्, n. a chaplet or wreath of flowers<BR>worn on the forehead.<BR>—ललामक-रूपक, अम्,<BR>n. (in rhetoric) a flowery metaphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललामन्
ललामन्, अ, n. = ललाम, an ornament, decora-<BR>tion; a mark, sectarial mark; sign, symbol, token;<BR>a banner, flag; any one who is the ornament of his<BR>class; any chief or principal person or thing; a tail;<BR>a horn (?) ; a species of stanza having ten syllables<BR>in the first two Pādas, eleven in the third, and thir-<BR>teen in the fourth; a horse, (in this sense probably<BR>आ, m.); = रम्य; = सुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललित|ललितं|ललितः
ललित ललित, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल्यान
लल्यान लल्यान, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल्ल
लल्ल लल्ल, अस्, m., N. of an astronomer;<BR>of certain other persons; (आ), f., N. of a courtezan<BR>(in Rāja-tarangiṇī VIII. 1834, &c.).<BR>—लल्ल-वा-<BR>राह-सुत, अस्, m. the son of Lalla and Vārāha, N.<BR>of the author of the Nakṣatra-samuccaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल्लिय
लल्लिय लल्लिय, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल्लुजीलाल
लल्लुजीलाल लल्लुजीलाल, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव|लवं|लवः
लव लव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. लू), the act of<BR>cutting, reaping (of corn), mowing, plucking or<BR>gathering (of flowers, &c.); that which is cut or<BR>shorn off, a shorn fleece, wool, hair; anything cut<BR>off, a section, fragment, fraction, piece, particle, bit,<BR>drop, small piece, small quantity, little, (जल-ल्˚, a<BR>drop of water; तृण-ल्˚, a piece of straw; अपरा-<BR>ध-ल्˚, a little blame); a minute division of time,<BR>the sixtieth of a twinkling, half a second, a moment,<BR>an instant, (according to others (1/4000) or (1/5400) or<BR>(1/20250) of a Muhūrta); a degree (in astronomy);<BR>the numerator of a fraction; loss, destruction; sport<BR>[cf. लल]; N. of a son of Rāma-candra and Sītā,<BR>(he and Rāma's other son Kuśa were the two rhap-<BR>sodists who first committed the Rāmāyaṇa to memory<BR>and recited it at assemblies, see Rāmāyaṇa I. 4. and<BR>cf. कुशीलव); N. of a king of Kaśmīra (father of<BR>Kuśa); a kind of quail, Perdix Chinensis; (अम्),<BR>ind. a little; लवम् अपि, even a little; (अम्), n.<BR>nutmeg; cloves; the root of Andropogon Muricatus.<BR>—लव-राज, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—लव-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, lasting only for a moment.<BR>—लव-<BR>शस्, ind. in small pieces or fragments, bit by bit,<BR>piecemeal, in minute divisions or instants, after an<BR>instant, after some moments.<BR>—लवेप्सु (˚व-ईप्˚),<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to cut or reap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवक|लवकः
लवक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who cuts or reaps, &c.,<BR>a cutter, reaper, shearer; N. of a particular substance,<BR>(see स-ल्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवङ्ग|लवंग|लवङ्गं|लवंगः|लवङ्गः
लवङ्ग, अस्, m. the clove tree; (अम्), n. cloves.<BR>—लवङ्ग-कलिका, f. cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवङ्गक|लवंगक|लवंगकं|लवङ्गकं
लवङ्गक, अम्, n. cloves; (इका), f., N. of a<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवन|लवनं
लवन, अस्, ई, अम्, one who cuts, &c., a cutter,<BR>reaper; (ई), f. a particular fruit tree, Anona Reticu-<BR>lata; (अम्), n. the act of cutting, reaping, mowing,<BR>&c. (of corn); an implement for cutting, sickle,<BR>knife, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवनीय
लवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut, to be reaped or<BR>mown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवन्य
लवन्य, अस्, m., N. of a particular tribe of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवय
लवय, Nom. P. लवयति, &c., = लवम् आच-<BR>ष्टे, Pāṇ. I. 1, 58, Vārtt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवाक|लवाकः
लवाक, अस्, m. an implement for cutting, sickle,<BR>reaping-hook; the act of cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवाणक|लवाणकः
लवाणक, अस्, m. an implement for cutting, a<BR>sickle, reaping-hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवि|लविः
लवि, इस्, इस्, इ, cutting, sharp, edged (as a tool or<BR>instrument); (इस्), m. = लवित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवित्र|लवित्रं
लवित्र, अम्, n. an implement for cutting, a<BR>sickle, reaping-hook, scythe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0863-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव्य
लव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut, to be mown or<BR>hewn down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवट
लवट लवट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवण|लवणं|लवणः
लवण लवण, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. लू; according to others for original रवण),<BR>salt, (especially) sea-salt, rock or fossil salt, (गो-ल-<BR>वण, as much salt as is given to a cow); factitious<BR>salt or salt obtained from saline earth; (अस्), m. salt-<BR>ness, saline taste; the sea of salt water; N. of a<BR>hell; of a Rākṣasa or Daitya; of a king belonging<BR>to the family of Hari-ścandra; of a son of Rāma;<BR>of a river; = बल, अस्थि-भेद (?) ; (आ), f. lustre,<BR>beauty [cf. लावण्य]; a species of plant (= महा-<BR>ज्योतिष्मती); N. of a small river in Tirhut; (ई),<BR>f., N. of several rivers; (अस्, आ, अम्), saline, salt,<BR>briny, brinish; handsome, beautiful.<BR>—लवण-किं-<BR>शुका, f. a species of plant.<BR>—लवण-क्षार, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of salt (= लोणार).<BR>—लवण-खानि, इस्,<BR>f. a salt-mine; the district of Sambher in Ajmere<BR>celebrated for its fossil salt.<BR>—लवण-जल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having salt water; (अस्), m. the sea, ocean.<BR>—लवण-जल-धि or लवण-जल-निधि, इस्, m.<BR>‘receptacle of salt water,’ the sea, ocean.<BR>—लवण-<BR>जलोद्भव (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced in the<BR>sea; (अस्), m. a muscle, shell.<BR>—लवण-ता, f. or<BR>लवण-त्व, अम्, n. saltness, brinishness.<BR>—लवण-<BR>तृण, अम्, n. a kind of grass.<BR>—लवण-तोय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having salt water; (अस्), m. the sea, ocean.<BR>—लवण-धेनु, उस्, f. an offering of salt, (see<BR>धेनु.) -लवण-पाटलिका, f. a salt-bag.<BR>—ल-<BR>वण-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—लवण-प्र-<BR>गाढ, अस्, आ, अम्, strongly impregnated with salt.<BR>—लवण-मद, अस्, m. = लवण-क्षार.<BR>—ल-<BR>वण-मन्त्र, अस्, m. a prayer accompanied with<BR>an offering of salt.<BR>—लवण-मेह, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of urinary disease (discharging salty urine).<BR>—ल-<BR>वण-मेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from the above<BR>disease.<BR>—लवण-वारि, इस्, इस्, इ, having salt water;<BR>(इ), n. the sea, ocean.<BR>—लवण-समुद्र, अस्, m.<BR>the sea of salt water, salt-sea, sea, ocean.<BR>—लवण-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—लवणाकर (˚ण-<BR>आक्˚), अस्, m. a salt-mine; (metaphorically) a mine<BR>of grace or beauty.<BR>—लवणान्तक (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the slayer of the Rākṣasa Lavaṇa, N. of Śatru-<BR>ghna.<BR>—लवणाब्धि (˚ण-अब्˚), इस्, m. ‘receptacle<BR>of salt water, ‘the sea, ocean.<BR>—लवणाब्धि-ज,<BR>अम्, n. ‘produced from the sea,’ sea-salt.<BR>—लव-<BR>णाम्बु-राशि (˚ण-अम्˚), इस्, m. ‘a mass of salt water,’<BR>the sea, ocean.<BR>—लवणाम्भस् (˚ण-अम्˚), अस्, n.<BR>salt water; (आस्), m. ‘having salt water,’ the sea,<BR>ocean.<BR>—लवणार्णव (˚ण-अर्˚) or लवणालय<BR>(˚ण-आल्˚), अस्, m. the sea of salt water, ocean.<BR>—ल-<BR>वणाश्व (˚ण-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—ल-<BR>वणोत्तम (˚ण-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘best salt,’ river or<BR>rock salt; nitre.<BR>—लवणोत्थ (˚ण-उत्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>kind of salt (= लोणार).<BR>—लवणोत्स (˚ण-उत्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—लवणोद (˚ण-उद),<BR>अम्, n. salt water, brine; (अस्), m. ‘containing salt<BR>water, ‘the sea of salt water, ocean.<BR>—लवणोदक<BR>(˚ण-उद्˚), अम्, n. salt water, brine; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having or containing salt water; (अस्), m. the sea,<BR>ocean.<BR>—लवणोदधि (˚ण-उद्˚), इस्, m. ‘receptacle<BR>of salt water,’ the sea, ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणय
लवणय, Nom. P. लवणयति, to salt, season<BR>with salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणस्य
लवणस्य, Nom. P. लवणस्यति, to desire salt,<BR>long for salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणारज|लवणारजं
लवणारज, अम्, n. a kind of salt (= लोणार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणिमन्
लवणिमन्, आ, m. saltness; grace, beauty, loveli-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणीय
लवणीय, Nom. P. लवणीयति, &c., (probably)<BR>to wish for salt (Pāṇ. VII. 1, 51).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवन|लवनं
लवन लवन, &c. See p. 863, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवली
लवली लवली, f. Averrhoa Acida; a kind<BR>of metre.<BR>—लवली-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of the<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवेरणि
लवेरणि लवेरणि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव्य
लव्य लव्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लश्
लश् लश्, cl. 10. P. लाशयति, &c., to<BR>exercise an art, do anything scientifically<BR>(= rt. 1. लस्, cl. 10, of which it is sometimes con-<BR>sidered a various reading).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लशुन|लशुनं|लशुनः
लशुन लशुन, अम्, n., (rarely) अस्, m. garlic,<BR>(sometimes written लसुन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लशुनीय
लशुनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, garlicky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष्
लष् लष्, cl. 1. 4. P. A. लषति, -ते,<BR>लष्यति, -ते, ललाष, लेषे, लषिष्-<BR>यति, -ते, अलाषीत् or अलषीत्, अलषिष्ट, लषि-<BR>तुम्, to wish, desire, long for, be eager for (with<BR>acc.); cl. 10. P. लाषयति, to exercise an art, do<BR>anything scientifically, (in this sense a various reading<BR>for rt. लश् above): Pass. लष्यते, Aor. अलाषि:<BR>Caus. लाषयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अलीलषत्: Desid.<BR>लिलषिषति: Intens. लालष्यते, लालष्टि, to long<BR>for eagerly; [cf. Gr. λά-ω, (Dor. λῶ, λῇς, λῇ, 3rd<BR>pl. λῶντι), λῆ-μα, λῆ-σι-ς, λι-λα-ί-ο-μαι, λε-λίη-μαι,<BR>λία-ν, λαρός, λωΐων, λήλαντος, probably λα-μία,<BR>λάμος, λάρυγξ, λαιμός, λαίτμα; Lat. las-c-<BR>ivu-s; Goth. lus-tu-s, lus-to-n; Angl. Sax. lust,<BR>lyst, lystan; Slav. las-k-a-ti, ‘to flatter;’ Bohem.<BR>las-ka, ‘love.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लषण
लषण, अस्, &c., one who desires or longs for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लषणावती
लषणा-वती, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लषित
लषित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष्व|लष्वः
लष्व, अस्, m. a dancer, actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालष्यमाण
लालष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, eagerly longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लषमण
लषमण लषमण, अस्, m. (= लखमण,<BR>= लक्ष्मण), a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लषमादेवी
लषमा-देवी, f. (= लक्ष्मी-देवी), N. of a<BR>princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्
लस् 1. लस्, cl. 1. P. लसति, ललास (3rd<BR>du. लेसतुः), अलासीत् or अलसीत्, लसितुम्,<BR>to shine, flash, glitter, coruscate, glance; to appear,<BR>come to light, arise; to sound, resound, (connected<BR>with rt. 1: रस्); to embrace; to play, sport, move<BR>about rapidly, dance, jump, skip about [cf. रास];<BR>cl. 10. P. लासयति, &c., to exercise an art, do any-<BR>thing scientifically or skilfully, (in this sense = rts. लश्,<BR>लष्): Pass. लस्यते, Aor. अलासि, &c.: Caus. लास-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलीलसत्, to cause to sport or play,<BR>to cause to dance, teach to dance; to dance: Intens.<BR>लालस्यते, (this form does not seem to occur, but<BR>cf. लालस); [cf. probably Lat. ludo, (according to<BR>some) lascivus, lascivire.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्
2. लस्, अस्, अस्, अस्, shining, glittering; [cf. अ-लस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस|लसं
लस, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, glancing, playing, mov-<BR>ing hither and thither [cf. अ-लस]; (आ), f. saffron,<BR>turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसक|लसकः
लसक = लासक below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसत्
लसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shining, glittering, flashing,<BR>glancing; sporting, playing.<BR>—लसद्-अंशु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>having flashing or glancing rays (said of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसमान
लसमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, glittering; sport-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसित
लसित, अस्, आ, अम्, played, sported, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्त|लस्तः
लस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, embraced, grasped; skilled,<BR>skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्तक|लस्तकः
लस्तक, अस्, m. the middle of a bow (the part<BR>grasped).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्तकिन्
लस्तकिन्, ई, m. a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास|लासः
लास, अस्, m. the act of jumping, skipping or<BR>moving about, sporting, dancing, (probably con-<BR>nected with रास); dancing as practised by women;<BR>dalliance, wanton sport; soup, broth, boiled pulse,<BR>pea-water; saliva (? in अ-लास, q. v.).<BR>—लास-वती,<BR>f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लासक|लासकं|लासकः
लासक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who sports or gambols,<BR>playing; moving hither and thither, going through<BR>various evolutions; (अस्), m. a dancer, actor; N. of<BR>Śiva; a peacock; N. of a dancer; embracing, en-<BR>folding, surrounding; (इका), f. a female dancer; a<BR>harlot, wanton; a kind of dramatic performance;<BR>(अकी), f. a female dancer, dancing girl; (अम्), n. =<BR>a turret, tower, room on the top of a building (=<BR>अट्टक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लासयत्
लासयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to dance, causing<BR>to move about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लासिन्
लासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, moving to and fro, dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्य|लास्यं|लास्यः
लास्य, अम्, n. a dance, dancing; a dance accom-<BR>panied with instrumental music and singing; a dance<BR>in which the emotions of love are mimically repre-<BR>sented, the dance of the Indian dancing girls, a Nach<BR>dance (confined to attitude and gesticulation, with a<BR>shuffling motion of the feet seldom lifted from the<BR>ground; this style is said to have been invented by<BR>Pārvatī and communicated by her to the daughter<BR>of Vāṇāsura, by whom her female friends and com-<BR>panions were instructed in it; it is opposed to the<BR>Tāṇḍava, the more boisterous dance of Śiva and his<BR>followers); a part or particular kind of drama or dra-<BR>matic representation (said to be the occasional intro-<BR>duction of music and singing; also a style of dramatic<BR>composition in which there is abrupt transition from<BR>Prākṛt to Sanskrit and from Sanskrit to Prākṛt,<BR>&c.); (अस्), m. a dancer; (आ), f. a female dancer,<BR>dancing girl.<BR>—लास्याङ्ग (˚य-अङ्˚), अम्, n. that<BR>part of a drama in which the Lāsya described above<BR>is introduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्यक|लास्यकं
लास्यक, अम्, n. = लास्य, a dance, dancing in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसिका
लसिका लसिका, f. spittle, saliva, (perhaps<BR>a later form of रसिका, or connected with rt. 1. लस्;<BR>cf. लाला fr. rt. लल्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसीका
लसीका, f. spittle, saliva; the juice of the sugar-<BR>cane; lymph; matter, pus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसोफरञ्ज
लसोफरञ्ज लसोफरञ्ज, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्त|लस्तः
लस्त लस्त, लस्तक, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्पूजनी
लस्पूजनी लस्पूजनी, f., Ved. a large needle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहका
लहका लहका, f., see Gaṇa Kṣipakādi to<BR>Pāṇ. VII. 3, 45, Vārtt. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहर
लहर लहर, अस्, m., N. of a people, (also<BR>read लहड, लडह); N. of a province in Kaśmīra,<BR>(perhaps the present Lahore.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहरि|लहरिः
लहरि लहरि, इस्, or लहरी, f. a large wave,<BR>billow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहिक
लहिक लहिक, अस्, m. a diminutive from<BR>Lahoḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहोड
लहोड, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लह्य
लह्य लह्य, अस्, m. a proper N.; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the descendants of Lahya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ला
ला 1. ला, cl. 2. P. लाति, ललौ (3rd pl.<BR>ललुः), &c., to take, receive, obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ला
2. ला, आस्, f. the act of taking, receiving; the<BR>giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लात
लात, अस्, आ, अम्, taken, received, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाति|लातिः
लाति, इस्, f. taking, receiving, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लात्वा
लात्वा, ind. having taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाकिनी
लाकिनी लाकिनी, f., N. of a Tantra goddess;<BR>[cf. राकिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाकुच
लाकुच लाकुच, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लकुच), be-<BR>longing or relating to the Lakuca tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाकुचि
लाकुचि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Lakuca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाकुटिक|लाकुटिकः
लाकुटिक लाकुटिक for लागुडिक or (accord-<BR>ing to some) for लालाटिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षकी
लाक्षकी लाक्षकी, f., N. of Sītā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षण
लाक्षण लाक्षण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लक्षण),<BR>relating to signs or marks, knowing characteristic<BR>signs or marks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षणि
लाक्षणि, इ, m. a patronymic from Lakṣaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षणिक|लाक्षणिकः
लाक्षणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, knowing marks, acquainted<BR>with signs; relating to marks or signs, indicatory,<BR>characteristic; expressing indirectly or figuratively;<BR>having a figurative or metaphorical meaning, secon-<BR>dary, inferior, subordinate; technical; (अस्), m. one<BR>who knows or explains signs; a technical term, a<BR>word implying a definition.<BR>—लाक्षणिक-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the expressing by signs or figures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षण्य
लाक्षण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, conversant with signs or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">Page0865-a+ 74</a>]<BR>marks, explaining or interpreting signs, relating to a<BR>sign or mark, indicative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0864-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षा
लाक्षा लाक्षा, f. (probably a later form of<BR>राक्षा, and perhaps connected with राग fr. rt.<BR>रञ्ज्, to dye; according to some connected with<BR>लक्ष, from the thousands of insects forming the<BR>red dye), a species of plant (Ved.); a kind of red<BR>dye, lac (obtained from the cochineal insect or a<BR>similar insect as well as from the resin of a particular<BR>tree; according to some the nest of the insect is<BR>formed of a resinous substance used as sealing-wax<BR>and commonly termed Shel-lac); the insect or animal<BR>which produces the red dye.<BR>—लाक्षा-तरु, उस्, m.<BR>the tree Butea Frondosa (the insect being especially<BR>found in this tree).<BR>—लाक्षा-प्रसाद or लाक्षा-<BR>प्रसादन, अस्, m. the red Lodh tree (an astringent<BR>infusion prepared from its bark is used to fix colour<BR>in dyeing).<BR>—लाक्षा-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, coloured or<BR>dyed with lac.<BR>—लाक्षा-वृक्ष, अस्, m. Butea<BR>Frondosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षिक
लाक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to lac, coloured or<BR>dyed with lac, made of lac; relating to a large num-<BR>ber or to a lac, (in this sense fr. लक्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षेय
लाक्षेय लाक्षेय, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्ष्म
लाक्ष्म लाक्ष्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लक्ष्मी), ad-<BR>dressed to Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्ष्मण
लाक्ष्मण लाक्ष्मण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लक्ष्-<BR>मण), relating to the plant Lakṣmaṇā; (अस्), m. a<BR>patronymic from Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्ष्मणि
लाक्ष्मणि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्ष्मणेय
लाक्ष्मणेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Lakṣ-<BR>maṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्ष्यिक
लाक्ष्यिक लाक्ष्यिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = लक्ष्यम्<BR>अधीते वेद वा, Pāṇ. IV. 2, 60, Vārtt. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाख्
लाख् लाख् (= rt. राख्), cl. 1. P. लाखति,<BR>&c., to grow dry, be dry or arid; to<BR>adorn; to suffice, be competent; to prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लागुडिक
लागुडिक लागुडिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लगुड),<BR>armed with a club; (अस्), m. a sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघ्
लाघ् लाघ् (= rt. राघ्), cl. 1. A. ला-<BR>घते, &c., to be able or equal to, to<BR>be competent or suffice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघरकोलस|लाघरकोलसः
लाघरकोलस लाघरकोलस, अस्, m. a par-<BR>ticular form of jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघव|लाघवं
लाघव लाघव, अम्, n. (fr. लघु), quick-<BR>ness, swiftness, rapidity, speed; lightness, levity;<BR>activity, alacrity, versatility, dexterity, readiness; ease,<BR>facility; health; littleness, smallness, minuteness,<BR>delicacy, fineness; insignificance, unimportance,<BR>meanness; frivolity, inconsiderateness, rashness; (in<BR>prosody) shortness of a vowel or syllable; shortness<BR>of expression, brevity, conciseness; making light<BR>of, undervaluing, slighting, slight, disrespect, con-<BR>tempt, disgrace.<BR>—लाघवान्वित (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, possessed of brevity.<BR>—लाघवायन (˚व-आय्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघविक
लाघविक, अस्, ई, अम्, being quick or light, being<BR>short or brief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्काकायनि
लाङ्काकायनि लाङ्काकायनि, इस्, m. a metro-<BR>nymic from Laṅkā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्कायन
लाङ्कायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Laṅka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गल|लांगल|लांगलं|लाङ्गलं|लाङ्गलः
लाङ्गल लाङ्गल, अम्, n. (probably con-<BR>nected with rt. लग्; according to Uṇādi-s. I. 108.<BR>fr. rt. लङ्ग्), a plough; a particular appearance pre-<BR>sented by the moon; a plough-shaped beam or<BR>timber (used in the construction of a house); the<BR>palm tree; a kind of flower; membrum virile, (pro-<BR>bably incorrect for लाङ्गूल); (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>rice; N. of a son of Śuddhoda and grandson of<BR>Śākya; (ई), f., N. of various plants, Jussiæa Repens;<BR>Hemionitis Cordifolia; Rubia Munjista; Hedysarum<BR>Lagopodioides; = लाङ्गलिन्, the cocoa-nut tree; N. of<BR>a river.<BR>—लाङ्गल-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘plough-holder,’<BR>a ploughman, cultivator, peasant.<BR>—लाङ्गल-ग्र-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">Page0865-b+ 77</a>]<BR>हण, अम्, n. the act of holding or guiding the<BR>plough, ploughing.<BR>—लाङ्गल-चक्र, अम्, n. a par-<BR>ticular plough-shaped diagram.<BR>—लाङ्गल-दण्ड or<BR>लाङ्गल-दण्डक, अस्, m. the pole or beam of a<BR>plough.<BR>—लाङ्गल-ध्वज, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>plough for an ensign or characteristic; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of Bala-rāma, (see लाङ्गलिन्.)<BR>—लाङ्गल-पद्धति,<BR>इस्, f. a plough's path or line, furrow.<BR>—लाङ्गल-<BR>फाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a ploughshare.<BR>—लाङ्गलाख्य<BR>(˚ल-आख्˚) or लाङ्गलाह्वय (˚ल-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘plough-named, called after a plough,’ (a term ap-<BR>plied to the plant Jussiæa Repens; probably आ, f.)<BR>—लाङ्गलापकर्षिन् (˚ल-अप्˚), ई, इणी, इ, draw-<BR>ing the plough (said of an ox).<BR>—लाङ्गलीषा<BR>(˚ल-ईषा, anomalous), f. the pole of a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलक
लाङ्गलक at the end of a comp. = लाङ्गल, a<BR>plough; (अस्), m. a plough-shaped incision (in sur-<BR>gery); (इका,-इकी), f. = लाङ्गली, Jussiæa Repens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलायन
लाङ्गलायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Lāṅgala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलि|लांगलि
लाङ्गलि, इस्, m. (fr. लाङ्गल), a patronymic, N.<BR>of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलिक|लांगलिक|लाङ्गलिकः
लाङ्गलिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to a<BR>plough; (अस्), m. epithet of a particular vegetable<BR>poison; (ई), f. Methonica Superba; [cf. लाङ्गलिकी<BR>under लाङ्गलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलिन्|लांगलिन्
लाङ्गलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with or possessing<BR>a plough; (ई), m., N. of Bala-deva (who is repre-<BR>sented as armed with a ploughshare); N. of a pre-<BR>ceptor; the cocoa-nut tree; a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गुल|लांगुल|लांगुलं|लाङ्गुलं
लाङ्गुल लाङ्गुल, अम्, n. (probably fr. rt.<BR>लग्; but see लाङ्गूल), a tail; membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गुलिका
लाङ्गुलिका, f. Uraria Lagopodioides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गुलिनी
लाङ्गुलिनी, f., N. of a river; [cf. लाङ्गूलिनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गूल|लांगूल|लांगूलं|लाङ्गूलं
लाङ्गूल, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 90.<BR>fr. rt. लङ्ग्), a tail, a hairy tail; membrum virile;<BR>a granary?; (ई), f. Uraria Lagopodioides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गूलिका
लाङ्गूलिका, f. Hemionitis Cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गूलिन्|लांगूलिन्
लाङ्गूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, tailed, having a tail; (ई), m.<BR>a monkey, ape; a kind of medicinal plant; (इनी),<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज्
लाज् लाज् or लाञ्ज् [cf. rt. 2. लज्], cl. 1. P.<BR>लाजति (in Nirukta VI. 9. लाजते), लाञ्-<BR>जति, &c., to fry, roast, parch; to blame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज|लाजं|लाजः
लाज, अस्, m. (supposed by some to be connected<BR>with rt. 1. भ्रज्ज् or भृज्), fried or parched grain;<BR>wetted or sprinkled grain; (आस्), m. pl. parched or<BR>roasted grain, (also आ, f.); (अम्), n. the root of<BR>Andropogon Muricatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाजि
लाजि, इस्, m., Ved. a quantity of parched grain,<BR>(according to a commentator on Taittirīya-Brāhmaṇa<BR>III. 9, 4, 8, लाजि is voc. c. fr. लाजिन् = लाजोपल-<BR>क्षित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाजी
लाजी, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छ्|लांछ्
लाञ्छ् लाञ्छ् (connected with rt. लक्ष्,<BR>from which it is probably corrupted;<BR>cf. rt. लछ्), cl. 1. P. लाञ्छति, ललाञ्छ, &c., to<BR>mark, distinguish, decorate, deck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छन|लांछन|लांछनं|लाञ्छनं|लाञ्छनः
लाञ्छन, अम्, n. a mark, sign, token, spot; a<BR>landmark; a mark of ignominy, stain, spot; a name,<BR>appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छित|लांछित
लाञ्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, marked, distinguished, cha-<BR>racterized, designated; decorated, decked; furnished<BR>with (with inst. or at the end of a comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्ज्|लांज्
लाञ्ज् लाञ्ज् = rt. लाज् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाट|लाटः
लाट लाट, आस्, m. pl. (according to some<BR>formed fr. राष्ट्र), N. of a people and of the<BR>district inhabited by them (= Λαρικη of Ptolemy);<BR>(अस्), m. a king of the Lāṭas; clothes, dress; old or<BR>worn-out clothes, shabby ornaments, &c.; idle or<BR>childish language; repetition of words in the same<BR>sense but in a different application; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>relating to the Lāṭas, of or belonging to Lāṭa; old,<BR>worn, spoiled, &c.<BR>—लाटाचार्य (˚ट-आच्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the teacher of the Lāṭas, N. of an astronomer.<BR>—ला-<BR>टानुप्रास (˚ट-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘Lāṭa-repetition,’ the<BR>repetition of a word in the same sense but with a<BR>different application, (see लाटक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाटक
लाटक, अस्, इका, अम्, of or belonging to the<BR>Lāṭas, customary among them; (इका), f. a particular<BR>style of speech or composition, (see रीति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाटीय
लाटीय, अस्, आ, अम्, = लाटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाट्य
लाट्य लाट्य, Nom. P. लाट्यति, &c., to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाट्यायन
लाट्यायन लाट्यायन, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of a Sūtra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाड्
लाड् लाड् (= rt. लड्), cl. 10. P. लाडयति,<BR>लाडापयति, &c., to toss, throw; to<BR>blame, reproach; to fondle, cherish, caress, &c. (=<BR>लालयति, see rt. लल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाड
लाड लाड, अस्, m. a proper N.; N. of a<BR>royal race.<BR>—लाड-खान, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाडन
लाडन, अस्, m. a proper N.; (अम्), n. a various<BR>reading for लालन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाडम
लाडम लाडम, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाडि
लाडि लाडि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाण्ठनी|लांठनी
लाण्ठनी लाण्ठनी (?), f. = कुलटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लात
लात लात, लाति, &c. See rt. 1. ला, p. 864.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लातव्य
लातव्य लातव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Latu; N. of a chamberlain (in the Vikramorvaśī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लान्त
लान्त लान्त, अस्, m. a mystical term for<BR>the letter व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लान्तकज
लान्तकज लान्तक-ज, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>class of deities (with Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लान्द्र
लान्द्र लान्द्र, लान्द्रक, see Gaṇa Yāvādi<BR>to Pāṇ. V. 4, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाप|लापः
लाप लाप, लापिन्, &c. See p. 861, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाब|लाबः
लाब लाब (often written लाव), अस्, m. =<BR>लब, a sort of quail, Perdix Chinensis; (आ), f. the<BR>female of this bird.<BR>—लाबाक्ष (˚ब-अक्˚) or ला-<BR>बाक्षक, अस्, m. ‘quail-eyed,’ a kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाबक|लाबकः
लाबक, अस्, m. a sort of quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाबु|लाबुः
लाबु लाबु or लाबू = अ-लाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाबुकी
लाबुकी, f. a kind of lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाबुकायन|लाबुकायनः
लाबुकायन लाबुकायन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>philosophical writer mentioned in the Jaimini-sūtras,<BR>(probably incorrect for लामकायन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ्
लाभ् लाभ्, cl. 10. P. लाभयति, &c.,<BR>to throw, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ|लाभः
लाभ लाभ, &c. See p. 862, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लामकायन
लामकायन लामकायन, अस्, m. (fr. लमक),<BR>a patronymic; N. of a preceptor; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>descendants of Lamaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लामकायनि
लामकायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लामकायनिन्
लामकायनिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the school of Lāma-<BR>kāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लामगायनि
लामगायनि, इस्, m. = लामकायनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लामज्जक|लामज्जकं
लामज्जक लामज्जक, अम्, n. the root of the<BR>fragrant grass Andropogon Muricatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाम्पट्य|लांपट्य|लांपट्यं
लाम्पट्य लाम्पट्य, अम्, n. (fr. लम्पट),<BR>lasciviousness, lustfulness, lewdness, dissoluteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लायक
लायक लायक. See p. 868, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लायम्
लायम् लायम्, a word of uncertain mean-<BR>ing in Ṛg-veda X. 42, 1, (perhaps an indec. part.<BR>fr. rt. 1. ली), having bent down, bending; (according<BR>to Sāy.) = संश्लेषणम् = हृदय-वेधिनं<BR>शरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाल
लाल लाल, लालक, लालित, &c. See p. 863,<BR>cols. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालप्यमान
लालप्यमान लालप्यमान. See p. 861,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालस|लालसः
लालस लालस, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. 1. लस्, but probably connected also with rt.<BR>लष्), eagerly longing for, ardently desirous of, eager<BR>after; finding pleasure in, devoted to, totally given<BR>up to [cf. शोक-ल्˚]; (अस्, आ), m. f. longing or ardent<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">Page0866-a+ 70</a>]<BR>desire, eagerness; regret, sorrow; asking, soliciting;<BR>the longing of a pregnant woman; dalliance?; (आ),<BR>f. a particular metre, four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯˘¯¯,<BR>˘¯¯˘¯¯˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0865-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालसीक|लालसीकं
लालसीक, अम्, n. sauce, gravy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाट
लालाट लालाट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ललाट), being<BR>in or on the forehead, relating to it, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाटि
लालाटि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाटिक|लालाटिकः
लालाटिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the forehead,<BR>being on the forehead; relating to fate, arising from<BR>destiny; looking attentively at the forehead (of a<BR>master), attentive; useless, low, vile; (अस्), m. an atten-<BR>tive servant, one who watches a master's countenance<BR>and learns by it what is necessary to be done; one<BR>who is unfit for work (as depending too much on<BR>the look of his superior), a careless person or idler<BR>(perhaps as always gazing at the countenances of<BR>others); a mode of embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाटी
लालाटी, f. = ललाट, the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालामिक
लालामिक लालामिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = ललामं<BR>गृह्णाति, Pāṇ. IV. 4, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालिक|लालिकः
लालिक लालिक. See p. 863, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालुका
लालुका लालुका, f. a sort of necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव|लावः
लाव लाव. See p. 870, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण|लावणं
लावण लावण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लवण), saline,<BR>salt, salted, cooked or dressed with salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावणिक|लावणिकं|लावणिकः
लावणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to salt, impregnated<BR>with salt, prepared or dressed with salt, salted; deal-<BR>ing in salt; lovely, beautiful, graceful; (अस्), m. a<BR>dealer in salt, salt merchant; (अम्), n. a vessel holding<BR>salt, salt-cellar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्य|लावण्यं
लावण्य, अम्, n. saltness, the taste or property of<BR>salt; beauty, loveliness, charm.<BR>—लावण्य-कलित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with beauty.<BR>—लावण्य-मञ्-<BR>जरी, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—लावण्य-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, full of taste, full of loveliness or beauty, lovely,<BR>beautiful, handsome.<BR>—लावण्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessed of beauty or grace, beautiful, lovely; (अती),<BR>f., N. of various women.<BR>—लावण्य-श्री, ईस्, f.<BR>‘wealth of beauty,’ great beauty.<BR>—लावण्यार्जित<BR>(˚य-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, obtained through beauty;<BR>(अम्), n. the private property of a married woman<BR>(consisting of that which has been presented to her<BR>at her marriage as a token of respect or kindness or<BR>by her father or mother-in-law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावाणक|लावाणकः
लावाणक लावाणक, अस्, m., N. of a district<BR>adjacent to Magadha, (sometimes incorrectly written<BR>लावानक); N. of the third Lambaka of the Kathā-<BR>sarit-sāgara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाविक|लाविकः
लाविक लाविक, अस्, m. = लालिक, a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावु|लावुः
लावु लावु, लावू, &c. See लाबु, &c., p. 865,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावेरणि
लावेरणि लावेरणि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावेरणीय
लावेरणीय, see Gaṇa Gahādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव्य
लाव्य लाव्य. See p. 870, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाषुक
लाषुक लाषुक, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. rt. लष्),<BR>covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास|लासः
लास लास, लासिन्, लास्य. See p. 864.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्फोटनी
लास्फोटनी लास्फोटनी, f. a gimlet, auger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाहरिमल्ल
लाहरिमल्ल लाहरिमल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाह्य
लाह्य लाह्य, अस्, m. (fr. लह्य), a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाह्यायनि
लाह्यायनि, इस्, m. (fr. लाह्य), a patronymic of<BR>Bhujyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लि|लिः
लि लि, इस्, m. (a doubtful word, meaning<BR>according to some) weariness, fatigue; loss, destruc-<BR>tion; end, term; equality, sameness; a bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिकुच|लिकुचं|लिकुचः
लिकुच लिकुच, अस्, m. = लकुच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्षा
लिक्षा लिक्षा, f. (also written लिक्का), a nit,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">Page0866-b+ 80</a>]<BR>young louse, the egg of a louse; a minute measure<BR>of weight, (according to some, a poppy seed or =<BR>8 Trasa-reṇus or motes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्षिका
लिक्षिका, f. = लिक्षा, a nit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख्य|लिख्यः
लिख्य, अस्, m. a nit, the egg of a louse; (आ), f.<BR>a nit; a minute measure of weight; [cf. लिक्षा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख्
लिख् लिख् (the original form of this<BR>rt. was probably रिख्, q. v.), cl. 6. P.<BR>लिखति (according to some also A. लिखते), लिलेख,<BR>लेखिष्यति, अलेखीत्, लेखितुम् or लिखितुम्, to<BR>scratch, scrape, furrow, tear up, scarify, lance; to<BR>pick, peck (said of birds); to scratch or make an<BR>incision in or on, draw a line or streak, make a<BR>mark or sign, write, copy, write down, engrave, in-<BR>scribe; to sketch, trace, portray, draw, delineate,<BR>depict, draw a picture, paint; to make smooth,<BR>polish; to graze, touch; to unite sexually with a<BR>female: Pass. लिख्यते, Aor. अलेखि, to be written:<BR>Caus. लेखयति (also, according to some, लिखाप-<BR>यति), Aor. अलीलिखत्, to cause to scratch or write,<BR>&c.; to scratch; to write: Desid. लिलिखिषति, लि-<BR>लेखिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख|लिखः
लिख, अस्, आ, अम्, scratching, writing; a writer,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखत्
लिखत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, scratching, writing,<BR>&c.; painting, delineating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखन|लिखनं
लिखन, अम्, n. the act of scratching; writing,<BR>inscribing; a writing, written document, manuscript,<BR>scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखित|लिखितं|लिखितः
लिखित, अस्, आ, अम्, scratched, scraped, scarified;<BR>written; drawn, delineated, portrayed, sketched,<BR>traced, painted; (अस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi and author<BR>of a work on law (frequently mentioned together<BR>with Śaṅkha, q. v.); N. of Śaṅkha's brother, whose<BR>hands were cut off by king Su-dyumna as a punish-<BR>ment for eating some fruit without leave (described<BR>in Śānti-p. 668); (अम्), n. a writing, written docu-<BR>ment or composition, book, scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखित्वा
लिखित्वा, ind. having scratched; having written<BR>or delineated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख|लेखः
लेख, अस्, m. [cf. रेख], a writing, letter, epistle,<BR>manuscript, document, written document of any kind,<BR>(कूट-लेख, a spurious or forged document); a<BR>god, deity; a proper N.; (आ), f. a scratch, streak,<BR>line, (गण्ड-लेखा, ‘cheek-line,’ the outline of the<BR>cheek; cf. विद्युल्-ल्˚); stripe, stroke, furrow, row,<BR>groove; writing, handwriting, drawing lines, deline-<BR>ation, drawing, painting; a drawing, likeness, repre-<BR>sentation, figure, impression, mark; the curved line<BR>or pale streak of the young moon (when only faintly<BR>discernible), the moon's crescent; hem, border, rim,<BR>brim, edge, the horizon; = शिखा, चूडाग्र; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a class of gods under Manu Cākṣuṣa.<BR>—लेख-पत्त्र, अम्, n. or लेख-पत्त्रिका, f. a<BR>written document, writing, letter, epistle; writ, deed.<BR>—लेख-प्रतिलेख-लिपि, इस्, f. a particular kind of<BR>writing.<BR>—लेखर्षभ (˚ख-ऋष्), अस्, m. ‘best<BR>of deities, ‘N. of Indra.<BR>—लेख-सन्देश-हारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, taking or conveying a written message or<BR>instructions.<BR>—लेख-हार or लेख-हारक, अस्,<BR>m. a letter-carrier, the bearer of a letter.<BR>—लेख-<BR>हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking or conveying a letter.<BR>—ले-<BR>खाक्षर (˚ख-अक्˚), अम्, n. writing, (opposed to<BR>आलेख्य, painting.)<BR>—लेखाधिकारिन् (˚ख-अध्˚),<BR>ई, m. ‘presiding over written documents,’ a king's<BR>secretary.<BR>—लेखाभ्र (˚ख-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man; (आस्), m. pl. his descendants.<BR>—लेखा-भ्रू,<BR>ऊस्, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—लेखार्ह (˚ख-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘fit for writing on,’ a kind of palm tree (the<BR>leaves of which are used for writing on).<BR>—लेखा-<BR>वलय, अस्, अम्, m. n. an encircling line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखक|लेखकः
लेखक, अस्, m. a writer, scribe, copyist, clerk,<BR>amanuensis, secretary; one who delineates or paints;<BR>writing down, transcribing, (in this sense perhaps<BR>अम्, n.)<BR>—लेखक-प्रमाद, अस्, m. an error or<BR>mistake of a copyist.<BR>—लेखक-मुक्ता-मणि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘pearl-gem for scribes,’ N. of a treatise on the<BR>art of writing by Hari-dāsa (especially intended for<BR>scribes belonging to a royal court).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखन|लेखनं|लेखनः
लेखन, अस्, ई, अम्, scratching, scraping, scarify-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">Page0866-c+ 76</a>]<BR>ing, making an incision, lancing; writing; exciting,<BR>stimulating; (अस्), m. Saccharum Spontaneum, a sort<BR>of grass or reed of which pens are made; (ई), f. an<BR>instrument for writing, a writing-reed, pen, style,<BR>(also written लेखनि when required by the metre);<BR>a spoon, ladle; (अम्), n. the act of scratching or<BR>scraping; cutting or making incisions (in surgery);<BR>scarifying; the act of writing or writing down, tran-<BR>scribing, copying; scripture; an instrument or im-<BR>plement for scraping or furrowing; a kind of birch<BR>the bark of which is used for writing on [cf. भूर्ज],<BR>the leaf of the palm tree used for the same purpose;<BR>grazing, touching, coming in contact (said of heavenly<BR>bodies); thinning, attenuating, reducing corpulency.<BR>—लेखन-वस्ति, इस्, f. a kind of clyster or enema<BR>for thinning or reducing corpulency.<BR>—लेखन-सा-<BR>धन, अम्, n. writing materials.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनि
लेखनि. See under लेखन above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनिक|लेखनिकः
लेखनिक, अस्, m. one who makes another sign<BR>a document instead of himself, signing by proxy, or<BR>making a mark (from inability to write); the bearer<BR>of a letter, a letter-carrier, postman, express.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनिका
लेखनिका in चित्र-ल्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनीय|लेखनीयः
लेखनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be written; to be drawn<BR>or painted; serving as a scraper or as a lancet, &c.;<BR>(अम्), n. an accusation or defence in law (required to<BR>be given in writing) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखाय
लेखाय, Nom. P. लेखायति, &c., to be wanton,<BR>sport wantonly; to waver, totter, stumble, slip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखित|लेखितं
लेखित, अस्, आ, अम्, scratched, written, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखित्वा
लेखित्वा, ind. = लिखित्वा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखिन्
लेखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, scratching, scraping; writing;<BR>grazing, touching; (इनी), f. a spoon, ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्य|लेख्यं
1. लेख्य, Nom. P. लेख्यति, &c., = लेखाय<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्य|लेख्यं
2. लेख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be scratched or scraped,<BR>to be scarified; to be written or transcribed, proper<BR>to be written; to be drawn or painted; portrayed,<BR>painted; to be written down or numbered among<BR>(loc.); (अम्), n. writing, the art of writing; copying,<BR>transcribing; delineation, drawing, painting; a writ-<BR>ing, document, letter, manuscript; a written accusa-<BR>tion or defence; an inscription; a painted figure.<BR>—लेख्य-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done in writing, signed,<BR>executed.<BR>—लेख्य-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, represented<BR>in painting, painted.<BR>—लेख्य-चूर्णिका, f. a writing-<BR>pencil, drawing-pencil, paint-brush.<BR>—लेख्य-पत्त्र<BR>or लेख्य-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. the palmyra or palm<BR>tree; (अम्), n. a palm leaf for writing on; a written<BR>paper, writing, letter.<BR>—लेख्य-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>a written contract, record, document.<BR>—लेख्य-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, delineated, painted.<BR>—लेख्य-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. a writing place, office.<BR>—लेख्या-<BR>रूढ (˚य-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, committed to writing,<BR>recorded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यक
लेख्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, written, epistolary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखिखिल्ल
लिखिखिल्ल लिखिखिल्ल (?) अस्, m. a pea-<BR>cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख्य|लिख्यः
लिख्य लिख्य. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ख्|लिंख्
लिङ्ख् लिङ्ख् (= rt. लख्), cl. 1. P. लिङ्-<BR>खति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिगु|लिगुः
लिगु लिगु, उ, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 37.<BR>fr. rt. लग्), the mind, heart; (उस्), m. a fool, block-<BR>head; a deer; part of the earth; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्
लिङ् लिङ्, a technical term in grammar for<BR>the terminations of the Potential and Precative or<BR>for these Moods themselves (the Precative being<BR>usually distinguished by the fuller term लिङ् आशिषि or<BR>आशिर्-लिङ्).<BR>—लिङ्-अर्थ-वाद, अस्, m. ‘explanation of<BR>the sense of Liṅ, ‘N. of a grammatical treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्कवाराहतीर्थ
लिङ्कवाराहतीर्थ लिङ्क-वाराह-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ग्|लिंग्
लिङ्ग् लिङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. लिङ्गति, &c., to<BR>go; cl. 10. P. लिङ्गयति, &c. (more<BR>properly regarded as a Nom. fr. लिङ्ग, p. 867), to<BR>change or inflect a noun according to its gender;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-a" target="_blank">Page0867-a+ 81</a>]<BR>to paint, variegate; [cf. probably Old Germ. hring,<BR>hringjan; Angl. Sax. hring.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0866-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ग|लिंग|लिंगं|लिङ्गं
लिङ्ग, अम्, n. (perhaps connected with rt. लग्),<BR>a mark, sign, token, emblem, badge, anything which<BR>distinguishes or defines, distinguishing or discrimi-<BR>nating mark, characteristic mark, characteristic, sec-<BR>tarian mark; a symptom, mark of disease; a false<BR>badge, any badge or mark assumed with a view to<BR>deceive; a spot, stain; a proof, evidence, means of<BR>proof, proof from a sure sign or token; (in logic)<BR>= व्याप्य, the predicate of a proposition or the<BR>mark which characterizes the subject (as in the pro-<BR>position ‘there is fire because there is smoke, and<BR>fire has smoke, ‘smoke is the लिङ्ग), inference,<BR>conclusion, reason, (काव्य-लिङ्ग, a particular figure<BR>of speech in which the grounds of a statement are<BR>explained after the statement has been made); the<BR>sign of gender or sex, organ of generation; gender<BR>(in grammar, cf. पुं-लिङ्ग); the male organ;<BR>Śiva's genital organ or Śiva worshipped in the form<BR>of a Phallus, (this is usually of stone or marble, and<BR>set up in temples appropriated to Śiva; there were<BR>formerly twelve principal Śiva-liṅgas in India, of<BR>which two or three of the best known are Soma-nātha<BR>in Gujarāt, Mahākāla at Ujjayinī, Viśveśvara at Be-<BR>nares, &c.); the image of a god, an idol; the subtile<BR>frame or body which is not destroyed by death, the<BR>indestructible original of the gross or visible body<BR>[cf. लिङ्ग-शरीर, सूक्ष्म-श्˚]; = प्रातिपदिक, a<BR>nominal base, the crude form or base of a noun<BR>(shortened by Vopa-deva into लि); (according to<BR>some) Prakṛti or Pradhāna (i. e. the primary germ<BR>out of which all phenomena are evolved in the<BR>Sāṅkhya phil.); the effect or product (i. e. according<BR>to others, that which is evolved out of a primary<BR>cause, and becomes in its turn a producer, = व्यक्त<BR>in the Sāṅkhya phil.); the order of the religious<BR>student; N. of a Purāṇa, (see लिङ्ग-पुराण.)<BR>—लिङ्ग-जा, f. a kind of plant (= लिङ्गिनी).<BR>—लिङ्ग-<BR>तस्, ind. from a mark or sign, according to marks,<BR>&c.<BR>—लिङ्गतो-भद्र, अम्, n. epithet of a parti-<BR>cular magical circle.<BR>—लिङ्ग-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>of being a Liṅga or mark, &c.<BR>—लिङ्ग-देह, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. the subtile or primary body, see लिङ्ग-<BR>शरीर.<BR>—लिङ्ग-द्वादश-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>particular religious ceremony.<BR>—लिङ्ग-धर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, wearing marks, carrying distinctive signs,<BR>(मिथ्या-लिङ्गधर, wearing false marks, a hypo-<BR>crite; cf. सुहृल्-ल्˚.)<BR>—लिङ्ग-धारण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>wearing a badge; (अम्), n. the act of wearing a<BR>badge or any characteristic mark, the wearing of<BR>a Liṅga or Phallus.<BR>—लिङ्ग-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wear-<BR>ing a badge, wearing the Liṅga of Śiva; (ई), m. =<BR>लिङ्ग-वत्, q. v.; (इणी), f., N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in<BR>Naimiṣa.<BR>—लिङ्ग-नाश, अस्, m. loss of character-<BR>istic marks; a particular disease of the eyes, (loss of<BR>vision from cataract &c., considered to be a discolora-<BR>tion of the pupil); loss of the penis.<BR>—लिङ्ग-प-<BR>रामर्श, अस्, m. the groping after or seeking for<BR>a sign or token (in logic), the consideration of a sign<BR>or characteristic (as that smokiness is a sign of fire).<BR>—लिङ्ग-पीठ, अम्, n. the pedestal of a Liṅga.<BR>—लिङ्ग-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of one of the eigh-<BR>teen Purāṇas (in which Śiva, supposed to be present<BR>in the Agni-liṅga or great fiery Liṅga, gives an<BR>account of the creation &c. as well as of his own<BR>incarnations in opposition to those of Viṣṇu).<BR>—लिङ्ग-प्रतिष्ठा-विधि, इस्, m. rules for the<BR>establishment of a Liṅga.<BR>—लिङ्ग-माहात्म्य, अम्,<BR>n. the majesty or pre-eminence of the Liṅga, N. of<BR>a section of several Purāṇas.<BR>—लिङ्ग-मूर्ति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, having the form of the Phallus (said of Śiva).<BR>—लिङ्ग-लेप, अस्, m., N. of a particular disease.<BR>—लिङ्ग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having marks, possessed<BR>of signs or tokens; having various sexes or genders;<BR>furnished with a Liṅga or wearing a small repre-<BR>sentation of the Liṅga of Śiva round the neck or on<BR>one arm (applied as an epithet to a particular Śaiva<BR>sect, also called Jaṅgamas).<BR>—लिङ्ग-वर्धन, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, causing erections of the male organ; (अस्),<BR>m. Feronia Elephantum.<BR>—लिङ्ग-वर्धिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">Page0867-b+ 77</a>]<BR>ई, causing erections; (इनी), f. Achyranthes Aspera.<BR>—लिङ्ग-विपर्यय, अस्, m. change of gender.<BR>—लिङ्ग-विशेष-विधि, इस्, m. rules for the different<BR>genders, N. of a grammatical treatise ascribed to<BR>Vara-ruci.<BR>—लिङ्ग-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, making a live-<BR>lihood by false appearance or assumed outward marks,<BR>hypocritical; (इस्), m. a religious hypocrite, one who<BR>assumes the dress &c. of an ascetic to gain a liveli-<BR>hood.<BR>—लिङ्ग-वेदी, f. the pedestal of a Liṅga.<BR>—लिङ्ग-शरीर, अम्, n. the subtile body which<BR>accompanies the grosser in all its transmigrations and<BR>is not destroyed by death.<BR>—लिङ्ग-शास्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>a grammatical treatise on gender.<BR>—लिङ्ग-सम्-<BR>भूता, f., N. of a particular plant.<BR>—लिङ्ग-स्थ, अस्,<BR>m. a religious student.<BR>—लिङ्ग-हनी, f. = मूर्वा.<BR>—लिङ्गाग्र (˚ग-अग्˚), अस्, m. glans penis.<BR>—लिङ्-<BR>गानुशासन (˚ग-अन्˚), अम्, n. the doctrine or laws<BR>of grammatical gender.<BR>—लिङ्गार्चन (˚ग-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. worship of the Liṅga or Phallus.<BR>—लिङ्गार्-<BR>चन-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—लिङ्-<BR>गार्चा-प्रतिष्ठा-विधि (˚ग-अर्˚), इस्, m., N. of<BR>a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गक|लिंगक|लिंगकः|लिङ्गकः
लिङ्गक at the end of an adj. comp. = लिङ्ग;<BR>(अस्), m. the elephant or wood apple, Feronia Ele-<BR>phantum; [cf. लिङ्ग-वर्धन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गन|लिंगन|लिंगनं
लिङ्गन, अम्, n. = आ-लिङ्गन, embracing, an<BR>embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गिन्|लिंगिन्
लिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a mark or sign, wearing<BR>a distinguishing mark; having the character of,<BR>characterized by (at the end of a comp.); wearing<BR>or bearing the insignia (of any office or character),<BR>bearing false marks or signs, a hypocrite; only<BR>having the appearance or acting the part of (at the<BR>end of a comp.; cf. द्विज-ल्˚); having a right to<BR>wear signs or badges, one whose external appearance<BR>corresponds with his inner character; possessing or<BR>furnished with a Liṅga; having a subtile body; (ई),<BR>m. a Brāhman of a particular order, a religious<BR>student, an ascetic; N. of Parameśvara (as the sus-<BR>tainer of Liṅga or Pradhāna, cf. लिङ्ग, col. 1); a<BR>worshipper of Śiva in the Phallic type; a hypocrite<BR>or pretended devotee; = व्यापक, the subject of a<BR>proposition, that which possesses a characteristic mark<BR>(as in the proposition ‘there is fire because there is<BR>smoke, and fire has smoke, ‘fire is the लिङ्गिन्); the<BR>cause or source (i. e. that original substance into<BR>which a Liṅga is resolved, see under लिङ्ग); an<BR>elephant; (इनस्), m. pl., N. of a particular Śaiva<BR>sect [cf. लिङ्ग-वत्]; (इनी), f. a particular plant.<BR>—लिङ्गि-वेष, अस्, m. the dress or the insignia of<BR>a religious student (the skin, staff, bowl, &c.), the<BR>dress or appearance of a follower of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ग्य
लिङ्ग्य, ind. = 2. आ-लिङ्ग्य, having embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गालिका
लिङ्गालिका लिङ्गालिका, f. a kind of mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिच्छवि|लिच्छविः
लिच्छवि लिच्छवि, N. of a regal race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिट्
लिट् लिट्, a technical term in grammar for<BR>the terminations of the Reduplicated Perfect tense or<BR>for this tense itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिट्य
लिट्य लिट्य, Nom. P. लिट्यति, &c., to be<BR>little; to think little of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिधु
लिधु लि-धु, (in grammar) a technical<BR>term for Nominal verbs, (said to be a contraction of<BR>लिङ्ग, ‘the crude base of a noun,’ and धातु, ‘a<BR>root.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिन्दु|लिंदु
लिन्दु लिन्दु, Ved. = पिच्छल, slimy, slip-<BR>pery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्
लिप् लिप् (the later and classical form<BR>of rt. रिप्), cl. 6. P. A. लिम्पति, -ते,<BR>लिलेप, लिलिपे, लेप्स्यति, -ते, अलिपत्, अलिपत or<BR>अलिप्त, लेप्तुम्, to smear, besmear, anoint, daub,<BR>plaster, paint; to spread over, cover; to stain, soil,<BR>pollute, defile, contaminate; to inflame, kindle,<BR>burn: Pass. लिप्यते, to be smeared or anointed; to<BR>stick, cleave, adhere to: Caus. लेपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अलीलिपत्, to cause to smear, &c.; to smear,<BR>anoint, cover; to cause to be covered or decorated:<BR>Desid. लिलिप्सति, -ते: Intens. लेलिप्यते, लेलेप्ति;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">Page0867-c+ 81</a>]<BR>[cf. Gr. λίπ-α, λίπ-ος, λιπαρό-ς, λιπ-αρ-ής, λιπαρ-έ-ω,<BR>ἀ-λείφ-ω, ἄλειφ-αρ, ἄλειφα, λισσός: Lat.<BR>limpidus, lippus, li-no, li-mus, de-libuo; probably<BR>also liquidus, liqueo: Old Germ. salba: Goth.<BR>salbôn: Angl. Sax. sealf: Slav. lep-i-ti, lep-u:<BR>Lith. limp-u, lip-ti, lip-u-s: Hib. laib, laibe,<BR>‘mire, clay.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप|लिपः
लिप, अस्, m. smearing, anointing, plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपि|लिपिः
लिपि, इस्, or लिपी, f. smearing, besmearing, anoint-<BR>ing, plastering, spreading over; painting, drawing;<BR>writing, transcribing, handwriting; the art of writing;<BR>written characters, the letters; a writing, written<BR>paper or book, manuscript, document, letter.<BR>—लिपि-<BR>कर, अस्, m. an anointer, white-washer, plasterer;<BR>a writer, scribe; an engraver.<BR>—लिपि-कार, अस्, m. a<BR>writer, scribe, copyist.<BR>—लिपि-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>understands writing, one who can write.<BR>—लिपि-<BR>न्यास, अस्, m. ‘the act of putting down written<BR>characters, ‘writing, transcribing.<BR>—लिपि-फलक,<BR>अम्, n. a writing-tablet, leaf for writing on.<BR>—लिपि-<BR>शाला, f. a writing-school.<BR>—लिपि-सङ्ख्या, f. a<BR>number of written characters.<BR>—लिपि-सज्जा, f. imple-<BR>ments or materials for writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिका
लिपिका, f. = लिपि, a writing, written paper, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्त|लिप्तं
1. लिप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. लिप्त see p. 868, col. 1),<BR>smeared, besmeared, anointed; stained, soiled, de-<BR>filed; smeared with poison, poisoned, envenomed;<BR>eaten.<BR>—लिप्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has smeared<BR>or anointed, &c.<BR>—लिप्त-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the hands smeared or stained.<BR>—लिप्ताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having the body anointed with<BR>unguents, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तक|लिप्तकः
लिप्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, smeared, covered with poison;<BR>(अस्), m. a poisoned arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्प|लिंप|लिंपः|लिम्पः
लिम्प, अस्, m. smearing, anointing, plastering;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of one of Śiva's attendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पट|लिंपट|लिम्पटः
लिम्पट, अस्, आ, अम्, libidinous, lustful, lecherous;<BR>(अस्), m. a libertine; [cf. लम्पट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पत्
लिम्पत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, smearing, anointing,<BR>plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पाक|लिंपाक|लिम्पाकं|लिंपाकः|लिम्पाकः
लिम्पाक, अस्, m. an ass; a citron or lime tree;<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of the lime tree, a citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पि|लिंपिः|लिम्पिः
लिम्पि, इस्, f. = लिपि, a writing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिवि|लिविः
लिवि, इस्, or लिवी, f. writing, transcribing, a writing,<BR>&c., = लिपि.<BR>—लिवि-कर or लिविङ्-कर, अस्, m. a<BR>writer, scribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप|लेपः
लेप, अस्, m. the act of smearing, besmearing,<BR>daubing, anointing, plastering, anything smeared<BR>on, salve, ointment, unguent, plaster, mortar, chu-<BR>nam, white-wash; a coating of paint, &c.; the<BR>wipings of the hand after offering funeral oblations<BR>to three ancestors, (these wipings being considered<BR>as an oblation to paternal ancestors in the fourth,<BR>fifth, and sixth degrees); impurity, dirt, any grease<BR>or dirt sticking to vessels, &c., a spot, stain, pollu-<BR>tion, defilement, moral impurity, sin; food, victuals.<BR>—लेप-कर, अस्, m. plaster-maker, mortar-maker<BR>or plasterer, bricklayer, white-washer.<BR>—लेप-का-<BR>मिनी, f. = अञ्जनी.<BR>—लेप-भागिन्, ई, m. ‘sharing<BR>the Lepa, ‘a paternal ancestor in the fourth, fifth,<BR>and sixth degrees (Manu III. 216).<BR>—लेप-भुज्,<BR>क्, m. ‘eating the Lepa,’ = लेप-भागिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपक|लेपकः
लेपक, अस्, m. a plasterer, bricklayer; one who<BR>moulds or models; (a form लेपक for लेप is found<BR>at the end of some comps., see अ-ल्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपन|लेपनं|लेपनः
लेपन, अस्, m. olibanum, incense; (अम्), n.<BR>the act of smearing, besmearing, daubing, spreading<BR>on; anything smeared on, salve, ointment, plaster,<BR>mortar, white-wash; flesh, meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपनीय
लेपनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be smeared or anointed,<BR>fit to be plastered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपिन्
लेपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, smearing or besmearing with,<BR>covering with; smeared with, covered with; (ई), m. a<BR>plasterer, bricklayer, one who moulds or models.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्य|लेप्यं
लेप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be smeared or anointed;<BR>to be defiled, to be spotted or stained; moulded,<BR>modeled; (अम्), n. plastering, spreading or smearing<BR>ointment or mortar, making models, moulding,<BR>modeling.<BR>—लेप्य-कृत्, त्, m. one who makes<BR>models, a bricklayer, plasterer.<BR>—लेप्य-नारी, f.<BR>(probably) a modeled figure of a woman.<BR>—लेप्य-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">Page0868-a+ 75</a>]<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of mortar or clay, moulded;<BR>(ई), f. a doll, puppet.<BR>—लेप्य-योषित्, त्, f. = लेप्य-<BR>नारी.<BR>—लेप्य-स्त्री, f. a woman covered with un-<BR>guents, a perfumed woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0867-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्त|लिप्तं
लिप्त 2. लिप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. V. 55. fr. rt. 1. ली; for 1. लिप्त see p. 867,<BR>col. 3), united, joined, connected, embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्ता
लिप्ता लिप्ता or लिप्तिका, f. a minute, the<BR>sixtieth part of a degree; [cf. Gr. λεπτός.]<BR>—लिप्ती-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., Ved. to reduce to minutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सा
लिप्सा लिप्सा, लिप्सु, लिप्स्य, &c. See p. 862,<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिबि|लिबिः
लिबि लिबि, लिबी, = लिवि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिबुजा
लिबुजा लिबुजा, f., Ved. a creeping plant,<BR>creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्प|लिंप|लिंपः|लिम्पः
लिम्प लिम्प, लिम्पि, &c. See p. 867, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्बभट्ट
लिम्बभट्ट लिम्ब-भट्ट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिश्
लिश् 1. लिश् (according to some a later<BR>form of rt. 1. रिश्), cl. 6. P. लिशति (ac-<BR>cording to some also A. लिशते), to tear off, hurt,<BR>injure, (in this sense only if identified with rt. 1. रिश्);<BR>to go, move; cl. 4. P. लिश्यति (also A. लिश्यते),<BR>लिलेश, लिलिशे, लेक्ष्यति, -ते, अलिक्षत्, अलिक्षत,<BR>लेष्टुम्, to be small, lessen, become small [cf. rts.<BR>कृश्, क्लिश्]: Caus. लेशयति, अलीलिशत्: Desid. लि-<BR>लिक्षते: Intens. लेलिश्यते, लेलेष्टि; [cf. Gr. ὀλί-<BR>γος, perhaps also λίγδος; Lith. lesas.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिश्
2. लिश्, ट्, ट्, ट्, (probably) one who tears off or<BR>injures, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिश
लिश, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) tearing, injuring, &c.;<BR>(see कुलिश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिष्ट
लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, lessened, decreased, reduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश|लेशः
लेश, अस्, m. smallness, littleness; a small part or<BR>portion, particle, atom, bit, little bit, slight trace, small<BR>quantity, little (frequently at the end of comps., cf.<BR>दण्ड-ल्˚, स्वेद-ल्˚); a particular division or short<BR>space of time (= 2 Kalās); epithet of a particular<BR>modulation of sound or melody; (in rhetoric) a par-<BR>ticular figure of speech, employment of a comparison<BR>instead of a direct statement; representing as a dis-<BR>advantage what is otherwise regarded as an advantage<BR>and vice versa; N. of a king (a son of Su-hotra).<BR>—लेशोक्त (˚श-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, briefly said, only<BR>hinted or insinuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश्या
लेश्या, f. light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टव्य
लेष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) to be torn off<BR>or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टु|लेष्टुः
लेष्टु, उस्, m. a clod, lump of earth; [cf. लोष्ट,<BR>लोष्टु.]<BR>—लेष्टु-घ्न or लेष्टु-भेदन, अस्, m.<BR>a clod-breaker, clod-crusher, a harrow or other agri-<BR>cultural implement used for breaking clods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिष्व|लिष्वः
लिष्व लिष्व, अस्, m. = लष्व, a dancer,<BR>actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह्
लिह् 1. लिह् (a later form of rt. रिह्), cl.<BR>2. P. A. लेढि, लीढे (2nd sing. P. ले-<BR>क्षि, 2nd and 3rd du. लीढस्), Impf. P. अलेट् or<BR>अलेड् (2nd sing. अलेट्, 2nd du. अलीढम्), Impv. P.<BR>लेढु (2nd sing. लीढि), लिलेह, लिलिहे, लेक्ष्यति,<BR>-ते, अलिक्षत्, अलिक्षत or अलीढ, लेढुम्, to<BR>lick; to lick up; to taste, sip, lap, take any food by<BR>licking or lapping: Pass. लिह्यते, Aor. अलेहि, to be<BR>licked, &c.: Caus. लेहयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलीलिहत्,<BR>to cause to lick: Desid. लिलिक्षति, -ते: Intens.<BR>लेलिह्यते, लेलेढि, to lick frequently, be constantly<BR>licking, play with the tongue, dart out the tongue;<BR>[cf. Gr. λείχ-ω, λιχ-μά-ω, λιχ-μά-ζ-ω, λιχ-ανό-ς,<BR>λίχ-νο-ς; Lat. li-n-g-o, lig-uri-o, pol-lex; Goth.<BR>bi-laigô-n; Old Germ. lecchôn; Angl. Sax. liccian;<BR>Slav. liz-a-ti; Lith. lez-iu, liz-u-s; Hib. lighim,<BR>im-lighim, ‘I lick.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह्
2. लिह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, licking, licking up, tasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह|लिहः
लिह in गो-लिह, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिहत्
लिहत्, अन्, अती, अत्, licking, licking up, tasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह्यमान
लिह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being licked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीढ|लीढः
लीढ, अस्, आ, अम्, licked, tasted, licked up, de-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">Page0868-b+ 80</a>]<BR>voured, eaten.<BR>—लीढ-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, tasted<BR>and ejected, rejected after being tasted; (a com-<BR>pound formed like दग्ध-प्ररूढ, ‘growing<BR>again after being burnt.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीढ्वा
लीढ्वा, ind. having licked or licked up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिह|लेलिहः
लेलिह, अस्, m. (fr. the Intens.), ‘constantly licking,’<BR>a kind of parasitical worm; a serpent, snake; (आ), f. a<BR>particular Mudrā or position of the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिहत्
लेलिहत्, अत्, अती, अत्, constantly licking or playing<BR>with the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिहान|लेलिहानः
लेलिहान, अस्, आ, अम्, frequently licking or darting<BR>out the tongue; (अस्), m. a snake, serpent; epithet<BR>of Śiva; (आ), f. a particular Mudrā or position of<BR>the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिह्यमान
लेलिह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, constantly darting out<BR>the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेह|लेहः
लेह, अस्, m. licking, tasting; one who licks, a<BR>licker, sipper, (मधुनो लेहः, a sipper of honey,<BR>a bee, = मधु-लिह्); anything to be taken by<BR>licking, a lambative, electuary; food; epithet of one<BR>of the ten ways in which an eclipse can take place;<BR>(ई), f. a particular disease of the tips of the ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहक
लेहक, अस्, m. one who licks, a licker, taster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहन|लेहनं
लेहन, अम्, n. the act of licking, tasting or<BR>lapping with the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहनीय
लेहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be licked, &c., = लेह्य<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहम्
लेहम्, ind. having licked, &c., (क्षीर-लेहम्,<BR>having licked milk.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहिन्
लेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, licking, a licker; [cf. मधु-ल्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहिन|लेहिनः
लेहिन, अस्, m. borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेह्य|लेह्यं
लेह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be licked, lickable, capable<BR>of being licked, to be lapped or licked up or eaten<BR>by licking; (अम्), n. nectar, ambrosia, food that is<BR>licked or sipped, a lambative, syrup, electuary;<BR>food in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ली
ली 1. ली, cl. 9. P. लिनाति (this form not<BR>usually found), to adhere; to obtain (?);<BR>cl. 1. P. लयति (not usually found), to melt, liquefy,<BR>dissolve; cl. 4. A. लीयते (this is the usual form),<BR>लिल्ये, लेष्यति or लास्यति, लेष्यते or लास्यते,<BR>अलेष्ट or अलास्त, लेतुम्, लातुम्, to cling or press<BR>closely, join or adhere firmly, adhere or stick to-<BR>gether, cling to, embrace; to lie, recline, lie or rest<BR>upon, sit upon, dwell in, stay in, haunt, lurk in, hide<BR>in, cower down in; to be viscous or sticky; to be<BR>solvable, to be dissolved; to be absorbed in; to be<BR>devoted to; to disappear, vanish: Pass. लीयते, Aor.<BR>अलायि: Caus. (generally with prep. वि), -लापयति or<BR>-लाययति or -लीनयति or -लालयति, to melt, liquefy,<BR>dissolve, &c., (see वि-ली; according to Pāṇ. I. 3, 70,<BR>the form लापयते in Ātmane-pada is used in the<BR>sense of ‘to obtain honour,’ ‘cause to be honoured’):<BR>Desid. लिलीषति, -ते: Intens. लेलीयते, लेलयीति,<BR>लेलेति (for लेलायति, which some consider an intensive<BR>form of a rt. ली, see लेलाय); [cf. Gr. λεῖμαξ: Lat.<BR>līmus, po-lire, linere; according to some, liqueo,<BR>liquo: Old Germ. lim, leim: Angl. Sax. lime,<BR>lam.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लय|लयः
लय, अस्, m. the act of clinging, adhering, stick-<BR>ing, union, adherence; embracing, an embrace (=<BR>श्लेष, सं-श्लेषण); the act of lying, cowering,<BR>lurking, hiding; melting, fusion, solution, melting<BR>away, dissolution, absorption, extinction, disappearing,<BR>vanishing, disappearance, destruction, reduction (of<BR>the Universe &c.) into its original state, death,<BR>(लयं या or गम्, &c., to go to dissolution, melt<BR>away, disappear, vanish; to be destroyed, perish);<BR>rest, repose; place of rest, residence, house, dwelling;<BR>mental inactivity, spiritual indifference, slackness of<BR>mind; time (in music, regarded as of three kinds,<BR>viz. द्रुत, ‘quick,’ मध्य, ‘mean or moderate,’<BR>and विलम्बित, ‘slow’); a pause in music; a parti-<BR>cular agricultural implement, (perhaps a sort of harrow<BR>or hoe, Ved.); (अम्), n. the root of Andropogon<BR>Muricatus; (अस्, आ, अम्), making the mind inactive<BR>or indifferent.<BR>—लय-काल, अस्, m. time of disso-<BR>lution or destruction.<BR>—लय-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone<BR>to dissolution, dissolved, melted.<BR>—लय-पुत्री, f.<BR>‘daughter of (musical) time,’ a female dancer,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">Page0868-c+ 79</a>]<BR>actress.<BR>—लयारम्भ (˚य-आर्˚) or लयालम्ब<BR>(˚य-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘moving according to time,’ a<BR>dancer, actor.<BR>—लयार्क (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. the sun<BR>at the dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लयन|लयनं
लयन, अम्, n. the act of clinging, adhering,<BR>lying, &c.; rest, repose; a place of rest, house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लायक
लायक, अस्, &c., clinging, sticking, adhering, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ली
2. ली, ईस्, f. clinging to, adhering, embracing, &c.;<BR>liquefying, melting; = चपल; [cf. लेलाय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीन|लीनः
लीन, अस्, आ, अम्, clung or pressed closely together,<BR>embraced, clung to, adhered to, attached to; clinging<BR>to, sticking to, embracing, adhering, lying, lying on,<BR>resting on, staying in, lurking, hiding, entered into;<BR>dissolved, melted, absorbed, absorbed in or into,<BR>swallowed up in; intimately united with; devoted<BR>to, given up to; disappeared, effaced, vanished, de-<BR>parted; (अम्), n. the being dissolved, melting, being<BR>absorbed in, disappearance.<BR>—लीन-ता, f. or लीन-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of clinging together or adher-<BR>ing, adhesion, adhesiveness; the lying hidden or<BR>concealed.<BR>—लीनालि (˚न-अल्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having bees<BR>adhering (to anything), embraced or clung to by<BR>bees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेल्य
लेल्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens., Vopa-deva XXVI.<BR>29), clinging or adhering very closely, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीका
लीका लीका, f. epithet of particular evil<BR>spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीक्का
लीक्का लीक्का or लीक्षा, f. = लिक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीला
लीला लीला, f. (supposed by some to be a<BR>corruption of क्रीडा; perhaps connected with rt.<BR>1. लस् or with लेलाय), play, sport, diversion, amuse-<BR>ment, pastime; wanton sport, amorous pastime<BR>(shown in the imitation of a lover's gait, manner,<BR>&c.), wantonness; mere sport or play, mere amuse-<BR>ment, joking, frivolity, child's play, ease or facility<BR>in doing anything, (लीलया, out of sport, sportively,<BR>for amusement, as a mere joke, with the greatest<BR>ease, without effort); sportive appearance, semblance,<BR>dissembling, dissimulation, pretence, disguise, sham;<BR>air, mien, manner; grace, beauty, charm, loveliness;<BR>a species of metre, four times ¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘<BR>¯˘˘¯.<BR>—लीला-कमल, अम्, n. a woman's toy-<BR>lotus, a lotus-flower held in the hand as a plaything.<BR>—लीला-कर, अस्, m. a particular metre.<BR>—लीला-<BR>कलह, अस्, m. a quarrel or dispute in play, sham-<BR>fight, mock-fight.<BR>—लीला-खेल, अस्, आ, अम्, moving<BR>or sporting playfully, playful; (अम्, आ), n. f. a kind<BR>of metre, four times ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯<BR>—लीलागार (˚ला-आग्˚) or लीला-गृह or लीला-गेह,<BR>अम्, n. a pleasure-house, place of amusement or sport.<BR>—लीलाङ्ग (˚ला-अन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having graceful or<BR>playful limbs (said of a bull &c.).<BR>—लीलाचल (˚ला-<BR>अच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a district.<BR>—लीला-तनु, उस्, f. a<BR>form assumed for mere sport or pleasure.<BR>—लीला-<BR>ताण्डव-पण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in sportive<BR>dances (said of Śiva).<BR>—लीला-तामरस, अम्, n. a<BR>lotus-flower held in the hand as a plaything.<BR>—लीला-<BR>दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt to ashes or consumed<BR>without effort.<BR>—लीलाद्रि (˚ला-अद्˚), इस्, m. = लीला-<BR>चल.<BR>—लीला-नटन, अम्, n. a sportive dance.<BR>—लीला-पद्म, अम्, n. a toy-lotus, (see लीला-क-<BR>मल.)<BR>—लीला-पर्वत, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—लीलाब्ज (˚ला-अब्˚), अम्, n. = लीला-कमल.<BR>—ली-<BR>लाभरण (˚ला-आभ्˚), अम्, n. a sham ornament (as<BR>a bracelet made of a string of lotuses).<BR>—लीला-<BR>मधु-कर, अस्, m., N. of a drama.<BR>—लीला-म-<BR>नुष्य, अस्, m. a sham man, man in disguise, one<BR>not really a man.<BR>—लीला-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting<BR>of play or amusement, playful, sportive, relating to<BR>play or amusement.<BR>—लीला-मात्रेण, ind. out of<BR>mere sport, in mere play, without the least effort.<BR>—लीला-मानुष-विग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>human body merely for amusement, assuming the<BR>shape of a man for a pretext or pretence; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—लीलाम्बुज (˚ला-अम्˚), अम्, n.<BR>= लीला-कमल.<BR>—लीलायुध (˚ला-आय्˚), आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people, (perhaps for नीलायुध.)<BR>—लीला-<BR>रति, इस्, f. sportive amusement, sport, amusement.<BR>—लीलारविन्द (˚ला-अर्˚), अम्, n. = लीला-कमल.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">Page0869-a+ 75</a>]<BR>—लीला-वज्र, अम्, n. an implement or instrument<BR>shaped like a thunderbolt.<BR>—लीला-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessed of grace or beauty, graceful, beautiful,<BR>charming; (अती), f. a beautiful and charming woman,<BR>a wanton woman; N. of Durgā; of the wife of the<BR>Asura Maya; of a merchant's daughter (in the<BR>Hitopadeśa); a kind of metre; N. of a section of<BR>the Siddhānta-śiromaṇi; of a well known treatise<BR>on arithmetic, algebra, and geometry by Bhāskara<BR>Ācārya; of an elementary treatise on the Vaiśeṣika<BR>philosophy (= न्याय-ल्˚, q. v.); of a work on medi-<BR>cine.<BR>—लीलावतार (˚ला-अव्˚), अस्, m. the descent (of<BR>Viṣṇu on the earth) for his own amusement.<BR>—ली-<BR>लावधूत (˚ला-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, gracefully waved<BR>about.<BR>—लीला-वापी, f. a pleasure-tank or lake.<BR>—लीला-<BR>वेश्मन्, अ, n. a pleasure-house; [cf. लीलागार.]<BR>—लीला-शुक, अस्, m. ‘pleasure-parrot,’ N. of the<BR>poet Vilva-maṅgala.<BR>—लीला-साध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to<BR>be effected with ease.<BR>—लीला-स्वात्म-प्रिय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author held in esteem by the Tāntrikas or<BR>worshippers of Durgā.<BR>—लीलोद्यान (˚ला-उद्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a pleasure-garden, pleasure-grounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0868-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाय
लीलाय, Nom. P. A. लीलायति, -यते, -यितुम्, to<BR>play, sport, amuse one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलायत्
लीलायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or लीलायमान, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>playing, sporting, dallying, sporting wantonly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलायित|लीलायितं
लीलायित, अस्, आ, अम्, done playfully or sportively,<BR>written sportively; (अम्), n. play, sport, amusement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलोपवती
लीलोपवती (?), f. a kind of metre, four times<BR>¯¯¯¯, ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुक्
लुक् 1. लुक्, an artificial root probably<BR>meaning ‘to meet together,’ and apparently only in-<BR>vented to explain लुकेश्वर; the forms लुकिष्यसि<BR>and लुकितस्य being also given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुकेश्वर
लुकेश्वर (˚क-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुक्
लुक् 2. लुक् (probably fr. Pass. of rt. लुञ्च्;<BR>cf. लुच् below; the loc. c. however is लुकि, not लुचि),<BR>a technical term or symbol in grammar to express<BR>‘the dropping out’ or ‘disappearance’ of Pratyayas<BR>or affixes; (it is properly regarded as a substitute for<BR>an affix, preventing the appearance of any other affix<BR>in its place, and neutralizing the effect which this affix<BR>would have had on the base; the symbols लुक्, लुप्,<BR>and श्लु are distinguished from लोप, q. v., and are<BR>called लु-मत्, as containing the syllable लु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुङ्
लुङ् लुङ्, a technical term or symbol in<BR>grammar for the termination of the Aorist or Third<BR>Preterite or for that Tense itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुङ्ग
लुङ्ग लुङ्ग = मातुलुङ्ग, a citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्च्|लुंच्
लुञ्च् लुञ्च्, cl. 1. P. लुञ्चति, लुलुञ्च, &c.,<BR>to pluck, pull, tug, tear, pare, peel; to<BR>pull or pluck out, pull off, tear off: Pass. लुच्यते,<BR>to be plucked or pulled out, &c.; [cf. probably Lat.<BR>runcare; Old Germ. liuhhan; Angl. Sax. lyccan;<BR>(according to some) Slav. luc-i-ti; Goth. raupja;<BR>Mod. Germ. raufe.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुच्
लुच्, क्, f. plucking out or off, cutting off; drop-<BR>ping out; [cf. 2. लुक्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुचित्वा
लुचित्वा, ind. having plucked or pulled out; having<BR>torn off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्च|लुंचः|लुञ्चः
लुञ्च, अस्, आ, अम्, pulling or tearing out, one<BR>who plucks or pulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चक
लुञ्चक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who plucks or pulls<BR>out, a tearer, &c. [cf. केश-ल्˚]; (अस्), m. (perhaps)<BR>a kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चन|लुंचन|लुंचनं
लुञ्चन, अम्, n. the act of plucking, tearing,<BR>pulling out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चित|लुंचित
लुञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, plucked, pulled, plucked out,<BR>&c.; peeled.<BR>—लुञ्चित-केश, अस्, m. ‘having the<BR>hair torn out, ‘N. of a Jaina ascetic (so called as<BR>pulling out the hair of the head and body by way<BR>of mortification).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चित्वा
लुञ्चित्वा, ind. having plucked or pulled out, &c.;<BR>[cf. लुचित्वा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्ज्
लुञ्ज् लुञ्ज् = rt. 2. लञ्ज्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्
लुट् 1. लुट् [cf. rts. रुट्, 1. लुठ्], cl. 1. A.<BR>लोटते, &c., to repel, resist, oppose; to<BR>suffer pain, be affected with grief; to shine; cl. 10.<BR>P. लोटयति, to speak; to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्
लुट् 2. लुट् [cf. rt. 2. लुठ्], cl. 1. 4. P.<BR>लोटति, लुट्यति, लुलोट, अलोटीत् or अलुटत्,<BR>लोटितुम्, to roll, roll about, roll on the ground, wal-<BR>low; to be connected or in contact with (?); cl. 1. A.<BR>लोटते, &c., to go (according to Naigh. II. 14): Caus.<BR>लोटयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलूलुटत् or अलुलोटत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोटन|लोटनं
लोटन, अम्, n. rolling, wallowing, tumbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्
लुट् 3. लुट्, a technical term or symbol in<BR>grammar for the terminations of the First Future or<BR>for that Tense itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठ्
लुठ् 1. लुठ्, cl. 1. P. लोठति, लुलोठ,<BR>अलुठत्, लोठितुम्, to strike, knock down;<BR>cl. 1. A. लोठते, लुलुठे, अलोठिष्ट, to resist,<BR>oppose, repel; to suffer pain; to go (according to<BR>Naigh. II. 14); cl. 10. P. लोठयति [cf. rt. लुण्ठ्],<BR>to rob, plunder, steal, pillage, sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठ्
लुठ् 2. लुठ्, cl. 6. P. लुठति, लुलोठ,<BR>अलुठत्, &c., लुठितुम्, to roll, roll<BR>about, move about, move to and fro, roll on the<BR>ground, wallow, welter; to roll down; to agitate,<BR>move, stir, (in this sense = rt. लुड्): Caus. लोठ-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलूलुठत् or अलुलोठत्, to cause<BR>to roll, make to move to and fro: Desid. लुलुठि-<BR>षते, to wish to roll, intend to roll, to be on the<BR>point of rolling; [cf. Hib. liuth, ‘I move, hasten.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठत्
लुठत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, rolling, rolling on the<BR>ground, falling down; flowing, trickling (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठन|लुठनं
लुठन, अम्, n. the act of rolling, rolling or<BR>wallowing on the earth, rolling on the ground with<BR>sorrow.<BR>—लुठनेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚न-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठमान
लुठमान, अस्, आ, अम्, rolling, moving to and<BR>fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठित|लुठितः
लुठित, अस्, आ, अम्, rolled, rolled down, rolling<BR>on the ground (as a horse &c.); fallen; (अम्), n.<BR>the rolling on the ground (of a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठेश्वर
लुठेश्वर (˚ठ-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोठ|लोठः
लोठ, अस्, m. rolling, rolling on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोठन
लोठन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुड्
लुड् लुड् (= rt. लुल्, cf. rts. 2. लुट्, 2. लुठ्),<BR>cl. 1. P. लोडति, &c., to agitate, move<BR>about, stir, churn, disturb; cl. 6. P. लुडति, &c., to<BR>adhere, be attached; to cover: Caus. लोडयति, &c.,<BR>to set in motion, agitate, disturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोडन|लोडनं
लोडन, अम्, n. the act of agitating or disturbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोडयत्
लोडयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, agitating, disturbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोडित
लोडित, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. लोलित], agitated, troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोड्यमान
लोड्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being agitated, being<BR>stirred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ट्|लुंट्
लुण्ट् लुण्ट् [cf. rts. रुण्ट्, रुण्ठ्, 1. लुठ्,<BR>लुण्ड्], cl. 1. P. लुण्टति, &c., to rob,<BR>plunder; cl. 10. P. लुण्टयति, &c., to rob, plunder;<BR>to peel, (for rt. लुञ्च्); to disregard, despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टक|लुण्टकः
लुण्टक, अस्, m. a kind of vegetable; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टा|लुंटा
लुण्टा, f. robbing; rolling, (for लुठन, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टाक|लुंटाक|लुण्टाकः
लुण्टाक, अस्, m. a robber, thief; a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टित
लुण्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, robbed, plundered; peeled,<BR>(for लुञ्चित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठ्|लुंठ्
लुण्ठ् लुण्ठ् (= rt. रुण्ठ्), cl. 1. P. लुण्-<BR>ठति, &c., to go; to stir up, agitate,<BR>excite, set in motion (= rts. 2. लुठ्, लुड्); to be<BR>idle; to be lame; to repel, resist; to steal, rob,<BR>plunder, pillage [cf. rts. रुण्ट्, लुण्ट्, 1. लुठ्]: Caus.<BR>लुण्ठयति, to rob, steal, plunder, sack; to peel,<BR>(for rt. लुञ्च्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठक|लुंठक|लुंठकः|लुण्ठकः
लुण्ठक, अस्, m. a robber, plunderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठत्
लुण्ठत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, stirring up, exciting, agi-<BR>tating; rolling, (for लुठत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठन|लुंठन|लुंठनं|लुण्ठनं
लुण्ठन, अम्, n. the act of plundering, pillaging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठनदी
लुण्ठ-नदी, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठयत्
लुण्ठयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, plundering, pillaging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठा|लुंठा
लुण्ठा, f. robbing, pillaging, &c.; rolling, &c.,<BR>(for लुठन, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठाक|लुंठाक|लुंठाकः|लुण्ठाकः
लुण्ठाक, अस्, m. a robber; a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठि|लुंठि|लुंठिः|लुण्ठिः
लुण्ठि, इस्, f. plundering, pillaging, sacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठित
लुण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, plundered, pillaged, robbed,<BR>stolen; peeled, (for लुञ्चित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठी|लुंठी
लुण्ठी, f. = लुठन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ड्|लुंड्
लुण्ड् लुण्ड् (= rts. रुण्ट्, लुण्ट्, 1. लुठ्),<BR>cl. 1. 10. P. लुण्डति, लुण्डयति, &c.,<BR>to rob, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्डिका|लुंडिका
लुण्डिका लुण्डिका, f. a ball, round mass<BR>(of anything); proper behaviour, fitting conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्डी|लुंडी
लुण्डी, f. proper behaviour, becoming conduct,<BR>acting and judging rightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्डीकृ
लुण्डी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to roll into a<BR>ball, roll up, roll together.<BR>—लुण्डी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, made into a ball, rolled up together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुन्थ्|लुंथ्
लुन्थ् लुन्थ् [cf. rts. 1. लुठ्, 1. लुट्], cl.<BR>1. P. लुन्थति, &c., to strike, hurt,<BR>kill; to afflict; to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्
लुप् 1. लुप् (a later form of rt. 1. रुप्),<BR>cl. 6. P. A. लुम्पति, -ते, लुलोप, लुलुपे,<BR>लोप्स्यति, -ते, अलुपत्, अलुप्त, लोप्तुम्, to break,<BR>fracture, violate, break in pieces, cut, cut off, mutilate,<BR>destroy, injure, spoil; to seize, pounce upon; to rob,<BR>plunder, take away, deprive of; to suppress, elide, erase,<BR>cause to disappear; cl. 4. P. लुप्यति, लुलोप, लोपिष्-<BR>यति, लोपितुम्, to be suppressed or destroyed [cf. लुप्-<BR>यते below]; to disturb, bewilder, perplex, confound<BR>[cf. rt. लुभ्, with which लुप् appears to be connected;<BR>see लोलुप]: Pass. लुप्यते, Aor. अलोपि, to be<BR>broken or violated; to be suppressed or lost, be<BR>elided, suffer elision, disappear (in grammar): Caus.<BR>लोपयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलूलुपत् or अलुलोपत्, to<BR>cause to break or violate; to break, infringe, violate,<BR>offend against, thwart, injure; to omit, neglect, miss;<BR>to cause to swerve from (with abl.): Desid. लुलुप्-<BR>सति, -ते, लुलोपिषति, &c.: Intens. लोलुप्यते, लो-<BR>लोप्ति, to confound, disturb, bewilder, perplex; [cf.<BR>Gr. λυπ-ρό-ς, λυπ-ή, λυπ-έ-ω, λυπη-ρό-ς, perhaps<BR>also Ὄλυμπος: Lat. rump-o: Old Germ. raubon:<BR>(probably) Goth. raupjan, ‘to pull out:’ Angl. Sax.<BR>reaf, reafian: Old Norse rŷf: Lith. rup-e-ti,<BR>rup-u-s: Slav. lom-i-ti: Hib. reubaim, ‘I tear,<BR>lacerate;’ reuban, ‘plundering, robbery;’ lomaim,<BR>‘I sheer, shave, make bare.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्
2. लुप्, falling or dropping out, suppression, elision,<BR>cutting off, rejection, (लुप् is one of the three tech-<BR>nical terms for grammatical elision classed with लुक्,<BR>q. v.; it is especially applicable to a Taddhita affix,<BR>implying its disappearance and preventing the ap-<BR>pearance of any other affix in its place.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्त|लुप्तं
लुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, broken, violated, injured,<BR>destroyed; robbed, plundered, deprived of; omitted,<BR>left off, neglected; suppressed, cut off, elided (in<BR>grammar), rejected, fallen or dropped out, disap-<BR>peared, lost, obsolete, disused; (अम्), n. stolen pro-<BR>perty, plunder, booty.<BR>—लुप्त-ता, f. the state of<BR>being cut off or elided, disappearance, suppression,<BR>non-existence.<BR>—लुप्त-धर्म-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>excluded from or deprived of religious ordinances.<BR>—लुप्त-पद, अस्, आ, अम्, wanting (whole) words.<BR>—लुप्त-पिण्डोदक-क्रिय (˚ड-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>deprived of funeral rites.<BR>—लुप्त-प्रतिभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, deprived of reason.<BR>—लुप्त-विसर्ग-ता, f. the<BR>dropping of Visarga.<BR>—लुप्तोपम (˚त-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, wanting or failing in the particle of compa-<BR>rison; (आ), f. (in rhetoric) a mutilated or elliptical<BR>simile (the conjunction expressing comparison being<BR>omitted), a metaphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्यमान
लुप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being broken, being cut<BR>off, being perplexed or confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप|लोपः
लोप, अस्, m. breaking, violation, fracture, mutila-<BR>tion, cutting off, destruction; robbing, plundering,<BR>stealing, deprivation, want, deficiency, loss, interrup-<BR>tion, intermission, omission, separation, disappear-<BR>ance, dropping or falling out, rejection, annulling,<BR>cancelling, erasure, grammatical elision, (लोप is the<BR>technical term for elision generally as distinguished<BR>from the terms लुप्, श्लु, लुक्, which are only appli-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">Page0870-a+ 80</a>]<BR>cable to affixes; when लोप of an affix takes place,<BR>a blank is substituted, which exerts the same influence<BR>on the base as the affix itself, but when either लुक् or<BR>लुप् or श्लु of an affix is enjoined, then the affix is<BR>not only dropped but it is also inoperative on the<BR>base; thus in the 1st pl. of कति, where जस् is said<BR>to be elided by लुक्, the change of the final of the<BR>base to Guṇa does not take place, i. e. both the affix<BR>and its effect on the base are abolished; moreover,<BR>लोप may refer only to the last letter of an affix,<BR>whereas by लुक् &c. the dropping of the whole affix<BR>is implied); (आ), f. = लोपामुद्रा.<BR>—लोपापत्ति (˚प-<BR>आप्˚), इस्, f. the being cut off or elided, the being<BR>dropped.<BR>—लोपामुद्रा (˚प-अम्˚), f., N. of the<BR>reputed wife of Agastya (regarded as the authoress<BR>of Ṛg-veda I. 179, 4).<BR>—लोपामुद्रा-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘husband of Lopāmudrā,’ N. of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0869-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपक
लोपक, अस्, इका, अम्, interrupting, annihilating,<BR>(धार-लोपक, अम्, n. [probably] epithet of a par-<BR>ticular ceremony); (अस्), m. violation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपन|लोपनं
लोपन, अम्, n. the act of omitting or violating,<BR>violation; [cf. व्रत-ल्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाक|लोपाकः
लोपाक, अस्, m. a kind of jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपापक|लोपापकः
लोपापक, अस्, m. a kind of jackal; (इका), f. the<BR>female of this jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाश|लोपाशः
लोपाश, अस्, m. a jackal, fox, or a similar animal;<BR>[cf., according to some, Gr. ἀλώπηξ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाशक|लोपाशकः
लोपाशक, अस्, m. a jackal; a proper N.; (इका),<BR>f. the female of a jackal, a female fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपिन्
लोपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, causing loss, doing an injury or<BR>wrong, injuring; liable or subject to elision, suffering<BR>elision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्तृ
लोप्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who interrupts or violates,<BR>a violator, injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्त्र|लोप्त्रं
लोप्त्र, अम्, ई, n. f. stolen property, plunder, booty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्य
लोप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken or destroyed; to<BR>be rejected or elided, to be omitted or passed over;<BR>(perhaps) being among thickets or inaccessible places<BR>(Ved.; cf. उलुप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्ध|लुब्धः
लुब्ध लुब्ध, लुब्धक, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभ्
लुभ् लुभ्, cl. 4. P. लुभ्यति, लुलोभ<BR>(A. लुलुभे), लोभिष्यति, अलुभत्, लो-<BR>भितुम्, लोब्धुम्, to desire greatly or eagerly,<BR>covet, long for anything (dat. or loc.); to be inter-<BR>ested in; to allure, (मां लुलुभे, he allured me);<BR>to be perplexed or disturbed, become disordered, go<BR>astray; cl. 6. P. लुभति, &c., Aor. अलोभीत्, to be-<BR>wilder, confound, perplex, disturb: Caus. लोभयति,<BR>&c., to cause to desire or long for, make greedy; ex-<BR>cite greediness or covetousness, excite lust; to allure,<BR>entice, entice away, seduce, attract; to disturb, de-<BR>range: Desid. लुलुभिषति, लुलोभिषति: Intens.<BR>लोलुभ्यते, लोलोब्धि; [cf. Gr. λίψ, λιψ-ουρία,<BR>λίπ-τ-ομαι, ἐλευθερός: Lat. lub-et, lib-et, lib-ī-do,<BR>lib-er, Libentina: Goth. liub-s, ‘dear;’ brothra-<BR>lub-o, us-laubjan: Old Germ. liub-an, môt-luba,<BR>lob, lob-ô-n: Angl. Sax. leof, lyfan, lufian, lof,<BR>leaf, left: Slav. ljub-i-ti, ‘to love;’ liub-y, ljub-<BR>imi, liub-y-ti, liub-jaus: Lith. lubju.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्ध|लुब्धः
लुब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring, covetous, greedy,<BR>avaricious; desirous of, longing for, (sometimes with<BR>loc., e. g. यशसि लुब्धः, desirous of fame); (अस्),<BR>m. a hunter; a lustful man, libertine.<BR>—लुब्ध-<BR>जन, अस्, आ, अम्, having covetous followers.<BR>—लुब्-<BR>ध-ता, f. or लुब्ध-त्व, अम्, n. greediness, ava-<BR>riciousness, covetousness, eager desire for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्धक|लुब्धकः
लुब्धक, अस्, m. a covetous or greedy man; a<BR>lustful man, libertine; a hunter; the star Sirius (so<BR>called according to a legend which narrates that Śiva<BR>transformed himself into a hunter in order to shoot<BR>an arrow [represented by the three stars in the belt<BR>of Orion lying in a direct line with Sirius] at Brahmā<BR>transformed into a deer and pursuing his own daughter<BR>metamorphosed into a doe for the purpose of com-<BR>mitting incest with her; cf. मृग-व्याध); epi-<BR>thet of the hinder parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्ध्वा
लुब्ध्वा, ind. having desired or longed for, hav-<BR>ing coveted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभित|लुभितः
लुभित, अस्, आ, अम्, perplexed, disturbed, de-<BR>luded, fascinated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभित्वा
लुभित्वा, ind. having perplexed or disturbed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभ्यत्
लुभ्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, desiring greatly, coveting,<BR>longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ|लोभः
लोभ, अस्, m. eager desire or wish, covetousness,<BR>cupidity, avarice, greediness, greed; Avarice perso-<BR>nified (as a son of Puṣṭi or of Dambha and Māyā);<BR>desire for or after (with gen. or at the end of a<BR>comp.).<BR>—लोभ-मञ्जरी, f. the pearl of covetous-<BR>ness.<BR>—लोभ-मोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, beguiled by covet-<BR>ousness, infatuated through avarice.<BR>—लोभ-विरह,<BR>अस्, m. absence of avarice; (अस्, आ, अम्), free from<BR>cupidity.<BR>—लोभाकृष्ट (˚भ-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attracted by greediness, tempted by covetousness.<BR>—लोभान्वित (˚भ-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of<BR>covetousness, avaricious, greedy.<BR>—लोभाभिपातिन्<BR>(˚भ-अभ्˚), ई, इनी, इ, hastening through eager desire,<BR>rushing greedily.<BR>—लोभोत्कर्ष (˚भ-उत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>excess of avarice, excessive greed or avarice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभन
लोभन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Caus.), alluring, en-<BR>ticing, attracting, charming; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>alluring, allurement, enticement, temptation; gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभनीय
लोभनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired or longed<BR>for, alluring, enticing, seductive, attractive.<BR>—लोभ-<BR>नीय-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most worthy of being de-<BR>sired, most attractive.<BR>—लोभनीयतमाकृति (˚म-<BR>आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having a most attractive figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभयान
लोभयान, अस्, आ, अम्, alluring, enticing, seducing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभयित्वा
लोभयित्वा, ind. having allured or enticed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभायन
लोभायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभित
लोभित, अस्, आ, अम्, allured, enticed, seduced.<BR>—लोभित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has allured,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभित्वा
लोभित्वा, ind. See लुभित्वा, लुब्ध्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभिन्
लोभिन्, ई, इनी, इ, desirous, greedy, covetous, ava-<BR>ricious, longing for, eager after, desirous of (often at<BR>the end of comps., e. g. धन-लोभिन्, desirous of<BR>wealth); alluring, enticing, attracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ्य|लोभ्यः
लोभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be eagerly desired, desir-<BR>able, alluring, enticing, attractive; (अस्), m. Phaseolus<BR>Mungo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ्यमान
लोभ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being allured or enticed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुमत्
लुमत् लु-मत्. See under 2. लुक्, p. 869.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुम्ब्|लुंब्
लुम्ब् लुम्ब्, cl. 1. P. लुम्बति, &c., to<BR>torment, harass; cl. 10. P. लुम्बयति,<BR>&c., to torment; to be invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुम्बिका|लुंबिका
लुम्बिका लुम्बिका, f. a particular musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुम्बिनी
लुम्बिनी लुम्बिनी, f., N. of a princess; of<BR>a grove named after this princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुम्बिनीय
लुम्बिनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुल्
लुल् लुल् (closely connected with rt.<BR>लुड्), cl. 1. P. लोलति, &c., to move<BR>about, move hither and thither, roll about; to stir,<BR>agitate, disturb, make tremulous; cl. 6. P. लुलति,<BR>&c. (for लुडति, see rt. लुड्), to adhere, be attached:<BR>Caus. लोलयति, &c., to set in motion, agitate, dis-<BR>turb, confound, put in confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुलित|लुलितः
लुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, agitated, tossed about,<BR>moved to and fro, moving hither and thither, shaking<BR>about, fluttering, tremulous, heaving, waving, curling,<BR>disturbed, confused, bewildered; disarranged, injured,<BR>destroyed; adhering, coming in contact, touching;<BR>agreeable, elegant (for ललित?).<BR>—लुलित-मण्-<BR>डन, अस्, आ, अम्, having ornaments tossed about in<BR>confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोल|लोलः
लोल, अस्, आ, अम्, moving hither and thither, shak-<BR>ing, rolling, tossing, swinging about, dangling, pen-<BR>dent, tremulous, trembling, quivering, agitated,<BR>alarmed, unsteady, restless, uneasy; changeable, in-<BR>constant, fickle; desiring, desirous, coveting, long-<BR>ing for, eager or anxious for, greedy, lustful; (अस्),<BR>m. a proper N.; (आ), f. the tongue; lightning;<BR>the goddess of fortune or Lakṣmī (as ‘the fickle or<BR>changeable one’); N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in Utpalāvar-<BR>taka; of the mother of the Daitya Madhu; of a<BR>female personification in Hindū music; of a metre,<BR>four times twenty-four instants [cf. रोला]; of another,<BR>four times ¯¯¯˘˘¯¯, ¯¯¯˘˘¯¯.<BR>—लोल-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">Page0870-c+ 77</a>]<BR>कुण्डल, अस्, आ, अम्, having dangling or pendent<BR>ear-rings.<BR>—लोल-घट (?) , the wind.<BR>—लोल-जिह्व,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a rolling or restless tongue, in-<BR>satiable, greedy.<BR>—लोल-ता, f. or लोल-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>movableness, tremulousness, fickleness, unsteadiness,<BR>restlessness; eager desire for, cupidity, lustfulness,<BR>lust.<BR>—लोल-लोल, अस्, आ, अम्, being in constant<BR>motion, continually moving, ever restless.<BR>—लोलाक्षि<BR>(˚ल-अक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having a rolling eye.<BR>—लोला-<BR>क्षिका, f. (a woman) with a rolling eye.<BR>—लोला-<BR>पाङ्ग (˚ल-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having tremulous or<BR>quivering outer corners (said of the eyes).<BR>—लोलार्क<BR>(˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, m. a form of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलत्
लोलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, moving to and fro, rolling,<BR>tossing about.<BR>—लोलद्-भुज, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>swinging arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलन
लोलन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलमान
लोलमान, अस्, आ, अम्, rolling, tossing, rolling on<BR>the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलित|लोलितः
लोलित, अस्, आ, अम्, moved hither and thither,<BR>waved to and fro, shaken, agitated, tremulous, trem-<BR>bling; [cf. लोडित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुलाप|लुलापः
लुलाप लुलाप, अस्, m. (said to be con-<BR>nected with rt. लुल्), a buffalo.<BR>—लुलाप-कन्द, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of plant with a tuberous root (= महिष-<BR>कन्द).<BR>—लुलाप-कान्ता, f. a buffalo cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुलाय|लुलायः
लुलाय, अस्, m. a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुश
लुश लुश, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi with the<BR>patronymic Dhānāka (author of the hymns Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 35, 36).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुशाकपि
लुशाकपि लुशाकपि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुष्
लुष् लुष् [cf. rt. लूष्], cl. 1. P. लोषति,<BR>&c., to rob, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुषभ|लुषभः
लुषभ लुषभ, अस्, m. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. III. 124. fr. rt. 1. रुष्), an elephant in<BR>rut; [cf. Gr. λύσσα.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुह्
लुह् लुह् (connected with rt. लुभ्), cl.<BR>1. P. लोहति, &c., to covet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लू
लू 1. लू, cl. 9. P. A. लुनाति (Ved. also<BR>cl. 5. लुनोति), लुनीते, लुलाव (2nd sing. लु-<BR>लविथ, 3rd du. लुलुवतुस्), लुलुवे (2nd pl. लुलु-<BR>विध्वे or लुलुविढ्वे), लविष्यति, -ते, अलावीत्,<BR>अलविष्ट (2nd pl. अलविध्वम् or अलविढ्वम्),<BR>लवितुम्, to cut, sever, divide, clip, reap, pluck,<BR>gather; to cut off, cut up, cut to pieces, destroy:<BR>Pass. लूयते, Aor. अलावि: Caus. लावयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अलीलवत्, अलीलवत, to cause to cut: Desid.<BR>of Caus. लिलावयिषति: Desid. लुलूषति, -ते:<BR>Intens. लोलूयते, लोलोति, to cut completely off: Desid.<BR>of Intens. लोलूयिषते; [cf. Gr. λύ-ω, λύ-α, λύ-σι-ς,<BR>λυ-τήρ, λύ-τρο-ν, ἀπο-λαύω; Lat. re-lu-o,<BR>so-lv-o (for se-lu-o), so-lu-tu-s, lu-o, lucrum; Goth.<BR>lau-s-j-a, laus, us-laus-ein-s, fra-lius-an; Angl.<BR>Sax. leosan, lysan, leas, los; Lith. lauju; Slav.<BR>ru-a-ti, runo, rus-i-ti.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव|लवं|लवः
लव, लवक, लवनीय, &c. See p. 863, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवित्वा
लवित्वा, ind. having cut, having cut off or<BR>gathered. See लूत्वा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव|लावः
लाव, अस्, ई, अम्, cutting, severing, dividing, reap-<BR>ing; plucking, gathering, (कुसुम-लावी, a female<BR>gatherer of flowers); cutting off; cutting to pieces,<BR>destroying, killing [cf. शत्रु-ल्˚]; = लाब, a quail,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावक|लावकः
लावक, अस्, m. a cutter, divider, reaper; = ला-<BR>बक, a quail, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाविन्
लाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, cutting, reaping; gathering,<BR>plucking; [cf. पुष्प-ल्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव्य
लाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut, to be reaped, to be<BR>cut through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुनत्
लुनत्, अन्, अती, अत्, or लुनान, अस्, आ, अम्, cut-<BR>ting, severing, dividing, reaping, cutting off, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लू
2. लू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, cutting, dividing, cutting off,<BR>plucking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूत्वा
लूत्वा, ind. having cut or divided, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लून|लूनः
लून, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, severed, clipped; reaped;<BR>plucked, gathered (said of flowers); cut off, cut<BR>down, wounded; nibbled at, bitten; destroyed;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">Page0871-a+ 69</a>]<BR>(अम्), n. = लूम, a tail.<BR>—लून-यवम्, ind. after<BR>the barley has been cut, after barley-harvest.<BR>—लून-<BR>विष, अस्, आ, अम्, having poison in the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0870-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनक|लूनकः
लूनक, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, divided; (अस्), m. a cut,<BR>division, wound, anything cut or broken; sort,<BR>species, difference; an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनि|लूनिः
लूनि, इस्, f. the act of cutting, reaping, cutting off;<BR>rice (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनी
लूनी, see Vopa-deva III. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूयमान
लूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being cut, being plucked<BR>or gathered.<BR>—लूयमान-यवम्, ind. when the<BR>barley is cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुव
लोलुव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.), cutting much<BR>or often.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलूया
लोलूया, f. determination to cut.<BR>—लोलूया-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, resolved to cut or cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूक्ष
लूक्ष लूक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, = रूक्ष in अ-ल्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूता
लूता लूता, f. a spider; an ant; a kind of<BR>cutaneous disease (said to be produced by moisture<BR>from a spider).<BR>—लूता-तन्तु, उस्, m. a spider's web,<BR>cobweb.<BR>—लूता-मर्कटक, अस्, m. an ape; Arabian<BR>jasmine; = पुत्री.<BR>—लूतारि (˚ता-अरि), इस्, m. ‘spider-<BR>enemy, ‘a kind of shrub (= दुग्ध-फेनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूतिका
लूतिका, f. a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूम|लूमं
लूम लूम, अम्, n. (connected with लून,<BR>q. v.), a tail, a hairy tail (as a horse's or monkey's).<BR>—लूम-विष, अस्, m. ‘having poison in the tail,’<BR>any animal that stings with the tail (as a scorpion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूष्
लूष् लूष् [cf. rts. लुष्, रूष्], cl. 1. P. लू-<BR>षति, &c., to adorn, decorate; cl. 10. P.<BR>लूषयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलूलुषत्, to hurt, injure,<BR>kill; to rob, steal, (also cl. 1. P. लोषति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूष
लूष in अर्क-ल्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूह
लूह लूह, अस्, आ, अम्, bad?; (अस्), m. a<BR>proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूहसुदत्त
लूहसुदत्त, अस्, m. a proper N. (= लूह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌङ्
ऌङ् ऌङ्, a technical term or symbol for<BR>the terminations of the Conditional or for that Mood<BR>itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌट्
ऌट् ऌट्, a technical term or symbol for<BR>the terminations of the Second Future or for that<BR>Tense itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेक
लेक लेक, अस्, m. (said to be) N. of an<BR>Āditya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेकुञ्चिक
लेकुञ्चिक लेकुञ्चिक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख|लेखः
लेख लेख, लेखन, लेखिन्, लेख्य, &c.<BR>See p. 866, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेट्
लेट् लेट्, a technical term for the termina-<BR>tions of the Vedic Mood or for this Mood itself,<BR>(this is a kind of Subjunctive Mood only found in<BR>the Vedas; its characteristic is the insertion of short<BR>अ, often lengthened to आ, between the base and ter-<BR>minations.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेट
लेट लेट, अस्, m., N. of a particular mixed<BR>caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेट्य
लेट्य लेट्य (= लोट्य, q. v.), Nom. P. लेट्-<BR>यति, &c., to deceive, cheat; to be first; to sleep;<BR>to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेण्ड|लेंड|लेंडं|लेण्डं
लेण्ड लेण्ड, अम्, n. excrement; [cf. लण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेत|लेतं|लेतः
लेत लेत, अस्, अम्, m. n. tears; [cf. लोत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेदरी
लेदरी लेदरी, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्
लेप् लेप्, cl. 1. A. लेपते, &c., to go; to<BR>worship, serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप|लेपः
लेप लेप, लेपन, लेप्य, &c. See p. 867,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेय|लेयः
लेय लेय, अस्, m. (fr. Gr. λέων), Ved. the<BR>sign of the zodiac Leo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलया
लेलया लेलया. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलाय
लेलाय लेलाय (by some regarded as an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">Page0871-b+ 74</a>]<BR>Intens. fr. an unused rt. ली, as distinguished fr. rt. 1.<BR>ली), Nom. P. A. लेलायति, -ते, अलेलायत्, अलेलेत्, अले-<BR>लीयत, लेलायितुम्, Ved. to move to and fro, quiver,<BR>flicker, tremble, quake, shake; [cf. लेलया.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलया
लेलया, ind. (probably to be connected with ले-<BR>लाय above, though formed fr. the Intens. of rt.<BR>1. ली), Ved. quivering, flickering, shaking about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलायत्
लेलायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलायमाना
लेलायमाना, f. one of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिह|लेलिहः
लेलिह लेलिह, लेलिहान, &c. See p. 868.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेल्य
लेल्य लेल्य. See p. 868, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेवार
लेवार लेवार, अस्, m., N. of an Agra-hāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश|लेशः
लेश लेश. See p. 868, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टव्य
लेष्टव्य, लेष्टु, &c. See p. 868, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेसिक|लेसिकः
लेसिक लेसिक, अस्, m. a rider on an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेह|लेहः
लेह लेह, लेहन, लेह्य. See p. 868, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैख
लैख लैख, अस्, m. (fr. लेख), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैखाभ्रेय
लैखाभ्रेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Lekhā-<BR>bhra; a metronymic from Lekhā-bhrū.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैगवायन
लैगवायन लैगवायन, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Ligu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैगव्य
लैगव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Ligu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैङ्ग|लैंग|लैंगं|लैङ्गं
लैङ्ग लैङ्ग, अम्, n. (fr. लिङ्ग), N. of a<BR>Purāṇa; of an Upa-Purāṇa; (ई), f. a kind of creeper<BR>(= लिङ्गिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैङ्गिक|लैंगिक|लैङ्गिकः
लैङ्गिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or depending on<BR>a mark or token; (अस्), m. a maker of images or<BR>statues, statuary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैण्
लैण् लैण्, cl. 1. P. लैणति, &c., to go,<BR>approach; to send; to embrace, &c. (=<BR>rt. पैण्, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लो
लो लो, लौस्, m. a noun of agency said to<BR>be derived fr. लवय, q. v.; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक्
लोक् लोक् (more properly to be regarded<BR>as a Nom. fr. लोक below, or, according to<BR>some, as a secondary rt. developed out of रुच्, रोक,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. A. लोकते, लुलोके, लोकितुम्, to see, per-<BR>ceive; cl. 10. P. or Caus. लोकयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अलुलोकत्, to look, look at, view, contemplate; to<BR>see, perceive, be aware of, know; to shine; to<BR>speak, (भाषार्थ being a various reading for<BR>भासार्थ); [cf. Gr. λεύσσ-ω, Old Germ. luog-<BR>e-m; Eng. look; Lith. lauk-i-u; Lett. lûkô-t,<BR>‘to see.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक|लोकः
लोक, अस्, m. (cf. रोक; in the oldest texts of the<BR>Ṛg-veda लोक is generally preceded by उ, which<BR>according to the Pada-pāṭha = the particle 3. उ, and<BR>according to some may be an abbreviation of उरु,<BR>wide, or derived from the prep. अव, cf. उरु-लोक,<BR>अव-काश), open space (Ved.), space, room, inter-<BR>mediate space (Ved.; in Ṛg-veda VIII. 100, 12,<BR>देहि लोकम् = अवकाशम् प्र-यच्छ, make room),<BR>the vast space, the wide world, sky, heaven; any<BR>division of the universe, (three Lokas are com-<BR>monly given, viz. heaven, earth, and the lower<BR>world, but the fuller classification enumerates four-<BR>teen, seven descending one below the other and<BR>constituting together the lower world, sometimes<BR>called hell [see पाताल], and seven higher regions<BR>rising one above the other, as follow, 1. भूर्-लोक,<BR>the earth; 2. भुवर्-ल्˚, the space between the<BR>earth and the sun, the region of the Munis, Siddhas,<BR>&c.; 3. स्वर्-ल्˚, the heaven of Indra above the<BR>sun or between the sun and the polar star; 4. म-<BR>हर्-ल्˚, said to be one krore of Yojanas above the<BR>polar star and to be the abode of Bhṛgu and other<BR>saints who survive the destruction of the three worlds<BR>situated below; during the conflagration of these<BR>lower worlds the saints ascend to 5. जनर्-ल्˚, which<BR>is described as the abode of Brahmā's sons Sanat-<BR>kumāra, &c.; 6. तपर्-ल्˚, where the deified Vai-<BR>rāgins reside; 7. सत्य-ल्˚ or ब्रह्म-ल्˚ or the<BR>abode of Brahmā, translation to which world exempts<BR>beings from further birth: the first three worlds are<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-c" target="_blank">Page0871-c+ 81</a>]<BR>destroyed at the end of each Kalpa or day of<BR>Brahmā, the last three at the end of his life or of 100<BR>of his years; the fourth Loka is equally permanent,<BR>but is uninhabitable from heat at the time that the<BR>first three are burning: another enumeration calls<BR>these seven worlds, earth, sky, heaven, middle region,<BR>place of births, mansion of the blest, and abode of<BR>truth, placing the sons of Brahmā in the sixth divi-<BR>sion and affirming the fifth or जनर्-ल्˚ to be that<BR>where animals destroyed in the general conflagration<BR>are born again); a symbolical expression for the<BR>number seven; the world, earth, (इह लोके, in this<BR>world, on the earth, opposed to परत्र, पर-<BR>लोके, &c.); any place, region, tract, district, province;<BR>the inhabitants of the world, the human race, man-<BR>kind, folk, man, men (in this sense also आस्, m. pl.),<BR>people, subjects (as contrasted with the king); a<BR>company, community; common life, ordinary prac-<BR>tice, (especially) common usage (as contrasted with<BR>ancient usage or idiom of the Veda; लोके, ‘in ordi-<BR>nary usage, in the language of the people, ‘as opposed<BR>to वेदे, छन्दसि); seeing, looking, sight, regard;<BR>[cf. Lat. locus; Lith. laukas, ‘a plain.’]<BR>—लोक-<BR>कण्टक, अस्, m. ‘thorn of men,’ a wicked or inju-<BR>rious man, criminal; epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—लोक-<BR>कथा, f. a popular legend or fable.<BR>—लोक-कर्तृ,<BR>ता, m. the creator of the world (applied to Brahmā,<BR>Viṣṇu, and Śiva).<BR>—लोक-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, re-<BR>sembling or appearing like the world, becoming<BR>manifested in the form of the world; regarded by<BR>the world; (अस्), m. a period or age of the world.<BR>—लोक-कान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, world-loved, liked by<BR>every one, pleasing to all, popular; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>medicinal herb.<BR>—लोक-कार, अस्, m. = लोक-कर्तृ.<BR>—लोक-कारण-करण, अम्, n. cause of the causes<BR>of the world (a name applied to Śiva).<BR>—लोक-कृत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, making or creating free space, setting free<BR>(Ved.); (त्), m. = लोक-कर्तृ, the creator of the<BR>world.<BR>—लोक-कृत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. = लोक-कृत्,<BR>creating space.<BR>—लोक-क्षित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. dwelling<BR>in the sky, inhabiting heaven.<BR>—लोक-गति, इस्, f.<BR>‘the way of the world,’ actions of men.<BR>—लोक-<BR>गाथा, f. a verse or song (handed down orally)<BR>among men.<BR>—लोक-गुरु, उस्, m. a teacher of the<BR>world, instructor of the people.<BR>—लोक-चक्षुस्, उस्,<BR>n. ‘eye of the world,’ the sun, (according to some<BR>उस्, m.); (ऊंषि), n. pl. the eyes of men.<BR>—लोक-<BR>चर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, wandering through the world.<BR>—लोक-चारित्र, अम्, n. the way or proceedings of<BR>the world.<BR>—लोक-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, = लोक-चर.<BR>—लोक-जननी, f. ‘the mother of the world,’ epithet<BR>of Lakṣmī.<BR>—लोक-जित्, त्, त्, त्, winning or conquer-<BR>ing a region (Ved.); conquering Heaven; (त्), m. a<BR>conquerer of the world; a sage; N. of a Buddha.<BR>—लोक-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing the world, under-<BR>standing men.<BR>—लोकज्ञ-ता, f. knowledge of the<BR>world, knowledge of mankind.<BR>—लोक-ज्येष्ठ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the most distinguished or excellent among men,’<BR>epithet of Buddha.<BR>—लोक-तत्त्व, अम्, n. ‘world-<BR>truth, ‘knowledge of the world, knowledge of man-<BR>kind.<BR>—लोक-तन्त्र, अम्, n. the system or course of<BR>the world,<BR>—लोक-तस्, ind. from the world, according<BR>to ordinary life, popularly, as is usual or customary.<BR>—लोक-तुषार, अस्, m. ‘eath's-dew,’ camphor.<BR>—लोक-त्रय, अम्, ई, n. f. ‘world-triad,’ the three<BR>worlds (heaven, earth, and the lower regions).<BR>—लो-<BR>क-दम्भक, अस्, इका, अम्, deceiving the world,<BR>cheating or deluding mankind.<BR>—लोक-द्वार, अम्,<BR>n. the door or gate of heaven.<BR>—लोकद्वारीय, अम्,<BR>n. (fr. the preceding), N. of a Sāman.<BR>—लोक-<BR>धातु, उस्, m. epithet of a particular division of the<BR>world (with Buddhists).<BR>—लोक-धातृ, ता, m. ‘the<BR>creator or supporter of the world, ‘epithet of Śiva.<BR>—लोक-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of worlds,’ epithet of<BR>Brahmā; of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; of Śiva; a governor<BR>or ruler of the people, a king, sovereign; a Buddha;<BR>N. of a Buddha; of the author of the Pada-mañjarī.<BR>—लोकनाथ-रस, अस्, m., N. of a particular me-<BR>dicinal preparation.<BR>—लोक-निन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>blamed by the world, generally censured, found<BR>fault with by men.<BR>—लोक-नेतृ, ता, m. guide or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0872-a" target="_blank">Page0872-a+ 81</a>]<BR>ruler of the world; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—लोक-प, अस्,<BR>m. protector or guardian of the world, world-pro-<BR>tector (= लोक-पाल, q. v.).<BR>—लोक-पक्ति, इस्, f.<BR>world-reputation, general respectability, esteem among<BR>men.<BR>—लोक-पति, इस्, m. the lord of the world;<BR>epithet of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu; a lord or ruler of<BR>people, a king, sovereign.<BR>—लोक-पथ, अस्, m. way<BR>of the world, general or universal way, the usual way.<BR>—लोक-पद्धति, इस्, f. general or universal way.<BR>—लोक-पाल, अस्, m. a world-protector, guardian<BR>of the world, regent of a quarter of the world, any<BR>presiding deity, (the Loka-pālas are sometimes re-<BR>garded as deities appointed by Brahmā at the creation<BR>of the world to act as guardians of different orders of<BR>beings, but more commonly they are identified with<BR>the deities presiding over the four cardinal and four<BR>intermediate points of the compass, which, according to<BR>Manu V. 96, are 1. Indra, guardian of the East; 2. Agni,<BR>of the South-east; 3. Yama, of the South; 4. Sūrya, of<BR>the South-west; 5. Varuṇa, of the West; 6. Pavana or<BR>Vāyu, of the North-west; 7. Kuvera, of the North;<BR>8. Soma or Candra, of the North-east: other authorities<BR>substitute Nir-ṛti for 4. and Īśānī or Pṛthivī for 8);<BR>a protector or ruler of the people, king, sovereign,<BR>prince; N. of a king; protection of the people.<BR>—लोक-पालक, अस्, m. = लोक-पाल, a world-pro-<BR>tector, ruler of the universe; a king, sovereign.<BR>—लोकपाल-ता, f. or लोकपाल-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>being a Loka-pāla or guardian of the world.<BR>—लोक-<BR>पितामह, अस्, m. progenitor or creator of the world,<BR>the great forefather of mankind; epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—लोक-पुण्य, N. of a place.<BR>—लोक-पुरुष,<BR>अस्, m. ‘world-man,’ the World personified.<BR>—लोक-<BR>पूजित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured by the world, univer-<BR>sally worshipped; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—लोक-<BR>प्रकाशक, अम्, n., N. of a compilation by Kṣe-<BR>mendra.<BR>—लोक-प्रकाशन, अस्, m. ‘world-illumi-<BR>nator, ‘the sun.<BR>—लोक-प्रत्यय, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>world-currency, universal prevalence (of a custom,<BR>&c.).<BR>—लोक-प्रदीप, अस्, m. ‘light of the world,’<BR>N. of a Buddha.<BR>—लोक-प्रवाद, अस्, m. popular<BR>talk, common saying, current report, general rumour,<BR>news, popular opinion, commonly used expression.<BR>—लोक-प्रवाहिन्, ई, इनी or इणी, इ, flowing<BR>through the world.<BR>—लोक-प्रसिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>celebrated in the world, generally established or<BR>received, universally known or acknowledged, well-<BR>known, notorious.<BR>—लोक-प्रसिद्धि, इस्, f. uni-<BR>versal establishment or reception (of any custom<BR>&c.), general notoriety or prevalence.<BR>—लोक-बन्-<BR>धु, उस्, m. ‘universal friend, friend of all,’ epithet<BR>of the sun; of Śiva.<BR>—लोक-बान्धव, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>friend of all,’ epithet of the sun.<BR>—लोक-बाह्य, see<BR>लोक-वाह्य.<BR>—लोक-भर्तृ, ता, m. supporter of<BR>the people.<BR>—लोक-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. occupying<BR>space.<BR>—लोक-भावन, अस्, ई, अम्, or लोक-भाविन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, world-creating; promoting the welfare of<BR>men or of the world.<BR>—लोक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>containing space or room, spacious (Ved.); contain-<BR>ing the universe.<BR>—लोक-मर्यादा, f. popular ob-<BR>servance, established usage or custom.<BR>—लोक-मातृ,<BR>ता, m. the mother of the world; epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—लोक-मार्ग, अस्, m. general or universal way,<BR>prevalent custom.<BR>—लोकम्-पृण, अस्, आ, अम्, filling<BR>the world, penetrating everywhere; (आ), f., Ved.,<BR>scil. इष्टका, epithet of the bricks used for building<BR>the sacrificial altar (set up with the usual formula<BR>लोकम् पृण, those which have a peculiar formula<BR>being called यजुष्-मती, q. v.); scil. ऋच्, the<BR>formula लोकम् पृण.<BR>—लोक-यात्रा, f. the busi-<BR>ness and traffic of men, intercourse or business of<BR>the world, worldly affairs, popular usages and cus-<BR>toms, conduct of men, ordinary actions or conduct,<BR>&c.; support of life.<BR>—लोक-यात्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>relating to the business or traffic of the world.<BR>—लोक-रक्ष, अस्, m. ‘protector of the people,’<BR>a king, sovereign.<BR>—लोक-रञ्जन, अम्, n. pleasing<BR>the world, gaining public confidence, popularity.<BR>—लोक-रव, अस्, m. the talk of the world, popular<BR>report.<BR>—लोक-लेख, अस्, m. a general writing,<BR>public document, ordinary letter.<BR>—लोक-लोचन,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0872-b" target="_blank">Page0872-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, n. (according to some अस्, m.), ‘the eye of the<BR>world, ‘the sun; (आनि), n. pl. the eyes of men.<BR>—लोकलोचनापात (˚न-आप्˚), अस्, m. the attacks<BR>of men's eyes, i. e. the prying eyes of men.<BR>—लोक-<BR>वचन, अम्, n. people's talk, public rumour, popular<BR>report.<BR>—लोक-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing the world.<BR>—लोक-वर्तन, अम्, n. the conduct of men,<BR>general mode of acting, usual behaviour.<BR>—लोक-<BR>वाद, अस्, m. the talk of the world, popular report,<BR>public rumour, common talk, news.<BR>—लोक-वार्त्ता,<BR>f. the world's news, popular report or rumour.<BR>—लो-<BR>क-वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, excluded from the world,<BR>expelled from society, excommunicated; differing<BR>from the world, singular, eccentric; (अस्), m. an<BR>outcast.<BR>—लोक-विक्रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, abused by<BR>the world, censured by mankind, universally blamed<BR>or condemned.<BR>—लोक-विज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, univer-<BR>sally known or celebrated.<BR>—लोक-विद्, त्, त्, त्, know-<BR>ing or understanding the world; (त्), m. epithet of<BR>a Buddha.<BR>—लोक-विद्विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, hated by<BR>men, universally hated, disliked by people generally,<BR>unpopular.<BR>—लोक-विधि, इस्, m. the creator of the<BR>world, disposer of the universe; order or mode of<BR>proceeding prevalent in the world.<BR>—लोक-विना-<BR>यक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a particular class of deities<BR>presiding over diseases.<BR>—लोक-विन्दु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. creating room or space, gaining or obtaining<BR>freedom.<BR>—लोक-विन्दु-सार, अम्, n., N. of the last<BR>of the fourteen Pūrvas or most ancient Jaina writings.<BR>—लोक-विश्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, universally celebrated,<BR>far-famed, famous, current.<BR>—लोक-विश्रुति, इस्, f.<BR>world-wide fame, notoriety; unfounded rumour or<BR>report.<BR>—लोक-विसर्ग, अस्, m. the creation of the<BR>world.<BR>—लोक-विस्तार, अस्, m. universal spreading,<BR>general extension or diffusion.<BR>—लोक-वीर, आस्, m.<BR>pl. the world's heroes.<BR>—लोक-वृत्त, अम्, n. worldly<BR>intercourse, idle conversation; a universal custom.<BR>—लोक-वृत्तान्त, अस्, m. the events or occurrences<BR>of the world, course or proceedings of the world,<BR>circumstances of life, human conduct.<BR>—लोक-व्य-<BR>वहार, अस्, m. the affairs or business of the world,<BR>popular usage, general custom or course; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), universally used, commonly current.<BR>—लोक-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n. any observance prevalent in the<BR>world or among men, general practice or way of<BR>proceeding, general mode of life; N. of several<BR>Sāmans.<BR>—लोक-श्रुति, इस्, f. world-wide fame or<BR>reputation, universal notoriety.<BR>—लोक-संव्यव-<BR>हार, अस्, m. commerce or intercourse with the<BR>world, worldly business, trade and traffic.<BR>—लोक-<BR>संसृति, इस्, f. the course of the world, fate, destiny.<BR>—लोक-सङ्कर, अस्, m. confusion of mankind,<BR>general confusion in the world, acting a false cha-<BR>racter among men.<BR>—लोक-सङ्क्षय, अस्, m. the<BR>destruction of the world.<BR>—लोक-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>intercourse with the world, worldly experience; the<BR>propitiation or conciliation of men; the whole of<BR>the universe; the welfare of the world.<BR>—लोक-सनि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. causing room or space, effecting a<BR>free course.<BR>—लोक-साक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>the world as a witness, attested by the world or by<BR>others; (अम्), ind. before or in the presence of<BR>witnesses.<BR>—लोक-साक्षिन्, ई, m. witness of the<BR>world, universal witness; epithet of Brahman; of<BR>Fire; (ई, इनी, इ),= लोक-साक्षिक above.<BR>—लोक-<BR>सात्, ind. for the general good.<BR>—लोकसात्-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made or done for the general good.<BR>—लोक-<BR>साधक, अस्, इका, अम्, creating worlds.<BR>—लोक-<BR>सामन्, अ, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—लोक-सिद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, world-established, current among the people,<BR>generally done, usual, customary, popular, fashion-<BR>able, common; universally admitted, generally re-<BR>ceived.<BR>—लोक-सीमातिवर्तिन् (˚म-अत्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>passing beyond ordinary limits, extraordinary, super-<BR>natural.<BR>—लोक-सुन्दर, अस्, ई, अम्, generally es-<BR>teemed beautiful, universally considered handsome;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—लोक-स्थल, अम्, n.<BR>an incident of ordinary life, common or ordinary<BR>occurrence.<BR>—लोक-स्थिति, इस्, f. a universal law,<BR>generally established rule or maxim.<BR>—लोक-स्पृत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. = लोक-सनि (?).<BR>—लोक-हास्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0872-c" target="_blank">Page0872-c+ 81</a>]<BR>world-derided, ridiculed by mankind, any object of<BR>general ridicule.<BR>—लोकहास्य-ता, f. universal ridi-<BR>culousness.<BR>—लोक-हित, अम्, n. the welfare of the<BR>world, general weal.<BR>—लोकाकाश (˚क-आक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>space, sky; (according to the Jainas) a worldly<BR>region, the abode of unliberated beings.<BR>—लोकाक्षि<BR>(˚क-अक्˚), इस्, m. ‘eye of the world,’ N. of a pre-<BR>ceptor.<BR>—लोकाचार (˚क-आच्˚), अस्, m. usage or<BR>practice of the world, common practice, ordinary<BR>conduct, general or popular custom, universal habit.<BR>—लोकातिग (˚क-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, going beyond<BR>the usage of the world, extraordinary, supernatural.<BR>—लोकातिशय (˚क-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, superior to<BR>the world, surpassing ordinary usage (= लोकातिग).<BR>—लोकात्मन् (˚क-आत्˚), आ, m. the soul of the<BR>universe.<BR>—लोकादि (˚क-आदि), इस्, m. the begin-<BR>ning of the world, the beginner or creator of the<BR>world.<BR>—लोकाधिप (˚क-अध्˚), अस्, m. a ruler or<BR>governor of the world, a god, deity.<BR>—लोकाधिपति<BR>(˚क-अध्˚), इस्, m. the ruler or lord of the world.<BR>—लोकानुग्रह (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m. the welfare of<BR>the world, prosperity of all people, general weal.<BR>—लोकानुराग (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m. the love of man-<BR>kind, universal love or attachment, general bene-<BR>volence, philanthrophy, charity.<BR>—लोकान्तर (˚क-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. another world, the next world, a future<BR>life, decease, death, (लोकान्तरं गम् or या, to<BR>go into the next world, die.)<BR>—लोकान्तर-गत or<BR>लोकान्तर-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to another<BR>world, deceased, dead.<BR>—लोकान्तरिक (˚क-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, dwelling or situated between the worlds.<BR>—लोकापवाद (˚क-अप्˚), अस्, m. the reproach or<BR>censure of the world, general evil report, public<BR>scandal, general outcry against, popular accusation.<BR>—लोकाभिभाविन् (˚क-अभ्˚), ई, इनी, इ, overcom-<BR>ing the world; overspreading or pervading the world<BR>(said of light).<BR>—लोकाभिलषित (˚क-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, world-desired, universally coveted, generally<BR>liked; (अस्), m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—लोकाभ्युदय<BR>(˚क-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the prosperity of the world,<BR>general welfare.<BR>—लोकायत (˚क-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘world-extended (?),’ materialistic, atheistical; (अम्),<BR>n., scil. शास्त्र or मत or तन्त्र, materialism, the<BR>system of atheistical philosophy (taught by Cārvāka);<BR>(अस्), m. a materialist.<BR>—लोकायतिक (˚क-आय्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a materialist, follower of the Cārvāka system,<BR>atheist, unbeliever.<BR>—लोकायन (˚क-अय्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘refuge of the world,’ epithet of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—लोका-<BR>लोक (˚क-अल्˚), अम्, n., or औ, m. du. world and no<BR>world, the visible and invisible world; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a mythical belt or circle of mountains surrounding<BR>the outermost of the seven seas and dividing the<BR>visible world from the region of darkness, (the sun<BR>being within this circle these mountains are supposed<BR>to form a kind of wall, light on one side and dark<BR>on the other; cf. चक्र-बाल.)<BR>—लोकावेक्षण<BR>(˚क-अव्˚), अम्, n. consideration for the world,<BR>anxiety or care for the welfare of mankind.<BR>—लोकेश<BR>(˚क-ईश), अस्, m. the lord or ruler of the world;<BR>epithet of Brahmā; N. of a Buddha; quicksilver.<BR>—लोकेश-प्रभवाप्यय (˚व-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>owing both origin and end to the guardians of the<BR>world.<BR>—लोकेश्वर (˚क-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord or<BR>ruler of the world; N. of a Buddha.<BR>—लोकेश्वरात्-<BR>मजा (˚र-आत्˚), f. ‘Lokeśvara's daughter,’ N. of a<BR>Buddhist goddess.<BR>—लोकेष्टि (˚क-इष्˚), इस्, f., Ved.,<BR>N. of a particular Iṣṭi.<BR>—लोकैकबन्धु (˚क-<BR>एक्˚), उस्, m. ‘the only friend of the world,’ epithet<BR>of Gotama and of Śākya-muni.<BR>—लोकैषणा (˚क-<BR>एष्˚), f. desire or longing after heaven.<BR>—लोकोक्ति<BR>(˚क-उक्˚), इस्, f. a general or common saying, any<BR>saying commonly current among men, a proverb.<BR>—लोकोत्तर (˚क-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, excelling or<BR>surpassing the world, beyond what is common or<BR>general, unusual, extraordinary; (अस्), m. an un-<BR>common person, a king, prince.<BR>—लोकोत्तर-परि-<BR>वर्त, N. of a Buddhist Sūtra work.<BR>—लोकोत्तर-<BR>वादिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a Buddhist sect (probably<BR>so called from their pretending to be superior to or<BR>above the rest of the world).<BR>—लोकोद्धार (˚क-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0871-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकन|लोकनं
लोकन, अम्, n. the act of looking, seeing, viewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनीय
लोकनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be seen or perceived,<BR>visible, worthy of being looked at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकित
लोकित, अस्, आ, अम्, seen, beheld, looked at, viewed,<BR>perceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकिन्
लोकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. possessing a world, occupy-<BR>ing the world, possessing the best world; (इनस्),<BR>m. pl. the inhabitants of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक्य
लोक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, granting a free sphere of action,<BR>giving free space (Ved.); diffused over the world,<BR>world-wide; conducive to the attainment of a better<BR>world, heavenly; usual, customary, ordinary, right,<BR>real, actual; (अम्), n. free space or sphere (Ved.).<BR>—लोक्य-ता, f., Ved. (according to a commentator)<BR>the attainment of a better world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोग|लोगः
लोग लोग, अस्, m. (perhaps connected with<BR>rt. 1. रुज्), Ved. a clod of earth, lump of clay, clod,<BR>(Sāy. = लोष्ट.)<BR>—लोगाक्ष (˚ग-अक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘clod-eyed,’ a proper N.<BR>—लोगेष्टका (˚ग-इष्˚),<BR>f., Ved. a brick made from a lump of clay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच्
लोच् लोच् (connected with rts. लोक्,<BR>1. रुच्), cl. 1. A. लोचते, लुलोचे, लोचि-<BR>तुम्, to see, behold, look or gaze at, view, inspect,<BR>perceive; cl. 10. P. लोचयति, &c., to speak; to<BR>shine (?) : Caus. लोचयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अलुलोचत्,<BR>to cause to see: Desid. लुलोचिषते: Intens. लोलोच्-<BR>यते; [cf. Gr. λεύσσ-ω; Old Germ. luog-e-m;<BR>Lith. lauk-i-u; Lett. luko-t, ‘to see.']<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच|लोचं
लोच, अस्, m. sight?; (अम्), n. tears; [cf. लोत,<BR>लेत.]<BR>—लोच-मर्कट or लोच-मस्तक, अस्, m.<BR>cock's comb, the flower Celosia Cristata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचक|लोचकः
लोचक, अस्, m. a stupid or senseless person, (per-<BR>haps as gazing or staring in a senseless manner); the<BR>pupil of the eye; lamp-black (used as a stibium); a dark<BR>or black dress; a lump of flesh; a particular ornament<BR>worn by women on the forehead; a particular ear-<BR>ornament, ear-ring; a bow-string; the plantain tree,<BR>Musa Sapientum; a wrinkled skin, wrinkled or con-<BR>tracted eyebrow; the cast-off skin of a snake; (इका),<BR>f. a kind of pastry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचन|लोचनं
लोचन, अस्, ई, अम्, illuminating, brightening;<BR>visible, (अ-लोचन, invisible); (अस्), m., N. of an<BR>author; (आ), f., N. of a Buddhist goddess; (ई), f. a<BR>species of plant; (अम्), n. the organ of sight, in-<BR>strument of vision, the eye, (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp. the fem. generally ends in आ, cf. चारु-ल्˚,<BR>वाम-ल्˚); N. of a work.<BR>—लोचन-कार, अस्, m.<BR>the author of the Locana.<BR>—लोचन-गोचर, अस्, m.<BR>the range or horizon of the eye; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>within the range of vision.<BR>—लोचन-पथ or लो-<BR>चन-मार्ग, अस्, m. the path or range of the eyes,<BR>sphere of vision.<BR>—लोचन-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, useful<BR>or serviceable for the eyes; (आ), f. blue vitriol (used<BR>as a collyrium).<BR>—लोचनामय (˚न-आम्˚), अस्, m.<BR>eye-disease, ophthalmia.<BR>—लोचनोड्डारक (˚न-<BR>उड्˚), N. of a Grāma.<BR>—लोचनोत्स (˚न-उत्˚), N.<BR>of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोट्
लोट् 1. लोट् (= rt. लोड्), cl. 1. P. लोटति,<BR>&c., to be mad or foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोट्
लोट् 2. लोट्, a technical term or symbol<BR>in grammar for the terminations of the Imperative<BR>or for that Mood itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोटा
लोटा लोटा or लोटिका, f. sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोट्य
लोट्य लोट्य (= लेट्य, q. v.), Nom. P. लोट्-<BR>यति, &c., to deceive, cheat; to be first; to sleep;<BR>to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोठ|लोठः
लोठ लोठ, लोठन. See p. 869, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोड्
लोड् लोड् (= rts. रोड्, लोट्, लौड्), cl. 1. P.<BR>लोडति, &c., to be foolish or mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोडन|लोडनं
लोडन लोडन. See under rt. लुड्, p. 869.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोड्य
लोड्य लोड्य in अङ्क-ल्˚, अङ्ग-ल्˚, &c.,<BR>q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणतृण|लोणतृणं
लोणतृण लोण-तृण, अम्, n. = लवण-तृण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणा
लोणा, f. (for लवणा), a kind of sorrel (= क्षु-<BR>द्राम्लिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणाम्ला
लोणाम्ला (i. e. लोण-लवण-अम्˚), f. a kind<BR>of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणार|लोणारं|लोणारः
लोणार, अस्, m. a kind of salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणिका
लोणिका, f. = लोणाम्ला; Portulacca Oleracea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणी
लोणी in अम्ल-ल्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणितक
लोणितक लोणितक, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत|लोतं|लोतः
लोत लोत, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 86. fr. rt. 1. लू), tears [cf. लेत]; a token, sign,<BR>mark, spot; (अम्), n. booty, plunder, stolen pro-<BR>perty (= लोप्त्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत्र|लोत्रं
लोत्र, अम्, n. tears; booty, plunder, stolen goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोदी
लोदी लोदी, N. of a family or race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध|लोधः
लोध लोध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desirous, per-<BR>plexed, confused (= लुब्ध according to the Nirukta<BR>and Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 53, 23, according to<BR>others it may mean ‘red’ or may be the name of a<BR>particular animal); (अस्), m. = लोध्र below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध्र|लोध्रः
लोध्र लोध्र, अस्, m. = रोध्र, a tree the<BR>bark of which is used in dyeing, Symplocos Race-<BR>mosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध्रक
लोध्रक, अस्, m. = लोध्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप|लोपः
लोप लोप, लोपन, लोप्तृ, &c. See p. 869,<BR>col. 3, and p. 870, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ|लोभः
लोभ लोभ, लोभिन्, लोभ्य. See p. 870,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोम|लोमं|लोमः
लोम लोम, लोमक, &c. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमन्
लोमन् लोमन्, अ, n. (a later form of रोमन्,<BR>q. v.), the hair on the body of men and animals,<BR>(especially) short hair, wool, down, feathers, nap, &c.,<BR>(not so properly applicable to the hair of the head<BR>and beard nor to the mane and tail of animals); a<BR>tail (according to some).<BR>—लोम-करणी, f. a species<BR>of plant (= मांस-च्छदा).<BR>—लोम-कर्ण, अस्, m.<BR>‘hair-eared,’ a hare.<BR>—लोम-कीट, अस्, m. ‘hair-<BR>insect, ‘a louse.<BR>—लोम-कूप or लोम-गर्त, अस्,<BR>m. ‘hair-hole,’ a pore of the skin.<BR>—लोम-घ्न,<BR>अम्, n. ‘hair-destruction,’ loss of the hair through<BR>disease, morbid baldness.<BR>—लोम-पाद, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king of the Aṅgas.<BR>—लोमपाद-पुरी, f.<BR>Champā, the capital of Loma-pāda (the modern<BR>Bhāgalpur and its vicinity).<BR>—लोम-प्रवाहिन्, ई,<BR>इणी or इनी, इ, = लोम-वाहिन्.<BR>—लोम-फल, अम्,<BR>n. the fruit of Dillenia Indica.<BR>—लोम-मणि, इस्, m.<BR>an amulet made of hair.<BR>—लोम-यूक, अस्, m. a<BR>hair-louse.<BR>—लोम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, = रोम-वत्,<BR>having hair, hairy.<BR>—लोम-वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bearing<BR>or carrying hair, having feathers, feathered (said of an<BR>arrow); = रोम-वाहिन्, sharp enough to cut a hair.<BR>—लोम-विवर, अम्, n. = रोम-विवर, ‘hair-<BR>hole, ‘a pore of the skin.<BR>—लोम-विष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having poisonous hair, whose hair is poisonous (said<BR>of tigers and other animals).<BR>—लोम-वेताल, अस्, m.<BR>epithet of a particular demon.<BR>—लोम-शातन, अम्,<BR>n. an application for removing the hair of the body,<BR>a depilatory.<BR>—लोम-संहर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>causing the hair of the body to bristle, producing<BR>horripilation.<BR>—लोम-सातन, incorrect for लोम-श्˚.<BR>—लोम-सार, अस्, m. an emerald.<BR>—लोम-हर्ष,<BR>अस्, m. the bristling or erection of the hair of the<BR>body, thrill or shudder (caused by excessive joy, fear,<BR>&c.), horripilation [cf. रोम-हर्ष]; N. of a<BR>Rākṣasa.<BR>—लोम-हर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, causing<BR>bristling or erection of the hair of the body, pro-<BR>ducing horripilation, causing a shudder, exciting<BR>horror, exciting a thrill of joy, thrilling; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of Sūta (the pupil of Vyāsa and father of Sauti,<BR>who repeated the Mahā-bhārata to the Ṛṣis, cf.<BR>रोम-हर्षण); (अम्), n. the bristling of the<BR>hair of the body, horripilation, thrilling with delight,<BR>shuddering with horror.<BR>—लोम-हर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>= लोम-हर्षण.<BR>—लोम-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, = लो-<BR>म-वाहिन्.<BR>—लोम-हृत्, त्, त्, त्, removing the hair<BR>of the body, depilatory; (त्), m. yellow orpiment.<BR>—लोमाञ्च (˚म-अञ्˚), अस्, m. curling or erection<BR>of the hair of the body, a thrill of rapture, shudder,<BR>&c., = रोमाञ्च.<BR>—लोमालिका (˚म-आल्˚), f. a fox (?).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">Page0873-c+ 75</a>]<BR>—लोमावलि (˚म-आव्˚), इस्, f. the line of hair from<BR>the breast to the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोम|लोमं|लोमः
लोम at the end of comps. = लोमन्; (अम्), n.<BR>a hairy tail, tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमक
लोमक = लोमन् in प्रति-ल्˚, मृदु-ल्˚, (अ-लो-<BR>मक, having no hair, hairless.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकागृह
लोमकागृह, अम्, n. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकिन्
लोमकिन्, ई, m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमधि
लोमधि, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमश|लोमशः
लोमश, अस्, आ, अम्, hairy, woolly, downy, shaggy,<BR>bristly, covered with hair &c., made of hair, mixed<BR>with hair; containing hair; consisting in sheep or<BR>other woolly animals (as property &c.); woollen;<BR>overgrown with grass &c.; (अस्), m. a ram, sheep;<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi; of a cat (in Mahā-bh. Śānti-p. 4934);<BR>(आ), f. a fox; a female jackal (= शृगाली); an ape;<BR>green vitriol; N. of various plants, Nardostachys<BR>Jatamansi; Leea Hirta; Carpopogon Pruriens; Sida<BR>Cordifolia; Sida Rhombifolia; orris root (= वचा);<BR>Cucumis Utilissimus; = गन्ध-मांसी; = शण-<BR>पुष्पी; N. of a Śākinī or female divinity of an<BR>inferior class; an attendant on Durgā; (अम्), n. a<BR>kind of metre.<BR>—लोमश-कर्ण, अस्, m. a species<BR>of animal living in holes.<BR>—लोमश-काण्डा, f. Cu-<BR>cumis Utilissimus.<BR>—लोमश-पर्णिनी, f. Glycine<BR>Debilis.<BR>—लोमश-पुष्पक, अस्, m. Acacia Sirissa.<BR>—लोमश-मार्जार, अस्, m. the civet cat.<BR>—लो-<BR>मश-वक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. covered with hair<BR>on the breast or body.<BR>—लोमश-सक्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or लोमश-सक्थि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having hair<BR>or bristles on the thighs or hind feet; (according to<BR>Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-s. 24, 1 = बहु-रोम-<BR>पुच्छिक), having a hairy tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमश्य|लोमश्यं
लोमश्य, अम्, n. hairiness, woolliness; rough-<BR>ness; N. of a particular pronunciation of the sibi-<BR>lants (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमाययणि
लोमाययणि (?) , इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमाश|लोमाशः
लोमाश, अस्, m. a jackal or fox; [cf. लोमशा,<BR>लोपाश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमाशिका
लोमाशिका, f. the female of the jackal or fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोराय
लोराय लोराय, Nom. P. लोरायति, &c.,<BR>(said to be विलोचने.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोल|लोलः
लोल लोल, लोलित, &c. See p. 870.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलिका
लोलिका लोलिका, f. a sort of sorrel, Oxalis<BR>Pusilla, (according to some Rumex Vesicarius.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलिम्बराज
लोलिम्बराज लोलिम्ब-राज, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of the Vaidya-jīvana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुप|लोलुपः
लोलुप लोलुप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. 1. लुप्), very destructive, destroying; very de-<BR>sirous, very eager, ardently longing for, covetous, (in<BR>these senses a corruption of लोलुभ below); (आ), f.<BR>eager desire, appetite, longing, eagerness.<BR>—लोलुप-<BR>ता, f. or लोलुप-त्व, अम्, n. eager desire or longing;<BR>greediness, cupidity, desire, lust, lustfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुभ|लोलुभः
लोलुभ लोलुभ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. लुभ्), very desirous, eagerly longing for or<BR>coveting, ardently wishing for, greedy after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुव
लोलुव लोलुव, लोलूया. See p. 871, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलोर
लोलोर लोलोर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोल्लट
लोल्लट लोल्लट, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोशशरायणि
लोशशरायणि लोशशरायणि (?), इस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट्
लोष्ट् लोष्ट्, cl. 1. A. लोष्टते, लुलोष्टे,<BR>लोष्टितुम्, to heap up, accumulate, gather<BR>into a heap or lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट|लोष्टं|लोष्टः
लोष्ट, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according to Uṇādī-s. III.<BR>92. fr. rt. 1. लू), a lump of earth or clay, clod [cf.<BR>लोग]; a particular object serving as a mark; (अस्),<BR>m. a proper N.; (अम्), n. rust of iron, iron filings.<BR>—लोष्ट-घ्न, अस्, m. an agricultural implement<BR>for breaking clods, a harrow.<BR>—लोष्ट-धर, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—लोष्ट-भेदन, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>‘a clod-crusher,’ harrow.<BR>—लोष्ट-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made of clay or earth, earthen.<BR>—लोष्ट-मर्दिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, crushing or breaking clods.<BR>—१. लोष्ट-वत्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">Page0874-a+ 80</a>]<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, containing clods, mixed with lumps or<BR>particles of earth.<BR>—२. लोष्ट-वत्, ind. like a clod,<BR>as a lump of earth.<BR>—लोष्टाक्ष (˚ट-अक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.; [cf. लोगाक्ष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टक|लोष्टकः
लोष्टक, अस्, m. = लोष्ट, a clod; a particular<BR>object serving as a mark; a spot, (according to some<BR>अम्, n.); N. of various persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टन्
लोष्टन् = लोष्ट, a clod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टश
लोष्टश, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टु|लोष्टुः
लोष्टु, उस्, m. = लोष्ट, a clod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट्र
लोष्ट्र, लोष्ठ, लोष्ठक, incorrect for लोष्ट,<BR>लोष्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोस्तानी
लोस्तानी लोस्तानी, a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोह|लोहं|लोहः
लोह लोह, अस्, आ, अम् (probably a later<BR>form of रोह, fr. rt. 1. रुह्, or fr. a lost rt. रुध्,<BR>cf. रोहित, लोहित, रुधिर), red, reddish, copper-<BR>coloured; made of copper, coppery; made of iron;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. red metal, copper; iron (either<BR>crude or wrought); steel; any metal; gold; a<BR>weapon; a fish-hook; blood; (अस्), m. the red goat<BR>[cf. लोहाज]; a proper N.; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (अम्), n. aloe wood, Agallochum.<BR>—लोह-<BR>कण्टक, अस्, m. a kind of thorny shrub, Vanguiera<BR>Spinosa.<BR>—लोह-कान्त, अस्, m. a magnet, loadstone.<BR>—लोह-कार, अस्, m. a worker in iron, smelter of<BR>iron, iron-smith, blacksmith; (ई), f., N. of the Tantra<BR>goddess Atibalā.<BR>—लोह-कारक, अस्, m. an iron-<BR>smith, blacksmith.<BR>—लोहकार-भस्त्रा, f. a black-<BR>smith's bellows.<BR>—लोह-किट्ट, अम्, n. rust of iron<BR>or iron filings.<BR>—लोह-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—लोह-घातक, अस्, m. ‘iron-striker,’ a<BR>blacksmith.<BR>—लोह-चारिणी, f., N. of a river.<BR>—लो-<BR>ह-चूर्ण, अम्, n. rust of iron, iron filings.<BR>—लोह-<BR>ज, अम्, n. bell-metal; rust of iron or iron filings.<BR>—लोह-जङ्घ, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—लोह-जाल, अम्, n. an<BR>iron net, a coat of mail.<BR>—लोह-जित्, त्, m. ‘con-<BR>quering iron (in hardness), ‘a diamond.<BR>—लोह-ता-<BR>रणी, f., N. of a river, (also read लोह-तारिणी, लोह-<BR>चारिणी.)<BR>—लोह-दारक, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>twenty-one hells (Manu IV. 90).<BR>—लोह-द्राविन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, melting copper or iron, fusing metal; (ई),<BR>m. borax.<BR>—लोह-नगर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—लोह-नाल, अस्, m. an iron arrow.<BR>—लोह-पाश,<BR>अस्, m. an iron chain.<BR>—लोह-पुर, N. of a place.<BR>—लोह-पृष्ठ, अस्, m. ‘iron-backed,’ a heron.<BR>—लोह-प्रतिमा, f. an iron image; an anvil.<BR>—लोह-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, studded with iron (as<BR>a war-club).<BR>—लोह-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of iron<BR>or copper, composed or consisting of iron, iron.<BR>—लोह-मारक, अस्, इका, अम्, calcining metal;<BR>(अस्), m. Achyranthes Triandra.<BR>—लोह-मुक्तिका, f.<BR>a red pearl.<BR>—लोह-मेखल, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing<BR>a metal girdle; (आ), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR>—लोह-यष्टी, f., N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—लोह-रजस्, अस्, n. iron-dust, rust of iron<BR>or iron filings.<BR>—लोह-राजक, अम्, n. silver.<BR>—लो-<BR>ह-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. a boil or abscess filled with blood.<BR>—लोह-वर, अम्, n. the most precious metal, gold.<BR>—लोह-वर्मन्, अ, n. iron armour, mail.<BR>—लोह-<BR>वाल, अस्, m. a kind of rice. —लोह-शङ्कु^1, उस्, m.<BR>an iron pike, iron stake or spike; (उस्), m. ‘iron-<BR>spiked, ‘N. of one of the twenty-one hells (Manu<BR>IV. 90).<BR>—लोह-श्लेषण, अस्, ई, अम्, uniting<BR>metals; (अस्), m. borax.<BR>—लोह-सङ्कर, अम्, n.<BR>blue steel.<BR>—लोहाकर (˚ह-आक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>town.<BR>—लोहा-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (लोहा for लोह),<BR>Ved. red-eared.<BR>—लोहाङ्गारक (˚ह-अङ्˚), N. of a<BR>hell (‘pit of red-hot charcoal’).<BR>—लोहाचल (˚ह-<BR>अच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—लोहाज (˚ह-<BR>अज), अस्, m. the red goat.<BR>—लोहाज-वक्त्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of one of Skanda's attendants.<BR>—लोहाण्ड<BR>(˚ह-अण्˚ or ˚ह-आण्˚), see Gaṇa Gaurādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 41.<BR>—लोहाभिसार (˚ह-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a military ceremony performed on the tenth day<BR>after the Nī-rājana, (this ceremony or lustration of<BR>arms was formerly observed by kings before com-<BR>mencing a campaign, but is now usually confined to<BR>the domestic decoration and worship of the soldiers’<BR>weapons); = लोहाभिहार.<BR>—लोहाभिहार (˚ह-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-b" target="_blank">Page0874-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, m. = नी-राजन.<BR>—लोहामिष (˚ह-<BR>आम्˚), अम्, n. the flesh of the red-haired goat.<BR>—लो-<BR>हायस (˚ह-आय्˚), अम्, n., Ved. any metal mixed<BR>with copper.<BR>—लोहार्गल (˚ह-अर्˚), अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR>—लोहोत्तम (˚ह-उत्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>best metal, gold.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 311-315. note: dental nasal -> guttural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहक
लोहक = लोह in अष्ट-लोहक, इन्दु-ल्˚, त्रि-ल्˚,<BR>पञ्च-ल्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहर
लोहर, N. of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहल|लोहलः
लोहल, अस्, आ, अम्, iron, made of iron; lisping,<BR>speaking inarticulately; (अस्), m. the principal ring<BR>of a chain (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहि
लोहि, n. a kind of borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिका
लोहिका, f. an iron pot or vessel (being a sort of<BR>large shallow bowl, sometimes of iron, but usually<BR>of wood and bound with iron, used for washing<BR>rice, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहित|लोहितं|लोहितः
1. लोहित, अस्, आ or लोहिनी, अम् (a later form of<BR>रोहित, q. v.), red, red-coloured, reddish; made of<BR>copper, copper, metal; (अस्), m. red (the colour),<BR>any red colour; a particular disease attacking the<BR>eyelids; a kind of precious stone; a species of rice;<BR>a sort of bean or lentil; Dioscorea Purpurea; a kind<BR>of fish, Cyprinus Rohita; a sort of deer; a snake,<BR>serpent; the planet Mars; N. of a Nāga or serpent-<BR>demon; of a river (the Brahma-putra); of a sea; of<BR>a lake; of a country; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class<BR>of gods under the twelfth Manu; the descendants<BR>of Lohita; (आ), f., N. of one of the seven tongues<BR>of fire; of two plants (= वराह-क्रान्ता, रक्त-<BR>पुनर्नवा); = लोहिनी below; (इनी), f. a woman<BR>with a red-coloured skin or red with anger; (अम्),<BR>n. copper, metal; blood, (in this sense also अस्, m.);<BR>battle; saffron; red sanders; a kind of sandal-wood<BR>(= गो-शीर्ष); a kind of Agallochum; an imperfect<BR>form of rainbow.<BR>—लोहित-कल्माष, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>variegated with red, red-spotted.<BR>—लोहित-कूट, N.<BR>of a place.<BR>—लोहित-कृष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, of a<BR>reddish black colour, dark-red.<BR>—लोहित-क्षय,<BR>अस्, m. loss of blood.<BR>—लोहित-क्षयक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, suffering from loss of blood.<BR>—लोहित-क्षीर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. yielding red or bloody milk.<BR>—लो-<BR>हित-गङ्ग, N. of a place; (अम्), ind, where the<BR>Ganges appears red.<BR>—लोहित-गङ्गक, N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—लोहित-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, red-necked, hav-<BR>ing a red neck; (अस्), m. epithet of Agni.<BR>—लोहित-<BR>चन्दन, अम्, n. saffron.<BR>—लोहित-जह्नु, उस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—लोहित-ता, f. or लोहित-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>redness, red colour.<BR>—लोहित-ध्वज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>red-bannered, having a red flag; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a particular association of persons.<BR>—लोहित-नयन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, red-eyed, having the eyes reddened with<BR>anger or passion.<BR>—लोहित-पाद-देश, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a place.<BR>—लोहित-पित्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, subject to<BR>hemorrhage, suffering from hemorrhage; [cf. रक्त-<BR>पित्तिन्.]<BR>—लोहित-पुर, N. of a place.<BR>—लोहित-<BR>पुष्प, अस्, आ, अम्, red-flowering, bearing red<BR>flowers.<BR>—लोहित-पुष्पक, अस्, आ, अम्, red-flower-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. the granate tree.<BR>—लोहित-मुक्ता, f.<BR>a red pearl.<BR>—लोहित-मृत्तिका, f. red earth, red<BR>chalk, ruddle.<BR>—लोहित-राग, अस्, m. a red colour,<BR>red hue.<BR>—लोहित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing blood.<BR>—लोहित-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having red or blood-<BR>stained garments.<BR>—लोहित-शतपत्त्र, अम्, n. a<BR>red lotus-flower.<BR>—लोहित-शवल or लोहित-सारङ्-<BR>ग, अस्, आ, अम् variegated with red, dappled with red.<BR> — 1. लोहिताक्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, m. a red die (used<BR>in gaming).<BR>—२. लोहिताक्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>red-eyed; (अस्), m. a kind of snake; the Indian<BR>cuckoo; N. of Viṣṇu; of one of Skanda's attend-<BR>ants; of a man; (ई), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda; scil. सिरा, an artery or vein<BR>situated either at the thigh-joint or at the arm-joint;<BR>(अम्), n. a part of the arm and of the thigh, the<BR>place where these are joined to the body, the arm-<BR>joint, thigh-joint, hip.<BR>—लोहिता-गिरि, इस्, m. (लोहिता<BR>for लोहित), N. of a mountain.<BR>—लोहिताङ्ग (˚त-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘red-limbed,’ the planet Mars; a species<BR>of plant (= कम्पिल्लक).<BR>—लोहितानन (˚त-आन्˚),<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, red-faced; (अस्), m. an ichneumon.<BR>—लो-<BR>हिता-मुखी, f., N. of a club (in the Rāmāyaṇa).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">Page0874-c+ 78</a>]<BR>—लोहितायस् (˚त-अय्˚), अस्, n. ‘red-iron,’ copper.<BR>—लोहितायस, अस्, आ, अम्, made of red metal; (अम्),<BR>n. (probably) copper.<BR>—लोहितार्ण (˚त-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—लोहितार्द्र (˚त-आर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, wet or dripping with blood, soaked in blood.<BR>—लोहितार्मन् (˚त-अर्˚), अ, n. a red swelling or<BR>blood-shot appearance in the whites of the eyes.<BR>—लोहितावभास (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>red appearance, reddish.<BR>—लोहिताशोक (˚त-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a red-flowering Aśoka.<BR>—लोहिताश्व (˚त-<BR>अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having or driving red horses.<BR>—लो-<BR>हितास्य (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a red or blood-<BR>stained mouth.<BR>—लोहिताहि (˚त-अहि), इस्, m. a red<BR>snake.<BR>—लोहिती-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to be<BR>or become red, to be reddened.<BR>—लोहितेक्षण<BR>(˚त-ईक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, red-eyed.<BR>—लोहितैत (˚त-<BR>एत), अस्, आ, अम्, = रोहितैत, variegated with red.<BR>—लोहितोत्पल (˚त-उत्˚), अम्, n. the flower of<BR>Nymphæa Rubra.<BR>—लोहितोद (˚त-उद), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having blood-red water, having red water, hav-<BR>ing blood instead of water; (अस्), m., N. of a parti-<BR>cular hell.<BR>—लोहितोर्ण (˚त-ऊर्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>red wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहित|लोहितं|लोहितः
2. लोहित, Nom. P. लोहितति, &c., to be or become<BR>red, redden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितक|लोहितकं|लोहितकः
लोहितक, अस्, इका or लोहिनिका, अम्, red, of a<BR>red colour, reddish; (अस्), m. a ruby; a kind of rice;<BR>the planet Mars; N. of a Stūpa; (इका), f. a parti-<BR>cular vein or artery; a species of plant; (अम्), n.<BR>bell-metal; calx of brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिताय|लोहितायः
लोहिताय, Nom. P. A. लोहितायति, -ते, &c., to<BR>be or become red, redden, grow red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितायन
लोहितायन, अस्, m. a patronymic, (probably for<BR>लौहितायन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितायनि
लोहितायनि, इस्, f. a patronymic, (perhaps for लौ-<BR>हितायनि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितिमन्
लोहितिमन्, आ, m. redness, red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहित्य|लोहित्यः
लोहित्य, अस्, m. a kind of rice; N. of a man; of<BR>the Brahma-putra river; of a village; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>celestial female (in Hari-vaṃśa 9534); of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिनिका
लोहिनिका. See under लोहितक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिनी
लोहिनी. See under 1. लोहित, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिनीका
लोहिनीका, f. (fr. लोहिनी), Ved. red glow or lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिन्य
लोहिन्य, अस्, m. a patronymic, (probably for लो-<BR>हित्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकाक्ष
लौकाक्ष लौकाक्ष, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>school, (perhaps for लौगाक्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकायतिक|लौकायतिकः
लौकायतिक लौकायतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>लोकायत), following the teaching of Cārvāka; (अस्),<BR>m. a follower of Cārvāka, a materialist, atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकिक|लौकिकः
लौकिक लौकिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लोक), worldly,<BR>mundane, terrestrial, popular, familiar (as opposed to<BR>अ-लौकिक, ‘technical’), belonging to ordinary life,<BR>occurring in every-day life, vulgar, common, usual,<BR>ordinary, fashionable, publicly received, customary,<BR>temporal, secular, not sacred (as opposed to वैदिक,<BR>आर्ष, शास्त्रीय); belonging to the world of (at the<BR>end of a comp., e. g. ब्रह्म-लौकिक, belonging<BR>to the world of Brahmā); (आस्), m. pl. common or<BR>ordinary men (as opposed to ‘the learned, initiated,’<BR>&c.), men in general, the human race; men familiar<BR>with the ways of the world, men of the world;<BR>(अम्), n. anything occurring in the world, the laws<BR>or ordinances of the world, general custom, usage.<BR>—लौकिक-ता, f. or लौकिक-त्व, अम्, n. worldli-<BR>ness, commonness, worldly currency or custom, popu-<BR>larity, usual custom, usage, general prevalence.<BR>—लौ-<BR>किक-विषय-विचार, अस्, m. ‘consideration of ordi-<BR>nary objects, ‘N. of a philosophical treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौक्य
लौक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the world,<BR>being in the world, extended through the world,<BR>generally diffused, worldly, mundane, terrestrial,<BR>human, general, ordinary, common, common-place;<BR>(अस्), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौगाक्षि
लौगाक्षि लौगाक्षि, इस्, m. (fr. लोगाक्ष),<BR>a patronymic, N. of the author of a Dharma-śāstra.<BR>—लौगाक्षि-भास्कर, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of several modern philosophical works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0874-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौठरथ
लौठरथ लौठरथ, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौड्
लौड् लौड् (= rts. लोट्, लोड्), cl. 1. P.<BR>लौडति, &c., to be foolish or mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौपायन
लौपायन लौपायन, अस्, m., Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौप्स
