लौल्य|लौल्यं
लौल्य लौल्य, अम्, n. (fr. लोल), restlessness,<BR>instability, inconstancy, fickleness; lustfulness, eager-<BR>ness, eager desire, greediness, passion, (अ-लौल्य,<BR>अम्, n. absence of all desire.)<BR>—लौल्य-ता, f. lustful-<BR>ness, eager desire.<BR>—लौल्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, eagerly<BR>desirous, eager, greedy, avaricious, lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौश
लौश लौश, अम्, n. (fr. लुश), N. of various<BR>Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौह|लौहः
लौह लौह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लोह), made of<BR>copper or metal, coppery, metallic; made of iron,<BR>composed or consisting of iron, belonging to iron,<BR>iron; coming from or belonging to the red-coloured<BR>goat; copper-coloured, red; (आ), f. a metal or iron<BR>cooking-pot, kettle, pan; (अम्), n. iron, metal.<BR>—लौह-कार, अस्, m. = लोह-कार, a blacksmith.<BR>—लौह-चारक, अस्, m., N. of a hell; [cf. लोह-<BR>दारक.]<BR>—लौह-ज, अम्, n. = लोह-ज, the rust<BR>of iron.<BR>—लौह-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of a treatise<BR>on metals.<BR>—लौह-बन्ध, अस्, अम्, m. n. an<BR>iron chain, iron fetters.<BR>—लौह-भाण्ड, अम्, n.<BR>an iron vessel, metal mortar.<BR>—लौह-भू, ऊस्, f. a<BR>metal pan, boiler, caldron, kettle.<BR>—लौह-मल,<BR>अम्, n. the rust of iron.<BR>—लौह-शङ्कु, उस्, m. =<BR>लोह-शङ्कु.<BR>—लौह-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a Śāstra treat-<BR>ing of metals.<BR>—लौहाचार्य (˚ह-आच्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>teacher of metallurgy or the art of working metals.<BR>—लौहात्मन् (˚ह-आत्˚), आ, m. = लौह-भू.<BR>—लौहेष (˚ह-ईष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a metal<BR>pole (said of a carriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहायन
लौहायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Loha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहायस
लौहायस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. लोहायस), made of<BR>metal, metallic, made of copper, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहि
लौहि लौहि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Aṣṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित|लौहितः
लौहित लौहित, अस्, m. (fr. 1. लोहित), the<BR>trident of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहितध्वज
लौहितध्वज, अस्, m. (fr. लोहित-ध्वज), a<BR>follower of the Lohita-dhvajas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहितीक|लौहितीकः
लौहितीक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. लोहित), reddish, hav-<BR>ing a reddish lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित्य|लौहित्यं|लौहित्यः
लौहित्य, अस्, m. (fr. 1. लोहित), a patronymic;<BR>N. of a river, the Brahma-putra; of a sea; of a<BR>mountain; of a Tīrtha, (in this sense probably अम्,<BR>n.); (अम्), n. red colour, redness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित्यायनी
लौहित्यायनी, f. (feminine form of the above),<BR>a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्पी
ल्पी ल्पी or ल्यी, cl. 9. P. ल्पिनाति, ल्यिनाति,<BR>&c., to join, unite, be attached to, mix<BR>with, (various readings for rt. 1. ली.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्युट्
ल्युट् ल्युट्, (in grammar) a technical symbol<BR>for the Kṛt affix अन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्वी
ल्वी ल्वी, cl. 9. P. ल्विनाति, ल्वीनाति, &c., to<BR>go, move, approach, (a various reading for<BR>rt. व्ली or प्ली.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्वीन
ल्वीन, अस्, आ, अम्, gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व 1. व, the twenty-ninth consonant of<BR>the Devanāgarī alphabet, being the semivowel of the<BR>vowels उ, ऊ, and having the sound of the English<BR>v, except when forming the last member of a con-<BR>junct consonant, in which case it is pronounced like<BR>w; it is often confounded with the labial consonant<BR>ब्, with which it may frequently be interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व 2. व, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. वा), air, wind;<BR>the arm; N. of Varuṇa; addressing; conciliation;<BR>auspiciousness; reverence; a dwelling; the residence<BR>of Varuṇa; the ocean, water; a tiger; cloth; the escu-<BR>lent root of the water-lily; (आ), f. going; hurting, in-<BR>jury; an arrow; weaving; (अम्), n. a sort of incantation<BR>or Mantra (of which the object is the deity Varuṇa);<BR>= प्र-चेतस्; (अस्, आ, अम्), strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व 3. व, ind. = इव, like, as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश|वंशः
वंश वंश, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. वन्,<BR>to sound, or connected with rt. वङ्क्), a bamboo<BR>cane, bamboo; a staff; a term for the rafters and laths<BR>fastened to the beams of a house (as generally made<BR>of split bamboos), or laths running across a roof [cf.<BR>प्राचीन-वंश, प्राग्-वंश], a cross-beam, joint;<BR>a sort of sugar-cane; the Śāl tree, Shorea Robusta;<BR>a reed-pipe, tube, flute, pipe, fife; the back-bone,<BR>spine [cf. पृष्ठ-व्˚]; the central projecting part<BR>of a cimeter or sabre; the joints in a bamboo; the<BR>line of a pedigree or genealogy (from its resemblance<BR>to the succession of joints in a bamboo), a lineage,<BR>race, family, stock; offspring, a son; a dynasty, race<BR>of kings; a succession or collection of similar things<BR>(as of chariots, stars, &c.), an assemblage, multitude,<BR>host; a particular measure of length (= 10 Hastas);<BR>bamboo-manna; N. of Viṣṇu ?; (आ), f., N. of an<BR>Apsaras (a daughter of Prādhā); (ई), f. a flute,<BR>pipe; an artery, vein; a particular weight (= 4 Kar-<BR>shas); bamboo-manna; [cf. Goth. rausa, ‘a reed;’<BR>Old Germ. rohr.]<BR>—वंश-ऋषि, इस्, m. a Ṛṣi<BR>mentioned in a Vaṃśa-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—वंश-कठिन,<BR>अस्, m. a clump or thicket of bamboos.<BR>—वंश-<BR>कफ, अम्, n. ‘bamboo-phlegm,’ cottony or floc-<BR>culent seeds floating in the air.<BR>—वंश-कर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, making or founding a family, propagating or<BR>perpetuating a race; (अस्), m. an ancestor; a proper<BR>N.; (आ). f., N. of a river rising in the Mahendra<BR>mountains.<BR>—वंश-कर्पूर-रोचना, f. = वंश-<BR>रोचना, q. v.<BR>—वंशकर्म-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, doing<BR>bamboo-work, engaged in the manufacture of baskets,<BR>&c.<BR>—वंश-कर्मन्, अ, n. bamboo-work, manu-<BR>facture of baskets, &c.<BR>—वंश-कीर्त्ति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>having great family renown, celebrated.<BR>—वंश-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, = वंशकर्म-कृत्; (त्), m. the<BR>founder of a family.<BR>—वंश-क्रमागत (˚म-<BR>आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, descended or inherited lineally,<BR>what comes from one's family in regular succession,<BR>obtained by family inheritance.<BR>—वंश-क्षय, अस्,<BR>m. decay of a family.<BR>—वंश-क्षीरि, f. bamboo-<BR>manna.<BR>—वंश-गुल्म, N. of a sacred bathing-<BR>place.<BR>—वंश-चरित्र, अम्, n. the history of any<BR>race or dynasty, a genealogical account of the doings<BR>of any family.<BR>—वंश-चिन्तक, अस्, m. one familiar<BR>with pedigrees, a genealogist.<BR>—वंश-च्छेत्तृ, ता,<BR>m. one who cuts off the line of descent, the last of<BR>a family or race.<BR>—वंश-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, made of<BR>or produced from bamboos; born in the family of,<BR>belonging to the family of (with loc. or at the end<BR>of a comp.), sprung from a good family; (अस्), m.<BR>the seed of the bamboo; (आ, अम्), f. n. bamboo-<BR>manna.<BR>—वंश-तण्डुल, अस्, m. the seed of the<BR>bamboo.<BR>—वंश-दला, f. a kind of plant or grass<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-c" target="_blank">Page0875-c+ 81</a>]<BR>(= vaṃśa-pattrī, jīrikā).<BR>—वंश-धर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, carrying or holding a bamboo, &c.; maintain-<BR>ing or supporting a family.<BR>—वंश-धान्य, अम्,<BR>n. the seed of the bamboo.<BR>—वंश-धारा, f., N. of<BR>a river rising in the Mahendra mountains.<BR>—वंश-<BR>धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, = वंश-धर.<BR>—वंश-नर्तिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘family-dancer,’ a buffoon.<BR>—वंश-नाडिका, f.<BR>a tube or pipe made of bamboo.<BR>—वंश-नाथ, अस्,<BR>m. the head of a family, chief of a race.<BR>—वंश-<BR>नालिका, f. a pipe or lute made of bamboo, a reed,<BR>flute.<BR>—वंश-नेत्र, अम्, n. a kind of sugar-cane,<BR>the root of sugar-cane (= इक्षु-मूल).<BR>—वंश-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. a bamboo leaf; a kind of metre, =<BR>वंशपत्त्र-पतित; (अस्), m. a reed; (ई), f. a<BR>particular kind of grass; = नाडी-हिङ्गु.<BR>—वंश-<BR>पत्त्रक, अस्, m. a reed; white sugar-cane; a sort<BR>of fish, Cynoglossus Lingua; (अम्), n. yellow orpi-<BR>ment.<BR>—वंशपत्त्र-पतित, अम्, n. ‘fallen on a<BR>bamboo leaf, ‘a species of metre, four times ¯˘˘<BR>¯˘¯˘˘˘¯, ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯.<BR>—वंश-परम्परा,<BR>f. family succession, lineage, descent.<BR>—वंश-पात्र-<BR>कारिणी, f. a woman who makes bamboo vessels or<BR>baskets.<BR>—वंश-पीत, अस्, m., N. of a plant (=<BR>कण-गुग्गुलु).<BR>—वंश-पुष्पा, f., N. of a plant<BR>(= सह-देवी).<BR>—वंश-पूरक, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>sugar-cane (= इक्षु-मूल).<BR>—वंश-प्रतिष्ठा-<BR>न-कर, अस्, m. one who establishes his family on<BR>a firm foundation.<BR>—वंश-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a chronological list of ancient teachers.<BR>—वंश-<BR>भार, अस्, m. a load of bamboos.<BR>—वंश-भृत्,<BR>त्, m. the supporter of a family, head of a race.<BR>—वंश-भोज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be possessed by<BR>a family, hereditary; (अम्), n. an hereditary estate.<BR>—वंश-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of bamboo.<BR>—वंश-मूलक, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-<BR>place.<BR>—वंश-राज, अस्, m. a very high or lofty<BR>bamboo; N. of a king.<BR>—वंश-रोचना or वंश-<BR>लोचना, f. an earthy concretion of a milk-white<BR>colour formed in the hollow of the bamboo and<BR>known by the name of bamboo-manna.<BR>—वंश-<BR>लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. the fortune of a family.<BR>—वंश-<BR>वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, increasing or prospering a<BR>family; (अम्), n. the act of causing prosperity to<BR>a family.<BR>—वंश-वर्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, increasing or<BR>exalting a family.<BR>—वंश-वितति, इस्, f. a clump or<BR>thicket of bamboos; family, descent.<BR>—वंश-विदा-<BR>रिणी, f. a woman employed in splitting bamboos.<BR>—वंश-विशुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, (made) of a good<BR>bamboo; of a pure or good family.<BR>—वंश-विस्तर,<BR>अस्, m. a complete genealogy.<BR>—वंश-वृद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. prosperity of a family.<BR>—वंश-शर्करा,<BR>f. = वंश-रोचना.<BR>—वंश-शलाका, f. a bamboo<BR>peg or screw at the lower end of a Vīṇā or lute,<BR>(according to some) the bamboo pipe that forms the<BR>body of the lute; any small bamboo pin or stake<BR>(as the bar of a cage, &c.).<BR>—वंश-समाचार, अस्,<BR>m. family usage.<BR>—वंश-स्तनित, अम्, n. a species<BR>of the Jagatī metre (= वंश-स्थ-विल).<BR>—वंश-<BR>स्थ, अम्, n. (or आ, f.?), a particular metre (=<BR>वंश-स्थ-विल).<BR>—वंश-स्थ-विल, अम्, n. the<BR>hollow or cavity found in a bamboo cane; N. of a<BR>species of the Jagatī metre, four times ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘<BR>¯˘¯˘¯ (the beginning of the Ṛtu-saṃhāra is in<BR>this metre.)<BR>—वंश-स्थिति, इस्, f. the state or con-<BR>dition of a family.<BR>—वंश-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, desti-<BR>tute of family or descendants, having no kindred.<BR>—वंशागत (˚श-आग्), अस्, आ, अम्, what comes<BR>from one's family, inherited, obtained by inheritance.<BR>—वंशाग्र (˚श-अग्˚), अम्, n. the point or end of<BR>a bamboo cane; the shoot of a bamboo.<BR>—वंश-<BR>कुर (˚श-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a bamboo shoot or sprout.<BR>—वंशानुकीर्तन (˚श-अन्˚), अम्, n. the publish-<BR>ing or proclaiming a family, genealogy.<BR>—वंशानु-<BR>क्रम (˚श-अन्˚), अस्, m. family succession, genea-<BR>logy, lineal inheritance.<BR>—वंशानुग (˚श-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being on or along the central projecting<BR>part of a sword; passing from family to family.<BR>—वंशानुचरित (˚श-अन्˚), अम्, n. the history of<BR>a family or dynasty, a genealogical list (one of the<BR>five Lakṣaṇas or distinguishing marks of a Pu-<BR>rāṇa).<BR>—वंशानुवंश-चरित (˚श-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">Page0876-a+ 78</a>]<BR>the history of both old and more recent families<BR>(one of the five Lakṣaṇas of a Purāṇa).<BR>—वंशा-<BR>वती, f. a proper N.<BR>—वंशावली (˚श-आव्˚), f. the<BR>line of a family, a pedigree, genealogy.<BR>—वंशाह्व<BR>(˚श-आह्˚), अस्, m. bamboo-manna.<BR>—वंशी-धर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, holding a flute or pipe; (अस्), m. a flute-<BR>player, piper; N. of Kṛṣṇa; of a learned man.<BR>—वंशी-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, holding or carrying a<BR>flute; (ई), m. a flute-player; N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—वंशी-<BR>वदन, अस्, m., N. of a Scholiast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशक|वंशकं|वंशकः
वंशक, अस्, m. a large kind of sugar-cane; a joint<BR>in a bamboo; a small fish, Cynoglossus Lingua; N. of<BR>a king; (इका), f. a kind of pipe or flute; aloe wood,<BR>Agallochum, (in this sense also अम्, n.; cf. वंशिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशिक|वंशिकं
वंशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>bamboo, pertaining to a family &c., lineal, genealo-<BR>gical; (अम्), n. aloe wood; [cf. वंशिका above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशिन्
वंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, belonging to a family; [cf.<BR>स्व-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशिवाद्य
वंशि-वाद्य, अम्, n. a flute, pipe, (probably<BR>wrong for वंशी-वाद्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशी
वंशी. See under वंश, p. 875, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशीय
वंशीय, अस्, आ, अम्, of or belonging to a family,<BR>of a good family, of the same family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश्य|वंश्यः
वंश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or attached to the<BR>main beam; connected with the back-bone or spine;<BR>of or belonging to a family; of a good family, of<BR>the same family; peculiar to a family; genealogical,<BR>lineal; (अस्), m. a cross-beam, joist; a bone in the<BR>arm; a bone in the leg; a member of a family; a<BR>son, lineal descendant, posterity; an ancestor, fore-<BR>father; a kinsman from seven generations above and<BR>seven below; a pupil; (आस्), m. pl. ancestors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंसग|वंसगः
वंसग वंसग, अस्, m., Ved. a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंह्
वंह् वंह्. See rt. बंह्, p. 671, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंहिष्ठ
वंहिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (see बंहिष्ठ), most,<BR>very much or great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंहीयस्
वंहीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (see बंहीयस्), more,<BR>greater; very much or large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्
वक् वक् (a form of rt. वङ्क्, q. v.), to go<BR>crookedly, &c., (in Ṛg-veda VII. 21, 3.<BR>वावक्रे = निर्गच्छन्ति, they issued forth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक
वक, अस्, m. a heron, crane, Ardea Nivea; a<BR>hypocrite, cheat, rogue, deceiver (the crane being<BR>regarded as an animal of great cunning and deceit<BR>as well as sagacity); a particular tree, Sesbana Gran-<BR>diflora; an apparatus for calcining or subliming<BR>metals or minerals (consisting of two crucibles, one<BR>inverted over the other and placed over a fire); N.<BR>of a Ṛṣi (having the patronymic Dālbhi or Dālbhya);<BR>of a Rākṣasa or demon (killed by Bhīma or Bhīma-<BR>sena, see वक-वध); of an Asura (said to have<BR>assumed the form of a crane and to have been con-<BR>quered by Kṛṣṇa); of Kuvera; of a king; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people; (ई), f. = पूतना.<BR>—वक-<BR>कच्छ, N. of a district.<BR>—वक-कल्प, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a particular Kalpa or period of the world.<BR>—वक-<BR>चर, अस्, m. = वक-व्रतिन्.<BR>—वक-चिञ्चिका, f. a<BR>sort of fish.<BR>—वक-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of Vaka,’<BR>N. of Bhīma-sena.<BR>—वक-त्व, अम्, n. the state or<BR>condition of a crane.<BR>—वक-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Dvīpa.<BR>—वक-धूप, अस्, m. a compound per-<BR>fume, (also read वृक-धूप.)<BR>—वक-नख, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra, (also read वक-नक.)<BR>—वक-निसूदन, अस्, m. ‘destroyer of Vaka,’ N.<BR>of Bhīma-sena.<BR>—वक-पञ्चक, अम्, n. a space of<BR>time consisting of the last five Tithis of the bright<BR>half of the month Kārttika.<BR>—वक-पुष्प, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of tree, Æschynomene Grandiflora; (अम्),<BR>n. the flower of this tree.<BR>—वक-यन्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>‘crane-like instrument,’ epithet of a particular form<BR>of retort.<BR>—वक-राज, अस्, m. the king of the cranes<BR>(named Rāja-dharman, he was son of Kaśyapa, see<BR>Mahā-bh. Śānti-p. 6336).<BR>—वक-वध, अस्, m.<BR>‘the killing of Vaka,’ N. of a section of the Ādi-<BR>parvan of the Mahā-bh. 6103-6315 (describing<BR>how Bhīma, while resident in the city of Eka-cakrā,<BR>delivered his family and the whole neighbourhood<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">Page0876-b+ 81</a>]<BR>from the tyranny of the demon named Vaka or<BR>Baka, who forced the citizens to send him every day<BR>a dish of food by a man whom he always devoured<BR>as his daintiest morsel at the end of the repast).<BR>—वक-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a kind of tree.<BR>—वक-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, one who acts or behaves like a crane,<BR>hypocritical; (इस्), m. a false or hypocritical devotee,<BR>hypocrite (compared to the crane which stations itself<BR>cunningly by a pool apparently absorbed in meditation<BR>till it sees a fish on which to dart).<BR>—वक-वैरिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘Vaka's enemy,’ N. of Bhīma-sena.<BR>—वक-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n. ‘crane-like observance,’ the conduct<BR>of a crane, hypocrisy.<BR>—वकव्रत-चर, अस्, m.<BR>one who acts like a crane, a hypocrite.<BR>—वक-व्र-<BR>तिक, अस्, or वक-व्रतिन्, ई, m. ‘one whose acts or<BR>observances are like those of a crane, ‘a false devotee,<BR>religious hypocrite, one who assumes the appearance<BR>of devotion or meditation for interested purposes,<BR>(see वक-वृत्ति.)<BR>—वक-सक्थ, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.; (आस्), m. pl. Vaka-saktha's descendants.<BR>—वक-<BR>सह-वासिन्, ई, m. ‘dwelling in the same abode as<BR>the crane, ‘a lotus.<BR>—वकारि (˚क-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of Vaka,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—वकेश (˚क-<BR>ईश), अस्, m., N. of a temple founded by Vaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकाची
वकाची, f. a sort of fish (= वक-चिञ्चिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकाय
वकाय, Nom. P. वकायति, &c., to represent or<BR>act like the Asura Vaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकायत्
वकायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, acting like the Asura Vaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकुल|वकुलः
वकुल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. वक् or वङ्क्),<BR>a kind of tree, Mimusops Elengi; a kind of drug;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a plant, = कटुका; (ई), f. a sort of<BR>drug (commonly called Kākolī); (अम्), n. the fra-<BR>grant flower of Mimusops Elengi.<BR>—वकुलावलिका<BR>(˚ल-आव्˚), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकुलित
वकुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with Mimusops<BR>Elengi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकूल|वकूलः
