वकेरुका
वकेरुका, f. a small crane; the branch of a tree<BR>bent by the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकोट
वकोट, अस्, m. a crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्र|वक्रं|वक्रः
वक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, winding, tortuous,<BR>curved, bent, bowed, meandering, curled, curly (as<BR>hair &c.); having an apparently backward motion,<BR>retrograde (said of planets); prosodially long (the<BR>form of the long mark being supposed to be curved),<BR>crooked in disposition, cunning, fraudulent, dishonest,<BR>prevaricating, indirect, evasive, ambiguous; cruel,<BR>malignant; (अस्), m. the planet Mars; the planet<BR>Saturn; Rudra or Śiva; the Asura Tripura; N. of<BR>a king of the Karūṣas; of a Rākṣasa; = पर्पट;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people, (also read चक्र); (आ),<BR>f., N. of a particular musical instrument; scil. गति,<BR>N. of a particular variation in the course of Mercury;<BR>(अम्), n. the winding course of a river, the arm or<BR>bend of a stream; the apparent retrograde motion<BR>of a planet; (in surgery) a form of fracture (when a<BR>bone is bent in a particular way or only partially<BR>broken); [cf. according to some, Lat. varus: Hib.<BR>fiar, ‘crooked, wicked;’ fiaras, ‘crookedness;’ fia-<BR>raim, ‘I incline, bend.’]<BR>—वक्र-कण्ट, अस्, m.<BR>‘having crooked thorns,’ the jujube tree.<BR>—वक्र-<BR>कण्टक, अस्, m. Acacia Catechu.<BR>—वक्र-खड्ग<BR>or वक्र-खड्गक, अस्, m. a bent sword, a cimeter,<BR>sabre.<BR>—वक्र-गति, इस्, f. crooked or winding course,<BR>tortuous motion, apparent retrograde motion or re-<BR>trogression (said of the course of Mars &c.); (इस्, इस्,<BR>इ), moving crookedly or tortuously, meandering.<BR>—वक्र-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going crookedly, moving<BR>tortuously or in zigzag, fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>—व-<BR>क्र-ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘crooked-necked,’ a camel.<BR>—व-<BR>क्र-चञ्चु, उस्, m. ‘crooked-beaked,’ a parrot.<BR>—वक्र-ता, f. or वक्र-त्व, अम्, n. crookedness,<BR>curvature, curvedness, tortuousness; retrograde motion<BR>(in astronomy); the going crooked or wrong, failure,<BR>mishap; perverseness, falseness, dishonesty, ambi-<BR>guity, prevarication.<BR>—वक्र-तुण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>crooked-beaked, having a crooked face; (अस्), m. a<BR>parrot; N. of Gaṇeśa (so called as represented with<BR>the trunk of an elephant).<BR>—वक्र-दंष्ट्र, अस्,<BR>m. ‘crooked-tusked,’ a boar, (wrongly read वक्त्र-<BR>द्˚.)<BR>—वक्र-दृष्टि, इस्, f. oblique vision, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-c" target="_blank">Page0876-c+ 75</a>]<BR>oblique look, squint; malignant regard, hostile view;<BR>(इस्, इस्, इ), looking asquint, squint-eyed, squinting;<BR>looking malignantly or with an evil eye at any one;<BR>jealous, envious.<BR>—वक्र-नक्र, अस्, m. ‘crooked-<BR>beaked, ‘a parrot; a low or depraved man.<BR>—वक्र-<BR>नाल, अम्, n. a sort of wind-instrument.<BR>—वक्र-<BR>नास, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked-nosed, having a crooked<BR>beak; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—वक्र-नासिक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘crooked-nosed,’ an owl.<BR>—वक्र-पाद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, crooked-legged.<BR>—वक्र-पुच्छ or वक्र-<BR>पुच्छिक, अस्, m. ‘crooked-tailed,’ a dog.<BR>—वक्र-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—वक्र-पुष्प, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a plant, Sesbana Grandiflora; Butea Fron-<BR>dosa.<BR>—वक्र-बालधि, इस्, m. ‘crooked-tailed,’ a<BR>dog.<BR>—वक्र-भणित, अम्, n. indirect speech,<BR>equivocation, prevarication, evasion.<BR>—वक्र-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. the state of being bent, curvature, crooked-<BR>ness; cunning, craft, deceit.<BR>—वक्र-रेखा, f. a<BR>curved line.<BR>—वक्र-लाङ्गूल, अम्, n. a crooked<BR>tail; (अस्), m. ‘crooked-tailed,’ a dog.<BR>—वक्र-<BR>वक्त्र, अस्, m. ‘crooked-faced, having a crooked<BR>snout, ‘a hog, boar.<BR>—वक्र-शल्या, f. a kind of<BR>small shrub or bush.<BR>—वक्र-शृङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having crooked or bent horns.<BR>—वक्र-संस्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, placed transversely.<BR>—वक्राग्र (˚र-<BR>अग्˚), अम्, n., N. of a plant (commonly called Bétu).<BR>—वक्राङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a crooked limb;<BR>(अस्), m. a goose; the ruddy goose (‘having a curved<BR>body’); a snake.<BR>—वक्राङ्घ्रि (˚र-अङ्˚), इस्, m.<BR>a crooked leg.<BR>—वक्री-करण, अम्, n. the act of<BR>making crooked, bending, distorting.<BR>—वक्री-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make curved or crooked.<BR>—वक्री-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made crooked or curved,<BR>bent.<BR>—वक्री-भाव, अस्, m. curvature, curve;<BR>fraudulent or dishonest disposition.<BR>—वक्री-भू, cl.<BR>1. P. -भवति, &c., to become crooked or bent;<BR>to retrograde (said of planets).<BR>—वक्री-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, become crooked, curved, bent, dishonest.<BR>—व-<BR>क्रेतर (˚र-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अत्, reverse of crooked,<BR>straight, not curved or curled.<BR>—वक्रोक्ति (˚र-उक्˚),<BR>इस्, f. indirect or perverse speech, equivocation, pre-<BR>varication, evasive speech or reply, evasion; hint,<BR>insinuation; pun; sarcasm.<BR>—वक्रोक्ति-जीवित, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—वक्रोष्ठि, इस्, or वक्रोष्ठिका,<BR>f. (fr. वक्र + ओष्ठ), a slight smile, one in which<BR>the lips are drawn on one side without the teeth<BR>being shewn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

