वक्ष्
वक्ष् वक्ष् (closely connected with rt.<BR>2. उक्ष्, q. v.), cl. 1. P. (Ved. also A.)<BR>वक्षति, ववक्ष, (in the Veda only the follow-<BR>ing Perfect forms are found, ववक्ष, ववक्षि-<BR>थ, ववक्षुस्, ववक्षे, ववक्षिरे), वक्षि-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to grow, increase, become tall; to accu-<BR>mulate; to be great or strong, to be powerful, (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 64, 3. ववक्षुः =<BR>प्रापयितुम् इच्छन्ति, they wish to bring; II. 22,<BR>3. ववक्षिथ = वोढुम् इच्छसि, thou desirest to<BR>support, as if fr. rt. 1. वह्); to be angry: Caus.<BR>वक्षयति, &c., Ved. to make grow, cause to<BR>increase, cause to be strong; [cf. Zend ukhs, ‘to<BR>grow:’ Gr. αὔξ-ω, αὐξ-άν-ω, αὔξ-η, αὔξ-η-σι-ς,<BR>αὔξ-η-μα: Lat. vas-tus: Goth. vahs-ja, vahs-tu-s:<BR>Angl. Sax. weaxan: Lith. augu, auks-tas: Hib.<BR>fasaim, ‘I grow;’ fasamhuil, ‘growing.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षण|वक्षणं
वक्षण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) strengthen-<BR>ing, refreshing; (अम्), n. the breast; (perhaps)<BR>refreshment, strengthening, (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 23, 6. वक्षणानि = वाहकानि स्तो-<BR>त्राणि, as if fr. rt. 1. वह्); fire (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda V. 19, 5); (आस्), f. pl. the stomach,<BR>abdomen, interior, (perhaps connected with rt.<BR>1. वह्); the sides, flank; the bed of a river; (ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. I. 13) = नदी, a river.<BR>—वक्-<BR>षणे-स्था, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. being in fire, (Sāy. =<BR>वह्नौ स्थित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षणि
