वक्षथ|वक्षथः
वक्षथ, अस्, m., Ved. the act of strengthening,<BR>invigorating; growing, increasing; growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षस्
वक्षस्, अस्, n. (according to some originally<BR>पक्षस्), strength (Ved.); the breast, bosom, chest,<BR>(in this sense perhaps fr. rt. 1. वह्); (आस्), m. an<BR>ox, bullock; [cf. perhaps Lat. pectus; Hib. uchd,<BR>‘the breast.’]<BR>—वक्षः-सम्मर्दिनी, f. a wife (as<BR>pressing or reclining on her husband's breast).<BR>—वक्-<BR>षः-स्थल or वक्षस्-स्थल, अम्, n. the place of<BR>the breast, the breast, bosom, heart.<BR>—वक्षस्-तटा-<BR>घात (˚ट-आघ्˚), अस्, m. a blow on the chest; [cf.<BR>तट.]<BR>—वक्षो-ग्रीव, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—वक्षो-ज, अस्, m. or औ, m. du.<BR>‘chest-born,’ the female breast; [cf. उरो-ज.]<BR>—वक्-<BR>षो-मण्डलिन्, ई, m., scil. हस्त, a position of the<BR>hands in dancing.<BR>—वक्षो-रुह्, ट्, or वक्षो-रुह,<BR>अस्, m. ‘chest-growing,’ the female breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षी
