वग्नु वग्नु, वग्वनु. See p. 878, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वघा
वघा वघा, f., Ved. a kind of noxious<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्|वंक्
वङ्क् वङ्क् (probably connected with rt.<BR>वञ्च्; cf. rt. वक्, with which rt. वङ्क् is<BR>identical; cf. also rt. वङ्ग्), cl. 1. A. वङ्कते, वङ्कि-<BR>तुम्, to go or proceed crookedly, be crooked; to go;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἀγκή, ἄγκος, ἀγκών, ἀγκύλος, ἄγκυρα,<BR>(probably) ὄκνος: Lat. angulus; vacillare, vacare,<BR>vacuus: Old Germ. winkil, waga, wagon, waga,<BR>wank, wankon: Angl. Sax. vincel, wœg, woh, wog,<BR>wo, wancol: Lith. wingis.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क|वंक|वंकः|वङ्कः
वङ्क, अस्, m. the bend or elbow of a river, the<BR>winding course of a stream; crookedness; (आ), f. the<BR>pummel of a saddle.<BR>—वङ्क-सेन, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of tree (= वक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्कटक
वङ्कटक, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्कर
वङ्कर, अस्, m. = वङ्क, the bending of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्कालकाचार्य
वङ्कालकाचार्य (˚क-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an<BR>astronomer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्काला
वङ्काला, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्किणी
वङ्किणी, f. a kind of plant (= कोल-नासिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्किल|वंकिल|वंकिलः|वङ्किलः
वङ्किल, अस्, m. a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्कु
वङ्कु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. going crookedly, (Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda I. 51, 11 = वक्र-गमन-शील; but<BR>Ṛg-veda V. 45, 6 = वन-गामिन्, going to the<BR>wood); going hurriedly, hastening (according to<BR>some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्य|वङ्क्यः
वङ्क्य, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, curved, flexible,<BR>pliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्रि|वंक्रि|वंक्रिः|वङ्क्रिः
वङ्क्रि, इस्, m. a rib, the rib of any animal (as of<BR>a horse, ox, &c.); the ribs of a building; the timber<BR>of a roof; a particular musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्षण|वंक्षणं|वङ्क्षणः
वङ्क्षण वङ्क्षण, अम्, n. (probably con-<BR>nected with वक्षण under rt. वक्ष्), the groin,<BR>the pubic and iliac regions; the joint of the thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्षु|वंक्षु|वंक्षुः|वङ्क्षुः
वङ्क्षु वङ्क्षु, उस्, f. a small arm or branch<BR>of the Ganges [cf. वङ्क, वङ्कु]; the Oxus;<BR>[cf. वक्षु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ख्|वंख्
वङ्ख् वङ्ख् = rt. वख्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्खर
वङ्खर वङ्खर, अस्, आ, अम्, = चारु; (उस्),<BR>m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ग्|वंग्
वङ्ग् वङ्ग् [cf. rt. वङ्क्], cl. 1. P. वङ्-<BR>गति, वङ्गितुम्, to go; to go lamely,<BR>limp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ग|वंग|वङ्गं|वङ्गः
वङ्ग वङ्ग, अस्, m. Bengal proper or the<BR>eastern parts of the modern province; N. of the son<BR>of Bali; of a king of the lunar race (regarded as<BR>the common ancestor of the people of Bengal);<BR>cotton; the egg-plant, Solanum Melongena; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the inhabitants of the above country; (अम्),<BR>n. tin; lead; [cf. Hib. ban, ‘copper.’]<BR>—वङ्ग-ज,<BR>अम्, n. brass, red-lead.<BR>—वङ्ग-जीवन, अम्, n.<BR>silver.<BR>—वङ्ग-देश, अस्, m. the country of Bengal.<BR>—वङ्ग-सेन, अस्, m. = वङ्क-सेन; a proper N.<BR>—वङ्ग-सेनक, अस्, m. the Sesbana Grandiflora.<BR>—वङ्गारि (˚ग-अरि), इस्, m. yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गन|वङ्गनः
वङ्गन, अस्, m. the egg-plant, Solanum Melon-<BR>gena; [cf. वङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गीय
वङ्गीय, see Gaṇa Gahādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गला
वङ्गला वङ्गला, f., N. of a particular<BR>Rāgiṇī or modification of a musical mode, (see<BR>रागिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गाल|वङ्गालः
वङ्गाल, अस्, m., N. of the son of the Rāga or<BR>musical mode called Bhairava; (ई), f., N. of the<BR>wife of the Rāga Bhairava, (see राग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गालिका
वङ्गालिका, f. = वङ्गाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गुला
वङ्गुला, f. = वङ्गला above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गिरि|वंगिरि
वङ्गिरि वङ्गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गृद
वङ्गृद वङ्गृद, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्घ्|वंघ्
वङ्घ् वङ्घ्, cl. 1. A. वङ्घते, वङ्घि-<BR>तुम्, to go; to begin moving; to begin;<BR>to move swiftly; to blame or censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्घ
वङ्घ वङ्घ, अस्, m. a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्
वच् वच्, cl. 2. P. (in the non-conjuga-<BR>tional tenses also A.), वक्ति (1st sing.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">Page0877-c+ 81</a>]<BR>वच्मि, &c., see Gram. 650; Ved. also cl. 3. P.<BR>विवक्ति, 1st sing. विवक्मि, as if fr. a form वक्;<BR>said to be also cl. 1. P. वचति), उवाच (Ved. [प्र]-<BR>ववाच, Ṛg-veda I. 67, 4), उचे (2nd sing. ऊचिषे,<BR>Ved. [प्र]ववक्षे), वक्ष्यति, -ते, अवोचत्,<BR>अवोचत (other anomalous forms fr. the base<BR>वोच् are वोचसि, वोचन्ति, वोचाम, वोचेस्, वोचेम,<BR>&c., वोच, वोचतु, वोचे, वोचन्त, वोचेय, वोचे-<BR>महि), वक्तुम् (Ved. वक्तवे, वक्तोस्), to say,<BR>speak, (पुनर् वच्, to speak again, answer, reply);<BR>to tell, declare, utter, (sometimes with a double acc.,<BR>e. g. तम् इदं वाक्यम् उवाच, he spoke this<BR>speech to him); to mention, describe; to call,<BR>name; to recite, repeat; to announce, proclaim,<BR>publish; to speak ill of, revile (with acc.): Pass.<BR>उच्यते, Aor. अवाचि, to be said or spoken; to be<BR>spoken about; to be told; to be admonished; to<BR>be called or named, &c.; to be regarded as, pass<BR>for: Caus. वाचयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अवीवचत्, to<BR>cause to say or speak, order to speak; to cause to<BR>be recited, cause (anything written) to be uttered or<BR>pronounced, to read; to say, tell, declare; to promise:<BR>Desid. विवक्षति, &c., to desire to say or speak,<BR>&c.: Pass. of Desid. विवक्ष्यते; [cf. Gr. ἐπ (for<BR>ϝεπ for ϝεκ) in εἶπ-ο-ν, ἔπ-ος, ὄψ, ὄσσα, ἐν-οπ-ή,<BR>θεό-προπος, πέπρωται: Lat. vŏc-are, vox, vôc-is,<BR>in-vī-tare, con-viciu-m; Old Germ. wah-an, ga-<BR>wah-anian, gi-wah-t: Mod. Germ. er-wähnen:<BR>Old Pruss. en-wack-e-mai, ‘we invoke;’ en-wacke:<BR>Hib. faighim, ‘I speak, talk;’ faigh, ‘a prophet;’<BR>faighle, faighleadh, ‘words, talk.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तव्य|वक्तव्यः
वक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken or uttered, fit<BR>or proper to be said; to be named or called; to be<BR>spoken to or addressed; to be spoken about or<BR>against, having a bad name or reputation, blam-<BR>able, reprehensible, vile, low, base, bad; liable to be<BR>called upon for an account, answerable, accountable,<BR>responsible; subject, dependent; (अम्), n. a rule,<BR>precept, sentence, dictum, aphorism, speech; speak-<BR>ing; reproach, censure.<BR>—वक्तव्य-ता, f. or वक्-<BR>तव्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being fit or proper<BR>to be said or spoken about, the state of being spoken<BR>against, the having a bad name or reputation, re-<BR>proachableness, blamableness, reprehension, blame;<BR>responsibility; subjection, dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्ति
वक्ति, इस्, f., Ved. speech; [cf. उक्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तु
वक्तु, उस्, m. (according to Sāy. = परुष-<BR>वाक्यानां वक्तृ), a speaker of harsh language,<BR>reviler; (but according to modern scholars वक्तवे<BR>in Ṛg-veda VII. 31, 5. is a Vedic infin.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तुकाम
वक्तु-काम, अस्, आ, अम् (वक्तु for वक्तुम्), in-<BR>tending to speak, desirous of speaking, about to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तुमनस्
वक्तु-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (वक्तु for वक्तुम्),<BR>having a mind to speak, being about to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तृ
वक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who speaks, a speaker;<BR>speaking, saying, loquacious, talkative; speaking<BR>well or sensibly, eloquent, learned, wise; speaking<BR>truly, honest, sincere; (ता), m. a speaker, orator,<BR>expounder, teacher; [cf. Lat. auctor.]<BR>—वक्तृ-ता,<BR>f. or वक्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. ability to speak, talkative-<BR>ness, eloquence, elocution.<BR>—वक्तृत्व-शक्ति, इस्, f.<BR>ability to speak, eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तृक
वक्तृक, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of an adj. comp.<BR>= वक्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्र|वक्त्रं
वक्त्र, अम्, n. the organ of speech, the mouth;<BR>the face; a muzzle, snout, proboscis, beak, &c.; the<BR>point (of an arrow), the spout of a jug or vessel;<BR>beginning, commencement; (in algebra) the initial<BR>quantity or first term of a progression; a sort of<BR>metre containing four times eight syllables (said to<BR>be like the श्लोक); a sort of garment; the root of<BR>Tabernæmontana Coronaria; [cf. perhaps Lat. la-<BR>trare for vactrare.]<BR>—वक्त्र-खुर, अस्, m. ‘mouth-<BR>hoof, ‘a tooth.<BR>—वक्त्र-ज, अस्, m. ‘sprung from<BR>the mouth (of Brahmā), ‘a Brāhman.<BR>—वक्त्र-<BR>ताल, अम्, n. a musical instrument played with the<BR>mouth; (said to mean also ‘making a noise by strik-<BR>ing the mouth with the hand at the moment of utter-<BR>ing sound.’)<BR>—वक्त्र-तुण्ड, अस्, m. ‘having a pro-<BR>boscis instead of a face, ‘N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—वक्त्र-<BR>दल, अम्, n. a part of the mouth, the palate.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">Page0878-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—वक्त्र-द्वार, अम्, n. the opening of the mouth.<BR>—वक्त्र-पट, a veil.<BR>—वक्त्र-पट्ट, अस्, m. a<BR>bag containing corn tied round a horse's head.<BR>—वक्त्र-परिस्पन्द, अस्, m. ‘motion of the<BR>mouth, ‘speech, discourse.<BR>—वक्त्र-भेदिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, mouth-piercing, mouth-cutting, pungent, bitter,<BR>sharp.<BR>—वक्त्र-योधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fighting with the<BR>mouth; (ई), m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—वक्त्र-रन्-<BR>ध्र, अम्, n. the aperture of the mouth.<BR>—वक्त्र-<BR>रुह, ‘growing on the face,’ hair growing on<BR>the face, hair on the proboscis (of elephants &c.).<BR>—वक्त्र-रोग, अस्, m. mouth-disease, a disease of<BR>the mouth.<BR>—वक्त्र-रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, suffering from<BR>a disease of the mouth.<BR>—वक्त्र-वास, अस्, m.<BR>‘mouth-scenting,’ an orange.<BR>—वक्त्र-शोधन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, cleansing or purifying the mouth; (अम्),<BR>n. the act of cleansing the mouth; the fruit of<BR>Averrhoa Carambola; a lime, citron.<BR>—वक्त्र-<BR>शोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, purifying the mouth; (ई), m. the<BR>citron tree; (इ), n. a citron or lime.<BR>—वक्त्रासव<BR>(˚र-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘mouth-liquor,’ saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0877-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रक
वक्त्रक at the end of an adj. comp. = वक्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्व
वक्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = वक्तव्य, to be<BR>uttered or spoken; (according to Sāy. वक्त्वानाम्<BR>= वक्तव्यानां वेद-वाक्यानाम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्मन्
वक्मन्, अ, n., Ved. (Sāy. = मार्ग), path, road;<BR>(= वचन, स्तोत्र), speech, hymn of praise.<BR>—वक्-<BR>म-राज-सत्य, अस्, m., Ved. faithful to those who<BR>are the rulers or ordainers of hymns (of praise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्म्य
वक्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be praised, worthy<BR>of celebration, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्वन्
वक्वन्, आ, -वरी, अ, Ved. (according to modern<BR>scholars) = वक्व, p. 876, col. 3; (आ), m. a speaker,<BR>singer, chanter, great talker, chatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्ष्यमाण|वक्ष्यमाणः
वक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, about to be said or<BR>described, intended to be spoken about afterwards,<BR>to be mentioned hereafter or subsequently.<BR>—वक्ष्-<BR>यमाण-त्व, अम्, n. the being about to be men-<BR>tioned, the being about to be spoken of hereafter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग्नु|वग्नुः
वग्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, talkative; (उस्), m. a speaker;<BR>a sound; the cry (of an animal), croak (of a frog,<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 103, 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग्वन
वग्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) talkative,<BR>chattering; praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग्वनु|वग्वनुः
वग्वनु, उस्, m., Ved. a sound, noise, (Sāy. =<BR>शब्द.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच|वचः
वच, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, talking, saying, &c.<BR>[cf. कु-व्˚]; (अस्), m. a parrot; = सूर्य, the sun;<BR>= कारण; (आ), f. a kind of talking bird, Turdus<BR>Salica (= सारिका); a kind of aromatic root, (accord-<BR>ing to some, orris root); (अम्), n. the act of speak-<BR>ing, talk; [cf. दुर्-व्˚.]<BR>—वचाचार्य (˚च-आच्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—वचार्च (˚च-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a sun-worshipper, Parsee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचक्नु|वचक्नुः
वचक्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, talkative, loquacious, eloquent;<BR>(उस्), m. a Brāhman; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचण्डा
वचण्डा, f. a kind of talking bird, Turdus Salica<BR>or the Maina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचण्डी
वचण्डी, f. = वचण्डा; = वर्त्ति; a kind of<BR>weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचन|वचनं
वचन, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, a speaker, elo-<BR>quent (Ved.); to be praised, laudable (Ved.);<BR>being pronounced (Ved.); mentioning, indicat-<BR>ing, pointing out, signifying (at the end of a<BR>comp.); (अम्), n. the act of speaking or pronounc-<BR>ing, speaking, uttering, declaring, ordering, enjoin-<BR>ing, declaration, affirmation, promise; pronunciation;<BR>the pronunciation of a letter (in grammar); the act<BR>of reciting or repeating, recitation; mentioning,<BR>naming, being called; a speech, word, expression,<BR>utterance, sentence, message; a text, dictum, apho-<BR>rism, rule, precept, passage of a sacred book or code<BR>of laws; counsel, advice, instruction; proclamation,<BR>edict, order, injunction, command, (वचनात्, and less<BR>frequently वचनेन, ‘in the name of,’ e. g. मम<BR>वचनात्, ‘in my name,’ ‘by my order’); sound,<BR>voice; the meaning of a word (in grammar); num-<BR>ber (in grammar; cf. एक-व्˚, द्वि-व्˚, बहु-व्˚); dry<BR>ginger.<BR>—वचन-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, making a speech,<BR>speaking; acting according to injunction, doing what<BR>one is told, obeying orders, obedient; (अस्), m. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">Page0878-b+ 80</a>]<BR>author or enunciator of a precept.<BR>—वचन-कारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, doing what is commanded, obeying orders,<BR>obedient.<BR>—वचन-क्रम, अस्, m. order of words,<BR>discourse.<BR>—वचन-गोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, forming a<BR>subject of conversation.<BR>—वचन-गौरव, अम्, n.<BR>respect for an order, deference to a command.<BR>—व-<BR>चन-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, accepting or obeying orders,<BR>attentive to a command, obedient, compliant, con-<BR>formable, submissive, humble.<BR>—वचन-पटु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, skilful in speech, eloquent.<BR>—वचन-मात्र,<BR>अम्, n. mere words, assertion unsupported by facts.<BR>—वचन-विरुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, opposed to a<BR>declaration or precept, contrary to a text.<BR>—वचन-<BR>विरोध, अस्, m. inconsistency of precepts or texts,<BR>incongruity, contradiction.<BR>—वचन-व्यक्ति, इस्, f.<BR>distinctness or perspicuity of a text.<BR>—वचन-शत,<BR>अम्, n. a hundred speeches, repeated speech or decla-<BR>ration.<BR>—वचन-सहाय, अस्, m. a companion for<BR>(the sake of) conversation, any sociable companion<BR>with whom one may talk.<BR>—वचनानुग (˚न-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, following advice or orders, obedient,<BR>submissive.<BR>—वचना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. pos-<BR>sessed of speech, eloquent, gifted with the power of<BR>praising or singing; making a sound, lowing (as<BR>kine; Sāy. = हम्भा-रवादि-शब्द-वत्).<BR>—वचनी-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make a reproach.<BR>—वचनी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made a reproach, ex-<BR>posed to censure or abuse.<BR>—वचने-स्थित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, abiding in a command, obeying orders, com-<BR>pliant, conformable, obedient.<BR>—वचनोपक्रम<BR>(˚न-उप्˚), अस्, m. commencement of a speech, ex-<BR>ordium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनीय|वचनीयः
वचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken or uttered,<BR>fit or proper to be said, mentionable; to be called<BR>or named; to be spoken about or against, to be<BR>reproved, censurable, liable to reproach; (अम्), n.<BR>reproach, censure, blame.<BR>—वचनीय-ता, f. or व-<BR>चनीय-त्व, अम्, n. liability to be spoken about or<BR>against; rumour, report, evil report, blamableness,<BR>detraction, scandal; blame, reprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचर|वचरः
वचर, अस्, m. a cock; a low person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचलु|वचलुः
वचलु, उस्, m. = शत्रु, a malevolent person,<BR>enemy; offence, fault (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्
वचस्, अस्, n. speech, voice; a speech, word; a<BR>hymn; singing, song (of birds); advice, counsel;<BR>proclamation, edict, command, order; a sentence;<BR>declaration of fate, oracle; number (in grammar,<BR>cf. द्वि-व्˚).<BR>—वचः-क्रम, अस्, m. course of speech,<BR>mode of address, discourse.<BR>—वचसाम्-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘lord of speeches,’ N. of Bṛhas-pati; the planet<BR>Jupiter.<BR>—वचस्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, accomplishing the<BR>words or commands of another; doing what is en-<BR>joined or commanded, obedient, compliant.<BR>—वचो-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, receiving words or commands,<BR>comprehending or apprehending words; (अस्), m. the<BR>ear.<BR>—वचो-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. harnessed at (his)<BR>word; harnessed with hymns.<BR>—वचो-विद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. skilful in speech, eloquent; knowing hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस
1. वचस, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 880), talkative,<BR>eloquent, wise; (at end of comp.) = वचस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्य
1. वचस्य (fr. वचस्), Nom. A. वचस्यते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to babble, rattle (said of the sound of the<BR>running Soma); to be praised or glorified, (Sāy. =<BR>स्तूयते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्य
2. वचस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) worthy<BR>of mention, praiseworthy, celebrated; (or perhaps<BR>for 1. वचस्यु, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्या
वचस्या, f. (fr. 1. वचस्य), Ved. desire of<BR>speaking, readiness of speech, eloquence; desire of<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्यु
1. वचस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ (for 2. see p. 880, col. 1),<BR>Ved. eloquent; desirous of praise, (Sāy. = स्तुति-का-<BR>म.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचि
वचि, Ved. name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्यमान
1. वच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being spoken or<BR>uttered, (Sāy. = उच्यमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्यमान
वच्यमान 1. and 2. वच्यमान. See above<BR>and p. 880, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्छला
वच्छला वच्छला, a various reading for<BR>वत्सला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्छिका
वच्छिका वच्छिका in दीर्घ-व्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्
वज् वज्, cl. 1. P. वजति, ववाज (2nd<BR>sing. ववजिथ, 3rd du. ववजतुस्), व-<BR>जितुम्, to go, roam about [cf. rt. व्रज्]; to increase;<BR>to be hard or strong, (these senses are assumed to<BR>explain वज्र, वाज, &c., q. v., but a lost rt. उज् =<BR>वज् may be conjectured; cf. उग्र, ओजस्, &c.); cl.<BR>10. P. वाजयति, &c., to make possessed of food or<BR>strength, to desire or ask for food or strength, (in<BR>these senses more properly a Nom. fr. वाज, see<BR>वाजय); to prepare the way; to trim or feather an<BR>arrow, to prepare, make; to go; [cf. Zend vaz,<BR>vaz-y-ant, vaz-d-vare; Gr. ὑγι-ής, ὑγιη-ρό-ς,<BR>ὑγίε-ια, ὑγιαίν-ω, ὑγιάζ-ω; Lat. veg-e-o, vig-e-o,<BR>veg-e-tu-s, vig-or, vig-il, aug-eo, aug-men-tu-m,<BR>(perhaps) vagarī; Goth. auka, vokrs; Old Germ.<BR>auhon; Angl. Sax. eacan, (probably also) wacor,<BR>wacian; Lith. ug-i-s, ug-a, aug-u, aug-mu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्र|वज्रं|वज्रः
वज्र, अस्, आ, अम्, adamantine, hard, impene-<BR>trable; severe; shaped like a kind of cross with two<BR>transverse lines bisecting each other diagonally, cross,<BR>forked, zigzag; (अस्, अम्), m. n. (in the earlier lan-<BR>guage अस्, m.), the thunderbolt and weapon of Indra<BR>(said to have been formed out of the bones of a<BR>celebrated Ṛṣi called Dadhīca or Dadhīci, see द-<BR>धीच, दधीच्य्-अस्थि; it is sometimes described<BR>as circular like the Cakra or discus of Viṣṇu or<BR>shaped like a quoit but with a broader circumference<BR>and smaller central hole, and when made to revolve<BR>and launched at an enemy, the fire of lightning is<BR>supposed to issue in destructive flames from its<BR>periphery, elicited by the intensity of its centrifugal<BR>energy; the thunderbolt is also regarded as having<BR>the form of two transverse bolts or lines crossing<BR>each other thus X); any destructive weapon like a<BR>discus or thunderbolt (as used by various gods, evil<BR>beings, or persons of superhuman power, e. g. by<BR>Viṣṇu, Kṛṣṇa, the Rākṣasas, and Viśvā-mitra); a<BR>thunderbolt in general or the lightning supposed to<BR>issue from the centrifugal energy of the circular thun-<BR>derbolt of Indra; a diamond, (this gem being con-<BR>sidered to possess the hardness of the thunderbolt or<BR>to be of the same substance); sour gruel; (अस्), m.<BR>a form of military array; a particular kind of column<BR>or pillar; a particular figure or diagram the form of<BR>which is supposed to resemble that of the thunder-<BR>bolt; any symbol with two lines crossing each other<BR>in a diagonal direction; a particular form of the<BR>moon; N. of various plants, Euphorbia Antiquorum;<BR>Asteracantha Longifolia; white-flowering Kuśa grass;<BR>N. of the fifteenth of the twenty-seven Yogas or<BR>astronomical periods of time, (see योग); of a parti-<BR>cular Soma ceremony; of a particular penance; a<BR>kind of very tenacious mortar or hard cement; N.<BR>of a son of Aniruddha or of a grandson of Kṛṣṇa; of<BR>a son of Viśvā-mitra; of a son of Manu Sāvarṇa; of<BR>one of the seven Jaina Daśa-pūrvins; of a Ṛṣi;<BR>of a minister of Narendrāditya; of a son of Bhūti;<BR>of a king; (आ), f. Cocculus Cordifolius; Euphorbia<BR>Antiquorum; N. of Durgā; of a daughter of Vai-<BR>śvānara; (ई), f. a kind of Euphorbia; (अम्), n. a<BR>kind of hard iron, steel; a kind of talc; = वाग्-<BR>वज्र, thunder-like denunciation, very harsh or<BR>severe language; a particular mode of sitting; Em-<BR>blic Myrobalan; the blossom of the sesamum or of<BR>any plant called Vajra; N. of a particular configura-<BR>tion of the planets and stars (viz. when the favour-<BR>able planets are situated in the first and seventh houses<BR>and the unfavourable ones in the fourth and tenth);<BR>= बालक, a child, pupil; [cf. Zend vaz-ra, ‘a club;’<BR>Old Germ. weggi; Angl. Sax. wœcg, wecg.]<BR>—वज्र-कङ्कट, अस्, m. ‘adamantine-armoured,’<BR>N. of Hanumat the monkey god.<BR>—वज्र-कण्ट,<BR>अस्, m. Euphorbia Neriifolia or Antiquorum.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>कण्टक, अस्, m. = वज्र-कण्ट; Asteracantha Lon-<BR>gifolia.<BR>—वज्र-कण्टक-शाल्मली, f. a cotton tree<BR>with very hard thorns; N. of a hell.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>कन्द, अस्, m. a sort of esculent root, (perhaps)<BR>yam.<BR>—वज्र-कपाट-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having ada-<BR>mantine doors.<BR>—वज्र-कपालिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0879-a" target="_blank">Page0879-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Buddha.<BR>—वज्र-कर्ण, अस्, m. = वज्र-कन्द.<BR>—वज्र-कालिका, f., N. of the mother of Śākya-<BR>muni.<BR>—वज्र-काली, f. epithet of a Jina-śakti.<BR>—वज्र-कीट, अस्, m. a kind of penetrating insect<BR>which bores holes in wood and stone, (see वज्र-<BR>दंष्ट्र.)<BR>—वज्र-कील, अस्, m. a thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्र-कीलाय, Nom. A. -कीलायते, &c., to act<BR>or be like a thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्र-कीलायित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, struck as it were by thunderbolts.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>कुक्षि, N. of a cave.<BR>—वज्र-कूट, अस्, m. ‘dia-<BR>mond-peak, ‘a mountain consisting of diamonds;<BR>N. of a mountain; of a mythical town on the<BR>Himālaya mountains.<BR>—वज्र-केतु, उस्, m. ‘having<BR>a Vajra for an ensign, ‘N. of the demon Naraka.<BR>—वज्र-क्षार, अम्, n. an alkaline earth or an<BR>impure carbonate of soda.<BR>—वज्र-गर्भ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—वज्र-गोप, अस्, m. = इन्द्र-<BR>गोप.<BR>—वज्र-घात, अस्, m. a thunder-stroke, stroke<BR>of a thunderbolt, thunder-clap, thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>घोष, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding like a thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्र-चञ्चु, उस्, m. ‘hard-beaked,’ a vulture;<BR>[cf. वज्र-तुण्ड.]<BR>—वज्र-चर्मन्, आ, m. ‘having<BR>a very hard or impenetrable skin, ‘a rhinoceros.<BR>—वज्र-चिह्न, अम्, n. a Vajra-like mark.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>च्छेदक-प्रज्ञा-पारम्-इता, f., N. of a Buddhist<BR>Sūtra work, (also वज्र-च्छेदिका.)<BR>—वज्र-जित्, त्,<BR>m. ‘conquering the thunderbolt,’ N. of Garuḍa (who<BR>was invulnerable to the strokes of Indra's bolt; cf.<BR>वज्रि-जित्).<BR>—वज्र-ज्वलन, अम्, n. ‘thunder-flash,’<BR>lightning.<BR>—वज्र-ज्वाला, f. ‘thunder-flash' light<BR>ning; N. of a granddaughter of Vairocana.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>टीक, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—वज्र-णखा, f. a<BR>proper N., (see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 58; cf. वज्र-नख.]<BR>—वज्र-तर, अस्, m. epithet of a kind of very<BR>tenacious mortar or cement.<BR>—वज्र-ता, f. or वज्र-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. great hardness or impenetrableness,<BR>severity.<BR>—वज्र-तुण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, hard-beaked;<BR>(अस्), m. a vulture; a mosquito, gnat; N. of Garuḍa;<BR>of Gaṇeśa; the plant Cactus Opuntia.<BR>—वज्र-तुल्य,<BR>अस्, m. ‘resembling a diamond,’ the azure stone,<BR>lapis lazuli.<BR>—वज्र-दंष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>teeth as hard as adamant; (अस्), m. = वज्र-कीट;<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa; of an Asura; of a king of the<BR>Vidyā-dharas; of a lion (in the Pañca-tantra).<BR>—व-<BR>ज्र-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, holding a thunderbolt in<BR>the right hand; (अस्), m., N. of Indra.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, having a staff studded with<BR>diamonds.<BR>—वज्र-दण्डक, अम्, n. the plant<BR>Cactus Opuntia.<BR>—वज्र-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Bhaga-datta; of a Buddhist author.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>दन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘hard-toothed,’ a hog, boar; a<BR>rat.<BR>—वज्र-दशन, अस्, आ, अम्, having hard teeth;<BR>(अस्), m. a rat.<BR>—वज्र-दृढ-नेत्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king of the Yakṣas.<BR>—वज्र-देश, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a district.<BR>—वज्र-देह, अस्, आ, अम्, or वज्र-<BR>देहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a frame hard as adamant,<BR>having a very robust or hardy body.<BR>—वज्र-द्रु,<BR>उस्, or वज्र-द्रुम, अस्, m., N. of certain plants,<BR>Euphorbia of various species.<BR>—वज्रद्रुम-केसर-<BR>ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Gandharvas.<BR>—वज्र-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, holding a thunderbolt;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Indra; of a Buddhist saint; of a<BR>king.<BR>—वज्र-धात्री, f., N. of the wife of Vairo-<BR>cana.<BR>—वज्र-नख, अस्, आ, अम्, having hard claws.<BR>—वज्र-नगर, अम्, n., N. of the city of the<BR>Dānava Vajra-nābha.<BR>—वज्र-नाभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a hard nave (as a wheel &c.); (अस्), m. the<BR>discus of Kṛṣṇa; N. of one of Skanda's attendants;<BR>of a Dānava; of a king (a son of Uktha, also a son<BR>of Unnābha, also a son of Sthala).<BR>—वज्रनाभीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, relating to (the Dānava) Vajra-nābha.<BR>treating of him.<BR>—वज्र-निर्घोष, अस्, m. a clap<BR>of thunder.<BR>—वज्र-निष्पेष, अस्, m. sound pro-<BR>duced by the clashing or concussion of thunder-<BR>clouds, a clap of thunder.<BR>—वज्र-पञ्जर, epithet<BR>of certain prayers addressed to Durgā; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a Dānava.<BR>—वज्र-पत्त्रिका, f. Asparagus Race-<BR>mosus.<BR>—वज्र-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘thunderbolt-handed,’<BR>holding a thunderbolt in the hand, grasping a thun-<BR>derbolt; whose thunderbolt is the hand (said of<BR>Brāhmans); (इस्), m., N. of Indra; of a class of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0879-b" target="_blank">Page0879-b+ 81</a>]<BR>divine beings (with Buddhists); of a Dhyāni-Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR>—वज्रपाणि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of one<BR>who holds a thunderbolt in the hand.<BR>—वज्र-पा-<BR>णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘thunderbolt-handed,’ grasping a thun-<BR>derbolt.<BR>—वज्र-पात, अस्, m. the fall of a thunder-<BR>bolt, a stroke of lightning; (अस्, आ, अम्), falling like<BR>a thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्र-पाषाण, अस्, m. ‘diamond-<BR>stone,’ a kind of spar or valuable stone.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of the city of the Dānava Vajra-<BR>nābha.<BR>—वज्र-पुष्प, अम्, n. ‘diamond-flower,’<BR>a valuable flower; the blossom of sesamum; (आ), f.<BR>a kind of fennel, Anethum Sowa.<BR>—वज्र-प्रभ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Vidyā-dhara.<BR>—वज्र-प्रभाव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of the Karūṣas.<BR>—वज्र-प्रस्ता-<BR>रिणी, f., N. of a Tantra goddess.<BR>—वज्र-प्रस्ता-<BR>रिणी-मन्त्र, आस्, m. pl. an epithet of particular<BR>magical formulas.<BR>—वज्र-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, like<BR>adamant, adamantine, exceedingly hard.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>बध, see वज्र-वध.<BR>—वज्र-बाहु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, ‘thunderbolt-armed,’ holding a thunderbolt in the<BR>hand, wielder of the thunderbolt (said of Indra, of<BR>Indra and Agni, and of Rudra); (उस्), m., N. of a<BR>king of Orissa; of another person.<BR>—वज्र-भूमि,<BR>इस्, f., N. of a place.<BR>—वज्र-भूमि-रजस्, अस्, n. a<BR>particular precious stone (= वैक्रान्त).<BR>—वज्र-<BR>भृकुटि, इस्, f., N. of a Tantra goddess.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>भृत्, त्, त्, त्, carrying or wielding a thunderbolt;<BR>(त्), m., N. of Indra.<BR>—वज्र-मणि, इस्, m. ‘thun-<BR>derbolt-gem, ‘a diamond.<BR>—वज्र-मण्डा, f., N. of<BR>a Dhāraṇī.<BR>—वज्र-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of dia-<BR>mond, hard as diamond, hard, adamantine; hard-<BR>hearted.<BR>—वज्र-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—वज्र-मुकुट, अस्, m., N. of a son of Pratāpa-<BR>mukuṭa.<BR>—वज्र-मुष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, holding a thun-<BR>derbolt in the fist; having a hard or iron fist; (इस्),<BR>m., N. of Indra; of a Rākṣasa; of a Kṣatriya or<BR>warrior.<BR>—वज्र-मूली, f. a kind of leguminous<BR>shrub (= माष-पर्णी).<BR>—वज्र-योगिनी, f., N. of<BR>a goddess.<BR>—वज्र-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, whose thun-<BR>derbolt is a war-chariot (said of a Kṣatriya).<BR>—व-<BR>ज्र-रद, अस्, आ, अम्, having teeth or tusks as hard<BR>as adamant; (अस्), m. a hog, boar.<BR>—वज्र-रात्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—वज्र-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>shaped like a Vajra, crossed, (see वज्र.)<BR>—वज्र-<BR>लिपि, इस्, f. a particular style of writing.<BR>—वज्र-लेप,<BR>अस्, m. a particular kind of very hard mortar or<BR>cement.<BR>—वज्रलेप-घटित, अस्, आ, अम्, joined<BR>with adamantine cement.<BR>—वज्र-लेपाय, Nom. A.<BR>वज्रलेपायते, &c., to be like Vajra-lepa, to be as<BR>hard or tenacious as cement.<BR>—वज्र-लोहक, a<BR>magnet, loadstone.<BR>—वज्र-वध, अस्, m. death by<BR>a thunderbolt or lightning; oblique or cross multi-<BR>plication.<BR>—वज्र-वर-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king of Orissa.<BR>—वज्र-वल्ली, f. a species of sun-<BR>flower, Heliotropium Indicum.<BR>—वज्र-वह् or व-<BR>ज्र-वाह्, ट्, m. carrying or wielding a thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्र-वारक, अस्, m. a title of respect applied<BR>to certain sages.<BR>—वज्र-वाराही, f., N. of the mother<BR>of Śākya-muni; [cf. वज्र-कालिका.]<BR>—वज्र-विद्रा-<BR>विणी, f., N. of a Buddhist goddess.<BR>—वज्र-विष्-<BR>कम्भ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Garuḍa.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>विहत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. struck by a thunderbolt or<BR>lightning.<BR>—वज्र-वीजक, अस्, m. a kind of creeper,<BR>Guilandina Bonduc.<BR>—वज्र-वीर, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Mahā-kāla.<BR>—वज्र-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>plant, Cactus Opuntia.<BR>—वज्र-वेग, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Rākṣasa; of a Vidyā-dhara.<BR>—वज्र-व्यूह,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of military array.<BR>—वज्र-शरीर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, = वज्र-देह, q. v.<BR>—वज्र-शल्य, अस्, m.<BR>‘having hard quills or prickles,’ a porcupine.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>शाखा, f., N. of a branch or sect of the Jainas<BR>founded by Vajra-svāmin.<BR>—वज्र-शीर्ष, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Bhṛgu.<BR>—वज्र-शृङ्खला, f. a<BR>female personification peculiar to the Jainas and one<BR>of their sixteen Vidyā-devīs.<BR>—वज्र-शृङ्खलिका,<BR>f. Asteracantha Longifolia.<BR>—वज्र-संहत, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—वज्र-सङ्घात, अस्, m.<BR>having the hardness or compactness of adamant<BR>(applied to Bhīma in Mahā-bh. Ādi-p. 4775); epi-<BR>thet of a kind of mortar or cement.<BR>—वज्र-सत्त्व,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a soul or heart of adamant; (अस्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0879-c" target="_blank">Page0879-c+ 81</a>]<BR>m., N. of a Dhyāni-buddha.<BR>—वज्रसत्त्वात्मिका<BR>(˚व-आत्˚), f., N. of the wife of Vajra-sattva.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>समाधि, इस्, m. a particular kind of abstract medi-<BR>tation with Buddhists.<BR>—वज्र-समुत्कीर्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, perforated by a diamond or any hard instrument.<BR>—वज्र-सार, अस्, आ, अम्, having the essence or<BR>nature of a diamond, hard as a diamond; made of<BR>diamond; a diamond (gender doubtful); (अस्), m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—वज्रसार-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of<BR>the essence of a diamond, hard as a diamond, made<BR>of diamond.<BR>—वज्रसारी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c.,<BR>to make hard as diamond.<BR>—वज्र-सूचि, इस्, or<BR>वज्र-सूची, f. a diamond needle; N. of an Upani-<BR>shad ascribed to Śaṅkarācārya; of a work by Aśva-<BR>ghoṣa.<BR>—वज्र-सूर्य, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—वज्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king of Śrāvastī; of<BR>a preceptor.<BR>—वज्र-स्थान, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—वज्र-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of one of the seven<BR>Jaina Daśa-pūrvins.<BR>—वज्र-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘thunderbolt-handed,’ wielding the thunderbolt (said<BR>of Indra, Agni, the Maruts, Śiva, &c.); (आ), f., N.<BR>of one of the nine Samidhs; of a Buddhist goddess.<BR>—वज्र-हूण, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—वज्र-<BR>हृदय, अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—व-<BR>ज्रांशु (˚र-अं˚), उस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—वज्राकर (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, m. a diamond mine;<BR>N. of a place.<BR>—वज्राकार (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or वज्राकृति (˚र-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, shaped like a thun-<BR>derbolt, having the shape of a Vajra, having trans-<BR>verse lines, (see वज्र); any cross-shaped symbol, (a<BR>symbol shaped like a cross was formerly used in gram-<BR>mars as the sign of the Jihvāmūlīyas.)<BR>—वज्राख्य<BR>(˚र-आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the name of Vajra,<BR>called Vajra; (अस्), m. a kind of mineral spar; [cf.<BR>वज्र-पाषाण.]<BR>—वज्राघात (˚र-आघ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the stroke of a thunderbolt, a stroke of lightning;<BR>any sudden shock or calamity.<BR>—वज्राङ्कित (˚र-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, marked with a Vajra or with a<BR>Vajra-like symbol, (see वज्र.)<BR>—वज्राङ्कुशी (˚र-<BR>अङ्˚), f., N. of a Tantra goddess.<BR>—वज्राङ्ग (˚र-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. a snake, (probably for वक्राङ्ग);<BR>(ई), f. a sort of grain, Coix Barbata; Heliotropium<BR>Indicum.<BR>—वज्राचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m. ‘diamond-<BR>like teacher, ‘N. of a preceptor.<BR>—वज्रादित्य (˚र-<BR>आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king of Kaśmīra.<BR>—वज्राभ<BR>(˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, diamond-like, resembling a<BR>diamond; (अस्), m. a kind of spar or valuable stone,<BR>(perhaps) the opal; [cf. वज्राख्य.]<BR>—वज्राभ्यास<BR>(˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m. multiplication crosswise or zigzag,<BR>cross multiplication.<BR>—वज्राम्बुजा (˚र-अम्˚), f.,<BR>N. of a Tantra goddess.<BR>—वज्रायुध (˚र-आय्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, thunderbolt-armed, having the thunder-<BR>bolt for a weapon; (अस्), m., N. of Indra; a proper<BR>N.<BR>—वज्राशनि (˚र-अश्˚), इस्, m. f. Indra's thunder-<BR>bolt.<BR>—वज्रासन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. a diamond seat<BR>or throne; a particular way of sitting.<BR>—वज्रासु<BR>= वज्रांशु (according to one reading).<BR>—वज्रा-<BR>स्थि-शृङ्खला (˚र-अस्˚), f. Asteracantha Longifolia,<BR>(perhaps resolvable into the name of two plants, viz.<BR>Vajra-śṛṅkhalā and Asthi-śṛṅkhalā.)<BR>—वज्राहत<BR>(˚र-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, struck by a thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्राहिका (˚र-अह्˚), f. Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR>—वज्री-करण, अम्, n. the making into a Vajra<BR>or into the form of a thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्री-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, become a thunderbolt, turned into a<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>—वज्रेन्द्र (˚र-इन्˚), अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—वज्रेश्वरी (˚र-ईश्˚), f., N. of a Buddhist god-<BR>dess.<BR>—वज्रोदरी (˚र-उद्˚), f., N. of a Rākṣasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0878-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रक|वज्रकं
वज्रक, अम्, n., scil. तैल, a kind of oil pre-<BR>pared with various substances (used as a remedy<BR>for cutaneous eruptions); a particular appearance or<BR>phenomenon of the sky; = वज्र-क्षार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0879-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राय
वज्राय, Nom. A. वज्रायते, &c., to become a<BR>thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0879-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रिन्
वज्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, holding or wielding the thunder-<BR>bolt (said of Indra, Agni, Śiva, &c.); containing<BR>the word वज्र (Ved.); (ई), m. ‘the Thunderer,’<BR>N. of Indra; a Buddha or Jaina deified saint; (इणी),<BR>f. epithet of certain Iṣṭakās (Ved.).<BR>—वज्रि-जित्, त्,<BR>m. ‘conqueror of Indra,’ N. of Garuḍa, (see वज्र-<BR>जित्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0879-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रिवस्
वज्रिवस्, voc. c. a Vedic form (see Ṛg-veda I.<BR>121, 14) = वज्र-वन्, voc. c. of वज्र-वत्, having<BR>or wielding a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वजआण
वजआण वजआण and वजहूण, N. of<BR>places; [cf. वज्र-हूण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रट
वज्रट वज्रट, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Uvaṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रोली
वज्रोली वज्रोली, f. a particular position of<BR>the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्च्|वंच्
वञ्च् वञ्च् (probably connected with rt.<BR>वङ्क्), cl. 1. P. वञ्चति, ववञ्च, Prec.<BR>वच्यात्, वञ्चितुम्, to move to and fro, shake,<BR>vibrate, tremble, totter, rock about, waver (Ved.);<BR>to go crookedly; to go slyly or secretly, sneak along;<BR>to go, go to, arrive at; to pass over, wander over,<BR>go astray: Pass. वच्यते, Ved. to move or rock to<BR>and fro, roll, hurry along, (but according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 46, 3. वच्यन्ते = उच्यन्ते, as if fr. rt.<BR>वच्, to speak, proclaim, address, &c.): Caus. P.<BR>वञ्चयति, &c., to move or go away from,<BR>avoid, escape, shun, evade (generally P. and with<BR>acc.): Caus. A. वञ्चयते, &c., to cause to go<BR>astray, deceive, defraud, delude, trick, cheat, (in these<BR>senses properly A., but sometimes also P.): Pass. of<BR>Caus. वञ्च्यते, to be deceived: Desid. विवञ्चि-<BR>षते: Intens. वनीवच्यते, वनीवञ्चीति; [cf. pro-<BR>bably Gr. ἄτη, ἀτάω, ἀπάτη, ἀτάσθαλος, ἀτύξομαι;<BR>Lat. vafer.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्वा
वक्त्वा or वचित्वा, ind. = वञ्चित्वा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस
2. वचस, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 878, col. 2),<BR>Ved. oscillating, moving about, rolling (said of car-<BR>riages).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्यु
2. वचस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ (for 1. see p. 878, col. 2),<BR>Ved. shaking, tossing, tottering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्यमान
2. वच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being urged on<BR>or incited, being inspired, (according to Sāy. वच्य-<BR>मान = both उच्यमान and प्रेर्यमाण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चक|वंचक|वञ्चकः
वञ्चक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.), deceiving,<BR>cheating, one who deceives, a deceiver, rogue, cheat,<BR>knave; fraudulent, deceitful, crafty; (अस्), m. a<BR>jackal; a musk-rat; a tame or house-ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चथ|वंचथ|वंचथः|वञ्चथः
वञ्चथ, अस्, m. a deceiver, rogue, knave, cheat;<BR>the Indian cuckoo; cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चन|वंचन|वंचनं|वञ्चनं
वञ्चन, अम्, आ, n. f. (fr. the Caus.), the act of<BR>deceiving, cheating, defrauding, fraud, deceit, (वञ्-<BR>चनम् or वञ्चनां कृ, to practise fraud, cheat);<BR>illusion, delusion, hallucination.<BR>—वञ्चन-ता, f.<BR>trickery, deception, roguishness.<BR>—वञ्चन-प्र-<BR>वण, अस्, आ, अम्, inclined to fraud or deception.<BR>—वञ्चन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, deceitful, crafty, fraudu-<BR>lent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चनीय
वञ्चनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be avoided or shunned;<BR>to be deceived, capable of being cheated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चयितव्य
वञ्चयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be tricked or cheated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चयितृ
वञ्चयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who deceives, a<BR>deceiver, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चयित्वा
वञ्चयित्वा, ind. having cheated or deceived,<BR>having deluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चित|वंचित|वञ्चितः
वञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), deceived,<BR>tricked, cheated, deluded, imposed upon; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of riddle or enigma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चितक
वञ्चितक in पक्ष-व्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चित्वा
वञ्चित्वा, ind. having cheated or deceived, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चिन्
वञ्चिन्, ई, इनी, इ, deceiving, cheating (at the end<BR>of a comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चुक|वंचुक|वञ्चुकः
वञ्चुक or वञ्चूक, अस्, ई, अम्, deceptive, fraudu-<BR>lent, dishonest, crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्च्य|वञ्च्यं
वञ्च्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone, to be avoided,<BR>&c.; to be cheated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चति|वंचति|वंचतिः|वञ्चतिः
वञ्चति वञ्चति, इस्, m. fire; [cf. अञ्चति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जरा
वञ्जरा वञ्जरा, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जुल|वंजुल|वञ्जुलः
वञ्जुल वञ्जुल, अस्, m. the tree Dalbergia<BR>Ougeinensis; another tree, Jonesia Aśoka; common<BR>cane or ratan, Calamus Rotang; a kind of flower,<BR>Hibiscus Mutabilis; a sort of bird; (आ), f. a cow<BR>that yields abundance of milk; N. of a river.<BR>—वञ्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">Page0880-b+ 80</a>]<BR>जुल-द्रुम, अस्, m. the Aśoka tree.<BR>—वञ्जुल-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m. the ratan, Calamus Rotang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जुलक|वञ्जुलकः
वञ्जुलक, अस्, m. a kind of plant; a sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट्
वट् 1. वट् (probably connected with rt.<BR>1. वृत्), cl. 1. P. वटति, ववाट, वटितुम्,<BR>to surround, encompass; cl. 10. P. वटयति, &c.,<BR>to tie, string, connect; to divide, partition: Caus.<BR>वटयति, -यितुम्, to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट|वटः
वट, अस्, m. the banyan or Indian fig-tree, Ficus<BR>Indica, (said to be also अम्, n.); a small shell, the<BR>Cypræa Moneta or cowry; a sort of bird; a little<BR>ball, globule, pill, small lump or roundish mass; a<BR>cake made of pulse ground and fried with oil or<BR>butter [cf. वटक]; a round figure, circle, cipher;<BR>equality in shape or dimension; N. of one of<BR>Skanda's attendants; (अस्, ई, अम्), m. f. n. a string,<BR>rope, tie; (ई), f. a pill, bolus; a kind of tree (=<BR>नदी-वट); गढा वटी, a particular position in<BR>the game of Catur-aṅga or chess.<BR>—वट-कणिका or<BR>वट-कणीका, f. a very small particle of the Indian<BR>fig-tree.<BR>—वट-ज, अस्, m., see Pāṇ. VI. 2, 82.<BR>—वट-तले, ind. at the bottom of an Indian fig-tree,<BR>under a banyan tree.<BR>—वट-तीर्थ-नाथ, N. of a<BR>Liṅga.<BR>—वट-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a kind of white basil;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of jasmine; a plant from the fibrous<BR>leaves of which bow-strings are made, Aletris Hyacin-<BR>thoides; Sanseviera Zeylanica; (ई), f. a kind of<BR>plant (= इरावती).<BR>—वट-यक्षिणी-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—वट-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in<BR>the Indian fig-tree; (ई), m. a Yakṣa.<BR>—वटेश्वर<BR>(˚ट-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Liṅga; of the author of<BR>a commentary on the drama called Mudrā-rākṣasa.<BR>—वटेश्वर-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—वटोदका (˚ट-उद्˚), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटक|वटकः
वटक, अस्, m. a small lump or round mass, ball,<BR>globule; a kind of cake made of pulse fried in oil<BR>or butter, (said to be also अम्, n.); a particular<BR>weight, = 8 Māṣas or 2 Śāṇas; (इका), f. a pill,<BR>bolus; a chess-man, (see under वट above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटकिनी
वटकिनी, f. (fr. वटक), N. of a particular night<BR>of full moon (when it is customary to eat Vaṭaka<BR>cakes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटर|वटरः
वटर, अस्, आ, अम्, wicked, villainous, unsteady;<BR>(अस्), m. a thief; a cock; a cloth worn round the<BR>head, turban; a mat; a fragrant grass, Cyperus;<BR>a churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटाकर|वटाकरः
वटाकर, अस्, m. a cord, string (= वराटक,<BR>वटारक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटारक|वटारकः
वटारक, अस्, m. a cord, string, rope (= वरा-<BR>टक, वटाकर); N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. this<BR>man's descendants.<BR>—वटारक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made or consisting of a rope, made of string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटि|वटिः
वटि, इस्, f. a sort of ant (= दिवी and उपजिह्वा);<BR>a kind of louse or other insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटिक|वटिकः
वटिक, अस्, m. a pawn or common man at chess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटिन्
वटिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a string, stringed; circular,<BR>globular; (ई), m. = वटिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटिभ
वटिभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having or containing the<BR>insect called Vaṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटी
वटी, f. See under वट above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटु|वटुः
वटु, उस्, m. (also written बटु), a boy, lad,<BR>stripling, youth; a young Brāhman or Brahma-cārin,<BR>religious student; N. of a class of priests; a form<BR>of Śiva (so called from being represented by boys in<BR>the rites of the Śāktas); a plant, Colosanthes Indica<BR>or Bignonia Indica.<BR>—वटु-मात्र, a mere stripling.<BR>—वटु-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having the form of a lad<BR>or stripling.<BR>—वटू-करण, अम्, n. the act of<BR>making into a youth, the introduction of a boy to<BR>his preceptor [cf. उप-नयन], investiture with<BR>the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटुक|वटुकः
वटुक, अस्, m. a boy, lad, youth; a young Brāh-<BR>man or religious student; a stupid fellow, blockhead;<BR>N. of a class of priests; a form of Śiva (among the<BR>Śāktas).<BR>—वटुक-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—वटुक-भैरव, अस्, m. a form<BR>of Bhairava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटूरिन्
वटूरिन् or महा-वटूरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. broad,<BR>wide, wide-spreading, (Sāy. = वेष्टन-शील or अति-<BR>विस्तृत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट्य
वट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the Vaṭa or Indian<BR>fig-tree; a kind of mineral, (gender doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट्
वट् 2. वट्, ind., Ved. an interjection or<BR>exclamation used in sacrificial ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटावीक|वटावीकः
वटावीक वटावीक, अस्, m. one who assumes<BR>a false name; notorious thief (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट्ट
वट्ट वट्ट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वट्ट-देव,<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठ्
वठ् वठ् (also written बठ्), cl. 1. P.<BR>वठति, ववाठ (3rd pl. ववठुस्), व-<BR>ठितुम्, to be large; to be powerful or able; to<BR>be fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठर|वठरः
वठर वठर, अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. V. 39. fr. rt. वच् with substitution of ठ्<BR>for च्), stupid, slow, dull; vile, wicked, abandoned<BR>[cf. वटर]; (अस्), m. a fool, blockhead; a phy-<BR>sician; a water-pot; = शब्द-कार; = वक्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडभि|वडभिः
वडभि वडभि, इस्, or वडभी, f. the wooden<BR>frame of a roof; a flat roof, house-top, top room,<BR>turret, top floor, balcony, any temporary erection on<BR>the top of a palace, awning, tent; [cf. वलभि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडवा
वडवा वडवा, f. (also written वडबा, ब-<BR>डवा, q. v.), a female horse, mare, (also वडव, अस्,<BR>m. in Taittirīya-s. II. 1, 8, 3, in the sense of a horse<BR>resembling a mare); the nymph Aśvinī (who, in<BR>the form of a mare as the wife of Vivasvat or the<BR>Sun, became the mother of the two Aśvins, see<BR>अश्विनी); the personification of the constellation<BR>represented by a horse's head; a female slave; a<BR>harlot, prostitute; N. of a woman (having the patro-<BR>nymic Prātitheyī); of a wife of Vasu-deva (having<BR>the epithet Pari-cārikā, Hari-vaṃśa 1949); of a river;<BR>of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—वडव-धेनु, उस्, f., Ved.<BR>a mare.<BR>—वडवाग्नि (˚वा-अग्˚), इस्, m. ‘mare's fire,’<BR>submarine fire or the fire of the lower regions (fabled<BR>to be at the South-pole and not extinguishable by<BR>the sea water; see और्व, बडवाग्नि).<BR>—वडवा-<BR>नल (˚वा-अन्˚), अस्, m. = वडवाग्नि; a kind of<BR>medicinal powder (composed of pepper and other<BR>pungent materials and used to facilitate digestion).<BR>—वडवा-मुख, अम्, n. ‘the mare's mouth,’ the<BR>entrance to the lower regions at the South-pole;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), belonging to the submarine fire at the<BR>South-pole; (अस्), m. the submarine fire described<BR>above; N. of Śiva; a personification of a Maharṣi<BR>(identified with Nārāyaṇa); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>mythical people.<BR>—वडवा-वक्त्र, अम्, n. = व-<BR>डवा-मुख.<BR>—वडवा-हृत, a term applied to<BR>a kind of slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडविन्
वडविन्, ई, इनी, इ, an adjective formed from<BR>वडवा, see Gaṇa Vrīhyādi to Pāṇ. V. 2, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडा
वडा वडा or वडिका, f. = वट, pulse ground<BR>and fried with oil or butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडिश
वडिश वडिश, अम्, n. (rarely अस्, m., and<BR>according to some also आ, ई, f.), a hook, fish-hook;<BR>a particular surgical instrument in the form of a<BR>hook; [cf. वलिश.]<BR>—वडिश-युत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>joined to or fastened on a hook (said of a bait).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडौसक
वडौसक वडौसक, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वड्र|वड्रं
वड्र वड्र, अस्, आ, अम्, large, great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्
वण् वण् (also written बण्), cl. 1. P.<BR>वणति, ववाण (Caus. Aor. अवीवणत् or<BR>अववाणत्), वणितुम्, to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण|वणः
वण, अस्, m. sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वणथलग्राम
वणथलग्राम वणथल-ग्राम, अस्, m. (pro-<BR>bably a corruption of वन-स्थल-ग्˚), N. of a<BR>village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वणिज्
वणिज् वणिज्, क्, m. (also written बणिज्,<BR>q. v.), a merchant, trader; the sign of the zodiac<BR>Libra or the Scales; (क्), f. trade, merchandise.<BR>—व-<BR>णिक्-कर्मन्, अ, n. or वणिक्-क्रिया, f. the business<BR>or occupation of a trader, trade, merchandise.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">Page0881-a+ 75</a>]<BR>—वणिक्-पथ, अस्, m. (see बणिक्-पथ), ‘trader's<BR>path, ‘a trader's business, merchandise, traffic; a<BR>merchant's shop; a merchant; the zodiacal sign<BR>Libra or the Scales.<BR>—वणिक्-सार्थ, अस्, m. a com-<BR>pany of traders or merchants, caravan.<BR>—वणिग्-<BR>जन, अस्, m. a tradesman, merchant; tradespeople,<BR>merchants.<BR>—वणिग्-बन्धु, वणिग्-भाव, वणिग्-<BR>वह, see बणिग्-ब्˚, &c.<BR>—वणिग्-वृत्ति, इस्, f. ‘live-<BR>lihood by trade,’ trade, traffic, retail or petty trade, low<BR>trade, huckstering.<BR>—वणिङ्-मार्ग, अस्, m. ‘trader's<BR>path or road,’ a merchant's shop, &c. (= विपणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0880-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वणिज|वणिजः
वणिज, अस्, m. = वणिज्, a merchant; the zodiacal<BR>sign Libra; N. of a particular Karaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वणिजक|वणिजकः
वणिजक, अस्, m. a merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वणिज्य|वणिज्यं
वणिज्य, अम्, आ, n. f. trade, traffic, (for वाणिज्य;<BR>cf. बणिज्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट्|वंट्
वण्ट् वण्ट् (also written बण्ट्, connected<BR>with rt. वण्ड्), cl. 1. 10. P. वण्टति,<BR>वण्टयति (also, according to some, वण्टापयति),<BR>&c., to partition, apportion, share, separate, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट|वंट|वण्टः
वण्ट, अस्, m. a part, portion; the handle of a sickle;<BR>an unmarried man; (अस्, आ, अम्), unmarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टक|वंटक|वंटकः|वण्टकः
वण्टक, अस्, m. dividing; an apportioner, distri-<BR>buter; a part, portion, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टन|वंटन|वंटनं
वण्टन, अम्, n. the act of portioning, apportion-<BR>ing, partitioning, dividing into shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टनीय
वण्टनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be apportioned, divisi-<BR>ble, to be divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टित
वण्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, divided into shares, distri-<BR>buted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टाल|वंटाल|वंटालः|वण्टालः
वण्टाल वण्टाल or वण्ठाल, अस्, m. a<BR>spade, shovel, hoe; a boat; a kind of battle, the<BR>contest of heroes; [cf. वण्डाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठ्|वंठ्
वण्ठ् वण्ठ्, cl. 1. A. वण्ठते, ववण्ठे,<BR>वण्ठितुम्, to go or move alone, go un-<BR>accompanied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठ|वंठ|वण्ठः
वण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, crippled, maimed; unmarried;<BR>(अस्), m. an unmarried man; a servant; a dwarf; a<BR>javelin; [cf. वण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठर|वंठर|वंठरः|वण्ठरः
वण्ठर, अस्, m. the new shoot of the Tāl or<BR>palm tree; the sheath that envelopes the young<BR>bamboo; a rope for tying a goat, &c.; the female<BR>breast; a dog's tail; a dog; a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ड्|वंड्
वण्ड् वण्ड् (connected with rt. वण्ट्),<BR>cl. 1. A. वण्डते, ववण्डे, वण्डितुम्,<BR>to partition, apportion, share, divide; to surround,<BR>encompass; to cover; cl. 10. P. वण्डयति, &c.,<BR>to partition, share, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ड|वंड|वण्डः
वण्ड वण्ड, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. वन् or वण्), maimed, defective, crippled (espe-<BR>cially in the hands or feet or tail), one whose<BR>hands have been cut off [cf. वण्ठ]; impotent,<BR>emasculated [cf. पण्ड]; (अस्), m. a man who is<BR>circumcised or has no prepuce, (probably a wrong<BR>reading for चण्ड); an ox without a tail [cf. अ-वण्ड];<BR>(आ), f. an unchaste woman, (probably a wrong reading<BR>for रण्डा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्डर|वंडर|वंडरः|वण्डरः
वण्डर, अस्, m. a niggard, miser; a eunuch or<BR>attendant on the women's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्डाल|वंडाल|वंडालः|वण्डालः
वण्डाल वण्डाल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>वण्ड्), a particular mode of fighting, the contest of<BR>heroes; a boat; a spade, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्
वत् 1. वत्, ind. an affix (technically termed<BR>वति) added to words to imply likeness or resem-<BR>blance, and generally translatable by ‘as,’ ‘like’ (e. g.<BR>ब्राह्मण-वत्, like a Brāhman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्
वत् 2. वत्, a Vedic rt. usually connected<BR>with अपि, (probably) cl. 1. वतति, &c.,<BR>to understand, comprehend, apprehend, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 3, 10. वतेम = सम्भ-<BR>जेमहि, ‘may we share in or possess or obtain,’<BR>where वत् is said to stand for rt. 1. वन्): Caus.<BR>वातयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अवीवतत्, to cause to under-<BR>stand, make intelligible; to excite, awaken, (Sāy. =<BR>प्रापयति, आगमयति, प्रेरयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतत्
वतत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, understanding, comprehending,<BR>(Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 60, 6 = गच्छत्, going.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातयत्
वातयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to understand;<BR>exciting, &c., (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>165, 13. अपि-वातयत् = सम्पूर्णम् प्रापयत्,<BR>causing to obtain completely.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत
वत 1. वत, ind. in the earlier language<BR>generally written बत, q. v.; for 2. वत see<BR>p. 883, col. 1), a particle expressing sorrow, com-<BR>passion, pleasure, surprise, &c., and generally trans-<BR>latable by ‘ah!’ ‘alas!’ ‘oh!’ also used as a vocative<BR>particle; (in later Sanskrit वत is often found in<BR>the middle of a sentence.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतंस|वतंसः
वतंस व-तंस or व-तंसक, अस्, m. =<BR>अव-तंस, a garland; a ring-shaped ornament, ear-<BR>ring, ear-ornament; a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतण्ड|वतण्डः
वतण्ड वतण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a Muni; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the descendants of Vataṇḍa, (तण्ड-वतण्-<BR>डास्, m. pl. the descendants of Taṇḍa and Vataṇḍa);<BR>(ई), f. a female descendant^1 of Vataṇḍa.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वति|वतिः
वति वति, see under rt. 1. वन्. (For the<BR>affix वति see 1. वत्, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतू
वतू वतू, ऊस्, f. a river of heaven; (ऊस्), m. one<BR>who speaks the truth, a road; a disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतोका
वतोका व-तोका, f. = अव-तोका, a cow mis-<BR>carrying from accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्स|वत्सं|वत्सः
वत्स वत्स, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 62. fr. rt. वद्), a calf, a young animal or the<BR>young of any animal, offspring, child, (वत्स, voc. c.<BR>‘my dear child, my darling,’ used as a term of en-<BR>dearment; जीवद्-वत्सा, a woman whose child is still<BR>alive); a son, boy, (बाल-वत्सा, a woman whose<BR>son is still a boy); a year [cf. वत्सर]; N. of a<BR>son or descendant of Kaṇva; of a descendant of<BR>Agni (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 187); of a<BR>descendant of Kaśyapa; of the author of a law-book;<BR>of a son of Pratardana; of a son of Prasena-jit; of<BR>a son of Akṣa-mālā; of a son of Uru-kṣepa; of a<BR>son of Soma-śarman; N. of a country (its chief town<BR>is Kauśāmbhī); (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Vatsa;<BR>N. of the inhabitants of Vatsa and of the country;<BR>(आ), f. a female calf; a little daughter, little girl,<BR>(वत्से, voc. c. ‘my dear child,’ used as a term of<BR>endearment); (अम्), n. the breast, chest, (according<BR>to some authorities also अस्, m.); [cf. Gr. ἰτ-αλό-ς<BR>(for ϝιταλός,); Lat. vitulu-s, vitula; Osk. Viteliu<BR>(= Italia); Slav. tel-ici; Bohem. tel-e; Lith.<BR>telycza.]<BR>—वत्स-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, child-loving,<BR>fondly loving or affectionate towards offspring; (आ),<BR>f. a cow longing for her calf; a mother anxious after<BR>her child.<BR>—वत्स-गुरु, उस्, m. a teacher of children,<BR>preceptor.<BR>—वत्स-तन्त्री, ईस्, f. a rope for tying calves.<BR>—वत्स-तर, अस्, m. ‘more than a calf,’ a weaned<BR>calf, young ox or bull, bullock, steer, (also applied<BR>to the young of goats); (ई), f. a heifer.<BR>—वत्सत-<BR>रार्ण (˚र-ऋण), अम्, n. the debt or loan of a<BR>bullock (?) ; see Vopa-deva II. 9.<BR>—वत्स-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state or condition of a calf.<BR>—वत्स-दन्त,<BR>अस्, m. ‘calf-toothed,’ a kind of arrow (having a<BR>point like the tooth of a calf); (अम्), n. an arrow<BR>point like a calf's tooth.<BR>—वत्स-नपात्, m., N. of<BR>a descendant of Babhru.<BR>—वत्स-नाभ, अस्, m. a<BR>particular tree; a particular kind of strong poison<BR>prepared from the root of a kind of aconite (said to<BR>resemble the nipple of a cow; the poison is also<BR>called Mīthā zahr); a proper N.; (अम्), n. a hole<BR>of a particular shape in the frame of a bedstead.<BR>—वत्स-नाभक, अस्, m. the poison described<BR>above.<BR>—वत्स-प, अस्, m. a keeper of calves; N. of<BR>a demon (Ved.).<BR>—वत्स-पति, इस्, m. a king or lord<BR>of the Vatsas, (or) N. of a king.<BR>—वत्स-पत्तन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘Vatsa town,’ N. of a city in the north of<BR>India, (also called Kauśāmbhī.)<BR>—वत्स-पाल, अस्,<BR>m. a keeper of calves; N. of Kṛṣṇa; of Bala-deva.<BR>—वत्स-पालन, अम्, n. the act of keeping calves.<BR>—वत्स-प्रचेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. minding or<BR>taking care of Vatsa or the Vatsas, (Sāy. = स्तोतरि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">Page0881-c+ 79</a>]<BR>प्रकृष्ट-ज्ञान, favourably-minded towards a<BR>worshipper.)<BR>—वत्स-प्री, ईस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the hymns Ṛg-veda IX. 68, X. 45, 46, (his<BR>patronymic is Bhālandana.)<BR>—वत्स-प्रीति, इस्, m. =<BR>वत्स-प्री.<BR>—वत्स-बन्धा, f. a cow longing for<BR>her calf.<BR>—वत्स-बालक, अस्, m., N. of a brother<BR>of Vasu-deva.<BR>—वत्स-भूमि, इस्, f. the land of the<BR>Vatsas, N. of a country; (इस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Vatsa.<BR>—वत्स-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a certain Go-<BR>bhila.<BR>—वत्स-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, calf-faced, having<BR>the face of a calf.<BR>—वत्स-राज, अस्, m. a king of<BR>the Vatsas; a proper N.<BR>—वत्स-राज-देव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—वत्स-राज्य, अम्, n. sovereignty or<BR>authority over the Vatsas.<BR>—वत्स-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having or possessing a calf; (आन्), m., N. of one of<BR>the sons of Śūra.<BR>—वत्स-विन्द, अस्, m. a proper N.;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. Vatsa-vinda's descendants.<BR>—वत्स-वृद्-<BR>ध, अस्, m., N. of a son of Uru-kriya.<BR>—वत्स-<BR>व्यूह, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vatsa.<BR>—वत्स-शाला, f.<BR>a calf-shed; (अस्, आ, अम्), born in a calf-shed.<BR>—वत्-<BR>साक्षी (˚स-अक्˚), f. a kind of cucumber, Cucumis<BR>Madraspatanus.<BR>—वत्साङ्क (˚स-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—वत्साजीव (˚स-आज्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, living<BR>by calves, obtaining a livelihood by keeping calves;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of a Piṅgala.<BR>—वत्सादन (˚स-<BR>अद्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, eating calves; (अस्), m. a wolf; (ई),<BR>f. ‘eating its own offspring,’ Cocculus Cordifolius (so<BR>called as not bringing all its berries to maturity).<BR>—वत्सासुर (˚स-अस्˚), अस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—वत्सेश or वत्सेश्वर (˚स-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a king<BR>of Vatsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सक|वत्सकं|वत्सकः
वत्सक, अस्, m. a little calf, calf, or young animal<BR>in general; a child, offspring; a medicinal plant,<BR>Wrightia Antidysenterica; N. of a son of Śūra; of<BR>an Asura; (इका), f. a calf, female calf, a heifer,<BR>young cow; (अम्), n. green or black sulphate of<BR>iron.<BR>—वत्सक-वीज, अम्, n. the seed of Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सर|वत्सरः
वत्सर, अस्, m. the fifth year in a cycle of five or<BR>six years; the sixth year in a cycle of six years; a<BR>year; the Year personified as a son of Dhruva and<BR>Bhrami; N. of Viṣṇu; of a Sādhya; of a son of<BR>Kaśyapa; [cf. Gr. ἔτος (ϝέρος), ἐτήσιο-ς, ἐτησίαι,<BR>δυσετηρία; Lat. vetus, vetus-tu-s, vetulu-s; Lith.<BR>wasara; Slav. vetuchu.]<BR>—वत्सरादि (˚र-आदि), इस्,<BR>m. the first month of the Hindū year, the month<BR>Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR>—वत्सरान्तक (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘Year-destroyer,’ N. of the month Phālguna.<BR>—वत्-<BR>सरार्ण (˚र-ऋण), अम्, n. a debt or loan for a<BR>year (?); see Vopa-deva II. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सल|वत्सलः
वत्सल, अस्, आ, अम्, child-loving, affectionate<BR>towards offspring, affectionate in general; kind, lov-<BR>ing, tender; fond of, wholly given up to, devoted to,<BR>longing for (sometimes with loc., e. g. गावो वत्सेषु<BR>वत्सलाः, cows longing for their calves); (अस्), m. a<BR>fire fed with grass (i. e. quickly burning away); N.<BR>of one of Skanda's attendants; (आ), f. a cow fond of<BR>her calf; (अम्), n. affection, fondness.<BR>—वत्सल-ता,<BR>f. or वत्सल-त्व, अम्, n. affectionateness, loving-<BR>ness, tenderness, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सलय
वत्सलय, Nom. P. वत्सलयति, &c., to make<BR>tender or affectionate (especially towards offspring or<BR>children).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्साय
वत्साय, Nom. P. वत्सायति, &c., to represent<BR>or be like a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सायत्
वत्सायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, acting like a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सार
वत्सार, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kaśyapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सिन्
वत्सिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a calf; (ई), m. (perhaps)<BR>‘having many children,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सिमन्
वत्सिमन्, आ, m. childhood, youth, early youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सीय|वत्सीयः
वत्सीय, अस्, आ, अम्, proper or fit for a calf; (अस्),<BR>m. a cowherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सणुरकतीर्थ
वत्सणुरकतीर्थ वत्सणुरक-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वथ्सर
वथ्सर वथ्सर, अस्, m. = वत्सर (accord-<BR>ing to the grammarian Pauṣkarasādi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद्
वद् वद् (sometimes lengthened in ep.<BR>into वाद् on account of the metre), cl. 1. P.<BR>A. वदति, वदते, उवाद (3rd du. ऊदतुस्, 3rd<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">Page0882-a+ 81</a>]<BR>pl. ऊदुस्; according to Vopa-deva VIII. 52, 2nd sing.<BR>also वेदिथ, 3rd du. वेदतुस्, 3rd pl. वेदुस्), ऊदे (3rd<BR>du. ऊदाते, 3rd pl. ऊदिरे), वदिष्यति, -ते, अवादीत्,<BR>अवदिष्ट, Prec. उद्यात्, वदितुम्, to speak, say,<BR>utter, tell, speak to, address (with acc. of the thing<BR>said and of the person addressed and sometimes with<BR>prep. अभि and acc., both P. and A. being used<BR>indiscriminately, e. g. यद् वदसि माम्, that which<BR>thou sayest to me; माम् अभि वदति, he speaks<BR>to me; किं वदामि or वदे, what must I say?<BR>मैवं वद or वदस्व, do not speak so; स-<BR>त्यं वद or वदस्व, speak the truth; देवानां<BR>वचनात् त्वां वदामि or वदे, I speak to thee in<BR>the name of the gods; प्रतिवाक्यं वद or वद-<BR>स्व, speak a reply); to speak about, declare, proclaim,<BR>announce, communicate, inform, notify; to maintain,<BR>affirm; to designate, call, name; to raise the voice,<BR>sign, utter a cry (said of birds &c.); to discuss, dispute<BR>about, contend, quarrel (Ved. A.); to be called, be con-<BR>sidered (Ved. A.); to state authoritatively (?), be an<BR>authority (A.); to exert one's self, strive for (A.):<BR>Pass. उद्यते, Aor. अवादि, Part. उदित (see 2. उदित),<BR>to be said or spoken, to be addressed or spoken to;<BR>to be declared or announced, to be published or<BR>proclaimed: Caus. वादयति, -यते, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अवीवदत्, to cause to speak or say, to urge or invite<BR>to speak; to cause to sound forth, play (a musical<BR>instrument; generally P.), to play music; to cause<BR>to be played by any one (inst.); to speak, recite,<BR>rehearse: Pass. of Caus. वाद्यते: Desid. विवदि-<BR>षति, -ते, to desire to speak: Intens. वावद्यते,<BR>वावत्ति, वावदीति, to speak aloud; to sound loudly;<BR>[cf. Gr. ὕδ-ω, ὑδ-έ-ω, ὕδ-η-ς, ἀ(ϝ)είδ-ω, ἀοιδό-ς,<BR>ἀοιδή, ἀηδών, (according to some) αὐδή, αὐδάω,<BR>(perhaps also) φράζω, φραδάω: (probably) Lat. vas<BR>(vad-is): (perhaps) Old Germ. far-wāzan: Old<BR>Sax. for-wātan: Lith. vad-i-n-u, ‘I call:' Slav.<BR>vad-i-ti, vāda, ‘accusation;’ us-ta, ‘mouth:’ Hib.<BR>feadaim, ‘I say;' (perhaps) luadhaim, ‘I men-<BR>tion;’ raidim, ‘I say.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0881-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद|वदः
वद, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, able to speak, speak-<BR>ing well or sensibly, (frequently at the end of comps.;<BR>cf. प्रियं-व्˚, कु-व्˚); (अस्), m., N. of a so-called<BR>Veda (with the Magians).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदक
वदक = वद in दुर्-वदक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदत्
वदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, speaking, saying, telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन|वदनं
वदन, अम्, n. the act of speaking or saying;<BR>sounding (Ved.); the mouth, face, countenance,<BR>(काल-वदन, ‘the face of Time,’ N. of a Śaiva<BR>work), aspect, appearance, look; the front, point;<BR>the first term, initial quantity or term of a progres-<BR>sion (in algebra); the summit or apex of a triangle;<BR>[cf. Hib. aodann, ‘the face;’ eudan, ‘the fore-<BR>head.’]<BR>—वदन-दन्तुर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—वदन-मदिरा, f. the wine or nectar of the<BR>mouth.<BR>—वदन-रोग, अस्, m. mouth-disease.<BR>—वदन-श्यामिका, f. blackness of the face; a<BR>kind of disease.<BR>—वदन-सरोज, अम्, n. ‘face-<BR>lotus, ‘the face of a mistress.<BR>—वदनामय (˚न-<BR>आम्˚), अस्, m. mouth-disease, face-sickness.<BR>—वद-<BR>नासव (˚न-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘mouth-liquor,’ saliva,<BR>spittle.<BR>—वदनी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to<BR>become a face, be changed into a face.<BR>—वदनी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, changed into a face.<BR>—वद-<BR>नेन्दु (˚न-इन्˚), उस्, m. ‘face-moon,’ the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्त
वदन्त in किं-व्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्ति|वदन्तिः
वदन्ति, इस्, or वदन्ती, f. speech, discourse, talk,<BR>(according to some only used in किं-व्˚, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्तिक
वदन्तिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्य|वदन्यः
वदन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = वदान्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदमान
वदमान, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, saying, telling;<BR>calling; explaining, declaring; glorifying, boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदान्य|वदान्यः
वदान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, eloquent, speaking kindly<BR>or agreeably, affable; bountiful, liberal, munificent,<BR>(in this sense probably for 1. अव-दान्य); (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदावद|वदावदः
वदावद, अस्, आ, अम्, or वदावदिन्, ई, इनी, इ<BR>(probably an old Intens., cf. 2. महामह), speak-<BR>ing much, talkative, chattering, speaking, a speaker;<BR>able to speak well, eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदितव्य
वदितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be said or spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदितृ
वदितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, saying, speaking, a speaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदिष्ठ
वदिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. speaking very well,<BR>speaking best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद्य
वद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken &c., (used only<BR>in comp., cf. अ-वद्य, अन्-अवद्य); an epithet of<BR>the days of the dark lunar fortnight, (see वद्य-<BR>पक्ष); (अम्), n. speech, speaking about, con-<BR>versing, (only at the end of a comp., cf. ब्रह्म-व्˚,<BR>सत्य-व्˚.)<BR>—वद्य-पक्ष, अस्, m. the dark fort-<BR>night of the lunar month (in which the moon is<BR>waning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदर|वदरं|वदरः
वदर वदर, वदरि, &c. See बदर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदरिक
वदरिक, अस्, m. a jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदाम|वदामं|वदामः
वदाम वदाम, अस्, m. (fr. the Persian<BR>بادام), an almond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदाल|वदालः
वदाल वदाल, अस्, m. a kind of Silurus or<BR>sheat-fish; an eddy or whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदालक|वदालकः
वदालक, अस्, m. = वदाल, a kind of sheat-fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदि
वदि वदि, ind. (according to some for ब-<BR>दि, contracted fr. बहुल-दिन, but cf. वद्य), in<BR>the dark half of any month, (affixed to the names of<BR>months in giving dates at the end of MSS.; cf.<BR>वैशाख-व्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद्दिवास
वद्दिवास वद्दिवास, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद्ध्री
वद्ध्री वद्ध्री. See under वध्र, p. 883.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्
वध् वध् (a defective rt. frequently<BR>written बध्, see 3. बध्, properly only<BR>used in the Aorist and Precative tenses, the other tenses<BR>being supplied fr. rt. हन्, q. v.), Aor. P. A. अव-<BR>धीत्, अवधिष्ट, (मा वधिष्ठाः, do not kill);<BR>Prec. 1st sing. वध्यासम्, 3rd sing. वध्यात्, (in<BR>the Veda the Potential also occurs, e. g. 1st sing.<BR>वधेयम्, 3rd sing. वधेत्; in epic poetry the<BR>2nd Fut. P. A. वधिष्यति, -ते, and some tenses<BR>and forms of the Pass.; other Vedic forms are व-<BR>धीम्, वधिष्टन), to strike; to slay, kill, put<BR>to death, destroy, murder: Pass. वध्यते (ep. P.<BR>वध्यति), 3rd sing. Impv. वध्यताम्, Aor. अव-<BR>धि, Prec. वधिषीष्ट, to be slain or killed: Caus.<BR>वध्यति, -यितुम्, to kill, slay; [cf. according to<BR>some, Lat. lœdo: Hib. fœthaim, ‘I kill;’ fœthadh,<BR>‘killing;’ fesaim, ‘I kill, destroy;’ feadhm, ‘kill-<BR>ing.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध|वधः
वध, अस्, m. one who kills or slays, a killer,<BR>slaughterer; a vanquisher, victor; a deadly weapon,<BR>Indra's thunderbolt (Ved.); the act of striking, kill-<BR>ing, slaying, slaughter, murder, death, destruction;<BR>a blow, stroke, corporal punishment; paralysis;<BR>destruction, disappearance (said of inanimate objects);<BR>multiplication.<BR>—वध-कर्माधिकारिन् (˚म-<BR>अध्˚), ई, m. ‘one who superintends the act of put-<BR>ting to death,’ an executioner, hangman.<BR>—वध-<BR>काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wishing for death.<BR>—वध-<BR>काम्या, f. the desire to kill, intention to hurt.<BR>—वध-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, living by the death (of<BR>animals); (ई), m. a butcher; a hunter, fowler.<BR> — 1. वध-त्र, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. वधत्र<BR>see col. 3), protecting from death or destruction.<BR>—वध-दण्ड, capital punishment; corporal<BR>punishment (e. g. whipping &c., Manu VIII. 129).<BR>—वध-निर्णेक, अस्, m. expiation for killing,<BR>atonement for murder or manslaughter.<BR>—वध-<BR>भूमि, इस्, f. execution-ground, place of execution.<BR>—वध-स्थली, f. or वध-स्थान, अम्, n. a<BR>place of execution; a slaughter-house.<BR>—वधाङ्-<BR>गक (˚ध-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a prison.<BR>—वधार्ह<BR>(˚ध-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deserving death.<BR>—वधै-<BR>षिन् (˚ध-एष्˚), ई, इणी, इ, desirous of killing, in-<BR>tending to kill.<BR>—वधोदर्क (˚ध-उद्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, resulting in death, effecting death.<BR>—वधोद्यत<BR>(˚ध-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, prepared or ready to kill,<BR>intending to put to death, murderous; an assassin,<BR>murderer.<BR>—वधोपाय (˚ध-उप्˚), अस्, m. an in-<BR>strument or means of putting to death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधक|वधकः
वधक, अस्, अका or इका, अम्, killing, destructive,<BR>pernicious, injurious; (अस्), m. one who kills, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">Page0882-c+ 79</a>]<BR>murderer, assassin; an executioner, hangman, (also<BR>written बधक); a particular sort of reed or rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधत्र|वधत्रं
2. वधत्र, अम्, n. (for 1. वध-त्र see<BR>col. 2), ‘an instrument of death,’ deadly weapon,<BR>dart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधना
वधना, f., Ved. a deadly weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधर्
वधर्, n., Ved. a destructive weapon, the weapon<BR>or thunderbolt of Indra, a thunderbolt (= वज्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधर्य
वधर्य, Nom. P. वधर्यति, &c., to desire<BR>the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधर्यत्
वधर्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, desiring the thunderbolt<BR>of Indra; (अन्ती), f. ‘casting a bolt,’ i. e. (according<BR>to some) lightning; (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 161, 9) a line of clouds or the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधस्
वधस् = वधर् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधस्न
वधस्न (apparently only used in the inst. pl.<BR>वधस्नैस्), Ved. a destructive or deadly weapon,<BR>the weapon of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधस्नु
वधस्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. bearing a deadly<BR>weapon, (Sāy. = प्रहारेण प्रस्रवण-शील.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधिक|वधिकः
वधिक, musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधित्र|वधित्रं
वधित्र, अम्, n. the god of love, love, sexual<BR>love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधिन्
वधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, incurring death, killed by, (at<BR>the end of a comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्य|वध्यः
वध्य, अस्, आ, अम् (frequently written बध्य),<BR>to be slain or killed, to be put to death, punished<BR>with death; to be punished or chastised, to be cor-<BR>porally punished, subject to corporal punishment;<BR>vulnerable, liable to be killed, to be destroyed, to<BR>be annihilated; (अस्), m. an enemy.<BR>—वध्य-घ्न,<BR>अस्, m. killing one sentenced to death, carrying out<BR>the duties of public executioner.<BR>—वध्य-ता, f. or<BR>वध्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being sentenced to<BR>be killed or of deserving death; fitness to be killed;<BR>destruction.<BR>—वध्य-पटह, अस्, m. a drum<BR>beaten at the time of the execution of a criminal.<BR>—वध्य-भू, ऊस्, or वध्य-भूमि, इस्, f. a<BR>place of public execution.<BR>—वध्य-माला, f. a gar-<BR>land placed on one condemned to death or about to<BR>be executed.<BR>—वध्य-वासस्, अस्, n. the clothes of<BR>a criminal who has been executed (given to a Caṇ-<BR>ḍāla, Manu X. 56).<BR>—वध्य-शिला, f. a stone or<BR>rock on which malefactors are executed, executioner's<BR>block, scaffold; a slaughter-house, shambles.<BR>—व-<BR>ध्य-स्थान, अम्, n. a place of execution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्यत्
वध्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being struck, being killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्यमान
वध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being killed, being<BR>destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्या
वध्या, f. killing, murder; [cf. आत्म-व्˚, ब्रह्-<BR>म-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्रि
वध्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. ‘one whose testicles are<BR>cut out, ‘castrated, emasculated, unmanly (= छिन्न-<BR>मुष्क, opposed to वृषन्).<BR>—वध्रि-मती, f.<BR>(fem. of an unused form वध्रि-मत्), Ved. having<BR>an impotent husband; a proper N.<BR>—वध्रि-वाच्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, Ved. speaking unmanly or useless words, idly<BR>talking, (Sāy. = जल्पक.)<BR>—वध्र्य्-अश्व, अस्, m.<BR>‘having castrated horses,’ a proper N.; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the family of Vadhry-aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्रिका
वध्रिका, m. (Pāṇ. I. 2, 52, Vārtt. 3), a cas-<BR>trated person, eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधा
वधा वधा, ind. a various reading for<BR>वध्वा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधु|वधुः
वधु वधु, वधुका. See p. 883, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधू
वधू वधू, ऊस्, f. (fr. वध् = rt. 1. वह्; or,<BR>according to others, fr. rt. बन्ध्, and then more<BR>properly written बधू), a bride or newly mar-<BR>ried woman (as ‘recently brought or led home’), a<BR>young wife, spouse; a woman in general, female,<BR>girl, maiden, (in Ṛg-veda VIII. 19, 36. perhaps ‘a<BR>handmaid’ or ‘female slave’ or, according to some,<BR>‘a mare or animal used for draught;’ cf. वधू-<BR>मत्); the female of any animal (e. g. मृग-<BR>वधू, the female of a deer, cf. व्याघ्र-व्˚); a<BR>daughter-in-law; the wife of a younger relation,<BR>younger brother's wife, nephew's wife, younger<BR>female relation; N. of various plants, Trigonella<BR>Corniculata; Echites Frutescens; Curuma Zerumbet;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">Page0883-a+ 77</a>]<BR>[cf. Hib. badhbh, ‘an evil-minded woman, witch.’]<BR>—वधू-काल, अस्, m. the time during which a<BR>woman is held to be a bride.<BR>—वधू-गृह-प्र-<BR>वेश or वधू-प्रवेश, अस्, m. the ceremony of the<BR>entrance of a bride into the house of her husband.<BR>—वधू-जन, अस्, m. a woman, female, wife.<BR>—वधू-दर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. looking at a<BR>bride.<BR>—वधू-पक्ष, अस्, m. the party or side of<BR>the bride (at a wedding).<BR>—वधू-पथ, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. the path or way of a bride.<BR>—वधू-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having or possessing a wife, ac-<BR>companied by a wife, having women; furnished or<BR>harnessed with yoke animals or with female animals<BR>suitable for draught; fit for harness, suitable for the<BR>yoke.<BR>—वधू-वस्त्र, अम्, n. bridal apparel.<BR>—व-<BR>धू-सरा, f., N. of a river (fabled to have sprung<BR>from the weeping eyes of Pulomā, wife of Bhṛgu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0882-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधु|वधुः
वधु, उस्, or वधुका, f. = वधू, a young wife<BR>or woman in general; a son's wife, daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधुटी
वधुटी or वधूटी, f. a young woman living in<BR>her father's house (whether married or not); a son's<BR>wife, daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूयु
वधूयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one who loves his wife,<BR>longing for a wife, desiring marriage, eager to marry,<BR>uxorious, lustful; one who seeks a wife, a wooer,<BR>suitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्वती
वध्वती, f. = वधूटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूटशयन|वधूटशयनः
वधूटशयन वधूटशयन, अस्, m. a lattice,<BR>window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्न
वध्न वध्न, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people,<BR>(more correctly written वध्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्य|वध्यः
वध्य वध्य, &c. See p. 882, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्र|वध्रं
वध्र वध्र, अम्, n. (more properly written<BR>बध्र, q. v.), a leathern strap or thong; lead; (ई),<BR>f. a leathern strap or thong, (sometimes spelt वद्-<BR>ध्री.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्रक
वध्रक, lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्रस्व
वध्रस्व, a various reading for वध्र्य्-अश्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्र्य|वध्र्यः
वध्र्य, अस्, m. (also written बध्र्य), a shoe,<BR>slipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्रि
वध्रि वध्रि, &c. See p. 882, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्वा
वध्वा वध्वा, ind., see Gaṇa Cādi to Pāṇ.<BR>I. 4, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्
वन् 1. वन्, cl. 1. P. वनति, &c., to<BR>sound; to serve, honour, worship, help,<BR>aid; cl. 8. P. A. वनोति, वनुते, ववान, ववने,<BR>&c. (Vedic forms वनाति, वनास्, ववन्म, वव्ने,<BR>वंसाम, वंसीमहि, वनुयाम, वनवत् [ =<BR>वनुयात् = हिंस्यात्], वनिषत्, वनुषन्त, वनि-<BR>षन्त, वन्त [as if cl. 2], वंस्व, वावनस्, वा-<BR>वन्धि), Inf. वनितुम् (Ved. [प्र]वन्तवे), to<BR>ask, request, beg, seek; (the following senses are<BR>mostly peculiar to Ved.), to like, love; to wish, de-<BR>sire; to obtain, acquire, procure, furnish, offer, give;<BR>to gain or obtain by conquest, become master of,<BR>conquer, possess; to make ready, prepare for, aim<BR>at; to hurt, injure: Caus. वनयति (when com-<BR>bined with preps.), वानयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>sound, &c.; to act, transact business; to hurt, kill;<BR>(the rt. वन् in cl. 10. 1. वानयति, वनति, &c.<BR>also means ‘to confide,’ ‘believe in,’ but in this sense<BR>is a various reading for rt. 2. तन्, q. v.); [cf. per-<BR>haps Gr. ὀνίνημι, ὀνήσω, ὄνειαρ; Lat. Ven-us, ve-<BR>nustas, veneror; Goth. vens; Old Germ. wini,<BR>winia, wunna; Angl. Sax. wyn, ge-wenian, to-<BR>wenan; (according to some also) Gr. φένω, φόνος,<BR>φονεύς; Lat. funus; Hib. bana, ‘death.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत
2. वत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 881, col. 2), sounded,<BR>spoken, uttered; asked, begged; killed, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वति|वतिः
वति, इस्, f. (perhaps) asking, begging, (see Pāṇ. VI.<BR>4, 37.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्
2. वन् (only used in the loc. and gen. pl. वंसु,<BR>वनाम्), Ved. = 1. वन, a wooden vessel, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. वंसु = उदकेषु); = अरणि, the wood<BR>used for kindling fire by attrition, (according to Sāy.<BR>गर्भो वनाम् = the offspring of the pieces of wood<BR>so used); love, worship (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन|वनं
1. वन, अम्, n. (for 2. वन see p. 885, col. 1), a<BR>wood, forest, grove, thicket, a quantity of lotuses or<BR>other plants growing in a thick bed or cluster (e. g.<BR>कुमुद-व्˚, a bed or cluster of water-lilies); wood,<BR>timber; a wooden vessel or barrel (for the Soma<BR>juice); ‘the vessel in the sky,’ i. e. a cloud (Ved.);<BR>water (Ved.); a fountain, spring; a place of abode,<BR>residence; dwelling in a forest, residence abroad;<BR>(according to Naigh. I. 4) = रश्मि, a ray of light;<BR>(according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 24, 7) light (=<BR>तेजस्); the body of a carriage (so suggested by<BR>modern scholars as an interpretation in Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>34, 18); worshipping; (perhaps) longing, earnest<BR>desire; Cyperus Rotundus; (आ), f. = अरणि, wood<BR>used to produce fire by attrition; (in Ṛg-veda III.<BR>1, 13) Wood for so kindling fire personified; (ई), f.<BR>a wood, forest; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Uśīnara;<BR>of one of the ten orders of mendicants founded by<BR>a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya, the members of which<BR>order affix वन to their names; [cf. रामेन्द्र-<BR>वन.]<BR>—वन-कचु, उस्, m. the plant Arum Colo-<BR>casia.<BR>—वन-कणा, f. wild pepper.<BR>—वन-कण्-<BR>डुल (?) , अस्, m. = वन-शूरण.<BR>—वन-कदली,<BR>f. wild banana or plantain.<BR>—वन-कन्द, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of two kinds of tuberous plants (= वन-शूरण,<BR>धरणी-कन्द).<BR>—वन-कपीवत्, आन्, m., N. of<BR>a son of Pulaha, (also read घन-क्˚, धन-क्˚.)<BR>—वन-करिन्, ई, m. a wild elephant.<BR>—वन-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, loving the forest, fond of wander-<BR>ing in woods.<BR>—वन-कार्पासी, f. the wild cotton<BR>tree, (also written वन-कार्पासि.)<BR>—वन-कुक्कुट,<BR>अस्, m. a wild fowl, jungle fowl.<BR>—वन-कुञ्जर,<BR>अस्, m. a wild elephant.<BR>—वन-कोकिलक, अम्, n.<BR>a kind of metre, four times ˘˘˘˘¯˘¯, ˘˘˘¯˘˘,<BR>¯˘˘¯<BR>—वन-कोलि, इस्, f. the wild jujube.<BR>—वन-<BR>क्रक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) crackling or<BR>bubbling in the Soma vessel; (according to Sāy.)<BR>scattered or distributed in wooden vessels or attract-<BR>ing water (काष्ठेषु पात्रेषु विप्रकीर्ण or<BR>उदकानं कर्षक); distributing water (accord-<BR>ing to others).<BR>—वन-खण्ड, अम्, n. a wood,<BR>forest.<BR>—वन-गज, अस्, m. a wild elephant.<BR>—वन-<BR>गव, अस्, m. the wild ox, Bos Gavæus.<BR>—वन-<BR>गहन, अम्, n. the depth or thick part of a forest;<BR>a thicket.<BR>—वन-गुप्त, अस्, m. a spy, emissary.<BR>—वन-गुल्म, अस्, m. a forest shrub or bush,<BR>wild shrub.<BR>—वन-गो, गौस्, f. the Gāyal, Bos<BR>Gavæus.<BR>—वन-गोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, dwelling in a<BR>forest, frequenting forests; living in water; (अस्), m.<BR>a hunter, forester; (अम्), n. a forest.<BR>—वन-घोली,<BR>f. = अरण्य-घोली.<BR>—वनङ्-करण, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>‘water-making (?),’ epithet of a particular part of<BR>the body, (Sāy. वनम् = उदकं क्रियते विसृज्-<BR>यते येन.)<BR>—वन-चन्दन, अम्, n. aloe wood<BR>or Agallochum; a sort of pine, Pinus Deodora.<BR>—वन-चन्द्रिका, f. a kind of jasmine, Jasminum<BR>Zambac.<BR>—वन-चम्पक, अस्, m. the wild Cam-<BR>paka tree.<BR>—वन-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, roaming in<BR>woods, living in a forest, haunting forests, sylvan;<BR>(अस्), m. an inhabitant of forests, woodman, forester;<BR>a wild animal; the fabulous eight-legged animal<BR>called Śarabha.<BR>—वन-चर्या, f. the roaming about<BR>in a forest, residence in a wood.<BR>—वन-चारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, = वन-चर above.<BR>—वन-च्छाग, अस्, m.<BR>a wild goat; a boar, hog.<BR>—वन-च्छिद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>cutting wood, felling timber; (त्), m. a woodcutter.<BR>—वन-च्छेद, अस्, m. cutting timber.<BR>—वन-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, forest-born, born or produced in a wood,<BR>sylvan, wild; (अस्), m. an elephant, a fragrant grass,<BR>Cyperus Rotundus; N. of certain other plants (=<BR>गुल्म, वन-शूरण, तुम्बुरु); the wild citron<BR>tree; (आ), f. Phaseolus Trilobus; the wild cotton tree;<BR>wild ginger; N. of certain other plants (= वन्यो-<BR>पादकी, अश्व-गन्धा, गन्ध-पत्त्रा, मिश्रेया);<BR>(अम्), n. ‘produced in water,’ a blue lotus-flower.<BR>—वन-जीर, अस्, m. wild cumin.<BR>—वन-जीविन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘living in the wood,’ a woodman, forester.<BR>—वन-तिक्त, अस्, m. a sort of myrobalan, Termi-<BR>nalia Chebula; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= श्वेत-<BR>बुह्ना, ग्रीष्मा).<BR>—वन-तिक्तिका, f. Clypea Her-<BR>nandifolia.<BR>—वन-द, अस्, m. ‘giving or distributing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-c" target="_blank">Page0883-c+ 81</a>]<BR>rain, ‘a cloud.<BR>—वन-दमन, अस्, m. = अरण्य-<BR>दमन.<BR>—वन-दारक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—वन-दाह, अस्, m. a forest conflagration.<BR>—वन-दीप, अस्, m. = वन-चम्पक.<BR>—वन-<BR>दीय-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—वन-<BR>देवता, f. a forest goddess, Dryad.<BR>—वन-द्रुम,<BR>अस्, m. a forest tree, a tree growing in a wood.<BR>—वन-द्विप, अस्, m. a wild elephant.<BR>—वन-<BR>धारा, f. an avenue of trees.<BR>—वन-धिति, इस्, f.,<BR>Ved. (perhaps) a layer of wood to be laid on the<BR>altar; (Sāy.) the instrument to be applied to a forest<BR>to cut down the trees, a hatchet; [cf. स्वधिति,<BR>perhaps for स्व-धिति.]<BR>—वन-धेनु, उस्, f. the<BR>cow or female of the Bos Gavæus.<BR>—वन-नित्य,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR>—वन-प, अस्,<BR>m. a forest protector, woodman.<BR>—वन-पन्नग,<BR>अस्, m. a serpent living in woods.<BR>—वन-पर्वन्,<BR>अ, n. ‘forest-Parva,’ N. of the third book of the<BR>Mahā-bhārata (describing the abode of Yudhiṣṭhira<BR>and his brothers, the Pāṇḍava princes, in the Kām-<BR>yaka forest and adjacent district).<BR>—वन-पल्लव,<BR>अस्, m. Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR>—वन-पांसुल, अस्,<BR>m. a hunter, deer-killer.<BR>—वन-पादप, अस्, m. a<BR>forest tree.<BR>—वन-पार्श्व, अस्, m. the neighbour-<BR>hood of a wood, a wood.<BR>—वन-पाल, अस्, m. a<BR>forest protector, woodman; a proper N.<BR>—वन-<BR>पिप्पली, f. wild pepper.<BR>—वन-पुष्प, अम्, n. a<BR>forest-flower, field-flower; (आ), f. a sort of dill, Ane-<BR>thum Sowa.<BR>—वनपुष्प-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made<BR>or consisting of forest-flowers.<BR>—वन-पूरक, अस्,<BR>m. the wild citron tree.<BR>—वन-पूर्व, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a village.<BR>—वन-प्रक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. liv-<BR>ing in water, (a various reading for वन-क्रक्ष.)<BR>—वन-प्रवेश, अस्, m. the act of entering a wood,<BR>(especially) a festive procession into a forest for the<BR>purpose of cutting wood for an idol; commencing<BR>to live as a hermit.<BR>—वन-प्रस्थ, a wood situated<BR>on an elevation or on table-land; N. of a place;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), retiring into a forest, withdrawing into<BR>the woods, leading the life of an anchorite, (see<BR>वानप्रस्थ.)<BR>—वन-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, loving<BR>the wood, fond of the forest; (अस्), m. the Indian<BR>cuckoo; (अम्), n. the cinnamon tree, a kind of<BR>Cassia.<BR>—वन-फल, अम्, n. wood fruit, wild fruit.<BR>—वन-बर्बर, वन-बर्हिण, &c., see वन-व्˚.<BR>—वन-भद्रिका, f. Sida Cordifolia.<BR>—वन-भुज्,<BR>क्, m. a particular medicinal herb (= ऋषभ).<BR>—वन-भू, ऊस्, f. woody ground, the neighbour-<BR>hood of a wood.<BR>—वन-मक्षिका, f. a gad-fly.<BR>—वन-मल्ली, f. wild jasmine.<BR>—वन-मानुष,<BR>अस्, m. ‘wild-man,’ the orang-outang; the Lemur<BR>Tardigradus.<BR>—वन-माला, f. a garland of wood-<BR>flowers, the chaplet worn by Kṛṣṇa; a kind of<BR>metre, four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯˘¯¯, ˘¯¯˘¯¯˘¯<BR>N. of a work; (अस्, आ, अम्), adorned with a garland<BR>of wood-flowers; (अस्), m. epithet of Kṛṣṇa or<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—वनमाला-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a<BR>chaplet of wood-flowers; (अम्), n. a kind of metre,<BR>four times ˘˘˘˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯¯˘¯.<BR>—व-<BR>न-मालिका, f. = वन-माला; N. of a plant (=<BR>वाराही-कन्द); a particular metre (= वन-मा-<BR>लिनी); N. of one of Rādhā's female attendants; of<BR>a river.<BR>—वन-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, adorned with a<BR>chaplet of wood-flowers; (ई), m. epithet of Kṛṣṇa<BR>or Viṣṇu; N. of a poet; (इनी), f. = वाराही, (pro-<BR>bably a kind of plant, according to others a female<BR>energy of Kṛṣṇa); N. of the town Dvārakā.<BR>—वनमालीशा (fr. वन-मालिन् + ईश), f. ‘having<BR>as a husband one adorned with a chaplet of wood-<BR>flowers, i. e. Kṛṣṇa, ‘epithet of Rādhā.<BR>—वन-<BR>मुच्, क्, क्, क्, pouring forth rain, scattering water;<BR>(क्), m. a cloud.<BR>—वन-मुद्ग, अस्, आ, m. f. a sort<BR>of kidney-bean, Phaseolus Trilobus.<BR>—वन-मूत,<BR>अस्, m. a cloud,<BR>—वन-मूर्ध-जा, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= कर्कट-शृङ्गी).<BR>—वन-मूल, अस्, m.<BR>the shrub Tetranthera Lanceifolia.<BR>—वन-मूल-<BR>फल, अम्, n. roots and fruit of the forest.<BR>—वन-<BR>मृग, अस्, m. a forest deer.<BR>—वन-मोचा, f. wild<BR>plantain.<BR>—वन-रक्षक, अस्, m. the keeper of<BR>a garden or forest.<BR>—वन-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of<BR>the forest, ‘the lion; the plant Verbesina Scandens.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-a" target="_blank">Page0884-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—वन-राजि, इस्, or वन-राजी, f. a row of trees; a<BR>long tract of forest; a path in a forest; (ई), f., N.<BR>of a female slave belonging to Vasu-deva; (इस्, इस् or<BR>ई, इ), embellishing or beautifying a forest.<BR>—वन-<BR>राज्य, अम्, n., N. of a kingdom.<BR>—वन-राष्ट्र<BR>or वन-राष्ट्रक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—वन-रुह, अम्, n. ‘growing in water,’ a lotus-<BR>flower.<BR>—वनर्द्धि (˚न-ऋद्˚), इस्, m. an ornament<BR>of the forest.<BR>—वन-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. an ornament of<BR>the wood; the plantain, Musa Sapientum.<BR>—वन-<BR>लता, f. a creeper growing in the forest.<BR>—वन-<BR>लेखा, f. = वन-राजि.<BR>—वन-वराह, अस्, m. a<BR>wild hog.<BR>—वन-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, residing in the<BR>woods.<BR>—वन-वर्वर, अस्, m. a kind of basil,<BR>Ocimum Sanctum.<BR>—वन-वर्वरिका, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= दोषा-क्लेशी).<BR>—वन-वर्हिण, अस्, m. a<BR>wild peacock.<BR>—वनवर्हिण-त्व, अम्, n. the con-<BR>dition of a wild peacock.<BR>—वन-वल्लरी, f. a kind<BR>of grass.<BR>—वन-वह्नि, इस्, m. a forest fire, wood<BR>on fire, forest conflagration.<BR>—वन-वात, अस्, m. a<BR>forest wind.<BR>—वन-वास, अस्, m. the living in a<BR>wood, residence in a forest; a wild or unsettled<BR>manner of life, wandering habits; N. of a country;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), residing in a forest or wood; (अस्), m.<BR>a wood-dweller, inhabitant of forests.<BR>—वन-वा-<BR>सक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—वन-वासन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘wood-dweller,’ a pole-cat, civet-cat.<BR>—वन-<BR>वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in a wood; (ई), m. a<BR>dweller in woods, inhabitant of a forest, forester,<BR>hermit, anchorite; N. of a country in the south of<BR>India; of various plants (= ऋषभ, मुष्कक,<BR>वाराही-कन्द, शाल्मली-कन्द, नील-महिष-<BR>कन्द).<BR>—वन-वास्य, N. of a country (= वन-<BR>वासिन्).<BR>—वन-वाह्यक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—वन-विडाल, अस्, m. a kind of wild cat, Felis<BR>Caracal.<BR>—वन-विरोधिन्, ई, m. ‘wood-enemy,’ N.<BR>of one of the Hindū months, (that succeeding Ni-<BR>dāgha, q. v.)<BR>—वन-वीज or वन-वीजक or वन-<BR>वीज-पूरक, अस्, m. the wild citron tree.<BR>—वन-<BR>वृन्ताकी, f. the egg-plant.<BR>—वन-व्रीहि, इस्, m.<BR>wild rice.<BR>—वन-शूकरी, f. cowach, Mucuna Pru-<BR>ritus.<BR>—वन-शूरण, अस्, m. a kind of plant (=<BR>अरण्य-शूरण).<BR>—वन-शृङ्गाट or वन-शृङ्-<BR>गाटक, अस्, m. the plant Asteracantha Longifolia.<BR>—वन-शोभन, अम्, n. ‘water-beautifier,’ a lotus-<BR>flower.<BR>—वन-श्वन्, आ, m. ‘forest-dog,’ a jackal;<BR>a tiger; a civet-cat, pole-cat.<BR>—वन-षद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>= वन-सद् below.<BR>—वन-सङ्कट, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of pulse, Ervum Hirsutum.<BR>—वन-सद्, त्, त्, त्, abid-<BR>ing or dwelling in a wood; (त्), m. a forester.<BR>—व-<BR>न-सन्निवासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in a forest; (ई),<BR>m. a forester.<BR>—वन-समूह, अस्, m. a thick<BR>forest, a quantity of groves or forests, a thick wood.<BR>—वन-सम्प्रवेश, अस्, m. the entering into a<BR>wood, (especially) a festive procession into a forest<BR>for the purpose of cutting wood for an idol.<BR>—वन-<BR>सरोजिनी, f. the wild cotton plant.<BR>—वन-साह्वया,<BR>f. a kind of creeping plant (= वन्योपादकी).<BR>—व-<BR>न-स्तम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a son of Gada.<BR>—वन-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, forest-abiding, living in the wood;<BR>(अस्), m. a deer, gazelle; a hermit, ascetic; (आ), f.<BR>the holy fig-tree (= अश्वथी).<BR>—वन-स्थली, f. the<BR>neighbourhood of a forest, a wood.<BR>—वन-स्थान (?),<BR>N. of a kingdom.<BR>—वन-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being<BR>or abiding in a wood; (ई), m. a hermit, anchorite.<BR>—वन-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, situate or being in a<BR>forest.<BR>—वनस्-पति, इस्, m. (वनस् probably a form<BR>of the gen., cf. रथस्-पति), ‘the king of the wood,’<BR>a large forest tree, a large tree bearing fruit, but<BR>apparently having no blossoms (as several species of<BR>the fig, the jack-tree, &c.); any tree; the god of<BR>large trees, (in Ṛg-veda VIII. 23, 25. Agni is<BR>described as ‘the son of the Vanaspatis’); the Soma<BR>plant (regarded as the king of plants); Bignonia<BR>Suaveolens; a stem, trunk; a beam, timber, pole,<BR>post; the sacrificial posts (enumerated among the<BR>Āprī divinities); an offering to Vanas-pati; the<BR>timber of which a car or carriage is made (Ved.);<BR>a drum made of wood (Ved.); a wooden amulet; a<BR>block on which criminals are executed; an ascetic;<BR>N. of a son of Ghṛta-pṛṣṭha.<BR>—वनस्पति-काय,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-b" target="_blank">Page0884-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. the whole body or world of plants.<BR>—वनस्-<BR>पति-सव, अस्, m., N. of an Ekāha.<BR>—वन-स्रज्, क् or<BR>ग्, f. a garland of forest-flowers.<BR>—वन-हरि, इस्, m.<BR>a lion (?).<BR>—वन-हरिद्रा, f. wild turmeric.<BR>—व-<BR>न-हास, अस्, m. a sort of grass, Saccharum Spon-<BR>taneum; a fragrant oleander.<BR>—वन-हासक, अस्,<BR>m. Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—वन-हुताशन (˚त-<BR>अश्˚), अस्, m. a forest conflagration.<BR>—वनाकम्प<BR>(˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m. the shaking of the trees of a wood<BR>by the wind.<BR>—वनाखु (˚न-आखु), उस्, m. ‘wood-<BR>rat, ‘a hare.<BR>—वनाखुक, अस्, m. a sort of bean,<BR>Phaseolus Mungo.<BR>—वनाग्नि (˚न-अग्˚), इस्, m. a<BR>forest conflagration, burning of a wood.<BR>—वनाज<BR>(˚न-अज), अस्, m. the wild goat.<BR>—वनाटन (˚न-<BR>अट्˚), अम्, n. the act of roaming or wandering about<BR>in a forest.<BR>—वनाटु (˚न-आटु?), उस्, m. ‘wood-<BR>roamer,’ a kind of blue fly.<BR>—वनाधिवासिन् (˚न-<BR>अध्˚), ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in a forest.<BR>—वनान्त<BR>(˚न-अन्˚), अस्, m. the skirts of a wood, neighbour-<BR>hood of a forest; (अस्, आ, अम्), having a wood for a<BR>boundary, bounded by a wood.<BR>—वनान्तर (˚न-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. the middle or interior of a wood, (व-<BR>नान्तरात्, out of the wood); another wood.<BR>—व-<BR>नान्तर-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, wandering about in a<BR>forest.<BR>—वनापग (˚न-अप्˚), a forest stream,<BR>river.<BR>—वनाब्जिनी (˚न-अब्˚), f. a lotus-plant grow-<BR>ing in the water.<BR>—वनाभिलाव (˚न-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, wood-destroying.<BR>—वनामल (˚न-आम्˚), अस्,<BR>m. (आमल for आमलक), Carissa Carandas; [cf.<BR>कृष्ण-पाक.]<BR>—वनाम्बिका (˚न-अम्˚), f., N. of<BR>a tutelary divinity in the family of Dakṣa.<BR>—व-<BR>नाम्र (˚न-आम्˚), अस्, m., N. of a plant (= को-<BR>शाम्र).<BR>—वनारिष्टा (˚न-अर्˚), f. wild turmeric<BR>(= वन-हरिद्रा).<BR>—वनार्चक (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘wood-worshipper,’ a flower-gatherer, florist, maker of<BR>garlands.<BR>—वनार्द्रका (˚न-आर्˚), f. wild ginger;<BR>(अम्), n. the root of wild ginger.<BR>—वनालक्त (˚न-<BR>अल्˚), अम्, n. ‘wild lac,’ red earth, ruddle.<BR>—वना-<BR>लय (˚न-आल्˚), अस्, m. a forest-abode, forest-habita-<BR>tion.<BR>—वनालय-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, living in forests.<BR>—वनालिका (˚न-अल्˚), f. a sun-flower, Heliotropium<BR>Indicum.<BR>—वनाली (˚न-आली), f. = वन-राजी.<BR>—व-<BR>नाश्रम (˚न-आश्˚), अस्, m. abode in the forest, the<BR>third Āśrama or stage in a Brāhman's life (when he<BR>is a Vānaprastha or hermit, see आश्रम).<BR>—वना-<BR>श्रमिन्, ई, m. (fr. the preceding), a Vānaprastha or<BR>Brāhman dwelling in the woods, one in the third<BR>period of life, an anchorite.<BR>—वनाश्रय (˚न-आश्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, living in the forest; (अस्), m. an inha-<BR>bitant of the wood; a sort of crow or raven.<BR>—वना-<BR>श्रित (˚न-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has sought<BR>refuge in the woods, repaired to the forest, leading<BR>the life of a hermit.<BR>—वने-किंशुक, आस्, m. pl.<BR>‘Butea Frondosa in the wood,’ anything found unex-<BR>pectedly.<BR>—वने-क्षुद्रा, f. the tree Pongamia<BR>Glabra (commonly called Karañja).<BR>—वने-चर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, wandering in a forest, dwelling in or<BR>inhabiting a wood; (अस्), m. an inhabitant of the<BR>forest, forester, anchorite, hermit; a sylvan, satyr; an<BR>imp, demon; a wild beast.<BR>—वनेचराग्र्य (˚र-<BR>अग्˚), अस्, m. ‘chief of foresters,’ an ascetic, anchorite,<BR>sage.<BR>—वने-जा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. born or generated<BR>in the woods.<BR>—वने-बिल्वक, आस्, m. pl. an Ægle<BR>Marmelos in the forest; (metaphorically) anything<BR>found unexpectedly.<BR>—वने-राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. shining<BR>or blazing in the wood; (ट्), m. epithet of Agni.<BR>—वने-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, living in the woods.<BR>—वने-षह् (i. e. वने + सह्), षाट्, ट्, ट्, Ved.<BR>overpowering or prevailing in the wood or over the<BR>wood, (Sāy. = काष्ठानाम् अभिभवितृ.)<BR>—वने-<BR>सर्ज, अस्, m. Terminalia Tomentosa.<BR>—वनैक-<BR>देश (˚न-एक्˚), अस्, m. a part of a wood or thicket.<BR>—वनोत्साह (˚न-उत्˚), अस्, m. a rhinoceros.<BR>—व-<BR>नोद्देश (˚न-उद्˚), अस्, m. the neighbourhood of a<BR>forest, a particular spot in a wood.<BR>—वनोद्भव<BR>(˚न-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced in a forest, being in<BR>a wood; (आ), f. the wild cotton plant.<BR>—वनोप-<BR>प्लव (˚न-उप्˚), अम्, n. a forest conflagration.<BR>—वनोर्वी (˚न-उर्˚), f. the neighbourhood of a<BR>forest.<BR>—वनौक (˚न-ओक), अस्, m. = वनौकस्,<BR>an inhabitant of a wood.<BR>—वनौकस् (˚न-ओक्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">Page0884-c+ 81</a>]<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, living in a forest; (आस्), m. an inha-<BR>bitant of a wood, a forester; an anchorite, ascetic,<BR>hermit; an animal living in woods, an ape, wild<BR>boar, &c.<BR>—वनौघ (˚न-ओघ), अस्, m. ‘thick<BR>forest, ‘N. of a district or mountain in the west of<BR>India.<BR>—वनौषधि (˚न-ओष्˚), इस्, f. a medicinal<BR>herb growing wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनद्
वनद्, m. (only in pl. वनदस्), a praiser,<BR>honourer, one who joins in praising; sounding forth<BR>loudly, praising greatly, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda II. 4, 5. वनदः = वनन्तः = सम्भक्तारः<BR>or may be for अव-नदः = भृशं शब्दयन्तः<BR>= स्तोतारः; according to Durga वनदः is for<BR>वन-दाः, ‘givers of the desirable oblation;’ accord-<BR>ing to modern scholars वनद् may perhaps mean<BR>‘longing, earnest desire.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनन|वननं
वनन, अम्, n., Ved. longing, desire, (Sāy.)<BR>wealth, = धन; (आ), f. (perhaps) wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वननीय
वननीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be desired, desir-<BR>able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनन्व
वनन्व, Nom. P. वनन्वति, &c., Ved. to be<BR>in possession, be at hand, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>102, 19. वनन्वति = काष्ठानि हन्ति, [the axe]<BR>fells timber.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनन्वत्|वनन्वन्त्
वनन्वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. (according to Sāy. =<BR>वनन-वत् = धन-वत् = उदक-वत् = सम्-<BR>भक्त-वत्), possessing wealth, &c., bountiful; (ac-<BR>cording to modern scholars) possessing, being in<BR>possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनयितृ
वनयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who causes to ask, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्
वनस्, अस्, n., Ved. (perhaps) desire, longing;<BR>attractiveness, loveliness, (Sāy. = तेजस्, glory, or<BR>धन, wealth); a wood; [cf. Lat. venus in venus-<BR>tas.]<BR>—वनर्-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, moving about in a wood;<BR>wandering in a forest or wilderness, (Sāy. = वन-<BR>गामिन्); (उस्), m. = स्तेन (according to Naigh. III.<BR>24).<BR>—वनर्-ज, अस्, m. a particular plant (=<BR>शृङ्गी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस
वनस, see Gaṇa Tṛṇādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्पति|वनस्पतिः
वनस्-पति. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्यु
वनस्यु in गिर्-व्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायु|वनायुः
वनायु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Purū-ravas; of a<BR>Dānava; of a district inhabited by the Vanāyus;<BR>(अवस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—वनायु-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced or bred in Vanāyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनि|वनिः
वनि, इस्, m., Ved. fire, Agni, the god of fire;<BR>(इस्), f. wish, desire; (इस्, इस्, इ), used at the end of<BR>comps., see ब्रह्म-व्˚, क्षत्र-व्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिका
वनिका, f. a little wood, grove, (in अशोक-व्˚, a grove<BR>of Aśoka trees; also अशोक-वनिक, अम्, n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिकावास
वनिकावास, अस्, m., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनित|वनितः
वनित, अस्, आ, अम्, solicited, begged, asked,<BR>wished for, desired, loved; served; (आ), f. a loved<BR>woman, wife, mistress; a woman in general; the<BR>female of an animal; a particular metre, four times<BR>˘˘¯˘˘¯; [cf. Old Germ. winia, ‘a wife;’ Hib.<BR>ban, ‘a woman.’]<BR>—वनिता-द्विष्, ट्, m. hating<BR>women, a misogynist.<BR>—वनिता-भोगिन्, ई, m. a<BR>woman like a serpent, serpent of a woman.<BR>—व-<BR>निता-मुख, आस्, m. pl. ‘woman-faced,’ N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—वनिता-विलास, अस्, m. the wantonness of<BR>women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनितास
वनितास, अम्, n., N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनितृ
वनितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, an asker, &c.; one who<BR>possesses or owns, a possessor (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिन्
वनिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. the rt. and in some meanings<BR>fr. 1. वन), Ved. worshipping, honouring, serving;<BR>desiring, wishing for; distributing, bestowing, giving<BR>(said of the Maruts &c.); rain-dispensing; having<BR>water, granting water, abounding in water; belong-<BR>ing to a wood, living in a wood; filled with or<BR>possessed of wood; (ई), m. a tree; the Soma plant;<BR>a Brāhman residing in the forest, one in the third<BR>stage of life, a Vānaprastha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिन
वनिन, अम्, n., Ved. anything growing in a<BR>forest, a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिल
वनिल, see Gaṇa Kāśādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्ठ
वनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. obtaining most;<BR>bestowing or imparting most, very munificent or<BR>liberal, (Sāy. = दातृतम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्ठु|वनिष्ठुः
वनिष्ठु, उस्, m., Ved. part of the entrails of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">Page0885-a+ 75</a>]<BR>an animal offered in sacrifice; the rectum; (according<BR>to others) a part of the intestines near the omentum,<BR>(Sāy. = स्थविरान्त्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0884-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्णु
वनिष्णु, incorrect for वनिष्ठु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनी
वनी, f. See under 1. वन, p. 883, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीक|वनीकः
वनीक or वनीपक or वनीयक, अस्, m. a<BR>beggar, mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीय
वनीय, Nom. P. वनीयति, &c., to beg, ask<BR>alms; to entreat, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीयस्
वनीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, asking or obtaining more,<BR>obtaining most; to be honoured, to be favoured,<BR>(Sāy. = सम्भजनीय = सम्भाव्य); imparting<BR>or bestowing most.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीवन्
वनीवन्, आ, आ, अ (an Intensive form), asking for,<BR>demanding, (Sāy. = वनन-वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनु|वनुः
वनु, उस्, m., Ved. one who plots against or<BR>injures, a malignant or malicious person, (Sāy. =<BR>हिंसक); an adherent (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनुष
वनुष (fr. वनुस्), Nom. A. वनुषते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to obtain, acquire; (Sāy.) to worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनुष्य
वनुष्य (fr. वनुस्), Nom. P. A. वनुष्यति,<BR>-ते, &c., Ved. to have a design upon, plot against,<BR>seek to injure, to be fond of battle; to emulate<BR>(with inst.); to overpower, defeat, attack, (according<BR>to Naigh. II. 12 = क्रुध्यति; according to Nirukta<BR>V. 2 = हन्ति); (A.) to wish for, desire, (Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda IX. 7, 6. वनुष्यते = सेव्यते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनुष्यत्
वनुष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, seeking to injure, ma-<BR>levolent, hostile, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनुस्
वनुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. desiring, anxious for, eager,<BR>zealous; devoted, attached to, loving; enjoying, an<BR>enjoyer, worshipping, a worshipper, honourer, (Sāy.<BR>= सम्भक्तृ); (उस्), m. any one eager to injure<BR>(others), an enemy, plotter, warrior; the act of possess-<BR>ing, enjoying, distributing, (Sāy. = सम्भजन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेज्य|वनेज्यः
वनेज्य, अस्, m. a kind of mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेयु
वनेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्ति
वन्ति, इस्, f., see Pāṇ. VI. 4, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्तृ
वन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who enjoys or possesses,<BR>a possessor, owner, (Sāy. = सम्भक्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्य|वन्यं|वन्यः
वन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, growing in woods, of or be-<BR>longing to a wood, forest, produced in a wood, living<BR>in woods, wild, savage; being or existing in a wood<BR>(said of Agni, Ved.); made of wood, wooden; (अस्),<BR>m. an animal of the forest, wild animal, wild beast;<BR>a wild plant; N. of particular wild plants (= वन-<BR>शूरण, वाराही-कन्द, देव-नाल); (आ), f. a<BR>multitude of groves, a large forest; abundance of<BR>water, a flood, deluge; N. of various plants, Physalis<BR>Flexuosa; = मद्गु-पर्णी, गोपाल-कर्कटी, गुञ्जा,<BR>मिश्रेया, भद्र-मुस्ता, गन्ध-पत्त्रा; (अम्),<BR>n. anything grown in a wood, the fruit or roots of<BR>wild plants; = त्वच; [cf. other meanings of the<BR>word वन्य in चक्षुर्-व्˚, अजीत-पुनर्वण्य.]<BR>—वन्य-द्विप, अस्, m. a wild elephant.<BR>—वन्य-<BR>पक्षिन्, ई, m. a wild bird, forest bird; [cf. पुर-<BR>पक्षिन्.]<BR>—वन्य-वृत्ति, इस्, f. forest fare.<BR>—व-<BR>न्याशन (˚य-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, eating wild fruits, &c.<BR>—वन्येतर (˚य-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अत्, different from<BR>wild tame, civilized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्योपादकी
वन्योपादकी, f. a kind of creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ववन्वस्
ववन्वस्, वान्, उषी, वत्, Ved. one who has<BR>desired or asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन|वनं
वन 2. वन, ind. (for 1. वन see p. 883,<BR>col. 2), see Gaṇa Cādi to Pāṇ. I. 4, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनर|वनरः
वनर वनर, अस्, m. = वानर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनर्गु
वनर्गु वनर्-गु. See under वनस्, p. 884.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनहबन्दि
वनहबन्दि वनहबन्दि, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाहिर|वनाहिरः
वनाहिर वनाहिर, अस्, m. a hog, wild boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीवाहन
वनीवाहन वनीवाहन, अम्, n. (an anoma-<BR>lous Intens. fr. rt. 1. वह्), Ved. the act of carrying<BR>or moving hither and thither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनौकस्
वनौकस् वनौकस्, वनौषधि. See<BR>p. 884, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्तव
वन्तव वन्तव (?) , अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्|वंद्
वन्द् वन्द् (connected with rt. वद्), cl.<BR>1. A. (Ved. and ep. sometimes P.) वन्-<BR>दते, ववन्दे (Ved. ववन्द, ववन्दिम), अवन्-<BR>दिष्ट, वन्दितुम् (Ved. Inf. वन्दध्यै), to<BR>praise, celebrate, laud, extol, eulogize, bless, pro-<BR>nounce a blessing; to show honour, do homage,<BR>salute respectfully, greet, make obeisance to; to<BR>venerate, worship, adore: Pass. वन्द्यते, Aor.<BR>अवन्दि, to be praised, &c.: Caus. वन्दयति, -यते,<BR>-यितुम्, Aor. अववन्दत्, अववन्दत, to show<BR>honour to any one, make obeisance to, greet respect-<BR>fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द|वन्दः
वन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, praising, extolling; [cf. देव-<BR>वन्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दक|वंदकः|वन्दकः
वन्दक, अस्, आ, m. f. a praiser, &c.; a parasitical<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दथ|वंदथ|वंदथः|वन्दथः
वन्दथ, अस्, m. a praiser, panegyrist, eulogist,<BR>bard; one deserving praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दद्वार
वन्दद्-वार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. blessing the mul-<BR>titude, i. e. men, (in Sāma-veda I. 1, 2, 3, 6. for<BR>वन्दे दारुम्, which is the correct reading in the<BR>corresponding passage of the Ṛg-veda.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दद्वीर
वन्दद्-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. blessing heroes,<BR>(in Sāma-veda I. 4, 2, 3, 1. for मन्दद्-वीर,<BR>which is the correct reading in the corresponding<BR>passage of the Ṛg-veda.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दन|वंदन|वंदनं|वन्दनं
वन्दन, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi (described in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 112, 5. as having been cast into a well,<BR>along with Rebha, by the Asuras, and rescued by the<BR>Aśvins); (आ), f. praise, praising, worship, adoration;<BR>a mark or sign worn on the body (made with ashes<BR>&c.); (ई), f. making obeisance, reverence, worship,<BR>adoring; begging, soliciting, asking; the hip (?) ; a<BR>drug for reviving the dead; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>praising, praise; obeisance to a Brāhman or superior<BR>(by touching the feet &c.), reverence, adoration;<BR>the face, mouth (= वदन); a parasitical plant<BR>(perhaps a kind of lichen); a disease attacking the<BR>limbs or joints, a cutaneous eruption, scrofula (some-<BR>times personified as a demon).<BR>—वन्दन-माला or<BR>वन्दन-मालिका, f. a festoon suspended across gate-<BR>ways (in honour of the arrival of any distinguished<BR>personage, or on the occasion of a marriage or other<BR>festival).<BR>—वन्दन-श्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. listening to<BR>praise, a hearer of praises, (Sāy. = स्तुतीनां श्रोतृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनीय|वंदनीय|वन्दनीयः
वन्दनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised or wor-<BR>shipped, praiseworthy, adorable, to be greeted with<BR>homage, to be saluted or made obeisance to; (अस्),<BR>m. a yellow-flowering Verbesina; (आ), f. the yellow<BR>pigment called गो-रोचना, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दमान
वन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, praising, celebrating, pro-<BR>nouncing a blessing, honouring, reverencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दयित्वा
वन्दयित्वा, ind. (fr. the Caus.), having praised,<BR>having saluted or shown honour to, having made<BR>obeisance to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दा|वंदा
वन्दा, f. a parasitical plant, the parasitical plant<BR>Epidendrum Tesselatum, &c.; a female beggar or<BR>mendicant; = वन्दि, वन्दी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दाक|वन्दाकः
वन्दाक, अस्, m., आ, ई, f. a parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दार|वन्दारः
वन्दार, अस्, m. a parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दारु|वंदारु|वन्दारुः
वन्दारु, उस्, उस्, उ, praising, celebrating; respect-<BR>ful, reverential, civil, complimentary, polite; (उस्), m.<BR>a panegyrist, bard; a proper N.; (उ), n. praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दि|वन्दिः
1. वन्दि, इस्, m. (for 2. वन्दि see col. 3), a praiser,<BR>panegyrist, &c. (= वन्दिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दित
वन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, praised, extolled, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दितव्य
वन्दितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised or cele-<BR>brated, laudable, to be treated with awe or respect,<BR>one to whom obeisance is to be made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दितृ
वन्दितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who praises or<BR>celebrates, a praiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिन्|वंदिन्
वन्दिन्, ई, m. one who praises or extols, a praiser,<BR>panegyrist, encomiast, bard, poet, herald (whose duty<BR>is to proclaim the titles of a great man as he passes<BR>along, or who sings the praises of a prince in<BR>his presence or accompanies an army to chaunt<BR>martial songs; these bards are regarded as belonging<BR>to a distinct tribe, being considered the descendants<BR>of a Kṣatriya by a Śūdra female); a captive, slave,<BR>(in this sense more properly written बन्दिन्, cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">Page0885-c+ 75</a>]<BR>2. वन्दि.)<BR>—वन्दि-पाठ, अस्, m. the panegyric<BR>of a bard or Vandin, eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिनीका
वन्दिनीका or वन्दिनीया, f., N. of Dākṣāyaṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्य|वंद्य
वन्द्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, laudable, com-<BR>mendable, praiseworthy; to be reverentially saluted,<BR>to be honoured or worshipped, adorable, very vene-<BR>rable; to be regarded or respected; (अस्), m. a<BR>proper N.; (आ), f. = वन्दा, a parasitical plant; =<BR>गो-रोचना; N. of a Yakṣī.<BR>—वन्द्य-ता, f. lauda-<BR>bility, praiseworthiness, venerableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्यमान
वन्द्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being praised or cele-<BR>brated, being saluted or greeted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्र|वंद्र|वन्द्रं|वंद्रः|वन्द्रः
वन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, praising, worshipping, honour-<BR>ing, doing homage; (अस्), m. a worshipper, votary,<BR>follower; (अम्), n. prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दि|वन्दिः
वन्दि 2. वन्दि, इस्, or वन्दी, f. (more pro-<BR>perly written बन्दि, बन्दी; probably connected<BR>with rt. बन्ध्, cf. the Persian بنده for 1. वन्दि<BR>see col. 2), a captive or prisoner in general<BR>(male or female); a woman in captivity, female<BR>captive or slave; an animal confined in a cage; a<BR>ladder or stairs; plunder, booty, spoil.<BR>—वन्दि-<BR>ग्राह, अस्, m. ‘plunder-seizer,’ a housebreaker<BR>(especially one breaking into a temple or place where<BR>sacred fire is preserved).<BR>—वन्दि-चौर, अस्, m. =<BR>वन्दि-ग्राह above.<BR>—वन्दी-कार, अस्, m. one who<BR>commits robbery, a robber, thief, housebreaker, bur-<BR>glar.<BR>—वन्दी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to make captive, take prisoner, capture,<BR>rob.<BR>—वन्दी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made prisoner, taken<BR>captive.<BR>—वन्दी-पाल, अस्, m. a keeper of prisoners,<BR>a jailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दीक
वन्दीक वन्दीक, अस्, m. (also written बन्-<BR>दीक), N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धा
वन्धा वन्धा, ind., see Gaṇa Ūry-ādi to<BR>Pāṇ. I. 4, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धुर्
वन्धुर् वन्धुर्. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धुर|वंधुर
वन्धुर वन्धुर, अम्, n. (probably con-<BR>nected with rt. बन्ध् and perhaps more properly<BR>written बन्धुर), the seat of a charioteer, the<BR>fore part of a chariot or place at the end of the<BR>shafts, a carriage-seat or driver's box; the frame-<BR>work [cf. हिरण्य-व्˚] of a carriage, (the word वन्-<BR>धुरम् occurs frequently in Ved. and is variously<BR>explained by Sāy. as नीड-बन्धनाधार-भूतम्,<BR>उन्नतानत-रूप-बन्धन-काष्ठम्, वेष्टि-<BR>तं सारथेः स्थानम्, सारथ्य्-आश्रय-स्थानम्,<BR>&c.; the car of the Aśvins, which is described as<BR>‘three-wheeled’ as well as triple in other parts of<BR>its construction, is said to be also त्रि-वन्धुर or<BR>त्रि-बन्धुर, i. e. ‘having three poles or pieces<BR>of wood for securing the occupant’ or ‘having a<BR>triple standing-place or seat for the charioteer.’)<BR>—वन्धुरे-ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम् (i. e. वन्धुरे,<BR>loc. c. + स्था), Ved. standing or sitting on the<BR>chariot-seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धुर्
वन्धुर्, m., Ved. = वन्धुर above; (in Atharva-<BR>veda III. 9, 3. the sense is doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धुरायु
वन्धुरायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having a standing-<BR>place in front or a seat for driving (said of the car<BR>of the Aśvins).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धुल
वन्धुल वन्धुल, अस्, m. (also written बन्-<BR>धुल, q. v.), N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्ना
वन्ना वन्ना, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्र|वन्रः
वन्र वन्र, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 28. fr. rt. 1. वन्), a co-partner, co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्
वप् वप्, cl. 1. P. A. वपति, वपते,<BR>उवाप (1st sing. उवप or उवाप, 2nd<BR>sing. उवपिथ), ऊपे (according to some also [आ]वेपे),<BR>वप्स्यति, -ते (ep. वपिष्यति), अवाप्सीत्, अवप्त,<BR>वप्तुम्, to shear, cut, shave (the hair, beard, &c.,<BR>Ved.); to shear off, crop off, eat off, graze, mow<BR>(grass &c., in Ṛg-veda VI. 6, 4. वपन्ति = मुण्-<BR>डयन्ति); to shave one's self, be shaven or shorn<BR>(Ved. A.); to strew, scatter (especially seed), sow<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">Page0886-a+ 81</a>]<BR>seed, sow, plant; to throw, cast (dice &c.); to pro-<BR>create, beget; to weave, (in this sense probably a<BR>kind of Caus. of rt. वे): Pass. उप्यते (Part. उप्त,<BR>q. v.; the forms उपित and वपित are also given),<BR>to be scattered or sown: Caus. वापयति, -यते,<BR>-यितुम्, Aor. अवीवपत्, to cause to shear or shave<BR>(Ved.); to cause to be shorn (Ved. A.); to sow,<BR>put in the ground, plant: Desid. विवप्सति, -ते:<BR>Intens. वावप्यते, वावप्ति; [cf. Gr. ὀπυίω, οἴφω,<BR>οἰφέω, (perhaps also) ὅπλοω, ὑφαίνω; Angl. Sax.<BR>wif, wœpen; Goth. vepn.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0885-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप|वपः
वप, अस्, m. shaving, shearing; one who sows, a<BR>sower; sowing seed; weaving; (आ), f. the skin or<BR>covering of the intestines, omentum; the mucous or<BR>glutinous secretion of the bones or flesh, marrow, fat<BR>(= मेदस्, q. v.); a mound or heap thrown up by<BR>ants; a cavity, hollow, hole.<BR>—वपा-कृत्, त्, m.<BR>marrow.<BR>—वपा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with<BR>omentum, enveloped in omentum, covered with fat,<BR>&c.<BR>—वपोदर (˚पा-उद्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. fat-<BR>bellied, corpulent (said of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपन|वपनं
वपन, अम्, n. the act of shearing, shaving; the<BR>act of sowing seed, sowing; semen virile; (ई), f. a<BR>barber's shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपनीय
वपनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be shorn [cf. केश-व्˚];<BR>to be sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपा
वपा. See under वप above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपिल|वपिलः
वपिल, अस्, m. a procreator, father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपु|वपुः
वपु, उस्, m. a body; (उस्), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुन|वपुनः
वपुन, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. वप्), a deity;<BR>(अम्), n. knowledge, (probably for वयुन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुर्धर
वपुर्-धर. See under वपुस् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष
वपुष, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. = वपुस्, having form<BR>or beautiful form, handsome, (according to modern<BR>Vedic scholars also) wonderful; (अम्), n. beauty or<BR>elegance of form, wonderful figure, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>III. 2, 15. वपुषाय = रूपार्थम्, for beauty of<BR>form, on account of beauty of form); body, form,<BR>(at the end of a comp., cf. वराह-व्˚); (आ), f. a<BR>particular article of commerce (= हवुषा?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्य
1. वपुष्य, Nom. P. वपुष्यति, &c., Ved. to<BR>cause beauty or lustre of form, (Sāy. वपुर्-दीप्तिं<BR>कृ); to desire form or beauty of form, (Sāy. =<BR>वपुर् इष्); to wonder, be astonished, (this latter<BR>sense is thought probable by modern scholars.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्य
2. वपुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having form or<BR>beauty of form, handsome; conducive to bodily<BR>welfare, (Sāy. = वपुषि हित); wonderfully beauti-<BR>ful, wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुस्
वपुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, having form or beautiful form<BR>(Ved.), embodied, handsome, (according to modern<BR>Vedic scholars also) wonderful; (उस्), n. form, figure,<BR>shape, body, person, appearance; essence, nature,<BR>character; a beautiful form or figure; beautiful ap-<BR>pearance, beauty, (वपुषे, dat. c. for beauty of<BR>form, in order to be beautiful); beautiful or won-<BR>derful appearance of any kind, (according to modern<BR>Vedic scholars) marvellous phenomenon, wonder;<BR>water (according to Naigh. I. 12); N. of a daughter<BR>of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma.<BR>—वपुः-प्रकर्-<BR>ष, अस्, m. excellence of form, personal beauty.<BR>—वपुः-स्रव, अस्, m. a humor of the body.<BR>—वपुर्-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, having form, em-<BR>bodied, having beautiful form, beautiful, handsome.<BR>—वपुष्-टम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most beautiful<BR>or excellent in form, most beautiful or handsome;<BR>most wonderful; (आ), f. Hibiscus Mutabilis; N.<BR>of the wife of Janam-ejaya.<BR>—वपुष्-टर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. more or most beautiful in form,<BR>more handsome, more or most wonderful.<BR>—व-<BR>पुष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a body, corpo-<BR>real, corporate, embodied; having a beautiful form,<BR>beautiful, handsome; containing the word वपुस्;<BR>(आन्), m., N. of a deity enumerated among the<BR>Viśve Devāḥ; of a son of Priya-vrata; of a king<BR>of Kuṇḍina; (अती), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending upon Skanda.<BR>—वपुष्-मत, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king of Kuṇḍina, (for वपुष्-मत्.)<BR>—वपुस्-सात्, ind. into the state of a body, to a<BR>form or body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तव्य
वप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sown; to be immitted<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">Page0886-b+ 78</a>]<BR>seminally; to be impregnated or begotten; to be<BR>implanted, to be given or conferred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तृ
वप्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who shears, a shearer,<BR>cutter, shaver; one who sows or plants, a planter,<BR>sower, husbandman; (ता), m. one who fertilizes or<BR>fecundates, a procreator, progenitor, father; a poet,<BR>sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्यनील
वप्य-नील, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्र|वप्रं|वप्रः
वप्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. a rampart, earth-work,<BR>mud-wall, mound, hillock, earth taken from the<BR>ditch of a town and raised as a wall or buttress;<BR>the foundation of a building; the gate of a fortified<BR>city; the bank of a river, shore or bank in general,<BR>(अनु-वप्रम्, along the bank or shore, Kirāt. VI.<BR>4); the slope or declivity of a hill, table-land on a<BR>mountain; a ditch; the circumference of a sphere or<BR>globe; a sown field, field in general; dust, earth;<BR>the butting of an elephant or bull, (see वप्र-<BR>क्रीडा); = निष्-कुट, वन-ज, वाजिका (?), पाटीर;<BR>(अम्), n. lead [cf. वर्ध्र]; (अस्), m. a father<BR>[cf. वप्तृ]; = प्रजा-पति; N. of a Vyāsa in the<BR>fourteenth division of the Dvāpara age; of a son of<BR>the fourteenth Manu; (आ), f. Bengal madder (=<BR>मञ्जिष्ठा); N. of the mother of Nimi (the<BR>twenty-first Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī); (ई),<BR>f. a hillock, ant-hill.<BR>—वप्र-क्रिया, f. = वप्र-<BR>क्रीडा below.<BR>—वप्र-क्रीडा, f. the playful butting<BR>(of an elephant or bull) against a bank or mound of<BR>any kind, (this is called तटाघात in Kumāra-s. II.<BR>50.)<BR>—वप्रानत (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bowed or<BR>stooping to butt at a bank or wall.<BR>—वप्रान्तर्<BR>(˚र-अन्˚), ind. in or between banks or mounds.<BR>—वप्राभिघात (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m. butting at a<BR>bank or mound.<BR>—वप्राम्भः-स्रुति, इस्, f. the<BR>stream of water flowing along a bank or issuing<BR>from a bank, a rivulet.<BR>—वप्राम्भस् (˚र-अम्˚),<BR>अस्, n. the water flowing along a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रक|वप्रकः
वप्रक, अस्, m. the circumference of a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रि|वप्रिः
वप्रि = क्षेत्र, a field; = दुर्-गति, समुद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्सस्
वप्सस्, Ved. form, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 181, 8 = वपुस् or रूप.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपाटिका
वपाटिका व-पाटिका, f. = अव-पाटिका, lacera-<BR>tion of the prepuce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्प
वप्प वप्प or वप्पक, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्पटदेवी
वप्पट-देवी, f., N. of a princess, (also read<BR>वप्यट-देवी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्पीय
वप्पीय or वप्पीयक, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्पीह
वप्पीह वप्पीह, अस्, m. Cuculus Melano-<BR>leucus (= चातक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वभ्र्
वभ्र् वभ्र् (perhaps more properly writ-<BR>ten बभ्र्, which may be a reduplicated<BR>form of rt. भ्रम्), cl. 1. P. वभ्रति, ववभ्र,<BR>अवभ्रीत्, वभ्रितुम्, to go, go astray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्
वम् वम्, cl. 1. P. वमति (Ved. also<BR>वमिति), ववाम (2nd sing. ववमिथ,<BR>3rd pl. ववमुस् by Pāṇ. VI. 4, 126; according to<BR>some वेमिथ, वेमुस्), वमिष्यति, अवमीत् (Pāṇ.<BR>VII. 2, 5), वमितुम्, to vomit, eject from the<BR>mouth, spit out; to eject, emit, send forth, give<BR>forth, give out, give off, divulge; to reject: Pass.<BR>वम्यते, Aor. अवामि (Part. वान्त and वमित):<BR>Caus. वामयति, वमयति (with prepositions the<BR>latter only is used), -यितुम्, Aor. अवीवमत्, to cause<BR>to vomit, sicken: Desid. विवमिषति: Intens. वं-<BR>वम्यते, वंवन्ति; [cf. Zend vam, ‘to vomit;’<BR>Gr. ἐμ-έ-ω, ἔμ-ε-το-ς, ἔμ-εσι-ς; Lat. vom-o, vom-<BR>i-tu-s, vom-i-tio; Goth. vamm, ana-vammjan;<BR>Angl. Sax. wemman; Old Norse vom-a, vœma;<BR>Lith. vem-j-u, vem-ti, vem-alai.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम|वमः
वम, अस्, ई, m. f. vomiting, ejecting, giving out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमथु|वमथुः
वमथु, उस्, m. vomiting, ejecting from the<BR>mouth; water ejected from an elephant's trunk; =<BR>काश, a cough (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमन|वमनं|वमनः
वमन, अम्, n. the act of vomiting, ejecting<BR>anything from the mouth; causing vomiting, an<BR>emetic; offering oblations to fire; taking, getting;<BR>pain, paining; (अस्), m. hemp; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people; (ई), f. a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमनीय
वमनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be vomited; (आ), f. a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमि|वमिः
वमि, इस्, f. vomiting, sickness, nausea, qualmishness;<BR>an emetic; (इस्), m., N. of fire; a rogue, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमित|वमितः
वमित, अस्, आ, अम्, vomited, made to vomit,<BR>sickened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमितव्य
वमितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be vomited, to be<BR>ejected from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमित्वा
वमित्वा, ind. having vomited, having been sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमिन्
वमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, vomiting, being sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्त|वांत|वान्तः
वान्त, वान्ति. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्भ|वंभः|वम्भः
वम्भ वम्भ, अस्, m. = वंश, a bamboo, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्भारव|वंभारव|वंभारवः|वम्भारवः
वम्भारव वम्भा-रव, अस्, m. (onomato-<BR>poetic), the lowing of cattle, (better written बम्भा-<BR>रव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्मागदेश
वम्मागदेश वम्माग-देश, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्र|वम्रः
वम्र वम्र, अस्, m. (or more frequently)<BR>ई, f. (probably connected with वल्मी), an ant, (said<BR>to be also आ, f.); (अस्), m. a proper N., (Vamra<BR>Vaikhānasa is the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X.<BR>99); [cf. Gr. μύρμο-ς, μύρμ-ηξ; Lat. form-ica.]<BR>—वम्री-कूट, अम्, n. an ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्रक
वम्रक, अस्, m., Ved. a small ant; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>small, little (= ह्रस्व, according to Naigh. III. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय्
वय् वय्, cl. 1. A. वयते, वेये, वयितुम्, to<BR>go; (for cl. 1. P. वयति, &c., see rt. वे.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय|वयं|वयः
वय वय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वे), one who<BR>weaves, a weaver; (ई), f., Ved. a female weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयत्|वयन्त्
वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, weaving, interweaving;<BR>(अन्), m., Ved. a proper N.; (according to some<BR>वयत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयन|वयनं
वयन, अम्, n. the act of weaving, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयियु
वयियु, Ved. anything woven, cloth, clothes, (Ṛg-<BR>veda VIII. 19, 37. according to Durga = वस्त्रादि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयिष्यत्
वयिष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. about to weave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयम्
वयम् वयम् (nom. pl. of अहम्, see अस्मद्,<BR>p. 108), we.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्
वयस् वयस्, अस्, n. (in some senses fr. rt.<BR>1. वी), food, victuals, sacrificial food, oblation, offering<BR>(Ved.); energy (both bodily and mental), strength,<BR>vigour, power, might (Ved.); soundness, health<BR>(Ved.); the time of health and strength, youth, the<BR>prime of life; any period of life, age, time of life,<BR>stage of existence, year of life or age; any period,<BR>step, degree, kind; a bird, any winged animal, the<BR>winged tribe (especially applied to smaller birds, cf.<BR>2. वि).<BR>—वयः-परिणति, इस्, f. ripeness of age.<BR>—वयः-प्रमाण, अम्, n. measure or length of<BR>life, duration of life, age.<BR>—वयः-सन्धि, इस्, m.<BR>‘age-junction,’ puberty.<BR>—वयः-सम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of the same age, equal in age.<BR>—वयः-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being in the period of youth or in the prime of<BR>life, young, youthful; grown up, mature, middle-<BR>aged; strong, powerful; (अस्), m. a contemporary,<BR>associate, friend; (आ), f. a female contemporary,<BR>female friend or companion [cf. वयस्या]; N. of<BR>several plants, Emblica Officinalis; the moon-plant,<BR>Asclepias Acida; a medicinal root (= काकोली, क्षीर-<BR>काकोली); Terminalia Chebula or Citrina; Cocculus<BR>Cordifolius; Bombax Heptaphyllum; = अत्य्-अम्ल-<BR>पर्णी; small cardamoms.<BR>—वयः-स्थान, अम्,<BR>n. the firmness or freshness of youth.<BR>—वयः-<BR>स्थापन, अस्, ई, अम्, maintaining or preserving the<BR>freshness of youth.<BR>—वयस्-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>causing life or health; of mature age (?) .<BR>—वयस्-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. causing strength, preserving health<BR>or youth; giving life, (Sāy. आयुष्य-प्रद.)<BR>—व-<BR>यस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of power or<BR>vigour, mighty, vigorous; possessing or supplying<BR>food, (Sāy. = अन्न-युक्त.)<BR>—वयो-गत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>arrived at age, come of age, advanced in years, old,<BR>aged; (अम्), n. the departure of youth; वयो-गते,<BR>when youth is past.<BR>—वयो-जू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. ex-<BR>citing or increasing strength.<BR>—वयो-ऽतिग or वयो-<BR>ऽतीत, अस्, आ, अम्, advanced in age, exceedingly old<BR>or decrepit; passing beyond or liberated from all<BR>periods or stages of existence.<BR>—वयो-धस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">Page0887-a+ 80</a>]<BR>अस्, Ved. = वयो-धा below.<BR>—वयो-धा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम् (acc. -धाम्, voc. -धस्, nom. pl. m. f. -धास्,<BR>borrowing some of its cases fr. वयो-धस् above),<BR>Ved. giving strength, bestowing or granting health;<BR>possessing strength, powerful, mighty, vigorous,<BR>youthful, young, middle-aged; giving food, (Sāy.<BR>= अन्नस्य दातृ); (आस्), f. strength, power, might,<BR>vigour.<BR>—वयो-ऽधिक, अस्, आ, अम्, superior in years,<BR>older in age; very old or advanced in age, exceed-<BR>ingly old; (अस्), m. an old man.<BR>—वयो-धेय, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. power, energy, vigour.<BR>—वयो-नाध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम् (नाध fr. rt. नह्), Ved. (perhaps) esta-<BR>blishing health.<BR>—वयो-वयः-शय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. resting on all kinds of food or where food of<BR>every kind rests.<BR>—वयो-ऽवस्था, f. a stage or state<BR>of life (generally considered to be three, viz. बाल-<BR>त्व, childhood, तरुण-त्व, youth, and वृद्ध-<BR>त्व, old age).<BR>—वयो-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. of<BR>the kind or nature of birds.<BR>—वयो-वृद्ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, advanced in years, old.<BR>—वयो-वृध्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. increasing strength or energy, strengthening,<BR>invigorating (said of the Maruts and of Morning and<BR>Night); increasing food, (Sāy. = अन्नस्य वर्ध-<BR>यितृ.)<BR>—वयो-हानि, इस्, f. loss of youth or vigour,<BR>the growing old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0886-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस
वयस, अस्, m., Ved. = वयस्, a bird; (अम्), n.<BR>age, (at the end of a comp., e. g. मध्यम-वय-<BR>सम्, middle age; cf. उत्तर-व्˚, पूर्व-व्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयसिन्
वयसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being in any age or period of<BR>life, (at the end of comps., see पूर्व-व्˚, प्रथ-<BR>म-व्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्क
वयस्क = वयस्, age, (at the end of an adj. comp.,<BR>e. g. अभिनव-वयस्का, a woman in the fresh bloom<BR>of youth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्य|वयस्यः
वयस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to age, being of<BR>the same age, contemporary; (अस्), m. a contempo-<BR>rary, associate, companion, friend; (आ), f. a female<BR>companion or friend, a woman's confidante or faith-<BR>ful female servant; scil. इष्टका, Ved. epithet of<BR>nineteen bricks used for building the sacrificial altar<BR>(so called from the word वयस् being contained in<BR>the formula of consecration).<BR>—वयस्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. or वयस्य-भाव, अस्, m. the condition of being<BR>a contemporary, companionship, friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्यक
वयस्यक, अस्, m. a contemporary, friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वया
वया, f., Ved. strength, power, (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda I. 165, 15. वयाम् = वयम्, we); a<BR>branch, twig; a race, family, (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 124, 3. वयायाः = गन्तव्यायाः.)<BR>—वया-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. = वयस्-वत्, pos-<BR>sessed of power or vigour; (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI. 2,<BR>5. वया = शाखा = पुत्र-पौत्रादि, having pos-<BR>terity, peopled with descendants.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयाक|वयाकः
वयाक, अस्, m. a little branch, tendril, creeper<BR>(= लता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयाकिन्
वयाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having little branches or<BR>tendrils, ramifying (said of the Soma plant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयुन|वयुनं|वयुनः
1. वयुन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) having vital<BR>power, endowed with life (in Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa<BR>VIII. 2, 2, 8).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयियु
वयियु वयियु. See under वय, p. 886,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयुन|वयुनं|वयुनः
वयुन 2. वयुन, अम्, n. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. III. 61. fr. rt. वी, substituted for rt. अज्), a<BR>mark, token, sign, characteristic (Ved.); a rule,<BR>ordinance, sacred rite, appointment, order; manner,<BR>custom, mode of acting, actions; distinctness, clear-<BR>ness, (in the preceding senses generally Ved. and<BR>frequently आनि, n. pl.); the faculty of perceiving,<BR>consciousness, knowledge, wisdom, information, in-<BR>struction, (Sāy. = प्रज्ञा, प्रज्ञान, ज्ञान-सा-<BR>धन, ज्ञान); a temple; (अस्), m., N. of a son<BR>of Kṛśāśva and Dhiṣaṇā; (आ), f. knowledge; N.<BR>of a daughter of Svadhā.<BR>—वयुन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. wisdom-bestowing, endowed with wisdom or<BR>sense, (Sāy. = प्रज्ञोपेत); clear, distinct, bright,<BR>(Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI. 21, 3 = प्रकाश-वत्.)<BR>—व-<BR>युन-शस्, ind., Ved. according to rule or order, in<BR>due order, in the order of knowledge, (Sāy. = ज्ञान-<BR>क्रमेण.)<BR>—वयुना-विद्, त्, त्, त् (in the Pada-pāṭha<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-b" target="_blank">Page0887-b+ 79</a>]<BR>text वयुन-विद्), Ved. learned in rules, well versed<BR>in ordinances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोवङ्ग|वयोवङ्गं
वयोवङ्ग वयोवङ्ग (?) , अम्, n. lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय्य
वय्य वय्य, अस्, m., Ved., N. of an Asura<BR>(a companion of Turvīti, both of whom Indra helped<BR>over a stream which obstructed their course; but<BR>according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 54, 6. वय्यम् =<BR>वय्य-कुल-जम्, Vayya being merely a patronymic<BR>of Turvīti); a companion, friend (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्
वर् वर्, the form assumed by the rt.<BR>वृ (q. v.) in cl. 10. and causal, and in the<BR>following derivatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
वर, अस्, m. surrounding, encompassing; circum-<BR>ference, compass, space, room (Ved., cf. उरु, with<BR>which वर in this sense is connected); stopping,<BR>checking (= निवारण, निग्रह, Ved.); the act of<BR>selecting, choosing, appointing, engaging; request-<BR>ing, soliciting, entreating; choice, election, wish,<BR>desire, request, boon, blessing, favour, (rarely अम्,<BR>n.); anything chosen as a present, gift, reward,<BR>recompense; any desirable object, benefit, advantage,<BR>privilege; a dowry; charity, alms; a kind of grain<BR>(= वरट); bdellium; a sparrow; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>one who chooses, a chooser, choosing, selecting, &c.;<BR>one who solicits a girl in marriage, a suitor, wooer,<BR>lover, (in these senses only masc.); a bridegroom, hus-<BR>band (m.); a bridegroom's friend; a son-in-law (m.);<BR>a dissolute man (m.); wished for, desirable, valuable,<BR>precious, excellent, best; the best, most excellent<BR>or eminent, (frequently with gen. pl., e. g. सरितां<BR>वरा, the best of rivers: also with a loc. and even<BR>abl. pl., e. g. नरेषु वरः, the best among men;<BR>नारीभ्यो वरा, the best of women: frequently also<BR>at the end of a comp., cf. रथ-व्˚, नर-व्˚);<BR>better, preferable, better than (with abl. and some-<BR>times even with gen., e. g. ग्रन्थिभ्यो धारिणो<BR>वराः, those who remember are better than those<BR>who merely read books; कामो धर्मार्थयोर्<BR>वरः, pleasure is better than religion or wealth);<BR>eldest; (अम्), ind. preferably, rather, better, prefer-<BR>able, (in Ved. sometimes with abl., e. g. अग्निभ्यो<BR>वरम्, better than fires; or sometimes with abl.<BR>and आ, e. g. सखिभ्य आ वरम्, better than com-<BR>panions); it is better that, it would be best if (with<BR>pres., e. g. वरं गच्छामि, it is better that I go;<BR>or even with ellipsis of the verb, e. g. वरं सिंहात्,<BR>it would be better if [death should happen] from the<BR>lion; sometimes with pot., e. g. वरं तत् कुर्यात्,<BR>better that he should do that); better than, rather than,<BR>(in these senses वरम् is followed by न or न च<BR>or न तु or न पुनर् &c., and may be translated<BR>by ‘better and not;’ वरम् मृत्युर् न चाकीर्त्तिः,<BR>better death than infamy, or better death and not<BR>infamy); (आ), f., N. of several plants and vegetable<BR>products, the three kinds of myrobalan; Clypea<BR>Hernandifolia; Asparagus Racemosus; Cocculus<BR>Cordifolius; a sort of perfume (= रेणुका); tur-<BR>meric; = ब्राह्मी, मेदा, विदङ्ग; N. of Pārvatī;<BR>of a river; (ई), f. the plant Asparagus Racemosus;<BR>N. of Chāyā the wife of Sūrya; (अम्), n. saffron;<BR>[cf. Lat. vir: Goth. vair, vaila: Old Germ. wela:<BR>Angl. Sax. wel, wela: Lith. wyras: Hib. fear,<BR>‘good;’ ‘a husband.’]<BR>—वर-कल्याण, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—वर-काष्ठका, f. the plant Clero-<BR>dendrum Siphonanthus; a grain similar to Varāṭikā.<BR>—वर-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वर-क्रतु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of Indra.<BR>—वर-ग, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—वर-घण्टिका or वर-घण्टी, f. the<BR>plant Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>—वर-चन्दन, अम्,<BR>n. a dark sort of sandal-wood; a sort of pine, Pinus<BR>Deodora.<BR>—वर-ज = वरे-ज, Pāṇ. VI. 3, 16.<BR>—वर-जानुक, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—वर-<BR>तनु, उस्, ऊस्, उ, having a beautiful body or person;<BR>(ऊस्), f. an elegant woman; a kind of metre, four<BR>times ˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯˘.<BR>—वर-तन्तु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of an ancient preceptor; (अवस्), m. pl.<BR>Vara-tantu's descendants.<BR>—वर-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>most preferable or excellent.<BR>—वर-तिक्त, अस्, m.<BR>Wrightia Antidysenterica.<BR>—वर-तिक्तक, अस्, m.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-c" target="_blank">Page0887-c+ 81</a>]<BR>N. of a plant, Azadirachta Indica; of another, =<BR>पर्पट; (इका), f. Clypea Hernandifolia.<BR>—वर-<BR>तोया, f. ‘having excellent water,’ N. of a river.<BR>—वर-त्वच, अस्, m. the Nimb tree, Azadirachta<BR>Indica.<BR>—वर-द, अस्, आ, अम्, granting wishes,<BR>conferring a boon, ready to fulfil requests or answer<BR>prayers, propitious, favourable; (अस्), m. a bene-<BR>factor; N. of Agni in Śāntika; fire for burnt offer-<BR>ings of a propitiatory character; N. of one of Skanda's<BR>attendants; of a particular class of Manes; of a<BR>Dhyāni-buddha; (आ), f. a young woman, girl,<BR>maiden; N. of a guardian goddess in the family of<BR>Vara-tantu; N. of various plants, Physalis Flexuosa;<BR>Polanisia Icosandra; Helianthus; Linum Usitatissi-<BR>mum; the root of yam; = त्रि-पर्णी; N. of a river.<BR>—वर-दक्षिणा, f. a present made to the bride-<BR>groom by the father of the bride in giving her away;<BR>a term for expence or costs incurred in fruitless en-<BR>deavours to recover a loss.<BR>—वरद-चतुर्थी, f.,<BR>N. of the fourth day in the light half of the month<BR>Māgha.<BR>—वर-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, given as a boon,<BR>granted in consequence of a request; (अस्), m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—वरद-राज, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Laghu-kaumudī and of the Madhya-siddhānta-<BR>kaumudī; of various other persons.<BR>—वरद-रा-<BR>जीय, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or relating to Varada-<BR>rāja, composed by Varada-rāja.<BR>—वर-दर्शिनी, in<BR>Rāmāyaṇa II. 55, 21, probably incorrect for वर-<BR>वर्णिनी.<BR>—वरद-हस्त, अस्, m. the beneficent<BR>hand (of a deity or benefactor of any kind).<BR>—व-<BR>रदा-चतुर्थी, f. = वरद-चतुर्थी.<BR>—वर-दा-<BR>तु, उस्, m. a kind of tree (= द्वार-दातु).<BR>—वर-<BR>दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, = वर-द.<BR>—वरदाधीश-<BR>यज्वन् (˚द-अध्˚), आ, m., N. of an author.<BR>—व-<BR>र-दान, अम्, n. the granting a boon or request,<BR>giving compensation or reward; N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—वरदान-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, caused<BR>by the granting a request, arising from the grant of<BR>a favour or bestowal of a boon.<BR>—वर-दानिक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, caused by bestowing a boon.<BR>—वर-दारु,<BR>Tectona Grandis.<BR>—वर-दारुक, a kind of plant<BR>with poisonous leaves.<BR>—वर-दाश्वस् = वर-द.<BR>—वर-द्रुम, अस्, m. ‘excellent-tree,’ Agallochum.<BR>—वर-धर्म, अस्, m. a noble act of justice, ex-<BR>cellent work, &c.<BR>—वरधर्मी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -क-<BR>रोति, &c., to do a noble act towards any one.<BR>—वर-<BR>नारी, f. the best woman, a most excellent woman.<BR>—वर-निश्चय, अस्, m. the determining or choos-<BR>ing of a person to be a husband, choice of a bride-<BR>groom.<BR>—वर-पक्ष, अस्, m. the party or side<BR>of a bridegroom at a wedding.<BR>—वर-पक्षिणी,<BR>f., N. of a Tantra goddess.<BR>—वर-पक्षीय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, belonging to the party of the bridegroom.<BR>—वर-पण्डित, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—वर-<BR>पर्णाख्य (˚ण-आख्˚), अस्, m. Lipeocercis Serrata.<BR>—वर-पाण्ड्य, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वर-पी-<BR>तक, talc.<BR>—वर-पोत, a kind of plant (= श्रेष्ठ-<BR>शाक).<BR>—वर-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, = वर-द, con-<BR>ferring a boon, granting a favour; (आ), f., N. of<BR>Lopāmudrā.<BR>—वर-प्रदान, अम्, n. = वर-दान,<BR>the bestowal of a boon.<BR>—वर-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having excellent brightness; (अस्), m., N. of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR>—वर-प्रस्थान, अम्, n. the setting out<BR>of a bridegroom in procession towards the house of<BR>the bride for the celebration of the marriage.<BR>—व-<BR>र-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing or yielding the<BR>best fruits; (अस्), m. the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—वर-<BR>बाल्हीक, अम्, n. saffron, (also written वर-वाह्-<BR>लीक.)<BR>—वर-मुखी, f. a kind of perfume (=<BR>रेणुका).<BR>—वर-यात्रा, f. the procession of a suitor<BR>or bridegroom (to the house of the bride).<BR>—वर-<BR>युवति, इस्, or वर-युवती, f. a beautiful young<BR>woman, handsome girl; a kind of metre, four times<BR>¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯¯˘˘˘˘˘˘¯.<BR>—वर-योग्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, worthy of a boon or reward.<BR>—वर-यो-<BR>निक, (probably) a kind of plant (= केसर).<BR>—व-<BR>र-रुचि, इस्, m., N. of a poet, grammarian, lexico-<BR>grapher, and writer on medicine, (sometimes identi-<BR>fied with Kātyāyana, the reputed author of the<BR>Vārttikas or supplementary rules of Pāṇini; he is<BR>placed by some among the nine gems of the court<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-a" target="_blank">Page0888-a+ 81</a>]<BR>of Vikramāditya, and by others among the ornaments<BR>of the court of Bhoja; he was the author of the<BR>Prākṛt grammar called Prākṛta-prakāśa, and is said<BR>to be the first grammarian who reduced the various<BR>dialects of Prākṛt to a system); N. of Śiva.<BR>—वर-<BR>रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, having an excellent or noble form;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—वर-लब्ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who has obtained a boon; received as a<BR>boon; (अस्), m. Michelia Champaka; Bauhinia Va-<BR>riegata.<BR>—वर-वत्सला, f. a mother-in-law.<BR>—वर-<BR>वर्ण, अस्, m. ‘best-coloured,’ gold; [cf. सु-वर्ण.]<BR>—वर-वर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a beautiful com-<BR>plexion or colour; (इनी), f. a woman with a beautiful<BR>complexion, an excellent or handsome woman, a<BR>virtuous woman; a woman in general; N. of Durgā;<BR>of Sarasvatī; of Lakṣmī; turmeric; lac; a brownish<BR>yellow pigment; a kind of plant (= प्रियङ्गु,<BR>फलिनी).<BR>—वर-वारण, अस्, m. a fine elephant.<BR>—वर-वासि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—वर-<BR>वाह्लीक, see वर-बाल्हीक.<BR>—वर-वृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, received as a boon or reward.<BR>—वर-वृद्ध,<BR>अस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—वर-शिख, अस्, m., Ved., N.<BR>of an Asura whose family was destroyed by Indra<BR>(Ṛg-veda VI. 27, 4, 5).<BR>—वर-शीत, cinnamon.<BR>—वर-श्रेणी, f. a kind of plant.<BR>—वर-सद्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, Ved. dwelling in an orb or sphere, (Sāy. = वर-<BR>णीये मण्डले सीदत्, dwelling in the most excellent<BR>orb, i. e. the sun.)<BR>—वर-सुन्दरी, f. a very beauti-<BR>ful woman; a kind of metre, four times ¯˘˘˘¯˘<BR>˘˘¯˘˘˘¯¯.<BR>—वर-सुरत, अस्, आ, अम्, well ac-<BR>quainted with the secrets of sexual enjoyment, very<BR>wanton.<BR>—वर-सेन (?) , N. of a mountain pass.<BR>—वर-स्त्री, f. an excellent woman.<BR>—वर-स्रज्,<BR>क्, f. a bridegroom's garland, the garland placed by<BR>a maiden on the head of a chosen suitor.<BR>—वराङ्ग<BR>(˚र-अङ्˚), अम्, n. the best or most beautiful member<BR>of the body; the head; the female pudenda; the<BR>principal piece or part; an elegant form or body;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), having an excellent form, excellent or<BR>beautiful in all parts; (अस्), m. an elephant; epithet<BR>of a Nakṣatra year consisting of 324 days; N. of<BR>Viṣṇu; (ई), f. turmeric; N. of a daughter of Dṛ-<BR>shad-vat and wife of Sañjāti; (अम्), n. Cassia bark,<BR>green cinnamon; sorrel (?) .<BR>—वराङ्गक, अम्, n.<BR>= वराङ्ग, Cassia bark.<BR>—वराङ्गना (˚र-अङ्˚),<BR>f. a beautiful or noble woman.<BR>—वराङ्ग-रूपोपेत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, handsome and well shaped.<BR>—वराङ्गिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘beautiful-limbed,’ sorrel, Rumex Vesicarius.<BR>—वराजीविन् (˚र-आज्), ई, m. an astrologer.<BR>—व-<BR>राज्य (˚र-आज्˚), अम्, n. the choicest ghee or clarified<BR>butter.<BR>—वरादन (˚र-अद्˚), अम्, n. a sort of<BR>Mimusops (= राजादन).<BR>—वरानना (˚र-आन्˚),<BR>f. a lovely-faced woman.<BR>—वराभिध (˚र-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. one who has a good name; sorrel, Rumex Ve-<BR>sicarius.<BR>—वराम्र (˚र-अम्˚), अस्, m. a sort of acid<BR>fruit tree, Carissa Carandas.<BR>—वरारोह (˚र-आर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an excellent rider; a rider on an elephant or<BR>horse; a rider in general; mounting, riding; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), having fine hips; (अस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu,<BR>(perhaps incorrect for वराह); (आ), f. a handsome<BR>or elegant woman, noble lady; N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in<BR>Someśvara; the hip or flank.<BR>—वरार्थिन् (˚र-अर्˚),<BR>ई, इनी, इ, seeking for a boon, asking for a blessing.<BR>—वरार्ह (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of a boon;<BR>exceedingly worthy, being in high esteem; very<BR>costly or expensive.<BR>—वरालि (˚र-आलि), इस्, m. the<BR>moon; a division of music; [cf. वराडी.]<BR>—वरा-<BR>लिका, f. (fr. वर + आलि), N. of Durgā.<BR>—वरासन<BR>(˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. an excellent seat, the best seat, a<BR>throne; N. of a town; the China rose, Hibiscus<BR>Rosa Sinensis; a cistern, reservoir, (for वार्-आसन,<BR>q. v.); (अस्, आ, अम्), having an excellent seat; (अस्),<BR>m. a door-keeper; a lover, paramour.<BR>—वरे-ज =<BR>वर-ज, Pāṇ. VI. 3, 16.<BR>—वरेन्द्र (˚र-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a chief, sovereign; Indra; N. of a part of<BR>Bengal; (ई), f. ancient Gauḍa or Gaur, the capital<BR>and district so named (according to some).<BR>—वरेश<BR>(˚र-ईश), अस्, आ, अम्, presiding over boons, able to<BR>grant wishes.<BR>—वरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>वरेश; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—वरोरु (˚र-ऊरु),<BR>उस्, m. a beautiful thigh; (उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ), having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">Page0888-b+ 81</a>]<BR>beautiful thighs; (उस् or ऊस्), f. a beautiful-thighed<BR>woman, well-formed woman, (see ऊरु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0887-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरंवरा
वरंवरा, f. a particular plant (= चक्र-पर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरक|वरकं|वरकः
वरक, अस्, m. a cloak; one who asks a female<BR>in marriage; a wish, request, boon; a kind of wild<BR>bean, Phaseolus Trilobus; a particular medicinal<BR>plant (= पर्पट); a kind of grass (= रूक्ष);<BR>= शर-पर्णिका; N. of a king, (also read ध-<BR>नक, कनक); (अम्), n. a towel, cloth, wiper;<BR>the cover or awning of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरट|वरटं|वरटः
वरट, अस्, m. a kind of grain (probably the seed<BR>of safflower or Carthamus Tinctorius); a kind of<BR>wasp; a gander; an artisan of a particular class<BR>(placed among Mlecchas or barbarians); (आ), f. the<BR>seed of Carthamus Tinctorius; a kind of wasp; a<BR>goose; (ई), f. a kind of wasp; (अम्), n. a jasmine<BR>flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरटक
वरटक, अस्, m. or वरट्टिका, f. a kind of<BR>grain (= वरट above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण|वरणं|वरणः
वरण, अस्, m. a rampart, mound, wall of ma-<BR>sonry, &c., outer enclosure; a causeway, bridge; the<BR>tree Cratæva Roxburghii (found in every part of<BR>India; it is used in medicine, and supposed to pos-<BR>sess magical virtues; cf. वरुण, सेतु); any tree;<BR>a camel; a kind of ornament or decoration on a<BR>bow; N. of a particular magical formula recited over<BR>weapons; N. of Indra; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>of a kingdom; (आ), f., N. of a small river (running<BR>past the north of Benares into the Ganges and now<BR>called Burnah); (अम्), n. the act of screening, cover-<BR>ing, protecting, supporting; enclosing, encircling,<BR>surrounding, encompassing; keeping off, prohibiting;<BR>the act of choosing, selecting, choice of a bride; wish-<BR>ing, requesting, soliciting.<BR>—वरण-माला or व-<BR>रण-स्रज्, क्, f. the garland placed by a maiden on<BR>the head of a selected suitor.<BR>—वरणा-वती, f., Ved.<BR>(perhaps) N. of a river (in Atharva-veda IV. 7, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणक
वरणक, अस्, आ, अम्, covering, covering over,<BR>concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणसी
वरणसी, f. (fr. वरणा), Benares, (more usually<BR>written वाराणसी, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणीय
वरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be chosen, to be selected,<BR>&c.; to be solicited (for a boon &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्ड|वरंड|वरंडः|वरण्डः
वरण्ड, अस्, m. a multitude; an eruption on the<BR>face; a veranda, portico; a heap of grass; the string<BR>of a fish-hook; a packet, package; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>thrush (= सारिका); a dagger, knife; the wick of a<BR>lamp.<BR>—वरण्डालु (˚ड-आलु), उस्, m. a kind of<BR>bulbous plant (= फल-पुच्छ); the castor-oil<BR>tree, Ricinus Communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डक|वरंडक|वरण्डकः
वरण्डक, अस्, m. a small mound of earth; the<BR>seat or canopy on an elephant, a howdah; an eruption<BR>on the face; a wall; (अस्, आ, अम्), round; large,<BR>great, large in compass or circumference; miserable,<BR>wretched, miserly; fearful, terrified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्य
वरण्य, Nom. P. वरण्यति, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्करी
वरत्करी, f. a sort of perfume (= रेणुका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्रा
वरत्रा, f. a strap, thong, strip of leather, girth;<BR>an elephant's or horse's girth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयितव्य
वरयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be chosen or selected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयितृ
वरयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a suitor, wooer, lover,<BR>bridegroom, husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयु
वरयु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरल|वरलः
वरल, अस्, आ, m. f. a sort of gad-fly or wasp;<BR>(आ), f. a goose; (ई), f. = वरटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरस्
वरस्, अस्, n., Ved. width, breadth, room, space;<BR>[cf. Gr. εὖρος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरसान
वरसान, Ved. = दारिक (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 86).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरस्या
वरस्या, f., Ved. wish. desire, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराक|वराकः
वराक, अस्, आ, अम्, pitiable, miserable, unhappy,<BR>poor, wretched, low, vile; impure; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>Śiva; battle, war; N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराट|वराटः
वराट, अस्, m. a cowry (used as a coin); a rope,<BR>cord; (ई), f. = वराडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटक|वराटकः
वराटक, अस्, इका, m. f. a cowry, Cypræa Mo-<BR>neta = (1/20) of a Kākiṇī or (1/80) of a Paṇa); (अस्), m.<BR>the seed-vessel of a lotus-flower; a rope, cord, string;<BR>(इका), f. the plant Mirabilis Jalapa; (अम्), n. a par-<BR>ticular vegetable poison.<BR>—वराटक-रजस्, आस्, m.<BR>a kind of plant, Mesua Roxburghii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराडी
वराडी, f. (?), N. of a Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराण|वराणः
वराण, अस्, m. = वरण, the tree Cratæva Rox-<BR>burghii; N. of Indra, (in this sense said to be a<BR>Pres. Part. A. of rt. वृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराणसी
वराणसी, f. the city of Benares, (more usually<BR>written वाराणसी, see वरणसी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरातुष्ट
वरातुष्ट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराय
वराय, Nom. A. (?) वरायते, &c., to represent<BR>or become like a boon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरायित
वरायित, अस्, आ, अम्, become like a boon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराल|वरालः
वराल, cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालक|वरालकः
वरालक, cloves; (अस्), m. Carissa Carandas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरितृ
वरितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who covers or screens;<BR>a chooser, choosing, &c.; [cf. वरीतृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिन्
वरिन्, ई, m., N. of a divine being enumerated<BR>among the Viśve Devāḥ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिमन्
वरिमन्, आ, अ, m. n. circumference, circuit,<BR>compass (Ved.); width, breadth, extent, greatness,<BR>expanse (Ved., in this sense an abstract noun of उरु,<BR>q. v.); excellence, superiority, pre-eminence, (in this<BR>sense fr. वर); the most excellent, best, (used as<BR>an adj. for वरिष्ठ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्
वरिवस्, अस्, n., Ved. room, width, space, (वरि-<BR>वः कृ, to make room or space, procure ample<BR>space); freedom, relief, comfort, ease, rest, repose,<BR>bliss, happiness; wealth, treasure (= धन according<BR>to Sāy. and Naigh. II. 10); worship, service, honour.<BR>—वरिवस्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. acquiring room, pro-<BR>curing space, affording relief, freeing, delivering,<BR>(Sāy. = धनस्य कर्तृ, the causer or giver of<BR>wealth.)<BR>—वरिवो-द, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving room<BR>or space, granting freedom or relief.<BR>—वरिवो-धा,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. causing room, making a free<BR>course; granting bliss; (Sāy.) conferring riches (=<BR>धनस्य दातृ).<BR>—वरिवो-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. ob-<BR>taining or causing room, granting freedom, bestowing<BR>comfort or repose; granting treasures or affluence;<BR>bestowing honour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवसित|वरिवसितः
वरिवसित, अस्, आ, अम्, (another form of वरि-<BR>वस्यित below), served, honoured, adored (said of a<BR>deity or of a spiritual teacher).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्य
वरिवस्य, Nom. P. वरिवस्यति, &c., to grant<BR>room or space, give room to, give relief, concede,<BR>grant, permit (Ved.); to make happy or comfort-<BR>able, show favour, serve, honour, adore, worship;<BR>(Sāy.) to desire wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्यत्
वरिवस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, granting room or space;<BR>(Sāy.) desiring wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्या
वरिवस्या, f. service, honour, worship, devotion,<BR>devoted obedience to a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्यित|वरिवस्यितः
वरिवस्यित, अस्, आ, अम्, served, honoured, adored,<BR>reverenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठ|वरिष्ठं|वरिष्ठः
वरिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, the most excellent, best,<BR>dearest, most preferable (= वर-तम); better<BR>than (with abl.); widest, broadest, largest, greatest,<BR>most extensive, heaviest, (in these senses regarded as<BR>a superl. of उरु); the most conspicuous (in a bad<BR>sense), worst, most wicked; (अस्), m. the Francoline<BR>partridge; the orange tree; N. of a son of Manu<BR>Cākṣuṣa; of one of the seven sages in the eleventh<BR>Manv-antara; of a Daitya; (आ), f. Polanisia Icosan-<BR>dra; (अम्), n. copper; pepper; [cf. Gr. ἄριστος;<BR>Lith. wrausas, ‘noblest, oldest.’]<BR>—वरिष्ठाश्र-<BR>म (˚ठ-आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठक
वरिष्ठक, अस्, आ, अम्, = वरिष्ठ, most excel-<BR>lent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीतृ
वरीतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who covers or screens,<BR>covering, screening; [cf. वरितृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीमन्
वरीमन्, अ, n. (= वरिमन्, q. v.), circumfer-<BR>ence, width, breadth, extent (Ved.); (आ), m. excel-<BR>lence, superiority, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीयस्
वरीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, more excellent, better, pre-<BR>ferable; the most excellent, best; larger, very large,<BR>wider, broader, most extensive, (in this sense regarded<BR>as a compar. of उरु, cf. वरिष्ठ); extremely<BR>young or tender; (अस्), ind. wider, more distant,<BR>further off or away; (अस्), n., Ved. = वरिवस्, rest,<BR>repose; (आन्), m., N. of one of the twenty-seven<BR>divisions of the ecliptic, the eighteenth astronomical<BR>Yoga; of a son of Manu Sāvarṇa; of a son of<BR>Pulaha by Gati; [cf. Gr. ἀρείων; Lat. melior (v<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-a" target="_blank">Page0889-a+ 81</a>]<BR>being changed into m); Lith. wyresnis, ‘nobler,<BR>older.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0888-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरु
वरु, उस्, m., Ved., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुण|वरुणः
वरुण, अस्, m. ‘Universal encompasser, All-en-<BR>veloper, ‘N. of an Āditya, (as a Vedic deity com-<BR>monly associated with Mitra and presiding over the<BR>night as Mitra over the day [see 1. मित्र], but<BR>often celebrated separately, whereas Mitra is rarely<BR>invoked alone; Varuṇa is one of the oldest of the<BR>Vedic gods, corresponding in name and partly in<BR>character to the Οὐρανός of the Greeks, and is<BR>often regarded as the supreme deity, being then<BR>styled ‘king of the gods’ or ‘king of both gods and<BR>men’ or ‘king of the universe;’ no other deity has<BR>such grand attributes and functions assigned to him;<BR>he is described as fashioning and upholding heaven<BR>and earth, as possessing extraordinary power and<BR>wisdom called माया, as sending his spies or messen-<BR>gers throughout both worlds, as numbering the very<BR>winkings of men's eyes, as hating falsehood, as<BR>seizing transgressors with his पाश or noose, as in-<BR>flicting diseases, especially dropsy, as pardoning sin,<BR>as the guardian of immortality; though generally<BR>associated with Mitra, he is also invoked in the Veda<BR>together with Indra, and in later Vedic literature<BR>together with Agni, with Yama, and with Viṣṇu;<BR>in Ṛg-veda IV. 1, 2. he is even called the brother<BR>of Agni; though not generally regarded in the Veda<BR>as a god of the ocean, yet he is often connected with<BR>the waters, especially the waters of the atmosphere<BR>or firmament, and in one place [Ṛg-veda VII. 64, 2]<BR>is called with Mitra सिन्धु-पति, ‘lord of the sea or<BR>of rivers;’ hence in the later mythology he became<BR>a kind of Neptune, and is there best known in his<BR>character of god of the ocean; in the Mahā-bhārata<BR>Varuṇa is said to be a son of Kardama and father of<BR>Puṣkara, and is also variously represented as one<BR>of the Deva-gandharvas, as a Nāga, as a king of the<BR>Nāgas, and as an Asura; he is the regent of the<BR>western quarter [cf. लोक-पाल] and of the Nakṣatra<BR>Śata-bhiṣaj; the Jainas consider Varuṇa as a servant<BR>of the twentieth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī);<BR>the sun (‘the warder off or dispeller of darkness,’<BR>cf. Ṛg-veda V. 48, 5, Sāy. = तमो-वारक); the<BR>firmament; the ocean, waters; N. of a particular<BR>magical formula recited over weapons; the tree Cra-<BR>tæva Roxburghii [cf. वरण]; (आस्), m. pl. (per-<BR>haps) the gods generally (so explained by some in<BR>Atharva-veda III. 4, 6); (आ), f., N. of a river; [cf.<BR>Zend Varena; Gr. Οὐρανό-ς; Hib. burne, ‘water.’]<BR>—वरुण-गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. seized by Va-<BR>ruṇa, afflicted with disease (especially with dropsy;<BR>see under वरुण).<BR>—वरुण-ग्राह, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>seizure by Varuṇa.<BR>—वरुण-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—वरुण-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state or nature of Varuṇa.<BR>—वरुण-दत्त, अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—वरुण-देव or वरुण-दैवत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having Varuṇa for a deity; (अम्), n. the<BR>Nakṣatra Śata-bhiṣaj.<BR>—वरुण-ध्रुत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. deceiving Varuṇa; (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda VII. 60, 9. वरुण-ध्रुतः = वरुणेन<BR>हिंसितः.)<BR>—वरुण-पाश, अस्, m. Varuṇa's snare<BR>or noose (Ved.); a shark.<BR>—वरुण-पुरुष, अस्,<BR>m. a servant of Varuṇa.<BR>—वरुण-प्रघास, आस्,<BR>m. pl. the second of certain periodical oblations<BR>offered on the full moon of Āṣāḍha or Śrāvaṇa<BR>and observed for the purpose of obtaining exemption<BR>from the snares or bonds of Varuṇa, (so called from<BR>the custom of eating barley on this festival in honour<BR>of the god Varuṇa.)<BR>—वरुण-प्रशिष्ट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ruled over or guided by Varuṇa.<BR>—वरुण-<BR>भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of an astronomer.<BR>—वरुण-<BR>मति, इस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—वरुण-मित्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Gobhila.<BR>—वरुण-मेनि, इस्, f.,<BR>Ved. Varuṇa's wrath.<BR>—वरुण-राजन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>having Varuṇa as king.<BR>—वरुण-लोक, अस्, m.<BR>Varuṇa's world or sphere; Varuṇa's province, i. e.<BR>water.<BR>—वरुण-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a warrior<BR>on the side of the gods in their war against the<BR>Daityas.<BR>—वरुण-शेषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. being<BR>Varuṇa's posterity; (Sāy.) having descendants capable<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">Page0889-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of protecting (= वारकाः पुत्रा येषम्; accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. शेषस् = अपत्य).<BR>—वरुण-श्राद्-<BR>ध, अम्, n., N. of a particular funeral offering.<BR>—वरुण-सव, अस्, m., Ved. Varuṇa's aid or<BR>approval.<BR>—वरुण-सेना or वरुण-सेनिका, f., N.<BR>of a princess.<BR>—वरुण-स्रोतस, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain, (also read वरुण-श्रोतस.)<BR>—वरु-<BR>णाङ्ग-रुह (˚ण-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘Varuṇa's offspring<BR>or scion, ‘a patronymic of Agastya.<BR>—वरुणात्मजा<BR>(˚ण-आत्˚), f. ‘Varuṇa's daughter,’ spirituous or vinous<BR>liquor (so called from being one of the precious<BR>things produced at the churning of the ocean).<BR>—व-<BR>रुणाद्रि (˚ण-अद्˚), इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—व-<BR>रुणालय (˚ण-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘Varuṇa's habitation,’<BR>the sea, ocean, (करुणा-वरुणालय, the sea of<BR>compassion.)<BR>—वरुणावास (˚ण-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘Va-<BR>ruṇa's abode, ‘the sea, ocean.<BR>—वरुणेश (˚ण-ईश),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having Varuṇa as lord or governor; (अम्),<BR>n. the Nakṣatra Śata-bhiṣaj.<BR>—वरुणेश-देश,<BR>अस्, m. the district or sphere governed by Varuṇa.<BR>—वरुणेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚ण-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—वरुणोद (˚ण-उद), अम्, n. ‘Varuṇa's<BR>water, ‘N. of a sea.<BR>—वरुणोपनिषद् (˚ण-उप्˚),<BR>त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणक
वरुणक, अस्, m. = वरुण, Cratæva Roxburghii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणानी
वरुणानी, f. Varuṇa's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणावि|वरुणाविः
वरुणावि, इस्, or वरुणाविस्, f., N. of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणिक
वरुणिक or वरुणिय or वरुणिल, अस्, m.<BR>(diminutives fr. वरुण-दत्त), see Pāṇ. V. 3, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुण्य
वरुण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. coming from Varuṇa,<BR>belonging to him, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुतृ
वरुतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, = वरूतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुत्र|वरुत्रं
वरुत्र, अम्, n. an upper and outer garment,<BR>cloak, mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुल|वरुलः
वरुल, अस्, &c. = सम्भक्त (according to the<BR>Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूतृ
वरूतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who wards off or<BR>protects, a protector, defender; (ता), m. a god who<BR>protects, guardian deity, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 55,<BR>1 = सम्भक्तृ); N. of an Asura priest, (in the<BR>Kāṭhaka-Brāhmaṇa II. 30, 1. Tṛṣṭha and Varūtṛ<BR>are said to be priests of the Asuras); (त्री), f. a female<BR>defender, guardian goddess; N. of a goddess (some-<BR>times invited to a sacrifice along with Sarasvatī); of<BR>a class of guardian goddesses, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>22, 10. वरूत्री = वरणीया, to be chosen, excel-<BR>lent; III. 62, 3. वरूत्रीः = सर्वैः सम्भजनीया<BR>देवपत्न्यः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथ|वरूथं|वरूथः
वरूथ, अम्, n. protection, defence, shelter (Ved.);<BR>a sort of wooden ledge or fender fastened round a<BR>chariot as a defence against collision, (in this sense<BR>also अस्, m.); armour, a coat of mail; a shield<BR>(made of leather &c.); a house, dwelling (so called<BR>according to Sāy. because it shelters from the cold<BR>and wind); a family or assemblage of sons &c.<BR>(Ved.); any multitude, host, swarm, flock, quantity,<BR>assemblage; (अस्), m. the Indian cuckoo; time; =<BR>निज-राष्ट्रक (?); N. of a Grāma; of a person<BR>mentioned in the Mārkaṇḍeya-Purāṇa.<BR>—वरूथ-<BR>प, अस्, m. the leader of a multitude or host, com-<BR>mander of an army, general.<BR>—वरूथ-शस्, ind. in<BR>multitudes or hosts, in heaps or masses.<BR>—वरूथा-<BR>धिप (˚थ-अध्˚), अस्, m. the leader of a multitude<BR>or army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथिन्
वरूथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing or carrying defensive<BR>arms or armour; furnished with a protecting plank<BR>or ledge (said of a chariot); having a fender; afford-<BR>ing protection or defence, sheltering; being in a<BR>carriage or chariot; surrounded by a quantity or<BR>troop (at the end of a comp., cf. ललना-व्˚); (ई),<BR>m. a guard, defender; a car; (इनी), f. a multitude,<BR>troop, army; N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—वरूथिनी-पति,<BR>इस्, m. the leader of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथ्य
वरूथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. affording protection<BR>or shelter, sheltering, protected; to be chosen or<BR>worshipped, (Sāy. = वरणीय = सम्बजनीय);<BR>domestic, favourable or auspicious to a family or<BR>house, (Sāy. = गृहार्ह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्
वरेण्, a Kvip formation fr. वरेण्यय (accord-<BR>ing to Puruṣottama-deva, cf. Uṇādi-s. III. 98).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्य|वरेण्यं|वरेण्यः
वरेण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps a kind of anom.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">Page0889-c+ 76</a>]<BR>fut. pass. part. of rt. वृ), desirable, to be wished<BR>for, eligible; excellent, superior, chief, principal, pre-<BR>eminent; (अस्), m., N. of a particular class of Manes;<BR>of a son of Bhṛgu; (आ), f., N. of Śiva's wife;<BR>(अम्), n. saffron.<BR>—वरेण्य-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>having excellent understanding, intelligent, wise,<BR>learned, (Sāy. = वरणीय-प्रज्ञ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्यय
वरेण्यय, Nom. P. वरेण्ययति, &c. (Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 98).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेय
वरेय, Nom. P. वरेयति, &c., Ved. to be a<BR>suitor, ask in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेयु
वरेयु, उस्, m., Ved. one who woos, a wooer,<BR>suitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तु
1. वर्तु in दुर्-वर्तु, q. v. (For 2. वर्तु see<BR>p. 892, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तृ
वर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who keeps back or<BR>off, one who wards off, one who resists or opposes;<BR>an encourager, propeller, (Sāy. = वारयितृ, निवार-<BR>यितृ, प्रवर्तयितृ, प्रेरक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्र
वर्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. keeping or warding off,<BR>protecting, defending; (अम्), n. a dike, dam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्ट
वरण्ट वरण्ट in जल-व्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरम्बरा
वरम्बरा वरम्बरा, f. the Nux Vomica<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरहक
वरहक वरहक, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारक|वरारकं
वरारक वरारक, अम्, n. a diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराशि|वराशिः
वराशि वराशि, coarse cloth, &c.; (see ब-<BR>रासी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासि|वरासिः
वरासि वरासि (?) = वराशि above; (इस्), m.<BR>a swordsman (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराह|वराहः
वराह वराह, अस्, m. (thought by some<BR>to be fr. rt. 1. वृह्, to tear up roots, &c.), a boar,<BR>hog, wild boar, (at the end of a comp. वराह<BR>denotes ‘superiority,’ ‘pre-eminence,’ see Gaṇa Vyā-<BR>ghrādi to Pāṇ. II. 1, 5, 6); (according to Naigh. I.<BR>10, &c.) = मेघ, a cloud; a bull; a ram; Del-<BR>phinus Gangeticus; N. of Viṣṇu in the third or<BR>boar-incarnation (in which he raised the earth from<BR>the bottom of the sea with his tusks, cf. वराहाव-<BR>तार); an array of troops in the form of a boar;<BR>N. of a Daitya; of a Muni; of Varāha-mihira; of<BR>a mountain; of one of the eighteen Dvīpas; a par-<BR>ticular measure; Cyperus Rotundus; = वाराही-कन्-<BR>द; N. of an Upaniṣad; of a Purāṇa (see वराह-<BR>पुराण); (ई), f., N. of two plants (= भद्र-<BR>मुस्ता, सूकर-कन्द); [cf. Lat. verres, porcus;<BR>Old Germ. farh, varh, farah; Mod. Germ. Fer-<BR>kel; Lith. parsa-s; Russ. porosenok; Hib. uir-<BR>chin.]<BR>—वराह-कन्द, अस्, m. an esculent root,<BR>a sort of yam.<BR>—वराह-कर्ण, अस्, m. ‘boar-eared,’<BR>epithet of a kind of arrow; N. of a Yakṣa; (ई), f.<BR>Physalis Flexuosa.<BR>—वराह-कर्णिका, f. a kind of<BR>missile weapon.<BR>—वराह-कल्प, अस्, m. the period<BR>during which Viṣṇu assumed the form of a boar.<BR>—वराह-कान्ता, f. a kind of yam.<BR>—वराह-<BR>कालिन्, ई, m. a kind of sunflower, Helianthus Annus.<BR>—वराह-क्रान्ता, f. a sort of sensitive plant, Mi-<BR>mosa Pudica; (according to some) Lycopodium<BR>Imbricatum.<BR>—वराह-दंष्ट्र, अस्, आ, m. f.<BR>‘boar-toothed,’ N. of a disease (placed among the<BR>Kṣudra-rogas).<BR>—वराह-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, or व-<BR>राह-दन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having boar's teeth.<BR>—व-<BR>राह-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a merchant (in the<BR>Kathā-sarit-s. 37, 100).<BR>—वराह-द्वादशी, f., N.<BR>of a festival in honour of the boar-incarnation of<BR>Viṣṇu (observed on the twelfth day in the light half<BR>of the month Māgha).<BR>—वराह-द्वीप, N. of a<BR>Dvīpa.<BR>—वराह-नामन्, आ, m. the plant Mimosa<BR>Pudica; an esculent root, yam.<BR>—वराह-पुराण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of the fifteenth Purāṇa celebrating Viṣṇu<BR>in his boar-incarnation; [cf. पुराण.]<BR>—वराह-<BR>मिहिर, अस्, m., N. of an astronomer (son of<BR>Āditya-dāsa and author of the Vṛhaj-jātaka, the<BR>Vṛhat-saṃhitā, &c.).<BR>—वराह-मूल, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a place having a statue of Viṣṇu in his form of<BR>a boar.<BR>—वराह-वत्, ind. like a boar.<BR>—वराह-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">Page0890-a+ 70</a>]<BR>वपुष, अम्, n. the body of a boar.<BR>—वराह-<BR>शृङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘boar-horned,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—व-<BR>राह-शैल, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—वराह-<BR>संहिता, f., N. of a work.<BR>—वराह-स्वामिन्, ई,<BR>m., N. of a mythical king.<BR>—वराहाद्रि (˚ह-अद्˚),<BR>इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—वराहावतार (˚ह-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. the boar-incarnation, the third incarna-<BR>tion of Viṣṇu, (in which Viṣṇu, in the form of a<BR>boar, raised up on one of his tusks the earth which<BR>lay buried beneath the waters when the whole world<BR>had become one ocean.)<BR>—वराहाश्व (˚ह-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Daitya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0889-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहक
वराहक, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-demon; (इका),<BR>f. Mucuna Pruritus; (अम्), n., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहयु
वराहयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. eager after boars,<BR>useful or fit for boar-hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहु|वराहुः
वराहु, उस्, m., Ved. a boar, hog; killing dis-<BR>tinguished enemies (said of the Maruts, Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 88, 5 = उत्कृष्टस्य शत्रोर् हन्तृ; other<BR>interpretations of Sāy. are उत्कृष्टानां देवता-<BR>नाम् आह्वातृ, उत्कृष्टस्य वृष्ट्य्-आहर्तृ, व-<BR>रस्य हविषो भक्षयितृ, वराहार, cf. वर;<BR>Sāy. also applies the epithet Varāhavaḥ to gods of<BR>the middle sphere).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरितृ
वरितृ वरितृ, वरिमन्. See p. 888, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्
वरिवस् वरिवस्, वरिवो-द, &c. See p. 888,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिशी
वरिशी वरिशी, f. = वडिशी, वडिश, a fish-<BR>hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष|वरिषं
वरिष वरिष, अस्, m. (a modern form of<BR>वर्ष, q. v., cf. हरिष, the separation of an र्<BR>from a following consonant by an intervening इ being<BR>not unfrequent in modern Sanskrit), rain; (आस्), f. pl.<BR>the rains, rainy season; (अम्), n. a year.<BR>—वरिषा-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘the friend of the rainy season,’ the Cā-<BR>taka bird (being supposed to drink only rain-water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठ|वरिष्ठं|वरिष्ठः
वरिष्ठ वरिष्ठ, वरीमन्, वरीयस्. See<BR>p. 888, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरी
वरी वरी, -र्यस्, f. pl. (for वरी, fem. of<BR>वर, see under वर, p. 887, col. 2), Ved. streams,<BR>rivers (according to Naigh. I. 13; cf. वार्, वारि).<BR>—वरी-दास, अस्, m., N. of the father of the Gan-<BR>dharva Nārada.<BR>—वरी-धरा, f. a kind of metre,<BR>the first, second, and fourth lines consisting of ¯¯˘¯¯<BR>˘˘¯˘¯¯, and the third ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीवर्द|वरीवर्दः|वरीवर्द्द|वरीवर्द्दः
वरीवर्द वरीवर्द, अस्, m. = बलीवर्द, an<BR>ox, bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीवृजत्
वरीवृजत् वरीवृजत्, अत्, अती, अत् (fr. Intens.<BR>of rt. वृज्), Ved. turning aside, diverting, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 24, 4 = भ्रिशं हिंसत्,<BR>excessively injuring, overthrowing repeatedly.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीवृत
वरीवृत वरीवृत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of<BR>rt. 1. वृत्), Ved. turning frequently, rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीषु|वरीषुः
वरीषु वरीषु, उस्, m., N. of Kāma-deva;<BR>[cf. रवीषु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरु
वरु वरु. See p. 889, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुक|वरुकः
वरुक वरुक, अस्, m. a species of inferior<BR>grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुट|वरुटः
वरुट वरुट, अस्, m., N. of a class of<BR>Mlecchas, (also read वरट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुड|वरुडः
वरुड, अस्, m., N. of a low mixed caste (one of<BR>the seven low castes called Antya-ja, whose occupation<BR>is splitting canes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुण|वरुणः
वरुण वरुण, &c. See p. 889, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुत्र|वरुत्रं
वरुत्र वरुत्र, वरूतृ, &c. See p. 889,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथ|वरूथं|वरूथः
वरूथ वरूथ, &c. See p. 889, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण
वरेण वरेण, अस्, m. a wasp [cf. वरोल];<BR>(आ), f. probably incorrect for वरेण्या, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्य|वरेण्यं|वरेण्यः
वरेण्य वरेण्य, वरेय. See p. 889, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोट|वरोटं|वरोटः
वरोट वरोट, अस्, m., N. of a plant (=<BR>मरुवक); (अम्), n. its flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोल|वरोलः
वरोल वरोल, अस्, m. a kind of wasp; (ई),<BR>f. a smaller kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कर|वर्करः
वर्कर वर्कर, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. rt. वृक्?),<BR>any young domestic animal; (अस्), m. a kid, lamb;<BR>a goat; pleasure, pastime, sport, mirth, festivity.<BR>—वर्कर-कर्कर, (perhaps) of all kinds or sorts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कराट|वर्कराटः
वर्कराट वर्कराट, अस्, m. a side glance,<BR>wink, leer; the rays of the ascending sun; the marks<BR>of a lover's finger-nails on the bosom of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्करीकुण्ड
वर्करीकुण्ड वर्करीकुण्ड, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कुट|वर्कुटः
वर्कुट वर्कुट, अस्, m. a pin, bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग|वर्गः|वर्ग्ग
वर्ग वर्ग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वृज्), one who<BR>excludes or removes; a class or multitude of similar<BR>things (animate or inanimate), division, group, class,<BR>tribe, troop, company, society, family, party, side,<BR>(frequently compounded with numerals, e. g. त्रि-<BR>वर्ग, any group or division consisting of three<BR>objects, a triad, cf. चतुर्-व्˚, &c.); any series or<BR>group of words classified together, a class or series of<BR>consonants in the alphabet (seven such classes being<BR>given, viz. क-वर्ग, ‘the class of Guttural letters;’<BR>च-वर्ग, ‘the Palatals;’ ट-वर्ग, ‘the Cerebrals;’<BR>त-वर्ग, ‘the Dentals;’ प-वर्ग, ‘the Labials;’<BR>य-वर्ग, ‘the Semivowels and the aspirate ह्:’ the<BR>first consonant of each Varga is called वर्ग-प्र-<BR>थम or simply प्रथम, the second वर्ग-<BR>द्वितीय or द्वितीय, &c.); everything embraced<BR>or comprehended under any department or head,<BR>everything included under a category; a sphere,<BR>province; the whole class of objects or pursuits of<BR>life, (viz. काम, अर्थ, and धर्म, see त्रि-<BR>वर्ग); a section, chapter, division of a book; a<BR>subdivision of an Adhyāya in the Ṛg-veda, (ac-<BR>cording to the arrangement which has reference to<BR>mere bulk and not authorship, the Saṃhitā consists<BR>of 8 Aṣṭakas, which are divided into 64 Adhyāyas<BR>or lessons, and these into 2006 Vargas or sections,<BR>and these into Ṛcs and Padas, see मण्डल); a<BR>similar subdivision in the Bṛhad-devatā; (in algebra)<BR>the square or second power of a number, (पञ्च-<BR>वर्ग, the square of five; cf. भिन्न-व्˚); = बल,<BR>strength (fr. rt. वृज् in a sense ‘to be strong,’ see<BR>वर्गस्; cf. ऊर्ज्; cf. also Zend verez; Gr. ϝἐργά-<BR>ζομαι); N. of a country; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras;<BR>[cf. probably Lat. vulgus.]<BR>—वर्ग-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>an operation relating to square numbers.<BR>—वर्ग-<BR>घन, अम्, n. the cube of a square.<BR>—वर्ग-<BR>घन-घात, अस्, m. the fifth power (in arithmetic).<BR>—वर्ग-पद, अम्, n. square root.<BR>—वर्ग-<BR>पाल, अस्, m. a protector of a company or tribe (of<BR>dependants &c.).<BR>—वर्ग-प्रकृति, इस्, f. an affected<BR>square (in arithmetic).<BR>—वर्ग-प्रथम, अस्, m.<BR>the first letter of a Varga, (see above.)<BR>—वर्ग-<BR>प्रशंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, praising one's own company<BR>(of relatives, dependants, &c.).<BR>—वर्ग-मूल, अम्,<BR>n. square root.<BR>—वर्ग-वर्ग, अस्, m. the square<BR>of a square, a biquadratic number.<BR>—वर्ग-वर्ग-<BR>वर्ग, अस्, m. the square of a squared square.<BR>—वर्ग-शस्, ind. according to divisions, in groups.<BR>—वर्ग-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing by a party or<BR>side, faithful or devoted to a party.<BR>—वर्गान्त्य<BR>(˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, m. the last consonant in the first five<BR>classes of consonants, a nasal.<BR>—वर्गी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, made into classes, classified, arranged; (in<BR>algebra) raised to a square, squared.<BR>—वर्गोत्तम<BR>(˚ग-उत्˚), अस्, m. the last consonant in one of the<BR>first five classes of consonants, a nasal letter; the<BR>chief or most remarkable of a class, epithet of the Ram,<BR>the Bull, and the Twins (being the first signs in a<BR>particular grouping of the sings of the zodiac).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गणा
वर्गणा, f. (fr. वर्गय), multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गय
वर्गय, Nom. P. वर्गयति, &c., to multiply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गस्
वर्गस्, Ved. = बल-नाम (Naigh. II. 9).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गिन्
वर्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, belonging to a class, devoted<BR>to a side or party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीण
वर्गीण, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the class or<BR>category of, belonging to the family or party of (at<BR>the end of a comp., cf. मद्-व्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीय|वर्गीयः
वर्गीय, अस्, आ, अम्, = वर्गीण above; belonging<BR>to a class of consonants, (क-वर्गीय, a Guttural;<BR>प-वर्गीय, a Palatal.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग्य|वर्ग्यः
वर्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a class or divi-<BR>sion, belonging to a side or party, &c.; (अस्), m. a<BR>member of a society, a colleague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज|वर्जं|वर्जः|वर्ज्ज
वर्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, free from, devoid of (at the end<BR>of comps.); excluding, excepting, with the exception<BR>of; (अस्), m. the act of leaving, abandoning; leaving<BR>out; (अम्), ind. see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जक|वर्ज्जक
वर्जक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.),<BR>excluding, exclusive of; avoiding, shunning, leaving,<BR>leaving out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जन|वर्जनं|वर्ज्जन|वर्ज्जनं
वर्जन, अम्, n. the act of excluding, avoiding,<BR>leaving, abandoning, giving up, renouncing; deser-<BR>tion; exception; the act of killing, hurting, injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जनीय|वर्ज्जनीय|वर्ज्जनीयं
वर्जनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be excluded, to be<BR>avoided or shunned, improper, censurable, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जम्|वर्ज्जम्
वर्जम्, ind. excluding, exclusive of, with the<BR>omission or exception of, without (at the end of a<BR>comp., cf. मन्त्र-व्˚); excepting, except.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जयितव्य
वर्जयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be avoided or<BR>shunned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जयितृ
वर्जयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who excludes or<BR>avoids or shuns; one who pours out, a discharger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जयित्वा|वर्ज्जयित्वा
वर्जयित्वा, ind. having excluded, having shunned<BR>or avoided, having omitted or excepted, excepting,<BR>leaving out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जित|वर्ज्जित|वर्ज्जितः
वर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, excluded, abandoned, avoided;<BR>relinquished; left, remnant; deprived of, destitute of,<BR>without (with inst. or at the end of a comp., e. g.<BR>छिद्र-व्˚, without a break, uninterrupted); ex-<BR>cepted; given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जिन्
वर्जिन्, ई, इनी, इ, avoiding, shunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्य|वर्ज्ज्यः
वर्ज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be excluded, to be shunned<BR>or avoided, to be excepted, to be left out; with the<BR>exception of, exclusive of (at the end of a comp.,<BR>e. g. त्वद्-वर्ज्यम्, except thee); (अम्), n. a point<BR>in each lunar mansion during which no business should<BR>be begun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्|वर्च्च्
वर्च् वर्च्, cl. 1. A. वर्चते, ववर्चे,<BR>वर्चितुम्, to shine, be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च|वर्च्च|वर्च्चः
वर्च, अस्, m., N. of an ancient sage (= सु-वर्-<BR>चक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चल
वर्चल in सु-वर्चला, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्|वर्च्चस्
वर्चस्, अस्, n. vital power, vigour, energy, efficacy,<BR>efficiency, activity, the illuminating power of fire or<BR>of the sun, (in the preceding senses mostly Ved.);<BR>light, lustre, brightness, brilliancy; form, figure, shape,<BR>colour; excrement, ordure, feces; (आस्), m., N. of a<BR>son of Soma; of a son of Su-tejas; of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—वर्चस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing vital<BR>energy or vigour, vigorous, active; shining, bright;<BR>containing the word वर्चस्.<BR>—वर्चस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>full of power or vigour, vigorous, active, energetic;<BR>bright; (ई), m., N. of a son of Varcas and grandson<BR>of Soma.<BR>—वर्चो-ग्रह, अस्, m. obstruction of the<BR>feces, constipation.<BR>—वर्चो-दा or वर्चो-धा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, Ved. granting power, bestowing vigour or<BR>energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस
वर्चस, अम्, n. (at the end of a comp.) = वर्चस्,<BR>(चन्द्र-वर्चस, moon-shine.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चसिन्
वर्चसिन् in ब्रह्म-व्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्क|वर्चस्कः|वर्च्चस्क|वर्च्चस्कः
वर्चस्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. power, vigour, bright-<BR>ness, &c. (= वर्चस्); ordure, excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्य
वर्चस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, bestowing vital power or<BR>vigour (Ved.); relating to वर्चस्; acting on the<BR>excrement; (आ), f., scil. इष्टका, a term applied to<BR>certain sacrificial bricks (at the laying of which a par-<BR>ticular Mantra containing the word वर्चस् is used).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चाय
वर्चाय, Nom. A. वर्चायते, -यितुम्, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चिन्
वर्चिन्, ई, m., Ved., N. of an Asura or demon<BR>(who with his family and dependants was slain by<BR>Indra [Ṛg-veda II. 14, 6], or by Indra and Viṣṇu<BR>jointly, Ṛg-veda VII. 99, 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चटी|वर्च्चटी
वर्चटी वर्चटी (?) , f. a kind of rice; a<BR>harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0890-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज|वर्जं|वर्जः|वर्ज्ज
वर्ज वर्ज, &c. See p. 890, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण्
वर्ण् वर्ण् (more properly regarded as<BR>a Nom. fr. वर्ण below), cl. 10. P. वर्-<BR>णयति (according to some also A.<BR>—ते), वर्णयाम्-<BR>आस, अववर्णत्, -त, वर्णयितुम् (anom. Inf.<BR>वर्णितुम्), to paint, colour, dye; to depict, deli-<BR>neate, picture, write, describe, enumerate, relate,<BR>tell, explain, illustrate; to praise, extol; to illumi-<BR>nate; to spread, extend; to exert one's self; to<BR>send, cast (or to grind, pound): Pass. वर्ण्यते, Aor.<BR>अवर्णि, to be coloured; to be described; to be<BR>praised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण|वर्णं|वर्णः|वर्ण्ण
वर्ण, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 10. fr.<BR>rt. वृ), a covering, cloak, mantle; a cover, covering,<BR>lid; outward appearance, exterior, form, figure;<BR>colour, hue, tint, dye, paint; lustre, beauty; a<BR>coloured cloth thrown over an elephant, housings;<BR>staining or anointing the body with coloured un-<BR>guents; dress, embellishment; gold; the purity of<BR>gold as ascertained by its streak; sort, kind, species,<BR>class, race, tribe; class of men, order, caste (as being<BR>originally perhaps connected with colour or com-<BR>plexion; but the word वर्ण is more properly<BR>applicable to the four principal classes described in<BR>Manu's code, viz. Brāhmans, Kṣatriyas, Vaiśyas,<BR>and Śūdras, and not to the numerous mixed castes<BR>of later times; the more modern word for ‘caste’<BR>is जाति); a letter, sound, vowel, syllable, word, (in<BR>these and some of the preceding senses said to be<BR>also अम्, n.); quality, property; a musical mode; a<BR>particular time in music, the order or arrangement<BR>of a song, &c.; praise, commendation, renown,<BR>fame, glory, celebrity; (in algebra) an unknown<BR>magnitude or quantity; (in arithmetic) the figure<BR>one, (according to some) a coefficient; a religious<BR>observance; (अम्), n. coloured unguent or perfume;<BR>saffron; (आ), f. a kind of plant or leguminous shrub,<BR>Cajanus Indicus; [cf. Slav. vran, ‘black;] a raven:’<BR>Russ. voronj, ‘the azure colour of swords;’ vornoi,<BR>‘black;’ voron, ‘a raven:’ Lith. warnas, ‘a raven.’]<BR>—वर्ण-कवि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Kuvera.<BR>—वर्ण-कूपिका, f. any vessel containing colour<BR>or paint, an ink-bottle, ink-stand.<BR>—वर्ण-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, causing or giving colour.<BR>—वर्ण-क्रम, अस्,<BR>m. order or succession of colours; order of castes;<BR>order or series of letters, alphabetical arrangement,<BR>the alphabet; (एण), ind. according to the order of<BR>the castes<BR>—वर्ण-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘gone to<BR>colour,’ coloured, described; algebraical.<BR>—वर्ण-<BR>चारक, अस्, m. a painter, colourer.<BR>—वर्ण-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced from castes, relating to castes.<BR>—वर्ण-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, highest in caste;<BR>(अस्), m. a Brāhman.<BR>—वर्ण-तनु, उस्, f., N. of a<BR>particular Mantra addressed to Sarasvatī.<BR>—वर्ण-<BR>तस्, ind. by or with colour &c.<BR>—वर्ण-ता, f. or<BR>वर्ण-त्व, अम्, n. the state of colour, colour,<BR>(अन्य-वर्ण-त्व, the being of another colour);<BR>the state or condition of caste, division into classes;<BR>the state or condition of a letter or sound.<BR>—वर्ण-<BR>ताल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—वर्ण-तूलि, इस्, or<BR>वर्ण-तूलिका or वर्ण-तूली, f. ‘letter-brush,’ a pen,<BR>pencil, paint-brush.<BR>—वर्ण-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving<BR>colour, colouring, dyeing; giving tribe, &c.; (अम्),<BR>n. a kind of fragrant yellow wood.<BR>—वर्ण-दातृ,<BR>ता, m. a granter or bestower of colour, &c.; (त्री), f.<BR>turmeric.<BR>—वर्ण-दूत, अस्, m. ‘a letter as a mes-<BR>senger,’ a letter, epistle.<BR>—वर्ण-दूषक, अस्, इका,<BR>अम्, violating or disturbing the distinctions of caste.<BR>—वर्ण-देशना, f. ‘instruction in sounds,’ N. of a<BR>lexicon.<BR>—वर्ण-द्वय-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consist-<BR>ing of two syllables.<BR>—वर्ण-धर्म, अस्, m. the<BR>particular duty or occupation of each caste or tribe.<BR>—वर्ण-पात, अस्, m. the dropping or omission of<BR>a letter in pronunciation.<BR>—वर्ण-पात्र, अम्, n. a<BR>vessel or receptacle for colours, paint-box, (according<BR>to some this word should be वर्ण-पत्त्र, a leaf<BR>on which a painter mixes his colours, a pallet.)<BR>—वर्ण-पुष्प, अम्, n. the blossom of the globe-<BR>amaranth; (ई), f. a kind of plant (= उष्ट्र-काण्डी).<BR>—वर्ण-पुष्पक, अस्, m. globe-amaranth.<BR>—वर्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-b" target="_blank">Page0891-b+ 81</a>]<BR>ण-प्रकर्ष, अस्, m. excellence or beauty of<BR>colour.<BR>—वर्ण-प्रबोध, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—वर्ण-प्रसादन, अम्, n. aloe wood, Agallo-<BR>chum.<BR>—वर्ण-भेदिनी, f. a kind of plant (?).<BR>—वर्ण-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of colours;<BR>consisting of letters or sounds.<BR>—वर्ण-मातृ, ता,<BR>f. ‘letter-mother,’ a pen, pencil, &c.<BR>—वर्ण-मा-<BR>तृका, f., N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>—वर्ण-मात्रा, f. a kind<BR>of metre.<BR>—वर्ण-माला, f. order or series of letters,<BR>(especially) rows of letters (written on a board or in a<BR>diagram), the alphabet.<BR>—वर्ण-राशि, इस्, m. ‘mul-<BR>titude or series of letters,’ the alphabet.<BR>—वर्ण-<BR>रेखा or वर्ण-लेखा or वर्ण-लेखिका, f. chalk<BR>or a white substance often confounded with chalk.<BR>—वर्ण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having colour, &c.; (अती),<BR>f. turmeric.<BR>—वर्ण-वर्ति, इस्, or वर्ण-वर्तिका, f. a<BR>writing-pen, pencil, &c.<BR>—वर्ण-वादिन्, ई, m. a speaker<BR>of praise, panegyrist.<BR>—वर्ण-विपर्यय, अस्, m.<BR>the change or substitution of one letter for another.<BR>—वर्ण-विलासिनी, f. turmeric.<BR>—वर्ण-विलोडक,<BR>अस्, m. a plagiarist; a house-breaker.<BR>—वर्ण-विवेक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘distinction of words,’ N. of a dictionary.<BR>—वर्ण-वृत्त, अम्, n. metre regulated by the<BR>number of syllables, (this term applies to a common<BR>class of metres, such as the Śloka or Anuṣṭubh, the<BR>Indra-vajrā, &c., which are regulated by the number<BR>of syllables in the half-line; cf. मात्रा-वृत्त.)<BR>—वर्ण-व्यवस्थिति, इस्, f. ‘caste-system,’ insti-<BR>tution of caste.<BR>—वर्ण-शिक्षा, f. instruction in<BR>sounds or letters.<BR>—वर्ण-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>longing to the best of the tribes; (अस्), m. a Brāhman<BR>or member of the highest caste.<BR>—वर्ण-संयोग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘union of tribe or caste,’ matrimonial con-<BR>nection or marriage between persons of the same<BR>caste.<BR>—वर्ण-संसर्ग, अस्, m. mixture or con-<BR>fusion of castes, matrimonial connection or marriage<BR>with members of other castes.<BR>—वर्ण-संहार,<BR>अस्, m. an assemblage or mixture of different castes,<BR>an assembly in which all the four tribes are repre-<BR>sented.<BR>—वर्ण-सङ्कर, अस्, m. mixture or blend-<BR>ing of colours; mixture or confusion of castes through<BR>intermarriage with different castes; a tribe of different<BR>origin, a man descended from a father and mother<BR>of different castes.<BR>—वर्ण-सङ्करिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who causes a mixture of castes by marrying a<BR>member of a different caste.<BR>—वर्ण-सङ्घाट or<BR>वर्ण-सङ्घात or वर्ण-समाम्नाय, अस्, m. an<BR>assemblage or aggregate of letters, the alphabet.<BR>—वर्ण-स्थान, अम्, n. the place or organ of<BR>utterance of any sound or letter, (of these there are<BR>eight, such as ‘the throat’ &c., see under स्थान.)<BR>—वर्ण-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of caste, out-<BR>cast.<BR>—वर्णागम (˚ण-आग्˚), अस्, m. the addition<BR>of a letter to a word.<BR>—वर्णाङ्का (˚ण-अङ्˚), f.<BR>‘letter-marker,’ a pen.<BR>—वर्णात्मन् (˚ण-आत्˚), आ,<BR>m. ‘consisting of sounds or letters,’ a word.<BR>—वर्-<BR>णाधिप (˚ण-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘caste-presider,’ a<BR>planet presiding over a class or caste.<BR>—वर्णान्य-<BR>त्व (˚ण-अन्˚), अम्, n. change of complexion.<BR>—वर्-<BR>णापसद (˚ण-अप्˚), अस्, m. one who goes out<BR>from caste, excluded from caste, an outcast.<BR>—वर्-<BR>णापेत (˚ण-अप्˚), अस्, m. destitute of caste, born<BR>in a mixed caste, outcast, degraded.<BR>—वर्णार्ह<BR>(˚ण-अर्˚), अस्, m. a sort of bean, Phaseolus Mungo.<BR>—वर्णाश्रम (˚ण-आश्˚), अम्, n. caste and order,<BR>class and stage of life, (see आश्रम.)<BR>—वर्णा-<BR>श्रम-धर्म, अस्, m. the duties of caste and<BR>order.<BR>—वर्णाश्रम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, or वर्णा-<BR>श्रमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessed of caste and order.<BR>—वर्-<BR>णी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become or be<BR>changed into an articulate sound.<BR>—वर्णेश्वरी<BR>(˚ण-ईश्˚), f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—वर्णोदक (˚ण-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. coloured water.<BR>—वर्णोपेत (˚ण-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having tribe or caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णक|वर्णकं|वर्णकः|वर्ण्णक
वर्णक, अस्, आ, m. f. a mask, the dress of an<BR>actor, &c.; paint, pigment; colour for painting,<BR>paint, anything for smearing on the body; (अस्), m.<BR>a panegyrist, encomiast, bard, strolling player or<BR>singer; a letter, syllable (= वर्ण, generally at the<BR>end of an adj. comp.); a kind of plant; the sandal<BR>tree, sandal; (आ), f. a kind of outer or upper gar-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">Page0891-c+ 80</a>]<BR>ment, mantle; fine gold, purity of gold; (इका), f. a<BR>mask, dress of an actor, &c.; colour; ink; a pen,<BR>pencil; (अम्), n. paint, pigment (as orpiment, in-<BR>digo, &c.); sandal; a chapter, section, division; a<BR>circle, orb; (perhaps) a model or specimen, (in this<BR>sense the gender is doubtful.)<BR>—वर्णक-दण्-<BR>डक, a painting-stick; N. of a metre.<BR>—वर्णक-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, composed or consisting of colours,<BR>painted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णकित
वर्णकित, see Gaṇa Tārakādi to Pāṇ. V. 2, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णट
वर्णट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णन|वर्णनं
वर्णन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of painting, colour-<BR>ing, delineation, description, representation, explana-<BR>tion, describing, expatiating, pointing out qualities,<BR>&c.; writing; a statement, assertion; (आ), f. praise,<BR>commendation, panegyric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णनीय
वर्णनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be painted or coloured,<BR>to be delineated or described; to be praised; to be<BR>illustrated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णयितव्य
वर्णयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be delineated or<BR>described, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णयितृ
वर्णयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who colours or de-<BR>picts or describes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णयित्वा
वर्णयित्वा, ind. having depicted, having de-<BR>scribed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णयिष्यत्
वर्णयिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to<BR>depict or describe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णस
वर्णस, see Gaṇa Tṛṇādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाट|वर्णाटः
वर्णाट, अस्, m. a painter; a singer; one who<BR>makes his living by his wife; a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाशा
वर्णाशा, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णि|वर्णिः
वर्णि (gender doubtful), gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिक|वर्णिकः
वर्णिक in ऐकवर्णिक, being of one kind, &c.;<BR>(अस्), m. a writer, scribe, secretary, (for वार्णिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णित|वर्णितः
वर्णित, अस्, आ, अम्, painted, delineated; described,<BR>explained; praised, eulogized, extolled.<BR>—वर्णित-<BR>वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, one who has painted or described,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिन्
वर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ (at the end of a comp.), having<BR>the colour or appearance of; belonging to a tribe;<BR>belonging to the caste of (e. g. ब्राह्मण-वर्णिन्,<BR>belonging to the Brāhman caste); (ई), m. a person<BR>belonging to one of the four castes; a Brāhman in<BR>the first order of life, a religious student or Brahma-<BR>cārin, q. v.; a painter; a writer, scribe; (perhaps)<BR>a kind of plant; (इनस्), m. pl., N. of a particular<BR>sect; (इनी), f. a woman belonging to one of the<BR>higher castes, caste-woman; a woman or wife in<BR>general; turmeric.<BR>—वर्णि-लिङ्गिन्, ई, m. one wear-<BR>ing the marks of a religious student.<BR>—वर्णि-वध,<BR>अस्, m. killing or occasioning the death of a man<BR>belonging to one of the four castes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिल
वर्णिल, see Gaṇa Picchādi to Pāṇ. V. 2, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण्य
1. वर्ण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be delineated or described,<BR>to be pictured, describable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण्य
2. वर्ण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to colour, useful for<BR>colour, giving colour; (अम्), n. = वर्ण, saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण्यमान
वर्ण्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being painted; being<BR>described; being extolled or praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसि|वर्णसिः
वर्णसि वर्णसि (according to Uṇādi-s. IV.<BR>107. fr. rt. वृ), water; [cf. पर्णसि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णु|वर्णुः
वर्णु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 38. fr.<BR>rt. वृ), N. of a river and of the adjacent district;<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त|वर्तः|वर्त्त
वर्त वर्त, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. वृत्), manner<BR>of existence or subsistence, livelihood, living (gene-<BR>rally at the end of comps., cf. कल्य-व्˚, बहु-व्˚,<BR>&c.).<BR>—वर्त-जन्मन्, आ, m. a cloud.<BR>—वर्त-लोह,<BR>अम्, n. a sort of brass, mixed or bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तक|वर्तकः|वर्त्तक|वर्त्तकं|वर्त्तकः
वर्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what abides or exists,<BR>abiding, existing, living; given up to, devoted or<BR>attached to (generally at the end of comps.); (अस्),<BR>m. a sort of quail; a horse's hoof; (अका, अकी, इका),<BR>f. a quail; (अम्), n. a sort of brass or bell-metal (=<BR>वर्त-लोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तन|वर्तनः|वर्त्तन|वर्त्तनं|वर्त्तनः
वर्तन, अस्, आ, अम्, = वर्तिष्णु, abiding, stay-<BR>ing; stationary, stable; causing to move or live,<BR>giving life, causing to be; (अस्), m. a dwarf; (ई), f.<BR>staying, abiding, living, life; a way, road, path;<BR>rubbing, grinding, pounding (= पेषण); sending<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">Page0892-a+ 81</a>]<BR>off, dispatching (= प्रेषण, according to some);<BR>a spindle or distaff, the ball at one end of a spindle;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of turning or moving, revolving;<BR>rolling on, moving forward, moving about; staying,<BR>abiding, living, abode, residence; causing to move;<BR>causing to be or exist; appointing; living on, sup-<BR>porting life by (with inst. or at the end of a comp.),<BR>livelihood, subsistence; earnings, hire, wages, salary;<BR>occupation, profession; intercourse, commerce, traffic;<BR>proceeding, conduct, behaviour; colouring, covering<BR>with colour (such as lac &c.); a spindle or distaff or<BR>(according to some) a ball of cotton from which the<BR>threads are spun; a ball, globe.<BR>—वर्तन-दान,<BR>अम्, n. the gift of means of subsistence or wages.<BR>—वर्तन-विनियोग, अस्, m. appointment or assign-<BR>ment of means of subsistence, i. e. of salary, wages,<BR>&c.<BR>—वर्तनाभाव (˚न-अभ्˚), अस्, m. want of<BR>means of subsistence, destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0891-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तनि|वर्तनिः|वर्त्तनि|वर्त्तनिः
वर्तनि, इस्, f. a wheel (Ved.), the circle or felloe<BR>of a wheel (Ved.); the track of a wheel (Ved.); the<BR>track of a road, way, road, course; the eyelashs<BR>[cf. वर्त्मन्]; (इस्), m. the eastern country or<BR>eastern India; = स्तोत्र, see Gaṇa Uñchādi to Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 1, 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तनिन्
वर्तनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having wheels (at the<BR>end of a comp., e. g. एक-वर्तनिन्, having one<BR>wheel; cf. सहस्र-व्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तनीय|वर्त्तनीय
वर्तनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be lived, to be stayed<BR>or dwelt in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तमान|वर्तमानः|वर्त्तमान|वर्त्तमानः
वर्तमान, अस्, आ, अम्, turning, turning round,<BR>revolving, moving; being, existing, living, being<BR>present; dwelling or abiding in; (अम्), n. presence;<BR>(in grammar) the present tense.<BR>—वर्तमान-ता,<BR>f. or वर्तमान-त्व, अम्, n. the being present, the<BR>condition of present time.<BR>—वर्तमानाक्षेप (˚न-<BR>आक्˚), अस्, m. denying or not agreeing with any pre-<BR>sent event or circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तयत्|वर्त्तयत्
वर्तयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to turn; causing to<BR>be or exist; living, subsisting; dwelling, abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तस्
वर्तस्, आस्, m., Ved. the eyelashes; [cf. वर्-<BR>तनि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ति|वर्तिः|वर्त्ति|वर्त्तिः
वर्ति, इस्, or वर्ती, f. anything rolled or wrapped<BR>round, a pad or kind of bandage on a wound;<BR>ointment, unguent, perfume for the person, rouge,<BR>eye-salve, collyrium or any cosmetic remedy pre-<BR>pared from various substances and dried in the shape<BR>of a ball or pill; the wick of a lamp; a lamp, a<BR>magical lamp; the projecting threads or unwoven<BR>ends of woven cloth, a kind of fringe; a projecting<BR>rim or protuberance round a vessel; a swelling or<BR>polypus in the throat; a swelling or protuberance<BR>formed by internal rupture, (मूत्र-वर्ति, rupture<BR>of the scrotum); a surgical instrument, bougie; a<BR>streak, line, stripe, ruled line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिक|वर्तिकः|वर्त्तिक|वर्त्तिकः
वर्तिक, अस्, m. = वर्तक, a sort of quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिका|वर्त्तिका
वर्तिका, f. (fr. वर्ति), = दीर्घ-यष्टि; the<BR>wick of a lamp [cf. योग-व्˚]; a paint-brush;<BR>colour, paint; Odina Pinnata; a quail, (see under<BR>वर्तक, p. 891, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तित|वर्त्तित
वर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be or exist, brought<BR>about, accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तितव्य|वर्त्तितव्य
वर्तितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be lived or dwelt, to<BR>be stayed, to be remained or continued, to be carried<BR>out, to be accomplished or performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तित्वा
वर्तित्वा, ind. having lived, having dwelt, having<BR>remained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिन्|वर्त्तिन्
वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, turning, moving, going; abid-<BR>ing, staying, resting, being, situated, (frequently at<BR>the end of comps., cf. हस्त-व्˚, समीप-व्˚); being or<BR>remaining fixed in any position or condition; conduct-<BR>ing one's self, behaving, acting, practising, perform-<BR>ing; acting with propriety, (अ-वर्तिन्, behaving<BR>improperly.)<BR>—वर्ति-ता, f. or वर्ति-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>conduct to be observed towards (e. g. गुरु-वर्ति-ता,<BR>proper behaviour to a superior).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिर|वर्तिरः
वर्तिर, अस्, m. = वर्तीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिष्णु|वर्त्तिष्णु|वर्त्तिष्णुः
वर्तिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, turning, revolving, circular;<BR>abiding, staying, being stationary or fixed; standing<BR>firm in battle, facing (an enemy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिष्यमाण|वर्त्तिष्यमाण|वर्त्तिष्यमाणः
वर्तिष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, about to be, about to<BR>take place, future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिस्
वर्तिस्, इस्, n., Ved. circuit, orbit; a way, road (=<BR>मार्ग, according to Mahī-dhara); a residence,<BR>dwelling, abode (= गृह, according to Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तीर|वर्तीरः
वर्तीर, अस्, m. a sort of quail or partridge; [cf.<BR>वर्तक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तु
2. वर्तु in त्रि-वर्तु, q. v. (For 1. वर्तु see<BR>p. 889, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तुल|वर्तुलः|वर्त्तुल|वर्त्तुलं|वर्त्तुलः
वर्तुल, अस्, आ, अम्, round, circular, globular,<BR>spherical; (अस्), m. a kind of pulse, a pea; a ball;<BR>N. of one of Śiva's attendants; (आ), f. a ball at the<BR>end of a spindle to assist its rotation, the ring be-<BR>longing to a spindle; (ई), f. a plant bearing a seed<BR>resembling pepper, Scindapsus Officinalis; (अम्), n.<BR>a circle; the round bulb of a kind of onion.<BR>—वर्-<BR>तुलाकार (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of circular shape,<BR>round, globular, spherical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मक
वर्त्मक at the end of an adj. comp. = वर्त्मन्<BR>below, (रक्त-वर्त्मक, अस्, m. ‘having red eye-<BR>lids, ‘a kind of bird.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मन्
वर्त्मन्, अ, n. the track of a wheel or of a road,<BR>a way, road, path, track, course, passage, (वर्त्मना,<BR>inst. c. by the way of, frequently at the end of<BR>comps., e. g. अम्बुधि-वर्त्मना, by sea; आकाश-<BR>वर्त्मना, through the air; द्वार-वर्त्मना,<BR>through the door); an edge, border; an eyelid<BR>(as encircling the eye).<BR>—वर्त्म-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>the business or science of road-making, engineer-<BR>ing.<BR>—वर्त्म-द, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school be-<BR>longing to the Atharva-veda.<BR>—वर्त्म-पात, अस्,<BR>m. deviation from the road, aberration.<BR>—वर्त्म-<BR>बन्ध or वर्त्म-विबन्धक, अस्, m. a disease<BR>attacking the eyelids and obstructing their proper<BR>movement.<BR>—वर्त्म-रोग, अस्, m. a disease of the<BR>eyelids.<BR>—वर्त्म-शर्करा, f., N. of certain hard<BR>excrescences on the eyelids.<BR>—वर्त्मायास (˚म-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘road-fatigue,’ weariness after a journey.<BR>—वर्त्मावरोध (˚म-अव्˚), अस्, m. rigidity of<BR>the eyelids (preventing them from closing).<BR>—वर्त्-<BR>मोन्मुख (˚म-उन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, looking up at the<BR>path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मनि|वर्त्मनिः
वर्त्मनि, इस्, f. = वर्तनि, a road, way, track.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्स्यत्|वर्त्स्यन्त्
1. वर्त्स्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत् (for 2. see<BR>below), about to be or take place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तरूक|वर्तरूकः|वर्त्तरूक|वर्त्तरूकः
वर्तरूक वर्तरूक, अस्, m. standing water,<BR>a pool, puddle; a crow's nest; a door-keeper, cham-<BR>berlain; N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तृ
वर्तृ वर्तृ, वर्त्र. See p. 889, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्स
वर्त्स वर्त्स, अस्, m., Ved. (according to a<BR>commentator) a swelling or fleshy formation of the<BR>gum on the inner side of the jaw; [cf. बर्स्व.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्स्य
वर्त्स्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the above swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्स्यत्|वर्त्स्यन्त्
वर्त्स्यत् 2. वर्त्स्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत् (fut.<BR>part. of rt. वृध्; for 1. see above), intending or<BR>going to augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध्
वर्ध् वर्ध्, cl. 10. P. वर्धयति (also<BR>वर्धापयति), &c., to cut, divide, shear,<BR>cut off; to fill, (in this sense perhaps rather a Caus.<BR>of rt. वृध्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध|वर्द्धं|वर्द्धः|वर्धः
1. वर्ध, अस्, m. (for 2. वर्ध see col. 3),<BR>cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धक|वर्द्धकः|वर्धकः
1. वर्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, cutting, dividing, cut-<BR>ting off, shearing [cf. माष-व्˚, श्मश्रु-व्˚]; (अस्),<BR>m. a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धकि|वर्द्धकिः|वर्धकिः
वर्धकि, इस्, or वर्धकिन्, ई, m. a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धन|वर्द्धनं|वर्द्धनः|वर्धनः
1. वर्धन, अम्, n. the act of cutting or cutting<BR>off; [cf. नाभि-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धापक
वर्धापक, अस्, m. (probably) one who performs<BR>the ceremony of cutting the umbilical cord; (perhaps)<BR>the presents distributed at this ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धापन|वर्द्धापनं|वर्धापनं
वर्धापन, अम्, n. the act of cutting or divid-<BR>ing; the cutting of the umbilical cord; the ceremony<BR>in commemoration of the day of the above rite; a<BR>birthday ceremony, festival on a birthday or any<BR>festive occasion when wishes for prosperity and other<BR>congratulatory expressions are offered, (in this sense<BR>equally referrible to the Caus. of rt. वृध्), (pro-<BR>bably) = वर्धापक, presents distributed at the<BR>ceremony of cutting the umbilical cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धापनक
वर्धापनक = वर्धापन, the cutting of the<BR>umbilical cord, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धित|वर्द्धितं
1. वर्धित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, off, divided;<BR>filled, full, (in this sense probably rather to be placed<BR>under 2. वर्धित below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध|वर्द्धं|वर्द्धः|वर्धः
वर्ध 2. वर्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वृध्; for<BR>1. वर्ध see col. 2), increasing, augmenting,<BR>strengthening; exhilarating, animating, &c.; (अस्),<BR>m. the act of increasing, giving increase or prosperity,<BR>making happy; increase, augmentation; the plant<BR>Clerodendrum Siphonanthus; (अम्), n. lead, red<BR>lead.<BR>—वर्ध-माल, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धक|वर्द्धकः|वर्धकः
2. वर्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, increasing, strength-<BR>ening, &c.; (अस्), m. the plant Clerodendrum Sipho-<BR>nanthus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धन|वर्द्धनं|वर्द्धनः|वर्धनः
2. वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, increasing, augmenting,<BR>growing, thriving; enlarging, causing to increase,<BR>magnifying, strengthening; exhilarating, making joy-<BR>ful, animating; bestowing prosperity; (अस्), m. a<BR>granter of increase, bestower of prosperity; N. of<BR>Śiva; a tooth growing over another tooth; N. of<BR>one of Skanda's attendants; of a son of Kṛṣṇa and<BR>Mitra-vindā; (ई), f. a broom, brush; a water-jar of<BR>a particular shape; (अम्), n. the act of increasing,<BR>growing, thriving; increase, growth, prosperity, suc-<BR>cess; the act of making larger, enlargement, making<BR>great, magnifying; elevation; a means of strength-<BR>ening, restorative; animation, exhilaration; rearing,<BR>educating.<BR>—वर्धन-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>tendency to increase or grow, increasing, growing.<BR>—वर्धन-सूरि, इस्, m., N. of a Jaina preceptor.<BR>—वर्धन-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a particular<BR>temple or statue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धनिका
वर्धनिका, f. (with Buddhists) a small vessel in<BR>which the sacred water is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धनीय
वर्धनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be increased or<BR>strengthened, to be made prosperous or happy.<BR>—वर्धनीय-ता, f. or वर्धनीय-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>augmentability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धमान|वर्द्धमानः|वर्धमानः
वर्धमान, अस्, आ, अम्, increasing, growing,<BR>thriving, prospering, prosperous; (अस्), m. the castor-<BR>oil plant, Ricinus Communis (so called from its<BR>vigorous growth); sweet citron, (also आ, f.); a par-<BR>ticular way of joining the hands; a kind of riddle or<BR>charade; N. of Viṣṇu; of a mountain and district<BR>(now called Bardwān; in this sense also आ, f.); of a<BR>Grāma; of various persons; of the last and most<BR>celebrated of the twenty-four Arhats of the present<BR>Ava-sarpiṇī; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a dish or platter of a particular shape (some-<BR>times used as a lid or cover to water-jars, &c.); a<BR>house having no door or entrance on the south side;<BR>a kind of mystical figure or diagram; a palace or<BR>temple built in the shape of the above diagram; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a commentary written by Vardhamāna;<BR>(आ), f. a species of Gāyatrī metre; (अम्), n. a kind<BR>of metre.<BR>—वर्धमान-द्वार, अम्, n. the gate<BR>leading to Vardhamāna, N. of a gate in Hastināpura.<BR>—वर्धमान-पुर, अम्, n. the town of Bardwān.<BR>—वर्धमान-पुरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from<BR>or born in Vardhamāna-pura.<BR>—वर्धमान-मति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—वर्धमान-मिश्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a grammarian (author of the Kā-<BR>tantra-vistara).<BR>—वर्धमानेन्दु (˚न-इन्˚), उस्,<BR>m., N. of a commentary on the Vardhamānī.<BR>—वर्-<BR>धमानेश (˚न-ईश), अस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>temple or statue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धमानक|वर्द्धमानकः|वर्धमानकः
वर्धमानक, अस्, m. = वर्धमान, a dish<BR>or saucer of a particular shape, a lid or cover; a par-<BR>ticular way of joining the hands; N. of a class of<BR>persons following a particular trade; of a district or<BR>of a people; of a serpent-demon; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धयितृ
वर्धयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who causes to grow<BR>or increase; one who rears or educates, a guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धित|वर्द्धितं
2. वर्धित, अस्, आ, अम्, increased, grown, ex-<BR>panded; [cf. 1. वर्धित above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धितृ
वर्धितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who increases<BR>or strengthens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धिन्
वर्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, increasing, growing, thriving;<BR>augmenting, strengthening, &c. (at the end of comps.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0892-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धिष्णु|वर्द्धिष्णुः
वर्धिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, increasing, growing,<BR>thriving; strengthening, enlarging, expanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध्मन्
वर्ध्मन् in अन्त्र-वर्ध्मन्, internal rupture<BR>or hernia (= अन्त्र-वृद्धि).<BR>—वर्ध्म-रोग, अस्,<BR>m. the above disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध्र|वर्द्ध्रं|वर्ध्रं
वर्ध्र, अस्, m. (also written वर्द्ध्र), a strap<BR>or leather band of any kind (Ved.); (अम्), n. a<BR>leather strap, thong, girth for securing a saddle, (also<BR>ई, f.); leather; lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध्रिका
वर्ध्रिका, f. a strap, thong; (perhaps) a person<BR>as supple or flexible as leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्पस्
वर्पस् वर्पस्, अस्, n. (said to be fr. rt. वृ),<BR>Ved. a pretended or assumed form, any form, shape,<BR>figure, aspect, (Sāy. = रूप); plot, trick, artifice,<BR>stratagem, design, scheme; (Sāy.) praise (= स्तोत्र);<BR>anything which opposes or wards off (= आवरक,<BR>वारक); [cf. perhaps Gr. μορφή.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्पणीति
वर्प-णीति, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. वर्प = वर्पस् + नीति),<BR>taking a pretended form, acting artfully; (Sāy.)<BR>mighty in warding off enemies, (Ṛg-veda III. 34,<BR>3 = युद्धे पर-प्रहाराणां निवारक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्फस्
वर्फस्, a various reading for वर्पस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्फ्
वर्फ् वर्फ्, cl. 1. P. वर्फति, &c., to go,<BR>move; to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मन्|वर्म्मन्
वर्मन् वर्मन्, अ, n. (according to some<BR>also) आ, m. (fr. rt. वृ), defensive armour, a coat of<BR>mail, armour; a bulwark, shelter, defence, protection,<BR>(frequently found at the end of the names of Kṣa-<BR>triyas); bark, rind; N. of particular preservative<BR>formulas or prayers; of the mystical syllable हुम्.<BR>—वर्म-कण्टक, अस्, m. a kind of medicinal<BR>plant, Gardenia Latifolia or Fumaria Parviflora.<BR>—वर्म-कषा, f. a kind of plant (= चर्म-क-<BR>षा).<BR>—वर्मण्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having armour<BR>or a coat of mail. mailed.<BR>—वर्म-मन्त्र, अस्, m.<BR>a particular sacred Mantra.<BR>—वर्म-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having armour or a coat of mail, mailed; (अत्),<BR>n. an unfortified (?) town.<BR>—वर्म-हर, अस्, आ or<BR>ई, अम्, wearing armour or mail, old enough to wear<BR>armour, being young or of a military age; (अस्), m.<BR>one who takes arms or spoils another of them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म|वर्म्म
वर्म, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of an adj. comp.<BR>= वर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मक
वर्मक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मण|वर्मणः
वर्मण, अस्, m. the orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्माय
वर्माय, Nom. A. वर्मायते, &c., see Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मिक
वर्मिक, अस्, आ, अम्, clad in armour, mailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मित|वर्म्मित|वर्म्मितः
वर्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, clad in armour, mailed,<BR>accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मिन्
वर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, clad in armour, mailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मि|वर्मिः|वर्म्मि|वर्म्मिः
वर्मि वर्मि, इस्, m. a kind of fish, (com-<BR>monly called वानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मुष|वर्मुषः|वर्म्मुषः
वर्मुष, अस्, m. a kind of fish, (commonly<BR>called वामिरूष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्य|वर्यः|वर्य्य|वर्य्यं|वर्य्यः
वर्य वर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वृ), to be<BR>chosen, eligible; to be wooed, to be solicited, to be<BR>asked or obtained in marriage; excellent, eminent,<BR>chief, principal, the best, (frequently at the end of<BR>comps., e. g. नर-वर्य, the best of men, an excel-<BR>lent man); (अस्), m. the god of love, Kāma-deva;<BR>(आ), f. a girl choosing her own husband (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व
वर्व वर्व, (perhaps) a particular coin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वट|वर्व्वट
वर्वट वर्वट, अस्, ई, m. f. a sort of bean,<BR>(see बर्बट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वणा|वर्व्वणा
वर्वणा वर्वणा, f. = बर्बणा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वर|वर्वरः|वर्व्वर|वर्व्वरं|वर्व्वरः
वर्वर वर्वर, अस्, आ, अम् (also written बर्-<BR>बर, q. v.; said to be fr. rt. वृ), stammering,<BR>babbling; curled, curly, woolly; (अस्), m. a man of<BR>low origin, barbarian (see बर्बर), one belonging<BR>to a degraded tribe or occupation, an outcast, a<BR>piteous wretch; curly hair; a kind of shrub, Clero-<BR>dendrum Siphonanthus; another plant (= कृष्ण-<BR>वर्वरक); a sort of worm; the noise or clash<BR>of weapons; a mode of dancing; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">Page0893-b+ 79</a>]<BR>basil; a sort of pot-herb; a particular flower; a kind<BR>of fly or bee; (ई), f. a kind of basil; a kind of fly<BR>or bee; = वर्वर, वर्वरीक; (अम्), n. = वर्-<BR>वरी, वर्वरीक; vermilion; gum-myrrh; yellow<BR>sandal-wood.<BR>—वर्वरोत्थ (˚र-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘grow-<BR>ing in the land of barbarians, ‘white sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वरक|वर्वरकं|वर्व्वरकं
वर्वरक, अम्, n. a sort of sandal-wood; [cf.<BR>कृष्ण-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वरि
वर्वरि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वरिल
वर्वरिल, see Gaṇa Kāśādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वरीक|वर्वरीकः|वर्व्वरीक|वर्व्वरीकः
वर्वरीक, अस्, m. curly or woolly hair; a kind<BR>of shrub (= ब्राह्मण-यष्टिका); a kind of basil<BR>(= अज-गन्धिका);= चर्चरीक; (अम्), n. = वर्-<BR>वर, वर्वरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वा|वर्व्वा
वर्वा, f. = वर्वरी, a kind of basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वि|वर्विः|वर्व्वि|वर्व्विः
वर्वि वर्वि, इस्, इस्, इ (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 53. fr. rt. वृ), voracious; (इस्), m. a glutton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वूर|वर्वूरः|वर्व्वूरः
वर्वूर वर्वूर, अस्, m. a kind of plant (=<BR>युगलाख्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्श्मन्
वर्श्मन् वर्श्मन्, आ, m. Zend बरेश्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष|वर्षं|वर्षः
वर्ष वर्ष, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in some senses<BR>fr. rt. वृष्, in others fr. rt. वृ, to surround, &c., cf.<BR>Uṇādi-s. III. 62), rain, raining, a shower of rain;<BR>sprinkling, effusion; seminal sprinkling or effusion;<BR>a cloud; a year, (वर्षे वर्षे, year by year, every<BR>year; आ वर्षात्, for a whole year; वर्षात्, after a year;<BR>वर्षेण, in a year, within a year); a day (?) ; a divi-<BR>sion of the world or known continent, (in this sense<BR>probably fr. rt. वृ); the plains or low land situated<BR>between certain principal mountains, (nine such<BR>divisions are enumerated, viz. Kuru, Hiraṇmaya,<BR>Ramyaka, Ilāvṛta, Hari, Ketu-mālā, Bhadrāśva,<BR>Kinnara, and Bhārata); India (= भारत-वर्ष,<BR>जम्बु-द्वीप); (आणि), n. pl. the rains, rainy season<BR>(Ved.); (आ), f. rain, the rains; a kind of plant (=<BR>कोटि-वर्षा), (आस्), f. pl. the rains, rainy season,<BR>monsoon (lasting two months according to the Hindū<BR>classification of the seasons which divides the whole<BR>year into six seasons [see ऋतु], the rains falling in<BR>some places during Śrāvaṇa and Bhādra, and in<BR>others during Bhādra and Āśvina; but the duration<BR>of the monsoon is longer in parts of India, being<BR>reckoned on the west coast from about June to<BR>October); rain; (अस्), m., N. of a grammarian;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἔρσ-η (Hom. ἐέρσ-η, ἕρσ-η, ἑρσή-εις.)]<BR>—वर्ष-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, making or pro-<BR>ducing rain; (अस्), m. a cloud; (ई), f. a cricket<BR>(this animal chirping in wet weather).<BR>—वर्ष-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n., Ved. the act of raining, &c.<BR>—वर्-<BR>ष-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring or anxious for rain.<BR>—वर्ष-कृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be done or com-<BR>pleted in a year; (अम्), n., N. of a work by Vidyā-<BR>pati.<BR>—वर्ष-केतु, उस्, m. a red-flowering Punar-<BR>navā; N. of a son of Ketu-mat.<BR>—वर्ष-कोश or<BR>वर्ष-कोष, अस्, m. ‘year-sheath,’ a month; an<BR>astrologer.<BR>—वर्ष-गणित-पद्धति, इस्, f., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—वर्ष-गिरि, इस्, m. a Varṣa moun-<BR>tain, i. e. a mountain separating a Varṣa, (see वर्-<BR>ष-पर्वत.)<BR>—वर्ष-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or<BR>produced in the rainy season.<BR>—वर्ष-धर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘restrainer of generative power,’ a eunuch or<BR>attendant on the women's apartments; a cloud.<BR>—वर्ष-धर्ष, अस्, m. a eunuch or attendant<BR>on the women's apartments.<BR>—वर्ष-निर्णिज्, क्,<BR>क्, क्, Ved. clothed with rain (said of the Maruts);<BR>(Sāy. on Ṛg-veda V. 57, 4 = वृष्टेः शोधयितृ,<BR>rain-purifier, or वर्षम् एव रूपं येषाम्, hav-<BR>ing the form of rain.)<BR>—वर्ष-पर्वत, अस्, m.<BR>one of the mountainous ranges supposed to separate<BR>the various Varṣas or divisions of the globe from<BR>each other, (six names are enumerated from north<BR>to south, viz. Hima-vat, Hema-kūṭa, Niṣadha, Nīla,<BR>Śveta, and Śṛṅgin or Śṛṅga-vat; Meru consti-<BR>tutes a seventh, and other names are given.)<BR>—वर्-<BR>ष-पाकिन्, ई, m. ‘ripening in the rains,’ the hog<BR>plum, Spondias Mangifera.<BR>—वर्ष-पुष्पा, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= सह-देवी).<BR>—वर्ष-पूग, अस्,<BR>m. a series or succession of years.<BR>—वर्ष-प्रति-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. obstruction of rain, drought.<BR>—वर्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">Page0893-c+ 80</a>]<BR>ष-प्रवेश, अस्, m. the entrance into a new year.<BR>—वर्ष-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘fond of rain,’ the Cātaka,<BR>Cuculus Melanoleucus.<BR>—वर्ष-मात्र, अम्, n. one<BR>year only.<BR>—वर्षर्तु (˚ष-ऋतु), उस्, m. the<BR>rainy season.<BR>—वर्ष-लम्भक, अस्, &c. (per-<BR>haps) marking off or bounding a Varṣa.<BR>—वर्-<BR>ष-वर, अस्, m. a eunuch, one employed in the<BR>women's apartments.<BR>—वर्ष-वर्धन, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, causing increase of years; (अम्), n. increase of<BR>years.<BR>—वर्ष-वृद्धि, इस्, f. ‘year-increase,’ birth-<BR>day.<BR>—वर्ष-शत, अम्, n. a century.<BR>—वर्षश-<BR>ताधिक (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, more than a century.<BR>—वर्ष-सहस्र, अम्, n. a thousand years.<BR>—वर्-<BR>षांश or वर्षांशक (˚ष-अं˚), अस्, m. ‘por-<BR>tion of a year, ‘a month.<BR>—वर्षा-काल, अस्, m. the<BR>rainy season.<BR>—वर्षाकालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging<BR>to or produced in the rainy season.<BR>—वर्षाघोष<BR>(˚ष-आघ्˚), अस्, m. ‘uttering cries in the rainy<BR>season, ‘a frog.<BR>—वर्षाङ्ग (˚ष-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘member or portion of a year,’ a month; (ई), f.,<BR>N. of a plant (= पुनर्-नवा).<BR>—वर्षा-प्रभञ्-<BR>जन, अस्, आ, अम्, rain-scattering; (अस्), m. a high<BR>wind, a gale.<BR>—वर्षा-भव, अस्, m. ‘produced in<BR>the rains, ‘N. of a plant (= रक्त-पुनर्नवा).<BR>—वर्षा-भू, ऊस्, m. ‘produced in the rains,’ a<BR>frog; (ऊस् or वी), f. a female frog, any small frog;<BR>hogweed; an earth-worm.<BR>—वर्षामद (˚ष-<BR>आम्˚), अस्, m. ‘krejoicing in the rains,’ a peacock.<BR>—वर्षाम्बु (˚ष-अम्˚), उ, n. rain-water.<BR>—वर्-<BR>षाम्बु-प्रवह, अस्, m. a receptacle or reservoir<BR>of rain-water.<BR>—वर्षाम्भः-पारणा-व्रत (˚ष-<BR>अम्˚), अस्, m. ‘breakfasting on rain-water,’ the Cā-<BR>taka bird, (see चातक.)<BR>—वर्षायुत (˚ष-अय्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ten thousand years.<BR>—वर्षा-रात्र, अस्, m.<BR>a night in the rainy season, rainy season.<BR>—वर्-<BR>षार्चिस् (˚ष-अर्˚), इस्, m. the planet Mars (as visible<BR>in the rainy season).<BR>—वर्षा-लङ्कायिका, f., N.<BR>of a plant (= पृक्का).<BR>—वर्षावसान (˚ष-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘the close of the rains,’ autumn, the autumnal<BR>season.<BR>—वर्षा-शरदौ, f. du. the rainy season<BR>and autumn.<BR>—वर्षा-समय, अस्, m. = वर्षा-<BR>काल.<BR>—वर्षे-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced in<BR>the rains.<BR>—वर्षैक (˚ष-एक?), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>yearly, annual.<BR>—वर्षोपल (˚ष-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘rain-stone,’ hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षक
वर्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, raining, falling like rain;<BR>= वर्ष, a year (at the end of an adj. comp., e. g.<BR>पञ्च-वर्षक, five years old).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षण|वर्षणं
वर्षण, अम्, n. raining, rain; sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षणि|वर्षणिः
वर्षणि, इस्, f. raining, &c. (= वर्षण); abid-<BR>ing, staying; action, act; a rite, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षत्|वर्षन्त्
वर्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, raining, showering, sprink-<BR>ling, (वर्षति, loc. c. while it rains, Manu IV. 38);<BR>a summer-house, (gender doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षमाण
वर्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, raining, showering,<BR>sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिक
वर्षिक, अस्, आ, अम्, raining, rainy, relating or<BR>belonging to the rains; shedding, showering, pouring<BR>down; (अम्), n. aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षित|वर्षितं
वर्षित, अम्, n. rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षितृ
वर्षितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, raining, raining down, one<BR>who pours forth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिन्
वर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, raining, showering, sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षुक|वर्षुकः
वर्षुक, अस्, ई, अम्, rainy, watery.<BR>—वर्षु-<BR>काब्द (˚क-अब्˚), अस्, m. a rainy cloud.<BR>—वर्षु-<BR>काम्बुद (˚क-अम्˚), अस्, m. a rain-cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्म|वर्ष्मं
वर्ष्म, अम्, n. body, form, = वर्ष्मन् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्मन्
वर्ष्मन्, अ, n. body, form, shape; measure;<BR>height, elevation; a handsome form; (आ, आ, अ), Ved.<BR>holding rain, (Sāy. = उदकस्य वारक.)<BR>—वर्ष्-<BR>म-वीर्य, अम्, n. vigour of body.<BR>—वर्ष्माभ<BR>(˚म-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, resembling the body or<BR>form (of anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्य
वर्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be rained or showered;<BR>to be sprinkled; of or belonging to rain, rainy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिष्ठ|वर्षिष्ठः
वर्षिष्ठ वर्षिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of<BR>वर्ष, substituted for वृद्ध; cf. वृषन्), oldest,<BR>very old; largest, greatest, strongest; best, most ex-<BR>cellent (Ved.).<BR>—वर्षिष्ठ-क्षत्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having the greatest power or might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0893-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षीयस्
वर्षीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of वृद्ध),<BR>older, very old, very aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह्
वर्ह् वर्ह् (also written बर्ह्, q. v.), cl. 1.<BR>A. वर्हते, ववर्हे, वर्हितुम्, to speak,<BR>tell; to hurt, injure, kill; to give; to protect, cover;<BR>to be pre-eminent; cl. 10. P. वर्हयति, &c., to<BR>speak; to kill, hurt; to shine; to be excellent or<BR>pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह|वर्हं
वर्ह वर्ह, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably fr. rt.<BR>2. वृह्; also written बर्ह, q. v.), a tail-feather,<BR>plumage of the tail, the tail of a bird, (especially) a<BR>peacock's tail [cf. चित्र-बर्ह]; a leaf; a retinue,<BR>train; (अम्), n. a kind of perfume (= ग्रन्थि-<BR>पर्ण, commonly called Ganthiāla).<BR>—वर्ह-केतु,<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the sons of the ninth Manu.<BR>—वर्ह-भार, अस्, m. ‘tail-burden,’ a peacock's<BR>tail; a tuft of peacock's feathers on the shaft of a<BR>lance or on the handle of a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हण|वर्हणं
वर्हण, अम्, n. (also written बर्हण), a leaf;<BR>the act of pulling out, (in this sense fr. rt. 1. वृह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हाय
वर्हाय, Nom. A. वर्हायते, &c., to be like<BR>the tail (of a peacock).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हायित
वर्हायित, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the above), resembling<BR>the eyes on a peacock's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिण|वर्हिणः
वर्हिण, अस्, m. a peacock; (अस्, आ, अम्), adorned<BR>with peacock's feathers.<BR>—वर्हिण-लक्षण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, adorned with peacock's feathers.<BR>—वर्हिण-<BR>वाज, अस्, m. an arrow feathered with a peacock's<BR>plumes.<BR>—वर्हिण-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘riding on a<BR>peacock, ‘epithet of Skanda or Kārttikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिन्
वर्हिन्, ई, m. a peacock; N. of a Deva-gandharva<BR>descended from Prādhā; of a holy sage; (इ), n. a<BR>kind of perfume (= वर्हि-पुष्प).<BR>—वर्हि-कु-<BR>सुम, अम्, n. = वर्हि-पुष्प.<BR>—वर्हि-चित्रक,<BR>अम्, n., N. of the forty-seventh Adhyāya of Varāha-<BR>mihira's Vṛhat-saṃhitā; [cf. मयूर-चित्रक.]<BR>—वर्हि-ध्वजा, f. ‘symbolized by a peacock,’ an<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—वर्हि-पुष्प, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>perfume.<BR>—वर्हि-यान, अस्, m. ‘having a peacock for<BR>a vehicle, ‘an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—वर्हि-वाहन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘riding on a peacock,’ an epithet of Gaṇeśa (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिष्ठ|वर्हिष्ठं
वर्हिष्ठ वर्हिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of<BR>वृहत्), largest, strongest, broadest, thickest, highest,<BR>very large, &c.; (अम्), n. a species of fragrant grass,<BR>Andropogon Muricatus; the resin of Pinus Longi-<BR>folia; (अम्), ind., Ved. most mighty, very loudly;<BR>(also often written बर्हिष्ठ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिस्
वर्हिस् वर्हिस्, इस्, m. n. (in the earlier lan-<BR>guage generally written बर्हिस्, q. v.), Kuśa grass,<BR>&c., (according to some only n., see बर्हिस्); sacri-<BR>fice, oblation, (according to some only m.); (इस्), m.<BR>fire, light, lustre, splendor; (इस्), n. a kind of<BR>vegetable perfume (= ग्रन्थि-पर्ण, commonly<BR>called Ganthiāla).<BR>—वर्हिः-पुष्प, &c., see बर्-<BR>हिः-पुष्प, &c., under बर्हिस्, p. 675, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्
वल् वल् [cf. rts. 1. बल्, वल्ल्, वृ], cl. 1.<BR>A. वलते, ववले, वलितुम्, to cover,<BR>enclose; to be covered or surrounded, to be enclosed;<BR>to move round in a circle; to go, approach, hasten;<BR>to be attached to, be drawn towards; to move to<BR>and fro; to increase: Caus. वलयति or वालयति,<BR>to cause to move, move; to cherish, &c. (see बाल-<BR>यति under rt. 2. बल्); [cf. Hib. falaim, ‘I hedge,<BR>enclose.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल|वलं|वलः
वल, अस्, m., Ved. a cloud (according to Naigh. I.<BR>10); N. of an Asura (fabled to have stolen the cows<BR>of the gods and to have concealed them in a cave;<BR>Indra surrounded the cave with his army and recovered<BR>the cattle; in Ṛg-veda X. 68, 9, he is said to have<BR>assumed the form of a bull and to have been destroyed<BR>by Bṛhas-pati; elsewhere he is identified with a<BR>cloud); (अम्), n. strength, force; an army, &c. (see<BR>बल).<BR>—वलं-रुज, अस्, m., Ved. one who breaks<BR>the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलग
वलग (?) , a kind of magical Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलन|वलनं
वलन, अम्, n. turning, moving round in a circle;<BR>agitation; deflection (in astronomy).<BR>—वलनांश<BR>(˚न-अं˚), अस्, m. a degree of deflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलभि|वलभिः
वलभि, इस्, m. or वलभी, f. (also written व-<BR>डभि), the wooden frame of a thatch, a roof; a<BR>turret or temporary building on the roof of a house;<BR>= वल्लभी.<BR>—वलभि-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलय|वलयं|वलयः
वलय, अस्, अम्, m. n. (sometimes written ब-<BR>लय), a bracelet, armlet, ring; a zone, girdle of a<BR>married woman; a circle, boundary, circumference,<BR>(दिग्-वलय, the circumference of the sky, the<BR>universe); (अस्), m. a boundary, enclosure, fence;<BR>a branch; sore throat, inflammation of the larynx,<BR>&c.<BR>—वलय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of or en-<BR>dowed with bracelets, &c.<BR>—वलयी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, made into a bracelet or girdle, girdled.<BR>—वलयी-<BR>कृत-वासुकि, इस्, m. ‘who has made the serpent Vā-<BR>suki his bracelet, ‘epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वलयी-भूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, become or serving as a girdle, surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलयित|वलयितं
वलयित, अस्, आ, अम्, encircled, surrounded, encom-<BR>passed, enclosed; whirling round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलयिन्
वलयिन् in ज्योतिर्-लेखा-व्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाक|वलाकः
वलाक, अस्, m. (also written बलाक, q. v.), a<BR>crane; (आ), f. a female crane; a crane in general;<BR>a flight of cranes; a mistress or loved woman; (आ,<BR>ई), f. a small kind of crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाकिन्
वलाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having or attended by cranes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलि|वलिः
वलि, इस्, m. (usually written बलि, q. v.), tax,<BR>tribute, offering, oblation, &c. (see बलि); (इस्, ई),<BR>f. a line or streak made with fragrant unguents on<BR>the person; a natural line or fold of skin, wrinkle,<BR>fold of skin over the navel (especially of women).<BR>—वलि-क्रिया, f. making offerings to all beings;<BR>making lines on the person, &c.<BR>—वलि-मुख,<BR>&c., see बलि-मुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिक|वलिकं|वलिकः
वलिक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the edge of a thatched<BR>roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलित|वलितः
वलित, अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded; moved, moving;<BR>turned, constrained; wrinkled, having wrinkles, con-<BR>tracted into wrinkles; [cf. 2. बलित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिभ|वलिभः
वलिभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having the fold of skin called<BR>वलि; having wrinkles, wrinkled, (see बलिभ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वली
वली, f. See under वलि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलीक|वलीकं
वलीक, अम्, n. the edge of a thatched roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलूक|वलूकं|वलूकः
वलूक, अम्, n. the root of a lotus; (अस्), m. a<BR>bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलूल|वलूलः
वलूल, अस्, आ, अम्, = बलूल, strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्क|वल्कं|वल्कः
वल्क, अम्, n. the bark of a tree; the scales of a<BR>fish.<BR>—वल्क-तरु, उस्, m. a species of tree (=<BR>पूग).<BR>—वल्क-द्रुम, अस्, m. a kind of birch<BR>tree.<BR>—वल्क-लोध्र, अस्, m. a kind of Lodhra<BR>tree; = पट्टिका-लोध्र.<BR>—वल्क-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having bark, having scales; wearing a bark dress;<BR>(आन्), m. a fish.<BR>—वल्क-वासस्, अस्, n. clothing<BR>made of bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कल|वल्कलं|वल्कलः
वल्कल, अस्, अम्, m. n. the bark of a tree; a<BR>garment made of bark (worn by ascetics, &c.); (आ),<BR>f. = शिला-वल्का, a medicinal substance said to be of<BR>cooling and lithonthryptic properties, (commonly<BR>called सिलाबाक्.)<BR>—वल्कल-क्षेत्र-माहात्म्य,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the praise of Valkala-kṣetra,’ part of the<BR>Adhyātma-rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—वल्कल-संवीत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, clad in bark, clothed in a bark dress.<BR>—वल्क-<BR>लाजिन-संवृत (˚ल-अज्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, clad in bark<BR>and deer-skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कलिन्
वल्कलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dressed in bark, clothed in a<BR>bark dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्किल|वल्किलः
वल्किल, अस्, m. a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कुत|वल्कुतं
वल्कुत, अम्, n. bark, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलकेश्वरतीर्थ
वलकेश्वरतीर्थ वलकेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚क-ईश्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलक्ष|वलक्षः
वलक्ष वलक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, white; (अस्), m.<BR>white, the colour; [cf. पलक्ष, बलक्ष, अव-<BR>लक्ष.]<BR>—वलक्ष-गु, उस्, m. ‘having white<BR>rays of light, ‘the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलग्न|वलग्नं|वलग्नः
वलग्न व-लग्न, अस्, अम्, m. n. = अव-<BR>लग्न, the waist, middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलन्तिका
वलन्तिका वलन्तिका, f. a particular air or<BR>mode in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलम्ब|वलंब|वलम्बः
वलम्ब व-लम्ब, अस्, m. = अव-लम्ब, a<BR>perpendicular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलम्भ
वलम्भ वलम्भ, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलासक|वलासकः
वलासक वलासक, अस्, m. (perhaps for अव-<BR>लासक), the Koïl or Indian cuckoo; a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाहक|वलाहकः
वलाहक वलाहक, अस्, m. a cloud, thunder-<BR>cloud; N. of one of the seven clouds at the destruc-<BR>tion of the world; a mountain; a kind of crane<BR>(= वलाक); N. of a Daitya; of a brother of Jayad-<BR>ratha; one of the Nāgas; one of the four horses of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिर|वलिरः
वलिर वलिर, अस्, आ, अम्, squint-eyed,<BR>squinting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिश|वलिशं
वलिश वलिश, अम्, ई, n. f. or वलिशि, इस्, f. a<BR>fish-hook; [cf. वडिश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0894-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिशान|वलिशानः
