वह्
वह् 1. वह् (connected with rt. 1. ऊह्,<BR>q. v.; cf. 1. ऊढ), cl. 1. P. A. वहति,<BR>-ते, उवाह (2nd sing. उवहिथ or उवोढ), ऊहे,<BR>वक्ष्यति (ep. also वहिष्यति), -ते, अवाक्षीत् (3rd<BR>du. अवोढाम्, 3rd pl. अवाक्षुस्), अवोढ (1st sing.<BR>अवक्षि, 3rd du. अवक्षाताम्, 3rd pl. अवक्षत),<BR>Prec. उह्यात्, वक्षीष्ट (Ved. forms वक्षि, वक्-<BR>षति, वक्ष्व), वोढुम् (Ved. Inf. वहध्यै,<BR>वोऌहवे, वोढवे, see यज्ञ-व्˚), to bear, carry, con-<BR>vey, transport; to draw, lead; to convey in a carriage,<BR>&c.; to carry away, carry off; to bring or carry near;<BR>to take in marriage, marry a wife; to be carried or<BR>borne along, proceed, move; to feel, experience,<BR>have; to flow; to breathe; to spit out, vomit (pro-<BR>bably for rt. वम्): Pass. उह्यते, Aor. अवाहि, to be<BR>borne or carried; to ride, (Pres. part. उह्यत्, अन्,<BR>अन्ती, अत्, or उह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being carried<BR>or borne): Caus. वाहयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अवी-<BR>वहत्, to cause to bear or carry, cause to convey or<BR>draw; to cause to be conveyed (A.); to ship or place<BR>in a boat; to cause to be brought or led; to cause<BR>to take in marriage; to cause to proceed or move,<BR>guide, drive, impel, direct; to travel (A.), proceed, go;<BR>to go to, visit; to carry out, perform, finish: Pass. of<BR>Caus. वाह्यते, to be caused to bear or carry, to be<BR>made to convey: Desid. विवक्षति, -ते: Intens.<BR>वावह्यते, वावोढि; [cf. Gr. ὄχο-ς, ὀχέ-ο-μαι,<BR>ὀχεύ-ω, ὄχη-μα, ὄχ-λο-ς, ὀχ-λέ-ω, ὀχ-ετό-ς, αὐχήν,<BR>ἄχθος; Lat. veho, vehi-culu-m, vehe-s, vectura,<BR>via, vexo, vêlu-m (for veh-lu-m), uxor, probably<BR>bajulus; Goth. ga-vig-an, ga-vag-ja, vêg-s, vig-s;<BR>Old Germ. wag-an, wâga; Angl. Sax. wegan, weg,<BR>wœgan, weddian; Slav. vez-a, vozu, vez-lo; Lith.<BR>vez-u, vez-ima-s, veze; Hib. feon, ‘a carriage.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्
2. वह् in वज्र-वह्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह|वहः
वह, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing, carrying, conveying,<BR>bringing (often at the end of comps., e. g. पुष्प-<BR>गन्ध-व्˚, ‘bringing flowers and perfumes,’ and<BR>sometimes with a passive sense, cf. दुर्-व्˚, सु-व्˚);<BR>one who bears or carries; (अस्), m. the act of bearing<BR>or conveying; any vehicle or means of conveyance<BR>(as a car, carriage, horse, &c.); the shoulder of an<BR>ox; a road, way; a measure of four Droṇas; air,<BR>wind; any male river; a current; (आ), f. a river,<BR>stream in general.<BR>—वहं-लिह, अस्, m. ‘shoulder-<BR>licking (?), ‘an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहत्
वहत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bearing, carrying, conveying;<BR>wearing, taking, assuming; possessing, having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहत|वहतः
वहत, अस्, m. an ox; a traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहति|वहतिः
वहति, इस्, m. an ox; air, wind; a friend, coun-<BR>sellor; (ई), f. a river, stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहतु|वहतुः
वहतु, उस्, m. an ox; a traveller (Ved.); a mar-<BR>riage, bridal, nuptial ceremony, (Sāy. = विवाह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन|वहनं
वहन, अम्, n. the act of bearing, carrying, con-<BR>veying; flowing (as a stream); any vehicle or means<BR>of conveyance; a raft, float, boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहनीय
वहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be carried or borne;<BR>portable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन्त|वहंत|वहंतः|वहन्तः
वहन्त, अस्, m. air, wind; an infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहमान
वहमान, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing, carrying, con-<BR>veying, being carried or riding on (with inst.); pos-<BR>sessing, having; flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहल|वहलः
वहल, अम्, n. a raft, float; (अस्, आ, अम्), hard,<BR>firm, compact, &c., (in this sense more correctly<BR>written बहल, q. v.)<BR>—वहल-गन्ध, &c., see<BR>बहल-ग्˚, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहित|वहितः
वहित, अस्, आ, अम्, borne, conveyed, carried;<BR>obtained; known, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहित्र|वहित्रं
वहित्र or वहित्रक, अम्, n. a raft, float, boat,<BR>vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिन्
वहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bearing, conveying; (इनी), f. a<BR>boat, vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्ठ
वहिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. carrying heavy bur-<BR>dens, bearing much, (Sāy. = वोढृ-तम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहीरु
वहीरु, उस्, m. (?), a tendon, nerve, muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्नि|वह्निः
वह्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, bearing, carrying, bringing (Ved.);<BR>luminous, bright (Ved.); (इस्), m. one who bears an<BR>oblation (to the gods), a sacrificer, priest (Ved.);<BR>‘borne along,’ an epithet of the Maruts (Ved.); of<BR>Soma (Ved.); of the gods in general (Ved.); fire<BR>(= Agni); a horse (Naigh. I. 14); any vehicle;<BR>lead-wort, Plumbago Zeylanica; the marking-nut<BR>plant; the fire of the stomach, digestive faculty,<BR>gastric fluid; digestion, appetite.<BR>—वह्नि-कर, अस्,<BR>आ or ई, अम्, making fire, igniting, lighting; pro-<BR>moting digestion, giving appetite, stomachic; (ई), f.,<BR>N. of the tree Grislea Tomentosa.<BR>—वह्नि-काष्ठ,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of Agallochum used as incense.<BR>—वह्-<BR>नि-गन्ध, अस्, m. incense; resin.<BR>—वह्नि-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, m. a bamboo; a sort of Mimosa, Mimosa Suma.<BR>—वह्नि-चक्रा, f. a kind of plant (= कलिकारी).<BR>—वह्नि-ज्वाला, f., N. of the plant Grislea Tomen-<BR>tosa.<BR>—वह्नि-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most luminous,<BR>brightest.<BR>—वह्नि-तस्कर-पार्थिव, आस्, m. pl. fire,<BR>robbers, and the king.<BR>—वह्नि-दमनी, f., N. of<BR>a plant.<BR>—वह्नि-दाह-समुद्भव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>produced by burning.<BR>—वह्नि-दीपक, अस्, m. saf-<BR>flower; (इका), f. = अज-मोदा.<BR>—वह्नि-नामन्, आ,<BR>m. ‘called after fire,’ the marking-nut plant; lead-<BR>wort.<BR>—वह्नि-नी, f., N. of a plant, Nardostachys<BR>Jatamansi.<BR>—वह्नि-पुराण, N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—वह्नि-पुष्पी, f., N. of a plant (= धातकी).<BR>—वह्नि-भोग्य, अम्, n. ‘that which is to be con-<BR>sumed by fire,’ ghee or clarified butter.<BR>—वह्नि-<BR>मन्थ, अस्, m. the tree Premna Spinosa (the wood<BR>of which is used to procure fire by attrition).<BR>—वह्-<BR>नि-मारक, अम्, n. fire-destroyer.<BR>—वह्नि-मित्र,<BR>अस्, m. ‘friend of fire,’ air, wind.<BR>—वह्नि-रेतस्, आस्,<BR>m. ‘fire-semen,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वह्नि-लोह<BR>or वह्नि-लोहक, अम्, n. ‘fire-like iron,’ copper.<BR>—वह्नि-वधू, ऊस्, f. the wife of Agni or Fire.<BR>—वह्नि-वर्ण, अम्, n. ‘fire-coloured,’ the red<BR>water-lily.<BR>—वह्नि-वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘fire-beloved,’<BR>resin.<BR>—वह्नि-वीज, अम्, n. ‘fire-seed,’ gold; the<BR>common lime (= निम्बूक); = रं-वीज, i. e. the<BR>mystical syllable रम् (repeated as the peculiar prayer<BR>of fire in the Tantra system).<BR>—वह्नि-शिख, अम्,<BR>n. safflower, Carthamus Tinctorius; saffron; (आ), f.<BR>a pot-herb, Echites Dichotoma; [cf. अग्नि-शिखा.]<BR>—वह्नि-शिखर, अस्, m. the flower Celosia Cris-<BR>tata or cock's comb.<BR>—वह्नि-सख, अस्, m. ‘friend<BR>of fire, ‘the wind; a kind of plant (= जीरक).<BR>—वह्नि-सञ्ज्ञक, अस्, m. = चित्रक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्य|वह्यं
वह्य, अम्, n. a vehicle, carriage, conveyance of<BR>any sort, cart, &c.; (आ), f. the wife of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिस्
वहिस् वहिस्, ind. (in the earlier language<BR>usually written बहिस्, q. v.; according to some con-<BR>nected with rt. 1. वह्, according to others with<BR>अवधि), out, without, outwards, outside; on the<BR>outside, out-of-doors, in the open air, outside of<BR>(with abl. or gen.); besides, except (with abl. or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-c" target="_blank">Page0898-c+ 81</a>]<BR>gen.; in Manu IV. 72. वहिस् is said to mean ‘except<BR>on the hair’); apart, separately, away from others;<BR>वहिर् भू, to become or be on the outside, go<BR>outside.<BR>—वहिः-कुटी-चर, see वहिष्-कुटी-चर.<BR>—वहिः-शीत, अस्, आ, अम्, cool or cooling on the out-<BR>side.<BR>—वहिः-श्रि, ind., Ved. externally, in an external<BR>direction (?) .<BR>—वहिः-संस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situated<BR>outside (the town).<BR>—वहिः-स्थ or वहिः-स्थित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or वहिः-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being out-<BR>side, external, outer.<BR>—वहिर्-अङ्ग, अस्, m. an<BR>external part, outer limb or member; property (as<BR>an external possession); a stranger, indifferent person;<BR>the preliminary part of a religious ceremony; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), relating to the exterior, external, exterior, un-<BR>essential, (opposed to अन्तर्-अङ्ग, q. v.)<BR>—वहिर्-<BR>अङ्ग-ता, f. or वहिरङ्ग-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>of being external, exteriority, externality.<BR>—वहिर्-<BR>अन्ते, ind. externally and internally.<BR>—वहिर्-अर्गल,<BR>अस्, m. an outer bolt or bar.<BR>—वहिर्-अर्थ, अस्, m.<BR>an external object.<BR>—वहिर्-इन्द्रिय, अम्, n. an<BR>outer organ, outward sense, organ of sense or per-<BR>ception (as the eye &c.), an organ of action (as the<BR>hand &c.).<BR>—वहिर्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone out or<BR>forth, manifested in an external or bodily form.<BR>—वहिर्-गमन, अम्, n. the act of going out or<BR>forth.<BR>—वहिर्-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going out or forth.<BR>—वहिर्-गिरि, इस्, m. a country situated on the other<BR>side of a mountain; (अयस्), m. pl. the inhabitants<BR>of such a country.<BR>—वहिर्-गेहम्, ind. outside the<BR>house, out-of-doors, abroad.<BR>—वहिर्-ग्रामम्, ind.<BR>outside a village.<BR>—वहिर्-देश, अस्, m. a foreign<BR>country; a place without a town or village; the out-<BR>skirts of a town or village.<BR>—वहिर्-द्वार, अम्, n.<BR>an outer gate; the space outside a gate or door.<BR>—वहिर्द्वार-प्रकोष्ठक, अम्, n. a covered<BR>terrace in front of the door of a house, a portico or<BR>porch before a house.<BR>—वहिर्-ध्वजा, f., N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—वहिर्-निःसारण, अम्, n. the act of re-<BR>moving or turning out, expulsion, removal.<BR>—व-<BR>हिर्-निर्गमन, अम्, n. the act of going out or<BR>away from (with abl.).<BR>—वहिर्-भव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being on the outside, produced externally, external,<BR>(opposed to अन्तर्-ज, q. v.)<BR>—वहिर्-भवन, अम्,<BR>n. the being out or outside, the coming out, emana-<BR>tion.<BR>—वहिर्-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being out, being<BR>outside, expelled, excluded; expired (said of a period<BR>of time); inattentive, careless.<BR>—वहिर्-मनस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, external to the mind, external.<BR>—वहिर्-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, one who turns his face away,<BR>turning away from, indifferent to, averse from;<BR>greatly devoted to external things; coming out of<BR>the mouth, (opposed to अन्तर्-मुख); (अस्), m.<BR>a deity, (in this sense incorrect for बर्हिर्-मुख.)<BR>—वहिर्-यात्रा, f. or वहिर्-यान, अम्, n. a journey<BR>out, excursion.<BR>—वहिर्-यूति, इस्, इस्, इ, placed or<BR>fastened outside.<BR>—वहिर्-योग, अस्, आ, अम्, relating<BR>to the exterior, external; (अस्), m. a proper N.;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. Vahir-yoga's descendants.<BR>—वहिर्-लम्-<BR>ब, अस्, आ, अम्, having the perpendicular outside, obtuse-<BR>angular; (आ), f. an obtuse-angled triangle (whose<BR>perpendicular falls outside).<BR>—वहिर्-लापिका, f. a kind<BR>of enigma, one not containing a solution, (opposed<BR>to अन्तर्-लापिका.)<BR>—वहिर्-लोम, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>hair outside, having the hair turned outwards.<BR>—व-<BR>हिर्-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being on the outside.<BR>—वहिर्-<BR>वासस्, अस्, n. an outer or upper garment, (opposed<BR>to अन्तर्-वासस्.)<BR>—वहिर्-विकार, अस्, m. ‘outward<BR>change or disfigurement, ‘syphilis.<BR>—वहिर्-वृत्ति,<BR>इस्, f. occupation with external objects.<BR>—वहिर्-वेदि,<BR>इस्, f. the space outside the Vedi or sacrificial altar; वहिर्-<BR>वेद्याम् or वहिर्-वेदि, ind. outside the sacrificial altar.<BR>—वहिर्-वेदिक, अस्, आ, अम्, performed or taking<BR>place outside the Vedi.<BR>—वहिर्-व्यसन, अम्, n.<BR>‘external vice,’ evil practices or dissolute conduct out-<BR>of-doors; licentiousness, immorality.<BR>—वहिर्-व्य-<BR>सनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, practising vice, addicted to immoral<BR>practices, dissolute.<BR>—वहिश्-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going<BR>out, bustling about outside, looking after external<BR>matters; being on the outside, external, foreign;<BR>(अस्), m. ‘crawling out of its shell,’ a crab.<BR>—वहिष्-<BR>करण, अम्, n. an outer or external organ; expelling,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">Page0899-a+ 78</a>]<BR>expulsion, excluding, excepting; expulsion from (with<BR>abl.).<BR>—वहिष्-कार, अस्, m. putting or placing out-<BR>side, expulsion, exclusion.<BR>—वहिष्-कार्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fit to be removed or expelled, deserving re-<BR>jection.<BR>—वहिष्-कुटी-चर, अस्, m. a crab (as<BR>‘crawling out of its shell,’ cf. वहिश्-चर).<BR>—व-<BR>हिष्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, turned out, thrust out,<BR>expelled, excluded, rejected, excommunicated; ex-<BR>cepted; manifested in an external form.<BR>—वहिष्-<BR>कृति, इस्, f. = वहिष्-कार.<BR>—वहिष्-क्रिय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, excluded from sacred rites.<BR>—वहिष्-क्रिया, f.<BR>an outer act, external rite or ceremony.<BR>—वहिष्-<BR>पट, an upper or outer garment.<BR>—वहिष्-प्राकार,<BR>अस्, m. an outer wall or rampart.<BR>—वहिष्-प्राण,<BR>अस्, m. external breath or life, anything as dear as<BR>life, anything near the heart; money; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having the breath or life existing outside (i. e. having<BR>one dear as life existing externally to one's self).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्क
वहिष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, outer, external.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्टात्
वहिष्टात्, ind. on the outside, without, abroad.<BR>—वहिष्टाज्-ज्योतिस्, इस्, f. epithet of a Triṣṭubh the<BR>last Pāda of which contains eight syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहेडुक|वहेडुकः
वहेडुक वहेडुक, अस्, m. the Vibhītaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्नि|वह्निः
वह्नि वह्नि, वह्नि-कर, वह्य, &c. See<BR>p. 898, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्लि
वह्लि वह्लि, इस्, m., N. of a country, (more<BR>correctly written बल्हि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्लिक
वह्लिक, वह्लीक. See बल्हिक, बल्हीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा 1. वा, ind. (excluded, like the Lat. ve,<BR>from the first place in a sentence, and generally com-<BR>ing immediately after the word to which it refers),<BR>as, like, so (not commonly used in this sense); either,<BR>or, whether; either — or not, i. e. optionally, (in<BR>grammar the word वा is placed after a rule to<BR>denote its being optional); else; or if, but if; but;<BR>only, no other; indeed, truly, even, very (in as-<BR>severation or confirmation); and (as a conjunction);<BR>वा is also sometimes used as an expletive; it is also<BR>somewhat pleonastically or perhaps emphatically added<BR>to an interrogative pronoun especially when followed<BR>by the negative न (e. g. को वा न, के वा न, which<BR>may be translated by ‘very on,’ ‘all’); वा — वा,<BR>either — or; on the one side — on the other; अथ वा,<BR>or else; or, or if, or rather, but, certainly, see अथ;<BR>न वा, or not; यदि वा, or if, or whether, whether,<BR>whether or no, see under यदि, p. 808; यद् वा,<BR>or, or else; किं वा, whether? किं वा — न वा, is<BR>it — or not? see under किम्; [cf. Gr. ἤ; Lat. ve.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा 2. वा (according to some originally<BR>अव् + आ, cf. ἄημι), cl. 2. P. वाति, ववौ,<BR>वास्यति, अवासीत्, वातुम्, to blow (as the wind); to<BR>move, go; to pierce, strike, hurt, injure; cl. 4. P.<BR>वायति, &c., to be dried up (by the wind), become<BR>dry or languid, to dry, (in this sense, according to<BR>some, the form of the rt. is वै); to be extin-<BR>guished; (according to some authorities also cl. 10.<BR>P. in the senses, to be happy; to go, move; to<BR>worship): Caus. वापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>blow, cause to move, excite; to cut, shave, (in<BR>this sense confounded with Caus. of rt. वप्):<BR>Desid. विवासति, Ved. to wish to blow, wish to fan;<BR>to favour, honour, worship (Naigh. III. 5); to be<BR>favourable or kind towards; to bestow, grant; [cf.<BR>Zend vā: Gr. .α-ω, ἄ-ος, ἄη-μι, ἀή-τη-ς, ἄ-ελλα,<BR>αὔ-ρα, ἀ-ήρ, ἀ-ΐ-σθ-ω, ἀά-ζ-ω, ἆσθ-μα, μετέωρος,<BR>ἀείρω, ἄρδην, ἀρτάω, ἀορτήρ, αἰωρέω (probably<BR>also) αὐλός, οὖρος; ἀϋτμήν (= आत्मन्), ἀτμή: Lat.<BR>ven-tu-s, a-er, probably also vanus, vapor (fr. the<BR>Caus.): Goth. vaian, vind-s: Old Germ. wa-dal,<BR>‘a fan;’ wat, wait, waiet, wahet, ‘to blow:’ Slav.<BR>ve-j-a: Lith. ve-je-s, ‘wind;’ o-ra-s: Hib. bad,<BR>‘wind:’ Pers. bād.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्
1. वात्, आन्, आती or आन्ती, आत् (for rt. 2. वात् see<BR>p. 902, col. 2), blowing; going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
1. वात, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. वात see p. 902, col. 2),<BR>blown; (अस्), m. wind, air, breeze; the god of the wind<BR>(usually called Vāyu, q. v., but addressed under the<BR>name Vāta in Ṛg-veda X. 168. and X. 186); wind<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-b" target="_blank">Page0899-b+ 81</a>]<BR>or air as one of the humors of the body; morbid<BR>affection of the windy humor, rheumatism, gout,<BR>inflammation of the joints; [cf. Gr. ἐτώσιος; Lat.<BR>ventus; Goth. vinds; Angl. Sax. wind, weder;<BR>Old Germ. weder.]<BR>—वात-कर्मन्, अ, n. breaking<BR>wind.<BR>—वात-कुण्डलिका, f. scanty and painful flow<BR>of urine.<BR>—वात-कुम्भ, अस्, m. the part of an<BR>elephant's forehead below the frontal sinuses.<BR>—वात-<BR>केतु, उस्, m. ‘wind-sign,’ dust.<BR>—वात-केलि, इस्, m.<BR>amorous sport or converse, speaking in whispers;<BR>the marks of finger-nails on a lover's person.<BR>—वात-<BR>गामिन्, ई, m. ‘wind-goer,’ a bird.<BR>—वात-गुल्म,<BR>अस्, m. ‘wind-cluster,’ a gale, high wind; acute gout<BR>or rheumatism.<BR>—वात-गोपा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing the Wind as protector.<BR>—वात-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘wind-seized,’ epileptic; rheumatic.<BR>—वात-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, removing disorders of the wind;<BR>(ई), f. the shrub Hedysarum Gangeticum.<BR>—वात-<BR>चोदित, अस्, आ, अम्, driven by the wind.<BR>—वात-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, produced by or arising from wind.<BR>—वा-<BR>त-जव, अस्, आ, अम्, fleet as the wind.<BR>—वात-जूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. impelled or driven by the wind.<BR>—वात-जूति, इस्, m., N. of the author of Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 136, 2 (having the patronymic Vātaraśana).<BR>—वात-ज्वर, अस्, m. ‘wind-fever,’ fever arising<BR>from vitiated wind.<BR>—वातज्वर-प्रतीकार, अस्, m.<BR>the remedying or counteraction of the above disease.<BR>—वात-तूल, अम्, n. cottony or flocculent seeds<BR>floating in the air.<BR>—वात-त्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. bril-<BR>liant or radiant with the wind (said of the Maruts).<BR>—वात-थुडा, f. (?) , a gale, a high wind; acute gout<BR>or rheumatism; a disease, a sort of small-pox; a<BR>handsome woman.<BR>—वात-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘wind-<BR>sign, ‘a cloud.<BR>—वातन्-धम, see Vopa-deva XXVI.<BR>55.<BR>—वात-पित्त, अम्, n. ‘wind-bile,’ a form of<BR>rheumatism or rheumatic fever.<BR>—वातपित्त-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced by the above disease.<BR>—वात-<BR>पित्तज-शूल, अम्, n. a form of the disease called<BR>शूल.<BR>—वात-पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son of the wind,’ N. of<BR>Bhīma; the monkey Hanumat; a cheat, swindler.<BR>—वात-पोथ or वात-पोथक, अस्, m. the Palāśa<BR>tree, Butea Frondosa.<BR>—वात-प्रकोप, अस्, m. (in<BR>medicine) excess of wind.<BR>—वात-प्रबल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, (in medicine) having an excess of wind.<BR>—वात-<BR>प्रमी, ईस्, m. f. ‘wind-surpassing,’ a swift antelope,<BR>(see Gram. 126. f.)<BR>—वात-फुल्ल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘wind-inflated,’ swollen or puffed up with wind.<BR>—वात-फुल्लान्त्र (˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘wind-swollen<BR>stomach, ‘flatulence in the bowels, colic.<BR>—वातम्-<BR>अज, अस्, आ, अम्, going towards or against the wind;<BR>(अस्), m. a swift antelope.<BR>—वात-मण्डली, f. ‘wind-<BR>circle, ‘a whirlwind.<BR>—वात-मृग, अस्, m. ‘wind-<BR>deer, ‘a swift antelope.<BR>—वात-रंह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or वात-रंहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the impetuosity<BR>of the wind, swift as the wind.<BR>—वात-रक्त, अम्,<BR>n. acute gout or rheumatism (ascribed to a vitiated<BR>state of the ‘wind and blood’).<BR>—वातरक्त-घ्न,<BR>अस्, m. ‘destroying or curing the disease Vāta-rakta,’<BR>a plant or shrub (= कुक्कुर, commonly called Ku-<BR>kurmurā).<BR>—वातरक्तारि (˚त-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy<BR>of Vāta-rakta, ‘a plant, Menispermum Glabrum (=<BR>पित्त-घ्नी).<BR>—वात-रङ्ग, अस्, m. the fig-tree (= अश्-<BR>वत्थ).<BR>—वात-रूष, अस्, m. [cf. rt. रूष्], a gale,<BR>storm; the rainbow; a bribe.<BR>—वात-रोग, अस्, m.<BR>‘wind-disease,’ rheumatism, gout.<BR>—वातरोगिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, afflicted with gout or rheumatism, rheumatic.<BR>—वातर्द्धि (˚त-ऋद्˚), इस्, m. a sort of cup made<BR>of wood and iron or a vessel made of wood with<BR>an iron stand; a mace, a club or stick bound with<BR>iron.<BR>—वात-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, windy, gusty.<BR>—वात-<BR>वलासक, अस्, m. nervous fever (?) .<BR>—वात-वस्ति,<BR>इस्, f. suppression of urine.<BR>—वात-विकार, अस्, m.<BR>disease of the wind, rheumatism.<BR>—वात-वृद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. swelled testicle.<BR>—वात-वेग, अस्, m. ‘fleet as<BR>wind, ‘N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—वात-वैरिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘enemy of wind-disease,’ the castor-oil tree,<BR>&c.; [cf. वातारि.]<BR>—वात-व्याधि, इस्, m. any mor-<BR>bid affection of the wind.<BR>—वातव्याधि-चिकित्सा,<BR>f. the cure of the above disease.<BR>—वातव्याधि-नि-<BR>दान, अम्, n. the cause of the above disease.<BR>—वात-<BR>शीर्ष, अम्, n. ‘wind-source,’ the lower belly.<BR>—वा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">Page0899-c+ 81</a>]<BR>त-शूल, अम्, n. ‘wind-pain,’ colic with flatulence.<BR>—वात-शोणित, अम्, n. acute gout or rheumatism<BR>(ascribed to a vitiated state of ‘the wind and blood’).<BR>—वात-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, suffering from wind-<BR>disease, gouty, rheumatic; bearing wind, able to<BR>resist gusts and gales.<BR>—वात-सारथि, इस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing the wind for a charioteer, ‘Agni or Fire.<BR>—वा-<BR>त-स्कन्ध, अम्, n. the part of the atmosphere<BR>where the wind blows.<BR>—वात-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sounding or roaring like the wind.<BR>—वात-हन्, आ,<BR>घ्नी, अ, = वात-घ्न, q. v.<BR>—वाताट (˚त-अट), अस्,<BR>m. ‘wind-goer,’ a horse of the sun; an antelope.<BR>—वा-<BR>ताण्ड (˚त-अण्˚), अस्, m. a disease of the testicles.<BR>—वातातिसार (˚त-अत्˚), अस्, m. dysentery produced<BR>by vitiated wind.<BR>—वाताद (˚त-आद), अस्, m. a kind<BR>of fruit tree.<BR>—वातानुलोमन (˚त-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>forcing the wind in the right direction or downwards<BR>(as in inflating the lungs).<BR>—वाता-पर्जन्या, m. du.,<BR>Ved. the gods Vāta and Parjanya (who are invoked<BR>together in Ṛg-veda X. 66, 10, &c.).<BR>—वातापि<BR>(˚त-आपि?), इस्, m., N. of an Asura (devoured by<BR>Agastya).<BR>—वातापि-द्विष्, ट्, or वातापि-सूदन, अस्,<BR>or वातापि-हन्, आ, m. ‘destroyer of the Asura Vā-<BR>tāpi, ‘epithet of the Muni Agastya.<BR>—वाताप्य (˚त-<BR>आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. swelling or filling with air or<BR>wind, fermenting; (अम्), n. fermentation; water;<BR>Soma; (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IX. 93, 5 =<BR>उदक.)<BR>—वातामोदा (˚त-आम्˚), f. musk.<BR>—वाताय<BR>(˚त-अय), अम्, n. ‘wind-going,’ a leaf.<BR>—वातायन<BR>(˚त-अय्˚), अम्, n. ‘wind-passage, air-passage,’ a window,<BR>air-hole, loop-hole; a porch, portico; a covered shed,<BR>pavilion; (अस्), m. a horse; a patronymic of Anila<BR>(author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 168); of Ula<BR>(author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 186).<BR>—वातायन-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or being at the window.<BR>—वातायु (˚त-अयु), उस्, m. an antelope, deer.<BR>—वातारि (˚त-अरि), इस्, f. ‘enemy of wind-disease,’<BR>the castor-oil tree; a plant, Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>—वाताली (˚त-आली), f. a whirlwind, gale.<BR>—वाताश्व<BR>(˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m. a swift horse or one of good breed.<BR>—वातासह (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, suffering from<BR>wind-disease, rheumatic, gouty.<BR>—वाताहत (˚त-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, stirred or shaken by the wind;<BR>struck by wind-disease, affected by rheumatism.<BR>—वाताहत-नौ, नौस्, f. a ship tossed by the<BR>winds.<BR>—वाताहति (˚त-आह्˚), इस्, f. ‘wind-stroke,’ a<BR>violent gust of wind, the action of the wind; an<BR>attack of rheumatism or gout, occurrence of arthritic<BR>pains.<BR>—वातेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—वातोन (˚त-ऊन), अस्, आ, अम्, deficient in wind<BR>or the windy humor; (आ), f., N. of a plant (= गो-<BR>जिह्वा).<BR>—वातोपजूत (˚त-उप्˚) or वातोपधूत<BR>(˚त-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. raised by the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातक|वातकः
वातक, अस्, m. the plant Marsilea Quadrifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकिन्
वातकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, rheumatic, gouty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातय
वातय (fr. 1. वात, but cf. rt. 2. वात्), Nom. P. वात-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to blow (as the wind), blow gently, to<BR>raise a wind, fan, ventilate; to blow favourably, to<BR>serve, &c. (see rt. 2. वात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर
वातर, अस्, आ, अम्, windy, stormy; swift (as the<BR>wind); [cf. Goth. vintrus; Angl. Sax. winter.]<BR>—वातरायण (˚र-अय्˚), अस्, m. an arrow; arrow's<BR>flight, discharge of an arrow, bow-shot; a saw; a<BR>mountain-peak; a mad-man, intoxicated person; an<BR>idler, useless person; the Sarala tree, a sort of pine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातल|वातलः
वातल, अस्, आ, अम्, windy, stormy; flatulent; (अस्),<BR>m. wind; a sort of pulse, Cicer Arietinum; (आ), f. a<BR>morbid state of the uterus.<BR>—वातल-मण्डली, f.<BR>a whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायन|वातायनं|वातायनः
वातायन, अस्, m. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाति|वातिः
वाति, इस्, m. air, wind; the sun; the moon.<BR>—वाति-<BR>ग, अस्, आ, अम्, acquainted with or working in mine-<BR>rals, &c., a mineralogist, metallurgist; (अस्), m. the<BR>egg-plant, Solanum Melongena.<BR>—वाति-गम or<BR>वातिङ्-गण, अस्, m. the egg-plant (= भण्टाकी,<BR>वार्त्ताकु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिक|वातिकः
वातिक, अस्, ई, अम्, windy, stormy; affected by<BR>wind-disease, rheumatic; produced by or proceeding<BR>from disorder of the wind; mad; (अम्), n. fever or<BR>inflammation ascribed to a vitiated state of the wind<BR>or aerial humor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0899-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातीय|वातीयं
वातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, windy, relating or belonging<BR>to wind, &c.; (अम्), n. sour rice-gruel (= काञ्जिक,<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुल|वातुलः
वातुल, अस्, आ, अम्, inflated with wind, affected<BR>by wind-disease, gouty, rheumatic; mad, crazy; (अस्),<BR>m. a whirlwind, gale.<BR>—वातुल-तन्त्र and वातुलोत्-<BR>तर-तन्त्र (˚ल-उत्˚), अम्, n., N. of two Tantra<BR>works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुलि|वातुलिः
वातुलि, इस्, f. a large bat (commonly called ‘the<BR>flying fox’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातूल|वातूलः
वातूल, अस्, आ, अम्, inflated with wind; affected<BR>with wind-disease; gouty, rheumatic; mad, insane,<BR>inebriate; (अस्), m. a whirlwind, gale, hurricane;<BR>[cf. वातुल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातृ
वातृ, ता, m. ‘the blower,’ air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्या
वात्या, f. a strong wind, gale, storm, whirlwind,<BR>hurricane.<BR>—वात्यौपम्य (˚या-औ˚), अम्, n. re-<BR>semblance to a storm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
1. वान, अस्, आ, अम्, blown (as the wind), blown<BR>upon so as to be dried, dry, dried; (अस्, आ, अम्), m.<BR>f. n. dry or dried fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
2. वान, अम्, n. (for 3. see p. 903, col. 1), blowing;<BR>living; going, moving, rolling; the rolling of water<BR>or of the tide; the high wave in Indian rivers (com-<BR>monly called ‘the Bore’); a perfume, fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांश|वांशः
वांश वांश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वंश), made of<BR>bamboo, of or belonging to bamboo; (ई), f. bamboo<BR>manna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांशिक|वांशिकः
वांशिक, अस्, a bamboo-cutter, &c.; a flute-<BR>player, piper, fifer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाःकिटि|वाःकिटिः
वाःकिटि वाः-किटि, वाः-पुष्प, &c. See<BR>under वार्, p. 904.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक|वाकं|वाकः
वाक 1. वाक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वक; for 2. वाक<BR>see col. 3), belonging or relating to a crane; (अम्),<BR>n. a flight of cranes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकुची
वाकुची वाकुची, f. (said to be fr. वा for वात,<BR>‘wind,’ and rt. कुच्, ‘to contract’), the plant Serratula<BR>Anthelmintica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकुल|वाकुलं
वाकुल वाकुल, अम्, n. (fr. वकुल), scil.<BR>फल, the fruit of the Vakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्य|वाक्यं
वाक्य वाक्य. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागा
वागा वागा, f. a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुजी
वागुजी वागुजी, f. the plant Serratula An-<BR>thelmintica (= सोम-राजी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुण|वागुणः
वागुण वागुण, अस्, m. the plant Averrhoa<BR>Carambola (= कर्मरङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरा
वागुरा वागुरा, f. (fr. rt. 2. वा?), a net (for<BR>catching deer or wild animals), trap, toils, snare,<BR>noose.<BR>—वागुरा-वृत्ति, इस्, f. livelihood obtained<BR>by snaring or catching wild animals; (इस्), m. one<BR>who lives by snaring animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरिक|वागुरिकः
वागुरिक, अस्, m. one who uses nets for catching<BR>deer, &c., a deer-catcher, hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुस
वागुस वागुस, अस्, m. a sort of large fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाघत्|वाघन्त्
वाघत् वाघत्, त्, m. (according to some fr.<BR>rt. 1. वह्, probably Pres. part. of a lost rt. वाघ् = Lat.<BR>vāgire, Gr. εὔχομαι), Ved. praying; a priest (ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. III. 18 = ऋत्विज्); = मेधाविन्<BR>(Naigh. III. 15); a horse, (Sāy. = वाहक = अश्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाघेल्ल
वाघेल्ल वाघेल्ल, N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्क|वांक|वांकः|वाङ्कः
वाङ्क वाङ्क, अस्, m. (fr. वङ्क), the ocean,<BR>the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्क्ष्|वांक्ष्
वाङ्क्ष् वाङ्क्ष् [cf. rts. काङ्क्ष्, वाञ्छ्,<BR>वश्], cl. 1. P. वाङ्क्षति, ववाङ्क्ष,<BR>वाङ्क्षितुम्, to wish, desire; [cf. Old Germ.<BR>wunsc, wunskian: Angl. Sax. wiscan: Cambro-<BR>Brit. gwanc, ‘desire:’ perhaps Hib. miangas, ‘in-<BR>clination, appetite;’ mianuighim, ‘I desire, wish,<BR>intend.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मय|वाङ्मयं
वाङ्मय वाङ्-मय, वाङ्-मुख, &c. See<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्
वाच् वाच्, क्, f. (fr. rt. वच्), speech, voice, talk,<BR>language, discourse, speaking (often at end of comps.,<BR>cf. अनृत-व्˚, दुष्ट-व्˚); a word, saying, phrase,<BR>proverb; assertion, asseveration, assurance, promise<BR>[cf. अभय-व्˚]; voice, sound; N. of Sarasvatī, goddess<BR>of speech, (in the Veda and Brāhmaṇas Vāc or Speech<BR>is herself the goddess, and is represented as created<BR>by Prajā-pati and married to him; one of the hymns<BR>of the Ṛg-veda [X. 125] is attributed to this goddess<BR>under the title of Vāc Āmbhṛṇī; in other places she<BR>is called the mother of the Vedas and wife of Indra;<BR>cf. Taittirīya-Br. II. 8, 8, 5, Śatapatha-Br. VII. 5, 2,<BR>52); [cf. Lat. voc-s; Gr. ὄπ-ς.]<BR>—वाक्-कलह,<BR>अम्, n. ‘speech-strife,’ quarrel, dispute.<BR>—वाक्-कीर,<BR>अस्, m. a wife's brother, (said to be fr. वाच्, speech,<BR>and कीर, a parrot.)<BR>—वाक्-चपल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>frivolous or inconsistent in speech, an idle or careless<BR>talker, chattering, impertinent.<BR>—वाक्-चापल्य, अम्,<BR>n. frivolity of speech, gossiping, chattering, idle or<BR>improper talk.<BR>—वाक्-छल, अम्, n. ‘fraud in speech,’<BR>prevarication, equivocation.<BR>—वाक्-छलान्वित (˚ल-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, equivocating, evasive.<BR>—वाक्-पटु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, skilled in speech, eloquent.<BR>—वाक्पटु-ता,<BR>f. or वाक्पटु-त्व, अम्, n. skill or ability in speech,<BR>eloquence.<BR>—वाक्-पति, इस्, इस्, इ, eloquent; (इस्), m.<BR>‘lord of speech,’ N. of Vṛhas-pati.<BR>—वाक्पति-राज,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—वाक्-पथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>suitable or seasonable for discourse.<BR>—वाक्-पारुष्य,<BR>अम्, n. harshness or severity of language; violence in<BR>words, abusive or contumelious language, scurrility,<BR>defamation.<BR>—वाक्-प्रचोदन, अम्, n. a command<BR>expressed in words; (आत्), ind. at the words of com-<BR>mand, in obedience to an order.<BR>—वाक्-प्रतोद, अस्,<BR>m. goading words, cutting or taunting language.<BR>—वाक्-प्रलाप, अस्, m. eloquence.<BR>—वाक्-प्रसा-<BR>रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. spreading out or abounding in<BR>speech, eloquent.<BR>—वाक्-संयम, अस्, m. restraint<BR>or control of speech, modesty.<BR>—वाग्-अपहारक,<BR>अस्, m. a stealer of words or books; a reader of pro-<BR>hibited works or passages.<BR>—वाग्-अर्थ, औ, m. du.<BR>a word and its sense (between which, according to<BR>the Mīmāṃsā, there is an eternal connection).<BR>—वाग्-<BR>असि, इस्, f. ‘speech-sword,’ sharp or cutting speech.<BR>—वाग्-आडम्बर, अस्, m. ‘confused sound of words,’<BR>bombast.<BR>—वाग्-ईश, अस्, आ, अम्, one who is a master<BR>of language, eloquent; (अस्), m. an orator, author,<BR>poet, &c.; an epithet of Vṛhas-pati, the preceptor of<BR>the gods; of Brahmā; (आ), f. the goddess of speech or<BR>eloquence, Sarasvatī.<BR>—वाग्-ईश्वर, अस्, m. a master of<BR>language, an orator, learned man; (with Buddhists) a<BR>deified sage (= मञ्जु-घोष); Brahmā; the author<BR>of the Māna-manohara; (ई), f. Sarasvatī (goddess<BR>of speech).<BR>—वाग्-उत्तर, अम्, n. speech and reply.<BR>—वाग्-ऋषभ, अस्, m. any one eminent in speech,<BR>an eloquent or learned man.<BR>—वागृषभ-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. eminence or excellence in speaking, eloquence,<BR>learning, erudition.<BR>—वाग्-गुद, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>bird.<BR>—वाग्-गुलि, इस्, m. the betel-bearer (of a king<BR>or prince &c.).<BR>—वाग्गुलिक, अस्, m. a betel-bearer.<BR>—वाग्-घस्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (i. e. वाच् + हस्त),<BR>possessed of speech and hands.<BR>—वाग्-जाल, अम्, n.<BR>‘multitude of words,’ bombast.<BR>—वाग्-डम्बर, अस्,<BR>m. graceful or eloquent language.<BR>—वाग्-दण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. ‘speech-assault,’ abusive or scurrilous language,<BR>reproof, reprimand; speech-control, restraint of speech<BR>(Manu XII. 10).<BR>—वाग्-दण्ड-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, spring-<BR>ing from scurrilous language and open assault (Manu<BR>VII. 48).<BR>—वाग्-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘given by word<BR>of mouth, ‘promised; (आ), f. a betrothed virgin.<BR>—वाग्-दरिद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, poor in speech, of few<BR>words, speaking little or humbly, speaking guardedly.<BR>—वाग्-दल, अम्, n. ‘speech-leaf,’ a lip.<BR>—वाग्-<BR>दान, अम्, n. ‘gift by word of mouth,’ the promise<BR>of a maiden in marriage.<BR>—वाग्-दुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>speaking ill or abusively, abusive, scurrilous; speak-<BR>ing ungrammatically; (अस्), m. a rude or scurrilous<BR>speaker, defamer; a Brāhman who has past the<BR>proper time of life without investiture with the<BR>sacred thread, &c.<BR>—वाग्-देवता, f. ‘speech-divinity,’<BR>epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR>—वाग्-देवी, f. ‘the goddess of<BR>speech or eloquence, ‘epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR>—वाग्देवी-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-c" target="_blank">Page0900-c+ 81</a>]<BR>कुल, अम्, n. ‘the family of Sarasvatī,’ science, learn-<BR>ing, eloquence.<BR>—वाग्-दैवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>speech for a divinity, sacred to Sarasvatī.<BR>—वाग्-<BR>दोष, अस्, m. ‘speech-vice,’ the act of speaking ill,<BR>defamation, abuse; ungrammatical speech; uttering<BR>a disagreeable sound.<BR>—वाग्-बन्धन, अम्, n.<BR>‘speech-binding,’ the stopping of speech, silencing.<BR>—वाग्-भट, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Vāgbhaṭālaṅkāra, a work on rhetoric; of the author<BR>of the Aṣṭāṅga-hṛdaya-saṃhitā.<BR>—वाग्-भट्ट, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—वाग्-मनस, see वाङ्-मनस.<BR>—वाग्-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having root or origin in<BR>speech.<BR>—वाग्-यत, अस्, आ, अम्, reserved in speech,<BR>taciturn, silent.<BR>—वाग्-याम, अस्, m. a dumb man,<BR>one silent from necessity.<BR>—वाग्-युद्ध, अम्, n.<BR>war of words, controversy, vehement debate or dis-<BR>cussion.<BR>—वाग्-रोध, अस्, m. the stopping of speech,<BR>silencing.<BR>—वाग्-वज्र, अम्, n. ‘thunder of words,’<BR>boisterous or harsh language.<BR>—वाग्-विदग्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, skilled in language, clever in speech; (आ), f.<BR>a kindly-speaking or fascinating woman.<BR>—वाग्-वि-<BR>निःसृत, अस्, आ, अम्, emitted or put forth by speech.<BR>—वाग्-विलास, अस्, m. graceful or elegant speech.<BR>—वाग्-व्यय, अस्, m. expenditure of words or<BR>speech, waste of breath.<BR>—वाग्-व्यापार, अस्, m.<BR>manner of speaking, style or habit of speech; cus-<BR>tomary phraseology.<BR>—वाङ्-निश्चय, अस्, m. ‘speech-<BR>settlement, ‘marriage contract, affiance by word of<BR>mouth.<BR>—वाग्-निष्ठा, f. abiding by one's words,<BR>punctuality in fulfilling a promise, faithfulness.<BR>—वाङ्-<BR>मती, f., N. of a sacred stream (said to be situated<BR>on the summit of the Himālaya).<BR>—वाङ्-मधुर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, sweet in speech.<BR>—वाङ्-मनस, अम्, n.<BR>or ए, n. du. speech and mind.<BR>—वाङ्-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, relating to speech; endowed with speech; con-<BR>sisting of words; eloquent, rhetorical; (ई), f. the<BR>goddess Sarasvatī; (अम्), n. speech, language;<BR>eloquence; rhetoric.<BR>—वाङ्मयाधिकृत-ता, f.<BR>the state of presiding over eloquence (said of the<BR>goddess of speech).<BR>—वाङ्-मात्र, अम्, n. mere<BR>words, words alone, only speech.<BR>—वाङ्-मुख, अम्,<BR>n. the opening or commencement of a speech, an<BR>exordium.<BR>—वाचं-यम, अस्, m. ‘speech-restrainer,’<BR>a sage who practises rigid taciturnity.<BR>—वाचम्-<BR>ईङ्खय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘word-moving,’ i. e.<BR>singing a hymn; ‘making a sound,’ epithet of the<BR>Soma.<BR>—वाचसाम्-पति, इस्, m. (probably for वा-<BR>चाम्पति), ‘lord of speech,’ N. of Vṛhas-pati.<BR>—वा-<BR>चस्-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of speech,’ N. of Vṛhas-pati<BR>(preceptor of the gods and regent of the planet<BR>Jupiter); N. of a grammarian and lexicographer<BR>(the author of the Adhyāsa-bhāṣya-vyākhyā com-<BR>mentary, also author of a work called Kalpa-taru and<BR>of the Ātaṅka-darpaṇa).<BR>—वाचस्पति-गोविन्द, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of a commentary on the<BR>Megha-dūta.<BR>—वाचस्पति-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>celebrated lawyer (the author of several works on<BR>law, among which the Kṛtya-kalpa-latā, the Tīrtha-<BR>cintā-maṇi, the Vivāda-cintā-maṇi, &c. are enume-<BR>rated); of an author of various works, especially of<BR>the Bhāmatī-nibandha and Sāṅkhya-tattva-kaumudī;<BR>of the author of several commentaries.<BR>—वाचस्-<BR>पत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, declared by Vācas-pati; (अम्),<BR>n. fine language, an eloquent speech, harangue.<BR>—वाचो-युक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, possessing fitness or dex-<BR>terity of speech.<BR>—वाचोयुक्ति-पटु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ,<BR>skilled in fitness of speech, eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक|वाकं|वाकः
2. वाक, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding, speaking (at the<BR>end of some comps., cf. चक्र-व्˚, चीरी-व्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्य|वाक्यं
वाक्य, अम्, n. speech, saying, assertion, statement,<BR>word, (मम वाक्यात्, by my order, in my name);<BR>a sentence, period; a rule, precept, aphorism; (in<BR>astronomy) the solar process for all astronomical com-<BR>putations.<BR>—वाक्य-खण्डन, अम्, n. refutation of<BR>an assertion.<BR>—वाक्य-तस्, ind. conformably to the<BR>saying.<BR>—वाक्य-पद, अम्, n. a word in a sentence.<BR>—वाक्य-पदीय, अम्, n.? (relating to the words<BR>of a sentence), N. of a poem on grammar by Bhartṛ-<BR>hari.<BR>—वाक्य-पद्धति, इस्, f. the manner or rule<BR>of constructing sentences.<BR>—वाक्य-प्रबन्ध, अस्,<BR>m. connection or relation of sentences, connected<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">Page0901-a+ 80</a>]<BR>composition.<BR>—वाक्य-प्रयोग, अस्, m. employment<BR>or application of speech or language.<BR>—वाक्य-रचना,<BR>f. the arrangement or construction of sentences, syntax.<BR>—वाक्य-वज्र-विषम, अस्, आ, अम्, rough or<BR>course by (using) thunderbolt-like words.<BR>—वाक्य-<BR>विन्यास, अस्, m. the arrangement or order of a<BR>sentence, syntax.<BR>—वाक्य-विशारद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>skilled in speech, eloquent.<BR>—वाक्य-शेष, अस्, m.<BR>the remainder of a speech (i. e. anything intended to<BR>be said but left unsaid).<BR>—वाक्य-सार, N. of a work.<BR>—वाक्य-सुधा, f., N. of a philosophical treatise<BR>ascribed to Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—वाक्य-स्थ or वाक्य-<BR>स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, being or contained in a sentence;<BR>attentive to what is said.<BR>—वाक्य-स्फोट, see स्फो-<BR>ट.<BR>—वाक्यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. the meaning<BR>of a word or sentence.<BR>—वाक्यालाप (˚य-आल्˚), अस्,<BR>m. talking, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0900-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागर|वागरः
वागर, अस्, m. a sage, holy man, one desirous of<BR>final emancipation; a scholar, Paṇḍit, learned Brāh-<BR>man; a hero, brave man, intrepid or fearless person;<BR>certainty, ascertainment; a whetstone; an obstacle,<BR>impediment, obstruction; submarine fire; a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागारु|वागारुः
वागारु, उस्, उस्, उ (said to be fr. वाच्, compounded<BR>with आरु fr. rt. 4. ऋ, q. v.), breaking promise or<BR>faith, disappointing, a disappointer, deceiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागाशनि|वागाशनिः
वागाशनि, इस्, m. a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मिन्
वाग्मिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking much, loquacious, talka-<BR>tive, verbose, wordy; speaking well, eloquent; (ई), m.,<BR>N. of Vṛhas-pati (preceptor of the gods).<BR>—वाग्मि-<BR>ता, f. or वाग्मि-त्व, अम्, n. loquacity, eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्य|वाग्यः
वाग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking little, speaking cau-<BR>tiously or humbly (perhaps fr. वाच् + य fr. rt. यम्;<BR>cf. वाग्-यत); speaking truly; (अस्), m. modesty,<BR>humility, self-disparagement; doubt, alternative (?).<BR>—वाग्य-तस्, ind. silently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचक|वाचकः
वाचक, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, declaratory, expla-<BR>natory, expressive of, significant, expressing, signifying;<BR>verbal, expressed by words; (अस्), m. a speaker, reader;<BR>a significant sound, word; a messenger.<BR>—वाचक-<BR>ता, f. or वाचक-त्व, अम्, n. expressiveness, signifi-<BR>cance.<BR>—वाचक-पद, अम्, n. an expressive or sig-<BR>nificant word, explicit term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचन|वाचनं
वाचन, अम्, n. the act of reciting or reading,<BR>recitation; the act of relating or declaring, procla-<BR>mation, declaration; [cf. स्वस्ति-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनक|वाचनकं
वाचनक, अम्, n. an enigma, riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनिक
वाचनिक, अस्, ई, अम्, verbal, expressed by words,<BR>textual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचा
वाचा, f. speech; a holy word, sacred text; an oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाट|वाचाटः
वाचाट, अस्, आ, अम्, talkative, talking much or idly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाल|वाचालः
वाचाल, अस्, आ, अम्, talkative, chattering, talking<BR>much or idly; boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिक|वाचिकं|वाचिकः
वाचिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, verbal, oral; communicated<BR>by speech or by word of mouth, (पारुष्ये दण्ड-<BR>वाचिके, the two violences, whether by blows or speech,<BR>i. e. assault and slander); (अम्), n. news, tidings, intel-<BR>ligence.<BR>—वाचिक-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a letter, dispatch; a<BR>newspaper, gazette.<BR>—वाचिक-हारक, अस्, m. ‘news-<BR>conveyer,’ a letter, epistle; a messenger, courier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिन्
वाचिन् in जाति-वाचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, expressing genus,<BR>generic; [cf. जाति-वाचक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्य|वाच्यं
वाच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken or said, proper to<BR>be said; to be spoken against or gainsaid^1, blamable,<BR>censurable, vile, bad, contemptible, low, outcast; to<BR>be predicated (of anything), attributive, adjective,<BR>declinable as an adjective, taking three genders; (अस्),<BR>m. a patronymic of the Ṛṣi Prajā-pati; (अम्), n.<BR>that which may be said of anything; blame, censure;<BR>(in gram.) a predicate; the voice of a verb (e. g.<BR>कर्तरि-वाच्यम्, the active voice; कर्मणि-वा-<BR>च्यम्, the passive voice).<BR>—वाच्य-चित्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>fanciful in sense (as poetry).<BR>—वाच्य-ता, f. or वाच्य-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. blamableness, blame, reproach; ill repute,<BR>infamy; the quality of being predicable; conjugation.<BR>—वाच्य-वज्र, अम्, n. ‘thunder of words,’ boisterous<BR>or severe language; [cf. वाग्-वज्र.]<BR>—वाच्यार्थ<BR>(˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. expressed meaning (in rhetoric).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यमान
वाच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being made to speak;<BR>being read aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच|वाचं|वाचः
वाच वाच, अस्, m. a plant. See मदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाज|वाजं|वाजः
वाज वाज, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वज्), strength,<BR>vigour, energy (Ved.); food, sacrificial food (Ved.);<BR>wealth (Ved.); speed; a month, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>III. 27, 1. वाजाः = मासाः); battle, conflict, contest,<BR>(according to Naigh. II. 17; वाजे वाजे, in every con-<BR>flict); a wing; a feather, the feather of an arrow<BR>[cf. गृध्र-व्˚, चित्र-व्˚, पत्त्र-व्˚]; sound; N. of<BR>a Muni; of one of the Ṛbhus or sons of Su-dhanvan,<BR>see ऋभु; (आस्), m. pl., N. of certain semi-divine<BR>or deified personages of the family of Vāja and<BR>closely connected or identified with the Ṛbhus, see<BR>ऋभु; (अम्), n. ghee or clarified butter; an oblation<BR>of rice offered at a Śrāddha or obsequial ceremony;<BR>rice or food in general; water; an acetous mixture<BR>of ground meal and water left to ferment; a Mantra<BR>or prayer concluding a sacrifice; [cf. perhaps Eng.<BR>wing.]<BR>—वाज-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. performing<BR>mighty works.<BR>—वाज-गन्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having the smell of strength, i. e. having a little<BR>strength.<BR>—वाज-दावन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. granting food,<BR>(Sāy. = अन्न-प्रद.)<BR>—वाज-द्रविणस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. possessing strength or food.<BR>—वाज-पति, इस्,<BR>m., Ved. lord of strength or food, &c.<BR>—वाज-पस्त्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. in whose house there is food, having<BR>a house abounding in food or overflowing with plenty.<BR>—वाज-पेय, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. वाज,<BR>‘an acetous mixture of meal and water,’ + पेय, ‘to be<BR>drunk’ by the gods), a particular sacrifice; N. of the<BR>sixth book of the Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—वाज-<BR>प्रमह, अस्, आ, अम्, famous or illustrious for<BR>wealth, (Sāy. = धनैर् प्रकृष्टम् महस् तेजो<BR>यस्य or धनैर् प्रमहनीय.)<BR>—वाज-प्रसूत,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. bearing food or strength.<BR>—वाज-भो-<BR>जिन्, ई, m., Ved. a particular sacrifice; see वाज-<BR>पेय.<BR>—वाजम्-भर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bearing<BR>food or oblations; a patronymic of Sapti, (in this<BR>case written वाजम्भर.)<BR>—वाज-रत्न, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, rich in food, &c.; having agreeable food, &c.<BR>—वाज-श्रवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. bestower of food<BR>(said of Agni).<BR>—वाज-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, or वाज-सा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम् (see rt. सन्), Ved. granting food or strength.<BR>—वाज-सातम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. a liberal dispenser<BR>of food.<BR>—वाज-साति, इस्, f., Ved. the granting of<BR>strength or food; gaining food; a sacrifice; war,<BR>battle (as yielding spoil); (इस्, इस्, इ), granting food<BR>or strength.<BR>—वाजी-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, strength-<BR>ening, stimulating, aphrodisiac.<BR>—वाजी-करण, अम्,<BR>n. the act of strengthening or stimulating, excitement<BR>of amorous desires by aphrodisiacs, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजय
वाजय [cf. rt. वज्, cl. 10], Nom. P., Ved. वाज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to desire or ask for strength or food; to<BR>worship, (according to Naigh. III. 14 = अर्चति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजयत्
वाजयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. desiring food or<BR>strength, (Sāy. = अन्नम् इच्छत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजयु
वाजयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desiring or asking for<BR>strength or food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनेय|वाजसनेयः
वाजसनेय, अस्, m. (according to the Śabda-k.),<BR>N. of a Vedic work compiled by Janam-ejaya, after-<BR>wards destroyed through the curse of Vaiśampāyana,<BR>(according to the Matsya-Purāṇa a dispute arose<BR>between Janam-ejaya and Vaiśampāyana in conse-<BR>quence of the former's patronage of the Vājasaneyin<BR>branch of the Yajur-veda founded by Yājñavalkya in<BR>opposition to Vaiśampāyana, the author of the Black or<BR>Taittirīya branch); a follower of the sect of the Vāja-<BR>saneyins.<BR>—वाजसनेय-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n. a Brāh-<BR>maṇa of the Vājasaneyin branch of the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनेयक
वाजसनेयक, अस्, m. a Vājasaneyin; (अम्), n. a<BR>text of the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनेयिन्
वाजसनेयिन्, ई, m. a member of the sect of the Vā-<BR>jasaneyins, a follower of the White Yajur-veda; a N. of<BR>Yājñavalkya.<BR>—वाजसनेयि-शाखा, f. the branch or<BR>sect of the Vājasaneyins.<BR>—वाजसनेयि-संहिता, f.<BR>‘the collection of the Vājasaneyins,’ (i. e. the collection<BR>of hymns of the White Yajur-veda ascribed to the Ṛṣi<BR>Yājñavalkya and called ‘white’ or शुक्ल to distinguish<BR>it from the Black or Dark Yajur-veda, which was<BR>the name given to the oldest collection or Taittirīya-<BR>saṃhitā [q. v.] of the Yajur-veda, because in this<BR>last, the separation between the Saṃhitā or collection<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">Page0901-c+ 80</a>]<BR>of Mantras and the Brāhmaṇa portion is greatly<BR>obscured, and the two are blended together; whereas<BR>the White Saṃhitā is clearly distinguished from the<BR>Brāhmaṇa; it is divided into 40 Adhyāyas with<BR>303 Anuvākas, comprising 1975 sections or Kaṇ-<BR>ḍikās; the legend relates that the Yajus in its ori-<BR>ginal form was taught by the Ṛṣi Vaiśampāyana<BR>to his pupil Yājñavalkya, but that the latter having<BR>incurred his teacher's anger was made to disgorge all<BR>the texts he had learnt, which were then picked up<BR>by Vaiśampāyana's other disciples in the form of<BR>partridges [see तैत्तिरीय-संहिता]; Yājñavalkya<BR>then hymned the Sun, who gratified by his homage,<BR>appeared in the form of a वाजिन् or horse, and consented<BR>to give him fresh Yajus texts, which were not known<BR>to his former master; those who studied these texts<BR>were called Vājins from the shape assumed by the<BR>Sun.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन्
वाजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. possessing strength, possessed<BR>of food or sacrificial food, possessing wings; swift,<BR>powerful, strong, impetuous, quick; hastening (to<BR>aid others); epithet of the horse in general and of<BR>the representations of the Sun in the shape of a<BR>horse (see Dadhi-krā, Dadhi-krāvan, Tārkṣya); of<BR>Indra; of Bṛhas-pati and other gods; (ई), m. a<BR>horse; a follower of the Vājasaneyin branch of the<BR>Yajur-veda; an arrow; a bird; a plant, Justicia Adhe-<BR>natoda; (इनस्), m. pl., N. of the Ṛbhus (Ṛg-veda<BR>IV. 37, 4); (इनी), f. food (Ved.); a mare; N. of<BR>Uṣas (goddess of the dawn); of the mother of<BR>Bharad-vāja.<BR>—वाजि-गन्ध, अस्, m. the plant Phy-<BR>salis Flexuosa, (also written वाजिगन्धक.)<BR>—वाजि-<BR>ता, f. or वाजि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of having strength<BR>or food or wings; the state or nature of a horse.<BR>—वाजि-<BR>दन्त or वाजिदन्तक, अस्, m. the plant Justicia Adhe-<BR>natoda.<BR>—वाजिनी-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of Vā-<BR>jinī, i. e. of food, &c. (the adj. being used for the sub-<BR>stantive), yielding nutriment; possessed of sacrifices;<BR>abounding in worship or prayers (which are offered<BR>at dawn), highly honoured; (अती), f. epithet of Uṣas<BR>(goddess of the dawn); of Sarasvatī (goddess of<BR>speech or eloquence).<BR>—वाजिनी-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>lord of wealth; (Sāy.) abiding in the sacrificial rite;<BR>rich in food (said of Indra, Agni, Vāyu, and the<BR>Aśvins).<BR>—वाजिन्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very strong<BR>or vigorous.<BR>—वाजि-पृष्ठ, अस्, m. the globe-<BR>amaranth.<BR>—वाजि-भक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>chick-pea.<BR>—वाजि-भूमि, इस्, f. a place where horses<BR>are bred or a spot abounding in or suitable for<BR>horses.<BR>—वाजि-भोजन, अस्, m. ‘affording food to<BR>horses,’ a sort of kidney-bean (= मुद्ग).<BR>—वाजि-<BR>मत्, आन्, m. a kind of cucumber, (see पटोल.)<BR>—वाजि-मेध, अस्, m. the horse sacrifice; [cf. अश्व-<BR>मेध.]<BR>—वाजि-शाला, f. ‘horse-house,’ a stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन|वाजिनं
वाजिन, अम्, n. impetuosity, prowess, a heroic act,<BR>heroism (Ved.); a conflict, contest (Ved.); the scum<BR>of curdled milk; curd of two-milk whey or whey<BR>from which the curds have been separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिनेय
वाजिनेय, अस्, m., Ved. the son of Vājinī, i. e.<BR>Bharad-vāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छ्|वांछ्
वाञ्छ् वाञ्छ् [cf. rt. वाङ्क्ष्], cl. 1. P.<BR>(sometimes also A.) वाञ्छति (-ते),<BR>ववाञ्छ, अवाञ्छीत्, वाञ्छितुम्, to desire, wish;<BR>to wish for, ask for, seek after, pursue: Pass. वाञ्छ्-<BR>यते, Aor. अवाञ्छि, to be wished, &c.: Caus. वाञ्-<BR>छयति, -ते, Aor. अववाञ्छत्, to cause to wish,<BR>&c.; [cf. Old Germ. wunsc, ‘wish;’ wunskian,<BR>‘to wish;’ Angl. Sax. wiscan: Eng. wish.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छक
वाञ्छक, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing, desiring; a wisher,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छत्
वाञ्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छन|वांछन|वांछनं
वाञ्छन, अम्, n. the act of desiring, wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छनीय
वाञ्छनीय, to be wished for, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छा|वांछा
वाञ्छा, f. wish, desire; desire for (with loc.,<BR>Kirāt. IV. 25).<BR>—वाञ्छा-सिद्धि, इस्, f. the accom-<BR>plishment of a wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छित|वांछित|वाञ्छितं
वाञ्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired, longed for;<BR>wishing, desiring; (अम्), n. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छितव्य
वाञ्छितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be wished or desired,<BR>desirable, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0901-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छित्वा
वाञ्छित्वा, ind. having wished, having desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छिन्|वांछिन्
वाञ्छिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wishing, desirous; lustful; (इनी),<BR>f. a libidinous woman; a wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छ्य
वाञ्छ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = वाञ्छनीय, p. 901, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छ्यमान
वाञ्छ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being wished or de-<BR>sired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्
वाट् वाट्, ind. an exclamation on making<BR>an oblation of butter, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट|वाटं|वाटः
वाट वाट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वट), made or<BR>consisting of the Indian fig-tree or its wood, &c.;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), m. f. n. an enclosure, piece of enclosed<BR>ground, court-yard; a garden, park, orchard, planta-<BR>tion; the enclosure of a town or village, fence, wall,<BR>hedge, &c.; a road; a sort of grain, Panicum Spi-<BR>catum; the groin; (ई), f. the site of a house or<BR>building; a house, dwelling; a kind of plant (=<BR>वाट्यालक).<BR>—वाट-धान, अस्, m. the descendant<BR>of an outcast Brāhman by a Brāhman female; N. of<BR>a degraded tribe.<BR>—वाट-शृङ्खला, f. the chain<BR>of an enclosure, a sort of fence (?).<BR>—वाटी-दीर्घ,<BR>अस्, m. a sort of grass or reed (= इक्कट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटिका
वाटिका, f. the site of a house; a garden, orchard;<BR>the plant Sida Cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटिदीर्घ
वाटि-दीर्घ, अस्, m. = वाटी-दीर्घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्य|वाट्यः
वाट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a house or garden;<BR>(अस्), m., see Nirukta II. 1; (आ), f. the plant Sida Cor-<BR>difolia.<BR>—वाट्य-पुष्प, अम्, n. sandal; saffron; (ई),<BR>f. the plant Sida Cordifolia, (also called Atibalā.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्याल|वाट्यालः
वाट्याल, अस्, ई, m. f. a herbaceous shrub, Sida<BR>Cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यालक|वाट्यालकः
वाट्यालक, अस्, m. the plant Sida Cordifolia (com-<BR>monly called Bariyāla).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्टक|वाट्टकं
वाट्टक वाट्टक, अम्, n. fried barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाड्
वाड् वाड् (more properly written बाड्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. A. वाडते, वाडितुम्, to bathe;<BR>to dive and emerge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडव|वाडवं|वाडवः
वाडव वाडव, अस्, m. submarine fire (see<BR>under वडवा, बडवा); a Brāhman; (अम्), n. a<BR>stud, a collection of mares.<BR>—वाडवाग्नि (˚व-अग्˚),<BR>इस्, m. the fire of the lower regions, hell; see वड-<BR>वाग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवेय|वाडवेयः
वाडवेय, अस्, m. a bull; (औ), m. du. the two<BR>Aśvins as the sons of Vaḍavā or Aśvinī (see अश्विनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडव्य|वाडव्यं
वाडव्य, अम्, n. a number of Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाढ
वाढ वाढ, अस्, आ, अम् (probably the origi-<BR>nal form of ऊढ, past part. of rt. 1. वह्; compar.<BR>साधीयस्, superl. साधिष्ठ, q. q. v. v.; cf. बहु,<BR>वहल), hard, firm; much, abundant, excessive, ex-<BR>ceeding; (अम्), ind. much, excessively; indeed,<BR>truly; very well, very good, well, yes, indeed, truly,<BR>surely, positively; consequently.<BR>—वाढ-विक्रम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of excessive prowess, powerful, very<BR>strong, mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाण|वाणः
वाण 1. वाण, अस्, आ, अम् (often written बाण,<BR>q. v.; fr. rt. वण्, ‘to sound’), sounding (Kirāt. XV.<BR>10), making a sound; (अस्), m. a reed, reed-shaft,<BR>shaft, arrow, (in this and some other senses said to<BR>be also अम्, n.); a symbolical expression for the<BR>number five (from the five arrows of Kāma-deva,<BR>cf. पञ्च-वाण); a particular kind of reed or cane;<BR>a pipe, flute, lute, (in Ṛg-veda I. 85, 10. the Maruts<BR>are described as वाणम् धमन्तः, ‘blowing on<BR>their pipe’ or ‘playing on their lute,’ वाण being<BR>explained by Sāy. as ‘a kind of lute with a hundred<BR>strings’); a sound, voice; a word spoken, agreement<BR>(Ved., Sāy. = वचन); a mark for arrows, aim; the<BR>udder of a cow; alone, solitary (= केवल); N. of<BR>an Asura (a son of Bali, an enemy of Viṣṇu, and<BR>favourite of Śiva); of one of Skanda's attendants;<BR>of a king; of a poet (the author of the Kādambarī,<BR>of the Harṣa-carita, and perhaps also of the Ratnā-<BR>valī); of a person (mentioned in Rāja-taraṅginī VI.<BR>318); fire (?), lightning (?); (अस्, आ), m. f. a blue-<BR>flowering Barleria; the hind part or feathered end<BR>of an arrow; (ई), f. sound, speech, (कठोरा वाणी,<BR>a harsh speech); voice; praise, laudation; a literary<BR>production; N. of Sarasvatī (the goddess of speech<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">Page0902-b+ 76</a>]<BR>and eloquence); (अम्), n. the flower of Barleria;<BR>the body.<BR>—वाण-गङ्गा, f. ‘arrow Ganges,’ N. of<BR>a river flowing past Someśa (and said to have been<BR>produced by Rāvaṇa by cleaving a mountain with an<BR>arrow).<BR>—वाण-गोचर, अस्, m. the range of an<BR>arrow.<BR>—वाण-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of the Asura<BR>Vāṇa,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वाण-तूण, अस्, m.<BR>‘arrow-quiver,’ a quiver.<BR>—वाणतूणी-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made into a quiver.<BR>—वाण-धि, इस्, m.<BR>‘arrow-receptacle,’ a quiver.<BR>—वाण-नाशा, f., N. of<BR>a river.<BR>—वाण-निकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced or<BR>wounded by an arrow.<BR>—वाण-पञ्चानन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—वाण-पथ, अस्, m. ‘arrow-path,’<BR>the range of an arrow, a bow-shot.<BR>—वाणपथातीत<BR>(˚थ-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, passed beyond the range of<BR>an arrow.<BR>—वाण-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘arrow-handed,’<BR>having arrows in the hand, armed with arrows.<BR>—वाण-पात, अस्, m. arrow-fall, an arrow-shot (as<BR>a measure of distance), the range of an arrow.<BR>—वा-<BR>णपात-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being within the range<BR>of an arrow.<BR>—वाण-पुङ्खा, f. the feathered end<BR>of an arrow or that part of an arrow which includes<BR>the feathers and shaft.<BR>—वाण-पुर्, ऊर्, f. or वाण-<BR>पुर, अम्, n. the capital of Vāṇa-rāja.<BR>—वाण-<BR>भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—वाण-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, consisting of arrows, arrowy.<BR>—वाण-मुक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. or वाण-मोक्षण, अम्, n. discharge of an<BR>arrow, shooting an arrow.<BR>—वाण-योजन, अम्, n.<BR>‘arrow-union,’ a quiver.<BR>—वाण-राज, अस्, m. ‘king-<BR>Vāṇa,’ epithet of the Asura.<BR>—वाण-रेखा, f. a<BR>long wound made by an arrow.<BR>—वाण-लिङ्ग, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Liṅga on the bank of the Narma-dā river.<BR>—वाण-वर्षण, अम्, n. or वाण-वृष्टि, इस्, f.<BR>showering down arrows or darts.<BR>—वाण-वर्षिन्,<BR>ई, इणि, इ, showering arrows.<BR>—वाण-वार, अस्, m.<BR>‘arrow-defender,’ a breastplate, cuirass, armour.<BR>—वा-<BR>ण-सन्धान, अम्, n. the fitting of an arrow to the<BR>bow-string.<BR>—वाण-सिद्धि, इस्, f. the hitting of a<BR>mark by an arrow.<BR>—वाण-सुता, f. ‘daughter of<BR>Vāṇa,’ epithet of Uṣā or the Dawn (wife of Ani-<BR>ruddha, see Uṣā).<BR>—वाण-हन्, आ, or वाणारि (˚ण-<BR>अरि˚), इस्, m. ‘killer or enemy of Vāṇa,’ an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वाणावली (˚ण-आव्˚), f. a series of five<BR>Ślokas (containing only one sentence).<BR>—वाणाश्रय<BR>(˚ण-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘arrow-receptacle,’ a quiver.<BR>—वाणासन (˚ण-अस्˚), अम्, n. ‘arrow-discharger,’<BR>a bow.<BR>—वाणेश्वर (˚ण-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिन्
वाणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having an arrow or arrows; speak-<BR>ing; (इनी), f. a sharp or clever woman, an intriguing<BR>woman; an actress, dancer, Nāch girl; a drunken<BR>woman, one literally or figuratively intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणीची
वाणीची, f., Ved. speech or the goddess of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाण|वाणः
वाण 2. वाण (fr. rt. वे) for 2. वान, q. v.<BR>—वाण-दण्ड, अस्, m. a weaver's loom (for वान-<BR>दण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणि|वाणिः
वाणि, इस्, f. weaving; a weaver's loom; a species<BR>of the Aṣṭi metre, (also written वाणी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिज|वाणिजः
वाणिज वाणिज, अस्, m. (usually spelt बा-<BR>णिज, q. v.), a merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिज्य|वाणिज्यं
वाणिज्य, अम्, n. traffic, trade, (see बाणिज्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणी
वाणी वाणी, f. See under 1. वाण, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणीची
वाणीची वाणीची. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्
वात् 2. वात् (probably to be regarded as<BR>a Nom. fr. 1. वात, cf. rt. 2. वत्, वातय;<BR>for 1. वात् see p. 899, col. 1), cl. 10. P. वातयति,<BR>&c., to blow, blow gently; to fan, ventilate; to blow<BR>favourably; to serve, make happy, act favourably<BR>(towards one setting out on a journey); to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
वात 2. वात, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. वन्; for<BR>1. वात see p. 899, col. 1), = वनित, solicited, wished<BR>for, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरशन
वातरशन वातरशन, अस्, m., Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic; (आस्), m. pl., N. of certain Ṛṣis or semi-<BR>divine beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुल|वातुलः
वातुल वातुल, See p. 900, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सक|वात्सकं
वात्सक वात्सक, अम्, n. (fr. वत्स), a herd<BR>of calves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सल्य|वात्सल्यं|वात्सल्यः
वात्सल्य, अम्, n. (fr. वत्सल), affection or ten-<BR>derness towards offspring, affection or love in general;<BR>fondness, fond or foolish partiality.<BR>—वात्सल्य-बन्-<BR>धिन्, इ, इनी, इ, evincing tenderness, displaying affec-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सायन
वात्सायन, अस्, m., N. of a philosophical writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सी
वात्सी, f. (fr. वत्स?), the daughter of a Śūdra<BR>woman by a Brāhman.<BR>—वात्सी-पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of a Vātsī,’ a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्स्य|वात्स्यः
वात्स्य, अस्, m. (fr. वत्स), N. of a Muni.<BR>—वात्स्य-<BR>गुल्मक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्स्यायन|वात्स्यायनः
वात्स्यायन, अस्, m., N. of a Muni and of a<BR>writer on amorous subjects (author of the Kāma-<BR>sūtras and of the Nyāya-bhāṣya).<BR>—वात्स्यायन-<BR>सूत्र = काम-सूत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्स्यायनीय
वात्स्यायनीय, अम्, n. the Kāma-sūtras of Vātsyā-<BR>yana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद|वादः
वाद वाद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वद्), speaking,<BR>talking, (काम-वाद, talking as one pleases, speak-<BR>ing freely); discourse, speech, assertion, proposition,<BR>allegation; statement, discussion, dispute, controversy,<BR>words; explanation, exposition (of holy texts &c.);<BR>demonstrated conclusion; reply; a plaint, accusation;<BR>report, rumour; sound, sounding.<BR>—वाद-कर, अस्,<BR>आ, or ई, अम्, or वाद-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, making a discus-<BR>sion, causing a dispute.<BR>—वाद-चञ्चु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>clever in repartee, a good jester.<BR>—वाद-प्रतिवाद,<BR>अस्, m. or औ, m. du. a set disputation, assertion and<BR>counter assertion, statement and contradiction, con-<BR>troversy, disputation.<BR>—वाद-युद्ध, अम्, n. a war<BR>of words, controversial war, controversy, dispute.<BR>—वादयुद्ध-प्रधान, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in<BR>the war of controversy, an eminent controversialist.<BR>—वाद-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, adhering to or following<BR>any particular proposition or doctrine; addicted to<BR>controversy, disputatious.<BR>—वाद-वादिन्, ई, m. a<BR>Jaina (= आर्हत).<BR>—वाद-विवाद, अस्, m. or औ,<BR>m. du. a discussion about any statement, argument and<BR>disputation, debate, dispute, argumentation, litigation.<BR>—वाद-साधन, अम्, n. the proof of an assertion,<BR>the maintaining of an argument, controversy.<BR>—वा-<BR>दानुवाद (˚द-अन्˚), औ, m. du. assertion and<BR>reply, attack and rejoinder, plea and counterplea,<BR>accusation and defence, plaint and reply, controversy,<BR>dispute, disputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादक|वादकः
वादक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. Caus. of rt. वद्), making<BR>a speech, speaking; (अस्), m. a speaker; a musician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादन|वादनं|वादनः
वादन, अम्, n. the act of sounding, sound; in-<BR>strumental music, the sound of musical instruments.<BR>—वादन-दण्ड, अस्, m. a stick &c. for striking<BR>a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादयत्
वादयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to speak, causing<BR>to sound; sounding, playing a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादि|वादिः
वादि, इस्, इस्, इ, speaking; learned; wise, sage,<BR>skilful.<BR>—वादि-राज्, ट्, m. a Bauddha sage; = मञ्जु-<BR>घोष, मञ्जु-श्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादित
वादित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus. of rt. वद्), made<BR>to speak, caused to be uttered; made to sound,<BR>sounded, played.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादित्र|वादित्रं
वादित्र, अम्, n. a musical instrument; instrumental<BR>music.<BR>—वादित्र-गण, अस्, m. a band of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिन्
वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking, discoursing; asserting,<BR>declaring; disputing; (ई), m. a speaker; a disputant;<BR>a plaintiff, accuser; an explainer, expounder (of the law,<BR>Śāstras, &c.); the leading or key-note (in music).<BR>—वादि-त्व, अम्, n. in सत्य-वादि-त्व.<BR>—वादीन्-<BR>द्र (˚दि-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिश|वादिशः
वादिश, अस्, m. a learned and good man, a sage,<BR>seer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्य|वाद्यं|वाद्यः
वाद्य, अम्, n. any musical instrument.<BR>—वाद्य-<BR>कर, अस्, m. a musician.<BR>—वाद्य-निर्घोष, अस्,<BR>m. the sound of musical instruments.<BR>—वाद्य-<BR>भाण्ड, अम्, n. a multitude of musical instruments,<BR>a band; any musical instrument.<BR>—वाद्यभाण्ड-<BR>मुख, अम्, n. the mouth or top part or point of<BR>a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्यमान
वाद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being made to speak<BR>or sound, played.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0902-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादर|वादरं|वादरः
वादर वादर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वदर for<BR>बदर, q. v.), made or consisting of cotton, &c.<BR>(see बादर); (आ), f. the cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरिक|वादरिकः
वादरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who collects cotton, &c.<BR>(See बादरिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरङ्ग|वादरंग|वादरंगः|वादरङ्गः
वादरङ्ग वादरङ्ग, अस्, m. the sacred fig-<BR>tree. (See अश्वत्थ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरायण|वादरायणः
वादरायण वादरायण, अस्, m., N. of Vyāsa,<BR>(also written बादरायण, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादल|वादलं|वादलः
वादल वादल, अम्, n. [cf. बादर], liquorice<BR>or the root of the Abrus Precatorius (used for it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादान्य|वादान्यः
वादान्य वादान्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for वदान्य,<BR>q. v.), munificent, liberal, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादाल|वादालः
वादाल वादाल, अस्, m. the sheat fish (=<BR>वदाल, सहस्र-दंष्ट्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिर|वादिरं
वादिर वादिर, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>tree (resembling the Vadarī or Badarī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाध्
वाध् वाध् (more correctly written बाध्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. A. वाधते, ववाधे, वा-<BR>धिष्यते, अवाधिष्ट, वाधितुम्, to press, oppress,<BR>vex, give pain, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधन|वाधनं
वाधन, अम्, n. the act of oppressing, paining,<BR>vexing, &c. (See बाधन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधा
वाधा, f. pain, affliction, opposition. (See बाध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधुक्य|वाधुक्यं
वाधुक्य वाधुक्य, अम्, n. (fr. वधुका),<BR>marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधू
वाधू वाधू, ऊस्, f. (probably connected<BR>with rt. 1. वह्), a vessel, boat, raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधूय
वाधूय वाधूय, अम्, n. (fr. वधू), Ved. a<BR>bride's garment, bridal dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाध्रीणस|वाध्रीणसः
वाध्रीणस वाध्रीणस, अस्, m. a rhinoceros;<BR>(according to some also वाध्रीनस.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
वान 3. वान, अम्, n. (fr. rt. वे), the act of<BR>weaving, sewing; a mat of straw; a hole in the wall<BR>of a house.<BR>—वान-दण्ड, अस्, m. a weaver's loom;<BR>[cf. वाण-दण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीय
वानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be woven, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
वान 4. वान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. वन), belonging<BR>or relating to a wood or forest; relating to a dwelling<BR>in a wood or to a house, &c.; (अम्), n. a multitude<BR>of woods, collection of groves or thickets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानप्रस्थ|वानप्रस्थः
वानप्रस्थ, अस्, m. (fr. वन-प्रस्थ), a<BR>Brāhman of the third order who has passed through<BR>the stages of student and householder and has left<BR>his house and family for the woods, (see आश्रम);<BR>a hermit, anchorite; a class of supernatural beings;<BR>the tree Bassia Latifolia; the Palāśa tree, Butea<BR>Frondosa.<BR>—वानप्रस्थ-धर्म, अस्, m. the law<BR>or duty of a Vānaprastha.<BR>—वानप्रस्थाश्रम<BR>(˚थ-आश्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. the Āśrama or order of<BR>a Vānaprastha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानर|वानरः
वानर, अस्, m. (fr. वनर, which is probably fr.<BR>1. वन, ‘a wood;’ according to others fr. वा, ‘like,’<BR>नर, ‘a man’), a monkey, ape; (ई), f. a female<BR>monkey or ape; cowach, Carpopogon Pruriens; (अस्,<BR>ई, अम्), belonging to a monkey, monkey-like.<BR>—वा-<BR>नर-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘dear to monkeys,’ the tree<BR>Mimusops Kauki.<BR>—वानराक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘monkey-eyed,’ a wild goat.<BR>—वानराघात (˚र-<BR>आघ्˚), अस्, m. ‘monkey-stroke,’ i. e. ‘struck or in-<BR>jured by monkeys,’ the tree Symplocos Racemosa<BR>(commonly called Lodhra or Lodh).<BR>—वानराप-<BR>सद (˚र-अप्˚), अस्, m. a contemptible monkey.<BR>—वानरेन्द्र (˚र-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘monkey-chief,’<BR>epithet of Sugrīva; of Hanu-mat.<BR>—वानरेश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानल|वानलः
वानल, अस्, m. (probably fr. 1. वन), the black<BR>species of Tulasī or holy basil, Ocymum Sanctum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानस्पत्य|वानस्पत्यः
वानस्पत्य, अस्, m. (fr. वनस्-पति), a tree the<BR>fruit of which is produced from blossom (= पुष्प-<BR>जात-फल-वृक्ष; cf. वनस्-पति, which is said<BR>to be used in a different sense; examples of a Vānas-<BR>patya are the Mango, Eugenia, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाना
वाना, f. (probably fr. 1. वन), a quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीर|वानीरः
वानीर, अस्, m. (fr. 1. वन, ‘a wood or water’), a<BR>sort of cane or ratan, Calamus Rotang, a reed.<BR>—वा-<BR>नीर-गृह, अम्, n. or आस्, m. pl. an arbour of reeds.<BR>—वानीर-ज, अम्, n. a plant (= कुष्ठ, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीरक|वानीरकः
वानीरक, अस्, m. a sort of rush or grass, Saccha-<BR>rum Munja; [cf. मुञ्ज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानेय|वानेयं
वानेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to a wood<BR>or to water, &c.; (अस्), m. the fragrant grass Cyperus<BR>Rotundus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्या
वान्या, f. a collection of woods, multitude of<BR>groves or thickets; [cf. वन्या.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानायु|वानायुः
वानायु वानायु, उस्, m. (fr. वनायु), a coun-<BR>try to the north-west of India, also called Vanāyu.<BR>—वानायु-ज, अस्, m. ‘Vānāyu-born,’ a Vānāyu or Va-<BR>nāyu horse (regarded as of a particularly good breed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीर|वानीरः
वानीर वानीर. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्त|वांत|वान्तः
वान्त वान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वम्), vomited,<BR>ejected from the mouth, effused; one who has vo-<BR>mited; वान्ते, ind. when one has vomited; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Particular family of priests.<BR>—वान्त-वृष्टि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, (a cloud &c.) that has vomited out rain.<BR>—वान्ताद (˚त-अद˚), अस्, m. ‘eating what is vomited,’<BR>a dog.<BR>—वान्ताशिन् (˚त-अश्˚), ई, m. ‘eating what is<BR>vomited,’ a foul-feeding demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ति|वांति|वान्तिः
वान्ति, इस्, f. the act of vomiting, ejecting from<BR>the mouth.<BR>—वान्ति-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing vomiting,<BR>emetic; (त्), m. the thorny plant Vangueria Spinosa.<BR>—वान्ति-द, अस्, आ, अम्, causing vomiting, emetic;<BR>(आ), f. a medicinal plant (= कटुकी); Helleborus<BR>Niger or Wrightea Antidysenterica or Calotropis<BR>Gigantea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्त्वा
वान्त्वा, ind. having vomited, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाम|वामं|वामः
1. वाम, अस्, m. (for 2. see below), the act of<BR>vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामक|वामकः
1. वामक, अस्, &c. (for 2. see col. 3), one who<BR>vomits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिन्
वामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, vomiting, ejecting from the<BR>mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्दन
वान्दन वान्दन, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Duvasyu (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 100).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप|वापः
वाप वाप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वप् or connected<BR>with Caus. of rt. वे), sowing seed; weaving; shear-<BR>ing, shaving.<BR>—वाप-दण्ड, अस्, m. a weaver's<BR>loom; [cf. वाय-दण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापक|वापकः
वापक, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to sow (seed &c.);<BR>causing to weave, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापन|वापनं
वापन, अम्, n. the act of causing to sow or<BR>sowing; shaving, shearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापि|वापिः
वापि, इस्, or वापी, f. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV.<BR>124. fr. rt. वप्), a large oblong pond, an oblong<BR>reservoir of water, a pool or lake; क्रीडा-वापी, f.,<BR>Ved. ‘pleasure-pond,’ a pond in which tortoises,<BR>fishes, &c. are kept for amusement.<BR>—वापी-ह, अस्,<BR>m. ‘abandoning pools,’ the Cātaka bird, Cuculus<BR>Melanoleucos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापित|वापितं
वापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be sown, sown (as<BR>seed); shaven, shorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप्य|वाप्यं
वाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sown, to be cast or<BR>thrown; (अस्), m. Costus Speciosus (= कुष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाम|वामं|वामः
वाम 2. वाम, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. 1. 139. fr. rt. 2. वा; according to others<BR>fr. rt. 1. वन्, ‘to hurt or to like’), reverse, adverse,<BR>opposite, contrary, inverted; left, not right; crooked;<BR>bad, vile, base, wicked; short; beautiful, handsome,<BR>pleasing; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva; of Kāma (god of<BR>love); a breast, udder; a pot-herb, Chenopodium<BR>Album; an animal, sentient being; a snake; (अम्),<BR>n. anything desirable or pleasing, wealth, possessions;<BR>(आ), f. a woman; N. of Gaurī; of Lakṣmī; of<BR>Sarasvatī; (ई), f. a mare; a she-ass; a young<BR>female elephant; the female of the jackal; [cf. Old<BR>Germ. winistar; Angl. Sax. wynstre.]<BR>—वाम-<BR>जात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. produced from wealth.<BR>—वा-<BR>म-जुष्ट, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work (= वाम-<BR>केश्वर-तन्त्र).<BR>—वाम-ता, f. or वाम-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. contrariety, perverseness; wickedness, craftiness;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-c" target="_blank">Page0903-c+ 80</a>]<BR>disfavour; loveliness.<BR>—वाम-दृश्, क्, f. a woman.<BR>—वाम-देव, अस्, m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi (having<BR>the patronymic Gautama, author of the hymns Ṛg-<BR>veda IV. 1 — 41, 45 — 48, comprising nearly the whole<BR>fourth Maṇḍala); of Śiva; of an author.<BR>—वाम-<BR>देव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic of Aṃho-muc (author<BR>of Ṛg-veda X. 127); of Bṛhad-uktha; of Mūrdhan-<BR>vat.<BR>—वाम-नीति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. leading or guiding<BR>to wealth, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI. 47, 7. वननीया-<BR>नां धनानां नेतृ.)<BR>—वाम-नेत्र, अम्, n. a<BR>mystical name of the long vowel ई; (आ), f. a woman<BR>with beautiful eyes, a handsome woman in general.<BR>—वाम-मार्ग, अस्, m. the left hand way or ritual;<BR>see वामाचार.<BR>—वाम-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, fine-<BR>eyed; (आ), f. a handsome-eyed woman.<BR>—वाम-<BR>शील, अस्, आ, अम्, refractory in disposition; (अस्), m.<BR>an epithet of Kāma.<BR>—वामाक्ष (˚म-अक्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, having beautiful eyes; (ई), f. a woman with<BR>lovely eyes.<BR>—वामाक्षि (˚म-अक्˚), इ, n. the left eye.<BR>—वामाचार (˚म-आच्˚), अस्, m. the left hand ritual<BR>or doctrine of the Tantras, i. e. the worship of the<BR>Śakti or Female Energy personified as the wife of<BR>Śiva according to the grosser system (in which the<BR>eating of flesh, drinking of spirits, &c. is practised,<BR>cf. दक्षिणाचार).<BR>—वामाचारिन्, ई, m. a follower<BR>of the left hand ritual of the Tantras.<BR>—वामापीडन<BR>(˚म-आप्˚?), अस्, m. the tree Salvadora Persica, &c.<BR>(= पीलु).<BR>—वामावर्त (˚म-आव्˚), अस्, m. a conch-<BR>shell with the spiral running from right to left.<BR>—वामोरु (˚म-ऊरु˚), उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ, having<BR>handsome thighs; (उस् or ऊस्), f. a handsome-thighed<BR>woman.<BR>—वामोरु-तरा or वामोरू-तरा, f. a very<BR>handsome-thighed woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामक|वामकः
2. वामक, अस्, आ, अम्, left, not right; (अम्), n.<BR>a kind of gesture.<BR>—वामकेश्वर-तन्त्र (˚क-ईश्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिका
वामिका, f. an epithet of the goddess Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामन|वामनः
वामन वामन, अस्, आ, अम् (probably fr. 2. वा-<BR>म; said to be fr. rt. वम्), dwarfish, short in stature,<BR>a dwarf; depressed, pressed flat or down; low, vile,<BR>base; (अस्), m. Viṣṇu in his dwarf incarnation, (this<BR>was the fifth of the descents of Viṣṇu, and under-<BR>taken to humble the pride of the Daitya Bali, who<BR>had acquired dominion over the three worlds [see<BR>बलि]; the germ of the story of this incarnation<BR>seems to be contained in Śatapatha-Br. I. 2, 5, 1,<BR>the later legend is given in Rāmāyaṇa I. 31, 2);<BR>the elephant that supports the south quarter; the tree<BR>Alangium Hexapetalum; N. of the author of the<BR>Kāvyālaṅkāra-vṛtti; of the Kāśikā-vṛtti commen-<BR>tary; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras; (ई), f. a female<BR>dwarf; a sort of woman; a mare; a disease of the<BR>Vagina.<BR>—वामन-तनु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ, dwarf-<BR>bodied.<BR>—वामन-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of one<BR>of the eighteen Purāṇas (said to have been related<BR>by Pulastya to Nārada, and containing an account<BR>of the dwarf incarnation of Viṣṇu; see पुराण).<BR>—वामन-प्रादुर्भाव, अस्, m. the manifestation<BR>or incarnation of the dwarf; see above.<BR>—वामन-<BR>रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, dwarf-formed, being in the form of<BR>a dwarf.<BR>—वामन-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary on Pāṇini's grammar by Vāmana Jayāditya, (see<BR>काशिक.)<BR>—वामन-वृत्ति-टीका, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary by Maheśvara on the Kāvyālaṅkāra-vṛtti.<BR>—वा-<BR>मन-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular Vrata to be<BR>observed on the twelfth day of Śrāvaṇa in celebration<BR>of Viṣṇu's dwarf incarnation.<BR>—वामन-सूक्त, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Vedic hymn.<BR>—वामन-स्वामिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—वामनाकृति (˚न-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>dwarf-shaped, dwarfish.<BR>—वामनाचार्य (˚न-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—वामनावतार (˚न-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. the dwarf incarnation; see under वामन<BR>above.<BR>—वामनावतार-कथन, अम्, n. the story<BR>of the dwarf incarnation, N. of a chapter of the<BR>Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—वामनी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, pressed<BR>down, shortened, flattened.<BR>—वामनेन्द्र-स्वा-<BR>मिन्, ई, m. a proper N.<BR>—वामनोपपुराण (˚न-<BR>उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनिका
वामनिका, f. a female dwarf; a sort of woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलूर|वामलूरः
वामलूर वामलूर, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">Page0904-a+ 77</a>]<BR>वम्रा, वल्मी, वल्मीक), an ant-hill, mole-hill,<BR>hillock thrown up by white ants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0903-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिल|वामिलः
वामिल वामिल, अस्, आ, अम् (probably con-<BR>nected with 2. वाम), proud, haughty, deceitful;<BR>handsome, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय|वायः
वाय वाय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वे), weaving,<BR>sewing.<BR>—वाय-दण्ड, अस्, m. a weaver's loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायक|वायकः
वायक, अस्, m. a weaver [cf. पट्टिका-व्˚]; a<BR>heap, multitude, number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायिन्
वायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, weaving, sewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायत
वायत वायत, अस्, m. (fr. वयत्), Ved. ‘son<BR>of Vayat,’ a patronymic of Pāśa-dyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायन|वायनं
वायन वायन or वायनक, अम्, n. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. 2. वा), sweetmeats or cakes which may be<BR>eaten during a religious fast, presents of sweetmeats<BR>&c. (forming part of an offering to a deity, or pre-<BR>pared on festive occasions, such as marriages &c., and<BR>sent as presents to friends and acquaintances).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव
वायव वायव. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायस|वायसः
वायस वायस, अस्, m. (probably fr. वयस्,<BR>‘age,’ but according to Uṇādi-s. III. 120. fr. rt. वय्),<BR>‘the long-lived one,’ a crow; Agallochum or fragrant<BR>aloe (= अगुरु); turpentine; (अस्, ई, अम्), used by<BR>crows (?); consisting of birds; (ई), f. a female crow;<BR>a species of fig, Ficus Oppositifolia; a particular<BR>vegetable, Solanum Indicum.<BR>—वायसादनी (˚स-<BR>अद्˚), f. a kind of plant or tree (= काक-तुण्डी).<BR>—वायसारि (˚स-अरि˚), इस्, m. or वायसाराति (˚स-<BR>अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘crow's enemy,’ an owl.<BR>—वायसाह्वा<BR>(˚स-आह्˚), f. an esculent vegetable, Solanum Indicum<BR>(= काक-माचिका).<BR>—वायसेक्षु (˚स-इक्˚), उस्, m.<BR>a sort of long grass, Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसोली
वायसोली or वायसोलिका, f. a medicinal root (=<BR>काकोली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायु|वायुः
वायु वायु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. वा), air, wind,<BR>the god of the wind (often associated with Indra in the<BR>Ṛg-veda, but not occupying a very prominent posi-<BR>tion; in the Puruṣa-sūkta he is said to have sprung<BR>from the breath of Puruṣa, and elsewhere is described<BR>as the son-in-law of Tvaṣṭṛ; he is said to move in<BR>a shining car drawn by a pair of red or purple horses<BR>or by several teams consisting of ninety-nine or a<BR>hundred or even a thousand horses; he is often<BR>made to occupy the same chariot with Indra, and in<BR>conjunction with him honoured with the first draught<BR>of the Soma libation; he is rarely connected with<BR>the Maruts, although in 1. 134, 4. he is said to have<BR>begotten them from the rivers of heaven; he is<BR>regent of the north-west quarter, see लोक-पाल);<BR>the air of the body, a vital air (of which five are<BR>reckoned, viz. प्राण, अपान, समान, उदान,<BR>and व्यान); morbid affection of the windy humor.<BR>—वायु-केतु, उस्, m. ‘wind-sign,’ i. e. ‘sign of wind,’<BR>dust.<BR>—वायु-केश, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. having hair<BR>(waving) in the wind (said of the Gandharvas).<BR>—वायु-कोण, अस्, m. ‘wind-corner,’ the north-west.<BR>—वायु-गण्ड, अस्, m. ‘wind-swelling,’ flatulence,<BR>indigestion.<BR>—वायु-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, going like the<BR>wind, swift as the wind, fleet.<BR>—वायु-गीत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, chanted by the breeze.<BR>—वायु-गुल्म, अस्, m.<BR>‘wind-cluster,’ a whirlwind, hurricane; a whirlpool,<BR>eddy.<BR>—वायु-गोचर, अस्, m. the track or range of<BR>the wind.<BR>—वायु-गोपा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. having<BR>the Wind as protector.<BR>—वायु-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘wind-seized,’ affected by wind, flatulent, epileptic,<BR>mad.<BR>—वायु-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘wind-destroying,’<BR>curing windy disorders.<BR>—वायु-ज, ‘air-born,’ N.<BR>of a tree.<BR>—वायु-जात, अस्, m. ‘wind-born,’ epithet<BR>of Hanu-mat.<BR>—वायु-तनय or वायु-नन्दन,<BR>अस्, m. = वायु-पुत्र.<BR>—वायु-दारु, उस्, m. ‘air-<BR>tearer, air-scatterer,’ a cloud.<BR>—वायु-नाना-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. diversity or multiplicity of air (said to be inferred<BR>from the concurrence [सम्मूर्छन] of two winds).<BR>—वायु-निघ्न, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘subject to wind,’ mad,<BR>frantic.<BR>—वायु-निवृत्ति, इस्, f. ‘cessation of wind,’<BR>a calm, lull; cure of windy disorders.<BR>—वायु-पञ्-<BR>चक, अम्, n. the set of five vital airs.<BR>—वायु-प-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-b" target="_blank">Page0904-b+ 80</a>]<BR>रमाणु, उस्, m. a primary aerial atom.<BR>—वायु-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son of the wind,’ epithet of<BR>Bhīma; of Hanu-mat.<BR>—वायु-पुराण, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of one of the eighteen Purāṇas, (it is probably<BR>one of the oldest, and is supposed to have been<BR>revealed by the god Vāyu; it treats of the creation<BR>of the world, the origin of the four classes, the<BR>worship of Śiva, &c.)<BR>—वायु-फल, अम्, n. ‘wind-<BR>fruit,’ the rainbow; hail.<BR>—वायु-भक्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, air-eating, fasting; (अस्), m. a snake; an ascetic.<BR>—वायु-भक्षण, अम्, n. the act of eating or<BR>living on air, fasting.<BR>—वायु-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>come air, become like the wind; going everywhere<BR>at will.<BR>—वायु-मार्ग, अस्, m. the path or track of<BR>the wind.<BR>—वायु-रुग्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, broken off by<BR>the wind.<BR>—वायु-रोषा, f. ‘raging with wind,’<BR>night.<BR>—वायु-लक्षण, अम्, n. the character or<BR>property of air (viz. touch).<BR>—वायु-वर्त्मन्, आ, m.<BR>‘wind-path,’ the atmosphere, sky, heaven.<BR>—वायु-<BR>वाह, अस्, m. ‘having the wind for a vehicle,’ smoke,<BR>vapour.<BR>—वायु-वाहिनी, f. ‘wind-conveying,’ a vessel<BR>of the body, artery, vein, nerve, &c. (supposed to con-<BR>vey the aerial humor).<BR>—वायु-वेग, अस्, m. the ve-<BR>locity of the wind, a gust or blast of wind; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having the velocity of wind, fleet as the wind; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—वायुवेग-सम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, equal to the velocity of wind, swift as<BR>the wind.<BR>—वायु-संहिता, f. the ‘Vāyu compen-<BR>dium’ or collection of legends according to the Vāyu-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—वायु-सख, अस्, or वायु-सखि, खा, m.<BR>‘wind-friend, having the wind for a friend,’ fire.<BR>—वायु-सम, अस्, आ, अम्, equal to the wind, swift;<BR>like air or wind, unsubstantial.<BR>—वायु-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, m. ‘wind-born,’ epithet of Hanu-mat.<BR>—वायु-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. = वायु-पुत्र above.<BR>—वायु-हीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of wind, having a deficiency of<BR>the windy humor.<BR>—वायु-अग्नि, ई, m. du. Vāyu<BR>and Agni, the gods of wind and fire.<BR>—वायु-आस्पद,<BR>अम्, n. ‘place or site of the wind,’ the atmosphere,<BR>sky, ether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव
वायव, अस्, ई, अम्, windy, relating or belonging<BR>to the wind or to Vāyu; given by Vāyu; aerial; (ई),<BR>f. the quarter or region of the wind, the north-west<BR>(as presided over by Vāyu in his character of the<BR>sixth Loka-pāla).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायवीय
वायवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the wind or<BR>Vāyu, belonging to air or wind, aerial.<BR>—वायवीय-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव्य|वायव्यं
वायव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the wind, coming<BR>from or relating to Vāyu, sacred to Vāyu, aerial.<BR>—वायव्य-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय्य
वाय्य वाय्य, अस्, m., Ved. ‘son of Vayya,’<BR>epithet of Satya-śravas (represented as a poet and an<BR>Ātreya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्
वार् वार्, र्, n. (fr. rt. वृ), water; [cf. व-<BR>रुण: cf. also Zend वार, ‘rain:’ Gr. οὖρο-ν,<BR>οὐρ-έ-ω, οὐρ-ί-α, οὐράνη, οὐρή-θρα, οὔρη-μα, perhaps<BR>also ὑρτήρ, ὕρχη: Lat. ur-ina, urin-a-ri, urina-<BR>tor, urceus, urna; mare; Old Germ. mari:<BR>Slav. more; Hib. burn, ‘water;’ fairge, ‘ocean;’<BR>fual, ‘urine;’ muir: Welsh mor.]<BR>—वाः-किटि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘water-pig,’ a porpoise, the Gangetic porpoise (=<BR>शिशुमार).<BR>—वाः-पुष्प, अम्, n. cloves.<BR>—वाः-<BR>सदन, अम्, n. ‘water-abode,’ a reservoir of water,<BR>cistern, large water-jar.<BR>—वाः-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>standing or remaining in water.<BR>—वारां-निधि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘receptacle of waters,’ the ocean.<BR>—वार्-<BR>आसन, अम्, n. ‘water-seat,’ a reservoir of water,<BR>cistern, large water-jar.<BR>—वार्-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. to be performed with water, (Sāy. = वार्भिर्<BR>निष्पाद्य); granting or effecting rain.<BR>—वार्-च,<BR>अस्, m. ‘water-going,’ a gander, goose (Vopa-deva<BR>XXVI. 33).<BR>—वार्-द, अस्, आ, अम्, water-giving;<BR>(अस्), m. a cloud.<BR>—वार्-दर, अम्, n. water; speech;<BR>silk; the seed of the Abrus Precatorius; the seed of<BR>the Mango; a conch-shell (= दक्षिणावर्त); a<BR>sort of curl on the right side of a horse's neck (re-<BR>garded as an auspicious mark).<BR>—वार्दल, अम्, n.<BR>(fr. वार्द + ल), a rainy day, bad weather; (अस्), m.<BR>an ink-stand.<BR>—वार्-धि, इस्, m. ‘water-holder,’ the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">Page0904-c+ 79</a>]<BR>ocean.<BR>—वार्धि-भव or वार्-धेय, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of salt (= द्रोणि-लवण).<BR>—वार्धि-वत्, ind.<BR>like the ocean.<BR>—वार्-भट, अस्, m. ‘water-com-<BR>batant,’ an alligator.<BR>—वार्-मुच्, क्, m. ‘water-dis-<BR>charger,’ a cloud.<BR>—वार्-राशि, इस्, m. ‘water-heap,’<BR>the ocean.<BR>—वार्-वट, अस्, m. ‘water-enclosure (?),’<BR>a boat, vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार|वारं|वारः
1. वार, अस्, m. (for 2. see p. 905, col. 1), anything<BR>which covers or surrounds, a cover; a multitude, quan-<BR>tity, heap; a flock, herd, troop; time; a day of the<BR>week [cf. रवि-व्˚, सोम-व्˚, मङ्गल-व्˚, बुध-व्˚,<BR>गुरु-व्˚, शुक्र-व्˚, शनि-व्˚]; a moment, occasion, op-<BR>portunity; turn, time (used adverbially like the English<BR>‘times,’ or like the French ‘fois,’ e. g. वारेण or<BR>बहु-वारम् or वारं वारम्, many times, repeat-<BR>edly, often); N. of Śiva; anything which causes an<BR>obstruction, a gate, door, door-way; the plant Achy-<BR>ranthes Aspera (= कुब्ज); the opposite bank of a<BR>river or of the sea, (for पार); (अम्), n. a vessel for<BR>holding spirituous liquor; [cf. Gr. ἦρα: Hib. vair,<BR>‘an hour, time;’ air uairibh, ‘sometimes;’ Cambro-<BR>Brit. aur; Old Island. var in tvis-var, ‘twice;’<BR>thris-var, ‘thrice:’ Old Germ. or, o, in zuir-or,<BR>zuir-o, twice:’ Pers. بار bār, ‘time;’ بارى bāre,<BR>‘once;’ ber in September, October, &c.]<BR>—वार-<BR>नारी, f. a common woman, harlot, courtezan.<BR>—वा-<BR>र-बुषा or वार-बूषा, f. the plantain or banana<BR>(= कदली; cf. वारण-बुषा).<BR>—वार-मुख्या,<BR>f. the chief of a number of harlots, a royal<BR>courtezan.<BR>—वार-युवति, इस्, f. or वार-योषित्,<BR>त्, f. a courtezan, harlot; a dancing-girl.<BR>—वार-<BR>वधू, ऊस्, f. the chief of a number of harlots.<BR>—वार-वाण, अस्, अम्, m. n. armour, mail, an iron<BR>cuirass or thick quilted jacket (so called as ‘ward-<BR>ing off arrows,’ cf. वाण-वार).<BR>—वार-वाणि, इस्, m.<BR>a player on the flute; a principal singer, musician; a<BR>judge; a year; (इस् or ई), f. a harlot or the chief of<BR>a number of harlots.<BR>—वार-विलासिनी, f. a harlot.<BR>—वार-वेला, f. a period of the day in which any act<BR>is suspended.<BR>—वार-सुन्दरी, f. a harlot, prostitute.<BR>—वार-सेवा, f. the practice of harlotry, prostitution;<BR>a number of courtezans.<BR>—वार-स्त्री, f. a harlot,<BR>courtezan.<BR>—वाराङ्गना (˚र-अङ्˚), f. a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारक|वारकं|वारकः
वारक, अस्, आ, अम्, restraining, opposing, ob-<BR>structing, resisting, anything which restrains or ob-<BR>structs, an obstacle; (अस्), m. a sort of horse; a<BR>horse in general; one of a horse's paces; (अम्), n.<BR>the seat of pain; a sort of perfume or fragrant grass<BR>(= बाल, ह्री-वेर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकिन्
वारकिन्, ई, m. an opposer, obstructor, enemy;<BR>the ocean; a horse with good marks; an ascetic,<BR>a hermit who lives on leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारण|वारणं|वारणः
वारण, अस्, ई, अम्, warding off, keeping off,<BR>restraining, resisting, opposing; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>restraining, keeping back, warding, warding off,<BR>guarding, protecting, defending, defence, resistance,<BR>opposition, prohibition, obstacle, impediment; (अस्),<BR>m. armour, mail, a cuirass; an elephant.<BR>—वारण-<BR>प्रतिवारण, अस्, आ, अम्, having armour for a de-<BR>fence, protected by armour; keeping off elephants.<BR>—वारण-बुषा or वारण-बुसा, f. the plantain<BR>or banana, Musa Sapientum.<BR>—वारण-वल्लभा, f.<BR>the plantain tree.<BR>—वारण-साहवय, अम्, n. ‘hav-<BR>ing a name synonymous with an elephant,’ epithet<BR>of Hastinā-pura or Hāstina-pura; [cf. गज-साह्वय.]<BR>—वारणेन्द्र (˚ण-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘elephant-chief,’<BR>a large and excellent elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणावत|वारणावतं|वारणावतः
वारणावत, अस्, अम्, m. n., N. of a town (sup-<BR>posed to be the modern Allahabad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणावतक
वारणावतक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Vāraṇāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणीय|वारणीयं
वारणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be warded off, to be<BR>restrained or resisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारयितृ
वारयितृ, ता, m. a protector; a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारयित्वा
वारयित्वा, ind. having warded or driven off, having<BR>restrained or prohibited, having repelled or expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारि|वारिः
वारि, n. water; a fluid, fluidity; a particular drug<BR>or perfume, = बाल, ह्री-वेर; (इस्), f., N. of Saras-<BR>vatī (goddess of speech or eloquence); the place for<BR>tying or fastening an elephant; a captive, prisoner;<BR>(इस् or ई), f. a water-pot, pitcher, jar; a rope for<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-a" target="_blank">Page0905-a+ 80</a>]<BR>fastening an elephant; a hole or trap for catching<BR>elephants.<BR>—वारि-कण्टक, अस्, m. an aquatic plant,<BR>Trapa Bispinosa (= शृङ्गाटक).<BR>—वारि-कर्णिका,<BR>f. the plant Pistia Stratiotes (= ख-मूली).<BR>—वारि-<BR>कर्पूर, अस्, m. the Ilīśa fish, (see इलीश.).<BR>—वारि-<BR>कुब्ज or वारि-कुब्जक, अस्, m. the aquatic plant<BR>Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—वारि-क्रिमि, इस्, m. ‘water-worm,’<BR>a leech.<BR>—वारि-चत्वर, अस्, m. a piece of water;<BR>the aquatic plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—वारि-चर, अस्,<BR>आ or ई, अम्, living or moving in water, aquatic;<BR>(अस्), m. a fish.<BR>—वारि-चामर, अम्, n. a sort of<BR>aquatic fish, Vallisneria (= शैवाल).<BR>—वारि-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, born or produced in or by water; (अस्), m. a<BR>conch-shell; any bivalve shell; (अम्), n. a lotus;<BR>salt.<BR>—वारि-जावन्, see Vopa-deva XXVI. 69.<BR>—वा-<BR>रि-तस्कर, अस्, m. ‘water-thief,’ a cloud.<BR>—वारि-त्रा,<BR>f. ‘protecting from water,’ an umbrella, a screen of<BR>leaves carried on the head as an umbrella.<BR>—वारि-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, water-giving, yielding water; (अस्),<BR>m. a cloud; (अम्), n. a sort of vegetable perfume<BR>(= बाल).<BR>—वारि-दुर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, inaccessible by<BR>reason of water.<BR>—वारि-द्र, अस्, m. the Cātaka<BR>bird, Cuculus Melanoleucus.<BR>—वारि-धर, अस्, m.<BR>‘water-holder,’ a cloud.<BR>—वारि-धारा, f. a shower<BR>of rain.<BR>—वारि-धि, इस्, m. ‘water-holder,’ the sea,<BR>ocean.<BR>—वारि-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of the waters,’ the<BR>deity Varuṇa; the ocean; a cloud; the habitation of<BR>the serpent race.<BR>—वारि-निधि, इस्, m. ‘water-recep-<BR>tacle,’ the ocean.<BR>—वारि-पथ, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘water-<BR>path,’ a voyage.<BR>—वारि-पथिक, अस्, ई, अम्, proceeding<BR>or conveyed by water.<BR>—वारि-पर्णी or वारि-पालिका, f.<BR>Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—वारि-प्रवाह, अस्, m. a current<BR>or flow of water, a water-fall, cascade.<BR>—वारि-प्रश्नी,<BR>f. the aquatic plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—वारि-बदरा,<BR>f. the plant Flacourtia Cataphracta (= प्राचीनाम-<BR>लक).<BR>—वारि-बालक, अम्, n. a perfume (= बाल).<BR>—वारि-भव, अम्, n. (probably) a kind of plant<BR>(= श्रोतोञ्जन).<BR>—वारि-मसि, इस्, m. ‘water-ink,’ a<BR>cloud.<BR>—वारि-मुच्, क्, m. ‘water-discharger,’ a cloud.<BR>—वारि-मूलि, f. the aquatic plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—वारि-र, अस्, आ, अम्, giving or shedding water;<BR>(अस्), m. a cloud.<BR>—वारि-रथ, अस्, m. ‘water-car-<BR>riage,’ a raft, boat, float.<BR>—वारिरारव (˚र-आर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, sounding like clouds or like thunder.<BR>—वारि-राशि, इस्, m. ‘water-heap,’ a large body of<BR>water, the sea, ocean; a lake.<BR>—वारि-रुह, अम्, n.<BR>‘water-grower,’ a lotus.<BR>—वारि-लोमन्, आ, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing watery hair,’ epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—वारि-वदन,<BR>अम्, n. the fruit Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR>—वारि-वर,<BR>अम्, n. the fruit of the tree Carissa Carandas (=<BR>कर-मर्द).<BR>—वारि-वल्लभा, f. a kind of plant<BR>(= विदारी).<BR>—वारि-वास, अस्, m. a distiller of spirit,<BR>dealer in spirituous liquors.<BR>—वारि-वाह or वारि-<BR>वाहन, अस्, m. ‘water-bearer,’ a cloud.<BR>—वारिवाह-<BR>जाल, अम्, n. a mass of clouds.<BR>—वारि-श, अस्, m.<BR>(said to be fr. वारि + श fr. rt. शी, to sleep), N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—वारि-सम्भव, अम्, n. ‘water-produced,’<BR>cloves; a kind of antimony (= सौवीराञ्जन); the<BR>root of the plant Andropogon Muricatus (= उशीर);<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of cane (= यावनाल-शर).<BR>—वारि-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing in water, reflected in the<BR>water (said of the sun, Maun IV. 37).<BR>—वारीश<BR>(˚रि-ईश˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of waters,’ the ocean.<BR>—वार्य्-<BR>उद्भव, अम्, n. ‘water-born,’ a lotus.<BR>—वार्य्-ओक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘water-dwelling,’ a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0904-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारित
वारित, अस्, आ, अम्, warded off, prevented, hin-<BR>dered, impeded, restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारीट|वारीटः
वारीट, अस्, m. (said to be fr. वारि, a trap, + अट,<BR>going), an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारु|वारुः
वारु, उस्, m. a royal or war elephant carrying a<BR>standard (= विजय-कुञ्जर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य|वार्यं|वार्यः|वार्य्य|वार्य्यं
वार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be warded off or prevented,<BR>to be checked or impeded, to be stopped or obstructed;<BR>to be chosen, to be selected or appointed; eligible,<BR>desirable, excellent; (अम्), n. anything to be chosen<BR>or desired, a blessing, boon; (आणि), n. pl. goods,<BR>possessions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्यमाण|वार्य्यमाण
वार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being prevented, being<BR>impeded or prohibited or resisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार|वारं|वारः
वार 2. वार, अस्, m., Ved. for वाल = बाल,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">Page0905-b+ 73</a>]<BR>a tail; the tail (of sheep &c.) used to filter Soma<BR>juice, (also अम्, n.); (आस्), m. pl. the hairs of a tail.<BR>—वार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a tail, (see<BR>Nirukta I. 20.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकीर|वारकीरः
वारकीर वारकीर, अस्, m. a wife's brother,<BR>brother-in-law (= श्यालक); submarine fire (= वा-<BR>डव); a louse; a small comb; a horse of high spirit,<BR>war horse, charger; a bearer of burdens, porter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारङ्क|वारंक|वारंकः|वारङ्कः
वारङ्क वारङ्क, अस्, m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारङ्ग|वारंग|वारंगः|वारङ्गः
वारङ्ग वारङ्ग, अस्, m. the handle of a<BR>sword or knife or sickle, &c.; the narrow end to<BR>which the handle is fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारट|वारटं
वारट वारट, अम्, n. a field; a number of<BR>fields; (आ), f. a goose (= वरटा, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारला
वारला, f. a wasp; a goose (= वरटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणसी
वारणसी वारणसी, f. = वाराणसी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारतन्तवीय
वारतन्तवीय वारतन्तवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, com-<BR>posed by Vara-tantu (as a book &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारत्र|वारत्रं
वारत्र वारत्र, अम्, n. (fr. वरत्रा), a<BR>leather thong, leather fit for making thongs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाररुच
वाररुच वाररुच, अस्, ई, अम्, composed by<BR>Vara-ruci.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारला
वारला वारला, f. See under वारट above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारलीक|वारलीकः
वारलीक वारलीक, अस्, m. a sort of grass,<BR>Eleusine Indica (= वल्व-जा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसी
वाराणसी वाराणसी, f. the holy city Benares,<BR>(also written वराणसी, q. v.)<BR>—वाराणसी-माहात्-<BR>म्य, अम्, n. ‘the glory of Benares,’ N. of a section<BR>in the Kūrma and other Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसेय|वाराणसेयः
वाराणसेय, अस्, ई, अम्, produced at or born in<BR>Benares, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराह|वाराहः
वाराह वाराह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वराह), re-<BR>lating or belonging to a boar, boarish; (अस्), m. a<BR>boar; a kind of tree, = महा-पिण्डीतक; (ई), f. a sow;<BR>N. of one of the divine mothers or Mātṛs attending<BR>on Skanda; of a Yoginī; of the Śakti of Viṣṇu<BR>in the form of a boar; the earth; a measure; a<BR>particular kind of bulbous plant (said to be an escu-<BR>lent root or yam, = बदरा, घृष्टि).<BR>—वाराह-<BR>कर्णी, f. or वाराह-पत्त्री, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>अश्व-गन्धा, q. v.).<BR>—वाराह-कल्प, अस्, m. ‘boar<BR>Kalpa,’ N. of the now existing Kalpa or day of<BR>Brahmā (being the first of the second Parārdha<BR>of Brahmā's existence).<BR>—वाराह-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—वाराह-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of<BR>one of the eighteen Purāṇas (said to have been<BR>revealed to the Earth by Viṣṇu in the form of a<BR>boar; it contains an account of the creation, the<BR>various forms of Viṣṇu, and a vast number of<BR>legends and directions relating to the Vaiṣṇava sect).<BR>—वाराहाङ्गी (˚ह-अङ्˚), f. the plant Croton Poly-<BR>andrum (= दन्ती).<BR>—वाराही-कन्द, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of bulbous plant (= ब्राह्मी-कन्द).<BR>—वाराही-तन्-<BR>त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराहीय
वाराहीय, अम्, n., N. of a work or a class of<BR>works; [cf. यामलीय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराह्या
वाराह्या, f. a female descendant of Varāha (Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 78).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुठ|वारुठः
वारुठ वारुठ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>वृ), a bier, the bed on which a corpse is carried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण|वारुणं|वारुणः
वारुण वारुण, अस्, ई, अम्, connected with or<BR>belonging to Varuṇa, sacred to or given by Varuṇa, q. v.;<BR>epithet of a weapon; (अस्), m., N. of one of the nine<BR>divisions of Bhārata Varṣa; (अम्), n. water; (ई), f.<BR>the western quarter or region presided over by Varuṇa<BR>[cf. लोक-पाल]; the west; N. of the lunar asterism<BR>commonly called Śata-bhiṣaj (of which Varuṇa is<BR>the ruling deity; cf. नक्षत्र); a particular kind<BR>of spirit (prepared from hogweed ground with the<BR>juice of the date or palm and then distilled), any<BR>spirituous liquor; a species of Dūrbā grass.<BR>—वारु-<BR>ण-कर्मन्, अ, n. ‘Varuṇa's work,’ any work con-<BR>nected with the supply of water, the digging of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">Page0905-c+ 75</a>]<BR>tanks or wells, &c.<BR>—वारुण-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR>—वारुणी-वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘beloved<BR>by the asterism Vāruṇī,’ epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—वारु-<BR>णेन्द्र (˚ण-इन्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वारुणे-<BR>श्वर-तीर्थ (˚ण-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—वारुणोपपुराण (˚ण-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an<BR>Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणि|वारुणिः
वारुणि, इस्, m. ‘son of Varuṇa,’ the saint Agastya;<BR>a patronymic of Bhṛgu; of Satya-dhṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण्ड|वारुंड|वारुंडः|वारुण्डः
वारुण्ड वारुण्ड, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>वृ), the chief of the serpent race; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>the rheum or excretion of the eyes; the wax of the<BR>ear; a vessel for baling water out of a boat; (ई), f.<BR>a door-step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारेन्द्री|वारेंद्री
वारेन्द्री वारेन्द्री, f. (said to be fr. वरेन्-<BR>द्र), N. of a tract of country north of the Ganges or<BR>a part of Bengal and Behar now called Rājṣāhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्कार्य
वार्कार्य वार्-कार्य, &c. See under वार्,<BR>p. 904, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्केण्य
वार्केण्य वार्केण्य, अस्, m. (fem. वार्केणी), ac-<BR>cording to Pāṇ. V. 3, 115. this word is formed from<BR>वृक, and the pl. is वृकास्, which appears to mean<BR>‘soldiers or fighting men in the country Vāhīka.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष
वार्क्ष वार्क्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वृक्ष), made<BR>of or belonging to a tree; consisting of trees, arboreous;<BR>made of bark; (ई), f., N. of a sort of female Dryad<BR>mentioned in the Mahā-bhārata; (अम्), n. a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष्य|वार्क्ष्यं
वार्क्ष्य, अस्, ई, अम्, made of a tree, made with<BR>trees; (अम्), n. a fence &c. made with felled trees<BR>or wooden stakes, a stockade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्णिक|वार्णिकः
वार्णिक वार्णिक, अस्, m. (fr. वर्ण), a scribe,<BR>writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ता|वार्त्ता
वार्ता वार्ता, f., often incorrectly written<BR>for वार्त्ता. See under वार्त्त below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ताक|वार्ताकः|वार्त्ताक|वार्त्ताकः
वार्ताक वार्ताक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. वृत्, Uṇā-<BR>di-s. III. 79), the egg-plant, Solanum Melongena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ताकि|वार्ताकिः|वार्त्ताकि
वार्ताकि, इस्, or वार्ताकी, f. = वार्ताक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ताकिन्|वार्त्ताकिन्
वार्ताकिन्, ई, m. = वार्ताक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ताकु|वार्ताकुः|वार्त्ताकु|वार्त्ताकुः
वार्ताकु, उस्, m. (or according to some f.) = वार्-<BR>ताक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्तिका|वार्त्तिका
वार्तिका वार्तिका, f. (fr. वर्तक, q. v.), a<BR>kind of quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्तीर
वार्तीर वार्तीर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वर्तीर), con-<BR>nected with a quail or partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्त|वार्त|वार्त्तं|वार्त्तः
वार्त्त वार्त्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वृत्ति, cf. वृत्त),<BR>being in a good state, healthy, hale, well; practising<BR>any business or profession; (आ), f. abiding, staying,<BR>being; livelihood, business, profession; agriculture,<BR>trade, the occupation of the Vaiśya; an account of<BR>anything that has happened, tidings, report, rumour,<BR>news, intelligence, (in this sense sometimes वार्त्तास्,<BR>pl.); a particular figure of rhetoric, simple descrip-<BR>tion, the mere narration of facts without rhetorical or<BR>poetical embellishment; the egg-plant [cf. वार्ताक];<BR>(अम्), n. welfare, health; chaff.<BR>—वार्त्ता-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. the practice of agriculture or trade.<BR>—वार्त्ता-<BR>नुयोग (˚ता-अन्˚), अस्, m. inquiry after news or<BR>health.<BR>—वार्त्ता-मात्र, अम्, n. mere report; super-<BR>ficial knowledge.<BR>—वार्त्तारम्भ (˚ता-आर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>commercial enterprise, (according to Kullūka कृषि-<BR>बाणिज्य-पशुपालनादि-वार्त्ता तद्-आरम्भो ध-<BR>नोपायार्थः.)<BR>—वार्त्ता-वह, अस्, m. a news-<BR>bearer, messenger; a vendor of grain, rice, oil, &c.,<BR>a chandler.<BR>—वार्त्ता-वृत्ति, इस्, m. one whose<BR>business is agriculture, a householder.<BR>—वार्त्ता-<BR>व्यतिकर, अस्, m. the passing of a rumour from<BR>one to another, general report, common rumour.<BR>—वार्त्ता-हर, अस्, m. a carrier of tidings, mes-<BR>senger, courier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तायन|वार्तायन|वार्त्तायनः
वार्त्तायन, अस्, m. a news-bearer, newsmonger,<BR>intelligencer, spy, emissary, agent, ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तिक|वार्तिक|वार्त्तिकं|वार्त्तिकः
वार्त्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (sometimes written वार्तिक),<BR>relating to news, bringing or conveying intelligence,<BR>&c.; explanatory, glossarial, containing or relating to<BR>a critical gloss or annotation, see वार्त्तिकम् below;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">Page0906-a+ 73</a>]<BR>(अस्), m. an intelligencer, an informer, spy, agent,<BR>envoy; a man of the third or Vaiśya tribe, a hus-<BR>bandman, trader; (इका), f. a sort of quail, (more<BR>properly वार्तिका; cf. वर्तक); (अम्), n. an ex-<BR>planatory or supplementary rule, critical gloss or<BR>annotation (added to a grammatical or philosophical<BR>Sūtra and defined to be ‘the exposition of the mean-<BR>ing, of that which is said, of that which is left unsaid,<BR>and of that which is ill or imperfectly said;’ the term<BR>Vārttika is, however, especially applied to Kātyāya-<BR>na's critical annotations on the aphorisms of Pāṇini's<BR>grammar, the object of each Vārttika being to limit<BR>a too general rule, amplify a too limited one, and<BR>give the relations of the Sūtras of Pāṇini to each<BR>other).<BR>—वार्त्तिक-कार, अस्, m. an epithet of Kā-<BR>tyāyana as the author of the Vārttikas to Pāṇini's<BR>grammatical aphorisms; of Kumārila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0905-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्रघ्न|वार्त्त्रघ्नः|वार्त्रघ्नः
वार्त्रघ्न वार्त्रघ्न, अस्, m. (fr. वृत्र-घ्न),<BR>‘son of the Vṛtra-slayer,’ epithet of Arjuna (as son<BR>of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्रहत्य
वार्त्रहत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to the<BR>destruction of Vṛtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द|वार्दः
वार्द वार्-द, वार्-दर, वार्दल. See under<BR>वार्, p. 904, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक
वार्द्धक वार्द्धक, अम्, n. (fr. वृद्ध), a<BR>collection of old men; old age; the imbecility or<BR>infirmity of old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक्य
वार्द्धक्य, अम्, n. old age, senility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक्षत्रि
वार्द्धक्षत्रि, इस्, m. (fr. वृद्ध-क्षत्र),<BR>a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुक
वार्द्धुक, अम्, n. = वार्द्धक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषि
वार्द्धुषि वार्द्धुषि, इस्, m. (fr. वृद्धि, q. v.,<BR>or perhaps better spelt वार्धुषि fr. rt. वृध्), one<BR>who exacts high interest, a usurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषिक
वार्द्धुषिक, अस्, m. one who lives by lending<BR>money at a high rate of interest, a usurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषिन्
वार्द्धुषिन्, ई, m. a usurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुष्य
वार्द्धुष्य, अम्, n. high interest, usurious loan,<BR>usury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्धि|वार्द्धिः|वार्धिः
वार्धि वार्-धि. See under वार्, p. 904, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ध्र|वार्द्ध्रं|वार्ध्रं
वार्ध्र वार्ध्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वर्ध्र), made<BR>of leather, leathern; (अम्, ई), n. f. a leather thong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ध्रीणस|वार्द्ध्रीणसः|वार्ध्रीणसः
वार्ध्री-णस, अस्, m. (fr. वार्ध्री + नस), a<BR>rhinoceros (perhaps so called as having a leather-like<BR>snout); a white goat with long ears; (according to<BR>some) a kind of fabulous bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्भट|वार्भटः
वार्भट वार्-भट, वार्-वट. See p. 904,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्मण|वार्मणं|वार्म्मण|वार्म्मणं
वार्मण वार्मण, अम्, n. (fr. वर्मन्), a col-<BR>lection of coats of mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्मिण|वार्म्मिण|वार्म्मिणं
वार्मिण, अम्, n. (fr. वर्मिन्), a multitude of<BR>men in armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य|वार्यं|वार्यः|वार्य्य|वार्य्यं
वार्य वार्य, वार्यमाण. See p. 905, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्वणा|वार्व्वणा
वार्वणा वार्वणा, f. a kind of blue fly (= नीली;<BR>cf. वर्वणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्श
वार्श वार्श, अम्, n. (fr. वृश), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ष
वार्ष वार्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वर्ष), belong-<BR>ing to the rains, &c., belonging to a year, yearly,<BR>annual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिक|वार्षिकं|वार्षिकः
वार्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the rainy season,<BR>growing in the rains, filled with rain, yearly, annual,<BR>belonging to a year; lasting a whole year (e. g. a<BR>river the water of which does not dry up in the<BR>hot season); (अम्), n. a medicinal plant (= त्राय-<BR>माणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिला
वार्षिला, f. hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षुक|वार्षुकः
वार्षुक, अस्, ई, अम्, raining, showering, sprinkling,<BR>wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षगण्य
वार्षगण्य वार्षगण्य, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षदंश
वार्षदंश वार्षदंश, अस्, m. (fr. वृषद्-<BR>अंश), a patronymic, (some form two distinct patro-<BR>nymics, वार्षद and आंश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षभाणवी
वार्षभाणवी वार्षभाणवी or वार्षभा-<BR>नवी, f. (fr. वृष-भाणु), the daughter of Vṛṣa-<BR>bhāṇu, i. e. Rādhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षागिर
वार्षागिर वार्षागिर, आस्, m. pl. (fr. वृ-<BR>षागिर्), Ved. the five sons of Vṛṣāgir (viz. Am-<BR>barīṣa, Ṛjrāśva, Bhayamāna, Saha-deva, and Su-<BR>rādhas, authors of the hymn Ṛg-veda I. 100).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ष्टिहव्य
वार्ष्टिहव्य वार्ष्टिहव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>of Upa-stuta (author of Ṛg-veda X. 115).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ष्णेय|वार्ष्णेयः
वार्ष्णेय वार्ष्णेय, अस्, m. a descendant of<BR>Vṛṣṇi, epithet of Kṛṣṇa; N. of Nala's charioteer.<BR>—वार्ष्णेय-सहित, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by<BR>Vārṣṇeya.<BR>—वार्ष्णेय-सारथि, इस्, इस्, इ, having<BR>Vārṣṇeya for a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ह
वार्ह वार्ह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वर्ह), made of<BR>the feathers of a peacock's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हिण
वार्हिण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वर्हिण), derived from<BR>a peacock (as feathers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हत|वार्हतं
वार्हत वार्हत, अम्, n. See बार्हत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हद्रथ|वार्हद्रथः
वार्हद्रथ वार्हद्रथ, अस्, or वार्हद्रथि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘son of Vṛhad-ratha,’ epithet of Jarā-sandha.<BR>See बार्हद्रथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत
वार्हस्पत वार्हस्पत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वृहस्-<BR>पति), sacred to or declared by Vṛhas-pati; see<BR>Bṛhas-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत्य
वार्हस्पत्य, अम्, n. the science taught by Vṛhas-<BR>pati, rules of conduct, ethical precepts, ethics, morality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल|वालः
वाल वाल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वल्?), hair; (अस्,<BR>आ), m. f. a tail; [cf. बाल.]<BR>—वाल-धि, वाल-हस्त,<BR>&c., see बाल-धि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालक|वालकः
वालक वालक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वल्; cf. व-<BR>लय), a bracelet; a finger-ring, (also आ, f.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालखिल्य|वालखिल्यः
वालखिल्य वालखिल्य, अम्, n. a collection<BR>of eleven additional or apocryphal hymns inserted<BR>between the forty-eighth and forty-ninth hymns of<BR>the eighth Maṇḍala of the Ṛg-veda; [cf. बाल-<BR>खिल्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालम्मदेश
वालम्मदेश वालम्म-देश, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालव|वालवः
वालव वालव, अस्, m. the second of the<BR>eleven Karaṇas or astrological divisions of time, (see<BR>करण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालवितु
वालवितु वालवितु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालि|वालिः
वालि वालि. See बालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालिखिल्येश्वरतीर्थ
वालिखिल्येश्वरतीर्थ वालिखिल्येश्वर-तीर्थ<BR>(˚य-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालुका
वालुका वालुका, f. (more commonly written<BR>बालुका, q. v.), sand, gravel; (ई), f. a species of<BR>cucumber.<BR>—वालुकेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚का-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालुकिन्
वालुकिन्, ई, m. = भालुकिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्क|वाल्कं
वाल्क वाल्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वल्क), made of<BR>the bark of trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्कल|वाल्कलं
वाल्कल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वल्कल), made of bark;<BR>(ई), f. spirituous liquor; (अम्), n. a bark dress worn<BR>by ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मीक|वाल्मीकः
वाल्मीक वाल्मीक, अस्, m. (fr. वल्मीक, q. v.)<BR>= वाल्मीकि below; a proper N.<BR>—वाल्मीकेश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ (˚क-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मीकि|वाल्मीकिः
वाल्मीकि, इस्, m. (also spelt वाल्मिकि), N. of the<BR>celebrated author of the Rāmāyaṇa, (so called, ac-<BR>cording to some, because when immersed in thought<BR>he allowed himself to be overrun with ants like an<BR>ant-hill; according to one tradition he began life as<BR>a robber, but repenting of his misdeeds betook him-<BR>self to a hermitage on a hill in the district of Banda<BR>in Bundelkund, where he eventually received Sītā,<BR>the wife of Rāma, when banished by her husband.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मीकीय
वाल्मीकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, composed by Vālmīki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्लभ्य|वाल्लभ्यं
वाल्लभ्य वाल्लभ्य, अम्, n. (fr. वल्लभ), the<BR>state of being a favourite or of being beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाव
वाव वाव, ind. (i. e. probably वा + एव),<BR>verily, indeed, (sometimes used in a question.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावदत्
वावदत् वावदत्, अत्, अती, अत् (fr. Intens. of<BR>rt. वद्), Ved. uttering or causing loud sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावदूक|वावदूकः
वावदूक, अस्, आ, अम्, talking much, gabbling,<BR>prattling; eloquent.<BR>—वावदूक-ता, f. or वावदूक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. garrulity, loquaciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावद्यमान
वावद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, talking much, uttering<BR>loud sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावय|वावयः
वावय वावय, अस्, m. a sort of basil, Ocy-<BR>mum Sanctum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावशान
वावशान 1. वावशान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the<BR>Intens. of rt. वश्; for 2. see below), Ved. eagerly<BR>desiring or longing for, ardently loving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावहि
वावहि वावहि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. the Intens. of<BR>rt. 1. वह्), bearing or carrying much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावातृ
वावातृ वावातृ, ता, m., Ved. one who is<BR>favourable to or serves another, a worshipper, (in the<BR>Pada text ववातृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावुट|वावुटः
वावुट वावुट, अस्, m. a raft, boat, vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्
वावृत् वावृत् (rather to be regarded as<BR>an old Intens. of rt. 3. वृत्, q. v.), cl.<BR>4. A. वावृत्यते, &c., to choose, select, prefer, love,<BR>like; to serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्त|वावृत्तः
वावृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, chosen, selected, appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्यमान
वावृत्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, choosing, preferring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृधान
वावृधान वावृधान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वृध्,<BR>in the Pada-pāṭha ववृधान), Ved. growing, in-<BR>creasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृधेन्य
वावृधेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be increased, (Sāy.<BR>= वर्धनीय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्
वाश् वाश् (also written वास्), cl. 4. A.<BR>वाश्यते (ep. also cl. 1. P. A. वाशति,<BR>-ते), ववाशे, वाशिष्यते, अवाशिष्ट, वाशितुम्, to<BR>roar, howl, low (as a cow), cry, shriek, sing (like a<BR>bird), sound; to call: Caus. वाशयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अववाशत् (Ved. also अवीवशत्), to cause to roar or<BR>sound: Desid. विवाशिषते: Intens. वावाश्यते, वा-<BR>वाष्टि (in Ved. the vowel of the rt. is sometimes<BR>shortened), to roar vehemently, cry repeatedly, praise<BR>repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावशत्
वावशत्, अत्, अती, अत् (anom. intens. part.), Ved.<BR>sounding or lowing loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावशान
2. वावशान, अस्, आ, अम् (anom. intens. part.),<BR>Ved. roaring aloud, sounding, crackling, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 26, 2 = शब्दायमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश
वाश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. roaring, crying; (आ), f. the<BR>plant Justicia Ganderussa; [cf. वास.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशक
वाशक, अस्, &c., roaring, crying, sounding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशत्
वाशत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, roaring, crying, singing (like<BR>a bird &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशन|वाशनं
वाशन, अस्, आ, अम्, roaring, singing, crying; (अम्),<BR>n. the cry or song of birds, hum of bees, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशि|वाशिः
वाशि, इस्, m. fire or the god of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशिका
वाशिका, f. (for वासिका, q. v.), the plant Justicia<BR>Ganderussa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशित|वाशितं|वाशितः
वाशित, अस्, आ, अम्, roared, cried, called out, sung;<BR>perfumed, scented, (in this sense incorrect for 1. वा-<BR>सित); (अम्), n. the cry of birds or animals; (आ), f.<BR>a woman; a female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशी
वाशी, f., Ved. roaring, crying, singing; a weapon<BR>of the Maruts, an axe, spear, weapon in general;<BR>(according to some, perhaps) the roaring thunder-<BR>bolt, (according to Sāy. = आराख्यम् आयुधम्);<BR>voice, speech (= वाच्, Naigh. I. 11); a war-cry.<BR>—वाशी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. roaring; having or<BR>bearing the weapon called वाशी, armed with an axe,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशुरा
वाशुरा, f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्र|वाश्रं|वाश्रः
वाश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, bellowing, lowing, roaring<BR>(Ved.); (अस्), m. a bull (Ved.); a day, (also read<BR>वास्र; cf. वासर); (आ), f. a cow (Ved.); (espe-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">Page0907-a+ 78</a>]<BR>cially) a cow with a calf; a mother; (अम्), n. an<BR>edifice, dwelling, building; a place where four roads<BR>meet; dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0906-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशिष्ठ|वाशिष्ठः
वाशिष्ठ वाशिष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम् (better written<BR>वासिष्ठ, q. v.), relating to Vaśiṣṭha or Vasiṣṭha;<BR>descended from Vaśiṣṭha, see वासिष्ठ; (ई), f. the<BR>Go-matī or Goomtī river (which passes Lucknow and<BR>falls into the Ganges below Benares).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्कल|वाष्कलः
वाष्कल वाष्कल, अस्, आ, अम्, large, great;<BR>(अस्), m. a warrior; a proper N.; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a family or race (the descendants of Viśvā-mitra;<BR>also written वास्कल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्प|वाष्पं|वाष्पः
वाष्प वाष्प (also written वास्प), अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. (perhaps connected with वार्; according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. III. 28. fr. rt. वाध्, the final being changed<BR>to ष्; cf. अश्रु), vapour, hot vapour, steam, mist;<BR>an incipient tear, water swimming in the eye, a tear,<BR>tears; iron; a kind of pot-herb, = वाष्पिका; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of one of the five pupils of Śākya-muni;<BR>(ई), f. a drug (commonly हिङ्गु-पत्त्री); [cf. Lat.<BR>vappa, perhaps vapor.]<BR>—वाष्प-कण्ठ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having tears in the throat, choking with tears.<BR>—वाष्प-कल, अस्, आ, अम्, inarticulate through tears.<BR>—वाष्प-दुर्दिन, अस्, आ, अम्, clouded by tears.<BR>—वाष्प-पूर, अस्, m. a flood of tears.<BR>—वाष्प-<BR>प्रमोचन, अम्, n. the shedding of tears, act of shed-<BR>ding tears.<BR>—वाष्प-मोचन, अम्, n. the shedding<BR>of tears.<BR>—वाष्प-विक्लव, अस्, आ, अम्, overcome or<BR>agitated with tears, confused with weeping.<BR>—वाष्प-<BR>विन्दु, उस्, m. a tear-drop, tear.<BR>—वाष्प-सन्दिग्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, indistinct or hesitating through suppressed<BR>tears.<BR>—वाष्पाकुल (˚प-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, inter-<BR>rupted by tears.<BR>—वाष्पाम्बु-पूर (˚प-अम्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a flood of tears.<BR>—वाष्पाविलेक्षण (˚प-आविल-<BR>ईक्˚), having the eyes dimmed by tears.<BR>—वाष्पोद्-<BR>भव (˚प-उद्˚), the rising or starting of tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पक|वाष्पकः
वाष्पक, अस्, m. a kind of vegetable or pot-herb,<BR>= मारिष; (आ), f. a drug (= हिङ्गु-पत्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पाय
वाष्पाय, Nom. A. वाष्पायते, -यितुम्, to weep,<BR>shed tears; to emit vapour or steam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पिका
वाष्पिका or वाष्पीका, f. a drug (= हिङ्गु-पत्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पिन्
वाष्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, discharging or shedding tears<BR>(at the end of a comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्
वास् वास् (perhaps rather to be regarded<BR>as a Nom. fr. 1. वास below), cl. 10. P.<BR>वासयति (ep. also A. वासयते), -यितुम्, to fill with<BR>(perfumes &c.); to infuse (fragrant odours or other<BR>qualities), steep, macerate; to perfume, make fra-<BR>grant, fumigate, incense; to spice, season; cl. 4. A.<BR>वास्यते, to sound, cry, (in this sense for rt. वाश्,<BR>q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास|वासः
1. वास, अस्, m. perfuming, perfume; (अस्, आ), m. f.<BR>the plant Justicia Ganderussa.<BR>—वास-ताम्बूल, अम्,<BR>n. betel mixed with fragrant substances (such as car-<BR>damoms, camphor, &c.).<BR>—वास-योग, अस्, m. fra-<BR>grant powder sprinkled on the clothes, (especially)<BR>the red powder scattered about at the Holī festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासक|वासकः
1. वासक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, perfuming, fumi-<BR>gating, filling with perfume; (अस्, आ or इका), m. f.<BR>‘giving perfume,’ the plant Justicia Ganderussa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन|वासनं
1. वासन, अम्, n. the act of perfuming, fumigating<BR>with fragrant vapours or incense, infusing, steeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिका
वासिका, f. See under 1. वासक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासित|वासितं|वासितः
1. वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, infused, steeped, perfumed,<BR>scented, made fragrant, filled with fragrance; spiced,<BR>seasoned (as sauces &c.); (अम्), n. the cry of birds,<BR>sound, (for वाशित, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास|वासः
वास 2. वास, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 6. वस्), dwell-<BR>ing, resting, living; a dwelling-place, house, habita-<BR>tion; site, situation, abode, place of staying or abid-<BR>ing, [cf. Hib. fos, ‘staying, resting.’]<BR>—वास-कर्णी,<BR>f. a hall where public exhibitions (as Nāches &c. are<BR>held).<BR>—वास-गृह, अम्, n. ‘dwelling-house,’ the<BR>inner part of a house, an inner or sleeping-room,<BR>bed-chamber.<BR>—वास-पर्यय, अस्, m. change of<BR>residence.<BR>—वास-भवन, अम्, n. or वास-भूमि,<BR>इस्, f. a place of abode, dwelling-place, house.<BR>—वास-<BR>यष्टि, इस्, f. a pole or pillar for a bird to perch on,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">Page0907-b+ 79</a>]<BR>a roosting perch.<BR>—वास-वेश्मन्, अ, n. the inner<BR>part of a house.<BR>—वासागार (˚स-आग्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘abiding apartment,’ the inner or sleeping apartment.<BR>—वासौकस् (˚स-ओक्˚), अस्, n. ‘dwelling-house,’ the<BR>inner or private apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासक|वासकः
2. वासक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, causing to inhabit,<BR>making to dwell or abide, populating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासतेय
वासतेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वसति), habitable, fit or<BR>proper to be dwelt in; (ई), f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन|वासनं
2. वासन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to an abode, fit<BR>for a dwelling; (अम्), n. causing to abide; abiding,<BR>abode; a particular posture (conceived to be pecu-<BR>liarly proper for ascetics during abstract meditation;<BR>also said to be practised by princes, when it is de-<BR>scribed as sitting with the knees bent and the feet<BR>turned backwards); any receptacle or vessel, a water-<BR>jar, box, basket; knowledge; (आ), f. knowledge de-<BR>rived from memory, the present consciousness of past<BR>perceptions or an impression remaining unconsciously<BR>in the mind from past good or evil actions and<BR>hence producing pleasure or pain (= संस्कार);<BR>fancy, imagination, idea, inclination [cf. दुर्-व्˚];<BR>false fancy, ignorance; expectation, desire, trust,<BR>confidence.<BR>—वासन-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, placed in a<BR>box or basket, packed, folded.<BR>—वासना-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, full of imagination, consisting in fancy.<BR>—वा-<BR>सनामय-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being full of<BR>imagination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासि|वासिः
वासि, इस्, m. abiding, dwelling; (इस्, ई), m. f. a small<BR>hatchet or axe, chopper, adze, chisel; [cf. वाशी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासित|वासितं|वासितः
2. वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, peopled, populous (as a<BR>country); flourishing, famous, celebrated; possessed<BR>of, possessing, having; (अम्), n. the act of rendering<BR>populous or causing to be inhabited; knowledge<BR>(especially derived from memory, see वासना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिन्
1. वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, abiding, staying, inhabiting; (ई),<BR>m. an inhabitant (at the end of a comp.); (इनी), f. a<BR>sort of white Jhiṇṭī or Barleria (= शुक्ल-झिण्टी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास|वासः
वास 3. वास, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 5. वस्), dress-<BR>ing, dress, cloth, clothes.<BR>—वास-सज्जा, f. a woman<BR>dressed in all her ornaments to receive her lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासक|वासकः
3. वासक, अस्, m. clothing, clothes.<BR>—वासक-<BR>सज्जा or वासक-सज्जिका, f. a woman dressed in all<BR>her ornaments to receive her lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन|वासनं
3. वासन, अस्, आ, अम्, enveloping, covering, cloth-<BR>ing; (अम्), n. cloth, clothes; an envelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासस्
वासस्, अस्, n. cloth, clothes, dress, a garment; a<BR>pall; a curtain.<BR>—वासः-कुटी, f. a tent.<BR>—वासः-<BR>खण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. a piece of cloth, a rag.<BR>—वासो-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving clothes.<BR>—वासो-यु-<BR>ग, अम्, n. a pair of garments, suit of clothes, (the<BR>dress of the Hindūs usually consisting of two pieces<BR>of cloth, viz. a lower garment fastened round the<BR>waist, and an upper one thrown loosely over the<BR>shoulders.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासित|वासितं|वासितः
3. वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, clothed, dressed; (आ), f. a<BR>woman; a female elephant; the female of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिन्
2. वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having or wearing clothes,<BR>dressed, arrayed, clothed, (पीत-कौशेय-वासिनी, a<BR>woman wearing a yellow silk garment.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्य|वास्यः
वास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be clothed; to be covered<BR>or pervaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासत|वासतः
वासत वासत, अस्, m. an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्त|वासंत|वासन्तः
वासन्त वासन्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वसन्त),<BR>vernal, relating to spring, suitable to spring, produced<BR>in the spring season; being in the spring of life,<BR>young; attentive or diligent (in the performance of<BR>religious ceremonies &c.); situated, (? perhaps con-<BR>nected with 2. वास); (अस्), m. a camel; the Indian<BR>cuckoo; a young elephant, any young animal; the<BR>southern or western wind (= मलयानिल, q. v.); a<BR>sort of kidney-bean (Phaseolus Mungo), a kind of<BR>black bean (= कृष्ण-मुद्ग); the plant Vangueria<BR>Spinosa; a dissolute man; (ई), f. a large creeper,<BR>Gærtnera Racemosa; a species of jasmine, Jasminum<BR>Auriculatum (= माधवी, यूथी); long pepper;<BR>the trumpet-flower; N. of a deity; a festival in<BR>honour of Kāma-deva (held in the month Caitra;<BR>in some places Durgā is worshipped at this festival);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">Page0907-c+ 73</a>]<BR>a species of the Śakvarī metre.<BR>—वासन्ती-पूजा, f.<BR>the worship of Durgā in the month Caitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तक|वासन्तकं
वासन्तक, अस्, ई, अम्, vernal, sown or grown in<BR>spring; suitable to the spring season; relating or<BR>belonging to it, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तिक|वासंतिक|वासन्तिकः
वासन्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, vernal; (अस्), m. the<BR>buffoon or Vidūṣaka in a drama (see विदूषक);<BR>an actor, dancer (the spring being the season for<BR>dancing, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासर|वासरं|वासरः
वासर वासर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. वस्; cf.<BR>उषस्), Ved. shining, giving light, (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 48, 7. वासराणि = जगद्-<BR>वासकानि); (अस्, अम्), m. n. a day; (अस्), m. one of<BR>the Nāgas or serpents, a kind of snake; (ई), f. epi-<BR>thet of a cow.<BR>—वासर-सङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘day-junc-<BR>tion,’ the morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासव|वासवः
वासव वासव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वसु), belong-<BR>ing to Indra; accompanied by the Vasus; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of Indra; (ई), f. the mother of Vyāsa.<BR>—वासव-<BR>दत्ता, f., N. of the wife of Nidhi-pati; of a work by<BR>Subandhu (describing the amours of Kandarpa-ketu<BR>and Vāsava-dattā).<BR>—वासवेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—वासवोपम (˚व-उप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, resembling or like Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिन्
वासिन् 1. and 2. वासिन्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिषुम्फ
वासिषुम्फ वासिषुम्फ, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिष्ट|वासिष्टं
वासिष्ट वासिष्ट, अम्, n. blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिष्ठ|वासिष्ठं|वासिष्ठः
वासिष्ठ वासिष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वसिष्ठ,<BR>q. v., cf. वाशिष्ठ), belonging to Vasiṣṭha, com-<BR>posed by or revealed to the Ṛṣi Vasiṣṭha (as the<BR>seventh Maṇḍala of the Ṛg-veda); (अस्), m. a son<BR>or descendant of Vasiṣṭha (applied as a patronymic<BR>to various Ṛṣis); (ई), f. a female descendant of<BR>Vasiṣṭha; (अम्), n. = योग-वासिष्ठ.<BR>—वासिष्ठ-<BR>रामायण, अम्, n. = योग-वासिष्ठ.<BR>—वासिष्ठ-<BR>लैङ्ग-पुराण^1, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—वा-<BR>सिष्ठ-सार, अस्, m. = योग-व्˚.<BR>—वासिष्ठोपपु-<BR>राण (˚ठ-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 311-315. note: dental nasal -> guttural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासु|वासुः
वासु वासु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 6. वस्), N. of<BR>Viṣṇu (as dwelling in all beings); the soul; the<BR>Supreme Being considered as the soul of the universe.<BR>—वासु-पूज्य, अस्, m. the twelfth Jina of the present<BR>era.<BR>—वासु-भद्र, अस्, m. a N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासू
वासू, ऊस्, f. (in theatrical language) a young girl,<BR>maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकि|वासुकिः
वासुकि वासुकि, इस्, m. (fr. वसुक, said to<BR>be a N. of Kaśyapa), the serpent Vāsuki, sovereign<BR>of the snakes.<BR>—वासुकि-ह्रद, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकेय|वासुकेयः
वासुकेय, अस्, m. the serpent Vāsuki.<BR>—वासु-<BR>केय-स्वसृ, सा, f. ‘sister of Vāsuki,’ epithet of the<BR>goddess Manasā (presiding over serpents and regarded<BR>as wife of Jarat-kāru).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुक्र
वासुक्र वासुक्र, अस्, m. (fr. वसु-क्र), Ved.<BR>a patronymic of Vasu-karṇa; of Vasu-kṛt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुदेव|वासुदेवः
वासुदेव वासुदेव, अस्, m. (fr. वसु-देव),<BR>‘son of Vasu-deva,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa; a descendant<BR>of Vasu-deva; N. of a class of persons peculiar to<BR>the Jainas; N. of an author; of a poet; of a phy-<BR>sician.<BR>—वासुदेव-प्रियङ्करी, f. a kind of shrub<BR>(= शतावरी).<BR>—वासुदेवोपनिषद् (˚व-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f., N. of one of the more recent Upaniṣads of the<BR>Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुरा
वासुरा वासुरा, f. (fr. rt. 6. वस् or rt. वास्),<BR>night; the earth; a woman; a female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासोद
वासोद वासो-द, वासो-युग. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासौकस्
वासौकस् वासौकस्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्कल
वास्कल वास्कल. See वाष्कल, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त
वास्त वास्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वस्त), made or<BR>derived from a goat, coming from goats, goatish,<BR>(also written बास्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तिक|वास्तिकं
वास्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to goats; (अम्), n. a<BR>collection of goats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव|वास्तवं
वास्तव वास्तव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वस्तु), sub-<BR>stantial, real; being anything in the true sense of the<BR>word, substantiated, fixed, determined, demonstrated;<BR>(आ), f. dawn; (अम्), n. anything fixed or appointed.<BR>—वास्तवोषा, f. ‘real twilight,’ night, (according<BR>to some this is not a compound but two words,<BR>उषा, ‘dawn,’ being the explanation of वास्तवा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तविक|वास्तविकं|वास्तविकः
वास्तविक, अस्, ई, अम्, substantial, real, material,<BR>genuine; demonstrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव्य|वास्तव्यः
वास्तव्य वास्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (anom. fut.<BR>part. of rt. 6. वस्), fit to be abided or dwelt in, fit<BR>to be inhabited; making a habitation, inhabiting,<BR>dwelling; (अस्), m. a dweller, resident, inhabitant,<BR>citizen, dependant; [cf. ग्राम-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तु
वास्तु वास्तु, उस्, उ, m. n. (fr. rt. 6. वस्; see<BR>Uṇādi-s. 1. 77), the site or foundation of a house,<BR>ground suitable for building a house, a building-place,<BR>building-ground, site, ground [cf. पुर-व्˚]; a house,<BR>habitation, abode, region; (उ), n. a kind of vegetable<BR>(= वास्तुक).<BR>—वास्तु-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a part of<BR>the Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—वास्तु-प्रदीप, N. of a work.<BR>—वास्तु-याग, अस्, m. a sacrificial rite observed on<BR>measuring the ground and laying the foundation of<BR>a house.<BR>—वास्तु-याग-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a part<BR>of the Smṛti-tattva (giving the rules for the above<BR>rite).<BR>—वास्तु-शास्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—वास्तु-<BR>संशमन or वास्तु-संशमनीय, अम्, n. a cere-<BR>mony performed on laying the foundation or setting<BR>out the ground for a new house, a sacrifice performed<BR>on preparing a foundation or on entering a new man-<BR>sion.<BR>—वास्तु-ह, अम्, n. in Aitareya-Br. V. 14. in-<BR>terpreted to mean ‘what is left on the sacred spot.’<BR>—वास्तोष्-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the Vāstu,’ i. e.<BR>‘protector of the foundation of a house,’ or generally<BR>‘house-protector,’ N. of one of the more recent deities<BR>of the Ṛg-veda (regarded as presiding over the founda-<BR>tion of a house, and addressed in VII. 54. and VII. 55);<BR>an epithet of Indra, (also written वास्तोस्-पति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुक|वास्तुकं
वास्तुक or वास्तूक, अम्, n. the pot-herb Che-<BR>nopodium Album.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुकी
वास्तुकी, f. a species of vegetable (= चिल्ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तेय|वास्तेयं
वास्तेय वास्तेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वस्ति), relat-<BR>ing or belonging to the belly, abdominal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त्र|वास्त्रः
वास्त्र वास्त्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वस्त्र), made<BR>of cloth, covered with cloth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्थ|वास्थः
वास्थ वा-स्थ = वाः-स्थ. See under वार्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्प|वास्पः
वास्प वास्प, अस्, m. (more correctly written<BR>वाष्प, q. v.), a tear, tears, hot vapour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्पेय|वास्पेयः
वास्पेय, अस्, m. the tree Nāga-keśara, (commonly<BR>called नागेशर्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्य|वास्यः
वास्य वास्य. See p. 907, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्
वाह् 1. वाह् (also written बाह्; connected<BR>with rt. 1. वह्), cl. 1. A. वाहते (ep. also P.<BR>वाहति), ववाहे, वाहितुम्, to endeavour, make effort,<BR>strive, exert one's self, try: Caus. वाहयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to labour or work, use, employ, occupy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहन|वाहनं
1. वाहन, अम्, n. the act of making effort, en-<BR>deavouring, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहयत्
वाहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to labour, employ-<BR>ing, making use of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहित|वाहितं
1. वाहित, अस्, आ, अम्, exerted, endeavoured; mys-<BR>tified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्
वाह् 2. वाह्, ट्, -ही, ट् (fr. rt. 1. वह्), bear-<BR>ing, carrying, &c. (at the end of comps.; cf. भार-<BR>व्˚, वज्र-व्˚, Gram. 182. c).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह|वाहः
वाह, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing, carrying, (अति-भार-<BR>वाह, carrying too heavy burdens); (अस्), m. bear-<BR>ing, carrying, drawing; a bearer, porter, carrier of<BR>burdens, &c.; any animal used for draught, a beast<BR>of burden; a horse; a buffalo; a bull; any vehicle,<BR>carriage, conveyance, car; the arm; air, wind; a<BR>measure of capacity containing ten Kumbhas (nearly<BR>equal to the weight of an English wey).<BR>—वाह-<BR>द्विषत्, अन्, m. a buffalo (said to be so called as<BR>‘hostile to the horse’).<BR>—वाह-भ्रंश्, -भ्रट्, ट्, ट्<BR>(or वाह-भ्रंस्, -भ्रत्, त्, त्), falling from a vehi-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">Page0908-b+ 79</a>]<BR>cle, &c.<BR>—वाह-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. ‘best of draught-<BR>animals,’ a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहक|वाहकः
वाहक, अस्, इका, अम्, bearing, carrying, convey-<BR>ing, conducting; (अस्), m. a porter, carrier; the driver<BR>of a chariot; a horseman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहन|वाहनं
2. वाहन, अम्, n. the act of carrying, bearing,<BR>conveying, conducting; the act of driving or govern-<BR>ing (horses); a vehicle, chariot, carriage, a convey-<BR>ance of any kind; any animal used in riding or<BR>draught, a horse, an elephant; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>Muni; [cf. Old Germ. wagana, ‘a chariot;’ Hib.<BR>feun, ‘a chariot.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहयित्वा
वाहयित्वा, ind. having caused to be conveyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहस्
वाहस्, आस्, m., Ved. one who carries or bears (at<BR>the end of comps.; cf. स्तोम-व्˚, नृ-व्˚, गिर्-व्˚,<BR>ब्रह्म-व्˚); ‘one who bears the oblation or sacrifice’<BR>[cf. यज्ञ-व्˚], epithet of Agni; (अस्), n. a hymn,<BR>(Sāy. = स्तोत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहस|वाहसः
वाहस, अस्, m. a water-course; a large snake<BR>(especially the boa constrictor); the pot-herb Mar-<BR>silia Dentata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिक|वाहिकः
वाहिक, अस्, m. a car or vehicle drawn by oxen;<BR>a large drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहित|वाहितं
2. वाहित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be borne or con-<BR>veyed; (अम्), n. a heavy burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिन्
वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bearing, carrying (often at the<BR>end of comps.); (ई), m. a chariot; (इनी), f. an army,<BR>body of forces; a division of an army (consisting of<BR>81 elephants, 81 cars, 243 horse, 405 foot), a<BR>battalion; a river.<BR>—वाहि-त्थ, अम्, n. (for वाहि-<BR>स्थ), the part of an elephant's forehead below the<BR>frontal globes.<BR>—वाहिनी-निवेश, अस्, m. the camp of<BR>an army.<BR>—वाहिनी-पति, इस्, m. the lord or leader<BR>of an army, a general, commanding officer; ‘lord of<BR>rivers,’ epithet of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिष्ठ
वाहिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bearing or carrying<BR>best, bearing most effectually, (according to Nirukta<BR>V. 1 = वोढृ-तम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहीक|वाहीकः
1. वाहीक, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying, bearing burdens;<BR>(अस्), m. an ox; N. of a priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहुक
वाहुक, अस्, m., N. of a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्य|वाह्यं|वाह्यः
1. वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be carried or borne; (अम्),<BR>n. a carriage, vehicle; (अस्), m. any beast of burden,<BR>an ox, horse, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्यमान
वाह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being borne, being<BR>carried or conveyed, being conducted; being driven,<BR>being urged or incited; being induced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहादुर
वाहादुर वाहादुर. See बाहादुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिर्वेदिक
वाहिर्वेदिक वाहिर्वेदिक. See बाहिर्वेदिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहीक|वाहीकः
वाहीक 2. वाहीक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वहिस्), outer,<BR>external; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a country (said to be<BR>part of the Pañjāb).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्य|वाह्यं|वाह्यः
वाह्य 2. वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वहिस्, q. v.;<BR>in the Veda usually written बाह्य, q. v.), being out-<BR>side, situated without (a city &c.), outer, external,<BR>exterior (often at the end of a comp.; cf. धर्म-<BR>व्˚, नगर-व्˚, वेद-व्˚); not belonging to the<BR>family or the country, strange, foreign; expelled<BR>from caste or from society, an outcast, one of a low<BR>tribe; (अस्), m. a foreigner; a proper N.; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of the descendants of Vāhya; of a people;<BR>(आ), f., scil. त्वच्, the outer bark of a tree; (अम्,<BR>एन, ए), ind. outside, on the outside of, without;<BR>(आत्), ind. from without.<BR>—वाह्य-कक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>the outer side (of a house).<BR>—वाह्य-करण, अम्,<BR>n. an external organ of sense.<BR>—वाह्य-कर्ण, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Nāga.<BR>—वाह्य-कुण्ड, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Nāga.<BR>—वाह्य-तद्धित, अस्, m. (in grammar) an<BR>external Taddhita affix.<BR>—वाह्य-तर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>more external or foreign, of a lower caste, a lower<BR>outcast (Manu X. 30).<BR>—वाह्य-तस्, ind. externally,<BR>out-of-doors, &c.; out of, outside of (with gen. or abl.).<BR>—वाह्य-ता, f. or वाह्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being<BR>outside, exclusion, deviation from.<BR>—वाह्यतो-नर,<BR>आस्, m. pl. ‘external men,’ N. of a people.<BR>—वाह्य-<BR>द्रुति, इस्, f. ‘external solution,’ a process in the<BR>preparation of quicksilver.<BR>—वाह्य-प्रयत्न, अस्,<BR>m. (in grammar) the external effort in the production<BR>of articulate sounds.<BR>—वाह्य-रत, अम्, n. ‘external<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-c" target="_blank">Page0908-c+ 79</a>]<BR>coition,’ (probably) the gratification of the sexual<BR>impulse externally to the vulva.<BR>—वाह्य-वस्तु, उ,<BR>n. external wealth or riches.<BR>—वाह्य-वासिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, dwelling outside the village or town (said of Caṇ-<BR>ḍālas).<BR>—वाह्य-सम्भोग, अस्, m. external coi-<BR>tion; [cf. वाह्य-रत.]<BR>—वाह्यान्तर् (˚य-अन्˚),<BR>ind. outside and inside, externally and internally.<BR>—वाह्यायाम (˚य-आय्˚), अस्, m. a particular disease<BR>of the nerves.<BR>—वाह्यालय (˚य-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘ex-<BR>ternal abode,’ the abode of outcasts, i. e. the country<BR>of the Vāhīkas.<BR>—वाह्येन्द्रिय (˚य-इन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>an outer organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्यका
वाह्यका, f., N. of a Sṛñjarī (an older sister of<BR>Upa-vāhyakā and one of the two wives of Bhaja-<BR>māna, Hari-vaṃśa 2001).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्यायनि
वाह्यायनि वाह्यायनि, इस्, m. (fr. वह्य),<BR>a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लि|वाह्लिः
वाह्लि वाह्लि, इस्, f. (also written बाह्लि, बाल्हि,<BR>q. v.), N. of a country lying north-west of Afghānistān,<BR>Balkh.<BR>—वाह्लि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or bred in Balkh;<BR>(अस्), m. a Balkh-bred horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लिक|वाह्लिकं|वाह्लिकः
वाह्लिक or वाह्लीक, अस्, m. (also written बाह्लिक,<BR>बाल्हिक, बाल्हीक, q. v.), a country lying north-west<BR>of Afghānistān, Balkh; a horse from Balkh (considered<BR>to be of a good breed); one of the principal Gan-<BR>dharvas or choristers of heaven; a proper N.; (अम्),<BR>n. saffron; Asa Fœtida; (अस्, ई, अम्), of or belonging<BR>to the Vāhlīkas, spoken by the Vāhlīkas, (वाह्लीकी<BR>भाषा, the language spoken by the Vāhlīkas.)<BR>—वाह्लीक-देश, अस्, m. the country of the Vāhlīkas,<BR>—वाह्लीक-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the<BR>country of the Vāhlīkas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वि|विः
वि 1. वि, ind. (thought by some to be for<BR>an original द्वि, meaning ‘in two parts;’ as a prepo-<BR>sition or prefix to verbs it is opposed to सम्, q. v.,<BR>and expresses) apart, apart from, asunder, in different<BR>directions, to and fro, about, away, away from, off,<BR>&c. (e. g. वि-युज्, to disjoin, separate; वि-दॄ, to<BR>tear asunder; वि-कॄ, to scatter in different direc-<BR>tions; वि-चल्, to move to and fro; वि-च्छिद्, to cut<BR>away, cut off); when prefixed to some roots, वि gives<BR>a meaning opposite to the idea contained in the<BR>simple rt. (e. g. क्री, to buy; वि-क्री, to sell; स्मृ,<BR>to remember; वि-स्मृ, to forget); in other cases<BR>it appears either not to affect or simply to intensify<BR>that idea [cf. नश्, वि-नश्, हिंस्, वि-हिंस्]. वि may<BR>also be used with verbs or nouns, and other parts of<BR>speech derived from verbs, to express ‘division’ [cf.<BR>वि-भिद्, वि-भेद, वि-भज्, वि-भाग]; ‘distinction’<BR>[cf. वि-शिष्, वि-शेष, वि-विच्, वि-वेक]; ‘discrimi-<BR>nation’ [cf. व्य्-अवच्छिद्, व्य्-अवच्छेद]; ‘distri-<BR>bution,’ ‘arrangement,’ ‘order’ [cf. वि-धा, वि-<BR>धान]; ‘opposition’ [cf. वि-रुध्, वि-रोध];<BR>‘discussion,’ ‘deliberation’ [cf. वि-चर्, वि-चार];<BR>‘privation’ [cf. वि-नी, वि-नयन]. वि may<BR>also be used with nouns, adjective or substantive,<BR>not immediately connected with verbs, to express<BR>‘difference’ [cf. वि-लक्षण]; ‘variety’ [cf. वि-<BR>चित्र]; ‘distinction’ [cf. वि-शेष]; ‘intensity,’<BR>‘greatness,’ ‘largeness’ [cf. वि-कराल]; ‘change’<BR>[cf. वि-कार]; ‘manifoldness’ [cf. वि-विध]; ‘con-<BR>trariety’ [cf. वि-लोम]; ‘impropriety,’ ‘deviation<BR>from right’ [cf. वि-जन्मन्, वि-कर्मिक]; ‘nega-<BR>tion’ or ‘privation’ (e. g. वि-जन, devoid of men;<BR>in this sense वि is used like निस्, q. v., and like 3. अ,<BR>q. v.); in this latter signification the use of वि often<BR>corresponds to that of the Latin dis, se, and the English<BR>prefixes a, ex, de, dis, in, un, &c.; [cf. Old Germ.<BR>wi-dar, ‘against;’ Pers. بى bī, ‘without;’ perhaps<BR>Lat. vê, in words like ve-cors, ve-sanus, vi in di-<BR>vi-dere; Lith. be, ‘without;’ Slav. beζ (perhaps =<BR>वहिस्).]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वि|विः
वि 2. वि, इस्, m. f. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 133. fr. rt. वा, the final of the rt. being rejected;<BR>a form वी is also given, and according to some the<BR>word वि may be fr. rt. 1. वी), Ved. a goer; a bird<BR>[cf. वीक]; a horse (from its fleetness); a rein (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy.); epithet of the Soma; of a sacri-<BR>ficer; the eye (?); heaven (?); the region of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">Page0909-a+ 75</a>]<BR>wind (?); [cf. Zend vi; Gr. οἰ-ωνό-ς, αἰ-ε-τό-ς,<BR>ὤϊον, ὠόν; Lat. avis, ovum; Old Germ. ei; Angl.<BR>Sax. œg.] — 1. वि-गत, अम्, n. (for 2. see under वि-<BR>गम्), the flight of birds.<BR>—१. वि-च्छाय, अम्, n.<BR>(for 2. see s. v.), the shadow of a flock of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0908-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंश|विंशः
विंश विंश, विंशक, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशति|विंशतिः
विंशति विंशति, इस्, f. (perhaps contracted<BR>fr. द्वि-दशति, ‘two tens’), twenty, a score; (ती), f.<BR>du. two twenties; (तयस्), f. pl. many twenties;<BR>[cf. Gr. εἴκατι, εἴκοαι (Lacon. βείκατι); Lat. vi-<BR>ginti; Hib. fichead; Cambro-Brit. ugaint.]<BR>—विं-<BR>शतिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, worth twenty, produced<BR>from or bought with twenty, &c.<BR>—विंशति-तम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, twentieth.<BR>—विंशति-भाग, अस्, m. a<BR>twentieth part.<BR>—विंशति-वर्ष-देशीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>about twenty years old.<BR>—विंशतीश (˚ति-ईश), अस्, or<BR>विंशतीशिन्, ई, m. a governor of twenty villages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंश|विंशः
विंश, अस्, ई, अम्, twentieth; (अस्), m., scil. भाग,<BR>a twentieth part (= विंशति-भाग, Manu VIII. 398);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशक|विंशकः
विंशक, अस्, ई, अम्, twenty, an aggregate of twenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशत्
विंशत् in एक-व्˚, परि-व्˚, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशतिम
विंशतिम, abbreviated for विंशति-तम in पञ्-<BR>चविंशतिम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशिन्
विंशिन्, ई, m. twenty, a score; a lord of twenty<BR>towns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्
विक् विक्, (in Pāṇini's system) the aug-<BR>ment वि at the end of a syllable of reduplication,<BR>(see Intens. of rt. 2. द्युत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक|विकं
विक विक, अम्, n. the milk of a cow that<BR>has just calved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकङ्कट|विकंकट|विकंकटः|विकङ्कटः
विकङ्कट वि-कङ्कट, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Asteracantha Longifolia (= गो-क्षुर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकङ्कत|विकंकत|विकंकतः|विकङ्कतः
विकङ्कत वि-कङ्कत, अस्, m. a kind of tree<BR>(= ग्रन्थिल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकच|विकचः
विकच 1. वि-कच, अस्, आ, अम्, blown, opened,<BR>expanded (as a flower &c.), spread; (अस्), m. a Bud-<BR>dhist mendicant; epithet of Ketu or the personified<BR>descending node.<BR>—विकची-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to cause to blow or expand, to open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकच|विकचः
2. वि-कच, अस्, आ, अम्, having no hair, hairless,<BR>bald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकट|विकटः
विकट 1. वि-कट, अस्, आ, अम् (see कट), large,<BR>great; formidable, hideous, ugly, uncouth, horrible,<BR>frightful; large-toothed; knitted (said of the brows),<BR>frowning; changed in form or appearance; beautiful;<BR>obscure, obsolete; (अस्), m. a proper N.; (अम्), n.<BR>a boil, tumour; (आ), f. a kind of female divinity<BR>peculiar to Buddhists.<BR>—विकट-मूर्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, hav-<BR>ing a hideous or distorted shape, deformed, ugly.<BR>—विकटानन (˚ट-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘ugly-faced,’ N.<BR>of one of the sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकट|विकटः
2. वि-कट, अस्, आ, अम्, having no mat, without a<BR>mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकण्टक|विकण्टकः
विकण्टक वि-कण्टक, अस्, m. a herbaceous<BR>plant, Hedysarum Alhagi or Alhagi Maurorum (as<BR>‘having no thorns’ or as ‘having spreading thorns,’<BR>= यवास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थ्
विकत्थ् वि-कत्थ्, cl. 1. A. -कत्थते (some-<BR>times also P. -कत्थति), -कत्थितुम्, to boast, vaunt,<BR>boast of (with inst., e. g. विद्यया विकत्थते, he<BR>boasts of his learning); to praise, praise ironically,<BR>mock; to humiliate; to speak ill of (with acc.); to<BR>proclaim loudly, make a noise about anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थन|विकत्थनं
वि-कत्थन, अस्, आ, अम्, boasting, vaunting,<BR>boastful, speaking boastfully or ostentatiously, prais-<BR>ing; praising ironically; (अम्), n. the act of boast-<BR>ing; the act of proclaiming loudly; the act of prais-<BR>ing, praise; ironical or false praise, irony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थनीय
वि-कत्थनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be vaunted, to be<BR>boasted of, to be praised, commendable; to be praised<BR>ironically; ridiculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थमान
वि-कत्थमान, अस्, आ, अम्, boasting, vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थयित्वा
वि-कत्थयित्वा, ind. (anom. for वि-कत्थ्य), hav-<BR>ing praised ironically, having mocked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्था
वि-कत्था, f. boasting, boast, vaunt; praise; ironi-<BR>cal praise, irony; proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थिन्
वि-कत्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, boasting, vaunting, pro-<BR>claiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्प्|विकंप्
विकम्प् वि-कम्प्, cl. 1. A. -कम्पते, -कम्-<BR>पितुम्, to tremble greatly, quiver, heave, move about,<BR>move from or change a position; to become changed<BR>or deformed; to shrink or retreat from: Caus. P.<BR>-कम्पयति, -यितुम्, to cause to tremble, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकपित
वि-कपित, अस्, आ, अम्, = वि-कम्पित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्प|विकंप
वि-कम्प, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, heaving; un-<BR>steady, not firm, inconstant; shrinking from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्पमान
वि-कम्पमान, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, quivering,<BR>heaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्पित|विकंपित|विकम्पितः
वि-कम्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, tremulous,<BR>quivering, moving about, (अ-विकम्पित, not trem-<BR>bling, immovable); palpitating, heaving; agitated,<BR>unsteady, broken, interrupted; shrinking from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर|विकरः
विकर वि-कर, &c. See under वि-कृ,<BR>p. 910, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकराल|विकरालः
विकराल वि-कराल, अस्, आ, अम्, very formida-<BR>ble or terrible, frightful.<BR>—विकराल-ता, f. formidable-<BR>ness, dreadfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्ण|विकर्णः
विकर्ण 1. वि-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, having large<BR>ears; (अस्), m., N. of one of the Kuru princes (on<BR>the side of Duryodhana in the war against the Pāṇ-<BR>ḍavas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्ण|विकर्णः
2. वि-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, earless, having no ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्णिक|विकर्णिकः
वि-कर्णिक, अस्, m. the district called Sārasvata<BR>(in the north-west of Hindūstān, generally considered<BR>to be part of the Pañjāb, said to be so called as<BR>being ‘the region from which Karṇa was excluded’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्तन|विकर्तनः|विकर्त्तन|विकर्त्तनः
विकर्तन वि-कर्तन. See under वि-कृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्मन्|विकर्म्मन्
विकर्मन् वि-कर्मन्. See p. 910, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्ष|विकर्षः
विकर्ष वि-कर्ष, &c. See under वि-कृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल|विकलः
विकल वि-कल, अस्, आ, अम् (see कला), de-<BR>prived of a part, destitute of a portion, deprived of<BR>a limb or member, defective, imperfect; wanting,<BR>failing; decayed, impaired, withered, waned; con-<BR>fused, confounded, agitated, sorrowful; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a Daitya; (आ, ई), f. a woman in whom menstru-<BR>ation has ceased; (आ), f. the sixtieth part of a<BR>Kalā, the second of a degree.<BR>—विकल-पाणिक, अस्,<BR>m. one who has a mutilated or withered hand, a<BR>cripple.<BR>—विकल-वध, अस्, m. ‘death of Vikala,’<BR>N. of a chapter in the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—विकलाङ्ग<BR>(˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having mutilated or defective<BR>limbs, deformed, crippled, maimed.<BR>—विकली-करण,<BR>अम्, n. the act of depriving of a limb, mutilating,<BR>maiming, breaking, spoiling; confusing, agitating.<BR>—विकली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to deprive<BR>of a limb, mutilate, maim, spoil, break; to agitate,<BR>confound.<BR>—विकली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, mutilated,<BR>maimed, impaired, broken, injured; lame; sick;<BR>confused, distressed.<BR>—विकली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>mutilated, maimed, defective; agitated, distressed.<BR>—विकलेन्द्रिय (˚ल-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having any<BR>of the organs of sense impaired or defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्प|विकल्पः
विकल्प वि-कल्प, &c. See under वि-कॢप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्मष
विकल्मष वि-कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, spotless,<BR>sinless, guiltless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकश्वर|विकश्वरः
विकश्वर वि-कश्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, for वि-कस्-<BR>वर, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकषा
विकषा वि-कषा, f. = वि-कसा, Bengal mad-<BR>der.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकष्वर
वि-कष्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, for वि-कस्वर, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस्
विकस् वि-कस्, cl. 1. P. -कसति, -कसितुम्, to<BR>burst, become split or divided or rent asunder; to<BR>open, become expanded, blossom, bloom, blow (as<BR>a flower): Caus. P. -कासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>open, cause to expand or blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस|विकसः
वि-कस, अस्, m. the moon; (आ), f. Bengal madder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसत्
वि-कसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, opening, expanding; bud-<BR>ding, blowing; glowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसित|विकसितं
वि-कसित, अस्, आ, अम्, blown (as a flower), budded,<BR>opened, expanded.<BR>—विकसित-कुमुदेन्दीवरालो-<BR>किन् (˚द-इन्˚, ˚र-आल्˚), ई, इनी, इ, looking like the<BR>expanded white and blue lotus.<BR>—विकसित-वदन-<BR>कमल, अस्, आ, अम्, opening [her] lotus-like mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस्त
वि-कस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. split or rent asunder,<BR>divided, mutilated, (Sāy. = वि-च्छिन्न.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस्वर|विकस्वरः
वि-कस्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, opening, expanding; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of plant (= रक्त-पुनर्नवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकास|विकासः
वि-कास, अस्, m. opening, expanding, expansion,<BR>blossoming, blooming, budding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासक
वि-कासक, अस्, इका, अम्, causing to expand or blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासन|विकासनं
वि-कासन, अम्, n. the causing to expand or blow,<BR>expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासित
वि-कासित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to open or blow,<BR>expanded; radiant, (in this sense better वि-काशित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासिन्
वि-कासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, expanding, opening, budding,<BR>blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाङ्क्षा
विकाङ्क्षा वि-काङ्क्षा, f. freedom from de-<BR>sire or eagerness, hesitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकार|विकारः
विकार वि-कार, &c. See under वि-कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाल|विकालः
विकाल वि-काल, अस्, m. twilight, evening,<BR>afternoon, the close of day; [cf. वैकालिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकालक|विकालकः
वि-कालक, अस्, m. twilight, evening; (इका), f. =<BR>मान-रन्ध्रा, a perforated copper vessel (which<BR>when placed in a pan of water marks the time by<BR>gradually filling); a sort of clepsydra or water-clock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश्
विकाश् वि-काश्, cl. 1. A. -काशते, -काशितुम्,<BR>to appear, become visible, shine forth: Caus. P. -का-<BR>शयति, -यितुम्, to cause to appear or shine forth, dis-<BR>play, blazon abroad, publish; illuminate, make clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश|विकाशः
1. वि-काश, अस्, m. appearance, becoming visible,<BR>display, manifestation, exhibition; open or splendid<BR>appearance; expanse, sky, heaven, ether; an open or<BR>direct course (= प्रसार, Kirāt. XV. 52); an ob-<BR>lique course (= विषम-गति, Kirāt. XV. 52);<BR>opening; budding, blowing (as a flower, but in these<BR>senses better वि-कास); pleasure, joy, enjoyment.<BR> — 1. विकाश-ता, f. or 1. विकाश-त्व, अम्, n. appear-<BR>ance, display; expansion, diffusion.<BR>—विकाश-भृत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, possessing expansion, full-blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश|विकाशः
2. वि-काश, अस्, m. absence of manifestation or<BR>display, solitude, loneliness, privacy.<BR>—२. विकाश-ता,<BR>f. or 2. विकाश-त्व, अम्, n. absence of manifestation,<BR>loneliness, solitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशक
वि-काशक, अस्, इका, अम्, displaying, causing to<BR>appear or shine forth, illustrating; causing to expand<BR>or bloom, opening (= वि-कासक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशन|विकाशनं
वि-काशन, अम्, n. manifestation, display, exhi-<BR>bition, extent; expansion, blowing (of a flower; but<BR>in this sense better वि-कासन); the causing to ex-<BR>pand or blow (= वि-कासन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशित
वि-काशित, अस्, आ, अम्, made visible, displayed,<BR>made to shine, illumined, resplendent; expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशिन्
वि-काशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, becoming visible or apparent,<BR>becoming manifested, shining forth; expanding, spread-<BR>ing, developing, opening, budding, blowing, (in these<BR>senses better वि-कासिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचाकसत्
वि-चाकसत्, अत्, अती, अत्, Ved. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाषिन्
विकाषिन् वि-काषिन् for विकासिन् and विकाशिन्,<BR>q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकास|विकासः
विकास वि-कास, वि-कासित. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिर|विकिरः
विकिर वि-किर, वि-किरत्, &c. See under<BR>वि-कॄ, p. 910, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुक्षि|विकुक्षिः
विकुक्षि वि-कुक्षि, इस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Ikṣvāku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुञ्च्
विकुञ्च् वि-कुञ्च्, cl. 10. P. -कुञ्चयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to contract; to bend or turn back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुञ्चित
वि-कुञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, contracted, crisped, curled;<BR>drawn into wrinkles, knitted (as the brow), frowning.<BR>—विकुञ्चित-ललाट-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, having a scowling<BR>brow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुण्ठ|विकुंठ
विकुण्ठ वि-कुण्ठ (perhaps ‘not blunted,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">Page0910-a+ 78</a>]<BR>‘not worn out,’ ‘ever fresh;’ cf. अ-कुण्ठ), N. of<BR>Viṣṇu's heaven; (आ), f., N. of the mother of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0909-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुण्ठित|विकुंठित
वि-कुण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, obtuse, blunt; weak,<BR>feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुस्र|विकुस्रः
विकुस्र वि-कुस्र, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. II. 15.<BR>said to be fr. rt. कस् with वि), the moon, (said to<BR>be also written वि-क्रस्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूज्
विकूज् वि-कूज्, cl. 1. P. -कूजति, -कूजितुम्,<BR>to coo, chirp, sing (as a bird &c.), make any cry or<BR>sound, hum, buzz.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूजन|विकूजनं
वि-कूजन, अम्, n. cooing, chirping, humming,<BR>grumbling, rumbling, (अन्त्र-विकूजन, rumbling<BR>of the bowels.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूण्
विकूण् वि-कूण्, cl. 10. P. -कूणयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Ved. to contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणन|विकूणनं
वि-कूणन, अम्, n. a side-glance, leer, wink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणिका
वि-कूणिका, f. the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृ
विकृ वि-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to make different, form variously, give a<BR>different shape to anything, transform, alter, change,<BR>convert, cause to alter; to cause any one to change<BR>his state or opinions; to cause to change for the<BR>worse, distort, deprave, pervert, deform, render de-<BR>formed, spoil; to display; to form or produce variously<BR>(as sound, A.); to be changed, undergo a change,<BR>change for the worse, deteriorate, change one's state or<BR>opinions (A.); to rejoice (A.); to feel aversion (A.);<BR>to act in various ways (A.); to decorate in various<BR>manners; to move to and fro, become restless (A.);<BR>to put into practice, exercise; to distribute; to ex-<BR>tend; to destroy, annihilate; to act in a hostile or un-<BR>friendly way towards (with gen. or loc. of the person);<BR>to contend together: Pass. वि-क्रियते, &c., to be<BR>changed, undergo a change; to act as a substitute for,<BR>act in place of (with acc., Ved.): Caus. -कारयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to change or be changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर|विकरः
वि-कर, अस्, m. sickness, disease, loss of health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकरण|विकरणः
वि-करण, अस्, m., scil. प्रत्यय, (in grammar)<BR>a term for the affix or conjugational characteristic<BR>which is placed between the root and terminations,<BR>the inserted conjugational affix; (according to Pāṇini<BR>these affixes are शप्, शपो लुक्, श्लु, श्यन्, श्नु,<BR>श, श्नम्, उ, यक्, and च्लि with its substitutes तासि,<BR>स्य, and सिप्, the first eight of which are added in<BR>the Present, Imperfect, Imperative, and Potential,<BR>and before a Kṛt which contains a mute palatal श्,<BR>when these affixes denote the Kartṛ or Agent, i. e.<BR>the Active; when, however, they denote the Karman<BR>or Bhāva, i. e. the Passive or Neuter, then यक् is<BR>added; च्लि is added in the Aorist, तासि in the Ist<BR>Future, स्य in the 2nd Future and Conditional, and<BR>सिप् before Leṭ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्मन्|विकर्म्मन्
1. वि-कर्मन्, अ, n. various business or duty; pro-<BR>hibited or unlawful act, fraud; retiring from business;<BR>(आ, आ, अ), acting variously; acting wrongly.<BR>—वि-<BR>कर्म-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, acting in various ways, acting<BR>wrongly or illegally, one who does forbidden acts.<BR>—विकर्म-क्रिया, f. an illegal or immoral act,<BR>vicious conduct.<BR>—विकर्म-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, doing<BR>what is illegal or immoral, addicted to vice, engaged<BR>in prohibited acts; engaged in various business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्मन्|विकर्म्मन्
2. वि-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, not acting, free from action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्मिक|विकर्मिकः|विकर्म्मिक
विकर्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, transacting various affairs;<BR>doing forbidden acts; acting wrongly; (अस्), m. a<BR>clerk or superintendant of markets or fairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकार|विकारः
वि-कार, अस्, m. change of form or nature, altera-<BR>tion or deviation from any natural state; change for<BR>the worse, change from a state of health, disease,<BR>sickness; a wound; change of mind; change from<BR>the quiescent condition of the soul, perturbation,<BR>emotion, passion, feeling, excitement; (in the Sāṅkhya<BR>philosophy) a production or that which is evolved<BR>from a previous source or प्र-कृति, q. v., a modifi-<BR>cation or result of the modification of the प्रकृतयः<BR>or producers.<BR>—विकार-तस्, ind. from change, through<BR>change.<BR>—विकार-त्व, अम्, n. the state of change,<BR>condition of transforming, transformation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारित
वि-कारित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be changed, made<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">Page0910-b+ 79</a>]<BR>to undergo a change, converted, perverted; rendered<BR>unfavourable or unfriendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारिन्
वि-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, producing a change, modifying;<BR>undergoing a change; producing a change for the<BR>worse, spoiling; feeling emotion, falling in love; (ई),<BR>m., N. of the seventh year of Jupiter's cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुर्वाण|विकुर्व्वाण|विकुर्व्वाणः
वि-कुर्वाण, अस्, आ, अम्, undergoing or causing<BR>a change of form or of mind, &c.; feeling emotions<BR>of joy, &c., rejoicing, being glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृत|विकृतं
वि-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, altered, changed, modified, trans-<BR>formed, changed in form or feeling; changed for the<BR>worse, sick, diseased, mutilated, maimed, deformed,<BR>disfigured; unnatural; imperfect, unfinished, incom-<BR>plete; affected by passion, overcome by emotion; enter-<BR>taining feelings of disgust or aversion, averse, estranged;<BR>strange, extraordinary; (अम्), n. change, alteration;<BR>change for the worse, a diseased state; disgust, aver-<BR>sion.<BR>—विकृत-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, changed in<BR>appearance.<BR>—विकृत-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, changed<BR>in mind, estranged, made unfriendly or ill-disposed.<BR>—विकृत-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, having excited eyes.<BR>—विकृत-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a distorted<BR>face, ugly-faced.<BR>—विकृताकार (˚त-आक्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, changed in form or appearance, misshaped,<BR>distorted in form.<BR>—विकृताकृति (˚त-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>having a deformed shape or aspect.<BR>—विकृताङ्ग<BR>(˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, changed in form, having mis-<BR>shaped limbs, deformed.<BR>—विकृतानन (˚त-आन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a distorted countenance, ugly-faced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृति|विकृतिः
वि-कृति, इस्, f. change, alteration of any kind (as<BR>of purpose, mind, form, nature, &c.), change from<BR>a natural or healthy state, sickness, disease; change<BR>from a quiescent state, emotion, anger, wrath, fear;<BR>(in the Sāṅkhya philosophy) a production or that<BR>which is evolved from a previous प्र-कृति or pro-<BR>ducer (see वि-कार, col. 1); fermented or spirituous<BR>liquor; a species of metre (the stanza consisting of<BR>four lines of two syllables each, variously arranged);<BR>= डिम्भ (according to Śabda-k.); (इस्), m., N. of<BR>a king.<BR>—विकृति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of<BR>change, changed; diseased, wounded; changeable.<BR>—विकृति-विज्ञानीय, N. of a chapter in the Ash-<BR>ṭāṅga-hṛdaya-saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृती
वि-कृती, f. = वि-कृति above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रिया
वि-क्रिया, f. alteration, change; transformation,<BR>change of mind, &c., any change from a natural or<BR>quiescent state, disease, injury, mischief, emotion,<BR>anger, any sudden affection or seizure [cf. भूत-व्˚,<BR>रोम-व्˚]; a preparation or dish of rice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृत्
विकृत् वि-कृत्, cl. 6. P. -कृन्तति, -कर्तितुम्,<BR>to cut into or through, divide by cutting, tear to<BR>pieces, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्त
वि-कर्त, वि-कर्त्तृ in गो-व्˚, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्तन|विकर्तनः|विकर्त्तन|विकर्त्तनः
