विगन्धिका, f. = हपुषा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगम्
विगम् वि-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति, -गन्तुम्,<BR>to go away, pass away, depart, disappear, cease, die,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">Page0912-b+ 77</a>]<BR>disperse: Caus. -गमयति, -यितुम्, to cause to go<BR>or pass away; to spend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगत|विगतः
2. वि-गत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. वि-गत see under<BR>2. वि), gone away, departed, disappeared, ceased, gone;<BR>dead; parted, severed, separated; freed or exempt from,<BR>devoid of; lost; destitute of light, obscured, gloomy,<BR>dark.<BR>—विगत-कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>stain or soil, unsoiled, free from sin, sinless; pure,<BR>righteous.<BR>—विगत-क्लम, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>fatigues have ceased, relieved from fatigue.<BR>—वि-<BR>गत-ज्ञान, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has lost his wits.<BR>—विगत-ज्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, cured of fever; freed<BR>from feverishness or morbid feeling, freed from<BR>trouble or distress of mind; exempt from decay.<BR>—विगत-भी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, one whose fears are gone,<BR>free from fear.<BR>—विगत-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, free<BR>from resentment.<BR>—विगत-राग, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid<BR>of passion or affection.<BR>—विगत-लक्षण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, devoid of good or lucky marks, unfortunate, un-<BR>lucky.<BR>—विगत-श्रीक, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of for-<BR>tune, unfortunate, unprosperous.<BR>—विगत-सङ्कल्-<BR>प, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of purpose or design, without<BR>resolution.<BR>—विगत-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, void of affec-<BR>tion.<BR>—विगत-स्नेह-सौहृद, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has relinquished love and friendship.<BR>—विगत-<BR>स्पृह, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of wish or desire, in-<BR>different.<BR>—विगतार्तवा (˚त-आर्˚), f. a woman in<BR>whom the menstrual excretion has ceased, one past<BR>child-bearing or one past the age of fifty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगम|विगमः
वि-गम, अस्, m. departure, secession, decease,<BR>death, withdrawing, relinquishment, separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाम
वि-गाम, अस्, m., Ved. a step, pace, stride, (in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 155, 4. applied to the three strides of<BR>Viṣṇu; Sāy. = विविध-गमन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर|विगरः
विगर वि-गर, अस्, m. ‘not swallowing,’ an<BR>abstemious man; a naked ascetic; a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ज्
विगर्ज् वि-गर्ज्, cl. 1. P. -गर्जति, -गर्जितुम्,<BR>to roar out, cry out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्
विगर्ह् वि-गर्ह्, cl. 1. A. -गर्हते, -गर्हि-<BR>तुम्, to blame, abuse, reproach, revile; to disdain,<BR>despise, contemn: Caus. -गर्हयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>revile, rail at, vituperate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हण|विगर्हणं
वि-गर्हण, अम्, आ, n. f. blaming, blame, abusing,<BR>abuse, censure, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हणीय
वि-गर्हणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, reprehensible, blam-<BR>able, bad, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हित|विगर्हितः
वि-गर्हित, अस्, आ, अम्, abused, reviled, blamed;<BR>disdained, despised; reprobated, scouted, condemned;<BR>prohibited; low, vile; wicked, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्य
1. वि-गर्ह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, reprehensible, blamable.<BR>—विगर्ह्य-कथा, f. reprehensible speech, scandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्य
2. वि-गर्ह्य, ind. having blamed or reviled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगल्
विगल् वि-गल्, cl. 1. P. -गलति, -गलितुम्,<BR>to flow or ooze or trickle away, drain off, fall in<BR>drops, drip, distil; to melt away, liquefy, pass away,<BR>disappear, fade away, disperse; to fall down or out,<BR>drop down, drop out; to become loose or untied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलत्
वि-गलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, flowing away, trickling,<BR>dropping, oozing; melting away, dissolving, fading,<BR>dispersing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलित|विगलितः
वि-गलित, अस्, आ, अम्, flowed away, flowing,<BR>trickled, distilled, oozed, fallen, dropped, melted<BR>away, liquefied, dissolved; dissipated, dispersed,<BR>gone, decayed; slackened, untied (as a knot);<BR>loose, disordered (as hair or dress), untied, detached.<BR>—विगलित-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, having dishevelled hair.<BR>—विगलित-नीवि, इस्, इस्, इ, having the knot untied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

