विच्छिद्
विच्छिद् वि-च्छिद् (see rt. 1. छिद्), cl. 7. P.<BR>A. -च्छिनत्ति, -च्छिन्त्ते, -च्छेत्तुम्, to cut or tear<BR>asunder, cleave or split in two, break asunder, divide,<BR>separate; to cut off, break off; to interrupt, inter-<BR>cept, disturb; to destroy; to be divided (Ved.):<BR>Pass. -च्छिद्यते, to be cut asunder; to be cut off or<BR>destroyed; to come to an end, cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0914-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छित्ति|विच्छित्तिः
वि-च्छित्ति, इस्, f. cutting asunder, dividing, sepa-<BR>rating, separation; cutting off, excision; breaking<BR>off, fracture; interruption, cessation; absence, disap-<BR>pearance, loss, destruction; cesura, pause in a verse;<BR>boundary, limit (as of a house &c.); N. of certain<BR>amorous gestures practised by a mistress or heroine<BR>in a drama (described as irregularity or carelessness<BR>in dress and decoration); colouring or marking the<BR>body with coloured unguents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0914-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिद्य
वि-च्छिद्य, ind. having cut asunder; having se-<BR>parated; separatively, interruptedly, (विच्छिद्य वि-<BR>च्छिद्य, on separate occasions.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0914-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिद्यमान
वि-च्छिद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being cut off, being<BR>destroyed or exterminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0914-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्न|विच्छिन्नः
वि-च्छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, cut asunder, severed, se-<BR>parated, divided, parted, scattered, distributed, por-<BR>tioned, shared; cut off; broken off, broken, inter-<BR>rupted, prevented, intercepted, ceased, ended, termi-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">Page0915-a+ 77</a>]<BR>nated; hidden, absent; variegated, diversified, coloured,<BR>anointed, smeared or marked with unguents; crooked,<BR>curved.<BR>—विच्छिन्न-धूम-प्रसर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the free course of the smoke interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0914-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेद|विच्छेदः
वि-च्छेद, अस्, m. cutting asunder, dividing, sepa-<BR>ration, disjunction, cutting off, breaking off, breaking,<BR>interruption, termination; prohibition, prevention,<BR>removal; the division of a book, a section, chapter;<BR>dissension, difference; space, interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदक
वि-च्छेदक, अस्, इका, अम्, cutting asunder, di-<BR>viding, separating, &c.; (अस्), m. a cutter off, divider,<BR>sector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदन|विच्छेदनं
वि-च्छेदन, अम्, n. the act of cutting asunder,<BR>severing, dividing, separating, &c.; destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदनीय
वि-च्छेदनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut asunder, to<BR>be divided or separated, &c.; divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुर्
विच्छुर् वि-च्छुर् (see rt. छुर्), cl. 6. P.<BR>-च्छुरति, -च्छुरितुम्, to inlay; to overspread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुरित|विछुरित
वि-च्छुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, inlaid; coated, overspread,<BR>covered; anointed, besmeared; suffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छो
विच्छो वि-च्छो (see rt. छो), Caus. -च्छा-<BR>ययति, -यितुम्, Ved. to cut about, wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्यु
विच्यु वि-च्यु, cl. 1. A. -च्यवते, -च्योतुम्, to<BR>fall asunder, fall to pieces, split in two, perish; to fall<BR>or depart from, deviate or swerve from (with abl.);<BR>to fall off or down, decline; to fail, err, make a mis-<BR>take; to displace (Ved.): Caus. -च्यावयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to fall to pieces, throw down, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युत|विच्युतः
वि-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen apart, fallen down,<BR>slipped off; fallen or deviated from, displaced, thrown<BR>down; (in surgery) separated from the living part,<BR>sloughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युति|विच्युतिः
वि-च्युति, इस्, f. falling to pieces; downfall, deca-<BR>dence, decline; deviation from; severance, separa-<BR>tion; failure, miscarriage, (गर्भ-व्˚, miscarriage<BR>of the fetus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विछ्|विच्छ्
विछ् विछ् (connected with rt. 1. वी), cl.<BR>6. P. विच्छति or विच्छायति, विविच्छ<BR>or विच्छायाञ्-चकार (Part. विविच्छ्वस् or विविश्वस्),<BR>अविच्छीत् or अविच्छायीत्, विच्छितुम् or विच्छायितुम्,<BR>to go, approach; cl. 10. P. विच्छयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>speak; to shine [cf. विश्न]: Intens. वेविच्छीति; [cf.<BR>Gr. οἰχνέω, οἴχομαι.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्
विज् 1. विज्, cl. 7. P. विनक्ति, विवेज, वि-<BR>जिष्यति, अविजीत्, cl. 6. A. (usually with<BR>prep. उद्) विजते, विविजे, विजिष्यते, अविजिष्ट, वि-<BR>जितुम्, to shake, tremble; to be agitated; to tremble<BR>with fear; to fear, be afraid; to be distressed or<BR>afflicted; cl. 3. P. A. (= rt. विच्, with which, as a verb<BR>of the 3rd class in the sense ‘to separate, discrimi-<BR>nate,’ it may be identified, see rt. विच्) वेवेक्ति, वे-<BR>विक्ते, &c., to separate, divide; to separate by the<BR>reason, distinguish, discriminate, judge; to be sepa-<BR>rate, &c.: Pass. विज्यते, Aor. अवेजि: Caus. वेज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अवीविजत्, to terrify, frighten:<BR>Desid. विविजिषति: Intens. वेविज्यते, वेवेक्ति, to<BR>shake or tremble violently; [cf. probably Gr. ἀΐσσω;<BR>Angl. Sax. wicelian, wince.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्न
विग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, trembling, agitated,<BR>disturbed, alarmed; [cf. उद्-विग्न.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्
2. विज्, m., Ved., according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>1. 92, 10. विजः = पक्षिणः, ‘birds,’ but according<BR>to modern scholars the meaning is rather ‘dice.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज
विज, अस्, m., Ved. one who trembles or is agitated;<BR>a gamester, gambler; a harasser, vexer, (Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda II. 12, 5 = उद्-वेजक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितव्य
विजितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be apprehended or feared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितृ
विजितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what separates or<BR>divides, separating, &c.; (ता), m. a discriminator,<BR>distinguisher, judge; a partner, co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजग्ध
विजग्ध वि-जग्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (see rt. 1. जक्ष्),<BR>eaten up, devoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजटीकृ
विजटीकृ वि-जटी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to comb out braided or matted hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्
विजन् वि-जन्, cl. 4. A. -जायते, -जनितुम्, to<BR>be born or produced; to bear young, generate, en-<BR>gender, bring forth, produce; to be transformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजनन|विजननं
वि-जनन, अम्, n. the act of generating or bearing<BR>young, bringing forth, procreation, birth, delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजनित
वि-जनित, अस्, आ, अम्, brought forth, engendered,<BR>begotten, born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्मन्
वि-जन्मन्, अ, n. separate birth, birth in general;<BR>(आ, आ, अ), born illegitimately, bastard; (आ), m. a<BR>bastard, illegitimate child, the son of an outcast or<BR>of a degraded Vaiśya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजात|विजातः
वि-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born separately; base born,<BR>of mixed origin; generated; born; transformed;<BR>(आ), f. a woman who has borne children, a mother,<BR>matron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजाति|विजातिः
वि-जाति, इस्, f. different origin or birth; different<BR>species; different caste or tribe or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातीय|विजातीयः
वि-जातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, of different or mixed origin;<BR>of different birth or caste; of different tribe or species;<BR>of a different kind or sort, dissimilar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजामन्
वि-जामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. variously born, manifold,<BR>(Sāy. = वि-जन्मन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजायमान
वि-जायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being born or pro-<BR>duced; generating, producing offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजावन्
वि-जावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. variously productive,<BR>prolific, widely-spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन|विजनः
विजन वि-जन, अस्, आ, अम्, free from people,<BR>private, lonely, solitary; (अम्), n. a solitary place,<BR>desert; (ए), ind. privately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजपिल|विजपिलं
विजपिल विजपिल, अम्, n. (etymology<BR>doubtful), mud (= पङ्क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजय|विजयः
विजय वि-जय, विजयिन्, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन|विजयिनं
विजयिन विजयिन, अस्, आ, अम्, sauce mixed<BR>with the water of boiled rice; [cf. विजल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजर|विजरः
विजर वि-जर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from decay,<BR>fresh, young; (अम्), n. a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल|विजलं
विजल विजल, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. sauce &c.<BR>mixed with rice-water or gruel (= विजिन, पिच्छिल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्प्
विजल्प् वि-जल्प्, cl. 1. P. -जल्पति, -जल्पितुम्,<BR>to speak foolishly, chatter, talk, speak (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्प|विजल्पः
वि-जल्प, अस्, m. speech, talk, idle or foolish talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्पित
वि-जल्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken foolishly, spoken<BR>or talked about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजात|विजातः
विजात वि-जात, वि-जाति. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजानत्
विजानत् वि-जानत्. See under वि-ज्ञा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजामन्
विजामन् वि-जामन्. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजामातृ
विजामातृ वि-जामातृ, ता, m., Ved. an in-<BR>ferior daughter's husband, defective son-in-law (ex-<BR>plained by Yāska as ‘one who has not all the neces-<BR>sary qualifications,’ see Nirukta VI. 9, where it is also<BR>said that the people of the south always speak of<BR>this word as denoting ‘a man who has purchased his<BR>wife’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजि
विजि वि-जि, cl. 1. A. -जयते (rarely P. -ज-<BR>यति), -जेतुम्, to conquer, vanquish, be victorious,<BR>overcome, defeat, overpower; to win or acquire by<BR>conquest; to contend victoriously with (with inst.);<BR>to surpass, excel: Caus. -जापयति, -यितुम् (anom.<BR>Aor. अजीजयत्), to cause to conquer; to conquer:<BR>Desid. -जिगीषति, to wish to conquer; to attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजय|विजयः
वि-जय, अस्, m. conquest, victory, triumph, over-<BR>coming, defeating, overpowering, excelling; a divine<BR>car, chariot of the gods; N. of Arjuna; of Yama;<BR>of a son of Cuñcu; of a son of Jaya; of a son of<BR>Sañjaya; of a son of Jayad-ratha; of a king of the<BR>Āndhra race; of the father of the twenty-first Jina;<BR>of one of the persons named Śukla-Balas by the<BR>Jainas [cf. बल]; of the founder of Buddhist<BR>civilisation in Ceylon; of a particular auspicious<BR>period; of the first year of Jupiter's cycle; (आ),<BR>f., N. of the goddess Durgā; of one of her<BR>female attendants; of one of the wives of Yama;<BR>of a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Kṛśāśva; of<BR>various plants, hemp, Cannabis Sativa, or the tops<BR>of the plant used as a narcotic; yellow myrobalan,<BR>Terminalia Chebula; orris root; N. of a particular<BR>Tithi or lunar day (the third, eighth, or thirteenth<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">Page0915-c+ 78</a>]<BR>of a fortnight); of a festival in honour of Durgā (on<BR>the tenth day of the light half of the month Āśvina,<BR>when the image of Durgā is cast into the water);<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—विजय-कुञ्जर, अस्,<BR>m. a royal or war elephant (which carries a standard).<BR>—विजय-च्छन्द, अस्, m. a kind of necklace, one<BR>of 500 rows or strings.<BR>—विजय-डिण्डिम, अस्, m.<BR>‘drum of victory,’ a large military drum.<BR>—विजय-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—विजय-दशमी,<BR>f. the tenth day of the light half of the month<BR>Āśvina, the day of the Daśa-harā, &c.<BR>—विजय-<BR>नगर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—विजय-नन्दन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a sovereign of the race of Ikṣvāku.<BR>—विजय-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having victory for a<BR>result.<BR>—विजय-मर्दल, अस्, m. ‘drum of victory,’<BR>a large military drum.<BR>—विजय-राम, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—विजय-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f., N. of the<BR>mother of Veṅkaṭa.<BR>—विजय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessing victory, triumphant.<BR>—विजय-सिद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>accomplishment of victory, success.<BR>—विजयाभिनन्-<BR>दन (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a great warrior yet<BR>to arise and to be the founder of an era.<BR>—विजया-<BR>भ्युपाय (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, m. means of victory.<BR>—विजयार्थम् (˚य-अर्˚), ind. on account of vic-<BR>tory, for victory.<BR>—विजयार्थिन् (˚य-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>seeking victory, desirous of conquest.<BR>—विजया-सप्-<BR>तमी, f. the seventh day of the light half of a month<BR>falling on a Sunday.<BR>—विजयेश (˚य-ईश), अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of victory,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—विजयोत्सव<BR>(˚य-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘victory-festival,’ N. of a festival<BR>in honour of Viṣṇu celebrated on the tenth day of the<BR>light half of the month Āśvina (= विजय-दशमी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयन्त|विजयंत|विजयंतः|विजयन्तः
वि-जयन्त, अस्, m. ‘the victorious,’ epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयमान
वि-जयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, conquering, victorious,<BR>triumphant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन्
विजयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, conquering, victorious, trium-<BR>phant; (ई), m. a conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीष|विजिगीषः
वि-जिगीष, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of victory, wishing<BR>to overcome or conquer; emulous; (आ), f. a desire<BR>to conquer or overcome or subdue, wish to surpass,<BR>desire to excel, competition, emulation, ambition.<BR>—विजिगीषा-विवर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of am-<BR>bition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषत्
वि-जिगीषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing or striving to<BR>conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषिन्
वि-जिगीषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, desirous to conquer or over-<BR>come, desirous of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषु|विजिगीषुः
वि-जिगीषु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of victory or con-<BR>quest, desirous to overcome or surpass, emulative,<BR>emulous, ambitious; (उस्), m. a warrior; an invader,<BR>antagonist; a disputant; an opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित|विजितः
वि-जित, अस्, आ, अम्, conquered, subdued, defeated,<BR>won, gained.<BR>—विजित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who<BR>has conquered.<BR>—विजितात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ,<BR>one who has conquered himself, self-subdued.<BR>—वि-<BR>जिताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son of Pṛthu.<BR>—विजितासन (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, indifferent about<BR>a seat.<BR>—विजितेन्द्रिय (˚त-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the organs of sense or passions subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिति|विजितिः
वि-जिति, इस्, f. conquest, victory, triumphing over,<BR>vanquishing; victory over various enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित्य
वि-जित्य, ind. having conquered, having won.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजेतृ
वि-जेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, victorious, a victor, conqueror,<BR>gainer, winner, (पुरां विजेतृ, ‘conqueror of towns,’<BR>an epithet of Śiva.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिग्राहयिषु
विजिग्राहयिषु वि-जिग्राहयिषु, वि-जिघृ-<BR>क्षु. See p. 913, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिन|विजिनं|विजिनः
विजिन विजिन, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. sauce<BR>&c. mixed with rice-water or gruel; [cf. विजल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिल|विजिलं|विजिलः
विजिल or विजिविल = विजिन above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिहीर्षा
विजिहीर्षा वि-जिहीर्षा, f. (fr. Desid. of वि-<BR>हृ), wish or intention to roam about or take one's<BR>pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिहीर्षु
वि-जिहीर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing or seeking to<BR>roam about or sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्म|विजिह्मः
विजिह्म वि-जिह्म, अस्, आ, अम्, curved, bent;<BR>crooked in mind or purpose, dishonest, depraved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">Page0916-a+ 75</a>]<BR>—विजिह्म-ता, f. or विजिह्म-त्व, अम्, n. crooked-<BR>ness, dishonesty, craftiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0915-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजीव्
विजीव् वि-जीव्, cl. 1. P. -जीवति, -जीवितुम्, to<BR>revive, return to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजुल|विजुलः
विजुल विजुल, अस्, m. the silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भ्|विजृंभ्
विजृम्भ् वि-जृम्भ्, cl. 1. A. -जृम्भते, -जृम्-<BR>भितुम्, to yawn, gape; to open (intrans.), unfold,<BR>expand, become expanded or developed or exhibited,<BR>spread out, blossom; to extend; to spring open, spring<BR>back (as a bow); to become displayed, break forth<BR>or out, appear, rise; to display activity or energy,<BR>exhibit courage, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भण|विजृंभण|विजृंभणं|विजृम्भणं
वि-जृम्भण, अम्, n. yawning, gaping; expand-<BR>ing, unfolding, displaying, exhibiting, extending;<BR>blossoming, budding; pastime, sport (especially<BR>amorous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भित|विजृंभित|विजृम्भितं|विजृम्भितः
वि-जृम्भित, अस्, आ, अम्, yawned, gaped; ex-<BR>panded, opened, unfolded, displayed, exhibited, acted;<BR>blossomed; arisen, appeared; sported, wantoned;<BR>(अम्), n. pastime, sport; wish, desire; act.<BR>—वि-<BR>जृम्भित-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, displaying affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजेह्
विजेह् वि-जेह्, cl. 1. A. -जेहते, -जेहितुम्, to<BR>open the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजेहमान
वि-जेहमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. opening wide;<BR>darting forth, (Sāy. = प्रक्षिपत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजोषस्
विजोषस् वि-जोषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. dis-<BR>united, estranged from each other, no longer friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जन|विज्जनं
विज्जन विज्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. sauce &c.<BR>mixed with rice-water or gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जल|विज्जलं
विज्जल, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. = विज्जन above;<BR>(अम्), n. an arrow.<BR>—विज्जल-पुर, N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जिल|विज्जिलं
विज्जिल, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. sauce &c. mixed with<BR>rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जाका
विज्जाका विज्जाका, f., N. of a female poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जूलिका
विज्जूलिका विज्जूलिका, f., N. of a kind of<BR>plant (= जतुका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञ|विज्ञः
विज्ञ वि-ज्ञ. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञा
विज्ञा वि-ज्ञा, cl. 9. P. A. -जानाति, -जानीते,<BR>ज्ञातुम्, to distinguish, discern, understand, observe,<BR>perceive, know, recognise, know thoroughly or well,<BR>have a right knowledge of; to be familiar with; to<BR>find out, investigate, inquire, ascertain, learn, learn<BR>from (with gen.); to hear, to consider as; to explain;<BR>to become wise or learned (Manu IV. 20): Caus.<BR>-ज्ञपयति and -ज्ञापयति, -यितुम्, to make known,<BR>declare, report, communicate, announce to any one<BR>(acc.); to make any one understand, apprise, teach,<BR>instruct; to make a representation or request (in a<BR>respectful manner), ask, beg; to inform any one of<BR>anything (with two acc.): Desid. -जिज्ञासति, to wish<BR>to understand or know, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजानत्
वि-जानत्, अन्, अती, अत्, distinguishing, understand-<BR>ing, knowing, recognising, possessing various or<BR>extended knowledge, wise, considerate; (अन्), m. a<BR>wise man, sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिज्ञासा
वि-जिज्ञासा, f. a desire of knowing distinctly, wish<BR>to prove or try.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञ|विज्ञः
वि-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing, intelligent; wise,<BR>learned; proficient, conversant, clever, experienced,<BR>skilful, prudent, discreet; (अस्), m. a wise man.<BR>—विज्ञ-ता, f. or विज्ञ-त्व, अम्, n. intelligence,<BR>wisdom, learning, skill, cleverness.<BR>—विज्ञ-बुद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. Indian spikenard (= जटा-मांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्त
वि-ज्ञप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, made known, reported, re-<BR>presented; apprised, respectfully informed or told.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्ति|विज्ञप्तिः
वि-ज्ञप्ति, इस्, f. information, representation, re-<BR>spectful statement or communication; a report, an-<BR>nouncement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञात|विज्ञातः
वि-ज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, discerned, understood, known,<BR>perceived; celebrated, famous, notorious.<BR>—विज्ञा-<BR>तार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who is acquainted<BR>with any matter or the true state of a case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञातृ
वि-ज्ञातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who knows or under-<BR>stands, an experienced person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञान|विज्ञानं
वि-ज्ञान, अम्, n. the act of distinguishing or per-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">Page0916-b+ 78</a>]<BR>ceiving or recognising, discerning, understanding,<BR>comprehending, distinction, intelligence, knowledge,<BR>science, learning, worldly knowledge of any kind<BR>(including all subjects except that understanding of<BR>the true nature of God or Brahma which is acquirable<BR>only by abstract meditation and the study of the<BR>Vedas), wisdom; business, employment; music.<BR>—विज्ञान-कन्द, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—विज्ञान-<BR>कौमुदी, f., N. of a Buddhist woman.<BR>—विज्ञान-<BR>पाद, अस्, m. (see पाद), an epithet of Vyāsa.<BR>—वि-<BR>ज्ञान-भिक्षु, उस्, m., N. of the author of the Yoga-<BR>sāra-saṅgraha, the Yoga-vārttika, the Sāṅkhya-sāra,<BR>and the Brahmādarśa.<BR>—विज्ञान-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of knowledge or intelligence, all knowledge,<BR>intellectual (said of the first or innermost of the<BR>several sheaths of the soul).<BR>—विज्ञानमय-कोष,<BR>अस्, m. the sheath consisting of intelligence, the in-<BR>telligent sheath (of the soul, according to the Vedānta<BR>philosophy) or that sheath which is caused by the<BR>understanding being associated with the organs of<BR>perception.<BR>—विज्ञान-मातृक, अस्, m. ‘parent of<BR>knowledge,’ an epithet of Buddha.<BR>—विज्ञान-ललित,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—विज्ञान-वाद, अस्, m. the theory<BR>of Vi-jñāna, ideal theory.<BR>—विज्ञानेश्वर (˚न-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘master of knowledge,’ N. of the author<BR>of the Mitākṣarā commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानिक|विज्ञानिकः
विज्ञानिक, अस्, ई, अम्, learned, well-informed,<BR>clever, skilful, proficient, conversant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापक|विज्ञापकः
वि-ज्ञापक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.), who or<BR>what makes known or apprises, making known,<BR>giving information; (अस्), m. an informant; an<BR>instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापन|विज्ञापनं
वि-ज्ञापन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of making known<BR>or acquainting, teaching; representing, informing;<BR>information, instruction; respectful communication or<BR>representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापनीय
वि-ज्ञापनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made known or<BR>represented, to be apprised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापित
वि-ज्ञापित, अस्, आ, अम्, apprised, informed, in-<BR>structed; respectfully told or represented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञाप्ति|विज्ञाप्तिः
वि-ज्ञाप्ति, इस्, f. representing, informing; respectful<BR>communication or representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञाय
वि-ज्ञाय, ind. having known or perceived, having<BR>understood, having ascertained, having recognised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञेय|विज्ञेयं
वि-ज्ञेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be perceived or known<BR>or understood; cognizable, intelligible, comprehen-<BR>sible, discernible, recognizable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्वर
विज्वर वि-ज्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from fever<BR>or pain; free from distress; exempt from decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विझर्झर
विझर्झर वि-झर्झर, अस्, आ, अम्, making a<BR>harsh or rattling sound, discordant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञिलविन्दु
विञिलविन्दु विञिलविन्दु, N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जामर|विंजामर|विंजामरं|विञ्जामरं
विञ्जामर विञ्जामर, अम्, n. the white of<BR>the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जोली|विंजोली
विञ्जोली विञ्जोली, f. a line, row, range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्
विट् विट् (also written बिट्; cf. rt. 1. विड्),<BR>cl. 1. P. वेटति, वेटितुम्, to sound; to<BR>curse, swear at, revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट|विटः
विट, अस्, m. a voluptuary; a paramour; (in the<BR>drama) the companion of a prince or dissolute young<BR>man or sometimes of a courtezan, (he resembles in<BR>some respects the Vidūṣaka, being generally repre-<BR>sented as a parasite on familiar terms with his asso-<BR>ciate, but at the same time accomplished in the arts<BR>of poetry, music, and singing); a catamite; a rogue,<BR>cheat; N. of a mountain; the Khayar tree, Mimosa<BR>Catechu; a medicinal salt (= विड्-लवण); a rat;<BR>the orange tree; a branch and its shoot.<BR>—१. विट-<BR>प, अस्, m. a keeper of catamites.<BR>—विट-प्रिय, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of tree (= मुद्गर).<BR>—विट-माक्षिक,<BR>अस्, m. a sort of mineral (= ताप्य).<BR>—विट-लवण,<BR>अम्, n. a medicinal salt (= विड्-लवण, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटप|विटपः
2. विटप, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 145. fr. rt. विट् in the sense ‘to sound’), the<BR>young branch of a tree or creeper; a new shoot or<BR>sprout, branch (in general); a bush; a clump, cluster,<BR>thicket, tuft; spreading, expansion; the septum of the<BR>scrotum.<BR>—विटप-शस्, ind. in branches, in shoots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपिन्
विटपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having branches; (ई), m. a tree<BR>(in general); the large Indian fig-tree, Ficus Indica.<BR>—विटपि-मृग, अस्, m. ‘tree-animal,’ a monkey,<BR>ape; [cf. तरु-मृग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्क|विटंक|विटंकः|विटङ्कः
विटङ्क वि-टङ्क or वि-टङ्कक, अस्, अम्, m.<BR>n. (see rt. टङ्क्), a dove-cot, an aviary (perhaps in<BR>this sense fr. 2. वि, a bird, + टङ्क); the loftiest<BR>point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्कित|विटंकित
वि-टङ्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, marked, stamped, laden<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटि|विटिः
विटि विटि, इस्, f. yellow sanders.<BR>—विटि-कण्-<BR>ठी-रव, अस्, m., N. of the grammarian Varada-rāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्कारिका
विट्कारिका विट्-कारिका, विट्-चर, &c. See<BR>under 3. विष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्ठल|विट्ठलः
विट्ठल विट्ठल, अस्, m. (or commonly विठ्-<BR>ठल), N. of a god worshipped at Pandhar-pur or<BR>Punderpoor in the Bombay presidency, (he is stated<BR>to be an incarnation of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa himself,<BR>who is believed to have visited this city); N. of the<BR>author of the Prasāda commentary and of the Vaiṣ-<BR>ṇava-siddhānta-dīpikā.<BR>—विट्ठल-दीक्षित, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the Kuṇḍa-maṇḍapa-siddhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्पण्य
विट्पण्य विट्-पण्य, विट्-पति, &c. See<BR>under 2. विश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठङ्क|विठंक
विठङ्क विठङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठर|विठरः
विठर विठर, अस्, m. an epithet of Vṛhas-<BR>pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
विड् 1. विड् (= rt. विट्, q. v.), cl. 1. P. वे-<BR>डति, वेडितुम्, to call out, cry out against,<BR>curse, swear at, revile; to break (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
2. विड्, ट्, f. a fragment, bit (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड|विडं|विडः
विड, अम्, n. a kind of factitious salt (procured<BR>by boiling earth impregnated with saline particles);<BR>a particular kind of fetid salt (used medicinally as a<BR>tonic aperient, commonly called Vit-lavan or Bit-<BR>noben, cf. विड्-लवण; it is black in colour and is<BR>prepared by fusing fossil salt with a small portion of<BR>Emblic Myrobalan, the product being muriate of soda<BR>with small quantities of muriate of lime, sulphur,<BR>and oxide of iron); a fragment, bit, portion (?).<BR>—विड-गन्ध, अम्, n. the medicinal salt described<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडङ्ग|विडंग|विडङ्गं|विडङ्गः
विडङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, clever, able, skilful, con-<BR>versant; (अस्, अम्), m. n. Erycibe Paniculata, a<BR>vegetable and medicinal substance (considered of<BR>great efficacy as a vermifuge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्ब्|विडंब्
विडम्ब् वि-डम्ब्, cl. 10. P. -डम्बयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to imitate, act like (= अनु-कृ), copy, emulate,<BR>simulate (with acc., e. g. तडिद्-विलसितानि विडम्ब-<BR>यन्ति, they imitate the flashes of lightning); to<BR>give anything another form, transform, distort; to<BR>impose upon, deceive, cheat; to ridicule, deride,<BR>mock; to afflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्ब|विडंब|विडंबः|विडम्बः
वि-डम्ब, अस्, m. imitation; afflicting, distress-<BR>ing, annoyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बन|विडंबन|विडंबनं|विडम्बनं
वि-डम्बन, अम्, आ, n. f. imitation, copying,<BR>assuming a similar appearance or dress, disguise,<BR>masquerade, transformation, imposture, (कु-विडम्-<BR>बना, f. base imposture); deceiving, deception,<BR>fraud, breach of faith; disappointing, frustrating;<BR>afflicting, distressing, vexation, mortification, pain,<BR>distress; ridiculing, ridiculousness, ludicrousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बनीय
वि-डम्बनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be imitated, to be<BR>assumed as a disguise; to be distressed or annoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बयत्
वि-डम्बयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, imitating, copying;<BR>assuming, putting on (a borrowed dress or appear-<BR>ance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बित|विडंबित|विडम्बितः
वि-डम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, imitated, copied, assumed,<BR>put on (as a borrowed from &c.), simulated, trans-<BR>formed, distorted; mocked at, ridiculed, derided;<BR>deceived, disappointed, frustrated; vexed, mortified;<BR>distressed, low, poor, abject; (अम्), n. an object of<BR>ridicule or contempt, despicable object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बिन्
विडम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, imitating, resembling; causing<BR>deception or error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0916-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडारक|विडारकः
विडारक विडारक, अस्, m. = विडालक, a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडाल|विडालः
विडाल विडाल, अस्, m. (also written बिडाल,<BR>in Uṇādi-s. I. 117. said to be fr. rt. विड्, ‘to cry out;’<BR>according to others perhaps fr. विश् + आल, ‘having<BR>habitation with man’), a cat; the eye-ball; (ई), f. a<BR>female cat; N. of a plant (= विदारी, q. v.).<BR>—विडाल-<BR>पद, अस्, m. a measure of weight (the same as the<BR>Karṣa or weight of sixteen Māṣas).<BR>—विडाल-प-<BR>दक, अम्, n. the measure of a Karṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडालक|विडालकं|विडालकः
विडालक, अस्, m. a cat; application of ointment<BR>to the exterior of the eye (especially to the eyelids<BR>when the lashes have fallen off or are ulcerated);<BR>(अम्), n. yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडाली
विडाली, f. See under विडाल above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडी
विडी वि-डी, cl. 1. 4. A. -डयते, -डीयते,<BR>-डयितुम्, to fly asunder, fly apart, fly separately,<BR>fly on one side or obliquely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडीन|विडीनं
वि-डीन, अम्, n. the act of flying apart or ob-<BR>liquely, one of the different modes of flight attributed<BR>to birds; [cf. अ-विडीन; other modes of flight are<BR>अव-डीन, उड्डीन, नि-डीन, प्र-डीन, परि-डीन,<BR>सण्-डीन, डीन-डीनक, q. q. v. v.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडीनक
वि-डीनक, अम्, n. flying apart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडुल|विडुलः
विडुल विडुल, अस्, m. a sort of cane, Cala-<BR>mus Rotang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडूरज|विडूरजं
विडूरज विडूर-ज, अम्, n. lapis lazuli,<BR>(for विदूर-ज, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडोजस्
विडोजस् विड्-ओजस् or विड्-औजस्, आस्, m. (said<BR>to be fr. विड् or 2. विश् + ओजस्), N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्गन्ध|विड्गन्धं
विड्गन्ध विड्-गन्ध, विड्-ग्रह, &c. See<BR>under 3. विष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विण्ट्
विण्ट् विण्ट् (= rt. वुण्ट्), cl. 10. P. विण्ट-<BR>यति, &c., to kill; to waste away, perish,<BR>decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंस|वितंसः
वितंस वि-तंस, अस्, m. (see rt. तंस्), a bird-<BR>cage (perhaps fr. 2. वि, a bird, + तंस), any net or<BR>chain or apparatus for confining beasts or birds; [cf.<BR>वी-तंस.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितक्ष्
वितक्ष् वि-तक्ष्, cl. 1. P. -तक्षति, -तक्षि-<BR>तुम्, -तष्टुम्, Ved. to cut off; to cleave or split in<BR>pieces; to carve out, plane off, chisel; to wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितष्ट
वि-तष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, hewn or carved out, planed,<BR>fashioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितड्
वितड् वि-तड्, cl. 10. P. -ताडयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to strike or dash to pieces; to strike back; to strike<BR>against (with loc.); to wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितण्ड|वितंडः|वितण्डः
वितण्ड वि-तण्ड, अस्, m. (probably con-<BR>nected with वि-तड् above), a sort of lock or bolt<BR>with three divisions or wards; an elephant; (आ), f.<BR>cavil, captious objection, hypercriticism, perverse or<BR>frivolous argument (especially, in the Nyāya phil.,<BR>idly carping at the arguments or assertions of another<BR>without attempting to establish the opposite side of<BR>the question), frivolous or fallacious controversy or<BR>wrangling, debate, criticism (in general); an esculent<BR>root, Arum Colocasia; the oleander plant, Nerium<BR>Odorum; a ladle, spoon; benzoin or storax (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितण्डक
वि-तण्डक, अस्, m., N. of the author of a<BR>Dharma-śāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत|विततं
वितत वि-तत. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ|वितथं
वितथ वि-तथ, अस्, आ, अम्, untrue, false,<BR>incorrect, unreal, vain, futile; [cf. यथा-तथ.]<BR>—वितथ-प्रयत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose efforts<BR>are futile, endeavouring in vain.<BR>—वितथ-मर्याद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, incorrect in behaviour.<BR>—वितथी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, rendered vain or futile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ्य|वितथ्यं
वि-तथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, untrue (= वि-तथ above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितद्रु|वितद्रुः
वितद्रु वितद्रु, उस्, f., N. of a river said to<BR>be situated in the Pañjāb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्
वितन् वि-तन्, cl. 8. P. A. -तनोति, -तनुते, -त-<BR>नितुम्, to stretch out, spread through, extend, expand,<BR>lengthen out, spread over, cover over, fill; to spread<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">Page0917-b+ 78</a>]<BR>(a net, snare, &c.); to stretch (a cord &c.); to<BR>draw or bend (a bow); to unfold, develop, manifest,<BR>exhibit; to carry out, execute, perform, accomplish<BR>(any rite or ceremony); to offer an oblation, sacrifice,<BR>&c.; to effect, cause, produce; to prepare, make<BR>ready, arrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत|विततं
वि-तत, अस्, आ, अम्, stretched out, extended,<BR>spread out, stretched, expanded; lengthened out,<BR>lengthened, elongated, large, broad, wide; spread<BR>over, covered, prepared, diffused, performed, accom-<BR>plished, celebrated; effected; (अम्), n. any stringed<BR>instrument, such as a lute, &c.<BR>—वितत-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. extendedness, extension, expansiveness, largeness.<BR>—वितत-धन्वन्, आ, m. one who has drawn a<BR>bow to its full stretch.<BR>—वितत-वपुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्,<BR>having an elongated body.<BR>—वितती-करण, अम्, n.<BR>the act of stretching out, spreading.<BR>—वितती-कृ, cl.<BR>8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to stretch out,<BR>expand, spread.<BR>—वितती-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, stretched<BR>out, spread, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितति|विततिः
वि-तति, इस्, f. stretching out, spreading, extension,<BR>expansion; collection, quantity; a clump, cluster (of<BR>trees &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत्य
वि-तत्य, ind. having stretched or spread out, hav-<BR>ing spread through; having stretched, having drawn<BR>or bent (as a bow); stretching into, extending far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्वत्
वि-तन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, stretching or spreading<BR>out, stretching, extending, expanding, bending (a<BR>bow &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्वान
वि-तन्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, extending, spreading out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितान|वितानं|वितानः
वि-तान, अस्, अम्, m. n. stretching or spreading<BR>out, expansion; an awning, canopy, cover; a cushion;<BR>an oblation, sacrifice; the sacrificial hearth on which the<BR>sacred fires are kept, or the sacred fire itself; a heap,<BR>quantity; season, opportunity; (अम्), n. a form of<BR>the metre Anuṣṭubh or verse of four lines of eight<BR>syllables each, (each line of the stanza is said to con-<BR>sist of two Iambics, one Trochee, and one Spondee);<BR>leisure, rest, interval of occupation; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>empty, vacant; pithless, sapless; dull, stupid; wicked,<BR>abandoned.<BR>—वितान-मूलक, अम्, n. the fragrant<BR>root of Andropogon Muricatus (= उशीर).<BR>—वितान-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a canopy or awning.<BR>—वि-<BR>तानी-करण, अम्, n. the act of overspreading or<BR>covering.<BR>—वतानी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-<BR>रुते, -कर्तुम्, to spread over, extend over (as a<BR>canopy &c.), form an awning, overshadow.<BR>—वि-<BR>तानी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, spread or extended over (as<BR>a canopy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानक|वितानकं|वितानकः
वितानक, अस्, अम्, m. n. an awning, canopy,<BR>(especially) a cloth spread over a large open hall or<BR>court (in which dancing, singing, &c. are exhibited);<BR>an expanse; a heap, quantity; (अस्), m. the Māḍa<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानाय
वि-तानाय, Nom. A. -तानायते, &c., to become<BR>a canopy, turn into an awning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितायमान
वि-तायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being stretched out,<BR>being spread abroad or overspread, being covered or<BR>shaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितनु|वितनुः
वितनु वि-तनु, उस्, वी, उ, very thin, delicate,<BR>graceful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्तु|वितंतुः|वितन्तुः
वितन्तु वि-तन्तु, उस्, m. a good horse; (उस्),<BR>f. a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितप्
वितप् वि-तप्, cl. 1. P. A. -तपति, -ते, -तप्-<BR>तुम्, to give out heat, be hot, burn; to warm one's<BR>self (or any member of the body, A.); to be heated,<BR>to feel or suffer pain; to pervade, penetrate (Ved.):<BR>Caus. -तापयति, -यितुम्, to make hot, heat, warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितमस्
वितमस् वि-तमस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, free from<BR>darkness, light; exempt from the quality of igno-<BR>rance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरण|वितरणं
वितरण वि-तरण. See under वि-तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क्
वितर्क् वि-तर्क्, cl. 10. P. -तर्कयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to reason or think about, make conjectures about<BR>(with acc.), to infer, conjecture, guess, suppose,<BR>imagine, think, believe; to anticipate, expect; to<BR>deliberate or reflect about, discuss (with acc.); to<BR>consider as, take for; to find out, ascertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क|वितर्कः
वि-तर्क, अस्, m. reasoning, argument, inference,<BR>conjecture, guess, supposition, opinion, anticipation,<BR>discussion; deliberation, consideration of probabilities<BR>or alternatives, doubt, apprehension; a teacher, an<BR>instructor in divine knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कण|वितर्कणं
वि-तर्कण, अम्, n. reasoning, conjecturing, in-<BR>ferring, drawing an inference, argument, discussion,<BR>reflection; doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कित
वि-तर्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, conjectured, imagined,<BR>anticipated, (अ-वितर्कित, unexpected.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क्य
1. वि-तर्क्य, ind. having deliberated or con-<BR>sidered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क्य
2. वि-तर्क्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be conjectured or<BR>supposed or imagined, questionable, doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्ज्
वितर्ज् वि-तर्ज्, cl. 1. P. -तर्जति, -तर्जितुम्,<BR>to threaten, menace, revile, abuse, inveigh against,<BR>blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्तुरम्
वितर्तुरम् वि-तर्तुरम्, वि-तर्तुराण. See<BR>p. 918, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्दि|वितर्दिः|वितर्द्दिः
वितर्दि वि-तर्दि, इस्, f. or वितर्दिका, f. or<BR>वितर्दी, f. (said to be fr. rt. तृद्), a raised square<BR>piece of ground in the centre of a house or temple;<BR>a kind of covered terrace in the middle of a court-<BR>yard; a quadrangular seat or bench made of wood, a<BR>place in a court-yard for sitting in or standing under;<BR>a floor on four posts, a kind of altar or temporary<BR>stage or shed in the middle of a court-yard (for per-<BR>forming sacrifices &c. = वेदिका); a covered tempo-<BR>rary platform on which idols are sometimes placed;<BR>a verandah, balcony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धि
वि-तर्द्धि, इस्, f. or वि-तर्द्धिका, f. or वि-<BR>तर्द्धी, f. = वि-तर्दि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितल|वितलं
वितल वि-तल, अम्, n. the second in order<BR>of the seven lower regions or regions under the<BR>earth; [cf. पाताल.]<BR>—वितल-लोक, अस्, m. the world<BR>or lower region of Vi-tala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्तपुरी
वितस्तपुरी वितस्त-पुरी, f., N. of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्ता
वितस्ता वितस्ता, f., N. of a river in the<BR>Pañjāb, now called Jhelum or Betusta or Behut (the<BR>Hydaspes of the Greeks; cf. पञ्च-नद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्ति|वितस्तिः
वितस्ति वि-तस्ति, इस्, f. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तस् or तंस् with prep. वि), a long span measured by<BR>the extended thumb and little finger, equal to twelve<BR>Aṅgulas.<BR>—वितस्ति-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, almost a Vi-<BR>tasti long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्थान
वितस्थान वि-तस्थान, वि-तिष्ठमान. See<BR>under 1. वि-ष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितान|वितानं|वितानः
वितान वि-तान. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितिमिर
वितिमिर वि-तिमिर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>darkness, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितीर्ण
वितीर्ण वि-तीर्ण. See under वि-तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुद्
वितुद् वि-तुद्, cl. 6. P. A. -तुदति, -ते, -तोत्-<BR>तुम्, to pierce, strike, sting; to tear, scratch; to<BR>scourge, whip: Caus. -तोदयति, Ved. -तुदायति,<BR>-यितुम्, to pierce, strike, tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुद्यमान
वि-तुद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being pierced, being<BR>struck, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्न|वितुन्नं
वि-तुन्न, अम्, n. the pot-herb Marsilia Quadri-<BR>folia (= सु-निषण्णक); the aquatic plant Śaivala,<BR>Vallisneria Octandra; (आ), f. the tree Flacourtia Cata-<BR>phracta (= तामलकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नक|वितुन्नकं|वितुन्नकः
वितुन्नक, अस्, m. Flacourtia Cataphracta; (अम्),<BR>n. coriander seed; blue vitriol; (इका), f. Flacourtia<BR>Cataphracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुष्ट
वितुष्ट वि-तुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, displeased, dis-<BR>satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितूस्तय
वितूस्तय वि-तूस्तय (fr. तूस्त, q. v. + वि),<BR>Nom. P. -तूस्तयति, -यितुम्, to comb out matted or<BR>braided hair (= केशान् विजटी-कृ), clean or smooth<BR>the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृद्
वितृद् वि-तृद्, cl. 7. P. A. -तृणत्ति, -तृन्त्ते,<BR>-तर्दितुम्, to pierce, bore, cleave; to break through;<BR>to excavate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0917-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृप्
वितृप् वि-तृप्, cl. 4. P. -तृप्यति, -तर्पितुम्,<BR>-तर्प्तुम्, -त्रप्तुम्, to be satisfied, become satiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृप्त
वि-तृप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied, satiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्
वितृष् वि-तृष्, cl. 4. P. -तृष्यति, -तर्षि-<BR>तुम्, to be thirsty: Caus. -तर्षयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make thirsty, cause to thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्ण
वितृष्ण वि-तृष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>thirst or desire, satisfied, content.<BR>—वितृष्ण-ता, f.<BR>or वितृष्ण-त्व, अम्, n. freedom from desire, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितॄ
वितॄ वि-तॄ, cl. 1. P. -तरति, -तरितुम्, -त-<BR>रीतुम्, to pass across or over, cross over, go over, go<BR>or pass through, pervade; to convey or bring away;<BR>to give away; to give, grant, bestow, allow, yield,<BR>afford, favour with, (उत्तरं वितॄ, to favour with<BR>an answer); to give (medicine), apply a remedy; to<BR>forgive; to cause, produce (= जनयति, Kirāt. V.<BR>31); to do, perform, effect; to increase, enhance:<BR>Caus. -तारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to go through,<BR>to carry through, accomplish: Intens., Ved. -तर्तूर्-<BR>यते, to pass over vehemently, labour or perform<BR>energetically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरण|वितरणं
वि-तरण, अम्, n. the act of crossing or passing<BR>over; donation, gift; giving up, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरम्
वि-तरम्, ind., Ved. widely, vastly, exceedingly,<BR>(Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 100, 12 = अत्य्-अन्तम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरित्रत्
वि-तरित्रत्, अत्, अती, अत्, Ved. excessively carrying<BR>through or accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्तुरम्
वि-तर्तुरम्, ind., Ved. with alternate movements,<BR>alternately, (Sāy. = परस्पर-व्यतिहारेण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्तुराण
वि-तर्तुराण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. alternating; (Sāy.)<BR>injuring, despoiling (= हिंसत्, Ṛg-veda VI. 47, 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितीर्ण
वि-तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, crossed, passed, gone over<BR>or through; subdued, overcome; effaced; conveyed;<BR>given, bestowed, conferred, yielded, afforded; widely<BR>distant.<BR>—वितीर्ण-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more widely<BR>distant, situated further off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त्
वित्त् वित्त्, cl. 10. P. (probably rather to<BR>be regarded as a Nom. fr. वित्त, col. 2),<BR>वित्तयति, -यितुम्, to abandon (especially by giving<BR>away), to give, give alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त वित्त, वित्तक, वित्ति. See cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रप
वित्रप वित्रप, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रस्
वित्रस् वि-त्रस्, cl. 1. 4. P. -त्रसति, -त्रस्-<BR>यति, -त्रसितुम्, to tremble, be frightened: Caus.<BR>-त्रासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to tremble, terrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रस्त|वित्रस्तः
वि-त्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, frightened, alarmed, terrified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रास|वित्रासः
वि-त्रास, अस्, m. fear, terror, alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रासित
वि-त्रासित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to tremble, fright-<BR>ened, terrified.<BR>—वित्रासित-विहङ्गम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having (its) birds frightened away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्वक्षण
वित्वक्षण वि-त्वक्षण, अस्, m., Ved. = वि-<BR>शेषेण तनू-कर्तृ, one who greatly thins or<BR>emaciates or destroys (his enemies; see rt. त्वक्ष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्सन|वित्सनः
वित्सन वित्सन, अस्, m. an ox, bull (=<BR>वृषभ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ्
विथ् विथ् (= rts. वेथ्, 1. विध्), cl. 1. A.<BR>वेथते, विविथे or विवेथे, वेथिष्यते,<BR>अवेथिष्ट, वेथितुम्, to ask, beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथुर|विथुरः
विथुर विथुर, अस्, आ, अम् (connected with<BR>rt. व्यथ्), agitated, troubled, (Sāy. = व्यथित);<BR>trembling, frail, fragile, weak, feeble, poor, (Sāy. =<BR>हीन); (अस्), m. a thief; a demon, Rākṣasa; (आ),<BR>f. a widow (according to Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथुर्य
विथुर्य, Nom. P. विथुर्यति, -यितुम्, Ved. to<BR>be agitated or troubled, (Sāy. = व्यथते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ्या
विथ्या विथ्या, f. a kind of plant (commonly<BR>called Go-jihvā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद् 1. विद्, cl. 2. P. वेत्ति (ep. also A.<BR>वित्ते, 3rd pl. A. विदते or विद्रते; a form<BR>of the Perf., viz. वेद contracted from विवेद, is<BR>often substituted for the Pres. वेत्ति; 3rd pl. विदुस्,<BR>contracted from विविदुस्, being also much used for<BR>विदन्ति, वेत्थ for वेत्सि, &c.), Impf. अवेत् (Ist<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-b" target="_blank">Page0918-b+ 81</a>]<BR>sing. अवेदम्, 2nd sing. अवेत् or अवेस्, 3rd pl. अवि-<BR>दुस् and according to Vopa-deva also अविदन्; 3rd<BR>pl. A. अविदत or अविद्रत), Pot. विद्यात्, Impv.<BR>वेत्तु or विदां-करोतु (3rd pl. A. विदताम् or वि-<BR>द्रताम्), विवेद (according to Vopa-deva also वि-<BR>दाम्-बभूव), वेदिष्यति (sometimes वेत्स्यति),<BR>अवेदीत्, वेदितुम् (originally ‘to see,’ = Lat. video);<BR>to perceive, understand, know, learn, ascertain, find<BR>out, experience, feel; to consider, regard, look upon,<BR>value, take for, name, call (especially in the 3rd pl.<BR>विदुः of वेद above, used with a present significa-<BR>tion, e. g. तं स्थविरं विदुः, they consider or<BR>call him aged; राजर्षिर् इति मां विदुः, they<BR>consider me a Rājarṣi); to notice, take notice of<BR>(with gen.; Ved.); to convey, bestow, grant (Ved.);<BR>cl. 6. P. A. विन्दति, -ते (in Ṛg-veda I. 7, 7. विन्-<BR>धे = 1st sing. A. विन्दे, 3rd pl. ep. विन्दते), Pot.<BR>विन्देत् (ep. विन्द्यात्, Ved. 1st sing. P. विदेयम्,<BR>A. विदेय), विवेद (3rd sing. Ved. विविदत् = लब्-<BR>ध-वान् in Ṛg-veda VII. 21, 6), विविदे (2nd sing.<BR>विविदिषे, Ved. विवित्से; 3rd pl. Ved. विद्रे = लब्-<BR>ध-वन्तः, Ṛg-veda I. 87, 6), वेदिष्यति, -ते (or<BR>according to others वेत्स्यति, -ते), अविदत्, अविदत,<BR>वेदितुम् (or वेत्तुम्), to find, discover, meet with; to<BR>obtain, gain, get, acquire, possess; to take in mar-<BR>riage, choose a husband or wife, marry, (in this sense<BR>generally A.); to convey, cause to obtain, grant (Ved.,<BR>in Ṛg-veda I. 86, 8. विदा = विद, which according<BR>to Sāy. is for 2nd pl. Impv. = लम्भयत); cl. 7.<BR>A. (ep. also P.) विन्त्ते (विनत्ति), विविदे, वेत्स्यते,<BR>अवित्त, वेत्तुम्, to perceive, understand, know; to<BR>consider, regard, value, take for; to find, meet with,<BR>obtain; to reason, reflect: Pass. or cl. 4. A. विद्यते,<BR>विविदे, वेत्स्यते, Aor. अवेदि, to be known; to be<BR>found or obtained; to happen; to be or exist:<BR>Caus. वेदयति, -यते, -यितुम्, Aor. अवीविदत्, to<BR>cause to know, make known, announce, report, in-<BR>form of, apprise, tell, narrate, teach (sometimes with<BR>loc. of person); to cause to find or discover; to<BR>know; to perceive, feel; to be perceived or felt (A.,<BR>Manu XII. 13); to dwell, inhabit (?): Desid. विवि-<BR>दिषति, -ते, विवित्सति, -ते, to desire to know, strive<BR>to know; to wish to find or discover: Intens. वेविद्-<BR>यते, वेवेत्ति; [cf. Gr. ἴδ-ο-ν, εἶδ-ο-ν (i. e. ἔϝιδον),<BR>εἴδ-ο-μαι, οἶδ-α (= वेद), εἶδ-ος. εἴδ-ωλο-ν, ἴνδαλμα,<BR>ἀ-ειδ-ής, ἀ-ίδη-ς, ἄ-ῐστ-ο-ς, είδ-ώς, ἴδ-μην, ἴστωρ,<BR>ἰστορ-έ-ω, ἴδ-ρι-ς, ἰνδ-άλλομαι, ὕδνης, ὕδω,<BR>ὑδέω, ἀείδω: Lat. vid-eo, visu-s (Umbr. virs-e-<BR>to), vis-o, vi-tru-m: Goth. vait, un-vit-i, ‘igno-<BR>rance;’ vit-an, far-veit-l, vitôth, in-veitan, veit-<BR>vods: Old Germ. wizan, gi-wizo, wîzago, wîza-<BR>gôn: Angl. Sax. witan, wita, ge-wit, ge-wittig,<BR>wisian, ge-wis, wite, ‘punishment;’ witnian, ‘to<BR>punish:’ Slav. vid-e-ti, ‘to see;’ ved-e-ti, ‘to know:’<BR>Lith. veid-a-s, vyzd-i-s, veizd-mi: Hib. fêth,<BR>‘science, instruction;’ (perhaps) feidhim, ‘I mani-<BR>fest, relate;’ feidir, ‘power;’ (perhaps also) aithnim,<BR>aithnighim, ‘I know;’ aithne, ‘known;’ ‘know-<BR>ledge;’ fios, ‘knowledge;’ fiosach, ‘knowing.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Pāṇ. VIII. 2, 56.<BR>the forms वित्त and विन्न belong to the root when<BR>used in cl. 7; according to Vopa-deva also in cl. 6),<BR>known, notorious, famous; found out, discovered,<BR>investigated, examined, discussed, judged; found,<BR>acquired, gained, possessed; (अम्), n. wealth, pro-<BR>perty, possessions, goods, money, substance, thing;<BR>power.<BR>—वित्त-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of wealth.<BR>—वित्त-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by wealth.<BR>—वित्त-<BR>जानि, इस्, इस्, इ, one who has taken or married a wife,<BR>(Sāy. = लब्ध-भार्य.)<BR>—वित्त-द, अस्, m. ‘wealth-<BR>giver,’ one who gives away property, a benefactor.<BR>—वित्त-दुग्ध, अम्, n. ‘wealth-milk,’ wealth like<BR>milk.<BR>—वित्त-मात्रा, f. ‘materials of property,’<BR>wealth.<BR>—वित्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having property,<BR>wealthy, opulent, rich.<BR>—वित्त-वर्धन, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, increasing wealth, lucrative, profitable.<BR>—वित्त-<BR>विवर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, increasing property or<BR>capital, bearing interest.<BR>—वित्त-शाठ्य, अम्, n.<BR>cheating in money matters.<BR>—वित्त-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>deprived of wealth, indigent.<BR>—वित्तागम (˚त-आग्˚),<BR>अस्, m. acquisition of property, any source of wealth,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">Page0918-c+ 81</a>]<BR>means of acquiring property.<BR>—वित्तेश (˚त-ईश), अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of riches,’ epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—वित्तेहा<BR>(˚त-ईहा), f. desire of wealth, cupidity, avarice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तक
वित्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, known, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्ति|वित्तिः
वित्ति, इस्, f. knowledge, judgment, investigation,<BR>discussion, discrimination; probability, likelihood;<BR>acquisition, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त्वा
वित्त्वा, ind. having found or met with, having<BR>obtained; having married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
2. विद्, त्, त्, त्, who or what knows, a knower,<BR>knowing; obtaining [cf. वरिवो-विद्]; (त्), f. know-<BR>ing, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद|विदः
विद, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing, a knower (= 2. विद्<BR>at the end of comps.); (अस्), m. a knower; a wise<BR>man, sage; (आ), f. knowledge, learning; understand-<BR>ing, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदत्
विदत्, अन्, अती, अत्, knowing, learned, wise, intel-<BR>ligent; granting, bestowing (Ved.).<BR>—विदद्-अश्व,<BR>अस्, m. ‘granting horses,’ a proper N.<BR>—विदद्-वसु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. possessing wealth, granting wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथ|विदथः
विदथ, अम्, n. anything known, knowledge<BR>(Ved.); a sacrificial rite, sacrifice, ceremony, rite<BR>(Ved.); battle (according to some); (अस्), m. a<BR>sacrifice (according to Naigh. III. 17); a wise or<BR>learned man, sage, scholar; a saint, devotee, ascetic;<BR>a proper N. (Ved.); [cf. Goth. vitoth.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथिन्
विदथिन्, ई, m., Ved., N. of a king (father of<BR>Ṛjiśvan).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथ्य
विदथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worthy of sacrifice or<BR>sacrificial worship, adorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदान
विदान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. knowing, wise, one<BR>who knows, a knower, (Sāy. = विद्वस्); known,<BR>discovered; making known, showing, exhibiting,<BR>(Sāy. = प्र-ज्ञापयत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित|विदितं|विदितः
विदित, अस्, आ, अम्, perceived, known, understood;<BR>apprised, informed; represented; promised, agreed;<BR>(अस्), m. a learned man, sage; (अम्), n. knowledge,<BR>information, representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित्वा
विदित्वा, ind. having perceived, having known,<BR>having ascertained or considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदु|विदुः
विदु, उस्, m. the hollow between the frontal globes<BR>of an elephant; a hippopotamus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुर|विदुरः
विदुर, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing, wise, intelligent;<BR>(अस्), m. a learned or clever man; an intriguer; N.<BR>of the younger brother of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra and Pāṇḍu,<BR>(they were all three sons of Vyāsa, but only the<BR>latter two by the two widows of Vicitra-vīrya; when<BR>Vyāsa wanted a third son, the elder widow sent him<BR>one of her slave-girls, dressed in her own clothes,<BR>and this girl became the mother of Vidura, who is<BR>sometimes called Kṣattṛ as if he were the son of a<BR>Kṣatriya man and Śūdra woman: Vidura is described<BR>as सर्व-बुद्धिमतां वरः, and is one of the<BR>wisest characters in the Mahā-bhārata, always ready<BR>with good advice both for his nephews, the Pāṇḍavas,<BR>and for his brother Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुल|विदुलः
विदुल, अस्, m. a sort of reed or ratan (Calamus<BR>Rotang); the same reed growing in water (Calamus<BR>Fasciculatus); gum-myrrh; (आ), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुषी
विदुषी, f. (fem. of विद्वस्, q. v.), a wise woman.<BR>—विदुषि-तरा or विदुषी-तरा, f. a very wise<BR>woman (= विद्वत्-तरा, Vopa-deva VII. 49).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुष्टर
विदुष्-टर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = विद्वत्-तर,<BR>more wise, very wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुष्मत्|विदुष्मन्त्
विदुष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, full of learned men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुस्
विदुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. = विद्वस्, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्मन्
विद्मन्, Ved. knowledge (according to Sāy. =<BR>ज्ञान).<BR>—विद्मनापस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (for विद्मना<BR>+ अपस्), Ved. pervading all things by knowledge<BR>or knowing all acts, (according to Nirukta XI. 33 =<BR>विदित-कर्मन्, according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>31, 1. विद्मनापसः = ज्ञानेन व्याप्नुवानाः<BR>or ज्ञात-कर्माणः), executing work with know-<BR>ledge, working skilfully (= उत्कृष्ट-ज्ञानेन<BR>निष्पाद्य-कर्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्मन
विद्मन, an adj. formed by Sāy. from विद्मन्<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यमान|विद्यमानः
विद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being perceived or known,<BR>being found, being present (sometimes applied to<BR>present time in grammar), being in existence, exist-<BR>ing, being, being preserved; actual, real, possessed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-a" target="_blank">Page0919-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(as property), being in one's possession.<BR>—विद्य-<BR>मान-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, one who possesses hair.<BR>—विद्यमान-ता, f. or विद्यमान-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>existence, presence.<BR>—विद्यमान-मति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>possessing understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0918-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्या
विद्या, f. knowledge, (काल-व्˚, knowledge of time,<BR>i. e. of the almanac), learning, scholarship, philosophy,<BR>science, (according to some there are four Vidyās or<BR>sciences, 1. त्रयी, the triple Veda; 2. आन्वीक्षिकी,<BR>logic and metaphysics; 3. दण्ड-नीति, the science of<BR>government; 4. वार्त्ता, practical arts, such as agri-<BR>culture, commerce, medicine, &c.; and Manu VII.<BR>43. adds a fifth, viz. आत्म-विद्या, knowledge of soul<BR>or sublime theological truth: according to others,<BR>Vidyā has fourteen divisions, viz. the four Vedas,<BR>the six Vedāṅgas, the Purāṇas, the Mīmāṃsā, Nyāya,<BR>and Dharma or law; or with the four Upa-vedas,<BR>eighteen divisions); a spell, incantation; the god-<BR>dess Durgā; the tree Premna Spinosa; magical skill;<BR>a kind of magical pill (which placed in the mouth<BR>is supposed to give the power of ascending to heaven).<BR>—विद्या-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing wisdom, giving<BR>knowledge or science; (अस्), m. a learned man, (in<BR>this sense the word may also be divided into विद्या-<BR>आकर, ‘a mine of learning.’)<BR>—विद्याकर-वाज-<BR>पेयिन्, ई, m., N. of an author.<BR>—विद्यागम (˚या-<BR>आग्˚), अस्, m. acquirement of knowledge, proficiency<BR>in science.<BR>—विद्या-चण, अस्, आ, अम्, or विद्या-<BR>चुञ्चु, उस्, उस्, उ (चण and चुञ्चु are regarded by<BR>Pāṇini as Taddhita affixes), famous for learning or<BR>knowledge.<BR>—विद्या-तस्, ind. from learning, than<BR>learning (after a compar.).<BR>—विद्या-दल, अस्, m.<BR>‘science-leafed,’ N. of the Bhūrja or Bhojpattra tree<BR>(the leaves of which are used for writing).<BR>—विद्या-<BR>दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who gives or imparts know-<BR>ledge, a teacher, instructor.<BR>—विद्या-दान, अम्, n.<BR>the giving of knowledge, teaching.<BR>—विद्या-देवी, f.<BR>‘goddess of learning,’ a female divinity peculiar to<BR>the Jainas, (sixteen are named, Rohiṇī, Prajñaptī,<BR>Vajra-śṛṅkhalā, Kuliśāṅkuśā, Cakreśvarī, Nara-<BR>dattā, Kālī, Mahā-kālī, Gaurī, Gandhārī, Sarvāstra-<BR>mahājvālā, Mānavī, Vairāṭyā, A-cchuptā, Mānasī,<BR>Mahā-mānasikā.)<BR>—विद्या-धन, अम्, n. wealth<BR>consisting in learning, money acquired by scholarship.<BR>—विद्या-धर, अस्, m. ‘magical-knowledge holder,’<BR>a particular kind of good or evil genius attending<BR>upon the gods, (according to Kullūka on Manu XII.<BR>47 = देवानुयायिन्); a kind of spirit or fairy; N.<BR>of several persons; (ई), f. a female of the same class<BR>of genii, a fairy, sylph.<BR>—विद्याधर-ताल, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a particular time in music.<BR>—विद्याधरा-<BR>चार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—विद्या-<BR>धरी-परिजन, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by Vidyā-<BR>dharīs.<BR>—विद्याधार (˚या-आध्˚), अस्, m. a recep-<BR>tacle of knowledge.<BR>—विद्याधिराज (˚या-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—विद्या-नगर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>city.<BR>—विद्या-नन्द, अस्, m. ‘pleasure of know-<BR>ledge,’ N. of a chapter of the Pañca-daśī; of an<BR>author.<BR>—विद्या-निवास, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of a commentary on the Mugdha-bodha.<BR>—विद्या-<BR>निवास-भट्टाचार्य, अस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>the Sac-carita-mīmāṃsā.<BR>—विद्यानुपालन (˚या-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. the act of cherishing or patronising<BR>learning, encouragement or cultivation of science;<BR>acquiring learning, studying.<BR>—विद्यानुपालिन् (˚या-<BR>अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, cherishing or encouraging science,<BR>acquiring learning.<BR>—विद्यानुसेवन (˚या-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the cultivation of science or learning.<BR>—वि-<BR>द्यानुसेविन् (˚या-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, cultivating learning,<BR>engaged in study.<BR>—विद्यान्त (˚या-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>the end of knowledge.<BR>—विद्या-पति, इस्, m., N. of<BR>a poet; of the author of the Gaṅgā-vākyāvalī; of<BR>the author of the Varṣa-kṛtya.<BR>—विद्या-प्रदान,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the bestowing of knowledge,’ N. of a sec-<BR>tion of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—विद्या-प्राप्ति, इस्, f.<BR>acquirement of knowledge; any acquisition made by<BR>learning.<BR>—विद्या-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of learn-<BR>ing.<BR>—विद्याभिमान (˚या-अभ्˚), अम्, n. the fancy<BR>or idea that one possesses learning.<BR>—विद्याभिमान-<BR>वत् (˚या-अभ्˚), आन्, अती, अत्, fancying that one pos-<BR>sesses learning, imagining one's self learned.<BR>—विद्या-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">Page0919-b+ 78</a>]<BR>भ्यास (˚या-अभ्˚), अस्, m. practice or pursuit of<BR>learning, application to books, study.<BR>—विद्यारण्य<BR>(˚या-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a poet; of the author of<BR>the Vidyārtha-dīpikā.<BR>—विद्या-रत्न, अम्, n. the<BR>jewel of learning; valuable knowledge.<BR>—विद्या-<BR>रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work by<BR>Dhana-pati.<BR>—विद्यारम्भ (˚या-आर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘commencement of knowledge,’ N. of a section in<BR>the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—विद्यार्जन (˚या-अर्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the acquirement of knowledge; acquiring anything<BR>by knowledge or by teaching.<BR>—विद्यार्जित (˚या-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, acquired or gained by knowledge.<BR>—विद्यार्थ (˚या-अर्˚), अस्, m. the seeking for<BR>knowledge.<BR>—विद्यार्थ-दीपिका, f., N. of a work<BR>by Vidyāraṇya.<BR>—विद्यार्थ-प्रकाशिका, f., N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—विद्यार्थिन् (˚या-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, seeking<BR>for knowledge, studious; (ई), m. a student, pupil,<BR>scholar, disciple.<BR>—विद्यालङ्कार-भट्टाचार्य (˚या-<BR>अल्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author of annotations on<BR>Goyīcandra's commentary.<BR>—विद्या-लब्ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, acquired or gained by learning.<BR>—विद्यालय<BR>(˚या-आल्˚), अस्, m. abode or seat of learning, a school,<BR>college; N. of a place.<BR>—विद्या-लाभ, अस्, m.<BR>acquisition of learning; any acquirement gained by<BR>learning.<BR>—विद्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of<BR>learning or science, learned.<BR>—विद्या-वयो-वृद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, advanced in learning and years.<BR>—विद्या-<BR>विनोद, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—विद्या-विशिष्ट, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, distinguished by learning, possessed of science<BR>or scholarship.<BR>—विद्या-विहीन, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived<BR>of knowledge, misinstructed, ignorant.<BR>—विद्या-<BR>वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, old in knowledge, increased or<BR>advanced in learning.<BR>—विद्या-व्यवसाय, अस्, m.<BR>the pursuit of science.<BR>—विद्या-व्रत-स्नातक or<BR>विद्या-स्नातक, अस्, m. a Brāhman who has finished<BR>his period of studentship, (see स्नातक.)<BR>—विद्या-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of knowledge or learning,<BR>uninstructed, ignorant.<BR>—विद्योपार्जन (˚या-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n. acquisition of knowledge.<BR>—विद्योपार्जित<BR>(˚या-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, acquired by learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वस्
विद्वस्, वान्, उषी, वत्, one who knows, knowing,<BR>understanding (with acc., Ṛg-veda X. 8, 8; Kirāt.<BR>XI. 30), learned, (काल-व्˚, ‘learned in time,’ an<BR>almanac-maker); intelligent, wise; (वान्), m. a wise<BR>man, scholar, sage, seer.<BR>—विद्वज्-जन, अस्, m. a<BR>wise man, a sage, seer.<BR>—विद्वत्-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>a little learned, slightly learned.<BR>—विद्वत्-तम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, wisest, very wise.<BR>—विद्वत्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>wiser, very wise; [cf. विदुष्-टर.]<BR>—विद्वत्-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. scholarship, science, wisdom.<BR>—विद्वद्-दे-<BR>शीय or विद्वद्-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = विद्वत्-कल्प.<BR>—विद्वन्-मोद-तरङ्गिणी, f., N. of a philoso-<BR>phical work by Rāma-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्द|विन्दः
विन्द, विन्दमान, &c. See p. 925, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्न|विन्नः
विन्न, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. वित्त], known; discussed,<BR>judged; obtained, gained; married; placed, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविदिवस्
विविदिवस्, आन्, उषी, अत्, one who has known or<BR>obtained or found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविद्वस्
विविद्वस्, आन्, उषी, अत्, one who has known,<BR>knowing, wise; one who has obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद|वेदः
वेद, वेद्य, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदंश्
विदंश् वि-दंश्, cl. 1. P. -दशति, -दंष्टुम्,<BR>to bite into pieces, bite asunder, bite; to crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदंश|विदंशः
वि-दंश, अस्, m. any pungent food which excites<BR>thirst (= अव-दंश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदश्यमान
वि-दश्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being bitten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्ध|विदग्धः
विदग्ध वि-दग्ध. See under वि-दह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदय्
विदय् वि-दय्, cl. 1. A. -दयते, -दयितुम्,<BR>Ved. to divide asunder, separate; to dissipate, dispel,<BR>(Sāy. = वि-बाधते); to destroy, injure greatly; to<BR>consume, devour, (Sāy. = भक्षयति); to distri-<BR>bute, grant, bestow, (Sāy. = विशेषेण ददाति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदयमान
वि-दयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, dividing; dissipating;<BR>destroying; distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर|विदरं|विदरः
विदर वि-दर. See under वि-दॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भ|विदर्भः
विदर्भ वि-दर्भ, अस्, आ, m. f. (said to be<BR>fr. वि, ‘without,’ + दर्भ, ‘sacred grass,’ supposed<BR>not to grow in Vidarbha because the son of a saint<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">Page0919-c+ 77</a>]<BR>died of a wound inflicted by a sharp blade of this<BR>grass), a district and city to the south-west of Bengal,<BR>the modern Berar proper; (अस्), m. the king of<BR>Vidarbha; any dry or desert soil; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people.<BR>—विदर्भ-जा, f. ‘Vidarbha-born,’ epi-<BR>thet of the wife of the saint Agastya; of Damayantī<BR>(wife of Nala and heroine of the poem so called);<BR>of Rukmiṇī (wife of Kṛṣṇa).<BR>—विदर्भ-तनया<BR>or विदर्भ-राज-तनया or विदर्भ-सुभ्रू, ऊस्,<BR>f. ‘daughter of the king of Vidarbha,’ Damayantī.<BR>—विदर्भ-नगरी, f. the city of Vidarbha.<BR>—वि-<BR>दर्भ-पति, इस्, or विदर्भ-राज्, ट्, or विदर्भ-<BR>राज, अस्, or विदर्भ-राजन्, आ, or विदर्भाधि-<BR>पति (˚भ-अध्˚), इस्, m. the king of Vidarbha.<BR>—विदर्भ-राजधानी, f. the city or capital of<BR>Vidarbha.<BR>—विदर्भाभिमुख (˚भ-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having the face turned towards Vidarbha,<BR>facing Vidarbha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्शिन्
विदर्शिन् वि-दर्शिन्. See under वि-दृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल्
विदल् वि-दल्, cl. 1. P. -दलति, -दलितुम्,<BR>to break or burst asunder, burst or break to pieces;<BR>to be rent or split; to open, expand, blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल|विदलं|विदलः
1. वि-दल, अस्, आ, अम्, rent asunder, split; opened,<BR>expanded, blown (as a flower &c.); (अस्), m. rend-<BR>ing, dividing, separating; a cake; mountain ebony,<BR>Bauhinia Variegata; (आ), f. a plant, = त्रिवृत्; (अम्),<BR>n. a shallow basket made of split bamboos or any<BR>vessel of wicker-work; split peas; pomegranate bark;<BR>the cuttings or chips of any substance, anything pared<BR>or split; a twig.<BR>—विदली-करण, अम्, n. the act<BR>of rending asunder, dividing, &c.<BR>—विदली-कृ, cl.<BR>8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to rend asunder,<BR>tear, split, divide.<BR>—विदली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, rent<BR>asunder, split, torn, broken; cut, divided, separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलन|विदलनं
वि-दलन, अम्, n. the act of tearing or rending<BR>asunder, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलित
वि-दलित, अस्, आ, अम्, burst asunder, rent, torn,<BR>split; crushed; blown, expanded (as a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल|विदलं|विदलः
विदल 2. वि-दल, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>leaves, leafless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदस्
विदस् वि-दस्, cl. 4. P. -दस्यति, -दसितुम्,<BR>Ved. to waste away, become exhausted, fail, be want-<BR>ing, wither away, come to an end, (Sāy. = उप-<BR>क्षीयते, वि-शुष्यति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदस्त
वि-दस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, wasted away, exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदह्
विदह् वि-दह्, cl. 1. P. -दहति, -दग्धुम्,<BR>to burn out, cauterize (a wound &c.); to burn, con-<BR>sume by fire, scorch, parch, shrivel up, destroy by fire:<BR>Pass. -दह्यते, to be burnt; to suffer from internal<BR>heat, burn, be inflamed; to be consumed by grief;<BR>to be puffed up, boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्ध|विदग्धः
1. वि-दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt, inflamed; con-<BR>sumed by fire or internal heat; cooked; digested;<BR>destroyed, decomposed, corrupt, spoiled, turned sour;<BR>clever, shrewd, well-bred, knowing, witty, sharp;<BR>subtle, cunning, crafty, sly, artful, intriguing; (अस्),<BR>m. a learned or clever man, a scholar, Paṇḍit; a<BR>libertine, intriguer; N. of a teacher of the school<BR>of the Vājasaneyins or White Yajur-veda; (आ), f. a<BR>sharp or knowing woman.<BR>—विदग्ध-ता, f. or<BR>विदग्ध-त्व, अम्, n. sharpness, shrewdness, clever-<BR>ness, wit; elegance.<BR>—विदग्ध-माधव, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a drama ascribed to Rūpa (containing seven<BR>acts and written A. D. 1549; it relates to the loves<BR>of Kṛṣṇa and Rādhā, and is in fact the Gīta-<BR>govinda dramatised).<BR>—विदग्ध-मुख-मण्ड-<BR>न, अम्, n., N. of a work by Dharma-dāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्ध|विदग्धः
2. वि-दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, unburnt, uncooked,<BR>undigested, ill-concocted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0919-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाह|विदाहः
