विदेशीय
विदेशीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a foreign<BR>country, foreign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेह|विदेहः
विदेह वि-देह, अस्, आ, अम्, without body, bodi-<BR>less, incorporeal; trunkless; (अस्), m. a sovereign of the<BR>family of Janaka, king of Mithilā; N. of the author<BR>of a work on medicine; (अस्, आ), m. f. a district in<BR>the province of Behar (ancient Mithilā or the modern<BR>Tirhut); (आस्), m. pl. the people of Videha.<BR>—वि-<BR>देह-मुक्ति, इस्, f. incorporeal deliverance.<BR>—विदेह-<BR>मुक्त्य्-आदि-कथन, अम्, n., N. of a short treatise<BR>on the duties and exercises of ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदो
विदो वि-दो (see 2. वि-दा), cl. 2. 4. P. -दाति,<BR>-द्यति, -दातुम्, to cut into pieces, cut up, crush;<BR>to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित्य
वि-दित्य, ind. (?), having cut up or destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्ध|विद्धः
विद्ध विद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. व्यध्, q. v.),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">Page0920-c+ 77</a>]<BR>pierced, perforated, penetrated, stabbed, wounded;<BR>beaten, lashed, whipped; thrown, cast, sent, directed;<BR>opposed, impeded; resembling, like; (अस्), m. the<BR>tree Echites Scholaris; (अम्), n. a wound.<BR>—विद्ध-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, having bored ears, having the ears<BR>pierced or slit; (अस्, आ or ई), m. f. a species of plant<BR>(= पाठा, q. v.).<BR>—विद्ध-कर्णिका, f. = विद्ध-<BR>कर्णी.<BR>—विद्ध-शाल-भञ्जिका, f., N. of a drama<BR>by Rāja-śekhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्मनापस्
विद्मनापस् विद्मनापस्. See p. 918, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यमान|विद्यमानः
विद्यमान विद्यमान. See p. 918, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्या
विद्या विद्या. See p. 919, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्
विद्युत् 1. वि-द्युत्, cl. 1. A. -द्योतते (ep. also<BR>P. -द्योतति; Perf. -दिद्युते), -द्योतितुम्, to shine<BR>forth, radiate, flash, be brilliant or radiant, sparkle;<BR>to light, lighten; to illuminate: Caus. -द्योतयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to illuminate, irradiate, enlighten, make<BR>brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदविद्युतत्
वि-दविद्युतत्, अत्, अती, अत् (Intens. part. Ved.),<BR>shining brightly, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्
2. वि-द्युत्, त्, f. lightning; a thunderbolt (a<BR>weapon of the Maruts); a species of the Atijagatī<BR>metre; (त्), m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—विद्युज्-जिह्व, अस्,<BR>m. ‘lightning-tongued,’ a kind of Rākṣasa.<BR>—वि-<BR>द्युज्-ज्वाला, f. the flashing of lightning; N. of a<BR>particular plant (= कलि-कारी).<BR>—विद्युत्-केश, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Rākṣasa (son of Heti and father of<BR>Su-keśa).<BR>—विद्युत्-केशिन्, ई, m., N. of a king of the<BR>Rākṣasas.<BR>—विद्युत्-पताक, अस्, m. ‘having light-<BR>ning for its banner,’ epithet of one of the seven kinds<BR>of cloud at the destruction of the world; [cf. वला-<BR>हक.]<BR>—विद्युत्-पात, अस्, m. the falling or darting<BR>of lightning, a stroke of lightning.<BR>—विद्युत्-प्रभ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the splendor of lightning, flashing<BR>like lightning.<BR>—विद्युत्-प्रिय, अम्, n. ‘lightning-<BR>loved,’ bell-metal.<BR>—विद्युत्-वत् or विद्युन्-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having or containing lightning, electrical (a<BR>cloud &c.).<BR>—विद्युद्-उन्मेष, अस्, m. a flash of<BR>lightning.<BR>—विद्युद्-दामन्, अ, n. ‘a garland or<BR>mass of lightning,’ a flash or streak of zigzag light-<BR>ning.<BR>—विद्युद्-द्योत, अस्, m. the brightness or<BR>brilliance of lightning.<BR>—विद्युद्-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having lightning for a vehicle (said of the<BR>Maruts).<BR>—विद्युन्-महस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. brilliant<BR>or radiant with lightning (said of the Maruts; Sāy.<BR>= विद्योतमान-तेजस्).<BR>—विद्युन्-माला, f. ‘gar-<BR>land of lightning,’ N. of a metre in Sanskrit prosody.<BR>—विद्युन्-मालिन्, ई, m. ‘garlanded with lightning,’<BR>N. of an Asura.<BR>—विद्युल्-लता, f. ‘lightning-creeper,’<BR>forked or zigzag lightning.<BR>—विद्युल्-लेखा, f. a streak<BR>of lightning, flash of lightning, forked lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्
3. वि-द्युत्, त्, त्, त्, devoid of splendor, lustreless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युतय
विद्युतय, Nom. A. विद्युतयते, -यितुम्, Ved.<BR>to flash or gleam (like lightning), be radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योतन
वि-द्योतन, अस्, ई, अम्, irradiating, illuminating,<BR>enlightening; illustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योतमान
वि-द्योतमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, blazing,<BR>flashing, lightening, (विद्योतमाने, ind. when the<BR>lightning flashes, when it lightens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्र|विद्रं|विद्रः
विद्र विद्र, अम्, n. (probably fr. वि-दॄ or<BR>connected with rt. व्यध्), tearing, splitting, pierc-<BR>ing, perforating; a fissure, hole, chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रध
विद्रध, अस्, आ, अम् (probably connected with<BR>rt. व्यध्), Ved. divided, (according to Yāska =<BR>विद्ध, according to Durga = विकुषिताधोभाग;<BR>see Nirukta IV. 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रधि|विद्रधिः
विद्रधि, इस्, m. an abscess (especially when deep-<BR>seated or internal).<BR>—विद्रधि-नाशन, अस्, m.<BR>‘abscess-destroyer,’ the tree Hyperanthera Morunga<BR>(= शोभाञ्जन, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रा
विद्रा वि-द्रा or वि-द्रै, cl. 2. 1. (or 4.) P.<BR>-द्राति, -द्रायति, -द्रातुम्, (probably) to awake out<BR>of sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्राण
वि-द्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, awakened out of sleep,<BR>awaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रु
विद्रु वि-द्रु, cl. 1. P. -द्रवति, -द्रोतुम्,<BR>to run in different directions, disperse, escape; to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">Page0921-a+ 77</a>]<BR>part asunder, become divided, burst asunder; to flow<BR>asunder, melt, become melted, liquefy: Caus. -द्रा-<BR>वयति, -यितुम्, to cause to disperse, drive away,<BR>put to flight, frighten away, scare, chase away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0920-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रव|विद्रवः
वि-द्रव, अस्, m. running in different directions,<BR>running away, flight, panic, agitation; retreat, escape;<BR>flowing out, oozing; flowing asunder, melting, lique-<BR>faction; censure, abuse, reproach; intellect, under-<BR>standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्राव|विद्रावः
वि-द्राव, अस्, m. running away, flight, panic,<BR>retreat; liquefaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावक
वि-द्रावक, अस्, इका, अम्, driving away; causing<BR>to flow or melt, liquefying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावण|विद्रावणं
वि-द्रावण, अम्, n. the act of driving away,<BR>chasing, defeating; causing to flow or melt, lique-<BR>fying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावित|विद्रावितं
वि-द्रावित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to disperse, driven<BR>away, put to flight; liquefied, fused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुत|विद्रुतः
वि-द्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, flown, fled; running hither<BR>and thither, going fast; agitated, alarmed; liquefied,<BR>liquid, fluid (as an oily or metallic substance when<BR>heated).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुम|विद्रुमः
विद्रुम वि-द्रुम, अस्, m. a tree bearing<BR>precious gems; coral; a young sprout or shoot.<BR>—विद्रुम-तट, अस्, आ, अम्, having banks of coral.<BR>—विद्रुम-देहली, f. a threshold of coral.<BR>—वि-<BR>द्रुम-लता, f. a branch of coral; a sort of vegetable<BR>perfume.<BR>—विद्रुम-लतिका, f. a kind of perfume<BR>(= नलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रै
विद्रै वि-द्रै (see वि-द्रा), cl. 1. P. -द्रा-<BR>यति, -द्रातुम्, to awake from one's sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वस्
विद्वस् विद्वस्, विद्वत्-त्व, &c. See p. 919.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्
विद्विष् 1. वि-द्विष्, cl. 2. P. A. -द्वेष्टि,<BR>-द्विष्टे, -द्वेष्टुम्, to dislike, hate, be hostile to;<BR>(A.) to hate each other mutually, dislike one another:<BR>Caus. -द्वेषयति, -यितुम्, to cause to dislike or<BR>hate, make hostile, render an enemy, make hostile<BR>towards one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्
2. वि-द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, hostile, inimical; an enemy,<BR>foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष|विद्विषः
वि-द्विष, अस्, आ, अम्, hating, inimical, adverse;<BR>(अस्), m. an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विषत्|विद्विषन्त्
वि-द्विषत्, अन्, अती, अत्, hating, hostile; an enemy,<BR>foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्ट
वि-द्विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, hated, disliked, odious.<BR>—विद्विष्ट-ता, f. hatred, dislike, hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेष|विद्वेषः
वि-द्वेष, अस्, m. enmity, hatred, contempt.<BR>—वि-<BR>द्वेष-वीर, अस्, m., N. of a chief of the Śaivas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषक|विद्वेषकः
वि-द्वेषक, अस्, इका, अम्, hating, hostile; a<BR>hater, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषण|विद्वेषणं|विद्वेषणः
वि-द्वेषण, अस्, m. one who hates, a hater; (ई),<BR>f. a woman of a resentful disposition; (अम्), n. caus-<BR>ing abhorrence, hatred, enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषिन्
वि-द्वेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, hating, hostile, inimical;<BR>(ई), m. an enemy.<BR>—विद्वेषि-प्रभव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>proceeding from an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेष्टृ
वि-द्वेष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, one who hates, an enemy;<BR>hating, hostile, inimical, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्
विध् 1. विध् (= rt. विथ्), cl. 1. A. वे-<BR>धते, वेधितुम्, to ask, beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्
विध् 2. विध् (thought by some to have<BR>been developed out of वि-धा and rt.<BR>व्यध्), cl. 6. P. विधति, विवेध, वेधिष्यति,<BR>अवेधीत्, वेधितुम्, to dispose (Ved.); to perform<BR>(Ved.); to administer, govern, rule, command; to wor-<BR>ship, honour, sacrifice; to pierce, (in this sense for rt.<BR>व्यध्): Caus. वेधयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अवीविधत्:<BR>Desid. विविधिषति and विवेधिषति: Intens. वे-<BR>विध्यते, वेविधीति, वेवेद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध|विधः
1. विध, अस्, आ, m. f. (more properly fr. rt. व्यध्),<BR>piercing, penetrating, penetration. (For 2. वि-ध<BR>see under वि-धा, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधत्
विधत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, Ved. worshipping,<BR>honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधन
विधन वि-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of<BR>wealth, having no riches, poor.<BR>—विधन-ता, f.<BR>destitution, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधर्तृ
विधर्तृ वि-धर्तृ, वि-धर्मन्, &c. See<BR>under वि-धृ, p. 922, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवन|विधवनं
विधवन वि-धवन, &c. See p. 922, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवा
विधवा वि-धवा, f. (see 2. धव), a hus-<BR>bandless woman, a widow; [cf. Lat. vidua, vi-<BR>duus; Goth. viduvo; Angl. Sax. wuduwe, wu-<BR>duwa; Slav. vidova; Hib. feadhb; perhaps Gr.<BR>ἠΐθεος.]<BR>—विधवा-गामिन्, ई, m. one who has in-<BR>tercourse with a widow.<BR>—विधवा-धर्म, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the duty of widows,’ N. of a section of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—विधवावेदन (˚वा-आव्˚), अम्,<BR>n. marrying a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधा
विधा वि-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति, -धत्ते,<BR>-धातुम्, to distribute, apportion, bestow, grant; to<BR>procure, furnish; to give out, diffuse; to extend (Ved.);<BR>to put in order, arrange, regulate, dispose, make ready,<BR>prepare, attend to; to prescribe, ordain, direct, enjoin,<BR>settle, fix; to appoint, commission, depute; to place<BR>on, put on or in, put down, lay down, lay aside; to<BR>place, put, lay (in general); to hold, possess, assume,<BR>take; to form, build, create; to perform, effect,<BR>accomplish, produce, establish, cause, occasion, render,<BR>make, do, act, act towards, treat as, (these senses<BR>may be almost endlessly modified by using वि-धा,<BR>like कृ, in connection with various nouns, e. g. सिं-<BR>हत्वं विधा, to change into a lion; कामं वि-<BR>धा, to fulfil a wish; वृत्तिं विधा, to fix a liveli-<BR>hood or maintenance; हृदये विधा, to lay to<BR>heart; शस्त्राणि विधा, to lay down arms; मन्त्रं<BR>विधा, to hold a consultation; राज्यं विधा, to<BR>carry on a government, rule; पूजां विधा, to do<BR>honour to, show respect to, worship; शौचं विधा,<BR>to perform purification; लज्जां विधा, to display<BR>bashfulness; मैत्र्यं विधा, to make friendship;<BR>सन्धिं विधा, to conclude peace; कलहं विधा,<BR>to pick a quarrel; वैरं विधा, to declare war; को-<BR>लाहलं विधा, to raise a clamour; तं नृपं<BR>विदधुः, they made him king): Pass. -धीयते,<BR>to be distributed or apportioned; to be arranged or<BR>attended to; to be prescribed or settled, &c.; to<BR>be taken or reckoned for, &c.: Caus. -धापयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to put in order or arrange or fix;<BR>to cause to put, cause to be laid: Desid. -धित्सति,<BR>-ते, to wish to distribute or bestow, to wish to arrange,<BR>try to fix; to wish or intend to do or perform or<BR>accomplish or effect; to wish to render, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदधत्
वि-दधत्, अत्, अती, अत्, distributing, granting, pro-<BR>curing, arranging, prescribing, fixing, performing, &c.;<BR>holding, having, assuming, wearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध|विधः
2. वि-ध, अस्, m. form, manner, measure, kind, sort<BR>(often at the end of comps., see एवं-व्˚, तथा-व्˚,<BR>द्वि-व्˚, बहु-व्˚, &c.); fold (at the end of comps.,<BR>especially after numerals, see अष्ट-व्˚, सप्त-व्˚);<BR>the food of elephants; prosperity; (आ), f. form,<BR>formula, rule; manner, kind, sort; act, action; doing<BR>well, prosperity, affluence; wages, hire; fodder, the<BR>food of elephants, horses, &c.; [cf. Old Pruss. wida-s,<BR>wid-s, sta-wida-s, sta-wids, ‘of such sort;’ ka-<BR>wid-s (fem. ka-wida), ‘of which kind;’ kitta-<BR>widin, kitte-widei, ‘in any way.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधस्
वि-धस्, आस्, m., N. of Brahmā; [cf. वेधस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातव्य
वि-धातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be done according to<BR>rule, to be observed (as a rite or ceremony); to be<BR>prescribed or regulated; to be done or performed or<BR>effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृ
वि-धातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, arranging, disposing, mak-<BR>ing, creating; = मेधाविन् (according to Naigh. III.<BR>15); (ता), m. an arranger, disposer, maker, creator;<BR>N. of Brahmā (as creator of the world); N. of Viśva-<BR>karman; fate, destiny; N. of Kāma (god of love);<BR>of a son of Bhṛgu; of a son of Viṣṇu and Lakṣmī;<BR>spirituous liquor; (त्री), f. long pepper.<BR>—विधातृ-<BR>भू, ऊस्, m. ‘son of Brahmā,’ epithet of Nārada,<BR>(see नारद.)<BR>—विधातृ-वशात्, ind. from the will<BR>of Brahmā; through the power of fate or destiny.<BR>—विधात्रायुस् (˚तृ-आय्˚), उस्, m. the sunflower;<BR>sunshine, (according to Śabda-k. = सूर्य-शोभा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधान|विधानं
वि-धान, अम्, n. the act of arranging, disposing,<BR>prescribing, enjoining, ordering, performing, making;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-c" target="_blank">Page0921-c+ 81</a>]<BR>arrangement, disposition, creation; act, action, (espe-<BR>cially) the performance of prescribed acts or rites; rule,<BR>precept, ordinance, injunction, regulation, sacred text;<BR>act of worship, rite, ceremony; form, formula, mode,<BR>method, manner, (तथा-व्˚, following such a mode<BR>or method); means, expedient; gaining, obtaining,<BR>taking, possessing; wealth; act of hostility; conflict<BR>of opposite feelings; an elephant's fodder; (in gram-<BR>mar) affixing, prefixing, taking as an affix, &c.; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), acting, performing, possessing, assuming,<BR>wearing, having.<BR>—विधान-ग, अस्, m. ‘rule-goer,’<BR>a Paṇḍit, a wise or learned man, teacher.<BR>—विधान-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, m. one who knows rules or rites, a Paṇḍit,<BR>wise man.<BR>—विधान-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, agreeable<BR>to rule, conformable to sacred precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानक|विधानकं
वि-धानक, अस्, आ, अम्, disposing, arranging,<BR>one who knows how to arrange; (अम्), n. affliction,<BR>distress, pain (= व्यथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाय
वि-धाय, ind. having disposed or arranged, having<BR>placed or put on; having taken or assumed, &c.;<BR>having formed or created; having rendered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायक|विधायकः
वि-धायक, अस्, इका, अम्, disposing, arranging,<BR>performing; consigning, delivering, one who entrusts<BR>or deposits anything or causes it to be fixed or secure.<BR>—विधायक-त्व, अम्, n. consignment or delivery<BR>of anything, making anything firm or secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायिन्
वि-धायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, disposing, arranging; mak-<BR>ing, forming, building; causing, occasioning; placing,<BR>fixing, securing; delivering, entrusting; establishing<BR>a rule or law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधास्यत्
वि-धास्यत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, wishing or pur-<BR>posing to arrange; intending to direct or enjoin or<BR>prescribe, wishing to make or do or perform, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधि|विधिः
वि-धि, इस्, m. a rule, form, formula, sacred pre-<BR>cept, injunction, rubric, sacred text or scripture, text<BR>prescribing any act or observance, order, command,<BR>ordinance, statute, law, direction for the performance<BR>of a rite as given in the Brāhmaṇa portion of the<BR>Veda, (according to Sāy. the Brāhmaṇa consists of<BR>two parts, 1. Vidhi or commandment, e. g. यजेत,<BR>he ought to sacrifice; कुर्यात्, he ought to perform;<BR>2. Artha-vāda or explanatory statements as to the<BR>origin of rites and use of the Mantras, mixed up with<BR>legends and illustrations), any prescribed act or rite or<BR>ceremony, an act or action in general, behaviour, con-<BR>duct, mode of life, method, manner, way, means;<BR>kind, sort; creation; the creator; N. of Brahmā;<BR>of Viṣṇu; fate, destiny, luck; time; fodder, food<BR>for elephants or horses; a physician; (इस्), f., N. of<BR>a goddess.<BR>—विधि-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘rule-destroy-<BR>ing,’ one who deviates from or disregards rules, dis-<BR>turbing modes of proceeding.<BR>—विधि-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘rule-knowing,’ one who knows the prescribed<BR>mode or form; learned in ritual; (अस्), m. a Brāhman<BR>who knows the ritual, a ritualist.<BR>—विधि-तस्, ind.<BR>according to rule.<BR>—विधि-दर्शक, अस्, or विधि-<BR>दर्शिन्, ई, m. ‘rule-shower,’ a priest whose business<BR>is to see that everything at a sacrifice is done accord-<BR>ing to prescribed rules and to correct any deviation<BR>from them.<BR>—विधि-दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, prescribed<BR>or approved by rule.<BR>—विधि-देशक, अस्, m. ‘rule-<BR>shower,’ a priest who corrects errors at a sacrifice.<BR>—वि-<BR>धि-द्वैध, अम्, n. diversity of rule, variance of rite.<BR>—विधि-पर्यागत, अस्, आ, अम्, come into possession<BR>through destiny.<BR>—विधि-पूर्वकम्, ind. after due<BR>observance of rule, according to rule.<BR>—विधि-प्र-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, performed according to rule.<BR>—विधि-प्रयोग, अस्, m. the application of a rule,<BR>acting according to rule.<BR>—विधि-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>application of a rule, acting upon a rule.<BR>—विधि-<BR>यज्ञ, अस्, m. a ceremonial act of worship.<BR>—विधि-<BR>योग, अस्, m. the occurrence of fated or predestined<BR>events; combining for any act or rite.<BR>—विधि-र-<BR>सायन, N. of a work by Appayya Dīkṣita (con-<BR>futing the Mīmāṃsā as expounded by Bhaṭṭa Kumā-<BR>rila).<BR>—विधि-वत्, ind. agreeably to rule, according to<BR>law, in due form, conformably to established ordinances.<BR>—विधि-वधू, ऊस्, f. ‘wife of Brahmā,’ epithet of<BR>Sarasvatī.<BR>—विधि-विहित, अस्, आ, अम्, established by<BR>rule, prescribed by law.<BR>—विधि-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>destitute of rule, unauthorised, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0921-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सत्
वि-धित्सत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, = वि-धित्समान below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्समान
वि-धित्समान, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to bestow;<BR>desiring to fix or place; wishing to perform; having<BR>certain intentions, following certain aims.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सा
वि-धित्सा, f. the wish to arrange; desire to do or<BR>make; design, purpose, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सित
वि-धित्सित, अम्, n. design, purpose, intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सु
वि-धित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to arrange; intending<BR>to make; purposing to perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधीयमान
वि-धीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being arranged, being<BR>enjoined, being defined, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेय|विधेयः
वि-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be arranged or prescribed;<BR>to be enjoined (as a rule &c.); to be performed or<BR>practised or done; liable to be ruled or governed or<BR>influenced by, governable, subject to; compliant, sub-<BR>missive, tractable.<BR>—विधेय-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing<BR>what ought to be done.<BR>—विधेय-ता, f. or विधेय-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. fitness to be prescribed or enjoined; fitness<BR>for enactment (as a rule or law), necessary or proper<BR>act or conduct; tractableness, docility, submission.<BR>—विधेय-पद, अम्, n. an object to be accom-<BR>plished.<BR>—विधेय-मार्ग, अस्, m. the seeking to<BR>do a necessary act.<BR>—विधेयात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, m.<BR>‘having a well-governed nature,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित|विहितः
वि-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, arranged, settled, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाव्
विधाव् 1. वि-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति,<BR>-ते, -धावितुम्, to run or flow through, flow off (as<BR>water), to percolate or trickle through, flow away; to<BR>run or flee away (in disorder), be dispersed; to run<BR>through; to rush upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधावत्
वि-धावत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, running away, running<BR>through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाव्
विधाव् 2. वि-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति,<BR>-ते, -धावितुम्, to wash off, wash away, cleanse off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधौत
वि-धौत, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed by washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधु|विधुः
विधु 1. विधु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 24. fr. rt. व्यध्, ‘to pierce,’ because the moon<BR>pierces the absent with sorrowful feelings; more pro-<BR>bably connected with rt. 2. विध् or with वि-धा), one<BR>who arranges or disposes or rules or maintains (Ved.);<BR>the moon; N. of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu; a Rākṣasa,<BR>fiend; an expiatory oblation; camphor.<BR>—विधु-<BR>क्षय, अस्, m. the wane of the moon, the dark<BR>days of the month.<BR>—विधुन्-तुद, अस्, m. ‘moon-<BR>troubler,’ epithet of Rāhu or the personified ascend-<BR>ing Node (causing the moon's eclipses).<BR>—विधु-<BR>पञ्जर, अस्, m. a scimitar, sabre.<BR>—विधु-प्रिया,<BR>f. ‘dear to the moon,’ a lunar mansion or Nakṣatra<BR>(personified as a nymph, the daughter of Dakṣa and<BR>wife of the Moon, see नक्षत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुर|विधुरं|विधुरः
विधुर, अस्, आ, अम् (probably fr. rt. व्यध्, cf. वि-<BR>थुर), agitated, troubled, distressed, bewildered, con-<BR>fused (with fear, liquor, &c.), trembling; suffering se-<BR>paration or absence from a mistress or lover, being in<BR>a state of bereavement, abandoned; adverse, hostile;<BR>(अस्), m. a widower; (अम्), n. agitation of mind,<BR>anxiety, alarm, terror; danger; separation from a<BR>mistress or lover; (आ), f. curds mixed with sugar<BR>and spices.<BR>—विधुर-ता, f. a state of agitation or<BR>trouble of mind, state of trepidation or alarm.<BR>—वि-<BR>धुर-दर्शन, अम्, n. the sight of anything alarm-<BR>ing; a feeling of agitation or uneasiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधु|विधुः
विधु 2. वि-धु = वि-धू below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधू
विधू वि-धू, cl. 5. P. A. -धूनोति, -धूनुते<BR>(later also -धुनोति, -धुनुते), cl. 6. P. -धुवति,<BR>-धवितुम्, -धोतुम्, to shake about, move to and fro,<BR>agitate, excite, wave about, toss about; to shake off,<BR>drive away, disperse, remove, destroy; to shake off<BR>from one's self, relinquish, abandon, leave off (A.);<BR>to fan, agitate by blowing: Pass. -धूयते, to be<BR>shaken about, to be waved about, to be fanned, &c.:<BR>Caus. -धूनयति, -यितुम्, to cause to shake about,<BR>shake violently, agitate, cause to stagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवन|विधवनं
वि-धवन, अम्, n. the act of shaking about,<BR>agitation, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधव्य|विधव्यं
वि-धव्य, अम्, n. agitation, trembling, tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाव्य|विधाव्यं
वि-धाव्य, अम्, n. agitation, shaking about, tre-<BR>pidation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुत|विधुतः
वि-धुत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken about; shaken off,<BR>driven away; abandoned, relinquished, left off.<BR>—वि-<BR>धुत-बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, released from bonds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुति|विधुतिः
वि-धुति, इस्, f. shaking, trembling, trepidation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुनन|विधुननं
वि-धुनन, अम्, n. the act of shaking or tossing<BR>about, trembling, tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुन्वत्
वि-धुन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, shaking, tossing about,<BR>waving about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुन्वान
वि-धुन्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking about, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुवत्
वि-धुवत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, shaking or waving<BR>about, brandishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुवन|विधुवनं
वि-धुवन, अम्, n. trembling, tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूत|विधूतं
वि-धूत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken or tossed about,<BR>waved, waving; trembling, tremulous; unsteady;<BR>shaken off, dispelled, removed; abandoned; (अम्),<BR>n. the repelling of affection, repugnance.<BR>—विधूत-<BR>कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, having sin dispelled or re-<BR>moved, delivered from sin.<BR>—विधूत-केश, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, who or what has tossed about the hair (Kirāt.<BR>VIII. 33).<BR>—विधूत-निद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, roused<BR>from sleep, awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूति|विधूतिः
वि-धूति, इस्, f. agitation, tremor; shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनन|विधूननं
वि-धूनन, अम्, n. causing to shake or tremble,<BR>shaking, trembling, tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनयत्
वि-धूनयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, violently shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनित|विधूनितं
वि-धूनित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken about, tossed<BR>about, agitated, alarmed; harassed, annoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूय
वि-धूय, ind. having shaken about, having<BR>shaken off, having removed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूयत्
वि-धूयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being shaken, being<BR>agitated or waved about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूयमान
वि-धूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being shaken, being<BR>agitated, being waved about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूम
विधूम वि-धूम, अस्, आ, अम्, smokeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृ
विधृ वि-धृ, cl. 10. P. -धारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to keep asunder, keep apart, separate, divide, distri-<BR>bute; to arrange; to manage; to keep off; to lay hold<BR>of, seize; to keep back, withhold, restrain, obstruct;<BR>to hold up, bear, carry, support, maintain, sustain,<BR>preserve, take care of; to keep fixed, (with मनस्,<BR>to fix the mind upon.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधर्तृ
वि-धर्तृ, ता, m., Ved. one who supports, a sup-<BR>porter, bearer, sustainer (= विधारयितृ, Nirukta<BR>XII. 14); the performer of various functions, (Sāy.<BR>= विविध-कारक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधर्मन्
वि-धर्मन्, अ, n., Ved. the function of support-<BR>ing (the universe); various function or office; bear-<BR>ing, supporting; epithet of the sky (as the bearer of<BR>light and rain); epithet of the vessel used in the pre-<BR>paration of the Soma juice; order, rule, right, might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधार
वि-धार, अस्, m., Ved. bearing, supporting; epi-<BR>thet of the sky (as the bearer of rain and light).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृत|विधृतं
वि-धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, kept asunder or apart,<BR>separated; seized, grasped, held; taken, assumed,<BR>possessed; withheld, restrained, (अ-विधृत, unre-<BR>strained, unchecked); (अम्), n. disregard of an<BR>injunction or wish; dissatisfaction.<BR>—विधृतायुध<BR>(˚त-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, holding weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृति|विधृतिः
वि-धृति, इस्, f. arrangement, rule, regulation,<BR>ordinance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृष्
विधृष् वि-धृष्, Caus. -धर्षयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to violate, ravish; to spoil, injure; to annoy,<BR>trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्मा
विध्मा वि-ध्मा, cl. 1. P. -धमति, -ध्मा-<BR>तुम्, to blow away, blow off; to scatter, disperse,<BR>destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यत्|विध्यन्त्
विध्यत् विध्यत्, &c. See under rt. व्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंस्
विध्वंस् वि-ध्वंस् or वि-ध्वस्, cl. 1. A.<BR>-ध्वंसते (ep. also P. -ति), -ध्वंसितुम्, to fall<BR>to pieces, crumble into dust or powder; to be scat-<BR>tered or whirled about (like dust), be dispersed; to<BR>be destroyed, perish: Caus. -ध्वंसयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to fall to pieces or crumble, dash to pieces,<BR>crush, destroy, annihilate; to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंस|विध्वंसः
वि-ध्वंस, अस्, m. falling to pieces, ruin, de-<BR>struction; aversion, disrespect, enmity, dislike; in-<BR>sult, offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसमान
वि-ध्वंसमान, अस्, आ, अम्, falling or crumbling<BR>to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसित
वि-ध्वंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, dashed or broken to<BR>pieces, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसिन्
वि-ध्वंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling to pieces, falling<BR>asunder, being scattered or dispersed, falling down,<BR>being ruined, perishing; causing to fall, ruining,<BR>destroying; hostile, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वस्त
वि-ध्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen asunder, fallen to<BR>pieces, destroyed, ruined, scattered about or tossed<BR>up, whirled up (as dust); obscured, darkened, oblite-<BR>rated, eclipsed (in astronomy).<BR>—विध्वस्त-नग-<BR>राश्रम (˚र-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having ruined cities<BR>and hermitages.<BR>—विध्वस्त-पर-गुण, अस्, m.<BR>one who detracts from the merits of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनङ्गृस|विनंगृस
विनङ्गृस विनङ्-गृस, अस्, m., Ved. accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IX. 72, 3 = कमनीयं<BR>स्तोत्रं गृह्णाति यः; (औ), m. du. the two arms<BR>(according to Naigh. II. 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद्
विनद् वि-नद्, cl. 1. P. -नदति, -नदितुम्,<BR>to sound forth, cry out, scream out, roar, bellow; to<BR>thunder (as clouds); to roar or scream at (with acc.);<BR>to fill with cries: Caus. -नादयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to sound or resound, cause to make a noise; to fill<BR>with noise or cries; to sound aloud: Pass. of Caus.<BR>-नाद्यते, to be made to sound, be made to cry, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद|विनदः
वि-नद, अस्, m. sound, noise; a kind of tree,<BR>Echites Scholaris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनदत्
वि-नदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shouting, bellowing, lowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनदिन्
वि-नदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, roaring, thundering, grumbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनदी
वि-नदी, f., N. of a river, (also read वैनदी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद्य
वि-नद्य, ind. having sounded, sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनादित
वि-नादित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to resound, caused to<BR>sound aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनादिन्
वि-नादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding forth, crying out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाद्यमान
वि-नाद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being made to sound<BR>or cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनन्द्
विनन्द् वि-नन्द्, cl. 1. P. A. -नन्दति, -ते,<BR>-नन्दितुम्, to rejoice, be glad or joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्
विनम् वि-नम्, cl. 1. P. A. -नमति, -ते,<BR>-नन्तुम्, to bend down, bow down, stoop: Caus.<BR>-नमयति, -नामयति, -यितुम्, to bend down, bend<BR>a bow; (in grammar) to cerebralize or change into<BR>a cerebral letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनत|विनतः
वि-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, bent down, bowed, stooping,<BR>inclined, sunk down, depressed, deepened; curved,<BR>crooked; humble, modest; depressed, dispirited; (in<BR>grammar) changed into a cerebral letter, see वि-<BR>नाम below; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Su-dyumna;<BR>(आ), f., N. of one of the wives of Kaśyapa and<BR>mother of Aruṇa and Garuḍa, (in Mahā-bh. Ādi-p.<BR>2520, Vinatā is enumerated among the thirteen<BR>daughters of Dakṣa; the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa makes<BR>her the wife of Tārkṣa; the Vāyu describes the<BR>metres of the Veda as her daughters, while the Padma<BR>gives her only one daughter, Saudāminī); a sort of<BR>basket.<BR>—विनत-काय, अस्, आ, अम्, having the body<BR>bent, stooping.<BR>—विनतानन (˚त-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the face bent or cast down, dejected, dispirited.<BR>—विनता-सूनु, उस्, m. epithet of Aruṇa (charioteer<BR>of the Sun); of Garuḍa (younger brother of Aruṇa).<BR>—विनतोदर (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, with bending<BR>waist, bending at the waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनति|विनतिः
वि-नति, इस्, f. bowing down, bending; humility,<BR>modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमन|विनमनं
वि-नमन, अम्, n. the act of bending down,<BR>bowing, bending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमित
वि-नमित, अस्, आ, अम्, bowed down, inclined,<BR>declined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्र
वि-नम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, bent down, bowed; de-<BR>pressed; humble, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्रक|विनम्रकं
विनम्रक, अम्, n. the flower of the plant Ta-<BR>gara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाम|विनामः
वि-नाम, अस्, m. (in grammar) conversion into a<BR>cerebral letter, the substitution of ष् for स् and ण्<BR>for न्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाम्य
वि-नाम्य, ind. (fr. the Caus.), having bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनय|विनयः
विनय वि-नय. See under वि-नी, p. 925.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0922-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनर्द्
विनर्द् वि-नर्द्, cl. 1. P. A. -नर्दति, -ते,<BR>-नर्दितुम्, to cry out, roar out, make a loud sound,<BR>thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनर्दत्|विनर्द्दत्
वि-नर्दत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, crying out, making a<BR>loud noise, sounding forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनर्दमान
वि-नर्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding loudly,<BR>thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्
विनश् वि-नश्, cl. 1. 4. P. -नशति, -नश्यति,<BR>-नशितुम्, -नंष्टुम्, to be completely lost or<BR>ruined; to be destroyed, perish; to disappear, vanish;<BR>to come to nothing, be frustrated: Caus. -नाशयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to be lost or ruined, destroy, anni-<BR>hilate; to cause to disappear or vanish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनशन|विनशनं|विनशनः
वि-नशन, अम्, n. perishing, loss, disappearance;<BR>destruction; N. of the place where the river Sa-<BR>rasvatī is lost in the sand; a country in the north-<BR>west of Delhi (said to be the same as Kuru-kṣetra<BR>or the country adjacent to the modern Paniput; see<BR>Manu II. 21).<BR>—विनशन-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. the<BR>district of Vinaśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्यत्
वि-नश्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being lost or ruined,<BR>perishing, decaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्वर
वि-नश्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, liable to be destroyed,<BR>perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्ट|विनष्टः
वि-नष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, utterly lost or ruined, dis-<BR>appeared, perished; destroyed; spoilt, corrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्टि|विनष्टिः
वि-नष्टि, इस्, f. utter loss or destruction, ruin,<BR>disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाश|विनाशः
वि-नाश, अस्, m. utter loss, annihilation, perdition,<BR>ruin, destruction, decay, death; removal.<BR>—विनाश-<BR>धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, or विनाश-धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>subject to the law of decay.<BR>—विनाश-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, m. a source of destruction, cause of subsequent<BR>non-existence of a composite body (अवयविन्).<BR>—विनाशोन्मुख (˚श-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, about to<BR>perish, verging on decay, full ripe or mature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशक|विनाशकः
वि-नाशक, अस्, इका, अम्, annihilating, destroying;<BR>a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशन|विनाशनं|विनाशनः
वि-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying, destructive,<BR>ruinous; (अस्), m. one who destroys, a destroyer;<BR>(अम्), n. destruction, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशयत्
वि-नाशयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, destroying, annihilating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशयितृ
वि-नाशयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who destroys, a<BR>destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशित
वि-नाशित, अस्, आ, अम्, utterly destroyed, ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशिन्
वि-नाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, perishing, being destroyed; un-<BR>dergoing transformation; destructive, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनस|विनसः
विनस वि-नस, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, noseless,<BR>without a nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनासक|विनासकः
वि-नासक or वि-नासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, noseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विना
विना विना, ind. (probably a kind of inst.<BR>of 1. वि), without, except (with acc., inst., or occa-<BR>sionally abl., e. g. भूषणम् or भूषणेन or<BR>भूषणाद् विना, without ornament); short of, ex-<BR>clusive of.<BR>—विना-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘made-without,’<BR>deprived of, bereaved, abandoned, left, relinquished.<BR>—विनान्योन्यम् (˚ना-अन्˚), ind. without each<BR>other, one without the other.<BR>—विनोक्ति (˚ना-उक्˚),<BR>इस्, f. ‘the utterance of विना,’ i. e. the use of the<BR>word विना in composition (e. g. का निशा शशिना<BR>विना, what is the night without the moon?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाडिका
विनाडिका वि-नाडिका or वि-नाडी, f. a period<BR>of twenty-four seconds, the sixtieth part of a Nāḍī or<BR>Indian hour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाथ
विनाथ वि-नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having no lord<BR>or master, unprotected, unowned, deserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायक|विनायकः
विनायक वि-नायक. See p. 925, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनारुहा
विनारुहा विनारुहा, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>त्रि-पर्णिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाह|विनाहः
विनाह वि-नाह, अस्, m. (see rt. 1. नह्), a<BR>top or cover for the mouth of a well; [cf. वीनाह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःकम्प
विनिःकम्प वि-निः-कम्प, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>motionless, immovable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःश्वस्
विनिःश्वस् वि-निः-श्वस्, cl. 2. P. -श्वसिति,<BR>-श्वसितुम्, to breathe hard, sigh, heave a deep sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःश्वस्य
वि-निःश्वस्य, ind. having sighed, having heaved<BR>a sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःसृ
विनिःसृ वि-निः-सृ, cl. 1. P. -सरति, -सर्तुम्,<BR>to go forth, issue out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःसरण
वि-निःसरण, अम्, n. the act of going forth or<BR>out, issuing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःसृत
वि-निःसृत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone forth or out, issued<BR>forth, sprung from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकृ
विनिकृ वि-नि-कृ (see rt. 1. कृ), cl. 8. P. A.<BR>-करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to act badly towards,<BR>ill-treat, offend, hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकृत
वि-निकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-treated, injured, damaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकृत्
विनिकृत् वि-नि-कृत् (see rt. 2. कृत्), cl. 6. P.<BR>-कृन्तति, -कर्तितुम्, to cut or hew in pieces, cut<BR>off, cut away, cut about, mutilate; to tear off; to<BR>destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकृत्त
वि-निकृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cut or hewn in pieces,<BR>mutilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकृत्य
वि-निकृत्य, ind. having cut away or asunder,<BR>having destroyed, having dissipated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकॄ
विनिकॄ वि-नि-कॄ (see rt. 1. कॄ), cl. 6. P.<BR>-किरति, -करितुम् or -करीतुम्, to scatter in dif-<BR>ferent directions, throw about; to scatter or cast<BR>down; to scatter over, cover; to cast off, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकीर्ण
वि-निकीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, scattered over, covered;<BR>spread over; crowded, filled; outstretched; dispersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्ष्
विनिक्ष् वि-निक्ष्, cl. 1. P. -निक्षति, &c.<BR>(Ved. Inf. विनिक्षे), to pierce, penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षण
वि-निक्षण, अम्, n. the act of piercing; [cf.<BR>Nirukta IV. 18.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षिप्
विनिक्षिप् वि-नि-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. A. -क्षि-<BR>पति, -ते, -क्षेप्तुम्, to throw or cast down, over-<BR>throw; to put or place down; to put or place in or<BR>on, infix, insert; to deposit, deliver over, entrust<BR>with; to occupy with or engage in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षिप्त|विनिक्षिप्तः
वि-निक्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or tossed down;<BR>fixed, infixed, inserted; deposited; dispatched, sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षिप्य
वि-निक्षिप्य, ind. having thrown or flung down,<BR>having put down, having delivered over, having given<BR>into charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षेप|विनिक्षेपः
वि-निक्षेप, अस्, m. the act of throwing or tossing<BR>down, sending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगड
विनिगड वि-निगड, अस्, आ, अम्, fetterless,<BR>without fetters.<BR>—विनिगडी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to render fetterless, unfetter, unshackle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगद्
विनिगद् वि-नि-गद्, cl. 1. P. -गदति, -गदि-<BR>तुम्, to speak to, address, accost: Pass. -गद्यते,<BR>to be called or named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगुह्
विनिगुह् वि-नि-गुह्, cl. 1. P. A. -गूहति,<BR>-ते, -गूहितुम् or -गोढुम्, to cover over, conceal,<BR>hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगूहित
वि-निगूहित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered, concealed, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रह्
विनिग्रह् वि-नि-ग्रह्, cl. 9. P. A. -गृह्णाति,<BR>गृह्णीते, -ग्रहीतुम्, to lay hold of, seize; to hold in,<BR>keep back, keep in check, restrain, obstruct, impede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगृह्य
वि-निगृह्य, ind. having seized, having restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रह|विनिग्रहः
वि-निग्रह, अस्, m. restraining, subduing, restraint;<BR>disjunction, mutual opposition, an antithesis which im-<BR>plies that when two propositions are antithetically stated<BR>peculiar stress is laid on one of them.<BR>—विनिग्र-<BR>हार्थ (˚ह-अर्˚), अस्, m. the sense of the above<BR>antithesis.<BR>—विनिग्रहार्थीय, अस्, आ, अम्, standing<BR>in the sense of the above antithesis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिघ्नत्
विनिघ्नत् वि-निघ्नत्. See under वि-नि-हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिचूर्ण्
विनिचूर्ण् वि-नि-चूर्ण्, cl. 10. P. -चूर्णयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to grind or crush to pieces, pulverize, pound,<BR>rub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्र|विनिद्रः
विनिद्र वि-निद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, sleepless, awake;<BR>blown, budded.<BR>—विनिद्र-करण, अम्, n. rendering<BR>sleepless.<BR>—विनिद्र-ता, f. or विनिद्र-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>sleeplessness, wakefulness, vigilance, waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिधा
विनिधा वि-नि-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, to put or lay down in different<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-c" target="_blank">Page0923-c+ 75</a>]<BR>places, distribute; to put off; to lay or put down;<BR>to put away; to place or put on; to put by, lay aside,<BR>store up; to fix upon, direct, (with दृष्टिम्, &c.,<BR>to fix the eyes upon; with मनस्, &c., to fix or<BR>direct the mind upon; with हृदि or हृदये, to fix<BR>in the heart, keep fixed in the heart, bear in mind.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिधाय
वि-निधाय, ind. having put in different places,<BR>having distributed; having placed or taken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहित
वि-निहित, अस्, आ, अम्, put off or down, &c.; fixed<BR>on, directed.<BR>—विनिहित-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, having<BR>the eyes fixed upon, eagerly looking at, intent on.<BR>—विनिहित-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the mind<BR>fixed upon, intent upon, devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0923-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिध्वंस्
