वि-निष्क्रामत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, stepping forth,<BR>coming out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्क्रिय
विनिष्क्रिय वि-निष्क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, abstain-<BR>ing or desisting from ceremonial rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्टप्
विनिष्टप् वि-निष्-टप् (-निस्-तप्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-तपति, -तप्तुम्, to heat or roast thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्टप्त
वि-निष्टप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well roasted, well fried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पट्
विनिष्पट् वि-निष्-पट् (-निस्-पट्), cl. 10. P.<BR>-पाटयति, -यितुम्, to split or cleave asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पत्
विनिष्पत् वि-निष्-पत् (-निस्-पत्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-पतति, -पतितुम्, to fall out of, fly forth from,<BR>rush out, jump forth, leap out, come forth; to go<BR>or run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पतित
वि-निष्पतित, अस्, आ, अम्, rushed forth, lept out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पत्य
वि-निष्पत्य, ind. having rushed out, having<BR>come forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पिष्
विनिष्पिष् वि-निष्-पिष् (-निस्-पिष्), cl. 7. P.<BR>-पिनष्टि, -पेष्टुम्, to grind to pieces, crush, bruise;<BR>to rub together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पिष्ट
वि-निष्पिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, ground to pieces,<BR>crushed into powder, smashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पिष्य
वि-निष्पिष्य, ind. having ground or rubbed to-<BR>gether, having battered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पेष|विनिष्पेषः
वि-निष्पेष, अस्, m. grinding to pieces, bruising,<BR>rubbing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिसूद्
विनिसूद् वि-नि-सूद्, Caus. -सूदयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to kill or destroy utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिसृ
विनिसृ वि-नि-सृ = वि-निः-सृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिसृत
वि-निसृत = वि-निःसृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिस्तप्
विनिस्तप् वि-निस्-तप्, cl. 1. P. -तपति, &c.,<BR>see वि-निष्-तप्; (स् is only retained before त् when<BR>repeated action is intended; in other cases it becomes<BR>ष् by Pāṇini VIII. 3, 102.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहन्
विनिहन् वि-नि-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -हन्-<BR>तुम्, to strike down, strike, kill, wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिघ्नत्
वि-निघ्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, striking down, wound-<BR>ing; killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहत|विनिहतः
वि-निहत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck down, struck,<BR>wounded; completely killed; overcome; (अस्), m. a<BR>great or unavoidable calamity, the infliction of fate<BR>or heaven; a portent, comet, meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहत्य
वि-निहत्य, ind. having struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिह्नुत
विनिह्नुत वि-निह्नुत, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. नि-<BR>ह्नुत], hidden, concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनी
विनी वि-नी, cl. 1. P. -नयति, -नेतुम्, to<BR>lead away, take away, remove; to lead, conduct,<BR>bring, guide; to train, educate; to tame, govern; to<BR>advise, instruct, direct, give directions; to conduct,<BR>perform; to bend down, incline; to pour out; to<BR>present, offer; to spend, pass (time); to spend, pay<BR>(money); to spread: Pass. -नीयते, to be led or<BR>guided &c., to be conducted or performed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनय|विनयः
वि-नय, अस्, m. leading, guidance, moral training,<BR>training, discipline; gentlemanly refinement, gentle-<BR>manlike bearing; good behaviour, propriety of con-<BR>duct, decorum, decency; modesty, affability, humi-<BR>lity, mildness; reverence, obeisance, courtesy; conduct<BR>or behaviour (in general); N. of a son of Dharma;<BR>(आ), f. the plant Sida Cordifolia; (अस्, आ, अम्), cast,<BR>thrown; secret; a man of subdued senses; a mer-<BR>chant, trader, (these four senses are given on the<BR>authority of the Śabda-k.)<BR>—विनय-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, conforming to rules of discipline, compliant, tract-<BR>able, humble.<BR>—विनय-पिटक, अस्, m. ‘basket of<BR>discipline,’ N. of those Buddhist works which contain<BR>moral precepts and rules of discipline; [cf. त्रि-पिटक.]<BR>—विनय-प्रधान, अस्, आ, अम्, having humility<BR>pre-eminent, of which modesty is chief.<BR>—विनय-<BR>प्रमाथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, violating propriety, behaving<BR>ill or improperly.<BR>—विनय-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, possess-<BR>ing propriety or modesty, well-behaved, modest.<BR>—विनय-योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing humility.<BR>—विनय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of modesty,<BR>well-behaved, modest.<BR>—विनय-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, speak-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">Page0925-b+ 79</a>]<BR>ing humbly or modestly; (क्), f. modest speech.<BR>—विनय-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, conforming to disci-<BR>pline, compliant, tractable, governable.<BR>—विनयाव-<BR>नत (˚य-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bending down modestly,<BR>bowing low with modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयन|विनयनं
वि-नयन, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, taking away, remov-<BR>ing; (अम्), n. the act of leading away, removing,<BR>taking away; training, education, instruction, accom-<BR>plishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायक|विनायकः
वि-नायक, अस्, इका, अम्, taking away, removing;<BR>(अस्), m. a remover (of obstacles); a Buddha or<BR>Buddhist deified teacher; N. of the god Gaṇeśa; of<BR>Garuḍa (the bird and vehicle of Viṣṇu); of a poet;<BR>a Guru or spiritual preceptor; an obstacle, impedi-<BR>ment, difficulty; (इका), f. the wife of Garuḍa.<BR>—वि-<BR>नायक-चरित, अम्, n., N. of the seventy-third<BR>chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa or second part of the<BR>Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—विनायक-पण्डित, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a poet; = नन्द-पण्डित.<BR>—विनायक-भट्ट,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a modern author.<BR>—विनायक-भो-<BR>जन-वर्णना, f., N. of a chapter of the Gaṇeśa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—विनायकावतार-वर्णन (˚क-अव्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of part of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—विना-<BR>यकाविर्भाव (˚क-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘manifestation of<BR>Gaṇeśa,’ N. of the sixth chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa<BR>or second part of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—विनायकोत्-<BR>पत्ति (˚क-उत्˚), इस्, f. ‘birth of Gaṇeśa,’ N. of the<BR>102nd chapter of the first part of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीत|विनीतः
वि-नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, led away, taken away, removed;<BR>led, conveyed; taken; thrown, sent, dismissed; well-<BR>trained, educated, disciplined, refined, gentleman-<BR>like, well-behaved, well-controlled; compliant, go-<BR>vernable, tractable; modest, demure, meek, virtuous,<BR>gentle, placid, decent, decorous; having the passions<BR>restrained, having the senses under subjection; tamed,<BR>broken in (as a horse, ox, &c.); chastised, punished;<BR>plain, neat (in dress &c.); lovely, handsome; (अस्),<BR>m. a trained horse; a merchant, trader; N. of a son<BR>of Pulastya.<BR>—विनीत-त्व, अम्, n. modesty, decency,<BR>decorum.<BR>—विनीत-वेष, अस्, m. a modest or ap-<BR>propriate garb, plain attire.<BR>—विनीतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚),<BR>आ, आ, अ, having a well-controlled mind, well-behaved;<BR>humble, lowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतक|विनीतकं
वि-नीतक, अस्, अम्, m. n. any medium of convey-<BR>ance (= वैनीतक, q. v.); a bearer (carrying a<BR>litter); a horse (dragging a carriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीति|विनीतिः
वि-नीति, इस्, f. training, good behaviour, reverence,<BR>obeisance, homage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीय|विनीयः
1. वि-नीय, ind. having taken away or removed;<BR>having conducted; having guided or trained; having<BR>inclined; having passed (as time &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीय|विनीयः
2. वि-नीय, अस्, m. sediment, dregs; sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेतृ
वि-नेतृ, ता, m. a leader, guide, instructor, teacher;<BR>a governor, chastiser, ruler, king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेय|विनेयः
वि-नेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken away or removed;<BR>to be governed or directed, governable, tractable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेष्यत्
वि-नेष्यत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, wishing or in-<BR>tending to take away, wishing to deprive of, wishing<BR>to conduct, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनील
विनील वि-नील, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-blue, blue.<BR>—विनील-बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, having dark-blue<BR>stalks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनु
विनु वि-नु, cl. 1. A. -नवते, &c., Ved. to<BR>go or spread in different directions, (Sāy. = विविधं<BR>व्य्-आप्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनुद्
विनुद् वि-नुद्, cl. 6. P. A. -नुदति, -ते,<BR>-नोत्तुम्, to drive asunder, drive away, scare away,<BR>dispel, remove; to wound; to strike (the cords of a<BR>lute &c.), play (on a musical instrument): Caus.<BR>-नोदयति, -यितुम्, to drive away, dispel, remove;<BR>to pass away or spend (time &c.); to divert, amuse,<BR>entertain; to delight in (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनुद्यमान
वि-नुद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being driven away,<BR>being sent away, being dispatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोद|विनोदः
वि-नोद, अस्, m. driving away, removing, dismiss-<BR>ing, abandoning; diversion, sport, pastime, play;<BR>interest, interesting pursuit or occupation, pleasure,<BR>gratification, happiness; eagerness, vehemence; N.<BR>of a work on music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदन|विनोदनं
वि-नोदन, अम्, n. the act of driving away or re-<BR>moving; diversion, play, sport, pastime, enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदित
वि-नोदित, अस्, आ, अम्, driven away, dispelled,<BR>dissipated, dispersed; dismissed; diverted, amused;<BR>delighted, made happy; allayed, soothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदिन्
वि-नोदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, driving away; diverting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोक्ति|विनोक्तिः
विनोक्ति विनोक्ति. See under विना, p. 923.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्द्|विंद्
विन्द् विन्द्. See rt. 1. विद्, p. 918.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्द|विन्दः
विन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, finding, getting, gaining, one<BR>who finds, &c.; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Jaya-sena;<BR>of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दमान
विन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, finding, acquiring, ob-<BR>taining, gaining, taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दु|विंदु|विन्दुः
विन्दु, उस्, उस्, उ, intelligent, knowing; liberal,<BR>munificent; finding, obtaining [cf. लोक-व्˚]; (उस्),<BR>m. a detached particle, drop, (in the Vedas usually<BR>spelt बिन्दु, q. v., and in this sense, according to<BR>some, fr. rt. बिद् or बिन्द्); a drop of water or other<BR>liquid, tear-drop [cf. जल-व्˚, वाष्प-व्˚; rarely<BR>neut., e. g. in Mahā-bh. Droṇa-p. 2113. अश्रु-विन्-<BR>दूनि, ‘drops of tears’]; a drop of water taken as a<BR>measure; a spherule, globule, spot, dot, mark; a<BR>mark or spot of coloured paint on an elephant's<BR>trunk; the dot over a letter representing the Anu-<BR>svāra; (in manuscripts) a mark over an erased word<BR>to show that the word ought not to be erased [cf.<BR>कुण्डलना]; a mark made by the teeth of a lover<BR>on the lips of his mistress; a peculiar mark like a<BR>dot made in cauterizing; a particular part of the<BR>mystic rites of the Śaivas; the part of the forehead<BR>between the eyebrows; (in the drama) the unex-<BR>pected development of a secondary incident (which,<BR>like a drop of oil in water, expands and furnishes an<BR>important element in the plot); N. of the author of<BR>a Rasa-paddhati; (अवस्), m. pl., N. of a warrior<BR>tribe.<BR>—विन्दु-घृत, अम्, n., Ved., N. of a parti-<BR>cular medicinal compound taken in small quantities.<BR>—विन्दु-चित, अस्, m. a kind of deer or other animal<BR>(= रोहिष).<BR>—विन्दु-चित्रक, अस्, m. the spotted<BR>antelope.<BR>—विन्दु-जाल or विन्दु-जालक, अम्, n.<BR>a mass of dots or spots; coloured marks or spots on<BR>an elephant's face and trunk.<BR>—विन्दु-तन्त्र, अस्,<BR>m. a die, dice; a kind of chess-board.<BR>—विन्दु-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—विन्-<BR>दु-देव, अस्, m. = ण, a Buddhist deity; N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—विन्दु-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a teacher of<BR>the Haṭha-vidyā.<BR>—विन्दु-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a species<BR>of birch tree.<BR>—विन्दु-पत्त्रक, a species of ama-<BR>ranth used as a vegetable.<BR>—विन्दु-फल, अम्, n.<BR>a pearl.<BR>—विन्दु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing drops,<BR>formed into balls or globules (Ved.); (आन्), m., N.<BR>of a son of Marīci by Vindu-matī; (अती), f. epithet<BR>of certain verses mentioned in the Śārṅgadhara-<BR>paddhati; N. of a particular treatise; of the wife of<BR>Marīci and mother of Vindu-mat; of a daughter<BR>of Śaśa-vindu and wife of Māndhātṛ; of various<BR>other women.<BR>—विन्दु-माधव, अस्, m. a form<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—विन्दु-रेखक, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR>—विन्दु-रेखा, f. a row or line of points or dots;<BR>N. of a daughter of Caṇḍa-vikrama.<BR>—विन्दु-वा-<BR>सर, अस्, m. the day of fecundation or conception.<BR>—विन्दु-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a work on<BR>medicine.<BR>—विन्दु-सन्दीपन, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>commentary on the Siddhānta-tattva-vindu.<BR>—विन्दु-<BR>सरस्, अस्, n., N. of a sacred lake, (also written<BR>विन्दु-सर.)<BR>—विन्दु-सार, अस्, m., N. of a king<BR>(a son of Candra-gupta).<BR>—विन्दु-सेन, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king (a son of Kṣatraujas).<BR>—विन्दु-ह्रद,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुक
विन्दुक, अस्, m. = विन्दु, a drop, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुकित
विन्दुकित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with drops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्
विन्ध् विन्ध्, a Vedic rt. (of which the<BR>form विन्धे, ‘I know,’ occurs in Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 7, 7), referred by some to rt. विध् or व्यध्,<BR>and by others connected with rt. विन्द्, (see Nirukta<BR>VI. 18.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्धपत्त्र
विन्धपत्त्र विन्ध-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a plant<BR>(commonly called Bel Suṇṭh).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0925-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्य|विंध्यः|विन्ध्यः
विन्ध्य विन्ध्य, अस्, m. (perhaps connected<BR>with rt. बिन्द् or बिद्, ‘to divide’), N. of a range of<BR>mountains connecting the Northern extremities of<BR>the Western and Eastern Ghauts, and separating Hin-<BR>dūstān proper from the Dekhan, (the Vindhya range<BR>is reckoned among the seven principal mountains of<BR>Bhārata-varṣa [see कुलाचल, p. 240, col. 3], and<BR>according to Manu II. 21. forms the Southern limit<BR>of Madhya-deśa or the middle region, regarded as<BR>the sacred land of the Hindūs; according to a legend<BR>related in the Vana-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata,<BR>1. 8782 &c., the personified Vindhya mountain,<BR>jealous of Himālaya, demanded that the sun should<BR>revolve round him in the same way as about Meru,<BR>which the sun declining to do, the Vindhya then began<BR>to elevate himself that he might bar the progress of<BR>both sun and moon; the gods alarmed, asked the<BR>aid of the saint Agastya, who approached the moun-<BR>tain and requested that by bending down he would<BR>afford him an easy passage to the South country,<BR>begging at the same time that he would retain a low<BR>position till his return; this the mountain promised<BR>to do, but Agastya never returned, and the Vindhya<BR>range consequently never attained the elevation of<BR>the Himālaya); a hunter; (आ), f. a kind of plant<BR>or tree (= लवली); small cardamoms (= त्रुटि).<BR>—विन्ध्य-कन्दर, N. of a place.<BR>—विन्ध्य-<BR>कूट or विन्ध्य-कूटन, अस्, m. epithet of the<BR>saint Agastya.<BR>—विन्ध्य-पर्वत, अस्, m. the Vindhya<BR>mountains.<BR>—विन्ध्य-मूलिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—विन्ध्य-वासिन्, ई, m. ‘dwelling in the<BR>Vindhya,’ epithet of the celebrated grammarian and<BR>lexicographer Vyāḍi; (इनी), f., N. of Durgā; a<BR>village and temple sacred to Durgā under the forms<BR>of Yoga-māyā and Bhoga-māyā (said to be a place<BR>of great resort, situated about three miles from Mirza-<BR>pur on the Ganges).<BR>—विन्ध्य-शक्ति, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—विन्ध्य-शैल, अस्, m. the Vindhya<BR>mountains.<BR>—विन्ध्य-स्थ, अस्, m. ‘living in the<BR>Vindhya,’ epithet of Vyāḍi (regarded as an inspired<BR>grammarian and Muni).<BR>—विन्ध्याचल (˚य-अच्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the Vindhya range of mountains.<BR>—विन्ध्या-<BR>टवी (˚य-अट्˚), f. the great Vindhya forest (which<BR>appears to have spread at one time from near Ma-<BR>thurā to the Narma-dā).<BR>—विन्ध्याद्रि-वासिनी, f. =<BR>विन्ध्य-वासिनी.<BR>—विन्ध्यावलि (˚य-आव्˚), इस्, or<BR>विन्ध्यावली, f., N. of the wife of the Asura Bali.<BR>—विन्ध्यावली-पुत्र or विन्ध्यावली-सुत (˚य-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. ‘son of Vindhyāvalī,’ N. of the Asura<BR>Vāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्न|विन्नः
विन्न विन्न. See p. 919, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्नप
विन्नप विन्नप, अस्, m. (perhaps fr. विन्न,<BR>q. v. + प), the saint Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्
विन्यस् वि-न्य्-अस् (वि-नि-), cl. 4. P. -अस्यति,<BR>-असितुम्, to put or place down in different places;<BR>to put down, deposit; to place in order, adjust, dis-<BR>pose, arrange, distribute; to put or place on, lay on;<BR>to set the mind on; to fix the eyes upon; to put or<BR>place into; to deliver over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्त|विन्यस्तः
वि-न्यस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, placed down, deposited,<BR>fixed; inlaid, paved; delivered; offered, presented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्य
वि-न्यस्य, ind. having put or laid down; having<BR>laid on, &c.; having arranged or disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्यत्
वि-न्यस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, putting down, putting<BR>or placing on; setting or fixing the eyes upon;<BR>arranging, fixing, settling, determining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यास|विन्यासः
वि-न्यास, अस्, m. putting or placing down, de-<BR>positing, entrusting; a deposit; orderly arrangement,<BR>disposition; any site or receptacle on or in which<BR>anything is placed or deposited; collecting, collection,<BR>assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्याक|विन्याकः
विन्याक विन्याक, अस्, m. the tree Echites<BR>Scholaris (= विद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् 1. विप् [cf. rts. वप्, व्यप्], cl. 10.<BR>P. वेपयति (Ved. also विपयति), -यि-<BR>तुम्, to throw, cast; to strew, scatter, (Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>21, 2. विपयन्ति बर्हिः, they strew the sacred<BR>grass; Sāy. = स्तृणन्ति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् 2. विप्, प्, प्, प्, Ved. (perhaps con-<BR>nected with rt. 1. विप्, in the sense ‘pouring out,’ ‘ut-<BR>tering’), uttering hymns of praise, praising; (प्), m.<BR>a singer of hymns, praiser; = विप्र; = मेधाविन्,<BR>a wise man; (प्), f. praise, a hymn; a finger.<BR>—वि-<BR>पश्-चित्, त्, त्, त्, excogitating praise or hymns of praise<BR>(Ved.); wise, learned, prudent; (त्), m. a Ṛṣi, sage,<BR>teacher, learned Brāhman (= मेधाविन्, Naigh. III.<BR>15); N. of the Indra in the second Manv-antara.<BR>—विपो-धा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. singing hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप
विप, अस्, m., Ved. a praiser (= मेधाविन्, ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. III. 15); (आ), f. = वाच् (according<BR>to Naigh. I. 11).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्र|विप्रः
विप्र, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. II. 28. fr. rt.<BR>वप्, ‘to strew;’ cf. rt. 1. विप्), an utterer of praise,<BR>singer of hymns, Ṛṣi, praiser, poet, any one skilled<BR>in hymns; a Brāhman, priest; a sage, seer, wise<BR>man (= मेधाविन्, Naigh. III. 15); a foot of four<BR>short syllables (in prosody); N. of a son of Dhruva;<BR>of a son of Śrutañ-jaya.<BR>—विप्र-कन्या, f. a Brāh-<BR>man girl, maiden of the sacerdotal class, Brāhmaṇī.<BR>—विप्र-काष्ठ, अम्, n. the cotton tree (= तूल-<BR>वृक्ष).<BR>—विप्र-चूडामणि, इस्, m. ‘Brāhman-<BR>jewel,’ an excellent Brāhman.<BR>—विप्र-जन, अस्, m.<BR>a person of the sacerdotal caste, a Brāhman; a com-<BR>pany of Brāhmans.<BR>—विप्र-जूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>impelled or urged by priests, invoked by the wise,<BR>(Sāy. = मेधाविभिर् ऋत्विग्भिः प्रेरितः, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 3, 5.)<BR>—विप्र-जूति, इस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of Ṛg-veda X. 136, 3, (having the patronymic<BR>Vātaraśana.)<BR>—विप्र-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most<BR>wise, wisest.<BR>—विप्र-देव, अस्, m., N. of a leader<BR>of the Bhāgavata sect.<BR>—विप्र-प्रिय, अस्, m.<BR>‘Brāhman-favourite,’ epithet of the Palāśa tree.<BR>—विप्र-बन्धु, उस्, m., N. of the author of Ṛg-<BR>veda V. 24, 4, X. 57-60, (having the patronymic<BR>Gaupāyana or Laupāyana.)<BR>—विप्र-राज्य, अम्, n.<BR>the kingdom or sovereignty of the Brāhmans or<BR>priests.<BR>—विप्रर्षि (˚र-ऋषि), इस्, m. a Brāhman-<BR>ṛṣi, a sage of the Brāhmanical class (e. g. Vasiṣṭha).<BR>—विप्र-लोभिन्, ई, m. ‘Brāhman-enticing,’ epithet<BR>of the Kiṅkirāta tree.<BR>—विप्र-वचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. possessing the hymns of Ṛṣis or poets, (Sāy.<BR>= विविध-प्रकृष्ट-वचन.)<BR>—विप्र-समा-<BR>गम, अस्, m. a concourse of Brāhmans.<BR>—विप्र-<BR>सात्, ind. to the state of a Brāhman.<BR>—विप्र-सेवा,<BR>f. attendance on Brāhmans, service of a Brāhman<BR>master (Manu X. 123).<BR>—विप्र-स्व, अम्, n. the<BR>property of a Brāhman.<BR>—विप्रापवाद (˚र-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. abuse of a Brāhman.<BR>—विप्रेन्द्र (˚र-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. chief of Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्त्रिम
विपक्त्रिम वि-पक्त्रिम, वि-पक्व. See un-<BR>der वि-पच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्ष|विपक्षः
विपक्ष वि-पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, being on a<BR>different or opposite side, opposed, adverse, contrary,<BR>inimical; (अस्), m. an opponent, enemy, adversary,<BR>rival; a disputant; (in grammar) an exception;<BR>(in logic) a negative instance, a syllogism in which<BR>the major term is not found; an instance on the<BR>opposite side (as ‘there cannot be fire in a lake,<BR>because there is no smoke there’).<BR>—विपक्ष-तस्,<BR>ind. hostilely, inimically; from a rival, (चरमं<BR>विपक्षतः, after a rival, Kirāt. VIII. 54.)<BR>—वि-<BR>पक्ष-ता, f. or विपक्ष-त्व, अम्, n. hostility,<BR>enmity, opposition, controversy, contradiction.<BR>—वि-<BR>पक्ष-भाव, अस्, m. hostile disposition, state of<BR>hostility.<BR>—विपक्ष-शूल, अस्, m., N. of a chief of<BR>a sect called Ārādhya.<BR>—विपक्षाक्रान्त (˚ष-<BR>आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, seized by an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षस्
वि-पक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. placed or yoked on<BR>both sides (e. g. युञ्जन्ति काम्या हरी विपक्षसा<BR>रथे, they harness the two favourite bay horses<BR>[of Indra] to the chariot on both sides, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 6, 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षपात
विपक्षपात वि-पक्षपात, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from partizanship, impartial, indifferent; (अस्), m.<BR>impartiality, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपच्
विपच् वि-पच्, cl. 1. P. A. -पचति, -ते,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">Page0926-c+ 77</a>]<BR>पक्तुम्, to cook thoroughly, overcook; to<BR>roast; to dissolve by cooking or boiling, melt,<BR>liquefy; to digest; to mature, ripen: Pass. -पच्-<BR>यते, to be cooked or baked; to be digested; to be<BR>completely matured or ripened; to be developed:<BR>Caus. -पाचयति, -यितुम्, to cook thoroughly, over-<BR>cook; to dissolve by cooking, melt, liquefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्त्रिम
वि-पक्त्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, thoroughly matured,<BR>ripened; fulfilled, developed, come to pass (as the<BR>consequence of former actions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्व
वि-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, cooked, dressed; ripened,<BR>matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाक|विपाकः
वि-पाक, अस्, m. cooking thoroughly, cooking,<BR>dressing; ripening, maturing, ripeness, maturity;<BR>conversion of food into a state differing from its<BR>original one, digestion; change of state (in general);<BR>unexpected consequence of actions, unexpected event<BR>or occurrence, improbable result; the consequence<BR>or result of any action either in this or in a former<BR>birth matured by the operation of time; calamity,<BR>distress, poverty, difficulty, embarrassment; flavour,<BR>taste; (अस्, आ, अम्), having mature fruit, fruitful,<BR>(Sāy. = परिपक्व-फल.)<BR>—विपाक-विस्फूर्ज-<BR>थु, उस्, m. the thunder or thunderbolt of the con-<BR>sequences (of sins committed in a former birth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाकिन्
वि-पाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having unexpected consequences<BR>or results, resulting in, followed by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपञ्ची|विपंची
विपञ्ची वि-पञ्ची, f. (said to be fr. rt. पञ्च्<BR>with वि), play, sport, pastime; a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपञ्चिका|विपंचिका
वि-पञ्चिका, f. a lute (= वीणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपट्
विपट् वि-पट्, cl. 10. P. -पाटयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to split in two, tear open; to tear out, eradicate,<BR>root up, destroy; to open, unfold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटन|विपाटनं
वि-पाटन, अम्, n. the act of splitting in two,<BR>tearing open, uprooting, eradication; driving away,<BR>spoliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटित
वि-पाटित, अस्, आ, अम्, split or torn open, rooted up,<BR>eradicated, destroyed.<BR>—विपाटितारिष्ट (˚त-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, destroying or driving away ill luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपठ्
विपठ् वि-पठ्, cl. 1. P. -पठति, -पठितुम्,<BR>to read through, read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपण्
विपण् वि-पण्, cl. 1. A. -पणते (ep. also<BR>P. -ति), -पणितुम्, to sell; to bet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपण|विपणः
वि-पण, अस्, m. or वि-पणन, अम्, n. sale,<BR>contract of sale; low or petty traffic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणत्
वि-पणत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, selling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणि|विपणिः
वि-पणि, इस्, m. f. or वि-पणी, f. a place where<BR>things are sold, a shop, stall, fair, market, market-<BR>place; the street of a market; any article or com-<BR>modity for sale; traffic.<BR>—विपणि-मध्य-ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, being in the midst of the market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणिन्
वि-पणिन्, ई, m. a dealer, trafficker, shopkeeper,<BR>merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्
विपत् वि-पत्, cl. 1. P. -पतति, -पतितुम्,<BR>to fall or break through, dash through (Ved., Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda I. 168, 6. वि-पतथ = विशीर्णम्<BR>पातयथ); to fall off, fly apart, fall asunder, burst<BR>asunder, be reft asunder, be divided or separated:<BR>Caus. -पातयति, -यितुम्, to cause to fly off or away,<BR>shoot off, discharge (arrows &c.); to cause to fly<BR>apart or burst asunder; to destroy, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपथ|विपथः
विपथ वि-पथ, अस्, अम्, m. n. a different<BR>path, wrong way, bad road; (अस्), m., Ved. a kind<BR>of war-chariot.<BR>—विपथ-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going<BR>in a wrong way or evil course.<BR>—विपथ-यमक,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of Yamaka, q. v., in which the parono-<BR>masia is only at the beginning and end of the verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपथि
वि-पथि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. going on paths that spread<BR>in different directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद् 1. वि-पद्, cl. 4. A. -पद्यते, -पत्-<BR>तुम्, to go apart, go badly or wrongly, fail, mis-<BR>carry; to fall into a bad state, fall into misfortune;<BR>to be disabled or incapacitated; to perish, die; to<BR>hinder, obstruct: Caus. -पादयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to go wrong, cause to perish, destroy, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्ति|विपत्तिः
1. वि-पत्ति, इस्, f. going wrongly, adversity, cala-<BR>mity, misfortune, disaster, mishap, (opposed to सम्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">Page0927-a+ 76</a>]<BR>पत्ति); pain, agony; death, dying.<BR>—विपत्ति-काल,<BR>अस्, m. a season of adversity or distress.<BR>—विपत्ति-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, attended with misfortune, unfor-<BR>tunate.<BR>—विपत्ति-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, free from mis-<BR>fortune, prosperous, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्ति|विपत्तिः
2. वि-पत्ति, इस्, m. a distinguished or excellent<BR>foot-soldier (= विशिष्टः पदातिः, Kirāt. XV. 16).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
2. वि-पद्, त्, f. going wrongly, calamity, adversity,<BR>distress, misfortune; death.<BR>—विपत्-काल, अस्, m. a<BR>time of calamity, season of misfortune, adversity,<BR>—विपत्-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, resulting in misfortunes,<BR>calamitous in result.<BR>—विपत्-सागर, अस्, m. an<BR>ocean of misfortunes, heavy calamity.<BR>—विपद्-उद्-<BR>धरण, अम्, n. or विपद्-उद्धार, अस्, m. extri-<BR>cation from misfortune.<BR>—विपद्-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>seized or devoured by misfortune, overtaken by or<BR>involved in calamity.<BR>—विपद्-दशा, f. a state of<BR>misfortune, calamitous condition.<BR>—विपद्-युक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, attended with misfortune, unhappy, un-<BR>fortunate.<BR>—विपद्-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>misfortune, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदा
वि-पदा, f. misfortune, adversity, calamity, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्न|विपन्नः
वि-पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, gone wrong, fallen into<BR>adversity or misfortune, unfortunate, afflicted, dis-<BR>tressed; declined, failed; disabled, incapacitated;<BR>lost, destroyed, annihilated; dead, defunct; (अस्), m.<BR>a snake.<BR>—विपन्नापत्य (˚न-अप्˚), आ, f. a woman<BR>who has lost a child by abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्नक
विपन्नक, अस्, आ, अम्, unfortunate; dead; de-<BR>stroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादन|विपादनं
वि-पादन, अम्, n. the act of destroying, destroy-<BR>ing, killing, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादनीय
वि-पादनीय or वि-पादयितव्य or वि-पाद्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, proper to be destroyed, fit to be killed,<BR>destructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादित
वि-पादित, अस्, आ, अम्, destroyed, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्य
विपन्य वि-पन्य (probably fr. विपन्या<BR>below), Nom. A. -पन्यते, &c., Ved. to praise in<BR>various ways, praise, (Sāy. = विविधं स्तु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्या
विपन्या, f., Ved. desire of praising; praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्यु
विपन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desirous of praising,<BR>wishing to praise, diligent in praise, singing praises,<BR>praising, (Sāy. = स्तोतृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपयस्
विपयस् वि-पयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, waterless,<BR>destitute of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिक्रम्
विपरिक्रम् वि-परि-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रा-<BR>मति, -क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to step or walk round<BR>or on all sides, go round, circumambulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिक्रान्त
वि-परिक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has shown<BR>valour (in battle), courageous, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिक्रामम्
वि-परिक्रामम्, ind., Ved. having walked round,<BR>going all about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिगा
विपरिगा वि-परि-गा, cl. 3. P. -जिगाति, -गा-<BR>तुम्, to go over, be overturned or upset (as a cart).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिच्छिद्
विपरिच्छिद् वि-परि-च्छिद् (-छिद्), cl. 7. P. A.<BR>-च्छिनत्ति, -च्छिन्त्ते, -च्छेत्तुम्, to cut on all sides,<BR>cut round, cut to pieces, cut off, destroy utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिच्छिन्न
वि-परिच्छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, cut on all sides, cut<BR>to pieces, cut off, utterly destroyed.<BR>—विपरिच्छिन्न-<BR>मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having the roots cut completely<BR>round or off, entirely uprooted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणम्
विपरिणम् वि-परि-णम् (-नम्), Pass. -णम्-<BR>यते, to be changed into; to undergo change or<BR>alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणमन|विपरिणमनं
वि-परिणमन, अम्, n. changing, alteration, un-<BR>dergoing change or alterations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणाम|विपरिणामः
वि-परिणाम, अस्, m. change of state or form,<BR>transformation, change, alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणामिन्
वि-परिणामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, undergoing or producing<BR>change of state or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरितप्
विपरितप् वि-परि-तप्, cl. 4. A. or Pass.<BR>-तप्यते, to be greatly distressed, suffer great pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिधा
विपरिधा वि-परि-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, to exchange, change, alter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिधाय
वि-परिधाय, ind. having changed, having<BR>changed a dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिधाव्
विपरिधाव् वि-परि-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धा-<BR>वति, -ते, -धावितुम्, to run about, run in all direc-<BR>tions; to run through, overrun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिमुच्
विपरिमुच् वि-परि-मुच्, Pass. -मुच्यते, to<BR>be freed from, be released from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिम्लै
विपरिम्लै वि-परि-म्लै, cl. 1. P. A. -म्लायति,<BR>-ते, -म्लातुम्, to fade or wither away entirely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिम्लान
वि-परिम्लान, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely faded, com-<BR>pletely withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिलुप्
विपरिलुप् वि-परि-लुप्, cl. 6. P. A. -लुम्-<BR>पति, -ते, -लोप्तुम्, to break to pieces or destroy<BR>utterly, break up, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिलुप्त
वि-परिलुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, broken or destroyed<BR>utterly, broken up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिलोप
वि-परिलोप, अस्, m. breaking or destroying utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवृत्
विपरिवृत् वि-परि-वृत्, cl. 1. A. -वर्तते,<BR>&c., -वर्तितुम्, to turn round, revolve, move in a<BR>circle; to roll about; to go to and fro, wander all<BR>round, wander about; to turn round or back, return;<BR>to be changed or altered; to surround, attend upon<BR>(with acc.): Caus. -वर्तयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to turn round or revolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्तन|विपरिवर्तनं|विपरिवर्त्तन
वि-परिवर्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to turn round,<BR>causing to return; (ई), f., scil. विद्या, a magical<BR>knowledge producing the return of any one; (अम्),<BR>n. turning about, turning away from or back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्तमान
वि-परिवर्तमान, अस्, आ, अम्, wandering or<BR>roaming about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्तित|विपरिवर्त्तित
वि-परिवर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, turned away from or<BR>back, reverted, averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्त्य
वि-परिवर्त्य, ind. having turned round, having<BR>turned away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवृत्ति
वि-परिवृत्ति, इस्, f. turning round, revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरी
विपरी वि-परी (-परि-इ), cl. 2. P. -पर्य्-एति,<BR>-एतुम्, to go or turn round in an opposite direction;<BR>to turn round the wrong way; to go round, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीत|विपरीतः
वि-परीत, अस्, आ, अम्, turned round, turned the<BR>wrong way, reversed, inverted, inverse, converse,<BR>opposite, adverse, perverse, contrary, repugnant; con-<BR>trary to what is right, wrong, contrary to rule, incor-<BR>rect; being the reverse of anything (abl.); being in<BR>altered or changed circumstances; acting in an oppo-<BR>site manner, having a contrary disposition, going<BR>asunder or in opposite directions, different; cross;<BR>disagreeable; inauspicious, unfavourable; (आ), f. a<BR>perverse woman; a disloyal or unchaste wife.<BR>—वि-<BR>परीत-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, or विपरीत-कारिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, or विपरीत-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, acting in a con-<BR>trary manner, perverse, contradictory.<BR>—विपरीत-<BR>क्रीडा, f., N. of the 125th chapter of the Śārṅga-<BR>dhara-paddhati.<BR>—विपरीत-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, going<BR>backwards, going in a contrary or reverse direction;<BR>(इस्), f. inverse or reverse motion.<BR>—विपरीत-चेतस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, contrary-minded, having a perverted mind<BR>or impaired mental faculties.<BR>—विपरीत-ता, f. or<BR>विपरीत-त्व, अम्, n. contrariety, inversion, per-<BR>verseness, reverse or opposite state or condition;<BR>counterpart.<BR>—विपरीत-पथ्या, f. a sort of metre.<BR>—विपरीत-बोध, अस्, आ, अम्, having a perverted<BR>understanding or intellect.<BR>—विपरीत-रत, अम्, n.<BR>inverted sexual intercourse.<BR>—विपरीत-लक्षणा, f.<BR>ironical description of an object by mentioning its<BR>contrary properties.<BR>—विपरीत-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, act-<BR>ing or behaving in a contrary manner.<BR>—विपरीता-<BR>ख्यानकी (˚त-आख्˚), f. a sort of metre.<BR>—विपरी-<BR>तायन (˚त-अय्˚), अम्, n. a contrary Ayana or<BR>progress of the sun from solstice to solstice.<BR>—विप-<BR>रीतायन-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, (in astronomy) situated<BR>in contrary Ayanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यय|विपर्ययः|विपर्य्यय|विपर्य्ययः
वि-पर्यय, अस्, m. reverse, inversion, contra-<BR>riety, (विपर्यये, on the contrary; रात्रेर् विपर्-<BR>ययः, the contrary of night, i. e. day); inverted<BR>order or succession, perverseness, obstruction, opposi-<BR>tion; change, interchange, exchange, barter, (द्र-<BR>व्य-व्˚, exchange of goods, buying and selling, trade);<BR>morbid change, reverse of fortune, calamity, mis-<BR>fortune, adverse fate; error, transgression, trespass;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">Page0927-c+ 71</a>]<BR>misapprehension, mistake, failure of conception; per-<BR>verseness of disposition; change of purpose or conduct,<BR>enmity, hostility; overthrow, destruction, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्याय|विपर्यायः|विपर्य्याय|विपर्य्यायः
वि-पर्याय, अस्, m. = वि-पर्यय, reverse, con-<BR>trariety, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरे
विपरे वि-परे (-परा-इ), cl. 2. P. -परैति,<BR>-परैतुम्, Ved. to go back again, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्णक|विपर्णकः
विपर्णक वि-पर्णक, अस्, m. the Palāśa tree,<BR>Butea Frondosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्
विपर्यस् वि-पर्य्-अस् (-परि-अस्), cl. 4. A.<BR>-अस्यते, -असितुम्, to throw or turn over, overturn,<BR>turn the wrong way, reverse, invert; to change<BR>about, interchange, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्त|विपर्य्यस्त
वि-पर्यस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, reversed, inverted, re-<BR>verse, opposite, contrary; interchanged, inverted (in<BR>grammar); erroneously conceived to be real.<BR>—वि-<BR>पर्यस्त-पुत्रा, f. a woman bearing no male chil-<BR>dren.<BR>—विपर्यस्त-मनश्-चेष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing mind and actions perverted or inverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्य
वि-पर्यस्य, ind. having turned over, having<BR>inverted, having changed or exchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यास|विपर्यासः|विपर्य्यास|विपर्य्यासः
वि-पर्यास, अस्, m. reverse, contrariety, opposi-<BR>tion; interchange [cf. वि-पर्यय]; error, mistake,<BR>delusion, imagining what is unreal or false to be real<BR>or true, error, mistake; (अम्), ind., Ved. alternately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यावृत्
विपर्यावृत् वि-पर्य्-आ-वृत् (-परि-आ-वृत्), cl.<BR>1. A. -वर्तते, &c., to be turned back: Caus. -वर्-<BR>तयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause to turn away from,<BR>cause to be overturned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यूह्
विपर्यूह् वि-पर्य्-ऊह् (-परि-ऊह्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-ऊहति, -ऊहितुम्, Ved. to place or fix separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्व
विपर्व वि-पर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. dismem-<BR>bered, mutilated, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>187, 1 = विच्छिन्न-सन्धिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपल|विपलं
विपल वि-पल, अम्, n. a moment, instant<BR>(= a Pala or second or, according to some, (1/6)th of it);<BR>a simple breathing (or, according to some, (1/10)th<BR>of it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलाय्
विपलाय् वि-पलाय् (fr. rt. अय् = rt. 5. इ with<BR>पला for परा and वि), cl. 1. A. -पलायते, -यितुम्,<BR>to run away in different directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायन|विपलायनं
वि-पलायन, अम्, n. running away, flying in<BR>different directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायित
वि-पलायित, अस्, आ, अम्, run away, running away,<BR>routed, put to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपल्यङ्ग्
विपल्यङ्ग् वि-पल्य्-अङ्ग् (-परि-अङ्ग्), Caus.<BR>-अङ्गयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to envelop, surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपल्यय्
विपल्यय् वि-पल्य्-अय् (fr. rt. अय् = rt. 5. इ<BR>with पलि for परि and वि), cl. 1. A. -पल्ययते,<BR>&c., Ved. to go back, turn round, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपव्य|विपव्यं
विपव्य वि-पव्य. See under वि-पू, P. 928.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपशिन्
विपशिन् वि-पशिन्, ई, m. (probably fr. rt.<BR>1. पश् with वि), a Buddhist saint, the first of the<BR>seven principal Buddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्य
वि-पश्य, अम्, n. knowledge (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्चित्
विपश्चित् विपश्-चित्. See under 2. विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपा
विपा वि-पा, cl. 1. P. -पिबति, &c., -पातुम्,<BR>to drink at different times; to drink up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिपान
वि-पिपान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. drinking much or<BR>variously; drinking especially, (Sāy. = विशेषेण<BR>पिबत्, Ṛg-veda I. 112, 15; = विपीत-वत् or वि-<BR>पिबत्, Ṛg-veda VII. 22, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपीत
वि-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, drunk up.<BR>—विपीत-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, one who has drunk up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाक|विपाकः
विपाक वि-पाक. See under वि-पच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटन|विपाटनं
विपाटन वि-पाटन. See under वि-पट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटल
विपाटल वि-पाटल, अस्, आ, अम्, pale-red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाठ|विपाठः
विपाठ विपाठ, अस्, m. (perhaps for वि-<BR>पाट, fr. rt. पट्), a kind of large arrow (described<BR>by the commentator on the Mahā-bhārata as विशालो<BR>वैशाखी-मुख-वत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0927-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाण्डु|विपांडु
विपाण्डु वि-पाण्डु, उस्, उस्, उ, pale, pallid<BR>(Kirāt. IV. 24), painted with different yellow colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाण्डुर
वि-पाण्डुर, अस्, आ, अम्, pale, pallid, white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादिका
विपादिका वि-पादिका, f. (fr. पाद with वि),<BR>a disease of the foot, a sore or tumour on the foot;<BR>a riddle, enigma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपापा
विपापा वि-पापा, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाल
विपाल वि-पाल, अस्, आ, अम्, having no keeper<BR>or attendant, unguarded, unattended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश्
विपाश् वि-पाश्, ट्, f. (according to Sāy. fr.<BR>rt. पट् or rt. पश्), the Vipāś or Vipāśā river, (see<BR>below.)<BR>—विपाट्-छुतुद्री, f. du. the rivers Vipāś and<BR>Śutudrī, (in Ṛg-veda III. 33. is a dialogue between<BR>Viśvā-mitra and these two rivers.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश
वि-पाश, अस्, आ, अम्, unnoosed, uncorded, unfast-<BR>ened, untied, unfettered, freed from a noose, devoid<BR>of fastenings or ties; (आ), f. the Vipāśā or Beas<BR>river, one of the five rivers of the Pañjāb (said to<BR>be so called as having destroyed the cord which the<BR>Muni Vasiṣṭha had tied round his neck when about<BR>to hang himself through grief for the death of his<BR>son slain by Viśvā-mitra; this river is considered<BR>to be indentical with the Hyphasis of Arrian, the<BR>Greek name being a corruption of Bipasha; it rises<BR>in the Himālaya, and after a course of about 220<BR>miles joins the Sutlej south-east of Amritsar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाशिन्
वि-पाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. without fastenings, with<BR>unloosed or dissevered fastenings or cords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिन|विपिनं
विपिन विपिन, अम्, n. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. II. 52. fr. rt. वेप्), a wood, forest, thicket, grove.<BR>—विपिन-तिलक, a species of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिनाय
विपिनाय, Nom. A. विपिनायते, &c., to be like<BR>a wood or thicket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुल|विपुलः
विपुल वि-पुल, अस्, आ, अम् (see rt. पुल्),<BR>large, great, extensive, broad, wide, spacious, roomy,<BR>capacious; abundant; deep, profound; (अस्), m. the<BR>mountain Meru (or the western branch of it); the<BR>Himālaya mountain; a respectable man; N. of a<BR>pupil of Deva-śarman (who guarded the virtue of<BR>Ruci, his preceptor's wife, when tempted by Indra<BR>during her husband's absence); (आ), f. the earth;<BR>N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in Vipula; a form of the Āryā<BR>metre in which the line is irregularly divided by the<BR>cesura or pause, (three species of this form are rec-<BR>koned, viz. Ādi-vipulā, having the pause in the first<BR>line; Antya-vipulā, having it in the second; Ubhaya-<BR>vipulā, having it in both lines.)<BR>—विपुल-च्छाय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having ample shade, shady, umbrageous.<BR>—विपुल-जघना, f. a woman with large hips.<BR>—विपुल-ता, f. or विपुल-त्व, अम्, n. largeness,<BR>greatness, magnitude, extent, width, spaciousness.<BR>—विपुल-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, endowed with great un-<BR>derstanding.<BR>—विपुल-रस, अस्, m. ‘having abun-<BR>dant juice,’ the sugar-cane.<BR>—विपुल-व्रत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who practises great devotion.<BR>—विपुल-<BR>श्रोणी, f. (a woman) having swelling hips, round-<BR>limbed.<BR>—विपुलायताक्ष (˚ल-आय्˚, ˚त-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having large and long eyes.<BR>—विपुलेक्षण<BR>(˚ल-इक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, large-eyed.<BR>—विपुलोरस्क<BR>(˚ल-उर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, broad-chested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलक
विपुलक वि-पुलक, अस्, ई, अम्, free from<BR>erection of the hair, devoid of horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलिन
विपुलिन वि-पुलिन, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>islands, having no islands or sandbanks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुष्ट
विपुष्ट वि-पुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-fed, under-<BR>fed; [cf. पुष्ट-विपुष्टौ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपू
विपू वि-पू, cl. 9. P. -पुनाति, -पवितुम्, to<BR>cleanse thoroughly, purify effectually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपव्य|विपव्यं
वि-पव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cleansed or purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपूय|विपूयः
1. वि-पूय, अस्, m. the Muñja grass, Saccharum<BR>Munja (so called from being cleaned before being<BR>made into ropes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपूय|विपूयः
2. वि-पूय, ind., Ved. having purified, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपृक्वत्|विपृक्वन्त्
विपृक्वत् विपृक्वत् [cf. rt. 1. पृच्], Ved. =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">Page0928-b+ 72</a>]<BR>सर्वतो व्याप्तम्, that which is everywhere diffused,<BR>(Ṛg-veda V. 2, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपृच्
विपृच् वि-पृच्, क्, f. (see rt. 1. पृच्), Ved.<BR>disuniting, expelling, driving away, (Sāy. = पृथक्-<BR>करण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपृच्छम्
विपृच्छम् वि-पृच्छम्, ind. to ask, to make<BR>various inquiries, (Sāy. = विविधम् प्रष्टुम्,<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 86, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपृथ
विपृथ वि-पृथ, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Citraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपृथु
विपृथु वि-पृथु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपोधा
विपोधा विपो-धा. See under 2. विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्र|विप्रः
विप्र विप्र, विप्र-कन्या, &c. See p. 926,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृ
विप्रकृ वि-प्र-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-<BR>रुते, -कर्तुम्, to treat with disrespect, hurt, injure;<BR>to offend, disturb, oppress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकार|विप्रकारः
वि-प्रकार, अस्, m. treating with disrespect, in-<BR>jury, offence; contumely, abuse; opposition, coun-<BR>teraction; retaliation; wickedness; various manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकारिन्
वि-प्रकारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, treating with contempt,<BR>opposing, opposed to, retaliating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृत|विप्रकृतः
वि-प्रकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, treated with disrespect<BR>or contempt, injured, offended, oppressed; reviled,<BR>abused; opposed, counteracted; retaliated, requited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृति|विप्रकृतिः
वि-प्रकृति, इस्, f. injury, offence; abuse, con-<BR>tumely; retort, retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्
विप्रकृष् वि-प्र-कृष्, cl. 1. P. -कर्षति,<BR>-कर्ष्टुम्, -क्रष्टुम्, to draw apart, draw away,<BR>draw out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकर्ष|विप्रकर्षः
वि-प्रकर्ष, अस्, m. distance, remoteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्ट|विप्रकृष्टः
वि-प्रकृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn or removed<BR>away, drawn out, extended, protracted, lengthened;<BR>remote, distant; carried away, carried off; (अम्),<BR>ind. far, far away.<BR>—विप्रकृष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. re-<BR>moteness, distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्टक|विप्रकृष्टकं
वि-प्रकृष्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, remote, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकॄ
विप्रकॄ वि-प्र-कॄ, cl. 6. P. -किरति, -करि-<BR>तुम् or -करीतुम्, to scatter or throw about, spread<BR>abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकीर्ण
वि-प्रकीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown about, scattered<BR>or spread abroad, dispersed; dishevelled, loose;<BR>dashed to pieces; outstretched, expanded, wide,<BR>broad.<BR>—विप्रकीर्ण-शिरोरुह, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>dishevelled or flowing hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रगम्
विप्रगम् वि-प्र-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to go apart or asunder, be dispersed or<BR>scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रचित्ति|विप्रचित्तिः
विप्रचित्ति विप्रचित्ति, इस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रचिन्त्
विप्रचिन्त् वि-प्र-चिन्त्, cl. 10. P. -चिन्तयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to meditate or reflect on, think about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रचिन्त्य
वि-प्रचिन्त्य, having reflected on, having thought<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रणश्
विप्रणश् वि-प्र-णश् (-नश्), cl. 1. 4. P. -ण-<BR>शति, -णश्यति, -नंष्टुम्, -नष्टुम् (see 2. प्र-<BR>णश्), to be lost, disappear; to have no effect or result,<BR>bear no fruit: Caus. -णाशयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>be lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रनष्ट
वि-प्रनष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (not वि-प्रणष्ट, see<BR>2. प्र-णश्; cf. Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 36), lost, disappeared,<BR>vanished; vain, fruitless.<BR>—विप्रनष्ट-विशेषक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has lost his discriminative faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकृ
विप्रतिकृ वि-प्रति-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c.,<BR>to counteract, oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकार|विप्रतिकारः
वि-प्रतिकार, अस्, m. counteraction, opposition,<BR>contradiction, reverse; retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकृत
वि-प्रतिकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, counteracted, opposed;<BR>requited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्
विप्रतिपद् वि-प्रति-पद्, cl. 4. A. -पद्यते,<BR>-पत्तुम्, to go in different or opposite directions, go<BR>hither and thither, turn here and there; to be per-<BR>plexed or confused, be uncertain how to act, waver;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">Page0928-c+ 73</a>]<BR>to differ, be of different opinions or interests, be<BR>mutually opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपत्ति|विप्रतिपत्तिः
वि-प्रतिपत्ति, इस्, f. going in different or opposite<BR>directions, perplexity, confusion; difference, opposition<BR>(of opinion or interests), mutual contrariety, dis-<BR>crepancy, contest, dispute, contradiction, conflict (of<BR>evidence), dissent, objection (in argument); various<BR>acquirement or acquisition, conversancy; mutual con-<BR>nection or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्य
वि-प्रतिपद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be mutually opposed<BR>or contradicted, to be contested; to be variously<BR>acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्यमान
वि-प्रतिपद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being disputed<BR>or contested; being in course of acquirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपन्न
वि-प्रतिपन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, gone in different or<BR>opposite directions, perplexed, confused, bewildered;<BR>mutually opposed, opposite, dissentient, being at<BR>variance; contradicted, disputed, contested; con-<BR>versant or acquainted with in various ways; mutually<BR>connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिभा
विप्रतिभा वि-प्रति-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति,<BR>-भातुम्, to appear as, seem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिषिद्ध|विप्रतिषिद्धं
विप्रतिषिद्ध वि-प्रतिषिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>rt. सिध् with प्रति and वि), contradicted, opposed,<BR>prohibited, forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिषेध|विप्रतिषेधः
वि-प्रतिषेध, अस्, m. a grammatical term im-<BR>plying that two different operations can be undertaken<BR>according to two different rules (the last mentioned<BR>being then generally regarded as operative पर-<BR>विप्रतिषेधेन, ‘by the prohibition of the other’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिसार|विप्रतिसारः
विप्रतिसार वि-प्रतिसार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सृ<BR>with प्रति and वि), repentance; evil, wickedness,<BR>evil action; hate, enmity, rage, wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतीसार|विप्रतीसारः
वि-प्रतीसार, अस्, m. = वि-प्रतिसार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतॄ
विप्रतॄ वि-प्र-तॄ, Caus. -तारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to impose upon, deceive, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतारित
वि-प्रतारित, अस्, आ, अम्, imposed upon, deceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रथ्
विप्रथ् वि-प्रथ्, cl. 1. A. -प्रथते (Ved.<BR>also P. -प्रथति), -प्रथितुम्, to spread out, extend<BR>(Ved. P.), to be widely extended, be expanded or<BR>spread abroad: Caus. -प्रथयति, -यितुम्, to spread<BR>out, extend, spread abroad, celebrate; to display,<BR>exhibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रथयत्
वि-प्रथयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, spreading abroad,<BR>diffusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रथित
वि-प्रथित, अस्, आ, अम्, spread out, spread abroad,<BR>widely diffused or extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदह|विप्रदहः
विप्रदह वि-प्र-दह, अस्, m. (probably fr. rt.<BR>1. दह् with प्र and वि), dried fruit or roots, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्ट
विप्रदुष्ट वि-प्रदुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (see rt. दुष्),<BR>very sensual or dissolute, spoiled, vitiated, defiled;<BR>corrupt, bad.<BR>—विप्रदुष्ट-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a very vicious or sensual disposition, vicious,<BR>sensual, corrupt, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुह्
विप्रदुह् वि-प्र-दुह्, cl. 2. P. -दोग्धि, -दोग्-<BR>धुम्, Ved. to receive, accept, take, (Sāy. विप्र-<BR>दुहन्ति = लभन्ते, Ṛg-veda IV. 24, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रधाव्
विप्रधाव् वि-प्र-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति,<BR>-ते, -धावितुम्, to run in different directions, disperse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रनष्ट
विप्रनष्ट वि-प्रनष्ट. See वि-प्र-णश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रबुध्
विप्रबुध् वि-प्र-बुध्, cl. 4. A., 1. P. -बुध्-<BR>यते, -बोधति, &c., to awake: Caus. -बोधयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to awaken, arouse; to admonish, advise,<BR>explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रबुद्ध
वि-प्रबुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, awakened, awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रबोधित
वि-प्रबोधित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), aroused,<BR>admonished, explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमत्त
विप्रमत्त वि-प्रमत्त (?), see Kathā-s. 34,<BR>255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुच्
विप्रमुच् वि-प्र-मुच्, cl. 6. P. A. -मुञ्चति,<BR>-ते, -मोक्तुम्, to loosen, unfasten, take off; to liberate,<BR>release, set free, deliver; to discharge, cast, hurl,<BR>shoot: Pass. -मुच्यते, to be liberated or released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0928-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुक्त
वि-प्रमुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, set free, loosed, loosened,<BR>let go, escaped, liberated; discharged, shot; free<BR>from, (गुण-व्˚, free from qualities.)<BR>—विप्रमुक्त-<BR>भय, अस्, आ, अम्, removed from danger, free from<BR>fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुच्य
वि-प्रमुच्य, ind. having taken off, having libe-<BR>rated or released, having discharged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमोच्य
वि-प्रमोच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be liberated or freed<BR>from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुह्
विप्रमुह् वि-प्र-मुह्, Caus. -मोहयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to bring into confusion or disorder, render<BR>confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमोहित
वि-प्रमोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, utterly bewildered, in-<BR>fatuated; fascinated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रया
विप्रया वि-प्र-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -यातुम्, to<BR>go asunder, run away in disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयाण|विप्रयाणं
वि-प्रयाण, अम्, n. going or flying away, flight,<BR>retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयात
वि-प्रयात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone apart or asunder,<BR>fled in all directions, run away in disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुज्
विप्रयुज् वि-प्र-युज्, cl. 7. P. A. -युनक्ति,<BR>-युङ्क्ते, -योक्तुम्, to disunite, separate, dissever,<BR>deprive of (with inst.): Pass. -युज्यते, to be dis-<BR>united, be separated from (with inst.): Caus. -योज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to disunite, cause to be separated from<BR>(with inst.), to deprive of, free from, release from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुक्त|विप्रयुक्तः
वि-प्रयुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, disjoined, disunited, sepa-<BR>rated, severed, divorced; separated from, freed from,<BR>released from (with inst. or at the end of a comp.,<BR>e. g. बन्धन-व्˚, freed from fetters); deprived of,<BR>without (e. g. मणि-व्˚, without jewels); absent from,<BR>away from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुज्य
वि-प्रयुज्य, ind. having separated, having de-<BR>prived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयोग|विप्रयोगः
वि-प्रयोग, अस्, m. disjunction, disunion, dissocia-<BR>tion, severance, separation, divorce, absence, the sepa-<BR>ration of lovers; separation from (with inst. and even<BR>with सह, e. g. प्रियैर् or प्रियैः सह विप्र-<BR>योगः, separation from loved objects); quarrel, disa-<BR>greement; the being fit or deserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयोजित
वि-प्रयोजित, अस्, आ, अम्, separated from, deprived<BR>of, freed or delivered from (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलप्
विप्रलप् वि-प्र-लप्, cl. 1. P. -लपति, -लपि-<BR>तुम्, to discourse or speak about variously, discuss;<BR>to talk idly, prate, prattle, wrangle; to complain,<BR>lament, bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलपित
वि-प्रलपित, अस्, आ, अम्, discussed, debated about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलप्त|विप्रलप्तं
वि-प्रलप्त, अम्, n. discussion, debate, disquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलाप|विप्रलापः
वि-प्रलाप, अस्, m. talking idly, prattling, prattle,<BR>unmeaning discourse, nonsense, mutual contradiction,<BR>wrangling, quarrelling, quarrel; infraction of a pro-<BR>mise or engagement, deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलभ्
विप्रलभ् वि-प्र-लभ्, cl. 1. A. -लभते (ep.<BR>also -लम्भते), -लब्धुम्, to overreach, deceive,<BR>cheat; to mock, insult, to disregard, violate; to<BR>receive back, regain, recover: Caus. -लम्भयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to mock, insult; to offend against, violate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्ध|विप्रलब्धः
वि-प्रलब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, cheated, deceived,<BR>tricked; hurt, injured; disappointed; (आ), f. a female<BR>disappointed by her lover's breaking his appointment,<BR>(one of the incidental characters in a drama.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्धृ
वि-प्रलब्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, deceiving; one<BR>who deceives, a deceiver, traitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भ|विप्रलंभ|विप्रलंभः|विप्रलम्भः
वि-प्रलम्भ, अस्, m. overreaching, deceiving,<BR>tricking, disappointing, deceiving by false assertions<BR>or by not keeping a promise, deception, deceit (in<BR>general); quarrel, disagreement; separation of lovers;<BR>disunion, disjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भक
वि-प्रलम्भक, अस्, इका, अम्, deceiving, a<BR>deceiver, fallacious.<BR>—विप्रलम्भ-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>deceptiveness, fallaciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भन|विप्रलंभनं
वि-प्रलम्भन, अम्, n. the act of overreaching<BR>or deceiving, deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भिन्
वि-प्रलम्भिन्, ई, इनी, इ, deceiving, deceptive<BR>fallacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रली
विप्रली वि-प्र-ली, cl. 4. A. -लीयते, &c., to<BR>dissolve away, become dissolved; to be dispersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलय|विप्रलयः
वि-प्रलय, अस्, m. dissolution, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलीन
वि-प्रलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, dispersed or scattered in<BR>all directions (said of a defeated army).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुड्
विप्रलुड् वि-प्र-लुड्, Caus. -लोडयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to stir about, agitate, disturb, throw into disorder or<BR>confusion, disorder, disarrange, spoil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलोडित
वि-प्रलोडित, अस्, आ, अम्, disarranged, spoiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुप्
विप्रलुप् वि-प्र-लुप्, cl. 6. P. A. -लुम्पति,<BR>-ते, -लोप्तुम्, to tear away, carry off, snatch away,<BR>rob, plunder; to break in upon, interrupt, disturb,<BR>confound: Pass. -लुप्यते, to be robbed or plundered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुप्त
वि-प्रलुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, snatched away, carried off,<BR>plundered; broken in upon, interrupted, disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुम्पक
वि-प्रलुम्पक, अस्, इका, अम्, rapacious, exacting,<BR>avaricious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुभ्
विप्रलुभ् वि-प्र-लुभ्, Caus. A. -लोभयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to allure, entice, try to lead astray or deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलू
विप्रलू वि-प्र-लू, cl. 9. P. A. -लुनाति, -लु-<BR>नीते, -लवितुम्, to cut off, sever, pluck, gather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलून
वि-प्रलून, अस्, आ, अम्, cut off, plucked off,<BR>gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवद्
विप्रवद् वि-प्र-वद्, cl. 1. P. A. -वदति, -व-<BR>दते, -वदितुम्, to speak variously, be at variance<BR>with one another, disagree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवस्
विप्रवस् वि-प्र-वस् (see rt. 6. वस्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-वसति, -वस्तुम्, to dwell at a distance, dwell abroad,<BR>be absent: Caus. -वासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>dwell away, banish, expel; to take away, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवसित
वि-प्रवसित, अस्, आ, अम्, withdrawn, departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवास|विप्रवासः
वि-प्रवास, अस्, m. dwelling at a distance, residence<BR>in a foreign country, staying abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासन|विप्रवासनं
वि-प्रवासन, अम्, n. banishment, expulsion;<BR>residence abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासित
वि-प्रवासित, अस्, आ, अम्, banished, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषित|विप्रोषितः
वि-प्रोषित, अस्, आ, अम् (वि-प्र-उषित), dwelling<BR>abroad, absent, away from; banished.<BR>—विप्रोषित-<BR>भर्तृका, f. a woman whose husband or lover is<BR>absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोष्य
वि-प्रोष्य, ind. having dwelt abroad, having been<BR>absent, returning after having been absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रव्यध्
विप्रव्यध् वि-प्र-व्यध्, cl. 4. P. -विध्यति,<BR>-व्यद्धुम्, to strike through, strike down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रविद्ध
वि-प्रविद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, struck through, struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रश्निका
विप्रश्निका वि-प्रश्निका, f. (fr. rt. प्रछ् with<BR>वि), a female fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रसृ
विप्रसृ वि-प्र-सृ, cl. 1. P. -सरति, &c., to<BR>spread, be expanded or extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रस्था
विप्रस्था वि-प्र-स्था, cl. 1. A. (sometimes<BR>P.) -तिष्ठते (-ति), -स्थातुम्, to go away, depart;<BR>to extend, be extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रहीण
विप्रहीण वि-प्रहीण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. हा<BR>with प्र and वि), deprived of, destitute of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रिय|विप्रियः
विप्रिय वि-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, unpleasant,<BR>disagreeable, disliked, distasteful, unbeloved; (अम्),<BR>n. offence, transgression.<BR>—विप्रिय-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>doing what is displeasing, acting unkindly, offensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुत
विप्रुत वि-प्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = वि-प्लुत,<BR>immersed, submerged; having torn or wounded<BR>limbs, (Sāy. = विश्लिष्टावयव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुष्
विप्रुष् वि-प्रुष्, ट्, f. (also written वि-प्लुष्,<BR>see rts. 1. प्रुष्, प्लुष्), a drop of water or other<BR>liquid; a spot, mark, dot.<BR>—विप्रुड्-ढोम, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. an expiatory offering designed to atone for the<BR>drops of Soma accidentally let fall at a sacrifice.<BR>—वि-<BR>प्रुष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, filled with drops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रे
विप्रे वि-प्रे (-प्र-इ), cl. 2. P. -प्रैति, -प्रै-<BR>तुम्, to go forth in different directions, depart in<BR>different ways; to be dispersed or scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रेत
वि-प्रेत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone forth, departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रेक्ष्
विप्रेक्ष् वि-प्रेक्ष् (-प्र-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-प्रेक्षते, -प्रेक्षितुम्, to look here and there,<BR>look on all sides; to regard, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषित|विप्रोषितः
विप्रोषित वि-प्रोषित, &c. See under वि-<BR>प्र-वस्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लु
विप्लु वि-प्लु, cl. 1. A. -प्लवते, -प्लोतुम्, to<BR>swim or float or drift in different directions, float<BR>about, fluctuate, be submerged; to be dispersed or<BR>scattered; to fall into disorder or confusion, become<BR>disarranged or confused; to be lost or ruined, to come<BR>to disgrace or dishonour: Caus. -प्लावयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to swim or float about, cause to drift hither<BR>and thither; to make known, spread abroad, make<BR>public, divulge; to bring to ruin or calamity; to<BR>perplex, confuse, confound, (in this sense the form<BR>वि-प्लवयति is found.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लव|विप्लवः
वि-प्लव, अस्, m. floating or drifting about or in<BR>different directions; confusion, perplexity, contra-<BR>riety, opposition, perversity; trouble, disaster, evil,<BR>calamity; sin, wickedness; the rust on a mirror<BR>(Kirāt. II. 26); tumult, rapine, extortion; predatory<BR>or devastating warfare, devastation; affray, scuffle,<BR>disturbance; terrifying an enemy by shouts and<BR>gestures; spreading abroad, divulging, (विप्लवं<BR>गम्, to become known.)<BR>—विप्लव-तस्, ind. in<BR>consequence of misfortune, by reason of disturbance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लवमान
वि-प्लवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, floating or drifting<BR>about, falling into disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लाव|विप्लावः
वि-प्लाव, अस्, m. causing tumult or disturbance,<BR>devastating; deluging, inundating; a horse's canter<BR>or gallop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लावित
वि-प्लावित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to drift or swim about,<BR>turned adrift, floated; spread abroad, divulged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लाव्य
वि-प्लाव्य, ind. having caused to swim or float<BR>about; having caused to be deluged or devastated,<BR>having confused or disturbed; having divulged, hav-<BR>ing made public or common, (applied in Manu XI.<BR>198. to the teaching of the Veda to improper persons<BR>or at improper seasons.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुत|विप्लुतः
वि-प्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, turned adrift, confounded,<BR>disturbed, fallen into confusion, scattered, dispersed;<BR>devastated, ravaged; ruined, disgraced, dishonoured,<BR>lost, disappeared; overwhelmed; drowned, deluged,<BR>bathed; obscured, dimmed, disfigured; depraved,<BR>wicked, abandoned, dissolute, addicted to evil prac-<BR>tices, guilty of lewdness or promiscuous intercourse;<BR>contrary, adverse, averse.<BR>—विप्लुत-नेत्र or वि-<BR>प्लुत-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, having eyes bathed or<BR>dimmed (with tears, joy, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुष्
विप्लुष् वि-प्लुष्, ट्, f. (also written वि-प्रुष्;<BR>see rts. प्लुष्, 1. प्रुष्), a drop of any fluid; a<BR>spot, dot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्सा
विप्सा विप्सा, f. = वीप्सा, repetition, suc-<BR>cession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफल्
विफल् वि-फल्, cl. 1. P. A. -फलति, -ते,<BR>-फलितुम्, to bear or produce fruit, become fruitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफल|विफलं
विफल वि-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, fruitless, use-<BR>less, ineffectual, unmeaning, vain, idle; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of plant or tree (= केतकी),<BR>—विफल-ता, f.<BR>or विफल-त्व, अम्, n. fruitlessness, unprofitableness.<BR>—विफल-प्रेरण, अस्, आ, अम्, flung in vain.<BR>—विफली-करण, अम्, n. frustrating, foiling, de-<BR>feating; doing anything in vain.<BR>—विफली-कृ, cl.<BR>8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to make fruit-<BR>less or useless, frustrate, foil.<BR>—विफली-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, rendered fruitless or ineffectual, frustrated; done<BR>in vain.<BR>—विफलीकृत-यत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, making<BR>fruitless efforts.<BR>—विफली-भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>becoming or become useless or unprofitable.<BR>—वि-<BR>फलीभविष्णु-ता, f. or विफलीभविष्णु-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. unprofitableness.<BR>—विफली-भू, cl. 1. P.<BR>-भवति, -भवितुम्, to become useless, be unprofit-<BR>able.<BR>—विफली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्ध्|विबंध्
विबन्ध् वि-बन्ध्, cl. 9. P. -बध्नाति, -बन्द्-<BR>धुम्, to bind or fasten on different sides, fasten on<BR>both sides, fasten; to stretch out, extend: Intens.<BR>-बाबधे, Ved. to lavish, bestow liberally, distribute,<BR>(according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 36, 5. वि-बाब-<BR>धे = वि-बध्नाति = ददाति; according to others<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">Page0930-a+ 78</a>]<BR>the form वि-बाबधे is assigned to वि-बाध्); to set<BR>free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0929-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबद्ध
वि-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound or fastened on different<BR>sides, fastened; entirely stopped, obstructed, consti-<BR>pated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबध्य
वि-बध्य, ind. having bound or fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्ध|विबंध|विबंधः|विबन्धः
वि-बन्ध, अस्, m. binding, obstruction, constipa-<BR>tion, ischury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्धन
वि-बन्धन, अम्, n. the act of fastening or bind-<BR>ing on both sides, (परस्पर-विबन्धन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, mutually bound, depending on each other.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाध्
विबाध् वि-बाध्, cl. 1. A. -बाधते, -बाधि-<BR>तुम्, to press or drive asunder or in different direc-<BR>tions; to press hard upon, drive away, chase away;<BR>to oppress, molest, harass, torment, persecute, pain,<BR>injure: Intens. वि-बाबधे (see under वि-बन्ध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाधा
वि-बाधा, f. pressure, pain, agony, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाल्य
विबाल्य वि-बाल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. passed<BR>beyond a state of youth, in full vigour; swollen (said<BR>of a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध्
विबुध् वि-बुध्, cl. 4. A. -बुध्यते, -बोद्-<BR>धुम्, to awake (intrans.), be awake or awakened;<BR>to become conscious, perceive, observe, learn, ascer-<BR>tain: Caus. -बोधयति, -यितुम्, to awaken; to<BR>cause to perceive or observe, make conscious, restore<BR>to consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुद्ध
1. वि-बुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, wide awake, awakened,<BR>aroused, awake, expanded, blossomed; clever, expe-<BR>rienced, knowing, skilful (e. g. कर्मसु विबुद्-<BR>धः, skilful in business).<BR>—विबुद्ध-कमल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having expanded lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुद्ध
2. वि-बुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, without consciousness,<BR>unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध|विबुधः
वि-बुध, अस्, m. a learned or wise man, teacher,<BR>Paṇḍit; a god, immortal; the moon; N. of the<BR>author of the Janma-pradīpa.<BR>—विबुध-प्रिया, f.<BR>‘favourite of the gods,’ N. of a metre.<BR>—विबुध-<BR>विजय, अस्, m. a victory (won) by the gods.<BR>—वि-<BR>बुध-विद्विष्, ट्, or विबुध-शत्रु, उस्, m. a foe<BR>of the gods; a demon.<BR>—विबुधाधिपति (˚ध-<BR>अध्˚), इस्, or विबुधेश्वर (˚ध-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>lord of the immortals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधान|विबुधानः
वि-बुधान, अस्, m. a wise man, teacher, pre-<BR>ceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध्य
वि-बुध्य, ind. having become conscious, having<BR>perceived or learnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोध|विबोधः
1. वि-बोध, अस्, m. awaking; perceiving, observ-<BR>ing, discovering; intelligence; (in the drama) the<BR>unfolding of the faculties, becoming conscious, awak-<BR>ing, (one of the Vyabhicāra-bhāvas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोध|विबोधः
2. वि-बोध, अस्, m. want of consciousness, inat-<BR>tention, absence of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोधन|विबोधनं
वि-बोधन, अम्, n. the act of awakening, awak-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोधित
वि-बोधित, अस्, आ, अम्, awakened, aroused; caused<BR>to perceive or know, instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्बोक|विब्बोकः
विब्बोक विब्बोक, अस्, m. (also written बिब्-<BR>बोक, विव्वोक, q. q. v. v.), (in erotic poetry) affec-<BR>tation of indifference to a beloved object through<BR>pride and conceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्रू
विब्रू वि-ब्रू, cl. 2. P. A. -ब्रवीति, -ब्रूते,<BR>&c. (see rt. ब्रू), to speak out, say, speak, utter;<BR>to speak in detail, particularize, interpret, explain,<BR>declare; to speak of or about (with acc.); to speak<BR>at variance; to say what is false, declare falsely, ex-<BR>plain falsely; to contradict, disagree with, be at vari-<BR>ance with; to dispute, contend about (Ved. A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्रुवत्
वि-ब्रुवत्, अन्, अती (ep. अन्ती), अत्, speaking out,<BR>speaking, saying, declaring, particularizing, interpret-<BR>ing; speaking falsely, saying what is untrue or<BR>unjust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्रुवाण
वि-ब्रुवाण, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking out, saying,<BR>declaring, uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्
विभज् वि-भज्, cl. 1. P. A. -भजति, -ते,<BR>-भक्तुम् (Ved. inf. -भाजम्), to divide, apportion,<BR>distribute, assign; to share together or with each other,<BR>participate in (A.); to take possession of; to separate,<BR>divide, part, cut; to honour, worship: Caus. -भाज-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">Page0930-b+ 79</a>]<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to distribute or divide or share,<BR>apportion: Pass. of Caus. -भाज्यते, to be caused<BR>to be divided, be apportioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्त|विभक्तः
वि-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, divided, portioned, par-<BR>titioned; parted, separated, distinct; different, multi-<BR>farious; retired, secluded, isolated; measured; regu-<BR>lar, symmetrical; ornamented; (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Kārttikeya; (अम्), n. solitude, separatedness;<BR>isolation.<BR>—विभक्त-ज, अस्, m. a son born after<BR>the partition of the family property between his<BR>parents and brethren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्ति|विभक्तिः
वि-भक्ति, इस्, f. a division, partition; part, portion,<BR>share of inheritance, &c.; (in grammar) inflection<BR>of nouns, declension, an affix of declension, case;<BR>(according to Pāṇini's system) a termination or in-<BR>flection either of a case or of the persons of a tense,<BR>(certain Taddhita affixes which are used like case-<BR>terminations have also the name वि-भक्ति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तृ
वि-भक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who distributes or<BR>dispenses, a dispenser, distributer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभजनीय|विभजनीयं
वि-भजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be apportioned or<BR>partitioned; to be divided, divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्य
वि-भज्य, ind. having divided or parted, having<BR>portioned or distributed, having allotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्यमान
वि-भज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being divided or<BR>parted; being apportioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाग|विभागः
वि-भाग, अस्, m. division, separation, disjunction,<BR>(one of the twenty-four Guṇas of the Nyāya); por-<BR>tion, part, share; the share or portion of an inherit-<BR>ance; partition of inheritance, law of inheritance, distri-<BR>bution, apportionment; arrangement; a section, (कूर्-<BR>म-व्˚, a section of a globe, hemisphere); the numerator<BR>of a fraction (in arithmetic).<BR>—विभाग-कल्पना, f.<BR>apportioning or allotment of shares or portions.<BR>—वि-<BR>भाग-तस्, ind. according to a part or share, pro-<BR>portionately.<BR>—विभाग-धर्म, अस्, m. the law of<BR>division, rule of inheritance.<BR>—विभाग-पत्त्रिका, f.<BR>a deed of partition.<BR>—विभाग-भाज्, क्, m. one who<BR>shares in a portion of property already distributed,<BR>(applied especially to a son by a father and mother<BR>of the same tribe, born subsequently to a distribution<BR>of property amongst his parents and brethren, in which<BR>case he inherits the portion allotted or reserved to<BR>the parents.)<BR>—विभाग-शस्, ind. according to a<BR>part or share, part by part, share by share, propor-<BR>tionately.<BR>—विभागेच्छु (˚ग-इच्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, wish-<BR>ing for a partition or distribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाजन|विभाजनं
वि-भाजन, अम्, n. the act of causing to share<BR>or distribute, participation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाजित
वि-भाजित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be divided, dis-<BR>tributed, apportioned, partitioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाज्य|विभाज्यं
वि-भाज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be divided or appor-<BR>tioned, portionable, divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाज्यमान
वि-भाज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being caused to be<BR>divided, being distributed or apportioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभञ्ज्|विभंज्
विभञ्ज् वि-भञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. -भनक्ति, -भङ्क्-<BR>तुम्, to break asunder, break to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभग्न
वि-भग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, broken asunder, broken to<BR>pieces, shattered, crushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्ग|विभंग|विभंगः|विभङ्गः
वि-भङ्ग, अस्, m. breaking, fracture; division;<BR>stopping, stoppage, obstruction; bending, contracting<BR>(especially of the eyebrows); expression or play of<BR>features.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्गिन्
विभङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wavy, undulating, wrinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभव|विभवः
विभव वि-भव, &c. See under 1. वि-भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा 1. वि-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति, -भातुम्,<BR>to shine or gleam forth; to shine brightly, glitter; to<BR>appear as, appear to be, seem; to come to light, be<BR>visible, appear; to lighten up, illuminate, brighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
2. वि-भा, f. light, lustre; a ray of light; beauty.<BR>—विभा-कर, अस्, m. ‘light-maker,’ the sun; fire;<BR>N. of a kind of plant or tree (= अर्क, चित्रक).<BR>—विभा-वस्, आन्, m. (a doubtful word), the sun (?).<BR>—विभा-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, abounding in light, (Sāy.<BR>दीप्ति-रोचन); (उस्), m. the sun, fire; the moon;<BR>a sort of necklace or garland; N. of a Gandharva<BR>(who is said to have stolen the Soma from Gāyatrī<BR>as she was carrying it to the gods).<BR>—विभा-साह्, ट्,<BR>ट्, ट्, Ved. splendor-surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभात्
वि-भात्, आन्, आती, or आन्ती, आत्, shining, splendid;<BR>(आती), f. epithet of the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभात|विभातं
वि-भात, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, bright, luminous;<BR>(अम्), n. dawn, day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावन्
विभा-वन्, वा, वरी, व, Ved. radiant, shining,<BR>resplendent, illuminating, (in Ṛg-veda X. 8, 4. वि-<BR>भावा is by some translated ‘the divider,’ as if from<BR>वि-भू); (वरी), f. the dawn (= उषस्, Naigh. I.<BR>8); night, (in this sense वि is probably privative);<BR>turmeric; a harlot, bawd; the shreds of a garment<BR>torn in a scuffle (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाण्डक|विभाण्डकः
विभाण्डक विभाण्डक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>hermit; of a Muni (son of Kaśyapa and father of<BR>Ṛṣya-śṛṅga).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाण्डी
वि-भाण्डी, f. a kind of creeping plant (= आ-वर्-<BR>तकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव|विभावः
विभाव वि-भाव. See p. 931, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाष्
विभाष् वि-भाष्, cl. 1. A. -भाषते, -भा-<BR>षितुम्, to speak variously; to speak against, revile,<BR>abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाषा
वि-भाषा, f. an alternative, option, one of two<BR>ways; (in grammar) the allowing a rule to be<BR>optional, (it is of two kinds, viz. 1. प्राप्त-व्˚ or<BR>प्राप्ते व्˚, an option allowed in a particular opera-<BR>tion which another rule makes necessary; 2. अप्राप्-<BR>त-व्˚ or अप्राप्ते व्˚, an option allowed in a particu-<BR>lar operation which another rule makes impossible.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाषित
वि-भाषित, अस्, आ, अम्, made optional (in gram-<BR>mar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाष्य
वि-भाष्य, ind. having reviled or abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभास्
विभास् वि-भास्, cl. 1. A. (Ved. also P.)<BR>-भासते (-भासति), -भासितुम्, to shine brightly<BR>or pleasantly, be bright: Caus. -भासयति, &c., to<BR>cause to shine, illuminate, brighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासा
वि-भासा, f. shining brightly, light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासित
वि-भासित, अस्, आ, अम्, made bright, lighted, illu-<BR>minated, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिद्
विभिद् वि-भिद्, cl. 7. P. A. -भिनत्ति,<BR>-भिन्त्ते, -भेत्तुम्, to split or break in two, break<BR>in pieces, cleave apart or asunder, cleave, divide,<BR>separate, pierce, open; to loosen, untie; to scatter,<BR>disperse, dispel, drive away, destroy; to disunite,<BR>cause disunion, set at variance, estrange: Pass. -भिद्-<BR>यते, to burst asunder; to become disunited; to be<BR>set at variance, be estranged or alienated; to change,<BR>become changed: Caus. -भेदयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>divide; to alienate, estrange; to dispel, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबिभित्सु
वि-बिभित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to break asunder,<BR>purposing to cleave or pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिद्य
वि-भिद्य, ind. having split in two, having cut<BR>asunder, having cleaved; having divided or separated,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिद्यमान
वि-भिद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being broken or<BR>split asunder; being divided or scattered; being<BR>pierced or wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्दु
वि-भिन्दु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. splitting or cleaving<BR>asunder, dissevering, shattering; (उस्), m., Ved. a<BR>proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्न|विभिन्नः
वि-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, broken or split asunder,<BR>divided, pierced, broken, wounded; scattered, dis-<BR>persed, dispelled, destroyed; bewildered estranged,<BR>alienated, perplexed, deceived; moved to and fro;<BR>disappointed; become faithless; various, different;<BR>mixed, intermixed, mingling (with inst.); (अस्), m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—विभिन्न-तमिस्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the darkness dispelled.<BR>—विभिन्न-ता, f. or<BR>विभिन्न-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being broken or<BR>split asunder; the state of being scattered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेत्तृ
वि-भेत्तृ, ता, m. one who splits or breaks asun-<BR>der, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेद|विभेदः
वि-भेद, अस्, m. breaking asunder, dividing,<BR>breaking, division, separation; piercing, wounding;<BR>violating; bewildering, perplexing, confusing; con-<BR>tradiction; enmity, opposition; variety, distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेदन
वि-भेदन, अम्, n. the act of splitting or cleaving<BR>asunder; breaking, dividing; separating, setting at<BR>variance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0930-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभी
विभी 1. वि-भी, cl. 3. P. -बिभेति, &c., to<BR>be afraid of, fear: Caus. -भीषयति, &c., to<BR>frighten, terrify, intimidate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभी
2. वि-भी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, free from fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीत|विभीतं|विभीतः
वि-भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, fearless; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n.<BR>the plant Terminalia Belerica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतक|विभीतकं|विभीतकः
विभीतक, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. the tree Termi-<BR>nalia Belerica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषक
वि-भीषक, अस्, इका, अम्, frightening, terrifying,<BR>intimidating, threatening, bullying; (इका), f. the act<BR>of terrifying, terror; a means of terrifying.<BR>—विभी-<BR>षिका-स्थान, अम्, n. an object or means of terri-<BR>fying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषण|विभीषणः
वि-भीषण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, terrifying, intimi-<BR>dating, terrific, fearful, terrible, formidable, horrible;<BR>bullying or blustering (as language); (अम्, आ), n. f.<BR>the act of terrifying, the property of exciting fear, a<BR>means of terrifying, terror; (अस्), m., N. of a brother<BR>of Rāvaṇa, (his other brothers were Kuvera [by a<BR>different mother] and Kumbha-karṇa; both Rāvaṇa<BR>and Vibhīṣaṇa are said to have propitiated Brahmā<BR>by their penances, so that the god granted them<BR>both boons, and the boon chosen by Vibhīṣaṇa<BR>was that he should never, even in the greatest cala-<BR>mity, stoop to any mean or wicked action; hence<BR>he is represented in the Rāmāyaṇa as opposing and<BR>endeavouring to counteract the malice of his brother<BR>Rāvaṇa, in consequence of which he was so ill-<BR>treated and insulted by Rāvaṇa that, leaving Laṅkā,<BR>he joined the side of Rāma, by whom, after the<BR>death of Rāvaṇa, Vibhīṣaṇa was placed on the<BR>throne of Laṅkā); N. of several kings, (in later<BR>times Vibhīṣaṇa appears to have been used as a<BR>general name of the kings of Laṅkā.)<BR>—विभीषण-<BR>वाक्य, अम्, n. ‘speech of Vibhīṣaṇa,’ N. of several<BR>chapters in the Sundara-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—विभीषणाभिषेक (˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘inau-<BR>guration of Vibhīṣaṇa,’ N. of the ninety-first chapter<BR>of the Sundara-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa (according<BR>to one recension).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषयत्
वि-भीषयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, terrifying, causing<BR>terror or alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीदक
विभीदक विभीदक, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>tree (from the nuts of which dice are made; cf.<BR>वि-भीतक); dice, gambling, (Sāy. = अक्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुग्न
विभुग्न वि-भुग्न, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 1. भुज्),<BR>bent, bowed, crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभू
विभू 1. वि-भू, cl. 1. P. A. -भवति, -ते,<BR>-भवितुम्, to arise, be produced, become developed,<BR>be manifested, expand, appear; to pervade; to be<BR>equal to, suffice for; to prevail, have power, be<BR>capable of, be able to (with inf.): Caus. -भावयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to arise, cause to be developed or<BR>expand, make manifest, develop, cause to appear<BR>clearly, manifest, reveal, show forth, display; to<BR>cause to be apart, separate; to perceive distinctly,<BR>find out, trace out, discover, ascertain, detect, ob-<BR>serve, know, feel; to recognise; to suppose, fancy,<BR>imagine; to suppose anything (acc.) of or about<BR>any one (loc.); to think about, reflect upon; to<BR>make clear, establish, prove, decide; to convict, con-<BR>vince: Pass. of Caus. -भाव्यते, to be considered<BR>or regarded as, to appear, seem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोभुवत्
वि-बोभुवत्, अत्, अती, अत् (fr. the Intens.), Ved.<BR>spreading in every direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभव|विभवः
वि-भव, अस्, m. power, might, supreme power,<BR>superhuman power; substance, thing, property,<BR>wealth; magnanimity, lofty-mindedness; emanci-<BR>pation from existence; N. of the thirty-sixth year<BR>of Jupiter's cycle.<BR>—विभव-तस्, ind. according to<BR>power, according to dignity or majesty; in regal state<BR>or ceremony.<BR>—विभव-मद, अस्, m. the pride<BR>of power.<BR>—विभव-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of<BR>power, wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभवत्|विभवन्त्
वि-भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, pervading, prevailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव|विभावः
वि-भाव, अस्, m. any condition which excites or<BR>develops a particular state of mind or body, (in<BR>dramatic composition one of the three divisions of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">Page0931-b+ 80</a>]<BR>Bhāvas, the other two being Anu-bhāvas and Sāt-<BR>tvika-bhāvas, see भाव); any causative or exciting<BR>property (as dress, perfumes, &c. causing amorous<BR>desire, extravagant gesture causing mirth, distress<BR>causing tenderness, arms and tumult causing wrath<BR>or heroism); a friend, acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावक
वि-भावक, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to appear clearly,<BR>manifesting, showing, illustrating; discussing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावन|विभावनं
वि-भावन, अम्, आ, n. f. the causing to appear<BR>distinctly, clear perception, distinguishing or perceiv-<BR>ing distinctly, conception, imagination, examination,<BR>discrimination, judgment, clear ascertainment; dis-<BR>cussion; (in rhetoric) description of effects not<BR>arising from the usual causes, peculiar causation; or,<BR>according to some, description by negatives, bring-<BR>ing out the qualities of any object more clearly than<BR>by positive description.<BR>—विभावनालङ्कार (˚ना-<BR>अल्˚), अस्, m. (in rhetoric) the rhetorical figure de-<BR>scribed above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावनीय
वि-भावनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, distinguishable, ascer-<BR>tainable, to be judged or determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावित|विभावितः
वि-भावित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to appear clearly,<BR>manifested; proved, established; judged, discrimi-<BR>nated; perceived, ascertained, seen, conceived, known,<BR>understood, convicted, convinced.<BR>—विभावित-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the state of being perceived or judged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाविन्
विभाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, filled with amorous sentiments,<BR>exciting emotion of love, (see वि-भाव, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव्य
वि-भाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, distinguishable, to be<BR>clearly perceived or seen or observed; remarkable;<BR>to be conceived or imagined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभु|विभुः
वि-भु, उस्, उस्, or वी, उ (in Ved. the fem. is<BR>always विभ्वी, Pāṇ. IV. 1, 47), being everywhere,<BR>pervading all material things, developing in all direc-<BR>tions, omnipresent, eternal (Ved.); mighty, very<BR>powerful or great, excellent, eminent, supreme; ca-<BR>pable, able to (with inf., e. g. पूरयितुं विभुः,<BR>able to fill); firm, solid, hard; (उस्), m. (Ved. acc.<BR>विभ्वम्, Ved. nom. pl. विभ्वस्), ether; space;<BR>time; the soul; a lord, ruler, sovereign, master,<BR>owner (often used in addressing a superior); N. of<BR>Brahmā; of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of a son of Bhṛgu;<BR>a servant.<BR>—विभु-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. mighty<BR>in action, effecting much, (Sāy. = बहु-कर्मन्.)<BR>—विभु-ता, f. or विभु-त्व, अम्, n. might, power,<BR>capacity, supremacy.<BR>—विभु-प्रमित, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>the hall of Brahmā.<BR>—विभु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. mighty, powerful.<BR>—विभू-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ<BR>(for विभु-वसु), Ved. having mighty treasures or<BR>wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभू
2. वि-भू, ऊस्, &c., Ved. expanding, pervading,<BR>epithet of a particular Prāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूत
वि-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, arisen, produced, developed,<BR>manifested, appeared, displayed; great, mighty.<BR>—विभूत-द्युम्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. abounding<BR>in glory or in food, (Sāy. = प्रभूत-यशस् or<BR>प्रभूतान्न.)<BR>—विभूत-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. mak-<BR>ing great gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूति|विभूतिः
वि-भूति, इस्, m. great power, might, dominion,<BR>supremacy, dignity; great success, prosperity, wel-<BR>fare; superhuman power (consisting of eight facul-<BR>ties, especially attributed to Śiva, but supposed also<BR>to be attainable by human beings through a course<BR>of austere worship in honour of that deity, viz. अणि-<BR>मन्, the power of becoming as minute as an atom;<BR>लघिमन्, extreme lightness; प्राप्ति, the power<BR>of attaining or reaching anything, as illustrated by<BR>the power of touching the moon with the tip of<BR>the finger; प्राकाम्य, irresistible will; महिमन्,<BR>illimitable bulk; ईशिता, supreme dominion; वशिता,<BR>the power of subjugating by magic; and कामाव-<BR>सायिता, the power of suppressing all desires); the<BR>ashes of cow-dung &c. (with which Śiva is said to<BR>smear his body, and hence used in imitation of him<BR>by devotees); (इस्, इस्, इ), Ved. very powerful, mighty.<BR>—विभूति-द्वादशी, f., N. of a particular Vrata or<BR>religious observance.<BR>—विभूति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>powerful, possessed of excellence or dignity, super-<BR>human; smeared with ashes.<BR>—विभूति-योग, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the sixth canto of the Śiva-gītā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्वन्
वि-भ्वन्, आ, &c., Ved. displayed, developed, dif-<BR>fused; great, mighty; (आ), m., N. of a son of<BR>Su-dhanvan (brother of Ṛbhu, q. v., regarded as<BR>one of the three Ṛbhus).<BR>—विभ्व-तष्ट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. cut out or fashioned by Vibhvan (said of<BR>the rivers which were supposed to be carved out by<BR>him, as the artificer of Varuṇa); modelled by Vi-<BR>bhvan, very perfect or handsome (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda V. 58, 4).<BR>—विभ्वा-सह् (विभ्वा for<BR>विभ्व), Ved. conquering or overcoming the mighty,<BR>(Sāy. = महतो-ऽभिभवितृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूष्
विभूष् वि-भूष्, cl. 1. 10. P. -भूषति,<BR>-भूषयति, -भूषितुम्, -भूषयितुम्, to deco-<BR>rate, adorn; to shine forth, appear, (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 112, 4. विभूषति may = व्य्-<BR>आप्तो भवति, the rt. भूष् being sometimes used<BR>in the Veda as another form of rt. 1. भू, in the<BR>sense of ‘to obtain, attain.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषण|विभूषणं
वि-भूषण, अम्, n. decoration, ornament.<BR>—वि-<BR>भूषणोद्भासिन् (˚ण-उद्˚), ई, इनी, इ, glittering<BR>with ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषा
वि-भूषा, f. ornament, decoration; light, lustre,<BR>splendor, beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषित|विभूषितः
वि-भूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned, decorated, orna-<BR>mented.<BR>—विभूषिताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>decorated about the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषिन्
वि-भूषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, adorning, decorating;<BR>adorned, decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूष्य
वि-भूष्य, ind. having adorned or decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृ
विभृ वि-भृ, cl. 1. P. A. -भरति, -ते, cl.<BR>3. P. A. -बिभर्ति, -बिभृते, &c., -भर्तुम्, to<BR>support; to bear or carry in different directions,<BR>spread out; to distribute, diffuse (A.): Intens. (for<BR>Intensive forms see under rt. भृ), to move to and<BR>fro, wave about, brandish, toss about; to roam or<BR>sport about, (according to Sāy. in this sense for<BR>वि-हृ; cf. वि-भृत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृत|विभृतः
वि-भृत, अस्, आ, अम्, upheld, supported, main-<BR>tained, held, retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृत्र
वि-भृत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. borne in various direc-<BR>tions, (Sāy. = नाना-स्थानेषु विहृत); employed<BR>in various sacred rites, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 71, 3. वि-भृत्राः = अग्नि-होत्रादि-कर्मणि<BR>विहरन्त्यः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृत्वन्
वि-भृत्वन्, आ, m., Ved. one who bears or sup-<BR>ports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंश्
विभ्रंश् वि-भ्रंश् (sometimes written वि-<BR>भ्रंस्), cl. 4. P., 1. A. -भ्रश्यति, -भ्रंशते,<BR>-भ्रंशितुम्, to fall down, fall, go to ruin, decay;<BR>to fall away, fall off; to disappear, vanish; to be<BR>unfortunate, fail; to fall away from, stray from, be<BR>separated from (with abl.); to be deprived of, lose:<BR>Caus. -भ्रंशयति, -यितुम्, to cause to fall off,<BR>strike or knock off, break off, to cause to fall, lead<BR>astray, seduce; to cause to disappear or vanish,<BR>destroy, annihilate, ruin; to divert from (with abl.),<BR>deprive of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंश|विभ्रंशः
वि-भ्रंश, अस्, m. falling away, &c.; a precipice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंशित
वि-भ्रंशित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), caused<BR>to fall away; struck off, broken off; led astray,<BR>seduced; made to disappear, destroyed; deprived of.<BR>—विभ्रंशित-ज्ञान, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of<BR>reason or consciousness.<BR>—विभ्रंशित-पुष्प-<BR>पत्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having the flowers and leaves<BR>knocked off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंशिन्
वि-भ्रंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling away, falling off;<BR>dropping, falling, fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रष्ट
वि-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen away or off, broken<BR>off or from, separated from, gone astray; fallen, de-<BR>cayed, failed, ruined, lost, disappeared, vanished.<BR>—विभ्रष्ट-तिमिर, अस्, आ, अम्, whose darkness<BR>has vanished or disappeared (said of the sky).<BR>—वि-<BR>भ्रष्ट-हर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from or deprived<BR>of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रम्
विभ्रम् वि-भ्रम्, cl. 1. 4. P. -भ्रमति,<BR>-भ्राम्यति, -भ्रमितुम्, to wander or roam about,<BR>roam through or over; to flit or hover about; to move<BR>to and fro, roll about; to disperse, scatter, scare or<BR>frighten away; to fall into disorder or confusion,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">Page0932-a+ 76</a>]<BR>become disarranged or bewildered: Caus. -भ्रम-<BR>यति, -भ्रामयति, -यितुम्, to confuse, perplex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0931-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रम|विभ्रमः
वि-भ्रम, अस्, m. roaming or wandering about,<BR>whirling round, whirling or rolling about, going<BR>round, any whirling motion; error, mistake, blunder,<BR>erroneous use or application; hurry, confusion, agita-<BR>tion, perturbation, flurry (one of the classes of femi-<BR>nine action proceeding from love, as when a woman<BR>through flurry puts on her ornaments in the wrong<BR>places); amorous action of any kind; caprice, whim;<BR>beauty, grace; play (of the eyes); rapture; doubt,<BR>apprehension; (आ), f. old age.<BR>—विभ्रम-तन्त्र<BR>or विभ्रम-सूत्र, N. of a treatise on grammar<BR>(attributed to Hema-candra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रमत्
वि-भ्रमत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, roaming about, roaming<BR>through, whirling round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रमित्वा
वि-भ्रमित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having whirled<BR>or frightened away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्त|विभ्रांत|विभ्रान्तः
वि-भ्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, whirled about, agitated,<BR>bewildered, hurried, flurried, confused (through pre-<BR>cipitation &c.).<BR>—विभ्रान्त-नयन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having rolling eyes.<BR>—विभ्रान्त-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>bewildered or confused in mind.<BR>—विभ्रान्त-शील,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, confused in mind or disposition; drunk,<BR>intoxicated, insane; (अस्), m. a monkey; the disk of<BR>the sun or moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्ति|विभ्रांति|विभ्रांतिः|विभ्रान्तिः
वि-भ्रान्ति, इस्, f. whirling round, going round,<BR>error, confusion; hurry, flurry, precipitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज् 1. वि-भ्राज्, cl. 1. A. -भ्राजते, -भ्रा-<BR>जितुम् (Ved. inf. विभ्राजम्), to shine forth, shine,<BR>glitter, gleam, be bright or radiant; to shine through:<BR>Caus. -भ्राजयति, -यितुम्, to cause to radiate or<BR>beam or shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
2. वि-भ्राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, shining, splendid, luminous;<BR>elegant, richly dressed or decorated; (ट्), m., N. of<BR>the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 170 (having<BR>the patronymic Saurya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राजत्
वि-भ्राजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shining, glittering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राजमान
वि-भ्राजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, resplendent, glittering,<BR>shining, dazzling, radiant, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राजित
वि-भ्राजित, अस्, आ, अम्, made splendid or bright,<BR>caused to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राष्टि
वि-भ्राष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. radiance, flame, blaze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्वन्
विभ्वन् वि-भ्वन्. See p. 931, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमंह्
विमंह् वि-मंह्, cl. 1. A. -मंहते, &c., Ved.<BR>to distribute, bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमंहमान
वि-मंहमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. distributing,<BR>giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमज्ज्
विमज्ज् वि-मज्ज्, cl. 6. P. -मज्जति, &c., to<BR>plunge or dive in, enter into, (probably wrongly for<BR>नि-मज्ज्): Caus. -मज्जयति, &c., to submerge,<BR>cause to plunge into or enter in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत|विमतः
विमत वि-मत, वि-मति. See under वि-मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्सर
विमत्सर वि-मत्सर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>envy or jealousy, unenvious, unambitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमथ्
विमथ् वि-मथ् or वि-मन्थ्, cl. 1. 9. P. -म-<BR>थति, -मन्थति, -मथ्नाति (Ved. generally A.<BR>-मथ्नीते), &c., -मथितुम्, -मन्थितुम्, to crush<BR>or dash to pieces, rend asunder, bruise (Ved. A.); to<BR>cut to pieces, annihilate, destroy, disperse, scatter; to<BR>confuse, perplex, bewilder, embarrass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमथित
वि-मथित, अस्, आ, अम्, crushed or dashed to<BR>pieces, rent asunder, bruised, destroyed, annihilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमथ्नत्
वि-मथ्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, dashing to pieces, crush-<BR>ing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमथ्य
वि-मथ्य, ind. having crushed completely, having<BR>destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमाथ|विमाथः
वि-माथ, अस्, m. the act of crushing or destroy-<BR>ing utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमाथिन्
वि-माथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crushing or dashing to pieces,<BR>destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद्
विमद् वि-मद्, cl. 4. P. -माद्यति (Ved. also<BR>-मदति), &c., -मदितुम्, to become perplexed or<BR>confused, be disconcerted; to confound, embarrass,<BR>disturb: Caus. -मादयति, &c., -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>be perplexed, to confuse, embarrass; to intoxicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्त
वि-मत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, intoxicated; being in rut,<BR>ruttish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद
वि-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, free from intoxication;<BR>joyless; (अस्), m., N. of the author of the hymns<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 20-26 (having the patronymic Aindra<BR>or Prājāpatya; Vasu-kṛt Vāsukra is also regarded<BR>as the author of these hymns).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमदित
वि-मदित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), = वि-मत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमध्य
विमध्य वि-मध्य, Ved. an unfathomable<BR>depth, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 51, 3. explains तमसो<BR>विमध्ये by अत्यन्त-गाढान्धकारे, ‘in un-<BR>fathomable darkness.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्
विमन् वि-मन्, cl. 8. 4. A., 1. P. -मनुते,<BR>-मन्यते, -मनति, &c., -मन्तुम्, to distinguish<BR>(?, Ved.); to dishonour, offend: Caus. -मानयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to dishonour, slight, treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत|विमतः
वि-मत, अस्, आ, अम्, disagreed, disagreeing, dis-<BR>senting, disapproving; at variance, inconsistent, averse,<BR>hostile to; slighted, despised, offended, displeased; of<BR>a different mind or disposition; (अस्), m. an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमति|विमतिः
वि-मति, इस्, f. difference of mind or opinion,<BR>dissent, disagreement; dislike, aversion; stupidity.<BR>—विमति-ता, f. difference of opinion, want of mind,<BR>stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमान|विमानं|विमानः
1. वि-मान, अस्, अम्, m. n. (for 2. see under 2.<BR>वि-मा), disrespect, dishonour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानना
वि-मानना, f. dishonour, disrespect, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानित
वि-मानित, अस्, आ, अम्, dishonoured, slighted,<BR>treated with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्
विमनस् वि-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, changed in<BR>mind or feeling; averse, displeased; out of one's<BR>mind, distraught, depressed in mind or spirit, sad,<BR>distressed, discomposed; heart-broken; absent in<BR>mind, thinking of something else; perplexed, dis-<BR>ordered, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्क|विमनस्कः
वि-मनस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, out of one's mind, de-<BR>pressed in spirit, heart-broken, sad, melancholy, be-<BR>wildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीकृत
विमनी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, altered in mind or<BR>feeling; displeased, offended; depressed in mind,<BR>sad, sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीभूत
विमनी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become changed in<BR>mind or feeling; brought into a melancholy frame<BR>of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्थ्|विमंथ्
विमन्थ् वि-मन्थ्. See वि-मथ्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्यु
विमन्यु वि-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, free from anger<BR>or passion, free from grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमय|विमयः
विमय वि-मय, अस्, m. (see rt. मे), change,<BR>exchange, barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द|विमर्दः|विमर्द्द|विमर्द्दः
विमर्द वि-मर्द, &c. See under वि-मृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्श|विमर्शः
विमर्श वि-मर्श, &c. See under वि-मृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्ष|विमर्षः
विमर्ष वि-मर्ष, &c. See under वि-मृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमल|विमलं|विमलः
विमल वि-मल, अस्, आ, अम्, stainless, free<BR>from dirt or impurity, spotless, pure, clean; white,<BR>transparent, beautiful; (अस्), m. an Arhat or Jaina<BR>deified sage; N. of the father of Padma-pāda; of a<BR>son of Su-dyumna; (आ), f. a particular plant, = सप्तला,<BR>(commonly called Charmaghās); a sort of soil; N.<BR>of Dākṣāyaṇī; (अम्), n. silver gilt; talc.<BR>—विमल-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—विमल-ता,<BR>f. or विमल-त्व, अम्, n. stainlessness, cleanliness,<BR>purity, clearness.<BR>—विमल-दान, अम्, n. a gift or<BR>offering to a deity.<BR>—विमल-नाथ-पुराण, N. of<BR>a Jaina work by Kṛṣṇa-dāsa.<BR>—विमल-प्रभा, f.,<BR>N. of one of the wives of Narendrāditya.<BR>—विमल-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. ‘clear-gem,’ crystal.<BR>—विमलात्मक<BR>(˚ल-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pure-minded, clean, pure.<BR>—वि-<BR>मलात्मन् (˚ल-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, pure-souled, unde-<BR>filed, pure.<BR>—विमलादित्य (˚ल-आद्˚), अस्, m. ‘clear-<BR>sun,’ a particular form of the sun.<BR>—विमलाद्रि (˚ल-<BR>अद्˚), इस्, m. ‘pure mountain,’ N. of the mountain<BR>Vimala or Girnar in Gujarāt, (this mountain is cele-<BR>brated for its inscriptions; it is also called Śatruñ-jaya,<BR>q. v.)<BR>—विमलार्थक (˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of pure<BR>purpose, pure-minded; pure, clean, clear.<BR>—विम-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">Page0932-c+ 73</a>]<BR>लाश्व (˚ल-अश्˚), N. of a country in Kaśmīra.<BR>—विमली-<BR>करण, अम्, n. the act of making pure.<BR>—विमली-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make clean or pure.<BR>—विमलेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚ल-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>chapter in the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलोग्यतन्त्र
विमलोग्य-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमस्तकित
विमस्तकित वि-मस्तकित, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>headed, decapitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमहत्|विमहन्त्
विमहत् वि-महत्, आन्, अती, अत्, very great,<BR>immense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमहस्
वि-महस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. of various or excellent<BR>might or splendor, very vigorous, very brilliant or<BR>resplendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमहि
वि-महि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. very large or great, (Sāy. =<BR>विशेषेण महत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमा
विमा 1. वि-मा, cl. 3. A. -मिमीते, &c. (see rt.<BR>2. मा), Ved. to bellow, roar, cry (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमा
विमा 2. वि-मा (see rt. 3. मा), cl. 2. P., 3. 4.<BR>A. -माति, -मिमीते, -मायते, -मातुम्, (Ved.) to<BR>measure out, to traverse, pass over (a course); (Ved.)<BR>to set in order, set right, prepare; to count, count<BR>over; to measure; to pervade; to make in various<BR>ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमान|विमानं|विमानः
2. वि-मान, अस्, अम्, m. n. (for 1. वि-मान see<BR>under वि-मन्), a measure; a car or chariot of the<BR>gods (sometimes serving as a seat or throne, sometimes<BR>self-moving and carrying its occupant through the<BR>skies; other descriptions make the Vimāna more like<BR>a house or palace, and one kind is said to be seven<BR>stories high; that of Rāvaṇa was called पुष्पक,<BR>q. v.); any car or vehicle; a horse; a palace, the<BR>palace of an emperor or supreme monarch.<BR>—विमान-<BR>गमन, अम्, n. ‘going in a car,’ N. of the fifty-<BR>second chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—विमान-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, travelling in a<BR>celestial car.<BR>—विमान-ता, f. the state or condition<BR>of a chariot.<BR>—विमान-प्रभुता, f. the ownership<BR>or possession of a celestial chariot.<BR>—विमान-यान,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, going or driving in a car.<BR>—विमान-राज,<BR>अस्, m. the driver of a chariot of the gods.<BR>—विमान-<BR>वत्, ind. like a self-moving car, (Kirāt. VII. 4.)<BR>—वि-<BR>मान-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing on a divine chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिमान
वि-मिमान, अस्, आ, अम्, measuring out, preparing,<BR>making; measured, conceived, (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 155, 6 = विविधम् मिमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमांस|विमांसं|विमांसः
विमांस वि-मांस, अस्, अम्, m. n. unclean<BR>meat (as the flesh of dogs &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृ
विमातृ वि-मातृ, ता, f. a stepmother, a fa-<BR>ther's wife.<BR>—विमातृ-ज, अस्, m. a stepmother's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानना
विमानना वि-मानना, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमाय
विमाय वि-माय, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of magic,<BR>free from illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्ग|विमार्गः
विमार्ग वि-मार्ग, अस्, m. a bad road, by-<BR>road; a wrong road (literally or figuratively); evil<BR>conduct, immorality; a broom, brush; [cf. rt. मार्ग्.]<BR>—विमार्ग-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going in a wrong<BR>road, following an evil course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गण|विमार्गणं
वि-मार्गण, अम्, n. the act of searching or seek-<BR>ing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमि
विमि वि-मि (see rt. 1. मि), cl. 5. P. A. -मि-<BR>नोति, -मिनुते, -मातुम्, Ved. to fix, build, erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमित
वि-मित, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed, built; (अम्), n., Ved. a<BR>square shed or large building resting on four posts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिन्वत्
वि-मिन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, fixing; (Sāy.) separating<BR>and fixing (= परि-च्छिन्दत् स्थापयत्, Ṛg-veda<BR>IV. 56. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्र्
विमिश्र् वि-मिश्र्, cl. 10. P. -मिश्रयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to mix or mingle together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्र
वि-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed or mingled together,<BR>commingled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्रित
वि-मिश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed together, mingled;<BR>mixed with, attended or accompanied by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्त|विमुक्तः
विमुक्त वि-मुक्त, &c. See under 1. वि-मुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0932-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुख|विमुखः
विमुख वि-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having the face<BR>turned away or cast down, averted; disinclined, op-<BR>posed.<BR>—विमुख-ता, f. or विमुख-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of having the face averted, turning away; dis-<BR>inclination, opposition; disappearance, departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखिन्
विमुखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having the face averted, turned<BR>away; averse from, hostile.<BR>—विमुखि-ता, f. or वि-<BR>मुखि-त्व, अम्, n. a state of aversion, enmity;<BR>opposition; departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखीकृ
विमुखी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make the face averted, turn away the face,<BR>turn away from, leave.<BR>—विमुखी-करण, अम्, n.<BR>the act of turning away or averting the face, leaving.<BR>—विमुखी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, turned away from,<BR>averted, departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुग्ध
विमुग्ध वि-मुग्ध. See under वि-मुह्<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्
विमुच् 1. वि-मुच्, cl. 6. P. A. -मुञ्चति,<BR>-ते, -मोक्तुम्, to unloose, loosen, unharness, un-<BR>fasten, untie, release, set free, liberate; to take off<BR>(clothes), undress; to free from (with abl.); to leave<BR>off, stop, cease; to become loose (A.); to yield, re-<BR>linquish, quit, give up, lose; to emit, pour forth, shed,<BR>send forth; to assume, take: Pass. -मुच्यते, to be<BR>loosened, become detached; to be freed from (with<BR>abl. or inst.); to escape; to be deprived of (with<BR>inst.): Caus. -मोचयति, -यितुम्, to loosen, set free,<BR>unfasten, liberate: Desid. -मुमुक्षति, -ते, to wish<BR>to set free, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्त|विमुक्तः
वि-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, loosed, let loose, liberated;<BR>freed from (with inst. or abl., e. g. पाशैः or पाशे-<BR>भ्यो विमुक्तः, freed from fetters); quitted, aban-<BR>doned; issued from, given vent to; hurled, thrown,<BR>discharged.<BR>—विमुक्त-कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a loosened throat or voice, raising a loud cry.<BR>—वि-<BR>मुक्त-प्रग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, having loosened reins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्ति|विमुक्तिः
वि-मुक्ति, इस्, f. liberation, release, remission;<BR>escape, salvation, final emancipation (from all future<BR>existence); separation, parting.<BR>—विमुक्ति-पथ,<BR>अस्, m. the path or way of final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्
2. वि-मुच्, क्, क्, क्, one who lets loose or sends<BR>forth, a creator; a deliverer; (क्), m., N. of Prajā-<BR>pati; a cloud, (Sāy. = जल-विमोचक मेघ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्य
2. वि-मुच्य, ind. having let go; having quitted,<BR>quitting, releasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्यमान
वि-मुच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being let loose or<BR>liberated; being poured forth or sent forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुञ्चत्
वि-मुञ्चत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, unloosing, loosen-<BR>ing; shedding, letting fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्तव्य
वि-मोक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be let loose or set<BR>free or discharged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचन|विमोचनं
वि-मोचन, अस्, m. one who delivers, a deliverer,<BR>liberator, (Sāy. = पापाद् विमोचयितृ); (अम्), n.<BR>the act of unloosing, liberating, unharnessing, unyok-<BR>ing; liberation, emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचित
वि-मोचित, अस्, आ, अम्, loosened, liberated, set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुद्र|विमुद्रः
विमुद्र वि-मुद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, unsealed, un-<BR>closed; opened as a bud or flower, budded, blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुह्
विमुह् वि-मुह्, cl. 4. P. A. -मुह्यति, -ते,<BR>-मोग्धुम् or -मोढुम्, to be confused, become<BR>perplexed or bewildered; to faint away: Caus. -मो-<BR>हयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be confused, disturb,<BR>deprive of consciousness, infatuate, bewilder, lead<BR>astray, bewitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुग्ध
वि-मुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, confused, bewildered,<BR>infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुह्यमान
वि-मुह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being bewildered or<BR>stupefied, embarrassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढ|विमूढः
1. वि-मूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, confounded, bewildered,<BR>discomposed; beguiled, led astray, seduced, tempted;<BR>foolish.<BR>—विमूढ-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or विमूढ-<BR>धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, foolish-minded, foolish, simple.<BR>—वि-<BR>मूढ-भाव, अस्, m. bewildered state, perplexed<BR>condition, confusion.<BR>—विमूढ-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bewildered in mind, senseless, unconscious.<BR>—विमू-<BR>ढात्मन् (˚ढ-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, foolish-minded, sense-<BR>less, foolish, beguiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढ|विमूढः
2. वि-मूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, not foolish or infatuated,<BR>wise; (अस्), m. a kind of divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहन|विमोहनं|विमोहनः
वि-मोहन, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, alluring, seducing,<BR>seductive, bewitching, tempting, fascinating, one who<BR>fascinates, &c.; (अस्, अम्), m. n., N. of one of the di-<BR>visions of Naraka (see नरक); (अम्), n. the act of<BR>seducing, seduction, temptation, exciting the passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहित|विमोहितः
वि-मोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, allured, seduced, bereft of con-<BR>sciousness, beguiled; stupefied, infatuated, bewitched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृज्
विमृज् वि-मृज्, cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि (some-<BR>times also A. -मार्ष्टे), -मार्जितुम्, -मार्ष्टुम्,<BR>to rub off or out, purify, cleanse; to rub, stroke; to<BR>rub dry, wipe off, wipe; to rub on, anoint: Intens.,<BR>Ved. -मामृजीति, to cleanse, purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृज्य
वि-मृज्य, ind. having rubbed or stroked, having<BR>wiped or swept away, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृष्ट
1. वि-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed off, purified,<BR>cleansed, wiped.<BR>—विमृष्ट-राग, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing the colour refined or purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृद्
विमृद् वि-मृद्, cl. 9. 1. P. -मृद्नाति, -मर्-<BR>दति, &c., -मर्दितुम्, to press or crush to pieces,<BR>bruise, pound, trample down, lay waste, devastate,<BR>destroy; to rub together: Caus. -मर्दयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to crush to pieces, bruise; to rub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द|विमर्दः|विमर्द्द|विमर्द्दः
वि-मर्द, अस्, m. crushing, bruising; devasta-<BR>tion, destruction, pressing or rubbing together, fric-<BR>tion; the trituration of perfumes; rubbing against,<BR>touch, contact; conjunction of the sun and moon,<BR>total obscuration, eclipse; war, battle; weariness,<BR>tediousness; the plant Cassia Esculenta.<BR>—विमर्-<BR>दार्ध (˚द-अर्˚), अम्, n. the time from the appa-<BR>rent conjunction to the end of an eclipse.<BR>—विमर्-<BR>दोत्थ (˚द-उत्˚), अस्, m. a scent arising from the<BR>trituration of perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दक|विमर्दकः|विमर्द्दकः
वि-मर्दक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who crushes or<BR>pounds, a crusher, destroyer, &c.; (अस्), m. pound-<BR>ing, grinding, destroying; rolling; the trituration of<BR>perfumes; the conjunction of the sun and moon,<BR>an eclipse; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दन|विमर्दनं|विमर्द्दन|विमर्द्दनं
वि-मर्दन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of grinding,<BR>pounding, crushing, trampling down, rubbing; the<BR>trituration of perfumes; the conjunction of the sun<BR>and moon, an eclipse; destroying, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दित
वि-मर्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, crushed to pieces, bruised,<BR>pounded, broken to pieces, trampled on; rubbed,<BR>anointed; [cf. स्नेह-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दिन्
वि-मर्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crushing to pieces, destroy-<BR>ing, removing,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृदित
वि-मृदित, अस्, आ, अम्, bruised, ground, pounded;<BR>broken, rubbed.<BR>—विमृदित-ध्वज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a crushed or broken banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृद्य
वि-मृद्य, ind. having bruised or pounded or<BR>crushed, having trampled upon; having rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्
विमृश् वि-मृश् (often confounded with वि-<BR>मृष्, q. v.), cl. 6. P. -मृशति, -मर्ष्टुम्,<BR>-म्रष्टुम्, to touch (with the hands), feel, stroke,<BR>rub; to touch (mentally), be sensible of, be aware<BR>of, perceive; to ponder, meditate, consider, reflect on,<BR>deliberate about; to observe; to investigate, examine;<BR>to think about with hesitation, hesitate about doing<BR>anything (with inf.): Caus. -मर्शयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>ponder, reflect on, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्श|विमर्शः
वि-मर्श, अस्, m. consideration, deliberation, in-<BR>vestigation, trial, examination by reason, reasoning,<BR>discussion, hesitation; a conflicting judgment.<BR>—वि-<BR>मर्श-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, uttering discussions, one<BR>who reasons, a reasoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शन|विमर्शनं
वि-मर्शन, अम्, n. the act of investigating, dis-<BR>cussing, investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शिन्
वि-मर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, deliberating, thinking about,<BR>reflecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृशत्
वि-मृशत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, reflecting, con-<BR>sidering, musing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्य
1. वि-मृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be deliberated about<BR>or investigated, to be discussed or reflected upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्य
2. वि-मृश्य, ind. having considered, after due<BR>deliberation or reflection, (अ-विमृश्य, without due<BR>deliberation.)<BR>—विमृश्य-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting<BR>after due deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृष्ट
2. वि-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, reflected on, considered,<BR>weighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृष्
विमृष् वि-मृष् (in many passages where this<BR>verb occurs the forms used may equally be referred<BR>to वि-मृश्), cl. 1. 4. P. A. -मर्षति, -ते, -मृष्-<BR>यति, -ते, -मर्षितुम्, to bear with indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्ष|विमर्षः
वि-मर्ष, अस्, m. dissatisfaction, displeasure;<BR>want of forbearance, impatience, (in these senses वि<BR>is privative); change in the prosperous course of a<BR>dramatic plot, unforeseen reverse or adverse event in<BR>the course of a love-story.<BR>—विमर्षाङ्ग (˚ष-<BR>अङ्˚), a division of the dramatic Vimarṣa (of which<BR>there are said to be thirteen).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्षण
वि-मर्षण, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Kirātas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्षिन्
वि-मर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, disliking, dissatisfied, averse;<BR>impatient, intolerant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्ष्
विमोक्ष् वि-मोक्ष्, cl. 10. P. -मोक्षयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to set free, liberate, let loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्ष|विमोक्षः
वि-मोक्ष, अस्, m. liberation, freedom, letting<BR>loose, letting off; discharging, shooting, dismissing;<BR>becoming loose or free, escape, final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षण|विमोक्षणं
वि-मोक्षण, अम्, आ, n. f. untying, the act of<BR>setting free, liberation, release; discharging, (अण्ड-<BR>व्˚, the act of laying eggs); quitting, abandoning,<BR>resigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षिन्
वि-मोक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, setting free, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्ब|विंब|विंबं|विम्बं|विंबः|विम्बः
विम्ब विम्ब or विम्व, अस्, अम्, m. n. (ac-<BR>cording to Uṇādi-s. IV. 95. fr. rt. 1. वी, but the<BR>etymology is doubtful; frequently written बिम्ब),<BR>the disk of the sun or moon; any disk, a ball,<BR>hemisphere; any round or disk-like appearance; a<BR>looking-glass, mirror; a jar, water-pot (?); an image,<BR>shadow, reflected or represented form, picture, type;<BR>the object compared (as opposed to प्रति-विम्ब, ‘the<BR>counterpart’ to which it is compared); (अस्), m. a<BR>lizard, chameleon; a proper N.; (आ, ई), f. a plant<BR>bearing a bright-red gourd, Momordica Monadelpha;<BR>(आ), f., N. of two metres, four times ˘˘˘˘˘¯˘¯¯;<BR>four times ¯¯¯¯¯, ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯, ¯¯˘¯¯˘¯; N.<BR>of the wife of Bālāditya (a king of Kaśmīra); of the<BR>mother of king Vimbi-sāra; (अम्), n. the fruit of<BR>the Momordica Monadelpha, (the lips are frequently<BR>compared to this fruit; cf. विम्बोष्ठ.)<BR>—विम्ब-<BR>जा, f. the plant Momordica Monadelpha or the<BR>gourd.<BR>—विम्ब-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of the<BR>Vimba.<BR>—विम्ब-सार, a various reading for विम्बि-<BR>सार.<BR>—विम्बागत (˚ब-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘gone to<BR>an image,’ reflected.<BR>—विम्बेश्वर (˚बा-ईश्˚), N. of<BR>a temple founded by the princess Vimbā.<BR>—विम्-<BR>बोष्ठ or विम्बौष्ठ (˚ब-ओष्˚), अस्, आ, or ई,<BR>अम्, having lips like the Vimba fruit, red-lipped,<BR>‘cherry-lipped.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बक|विंबक|विम्बकं
विम्बक, अम्, n. the disk of the sun or moon;<BR>the fruit of the Momordica Monadelpha; (इका), f.<BR>the disk of the sun or moon; a cucurbitaceous plant,<BR>Momordica Monadelpha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बकि
विम्बकि, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बट|विंबट|विंबटः|विम्बटः
विम्बट, अस्, m. the mustard plant, Sinapis Di-<BR>chotoma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बर
विम्बर, a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बाव
विम्बाव, अम्, n., see Vārtt. to Pāṇ. V. 2, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बित|विंबित
विम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, imaged, reflected, pictured,<BR>painted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बिन्
विम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, coming from or relating to<BR>Vimba.<BR>—विम्बि-सार, अस्, m., N. of a king of Ma-<BR>gadha (a contemporary of Śākya-muni; also written<BR>विम्बि-सर, विधि-सार, विद्मि-सार, विन्दु-सेन,<BR>विन्ध्य-सेन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बिय
विम्बिय, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बु|विंबु|विंबुः|विम्बुः
विम्बु विम्बु, उस्, m. the betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्रद्
विम्रद् वि-म्रद्, cl. 1. A. -म्रदते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to make soft or tender, to soften.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्रित्
विम्रित् वि-म्रित्, cl. 4. P. -म्रित्यति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to fall to pieces, crumble away, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लै
विम्लै वि-म्लै, cl. 1. P. A. -म्लायति, -ते,<BR>&c., to wither away, fade, languish, become weak<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">Page0934-a+ 77</a>]<BR>or feeble or weary: Caus. -म्लापयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make to wither or languish, cause to fade or disap-<BR>pear; to weary, enfeeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0933-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लान
1. वि-म्लान, अस्, आ, अम्, faded or withered away;<BR>refreshed, fresh, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लान
2. वि-म्लान, अस्, आ, अम्, unfaded, free from decay;<BR>unsoiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लापन|विम्लापनं
1. वि-म्लापन, अम्, n. the act of causing to wither<BR>or fade away, causing to languish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लापन|विम्लापनं
2. वि-म्लापन, अम्, n. the act of removing decay<BR>or fatigue; refreshing, reviving; cleaning, wiping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्|वियन्त्
वियत् 1. वि-यत्, cl. 1. A. -यतते, -यतितुम्,<BR>to dispose in various rows (?): Caus. -यातयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to place in rows, arrange, dispose of; to do<BR>penance; to pain, torment, harass, disturb; to punish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्|वियन्त्
वियत् 2. वि-यत्, त्, n. (probably connected<BR>with वि-यम् below; but according to some, pres.<BR>part. of rt. 5. इ with 2. वि; according to others fr.<BR>rt. 1. वी), sky, heaven, ether, atmosphere.<BR>—वियच्-<BR>चारिन्, ई, m. ‘sky-goer,’ a kite (= चिल्ल).<BR>—वियद्-<BR>गङ्गा, f. ‘sky-Ganges,’ the heavenly Ganges; the<BR>galaxy.<BR>—वियद्-गति, इस्, f. going or moving in the<BR>air.<BR>—वियद्-भूति, इस्, f. ‘sky-power,’ darkness.<BR>—वियन्-मणि, इस्, m. ‘sky-gem,’ the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियति|वियतिः
वि-यति, इस्, m. (perhaps connected with the above),<BR>a bird; N. of a son of Nahuṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियम्
वियम् वि-यम्, cl. 1. P. -यच्छति, -यन्तुम्,<BR>to stretch out, extend, spread out; to present, grant,<BR>bestow, give; to stretch apart; to restrain: Caus.<BR>-यामयति, -यितुम्, to cause to stretch out, extend,<BR>expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत
वि-यत, अस्, आ, अम्, stretched out, extended, kept<BR>apart; (अम्), ind. separately, at intervals, intermit-<BR>tingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियम|वियमः
वि-यम, अस्, m. restraint, check; rest, cessation,<BR>stop; pain, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियाम|वियामः
वि-याम, अस्, m. restraint, &c. (= वि-यम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विया
विया वि-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -यातुम्, to go<BR>away, depart, leave; to go through, pervade, pass<BR>through, go across, to run through, drive through;<BR>to pierce, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियात|वियातः
वि-यात, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘gone apart or from the right<BR>path,’ abandoned; shameless, impudent, ill-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियु
वियु वि-यु (see rt. 1. यु), cl. 3. P. -यु-<BR>योति, &c., to be separated or parted, to separate (in-<BR>trans.), be dissolved; to be separated from or deprived<BR>of (with inst.); to separate, exclude, deprive of (with<BR>inst.); to keep off, ward off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुत
वि-युत, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. and 2. युत, p. 817),<BR>separated, deprived of, separated from (with inst.,<BR>e. g. वत्सैर् वियुताः, [cows] separated from their<BR>calves).<BR>—वियुतार्थक (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, void<BR>of meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोतृ
वि-योतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. separating; warding<BR>off, defending; (Sāy.) one who does not mix, not<BR>mixing (= दुःखानाम् अमिश्रयितृ, Ṛg-veda IV.<BR>55, 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुज्
वियुज् वि-युज्, cl. 7. P. A. -युनक्ति, -युङ्क्ते,<BR>-योक्तुम्, to disjoin, detach, separate, divide; to free<BR>or liberate from, separate from (with inst., rarely<BR>with abl.); to relax, be slackened, give way, yield<BR>(A.): Pass. -युज्यते, to be separated from, be de-<BR>prived of (with inst.); to be relaxed, yield, give way:<BR>Caus. -योजयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause to be disjoined,<BR>separate; to free or deliver from, deprive of (with<BR>inst. or abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुक्त|वियुक्तः
वि-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, disjoined, detached, sepa-<BR>rated, sundered, severed; separated from, free from,<BR>deprived of, deserted by (with inst. or at the end of<BR>a comp.); failing, deficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुज्य
वि-युज्य, ind. having separated or detached, hav-<BR>ing freed or delivered from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोग|वियोगः
वि-योग, अस्, m. separation, disunion, disjunction;<BR>loss, death, absence (especially of lovers).<BR>—वियोग-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, suffering separation.<BR>—वियोग-वाह्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, excluded from separation, not separated.<BR>—वियोगावसान (˚ग-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ending or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">Page0934-b+ 77</a>]<BR>terminating in separation.<BR>—वियोगावसान-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. termination in separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिन्
वियोगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being separated or disjoined;<BR>apart, absent, remote; (ई), m. the ruddy goose; (इनी), f.<BR>a woman separated from her husband or lover; a kind<BR>of metre having two unequal half lines, the first con-<BR>taining ten and the second eleven syllables, as follow,<BR>˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯, ˘˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯, (the fourth<BR>Canto of the Kumāra-sambhava is chiefly written in<BR>this metre.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोजयत्
वि-योजयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, separating, separating<BR>from; depriving of; lavishing, expending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोजित|वियोजितः
वि-योजित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), separated,<BR>disjoined, disunited; separated from, parted from,<BR>deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोतृ
वियोतृ वि-योतृ. See under वि-यु, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोनि|वियोनिः
वियोनि वि-योनि, इस्, or वि-योनी, f. various<BR>or manifold birth, (according to Kullūka on Manu<BR>XII. 27. ‘the womb of animals’); an ignominious<BR>birth.<BR>—वियोनि-जन्माध्याय (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a chapter of Varāha-mihira's Vṛhaj-jātaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विर
विर विर, अस्, m. (according to Sāy. fr. rt.<BR>वृ), Ved. one who goes or departs this life (=<BR>गन्तृ = प्रेत).<BR>—विरा-सह् or विरा-साह्, -षाट्, ट्,<BR>ट्, Ved. bearing or leading departed spirits, (Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 35, 6 = प्रेतान् पुरुषान् सहते यः;<BR>cf. जला-सह्, तुरा-षाह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्त|विरक्तः
विरक्त वि-रक्त. See under वि-रञ्ज्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्ष्
विरक्ष् वि-रक्ष्, cl. 1. P. -रक्षति, -रक्षि-<BR>तुम्, to watch over, guard, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरच्
विरच् वि-रच्, cl. 10. P. -रचयति, -यितुम्<BR>(Aor. व्य्-अररचत्; in one passage -अरीरचत्), to<BR>arrange, construct, fabricate, contrive, form, make,<BR>prepare; to compose, write (a book); to put on,<BR>lay on, inlay; to effect, perform: Pass. -रच्यते<BR>(Aor. व्य्-अरचि), to be arranged or composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचन|विरचनं
वि-रचन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of arranging,<BR>arrangement; constructing, contriving, contrivance;<BR>making; compiling, composing, composition, com-<BR>pilation; embellishing; embellishment, any artificial<BR>or ornamental fabric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचनीय
वि-रचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made, to be com-<BR>posed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचयत्
वि-रचयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, arranging, making,<BR>fabricating, composing, embellishing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचय्य
वि-रचय्य, ind. having arranged, having com-<BR>posed; having marked out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचित|विरचितः
वि-रचित, अस्, आ, अम्, arranged, trimmed, con-<BR>structed, formed, contrived, made, prepared; written,<BR>compiled, composed; put on, worn; put in, inlaid, set;<BR>embellished, ornamented, furnished with (with inst.).<BR>—विरचित-वपुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, having the body<BR>arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरज|विरजः
विरज वि-रज. See under वि-रजस् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्
विरजस् वि-रजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, free from dust;<BR>devoid of passion, passionless; free from the men-<BR>strual excretion; (आस्), m., N. of a son of Paurṇa-<BR>māsa; of a son of Vasiṣṭha; of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra; (आस्), f. a woman who has ceased to men-<BR>struate.<BR>—वि-रजस्-तमस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, free from (the<BR>qualities of) passion and ignorance.<BR>—विरजो-ऽम्बर-<BR>भूषण, अस्, आ, अम्, having apparel and ornaments<BR>free from dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरज|विरजः
वि-रज, अस्, आ, अम्, free from dust; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of Viṣṇu; of a son of Tvaṣṭṛ; (आ), f. a plant<BR>(commonly called Kavitthānī); Dūrvā grass; N. of<BR>a river; of the wife of Nahuṣa (daughter of a class<BR>of Manes called Sva-svadha).<BR>—विरजा-क्षेत्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्क
वि-रजस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, free from dust, &c., = वि-<BR>रजस्; (आ), f. a woman who has ceased to menstruate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीकृ
विरजी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to render free from dust or passion.<BR>—विरजी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, freed from dust, unsoiled, clean; exempt<BR>from passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीभू
विरजी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become free from dust or passion.<BR>—विरजी-भूत,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">Page0934-c+ 76</a>]<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, free from dust, clean, clear; free from<BR>passion, pure, holy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्च|विरंच|विरंचः|विरञ्चः
विरञ्च वि-रञ्च, अस्, m. (perhaps connected<BR>with वि-रच्), N. of Brahmā; [cf. विरिञ्च.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्चि|विरंचि|विरंचिः|विरञ्चिः
वि-रञ्चि, इस्, m., N. of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्ज्|विरंज्
विरञ्ज् वि-रञ्ज्, cl. 1. 4. P. A. -रजति, -ते,<BR>-रज्यति, -ते, -रङ्क्तुम्, to be changed in colour,<BR>be discoloured, lose the natural colour; to become<BR>changed in disposition, become indifferent to, take<BR>no interest in, regard with indifference, become<BR>estranged or disaffected, grow cold: Caus. -रञ्ज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to colour, dye, make of various colours;<BR>to cause to be indifferent, make estranged, cause to<BR>dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्त|विरक्तः
वि-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, discoloured, changed in<BR>colour; changed in disposition, disaffected, estranged,<BR>averse, indifferent; displeased; free from passion or<BR>affection, void of attachment to worldly objects, (in<BR>these senses वि appears to be privative); impassioned,<BR>feeling excessive passion, (in these senses वि only<BR>intensifies the root.)<BR>—विरक्त-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>disaffected at heart, estranged.<BR>—विरक्त-प्रकृति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, whose chiefs or principal officers are disaf-<BR>fected.<BR>—विरक्त-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, having the heart<BR>or affections estranged, disinclined to, disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्ति|विरक्तिः
वि-रक्ति, इस्, f. change of disposition or feeling,<BR>estrangement, alienation of mind, aversion, disincli-<BR>nation, dissatisfaction; absence of affection or attach-<BR>ment, freedom from passion, weanedness from the<BR>world, (in these senses वि appears to be privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराग|विरागः
वि-राग, अस्, m. change of colour or feeling, change<BR>of nature, (applied in Vedic grammar to the change<BR>in consonants which mutually affect each other);<BR>absence of desire or passion, indifference, disinclina-<BR>tion; disregard of all sensual enjoyment either in<BR>this world or the next; stoicism.<BR>—विराग-विष-<BR>भृत्, त्, त्, त्, cherishing the poison of dislike, har-<BR>bouring the poison of aversion.<BR>—विरागार्ह (˚ग-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, qualified for freedom from passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागिन्
विरागिन्, ई, इणी, इ, changed in feeling, estranged;<BR>void of passion or desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरट|विरटः
विरट विरट, अस्, m. a kind of black Agal-<BR>lochum; N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरण्
विरण् वि-रण्, Caus. -रणयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make to sound forth, cause to sound, play upon (a<BR>musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरण|विरणं
विरण विरण, अम्, n. a fragrant grass used<BR>in certain religious ceremonies, Andropogon Aroma-<BR>ticum or Muricatum; [cf. वीरण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरथ
विरथ वि-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having no car or<BR>chariot, chariotless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरद्
विरद् वि-रद्, cl. 1. P. -रदति, &c., Ved. to<BR>divide, separate, sever, cut through, open; to conduct,<BR>convey; to bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरप्श्
विरप्श् वि-रप्श् (according to some रप्श्<BR>may be fr. an old Desid. form of rt. रप् or रभ्,<BR>according to Sāy. रप्श् is fr. rt. रप् = लप्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-रप्शते, &c., Ved. to be full to overflowing, be<BR>ready to burst, to be distended or inflated; to have<BR>too much of (inst.); to be praised or hymned, (Sāy.<BR>= विविधं स्तूयते); to shine forth variously,<BR>(Sāy. = विविधं राजते); to sound forth, utter a<BR>murmuring sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरप्श
वि-रप्श, अम्, n., Ved. sound, voice, utterance,<BR>(Sāy. विरप्शम् = वाक्यम्; but in Ṛg-veda IV.<BR>50, 3. विरप्शम् = विशेषेण शब्देन स्तोत्रं<BR>यथा भवति तथा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरप्शिन्
वि-रप्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. copious, abundant,<BR>great, powerful, mighty, (according to Nirukta III.<BR>3 = महत्); singing, sounding forth, loud-sounding,<BR>uttering various sounds of praise, having various<BR>sounds or utterances, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>IV. 17, 20. विरप्शी = बहु-विध-शब्दवान्; in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 8, 8. विरप्शी = विविध-वाक्य-युक्ता,<BR>and appears to be used for विरप्शिनी); shaking,<BR>tossing, rocking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0934-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम्
विरम् वि-रम्, cl. 1. P. -रमति (rarely<BR>also A. -रमते), -रन्तुम्, to cease or desist from,<BR>rest from (with abl.); to leave off or discontinue<BR>anything (especially applied to discontinuing a speech,<BR>e. g. विरराम or even वचनं विरराम, he<BR>ceased speaking), stop, pause, end, come to an end<BR>(e. g. रात्रिर् व्यरंसीत्, the night ended): Caus.<BR>-रमयति, -रामयति, -यितुम्, to cause to leave<BR>off or discontinue, make to cease or desist from; to<BR>bring to an end, finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरत|विरतः
वि-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, ceased from, desisting from<BR>(with abl., e. g. पापाद् विरतः, ceased from sin),<BR>stopped, ceased (e. g. विरतेषु मुनिषु, when the<BR>Munis had ceased speaking); rested, ended, con-<BR>cluded.<BR>—विरत-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>left off a habit or practice, one whose occupation has<BR>ceased, having no occupation.<BR>—विरताशय (˚त-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose desires have ceased, one<BR>who has resigned worldly intentions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरति|विरतिः
वि-रति, इस्, f. cessation, discontinuance, stop, rest,<BR>pause, end, term; indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम|विरमः
वि-रम, अस्, m. ceasing, desisting, cessation;<BR>sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमत्
वि-रमत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, ceasing, desisting, resting,<BR>stopping; sporting or playing about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमित
वि-रमित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), made to<BR>cease, stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम्य
वि-रम्य, ind. having ceased or desisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराम|विरामः
वि-राम, अस्, m. leaving off, cessation, rest, repose,<BR>discontinuance (of working, speaking, &c.); stop-<BR>page, stop, pause, pause of the voice, stoppage of<BR>sound; (in gram.) ‘the stop,’ N. of a small oblique<BR>stroke placed under a consonant to denote that it is<BR>quiescent, i. e. that it has no vowel inherent or other-<BR>wise pronounced after it, (this mark is sometimes used<BR>in the middle of conjunctions of consonants; but its<BR>proper use, according to native grammarians, is only<BR>as a stop at the end of a sentence ending in a conso-<BR>nant); end, conclusion, term; N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल विरल, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps for विल-<BR>ल, possessing holes), having interstices, separated by<BR>intervals (whether of space or time); not close or<BR>compact, open in texture, not thick or dense, fine,<BR>thin, delicate; loose, relaxed, wide apart; rare, un-<BR>frequent; single; remote; little, few; (अम्), ind.<BR>rarely, seldom, unfrequently; (अम्), n. sour curds,<BR>coagulated milk (= दधि).<BR>—विरल-जानुक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having knees wide apart,’ a bandy-legged man.<BR>—विरल-द्रवा, f. gruel made of rice or other grain<BR>with the addition of ghee, &c. (= श्लक्ष्ण-यवागू).<BR>—विरलागत (˚ल-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, happening<BR>rarely, of unfrequent occurrence, rare.<BR>—विरली-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make rare, lessen, diminish.<BR>—विरलेतर (˚ल-इत्˚), अस्, &c., ‘other than wide<BR>apart,’ dense, thick, compact, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलित
विरलित, अस्, आ, अम्, not compacted, not dense, (अ-वि-<BR>रलित-कपोलम्, ind. with closely-united cheeks.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस्
विरस् वि-रस्, cl. 1. P. -रसति, -रसितुम्, to<BR>cry out, cry aloud, scream, shriek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस|विरसः
विरस वि-रस, अस्, आ, अम्, juiceless, sapless,<BR>flavourless, tasteless, insipid; painful; (अस्), m. pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरह्
विरह् वि-रह्, cl. 1. 10. P. -रहति, -रहयति,<BR>-रहितुम्, &c., to abandon, desert, relinquish, leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरह|विरहः
वि-रह, अस्, m. separation, parting, absence, (espe-<BR>cially) the separation of lovers; separation from (with<BR>inst.); loneliness, distance; want; abandonment, de-<BR>sertion, cessation, relinquishment.<BR>—विरह-गुणित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, increased by separation.<BR>—विरह-ज or<BR>विरह-जनित, अस्, आ, अम्, arising from or produced<BR>by separation.<BR>—विरह-ज्वर, अस्, m. the anguish<BR>of separation.<BR>—विरह-व्यापद्, त्, त्, त्, impaired or<BR>decreased by absence.<BR>—विरह-शयन, अम्, n. a<BR>solitary couch or bed, i. e. one slept on alone.<BR>—वि-<BR>रहाधिगम (˚ह-अध्˚), अस्, m. experiencing the<BR>absence of any one, (according to Malli-nātha =<BR>विरह-ज्ञान.)<BR>—विरहानल (˚ह-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the fire of separation.<BR>—विरहार्त (˚ह-आर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, pained by the absence of a lover.<BR>—विरहा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">Page0935-b+ 79</a>]<BR>वस्था (˚ह-अव्˚), f. a state of separation or absence.<BR>—विरहोत्कण्ठिता (˚ह-उत्˚), f. a woman who longs<BR>after her absent lover or husband, one distressed by<BR>the absence of her husband (said to be one of the<BR>incidental characters in a drama).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहयत्
वि-रहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, abandoning, relinquish-<BR>ing, deserting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहय्य
वि-रहय्य, ind. having abandoned, having for-<BR>saken, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहित|विरहितः
वि-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, abandoned, deserted, for-<BR>saken, relinquished, left, left alone, solitary, lonely,<BR>retired or withdrawn from company, separated; de-<BR>void of, exempt from, bereft of, destitute of, free<BR>from (with inst. or at the end of a comp., and<BR>sometimes even with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिन्
विरहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, being separated from, absent<BR>(from another), apart from; lonely, solitary; (इणी),<BR>f. a woman separated from her husband or suffering<BR>the pangs of absence from her lover; wages, hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराग|विरागः
विराग वि-राग, &c. See p. 934, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
विराज् 1. वि-राज्, cl. 1. P. A. -राजति (in Ved.<BR>only P.), -ते, -राजितुम्, to reign over, rule, govern<BR>(Ved. P.); to be illustrious or eminent, be conspicuous,<BR>appear to advantage, shine forth, shine out, shine,<BR>glitter; to appear as: Caus. -राजयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to shine forth, make to glitter, fill with bright-<BR>ness, give radiance or lustre, brighten, illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
2. वि-राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, shining, radiant; (ट्), m. splendor,<BR>beauty; a man of the regal or military class; the<BR>first progeny of Brahmā, (according to Manu I. 32,<BR>&c., Brahmā having divided his own substance into<BR>male and female, produced from the female the male<BR>power Virāj, who then produced the first Manu or<BR>Manu Svāyambhuva, who then created the ten Prajā-<BR>patis; the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa states that the male<BR>half of Brahmā was Manu, and the other half Śata-<BR>rūpā, and does not allude to the intervention of Virāj;<BR>other Purāṇas describe the union of Śata-rūpā with<BR>Virāj or Puruṣa in the first instance, and with Manu<BR>in the second; as a sort of secondary creator, Virāj<BR>is sometimes called Prajā-pati, while in Ṛg-veda X.<BR>90, 5. he is represented as born from Puruṣa, and<BR>Puruṣa from him; in the Atharva-veda VIII. 10,<BR>24, XI. 8, 30, Virāj is spoken of as a female, and<BR>regarded as a cow, being elsewhere, however, identi-<BR>fied with Prāṇa); ‘ruler of the various forms of<BR>bodies,’ N. of Intellect located in and ruling over<BR>the collective aggregate of bodies, the consciousness<BR>which perceives collections or aggregates (in the<BR>Vedānta phil.); the body; N. of a son of Rādhā;<BR>of a district; (ट्), f. a particular Vedic metre consisting<BR>of four Pādas of ten syllables each, (in Ṛg-veda X.<BR>130, 5. this metre is represented as attaching itself<BR>to Mitra and Varuṇa, and in Aitareya-Br. I. 4. Virāj<BR>is mystically regarded as ‘food,’ and invocations are<BR>directed to be made in this metre when food is the<BR>especial object of prayer.)<BR>—विराट्-कामा, f. a Vedic<BR>form of the Sammā metre.<BR>—विराट्-क्षेत्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a district.<BR>—विराट्-पूर्वा, f. a Vedic form of<BR>the Tri-ṣṭubh metre.<BR>—विराट्-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of<BR>Virāj,’ epithet of a class of Pitṛs called Soma-sads<BR>(Manu III. 195).<BR>—विराट्-स्थाना, f. a Vedic form of<BR>the Tri-ṣṭubh metre.<BR>—विराट्-स्वरूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>consisting of Virāj, (applied to the Supreme Being.)<BR>—विराड्-देह, अस्, m. ‘having the body of Virāj,’<BR>a term for the universe.<BR>—विराड्-रूपा, f. a Vedic<BR>form of the Tri-ṣṭubh metre (3 × 11 + 8 or rather +<BR>7, giving forty syllables in all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज|विराजः
वि-राज, अस्, m. = 2. वि-राज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजत्
वि-राजत्, अन्, अन्ती (ep. also अती), अत्, shining,<BR>splendid; handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजमान|विराजमानः
वि-राजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, brilliant, splen-<BR>did, handsome, gorgeous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजयत्
वि-राजयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to shine, giving<BR>radiance or lustre to, brightening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजित|विराजितः
वि-राजित, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminated, irradiated, splen-<BR>did; made visible, manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराट|विराटः
विराट विराट, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>midland or north-west districts of India (perhaps<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">Page0935-c+ 73</a>]<BR>Berar); N. of an ancient king of a particular district<BR>in India, (the Pāṇḍavas being obliged to live in con-<BR>cealment during the thirteenth year of their exile,<BR>journied to the court of this king and entered his<BR>service in various disguises.)<BR>—विराट-ज, अस्, m. =<BR>राज-पट्ट, a sort of inferior diamond (said to be<BR>found in the country Virāṭa).<BR>—विराट-पर्वन्, अ,<BR>n., N. of the fourth book of the Mahā-bhārata (describ-<BR>ing the adventures of the Pāṇḍu princes when living<BR>in the service of king Virāṭa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटक|विराटकः
विराटक, अस्, m. a diamond of inferior quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराणिन्
विराणिन् वि-राणिन्, ई, m. (probably fr. rt.<BR>रण् with वि), an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध्
विराध् वि-राध्, cl. 4. P. -राध्यति, &c.,<BR>-राद्धुम्, to lose or be deprived of anything (inst.,<BR>Ved.); to hurt, offend, injure, do an injury: Caus.<BR>-राधयति, -यितुम्, to oppose, thwart, be at vari-<BR>ance, disagree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्ध
वि-राद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, opposed, thwarted; injured,<BR>hurt, offended, treated with disrespect, reviled, abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्धृ
वि-राद्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, opposing, thwarting;<BR>offending, injuring; abusive, calumnious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध|विराधः
वि-राध, अस्, m. opposition, prevention; vexa-<BR>tion, annoyance; a kind of Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधन|विराधनं
वि-राधन, अम्, n. the act of opposing, injuring,<BR>hurting; pain, agony, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधयत्
वि-राधयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, opposing, being at<BR>variance, disagreeing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधान|विराधानं
वि-राधान, अम्, n. pain (= वि-राधन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध्यत्
वि-राध्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, opposing, thwarting;<BR>offending, annoying, injuring, being at variance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराल|विरालः
विराल विराल, अस्, m. = विडाल, a cat, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराव|विरावः
विराव वि-राव. See p. 936, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरि
विरि वि-रि or वि-री (see rts. 1. रि, री), cl. 9.<BR>P. A. -रिणाति, -रिणीते, -रेतुम्, Ved. to cleave asunder,<BR>separate, cut to pieces, kill, destroy, (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 19, 3. वि-रिणाः = व्य्-अरिणाः =<BR>विशेषेण हतवान् असि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिच्
विरिच् वि-रिच्, cl. 7. P. A. -रिणक्ति, -रिङ्क्ते,<BR>-रेक्तुम्, to empty, make empty, evacuate: Pass.<BR>-रिच्यते, to extend or be extended, reach out, sur-<BR>pass, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 16, 5. वि-<BR>रेचि = अति-रिरिचे, अधिको बभूव); to be emptied<BR>or purged: Caus. -रेचयति, -यितुम्, to cause purg-<BR>ing, purge, empty, make empty, cleanse, purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिक्त|विरिक्तः
वि-रिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, evacuated, emptied, purged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेक|विरेकः
वि-रेक, अस्, m. purging, evacuation of the bowels;<BR>a purgative, cathartic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचन|विरेचनं|विरेचनः
वि-रेचन, अम्, n. purging, evacuation of the<BR>bowels; a purgative.<BR>—विरेचन-द्रव्य, अम्, n.<BR>any purging substance or medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचित
वि-रेचित, अस्, आ, अम्, purged, emptied, evacuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेच्य
वि-रेच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be purged or emptied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्च|विरिंच|विरिंचः|विरिञ्चः
विरिञ्च वि-रिञ्च or वि-रिञ्चन, अस्, m. a N.<BR>of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चि|विरिंचि|विरिंचिः|विरिञ्चिः
वि-रिञ्चि, इस्, m., N. of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu; of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिफित
विरिफित वि-रिफित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. de-<BR>prived of the sound of र्; pronounced or uttered<BR>with great effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिब्ध|विरिब्धः
विरिब्ध वि-रिब्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. रिभ् with<BR>वि), sounded; (अस्), m. a note, tone, sound (= स्वर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिभित
वि-रिभित, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VII. 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेभित|विरेभितः
वि-रेभित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिश्
विरिश् वि-रिश् or वि-लिश् (see rt. रिश्), cl. 6. A.<BR>-रिशते, &c., Ved. to be dragged or rent apart, to be<BR>disarranged or disordered; to be torn off, break off,<BR>become rent or torn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिष्ट
वि-रिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rent asunder, broken<BR>off, out of due order; (अम्), n. a defect in a sacri-<BR>fice, (also written वि-लिष्ट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरी
विरी वि-री. See वि-रि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरु
विरु वि-रु, cl. 2. P. -रौति, -रवीति, -रवितुम्,<BR>to roar aloud, scream or shout out, cry, buzz, hum,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">Page0936-a+ 78</a>]<BR>yell, bray; to sound, jingle, rattle; to lament, weep,<BR>appeal to with lamentations, call on, invoke: Caus.<BR>-रावयति, -यितुम्, to roar or scream aloud, fill with<BR>noise or clamour; to make to sound or resound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0935-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरव
वि-रव, अस्, m., Ved. outcry, clamour, sound,<BR>noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराव|विरावः
वि-राव, अस्, m. crying or shouting out, clamour,<BR>sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराविन्
वि-राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, shouting or roaring out, re-<BR>sounding, crying, singing; lamenting; (इणी), f. weep-<BR>ing, crying; a broom; N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुत
वि-रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, roared aloud, screamed; re-<BR>sounded, resounding, filled with cries, (मयूर-<BR>विरुत, filled with the cries of peacocks); (अम्), n.<BR>shrieking, howling, crying, singing, humming (of<BR>bees), chirping; clamour, noise, din, howling (of the<BR>wind &c.), sound, tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुवत्
वि-रुवत्, अन्, अती, अत्, howling, crying, shrieking,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुच्
विरुच् वि-रुच्, cl. 1. A. -रोचते (Ved. also<BR>P. -रोचति, in Raghu-v. VI. 5. and in one or two<BR>other later works the Aor. P. व्य्-अरुचत् is found),<BR>-रोचितुम्, to shine forth, glitter, be bright or radiant;<BR>to be conspicuous, become visible, appear; to become<BR>eminent or famous; to cause to shine, illuminate,<BR>make bright (P.); to please, delight: Caus. -रोच-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to shine, illuminate, brighten;<BR>to find pleasure in, delight in; to sport with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुक्मत्|विरुक्मन्त्
विरुक्मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. shining, brilliant,<BR>splendid; (आन्), m. a bright weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोक|विरोकं|विरोकः
वि-रोक, अस्, m. a ray of light; (अम्), n. a hole,<BR>chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोकिन्
वि-रोकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. shining, glowing, gleam-<BR>ing, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचन|विरोचनः
वि-रोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, illuminating; (अस्),<BR>m. the sun; the moon; fire; N. of the son of<BR>Prahlāda or Prahrāda; (अम्), n. (?), light, lustre.<BR>—विरोचन-वध, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—विरोचन-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of Virocana,’ epithet of Bali<BR>(sovereign of Mahābali-pura).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचमान
वि-रोचमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, glittering,<BR>radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचयत्
वि-रोचयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to shine, mak-<BR>ing bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचिष्णु
वि-रोचिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, shining; illuminating,<BR>making visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुज्
विरुज् वि-रुज्, cl. 6. P. -रुजति, -रोक्तुम्, to<BR>break to pieces, tear asunder; to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुग्ण
वि-रुग्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (less correctly written वि-<BR>रुग्न), broken to pieces, torn asunder; bent;<BR>blunted; destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुज्य
वि-रुज्य, ind. having broken to pieces, having<BR>torn asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्
विरुद् वि-रुद्, cl. 2. P. -रोदिति, -रोदितुम्,<BR>to weep or cry aloud, sob, lament, bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद|विरुदं|विरुदः
वि-रुद, अस्, m. crying; proclaiming; a laudatory<BR>poem, panegyric.<BR>—विरुदावली (˚द-आव्˚), f., N. of<BR>a poem by Raghu-deva celebrating the praises of a<BR>certain king of Mithilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदित|विरुदितं
वि-रुदित, अम्, n. loud lamentation, intense grief,<BR>bewailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुध्
विरुध् 1. वि-रुध् (= वि-रुह्), cl. 1. P. -रो-<BR>धति, &c., Ved. to grow or sprout out, shoot forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुध्
विरुध् 2. वि-रुध्, cl. 7. P. A. -रुणद्धि,<BR>-रुन्द्धे, -रोद्धुम्, to hinder, obstruct; to en-<BR>counter opposition (A., Ved.): Pass. -रुध्यते (ep.<BR>also P. -ति), to be impeded or checked or kept back<BR>or withheld; to be opposed to, contend with, com-<BR>bat (with inst., or with inst. and सह, or with gen.,<BR>or with loc., or with acc. and प्रति); to be at<BR>variance, disagree, be inconsistent; to fail: Caus.<BR>-रोधयति, -यितुम्, to cause to hinder or obstruct,<BR>to render hostile, set at variance; to oppose, en-<BR>counter, fight against, contend with: Pass. of Caus.<BR>-रोध्यते, to be impeded or kept back; to be ren-<BR>dered hostile or set at variance: Desid. -रुरुत्सति,<BR>to wish to oppose, intend commencing hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्ध|विरुद्धः
वि-रुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, opposed, hindered, checked,<BR>restrained, arrested, obstructed, blocked or shut up,<BR>besieged, barred or locked up, blockaded; opposed<BR>or contrasted in quality (as sweet to sour &c.); con-<BR>trary, repugnant, opposite, contradictory, perverse,<BR>reverse, (a reason) proving the reverse (in logic);<BR>incongruous, inconsistent, incompatible, mutually dis-<BR>agreeing (as medicine and food); hostile, adverse, at<BR>variance, at enmity; unpropitious, unfavourable, dis-<BR>agreeable; prohibited, forbidden; excluded, disquali-<BR>fied; doubtful, uncertain; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>deities; (अम्), n. opposition, hostility, disagreement,<BR>discord, a feeling of repugnance; (अम्), ind. per-<BR>versely, incongruously.<BR>—विरुद्ध-ता, f. or विरुद्-<BR>ध-त्व, अम्, n. opposition, contrariety, perverseness,<BR>incongruity; hostility, enmity, disagreeableness.<BR>—वि-<BR>रुद्ध-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, having a hostile disposition,<BR>malevolently disposed, malignant.<BR>—विरुद्ध-प्र-<BR>सङ्ग, अस्, m. a prohibited or unlawful occupation.<BR>—विरुद्ध-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, eating incompatible or<BR>unsuitable food.<BR>—विरुद्ध-भोजन, अम्, n. in-<BR>compatible food.<BR>—विरुद्ध-लक्षण, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a section of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—विरुद्-<BR>धाचरण (˚ध-आच्˚), अम्, n. a wrong or improper<BR>course of conduct.<BR>—विरुद्धान्न (˚ध-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. incompatible or forbidden food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोद्धव्य
वि-रोद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be opposed, to be<BR>obstructed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोध|विरोधः
वि-रोध, अस्, m. opposition, obstruction, hin-<BR>drance, impediment; impediment to the successful<BR>progress of a plot (in a drama); restraint, check;<BR>blocking up, surrounding, investing, siege, blockade,<BR>confinement; contradiction (in logic), contrariety,<BR>antithesis, contrast; inconsistency, opposition of<BR>qualities (in food, medicine, &c.); hostility, enmity,<BR>animosity, quarrel, war, calamity, misfortune; (ई),<BR>f. a fixed rule, ordinance (?).<BR>—विरोध-कारक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, causing opposition or disagreement,<BR>fomenting quarrels.<BR>—विरोध-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing<BR>hindrance or opposition; an enemy; (त्), m., N. of<BR>the nineteenth year of Jupiter's cycle.<BR>—विरोधा-<BR>भास (˚ध-आभ्˚), अस्, m. the semblance of oppo-<BR>site qualities, a particular figure in rhetoric.<BR>—वि-<BR>रोधालङ्कार (˚ध-अल्˚), अस्, m. (in rhetoric) ‘the<BR>ornament of contradiction,’ a particular figure of<BR>speech or mode of writing.<BR>—विरोधोक्ति (˚ध-<BR>उक्˚), इस्, f. adverse or contradictory speech, quarrel,<BR>dispute, mutual contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधक
वि-रोधक, अस्, इका, अम्, opposing, contradicting,<BR>incongruous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधन|विरोधनं
वि-रोधन, अम्, n. the act of opposing, hinder-<BR>ing, obstructing, preventing, blockading, besieging,<BR>encountering, defying; opposition, resistance, con-<BR>tradiction; incongruity, inconsistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधित
वि-रोधित, अस्, आ, अम्, opposed, contended against,<BR>fought with, rendered hostile, set at variance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिन्
वि-रोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, opposing, hindering, prevent-<BR>ing, obstructing, besieging; obstructive; excluding,<BR>disqualifying; inimical, adverse, hostile; contradic-<BR>tory, inconsistent; having opposite or incompatible<BR>qualities (as food, medicine, &c.); contentious, quar-<BR>relsome; (ई), m. an opponent, enemy; N. of the<BR>fifty-seventh year of Jupiter's cycle; (इनी), f. a woman<BR>who causes enmity or promotes quarrels (between<BR>husband and wife &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोध्य
1. वि-रोध्य, ind. having opposed, having con-<BR>tended with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोध्य
2. वि-रोध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be opposed or con-<BR>tended against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुष्
विरुष् वि-रुष्, cl. 1. P. -रोषति, &c., -रो-<BR>षितुम् or -रोष्टुम्, to displease, annoy, irritate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुष्ट
वि-रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, very angry, very much irri-<BR>tated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुष्यमाण
वि-रुष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being very angry at<BR>(with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोष
वि-रोष, अस्, आ, अम्, very angry, wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुह्
विरुह् वि-रुह्, cl. 1. P. -रोहति, -रोढुम्,<BR>to grow or shoot out, shoot forth, sprout, bud; to<BR>go forth, arise, proceed; to mount, ascend, increase:<BR>Caus. -रोहयति, -रोपयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">Page0936-c+ 77</a>]<BR>grow, plant; to cause to grow over or cicatrize, heal;<BR>to thrust out, remove, expel, dethrone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूढ|विरूढः
वि-रूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, grown or shot out, budded,<BR>blossomed; grown, increased, arisen, produced, born;<BR>ascended, mounted, ridden.<BR>—विरूढ-बोध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one whose intelligence has increased or matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोपण|विरोपणं
वि-रोपण, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to grow, planting;<BR>causing to grow over, healing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोपित
वि-रोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, planted; caused to grow<BR>over, healed.<BR>—विरोपित-व्रण, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose wound is healed or cicatrized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोह|विरोहः
वि-रोह, अस्, m. growing out, shooting forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोहण|विरोहणं
वि-रोहण, अम्, n. the act of growing out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूक्षण|विरूक्षणं
विरूक्षण वि-रूक्षण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>रूक्ष् with वि), making rough or dry, drying, astrin-<BR>gent; (अम्), n. the act of roughening or contract-<BR>ing, acting as an astringent; censure, blame, reviling,<BR>abuse; oath, imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूक्षित
वि-रूक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, made rough; smeared<BR>over, covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूप्
विरूप् वि-रूप्, cl. 10. P. -रूपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to deform, make deformed, disfigure, mutilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूप|विरूपं|विरूपः
वि-रूप, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, deformed, badly formed,<BR>misshapen, ugly, unusual in form or nature, mon-<BR>strous, unnatural; of various form, multiform, diver-<BR>sified; (अस्), m., N. of one of the descendants of<BR>Vaivasvata Manu; N. of a descendant of Aṅgiras<BR>(author of the hymns Ṛg-veda VIII. 43, 44, 64);<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a family belonging to the race<BR>of Aṅgiras; (अम्), n. deformity, irregular or mon-<BR>strous shape; difference of form, variety of nature or<BR>character; (आ), f., N. of the wife of Yama.<BR>—वि-<BR>रूप-करण, अम्, n. deformation, disfiguring.<BR>—वि-<BR>रूप-चक्षुस्, उस्, m. ‘diversely-eyed,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva, (see विरूपाक्ष.)<BR>—विरूप-ता, f. deformity,<BR>malformation.<BR>—विरूप-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>deformed shape, of a monstrous form, misshapen.<BR>—विरूपाक्ष (˚प-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, diversely-<BR>eyed, having deformed eyes; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva (as represented with an odd number of eyes,<BR>one being in his forehead, cf. त्रि-लोचन); N. of a<BR>Rudra; of a teacher of the Haṭha-vidyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपक|विरूपकः
वि-रूपक, अस्, इका, अम्, deformed, misshapen;<BR>monstrous, frightful, hideous; (अस्), m. a nickname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपित
वि-रूपित, अस्, आ, अम्, deformed, disfigured, muti-<BR>lated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेपस्
विरेपस् वि-रेपस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (see rt. 1. रिप्),<BR>stainless, faultless, without blemish or defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेफ|विरेफः
विरेफ वि-रेफ, अस्, m. the absence of the<BR>letter र्; a river, stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेभित|विरेभितः
विरेभित वि-रेभित. See under वि-रिब्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोष
विरोष वि-रोष. See under वि-रुष्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्
विल् विल्, cl. 6. P. विलति, वेलितुम्, to<BR>cover, conceal, clothe; to break or<BR>divide, (in this sense more usually written बिल्); cl.<BR>10. P. वेलयति, -यितुम्, to throw, cast, direct, send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल|विलं|विलः
विल, अम्, n. an aperture, opening, hole, chasm,<BR>vacuity; a burrow, cave, cavern, den; the vagina;<BR>(अस्), m. one of Indra's horses; a sort of reed or<BR>cane, Calamus Rotang.<BR>—विल-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, mak-<BR>ing holes, burrowing; (ई), m. a mouse.<BR>—विलङ्-<BR>गम, अस्, m. ‘hole-goer,’ a serpent, snake.<BR>—वि-<BR>ल-धावन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. (sensu obsceno)<BR>rimam tergens.<BR>—विल-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, of the breed<BR>of Vila (said of horses).<BR>—विल-वास, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>living in holes, burrowing; (अस्), m. an animal<BR>which lives in holes; a polecat (= जाहक).<BR>—विल-<BR>वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living in a hole, burrowing; (ई), m.<BR>a snake.<BR>—विल-शय, अस्, ई, अम्, living or burrowing<BR>in holes; (अस्), m. any animal that lives in holes; a<BR>snake.<BR>—विल-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, lying in a hole, living<BR>in holes; (ई), m. any animal that lives in holes.<BR>—विले-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living or burrowing in holes;<BR>(ई), m. a snake.<BR>—विले-शय, अस्, m. any animal<BR>living in holes; a snake; a rat; a hare or rabbit;<BR>N. of a teacher of the Haṭha-vidyā.<BR>—विलेश्वर<BR>(˚ल-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a place of pilgrimage;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">Page0937-a+ 78</a>]<BR>(perhaps incorrectly for बिल्वेश्वर.)<BR>—विलौकस्<BR>(˚ल-ओक्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, living in a hole; (आस्), m. any<BR>animal that lives in holes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0936-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलस
विलस, अस्, आ, अम्, see Gaṇa Tṛṇādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष्
विलक्ष् वि-लक्ष्, cl. 10. P. A. -लक्षयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to distinguish, mark, characterize; to<BR>observe, perceive, see, notice; to be without the<BR>power of fixing the eye on any object, to become<BR>bewildered or confused or embarrassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष|विलक्षः
वि-लक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. लक्ष with वि in a<BR>privative sense or expressing difference), markless,<BR>unmarked, having no distinguishing mark or aim;<BR>having no characteristic mark or property; having a<BR>different mark, having a character different to what<BR>is usual or natural, strange, extraordinary; bewildered,<BR>embarrassed; astonished, surprised; abashed, ashamed.<BR>—विलक्ष-ता, f. or विलक्ष-त्व, अम्, n. absence<BR>of mark or aim, absence of distinguishing property;<BR>confusion, bewilderment, surprise; shame.<BR>—वि-<BR>लक्षी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make bewil-<BR>dered or confused, scoff at, insult.<BR>—विलक्षी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, scoffed at, insulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
1. वि-लक्षण, अम्, n. the act of distinguishing,<BR>perceiving, seeing, observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
2. वि-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having no distinguish-<BR>ing marks; having different or opposite marks or<BR>characteristics, having distinguishing qualities or<BR>features, other, different, strange, extraordinary;<BR>(अम्), n. any state or condition which is without<BR>distinguishing mark or for which no cause can be<BR>assigned, vain or causeless state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षित
1. वि-लक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, distinguished, marked,<BR>recognised, discerned, perceived, seen, observed,<BR>noticed, discernible by; perplexed, dismayed, dis-<BR>concerted, affected without cause, embarrassed, puz-<BR>zled, vexed, annoyed, disappointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षित
2. वि-लक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, undistinguished, un-<BR>discriminated, unmarked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष्य
वि-लक्ष्य, ind. having perceived or noticed, hav-<BR>ing observed; having become bewildered or confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्
विलग् वि-लग्, cl. 1. P. -लगति, &c., to<BR>hang to, cling to, stick to, hold on to (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलगित
वि-लगित, अस्, आ, अम्, attached to, &c., (but see<BR>वि-लगित below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्न|विलग्नं
वि-लग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, clung to, clinging to, fastened<BR>or attached to, resting on, fixed on, connected with;<BR>brought close to; gone by, passed away; slender,<BR>thin, delicate (said of the waist); (अम्), n. = लग्न,<BR>the rising of constellations, a horoscope, &c.; the<BR>waist, middle (as connecting the upper and lower<BR>parts of the body).<BR>—विलग्न-मध्या, f. a woman<BR>with a slender waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्य
वि-लग्य, ind. having clung to, having stuck to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलगित
विलगित वि-लगित or वि-लङ्गित, referred<BR>to rt. लङ्ग् with वि in Pāṇ. VI. 4, 24, Vārtt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घ्|विलंघ्
विलङ्घ् वि-लङ्घ्, cl. 1. P. A. -लङ्घति, -ते,<BR>-लङ्घितुम्, to leap or spring about, jump, skip; cl.<BR>10. P. or Caus. -लङ्घयति, -यितुम्, to leap or jump<BR>over, overstep, pass over, pass or rise beyond, pass<BR>by, transgress, violate, neglect, contemn; to over-<BR>come, surmount, get the better of, surpass, excel,<BR>frustrate; to rise towards, ascend to; to give up,<BR>abandon; to act wrongly towards, offend; to cause<BR>to pass over the right time for eating, cause to fast,<BR>make to abstain from food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घन|विलंघन|विलंघनं
वि-लङ्घन, अम्, n. the act of passing beyond,<BR>transgressing, overstepping; striking against, trans-<BR>gression, offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घनीय
वि-लङ्घनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be overstepped or<BR>passed over, to be transgressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घयित्वा
वि-लङ्घयित्वा, anom. ind. part. having surpassed<BR>or surmounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घित|विलंघित
वि-लङ्घित, अस्, आ, अम्, overleaped, overstepped,<BR>transgressed; overcome, surpassed, excelled.<BR>—वि-<BR>लङ्घिताकाश (˚त-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, passing or rising<BR>beyond the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घिन्
वि-लङ्घिन्, ई, इनी, इ, transgressing, ascending to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घ्य
वि-लङ्घ्य, ind. having jumped or passed over,<BR>having omitted or neglected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज्
विलज्ज् वि-लज्ज्, cl. 6. A. -लज्जते (some-<BR>times also P. -लज्जति), -लज्जितुम्, to become ashamed<BR>or abashed, feel ashamed, blush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज|विलज्जः
वि-लज्ज, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. लज्जा with वि in a priva-<BR>tive sense), shameless, unabashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्जत्
वि-लज्जत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, being ashamed,<BR>feeling ashamed, modest, bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्जमान
वि-लज्जमान, अस्, आ, अम्, ashamed, abashed,<BR>modest, blushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्जित
वि-लज्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, ashamed, abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलप्
विलप् वि-लप्, cl. 1. P. A. -लपति, -ते, -ल-<BR>पितुम्, -लप्तुम्, to wail, moan, weep, cry, utter<BR>cries or lamentations, to mourn, bewail, lament (with<BR>acc.), complain; to speak variously, talk much or<BR>idly, prattle, chatter, talk (in general): Caus. -लाप-<BR>यति, -यते, -यितुम्, to cause to mourn or lament;<BR>to cause to speak much (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपत्
वि-लपत्, अन्, अन्ती (ep. also अती), अत्, lamenting,<BR>wailing, moaning, complaining; prating, talking idly<BR>or wildly; talking, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपन|विलपनं
वि-लपन, अम्, n. the act of lamenting, wailing,<BR>complaining, &c.; chattering, talking idly or wildly;<BR>talking; the dirt or sediment of any oily substance<BR>(as of clarified butter &c.).<BR>—विलपन-विनोद, अस्,<BR>m. removing (grief) by weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपमान
वि-लपमान, अस्, आ, अम्, lamenting, wailing,<BR>weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपित|विलपितं
वि-लपित, अस्, आ, अम्, lamented, bewailed; chat-<BR>tered; spoken idly, spoken; (अम्), n. lamentation,<BR>wailing; a moan, wail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपिष्यत्
वि-लपिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to lament<BR>or bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलप्य
वि-लप्य, ind. having bewailed or lamented,<BR>lamenting, bewailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलप्यत्
वि-लप्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (ep. for वि-लपत्),<BR>lamenting, bewailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाप|विलापः
वि-लाप, अस्, m. lamentation, crying, wailing,<BR>moaning, complaint; a moan, wail, groan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलभ्
विलभ् वि-लभ्, cl. 1. A. -लभते, -लब्धुम्,<BR>to take away, remove; to grant, bestow, provide;<BR>to consign, hand over, deliver: Caus. -लम्भयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to receive or fall to the share of<BR>9with double acc.): Desid. -लिप्सते, to desire to<BR>take away, wish to share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलब्ध
वि-लब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, taken away, taken; given,<BR>bestowed, consigned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्भ|विलंभ|विलंभः|विलम्भः
वि-लम्भ, अस्, m. giving, gift, donation; libe-<BR>rality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्ब्|विलंब्
विलम्ब् वि-लम्ब्, cl. 1. A. -लम्बते (ep.<BR>also P. -लम्बति), -लम्बितुम्, to hang on both<BR>sides (Ved.), hang down, hang on, hang to or from,<BR>be attached to (with loc.); to sink, set, decline; to<BR>continue hanging, linger, loiter, delay (e. g. मा वि-<BR>लम्बस्व, do not delay), tarry, hesitate, procrasti-<BR>nate: Pass. -लम्ब्यते, to be lingered or loitered,<BR>to be delayed: Caus. -लम्बयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to linger or loiter, detain, delay; to spend un-<BR>profitably, waste, lose; to put off, procrastinate; to<BR>loiter, delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्ब|विलंब|विलंबः|विलम्बः
वि-लम्ब, अस्, m. hanging or falling down, pen-<BR>dulousness; slowness, tardiness, delay, procrastina-<BR>tion; N. of the sixth year of Jupiter's cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बत्
वि-लम्बत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, hanging down, falling<BR>down, delaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बन|विलंबन|विलंबनं|विलम्बनं
वि-लम्बन, अम्, n. hanging down or from, de-<BR>pending; delaying, delay, procrastination, retarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बमान
वि-लम्बमान, अस्, आ, अम्, hanging down, hang-<BR>ing from; hanging or suspended on; declining, set-<BR>ting (said of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिका|विलंबिका
वि-लम्बिका, f. retardation of the feces, constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बित|विलंबित|विलम्बितं
वि-लम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, hanging or falling down,<BR>depending; pendulous; hanging on, closely con-<BR>nected with or dependent on; retarded, procrasti-<BR>nated, slow, tardy; slow (as time in music or in<BR>chanting the Veda &c.; cf. वृत्ति); spent use-<BR>lessly, wasted; (अम्), ind. slowly, tardily; (अम्), n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">Page0937-c+ 77</a>]<BR>delay, (अ-विलम्बितम्, ind. without delay); (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. slow time.<BR>—विलम्बित-गति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>slow or tardy in motion; epithet of a kind of metre.<BR>—विलम्बित-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having the fruit<BR>or fulfilment delayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिन्|विलंबिन्
वि-लम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hanging down or from, de-<BR>pending, pendulous; delaying, retarding, dilatory,<BR>slow; (ई), m. the thirty-second year of the Indian<BR>cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्ब्य
वि-लम्ब्य, ind. having lingered or loitered,<BR>loitering, dallying, (अ-विलम्ब्य, without delay.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलय|विलयः
विलय वि-लय, &c. See under वि-ली, p. 938.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलला
विलला वि-लला, f. (probably fr. rt. लल् with<BR>वि), a sort of plant, Sida Cordifolia (= श्वेत-बला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलस्
विलस् वि-लस्, cl. 1. P. -लसति, -लसितुम्, to<BR>gleam, flash, glitter, shine; to shine forth, come to<BR>light, appear, arise, be manifested; to play, sport, be<BR>sportive or wanton, be amused or delighted; to jump<BR>or frisk about, move about, dart, wave; to sound,<BR>echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसत्|विलसन्त्
वि-लसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, flashing, shining, glitter-<BR>ing, brilliant, beautiful, splendid; shining forth, ap-<BR>pearing; playing, sporting, sportive, wanton; frisk-<BR>ing or moving about, waving, darting, flashing (as<BR>lightning); sounding, echoing.<BR>—विलसत्-पताक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a gleaming or waving flag.<BR>—वि-<BR>लसन्-मरीचि, इस्, इस्, इ, having rays of light gleam-<BR>ing or playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसन|विलसनं
वि-लसन, अम्, n. the act of flashing, gleaming,<BR>sporting, dallying, play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसित
वि-लसित, अस्, आ, अम्, gleaming, glittering, shin-<BR>ing, shining forth, appearing, appeared, manifested;<BR>played, sported; sportive, wanton; (अम्), n. gleam-<BR>ing, flashing; appearance, manifestation, (विद्या-व्˚,<BR>manifestation of knowledge); a gleam, flash; sport,<BR>play, pastime, dalliance, wanton gestures; a brilliant<BR>action, action or gesture (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलास|विलासः
वि-लास, अस्, m. sport, pastime, play, merriness,<BR>(especially) amorous pastime, diversion (with women,<BR>dancers, singers, &c.), dalliance, coquetry, affecta-<BR>tion of coyness, wantonness, (a form of feminine<BR>gesture considered as indicative of amorous senti-<BR>ments, such as change of place, posture, gait, look,<BR>hiding at the approach of a lover, assuming a look<BR>of displeasure, &c.); grace, elegance, charm, beauty.<BR>—विलास-कानन, अम्, n. a pleasure-grove, pleasure-<BR>ground.<BR>—विलास-मन्दिर, अम्, n. a pleasure-house,<BR>summer-house.<BR>—विलास-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, sportive,<BR>playful, dallying, wanton; (अती), f. a wanton or<BR>coquettish woman.<BR>—विलास-विभवानस (?), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, greedy, covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासन|विलासनं
वि-लासन, अम्, n. (perhaps for the more correct<BR>form वि-लसन), sport, pastime, play, dalliance,<BR>wantonness; fascination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिका
वि-लासिका, f. a drama in one act on any light<BR>subject or adventure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिन्
वि-लासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wanton, sportive, coquettish,<BR>playful, dallying; (ई), m. a sporter, voluptuary, sen-<BR>sualist; fire; the moon; a snake; an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; of Kṛṣṇa; of Śiva; of Kāma, god of<BR>love; (इनी), f. a wanton woman, harlot; a coquettish<BR>woman, any woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाता
विलाता विलाता, f., Ved. a young girl (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाल|विलालः
विलाल वि-लाल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. लल् with वि),<BR>an instrument, machine (= यन्त्र); a cat, (in this<BR>sense = विडाल, विराल, q. q. v. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिख्
विलिख् वि-लिख्, cl. 6. P. -लिखति, -लेखितुम्<BR>(Ved. inf. -लिखस्), to scratch, scratch up, tear, tear<BR>open, scarify, scrape, rub, rub against, touch, reach<BR>to; to scratch in or on, make a furrow or mark,<BR>make an incision, write, write down, delineate, paint:<BR>Caus. -लेखयति, -यितुम्, to cause to scratch, cause<BR>to write.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिखत्
वि-लिखत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, scratching, tearing,<BR>scraping, writing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिखन|विलिखनं
वि-लिखन, अम्, n. the act of scratching, scraping,<BR>writing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0937-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिखित
वि-लिखित, अस्, आ, अम्, scratched, scraped, scarified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिख्य
वि-लिख्य, ind. having scratched, having written, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखन|विलेखनं
वि-लेखन, अम्, n. making an incision or mark<BR>or furrow; dividing, splitting; digging, delving,<BR>rooting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखिन्
वि-लेखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, scratching, scraping, touching,<BR>reaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्
विलिप् वि-लिप्, cl. 6. P. A. -लिम्पति, -ते,<BR>-लेप्तुम्, to smear over, besmear, plaster, spread over,<BR>anoint; to smear or spread on; to pollute: Pass.<BR>-लिप्यते, to be anointed, be smeared over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्त
वि-लिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, smeared over, besmeared,<BR>anointed, plastered, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिम्पित
वि-लिम्पित, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. the Caus.),<BR>smeared over, besmeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप|विलेपः
वि-लेप, अस्, m. ointment, unguent, (especially<BR>the fragrant unguent of sandal, agallochum, &c.);<BR>anointing, plastering; mortar, plaster; (ई), f. rice-<BR>gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपन|विलेपनं
वि-लेपन, अम्, n. the act of smearing, anointing,<BR>plastering over, smearing or anointing the body<BR>(with fragrant oils, &c.); perfume for the person (as<BR>unguent or oil of sandal, saffron, camphor, bdellium,<BR>&c.); ointment of any kind; (ई), f. a woman<BR>scented with perfumes, &c.; rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपनिन्
विलेपनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing unguents or per-<BR>fumes, (अ-विलेपनिन्, deprived of ointments.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपिका
वि-लेपिका, f. rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपिन्
वि-लेपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, smearing or plastering over,<BR>one who anoints, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप्य|विलेप्यः
वि-लेप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spread over or plastered;<BR>(अस्), m. rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिश्
विलिश् वि-लिश् = वि-रिश्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिष्ट
वि-लिष्ट = वि-रिष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिस्तेङ्गा
विलिस्तेङ्गा विलिस्तेङ्गा, f., N. of a Dānavī<BR>(of whom Indra was enamoured).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिह्
विलिह् वि-लिह्, cl. 2. P. A. -लेढि, -लीढे,<BR>-लेढुम्, to lick, lick up, lap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेलिहत्
वि-लेलिहत्, अत्, अती, अत् (Intens. pres. part.; in<BR>Mahā-bh. Śānti-p. 8075. वि-लेलिहन्, nom. case<BR>masc.), licking continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेलिहान
वि-लेलिहान, अस्, आ, अम्, continually or repeatedly<BR>licking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विली
विली वि-ली, cl. 4. A. -लीयते, -लातुम् or -ले-<BR>तुम्, to cling to, lie close to, stick to, cleave to, be<BR>united or addicted or attached to; to settle on, alight<BR>or perch on; to become disunited or dissolved, be-<BR>come liquid, melt away; to become dissipated or<BR>dispersed, become ineffectual; to fall to pieces, be<BR>destroyed, perish, vanish, disappear, become hidden;<BR>cl. 1. P. -लयति, to make liquid or fluid, melt:<BR>Caus. -लीनयति, -लापयति, -लालयति, -लाययति,<BR>(according to some grammarians this last is the form<BR>to be used when not speaking of liquefying butter or<BR>similar substances, see Pāṇ. VII. 3, 39), -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to become disunited or dissolved, cause to be<BR>dissolved in (with loc.); to make liquid, dissolve,<BR>melt; to cause to vanish or disappear, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलय|विलयः
वि-लय, अस्, m. dissolution, liquefaction, death,<BR>destruction, destruction of the world, (विलयं गम्,<BR>to be dissolved, to end.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयन|विलयनं
वि-लयन, अम्, n. the act of dissolving, liquefy-<BR>ing, dissolution, liquefaction, destroying; corroding,<BR>eating away; removing, taking away; attenuating;<BR>an attenuant, escharotic (in medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलापित
वि-लापित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), caused to be<BR>dissolved, liquefied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाप्यमान
वि-लाप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being caused to be<BR>dissolved, being liquefied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाय|विलायं|विलायः
वि-लाय, ind. = वि-लीय, Pāṇ. VI. 1, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलायम्
वि-लायम्, ind. becoming dissolved, melting away,<BR>becoming dispersed, (अभ्र-विलायम्, in the manner<BR>of the dissolving of a cloud, Kirāt. XI. 79.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलायित
वि-लायित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), made liquid,<BR>dissolved, melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीन|विलीनः
वि-लीन, अस्, आ, अम्, clinging to, sticking or cleav-<BR>ing to, attached to, addicted to, immersed in; settled<BR>on, alighting on [cf. शाखा-व्˚]; contiguous to, in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">Page0938-b+ 77</a>]<BR>contact with, united or blended with; infused into<BR>the mind, imagined; dissolved, liquid, liquefied,<BR>melted, semifluid (as melted oil or butter, &c.);<BR>disappeared, perished, vanished.<BR>—विलीन-षट्पद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having bees clinging or attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीय
वि-लीय, ind. having settled down, having become<BR>dissolved, having disappeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीयत्
वि-लीयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, clinging to, settling; be-<BR>coming dissolved, liquefying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीयमान
वि-लीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being dissolved or<BR>melted, &c., disappearing, being hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुञ्च्
विलुञ्च् वि-लुञ्च्, cl. 1. P. -लुञ्चति, -लुञ्चितुम्,<BR>to tear off, tear out, pluck off, tear to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुञ्चन|विलुंचनं
वि-लुञ्चन, अम्, n. the act of tearing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुठ्
विलुठ् वि-लुठ्, cl. 6. P. -लुठति, -लुठितुम्,<BR>to roll, roll or move about, move to and fro, quiver,<BR>flicker; to agitate, move, stir, rouse, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुठत्
वि-लुठत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, rolling, moving to<BR>and fro, sparkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुठित
वि-लुठित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुड्
विलुड् वि-लुड् (closely connected with वि-<BR>लुल्), Caus. -लोडयति, &c., to agitate, stir about,<BR>stir up, rouse, move to and fro, toss about; to turn<BR>over, upset; to disarrange, disturb, disorder, confuse,<BR>throw into disorder or confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडन|विलोडनं
वि-लोडन, अम्, n. the act of agitating, shaking,<BR>stirring, churning, rolling, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडयितृ
वि-लोडयितृ, ता, m. an agitator, disturber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडित|विलोडितं
वि-लोडित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, shaken, churned;<BR>rolling or tumbling on the ground; (अम्), n. butter-<BR>milk (= तक्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोड्यमान
वि-लोड्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being agitated, being<BR>stirred about or up, being tossed about; being thrown<BR>into disorder, being disarranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुण्ट्य
विलुण्ट्य वि-लुण्ट्य, ind. having taken<BR>away, having taken off the husk, (in Pañca-tantra,<BR>p. 121, 13, a better reading has लुञ्चित्वा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुण्ठ्
विलुण्ठ् वि-लुण्ठ्, cl. 1. P. -लुण्ठति, -लुण्-<BR>ठितुम्, to carry off, rob, plunder, steal: Pass.<BR>-लुण्ठ्यते, to be plundered or ravaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुण्ठन|विलुंठन|विलुंठनं
वि-लुण्ठन, अम्, n. the act of plundering, robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुण्ठित
वि-लुण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, robbed, plundered, pil-<BR>laged; rolled or rolling about (= वि-लुठित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्
विलुप् वि-लुप्, cl. 6. P. A. -लुम्पति, -ते,<BR>-लोप्तुम्, to tear or break off, cut off; to tear or<BR>break to pieces, pull out or up; to tear or carry<BR>away, carry off, ravish, seize, plunder, rob, pillage;<BR>to destroy, confound, ruin; to fall to pieces, be<BR>ruined (A.): Pass. -लुप्यते, to be torn away or<BR>carried off, be plundered, be destroyed, perish, be<BR>lost, disappear, fail: Caus. -लोपयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>tear or carry away, withhold, keep back; to cause to<BR>disappear, destroy, ruin, oppress, extinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्त
वि-लुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, torn off or away, broken off,<BR>broken; carried off or away, snatched away, seized,<BR>taken, plundered, robbed; destroyed, ruined, lost;<BR>impaired, mutilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुम्पक|विलुंपक|विलुंपकः|विलुम्पकः
वि-लुम्पक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who breaks or cuts<BR>off; one who seizes or robs; a robber, ravisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुम्पत्
वि-लुम्पत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, tearing or pluck-<BR>ing off, tearing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोप|विलोपः
वि-लोप, अस्, m. carrying off, seizing, taking away;<BR>a break or interruption in the Saṃhitā (according<BR>to the Prātiśākhyas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपन|विलोपनं
वि-लोपन, अम्, n. the act of tearing or breaking<BR>to pieces, cutting off, destroying, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपित
वि-लोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn away, broken, ruined,<BR>destroyed, oppressed, extinguished, put out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभ्
विलुभ् वि-लुभ्, cl. 4. P. -लुभ्यति, -लोभि-<BR>तुम् or -लोब्धुम्, to become disordered or disar-<BR>ranged, fall into disorder or confusion: Caus. -लोभ-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to lead astray, perplex, confuse; to<BR>allure, entice, tempt; to divert, amuse, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभित
वि-लुभित, अस्, आ, अम्, disordered, disarranged,<BR>disturbed, agitated, bewildered; tossed or shaken<BR>about.<BR>—विलुभित-प्लव, अस्, आ, अम्, going in an<BR>agitated manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ|विलोभः
वि-लोभ, अस्, m. attraction, delusion, seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभन|विलोभनं
वि-लोभन, अम्, n. the act of leading astray, per-<BR>plexing, beguiling; allurement, attraction, temptation,<BR>seduction; flattering, praise, commendation (especially<BR>by contrast with inferiority).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभयत्
वि-लोभयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, alluring, enticing;<BR>diverting, amusing, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभित
वि-लोभित, अस्, आ, अम्, allured, beguiled; deceived;<BR>flattered, praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ्य
वि-लोभ्य, ind. having enticed or beguiled, having<BR>fascinated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ्यमान
वि-लोभ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being allured or en-<BR>ticed, being fascinated, being overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुल्
विलुल् वि-लुल् (closely connected with वि-<BR>लुड्), cl. 1. P. -लोलति, &c., to move or roll about;<BR>to become disarranged or confused: Caus. -लोलयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to move or roll about, agitate, dis-<BR>turb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुलित
वि-लुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, moved hither and thither;<BR>shaken down, falling down, rolling down; shaken,<BR>shaking about, agitated, waving, tremulous, unsteady,<BR>fickle; disordered, disarranged.<BR>—विलुलितालक (˚त-<BR>अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having disordered or dishevelled<BR>locks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोल|विलोलः
वि-लोल, अस्, आ, अम्, moving or shaking about;<BR>shaking, trembling, tremulous, fickle, unsteady, loose;<BR>rolling (as the eye), rolling or tossing about, waving.<BR>—विलोल-ता, f. or विलोल-त्व, अम्, n. tremulousness,<BR>unsteadiness; rolling (of the eyes).<BR>—विलोल-हार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having necklaces tossing about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलन|विलोलनं
वि-लोलन, अम्, n. the act of shaking; stirring,<BR>agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलित
वि-लोलित, अस्, आ, अम्, moved hither and thither,<BR>shaken about, agitated, tossed about.<BR>—विलोलित-दृश्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, rolling the eyes, having tremulous eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलून
विलून वि-लून, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, cut asunder,<BR>cut off, cut, (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 52, Vārtt. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक्
विलोक् वि-लोक्, cl. 1. A. -लोकते, -लोकितुम्,<BR>to look at or upon, regard; to examine, test, study;<BR>cl. 10. P. or Caus. -लोकयति, -यितुम्, to look at,<BR>look on or upon, look towards, behold, regard, ob-<BR>serve, consider, examine; to perceive, see, discover,<BR>be aware of; to look over or beyond (with acc.):<BR>Pass. -लोक्यते, to be seen, be visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकन|विलोकनं
वि-लोकन, अम्, n. the act of looking or regarding,<BR>discerning, seeing, spying; sight, observation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकनीय
वि-लोकनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be looked at; worthy<BR>of being looked at, agreeable, beautiful.<BR>—विलोकनीय-<BR>ता, f. or विलोकनीय-त्व, अम्, n. a state worthy of<BR>being looked at, loveliness, beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकयत्|विलोकयन्त्
वि-लोकयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, looking at, seeing; dis-<BR>cerning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकित|विलोकितं
वि-लोकित, अस्, आ, अम्, looked at, beheld, seen,<BR>observed, regarded, examined, contemplated; (अम्),<BR>n. a look, glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक्य
वि-लोक्य, ind. having looked at, having seen or<BR>observed, having perceived or noticed or witnessed;<BR>having regard to, paying attention to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक|विलोकः
विलोक वि-लोक, अस्, आ, अम्, apart from the<BR>world, solitary, lonely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचन|विलोचनं
विलोचन वि-लोचन, अम्, n. the eye, sight.<BR>—विलोचन-पात, अस्, m. a cast or glance of the<BR>eye, a glance, look.<BR>—विलोचनाम्बु (˚न-अम्˚), उ,<BR>n. ‘eye-water,’ tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोटक|विलोटकः
विलोटक वि-लोटक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. लुट् with<BR>वि), a sort of fish, Clupea Cultrata (= नल-मीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडन|विलोडनं
विलोडन वि-लोडन, &c. See under वि-लुड्,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोप|विलोपः
विलोप वि-लोप, &c. See under वि-लुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ|विलोभः
विलोभ वि-लोभ, &c. See under वि-लुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोम|विलोमं|विलोमः
विलोम वि-लोम, अस्, ई, अम्, against the hair,<BR>against the grain, out of the usual or proper course,<BR>reverse, inverted, inverse, turned the wrong way,<BR>turned backward, contrary, opposite; produced in<BR>the reverse order [cf. विलोम-ज]; (अस्), m. reverse<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">Page0939-a+ 77</a>]<BR>order, opposite course, reverse; a snake; a dog; an<BR>epithet of Varuṇa (the regent of the waters); (अम्),<BR>n. a water-wheel or machine for raising water from<BR>a well (= अर-घट्टक); (ई), f. Emblic Myrobalan.<BR>—विलोम-क्रिया, f. reverse action, doing anything<BR>in reverse order or backwards; (in arithmetic) rule of<BR>inversion.<BR>—विलोम-ज or विलोम-जात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘born out of the proper course or in the reverse<BR>order,’ i. e. one whose father and mother have their<BR>stations reversed, the father being of an inferior caste<BR>and the mother of a superior.<BR>—विलोम-जिह्व, अस्,<BR>m. an elephant (as having a tongue which moves<BR>backwards ?).<BR>—विलोम-त्रैराशिक, अम्, n. rule of<BR>three inverse.<BR>—विलोम-वर्ण, अस्, m. ‘of reverse<BR>caste,’ a man of mixed or inferior birth, (see विलोम-<BR>ज above.)<BR>—विलोम-विधि, इस्, m. an inverted rite,<BR>reversed ceremony; (in arithmetic) rule of inversion.<BR>—विलोमाक्षर-काव्य (˚म-अक्˚), अम्, n. a poem<BR>which may be read either backwards or forwards; =<BR>राम-कृष्ण-काव्य, q. v.<BR>—विलोमोत्पन्न (˚म-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, = विलोम-ज above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0938-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमित
वि-लोमित, अस्, आ, अम्, reversed, inverted, made<BR>averse or disaffected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोल|विलोलः
विलोल वि-लोल, वि-लोलित, &c. See p. 938.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोहित|विलोहितः
विलोहित वि-लोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, of a deep-red<BR>or purple colour; (अस्), m. epithet of Rudra and Fire<BR>(as identified with Rudra); (आ), f. (according to<BR>some), epithet of one of the tongues of fire; [cf. सु-<BR>लोहित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्ल|विल्लं
विल्ल विल्ल, अम्, n. (probably connected with<BR>विल), a pit, hole, a basin for water round the root<BR>of a tree (= आलवाल); Asa Fetida.<BR>—विल्ल-मूला,<BR>f. a sort of yam (= वाराही).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्व|विल्वं|विल्वः
विल्व विल्व, अस्, m. (fr. rt. विल्, also written<BR>बिल्व, q. v.), the tree Ægle Marmelos (commonly<BR>called Bel); (अम्), n. the fruit of the Bel; a particu-<BR>lar weight, (see बिल्व.) For the compounds of विल्व<BR>see बिल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्वस्
विवक्वस् विवक्वस्, वान्, m. (fr. rt. वच्, q. v.),<BR>Ved. one who repeats (praises), praising, a praiser,<BR>(Sāy. = स्तुतीनां वक्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षा
विवक्षा विवक्षा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. वच्), a<BR>wish or desire to speak; meaning, sense; intention, pur-<BR>pose, wish, desire; a question.<BR>—विवक्षा-वशात्, ind.<BR>according to the meaning (of a speaker or writer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षण
विवक्षण, अस्, &c., Ved. (fr. rt. वच् or rt. 1.<BR>वह्), ‘making eloquent,’ or according to Sāy. ‘bring-<BR>ing to heaven’ (= स्वर्ग-प्रापण-शील), an epithet<BR>of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षत्
विवक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, desiring to mention,<BR>wishing or intending to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षमाण
विवक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing or desiring<BR>to speak about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षित|विवक्षितः
विवक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished or intended to be<BR>spoken or said; purposed, intended; meant, signified,<BR>really meant, literal (not figurative); wished, desired;<BR>favourite, handsome; (अम्), n. what is intended to be<BR>said or declared, meaning, sense, purpose, intention,<BR>any desired object or aim; (आ), f. meaning, purpose,<BR>wish (?).<BR>—विवक्षित-त्व, अम्, n. the being intended<BR>or meant to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षु
विवक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to speak, intending<BR>to say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवच्
विवच् वि-वच् (see rt. वच्), cl. 2. P. -वक्ति (in<BR>the non-conjugational tenses also A.), -वक्तुम्, to de-<BR>clare, announce, explain, interpret, solve; to dispute<BR>about, speak against, oppose in argument; to speak va-<BR>riously or differently, to dispute with one another (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्तृ
वि-वक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who declares or ex-<BR>plains, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाक|विवाकः
वि-वाक, अस्, m. one who decides causes, a judge;<BR>[cf. प्रश्न-व्˚, प्राड्-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाच्
वि-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. of various speech, having<BR>various speeches, variously praising, (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda VI. 33, 2. वि-वाचः = विविध-स्तुति-<BR>रूपा वाचो येषाम्, whose words have the form of<BR>many kinds of praise); (क्), f., Ved. various speech or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">Page0939-b+ 74</a>]<BR>praise; N. of a particular sacrifice in which various<BR>prayers and praises are repeated; dispute, controversy,<BR>contention, strife (= सङ्ग्राम, Naigh. II. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवञ्चिषु|विवंचिषु
विवञ्चिषु विवञ्चिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. वञ्च्), wishing to deceive; crafty, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवत्सा
विवत्सा वि-वत्सा, f. a calfless cow, one<BR>whose calf is dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवद्
विवद् वि-वद्, cl. 1. P. A. -वदति, -ते, -व-<BR>दितुम्, to dispute, oppose in argument, contradict,<BR>controvert, litigate, dispute about, discuss about (with<BR>loc. of the thing disputed about); to dispute with or<BR>engage in a discussion with any one (acc.); to cry out:<BR>Caus. -वादयति, -यितुम्, to cause to dispute or liti-<BR>gate, commence an action or lawsuit: Intens. -वाव-<BR>दीति, &c., to roar aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदत्
वि-वदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wrangling, disputing, argu-<BR>ing, contending, debating, contradicting; litigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदमान|विवदमानः
वि-वदमान, अस्, आ, अम्, disputing, contending,<BR>mutually disagreeing or contradictory; litigating;<BR>crying out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदित
वि-वदित, अस्, आ, अम्, disputed, controverted, liti-<BR>gated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाद|विवादः
वि-वाद, अस्, m. a dispute, quarrel, controversy,<BR>debate, contest, strife, contention; an argument;<BR>contest at law, legal dispute, litigation, lawsuit; crying<BR>out, sound.<BR>—विवाद-कल्पतरु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—विवाद-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a compen-<BR>dium of civil law by an author named Misarū-miśra.<BR>—विवाद-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m., N. of a work by Vā-<BR>caspati-miśra.<BR>—विवाद-भङ्गार्णव (˚ग-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a compendium of civil law by Jagan-<BR>nātha (compiled at the close of the eighteenth cen-<BR>tury).<BR>—विवाद-शमन, अम्, n. the allaying or<BR>settling of a dispute, pacification.<BR>—विवाद-सं-<BR>वाद-भू, ऊस्, f. a matter or subject of controversy<BR>and discussion.<BR>—विवादानुगत (˚द-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘gone through a lawsuit,’ disputed, litigated.<BR>—विवादार्थिन् (˚द-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, seeking for a<BR>dispute; (ई), m. a litigant, prosecutor, plaintiff.<BR>—वि-<BR>वादास्पदी-भूत (˚द-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, become the<BR>subject of a lawsuit, litigated, contested at law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादिन्
विवादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, disputing, contending, litigating,<BR>disputatious, contentious; a litigant, party in a lawsuit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवावदत्
वि-वावदत्, अत्, अती, अत्, Ved. roaring aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवध्
विवध् वि-वध् (a defective verb, see rt.<BR>वध्), Ved. to destroy utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवध|विवधः
विवध वि-वध, अस्, m. (probably fr. rt. 1.<BR>वह् with वि), a yoke for carrying burdens, a load;<BR>a road, highway; storing grain, hay, &c.; a ewer,<BR>pitcher; [cf. वी-वध.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधिक|विवधिकः
विवधिक, अस्, m. a man who carries a burden;<BR>a dealer, peddler, hawker; [cf. वीवधिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवन्दिषु
विवन्दिषु विवन्दिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid.<BR>of rt. वन्द्), intending to praise; wishing to salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवप्
विवप् वि-वप्, cl. 1. P. A. -वपति, -ते, -वप्-<BR>तुम्, to strew or scatter about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युप्त
व्य्-उप्त. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर|विवरं|विवरः
विवर वि-वर, &c. See under वि-वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जन|विवर्जनं|विवर्ज्जन
विवर्जन वि-वर्जन, &c. See under वि-वृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ण|विवर्णः
विवर्ण वि-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, colourless, want-<BR>ing colour, changing colour, pale, wan, pallid; bad-<BR>coloured, discoloured; low, vile; unlettered, ignorant,<BR>stupid; (अस्), m. a man of low caste or of degrading<BR>occupation, an outcast.<BR>—विवर्ण-मणी-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, (a bracelet &c.) which has its jewels ren-<BR>dered discoloured.<BR>—विवर्ण-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pale-faced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त|विवर्तः|विवर्त्त|विवर्त्तः
विवर्त वि-वर्त, &c. See under वि-वृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ध्
विवर्ध् वि-वर्ध्, cl. 10. P. -वर्धयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cut off, sever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धन|विवर्धनं
1. वि-वर्धन, अम्, n. (for 2. see वि-वृध्), the<BR>act of cutting off, cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धित
1. वि-वर्धित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see वि-वृध्),<BR>cut off, cut, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्षत्
विवर्षत् वि-वर्षत्. See under वि-वृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवल्
विवल् वि-वल्, cl. 1. P. A. -वलति, -ते, -व-<BR>लितुम्, to turn away, avert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवलित
वि-वलित, अस्, आ, अम्, turned away, averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवल्ग्
विवल्ग् वि-वल्ग्, cl. 1. P. -वल्गति, &c., to<BR>leap, jump, spring; to burst asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवश|विवशः
विवश वि-वश, अस्, आ, अम्, unrestrained, un-<BR>subdued, uncontrolled; independant; subject, sub-<BR>jected; apprehensive of death; desirous of death (as<BR>having the soul free from worldly cares and fears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्
विवस् 1. वि-वस् (see rts. 3. वस्, 2. उष्, 2. व्य्-<BR>उष्), cl. 6. P. -उच्छति, &c., Ved. to shine forth,<BR>shine, dawn: Caus. -वासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वत्|विवस्वन्त्
विवस्वत्, आन्, m. ‘the brilliant one,’ N. of the<BR>Sun, (sometimes regarded as one of the eight Ādityas<BR>or sons of Aditi, his father being Kaśyapa; elsewhere<BR>he is said to be a son of Dākṣāyaṇī and Kaśyapa;<BR>in epic poetry he is held to be the father of Manu<BR>Vaivasvata [or according to another legend of Manu<BR>Sāvarṇi by Sa-varṇā], and therefore a kind of parent<BR>of the human race [see Manu]; in Ṛg-veda X. 17,<BR>1. he is described as the father of Yama Vaivasvata,<BR>and in Ṛg-veda X. 17, 2. as father of the Aśvins by<BR>Saraṇyū, and elsewhere as father of both Yama and<BR>Yamī; according to Nīla-kaṇṭha, the name विवस्वत्<BR>is derived fr. 2. वि-वस्, in the sense विशेषेण आच्छा-<BR>दयति); N. of Aruṇa (charioteer of the Sun); of<BR>the seventh or present Manu, (more properly called<BR>Vaivasvata, as son of Vivasvat); a god; N. of the<BR>author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 13 (having the<BR>patronymic Āditya); N. of the author of a Dharma-<BR>śāstra; (अती), f., N. of the city of the Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वन्
विवस्वन्, आ, &c., Ved. shining, possessing bright-<BR>ness; (Sāy. also ‘possessing wealth;’ in Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 102, 22. विवस्वभिः = ऋत्विग्भिः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासन|विवासनं
1. वि-वासन, अम्, n. manifestation, (Sāy. = प्र-<BR>काशन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
व्य्-उष्ट. See under 2. व्य्-उष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्
विवस् 2. वि-वस्, cl. 2. A. -वस्ते, -वसितुम्, to<BR>exchange clothes; to wear, put on (a garment), clothe:<BR>Caus. -वासयति, -यितुम्, to clothe, put on, cover:<BR>Pass. of Caus. -वास्यते, to be clothed or clad in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्
विवस् 3. वि-वस्, cl. 1. P. -वसति, -वस्तुम्,<BR>to change an abode, to depart, go off, retire, with-<BR>draw; to dwell, abide; to pass, spend (time &c.);<BR>to pass away: Caus. -वासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>dwell apart, banish, expel, drive into exile, transport,<BR>dismiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास|विवासः
1. वि-वास, अस्, m. banishment, expulsion.<BR>—विवास-<BR>करण, अम्, n. causing banishment, banishment,<BR>transporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासन|विवासनं
2. वि-वासन, अम्, n. the act of banishing, banish-<BR>ment, exile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासित
वि-वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, banished, expelled, forced<BR>into exile, transported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास्य
वि-वास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be expelled or exiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास्यमान
वि-वास्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being banished, being<BR>exiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युषित
व्य्-उषित, व्य्-उष्ट, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवसन|विवसनः
विवसन वि-वसन, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of<BR>garments, unclothed, naked; (अस्), m. a Jaina ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्त्र
वि-वस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of clothing, unclothed,<BR>naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास|विवासः
2. वि-वास, अस्, आ, अम्, or वि-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>without clothes, naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवह्
विवह् वि-वह्, cl. 1. P. -वहति, -वोढुम्, to<BR>bear away, remove, carry off, lead away; to conduct<BR>home, take in marriage, marry: Caus. -वाहयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cause to marry, give in marriage; to marry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवह|विवहः
वि-वह, अस्, m. ‘carrying away,’ epithet of one<BR>of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह|विवाहः
वि-वाह, अस्, m. the taking a wife, marriage, (eight<BR>kinds of marriage are enumerated in Manu III. 21,<BR>viz. Brāhma, Daiva, Ārṣa, Prājāpatya, Āsura, Gān-<BR>dharva, Rākṣasa, and Paiśāca; see also Yājñavalkya<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">Page0940-a+ 76</a>]<BR>I. 58 — 61.)<BR>—विवाह-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of<BR>marriage.<BR>—विवाह-चतुष्टय, अम्, n. a quadru-<BR>ple marriage, the marrying four wives.<BR>—विवाह-<BR>तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a part of the Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—विवाह-दीक्षा, f. the marriage rite, marriage<BR>ceremony.<BR>—विवाह-दीक्षा-तिलक, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>a Tilaka made on the forehead for a matrimonial cere-<BR>mony.<BR>—विवाह-दीक्षा-विधि, इस्, m. the preparatory<BR>rites of matrimony.<BR>—विवाह-यज्ञ, अस्, m. a matri-<BR>monial sacrifice.<BR>—विवाह-विधि, इस्, m. the law of<BR>marriage.<BR>—विवाह-वृन्दा-वन, N. of an astro-<BR>logical work by Keśavārka.<BR>—विवाहार्थ (˚ह-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. purpose of marriage, a marriage suit.<BR>—विवा-<BR>हेच्छु (˚ह-इच्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0939-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहित|विवाहितः
वि-वाहित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to marry, married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहिन्
विवाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, taking a wife, marrying; re-<BR>lating to marriage; [cf. अ-विवाहिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह्य|विवाह्यः
वि-वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be married, marriageable;<BR>(अस्), m. a son-in-law; a bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवोढृ
वि-वोढृ, ढा, m. one who takes in marriage, a<BR>bridegroom, husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढ|व्यूढः
व्य्-ऊढ. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवा
विवा वि-वा, cl. 2. P. -वाति, -वातुम्, to blow on<BR>all sides, blow in every direction, blow, blow through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवात्
वि-वात्, आन्, आती or आन्ती, आत्, blowing on all sides,<BR>blowing, blowing gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवायमन
वि-वायमन, अस्, आ, अम्, blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाक|विवाकः
विवाक वि-वाक, वि-वाच्. See under वि-वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाश
विवाश विवाश, आस्, m. pl., N. of a mythical<BR>caste in Plaksha-dvīpa (corresponding to the Vaiśyas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविंशति
विविंशति वि-विंशति, इस्, m., N. of one of<BR>Dhṛtarāṣṭra's sons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्वस्
विविक्वस् विविक्वस्, आन्, m. (fr. rt. विच्), Ved.<BR>one who possesses discrimination, discriminating; an<BR>epithet of Indra (in Ṛg-veda III. 57, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्ष्
विविक्ष् विविक्ष्, विविक्षत्, &c. See under<BR>rt. 1. विश्, p. 941, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविग्न
विविग्न वि-विग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, very agitated<BR>or alarmed, terrified; very angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविच्
विविच् वि-विच्, cl. 7. 3. P. A. -विनक्ति,<BR>-विङ्क्ते, -वेवेक्ति, -वेविक्ते, -वेक्तुम्, to separate or<BR>divide asunder, rend or tear asunder; to distinguish,<BR>discriminate, decide, judge between (two sides of a<BR>question); to alter; to tear up, remove: Caus. -वेच-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to separate, distinguish, discriminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्त|विविक्तं
वि-विक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, separated, disjoined, detached,<BR>kept apart, scattered, abstracted, sequestered; single,<BR>alone, lonely, solitary, private, deserted; distinguished,<BR>discriminated, judged; discriminative, judicious; pro-<BR>found (as judgment or thought); pure, faultless;<BR>intent on; (अम्), n. separation, loneliness, privacy,<BR>abstraction; a solitary place.<BR>—विविक्त-तर्क, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, clear in reasoning.<BR>—विविक्त-ता, f. the<BR>being separated, separation, loneliness, privacy; an<BR>empty or free space.<BR>—विविक्त-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a mind separated or abstracted (from other<BR>pursuits), intent on any object.<BR>—विविक्त-वर्ण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having letters or syllables distinctly enunciated.<BR>—विविक्त-सेविन्, ई, इनी, इ, seeking solitude, solitary,<BR>retired, recluse.<BR>—विविक्तासन (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a secluded seat, sitting in a sequestered place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविचि
वि-विचि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. separating, discriminating,<BR>a discriminator, (Sāy. = विवेचक); (इस्), m. ‘the<BR>separator,’ epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविच्य
वि-विच्य, ind. having discriminated or judged,<BR>having discussed or considered; having properly dis-<BR>criminated; dividing or discriminating in regular<BR>order; severally, one by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक|विवेकः
वि-वेक, अस्, m. discrimination, judgment, the<BR>faculty of distinguishing and classifying things ac-<BR>cording to their real properties; (in the Vedānta<BR>system) the power of separating the invisible Spirit<BR>from the visible world, (or spirit from matter, truth<BR>from untruth, reality from mere semblance or illu-<BR>sion); true knowledge; discretion; discussion, in-<BR>vestigation; a receptacle for water, reservoir, basin<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">Page0940-b+ 78</a>]<BR>(= जल-द्रोणी).<BR>—विवेक-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>or arising from discrimination.<BR>—विवेक-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, skilled in discrimination, intelligent.<BR>—विवेक-<BR>ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge arising from discrimina-<BR>tion, faculty of discrimination.<BR>—विवेक-ता, f. or<BR>विवेक-त्व, अम्, n. judgment, discrimination, the<BR>faculty of judgment.<BR>—विवेकदृश्व-ता, f. or विवेक-<BR>दृश्व-त्व, अम्, n. the character of a discerning man,<BR>discrimination, discernment.<BR>—विवेक-दृश्वन्, आ,<BR>m. one who sees or is conversant with true know-<BR>ledge, a wise or discerning man.<BR>—विवेक-पदवी,<BR>f. ‘path of discrimination,’ reflection.<BR>—विवेक-विलास,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—विवेक-सार, N. of a general<BR>Vedānta disquisition in sixteen sections by Rāmendra-<BR>yati.<BR>—विवेक-सिन्धु, N. of an elementary treatise<BR>on the Vedānta by Mukunda-rāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिन्
विवेकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, discriminating, discriminative,<BR>judicious, prudent, discreet; (ई), m. a judge, dis-<BR>criminator, sage, philosopher.<BR>—विवेकि-ता, f. or वि-<BR>वेकि-त्व, अम्, n. discriminativeness, discrimination,<BR>discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तव्य
वि-वेक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be distinguished or<BR>discriminated, to be discussed or judged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तृ
वि-वेक्तृ, ता, m. one who judges, a judge, decider<BR>(of questions or causes), sage, wise man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचन|विवेचनं
वि-वेचन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of discrimination,<BR>discriminating or distinguishing (as truth from false-<BR>hood, reality from semblance), the making a distinc-<BR>tion; investigation, judgment, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचनीय|विवेचनीयः
वि-वेचनीय or वि-वेच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be distin-<BR>guished or judged, to be discussed, distinguishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचित
वि-वेचित, अस्, आ, अम्, discriminated, distinguished,<BR>investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविदिवस्
