विविध|विविधं
विविध वि-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of various sorts<BR>or kinds, divers, manifold, sundry, various, multiform;<BR>(अम्), n. variety of action or gesture.<BR>—विविध-<BR>रूप-धृत्, त्, त्, त्, having various forms.<BR>—विविधा-<BR>गम (˚ध-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, comprising various<BR>sacred (or traditional) works.<BR>—विविधोपल-भू-<BR>षित (˚ध-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, decorated with various<BR>jewels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविशिवस्
विविशिवस् विविशिवस्, विविश्वस्. See p. 941.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीत|विवीतः
विवीत वि-वीत, अस्, m. an inclosed spot of<BR>ground (abounding in grass, wood, &c.), a preserved<BR>or inclosed pasture ground, paddock.<BR>—विवीत-भर्तृ,<BR>ता, m. the owner of a preserved or inclosed pasture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृ
विवृ वि-वृ, cl. 5. 9. P. A. -वृणोति, -वृणुते,<BR>वृणाति, -वृणीते (in the Veda the form व्य्-अवर्<BR>frequently becomes व्य्-आवर् or व्य्-आवः), -वरितुम्,<BR>-वरीतुम्, to uncover, spread out, open, unfold, dis-<BR>play, discover, reveal, make clear, illuminate, make<BR>manifest, proclaim, publish, explain, describe, com-<BR>ment upon; to cover over, cover up, stop up; to<BR>obtain (Ved., according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 90,<BR>4. विवव्रुः = व्यवृण्वन् = अलभन्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर|विवरं|विवरः
वि-वर, अस्, m. expansion, opening, widening,<BR>separation; (अम्), n. a fissure, hole, chasm, cave,<BR>cavern, burrow, hollow, vacuity; a sequestered or<BR>solitary place; interval, intermediate space, space; a<BR>breach, fault, flaw, defect, vulnerable place, weak<BR>point, wound; a symbolical expression for the number<BR>nine, (see रन्ध्र.)<BR>—विवर-नालिका, f. a pipe,<BR>fife, flute.<BR>—विवरे-सद्, त्, त्, त्, abiding in inter-<BR>mediate space, an inhabitant of the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरण|विवरणं
वि-वरण, अम्, n. the act of uncovering, spreading<BR>out, expanding, opening, unfolding, displaying, ex-<BR>posing, laying bare or open; explanation, exposition,<BR>interpretation, gloss, comment, translation; detailing,<BR>describing, description, specification, detailed account;<BR>a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरिषु
विवरिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to make manifest<BR>or display; wishing to explain or declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवार|विवारः
वि-वार, अस्, m. dilatation, expansion; open or<BR>expanded state of the organs of speech, expansion of<BR>the throat in articulation, (one of the Ābhyantara-<BR>prayatnas or efforts of articulate utterance which take<BR>place within the mouth, opposed to सं-वार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृण्वत्
वि-वृण्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, making manifest, explain-<BR>ing, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृण्वान
वि-वृण्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, uncovering, explaining,<BR>publishing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत|विवृतं
वि-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, uncovered, unconcealed, (अ-वि-<BR>वृत, hidden, concealed), unclosed, opened, open<BR>(as the organs of speech for articulation); bare, barren<BR>(as ground, earth, &c.); spread out, expanded, ex-<BR>tended, extensive, ample, spacious, large; displayed,<BR>unfolded, exposed, discovered, made manifest, evi-<BR>dent; published, divulged, proclaimed, explained,<BR>interpreted, expounded; (अम्), ind. openly, in the<BR>sight of every one; (आ), f. a particular disease, an<BR>ulcer attended with much pain and heat; (अम्), n.<BR>(in grammar) open articulation, approach of the tongue<BR>towards the organ of speech but without contact.<BR>—विवृत-पौरुष, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose prowess<BR>is displayed, displaying valour.<BR>—विवृत-स्मयन,<BR>अम्, n. an open smile, a smile by which the teeth<BR>are shown.<BR>—विवृताक्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, open-<BR>eyed, large-eyed; (अस्), m. a cock.<BR>—विवृतास्य<BR>(˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, open-mouthed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतवत्
विवृतवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has opened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृति|विवृतिः
वि-वृति, इस्, f. expansion, making clear, manifesta-<BR>tion; display; exposure, discovery; explanation, ex-<BR>position, gloss, comment, interpretation.<BR>—विवृति-<BR>विमर्शिनी, f., N. of a work by Abhinava-gupta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्य
वि-वृत्य, ind. having uncovered, having opened,<BR>having expanded, displaying wide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्ण
विवृक्ण वि-वृक्ण. See under वि-व्रश्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृज्
विवृज् वि-वृज्, Caus. or cl. 10. P. A. -वर्ज-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, to exclude; to avoid, shun, abandon,<BR>leave; to distribute, give: Pass. of Caus. -वर्ज्यते,<BR>to be avoided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जन|विवर्जनं|विवर्ज्जन
वि-वर्जन, अम्, n. the act of excluding, abandon-<BR>ing, leaving, shunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जनीय|विवर्ज्जनीय
वि-वर्जनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be excluded, to be<BR>abandoned, to be shunned or avoided, to be quitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जयत्|विवर्ज्जयत्
वि-वर्जयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, avoiding, shunning,<BR>leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जित|विवर्ज्जित
वि-वर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, left, abandoned; avoided<BR>by, shunned by (with inst. or at the end of a comp.);<BR>destitute of, deprived of, entirely free or exempt<BR>from, without, (मान-विवर्जितम्, ind. without<BR>honour, dishonourably); excepting, excluding; dis-<BR>tributed, given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्य
वि-वर्ज्य, ind. having avoided, having abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्त
वि-वृक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, abandoned, left; (आ), f. a<BR>woman disliked or deserted by her husband (= दुर्-<BR>भगा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृण्
विवृण् वि-वृण्, cl. 6. P. -वृणति, &c., or<BR>Caus., to exhilarate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्
विवृत् वि-वृत्, cl. 1. A. -वर्तते (rarely P.<BR>-वर्तति), -वर्तितुम्, to turn round, roll round, re-<BR>volve, whirl round; to roll onwards, become unrolled;<BR>to roll over; to turn or roll about, roll or turn hither<BR>and thither, move about, wind about; to move<BR>through; to roll or turn away from, depart from,<BR>turn back, return; to roll down, descend; to attack:<BR>Caus. -वर्तयति, -यितुम्, to cause to turn round or<BR>revolve, cause to alternate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त|विवर्तः|विवर्त्त|विवर्त्तः
वि-वर्त, अस्, m. turning round, revolving, revolu-<BR>tion, going or whirling round; dancing; rolling<BR>onwards; unrolling, rolling back, returning, rolling<BR>about, moving hither and thither, changing from one<BR>state to another, passing through various existences<BR>or states of being; modification, altered condition;<BR>human error (consisting in the mistaking unreal<BR>objects and conceiving them to be what they are<BR>not, as mirage for water, a rope for a snake, &c.);<BR>the unreal (as opposed to Brahma the only real<BR>essence); collection, assemblage, heap, multitude.<BR>—विवर्त-वाद, अस्, m. maintaining or asserting<BR>that Brahma or the one eternal essence manifests<BR>himself in various illusory forms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तन|विवर्तनं|विवर्त्तन|विवर्त्तनं
वि-वर्तन, अम्, n. (in some senses fr. the Caus.),<BR>turning round, revolving, revolution (as of a wheel<BR>&c.), whirling or going round, circumambulating<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">Page0941-a+ 75</a>]<BR>(an altar &c.); reverential salutation; rolling back,<BR>returning; rolling down, descending; passing through<BR>a change or succession of various states or existences;<BR>existing, being, abiding, continuing; tossing to and<BR>fro; causing to revolve or go round; whirling round;<BR>causing to change, overturning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0940-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तमान|विवर्त्तमान
वि-वर्तमान, अस्, आ, अम्, turning back or round,<BR>revolving, rolling onwards, turning back, declining,<BR>setting (as the sun), returning, recoiling; continuing<BR>or abiding (in any course of action).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तित|विवर्त्तित
वि-वर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, turned round, revolved,<BR>rolled or rolling about; whirled round; turned or<BR>moved about, moving hither and thither; unrolled,<BR>unfolded; returned, turned back or away, averted,<BR>turned the wrong way, distorted, bent, bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तिन्
वि-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, turning round, revolving;<BR>turning back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्त|विवृत्तं
वि-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, turned or twisted round,<BR>whirling, revolving, rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्ति|विवृत्तिः
वि-वृत्ति, इस्, f. turning round, revolution, rolling,<BR>whirling, tumbling; (in grammar) interval between<BR>two vowels, hiatus.<BR>—विवृत्ति-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>preceded by a hiatus.<BR>—विवृत्त्य्-अभिप्राय, अस्, m.<BR>an intended or apparent hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्सत्
विवृत्सत् विवृत्सत्. See under rt. 1. वृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृध्
विवृध् वि-वृध्, cl. 1. A. -वर्धते, -वर्-<BR>धितुम्, to grow up, increase, swell, become en-<BR>larged, become powerful; to prosper, thrive; to<BR>spring up, arise; to have reason to rejoice or be<BR>congratulated: Caus. -वर्धयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to grow or increase, enlarge, augment, magnify,<BR>amplify; to cause to prosper, advance, further; to<BR>elevate; to gratify, exhilarate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धत्
वि-वर्धत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, increasing, growing<BR>bigger, thriving, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धन|विवर्धनं
2. वि-वर्धन, अम्, n. (for 1. see वि-वर्ध्),<BR>the act of increasing, augmenting, increase, growth,<BR>augmentation, amplification, aggrandizement; (अस्, आ<BR>or ई, अम्), growing, increasing, advancing, furthering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धमान
वि-वर्धमान, अस्, आ, अम्, growing up, increas-<BR>ing, thriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धित
2. वि-वर्धित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see वि-वर्ध्),<BR>increased, augmented, enlarged; advanced, furthered;<BR>gratified, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्ध
वि-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, grown up, increased, en-<BR>larged, enhanced, augmented, intensified; large,<BR>abundant.<BR>—विवृद्ध-मत्सर, अस्, आ, अम्, whose<BR>anger or resentment is increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्धि|विवृद्धिः
वि-वृद्धि, इस्, f. growth, increase, great growth,<BR>augmentation, enlargement; prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृष्
विवृष् वि-वृष्, cl. 1. P. -वर्षति, -वर्षि-<BR>तुम्, to rain down, rain: Caus. -वर्षयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to rain, rain down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्षत्
वि-वर्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, deluging with rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृह्
विवृह् वि-वृह् (see rt. 1. वृह्), cl. 6. P. -वृहति,<BR>-वर्हितुम्, Ved. to rend asunder, tear to pieces, break<BR>up, split; to tear away, draw away, tear out, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृढ
वि-वृढ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. torn asunder, rent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृहत्|विवृहन्त्
विवृहत् विवृहत्, अन्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 163 (having the patro-<BR>nymic Kāśyapa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवे
विवे वि-वे, cl. 1. P. A. -वयति, -ते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to interweave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूत|व्यूतं
व्य्-ऊत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. interwoven, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेन्
विवेन् वि-वेन्, cl. 1. P. A. -वेनति, -ते, &c., to<BR>be hostile or ill-disposed, (in Ṛg-veda V. 78, 1. मा<BR>वि-वेनतम् = मा वि-कामौ भवतम्, [O Aśvins]<BR>be not ill-disposed.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेल्ल्
विवेल्ल् वि-वेल्ल्, cl. 1. P. -वेल्लति, &c., to<BR>struggle, tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवोढृ
विवोढृ वि-वोढृ. See under वि-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्रत
विव्रत वि-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. perform-<BR>ing various religious actions or ceremonies; many-<BR>actioned (said of horses; Sāy. = विविध-कर्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्रश्च्
विव्रश्च् वि-व्रश्च्, cl. 6. P. -वृश्चति, &c.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">Page0941-b+ 79</a>]<BR>Ved. to cut off, cut asunder, separate, sever; to<BR>destroy; to be cut asunder, cut off, (Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda III. 53, 22 = विच्छिद्यते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्ण
वि-वृक्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. entirely severed or<BR>cut asunder, cut off, (Sāy. = विशेषतश् छिन्न.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृश्चत्
वि-वृश्चत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, Ved. cutting<BR>asunder, separating, scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्वोक|विव्वोकः
विव्वोक विव्वोक, अस्, m. (etymology doubt-<BR>ful), affectation of indifference, (one of the ten forms<BR>of amorous dalliance practised by women to excite<BR>love; cf. वि-कृत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश् 1. विश् (some of the forms and<BR>meanings of this rt. are identical with<BR>those of rt. 2. विष्), cl. 6. P. विशति (ep. also A. -ते),<BR>विवेश, वेक्ष्यति, अविक्षत्, वेष्टुम् (Ved. Impv.<BR>2nd sing. विविड्ढि = प्रविश, according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda I. 27, 10, but cf. rt. 2. विष्), to<BR>enter, enter in (with acc.); to pierce, penetrate;<BR>to pervade; to sit or settle down on (with acc.); to<BR>come to, come into the possession of, fall to the lot<BR>of; to undertake, begin, (in Naigh. II. 14. वेशिष्टि<BR>is enumerated among the गति-कर्माणः): Caus.<BR>वेशयति, -यितुम्, अवीविशत्, to cause to enter, &c.:<BR>Desid. विविक्षति: Intens. वेविश्यते, वेवेष्टि; [cf.<BR>Zend vīś, ‘to come;’ Gr. ἵκ-ω, ἱκ-νέ-ο-μαι, ἱκ-αν-ω, ἱκ-έ-τη-ς,<BR>ἱκ-τήρ, ἱκ-τήρ, ἱκετή-σιο-ς, ἱκ-ανό-ς, ἴκ-μενο-ς.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्ष्
विविक्ष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, or ड्, ड्, ड् (fr. the Desid.), one<BR>who wishes to enter, (see Vopa-deva III. 151.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षत्
विविक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing to enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षु
विविक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing or intending to enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविशिवस्
विविशिवस्, आन्, उषी, अत्, one who has entered,<BR>(see Pāṇ. VII. 2, 68.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविश्वस्
विविश्वस्, आन्, उषी, अत्, = विविशिवस् above; [cf.<BR>also विविश्वस् under rt. विछ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
2. विश्, ट्, m. (Ved. loc. pl. विक्षु, Ṛg-veda IV.<BR>37, 1), a man who settles down on or occupies the soil,<BR>an agriculturist, merchant, a man of the third or agri-<BR>cultural caste (= वैश्य, q. v.); a man in general;<BR>people; N. of any class of gods designated by troops<BR>(Ved.); (ट्), f. entrance; a family, house, tribe,<BR>host, race (Ved.); a daughter; [cf. Zend vīś, ‘a<BR>house, hamlet;’ Goth. vaihts; Angl. Sax. wiht;<BR>Old Germ. ni-wiht, eo-wiht, neo-wiht.]<BR>—विट्-<BR>पण्य, अम्, n. the wares of a man of the mercantile<BR>class, goods, merchandise.<BR>—विट्-पति, इस्, m. a chief<BR>of men of the mercantile class, head merchant; a<BR>daughter's husband, son-in-law.<BR>—विट्-शूद्र, आस्, m.<BR>pl. Vaiśyas and Śūdras.<BR>—विशाम्-पति, इस्, m. a lord<BR>of men, lord of people, a king, sovereign, (perhaps<BR>so called as especially ‘lord of the Vaiśyas,’ the<BR>Brāhmans being his superiors and the Kṣatriyas his<BR>equals.)<BR>—विश्-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of the house,<BR>lord of men, lord of the people, king; epithet of<BR>Agni; [cf. Zend viś-paiti; Lith. wies-patis, wies-<BR>patene; Mold. hospodar; (perhaps also) Gr. δεσπότης.<BR>]<BR>—विश्-पत्नी, f., Ved. the mistress or protec-<BR>tress of mankind (applied to the fire of attrition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश|विशं
विश = 2. विश् (at the end of a comp.); (अम्), n.<BR>the film or fibres of the stalk of the water-lily (=<BR>विष, विस).<BR>—विशं-वरा, f. = पल्ली.<BR>—विश-<BR>कण्ठिन्, ई, m. a kind of crane; [cf. विस-कण्-<BR>ठिका.]<BR>—विशाकर (˚श-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘filled with<BR>fibres,’ the plant Euphorbia (= भद्र-चूड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशत्
विशत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, entering, entering into,<BR>penetrating, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्य
विश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to the people,<BR>kindly disposed to the people, (Sāy. = विड्भ्यो हित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ट|विष्टः
1. विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 946, col. 3), en-<BR>tered, penetrated, pervaded.<BR>—विष्ट-पुर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टि|विष्टिः
1. विष्टि, इस्, f. (for 2. see p. 946, col. 3), N. of<BR>particular astronomical Karaṇas; N. of a daughter<BR>of Sūrya and Chāyā.<BR>—विष्टि-व्रत, अम्, n. a parti-<BR>cular religious ceremony in honour of Viṣṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश|वेशः
वेश, वेश्य, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्क्|विशंक्
विशङ्क् वि-शङ्क्, cl. 1. A. -शङ्कते, -शङ्कि-<BR>तुम्, to suspect, doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्क|विशंक|विशङ्कः
वि-शङ्क, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वि privative + शङ्का),<BR>fearless, undaunted; (अम्), ind. fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कनीय
वि-शङ्कनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be suspected or<BR>doubted, doubtful, suspicious; questionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कमान
वि-शङ्कमान, अस्, आ, अम्, suspecting, doubting,<BR>fearing, apprehending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्का
वि-शङ्का, f. suspicion, doubt, fear, apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कट|विशंकट|विशङ्कटः
विशङ्कट वि-शङ्कट, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (for वि-<BR>सङ्कट), great, large; strong, vehement; (अम्),<BR>ind. vehemently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशद्
विशद् वि-शद्, Caus. -शातयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to fall to pieces, break to pieces; to rend<BR>asunder; to scatter in all directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशद|विशदः
वि-शद, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be connected with<BR>वि-शद् above), clear, pure, pellucid, spotless, perspi-<BR>cuous; white, of a white colour; evident, apparent,<BR>obvious, manifest; beautiful; (अस्), m. white, the<BR>colour.<BR>—विशद-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, of pure efful-<BR>gence, shedding pure light.<BR>—विशदी-कृ, cl. 8. P.<BR>-करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make clear, explain, illustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशातन|विशातनं|विशातनः
वि-शातन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Caus.), causing to<BR>fall to pieces, rending asunder; setting free, de-<BR>livering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशातयित्वा
वि-शातयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having broken in<BR>pieces, having scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशय|विशयः
विशय वि-शय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शी with वि),<BR>doubt, uncertainty; refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशयिन्
विशयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dubious, uncertain; doubting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाय|विशायः
वि-शाय, अस्, m. sleeping and watching alternately<BR>(applied to watchmen who sleep and watch by turns;<BR>cf. उप-शाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशर|विशरः
विशर वि-शर, &c. See under वि-शॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल
विशल विशल, अस्, m. (for विशाल?), N. of the<BR>son of Abja; (आ), f., N. of a town; [cf. वैशली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्य|विशल्यः
विशल्य वि-शल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>thorns or darts; free from trouble or embarrass-<BR>ment, without care or pain; (आ), f. a twining shrub,<BR>Menispermum Cordifolium; a sort of pot-herb; the<BR>plant Croton Polyandrum (commonly called Danti);<BR>Convolvulus Turpethum (commonly called Teori);<BR>a sort of fruit, Langaliya; (probably) N. of a stream<BR>or river.<BR>—विशल्य-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, freeing from pain<BR>or distress; (त्), m. the climbing plant Echites Di-<BR>chotoma.<BR>—विशल्या-सङ्गम, अस्, m. ‘union with<BR>Viśalyā,’ N. of a chapter of the Revā-māhātmya.<BR>—विशल्या-सम्भव, अस्, m. ‘origin of Viśalyā,’<BR>N. of a chapter of the Revā-māhātmya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्
विशस् वि-शस्, cl. 1. P. -शसति, -शसितुम्, to<BR>cut up, dissect, kill, destroy; to immolate, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसन|विशसनं|विशसनः
वि-शसन, अम्, n. the act of cutting up, dissect-<BR>ing; killing, slaying, immolating, slaughter; ruin;<BR>N. of one of the divisions of Naraka; (अस्), m. a<BR>sabre, crooked sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसित|विशसितः
वि-शसित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut up, dissected; killed, im-<BR>molated; rude, ill-mannered, (see 1. वि-शस्त below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसितृ
वि-शसितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who cuts up or dissects<BR>(Manu V. 51), a dissector; a killer, immolator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त|विशस्तः
1. वि-शस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cut up, dissected; bold,<BR>fierce, ill-mannered, rude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्तृ
वि-शस्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who kills or dis-<BR>sects; (ता), m. an immolator, sacrificer; a Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्य
वि-शस्य, ind. having cut up or dissected, having<BR>immolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त|विशस्तः
विशस्त 2. वि-शस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. शंस्<BR>with वि), praised, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त्र
विशस्त्र वि-शस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, weaponless,<BR>disarmed, unarmed.<BR>—विशस्त्र-त्व, अम्, n. an un-<BR>armed or defenceless condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाकार
विशाकार विशाकार, अस्, m. the plant Eu-<BR>phorbia, (probably for विशाकर, see under विश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाख|विशाखः
विशाख वि-शाख, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. शाखा with<BR>वि), branchless; having spreading branches; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Kārttikeya; of a son of Kārttikeya (as son<BR>of Agni); an attitude in shooting (standing with<BR>the feet a span apart); a solicitor, petitioner, beggar;<BR>a spindle; (आ), f. or (ए), f. du., N. of one of the<BR>lunar asterisms (figured by a decorated gateway or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">Page0942-a+ 74</a>]<BR>arch and containing four or originally two stars<BR>placed under the regency of a dual divinity, इन्द्राग्नी,<BR>Indra and Agni; it is probably to be connected with<BR>the quadrangle of stars ι, α , β, γ Libræ; see नक्-<BR>षत्र); the cucurbitaceous plant Momordica Cha-<BR>rantia, (in this sense fem. sing.)<BR>—विशाख-ज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘born under the asterism Viśākha,’ the orange,<BR>Citrus Aurantium (as coming into season when the<BR>sun is in this asterism, or about the end of October).<BR>—विशाख-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Mudrā-rākṣasa drama.<BR>—विशाख-यूप, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0941-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखल|विशाखलं
विशाखल, अम्, n. an attitude in shooting. (See<BR>वि-शाख.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखिल
विशाखिल विशाखिल, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशातन|विशातनं|विशातनः
विशातन वि-शातन, &c. See under वि-शद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाप
विशाप विशाप, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारण|विशारणं
विशारण वि-शारण. See under वि-शॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारद|विशारदः
विशारद विशारद, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be<BR>connected with विशाल), learned, wise; skilful, skilled<BR>in, versed in, conversant with (often at the end of<BR>comps., cf. सर्व-शास्त्र-व्˚); famous, celebrated;<BR>confident, bold, presuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाल|विशालः
विशाल विशाल, अस्, आ, अम् (in Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>117. said to be fr. rt. 1. विश्; according to some<BR>connected with 2. वि-श्रि), large, great, wide, broad,<BR>extensive; great, eminent, illustrious; (अस्), m. a<BR>sort of deer; a sort of bird; N. of a son of Tṛṇa-<BR>vindu; (आ), f., N. of the city Ujjayinī or Ougein;<BR>of another town (see वैशाली, वैशली); the bitter<BR>apple, Cucumis Colocynthis; (ई), f. a particular plant<BR>(= अज-मोदा).<BR>—विशाल-कुल, अम्, n. a great or<BR>illustrious family; (अस्, आ, अम्), of noble family.<BR>—विशाल-कुल-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from<BR>an illustrious race.<BR>—विशाल-ता, f. or विशाल-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. largeness, greatness, width, breadth, expansion,<BR>magnitude, bulk; eminence, distinction.<BR>—विशाल-<BR>त्वच्, क्, m. ‘having large bark,’ the tree Echites<BR>Scholaris.<BR>—विशाल-नगर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—विशाल-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, large-eyed.<BR>—विशाल-<BR>पुरी, f., N. of a town.<BR>—विशालाक्ष (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, large-eyed, having beautiful eyes; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Śiva; of Garuḍa; N. of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra; (ई), f. epithet of Pārvatī; N. of a daughter<BR>of Śāṇḍilya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिक्षु
विशिक्षु वि-शिक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ (see शिक्षु),<BR>Ved. especially instructing or accomplishing, (Sāy. =<BR>विशेषेण शिक्षयितृ, साधयितृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिख|विशिखः
विशिख वि-शिख, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of the<BR>Śikhā or tuft of hair left on the head after tonsure;<BR>pointless, without a point or top, without a crest;<BR>weak (Ved. ?); (अस्), m. an arrow; an iron crow,<BR>(in these and some following senses वि may denote<BR>intensity or largeness); a sort of Śara or reed; (आ),<BR>f. a spade; a hoe; a minute arrow; a sort of pin or<BR>needle; a spindle; a highway, broad or carriage<BR>road; a barber's wife; a sick room or the dwelling<BR>of the sick.<BR>—विशिख-श्रेणी or विशिखावली (˚ख-<BR>आव्˚), f. a line of arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिञ्ज्
विशिञ्ज् वि-शिञ्ज्, cl. 2. A. -शिङ्क्ते, -शिञ्जितुम्,<BR>to sound, resound, tinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिञ्जान
वि-शिञ्जान, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding, singing, uttering<BR>cries; tinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशित
विशित वि-शित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शि or rt.<BR>शो with वि), sharpened, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिप|विशिपं
विशिप विशिप, अम्, n. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 145.<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. विश्), a house; a palace; a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिशिप्र
विशिशिप्र विशि-शिप्र, अस्, m. (so divided in<BR>the Pada text), Ved. ‘deprived of jaws’ or ‘noseless,’<BR>N. of a person represented in Ṛg-veda V. 45, 6, as<BR>conquered by Manu, (Sāy. = विगत-हनु; Sāy. also<BR>says that Manu may stand for Indra, and Viśi-śipra<BR>may mean Vṛtra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्
विशिष् वि-शिष्, cl. 7. P. -शिनष्टि, -शेष्टुम्,<BR>to distinguish, make distinct or different; to particu-<BR>larize, specify, define, describe; to excel (with acc.):<BR>Pass. -शिष्यते, to be distinguished; to differ or be<BR>different from; to be better than or more excellent<BR>than (with abl. and sometimes with inst., e. g. मौ-<BR>नात् सत्यं विशिष्यते, truth is more excellent than<BR>silence; यज्ञैः स्थितिर् विशिष्यते, continuance<BR>in duty is better than sacrifices); to be of more<BR>weight; to be best: Caus. -शेषयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>distinguish, make distinct or different, define.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्ट|विशिष्टः
वि-शिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, distinguished, distinct, par-<BR>ticular, especial, special, peculiar; having distinctive<BR>qualities or exclusive properties; superior, excellent,<BR>choice, more excellent, better; distinguished by, en-<BR>dowed with, possessed of, having; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—विशिष्ट-ता, f. or विशिष्ट-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>distinction, individuality, the having distinguishing<BR>or characteristic qualities, speciality, peculiarity (of<BR>any kind); excellence, superiority, eminence.<BR>—वि-<BR>शिष्ट-बुद्धि, इस्, f. ‘differenced knowledge,’ dis-<BR>tinguishing knowledge (e. g. the knowledge of ‘a<BR>man carrying a staff’ which distinguishes him from<BR>‘a man’ indifferently).<BR>—विशिष्ट-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a distinguished colour.<BR>—विशिष्टाद्वैत-वा-<BR>दिन् (˚ट-अद्˚), ई, इनी, इ, one who asserts the identity<BR>of what is distinct, i. e. of the two distinct things<BR>Prakṛti and Puruṣa with Brahma.<BR>—विशिष्टोपमा<BR>(˚ट-उप्˚), f. a particular comparison.<BR>—विशिष्टोप-<BR>मा-युक्त (˚ट-उप्˚), अम्, n., scil. रूपक, a meta-<BR>phor which contains a particular comparison (said to<BR>be a variety of the Rūpaka or metaphor general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष|विशेषः
वि-शेष, अस्, m. the act of distinguishing or dis-<BR>criminating, discrimination; difference, distinction,<BR>individuality, individual identity (consisting in dis-<BR>tinction from every other individual or species),<BR>characteristic difference, peculiar mark, special pro-<BR>perty, speciality, peculiarity (sometimes at the begin-<BR>ning of compounds and to be translated by ‘peculiar,’<BR>‘special,’ &c., cf. विशेष-गुण); particularity; (in<BR>the Vaiśeṣika school of the Nyāya phil.) the eternal<BR>distinguishing nature or individual essence of each of<BR>the nine Dravyas or substances (i. e. of each of the<BR>five atoms of earth, water, fire, air, and mind, and<BR>of ether, time, space, and soul; these nine eternal<BR>substances are said to be so essentially different that<BR>one can never be the other); predicament (in logic);<BR>peculiar attribute; (in grammar) a word which de-<BR>fines or limits the meaning of another word, (any<BR>word in which the general meaning of another word<BR>is merged is said to be the Viśeṣa of that word); a<BR>distinguishing mark made on the forehead with<BR>sandal; species, kind, sort, variety, mode, manner,<BR>various method (often at the end of comps., e. g.<BR>वृक्ष-विशेष, a kind of tree; तपो-विशेषाः,<BR>m. pl. various kinds of penance: and sometimes to<BR>be translated by ‘different,’ ‘special,’ e. g. पुरुष-<BR>व्˚, a different man; दशा-व्˚, a special condition);<BR>variation, change, alteration for the better, amend-<BR>ment; a favourable turn or crisis in sickness; a dis-<BR>tinct or different object; a limb, member; distinc-<BR>tion, peculiar merit, excellence, superiority; the best<BR>of anything (at the end of comps. or even at the<BR>beginning, and sometimes to be translated by ‘excel-<BR>lent,’ ‘superior,’ e. g. रस-व्˚, an excellent juice, cf.<BR>प्रसाधन-व्˚); a particular figure in rhetoric<BR>(said to be of three kinds, cf. विशेषोक्ति, col. 3);<BR>N. of the mundane egg; विशेषेण or विशेषात्,<BR>ind. especially, particularly, even more.<BR>—विशेष-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, peculiarly desirous or amorous.<BR>—विशेष-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, making a distinction, dis-<BR>tinguishing.<BR>—विशेष-गुण, अस्, m. a special or<BR>distinct quality, distinguishing property; an object<BR>or substance of a single and distinct kind (as soul,<BR>time, space, ether, and the atoms of earth, water,<BR>fire, air, and mind).<BR>—विशेष-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing distinctions, critical, intelligent, wise, dis-<BR>criminating, a connoisseur.<BR>—विशेष-तस्, ind. espe-<BR>cially, particularly, in particular, specifically.<BR>—विशे-<BR>ष-धर्म, अस्, m. a peculiar or different duty; a<BR>special law.<BR>—विशेष-पदार्थ (˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-c" target="_blank">Page0942-c+ 81</a>]<BR>(in the Nyāya) the category of particularity.<BR>—विशे-<BR>ष-प्रतिषेध, अस्, m. a special exception.<BR>—वि-<BR>शेष-प्रमाण, अम्, n. special authority.<BR>—विशे-<BR>ष-भावना, f. reflecting on or perceiving differ-<BR>ences; (in mathematics) a particular operation in<BR>extracting roots, composition by the difference of the<BR>products.<BR>—विशेष-रमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, especially<BR>delightful, particularly pleasant.<BR>—विशेष-लक्षण,<BR>अम्, n. any specific or characteristic mark or sign.<BR>—विशेष-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. a particular mark, specific<BR>property, attribute of a subordinate class.<BR>—विशेष-<BR>वचन, अम्, n. a special text, different text, special<BR>rule or precept.<BR>—विशेष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed<BR>of some distinguishing property, peculiar, excellent,<BR>superior, better.<BR>—विशेष-विद्वस्, आन्, m. eminently<BR>learned, a sage, philosopher.<BR>—विशेष-विधि, इस्,<BR>m. a special rule or observance, special form.<BR>—वि-<BR>शेष-व्याप्ति, इस्, f. (in logic) a form of Vyāpti or<BR>pervasion, (according to Śabda-k. = प्रतियोगि-व्य-<BR>धिकरण-स्वसमानाधिकरणात्यन्ताभावा-<BR>प्रतियोगित्व.)<BR>—विशेष-शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing<BR>peculiar merit or excellence.<BR>—विशेष-शास्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. (in grammar) a special rule (= अप-वाद).<BR>—वि-<BR>शेषातिदेश (˚ष-अत्˚), अस्, m. a special supplemen-<BR>tary rule.<BR>—विशेषार्थम् (˚ष-अर्˚), ind. for the<BR>sake of distinction or difference.<BR>—विशेषार्थिन्<BR>(˚ष-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, seeking for excellence or dis-<BR>tinction; particular in searching for (anything).<BR>—वि-<BR>शेषोक्ति (˚ष-उक्˚), इस्, f. (in rhetoric) ‘statement<BR>of distinction’ or ‘description of excellence,’ (either<BR>coupling cause with effect so as to explain any pecu-<BR>liar condition or enhancing the beauty of a subject by<BR>dwelling upon certain adverse circumstances in spite<BR>of which this excellence exists); enumeration of<BR>merits, panegyric.<BR>—विशेषोच्छ्वसित (˚ष-उच्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the peculiar breath or life (of another), a<BR>peculiar treasure (applied to an object especially dear).<BR>—विशेषोद्देश (˚ष-उद्˚), अस्, m. (in the Nyāya)<BR>a particular kind of enunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषक|विशेषकः
वि-शेषक, अस्, आ, अम्, distinguishing, discrimina-<BR>tive, characteristic, attributive; (अस्, अम्), m. n. any<BR>distinguishing property or characteristic; an attribute,<BR>predicate; a mark on the forehead made with sandal<BR>&c. (worn either as an ornament or for sectarial dis-<BR>tinction; पत्त्र-विशेषक, strokes or lines drawn<BR>on the face with pigments); discriminative faculty<BR>or perception; a particular arrangement of poetical<BR>composition.<BR>—विशेषक-च्छेद्य, अम्, n. a parti-<BR>cular form of Tilaka or sectarial mark, (according to<BR>Śabda-k. = चतुःषष्टि-कलान्तर्गत-षष्ठ-<BR>कला.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषण|विशेषणं
वि-शेषण, अस्, ई, अम्, distinguishing, discrimina-<BR>tive, attributive; distinctive (as a property &c.);<BR>(अम्), n. the act of distinguishing or discriminating,<BR>distinction, discrimination; a distinguishing mark or<BR>attribute; a word which particularizes or defines<BR>another word, the ‘differencer’ or distinguisher of<BR>another word (which other word is called वि-शेष्य,<BR>q. v.); an epithet, attribute, adjective; a word used<BR>in apposition.<BR>—विशेषण-ता, f. the state of a dis-<BR>tinguisher or of distinguishing, the being a distin-<BR>guishing mark; the being an adjective; individuality.<BR>—विशेषणता-सम्बन्ध, अस्, m. the relation of<BR>predicability, relation of predicate to subject.<BR>—वि-<BR>शेषण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, endowed with discrimi-<BR>nation; having a distinguishing attribute.<BR>—विशे-<BR>षण-वर्ग, अस्, m., N. of a division of the Śabda-<BR>ratnāvalī lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणीय
वि-शेषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be distinguished or<BR>discriminated; to be marked as different or distinct;<BR>to be particularized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषित|विशेषितं
वि-शेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, distinguished, made different<BR>or distinct, defined, separated, divided; having as an<BR>attribute, distinguished by an attribute; predicated;<BR>excellent, superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्य|विशेष्यः
वि-शेष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be distinguished or dis-<BR>criminated; requiring to be defined or determined;<BR>distinguished, pre-eminent, principal, primary, chief;<BR>(अम्), n. the word to be ‘differenced’ or distin-<BR>guished, the thing or object to be particularized or<BR>defined by another word (which other word is called<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">Page0943-a+ 76</a>]<BR>विशेषण, q. v.), a substantive, noun, the object or<BR>subject of a predicate, (according to some, in these<BR>senses, also masc.)<BR>—विशेष्य-ता, f. the being to be<BR>described or defined; the condition of a substantive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0942-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्यक
वि-शेष्यक in तद्वद्-विशेष्यक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to (an object) possessing such an attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्षन्
विशीर्षन् वि-शीर्षन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. headless,<BR>without a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशील
विशील वि-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-behaved,<BR>indecorous, immoral; badly conducted, ill-mannered,<BR>not observing approved usages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुध्
विशुध् वि-शुध्, cl. 4. P. -शुध्यति, -शोद्-<BR>धुम्, to be completely purified or cleansed; to<BR>become pure: Caus. -शोधयति, -यितुम्, to purify,<BR>cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्ध|विशुद्धं
वि-शुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, completely purified or<BR>cleansed; cleared; clean; pure, free from all vice or<BR>fault; pious, virtuous, honest; humble, modest,<BR>compliant; rectified, corrected, accurate; (अम्), n.<BR>a kind of mystical circle in the body, (see चक्र,<BR>cf. विशुद्धि-चक्र.)<BR>—विशुद्ध-धिषण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the understanding or mind purified.<BR>—विशुद्ध-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, having a pure mind<BR>or disposition, pure-minded.<BR>—विशुद्ध-वंश्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of a pure family.<BR>—विशुद्ध-सत्त्व-<BR>प्रधान, अस्, आ, अम्, chiefly characterized by pure<BR>goodness.<BR>—विशुद्धात्मन् (˚ध-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ,<BR>having a pure soul, pure-minded, innocent.<BR>—विशुद्-<BR>धेश्व-तन्त्र (˚ध-इश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धि|विशुद्धिः
वि-शुद्धि, इस्, f. complete purity; purifying; pu-<BR>rification, sanctification, holiness; rectitude, rectifica-<BR>tion, correction, correctness, removal of error or doubt;<BR>equality, sameness, similarity; (in algebra) a sub-<BR>tractive quantity.<BR>—विशुद्धि-चक्र, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of mystical circle or mark in the body (said by<BR>some to be in the region of the throat).<BR>—विशुद्धि-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, possessing purity, free from sin or<BR>vice, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधन|विशोधनं
वि-शोधन, अम्, n. the act of purifying, cleaning,<BR>freeing from soil, defect, or sin; expiation; (ई), f. a<BR>particular plant or tree (= दन्ती); N. of the capital<BR>of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधनीय
वि-शोधनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be purified or<BR>cleansed, to be freed from taint or sin; to be rectified<BR>or corrected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधित
वि-शोधित, अस्, आ, अम्, purified, cleansed, freed<BR>from soil or taint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधितव्य
वि-शोधितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = वि-शोधनीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधिन्
वि-शोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, purifying, cleaning, clearing;<BR>(इनी), f. a particular plant (= नाग-दन्ती).<BR>—विशो-<BR>धि-ता, f. or विशोधि-त्व, अम्, n. purifying, clean-<BR>ing; clearing, freeing from obstructions; rectifying,<BR>correcting.<BR>—विशोधिनी-वीज, अम्, n. = जय-पाल<BR>(according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोध्य
वि-शोध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be purified or cleaned,<BR>to be freed from taint or fault; to be rectified;<BR>(अम्), n. a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुभ्
