विश्रु
विश्रु 2. वि-श्रु = वि-स्रु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राव|विश्रावः
2. वि-श्राव, अस्, m. flowing forth or away, drop-<BR>ping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रावण
2. वि-श्रावण, अम्, n. causing to flow forth;<BR>bleeding, (see वि-स्रावण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुत|विश्रुतः
2. वि-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, flowed away, flowing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुति|विश्रुतिः
2. वि-श्रुति, इस्, f. flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथ्
विश्लथ् वि-श्लथ् [cf. वि-श्रथ्], cl. 1. P.<BR>-श्लथति, cl. 10. P. -श्लथयति, &c., to be loose<BR>or relaxed; to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथ
वि-श्लथ, अस्, आ, अम्, untied, loose, relaxed, lan-<BR>guid.<BR>—विश्लथाङ्ग (˚थ-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>relaxed limbs, relaxed, weak, nerveless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्
विश्लिष् वि-श्लिष्, cl. 4. P. -श्लिष्यति, -श्लेष्-<BR>टुम्, to be disunited or separated, be divided, be<BR>broken: Caus. -श्लेषयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be<BR>disunited, separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्ट
वि-श्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, disunited, disjoined, sepa-<BR>rated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेष|विश्लेषः
वि-श्लेष, अस्, m. disunion, disjunction, separation<BR>(especially of lovers, or of husband and wife); distance,<BR>absence, bereavement; a chasm; (in arithmetic) the<BR>converse of addition.<BR>—विश्लेष-जाति, इस्, f. (in arith-<BR>metic) the assimilation of difference, the reduction<BR>of fractional difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0943-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषित
वि-श्लेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, disunited, severed, sepa-<BR>rated, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषिन्
वि-श्लेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, disunited, severed, falling from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लोक
विश्लोक वि-श्लोक, अस्, m. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्व|विश्वं|विश्वः
विश्व विश्व, अस्, आ, अम् (in Uṇādi-s. I. 151.<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. विश्, ‘to pervade;’ according to some<BR>connected with rt. श्वि with वि; declined as a pro-<BR>nominal, like सर्व, nom. pl. masc. विश्वे, see Gram.<BR>238; cf. शश्वत्, शाश्वत), all, every, every one,<BR>(विश्वस्माद् इन्द्र उत्तरः, Indra is higher than<BR>all, Ṛg-veda X. 86, 1), entire, whole, universal;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a kind of deity belonging to a class<BR>of ten (forming one of the nine Gaṇas or classes<BR>enumerated under Gaṇa-devatā, q. v.: in Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 130, 5. they are associated with the Jagatī metre,<BR>and called Viśve devāḥ, which may have originally<BR>denoted ‘all the gods collectively,’ though the intro-<BR>duction of the Viśvas under the name विश्व-देवाः<BR>or विश्वे-देवाः, as a separate troop or Gaṇa of deities,<BR>seems to have taken place at an early period: accord-<BR>ing to the Viṣṇu and other Purāṇas they were sons<BR>of Viśvā, daughter of Dakṣa, and their names are<BR>given as follow, 1. Vasu, 2. Satya, 3. Kratu, 4.<BR>Dakṣa, 5. Kāla, 6. Kāma, 7. Dhṛti, 8. Kuru, 9.<BR>Purū-ravas, 10. Mādravas; two others are added by<BR>some authorities, viz. 11. Rocaka or Locana, 12.<BR>Dhvani [also written Dhūri ?]: they are particularly<BR>worshipped at the Śrāddhas or funeral obsequies in<BR>honour of deceased ancestors: moreover, according<BR>to Manu III. 90, 121, offerings should be made to<BR>them daily, — these privileges having been bestowed<BR>on them, it is said, by Brahmā and the Pitṛs, as a<BR>reward for certain severe austerities they had per-<BR>formed on the Himālaya: sometimes, however, it is<BR>difficult to decide whether the expression विश्वे देवाः<BR>refers to all the gods or to the particular troop of<BR>deities described above); N. of Intellect in the Ve-<BR>dānta philosophy, or (according to some) the faculty<BR>which perceives Singleness, (perhaps translatable by<BR>‘the Pervader;’ according to a commentator =<BR>स्थूल-शरीर-व्यष्ट्य्-उपहित-चैतन्य, ‘intel-<BR>lect located in the distributive aggregate of material<BR>bodies’); N. of a well known lexicon, = विश्व-प्र-<BR>काश, q. v.; (आ), f., N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and<BR>wife of Dharma; the plant Aconitum Ferox; a tree<BR>used for dying red (commonly called Atis = Betula);<BR>the shrub Asparagus Racemosus (= शतावरी);<BR>another plant (= पिप्पली); dry ginger; (अम्), n.<BR>the whole world, universe, whole creation; dry ginger.<BR>—विश्व-कद्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, wicked, vile; (उस्), m.<BR>a dog trained for the chase; sound, noise.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>कर्मन्, आ, m. ‘one who does universal acts, all-<BR>doer, all-creator, all-maker,’ N. of the architect or<BR>artist of the gods (said to be son of Brahmā, and in<BR>the later mythology sometimes identified with Tvash-<BR>ṭṛ, q. v., not only as an architect, but as a kind of<BR>chief engineer or forger of divine weapons, and in-<BR>ventor of the अग्न्य्-अस्त्र, q. v.; in this capacity<BR>Viśva-karman is said to have revealed the Sthāpatya-<BR>veda, q. v., or fourth Upa-veda, and to preside over<BR>all manual labours as well as the sixty-four mechanical<BR>arts, [whence he is worshipped by Kārus or artizans];<BR>in the Vedic mythology, however, the office of Indian<BR>Vulcan is assigned to Tvaṣṭṛ as a distinct deity,<BR>Viśva-karman being rather identified with Prajā-pati<BR>[Brahmā] himself as the creator of all things and<BR>architect of the universe; in the hymns Ṛg-veda X.<BR>81, 82. he is represented as the universal Father and<BR>Generator, the one all-seeing God, who has on every<BR>side eyes, faces, arms, and feet, who blows forth heaven<BR>and earth with his arms and wings, who knows all<BR>worlds, gives the gods their names, and is beyond<BR>the comprehension of mortals; in Nirukta X. 26.<BR>and elsewhere in the Brāhmaṇas he is called a son<BR>of Bhuvana, and Viśva-karman Bhauvana is described<BR>as the author of the two Ṛg-veda hymns X. 81, 82,<BR>mentioned above; moreover, a doubtful legend is told<BR>of his having offered up all beings, including himself,<BR>in sacrifice; the Rāmāyaṇa represents him as having<BR>built the city of Laṅkā for the Rākṣasas, and as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0944-b" target="_blank">Page0944-b+ 81</a>]<BR>having generated the ape Nala, who made Rāma's<BR>bridge from the continent to the island; the name<BR>Viśva-karman, meaning ‘doing all acts,’ appears to<BR>be sometimes applicable as an epithet to any great<BR>divinity); epithet of Sūrya or the Sun; of one of the<BR>seven principal rays of the sun (supposed to supply<BR>heat to the planet Mercury); epithet of Mahā-deva<BR>(Mahā-bh. Śānti-parvan 10332); epithet of Indra<BR>(Ṛg-veda VIII. 87, 2); of a son of the Vasu Pra-<BR>bhāsa; any great saint.<BR>—विश्वकर्म-सुता or<BR>विश्वकर्म-जा, f. ‘daughter of Viśva-karman,’<BR>epithet of Sañjñā (one of the wives of the Sun).<BR>—विश्व-काय, अस्, आ, अम्, whose body is the universe<BR>(said of Viṣṇu); (आ), f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>कार्य, अस्, m., N. of one of the seven principal rays<BR>of the sun (supposed to supply heat to the planet<BR>Venus; cf. विश्व-कर्मन्).<BR>—विश्व-कृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>making or creating all; (त्), m. the creator or maker<BR>of all things; epithet of Viśva-karman, son of Brahmā,<BR>(see above); N. of a son of Gādhi or Gāthin, and<BR>brother of Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—विश्व-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>made by Viśva-karman (?).<BR>—विश्व-कृष्टि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, Ved. (probably) known to all men; [cf. विश्व-<BR>चर्षणि.]<BR>—विश्व-केतु, उस्, m. ‘whose banner is<BR>the universe,’ epithet of A-niruddha, (a form of Kāma,<BR>as son of Pradyumna.)<BR>—विश्व-कोष, अस्, m. the<BR>lexicon called Viśva (= विश्व-प्रकाश).<BR>—विश्व-ग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘going everywhere,’ N. of Brahmā.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>गन्ध, अस्, m. ‘having much odour,’ an onion;<BR>(आ), f. ‘having all fragrance,’ the earth (as having<BR>the quality of odour, see गुण); (अम्), n. myrrh<BR>(= वोल).<BR>—विश्व-गुणादर्श (˚ण-आद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘mirror of the virtues of the world,’ N. of a work by<BR>Veṅkaṭa (relating the history of Southern India).<BR>—विश्व-गुध्, घुत्, त्, त्, all-enveloping.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>गूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. approved by every body,<BR>accomplisher of all deeds, prepared for all acts, (Sāy.<BR>= सर्वेषु कार्येषूद्यत, Ṛg-veda VIII. 1, 22.)<BR>—विश्व-गोप्तृ, ता, m. ‘preserver of the universe,’<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; of Indra.<BR>—विश्व-ग्रन्थि, इस्, f.<BR>the plant Cissus Pedata (= हंस-पदी).<BR>—विश्वङ्-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, all-creating, making all; (अस्),<BR>m. the eye.<BR>—विश्व-चक्र, अम्, n., N. of a par-<BR>ticular kind of large gift or offering consisting of a<BR>mass of pure gold.<BR>—विश्व-चक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>all-seeing.<BR>—विश्व-चक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. all-seeing,<BR>all-beholding, (said of Viśva-karman, Ṛg-veda X. 81,<BR>2, and of Sūrya I. 50, 2.)<BR>—विश्व-चन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. all-radiant, all-brilliant.<BR>—विश्व-चर्षणि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. known to all men, extending everywhere,<BR>world-wide, seeing everything, comprising all men.<BR>—विश्व-जन, अम्, n. all men, all mankind, man-<BR>kind generally.<BR>—विश्व-जनीन, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or<BR>good for all men, suitable to all mankind.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>जनीन-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, whose conduct or actions are<BR>for the benefit of the whole world.<BR>—विश्व-जनीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, relating or suitable to all men.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>जन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to all man-<BR>kind, fit or good for all men, universally beneficial.<BR>—विश्व-जित्, त्, त्, त्, all-conquering, all-subduing;<BR>(त्), m., N. of a particular ceremony or sacrifice; the<BR>cord or noose of Varuṇa; N. of a son of Gādhi and<BR>brother of Viśvā-mitra; of a son of Satya-jit.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>जिन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. all-refreshing, all-sustaining.<BR>—विश्व-जू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. all-impelling, (Sāy. =<BR>विश्वस्य प्रेरयितृ, Ṛg-veda IV. 33, 8.)<BR>—विश्व-<BR>तस्, &c., see p. 945, col. 3.<BR>—विश्व-तुर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, ऊर्,<BR>Ved. all-subduing, conquering everything.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>दर्शत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. all-conspicuous, visible to<BR>all; to be honoured by all.<BR>—विश्व-देव, अस्, m. a<BR>Viśva-deva or deity of a particular class, see under<BR>विश्व; (आ), f. the plant Hedysarum Lagopodioides;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), possessing all divine attributes, contain-<BR>ing all the gods.<BR>—विश्व-देव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>distinguished by all divine attributes; relating or ac-<BR>ceptable to all the gods, Ṛg-veda III. 2, 5.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>दोहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. milking or yielding all<BR>things, all-productive.<BR>—विश्व-धर, अस्, m. ‘all-<BR>containing,’ a proper N.<BR>—विश्व-धायस्, आस्, आस्, अस्<BR>(see 1. and 2. धायस्), Ved. one who bears every-<BR>thing, all-sustaining, all-nourishing.<BR>—विश्व-धारिन्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0944-c" target="_blank">Page0944-c+ 81</a>]<BR>ई, इणी, इ, all-maintaining, all-sustaining; (ई), m. a<BR>deity; (इणी), f. the earth.<BR>—विश्व-धृक्, क्, क्, sus-<BR>taining everything, (see धृक्.)<BR>—विश्व-धेना, f.,<BR>Ved. ‘all-cherisher, all-fosterer,’ epithet of the earth.<BR>—विश्व-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of the universe,’ N. of<BR>Śiva (especially as the object of adoration at Benares,<BR>cf. विश्वेश); N. of the author of the Candra-kalā<BR>drama, the Sāhitya-darpaṇa, and various other works;<BR>of several other authors and commentators.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>नाथ-देव, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Kuṇḍa-<BR>maṇḍapa-kaumudī.<BR>—विश्वनाथ-पञ्चानन or<BR>विश्वनाथ-भट्टाचार्य, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Bhāṣā-pariccheda, and of a commentary on<BR>the Nyāya-sūtra of Gotama.<BR>—विश्व-पा, आस्, m. ‘all-<BR>protecting, all-nourishing,’ the sun; the moon; fire.<BR>—विश्व-पाल, अस्, m. ‘all-protector,’ N. of a mer-<BR>chant.<BR>—विश्व-पावन, अस्, ई, अम्, world-purifying;<BR>(ई), f. holy basil (= तुलसी).<BR>—विश्व-पिश्, Ved. having<BR>all sorts of ornaments; (Sāy.) having many forms<BR>(= बहु-रूप).<BR>—विश्व-पुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, all-nourishing.<BR>—विश्व-पूजिता, f. ‘adored by all,’ holy basil (=<BR>तुलसी).<BR>—विश्व-पेशस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. containing<BR>all beauties; multiform, (Sāy. = बहु-विध-रूप-<BR>युक्त.)<BR>—विश्व-प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a lexicon<BR>by Maheśvara (more briefly called Viśva).<BR>—विश्व-<BR>प्सन्, आ, m. (according to some corrupted form<BR>विश्व + भसन्, cf. भसद्), a god; fire or the<BR>deity of fire, Agni; the moon; the sun.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>प्स्न्य, अस्, आ, अम् (प्स्न्य said to be for प्सन्य fr.<BR>rt. प्सा), Ved. feeding everything; having many<BR>forms or whose forms pervade everything, (Sāy. =<BR>व्याप्त-रूप.)<BR>—विश्व-बुद्बुद, अस्, m. the world<BR>regarded as a bubble.<BR>—विश्व-बोध, अस्, m. a<BR>Buddha or Buddhist deified saint.<BR>—विश्व-भरस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. all-bearing, all-supporting.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>भानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having light on all sides, all-<BR>illumining, (Sāy. = सर्वतो व्याप्त-तेजस्क.)<BR>—वि-<BR>श्व-भावन, अस्, m. ‘creator of the universe,’ N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—विश्व-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, all-enjoying, all-pos-<BR>seesing; eating all things; (क्), m. epithet of Indra.<BR>—विश्व-भुजा, f., N. of a tutelary goddess.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>भू, ऊस्, m. the third of the Buddhas (according to<BR>some systems).<BR>—विश्व-भेषज, अम्, n. ‘univer-<BR>sal-medicine,’ dry ginger; (अस्), m., Ved. a universal<BR>remedy, panacea.<BR>—विश्व-भोजन, अम्, n. the eating<BR>of all sorts of food.<BR>—विश्व-भोजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>all-nourishing, one who enjoys all things, granting<BR>all enjoyment.<BR>—विश्व-भ्राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. all-illumi-<BR>nating.<BR>—विश्व-मदा, f. ‘all-delighting,’ N. of one<BR>of the seven tongues of fire.<BR>—विश्व-मनस्, आस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the hymns Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>23-26 (having the patronymic Vaiyaśva).<BR>—विश्व-<BR>मनुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. (probably) known to all<BR>men; [cf. विश्व-कृष्टि.]<BR>—विश्व-मानुष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. (probably) known to all men [cf. विश्व-<BR>मनुस्]; (अस्), m. every mortal, (Sāy. = सर्वो म-<BR>नुष्यः, Ṛg-veda VIII. 45, 42.)<BR>—विश्वम्-इन्व,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. expanding everywhere, pervading<BR>everything, (Sāy. = विश्वं व्याप्नुवान); gratify-<BR>ing all, (Sāy. = विश्व-तर्पण.)<BR>—विश्व-मुखी, f.,<BR>N. of Dākṣāyaṇī (as worshipped in Jālandhara).<BR>—विश्व-मूर्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, one whose form is the<BR>universe, existing in all forms; an epithet of the Su-<BR>preme Spirit.<BR>—विश्वमूर्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>or taking all forms, existing in all forms, omnipresent.<BR>—विश्वम्-एजय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shaking everything,<BR>making everything tremble; [cf. जनम्-एजय.]<BR>—विश्व-मेदिनी, f., N. of a lexicon.<BR>—विश्वम्-<BR>भर, अस्, आ, अम्, supporting the universe, all-sus-<BR>taining, all-maintaining; (अस्), m. the Supreme Being;<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; of Indra; (आ), f. the earth.<BR>—विश्-<BR>वम्भराधिप (˚रा-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>earth,’ a king.<BR>—विश्व-योनि, इस्, m. ‘source of the<BR>universe,’ N. of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu.<BR>—विश्व-रथ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Gādhi and brother of Viśvā-<BR>mitra.<BR>—विश्व-राज्, ट्, m. a universal sovereign.<BR>—विश्व-रुची, f. ‘all-glittering,’ epithet of one of<BR>the seven tongues of fire, (sometimes regarded as a<BR>goddess.)<BR>—विश्व-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, taking all forms,<BR>existing in all forms, of every kind, universal, omni-<BR>present; (अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-a" target="_blank">Page0945-a+ 81</a>]<BR>son of Tvaṣṭṛ (a three-headed monster slain by<BR>Indra); of a lexicographer; of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya;<BR>of several other persons; (अम्), n. Agallochum.<BR>—विश्वरूप-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the<BR>greatest variety of forms or colours.<BR>—विश्वरूप-<BR>दर्शन, अम्, n., N. of two chapters in the Krīḍā-<BR>khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—विश्वरूपाचार्य<BR>(˚प-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author of a Vārttika.<BR>—विश्व-रेतस्, आस्, m. ‘containing the seed of all<BR>things,’ epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—विश्व-रोचन, अस्, m.<BR>an esculent root, Arum Colocasia.<BR>—विश्व-लिङ्ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. containing the distinguishing word विश्व.<BR>—विश्व-लोचन = विश्व-प्रकाश.<BR>—विश्व-वद,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a so-called Veda (with the Magians).<BR>—विश्व-वसु, उस्, m. ‘wealth of all,’ N. of a son<BR>of Purū-ravas.<BR>—विश्व-वार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pos-<BR>sessed of all desirable things, containing all good<BR>things, granting all boons (Ṛg-veda VII. 10, 4);<BR>adored or cherished by all, (Sāy. = विश्वैर् वरणीय,<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 113, 19); (आ), f., N. of the authoress<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda V. 28 (belonging to the<BR>family of Atri).<BR>—विश्व-वार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. all-<BR>desired, (Sāy. = विश्वैर् वरणीय, Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>19, 11.)<BR>—विश्व-वाह्, -वाट्, विश्वौही, -वाट् (inst. c.<BR>विश्वौहा, cf. भार-वाह्), all-sustaining.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>विद्, त्, त्, त्, ved. knowing everything, omniscient.<BR>—विश्व-विधायिन्, ई, m. all-making, all-arranging, a<BR>creator, deity.<BR>—विश्व-वृत्ति, इस्, f. universal practice.<BR>—विश्व-वेदस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, one who knows all things,<BR>all-knowing, omniscient, obtaining or possessing all;<BR>a sage, saint.<BR>—विश्व-व्यचस्, आस्, f. ‘all-embracing,’<BR>epithet of Aditi.<BR>—विश्व-व्यापक, अस्, आ, अम्, all-<BR>pervading, everywhere diffused.<BR>—विश्व-व्यापिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, all-diffused, all-pervading, ubiquitous, omni-<BR>present.<BR>—विश्व-व्याप्ति, इस्, f. universal diffusion or<BR>permeation.<BR>—विश्व-शम्भू, ऊस्, m. one who is the<BR>source of all prosperity; epithet of Viśva-karman<BR>(Ṛg-veda X. 81, 7; in Ṛg-veda I. 160, 4. the dual<BR>form विश्व-भुवा, ‘all-beneficial,’ is an epithet of<BR>रोदसी, or heaven and earth).<BR>—विश्व-शर्धस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, Ved. displaying great power, making great<BR>exertion, (Sāy. = व्याप्त-बल or बहूत्साह.)<BR>—विश्व-शारद, अस्, m., Ved. epithet of the disease<BR>called Takman (as likely to occur every autumn).<BR>—विश्व-शुचि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. all-enlightening, purifying<BR>everything (said of Agni).<BR>—विश्व-सह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>all-bearing, all-enduring; (अस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Ilavila; (आ), f. the earth; epithet of one of the tongues<BR>of fire.<BR>—विश्व-सामन्, आ, m., N. of the author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda V. 22 (having the patronymic<BR>Ātreya).<BR>—विश्व-सारक, अम्, n. ‘having all es-<BR>sence,’ the prickly pear, Cactus Indicus.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>सुविद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. granting everything well, giving<BR>every good thing, bestowing every sort of wealth.<BR>—विश्व-सृज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, creating the universe; (ट्), m.<BR>a creator of the universe (of whom there are ten ac-<BR>cording to some accounts); an epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—विश्व-सेन, अस्, m. epithet of the eighteenth Mu-<BR>hūrta.<BR>—विश्व-सौभग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bestow-<BR>ing all blessings, containing all good things.<BR>—विश्व-<BR>स्फटिक, अस्, m., N. of a king of Magadha.<BR>—विश्व-स्रष्टृ, टा, m. the creator of the universe,<BR>God.<BR>—विश्वाङ्ग (˚व-अङ्˚), अस्, m. universal-mem-<BR>bered (said of Viṣṇu).<BR>—विश्वात्मन् (˚व-आत्˚), आ, m.<BR>‘Universe-spirit,’ the Soul of the Universe, the Univer-<BR>sal Spirit, the Supreme Being, God; Brahman; Śiva;<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—विश्वा-धायस्, आस्, m. (for विश्व-धायस्,<BR>q. v.), ‘all-sustaining,’ a deity, god.<BR>—विश्वा-नर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘rulling all men, benefiting all men,’ epithet<BR>of Savitṛ; N. of the father of Agni.<BR>—विश्वान्तर<BR>(˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m., Ved., N. of a son of Su-shadman.<BR>—विश्वाप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having all forms,<BR>multiform, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 148.<BR>अप्सु = रूप, विश्वाप्सु = नाना-रूप; but cf.<BR>प्सु.)<BR>—विश्वा-मित्र, अस्, m. (according to some<BR>authorities for विश्व + अमित्र, and meaning ‘no<BR>friend to all;’ but more probably for विश्व-मित्र, ‘the<BR>friend of all,’ the final of विश्व being lengthened),<BR>N. of a celebrated Kṣatriya, described as son of<BR>Gāthin or Gādhi, deriving his lineage from an an-<BR>cestor of Kuśika, named Purū-ravus, of the lunar race<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-b" target="_blank">Page0945-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of kings, and himself sovereign of Kanyā-kubja or<BR>Kanoj, (according to one account he was brother of<BR>Satya-vatī, wife of Ṛcīka and mother by him of<BR>Jamad-agni, q. v., who was the father of Paraśu-rāma;<BR>he had one hundred sons, fifty of whom offended<BR>their father, and being degraded by him to the con-<BR>dition of outcasts, became the progenitors of various<BR>barbarous tribes and Dasyus: the fame of Viśvā-<BR>mitra rests chiefly on his contests with the great<BR>Brāhman Vasiṣṭha, and his success in elevating him-<BR>self, though a Kṣatriya, to the rank of a Brāhman,<BR>see Manu VII. 42: the Rāmāyaṇa, which makes<BR>him a companion and counsellor of the young Rāma-<BR>candra, records [I. 51-65] how Viśvā-mitra, on his<BR>accession to the throne, visited the hermitage of<BR>Vasiṣṭha, and seeing there the cow of plenty [proba-<BR>bly typical of गो, ‘the earth’], offered the Muni un-<BR>told treasures in exchange for it, but being refused,<BR>prepared to take it by force; a long contest ensued<BR>between the king and the saint [symbolical of the<BR>struggles between the Kṣatriya and Brāhmanical<BR>classes], which ended in the defeat of Viśvā-mītra,<BR>whose vexation was such that, in order to become a<BR>Brāhman and thus conquer his rival, he devoted<BR>himself to intense austerities, gradually increasing the<BR>rigour of his mortification through thousands of years,<BR>till he successively earned the titles of Rājarṣi, Ṛṣi,<BR>Maharṣi, and finally Brahmarṣi; during the course<BR>of these penances Indra and the gods jealous of his<BR>increasing power — as exhibited in his transporting<BR>king Tri-śaṅku to the skies, and in saving his nephew<BR>Śunaḥ-śepha, son of his own brother-in-law Ṛcīka,<BR>out of the hands of Indra, to whom he had been<BR>promised by king Ambarīṣa as a victim in a sacri-<BR>fice — sent first the nymph Menakā and subsequently<BR>Rambhā to seduce him from his passionless life, and<BR>his surrender to the allurements of the first of these<BR>nymphs led to the birth of a daughter called Śakun-<BR>talā, q. v., the heroine of the celebrated drama; the<BR>rivalry between Viśvā-mitra and Vasiṣṭha is alluded<BR>to in many passages of the Ṛg-veda; it is thought,<BR>therefore, that as caste distinctions had not then<BR>become fixed, the later myths on the subject of this<BR>rivalry may have rested on a Vedic legend, according<BR>to which king Su-dās, having employed Vasiṣṭha as<BR>his domestic priest, allowed on various occasions Viśvā-<BR>mitra also to officiate, which of course led to jealousies<BR>and quarrels between these two functionaries: the whole<BR>of the hymns of the third Maṇḍala of the Ṛg-veda<BR>and a few others are attributed to Viśvā-mitra or to<BR>members of his family); विश्वामित्रस्यात्यर्ध,<BR>N. of a Sāman; (आस्), m. pl. the family or descendants<BR>of Viśvā-mitra; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—विश्वामित्र-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘dear to Viśvā-mitra,’ the cocoa-nut<BR>tree, (the fruit being said to have been created by<BR>that saint.)<BR>—विश्वामित्र-सृष्टि, इस्, f., Viśvā-<BR>mitra's creation, (in allusion to several things fabled<BR>to have been created by this saint in rivalry of Brahmā,<BR>e. g. the fruit of the Palmyra in imitation of the<BR>human skull, the buffalo in imitation of the cow, the<BR>ass of the horse, &c.)<BR>—विश्वायु (˚व-आय्˚), उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. containing all life, of full vitality, life-sustain-<BR>ing, abounding in food; going everywhere, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 28, 2 = सर्वतो गन्तृ.)<BR>—विश्वायु-पोषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. feeding or<BR>nourishing all living beings.<BR>—विश्वायु-वेपस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. whose energy goes everywhere or pervades<BR>all things, (Sāy. = सर्व-गत-बल, Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>43, 25.)<BR>—विश्वा-राज्, ट्, m. a king of the universe.<BR>—विश्वा-वसु, उस्, m. ‘wealth of all,’ N. of one of<BR>the Gandharvas (regarded as the author of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 139); epithet of one of the Manus;<BR>N. of a poet; of the thirteenth year of Jupiter's cycle;<BR>(उस्), f. epithet of a particular night.<BR>—विश्वा-सह् or<BR>विश्वा-साह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. all-conquering, subduing all<BR>foes.<BR>—विश्वे-देवास्, m. pl. the Viśva-devas, see<BR>विश्व; (according to the Śabda-k. there is a form<BR>विश्वे-देवास्, nom. m. sing. meaning ‘Fire,’ cf. विश्वे-<BR>वेदस्.)<BR>—विश्वे-देवृ, आ, m. the clitoris (?).<BR>—विश्वे-<BR>भोजस्, आस्, m. (for विश्व-भ्˚), an epithet of Indra.<BR>—विश्वे-वेदस्, आस्, m. (for विश्व-व्˚), an epithet of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">Page0945-c+ 80</a>]<BR>Agni or Fire.<BR>—विश्वेश (˚व-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>the universe,’ N. of Śiva (as worshipped at Benares,<BR>where a celebrated temple is appropriated to him,<BR>cf. विश्व-नाथ above); the Supreme Spirit; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma.<BR>—विश्वेश्वर (˚व-ईश्˚), अस्, m. lord of the uni-<BR>verse, = विश्वेश above; N. of the author of the<BR>Madana-pārijāta, the Mahārṇava, the Smṛti-kau-<BR>mudī, and a commentary on the Mitākṣarā; of the<BR>author of a commentary on the Aṣṭā-vakra-saṃhitā.<BR>—विश्वेश्वर-तीर्थ, अस्, m., N. of a commentator;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a place.<BR>—विश्वेश्वर-भट्ट, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the Karma-vipāka.<BR>—विश्वैक-<BR>सार (˚व-एक्˚), ‘sole essence of the universe,’ N. of<BR>a plain in Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वक
विश्वक, अस्, m., Ved., N. of the father of Vish-<BR>ṇāpū; of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda VIII. 75<BR>(having the patronymic Kārṣṇi); (आ), f. a sort of<BR>gull, Larus Ridibundus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वक्सेन
विश्वक्-सेन, अस्, m., for विष्वक्-सेन, see under<BR>विष्व्-अञ्च्, p. 948.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वगश्व
विश्वग्-अश्व, विश्वग्-गति, &c., for विष्वग्-अश्व,<BR>&c., see under विष्व्-अञ्च्, p. 948.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वञ्च्
विश्वञ्च्, an incorrect form for विष्व्-अञ्च्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वतस्
विश्व-तस्, ind. everywhere, all around, univer-<BR>sally.<BR>—विश्वतश्-चक्षुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. having<BR>eyes on every side, (Ṛg-veda VIII. 81, 3.)<BR>—विश्-<BR>वतस्-पाद्, त्, m., Ved. having feet on every side;<BR>epithet of Viśva-karman.<BR>—विश्वतो-दावन्, आ, &c.,<BR>Ved. granting from all sides.<BR>—विश्वतो-धी, ईस्, m.,<BR>Ved. supporter of the universe, (Sāy. = सर्व-जगतो<BR>धारक.)<BR>—विश्वतो-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having<BR>arms on every side.<BR>—विश्वतो-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having a face on every side, facing all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वथा
विश्वथा, ind. everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वदानीम्
विश्वदानीम्, ind., Ved. at all times, at all seasons;<BR>[cf. तदानीम्, इ-दानीम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वद्र्यञ्च्
विश्वद्र्यञ्च्, अङ्, ईची, अक् (fr. विश्व + अद्रि sub-<BR>stituted for the final अ + अञ्च्), moving everywhere or<BR>universally, going in all directions, (better written<BR>विष्वद्र्यञ्च्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वध
विश्वध, ind., Ved. at all times, on every occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वधा
विश्वधा, ind., Ved. on all sides, everywhere,<BR>(Sāy. = बहु-विधम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वन्तर|विश्वंतर
विश्वन्तर, अस्, m., N. of a king (son of Su-<BR>shadman; perhaps for विश्वान्तर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वयु|विश्वयुः
विश्वयु, उस्, m. (for विश्वायु?), air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वह
विश्वह, ind., Ved. on all days, at all times, (Sāy.<BR>= सर्वेष्व् अप्य् अहःसु, सर्वदा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वहा
विश्वहा, ind., Ved. everywhere, in every place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाहा
विश्वाहा, ind. (probably fr. विश्व + अहन्), every<BR>day, at all times, (Sāy. = सर्वदा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्व्या
विश्व्या, ind., Ved. from every place, from every<BR>quarter, (Sāy. = विश्व-तस्, सर्वासु दिक्षु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्
विश्वस् वि-श्वस्, cl. 2. P. -श्वसिति, -श्वसितुम्,<BR>to confide, trust, confide in, trust in, depend on (with<BR>loc. or gen.), to be trustful or confident, to be free<BR>from apprehension: Caus. -श्वासयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to trust, inspire with confidence, give confidence<BR>to, free from apprehension, console, encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसन
वि-श्वसन, अम्, n. trusting, confiding in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसनीय
वि-श्वसनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be trusted or relied<BR>on, reliable, trustworthy, credible.<BR>—विश्वसनीय-ता,<BR>f. trustworthiness, credibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसित|विश्वसितः
वि-श्वसित, अस्, आ, अम्, trusted; believed or con-<BR>fided in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्त|विश्वस्तः
वि-श्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, trusted, confided in, relied<BR>on; worthy of trust, deserving confidence; faithful;<BR>full of confidence, bold, fearless, unsuspecting; (आ),<BR>f. a widow.<BR>—विश्वस्त-वत्, ind. as if confiding, as<BR>though trustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास|विश्वासः
वि-श्वास, अस्, m. trust, confidence, faith, belief, re-<BR>liance; a confidential communication, secret.<BR>—विश्वा-<BR>स-कारण, अम्, n. cause of confidence, motive of trust.<BR>—विश्वास-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, inspiring confidence, causing<BR>trust.<BR>—विश्वास-घात, अस्, m. destruction of confi-<BR>dence, breach of faith, violation of trust, treachery.<BR>—विश्वास-घातक, अस्, or विश्वास-घातिन्, ई, m.<BR>destroying confidence, one who betrays confidence,<BR>a traitor.<BR>—विश्वास-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, produced from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">Page0946-a+ 77</a>]<BR>confidence.<BR>—विश्वास-देवी, f., N. of the patroness<BR>of Vidyā-pati (to whom he dedicated his Gaṅgā-<BR>vākyāvalī, a work on the worship of the waters of<BR>the Ganges).<BR>—विश्वास-पात्र, अम्, n. a confidential<BR>agent, one worthy to be trusted.<BR>—विश्वास-प्रति-<BR>पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of confidence, confiding,<BR>trusting.<BR>—विश्वास-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, giving or in-<BR>spiring confidence.<BR>—विश्वास-भङ्ग, अस्, m. breach<BR>of faith, violation of confidence.<BR>—विश्वास-भूमि,<BR>इस्, f. ground for trust, an object of trust, a trust-<BR>worthy person, any one worthy of confidence.<BR>—वि-<BR>श्वास-स्थान, अम्, n. an object or person of trust<BR>or confidence, anything which produces confidence;<BR>a hostage.<BR>—विश्वासैकसार (˚स-एक्˚), अस्, m. one<BR>whose sole essence is trust; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0945-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासन|विश्वासनं
वि-श्वासन, अम्, आ, n. f. causing to trust or con-<BR>fide, producing confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासयित्वा
वि-श्वासयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having caused or<BR>persuaded to trust, having inspired confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासिक
वि-श्वासिक, अस्, आ, अम्, trusty, confidential.<BR>—वि-<BR>श्वासिक-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more trusty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासित
वि-श्वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to trust, inspired<BR>with confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासिन्
विश्वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, confiding, trusting, believing,<BR>confiding in; trusty, honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास्य
1. वि-श्वास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be trusted or confided<BR>in, trustworthy; to be believed; to be made to trust<BR>or inspired with confidence; to be encouraged.<BR>—वि-<BR>श्वास्य-ता, f. trustworthiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास्य
2. वि-श्वास्य, ind. having made to trust, having in-<BR>spired with confidence or hope; having encouraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाची
विश्वाची विश्वाची, f. (probably fr. विश्व +<BR>अच् or अञ्च्, making a form विश्वाच् or विश्वाञ्च्, cf.<BR>घृताची, विष्वाञ्च्), N. of one of the Apsarases or<BR>nymphs of Svarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वि
विश्वि वि-श्वि, cl. 1. P. -श्वयति, -श्वयितुम्,<BR>to be spread or extended in all directions; to be<BR>manifested, appear, shine forth, (Sāy. = व्य्-अश्वैत् =<BR>सर्वं जगद् व्याप्नोत् or तेजसा प्रवृद्धासीत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
विष् 1. विष्, cl. 1. P. वेषति, विवेष,<BR>वेक्ष्यति, अविक्षत्, वेष्टुम् or (ac-<BR>cording to Vopa-deva) वेषितुम्, to sprinkle, pour<BR>out; cl. 9. P. विष्णाति, &c., to separate, disjoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ट्वा
विष्ट्वा or वेषित्वा, ind. having sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
विष् 2. विष्, cl. 3. P. A. (some of the<BR>forms of this rt. are liable to be con-<BR>founded with those of rt. 1. विश्), वेवेष्टि, वेविष्टे<BR>(Impv. 2nd sing. विविड्ढि = कुरु according to Ni-<BR>rukta X. 8; = प्रविश, see under rt. 1. विश्), विवेष,<BR>विविषे, वेक्ष्यति, -ते, अविक्षत् or अविषत् (?),<BR>अविक्षत, वेष्टुम्, (in Naigh. II. 6. वेष्टि is<BR>enumerated among the कान्ति-कर्माणः; in Naigh.<BR>II. 14. वेषिष्टि and विषिष्टि are mentioned among<BR>the गति-कर्माणः), to pervade, spread through, ex-<BR>tend through, go through, penetrate, invest; to spread,<BR>extend; to embrace; to go to, go against, meet (in<BR>a hostile manner); to cause to obtain, convey, (Sāy.<BR>= प्रापयति); to accomplish, perform; to eat,<BR>consume (according to Naigh. II. 8).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
3. विष्, ट्, f. spreading, diffusion; feces, ordure,<BR>excrement; (ट्, ट्, ट्), spreading, diffusing, all-pervad-<BR>ing (Ved.); (ट्), m. one who pervades, a pervading<BR>deity (Ved.).<BR>—विट्-कारिका, f. ‘ordure-maker,’ a kind<BR>of bird (probably a variety of the Turdus Salica).<BR>—विट्-खदिर, अस्, m. a kind of fetid Mimosa.<BR>—विट्-चर, अस्, m. ‘filth-goer,’ a tame or village<BR>hog.<BR>—विट्-सङ्ग, अस्, m. coherence or obstruction<BR>of the feces, constipation.<BR>—विट्-सारिका, f. a sort of<BR>thrush or variety of the bird inaccurately called<BR>‘Maina’ in Bengal.<BR>—विड्-गन्ध, अस्, m. a medi-<BR>cinal salt (= विड्-लवण).<BR>—विड्-ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>seizure or obstruction of the feces, constipation.<BR>—विड्-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced from ordure; (अम्), n. a<BR>fungus.<BR>—विड्-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced<BR>from ordure.<BR>—विड्-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, feeding on ordure<BR>(Manu XII. 56).<BR>—विड्-लवण, अम्, n. a medicinal<BR>salt (commonly called Vitlaban or Bitnoben).<BR>—विड्-<BR>वराह, अस्, m. a village or tame hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष|विषं|विषः
विष, अस्, अम्, n. poison, venom, bane, any-<BR>thing baneful or deadly; (अम्), n. water; the fibres<BR>attached to the stalk of the lotus; gum-myrrh; a<BR>kind of very active vegetable poison, Aconitum Ferox,<BR>= वत्स-नाभ; (आ), f. a tree (commonly called<BR>Atis, the bark of which is used as a red dye, also<BR>called अति-विषा); excrement; (for वि-षा, ‘intel-<BR>lect,’ see under वि-षो.)<BR>—विष-कण्टकिनी, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= बन्ध्या-कर्कोटकी).<BR>—विष-<BR>कन्द, अस्, m. a species of bulbous plant (= नील-<BR>कन्द).<BR>—विष-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a jar of poison.<BR>—विष-खा, आस्, m. one who digs for the fibres of<BR>the stem of the lotus, (also written बिस-खा.)<BR>—वि-<BR>ष-ग्रन्थि, N. of a plant (?).<BR>—विष-घा, f. a<BR>kind of twining shrub, Menispermum Cordifolium<BR>or Cocculus Cordifolius (= गुडूची).<BR>—विष-घातिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, poison-destroying, antidotal, an antidote;<BR>(ई), m. the tree Mimosa Sirissa (= शिरीष).<BR>—विष-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying or counteracting poison,<BR>antidotal, an antidote; (अस्), m. the tree Mimosa<BR>Sirissa; the plant Hedysarum Alhagi; Beleric Myro-<BR>balan, Terminalia Belerica; (ई), f. the pot-herb<BR>Hingtsha Repens; another plant (commonly called<BR>Bicchati); turmeric; bitter apple or colocynth.<BR>—विष-जुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of poison,<BR>poisonous; poisoned.<BR>—विष-ता, f. or विष-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the state or condition of poison, poisonous-<BR>ness.<BR>—विष-तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, resembling poison,<BR>fatal, deadly.<BR>—विष-द, अस्, आ, अम्, yielding or<BR>giving poison, poisonous; shedding water; (अस्), m.<BR>a cloud; (अम्), n. green vitriol.<BR>—विष-दंष्ट्रा,<BR>f. a medicinal plant and antidote (= सर्प-कङ्कालि).<BR>—विष-दन्तक, अस्, m. ‘having poisonous teeth,’<BR>a snake.<BR>—विष-दर्शन-मृत्युक, अस्, m. ‘dying<BR>at the sight of poison,’ a kind of pheasant; [cf. विष-<BR>मृत्यु.]<BR>—विष-दायक, अस्, इका, अम्, or विष-<BR>दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, giving poison, poisoning.<BR>—विष-<BR>दिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, smeared with poison, empoisoned,<BR>poisoned.<BR>—विष-दूषण, अम्, n. corrupting by<BR>poison, poisoning.<BR>—विष-दोष-हर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>taking away the ill effects of poison.<BR>—विष-द्रुम,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of poison tree, Upas tree.<BR>—विष-<BR>धर, अस्, आ, अम्, holding or containing poison,<BR>venomous, poisonous; (अस्), m. a snake.<BR>—विष-<BR>धर-निलय, अस्, m. ‘abode of snakes,’ Pātāla<BR>or the lower regions.<BR>—विष-धर्मा, f. cowach,<BR>Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR>—विष-धात्री, f. ‘poison-<BR>holder,’ N. of a goddess presiding over snakes, (she<BR>was wife of the Ṛṣi Jarat-kāru and sister of Vāsuki;<BR>cf. मनसा.<BR>—विष-नाशक, अस्, इका, अम्, poison-<BR>destroying, antidotal.<BR>—विष-नाशन, अस्, m. ‘poison-<BR>destroyer,’ an antidote; the tree Mimosa Sirissa;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of removing or curing poison.<BR>—विष-नाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, poison-destroying, any<BR>antidote; (इनी), f. a kind of plant (= विष-दंष्-<BR>ट्रा).<BR>—विष-निमित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, caused by poison.<BR>—विष-नुद्, त्, m. ‘poison-expeller,’ the plant<BR>Bignonia Indica.<BR>—विष-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has drunk poison.<BR>—विष-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>poisonous flowers,’ the plant Vangueria Spinosa;<BR>(अम्), n. the blue lotus.<BR>—विष-पुष्पक, अस्, m.<BR>sickness or disease caused by eating poisonous flowers.<BR>—विष-प्रयोग, अस्, m. the use or employment<BR>of poison, administering poison as a medicine.<BR>—वि-<BR>ष-भक्षण, अम्, n. the act of eating poison,<BR>taking poison.<BR>—विष-भिषज्, क्, m. a poison-<BR>doctor; a dealer in antidotes, one who pretends to<BR>cure the bites of snakes.<BR>—विष-भुजङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>a poisonous snake.<BR>—विष-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, bearing or<BR>containing poison, venomous, poisonous; (त्), m. a<BR>snake.<BR>—विष-मन्त्र, अस्, m. a snake-charmer,<BR>snake-catcher, one who pretends to charm snakes,<BR>one who cures the bite of snakes; (अम्), n. a charm<BR>for curing snake-bites.<BR>—विष-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of poison, poisonous.<BR>—विष-मुष्टि, इस्,<BR>f. a kind of shrub possessing medicinal properties (com-<BR>monly called Bishdori or Karsinh).<BR>—विष-मृत्यु,<BR>उस्, m. a sort of bird, a kind of pheasant (‘to whom<BR>poison is death,’ cf. विष-दर्शन-मृत्युक).<BR>—विष-रस, अस्, m. ‘poison-juice,’ a poisoned<BR>draught or potion.<BR>—विष-वल्लरी, f. a poisonous<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">Page0946-c+ 80</a>]<BR>creeper.<BR>—विष-विद्या, f. ‘poison-science,’ the ad-<BR>ministration of antidotes, the cure of poisons by drugs<BR>or charms.<BR>—विष-विधान, अम्, n. administering<BR>poison judiciously or by way of ordeal.<BR>—विष-<BR>विमुक्तात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, one whose soul<BR>or whose nature is released from poison.<BR>—विष-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m. a poison tree, the Upas tree.<BR>—वि-<BR>ष-वेग, अस्, m. ‘poison-force,’ the effect of poison<BR>(shown by various bodily effects or changes).<BR>—वि-<BR>ष-वैद्य, अस्, m. ‘poison-doctor,’ a dealer in<BR>antidotes or one professing to cure the bites of<BR>snakes.<BR>—विष-वैरिणी, f. ‘poison-enemy,’ a kind<BR>of grass used as an antidote (= निर्-विषा, q. v.).<BR>—विष-शालूक, अस्, m. the root of the lotus.<BR>—वि-<BR>ष-शूक, अस्, m. or विष-शृङ्गिन्, ई, m. ‘having<BR>a poisonous sting,’ a wasp.<BR>—विष-सूचक, अस्, m.<BR>‘poison-indicator,’ the Greek partridge, Perdix Rufa<BR>(= चकोर).<BR>—विष-सृक्कन्, आ, m. ‘poison-<BR>mouthed,’ a wasp.<BR>—विष-ह, अस्, आ, अम्, removing<BR>poison; (आ), f., N. of various plants (= देव-दाली;<BR>= निर्-विषा).<BR>—विष-हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, destroy-<BR>ing or counteracting poison; (त्री), f., N. of various<BR>plants (= अ-पराजिता; = निर्-विषा).<BR>—विष-हर,<BR>अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, removing venom, antidotal; (आ or ई),<BR>f. the goddess who protects from the venom of snakes,<BR>(see विष-धात्री, मनसा.)<BR>—विष-हृदय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, poison-hearted, cherishing hatred or hostility,<BR>malicious, malignant.<BR>—विषाक्त (˚ष-अक्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, smeared with poison, poisoned.<BR>—विषाग्नि<BR>(˚ष-अग्˚), इस्, m. the fire of poison.<BR>—विषाङ्कुर<BR>(˚ष-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘having a poisoned point,’ a<BR>spear, dart.<BR>—विषादनी (˚ष-अद्˚), f. ‘poison-<BR>destroying,’ a kind of creeper (= पलाशी).<BR>—विषा-<BR>नन (˚ष-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘having a poisonous mouth,’<BR>a snake.<BR>—विषान्तक (˚ष-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, poison-<BR>destroying, antidotal; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva,<BR>(so called because he swallowed the deadly poison<BR>produced at the churning of the ocean.)<BR>—वि-<BR>षापह (˚ष-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, poison-repelling,<BR>antidotic, an antidote, (मन्त्रैर् विषापहैः,<BR>with texts or charms which have the power of repel-<BR>ling poison); (अस्), m. a kind of tree, = मुष्कक;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of birth-wort, Aristolochia Indica (=<BR>अर्क-मूला; various other plants, = इन्द्र-वारुणी;<BR>= निर्-विषा; = नाग-दमनी; = सर्प-कङ्कालि-<BR>का).<BR>—विषाभावा (˚ष-अभ्˚), f. ‘having no poison,’<BR>a species of plant (= निर्-विषा).<BR>—विषायुध<BR>(˚ष-आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘armed with venom,’ a snake.<BR>—विषाराति (˚ष-अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘poison-enemy,’ a<BR>species of plant (= कृष्ण-धत्तूरक).<BR>—विषारि<BR>(˚ष-अरि), इस्, m. ‘poison-enemy,’ a kind of plant<BR>or tree (= महा-चञ्चू; = घृत-करञ्ज).<BR>—वि-<BR>षास्य (˚ष-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘poison-mouthed,’ a<BR>snake; (आ), f. the marking-nut plant, Semecarpus<BR>Anacardium.<BR>—विषास्वाद (˚ष-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>tasting poison (Manu XI. 9; cf. मध्व्-आपात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषणि
विषणि, इस्, m. a sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषल|विषलं|विषलः
विषल, अस्, m. poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाय
विषाय, Nom. A. विषायते, -यितुम्, to become<BR>poison, turn into poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषार|विषारः
विषार, अस्, m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषालु
विषालु, उस्, उस्, उ, venomous, poisonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषित
1. विषित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. extended, spread, cast,<BR>(perhaps for 2. वि-षित, see under वि-षि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ट|विष्टः
2. विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 941, col. 2),<BR>pervaded; (आ), f. the feces, excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टि|विष्टिः
2. विष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ (for 1. see p. 941, col. 2), per-<BR>forming, labouring; (इस्), f. pervading, penetrating;<BR>occupation, act, action; hire, wages; unpaid labour;<BR>sending, dispatching; consigning to hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ट्वी
विष्ट्वी, ind., Ved. having pervaded; having per-<BR>formed, (Sāy. = व्याप्य, कृत्वा; in Naigh. II. 1.<BR>enumerated among the कर्म-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्य|विष्यः
विष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of poison, deserving<BR>death by poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषञ्ज्|विषंज्
विषञ्ज् वि-षञ्ज् (-सञ्ज्), cl. 1. P. -षजति,<BR>-षङ्क्तुम्, to attach to, fix or fasten to, fix on;<BR>to hang or suspend upon (anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषक्त
वि-षक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, firmly fixed or fastened to<BR>or entangled in (with loc.); clinging closely, adhering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">Page0947-a+ 79</a>]<BR>to, firmly rooted; in contact with, hung or sus-<BR>pended on (anything); emaciated, (Sāy. = विशेषेण<BR>सक्तावयव, कृशावयव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0946-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषङ्ग
वि-षङ्ग, अस्, m. attachment, contact; hanging<BR>or depending on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्ड|विषंड|विषंडं|विषण्डं
विषण्ड विषण्ड, अम्, n. the fibres of the<BR>stalk of the water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषत्वर
विषत्वर विषत्वर, अस्, m. a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषद्
विषद् वि-षद् (-सद्), cl. 1. 6. P. -षीदति<BR>(Impf. व्य्-अषीदत्, or व्य्-असीदत्, Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 119;<BR>Perf. वि-षसाद, Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 118), -षत्तुम्, to<BR>sink down, be exhausted; to be sorrowful or afflicted<BR>or dejected; to despair, despond; to be afraid: Caus.<BR>-षादयति, -यितुम्, to cause to sink down, exhaust,<BR>make sorrowful or fearful, afflict, vex, grieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्ण|विषण्णः
वि-षण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, dejected, sad, desponding,<BR>spiritless, downcast, out of spirits, wanting in energy,<BR>disinclined to exertion.<BR>—विषण्ण-ता, f. or वि-<BR>षण्ण-त्व, अम्, n. dejection, sadness, want of<BR>energy or spirit, languor, lassitude (especially as one<BR>of the effects of unsuccessful love).<BR>—विषण्ण-मु-<BR>ख, अस्, ई, अम्, or विषण्ण-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dejected in countenance, looking sad or dejected.<BR>—विषण्ण-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, having a sorrowful<BR>aspect, being in a sorrowful mood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाद|विषादः
वि-षाद, अस्, m. dejection, depression, lowness of<BR>spirits, despondency, want of energy, languor, lassi-<BR>tude (especially as the result of unrequited love);<BR>sadness, sorrow, affliction; disappointment, despair<BR>(one of the Vyabhicāri-bhāvas); fear, weakness;<BR>dulness, stupidity, insensibility (= मोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषादित
वि-षादित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to sink down,<BR>made sorrowful, dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषादिन्
विषादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dejected, disconsolate, sad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषीदत्
वि-षीदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sinking down, despond-<BR>ing, sorrowing, despairing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषम|विषमं|विषमः
विषम वि-षम, अस्, आ, अम्, uneven, rough,<BR>rugged, hilly, difficult of access; unequal, irregular;<BR>odd, not even (in numbers); different; difficult, hard<BR>to be understood (as a book); rough, coarse, rude,<BR>cross; disagreeable, painful, troublesome, vexatious;<BR>odd, unusual, unequalled, unparalleled; intermittent,<BR>inconstant; unfair, dishonest, partial; bad, adverse,<BR>unpropitious; wicked; fearful, awful, unhappy; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. unevenness, inequality;<BR>oddness (of numbers); an inaccessible place, thicket,<BR>pit, precipice; difficulty, pain, misfortune; (in rhe-<BR>toric) description of unusual or incompatible cause<BR>and effect; (अम्), ind. unequally, unfairly.<BR>—विष-<BR>म-कर्ण, अस्, m. (or अम्, n. ?), a quadrangle or<BR>tetragon with unequal diagonals; the hypothenuse<BR>of a right-angled triangle (especially as formed be-<BR>tween the gnomon of a dial and the two sides of the<BR>shadow).<BR>—विषम-कर्मन्, अ, n. an odd or un-<BR>equalled act; (in arithmetic or algebra) the finding<BR>of two quantities when the difference of their squares<BR>is given and either the sum or difference of the<BR>quantities.<BR>—विषम-काल, अस्, m. an unfavourable<BR>time, inauspicious season.<BR>—विषम-खात, अम्,<BR>n. an irregular excavation or solid, one with unequal<BR>sides.<BR>—विषम-चतुरस्र or विषम-चतुर्-<BR>भुज, अम्, n. an unequal four-sided figure, a tra-<BR>pezium.<BR>—विषम-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘having uneven<BR>or odd leaves,’ the plant Echites Scholaris.<BR>—वि-<BR>षम-च्छाया, f. ‘uneven-shadow,’ the shadow of the<BR>gnomon at noon when the sun is on the equinoctial<BR>line.<BR>—विषम-ज्वर, अस्, m. irregular fever, irre-<BR>gularly remittent fever.<BR>—विषम-त्रिभुज, अस्,<BR>m. a scalene triangle.<BR>—विषम-धातु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>one whose bodily humors are unequally proportioned,<BR>unhealthy.<BR>—विषम-नयन, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>three or an odd number of eyes,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—विषम-पद, अस्, ई, अम्, having unequal foot-<BR>marks.<BR>—विषम-भोजन, अम्, n. eating at irre-<BR>gular hours.<BR>—विषम-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, produced<BR>by or resulting from inequality.<BR>—विषम-रूप्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, produced by or resulting from unequal<BR>quantities or qualities.<BR>—विषम-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f.<BR>adverse fortune, bad luck.<BR>—विषम-विभाग, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">Page0947-b+ 77</a>]<BR>m. unequal division of property amongst co-heirs.<BR>—विषम-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sleeping irregularly.<BR>—विषम-शिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘unfairly left,’ unjust,<BR>unfair (as applied to a division of property &c.).<BR>—विषम-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘having an uneven dis-<BR>position,’ cross tempered, rough, difficult.<BR>—विष-<BR>म-साहस, अम्, n. irregular boldness, temerity,<BR>daring.<BR>—विषम-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing un-<BR>evenly; being in an inaccessible position; being in<BR>embarrassed circumstances, being in difficulty or mis-<BR>fortune.<BR>—विषमाक्ष (˚म-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>three or an odd number of eyes,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—विषमान्न (˚म-अन्˚), अम्, n. irregular or<BR>unusual food.<BR>—विषमायुध (˚म-आय्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘having five or an odd number of arrows,’ an epithet<BR>of Kāma-deva.<BR>—विषमावतार (˚म-अव्˚), अस्,<BR>m. descending on uneven ground.<BR>—विषमाशन<BR>(˚म-अश्˚), अम्, n. eating irregularly (either as to<BR>quantity or time).<BR>—विषमाशय (˚म-आश्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having an unfair disposition, dishonest, crafty.<BR>—विषमी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become<BR>uneven or irregular, to stumble.<BR>—विषमेक्षण<BR>(˚म-ईक्˚), अस्, m. = विषमाक्ष, an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—विषमेषु (˚म-इष्˚), उस्, m. ‘having an<BR>odd number of arrows,’ an epithet of Kāma-deva;<BR>[cf. विषमायुध.]<BR>—विषमोन्नत (˚म-<BR>उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, unevenly raised.<BR>—विषमोपल<BR>(˚म-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having rough stones or rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमित
विषमित, अस्, आ, अम्, made uneven or irregular,<BR>made crooked, frowning, (विषमित-चक्षुषा,<BR>with frowning or scowling eye); made difficult to<BR>be walked on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमीय|विषमीयं
विषमीय, अस्, आ, अम्, connected with or pro-<BR>duced by inequality, resulting from inequalities, un-<BR>equal, uneven, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषय|विषयः
विषय वि-षय. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्
विषह् वि-षह् (-सह्), cl. 1. A. -षहते,<BR>-षहितुम् or -सोढुम् (not -षोढुम्, Pāṇ. VIII.<BR>3, 115), to endure, bear, suffer, sustain; to be able<BR>to resist or overcome; to be able to conquer; to be<BR>able to settle or determine; to be able to do any-<BR>thing (with infin., e. g. विहातुम् विषेहे, he was<BR>able to quit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्य
1. वि-षह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne or endured;<BR>possible to be determined, (सीमायाम् अविषह्या-<BR>याम्, when a boundary is not possible to be settled,<BR>Manu VIII. 265); possible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्य
2. वि-षह्य, ind. having endured, having borne,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसोढ
वि-सोढ, अस्, आ, अम् (Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 115), en-<BR>dured, borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषा
विषा वि-षा, ind. See वि-षो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाण|विषाणं|विषाणः
विषाण विषाण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably<BR>fr. वि-षो, thought by others to be fr. rt. 2. विष्),<BR>a horn, the horn of any animal (usually neut., ख-<BR>री-व्˚, an ass's horn, i. e. a mere chimera or impos-<BR>sibility, = शश-व्˚, q. v.), the tusk of an elephant or<BR>boar; (ई), f. a particular plant (the fruit of which is<BR>compared to a ram's horn, = मेष-शृङ्गी); a medi-<BR>cinal root, = क्षीर-काकोली; (अम्), n. a sort of<BR>medicinal plant, Costus Speciosus (= कुष्ठ).<BR>—वि-<BR>षाण-कोष, अस्, m. the hollow of a horn.<BR>—वि-<BR>षाणोन्नामित-स्कन्ध (˚ण-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having shoulders raised up towards (or high enough<BR>to meet) the horns.<BR>—विषाणोल्लिखित-स्कन्ध<BR>(˚ण-उल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, whose shoulders are grazed<BR>or scratched by his horns (said of the leader of a<BR>herd of cattle to mark superiority).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिका
विषाणिका, f. a sort of plant (= मेष-शृङ्गी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिन्
विषाणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having horns, horned, having<BR>huge tusks; (ई), m. any horned animal or animal<BR>having tusks; a bull; an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाद|विषादः
विषाद वि-षाद. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषि
विषि वि-षि (-सि), cl. 5. 9. P. A. -षिणोति,<BR>-षिणुते, -षिणाति, -षिणीते, -षेतुम्, to bind to<BR>(any one or anything), attach, connect; to conciliate,<BR>appease (Ved.); to unbind, loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषय|विषयः
वि-षय, अस्, m. an object of sense, (these are<BR>five in number, the five इन्द्रिय or organs of sense<BR>having each their proper विषय or object, viz. 1.<BR>शब्द, ‘sound,’ for the ear, cf. श्रुति-विषय;<BR>2. स्पर्श, ‘tangibility,’ for the skin; 3. रूप,<BR>‘form’ or ‘colour,’ for the eye; 4. रस, ‘savour,’<BR>for the tongue; 5. गन्ध, ‘odour,’ for the nose:<BR>and these five Viṣayas are sometimes called the<BR>Guṇas or ‘properties’ of the five elements, ether, air,<BR>fire, water, earth, respectively; cf. श्रुति-विषय-<BR>गुण); a symbolical expression for the number five;<BR>anything perceptible by the senses, any object (of<BR>affection, of desire, of art, &c.); object of concern<BR>or attention, worldly object or aim, pursuit, affair,<BR>concern, business, transaction; worldly or sensual en-<BR>joyment, pleasure of sense, sensuality, subject, subject-<BR>matter, topic, the subject of a book, (at the end of an<BR>adj. comp. = ‘being on the subject of,’ ‘treating of,’<BR>‘relating to,’ e. g. धन-विषय, अस्, आ, अम्, re-<BR>lating to wealth); subject of an argument, general<BR>head, (one of the Adhikaraṇas, see अधि-करण);<BR>a country, native country, home, region, district,<BR>province, kingdom, realm, domain, empire, place;<BR>department, field, sphere, element, peculiar province,<BR>peculiar abode (e. g. a particular study is the विषय<BR>of its professors, a particular town of its citizens, water<BR>of fish, air of birds, &c.); that which comes within<BR>the range of sight, horizon, scope, range, compass,<BR>reach [cf. चक्षुर्-व्˚]; refuge, asylum; anything<BR>indigenous or peculiar to a province, &c.; a religious<BR>obligation or observance; a collection of villages;<BR>a lover, husband; semen virile; विषये, loc. c. sing.<BR>in or on any object, (often used by commentators to<BR>denote that a word is in the loc. c.), on the subject<BR>of, in relation to, in regard to, concerning, regarding,<BR>with reference to, (अत्र विषये, with regard to<BR>this object; स्त्रीणां विषये, concerning women;<BR>धन-विषये, on the subject of wealth.) विषय<BR>may be often used in some of the above senses at<BR>the end of adj. comps. (e. g. अवकाश-विषय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having space as a sphere of action; अनन्य-व्˚,<BR>having regard to no other object; cf. पलायन-व्˚,<BR>अ-चक्षुर्-व्˚).<BR>—विषय-कर्मन्, अ, n. worldly<BR>business or act.<BR>—विषय-काम, अस्, m. desire of<BR>worldly goods or pleasures.<BR>—विषय-ग्राम, अस्,<BR>m. the aggregate or assemblage of objects of sense<BR>or visible objects.<BR>—विषय-ज्ञान, अम्, n. acquaint-<BR>ance with worldly affairs.<BR>—विषय-ता, f. or विषय-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the character or condition of an object, the<BR>relation between an object and the knowledge of it<BR>(in phil.).<BR>—विषय-प्रत्यभिज्ञान, अम्, n. the<BR>recognition of objects (in phil.).<BR>—विषय-प्रवण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, attached to objects of sense, addicted to<BR>sensual objects.<BR>—विषय-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, engaged<BR>in the affairs of life.<BR>—विषय-विचार, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a treatise by Gadādhara.<BR>—विषय-सङ्ग-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, produced by addiction to sensuality.<BR>—विषय-सुख, अम्, n. the pleasures of sense.<BR>—विषय-स्पृहा, f. desire for objects of sense,<BR>longing for sensual objects.<BR>—विषयात्मक (˚य-<BR>आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of or identified with<BR>sensual or worldly objects, having a sensual nature,<BR>sensual, carnal.<BR>—विषयाभिरति (˚य-अभ्˚), इस्, f.<BR>the enjoyment of objects of sense.<BR>—विषयासक्त<BR>(˚य-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, attached to objects of sense,<BR>devoted to the world.<BR>—विषयी-करण, अम्, n. the<BR>making anything an object of perception or thought,<BR>taking cognizance of an object.<BR>—विषयी-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make anything an object of<BR>sense or an object of thought; to apprehend, take<BR>cognizance of, perceive.<BR>—विषयी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>made an object of sense or activity; perceived.<BR>—वि-<BR>षयी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to become<BR>an object of sense or perception; to become an object<BR>of concern or attention; to become the province or<BR>property of any one or anything.<BR>—विषयी-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, become or made an object of perception,<BR>&c.<BR>—विषयैषिन् (˚य-एष्˚), ई, इणी, इ, desirous<BR>of objects of sense, devoted to worldly pursuits.<BR>—विषयोपसेवा (˚य-उप्˚), f. addiction to plea-<BR>sures of sense, sensuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0947-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयक
विषयक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to an object; (at<BR>the end of comps.) having for an object or subject,<BR>relating to, having reference to, on the subject of,<BR>treating of, concerning.<BR>—विषयक-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being an object, the state of an object or affair<BR>or circumstance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयायिन्
विषयायिन्, ई, m. (according to some fr. विषय +<BR>यिन् = विन्), any one addicted to objects of sense or<BR>attentive to worldly objects; a man of business, man<BR>of the world; a king; a sensualist, voluptuary, epicu-<BR>rean; epithet of Kāma-deva (the god of love); a<BR>materialist, one who disbelieves the existence of<BR>anything not cognizable by the senses; an organ of<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयिन्
विषयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, relating to objects of sense,<BR>attached to sensual objects, engaged or interested in<BR>worldly occupations or enjoyments; sensual, carnal,<BR>worldly; (ई), m. a king (as ruling a country or en-<BR>gaged in the business of government); a man of<BR>business, man of the world, worldling; a sensualist,<BR>voluptuary; epithet of Kāma-deva (god of love);<BR>a materialist, one who disbelieves or denies the exist-<BR>ence of everything except objects of sense; (इ), n.<BR>an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयीय
विषयीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to an object, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषित
2. वि-षित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 946, col. 3;<BR>for 3. see under वि-षो), unfastened, loosened, let<BR>loose, unarrested, discharged, (Sāy. = वि-मुक्त, वि-<BR>ष्यूत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषु
विषु विषु, ind. (perhaps connected with<BR>1. वि or for an original द्विषु, loc. pl. of द्वि, see<BR>1. वि), in two equal parts, equally, variously, differ-<BR>ently, manifold, many; same, like.<BR>—विषु-पद,<BR>अम्, n. the autumnal equinox (?).<BR>—विषु-रूप, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. of various or different shape or colour,<BR>&c.<BR>—विषू-वृत्, त्, त्, त् (विषू for विषु), Ved.<BR>turning or moving everywhere, existing everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुण|विषुणः
विषुण, अस्, आ, अम्, having various motion or<BR>extension, moving variously, going in various ways,<BR>having various forms, (Sāy. = विष्व्-अञ्च् or विष्वग्-<BR>अञ्चन or नाना-रूप); having uniform motion;<BR>adverse, hostile, disorderly, wicked, (Sāy. = वि-षम,<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 21, 5; = पराङ्-मुख, Ṛg-veda V.<BR>34, 6); (अस्), m. the equinox (= विषुव below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुप|विषुपं
विषुप, अम्, n. = विषुव, the equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुव|विषुवं
विषुव, अम्, n. (abbreviated from विषु-वत्),<BR>‘point of equal separation,’ the equinoctial point, the<BR>first point of Aries or Libra into which the sun enters<BR>at the vernal or autumnal equinox.<BR>—विषुव-<BR>च्छाया, f. the shadow of the gnomon or index of a<BR>dial at noon when the sun is on the equinoctial<BR>points.<BR>—विषुव-दिन, अम्, n. the day of the<BR>equinox.<BR>—विषुव-रेखा, f. the equinoctial line.<BR>—विषुव-सङ्क्रान्ति, इस्, f. the sun's equinoctial<BR>passage, the passing of the sun into the next sign at<BR>either equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवत्|विषुवन्त्
विषु-वत्, त्, n. (probably formed fr. विषु +<BR>वत्), ‘possessing a separation into two equal parts,’<BR>the point of equal separation, i. e. the equinoctial<BR>point or equinox; the central day in a Sattra or<BR>sacrificial session.<BR>—विषुवत्-प्रभा, f. the equi-<BR>noctial shadow.<BR>—विषुवत्-सङ्क्रान्ति, इस्, f. the<BR>sun's equinoctial passage, the passing of the sun into<BR>the next sign at either equinox.<BR>—विषुवद्-भा, आस्,<BR>f. the equinoctial shadow.<BR>—विषुवद्-वृत्त, अम्,<BR>n. the equinoctial circle or line.<BR>—विषुवन्-मण्-<BR>डल, अम्, n. the equinoctial circle or line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वञ्च्|विष्वंच्
विष्व्-अञ्च्, अङ्, -षूची, अक् (fr. विषु + अञ्च्; some-<BR>times incorrectly written विश्वञ्च्), going everywhere,<BR>all-pervading; separating into two or into several<BR>parts, different, various; alternately (as day and<BR>night); (अक्), n. the equinox; (अक्), ind. every way,<BR>all around, all about, everywhere; alternately, (Sāy.<BR>= संयक्, Ṛg-veda I. 146, 3.)<BR>—विष्वक्-षेण<BR>or विष्वक्-सेन, अस्, m. (sometimes written विश्वक्-<BR>सेन), ‘whose hosts or powers go everywhere,’<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu, or of a particular form of that<BR>deity to whom the fragments of a sacrifice are<BR>offered; N. of the fourteenth Manu; of a king;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of plant (commonly called Priyaṅgu).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">Page0948-b+ 76</a>]<BR>—विष्वक्सेन-प्रिया, f. ‘beloved of Viṣṇu,’ an<BR>epithet of Lakṣmī; a sort of yam, Dioscorea.<BR>—विष्वग्-अश्व, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—विष्वग्-<BR>आयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, spreading or going in every<BR>direction.<BR>—विष्वग्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone all about,<BR>spread, extended.<BR>—विष्वग्-गति, इस्, f. going all<BR>about, going everywhere, entering into every (topic).<BR>—विष्वग्-ज्योतिस्, इस्, m., N. of the eldest of the<BR>100 sons of Śata-jit.<BR>—विष्वग्-वायु, उस्, m. a<BR>kind of noxious wind which blows from all quarters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वद्र्यञ्च्|विष्वद्र्यंच्
विष्वद्र्यञ्च्, अङ्, -द्रीची, अक् (fr. विषु + अद्रि +<BR>अञ्च्; cf. तद्र्यञ्च्, मद्र्यञ्च्), going everywhere,<BR>all-pervading, going in all directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वाञ्च्
विष्वाञ्च्, आङ्, m. (for विष्व्-अञ्च्), Ved., N. of an<BR>Asura who had the power of going everywhere (Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 117, 16).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषूचिका
विषूचिका वि-षूचिका, f. cholera, = वि-शू-<BR>चिका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषूवत्|विषूवन्त्
विषूवत् विषूवत्, आन्, अती, अत् (in the Pada<BR>text of Ṛg-veda I. 84, 10. विषु-वत्), Ved. pervad-<BR>ing, (Sāy. = व्याप्ति-युक्त, as if fr. rt. 2. विष्);<BR>poured forth (as Soma juice); prepared in the sacri-<BR>fice, (as if for वि-षुवत् fr. rt. 3. सु); (आन्), m. a<BR>particular kind of sacrifice; [cf. विषु-वत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषो
विषो वि-षो (-सो), cl. 4. P. -ष्यति, -षातुम्,<BR>Ved. to gush out, rush forth; to bring to an end or<BR>issue, cause to issue out; to open, distend, (Sāy. =<BR>विवृतं कृ); to offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषा
वि-षा, ind. (said in Uṇādi-s. IV. 36. to be fr.<BR>वि-षो above), intellect, understanding. (For विषा<BR>see under विष, p. 946, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषित
3. वि-षित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 946, col. 3;<BR>for 2. see col. 1), opened, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यत्
वि-ष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, throwing, hurling, (Sāy. =<BR>प्र-क्षिपत्, Ṛg-veda V. 45, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्क्
विष्क् विष्क् [cf. rt. वष्क्], cl. 10. P.<BR>विष्कयति, -यितुम्, to see, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्द्|विष्कंद्
विष्कन्द् वि-ष्कन्द् (also written वि-स्कन्द्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. P. -ष्कन्दति (or -स्कन्दति), -ष्कन्-<BR>तुम् (or -स्कन्तुम्), to go in different directions,<BR>wander about, stray, disperse; to go away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्त्तृ
वि-ष्कन्त्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, going in various direc-<BR>tions, dispersing; going away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्द|विष्कंद|विष्कंदः|विष्कन्दः
वि-ष्कन्द, अस्, m. dispersing, going away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्न
वि-स्कन्न, अस्, आ, अम् (not वि-ष्कण्ण, see Pāṇ.<BR>VIII. 3, 73), gone in various directions, dispersed,<BR>gone away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कभ्
विष्कभ् वि-ष्कभ्. See वि-ष्कम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भ्|विष्कंभ्
विष्कम्भ् वि-ष्कम्भ् (also written वि-<BR>स्कम्भ्, q. v.), cl. 5. 9. P., 1. A. -ष्कभ्नोति,<BR>-ष्कभ्नाति, -स्कम्भते (Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 77),<BR>-ष्कम्भितुम् (Ved. Inf. विष्कभे, Sāy. = वि-<BR>ष्कम्भणाय), to fix firmly, support, prop; to<BR>obstruct; to fix asunder, fix separately, hold asunder;<BR>to set free, allow to come forth, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कब्ध
वि-ष्कब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed firmly, obstructed,<BR>impeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कभित
वि-ष्कभित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fixed or held asunder,<BR>separately fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भ|विष्कंभ|विष्कंभः|विष्कम्भः
वि-ष्कम्भ अस्, m. obstacle, hindrance, impedi-<BR>ment, resistance; the bolt or bar of a door, the sup-<BR>porting beam or pillar of a house; a post; a tree;<BR>the first of the twenty-seven astronomical periods<BR>called Yogas, the leading star of the first lunar man-<BR>sion; an interlude or introductory scene (coming<BR>between the acts [अङ्कयोर् मध्य-वर्ती] and<BR>performed by an inferior actor or actors [नीच-पात्र-<BR>प्रयोजितः], who explain to the audience the pro-<BR>gress of the plot, and thus bind firmly together the<BR>story of the drama by concisely alluding to what is<BR>supposed to have happened in the intervals of the<BR>acts or what is likely to happen at the end, cf. प्र-<BR>वेशक); spreading, extension; the breadth or dia-<BR>meter of a circle; action, doing anything; a parti-<BR>cular posture practised by Yogins or devotees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भक|विष्कंभक
वि-ष्कम्भक, अस्, m. = वि-ष्कम्भ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भण
वि-ष्कम्भण, अम्, n. the act of obstructing,<BR>impeding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भित|विष्कंभित
वि-ष्कम्भित, अस्, आ, अम्, impeded, hindered,<BR>obstructed, precluded, shut out from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भिन्|विष्कंभिन्
वि-ष्कम्भिन्, ई, इणी, इ, obstructive, impeding;<BR>(ई), m. the bolt or bar of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्किर|विष्किरः
विष्किर विष्-किर, अस्, m. (fr. वि-कॄ with eu-<BR>phonic स् inserted, cf. वि-किर), scattering about, tearing<BR>to pieces; one who scatters about or tears in pieces;<BR>a cock; a bird (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ट|विष्टः
विष्ट विष्ट. See p. 946, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टन्
विष्टन् वि-ष्टन् (वि-स्तन्), cl. 1. P. -ष्टनति,<BR>-ष्टनितुम्, to groan, sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टप्
विष्टप् विष्टप्, प्, f. (probably connected<BR>with वि-ष्टम्भ् below), ‘anything fixed,’ a place,<BR>region, world; the firmament, heaven, (Sāy. = स्वर्ग-<BR>लोक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टप|विष्टपं|विष्टपः
विष्टप, अस्, अम्, m. n. a world, region, place,<BR>(Sāy. = स्थान; cf. पिष्टप); a vessel, cup (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भ्|विष्टंभ्
विष्टम्भ् वि-ष्टम्भ् (-स्तम्भ्), cl. 5. 9. P.<BR>-ष्टभ्नोति, -ष्टभ्नाति (Perf. वि-तस्तम्भ),<BR>-ष्टम्भितुम्, to prop or fix asunder, hold or keep<BR>apart, fix firmly, prop, support; to place or put down<BR>firmly, plant (the feet) firmly; to obstruct, stop, pro-<BR>hibit, hinder: Caus. -ष्टम्भयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to stop, obstruct; to paralyse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टब्ध
वि-ष्टब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed apart; fixed firmly,<BR>propped, supported, stayed, fixed, firm, well-supported,<BR>placed firmly, planted in or upon; obstructed, stopped,<BR>hindered, paralysed, made stiff or motionless.<BR>—वि-<BR>ष्टब्ध-ता, f. firmness, confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टभ
वि-ष्टभ, अम्, n. ‘that which is fixed or planted<BR>firmly,’ the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टभित
वि-ष्टभित, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed firmly, propped,<BR>supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टभ्य
वि-ष्टभ्य, ind. having fixed asunder, having<BR>propped, having planted (the feet) firmly, having rested<BR>upon, having stopped, having made to stand still.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भ|विष्टंभ|विष्टंभः|विष्टम्भः
वि-ष्टम्भ, अस्, m. a support, supporter, prop<BR>(Ved.); planting firmly, placing in or on; stepping,<BR>planting the feet; obstruction, impediment, hindrance,<BR>obstacle; stopping, staying; obstruction of the urine or<BR>feces, ischury, constipation; paralysis, loss of motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भिन्|विष्टंभिन्
वि-ष्टम्भिन्, ई, इनी, इ, obstructing, stopping, im-<BR>peding, hindering; checking (as perspiration &c.),<BR>chilling; making motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टर|विष्टरः
विष्टर वि-ष्टर, अस्, m. (= वि-स्तर, see<BR>under वि-स्तृ), anything spread out, a layer, bed,<BR>couch; a seat, stool, chair, couch, &c.; the seat of<BR>the presiding Brāhman at a sacrifice (either real or<BR>in effigy); a seat made of twenty-five straws of Kuśa<BR>grass tied up in a sheaf; a handful of Kuśa grass; a<BR>tree.<BR>—विष्टर-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, occupying a seat,<BR>seated.<BR>—विष्टर-श्रवस्, आस्, m. ‘having broad or<BR>spreading ears (?),’ an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—विष्टर-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting on a seat, re-<BR>clining on a bed (of leaves &c.).<BR>—विष्टरोत्तर<BR>(˚र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, covered with Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टार|विष्टारः
वि-ष्टार, अस्, m. (only used for वि-स्तार when<BR>metre is denoted, according to Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 94,<BR>III. 3, 34), expansion, extension.<BR>—विष्टार-पङ्क्ति,<BR>इस्, f. a particular form of Paṅkti metre (consisting<BR>of four lines, the first and last lines having eight syl-<BR>lables each and the second and third twelve each).<BR>—विष्टार-बृहती, f. a species of Bṛhatī metre<BR>(containing eight syllables in the first and fourth lines<BR>and ten in the second and third lines).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टारिन्
विष्टारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. epithet of a kind of ob-<BR>lation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टि|विष्टिः
विष्टि विष्टि. See p. 941, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टिरस्
विष्टिरस् विष्टिरस्, pl., this word occurs in<BR>Ṛg-veda II. 13, 10. in connection with षट्, and<BR>is said by Sāy. to mean the six widely spread objects<BR>(विस्तीर्णाः षट्), viz. heaven, earth, day, night,<BR>water, and plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टु
विष्टु वि-ष्टु (-स्तु), cl. 2. P. -ष्टौति, -ष्ट-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">Page0949-a+ 78</a>]<BR>वीति (Impf. व्य्-अष्टौत् or व्य्-अस्तौत्, Pāṇ. VIII. 3,<BR>71), -ष्टोतुम्, to praise very much, extol with praises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0948-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टाव
वि-ष्टाव, N. of a division of the Vi-ṣṭuti (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टुत
वि-ष्टुत, अस्, आ, अम्, praised highly, extolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टुति
वि-ष्टुति, इस्, f. a variety of arrangement for re-<BR>citing the verses of the Tri-vṛt Stoma, (three such<BR>varieties are enumerated, viz. उद्यती, परिवर्तिनी,<BR>and कुलायिनी); (अयस्), f. pl., N. of particular trea-<BR>tises on Vedic ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठल|विष्ठलं
विष्ठल वि-ष्ठल (i. e. वि-स्थ्˚), अम्, n. a re-<BR>mote place, a spot situated apart or at a distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठा
विष्ठा 1. वि-ष्ठा (-स्था), cl. 1. A. -तिष्ठते<BR>(ep. also P. -ति), Aor. व्य्-अष्ठात्, -ष्ठातुम्, to<BR>stand apart; to stand firmly, remain stationary or<BR>fixed, stay, abide, remain, dwell, stop; to be diffused<BR>or spread abroad; to spread everywhere, be present<BR>in; to go out; to attack, invade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्थान
वि-तस्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (for वि-तिष्ठमान),<BR>stopping, being stopped or impeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितिष्ठमान
वि-तिष्ठमान, अस्, आ, अम्, remaining fixed or<BR>stationary, abiding, staying, being permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठा
2. वि-ष्ठा, f., Ved. intermediate space, interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठित
वि-ष्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, abiding, stopping; fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठा
विष्ठा 3. विष्ठा, f. (probably connected<BR>with विष्टा, see under 2. विष्ट), feces, excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णापू
विष्णापू विष्णापू, ऊस्, m., Ved., N. of a Ṛṣi<BR>(restored to his father Viśvaka by the Aśvins).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णु|विष्णुः
विष्णु विष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ (in Uṇādi-s. III.<BR>39. said to be fr. rt. 2. विष्, ‘to pervade;’ according<BR>to some fr. rt. 1. विश्), all-pervading, encompassing,<BR>pervading, penetrating (Ved); (उस्), m., N. of one<BR>of the principal Hindū deities, (in the later mythology<BR>regarded as ‘the preserver,’ and with Brahmā ‘the<BR>creator’ and Śiva ‘the destroyer,’ constituting the<BR>well-known Tri-mūrti or triad; although Viṣṇu<BR>comes second in the triad he is identified with the<BR>supreme deity by his worshippers; in the Vedic<BR>period, however, he is not placed in the foremost<BR>rank, and though frequently invoked with Indra,<BR>Varuṇa, the Maruts, Rudra, Vāyu, and the Ādityas,<BR>his superiority to these is never stated, and he is even<BR>described in one place as celebrating the praises of<BR>Indra and deriving his power from that god [cf.<BR>his later name इन्द्रानुज, ‘younger brother of<BR>Indra’], the point which distinguishes him from the<BR>other Vedic deities being chiefly his striding over the<BR>heavens, which he is said to do in three paces [see<BR>त्रि-विक्रम], explained as denoting the threefold<BR>manifestations of light in the form of fire, lightning,<BR>and the sun, or as designating the three daily stations<BR>of the sun in his rising, culminating, and setting;<BR>the later legend of the Vāmana Ava-tāra grew out<BR>of this Vedic conception [see बलि]; he does not<BR>appear to have been included at first among the<BR>Ādityas or sons of Aditi, whose number in the Vedic<BR>period varies from six to eight, though in later times,<BR>when their number was raised to twelve, represent-<BR>ing the sun in the twelve months of the year, Viṣṇu<BR>is accorded the foremost place among them; in the<BR>Brāhmaṇas he is identified with sacrifice, and in one<BR>described as a dwarf; in the Mahā-bhārata and Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa he is not connected with the sun, but gradually<BR>rises to the supremacy which he now enjoys as the most<BR>popular deity of modern Hindū worship, and although<BR>in some passages of the former he is represented as<BR>paying homage to Śiva [cf. his name शिव-कीर्तन],<BR>the great rivalry between these gods and their wor-<BR>shippers — who are respectively called Vaiṣṇavas and<BR>Śaivas, and who each exalt their favourite to the first<BR>place in the Hindū Pantheon — is not fully developed<BR>till the period of the Purāṇas: the distinguishing<BR>feature in the character of the Post-vedic Viṣṇu is<BR>his condescending to become incarnate in a portion<BR>of his essence on ten principal occasions, to set right<BR>particular disturbances or deliver mankind from certain<BR>great dangers; his ten principal incarnations or Ava-<BR>tāras are, 1. the Matsya or ‘fish;’ 2. the Kūrma or<BR>‘tortoise;’ 3. the Varāha or ‘boar;’ 4. the Nara-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-b" target="_blank">Page0949-b+ 81</a>]<BR>siṃha or ‘man-lion;’ 5. the Vāmana or ‘dwarf’ [see<BR>बलि]; 6. Paraśu-rāma or ‘Rāma with the axe,’<BR>i. e. Rāma, son of Jamad-agni; 7. Rāma-candra or<BR>‘the illustrious Rāma,’ i. e. Rāma, the son of Daśa-<BR>ratha and hero of the Rāmāyaṇa; 8. Kṛṣṇa or<BR>‘the dark One,’ who is held by the Vaiṣṇavas to be<BR>not so much an incarnation of Viṣṇu as the very<BR>essence of Viṣṇu or rather Viṣṇu himself, so that<BR>the Bala-rāma incarnation, which is sometimes mixed<BR>up with this eighth Ava-tāra, is also occasionally<BR>substituted for it; 9. Buddha or ‘the enlightened<BR>One,’ by adopting whom the Brāhmans appear to<BR>have desired to effect a compromise between their<BR>own creed and Buddhism; 10. Kalki, which is<BR>yet to come; see these various incarnations s. v.;<BR>some of the Purāṇas multiply these Ava-tāras to the<BR>number of twenty-two or even twenty-four; as the<BR>supreme being Viṣṇu is often identified with Nārā-<BR>yaṇa, the personified Puruṣa or primeval living spirit<BR>[described as moving on the waters, reclining on<BR>Śeṣa, the serpent of infinity, while the god Brahmā<BR>emerges from a lotus growing from his navel; cf.<BR>Manu I. 10]; the wife of Viṣṇu is Lakṣmī or<BR>Śrī, and his paradise is called Vaikuṇṭha; he is<BR>usually represented with a peculiar mark on his breast<BR>called Śrī-vatsa, and as holding a शङ्ख or conch-<BR>shell called Pāñcajanya, a चक्र or quoit-like missile-<BR>weapon called Su-darśana, a गदा or club called Kau-<BR>modakī, and a पद्म or lotus; he has also a bow<BR>called Śārṅga, and a sword called Nandaka; his वाहन<BR>or vehicle is Garuḍa, q. v.; he has a jewel on his<BR>wrist called Syamantaka, another on his breast called<BR>Kaustubha, and the river Ganges is said to issue from<BR>his foot; the demons slain by him in his character of<BR>‘preserver from evil,’ or by Kṛṣṇa as identified<BR>with him, are Madhu, Dhenuka, Cāṇūra, Yamala,<BR>and Arjuna [see यमलार्जुन], Kālanemi, Haya-<BR>grīva, Śakaṭa, Ariṣṭa, Kaiṭabha, Kaṃsa, Keśin,<BR>Mura, Sālva, Mainda, Dvi-vida, Rāhu, Hiraṇya-<BR>kaśipu, Vāṇa, Kāliya, Naraka, Bali; he is wor-<BR>shipped under a thousand names, which are all<BR>enumerated in the Anuśāsana-parvan of the Mahā-<BR>bhārata, II. 6950-7056; for his epithet, ‘younger<BR>brother of Indra,’ see बलि; he is sometimes regarded<BR>as the divinity of the lunar mansion called Śravaṇa;<BR>Viṣṇu Prājāpatya is said to be the author of Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 184); N. of Agni or fire; of one of the<BR>Vasus; of an ancient law-giver or writer of a law-<BR>book; a pure or pious person (= शुद्ध).<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>ऋक्ष, अम्, n. (according to the Śabda-k.) the<BR>Nakṣatra or lunar mansion called Śravaṇa (presided<BR>over by Viṣṇu).<BR>—विष्णु-कन्द, a species of bul-<BR>bous root (= जल-वास, बहु-सम्पुट).<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>कवि, इस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—विष्णु-काञ्ची, f., N. of<BR>a town (said to have been founded by Śaṅkara).<BR>—विष्णु-कान्ती-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—विष्णु-क्रम, अस्, m. the step of Viṣṇu; [cf.<BR>त्रि-विक्रम.]<BR>—विष्णु-क्रान्ता, f. the plant Clitorea<BR>Ternatea (= अ-पराजिता).<BR>—विष्णु-गुप्त, अस्, m.<BR>‘hidden by Viṣṇu,’ N. of the Muni Vātsyāyana;<BR>of the saint Kauṇḍinya (said to have been concealed<BR>by Viṣṇu when pursued by Śiva, whom he had in-<BR>censed); N. of the sage Cāṇakya; of a follower of<BR>Śaṅkarācārya; a species of root (= विष्णु-कन्द).<BR>—विष्णु-गुप्तक, अम्, n. a kind of root (= चा-<BR>णक्य-मूलक).<BR>—विष्णु-गृह, अम्, n. ‘Viṣṇu's<BR>abode,’ N. of a country or city, (also called Stamba-<BR>pura.)<BR>—विष्णु-चक्र, अम्, n. the discus or quoit-<BR>like weapon of Viṣṇu; epithet of a particular mys-<BR>tical circle (formed from the lines in the hand).<BR>—विष्णु-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of an astronomer.<BR>—विष्णु-तत्त्व-निर्णय, अस्, m. ‘investigation or<BR>proof of the essence of Viṣṇu,’ N. of a work.<BR>—विष्णु-तीर्थ, अम्, n. ‘Viṣṇu's Tīrtha,’ N. of<BR>a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—विष्णु-तुल्य-पराक्रम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having power equal to that of Viṣṇu,<BR>—विष्णु-तैल, अम्, n. a kind of medicinal oil (said<BR>to have been fabricated by the Aśvins, = पूरण).<BR>—विष्णु-दत्त, अस्, m. ‘Viṣṇu-given,’ a proper N.<BR>—विष्णु-दत्तक, अस्, m., N. of a scribe.<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>दास, अस्, m. ‘Viṣṇu's slave,’ N. of a Brāhman.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-c" target="_blank">Page0949-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—विष्णु-दैवत, अस्, &c., having Viṣṇu for a<BR>presiding deity.<BR>—विष्णु-दैवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having Viṣṇu for a presiding deity; (आ), f., N. of<BR>the eleventh and twelfth lunar day of each fort-<BR>night.<BR>—विष्णु-धर्म, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>Śrāddha.<BR>—विष्णु-धर्मोत्तर (˚म-उत्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work consisting of a dialogue between<BR>the son of Janam-ejaya and Śaunaka, &c.<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>द्विष्, ट्, m. ‘hating Viṣṇu,’ (with Jainas) an<BR>epithet of nine beings at enmity with Vāsudeva<BR>(= प्रति-वासुदेव).<BR>—विष्णु-पञ्जर, अम्, n.<BR>a kind of mystical prayer or charm for securing<BR>the favour of Viṣṇu, (see पञ्जर.)<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>पद, अम्, n. ‘station or step of Viṣṇu,’ the<BR>meridian sky (Ved. = माध्यन्दिनम् अन्तरि-<BR>क्षम्), the sky, heaven, atmosphere; an image of<BR>the foot of Viṣṇu worshipped at Gayā; the sea of<BR>milk; a lotus; (ई), f., N. of the Ganges (as issuing<BR>from Viṣṇu's foot); one of the twelve Saṅkrāntis<BR>or sun's passages into a sign of the zodiac (especially<BR>the first sign after the equinox).<BR>—विष्णुपद-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha sacred to Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णुपदी-चक्र, अम्, n. a particular astrologi-<BR>cal circle or diagram.<BR>—विष्णुपद्य्-उत्पत्ति, इस्, f.<BR>‘source of the Viṣṇu-padī,’ N. of a chapter in the<BR>Sṛṣṭi-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—विष्णु-पुर,<BR>अम्, n. Viṣṇu's city or abode; (ई), f., N. of a city.<BR>—विष्णु-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of one of the most<BR>celebrated of the eighteen Purāṇas, (this Purāṇa con-<BR>forms more than any other to the definition पञ्च-<BR>लक्षण, q. v.; it is divided into six books, the first<BR>treats of the details of creation, and explains how the<BR>universe proceeded from Pra-kṛti or the eternal germ<BR>of all material things, and how after the world had<BR>been fitted for the reception of living creatures, it was<BR>peopled by the Prajā-patis or patriarchs and their<BR>posterity, who are described as governing the earth<BR>during the Svāyambhuva Manv-antara; the second<BR>continues the kings of this period, and the mention<BR>of Bharata, who gave his name to India, leads to<BR>many curious geographical and astronomical details;<BR>the third treats of the Vedas and other sacred writings,<BR>as well as of caste and the principal Hindū institutions;<BR>the fourth gives a list of dynasties and a kind of his-<BR>torical chronicle mixed with fable; the fifth is entirely<BR>devoted to the life of Kṛṣṇa; the sixth contains an<BR>account of the dissolution of the world and the end<BR>and renovation of all things.)<BR>—विष्णु-प्रीति, इस्,<BR>f. land granted rent-free to Brāhmans in honour of<BR>Viṣṇu or to maintain his worship.<BR>—विष्णु-भक्त,<BR>अस्, m. a worshipper of Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णु-भक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. the worship of Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णु-भक्ति-चन्-<BR>द्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>भक्ति-रहस्य, अम्, n. ‘mystery of the worship of<BR>Viṣṇu,’ N. of a work.<BR>—विष्णु-भट्ट, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a scribe.<BR>—विष्णु-मन्दिर, अम्, n. Viṣṇu's<BR>temple; = विष्णु-गृह, q. v.<BR>—विष्णु-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, emanated from Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णु-माया, f.<BR>‘Viṣṇu's illusion,’ N. of Durgā.<BR>—विष्णु-माहात्-<BR>म्य, अम्, n. ‘the glory or majesty of Viṣṇu,’ N.<BR>of a chapter of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR>—विष्णु-मित्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a priest; of the author of a Prāti-<BR>śākhya commentary (with the surname Kumāra).<BR>—विष्णु-यशस्, आस्, m., N. of the son of Brahma-<BR>yaśas and father of Kalki.<BR>—विष्णु-यामल-तन्त्र,<BR>N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—विष्णु-रथ, अस्, m. ‘Vish-<BR>ṇu's chariot,’ N. of Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णु-रहस्य, अम्, n. ‘mystical doc-<BR>trine of Viṣṇu,’ N. of a work.<BR>—विष्णु-रात, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Viṣṇu-given,’ N. of king Parīkṣit.<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>लिङ्गी, f. a quail.<BR>—विष्णु-लोक, अस्, m. Viṣṇu's<BR>world; = ब्रह्म-लोक (according to some accounts;<BR>or placed above it, according to others).<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, आ, अम्, beloved by Viṣṇu; (आ), f.<BR>the plant Echites Caryophyllata; a small fragrant<BR>shrub, Ocymum Sanctum; an epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—विष्णु-वाजपेयिन्, ई, m., N. of an author.<BR>—विष्णु-वाहन or विष्णु-राह्य, अस्, m. ‘Vish-<BR>ṇu's vehicle,’ epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—विष्णु-शर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a leader of the sect of Bhaktas; of the<BR>author of the Pañca-tantra; of a scribe.<BR>—विष्णु-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">Page0950-a+ 73</a>]<BR>सरस्-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha sacred to<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णु-सहस्र-नाम-कथन, अम्, n.<BR>‘enumeration of the thousand names of Viṣṇu,’ N.<BR>of a small portion of the Ānuśāsanika section of the<BR>Anuśāsana-parvan (ll. 6936-7078) of the Mahā-<BR>bhārata.<BR>—विष्णु-सहस्र-नाम-भाष्य, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a commentary by Śaṅkarācārya on the<BR>thousand names of Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णु-सिंह, अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—विष्णु-सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of a Vedic<BR>hymn.<BR>—विष्णु-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of the original<BR>teacher of the Vaiṣṇava sect of the Rudra-sampradā-<BR>yins, (he was the predecessor of a more celebrated<BR>teacher called Vallabhācārya, q. v.); a temple or<BR>statue built in honour of Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णूत्तर (˚णु-<BR>उत्˚), a grant of land rent-free for the worship of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्णूत्सव (˚णु-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘Viṣṇu's<BR>festival,’ a particular day sacred to Viṣṇu.<BR>—विष्ण्व्-<BR>अवतार, अस्, m. a descent or incarnation of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णूय
विष्णूय, Nom. P. विष्णूयति, &c., to treat as<BR>Viṣṇu, act towards any one (loc.) as Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पन्द्|विष्पंद्
विष्पन्द् वि-ष्पन्द् (वि-स्पन्द्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-ष्पन्दते, -ष्पन्दितुम्, to throb, beat; to<BR>struggle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पन्द|विष्पंद|विष्पंदः|विष्पन्दः
वि-ष्पन्द, अस्, m. throbbing, beating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पर्धस्
विष्पर्धस् वि-ष्पर्धस् (वि-स्पर्दस्), आस्, आस्,<BR>अस् [cf. वि-स्पर्ध्], Ved. emulating, envious, (Sāy.<BR>वि-स्पर्धसः = विविध-स्पर्धाः, Ṛg-veda V.<BR>87, 4); free from emulation or rivalry, (Sāy. = वि-<BR>गत-स्पर्ध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पश्
विष्पश् वि-ष्पश् (वि-स्पश्), ट्, m., Ved. one<BR>who frees from obstruction, a deliverer; an especial<BR>adversary, (Sāy. = विशेषेण बाधक, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>189, 6; cf. वि-स्पष्ट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पित
विष्पित वि-ष्पित, अस्, m. (probably con-<BR>nected with rts. पी, प्यै, स्फाय्), Ved. (according to<BR>some) a desert; expanse, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda VII. 60, 7. विष्पितस्य = व्याप्तितस्य कर्-<BR>मणः; according to Durga = विस्तीर्ण = इतश्-<BR>चेतश्-च सर्वतः प्राप्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पुलिङ्गक
विष्पुलिङ्गक वि-ष्पुलिङ्गक, अस्, m. (or आ,<BR>f. ?), Ved. a spark of fire (= वि-स्फुलिङ्ग, q. v.;<BR>this word occurs in Ṛg-veda I. 191, 12, where,<BR>according to Sāy., it may mean one of the twenty-<BR>one sparks produced by a multiplication of the seven<BR>tongues of fire or may be a synonym of चटिका, a<BR>female sparrow, of which there are twenty-one vari-<BR>eties, eaters of poison with impunity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्फार|विष्फारः
विष्फार वि-ष्फार, अस्, m. (fr. वि-ष्फर्<BR>= वि-ष्फुर् below), vibrating; the twang of a bow,<BR>&c. See वि-स्फार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्फुर्
विष्फुर् वि-ष्फुर्, cl. 6. P. -ष्फुरति, &c.<BR>See वि-स्फुर्, which is an alternative form according<BR>to Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्फुरत्
वि-ष्फुरत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, Ved. = वि-<BR>स्फुरत्, quivering; injuring, harassing, (Sāy. = वि-<BR>हिंसत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्फुल्
विष्फुल् वि-ष्फुल् = वि-स्फुल्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्य|विष्यः
विष्य विष्य. See p. 946, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यत्
विष्यत् वि-ष्यत्. See under वि-षो, p. 948.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्द्|विष्यंद्
विष्यन्द् वि-ष्यन्द् (also written वि-स्यन्द्;<BR>according to Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 72. वि-स्यन्द् is the only<BR>form allowed when the verb is used with reference<BR>to living beings), cl. 1. A. -ष्यन्दते or -स्यन्दते,<BR>&c. (see rt. स्यन्द्), to flow out or away, flow off,<BR>trickle down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्द|विष्यंदः|विष्यन्दः
वि-ष्यन्द, अस्, m. flowing, trickling, issuing<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्दमान
वि-ष्यन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, flowing, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्व|विष्वः
विष्व विष्व, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>2. विष्), injurious, hurtful, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वञ्च्|विष्वंच्
विष्वञ्च् विष्व्-अञ्च्, विष्वक्-षेण, &c. See<BR>under विषु, p. 948.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वन्
विष्वन् वि-ष्वन् (वि-स्वन्), cl. 1. P. -ष्वणति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">Page0950-b+ 75</a>]<BR>-ष्वणितुम् (Impf. व्य्-अष्वणत्, Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 63),<BR>to make a sound in eating, smack the lips (restricted<BR>to this sense according to Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 69; if any<BR>other sound is denoted, the dental स् remains, see वि-<BR>स्वन्, cf. अव-ष्वन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वणन|विष्वणनं
वि-ष्वणन, अम्, n. smacking the lips in eating,<BR>eating with a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वाण|विष्वाणः
वि-ष्वाण, अस्, m. eating with a noise, noisy<BR>eating; [cf. अव-ष्वाण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्
विस् विस् (connected with rts. बिस्, पिस्,<BR>&c.), cl. 1. P. वेसति, (if identified with<BR>rt. बिस्, then cl. 4. P. विस्यति), वेसितुम्, to go, move;<BR>to cast, throw, send (cl. 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस|विसं
विस, अम्, n. (in Ved. more usually बिस, q. v., cf.<BR>विश), the film or fibre of the water-lily or lotus, the<BR>fibres of the stalk or the stalk itself.<BR>—विस-कण्ठिका,<BR>f. or विस-कण्ठिन्, ई, m. a small crane.<BR>—विस-<BR>कुसुम, अम्, n. ‘fibre-(produced) flower,’ a lotus-<BR>flower.<BR>—विस-खादिका, f. ‘the eating of fibres or<BR>shoots,’ N. of a play mentioned in Vātsyāyana's<BR>Kāma-sūtra.<BR>—विस-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. a knot on the<BR>stalk of the lotus (used for filtering or clearing water);<BR>a particular disease of the eyes.<BR>—विस-च्छेद, अस्,<BR>m. a cutting or portion of the fibres of the lotus.<BR>—विस-ज, अम्, n. ‘fibre-produced,’ a lotus-flower,<BR>lotus.<BR>—विस-तन्तु, उस्, m. a lotus fibre.<BR>—विस-ना-<BR>भि, इस्, m. a quantity of lotuses; the plant Nelum-<BR>bium Speciosum (= पद्मिनी).<BR>—विस-नासिका, f.<BR>‘having a nose like a lotus-stalk,’ a sort of crane.<BR>—विस-पुष्प, अम्, n. a lotus-flower.<BR>—विस-प्र-<BR>सून, अम्, n. a lotus-flower, lotus (Nelumbium Spe-<BR>ciosum).<BR>—विस-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. a particular disease<BR>of the eyelid.<BR>—विसाकर (˚स-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘abound-<BR>ing in fibres,’ a species of Euphorbia (= भद्र-<BR>चूड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसल|विसलं
विसल, अम्, n. a sprout, bud, young shoot; [cf.<BR>किसल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसिनी
विसिनी, f. an assemblage of lotus-flowers; the lotus<BR>plant Nelumbium Speciosum; lotus fibres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसिल
विसिल, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or relating to<BR>Visa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंयुक्त
विसंयुक्त वि-संयुक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. युज्<BR>with सम् and वि), disjoined, detached, separate,<BR>abstaining from, keeping aloof from, omitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंयोग|विसंयोगः
वि-संयोग, अस्, m. disjunction, separation, omis-<BR>sion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवद्
विसंवद् वि-सं-वद्, cl. 1. P. -वदति, -व-<BR>दितुम्, to assert falsely; to fail in an agreement,<BR>break one's word, break a promise, to disappoint,<BR>deceive; to contradict, raise objections, disagree with,<BR>murmur against: Caus. -वादयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>disappointed, disappoint; to fail to prove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवाद|विसंवादः
वि-संवाद, अस्, m. false assertion, breaking or<BR>falsifying one's word, deceiving by a false assertion,<BR>breaking a promise, disappointing, deceiving; con-<BR>tradiction, disagreeing, disagreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवादित
वि-संवादित, अस्, आ, अम्, disappointed, deceived,<BR>contradicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवादिन्
विसंवादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, breaking one's word, dis-<BR>appointing, deceiving; cunning, crafty, fraudulent;<BR>contradicting, disagreeing; disputing, contesting,<BR>contentious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंशयम्
विसंशयम् वि-संशयम्, ind. without doubt,<BR>without suspicion, undoubtedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंष्ठुल
विसंष्ठुल वि-संष्ठुल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>स्था with सम् and वि; cf. अप-ष्ठु, अप-ष्ठुल,<BR>p. 53, col. 2), unsteady, agitated.<BR>—विसंष्ठुल-<BR>गमन, अस्, आ, अम्, going unsteadily, tottering,<BR>staggering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसङ्कट|विसंकट|विसंकटः|विसङ्कटः
विसङ्कट वि-सङ्कट, अस्, m. a lion; the<BR>Ingudī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसङ्गत|विसंगत
विसङ्गत वि-सङ्गत, अस्, आ, अम्, uncon-<BR>nected, inconsistent, not in harmony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसञ्ज्ञ|विसंज्ञ
विसञ्ज्ञ वि-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, insensible,<BR>unconscious; bereft of sense, lifeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसन्नाह|विसंनाह
विसन्नाह वि-सन्नाह, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>coat of mail; without clothes, unclothed, naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसम्मुह्
विसम्मुह् वि-सम्-मुह्, cl. 4. P. -मुह्यति,<BR>-मोहितुम् or -मोग्धुम् or -मोढुम्, to be utterly<BR>bewildered or infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसम्मूढ|विसंमूढ
वि-सम्मूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, utterly bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर|विसरः
विसर वि-सर, वि-सार, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ग|विसर्गः
विसर्ग वि-सर्ग, वि-सर्जन, &c. See under<BR>वि-सृज् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसल|विसलं
विसल विसल. See under rt. विस्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसामग्री
विसामग्री वि-सामग्री, f. the absence of<BR>means, the absence of causes calculated to produce<BR>an effect (in phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसि
विसि वि-सि. See under वि-षि, (according to<BR>Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 70. the participle must be वि-षित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूचन
विसूचन वि-सूचन, अम्, n. making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूचिका
वि-सूचिका, f. (rt. सूच्), symptom of disease; spas-<BR>modic cholera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरण|विसूरणं
विसूरण वि-सूरण, अम्, आ, n. f. (fr. rt. सूर्<BR>with वि), sorrow, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरित|विसूरितं
वि-सूरित, अम्, n. repentance; (आ), f. a fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृ
विसृ वि-सृ, cl. 1. 3. P. -सरति, -सिसर्ति<BR>(Ved. also A. -ते), -सर्तुम्, to go forth or in various<BR>directions, spread out, stretch out, unfold, display<BR>(Ved.), to be spread out, be extended, extend, spread<BR>through, stretch; to return: Pass. -स्रियते, to be<BR>spread out, (Perf. वि-सस्रे, it was spread abroad):<BR>Caus. -सारयति, -यितुम्, to stretch forth, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर|विसरः
वि-सर, अस्, m. going forth or abroad; going;<BR>spreading, extending; a multitude, crowd, assemblage,<BR>flock, herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसरण
वि-सरण, अम्, n. the act of going forth or out,<BR>spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसार|विसारः
वि-सार, अस्, m. going out or forth, spreading out,<BR>expansion, diffusion; flowing, creeping, sliding, glid-<BR>ing along; a fish; (अम्), n. a wood; timber; (ई),<BR>f. the region of the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसारित|विसारितः
वि-सारित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to go forth or spread,<BR>set on foot, occasioned; effected, performed.<BR>—वि-<BR>सारिताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having an expanded<BR>or extended body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसारिन्
वि-सारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going forth or in all directions,<BR>spreading over or through, spreading, diffusing;<BR>creeping along; flowing, gliding; (ई), m. a fish;<BR>(इणी), f. a kind of shrub (= माष-पर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसार्य
वि-सार्य, ind. having spread out, having extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृत|विसृतं
वि-सृत, अस्, आ, अम्, spread out, extended, ex-<BR>panded, drawn (as a bow-string); uttered.<BR>—विसृत-<BR>गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, having the string (of a bow &c.)<BR>stretched out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृत्वर|विसृत्वरः
वि-सृत्वर, अस्, ई, अम्, spreading about, becoming<BR>diffused; gliding along, creeping, flowing, sliding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृमर|विसृमरः
वि-सृमर, अस्, आ, अम्, creeping along, moving<BR>onwards gently, flowing, gliding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृज्
विसृज् वि-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति (ep. also<BR>A. -ते), -स्रष्टुम्, to send forth, let go, emit, let<BR>loose, pour forth; to create, produce; to let fall,<BR>drop, shed; to cast, hurl, throw, discharge, throw<BR>away; to emit sound, utter, sound forth; to send<BR>away, dismiss, abandon, cast off, repudiate, reject;<BR>to bestow, give, grant; to deliver, hand over to:<BR>Caus. -सर्जयति, -यितुम्, to send forth, emit, pour<BR>forth, shed; to send away, dismiss; to spare; to repel,<BR>repudiate, get rid of; to reject, put off; to lose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ग|विसर्गः
वि-सर्ग, अस्, m. sending forth, letting go, emis-<BR>sion, letting loose; creating, creation; emanation;<BR>voiding, evacuation (of excrement &c.); getting rid<BR>of, sending away, dismissal, abandonment, rejection,<BR>relinquishment; giving away, gift, donation; de-<BR>parture; separation; final emancipation, beatitude,<BR>exemption from worldly existence; the sun's southern<BR>course; light, lustre, splendor; (in grammar) N. of a<BR>symbol usually marked by two perpendicular dots [:]<BR>representing a hard and distinctly audible aspiration,<BR>(it usually, though not always, occurs at the end of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">Page0951-a+ 78</a>]<BR>word, and is really a kind of sibilant, often taking the<BR>place of final स् and र् when these letters pass into<BR>aspirations; it must be preceded by a vowel, but<BR>cannot be followed by one; it is called Visarga either<BR>from its liability to be rejected or from its being<BR>pronounced with a full emission of breath.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0950-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जन|विसर्जनं|विसर्ज्जनं
वि-सर्जन, अम्, n. the act of sending forth,<BR>emitting, letting loose, sending among, dismissing,<BR>dispatching, dismissal; setting a bull at liberty on<BR>particular occasions; throwing the image of a deity<BR>into holy water (as the concluding rite of a festival);<BR>abandoning, relinquishing, quitting, abandonment,<BR>giving up; giving away, gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जनीय|विसर्जनीयः|विसर्ज्जनीय
वि-सर्जनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sent forth or<BR>emitted; to be abandoned or left, to be given away,<BR>&c.; proper or fit to be abandoned; (अस्), m. = Vi-<BR>sarga (in grammar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जयित्वा
वि-सर्जयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having let go,<BR>having dismissed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जित|विसर्ज्जित
वि-सर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, sent forth, let go, emitted,<BR>sent away, dismissed; abandoned, left; given away,<BR>given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृजत्
वि-सृजत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, letting go, sending<BR>forth, emitting, abandoning; giving away, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृज्य
1. वि-सृज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be let go, to be aban-<BR>doned, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृज्य
2. वि-सृज्य, ind. having let go, having sent away<BR>or dismissed, having discharged, having got rid of,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृष्ट|विसृष्टः
वि-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, let go, sent forth, emitted,<BR>emanated, created; let fall, shed; sent away, dis-<BR>missed, discharged; shot off; cast off, abandoned,<BR>relinquished, parted with; got rid of, cast out, ex-<BR>pelled; given away, bestowed, granted.<BR>—विसृष्ट-<BR>भूमि, इस्, इस्, इ, having space or room given, one<BR>who is allowed room (to sit down &c.).<BR>—विसृष्ट-<BR>राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. munificent in gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृष्टि|विसृष्टिः
वि-सृष्टि, इस्, f. letting go, sending forth, emana-<BR>tion, creation; dismissing, abandonment, leaving,<BR>quitting; giving, offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृप्
विसृप् वि-सृप्, cl. 1. P. -सर्पति, -सर्प्तुम्<BR>or -स्रप्तुम् (Ved. Inf. वि-सृपस्), to creep away or<BR>about, go or run away, sneak off, roam about,<BR>escape; to fly about, glide, soar, hover about; to<BR>flow over (with acc.); to spread about, become dif-<BR>fused; to wander, wind, meander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्प|विसर्पः
वि-सर्प, अस्, m. creeping about; flying to and<BR>fro, gliding; going or spreading about; an unwished<BR>for consequence of any act; a particular disease,<BR>erysipelatous inflammation, a sort of dry spreading<BR>itch.<BR>—विसर्प-घ्न, अम्, n. bee's-wax (as destroy-<BR>ing the above disease?).<BR>—विसर्प-चिकित्सा, f. the<BR>cure of the above disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पण|विसर्पणं
वि-सर्पण, अम्, n. the act of creeping or going<BR>about; soaring, gliding, flying, going gently; spread-<BR>ing, extending, diffusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पत्
वि-सर्पत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, creeping about, going<BR>along; flying gently, gliding, soaring, hovering<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पमाण
वि-सर्पमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, creeping about, flying<BR>or hovering about; wandering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पि|विसर्पिः
विसर्पि, इस्, m. a cutaneous disease (= वि-सर्प<BR>above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पिका
वि-सर्पिका, f. a sort of dry spreading itch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पिन्
वि-सर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, creeping about; gliding, going<BR>gently; spreading over or along; winding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्द्
विस्कन्द् वि-स्कन्द्. See वि-ष्कन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्त्तृ
वि-स्कन्त्तृ, वि-स्कन्द. See under वि-ष्कन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्न
वि-स्कन्न. See under वि-ष्कन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कम्भ्
विस्कम्भ् वि-स्कम्भ्, according to Pāṇ.<BR>VIII. 3, 77. the स् is retained only in A.; see वि-<BR>ष्कम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्त|विस्तः
विस्त विस्त, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. विस्), a weight of gold (= eighty Raktikās or a<BR>Karṣa of sixteen Māṣas, about half an ounce troy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृ
विस्तृ वि-स्तृ, cl. 5. or वि-स्तॄ, cl. 9. P. A.<BR>-स्तृणोति, -स्तृणुते, -स्तृणाति, -स्तृणीते, -स्तर्तुम्<BR>or -स्तरितुम् or -स्तरीतुम्, to spread out, spread<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">Page0951-b+ 77</a>]<BR>abroad, diffuse, extend, expand; to spread or strew<BR>or scatter about: Pass. -स्तर्यते or -स्तीर्यते, to be<BR>spread abroad or widely diffused: Caus. -स्तारयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to extend, expand, make broad or wide,<BR>widen, broaden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तर|विस्तरः
वि-स्तर, अस्, m. [cf. वि-ष्टर], spreading, ex-<BR>tension, expansion, prolixity, diffuseness, detailed<BR>description, minute detail; affectionate solicitation;<BR>anything spread out, a layer, bed; a seat, a stool;<BR>abundance, quantity, multitude, number, assemblage,<BR>a large company; (एण), ind. diffusely, at length,<BR>fully, in detail.<BR>—विस्तर-तस् or विस्तर-शस्, ind.<BR>diffusely, at length, fully, in detail, with full parti-<BR>culars.<BR>—विस्तर-ता, f. expansion, spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तरणीय
वि-स्तरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spread or ex-<BR>tended, capable of being extended or expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तार|विस्तारः
वि-स्तार, अस्, m. spreading, expansion, extension,<BR>diffusion; breadth, amplitude; vastness, expanse;<BR>particularising at length, detail, amplification; the<BR>breadth or diameter of a circle; the branch of a tree<BR>with its new shoots; a shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तारण
वि-स्तारण, अम्, n. the act of spreading or extend-<BR>ing or enlarging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तारित
वि-स्तारित, अस्, आ, अम्, spread, extended, enlarged,<BR>expanded; fully stated, amplified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तारिन्
वि-स्तारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, extending, large; powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्ण|विस्तीर्णः
वि-स्तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, spread about, strewed about,<BR>strewed, spread out, extended, spread, expanded;<BR>broad; large, great, roomy, wide.<BR>—विस्तीर्ण-ता, f.<BR>or विस्तीर्ण-त्व, अम्, n. breadth, diffusion, extension,<BR>vastness, largeness, amplitude.<BR>—विस्तीर्ण-पर्ण,<BR>अम्, n. a sort of esculent root, Arum Indicum (=<BR>मानक).<BR>—विस्तीर्णोरःस्थल (˚ण-उर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a broad chest or breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्य
वि-स्तीर्य, ind. having spread or diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृत|विस्तृतः
वि-स्तृत, अस्, आ, अम्, diffused, extended, spread;<BR>diffuse; expanded, broad; ample.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृति|विस्तृतिः
वि-स्तृति, इस्, f. spreading, expansion; extent,<BR>width, breadth; the diameter of a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्थान
विस्थान वि-स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, (in Vedic<BR>grammar) belonging to another place or order of<BR>letters (e. g. वि-स्थाने स्पर्श उदये म-कारः,<BR>the letter म्, when a consonant of any other class<BR>follows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पन्द्
विस्पन्द् वि-स्पन्द्. See वि-ष्पन्द्, p. 950.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पर्ध्
विस्पर्ध् वि-स्पर्ध्, cl. 1. A. -स्पर्धते,<BR>-स्पर्धितुम्, to vie with, emulate, envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पर्धमान
वि-स्पर्धमान, अस्, आ, अम्, vying with, emu-<BR>lating, envying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पर्धा
वि-स्पर्धा, f. absence of envy; [cf. वि-ष्पर्-<BR>धस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पष्ट|विस्पष्टः
विस्पष्ट वि-स्पष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (see rt. स्पश्;<BR>cf. वि-ष्पश्), clear, apparent, manifest, evident, dis-<BR>tinct, open; plain, intelligible; (अम्), ind. clearly,<BR>evidently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फर्
विस्फर् वि-स्फर्. See under वि-स्फुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार|विस्फारः
वि-स्फार, वि-स्फारित, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुर्
विस्फुर् वि-स्फुर् (also written वि-ष्फुर्,<BR>q. v.; the base is changed to वि-स्फर् in the Caus.<BR>and in some derivatives, e. g. वि-स्फार), cl. 6. P.<BR>-स्फुरति, &c., -स्फुरितुम्, to quiver, tremble,<BR>throb, vibrate, flash, flicker, glitter; to struggle<BR>against, resist: Pass. -स्फुर्यते (Perf. वि-पुस्फुरे,<BR>Kirāt. XIV. 30), to be flashed: Caus. -स्फारयति,<BR>-स्फोरयति, -यितुम्, to cause to tremble, make to<BR>quiver or vibrate, draw (a bow); to make to glitter<BR>or flash, cause to shine: Pass. of Caus. -स्फार्यते,<BR>to be made to quiver or vibrate (as a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार|विस्फारः
वि-स्फार, अस्, m. (also written वि-ष्फार),<BR>trembling, quivering, vibrating, agitating; the twang<BR>of a bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फारयत्
वि-स्फारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to tremble or<BR>vibrate, drawing (a bow), drawing to the full stretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फारित|विस्फारितः
वि-स्फारित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to vibrate or trem-<BR>ble; twanged or drawn (as a bow-string); shaken;<BR>trembling, tremulous, flashing; made open, displayed,<BR>manifested, evident, apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार्यमाण|विस्फार्य्यमाण
वि-स्फार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being drawn or<BR>twanged (as a bow-string); being made open or<BR>manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुरत्
वि-स्फुरत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, quivering, throb-<BR>bing, trembling; swelling, enlarging; struggling,<BR>resisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुरमाण
वि-स्फुरमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, quivering, throbbing,<BR>trembling.<BR>—विस्फुरमाणौष्ठ (˚ण-ओष्˚), अस्,<BR>आ or ई, अम्, having quivering or trembling lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुरित|विस्फुरितः
वि-स्फुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, quivering, shaken, tre-<BR>mulous; swollen, enlarged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुर्य
वि-स्फुर्य, ind. (Mahā-bh. Vana-parvan 15639.<BR>वि-स्फूर्य), having trembled or quivered, quivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुर्ज्
विस्फुर्ज् वि-स्फुर्ज्, cl. 1. P. -स्फूर्जति,<BR>-स्फूर्जितुम्, to roar, resound, thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फूर्जथु|विस्फूर्जथुः
वि-स्फूर्जथु, उस्, m. roaring, resounding, thun-<BR>dering, rumbling; a clap of thunder; rolling.<BR>—वि-<BR>स्फूर्जथु-प्रख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, like or resembling<BR>a clap of thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फूर्जित|विस्फूर्जितं
वि-स्फूर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, resounded, resounding;<BR>(अम्), n. roar, shout; rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुल्
विस्फुल् वि-स्फुल् (also written वि-ष्फुल्,<BR>Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 76; connected with वि-स्फुर्, col. 2),<BR>cl. 6. P. -स्फुलति, -स्फुलितुम्, to quiver; to leap<BR>about, jump for joy, go (merrily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलत्
वि-स्फुलत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, trembling, shaking,<BR>quivering; going briskly or (merrily); appearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलिङ्ग|विस्फुलिंग|विस्फुलिंगः|विस्फुलिङ्गः
वि-स्फुलिङ्ग, अस्, m. a spark of fire; a sort of<BR>poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फोट|विस्फोटः
विस्फोट वि-स्फोट, अस्, आ, m. f. a boil,<BR>tumour, pustule; small-pox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मि
विस्मि वि-स्मि, cl. 1. A. -स्मयते (some-<BR>times also P. -स्मयति), -स्मेतुम्, to wonder, be sur-<BR>prised; to wonder at, be surprised at (with inst., loc.,<BR>or acc.); to admire; to be proud of (with inst.):<BR>Caus. -स्माययति, -स्मापयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to wonder; to astonish any one (acc.) with<BR>anything (inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मय|विस्मयः
वि-स्मय, अस्, m. wonder, surprise, amazement,<BR>astonishment, admiration; dismay; pride, arrogance;<BR>doubt, uncertainty, perplexity; (in the drama) one<BR>of the Bhāvas.<BR>—विस्मय-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>causing astonishment or admiration.<BR>—विस्मयङ्-<BR>गम, अस्, आ, अम्, being an object of astonishment,<BR>astonishing.<BR>—विस्मय-हर्ष-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>caused by astonishment and joy.<BR>—विस्मयाकुल<BR>(˚य-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bewildered with wonder,<BR>amazed, astounded.<BR>—विस्मयान्वित (˚य-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, filled with wonder, astonished, surprised.<BR>—विस्मयाविष्ट (˚य-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, filled with<BR>astonishment or wonder.<BR>—विस्मयोत्फुल्ल-नयन<BR>or विस्मयोत्फुल्ल-लोचन (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing eyes wide open or staring with astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयत्
वि-स्मयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wondering, admiring,<BR>being surprised, being dismayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयिन्
विस्मयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, astonished, surprised, amazed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मापन|विस्मापनः
वि-स्मापन, अम्, n. the act of causing wonder<BR>or surprise, exciting astonishment; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>astonishing, surprising; (अस्), m. illusion, deceit; a<BR>city of the Gandharvas (a kind of magical or en-<BR>chanted city that appears and disappears unexpect-<BR>edly); an epithet of Kāma (god of love).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मित|विस्मितः
वि-स्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, astonished, surprised, amazed,<BR>wonderstruck, astounded, dismayed, disconcerted, per-<BR>plexed; (आ, अम्), f. n. a species of the Ati-dhṛti<BR>metre (= मेघ-विस्फूर्जित).<BR>—विस्मित-मानस,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, surprised or perplexed in mind.<BR>—विस्मि-<BR>तानन (˚त-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a surprised<BR>face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मिति|विस्मितिः
वि-स्मिति, इस्, f. astonishment, wonder, surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मेर
वि-स्मेर, अस्, आ, अम्, wondering, astonished, sur-<BR>prised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृ
विस्मृ वि-स्मृ, cl. 1. P. -स्मरति (ep. also<BR>A. -ते), -स्मर्तुम्, to forget, be unmindful of, lose<BR>the remembrance of (with acc. or gen.): Pass.<BR>-स्मर्यते, Aor. व्य्-अस्मारि, to be forgotten: Caus.<BR>-स्मारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0951-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरण|विस्मरणं
वि-स्मरण, अम्, n. the act of forgetting, ob-<BR>livion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरणीय
वि-स्मरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be forgotten; worthy<BR>of being forgotten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरत्
वि-स्मरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, forgetting, losing the<BR>remembrance of, unmindful of (anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मर्य|विस्मर्य्य
वि-स्मर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be forgotten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृत|विस्मृतः
वि-स्मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, forgotten, passed out of the<BR>memory or recollection.<BR>—विस्मृत-पूर्व-संस्का-<BR>र, अस्, आ, अम्, forgetting a former promise or reso-<BR>lution.<BR>—विस्मृत-संस्कार, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>forgets an agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृति|विस्मृतिः
वि-स्मृति, इस्, f. forgetting, forgetfulness, loss of<BR>memory, oblivion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृत्य
वि-स्मृत्य, ind. having forgotten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्यन्द्
विस्यन्द् वि-स्यन्द्. See वि-ष्यन्द्, p. 950.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्यन्द
वि-स्यन्द, &c. See वि-ष्यन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्र|विस्रं
विस्र विस्र, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. विस्),<BR>a smell like that of raw meat; (आ), f. a particular<BR>substance smelling like raw meat (= हपुषा).<BR>—विस्र-गन्धि, इस्, m. ‘smelling like raw meat,’<BR>yellow orpiment.<BR>—विस्र-ता, f. or विस्र-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>rawness of smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंस्
विस्रंस् वि-स्रंस्, cl. 1. A. -स्रंसते, -स्रं-<BR>सितुम्, to fall asunder, fall down, drop; slip off:<BR>Caus. -स्रंसयति, -यितुम्, to cause to drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंस|विस्रंसः
वि-स्रंस, अस्, आ, m. f. falling down, falling asun-<BR>der, relaxation, laxness, weakness, debility, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंसन
वि-स्रंसन, अम्, n. the act of falling; flowing,<BR>dropping; loosening, unfastening, untying; a laxative,<BR>aperient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रस्
वि-स्रस्, Ved. = वि-स्रस्त below (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 48, 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रसा
वि-स्रसा, f. decay, decrepitude, weakness, the in-<BR>firmity of old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रस्त
वि-स्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen down, loosened,<BR>detached; infirm, weak.<BR>—विस्रस्त-हार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the necklace slipped off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भ्
विस्रम्भ् वि-स्रम्भ् = वि-श्रम्भ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रब्ध|विस्रब्धः
वि-स्रब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, trusted, confided in;<BR>steady, diligent; tame, humble, placid, &c. (See<BR>वि-श्रब्ध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भ|विस्रंभ|विस्रम्भः
वि-स्रम्भ, अस्, m. trust, confidence; affection,<BR>regard, affectionate solicitation; acquaintance; kill-<BR>ing, &c. (See वि-श्रम्भ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भिन्
वि-स्रम्भिन्, ई, इणी, इ, trusting, confiding in, &c.<BR>(See वि-श्रम्भिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रस्
विस्रस् वि-स्रस्. See under वि-स्रंस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रु
विस्रु वि-स्रु, cl. 1. P. -स्रवति, -स्रोतुम्, to<BR>flow forth or away, flow, stream, trickle, ooze: Caus.<BR>-स्रावयति, -यितुम्, to cause to flow forth (as blood<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्राव|विस्रावः
वि-स्राव, अस्, m. flowing forth, dropping, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावण|विस्रावणं
वि-स्रावण, अम्, n. the act of causing to flow out;<BR>bleeding; distilling; a spirit distilled from molasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावणीय
वि-स्रावणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, = वि-स्राव्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावित
वि-स्रावित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to flow out; bled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावितव्य
वि-स्रावितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = वि-स्राव्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्राव्य
वि-स्राव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made to flow; to be<BR>bled, requiring bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रुत|विस्रुतः
वि-स्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, flowed forth, flowed, dropped,<BR>flowing; spread, diffused, stretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रुति|विस्रुतिः
वि-स्रुति, इस्, f. flowing forth, oozing, flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रुह्
विस्रुह् वि-स्रुह्, f. (fr. rt. 1. रुह् or स्रु with<BR>वि-स्), Ved. a stream, river, (Sāy. विस्रुहः = नद्यः,<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 7, 6); a plant, (perhaps वि-स्रुहा;<BR>according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda V. 44, 3. विस्रुहा =<BR>विस्रुहाणाम् = ओषधीनाम्, ‘of plants;’ cf. वीरुध्,<BR>वीरुधा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वन्
विस्वन् वि-स्वन्, cl. 1. P. -स्वनति, -स्वनि-<BR>तुम्, to sound forth, sound, (but see वि-ष्वन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वर|विस्वरः
विस्वर वि-स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, discordant, un-<BR>harmonious, unmusical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वाद
विस्वाद वि-स्वाद, अस्, आ, अम्, tasteless,<BR>flavourless, insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहग|विहगः
विहग विह-ग, विहङ्-ग, &c. See वि-ह<BR>under 1. वि-हा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहन्
विहन् वि-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति (ep. even cl.<BR>4. P. -हन्यति), -हन्तुम्, to strike apart, separate;<BR>to strike down, strike violently, strike; to destroy<BR>utterly, kill, destroy; to afflict; to oppose, impede,<BR>resist; to strike back, reject, refuse, deny; to hinder,<BR>interrupt, obstruct: Caus. -घातयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to be killed or destroyed; to afflict, drive into<BR>straits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहत्
वि-हत्, f. a cow that miscarries from unseasonable<BR>gestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहत|विहतः
वि-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck, killed, completely<BR>destroyed; hurt; opposed, impeded, resisted; (अस्),<BR>m. a Buddhist or Jaina temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहति|विहतिः
वि-हति, इस्, f. striking, killing; defeat; failure;<BR>(इस्), m. a friend, companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहनन|विहननं
वि-हनन, अम्, n. the act of striking; killing<BR>outright; hurting, injury; opposition, obstruction,<BR>impediment; a bow for cleaning cotton; [cf. तूल-<BR>कार्मुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर|विहरः
विहर वि-हर, &c. See under वि-हृ,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर्ष|विहर्षः
विहर्ष वि-हर्ष, अस्, m. excessive joy or<BR>gladness, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहव
विहव वि-हव. See under वि-ह्वे, p. 953.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहव्य
विहव्य वि-हव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be<BR>offered; (अस्), m., N. of a descendant of Aṅgiras<BR>(author of Ṛg-veda X. 128).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्
विहस् वि-हस्, cl. 1. P. -हसति, -हसितुम्,<BR>to laugh gently, smile, laugh; to laugh at (with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसत्
वि-हसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, laughing, smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसन|विहसनं
वि-हसन, अम्, n. laughing gently, smiling (=<BR>मध्यम-हास्य), laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसित|विहसितं
वि-हसित, अस्, आ, अम्, smiled, laughed; smiled<BR>at; (अम्), n. a gentle laugh, smile, laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्य
वि-हस्य, ind. having smiled; laughing at, ridi-<BR>culing, contemning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्यमान
वि-हस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being laughed at,<BR>being smiled upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहास|विहासः
वि-हास, अस्, m. a gentle laugh, smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्त|विहस्तः
विहस्त वि-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, handless, help-<BR>less; confounded, perplexed, bewildered; wise,<BR>learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
विहा 1. वि-हा, cl. 3. A. -जिहीते, &c., Ved.<BR>to go apart, (Sāy. वि-जिहीष्व = वि-गच्छ, Ṛg-<BR>veda V. 78, 5), become expanded, open, gape open<BR>(Lat. dehisco, Gr. χαίνω).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह
वि-ह (for 2. वि-हा below), the sky, air (only<BR>used in comps.).<BR>—विह-ग, अस्, m. ‘sky-goer,’ a<BR>bird; a cloud; an arrow; the sun; the moon; a<BR>planet.<BR>—विहगोपघुष्ट (˚ग-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>resounding with (the notes) of birds, resonant with<BR>birds.<BR>—विहङ्-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, sky-going, flying,<BR>going swiftly; (अस्), m. a bird; a cloud; an arrow;<BR>the sun; the moon.<BR>—विहङ्-गम, अस्, m. ‘sky-<BR>goer,’ a bird; the sun; (आ), f. a pole or yoke for<BR>carrying burdens (= भार-यष्टि).<BR>—विहङ्ग-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘king of the birds,’ epithet of Garuḍa<BR>(the vehicle of Viṣṇu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्गिका|विहंगिका
विहङ्गिका, f. a sort of pole or yoke for carrying<BR>burdens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
2. वि-हा, ind. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 36. fr.<BR>1. वि-हा), heaven, paradise, sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस्
वि-हायस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (probably formed fr. 1. वि-हा<BR>above, as 1. धायस् fr. rt. 1. धा), ‘expanding,’<BR>extensive, vast, great (= महत् according to Naigh.<BR>III. 3), all-pervading; (Sāy. = विविध-गमन-<BR>युक्त); (perhaps) going quickly, impetuous, spirited,<BR>active; (आस्, अस्), m. n. the open air, air, space (Gr.<BR>χάος), sky, atmosphere; (आस्), m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस|विहायसं|विहायसः
वि-हायस, अस्, अम्, m. n. heaven, sky, atmo-<BR>sphere; (अस्), m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायसा
वि-हायसा, ind. (inst. c. of वि-हायस् above),<BR>through the sky or air; heaven, sky, atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
विहा 3. वि-हा, cl. 3. P. -जहाति (2nd sing.<BR>Impv. वि-जहीहि, Kirāt. XI. 31), -हातुम्, to relin-<BR>quish, quit, abandon, leave, give up or lay aside<BR>entirely, lose: Caus. -हापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>quit or abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहापित|विहापितं
वि-हापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to abandon or give<BR>up; made to yield, extorted, given up, given; (अम्),<BR>n. gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहाय|विहायः
वि-हाय, ind. having abandoned or left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायत
वि-हायत, अम्, n. (?), donation, gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीन|विहीनः
वि-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely abandoned, left,<BR>deserted, destitute, bereaved, deprived of, void or<BR>devoid of, free from, without.<BR>—विहीन-ता, f. the<BR>state of being wholly abandoned, abandonment.<BR>—वि-<BR>हीन-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, low-born, base-born, brutish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहार|विहारः
विहार वि-हार, &c. See वि-हृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिंस्
विहिंस् वि-हिंस्, cl. 7. 1. P. -हिनस्ति, -हिंसति,<BR>-हिंसितुम्, to injure severely, injure, hurt, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिंसक
वि-हिंसक, अस्, इका, अम्, injuring, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिंसत्
वि-हिंसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, injuring, harming, hurt-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिंसित
वि-हिंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, injured, hurt, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित|विहितः
विहित 1. वि-हित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वि-धा),<BR>distributed, apportioned, bestowed; put in order,<BR>arranged, appointed, determined, fixed, settled, pre-<BR>scribed, enjoined, enacted, decreed, ordained, ordered;<BR>proper to be done; deposited, placed; done, per-<BR>formed, undertaken, acted, made; framed, con-<BR>structed, formed; furnished with, possessed of.<BR>—वि-<BR>हित-दुर्ग-रचन, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has en-<BR>joined the building of a fortress.<BR>—विहितागस् (˚त-<BR>आग्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, one who has committed a fault,<BR>offending, faulty, wicked.<BR>—विहिताञ्जलि (˚त-अञ्˚),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, making a respectful obeisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितवत्
विहित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has performed<BR>or undertaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिति|विहितिः
वि-हिति, इस्, f. action, performance, acting, doing;<BR>arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित्रिम
विहित्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, done according to rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित|विहितः
विहित 2. वि-हित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वि privative<BR>+ हित), improper, unfit, unsuitable, not good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीन|विहीनः
विहीन वि-हीन. See under 3. वि-हा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहुत्मती
विहुत्मती वि-हुत्-मती, f. (a Kvip formation<BR>fr. rt. हु with prep. वि and affix मत्), a special<BR>oblation or offering, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>1. 134, 6. विहुत्मतीनाम् = विशेषेण होमवती-<BR>नाम् or else आह्वानवतीनाम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृ
विहृ वि-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते, -हर्-<BR>तुम्, to take away, remove, destroy; to go in<BR>various directions; to walk or roam about or ramble<BR>for pleasure, saunter, amuse or divert one's self, sport,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda 1. 28, 7. विजर्भृतस् = विशेषेण<BR>पुनः पुनर् विहारं कुरुतः); to vary, change,<BR>alternate, mix; to spend or pass (time &c.); to<BR>live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर|विहरः
वि-हर, अस्, m. taking away; expanding, going<BR>apart or in different directions, separation, disunion,<BR>absence; changing, exchanging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरण|विहरणं
वि-हरण, अम्, n. the act of taking away or<BR>removing, taking; going about for pleasure or exer-<BR>cise, rambling, roaming, taking a walk or airing;<BR>expatiating; relaxation, pastime, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरणीय
वि-हरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken away; to be<BR>rambled or sported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरत्
वि-हरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, roaming for pleasure,<BR>sauntering about, ranging at large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर्तृ|विहर्त्तृ
वि-हर्तृ, ता, m. one who takes away, a robber;<BR>one who rambles about, rambling, roaming; a roamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहार|विहारः
वि-हार, अस्, m. taking away, removing; expan-<BR>sion, opening; too great expansion of the organs of<BR>speech (consisting in too great lengthening or drawl-<BR>ing in pronunciation; opposed to सं-हार; cf.<BR>व्य्-आस); walking for pleasure or amusement, taking<BR>an airing, wandering, roaming, gadding, going about;<BR>sporting, play, sport, recreation, pastime, pleasure,<BR>relaxation; a pleasure-garden, garden; a Buddhist or<BR>Jaina temple or convent (originally the hall where<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">Page0953-a+ 77</a>]<BR>the Buddhist priests met or walked about; afterwards<BR>these halls were used as temples, and sometimes be-<BR>came the centre of a whole monastic establishment);<BR>a temple; the palace of Indra or a banner (= वै-<BR>जयन्त?); a palace; N. of a district; the shoulder;<BR>a sort of bird, = विन्दु-रेखक; (in Vedic ritual)<BR>a term for varying a verse (by taking it to pieces,<BR>joining to each of its Pādas a Pāda taken from<BR>another verse, and reciting both parts in such a way<BR>as if they formed only one verse; cf. व्य्-अतिमर्श).<BR>—विहार-गृह, अम्, n. a pleasure-house, play-<BR>house, theatre.<BR>—विहार-भूमि, इस्, f. ground or<BR>place for roaming about, grazing ground, pasturage.<BR>—विहार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, taking pleasure or relax-<BR>ation, enjoying one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0952-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारक
विहारक or विहारिक, अस्, इका, अम्, roaming or<BR>walking about, a roamer; belonging to a Buddhist<BR>temple or convent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारिन्
विहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, expanding; taking pleasure or<BR>relaxation, wandering or roaming about for pleasure,<BR>enjoying one's self; beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृत|विहृतं
वि-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, expanded; sported, played;<BR>taken out, transposed, varied, (in Vedic ritual applied<BR>to the transposing of the Pādas in singing the Ṣo-<BR>ḍaśī hymns, see वि-हार); (अम्), n. one of the ten<BR>blandishments or feminine modes of indicating love,<BR>hesitation or reluctance to avow feelings to a lover,<BR>(some of the others are लीला, ललित, कुट्टमित,<BR>मोट्टायित, वि-च्छित्ति, किल-किञ्चित, &c., q. q. v. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृति|विहृतिः
वि-हृति, इस्, f. taking away; opening, expansion;<BR>sport, pastime, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृत्य
वि-हृत्य, ind. having opened or spread out,<BR>having expanded; having roamed about or sported,<BR>having rambled, having disported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठ|विहेठः
विहेठ वि-हेठ, अस्, m. (see rt. हेठ्), hurt,<BR>injury; the act of afflicting or harassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठक|विहेठकः
वि-हेठक, अस्, m. an injurer, one who inflicts<BR>pain or injury on another; a reviler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठन|विहेठनं
वि-हेठन, अम्, n. the act of injuring, hurting,<BR>wounding, killing; afflicting, distressing; rubbing,<BR>grinding; injury, harm, pain, sorrow, affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्रु
विह्रु वि-ह्रु (ह्रु = ह्वृ, cf. वि-ह्वृ below),<BR>cl. 9. P. -ह्रुणाति, &c., Ved. to injure, hurt, destroy,<BR>(Sāy. वि-ह्रुणाति = वि-ह्वरति, Ṛg-veda I. 166,<BR>12.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्रुत
वि-ह्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. injured, hurt, spoiled<BR>[cf. अ-व्˚]; fractured, dissevered, (Sāy. = वि-च्छिन्न,<BR>वि-बाधित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्लण
विह्लण विह्लण, अस्, m., N. of a native of<BR>Kaśmīra (author of the following poem).<BR>—विह्लण-<BR>काव्य, अम्, n. ‘the poem of Vihlaṇa,’ N. of a poem<BR>(containing the Caura-pañcāśikā, said to have been<BR>recited when Vihlaṇa was on the point of being put<BR>to death by king Vīra-siṃha, whose daughter he had<BR>secretly espoused).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वल्
विह्वल् वि-ह्वल्, cl. 1. P. -ह्वलति, -ह्वलि-<BR>तुम्, to shake or move about, stagger, tremble, be<BR>agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वल|विह्वलः
वि-ह्वल, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking about, agitated,<BR>alarmed, perturbed, disquieted, confused, overcome<BR>with fear, beside one's self, delirious; distressed,<BR>afflicted; languishing; desponding; fused, liquid.<BR>—विह्वल-ता, f. or विह्वल-त्व, अम्, n. agitation,<BR>perturbation, consternation, anxiety.<BR>—विह्वली-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, made confused or agitated; fused, liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वलत्
विह्वलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, trembling, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वलित
वि-ह्वलित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, alarmed, stag-<BR>gering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वृ
विह्वृ वि-ह्वृ, cl. 1. P. -ह्वरति, -ह्वर्तुम्,<BR>Ved. to be crooked, curved; to hurt (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वे
विह्वे वि-ह्वे, cl. 1. P. A. -ह्वयति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to call upon, invoke, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहव
वि-हव, अस्, m., Ved. an invocation, invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी 1. वी, cl. 2. P. वेति (2nd sing. Impv.<BR>वीहि, 3rd pl. व्यन्तु), विवाय, वेष्यति,<BR>अवैषीत्, वेतुम्, to go, move; to go towards, ap-<BR>proach, (in Ṛg-veda I. 77, 2. वेः 2nd sing. Impf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">Page0953-b+ 80</a>]<BR>= वेति = गच्छति); to pervade; to bring, convey,<BR>offer; to attain, obtain, accept; to conceive, become<BR>pregnant, engender, bring forth; to desire, love, wish<BR>for, (according to Nirukta IX. 42, 43. वीताम् = पि-<BR>बताम् or कामयेताम्); to eat, enjoy, consume,<BR>partake of (with gen. or acc.); to send, throw, hurl,<BR>cast; to drive (in this sense regarded as a substitute<BR>for rt. अज्): Pass. or cl. 4. A. वीयते, to be gone,<BR>&c.: Caus. वाययति, -यितुम्, Aor. अवीवयत्, to<BR>cause to go or approach; to cause to obtain or<BR>accept; to cause to eat or partake of; to cause to<BR>desire or love; to cause to conceive (in this sense<BR>also वापयति): Desid. विवीषति: Intens. वेवीयते,<BR>वेवयीति, वेवेति, (see also वेवी); [cf. Gr. οἴσω,<BR>οἴαξ, οἰήϊον; Lat. in-vītus, in-vitare.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
2. वी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. going, moving, (according to<BR>Sāy. वेः = गन्त्र्याः, Ṛg-veda III. 5, 5); pervad-<BR>ing, extensive, (Sāy. = व्याप्त, Ṛg-veda IV. 5, 8);<BR>(ईस्), f. the act of going, motion; covering. (For वी,<BR>‘a bird,’ see under 2. वि, p. 908.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक|वीकः
वीक, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 47. fr. वी,<BR>a substitute for rt. अज्), a bird; air, wind; the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीत|वीतं|वीतः
1. वीत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, approached; led round<BR>the sacrificial fire (said of a horse, Ṛg-veda 1. 162,<BR>15); accepted, acceptable, approved, liked, loved;<BR>desired, wished for, beautiful (Ved.); tranquil, quiet,<BR>tame, unfit for war; (अस्), m. a horse or elephant<BR>untrained or unfit for war; (अम्), n. the goading of<BR>an elephant.<BR>—वीत-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most<BR>acceptable, (Sāy. = अतिशयेन कान्त, Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>1, 18.)<BR>—वीत-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>beautiful backs (said of horses, Sāy. = कान्त-पृष्-<BR>ठ, Ṛg-veda I. 162, 7).<BR>—वीत-वार, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>(see 2. वार), Ved. having a handsome tail, (Sāy.<BR>= क्रान्त-बल, प्राप्त-बल, Ṛg-veda VIII. 46,<BR>23.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीति|वीतिः
वीति, इस्, f. going, moving, motion; engendering,<BR>producing; eating, food, (वीती, Ved. inst. = वीत्या,<BR>‘with food,’ Ṛg-veda VI. 16, 46); enjoyment;<BR>cleaning, cleansing; light, lustre; (इस्), m. a horse.<BR>—वीति-होत्र, अस्, m., N. of Agni or fire; of the<BR>sun; of a son of Priya-vrata; of a son of Tāla-<BR>jaṅgha; (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. one who offers the<BR>sacrificial meal to the gods; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>sect of fire-worshippers; of a branch of the Haihaya<BR>tribe.<BR>—वीति-होत्रक, अस्, m., N. of Agni or fire;<BR>of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्
व्यत्, अन्, अती, अत्, going, moving, &c., (Sāy.<BR>व्यन्तः = गच्छन्तः, Ṛg-veda VI. 1, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी 3. वी (वि-इ), cl. 2. P. व्य्-एति (3rd pl.<BR>वि-यन्ति), Impf. व्य्-ऐत्, Perf. वीयाय, व्य्-एतुम् (for<BR>व्ययति, व्यययति, see व्यय्), to go apart or in<BR>different directions; to go or extend in every direc-<BR>tion, to be diffused or scattered, become distributed<BR>or divided; to go away, disappear, vanish, be lost;<BR>to go through, traverse: cl. 4. A. वीयते, to go<BR>apart or away, &c., (Sāy. वीयसे = गच्छसि, Ṛg-<BR>veda IX. 86, 37; according to some वीयसे is an<BR>Intens. form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीत|वीतं|वीतः
2. वीत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 3. वीत see under rt. व्ये),<BR>gone away, departed, disappeared; set free, loosed,<BR>let go, exempt, freed from, devoid of.<BR>—वीत-कल्-<BR>मष, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from taint or sin.<BR>—वीत-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, free from desire.<BR>—वीत-घृण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one from whom mercy has departed,<BR>merciless.<BR>—वीतघृण-ता, f. mercilessness.<BR>—वीत-<BR>जन्म-जरस, अस्, आ, अम्, not subject to birth or<BR>old age.<BR>—वीत-दम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, free from pride,<BR>not proud, humble, lowly.<BR>—वीत-भय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>fearless, undaunted; (अस्), m. epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वीत-भी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, free from fear, intrepid.<BR>—वीत-<BR>मत्सर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from envy, free from<BR>passion.<BR>—वीत-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, exempt or free<BR>from sorrow; free from resentment or anger.<BR>—वीत-<BR>मल, अस्, आ, अम्, free from obscurity or darkness,<BR>clear, pure.<BR>—वीत-मोह, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>illusion.<BR>—वीत-राग, अस्, आ, अम्, having the passions<BR>gone, free from passions or affections, dispassionate,<BR>devoid of desire, calm, tranquil; colourless, bleached;<BR>(अस्), m. a sage with subdued passions; a deified<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">Page0953-c+ 76</a>]<BR>Buddhist or Jaina saint.<BR>—वीत-राग-स्तुति, इस्, f., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—वीत-विरुद्ध-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, one<BR>whose hostile feelings have passed away, without<BR>hostile intentions, peaceable.<BR>—वीत-शङ्क, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, freed from fear, fearless.<BR>—वीत-शोक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, free from care or sorrow; (अस्), m. the Aśoka<BR>tree, Jonesia Aśoka.<BR>—वीत-शोक-भयाबाध (˚य-<BR>आब्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, free from the disturbance of sorrow<BR>and fear.<BR>—वीत-स्पृह, अस्, आ, अम्, free from wish<BR>or desire.<BR>—वीत-हव्य, अस्, m., N. of a descendant<BR>of Aṅgiras (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda VI. 15);<BR>of a king.<BR>—वीतोच्चय-बन्ध (˚त-उच्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the fastening of the knot gone, (Kirāt.<BR>VIII. 51.)<BR>—वीतोत्तर (˚त-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no answer, unable or disinclined to reply; (अम्), ind.<BR>without answering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश|विकाशः
विकाश 1. वी-काश, अस्, m. (for 1. वि-काश),<BR>manifestation, display; ether, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीकाश|वीकाशः
2. वी-काश, अस्, m. (for 2. वि-काश), absence of<BR>manifestation; solitude, privacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्
वीक्ष् वीक्ष् (वि-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A. वीक्षते (ep.<BR>also P. -ति), वीक्षितुम्, to see, behold, view, ob-<BR>serve, look at, consider, regard, discern, (हृदि<BR>वीक्ष्, to see in the heart, ponder); to look upon<BR>as, regard as (e. g. पितृ-वद् वीक्ष्, to look upon as<BR>a father): Pass. वीक्ष्यते, to be seen; to look<BR>like, appear, seem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष|वीक्षं|वीक्षः
वीक्ष, अस्, आ, m. f. sight, gazing at, seeing,<BR>investigation; (अम्), n. surprise, astonishment; any<BR>visible object.<BR>—वीक्षापन्न (˚ष-आप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who experiences surprise, astonished, sur-<BR>prised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षण|वीक्षणं
वीक्षण, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of seeing or<BR>observing, looking at, sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षणीय
वीक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, visible, perceptible, ob-<BR>servable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षमाण
वीक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, seeing, looking at, ob-<BR>serving, regarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षित|वीक्षितं|वीक्षितः
वीक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, seen, viewed, beheld, re-<BR>garded, considered; (अम्), n. a look, glance, sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्य|वीक्ष्यं|वीक्ष्यः
1. वीक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, visible, perceptible; to be<BR>gazed at, astonishing, wonderful; (अम्), n. any visible<BR>object, anything to be gazed at; wonder, surprise;<BR>(अस्), m. a dancer, actor; a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्य|वीक्ष्यं|वीक्ष्यः
2. वीक्ष्य, ind. having seen or viewed, having<BR>considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्यमाण
वीक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being seen or beheld,<BR>being gazed at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीखा
वीखा वीखा, f. walking, (for वीङ्खा?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्ख्
वीङ्ख् वीङ्ख् (वि-इङ्ख्), Caus. वीङ्खयति,<BR>यितुम्, to toss to and fro (trans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्खा|वींखा
वीङ्खा, f. going, moving, proceeding, progress,<BR>locomotion; a particular mode of moving; dancing;<BR>one of a horse's paces; cowach, Carpopogon Pruriens<BR>(= शूक-शिम्बी); = सन्धि (according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्ग्
वीङ्ग् वीङ्ग् (वि-इङ्ग्), cl. 1. P. वीङ्गति, वीङ्-<BR>गितुम्, Ved. to move to and fro, oscillate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्गित
वीङ्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, moved to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचयन
वीचयन वी-चयन, अम्, n. (for वि-चयन,<BR>see under 3. वि-चि, p. 914), research, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचि|वीचिः
वीचि वीचि, इस्, m. f. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 72. fr. rt. वे), a wave, small wave, ripple; in-<BR>constancy, thoughtlessness; pleasure, delight, happi-<BR>ness; leisure, interval, rest; a ray of light; small,<BR>little.<BR>—वीचि-क्षोभ, अस्, m. agitation or roughness<BR>of waves.<BR>—वीचि-मालिन्, ई, m. ‘wave-garlanded,’ the<BR>ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीची
वीची, f. = वीचि above.<BR>—वीची-तरङ्ग-न्याय, अस्,<BR>m. wave-undulation-method, (according to the Bhā-<BR>ṣā-pariccheda 166 and Siddhānta-muktāvalī, p. 103,<BR>the cause of the production of sound in the ear.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्
वीज् वीज् [cf. rt. 1. विज्], cl. 1. A. वीजते,<BR>वीजितुम्, to go; cl. 10. P. वीजयति,<BR>यितुम् (perhaps a Nom. fr. व्यज, q. v.), to fan,<BR>cool by blowing upon or fanning: Pass. वीज्यते, to<BR>be fanned; [cf. Lat. vigeo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0953-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजन|वीजनं|वीजनः
वीजन, अम्, n. fanning, the being fanned; a fan<BR>[cf. व्यजन]; a thing, substance; (अस्), m. a sort<BR>of pheasant; the ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजित
1. वीजित, अस्, आ, अम्, fanned, cooled by fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्यमान
वीज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being fanned, fanned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज|वीजं
वीज वीज, अम्, n. (in the older language<BR>frequently written बीज; perhaps fr. rt. जन् with वि;<BR>according to some connected with rt. 1. वी), seed<BR>(of plants &c.), seed-corn, grain; semen virile;<BR>(perhaps also) quicksilver; marrow; any germ, ele-<BR>ment, beginning, cause, source, primary cause or<BR>principle, origin; the germ or origin of any compo-<BR>sition (as of a poem, of the plot of a drama, of a<BR>magical formula, &c.); calculating primary causes,<BR>analysis, algebra; truth, divine truth (as the seed or<BR>cause of being); the mystical letter or syllable which<BR>forms the essential part of the Mantra of any deity;<BR>receptacle, place of deposit; a particular correction<BR>in astronomy; (अस्), m. = वीजक, the citron tree.<BR>—वीज-कर्तृ, ता, m. ‘producer of seed,’ epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—वीज-काण्ड-प्ररोहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or वीज-<BR>काण्ड-रुह, अस्, आ, अम्, springing from a seed or<BR>from the (slip or portion taken from a) stalk.<BR>—वीज-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, producing semen; (त्), n. an aphro-<BR>disiac.<BR>—वीज-कोश or वीज-कोष, अस्, m. a seed-<BR>vessel, the pericarp of a flower; the seed-vessel of<BR>the lotus; (ई), f. a pod, legume.<BR>—वीज-क्रिया, f.<BR>the operation of analysis, elemental or algebraic<BR>solution.<BR>—वीज-गणित, अम्, n. calculation of pri-<BR>mary causes, causal calculus, analysis, algebra; N. of a<BR>treatise on algebra.<BR>—वीज-गर्भ, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Trichosanthes Diœca.<BR>—वीज-गुप्ति, इस्, f. ‘seed-<BR>protection,’ a pod, legume.<BR>—वीज-तस्, ind. from seed,<BR>according to the seed.<BR>—वीज-त्व, अम्, n. the being<BR>an origin or cause, causality.<BR>—वीज-दर्शक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘explainer of the germ or plot of a play,’ a play-<BR>director, stage-manager.<BR>—वीज-धानी, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—वीज-धान्य, अम्, n. coriander.<BR>—वीज-<BR>न्यास, अस्, m. (in dramatic language) laying down<BR>or making known the germ or plot of a play.<BR>—वीज-<BR>पादप, अस्, m. the plant Semecarpus Anacardium<BR>(= भल्लातक).<BR>—वीज-पुर, incorrect for वीज-<BR>पूर.<BR>—वीज-पुरुष, अस्, m. the progenitor of<BR>a tribe or family.<BR>—वीज-पुष्प, अम्, n. common<BR>citron; a thorny plant, Vangueria Spinosa (= म-<BR>रुवक).<BR>—वीज-पुष्पिका, f. a sort of grain, An-<BR>dropogon Saccharatus.<BR>—वीज-पूर or वीज-पूरक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘seed-filling,’ common citron; a variety of<BR>citron, Citrus Medica; (अम्), n. the fruit of the<BR>citron.<BR>—वीज-पूर्ण, अस्, m. ‘seed-filled,’ epithet of<BR>the common citron (= छोलङ्ग); Citrus Medica.<BR>—वीज-पेशिका, f, ‘seed-sheath,’ the scrotum.<BR>—वीज-<BR>प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, yielding seed, sowing seed, &c.;<BR>generating; (अस्), m. a generator.<BR>—वीज-प्रबोध,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentary on the Vīja-gaṇita.<BR>—वीज-प्ररोह, अस्, आ, अम्, or वीज-प्ररोहिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, growing from seed.<BR>—वीज-फलक, अस्, m.<BR>the plant Citurs Medica; a citron or lemon.<BR>—वीज-<BR>मति, इस्, f. (in algebra) a mind capable of analysis,<BR>penetration of causes or principles, causal sagacity.<BR>—वीज-मन्त्र, अम्, n. epithet of a mystical syllable<BR>with which a Mantra or magical formula commences.<BR>—वीज-मातृका, f. the pericarp or seed-vessel of<BR>the lotus.<BR>—वीज-मात्र, अम्, n. only as much as<BR>is required for seed, only what is required for the<BR>procreation of offspring or for the preservation of a<BR>family; epithet of the ninth Maṇḍala of the Ṛg-<BR>veda.<BR>—वीज-मुक्तावली, f., N. of a work.<BR>—वीज-<BR>यज्ञ, अस्, m. ‘seed-offering,’ N. of a particular<BR>allegorical sacrifice or offering.<BR>—वीज-रत्न, अस्, m.<BR>‘having gems of seeds,’ a kind of bean.<BR>—वीज-रुह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, growing from seed; (अस्), m. grain,<BR>corn.<BR>—वीज-रेचन, अम्, n. Croton Jamalgota (=<BR>जय-पाल).<BR>—१. वीज-वत्, ind. like seed.<BR>—२. वीज-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing seed, furnished or pro-<BR>vided with seed; provided with grain.<BR>—वीज-व-<BR>पन, अम्, n. the act of sowing seed.<BR>—वीज-वर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘best of grains,’ a kidney-bean, Phaseolus<BR>Radiatus.<BR>—वीज-वाप, अस्, m. a sower of seed;<BR>the act of sowing seed.<BR>—वीज-वापिन्, ई, m. ‘sowing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">Page0954-b+ 78</a>]<BR>seed,’ a sower.<BR>—वीज-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘seed-bearer,’<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>—वीज-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the plant Ter-<BR>minalia Tomentosa.<BR>—वीज-सञ्चय, अस्, m. a heap<BR>or collection of seed or grain.<BR>—वीज-सू, ऊस्, f.<BR>‘bringing forth seed,’ the earth.<BR>—वीज-सेक्तृ, ता,<BR>m. a sprinkler of seed, procreator, progenitor.<BR>—वीज-<BR>हरा or वीज-हारिणी, f. ‘taking away seed,’ epithet<BR>of a witch (a daughter of Duḥsaha).<BR>—वीजा-कृत,<BR>see below.<BR>—वीजाक्षर (˚ज-अक्˚), अम्, n. the first<BR>syllable of a magical formula, the syllable at the<BR>commencement of a Mantra or form of prayer.<BR>—वीजाङ्कुर (˚ज-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a sprout or first<BR>shoot from a seed, seed-shoot, seed-lobe, cotyledon,<BR>seedling; (औ), m. du. seed and shoot, seed and<BR>blade.<BR>—वीजाङ्कुर-वत्, ind. (in phil.) like the<BR>(continuous succession of) seed and shoot.<BR>—वीजा-<BR>ढ्य (˚ज-आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in seed; (अस्),<BR>m. = वीज-पूर.<BR>—वीजाध्यक्ष (˚ज-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘presiding over seed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वीजापहा-<BR>रिणी (˚ज-अप्˚), f. = वीज-हरा.<BR>—वीजाभिधान<BR>(˚ज-अभ्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—वीजाम्ल<BR>(˚ज-अम्˚), अम्, n. = वृक्षाम्ल.<BR>—वीजार्णव-<BR>तन्त्र (˚ज-अर्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—वीजाश्व (˚ज-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘seed-horse,’ an entire<BR>horse, stallion.<BR>—वीजोत्कृष्ट (˚ज-उत्˚), अम्, n.<BR>good seed.<BR>—वीजोदक (˚ज-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘seed-<BR>water, grain-like water,’ hail.<BR>—वीजोप्ति (˚ज-उप्˚),<BR>इस्, f. sowing seed.<BR>—वीजोप्ति-चक्र, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of astrological diagram shaped like a serpent for<BR>indicating good or bad luck following on the sowing<BR>of seed.<BR>—वीजोप्ति-विधि, इस्, m. the manner of sow-<BR>ing seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजक|वीजकः
वीजक, अम्, n. seed; = वीज above (at the end of<BR>comps.); (अस्), m. common citron, Citrus Medica<BR>(= मातुलङ्ग); a citron or lemon; Terminalia<BR>Tomentosa (= पीत-शाल); the position of the arm<BR>of a child at birth; N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजल
वीजल, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with seed or grain,<BR>seedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजा
वीजा, ind. by or with seed, sowing with seed.<BR>—वीजा-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to sow with seed,<BR>sow; to harrow over after sowing.<BR>—वीजा-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, sown with seed, sown; harrowed or ploughed<BR>over after sowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजिक
वीजिक, अस्, आ, अम्, seedy, abounding in seeds; see<BR>Gaṇa Kumud-ādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजित
2. वीजित, अस्, आ, अम्, sown with seed, sown with,<BR>having for seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजिन्
वीजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having or possessing seed, bearing<BR>seed, seedy; being of the race or blood of (at the<BR>end of a comp., cf. राज-व्˚); (ई), m. a real proge-<BR>nitor (as opposed to क्षेत्रिन्, the nominal father or<BR>merely the husband of a woman, Manu IX. 51 sq.);<BR>a procreator, father (in general); the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्य|वीज्यः
वीज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, sprung or produced from seed;<BR>sprung from or belonging to any family; of a good<BR>family (at the end of a comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटा
वीटा वीटा, f. a small piece of wood shaped<BR>like a barley-corn and about a span long, (it was<BR>struck with a stick or bat in a kind of game, like<BR>hockey, played by boys; according to others the वीटा<BR>was a metal ball of some kind; see Mahā-bh. Ādi-p.<BR>5050, Schol.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटि|वीटिः
वीटि वीटि, इस्, or वीटिका or वीटी, f. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. इट् with वि), the betel plant, Piper Betel (=<BR>ताम्बूल-वल्लिका); a preparation of the Areca nut<BR>with spices and chunam enveloped in a leaf of the<BR>betel plant, betel, Pān; a tie, fastening; [cf. वेत्र,<BR>वेतस; cf. also Gr. ἴ-τυ-ς, ἰ-τέα; Lat. vi-tex, vitta,<BR>vi-men, vi-ti-s; Old Germ. wi-d, wi-da; Angl.<BR>Sax. widde.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीडु
वीडु वीडु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. strong, firm, &c.,<BR>see वीऌउ.<BR>—वीडु-जम्भ, &c., see वीऌउ-जम्भ.<BR>—वीड्व्-अङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having strong limbs,<BR>firm in body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीडय
वीडय = वीऌअय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणा
वीणा वीणा, f. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 15. said to<BR>be fr. rt. 1. वी), the Vīṇā or Indian lute, (an instru-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">Page0954-c+ 73</a>]<BR>ment of the guitar kind, supposed to have been<BR>invented by Nārada, q. v., usually having seven wires<BR>or strings raised upon nineteen frets or supports fixed<BR>on a long rounded board, towards the ends of which<BR>are two large gourds; its compass is said to be two<BR>octaves, but it has many varieties according to the<BR>number of strings, &c.); lightning.<BR>—वीणा-दण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. ‘lute-stick,’ the neck or long rounded board<BR>of a lute.<BR>—वीणानुबन्ध (˚णा-अन्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>tie of a lute or lower part of one of its ends where the<BR>wires are fixed (sometimes called ‘the tail-piece’).<BR>—वीणा-भिद्, त्, f. a kind of lute, (वीणा-भिदां<BR>विवेक, description of the different kinds of lutes.)<BR>—वीणा-वाद or वीणा-वादक, अस्, m. a player on<BR>the Vīṇā, a lutanist.<BR>—वीणास्य (˚णा-आस्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘lute-faced,’ epithet of Nārada (the son of Brahmā<BR>and inventor of the Vīṇā described above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणिन्
वीणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with lutes, a player on<BR>a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीत|वीतं|वीतः
वीत वीत, वीति, &c. See p. 953, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतंस|वीतंसः
वीतंस वी-तंस, अस्, m. (for वि-तंस, q. v.),<BR>a cage, a chain or net for confining birds or beasts;<BR>an enclosure for taming birds or animals, an aviary,<BR>menagerie; a place for keeping or preserving game,<BR>preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतन|वीतनः
वीतन वीतन, औ, m. du. (possibly con-<BR>nected with वि-तन्), the sides or cartilages of the<BR>larynx or throat (= कृक-पार्श्व-द्वय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथि|वीथिः
वीथि वीथि, इस्, or वीथी, f. (probably fr. rt.<BR>1. वी or 3. वी), a row, line; a road; a terrace in front<BR>of a house; a stall, shop; a sort of drama (or the<BR>dramatic narration of an amatory intrigue, said to be<BR>in one act and to be performed by one or two play-<BR>ers); (इस्), f. a particular division of the planetary<BR>sphere (comprising three asterisms).<BR>—वीथ्य्-अङ्ग,<BR>अम्, n. a division or constituent part of the dramatic<BR>entertainment called Vīthi, (it is described as a kind<BR>of dialogue consisting in quibble, equivoque, jest,<BR>abuse, and the like.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथिका
वीथिका, f. = वीथि, a road, &c.; a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीध्र|वीध्रं|वीध्रः
वीध्र वीध्र, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 26. fr. rt. इन्ध् with वि), clear, clean, pure; (अम्),<BR>n. the sky, atmosphere; wind; fire; [cf. Gr. αἰθρία.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीन्
वीन् वीन् (वि-इन्), cl. 8. P. वीनोति, &c., Ved.<BR>to cause to go out, drive away, remove, scatter, dis-<BR>perse, (Sāy. = विविधं गमयति); to send forth<BR>in various ways, (Sāy. = विविधम् प्रेरयति); to<BR>bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीना
वीना वीना, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीनाह|वीनाहः
वीनाह वीनाह, अस्, m. = वि-नाह, the top<BR>or cover of a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीन्व्
वीन्व् वीन्व् (वि-इन्व्), cl. 1. P. वीन्वति, &c.,<BR>= वीन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीपा
वीपा वीपा, f. lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीप्सा
वीप्सा वीप्सा, f. (fr. the Desid. of व्य्-आप्,<BR>q. v.), ‘the desire of pervading (with any property or<BR>quality simultaneously or continuously),’ several or<BR>successive order or series, the arrangement of things<BR>or properties in regular succession or each by each,<BR>repetition, the repetition of words to imply continu-<BR>ous or successive action (e. g. वृक्षं वृक्षं<BR>सिञ्चति, he waters tree after tree; प्रभुर् भूतम्<BR>भूतम् अभि सर्व-प्राणिष्व् अस्ति, the supreme<BR>being is in all living beings creature after creature;<BR>cf. Pāṇ. VIII. 1, 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीबुकोश|वीबुकोशः
वीबुकोश वीबुकोश, अस्, m. (?), a cowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीभ्
वीभ् वीभ् (= rt. चीभ्), cl. 1. A. वीभते,<BR>वीभितुम्, to boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्
वीर् 1. वीर् (वि-ईर्), Caus. वीरयति (Impf.<BR>-ऐरयत्, Aor. Ved. -ऐरत्), -यितुम्, Ved. to scatter or<BR>drive in various directions; to split into pieces, break,<BR>divide asunder, break open, (Sāy. व्य्-ऐरत् = उद्घा-<BR>टित-वत्, Ṛg-veda II. 15, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0954-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्
वीर् 2. वीर्, cl. 10. P. (perhaps to be re-<BR>garded as a Nom. fr. वीर below), वीर-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to be powerful or valiant; to make<BR>heroic effort, display heroism, act like a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर|वीरं|वीरः
वीर, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s. II. 13. fr.<BR>वी substituted for rt. अज्; according to some perhaps<BR>for an original वार, fr. rt. वृ), heroic, mighty,<BR>powerful, strong, robust, excellent, eminent; (अस्),<BR>m. a hero, brave man, warrior, champion, eminent<BR>man; the last Jina or Jaina pontiff of the present<BR>era; an actor; heroism (as one of the eight Rasas<BR>which give to poetic and dramatic composition its<BR>flavour or taste; the Rasa of heroism is said to be<BR>displayed by munificence, clemency, and valour; the<BR>Vīra-carita, q. v., exhibits an example of this Rasa);<BR>the flower Nerium Odorum; fire; sacrificial fire [cf.<BR>वीर-हन्]; (आ), f. the wife of a hero; a wife, mother,<BR>matron; a sort of perfume (commonly called Murā);<BR>a medicinal root (= क्षीर-काकोली); the plant Fla-<BR>courtia Cataphracta; the drug Elabāluka; the plantain<BR>tree; a sort of Asclepias, Asclepias Rosea; opposite-<BR>leaved fig-tree; Convolvulus Paniculatus (the white<BR>and dark kinds); the tree Gmelina Arborea; an aloe;<BR>the plant called Atis; spirituous liquor or a particular<BR>kind of it; N. of a river; (अम्), n. a reed, Arundo<BR>Tibialis; the root of ginger (?); pepper; rice-gruel;<BR>the root of Costus Speciosus; the root of Andropogon<BR>Muricatus; [cf. probably Gr. ἥρω-ς, Ἥρα, Ἡρακλῆς,<BR>εἰρήν; Lat. vir; Goth. vair; Angl. Sax. wer;<BR>Lith. vyra-s.]<BR>—वीर-कर्म, अम्, n., Ved. hero-<BR>forming (seed).<BR>—वीर-कीट, अस्, m. ‘worm of a<BR>hero,’ a pitiful warrior.<BR>—वीर-केशरिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—वीरङ्-करा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—वीर-<BR>चरित or वीर-चरित्र, अम्, n. ‘exploits of the hero,’<BR>N. of a celebrated drama by Bhava-bhūti (= महा-<BR>वीर-चरित, q. v.).<BR>—वीर-जयन्तिका, f. a kind of<BR>dance performed by soldiers after a victory or on<BR>going to battle, a war-dance; war, battle.<BR>—वीर-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—वीर-तर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bolder; (अस्), m. a great hero; an arrow;<BR>a corpse (?); (अम्), n. = वीरण, Andropogon Muri-<BR>catus.<BR>—वीरतरासन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. a particular<BR>posture.<BR>—वीर-तरु, उस्, m. the tree Pentaptera<BR>Arjuna; the shrub Barleria Longifolia.<BR>—वीर-ता, f.<BR>or वीर-त्व, अम्, n. heroism.<BR>—वीर-धन्वन्, आ,<BR>m. ‘having a powerful bow,’ epithet of Kāma-deva<BR>(god of love).<BR>—वीरन्-धर, अस्, m. a peacock;<BR>fighting with wild beasts; a leather cuirass or jacket;<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—वीर-पट्ट, अस्, m. a kind of mili-<BR>tary dress or war accoutrement.<BR>—वीर-पत्त्रा, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= वि-जया); N. of a river (Ved.).<BR>—वी-<BR>र-पत्नी, f. the wife of a hero.<BR>—वीर-पर्ण, अम्,<BR>n. a particular drug (= सुर-पर्ण).<BR>—वीर-पाण or<BR>वीर-पान, अम्, n. the drink of warriors, (taken,<BR>before or during a battle, for refreshment or to raise<BR>the courage.)<BR>—वीर-पाण्ड्य, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—वीर-पुष्पी, f. a kind of plant (= सिन्दूर-पुष्-<BR>पी).<BR>—वीर-पेशस्, आस्, m., Ved. a vigorous frame,<BR>(according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 11, 3. the masc.<BR>is used for the neut.)<BR>—वीर-प्रजायिनी, f. the mo-<BR>ther of a hero.<BR>—वीर-प्रजावती, f. the mother of<BR>a hero.<BR>—वीर-प्रसवा, f. a woman who brings<BR>forth heroes.<BR>—वीर-बाहु, उस्, m. ‘strong-armed,’<BR>N. of Viṣṇu; of a king.<BR>—वीर-भद्र, अस्, m.<BR>a distinguished hero; an Ava-tāra or son of Śiva, (in<BR>the Vāyu-Purāṇa he is said to have been created from<BR>Śiva's mouth in order to spoil the sacrifice of Dakṣa,<BR>and is described as having a thousand heads, a thou-<BR>sand eyes, a thousand feet, and wielding a thousand<BR>clubs; his appearance is fierce and terrific, he is clothed<BR>in a tiger's skin dripping with blood, and he bears a<BR>blazing bow and battle-axe; in another Purāṇa he<BR>is described as produced from a drop of Śiva's sweat;<BR>this form of Śiva is said to be more especially wor-<BR>shipped in the Marāṭha country); N. of one of the<BR>Rudras; of an author; a horse fit for the Aśva-<BR>medha sacrifice; a fragrant grass (= वीरण).<BR>—वीर-<BR>भद्रक, अम्, n. the fragrant grass Andropogon<BR>Muricatus.<BR>—वीर-भानु, उस्, m., N. of a king; of<BR>a work.<BR>—वीर-भार्या, f. the wife of a hero.<BR>—वीर-भुक्ति, N. of a place, (probably for तीर-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-b" target="_blank">Page0955-b+ 81</a>]<BR>भुक्ति.)<BR>—वीर-भूपति, इस्, m., N. of the patron<BR>of Cauṇḍapācārya.<BR>—वीर-मातृ, ता, f. the mother<BR>of a hero.<BR>—वीर-मुकुन्द-देव, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king (the patron of Mārkaṇḍeya-kavīndra).<BR>—वीर-<BR>मुद्रिका, f. an ornament or ring worn on the middle<BR>toe.<BR>—वीर-रजस्, अस्, n. red lead, minium (= सिन्-<BR>दूर).<BR>—वीर-रस, अस्, m. the Rasa of heroism,<BR>(see रस.)<BR>—वीर-रेणु, उस्, m., N. of Bhīma-sena.<BR>—वीर-लोक, अस्, m. ‘hero-world,’ region of warriors or<BR>champions.<BR>—वीर-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in heroes,<BR>having a champion or hero; accompanied with heroes<BR>or progeny; (अती), f. a woman whose husband is liv-<BR>ing; a particular fragrant plant (= मांस-रोहिणी);<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—वीर-वत्सा, f. the mother of a hero.<BR>—वीर-वर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वीर-वामन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—वीर-विप्लावक, अस्, m.<BR>‘disturber of the sacrificial fire,’ a Brāhman who<BR>performs oblations with money procured from the<BR>lowest or Śūdra caste.<BR>—वीर-विरुद, N. of a kind<BR>of artificial verse; [cf. शूर-श्लोक.]<BR>—वीर-वृक्ष,<BR>अस्, m. the marking-nut plant, Semecarpus Anacardium;<BR>the tree Pentaptera Arjuna; a sort of grain, Andro-<BR>pogon or Holcus Sorghum.<BR>—वीर-शय्या, f. a parti-<BR>cular posture; [cf. वीर-स्थान.]<BR>—वीर-शुष्म,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having heroic or mighty strength,<BR>very powerful or efficacious.<BR>—वीर-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m.<BR>a matchless hero.<BR>—वीर-समन्वित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attended or accompanied by heroes.<BR>—वीर-सिंह,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king of Gūrjara; of the author of<BR>the Durgā-bhakti-taraṅgiṇī.<BR>—वीर-सिंह-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the patron of Mitra-miśra.<BR>—वीर-सू, ऊस्,<BR>f. ‘hero-bearing,’ the mother of a hero; the mother<BR>of a male child.<BR>—वीर-सेन, अस्, m. ‘having an<BR>army of heroes,’ N. of the father of Nala; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a particular plant (= आरुक).<BR>—वीरसेन-ज or<BR>वीरसेन-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of Vīra-sena,’ epithet of<BR>Nala (a celebrated prince, hero of several well-known<BR>poems and episodes, as the Nalopākhyāna, Naiṣadha,<BR>Nalodaya, &c.).<BR>—वीर-सैन्य, अम्, n. garlic.<BR>—वीर-<BR>सोम, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Hasti-vaidyaka.<BR>—वीर-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. ‘having powerful shoul-<BR>ders,’ a buffalo.<BR>—वीर-स्थान, अम्, n. a particular<BR>posture (practised by ascetics; cf. वीरासन).<BR>—वीर-<BR>हण, अस्, ई, अम्, hero-killing.<BR>—वीर-हत्या, f. the<BR>killing of a man, murder of a son, (Manu XI. 41.)<BR>—वीर-हन्, आ, m. ‘destroyer of the sacrificial fire,’<BR>a Brāhman who has suffered the sacred domestic fire<BR>to become extinct (either from carelessness, impiety,<BR>or absence); N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वीराम्ल (˚र-अम्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a kind of dock or sorrel (= अम्ल-वेतस).<BR>—वीरारुक (˚र-आर्˚), अम्, n. a medicinal plant<BR>(= आरुक).<BR>—वीराशंसन (˚र-आश्˚), अम्, n. ‘the<BR>place wished for by heroes,’ the post of danger<BR>in a battle; a forlorn hope; keeping watch.<BR>—वीरा-<BR>सन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘hero-sitting, hero-posture,’<BR>kneeling on one knee; sleeping out in the open<BR>air, the station of a guard or sentinel; a bivouac;<BR>a particular posture in sitting practised by ascetics,<BR>(sitting on the thighs, one leg being in the other, =<BR>पर्यङ्क, q. v., see 1. आसन); a field of battle.<BR>—वीरेश (˚र-ईश), अस्, m. ‘chief of heroes,’ N. of<BR>Śiva or Vīra-bhadra.<BR>—वीरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘chief of heroes,’ epithet of Śiva or Vīra-bhadra, q. v.;<BR>any great hero.<BR>—वीरेश्वर-लिङ्ग, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a sacred Liṅga.<BR>—वीरोज्झ (˚र-उज्˚), अस्, m. ‘sacri-<BR>ficial-fire abandoning,’ a Brāhman who omits offering<BR>burnt offerings or neglects his sacrificial fire.<BR>—वीरो-<BR>पजीविक (˚र-उप्˚), अस्, m. ‘subsisting by the sacri-<BR>ficial fire,’ a Brāhman who claims alms or presents<BR>for having preserved his sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरक|वीरकः
वीरक, अस्, m., Ved. = वीर, a hero; the plant<BR>कर-वीर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरण|वीरणं
वीरण, अस्, m., N. of a sage (father of Vīraṇī);<BR>of the father of Asiknī; of a teacher of the Yajur-<BR>veda; (ई), f. a side-glance, leer; a deep place; N.<BR>of a daughter of Vīraṇa and mother of Cākṣuṣa;<BR>(अम्), n. a fragrant grass, Andropogon Muricatus;<BR>[cf. विरण, वैरिण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरणिन्
वीरणिन्, ई, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरयु
वीरयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. fond of heroes, desiring<BR>heroes; (Sāy.) desiring to kill heroes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीराय
वीराय, Nom. A. वीरायते, &c., to act like a<BR>hero, show heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरिका
वीरिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरिणी
वीरिणी, f. the mother of a hero (Ved.); N. of a<BR>river; of a wife of Dakṣa (daughter of Vīraṇa and<BR>mother of a thousand sons, = असिक्नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य|वीर्यं|वीर्य्य|वीर्य्यं
वीर्य, अम्, n. vigour, strength, power; heroism,<BR>prowess, valour, fortitude, courage, firmness; virile<BR>energy, virility; dignity, consequence; splendor, lustre;<BR>semen virile; the seed of plants, &c.; (आ), f. vigour,<BR>energy, virility.<BR>—वीर्य-ज, अस्, m. a son.<BR>—वीर्य-<BR>धर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race.<BR>—वीर्य-पार-<BR>मिता, f. one of the six perfections (with Buddhists).<BR>—वीर्य-प्रपात, अस्, m. discharge of semen virile.<BR>—वीर्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing vigour, vigor-<BR>ous, strong, stout, robust; efficacious, overcoming,<BR>victorious.<BR>—वीर्य-विरहित, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of<BR>prowess or vigour, &c.<BR>—वीर्य-विशिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessed of courage, vigour, &c.<BR>—वीर्य-वृद्धि-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing an increase of virile energy;<BR>(अम्), n. an aphrodisiac.<BR>—वीर्य-शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>possessing vigour or heroism, strong, heroic.<BR>—वीर्य-<BR>शुल्क, अस्, आ, अम्, having prowess or heroism as<BR>its price, to be purchased by valour.<BR>—वीर्य-हानि,<BR>इस्, f. loss of vigour or virile energy; impotence.<BR>—वीर्य-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of strength;<BR>cowardly; seedless.<BR>—वीर्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>= वीर्य-वत्.<BR>—वीर्यावदान (˚य-अव्˚), अम्, n.<BR>effecting anything by prowess; (आनि), n. pl. valour<BR>and achievements.<BR>—वीर्यावधूत (˚य-अव्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, overcome or surpassed in prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरानक
वीरानक वीरानक, अम्, n. (?), N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुध्
वीरुध् वीरुध्, त्, f. (fr. rt. 1. रुध् = rt. 1.<BR>रुह् with वि; cf. वि-स्रुह्), a spreading creeper; a<BR>branch, shoot; a plant which grows again after being<BR>cut; a shrub, plant in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुधा
वीरुधा, f. = वीरुध् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीळु
वीळु वीऌउ or वीडु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. strong,<BR>firm, (sometimes written वीलु); (उ), n. anything<BR>strong, a fortified place, stronghold; [cf. according to<BR>some Gr. Ἴλιος]<BR>—वीऌउ-जम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having strong jaws or teeth, (Sāy. = दृढ-दन्त.)<BR>—वीऌउ-द्वेषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. hating the strong<BR>or violent (said of Brahmaṇas-pati).<BR>—वीऌउ-पत्मन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. strong-going, moving with rapid<BR>flight.<BR>—वीऌउ-पवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having strong<BR>tires (said of the chariot of the Maruts).<BR>—वीऌउ-<BR>पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. strong-handed, strong-hoofed.<BR>—वीऌउ-हर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. having strong or<BR>violent joy, exulting, fiercely passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीळय
वीऌअय, Nom. P. वीऌअयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to be<BR>strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीळित
वीऌइत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. made strong, strengthened,<BR>(Sāy. = दृढी-कृत, Ṛg-veda III. 53, 19.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवध|वीवधः
वीवध वी-वध, अस्, m. = वि-वध, a yoke<BR>or pole for carrying burdens; a burden; storing or<BR>heaping corn; a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवधिक|वीवधिकः
वीवधिक, अस्, ई, m. f. a man or woman who car-<BR>ries a load by means of a yoke; a general dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीविध
वीविध वीविध for वि-विध, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवृत
वीवृत वीवृत, अस्, आ, अम्, = वि-वृत, revealed,<BR>published.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीष्
वीष् 1. वीष् (वि-ईष्), cl. 1. P. A. वीषति,<BR>-ते, वीषितुम्, Ved. to go in various directions, spread,<BR>be extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीष्
वीष् 2. वीष् (वि-इष्, see rt. 3. इष्), cl. 1. P.<BR>वीच्छति, &c., Ved. to seek for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीहार|वीहारः
वीहार वीहार, अस्, m. (for वि-हार, q. v.), a<BR>temple, sanctuary, (especially) a Jaina or Buddhist<BR>convent or temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुक
वुक वुक, अस्, m. a species of plant, (a va-<BR>rious reading for वक, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुङ्ग्|वुंग्
वुङ्ग् वुङ्ग् (= rt. बुङ्ग्), cl. 1. P. वुङ्गति,<BR>&c., to leave, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0955-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुण्ट्|वुंट्
वुण्ट् वुण्ट् (= rt. विण्ट्), cl. 10. P. वुण्ट-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to hurt, kill; to waste away,<BR>decay, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुन्ध्
वुन्ध् वुन्ध्, वुस्, &c. See rts. बुन्ध्,<BR>बुस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वूर्ण
वूर्ण वूर्ण. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वूवशर्मन्
वूवशर्मन् वूव-शर्मन्, आ, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृ
वृ वृ, cl. 1. P. A. वरति, वरते, &c.; cl.<BR>5. P. A. वृणोति, वृणुते, &c.; or वॄ, cl. 9.<BR>P. A. वृणाति, वृणीते, &c., Perf. ववार (2nd sing.<BR>ववरिथ, Ved. ववर्थ, Ist du. ववृव or ac-<BR>cording to some ववरिव, 3rd du. वव्रतुस्, 3rd<BR>pl. वव्रुस् or ववरुस्), वव्रे or ववरे (2nd sing.<BR>ववृषे or ववुरिषे, 1st pl. ववृमहे), 2nd Fut.<BR>वरिष्यति, -ते, or वरीष्यति, -ते, Aor. अवारीत् (1st<BR>sing. अवारिषम्), अवरिष्ट or अवरीष्ट or<BR>अवृत or अवूर्ष्ट, (Ved. forms अवर्, आवर्, वर्,<BR>अव्रन्, व्रन्, [अप] वम् = वृणोमि in Ṛg-veda X.<BR>28, 7, अवृणि, अव्रि, अवृषत, वर्षथस्, वुरीत,<BR>वृद्धि, वर्तम्), वरितुम्, वरीतुम् (ep. Inf. also<BR>वर्तुम्), to screen, cover, cover over, conceal, hide,<BR>encompass, surround, envelop; to restrain, keep<BR>back, ward off; to prevent, impede, obstruct, hinder,<BR>check, stop; resist, confine; to choose for one's self<BR>(A.), choose, select, prefer, choose anything (acc.) in<BR>preference to anything else (abl.); to love, adore<BR>(generally A.); to woo, solicit, beg, ask for, desire<BR>(generally A.); to solicit anything (acc.) from any<BR>one (acc.); cl. 10. P. A. or Caus. वरयति, -यते,<BR>-यितुम्, to choose, select, ask or choose in marriage;<BR>to make a request, ask for, beg, solicit (sometimes<BR>with a double acc.): Pass. व्रियते, Aor. अवारि, to<BR>be screened or covered; to be restrained or impeded,<BR>be blocked up: Caus. वारयति, -यते, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अवीवरत्, अवीवरत (Ved. अवावरीत्), to cover,<BR>conceal, &c.; to prevent, impede, &c.; to keep off,<BR>ward off; to avert from (with abl.); to restrain, hinder,<BR>suppress, forbid, prohibit, withhold: Desid. विवरि-<BR>षति, -ते, or विवरीषति, -ते, or वुवूर्षति, -ते:<BR>Intens. वेव्रीयते, वोवूर्यते, वर्वर्ति; [cf. Gr.<BR>ἐρύω, ἀρνέομαι, ὄρομαι, ὤρα, εὑρίσκω; ἀρά, ἀρείνω,<BR>ἄριστος, ἦρα, βούλομαι, βουλή, βελτίων, βέλτιστος;<BR>perhaps Lat. aperio, operio, probably velum,<BR>velare; verus, valeo, valor; velle: Old Germ.<BR>wara, wâr, ‘true;’ wari, werna, warnôn, weljan,<BR>‘to choose:’ Goth. varjan, valjan: Angl. Sax. ware,<BR>‘heed;’ wreon, ‘to cover;’ warian, werian, ‘to ward<BR>off;’ wearne, warnian, wearnian, willan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
वर, वरण, &c. See pp. 887, 888.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्य|वर्यः|वर्य्य|वर्य्यं|वर्य्यः
वर्य. See p. 893, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वूर्ण
वूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, chosen, selected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृणान
वृणान, अस्, आ, अम्, choosing, preferring; suppli-<BR>cating, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्वत्
वृण्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, choosing, electing, preferring<BR>(especially as a husband or wife).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्वान
वृण्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, choosing, selecting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत|वृतः
वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded, covered, screened,<BR>defended; chosen, selected; hired; preferred; agreed,<BR>assented to; served; affected by; vitiated, spoiled;<BR>(अम्), n., Ved. a treasure, wealth (according to<BR>Naigh. II. 10).<BR>—वृत-पत्त्रा, f. a kind of plant<BR>(= पुत्र-दात्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृति|वृतिः
वृति, इस्, f. surrounding, encompassing; hiding,<BR>secreting; an enclosure, hedge, fence, an enclosed<BR>piece of ground or place enclosed for particular culti-<BR>vation (especially that of the Piper Betel, which in<BR>many parts of India is surrounded and screened by<BR>mats); selecting, choosing, preferring, appointing;<BR>a selection, choice, soliciting, asking, requesting; a<BR>request.<BR>—वृतिङ्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, making an en-<BR>closure, surrounding, encompassing; (अस्), m. the<BR>plant Flacourtia Sapida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्य|वृत्यं
1. वृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see p. 958, col. 1),<BR>to be surrounded or encompassed, &c.; to be chosen,<BR>eligible, preferable, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्वा
वृत्वा, ind., Ved. having enveloped, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंह्
वृंह् वृंह् (= rts. 2. वृह्, बृंह्, 2. बृह्),<BR>cl. 1. P. वृंहति, वृंहितुम्, to grow, in-<BR>crease; to roar, bellow (frequently applied to the<BR>noise made by elephants); cl. 1. and 10. P. वृं-<BR>हति, वृंहयति, to speak; to shine: Caus. वृं-<BR>हयति, -यितुम्, to cause to increase, to augment,<BR>strengthen, fatten; [cf. Gr. βράχω, βράζω, βράγχος,<BR>βρόγχος, βρόχθος, (probably also) βράσσω, βρυχάομαι;<BR>ῥόχθος, ὀρεχθέω, ῥαχία, ῥέγχω, ῥόγχος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहण|वृंहणः
वृंहण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing to increase,<BR>nourishing, fostering, fattening, nutritious; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of sweetmeat (made of sugar, milk, spices, &c.<BR>fried in ghee, and powdered with coarse sugar, &c.);<BR>(अम्), n. the act of fattening, nourishing.<BR>—वृंहण-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the quality of strengthening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहणीय
वृंहणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be increased; to be<BR>nourished or fatted or strengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहत्
वृंहत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, growing, increasing; roar-<BR>ing, bellowing, making a cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहयितव्य
वृंहयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be increased, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहित|वृंहितं
वृंहित, अस्, आ, अम्, grown, increased; cherished,<BR>nourished; (अम्), n. the roar or noise made by ele-<BR>phants; (आ), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending<BR>on Skanda (also written वृंहिला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्
वृक् वृक्, cl. 1. A. वर्कते, ववर्के, वर्-<BR>कितुम्, to take, accept, seize: Caus. वर्-<BR>कयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अववर्कत् or अवीवृकत्:<BR>Desid. विवर्किषते: Intens. वरीवृक्यते, वर्-<BR>वर्क्ति, वरिव्˚, वरीव्˚, वर्वृकीति, वरिव्˚, वरीव्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक|वृकः
वृक, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 41.<BR>fr. rt. वृ; perhaps connected with rt. व्रश्च्), seiz-<BR>ing, rapacious, malignant, impious (Ved.); (अस्), m.<BR>a wolf; a jackal; a hyena; a crow; a plough (as<BR>tearing up the earth, Ved.; Sāy. = लाङ्गल); = व-<BR>ज्र (according to Naigh. II. 20); = स्तेन (Naigh.<BR>III. 24); an epithet of the moon (Ved.); the tree<BR>Sesbana Grandiflora (= वक-पुष्प); turpen-<BR>tine; compounded perfume; N. of an Asura; of a<BR>son of Pṛthu; of a son of Vijaya; of a son of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people (see वार्-<BR>केण्य, cf. Pāṇ. V. 3, 115); (आ), f. the plant Cis-<BR>sampelos Hexandra, = अम्ब-ष्ठा; (ई), f. a she-<BR>wolf, (in Ṛg-veda I. 117, 18. the nom. case is<BR>वृकीस्); a kind of plant, = पाठा; [cf. Gr. λύκό-ς;<BR>Lat. lupu-s; Goth. vulf-s; Angl. Sax. wulf;<BR>Slav. vluk-u; Lith. vilka-s.]<BR>—वृक-कर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a leader of the Daityas.<BR>—वृक-ताति, इस्,<BR>f., Ved. wolfishness, rapacity (see Pāṇ. V. 4, 41);<BR>wolf-like, rapacious; [cf. ज्येष्ठ-ताति.]<BR>—वृक-<BR>तेजस्, आस्, m., N. of a son of Dhruva.<BR>—वृक-<BR>दंश, अस्, m. ‘wolf-biting,’ a dog.<BR>—वृक-देवा,<BR>f., N. of a daughter of Devaka.<BR>—वृक-धूप,<BR>अस्, m. compounded perfume; turpentine.<BR>—वृक-<BR>धूर्त, अस्, m. ‘wolf-rogue,’ a jackal.<BR>—वृक-<BR>प्रेक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having the eyes of a wolf, looking<BR>at (anything) like a wolf.<BR>—वृकाक्षी (˚क-अक्˚),<BR>f. a kind of plant (= त्रि-वृत्).<BR>—वृकाराति (˚क-अर्˚),<BR>इस्, m. or वृकारि (˚क-अरि), इस्, m. ‘wolf-enemy,’<BR>a dog.<BR>—वृकासुर-वध (˚क-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘kill-<BR>ing of the Asura Vṛka,’ N. of the ninety-sixth chapter<BR>of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—वृ-<BR>कोदर (˚क-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘wolf-bellied,’ a N. of<BR>Brahmā; of Bhīma (the second son of Pāṇḍu, so<BR>called from his enormous appetite).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकति
वृकति, इस्, f. (probably) wolfishness, rapacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकल
वृकल, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhruva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्क|वृक्कः
वृक्क वृक्क, अस्, आ, m. f. (according to some<BR>also) अम्, n. the heart [cf. बुक्क]; a kidney, (in<BR>this sense usually in the dual.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्कक
वृक्कक, औ, m. du. the kidneys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ण|वृक्णं
वृक्ण वृक्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. व्रश्च्), cut,<BR>divided; cut down; torn; broken.<BR>—वृक्ण-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, one who has cut or severed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्त
वृक्त वृक्त, वृक्ति. See under rt. 1. वृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष्
वृक्ष् वृक्ष् (perhaps connected with rt.<BR>वृ), cl. 1. A. वृक्षते, ववृक्षे, वृ-<BR>क्षितुम्, to select, take, accept; to cover; to keep<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष|वृक्षः
वृक्ष वृक्ष, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rt. 2. वृह्; in Uṇādi-s. III. 66. said to be fr. rt.<BR>व्रश्च्, or fr. rt. वृक्ष्, ‘to cover’), a tree, shrub.<BR>—वृक्ष-कुक्कुट, अस्, m. ‘tree-cock,’ a wild cock.<BR>—वृक्ष-खण्ड, अम्, n. ‘a party, i. e. number<BR>of trees,’ a grove.<BR>—वृक्ष-गुल्मावृत (˚म-आव्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, covered with trees and shrubs.<BR>—वृक्ष-<BR>चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going or living in trees; (अस्), m.<BR>‘tree-goer,’ a monkey.<BR>—वृक्ष-च्छाया, f. the<BR>shade of a tree; (अम्), n. the shade of many trees,<BR>a grove.<BR>—वृक्ष-जातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to<BR>the genus tree.<BR>—वृक्ष-तल, अम्, n. the foot of<BR>a tree or the ground about it.<BR>—वृक्ष-धूप, अस्,<BR>m. ‘tree-resin,’ turpentine.<BR>—वृक्ष-नाथ, अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of trees,’ the Indian fig-tree.<BR>—वृक्ष-निर्यास,<BR>अस्, m. the exudation of trees, gum, resin.<BR>—वृक्ष-<BR>निवास, अस्, m. dwelling or living in a tree.<BR>—वृ-<BR>क्ष-पाक, अस्, m. the Indian fig-tree.<BR>—वृक्ष-<BR>भक्षा, f. a kind of parasitical plant (= वन्दाक).<BR>—वृक्ष-भवन, अम्, n. ‘tree-abode,’ the hol-<BR>low of a tree.<BR>—वृक्ष-भिद्, त्, f. ‘tree-splitter,’<BR>an axe.<BR>—वृक्ष-भेदिन्, ई, m. ‘tree-splitter,’ a<BR>carpenter's chisel; a hatchet.<BR>—वृक्ष-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, abounding with trees, consisting of trees.<BR>—वृक्ष-मर्कटिका, f. ‘tree-monkey,’ a squirrel.<BR>—वृक्ष-मूल, अम्, n. the root of a tree.<BR>—वृक्षमूल-निकेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, dwelling at<BR>the roots of trees (as a hermit).<BR>—वृक्ष-मृद्-<BR>भू, ऊस्, m. ‘tree-earth-born,’ a sort of cane or reed,<BR>Calamus Fascicularis.<BR>—वृक्ष-युद्ध, अम्, n. a<BR>fight with trees (instead of clubs).<BR>—वृक्ष-रुह, अस्,<BR>आ, m. f. ‘tree-grower,’ a parasitical plant which has its<BR>roots attached to another plant (as Cymbidum Tessa-<BR>loides).<BR>—वृक्ष-रोपक, अस्, m. a planter of trees.<BR>—वृक्ष-रोपण, अम्, n. the planting of trees.<BR>—वृक्ष-रोपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, planting trees.<BR>—वृ-<BR>क्ष-वाटी or वृक्ष-वाटिका, f. a grove of trees or<BR>garden near the residence of a minister of state, &c.<BR>—वृक्ष-श, अस्, m. (श said to be fr. rt. शी, ‘to<BR>sleep’), a lizard, a chameleon.<BR>—वृक्ष-शायिका, f.<BR>‘tree-sleeper,’ a squirrel.<BR>—वृक्ष-सर्पी, f., Ved.<BR>a female tree-serpent.<BR>—वृक्ष-सेचन, अम्, n.<BR>the watering of trees.<BR>—वृक्ष-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or वृक्ष-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or वृक्ष-स्थित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, staying in or on a tree.<BR>—वृक्षाग्र (˚ष-<BR>अग्˚), अम्, n. the top of a tree.<BR>—वृक्षाङ्घ्रि<BR>(˚ष-अङ्˚), इस्, m. the root of a tree.<BR>—वृक्षा-<BR>दन (˚ष-अद्˚), अस्, m. a carpenter's chisel or<BR>adze; a hatchet, chopper; the Indian fig-tree; the<BR>Piyāl tree, Buchanania Latifolia; (ई), f. a para-<BR>sitical plant, Epidendron; the shrub Hedysarum<BR>Gangeticum.<BR>—वृक्षादि-रुहक or वृक्षादि-<BR>रूढक, अम्, n. the embracing or entwining (of a<BR>creeper) round a tree &c., embracing (in general).<BR>—वृक्षादि-विद्या (˚ष-आद्˚), f. the science of<BR>tree &c., botany.<BR>—वृक्षाम्ल (˚ष-अम्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the hog-plum, Spondias Mangifera; (अम्), n.<BR>acid seasoning, the fruit of the tamarind so used.<BR>—वृक्षायुर्-वेद (˚ष-आय्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>short treatise by Sura-pāla on the planting and culti-<BR>vation of trees.<BR>—वृक्षारोपक (˚ष-आर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the planter of a tree.<BR>—वृक्षारोपण (˚ष-आर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the act of planting trees.<BR>—वृक्षार्हा (˚ष-<BR>अर्˚), f. = महा-मेदा.<BR>—वृक्षालय (˚ष-आल्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘having a tree for an abode,’ a bird.<BR>—वृक्षा-<BR>वास (˚ष-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘living in trees, living in the<BR>hollow of trees,’ an ascetic; a bird.<BR>—वृक्षाश्रयिन्<BR>(˚ष-आश्˚), ई, m. ‘tree-dweller,’ a kind of small owl.<BR>—वृक्षोत्थ (˚ष-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, growing on a<BR>tree.<BR>—वृक्षोत्पल (˚ष-उत्˚), अस्, m. the tree<BR>Pterospermum Acerifolium (= कर्णि-कार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षक|वृक्षकः
वृक्षक, अस्, m. a small tree; the tree Wrightea<BR>Antidysenterica (= कुटज); any tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृगल
वृगल वृगल, अम्, n., Ved. = विदल, a pea,<BR>split peas, (अर्ध-वृगल, half a pea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृच्
वृच् वृच् = rt. 1. वृज्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृचया
वृचया वृचया, f., Ved., N. of a woman<BR>(said to have been given by Indra to Kakṣīvat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0956-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृचीवत्|वृचीवन्त्
वृचीवत् वृचीवत्, आन्, m., Ved., N. of the<BR>oldest of the sons of the Asura Vara-śikha; (अन्तस्), m.<BR>pl. the sons or family of Vara-śikha (slain by Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृज्
वृज् 1. वृज्, cl. 1. P. वर्जति, cl. 7. P.<BR>(Ved. also A.) वृणक्ति, वृङ्क्ते (in this<BR>class the rt. is sometimes written वृच्), cl. 2. A. वृक्ते<BR>(in this cl. the rt. is sometimes written वृञ्ज्, to which<BR>the 3rd sing. Pres. वृङ्क्ते may be referred), व-<BR>वर्ज, ववृजे, (according to some also) ववर्च,<BR>ववृञ्जे, वर्जिष्यति, -ते (Ved. वर्क्ष्यति, -ते),<BR>अवर्जीत्, अवर्जिष्ट (Vedic forms अवृक्, वर्क्,<BR>वर्क्तम्; Perf. part. fem. ववर्जुषी), वर्जितुम्,<BR>(according to some also) वृञ्जितुम् (Ved. Inf. वृ-<BR>जध्यै, वृञ्जसे), to bend, turn (Ved.); to turn<BR>away, avert, divert, alienate (Ved. A.); to apply to<BR>one's own use, choose for one's self (A.); to exclude,<BR>ward or keep off, remove, set aside; to abandon,<BR>lose; to bestow (Ved.); to efface, atone for, purify,<BR>purge, (in the above senses generally A.); to clear;<BR>to pull up, dig up, or (according to Sāy.) cut or<BR>strew (the sacred grass); to cut off, cut to pieces,<BR>(Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI. 26, 3. वर्क् = छेदितवान्<BR>असि); to injure, kill, (Ṛg-veda VI. 18, 8): Pass.<BR>वृज्यते, to be bent, &c.; to be cut or injured, &c.,<BR>(Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 84, 6. वृज्यते = छिद्यते):<BR>Caus. or cl. 10. P. वर्जयति (sometimes also A.<BR>वर्जयते), -यितुम्, Aor. अववर्जत्, to cause to<BR>bend or turn or turn away; to exclude, remove, set<BR>aside, take away, deprive; to abandon, avoid, shun,<BR>abstain from, renounce, give up, leave off, omit,<BR>disclaim; to leave out, except, exempt, spare; to<BR>dismiss; to discharge, give out: Pass. of Caus. वर्-<BR>ज्यते, &c., to be excluded from or deprived of any-<BR>thing (inst.), lose (see वर्जित): Desid. विवर्जि-<BR>षति, -ते: Intens. वरीवृज्यते, वर्वर्क्ति, &c.,<BR>to turn aside, divert: Caus. of Intens. वरीवर्ज-<BR>यति, Ved. to turn or move in different directions;<BR>[cf. Gr. εἵργ-νυ-μι, εἴργ-ω, εἱργ-μό-ς, εἱρκ-τή,<BR>Λυ-κόοργο-ς: Goth.<BR>vrik-a, vruggo: Old Germ. reccheo; wurgjan:<BR>Angl. Sax. vring-an; wealc-an, ‘to roll;’ (probably<BR>also) wrenc, ‘deceit:’ Lith. verz-iu: Slav. vrag-u.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्त
वृक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cleared, cleaned; spread, strewn.<BR>—वृक्त-बर्हिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. one who has<BR>cleared the बर्हिस् (said of a sacrificial priest or<BR>Ṛtv-ij); one who has spread or strewn the sacrificial<BR>grass. (Sāy. = स्तीर्ण-बर्हिस्, Ṛg-veda III. 2, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ति
वृक्ति, इस्, f., Ved. texture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृज्
2. वृज्, in Naigh. II. 9. वृक् is enumerated among<BR>the बल-नामानि. (See वृजन below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजन|वृजनं|वृजनः
वृजन, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, curved (Ved.);<BR>strong, vigorous, (Sāy. = बल-वत्, Ṛg-veda V. 44,<BR>1); moving, transient, any living being regarded as<BR>transient, (Sāy. = गमन-शील = जङ्गम = प्राणि-<BR>जात, Ṛg-veda 1. 48, 5); (अस्), m. curled hair, hair;<BR>(अम्), n. an enclosure, field cleared for pasture or<BR>agriculture; a kind of camp or camping ground;<BR>sky, atmosphere; anything crooked or to be avoided;<BR>sin, wickedness, calamity; force, energy, strength<BR>(= बल, Naigh. II. 9); battle, conflict; oblation,<BR>sacrifice (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजि|वृजिः
वृजि, इस्, f., N. of a country, = व्रज (the modern<BR>Braj, to the west of Delhi and Agra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजिक
वृजिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the district of<BR>Vraja or Braj; a native &c. of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजिन|वृजिनं|वृजिनः
वृजिन, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, bent, curved;<BR>wicked; (अस्), m. curled hair, hair; (अम्), n. any-<BR>thing crooked or to be avoided, wrong, sin, vice,<BR>wickedness, (Sāy. = वर्जनीय, पाप, Ṛg-veda<BR>IV. 23, 8); distress, misery, affliction; red leather.<BR>—वृजिन-वर्तनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. going on wrong<BR>tracks or roads, following evil courses, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृज्य
वृज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bent, to be turned away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृञ्ज्
वृञ्ज् वृञ्ज्. See rt. 1. वृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृढ
वृढ वृढ. See under rt. 1. वृह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्
वृण् वृण्, cl. 8. P. A. वृणोति, वृणुते,<BR>to consume, eat; cl. 6. P. वृणति, to<BR>please, gratify, exhilarate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्
वृत् 1. वृत् (for rt. 3. वृत् see p. 958,<BR>col. 1), cl. 1. A. (in 2nd Fut., Aor., and<BR>Cond. also P.; in Ved. and ep. P. also in other<BR>forms) वर्तते (ep. वर्तति), Perf. ववृते (Ved.<BR>वावृते, P. ववर्त), 2nd Fut. वर्तिष्यते and<BR>वर्त्स्यति, Aor. अवर्तिष्ट and अवृतत्, Cond.<BR>अवर्तिष्यत and अवर्त्स्यत् (Vedic forms [अनु]-<BR>वर्त्ति, [आ] वर्त, अवर्त्, [सम्-आ] ववर्त्ति), वर्-<BR>तितुम्, to turn, turn one's self, turn round, revolve,<BR>roll, move, go; to move on, pass on, go on in<BR>regular course, proceed, run a course, follow on; to<BR>be or be situated in any particular manner or circum-<BR>stances, to be, exist, live, subsist, remain, dwell, be<BR>fixed, abide, stay, (मनसि or हृदये or हृदि<BR>वृत्, to dwell or be turned over or thought over in<BR>the mind, &c.); to be present; to take place, hap-<BR>pen, come to pass; to conduce, tend to (with dat.);<BR>to depend upon (with loc.); to occupy one's self,<BR>employ one's self, be occupied or engaged in (with<BR>loc., उपकारे वृत्, to give assistance); to behave,<BR>demean one's self, act, practice, do, act towards<BR>(with loc.), occupy one's self with (with inst.), act<BR>in any particular manner (with inst., e. g. धर्मेण<BR>वृत्, to act justly; अमायया वृत्, to act guilelessly;<BR>व्याजेन वृत्, to act deceitfully); to enter upon a<BR>particular course of conduct, act a part, (sometimes<BR>with acc. वृत्तिम् added, e. g. वर्तसे वृत्तिम्<BR>अक्षुद्राम्, thou art acting no mean part; यां<BR>वृत्तिं वर्तामि पाण्डवेषु, whatever course I<BR>enter upon towards the Pāṇḍavas): Pass. वृत्यते,<BR>Aor. अवर्ति, &c., to be turned, &c.: Caus. वर्त-<BR>यति, -ते, Aor. अवीवृतत्, अववर्तत्, to cause to<BR>turn or revolve, cause to roll, cause to move or move<BR>round, turn, move; to brandish (as a weapon); to<BR>cause to move away, remove (Ved.); to shed (as<BR>tears &c.); to cause to proceed, cause to be or exist,<BR>make; to cause to take place, cause to pass (as<BR>time), spend, pass, lead a life, live, (sometimes with<BR>acc. वृत्तिम् added, or sometimes with inst. वृत्त्या<BR>or वृत्तेन, or sometimes with inst. of other words,<BR>e. g. भैक्षेण वर्तयति, he lives by begging);<BR>to perform, practice, do, exhibit; to maintain one's<BR>self, subsist (A.); to relate, recount, declare; to<BR>perceive, comprehend; to care for (with dat.);<BR>to read, study [cf. वृत्त]; (according to some) to<BR>speak; to shine: Desid. विवर्तिषते and विवृत्-<BR>सति, to wish to remain, desire to stay, &c.: Intens.<BR>वरीवृत्यते, वरीवृतीति, वर्वृतीति, वरिवृतीति,<BR>वर्वर्त्ति, वरिवर्त्ति, वरीवर्त्ति; [cf. Lat. vert-o,<BR>versus; Goth. vairthan, ana-vairths, vaurs-tva;<BR>Mod. Germ. werde, ward; Angl. Sax. weordhan,<BR>ward, weard, wyrd; Lith. wartau, werciu, war-<BR>toju, wirs-tu; Slav. vrat-i-ti.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्सत्
विवृत्सत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. the Desid.), wishing<BR>to be or exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्सितृ
विवृत्सितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who wishes to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्
2. वृत्, त्, त्, त्, turning, turning round, moving,<BR>existing; (त्), f., Ved. a turn, action, act, deed; (त्),<BR>ind. ‘finished,’ a grammatical term signifying that a<BR>series of roots acted on by a grammatical rule ends<BR>with the word preceding वृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त|वृत्तं|वृत्तः
1. वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, turned; round, rounded,<BR>circular; been, existed, lived; happened, (किं-<BR>वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘one who says to himself, What<BR>has happened?’ one who allows himself to be taken<BR>by surprise, incautious); occurred, past, gone, finished;<BR>dead, deceased; done, performed, acted, engaged in,<BR>undertaken; proceeded, proceeding from, derived<BR>from; read through, studied; fixed, firm; unim-<BR>paired; famous; (अस्), m. a tortoise; (आ), f. a kind<BR>of tree or shrub (= झिञ्झिरिष्टा); (अम्), n. a<BR>circle, circumference; (in astronomy) the epicycle<BR>(= परिधि); event, occurrence, news; procedure;<BR>practice, profession, occupation, mode of life, means<BR>of subsistence; act, action, behaviour, manner, de-<BR>meanour, (उज्झित-धैर्य-वृत्तम्, without regard<BR>to dignity of manner); conduct; observance of any<BR>enjoined practice, established rule or usage, actual<BR>practice, law; ‘the turn of a line,’ final rhythm,<BR>rhythm; verse, metre.<BR>—वृत्त-कर्कटी, f. the<BR>water-melon (= षड्-भुजा).<BR>—वृत्त-खण्ड,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-c" target="_blank">Page0957-c+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, n. a portion or segment of a circle.<BR>—वृत्त-<BR>गन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, having only the smell of verse or<BR>rhythm; (इ), n. epithet of a particular kind of<BR>prose.<BR>—वृत्त-गुण्ड, अस्, m. a kind of grass (=<BR>दीर्घ-नाल).<BR>—वृत्त-चूड or वृत्त-चौल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, whose tonsure has been performed, tonsured,<BR>(this should be performed at the age of one or three<BR>years, cf. Manu II. 35.)<BR>—वृत्त-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing actions or established practices.<BR>—वृत्त-<BR>तण्डुल, अस्, m. a sort of grass (= यव-नाल).<BR>—वृत्त-तस्, ind. according to the practice or ob-<BR>servance of caste, according to usage or customary<BR>procedure, (वृत्ततः पापम्, a sin according to<BR>caste.)<BR>—वृत्त-निष्पाविका, f. a kind of leguminous<BR>plant (= नख-निष्पावी).<BR>—वृत्त-पर्णी, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= पाठा).<BR>—वृत्त-पुष्प, अस्, m. the<BR>Śirīṣa tree; the Kadamba; = वानीर; = कुब्जक;<BR>= मुद्गर.<BR>—वृत्त-प्रत्यभिज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well versed in sacred rites.<BR>—वृत्त-फल, अस्, m.<BR>the pomegranate (= दाडिम); the jujube; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of various plants, = वार्ताकी, = शशाण्डुली, =<BR>आमलकी; (अम्), n. black pepper.<BR>—वृत्त-बाहु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, round-armed, (see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 67.)<BR>—वृत्त-मल्लिका, f. a species of plant (= मोदिनी,<BR>= श्वेतार्क).<BR>—वृत्त-यमक, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>verse containing a play on words, (see यमक.)<BR>—वृत्त-रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘ocean of<BR>metres,’ N. of a short metrical treatise on Post-vedic<BR>metres by Kedāra.<BR>—वृत्त-रत्नाकर-टीका, f. and<BR>वृत्त-रत्नाकर-सेतु, उस्, m., N. of two commen-<BR>taries on the above-mentioned work.<BR>—वृत्त-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, one who has performed the duties of<BR>caste or calling, well-conducted.<BR>—वृत्त-वीज, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of plant, = भिण्डा; (आ), f. another plant,<BR>= आढकी.<BR>—वृत्त-वीजका, f. a kind of plant, =<BR>पाण्डुर-फली.<BR>—वृत्त-शत, अम्, n., N. of a work<BR>mentioned in the Śūdra-dharma-tattva.<BR>—वृत्त-<BR>शस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has studied (the<BR>science of) arms or warfare (= अधीत-शस्त्रविद्य,<BR>Bhaṭṭi-k. IX. 19).<BR>—वृत्त-सम्पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well behaved or conducted, behaving with propriety.<BR>—वृत्त-सादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroying established<BR>usage, worthless, mean, vile.<BR>—वृत्त-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, abiding in the duties of caste or calling.<BR>—वृत्-<BR>ताध्ययनर्द्धि (˚त-अध्˚, ˚न-ऋद्˚), इस्, f. in-<BR>crease of moral conduct and study, holiness resulting<BR>from observance of rules and study (of scripture).<BR>—वृत्तानुवर्तिन् (˚त-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, conforming<BR>to rule, obedient.<BR>—वृत्तानुसार (˚त-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. conforming to prescribed practice; conformity<BR>to metre; (आत्), ind. according to the metre or<BR>measure of a verse, for the sake of the metre.<BR>—वृत्तानुसारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, conforming to established<BR>rule or practice, doing what is enjoined or proper.<BR>—वृत्तान्त (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m., (rarely) अम्, n. ‘the<BR>end or result of a course of action,’ occurrence, inci-<BR>dent, event; tidings, rumour, report, intelligence;<BR>a tale, story, narrative, history, account; an ancient<BR>story; topic, subject; sort, kind, difference; mode,<BR>manner, state, condition; interval, rest, leisure, op-<BR>portunity; property, nature; the whole, totality;<BR>alone, solitary.<BR>—वृत्तान्त-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wit-<BR>nessing or being a spectator of any action.<BR>—वृत्-<BR>तान्तान्वेषक (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, inquiring into<BR>what takes place.<BR>—वृत्तेर्वारु (˚त-इर्˚), उस्, m. a<BR>water-melon (= षड्-भुजा).<BR>—वृत्तोरु (˚त-ऊरु),<BR>उस्, f. a round-thighed woman, (see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 69.)<BR>—वृत्तौजस् (˚त-ओज्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, having unim-<BR>paired power, whose (creative) energy had free and<BR>unobstructed course, (Manu 1. 6); of great energy,<BR>mighty, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तक|वृत्तकं
वृत्तक, अम्, n. a particular kind of prose com-<BR>position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्ति|वृत्तिः
वृत्ति, इस्, f. turning, turning round, revolving;<BR>the circumference of a circle or wheel; being, ex-<BR>istence, abiding (often at the end of comps., e. g.<BR>तद्-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, abiding in that), staying, re-<BR>maining; state, condition; proceeding, career, course<BR>of conduct, conduct, behaviour, action (often at the<BR>end of comps., cf. वक-व्˚); operation, practice,<BR>business, profession, function, office, employment<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-a" target="_blank">Page0958-a+ 80</a>]<BR>(at the end of comps. translatable by ‘employed<BR>about,’ ‘engaged in’), mode of life [cf. वागुरा-<BR>व्˚]; activity, cause or instrument of activity; treat-<BR>ment, respectful treatment; livelihood, maintenance,<BR>means of subsistence (often at the end of comps.,<BR>cf. उञ्छ-व्˚; the means of subsistence for a<BR>Brāhman are said in Manu IV. 4. to be, 1. ऋत,<BR>‘true,’ i. e. lawful gleaning; 2. अ-मृत, ‘not deadly,’<BR>i. e. unsolicited alms; 3. मृत, ‘deadly,’ i. e. soli-<BR>cited alms; 4. प्र-मृत, ‘very deadly,’ i. e. agri-<BR>culture; 5. सत्यानृत, ‘true and false,’ i. e. trade,<BR>traffic; 6. श्व-वृत्ति, ‘dog-maintenance,’ i. e. servi-<BR>tude; this last should never be engaged in, the preced-<BR>ing two, i. e. agriculture and trade, only in times of<BR>distress); wages, hire; customary allowance, perquisite,<BR>fee; mode of thinking, course of ideas; style, force,<BR>character, style in composition (especially dramatic<BR>style, said to be of four kinds, viz. 1. Kaiśikī,<BR>2. Bhāratī, 3. Sātvatī, 4. Ārabhaṭī, q. q. v. v.; the<BR>first three are described as suited to the Śṛṅgāra,<BR>Vīra, and Raudra Rasas respectively, the last as com-<BR>mon to all); comment, commentary, explanation,<BR>exposition, gloss; general character or force of a<BR>word; (in grammar) a complex formation which<BR>requires resolution or explanation (as distinguished<BR>from a simple or uncompounded form, e. g. any<BR>word formed with Kṛt or Taddhita affixes, any com-<BR>pound and even duals and plurals which are regarded<BR>as Dvandva compounds, of which only one member<BR>is left, and all derivative verbs such as desideratives<BR>&c.); a measure of the voice in reciting or chanting,<BR>(of which, according to the Prātiśākhyas, there are<BR>three, viz. वि-लम्बिता, मध्यमा, and द्रुता);<BR>N. of a commentary by Sa-nandana.<BR>—वृत्ति-कर्-<BR>षित, अस्, आ, अम्, distressed for (want of) a liveli-<BR>hood (Manu VIII. 411; according to Kullūka =<BR>भृत्य्-अभावेन पीडितः).<BR>—वृत्ति-च्छेद, अस्, m.<BR>taking away the means of subsistence, confiscation<BR>of a patrimony, deprivation of an hereditary office.<BR>—वृत्ति-ता, f. or वृत्ति-त्व, अम्, n. state of being<BR>or residing or being contained in, state of existence,<BR>state, condition [cf. अनायत्त-व्˚]; mode of sub-<BR>sistence, profession.<BR>—वृत्ति-दान, अम्, n. the giving<BR>of maintenance.<BR>—वृत्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>means of subsistence; abiding; having a particular<BR>way of thinking.<BR>—वृत्ति-लाभ, अस्, m. discovery of<BR>the concurrent (in phil.).<BR>—वृत्ति-वैकल्य, अम्,<BR>n. deficiency or lack of means of subsistence, want<BR>of a livelihood.<BR>—वृत्ति-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in<BR>any state or condition or employment; (अस्), m. a<BR>chameleon (= सरट).<BR>—वृत्ति-हेतु, उस्, m. cause<BR>or means of subsistence.<BR>—वृत्त्य्-अनुप्रास, अस्,<BR>m. alliteration suited to any style or expression.<BR>—वृत्त्य्-अर्थ-बोधक, अस्, इका, अम्, indicat-<BR>ing the meaning of a complex formation, (see<BR>under वृत्ति above.)<BR>—वृत्त्य्-अर्थम्, ind. for the<BR>sake of subsistence, in order to sustain life.<BR>—वृत्त्य्-<BR>उपाय, अस्, m. means of subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0957-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्य|वृत्यं
2. वृत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 956, col. 1),<BR>to be abided or stayed or remained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्
वृत् 3. वृत्, cl. 4. A. वृत्यते (according<BR>to others also cl. 1. वर्तते), to choose,<BR>like, &c., generally used in an old Intens. form वा-<BR>वृत्यते, (see वावृत्, which is classed by native<BR>grammarians among simple roots.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त|वृत्तं|वृत्तः
2. वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps incorrect for वृत),<BR>chosen, selected, appointed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्र|वृत्रः
वृत्र वृत्र, अस्, m. (probably fr. rt. वृ;<BR>according to Uṇādi-s. II. 13. fr. rt. 1. वृत्), ‘the<BR>coverer, hider, obstructer (of rain),’ N. of the Vedic<BR>personification of an imaginary malignant influence<BR>or demon of darkness and drought (supposed to take<BR>possession of the clouds, causing them to obstruct<BR>the clearness of the sky and keep back the waters;<BR>Indra is represented as battling with this evil influ-<BR>ence, and the pent up clouds being poetically pictured<BR>as mountains or castles are shattered by his thunder-<BR>bolt and made to open their receptacles; as a Dānava<BR>or demon, Vṛtra is the son of Danu, q. v., and is<BR>often associated with other evil spirits, such as Ahi,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-b" target="_blank">Page0958-b+ 79</a>]<BR>Śuṣṇa, Namuci, Pipru, Śambara, Uraṇa, whose<BR>malignant influences are generally exercised in pro-<BR>ducing darkness or drought); a cloud (in general);<BR>darkness; a mountain; an enemy; sound, noise;<BR>a wheel; N. of Indra (?); (अम्), n. a wicked person,<BR>an enemy.<BR>—वृत्र-खाद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘Vṛtra-<BR>devouring,’ destroying Vṛtra; (अस्), m. a devourer<BR>of enemies, epithet of Bṛhas-pati.<BR>—वृत्र-घ्नी, f.,<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—वृत्र-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. caus-<BR>ing great darkness, (Sāy. = अतिशयेन लोकानाम् आव-<BR>रकः or वृत्रैर् आवरणैः शत्रून् तरति यः,<BR>i. e. overcoming enemies with darkness, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>32, 5.)<BR>—वृत्र-तुर्, ऊर्, m., Ved. ‘Vṛtra-conquer-<BR>ing,’ epithet of Indra, conquering enemies (in gene-<BR>ral).<BR>—वृत्र-तूर्य, अम्, n., Ved. conquering<BR>enemies, destruction of enemies; battle (= सङ्ग्रा-<BR>म according to Naigh. II. 19).<BR>—वृत्र-द्विष्, ट्,<BR>m. ‘enemy of Vṛtra,’ epithet of Indra.<BR>—वृत्र-<BR>भोजन, अस्, m. a kind of pot-herb (commonly<BR>called Samaṭh, described by some as a sort of cucum-<BR>ber, = गण्डीर).<BR>—वृत्र-वध, अस्, m. ‘the kill-<BR>ing of Vṛtra,’ N. of the twenty-fifth and twenty-<BR>sixth chapters of the Bhūmi-khaṇḍa of the Padma-<BR>Purāṇa; of the seventy-ninth chapter of the Uttara-<BR>kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—वृत्र-शत्रु, उस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of Vṛtra,’ epithet of Indra.<BR>—वृत्र-हत्य,<BR>अम्, आ, n. f., Ved. the slaying of Vṛtra, (Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>89, 5.)<BR>—वृत्र-हथ, अस्, m., Ved. slaying Vṛtra,<BR>slaying enemies.<BR>—वृत्र-हन्, आ, m. ‘Vṛtra-killer,’<BR>epithet of Indra; killer of enemies, victorious.<BR>—वृ-<BR>त्रहन्-तम, अस्, m., Ved. ‘most mighty slayer<BR>of Vṛtra,’ epithet of Indra; a very victorious person.<BR>—वृत्रारि (˚र-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of Vṛtra,’ Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथा
वृथा वृथा, ind. (said to be fr. rt. वृ;<BR>according to some for वर-था), without trouble,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda IX. 76, 1 = अन्-आयासेन); without<BR>pain, without difficulty, with ease, easily (Ved.);<BR>without necessity, unnecessarily, uselessly, fruitlessly,<BR>in vain; unprofitably; foolishly, idly, wantonly,<BR>falsely; wrongly, incorrectly; vain, purposeless, use-<BR>less, fruitless; (if compounded with articles of food,<BR>वृथा is said to mean ‘hot’); [cf. Gr. ῥεῖα, βρᾶ,<BR>ῥᾷ, ῥάῐστος, ῥᾴδιος, &c.]<BR>—वृथा-कथा, f. idle<BR>talk, nonsense.<BR>—वृथाकार (˚था-आक्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>false form, mere appearance, empty show.<BR>—वृथा-<BR>कुल-समाचार, अस्, आ, अम्, whose family and prac-<BR>tices are low.<BR>—वृथाघात (˚था-आघ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>striking uselessly, killing unnecessarily.<BR>—वृथा-<BR>जन्मन्, अ, n. useless or unprofitable birth.<BR>—वृ-<BR>थाट्या (˚था-अट्˚), f. going or strolling about in an<BR>idle manner, travelling for pleasure (regarded as a<BR>vice in a king; Manu VII. 47).<BR>—वृथा-दान,<BR>अम्, n. useless or improper gift, a gift that may be<BR>annulled (or if promised, not made good, as a gift<BR>promised to courtezans, wrestlers, or money lost at<BR>play, &c.; according to some there are sixteen kinds<BR>of these gifts).<BR>—वृथा-पशु-घ्न, अस्, m. the<BR>slayer of an animal wrongly or unnecessarily (i. e. not<BR>for sacrifice).<BR>—वृथा-प्रतिज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>makes a promise rashly.<BR>—वृथा-भू, cl. 1. P. -भ-<BR>वति, &c., to be in vain, to be useless, to be frustrated.<BR>—वृथा-भोग, अस्, आ, अम्, enjoying in vain or<BR>to no purpose.<BR>—वृथा-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, foolish-<BR>minded, wrong-minded.<BR>—वृथा-मांस, अम्, n.<BR>‘useless flesh,’ i. e. flesh not destined for the gods or<BR>Pitṛs, (the eater of such flesh is said to be born as a<BR>goblin); (अस्), m. one who eats such flesh.<BR>—वृ-<BR>थालम्भ (˚था-आल्˚), अस्, m. cutting or plucking<BR>unnecessarily, (Manu XI. 144.)<BR>—वृथा-वादिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, speaking falsely.<BR>—वृथा-श्रम, अस्, m.<BR>vain exertion, useless labour.<BR>—वृथा-षाह्, -षाट्,<BR>m., Ved. one who easily overcomes or conquers,<BR>(Sāy. = अनायासेन शत्रूणाम् अभिभविता, Ṛg-<BR>veda 1. 63, 4.)<BR>—वृथा-सङ्कर-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born<BR>in vain by the mixture of different castes, one who<BR>neglects to perform his duties.<BR>—वृथोत्पन्न (˚था-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced in vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्ध|वृद्धं|वृद्धः
वृद्ध वृद्ध. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धि|वृद्धिः
वृद्धि 1. वृद्धि, इस्, f. (fr. a form वृध् for<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-c" target="_blank">Page0958-c+ 80</a>]<BR>rt. वर्ध्; for 2. वृद्धि see under rt. 1. वृध्),<BR>cutting off, abscission; (in law) forfeiture, deduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्
वृध् 1. वृध् (perhaps developed out of<BR>वि-ऋध्), cl. 1. A. (in Fut., Aor., and<BR>Cond. also P.; in Ved. and ep. P. also in other<BR>forms; sometimes confounded in occasional forms<BR>with rt. 1. वृत्), वर्धते (Ved. P. वर्धति, वृ-<BR>धति), Perf. ववृधे (Ved. P. ववर्ध), 2nd<BR>Fut. वर्धिष्यते and वर्त्स्यति (identical with<BR>2nd Fut. of rt. 1. वृत्), Aor. अवर्धिष्ट and अवृ-<BR>धत्, Cond. अवर्धिष्यत and अवर्त्स्यत् (iden-<BR>tical with Cond. of rt. 1. वृत्), वर्धितुम् (Ved.<BR>Inf. वृधे, वृधसे, वावृधध्यै), to increase,<BR>augment, cause to grow, make larger or stronger,<BR>raise, prosper, make to prosper, (in these active<BR>senses generally Ved. and always P.); to exhilarate,<BR>make joyful, inspirit, animate (Ved. P.); to increase,<BR>grow, become larger or stronger, prosper, be or be-<BR>come prosperous, (in these neuter senses generally<BR>A. except in the Vedic forms वृधति, ववर्ध,<BR>&c., and except in Fut., Aor., and Cond., which may<BR>be also P. in the classical language); to continue,<BR>last; to rise, ascend; to become joyful, have cause<BR>for congratulation: Caus. वर्धयति, -ते (also वर्-<BR>धापयति), -यितुम्, Aor. अवीवृधत्, अववर्-<BR>धत्, to cause to increase or grow, increase, augment,<BR>amplify, enhance, make larger or stronger, cause to<BR>prosper, make powerful, raise, exalt, to make joyful,<BR>gladden; (according to some) to speak; to shine:<BR>Desid. विवर्धिषते, विवृत्सति: Intens. वरी-<BR>वृध्यते, वरीवृधीति; [cf. Zend vared, vareda:<BR>Gr. βάλσ-τη, βλασ-τό-ς, βλαστ-άν-ω, βλωθ-ρό-ς,<BR>βραδινός, ῥαδινός, ῥίζα; ἄλσος: (perhaps) Lat.<BR>grandis: Goth. valdan, vaur-ts, ‘a root:’ Old<BR>Germ. uurza: Angl. Sax. waldan, vridian, weald:<BR>Slav. vladun, vlas, ‘hair:’ Hib. folt, ‘hair;’ fridh,<BR>‘a forest;’ (perhaps) for-bairt, ‘increase, profit.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्ध|वृद्धं|वृद्धः
वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (compar. ज्यायस् or वर्षी-<BR>यस्, superl. ज्येष्ठ or वर्षिष्ठ, q. q. v. v.),<BR>increased, augmented; grown up, full grown, duly<BR>expanded; old, aged, advanced in years, ancient,<BR>mighty, great, large; accumulated, heaped; wise,<BR>learned; (अस्), m. an old man or one past seventy;<BR>a sage, saint; a respectable man; a male descendant<BR>(= गोत्र); a proper N.; = वृद्ध-दारक below;<BR>(आ), f. an old woman (either one past childbearing<BR>or one with grey hair); a female descendant; (अम्),<BR>n. (in grammar) a word having a Vṛddhi vowel in<BR>the first syllable; benzoin.<BR>—वृद्ध-काक, अस्, m.<BR>‘large crow,’ a sort of crow or raven.<BR>—वृद्ध-<BR>काल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—वृद्ध-क्रम, अस्,<BR>m. rank due to age.<BR>—वृद्ध-गङ्गा, f., N. of<BR>a river (commonly called the Buḍi Gaṅgā).<BR>—वृद्-<BR>ध-गौतम, ‘the old Gautama,’ N. of an ancient<BR>recension of Gautama's law-book.<BR>—वृद्ध-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, oldest, most venerable.<BR>—वृद्ध-ता, f.<BR>or वृद्ध-त्व, अम्, n. old age, senility.<BR>—वृद्-<BR>ध-दारक, अस्, m. or वृद्ध-दारु, n. a kind<BR>of convolvulus or climbing plant (= छगला, ऋक्ष-<BR>गन्धा).<BR>—वृद्ध-द्विज-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, bear-<BR>ing the form of an old Brāhman.<BR>—वृद्ध-नगर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—वृद्ध-नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>‘large-naveled,’ having a prominent navel, pot-bellied,<BR>corpulent.<BR>—वृद्ध-प्रधान, अस्, m. a paternal<BR>great-grandfather.<BR>—वृद्ध-प्रपितामह, अस्,<BR>m. a paternal great-grandfather; (ई), f. a paternal<BR>great-grandmother.<BR>—वृद्ध-प्रमातामह, अस्,<BR>m. a maternal great-grandfather; (ई), f. a maternal<BR>great-grandmother.<BR>—वृद्ध-बला, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= महा-समङ्गा).<BR>—वृद्ध-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. the state of being old, old age.<BR>—वृद्ध-<BR>मत, अम्, n. an ancient precept, a precept of ancient<BR>sages.<BR>—वृद्ध-मनु, उस्, m. ‘the old Manu,’<BR>an ancient recension of the Mānava-dharma-śāstra;<BR>[cf. वृहन्-मनु.]<BR>—वृद्ध-महस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. having increased or mighty splendor, endowed<BR>with great strength, very mighty.<BR>—वृद्ध-याज्ञ-<BR>वल्क्य, a particular recension of Yājñavalkya's law-<BR>book.<BR>—वृद्ध-राज, अस्, m. a kind of dock or<BR>sorrel (= अम्ल-वेतस).<BR>—वृद्ध-वसिष्ठ, ‘the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-a" target="_blank">Page0959-a+ 81</a>]<BR>old Vasiṣṭha,’ N. of an ancient recension of Va-<BR>siṣṭha's law-book.<BR>—वृद्ध-वाहन, अस्, m. the<BR>mango tree.<BR>—वृद्ध-विभीतक, अस्, m. the hog-<BR>plum, Spondias Mangifera (= आम्रातक).<BR>—वृद्-<BR>ध-वृहस्पति, इस्, m. ‘the old Vṛhas-pati,’ N.<BR>of an ancient recension of Vṛhas-pati's law-book.<BR>—वृद्ध-शवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having increased<BR>or great force, very mighty, very rapid, (Sāy. = वृद्-<BR>ध-वेग, अतिशयेन वेग-वत्, Ṛg-veda VIII. 25,<BR>10.)<BR>—वृद्ध-शीलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having the disposition<BR>of an old man.<BR>—वृद्ध-शोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. in-<BR>creased in lustre, very bright.<BR>—वृद्ध-श्रवस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, having great glory; endowed with much food;<BR>(आस्), m. an epithet of Indra.<BR>—वृद्ध-सङ्घ,<BR>अस्, m. an assembly of old men, council or meeting<BR>of elders.<BR>—वृद्ध-सूत्रक, अम्, n. a flock of<BR>cotton, flocculent seeds flying in the air.<BR>—वृद्ध-<BR>सेवा, f. reverence for the aged, the serving or honour-<BR>ing of old persons.<BR>—वृद्ध-सेविन्, ई, इनी, इ, honour-<BR>ing or reverencing old persons, serving one's elders.<BR>—वृद्धाङ्गुलि (˚ध-अङ्˚), इस्, f. ‘the great<BR>finger,’ the thumb; the great toe.<BR>—वृद्धाङ्-<BR>गुष्ठ (˚ध-अङ्˚), अस्, m. the great toe; the<BR>thumb.<BR>—वृद्धाचार (˚ध-आच्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>practice of one's forefathers, ancient custom.<BR>—वृद्-<BR>धादित्य (˚ध-आद्˚), अस्, m. a form of the sun.<BR>—वृद्धानुशासन (˚ध-अन्˚), अम्, n. a seer's<BR>precept, direction or ordinance of the aged, an old<BR>man's advice.<BR>—वृद्धारण्य (˚ध-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘seer's grove,’ a place where the Purāṇas or other<BR>sacred works are read and expounded.<BR>—वृद्धा-<BR>वस्था (˚ध-अव्˚), f. the condition or period of<BR>old age, senility.<BR>—वृद्धाश्रम (˚ध-आश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the order or mode of life of an aged (Brāhman),<BR>roaming or wandering about as a religious mendicant;<BR>[cf. आश्रम.]<BR>—वृद्धोक्ष (˚ध-उक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>an old bull (= जरद्-गव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0958-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धि|वृद्धिः
2. वृद्धि, इस्, f. (for 1. वृद्धि see p. 958,<BR>col. 2), increase, increment, augmentation, growth, rise,<BR>rising, ascending; excess; a heap, quantity, assemblage,<BR>multitude; increase in wealth or dignity; increase<BR>of the digits of the sun or moon; progression of any<BR>kind, prosperity, success, advancement, happiness,<BR>pleasure; wealth, property; extension of power or<BR>revenue (as one of the three conditions or objects<BR>of regal power); profit, gain; paying back money<BR>lent with increase or interest, returning the prin-<BR>cipal with a proportionate increment; money-lending,<BR>usury, interest; enlargement of the scrotum (either from<BR>swelled testicle or hydrocele or other morbid affec-<BR>tions); (in grammar) a peculiar increase or length-<BR>ening to which vowels are subject under certain con-<BR>ditions (e. g. आ is the Vṛddhi of अ, ऐ of इ, ई,<BR>and ए, औ of उ, ऊ, and ओ; कृत-वृद्धि, a word<BR>of which the first vowel has been subjected to the<BR>above change); one of the eight principal drugs or<BR>medicinal roots (described as mild, cooling, &c., and<BR>as a remedy for phlegm, leprosy, and worms); a<BR>particular period or division of time, the eleventh of<BR>the astronomical Yogas (or the Yoga star of the<BR>eleventh lunar mansion); (इस्), m., N. of a poet.<BR>—वृद्धि-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, yielding or causing<BR>increase &c.<BR>—वृद्धि-जीवन, अम्, n. or वृद्धि-<BR>जीविका, f. gaining a livelihood by money-lending,<BR>subsistence by usury, the profession of usury.<BR>—वृद्-<BR>धि-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving increase, causing advance-<BR>ment or prosperity; (अस्), m., N. of a plant (= जी-<BR>वक, = शूकर-कन्द).<BR>—वृद्धि-पत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a kind of razor or lancet.<BR>—वृद्धि-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having increase, augmented, increased, in-<BR>creasing; prosperous; rich, wealthy.<BR>—वृद्धि-<BR>श्राद्ध, अम्, n. a Śrāddha or offering made to<BR>progenitors on any prosperous occasion (as on the<BR>birth of a son &c.).<BR>—वृद्ध्य्-आजीव, अस्, or वृद्-<BR>ध्य्-आजीविन्, ई, m. one who lives by money-lending<BR>or usury; a money-lender, usurer; (various kinds of<BR>interest are recognised by Hindū lawyers, viz. 1. का-<BR>यिका वृद्धि, ‘bodily interest,’ i. e. either the ad-<BR>vantage arising from the body of an animal pledged<BR>as security for a loan or interest paid repeatedly with-<BR>out reducing the body or principal; 2. कालिका व्˚,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">Page0959-b+ 77</a>]<BR>‘periodical interest,’ i. e. payable weekly, monthly,<BR>annually, &c., but most usually computed by the<BR>month; 3. चक्र-व्˚, ‘wheel-interest,’ i. e. interest<BR>upon interest, compound interest; 4. कारिता व्˚, ‘sti-<BR>pulated interest,’ or interest at a rate higher than the<BR>usual legal rate; 5. शिखा-व्˚, ‘growing continually<BR>like a lock of hair,’ i. e. interest at a usurious rate<BR>payable daily; 6. भोग-लाभ, ‘advantage ac-<BR>cruing to a creditor from the use' of any article<BR>handed over to him as security, e. g. the usufruct of<BR>lands, gardens, animals, &c.: ‘lawful interest’ is called<BR>धर्म-व्˚, ‘usurious interest’ अ-न्याय-व्˚, ‘interest<BR>at the highest legal rate' परम-व्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिका
वृद्धिका, f. a sort of drug or medicinal plant<BR>(= ऋद्धि, see under 2. वृद्धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्
2. वृध्, f. (only found in dat. वृधे used as a<BR>Ved. infinitive), increase, prosperity; blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध
वृध, अस्, m., Ved. one who increases or pro-<BR>motes or prospers, a prosperer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधसान|वृधसानः
वृधसान, अस्, आ, अम्, growing, increasing, being<BR>augmented or exalted (Ved.); (अस्), m. a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधसानु|वृधसानुः
वृधसानु, उस्, m. a man; a leaf; an act, action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधान
वृधान, अस्, आ, अम्, increasing, augmenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधु
वृधु, उस्, m., N. of a Takṣan or carpenter<BR>(whose cows were taken by Bharad-vāja when suffer-<BR>ing from hunger, see Manu X. 107).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्य|वृध्यं
वृध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be increased or augmented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्न
वृध्न वृध्न, अस्, m. a bubo in the groin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्त|वृंत|वृंतं|वृन्तं
वृन्त वृन्त, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. वृ),<BR>the footstalk of a leaf or fruit, a stalk; a nipple;<BR>the stand of a water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्ताक|वृंताक|वृंताकः|वृन्ताकः
वृन्ताक, अस्, ई, m. f. the egg-plant, Solanum<BR>Melongena (= वार्ताक).<BR>—वृन्ताक-विधि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्तिका|वृंतिका
वृन्तिका, f. a small stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्तिता
वृन्तिता, f. the medicinal plant Wrightea Anti-<BR>dysenterica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्द|वृंद|वृन्दं|वृन्दः
वृन्द वृन्द, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 98. fr. rt. वृ), numerous, many, much, all;<BR>(अम्), n. a heap, multitude, large number, quantity,<BR>aggregation; a flock, drove; (आ), f., N. of the forest<BR>in which Kṛṣṇa was educated; sacred basil, Ocy-<BR>mum Sanctum, = तुलसी; (अस्), m., N. of the author<BR>of a work on medicine.<BR>—वृन्दा-वन, अम्, n. a<BR>wood near the town Gokula in the district of Ma-<BR>thurā on the left bank of the Jumnā (celebrated as<BR>the place where Kṛṣṇa in the character of Go-pāla, or<BR>cowherd, passed his youth, associating with the cow-<BR>herds and milkmaids employed in tending the cattle<BR>grazing in the forest); a raised platform or mound<BR>of earth on which the worshippers of Kṛṣṇa plant<BR>and preserve the Tulasī; (ई), f. holy basil (= तुलसी).<BR>—वृन्दावन-वर्णन, अम्, n. ‘description of<BR>Vṛndā-vana,’ N. of a chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa<BR>of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दार|वृंदार|वृन्दारः
वृन्दार, अस्, आ, अम्, much, great; best, excel-<BR>lent, eminent; beautiful, handsome, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दारक|वृंदारक|वृन्दारकः
वृन्दारक, अस्, अका or इका, अम्, much, great;<BR>best, excellent, eminent, chief; respectable, venerable,<BR>reputable; handsome, agreeable, beautiful, pleasing;<BR>(अस्), m. a deity, immortal; a chief, the head or<BR>leader of a crowd or herd &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दिन्
वृन्दिन् in अश्व-वृन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, consisting of<BR>a large number of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दिष्ठ|वृंदिष्ठ|वृन्दिष्ठः
वृन्दिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of वृन्दार),<BR>very much or great; very excellent, very eminent or<BR>venerable; most beautiful or charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दीयस्|वृंदीयस्
वृन्दीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, very much or great; very<BR>eminent or excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्
वृश् वृश्, cl. 4. P. वृश्यति, ववर्श, वर्-<BR>शितुम्, to choose, select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश|वृशः
वृश वृश, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 104. fr. rt. वृ), a rat; the flower Justicia Gan-<BR>derussa; N. of the author of Ṛg-veda V. 2 (having<BR>the patronymic Jāra); (आ), f. a drug; (अम्), n.<BR>ginger; [cf. वृष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चत्
वृश्चत् वृश्चत्, &c. See under rt. व्रश्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिक|वृश्चिकः
वृश्चिक वृश्चिक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. व्रश्च्), a<BR>scorpion; the zodiacal sign Scorpio; the month when<BR>the sun is in Scorpio; a hairy caterpillar; a crab; a sort<BR>of beetle found in cow-dung; a centipede; a thorny<BR>shrub, Vangueria Spinosa; (आ), f. the pot-herb Ba-<BR>sella, (see the next.)<BR>—वृश्चिक-प्रिया, f. ‘dear to<BR>scorpions,’ the pot-herb Basella Rubra or Lucida.<BR>—वृश्चिकाली (˚क-आली), f. a line of scorpions; the<BR>shrub Tragia Involucrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्
वृष् वृष् (perhaps developed fr. rt.<BR>1. ऋष् with prep. वि), cl. 1. P. वर्षति<BR>(ep. also A. -ते), ववर्ष, वर्षिष्यति, अवर्षीत्<BR>(Ved. 2nd sing. Impv. A. वृषस्व), वर्षितुम्,<BR>to rain (often used impersonally or with Parjanya,<BR>Indra, the clouds, the sky, &c. in the nominative);<BR>to fall as rain (e. g. Ṛg-veda V. 84, 3. वर्षन्ति<BR>वृष्टयः, the showers fall, Sāy. वर्षन्ति = प-<BR>तन्ति); to rain or shower down, pour down, pour<BR>forth, effuse, shed (with acc., e. g. मेघाः शोणितं<BR>ववृषुः, the clouds rained blood); to sprinkle,<BR>moisten; to engender, generate; to drink, (आ-वृष्<BR>also appears to have this sense in the Veda as well<BR>as the sense ‘to eat’); to strike, hurt, vex, weary;<BR>to bestow, give; to have supreme power; cl. 10. A.<BR>वर्षयते, &c., to have the power of generation<BR>(according to some); to be powerful: Caus. वर्ष-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अववर्षत्, अवीवृषत्, to<BR>cause to rain, &c.: Desid. विवर्षिषति: Intens.<BR>वरीवृष्यते, वरीवर्ष्टि, &c.; [cf. Gr. ἔρσ-η<BR>(Hom. ἐέρσ-η), ἕρσ-η, ἑρσή-ει-ς, βρέχ-ω.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष|वृषं|वृषः
वृष, अस्, m. a rainer, sprinkler, (Sāy. = सेचक);<BR>a bull; the sign of the zodiac Taurus; the bull of<BR>Śiva; a strong or athletic man; an amorous or lustful<BR>man (one of the four classes into which men are<BR>divided in erotic works); N. of Kāma (god of love);<BR>a rat; the chief of a class or anything the best of<BR>its kind (e. g. वृषो ऽङ्गुलीनाम्, the chief among<BR>fingers, the thumb; often at the end of a comp. in<BR>the sense ‘chief,’ ‘excellent,’ ‘pre-eminent,’ e. g.<BR>कपि-वृषास्, the chief monkeys); the principal or<BR>chief die (in a game with dice); Justice or Virtue<BR>personified as a bull or as the bull of Śiva; justice,<BR>virtue, morality; an adversary, enemy; N. of Karṇa;<BR>of Viṣṇu; of the Indra of the eleventh Manv-antara;<BR>of a son of Vīti-hotra; a particular drug (= ऋष-<BR>भ); the plant Justicia Ganderussa; a piece of<BR>ground suitable for the foundation of a house; (ac-<BR>cording to some) N. of the fifteenth year of the<BR>Hindū cycle; (अम्), n. a peacock's plumage or tail;<BR>(आ), f. the plant Salvinia Cucullata (= मूषिक-<BR>पर्णी); cowach, Carpopogon Pruriens, = कपि-<BR>कच्छु; (ई), f., see s. v.<BR>—वृष-कर्णी, f. a par-<BR>ticular plant.<BR>—वृष-गन्धा, f. a particular plant<BR>(= वस्तान्त्री).<BR>—वृष-चक्र, अम्, n. a particular<BR>astrological diagram shaped like a bull and having<BR>reference to agriculture.<BR>—१. वृष-दंश or वृ-<BR>ष-दंशक, अस्, m. ‘rat-devourer,’ a cat.<BR>—वृ-<BR>ष-दर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śiva.<BR>—वृष-<BR>ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘having a bull for a sign,’ epithet<BR>of Śiva; ‘having a rat for a symbol,’ epithet of<BR>Gaṇeśa; ‘having virtue for a mark,’ a virtuous man.<BR>—वृष-ध्वाङ्क्षी, f. a species of grass, Cyperus<BR>(= नागर-मुस्ता).<BR>—वृष-नाशन, अस्, m. the<BR>medicinal plant Embelica Ribes (= विडङ्ग, com-<BR>monly called Virang).<BR>—वृष-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the bull,’ epithet of Śiva; a bull set at liberty;<BR>[cf. वृषोत्सर्ग.]<BR>—वृष-पत्त्रिका, f. a species<BR>of plant (= वस्तान्त्री).<BR>—वृष-पर्णी, f. the plant<BR>Salvinia Cucullata (= आखु-पर्णी).<BR>—वृष-पर्-<BR>वन्, आ, m. ‘bull-jointed, strong-jointed,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva; N. of a king of the Daityas or demons (father<BR>of Śarmiṣṭhā); a wasp; a sort of grass, Scirpus<BR>Kysoor (= कशेरु).<BR>—वृष-भानु, उस्, m. (some-<BR>times written वृष-भाणु and वृष-भान), N.<BR>of the son of Sūra-bhāna and father of Rādhā; [cf.<BR>वार्षभाणवी.]<BR>—वृषभानु-सुता or वृष-<BR>भाणु-सुता or वृष-भाणु-कन्या, f. ‘the daughter<BR>of Vṛṣa-bhānu,’ epithet of Rādhā.<BR>—वृष-भासा,<BR>f. the residence of Indra and of the immortals (=<BR>अमरावती).<BR>—वृष-राज-केतन, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-a" target="_blank">Page0960-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the king of bulls for a symbol,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वृष-लोचन, अस्, m. ‘having the eyes of a bull,’<BR>a rat.<BR>—वृष-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘whose vehicle is a<BR>bull,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वृष-शत्रु, उस्, m. ‘enemy<BR>of Vṛṣa or Karṇa,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—वृष-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a son of Karṇa.<BR>—वृष-स्कन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘bull-shouldered,’<BR>having the shoulders of a bull.<BR>—वृषाकर (˚ष-<BR>आक्˚) or वृषा-कर, अस्, m. a kind of bean (=<BR>माष).<BR>—वृषाङ्क (˚ष-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘bull-<BR>marked,’ epithet of Śiva; a pious man (as marked by<BR>virtue); the marking-nut plant; a eunuch, one em-<BR>ployed in the women's apartments.<BR>—वृषाङ्क-ज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘Śiva-produced,’ a small drum (held in one<BR>hand and played by means of a string attached to it,<BR>= डमरु).<BR>—वृषाञ्चन (˚ष-अञ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘going on a bull,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वृषाद्रि<BR>(˚ष-अद्˚), इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—वृषान्-<BR>तक (˚ष-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘destroyer of Vṛṣa,’ epi-<BR>thet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; [cf. वृष-शत्रु.]<BR>—वृषाहार (˚ष-आह्˚), अस्, m. ‘having rats for<BR>food,’ a cat.<BR>—वृषोत्सर्ग (˚ष-उत्˚), अस्, m. let-<BR>ting loose a bull or (according to some) a bull and<BR>four heifers on the occasion of a Śrāddha or funeral<BR>rite in honour of deceased ancestors; setting a bull<BR>at liberty on the occasion of a sacrifice or as a religious<BR>act generally; N. of a Pariśiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—वृषोत्सर्ग-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a part of the<BR>Smṛti-tattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषक
वृषक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Subala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषण|वृषणः
वृषण, अस्, ई, अम्, sprinkling, fertilizing; (अस्),<BR>m. the scrotum or bag containing the testicles; N.<BR>of a son of Kārtavīrya.<BR>—वृषण-कच्छू, ऊस्, f.<BR>ulceration of the scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषदञ्जि
वृषद्-अञ्जि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. sprinkling Soma<BR>libations, (Sāy. = वर्षकेण सोमेन सिञ्चत्, Ṛg-<BR>veda VIII. 20, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषन्
वृषन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. raining, pouring forth,<BR>sprinkling; bounteous; generating, engendering,<BR>male; strengthening, invigorating, manly, vigorous,<BR>young, strong (applied to the horses of Indra and to<BR>the car of the Aśvins); mighty, excellent [cf. वर्-<BR>षिष्ठ]; (आ), m. a rain-cloud, rain (Ved.); ‘the<BR>trickling beverage,’ i. e. Soma juice, a libation [cf.<BR>वृष-पान]; a bull; the zodiacal sign Taurus; a<BR>stallion, horse; epithet of Indra; of Agni; of Soma;<BR>epithet of various other gods; of the hero Karṇa; a<BR>kind of metre (Ved.); pain, sorrow; insensibility to<BR>pain.<BR>—वृष-कर्मन्, आ, m., Ved. a maker or<BR>sender of rain; a showerer of benefits or favours,<BR>(Sāy. = अभिमत-वर्षण-व्यापार-वत्.)<BR>—वृ-<BR>ष-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having vigorous or<BR>mighty strength, (Sāy. = वर्षण-कर्मन्, Ṛg-<BR>veda V. 36, 5.)<BR>—वृष-खादि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (ac-<BR>cording to some) having strong (ring-shaped) weapons<BR>or ornaments, (applied to the Maruts who are said<BR>to be armed or ornamented with rings on their arms,<BR>shoulders, and feet; according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>64, 10. ‘whose weapon is Vṛṣan, i. e. Indra,’ or<BR>‘whose food is Soma.’)<BR>—वृष-गण, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a descendant of Vasiṣṭha (author of Ṛg-veda IX.<BR>97, 7-9); (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Vṛṣa-<BR>gaṇa.<BR>—वृष-जूति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having the speed<BR>or velocity of a bull, (Sāy. = वृषभिर् आकृष्ट,<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 33, 10.)<BR>—वृषण्-अश्व, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having strong horses, strong-horsed (said<BR>of a chariot); (अस्), m. the horse of Indra; N. of<BR>the father of Menā.<BR>—वृषण्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. producing or causing rain, shedding, pouring<BR>forth.<BR>—वृषण्-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having rain<BR>for treasure, affluent in showers, (Sāy. = वर्षण-<BR>धन, Ṛg-veda VIII. 5, 36); (उ), n. the treasure<BR>of Indra.<BR>—वृष-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. manliness,<BR>vigour, strength.<BR>—वृष-त्वा, ind., Ved. by strength,<BR>in strength.<BR>—वृष-धूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. crushed<BR>by males, i. e. by stones (said of the Soma).<BR>—वृ-<BR>ष-नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a strong nave,<BR>strong-naved; (Sāy.) having wheels bestowing showers<BR>(= वर्षक-नाभि-युक्त).<BR>—वृषन्-तम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. most manly, very vigorous, most power-<BR>ful; (Sāy.) most bountiful (= अतिशयेन कामानां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-b" target="_blank">Page0960-b+ 81</a>]<BR>वर्षितृ, Ṛg-veda I. 100, 2).<BR>—वृष-पत्नी, f.,<BR>Ved. ‘having a rain-cloud or a bull for a husband,’<BR>epithet of water.<BR>—वृष-पाण, अम्, n. (i. e. वृ-<BR>षन् + पान), Ved. the drinking of a libation, a<BR>Soma draught.<BR>—वृष-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. strong-<BR>hoofed, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 75, 7<BR>= पांसूनां वर्षक-खुर, ‘having hoofs the<BR>showerers of dust,’ i. e. raising the dust with their<BR>hoofs.)<BR>—वृष-प्रभर्मन्, आ, m., Ved. sending<BR>the rain-cloud, (Sāy. = वर्षण-शीलस्य मेघस्य<BR>प्र-हर्तृ, Ṛg-veda V. 32, 4.)<BR>—वृष-प्रयावन्,<BR>आ, &c., Ved. moving vigorously, swift-passing, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 20, 9. वृष-प्रयाव्णे<BR>= सेक्तारः प्रकृष्टं गन्तारो मरुतो यस्-<BR>मिन् तस्मै.)<BR>—वृष-प्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. strong-<BR>shaped; rain-shedding, (Sāy. = वर्षक-रूप-<BR>युक्त, Ṛg-veda VIII. 20, 10.)<BR>—वृष-मणस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस् (i. e. वृषन् + मनस्), Ved. having the<BR>courage of a bull; disposed to pour forth or bestow<BR>benefits, benevolent-minded, (Sāy. = कामानां वर्-<BR>षण-पर-मनस्क, Ṛg-veda IV. 22, 6.)<BR>—वृ-<BR>ष-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a strong or<BR>mighty car; whose car showers down blessings.<BR>—वृष-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having shower-<BR>yielding reins.<BR>—वृष-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>acting like a bull, engaged in sprinkling (said of<BR>Soma).<BR>—वृष-व्रात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>troops or companies of males, forming troops of<BR>bulls; having abundance of rain, abounding in drops<BR>of rain.<BR>—वृष-शिप्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वृ-<BR>ष-शुष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. drying up or over-<BR>powering the strong, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>IV. 36, 8 = सेक्तॄणाम् बलवताम् शोषक); (अस्),<BR>m. (probably) ‘having manly strength,’ a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषन्धि|वृषंधि
वृषन्धि, इस्, m., Ved. a cloud (= मेघ ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. I. 10; in Ṛg-veda IV. 22, 2.<BR>Sāy. explains वृषन्धिम् by मेघ-भेदन-<BR>द्वारेण वर्षं कुर्वन्तम्, causing rain by di-<BR>viding the clouds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभ|वृषभः
वृषभ, अस्, m. a showerer of bounties, bene-<BR>factor (Ved., Sāy. = कामानां वर्षयितृ, Ṛg-<BR>veda VI. 44, 20); a male animal; a bull, (some-<BR>times used in the Veda as an adjective in the sense<BR>of ‘manly,’ ‘vigorous,’ ‘strong,’ ‘powerful,’ e. g.<BR>वृषभः शुष्मः, manly strength); anything<BR>good or excellent of its kind (often at the end of<BR>comps. in the sense of ‘good,’ ‘excellent,’ ‘pre-<BR>eminent,’ ‘chief’); the hollow or orifice of the ear<BR>[cf. ऋषभ]; an elephant's ear; a particular drug<BR>(= ऋषभ; it is described as a root brought from<BR>the Himālaya mountains, resembling the horn of a<BR>bull, of cooling and tonic properties, and serviceable<BR>in catarrh and consumption); the first of the Jaina<BR>pontiffs of the present era; epithet of the twenty-<BR>eighth Muhūrta; (ई), f. a widow; cowach; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—वृषभ-गति, इस्, m. ‘going on<BR>a bull,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वृषभ-ध्वज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having a bull for an emblem,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वृषभ-षोडश, अस्, ई, अम्, having a bull<BR>as sixteenth, i. e. fifteen (cows) and a bull.<BR>—वृष-<BR>भाक्ष (˚भ-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having the eyes<BR>of a bull; (ई), f. a species of plant (= इन्द्र-<BR>वारुणी).<BR>—वृषभेक्षण (˚भ-ईक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘having the eyes of a bull,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वृष-<BR>भैकादश (˚भ-एक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having a bull<BR>as the eleventh, i. e. ten (cows) and a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषल|वृषलः
वृषल, अस्, m. (in Manu VIII. 16. fancifully<BR>derived fr. वृष, ‘justice,’ + ल for अल fr. अलम्,<BR>implying ‘prevention;’ cf. अलम्, ‘away with’), a<BR>Śūdra or man of the last or servile tribe; epithet<BR>of king Candra-gupta; a man of one of the three<BR>highest classes who by neglecting his religious duties<BR>has lost his caste; a sinner, reprobate, wicked man;<BR>a horse; garlic; (ई), f. a woman of low caste; an<BR>unmarried girl twelve years old (in whom menstru-<BR>ation has commenced); a woman during menstruation;<BR>a barren woman; the mother of a still-born child.<BR>—वृषल-ता, f. or वृषल-त्व, अम्, n. the con-<BR>dition of a Śūdra, state of an outcast.<BR>—वृषलात्-<BR>मज (˚ल-आत्˚), अस्, m. the son of a Vṛṣala or of<BR>a reprobate.<BR>—वृषली-पति, इस्, m. the husband of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">Page0960-c+ 81</a>]<BR>a Śūdrā or woman of low caste or a Brāhman<BR>who owns such a woman as his mistress.<BR>—वृ-<BR>षली-फेन-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has drunk<BR>the moisture of a Śūdrā's (lips).<BR>—वृषली-सेवन,<BR>अम्, n. paying respect to a woman of low caste,<BR>intercourse with a Śūdra female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलक|वृषलकः
वृषलक, अस्, m. a poor or contemptible Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्य
वृषस्य, Nom. P. वृषस्यति, -यितुम्, to long<BR>for a bull, long for sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्यन्ती|वृषस्यंती
वृषस्यन्ती, f. a lascivious woman; a cow in heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपायी
वृषाकपायी, f. ‘wife of Vṛṣākapi,’ epithet of<BR>the Dawn (as the wife of the Sun); epithet of Lakṣmī;<BR>of Gaurī; of Svāhā (wife of Agni); of Śacī (wife of<BR>Indra); of the mother of Indra; Asparagus Race-<BR>mosus; the plant Celtis Orientalis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपि|वृषाकपिः
वृषाकपि, इस्, m. (probably connected with वृ-<BR>षन्, ‘sprinkler’ or ‘irrigator,’ and कपि meaning<BR>‘ape’ or ‘tremulous’), an epithet of the sun (so<BR>called as drawing up vapour and irrigating with<BR>mist); N. of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; of Śiva or Rudra;<BR>of one of the eleven Rudras (according to the Bhā-<BR>gavata-Purāṇa); of Agni or fire; N. of the author<BR>of part of Ṛg-veda X. 86 (having the patronymic<BR>Aindra); of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाणक|वृषाणकः
वृषाणक, अस्, m., N. of the author of Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 136, 4 (having the patronymic Vātaraśana);<BR>a N. or form of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाय
वृषाय, Nom. A. वृषायते, -यितुम्, Ved. to<BR>act like a bull; to roar like one; to fertilize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषायण|वृषायणः
वृषायण, अस्, m., N. of Śiva; a sparrow (=<BR>चटक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषायमाण
वृषायमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. acting like a<BR>bull, eager as a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषिन्
वृषिन्, ई, m. a peacock (either as ‘fond of rain’<BR>or as ‘having a particular plumage’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्ट
वृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, rained; raining down, shower-<BR>ing; raining; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Kukkura.<BR>—वृष्ट-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has rained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टि|वृष्टिः
वृष्टि, इस्, f. rain, a shower; (in the Sāṅkhya<BR>phil.) one of the four forms of internal acquiescence;<BR>[cf. सलिल.]<BR>—वृष्टि-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, producing<BR>rain, sprinkling, raining.<BR>—वृष्टि-काल, अस्, m. the<BR>rainy season.<BR>—वृष्टि-घ्नी, f. a kind of cardamoms<BR>(as ‘preventing moisture?’).<BR>—वृष्टि-जीवन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘living by rain,’ (land) nourished or watered<BR>by rain (= देव-मातृक).<BR>—वृष्टि-द्यावा, m.<BR>du., Ved. causing a rainy sky; epithet of Mitra and<BR>Varuṇa, (Ṛg-veda V. 68, 5.)<BR>—वृष्टि-भू, ऊस्,<BR>ऊस्, उ, born or produced in rain; (ऊस्), m. a frog.<BR>—वृष्टि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of rain, rain-<BR>producing, full of rain, rainy; (आन्), m. a cloud.<BR>—वृष्टि-वनि, इस्, f., Ved. a request or prayer for<BR>rain [cf. वसु-वनि]; (इस्, इस्, इ), desiring rain, seek-<BR>ing or praying for rain.<BR>—वृष्टि-सम्पात, अस्, m.<BR>a shower of rain.<BR>—वृष्टि-हव्य, अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्ट्वी
वृष्ट्वी, ind. having been showered down, (in<BR>Ṛg-veda V. 53, 14. according to Sāy. = वृष्टिषु<BR>प्रेरितासु सतीषु, on rain being sent.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्णि|वृष्णिः
वृष्णि, इस्, इस्, इ, raining, showering blessings<BR>(said of Indra; Sāy. = कामानां वर्षितृ, Ṛg-<BR>veda 1. 10, 2); angry, passionate; heretical, hete-<BR>rodox; (इस्), m. a ram; a ray of light; air, wind;<BR>a heretic, sectary; N. of a descendant of Yadu and<BR>ancestor of Kṛṣṇa; epithet of Kṛṣṇa [cf. वार्ष्-<BR>णेय]; of Indra; of Agni; (अयस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>tribe or family (descendants of Vṛṣṇi and relations<BR>of Kṛṣṇa); N. of a class of Kṣatriyas and Vaiśyas;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἀρνός, ἀρνειός, ῥήν, ἕρσαι, ἔριφος.].<BR>—वृ-<BR>ष्णि-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘born in the family of Vṛṣṇi,’<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—वृष्णि-मत्, आन्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्ण्य
वृष्ण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fecundating; (अम्),<BR>n. a vigorous or manly act; strength, (Sāy. = वीर्य.)<BR>—वृष्ण्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (in the Pada text वृ-<BR>ष्ण्य-वत्), Ved. possessed of vigour or strength,<BR>vigorous; (आन्), m. ‘the vigorous god,’ epithet of<BR>Parjanya; the causer of rain, (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda V. 83, 2 = वर्ष-कर्म-वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्य|वृष्यं|वृष्यः
वृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sprinkled or showered<BR>down, to be rained; aphrodisiac, provocative of sexual<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">Page0961-a+ 75</a>]<BR>vigour, stimulating; (अस्), m. a kind of kidney-bean,<BR>Phaseolus Radiatus; (आ), f. a kind of drug (= ऋद्-<BR>धि).<BR>—वृष्य-कन्दा, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>विदारी).<BR>—वृष्य-गन्धा, f. the pot-herb Con-<BR>volvulus Argenteus.<BR>—वृष्य-वल्लिका, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= विदारी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषदंश|वृषदंशः
वृषदंश 2. वृषद्-अंश (for 1. वृष-दंश<BR>see under वृष). See वार्षदंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषय|वृषयः
वृषय वृषय, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. IV. 100.<BR>said to be fr. rt. वृ, ‘to screen’), refuge, shelter;<BR>asylum, place of refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषसृक्की
वृषसृक्की वृषसृक्की, f. a wasp (= भृङ्-<BR>गरोल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषागिर्
वृषागिर् वृषागिर्, N. of a king (father of<BR>the five Vārṣāgiras, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषायण|वृषायणः
वृषायण वृषायण. See p. 960, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषी
वृषी वृषी, f. the seat of a religious stu-<BR>dent, a kind of seat or cushion made of Kuśa grass<BR>wound into a pad, the seat or cushion of an ascetic,<BR>(said to be also written वृसी, बृषी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्ट
वृष्ट वृष्ट, वृष्टि, &c. See p. 960, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृसय
वृसय वृसय = बृसय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृह्
वृह् 1. वृह् (also written बृह्), cl. 6. P.<BR>वृहति, ववर्ह, वर्हिष्यति or वर्क्ष्-<BR>यति, अवर्हीत् or अवृक्षत् (in Ṛg-veda IV. 16,<BR>12. [प्र] वृहतात् = प्रकर्षेण छिन्नवान् असि),<BR>वर्हितुम् or वर्ढुम्, to pull up, tear up, eradicate,<BR>root up; to make effort, raise, lift up, erect: Caus.<BR>वर्हयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अववर्हत् or अवीवृहत्:<BR>Desid. विवर्हिषति, विवृक्षति: Intens. वरीवृह्-<BR>यते, वरीवर्ढि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हित्वा
वर्हित्वा or वृढ्वा, ind. having rooted up;<BR>having raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृढ
वृढ, अस्, आ, अम्, pulled up, eradicated; lifted up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृह्
वृह् 2. वृह् (also written बृह्, cf. rts.<BR>2. बृह्, वृंह्, 1. वृध्), cl. 1. P. वर्-<BR>हति, cl. 6. P. वृहति (usually referred to rt. 2. बृह्),<BR>ववर्ह, वर्हितुम्, to grow, increase, expand; to<BR>roar, bellow (= rt. वृंह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृह्
3. वृह्, f. increase &c. in वृहस्-पति, p. 962.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्|वृहन्त्
वृहत्, अन्, अती, अत् (originally a pres. part. of rt.<BR>2. वृह्; in the earlier language written बृहत्,<BR>q. v., some compounds beginning with वृहत् will<BR>be found under बृहत्), ‘growing,’ ‘extending,’ great,<BR>large, bulky, big, lofty, high; broad, wide, extended,<BR>extensive, ample, abundant, much; dense, compact,<BR>thick, close; mighty, powerful; high, clear, loud<BR>(said of sounds &c.); (अन्), m., N. of one of the<BR>Maruts; of a king (a son of Su-hotra and father of<BR>Aja-mīḍha); (अती), f. a large lute, the lute of Nārada<BR>(= महती); Viśvā-vasu's lute; any metre contain-<BR>ing thirty-six syllables [cf. बृहती]; a symbolical<BR>expression for the number thirty-six; a part of the<BR>body between the breast and backbone; a mantle,<BR>wrapper [cf. वृहतिका]; a place containing water,<BR>reservoir; speech [cf. वृहती-पति]; a particular<BR>plant, (see बृहती); N. of a commentary; of a wife<BR>of Ripu; of a wife of Gada; of a wife of Devahotra;<BR>(अत्), n., scil. सामन्, see बृहत्; Brahma; the<BR>Veda; [cf. probably Goth. bairgahei; Angl. Sax.<BR>beorh, beorg.]<BR>—वृहच्-चक्षुस् (वृहत् + च्˚), उस्,<BR>m. a kind of vegetable.<BR>—वृहच्-चञ्चु (वृहत्-<BR>चञ्चु), उस्, m. a kind of vegetable; [cf. महा-<BR>चञ्चू.]<BR>—वृहच्-चाणक्य (वृहत् + च्˚), अम्, n.<BR>the large collection of precepts by Cāṇakya.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हच्-चित्त (वृहत्-च्˚), अस्, m. the citron tree (=<BR>फल-पूर).<BR>—वृहच्-छब्देन्दु-शेखर (वृ-<BR>हत् + शब्देन्दु-श्˚), the large grammatical work by<BR>Nāgeśa.<BR>—वृहच्-छरीर (वृहत् + श्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, large-bodied, gigantic.<BR>—वृहच्-छल्क (वृ-<BR>हत् + श्˚), अस्, m. ‘large-scaled,’ a kind of prawn.<BR>—वृहच्-छातातप (वृहच् + श्˚), अस्, m. ‘the<BR>larger Śātātapa,’ N. of a particular recension of Śā-<BR>tātapa's law-book.<BR>—वृहच्-छान्ति-स्तव (वृहत्<BR>+ श्˚), अस्, m. the larger Śānti-stava.<BR>—वृहच्-छाल<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-b" target="_blank">Page0961-b+ 81</a>]<BR>(वृहत् + श्˚), अस्, m. a large or lofty Shorea Ro-<BR>busta.<BR>—वृहच्-छृङ्गार-तिलक (वृहत् + श्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the larger Śṛṅgāra-tilaka.<BR>—वृहच्-छ्रवस्<BR>(वृहत् + श्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. loud-sounding;<BR>loudly praised, far-famed.<BR>—वृहच्-छ्रीक्रम (वृ-<BR>हत् + श्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—वृहच्-छ्लोक<BR>(वृहत् + श्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, loudly praised, far-famed;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of Uru-krama by Kīrtti.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हज्-जघन (वृहत् + ज्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having large<BR>hips, broad-hipped.<BR>—वृहज्-जन (वृहत् + ज्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a great or illustrious man.<BR>—वृहज्-जातक (वृ-<BR>हत् + ज्˚), अम्, n., N. of Varāha-mihira's larger work<BR>on nativities; [cf. स्वल्प-जातक.]<BR>—वृहज्जातक-<BR>श्लोक-व्याख्यान, अम्, n., N. of a metrical com-<BR>mentary by Bhaṭṭotpala on the preceding work.<BR>—वृहज्-जाबालोपनिषद् (वृहत् + ज्˚), त्, f., N.<BR>of an Upaniṣad on the divinity of Kālāgni-rudra.<BR>—वृहज्-जीवन्तिका or वृहज्-जीवन्ती or वृहज्-<BR>जीवा (वृहत् + ज्˚), f. a kind of large Jīvantikā plant<BR>(= प्रियङ्-करी).<BR>—वृहज्-ज्योतिस्, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>grandson of Brahmā; [cf. बृहज्-ज्योतिस्.]<BR>—वृहट्-<BR>टिक्क (वृहत् + ट्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वृहट्-<BR>टीका (वृहत् + ट्˚), f. ‘the large commentary,’ N. of a<BR>work by Kumārila.<BR>—वृहड्-ढक्का (वृहत् + ढ्˚),<BR>f. a large drum.<BR>—वृहती-पति, इस्, m., N. of Vṛhas-<BR>pati or the planet Jupiter; [cf. वृहस्-पति.]<BR>—वृ-<BR>हत्-कथा, f. ‘the large or extended narrative,’ N.<BR>of a collection of tales ascribed to Guṇāḍhya, (the<BR>Kathā-sarit-sāgara of Soma-deva is said to have been<BR>abridged from this work); N. of another work<BR>ascribed to Kṣemendra.<BR>—वृहत्-कन्द, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of bulbous root (either a species of large onion<BR>or a sort of garlic).<BR>—वृहत्-कर्मन्, आ, m. ‘doing<BR>mighty acts,’ N. of several kings.<BR>—वृहत्-कल्प,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Kalpa, the seventh day in the bright<BR>half of the moon in Brahmā's month, (see कल्प);<BR>the last day in the dark half of the month.<BR>—वृहत्-<BR>काय, अस्, ई, अम्, large-bodied, bulky, gigantic.<BR>—वृहत्-काल-ज्ञान, अम्, n. ‘the large Kāla-jñāna<BR>or knowledge of times,’ N. of a work.<BR>—वृहत्-<BR>काल-शाक, अस्, m. a shrub, Cassia Purpurea or a large<BR>variety of it.<BR>—वृहत्-काश, अस्, m. a particular<BR>kind of reed (= खड्गट).<BR>—वृहत्-कीर्त्ति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, far-famed (said of Vṛhas-pati); (इस्), m., N. of a<BR>grandson of Brahmā; of an Asura.<BR>—वृहत्-कुक्षि,<BR>इस्, इस् or ई, इ, having a large or prominent belly;<BR>pot-bellied, corpulent.<BR>—वृहत्-केतु, उस्, उस्, उ, hav-<BR>ing great clearness or brightness; (उस्), m. epithet<BR>of Agni; N. of a king.<BR>—वृहत्-क्षण, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king, (also read वृहत्-क्षय, वृहद्-<BR>रण.)<BR>—वृहत्-क्षत, अस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>mythical being.<BR>—वृहत्-क्षत्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—वृहत्-तपस्, अस्, n. great mortification;<BR>(आस्, आस्, अस्), having great devotion, very devout;<BR>(अस्), n. a particular severe penance.<BR>—वृहत्-ताल,<BR>अस्, m. Phœnix Paludosa (= हिन्ताल).<BR>—वृहत्-<BR>तिक्ता, f. the plant Clypea Hernandifolia.<BR>—वृहत्-<BR>तुहिन-शर्कर, अस्, आ, अम्, full of great pieces of<BR>ice.<BR>—वृहत्-तृण, अम्, n. strong grass, (opposed<BR>to मृदु-तृण); the bamboo cane.<BR>—वृहत्-ते-<BR>जस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having great energy.<BR>—वृहत्-तो-<BR>डल-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हत्-त्व, अम्, n. greatness, largeness, loftiness, large<BR>extent.<BR>—वृहत्-त्वच्, क्, m. the plant Alstonia<BR>Scholaris.<BR>—वृहत्-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘having large<BR>leaves,’ a species of bulbous plant; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>plant (= त्रि-पर्णिका).<BR>—वृहत्-पराशर, अस्, m.<BR>‘the larger Parāśara,’ N. of a particular recension of<BR>Parāśara's law-book.<BR>—वृहत्-पाटलि, इस्, f. the<BR>thorn-apple, Datura Metel.<BR>—वृहत्-पाद, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, large-footed; (अस्), m. the Indian fig-tree.<BR>—वृहत्-पारेवत, अम्, n. a kind of fruit tree<BR>(= महा-पारेवत).<BR>—वृहत्-पालिन्, ई, m. wild<BR>cumin.<BR>—वृहत्-पीलु, उस्, m. a kind of Pilu tree<BR>(= महा-पीलु).<BR>—वृहत्-पुष्प, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing large flowers; (ई), f. a kind of Crotolaria (=<BR>घण्टा-रवा).<BR>—वृहत्-पृष्ठ, see बृहत्-<BR>पृष्ठ.<BR>—वृहत्-प्रचेतस्, आस्, m. ‘the larger<BR>Pracetas,’ N. of a particular recension of a law-book<BR>by Pracetas.<BR>—वृहत्-प्रयोग, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—वृहत्-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having or bearing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-c" target="_blank">Page0961-c+ 81</a>]<BR>large fruit; bringing great profit or reward, great in<BR>results; (अस्), m. a species of plant, = चचेण्डा;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of Buddhist gods; (आ),<BR>f., N. of various plants (= कटु-तुम्बी; = महेन्-<BR>द्र-वारुणी; = कुष्माण्डी; = महा-जम्बू).<BR>—वृहत्-संवर्त, अस्, m. ‘the large Saṃvarta,’<BR>N. of a legal work mentioned in the Mitākṣarā or<BR>commentary on Yājña-valkya's code, (see संवर्त.)<BR>—वृहत्-संहिता, f. ‘the great composition,’ N. of<BR>an astrological work by Varāha-mihira; of a philo-<BR>sophical work.<BR>—वृहत्-सामन्, see बृहत्-सामन्.<BR>—वृहत्-सूर्य-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m. the large Sūrya-<BR>siddhānta.<BR>—वृहत्-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king; of<BR>a son of Sunakshatra; (आ), f., N. of Damayantī's<BR>nurse.<BR>—वृहत्-स्फिच्, क्, क्, क् (according to some<BR>वृहत्-स्फिज्), having large buttocks, large-hipped;<BR>(क्), m. a proper N.<BR>—वृहद्-अग्नि, इस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—वृहदग्नि-मुख, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>powder.<BR>—वृहद्-अङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम्, having large<BR>limbs, large-bodied, bulky; having many parts; (अस्),<BR>m. a large elephant (or one that is usually the<BR>leader of a wild herd).<BR>—वृहद्-अङ्गिरस्, आस्, m.<BR>‘the great Aṅgiras,’ N. of a particular recension of<BR>a law-book by Aṅgiras.<BR>—वृहद्-अत्रि, इस्, m. ‘the<BR>large Atri,’ N. of a work on medicine.<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>अभिधान-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m. the large or enlarged<BR>Abhidhāna-cintāmaṇi by Hema-candra.<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>अमर or वृहद्-अमर-कोश, अस्, m. ‘the large<BR>Amara-kośa,’ N. of a particular recension of the<BR>Amara-kośa with interpolations.<BR>—वृहद्-अम्बालिका,<BR>f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—वृहद्-अम्ल, अस्, m. the fruit tree Averrhoa<BR>Carambola.<BR>—वृहद्-अश्व, अस्, m., N. of the Ṛṣi<BR>who relates the story of Nala to Yudhi-ṣṭhira; of a<BR>king; of a son of Śrāvastaka; of a son of Saha-<BR>deva; of a Gandharva.<BR>—वृहद्-असृङ्-मति, इस्, m.<BR>‘having a great inclination for blood,’ an evil spirit,<BR>demon.<BR>—वृहद्-आत्रेय, अस्, m. ‘the large Ātreya,’<BR>N. of a work on medicine.<BR>—वृहद्-आरण्यक,<BR>see बृहद्-आरण्यक.<BR>—वृहदारण्यक-भा-<BR>ष्य, अम्, n., N. of a commentary to the Vṛhad-<BR>āraṇyaka Upaniṣad by Śaṅkarācārya, and of another<BR>by Śūreśvara.<BR>—वृहदारण्यकभाष्य-टीका, f.,<BR>N. of a commentary on the preceding work by<BR>Ānanda-jñāna.<BR>—वृहदारण्यकभाष्य-वार्त्-<BR>तिक, अम्, n., N. of a metrical commentary on Śaṅ-<BR>karācārya's Vṛhadāraṇyaka-bhāṣya by Sureśvara.<BR>—वृहदारण्यकोपनिषद्-व्याख्या (˚क-उप्˚),<BR>f., N. of a commentary on the Vṛhad-āraṇyaka<BR>Upaniṣad by Dviveda-gaṅga.<BR>—वृहद्-इषु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Ajamīḍha; of a son of Bāhyāśva<BR>or Bharmyāśva or Hary-aśva.<BR>—वृहद्-उक्थ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having loud praise,’ N. of a son of Deva-rāta;<BR>of an Agni (a son of Tapas); [cf. बृहद्-उक्थ.]<BR>—वृहद्-उक्थि, इस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi mentioned<BR>in the Vāyu-Purāṇa; (perhaps wrongly for वृहद्-<BR>उक्थ.)<BR>—वृहद्-उत्तर-तापिनी, f., N. of an Upa-<BR>niṣad.<BR>—वृहद्-एला, f. large cardamoms.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-गर्भ, a wrong reading for वृष-दर्भ.<BR>—वृहद्-गुरु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>गृह, अस्, m. ‘large-housed,’ N. of a country (=<BR>कारूष, described as lying behind the Vindhya<BR>mountains near the province of Malwa, and perhaps<BR>comprising Bandelkhand or the adjoining district;<BR>also read वृहद्-गुह, and derived from गुह,<BR>‘a cave,’ the country being mountainous and the<BR>people probably having been Troglodytes or dwellers<BR>in caves); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people (= कारू-<BR>षास्).<BR>—वृहद्-गोल, अम्, n. a water-melon.<BR>—वृहद्-गौरी-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>religious observance.<BR>—वृहद्-दर्भ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king, (also read वृहद्-भानु.)<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>दल, अस्, m. a species of Lodhra (= पट्टिका-<BR>लोध्र); Phœnix Paludosa; [cf. वृहत्-ताल.]<BR>—वृहद्-दुर्ग, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>द्युति, इस्, f. a great light, radiance, splendor.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-द्युम्न, अस्, m. and वृहद्-धनुस्, उस्, m.<BR>and वृहद्-धर्मन्, आ, m., N. of kings.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-धर्मप्रकाश, अस्, m. ‘the large Dharma-<BR>prakāśa,’ N. of a work.<BR>—वृहद्-धल (वृहत्-<BR>ह˚), अम्, n. a large plough (= हलि).<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-a" target="_blank">Page0962-a+ 81</a>]<BR>धारावली (वृहत्-हा˚), f. ‘the large Hārāvalī,’<BR>N. of a dictionary.<BR>—वृहद्-धारीत (वृहत्-हा˚),<BR>अस्, m. the large Hārīta.<BR>—वृहद्-धुस्तूर, अस्, m.<BR>a large thorn-apple.<BR>—वृहद्-धेमाद्रि (वृहत्-<BR>हे˚), इस्, m. the large Hemādri.<BR>—वृहद्-ध्वनी,<BR>f. ‘loud-sounding,’ N. of a river.<BR>—वृहद्-बल, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having great strength,’ N. of a king of Kośala;<BR>of another king (son of Deva-bhāga).<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>ब्रह्मन्, आ, m., N. of a grandson of Brahmā.<BR>—वृहद्ब्रह्मोत्तर-खण्ड (˚म-उत्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a part of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—वृहद्-भट्-<BR>टारिका, f., N. of Durgā.<BR>—वृहद्-भय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of the sons of the ninth Manu.<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>भानु, उस्, m. ‘having great brightness,’ fire or the<BR>god of fire, (see also बृहद्-भानु); an epithet of<BR>a particular Agni; N. of a son of Sattrāyaṇa and a<BR>manifestation of Viṣṇu; of a son of Kṛṣṇa; N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—वृहद्-भास, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>great splendor, clear-shining; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>grandson of Brahmā; (आ), f., N. of a daughter of the<BR>god of the sun and wife of Agni Bhānu.<BR>—वृहद्-<BR>यम, अस्, m. ‘the large Yama,’ N. of a particular<BR>recension of Yama's law-book.<BR>—वृहद्-याज्ञ-<BR>वल्क्य, अस्, m. ‘the large Yājñavalkya,’ N. of a par-<BR>ticular recension of Yājñavalkya's law-book.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-यात्रा, f., N. of a work by Varāha-mihira.<BR>—वृहद्-रण, अस्, m., N. of a king; [cf. वृहत्-<BR>क्षण.]<BR>—वृहद्-रथ, अस्, m. (see also बृहद्-<BR>रथ), ‘having a large chariot,’ epithet of Indra;<BR>N. of a man (supposed to be the same as Vāsiṣṭha,<BR>and mentioned together with Kaśyapa, Aṅgiras,<BR>Varca, and Prāṇa); N. of a king of the Māgadhas;<BR>of a son of Deva-rāta (king of the Videhas); of a son<BR>of the Vasu Upari-cara; of a son of Tigma (or Timi<BR>or Tigmātman); of a son of Bhadra-ratha; of the<BR>successor of Śaśa-dharman and last of the Maurya<BR>dynasty; a sacrificial vessel; a particular Mantra; a<BR>part of the Sāma-veda; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-राज, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—वृहद्-राज-<BR>मार्तण्ड, N. of a work mentioned in Raghu-<BR>nanda's Saṃskāra-tattva; [cf. राज-मार्तण्ड.]<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, crying loud; (ई), m. a species<BR>of small owl.<BR>—वृहद्-रूप, अस्, m., N. of a Marut.<BR>—वृहद्-रोम and वृहद्रोम-पट्टन, N. of<BR>places mentioned in the Romaka-siddhānta.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-वती, f., N. of a river; [cf. बृहद्-वत्.]<BR>—वृ-<BR>हद्-वल्क, अस्, m. a species of Lodhra (= पट्टिका-<BR>लोध्र).<BR>—वृहद्-वसिष्ठ, अस्, m. the large Va-<BR>siṣṭha.<BR>—वृहद्-वसु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—वृहद्-वात, अस्, m. a kind of plant (= अश्मरी-<BR>हर); a kind of grain, Andropogon Sorghum.<BR>—वृहद्-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, loud-speaking, boasting,<BR>a boaster.<BR>—वृहद्-वारुणी, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>महेन्द्र-वारुणी).<BR>—वृहद्-वासिष्ठ, अम्, n.<BR>the large Vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—वृहद्-विवाह-पटल, N.<BR>of a work by Varāha-mihira.<BR>—वृहद्-विष्णु, उस्,<BR>m. ‘the large Viṣṇu,’ N. of a larger recension of<BR>Viṣṇu's law-book.<BR>—वृहद्-वीज, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing large seeds; abounding in seed; (अस्), m. the<BR>plant Spondias Mangifera.<BR>—वृहद्-वृहस्पति, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a particular recension of Vṛhas-pati's law-<BR>book.<BR>—वृहद्-व्यास, अस्, m. the large Vyāsa.<BR>—वृहद्-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, observing the great<BR>vow, observing the vow of chastity.<BR>—वृहन्-नखी,<BR>f. a particular perfume (= गन्ध-सारण).<BR>—वृ-<BR>हन्-नट, अस्, m. an epithet of Arjuna; [cf. वृहन्-<BR>नल.]<BR>—वृहन्-नड, अस्, m. reed-grass, Amphi-<BR>donax Karka (= नल); an epithet of Arjuna; [cf.<BR>वृहन्-नल.]<BR>—वृहन्-नल, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>large reed, Arundo Gigantea (= महा-पोटगल);<BR>the arm; the name assumed by Arjuna when living<BR>in the family of king Virāṭa as a eunuch in female<BR>attire, (also fem., see the next.)<BR>—वृहन्-नला, f.<BR>the assumed name of Arjuna at the court of Virāṭa,<BR>(under this name Arjuna adopted a sort of woman's<BR>dress, putting on bracelets and ear-rings, and under-<BR>took as a kind of eunuch to teach dancing and music<BR>to the daughter of king Virāṭa and the other women<BR>of the palace.)<BR>—वृहन्-नारदीय, अम्, n. or वृ-<BR>हन्-नारदीय-पुराण, अम्, n. ‘the large Nāra-<BR>dīya,’ N. of one of the eighteen Purāṇas.<BR>—वृहन्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">Page0962-b+ 79</a>]<BR>नारदीय-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work mentioned<BR>in the Śakti-ratnākara.<BR>—वृहन्-नारायण or वृ-<BR>हन्-नारायणी or वृहन्-नारायणोपनिषद् (˚ण-<BR>उप्˚), त्, f. the large Nārāyaṇa Upaniṣad (treating<BR>of Vedāntic theology and forming the last Prapā-<BR>ṭhaka of the Taittirīya Āraṇyaka of the Black Yajur-<BR>veda).<BR>—वृहन्-निघण्टि, ‘the large glossary,’ N.<BR>of a dictionary.<BR>—वृहन्-निर्वाण-तन्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>‘the large Nirvāṇa-tantra,’ N. of a work mentioned<BR>in the Śakti-ratnākara.<BR>—वृहन्-निवेश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having large dimensions, large, protuberant.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हन्-नीली, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—वृहन्-नेत्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having large eyes, good-sighted, far-sighted.<BR>—वृहन्-नौका, f. epithet of a favourable position<BR>in the game of Catur-aṅga; [cf. नौकाकृष्ट.]<BR>—वृहन्-मनस्, आस्, m., N. of a grandson of<BR>Brahmā; of a king.<BR>—वृहन्-मनु, उस्, m. ‘the<BR>large Manu,’ N. of a law-book (probably the precursor<BR>of the present version, mentioned by Mādhava and<BR>other commentators).<BR>—वृहन्-मन्त्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a grandson of Brahmā.<BR>—वृहल्-लोहित, N. of a<BR>mythical tank or pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत
वृहत, अस्, m., N. of a son of the ninth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतिका
वृहतिका, f. an upper garment, mantle, wrapper;<BR>a small sort of egg-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतीपति|वृहतीपतिः
वृहती-पति. See under वृहत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्क|वृहत्कः
वृहत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, = वृहत्, large, great; (अस्<BR>or अम्), m. n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पति|वृहस्पतिः
वृहस्-पति, इस्, m. (in the earlier language more<BR>usually written बृहस्-पति, q. v.; fr. वृहस्, gen.<BR>of 3. वृह् + पति), ‘lord of increase,’ N. of the<BR>regent of the planet Jupiter and preceptor or Puro-<BR>hita of the gods, (in astronomy identified with the<BR>planet; he is regarded as the son of Aṅgiras and,<BR>like Sarasvatī, presides over speech; Tārā, who is<BR>fabled to have been carried off by Candra, is repre-<BR>sented as his wife; he is sometimes identified with<BR>Vyāsa; in the Veda his character and functions are<BR>somewhat different, and his name is there usually<BR>written Bṛhas-pati, q. v.); N. of a saint and law-<BR>giver, (sometimes written वृहसाम्-पति); N. of a<BR>philosopher; of a king (a great-grandson of Aśoka);<BR>of a king of Kaśmīra.<BR>—वृहस्पति-चक्र, अम्, n.<BR>‘cycle of Vṛhas-pati,’ the Hindū cycle of sixty years;<BR>a particular astrological diagram (shaped like a man and<BR>used for foretelling good or bad fortune).<BR>—वृहस्पति-<BR>चार, N. of the eighth Adhyāya of Varāha-mihira's<BR>Vṛhat-saṃhitā.<BR>—वृहस्पति-दत्त, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—वृहस्पति-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a commen-<BR>tator on the Raghu-vaṃśa.<BR>—वृहस्पति-वार, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Vṛhas-pati's day,’ Jupiter's day, Thursday.<BR>—वृ-<BR>हस्पति-शान्ति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—वृहस्पति-<BR>संहिता, f., N. of a short law-book (ascribed to<BR>Vṛhas-pati).<BR>—वृहस्पति-सम, अस्, आ, अम्, equal<BR>to Vṛhas-pati, like Vṛhas-pati.<BR>—वृहस्पति-सव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a particular festival or ceremony, (see<BR>बृहस्पति-सव.)<BR>—वृहस्पतिसव-प्रयोग, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a treatise on the performance of the Vṛhas-<BR>pati-sava ceremony.<BR>—वृहस्पति-सुरता, f. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—वृहस्पति-स्मृति, इस्, f. Vṛhas-pati's law-book<BR>(said to be classed among the Tāmasa works).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पतिक
वृहस्पतिक, अस्, m. (fr. वृहस्पति-दत्त), a<BR>familiar diminutive, (Pāṇ. V. 3, 83, Vārtt. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पतिय
वृहस्पतिय or वृहस्पतिल, अस्, m. = वृहस्-<BR>पतिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वॄ
वॄ वॄ = rt. वृ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वे
वे वे, cl. 1. P. A. वयति, -ते, ववौ or<BR>उवाय (2nd sing. उवयिथ, उविथ, उवाथ,<BR>3rd pl. ववुस्, ऊवुस्, ऊयुस्, Pāṇ. II. 4, 41), ववे or<BR>ऊवे or ऊये, वास्यति (also वयिष्यति), -ते, अवासीत्,<BR>अवास्त, Prec. ऊयात्, वासीष्ट, वातुम्; cl. 4. A. (=<BR>rt. ऊय्, q. v.), ऊयते, ऊयामास, ऊयिष्यते, ऊयिष्ट,<BR>ऊयितुम्, to weave, interweave, braid, plait; to string<BR>or join together artificially, make, compose (speeches,<BR>hymns, &c.); to sew; to cover: Pass. ऊयते, Aor.<BR>अवायि: Caus. वाययति (according to some वाप-<BR>यति), -ते, (ऊययति): Desid. विवासति, -ते, (ऊयि-<BR>यिषते): Intens. वावायते, वावाति or वावेति; [cf.<BR>Gr. ἤ-τριον, ὀθόνη, (probably also) ὀπέας, ἠπητής;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">Page0962-c+ 78</a>]<BR>ὑϕή, ὑϕαίνω Lat. viere, vimen, vitta: Old Germ.<BR>wât, weban: Angl. Sax. wœd, wefan, wœfels,<BR>weft, windan: Lith. u-dis, ‘texture’ (= 2. ūti);<BR>au-dziu, ‘I weave:’ Hib. fighim, ‘I weave;’ figh-<BR>te, ‘woven;’ fuaghaim, ‘I sew.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत|उतं
उत, अस्, आ, अम्, woven. See s. v., p. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊत|ऊतं
ऊत, ऊति. See s. v., p. 177.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयत्|वयन्त्
वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, weaving, sewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयिष्यत्
वयिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, Ved. about to<BR>weave, weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
वान, वानीय. See s. v., p. 903.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेम|वेमः
वेम, अस्, m. a loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेमन्
वेमन्, आ, अ, m. n. a loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेय
वेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be woven.<BR>—वेय-गान, अम्,<BR>n. a particular song-book or manual of singing giving<BR>(with the Āraṇya-gāna) the various modifications of<BR>intonation for the Ārcika division of the Sāma-veda,<BR>(the Staubhika division also has two of these song-<BR>books, viz. the Ūha-g˚ and Ūhya-g˚.)<BR>—वेय-च्छला,<BR>f., Ved., N. of a chapter of the Sāmaveda-cchalā, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेकट|वेकटः
वेकट वेकट, अस्, m. a youth; (in the<BR>drama) a buffoon (= वि-दूषक); a sort of fish<BR>(commonly called Bhekṭī); a jeweller (= वैक-<BR>टिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेकुरि
वेकुरि वेकुरि. See बेकुरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेक्ष्
वेक्ष् वेक्ष् (= rt. व्लेक्ष्), cl. 10. P. वे-<BR>क्षयति, -यितुम्, to see; [cf. अवेक्ष्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेग|वेगः
वेग वेग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. विज्), agitation,<BR>shaking, shock; impetus, impulse, momentum;<BR>impetuosity, speed, rapidity, quickness, velocity, (वे-<BR>गाद् वेगं गम्, to go from speed to speed, increase<BR>one's speed); haste, rashness, violence; onset;<BR>stream, current; blast, breeze; the flight of an arrow;<BR>any sudden impulse or transition of mind (as from<BR>passion to apathy &c.); energy, activity, force,<BR>power, strength, determination, promptitude; passion,<BR>love; pleasure, delight; external indication of any<BR>internal emotion or sensation (as convulsion, sweat,<BR>&c.); expulsion of the feces, evacuation of the natural<BR>excretions; semen virile; the fruit of a kind of<BR>mango.<BR>—वेग-तस्, ind. with speed, quickly, speedily,<BR>hastily.<BR>—वेग-नाशन, अम्, n. ‘preventing speed<BR>or activity,’ phlegm, the phlegmatic humor.<BR>—वेग-<BR>रोध, अस्, m. obstruction of speed or activity, re-<BR>tardation, check; obstruction of the movement of the<BR>bowels or of the natural excretions.<BR>—वेग-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessing velocity or activity, impetuous,<BR>rapid; quick, expeditious; agitated; (आन्), m., N.<BR>of a king; (अती), f., N. of a river; a species of<BR>metre (consisting of three anapests and a long syllable<BR>in the first Pāda, three dactyls and a spondee in the<BR>second Pāda).<BR>—वेगवत्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, speediest,<BR>quickest, very quick or swift.<BR>—वेगवत्-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, more speedy, quicker, swifter, very quick.<BR>—वेगवत्-ता, f. velocity, swiftness.<BR>—वेग-वाहिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, bearing swiftness, swift.<BR>—वेग-विधारण,<BR>अम्, n. retardation of velocity, obstruction of speed,<BR>stopping, retarding; constipation, &c.<BR>—वेग-सर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘going with speed,’ a mule; [cf. वेसर.]<BR>—वेगाघात (˚ग-आघ्˚), अस्, m. ‘speed-obstruc-<BR>tion,’ the sudden arresting of impetus or velocity,<BR>stop, check; obstruction of the natural excretions.<BR>—वेगानिल (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, m. breeze or blast caused<BR>by the velocity (of a moving object).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगित|वेगितः
वेगित, अस्, आ, अम्, impelled with speed or velocity,<BR>quickened, expedited, swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिन्
वेगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having velocity, swift, fleet, im-<BR>petuous, rapid; (ई), m. a courier, express; a hawk;<BR>(इनी), f. a river.<BR>—वेगि-ता, f. or वेगि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>impetus, velocity, quickness, speed.<BR>—वेगि-हरिण,<BR>अस्, m. an antelope (= श्री-कारी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेजित
वेजित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, frightened, terrified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेङ्कट|वेंकट|वेंकटः|वेङ्कटः
वेङ्कट वेङ्कट, N. of a mountain; of the<BR>son of Raghu-nātha-dīkṣita (author of the Viśva-<BR>guṇādarśa); of a king of Vijaya-nagara; of the<BR>author of the Śabdārtha-kalpa-taru lexicon, (his<BR>father's name was also Veṅkaṭa.)<BR>—वेङ्कट-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m. the mountain Veṅkaṭa.<BR>—वेङ्कट-नाथ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">Page0963-a+ 75</a>]<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—वेङ्कटाचलेश (˚ट-अच्˚,<BR>˚ल-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the Veṅkaṭa mountain,’<BR>epithet of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0962-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेचा
वेचा वेचा, f. (said to be fr. rt. विच्), hire,<BR>wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेजानी
वेजानी वेजानी, f. the medicinal plant Ser-<BR>ratula Anthelmintica (= सोम-राजी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेजित
वेजित वेजित. See under वेग, p. 962.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेटा
वेटा वेटा, f. the abode of the Vaiśya tribe(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेड|वेडं
वेड वेड, अम्, n. (probably fr. rt. 1. विड्),<BR>a kind of coarse sandal; (आ), f. a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेढमिका
वेढमिका वेढमिका, f. a kind of bread or<BR>cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण्
वेण् वेण्, cl. 1. P. A. वेणति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to go, move, move about; to play on an<BR>instrument, &c. (= rt. वेन्, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण|वेणः
वेण, अस्, m. (perhaps connected with वीणा and<BR>meaning ‘a lyre-player’), a musician (one by caste,<BR>the son of a Vaideha by an Amba-ṣṭhī or Amba-<BR>ṣṭha woman; see Manu X. 19, 49); N. of a Rā-<BR>jarshi or royal Ṛṣi (father of Pṛthu, and said to<BR>have perished through irreligious conduct and want<BR>of submissiveness to the Brāhmans; he is represented<BR>as having occasioned confusion of castes, see Manu<BR>VII. 41, IX. 66, 67, and as founder of the race of<BR>Niṣādas and Dhīvaras; according to the Viṣṇu-<BR>Purāṇa, Veṇa was a son of Aṅga and a descendant of<BR>the first Manu; a Veṇa Rāja-śravas is enumerated<BR>among the Veda-vyāsas or arrangers of the Veda;<BR>cf. वेन); (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणि|वेणिः
वेणि वेणि, इस्, f. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV.<BR>48. fr. rt. 1. वी, but rather fr. rt. वे), weaving, braid-<BR>ing, braided hair, a braid of hair, hair twisted into<BR>a single unornamented braid and allowed to fall on<BR>the back (as worn by widows and women whose<BR>husbands are absent, as a token of mourning; cf.<BR>एक-वेणि); the conflux or meeting of two or more<BR>rivers or streams in a common point of union (as at<BR>Prayāga or Allahabad, where the Gaṅgā, Yamunā,<BR>and Sarasvatī are supposed to unite; cf. त्रि-वेणी,<BR>प्र-याग).<BR>—वेणि-माधव, अस्, m. a particular<BR>square-shaped idol or stone image of a god at Pra-<BR>yāga.<BR>—वेणि-वेधनी, f. ‘hair-penetrating,’ a leech.<BR>—वेणि-वेधिनी, f. ‘braid-piercer,’ a comb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिका
वेणिका, f. braided hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणी
वेणी, f. braided hair, &c. = वेणि above; a stream,<BR>current; N. of a river; a sort of grass, Andropogon<BR>Serratum; a ewe.<BR>—वेणी-दास, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वेणी-बन्ध, अस्, m. the binding of the braid<BR>of mourning.<BR>—वेणी-माधव, see वेणि-माधव.<BR>—वेणी-माधव-बन्धु, उस्, m., N. of the father<BR>of Raṅga-nātha.<BR>—वेणी-संहार, अस्, m. ‘braid-<BR>seizing, hair-seizing,’ N. of a well-known drama by<BR>Bhaṭṭa-nārāyaṇa (the subject of which is an incident<BR>described in the Sabhā-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata,<BR>2229-2235, where it is narrated that after Yudhi-<BR>ṣṭhira had lost all his property, including Draupadī,<BR>to Duryodhana in gambling with dice, she was treated<BR>with great indignity by Duḥśāsana, who dragged her<BR>by her braided hair into the public assembly; Bhīma,<BR>who witnessed this insult, swore that in revenge he<BR>would one day dash Duḥśāsana to pieces and drink<BR>his blood — a threat which he fulfilled; this drama is<BR>said to be also called वेणी-संवरण, perhaps for<BR>˚-संहरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणीर|वेणीरः
वेणीर वेणीर, अस्, m. the soap-berry, Sa-<BR>pindus Detergens (= अरिष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणु|वेणुः
वेणु वेणु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 38. fr. वी substituted for rt. अज्, but probably<BR>connected with rt. वे), a bamboo; a reed; a flute,<BR>fife, pipe; N. of a king of the Yādavas.<BR>—वेणु-<BR>कर्कर, अस्, m. a species of thorny plant (= करीर,<BR>commonly called Karir or Karil).<BR>—वेणु-ज, अस्, m.<BR>bamboo seed or fruit.<BR>—वेणु-दत्त, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—वेणु-दल, अम्, n. a small shoot of a cane.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">Page0963-b+ 77</a>]<BR>—वेणु-दारि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—वेणु-दारिन्, ई,<BR>m., N. of a demon.<BR>—वेणु-ध्म, अस्, m. a flute-<BR>player, fifer, piper.<BR>—वेणु-निस्रुति, इस्, m. the sugar-<BR>cane.<BR>—वेणु-पत्त्री, f. a species of plant (= वंश-<BR>पत्त्री, हिङ्गु-पर्णी).<BR>—वेणु-यव, अस्, m. bamboo<BR>seed or fruit.<BR>—वेणु-यष्टि, इस्, m. f. a bamboo staff.<BR>—वेणु-वाद or वेणु-वादक, अस्, m. a flute-<BR>player, piper.<BR>—वेणु-वीज, अम्, n. bamboo seed.<BR>—वेणु-हय, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—वेणु-होत्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the father of king Bharga; of the<BR>father of Gārgya (according to another account).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुक|वेणुकं|वेणुकः
वेणुक, अस्, m. a goad with a bamboo handle<BR>(used for driving an elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुन|वेणुनं
वेणुन वेणुन, अम्, n. (also read वेणु-ज),<BR>black pepper (= मरिच).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत|वेतः
वेत वेत, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 118. said<BR>to be fr. rt. वे), a cane, reed, (probably a corruption<BR>of वेत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस|वेतसः
वेतस, अस्, ई, m. f. the ratan, Calamus Rotang;<BR>(अस्), m. the citron (Citrus Medica); N. of Agni;<BR>N. of a city; [cf. Gr. ἴ-τυ-ς, ἰ-τέα, οἶσος, οἶνος;<BR>Lat. vi-tex, vi-ti-s; Old Germ. wida; Angl. Sax.<BR>widhig.]<BR>—वेतस-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the leaf of the<BR>ratan; a lancet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतसिनी
वेतसिनी, f., N. of a river; [cf. वेदसिनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस्वत्|वेतस्वन्त्
वेतस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, reedy, abounding in reeds<BR>or canes (as a place, soil, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतन|वेतनं
वेतन वेतन, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 150. fr. rt. 1. वी; perhaps a corrupted form of<BR>वर्तन), hire, wages, stipend, salary; livelihood,<BR>subsistence; silver.<BR>—वेतन-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, sub-<BR>sisting by hire or wages, stipendiary.<BR>—वेतन-दान,<BR>अम्, n. the paying of wages, hiring.<BR>—वेतनादान<BR>(˚न-अद्˚), अम्, n. non-payment of wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतनिन्
वेतनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, receiving wages, stipendiary,<BR>(sometimes at the end of a comp., e. g. कुप्य-<BR>वेतनिन्, receiving very small pay.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतसु
वेतसु वेतसु, उस्, m., Ved., N. of an Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेताल|वेतालः
वेताल वेताल, अस्, m. (according to some<BR>for अव-इत + आल for आलय; according to others<BR>fr. वे, loc. c. of 2. व + ताल), a kind of ghost,<BR>spirit, goblin, vampire, demon (especially one occu-<BR>pying a dead body); a door-keeper, (in this sense pro-<BR>bably for वेत्र + आल.)<BR>—वेताल-पञ्चविंशति, इस्, or<BR>वेताल-पञ्चविंशतिका, f. a collection of twenty-five<BR>tales or fables told by a Vetāla to king Vikramāditya<BR>(of which there are three recensions extant, two by<BR>Śiva-dāsa and one by Jambhala-bhaṭṭa; versions of<BR>these popular tales exist in Hindī and almost every<BR>Hindū vernacular, as well as in Tamil and Telugu,<BR>and translations in other languages are also current).<BR>—वेताल-पञ्चविंशति-कथा, f., N. of part of the<BR>Vṛhat-kathā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्तृ
वेत्तृ 1. वेत्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. rt. 1. विद्), one<BR>who knows, knowing, understanding, acquainted<BR>with; a knower, &c.; one who obtains or acquires,<BR>obtaining; (ता), m. a sage, one who knows the<BR>nature of the soul and god; one who obtains in<BR>marriage, an espouser, husband.<BR>—वेत्तृ-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्र|वेत्रः
वेत्र वेत्र, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 166. fr. rt. 1. वी; probably rather fr. rt. वे), a<BR>reed, cane, the ratan; (अम्), n. a sort of creeper,<BR>(in this sense apparently also अस्, m.); a stick, staff;<BR>the rod or mace of an officer, staff of a door-keeper.<BR>—वेत्र-धर, अस्, m. a staff-bearer, mace-bearer;<BR>a door-keeper, warder.<BR>—वेत्र-धारक, अस्, m. a<BR>door-keeper, warder, porter; a mace-bearer.<BR>—वेत्र-<BR>पाणि, इस्, m. ‘staff-handed,’ a mace-bearer.<BR>—वेत्र-<BR>यष्टि, इस्, m. f. a staff of reed or cane.<BR>—वेत्र-लता,<BR>f. ‘reed-branch,’ a staff or stick.<BR>—वेत्र-वती, f. ‘full<BR>of reeds,’ the Betwa river (which, rising in the Vindhya<BR>mountains and following a north-easterly direction<BR>for about 340 miles, falls into the Jumnā below<BR>Kalpī); a female door-keeper; a proper N.<BR>—वेत्रा-<BR>घात (˚र-आघ्˚), अस्, m. a blow with a cane, a<BR>caning.<BR>—वेत्रासन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘cane-seat,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-c" target="_blank">Page0963-c+ 79</a>]<BR>a small cot or oblong low couch of cane work, (when<BR>furnished with bamboo sticks and a pole, it forms<BR>the common dooly or litter.)<BR>—वेत्रासनासीन (˚न-<BR>आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, seated on a seat of cane or reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रकीय|वेत्रकीयः
वेत्रकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, reedy, abounding with<BR>reeds or canes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रिन्
वेत्रिन्, ई, m. a staff-bearer, mace-bearer, porter,<BR>door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेथ्
वेथ् वेथ् (= rts. विथ्, 1. विध्), cl. 1. A.<BR>वेथते, विवेथे, वेथिष्यते, अवेथिष्ट,<BR>वेथितुम्, to ask, beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेथिलेह
वेथिलेह वेथिलेह, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद|वेदः
वेद वेद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. विद्; cf. Gr.<BR>οἶδα fr. ιδ, Lat. video fr. विद्, Goth. vait, Lith.<BR>weizd), knowing, knowledge; ‘the true knowledge,<BR>divine knowledge,’ N. of certain celebrated works<BR>which constitute the basis of the first period of the<BR>Hindū religion, (these works were originally three,<BR>viz. 1. the Ṛg-veda, 2. the Yajur-veda [of which<BR>there are, however, two divisions, see तैत्तिरीय-<BR>संहिता, वाजसनेयि-संहिता], 3. the Sāma-veda;<BR>these three works are sometimes called collectively,<BR>त्रयी, ‘the triple Vidyā’ or ‘threefold knowledge,’<BR>but the Ṛg-veda is really the only original work<BR>of the three, and much the most ancient, some of its<BR>hymns being rather Indo-European than Hindū, and<BR>representing the condition of the Āryans before their<BR>final settlement in India; subsequently a fourth Veda<BR>was added, called the Atharva-veda, which was pro-<BR>bably not completely accepted till after Manu, as his<BR>law-book often speaks of the three Vedas — calling<BR>them त्रयम् ब्रह्म सनातनम्, ‘the triple<BR>eternal Veda,’ and stating in I. 23. that the Creator<BR>drew forth the Ṛg-veda from fire, the Yajur-veda<BR>from air, and the Sāma-veda from the sun; and in<BR>another place, IV. 124, stating that the Ṛg has the<BR>gods for its deities, the Yajur has men, and the Sāma<BR>has the Pitṛs, on which account the sound of this<BR>latter is impure — but only once [XI. 33] mentions the<BR>revelation made to Atharvan and Aṅgiras, without,<BR>however, calling it by the later name of Atharva-<BR>veda, the songs and incantations of the Atharvans<BR>not being at that time recognised as a fourth Veda;<BR>each of the four Vedas has two distinct parts, viz.<BR>1. a Saṃhitā or collection of Mantras, i. e. of words<BR>of prayer and adoration often addressed either to fire<BR>or to some form of the sun or to some form of the<BR>air, sky, wind, &c., and praying for health, wealth, long<BR>life, cattle, offspring, victory, and even forgiveness of<BR>sins, which words of prayer or praise form what is<BR>usually called the Mantra portion of the Veda [see<BR>मन्त्र], and 2. a Brāhmaṇa portion consisting of<BR>Vidhi and Artha-vāda, i. e. directions for the detail<BR>of the ceremonies at which the Mantras were to be<BR>used and explanations of the legends &c. connected<BR>with the Mantras [see ब्राह्मण, विधि], both<BR>these portions being termed श्रुति, revelation orally<BR>communicated by the Deity, and heard but not com-<BR>posed or written down by men; although both portions<BR>are supposed by orthodox Hindūs to have existed<BR>from eternity, and not to require प्रमाण, ‘proof,’<BR>as they are themselves Pramāṇa, yet the oldest of<BR>the Mantras are not likely to belong to a much earlier<BR>date than the twelfth or thirteenth century B. C.;<BR>and it is certain that both Mantras and Brāhmaṇas<BR>were compositions spread over a considerable period,<BR>much of the latter being comparatively modern: as<BR>the Vedas are properly three, so the Mantras are<BR>properly of three forms, 1. Ṛc, which are verses of<BR>praise in metre, and intended for loud recitation;<BR>2. Yajus, which are in prose, and intended for use<BR>at sacrifices; 3. Sāman, which are in metre, and<BR>intended for chanting at the Soma or Moon-plant<BR>ceremonies, the Mantras of the Atharva-veda having<BR>no special name; but it must be borne in mind that<BR>the Yajur and Sāma-veda hymns, especially the latter,<BR>besides their own Mantras, borrow largely from the<BR>Ṛg-veda; the Yajur-veda and Sāma-veda being in<BR>fact not so much collections of prayers and hymns as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0964-a" target="_blank">Page0964-a+ 81</a>]<BR>special prayer and hymn-books intended as liturgical<BR>or sacrificial manuals for the Adhvaryu and Udgātṛ<BR>priests respectively, the necessity for which grew out<BR>of the vast and complicated ritual elaborated by the<BR>Āryans after they had settled down in India [see<BR>यजुर्-वेद, साम-वेद]; the more modern Atharva-<BR>veda-saṃhitā, on the other hand, is, like the Ṛg-<BR>veda, a real collection of original hymns mixed up with<BR>incantations, borrowing little from the Ṛg, having<BR>no direct relation to mere ritual or sacrifices, but<BR>supposed by mere recitation to produce long life, to<BR>cure diseases [generally in connection with the use of<BR>some plant or drug gifted with magical properties],<BR>to obtain success in love or gaming, to effect the<BR>ruin of enemies, and to secure the reciter's own pros-<BR>perity; each of the four Vedas seems to have passed<BR>through numerous Śākhās or schools, giving rise to<BR>various recensions of the text, though the Ṛg-veda<BR>is only preserved in the Śākala recension; as to<BR>arrangement, the Mantras being made up in the first<BR>instance of separate Padas or words are joined together<BR>so as to form Sūktas or hymns; the hymns of the<BR>Yajur-veda, with the exception of its last book, which<BR>is thought to be mystical, are arranged according to<BR>the sacrifices at which its Mantras were used, and<BR>those of the Sāma-veda with reference especially to<BR>the Moon-plant sacrifices, but those of the Ṛg-veda<BR>Mantras having no direct reference to sacrificial acts<BR>are arranged either according to their authors and<BR>the objects addressed or according to mere bulk;<BR>the former is the distribution into ten Maṇḍalas, the<BR>first and last three Maṇḍalas including a variety of<BR>authors or rather Ṛṣis [who are said to have seen<BR>the Vedas and not composed them], and each of the<BR>other Maṇḍalas belonging to one particular Ṛṣi;<BR>the latter is the distribution into Aṣṭakas [see मण्-<BR>डल, वर्ग]: a tradition makes Vyāsa the com-<BR>piler and arranger of the Vedas in their present<BR>form: they each have an Anukramaṇī or Index,<BR>giving the first word of every hymn, the number of<BR>verses, the name of the देवता or deified being<BR>about which the Mantra is concerned [sometimes,<BR>however, the देवता may be an inanimate object],<BR>the names and families of the authors and the metre,<BR>the principal work of this kind being the Sarvānu-<BR>kramaṇī or general Index; out of the Brāhmaṇa<BR>portion of the Veda grew two other departments of<BR>Vedic literature, sometimes included under the general<BR>name Veda, viz. the strings of aphoristic rules, called<BR>Sūtras [though these are often said to be पौरुषेय,<BR>i. e. human compositions], and the mystical treatises<BR>on the nature of God and the relation of soul and<BR>matter, called Upaniṣads, which were appended to<BR>the Āraṇyakas, certain chapters of the Brāhmaṇas so<BR>obscure and awe-inspiring in their allusions to the<BR>Supreme Spirit of the Universe that they had to be<BR>read in the solitude of forests; the most important<BR>of the former are the Kalpa-sūtras or Śrauta-sūtras<BR>as founded directly on Śruti; these strings of rules<BR>being in fact guides to the rambling discursive Brāh-<BR>maṇas and systematized directories for the due per-<BR>formance of every part of the ceremonial, while the<BR>Upaniṣads, on the other hand, taught the secret<BR>doctrine [called रहस्य in Manu II. 165. and वे-<BR>दान्त in VI. 83, 94] underlying the ceremonial, viz.<BR>the existence of one Universal Spirit, called Brahma,<BR>with which the whole creation and the human soul<BR>itself was identified; as the Śrauta-sūtras were fol-<BR>lowed by the Gṛhya and Sāmayācārika Sūtras or<BR>‘rules for domestic ceremonies and conventional cus-<BR>toms,’ which again became the forerunners of the<BR>Dharma-śāstras and thus linked the Veda with the<BR>code of Manu, so the Āraṇyakas were followed by<BR>the Upaniṣads, which latter became the real Veda of<BR>thinking Hindūs, leading to the Darśanas or systems<BR>of philosophy, and linking them also with Vedic<BR>literature: in modern writings the name of ‘fifth<BR>Veda' is accorded to the Itihāsas or legendary epic<BR>poems and the Purāṇas, and certain Upa-vedas or<BR>secondary Vedas are enumerated, that of the Ṛg-<BR>veda being the Āyur-veda or Veda on medicine, that<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0964-b" target="_blank">Page0964-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of the Yajur being the Dhanur-veda or Veda on<BR>archery, that of the Sāma being the Gāndharva-veda<BR>or Veda on music, and that of the Atharva-veda<BR>being either the Sthāpatya-veda or Artha-śāstra or<BR>Śilpa-śāstra, q. q. v. v.; the Vedāṅgas or works serv-<BR>ing as limbs [for preserving the integrity] of the<BR>Veda, of which the Kalpa-sūtras form a part, are<BR>explained under वेदाङ्ग, col. 3: the only other<BR>works included under the head of Veda being the<BR>Pariśiṣṭas, which supply rules for the ritual omitted<BR>in other works; in the Bṛhad-āraṇyaka Upaniṣad<BR>the Vedas and all the above literature are represented<BR>as the breathings of Brahmā, while in some of the<BR>Purāṇas the four Vedas are said to have been created<BR>by the four-faced Brahmā from his several mouths,<BR>and in the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa the Veda and Viṣṇu are<BR>identified); reading the Veda, (Sāy. = वेदाध्य-<BR>यन, Ṛg-veda VIII. 19, 5); comment, explana-<BR>tion; metre; epithet of Viṣṇu; obtaining, acqui-<BR>sition, wealth, = धन (Ved.); a bunch or bundle<BR>of Kuśa grass (= कुश-मुष्टि, Manu IV. 36; in<BR>this sense probably connected with वेदि, ‘an altar<BR>made of grass’); (आस्), m. pl. the Vedas, i. e. the<BR>three principal Vedas; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—वेद-<BR>कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, versed in or conversant with<BR>the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-कौलेयक, अस्, m. ‘belonging<BR>to the family of the Veda,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—वेद-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘Veda-filled,’ epithet of<BR>Brahmā; a Brāhman, man learned in the Veda.<BR>—वेद-गाम्भीर्य, अम्, n. the deep or recondite<BR>sense of the Veda.<BR>—वेद-गुप्ति, इस्, f. the preser-<BR>vation of the Vedas (by the Brāhmanical caste).<BR>—वेद-ज्ञ, अस्, m. ‘Veda-knower,’ a Brāhman<BR>skilled in the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-तत्त्व, अम्, n. ‘Veda-<BR>truth,’ the true doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-तात्-<BR>पर्य, अम्, n. the real object or true meaning of<BR>the Veda.<BR>—वेद-त्रय, अम्, ई, n. f. the three<BR>Vedas.<BR>—वेद-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘Veda-seeing,’ one<BR>who discerns the sense of the Veda, (according to<BR>Kullūka on Manu XI. 234 = वेदार्थ-ज्ञ.)<BR>—वेद-<BR>दीप, अस्, m. ‘lamp of knowledge,’ N. of Mahī-<BR>dhara's commentary on the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā.<BR>—वे-<BR>द-दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, approved of or sanctioned<BR>by the Vedas or by Vedic ritual.<BR>—वेद-धर,<BR>अस्, m. = वेदेश.<BR>—वेद-धर्म-विद्, त्, त्, त्, know-<BR>ing the Veda and the law.<BR>—वेद-नाद, अस्, m.<BR>‘Veda-sound,’ sound of chanting or repeating the<BR>Veda.<BR>—वेद-निधि, इस्, m. ‘Veda-treasure,’ N. of a<BR>priest.<BR>—वेद-निन्दक, अस्, m. ‘a Veda-reviler,’<BR>atheist, any seceder from the belief of the divine<BR>origin and character of the Vedas, unbeliever; a<BR>Jaina or Buddhist.<BR>—वेद-निन्दा, f. reviling the<BR>Vedas, heresy, unbelief, (Manu XI. 56.)<BR>—वेद-<BR>पारग, अस्, m. ‘one who has gone to the further<BR>end of the Veda,’ a Brāhman skilled in the Veda.<BR>—वेद-पुण्य, अम्, n. the sanctity or holiness of<BR>the Veda.<BR>—वेद-प्रदान, अम्, n. imparting or<BR>teaching the Veda, giving instruction in the Veda.<BR>—वेद-प्रवाद, अस्, m. a statement or declaration<BR>of the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-प्लाविन्, ई, m. one who pro-<BR>mulgates or publicly teaches the Veda.<BR>—वेद-बाहु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of a son of Pulastya.<BR>—वेद-भाष्य-<BR>कार, अस्, m. the author of a commentary on the<BR>Veda (epithet of Sāyaṇa).<BR>—वेद-मातृ, ता, f. ‘Veda-<BR>mother,’ epithet of the most sacred verse of the<BR>Veda called Gāyatrī or Sāvitrī (personified as the<BR>mother or source of the Vedas, see गायत्री).<BR>—वेद-<BR>मित्र, अस्, m. ‘friend of the Veda,’ N. of a teacher<BR>of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—वेद-मूर्ति, इस्, f. embodiment<BR>of the Veda (sometimes used as an honourable title<BR>before the names of learned Brāhmans).<BR>—वेद-<BR>मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘Veda-rooted,’ grounded on the<BR>Veda.<BR>—वेद-रक्षण, अम्, n. ‘Veda-preserva-<BR>tion,’ the preservation of the Vedas (as a duty of the<BR>Brāhmanical class).<BR>—वेद-वचन, अम्, n. a text<BR>of the Veda.<BR>—वेद-वती, f., N. of a river, (also<BR>written वेदसिनी, वेतसिनी); N. of a beautiful woman<BR>(daughter of Kuśa-dhvaja, whose story is told in the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa; she became an ascetic, and being in-<BR>sulted by Rāvaṇa in the wood where she was per-<BR>forming her penances, destroyed herself by entering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0964-c" target="_blank">Page0964-c+ 81</a>]<BR>fire, but was born again as Sītā).<BR>—वेद-वदन,<BR>अम्, n. grammar (= व्य्-आकरण).<BR>—वेद-वाक्य,<BR>अम्, n. a text of the Veda.<BR>—वेद-वास, अस्, m.<BR>‘Veda-abode,’ a Brāhman.<BR>—वेद-वाह्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, external to the Veda, not founded on the Veda<BR>(= न वेद-मूल); contrary to the Veda.<BR>—वे-<BR>द-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing the Veda, conversant with<BR>the Veda; (त्), m. a Brāhman versed in the Vedas;<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वेद-विद्वस्, आन्, m. one learned<BR>in the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-विहित, अस्, आ, अम्, taught or<BR>enjoined by the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-वृत्त, अम्, n. the<BR>doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-वृद्ध, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Muni.<BR>—वेद-वेदाङ्ग-पारग, अस्, m. well<BR>read in the Vedas and Vedāṅgas, (see पार-ग.)<BR>—वेद-व्यास, अस्, m. ‘Veda-arranger,’ epithet of<BR>Vyāsa or Bādarāyaṇa; (आस्), m. pl. the arrangers<BR>of the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-शब्द, अस्, m. a word or term<BR>in the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-शास्त्र, अम्, n. ‘Veda-ordinance,’<BR>the Veda or any Vedic composition.<BR>—वेद-शास्त्र-<BR>सम्पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, versed in the Vedas and<BR>Śāstras.<BR>—वेद-शिरस्, आस्, m., N. of a son of Mār-<BR>kaṇḍeya and Mūrdhanyā (regarded as the progenitor<BR>of the Bhārgava Brāhmans); of a son of Prāṇa; of<BR>a son of Kṛśāśva; (अस्), n. epithet of a weapon.<BR>—वेद-शीर्ष, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—वेद-<BR>श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—वेद-श्रुति, इस्, f.<BR>the hearing of the Veda.<BR>—वेद-संहिता, f. the<BR>Saṃhitā or collection of Mantras of the Veda.<BR>—वे-<BR>द-सन्न्यास, अस्, m. giving up or discontinuing the<BR>ritual of the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-सन्न्यासिक, अस्, m. or<BR>वेद-सन्न्यासिन्, ई, m. a religious mendicant (be-<BR>longing to the fourth आश्रम or order) who dis-<BR>continues the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-सम्मत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, conformable to the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-सम्-<BR>मित, अस्, आ, अम्, of equal measure with or con-<BR>formable to the Vedas.<BR>—वेद-स्तुति, इस्, f. ‘Veda-<BR>praise,’ N. of a celebrated composition.<BR>—वेदस्तुति-<BR>कारिका, f., N. of a metrical paraphrase of the pre-<BR>ceding work by Vallabhācārya (inculcating the doc-<BR>trine of faith as a means of salvation).<BR>—वेद-<BR>स्पर्श, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—वेद-स्मृता, f.,<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—वेद-स्मृति, इस्, f., N. of a river.<BR>—वेदाग्रणी (˚द-अग्˚), ईस्, f. ‘leader of the<BR>Veda’ (= सरस्वती).<BR>—वेदाङ्ग (˚द-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘a limb (for preserving the body) of the Veda,’ N.<BR>of certain works or classes of works regarded as<BR>auxiliary to and even in some sense as part of the<BR>Veda, (their object was to secure the proper pro-<BR>nunciation and correctness of the text and the right<BR>employment of the Mantras at sacrifices as taught<BR>in the Brāhmaṇas; six subjects are usually enume-<BR>rated under which these works are comprised, and<BR>six works are given as representatives of these subjects,<BR>mostly written in the Sūtra or aphoristic style, but<BR>whether all of these are the original representa-<BR>tives of the various subjects is doubtful; 1. शिक्षा,<BR>‘the science of proper articulation and pronunciation,’<BR>comprising the knowledge of letters, accents, quantity,<BR>the use of the organs of pronunciation, and phonetics<BR>generally, but especially the laws of euphony peculiar<BR>to the Veda; one short treatise consisting in one<BR>recension of thirty-five and in another of fifty-nine<BR>verses, and a chapter of the Taittirīya-āraṇyaka are<BR>regarded as the representatives of this subject; but<BR>the more modern Prātiśākhyas and other works<BR>on Vedic phonetics may be included under it, [see<BR>प्रातिशाख्य]: 2. छन्दस्, ‘metre,’ represented<BR>by a treatise ascribed to Piṅgala-nāga, which, how-<BR>ever, treats of Prākṛt as well as Sanskrit metres,<BR>and includes only a few of the leading Vedic metres:<BR>3. व्य्-आकरण, ‘linguistic analysis or grammar,’<BR>said to be represented by Pāṇini's celebrated Sūtras,<BR>but as this great work only treats of Vedic grammar<BR>exceptionally, this Vedāṅga is more properly identi-<BR>fied with the lost grammatical Sūtras which preceded<BR>Pāṇini: 4. निर्-उक्त, ‘explanation of difficult Vedic<BR>words,’ represented by the Nirukta of Yāska, which<BR>consists of five chapters of mere lists of words, three<BR>belonging to the Naighaṇṭuka section of synonyms,<BR>one to the Naigama of separate words, and one<BR>to the Daivata of divinities and the other objects<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-a" target="_blank">Page0965-a+ 81</a>]<BR>addressed in the Mantras; after which come twelve<BR>chapters of explanation with an introduction, to which<BR>is also added a Pariśiṣṭa of two other chapters, [see<BR>यास्क]: 5. ज्योतिष, ‘astronomy,’ or rather the<BR>Vedic calendar, represented by a small tract in a<BR>more modern style than the Sūtra works, the object<BR>of which is to fix the most auspicious days for sacri-<BR>fices: 6. कल्प, ‘ceremonial,’ represented by a large<BR>number of Sūtra works intended to systematize the<BR>tedious and confused ritualistic precepts of the Brāh-<BR>maṇas; each of the Vedas has its own Kalpa or<BR>Śrauta Sūtras, [see सूत्र and cf. वेद, p. 963]:<BR>the first and second of these Vedāṅgas is said to<BR>be intended to secure the correct reading or recitation<BR>of the Veda, the third and fourth the understanding<BR>of it, and the fifth and sixth its proper employment<BR>at sacrifices: the Vedāṅgas are alluded to by Manu,<BR>who calls them, in III. 184, Pravacanas, ‘expo-<BR>sitions,’ a term which is said to be also applied to<BR>the Brāhmaṇas.)<BR>—वेदाङ्गिन्, ई, m. one who studies<BR>or teaches the Vedāṅgas.<BR>—वेदादि (˚द-आदि), n.<BR>or वेदादि-वर्ण (˚द-आद्˚), अस्, m. or वेदादि-वीज<BR>(˚द-आद्˚), अम्, n. the first syllable of the Veda or<BR>the mystical name of God, the sacred syllable ॐ.<BR>—वेदाधिगम (˚द-अध्˚), अस्, m. the going over<BR>or study of the Vedas.<BR>—वेदाधिप (˚द-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>or वेदाधिपति (˚द-अध्˚), इस्, m. ‘one who presides<BR>over the Veda,’ a term applied to certain of the<BR>planets, (thus the Ṛg-veda is said to be presided<BR>over by the planet Jupiter or Bṛhas-pati, the Yajur-<BR>veda by Venus, the Sāma-veda by Mars, and the<BR>Atharva-veda by Mercury.)<BR>—वेदाध्ययन (˚द-<BR>अध्˚), अम्, n. the going over or study of the Vedas.<BR>—वेदाध्ययिन् or वेदाध्यायिन् (˚द-अध्˚), ई, m.<BR>one who studies the Veda.<BR>—वेदाध्यापक (˚द-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. one who causes to go over or study<BR>the Veda, a teacher of the Vedas.<BR>—वेदाध्यापन<BR>(˚द-अध्˚), अम्, n. the causing to go over the Vedas,<BR>teaching the Vedas.<BR>—वेदान्त (˚द-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘end of the Veda,’ N. of the second and most im-<BR>portant part of the Mīmāṃsā or third of the three<BR>great divisions of Hindū philosophy (so called either<BR>as teaching the ultimate aim and scope of the Veda<BR>or simply as founded on the Upaniṣads which come<BR>at the end of the Veda; this system, although be-<BR>longing to the Mīmāṃsā school [see मीमांसा] and<BR>sometimes called Uttara-mīmāṃsā, ‘examination of<BR>the later portion or ज्ञान-काण्ड of the Veda,’<BR>i. e. of that portion contained in the Āraṇyakas and<BR>Upaniṣads [which teach the knowledge of Brahma or<BR>the Universal Spirit], stands out prominently by itself<BR>as representing the popular pantheistic creed of the<BR>Hindūs of the present day, which is really based on<BR>the Upaniṣads and constitutes the true Veda of<BR>the modern cultivated Brāhman, underlying also<BR>all the polytheism and multiform mythology of<BR>the people; it explains the universe synthetically<BR>as a development from one principle, and so<BR>differs from the analytical Nyāya which treats of<BR>the various objects constituting the material world<BR>as it finds them, without investigating their mutual<BR>relation of effect and cause, and from the Sāṅkhya<BR>which, although also synthetic, propounds a duality<BR>of principles to account for the visible universe;<BR>according to the Vedānta doctrine, Brahma [nom.<BR>neut. of ब्रह्मन्] or the Supreme Soul, also called<BR>Paramātman, is both the efficient and material cause<BR>of the world; the Ātman or individual human soul,<BR>as well as all the phenomena of nature, being really<BR>identical with the Paramātman, and their existence<BR>being only the result of Ajñāna or an assumed igno-<BR>rance on the part of this Supreme Soul, who is<BR>described as both Creator and Creation, Actor and<BR>Act, Existence, Knowledge, Joy, and as devoid of<BR>the three qualities, [see गुण]; the liberation of the<BR>human soul, its deliverance from transmigrations, and<BR>re-union with the Paramātman, with which it is<BR>really identified, is only to be effected by a removal<BR>of that ignorance which prevents the consciousness<BR>of this identity and by a proper understanding of the<BR>truth of the Vedānta; this system is also sometimes<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">Page0965-b+ 81</a>]<BR>called Brahma-mīmāṃsā and Śārīraka-mīmāṃsā, ‘in-<BR>vestigation of the embodied soul:’ the founder of the<BR>school is said to have been Vyāsa, also called Bādarā-<BR>yaṇa, and its most eminent teacher was Śaṅkarā-<BR>cārya); (आस्), m. pl. the Upaniṣads (see Kullūka on<BR>Manu VI. 83), works on the Vedānta philosophy.<BR>—वेदान्त-कल्पतरु, उस्, m., N. of a work by<BR>Amalānanda Vyāsāśrama.<BR>—वेदान्त-कल्पलतिका,<BR>f., N. of a work by Madhu-sūdana-sarasvatī.<BR>—वे-<BR>दान्त-ग or वेदान्त-ज्ञ, अस्, m. a follower or<BR>knower of the Vedānta.<BR>—वेदान्त-प्रदीप, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a commentary by Rāmānuja on the Bā-<BR>darāyaṇa-sūtra.<BR>—वेदान्त-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a work by Vyāsa-tīrtha.<BR>—वेदान्त-सार, अस्, m.<BR>‘essence or epitome of the Vedānta,’ N. of a treatise<BR>on the Vedānta by Sadānanda; of a commentary on<BR>the Vedānta-sūtra by Rāmānujācārya; [cf. वेदान्त-<BR>प्रदीप.]<BR>—वेदान्त-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>aphorisms of the Vedānta philosophy ascribed to<BR>Bādarāyaṇa or Vyāsa, (these aphorisms are also called<BR>Brahma-sūtra and Śārīraka-sūtra.)<BR>—वेदान्ताचार्य<BR>(˚त-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author of a commentary<BR>on the Guṇa-ratna-kośa.<BR>—वेदान्ताभिहित (˚त-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, declared in the Upaniṣads or in<BR>the Vedānta.<BR>—वेदान्तिन्, ई, m. a follower of the<BR>Vedānta philosophy.<BR>—वेदान्तोपगत (˚त-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, derived from or produced by the Vedānta.<BR>—वेदाभ्यास (˚द-अभ्˚), अस्, m. study of the<BR>Veda; the repetition of the mystical syllable ॐ.<BR>—वेदार्थ (˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m. the meaning or<BR>sense of the Veda.<BR>—वेदार्थ-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who knows the meaning of the Veda.<BR>—वेदार्थ-<BR>प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of Sāyaṇa's commentary on<BR>the Ṛg-veda; of a commentary on the Taittirīya-<BR>saṃhitā by Mādhava.<BR>—वेदार्थ-सङ्ग्रह, N. of<BR>a work by Rāmānuja.<BR>—वेदावतार (˚द-अव्˚), अस्,<BR>m. descent of the Veda, revelation of the Veda,<BR>handing down of the Veda.<BR>—वेदाश्वा (˚द-अश्˚),<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR>—वेदेश (˚द-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the Veda,’ a proper N.<BR>—वेदेश-भिक्षु, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the Padārtha-kaumudī commen-<BR>tary.<BR>—वेदोक्त (˚द-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taught or<BR>declared in the Vedas, scriptural.<BR>—वेदोदय (˚द-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘origin of the Veda,’ epithet of Sūrya<BR>or the Sun, (the Sāma-veda being said to have pro-<BR>ceeded from the Sun, Manu 1. 23.)<BR>—वेदोदित<BR>(˚द-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taught or declared in the<BR>Vedas, scriptural.<BR>—वेदोपकरण (˚द-उप्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘Veda-instrument,’ a subordinate science for aiding<BR>or supporting the Veda (= वेदाङ्ग, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0963-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदन|वेदनं
वेदन, अम्, आ, n. f. perception, knowledge;<BR>knowledge obtained by the senses, feeling, sensation;<BR>obtaining, acquisition, property, wealth; presenting,<BR>delivering; marrying, marriage; the marriage of a<BR>Śūdra woman with a man of a higher caste, (see<BR>Manu III. 44; cf. उत्कृष्ट-व्˚); the ceremony<BR>of holding the ends of a mantle (observed by a<BR>Śūdra female on her marriage with a man of a<BR>higher caste); (ई), f. the true skin or cutis; (आ), f.<BR>pain, torment, smart, agony; Pain or Torture (per-<BR>sonified as a daughter of An-ṛta).<BR>—वेदना-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of pain, full of aches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनीय
वेदनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be perceived, perceptible;<BR>capable of being felt; to be known or understood;<BR>to be made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदय
1. वेदय, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what knows, know-<BR>ing; who or what obtains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदयान
वेदयान, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to know, making<BR>known, telling, (अ-वेदयान, not informing.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदस्
वेदस्, आस्, m. the Vedas collectively; (अस्), n.<BR>acquisition, wealth (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदस
वेदस in सर्व-वेदस, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदापय
वेदापय, Nom. P. वेदापयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to know, impart knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदि|वेदिः
वेदि, इस्, or वेदी, f. (in Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa I. 2,<BR>5, 7. said to be fr. rt. 1. विद्, ‘to acquire;’ but per-<BR>haps connected with rt. वे, ‘to weave or bind to-<BR>gether’), an altar or raised place made of Kuśa grass<BR>or strewed with it and prepared for an oblation for<BR>placing the vessels used at a sacrifice, a place or<BR>ground prepared for sacrifice, (it is more or less<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">Page0965-c+ 78</a>]<BR>raised and of various shapes); an altar (in general);<BR>a quadrangular spot in the court-yard of a temple or<BR>palace (usually furnished with a raised floor or seat<BR>and covered with a roof supported by pillars, = वि-<BR>तर्दि); a bench; a seal-ring; N. of Sarasvatī<BR>(wife of Brahmā); (इस्), m. a teacher, Paṇḍit.<BR>—वेदि-जा, f. ‘altar-born,’ epithet of Draupadī, wife<BR>of the Pāṇḍu princes, (the fee which Droṇa required<BR>for instructing the Pāṇḍu princes was that they should<BR>conquer Drupada, king of Pañcāla, who had insulted<BR>him; they therefore took him prisoner, and he,<BR>burning with resentment, undertook a sacrifice to<BR>procure a son who might avenge his defeat; two<BR>children were then born to him from the midst of<BR>the altar, out of the sacrificial fire, viz. a son Dhṛṣṭa-<BR>dyumna, and a daughter Draupadī or Kṛṣṇā, after-<BR>wards wife of the Pāṇḍavas.)<BR>—वेदि-प्रतिष्ठ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, erected on sacrificial ground.<BR>—वेदि-<BR>मेखला, f. the boundary cord of a sacrificial ground.<BR>—वेदि-वत्, ind. like the sacrificial altar.<BR>—वेदीश<BR>(˚दि-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the Vedi,’ epithet of Agni;<BR>of Brahmā (as husband of Sarasvatī).<BR>—वेद्य्-अन्त,<BR>अस्, m. the end of the Vedi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिका
वेदिका, f. ground prepared for sacrificial cere-<BR>monies, a kind of altar; a quadrangular open shed<BR>in the middle of a court-yard (erected for various<BR>purposes and furnished with a seat, = वि-तर्दि); an<BR>arbour; a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदित|वेदितः
वेदित, अस्, आ, अम्, make known, represented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदितव्य|वेदितव्यं
वेदितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be known or ascertained;<BR>to be made known, to be explained or expounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदितृ
वेदितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, knowing; a knower, &c.;<BR>wise, learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिन्
वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, knowing, acquainted with; es-<BR>pousing, marrying (e. g. शूद्रा-वेदी, a man who<BR>marries a Śūdra woman); (ई), m. a knower; a<BR>teacher; a learned Brāhman; Brahmā; (इ), n. a kind<BR>of plant (= अम्ब-ष्ठा).<BR>—वेदि-ता, f. or वेदि-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. knowledge, wisdom, learning, experience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदी
वेदी, f. = वेदि, an altar, &c. (See col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदीयस्
वेदीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. one who is wiser or very<BR>wise, (Sāy. = अतिशयेन विद्वस्, Ṛg-veda VII. 98, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद्य|वेद्यं
1. वेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be known or ascertained;<BR>to be made known; to be explained or taught; to<BR>be espoused or married; bringing or causing wealth<BR>(Ved., Sāy. = धन-हित, लाभ-हेतु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद्य|वेद्यं
2. वेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or agreeable to the<BR>Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदण्ड|वेदंड|वेदंडः|वेदण्डः
वेदण्ड वेदण्ड, अस्, m. (a doubtful word),<BR>an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमुख्या
वेदमुख्या वेदमुख्या, f. (a doubtful word,<BR>cf. वेध-मुख्य), a sort of insect, the winged bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसिनी
वेदसिनी वेदसिनी, f., N. of a river, (also<BR>written वेद-वती, वेतसिनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदार|वेदारः
वेदार वेदार, अस्, m. a chameleon; a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध|वेधः
वेध वेध, अस्, m. (fr. rt. व्यध्), penetra-<BR>tion, piercing, breaking through, perforation; punc-<BR>turing, wounding, wound; hole, excavation; the<BR>depth of any excavation, depth (in measurement); a<BR>particular measure or division of time (= 100 Truṭis).<BR>—वेध-मुख्य, अस्, m. a kind of Curcuma, =<BR>कर्चूर; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= कस्तूरी).<BR>—वे-<BR>ध-मुख्यक, अस्, m. zedoary, Curcuma Zerum-<BR>bet (= हरिद्रा, द्राविडक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद्धृ
वेद्धृ, धा, m. a piercer, perforator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधक|वेधकं|वेधकः
वेधक, अस्, आ, or इका, अम्, piercing, perforating,<BR>a piercer or perforator (of gems); sharp; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of one of the divisions of Naraka; camphor;<BR>(अम्), n. grain, rice in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधन|वेधनं
वेधन, अम्, n. the act of piercing, perforation;<BR>penetration, excavation; puncturing, pricking; wound-<BR>ing; a thrust; depth (in measurement); (ई), f. an<BR>instrument for piercing an elephant's ear; a small<BR>gimblet (for perforating gems, shells, &c.); an auger,<BR>gimblet, piercing instrument (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधनिका
वेधनिका, f. a sharp-pointed perforating instru-<BR>ment (used especially for piercing jewels or shells),<BR>an auger, awl, gimblet, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधनीय
वेधनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, capable of being pierced,<BR>penetrable, vulnerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधित|वेधितः
वेधित, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced, perforated, pene-<BR>trated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधिन्
वेधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, piercing, stabbing, perforating;<BR>hitting (a mark); (इनी), f. a leech.<BR>—वेधि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. capacity of piercing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध्य|वेध्यं
वेध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pierced or perforated;<BR>(अम्), n. a mark for shooting at, butt, target.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस्
वेधस् वेधस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 224. fr. वेध् substituted for वि-धा),<BR>arranging, creating; wise, learned (= मेधाविन्,<BR>Naigh. III. 15); (आस्), m. an arranger, disposer,<BR>creator, (कु-वेधस्, आस्, m. ‘evil creator,’ evil des-<BR>tiny); N. of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of the<BR>Sun; of Soma; a wise or learned man; a priest; a<BR>poet, Vedic Ṛṣi.<BR>—वेधस्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>most wise, wisest, (Sāy. = अतिशयेन मेधाविन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस|वेधसं
वेधस, अम्, n. the part of the hand under the<BR>root of the thumb (considered as sacred to Brahmā,<BR>see तीर्थ); (अस्), m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi (said to<BR>belong to the family of Aṅgiras).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस्या
वेधस्या, f., Ved. a desire of performing sacri-<BR>fices, (Sāy. = याग-विधानेच्छा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्
वेन् वेन् (also written वेण्, q. v.), cl. 1.<BR>P. A. वेनति, -ते, विवेन, विवेने, वेनि-<BR>तुम्, to go, move; to move about, circulate (Ved.,<BR>cf. वेनस्); to care for, be anxious for, wish, desire,<BR>love, favour (Ved.); to praise, worship (Ved.); to<BR>know, perceive, discern, recognise, reflect; to take;<BR>to play on an instrument: Caus. वेनयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अविवेनत्: Desid. विवेनिषति, -ते: Intens. वे-<BR>वेन्यते, वेवेन्ति; [cf. Gr. αἰνέω, αἴνη.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन|वेनः
वेन, अस्, m., Ved. a friend, lover, (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 63, 1 = कान्त); a knower,<BR>discerner, wise man; = यज्ञ (Naigh. III. 17); a<BR>priest; N. of the Sun; of Prajā-pati or Brahmā; of<BR>a son of Aṅga, (also written वेण, q. v.); of the<BR>author of the hymns Ṛg-veda IX. 85, X. 123 (hav-<BR>ing the patronymic Bhārgava); (आ), f. a loved one;<BR>N. of the wife of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेनत्
वेनत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. wishing, desiring, de-<BR>sirous; (अन्), m. a suppliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेनस्
वेनस्, अस्, n., Ved. circulation (of the vital airs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेनि
वेनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. loving, desiring, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 41, 3. वेनीः = कामय-<BR>मानाः प्रजाः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्य
वेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be loved or adored,<BR>adorable; (अस्), m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi; [cf. वैन्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्ना
वेन्ना वेन्ना, f. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 8.<BR>fr. rt. वन्), N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेप्
वेप् वेप् (connected with the Caus. of<BR>rt. 1. वी), cl. 1. A. वेपते (ep. also P. वे-<BR>पति), विवेपे, वेपिष्यते, वेपितुम्, to tremble,<BR>shake, move about, quiver: Caus. वेपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to tremble or move; [cf. Lat. vibrare;<BR>Old Germ. weibon, weibjan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपथु|वेपथुः
वेपथु, उस्, m. trembling, tremor.<BR>—वेपथु-<BR>परीत, अस्, आ, अम्, seized with or affected by tremor.<BR>—वेपथु-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, possessing tremor, trem-<BR>bling.<BR>—वेपथु-मत्, अन्, अती, अत्, possessed of<BR>tremor, trembling, quaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपन|वेपनं
वेपन, अम्, n. tremor, trembling; the discharg-<BR>ing of a bow, (in this sense perhaps to be connected<BR>with Caus. of rt. 1. वी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपमान
वेपमान, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, shaking, quiver-<BR>ing, quaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपयत्
वेपयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to tremble or quake,<BR>agitating; driving away, dispelling, (probably con-<BR>nected with Caus. of rt. 1. वी; according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 12, 2 = तमांसि वर्जयत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपस्
वेपस्, अस्, n. trembling, tremor, (Sāy. = वेपन);<BR>act, activity, energy (enumerated among the कर्म-<BR>नामानि in Naigh. II. 1); = अनवद्य (according<BR>to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपी
वेपी, in Ṛg-veda VI. 22, 5. perhaps ‘accom-<BR>panied with ceremonial acts,’ (Sāy. = वेपस्, i. e. या-<BR>गादि-लक्षणं कर्म तद्-वती.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेम|वेमः
वेम वेम, वेमन्, वेय. See under rt. वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेर|वेरं|वेरः
वेर वेर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>वी), the body; the egg-plant (= वार्ताक); saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरक|वेरकं|वेरकः
वेरक, अम्, n. camphor (= कर्पूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरट|वेरटः
वेरट वेरट, अस्, m. a low man, one of<BR>a mixed or inferior caste; (अम्), n. the fruit of<BR>the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्
वेल् 1. वेल् (rather to be regarded as a<BR>Nom. fr. वेला below), cl. 10. P. वेल-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to count or declare the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्
वेल् 2. वेल् or वेल्ल् (also written वेह्ल्),<BR>cl. 1. P. वेलति or वेल्लति, &c., to go,<BR>move; to shake about, tremble, move about, move<BR>round; to be wanton; [cf. perhaps Gr. εἴλω, ελύω;<BR>Lat. volvo; Old Germ. wuoljan; Goth. valvjan;<BR>Angl. Sax. willian, wœltan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल|वेलं|वेलः
वेल, अम्, n. a garden, grove; (आ), f. time, season,<BR>(वेलायाम्, seasonably); opportunity, interval, leisure;<BR>tide, flow, stream, current; the coast, sea-shore,<BR>(वेलायाम्, on the sea-shore, coast-wise); boundary,<BR>limit; speech; passion, emotion, feeling; easy or<BR>painless death (= अक्लिष्ट-मरण); sickness, dis-<BR>ease, (according to Śabda-k. = राग-स्थाने रोगः);<BR>the gums; the food of Śiva (= ईश्वरस्य भोजनम्);<BR>N. of a daughter of Meru and wife of Samudra; of<BR>the wife of Budha.<BR>—वेलाकुल (˚ला-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>agitated by the tide.<BR>—वेला-कूल, अम्, n. ‘stream-<BR>bank,’ N. of a district (the modern Tāmalipta or<BR>Tumlook, see ताम-लिप्त; said to be in the district<BR>of Midnapore or in the southern part of the present<BR>Hūglī district, forming the west bank of the Hūglī<BR>river at its union with the sea; a village called Beer-<BR>cool, said to be derived from Velā-kūla, is still found<BR>near the sea-shore).<BR>—वेला-मूल, अम्, n. the sea-<BR>shore.<BR>—वेला-वन, अम्, n. a wood on a shore or<BR>sea-coast.<BR>—वेलावली (˚ला-आव्˚), f., N. of a particular<BR>scale in Hindū music.<BR>—वेला-वित्त, अस्, m. (thought<BR>to be) a kind of judicial office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्ल|वेल्लं|वेल्लः
वेल्ल, अस्, m. going, moving; shaking; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a particular plant (the seed of which is used as<BR>a vermifuge (= विडङ्ग).<BR>—वेल्ल-ज, अम्, n. black<BR>pepper, Piper Nigrum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लन|वेल्लनं
वेल्लन, अम्, n. going, shaking; rolling on the<BR>ground (as a horse &c.); a sort of rolling-pin with<BR>which cakes &c. are prepared; (ई), f. a species of<BR>Dūrvā grass (= माला-दूर्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लन्तर|वेल्लन्तरः
वेल्लन्तर, अस्, m. a particular tree (= वीर-तरु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लहल|वेल्लहलः
वेल्लहल, अस्, m. a libertine (= केलि-नागर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लि|वेल्लिः
वेल्लि, इस्, f. a creeping plant; [cf. वल्लि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लिका
वेल्लिका or वेल्लिकाख्या (˚का-आख्˚), f. a plant<BR>(commonly called Bel Suṇṭh).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लित|वेल्लितं|वेल्लितः
वेल्लित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, trembling, tremulous;<BR>crooked; (अम्), n. going, moving; shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलिभुक्प्रिय|वेलिभुक्प्रियः
वेलिभुक्प्रिय वेलिभुक्-प्रिय, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of fragrant mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेविजान
वेविजान वेविजान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. 1. विज्), intimidating, terrifying, (Sāy. = भी-<BR>षयत्, Ṛg-veda IV. 26, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेविदान
वेविदान वेविदान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. 1. विद्), Ved. knowing or finding out most<BR>effectually; obtaining very much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेविषत्
वेविषत् वेविषत्, अत्, अती, अत् (fr. rt. 2. विष्),<BR>Ved. engaged in sacred rites, (Sāy. वेविषतः =<BR>कर्माणि प्राप्नुवन्तः, Ṛg-veda VI. 21, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेविषाण
वेविषाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. contending with, (Sāy.<BR>= युद्धार्थं सङ्गत, Ṛg-veda VII. 18, 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेवी
वेवी वेवी (perhaps to be regarded as<BR>an Intens. of rt. 1. वी, q. v.), cl. 2. A.<BR>वेवीते (Ved. also P. वेवेति, 3rd pl. A. वेव्यते), &c.,<BR>to go; to pervade, obtain; to conceive or become<BR>pregnant; to wish, desire, love; to throw, cast, hurl;<BR>to eat, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्
वेश् वेश्. See under rt. 1. वेस्, p. 967.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश|वेशः
वेश वेश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. विश्), entrance,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">Page0966-c+ 76</a>]<BR>ingress, access; a house, dwelling, abode; a house of<BR>prostitutes; a neighbour (Ved., Sāy. = प्रतिवेश्य, Ṛg-<BR>veda IV. 3, 13); dress, apparel; ornament, decora-<BR>tion [cf. वेष]; disguise, masquerade; [cf. Gr.<BR>οἶκο-ς, οἰκά-α; Lat. vicu-s, vic-inu-s; Goth. veihs;<BR>Angl. Sax. wic.]<BR>—वेश-दान, अस्, m. the sunflower<BR>(= सूर्य-शोभा).<BR>—वेश-धारिन्, ई, m. ‘wearing a<BR>disguise,’ a hypocrite, false devotee.<BR>—वेश-भृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, wearing dress or ornament, dressed, adorned;<BR>disguised.<BR>—वेश-वाट, अम्, n. house and court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशक|वेशकः
वेशक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, who or what enters, en-<BR>tering; (अस्), m. a house; (इका), f. entrance, ingress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशन|वेशनं
वेशन, अम्, n. the act of entering; a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशन्त|वेशंत|वेशंतः|वेशन्तः
वेशन्त, अस्, m. a basin, pool, small pond; a kind<BR>of ladle or basin for holding Soma (Ved., cf. वै-<BR>शन्त); fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशस|वेशसः
वेशस in यज्ञ-वेशस, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशि
वेशि, in astronomy = φάσις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशिन्
वेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a dress, dressed, assuming<BR>a particular dress or form; [cf. सर्व-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मन्
वेश्मन्, अ, n. a house, dwelling, abode, mansion; a<BR>palace; N. of the fourth astrological house.<BR>—वेश्म-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. house-building.<BR>—वेश्म-कलिङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘house-kaliṅga,’ a kind of sparrow (= च-<BR>टक).<BR>—वेश्म-कूल, अस्, m. a kind of creeper (=<BR>चचेण्डा).<BR>—वेश्म-नकुल, अस्, m. the musk rat or<BR>shrew.<BR>—वेश्म-भू, ऊस्, f. building-ground, ground<BR>suitable for a house, the site of a habitation.<BR>—वेश्म-<BR>स्थूणा, f. the main post or column of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्य|वेश्यं
वेश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be entered, to be occupied,<BR>accessible; (अम्), n. a habitation, abode, (Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 61, 14 = प्रवेशन); the habitation<BR>of harlots; (आ), f. a courtezan, harlot, prostitute,<BR>(sometimes written वेष्या); the plant Cissampelos<BR>Hexandra; a particular metre.<BR>—वेश्या-गण, अस्, m.<BR>a company of harlots.<BR>—वेश्या-गमन, अम्, n.<BR>going after prostitutes, debauchery.<BR>—वेश्या-गामिन्,<BR>ई, m. one who visits prostitutes, a whoremonger.<BR>—वेश्या-गृह, अम्, n. ‘harlot-house,’ a brothel.<BR>—वेश्याचार्य (˚या-आच्˚), अस्, m. the master or<BR>keeper of prostitutes or dancing girls, &c.; a pimp; a<BR>catamite.<BR>—वेश्या-जन, अस्, m. a courtezan.<BR>—वेश्या-<BR>जन-समाश्रय, अस्, m. a habitation of courtezans,<BR>brothel.<BR>—वेश्या-पण, अस्, m. reward or wages<BR>given to a harlot.<BR>—वेश्या-पति, इस्, m. the husband<BR>of a courtezan.<BR>—वेश्या-वार, अस्, m. a number or<BR>company of harlots.<BR>—वेश्याश्रय (˚या-आश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a habitation of harlots, abode of courtezans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशर|वेशरः
वेशर वेशर, अस्, m. (also written वेसर,<BR>q. v.), a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्वर|वेश्वरः
वेश्वर, अस्, m. a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशवार|वेशवारः
वेशवार वेशवार, अस्, m. = वेसवार, a kind<BR>of condiment or seasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेषवार|वेषवारः
वेषवार = वेशवार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशीजाता
वेशीजाता वेशीजाता, f. a kind of creeper<BR>(= पुत्र-दात्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्वर|वेश्वरः
वेश्वर वेश्वर, अस्, m. See वेशर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष|वेषः
वेष वेष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. विष्), dress, ap-<BR>parel [cf. वेश]; ornament, decoration; (in Naigh.<BR>II. 1. वेषः, or according to another reading वेशः,<BR>is enumerated among the कर्म-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेषण|वेषणं|वेषणः
वेषण, अस्, m. the shrub Cassia Sophora, = कास-<BR>मर्द; (आ), f. the plant Flacourtia Cataphracta, =<BR>वितुन्न; (अम्), n. occupation, possession, entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्य|वेष्यः
वेष्य, अस्, m. water [cf. वेष्प]; (आ), f. a<BR>courtezan, harlot, (for वेश्या.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्क
वेष्क वेष्क, अस्, m. (perhaps fr. rt. 2. विष्),<BR>Ved. a noose for strangling a sacrificial victim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट्
वेष्ट् वेष्ट्, cl. 1. A. वेष्टते, विवेष्टे,<BR>वेष्टिष्यते, वेष्टितुम्, to surround, en-<BR>close, encompass, envelop, encircle, wind or twist round<BR>or about, wrap round; to dress: Caus. वेष्टयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अविवेष्टत् and अववेष्टत्, to surround,<BR>encompass; to twist about; to invest, blockade: De-<BR>sid. विवेष्टिषते: Intens. वेवेष्ट्यते, वेवेष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट|वेष्टः
वेष्ट, अस्, m. surrounding, enclosing; an enclosure,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">Page0967-a+ 75</a>]<BR>fence; a turban; a kind of knot (Ved.); exudation,<BR>gum; resin in general; turpentine.<BR>—वेष्ट-वंश,<BR>अस्, m. a sort of bamboo, Bambusa Spinosa.<BR>—वेष्ट-<BR>सार, अस्, m. turpentine (= श्री-वेष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टक|वेष्टकं|वेष्टकः
वेष्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, surrounding, encompassing;<BR>a surrounder; anything which encompasses or en-<BR>closes or invests; (अम्), n. a turban; a wrapper;<BR>exudation, resin, gum, &c.; turpentine; (अस्), m. an<BR>enclosure, wall, fence; a pumpkin-gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टन|वेष्टनं
वेष्टन, अम्, n. the act of surrounding or en-<BR>compassing or enclosing or encircling, (अङ्गुलि-व्˚,<BR>that which invests or encircles the fingers, a finger<BR>ring); grasping; anything that surrounds or encom-<BR>passes; an envelope, wrapper; an enclosure, fence,<BR>wall; a turban, garland, tiara, diadem; a girdle; a<BR>bandage, band; a covering, case; the outer ear<BR>(i. e. the meatus auditorius and concha); a particular<BR>attitude in dancing, (either a disposition of the hands<BR>or crossing of the feet); bdellium.<BR>—वेष्टन-वेष्-<BR>टक, अस्, m. a particular attitude of the sexes in<BR>coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टनक|वेष्टनकः
वेष्टनक, अस्, m. a particular position in coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टनीय
वेष्टनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be surrounded or en-<BR>closed, to be wrapped or wound round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टयत्
वेष्टयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, surrounding, encompassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टयित्वा
वेष्टयित्वा, ind. having bound round, having<BR>encompassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टित|वेष्टितं|वेष्टितः
वेष्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded, encompassed,<BR>enclosed, encircled, enveloped, bound or wound<BR>round, wrapped up; dressed; invested; impeded,<BR>stopped, blocked, secured from access; (अम्), n. en-<BR>compassing, encircling; one of the gestures or atti-<BR>tudes of dancing, (a particular motion of the fingers<BR>or a crossing of the feet.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टितव्य
वेष्टितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be surrounded or<BR>encompassed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट्य
वेष्ट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = वेष्टितव्य above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्प|वेष्पः
वेष्प वेष्प, अस्, m. water; [cf. वाष्प.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्य|वेष्यः
वेष्य वेष्य. See under वेष, p. 966.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेस्
वेस् 1. वेस्, cl. 1. P. वेसति, वेसितुम्, to go,<BR>move; to desire, love, (Naigh. II. 6;<BR>another reading has वेशति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेस्
2. वेस्, Ved. in the phrase वेर् न, ‘like a bird;’<BR>[cf. 2. वि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसन|वेसनं
वेसन, अम्, n. a kind of flour made from a par-<BR>ticular ground vegetable (= द्विदल-चूर्ण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसर|वेसरः
वेसर वेसर, अस्, m. a mule, (also written<BR>वेशर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसवार|वेसवारः
वेसवार वेसवार, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>विस्), a particular condiment or kind of seasoning (con-<BR>sisting of ground coriander, mustard, pepper, ginger,<BR>spice, &c.; also written वेशवार, वेषवार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह्
वेह् वेह् (also written बेह्), cl. 1. A. वे-<BR>हते, विवेहे, वेहितुम्, to strive, make<BR>effort, endeavour diligently, resolve; cl. 1. P. वे-<BR>हति, &c. = वेहायते (according to Vopa-deva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेहत्
वेहत् वेहत्, त्, f. (said to be connected with<BR>वि-हन्), a cow miscarrying from taking the bull un-<BR>seasonably, a barren cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेहाय
वेहाय, Nom. A. वेहायते, -यितुम्, to miscarry<BR>(as a cow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेहार|वेहारः
वेहार वेहार, अस्, m., N. of a country<BR>(Behār).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह्ल्
वेह्ल् वेह्ल्, cl. 1. P. वेह्लति, &c. = rt.<BR>वेल्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
वै 1. वै (= rt. 2. वा, cl. 4), cl. 1. P.<BR>वायति, वातुम्, to dry, to become dried or<BR>withered; to be languid, be weary or faint, be ex-<BR>hausted, sink down, be extinguished, (Sāy. = शुष्-<BR>यति, श्राम्यते, शाम्यति); to go, (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda VIII. 31, 6. वायतः = गच्छतः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
3. वात, अस्, आ, अम् (often identified with 1. वात,<BR>p. 899, col. 1), dried, withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
5. वान, अस्, आ, अम्, dried, &c. See 1. and 2.<BR>वान, p. 900, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
वै 2. वै, ind. a particle of affirmation,<BR>generally translatable by ‘indeed,’ ‘truly,’ ‘certainly,’<BR>‘verily,’ ‘in sooth;’ it may also mean ‘so,’ ‘just,’<BR>‘although,’ ‘granted,’ ‘if,’ (तु वै, ‘but just;’ न<BR>वै, ‘perhaps not’); it is also said to be a vocative<BR>particle, and is often merely an expletive used for<BR>filling out a verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैंशतिक|वैंशतिकः
वैंशतिक वैंशतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विंशति),<BR>purchased with twenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्ष|वैकक्षं
वैकक्ष वैकक्ष, अम्, n. (fr. वि-कक्ष), a<BR>garland or string of flowers &c. worn over one<BR>shoulder and under the other (like the sacrificial<BR>thread); an upper garment, wrapper, mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्षक|वैकक्षकं
वैकक्षक or वैकक्षिक, अम्, n. a garland<BR>or string of flowers (worn as a kind of scarf hanging<BR>down below the hip, or like the sacrificial cord, over<BR>the left shoulder and under the right arm).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकङ्क|वैकंक
वैकङ्क वैकङ्क, N. of a mythical moun-<BR>tain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकङ्कत|वैकङ्कतः
वैकङ्कत वैकङ्कत, अस्, m. (fr. वि-कङ्कत),<BR>the plant Flacourtia Sapida (= वृन्तिङ्कर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकटिक|वैकटिकः
वैकटिक वैकटिक, अस्, m. (fr. वेकट), a<BR>jeweller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकर्ण|वैकर्णः
वैकर्ण वैकर्ण, अस्, m. = वि-कर्ण, epithet<BR>of the wind (as fond of large or hollow ears?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकर्त|वैकर्तः
वैकर्त वैकर्त, अस्, m. (fr. वि-कर्त), Ved.<BR>one who cuts up a sacrificial victim, a butcher; a<BR>particular part of a slaughtered animal (cut off and<BR>given to the priests at a sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकर्तन|वैकर्तनः|वैकर्त्तन
वैकर्तन, अस्, m. ‘son of Vi-kartana or the<BR>Sun,’ N. of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकर्म
वैकर्म वैकर्म, अस्, m., N. of the Muni<BR>Vātsya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्प|वैकल्पं
वैकल्प वैकल्प, अम्, n. (fr. वि-कल्प), du-<BR>biousness, uncertainty, ambiguity, optionality, inde-<BR>cision; [cf. अर्थ-व्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्पिक|वैकल्पिकः
वैकल्पिक, अस्, ई, अम्, doubtful, dubious, uncer-<BR>tain, admitting of difference of opinion, indetermi-<BR>nate, alternative, optional (= वि-कल्पित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्य|वैकल्यं
वैकल्य वैकल्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-कल), im-<BR>perfection, incompleteness, impairedness, deficiency,<BR>defect, mutilation, a defective or imperfect state of<BR>any limb or organ, lameness; incompetency, insuf-<BR>ficiency; agitation, flurry; non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकारिक|वैकारिकः
वैकारिक वैकारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-कार),<BR>modifying, a changer, modifier, (see वि-कार); mo-<BR>dified; (अस्), m. a class of deities.<BR>—वैकारिक-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. (in the Sāṅkhya phil.) one of the<BR>threefold forms of bondage, (see बन्ध, वि-कार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकाल|वैकालः
वैकाल वैकाल, अस्, m. (fr. वि-काल), even-<BR>ing, afternoon, (वैकाले, loc. c. in the evening.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकालिक
वैकालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, occurring in or belonging<BR>to the evening; (अम्), ind. in the afternoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकालीन
वैकालीन, अस्, ई, अम्, = वैकालिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकुण्ठ|वैकुंठ|वैकुंठः|वैकुण्ठः
वैकुण्ठ वैकुण्ठ, अस्, m. (fr. वि-कुण्ठ),<BR>N. of Viṣṇu; of Kṛṣṇa; of Indra, (Indra Vaikuṇṭha<BR>is regarded as the author of the hymns Ṛg-veda X.<BR>48-50); holy basil; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a particular<BR>class of gods; (अम्), n. the paradise or heaven of<BR>Vaikuṇṭha or Viṣṇu, (its site is variously described<BR>as in the northern ocean or on the eastern peak of<BR>mount Meru); talc.<BR>—वैकुण्ठ-चतुर्दशी, f. the<BR>fourteenth day of the light half of the month Kārt-<BR>tika (sacred to Viṣṇu).<BR>—वैकुण्ठ-पुरी, m., N.<BR>of an author and commentator, (also called विष्णु-<BR>पुरी.)<BR>—वैकुण्ठ-लोक, अस्, m. the world of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—वैकुण्ठ-वर्णन, अम्, n. a descrip-<BR>tion of Vaikuṇṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृत|वैकृतं|वैकृतः
वैकृत वैकृत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-कृति), un-<BR>dergoing change, changed (in mind or form); modi-<BR>fied; (अम्), n. change, modification, alteration;<BR>change of mind, aversion, disgust.<BR>—वैकृत-सर्ग,<BR>अस्, m. a kind or form of creation, (opposed to प्रा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">Page0967-c+ 73</a>]<BR>कृत-सर्ग.)<BR>—वैकृतापह (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>removing or preventing change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृतिक
वैकृतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, changed, modified, inci-<BR>dental; (in the Sāṅkhya phil.) belonging to a Vi-<BR>kāra, i. e. to an evolute or evolved principle, (see<BR>वि-कार, प्र-कृति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृत्य|वैकृत्यं
वैकृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, changed (in form or mind);<BR>(अम्), n. change, alteration; aversion, disgust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्रान्त|वैक्रांत|वैक्रांतं|वैक्रान्तं
वैक्रान्त वैक्रान्त, अम्, n. (fr. वि-क्रान्त), a<BR>kind of gem (= गो-नास, said to resemble a diamond<BR>or burnt diamond; according to others, the common<BR>loadstone or magnet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्लव|वैक्लवं
वैक्लव वैक्लव, अम्, n. (fr. वि-क्लव), agi-<BR>tation or distress of mind, bewilderment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्लव्य|वैक्लव्यं
वैक्लव्य, अम्, n. confusion, agitation, distress,<BR>affliction, despair, bewilderment, commotion, tumult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैखरी
वैखरी वैखरी, f. speech in the fourth<BR>of its four stages from the first stirring of the air or<BR>breath, articulate utterance, that utterance of sounds<BR>or words which is complete as consisting of full and<BR>intelligible sentences, (according to Malli-nātha =<BR>शब्द-निष्पत्तिः, Kumāra-sambhava II. 17); the<BR>faculty of speech or the divinity presiding over it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैखान
वैखान वैखान, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैखानस|वैखानसः
वैखानस वैखानस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-खा-<BR>नस), instituted by hermits, relating to hermits,<BR>monastic; (अस्), m. a Brāhman of the third religious<BR>order, a Vānaprastha or hermit, anchorite; N. of a<BR>sect of Vaiṣṇavas, (in Taittirīya-ār. 1. 23, 3. the<BR>Vaikhānasas are represented as having sprung from<BR>the nails of Prajā-pati); a patronymic of the Vedic<BR>Ṛṣi Vamra, (Śataṃ Vaikhānasāḥ are regarded as<BR>the authors of the hymn Ṛg-veda IX. 66); (ई), f.<BR>a vessel used for frying the meal offered in sacrifice.<BR>—वैखानस-मत, अम्, n. the laws ordained for<BR>hermits, (according to Kullūka = वैखानस-शास्-<BR>त्रोक्तो धर्मः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैगुण्य|वैगुण्यं
वैगुण्य वैगुण्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-गुण), ab-<BR>sence of or freedom from qualities, absence of attri-<BR>butes; difference of qualities or properties, contra-<BR>riety of properties, diversity, contrariety; inferiority,<BR>baseness, badness, vileness; unskilfulness, awkward-<BR>ness, clumsiness, waywardness; fault, defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैग्रहिक
वैग्रहिक वैग्रहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-ग्रह),<BR>corporeal, bodily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचक्षण्य|वैचक्षण्यं
वैचक्षण्य वैचक्षण्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-चक्-<BR>षण), proficiency, skill, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचित्त्य|वैचित्त्यं
वैचित्त्य वैचित्त्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-चित्ति), con-<BR>fusion of thought, distraction of mind, grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचित्र्य|वैचित्र्यं
वैचित्र्य वैचित्र्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-चित्र),<BR>variety, diversity; diversifiedness, manifoldness; sur-<BR>prisingness, surprise; sorrow, despair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैच्युत
वैच्युत वैच्युत, अस्, m. (fr. वि-च्युत), N. of<BR>a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजन
वैजन वैजन, अस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>the grammatical work called Prabodha-candrikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजनन|वैजननं|वैजननः
वैजनन वैजनन, अम्, n. (fr. वि-जनन),<BR>the last month of pregnancy (= प्रसव-मास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्त|वैजयंत|वैजयंतः|वैजयन्तः
वैजयन्त वैजयन्त, अस्, m. (fr. वि-जयन्त),<BR>the banner or emblem of Indra; a banner, flag; the<BR>palace of Indra; (ई), f. a flag, banner; an ensign;<BR>a kind of garland; the necklace of Viṣṇu (com-<BR>posed of five gems, viz. pearl, ruby, emerald, sap-<BR>phire, and diamond); N. of the eighth night of the<BR>civil month; the plant Sesbana Ægyptiaca; Premna<BR>Spinosa; N. of a lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्तिक|वैजयंतिक|वैजयंतिकः|वैजयन्तिकः
वैजयन्तिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, bearing a flag; (अस्),<BR>m. a flag-bearer, standard-bearer; (आ), f. a flag,<BR>banner; a kind of scarf or a string or necklace of<BR>pearls; the plant Sesbana Ægyptiaca (= जयन्ती);<BR>another plant (= अग्नि-मन्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयि|वैजयिः
वैजयि वैजयि, इस्, m. (fr. वि-जया), the third<BR>Jaina Cakra-vartin or emperor (= मघवन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयिक|वैजयिकं
वैजयिक वैजयिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-जय),<BR>relating to victory, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजवाप
वैजवाप वैजवाप, अस्, m. (fr. वीज-वाप),<BR>N. of a Muni; of the author of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजवापि
वैजवापि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. वीज-वापिन्), see Gaṇa<BR>Sutaṅgamādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80; (इस्), m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Vīja-vāpa or Vīja-vāpin; (अयस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजवापीय
वैजवापीय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वैजवापि), see<BR>Gaṇa Raivatikādi to Pāṇ. IV. 3, 131; (अस्), m. a<BR>prince of the Vaijavāpis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजात्य|वैजात्यं
वैजात्य वैजात्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-जाति), differ-<BR>ence of class or species or kind, difference of caste,<BR>diversity of ordinary character or conduct, extraor-<BR>dinariness, strangeness; exclusion from caste; loose-<BR>ness, wantonness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजिक|वैजिकं|वैजिकः
वैजिक वैजिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वीज), seminal,<BR>relating to seed, belonging to any primary cause or<BR>source or principle, original; relating to conception;<BR>relating to sexual union; (अस्), m. a young shoot,<BR>sprout, scion; (अम्), n. cause, source, origin, motive;<BR>the spiritual cause of existence, soul, spirit; oil pre-<BR>pared from the Śigru or Morunga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजि
वैजि, इस्, इस्, इ, see Gaṇa Gahādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2,<BR>138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजीय
वैजीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वैजि), see Gaṇa Gahādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजेय
वैजेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Vīja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैज्ञानिक|वैज्ञानिकः
वैज्ञानिक वैज्ञानिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-<BR>ज्ञान), conversant with, skilful, clever, proficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैडाल
वैडाल वैडाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विडाल), of or<BR>belonging to a cat, peculiar to cats, feline.<BR>—वैडाल-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n. ‘cat-like observance,’ putting on a<BR>show of virtue or piety to conceal malice and evil<BR>designs.<BR>—वैडाल-व्रति, इस्, m. one who leads a<BR>chaste or continent life merely from the absence of<BR>women or temptation.<BR>—वैडालव्रतिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>or वैडालव्रतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, acting like a cat, hypo-<BR>critical; any hypocritical religious impostor or pre-<BR>tended ascetic who, under an appearance of piety<BR>and virtue, conceals covetous or malignant designs<BR>(= भण्ड-तपस्विन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण|वैणः
वैण वैण, अस्, m. (fr. वेणु), a cutter of<BR>bamboos, a maker of bamboo-work; N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणव|वैणवं|वैणवः
वैणव, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to a bamboo,<BR>produced from or made of bamboo; (अस्), m. a<BR>student's staff cut from a bamboo, any bamboo staff;<BR>a worker in bamboo or wicker-work; N. of a sacred<BR>place of pilgrimage; (ई), f. bamboo manna; (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit or seed of the bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणविक|वैणविकः
वैणविक, अस्, m. a flutist, piper, flute-player.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणविन्
वैणविन्, ई, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणहोत्र
वैणहोत्र, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणुक|वैणुकं|वैणुकः
वैणुक, अम्, n. a goad or bamboo pike (pointed<BR>with iron and used to drive an elephant); (अस्), m.<BR>a piper, player on a pipe or flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणुकेय
वैणुकेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>a bamboo, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणिक|वैणिकः
वैणिक वैणिक, अस्, m. (fr. वीणा), a lutanist,<BR>a player on the Vīṇā or Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण्य|वैण्यः
वैण्य वैण्य, अस्, m. (fr. वेण), a patro-<BR>nymic of Pṛthu son of Veṇa, (he was the fifth<BR>sovereign of one branch of the solar race.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतंसिक|वैतंसिकः
वैतंसिक वैतंसिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-तंस), a<BR>vender of flesh, seller of the meat of beasts or birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतण्डिक|वैतंडिक|वैतंडिकः|वैतण्डिकः
वैतण्डिक वैतण्डिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-तण्डा), a<BR>disputatious or captious person, one fond of cavilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतण्ड्य
वैतण्ड्य, अस्, m., N. of a son of the Vasu Āpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतथ्य|वैतथ्यं
वैतथ्य वैतथ्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-तथ),<BR>falseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतनिक|वैतनिकः
वैतनिक वैतनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वेतन),<BR>living on wages, subsisting on a stipend; (अस्), m. a<BR>hireling, stipendiary; a labourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतरण
वैतरण वैतरण, अस्, m. (fr. वि-तरण),<BR>N. of a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतरणि|वैतरणिः
वैतरणि, इस्, or वैतरणी, f., N. of the river<BR>of Hell, i. e. of a river which must be crossed before<BR>entering the infernal regions, (this river is described<BR>as rushing with great impetuosity, hot, fetid in<BR>odour, and filled with blood, hair, and bones; its<BR>name is derived from वि-तरण in the sense either<BR>of ‘crossing’ or ‘giving,’ liberality being supposed<BR>to secure a passage); N. of a division of Naraka or<BR>Hell; of a sacred river in the country of the Kaliṅgas;<BR>N. of the mother of the Rākṣasas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतस|वैतसः
वैतस वैतस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वेतस), reed-<BR>like; (अस्), m. a sort of cane, Calamus Fasciculatus;<BR>= शेप (according to Naigh. III. 29).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतहव्य
वैतहव्य वैतहव्य, अस्, m. (fr. वीत-हव्य),<BR>a patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतान
वैतान वैतान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-तान), taken<BR>from the sacred hearth, sacrificial, sacred (as fire);<BR>(अम्), n. an oblation with fire; a sacrificial rite.<BR>—वैतान-कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in or con-<BR>versant with sacrificial rites.<BR>—वैतानोपासना (˚न-<BR>उप्˚), f. the regular presentation of burnt-offerings<BR>morning and evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतानिक|वैतानिकः
वैतानिक, अस्, ई, अम्, performed with the three<BR>sacred fires (i. e. with the Gārhapatya, Dakṣiṇa,<BR>and Āhavanīya fires); sacrificial, sacred (as fire);<BR>(अम्), n. a burnt-offering (especially of clarified<BR>butter, as presented daily by the Brāhmans).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालकि
वैतालकि वैतालकि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher<BR>of the Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालिक|वैतालिकः
वैतालिक वैतालिक, अस्, m. (fr. ताल with 1. वि<BR>or fr. वेताल), a bard whose duty it is to awaken a<BR>chief or prince at dawn with music and song; one<BR>who sings out of tune (?); one who is possessed by<BR>a Vetāla or demon, the servant of a Vetāla; the<BR>worshipper of a Vetāla; a magician, conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालीय
वैतालीय वैतालीय, अम्, n. (fr. वेताल), a<BR>kind of metre (the first and third Pāda containing<BR>fourteen Mātrās or the time of fourteen short sylla-<BR>bles, the second and fourth containing sixteen Mā-<BR>trās; each Pāda closes with a cretic and iambus, i. e.<BR>¯˘¯˘¯; but there are some varieties).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतृष्ण्य
वैतृष्ण्य वैतृष्ण्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-तृष्ण),<BR>freedom from thirst, quenching the thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैत्रक|वैत्रकः
वैत्रक वैत्रक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वेत्र), cany,<BR>reedy, relating to a cane or stick of any kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैत्रकीय|वैत्रकीयः
वैत्रकीय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a cane or<BR>stick, reedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद|वैदः
वैद वैद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विद), relating to<BR>or connected with a wise man, learned, knowing;<BR>(अस्), m. a wise man; (ई), f. the wife of a wise<BR>man, (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 73.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्ध|वैदग्धं
वैदग्ध वैदग्ध, अम्, n. (fr. वि-दग्ध),<BR>cleverness, dexterity, skill, intelligence, acuteness,<BR>sharpness, craft, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्धी
वैदग्धी, f. artifice, craft, trick (= भङ्गि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्ध्य|वैदग्ध्यं
वैदग्ध्य, अम्, n. cleverness, dexterity, skill,<BR>intelligence, knowingness, sharpness, acuteness, wit;<BR>cunning, craft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदथिन
वैदथिन वैदथिन, अस्, m. (fr. विदथिन्),<BR>Ved. a patronymic of Ṛjiśvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैददश्वि
वैददश्वि वैददश्वि, इस्, m. a patronymic,<BR>the son of Vidad-aśva, Ṛg-veda V. 61, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदर्भ|वैदर्भं|वैदर्भः
वैदर्भ वैदर्भ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-दर्भ or<BR>fr. दृभ formed fr. rt. 1. दृभ् with वि), coming<BR>from the country Vidarbha, produced in Vidarbha;<BR>(अस्), m. the sovereign of Vidarbha (father of Dama-<BR>yantī and father-in-law of Nala); a gum-boil; (ई),<BR>f. the law of the country Vidarbha (by which first<BR>cousins were allowed to intermarry); epithet of the<BR>wife of Agastya; of Damayantī (wife of Nala); of<BR>Rukmiṇī (one of Kṛṣṇa's wives); a particular style<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">Page0968-c+ 76</a>]<BR>of composition (see रीति); (अम्), n. crafty or indirect<BR>speech.<BR>—वैदर्भ-रीति, इस्, f. the Vidarbha style<BR>of composition (see रीति).<BR>—वैदर्भी-जननी, f.<BR>the mother of Damayantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदर्भक
वैदर्भक, अस्, इका, अम्, coming from Vidar-<BR>bha, a native of Vidarbha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदल|वैदलं|वैदलः
वैदल वैदल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-दल), made<BR>of wicker or cane, wicker or basket-work; (अस्), m.<BR>a flat unleavened cake (made of flour &c. with<BR>cumin or coriander seeds and fried in ghee); any<BR>leguminous vegetable or grain (as peas, beans, &c.);<BR>(अम्), n. the shallow cup or platter belonging to a<BR>religious mendicant (made of clay and sometimes<BR>of metal or wood or wicker); any seat or vessel of<BR>basket or wicker-work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदारव
वैदारव वैदारव, वैदार्व. See श्वैत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिक|वैदिकः
वैदिक वैदिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. वेद),<BR>derived from or conformable to the Vedas, relating<BR>to the Vedas, Vedic, prescribed by Vedic ritual,<BR>knowing the Vedas, scriptural, sacred; (अस्), m. a<BR>Brāhman versed in the Vedas.<BR>—वैदिक-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. an action enjoined by the Vedas.<BR>—वैदिक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. conformity to the Vedas, the being<BR>founded on or derived from the Vedas, sacredness.<BR>—वैदिक-पाश, अस्, m. a bad Veda-knower, one<BR>imperfectly versed in the Veda, (Pāṇ. V. 3, 47.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिश
वैदिश वैदिश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विदिशा), of or<BR>belonging to the city of Vidiśā, near Vidiśā.<BR>—वै-<BR>दिश-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिश्य|वैदिश्यं
वैदिश्य, अम्, n. a city not far from Vidiśā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदुष्य|वैदुष्यं
वैदुष्य वैदुष्य, अम्, n. (fr. विद्वस्), wisdom,<BR>learning, science, sapience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदुषी
वैदुषी, f. = वैदुष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदूर्य|वैदूर्य्य|वैदूर्य्यं
वैदूर्य वैदूर्य, अस्, ई, or री, अम् (fr. वि-दूर),<BR>brought from Vidūra; (अम्), n. a gem of a dark<BR>colour, lapis lazuli or a kind of turkois; N. of a<BR>mountain; of a mythical mountain.<BR>—वैदूर्य-म-<BR>य, अस्, ई, अम्, made or consisting of lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेशिक|वैदेशिकः
वैदेशिक वैदेशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-देश),<BR>belonging to another country, foreign, strange, a<BR>foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेश्य|वैदेश्यं
वैदेश्य, अम्, n. the state of belonging to a<BR>foreign country, foreignness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेह|वैदेहः
वैदेह वैदेह, अस्, m. (fr. वि-देह), the king<BR>of Videha (father of Sītā); a dweller in Videha;<BR>a trader by caste; the son of a Vaiśya by a Brāhman<BR>woman (Manu X. 11); an attendant on the women's<BR>apartments; (आस्), m. pl. people of Videha; people<BR>of mixed castes; (ई), f. Sītā (daughter of Janaka);<BR>the wife of a merchant, woman of the Vaideha<BR>caste; a sort of pigment (= रोचना); long pepper;<BR>a cow.<BR>—वैदेहि-बन्धु, उस्, m. (for वैदेही-ब्˚<BR>by Pāṇ. VI. 3, 63), ‘husband of the lady of Videha,’ an<BR>epithet of Rāma-candra, (Raghu-vaṃśa XIV. 33.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेहक|वैदेहकः
वैदेहक, अस्, m. a merchant or trader by caste;<BR>a man of a mixed caste (the offspring of a Vaiśya<BR>father and Brāhman mother whose business is attend-<BR>ance in the women's apartments).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेहिक|वैदेहिकः
वैदेहिक, अस्, m. a merchant (= वैदेहक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्य|वैद्यः
वैद्य वैद्य, अस्, -दी, अम् (fr. वेद), relating<BR>or belonging to the Vedas, conformable to the Vedas,<BR>Vedic; medical, medicinal, practising or relating to<BR>medicine [cf. आयुर्-वेद]; (अस्), m. a learned man,<BR>doctor, Paṇḍit, a follower of the Vedas or one well<BR>versed in them; a medical man, doctor, physician;<BR>a man of the medical caste (enumerated among the<BR>mixed classes and originally the offspring of a Brāh-<BR>man by a Vaiśya woman; he is also called Amba-<BR>ṣṭha, Manu X. 8); a man of another and lower<BR>mixed caste (said to be the descendant of a Śūdra<BR>father and Vaiśya mother; cf. चण्डाल, व्रात्य);<BR>the tree Justicia Ganderussa; (आ), f. a particular<BR>drug or medicinal substance (= काकोली).<BR>—वैद्य-<BR>क्रिया, f. the business of a physician.<BR>—वैद्य-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of physicians,’ epithet of Śiva;<BR>of Dhanvantari; of a poet; of a country.<BR>—वैद्य-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">Page0969-a+ 71</a>]<BR>बन्धु, उस्, m. the tree Cassia Fistula (= आरग्-<BR>बध).<BR>—वैद्य-भूषण, ‘ornament of phy-<BR>sicians,’ N. of a work by Rāmānanda-svāmin.<BR>—वैद्य-मातृ, ता, f. the mother of a physician;<BR>the tree Justicia Ganderussa (= 1. वासक).<BR>—वैद्य-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘favourite with physicians,’ N. of a<BR>medical work on the treatment of fever by Śārṅgha-<BR>dhara.<BR>—वैद्य-सिंही, f. the plant Justicia Gande-<BR>russa (= 1. वासक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यक|वैद्यकं|वैद्यकः
वैद्यक, अस्, ई, अम्, medical, relating to medi-<BR>cine; (अस्), m. a doctor, physician, medical man;<BR>(अम्), n. the science of medicine, the Āyur-veda,<BR>q. v.<BR>—वैद्यक-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the science of medi-<BR>cine.<BR>—वैद्यक-सर्व-स्व, अम्, n., N. of a work<BR>by Nakula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्याधर
वैद्याधर वैद्याधर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विद्या-<BR>धर), belonging to the Vidyā-dharas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्याधर
वैद्याधर वैद्याधर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विद्युत्),<BR>coming or proceeding from lightning, belonging to<BR>or connected with lightning, electric, electrical,<BR>(वैद्युतः कृशानुः, the fire of lightning.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध|वैधः
वैध वैध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विधि), enjoined<BR>by rule, conformable to rule, prescribed, appointed,<BR>giving rules or directions, preceptive, ritual; legal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधिक
वैधिक, अस्, ई, अम्, in accordance with rule,<BR>giving precepts or commands, preceptive, ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधर्म्य|वैधर्म्यं
वैधर्म्य वैधर्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-धर्म),<BR>unlawfulness, injustice, impropriety, irreligion, hete-<BR>rodoxy; difference of duty or obligation; opposition<BR>or contrariety of character, difference of characteristic<BR>qualities, difference, heterogeneity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधव|वैधवः
वैधव वैधव, अस्, m. (fr. विधु), the son<BR>of the Moon, i. e. Budha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधव्य|वैधव्यं
वैधव्य वैधव्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-धवा),<BR>widowhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधवेय|वैधवेयः
वैधवेय, अस्, m. the son of a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधात्र|वैधात्रः
वैधात्र वैधात्र, अस्, m. (fr. वि-धातृ), a<BR>patronymic of Sanat-kumāra (as son of Brahmā and<BR>eldest of the progenitors of mankind); (ई), f. =<BR>ब्राह्मी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधुर्य|वैधुर्यं|वैधुर्य्य
वैधुर्य वैधुर्य, अम्, n. (fr. विधुर), agi-<BR>tation, tremulousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधूमाग्नी
वैधूमाग्नी वैधूमाग्नी, f., N. of a city in<BR>the country of the Śālvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधृत|वैधृतं
वैधृत वैधृत, अस्, m. (fr. वि-धृत), N.<BR>of a particular position of the sun and moon when<BR>they are on the same side of either solstice and of<BR>equal declination but of opposite direction, (this is<BR>considered a malignant aspect; cf. व्य्-अतीपात.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधृति|वैधृतिः
वैधृति, इस्, f. the Yoga star of the twenty-<BR>seventh lunar mansion; = वैधृत above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधेय|वैधेयः
वैधेय 1. वैधेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-धेय),<BR>foolish, silly, weak, ignorant; (अस्), m. an idiot, fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधेय|वैधेयः
2. वैधेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विधि), relating to<BR>rule or precept, prescribed, preceptive; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a teacher of the White Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध्यत|वैध्यतः
वैध्यत वैध्यत, अस्, m., N. of Yama's<BR>porter or door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनतक|वैनतकं
वैनतक वैनतक, अम्, n. a vessel for<BR>holding or pouring out ghee (used at sacrifices).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनतेय|वैनतेयः
वैनतेय वैनतेय, अस्, m. (fr. वि-नता), N. of<BR>Garuḍa (as son of Vinatā); of Aruṇa (elder brother<BR>of Garuḍa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनयिक|वैनयिकः
वैनयिक वैनयिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-नय),<BR>relating to moral conduct or discipline; enforcing<BR>proper behaviour; performed by the officers of<BR>criminal justice, magisterial; (अस्), m. a chariot em-<BR>ployed in military exercises, a war-carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनायिक|वैनायिकः
वैनायिक वैनायिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-नायक),<BR>belonging or relating to Gaṇeśa, made by Gaṇeśa;<BR>a follower of Buddha, a Buddhist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनाशिक|वैनाशिकं|वैनाशिकः
वैनाशिक वैनाशिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-नाश), a<BR>dependant, subject, slave; a spider; an astrologer;<BR>(अम्), n. the twenty-third Nakṣatra or constellation<BR>from that under which any one is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनीतक|वैनीतकः
वैनीतक वैनीतक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. वि-<BR>नीत), an indirect means of conveyance (as a porter<BR>carrying a litter or dooly, a palanquin-bearer, horse<BR>dragging a carriage, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैन्दव
वैन्दव वैन्दव, अस्, m. (fr. विन्दु), a pa-<BR>tronymic from Vindu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैन्दवि
वैन्दवि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैन्दवीय
वैन्दवीय, अस्, m. a prince of the Vaindavis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैन्य|वैन्यः
वैन्य वैन्य, अस्, m. (fr. वेन), a patronymic<BR>of Pṛthī (Ved.); of Pṛthu (author of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 148, who is probably to be identified<BR>with Pṛthī); of king Pṛthu [cf. वैण्य]; N. of a<BR>deity (?).<BR>—वैन्य-दत्त, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैपथक
वैपथक वैपथक, अस्, आ, or ई, अम् (fr. वि-<BR>पथ), relating to a wrong path, going wrong,<BR>devious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैपरीत्य|वैपरीत्यं
वैपरीत्य वैपरीत्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-परीत),<BR>contrariety, opposition, adverseness, reverse; counter-<BR>part.<BR>—वैपरीत्य-लज्जालु, उस्, m. f. a particular<BR>species of sensitive plant or Mimosa Pudica (small<BR>in size but bearing large seed or fruit).<BR>—वैपरीत्य-<BR>सम्बन्ध, अस्, m. the relation of contrariety or<BR>contradictoriness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैपुल्य|वैपुल्यं
वैपुल्य वैपुल्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-पुल), large-<BR>ness, spaciousness, abundance, plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैफल्य|वैफल्यं
वैफल्य वैफल्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-फल), fruit-<BR>lessness, uselessness, unproductiveness, abortiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैबोधिक|वैबोधिकः
वैबोधिक वैबोधिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-बोध),<BR>a watchman, one who announces the hours of the<BR>night or awakes sleepers by calling out the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभव|वैभवं
वैभव वैभव, अम्, n. (fr. वि-भव), su-<BR>perhuman power or might; power, greatness, majesty,<BR>grandeur, glory, magnificence, splendor, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभाजित्र|वैभाजित्रं
वैभाजित्र वैभाजित्र, अम्, n. (fr. विभाज-<BR>यितृ), apportioning, dividing; apportionment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभाषिक
वैभाषिक वैभाषिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-<BR>भाषा), optional, alternative; epithet of one of the<BR>four great schools or systems of Buddhism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभोज
वैभोज वैभोज, आस्, m. pl., N. of a tribe<BR>(said to have been descended from Druhyu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभ्र|वैभ्रं
वैभ्र वैभ्र, अम्, n. (etymology doubtful;<BR>said to be fr. वि-भ्राज्), the heaven of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभ्राज|वैभ्राजं
वैभ्राज वैभ्राज, अम्, n. (fr. वि-भ्राज्), the<BR>garden of the gods, a celestial grove or garden; N.<BR>of a forest (said to be situated on the west of Meru).<BR>—वैभ्राज-लोक, अस्, m. the world or place inha-<BR>bited by the Manes called Barhi-shads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमत्य|वैमत्यं
वैमत्य वैमत्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-मति), differ-<BR>ence of opinion, dissension; aversion, dislike; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a school of the White Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमद
वैमद वैमद, अस्, ई, अम्, of or belonging<BR>to Vi-mada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमनस्य|वैमनस्यं
वैमनस्य वैमनस्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-मनस्),<BR>distraction or agitation of mind, great sadness or sor-<BR>row, distractedness, broken-heartedness; sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमल्य
वैमल्य वैमल्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-मल), spot-<BR>lessness, cleanliness, purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्र|वैमात्रः
वैमात्र वैमात्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-मातृ),<BR>born of a different mother, the offspring of a step-<BR>mother; (अस्), m. a step-mother's son, half brother;<BR>(आ or ई), f. a step-mother's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्रेय|वैमात्रेयः
वैमात्रेय, अस्, m. a step-mother's son; (ई), f. a<BR>step-mother's daughter; a half sister, one by a dif-<BR>ferent mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमानिक|वैमानिकः
वैमानिक वैमानिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-मान),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">Page0969-c+ 73</a>]<BR>relating to a heavenly car, borne in divine chariots;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a particular class of deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमुक्त|वैमुक्तं|वैमुक्तः
वैमुक्त वैमुक्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-मुक्त),<BR>liberated, emancipated, being at liberty or loose;<BR>(अम्), n. liberation, emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमुख्य|वैमुख्यं
वैमुख्य वैमुख्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-मुख),<BR>turning away the face, avertedness, flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमूल्य
वैमूल्य वैमूल्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-मूल्य),<BR>variety or difference of price, an unfair charge.<BR>—वैमूल्य-तस्, ind. at different or various prices,<BR>at unfair prices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमेय|वैमेयः
वैमेय वैमेय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. मे with वि),<BR>barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैम्बकि
वैम्बकि वैम्बकि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Vimba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयग्र|वैयग्रं
वैयग्र वैयग्र, अम्, n. (fr. व्य्-अग्र), dis-<BR>traction or agitation of mind, perplexity, bewilder-<BR>ment; the being totally absorbed or wholly engaged<BR>(in any occupation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयग्र्य|वैयग्र्यं
वैयग्र्य, अम्, n. perplexity, &c., = वैयग्र<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयर्थ्य|वैयर्थ्यं
वैयर्थ्य वैयर्थ्य, अम्, n. (fr. व्य्-अर्थ),<BR>unprofitableness, uselessness, inutility, unproductive-<BR>ness, vainness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयल्कस
वैयल्कस वैयल्कस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. व्य्-<BR>अल्कस), see Vopa-deva VII. 4, VII. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयश्व
वैयश्व वैयश्व, अस्, m. (fr. व्य्-अश्व), a<BR>patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Viśva-manas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयश्वि
वैयश्वि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Vy-aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाकरण|वैयाकरणः
वैयाकरण वैयाकरण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. व्य्-<BR>आकरण), relating to grammar, grammatical; (अस्),<BR>m. a grammatical analyst, a grammarian; (ई), f. a<BR>female grammarian.<BR>—वैयाकरण-पाश, अस्, m.<BR>a bad grammarian, (Pāṇ. V. 3, 47.)<BR>—वैयाक-<BR>रण-भार्य, अस्, m. a man who has a female<BR>grammarian for a wife.<BR>—वैयाकरण-भूषण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work by Koṇḍa-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—वैयाक-<BR>रण-सिद्धान्त-मञ्जूषा, f., N. of a work (=<BR>मञ्जूषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाघ्र|वैयाघ्रः
वैयाघ्र वैयाघ्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. व्याघ्र),<BR>belonging to a tiger, tiger-like, consisting or made<BR>of a tiger's skin, covered with a tiger's skin.<BR>—वै-<BR>याघ्र-परिच्छद, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with a<BR>tiger's skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाघ्रपद्य|वैयाघ्रपद्यः
वैयाघ्रपद्य, अस्, m. (fr. व्याघ्र-पद् or<BR>˚पाद्), N. of a Muni, the founder of a family called<BR>after him; (अस्, आ, अम्), composed by the gram-<BR>marian Vyāghra-pād.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाघ्र्य
वैयाघ्र्य, अम्, n. the state or condition of a<BR>tiger; a particular posture in sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयात्य|वैयात्यं
वैयात्य वैयात्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-यात), lasci-<BR>viousness, immodesty, boldness, impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयासकि|वैयासकिः
वैयासकि वैयासकि, इस्, m. (a patronymic<BR>fr. व्यास), a son or descendant of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयासिक|वैयासिकः
वैयासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, composed by Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयुष्ट|वैयुष्टः
वैयुष्ट वैयुष्ट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. व्य्-उष्ट),<BR>early, occurring at dawn, performed early in the<BR>morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैर|वैरं
वैर वैर, अम्, n. (fr. वीर), heroism, valour,<BR>prowess; enmity, hostility, animosity, revenge, grudge,<BR>malice, spite, hatred, vindictiveness, opposition, strife,<BR>quarrel.<BR>—वैर-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing hostility,<BR>occasioning enmity, mischief-making.<BR>—वैर-कार,<BR>अस्, m. ‘enmity-causer,’ an enemy.<BR>—वैर-कारण,<BR>अम्, n. a cause of hostility.<BR>—वैर-कृत्, त्, m.<BR>‘causing enmity,’ an enemy.<BR>—वैर-निर्यातन,<BR>अम्, n. requital of enmity or of a grudge, revenge,<BR>retaliation, requital of an injury.<BR>—वैर-प्रति-<BR>क्रिया, f. requital of hostile acts, revenge.<BR>—वैर-<BR>प्रतिमोचन, अम्, n. deliverance or setting free<BR>from enmity.<BR>—वैर-प्रतियातन, अम्, n. the<BR>requital of enmity, taking vengeance.<BR>—वैर-<BR>यातना, f. requital of a grudge, vengeance.<BR>—वैर-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">Page0970-a+ 75</a>]<BR>रक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, guarding against or warding off hos-<BR>tility.<BR>—वैर-शुद्धि, इस्, f. the removal or wiping<BR>out of a grudge, revenge, retaliation.<BR>—वैरातङ्क<BR>(˚र-आत्˚), अस्, m. the Arjuna tree.<BR>—वैरानुबन्-<BR>ध (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m. beginning or commencement<BR>of hostilities.<BR>—वैरानुबन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, com-<BR>mencing hostilities, leading to or resulting in enmity<BR>or hostility; (ई), m. the calorific or heating solar<BR>ray; epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वैरारोह (˚र-आर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. rise or advance of hostility, desperate combat.<BR>—वैरी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become<BR>hostile, be changed into enmity or hatred.<BR>—वै-<BR>रोद्धार (˚र-उद्˚), अम्, n. removal or redemption<BR>of a grudge, taking revenge, retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराय
वैराय, Nom. A. वैरायते, -यितुम्, to become<BR>hostile, behave inimically, act in a hostile manner,<BR>fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरायमाण
वैरायमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming hostile or<BR>inimical, being an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिन्
वैरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, hostile, malicious, revengeful;<BR>(ई), m. a hero; an enemy.<BR>—वैरि-ता, f. or वैरि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. heroism; enmity, hostility, malice, hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरक्त|वैरक्तं
वैरक्त वैरक्त, अम्, n. (fr. वि-रक्त), free-<BR>dom from worldly affections and passions, absence of<BR>affection or attachment, aversion, displeasure, dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरङ्गिक|वैरंगिकः|वैरङ्गिकः
वैरङ्गिक वैरङ्गिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-रङ्ग),<BR>one who has subdued all passions and desires, a<BR>devotee, ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरल्य|वैरल्यं
वैरल्य वैरल्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-रल), loose-<BR>ness or openness (of texture), fineness; rareness,<BR>scarceness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग|वैरागं
वैराग वैराग, अम्, n. (fr. वि-राग), absence<BR>of worldly passion, freedom from all desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिक|वैरागिकः
वैरागिक, अस्, m. an ascetic who has subdued<BR>his passions and is free from desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिन्
वैरागिन्, ई, m. an ascetic or devotee who has<BR>subdued all worldly desires; a particular class of reli-<BR>gious mendicants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग्य|वैराग्यं
वैराग्य, अम्, n. freedom from passion, dispas-<BR>sion, absence of all worldly desires and appetites,<BR>asceticism, devotion.<BR>—वैराग्य-शतक, अम्, n., N.<BR>of one hundred verses on asceticism by Bhartṛ-hari,<BR>(these verses constitute the third Śataka in his work.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराज|वैराजः
वैराज वैराज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. वि-राज्),<BR>consisting of the Virāj metre, composed in this<BR>metre; consisting of ten syllables (as a Pāda); of<BR>or belonging to the district called Virāj; epithet<BR>of particular worlds; (अस्), m. a son or descendant<BR>of Virāj, Manu Svāyambhuva; a patronymic of the<BR>Vedic Ṛṣi Ṛṣabha; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a parti-<BR>cular class of deities; of a class of Pitṛs; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of the Virāj metre; of a particular Sāman or<BR>portion of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराजक
वैराजक, अस्, m. epithet of the nineteenth Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराट|वैराटः
वैराट वैराट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-राट), relat-<BR>ing or belonging to Virāṭa; (अस्), m. an earth-worm;<BR>a particular insect (= इन्द्र-गोप).<BR>—वैराट-देश,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR>—वैराट-राज, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराट्या
वैराट्या, f., N. of one of the sixteen Vidyā-devīs<BR>or goddesses of learning (with Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिण
वैरिण वैरिण, अस्, m. (see वीरण), Ved. a<BR>kind of Vīraṇa grass, (Sāy. = वीरण-प्रकार, Ṛg-<BR>veda 1. 191, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिन्
वैरिन् वैरिन्. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरूप
वैरूप वैरूप, अम्, n. (fr. वि-रूप), Ved.,<BR>N. of a particular Sāman; (अस्), m. a patronymic<BR>of the Vedic Ṛṣi Aṣṭā-daṃṣṭra; of Nabha-pra-<BR>bhedana; of Śata-prabhedana; of Sadhri; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a race of Pitṛs (occupying the third or<BR>highest heaven).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरूप्य|वैरूप्यं
वैरूप्य, अम्, n. difference or diversity of form,<BR>variety of shape; deformity, ugliness.<BR>—वैरूप्य-<BR>ता, f. deformity, malformation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचन|वैरोचनः
वैरोचन वैरोचन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-रोचन),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">Page0970-b+ 73</a>]<BR>belonging to or coming from the Sun; descended<BR>from Virocana, &c.; (अस्), m. a Buddha (the third<BR>of the Dhyāni-buddhas); a patronymic of the cele-<BR>brated Daitya Bali (sovereign of Mahābali-pura, see<BR>बलि); of the son of Agni; of the son of Sūrya<BR>(the Sun); a Siddha, a sort of demigod or deified<BR>mortal.<BR>—वैरोचन-निकेतन, अम्, n. ‘abode of<BR>Bali,’ Pātāla or that portion of the lower regions<BR>over which Bali presides, (see बलि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचनि|वैरोचनिः
वैरोचनि, इस्, m. a Buddha; a patronymic of Bali,<BR>(see above); of the son of Agni; of the son of Sūrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचि|वैरोचिः
वैरोचि वैरोचि, इस्, m., N. of the Daitya<BR>Vāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल
वैल वैल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विल), relating or<BR>belonging to a hole or pit.<BR>—वैल-स्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. a pit, burying-place, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda 1. 133, 3. महा-वैलस्थे = सर्वैर् गन्तव्ये<BR>महा-श्मशाने or नाग-लोके.)<BR>—वैल-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. a place like a hole, a pit; a burying-<BR>place.<BR>—वैल-स्थानक, अम्, n., Ved. a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्षण्य|वैलक्षण्यं
वैलक्षण्य वैलक्षण्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-<BR>लक्षण), contrariety, difference, disparity, oppo-<BR>sition; पूर्वोक्त-वैलक्षण्येन, in opposition to<BR>what was before stated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्ष्य|वैलक्ष्यं
वैलक्ष्य वैलक्ष्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-लक्ष),<BR>absence of mark or characteristic; contrariety, re-<BR>verse, inversion; the reverse of what is usual or<BR>natural, unnaturalness, affectation; स-वैलक्ष्यम्,<BR>affectedly, in a forced manner, unnaturally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलोम्य|वैलोम्यं
वैलोम्य वैलोम्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-लोम),<BR>contrariety, reverseness, opposition, oppositeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल्व|वैल्वं
वैल्व वैल्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विल्व), relating<BR>or belonging to the Vilva tree; made of Vilva<BR>wood; (अम्), n. the fruit of the Vilva or Ægle<BR>Marmelos.<BR>—वैल्व-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or con-<BR>sisting of the Vilva or of its wood, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवधिक|वैवधिकः
वैवधिक वैवधिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-वध),<BR>a dealer, peddler, hawker, vender of various sub-<BR>stances (as grain, oil, ghee, fruit, sweetmeats, &c.,<BR>= विवधिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्ण्य|वैवर्ण्यं
वैवर्ण्य वैवर्ण्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-वर्ण),<BR>diversity of colour, change of colour or complexion;<BR>deviation or secession from tribe or caste, &c.; hete-<BR>rogeneousness, diversity, difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्त|वैवर्तं
वैवर्त वैवर्त, अम्, n. (fr. वि-वर्त), revo-<BR>lution, change or modification of existence; [cf.<BR>ब्रह्म-वैवर्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वत|वैवस्वतः
वैवस्वत वैवस्वत, अस्, m. (a patronymic<BR>fr. विवस्वत्), N. of Yama as son of Vivasvat, (see<BR>Yama); the seventh Manu or Manu of the present<BR>period (as son of Vivasvat and brother of Yama);<BR>the planet Saturn; one of the Rudras; (अम्), n.,<BR>scil. अन्तर, epithet of the seventh or present Manv-<BR>antara (as presided over by Manu Vaivasvata); (ई),<BR>f. a patronymic of Yamī; the south, the southern<BR>quarter.<BR>—वैवस्वत-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a cele-<BR>brated shrine and Tīrtha.<BR>—वैवस्वत-मन्वन्-<BR>तर, अम्, n., N. of the seventh or present Manv-<BR>antara, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिक|वैवाहिकः
वैवाहिक वैवाहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-वाह),<BR>belonging or relating to marriage, matrimonial, nup-<BR>tial; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a marriage, wedding; (अस्),<BR>m. a son's father-in-law or a daughter's father-in-law,<BR>i. e. the father of a son's wife or of a daughter's<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाह्य
वैवाह्य, अस्, -ही, अम्, relating to marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवृत्त
वैवृत्त वैवृत्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-वृत्ति), of<BR>or belonging to Vi-vṛtti; (अस्), m. a particular modi-<BR>fication of Vedic accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशद्य|वैशद्यं
वैशद्य वैशद्य, अम्, n. (fr. वि-शद), white-<BR>ness; cleanness, purity, clearness, perspicuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशन्त
वैशन्त वैशन्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वेशन्त),<BR>Ved. belonging to the Soma ladle or cup; (अम्), n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">Page0970-c+ 75</a>]<BR>a cup of Soma juice, (according to modern scholars<BR>Vaiśanta in Ṛg-veda VII. 33, 2. is probably the<BR>name of a river.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशम्पायन|वैशंपायन|वैशंपायनः|वैशम्पायनः
वैशम्पायन वैशम्पायन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>celebrated sage (the original teacher of the Taittirīya-<BR>saṃhitā or collection of hymns of the Black Yajur-<BR>veda, see तैत्तिरीय-संहिता; he was also the nar-<BR>rator of the Mahā-bhārata to Janam-ejaya); N. of the<BR>author of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशम्पायनीय|वैशंपायनीय
वैशम्पायनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, of or belonging to<BR>Vaiśampāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशली
वैशली वैशली, f. [cf. विशला], N. of a town<BR>to the north of Pāṭali-putra; [cf. वैशाली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस|वैशसं
वैशस वैशस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. a form वि-शस,<BR>derived fr. वि-शस्; cf. वि-शसन), relating to<BR>slaughter or destruction, destructive; (अम्), n.<BR>rending in pieces; slaughter, destruction; distress,<BR>pain, anguish, hindrance, impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस्त्र|वैशस्त्रं
वैशस्त्र 1. वैशस्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. वि-शस्तृ),<BR>government, sway, rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस्त्र|वैशस्त्रं
2. वैशस्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. वि-शस्त्र), the state of<BR>being unarmed, defencelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाख|वैशाखं|वैशाखः
वैशाख वैशाख, अस्, m. (fr. वि-शाखा), the<BR>first of the twelve months constituting the Hindū<BR>solar year (answering to April-May); a churning-<BR>stick; (अम्), n. a particular attitude in shooting<BR>(standing with the feet a span apart); (ई), f. the day<BR>of full moon in the month Vaiśākha (= रक्त-पु-<BR>नर्नवा); N. of a wife of Vasu-deva.<BR>—वैशाख-<BR>वदि, ind. in the dark half of the month Vaiśākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाख्य
वैशाख्य, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशारद्य|वैशारद्यं
वैशारद्य वैशारद्य, अम्, n. (fr. विशारद),<BR>cleverness, expertness, skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाल
वैशाल वैशाल, अस्, m. (fr. विशाल), N. of a<BR>Muni; (ई), f., N. of a town [cf. विशाला]; of a wife<BR>of Vasu-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिक|वैशिकः
वैशिक वैशिक, अस्, m. (fr. वेश्या), a parti-<BR>cular kind of Nāyaka or lover (in erotic poetry), one<BR>who associates with courtezans; (अम्), n. harlotry,<BR>the allurements of harlots, arts of courtezans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्ट|वैशिष्टं
वैशिष्ट वैशिष्ट, अम्, n. (fr. वि-शिष्ट), dis-<BR>tinction, difference (= वैशिष्ट्य below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्ट्य|वैशिष्ट्यं
वैशिष्ट्य, अम्, n. endowment with some dis-<BR>tinguishing property or attribute, endowment with,<BR>possession of; distinction, peculiarity, difference, the<BR>state of distinguishing or being distinguished, differ-<BR>encing; excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिक|वैशेषिकः
वैशेषिक वैशेषिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विशेष),<BR>characteristic; belonging to the Vaiśeṣika doctrine,<BR>(in this sense fr. वैशेषिक, अम्, n.); (अस्), m.<BR>a follower of the Vaiśeṣika doctrine; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of one of the two great divisions of the<BR>Nyāya school of philosophy founded by Kaṇāda,<BR>(it was probably a later development of the other<BR>great division or ‘Nyāya proper’ founded by Gau-<BR>tama, with which it agrees in its analytical method<BR>of treating the various subjects of inquiry, but from<BR>which it differs in propounding only seven categories<BR>or topics instead of sixteen; and more especially in<BR>its doctrine of विशेष, ‘particularity or individual<BR>essence,’ i. e. in its maintaining the eternally distinct<BR>or sui generis nature of the nine substances, air, fire,<BR>water, earth, mind, ether, time, space, and soul, of<BR>which the first five, including mind, are held to be<BR>atomic: the seven Padārthas or categories are,<BR>1. Dravya, ‘substance,’ divided into nine, as above<BR>stated; 2. Guṇa, ‘quality,’ of which there are twenty-<BR>four [see गुण]; 3. Karman, ‘action;’ 4. Sāmānya,<BR>‘genus’ and ‘species;’ 5. Viśeṣa, ‘particularity,’<BR>described above; 6. Samavāya, ‘co-inherence’ or<BR>‘perpetual intimate connection;’ 7. A-bhāva, ‘non-<BR>existence’ or ‘privation:’ Kaṇāda's system allows<BR>only two of the Pramāṇas, i. e. instruments or means<BR>of obtaining true knowledge, of the four admitted by<BR>the Nyāya proper, viz. प्रत्यक्ष or knowledge<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">Page0971-a+ 76</a>]<BR>arising from contact of a sense with its object, and<BR>अनुमान, inference of three kinds [a priori, a pos-<BR>teriori, and analogy], but the other Pramāṇas are<BR>said by some to be contained in these two; the<BR>system is taught in the form of Sūtras, and the<BR>Vaiśeṣika-sūtras, like those of the Nyāya proper,<BR>have been commented on by a triple set of com-<BR>mentaries, and expounded in various works, of which<BR>the best known are the Bhāṣā-pariccheda with its<BR>commentary, called Siddhānta-muktāvalī, and the<BR>Tarka-saṅgraha.)<BR>—वैशेषिक-सूत्र, अम्, n. the<BR>aphorisms of the Vaiśeṣika branch of the Nyāya<BR>philosophy (attributed to Kaṇāda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेष्य|वैशेष्यं
वैशेष्य, अम्, n. specific or generic distinction;<BR>difference, superiority, pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्य|वैश्यः
वैश्य वैश्य, अस्, m. (fr. 2. विश्), ‘a man<BR>who occupies the soil,’ ‘a man of the people,’ a<BR>Vaiśya or man of the third caste whose business was<BR>agriculture and trade; (आ), f. a woman of the Vaiśya<BR>caste.<BR>—वैश्य-कन्या, f. a Vaiśya damsel, girl of the<BR>agricultural class.<BR>—वैश्य-कर्मन्, अ, n. or वैश्य-<BR>क्रिया, f. the business of a Vaiśya, agriculture, trade.<BR>—वैश्य-ता, f. the state or condition of a Vaiśya,<BR>(वैश्यतां गम्, to become a Vaiśya.)<BR>—वैश्य-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. the mode of life or occupation of a<BR>Vaiśya, agriculture, trade.<BR>—वैश्या-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>born of a Vaiśya woman, the child of a Vaiśya mother.<BR>—वैश्या-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of a Vaiśya mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवण|वैश्रवणः
वैश्रवण वैश्रवण, अस्, m. (fr. वि-श्रवस्),<BR>‘son of Viśravas,’ epithet of Kuvera, the god of<BR>wealth; of Rāvaṇa (younger brother of Kuvera);<BR>N. of the fourteenth Muhūrta.<BR>—वैश्रवणानुज<BR>(˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, m. the younger brother of Kuvera, i. e.<BR>Rāvaṇa.<BR>—वैश्रवणालय (˚ण-आल्˚) or वैश्र-<BR>वणावास (˚ण-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘abode of Kuvera,’ the<BR>Indian fig-tree (= वट).<BR>—वैश्रवणोदय (˚ण-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘Kuvera's glory,’ the Indian fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेव|वैश्वदेवः
वैश्वदेव वैश्वदेव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विश्व-<BR>देव), belonging or dedicated to the Viśva-devas or<BR>Viśve-devāḥ, (वैश्वदेवो लोकः, the world of the<BR>Viśva-devas, Manu IV. 183); offered to the Viśva-<BR>devas; relating to all the divinities; (अम्), n. an<BR>offering or sacrifice to the Viśva-devas; an offering<BR>to all deities (said to be performed by casting a little<BR>food into fire before a meal); (ई), f. the eighth<BR>day of the second half of the month Māgha; a<BR>species of the Paṅkti metre.<BR>—वैश्वदेव-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. an oblation to the Viśva-devas; an offering to<BR>the deities collectively.<BR>—वैश्वदेव-होम, अम्,<BR>n. oblation to the Viśva-devas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वानर|वैश्वानरः
वैश्वानर वैश्वानर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विश्वा-<BR>नर), relating to or fit for all men, present with<BR>all men, common to all mankind, benefiting all men;<BR>(अस्), m. ‘son of Viśvā-nara,’ epithet of Agni or Fire,<BR>(Agni Vaiśvānara is regarded as the author of the<BR>hymns Ṛg-veda X. 79, 80); the fire of digestion;<BR>N. of a Dānava; (in the Vedānta phil.) ‘the Spirit<BR>of Humanity,’ N. of Intellect located in the collective<BR>aggregate of bodies, the general consciousness; (ई),<BR>f. a particular sacrifice performed at the beginning of<BR>every year; a particular division of the sun's path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वानरीय
वैश्वानरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to Vaiśvā-<BR>nara; (अम्), n., scil. सूक्त, a particular Vedic hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वामित्र
वैश्वामित्र वैश्वामित्र, अस्, m. (fr. विश्वा-<BR>मित्र), a son or descendant of Viśvā-mitra, a patro-<BR>nymic of several Vedic Ṛṣis; (ई), f. a female<BR>descendant of Viśvā-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वासिक
वैश्वासिक वैश्वासिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. वि-<BR>श्वास), deserving confidence, trustworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वी
वैश्वी वैश्वी, f. (fr. विश्व), N. of the Nak-<BR>ṣatra called Uttarā Aṣāḍhā or Uttarāṣāḍhā (so called<BR>because the Viśva-devas preside over this asterism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषम्य|वैषम्यं
वैषम्य वैषम्य, अम्, n. (fr. विषम),<BR>inequality, unevenness, oddness (opposed to evenness);<BR>difficulty; calamity, misery, distress; injustice, harsh-<BR>ness; solitariness, singleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषयिक|वैषयिकः
वैषयिक वैषयिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विषय),<BR>relating to an object, having for an object, (the<BR>आधार of an action is called वैषयिक when it<BR>is the aim or object of the action); belonging or<BR>relating to an object of sense, sensual, carnal; (अस्),<BR>m. a sensualist, one addicted to the pleasures of sense,<BR>one occupied with worldly objects or interests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषुवत
वैषुवत वैषुवत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विषु-वत्),<BR>relating to the equinox, equinoctial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्टुत|वैष्टुतं
वैष्टुत वैष्टुत, अम्, n. (fr. वि-ष्टुत), the<BR>ashes of a burnt-offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्ट्र|वैष्ट्रं|वैष्ट्रः
वैष्ट्र वैष्ट्र, अम्, n. (in Uṇādi-s. IV. 159.<BR>fr. rt. 1. विश्), the world, a division of the universe,<BR>= पिष्टप; (अस्), m. (?), the sky (= 3. दिव्); air,<BR>wind (= वायु); N. of Viṣṇu (according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्णव|वैष्णवं|वैष्णवः
वैष्णव वैष्णव, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or be-<BR>longing to Viṣṇu; worshipping Viṣṇu; (अस्), m.<BR>‘a worshipper or follower of Viṣṇu,’ N. of one of<BR>the three great divisions of modern Hindū sects,<BR>(the other two being the Śaivas and Śāktas; the<BR>Vaiṣṇavas believe in the supremacy of Viṣṇu over<BR>the other gods of the Tri-mūrti; they are divided<BR>into six principal sects, as follow, 1. the Rāmānujas<BR>or Śrī-sampradāyins, founded by the celebrated re-<BR>former Rāmānuja, who flourished in the south of<BR>India towards the latter part of the twelfth century;<BR>the most striking peculiarity of this sect, who are<BR>chiefly found in the south, is the scrupulous preparation<BR>and privacy of their meals; they are distinguished by<BR>two perpendicular white lines drawn from the root<BR>of the hair to the commencement of each eyebrow,<BR>and a connecting transverse streak across the root of<BR>the nose; their chief authoritative works are the<BR>Vedānta-sūtras and other Vedānta works, the Pañca-<BR>rātra of Nārada, the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa and other Pu-<BR>rāṇas: 2. the Rāmānandas, a sect founded by Rāmā-<BR>nanda, disciple of Rāmānuja, and very numerous in<BR>Gangetic India; they worship Viṣṇu under the form<BR>of Rāma-candra and his consort Sītā; their favourite<BR>work is the Bhakta-mālā: 3. the followers of Kabīr,<BR>a celebrated disciple of Rāmānanda, principally found<BR>in upper and central India; they do not observe all the<BR>ceremonies of the Hindūs, but conform to the usages<BR>of caste, and pay a sort of respect to Viṣṇu: 4. the<BR>Vallabhācāryas or Rudra-sampradāyins, see वल्ल-<BR>भाचार्य; this sect draws its doctrines from the<BR>Bhāgavata-Purāṇa and works of Vallabha: 5. the<BR>Mādhvas or Brahma-sampradāyins, founded by Ma-<BR>dhvācārya, who is regarded by his followers as an<BR>incarnation of Vāyu, the god of wind; they are<BR>found especially in the south of India, and appear to<BR>combine with their worship of Viṣṇu a friendly<BR>leaning towards the god Śiva: 6. the Vaiṣṇavas of<BR>Bengal, a sect founded by Caitanya, who is regarded<BR>as an incarnation of Kṛṣṇa; their chief ritual con-<BR>sists in constantly repeating the name of Kṛṣṇa);<BR>scil. यज्ञ, a particular sacrificial ceremony; epithet<BR>of the asterism Śravaṇa; (ई), f. the personified Śakti<BR>of Viṣṇu (regarded as one of the Mātṛs); N. of<BR>Durgā; the plant Clitoria Ternatea (= अ-पराजिता);<BR>Asparagus Racemosus (= शतावरी); sacred basil,<BR>Ocymum Sanctum; (अम्), n. a particular kind of<BR>prodigy or omen (belonging to or occurring in the<BR>परं दिवम् or upper sky), the ashes of a burnt-<BR>offering.<BR>—वैष्णव-त्व, अम्, n. belief in Viṣṇu,<BR>the worship of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वैष्णव-पुराण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—वैष्णव-शास्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of an astrological work by Nārāyaṇa-dāsa-<BR>siddha (= प्रश्नार्णव).<BR>—वैष्णव-सिद्धान्त-<BR>दीपिका, f., N. of a work by Rāma-candra.<BR>—वैष्-<BR>णवाकूत-चन्द्रिका (˚व-आक्˚), f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa by Ratna-garbha.<BR>—वैष्णवाचमन (˚व-आच्˚), अम्, n. sipping<BR>water three times in the worship of Viṣṇu.<BR>—वैष्-<BR>णवाचर (˚व-आच्˚), अस्, m. the rites or practices of<BR>the Vaiṣṇavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसारिण|वैसारिणः
वैसारिण वैसारिण, अस्, m. (fr. वि-सारिन्), a<BR>fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसूचन|वैसूचनं
वैसूचन वैसूचन, अम्, n. (fr. वि-सूचन),<BR>assumption of female attire by a man (in the drama).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहायस|वैहायसं
वैहायस वैहायस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. विहायस्),<BR>being in the air, aerial, suspended in the air; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहार्य|वैहार्य्य|वैहार्य्यः
वैहार्य वैहार्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वि-हार), to<BR>be played or sported with, to be conciliated by<BR>pleasantry (applied to a wife's brother or brother-in-<BR>law or other relations of a wife).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहासिक|वैहासिकः
वैहासिक वैहासिक, अस्, m. (fr. वि-हास), a<BR>comic actor, buffoon; an actor (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोच्
वोच् वोच्. See under rt. वच्, p. 877.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोटा
वोटा वोटा, f. (perhaps more correctly writ-<BR>ten बोटा = पोटा, q. v.), a female servant or slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोड्र|वोड्रः
वोड्र वोड्र, अस्, m. (etymology doubtful),<BR>a kind of large snake, the Bor or Boa Constrictor<BR>(= गो-नस); a sort of fish; (ई), f. the fourth part<BR>of a Paṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढव्य|वोढव्यः
वोढव्य वोढव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. वह्),<BR>to be borne or carried; able to be borne, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढु|वोढुः
वोढु, उस्, m. the son of a woman living in her<BR>father's house (whose husband is absent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढृ
वोढृ, ढा, ढ्री, ढृ, one who carries or bears<BR>or draws, carrying, bearing, drawing; (ढा), m. a<BR>bearer, porter; a leader, guide; a charioteer; a<BR>draught-horse; a bull; a bridegroom; [cf. Lat.<BR>vector.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोण्ट|वोंट|वोंटः|वोण्टः
वोण्ट वोण्ट, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वुण्ट्?), a stalk,<BR>stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोद|वोदः
वोद वोद, अस्, आ, अम् (etymology doubtful),<BR>wet, moist, damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोदाल|वोदालः
वोदाल वोदाल, अस्, m. the sheat fish, Si-<BR>lurus Boalis (= पाठीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोपदेव
वोपदेव वोप-देव, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Mugdha-bodha grammar, the Kavi-kalpa-<BR>druma, and various other works (including, according<BR>to some, the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa; he was a son of<BR>Keśava and pupil of Dhaneśvara, and is said to have<BR>flourished about the latter half of the thirteenth<BR>century at the court of Hemādri, king of Deva-giri,<BR>now Dowlatabad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोपालित
वोपालित वोपालित or वोपालित-सिंह, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोर
वोर वोर, अस्, m. (probably not a Sanskrit<BR>word), a sort of pulse, Dolichos Catjang.<BR>—वोर-<BR>पट्टी, f. a sort of mat or mattress for sleeping on<BR>(perhaps made of the straw of the Vora).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरक|वोरकः
वोरक वोरक, अस्, m. (= वोलक), a scribe,<BR>writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरट|वोरटः
वोरट वोरट, अस्, m. a sort of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरव|वोरवः
वोरव वोरव, अस्, m. a kind of rice (perhaps<BR>that called Boro, which is cut in March or April).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरुखान|वोरुखानः
वोरुखान वोरुखान, अस्, m. a horse (de-<BR>scribed as one of a white and red colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल|वोलं|वोलः
वोल वोल, अम्, n. gum-myrrh (= रक्ता-<BR>पह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोलक|वोलकः
वोलक वोलक, अस्, m. [cf. वोरक], a<BR>scribe, writer; (इका), f. a sort of cake or pudding<BR>made with flour and sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल्लासक
वोल्लासक वोल्लासक, N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल्लाह|वोल्लाहः
वोल्लाह वोल्लाह, अस्, m. a kind of horse<BR>(with a light mane and tail).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोळ्हृ
वोळ्हृ वोऌहृ, ऌहा, m., Ved. = वोढृ, a<BR>bearer, carrier; an animal used for draught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोहित्थ|वोहित्थं|वोहित्थः
वोहित्थ वोहित्थ, अम्, n. a vessel, ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वौद्ध|वौद्धं
वौद्ध वौद्ध, अम्, n. (for बौद्ध), the<BR>collective body of Buddhist writings, (applied also to<BR>other infidel writings such as those of the Jainas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वौषट्
वौषट् वौषट्, ind. (perhaps for a form<BR>वोक्षत् fr. rt. 1. वह्, and meaning ‘may he, i. e.<BR>Agni, carry the offering to the gods;’ according to<BR>others merely a lengthened form of वषट्, q. v.), an<BR>exclamation or formula used on offering an oblation to<BR>the gods or Manes with fire; [cf. Zend vaoshaṭ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्य|व्यः
व्य 1. व्य, अस्, m. (fr. rt. व्ये), a coverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्य|व्यः
व्य 2. व्य (contracted fr. अव्यय), a techni-<BR>cal symbol for indeclinables such as नि, चित्, स्वर्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंश
व्यंश व्य्-अंश, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vi-<BR>pracitti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशक|व्यंशकः
व्य्-अंशक, अस्, m. a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशुक|व्यंशुकः
व्यंशुक व्य्-अंशुक, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>garment, undressed, naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंस्
व्यंस् व्य्-अंस् (वि-अंस्), cl. 10. P. -अंसयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to divide asunder, divide; to render useless<BR>or harmless, foil, ward off; to deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसक|व्यंसकः
व्य्-अंसक, अस्, m. a cheat, rogue, juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसन|व्यंसनं
व्य्-अंसन, अम्, n. cheating, tricking, deceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसनीय
व्य्-अंसनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be deceived or cheated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसित|व्यंसितः
व्य्-अंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, tricked, deceived, cheated;<BR>disappointed in one's expectations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंस
व्यंस व्य्-अंस, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. without a<BR>shoulder, shoulderless, mutilated, (Sāy. = विगतांस-<BR>छिन्न-बाहु); (अस्), m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्त|व्यक्तः
व्यक्त व्य्-अक्त, व्य्-अक्ति. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्ष्
व्यक्ष् व्य्-अक्ष् (वि-अक्ष्), cl. 1. 5. P. -अक्षति,<BR>-अक्ष्णोति, &c. = व्य्-अश्, to pervade, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्ष|व्यक्षः
व्यक्ष व्य्-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, (in astronomy)<BR>having no latitude; [cf. निर्-अक्ष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्र|व्यग्रः
व्यग्र व्य्-अग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, bewildered, per-<BR>plexed, distracted; agitated, alarmed, frightened;<BR>zealous, eager, eagerly engaged in, occupied, zealously<BR>occupied; (अस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—व्यग्र-ता,<BR>f. or व्यग्र-त्व, अम्, n. perplexedness, perplexity,<BR>confusion, anxiety; zealous occupation, zeal.<BR>—व्य-<BR>ग्र-पुरन्ध्रि-वर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having compa-<BR>nies of matrons zealously occupied.<BR>—व्यग्र-मनस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, perplexed or bewildered in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्ग|व्यंग|व्यङ्गः
व्यङ्ग व्य्-अङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, limbless, de-<BR>formed, mutilated; lamed, lame; bodiless; ill-<BR>arranged; (अस्), m. a cripple; a frog; discoloration<BR>of the face, dark spots on the cheek.<BR>—व्यङ्ग-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. mutilation; the state of a cripple,<BR>maimedness.<BR>—व्यङ्गार्थ (˚ग-अर्˚), अस्, m. (in<BR>rhetoric) suggested sense or meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गय
व्यङ्गय, Nom. P. व्यङ्गयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>mutilate, maim, cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गार
व्यङ्गार व्य्-अङ्गार, अस्, आ, अम्, without char-<BR>coal, having no fire, (व्यङ्गारे, at the time when<BR>the burning charcoal is extinguished.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गुल|व्यंगुल|व्यंगुलं
व्यङ्गुल व्य्-अङ्गुल, अम्, n. the sixtieth part<BR>of an Aṅgula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यच्
व्यच् 1. व्यच् (probably connected with<BR>2. व्य्-अच्), cl. 6. P. विचति, विव्याच, व्य-<BR>चिष्यति, अव्यचीत् or अव्याचीत्, व्यचितुम्, to cheat,<BR>trick, defraud, deceive; to encompass, embrace, sur-<BR>round (Ved.); to pervade, contain (Ved.): Caus. व्या-<BR>चयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अविव्यचत्: Desid. विव्यचि-<BR>षति: Intens. वेविच्यते, वाव्यचीति or वाव्यक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यचस्
व्यचस्, अस्, n., Ved. anything which is expanded<BR>or spread, (Sāy. = व्याप्तम् अन्तरिक्षम्); expanse,<BR>amplitude, vastness, (Sāy. = व्यापन.)<BR>—व्यचस्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. expansive, (Sāy. = व्याप्ति-<BR>मत्, Ṛg-veda II. 3, 5); (according to some) emu-<BR>lous, (see Ṛg-veda VI. 25, 6, Nirukta VIII. 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यचिष्ठ
व्यचिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. expanding every-<BR>where, extending far and wide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यच्
व्यच् 2. व्य्-अच् or व्य्-अञ्च् (वि-अच्), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-अचति, -अञ्चति, -ते, -अञ्चितुम्, Ved. to force or bend<BR>asunder, sunder, separate; to make wide, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यच्यमान
व्य्-अच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being widened, being<BR>extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यज्
व्यज् व्य्-अज् (वि-अज्), cl. 1. P. -अजति, -अजितुम्,<BR>Ved. to throw in various directions, toss about, move<BR>to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यज|व्यजः
व्य्-अज, अस्, m. a fan (= व्य्-अजन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यजन|व्यजनं
व्य्-अजन, अम्, n. a palm-leaf or other substance<BR>used as a fan, a fan (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्ज्|व्यंज्
व्यञ्ज् व्य्-अञ्ज् (वि-अञ्ज्), cl. 7. P. A. -अनक्ति,<BR>अङ्क्ते, -अङ्क्तुम् or -अञ्जितुम्, to anoint thoroughly<BR>(Ved.); to decorate, adorn, make beautiful or hand-<BR>some (A., Ved.); to cause to appear, develop, mani-<BR>fest; to discriminate, make clear: Pass. -अज्यते, to<BR>be manifested or developed; to be expressed: Caus.<BR>-अञ्जयति, -यितुम्, to cause to appear, make clearly<BR>visible or manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्त|व्यक्तः
व्य्-अक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned, decorated, hand-<BR>some, beautiful (Ved.); caused to appear, manifested,<BR>developed, manifest, apparent, evident, specifically<BR>known or understood; specified, distinguished; spe-<BR>cific, individual; wise, learned; (अस्), m. ‘the mani-<BR>fested,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. ‘the discrete or<BR>discernible,’ that which is developed as the product<BR>of अ-व्यक्त, q. v. (in the Sāṅkhya philosophy);<BR>(अम्), ind. manifestly, evidently, clearly, certainly.<BR>—व्यक्त-गणित, अम्, n. calculation with known<BR>numbers, arithmetic.<BR>—व्यक्त-ता, f. or व्यक्त-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. distinctness, manifestation.<BR>—व्यक्त-तारक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having clear stars.<BR>—व्यक्त-दृष्टार्थ<BR>(˚ट-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, perceiving or witnessing a<BR>transaction with one's own eyes, any one present as<BR>an eye-witness, a witness (in general).<BR>—व्यक्त-<BR>भुज्, क्, क्, क्, consuming everything manifested or<BR>all visible things (said of time).<BR>—व्यक्त-राशि, इस्,<BR>f. (in arithmetic) known or absolute quantity.<BR>—व्यक्-<BR>त-रूप, अस्, m. ‘having a manifested form,’ epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—व्यक्त-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a<BR>discernible shape.<BR>—व्यक्त-लक्ष्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>having evident signs, having clear marks, clearly<BR>characterised.<BR>—व्यक्त-विक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, dis-<BR>playing valour.<BR>—व्यक्ती-करण, अम्, n. the act of<BR>making manifest or clear or distinct.<BR>—व्यक्ती-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>manifest, make clear or distinct.<BR>—व्यक्ती-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made clear or manifest, made distinct.<BR>—व्यक्ती-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become clearly visible, be distinct or clear.<BR>—व्यक्ती-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become clearly visible, distinct,<BR>clear.<BR>—व्यक्तोदित (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, spoken<BR>clearly or plainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्ति|व्यक्तिः
व्य्-अक्ति, इस्, f. visible appearance or manifestation,<BR>making clear or evident, clearness, distinctness, dis-<BR>cernibility, discrimination; specific appearance or<BR>variation, individuality; a person, an individual (op-<BR>posed to जाति), variety; gender (in gram.); case,<BR>inflection, the proper form of any inflected word;<BR>a vowel (?).<BR>—व्यक्ति-ता, f. or व्यक्ति-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>distinctness, individuality, personality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्ग्य|व्यंग्य|व्यङ्ग्यः
व्य्-अङ्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be indicated correctly,<BR>to be intimated by sarcastic allusions or insinuations<BR>(applied to figurative or poetical speech, allusive lan-<BR>guage or insinuation, sarcasm, covert expression of<BR>suspicion or contempt, &c.).<BR>—व्यङ्ग्योक्ति (˚य-<BR>उक्˚), इस्, f. covert language, sarcastic insinuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जक|व्यंजक|व्यञ्जकः
व्य्-अञ्जक, अस्, इका, अम्, making clear, clearly<BR>showing, manifesting, indicating, denoting, declar-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. external indication of passion or feel-<BR>ing, gesture, dramatic action; feeling; a sign, mark,<BR>symbol; figurative expression or insinuation.<BR>—व्यञ्-<BR>जक-त्व, अम्, n. the containing figurative or allusive<BR>expressions, indication by covert insinuations or ellip-<BR>tical language.<BR>—व्यञ्जकार्थ (˚क-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>(in rhetoric) a suggestive or significant sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जन|व्यंजन|व्यंजनं|व्यञ्जनं
व्य्-अञ्जन, अम्, n. the act of making clear, mark-<BR>ing, distinguishing, indicating; a consonant (as mark-<BR>ing or distinguishing sound); a mark, spot, sign,<BR>token; insignia, paraphernalia; a mark or sign of<BR>puberty; the beard; mark of sex or gender, a privy<BR>part (male or female); anything used in dressing or<BR>preparing food, anything mixed with food, seasoning,<BR>sauce, condiment; a limb, member (= अव-यव);<BR>day, = दिन; (अम्, आ), n. f. figurative expression or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">Page0972-c+ 75</a>]<BR>insinuation; irony, sarcasm; (आ), f. the third power<BR>of a word, suggestion.<BR>—व्यञ्जन-सङ्गम, अस्,<BR>m. a collection or group of consonants.<BR>—व्यञ्जन-<BR>सन्धि, इस्, m. the junction of consonants (in gram-<BR>mar).<BR>—व्यञ्जन-सन्निपात, अस्, m. the falling<BR>together or conjunction of consonants.<BR>—व्यञ्जन-<BR>स्थाने, ind. in the place of condiment, as seasoning.<BR>—व्यञ्जना-वृत्ति, इस्, f. figurative or elliptical<BR>style.<BR>—व्यञ्जनोदय (˚न-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, fol-<BR>lowed by a consonant.<BR>—व्यञ्जनोपध (˚न-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, preceded by a consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जयत्
व्य्-अञ्जयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, making clearly visible<BR>or manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जिजिषु
व्य्-अञ्जिजिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to make clearly<BR>visible, trying to make manifest, wishing to detect<BR>or expose, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जित|व्यंजित
व्य्-अञ्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, clearly manifested or made<BR>visible, distinguished, marked, characterised.<BR>—व्यञ्-<BR>जित-वृत्ति-भेद, अस्, आ, अम्, having varying actions<BR>manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यडम्बक|व्यडंबक|व्यडंबकः|व्यडम्बकः
व्यडम्बक व्यडम्बक or व्यडम्बन or<BR>व्यडम्बर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. अड् with<BR>वि), the castor-oil plant, Ricinus Communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्
व्यत् व्यत्. See under rt. 1. वी, p. 953.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकृ
व्यतिकृ व्य्-अति-कृ (वि-अति-), cl. 8. A. -कु-<BR>रुते, &c., to act mutually or reciprocally: Pass.<BR>-क्रियते, to be greatly changed or moved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकर|व्यतिकरः
1. व्य्-अतिकर, अस्, आ, अम्, acting reciprocally, acting<BR>on or with one another, reciprocal; pervading,<BR>spreading through or over; contiguous to, in contact<BR>with; (अस्), m. reciprocal action, reciprocity, mutual<BR>relation, exchange, interchange; contact, contiguity,<BR>union; alternation; action (in general); obstruction,<BR>hindrance, reverse, misfortune, calamity; opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकृत
व्य्-अतिकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, pervaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकॄ
व्यतिकॄ व्य्-अति-कॄ (वि-अति-), Pass. -कीर्यते,<BR>&c., to be scattered in different directions; to be<BR>mixed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकर|व्यतिकरः
2. व्य्-अतिकर, अस्, m. a scattering in different<BR>directions, mixing or blending together, mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकीर्ण
व्य्-अतिकीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, scattered about in dif-<BR>ferent directions, mixed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रम्
व्यतिक्रम् व्य्-अति-क्रम् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-क्रामति, -क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to go or pass by,<BR>pass over or beyond; to elapse, be spent (said of<BR>time); to step over, transgress, offend against; to<BR>excel, surpass, conquer; to neglect, omit, violate,<BR>forget; to apply one's self to anything (acc.) in a<BR>wrong manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रम|व्यतिक्रमः
व्य्-अतिक्रम, अस्, m. passing over or beyond,<BR>transgressing, deviating; violating, non-performance,<BR>disregard, neglect, breach, (संविदो व्यतिक्रमः,<BR>violation or breach of a contract); inverted order,<BR>inversion, reverse, contrariety, opposition, the con-<BR>trary of anything, the contrary of right, crime, vice,<BR>fault, sin; the contrary of prosperity, adversity, mis-<BR>fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रमिन्
व्य्-अतिक्रमिन्, ई, इणी, इ, passing over, deviating,<BR>transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रम्य
व्य्-अतिक्रम्य, ind. having passed over or beyond,<BR>having transgressed or violated; having disregarded<BR>or neglected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रान्त|व्यतिक्रांत
व्य्-अतिक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, passed over; gone by,<BR>elapsed; transgressed, violated, retracted; neglected,<BR>disregarded; reversed, inverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिगम्
व्यतिगम् व्य्-अति-गम् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. -गच्-<BR>छति, -गन्तुम्, to go or pass by, to be spent (as<BR>time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिगत
व्य्-अतिगत, अस्, आ, अम्, passed by, elapsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिगा
व्यतिगा व्य्-अति-गा (वि-अति-), cl. 3. P. -जिगाति,<BR>गातुम्, to pass by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिचर्
व्यतिचर् व्य्-अति-चर् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. (ep.<BR>also A.) -चरति (-ते), -चरितुम्, to transgress against,<BR>commit an offence against, offend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिचुम्ब्
व्यतिचुम्ब् व्य्-अति-चुम्ब् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">Page0973-a+ 74</a>]<BR>-चुम्बति, -चुम्बितुम्, to kiss or touch closely, be<BR>in immediate contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिचुम्बित
व्य्-अतिचुम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, touching closely, in<BR>immediate contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिजल्प्
व्यतिजल्प् व्य्-अति-जल्प् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-जल्पति, -जल्पितुम्, to chatter together, gossip, talk<BR>with one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिजि
व्यतिजि व्य्-अति-जि (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-जयति, -ते, -जेतुम्, to overcome, surpass, excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतितन्
व्यतितन् व्य्-अति-तन् (वि-अति-), cl. 8. A. -त-<BR>नुते, -तनितुम्, to extend mutually, vie with each<BR>other in extending or spreading out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतितॄ
व्यतितॄ व्य्-अति-तॄ (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. -तरति,<BR>-तरितुम् or -तरीतुम्, to pass completely across, pass<BR>over successfully, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिनी
व्यतिनी व्य्-अति-नी (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. -नयति,<BR>&c., Ved. to allow to pass away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिभा
व्यतिभा व्य्-अति-भा (वि-अति-), cl. 2. A. -भाते,<BR>-बभे, to shine forth fully or brightly (used imper-<BR>sonally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिभू
व्यतिभू व्य्-अति-भू (वि-अति-), cl. 1. A. -भ-<BR>वते, &c., to vie with any one (acc.), contend for<BR>precedence or superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिमर्श
व्यतिमर्श व्य्-अतिमर्श (वि-अति-), अस्, m. (in<BR>Vedic ritual) a particular kind of विहार, q. v., (it is<BR>described as the mutual transposition of the several<BR>Pādas or half verses or whole verses of the first and<BR>second Vālakhilya hymns which are repeated in sets,<BR>two being always taken together.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिमर्शम्
व्य्-अतिमर्शम्, ind., Ved. having skipped or<BR>passed over, having missed or taken alternately, alter-<BR>nating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिमुह्
व्यतिमुह् व्य्-अति-मुह् (वि-अति-), cl. 4. P. -मुह्-<BR>यति, &c., to be excessively perplexed or embarrassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिमूढ
व्य्-अतिमूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively perplexed<BR>or embarrassed, utterly distracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिया
व्यतिया व्य्-अति-या (वि-अति-), cl. 2. P. -याति,<BR>यातुम्, to go completely through, penetrate, per-<BR>vade (with acc., Ved.); to pass by, flow on (as<BR>time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतियात
व्य्-अतियात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone by, passed, spent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतियु
व्यतियु व्य्-अति-यु (वि-अति-), cl. 2. P., 9. P. A.<BR>-यौति, -युनाति, -युनीते, -यवितुम्, to join with<BR>one another, unite mutually, mix together, inter-<BR>mingle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरा
व्यतिरा व्य्-अति-रा (वि-अति-), cl. 2. A. -राते,<BR>व्य्-अत्य्-अरे, see Pāṇ. VI. 4, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरिच्
व्यतिरिच् व्य्-अति-रिच् (वि-अति-), Pass. -रिच्यते,<BR>to reach far beyond, leave behind, surpass, excel (with<BR>abl. or acc.); to be separated from, differ from, deviate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरिक्त|व्यतिरिक्तः
व्य्-अतिरिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, reaching beyond, passing<BR>or projecting beyond, surpassing, excelling, excessive,<BR>immoderate; separate, different from, distinct from:<BR>excepted; withdrawn, withheld; (अम्), ind. with<BR>the exception of, except, without (e. g. स्वर-व्˚,<BR>except the accent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेक|व्यतिरेकः
व्य्-अतिरेक, अस्, m. reaching or passing beyond, ex-<BR>celling, excellence; separation from, distinction, differ-<BR>ence, separateness, deviation; exception, exclusion,<BR>negation, interception; contrariety, contrast, dissimili-<BR>tude, a particular figure in rhetoric or poetry (the con-<BR>trasting of things compared in some respects with each<BR>other); logical discontinuance (opposed to अन्वय),<BR>negative inference; (एण), ind. with exception of,<BR>without; (ए), ind. on the contrary supposition.<BR>—व्य-<BR>तिरेक-व्याप्ति, इस्, f. ‘pervasion of difference or<BR>dissimilitude,’ a comprehensive argument derived<BR>from negation or non-existence of certain qualities.<BR>—व्यतिरेकालङ्कार (˚क-अल्˚), अस्, m. the rheto-<BR>rical figure called Vyatireka, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेकिन्
व्य्-अतिरेकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, passing beyond, excelling,<BR>distinguishing, discriminating; excepting; different,<BR>reverse.<BR>—व्यतिरेकि-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. an exclusive<BR>mark, i. e. a negative property (which excludes its<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">Page0973-b+ 74</a>]<BR>subject from the class possessing the corresponding<BR>positive property).<BR>—व्यतिरेक्य्-उदाहरण, अम्, n.<BR>illustration by contrast or negation (of certain pro-<BR>perties).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरुह्
व्यतिरुह् व्य्-अति-रुह् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. -रो-<BR>हति, -रोढुम्, to pass into various states of being,<BR>attain to or obtain another (state): Caus. -रोपयति<BR>or -रोहयति, -यितुम्, to eject, expel, remove, dis-<BR>possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरोपित
व्य्-अतिरोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, ejected, displaced, ex-<BR>pelled, ousted, dispossessed, removed from rightful<BR>possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिलङ्घिन्
व्यतिलङ्घिन् व्य्-अतिलङ्घिन्, ई, इनी, इ, passing<BR>or falling away from, slipping away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिलू
व्यतिलू व्य्-अति-लू (वि-अति-), cl. 9. A. -लुनीते<BR>(also P. -लुनाति if joined with इतरेतर, अन्योन्य,<BR>or परस्पर, see Pāṇ. 1. 3, 16), -लवितुम्, to cut<BR>or hurt one another, cut mutually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिवह्
व्यतिवह् व्य्-अति-वह् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. A. -व-<BR>हते, &c., to bear mutually or reciprocally, (see<BR>Vopa-deva XXIII. 55.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिवृत्
व्यतिवृत् व्य्-अति-वृत् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. A. -वर्-<BR>तते, &c. (in Fut., Cond., and Aor. also P., see rt.<BR>1. वृत्), -वर्तितुम्, to go or pass over, pass through;<BR>to escape, avoid; to glide or pass away, elapse; to<BR>depart from (with abl.), leave, quit, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषञ्ज्|व्यतिषंज्
व्यतिषञ्ज् व्य्-अति-षञ्ज् (वि-अति-सञ्ज्), cl. 1.<BR>P. -षजति (sometimes A. -षजते), -षङ्क्तुम्,<BR>to connect mutually, mix together (P.); to change<BR>(A.): Pass. -षज्यते, to be mutually connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषक्त
व्य्-अतिषक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, mutually connected or<BR>joined or related, &c.; intermarried, intermarrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषङ्ग|व्यतिषंग|व्यतिषंगः|व्यतिषङ्गः
व्य्-अतिषङ्ग, अस्, m. mutual connection, reci-<BR>procal junction or relation; fastening or tying to-<BR>gether; absorption (in Vedic grammar).<BR>—व्यति-<BR>षङ्ग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having mutual connection,<BR>connected, united, mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिसन्दह्|व्यतिसंदह्
व्यतिसन्दह् व्य्-अति-सन्-दह् (वि-अति-सम्-), cl.<BR>1. P. -दहति, -दग्धुम्, to burn up entirely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिसृप्
व्यतिसृप् व्य्-अति-सृप् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. -सर्-<BR>पति, -सर्प्तुम् or -स्रप्तुम्, to move to and fro,<BR>fly in every direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिसर्पत्
व्य्-अतिसर्पत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going or flying in all<BR>directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिहन्
व्यतिहन् व्य्-अति-हन् (वि-अति-), cl. 2. P.<BR>-हन्ति, -हन्तुम्, to strike one another; to strike<BR>again, strike in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिघ्नत्
व्य्-अतिघ्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, striking again or in<BR>return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिहस्
व्यतिहस् व्य्-अति-हस् (वि-अति-), cl. 1. P. -ह-<BR>सति, -हसितुम्, to laugh at each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिहृ
व्यतिहृ व्य्-अति-हृ (वि-अति-), cl. 1. A. -हरते,<BR>&c., to take or receive mutually, take in exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिहार|व्यतिहारः
व्य्-अतिहार, अस्, m. barter, exchange; reciprocity;<BR>exchange of blows or abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीहार|व्यतीहारः
व्य्-अतीहार, अस्, m. = व्य्-अतिहार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यती
व्यती 1. व्य्-अती (वि-अति-इ), cl. 2. P. व्यत्य्-<BR>एति, -एतुम्, to pass away or over, pass by, elapse;<BR>to go away, depart from, deviate or swerve from,<BR>leave (with abl.), take an irregular course; to go<BR>beyond, transgress, to pass a person or place (with<BR>acc.); to pass or spend (a fixed time, &c.); to sur-<BR>pass, excel, overcome, conquer; to disregard, neg-<BR>lect, omit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतियत्
व्य्-अतियत्, अन्, अती, अत्, passing away, passing by,<BR>&c.; disregarding, paying no attention to (any-<BR>thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीत|व्यतीतः
व्य्-अतीत, अस्, आ, अम्, passed away, passed by,<BR>elapsed, passed over, gone; departed, dead; departed<BR>from, left, abandoned; disregarded, omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीत्य
व्य्-अतीत्य, ind. having passed by, having gone<BR>through or passed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यय|व्यत्ययः
व्य्-अत्यय, अस्, m. passing or going away, going<BR>in a different direction, contrariety, opposition, oppo-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">Page0973-c+ 77</a>]<BR>sition to the usual rule, (व्यत्ययेन, by an irregu-<BR>larity, against the usual rule, in opposition to the usual<BR>rule); reverse; inverted or reverse order; transposi-<BR>tion, transmutation, interchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यती
व्यती 2. व्यती (perhaps connected with rt.<BR>1. वी or with व्य्-अती), Ved., according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda IV. 32, 17. व्यतीनाम् = गमनवताम्<BR>अश्वानाम्, of swift-going horses; on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>155, 6. व्यतीन् = विविधान् एव स्व-भावान्, various<BR>states or revolutions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीपात|व्यतीपातः
व्यतीपात व्य्-अतीपात, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पत् with<BR>वि and अति), falling entirely away, total departure,<BR>deviation from (right), excessive sin, great or por-<BR>tentous calamity, any portent or prodigy indicating<BR>or occasioning calamity (as a comet, earthquake,<BR>&c.); disrespect, contempt; the seventeenth of the<BR>astronomical Yogas; the day of new moon (when it<BR>falls on Ravi-vāra or Sunday, and when the moon<BR>is in certain mansions, such as Śravaṇā, Dhaniṣṭhā,<BR>&c.); a malignant aspect of the sun and moon<BR>(when they are on opposite sides of either solstice<BR>and their minutes of declination are the same; cf.<BR>वैधृत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीहार|व्यतीहारः
व्यतीहार व्य्-अतीहार. See व्य्-अति-हृ, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यस्
व्यत्यस् 1. व्य्-अत्य्-अस् (वि-अति-अस्), cl. 2. A.<BR>व्य्-अति-स्ते (1st sing. -अति-हे, 2nd sing. -अति-से, Pāṇ.<BR>VII. 4, 50, 52), to be above, excel, surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यस्
व्यत्यस् 2. व्य्-अत्य्-अस् (वि-अति-अस्), cl. 4. P.<BR>-अस्यति, -असितुम्, to throw or place in an inverted<BR>position, invert, place across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यस्त
व्य्-अत्यस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or placed in an<BR>inverted position, reversed, inverted, changed into<BR>the opposite; contrary, opposite, placed across or<BR>crosswise, crossed, (व्यत्यस्त-पाणिना, with crossed<BR>hands.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यास|व्यत्यासः
व्य्-अत्यास, अस्, m. inverted position, inverted or<BR>reverse order; contrariety, oppositeness, opposition,<BR>reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यासम्
व्य्-अत्यासम्, ind., Ved. having inverted, having<BR>placed crosswise; alternating, alternately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यूह्
व्यत्यूह् व्य्-अत्य्-ऊह् (वि-अति-ऊह्, see rt. 1. ऊह्),<BR>cl. 1. P. -ऊहति, -ऊहितुम्, Ved. to place or arrange<BR>differently; to be ever changing the order of any-<BR>thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्
व्यथ् व्यथ्, cl. 1. A. व्यथते (ep. also<BR>P. -ति), विव्यथे, व्यथिष्यते, अव्य-<BR>थिष्ट (Ved. व्यथिषत्), व्यथितुम् (Ved. Inf.<BR>व्यथिष्यै), to tremble, be agitated or disquieted<BR>or afflicted; to suffer pain, be sorrowful or unhappy<BR>or vexed, fall into misfortune; to be afraid of, fear<BR>(with abl.); to suffer; to dry, become dry: Pass.<BR>व्यथ्यते: Caus. व्यथयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अविव्य-<BR>थत्, to disquiet, pain, afflict, make uneasy; to destroy,<BR>baffle; to frighten; to lead or turn away: Desid.<BR>विव्यथिषते: Intens. वाव्यथ्यते, वाव्यत्ति; [cf.<BR>Goth. vithon; (perhaps also) Gr. ὄθη, ὄθομαι, ὠθέω,<BR>ἐνοσί-χθων, ἔννοσις.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथक|व्यथकः
व्यथक, अस्, इका, अम्, inflicting pain, paining,<BR>causing pain, torturing, painful; distressing, afflict-<BR>ing, causing alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथत्
व्यथत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, trembling, sorrowing,<BR>being in pain or trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथन|व्यथनं
व्यथन, अम्, n. the act of giving pain, paining;<BR>(in Vedic grammar) change, alteration, variation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथनीय
व्यथनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pained or afflicted,<BR>capable of being agitated or disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथमान
व्यथमान, अस्, आ, अम्, quivering, trembling,<BR>feeling pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथयत्
व्यथयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, paining, distressing,<BR>disquieting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथा
व्यथा, f. disquietude, perturbation, agitation;<BR>pain, agony; anguish, ache; distress; alarm, fear;<BR>disease.<BR>—व्यथा-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing pain<BR>(bodily or mental), painful, excruciating.<BR>—व्यथान्-<BR>वित (˚था-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, suffering pain, pained.<BR>—व्यथा-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, free from pain.<BR>—व्यथा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, full of pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथि
व्यथि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. agitated, quivering, moving<BR>about, troubled, distressed, (Sāy. = व्यथित, Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 59, 2; = चलित, X. 86, 2); (इस्), m. a weapon,<BR>(Sāy. = शस्त्र, Ṛg-veda VI. 28, 3); a malevolent<BR>or evil-disposed person, (Sāy. = बाधक, राक्षस,<BR>Ṛg-veda IV. 4, 3; = हिंसक, VI. 62, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथित|व्यथितः
व्यथित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, disquieted, per-<BR>turbed, pained, tortured; distressed, afflicted; dis-<BR>turbed, troubled; alarmed, frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथितव्य
व्यथितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pained or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथिस्
व्यथिस्, इस्, n., Ved. perturbation, anger (accord-<BR>ing to Naigh. II. 13; perhaps referrible to व्यथि<BR>above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्य
व्यथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pained or distressed,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्यमान
व्यथ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being disquieted or<BR>agitated, being pained or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्ययस्
व्यथ्ययस्, in Naigh. 1. 14. a various reading<BR>for अ-व्यथयस्, (see अ-व्यथि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यद्
व्यद् व्य्-अद् (वि-अद्), cl. 2. P. -अत्ति, -अत्तुम्,<BR>to bite through or on all sides, gnaw, nibble, eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्
व्यध् व्यध्, cl. 4. P. विध्यति, विव्याध,<BR>व्यत्स्यति, अव्यात्सीत्, व्यद्धुम् (ep.<BR>वेद्धुम्), to pierce, perforate; to strike, beat, smite,<BR>stab; to pick; to tear, hurt, wound; to wave in<BR>triumph: Pass. विध्यते, to be pierced: Caus. व्या-<BR>धयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अविव्यधत्: Desid. विव्यत्-<BR>सति: Intens. वेविध्यते, वाव्यद्धि (?); [cf. per-<BR>haps Gr. ϝεθ in ἄεθλος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्ध|विद्धः
विद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced, perforated, wounded,<BR>&c. See p. 920, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्धवा
विद्धवा, ind. having pierced, having struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यत्|विध्यन्त्
विध्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, piercing, perforating;<BR>stabbing, striking, wounding, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यमान
विध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being pierced or struck<BR>or wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध|वेधः
वेध, वेधक, &c. See p. 965, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध|व्यधः
व्यध, अस्, m. piercing, perforating; striking,<BR>smiting; a stroke, wound; (आ), f. bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधन
व्यधन, अम्, n. the act of piercing, perforating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्य|व्यध्यः
व्यध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pierced or wounded,<BR>(in this sense also व्याध्य); (अस्), m. an effigy or<BR>mark for archers to shoot at, a butt, target, (accord-<BR>ing to Śabda-k. = धनुर्-गुण ?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याध|व्याधं|व्याधः
व्याध, अस्, m. ‘one who pierces or wounds,’ a<BR>hunter, one who lives by killing deer, &c., (if re-<BR>garded as a particular caste, supposed to be the son<BR>of a Kṣatriya by a Sarvasvin mother); a low man,<BR>wicked person.<BR>—व्याध-ता, f. the state or busi-<BR>ness of a hunter.<BR>—व्याध-भीत, अस्, m. ‘afraid of<BR>hunters,’ a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाय
व्याधाय, Nom. A. व्याधायते, &c., to become<BR>a hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिन्
1. व्याधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing hunters, frequented<BR>by hunters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिन्
2. व्याधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, piercing, wounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधिकरण|व्यधिकरणं
व्यधिकरण व्य्-अधिकरण, अम्, n. the sub-<BR>sisting or inhering in different receptacles or subjects<BR>or substrata (sometimes applied to a loose or am-<BR>biguous argument; probably opposed to समाना-<BR>धिकरण, see विशेष-व्याप्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधित
व्यधित व्यधित, अस्, आ, अम् (a doubtful<BR>word), made, done (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्व|व्यध्वः
व्यध्व व्य्-अध्व, अस्, m. a bad road, wrong<BR>road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्वन्
व्य्-अध्वन्, आ, m., Ved. ‘having various paths,’<BR>epithet of Agni, (Sāy. = विविध-ज्वाल, Ṛg-veda 1.<BR>141, 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यन्
व्यन् व्य्-अन् (वि-अन्), cl. 2. P. -अनिति, -अनितुम्,<BR>Ved. to breathe through, breathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुधा
व्यनुधा व्य्-अनु-धा (वि-अनु-), cl. 3. A.<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, Ved. to unfold, display, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 166, 10. वि-धिरे =<BR>विविधं धारयन्ति, apparently connecting धिरे<BR>with वि and not with व्य्-अनु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनद्
व्यनुनद् व्य्-अनु-नद् (वि-अनु-), Caus. -ना-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">Page0974-b+ 75</a>]<BR>दयति, -यितुम्, to cause to resound or re-echo, fill<BR>with noise or cries, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनाद|व्यनुनादः
व्य्-अनुनाद, अस्, m. reverberation, loud and ex-<BR>tending sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनादयत्
व्य्-अनुनादयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to resound<BR>or reverberate, filling with sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यन्तर|व्यंतरः|व्यन्तरः
व्यन्तर व्य्-अन्तर, अस्, m. a kind of super-<BR>natural being, (eight classes are enumerated, viz.<BR>Piśāca, Bhūta, Yakṣa, Rākṣasa, Kinnara, Kim-<BR>puruṣa, Mahoraga, and Gandharva.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यन्वारभ्
व्यन्वारभ् व्य्-अन्व्-आ-रभ् (वि-अनु-आ-), cl. 1.<BR>A. -रभते, &c., Ved. to hold or touch on both<BR>sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यप्
व्यप् व्यप्, cl. 10. P. व्यापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to throw (= rt. 1. विप्); to throw away,<BR>diminish, waste; [cf. rt. व्यय्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपकृष्
व्यपकृष् व्य्-अप-कृष् (वि-अप-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-कर्षति, -कर्ष्टुम्, -क्रष्टुम्, to draw or drag<BR>away or off; to lead astray, seduce; to take off (as<BR>clothes), undress; to take away, remove, give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपकर्षत्
व्य्-अपकर्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, drawing off or away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपकृष्ट
व्य्-अपकृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn or dragged off,<BR>drawn aside, taken away, taken off, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपक्रम्
व्यपक्रम् व्य्-अप-क्रम् (वि-अप-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-क्रामति, -क्रमितुम्, to go away, move off, retire,<BR>depart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगम्
व्यपगम् व्य्-अप-गम् (वि-अप-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-गच्छति, -गन्तुम्, to go away, retire, retreat,<BR>escape, disappear; to move away from, be entirely<BR>removed from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगच्छत्
व्य्-अपगच्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going away, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगत
व्य्-अपगत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone away or off, gone;<BR>departed from, fallen away from (with abl.); disap-<BR>peared.<BR>—व्यपगत-शुच्, क्, क्, क्, one whose sor-<BR>row has departed, free from grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगम|व्यपगमः
व्य्-अपगम, अस्, m. going away, departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रप्
व्यपत्रप् व्य्-अप-त्रप् (वि-अप-), cl. 1. A.<BR>-त्रपते (ep. also P. -ति), -त्रपितुम्, -त्रप्तुम्, to<BR>turn away through shame or embarrassment; to be-<BR>come shy, be ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रप
व्य्-अपत्रप, अस्, आ, अम्, shameless, (in this word<BR>वि is privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रपत्
व्य्-अपत्रपत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, = व्य्-अपत्रपमाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रपमाण
व्य्-अपत्रपमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, turning away<BR>through shame, being ashamed; shy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिश्
व्यपदिश् व्य्-अप-दिश् (वि-अप-), cl. 3. 6. P.<BR>-दिदेष्टि, -दिशति, -देष्टुम्, to point out, indicate,<BR>represent, signify, mean, intend; to designate, name;<BR>to represent falsely, feign, pretend, hold forth as a<BR>pretext: Pass. -दिश्यते, to be represented or shown,<BR>(इति व्य्-अपदिश्यते, so it is represented, so it is said<BR>or intended or signified, such a form of expression<BR>is used): Caus. -देशयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be<BR>named after, call after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिशत्
व्य्-अपदिशत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, representing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिश्य
व्य्-अपदिश्य, ind. having represented or shown;<BR>having represented falsely, having feigned or pre-<BR>tended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिष्ट
व्य्-अपदिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, represented, signified,<BR>shown, informed, named; tricked; pleaded as a<BR>pretext or in excuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेश|व्यपदेशः
व्य्-अपदेश, अस्, m. representation, information,<BR>apprising, notice, hint; a particular form of speech;<BR>designation by name or appellation; a name, title,<BR>appellation; family, race; fame, renown; fraud,<BR>craft; stratagem, device, pretext, excuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेष्टृ
व्य्-अपदेष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, one who represents<BR>or shows, one who designates or names; one who<BR>represents falsely, one who pretends or makes pre-<BR>texts, deceiving, a cheat, impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदृश्
व्यपदृश् व्य्-अप-दृश् (वि-अप-), Pass. -दृश्-<BR>यते, to be clearly seen, be distinctly visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनश्
व्यपनश् व्य्-अप-नश् (वि-अप-), Caus. -ना-<BR>शयति, -यितुम्, to cause to disappear entirely, cause<BR>to perish, drive away, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनी
व्यपनी व्य्-अप-नी (वि-अप-), cl. 1. P. -न-<BR>यति, -नेतुम् (Ved. also -नयितुम्), to lead away,<BR>take away; to carry away, remove, drive away,<BR>banish; to take off, lay aside; to get rid of: Caus.<BR>-नाययति, -यितुम्, to cause to lead or carry away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनयत्
व्य्-अपनयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, leading or taking<BR>away, driving away, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनायित
व्य्-अपनायित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), caused<BR>to be led or taken away, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनीत
व्य्-अपनीत, अस्, आ, अम्, led off, taken away, taken<BR>off, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनीय
व्य्-अपनीय, ind. having led or taken away, hav-<BR>ing taken off or laid aside, having put away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनुद्
व्यपनुद् व्य्-अप-नुद् (वि-अप-), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>-नुदति, -ते, -नोत्तुम्, to drive away, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपमुच्
व्यपमुच् व्य्-अप-मुच् (वि-अप-), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>-मुञ्चति, -ते, &c., to loosen, take off, remove, lay<BR>aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपमुच्य
व्य्-अपमुच्य, ind. having loosed or taken off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपया
व्यपया व्य्-अप-या (वि-अप-), cl. 2. P. -याति<BR>(ep. also A. -ते), -यातुम्, to go away, retire from,<BR>withdraw; to pass away, disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपयात
व्य्-अपयात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone away, retired, with-<BR>drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरुध्
व्यपरुध् व्य्-अप-रुध्, cl. 7. P. A. -रुणद्-<BR>धि, -रुन्द्धे, to exclude from sovereignty or<BR>power, dethrone, dismiss, dispossess, (in Rāmāyaṇa<BR>II. 58, 23. [Bombay ed.] the Intens. form व्यप-<BR>रोरुधः occurs.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरुह्
व्यपरुह् व्य्-अप-रुह् (वि-अप-), Caus. -रोप-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to root up, eradicate, extirpate; to lay<BR>aside, remove, take off; to deprive of, expel from<BR>(with inst. or abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपण|व्यपरोपणं
व्य्-अपरोपण, अम्, n. the act of rooting up, extir-<BR>pating; expelling, removing; cutting up, cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपित
व्य्-अपरोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, rooted up, extirpated,<BR>eradicated; expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोप्य
व्य्-अपरोप्य, ind. having taken off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपवह्
व्यपवह् व्य्-अप-वह् (वि-अप-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-वहति, -ते, &c., to drive away, remove, expel; to<BR>manifest, display, exhibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोढ
व्य्-अपोढ, अस्, आ, अम्, driven or frightened away,<BR>expelled, removed; opposite, contrary, reverse; mani-<BR>fested, displayed, exhibited.<BR>—व्यपोढाभ्र (˚ढ-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the clouds driven away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह्य
व्य्-अपोह्य, ind. having driven away, having re-<BR>moved or got rid of; having passed through a place,<BR>(व्य्-अपोह्य and व्य्-अपोढ may equally be referred<BR>to व्य्-अपोह्, see rt. 1. ऊह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपवृज्
व्यपवृज् व्य्-अप-वृज् (वि-अप-), Caus. -वर्-<BR>जयति, -यितुम्, to leave off entirely, relinquish, give<BR>up, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपवर्जित
व्य्-अपवर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely relinquished<BR>or given up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपवृत्
व्यपवृत् व्य्-अप-वृत् (वि-अप-), cl. 1. A. -वर्-<BR>तते, &c. (see rt. 1. वृत्), to turn away from, leave;<BR>to desist from (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपव्यध्
व्यपव्यध् व्य्-अप-व्यध् (वि-अप-), cl. 4. P.<BR>-विध्यति, -व्यद्धुम्, to break to pieces, to throw<BR>or cast away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपविद्ध
व्य्-अपविद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, broken to pieces,<BR>thrown about in confusion, cast away, rejected, dis-<BR>carded.<BR>—व्यपविद्ध-वृषी-मठ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whose (ascetic) seats and cells were discarded or<BR>abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपसृज्
व्यपसृज् व्य्-अप-सृज् (वि-अप-), cl. 6. P.<BR>-सृजति, -स्रष्टुम्, to let go; to send away, dismiss,<BR>throw away, relinquish, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपसृप्
व्यपसृप् व्य्-अप-सृप् (वि-अप-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-सर्पति, -सर्प्तुम्, -स्रप्तुम्, to go away, creep<BR>away, run away, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपहृ
व्यपहृ व्य्-अप-हृ (वि-अप-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-हरति, -ते, -हर्तुम्, to take away, carry away,<BR>remove; to cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाकृति|व्यपाकृतिः
व्यपाकृति व्य्-अपाकृति, इस्, f. driving away,<BR>repelling, denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाकृष्
व्यपाकृष् व्य्-अपा-कृष् (वि-अप-आ-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-कर्षति, -कर्ष्टुम्, -क्रष्टुम्, to drag or draw<BR>away, tear off, tear away from, take away, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपानुद्
व्यपानुद् व्य्-अपा-नुद् (वि-अप-आ-), cl. 6. P.<BR>A. -नुदति, -ते, -नोत्तुम्, to drive away, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रि
व्यपाश्रि व्य्-अपा-श्रि (वि-अप-आ-), cl. 1. P.<BR>A. -श्रयति, -ते, -श्रयितुम्, to go to for refuge,<BR>seek refuge with, have recourse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रय|व्यपाश्रयः
व्य्-अपाश्रय, अस्, m. going away, secession; hav-<BR>ing recourse to, taking refuge with, relying upon,<BR>reliance on, trusting to; expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रित
व्य्-अपाश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has taken<BR>refuge with, relying upon, trusting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रित्य
व्य्-अपाश्रित्य, ind. having gone to for refuge,<BR>having taken refuge with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपे
व्यपे व्य्-अपे (वि-अप-इ), cl. 2. P. -अपैति,<BR>&c., -अपैतुम्, to go apart, go asunder, be severed<BR>or separated, separate; to go away, leave, depart,<BR>leave off, cease, stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेत
व्य्-अपेत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone apart or asunder,<BR>severed, separated; gone off or away, passed away,<BR>departed, got rid of; opposed to, contrary.<BR>—व्य-<BR>पेत-कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, having taint or guilt<BR>removed.<BR>—व्यपेत-धैर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has abandoned firmness.<BR>—व्यपेत-भय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or व्यपेत-भी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, one whose fears are<BR>gone, free from fear (= वीत-भी).<BR>—व्यपेत-हर्-<BR>ष, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्ष्
व्यपेक्ष् व्य्-अपेक्ष् (वि-अप-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-अपेक्षते, -एक्षितुम्, to look about for, look for,<BR>expect; to regard, mind, pay regard or attention to;<BR>to look back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्ष
व्य्-अपेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, looking about for, ex-<BR>pecting; expectant, waiting, attentive; regarding,<BR>minding; (आ), f. looking for, expectation; regard,<BR>consideration; mutual expectation or regard; mutual<BR>connection or relation; application, use; (in gram-<BR>mar) the mutual application of two rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षण|व्यपेक्षणं
व्य्-अपेक्षण, अम्, n. the act of looking for,<BR>expecting, expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षणीय
व्य्-अपेक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be looked for or<BR>expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षमाण
व्य्-अपेक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, looking about for,<BR>looking round, expecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षा
व्य्-अपेक्षा, f. See व्य्-अपेक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षित
व्य्-अपेक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, looked for, expected;<BR>mutually expected or looked to; mutually related;<BR>employed, applied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षितव्य
व्य्-अपेक्षितव्य or व्य्-अपेक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>to be looked for or expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोढ
व्यपोढ व्य्-अपोढ, व्य्-अपोह्य. See under<BR>व्य्-अप-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह्
व्यपोह् व्य्-अपोह् (वि-अप-ऊह्), cl. 1. P. -अपो-<BR>हति (ep. also A. -ते), -अपोहितुम्, to drive away<BR>from, keep off; to remove; to atone for, expiate,<BR>destroy; to heal, cure (sickness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह|व्यपोहः
व्य्-अपोह, अस्, m. driving away, keeping off,<BR>destroying.<BR>—व्यपोह-स्तव, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोहमान
व्य्-अपोहमान, अस्, आ, अम्, taking away, remov-<BR>ing; putting out, extinguishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह्य
व्य्-अपोह्य. See under व्य्-अप-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचर्
व्यभिचर् व्य्-अभि-चर्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.)<BR>-चरति (-ते), -चरितुम्, to act in an unfriendly way<BR>towards (with acc. or gen.), commit an offence<BR>against, offend, injure; to bewitch, practise sorcery;<BR>to go away, depart or deviate from; to go astray;<BR>to go wrong, fail, miscarry; to go beyond, trans-<BR>gress, exceed, surpass (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचार|व्यभिचारः
व्य्-अभिचार, अस्, m. going or departing from,<BR>wandering away, going astray, deviation, leaving or<BR>abandoning (the right way), following improper<BR>courses, doing what is prohibited or wicked; erring,<BR>straying, error, trespass, transgression, crime, vice,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">Page0975-b+ 80</a>]<BR>sin, profligacy, adultery, infidelity of a wife, &c.;<BR>wandering from an argument, erroneous or fallacious<BR>reasoning, the presence of the हेतु without the<BR>साध्य; straying from a rule, exception to a rule,<BR>irregularity, anomaly.<BR>—व्यभिचार-तस्, ind. in con-<BR>sequence of straying or erring; (in phil.) from the Vya-<BR>bhicāra involved in the other supposition.<BR>—व्यभि-<BR>चार-ता, f. or व्यभिचार-त्व, अम्, n. error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारिन्
व्य्-अभिचारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going astray, erring, tres-<BR>passing, deviating from (virtue), following or doing<BR>what is improper; profligate, wanton; untrue, false;<BR>irregular, anomalous; (a word) having a non-primi-<BR>tive or secondary meaning, having several meanings;<BR>(इणी), f. a wanton woman, unchaste wife, adulteress;<BR>(इ), n. anything transitory, a transitory feeling or<BR>state, (opposed to स्थायि, ‘a lasting state,’ q. v., and<BR>forming a particular condition of the mind or body<BR>described in poetical compositions; these Vyabhicāri-<BR>bhāvas are said to be thirty-four in number, viz.<BR>1. निर्वेद, disgust, despondency; 2. ग्लानि, ex-<BR>haustion, emaciation; 3. शङ्का, apprehension;<BR>4. असूया, envy; 5. मद, intoxication; 6. श्रम,<BR>fatigue; 7. आलस्य, indolence, languor; 8. दैन्य,<BR>indigence, distress; 9. चिन्ता, anxious reflection or<BR>thought; 10. मोह, perplexity, distraction; 11.<BR>स्मृति, recollection, effort to remember; 12. धृति,<BR>calm enjoyment, satisfaction of mind; 13. व्रीडा,<BR>shame; 14. चपलता, unsteadiness, want of firm-<BR>ness; 15. हर्ष, joy, delight; 16. आवेग, flurry;<BR>17. जडता, stupefaction, insensibility, apathy; 18.<BR>गर्व, pride, arrogance; 19. विषाद, depression,<BR>despair; 20. औत्सुक्य, regret, eager longing; 21.<BR>निद्रा, drowsiness; 22. अपस्मार, possession by<BR>an evil spirit, epilepsy; 23. सुप्त, sleep; 24. वि-<BR>बोध, waking; 25. अमर्ष, angry impatience;<BR>26. अवहित्था, dissimulation; 27. उग्रता, cruelty,<BR>rage; 28. मति, mental perception or conclusion;<BR>29. उपालम्भ, reviling, railing; 30. व्याधि, sick-<BR>ness; 31. उन्माद, madness, delirium; 32. मरण,<BR>death; 33. त्रास, fear; 34. वितर्क, doubt, delibera-<BR>tion.)<BR>—व्यभिचारि-ता, f. or व्यभिचारि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of going astray, error, doubt; (in gram-<BR>mar) the having a secondary meaning, the having<BR>several meanings.<BR>—व्यभिचारि-भाव, अस्, m. a<BR>transitory state (of mind or body; see above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभ्र
व्यभ्र व्य्-अभ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, unclouded, cloud-<BR>less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय्
व्यय् व्यय् (probably formed fr. rt. अय् for<BR>5. इ with वि), cl. 1. P. A. व्ययति, -ते, वव्या-<BR>य, वव्यये, व्ययितुम्, and cl. 10. P. व्यययति,<BR>यितुम्, to go, move; to expend, disburse, spend;<BR>to waste, give away or squander money, &c., (in these<BR>senses probably a Nom. fr. व्यय below); cl. 10. P.<BR>व्याययति or व्यापयति, वेपयति (rather to be re-<BR>ferred to rts. व्यप्, 1. विप्), -यितुम्, to throw, cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय|व्ययं|व्ययः
व्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, mutable, liable to change or<BR>decay [cf. अ-व्˚]; (अस्), m. disappearance, loss; perish-<BR>ing, decaying, decay, destruction, change, downfall,<BR>decline, misfortune; spending, expenditure, expense,<BR>outlay, disbursement, (opposed to आय, income);<BR>squandering, extravagance, waste, prodigality; N. of<BR>Pradhāna; N. of the twentieth (or fifty-fourth) year<BR>of Jupiter's cycle; (अम्), n. (in astrology) the twelfth<BR>station or house from the Lagna (= लग्नाद् द्वा-<BR>दश-स्थानम्).<BR>—व्यय-पराङ्मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>averse from expenditure, parsimonious.<BR>—व्यय-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing waste or decay, &c.;<BR>changeful, imperfect, incomplete.<BR>—व्यय-शील, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, disposed to prodigality, wasteful, spendthrift.<BR>—व्ययी-करण, अम्, n. the act of expending or<BR>disbursing, wasting.<BR>—व्ययी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, ex-<BR>pended, spent, wasted, lavished.<BR>—व्ययी-भूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, spent, squandered, wasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययन|व्ययनं
व्ययन, अम्, n. the act of expending, spending,<BR>expenditure, wasting, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययमान
व्ययमान, अस्, आ, अम्, expending, spending,<BR>wasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययित|व्ययितः
व्ययित, अस्, आ, अम्, expended, spent, disbursed,<BR>consumed, dissipated, dispersed; gone away, de-<BR>clined, fallen into decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययिन्
व्ययिन्, ई, इनी, इ, expending, spending, expensive,<BR>prodigal, lavish, extravagant; declining, falling into<BR>calamity, wasting, changing, decaying, (उदय-<BR>व्ययिन्, rising and falling.)<BR>—व्ययि-ता, f. or व्ययि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. prodigality, wastefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्ण|व्यर्ण्ण
व्यर्ण 1. व्य्-अर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see below),<BR>without water, rainless, dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थ|व्यर्थं
व्यर्थ व्य्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, useless, unprofit-<BR>able, fruitless, ineffectual, vain; unmeaning.<BR>—व्यर्-<BR>थ-ता, f. or व्यर्थ-त्व, अम्, n. uselessness, un-<BR>profitableness, (व्यर्थ-तां या or गम्, to become<BR>useless); inoffensiveness; want of meaning, non-<BR>sense.<BR>—व्यर्थ-यत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, making useless<BR>efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थक
व्यर्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, useless, vain, &c., = व्य्-<BR>अर्थ.<BR>—व्यर्थक-ता, f. or व्यर्थक-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. unprofitableness, uselessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्द्
व्यर्द् व्य्-अर्द् (वि-अर्द्), cl. 1. P. -अर्दति, -अर्-<BR>दितुम्, Ved. to go or move away, to flow away; to<BR>oppress, harass, pain: Caus. -अर्दयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to be scattered or dissolved, destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्ण|व्यर्ण्ण
2. व्य्-अर्ण or व्य्-अर्ण्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (see Pāṇ. VII.<BR>2, 24), gone away, gone; oppressed, pained, dis-<BR>tressed; asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यलीक|व्यलीकं|व्यलीकः
व्यलीक व्य्-अलीक, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. अलीक], dis-<BR>agreeable, displeasing, painful, offensive, strange;<BR>improper or unfit to be done; false; (अम्), n. any-<BR>thing displeasing; any cause of pain or uneasiness or<BR>disagreeableness, pain, grief, torture; any improper<BR>act, fault, transgression (= कामजापराध); re-<BR>verse, contrariety, inversion; cheating, tricking;<BR>falsehood; (अस्), m. a libertine (= नागर, काम-<BR>केलि); a catamite.<BR>—व्यलीक-ता, f. or व्यलीक-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. disagreeableness, painfulness; impropriety,<BR>displeasure.<BR>—व्यलीक-निःश्वास, अस्, m. a sigh of<BR>pain or grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यल्कश
व्यल्कश व्य्-अल्कश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>various branches, (Sāy. = विविध-शाख.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकलन|व्यवकलनं
व्यवकलन व्य्-अवकलन, अम्, n. (fr. rt.<BR>3. कल् with अव and वि), separation, subtraction,<BR>deduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकलित|व्यवकलितः
व्य्-अवकलित, अस्, आ, अम्, separated, subtracted,<BR>deducted; (अम्), n. subtraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकृष्
व्यवकृष् व्य्-अव-कृष् (वि-अव-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-कर्षति, -कर्ष्टुम्, -क्रष्टुम्, to draw or drag<BR>down or away from, tear away, alienate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकॄ
व्यवकॄ व्य्-अव-कॄ (वि-अव-), cl. 6. P. -कि-<BR>रति, -करितुम्, -करीतुम्, to scatter or pour down,<BR>pour on, scatter about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवक्रोशन|व्यवक्रोशनं
व्यवक्रोशन व्य्-अवक्रोशन, अम्, n. (fr. rt.<BR>क्रुश् with अव and वि), mutual altercation, wrangling,<BR>mutual abuse; abuse, reviling (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवगम्
व्यवगम् व्य्-अव-गम्, cl. 1. A. -गच्छते,<BR>-गन्तुम्, Ved. to go apart, part, separate, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवगाह्
व्यवगाह् व्य्-अव-गाह्, cl. 1. A. -गाहते, -गा-<BR>हितुम्, -गाढुम्, to dive down into, plunge into; to<BR>enter into, penetrate; to set in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवगाढ
व्य्-अवगाढ, अस्, आ, अम्, dived or plunged into,<BR>immersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवगाह्य
व्य्-अवगाह्य, ind. having plunged into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवग्रह्
व्यवग्रह् व्य्-अव-ग्रह्, cl. 9. P. A. -गृह्णाति,<BR>गृह्णीते, &c., -ग्रहीतुम्, Ved. to bring down, to<BR>bend or incline down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवगृहीत
व्य्-अवगृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. brought down,<BR>bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छिद्
व्यवच्छिद् व्य्-अव-च्छिद् (वि-अव-छिद्), cl. 7.<BR>P. A. -च्छिनत्ति, -च्छिन्ते, -च्छेत्तुम्, to cut off or in<BR>pieces, separate, separate from; to tear asunder, open,<BR>sever; to interrupt; to decide or resolve on (with<BR>प्रति): Pass. -च्छिद्यते, to be cut off or separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छिद्य
व्य्-अवच्छिद्य, ind. having cut off or separated;<BR>having decided or resolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छिन्न|व्यवच्छिन्नं|व्यवछिन्न
व्य्-अवच्छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, cut off; torn or rent<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">Page0976-a+ 76</a>]<BR>asunder; separated, divided; distinguished; particu-<BR>larized, specified; distinct; interrupted, (अ-व्यवच्-<BR>छिन्न, uninterrupted.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छेद|व्यवच्छेदः|व्यवछेद
व्य्-अवच्छेद, अस्, m. cutting off or in pieces;<BR>anatomy; dividing, separating; discrimination; par-<BR>ticularizing, specification; distinction, contrast; deci-<BR>sion, determination; a division, section; letting fly<BR>an arrow, shooting, darting.<BR>—व्यवच्छेद-विद्या,<BR>f. the science of anatomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छेदक
व्य्-अवच्छेदक, अस्, इका, अम्, cutting off, divid-<BR>ing in two, discriminating, distinguishing, particular-<BR>izing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवतिष्ठमान
व्यवतिष्ठमान व्य्-अवतिष्ठमान. See under<BR>1. व्य्-अव-स्था, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवदा
व्यवदा व्य्-अव-दा (see rt. 3. दा), cl. 2. 4.<BR>P. -दाति, -द्यति, -दातुम्, to cut off, cut in two,<BR>divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवदाय
व्य्-अवदाय, having cut in two or divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवदॄ
व्यवदॄ व्य्-अव-दॄ (वि-अव-), Pass. -दीर्यते,<BR>to be torn asunder; to burst asunder, split in two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवदीर्ण
व्य्-अवदीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, burst asunder, broken<BR>to pieces, distracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवदै
व्यवदै व्य्-अव-दै (वि-अव-), Pass. -दायते,<BR>to be brightly diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवदात
व्य्-अवदात, अस्, आ, (Ved. ई), अम्, = अव-दात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवदायमान
व्य्-अवदायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, brightly diffused<BR>or spread about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधा
व्यवधा 1. व्य्-अव-धा (वि-अव-), cl. 3. P. A.<BR>-दधाति, -धत्ते, -धातुम्, to place apart or asun-<BR>der; to put or place between, interpose; to separate,<BR>divide, interrupt, obstruct, cover, screen, conceal; to<BR>lay aside, leave out, omit, pass over; to put down<BR>here and there: Pass. -धीयते, to be separated or<BR>separated from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधा
2. व्य्-अवधा, f. anything which intervenes or<BR>conceals from sight; a screen, partition, covering,<BR>the state of being covered, concealment, disappear-<BR>ance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधातृ
व्य्-अवधातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who separates or<BR>interposes or screens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधान|व्यवधानं
व्य्-अवधान, अम्, n. the act of placing apart<BR>or between, intervening, intervention, interposition,<BR>separation, break, gap; anything which intervenes<BR>or screens; a screen, partition, intervening object;<BR>intervening space, interval, space (in general); (in<BR>grammar) the intervention of a syllable or letter;<BR>covering, a cover; obstruction, the being covered or<BR>concealed, concealment, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधाय
व्य्-अवधाय, ind. having placed apart or be-<BR>tween, having interposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधायक|व्यवधायकः
व्य्-अवधायक, अस्, इका, अम्, intervening, screen-<BR>ing, interposing, separating; covering, concealing,<BR>hiding, obstructing; intermediate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधि|व्यवधिः
व्य्-अवधि, इस्, m. anything which intervenes or<BR>screens, a covering; intervention, covering, conceal-<BR>ing, &c., (see व्य्-अवधान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधेय
व्य्-अवधेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be put in between<BR>or interposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहित|व्यवहितः
व्य्-अवहित, अस्, आ, अम्, placed apart, placed be-<BR>tween; separated by anything intervening, separated,<BR>interrupted; obstructed, stopped, impeded; screened<BR>from view, concealed, covered; not contiguous, not<BR>immediately connected, only relating to; placed<BR>asunder, placed opposite, hostile, opposed; laid<BR>aside, omitted, passed over, surpassed, excelled, put<BR>to shame; done, acted, performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधाव्
व्यवधाव् व्य्-अव-धाव् (वि-अव-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-धावति, -ते, -धावितुम्, to run away from one<BR>another, separate from; to run away from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधू
व्यवधू व्य्-अव-धू (वि-अव-), cl. 5. P. A.<BR>-धूनोति, -धूनुते (in the later language also<BR>-धुनोति, -धुनुते), -धवितुम्, -धोतुम्, to<BR>shake off, ward off, remove; to shake about, treat<BR>roughly or rudely; to overthrow: Pass. -धूयते,<BR>to be shaken off, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधूत
व्य्-अवधूत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken off, one who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">Page0976-b+ 75</a>]<BR>has shaken off all worldly desires, indifferent in regard<BR>of life, resigned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधूय
व्य्-अवधूय, ind. having shaken off, having<BR>removed or warded off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधूयमान
व्य्-अवधूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being shaken<BR>about, being roughly treated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवनी
व्यवनी व्य्-अव-नी (वि-अव-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-नयति, -ते, -नेतुम्, Ved. to pour in separately,<BR>pour in drop by drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवनीय
व्य्-अवनीय, ind., Ved. having poured in sepa-<BR>rately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवपद्
व्यवपद् व्य्-अव-पद् (वि-अव-), cl. 4. A.<BR>-पद्यते, -पत्तुम्, to fall down, fall asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवभक्ष्
व्यवभक्ष् व्य्-अव-भक्ष् (वि-अव-), cl. 10. P.<BR>-भक्षयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to swallow down or eat<BR>(in the interval of certain religious rites).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवभास्
व्यवभास् व्य्-अव-भास् (वि-अव-), Caus. -भा-<BR>सयति, -यितुम्, to cause to shine out brightly, to<BR>illuminate beautifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवभासित
व्य्-अवभासित, अस्, आ, अम्, brightly illuminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवमुच्
व्यवमुच् व्य्-अव-मुच् (वि-अव-), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>-मुञ्चति, -ते, -मोक्तुम्, to unloose, unfasten, take<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवमुच्य
व्य्-अवमुच्य, ind. having unloosed, having taken<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवरुह्
व्यवरुह् व्य्-अव-रुह् (वि-अव-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-रोहति, -ते, -रोढुम्, to ascend, mount, get upon:<BR>Caus. -रोपयति, -यितुम्, to displace, remove; to<BR>deprive of (with abl.): Pass. of Caus. -रोप्यते, to<BR>be expelled from or deprived of (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवरोपित
व्य्-अवरोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, displaced, removed,<BR>expelled; deprived of (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यववद्
व्यववद् व्य्-अव-वद् (वि-अव-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-वदति, -ते, -वदितुम्, Ved. to speak ill of, decry;<BR>to begin to speak, break silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसद्
व्यवसद् व्य्-अव-सद् (वि-अव-), cl. 1. P. -सी-<BR>दति, -सत्तुम्, to sink or fall down, sit down; to<BR>pine or waste away, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसाय|व्यवसायः
व्यवसाय व्य्-अवसाय. See under व्य्-अव-सो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसृज्
व्यवसृज् व्य्-अव-सृज् (वि-अव-), cl. 6. P. -सृ-<BR>जति, -स्रष्टुम्, to throw, cast, hurl; to put down,<BR>lay down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसो
व्यवसो व्य्-अव-सो (वि-अव-), cl. 4. P. -स्यति<BR>(ep. forms 1st sing. Pres. व्य्-अवसामि, Pot. व्य्-<BR>अवसेयम्, 2nd Fut. व्य्-अवसिष्यामि), -सातुम्, to<BR>settle, determine, resolve, decide, constitute, establish;<BR>to be convinced or persuaded; to make strenuous<BR>effort, strive, endeavour, act, be industrious; to strive<BR>for, labour after; to make an attempt upon (with<BR>acc.); to seek after, ask for, wish; to reflect: Caus.<BR>-साययति, -यितुम्, to cause to resolve, cause to<BR>make effort, excite, instigate, embolden, make<BR>vigorous or strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसाय|व्यवसायः
व्य्-अवसाय, अस्, m. settled determination, resolve,<BR>obstinacy; strenuous effort or exertion, activity,<BR>energy, industry, perseverance; action, performance;<BR>conduct, behaviour; following any business or pro-<BR>fession; a trade, business, livelihood; artifice, plan,<BR>device, stratagem, trick; boasting; N. of Viṣṇu; of<BR>Śiva; of a son of Dharma by Vapus (daughter of<BR>Dakṣa).<BR>—व्यवसायात्मिक (˚य-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>full of resolve or energy, relating to exertion, ener-<BR>getic, laborious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायिन्
व्य्-अवसायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who acts resolutely or<BR>energetically, resolute, energetic, active, enterprising,<BR>persevering, painstaking, industrious, laborious, dili-<BR>gent; acting, performing, undertaking (anything), one<BR>who performs his duty; engaged in trade or busi-<BR>ness; a tradesman, handicraftsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसित|व्यवसितः
व्य्-अवसित, अस्, आ, अम्, settled, decided, resolved,<BR>determined, ascertained; endeavoured, undertaken,<BR>performed; energetic, taking pains, making effort or<BR>exertion, persevering, endeavouring; planned, de-<BR>signed, schemed; deceived, tricked, cheated; (अम्),<BR>n. certainty, ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्य
व्य्-अवस्य, ind. having settled or resolved, having<BR>decided; having made effort, having acted with<BR>resolution, having performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था 1. व्य्-अव-स्था, cl. 1. A. -तिष्ठते,<BR>-स्थातुम्, to be placed or situated asunder; to be<BR>arranged in due order, to be adjusted or settled;<BR>Caus. -स्थापयति, -यितुम्, to place or set asunder;<BR>to cause to be properly arranged or settled, decide,<BR>establish; to lay down a law; to perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवतिष्ठमान
व्य्-अवतिष्ठमान, अस्, आ, अम्, placed asunder,<BR>situated apart; adjusted, arranged, placed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
2. व्य्-अवस्था, f. arrangement, settlement, placing<BR>apart, separating; placing in suitable order, adjusting,<BR>arranging, arrangement; relative position or state;<BR>placing or setting in or on, fixing on a firm basis,<BR>settlement, decision, decree, statute, rule, law, written<BR>declaration of the law, legal opinion (applied to the<BR>written extracts from the codes of law or proper<BR>adjustment of contradictory passages in different codes<BR>made by decisions of officers attached to the courts<BR>of justice), a decision (in general); engagement,<BR>agreement, contract; course, state, condition, system<BR>or order of things (in general).<BR>—व्यवस्थाति-<BR>क्रम (˚था-अत्˚), अस्, m. or व्यवस्थातिवर्तन<BR>(˚था-अत्˚), अम्, n. transgression or violation of the<BR>law, disregard of settled rule; breaking an agreement<BR>or contract.<BR>—व्यवस्थातिवर्तिन् (˚था-अत्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, transgressing the law, breaking an engagement or<BR>contract, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थान|व्यवस्थानं|व्यवस्थानः
व्य्-अवस्थान, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n.<BR>regular arrangement or distribution; steadiness, set-<BR>tlement, &c. (= व्य्-अवस्थिति below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापक
व्य्-अवस्थापक, अस्, इका, अम्, settling, adjusting,<BR>arranging in an orderly manner, deciding, establish-<BR>ing, any one who settles or legislates or gives a<BR>legal opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापन|व्यवस्थापनं
व्य्-अवस्थापन, अम्, n. the act of placing apart;<BR>placing in order, fixing, determining, appointing,<BR>declaring, deciding, laying down a law; fixing or<BR>placing (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापित
व्य्-अवस्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be placed<BR>or arranged in order; laid down (as a law, &c.),<BR>established, fixed, declared, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थाप्य
1. व्य्-अवस्थाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be established<BR>or declared or settled, to be fixed, &c.; (अम्), n.<BR>the state of being established, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थाप्य
2. व्य्-अवस्थाप्य, ind. having set or placed in<BR>proper order, having fixed or settled or determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थित|व्यवस्थितः
व्य्-अवस्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or situated<BR>apart or at a distance, stood aside, separated; ex-<BR>cerpted, extracted; going away; placed in order,<BR>adjusted, harmoniously arranged; staying or standing<BR>or remaining in or on, (with वाक्ये, abiding in what<BR>is said, obeying); depending on, fixed in or on,<BR>resting on, based, fixed, settled; appointed, agreed,<BR>declared, decided, decreed, constant, restricted.<BR>—व्य-<BR>वस्थित-विकल्प, अस्, m. an option fixed or de-<BR>clared by law.<BR>—व्यवस्थित-विभाषा, f. (in gram-<BR>mar) a fixed option or one applicable throughout,<BR>(the prescribed operation being in one case carried out<BR>throughout and in the other omitted throughout.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थिति|व्यवस्थितिः
व्य्-अवस्थिति, इस्, f. the being situated or placed<BR>apart, separation; extracting; arrangement in due<BR>order, settlement, decision, determination, appoint-<BR>ment; rule, statute; remaining firm, constancy,<BR>perseverance; extracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहा
व्यवहा व्य्-अव-हा, cl. 3. P. -जहाति, -हातुम्,<BR>to abandon, give up, relinquish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहाय
व्य्-अवहाय, ind. having abandoned or relin-<BR>quished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहास
व्यवहास व्य्-अवहास, अस्, m. (fr. rt. हस्<BR>with अव and वि), mutual laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहित|व्यवहितः
व्यवहित व्य्-अवहित. See under व्य्-अव-<BR>धा, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहृ
व्यवहृ व्य्-अव-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते,<BR>-हर्तुम्, to act, behave; to manage, transact, deal<BR>with, traffic with, carry on a business or trade; to stake<BR>at play (with gen. of the thing staked, = rt. 2. पण्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-a" target="_blank">Page0977-a+ 81</a>]<BR>q. v.); to carry on legal proceedings, litigate, contend;<BR>to recover, regain, obtain; to distinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहरत्
व्य्-अवहरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, acting, behaving, con-<BR>ducting one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्तव्य|व्यवहर्त्तव्य
व्य्-अवहर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be transacted or<BR>done; to be litigated or decided judicially; to be<BR>dealt with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्तृ|व्यवहर्त्तृ
व्य्-अवहर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who acts or trans-<BR>acts business, one engaged in any affair; observing<BR>or following established usages; (ता), m. the manager<BR>of any business, the conductor of any judicial pro-<BR>cedure, a judge, umpire; one engaged in litigation,<BR>a litigant, plaintiff, any one who institutes an action<BR>at law; an associate, partaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार|व्यवहारः
व्य्-अवहार, अस्, m. doing, performing, conduct,<BR>behaviour, practice, action; affair; occupation, work,<BR>profession, business, any pecuniary transaction, usury;<BR>dealing, traffic, commerce, trade; a contest at<BR>law, legal dispute, lawsuit, litigation; legal prac-<BR>tice, judicial procedure, administration of justice (as<BR>the examination of evidence, &c.); a title of legal<BR>procedure, occasion of litigation, any act cognizable<BR>in a court of justice; usage, habit, custom, rule,<BR>law, adherence to law; steadiness, propriety; a con-<BR>tract; mathematical determination or ascertainment;<BR>a sort of tree.<BR>—व्यवहार-काल, अस्, m. the period of<BR>action, a mundane period.<BR>—व्यवहार-ज्ञ, अस्, m.<BR>a person who understands business, one acquainted with<BR>practice or legal procedure, a young man of age, one<BR>no longer a minor (i. e. one who has passed his<BR>sixteenth year, at which period he can assert his own<BR>rights in a court of law).<BR>—व्यवहार-तत्त्व, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a treatise on civil law by Raghu-nandana<BR>(being part of the Smṛti-tattva).<BR>—व्यवहार-तस्,<BR>ind. according to established practice.<BR>—व्यवहार-<BR>दर्शन, अम्, n. judicial investigation, trial.<BR>—व्य-<BR>वहार-निर्णय, अस्, m. ‘legal-decision,’ N. of a<BR>work by Śrī-pati.<BR>—व्यवहार-पद, अम्, n. a<BR>title or head of legal procedure, occasion of litiga-<BR>tion, (according to Śabda-k. = वादिना राज्ञि निवे-<BR>दनम्, see व्यवहार-विषय.)<BR>—व्यवहार-<BR>पाद, अस्, m. the fourth part or quarter of a legal<BR>process, one of the four stages or divisions necessary<BR>to conduct a regular suit, (these are, 1. पूर्व-पक्-<BR>ष, the plaint; 2. उत्तर-पक्ष, the defence;<BR>3. क्रिया-पाद, the production of witnesses and<BR>written documents; 4. निर्णय-पाद, the decision or<BR>verdict.)<BR>—व्यवहार-प्राप्त, अस्, m. one who has<BR>attained a knowledge of business or legal procedure,<BR>a youth sixteen years of age.<BR>—व्यवहार-म-<BR>यूख, अस्, m., N. of a legal work forming part of<BR>the Bhagavad-bhāskara.<BR>—व्यवहार-मातृका, f.<BR>the material or matter of ordinary judicature, legal<BR>process in general, any act or subject relating to the<BR>formation of legal courts or the administration of<BR>justice (arranged under thirty heads in the beginning<BR>of the second book or Vyavahārādhyāya of the<BR>Mitākṣarā, viz. 1. व्यवहार-दर्शनम्, 2. व्य-<BR>वहार-लक्षणम्, 3. सभासदः, 4. प्राड्विवा-<BR>कादिः, 5. व्यवहार-विषयः, 6. राज्ञः कार्या-<BR>नुत्पादकत्वम्, 7. कार्यार्थिनि प्रश्नः, 8. आह्-<BR>वानानाह्वाने, 9. आसेधः, 10. प्रत्यर्थिन्य् आगते<BR>लेख्यादि-कर्तव्यता, 11. पञ्च-विधो हीनः,<BR>12. कीदृशं लेख्यम्, 13. पक्षाभासाः, 14.<BR>अनादेयाः, 15. आदेयः, 16. नियुक्त-जय-परा-<BR>जये वादि-जय-पराजयौ, 17. शोधित-लेख्य-<BR>निवेशनम्, 18. उत्तरावधि-शोधनम्, 19. शो-<BR>धिते पत्त्रारूढे उत्तर-कर्तव्यम्, 20. उत्तर-<BR>लक्षणम्, 21. सत्योत्तर-लक्षणम्, 22. मिथ्-<BR>योत्तर-लक्षणम्, 23. प्रत्यवस्कन्दनोत्त-<BR>रम्, 24. प्रान्-न्यायोत्तरम्, 25. उत्तराभासः,<BR>26. सङ्करानुत्तरम्, 27. प्रत्यर्थि-क्रिया-निर्-<BR>देशः, 28. उत्तरे पत्त्रे ऽभिनिवेशिते साधन-<BR>निर्देशः, 29. तत्-सिद्धौ सिद्धिः, 30. चतुष्-<BR>पाद्-व्यवहारः).<BR>—व्यवहार-मार्ग, अस्, m.<BR>course or title of legal procedure (= व्यवहार-<BR>विषय, q. v.).<BR>—व्यवहार-लक्षण, अम्, n. a<BR>characteristic of judicial investigation.<BR>—व्यवहार-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having occupation, occupied, work-<BR>ing with.<BR>—व्यवहार-विधि, इस्, m. legal enact-<BR>ment, rule of law, the precepts or code by which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">Page0977-b+ 79</a>]<BR>judicature is regulated, any code of law.<BR>—व्यव-<BR>हार-विषय, अस्, m. a subject or title of legal pro-<BR>cedure, any act or matter which may become the<BR>subject of legal proceedings, an actionable business,<BR>(according to Manu VIII. 4-7. there are eighteen<BR>principal heads, viz. 1. ऋणादानम्, contraction of<BR>debt; 2. निक्षेपः, deposit; 3. अस्वामि-विक्रयः,<BR>sale without ownership; 4. सम्भूय-समुत्था-<BR>नम्, engaging in business after joining partner-<BR>ship, concerns among partners; 5. दत्तस्यानप-<BR>कर्म, non-delivery or resumption of what has<BR>been given; 6. वेतनादानम्, non-payment of<BR>wages; 7. संविद्-व्यतिक्रमः, violation of agree-<BR>ment; 8. क्रय-विक्रयानुशयः, repenting of<BR>or rescinding either sale or purchase; 9. स्वामि-<BR>पालयोर् विवादः, dispute between master and ser-<BR>vant; 10. सीमा-विवादः, dispute about boundaries;<BR>11. वाक्-पारुष्यम्, violence in words, slander,<BR>abuse; 12. दण्ड-पारुष्यम्, violence by actual<BR>assault; 13. स्तेयम्, theft, larceny; 14. साहसम्,<BR>robbery with violence; 15. स्त्री-सङ्ग्रहणम्, im-<BR>proper intercourse with women, adultery; 16. स्त्री-<BR>पुन्-धर्मः, law of man and wife; 17. विभागः,<BR>apportionment of property, inheritance; 18. द्यूतम्<BR>and आह्वयः, gambling with dice and with fighting<BR>animals, laying wagers, &c.)<BR>—व्यवहार-समुच्चय,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a work by Bhoja-deva.<BR>—व्यवहार-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. a title or occasion of litigation (=<BR>व्यवहार-विषय, q. v.).<BR>—व्यवहार-स्थिति, इस्,<BR>f. judicial procedure.<BR>—व्यवहारांश (˚र-अं˚),<BR>अस्, m. any part or division of legal procedure.<BR>—व्यवहाराङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अम्, n. the body of<BR>civil and criminal law.<BR>—व्यवहाराभिशस्त (˚र-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, prosecuted, accused, proceeded<BR>against legally.<BR>—व्यवहारायोग्य (˚र-अय्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, unfitted or unsuited for legal proceedings;<BR>(अस्), m. one incompetent to conduct business, a<BR>minor, any one not yet of age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारक|व्यवहारकः
व्यवहारक, अस्, m. a dealer, trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिक|व्यवहारिकः
व्यवहारिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, relating to practice<BR>or business, transacting business, engaged in business,<BR>practical; relating to an action at law or legal process;<BR>litigant; one who is party to a suit; customary, usual;<BR>(इका), f. practice, usage, custom; a brush, broom;<BR>a plant (= इङ्गुद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिन्
व्यवहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, customary, usual; acting,<BR>transacting, practising (any business or trade); litigant,<BR>litigating, engaged in a lawsuit; relating to a legal<BR>process or action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार्य|व्यवहार्य्य|व्यवहार्य्यः
व्य्-अवहार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be transacted or per-<BR>formed, to be practised (as a duty, trade, business,<BR>&c.); actionable, liable to a legal process; to be<BR>employed or used; customary, usual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहृत
व्य्-अवहृत, अस्, आ, अम्, practised, employed, used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहृति|व्यवहृतिः
व्य्-अवहृति, इस्, f. practice, performance, action,<BR>process.<BR>—व्यवहृति-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a part<BR>of the Smṛti-tattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवे
व्यवे व्य्-अवे (वि-अव-इ), cl. 2. P. -अवैति,<BR>-अवैतुम्, to go or pass between, separate; (in<BR>Vedic grammar) to resolve or separate (by inserting<BR>a letter, &c.); to dissolve, decompose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवाय|व्यवायं|व्यवायः
व्य्-अवाय, अस्, m. separation, resolution (into<BR>separate parts), decomposition, dissolution, disap-<BR>pearance; dissipation; loose habits; intervention, in-<BR>terval, intervening space; an obstacle, impediment;<BR>covering, concealment; sexual intercourse, copulation;<BR>purity; (अम्), n. light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवायिन्
व्यवायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, separating, resolving (into<BR>separate parts), decomposing, pervading, diffusive;<BR>lustful; (ई), m. a libertine; a drug, aphrodisiac, any<BR>substance or liquid possessing stimulating or exciting<BR>properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवेत
व्य्-अवेत, अस्, आ, अम्, separated, resolved, decom-<BR>posed (into separate parts), different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्
व्यश् 1. व्य्-अश् (वि-अश्, see rt. 1. अश्), cl. 5.<BR>A. -अश्नुते (Ved. also frequently P. -अश्नोति), Perf.<BR>व्य्-आनशे (Vedic forms व्य्-आनट् = व्याप्नोतु, Ṛg-<BR>veda VII. 28, 2; व्य्-अश्युः = व्याप्नुवन्तु, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 73, 5), -अशितुम्, -अष्टुम्, to reach, attain<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">Page0977-c+ 78</a>]<BR>to, extend to; to obtain, take possession of, possess;<BR>to pervade, interpenetrate, fill, occupy; to fall to<BR>one's share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्नुवान
व्य्-अश्नुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, reaching, occupying,<BR>pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यष्टि
व्य्-अष्टि, इस्, f. (according to some fr. व्य्-अक्ष्),<BR>singleness, individuality; (in the Vedānta phil.) dis-<BR>tributive pervasion, a distributive aggregate, an aggre-<BR>gate or whole viewed as consisting of many separate<BR>bodies (e. g. an object, such as man, viewed as a<BR>separate part of a whole or constituting a part of the<BR>Universal Soul, while he is himself composed of<BR>parts or individuals; contra-distinguished from सम्-<BR>अष्टि, q. v.); power; (इस्), m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—व्यष्ट्य्-अभिप्राय, अस्, m. regarding (a group<BR>of objects) singly or individually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्
व्यश् 2. व्य्-अश् (वि-अश्, see rt. 2. अश्), cl. 9.<BR>P. (Ved. also A.) -अश्नाति (-अश्नीते), -अशितुम्, to eat<BR>up, consume by eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्व
व्यश्व व्य्-अश्व, अस्, आ, अम्, without horses,<BR>deprived of horses; (अस्), m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi<BR>(father of Viśva-manas).<BR>—व्यश्व-वत्, ind., Ved.<BR>like Vy-aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यष्टि
व्यष्टि व्य्-अष्टि. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्
व्यस् व्य्-अस् (वि-अस्, see rt. 2. अस्), cl. 4. P.<BR>-अस्यति (anomalous ep. Perf. विव्यास as if fr. a rt.<BR>व्यस्), -असितुम्, to throw asunder, cast in different<BR>directions, divide, divide into pieces, separate, sever,<BR>dispose, arrange; to throw about or in various direc-<BR>tions, toss about, scatter, disperse, dispel; to cast aside<BR>or away; to throw over, upset, expel, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसन|व्यसनं
व्य्-असन, अम्, n. the act of throwing in different<BR>directions, separating, separation; individuality; cast-<BR>ing away or dispelling (happiness &c.), violation,<BR>infraction; calamity, misfortune, ill-luck, evil destiny,<BR>fate, fated consequence, destruction, loss, defeat, fall-<BR>ing away, fall; setting (as of the sun or moon); sin,<BR>fault, vice, crime, bad practice, evil habit (said to<BR>arise either from love of pleasure or from anger; ten<BR>vices are enumerated in Manu VII. 47, 48, under<BR>the first head, viz. मृगया, hunting; द्यूत or<BR>अक्ष, gambling; दिवा-स्वप्न, sleeping in the<BR>day; परिवाद, calumny; स्त्रियः, addiction to<BR>women; मद, drinking spirits; तौर्य-त्रिक,<BR>dancing, singing, and instrumental music; वृथाट्या,<BR>idle roaming: and eight are said to proceed from<BR>anger, viz. पैशुन्य, tale-bearing; साहस, violence;<BR>द्रोह, insidious injury; ईर्ष्या, envy; असूया,<BR>detraction; अर्थ-दूषण, unjust seizure of pro-<BR>perty; वाक्-पारुष्य, violence in words or abuse;<BR>दण्ड-पारुष्य, violence by actual assault: the<BR>number and nature of these vices are variously given<BR>in other books); punishment, execution (of cri-<BR>minals); fruitless effort; incompetence, inability;<BR>throwing one's self into any pursuit, intent applica-<BR>tion or attachment to any object, inordinate addiction,<BR>diligence; air, wind.<BR>—व्यसन-प्रसारित-कर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the hand stretched forth for (inflicting)<BR>calamity.<BR>—व्यसन-प्रहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, inflicting<BR>calamity, giving trouble or pain.<BR>—व्यसन-रक्-<BR>षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, preserving from calamity.<BR>—व्यस-<BR>नाक्रान्त-त्व (˚न-आक्˚), अम्, n. distressful condition,<BR>grievous distress.<BR>—व्यसनातिभार (˚न-अत्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, weighed down with misfortunes, overbur-<BR>dened with calamities.<BR>—व्यसनान्वित (˚न-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, involved in calamity.<BR>—व्यसनाप्लुत<BR>(˚न-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, overwhelmed with calamity.<BR>—व्यसनार्त (˚न-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted by<BR>calamity or misfortune, suffering pain.<BR>—व्यसनो-<BR>दय (˚न-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, followed by or resulting<BR>in calamities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिन्
व्यसनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, calamitous, unfortunate, un-<BR>lucky; addicted to any kind of vice or evil practice<BR>(as gaming, drinking, &c., see above); vicious, dis-<BR>solute; attached intently to (any object).<BR>—व्यसनि-<BR>ता, f. or व्यसनि-त्व, अम्, n. calamitousness, calamity;<BR>viciousness, wickedness, dissoluteness; intent attach-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनीय
व्यसनीय, अस्, m. a vicious person, profligate,<BR>libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्त|व्यस्तः
व्य्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cast apart, thrown asunder,<BR>separated, divided, separate, severed, distinct, un-<BR>compounded, simple, broken asunder, broken to<BR>pieces, shattered; different, manifold, various, changed,<BR>altered; thrown or tossed about, scattered, dispersed;<BR>agitated, disturbed, troubled, confused, confounded,<BR>bewildered; cast aside or away, expelled, removed,<BR>spread; thrown upside down, upset, reversed, in-<BR>verted, disordered, disarranged, out of order, uneven,<BR>reverse, inverse, opposite, opposed to, set or struck<BR>against; penetrated, pervaded, inherent in or per-<BR>vading all the several parts of anything, (opposed to<BR>सम्-अस्त, q. v.); (अम्), ind. severally, separately,<BR>partially.<BR>—व्यस्त-केश, अस्, ई, अम्, having dishe-<BR>velled hair.<BR>—व्यस्त-ता, f. or व्यस्त-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>severalty, individuality; several inherence; agita-<BR>tion, bewilderment.<BR>—व्यस्त-त्रैराशिक, अम्, n.<BR>the rule of three inverted.<BR>—व्यस्त-पद, अम्, n.<BR>confused statement of a case (in a court of law),<BR>confusion in accusation and defence (as when a man<BR>is charged with debt his defence is that he has been<BR>struck); a simple or uncompounded word (in gram.,<BR>opposed to समस्त-पद, q. v.).<BR>—व्यस्त-रात्रिन्-<BR>दिव, अस्, आ, अम्, dividing or separating night and<BR>day.<BR>—व्यस्त-विधि, इस्, m. inverted rule, any rule for<BR>inversion.<BR>—व्यस्त-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, (a word) whose<BR>proper force or meaning is changed or altered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तार|व्यस्तारं|व्यस्तारः
व्यस्तार, अम्, n. (said to be fr. व्यस्त + आर fr.<BR>rt. 4. ऋ), the issue of the fluid from the temples of<BR>an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्य
व्य्-अस्य, ind. having thrown asunder, having<BR>thrown or tossed about, having dispersed or scattered;<BR>having arranged in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यास|व्यासः
व्य्-आस, अस्, m. distributing or disposing in dif-<BR>ferent directions, distribution or separation into parts,<BR>(in Atharva-veda Prātiśākhya III. 68. said to mean<BR>‘the disjoined or Pada text’); severing; severalty,<BR>distinction, detail; diffusing, extending; diffusion,<BR>extension, width, breadth, the breadth or diameter<BR>of a circle; a particular measure; a fault in pronun-<BR>ciation, a kind of drawl [cf. पीडन, वि-हार]; dis-<BR>posing in order, arranging, an arranger, compiler;<BR>N. of a celebrated sage and author (often called Veda-<BR>vyāsa and regarded as the original arranger of the<BR>Vedas &c. and founder of the Vedānta philosophy<BR>[see वेदान्त]; he was the son of the sage Parāśara<BR>and Satyavatī, who afterwards, as the wife of Śāntanu,<BR>gave birth to Vicitra-vīrya and Bhīṣma; he was<BR>therefore half-brother of these latter; Parāśara met<BR>Satyavatī, when quite a girl, as he was crossing the<BR>river Jumnā; their child Vyāsa was called Kṛṣṇa<BR>from his dark complexion, and Dvaipāyana because<BR>he was brought forth by Satyavatī on a Dvīpa or<BR>island in the Jumnā; when grown up he retired to<BR>the wilderness to lead the life of a hermit, but at<BR>his mother's request returned to become the husband<BR>of Vicitra-vīrya's two childless widows, by whom he<BR>was the father of the blind Dhṛta-rāṣṭra and of<BR>Pāṇḍu; he was also the father of Vidura by a slave<BR>girl [see विदुर, p. 918] and of Śuka, the supposed<BR>narrator of the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa: the Viṣṇu-Pu-<BR>rāṇa III. 3. enumerates twenty-eight Vyāsas or<BR>arrangers of the Vedas in the twenty-eight Dvāpara<BR>ages of the Vaivasvata Manv-antara; the first Vyāsa<BR>is said to have been Svayam-bhū or Brahmā himself,<BR>and the twenty-eighth was Kṛṣṇa-dvaipāyana: the<BR>name Vyāsa seems to have been given to any great<BR>compiler or author, and this title is conferred not<BR>only on the arranger of the Vedas and the Purāṇas,<BR>but also on the compiler of the Mahā-bhārata, the<BR>Brahma-sūtra of the Vedānta philosophy, a Dharma-<BR>śāstra, the Yoga-sūtra-bhāṣya, the Vakra-tuṇḍa-<BR>stotra, the Vakra-tuṇḍāṣṭaka hymns, and the Śiva-<BR>dhanur-veda: the following are synonyms for Vyāsa,<BR>Vādarāyaṇa or Bādarāyaṇa, Dvaipāyana, Kṛṣṇa-<BR>dvaipāyana, Pārāśari, Māṭhara, Kānīna, Sātyavata,<BR>Satya-bhārata, Satya-rata); a Brāhman who recites<BR>or expounds the Purāṇas &c. in public (= पाठक-<BR>ब्राह्मण).<BR>—व्यास-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">Page0978-b+ 76</a>]<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—व्यास-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the state or title of a compiler.<BR>—व्यास-दास, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a chief of the Vaikhānasa sect.<BR>—व्यास-<BR>देव, अस्, m. the divine sage Vyāsa.<BR>—व्यास-पूजा,<BR>f. honour paid to an expounder of the Purāṇas.<BR>—व्यास-भाष्य-व्याख्या, f., N. of a commentary<BR>by Vācas-pati.<BR>—व्यास-मातृ, ता, f. ‘mother of<BR>Vyāsa,’ epithet of Satyavatī.<BR>—व्यास-वन, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a sacred forest.<BR>—व्यास-शुक-संवाद, अस्,<BR>m. ‘dialogue between Vyāsa and Śuka,’ N. of a<BR>philosophical discourse on the vanity of everything<BR>except religion (said to be extracted from the Mahā-<BR>bhārata).<BR>—व्यास-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—व्यास-स्मृति, इस्, f., N. of a law-book.<BR>—व्या-<BR>साष्टक (˚स-अष्˚), N. of a hymn.<BR>—व्यासासन<BR>(˚स-आस्˚), अम्, n. the seat of an expounder of the<BR>Purāṇas.<BR>—व्यासेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासीय
व्यासीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसु
व्यसु व्य्-असु, उस्, उस्, उ, breathless, without<BR>breath, inanimate, lifeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यह्
व्यह् व्य्-अह् (वि-अह्), Perf. -आह (see rt. 3. अह्),<BR>to explain, assign a reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यह्न
व्यह्न व्य्-अह्न, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Vopa-<BR>deva III. 42. the loc. may be व्य्-अह्ने, व्य्-अहनि,<BR>or व्य्-अह्नि), done or happening on separate days;<BR>(according to some) done or produced in two days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकरण|व्याकरणं
व्याकरण व्य्-आकरण. See under व्य्-आ-कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकीर्ण
व्याकीर्ण व्य्-आकीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. कॄ<BR>with आ and वि), scattered or tossed in every direction,<BR>thrown about or away.<BR>—व्याकीर्ण-केशर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a disordered or rough mane.<BR>—व्याकीर्ण-<BR>माल्य-कवर, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated with inter-<BR>spersed garlands.<BR>—व्याकीर्णार्चिस् (˚ण-अर्˚), इस्, इस्,<BR>इस्, Ved. having scattered or divided flames.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुञ्चित
व्याकुञ्चित व्य्-आकुञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, distorted,<BR>crooked, contracted, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुल|व्याकुलः
व्याकुल व्य्-आकुल, अस्, आ, अम्, confounded,<BR>confused, agitated, discomposed, bewildered, per-<BR>plexed, troubled, dimmed, overcome with fear; busily<BR>occupied about anything.<BR>—व्याकुल-चित्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or व्याकुल-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or व्याकुल-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or व्याकुलात्मन् (˚ल-आत्˚), आ,<BR>आ, अ, agitated or perplexed in mind, flurried, having<BR>a mind distracted with grief.<BR>—व्याकुल-ता, f. or<BR>व्याकुल-त्व, अम्, n. perturbation, agitation, per-<BR>plexity, bewilderment, alarm.<BR>—व्याकुली-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to bewilder, render confused<BR>or perplexed, trouble.<BR>—व्याकुली-भू, cl. 1. P. -भ-<BR>वति, &c., to become perplexed.<BR>—व्याकुलेन्द्रिय<BR>(˚ल-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the senses bewildered,<BR>one who has lost his senses, discomposed, ruffled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलय
व्याकुलय, Nom. P. व्याकुलयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>agitate, flurry, confuse, frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलित
व्याकुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, flurried, perplexed,<BR>confounded, alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकूति|व्याकूतिः
व्याकूति व्य्-आकूति, इस्, f. wrong or evil in-<BR>tention, fraud, deception, disguise (= भङ्गि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृ
व्याकृ व्य्-आ-कृ (वि-आ-), cl. 8. P. A. -करोति,<BR>-कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to undo, decompose, analyse,<BR>separate, divide; to expound, explain, utter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकरण|व्याकरणं
व्य्-आकरण, अम्, n. undoing, analysis, explaining,<BR>expounding; grammatical analysis, grammar (regarded<BR>as one of the Vedāṅgas, see वेदाङ्ग, p. 964,<BR>col. 3).<BR>—व्याकरण-प्रक्रिया, f. grammatical for-<BR>mation of a word, etymology.<BR>—व्याकरण-सिद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, established by grammar, conformable to<BR>grammar, grammatical.<BR>—व्याकरणागम (˚ण-<BR>आग्˚), अस्, m. traditional rules of grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकार|व्याकारः
व्य्-आकार, अस्, m. transformation, change of form,<BR>distortion, deformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृत
व्य्-आकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, analysed, decomposed, sepa-<BR>rated, expounded, explained, made clear; transformed,<BR>disfigured, deformed, distorted, changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृति|व्याकृतिः
व्य्-आकृति, इस्, f. analysing, explaining, making<BR>clear; grammar; change of form, development.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृत्य
व्य्-आकृत्य, ind. having separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृष्
व्याकृष् व्य्-आ-कृष् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. -कर्-<BR>षति, -कर्ष्टुम्, -क्रष्टुम्, to draw or drag in<BR>different directions, draw apart, separate; to draw off<BR>or away, take off, put off, throw off; to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृष्ट
व्य्-आकृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn off, taken off,<BR>thrown off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोश|व्याकोशः
व्याकोश व्य्-आकोश, अस्, आ, अम्, expanded,<BR>blossomed, blown (as a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोष|व्याकोषः
व्य्-आकोष, अस्, आ, अम्, = व्य्-आकोश above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्रुश्
व्याक्रुश् व्य्-आ-क्रुश् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. -क्रोशति,<BR>-क्रोष्टुम्, to cry out aloud, complain, lament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्रोशत्
व्य्-आक्रोशत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, crying out aloud, mak-<BR>ing loud lamentations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षिप्
व्याक्षिप् व्य्-आ-क्षिप् (वि-आ-), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>-क्षिपति, -ते, -क्षेप्तुम्, to throw or toss about;<BR>to carry away; to stretch out or forth, open; to<BR>shoot off (as a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षिप्त
व्य्-आक्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, tossed hither and thither,<BR>tossed about; torn asunder, carried away, distracted,<BR>stretched out, stretched forth.<BR>—व्याक्षिप्त-मनस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, or व्याक्षिप्त-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the mind or heart tossed about, distracted in<BR>mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षेप|व्याक्षेपः
व्य्-आक्षेप, अस्, m. throwing or tossing about;<BR>obstruction, hinderance, delay, (अ-व्याक्षेप, absence<BR>of delay.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षोभ|व्याक्षोभः
व्याक्षोभ व्य्-आ-क्षोभ, अस्, m. commotion,<BR>perturbation, agitation, disturbed state, disturbance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्या
व्याख्या 1. व्य्-आ-ख्या (वि-आ-), cl. 2. P.<BR>-ख्याति, -ख्यातुम्, to explain in detail, expound,<BR>interpret, illustrate; to speak at length, tell in full;<BR>to relate, narrate, tell (a story); to communicate,<BR>inform; to name, call: Pass. -ख्यायते, to be ex-<BR>plained: Desid. -चिख्यासति, to intend or wish to<BR>explain, be about to expound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्या
2. व्य्-आख्या, f. explanation, exposition, interpreta-<BR>tion, gloss, comment, paraphrase.<BR>—व्याख्यागम्य<BR>(˚या-आग्˚), अम्, n. anything which can only be under-<BR>stood by explanation, a kind of उत्तराभास, q. v.;<BR>indistinct assertion or declaration (said to proceed from<BR>grammatical inaccuracy or faulty construction), any<BR>obscure statement or passage.<BR>—व्याख्या-सुधा, f.<BR>‘nectar of exposition,’ N. of a commentary on the<BR>Amara-koṣa by Bhānujī-dīkṣita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यात|व्याख्यातः
व्य्-आख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, explained in detail, ex-<BR>pounded, interpreted, illustrated; spoken in full,<BR>related, narrated, told, spoken, said; conquered, over-<BR>come (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यातव्य
व्य्-आख्यातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, requiring to be ex-<BR>pounded or commented upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यातृ
व्य्-आख्यातृ, ता, m. an explainer, commentator,<BR>expounder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यान|व्याख्यानं
व्य्-आख्यान, अम्, n. explaining, expounding,<BR>commenting; explanation, exposition; gloss, com-<BR>ment, interpretation.<BR>—व्याख्यान-योग्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, deserving exposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्येय
व्य्-आख्येय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be explained or ex-<BR>pounded, to be described.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याचिख्यासितग्रन्थ
व्याचिख्यासित-ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. one who is about<BR>to explain a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टन|व्याघट्टनं
व्याघट्टन व्य्-आघट्टन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. घट्ट्<BR>with आ and वि), rubbing together, friction; churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टित
व्य्-आघट्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed together, rubbed;<BR>churned, stirred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघात|व्याघातः
व्याघात व्य्-आघात, अस्, m. (fr. व्य्-आ-हन्),<BR>striking against, beating, wounding, destroying, de-<BR>struction; a blow, stroke; obstacle, impediment, hin-<BR>derance; the thirteenth of the astronomical Yogas;<BR>the tree Cassia Fistula; a particular figure of rhetoric<BR>(described as the production of two different effects<BR>from a similar cause or by similar agency); contra-<BR>diction, inconsistency of statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातक
व्य्-आघातक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, striking against,<BR>opposing, thwarting, hindering, impeding, resisting;<BR>one who opposes or resists, an obstructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातिन्
व्य्-आघातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who strikes against or<BR>opposes or resists, an opposer; obstructing, opposing,<BR>resisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघुट्
व्याघुट् व्य्-आ-घुट् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. A. -घोटते,<BR>cl. 6. P. -घुटति, -घोटितुम्, to turn back, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघुटित
व्य्-आघुटित, अस्, आ, अम्, turned back, returned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघुट्य
व्य्-आघुट्य, ind. having returned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघुष्
व्याघुष् व्य्-आ-घुष् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. -घो-<BR>षति, -घोषितुम्, to sound aloud: Caus. -घोष-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to call out aloud, shout or proclaim<BR>aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघुष्ट
व्य्-आघुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded aloud, loud-<BR>sounding, resounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघोषयत्
व्य्-आघोषयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, proclaiming aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघूर्ण्
व्याघूर्ण् व्य्-आ-घूर्ण् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-घूर्णति, -ते, -घूर्णितुम्, to whirl or wave about,<BR>shake to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघूर्णमान
व्य्-आघूर्णमान, अस्, आ, अम्, whirling or wav-<BR>ing about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघूर्णित
व्य्-आघूर्णित, अस्, आ, अम्, whirled about, tossed<BR>hither and thither, wheeled about, agitated, whirling<BR>round, tottering, shaking about, waving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघृ
व्याघृ व्य्-आ-घृ (वि-आ-), Caus. -घारयति,<BR>-यितुम्, Ved. to sprinkle round or over, besprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघारण
व्य्-आघारण, अम्, n. the act of sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघारित
व्य्-आघारित, अस्, आ, अम्, besprinkled, sprinkled<BR>with oil or ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्र|व्याघ्रः
व्याघ्र व्याघ्र, अस्, m. (fr. rt. घ्रा with आ<BR>and वि), a tiger, (चित्र-व्याघ्र, ‘spotted tiger,’ a<BR>hunting leopard; in the Vahni-Purāṇa tigers are<BR>said to be the offspring of Kaśyapa's wife, Daṃṣṭrā);<BR>any eminent person, best, pre-eminent (at the end<BR>of a comp., cf. पुरुष-व्˚ and see ऋषभ, सिंह,<BR>which are also used as the last member of com-<BR>pounds to express ‘eminence’); a red variety of the<BR>castor-oil plant (= रक्तैरण्ड); the tree Pon-<BR>gamia Glabra or Galedupa Arborea (= करञ्ज);<BR>N. of the author of a law-book; (ई), f. a female<BR>tiger, tigress; a sort of prickly nightshade, Solanum<BR>Jacquini (= कण्टकारी).<BR>—व्याघ्र-चर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>a tiger's skin.<BR>—व्याघ्रचर्म-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made of a tiger's skin.<BR>—व्याघ्र-ता, f. or व्याघ्र-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition of a tiger.<BR>—व्या-<BR>घ्र-दल, अस्, m. the castor-oil tree or a red variety<BR>of it.<BR>—व्याघ्र-नख, अस्, m. a tiger's claw; a<BR>particular plant (= स्नुही); a kind of perfume;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of medicinal herb with a fragrant<BR>root, (in Hindī called बघ्नहा); a sort of per-<BR>fume, (in this sense also ई, f.); a scratch, impres-<BR>sion of a finger-nail.<BR>—व्याघ्र-नखक, अम्, n.<BR>‘tiger's claw,’ a scratch, the impression of a finger-<BR>nail.<BR>—व्याघ्र-नायक, अस्, m. ‘tiger-leader,’ a<BR>jackal.<BR>—व्याघ्र-पाद्, -पात्, -पदी, -पात्, tiger-<BR>footed; (पात्), m., N. of the author of Ṛg-veda<BR>IX. 97, 16-18 (having the patronymic Vāsiṣṭha);<BR>N. of a grammarian and author of a law-book.<BR>—व्या-<BR>घ्र-पाद, अस्, m. ‘tiger-footed,’ N. of a lawgiver;<BR>the plant Flacourtia Sapida (= वि-कङ्कत).<BR>—व्या-<BR>घ्र-पुच्छ, अस्, m. a tiger's tail; the castor-oil<BR>tree, Palma Christi or Ricinus Communis.<BR>—व्या-<BR>घ्र-पुर, अम्, n. ‘tiger's town,’ N. of a town.<BR>—व्याघ्र-भूति, इस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR>—व्याघ्र-वधू, ऊस्, f. the female of a tiger, a<BR>tigress.<BR>—व्याघ्र-श्वन्, आ, m. a tiger-like dog.<BR>—व्याघ्राट (˚र-अट), अस्, m. a skylark (=<BR>भरद्-वाज).<BR>—व्याघ्रादनी (˚र-अद्˚), f. a<BR>particular plant (= त्रि-वृता).<BR>—व्याघ्रास्य (˚र-<BR>आस्˚), अम्, n. the mouth or face of a tiger; (अस्), m.<BR>‘tiger-faced,’ a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्री
व्याघ्री, f. See under व्याघ्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याङ्गि
व्याङ्गि व्याङ्गि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Vy-aṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याचक्ष्
व्याचक्ष् व्य्-आ-चक्ष् (वि-आ-), cl. 2. A. -चष्टे,<BR>-चष्टुम्, to recite, rehearse (Ved.); to explain,<BR>comment upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याचक्षाण
व्य्-आचक्षाण, अस्, आ, अम्, reciting; explaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याज|व्याजः
व्याज व्य्-आज, अस्, m. (fr. व्य्-अज्), deceit,<BR>deception, fraud, craft, art, cunning; disguise (either<BR>of purpose or of person); semblance, appearance,<BR>pretext, pretence (sometimes at the end of comps.,<BR>e. g. मृगया-व्याजेन, under the pretext of hunt-<BR>ing); contrivance, means; wickedness.<BR>—व्याज-<BR>निन्दा, f. ‘artful censure,’ a particular figure of<BR>rhetoric (praise veiled under apparent censure);<BR>ironical praise.<BR>—व्याज-भानु-जित्, त्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—व्याज-स्तुति, इस्, f. ‘artful praise,’ indirect<BR>eulogy, praise or censure conveyed in language that<BR>expresses the contrary (as when from blame praise<BR>is expressed, and when from praise blame); ironical<BR>commendation.<BR>—व्याजी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c.,<BR>to hold out as a pretence or pretext.<BR>—व्याजी-कृत्य,<BR>ind. having held out as a pretext, having pretended<BR>(= अपदिश्य).<BR>—व्याजोक्ति (˚ज-उक्˚), इस्, f. covert<BR>allusion (intended to mislead), innuendo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याड|व्याडः
व्याड व्याड, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. अड्<BR>with वि), a snake; a carnivorous animal, beast of<BR>prey; N. of Indra; a villain, rogue; a proper N.;<BR>[cf. व्याल.]<BR>—व्याडायुध (˚ड-आय्˚), अम्, n. a sort<BR>of vegetable perfume (= व्याघ्र-नख).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याडि|व्याडिः
व्याडि, इस्, m. (a patronymic fr. व्याड), N. of a<BR>celebrated grammarian and lexicographer (= विन्-<BR>ध्य-वासिन्, नन्दिनी-तनय, q. q. v. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याडीय
व्याडीय, अस्, m. a follower of Vyāḍi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यातन्
व्यातन् व्य्-आ-तन् (वि-आ-), cl. 8. P. A. -त-<BR>नोति, -तनुते, -तनितुम्, to stretch out, extend; to<BR>spread about or over, (व्यातेनिरे, they were spread<BR>about, Kirāt. XV. 42); to display; to produce, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्युक्षी
व्यात्युक्षी व्य्-आत्य्-उक्षी, f. (probably fr. rt.<BR>1. उक्ष् with अति, आ, and वि, cf. व्य्-आभ्य्-उक्षी),<BR>bathing together for amusement, mutual splashing<BR>and sporting in water (= रसिकानाम् अन्योन्यं<BR>जल-क्रीडनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादा
व्यादा व्य्-आ-दा (वि-आ-), cl. 3. P. A. -ददाति,<BR>-दत्ते, -दातुम्, to open wide, open, separate; to<BR>open the mouth, (also with मुखम् or similar<BR>words added); to make large or broad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्त|व्यात्तं
व्य्-आत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, opened, open, wide open,<BR>spread, extended, expanded, vast; (अम्), n. the open<BR>mouth.<BR>—व्यात्तानन (˚त-आन्˚) or व्यात्तास्य (˚त-<BR>आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, open-mouthed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याददान
व्य्-आददान, अस्, आ, अम्, opening (especially the<BR>mouth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादान|व्यादानं
व्य्-आदान, अम्, n. opening, setting open or ajar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादाय
व्य्-आदाय, ind. having opened; having opened<BR>the mouth, having gaped (with wonder &c.); with<BR>the mouth open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादित
व्य्-आदित, अस्, आ, अम् (ep. for व्य्-आत्त), opened<BR>(applied especially to the mouth).<BR>—व्यादितास्य (˚त-<BR>आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, open-mouthed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादिश्
व्यादिश् व्य्-आ-दिश् (वि-आ-), cl. 3. 6. P. -दि-<BR>देष्टि, -दिशति, -देष्टुम्, to point out separately,<BR>divide among, distribute; to point out, show; to<BR>explain, inform, teach; to prescribe, order, charge,<BR>command (with acc. of the person); to assign, ap-<BR>point (to any duty); to give an order or command;<BR>to speak about any one (acc.); to declare, foretel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादिश|व्यादिशः
व्य्-आदिश, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादिश्य
व्य्-आदिश्य, ind. having pointed out, having pre-<BR>scribed or ordered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादिष्ट
व्य्-आदिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, assigned or divided sepa-<BR>rately, distributed; pointed out, explained, instructed,<BR>taught; prescribed, ordered, charged, commanded;<BR>declared, indicated, foretold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादीर्घ
व्यादीर्घ व्य्-आदीर्घ, अस्, आ, अम्, very long<BR>or extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादृश्
व्यादृश् व्य्-आ-दृश्, Pass. -दृश्यते, to be<BR>clearly seen or visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याध|व्याधं|व्याधः
व्याध व्याध. See under rt. व्यध्, p. 974,<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधा
व्याधा व्य्-आ-धा (वि-आ-), cl. 3. P. A. -द-<BR>धाति, -धत्ते, -धातुम्, to separate, divide, dis-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">Page0979-c+ 75</a>]<BR>tract: Pass. -धीयते, Ved. to be separated or<BR>divided; to be out of health, feel unwell; [cf.<BR>व्याधि below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहित
व्य्-आहित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. diseased, unwell, ill,<BR>sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाम|व्याधामः
व्याधाम व्य्-आधाम, अस्, m. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. ध्मा with आ and वि, but perhaps fr. व्य्-आ-धा,<BR>cf. also व्य्-आधाव below), Indra's thunderbolt (=<BR>वज्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाव|व्याधावः
व्याधाव व्य्-आधाव. See under व्य्-आ-धू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधि|व्याधिः
व्याधि व्याधि, इस्, m. (probably to be con-<BR>nected with व्य्-आ-धा above, but also derived fr. rt.<BR>व्यध्, and perhaps connected with 2. आ-धि), pain,<BR>sickness, ailment, disease (in general); leprosy; N.<BR>of a son of Mṛtyu or Death.<BR>—व्याधि-कर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, causing sickness, unhealthy.<BR>—व्याधि-ग्रस्त<BR>or व्याधि-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, seized or afflicted with<BR>disease.<BR>—व्याधि-घात, अस्, m. ‘illness-destroyer,’<BR>the tree Cassia Fistula (= आरग्-बध).<BR>—व्याधि-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, removing or destroying disease.<BR>—व्याधि-दुर्भिक्ष-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted<BR>with sickness and famine.<BR>—व्याधि-निग्रह, अस्,<BR>m. suppression of disease.<BR>—व्याधि-निर्जय, अस्, m.<BR>the subduing a disease.<BR>—व्याधि-बहुल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>frequently visited with disease (as a village).<BR>—व्या-<BR>धि-भय, अम्, n. fear of disease.<BR>—व्याधि-युक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, suffering from illness, diseased, sick.<BR>—व्याधि-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, free from disease,<BR>convalescent.<BR>—व्याधि-हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, destroy-<BR>ing or removing disease; (ता), m. a kind of plant<BR>(= वाराही-कन्द).<BR>—व्याध्य्-आर्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pained with or suffering from disease.<BR>—व्याध्य्-<BR>उपशम, अस्, m. allaying or curing diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधित|व्याधितः
व्याधित, अस्, आ, अम्, diseased, sick, ill, ailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिन्
3. व्याधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, diseased, sick, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधू
व्याधू व्य्-आ-धू (वि-आ-), cl. 5. P. A. -धू-<BR>नोति, -धूनुते (later also -धुनोति, -धुनुते),<BR>-धवितुम्, -धोतुम्, to shake to and fro, move<BR>or toss about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाव|व्याधावः
व्य्-आधाव, अस्, m. Indra's thunderbolt; [cf. व्य्-<BR>आधाम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधुत|व्याधुतः
व्य्-आधुत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken about, tossed<BR>hither and thither, shaking, trembling, tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधुन्वत्
व्य्-आधुन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, shaking or waving<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधूत|व्याधूतः
व्य्-आधूत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken about, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधूय
व्य्-आधूय, ind. having shaken or waved about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधूयमान
व्य्-आधूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being shaken or<BR>tossed about, being moved hither and thither, being<BR>fanned; flickering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यान|व्यानः
व्यान व्य्-आन, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अन् with आ and<BR>वि), one of the five vital airs (that which circulates<BR>or is diffused through the body, see प्राण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानम्
व्यानम् व्य्-आ-नम् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. A. -न-<BR>मति, -ते, &c., to bend or bow down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानत|व्यानतं
व्य्-आनत, अस्, आ, अम्, bent down, having the<BR>face bent towards the ground; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>coitus.<BR>—व्यानत-करण, अम्, n. the posture as-<BR>sumed in the preceding kind of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानशि
व्यानशि व्य्-आनशि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. व्य्-अश्), Ved.<BR>one who has pervaded, pervading, penetrating, (Sāy.<BR>व्य्-आनशिः = व्याप्नुवत्, Ṛg-veda III. 49, 3; in<BR>Naigh. III. 1. व्यानशिः is enumerated among the<BR>बहु-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानशिन्
व्य्-आनशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. pervading, (Sāy. =<BR>व्यापन-शील.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानह्
व्यानह् व्य्-आ-नह्, cl. 4. P. A. -नह्यति, -ते,<BR>-नद्धुम्, to connect mutually, intersperse, inter-<BR>weave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानद्ध
व्य्-आनद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, connected mutually,<BR>interspersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानी
व्यानी व्य्-आ-नी, cl. 1. P. A. -नयति, -ते,<BR>-नेतुम्, Ved. to pour in separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्
व्याप् व्य्-आप् (वि-आप्), cl. 5. P. -आप्नोति (some-<BR>times also A. -आप्नुते), -आप्तुम्, to reach through,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">Page0980-a+ 81</a>]<BR>spread through, go everywhere, overspread, pervade,<BR>permeate, fill up, occupy, cover, fill; to reach as far<BR>as, extend to: Pass. -आप्यते, &c.: Caus. -आपयति,<BR>&c.: Desid. वीप्सति; [cf. वीप्सा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापक|व्यापकः
व्य्-आपक, अस्, इका, अम्, pervading, diffusive,<BR>comprehensive, going everywhere, widely spreading,<BR>extending over the whole of anything, extensive, in-<BR>variably concomitant or inherent; (in law) compre-<BR>hending all the points of an argument, pervading the<BR>whole plea; (अस्), m. (in logic) ‘the pervader,’ a<BR>pervading attribute, one invariably concomitant (i. e.<BR>always found where some other is found); (इका), f.<BR>an impudent woman; (अम्), n. an invariably con-<BR>comitant or inherent property or characteristic.<BR>—व्या-<BR>पक-ता, f. or व्यापक-त्व, अम्, n. pervasion,<BR>diffusion, extensiveness, comprehensiveness; invari-<BR>able concomitance or inherence.<BR>—व्यापक-न्यास,<BR>अस्, m. (in the Tantra system) a particular disposition<BR>or arrangement of mystical texts over the whole per-<BR>son, (according to Śabda-k. = शिरस्तः पादान्तम्<BR>पादतः शिरो ऽन्तम् मूल-मन्त्र-विन्यासः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापन|व्यापनं
व्य्-आपन, अम्, n. the act of spreading through or<BR>throughout, pervading, penetrating, penetration, fill-<BR>ing up; covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापनीय
व्य्-आपनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, fit to be pervaded or<BR>penetrated, permeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापित
व्य्-आपित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), filled up, filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापिन्
व्यापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, reaching through, pervading,<BR>extending over or to, covering; all-pervading, dif-<BR>fusive, comprehensive, co-extensive, invariably in-<BR>herent or concomitant; (ई), m. ‘the pervader,’ N.<BR>of Viṣṇu; a pervading property or characteristic.<BR>—व्यापि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of pervading, exten-<BR>siveness, extent, pervasion, diffusedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्त|व्याप्तं
व्य्-आप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, spread through, pervaded,<BR>pervading, extended, thoroughly occupied or pene-<BR>trated by (as the universe by spirit, &c.); encom-<BR>passed, surrounded; filled up, full; comprehended<BR>or included (under a general notion); having inhe-<BR>rent properties, invariably attended or accompanied<BR>(e. g. smoke is invariably attended by fire or neces-<BR>sarily includes or implies fire); obtained, possessed,<BR>possessed of; celebrated, famous; placed, fixed; open,<BR>outspread, expanded.<BR>—व्याप्त-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>most diffused.<BR>—व्याप्तान्तर (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having intervals or holes or recesses filled up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्ति|व्याप्तिः
व्य्-आप्ति, इस्, f. the act or state of pervading, per-<BR>vasion, pervadedness, permeation, pervading inhe-<BR>rence, the inherent and inseparable presence of any<BR>one thing in another (as of oil in sesamum seed,<BR>heat in fire, &c.), universal pervasion, inseparable in-<BR>volvedness, invariable concomitance, invariable attend-<BR>ance on an ascertained sign, universal distribution (in<BR>logic), universal accompaniment of the middle term<BR>by the major (e. g. smoke is always pervaded by<BR>fire or fire is necessarily involved in smoke; it is this<BR>idea of pervasion that constitutes the peculiarity of<BR>the Hindū syllogism); universality, universal or<BR>general rule or law without an exception; omni-<BR>presence, ubiquity (as a divine attribute); fulness;<BR>obtaining, gaining, acquiring.<BR>—व्याप्ति-कर्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, Ved. whose function is diffusion.<BR>—व्याप्ति-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, m. apprehension of a general proposition or<BR>of universal concomitance, induction.<BR>—व्याप्ति-ज्ञान,<BR>अम्, n. knowledge of pervading inherence or of the<BR>presence of invariably concomitant properties.<BR>—व्य्-<BR>आप्ति-निश्चय, अस्, m. (in logic) the ascertainment of<BR>pervading inherence or universal concomitance.<BR>—व्य्-<BR>आप्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing pervasion, univer-<BR>sally diffused, pervading; pervaded, attended by.<BR>—व्याप्ति-लक्षण, अम्, n. sign or proof of uni-<BR>versal pervasion or of the invariable attendance of an<BR>inherent property or characteristic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्नुवान
व्य्-आप्नुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, pervading, permeating,<BR>penetrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्य|व्याप्यं|व्याप्यः
1. व्य्-आप्य, ind. having pervaded, having pene-<BR>trated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्य|व्याप्यं|व्याप्यः
2. व्य्-आप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, permeable, penetrable;<BR>capable of being attended by any inherent character-<BR>istic or constantly pervaded or accompanied by it;<BR>(अम्), n. that which may be the site or locality of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">Page0980-b+ 79</a>]<BR>universal pervasion or of an invariably concomitant<BR>cause or characteristic (e. g. smoke is invariably per-<BR>vaded by fire); the sign or middle term of an infer-<BR>ence, the proof, reason, cause (= साधन, हेतु);<BR>a particular medicinal plant, Costus Speciosus (=<BR>कुष्ठ).<BR>—व्याप्य-ता, f. or व्याप्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>permeableness, the state or capacity of being invari-<BR>ably pervaded or attended by; capacity of obtaining.<BR>—व्याप्यत्वासिद्धि (˚व-अस्˚), इस्, f. (in logic) im-<BR>perfect conclusion (i. e. where the alleged invariable-<BR>ness of concomitancy is not real).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्यमान
व्य्-आप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being pervaded, being<BR>permeated or penetrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद्
व्यापद् 1. व्य्-आ-पद् (वि-आ-), cl. 4. A. -पद्-<BR>यते, -पत्तुम्, to fall away, fall down, fall into<BR>misfortune, perish; to disappear, be inaudible (as a<BR>sound): Caus. -पादयति, -यितुम्, to cause to perish,<BR>destroy, kill; to make worse, injure, hurt, spoil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापत्ति|व्यापत्तिः
व्य्-आपत्ति, इस्, f. falling into misfortune, ruin;<BR>change, substitution of one thing for another, (वर्-<BR>ण-व्˚, substitution of one letter for another; as the<BR>change of Visarga into its corresponding sibilant.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद्
2. व्य्-आपद्, त्, f. death, decease; ruin, disease,<BR>calamity; derangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापन्न|व्यापन्नः
व्य्-आपन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen into misfortune,<BR>miscarried, failed; dead, deceased, expired, killed,<BR>perished; diseased; deranged, disordered; hurt,<BR>injured; changed, altered, substituted (as one letter<BR>or symbol for another, especially applied to the<BR>change of the Visarjanīya or Visarga to its corres-<BR>ponding sibilants; when this symbol remains un-<BR>changed it is called विक्रान्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापाद|व्यापादः
व्य्-आपाद, अस्, m. destroying, destruction, ruin,<BR>injury, evil design, the wish or project to injure<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादक
व्यापादक, अस्, इका, अम्, destructive, murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादन|व्यापादनं
व्य्-आपादन, अम्, n. the act of destroying, de-<BR>struction, killing, slaying; malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादनीय
व्य्-आपादनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be killed, liable to<BR>death, worthy of death or destruction.<BR>—व्यापाद-<BR>नीय-ता, f. the necessity of being killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादयितव्य
व्य्-आपादयितव्य or व्य्-आपाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to<BR>be killed, to be put to death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादित|व्यापादितः
व्य्-आपादित, अस्, आ, अम्, destroyed, killed, slain;<BR>hurt, injured.<BR>—व्यापादित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one<BR>who has killed or destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृ
व्यापृ व्य्-आ-पृ (वि-आ-), cl. 6. A. -प्रियते,<BR>-पर्तुम्, to be occupied or engaged in (with loc.);<BR>to be busy or occupied about anything (with अर्थम्<BR>or हेतोः at the end of a comp.), be employed or<BR>placed in any office: Caus. -पारयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to be employed, set to work, set in motion or<BR>action; to occupy with, engage upon (with loc.,<BR>rarely with inst.); to employ, use, apply to any use<BR>or purpose, entrust with, charge, commission, place<BR>(in any office); to place, set, fix (e. g. व्यापारया-<BR>मास करम्, he placed his hand; व्यापारयामास<BR>विलोचनानि, he fixed his eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापार|व्यापारः
व्य्-आपार, अस्, m. occupation, employment, busi-<BR>ness, trade, profession; exercise, practice, exertion,<BR>activity; work, affair, operation, action, act, trans-<BR>action, doing, performance.<BR>—व्यापारावेश (˚र-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. the arising of a determination or resolve<BR>(in phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारयत्
व्य्-आपारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, setting to work, em-<BR>ploying; busying, exercising; placing; moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारित
व्य्-आपारित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to be busy, set to<BR>work, engaged, occupied, employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारिन्
व्यापारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, occupied, busy; transacting<BR>business; engaged in trade, a dealer, trader, agent;<BR>exercising, practising; causing action or motion,<BR>moving, motive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृत|व्यापृतः
व्य्-आपृत, अस्, आ, अम्, occupied, engaged or occu-<BR>pied in (with loc.), engaged, employed, busy, ap-<BR>pointed to any office; (अस्), m. a minister, employé,<BR>chargé d'affaires (= कर्म-सचिव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्रियमाण
व्य्-आप्रियमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being occupied or<BR>engaged in (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्त|व्याप्तं
व्याप्त व्य्-आप्त, व्य्-आप्ति. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभञ्ज्
व्याभञ्ज् व्य्-आ-भञ्ज् (वि-आ-), cl. 7. P. -भ-<BR>नक्ति, -भङ्क्तुम्, to break to pieces, shatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभग्न
व्य्-आभग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, broken to pieces, ṣat-<BR>tered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभाष्
व्याभाष् व्य्-आ-भाष् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. A. -भा-<BR>षते, -भाषितुम्, to speak to, address; to profess,<BR>declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभाषमाण
व्य्-आभाषमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking to, ad-<BR>dressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभाषित
व्य्-आभाषित, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken to, addressed;<BR>spoken, pronounced [cf. दुःख-व्˚]; (अम्), n. a<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभुज्
व्याभुज् व्य्-आ-भुज् (वि-आ-), cl. 6. P. -भुजति,<BR>-भोक्तुम्, to bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभुग्न
व्य्-आभुग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभ्युक्षी
व्याभ्युक्षी व्य्-आभ्य्-उक्षी, f. (probably fr. rt.<BR>1. उक्ष् with अभि, आ, and वि, cf. व्य्-आत्य्-उक्षी),<BR>gamboling in water, bathing for pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याम|व्यामः
व्याम व्याम, अस्, m. (probably for व्य्-<BR>आयाम, q. v.), a fathom or the space between the<BR>tips of the fingers of either hand when the arms are<BR>extended; disregard, disrespect (?); smoke (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामन|व्यामनं
व्यामन, अम्, n. = व्याम above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामर्ष|व्यामर्षः
व्यामर्ष 1. व्य्-आमर्ष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. मृष्<BR>with आ and वि), impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामर्ष|व्यामर्षः
व्यामर्ष 2. व्य्-आमर्ष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. मृश्<BR>with आ and वि), rubbing out, erasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामृष्ट
1. व्य्-आमृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed out, effaced,<BR>rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामिश्र|व्यामिश्रं
व्यामिश्र व्य्-आ-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, intermixed,<BR>blended together, mingled, confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामील्य
व्यामील्य व्य्-आ-मील्य, ind. (fr. rt. मील् with<BR>आ and वि), having closed and opened, having twinkled,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामुच्
व्यामुच् व्य्-आ-मुच् (वि-आ-), cl. 6. P. A. -मुञ्-<BR>चति, -ते, -मोक्तुम्, to emit, discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामोक|व्यामोकः
व्य्-आमोक, अस्, m. release or freeing from, getting<BR>rid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामुह्
व्यामुह् व्य्-आ-मुह् (वि-आ-), cl. 4. P. -मुह्यति,<BR>&c., to become stupified or bewildered, to be infatu-<BR>ated: Caus. -मोहयति, -यितुम्, to stupify, bewilder,<BR>perplex, infatuate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामूढ
व्य्-आमूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely stupified, thoroughly<BR>infatuated or bewildered, bewitched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामोह|व्यामोहः
व्य्-आमोह, अस्, m. bewilderment, embarrassment,<BR>error, foolishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामोहित
व्य्-आमोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, bewildered, infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामृज्
व्यामृज् व्य्-आ-मृज् (वि-आ-), cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि,<BR>&c., to rub off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामृष्ट
2. व्य्-आमृष्ट, rubbed off.<BR>—व्यामृष्ट-ति-<BR>लक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has the Tilaka mark<BR>rubbed off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायम्
व्यायम् व्य्-आ-यम् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. -यच्छति<BR>(Ved. and ep. also A. -ते), -यन्तुम्, -यमितुम्, to<BR>draw apart or asunder, stretch or draw out, extend;<BR>to drag or tear off (P.); to struggle or contend about<BR>(loc.), fight together (usually A.); to make efforts,<BR>strive, endeavour; to sport, dally: Caus. -यमयति or<BR>-यामयति, -यितुम्, to cause to stretch out or struggle,<BR>make great effort or exertion, take exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायच्छत्
व्य्-आयच्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, struggling or contend-<BR>ing about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायच्छमान|व्यायछमान
व्य्-आयच्छमान, अस्, आ, अम्, struggling or con-<BR>tending together; fighting, quarrelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायत|व्यायतं
व्य्-आयत, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn asunder, separated,<BR>drawn out, extended, long, tall; expanded, wide open;<BR>exercised, disciplined; busy, engaged, occupied; hard,<BR>firm; mighty, powerful, strong, intense, deep, much,<BR>excessive; (अम्), ind. excessively.<BR>—व्यायत-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. firmness.<BR>—व्यायत-पात, अस्, m. a strong<BR>or intense blow, a deep stroke (= अवगाढ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायाम|व्यायामः
व्य्-आयाम, अस्, m. drawing or stretching out; a<BR>particular measure of length (= a fathom measured<BR>by the two extended arms, cf. व्याम); struggling,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">Page0981-a+ 75</a>]<BR>struggle, contention; fatigue, labour; exercise, exer-<BR>tion, manliness, manly effort, athletic or gymnastic<BR>exercise (e. g. playing with heavy clubs, drawing a<BR>bow with a chain in place of a string, alternate rising<BR>and falling at full length on the ground, &c.); busi-<BR>ness, occupation; a difficult passage or impassable<BR>defile, any difficulty.<BR>—व्यायाम-शील, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>accustomed to exertion or exercise, fond of taking<BR>exercise, active, robust, athletic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामिक
व्यायामिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to exercise or<BR>exertion, gymnastic, athletic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामिन्
व्यायामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, taking exercise, undergoing<BR>fatigue, active, athletic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायाम्य
व्य्-आयाम्य, ind. having made exertion or effort,<BR>having taken exercise, having practised gymnastics,<BR>having made to undergo exercise or exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायुज्
व्यायुज् व्य्-आ-युज् (वि-आ-), cl. 7. P. A. -यु-<BR>नक्ति, -युङ्क्ते, -योक्तुम्, to disunite, separate, part,<BR>become disunited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायुज्य
व्य्-आयुज्य, ind. having disjoined or separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायोग|व्यायोगः
व्य्-आयोग, अस्, m. a kind of dramatic representa-<BR>tion or composition in one act (belonging to the<BR>Prakaraṇa class, and describing some military or heroic<BR>exploit in which no part of the interest is derived<BR>from female participation, the sentiment of love being<BR>thereby excluded).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यारब्ध
व्यारब्ध व्य्-आ-रब्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. रभ्<BR>with आ and वि), Ved. held on every side, upheld,<BR>maintained, properly carried into effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याल|व्यालः
व्याल व्याल, अस्, आ, अम् (connected with<BR>व्याड, q. v.), wicked, villainous, bad; cruel, fierce;<BR>vicious; (अस्), m. a villain, cheat, rogue; a snake;<BR>a beast of prey; a tiger; a hunting leopard; a<BR>vicious elephant; a king; N. of Viṣṇu; a species<BR>of the Daṇḍaka metre; (ई), f. a female snake;<BR>[cf. Old Germ. and Angl. Sax. al.]<BR>—व्याल-खड्ग,<BR>अस्, m. = व्याल-नख below.<BR>—व्याल-गन्धा, f.<BR>the ichneumon plant (= नाकुली).<BR>—व्याल-ग्राह,<BR>अस्, m. a snake-catcher.<BR>—व्याल-ग्राहिन्, ई, m. a<BR>snake-catcher, one who lives by catching and exhi-<BR>biting snakes.<BR>—व्याल-जिह्वा, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>महा-समङ्गा).<BR>—व्याल-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>fierce or cruel.<BR>—व्याल-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of plant (= गो-क्षुर).<BR>—व्याल-नख, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of medicinal herb with a fragrant root (in<BR>Hindī called बघ्नहा = व्याघ्र-नख).<BR>—व्याल-<BR>पत्त्रा, f. a kind of cucumber (= एर्वारु).<BR>—व्याल-<BR>पाणि-ज, अस्, m. = व्याल-नख.<BR>—व्याल-बल, अस्,<BR>m. = व्याल-नख.<BR>—व्याल-मृग, अस्, m. a fierce<BR>animal, wild stag; a hunting leopard.<BR>—व्याल-रूप,<BR>अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—व्याल-वत्, ind. like a<BR>serpent; like a beast of prey.<BR>—व्यालायुध (˚ल-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. a sort of vegetable perfume (=<BR>व्याल-नख, नखी, व्याडायुध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालक|व्यालकः
व्यालक, अस्, m. a vicious elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालम्ब्
व्यालम्ब् व्य्-आ-लम्ब्, cl. 1. A. -लम्बते, -लम्-<BR>बितुम्, to hang down; to stay behind, linger, delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालम्ब|व्यालंब|व्यालंबः|व्यालम्बः
व्य्-आलम्ब, अस्, m. the red Ricinus or castor-oil<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालिख्
व्यालिख् व्य्-आ-लिख् (वि-आ-), cl. 6. P. -लिखति,<BR>-लेखितुम्, to scratch or scrape against, rub against,<BR>touch, graze; to make an incision, scratch, draw<BR>lines, write.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालिखत्
व्य्-आलिखत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, scratching, scrap-<BR>ing, piercing; touching, grazing, extending to; draw-<BR>ing lines, delineating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालीन
व्यालीन व्य्-आलीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ली with<BR>आ and वि), clinging or sticking close together, cluster-<BR>ing, dense, thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालुड्
व्यालुड् व्य्-आ-लुड्, Caus. -लोडयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to stir about, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालोडित
व्य्-आलोडित, अस्, आ, अम्, = मथित, stirred about,<BR>agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालुप्
व्यालुप् व्य्-आ-लुप् (वि-आ-), cl. 6. P. -लुम्पति,<BR>-लोप्तुम्, to take away, carry off, remove: Pass.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">Page0981-b+ 71</a>]<BR>-लुप्यते, to be broken asunder or destroyed, be<BR>divided, be removed, to disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालू
व्यालू व्य्-आ-लू (वि-आ-), cl. 9. P. A. -लुनाति,<BR>-लुनीते, -लवितुम्, to cut off, cut away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालून
व्य्-आलून, अस्, आ, अम्, cut off.<BR>—व्यालून-मूर्-<BR>धज, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has the hair cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालोल
व्यालोल व्य्-आलोल, अस्, आ, अम्, rolling about,<BR>quivering, tremulous, shaking, waving.<BR>—व्यालोल-<BR>कुन्तल-कलाप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having dishevelled<BR>locks of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याळि
व्याळि व्याऌइ = व्याडि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावकलन|व्यावकलनं
व्यावकलन व्य्-आवकलन, अम्, n. = व्य्-अव-<BR>कलन, subtraction (in arithmetic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावकलित
व्य्-आवकलित, अस्, आ, अम्, subtracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावक्रोशी
व्यावक्रोशी व्य्-आवक्रोशी, f. (fr. rt. क्रुश् with<BR>अव, आ, and वि), mutual abuse or imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावप्
व्यावप् व्य्-आ-वप् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. A. -व-<BR>पति, -ते, -वप्तुम्, to sow, scatter, strew, (according<BR>to some the Ved. व्यावपाति, Pāṇ. III. 1, 34, is for<BR>व्यावयाति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावभाषी
व्यावभाषी व्य्-आवभाषी, f. (fr. rt. भाष्<BR>with अव, आ, and वि), mutual abuse or imprecation;<BR>[cf. व्य्-आवक्रोशी above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्ण्
व्यावर्ण् व्य्-आ-वर्ण् (वि-आ-), cl. 10. P. -वर्-<BR>णयति, -यितुम्, to enumerate, describe, narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्ण्य
व्य्-आवर्ण्य, ind. having narrated in detail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त|व्यावर्तः|व्यावर्त्त|व्यावर्त्तः
व्यावर्त व्य्-आवर्त. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावल्ग्
व्यावल्ग् व्य्-आ-वल्ग् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. -वल्-<BR>गति, &c., to jump, skip, leap; to gallop; to move<BR>quickly about, quiver, throb, be agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावल्गत्
व्य्-आवल्गत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, jumping, leaping, &c.;<BR>throbbing, being agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावल्गित
व्य्-आवल्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, jumped, moved, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारिक|व्यावहारिकः
व्यावहारिक व्यावहारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. व्य्-<BR>अवहार), relating to business or practice or action,<BR>practical, active; belonging to judicial procedure,<BR>judicial, legal; what has to be dealt with or is practised<BR>or intended for use, practicable, customary, usual, cur-<BR>rent; (अस्), m. a counsellor, minister; (अम्), n. use.<BR>—व्यावहारिक-त्व, अम्, n. practicalness; the state<BR>of belonging to the period of action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारी
व्यावहारी व्य्-आवहारी, f. (fr. rt. हृ with<BR>अव, आ, and वि), mutual seizing or taking (Vopa-deva<BR>XXVI. 177).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहासी
व्यावहासी व्य्-आवहासी, f. (fr. rt. हस् with<BR>अव, आ, and वि), mutual derision, reciprocal laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याविध
व्याविध व्य्-आ-विध, अस्, आ, अम् (see 2. वि-<BR>ध), of various kinds, multifarious, omnigenous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृ
व्यावृ व्य्-आ-वृ (वि-आ-), cl. 5. 9. 1. P. A.<BR>-वृणोति, -वृणुते, -वृणाति, -वृणीते, -वरति, -ते,<BR>-वरितुम्, -वरीतुम्, to cover over, conceal; to obstruct,<BR>stop; to choose, select; to open, (but forms like व्य्-<BR>आवर् in Ved. are referred to वि-वृ, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृण्वान
व्य्-आवृण्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, concealing or hiding<BR>one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत
व्य्-आवृत, अस्, आ, अम्, covered over, screened;<BR>obstructed; excluded, excepted, (perhaps for व्य्-<BR>आवृत्त); uncovered, opened, (in this sense वि is<BR>rather privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृति|व्यावृतिः
व्य्-आवृति, इस्, f. covering, screening; exclusion;<BR>[cf. व्य्-आवृत्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्य
1. व्य्-आवृत्य, ind. having covered over; having<BR>obstructed or stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृज्
व्यावृज् व्य्-आ-वृज् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. -वर्जति,<BR>&c., -वर्जितुम्, to exclude from; to divide or sepa-<BR>rate into parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृज्य
व्य्-आवृज्य, ind. having separated or divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्
व्यावृत् व्य्-आ-वृत् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. A. (in cer-<BR>tain tenses also P., see rt. 1. वृत्), -वर्तते, -वर्ति-<BR>तुम्, to become separated or singled out from (with<BR>inst.); to become separate or distinct, keep apart;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">Page0981-c+ 79</a>]<BR>to be split asunder or opened; to turn away from,<BR>become averted, go away, depart; to roll or turn<BR>back, return; to turn round, go round, revolve; to<BR>go down, set (said of the sun); to come to an end,<BR>cease, perish: Caus. -वर्तयति, -यितुम्, to separate<BR>from (with inst. or abl.); to turn away, turn out, set<BR>aside, exclude, put aside, lay down, remove, take<BR>away, destroy, overrule, annul; to throw down, throw<BR>about, strew; to turn about or round, cause to revolve;<BR>to retract; to exchange, substitute one for another,<BR>to contrive (?) : Pass. of Caus. -वर्त्यते, to be excluded,<BR>&c.: Desid. -वृत्सते, to wish to separate from, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त|व्यावर्तः|व्यावर्त्त|व्यावर्त्तः
व्य्-आवर्त, अस्, m. separating from, selecting, revo-<BR>lution, going round; encompassing, surrounding, en-<BR>closing; ruptured navel, umbilical hernia (= नाभि-<BR>कण्टक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तक|व्यावर्त्तक
व्य्-आवर्तक, अस्, इका, अम्, separating from, ex-<BR>cluding, excepting; turning away from; turning<BR>round; encircling, encompassing.<BR>—व्यावर्तक-ता,<BR>f. state of excluding, exclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तन|व्यावर्तनं|व्यावर्त्तन
व्य्-आवर्तन, अम्, n. the act of turning round or<BR>away, rolling round, revolving; a volute, fold, band;<BR>encompassing, surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तमान
व्य्-आवर्तमान, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming separated<BR>from, keeping apart from; turning away; desisting,<BR>ceasing; turning back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तित
व्य्-आवर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to turn away,<BR>made to desist, made to revolve; exchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त्य
व्य्-आवर्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be excluded or excepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्त|व्यावृत्तः
व्य्-आवृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, separated or singled out<BR>from; excluded, excepted, free from (with inst.);<BR>opened, split asunder; turned away from, turned back,<BR>returned, desisted, desisting, ceased; turned round, re-<BR>volved; encompassed, surrounded; fenced, screened,<BR>(probably for व्य्-आवृत); praised, hymned (?).<BR>—व्या-<BR>वृत्त-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, turned back from a course,<BR>desisting from any course of action.<BR>—व्यावृत्त-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the being separated or excluded from,<BR>&c.; the being non-extensive, (defined to be<BR>अल्प-देश-वृत्तित्वम्, the existing in few places,<BR>i. e. comprising but few individuals, said of a species<BR>in relation to its genus; opposed to अधिक-देश-<BR>वृत्तित्वम्, the characteristic of a genus viewed in<BR>relation to the species it contains.)<BR>—व्यावृत्त-देह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the body severed or split asunder.<BR>—व्यावृत्त-बुद्धि, इस्, f. ‘limited conception,’ the<BR>conception of a class denoting few individuals, i. e. of<BR>a class contained in a higher class.<BR>—व्यावृत्त-शिरस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, having the head turned round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्ति|व्यावृत्तिः
व्य्-आवृत्ति, इस्, f. separation from, selecting, selec-<BR>tion, choice, (perhaps for व्य्-आवृति); exception, ex-<BR>clusion, rejection; turning away; rolling back; roll-<BR>ing round, surrounding; screening, (perhaps for व्य्-<BR>आवृति); praise, eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्य
2. व्य्-आवृत्य, ind. having separated from, having<BR>parted with (with inst.), having turned or rolled<BR>away, having turned back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याव्यध्
व्याव्यध् व्य्-आ-व्यध् (वि-आ-), cl. 4. P. -विध्-<BR>यति, -व्यद्धुम्, to throw about; to brandish, wave<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याविद्ध
व्य्-आविद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or tossed about,<BR>dishevelled; glancing or darting in all directions;<BR>interlaced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याविध्य
व्य्-आविध्य, ind. having brandished or waved about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यास|व्यासः
व्यास व्य्-आस, व्यास-तीर्थ, &c. See p. 978.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासञ्ज्|व्यासंज्
व्यासञ्ज् व्य्-आ-सञ्ज् (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. -सजति,<BR>-सङ्क्तुम्, to attach firmly to, fasten on; to adhere<BR>separately or severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासक्त|व्यासक्तः
व्य्-आसक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, firmly attached to or con-<BR>nected with, adhering closely to (any one or any-<BR>thing), devoted to, intent on, occupied with; inher-<BR>ing separately; detached, disjoined, (in this sense वि<BR>is privative); bewildered, confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासङ्ग|व्यासंग|व्यासंगः|व्यासङ्गः
व्य्-आसङ्ग, अस्, m. excessive attachment, close<BR>adherence, devotion or addiction to, resting or sitting<BR>on; close attachment (of the thoughts), attention,<BR>assiduous application, diligent study; addition; de-<BR>tachment, separation, (in this sense वि is privative);<BR>perplexity, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासङ्गिन्
व्यासङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, attaching one's self or apply-<BR>ing closely to (anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासज्य
व्य्-आसज्य, ind. having firmly attached or fastened<BR>on, having adhered or inhered separately or severally.<BR>—व्यासज्य-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, inhering in more sub-<BR>jects than one (as a quality &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासिद्ध|व्यासिद्धः
व्यासिद्ध व्य्-आसिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (see 2. आ-सिद्-<BR>ध), prohibited, forbidden, restrained; contraband<BR>(i. e. not allowed to be sold except to particular<BR>persons or in certain places).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासेध|व्यासेधः
व्य्-आसेध, अस्, m. prohibition, hindrance, restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासुकि
व्यासुकि व्यासुकि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहन्
व्याहन् व्य्-आ-हन् (वि-आ-), cl. 2. P. -हन्ति,<BR>-हन्तुम्, to strike at excessively, strike back, repel,<BR>repulse; to foil, disappoint; to impede, obstruct,<BR>delay; to vex: Caus. -घातयति, -यितुम्, to repel,<BR>obstruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहत|व्याहतः
व्य्-आहत, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively struck at, struck<BR>or hit back; repelled, repulsed; obstructed, impeded;<BR>foiled, disappointed, expelled; confused, alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहन्यमान
व्य्-आहन्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being excessively<BR>struck back or repelled, being obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृ
व्याहृ व्य्-आ-हृ (वि-आ-), cl. 1. P. A. -हरति,<BR>-ते, -हर्तुम्, to utter or pronounce a sound, speak,<BR>say, tell, declare, narrate, report; to explain; to<BR>answer; to cry, scream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहरण|व्याहरणं
व्य्-आहरण, अम्, n. the act of uttering or pro-<BR>nouncing, utterance, pronunciation; speech, narra-<BR>tion, explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहरत्
व्य्-आहरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, uttering, pronouncing,<BR>speaking; uttering a cry (as an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहर्तव्य
व्य्-आहर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be told or declared<BR>or mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहार|व्याहारः
व्य्-आहार, अस्, m. utterance, speech, voice; a<BR>word, articulate sound, language; jest, joke, humorous<BR>speech, facetious allusion (a particular Alaṅkāra or<BR>figure in rhetoric).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहारिन्
व्य्-आहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking, saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृत
व्य्-आहृत, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken, uttered, pronounced,<BR>said, declared.<BR>—व्याहृत-सन्देश, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who tells news or communicates information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृति|व्याहृतिः
व्य्-आहृति, इस्, f. utterance, speech, voice; an utter-<BR>ance, articulate sound, word; a mystical word pro-<BR>nounced after ॐ by every Brāhman in commencing<BR>his daily prayers, (cf. Manu II. 76; भूर्, भुवः,<BR>स्वर् are the three great Vyāhṛtis, and महर्, q. v.,<BR>is said to be a fourth mystical word, cf. महा-<BR>व्याहृति.)<BR>—व्याहृति-त्रय, अम्, n. the three Vyā-<BR>hṛtis or mystical words (described above).<BR>—व्याहृति-<BR>पूर्वक, अस्, इका, अम्, preceded by the three mystical<BR>words भूर्, भुवः, स्वर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृत्य
व्य्-आहृत्य, ind. having uttered, having spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याह्वे
व्याह्वे व्य्-आ-ह्वे, cl. 1. P. A. -ह्वयति, -ते,<BR>&c., to call separately or distinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहाव|व्याहावः
व्य्-आहाव, अस्, अम्, m. n. a separate or distinct call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यु
व्यु व्य्-उ (वि-उ), cl. 5. P. -उनोति, Ved. to<BR>urge on, drive forward; to incite, animate, (Sāy. =<BR>प्रेरयति, Ṛg-veda V. 31, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युक्ष्
व्युक्ष् व्य्-उक्ष् (वि-उक्ष्, see rt. 1. उक्ष्), cl.<BR>6. P. A. -उक्षति, -ते, -उक्षितुम्, Ved. to sprinkle<BR>or pour out; to drip or flow or trickle over (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्चर्
व्युच्चर् व्य्-उच्-चर् (वि-उद्-चर्), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-चरति, -ते, -चरितुम्, to go forth in different direc-<BR>tions; to go out of the right path; to transgress or<BR>offend against, be faithless or disloyal towards (with<BR>acc.); to commit adultery with (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्चरत्
व्य्-उच्चरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, offending against, being<BR>faithless towards (with acc.); committing adultery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्चरमाण
व्य्-उच्चरमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, offending against,<BR>being faithless towards (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छत्
व्युच्छत् व्य्-उच्छत्. See 2. व्य्-उष्, 3. वि-वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छिद्
व्युच्छिद् व्य्-उच्-छिद् (वि-उद्-छिद्), cl. 7. P. A.<BR>-छिनत्ति, -छिन्त्ते, -छेत्तुम्, to cut entirely off,<BR>extirpate, cut up, destroy: Pass. -छिद्यते (ep. also<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">Page0982-b+ 79</a>]<BR>P. -छिद्यति), to be entirely cut off, be extirpated;<BR>to be interrupted, come to an end, become extinct,<BR>cease, fail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छित्ति|व्युच्छित्तिः
व्य्-उच्छित्ति, इस्, f. cutting off, cutting away, cutting<BR>short, destruction, rooting up, extirpation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छिन्न
व्य्-उच्छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, cut off, extirpated, com-<BR>pletely destroyed, interrupted, come to an end, ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छेत्तृ
व्य्-उच्छेत्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what cuts off or<BR>destroys, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छेद|व्युच्छेदः
व्य्-उच्छेद, अस्, m. cutting off, cutting short, de-<BR>struction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत|व्युतः
व्युत व्य्-उत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वि-वे), inter-<BR>woven, woven, sewn; separated, (Sāy. = विविक्त);<BR>stretched out, expanded, (according to Sāy. in this<BR>sense fr. rt. व्ये.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युति|व्युतिः
व्य्-उति, इस्, f. interweaving, weaving, sewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूत|व्यूतं
व्य्-ऊत, अस्, आ, अम्, interwoven, &c. = व्य्-उत<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूति|व्यूतिः
व्य्-ऊति, इस्, f. = व्य्-उति above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रम्
व्युत्क्रम् व्य्-उत्-क्रम् (वि-उद्-क्रम्), cl. 1. P.<BR>A. -क्रामति, -क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to go apart<BR>or in different directions, go in a wrong direction,<BR>go astray; to go or pass by, go beyond, overstep,<BR>deviate, go out of the right way, transgress; to dis-<BR>regard, neglect; to go away, depart, leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रम|व्युत्क्रमं|व्युत्क्रमः
व्य्-उत्क्रम, अस्, m. going astray or out of the<BR>right course, going or passing beyond, transgression,<BR>inverted order, reverse or irregular arrangement, de-<BR>rangement, disorder, confusion, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रम्य
व्य्-उत्क्रम्य, ind. having gone forth, having<BR>left; having passed by or gone beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रान्त|व्युत्क्रांत
व्य्-उत्क्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, gone asunder, gone<BR>forth, departed, left; passed by, gone beyond, over-<BR>stepped, transgressed, disregarded, neglected; (आ), f.<BR>a kind of riddle or enigma.<BR>—व्युत्क्रान्त-धर्म,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has overstepped his duty, neg-<BR>lectful of duty.<BR>—व्युत्क्रान्त-रजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, one<BR>whose impurity has gone away, free from passion.<BR>—व्युत्क्रान्त-वर्त्मन्, आ, आ, अ, one who has gone<BR>beyond the right path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रामत्
व्य्-उत्क्रामत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going asunder, going<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्था
व्युत्था व्य्-उत्-था (वि-उद्-स्था), Caus. -था-<BR>पयति, -यितुम्, to cause to rise up, stir up, excite<BR>greatly, rouse, instigate, incite, irritate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्थान|व्युत्थानं
व्य्-उत्थान, अम्, n. ‘excessive rising up,’ great<BR>activity; a kind of dancing or gesticulation; rising<BR>up against, opposition, contradiction, doing anything<BR>prohibited, obstruction, hindering; separate or indi-<BR>vidual exertion, independent action, following one's<BR>own inclination; the completion of a religious act or<BR>vow (as of contemplation or abstraction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्थापित
व्य्-उत्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to rise up, roused,<BR>brought up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पद्
व्युत्पद् व्य्-उत्-पद् (वि-उद्-पद्), cl. 4. A.<BR>-पद्यते, -पत्तुम्, to arise or originate clearly or<BR>in any well ascertained manner, to be produced from<BR>or out of; to originate; (in grammar) to be derived<BR>(from a root &c.); to have an etymology; to be<BR>an accomplished scholar, become perfectly proficient<BR>in or conversant with: Caus. -पादयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to issue out of, produce, cause; (in gram-<BR>mar) to derive, trace back to a root &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पत्ति|व्युत्पत्तिः
व्य्-उत्पत्ति, इस्, f. production, origin, derivation<BR>(especially of words from roots &c.), etymology; per-<BR>fection, completion, perfect conversancy with or pro-<BR>ficiency in (literature or science); scholarship, learn-<BR>ing.<BR>—व्युत्पत्ति-पक्षे, ind. on the side of deri-<BR>vation or etymology (an expression used by Vedic<BR>commentators when the accentuation is settled by<BR>the affixes and not according to the meaning of<BR>the words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पन्न|व्युत्पन्नः
व्य्-उत्पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, produced, generated,<BR>begotten; derived (from a root &c.; अ-व्युत्पन्-<BR>नम्, an underived or primitive word); formed (as a<BR>derivative word); completed, perfected, finished, ac-<BR>complished; quite conversant with or proficient in<BR>(literature &c.); learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पादक|व्युत्पादकः
व्य्-उत्पादक, अस्, इका, अम्, giving rise to, pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">Page0982-c+ 73</a>]<BR>ducing, originating, productive; tracing or forming<BR>(words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पाद्य
व्य्-उत्पाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, derivable, deducible,<BR>capable of being formed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पित्सु
व्य्-उत्पित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid.), desirous of<BR>making proficiency (in any science).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्सद्
व्युत्सद् व्य्-उत्-सद् (वि-उद्-), cl. 1. P. -सीदति,<BR>-सत्तुम्, to be unsettled; to be upset or overthrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युद्
व्युद् व्य्-उद् or व्य्-उन्द् (वि-उद्, &c.), cl. 7. P.<BR>-उनत्ति, -उन्दितुम्, Ved. to spring or gush forth; to<BR>wet or sprinkle thoroughly, water, drench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्त
व्य्-उत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well sprinkled or wetted,<BR>drenched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युन्दत्
व्य्-उन्दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. wetting thoroughly,<BR>sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युन्दन
व्य्-उन्दन, अम्, n. the act of well moistening or<BR>wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्
व्युदस् व्य्-उद्-अस् (वि-उद्-), cl. 4. P. -अस्यति,<BR>-असितुम्, to throw or scatter about, cast in every<BR>direction; to throw off, cast off, reject, lay aside,<BR>give up, abandon, exclude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्त
व्य्-उदस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or scattered about,<BR>cast off, put off, thrown aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्य
व्य्-उदस्य, ind. having thrown or scattered in all<BR>directions, having thrown off or put away, having<BR>thrown aside or abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदास|व्युदासः
व्य्-उदास, अस्, m. throwing or scattering in dif-<BR>ferent directions, throwing away or aside, rejection,<BR>exclusion (in grammar); prohibition; disregard for,<BR>indifference to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदित
व्युदित व्य्-उदित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वद् with<BR>वि), disputed, debated, discussed, contested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदूह्
व्युदूह् व्य्-उद्-ऊह् (वि-उद्-), cl. 1. P. -ऊहति,<BR>-ऊहितुम्, Ved. to push apart or asunder, move away,<BR>move out, remove; to sweep out or away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदूह्य
व्य्-उदूह्य, ind. having moved or placed asunder,<BR>having removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपदेश|व्युपदेशः
व्युपदेश व्य्-उपदेश, अस्, m. pretext, pre-<BR>tence, plausible but false plea, deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपनी
व्युपनी व्य्-उप-नी (वि-उप-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-नयति, -ते, -नेतुम्, Ved. to lead or bring sepa-<BR>rately or one by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपयुज्
व्युपयुज् व्य्-उप-युज् (वि-उप-), cl. 7. A.<BR>-युङ्क्ते, -योक्तुम्, to become closely attached, be<BR>concerned about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरम्
व्युपरम् व्य्-उप-रम् (वि-उप-), cl. 1. A. -र-<BR>मते (ep. also P. -ति), -रन्तुम्, to leave off or<BR>pause variously; to be at rest, be tranquil, have<BR>repose; to cease, desist from (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरत
व्य्-उपरत, अस्, आ, अम्, paused, rested, stopped,<BR>interrupted, ceased, desisted; calmed, tranquillized,<BR>tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरम|व्युपरमः
व्य्-उपरम, अस्, m. pause, cessation, interruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरमम्
व्य्-उपरमम्, ind., Ved. leaving off or pausing<BR>variously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरम्य
व्य्-उपरम्य, ind. having ceased or desisted<BR>from (with abl.), having stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपशम|व्युपशमः
व्युपशम व्य्-उपशम, अस्, m. non-cessation,<BR>not ceasing or desisting; inquietude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपारम्
व्युपारम् व्य्-उपा-रम् (वि-उप-आ-), cl. 1. A.<BR>-रमते (ep. P. -ति), -रन्तुम्, to desist from, leave<BR>off, cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपास्
व्युपास् व्य्-उपास् (वि-उप-अस्), cl. 4. P. -उपास्-<BR>यति, -उपासितुम्, to throw about, distribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युप्त
व्युप्त व्य्-उप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वि-वप्), scat-<BR>tered about, disordered, dishevelled.<BR>—व्युप्त-केश,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having dishevelled hair; (अस्), m. epi-<BR>thet of Rudra and Fire (as identified with Rudra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युब्ज्
व्युब्ज् व्य्-उब्ज् (वि-उब्ज्), cl. 6. P. -उब्जति,<BR>-उब्जितुम्, Ved. to uncover, open, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्
व्युष् 1. व्युष् (also read प्युष्), cl. 4.<BR>P. व्युष्यति, &c., to burn, (in this sense<BR>perhaps for rt. 1. उष् with वि); to divide, distribute,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">Page0983-a+ 76</a>]<BR>(in this sense also written प्युस्, पुष्, ब्युस्, बुस्);<BR>cl. 10. P. व्योषयति, -यितुम्, to reject, discharge,<BR>emit, (in this sense also written पुस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
1. व्युष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt, (perhaps to be<BR>written व्य्-उष्ट, see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्
व्युष् 2. व्य्-उष् (for 1. वि-वस्, q. v., cf.<BR>2. उष्), cl. 6. P. -उच्छति, &c., Ved. to shine forth,<BR>shine, dawn, arise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छत्
व्य्-उच्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. shining forth,<BR>dawning, (according to Sāy. व्युच्छन्ती = तमो<BR>वर्जयन्ती, Ṛg-veda I. 49, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छन
व्य्-उच्छन, अम्, n. shining forth, opening, mani-<BR>festation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्
3. व्य्-उष्, f., Ved. shining forth, dawning, (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. व्युषि = व्युच्छने सति, Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 45, 8, = विवासने or प्रकाशने सति, Ṛg-veda<BR>VII. 81, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युषित
1. व्य्-उषित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = 2. व्य्-उष्ट below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
2. व्य्-उष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, dawned, become day-light<BR>or dawn; become bright or clear; (अम्), n. dawn,<BR>day-break (personified as a son of Kalpa, in which<BR>case to be regarded as masc.), day; fruit, result,<BR>consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्टि|व्युष्टिः
व्य्-उष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. the rising or breaking of<BR>dawn, dawn; increase, prosperity, felicity; fruit,<BR>consequence; a hymn, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युषित
व्युषित 2. व्य्-उषित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 3. वि-<BR>वस्), lived away, dwelling abroad; dwelt, lodged,<BR>passed (e. g. व्य्-उषितो रात्रिम्, he lodged for a<BR>night, i. e. he passed or spent a night).<BR>—व्युषि-<BR>ताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king descended<BR>from Daśa-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
3. व्य्-उष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, dwelt, lodged; passed;<BR>one who has passed a night or lodged for a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्य
व्य्-उष्य, ind. having dwelt, having lodged, hav-<BR>ing passed or spent (e. g. रात्रिं व्य्-उष्य, having<BR>spent a night).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युस्
व्युस् व्युस्. See rt. ब्युस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढ|व्यूढः
व्यूढ 1. व्य्-ऊढ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. वि-वह्),<BR>married. (For 2. व्य्-ऊढ see under व्य्-ऊह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूत|व्यूतं
व्यूत व्य्-ऊत, व्य्-ऊति. See under व्य्-उत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूर्णु
व्यूर्णु व्य्-ऊर्णु (वि-ऊर्णु), cl. 2. P. A. -ऊर्णोति<BR>or -ऊर्णौति, -ऊर्णुते, -ऊर्णवितुम् or -ऊर्णुवितुम्,<BR>Ved. to uncover, open out, open; to display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूर्ण्वत्
व्य्-ऊर्ण्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. uncovering, dis-<BR>playing, revealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूह्
व्यूह् व्य्-ऊह् (वि-ऊह्, see rt. 1. ऊह्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-ऊहति, -ऊहितुम्, to push or move apart, place<BR>asunder, separate, divide, distribute; to separate,<BR>resolve (vowels, syllables, &c. in Vedic grammar);<BR>to dispose, arrange, place in order; to array, to place<BR>in battle-array, arrange in order of battle; to move<BR>from the proper place, change the position, trans-<BR>pose, alter, disarrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढ|व्यूढः
2. व्य्-ऊढ, अस्, आ, अम्, placed or moved apart,<BR>widely separated, expanded, developed, wide, broad;<BR>large, great, firm, compact; placed in order or array,<BR>arrayed, marshalled, arranged; placed out of order,<BR>disarranged, transposed, altered.<BR>—व्यूढ-कङ्कट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has arranged or put on armour,<BR>equipped in mail, accoutred, mailed, armed.<BR>—व्यू-<BR>ढ-छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having the metres<BR>disarranged or out of order.<BR>—व्यूढोरस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, or व्यूढोरस्क (˚ढ-उर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>an expanded chest, broad-chested, (व्यूढ = विपुल,<BR>comm.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढि|व्यूढिः
व्य्-ऊढि, इस्, f. orderly arrangement or disposition,<BR>distribution in various positions, array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूह|व्यूहः
व्य्-ऊह, अस्, m. placing apart, separation, distribu-<BR>tion; separation or resolution (of vowels, syllables,<BR>&c. in Vedic grammar); orderly arrangement, dis-<BR>position, array (e. g. चरण-व्यूह, array of Vedic<BR>schools), military array, (various forms of array are<BR>enumerated in Manu VII. 187 and elsewhere, e. g.<BR>दण्ड, that like ‘a staff;’ शकट, ‘a cart;’ व-<BR>राह, ‘a boar;’ मकर, ‘a sea-monster;’ सूचि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">Page0983-b+ 75</a>]<BR>‘a needle;’ गरुड, ‘the bird of Viṣṇu;’ वज्र,<BR>‘a thunderbolt;’ भोग, ‘a snake,’ i. e. in column;<BR>मण्डल, ‘a circle;’ असंहत, ‘mixed order;’<BR>पताक, ‘a flag,’ &c.); an army, host, squadron; a<BR>flock, multitude; (in phil.) arrangement or peculiar<BR>distribution (of the senses); formation, structure, manu-<BR>facture; the body; reasoning, logic, (in this sense<BR>rather to be derived fr. rt. 2. ऊह् with वि); breathing<BR>(according to the Nyāya-sūtras III. 31).<BR>—व्यूह-<BR>पार्ष्णि, इस्, m. the rear of an army (= प्रत्य्-<BR>आसार).<BR>—व्यूह-भङ्ग or व्यूह-भेद, अस्, m.<BR>breaking an array, throwing into disorder.<BR>—व्यूह-<BR>रचना, f. arrangement of troops.<BR>—व्यूह-राज,<BR>अस्, m. the chief or best form of military array.<BR>—व्यूहान्तर (˚ह-अन्˚), अस्, m. a different ar-<BR>rangement or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहत्
व्य्-ऊहत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, separating, dividing; dis-<BR>posing, arranging, putting in military array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहन|व्यूहनं
व्य्-ऊहन, अम्, n. the act of disposing in order,<BR>arrangement, arraying, array (of an army); dispo-<BR>sition or structure of the members of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूह्य
व्य्-ऊह्य, ind. having disposed in order, having<BR>arranged or arrayed, having placed in battle-array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृ
व्यृ व्य्-ऋ (वि-ऋ), cl. 5. 3. P. -ऋणोति or -ऋण्-<BR>वति, -इयर्ति, &c. (see rt. 4. ऋ), Ved. to go apart or<BR>asunder, open out, be divided; to open, throw open,<BR>spread abroad, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृछ्
व्यृछ् व्य्-ऋछ् (वि-ऋछ्), cl. 6. P. -ऋच्छति,<BR>-अर्च्छितुम्, Ved. to go apart or asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृध्
व्यृध् व्य्-ऋध् (वि-ऋध्), Pass. -ऋध्यते,<BR>Ved. to be unfortunate or unsuccessful; to be ex-<BR>cluded or deprived of (with inst.): Caus. -अर्ध-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to exclude from, deprive of (with<BR>inst.): Pass. of Caus. -अर्ध्यते, to be excluded<BR>from or deprived of: Desid. वीर्त्सति (Part. वीर्त्सत्),<BR>to wish to nullify or render vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृद्ध
व्य्-ऋद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of prosperity,<BR>deprived of, separated or excluded from; nullified;<BR>imperfect, defective, unfit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृद्धि|व्यृद्धिः
व्य्-ऋद्धि, इस्, f. (probably fr. वि privative + ऋद्-<BR>धि), non-prosperity, absence or loss of prosperity,<BR>misfortune, ill luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृष्
व्यृष् 1. व्य्-ऋष् (वि-ऋष्), cl. 1. P. -अर्षति,<BR>-अर्षितुम्, Ved. to flow through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृष्
व्यृष् 2. व्य्-ऋष् (वि-ऋष्), cl. 6. P. -ऋषति,<BR>-अर्षितुम्, to pierce, penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ये
व्ये व्ये (perhaps formed out of वि-इ, see<BR>3. वी), cl. 1. P. A. व्ययति, -ते, विव्याय (2nd<BR>sing. विव्ययिथ, Pāṇ. VII. 2, 66), विव्ये, व्यास्यति, -ते,<BR>अव्यासीत्, अव्यास्त, व्यातुम्, to cover, conceal, clothe:<BR>Caus. व्याययति: Desid. विव्यासति, -ते: Intens. वे-<BR>वीयते, वाव्येति or वाव्याति; [cf. Gr. ἱ in ἱμάτιον.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीत|वीतं|वीतः
3. वीत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. and 2. वीत see p. 953,<BR>col. 2), covered, clothed, put on, worn.<BR>—वीत-सू-<BR>त्र, अम्, n. the sacred thread or cord; [cf. नि-वीत,<BR>उप-वीत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्येत
व्येत व्य्-एत, अस्, -एनी, अम्, Ved. very bright,<BR>very white, (Sāy. व्येनी = विशेषेण श्वेता, Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 80, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्येनस्
व्येनस् व्य्-एनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. exempt<BR>from sin, free from misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योकार|व्योकारः
व्योकार व्यो-कार, अस्, m. (probably onoma-<BR>topoetic), ‘making the sound व्यो,’ a blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमन्
व्योमन् व्योमन्, अ, n. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. IV. 150. fr. rt. व्ये above; according to others<BR>fr. ओ for अव् with वि, cf. ओमन्, or connected<BR>with rt. 2. दिव्), sky, heaven, atmosphere, ether;<BR>water; a temple sacred to the sun, a place where<BR>the sun is especially worshipped; talc, mica; (आ),<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—व्योम-केश, अस्, or व्योम-<BR>केशिन्, ई, m. ‘sky-haired,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—व्यो-<BR>म-गङ्गा, f. the heavenly Ganges.<BR>—व्योम-चर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘sky-going,’ passing through the air.<BR>—व्योम-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, sky-going; (ई), m. ‘air-<BR>goer,’ ‘sky-goer;’ a god; a bird; a saint; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">Page0983-c+ 79</a>]<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—व्योमचारि-पुर, अम्, n. ‘sky-floating<BR>city,’ the city of Hari-ścandra (supposed to be sus-<BR>pended between heaven and earth).<BR>—व्योम-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of Śiva<BR>—व्योम-धूम, अस्, m. ‘sky-smoke,’<BR>a cloud.<BR>—व्योम-नासिका, f. a sort of quail.<BR>—व्योम-<BR>पञ्चक, अम्, n. an aggregate of five Vyomans (?) .<BR>—व्योम-मञ्जर, अम्, n. ‘sky-cluster,’ a flag,<BR>banner.<BR>—व्योम-मण्डल, अम्, n. ‘sky-circle,’ a<BR>flag, banner.<BR>—व्योम-मध्ये, ind. in the middle<BR>of the sky, in mid-air.<BR>—व्योम-माय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘sky-measuring,’ reaching to the sky, high as the<BR>heaven.<BR>—व्योम-मुद्गर, अस्, m. ‘sky-hammer,’<BR>a gust of wind.<BR>—व्योम-यान, अम्, n. ‘sky-vehicle,’<BR>a celestial car, chariot of the gods.<BR>—व्योम-वर्त्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. the path of the sky, (व्योम-वर्त्मना,<BR>inst. c. through the air or sky.)<BR>—व्योम-विस्तृत,<BR>अम्, n. the expanse of heaven, the sky, firmament.<BR>—व्योम-सद्, त्, m. ‘sky-dweller,’ a deity, divinity;<BR>a Gandharva; a spirit.<BR>—व्योम-स्थली, f. ‘ground<BR>or base of the sky,’ the earth.<BR>—व्योम-स्पृश्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, ‘sky-touching,’ ‘sky-reaching,’ lofty.<BR>—व्योमाभ<BR>(˚म-आभ), अस्, m. ‘heaven-like,’ a Buddha or a<BR>Jaina deified saint.<BR>—व्योमोदक (˚म-उद्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘sky-water,’ rain-water, dew (= दिव्योदक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योम्निक
व्योम्निक in परम-व्योम्निक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to the highest ether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योष|व्योषं
व्योष व्योष, अम्, n. (probably fr. rt. 1.<BR>व्युष् or fr. rt. 1. उष् with वि), the aggregate of three<BR>spices (black pepper, long pepper, and dry ginger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्
व्रज् व्रज्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) -व्र-<BR>जति (-ते), वव्राज, व्रजिष्यति, अव्राजीत्,<BR>व्रजितुम्, to go, proceed, travel; to go away, de-<BR>part, retire, withdraw; to pass away (as time); to<BR>go to, approach, visit, approach a woman (for adul-<BR>tery); to undergo; to go to any state or condition,<BR>attain to, become (with acc., especially with acc. of<BR>abstract noun, e. g. विनाशं व्रज्, to go to destruc-<BR>tion, become destroyed; छात्त्रतां व्रज्, to be-<BR>come a pupil; निर्वृतिं व्रज्, to grow happy; cf.<BR>rt. 1. या); to obtain, gain, (व्यापारं व्रज्, to<BR>obtain possession of anything, loc.): Caus. or cl. 10.<BR>P. व्राजयति, -यितुम्, to cause to go, send; to go;<BR>to prepare, decorate: Desid. विव्रजिषति: Intens.<BR>वाव्रज्यते, वाव्रक्ति, to go crookedly; [cf. Gr.<BR>ϝέργον; Goth. vrikan, vrakja, waurkjau; Angl.<BR>Sax. wrecan; Old Germ. rehhan, wreh.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज|व्रजं|व्रजः
व्रज, अस्, m. a road; a flock, herd, multitude,<BR>collection of anything; a station of cowherds, cow-<BR>pen, cattle-shed, stall, stable; a resting-place, abode;<BR>a cloud (= मेघ according to Naigh. I. 10); N.<BR>of the district surrounding Agra and Mathurā (the<BR>scene of Kṛṣṇa's juvenile adventures; it is com-<BR>monly called Braj, cf. वृजि); N. of a son of Havir-<BR>dhāna; (अम्), n. going, wandering, roaming; [cf.<BR>perhaps Lat. vulgus.]<BR>—व्रज-किशोर, अस्, m. ‘youth<BR>of Vraja,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—व्रज-नाथ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of Vraja,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—व्रज-<BR>भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, being or produced in Vraja; (ऊस्),<BR>m. the tree Nauclea Cordifolia, = केलि-कदम्ब;<BR>(ऊस्), f. the district of Vraja.<BR>—व्रज-मण्डल, अम्,<BR>n. the district of Vraja.<BR>—व्रज-मोहन, अस्, m.<BR>‘the fascinator of Vraja,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—व्र-<BR>ज-लाल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—व्रज-वर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘best in Vraja,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—व्रज-वल्-<BR>लभ, अस्, m. ‘beloved in Vraja,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—व्रजाङ्गना (˚ज-अङ्˚), f. ‘woman of Vraja,’ a<BR>Gopī, cowherdess, shepherdess.<BR>—व्रजाजिर (˚ज-<BR>अज्˚), अम्, n. a cow-yard, cattle-fold, cow-pen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजक|व्रजकः
व्रजक, अस्, m. a religious ascetic who wanders<BR>about (in quest of alms &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजत्
व्रजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going, proceeding, travel-<BR>ling; roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजन|व्रजनं
व्रजन, अम्, n. the act of going or proceeding,<BR>travelling, roaming; exile; a road, way, street (Ved.);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a brother of Jahnu (considered as<BR>one of the ancestors of the Kuśikas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजित
व्रजित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, proceeded; (अम्), n.<BR>going, roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजिन्
व्रजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. herded or grouped together,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">Page0984-a+ 79</a>]<BR>collected into a mass, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 45, 1. व्रजिनीः = तमः-पुञ्जवतीः, clustered<BR>gloom, i. e. nights.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्या
व्रज्या, f. travelling or wandering about (either<BR>as a religious act or in quest of alms); march,<BR>attack, invasion; a flock, tribe, class; a theatre (=<BR>रङ्ग).<BR>—व्रज्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, wandering,<BR>roaming; going gracefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण्
व्रण् 1. व्रण् (also written ब्रण्), cl. 1. P.<BR>व्रणति, वव्राण, व्रणितुम्, to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण्
व्रण् 2. व्रण् (perhaps rather to be re-<BR>garded as a Nom. fr. व्रण below), cl.<BR>10. P. व्रणयति, -यितुम्, to wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण|व्रणं|व्रणः
व्रण, अस्, अम्, m. n. a wound, sore, ulcer, boil,<BR>bruise, tumor; a fracture, scar, rent (see अ-व्˚, cf. Manu<BR>II. 47); [cf. Gr. οὐλή (i. e. ϝολνη), ἄπ-ελος; Lat.<BR>vulnus.]<BR>—व्रण-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, making a sore,<BR>wounding, ulcerating; corroding; (त्), m. the mark-<BR>ing-nut plant, Semecarpus Anacardium.<BR>—व्रण-<BR>केतु-घ्नी, f. a kind of small shrub (= दुग्ध-<BR>फेनी).<BR>—व्रण-द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, ‘hostile to sores,’<BR>healing sores; (ट्), m. the plant Siphonanthus Indica<BR>(= ब्राह्मण-यष्टिका).<BR>—व्रण-धूपन, अम्,<BR>n. fumigating a sore.<BR>—व्रण-वस्तु, n. a part liable<BR>to ulcerate (as skin, flesh, &c.).<BR>—व्रण-वेदना, f.<BR>the pain of a wound or sore.<BR>—व्रण-शोधन,<BR>अम्, n. the cleansing or cicatrising of a sore.<BR>—व्र-<BR>ण-ह, अस्, m. ‘destroying sores,’ the castor-oil tree;<BR>(आ), f. a sort of creeper or shrub (= गुडूची).<BR>—व्र-<BR>ण-हृत्, त्, m. ‘sore-removing,’ a particular plant (=<BR>कलि-कारी).<BR>—व्रणारि (˚ण-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy<BR>of sores,’ the plant Sesbana Grandiflora (= अगस्त्य-<BR>वृक्ष); gum-myrrh (= वोल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणित
व्रणित, अस्, आ, अम्, wounded, ulcerated, bruised,<BR>scarred.<BR>—व्रणित-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, heart-<BR>stricken, bruised or wounded at heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणिन्
व्रणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a sore or wound, afflicted<BR>with boils or ulcers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रत|व्रतं|व्रतः
व्रत व्रत, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably an old<BR>past pass. participle fr. rt. वृ), anything enclosed, an<BR>enclosed place, enclosure, realm, sphere, sway (Ved.);<BR>anything fenced off or settled, a law, ordinance, com-<BR>mand, rule, (अनु-व्रतम्, according to law or ordi-<BR>nance); rite, observance, practice [cf. अर्क-व्˚,<BR>यम-व्˚]; any religious act or obligation enjoined<BR>by the gods; a sacrifice; a self-chosen or voluntary<BR>act, any meritorious act of devotion or austerity,<BR>fasting, continence, vowed observance, solemn pur-<BR>pose, vow, (असि-धारा-व्रत or आसिधारं व्र-<BR>तम्, a vow to stand on the edge of a sword or a<BR>vow as difficult as standing on the edge of a sword);<BR>action, agency, doing, work, deed; a design, plan;<BR>eating, in पयो-व्रत, q. v.; [cf. probably Gr.<BR>ἑορτή.]<BR>—व्रत-कल्पद्रुम, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work by Ratnākara.<BR>—व्रत-चर्या, f. the practice of<BR>religious vows; (अस्), m. a religious student.<BR>—व्रत-<BR>चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. vow-performing, fulfilling or<BR>performing vows.<BR>—व्रत-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>part of the Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—व्रत-निमित्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, caused by a vow.<BR>—व्रत-पति, इस्, m., Ved.<BR>‘lord of vows,’ epithet of Agni.<BR>—व्रत-पा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, Ved. upholding ordinances, protecting sacred<BR>rites.<BR>—व्रत-पारण, अम्, आ, n. f. conclusion of<BR>a fast, eating or drinking after a fast.<BR>—व्रत-प्र-<BR>काश, अस्, m. ‘illustration of vows,’ N. of a work by<BR>Viśva-nātha on the subject of vows (compiled from<BR>the Purāṇas and other more ancient sources).<BR>—व्र-<BR>त-प्रतिष्ठा, f. the performance of a religious act<BR>voluntarily undertaken.<BR>—व्रत-भङ्ग, अस्, m. the<BR>interruption of an act of devotion, breach of a vow.<BR>—व्रत-भिक्षा, f. soliciting alms (as one of the<BR>ceremonies accompanying investiture).<BR>—व्रत-भृत्,<BR>त्, m., Ved. ‘bearer of sacrifices,’ epithet of Agni.<BR>—व्रत-राज, अस्, m. = व्रत-प्रकाश above.<BR>—व्रत-लुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has broken a<BR>vow (of fasting &c.).<BR>—व्रत-लोपन, अम्, n. the<BR>breaking of a vow (of fasting, chastity, &c.), violat-<BR>ing any religious vow or obligation.<BR>—व्रत-वै-<BR>कल्य, अम्, n. imperfection or incompletion of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">Page0984-b+ 76</a>]<BR>vow or religious observance.<BR>—व्रत-शेष, अस्, m.<BR>the remainder of a religious vow.<BR>—व्रत-संर-<BR>क्षण, अम्, n. the keeping of a vow, observing<BR>penance.<BR>—व्रत-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. undertaking any<BR>act of devotion, taking on one's self any voluntary<BR>religious obligation (= दीक्षा).<BR>—व्रत-स्थ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, engaged in religious austerities or in a vow<BR>of any kind, performing penance.<BR>—व्रत-स्नातक,<BR>अस्, m. a Brāhman who has completed his term of<BR>studentship, (see स्नातक.)<BR>—व्रताचरण (˚त-<BR>आच्˚), अम्, n. the act of observing a vow or religious<BR>obligation (especially that of continence, as the duty<BR>of a religious student; cf. ब्रह्म-चर्य).<BR>—व्र-<BR>तादान (˚त-आद्˚), अम्, n. undertaking the obliga-<BR>tions of a devotee.<BR>—व्रतादेश (˚त-आद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>investiture of a youth of one of the first three classes<BR>with the sacred cord.<BR>—व्रतोपवास (˚त-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. fasting as a religious obligation, a fast.<BR>—व्रतोपा-<BR>यन (˚त-उप्˚), अम्, n. = वायन, presents of cakes<BR>&c. which may be eaten during a religious feast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतय
व्रतय, Nom. P. व्रतयति, -यितुम्, to observe<BR>a vow; to fast or practise any abstinence in conse-<BR>quence of a vow; to eat together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिक
व्रतिक in वक-व्रतिक, वैडाल-व्˚, &c.,<BR>q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिन्
व्रतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, observing a vow (of continence,<BR>fasting, &c.), relating to a vow, practising any penance<BR>or religious observance, engaged in a sacrifice, devout,<BR>pious; (ई), m. an ascetic, devotee; a religious student;<BR>one who institutes a sacrifice and employs priests (=<BR>यजमान); N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतेयु
व्रतेयु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रत्य
व्रत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = व्रतिन् (Ṛg-v. VIII. 48, 8).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतति|व्रततिः
व्रतति व्रतति, इस्, f. (said to be fr. rt. 1. वृत्,<BR>according to Yāska fr. rts. वृ and 3. तन्), expansion,<BR>extension, spreading; a creeper.<BR>—व्रतति-वलय,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a creeper winding round like a bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतती
व्रतती, f. = व्रतति above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रध्न
व्रध्न व्रध्न, अस्, m. (also written ब्रध्न,<BR>q. v.), the sun; the root of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रन्द्
व्रन्द् व्रन्द् or व्रद् (a Vedic root said<BR>to be allied to rts. म्रद् and 1. मृड्,<BR>‘to rub, press, crush,’ &c.), cl. 1. P. A. व्रन्दति,<BR>-ते, &c., (probably) to soften; to become soft, (अव्र-<BR>दन्त वीलितेत्य् अपि निगमो भवति, Nirukta V.<BR>16); [cf. Gr. βραδύ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रन्दिन्
व्रन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. reduced to a state of<BR>softness or mildness; tamed, subdued, (or according<BR>to Sāy. connected with वृन्द, ‘a multitude;’ व्रन्-<BR>दिनः = मृदु-भावं प्राप्तान् or समूह-व-<BR>तः, Ṛg-veda I. 54, 4; see Nirukta V. 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रयस्
व्रयस् व्रयस्. See under rt. व्री, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्च्
व्रश्च् व्रश्च्, cl. 6. P. वृश्चति (Ved. वृ-<BR>णक्ति, Naigh. II. 19), वव्रश्च, व्र-<BR>श्चिष्यति or व्रक्ष्यति, अव्रश्चीत् or अव्राक्षीत्,<BR>व्रश्चितुम् or व्रष्टुम्, to cut, cut up, cut asunder,<BR>tear, lacerate, divide with an edged tool; to wound:<BR>Caus. व्रश्चयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अविव्रश्चत्: Desid.<BR>विव्रश्चिषति and विव्रक्षति: Intens. वरीवृ-<BR>श्च्यते, वरीवृश्चीति; [cf. Gr. ἔλκος, ῥάκος, λακίς,<BR>λακερός; Lat. lacerare, ulcus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ण|वृक्णं
वृक्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, torn, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चत्
वृश्चत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, cutting, lacerating,<BR>wounding.<BR>—वृश्चद्-वन, अस्, m., Ved. ‘consumer<BR>or destroyer of forests,’ epithet of Agni (Ṛg-v. VI. 6, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चन|व्रश्चनं|व्रश्चनः
व्रश्चन, अस्, ई, अम्, who or what cuts, cutting;<BR>(अस्), m. a small saw or chisel; a fine file or saw<BR>used by goldsmiths, &c.; the juice flowing from an<BR>incision in a tree; (अम्), n. cutting, wounding; a<BR>cut, incision.<BR>—व्रश्चन-प्रभव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>flowing from an incision (in a tree, as juices &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रह्मन्
व्रह्मन् व्रह्मन्, अ, n. = ब्रह्मन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रा
व्रा व्रा, f. (fr. rt. वृ), Ved. night; dawn,<BR>(Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 121, 2 = तमसा सर्वम्<BR>आच्छादयतीति व्रा रात्रिः or प्रकाशेन वृणोतीति<BR>व्रा उषाः); a multitude, troop, (see Nirukta V. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राचड
व्राचड व्राचड, अस्, m. a kind of corrupt<BR>dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राज|व्राजः
व्राज व्राज, अस्, m. (fr. rt. व्रज्), going,<BR>movement, motion; a troop, multitude (Ved.).<BR>—व्राज-बाहू, m. du., Ved. the spreading or out-<BR>stretched arms of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजि|व्राजिः
व्राजि, इस्, f. a gale of wind, whirlwind, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात|व्रातः
व्रात व्रात, अस्, m. (fr. व्रत or connected<BR>with rt. वृ), a multitude, flock, assemblage, troop,<BR>(व्रातं-व्रातम्, in companies, in troops, Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 53, 11); = मनुष्य (according to Naigh. II.<BR>3); the descendant of an outcast Brāhman, &c., (see<BR>व्रात्य); the company or attendants at a marriage<BR>feast; (अम्), n. manual or bodily labour; day labour,<BR>casual employment.<BR>—व्रात-जीवन, अम्, n. living<BR>by manual or bodily labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातीन|व्रातीनः
व्रातीन, अस्, m. one living by the profession of a<BR>Vrāta, a hired labourer, porter, cooly; one having no<BR>fixed employment; one living by violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्य|व्रात्यः
व्रात्य, अस्, m. a Brāhman or man of one of the<BR>first three classes who has lost caste through non-<BR>observance of the ten principal Saṃskāras (especially<BR>investiture with the thread; in the Atharva-veda XV.<BR>8, 1, XV. 9, 1. the Rājanyas and even the Brāhmans<BR>are said to have sprung from the Vrātya who is<BR>even identified with the Supreme Being); an out-<BR>cast; a man of a particular inferior class (regarded as<BR>the descendant of a Śūdra father and Kṣatriya<BR>mother; cf. वैद्य); a low or vile person; (आ), f.<BR>the daughter of an outcast, a female of a fallen<BR>Brāhman, &c.<BR>—व्रात्य-ता, f. or व्रात्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the condition of one who has lost caste by neglect<BR>of the Saṃskāras or sacred observances (such as investi-<BR>ture with the thread, &c.).<BR>—व्रात्य-ब्रुव, अस्, m.<BR>one who calls himself a Vrātya; [cf. ब्राह्मण-<BR>ब्रुव.]<BR>—व्रात्य-भाव, अस्, m. = व्रात्य-ता.<BR>—व्रा-<BR>त्य-याजक, अस्, m. one who sacrifices for a Vrātya.<BR>—व्रात्य-स्तोम, अस्, m. a particular sacrifice per-<BR>formed to recover the rights forfeited by a delay of<BR>the Saṃskāras (especially of investiture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राधत्
व्राधत् व्राधत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (probably a<BR>kind of pres. part. connected with rt. 1. वृध्), Ved.<BR>great, mighty, (Sāy. = महत्, Ṛg-veda IV. 32, 3;<BR>cf. Gr. βλωθ-ρός.)<BR>—व्राधन्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>greatest, most eminent, (Sāy. = प्रवृद्ध-तम,<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 150, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रिश्
व्रिश् व्रिश्, शस्, f. pl., Ved. the fingers<BR>(according to Naigh. II. 5; according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 144, 5. व्रिशः = विशः = परस्पर-<BR>विश्लिष्टाः, mutually separated).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री व्री (connected with rts. वृ, व्ली),<BR>cl. 9. P. व्रीणाति or व्रिणाति, विव्राय,<BR>व्रेष्यति, अव्रैषीत्, व्रेतुम्, to choose, elect; cl.<BR>4. A. व्रीयते, विव्रिये, व्रेष्यते, अव्रेष्ट, व्रे-<BR>तुम्, to choose (?); to be chosen or elected; to<BR>cover, screen: Caus. व्राययति (or according to<BR>others व्रेपयति), -यितुम्: Desid. विव्रीषति, -ते:<BR>Intens. वेव्रीयते, वेव्रयीति, वेव्रेति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रयस्
व्रयस्, Ved. abandoning, abandonment, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda II. 23, 16. वि व्रयस् =<BR>विशेषेण वर्जनम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीण
व्रीण, अस्, आ, अम्, chosen, elected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड्
व्रीड् व्रीड्, cl. 4. P. व्रीड्यति (ep. cl. 1. A.<BR>व्रीडते, see below), विव्रीड, व्रीडिष्-<BR>यति, अव्रीडीत्, व्रीडितुम्, to be ashamed, feel shame,<BR>to be modest or bashful; to throw, hurl, send; (ac-<BR>cording to Nirukta V. 16. व्रीडयति = वीडयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड|व्रीडः
व्रीड, अस्, आ, m. f. shame, modesty, bashfulness.<BR>—व्रीडानत (˚डा-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bowed down<BR>with shame, hanging down the head with shame,<BR>ashamed.<BR>—व्रीडान्वित (˚डा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ashamed, bashful, modest.<BR>—व्रीडा-युज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>possessing shame, ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडन|व्रीडनं
व्रीडन, अम्, n. shame, bashfulness, modesty;<BR>lowering, depression (= नीचैर्-भाव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडमान
व्रीडमान, अस्, आ, अम् (an epic form), being<BR>ashamed, blushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडित
व्रीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, ashamed, abashed, modest;<BR>(अम्), n. shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीळन
व्रीऌअन, अम्, n., Ved. = व्रीडन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस्
व्रीस् व्रीस् (= rt. व्रूस्), cl. 1. 10. P. व्री-<BR>सति, व्रीसयति, to hurt, injure; to kill,<BR>wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहि|व्रीहिः
व्रीहि व्रीहि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. व्री),<BR>rice, (eight principal sorts are enumerated by native<BR>authorities; rice is not mentioned in the Ṛg-veda,<BR>but is named in the Atharva-veda together with<BR>यव, माष, and तिल); a grain of rice, (व्रीहीन्<BR>प्रोक्षति, he sprinkles or scatters grains of rice);<BR>rice ripening in the rainy season; (अयस्), m. pl.<BR>grains of rice.<BR>—व्रीहि-काञ्चन, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>pulse, Ervum Lens or Hirsutum (= मशूर).<BR>—व्री-<BR>हि-पर्णी, f. a particular shrub (= शाल-पर्णी).<BR>—व्रीहि-भेद, अस्, m. a species of rice; a sort of<BR>grain, Panicum Miliaceum (= अणु).<BR>—व्रीहि-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, made or consisting of rice; (अस्), m. a<BR>rice-cake made with ghee (offered as an oblation).<BR>—व्रीहि-राजिक, अस्, m. panic seed, Panicum Itali-<BR>cum (= कङ्गु); another species, Panicum Milia-<BR>ceum.<BR>—व्रीहि-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. a kind of rice (=<BR>शालि-धान्य).<BR>—व्रीह्य्-अगार, अम्, n. ‘rice-house,’ a<BR>shed where rice or other grain is stored, granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिक|व्रीहिकः
व्रीहिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having rice, bearing rice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिन्
व्रीहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having or bearing rice (a field &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैह|व्रैहः
व्रैह, अस्, ई, अम्, made of rice, composed of<BR>rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय, अस्, ई, अम्, fit for rice, sown with rice<BR>(as a field &c.), made or consisting of rice; (अम्),<BR>n. a field of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड्
व्रुड् व्रुड्, cl. 6. P. व्रुडति, to cover; to<BR>heap; to sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस्
व्रूस् व्रूस् (also written व्रूष् or ब्रूष्;<BR>cf. rts. व्रीस्, कष्), cl. 1. 10. P. व्रूसति,<BR>व्रूसयति, &c., to hurt, injure, wound, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली व्ली (also written ब्ली; according to<BR>some fr. वि-ली, but cf. rt. व्री), cl. 9. P. व्लि-<BR>नाति (Ved. व्लीनाति^1), विव्लाय, व्लेष्यति, अव्लैषीत्,<BR>व्लेतुम्, to go, move; to choose, select, (in this sense<BR>for rts. वृ, व्री); to hold, maintain, support: Caus.<BR>व्लेपयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अविव्लिपत्: Desid. विव्ली-<BR>षति: Intens. वेव्लीयते, वेव्लयीति or वेव्लेति.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161213. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 316-318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लीन
व्लीन, अस्, आ, अम्, gone; held, supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेक्ष्
व्लेक्ष् व्लेक्ष् (also written वेक्ष्, q. v.),<BR>cl. 10. P. व्लेक्षयति, व्लेक्षापयति,<BR>यितुम्, to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श 1. श, the thirtieth consonant of the<BR>Nāgarī alphabet and first of the three sibilants; it<BR>belongs to the palatal class, and in sound often cor-<BR>responds to ष्, though in some words pronounced<BR>more like स्.<BR>—श-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound<BR>श.<BR>—श-वर्ग, अस्, m. the sibilating class of letters,<BR>i. e. the three sibilants and the letter ह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श 2. श, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शो), a cutter, de-<BR>stroyer (Kirāt. XV. 45); a weapon; N. of Śiva, (in<BR>this sense probably connected with 2. शम्); (अम्),<BR>n. or ind. happiness, &c., see 2. शम्, p. 993.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु शंयु, शंय्य, &c. See under 2. शम्,<BR>p. 993.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंर
शंर, शं-स्थ, &c. See p. 993, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवर|शंवरं
शंवर शंवर, शंवल. See शम्बर,<BR>शम्बल, p. 993.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्
शंस् शंस् [cf. rts. शश्, 1. शास्], cl. 1. P.<BR>शंसति (ep. also A. -ते), शशंस, शं-<BR>सिष्यति, अशंसीत्, Prec. शस्यात्, शंसितुम्, to recite,<BR>repeat, (in Vedic ritual शोंसाव, शोंसाम, ‘let us<BR>recite’); to relate, say, tell, report, declare, announce,<BR>communicate to (with dat. or gen. of the person);<BR>to praise, celebrate; to approve, wish, desire [cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">Page0985-b+ 80</a>]<BR>आ-शंस्]; to wish well or ill to; to calumniate, revile;<BR>to hurt, injure [cf. rt. 1. शस्]; to be unhappy (?):<BR>Pass. शस्यते, to be recited or uttered; to be<BR>praised or approved: Caus. शंसयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अशशंसत्, to cause to repeat or recite: Desid.<BR>शिशंसिषति: Intens. शाशस्यते, शाशंस्ति; [cf.<BR>Lat. censeo, cano, Cas-menœ, Ca-menœ, carmen,<BR>con-cinn-us: Old Germ. sagen: Angl. Sax. sagan,<BR>sœgan: Goth. hazjan, hana: Mod. Germ. Hahn:<BR>Slav. san-ti: (perhaps also) Lith. sakau: Hib.<BR>sant, ‘greediness, lust;’ santaighim, ‘I desire,<BR>covet.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस|शंसः
शंस, अस्, m., Ved. recitation, invocation; praise,<BR>prayer, (Sāy. = स्तुति); wishing well or ill to; a<BR>spell (for good or evil); a blessing; a curse;<BR>calumny; = नराशंस (Ved.); (आ), f. speech;<BR>praise, flattery, eulogium; wish, desire; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>reciting; praising; wishing; [cf. दुः-श्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसत्
शंसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, reciting, relating; praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसन|शंसनं
शंसन, अम्, n. the act of reciting or repeating,<BR>recitation; praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसित|शंसितः
शंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, said, told, declared; praised,<BR>extolled, celebrated; wished, desired, longed for [cf.<BR>आ-शंसित]; calumniated, falsely accused; ascertained,<BR>established, effected, (in these senses for सं-शित<BR>under सं-शो.)<BR>—शंसित-व्रत for संशित-व्रत,<BR>see सं-शो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसितृ
शंसितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a reciter, reciting, relating;<BR>a praiser; [cf. शंस्तृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिन्
शंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, saying, relating, announcing,<BR>foretelling, indicating, showing; praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तव्य
शंस्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be repeated or recited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तृ
शंस्तृ, ता, m. a reciter of Śastras or hymns of<BR>praise, one of the officiating priests at a sacrifice<BR>(identified with the Pra-śāstṛ and mentioned along<BR>with five others in Ṛg-veda 1. 162, 5; his sacrificial<BR>duties correspond with those of the Maitrāvaruṇa of<BR>the later ritual); a praiser, encomiast, panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्य|शंस्यः
शंस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, praiseworthy,<BR>meritorious; to be wished, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस् in उक्थ-शस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस
शस, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. reciting, repeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसित्वा
शसित्वा, ind. having praised, &c. (= शस्त्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
1. शस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. शस्त see under rt.<BR>1. शस्), recited, repeated; praised, eulogized; best,<BR>excellent; auspicious, happy, well, right; (अम्), n.<BR>happiness, excellence; the body.<BR>—शस्त-केशक,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, having excellent hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तव्य
शस्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be recited or repeated;<BR>to be praised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्ति|शस्तिः
शस्ति, इस्, f., Ved. a hymn of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्र|शस्त्रं|शस्त्रः
1. शस्त्र, अम्, n. (for 2. शस्त्र see under rt. 1. शस्),<BR>Ved. a hymn (recited either audibly or inaudibly, as<BR>opposed to स्तोम, which is sung), a recitative, recita-<BR>tion; a hymn of praise (generally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्वा
शस्त्वा, ind. having recited; having praised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्मन्
शस्मन्, अ, n., Ved. praise, a hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
1. शस्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. शस्य see under rt.<BR>1. शस्), = शंस्य, to be praised, praiseworthy; to be<BR>wished, desirable, excellent, best; (अम्), n. a good<BR>quality, merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यमान
शस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being recited, (op-<BR>posed to गीयमान, being sung); being hymned<BR>or praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्त्
शंस्त् शंस्त्, a Vedic root, = rt. 2. शस् or<BR>सस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् 1. शक्, cl. 5. P. शक्नोति, cl. 4. P. A.<BR>शक्यति, -ते (in the A. not to be dis-<BR>tinguished from the Pass., see below; Ved. forms,<BR>Impv. शग्धि, Pot. शकेयम्, शकेम), शशाक,<BR>शेके, शक्ष्यति, -ते, अशकत् (or if used in cl. 4. the<BR>following are said by some to be substituted, 2nd<BR>Fut. शकिष्यति, -ते, Aor. अशकीत् or असाकीत्, अश-<BR>किष्ट), शक्तुम् (शकितुम्, Ved. शक्तवे), to be<BR>able, to be able to effect, to be competent for<BR>(with inf., e. g. वीक्षितुं न शक्नोति, he is not<BR>able to look; मर्तुं न शक्यामि, I am not able<BR>to die; or even with part., e. g. पूरयन् न शक्-<BR>नोति, he is not able to fill); to be powerful; to<BR>bear, endure; to give, present (Ved.); to aid (Ved.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-c" target="_blank">Page0985-c+ 81</a>]<BR>to know (Ved.): Pass. शक्यते, Aor. अशाकि, to be<BR>able, be capable, be possible, be practicable (giving<BR>a passive sense to a following inf., e. g. तच् छेत्तुं<BR>शक्यते, that is able to be cut, that can be cut;<BR>तत् कर्तुं शक्यते, that can be done; न शक्-<BR>यन्ते त्यक्तुम्, they cannot be abandoned; some-<BR>times used with a participle, e. g. न शक्यते वार्-<BR>यमाणः, he cannot be restrained; or used imper-<BR>sonally, e. g. यदि त्वया शक्यते, if it can be done<BR>by thee): Caus. शाकयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशीशकत्:<BR>Intens. शाशक्यते, शाशकीति or शाशक्ति: Desid.<BR>शिक्षति, -ते [cf. शिक्ष्, s. v.], to wish to be able or<BR>to be able to effect; to learn; to give, bestow, enrich<BR>(Ved.); to aid, assist (Ved.); to instruct (Ved.):<BR>Caus. of Desid. शिक्षयति, -यितुम्, to teach, in-<BR>struct (with two acc., e. g. तं रण-शिक्षाम् अशि-<BR>क्षयत्, he instructed him in the art of war); [cf.<BR>Lat. queo (for quec-jo), ne-queo, conari: Old Norse<BR>hagr, ‘the right hand;’ hagna, ‘to be of service.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
2. शक्, क्, क्, क्, able, powerful (at the end of a<BR>comp., e. g. सर्व-शक्, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक, अस्, m., N. of a king (especially applied to<BR>Śāli-vāhana); an era, epoch (especially that of the<BR>monarch Śāli-vāhana, commencing seventy-eight<BR>years after the Christian; cf. शाक); N. of a country;<BR>of a particular tribe or race of people, (usually आस्, pl.;<BR>in the legends which relate the contests between<BR>Vasiṣṭha and Viśvā-mitra the Śakas are fabled to<BR>have been produced by the Cow of Vasiṣṭha, from<BR>her sweat, for the destruction of Viśvā-mitra's army;<BR>in Manu X. 44. they are mentioned together with<BR>the Pauṇḍrakas, Oḍras, Draviḍas, Kāmbojas, Javanas<BR>or Yavanas, Pāradas, Pahlavas, Cīnas, Kirātas, Da-<BR>radas, and Khaśas, who are all described by Kullūka<BR>as degraded tribes of Kṣatriyas, called after the dis-<BR>tricts in which they reside: according to the Viṣṇu-<BR>Purāṇa IV. 3. the great king Sagara made an effort<BR>to rid his kingdom of these tribes, who appear to<BR>have overrun the western districts of India; the Śakas<BR>who were not destroyed were deprived of their social<BR>position and were compelled to shave the fore part<BR>of their heads: they are sometimes regarded as the<BR>followers of Śaka or Śāli-vāhana, and probably to be<BR>identified with the Tartars or Scythians [Lat. Sacœ]<BR>who overran India before the Āryans, and were<BR>supposed to have been exterminated by the great<BR>Vikramāditya, king of Oujein and rival of Śāli-<BR>vāhana); (अम्), n., Ved. water (= उदक, Naigh. I.<BR>12; cf. शक-पूत, शक-मय, under शकन्).<BR>—शक-कर्तृ, ता, m. the founder or establisher of<BR>an era.<BR>—शक-देश, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR>—शक-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—शक-<BR>वृद्धि, इस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—शकाधिप-राज-<BR>धानी (˚क-अध्˚), f. the capital of the king of the<BR>Śakas, i. e. Ḍillī.<BR>—शकान्तक (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘destroyer of the Śakas,’ epithet of king Vikramā-<BR>ditya.<BR>—शकाब्द (˚क-अब्˚), अम्, n. a year of the<BR>Śaka era, (see above.)<BR>—शकारि (˚क-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of the Śakas,’ epithet of king Vikramāditya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकच
शकच, perhaps for शक-ज, ‘Scythian-born,’ in<BR>Rāja-taraṅgiṇī V. 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकित
शकित, अस्, आ, अम्, able, capable, (giving a passive<BR>sense to the inf., e. g. न शकितं छेत्तुम्, it<BR>could not be cut.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त|शक्तः
शक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, able, capable, competent (with<BR>inf. or with loc. in the sense of an inf., e. g. शक्तः<BR>परि-रक्षितुम् or शक्तः परि-रक्षणे, able to<BR>preserve); strong, mighty, powerful; one who has<BR>the power of giving, opulent, rich (Manu XI. 9);<BR>significant, expressive; speaking kindly or pleasantly<BR>(= प्रियं-वद); clever, diligent, attentive, in-<BR>tent.<BR>—शक्त-ता, f. or शक्त-त्व, अम्, n. ability,<BR>power, capacity.<BR>—शक्तार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a potential sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ति|शक्तिः
शक्ति, इस्, f. ability, power, capacity, capability,<BR>faculty, strength, energy, prowess; regal power (hav-<BR>ing three parts or constituent elements, viz. 1. प्र-<BR>भु-त्व, the majesty or pre-eminence of the king<BR>himself; 2. मन्त्र, the power of good counsel;<BR>3. उत्साह, the force of energy); the energy or<BR>active power of a deity personified as his wife and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-a" target="_blank">Page0986-a+ 81</a>]<BR>worshipped under various names, (sometimes only<BR>eight Śakti goddesses are enumerated, as follow, In-<BR>drāṇī, Vaiṣṇavī, Śāntā, Brahmāṇī, Kaumārī, Nāra-<BR>siṃhī, Vārāhī, and Māheśvarī, but some substitute<BR>Cāmuṇḍā and Caṇḍikā for the third and sixth of<BR>these: according to another reckoning there are nine,<BR>viz. Vaiṣṇavī, Brahmāṇī, Raudrī, Māheśvarī, Nāra-<BR>siṃhī, Vārāhī, Indrāṇī, Kārttikī, and Pradhānā: others<BR>reckon fifty different forms of the Śakti of Viṣṇu<BR>besides Lakṣmī, some of these are Kīrtti, Kānti,<BR>Tuṣṭi, Puṣṭā, Dhṛti, Śānti, Kriyā, Dayā, Medhā,<BR>&c.; and fifty forms of the Śakti of Śiva or Rudra<BR>besides Durgā or Gaurī, some of whom are Guṇo-<BR>darī, Virajā, Śālmalī, Lolākṣī, Vartulākṣī, Dīrgha-<BR>ghoṇā, Sudīrgha-mukhī, Go-mukhī, Dīrgha-jihvā,<BR>Kuṇḍodarī, Ardha-keśī, Vikṛta-mukhī, Jvālā-mukhī,<BR>Ulkā-mukhī, &c.; Sarasvatī is also named as a Śakti,<BR>both of Viṣṇu and Rudra: according to the Vāyu-<BR>Purāṇa the female nature of Rudra became twofold,<BR>one half असित or white, and the other सित or black,<BR>each of these again becoming manifold, those of the<BR>white or mild nature included Lakṣmī, Sarasvatī,<BR>Gaurī, Umā, &c.; those of the dark and fierce nature,<BR>Durgā, Kālī, &c.); the female organ (as the counter-<BR>part of the phallic representation of Śiva, and wor-<BR>shipped either literally or figuratively by a sect of<BR>Hindūs termed Śāktas, see शाक्त); the power or<BR>signification (of a word), force or meaning of a term<BR>(defined in the Nyāya as the relation of the term to<BR>the thing designated पदस्य पदार्थे सम्बन्-<BR>धः); an iron spear, lance, pike, dart [cf. शाक्-<BR>तीक]; a sword; a kind of implement or instrument<BR>used in gambling; allaying or appeasing opposition;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a Muni or sage (the eldest of Va-<BR>siṣṭha's hundred sons; according to Viṣṇu-Purāṇa<BR>I. 1. he was father of Parāśara, and was devoured by<BR>king Kalmāṣa-pāda, when changed to a man-eating<BR>Rākṣasa, in consequence of a curse pronounced upon<BR>him by the sage; he is represented as having over-<BR>come the power and speech of Viśvā-mitra at the<BR>sacrifice of king Saudāsa, and is regarded as the Ṛṣi<BR>of Ṛg-veda VII. 32, 26, IX. 97, 19 — 21, IX. 108,<BR>3, 14 — 16; Śakti is also identified with one of the<BR>Vyāsas, and elsewhere with the sage Jātūkarṇa).<BR>—शक्ति-कुण्ठन, अम्, n. (in phil.) the deadening<BR>of a capacity.<BR>—शक्ति-कुमार, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>poet.<BR>—शक्ति-गण, अस्, m. the company or assem-<BR>blage of the Śaktis, (see under शक्ति above.)<BR>—शक्ति-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, taking hold of the force or mean-<BR>ing (of a word or sentence); apprehending the<BR>meaning (in any particular sense), acceptation (of a<BR>word &c.); holding or bearing a spear or lance,<BR>armed with a spear; (अस्), m. perception or appre-<BR>hension of the force or sense (of a word); a spear-<BR>man, lancer; epithet of Śiva; of Kārttikeya.<BR>—शक्ति-<BR>ग्राहक, अस्, इका, अम्, who or what causes to ap-<BR>prehend the force or signification (of a word or<BR>phrase), determining or establishing the meaning of<BR>words (as a dictionary, grammar, &c.); taking hold<BR>of the force (of a word &c.); holding a spear, &c.<BR>—शक्ति-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born from Śakti; (अस्), m.<BR>son of Śakti.<BR>—शक्ति-तस्, ind. according to power,<BR>to the best of one's ability.<BR>—शक्ति-ता, f. power,<BR>capacity, faculty.<BR>—शक्ति-त्रय, अम्, n. the three<BR>constituents of regal power (viz. king, minister, and<BR>energy; see शक्ति).<BR>—शक्ति-धर, अस्, m. a spear-<BR>man, lancer; epithet of Kārttikeya.<BR>—शक्ति-धृक्<BR>(see धृक्, p. 459), bearing a spear.<BR>—शक्ति-पर्ण,<BR>अस्, m. the tree Echites Scholaris (= सप्त-पर्ण).<BR>—शक्ति-पाणि, इस्, m. ‘spear-handed,’ armed with a<BR>spear or lance, a spearman; epithet of Kārttikeya.<BR>—शक्ति-पात, अस्, m. prostration of strength.<BR>—शक्-<BR>ति-पूजक, अस्, m. a Śakti-worshipper, a Śākta, (see<BR>शक्ति, शाक्त.)<BR>—शक्ति-पूजा, f. Śakti-worship, (see<BR>above.)<BR>—शक्ति-पूर्व, अस्, m. ‘having Śakti for a<BR>forefather,’ epithet of Parāśara (as son of Śakti).<BR>—शक्ति-प्रकर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing superior<BR>capacity or extraordinary power.<BR>—शक्ति-भृत्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, bearing a spear, armed with a spear; (त्), m. a<BR>spearman, lancer; epithet of Kārttikeya.<BR>—शक्ति-<BR>भेद, अस्, m. difference of power; a special capacity.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">Page0986-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—शक्ति-भैरव-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra<BR>work.<BR>—शक्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of ability,<BR>powerful, mighty, able; possessing a competence,<BR>one who has gained a fortune.<BR>—शक्ति-यामल, N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—शक्ति-रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘jewel-mine of Śakti,’ N. of a work on the mystical<BR>worship of Śakti or Durgā, (it contains five chapters<BR>compiled from the Tantras and Purāṇas.)<BR>—शक्ति-<BR>वाद or शक्ति-विचार, अस्, m., N. of a philosophical<BR>work by Gadādhara-bhaṭṭācārya.<BR>—शक्ति-वादिन्, ई,<BR>m. one who asserts or believes in Śakti-worship.<BR>—शक्ति-वैकल्य, अम्, n. deficiency of power,<BR>impairment of strength, incapacity, debility.<BR>—शक्ति-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, powerless, impotent.<BR>—शक्ति-हे-<BR>तिक, अस्, m. one who has a spear for a weapon, a<BR>spearman, lancer, soldier armed with a lance.<BR>—शक्-<BR>त्य्-अपेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having regard or reference<BR>to ability, according to power or capacity.<BR>—शक्त्य्-<BR>अर्ध, अस्, m. perspiring and panting with exertion<BR>or fatigue, (according to Śabda-k. = श्रम-द्वारा<BR>कुक्षि-ललाट-ग्रीवासूत्पन्नो घर्मो दीर्घ-नि-<BR>श्वासश्-च.)<BR>—शक्त्य्-अवर, अस्, आ, अम्, junior to<BR>Śakti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ती
शक्ती, f. = शक्ति, see Vopa-deva IV. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त्रि|शक्त्रिः
शक्त्रि, इस्, m., N. of the eldest of the hundred<BR>sons of Vasiṣṭha (= शक्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त्रिन्
शक्त्रिन्, ई, m. a proper N., = शक्त्रि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्न|शक्नः
शक्न, अस्, आ, अम्, = शक्नु below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्नु|शक्नुः
शक्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, speaking kindly or pleasingly;<BR>[cf. rt. शच्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्नुवान
शक्नुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, having power, being able,<BR>(तत् सोढुम् अ-शक्नुवानः, not being able to bear<BR>that.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्मन्
शक्मन्, अ, n., Ved. power, strength; energy,<BR>action; (आ), m., Ved., N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्य|शक्यः
शक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, able, possible, capable, prac-<BR>ticable, able to be effected or done, easy to be ac-<BR>complished (frequently with inf. in passive sense,<BR>e. g. न सा शक्या नेतुम् बलात्, she cannot be con-<BR>ducted by force; तन् मया शक्यम् प्रतिपत्तुम्,<BR>that is able to be acquired by me); that may be<BR>conveyed or expressed (as sense or meaning by any<BR>particular word &c.).<BR>—शक्य-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>most possible, very possible or practicable, (तन् न<BR>शक्यतमं कर्तुं, that is not at all possible to<BR>be done.)<BR>—शक्य-ता, f. or शक्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>possibility, practicability, capacity, capability.<BR>—शक्-<BR>यतावच्छेदक (˚ता-अव्˚), अम्, n. (according to<BR>Śabda-k.) = शक्यांशे भासमान-धर्मः.<BR>—शक्-<BR>य-प्रतीकार, अस्, m. a possible remedy or counter-<BR>agent; (अस्, आ, अम्), capable of being counteracted,<BR>remediable.<BR>—शक्यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. admis-<BR>sible meaning, the meaning conveyed by a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्र|शक्रः
शक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, strong, powerful, mighty (Ved.);<BR>(अस्), m. ‘the powerful one,’ N. of the god Indra,<BR>(see इन्द्र); of one of the twelve Ādityas; of Śiva;<BR>the plant Wrightia Antidysenterica (or Nerium Anti-<BR>dysentericum); the tree Pentaptera Arjuna.<BR>—शक्र-<BR>क्रीडाचल (˚डा-आच्˚), अस्, m. ‘Indra's pleasure-moun-<BR>tain,’ epithet of the mountain Meru.<BR>—शक्र-गोप,<BR>अस्, m. a particular red insect, the coccinella or a<BR>lady-bird of various species (= इन्द्र-गोप).<BR>—श-<BR>क्र-ज or शक्र-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, Indra-born; (अस्),<BR>m. a crow.<BR>—शक्र-जित्, त्, m. ‘conquerer of Indra,’<BR>epithet of the son of Rāvaṇa, (his first name was<BR>Megha-nāda, but after his victory over Indra, described<BR>in the Rāmāyaṇa, Uttara-kāṇḍa XXXIV, his name<BR>was changed by Brahmā to Indra-jit, q. v.; he was<BR>killed by Lakṣmaṇa.)<BR>—शक्र-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>glorious or vigorous as Indra.<BR>—शक्र-द्रुम, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Indra's tree,’ the Deva-dāru.<BR>—शक्र-धनुस्,<BR>उस्, n. ‘Indra's bow,’ the rainbow.<BR>—शक्र-ध्वज,<BR>अस्, m. a standard or flag set up in honour of Indra.<BR>—शक्र-ध्वजोत्सव (˚ज-उत्˚), अस्, m. = शक्रोत्-<BR>सव below.<BR>—शक्र-नन्दन, अस्, m. ‘Indra's<BR>son,’ epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—शक्र-पर्याय, अस्, m.<BR>‘synonym of Indra,’ the medicinal shrub Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica (= कुट-ज).<BR>—शक्र-पादप, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Indra's tree,’ a sort of pine, Pinus Devadāru;<BR>Wrightia Antidysenterica.<BR>—शक्र-पुष्पिका or<BR>शक्र-पुष्पी, f. ‘having flowers like those of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">Page0986-c+ 80</a>]<BR>Pentaptera Arjuna,’ a sort of pot-herb (= विशल्या);<BR>another plant (= अग्नि-शिखा).<BR>—शक्र-प्रस्थ,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘presided over by Indra,’ N. of<BR>ancient Delhi (= इन्द्र-प्रस्थ).<BR>—शक्र-भ-<BR>वन or शक्र-भुवन, अम्, n. ‘the abode or<BR>heaven of Indra,’ Svarga, paradise, heaven, the sky.<BR>—शक्र-भिद्, त्, m. ‘Indra-conqueror,’ epithet of<BR>the son of Rāvaṇa, (see शक्र-जित्.)<BR>—शक्र-भू-<BR>भवा, f. colocynth, Cucumis Coloquintida.<BR>—श-<BR>क्र-मातृ, ता, f. the mother of Indra; a particular<BR>plant (= भार्गी).<BR>—शक्र-मातृका, f. a wooden<BR>peg or post driven into the ground for supporting<BR>Indra's banner.<BR>—शक्र-मूर्धन्, आ, m. ‘Indra's<BR>head,’ an ant-hill, hillock.<BR>—शक्र-यशो-विध्वं-<BR>सन, अम्, N. of the 108th chapter of the Krīḍā-<BR>khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—शक्र-रूप, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the form of Indra.<BR>—शक्र-लोक, अस्,<BR>m. the world or sphere of Indra, paradise, Svarga.<BR>—शक्रलोक-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, sharing the sphere of<BR>Indra, having a portion in paradise.<BR>—शक्र-वल्ली,<BR>f. colocynth (= इन्द्र-वारुणी).<BR>—शक्र-वाहन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘Indra's vehicle,’ a cloud.<BR>—शक्र-वीज, अम्,<BR>n. ‘Indra-seed,’ the seed of Wrightia Antidysenterica.<BR>—शक्र-शरासन, अम्, n. ‘Indra's bow,’ the rain-<BR>bow.<BR>—शक्र-शाखिन्, ई, m. ‘Indra's tree,’ Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica.<BR>—शक्र-शाला, f. ‘Indra's hall,’ a<BR>place or room prepared for sacrifices.<BR>—शक्र-शिरस्,<BR>अस्, m. ‘Indra's head,’ an ant-hill.<BR>—शक्र-सारथि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘the charioteer of Indra,’ epithet of Mātali.<BR>—शक्र-सुत, अस्, m. ‘Indra's son,’ epithet of Ar-<BR>juna; of the monkey Bāli.<BR>—शक्र-सुधा, f. ‘Indra's<BR>nectar,’ the resin of Boswellia Thurifera, gum oli-<BR>banum (= पालङ्की).<BR>—शक्र-सृष्टा, f. ‘Indra-<BR>created,’ yellow myrobalan, Terminalia Chebula (fabled<BR>to have sprung from the ground on which Indra spilt<BR>a drop of nectar).<BR>—शक्राख्य (˚र-आख्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘Indra-named,’ an owl.<BR>—शक्रात्मज (˚र-आत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. Indra's own son.<BR>—शक्राशन (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘Indra-food,’ the medicinal plant Wrightia Antidy-<BR>senterica (fabled to have sprung from the drops of<BR>Amṛta which fell on the ground from the bodies of<BR>Rāma's monkeys restored to life by Indra); (अम्),<BR>n. an intoxicating drink prepared from hemp (=<BR>भङ्गा).<BR>—शक्रासन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘Indra's<BR>seat,’ a throne.<BR>—शक्राह्व (˚र-आह्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘Indra-named,’ the seed of Wrightia Antidysenterica.<BR>—शक्रोत्थान (˚र-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘raising up of<BR>[the banner of] Indra,’ = शक्रोत्सव below; [cf.<BR>ध्वजोत्थान.]<BR>—शक्रोत्सव (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘Indra-festival,’ a festival in honour of Indra on the<BR>twelfth day of the light half of the month Bhādra<BR>(when a flag or banner was set up, = ध्वजोत्थान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राणी
शक्राणी, f., N. of Sacī (wife of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रि|शक्रिः
शक्रि, इस्, m. a cloud; a thunderbolt; an elephant;<BR>a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ल|शक्लः
शक्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking pleasingly or kindly,<BR>affable; [cf. rt. शच्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वन्
शक्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. powerful, able, mighty;<BR>(आ), m. an elephant; (अरी), f. a kind of river, &c.<BR>See under शक्वर below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वर|शक्वरः
शक्वर, अस्, m. a bull, an ox [cf. शक्कर];<BR>(ई), f. a kind of river (= नदी-विशेष, नदी-भेद);<BR>a finger, (according to some, a finger-ring); a zone,<BR>girdle; a particular metre, (a stanza of four Pādas of<BR>fourteen syllables each, comprising at least twenty<BR>varieties, of which one of the commonest is called<BR>Vasanta-tilaka; cf. शक्करी, शर्करी); an arm<BR>(Ved.); a cow; (the fem. शक्वरी may equally be<BR>referred to शक्वन् above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शग्म
शग्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. able, powerful, mighty<BR>[cf. तुवि-श्˚]; prosperous, happy, causing happiness<BR>(= सुख-कर or सुख, and according to Sāy. de-<BR>rived fr. शम् + rt. गम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शग्मन्
शग्मन्, अ, n., Ved. a various reading for शक्मन्<BR>in Naigh. II. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शग्म्य
शग्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. powerful, mighty;<BR>prosperous, happy; [cf. शग्म.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित, शिक्षु, &c. See p. 1004, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकट|शकटं|शकटः
शकट शकट, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according<BR>to Uṇādi-s. IV. 81. fr. rt. 1. शक्), a cart, waggon,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">Page0987-a+ 78</a>]<BR>(said to be also ई, f.); (अस्), m. the figure of a cart<BR>formed by the five stars composing the lunar asterism<BR>Rohiṇī; a form of military array resembling a wedge,<BR>(सूच्य्-आकाराग्रः पश्चात्-पृथुलः, Manu VII.<BR>187); a cart-load (= 2000 Palas); an implement<BR>for preparing grain; N. of a demon slain by the<BR>infant Kṛṣṇa; a particular tree (= तिनिश); N. of<BR>a place.<BR>—शकट-भेद, अस्, m. division of the Śa-<BR>kaṭa asterism by the moon or a planet passing through<BR>it.<BR>—शकट-विल, अस्, m. a kind of water-hen, gal-<BR>linule.<BR>—शकट-हन्, हा, m. ‘destroyer of the<BR>demon Śakaṭa,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—शकटाक्ष<BR>(˚ट-अक्˚), अस्, m. the axle of a cart.<BR>—शकटारि (˚ट-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of Śakaṭa,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—शकटासुर (˚ट-अस्˚), अस्, m. the demon Śakaṭa<BR>(killed by the infant Kṛṣṇa).<BR>—शकटाह्वा (˚ट-<BR>आह्˚), f. ‘cart-named,’ the asterism Rohiṇī, (the five<BR>stars of which are figured as a cart.)<BR>—शकटोच्चा-<BR>टन (˚ट-उच्˚), अम्, n. the upsetting or overturning<BR>of a cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटार
शकटार, अस्, m. a bird of prey, (perhaps a kind<BR>of vulture); N. of a minister of king Nanda, (in<BR>revenge for ill-treatment he conspired with the<BR>Brāhman Cāṇakya to effect his master's death); N.<BR>of an ape.<BR>—शकटारोपाख्यान (˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n.<BR>story of (the ape) Śakaṭāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाल
शकटाल, अस्, m. = शकटार, the minister of king<BR>Nanda or (according to some) of Śūdraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका, f. a small cart, a child's cart, toy-cart;<BR>[cf. मृच्-छकटिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकन्
शकन् शकन्, n. a defective word option-<BR>ally substituted for शकृत् in certain cases, see<BR>col. 2.<BR>—शक-धूम, अस्, m., Ved. the smoke of<BR>burnt or burning (cow-) dung.<BR>—शक-पूत, अस्, m.<BR>‘purified with cow-dung’ (or ‘purified with water;’<BR>cf. शक); N. of the author of Ṛg-veda X. 132<BR>(having the patronymic Nārmedha).<BR>—शक-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. consisting of dung, arising from cow-<BR>dung, (Sāy. = शुष्क-गोमय-सम्भूत, Ṛg-veda<BR>1. 164, 43.)<BR>—शक-लोट (for शक-लोष्ट), अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a lump or ball of cow-dung (= शकृत्-पिण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल|शकलं|शकलः
शकल शकल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. I. 111. fr. rt. 1. शक्; more probably con-<BR>nected with शर्करा, q. v.; cf. शल्क), a part, portion,<BR>piece, fragment; a potsherd; (अस्), m. a proper N.;<BR>(अम्), n. skin, bark; the scales of a fish [cf. शल्क, शल्-<BR>कल]; a kind of black pigment or die.<BR>—शकली-क-<BR>रण, अम्, n. the act of cutting or breaking in pieces.<BR>—शकली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to break<BR>in pieces, cut to pieces, reduce to fragments, divide,<BR>bruise.<BR>—शकली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, cut in pieces,<BR>reduced to fragments, broken to bits; divided, dis-<BR>sected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलित
शकलित, अस्, आ, अम्, reduced to fragments, mashed,<BR>bruised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having scales, scaled; (ई), m.<BR>a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल्येषिन्
शकल्येषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, in Atharva-veda I. 25, 2,<BR>according to Atharva-veda Prātiśākhya III. 52. for<BR>शकल्य-एषिन्, said to mean ‘desiring fragments of<BR>wood’ (as a flame of fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकव
शकव शकव, अस्, m. (doubtful), a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकशकायत्
शकशकायत् शकशकायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (part.<BR>of an onomatopoetic verb formed fr. the imitative<BR>sound शक), making a rustling noise, rustling (as<BR>the leaves of a tree in the wind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकार|शकारः
शकार शकार, अस्, m. the brother of a<BR>king's concubine, a king's brother-in-law by one of<BR>his wives not regularly married (represented in the<BR>drama as a foolish, frivolous, proud, low, and cruel<BR>man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन|शकुनं|शकुनः
शकुन शकुन, अस्, m. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. III. 49. fr. rt. 1. शक्), a bird (in general); a<BR>particular kind of bird, (perhaps = गृध्र, a vulture,<BR>or = चिल्ल, the common kite, or perhaps the Pondi-<BR>cherry eagle); a kind of Brāhman (= विप्र-भेद);<BR>a sort of hymn or song (sung at festivals to secure<BR>good fortune); (अस्, आ or ई?, अम्), indicating good<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">Page0987-b+ 80</a>]<BR>luck, auspicious; (ई), f. a kind of bird (= श्यामा);<BR>a hen-sparrow; the form assumed by Pūtanā, (see<BR>Hari-vaṃśa 3423); (अम्), n. any auspicious object<BR>or lucky omen, a prognostic or omen (in general,<BR>but rarely applied to anything inauspicious).<BR>—श-<BR>कुन-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing omens; (आ), f. a<BR>small house-lizard.<BR>—शकुन-ज्ञान, अम्, n. ‘omen-<BR>knowledge,’ N. of a chapter in the Śārṅga-dhara-<BR>paddhati.<BR>—शकुन-दीपिका, f. ‘omen-light,’ N. of a<BR>work on good and evil omens by Gaṇeśa.<BR>—शकुन-<BR>शास्त्र, अम्, n. ‘omen-book,’ N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनि|शकुनिः
शकुनि, इस्, m. a bird; a vulture, kite, eagle;<BR>(according to some) a cock; N. of the brother of<BR>queen Gāndhārī (and therefore the brother-in-law<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra and the Mātula or maternal uncle<BR>of the Kuru princes; as son of Su-bala, king of<BR>Gāndhāra, he is called Saubala; he often acted as<BR>counsellor of Duryodhana, and hence this name is<BR>sometimes applied to an old officious relative whose<BR>counsels tend to ruin); N. of one of the astronomical<BR>periods called invariable Karaṇas; N. of a son of<BR>Duḥ-saha; of a son of Vikukṣi; (ई), m. du., N. of<BR>the Aśvins; (इस्), f., N. of a demon causing a particular<BR>sickness of children; a demon slain by Kṛṣṇa; [cf.<BR>Old Norse haukr; Danish hog; Old Germ. habuh;<BR>Angl. Sax. hafoc.]<BR>—शकुनि-प्रपा, f. a trough or<BR>place for watering birds (= श्री-ग्रह).<BR>—शकुनि-<BR>वाद, अस्, m. the cry or sound of a bird; the crow-<BR>ing of a cock.<BR>—शकुनीश्वर (˚नि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of birds,’ epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनी
शकुनी. See under शकुन and शकुनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्त|शकुंत|शकुंतः|शकुन्तः
शकुन्त, अस्, m. a bird (in general); a particular<BR>kind of bird (probably the Indian vulture or perhaps<BR>a sort of falcon described as of aquatic habits); the<BR>blue jay; a sort of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तक|शकुंतक|शकुंतकः|शकुन्तकः
शकुन्तक, अस्, m. a bird; (see also शकुन्तिका<BR>below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तला|शकुंतला
शकुन्तला, f. (said to be fr. शकुन्त), N. of a<BR>daughter of the Apsaras Menakā by Viśvā-mitra, (she<BR>was supposed to have been born and left in a solitary<BR>forest, where she was protected by birds till found<BR>by the sage Kaṇva, who took her to his hermitage<BR>and reared her as his daughter; she was there seen<BR>by king Dushyanta, when on a hunting expedition,<BR>and married by him, and became the mother of<BR>Bharata, sovereign of all India; the story of Dush-<BR>yanta's accidental meeting with Śakuntalā, their<BR>marriage, separation, his repudiation of her through<BR>temporary loss of memory caused by a curse, his<BR>subsequent recognition of her by means of a ring<BR>he had once given her which she had lost but after-<BR>wards recovered, forms the subject of Kālidāsa's<BR>celebrated drama called Abhijñāna-śakuntala, q. v.)<BR>—शकुन्तलात्मज (˚ला-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘Śakuntalā's<BR>son,’ epithet of Bharata, sovereign of India.<BR>—श-<BR>कुन्तलोपाख्यान (˚ला-उप्˚), अम्, n. ‘story of Śa-<BR>kuntalā,’ N. of chapters 69-74 of the Ādi-parvan of<BR>the Mahā-bhārata and of the first five chapters of the<BR>Svarga-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्ति|शकुंति|शकुंतिः|शकुन्तिः
शकुन्ति, इस्, m. a bird (in general); a kind of<BR>bird, (see शकुन्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तिका|शकुंतिका
शकुन्तिका, f. a kind of bird, perhaps the Franco-<BR>line partridge [cf. शकुन्तक]; a locust, cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुल|शकुलः
शकुल शकुल, अस्, m. a kind of fish (per-<BR>haps the gilt-head); (ई), f. another sort of fish<BR>(commonly called Mṛgāl, Cyprinus Mrigala); [cf.<BR>शकलिन्.]<BR>—शकुल-गण्ड, अस्, m. a kind of fish<BR>(probably the gilt-head, = शाल).<BR>—शकुलाक्षक<BR>(˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘fish-eyed,’ white bent-grass, Pa-<BR>nicum Dactylon, (the blossoms are white and com-<BR>pared to the eye of a fish.)<BR>—शकुलाक्षी (˚ल-अक्˚),<BR>f. a kind of Dūrvā grass (= गण्ड-दूर्वा).<BR>—श-<BR>कुलादनी (˚ल-अद्˚), f. a medicinal plant (commonly<BR>called Kaṭki, = चक्राङ्गी); a kind of creeping plant;<BR>N. of various other plants; a sort of drug (commonly<BR>called Kāyaphal, = मांसी); an earth-worm.<BR>—श-<BR>कुलार्भक (˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, m. a sort of fish (= ग-<BR>डक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्
शकृत् शकृत्, त्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 58. fr. rt. 1. शक्; according to others connected<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">Page0987-c+ 77</a>]<BR>with rt. 1. कॄ; sometimes written सकृत्; the base<BR>of some cases is शकन्, following the analogy of य-<BR>कृत्, q. v.), excrement, ordure, feces, dung, cow-<BR>dung; [cf. Gr. σκώρ (gen. σκατ-ός), σκωρ-ία,<BR>σκέπ-βολος; Lat. sterc-us, ster-qui-liniu-m; Angl. Sax.<BR>skearn; Goth. spai-skuldrs, ‘spittle;’ Slav. skvri-<BR>na, skar-edovati.]<BR>—शकृत्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, dung-<BR>making; (ई), f. a calf.<BR>—शकृत्-करि, इस्, m. f. ‘dung-<BR>making,’ a calf.<BR>—शकृत्-कार, अस्, आ, अम्, making<BR>ordure.<BR>—शकृत्-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a lump or ball of<BR>cow-dung.<BR>—शकृद्-ग्रह, आस्, m. pl., N. of a bar-<BR>barous race, (also read शकृद्-गुह, शकृद्-वह.)<BR>—शकृद्-द्वार, अम्, n. ‘door of the feces,’ the<BR>anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्कर|शक्करः
शक्कर शक्कर, अस्, m. (= शक्वर), a bull;<BR>(ई), f. a river; a zone, girdle; a particular kind of<BR>metre (= शक्वरी, q. v.); a woman of impure caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्करि|शक्करिः
शक्करि, इस्, m. a bull; [cf. शक्कर above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तवः
शक्तवः शक्तवः, m. pl. See शक्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ति|शक्तिः
शक्ति शक्ति, &c. See p. 985, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तु|शक्तुः
शक्तु शक्तु, उस्, उ, m. n. (also written सक्तु,<BR>q. v.; according to some properly used in masc. pl.<BR>शक्तवः only), the flour or meal of barley or grain<BR>of any kind (fried or parched before it is ground),<BR>barley-meal.<BR>—शक्तु-फला, or ई, f. the Śami tree,<BR>Mimosa Suma, (also read सक्तु-फला, q. v.)<BR>—शक्-<BR>तु-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become flour, consisting of<BR>flour.<BR>—शक्तु-शराव, अस्, m. a pot full of barley-<BR>meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तुक|शक्तुकः
शक्तुक, अस्, m. a kind of poison or poisonous<BR>substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वन्
शक्वन् शक्वन्, &c. See p. 986, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शग्म
शग्म शग्म. See p. 986, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क्|शंक्
शङ्क् शङ्क्, cl. 1. A. शङ्कते (ep. also P.<BR>-ति), शशङ्के, शङ्किष्यते, अशङ्किष्ट,<BR>शङ्कितुम्, to doubt, be doubtful or uncertain, hesi-<BR>tate; to distrust, fear, dread, be afraid; to suspect,<BR>have a suspicion; to think probable, believe, imagine,<BR>think, opine; (in argumentative works) to ponder<BR>over or propound a doubt or objection: Pass. शङ्क्-<BR>यते, Aor. अशङ्कि, to be doubted, &c.: Caus. शङ्क-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अशशङ्कत्, -त, to cause to<BR>doubt; to frighten; [cf. Lat. cunc-tari; Goth.<BR>hugjan, hugs; Old Germ. hugjan, hugu; Angl.<BR>Sax. hangian, hige, hyge, hogu, hygian, hyggan,<BR>hicgan, hogian.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क|शंक|शंकः|शङ्कः
शङ्क, अस्, m. a draught-ox; (आ), f. doubt, un-<BR>certainty, hesitation, scruple, distrust, suspicion, mis-<BR>giving, fear, apprehension; an objection started in<BR>disputation; presumption; hope; error; a species<BR>of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR>—शङ्काकुल (˚का-आक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, bewildered by doubt, filled with fear or sus-<BR>picion.<BR>—शङ्का-निवर्तक, अस्, इका, अम्, putting<BR>an end to doubt.<BR>—शङ्कान्वित (˚का-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, filled with doubt, apprehensive, doubtful, afraid.<BR>—शङ्काभियोग (˚का-अभ्˚), अस्, m. accusation or<BR>charge on suspicion.<BR>—शङ्का-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, full<BR>of doubt or uncertainty, fearful, afraid.<BR>—शङ्का-<BR>शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a hesitating or diffident dispo-<BR>sition, prone to doubt.<BR>—शङ्कास्पद (˚का-आस्˚),<BR>अम्, n. cause or matter of doubt, subject of appre-<BR>hension, object of suspicion.<BR>—शङ्का-स्पृष्ट, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, touched with fear, seized with alarm.<BR>—शङ्का-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, free from doubt or apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कन
शङ्कन, अस्, m. ‘causing fear or awe,’ N. of a<BR>king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कनीय|शंकनीय
शङ्कनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be doubted or ques-<BR>tioned, questionable, doubtful; to be suspected or<BR>apprehended; to be supposed or imagined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कमान|शंकमान
शङ्कमान, अस्, आ, अम्, doubting, suspecting, fear-<BR>ing, apprehending; being doubtful or uncertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कित|शंकित|शङ्कितः
शङ्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, doubted, apprehended, feared,<BR>suspected, distrusted; doubtful, uncertain; alarmed,<BR>frightened, apprehensive, fearful of (with gen. or<BR>abl.); distrustful, suspicious, suspecting; weak, un-<BR>steady.<BR>—शङ्कित-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, one whose<BR>mind is doubtful or suspicious, faint-hearted, timid,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-a" target="_blank">Page0988-a+ 80</a>]<BR>apprehensive.<BR>—शङ्कित-वर्णक, अस्, m. ‘whose<BR>appearance or caste is doubted,’ a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कितव्य
शङ्कितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be doubted, doubtful,<BR>questionable, &c. (= शङ्कनीय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्किन्|शंकिन्
शङ्किन्, ई, इनी, इ, doubting, suspecting, fearing,<BR>fearful of; full of danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुर|शंकुर|शङ्कुरः
शङ्कुर, अस्, आ, अम्, fearful, formidable, frightful,<BR>terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क्य
शङ्क्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be doubted, to be appre-<BR>hended or feared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कर|शंकर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शङ्कर शङ्-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (i. e. 2. श<BR>or 2. शम् + 1. कर), causing happiness, conferring<BR>good fortune or prosperity, auspicious, propitious,<BR>well-disposed; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; N. of a<BR>celebrated teacher of the Vedānta philosophy, (see<BR>शङ्कराचार्य below); of a poet; of a com-<BR>mentator on the Bengālī recension of Kālidāsa's<BR>Śakuntalā; of an astronomer, (also called भट्ट-<BR>शङ्कर); of the author of a drama called Śāradā-<BR>tilaka; of the author of the Dvaita-nirṇaya; of<BR>the author of the Karma-vipāka and the Saṃskāra-<BR>bhāskara; of the author of the Rasa-candrikā com-<BR>mentary; of a Dānava; (आ), f. a particular Rāga or<BR>musical mode; (ई), f. the wife of Śiva; Bengal<BR>madder; the Śamī tree.<BR>—शङ्कर-किङ्कर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Śaṅkara's servant,’ a proper N.<BR>—शङ्कर-<BR>क्रोड, अस्, m., N. of a Nyāya commentary.<BR>—शङ्-<BR>कर-गीता, f., N. of a work.<BR>—शङ्कर-चेतो-विलास,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the play of Śaṅkara's wit,’ N. of an artificial<BR>poem by Śaṅkara-dīkṣita (celebrating the glories of<BR>Vārāṇasī, especially of its kings Yavanāri and Ceta-<BR>siṃha or Cheyt Singh).<BR>—शङ्कर-जी and शङ्कर-<BR>जीक, m., N. of two scribes.<BR>—शङ्कर-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—शङ्कर-<BR>दिग्-विजय, अस्, m. ‘Śaṅkara's victory over the<BR>world,’ = शङ्कर-विजय below; N. of another<BR>similar work by Mādhava or Abhinava-kālidāsa pro-<BR>fessing to be a short account of Śaṅkarācārya's con-<BR>troversial exploits.<BR>—शङ्कर-दीक्षित, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a writer of the last century (author of the Gaṅ-<BR>gāvatāraṇa-campū-prabandha, Pradyumna-vijaya, and<BR>Śaṅkara-ceto-vilāsa).<BR>—शङ्कर-प्रिय, अस्, m.<BR>‘dear to Śaṅkara,’ the Francoline partridge (= तित्-<BR>तिरि).<BR>—शङ्कर-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Kuṇḍoddyotana-darśana.<BR>—शङ्कर-वर्-<BR>धन, अस्, and शङ्कर-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of<BR>two persons.<BR>—शङ्कर-विजय, अस्, m. ‘Śaṅkara's<BR>victory,’ N. of a biography of Śaṅkarācārya by<BR>Ānanda-giri (recording his victories, as a Vedāntin,<BR>over numerous heretics, and refuting the superstitions<BR>prevalent in his day by a popular exposition of the<BR>Vedānta philosophy).<BR>—शङ्कर-संहिता, f., N.<BR>of a part of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—शङ्कर-सेन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of a commentary on the<BR>Nāḍī-prakāśa.<BR>—शङ्कराचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a celebrated teacher of the Vedānta philosophy,<BR>(he is thought to have lived between A. D. 650 and<BR>740, but according to tradition he flourished 200 B. C.,<BR>and was a native of Kerala or Malabar; all accounts<BR>describe him as having led an erratic controversial<BR>life; his learning and sanctity were in such repute<BR>that he was held to have worked various miracles<BR>[amongst others, animating the dead body of a king<BR>Amaru so as to be able to argue with the wife of<BR>Mandana], and to have been an incarnation of the<BR>god Śiva, whose worship he enjoined; he is said to<BR>have died at the age of thirty-two, and, before his<BR>death, to have resided in Cashmere, and afterwards<BR>in the Himālaya; he had four principal disciples,<BR>called Padma-pāda, Hastāmalaka, Sureśvara or Man-<BR>dana, and Troṭaka, and another of his disciples,<BR>Ānanda-giri, wrote a history of his controversial<BR>exploits, called Śaṅkara-vijaya, q. v.; tradition<BR>makes him the founder of one of the prin-<BR>cipal Śaiva sects, the Daś-nāmī-Daṇḍins or ‘Ten-<BR>named Mendicants,’ so called because divided into<BR>ten classes, each distinguished by one or other of the<BR>names of the ten pupils of the above-mentioned<BR>four disciples of Śaṅkara [see शैव]; he is the<BR>reputed author of a large number of original works<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">Page0988-b+ 79</a>]<BR>with the following titles, Ātma-bodha, Ānanda-laharī,<BR>Ānanda-laharī-stotra, Jñāna-bodhinī, A-parokṣānu-<BR>bhūti-sudhārṇava, Upadeśa-sahasrī, Vākya-sudhā,<BR>Kādi-krama-stuti, Dhanya-stotra, Maṇi-ratna-mālā,<BR>Ganeśa-bhujaṅga-prayāta-stotra, Caturdaśa-mata-<BR>viveka, Tārā-pajjhaṭikā, Tripurī-prakaraṇa; and<BR>commentaries on the following, Chāndogyopani-<BR>shad, Bṛhad-āraṇyakopaniṣad, Praśnopaniṣad, Īśā-<BR>vāsyopaniṣad, Kaṭha-vally-upaniṣad, Taittirīyopa-<BR>niṣad, Aitareyopaniṣad, Kenopaniṣad, Māṇḍūkyo-<BR>paniṣad, Muṇḍakopaniṣad, Brahma-mīmāṃsā or<BR>Śārīraka-mīmāṃsā or Vedānta-sūtra, Bhagavad-gītā,<BR>Mahā-bhārata, Viṣṇu-sahasra-nāman); a N. given<BR>to the president of a Maṭha or college founded by<BR>Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—शङ्कराचार्य-विजय-दिण्डिम,<BR>N. of a commentary by Dhana-pati on the Saṅkṣepa-<BR>śaṅkara-jaya.<BR>—शङ्करानन्द (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a commentary on the Muṇḍakopaniṣad.<BR>—शङ्कराभरण (˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, m. a particular<BR>Rāga or musical mode.<BR>—शङ्करावास (˚र-आव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the abode of Śiva, Kailāsa; a kind of cam-<BR>phor (= कर्पूर-भेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कव्य|शंकव्यं
शङ्कव्य शङ्कव्य. See under शङ्कु below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कु|शंकु|शंकुः|शङ्कुः
शङ्कु शङ्कु, उस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. I. 37. said to<BR>be fr. rt. शङ्क्; in some senses connected with rt. 1. शक्),<BR>fear, apprehension; a stake, spike, pile, post, pale,<BR>pin, nail, peg, pillar; the spoke of a wheel (Ved.);<BR>a dart, javelin, spear, dagger, weapon (in general);<BR>the trunk of a lopped tree; the style or pin of a<BR>dial (usually twelve fingers long); the measure of<BR>twelve fingers; (in astronomy) the sine of altitude;<BR>a measuring-rod; a long thin column in front of a<BR>pagoda; the penis; the fibres of a leaf; the tree<BR>Shorea Robusta; the skate fish; the perfume called<BR>Nakhī; a goose; an ant-hill; a very high number,<BR>ten billions (as implied by an innumerable collection<BR>of ants, but cf. शङ्ख); a demon; poison, sin;<BR>N. of Śiva; of a Gandharva attendant on Śiva; of<BR>a king; of Kāma; of a son of Ugra-sena; of a poet<BR>(a son of Mayūra).<BR>—शङ्कु-कर्ण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>having ears (pointed) like a spear, spike-eared,<BR>pricking the ears; (अस्), m. an ass.<BR>—शङ्कु-जीवा,<BR>f. (in astronomy) the gnomon-sine.<BR>—शङ्कु-तरु,<BR>उस्, or शङ्कु-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the Sāl tree, Shorea<BR>Robusta.<BR>—शङ्कु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, filled with<BR>stakes or spikes; (अती), f., N. of a metre.<BR>—शङ्कु-<BR>शिरस्, आस्, m. ‘spear-headed,’ N. of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कव्य|शंकव्यं
शङ्कव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for a stake; (अम्), n.<BR>anything fit for a stake (as wood &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुक
शङ्कुक, अस्, m., N. of a poet (the author of<BR>the Bhuvanābhyudaya); of a writer on rhetoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुचि|शंकुचिः|शङ्कुचिः
शङ्कुचि, इस्, m. a skate fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुला|शंकुला
शङ्कुला, f. a kind of lancet or knife; a pair of<BR>nippers or scissors (used to cut the betel-nut into<BR>small pieces; cf. दन्त-शङ्कु).<BR>—शङ्कुला-खण्ड,<BR>अम्, n. a piece cut off with a pair of nippers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कोच|शंकोचः|शङ्कोचः
शङ्कोच, अस्, or शङ्कोचि, इस्, m. a skate fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्ख|शंख|शंखं|शंखः|शङ्खः
शङ्ख शङ्ख, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>104. said to be fr. rt. 1. शम्), a shell, the conch-<BR>shell (used for offering libations or, when perforated<BR>at one end, for blowing as a horn); a horn, trumpet,<BR>(in the battle pieces of epic poetry each hero is<BR>represented as provided with a conch-shell, which<BR>serves as his horn, and often has a name; that of<BR>Kṛṣṇa was called पाञ्चजन्य, q. v.); (अस्), m.<BR>the temporal bone, temple; the bone of the forehead<BR>or frontal bone; an elephant's cheek or the part<BR>between his tusks (= हस्ति-दन्त-मध्य); a par-<BR>ticular high number (said to equal a hundred bil-<BR>lions or one hundred thousand Krores, = दश-नि-<BR>खर्व; cf. शङ्कु); one of Kuvera's treasures; a<BR>particular perfume (commonly called Nakhī and ap-<BR>parently a kind of dried shell-fish); a military drum<BR>or other martial instrument; N. of a Daitya (who<BR>conquered the gods, stole the Vedas, and carried<BR>them off to the bottom of the sea, from whence<BR>they were recovered by Viṣṇu in the form of a<BR>fish); N. of one of the eight chiefs of the Nāgas or<BR>serpents of Pātāla (described as of a yellow colour);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-c" target="_blank">Page0988-c+ 81</a>]<BR>N. of the author of a law-book; of a poet (one of<BR>the nine gems at the court of king Vikramāditya);<BR>of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 15 (having<BR>the patronymic Yāmāyana); of one of the six minor<BR>Dvīpas; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a Gotra; [cf. Gr. κόγχος,<BR>κόγχη, κόλχος, κόχλος, κάλχη; Lat. concha.]<BR>—शङ्-<BR>ख-कर्णी, f. a kind of poison; [cf. महा-पञ्च-<BR>विष.]<BR>—शङ्ख-कार or शङ्ख-कारक, अस्, m.<BR>a worker in shells, shell-cutter (described as a kind<BR>of mixed caste; cf. शाङ्खिक).<BR>—शङ्ख-कूट,<BR>N. of a mountain.<BR>—शङ्ख-क्षीर, अम्, n. ‘shell-<BR>milk,’ any impossibility or absurdity.<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>चक्र-गदा-धर, अस्, m. ‘holding a conch, a<BR>discus, and a mace,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>चरी or शङ्ख-चर्ची, f. a mark made with sandal<BR>on the forehead.<BR>—शङ्ख-चूर्ण, अम्, n. ‘shell-<BR>powder, powder produced from shells.<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, shell-born, produced from shells;<BR>(अस्), m. a large pearl shaped like a pigeon's egg.<BR>—शङ्ख-द्राव or -द्रावक, अस्, m. a solvent for<BR>dissolving the conch or other shells (used in medi-<BR>cine).<BR>—शङ्ख-द्राविन्, ई, m. ‘shell-fuser,’ a kind<BR>of sorrel (= अम्ल-वेतस).<BR>—शङ्ख-धर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of an author; of a poet; (आ), f. a pot-herb<BR>(= हिल-मोचिका).<BR>—शङ्ख-ध्म, अस्, or शङ्-<BR>ख-ध्मा, आस्, m. a shell-blower, horn-blower, one<BR>who plays on the conch or horn.<BR>—शङ्ख-ध्वनि,<BR>इस्, m. the sound of a conch or horn.<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>नख, अस्, m. a small shell, the shell of the Trochus<BR>Perspectivus; the perfume called Nakhī (said to be a<BR>kind of dried shell-fish, see नखी); another kind<BR>of perfume, = वृहन्-नखी; (आ or ई), f. the per-<BR>fume called Nakhī.<BR>—शङ्ख-नाभ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—शङ्ख-पाद्, त्, or शङ्ख-पाद, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Kardama (said to have been made<BR>regent of the south, Viṣṇu-Purāṇa I. 22).<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>पाल, अस्, m. ‘shell-nourisher,’ epithet of the sun;<BR>N. of a Nāga or serpent of Pātāla.<BR>—शङ्ख-पुष्-<BR>पी, f. a sort of plant (= कम्बु-पुष्पी).<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>प्रणाद, अस्, m. the sound of a conch or horn.<BR>—शङ्ख-प्रवर, अस्, अम्, m. n. an excellent<BR>shell, the best shell.<BR>—शङ्ख-प्रस्थ, अस्, m. a<BR>mark or spot on the moon.<BR>—शङ्ख-भिन्न, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, see Vopa-deva IV. 20.<BR>—शङ्ख-भृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>carrying or bearing a conch-shell; (त्), m. an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शङ्ख-मुक्ता, f. mother of pearl;<BR>(आस्), f. pl. shells and pearls.<BR>—शङ्ख-मुख, अस्,<BR>m. ‘shell-faced,’ an alligator.<BR>—शङ्ख-मूल, अम्,<BR>n. a particular esculent root (= मूलक).<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>राज्, ट्, m. the best of shells.<BR>—शङ्ख-रावित, अम्,<BR>n. a sound of conches.<BR>—शङ्ख-लिखित, औ, m. du.<BR>the two Ṛṣis, Śaṅkha and Likhita (authors of a<BR>law-book); (अस्), m. a king who practises justice,<BR>a just king; शङ्खलिखिता वृत्तिः, conduct re-<BR>sembling that of Śaṅkha and Likhita.<BR>—शङ्ख-<BR>लिखित-प्रिय, अस्, m. beloved by Śaṅkha and<BR>Likhita, a friend of strict justice.<BR>—शङ्ख-स्मृति,<BR>इस्, f. the law-book of Śaṅkha.<BR>—शङ्ख-स्वन, अस्,<BR>m. the sound of a conch or trumpet.<BR>—शङ्खाख्य<BR>(˚ख-आख्˚), अस्, m. a kind of perfume (= वृहन्-<BR>नखी).<BR>—शङ्खान्तर-द्योतिन् (˚ख-अन्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, shining in the middle of the frontal bone.<BR>—शङ्खासुर (˚ख-अस्˚), अस्, m. the Daitya<BR>Śaṅkha.<BR>—शङ्खाह्वा (˚ख-आह्˚), f. a sort of<BR>plant (= शङ्ख-पुष्पी).<BR>—शङ्खोदक (˚ख-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. the water poured into a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खक|शंखक|शंखकं|शङ्खकं|शंखकः|शङ्खकः
शङ्खक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the conch-shell; (अस्),<BR>m. a disease of the head (described as a pain in the<BR>forehead and heat with a puffiness in the temples);<BR>the temporal bone or temple; (अम्), n. a bracelet<BR>(often made of conch-shell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिका
शङ्खिका, f. a kind of grass, Andropogon Acicu-<BR>latum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिन्|शंखिन्
शङ्खिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing shells, having or<BR>holding a conch-shell; (ई), m. the ocean; a worker<BR>in shells; a shell-blower; an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>(इनी), f., N. of various plants, a sort of grass, Andro-<BR>pogon Aciculatum; a particular plant, Cissampelos<BR>Hexandra; another plant (= यव-तिक्ता); N. of one<BR>of the four classes into which females are divided<BR>(described as tall and handsome, with long eyes and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">Page0989-a+ 77</a>]<BR>hair, marked with three lines on the neck, amorous<BR>and irascible, and neither stout nor thin); a particular<BR>goddess or Śakti worshipped by Buddhists; a female<BR>spirit, a kind of semi-divine being or fairy (= उप-<BR>देवता-विशेष).<BR>—शङ्खिनी-फल, अस्, m. the<BR>Śirīṣa tree.<BR>—शङ्खिनी-फल, अस्, m. the<BR>Śirīṣa tree.<BR>—शङ्खिनी-वास, अस्, m. a small tree,<BR>Trophis Aspera (= शाखोट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शच्
शच् शच्, cl. 1. A. शचते, शेचे, शचितुम्,<BR>to speak, say, tell; to be strong, &c., (in<BR>this sense for rt. 1. शक्, see the derivatives below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचि|शचिः
शचि, इस्, f. = शची below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचिष्ठ
शचिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. strongest, most power-<BR>ful, very powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शची
शची, f. speech, power of speech, eloquence (= वाच्,<BR>Naigh. I. 11); activity, diligence, energy, skilfulness<BR>(= प्रज्ञा, Naigh. III. 9); power, strength, action,<BR>exploit, (Sāy. and Naigh. II. 1 = कर्म); any holy<BR>act, devotion; N. of the wife of Indra, (in the pre-<BR>ceding senses chiefly Ved.); the plant Asparagus<BR>Racemosus; the astronomical Karaṇa or period<BR>named Viṣṭi; Śacī Paulomī is given as the authoress<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 159.<BR>—शची-नर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of Kaśmīra.<BR>—शची-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘lord of power,’ or ‘husband of Śacī,’ epithet of<BR>Indra; (ई), m. du. ‘lords of pious acts,’ epithet of<BR>the Aśvins (Ved.)<BR>—शची-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>possessing power, strong, (Sāy. = कर्म-वत्); wise,<BR>(Sāy. = प्रज्ञा-वत्); (आन्), m. epithet of Indra,<BR>(शचीवस्, voc. c. ‘O powerful one.’)<BR>—शची-वसु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. rich or abounding in strength, en-<BR>riched by holy rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शञ्च्|शंच्
शञ्च् शञ्च् (= rt. श्वच्, q. v.), cl. 1. A.<BR>शञ्चते, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट्
शट् शट्, cl. 1. P. शटति, शटितुम्, to be<BR>sick or diseased; to divide, separate, pierce;<BR>to be dissolved; to be weary or dejected; to go;<BR>cl. 10. A. शाटयते, -यितुम्, to praise, flatter (= rt.<BR>1. शठ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट|शटः
शट, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. शट् above),<BR>sour, astringent, acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटि|शटिः
शटि, इस्, f. the plant called Zedoary or Curcuma<BR>Amhaldi (otherwise Curcuma Zerumbet; there are<BR>thirty-eight synonyms of this plant; cf. गन्धा,<BR>गन्ध-मूली, &c.); a particular kind of ginger (the<BR>fresh root of which is scented like a green mango).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटी
शटी, f. = शटि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटा
शटा शटा, f. (= सटा, जटा), an ascetic's<BR>clotted hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट्टक|शट्टकं
शट्टक शट्टक, अम्, n. flour of rice mixed<BR>with water and ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
शठ् 1. शठ् [cf. rts. शट्, शल्], cl. 10. A.<BR>शाठयते, -यितुम्, to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
शठ् 2. शठ् (= rt. 1. श्वठ्), cl. 10. P.<BR>शठयति, -यितुम्, to speak ill; (according<BR>to some) to speak correctly or well or elegantly; to<BR>be true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
शठ् 3. शठ् (= rts. 2. श्वठ्, सठ्, स्वठ्),<BR>cl. 10. P. शाठयति, -यितुम्, to accom-<BR>plish, finish, adorn; to leave unfinished or unorna-<BR>mented; to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
शठ् 4. शठ्, cl. 1. P. शठति, शठितुम्,<BR>to cheat, defraud, deceive; to hurt, kill;<BR>to suffer pain; cl. 10. P. शाठयति, -यितुम्, to be<BR>idle or lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ, अस्, आ, अम् (probably connected with शत्रु;<BR>cf. शतेर), wicked, depraved, perverse, dishonest,<BR>perfidious, cunning, crafty, deceitful; (अस्), m. a<BR>rogue, knave; a false husband or lover (who pretends<BR>affection for one female while his heart is fixed on<BR>another; one of the four classes into which husbands<BR>are divided); a fool, blockhead; an idler; a medi-<BR>ator, umpire, arbitrator; the thorn-apple, Datura<BR>Metel; (अम्), n. a sort of plant or its root (= त-<BR>गर); saffron, iron; [cf. Hib. sath, ‘evil;’ saith,<BR>‘vulgar, vile.’]<BR>—शठ-ता, f. or शठ-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>wickedness, depravity, roguery, knavery.<BR>—शठ-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">Page0989-b+ 77</a>]<BR>ताचरण (˚ता-आच्˚), अम्, n. wicked or roguish con-<BR>duct.<BR>—शठाम्बा (˚ठ-अम्˚), f. a particular plant<BR>(= अम्ब-ष्ठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्
शण् शण्, cl. 1. or 10. P. शणति, शण-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to give; to go (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण|शणं|शणः
शण, अम्, n. hemp, Cannabis Sativa; (अस्), m. a<BR>kind of hemp (commonly called Bengal Śaṇ; also<BR>Crotolaria Juncea); an arrow, (in this sense perhaps<BR>connected with शर); [cf. Gr. κάνναβις; Lat. can-<BR>nabis; Lith. kanápe†; Russ. kanopla; Hib. ca-<BR>naib; Old Iceland. hanp; Angl. Sax. hœnep;<BR>Old Germ. hanaf; Mod. Germ. hanf.]<BR>—शण-<BR>घण्टिका, f. = शण-पुष्पी.<BR>—शण-तन्तु, उस्, m.<BR>thread or string made of the flax of the Crotolaria<BR>Juncea.<BR>—शण-तान्तव (?), अस्, ई, अम्, made of<BR>hempen string.<BR>—शण-पर्णी, f. the tree Pentaptera<BR>Tomentosa.<BR>—शण-पुष्पी or शण-पुष्पिका, f.<BR>Crotolaria of various species.<BR>—शण-शकल, अस्, m. a<BR>piece of hemp.<BR>—शण-सूत्र, अम्, n. the fibre or flax<BR>of Śaṇ or hemp, hempen cord or string; a net made<BR>of hemp; the thread of the Crotolaria Juncea;<BR>cordage, twine.<BR>—शणसूत्र-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of hempen threads or cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणालु
शणालु, उस्, or शणालुक, अस्, m. the tree Cassia<BR>Fistula (= आरेवत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणिका
शणिका, f. = शण-पुष्पी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणीर|शणीरं
शणीर शणीर, अम्, n. a bank or alluvial<BR>island in the middle of the river Śoṇa; an insular<BR>spot enclosed by the branches of the river Surjoo at<BR>the point where it falls into the Ganges above Chu-<BR>pra, (this spot is also called Dardarī-taṭa, ‘Dardarī-<BR>bank.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ठ|शंठः
शण्ठ शण्ठ, अस्, m. a eunuch (= शण्ढ,<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ड्|शंड्
शण्ड् शण्ड्, cl. 1. A. शण्डते, शण्डितुम्,<BR>to hurt, wound, cause disease or sickness;<BR>to collect, heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ड|शंड|शण्डं|शंडः|शण्डः
शण्ड, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 113. fr.<BR>rt. शण्ड् above), a eunuch; an impotent man; a<BR>bull; a bull at liberty; N. of an Asura priest (Ved.);<BR>(अम्), n. a multitude of lotus-flowers.<BR>—शण्ड-ता,<BR>f. impotence, emasculation; the state of a bull or of<BR>a bull at liberty.<BR>—शण्डामर्क (˚ड-अम्˚) or (ac-<BR>cording to others) शण्डा-मर्क, औ, m. du. Śaṇḍa<BR>and Amarka or Marka, N. of two demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्डिक
शण्डिक, आस्, m. pl., Ved. the descendants of Śaṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्डिल|शण्डिलः
शण्डिल, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 55. fr.<BR>rt. शण्ड्), N. of an ancient sage (ancestor of a par-<BR>ticular family of Brāhmans); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>Gotra or family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ढ|शंढ|शंढः|शण्ढः
शण्ढ शण्ढ, अस्, m. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. I. 101. fr. rt. 1. शम्), a eunuch; an attendant<BR>in a harem or women's apartments; an impotent<BR>man; a bull; a bull at liberty; a mad man, drunken<BR>man; [cf. शण्ड, षण्ड, षण्ढ, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत|शतं
शत शत, अम्, n. (thought by some to be<BR>a corruption fr. दशत, cf. दशति), a hundred,<BR>(शतात् पर, beyond a hundred, exceeding a hun-<BR>dred: शत is used in the sing. with a plur. noun,<BR>e. g. शतम् पितरः or शतम् पितॄणाम्, a hundred<BR>ancestors; and used with other numerals thus, एका-<BR>धिकं शतम् or एक-शतम्, a hundred + one, 101;<BR>द्व्य्-अधिकं शतम् or द्वि-शतम्, a hundred +<BR>two, 102; एकादशाधिकं शतम् or एकादशं<BR>शतम् or एकादश-शतम्, a hundred + eleven or<BR>a hundred having eleven, 111; विंशत्य्-अधिकं<BR>शतम् or विंशं शतम्, a hundred + twenty, 120);<BR>any very large number (in comp., cf. शत-पत्त्र<BR>&c. below); (ए), n. du. two hundred (e. g. शते or<BR>द्वे शते or द्वि-शतम्, two hundred); (आनि), n. pl.<BR>hundreds (e. g. त्रीणि शतानि or त्रि-शतानि, three<BR>hundred; there occurs also rarely a form in आस्, m.<BR>pl., e. g. शतं शताः, ‘one hundred hundred,’ i. e.<BR>ten thousand; सप्त शताः, seven hundred); (अम्),<BR>ind., Ved. a hundred (in Ṛg-veda I. 48, 7); (ई), f.<BR>a hundred (used in comp., e. g. द्वि-शती, two hundred;<BR>दश-शती, ten hundred); (अस्, ई, अम्), the hundredth<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-c" target="_blank">Page0989-c+ 81</a>]<BR>(so used against Pāṇ. V. 2, 57); [cf. Gr. ἑ-κατόν<BR>(fr. ἑ=ἕν, ‘one,’ and κατο = शत); Lat. centum;<BR>Goth. hund; Angl. Sax. hund; Lith. szimta-s;<BR>Slav. sto; Hib. céat: Cambro-Brit. cant; Armor.<BR>kant.]<BR>—शत-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m., N. of an Arhat of the<BR>future Utsapiṇī.<BR>—शत-कुन्द, अस्, m. a particular<BR>plant (= कर-वीर).<BR>—शत-कुम्भ, अम्, n. gold;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a mountain; (आ), f. the plant Phyalis<BR>Flexuosa; N. of a river.<BR>—शत-कृत्वस्, ind. a hun-<BR>dred times.<BR>—शत-कोटि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a hundred<BR>edges; (इस्), m. Indra's thunderbolt; (इस्), f. a hun-<BR>dred Krores (= अब्ज).<BR>—शत-क्रतु, उस्, m. ‘having<BR>or honoured by a hundred sacrifices,’ epithet of Indra<BR>(a hundred Aśva-medhas elevating the sacrificer to the<BR>rank of Indra; cf. Gr. ἑκατομβαῖος).<BR>—शत-खण्-<BR>ड, अम्, n. ‘hundred-pieced,’ gold.<BR>—शतखण्ड-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of a hundred pieces;<BR>made of gold.<BR>—शत-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, possessed of a<BR>hundred cows.<BR>—शत-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, a hundred-<BR>fold, a hundred times.<BR>—शतगुणाधिकम् (˚ण-<BR>अध्˚), ind. more than a hundred times.<BR>—शत-<BR>गुणित, अस्, आ, अम्, repeated a hundred times.<BR>—श-<BR>तगुणी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become a hundred times<BR>(as strong).<BR>—शत-गुप्ता, f. Euphorbia Antiquorum<BR>(= पेषण).<BR>—शत-ग्रन्थि, इस्, f. ‘having a hun-<BR>dred knots,’ Dūrvā grass.<BR>—शत-ग्व, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>hundred-fold; [cf. दश-ग्व, नव-ग्व.]<BR>—शत-<BR>ग्विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. hundred-fold [cf. दश-ग्विन्];<BR>consisting of hundreds of flocks, (Sāy. = शत-सङ्ख्-<BR>याक-गवादि-विशिष्ट, Ṛg-veda I. 159, 5.)<BR>—श-<BR>त-घ्नी, f. ‘slaying hundreds,’ a kind of weapon<BR>(used as a missile, supposed by some to be a sort of<BR>fire-arms or rocket, but described by the commen-<BR>tator on the Mahā-bhārata as a stone or cylindrical<BR>piece of wood studded with iron spikes); a female<BR>scorpion; a kind of plant (= करञ्ज); a disease of<BR>the throat (enlargement of the tonsils); epithet of Śiva<BR>(masc.).<BR>—शत-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘having a hundred<BR>feathers,’ a sort of wood-pecker (= काष्ठ-कुट्ट).<BR>—शत-जित्, त्, m. ‘vanquishing hundreds,’ N. of a<BR>son of Raja; of a son of Sahasra-jit; of a son of Bhaja-<BR>māna.<BR>—शत-जिह्व, अस्, m. ‘hundred-tongued,’ epi-<BR>thet of Śiva.<BR>—शत-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the hundredth.<BR>—शत-तारा, f. ‘having a hundred stars,’ the con-<BR>stellation Śata-bhiṣaj, q. v., (also written शत-ता-<BR>रका.)<BR>—शत-तेजस्, आस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—शत-<BR>दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a hundred teeth (said<BR>of a comb, &c.).<BR>—शत-दन्तिका, f. a particular<BR>plant (= नाग-दन्ती).<BR>—शत-दला, f. ‘having a<BR>hundred leaves or petals,’ the Indian white rose.<BR>—शत-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. giving or granting a<BR>hundred.<BR>—शत-दातु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. hundred-<BR>fold.<BR>—शत-दाय, अस्, आ, अम्, giving a hundred;<BR>having abundant wealth; a hundred-fold, (fr. 2. दाय,<BR>q. v.)<BR>—शत-दावन्, आ, &c., Ved. giving a hundred,<BR>giving bountifully, liberal, munificent.<BR>—शत-दुर,<BR>अम्, n. a place having a hundred doors, a place se-<BR>cured by many gates, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 51, 3. शत-दुरेषु = शत-द्वारेषु यन्त्रे-<BR>षु.)<BR>—शत-द्युम्न, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Cākṣuṣa; of a son of Bhānu-mat.<BR>—शत-द्रु,<BR>उस्, f. ‘flowing in a hundred (branches),’ N. of a river<BR>now called the Sutlej, (it is the most easterly of the five<BR>rivers of the Pañjāb, and rises in the Mānasa Saro-<BR>vara or Mānasa lake on the Himālaya mountains;<BR>flowing in a south-westerly direction for 550 miles,<BR>it unites with the Vipāśā or Beas south-east of<BR>Amritsar, [see विपाश्]; it afterwards joins the Chenāb<BR>and falls into the Indus below Multan; it is also<BR>called शुतु-द्रि, शुतु-द्रु, शित-द्रु, &c.); N. of<BR>the Ganges.<BR>—शतद्-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ (for शत-<BR>वसु), Ved. having hundreds of treasures, containing<BR>much wealth.<BR>—शत-द्वार, अम्, n. a hundred doors<BR>or gates; (अस्, आ, अम्), hundred-gated, having many<BR>doors or outlets.<BR>—शत-धनु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—शत-धन्वन्, आ, आ, अ, having a hundred<BR>bows; (आ), m., N. of a person slain by Kṛṣṇa for<BR>having killed Satrā-jit.<BR>—१. शत-धा, f. Dūrvā grass,<BR>Panicum Dactylon.<BR>—२. शत-धा, ind. in a hundred<BR>ways; into a hundred parts, in a hundred pieces;<BR>a hundred-fold.<BR>—शत-धामन्, आ, m. ‘having a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0990-a" target="_blank">Page0990-a+ 81</a>]<BR>hundred forms,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शत-धार,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, flowing in a hundred streams; having a<BR>hundred edges; (अम्), n. the thunderbolt.<BR>—शत-<BR>धृति, इस्, m. ‘having a hundred sacrifices,’ epithet<BR>of Indra; of Brahmā; Svarga or heaven.<BR>—शत-<BR>पत्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having a hundred wings, borne<BR>by numerous conveyances (said of Bṛhas-pati); hav-<BR>ing a hundred, i. e. numberless leaves; (अम्), n. a<BR>lotus, Nelumbium Speciosum, &c.; (अस्), m. ‘having<BR>a hundred feathers,’ a peacock; the Sārasa or Indian<BR>crane; a wood-pecker; a parrot, the king parrot,<BR>Psittacus Lory; (आ), f. a woman; (ई), f. a kind of<BR>flower, the Indian, white rose, Rosa Glandulifera.<BR>—शतपत्त्रक, अस्, m. a wood-pecker [cf. शत-<BR>च्छद]; (इका), f. the Indian white rose.<BR>—शत-<BR>पत्त्र-निवास, अस्, आ, अम्, abiding in a lotus; (अस्),<BR>m. epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—शतपत्त्र-योनि, इस्, m.<BR>‘lotus-born,’ epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—शतपत्त्राय-<BR>तेक्षण (˚र-आय्˚, ˚त-ईक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>eyes are long as a lotus.<BR>—शत-पथ-ब्राह्मण,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the Brāhmaṇa with a hundred paths or<BR>lectures,’ N. of a well-known Brāhmaṇa attached to<BR>the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā or White Yajur-veda, (like<BR>the Saṃhitā, this Brāhmaṇa is ascribed to the Ṛṣi<BR>Yājñavalkya; it is perhaps the most modern of the<BR>Brāhmaṇas, and is preserved in two Śākhās or<BR>schools, Mādhyandina and Kāṇva; the version be-<BR>longing to the former is best known, and is divided<BR>into fourteen Kāṇḍas or books which contain one<BR>hundred Adhyāyas or lectures [or according to another<BR>arrangement into sixty-eight Prapāṭhakas]; the first<BR>nine Kāṇḍas are said to follow the first eighteen books<BR>of the Saṃhitā in quoting their verses and explaining<BR>their use at sacrifices almost word for word, like a<BR>running commentary; but the last five Kāṇḍas appear<BR>to be a more independent work, referring only occa-<BR>sionally to the Saṃhitā; the first of these five or<BR>the tenth Kāṇḍa is called Agni-rahasya, ‘fire-<BR>mystery;’ the eleventh Kāṇḍa, called Aṣṭādhyāyī,<BR>explains more fully the sacrifices previously mentioned,<BR>such as the Agny-ādhāna &c.; the twelfth, called<BR>Sautrāmaṇī, treats of Prāyaścitta or penance, and the<BR>thirteenth of the Aśva-medha; the fourteenth con-<BR>tains the Bṛhad-āraṇyaka [q. v.] Upaniṣad; the<BR>whole work is regarded as the most systematic and<BR>interesting of all the Brāhmaṇas, and though intended<BR>mainly for ritual and sacrificial purposes, is full of<BR>curious mythological details and legends; cf. यजुर्-<BR>वेद, वाजसनेयि-संहिता, ब्राह्मण.)<BR>—शत-<BR>पथिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शत-पथिन्), ‘having a<BR>hundred roads,’ following numberless paths or doc-<BR>trines.<BR>—शत-पद् or शत-पाद्, -पात्, -पात् or -पदी,<BR>पात् or -पत्, having a hundred feet; having a hun-<BR>dred wheels (Ved.); (-पात् or -पदी), f. a centipede.<BR>—शतपद-चक्र, अम्, n. an astronomical circle<BR>or diagram with a hundred divisions for exhibiting<BR>the various divisions of the Nakṣatras and Signs.<BR>—शत-पदी, see under शत-पद् above.<BR>—शत-<BR>पद्म, अम्, n. the white lotus.<BR>—शत-पर्वन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, having a hundred, i. e. numberless knots or<BR>joints; (आ), m. a bamboo.<BR>—शत-पर्वा, f. ‘hundred-<BR>jointed,’ Dūrvā grass, Panicum Dactylon; orris root;<BR>the wife of Bhārgava or Śukra; the day of full moon<BR>in the month Āśvina, (see को-जागर); a kind of<BR>plant (= कटुका).<BR>—शतपर्विका, f. Dūrvā grass;<BR>orris root; barley.<BR>—शतपर्वेश (˚वा-ईश), अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord or husband of Śata-parvā,’ the planet Venus<BR>or its regent.<BR>—शत-पवित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., see<BR>Nirukta V. 6.<BR>—शत-पाद्, see शत-पद्.<BR>—शत-<BR>पादिका, f. a medicinal root (= काकोली); a centipede<BR>or a kind of ear-wig.<BR>—शत-पादी, f. a centipede.<BR>—शत-पुत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having a hundred sons.<BR>—शतपुत्र-ता, f. the possession of a hundred sons.<BR>—शत-पुष्प, अस्, आ, अम्, having a hundred flowers,<BR>many-flowered; (अस्), m. epithet of the poet Bhāravi,<BR>(author of the Kirātārjunīya); (आ), f. a sort of dill or<BR>fennel, Anethum Sowa (= मिसि).<BR>—शतपुष्पिका,<BR>f. the plant Anethum Sowa.<BR>—शत-प्रभेदन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X.<BR>113 (having the patronymic Vairūpa).<BR>—शत-प्र-<BR>सूना, f. = शत-पुष्पा.<BR>—शत-प्रास, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0990-b" target="_blank">Page0990-b+ 81</a>]<BR>‘having a hundred spikes,’ a kind of oleander, Ne-<BR>rium Odorum (the leaves of which are compared to<BR>spears; = कर-वीर).<BR>—शत-बला, f., N. of a river.<BR>—शत-बलाक, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—शत-<BR>ब्रध्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hundred-pointed, having<BR>a hundred points (said of the arrow of Indra; Sāy.<BR>= शताग्र).<BR>—शत-भिषज्, क्, or शत-भिषा, f.<BR>‘requiring a hundred physicians,’ N. of one of the<BR>Nakṣatras or lunar mansions containing 100 stars,<BR>one of which is λ Aquarii, (this Nakṣatra is gene-<BR>rally placed twenty-fifth on the list, and is said to<BR>require innumerable physicians, because Dhanvantari<BR>himself cannot cure a person affected with disease<BR>whilst the moon is in this asterism.)<BR>—शत-भीरु,<BR>उस्, f. ‘fearful of a hundred (dangers),’ Arabian jas-<BR>mine.<BR>—शत-भुजि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. hundred-fold,<BR>vast, extensive, (Sāy. = अत्यन्तं विस्तृत, शत-<BR>गुण); having a hundred enclosures or fortifications;<BR>having innumerable enjoyments, (Sāy. = अ-सङ्ख्-<BR>यात-भोगवत्, Ṛg-veda I. 166, 8.)<BR>—शत-मख,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a hundred sacrifices,’ an epithet of<BR>Indra; [cf. शत-क्रतु.]<BR>—शत-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. receiving a hundred sacrifices; very spirited,<BR>very zealous; (उस्), m. epithet of Indra.<BR>—शत-<BR>मान, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘hundred-measure,’ a Pala of<BR>silver; an Āḍhaka, q. v.; (अस्, ई, अम्), a hundred-<BR>fold.<BR>—शत-मारिन्, ई, m. ‘hundred-killer,’ a man<BR>who has killed a hundred others.<BR>—शत-मार्ज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘cleaner of a hundred, i. e. numberless weapons,’<BR>an armourer, a cutler.<BR>—शत-मुख, अम्, n. a<BR>hundred mouths or openings; a hundred ways; (अस्,<BR>ई, अम्), having a hundred mouths, having a hundred<BR>outlets or openings; having a hundred issues or ways.<BR>—शतम्-ऊति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. granting a hundred aids<BR>or great protection; [cf. शतोति.]<BR>—शत-मूल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a hundred roots; (आ), f. Dūrvā grass; a<BR>kind of orris root, = वचा; (ई), f. Asparagus Race-<BR>mosus (of which forty-two synonyms are given).<BR>—शत-मूलिका, f. ‘having a hundred roots,’ the<BR>plant Asparagus Racemosus; another plant (= द्र-<BR>वन्ती).<BR>—शत-यज्वन्, आ, m. ‘sacrificing with a<BR>hundred,’ N. of Indra; [cf. शत-क्रतु.]<BR>—शत-<BR>यष्टिक, अस्, m. a necklace of a hundred strings.<BR>—शत-यातु, उस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—शत-या-<BR>मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having a hundred ways.<BR>—शत-<BR>योजन, अम्, n. a hundred Yojanas.<BR>—शतयोजन-<BR>यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going a hundred Yojanas.<BR>—शत-<BR>योजन-वत्, ind. as large as a hundred Yojanas.<BR>—शत-रा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. giving a hundred,<BR>bestowing hundreds, i. e. countless riches, (in Naigh.<BR>II. 3. शत-रा is enumerated among the सुख-<BR>नामानि.)<BR>—शत-रुद्रिय, अम्, n. a celebrated<BR>hymn and prayer of the Yajur-veda occurring in<BR>Vājasaneyi-s. XVI. 1 — 66, (different etymologies are<BR>given; in one place it is said to mean ‘that by<BR>which the hundred-headed Rudra is appeased;’ in<BR>another शत is derived from शम् as गत from<BR>गम्, and the word is regarded as = शान्त-रुद्रिय);<BR>N. of an Upaniṣad; (अस्, आ, अम्), much celebrated<BR>(= बहु-मन्त्रैः स्तुत according to Mahī-dhara).<BR>—शतरुद्रिय-होम, अस्, m. epithet of the six-<BR>teenth Adhyāya of the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā.<BR>—शत-<BR>रुद्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to Śabda-k.) having<BR>a hundred Rudras as divinity.<BR>—शत-रूप, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a hundred forms, having numberless<BR>shapes; (आ), f., N. of the daughter and wife of Brahmā,<BR>(from her incestuous intercourse with her father is<BR>said to have sprung Manu Svāyambhuva, but some<BR>Purāṇas make Śata-rūpā the wife not mother of the<BR>first Manu; in Manu 1. 32. no mention of Śata-<BR>rūpā is made; it is there simply said that Brahmā,<BR>having divided his own body into two, became with<BR>the half a man and with the other half a woman, and<BR>in her begot Virāj, who then produced Manu Svā-<BR>yambhuva.)<BR>—शतर्चिन् (˚त-ऋच्˚), इनस्, m. pl.<BR>epithet of the poets of the first Maṇḍala of the Ṛg-<BR>veda.<BR>—शत-लक्ष, अम्, n. a hundred lacs, ten<BR>millions.<BR>—शत-लुम्प or शत-लुम्पक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the poet Bhāravi (author of the Kirātārjunīya).<BR>—शत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of a hundred,<BR>amounting to hundreds.<BR>—शत-वध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0990-c" target="_blank">Page0990-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Ved. slaying hundreds.<BR>—शत-वनि, इस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—शत-वर्ष, अम्, n. a hundred years, a cen-<BR>tury; (अस्, आ, अम्), possessing or lasting a hundred<BR>years, of a hundred years, a century old.<BR>—शत-<BR>वल्श, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a hundred branches.<BR>—शत-वाज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. containing a hundred<BR>forces, having excessive power or energy.<BR>—शत-<BR>वीर्या, f. ‘containing a hundred seeds,’ white-flower-<BR>ing Dūrvā or Panicum Dactylon; a kind of aspa-<BR>ragus (= शतावरी); a kind of vine (= कपिल-<BR>द्राक्षा).<BR>—शत-वृषभ, अस्, m. epithet of the<BR>twenty-third Muhūrta.<BR>—शत-वेधिन्, ई, m. ‘pierc-<BR>ing a hundred,’ a sort of dock or sorrel, Oxalis<BR>Monadelpha or Rumex Vesicarius.<BR>—शत-शस्, ind.<BR>by hundreds, in hundreds, a hundred-fold.<BR>—शत-<BR>शाख, अस्, आ, अम्, having a hundred branches,<BR>many-branching; multiform, various.<BR>—शतशाख-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of having a hundred branches,<BR>condition of being much increased.<BR>—शत-शार-<BR>दाय, ind., Ved. for a hundred autumns or years<BR>(= शत-संवत्सरार्थम्).<BR>—शत-शृङ्ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘hundred-horned,’ having a hundred peaks;<BR>epithet of part of the Himālaya range.<BR>—शत-श्लोकी,<BR>f., N. of a metrical version of the Brahma-sūtra<BR>according to the views of Madhu by Uttama-śloka-<BR>tīrtha.<BR>—शत-श्लोकी-चन्द्र-कला, f. ‘lunar digit of<BR>a hundred Ślokas,’ N. of a work on medicine by<BR>Vopa-deva.<BR>—शत-सङ्ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, numbering<BR>a hundred; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of deities in<BR>the tenth Manv-antara.<BR>—शत-सङ्घ-शस्, ind. in<BR>collections of a hundred, by hundreds.<BR>—शत-स-<BR>हस्र, अम्, n. a hundred thousand.<BR>—शतसहस्र-<BR>यान, अम्, n. a hundred thousand roads.<BR>—शतस-<BR>हस्र-शस्, ind. by hundreds of thousands, by myriads.<BR>—शत-सा, आस्, आस्, अम् (see rt. सन्), Ved. granting<BR>a hundred, bestowing hundreds, i. e. countless riches.<BR>—शतसाहस्र, अस्, ई, अम्, having or containing<BR>a hundred thousand, bought with or consisting of a<BR>hundred thousand, a hundred thousand-fold.<BR>—शत-<BR>सेय, अम्, n. (see rt. 1. सो), Ved. the effecting or<BR>obtaining of unbounded wealth, (Sāy. = अपरिमित-<BR>धन-पर्यवसान.)<BR>—शत-स्पृह्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>wished for by hundreds, excessively desired.<BR>—शत-<BR>स्विन्, ई, m., Ved. the possessor of hundreds, possess-<BR>ing great wealth.<BR>—शत-हायन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>containing or lasting for a hundred years.<BR>—शत-<BR>हिम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. lasting for a hundred winters,<BR>i. e. for innumerable years, (Sāy. = अपरिमित-काल.)<BR>—शत-ह्रदा, f. ‘containing a hundred rays of<BR>light,’ lightning; the thunderbolt; N. of one of the<BR>daughters of Dakṣa.<BR>—शत-ह्रादा, f. ‘possessing a<BR>hundred sounds,’ the thunderbolt.<BR>—शतांश (˚त-<BR>अं˚), अस्, m. a hundredth part.<BR>—शताक्ष (˚त-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, hundred-eyed; (ई), f. night; a sort<BR>of fennel, Anethum Sowa; the goddess Pārvatī.<BR>—शताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of<BR>a hundred or various members; (played upon) in a<BR>hundred or numerous ways (as by the nails, fingers,<BR>mouth, sticks, bows, &c., said of musical instru-<BR>ments); a particular tree, = तिनिश; (अम्), n. a car,<BR>chariot, carriage.<BR>—शतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ,<BR>Ved. containing a hundred forms, having numerous<BR>manifestations (said of Agni).<BR>—शताधिक (˚त-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, exceeding a hundred, more than<BR>a hundred.<BR>—शतानक (˚त-आन्˚), अम्, n. a place<BR>where dead bodies are burnt or buried, a burial-<BR>ground, cemetery.<BR>—शतानना (˚त-आन्˚), f. ‘hun-<BR>dred-faced,’ epithet of a goddess.<BR>—शतानन्द (˚त-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘delighting hundreds,’ epithet of<BR>Brahmā; of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; of the sage Go-<BR>tama or Gautama; of the eldest son of Gotama (the<BR>Purohita or family priest of king Janaka); the car<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शतानीक (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>taining or possessing a hundred hosts; (अस्), m. an<BR>old man; N. of a sovereign, (according to some,<BR>the second of the lunar dynasty in the fourth age;<BR>he was son and successor of Janam-ejaya, and father<BR>of Sahasrānīka); N. of the son of king Su-dāsa; of<BR>a sage (the pupil of Vyāsa); of the son of Nakula<BR>and Draupadī.<BR>—शताब्द (˚त-अब्˚), अम्, n. a hun-<BR>dred years, century.<BR>—शता-मघ, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">Page0991-a+ 75</a>]<BR>(शता for शत), Ved. possessing a hundred treasures<BR>or resources; (अस्), m. epithet of Indra; [cf. मघ-<BR>वन्.]<BR>—शतायुस् (˚त-आय्˚), उस्, उस्, उस्, lasting for a<BR>hundred years; (उस्), m. a man a hundred years old,<BR>an old man; N. of a son of Purū-ravas.<BR>—शतार (˚त-<BR>आर), अम्, n. ‘hundred-angled,’ the thunderbolt.<BR>—श-<BR>तारित्र (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a hundred<BR>oars, many-oared.<BR>—शतारुस् (˚त-अर्˚), उस्, उषी,<BR>n. f. ‘having a hundred sores,’ a leprous disease of<BR>the skin.<BR>—शतार्णा (˚त-अर्˚), f. a particular plant,<BR>Anethum Sowa.<BR>—शतावधान (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, m.<BR>epithet of Rāghavendra (= भट्टाचार्य-श्˚).<BR>—श-<BR>तावय (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. comprising or<BR>numbering a hundred sheep, (Sāy. अनेकैर् अविभिर्<BR>युक्त, Ṛg-veda V. 61, 5.)<BR>—शतावर (˚त-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a fine of a hundred (Paṇas &c.); (ई), f. the<BR>shrub Asparagus Racemosus; a kind of plant,<BR>zedoary (= शटी); N. of the wife of Indra.<BR>—शता-<BR>वर्त (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu, (see the<BR>next.)<BR>—शतावर्तिन् (˚त-आव्˚), ई, m. ‘revolving in<BR>a hundred ways,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शताश्रि (˚त-अश्˚),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a hundred angles or edges<BR>(said of Indra's thunderbolt).<BR>—शताह्वा (˚त-आह्˚),<BR>f. a sort of dill or fennel, Anethum Sowa; another<BR>plant (= शतावरी).<BR>—शतेन्द्रिया (˚त-इन्˚), f. ‘hav-<BR>ing a hundred senses,’ a proper N.<BR>—शतेश (˚त-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of a hundred,’ the ruler or head<BR>man of a hundred (villages).<BR>—शतेषुधि (˚त-इष्˚),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. hundred-quivered, having a hundred<BR>quivers (said of Rudra).<BR>—शतोति (˚त-ऊति), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. protecting hundreds, granting great protection,<BR>resorted to by hundreds, (Sāy. = बहु-रक्षक<BR>or बहु-गमन, Ṛg-veda VI. 63, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतक|शतकः
शतक, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing or containing a<BR>hundred, a hundred; (अम्), n. a hundred (collec-<BR>tively), any collection of a hundred; a century; a<BR>cento, collection of one hundred stanzas, &c.; [cf.<BR>वैराग्य-श्˚, अमरु-श्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिक|शतिकः
शतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to a<BR>hundred; doing or effecting anything with a hun-<BR>dred; bearing tax or interest per hundred; bought<BR>with a hundred; changed with or for a hundred;<BR>indicative of a hundred, &c. (e. g. the throbbing of<BR>the right eye is a शतिकं निमित्तम् or omen indi-<BR>cating the acquisition of a hundred pieces of money<BR>or other property supposed to come from the favour<BR>of Kuvera, lord of wealth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिन्
शतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, consisting of hundreds, hundred-<BR>fold, numerous, manifold; (ई), m. one who is pos-<BR>sessed of a hundred, the owner of a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्य|शत्यः
शत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, bought with a hundred, &c.<BR>See शतिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोन|शतपोनः
शतपोन शतपोन, अस्, m. a sieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोनक|शतपोनकः
शतपोनक, अस्, m. fistula in ano with many<BR>external openings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोरक
शतपोरक शतपोरक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतरुद्रिय|शतरुद्रियं
शतरुद्रिय शत-रुद्रिय. See p. 990, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शताक्ष
शताक्ष शताक्ष, शताङ्ग, &c. See p. 990.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतृ
शतृ शतृ, a technical term for the Kṛt<BR>affix अत् used in forming present participles of the<BR>Parasmai-pada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतेर|शतेरः
शतेर शतेर, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 61. fr. rt. शद्; cf. शत्रु), an enemy; injury,<BR>detriment, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतोति
शतोति शतोति. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्त्रि
शत्त्रि शत्त्रि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 67. fr. rt. शद्; cf. शद्रि), an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रि|शत्त्रिः
शत्रि शत्रि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a Rājarṣi;<BR>[cf. शत्त्रि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रु|शत्रुः
शत्रु शत्रु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 103. fr. rt. शद्, and therefore perhaps more<BR>correctly written शत्त्रु, cf. शातक), one who<BR>causes to fall or perish, a destroyer, overthrower,<BR>conqueror; an enemy, foe, adversary; an antagonist,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">Page0991-b+ 80</a>]<BR>a political rival or hostile neighbouring king; [cf.<BR>Gr. ἔχθος, ἐκθρός, ὀχθέω; Lat. hod in odisse,<BR>hostis; Goth. hats; Angl. Sax. hate, hete.]<BR>—श-<BR>त्रुं-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing or patient with an<BR>enemy.<BR>—शत्रु-कर्षण, अस्, ई, अम्, overpower-<BR>ing enemies.<BR>—शत्रु-घात, अस्, आ, अम्, killing an<BR>enemy.<BR>—शत्रु-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, foe-killing, de-<BR>stroying enemies; (अस्), m., N. of one of Rāma-<BR>candra's brothers, (he was son of Su-mitrā and twin<BR>brother of Lakṣmaṇa, and was the chosen com-<BR>panion of Bharata, son of Kaikeyī, as Lakṣmaṇa<BR>was of Rāma, son of Kauśalyā, these three being<BR>the wives of Daśa-ratha.)<BR>—शत्रुघ्न-जननी, f.<BR>the mother of Śatru-ghna, i. e. Su-mitrā.<BR>—शत्रु-<BR>जित्, त्, त्, त्, foe-conquering; (त्), m., N. of a king<BR>(father of Ṛta-dhvaja or Kuvalayāśva).<BR>—शत्रुञ्-<BR>जय, अस्, आ, अम्, foe-conquering, subduing an<BR>enemy; (अस्), m. an elephant; N. of the mountain<BR>Vimala or Girnar in Gujarāt, (see विमलाद्रि); a<BR>proper N.<BR>—शत्रु-तस्, ind. from an enemy or<BR>enemies.<BR>—शत्रु-ता, f. or शत्रु-त्व, अम्, n. hos-<BR>tility, enmity.<BR>—शत्रु-दमन, अस्, ई, अम्, sub-<BR>duing enemies.<BR>—शत्रु-निकाय, अस्, m. a number<BR>of foes, host of enemies.<BR>—शत्रु-निबर्हण, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, foe-destroying, destroying enemies (Rāmāyaṇa<BR>I. 1, 11).<BR>—शत्रु-निलय, अस्, m. the dwelling of<BR>a foe.<BR>—शत्रुन्-तप, अस्, आ, अम्, foe-paining, sub-<BR>duing or destroying enemies.<BR>—शत्रु-पक्ष, अस्,<BR>m. the side or part of an enemy, a disaffected person,<BR>an antagonist, opponent, enemy.<BR>—शत्रु-बाधक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, harassing or distressing an enemy.<BR>—शत्रु-मर्दन, अस्, m. ‘foe-crusher,’ epithet of<BR>Śatru-ghna (brother of Rāma).<BR>—शत्रु-लाव, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, cutting an enemy to pieces, killing foes.<BR>—शत्रु-वत्, ind. like an enemy.<BR>—शत्रु-विग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. ‘foe-war,’ war of enemies, hostile invasion.<BR>—श-<BR>त्रु-विनाशन, अस्, m. ‘destroyer of foes,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—शत्रु-सम्मुखम्, ind. facing the enemy, in<BR>front of the enemy.<BR>—शत्रु-सह or शत्रु-साह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, sustaining the shock of a foe, enduring<BR>an enemy.<BR>—शत्रु-सेविन्, ई, इनी, इ, serving an<BR>enemy, being in the service of a hostile prince<BR>(Manu VII. 186).<BR>—शत्रु-हत्या, f. foe-slaughter,<BR>hosticide.<BR>—शत्रु-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, foe-slaying, a<BR>foe-slayer.<BR>—शत्रूपजाप (˚र-उप्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>treacherous whisperings of an enemy.<BR>—शत्रूप-<BR>जाप-दूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, corrupted or demoralized<BR>by an enemy's treachery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुय
शत्रुय, Nom. P., Ved. शत्रुयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>be an enemy, be hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रूयत्
शत्रूयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (Ved. for शत्रुयत्), one<BR>who is hostile or an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्वरी
शत्वरी शत्वरी, f. (said to be fr. rt. शद्; ac-<BR>cording to others fr. rt. 1. शम्; cf. शमनी), night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्
शद् शद्, cl. 1. or 6. A. (and P. in non-<BR>conjugational tenses, see Pāṇ. I. 3, 60),<BR>शीयते, शशाद (in Ṛg-veda I. 141, 9. there is a<BR>form शाशद्रे = शातयति or तीक्ष्णी-क्रियन्ते;<BR>other forms शाशद्महे, शाशदुः), शत्स्यति, अश-<BR>दत्, Cond. अशत्स्यत्, शत्तुम्, to fall, perish, perish<BR>gradually, wither, decay; to go: Caus. शातयति,<BR>-यितुम् (perhaps a kind of Nom., connected with<BR>शात fr. rt. शो), to cause to fall, fell, throw down,<BR>overthrow, destroy, slay, kill; शादयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to go, impel, drive on: Desid. शिशत्सति:<BR>Intens. शाशद्यते, शाशत्ति, to slay, kill, injure, hurt;<BR>[cf. Lat. cad-o.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद|शदः
शद, अस्, m. any edible vegetable product (as<BR>fruit, a root, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रि|शद्रिः
शद्रि, इस्, m. a cloud; an elephant; an epithet of<BR>Arjuna; (इस्), f. lightning; clayed or candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रु|शद्रुः
शद्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, falling, perishing, wasting, de-<BR>caying; going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्न
शन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen, decayed, withered; (this<BR>appears to be the regular past pass. part. fr. rt. शद्,<BR>but some authorities do not give it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाशदान
शाशदान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. doing injury, injuring,<BR>(Sāy. = हिंसत्, but in Ṛg-veda I. 123, 10. शाशदाना<BR>= शाशाद्यमाना = स्पष्टतां गच्छन्ती, going<BR>to manifestation, being manifested.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीयमान
शीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, perishing, decaying, wither-<BR>ing, fading away, departing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकावलि|शनकावलिः
शनकावलि शनकावलि, इस्, m. a particular<BR>shrub (= गज-पिप्पली; according to some शन-<BR>कावली, f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकैस्
शनकैस् शनकैस्, ind. See under शनैस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनपर्णी
शनपर्णी शन-पर्णी, f. (for शण-पर्णी?),<BR>the medicinal plant Wrightia Antidysenterica (= क-<BR>टुकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनि|शनिः
शनि शनि, इस्, m. (probably connected with<BR>शनैस् below), ‘slow-moving’ [cf. मन्द], the planet<BR>Saturn or its regent (fabled as the offspring of the<BR>Sun; he is represented as of a black colour or dressed<BR>in dark-coloured clothes; cf. नील-वासस्); N. of Śiva;<BR>of a son of Atri (according to the Vāyu-Purāṇa).<BR>—शनि-<BR>चक्र, अम्, n. an astrological diagram in the form<BR>of a man used to foretell good or bad fortune, (it is<BR>marked with twenty-seven compartments to repre-<BR>sent the Nakṣatras passed through by the planet<BR>Saturn.)<BR>—शनि-ज, अम्, n. ‘Saturn-produced,’ black<BR>pepper.<BR>—शनि-प्रदोष, अस्, m. a term for the<BR>worship performed to Śiva on the thirteenth day of<BR>the waxing or waning moon when it falls on a<BR>Saturday.<BR>—शनि-प्रसू, ऊस्, f. ‘mother of Saturn,’<BR>epithet of Chāyā, wife of the Sun.<BR>—शनि-प्रिय,<BR>अम्, n. ‘dear to Saturn,’ a dark-coloured stone, the<BR>emerald or sapphire (= नील-मणि).<BR>—शनि-वार<BR>or शनि-वासर, अस्, m. Saturn's day, Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैस्
शनैस् शनैस्, ind. (according to some per-<BR>haps for शम्नैस्, inst. pl. of an old part. of rt.<BR>1. शम्), quietly, slowly, tardily, sluggishly, stealthily;<BR>softly, mildly; gradually, by degrees, successively,<BR>little by little, step by step; independantly, (शनैः<BR>शनैः, very quietly, little by little, very slowly or<BR>softly or gently, step by step.)<BR>—शनैश्-चर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘slow-going,’ the planet Saturn or its regent, (a<BR>hymn of praise to Saturn, called the शनैश्चरस्य<BR>स्तोत्रम्, is said to have been composed by Vyāsa.)<BR>—शनैश्चर-संवत्सर, अस्, m. the year of<BR>Saturn (during which this planet completes his course<BR>through the twenty-eight Nakṣatras; in modern<BR>astronomy = thirty of our years).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकैस्
शनकैस्, ind. quietly, softly, gently, mildly,<BR>slowly, gradually, by degress, step by step, in every<BR>case that arises, with alternations, alternately.<BR>—श-<BR>नकैश्-चर, अस्, m. = शनैश्-चर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्त
शन्त शन्त, शन्ति, &c. See under rt. 1. शम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्तनु|शंतनु|शंतनुः|शन्तनुः
शन्तनु शन्तनु, उस्, m., N. of the younger<BR>brother of Devāpi (said to have usurped the sovereignty<BR>whilst his elder brother became a hermit); N. of a<BR>commentator; [cf. शान्तनवी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्न
शन्न शन्न. See under rt. शद्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् 1. शप्, a technical term, used by Pā-<BR>ṇini for the Vi-karaṇa अ, inserted between the root<BR>and terminations of the conjugational tenses in the<BR>1st class, &c. See वि-करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् 2. शप्, ind. a particle and prefix im-<BR>plying assent or acceptance, as in शप्-करोति, he<BR>admits or accepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् 3. शप्, cl. 1. 4. P. A. शपति, -ते,<BR>शप्यति, -ते, शशाप, शेपे, शप्स्यति, -ते,<BR>अशाप्सीत्, अशप्त, शप्तुम् (according to some per-<BR>haps originally ‘to cry aloud’), to curse, imprecate<BR>evil, execrate; to revile, scold, blame (with dat.);<BR>to take an oath, swear, promise or asseverate by<BR>oath: Caus. शापयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशीशपत्, to<BR>cause or order to swear (with inst. of object by which<BR>one is sworn); to conjure: Desid. शिशप्सति, -ते: In-<BR>tens. शाशप्यते (according to Vopa-deva XX. 8. also<BR>शंशप्यते), शाशप्ति; [cf. perhaps Gr. κόμπος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप|शपः
शप, अस्, m. an imprecation, curse, cursing; an<BR>oath; a corpse, (for शव, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपत्
शपत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, cursing, reviling, swearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथ|शपथः
शपथ, अस्, m. cursing, imprecating; an impre-<BR>cation, curse, anathema; an oath, administering an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">Page0992-a+ 79</a>]<BR>oath, swearing, asseveration by oath or ordeal; con-<BR>juration.<BR>—शपथ-पत्त्र, अम्, n. written testi-<BR>mony on oath, an affidavit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपन|शपनं
शपन, अम्, n. the act of imprecation, cursing,<BR>malediction; reviling, abuse; an oath, asseveration by<BR>oath or ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपमान
शपमान, अस्, आ, अम्, cursing, reviling, impre-<BR>cating, swearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्त|शप्तः
शप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cursed, reviled, abused, anathe-<BR>matized; sworn, taken as an oath; (अस्), m. a sort<BR>of grass, Saccharum Cylindricum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्त्वा
शप्त्वा, ind. having cursed or reviled, having sworn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफ|शफं|शफः
शफ शफ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (etymology doubt-<BR>ful), a hoof (in general); the hoof of a horse; the<BR>root of a tree; [cf. Old Germ. huof; Old Norse<BR>and Angl. Sax. hôf; Germ. hûf; Engl. hoof.]<BR>—शफ-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fallen from the<BR>hoofs.<BR>—१. शफ-वत्, ind. like a hoof.<BR>—२. शफ-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of hoofs; (अत्), n.<BR>any hoofed animal.<BR>—शफा-रुज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>breaking or destroying with the hoof; epithet of<BR>a kind of demon.<BR>—शफोरु (˚फ-ऊरु), ऊस्, f. a<BR>woman whose thighs resemble the two divisions of<BR>a cow's hoof, (see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 70.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफर|शफरः
शफर, अस्, ई, m. f. (also written सफर), a<BR>kind of carp; a kind of small glittering fish, Cyprius<BR>Sophore.<BR>—शफराधिप (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of Śaphara fish,’ the Ilisha or Hilsa fish, Ilisha<BR>Clupanodon (= इलीश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबर|शबरः
शबर शबर, अस्, m. = शवर, q. v., N.<BR>of a wild mountaineer tribe; N. of the author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 169 (having the patronymic<BR>Kākṣīvata); epithet of a Buddhist.<BR>—शबर-<BR>भाष्य, अम्, n. Śabara's commentary on the Mī-<BR>māṃsā-sūtra.<BR>—शबर-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a king<BR>(mentioned in the Kathārṇava).<BR>—शबर-स्वामिन्,<BR>ई, m., N. of the author of a Bhāṣya or commentary<BR>on the Mīmāṃsā-sūtras of Jaimini, (this Bhāṣya<BR>has been critically annotated by the great Mīmāṃsā<BR>authority Kumārila.)<BR>—शबरालय (˚र-आल्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the abode of savage tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबल|शबलः
शबल शबल, अस्, आ, अम् (see शवल), varie-<BR>gated, brindled; (ई), f. a spotted cow; Kāma-<BR>dhenu the cow of plenty (identified with the varying<BR>powers of nature).<BR>—शबली-होम, अस्, m. an offering<BR>to the cow Śabalī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द्
शब्द् शब्द्, cl. 10. P. (more properly to<BR>be regarded as a Nom. fr. शब्द below),<BR>शब्दयति (sometimes also A. शब्दायते, Pāṇ. III.<BR>1, 17, but see शब्दाय, शब्दायमान), -यितुम्,<BR>to sound, make any noise or sound; to utter any<BR>sound or cry, call out, call, speak; शब्दापयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to address, speak to: Pass. शब्द्यते, to be<BR>sounded, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द|शब्दः
शब्द, अस्, m. (in the Upaniṣads also अम्, n.;<BR>thought by some to be connected with rt. 3. शप् +<BR>2. द), sound, noise; a sound; a word, significant<BR>word; (in gram.) a declinable word (as a noun,<BR>pronoun, &c.); grammar; verbal communication,<BR>oral evidence, verbal authority (as one of the Pra-<BR>māṇas, see प्र-माण).<BR>—शब्द-कार, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>making noise or sound, sounding, sonorous.<BR>—शब्द-<BR>कोष, अस्, m. ‘word-repository,’ a dictionary, voca-<BR>bulary.<BR>—शब्द-कौस्तुभ, ‘word-jewel,’ N. of<BR>a commentary by Bhaṭṭoji on the Mahā-bhāṣya.<BR>—शब्द-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, being or residing in a<BR>word (as a poetical or metaphorical meaning).<BR>—शब्द-गुण, अस्, m. the quality of sound; a<BR>particular quality or style of speech.<BR>—शब्द-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. perceiving or catching sound; the ear; a<BR>fabulous arrow.<BR>—शब्द-ग्राम, अस्, m. the compass<BR>or range of sound.<BR>—शब्द-चन्द्रिका, f. ‘elucidation<BR>of words,’ N. of a lexicon by Cakra-pāṇi-datta.<BR>—शब्द-चातुर्य, अम्, n. skill in words, cleverness<BR>of diction, eloquence.<BR>—शब्द-चित्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>various or fanciful in sound (as poetry).<BR>—शब्द-<BR>चोर, अस्, m. ‘word-thief,’ a plagiarist.<BR>—शब्द-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, arising from sound, produced by words,<BR>by verbal communication.<BR>—शब्द-तन्मात्र, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-b" target="_blank">Page0992-b+ 81</a>]<BR>n. the subtile element of sound.<BR>—शब्द-नित्यत्व,<BR>अम्, n. the eternity of sound.<BR>—शब्द-निर्णय,<BR>अस्, m. ‘word-investigation,’ N. of a work by Vāca-<BR>spati-miśra.<BR>—शब्द-पति, इस्, m. ‘word-lord,’ a<BR>mere nominal sovereign, (according to Malli-nātha<BR>शब्दत एव पतिर् न त्व् अर्थतः, Raghu-v. VIII.<BR>51.)<BR>—शब्द-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, flying with a sound,<BR>making a noise in flight (said of an arrow); falling<BR>with a sound.<BR>—शब्द-प्रमाण, अम्, n. verbal<BR>testimony or proof, oral evidence.<BR>—शब्द-प्राछ्,<BR>ट्, ट्, ट्, enquiring after (the meaning of) a word.<BR>—शब्द-बोध, अस्, m. (in phil.) knowledge (de-<BR>rived) from verbal testimony.<BR>—शब्द-ब्रह्मन्, अ,<BR>n. ‘word-spirit,’ i. e. the Veda considered as a revealed<BR>word or sound and identified with Brahman, the<BR>Supreme Spirit.<BR>—शब्द-भेद, अस्, m. difference<BR>or distinction of sound.<BR>—शब्द-भेद-प्रकाश,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an appendix to the Viśva-prakāśa (con-<BR>taining a list of words similar in sound but different<BR>in meaning).<BR>—शब्द-भेदिन्, ई, m. ‘sound-piercer,’<BR>epithet of Arjuna [cf. शब्द-वेधिन्]; the anus; a<BR>particular fabulous arrow (which pierces an object<BR>the sound of which only is heard).<BR>—शब्द-मात्र,<BR>अम्, n. sound only, a mere sound.<BR>—शब्द-माला, f.<BR>‘a collection of words,’ N. of a lexicon by Rāme-<BR>śvara-śarman.<BR>—शब्द-योनि, इस्, f. ‘word-source,’<BR>the source or origin of a word, a radical word, root.<BR>—शब्द-रत्न, अम्, n. ‘word-jewel,’ N. of a<BR>lexicon.<BR>—शब्द-रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘mine of word-gems,’ N. of a dictionary of syno-<BR>nyms by Mahīpa.<BR>—शब्द-रत्नावली (˚न-आव्˚), f.<BR>‘word-necklace,’ N. of a lexicon of synonyms by<BR>Mathureśa.<BR>—शब्द-लिङ्गार्थ-चन्द्रिका (˚ग-<BR>अर्˚), f. ‘elucidation of the gender and meaning of<BR>words,’ N. of a lexicon.<BR>—शब्द-विरोध, अस्, m.<BR>opposition of words in a sentence.<BR>—शब्द-विशेष,<BR>अस्, m. difference or variety of sound; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the varieties of sound, (these the Sāṅkhya arranges<BR>according to the accents उदात्त, अन्-उदात्त, स्व-<BR>रित, and the notes of the gamut, as षड्ज,<BR>ऋषभ, गान्धार, मध्यम, पञ्चम,<BR>धैवत, निषाद, &c., q. q. v. v.)<BR>—शब्द-विशे-<BR>षण, अम्, n. (in grammar) the attribute of a word,<BR>an adjective.<BR>—शब्द-वृत्ति, इस्, f. (in rhetoric) the<BR>function of a word.<BR>—शब्दवेधि-त्व, अम्, n. capa-<BR>bility of piercing (an invisible object) the sound (of<BR>which only is heard).<BR>—शब्द-वेधिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>sound-piercing, piercing or terrifying enemies by<BR>mere shouts; (ई), m. an archer who can pierce an<BR>invisible object the sound of which only is heard; a<BR>warrior who pierces his enemies by mere shouts;<BR>epithet of Arjuna; of king Daśa-ratha.<BR>—शब्द-<BR>वैलक्षण्य, अम्, n. difference in word, verbal<BR>difference (as opposed to अर्थ-वैलक्षण्य or<BR>real difference).<BR>—शब्द-शक्ति, इस्, f. the force or<BR>signification of a word.<BR>—शब्द-शब्दार्थ-मञ्-<BR>जूषा (˚द-अर्˚), f. ‘a collection of words and their<BR>meanings,’ N. of a lexicon.<BR>—शब्द-शासन, अम्, n.<BR>a rule or law of grammar.<BR>—शब्द-शास्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. ‘science of words,’ rules of grammar, any gram-<BR>matical treatise, grammar, philology.<BR>—शब्द-शुद्-<BR>धि, इस्, f. purity or accuracy of language, correct use<BR>of words.<BR>—शब्द-श्लेष, अस्, m. play upon words,<BR>verbal equivoque, a rhetorical ornament by which<BR>the same words are used in different senses, punning.<BR>—शब्द-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. a collection of words,<BR>vocabulary, lexicon.<BR>—शब्द-सिद्धि, इस्, f. ‘the<BR>complete use of words,’ a section of the Kāvya-kalpa-<BR>latā-vṛtti-parimala.<BR>—शब्दाडम्बर (˚द-आड्˚),<BR>अस्, m. high-sounding words, verbosity, confusion of<BR>words, bombast.<BR>—शब्दातीत (˚द-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>beyond the reach of sound (used as an epithet of<BR>the deity).<BR>—शब्दादि (˚द-आदि), इस्, m., scil. वि-<BR>षय, the objects of sense beginning with sound,<BR>(these are शब्द, sound; स्पर्श, tangibility; रूप,<BR>form; रस, savour; गन्ध, odour; see विषय.)<BR>—शब्दादि-धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having the quality<BR>of sound, &c., (see विषय.)<BR>—शब्दाधिष्ठान<BR>(˚द-अध्˚), अम्, n. ‘receptacle of sound,’ the ear.<BR>—शब्दाध्याहार (˚द-अध्˚), अस्, m. the supply-<BR>ing of a word (to complete an ellipsis).<BR>—शब्दानु-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">Page0992-c+ 79</a>]<BR>रूप (˚द-अन्˚), अम्, n. conformity to sound, imita-<BR>tion of sound.<BR>—शब्दानुशासन (˚द-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘word-instruction, word explanation,’ the giving<BR>rules for words (used as a title of Pāṇini's grammar);<BR>N. of a grammatical work by Abhinava-śākaṭāyana;<BR>of a work on grammar by Hema-candra.<BR>—शब्दाब्-<BR>धि (˚द-अब्˚), इस्, m. ‘ocean of words,’ N. of a<BR>lexicon (compiled by order of Prāṇa-kṛṣṇa).<BR>—शब्-<BR>दार्णव (˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘ocean of words,’ N. of<BR>a lexicon.<BR>—शब्दार्थ (˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m. the sense<BR>or meaning of a word; (औ), m. du. a word and<BR>its sense.<BR>—शब्दार्थ-कल्पतरु, उस्, m. ‘Kalpa-<BR>tree of the meaning of words,’ N. of a lexicon by<BR>Veṅkaṭa.<BR>—शब्दालङ्कार (˚द-अल्˚), अस्, m. verbal<BR>ornament, rhetorical use of words (as alliteration<BR>&c.).<BR>—शब्दालोक-रहस्य and शब्दालोक-विवेक<BR>(˚द-आल्˚), N. of two philosophical commentaries.<BR>—शब्देन्दु-शेखर (˚द-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work by Nāgeśa-bhaṭṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दन|शब्दनः
शब्दन, अम्, n. the act of making a sound,<BR>uttering sounds, making a noise; a sound, noise;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), sounding, sonorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दयत्
शब्दयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, making a sound, sound-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाय
शब्दाय [cf. rt. शब्द् above], Nom. A. शब्दा-<BR>यते, -यितुम्, to make a noise, sound, cry; to bray:<BR>Caus. शब्दाययति, -यितुम्, to cause to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दायमान
शब्दायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding, making a<BR>noise, crying out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दित
शब्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, made to give out<BR>a sound (as a musical instrument &c.); uttered,<BR>articulated; called; explained; made public or<BR>manifest; converted into a noun; (अम्), n. noise,<BR>cry, the braying (of an ass).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम् 1. शम्, cl. 4. P. शाम्यति, शशाम,<BR>शमिष्यति, अशमत्, (the form शश-<BR>मते = शाम्यति or स्तौति, Ṛg-veda VI. 2, 4),<BR>शमितुम् (originally ‘to become tired’), to be ap-<BR>peased, grow calm, become pacified, be satisfied,<BR>become quiet or tranquil, be undisturbed or quies-<BR>cent; to cease, stop, leave off, desist; to pacify,<BR>cause to cease, put an end to, destroy, kill, sacrifice,<BR>(in these transitive senses also cl. 9. P. शम्नाति,<BR>according to Naigh. II. 19, and probably in some<BR>cases the forms used are referrible to Caus.); cl. 10.<BR>A. शामयते, -यितुम्, to look at, inspect; to show,<BR>display: Pass. शाम्यते, शम्यते (referrible also to<BR>Caus.), Aor. अशमि or अशामि, to be appeased or<BR>quieted, &c.: Caus. शमयति or शामयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. असीशमत्, to appease, allay, pacify, calm,<BR>tranquillize, soothe, settle; to console; to cause to<BR>cease, stop, suppress, extinguish, destroy; to remove,<BR>avert; to tame, subdue, defeat, conquer; to leave off,<BR>desist, (शमयाम्-बभूवुः, they desisted): Desid.<BR>शिशमिषति: Intens. शंशम्यते, शंशन्ति, to be<BR>entirely appeased, become tranquil; to cease; [cf. Gr.<BR>κάμνω, αιδηρο-κμής, κημός: Old Germ. chamo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्त
शन्त(= शान्त?), see Vopa-deva VII. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्ति
शन्ति(= शान्ति?), see Vopa-deva VII. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्तु
शन्तु, see Vopa-deva VII. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम|शमः
शम, अस्, m. quiet, tranquillity, rest, calm, peace;<BR>quietude, quietism, quiet of mind, restraint of the<BR>organs of sense, indifference to objects of sense,<BR>absence of passion (especially as a characteristic of<BR>the Vedāntin), abstract meditation on Brahma,<BR>stoicism; final happiness, emancipation from all the<BR>illusions of existence (= विक्षेप-कर्मोपरम);<BR>Quietism or Tranquillity (personified as a son of<BR>Dharma); allayment (of pain), alleviation or cure<BR>(of disease), convalescence^1; the hand; imprecation,<BR>malediction (for शप ?).<BR>—शम-पर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>devoted to quiet, calm, tranquil.<BR>—शम-स्थ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, engaged in quietism.<BR>—शमाङ्ग (˚म-<BR>अङ्˚), N. of a particular Agra-hāra or royal grant of<BR>land for Brāhmans.<BR>—शमान्तक (˚म-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘destroyer of tranquillity,’ epithet of Kāma (god<BR>of love).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमक|शमकः
शमक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, pacifying, tranquillizing,<BR>consolatory; a pacifier, tranquillizer, pacificator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमथ|शमथः
शमथ, अस्, m. quiet, tranquillity, calmness of<BR>mind, absence of passion; a counsellor, minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमन|शमनं|शमनः
शमन, अम्, n. the act of appeasing, allaying,<BR>tranquillizing, soothing, consoling, calming, suppress-<BR>ing, &c.; tranquillity, calmness, indifference; cessa-<BR>tion, termination, end, destruction, (शमनं या,<BR>to go to annihilation, be destroyed); hurting, injur-<BR>ing, injury; killing (animals for sacrifice), immola-<BR>tion; a mode of rinsing the mouth; swallowing,<BR>chewing; malediction, reviling, (for शपन ?); (अस्),<BR>m. ‘the settler or destroyer,’ epithet of Yama; an<BR>antelope; (ई), f. night.<BR>—शमन-स्वसृ, सा, f.<BR>‘Yama's sister,’ the river Yamunā or Jumnā.<BR>—श-<BR>मनी-षद, अस्, m. ‘night-goer,’ a Rākṣasa, evil<BR>spirit, demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनीय
शमनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be appeased or tran-<BR>quillized, consolable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमयत्
शमयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, appeasing, allaying;<BR>terminating, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमल|शमलं
शमल, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 111.<BR>fr. rt. 1. शम् above), feculent matter, sediment,<BR>feces, ordure; impurity; sin; calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमि|शमिः
1. शमि, इस्, f. a legume, pod; the Śamī tree [cf.<BR>शमी].<BR>—शमि-रोह, अस्, m. ‘ascending the Śamī<BR>tree,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमित|शमितः
शमित, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. शान्त], appeased, al-<BR>layed, calmed, stilled, tranquillized, pacified, calm,<BR>quiet, tranquil, sedate; alleviated, relieved, cured;<BR>tempered, moderated; relaxed, intermitted.<BR>—श-<BR>मित-रुचि, इस्, इस्, इ, whose lustre is moderated or<BR>dimmed.<BR>—शमितायाम (˚त-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the length diminished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमितव्य
शमितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = शमनीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमितृ
शमितृ, ता, m., Ved. ‘a settler, silencer,’ a killer,<BR>slaughterer (of a sacrificial victim).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमित्वा
शमित्वा, ind. having become tranquillized or<BR>calmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिन्
शमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, calm, tranquil, appeased, tran-<BR>quillized, pacific; (ई), m., N. of a son of Śūra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिर|शमिरः
शमिर, अस्, m. a small variety of the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिष्यत्
शमिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to appease<BR>or tranquillize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमी
शमी, f. (sometimes shortened into शमि, q. v.),<BR>a rite, sacrificial rite (Ved., according to Naigh. II.<BR>1. and Sāy. = कर्म); a legume, pod; the Śamī<BR>tree, Acacia Suma (possessing a very tough and hard<BR>wood supposed to contain fire, [cf. Manu VIII. 247,<BR>Raghu-vaṃśa III. 9]; it was employed to kindle<BR>the sacred fire by rubbing two dried pieces together,<BR>and a legend relates that Purū-ravas generated pri-<BR>meval fire by the friction of two branches of the Śamī<BR>and Aśvattha trees); the shrub Serratula Anthel-<BR>mintica (= वागुजी).<BR>—शमी-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>the Śamī tree as its place of origin, produced from<BR>the Śamī tree,’ epithet of Agni or fire; a Brāhman<BR>or man of the sacerdotal class.<BR>—शमी-धान्य, अम्,<BR>n. ‘pod-grain’ any pulse or grain growing in pods.<BR>—शमी-पत्त्री, f. ‘having Śamī leaves,’ a kind of<BR>sensitive plant, Mimosa Pudica.<BR>—शमी-मन्दार-<BR>माहात्म्य, अम्, n. ‘glorification of the Śamī and<BR>Mandāra trees,’ N. of the thirty-seventh chapter of<BR>the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीक|शमीकः
शमीक, अस्, m., N. of a Muni (son of Śūra and<BR>brother of Vasu-deva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीर|शमीरः
शमीर, अस्, m. = शमिर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्य
शम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be appeased, to be kept<BR>quiet, &c.; (आ), f. a wooden stick or post (as quiet-<BR>ing or making firm); a staff; the pin of a yoke;<BR>a kind of cymbal or other musical instrument held<BR>in the right hand (= ताल-विशेष); a sacrificial<BR>vessel.<BR>—शम्या-पात, अस्, m. the cast of a stick, i. e.<BR>the distance that a stick can be thrown.<BR>—शम्या-<BR>मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. having the measure of a<BR>Śamyā, as large as the pin of a yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त|शांत|शान्तं|शान्तः
शान्त, शान्त्वा, &c. See s. v., p. 1000.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्यत्
शाम्यत्, &c. See under शाम, p. 1001.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम् 2. शम्, ind. (perhaps to be connected<BR>with rt. 1. शम्, but also referrible to 2. श), happi-<BR>ness, welfare, prosperity, blessing, beatitude, health,<BR>hail, (according to Pāṇ. II. 3, 73. with dat. or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">Page0993-b+ 78</a>]<BR>gen., e. g. शं देवदत्ताय or शं देवदत्तस्य,<BR>hail to Devadatta); happy, auspicious, pleasant, sweet,<BR>kind, agreeable; happily, auspiciously, well; (used in<BR>the Veda as a subst., adj., and adv.; frequently found<BR>in the phrase शं योस् or शं च योश् च, ‘prosperity<BR>and succour,’ or ‘blessing and protection,’ Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 114, 2, II. 33, 13, &c., cf. योस्; sometimes<BR>joined with the verbs भू, अस्, कृ, या, &c., and<BR>sometimes occurring without any verb, e. g. शं नो<BR>भवत्व् अर्यमा, may Aryaman be kind or pro-<BR>pitious to us; सोमः शम् अस्तु ते हृदे, may the<BR>Soma be agreeable to thy heart; शं नः करतो<BR>अश्विना, may the two Aśvins do us good; शं याति,<BR>he attains happiness or becomes prosperous; शं<BR>तद् अस्मै, that is pleasant to him.)<BR>—शं-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, containing the word शम्.<BR>—शं-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or शं-स्था, आस्, आस्, अम्, being in pros-<BR>perity, happy, prosperous, faring well.<BR>—शं-कर,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing happiness, &c. = शङ्-<BR>कर, p. 988, col. 1.<BR>—शं-गय, अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, Ved. having a pleasant house, happily domiciled,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda IX. 97, 17. the fem. शं-गयीम् occurs.)<BR>—शं-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most happy, very<BR>fortunate, most pleasant or auspicious.<BR>—शं-ताति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. causing happiness, auspicious, (Sāy. =<BR>शान्ति-कर, Ṛg-veda VIII. 18, 7); (इस्), f., Ved.<BR>happiness, prosperity.<BR>—शम्-पाक, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of Cassia, Cassia Fistula (= आरग्-बध); lac, the<BR>red dye (= यावक); bringing to maturity or ripe-<BR>ness, cooking, maturing, (probably for सम्-पाक.)<BR>—शम्-पात, अस्, m. Cassia Fistula.<BR>—शम्-भवि-<BR>ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being greatly for happiness<BR>or welfare, granting much happiness or beatitude.<BR>—शम्-भु, उस्, उस्, उ, being for happiness or wel-<BR>fare, granting or causing happiness; (उस्), m., N. of<BR>a Vedic deity, (Sāy. = सुखस्य भावयिता, Ṛg-<BR>veda VII. 35, 10); N. of Śiva; of Brahmā; a sage,<BR>venerable man; a Jina or Jaina sanctified teacher;<BR>a particular semi-divine being (= सिद्ध); N. of<BR>one of the eleven Rudras (according to the Viṣṇu-<BR>Purāṇa); N. of an author; (उस्), f., N. of a wife of<BR>Dhruva.<BR>—शम्भु-तनय or शम्भु-नन्दन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘son of Śiva,’ an epithet of Kārttikeya; of<BR>Gaṇeśa.<BR>—शम्भु-नाथ, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—शम्भु-प्रिया, f. ‘dear to Śiva,’ an epithet of<BR>Durgā; Emblic Myrobalan.<BR>—शम्भु-रहस्य, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—शम्भु-वल्लभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>beloved by Śiva; (अम्), n. the white lotus.<BR>—शम्-<BR>भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, auspicious (Ved.); (ऊस्), m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—शम्भू-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Kāla-jñāna and of the Vaidyaka-sāra-saṅgraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु, उस्, उस्, उ, happy, prosperous, fortunate<BR>(= सुखयु, Nirukta IV. 2); (उस्), m. a sort of<BR>snake; N. of the author of the hymns Ṛg-veda VI.<BR>44-46, 48 (his patronymic is Bārhaspatya).<BR>—शं-<BR>यु-वाक, a particular sacrificial ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंय्य
शंय्य or शंय, अस्, आ, अम्, happy, fortunate;<BR>(आ), f. knowledge, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंव, अस्, आ, अम्, fortunate, prosperous; happy;<BR>(अस्), m. the thunderbolt of Indra; the iron head of<BR>a pestle; [cf. शम्ब.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवर|शंवरं
शंवर, अम्, n. water, &c. = शम्बर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पा|शंपा
शम्पा शम्पा, f. lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब्|शंब्
शम्ब् शम्ब्, cl. 1. P. शम्बति, शम्बितुम्,<BR>to go (in this sense = rt. शर्ब्), cl. 10. P.<BR>शम्बयति, -यितुम्, to accumulate, collect, heap<BR>together (in this sense = rts. सम्ब्, साम्ब्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब|शंब|शम्बः
शम्ब शम्ब, अस्, आ, अम् (either fr. rt. 1. शम्<BR>or 2. शम् or rt. शम्ब्), happy, fortunate [cf. शंव<BR>above]; poor (according to Śabda-k.); (अस्), m.<BR>Indra's thunderbolt (Sāy. = वज्र); the iron head<BR>of a pestle; an iron chain worn round the loins;<BR>ploughing in the regular direction; the second plough-<BR>ing of a field.<BR>—शम्बा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, (a field<BR>&c.) twice ploughed (= द्वि-हल्य, द्वि-सीत्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बर|शंबर|शम्बरं|शम्बरः
शम्बर शम्बर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>शम्ब् or fr. 2. शम् with rt. वृ; cf. शंवर,<BR>सम्बर, संवर), N. of a demon of drought<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">Page0993-c+ 76</a>]<BR>(represented in the Ṛg-veda as an enemy of Indra);<BR>a cloud (= मेघ, Naigh. I. 10); a mountain (in<BR>general) or a particular mountain; a sort of deer;<BR>a kind of fish; war; N. of a Daitya [cf. शम्बर-<BR>सूदन]; best, excellent; a Jina; N. of various<BR>plants or trees (= चित्रक; = लोध्र; = अर्जुन);<BR>(ई), f. a kind of drug or medicinal plant, Anthericum<BR>Tuberosum (= आखु-पर्णी); a female juggler; illu-<BR>sion; (अम्), n. water, (in Naigh. I. 12. enumerated<BR>among the उदक-नामानि, and in Naigh. II. 9.<BR>among the बल-नामानि); a cloud, (Sāy. शम्ब-<BR>राणि = मेघान्, Ṛg-veda II. 24, 2); wealth; a<BR>religious observance; a particular religious vow (with<BR>Buddhists); = चित्रम् (according to Śabda-k.).<BR>—शम्-<BR>बर-कन्द, अस्, m. a kind of bulbous plant (= वा-<BR>राही-कन्द).<BR>—शम्बर-चन्दन, अम्, n. a<BR>variety of sandal (= बहल-गन्ध).<BR>—शम्बर-<BR>सूदन, अस्, m. ‘destroyer of the Daitya Śambara,’<BR>epithet of Kāma-deva (god of love).<BR>—शम्बर-<BR>हत्य, अम्, आ, n. f. the killing of Śambara.<BR>—शम्-<BR>बरारि (˚र-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of (the Daitya)<BR>Śambara,’ epithet of Kāma-deva.<BR>—शम्बरासुर<BR>(˚र-अस्˚), अस्, m. the Asura or Daitya Śambara.<BR>—शम्बरासुर-वधोपख्यान (˚ध-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the story of the killing of the Daitya Śambara<BR>(told in the fifty-fifth chapter of the tenth book of<BR>the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बल|शंबल|शंबलं|शंबलः|शम्बलः
शम्बल शम्बल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. शम्ब्, also written शंवल, cf. सम्बल,<BR>संवल), provender or provisions for a journey,<BR>stock for travelling; a bank, shore; envy, jealousy,<BR>impatience of another's success; (ई), f. a procuress,<BR>bawd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बु|शंबु|शंबुः|शम्बुः
शम्बु शम्बु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>शम्), a bivalve shell.<BR>—शम्बु-वर्धन, अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बुक|शंबुक|शंबुकः|शम्बुकः
शम्बुक, अस्, m. (also written शाम्बुक, q. v.),<BR>a bivalve shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बुक्क|शंबुक्क|शंबुक्कः|शम्बुक्कः
शम्बुक्क, अस्, m. a bivalve shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बूक|शंबूक|शंबूकः|शम्बूकः
शम्बूक, अस्, आ, m. f. a bivalve shell; (अस्), m.<BR>a small conch-shell; a snail; N. of a Śūdra (who<BR>had become a devotee and was slain by Rāma-<BR>candra); the edge of the frontal protuberance of an<BR>elephant; N. of a Daitya; a proper N.; = घोङ्ग<BR>(according to Śabda-k.); [cf. Gr. σαμβύκη.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बूपुत्र
शम्बू-पुत्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भ|शंभ|शंभः|शम्भः
शम्भ शम्भ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 2. शम्<BR>with rt. 1. भा), a happy man [cf. शम्-भु]; Indra's<BR>thunderbolt; the iron-bound head of a pestle; [cf.<BR>शंव, शम्ब.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भल|शम्भलः
शम्भल शम्भल (perhaps connected with<BR>2. शम्), N. of a town situated between the Ratha-<BR>prā and Ganges (identified by some with Sumbhul<BR>in Moradabad; the town or district of Śambhala is<BR>fabled to be the place where Kalkī, the last incar-<BR>nation of Viṣṇu, is to appear in the family of a<BR>Brāhman named Viṣṇu-yaśas); (ई), f. a procuress,<BR>bawd.<BR>—शम्भल-ग्राम-माहात्म्य or शम्भ-<BR>ल-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. ‘the glory of the town Śam-<BR>bhala,’ N. of a part of the Skanda-Purāṇa (consisting<BR>of twenty-four chapters).<BR>—शम्भलेश्वर-लिङ्ग<BR>(˚ल-ईश्˚), N. of a Liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भु|शंभु|शंभुः|शम्भुः
शम्भु शम्-भु, शम्-भविष्ठ, &c. See<BR>under 2. शम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय|शयः
शय शय, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शी), ly-<BR>ing down, asleep, sleeping; (अस्), m. sleep, sleeping;<BR>a bed, couch; a hand; a snake, the boa constrictor;<BR>abuse, imprecation; (according to Śabda-k.) = पण;<BR>(आ), f., Ved. a place of rest or repose, [cf. सय्या;<BR>cf. also Gr. ὀρέσ-κοιος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयण्ड|शयंड|शयण्डः
शयण्ड, अस्, ई, अम्, sleeping, asleep, sleepy;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a place.<BR>—शयण्ड-भक्त, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a district, the district of Śayaṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयथ|शयथः
शयथ, अस्, आ, अम्, sleepy, asleep, sleeping; (अस्),<BR>m. death, dying; a sort of snake, the boa constric-<BR>tor; a boar; a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयन|शयनं
शयन, अम्, n. lying down, sleeping, reposing,<BR>sleep; a bed, couch; copulation.<BR>—शयन-गृह,<BR>अम्, n. ‘sleeping-house,’ a bed-chamber.<BR>—शयन-<BR>सखी, f. a bed-fellow.<BR>—शयन-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being or reclining on a couch.<BR>—शयन-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. a sleeping-place, sleeping-apartment.<BR>—शय-<BR>नागार (˚न-आग्˚), अस्, m. a sleeping-room, bed-<BR>chamber.<BR>—शयनैकादशी (˚न-एक्˚), f. the eleventh<BR>day of the light half of month Āṣāḍha (on which<BR>Viṣṇu's sleep commences).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनीय|शयनीयं
शयनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be slept, to be lain on,<BR>fit or suitable for sleep; (अम्), n. a bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनीयक|शयनीयकं
शयनीयक, अम्, n. a bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयान|शयानः
शयान, अस्, आ, अम्, lying down, reclining, resting,<BR>sleeping, slumbering, asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयानक|शयानकः
शयानक, अस्, m. a kind of snake, the boa con-<BR>strictor; a chameleon, lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयालु|शयालुः
शयालु, उस्, उस्, उ, sleepy, slothful, sluggish; (उस्),<BR>m. the boa snake; a dog; a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयित|शयितः
शयित, अस्, आ, अम्, reposed, lying, sleeping,<BR>asleep; (अस्), m. the plant Cordia Myxa; (अम्), n.<BR>sleep, sleeping.<BR>—शयित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who<BR>has lain down, gone to sleep, sleeping, asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयितव्य
शयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be lain or slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयित्वा
शयित्वा, ind. having lain down, having slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयिन्
शयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, lying, resting, reposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयु|शयुः
शयु, उस्, उस्, उ, lying down, reclining, sleeping;<BR>(उस्), m. a large snake, the boa constrictor; N. of<BR>a person protected by the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयुत्रा
शयुत्रा, ind., Ved. on or to a couch, (Sāy. =<BR>शयने, Ṛg-veda X. 40, 2); in or to a dwelling-<BR>place, (Sāy. = शयने, निवास-स्थाने, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>117, 12.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयुन|शयुनः
शयुन, अस्, m. a large snake, the boa constrictor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय्यम्भव|शय्यंभव
शय्यम्-भव, अस्, m., N. of one of the six<BR>Śruta-kevalins (with Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय्या
शय्या, f. a bed, couch, sofa; tying, stringing to-<BR>gether, winding.<BR>—शय्या-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to<BR>bed, lying in bed or on a couch, confined to bed.<BR>—शय्याच्छादन (˚या-आच्˚), अम्, n. a bed-cover-<BR>ing, counterpane, sheet.<BR>—शय्याध्यक्ष (˚या-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. = शय्या-पाल.<BR>—शय्या-पतित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, = शय्या-गत.<BR>—शय्या-पाल, अस्, m. the super-<BR>intendent of beds or sleeping apartments at the court<BR>of a Hindū prince, guardian of a king's bed-chamber.<BR>—शय्यापाल-त्व, अम्, n. the office of guarding a<BR>king's bed-chamber.<BR>—शय्योत्सङ्ग (˚या-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the side or edge of a bed; (according to some)<BR>the middle of a bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर|शरं|शरः
शर शर, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शॄ), injury, hurt,<BR>mischief, a wound; a sort of reed or grass, Saccharum<BR>Sara; an arrow, shaft; a symbolical term for the<BR>number five (from the five arrows of Kāma-deva);<BR>the upper part or cream of slightly curdled milk,<BR>cream [cf. सर]; N. of a son of Ṛcatka (Ved.);<BR>epithet of Śiva; (अम्), n. (in astronomy) the<BR>versed sine of an arc; water.<BR>—शर-काण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. the stem of the Saccharum Sara, a reed-stalk;<BR>the shaft of an arrow.<BR>—शर-घात, अस्, m. = शरा-<BR>घात.<BR>—शर-ज, अम्, n. ‘produced from cream,’<BR>fresh butter, butter made from new milk or from<BR>milk one day old.<BR>—शर-जन्मन्, आ, m. ‘reed-<BR>born,’ N. of Kārttikeya (fabled to have been born<BR>in a thicket of reeds).<BR>—शर-जाल, अम्, n. ‘net-work<BR>of arrows,’ a dense mass or multitude of arrows.<BR>—शर-धि, इस्, m. ‘arrow-holder,’ a quiver.<BR>—शर-<BR>पर्णिका or शर-पर्णी, f. ‘arrow-leaved,’ a kind<BR>of plant (= वरक).<BR>—शर-पात, अस्, m. an arrow's<BR>fall or flight.<BR>—शरपात-स्थान, अम्, n. the place<BR>of an arrow's fall, an arrow's flight or range, a bow-<BR>shot.<BR>—शर-पुङ्खा, f. the feathered end of an<BR>arrow or that part which includes the feathers and<BR>shaft, (in this sense अस्, m. according to some); a<BR>particular plant, a kind of Nīlī or indigo.<BR>—शर-<BR>प्रवेग, अस्, m. the rush or rapid flight of an arrow,<BR>a swift arrow.<BR>—शर-फल, अम्, n. the blade or barb<BR>of an arrow.<BR>—शर-भङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a hermit<BR>(in the Rāmāyaṇa).<BR>—शर-भू, ऊस्, m. ‘reed-born,’<BR>epithet of Kārttikeya (= शर-जन्मन्, q. v.).<BR>—श-<BR>र-भृष्टि, इस्, f. the point of an arrow.<BR>—शर-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">Page0994-b+ 80</a>]<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of Śara grass, consisting of<BR>reeds.<BR>—शर-मल्ल, अस्, m. ‘arrow-fighter,’ an<BR>archer, bowman; a small bird (considered as a va-<BR>riety of the Maina or Turdus Gosalica; in this sense<BR>also read शर-मन्द.)<BR>—शर-लोमन्, आ, m., N.<BR>of a Muni.<BR>—शर-वन, अम्, n. a thicket of reeds.<BR>—शरवन-भव or शरवनोद्भव (˚न-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘born in a thicket of reeds,’ epithet of Kārt-<BR>tikeya.<BR>—शर-वर्ष, अस्, m. a flight or shower<BR>of arrows.<BR>—शर-वर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, raining or<BR>showering down arrows.<BR>—शर-वाणि, इस्, m. the<BR>head of an arrow; a foot soldier; an archer; a<BR>maker of arrows.<BR>—शर-विद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced<BR>with arrows.<BR>—शर-वृष्टि, इस्, f. a shower or heavy<BR>fall of arrows.<BR>—शर-व्रात, अस्, m. a mass of ar-<BR>rows.<BR>—शर-सम्बाध, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with<BR>arrows.<BR>—शर-स्तम्ब, अस्, m. a clump of reeds.<BR>—शराक्षेप (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, m. flight of arrows.<BR>—शराग्र्य (˚र-अग्˚), अस्, m. an excellent arrow.<BR>—शराघात (˚र-आघ्˚), अस्, m. shooting with ar-<BR>rows, archery.<BR>—शराभ्यास (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>practice with bow and arrow, archery.<BR>—शरारोप<BR>(˚र-आर्˚), अस्, m. ‘that on which arrows are fixed,’<BR>a bow.<BR>—शरा-वती, f. ‘full of reeds,’ N. of a river.<BR>—शरावाप (˚र-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘casting arrows,’ a<BR>bow.<BR>—शराश्रय (˚र-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘arrow-recep-<BR>tacle,’ a quiver.<BR>—शरासन (˚र-अस्˚), अम्, n. shoot-<BR>ing arrows, an arrow-shooter, bow; (अस्), m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—शरासन-ज्या, f. a bow-string.<BR>—शरास्य<BR>(˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. a bow (= शरासन).<BR>—शराहत<BR>(˚र-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, struck or wounded by an<BR>arrow.<BR>—शरेषीका (˚र-इष्˚), f. ‘arrow-reed,’ an<BR>arrow.<BR>—शरेष्ट (˚र-इष्˚), अस्, m. ‘desired by ar-<BR>rows,’ the mango tree, (the mango being one of the<BR>trees the blossoms of which tip the arrows of Kāma-<BR>deva.)<BR>—शरोत्तम (˚र-उत्˚), अम्, n. best of arrows,<BR>a very good arrow.<BR>—शरौघ (˚र-ओघ), a<BR>multitude of arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण|शरणं
1. शरण, अम्, n. injuring, killing, slaying; who<BR>or what slays or injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणि|शरणिः
1. शरणि, इस्, f. injury, offence, crime (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्य|शरण्यः
1. शरण्य, अम्, n. injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव्य|शरव्यं
शरव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. शरु below), Ved. capable<BR>of wounding or injuring, (Sāy. = हिंसा-कुशल); (आ),<BR>f. an arrow, missile, shaft, the arrow personified as a<BR>deity (Ved.); (अम्), n. a butt or mark for arrows;<BR>aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारु|शरारुः
शरारु, उस्, उस्, उ, hurtful, injurious, noxious,<BR>mischievous; (उस्), m. a mischievous creature (Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 86, 9).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरि
शरि, इस्, इस्, इ, hurting, hurtful, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरी
शरी, f. a sort of grass (= एरका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरु|शरुः
शरु, उस्, m. (according to others f.), an arrow,<BR>dart; any weapon; the thunderbolt of Indra [cf.<BR>Gr. κεραυνός]; the weapon of the Maruts; anger,<BR>passion; N. of a son of Vasu-deva; a proper N.<BR>(Ved.); [cf. Goth. hairus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्य|शर्यः
शर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, hostile, injurious, hurtful<BR>(Ved.); (अस्), m. an enemy, foe, warrior (Ved.,<BR>Sāy. = योद्धृ, Ṛg-veda I. 119, 10); (आ), f.<BR>night; an arrow (either from its causing injury or<BR>from being made of reed, according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 148, 4; see also Nirukta V. 4, X. 29); a<BR>finger, (the fingers being compared to arrows in Ṛg-<BR>veda IX. 110, 5); a porcupine (according to some;<BR>cf. शल्य).<BR>—शर्य-हन्, आ, m., Ved. killing ene-<BR>mies, a warrior; killing with arrows, an archer, (Sāy.<BR>= वाणैः शत्रूणां हन्ता, Ṛg-veda VI. 16, 39.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरट|शरटः
शरट शरट, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rt. शॄ), a lizard, chameleon; a safflower (= कु-<BR>सुम्भ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण|शरणं
शरण 2. शरण, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (said to be<BR>fr. rt. शॄ, but evidently connected with rt. श्रि), pro-<BR>tecting, preserving (Ved., Sāy. = रक्षक, Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 47, 8); one who protects or preserves, a protector,<BR>preserver, defender; (आ), f. a particular plant, = प्र-<BR>सारणी; (ई), f. a road, path, (see 2. शरणि, col. 3);<BR>the plant Celtis Orientalis; another plant, = प्रसा-<BR>रणी; = जयन्ती; (अम्), n. protection, preservation,<BR>help, defence; a refuge, place of refuge, sanctuary,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">Page0994-c+ 77</a>]<BR>asylum, (sometimes applied to a person); a private<BR>apartment, closet; a house, habitation, abode; lair,<BR>resting-place (of an animal).<BR>—शरणङ्-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, gone for refuge, taken refuge.<BR>—शरणागत<BR>(˚ण-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, come for protection, one who<BR>comes for refuge or protection, a refugee, fugitive.<BR>—शरणापन्न (˚ण-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, gone to for<BR>protection, taken refuge.<BR>—शरणार्थम् (˚ण-अर्˚),<BR>ind. for the sake of protection.<BR>—शरणार्थिन् (˚ण-<BR>अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, soliciting an asylum, seeking refuge,<BR>asking for protection, dependant on others for protec-<BR>tion or aid; unfortunate, wretched, involved in cala-<BR>mity or ruin.<BR>—शरणार्पक (˚ण-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘requiring protection to be given,’ unfortunate, cala-<BR>mitous, distressed, ruined.<BR>—शरणैषिन् (˚ण-एष्˚),<BR>ई, इणी, इ, seeking for an asylum or protection, wishing<BR>for shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणि|शरणिः
2. शरणि, इस्, f. a road, path, way, (probably for<BR>सरणि); a row, line [cf. श्रेणि]; the earth (ac-<BR>cording to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणी
शरणी, f. a road, path, &c.; (probably for सरणी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्य|शरण्यः
2. शरण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or good for refuge, to<BR>be protected or aided, needing protection, poor,<BR>miserable, helpless; yielding protection, helping;<BR>(अम्), n. a place of refuge, asylum, house, refuge;<BR>protection, defence; a protection, a protector, who<BR>or what affords refuge and defence; (अस्), m. epithet<BR>of Śiva; (आ), f., N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्यु|शरण्युः
शरण्यु, उस्, m. a protector, defender (= भ-<BR>रण्यु); wind, air; a cloud; [cf. सरण्यु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्ड|शरंड|शरंडः|शरण्डः
शरण्ड शरण्ड, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>शॄ, probably for सरण्ड, q. v.), a bird (in general);<BR>a lizard, chameleon; a kind of ornament; a rogue,<BR>cheat; a libertine, lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरद्
शरद् शरद्, त्, f. (according to Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>129. fr. rt. शॄ), autumn, the season of autumn, (the<BR>sultry season of two months succeeding the rains; in<BR>some parts of India comprising the months Bhādra and<BR>Āśvina, in other places Āśvina and Kārttika; fluctuat-<BR>ing thus from August to November); a year; (दस्),<BR>f. pl. the seasons; (त्), m., N. of an Asura (Ved.).<BR>—श-<BR>रच्-चन्द्र, अस्, m. the autumnal moon.<BR>—शरत्-<BR>कामिन्, ई, m. ‘desirous of autumn,’ a dog.<BR>—शरत्-<BR>काल, अस्, m. the autumnal season.<BR>—शरत्कालीन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, belonging to the autumnal season, autumnal.<BR>—शरत्-त्रियामा, f. an autumnal night.<BR>—शरत्-<BR>पद्म, अस्, अम्, m. n. an autumnal lotus, the white<BR>lotus.<BR>—शरत्-पर्वन्, अ, n. a festival on the full<BR>moon of Āśvina (= कोजागर).<BR>—शरत्-पुष्प,<BR>अम्, n. a particular shrub (= आहुल्य).<BR>—शरत्-<BR>प्रतीक्षम्, ind. having expected the autumn.<BR>—शरद्-अन्त, अस्, m. the end of autumn, winter.<BR>—शरद्-अम्बुधर, अस्, m. an autumnal cloud.<BR>—शरदि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in autumn, au-<BR>tumnal.<BR>—शरद्-उदाशय (˚द-आश्˚), अम्, n. an<BR>autumnal lake or pond.<BR>—शरद्-घन, अस्, m. an<BR>autumnal cloud.<BR>—शरद्-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi<BR>(belonging to the family of Aṅgiras); of the father<BR>of Kṛpa (also called Gautama).<BR>—शरन्-मुख,<BR>अम्, n. the commencement of autumn.<BR>—शरन्-<BR>मेघ, अस्, m. an autumnal cloud.<BR>—शरन्मेघ-<BR>वत्, ind. like an autumnal cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरद
शरद at the end of a comp. = शरद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदा
शरदा, f. autumn, the sultry season; a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदक्ष
शरदक्ष शरदक्ष, अस्, m., N. of the au-<BR>thor of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरधि|शरधिः
शरधि शर-धि. See under शर, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरभ|शरभः
शरभ शरभ, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 122. fr. rt. शॄ), a fabulous animal (supposed to<BR>have eight legs and to inhabit the snowy moun-<BR>tains; it is represented as stronger than a lion, cf.<BR>अष्ट-पाद्, महा-स्कन्धिन्); a young elephant;<BR>N. of a monkey in Rāma's army; a camel; a grass-<BR>hopper [cf. शलभ]; a locust; [cf. perhaps Gr.<BR>κάραβος; Angl. Sax. crabba.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरयु|शरयुः
शरयु शरयु, उस्, or शरयू, ऊस्, f. (more cor-<BR>rectly written सरयु, q. v.), the Saryu or Saryū river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरल|शरलः
शरल शरल, अस्, आ, अम् (probably for<BR>सरल), upright, honest, pure-minded; crooked,<BR>fraudulent, = वि-गीत (according to Śabda-k.); (अस्),<BR>m. a tree, a sort of pine (= सरल, q. v.).<BR>—शरल-<BR>ता, f. or शरल-त्व, अम्, n. uprightness, sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरलक|शरलकं
शरलक, अम्, n. water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव
शरव शरव, अस्, m. (for शराव, q. v.), a<BR>lid, cover; N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव्य|शरव्यं
शरव्य शरव्य. See p. 994, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराक
शराक शराक, अस्, m., (apparently) N. of a<BR>mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराटि|शराटिः
शराटि शराटि, इस्, f. (said to be fr. शर<BR>and rt. अट्), a sort of bird, Turdus Ginginianus (=<BR>आटि and commonly called Śarāli).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराडि|शराडिः
शराडि, इस्, f. = शराटि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराति|शरातिः
शराति, इस्, f. = शराटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारि|शरारिः
शरारि, इस्, f. the Śarāli bird (= शराटि).<BR>—श-<BR>रारी-मुखी, f. a kind of scissors or an instrument<BR>pointed like the beak of the Śarāli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरालि|शरालिः
शरालि, इस्, or शरालिका, f. = शराटि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारु|शरारुः
शरारु शरारु. See p. 994, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराव|शरावं|शरावः
शराव शराव, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>शर, ‘mischief,’ and rt. अव्, ‘to protect’), a lid,<BR>cover; a shallow cup, dish, platter, plate, earthenware<BR>vessel; a tray; a measure equal to two Kuḍavas.<BR>—शराव-सम्पात, अस्, m. the removal of dishes<BR>(after a meal).<BR>—शरावार्ध (˚व-अर्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>measure equal to one Kuḍava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरावती
शरावती शरा-वती, f. See under शर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरि
शरि शरि, शरी, &c. See p. 994, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरिमन्
शरिमन् शरिमन् or शरीमन्, आ, m. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. शॄ), bearing, bringing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीतोस्
शरीतोस् शरीतोस्, in Ṛg-veda III. 53, 17.<BR>from decay, (Sāy. = विशारणात् प्राक्, ‘before decay-<BR>ing.’ See rt. शॄ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीर|शरीरं
शरीर शरीर, अम्, n. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. fr. rt. शॄ), ‘that which easily moulders or is<BR>dissolved,’ the body; bodily strength; a dead body.<BR>—शरीर-कर्तृ, ता, m. ‘body-maker,’ a father.<BR>—शरीर-कर्षण, अम्, n. emaciating the body.<BR>—शरीर-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by or in the body;<BR>(अस्), m. sickness, disease; the god of love (or<BR>Kāma); lust, passion; a son.<BR>—शरीर-जन्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, born or produced of or from the body.<BR>—श-<BR>रीर-तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, equal to the body, dear as<BR>one's own person.<BR>—शरीर-दण्ड, अस्, m. corporal<BR>punishment, mortification of body.<BR>—शरीर-धृक्<BR>(see धृक्, p. 459), bearing a body.<BR>—शरीर-<BR>पतन, अम्, n. or शरीर-पात, अस्, m. ‘fall of the<BR>body,’ death.<BR>—शरीर-पाक, अस्, m. ‘ripening or<BR>maturity of the body,’ decline of bodily strength,<BR>decay, emaciation.<BR>—शरीर-प्रधानता, f. the<BR>character or nature of the body; (तया), ind. in<BR>virtue of the body.<BR>—शरीर-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, en-<BR>dowed or invested with a body.<BR>—शरीर-बन्धक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘personal pledge,’ a hostage.<BR>—शरीर-भाज्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, having a body, embodied, corporeal.<BR>—श-<BR>रीर-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become a body, being a<BR>body.<BR>—शरीर-भेद, अस्, m. separation or dis-<BR>union of the body, death.<BR>—शरीर-मात्र, अम्, n.<BR>the mere person, the body only.<BR>—शरीर-यष्टि,<BR>इस्, f. a body like a stick, i. e. a slender or slim figure.<BR>—शरीर-यात्रा, f. means of bodily subsistence, sub-<BR>sistence, support.<BR>—शरीर-योग, अस्, m. union of<BR>the body, bodily union.<BR>—शरीर-रक्षा, f. defence<BR>of the body, protection of the person.<BR>—शरीर-<BR>विमोक्षण, अम्, n. liberation from the body,<BR>release of the soul from the body.<BR>—शरीर-वै-<BR>कल्य, अम्, n. imperfection or indisposition of the<BR>body, bodily ailment, disease.<BR>—शरीर-शुश्रूषा,<BR>f. ‘bodily obedience,’ personal attendance.<BR>—शरीर-<BR>शोषण, अम्, n. drying up or withering of the body,<BR>emaciation of the body.<BR>—शरीर-संस्कार, अस्,<BR>m. purification of the body (by various ceremonies<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">Page0995-b+ 78</a>]<BR>at conception, birth, initiation, and death); (अम्),<BR>n. decoration or adorning the person.<BR>—शरीर-<BR>सम्पत्ति, इस्, f. health or prosperity of body.<BR>—श-<BR>रीर-सम्बन्ध, अस्, m. ‘bodily connection,’ rela-<BR>tion by marriage.<BR>—शरीर-साद, अस्, m. exhaustion<BR>or weariness of body.<BR>—शरीरान्तकर (˚र-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the destroyer of bodies.<BR>—शरीरान्तर (˚र-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. another body.<BR>—शरीरान्तर-चारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, acting in another body.<BR>—शरीरावरण<BR>(˚र-आव्˚), अम्, n. ‘body-covering,’ ‘body-envelope,’<BR>the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरक|शरीरकं|शरीरकः
शरीरक, अम्, n. a small or inferior body; the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरिन्
शरीरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a body, embodied, cor-<BR>poreal; living; (ई), m. an animal or sentient being;<BR>a man; an embodied spirit; the soul whilst clad<BR>with the body; (इ), n. the incorporate soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करा
शर्करा शर्करा, f. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 3. fr. rt. शॄ), a fragment or piece of broken<BR>earthenware, potsherd; any fragment, part, piece,<BR>bit; any hard particle or nodule, (जल-शर्करा,<BR>hail); a small stone, pebble, gravel, grit [cf. कर्-<BR>कर]; gravelly mould; a soil abounding in stony<BR>or gritty fragments; granulated or candied sugar,<BR>brown sugar; gravel (the disease); [cf. Gr. κρόκη,<BR>κροκάλη, κάχληξ, χάλιξ, σάκχαρ, σάκχαρον; Lat.<BR>calx, calculus, saccharum.]<BR>—शर्कर-जा, f. (शर्-<BR>कर for शर्करा), clayed or candied sugar.<BR>—शर्-<BR>कराक्ष (˚रा-अक्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—शर्क-<BR>राचल (˚रा-अच्˚), अस्, m. ‘sugar-mountain,’ a kind<BR>of artificial mountain made of sugar.<BR>—शर्करा-<BR>चल-दान (˚रा-अच्˚), अम्, n. the gift of a mountain<BR>of sugar.<BR>—शर्करा-धेनु, उस्, f. a gift of sugar in<BR>the form of a cow, (see धेनु.)<BR>—शर्करा-प्रभा,<BR>f. ‘gravel-appearance,’ N. of the second of the Jaina<BR>hells, the hell of gravel.<BR>—शर्करा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>full of stony particles, gritty, gravelly.<BR>—शर्करा-<BR>सप्तमी, f. a particular religious observance on the<BR>seventh day of the light half of the month Vaiśākha.<BR>—शर्करोदक (˚रा-उद्˚), अम्, n. sugar-water,<BR>water sweetened with sugar, lemonade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करक|शर्करकः
शर्करक, अस्, m. a species of citron or lime<BR>(= मधुर-जम्बीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करिक|शर्करिकः
शर्करिक, अस्, ई, अम्, stony, gravelly, gritty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करिल|शर्करिलः
शर्करिल, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in stony or<BR>gravelly particles, gritty, gravelly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करी
शर्करी, f. a kind of metre (= शक्वरी, सक्करी);<BR>a river; a girdle; (according to Śabda-k.) = लेखनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्कु
शर्कु, उस्, m., Ved. (perhaps) a potsherd, (see<BR>Atharva-veda VIII. 6, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ध|शर्द्धः|शर्धः
शर्ध शर्ध, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शृध्), a troop,<BR>multitude; strength, power; breaking wind, flatu-<BR>lence (= अपानोत्सर्ग, cf. शृधु).<BR>—शर्धञ्-<BR>जह, अस्, आ, अम् (जह for जहत्), causing flatu-<BR>lence; (अस्), m. beans or any leguminous grain,<BR>pulse.<BR>—शर्ध-नीति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. one whose<BR>deeds are mighty, acting powerfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्धत्
शर्धत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. making effort or<BR>exertion, striving, vehement, (Sāy. = उत्सहमान,<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 18, 5); daring, presumptuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्धन
शर्धन, अम्, n. the act of breaking wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्धस्
शर्धस्, अस्, n., Ved. a troop, multitude, com-<BR>pany, host, (in the Ṛg-veda frequently applied to<BR>the hosts of the Maruts); strength, power.<BR>—शर्-<BR>धस्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. more powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्धित्वा
शर्धित्वा, ind. having broken wind, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ब्|शर्ब्ब्
शर्ब् शर्ब्, cl. 1. P. शर्बति, &c., to hurt,<BR>injure, kill (= rts. शर्व्, सर्व्); to go (=<BR>rts. सर्ब्, शम्ब्, सम्ब्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मन्|शर्म्मन्
शर्मन् शर्मन्, आ, आ, अ (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. IV. 144. fr. rt. शॄ, but probably connected<BR>with rt. श्रि; cf. 2. शरण), happy, prosperous,<BR>(Śarman is frequently found at the end of names<BR>of Brāhmans just as Varman is added to the names<BR>of Kṣatriyas and Gupta to those of Vaiśyas);<BR>(अ), n. a blessing; happiness, delight, pleasure;<BR>refuge, protection; a house, receptacle, (in Naigh.<BR>III. 4. enumerated among the गृह-नामानि, in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">Page0995-c+ 75</a>]<BR>Aitareya-Br. II. 40. Śarman is identified with वाच्,<BR>speech.)<BR>—शर्म-द, अस्, आ, अम्, conferring happi-<BR>ness, making prosperous, propitious.<BR>—शर्म-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of happiness, lucky, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मय
शर्मय, Nom. P. शर्मयति, -यितुम्, Ved.<BR>to grant happiness, confer prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मयत्
शर्मयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. conferring happi-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मर|शर्मरः|शर्म्मर|शर्म्मरः
शर्मर, अस्, m. a sort of garment or cloth;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of Curcuma, Curcuma Xanthorrhiza<BR>(= दारु-हरिद्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मिष्ठा
शर्मिष्ठा, f. ‘most fortunate,’ N. of one of<BR>the wives of Yayāti, (she was daughter of Vṛṣa-<BR>parvan and mother of Puru.)<BR>—शर्मिष्ठा-ययाति,<BR>N. of a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्य|शर्यः
शर्य शर्य. See p. 994, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्यणा
शर्यणा शर्यणा, f., N. of the country of<BR>Kuru-kṣetra.<BR>—शर्यणा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>sweet as honey (according to some); N. of a lake in<BR>the neighbourhood of Kuru-kṣetra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्यात
शर्यात शर्यात, अस्, m., Ved., N. of one of<BR>the sons of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्याति|शर्य्याति|शर्य्यातिः
शर्याति, इस्, m., N. of one of the sons of Manu<BR>Vaivasvata (and father of Ānarta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्|शर्व्व्
शर्व् शर्व्, cl. 1. P. शर्वति, &c., to hurt,<BR>injure, kill; [cf. rts. शर्ब्, सर्व्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वला|शर्व्वला
शर्वला or शर्वली, f. an iron crow (= सर्वला,<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व|शर्वः|शर्व्व|शर्व्वः
शर्व शर्व, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. शॄ),<BR>N. of a Vedic deity (often mentioned together with<BR>Bhava); of Śiva (in the form Kṣiti-mūrti); of<BR>Viṣṇu; [cf. सर्व.]<BR>—शर्व-दत्त, अस्, m. ‘given<BR>by Śarva,’ a proper N.<BR>—शर्व-वर्मन्, आ, m., N.<BR>of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वक
शर्वक, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वाणी|शर्व्वाणी
शर्वाणी, f., N. of Pārvatī (wife of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वट
शर्वट शर्वट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वर|शर्वरः|शर्व्वर|शर्व्वरं
शर्वर शर्वर, अम्, n. (fr. rt. शॄ), dark-<BR>ness; love, = कन्दर्प; (ई), f. night (= रात्रि,<BR>according to Naigh. 1. 7. and Sāy. on Ṛg-veda V.<BR>52, 3); evening; turmeric; a dark cow (according<BR>to some modern scholars); a woman; epithet of<BR>the eighth year of Jupiter's cycle; [cf. probably Gr.<BR>Κέρβερος..]<BR>—शर्वरी-दीपक, अस्, m. ‘lamp of<BR>night,’ epithet of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वरा
शर्वरा, f., Ved. = शर्वरी (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वरीक|शर्व्वरीक
शर्वरीक शर्वरीक, अस्, आ, अम् (probably incor-<BR>rect for शर्शरीक below), hurtful, mischievous, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्शरीक|शर्शरीकः
शर्शरीक शर्शरीक, अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 19. fr. rt. शॄ), hurtful, mischievous,<BR>cruel; (अस्), m. a mischievous man, a vile man,<BR>wretch, rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्षीका
शर्षीका शर्षीका, f. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्
शल् शल् [cf. rt. चल्], cl. 1. A. शलते,<BR>शेले, शलितुम्, to shake, tremble; to<BR>cover; cl. 1. P. शलति, शशाल, &c., to go, move,<BR>flow, run [cf. उच्-छल्, प्रोच्-छल्, rts. श्वल्, 3. शठ्];<BR>cl. 10. A. शालयते, -यितुम्, to praise, (in this<BR>sense also written शठ्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल|शलं|शलः
शल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt. शल्, but<BR>probably connected with rt. शॄ), the quill of a por-<BR>cupine; (अस्), m. a dart, spear; a stake; a kind of<BR>field; N. of Bhṛṅgi (one of Śiva's attendants); of<BR>Brahmā; of a son of Soma-datta; of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra; (ई), f. a small porcupine or hedgehog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलक|शलकः
शलक, अस्, m. a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलल|शललं
शलल, अम्, n. the quill of a porcupine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलली
शलली, f. the quill of a porcupine; a small porcu-<BR>pine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाका
शलाका, f. a javelin, dart; an arrow; a rib (of an<BR>umbrella &c.); a thin bar (as of a cage &c.), any<BR>small stake, stick, rod, peg, pin; a round pointed<BR>piece of wood or bamboo serving for various pur-<BR>poses; a ruler; a brimstone match; any pointed<BR>surgical instrument, a tent or probe (used in the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-a" target="_blank">Page0996-a+ 80</a>]<BR>treatment of external organic affections and some-<BR>times taken as the N. of this branch of surgery; cf.<BR>शालाक्य); a bone; an oblong quadrangular piece<BR>of ivory or bone (used in playing a particular game),<BR>a domino; a fibrous stick used as a brush, &c.; a<BR>tooth-brush; a tooth-pick; a pencil; a sprout, sprig,<BR>shoot of any kind [cf. रत्न-शलाका]; a porcupine;<BR>a particular thorny shrub, Vangueria Spinosa; the<BR>Sārikā bird, Turdus Salica.<BR>—शलाक-धूर्त, अस्,<BR>m. (for शलाका-ध्˚), cheating with dominoes, a<BR>sharper.<BR>—शलाका-परि, ind. an unlucky throw or<BR>movement of one of the pieces at the game of<BR>Śalākā, (see परि.)<BR>—शलाका-पुरुष, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of sixty-three divine personages according to the<BR>Jainas (viz. the twenty-four Jainas, twelve Cakra-<BR>vartins, nine Vāsudevas, nine Bala-devas, and nine<BR>Prati-vāsudevas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्य|शल्यं|शल्यः
शल्य, अस्, अम्, m. n. a dart, javelin, spear tipped<BR>with iron, (उप-शल्य, a short spear); a pike; an<BR>arrow, shaft; any stake or rod, spike, splinter, thorn,<BR>(in these senses usually अम्, n.); a pin, peg; (अस्),<BR>m. a porcupine, hedgehog; extraction of splinters<BR>or extraneous substances in surgery (as a branch of<BR>medicine or Āyur-veda, q. v.); the thorny shrub,<BR>Vangueria Spinosa (= मदन); another tree (=<BR>विल्व); a fence, boundary; a kind of fish; N. of<BR>the king of Madra (maternal uncle of the sons of<BR>Pāṇḍu and especially of Nakula and Sahadeva, Madrī<BR>the wife of Pāṇḍu being sister to Śalya); (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a son of Vipracitti; (अम्), n. an iron crow-<BR>bar; any extraneous substance lodged in the body<BR>(as an arrow, thorn, splinter); a bone; sin, crime;<BR>poison; difficulty, embarrassment, distress; abuse,<BR>defamation; [cf. Gr. κῆλα; Hib. cail, ‘a spear.’]<BR>—शल्य-कण्ठ, अस्, m. ‘quill-throated,’ a porcu-<BR>pine.<BR>—शल्य-क्रिया, f. the extraction of thorns or<BR>other extraneous substances lodged in the body.<BR>—शल्य-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a section of the<BR>Aṣṭāṅga-hṛdaya-saṃhitā (comprising chapters 25 —<BR>34 of the Uttara-tantra or sixth book, and treating<BR>of the cure of external wounds).<BR>—शल्य-पर्वन्,<BR>अ, n., N. of the ninth book of the Mahā-bhārata,<BR>(this book describes how, on the death of Karṇa,<BR>Śalya, king of Madra, was appointed to the command<BR>of the Kuru army, and how a combat with maces<BR>took place between Śalya and Bhīma, and another<BR>great battle between Śalya and Yudhi-ṣṭhira, in<BR>which the former was eventually killed.)<BR>—शल्य-<BR>प्रोत, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced or transfixed by an arrow.<BR>—शल्य-लोमन्, अ, n. a porcupine's quill.<BR>—शल्य-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing an arrow, owning shafts;<BR>shooting arrows, one who has shot an arrow; set<BR>with stakes, hampered or harassed with difficulties.<BR>—शल्य-वारङ्ग, अम्, n. ‘arrow-handle,’ the part<BR>by which an arrow or other foreign substance lodged<BR>in the body is laid hold of during the operation of<BR>extraction.<BR>—शल्य-शास्त्र, अम्, n. ‘splinter-(extrac-<BR>tion)-science,’ that part of surgery which treats of<BR>the removal of extraneous substances lodged in the<BR>body; [cf. आयुर्-वेद.]<BR>—शल्य-हर्तृ, ता, m. a<BR>remover of thorns, weeder.<BR>—शल्यारि (˚य-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. ‘enemy of Śalya,’ an epithet of Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR>—शल्याहरण-विधि (˚य-आह्˚), इस्, m. ‘method<BR>of extracting splinters or other foreign substances,’<BR>N. of the twenty-eighth chapter of the Sūtra-sthāna<BR>or first book of the Aṣṭāṅga-hṛdaya-saṃhita.<BR>—श-<BR>ल्योद्धार (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, m. extraction of arrows or<BR>thorns or other pointed substances from the body;<BR>weeding; the ceremony of cleansing or purifying a<BR>new house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यक|शल्यकः
शल्यक, अस्, m. a dart, javelin, spear, pike; a<BR>stake, thorn; a porcupine; a hedgehog; the thorny<BR>shrub Vangueria Spinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलङ्ग|शलंग|शलंगः|शलङ्गः
शलङ्ग शलङ्ग, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>शल्), a king, sovereign (= लोक-पाल), a kind of<BR>salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलभ|शलभः
शलभ शलभ, अस्, m. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. III. 122. fr. rt. शल्, but cf. शरभ), a grass-<BR>hopper; a locust; a moth; N. of an Asura.<BR>—श-<BR>लभ-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition of a grass-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">Page0996-b+ 70</a>]<BR>hopper.<BR>—शलभासुर (˚भ-अस्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>Asura Śalabha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाका
शलाका शलाका. See p. 995, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाट|शलाटः
शलाट शलाट, अस्, m. (etymology doubt-<BR>ful), a cartload (= 20 times 100 Palas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाटु|शलाटुः
शलाटु शलाटु, उस्, उस्, उ (said to be fr. rt.<BR>शल्), unripe (as fruit); (उस्), m. a kind of root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलातुर
शलातुर शलातुर, N. of the abode of the<BR>ancestors of Pāṇini; [cf. शालातुरीय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाभोलि|शलाभोलिः
शलाभोलि शलाभोलि, इस्, m. (etymology<BR>doubtful), a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलालु|शलालुः
शलालु शलालु, n. a sort of perfume or<BR>fragrant substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलालुक|शलालुकः
शलालुक, अस्, ई, अम्, purchased with or exchanged<BR>for the substance termed Śalālu; [cf. शालालुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्क|शल्कं
शल्क शल्क, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 43. fr. rt. शल्, but probably connected with शल<BR>and rt. शॄ), a part, portion, piece; bark (of a tree),<BR>rind; the scale of a fish; [cf. वल्क.]<BR>—शल्क-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, scaly, flaky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कल|शल्कलं
शल्कल, अम्, n. a part, portion; bark, rind; the<BR>scale of a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कलिन्
शल्कलिन्, ई, m. ‘having scales,’ a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्किन्
शल्किन्, ई, m. ‘having scales,’ a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्पदा
शल्पदा शल्पदा, f., N. of a plant or root<BR>(= मेदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्पपर्णिका
शल्पपर्णिका शल्प-पर्णिका = शल्पदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्भ्
शल्भ् शल्भ्, cl. 1. A. शल्भते, शशल्भे,<BR>शल्भितुम्, to praise; to boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्मलि|शल्मलिः
शल्मलि शल्मलि, इस्, m. the silk-cotton<BR>tree; [cf. शाल्मलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्मली
शल्मली, f. = शल्मलि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्य|शल्यं|शल्यः
शल्य शल्य, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्ल्
शल्ल् शल्ल्, a Sautra root meaning ‘to<BR>go.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्ल|शल्लं|शल्लः
शल्ल, अस्, m. a frog; (अम्), n. bark, rind; [cf.<BR>शल्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लक|शल्लकं|शल्लकः
शल्लक, अस्, m. the plant Bignonia Indica, =<BR>शोण; (अम्), n. bark, rind; (ई), f. a porcupine;<BR>the gum olibanum tree, Boswellia Thurifera (=<BR>गज-भक्षा, सुरभि).<BR>—शल्लकी-द्रव, अस्, m.<BR>‘Śallakī-essence,’ incense, olibanum (= सिह्ल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्व|शल्वः
शल्व शल्व, अस्, m., N. of a country, (more<BR>usually written शाल्व, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव्
शव् शव् (perhaps originally शु, and con-<BR>nected with rt. श्वि, ‘to swell, increase,’<BR>in the same way as rt. हु with rt. ह्वे), cl. 1. P.<BR>शवति, &c., to go, approach, (शवति is enumerated<BR>among the गति-कर्माणः in Naigh. II. 14. and<BR>among the परिचरण-कर्माणः according to<BR>some readings in Naigh. III. 5); to alter, change,<BR>transform, corrupt, cause to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव|शवं|शवः
शव, अस्, अम्, m. n. a dead body, corpse; (अम्),<BR>n. water.<BR>—शव-काम्य, अस्, m. ‘desirous of dead<BR>bodies,’ a dog.<BR>—शव-दाह, अस्, m. burning a<BR>corpse, cremation of a dead body.<BR>—शव-दाहक,<BR>अस्, or शव-दाहिन्, ई, m. a corpse-burner.<BR>—शव-<BR>भस्मन्, अ, n. the ashes of a corpse.<BR>—शव-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, become a corpse or like a corpse.<BR>—शव-<BR>यान, अम्, n. or शव-रथ, अस्, m. ‘corpse-vehicle,’<BR>a bier, hearse, litter for carrying a dead body.<BR>—शव-<BR>वाहक, अस्, m. a corpse-carrier.<BR>—शव-साधन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘corpse-rite,’ a magical and superstitious<BR>ceremony performed with a dead body.<BR>—शव-<BR>स्पर्श, अस्, m. touching a corpse.<BR>—शव-स्पृश्, क्,<BR>क्, क्, one who has touched a corpse (and is conse-<BR>quently defiled).<BR>—शवाच्छादन (˚व-आच्˚), अम्,<BR>ई, n. f. the covering of a corpse, a shroud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवर|शवरः
शवर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. शव, cf. शबर), a<BR>barbarian, savage, mountaineer, a Kirāta, (especially<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">Page0996-c+ 80</a>]<BR>one wearing peacocks’ feathers as a decoration); water;<BR>the hand; N. of Śiva; a particular Śāstra or sacred<BR>treatise; (ई), f. a Śavara female.<BR>—शवर-लोध्र,<BR>अस्, m. the white Lodhra or Lodh tree.<BR>—शवर-<BR>स्वामिन्, see शबर-स्˚.<BR>—शवराल (˚र-आल for<BR>आलय?), अस्, m. a sort of Lodhra or Lodh tree.<BR>—शवरालय (˚र-आल्˚) or शवरावास (˚र-आव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the abode of outcasts or of wild barbarous<BR>tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवल|शवलः
शवल, अस्, आ, अम् (also written शबल), varie-<BR>gated, of a variegated colour, brindled, mottled (with<BR>various hues, as with brown or yellow, &c.),<BR>spotted (applied in Ṛg-veda X. 14, 10. to the<BR>two four-eyed watch-dogs of Yama; the word श-<BR>बल being thought by some to be a corruption<BR>of शर्वर or शर्बर = Κέρβερος); diversified,<BR>varied, divided into various parts; articulate, imi-<BR>tative; (अस्), m. a variegated colour; (आ or ई), f. a<BR>brindled or spotted cow; the cow of plenty, Kāma-<BR>dhenu [cf. शबली]; (अम्), n. water; a religious<BR>observance peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>—शवल-गु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, having mottled cows.<BR>—शवल-ता, f. or<BR>शवल-त्व, अम्, n. variegation, variety of colour;<BR>variation, alternation.<BR>—शवली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>made of a variegated colour, variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवस्
शवस्, अस्, n. power, strength, vigour (Ved.);<BR>water (= उदक, Naigh. 1. 12); a corpse; (आस्), m.<BR>a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसान|शवसानः
शवसान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. powerful, very mighty,<BR>(Sāy. = बल-वत्, अति-बल); (अस्), m. a traveller;<BR>a road; (अम्), n. a cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसावत्|शवसावन्त्
शवसा-वत्, आन्, m., Ved. ‘powerful,’ epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसिन्
शवसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, powerful, mighty, (Sāy. =<BR>बल-वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शविष्ठ
शविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. strongest, most<BR>powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्
शश् शश्, cl. 1. P. शशति, शशाश, शशि-<BR>तुम्, to jump, leap, spring, bound, dance;<BR>A., Ved. to praise, laud, celebrate, (this sense ap-<BR>pears to be doubtful and to result from a confusion<BR>with शस् for rt. शंस्); [cf. Lith. szókti; Slav.<BR>skakati, ‘to dance.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश|शशः
शश, अस्, m. a hare, rabbit, (its flesh is said to be<BR>greatly valued and is offered at Śrāddhas); a spot or<BR>spots on the moon (supposed to resemble those on<BR>a hare); a man of mild and virtuous character but<BR>uxorious and easily led, (one of the four classes into<BR>which men are divided by erotic writers; he is<BR>described as gentle in speech and temper, with soft<BR>limbs and fine hair); the Lodh tree, Symplocos Race-<BR>mosa (= लोध्र); gum-myrrh; N. of a part of<BR>Jambu-dvīpa; [cf. Old Germ. haso; Angl. Sax.<BR>hara; Lith. kiszkis, zuikis; Russ. zœz.]<BR>—शश-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m. ‘rabbit-eared,’ N. of the author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda VIII. 9 (having the patronymic<BR>Kāṇva).<BR>—शश-धर, अस्, m. ‘having (marks<BR>like) a hare,’ the moon; camphor; N. of a com-<BR>mentator.<BR>—शशधर-मौलि, इस्, m. ‘moon-<BR>crested,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शश-धरीय, N. of<BR>Śaśa-dhara's philosophical treatise on the nature of<BR>atoms, &c.<BR>—शश-धर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king<BR>of the Maurya dynasty (a descendant of Candra-<BR>gupta).<BR>—शश-प्लुतक, अम्, n. a mark or scratch<BR>with a finger-nail.<BR>—शश-भृत्, त्, m. ‘hare-(mark)-<BR>possessing,’ the moon.<BR>—शशभृद्-भृत्, त्, or<BR>(according to Śabda-k.) शशभृद्-भृत, अस्, m.<BR>‘moon-bearer,’ epithet of Śiva (as bearing the moon<BR>on his brow).<BR>—शश-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘having<BR>the measure of a hare,’ as large as a hare.<BR>—शश-<BR>रजस्, अस्, n. ‘a speck of dust or dirt on a hare,’<BR>a particular measure.<BR>—शश-लक्ष्मण, अस्, m.<BR>‘hare-marked,’ epithet of the moon.<BR>—शश-लाञ्-<BR>छन, अस्, m. ‘hare-marked,’ the moon.<BR>—शश-<BR>लुप्त, अम्, n., see Pāṇ. VI. 2, 145.<BR>—शश-लोमन्,<BR>अ, n. the hair of a hare or rabbit, hare-skin, rabbit-<BR>skin.<BR>—शश-विन्दु, उस्, m. ‘hare-spotted,’ the moon;<BR>N. of a king (son of Citra-ratha); an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—शश-विषाण, अम्, n. ‘rab-<BR>bit's-horn,’ anything impossible or extraordinary, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">Page0997-a+ 81</a>]<BR>impossibility.<BR>—शश-शिम्बिका, f. a particular plant<BR>(= जीवन्ती).<BR>—शश-स्थली, f. the Doab or country<BR>between the Ganges and Jumnā rivers (= अन्तर्-<BR>वेदी).<BR>—शशाङ्क (˚श-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘hare-marked,’<BR>the moon; camphor.<BR>—शशाङ्क-किरण-प्रख्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, resembling a ray of the moon, like a<BR>moon-beam.<BR>—शशाङ्क-भास्, आस्, आस्, आस्, shining<BR>like the moon.<BR>—शशाङ्क-मूर्ति, इस्, m. ‘having<BR>a form marked like a hare,’ epithet of the moon.<BR>—शशाङ्क-लेखा, f. ‘moon-streak,’ a digit of the<BR>moon, the lunar crescent.<BR>—शशाङ्क-वती, f., N. of<BR>the twelfth book of the Kathā-sarit-sāgara.<BR>—श-<BR>शाङ्क-शृङ्ग, अम्, n. a horn or point of the moon's<BR>crescent (?).<BR>—शशाङ्कार्ध-मुख (˚क-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, crescent-headed (said of an arrow).<BR>—शशाद<BR>(˚श-अद), अस्, m. ‘hare-eater,’ a hawk, falcon; N.<BR>of a son of Ikṣvāku.<BR>—शशादन (˚श-अद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘hare-eater,’ a hawk, falcon.<BR>—शशोर्ण (˚श-ऊर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the hair of a hare or rabbit, hare-skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशक|शशकः
शशक, अस्, m. a hare, rabbit.<BR>—शशक-विषा-<BR>ण, अम्, n. = शश-विषाण.<BR>—शशकाधम (˚क-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. a miserable little rabbit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशत्
शशत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, leaping, jumping, going by<BR>leaps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशमान
1. शशमान, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps to be connected<BR>with rt. 1. शम्, see 2. शशमान), Ved. praising,<BR>celebrating, offering praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाङ्क|शशांक|शशाङ्कः
शशाङ्क. See under शश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाण्डुलि|शशाण्डुलिः
शशाण्डुलि, इस्, or शशाण्डुली, f. a kind of gourd<BR>or cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिक
शशिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिन्
शशिन्, ई, m. ‘hare-marked,’ the moon, (see शश-<BR>धर); the emblem of a particular Arhat or Jina;<BR>(इनी), f. epithet of one of the sixteen digits of the<BR>moon.<BR>—शशि-कर, अस्, m. a moon-beam.<BR>—शशि-<BR>कला, f. a digit of the moon (of which there are<BR>sixteen, see कला); a species of Atiśakvarī metre<BR>(consisting of fifteen syllables to the Pāda); N. of<BR>a daughter of king Vīra-siṃha, (also called Candra-<BR>lekhā); of a daughter of Su-bandhu.<BR>—शशिकला-<BR>भरण (˚ला-आभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘ornamented with a<BR>digit of the moon,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शशि-कान्त,<BR>अस्, m. ‘moon-loved,’ the moon-gem or moon-stone,<BR>see चन्द्र-कान्त; (अम्), n. a lotus.<BR>—शशि-किरण,<BR>अस्, m. a ray or beam of the moon.<BR>—शशि-कोटि,<BR>इस्, f. a horn of the moon.<BR>—शशि-ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>‘moon-seizure,’ an eclipse of the moon.<BR>—शशि-ज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘moon-born,’ ‘son of the moon,’ epithet of<BR>Budha or Mercury.<BR>—शशि-देव, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king, (also called Ranti-deva.)<BR>—शशि-धामन्, अ, n.<BR>the splendor or lustre of the moon.<BR>—शशि-ध्वज,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the king of Bhallāṭa-nagara, q. v.<BR>—शशि-पाद, अस्, m. a moon-beam.<BR>—शशि-प्र-<BR>भा, f. the lustre or radiance of the moon, moon-<BR>light; (अस्, आ, अम्), having the lustre of the moon,<BR>radiant as the moon; (आ), f. a proper N.; (अम्), n.<BR>the white esculent water-lily; = मुक्ता (according to<BR>Śabda-k.).<BR>—शशि-भास्, आस्, f. a moon-beam.<BR>—श-<BR>शि-भूषण, अस्, m. ‘moon-decorated,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva; [cf. शशि-शेखर.]<BR>—शशि-मयूख, अस्,<BR>m. a ray of the moon, moon-beam.<BR>—शशि-मुख,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, ‘moon-faced,’ having a beautiful face.<BR>—शशि-मौलि, इस्, m. ‘moon-crested,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—शशि-रश्मि, इस्, m. a moon-beam.<BR>—शशि-<BR>लेखा, f. ‘moon-streak,’ a digit of the moon; the<BR>plant Menispermum Glabrum or another plant (=<BR>गुडूची); N. of an Apsaras; a kind of metre (either<BR>a variety of the Atijagatī or of the Atiśakvarī; cf.<BR>शशि-कला).<BR>—शशि-वदना, f. ‘moon-faced,’ a<BR>woman with a beautiful face; a species of the Gā-<BR>yatrī metre.<BR>—शशि-वर्धन, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—शशि-वाटिका, f. a particular plant (= पुनर्-णवा).<BR>—शशि-शेखर, अस्, m. ‘moon-crested,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva (as represented with a crescent of the moon on<BR>his brow); of one of the Jaina pontiffs.<BR>—शशीश<BR>(˚शि-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the moon,’ Śiva.<BR>—श-<BR>शीश-शिशु-शी, ईस्, m. wounding the child of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशीयस्
शशीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. springing, leaping,<BR>assailing, (Sāy. = उत्प्लवमान, leaping up, Ṛg-<BR>veda IV. 32, 3); (असी), f., N. of the queen of king<BR>Taranta (Ṛg-veda V. 61, 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशमान
शशमान 2. शशमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>1. शम्; for 1. शशमान see col. 1), Ved. one<BR>who has pacified, &c.; being pacified, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशय
शशय शशय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शी), Ved.<BR>lying, reposing, being, (Sāy. = शयान, वर्तमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशयान
शशयान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. lying, reposing, sleep-<BR>ing, (Sāy. = शिश्यान, Ṛg-veda VII. 103, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्रमाण
शश्रमाण शश्रमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>श्रम्), Ved. toiling, struggling, serving laboriously<BR>or diligently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वचै
शश्वचै शश्वचै (fr. rt. श्वच्), Ved., accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 33, 10 = परिष्वज-<BR>नाय, connecting it with rt. श्वज् or स्वञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वत्|शश्वन्त्
शश्वत् शश्वत् (probably a reduplicated form<BR>fr. rt. श्वि, cf. विश्व; the form of the nom. masc.<BR>appears to be doubtful, but अती, अत् are found for the<BR>nom. fem. and neut., the latter being used adverbi-<BR>ally), ‘continually increasing,’ lasting, perpetual, con-<BR>tinuous (Ved.); many, numerous, (Sāy. and Naigh.<BR>III. 1 = बहु); (अत्), ind. perpetually, externally,<BR>continually, repeatedly, frequently, always, again and<BR>again, (शश्वच्-छश्वत्, again and again, constantly);<BR>(अती), f., N. of a woman belonging to the family of<BR>Aṅgiras (authoress of Ṛg-veda VIII. 1, 34); [cf.<BR>Gr. πᾶς for ἅπας.]<BR>—शश्वच्-छान्ति, इस्, f. (for<BR>शश्वत्-शान्ति), everlasting peace or tranquillity,<BR>eternal rest.<BR>—शश्वत्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most<BR>constant, very regular or frequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्व
शश्व, Nom. P. शश्वति = शश्वायते (Vopa-deva<BR>XXI. 8).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वधा
शश्वधा, ind., Ved. constantly, continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वाय
शश्वाय, Nom. A. शश्वायते, &c., to be or<BR>become eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्
शष् शष् [cf. rt. 1. शस्], cl. 1. P. शषति,<BR>शशाष, शषितुम्, to hurt, injure, strike,<BR>wound, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्कुल|शष्कुलः
शष्कुल शष्कुल, अस्, m. a particular plant<BR>or tree, = छित्ति, करञ्ज; (ई), f. the orifice of the<BR>ear, auditory passage; rice-gruel or barley-water<BR>(mixed with rice, sesamum, and other grain); a sort<BR>of fish (called Saurī in Hindī); a kind of baked cake<BR>or pie (= शस्कुली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्प|शष्पं|शष्पः
शष्प शष्प. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस् 1. शस् (said to be connected with<BR>rt. 1. शम्, cf. rt. शष्), cl. 1. P. शसति,<BR>शशास (3rd pl. शशसुः), शसितुम्, to cut, wound,<BR>hurt, injure, strike, kill, destroy; [cf. Lat. hostia;<BR>Goth. hunsl; Angl. Sax. husel.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्प|शष्पं|शष्पः
शष्प, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 28.<BR>fr. rt. 1. शस् above), young grass [cf. 2. शस्य]; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. loss of intellect or of confidence (= प्र-<BR>तिभा-क्षय, in this sense only masc. according<BR>to some); [cf. Lat. cœspes.]<BR>—शष्प-भुज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, eating grass, any animal feeding on grass.<BR>—शष्-<BR>प-वृषी, f. a seat of Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसन|शसनं
शसन, अम्, n. the act of wounding, killing,<BR>immolation, slaughtering an animal in sacrifice; [cf.<BR>शमन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसित
शसित in वि-शसित, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसितृ
शसितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a cutter, wounder. See वि-<BR>शसितृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसित्वा
शसित्वा, ind. having wounded or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
2. शस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. शस्त see p. 985,<BR>col. 2), wounded, injured; struck, killed, (प्र-<BR>शस्त, destroyed.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तक|शस्तकं
शस्तक, अम्, n. (probably to be connected with<BR>rt. 1. शस्, by some referred to 1. शस्त), a defence<BR>for the finger of an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तृ
शस्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a cutter &c., in वि-शस्तृ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्र|शस्त्रं|शस्त्रः
2. शस्त्र, अम्, n. (for 1. शस्त्र see p. 985, col. 2),<BR>an instrument for cutting or wounding, a cutting<BR>weapon, a weapon or arms (in general); an instru-<BR>ment or tool; iron; steel; (अस्), m. a sword, scymitar;<BR>(ई), f. a knife.<BR>—शस्त्र-कार, अस्, m. ‘weapon-<BR>maker,’ an armourer.<BR>—शस्त्र-कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>skilled or expert in arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-कोश, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">Page0997-c+ 81</a>]<BR>the sheath of a weapon.<BR>—शस्त्रकोश-तरु, उस्, m.<BR>a particular tree (= पिण्डी-तरु).<BR>—शस्त्र-क्षत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, killed by weapons.<BR>—शस्त्र-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. taking arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-ग्राहिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘weapon-taker,’ ‘weapon-holder,’ an armed man.<BR>—शस्त्र-घुष्ट-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, making a noise<BR>with iron weapons, &c.<BR>—शस्त्र-जाल, अम्, n. a<BR>quantity of weapons.<BR>—शस्त्र-जीविन्, ई, m. ‘living<BR>by weapons,’ a soldier by profession.<BR>—शस्त्र-त्या-<BR>ग, अस्, m. abandoning or throwing away a weapon.<BR>—शस्त्र-देवता, f. ‘weapon-deity,’ a deified<BR>weapon (represented as the offspring of Kṛśāśva,<BR>and according to some accounts one hundred in<BR>number).<BR>—शस्त्र-धर, अस्, m. ‘bearing weapons,’<BR>an armed man or soldier, a warrior.<BR>—शस्त्र-धा-<BR>रण, अम्, n. the act of carrying arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-<BR>धारण-जीवक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who lives by<BR>carrying arms; (अस्), m. a soldier.<BR>—शस्त्र-धा-<BR>रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, bearing arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-नित्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who is continually under arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-<BR>न्यास, अस्, m. the laying down of arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-<BR>पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘weapon-handed,’ bearing arms or<BR>weapons, armed; (इस्), m. an armed warrior.<BR>—शस्-<BR>त्र-पाणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, = शस्त्र-पाणि.<BR>—शस्त्र-पात,<BR>अस्, m. the fall or stroke of a weapon.<BR>—शस्त्र-<BR>पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, purified by arms, absolved from<BR>guilt by dying in the field of battle.<BR>—शस्त्र-प्र-<BR>हरण, अस्, आ, अम्, striking or wounding with<BR>weapons, using arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-प्रहार, अस्, m. a<BR>wound inflicted with a weapon.<BR>—शस्त्र-भृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, bearing weapons; (त्), m. an armed man; a<BR>soldier, warrior.<BR>—शस्त्र-मार्ज, अस्, m. a weapon-<BR>cleaner, furbisher, armourer.<BR>—शस्त्र-विद्या, f. the<BR>science of arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-विद्वस्, आन्, उषी, अत्,<BR>skilled in arms.<BR>—शस्त्र-वृत्ति, इस्, m. ‘making a<BR>livelihood by arms,’ a soldier, a man at arms.<BR>—शस्-<BR>त्र-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the science of arms, military<BR>science.<BR>—शस्त्र-शिखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, proud of (the<BR>practice of) weapons.<BR>—शस्त्र-संहति, इस्, f. or<BR>शस्त्र-समूह, अस्, m. a quantity or collection of<BR>weapons; an arsenal, armoury.<BR>—शस्त्र-सम्पात,<BR>अस्, m. descent or sudden fall of a number of weapons.<BR>—शस्त्र-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck or killed by a<BR>weapon.<BR>—शस्त्र-हस्त, अस्, m. ‘weapon-handed,’<BR>an armed man.<BR>—शस्त्राजीव (˚र-आज्˚), अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, living by arms; (अस्), m. a soldier; (ई), f.<BR>(with Śāktas) one of the eight Akulas.<BR>—शस्त्रा-<BR>भ्यास (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the practice of arms,<BR>military exercise (= अस्त्र-शिक्षा, खुरली).<BR>—शस्-<BR>त्रायस (˚र-अय्˚), अम्, n. iron; steel.<BR>—शस्त्रार्चिस्<BR>(˚र-अर्˚), इस्, इस्, इस्, blazing with weapons, one<BR>whose flame is a weapon.<BR>—शस्त्रास्त्र (˚र-अस्˚),<BR>अम्, n. weapons both for striking and throwing,<BR>arms and missile weapons, arms or weapons (gene-<BR>rally).<BR>—शस्त्रास्त्र-भृत्, त्, m. ‘bearing arms and<BR>missile weapons,’ a soldier, warrior.<BR>—शस्त्रास्त्र-<BR>भृत्-त्व, अम्, n. bearing arms for striking and<BR>throwing, the use of arms.<BR>—शस्त्रोत्थापन (˚र-<BR>उत्˚), अम्, n. the act of raising a weapon (so as to<BR>strike).<BR>—शस्त्रोद्यम (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m. lifting<BR>up a weapon.<BR>—शस्त्रोपकरण (˚र-उप्˚), अम्,<BR>n. arms and instruments of warfare, military appa-<BR>ratus.<BR>—शस्त्रोपजीविन् (˚र-उप्˚), ई, m. ‘living by<BR>arms,’ a soldier, a man at arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रक|शस्त्रकं
शस्त्रक, अम्, n. iron, steel; = 2. शस्त्र, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिक
शस्त्रिक, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of comps.), having<BR>a knife; (आ), f. a knife, blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिन्
शस्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having weapons, bearing arms,<BR>armed, armed with a sword, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्री
शस्त्री, f. a knife. See under 2. शस्त्र, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्वा
शस्त्वा, ind. having wounded, having hurt, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्प|शस्पं|शस्पः
शस्प, अम्, n. [cf. शष्प], young grass; loss of<BR>confidence or of understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
2. शस्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. शस्य see under rt.<BR>शंस्, p. 985), to be cut, to be wounded or injured;<BR>(अम्), n. corn or grain (in general); the fruit or<BR>produce of any plant or tree.<BR>—शस्य-क्षेत्र, अम्,<BR>n. a corn-field.<BR>—शस्य-ध्वंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroy-<BR>ing corn; (ई), m. the tree Cedrela Tunna (= तुन्न,<BR>and commonly called Toon).<BR>—शस्य-भक्षक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, corn-eating, granivorous; an eater of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">Page0998-a+ 76</a>]<BR>corn.<BR>—शस्य-भक्षण, अम्, n. the act of feed-<BR>ing upon grain.<BR>—शस्य-मञ्जरी, f. an ear or spike<BR>of corn; a fruit-stalk.<BR>—शस्य-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>garlanded with fruits, crowned with harvests (as the<BR>earth).<BR>—शस्य-रक्षक, अस्, m. ‘corn-guardian,’<BR>a watchman set to guard a field of corn.<BR>—शस्य-<BR>शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, abounding with corn.<BR>—शस्य-शूक,<BR>अम्, n. an awn or beard of corn.<BR>—शस्य-सम्पद्,<BR>त्, f. abundance of corn.<BR>—शस्य-सम्बर, अस्, m.<BR>the Śāl tree, Shorea Robusta.<BR>—शस्याद् (˚य-अद्),<BR>त्, त्, त्, eating grain.<BR>—शस्यारु (˚य-आरु?), उस्, m.<BR>a small variety of the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस् 2. शस्, cl. 2. P. शस्ति, &c., to sleep,<BR>= सस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस् 3. शस्, the technical case-termination<BR>of the accusative plural; the Taddhita affix शस् (form-<BR>ing adverbs from nouns, especially from numerals<BR>and words expressive of quantity, see शत-शस्,<BR>बहु-शस्, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्कुली
शस्कुली शस्कुली, f. a kind of baked cake<BR>or pie, (also written शष्कुली.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्ति|शस्तिः
शस्ति शस्ति, &c. See under rt. शंस्, p. 985.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्मन्
शस्मन् शस्मन्, शस्यमान, &c. See under<BR>rt. शंस्, p. 985.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
शस्य 1. and 2. शस्य. See under rts.<BR>शंस् and 1. शस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांशप|शांशपः
शांशप शांशप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शिंशपा with<BR>substitution of आ for इ), made of Śiṃśapā wood, &c.;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of cup or ladle made of Śiṃśapā wood;<BR>a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांशपायन|शांशपायनः
शांशपायन, अस्, m. a patronymic of Su-śar-<BR>man; N. of a Muni, teacher of the Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांशपायनि
शांशपायनि, इस्, m., N. of the author of a<BR>Saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांशपायनिका
शांशपायनिका, f., scil. सं-हिता, the Saṃhitā<BR>of Śāṃśapāyani.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक|शाकं|शाकः
शाक शाक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शक्), Ved.<BR>strong, mighty, powerful; (अम्, अस्), n. m. any herb<BR>‘able to be eaten,’ a vegetable, herb, pot-herb, greens,<BR>any edible leaf or fruit or root &c. used as a vege-<BR>table; (अस्), m. power, strength, energy, force; the<BR>Śirīṣa tree, Acacia Sirīsa; the Teak tree (= खर-<BR>पत्त्र); N. of the sixth of the seven Dvīpas<BR>(surrounded by the sea of milk or white sea,<BR>and inhabited by the Ṛta-vratas, Satya-vratas,<BR>Dāna-vratas, and Anu-vratas); N. of a people<BR>(the Śākas or Scythians); of a king; an era,<BR>period (usually commencing with some celebrated<BR>prince, as Yudhi-ṣṭhira, Vikramāditya, Śāli-vāhana,<BR>who are hence denominated Śākeśvarās; but applied<BR>especially to the era of Śāli-vāhana, commencing<BR>from the birth of that king, seventy-eight years after<BR>Christ); (आ), f., N. of a plant (= हरीतकी).<BR>—शाक-<BR>चुक्रिका, f. the tamarind (= चिञ्चा).<BR>—शाक-तरु,<BR>उस्, m. the Teak tree; the plant Capparis Trifoliata.<BR>—शाक-दास, अस्, m., N. of a teacher of the Sāma-<BR>veda.<BR>—शाक-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of a Dvīpa, (see<BR>above.)<BR>—शाकद्वीपीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to<BR>Śāka-dvīpa.<BR>—शाक-पण, अस्, m. a handful of vege-<BR>tables, &c. [cf. पण], a measure equal to a hand-<BR>ful.<BR>—शाक-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a particular plant or tree<BR>(= शिग्रु).<BR>—शाक-पात्र, अम्, n. a vessel for vege-<BR>tables, vegetable dish.<BR>—शाक-पार्थिव, अस्, m. the<BR>king of the period or era; [cf. मध्यम-पद-<BR>लोप.]<BR>—शाक-प्रति, ind. a little cowage.<BR>—शाक-<BR>बालेय, अस्, m. a particular plant (= ब्रह्म-यष्टि,<BR>बालेय-शाक).<BR>—शाकम्-भरी, f. ‘herb-nourishing,’<BR>epithet of Durgā; of a city (supposed to be the<BR>modern Sāmbhar); observances in honour of Durgā<BR>(according to some).<BR>—शाकम्भरीय, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of fossil salt from a lake in the vicinity of the<BR>town Śāmbhara or Sāmbhar in Ajmere.<BR>—शाक-<BR>योग्य, अस्, m. coriander (= धान्यक).<BR>—शाक-<BR>रचित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. composed of vegetables, &c.<BR>—शाक-राज, अस्, m. a particular pot-herb (= वास्-<BR>तूक).<BR>—शाक-विल्व or शाक-विल्वक, अस्, m. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">Page0998-b+ 78</a>]<BR>egg-plant, Solanum Melongena.<BR>—शाक-वीर, अस्,<BR>m. a particular herb, Chenopodium Album.<BR>—शाक-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m. the Teak tree.<BR>—शाक-व्रत, अम्,<BR>n. a particular vow, abstinence from vegetables, &c.<BR>—शाक-शाकट or शाक-शाकिन, अम्, n. a field<BR>cultivated for esculent plants, a field of vegetables,<BR>kitchen garden.<BR>—शाक-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. ‘best of<BR>herbs,’ a kind of vegetable, Chenopodium Album;<BR>(आ), f. a particular plant (= जीवन्ती); a kind of<BR>shrub (= डोडी); the egg-plant.<BR>—शाकाख्य (˚क-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, m. the Teak tree; (अम्), n. a vegetable,<BR>pot-herb, esculent plant.<BR>—शाकाङ्ग (˚क-अङ्˚), अम्,<BR>n. pepper (as an accessory to vegetables).<BR>—शाकाम्ल<BR>(˚क-अम्˚), अम्, n. the hog-plum (= वृक्षाम्ल).<BR>—शाकाम्ल-भेदन, अम्, n. sorrel (= चुक्र).<BR>—शाकालाबु (˚क-अल्˚), उस्, m. a species of gourd or<BR>cucumber (= राजालाबु).<BR>—शाकाष्टका (˚क-अष्˚),<BR>f. a festival on the eighth day of the second half of<BR>the month Māgha.<BR>—शाकाहार (˚क-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>eating vegetables, living on herbs, a vegetarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकिन्
शाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessed of power, powerful,<BR>mighty (Ved.); having vegetables or herbs; (इनी), f.,<BR>scil. भूमि, land planted with vegetables or pot-<BR>herbs, a field of vegetables; a kind of female demon<BR>or fairy attendant on Durgā; [cf. डाकिनी, योगिनी,<BR>खे-चरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकिन|शाकिनं
शाकिन, अम्, n. a field (at the end of a comp.,<BR>e. g. इक्षु-श्˚, a field of sugar-canes; cf. शाक-श्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकट|शाकटं|शाकटः
शाकट शाकट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शकट), be-<BR>longing or relating to a cart (as a load, horse, &c.),<BR>going in a cart, drawing a cart; (अस्), m. any yoked<BR>animal, a draught-ox; a kind of tree (= श्लेष्मान्-<BR>तक); (अम्), n. a field (at the end of a comp., e. g.<BR>इक्षु-श्˚, a field of sugar-canes; cf. शाक-श्˚).<BR>—शा-<BR>कटाख्य (˚ट-आख्˚), अस्, m. a particular tree (=<BR>1. धव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटायन|शाकटायनः
शाकटायन, अस्, m., N. of a philologist and<BR>grammarian (generally mentioned with Pāṇinī,<BR>Amara, Jainendra, Kāśa-kṛtsna, Jayanta, Candra,<BR>&c.); of the author of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटायनि
शाकटायनि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटिक|शाकटिकः
शाकटिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to a cart, &c.,<BR>going in or on a cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटीन|शाकटीनः
शाकटीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>cart; (अस्), m. a cart-load, a measure of weight or<BR>value equal to a cart-load (= 20 Tulās).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपूणि|शाकपूणिः
शाकपूणि शाकपूणि, इस्, m. (sometimes writ-<BR>ten शाकपूर्णि), N. of an ancient interpreter of the<BR>Veda (quoted as an authority in the Nirukta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकरी
शाकरी शाकरी, f. (probably for शाकारी),<BR>scil. वि-भाषा, one of the Vibhaṣās or corrupt<BR>dialects (that spoken by the Śakāra, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकल|शाकलः
शाकल शाकल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शकल, but in<BR>some senses fr. शाकल्य), relating to a piece or por-<BR>tion; (अस्), m. a school of the Ṛg-veda (whose<BR>founder is thought to have been the elder Śākalya,<BR>see below); a kind of sacrifice or sacrificial ceremony<BR>(one performed according to the rites of the Śākala<BR>school); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a tribe inhabiting Bhā-<BR>rata-varṣa; the followers of the Śākala school of<BR>the Veda; (अम्), n. a fragment, splinter (Ved. = श-<BR>कल); N. of the Ṛg-veda Prātiśākhya, (see below);<BR>N. of a town, (also read Sākala.)<BR>—शाकल-प्राति-<BR>शाख्य, अम्, n., N. of the Ṛg-veda Prātiśākhya<BR>ascribed to Śaunaka and preserved by his pupils for<BR>the use of the Śākalas or their school, (this is the<BR>only one of the numerous Ṛg-veda Prātiśākhyas<BR>that has come down to us; it is written in verse,<BR>the metres consisting of a mixture of the Śloka with<BR>other more ancient kinds.)<BR>—शाकल-शाखा, f. ‘the<BR>Śākala branch,’ i. e. the recension or traditional text<BR>of the Ṛg-veda preserved by the Śākalas (the only<BR>extant recension).<BR>—शाकल-संहिता, f. the Saṃhitā<BR>of Śākala.<BR>—शाकल-होम, अस्, m. a particular kind of<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—शाकलहोमीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or<BR>belonging to the Śākala-homa (Manu XI. 256).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलक|शाकलकः
शाकलक, अस्, m. a follower of Śakala (?) or of<BR>Śākalya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलिक|शाकलिकः
शाकलिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to Śa-<BR>kala, belonging to a piece or part, having a piece or<BR>portion, fragmentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकल्य|शाकल्यः
शाकल्य, अस्, m., N. of a poet; of an ancient<BR>grammarian (who preceded Pāṇini and is referred<BR>to four times in his grammar; he is supposed to<BR>have arranged the Pada text of the Ṛg-veda; there<BR>appear, however, to have been two Śākalyas, an<BR>elder called शाकल्य-पितृ, ‘the father of Śākalya’<BR>or Sthavira, and a younger whose opinions differed<BR>from those of his father).<BR>—शाकल्य-पितृ, ता, m.<BR>the father of Śākalya.<BR>—शाकल्य-संहिता-परि-<BR>शिष्ट, अम्, n. a sequel or supplement to the Saṃ-<BR>hitā of Śākalya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकार
शाकार शाकार, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शकार), act-<BR>ing or speaking like a Śakāra, i. e. in a low man-<BR>ner; (ई), f. the corrupt dialect spoken by the Śakāra,<BR>(see शकार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुण|शाकुणः
शाकुण शाकुण, अस्, ई, अम्, repentant, regret-<BR>ting, (according to Śabda-k. = परोत्तापिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन|शाकुनः
शाकुन शाकुन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शकुन), belong-<BR>ing or relating to birds; relating to omens, ominous,<BR>portentous.<BR>—शाकुन-सारोद्धार (˚र-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a treatise on omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनिक|शाकुनिकः
शाकुनिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to birds, belonging<BR>to omens, ominous; (अस्), m. a fowler, bird-catcher;<BR>(अम्), n. interpretation of omens or dreams, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनेय|शाकुनेयः
शाकुनेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to birds or omens;<BR>(अस्), m. a small owl (= डुण्डुल); N. of a Muni,<BR>(शाकुनेया धर्माः, the laws of Śākuneya.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तल|शाकुंतल|शाकुंतलः|शाकुन्तलः
शाकुन्तल शाकुन्तल, अस्, m. (fr. शकुन्तला),<BR>a metronymic of Bharata (sovereign of India as son<BR>of Śakuntalā and Dushyanta); (अम्), n. the drama<BR>commonly called Śakuntalā or Abhijñāna-śakuntala.<BR>—शाकुन्तलोपख्यान (˚ल-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an<BR>episode of the Mahā-bhārata (Ādi-parvan 2815-<BR>3125, giving an account of the love of Śakuntalā<BR>and Dushyanta, and of the origin of the family of<BR>the Bharatas; Kalidāsa derived the materials for his<BR>drama called Śakuntalā from this source).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तलेय|शाकुंतलेयः|शाकुन्तलेयः
शाकुन्तलेय, अस्, m. a metronymic of Bharata<BR>(= शाकुन्तल above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुलिक|शाकुलिकः
शाकुलिक शाकुलिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शकुल),<BR>belonging to fish; (अस्), m. a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्कर|शाक्करः
शाक्कर शाक्कर, अस्, m. (fr. शक्कर), an ox;<BR>(अम्), n. a particular kind of metre; [cf. शक्करी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्की
शाक्की शाक्की, f., N. of one of the five Vi-<BR>bhāṣās or corrupt dialects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त|शाक्तः
शाक्त शाक्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शक्ति), relating<BR>to power or energy, relating to Śakti or the divine<BR>energy under its female personification; (अस्), m. a<BR>worshipper of the divine power under its female<BR>representation, (this power or energy which was at<BR>first regarded as the mere will of the Supreme Being<BR>willing to create the universe was afterwards thought<BR>of as a separate deity, and identified with the wives<BR>of the Triad, Sarasvatī being the Śakti or Energy of<BR>Brahman, Lakṣmī of Viṣṇu, and Durgā of Śiva,<BR>but the latter being the Destroyer, his Energy became<BR>the personification of everything terrible, and his<BR>wife Durgā, representing this terrific power, became<BR>a favourite object of propitiation and worship; hence<BR>the Śāktas are generally worshippers of Durgā, and<BR>form one of the three principal sects of the Hindūs;<BR>the tenets of this sect are contained in the Tantras<BR>[see तन्त्र], and the ritual enjoined is of two<BR>kinds, the impurer being called वामाचार, q. v.,<BR>the purer दक्षिणाचार, q. v., which has led to a<BR>division of the sect into Vāmācārins and Dakṣiṇā-<BR>cārins); a teacher, preceptor (Ved., Sāy. = शक्ति-<BR>मत्, शिक्षक).<BR>—शाक्त-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Tantra work.<BR>—शाक्त-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work by Abhinava-gupta.<BR>—शाक्तानन्द-तरङ्गिणी<BR>(˚त-आन्˚), f., N. of a work compiled for the use of<BR>the Śāktas from the Tantras and Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तिक|शाक्तिकः
शाक्तिक, अस्, m. a worshipper of the Śakti or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">Page0999-a+ 78</a>]<BR>female personification of the divine energy, a Śākta,<BR>(see above); a spearman, (see शाक्तीक below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तीक|शाक्तीकः
शाक्तीक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>spear, spearing, speared; (अस्), m. a spearman,<BR>lancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तेय|शाक्तेयः
शाक्तेय, अस्, m. a worshipper of the Śakti, a<BR>Śākta, q. v.; the son of Śakti, i. e. Parāśara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त्य|शाक्त्यः
शाक्त्य, अस्, m. a worshipper of the female prin-<BR>ciple or Śakti; a patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi<BR>Gauri-vīti; of Parāśara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्मन्
शाक्मन् शाक्मन्, अ, n. = शक्मन्, Ved.<BR>power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्य|शाक्यः
शाक्य शाक्य, अस्, m. (fr. शाक or fr. rt.<BR>1. शक्), N. of the family of the Buddha par excel-<BR>lence (founder of the Buddhist religion); N. of<BR>Buddha himself, (see बुद्ध); N. of a son of<BR>Sañjaya.<BR>—शाक्य-भिक्षुक, अस्, m. a Buddhist<BR>ascetic or kind of religious mendicant; (ई), f. a<BR>Buddhist nun.<BR>—शाक्य-मुनि, इस्, m. ‘the Śākya<BR>saint,’ epithet of Buddha.<BR>—शाक्य-वंश, अस्, m.<BR>the Śākya family.<BR>—शाक्यवंशावतीर्ण (˚श-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. ‘incarnate in the family of the Śākyas,’<BR>epithet of Buddha.<BR>—शाक्य-सिंह, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>Śākya lion,’ epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्र
शाक्र शाक्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शक्र), relating<BR>to Śakra or Indra; (ई), f. the wife of Indra; N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्वर|शाक्वरः
शाक्वर शाक्वर, अस्, m. an ox; a bull, (see<BR>शाक्कर); a patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Ṛṣa-<BR>bha; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman (identified with the<BR>Rathantara-sāman in Aitareya-Br. IV. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख्
शाख् शाख् (= rt. श्लाख्), cl. 1. P. शाखति,<BR>शाखितुम्, to embrace, pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख|शाखः
शाख, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. शाख्, but accord-<BR>ing to others fr. rt. 1. शक्), a particular plant (= छित्ति);<BR>N. of Kumāra or Kārttikeya; of a son of Kumāra;<BR>of a place; (आ), f. the branch of a tree &c., a branch<BR>(in general); any part or division of an animal; an<BR>arm; a finger (Ved., the fingers being compared to<BR>branches); a sect, faction, party; a subdivision, sec-<BR>tion (of any work); a branch or school or traditional<BR>recension of the Vedas, (i. e. the Saṃhitā or collection<BR>of Mantras and the Brāhmaṇas in each Veda as re-<BR>ceived in conflicting schools, modified more or less<BR>both in variations of the actual text and in difference<BR>of arrangement, and even of interpretation; the<BR>work शाखा or branch is sometimes used to dis-<BR>tinguish the three original Vedas from each other,<BR>as when it is said that ‘Sāma hymns ought not to<BR>be recited in the neighbourhood of another Śākhā,’<BR>i. e. of the other two Vedas; but it properly<BR>applies to the various recensions or editions of any<BR>of the original Vedas handed down by different<BR>Caraṇas, i. e. by different schools or sects, each ad-<BR>hering to its own traditional text and interpretation:<BR>in the Caraṇa-vyūha, a work by Śaunaka treating of<BR>these various schools, five Śākhās are enumerated of<BR>the Ṛg-veda, viz. those of the Śākalas, Bāṣkalas,<BR>Āśvalāyanas, Śānkhāyanas, and Māṇḍukāyanas; forty-<BR>two or forty-four out of eighty-six are mentioned of<BR>the Yajur-veda, fifteen of which belong to the Vāja-<BR>saneyins, including those of the Kāṇvas and Mādh-<BR>yandinas; twelve out of a thousand said to have once<BR>existed of the Sāma-veda and nine of the Atharva-<BR>veda; of all these, however, the Ṛg-veda is said to<BR>be now extant in one only, viz. the Śākala-śākhā,<BR>the Yajur-veda in three and partially in four, the<BR>Sāma-veda in one or perhaps two, and the Atharva-<BR>veda in one: although the words चरण and शाखा<BR>are sometimes used synonymously, yet चरण pro-<BR>perly applies to the sect or collection of persons united<BR>in one school, and शाखा to the traditional text<BR>followed, as in the phrase शाखाम् अधीते, he reads<BR>a particular recension of the Veda); any part of an<BR>animal devoid of sensibility (as a horn &c.); = अन्-<BR>तिक (according to Śabda-k.); [cf. Lith. szakā;<BR>Russ. suk; Hib. geag.]<BR>—शाखा-कण्ठ, अस्, m.<BR>a particular tree (= स्नुही).<BR>—शाखा-चङ्क्रमण,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">Page0999-b+ 77</a>]<BR>अम्, n. skipping from branch to branch, desultory<BR>study.<BR>—शाखा-चन्द्र-न्याय, अस्, m. ‘the rule of<BR>the moon on a bough,’ a phrase adduced as an illus-<BR>tration when an object seen or matter debated has<BR>its position or relation assigned to it merely from<BR>the appearance of contiguity or connection.<BR>—शाखा-<BR>ध्येतृ (˚खा-अध्˚), ता, m. the reader of a Śākhā,<BR>follower of any particular text of the Veda.<BR>—शाखा-<BR>नगर or शाखा-पुर, अम्, n. ‘branch-town,’ a<BR>suburb.<BR>—शाखान्तरीय-कर्मन्, अ, n. the (rule<BR>of) action belonging to another school or sect.<BR>—शा-<BR>खा-पित्त, अस्, m. inflammation of the extremities,<BR>(i. e. of the hands, feet, shoulders, &c.)<BR>—शाखा-<BR>प्रकृति, अयस्, f. pl. the eight remoter princes to<BR>be considered in time of war; [cf. प्र-कृति.]<BR>—शा-<BR>खा-भृत्, त्, m. ‘branch-bearer,’ a tree.<BR>—शाखा-<BR>भेद, अस्, m. difference of school, (see शाखा.)<BR>—शाखा-मृग, अस्, m. ‘branch-animal,’ a monkey,<BR>ape; a squirrel.<BR>—शाखामृग-गणायुत (˚ण-आय्),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, filled with or possessed of troops of<BR>monkeys.<BR>—शाखामृगानीक-पति (˚ग-अन्˚), इस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of troops of monkeys,’ epithet of Sugrīva.<BR>—शाखाम्ला (˚खा-अम्˚), f. a kind of plant (=<BR>वृक्षाम्ल).<BR>—शाखा-रण्ड, अस्, m. a man who<BR>is faithless or a traitor to his Śākhā, i. e. a Brāhman<BR>who has changed his peculiar school of the Vedas.<BR>—शाखा-रथ्या, f. a branch road (properly sixteen<BR>cubits in width).<BR>—शाखा-विलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, settled<BR>or sitting on branches (said of birds).<BR>—शाखा-शिफा,<BR>f. ‘branch-root,’ a root growing from a branch (as<BR>in the Indian fig, the branches of which shoot<BR>downwards to the ground and take fresh root there,<BR>= अव-रोह); a creeper growing upwards from the<BR>root of a tree towards the top (according to some).<BR>—शाखाश्रय (˚खा-आश्˚), अस्, m. recourse to a<BR>Śākhā, following a particular school.<BR>—शाखास्थि<BR>(˚खा-अस्˚), n. the bone of the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाल|शाखालः
शाखाल, अस्, m. a sort of cane (= वानीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखिन्
शाखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having branches (literally or<BR>figuratively), branched, branching, ramifying; be-<BR>longing to any branch or school or sect, &c.; (ई),<BR>m. a tree; a Veda (as having various branches or<BR>schools); the follower of any school or sect, (often<BR>at the end of a comp., e. g. माध्यन्दिन-शाखिन्,<BR>a follower of the Mādhyandina school of the Vāja-<BR>saneyins, cf. काण्व-श्˚); an inhabitant of the northern<BR>districts bordering on India, a Turk, Tartar (= तु-<BR>रुष्क); N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख्य|शाख्यः
शाख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the branch of a<BR>tree, branching, ramifying (literally or figuratively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखोट|शाखोटः
शाखोट शाखोट or शाखोटक, अस्, m. the<BR>small tree Trophis Aspera (= पिशाच-द्रु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्कर|शांकर|शाङ्करं|शांकरः|शाङ्करः
शाङ्कर शाङ्कर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शङ्कर), be-<BR>longing to or composed by Śaṅkara; (अस्), m. a<BR>bull; (अम्), n. a form of metre; [cf. शाक्कर,<BR>शार्कर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्करि|शांकरि|शांकरिः|शाङ्करिः
शाङ्करि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Kārttikeya; of<BR>Gaṇeśa; fire; N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्कुची
शाङ्कुची शाङ्कुची, f. the skate fish (= शङ्-<BR>कुची, शङ्कोच).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्ख|शांखं|शाङ्खः
शाङ्ख शाङ्ख, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शङ्ख), relat-<BR>ing to the conch-shell, belonging to shells; (अम्),<BR>n. the sound of a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खमित्रि
शाङ्खमित्रि, इस्, m., N. of a Vedic grammarian,<BR>(also written शाङ्खमित्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खायन|शाङ्खायनः
शाङ्खायन, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Śāṅkhāyana-Brāhmaṇa and of certain Śrauta-sūtras.<BR>—शाङ्खायन-चरण, N. of a Caraṇa of the Ṛg-<BR>veda.<BR>—शाङ्खायन-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa (belonging to the Ṛg-veda; see ब्राह्-<BR>मण.)<BR>—शाङ्खायन-सूत्र, अम्, n. the Śrauta-<BR>sūtras attributed to Śāṅkhāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खायनिन्
शाङ्खायनिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the pupils of Śāṅ-<BR>khāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खिक|शांखिक|शांखिकः|शाङ्खिकः
शाङ्खिक, अस्, ई, अम्, made from the Śaṅkha,<BR>relating or belonging to the conch-shell or to any<BR>shell, shelly; (अस्), m. a shell-cutter, worker or dealer<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">Page0999-c+ 74</a>]<BR>in shells (constituting a particular caste called Śāṅ-<BR>khāri); a player on the Śaṅkha, shell-blower (=<BR>शङ्ख-ध्मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्गुष्ठा
शाङ्गुष्ठा शाङ्गुष्ठा, f. the shrub Abrus<BR>Precatorius (= गुञ्जा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्गोष्ठा
शाङ्गोष्ठा, f. another reading for शार्ङ्गष्ठा,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाचि
शाचि शाचि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. शच्, cf. शचि),<BR>distinguished, renowned; strong.<BR>—शाचि-गु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. having strong or renowned cattle; having<BR>powerful or clearly manifested rays.<BR>—शाचि-पूजन,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. vehement or earnest worship; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), Ved. having strong or earnest worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट|शाटः
शाट शाट, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शट्), a petticoat;<BR>a particular clean or white garment, gown; cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटक|शाटकं|शाटकः
शाटक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a petticoat, garment, cloth; a<BR>kind of play (= नाटक, according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटिका
शाटिका, f. a particular plant, the Zedoary (= शटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटी
शाटी, f. = शाट above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट्यायन|शाट्यायनं|शाट्यायनः
शाट्यायन शाट्यायन, अस्, m., N. of a Muni;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Brāhmaṇa; a particular oblation<BR>for remedying anything wrong in the performance<BR>of an act or rite; (अस्, ई, अम्), of or belonging to<BR>Śāṭyāyana or to the Śāṭyāyana-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—शाट्या-<BR>यन-होम, अस्, m. the above oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट्यायनक
शाट्यायनक, अम्, n. a passage from the Śāṭyā-<BR>yana-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट्यायनि
शाट्यायनि, इस्, m., N. of the author of a law-<BR>book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट्यायनिन्
शाट्यायनिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the followers of the<BR>Śāṭyāyana-Brāhmaṇa; N. of a Śākhā belonging to<BR>the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाठ्य|शाठ्यं
शाठ्य शाठ्य, अम्, n. (fr. शठ), wicked-<BR>ness, villainy, dishonesty, perfidy, deceit, roguery,<BR>knavery, hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाठ्यायनीय
शाठ्यायनीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Śākhā or<BR>school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड्
शाड् शाड्, cl. 1. A. शाडते, शाडितुम्, = rt.<BR>शाल्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड्वल|शाड्वलः
शाड्वल शाड्वल, अस्, आ, अम् (= शाद्वल),<BR>abounding in fresh grass, green, verdant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण|शाणं|शाणः
शाण 1. शाण, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. rt. शो), a<BR>whetstone, grindstone; touchstone [cf. शान]; a saw;<BR>[cf. Gr. κῶνο-ς, κωνίο-ν, κωνί-ς; Lat. cuneu-s; Engl.<BR>hone; Old Norse hein; Angl. Sax. hœnan.]<BR>—शाणा-<BR>जीव (˚ण-आज्˚), अस्, m. ‘living by a whetstone,’ an<BR>armourer.<BR>—शाणाश्म-घर्षण (˚ण-अश्˚), अम्, n.<BR>rubbing (anything) on a touchstone or whetstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणित|शाणितः
शाणित, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpened on a grindstone,<BR>whetted, ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण|शाणं|शाणः
शाण 2. शाण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शण), made of<BR>hemp or Bengal flax, hempen, flaxen; (अस्, ई), m. f.<BR>a weight of four Māṣas; (अम्), n. cloth made of<BR>hemp, coarse cloth, sack-cloth, canvas; a hempen<BR>garment; (ई), f. a hempen cloth or garment; a new<BR>unseamed and single breadth of cloth (given to a<BR>student at his investiture for his upper garment),<BR>ragged or torn raiment; coarse or tattered clothes<BR>given to a Jaina ascetic at his initiation; a small<BR>tent or screen (especially one used as a retiring-room<BR>for actors, tumblers, &c.); gesture, gesticulation,<BR>making signs with the hands or eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणि|शाणिः
शाणि, इस्, m. a plant from the fibres of which a<BR>coarse cloth or cordage is prepared, Corchorus Oli-<BR>torius (= पट्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणीर|शाणीरं
शाणीर शाणीर, अम्, n. (according to Śabda-<BR>k.) a bank in the Śoṇa river (or, according to some,<BR>in the river Dardarī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्ड
शाण्ड शाण्ड, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल
शाण्डिल शाण्डिल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शण्डिल),<BR>descended from Śaṇḍila, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिलीपुत्र
शाण्डिली-पुत्र, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिलीमातृ
शाण्डिली-मातृ, ता, f. a matron descended from<BR>Śaṇḍila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0999-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिलेय
शाण्डिलेय, अस्, m. a descendant of Śaṇḍila or of<BR>Śāṇḍilya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल्य|शांडिल्य|शांडिल्यः|शाण्डिल्यः
शाण्डिल्य, अस्, -ली, अम्, descended from Śaṇḍila;<BR>coming from Śāṇḍilya, composed by Śāṇḍilya; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a Muni or sage (from whom one of the<BR>three principal families of the Kanouj or Kānyakubja<BR>Brāhmans is said to be descended; he is the author<BR>of a law-book and of the Bhakti-sūtras); a form of<BR>Agni or fire; a kind of tree, Ægle Marmelos (=<BR>विल्व).<BR>—शाण्डिल्य-गोत्र, अम्, n. the family of<BR>Śāṇḍilya.<BR>—शाण्डिल्य-विद्या, f. the doctrine of Śāṇ-<BR>ḍilya (in the Chāndogya Upaniṣad).<BR>—शाण्डिल्य-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n. the aphorisms of Śāṇḍilya on faith<BR>and devotion (= भक्ति-सूत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल्यायन
शाण्डिल्यायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात|शातं|शातः
शात शात, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. शो, cf. शित; or<BR>in some senses perhaps to be regarded as an anom.<BR>past pass. part. of rt. शद्), sharpened, sharp, whetted;<BR>thin, slender, emaciated; weak, feeble; beautiful,<BR>handsome; happy, prosperous; (अम्), n. joy, plea-<BR>sure, happiness; the thorn-apple.<BR>—शात-शिख, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, sharp-pointed (as the nails &c.).<BR>—शातोदरी<BR>(˚त-उद्˚), f. a thin-waisted woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातन|शातनं
1. शातन, अम्, n. the act of sharpening, whetting;<BR>sharpness, thinness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकर्णि
शातकर्णि शातकर्णि, इस्, m. (fr. शत-कर्ण<BR>or शात-कर्ण?), N. of several Āndhra kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकुम्भ|शातकुंभ|शातकुंभं|शातकुम्भं|शातकुम्भः
शातकुम्भ, अम्, n. (fr. शत-कुम्भ), gold;<BR>the thorn-apple; (अस्), m. the plant Nerium Odorum<BR>(= करवीर).<BR>—शातकुम्भ-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made or consisting of gold, golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकौम्भ|शातकौंभ|शातकौंभं|शातकौम्भं
शातकौम्भ, अम्, n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपत्त्रक
शातपत्त्रक, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. शत-पत्त्र),<BR>moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातभिष
शातभिष, अस्, m. (fr. शत-भिषा), one who<BR>is born during the lunar mansion called शत-भिषा<BR>or शत-भिषज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातभिषज
शातभिषज, अस्, m. = शातभिष above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातभीरु|शातभीरुः
शातभीरु, उस्, m. (fr. शत-भीरु), a kind of<BR>Mallikā or Arabian jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमन्यव
शातमन्यव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शत-मन्यु), re-<BR>lating or belonging to Indra, worthy of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमान|शातमानं
शातमान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शत-मान), bought<BR>with the measure of one hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातवनेय
शातवनेय, अस्, m. (fr. शत-वनि), Ved. a son<BR>of Śata-vani.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातवाहन|शातवाहनः
शातवाहन, अस्, m. (fr. शत-वाहन), a proper<BR>N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातन|शातनं
शातन 1. शातन. See under शात above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपन्ता
शातपन्ता शातपन्ता, m. du., Ved., accord-<BR>ing to Say. on Ṛg-veda X. 106, 5 = सुखवन्तौ,<BR>‘possessors of happiness’ or ‘diminishers of unhappi-<BR>ness,’ (connected with rt. शो, तनू-करणे; in Naigh.<BR>III. 6. mentioned together with शिम्बाता and शत-रा<BR>among the सुख-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातय
शातय शातय. See under rt. शद्, p. 991.<BR>शातक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातन|शातनं
2. शातन, अम्, n. causing to fall or perish, causing<BR>to wither or decay; cutting off, withering, decaying;<BR>becoming thin or small, (in this sense perhaps con-<BR>nected with rt. शो, see शात.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातित
शातित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to fall or perish, over-<BR>thrown; cut off, (perhaps connected with rt. शो.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातिन्
शातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, cutting off, (at the end of a comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातला
शातला शातला, f. a particular plant or<BR>shrub (= सातला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातातप
शातातप शातातप, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of a law-book; [cf. वृहच्-छातातप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातातपीय
शातातपीय, अस्, आ, अम्, composed by Śātātapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रव|शात्रवं|शात्रवः
शात्रव शात्रव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शत्रु), be-<BR>longing to an enemy, hostile; (अस्), m. an enemy;<BR>(अम्), n. enmity, hostility; a multitude of enemies.<BR>—शात्रवेङ्गित (˚व-इङ्˚), अम्, n. an enemy's in-<BR>tention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रवीय
शात्रवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to an enemy,<BR>hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्वल
शात्वल शात्वल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Śākhā<BR>or school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद|शादः
शाद शाद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शद्), falling,<BR>dropping (Ved.); young or fresh grass; mud, (in these<BR>latter senses, according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 97, fr. rt.<BR>शो); [cf. Lith. szuda-s: Hib. caidhe, ‘dirt, a blemish;’<BR>caidheach, ‘polluted.’]<BR>—शाद-हरित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>green or fresh with young grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वल|शाद्वलः
शाद्वल, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in fresh or green<BR>grass; grassy; verdant, green; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a<BR>place abounding in young grass, a grassy spot; [cf.<BR>शड्वल.]<BR>—शाद्वल-स्थली, f. a grassy spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्
शान् शान् (properly a Nom. fr. शान be-<BR>low), used only in Desid. P. A. शीशां-<BR>सति, -ते, to whet, sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान|शानः
शान, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शो, cf. शाण), a touchstone;<BR>a whetstone, grindstone; (ई), f. a sort of cucumber<BR>or colocynth (= इन्द्र-वारुणी); [cf. Angl. Sax.<BR>hœnan.]<BR>—शान-पाद, अस्, m., N. of the Pāripātra<BR>mountain; a stone for grinding sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानच्
शानच् शानच्, (in grammar) a technical<BR>term for the Kṛt affix आन or अमान, used in<BR>forming present participles Ātmane-pada, or for आन<BR>substituted for हि, the affix of the 2nd sing. Impv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानैश्चर
शानैश्चर शानैश्चर (fr. शनैश्-चर), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, relating to Saturn; falling on a Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त|शांत|शान्तं|शान्तः
शान्त शान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शम्), ap-<BR>peased, allayed, calmed, alleviated, pacified, stilled,<BR>hushed, tranquil, calm, free from passions, contented,<BR>satisfied, undisturbed; put a stop to, put an end to,<BR>destroyed, annihilated, killed, deceased, dead, ceased,<BR>abated, subsided, extinguished; shaded, on the shady<BR>or auspicious side, auspicious (in augury, opposed to<BR>दीप्त, q. v.); meek, humble; purified, cleansed;<BR>(अस्), m. an ascetic whose passions are subdued, one<BR>absorbed in meditation on the deity; tranquillity,<BR>tranquil devotion, quietism (as one of the Rasas, see<BR>रस); indifference to all objects of pleasure and<BR>pain; (आ), f. a proper N.; N. of a Śakti; of the<BR>daughter of king Loma-pāda (wife of Ṛṣya-śṛṅga);<BR>(अम्), n. appeasing, pacifying, alleviation; (अम्), ind.<BR>enough, no more! hush! fie! for shame! heaven<BR>forbid! not so!<BR>—शान्त-क्रोध, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose anger is appeased.<BR>—शान्त-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>tranquil-minded; composed in mind, calm, unanxious.<BR>—शान्त-ज्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose fever is<BR>alleviated.<BR>—शान्त-ता, f. or शान्त-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>quietness, calmness, quietism, meekness.<BR>—शान्त-<BR>तोय, अस्, आ, अम्, having calm or still waters, gently<BR>flowing.<BR>—शान्त-देवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what<BR>appeases a god, that by which a divinity is appeased.<BR>—शान्त-मल, अस्, आ, अम्, having all defilement re-<BR>moved.<BR>—शान्त-मोह, अम्, n., scil. स्थान, ‘having<BR>delusion dispelled,’ one of the steps towards supreme<BR>happiness, (fourteen such Sthānas are enumerated in<BR>the Jaina system.)<BR>—शान्त-रय, अस्, आ, अम्, slack-<BR>ened in speed.<BR>—शान्त-रस, अस्, m. the sentiment<BR>of quietism or tranquillity (said to be illustrated in<BR>the Mahā-bhārata).<BR>—शान्तरस-नाटक, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a drama.<BR>—शान्त-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, calm, tran-<BR>quil.<BR>—शान्त-विवाद, अस्, आ, अम्, having disputes<BR>allayed, reconciled, appeased.<BR>—शान्तात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚),<BR>आ, आ, अ, of resigned or composed spirit, calm-minded,<BR>composed.<BR>—शान्तार्चिस् (˚त-अर्˚), इस्, इस्, इस्, whose<BR>flame is extinguished or abated, gone out (as fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्ति|शांति|शांतिः|शान्तिः
शान्ति, इस्, f. quiet, quietness, tranquillity, calmness,<BR>peace, ease, quietism, absence of passion, indifference<BR>to objects of pleasure or pain; rest, repose, remission;<BR>appeasing, pacification, allayment, alleviation, conso-<BR>lation, solace, satisfaction, reconciliation, settlement<BR>of differences; appeasing the stomach, satisfying<BR>hunger; any expiatory or propitiatory rite for avert-<BR>ing evil or calamity; Expiation (personified as a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma); ceasing,<BR>cessation; causing to cease; good fortune, auspicious-<BR>ness, felicity; preservation; (इस्), m., N. of the Indra<BR>of the tenth Manv-antara; of a pupil of Aṅgiras;<BR>of a king; the sixteenth Jina or Jaina deified sage<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">Page1000-c+ 79</a>]<BR>of the present era; one of the Jaina emperors of the<BR>universe.<BR>—शान्ति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing tran-<BR>quillity, calming, appeasing, soothing, consolatory.<BR>—शान्ति-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, causing tranquillity,<BR>calming, allaying; (ता), m. any divinity who averts<BR>evil.<BR>—शान्ति-कर्मन्, अ, n. any action leading to<BR>tranquillity or for averting evil.<BR>—शान्ति-काम, अस्,<BR>m. desire of tranquillity; (अस्, आ, अम्), desirous of<BR>tranquillity.<BR>—शान्ति-गृह, अम्, n. a room for rest<BR>or retirement near the place of sacrifice.<BR>—शान्ति-<BR>चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a poem by Kavi-candra.<BR>—शान्-<BR>ति-जल, अम्, n. = शान्त्य्-उद.<BR>—शान्ति-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>giving tranquillity, tranquillizing.<BR>—शान्ति-देवा, f.,<BR>N. of a daughter of Devaka.<BR>—शान्ति-पर्वन्, अ, n.<BR>‘Tranquillizing-section,’ N. of the twelfth book of<BR>the Mahā-bhārata, (the longest in the whole poem<BR>and consisting chiefly of stories, discourses, and epi-<BR>sodes narrated for the tranquillizing of the troubled<BR>spirit of Yudhi-ṣṭhira after the termination of the<BR>war and the slaughter of his many relatives.)<BR>—शान्ति-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Jaina work by Aśaga.<BR>—शान्ति-रत्न, अम्, n. ‘jewel of tranquillity,’ N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—शान्ति-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>religious observance (kept on the fifth day of the<BR>light half of the month Kārttika).<BR>—शान्ति-शतक,<BR>अम्, n. ‘a hundred verses on tranquillity,’ N. of a<BR>short poem by Śrī-śihlana.<BR>—शान्ति-शील, अस्, m.<BR>‘quiet-tempered,’ a proper N.<BR>—शान्ति-सर्वस्व,<BR>अम्, n. ‘essence of quietism,’ N. of a work.<BR>—शान्ति-<BR>सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of a hymn on quietism.<BR>—शान्ति-<BR>सूरि, इस्, m., N. of the author of a Jaina work.<BR>—शान्ति-होम, अस्, m. a propitiatory oblation, a<BR>burnt offering to avert or remedy evil.<BR>—शान्त्य्-<BR>उद or शान्त्य्-उदक, अम्, n. propitiatory water,<BR>water offered at sacrifices for propitiation, lustral<BR>water.<BR>—शान्त्युद-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a vessel holding<BR>propitiatory water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिक|शांतिक
शान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, propitiatory, expiatory; pro-<BR>ducing ease or quiet; relating to quiet, &c.; (अम्),<BR>n. observances or ceremonies for the removal of<BR>calamities.<BR>—शान्तिक-कर्मन्, अ, n. a magic rite<BR>performed for removing obstacles; [cf. शान्ति-कर्-<BR>मन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वा
शान्त्वा, ind. = शमित्वा, having been tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनु|शांतनु|शान्तनुः
शान्तनु शान्तनु, उस्, m. (fr. शन्तनु?), the<BR>twenty-first sovereign of the lunar dynasty in the<BR>Dvāpara or third age, (he was son of Pratīpa and<BR>was father of Bhīṣma by Gaṅgā before he became<BR>the father of Vicitra-vīrya by his wife Satya-vatī.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनव|शांतनव|शांतनवः|शान्तनवः
शान्तनव, अस्, m. (fr. शान्तनु above), a patro-<BR>nymic of Bhīṣma (as son of king Śāntanu, the re-<BR>puted great-uncle of the Pāṇḍavas); N. of the author<BR>of the Phiṭ-sūtras on accentuation; (ई), f., scil. टीका,<BR>the commentary composed by Śantanu.<BR>—शान्तन-<BR>वाचार्य (˚व-आच्˚), अस्, m. the author of the Phiṭ-<BR>sūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व्|शांत्व्
शान्त्व् शान्त्व् (probably connected with<BR>rt. 1. शम्; by some regarded as a Nom.<BR>fr. शान्त्व below; frequently, but less correctly, written<BR>सान्त्व्), cl. 10. P. A. शान्त्वयति, -ते, अशशान्त्वत्,<BR>शान्त्वयितुम्, to console, comfort, soothe, coax,<BR>pacify, conciliate; to address gently or kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व|शान्त्वं
शान्त्व, अम्, n. (less correctly written सान्त्व), con-<BR>solation, consoling, comforting; conciliation; mild-<BR>ness; mild speech; gentle or peaceable means.<BR>—शान्त्व-पूर्वम्, ind. in a conciliatory manner,<BR>coaxingly, (see पूर्व.)<BR>—शान्त्व-वाद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>speaking in a kindly and affectionate manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वन
शान्त्वन, अम्, n. (less correctly written सान्त्वन),<BR>the act of appeasing or reconciling, conciliation,<BR>reconcilement; mildness; (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp.) appeasing; (आ, अम्), f. n. speaking kindly<BR>and in a conciliatory manner; friendly salutation and<BR>inquiry; (आनि), n. pl. kind or flattering words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वयत्
शान्त्वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, consoling, appeasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वयित्वा
शान्त्वयित्वा, ind. having consoled or comforted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वित
शान्त्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, consoled, comforted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व्य
शान्त्व्य (anom. ind. part.), having consoled or<BR>comforted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1000-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वति|शान्त्वतिः
शान्त्वति शान्त्वति, इस्, f. a kind of plant or<BR>shrub (= ब्राह्मण-यष्टिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाप|शापः
शाप शाप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. शप्), curse, ana-<BR>thema, execration, cursing, reviling; abuse; oath,<BR>imprecation, affirmation by oath or ordeal; ban,<BR>interdiction.<BR>—शाप-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, seized by a<BR>curse, suffering under a curse.<BR>—शाप-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, arising from a curse.<BR>—शाप-नाशन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Muni.<BR>—शाप-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘curse-<BR>giving,’ uttering imprecations.<BR>—शाप-भीत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dreading a curse.<BR>—शाप-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>released from a curse.<BR>—शाप-मुक्ति, इस्, f. or शाप-<BR>मोक्ष, अस्, m. deliverance from a curse.<BR>—शाप-यन्-<BR>त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, restrained by a curse.<BR>—शापान्त<BR>(˚प-अन्˚) or शापावसान (˚प-अव्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>end of a curse or of the period during which an im-<BR>precation takes effect.<BR>—शापास्त्र (˚प-अस्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘having curses for weapons,’ a Muni, saint, (a curse<BR>pronounced by a Muni being formidable even to the<BR>deities.)<BR>—शापोत्सर्ग (˚प-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘pouring<BR>out a curse,’ the uttering of an imprecation.<BR>—शा-<BR>पोद्धार (˚प-उद्˚), अस्, m. deliverance from a<BR>curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापित
शापित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to take an oath, one<BR>to whom an oath has been administered, sworn,<BR>adjured, proved by ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापेय
शापेय, see Gaṇa Śaunakādi to Pāṇ. IV. 3, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापेयिन्
शापेयिन्, ई, m. a proper N.; (इनस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a school of the White Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापठिक|शापठिकः
शापठिक शापठिक, अस्, m. a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाफरिक|शाफरिकः
शाफरिक शाफरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शफर),<BR>relating to the Śaphara fish; (अस्), m. a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाफेय
शाफेय शाफेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Śākhā<BR>of the Yajur-veda; [cf. शापेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबर|शाबरः
शाबर शाबर, अस्, m., N. of the commen-<BR>tary written by Śabara-svāmin; of a work by Prāṇa-<BR>kṛṣṇa; of a Tantra work ascribed to Śiva.<BR>—शाबर-<BR>भाष्य, अम्, n. the commentary written by Śabara-<BR>svāmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्द|शाब्दः
शाब्द शाब्द, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शब्द), sonorous,<BR>sounding; relating to sound, (opposed to आर्थ,<BR>q. v.); relating to or derived from words; verbal,<BR>oral; nominal (as inflection); (अस्), m. a philologist,<BR>grammarian; (ई), f. Sarasvatī (as goddess of speech<BR>and eloquence).<BR>—शाब्द-बोध, अस्, m. ‘verbal<BR>knowledge,’ apprehension of the meaning of words,<BR>perception of the verbal or literal sense (of a sen-<BR>tence, &c.).<BR>—शाब्द-व्यञ्जना, f. (in rhetoric)<BR>suggestion or insinuation founded on words (as op-<BR>posed to आर्थ-व्यञ्जना or suggestion dependent<BR>upon the meaning of words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दिक|शाब्दिकः
शाब्दिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to sounds or words;<BR>making a noise, sounding; verbal; (अस्), m. one<BR>skilled in words, a philologist, grammarian.<BR>—शाब्-<BR>दिक-नरसिंह, अस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम
शाम शाम, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. 1. शम्), Ved.<BR>appeasing, curing, having curative properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन्
शामन्, अ, n. [cf. सामन्], appeasing, reconciling,<BR>reconciliation, conciliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन|शामनं|शामनः
शामन, अस्, m. one who ‘settles’ or destroys,<BR>N. of Yama (= शमन); (अम्), n. conciliation;<BR>tranquillity, peace; settling, killing, slaughter; end,<BR>(शामनं या, to go to an end, be destroyed);<BR>(ई), f. the southern quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामलदास
शामल-दास or शामल-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a modern poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामित्र|शामित्रं
शामित्र, अम्, n. a sacrificial vessel; a hearth or<BR>place (for cooking a sacrificial animal); a deadly<BR>blow; sacrificing; tying up cattle for sacrifice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामील|शामीलं
शामील, अम्, n. ashes (Pāṇ. IV. 3, 142).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीली
शामीली, f. a chaplet, garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामुल्य
शामुल्य, अम्, n. (probably connected with श-<BR>मल), Ved. (perhaps) anything requiring cleansing<BR>or expiation (as a dirty or defiled garment; according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X. 85, 29 = शमलं शारीरं<BR>शरीर-छिन्नस्य मलस्य धारकं वस्त्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामूल
शामूल, अम्, n., Ved. (according to some) an<BR>old woollen garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्यत्
शाम्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, becoming calm or tranquil,<BR>being appeased; one who is placid or quiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्ब|शांबः|शाम्बः
शाम्ब शाम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa<BR>and Jāmbavatī (frequently mentioned in the Purāṇas<BR>and in the Mausala-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata,<BR>where it is related that in consequence of the curse<BR>of some holy sages who had been deceived by a<BR>female disguise he had assumed, he was condemned<BR>to produce offspring in the shape of a terrific iron<BR>club for the destruction of the race of Vṛṣṇi and<BR>Andhaka; he is said to have been instructed by<BR>Nārada in the proper worship of the sun, and by<BR>Vyāsa in the ritual observances of the Magi; he is<BR>regarded as the author of the Sūrya-stotra hymn).<BR>—शाम्ब-पुर, अम्, n. or शाम्ब-पुरी, f., N. of<BR>a city founded by Śāmba (said to be situated on the<BR>banks of the Candra-bhāgā).<BR>—शाम्ब-पुराण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—शाम्बादित्य (˚ब-आद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a particular form of the sun.<BR>—शाम्बोप-<BR>पुराण (˚ब-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरिक|शाम्बरिकः
शाम्बरिक शाम्बरिक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरी|शांबरी
शाम्बरी शाम्बरी, f. (fr. शम्बर), jugglery,<BR>sorcery, illusion (as practised by the Daitya Śambara);<BR>a sorceress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बविक|शांबविक|शांबविकः|शाम्बविकः
शाम्बविक शाम्बविक, अस्, m. (fr. शम्बु), a<BR>worker or dealer in shells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बुक|शांबुक|शांबुकः|शाम्बुकः
शाम्बुक, अस्, m. a bivalve shell; [cf. शम्बुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बुवि
शाम्बुवि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a Śākhā or school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बूक|शांबूक|शांबूकः|शाम्बूकः
शाम्बूक, अस्, m. a bivalve shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भर|शांभर
शाम्भर शाम्भर, N. of a city in Ajmere<BR>(commonly called Sāmbhar or Sāmbher, where a par-<BR>ticular kind of fossil salt is found).<BR>—शाम्भर-<BR>नगर, अम्, n. the city of Śāmbhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भरायणी|शांभरायणी
शाम्भरायणी, f., N. of a woman, (also written<BR>साम्भरायणी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भव|शांभव|शाम्भवं|शाम्भवः
शाम्भव शाम्भव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शम्भु),<BR>belonging to Śiva; (अस्), m. a worshipper of Śiva;<BR>the son of Śambhu; camphor; a sort of poison; a<BR>kind of plant (= शिव-मल्ली); bdellium (= गुग्-<BR>गुलु); (ई), f., N. of Pārvatī; a kind of plant (=<BR>नील-दूर्वा); the aperture through which the soul<BR>is said to escape (= मुद्रा-मार्ग); (अम्), n. the<BR>Deva-dāru.<BR>—शाम्भव-देव, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाय|शायः
शाय शाय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. शी), lying,<BR>sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायक|शायकः
1. शायक, अस्, इका, अम्, lying, sleeping, reposing;<BR>(इका), f. sleeping, repose, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिन्
शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, lying down, reclining, sleeping,<BR>resting, abiding, (अधः-शायिन्, sleeping on the<BR>ground; एक-शायिन्, sleeping alone.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायक|शायकः
शायक 2. शायक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शो), an<BR>arrow; a sword; [cf. सायक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्
शार् शार् (also written सार्), cl. 10. P.<BR>शारयति, -यितुम्, to be weak or feeble;<BR>to weaken; [cf. rt. शॄ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार शार, अस्, ई, अम्, (in some senses fr. rt.<BR>शॄ; in others fr. शृ substituted for rt. सृ), varie-<BR>gated (in colour), of different colours (as dark hair<BR>mixed with grey); mottled, spotted; yellow; (अस्), m.<BR>hurting, injuring; variegating; a variegated colour;<BR>a mixture of blue and yellow, green; air, wind,<BR>(perhaps for सार); a chess-man, piece used at chess<BR>or at a kind of backgammon, (for सार, q. v.); (ई),<BR>f., Ved. an arrow; Kuśa grass; (अम्), n. a variegated<BR>colour.<BR>—शार-ता, f. or शार-त्व, अम्, n. variety of<BR>colour, yellowness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारङ्ग|शारंग|शारंगः|शारङ्गः
शारङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् [cf. सारङ्ग], of a variegated<BR>colour, spotted, dappled; (अस्), m. the Cātaka bird,<BR>Cuculus Melanoleucus; a peacock; a bee; a deer;<BR>an elephant; (ई), f. a particular musical instrument,<BR>a stringed instrument played with a bow, a sort of<BR>fiddle; N. of the wife of Manda-pāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारि|शारिः
शारि, इस्, m. a chess-man, piece at chess (or at a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">Page1001-c+ 79</a>]<BR>kind of draughts); a little round ball (= गुटिका);<BR>a kind of die; (इस्), f. a kind of bird, (see शारिका);<BR>an elephant's housings or armour; fraud, trick.<BR>—शारि-<BR>पट्ट, अस्, m. or शारि-फल, अम्, n. or शारि-फ-<BR>लक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a chequered cloth or table for<BR>playing draughts, &c.<BR>—शारि-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>disciple of Buddha.<BR>—शारि-शृङ्खला, f. a sort of<BR>die for playing at draughts, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिका
शारिका, f. a kind of bird (commonly called<BR>Maina, either the Gracula Religiosa or the Turdus<BR>Salica, cf. सारिका); a bow or stick used for playing<BR>the Vīṇā or any stringed instrument; chess-playing;<BR>a piece or man at chess or backgammon (according<BR>to some); N. of the tutelary goddess of Śārīṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारित
शारित, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिवा
शारिवा, f. a particular plant (the root of which is<BR>used medicinally as a substitute for sarsaparilla, =<BR>श्यामा, अनन्त-मूल, उत्पल-शारिवा, cf. सारिवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारी
शारी, f. a kind of bird (= शारिका); = कुशा (ac-<BR>cording to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारुक|शारुकः
शारुक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who injures or destroys<BR>(with acc.); mischievous, noxious, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद|शारदं|शारदः
शारद शारद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शरद्), autumnal,<BR>produced or growing in autumn; annual, lasting for<BR>a year or from year to year, perennial (said of the<BR>cities of the Asuras); new, recent [cf. रज्जु-शा-<BR>रद]; modest, diffident; belonging to the Asura<BR>Śarad (according to Sāy.); (अस्), m. autumnal sick-<BR>ness; autumnal sunshine; a year; a sort of kidney-<BR>bean (yellow Mūng and another kind, = पीत-मुद्ग,<BR>हरिन्-मुद्ग); a kind of plant (= कास); the<BR>Vakula tree; (औ), m. du., scil. मासौ, the two<BR>months of autumn (Ved.); (आ), f., N. of Sarasvatī;<BR>of Durgā; of a daughter of Deva-ratha; a kind of<BR>musical instrument, a sort of Vīṇā or lute; N. of<BR>certain plants (= ब्राह्मी, सारिवा); = शारदा-तिलक<BR>below; (ई), f. the plant Jussiæa Repens; the Sapta-<BR>parṇa tree; the day of full moon in the month<BR>Kārttika or (according to some) Āśvina, = कोजागर-<BR>पूर्णिमा; (अम्), n. corn, grain, fruit (as ripening in<BR>the autumn); the white lotus.<BR>—शारदा-तिलक,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a mystical poem by Lakṣmaṇa; of<BR>a drama by Śaṅkara.<BR>—शारदा-तिलक-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. the Tantra called Śāradā-tilaka.<BR>—शारदाम्बा<BR>(˚दा-अम्˚), f. the goddess Śāradā, i. e. Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिक|शारदिकं|शारदिकः
शारदिक, अम्, n. a particular funeral ceremony,<BR>an annual or autumnal Śrāddha; (अस्), m. autumnal<BR>sickness; heat or sunshine in autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिन्
शारदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, autumnal, belonging to autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदीय
शारदीय, अस्, ई, अम्, autumnal.<BR>—शारदीय-म-<BR>हापूजा, f. the autumnal great worship (of Durgā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद्वत|शारद्वतः
शारद्वत, अस्, ई, अम्, of or belonging to Śarad-<BR>vat, descended from Śarad-vat; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—शारद्वती-पुत्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद्वतायन
शारद्वतायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाराव
शाराव शाराव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शराव), placed<BR>on a shallow dish (as rice &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीटक
शारीटक शारीटक, N. of a town of Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीर|शारीरं|शारीरः
शारीर शारीर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शरीर), cor-<BR>poreal, bodily, relating to the body (of animals);<BR>belonging to or produced from the body; connected<BR>with the body, incorporate; (अम्), n. the incor-<BR>porate soul or spirit; a particular drug (= वृष,<BR>which may mean ‘a bull,’ ‘a kind of drug,’ &c.); ex-<BR>crement, excretion; (अस्), m. corporal punishment (?).<BR>—शारीर-व्रण, अस्, m. a bodily ulcer or tumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरक|शारीरकं
शारीरक, अस्, ई, अम्, corporeal, relating to the<BR>body; incorporate; (अम्), n. the soul or embodied<BR>spirit or the doctrine inquiring into the nature of<BR>the embodied spirit; N. of Śaṅkarācārya's commen-<BR>tary on the Vedānta or Brahma-sūtras.<BR>—शारीरक-<BR>टीका, f., N. of a work by Vācas-pati.<BR>—शारीरक-<BR>मीमांसा, f. an inquiry into the embodied spirit<BR>(= ब्रह्म-मीमांसा, उत्तर-मीमांसा, वेदान्त,<BR>q. q. v. v.).<BR>—शारीरक-मीमांसा-भाष्य, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a commentary by Rāmānuja on the Brahma-<BR>sūtras; of another by Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—शारीरक-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n. the aphorisms of the Vedānta philo-<BR>sophy (= ब्रह्म-सूत्र, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरकीय
शारीरकीय, अस्, ई, अम्, corporeal, psychological^1<BR>(as a book treating of the incorporate soul).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरिक|शारीरिकः
शारीरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the body, cor-<BR>poreal, personal, material, contained in the body,<BR>incorporate, psychological.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारुक|शारुकः
शारुक शारुक. See p. 1001, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्क|शार्कः
शार्क शार्क, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. शॄ, con-<BR>nected with शर्करा, q. v.), clayed or candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कक|शार्ककः
शार्कक, अस्, m. clayed or candied sugar; a lump<BR>of sugar; a lump or ball of meat; the froth of<BR>milk, syllabub; cream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कर|शार्करः
शार्कर, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. शर्करा), gravelly, stony;<BR>made of sugar, sugary; (अस्), m. a stony or gravelly<BR>place; the froth or skim of milk; cream [cf. शार्-<BR>कक]; (अम्), n. a kind of metre (= शाक्कर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करक|शार्करकः
शार्करक or शार्करिक, अस्, ई, अम्, gravelly,<BR>stony, &c.; (अस्), m. a place abounding in stones or<BR>gravel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कराक्ष
शार्कराक्ष, अस्, m. (probably fr. शर्कराक्ष),<BR>a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कराक्षि
शार्कराक्षि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करीय|शार्करीयः
शार्करीय, अस्, ई, अम्, stony, gravelly, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्गाल
शार्गाल शार्गाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शृगाल), of<BR>or belonging to a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्ग|शार्ंग|शार्ङ्गं|शार्ङ्गः
शार्ङ्ग शार्ङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शृङ्ग), made<BR>of horn, horny, corneous; (अस्), m. a bow, (accord-<BR>ing to some अम्, n.); N. of the bow of Viṣṇu;<BR>N. of a bird; a patronymic of several Vedic Ṛṣis;<BR>(अम्), n. ginger (= आर्द्रक).<BR>—शार्ङ्ग-देव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the Saṅgīta-ratnākara.<BR>—शार्ङ्ग-धन्वन्, आ, m. epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शार्ङ्ग-धर, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Vaidya-vallabha; of the author of the works mentioned<BR>below.<BR>—शार्ङ्गधर-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of an<BR>anthology of didactic verses.<BR>—शार्ङ्गधर-सं-<BR>हिता, f., N. of a medical work.<BR>—शार्ङ्ग-पाणि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘bow-handed,’ N. of Viṣṇu; of the father of<BR>Viṣṇu; of a chief of the Vaiṣṇava sect.<BR>—शार्ङ्ग-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. ‘carrying the bow Śārṅga,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गिका
शार्ङ्गिका, f. a kind of bird; [cf. लपिता.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गिन्|शार्ंगिन्
शार्ङ्गिन्, ई, m. a bowman, an archer; epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गरव
शार्ङ्गरव शार्ङ्गरव, अस्, m. (fr. शृङ्ग-<BR>रव?), a Śārṅgarava man, see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 73;<BR>(ई), f. a Śāṅgarava woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गष्ठा
शार्ङ्गष्ठा शार्ङ्गष्ठा, f. a kind of tree (=<BR>महा-करञ्ज; also written शाङ्गोष्ठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूल|शार्दूलः|शार्द्दूलः
शार्दूल शार्दूल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>शॄ), a tiger; a panther or leopard (= चित्रक); any<BR>eminent person, best, excellent, pre-eminent (at the<BR>end of comps., see व्याघ्र); another kind of<BR>animal (= शरभ); a Rākṣasa; a sort of bird;<BR>a variety of the Dhṛti metre, (see below); a species<BR>of the Atidhṛti metre, (see below); (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a Śākhā or school of the Sāma-veda; [cf. perhaps<BR>Gr. πάρδος (for κάρδος), πάρδαλις; Lat. pardus,<BR>pardalis; Lith. pardas.]<BR>—शार्दूल-चर्मन्, अ,<BR>n. a tiger's skin.<BR>—शार्दूल-मृग-सेवित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, frequented by tigers and deer.<BR>—शार्दूल-ल-<BR>लित, अम्, n. ‘tiger's sport,’ a variety of the Dhṛti<BR>metre (consisting of four Pādas of eighteen syllables<BR>each).<BR>—शार्दूल-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘riding on a<BR>tiger,’ N. of one of the twenty-five Pūrva-jinas.<BR>—शार्दूल-विक्रीडित, अम्, n. ‘tiger's play,’ a<BR>species of the Atidhṛti metre (having four Pādas of<BR>nineteen syllables each).<BR>—शार्दूल-सम-विक्रम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having prowess equal to a tiger, as bold<BR>as a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्यात
शार्यात शार्यात, अस्, m. (fr. शर्याति), N. of<BR>a Vedic Ṛṣi (author of Ṛg-veda X. 92, and having<BR>the patronymic Mānava); (आस्), m. pl. the sons of<BR>Śaryāta, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्व
शार्व शार्व, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. शर्व), belonging<BR>to Śarva or Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्वर|शार्व्वरं
शार्वर शार्वर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शर्वरी), be-<BR>longing to night, nocturnal; murderous, mischievous,<BR>pernicious; (अम्), n. darkness, gloom; (ई), f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्वरिन्
शार्वरिन्, ई, m., N. of the thirty-fourth year of<BR>Jupiter's cycle of sixty years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्
शाल् शाल् [cf. rt. शाड्], cl. 1. A. शालते,<BR>शालितुम्, to flatter, praise, coax; to<BR>boast; to shine or be endowed with [see Malli-<BR>nātha's commentary to Kirāt. V. 44].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल|शालः
शाल शाल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. शल् or<BR>rt. शाल् or rt. शो; in some senses also written साल,<BR>q. v.), a particular tree, the Shorea Robusta or Valeria<BR>Robusta (said to be one of the most valuable Indian<BR>timber trees, = सर्ज, cf. साल); a tree (in general);<BR>an enclosure, court, fence (= प्राकार); a kind of<BR>fish, Ophiocephalus Wrahl; N. of a river; of king<BR>Śāli-vāhana; (आ), f. a large branch, the upper or<BR>main branch of a tree; a hall, saloon, large room,<BR>apartment, room; a house; a stable; [cf. Angl. Sax.<BR>heal, ‘a hall;’ Mod. Germ. Saal, Halle.]<BR>—शाल-<BR>ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a sacred place or district; a par-<BR>ticular sacred stone worshipped by the Vaiṣṇavas, (it<BR>is said to be a kind of black ammonite, and its various<BR>circular formations are supposed to have a mystical<BR>significance and to be typical of Viṣṇu; these stones<BR>are chiefly found in or near the river Gaṇḍakī, and<BR>the circles or spirals they contain are thought by<BR>some to be formed by the Vajra-kīṭa or other in-<BR>sects; cf. साल-ग्राम.)<BR>—शालग्राम-गिरि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a mountain producing the Śāla-grāma.<BR>—शा-<BR>लग्राम-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—शाल-<BR>ग्राम-शिला, f. the Śāla-grāma stone.<BR>—शाल-ज,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of fish, (see above.)<BR>—शाल-निर्यास,<BR>अस्, m. resin, the resinous exudation of the Śāl tree<BR>or Shorea Robusta.<BR>—शाल-पर्णी, f. ‘having Śāl<BR>leaves,’ the shrub Hedysarum Gangeticum, (also<BR>written साल-पर्णी.)<BR>—शाल-पोत, अस्, m. a young<BR>Śāl tree.<BR>—शाल-भञ्जिका, f. a doll, wooden puppet;<BR>a courtezan, harlot; a kind of game played in the<BR>east of India; [cf. साल-भञ्जिका.]<BR>—शालभञ्-<BR>जिका-प्रख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, resembling the game<BR>called Śāla-bhañjikā.<BR>—शाल-भञ्जी, f. a doll, wooden<BR>puppet (as made of Śāl wood).<BR>—शाल-वेष्ट, अस्,<BR>m. the resin of the Śāl tree (used as incense &c.),<BR>resin (in general).<BR>—शाल-सार, अस्, m. a tree;<BR>Asa Fetida, (also written साल-सार.)<BR>—शालाङ्की<BR>(˚ला-अङ्˚?), f. a doll, puppet.<BR>—शालाजिर (˚ला-अज्˚?),<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a hollow earthen cup or saucer.<BR>—शाला-द्वार, अम्, n. the door or entrance of a<BR>hall.<BR>—शालाद्वार्य, अस्, m., scil. अग्नि, a kind of<BR>sacred or sacrificial fire.<BR>—शाला-मृग, अस्, m. ‘house-<BR>animal,’ a jackal (as prowling near houses?).<BR>—शाला-<BR>वती, f., N. of one of the wives of Viśvā-mitra and<BR>mother of Hiraṇyākṣa.<BR>—शालावत्य, आस्, m. pl., N.<BR>of a family descended from Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—शाला-वृक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘house-wolf,’ a dog; a cat; a jackal; a wolf; a<BR>deer; a monkey; a particular class of evil or malicious<BR>beings, (Mahā-bhārata, Śānti-parvan 1188.)<BR>—शाला-<BR>वृकेय, अस्, m. the offering of a Śālā-vṛka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालक|शालकः
शालक, अस्, m., N. of a man (perhaps a jester in<BR>a play).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाक्ष
शालाक्ष, आस्, m. pl., N. of a family or Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालानी
शालानी, f. the shrub Hedysarum Gangeticum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालार|शालारं
शालार, अम्, n. a ladder, flight of stairs or steps;<BR>a bird-cage; the claw of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिक|शालिकः
शालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to the<BR>Śāl tree; belonging to a hall, &c.; (अस्), m. a<BR>weaver; a village of artificers; a toll, tax; (आ), f. the<BR>shrub Hedysarum Gangeticum; N. of a Mīmāṃsā<BR>work by Śālikā-nātha (= प्रकरण-पञ्चिका).<BR>—शालिका-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Śālikā and of the Praśasta-pāda-bhāṣya-vyākhyāna<BR>commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिन्
शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, belonging to a house, domestic,<BR>&c.; endowed with, possessed of, possessing, having;<BR>shining or resplendent with (generally at the end of<BR>comps., cf. वीर्य-श्˚; in this sense apparently con-<BR>nected with rt. शाल्); (इनी), f. a mistress of a house,<BR>housekeeper; a kind of metre, four times ¯¯¯¯¯<BR>˘¯¯˘¯¯; a proper N.<BR>—१. शालि-ता, f. or शालि-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">Page1002-c+ 77</a>]<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the being endowed with, possession;<BR>confidence in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिन
शालिन, अस्, आ, अम्, for शालीन below.<BR>—शालिनी-<BR>करण, see शालीनी-करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाली
शाली, f. a kind of plant (= कृष्ण-जीरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीन|शालीनः
शालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, attached to the house or to<BR>one's own room, domestic, bashful, humble, retiring,<BR>ashamed; like, resembling; (अस्), m. a householder,<BR>one who devotes himself to household or worldly af-<BR>fairs; (आ), f. a sort of fennel (= मिश्रेया).<BR>—शालीन-<BR>ता, f. or शालीन-त्व, अम्, n. bashfulness, modesty.<BR>—शा-<BR>लीनत्व-विवर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of modesty,<BR>immodest.<BR>—शालीन-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a bashful dis-<BR>position or retiring nature.<BR>—शालीनशील-ता, f. bash-<BR>fulness.<BR>—शालीनी-करण, अम्, n. the making hum-<BR>ble, humbling; abuse, reproach.<BR>—शालीनी-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. -करोति, &c., to make humble, humiliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीय
शालीय, अस्, आ, अम्, of or belonging to a hall;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कटङ्कट|शालङ्कटङ्कटः
शालङ्कटङ्कट शालङ्कटङ्कट, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Rākṣasa (son of Śālaṅkaṭaṅkaṭā, wife of Vidyut-<BR>keśin; the N. is also written Śāla-kaṭaṅkaṭa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कायन|शालङ्कायनः
शालङ्कायन शालङ्कायन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Muni; of Śiva's attendant Nandin; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a family (descendants of Viśvā-mitra).<BR>—शालङ्का-<BR>यन-गोत्र, अम्, n. the family of the Śālaṅkāyanas.<BR>—शालङ्कायन-जीवसू, ऊस्, f. epithet of the mother<BR>of Vyāsa.<BR>—शालङ्कायनी-पुत्र, अस्, m., Ved., N.<BR>of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कायनिन्
शालङ्कायनिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कि|शालङ्किः
शालङ्कि, इस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालञ्च
शालञ्च शालञ्च, अस्, m. = शालाञ्चि below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाक|शालाकः
शालाक शालाक (fr. शलाका), Ved. a frag-<BR>ment or splinter of wood, a chip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाकिन्
शालाकिन्, ई, m. a spearman, one armed with a<BR>javelin or dart; a surgeon; a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाक्य|शालाक्यं|शालाक्यः
शालाक्य, अम्, n. a branch of surgery or medicine<BR>(comprising the inquiry into diseases of the head<BR>and its organs; cf. आयुर्-वेद).<BR>—शालाक्य-तन्त्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of the fourth part of the Aṣṭāṅga-<BR>hṛdaya-saṃhitā (treating of diseases of the head).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाञ्चि|शालाञ्चिः
शालाञ्चि शालाञ्चि, इस्, f. = शालिञ्च, p. 1003.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालातुरीय|शालातुरीयः
शालातुरीय शालातुरीय, अस्, m. (fr. शलातुर),<BR>epithet of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालालुक
शालालुक शालालुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शलालु),<BR>purchased with the perfume called Śalālu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालि|शालिः
शालि शालि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. शाल् or<BR>fr. rt. शॄ, cf. Uṇādi-s. IV. 127), rice (of which there<BR>are said to be ten varieties; but especially two kinds,<BR>one white, growing in deep water, and the other red,<BR>requiring only a moist soil); the civet-cat, pole-cat;<BR>N. of a Yakṣa transformed into a lion, (see शालि-<BR>वाहन); (अयस्), m. pl. grains of rice, rice.<BR>—शालि-<BR>कण, अम्, n. a grain of rice.<BR>—शालि-चूर्ण, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. rice-flower, ground rice.<BR>—२. शालि-ता, f.<BR>or शालि-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition of rice.<BR>—शालि-पर्णी, f. a kind of leguminous shrub (=<BR>माष-पर्णी).<BR>—शालि-पिष्ट, अम्, n. ‘flour of<BR>rice,’ crystal.<BR>—शालि-भवन, अम्, n. a rice field.<BR>—शालि-वाह्, वाट्, -ल्यूही, वाट्, see Vopa-deva IV.<BR>12.<BR>—शालि-वाह, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—शालि-वा-<BR>हन, अस्, m., N. of a celebrated sovereign of India<BR>(said to be so called either from having in his infancy<BR>ridden on a Yakṣa called Śāli, or from Śāli for Śāla,<BR>the Śāl tree, Śāli-vāhana being represented as borne<BR>on a cross made of that or other wood; he was the<BR>enemy of Vikramāditya and institutor of the era<BR>now called Śāka, commencing from his birth, seventy-<BR>eight years after Christ; his capital was Prati-ṣṭhāna<BR>on the Godāvarī).<BR>—शालि-शूक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king of the Maurya dynasty (a descendant of Candra-<BR>gupta).<BR>—शालि-होत्र, अस्, m. ‘receiving oblations of<BR>rice or corn,’ a horse; N. of a writer on veterinary<BR>subjects.<BR>—शालिहोत्र-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing (the<BR>precepts of) Śāli-hotra, skilled in veterinary surgery.<BR>—शालि-होत्रिन्, ई, m. a horse.<BR>—शाल्य्-ओदन, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेय|शालेयं|शालेयः
शालेय, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, fit for rice (as a field<BR>&c.); sown with rice; (अस्, आ), m. f. a sort of fennel,<BR>Anethum Panmori or Sowa, = मिश्रेया; (अम्), n. a<BR>field of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिक|शालिकः
शालिक शालिक. See under शाल, p. 1002.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिञ्च|शालिञ्चः
शालिञ्च शालिञ्च, अस्, m. the creeper Achy-<BR>ranthes Triandra (the leaves of which are used as a<BR>vegetable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिञ्ची
शालिञ्ची, f. a kind of vegetable (= शौल्फ, appa-<BR>rently somewhat different from the above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीन|शालीनः
शालीन शालीन. See p. 1002, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालु|शालुः
शालु शालु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>1. 5. fr. rt. शॄ, but in some senses connected with<BR>rt. शल्), a kind of astringent substance; a sort of<BR>perfume (commonly called Chor); a frog [cf. शा-<BR>लुर]; (उ), n. the root of the water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुक|शालुकं|शालुकः
शालुक, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 42.<BR>fr. rt. शल्), the esculent root of the different kinds<BR>of Nymphæa or water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुड
शालुड, अस्, m., Ved. a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुर|शालुरः
शालुर, अस्, m. a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूक|शालूकं|शालूकः
शालूक, अस्, m. a frog; the root of the water-lily<BR>(generally neut.); (अम्), n. the root of the water-lily,<BR>(see above); the nutmeg (= जाती-फल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूर|शालूरः
शालूर, अस्, m. a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालोत्तरीय|शालोत्तरीयः
शालोत्तरीय शालोत्तरीय, अस्, m. (for शाला-<BR>तुरीय, q. v.?), N. of the grammarian Pāṇini, (this<BR>word is given by Śabda-k. on the authority of the<BR>Trikāṇḍa-śeṣa; it is said to be derived from शाला<BR>+ उत्तरीय, and to account for this derivation a<BR>legend is told that Pāṇini was expelled from the<BR>house of his preceptor for his stupidity, and acquired<BR>his subsequent scholarship by propitiating Śiva.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मल|शाल्मलः
शाल्मल शाल्मल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>शल् or शाल्), the silk-cotton tree; the gum or resin<BR>of the cotton tree (= मोच-रस); one of the Dvīpas<BR>or divisions of the continent (= शाल्मलि below).<BR>—शालमल-द्वीप, अस्, m. the Śālmala-dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलि|शाल्मलिः
शाल्मलि, इस्, m. f. the Seemul or silk-cotton tree,<BR>Bombax Heptaphyllum, (कूट-शाल्मलि, a fabulous<BR>thorny rod of the cotton tree for torturing the wicked<BR>in hell); one of the seven Dvīpas or great divisions<BR>of the known continent (so called from the above<BR>tree said to grow there; it is surrounded by the sea<BR>of ghee or clarified butter); a kind of hell in which<BR>the wicked are tormented with the thorns or prickles<BR>of the Śālmali.<BR>—शाल्मलि-द्वीप, अस्, m. the Śāl-<BR>mali-dvīpa.<BR>—शाल्मलि-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. the Sapta-<BR>cchada tree.<BR>—शाल्मलि-स्थ, अस्, m. ‘Śālmali-abid-<BR>ing,’ epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामलिक
शामलिक, अस्, m. the tree Andersonia Rohitaka;<BR>(अम्), n. an inferior kind of Śālmali tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिन्
शाल्मलिन्, ई, m., N. of Garuḍa, the bird and<BR>vehicle of Viṣṇu; (इनी), f. the silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मली
शाल्मली, f. = शाल्मलि above; N. of a river in the<BR>infernal regions (Manu IV. 90); of a hell, (see शाल्-<BR>मलि); of one of the Śaktis of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शाल्मली-<BR>कन्द, अस्, m. the root of the Śālmali tree.<BR>—शाल्-<BR>मली-फल, अस्, m. a particular plant or tree (=<BR>तेजः-फल).<BR>—शाल्मली-फलक, अम्, n. a smooth<BR>board of Śālmalī wood (used to wash clothes upon).<BR>—शाल्मली-वेष्ट or शाल्मली-वेष्टक, अस्, m. the<BR>gum or resin of the silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्व|शाल्वः
शाल्व शाल्व, अस्, m., N. of a country, (also<BR>written साल्व, q. v.); a king of the Śālvas; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a tribe (inhabiting Bhārata-varṣa).<BR>—शाल्व-पति, इस्, or शाल्व-राज, अस्, or शाल्व-<BR>राजन्, आ, m. the king of the Śālvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्वण|शाल्वणः
शाल्वण, अस्, m., N. of a class of herbs (used<BR>medicinally for expelling wind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्वेय
शाल्वेय, आस्, m. pl. the inhabitants of Śalva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाव|शावः
शाव शाव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शव), cadaverous,<BR>relating to a dead body, produced by or belonging<BR>to a corpse; dead; of a cadaverous or dark yellowish<BR>colour, tawny; relating to purification from the de-<BR>filement caused by contact with a corpse or the death<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">Page1003-b+ 77</a>]<BR>of a relation; (अस्), m. a dark yellowish or tawny<BR>colour; the young of any animal, (in this sense pro-<BR>bably connected with rt. श्वि, cf. शिशु.)<BR>—शावाशौच<BR>(˚व-अश्˚), अम्, n. impurity caused by contact with<BR>a dead body or by the death of a relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावक|शावकः
शावक, अस्, m. the young of any animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावसायन
शावसायन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शावर शावर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शवर), relat-<BR>ing to a savage or barbarian, barbarous; low, vile;<BR>(अस्), m. fault, offence; sin, wickedness; the Lodh<BR>tree, = लोध्र; (ई), f. cowach, Carpopogon Pruriens;<BR>a sort of Prākṛt, (one of the five Vibhāṣās, said<BR>to be that spoken by the Śavaras.)<BR>—शावर-<BR>भाष्य, see शाबर-भ्˚.<BR>—शावर-भेदाख्य<BR>(˚द-आख्˚), अम्, n. copper.<BR>—शावरोत्सव (˚र-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, m. a festival observed by savage or bar-<BR>barous tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाशदान
शाशदान शाशदान. See under rt. शद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वत|शाश्वतं|शाश्वतः
शाश्वत शाश्वत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शश्वत्),<BR>eternal, constant, perpetual; all; about to happen,<BR>future; (अस्), m., N. of Vyāsa; of Śiva; of a king;<BR>of the author of the Nānārtha-koṣa; the sun; (ई),<BR>f. the earth; (अम्), n. heaven, ether; (अम्), ind.<BR>constantly, perpetually, eternally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतिक
शाश्वतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, eternal, constant, per-<BR>petual, permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वसत्
शाश्वसत् शाश्वसत्, अत्, अती, अत् (fr. Intens.<BR>of rt. श्वस्), Ved. breathing repeatedly, panting, con-<BR>stantly snorting (said of the horses of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुल
शाष्कुल शाष्कुल, अस्, ई, अम् (said to be an<BR>anom. form for शौष्कल fr. शुष्कल), eating<BR>flesh or fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुलिक|शाष्कुलिकं
शाष्कुलिक शाष्कुलिक, अम्, n. (fr. शष्-<BR>कुली), a quantity of baked cakes or pastry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास् 1. शास् (connected with rt. शंस्),<BR>cl. 2. P. शास्ति (Ved. and ep. also A.<BR>शास्ते; ep. also cl. 1. P. शासति; in some forms शास् is<BR>changed to शिस् and this again to शिष्, e. g. Pres. P. 1st<BR>du. शिष्वस्, 2nd du. शिष्ठस्, 3rd pl. शासति, Impf.<BR>2nd and 3rd sing. अशात्, Impv. 2nd sing. शाधि,<BR>Ved. शिशाधि), शशास, शासिष्यति, अशिषत्, (Ved.<BR>form शास्तन, Ṛg-veda X. 52, 1), शासितुम्, to rule,<BR>govern, command, order, direct, control; to enact,<BR>decree; to train, instruct, inform, teach (with two<BR>acc.); to report, proclaim [cf. rt. शंस्]; to correct,<BR>punish, chide; (Ved. A.) to implore, wish, desire<BR>[cf. आ-शास्, आ-शंस्]; Pass. शिष्यते, to be taught;<BR>to learn [cf. शिष्यते under rt. 2. शिष्]: Caus.<BR>शासयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशशासत्, to correct, punish:<BR>Desid. शिशासिषति: Intens. शेशिष्यते, शाशास्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
2. शास्, आस्, m. (connected with rt. शंस्), Ved.<BR>one who recites, a reciter, repeater [cf. उक्थ-शास्];<BR>a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास|शासः
शास, अस्, m., Ved. order, command, (Sāy. = शा-<BR>सन, Ṛg-veda I. 68, 5); praise, hymn of praise,<BR>(Sāy. = स्तुति; in this sense connected with rt. शंस्);<BR>N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi (having the patronymic Bhāra-<BR>dhvāja, and author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 152);<BR>epithet of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासक|शासकः
शासक, अस्, इका, अम्, a ruler, governor; a chastiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासत्
शासत्, अत्, अती, अत् (the nom. m. follows the rule for<BR>cl. 3), ruling, regulating, governing, commanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासन|शासनं
शासन, अस्, ई, अम्, one who instructs, instructing,<BR>directing, &c.; (ई), f., Ved. an instructress; (अम्),<BR>n. the act of governing, ruling, government; an<BR>order, edict, enactment, decree, command, direction;<BR>the act of instructing, instruction, discipline; a pre-<BR>cept; a royal grant, charter (usually a grant of land<BR>or of particular privileges, and frequently inscribed on<BR>stone or copper); a writing, deed, written contract or<BR>agreement; any written book or work of authority,<BR>scripture; the control or government of the passions,<BR>self-control, devotion.<BR>—शासन-दूषक, अस्, इका,<BR>अम्, disobeying the command of a king.<BR>—शासन-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘edict-plate,’ a plate of copper or of<BR>stone on which an edict or grant is inscribed; a sheet<BR>of paper on which an order is written.<BR>—शासन-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">Page1003-c+ 81</a>]<BR>हर, अस्, m. a command-bearer, one bearing an<BR>edict, a royal messenger.<BR>—शासन-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>bearing commands; (ई), m. a messenger, envoy.<BR>—शासनातिवृत्ति (˚न-अत्˚), इस्, f. the transgression<BR>of a command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनीय
शासनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be governed or directed;<BR>to be corrected, deserving punishment, punishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासित|शासितः
शासित, अस्, आ, अम्, governed, ruled, directed;<BR>corrected, punished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितव्य
शासितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be governed; to be<BR>ordered; to be corrected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितृ
शासितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, ruling, governing; ordering,<BR>commanding; one who rules or governs, a governor,<BR>commander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासिन्
शासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ruling, directing, controlling;<BR>correcting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासु
शासु, उस्, m., Ved. a governor, ruler [cf. शास्तृ];<BR>a command, (Sāy. = शासनम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्ति|शास्तिः
शास्ति, इस्, f. governing, ruling, ordering; a com-<BR>mand, order; correction, punishment; a punishment<BR>inflicted by royal command; a sceptre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who rules or governs or<BR>corrects; a ruler, governor, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda. I. 60, 2.<BR>शासुः = शासितुः, gen. c. ‘of a ruler’); teaching, in-<BR>structing; (ता), m. a ruler, governor, king; a father;<BR>a teacher, master, instructor; a Buddha or Jina or<BR>the deified teacher of either of these sects.<BR>—शास्तृ-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of a ruler, &c.; governing,<BR>chastising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्र|शास्त्रं
शास्त्र, अम्, n. ‘an instrument of directing or<BR>teaching,’ an order, command, rule, precept, institute;<BR>religious or scientific treatise, any sacred book or<BR>composition of divine or standard authority (applica-<BR>ble even to the Veda, and said to be of fourteen or<BR>even eighteen kinds, see under विद्या; the word<BR>शास्त्र is often found at the end of a comp. after the<BR>word denoting the subject of the book, or applied<BR>collectively to whole departments of knowledge,<BR>e. g. वेदान्त-श्˚, a work on the Vedānta philosophy<BR>or the whole body of teaching on that subject;<BR>धर्म-श्˚, a law-book or whole body of written<BR>laws; काव्य-श्˚, a poetical work or poetry in general;<BR>शिल्पि-श्˚, works on the mechanical arts; काम-श्˚,<BR>erotic compositions; अलङ्कार-श्˚, rhetoric, &c.);<BR>a book, treatise, body of teaching (in general),<BR>scripture, science.<BR>—शास्त्र-कृत्, त्, m. the author<BR>of a Śāstra; a writer or author (in general); a<BR>Ṛṣi or sage (as the author of sacred works).<BR>—शास्-<BR>त्र-कोविद, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in sacred works.<BR>—शास्त्र-गण्ड, अस्, m. a superficial reader of<BR>books; a general reader (= प्रघटा-विद्).<BR>—शास्-<BR>त्र-चक्षुस्, उस्, n. ‘the eye of science,’ grammer.<BR>—शास्त्र-चारण, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in the Śāstras,<BR>well-versed in sacred works or sciences.<BR>—शास्त्र-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing sacred works, acquainted<BR>with the Śāstras; knowing books; a mere theorist.<BR>—शास्त्रज्ञ-ता, f. or शास्त्रज्ञ-त्व, अम्, n. know-<BR>ledge of sacred works, acquaintance with the Śāstras.<BR>—शास्त्र-ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of sacred works,<BR>knowledge derived from the study of the Śāstras.<BR>—शास्त्र-तत्त्व, अम्, n. the truth (taught) in sacred<BR>works, the truth of the Śāstras.<BR>—शास्त्रतत्त्व-ज्ञ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, understanding the truth (as taught in)<BR>sacred works; (अस्), m. an astronomer, astrologer.<BR>—शास्त्र-तस्, ind. according to the Śāstras, accord-<BR>ing to sacred precept or law.<BR>—शास्त्र-दर्शिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, seeing or knowing the Śāstras, skilled in<BR>sacred works or sciences.<BR>—शास्त्र-दीपिका, f., N. of<BR>a commentary on the Nyāya-sūtras by Pārtha-sārathi.<BR>—शास्त्र-दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, seen in the Śāstras,<BR>stated in sacred works or in books treating of any<BR>science.<BR>—शास्त्र-निन्दा, f. reviling or denying the<BR>authority of sacred works.<BR>—शास्त्र-प्रसङ्ग, अस्,<BR>m. the subject of the Śāstras; the discussion of<BR>sacred works.<BR>—शास्त्र-योनि, इस्, m. the source of the<BR>Śāstras.<BR>—शास्त्रयोनि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of<BR>being the source of the Śāstras.<BR>—शास्त्र-वक्तृ,<BR>ता, m. one who expounds sacred books.<BR>—१. शास्त्र-<BR>वत्, ind. like the sacred writings, conformably or<BR>according to written authority.<BR>—२. शास्त्र-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having or following sacred institutes, skilled<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">Page1004-a+ 79</a>]<BR>in sacred writings.<BR>—शास्त्र-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing<BR>the Śāstras, understanding or conversant with the<BR>scriptures, skilled in sacred sciences.<BR>—शास्त्र-वि-<BR>धान, अम्, n. or शास्त्र-विधि, इस्, m. scripture-<BR>precept, sacred ritual, ceremonial injunction.<BR>—शास्-<BR>त्रविधानोक्त (˚न-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, prescribed by<BR>scriptural precept or sacred injunction.<BR>—शास्त्र-<BR>विप्रतिषिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, forbidden by the Śās-<BR>tras, contrary to the scriptures, illegal.<BR>—शास्त्र-वि-<BR>प्रतिषेध, अस्, m. opposition to the Śāstras, any<BR>act contrary to sacred precept or scriptural injunction.<BR>—शास्त्र-विमुख, अस्, ई, अम्, disinclined to learn-<BR>ing, averse from study.<BR>—शास्त्र-विरुद्ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, opposed to the Śāstras, contrary to law or reli-<BR>gious precept.<BR>—शास्त्र-विरोध, अस्, m. opposition<BR>to sacred precept; mutual contradiction of books,<BR>incompatibility of different works.<BR>—शास्त्र-व्युत्-<BR>पत्ति, इस्, f. perfect conversancy with sacred writings.<BR>—शास्त्र-शिल्पिन्, ई, m. the country of Kaśmīra;<BR>(इनस्), m. pl. the people of Kaśmīra (commonly<BR>called Cashmere).<BR>—शास्त्र-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>established by the Śāstras, proved by sacred works.<BR>—शास्त्राचरण (˚र-आच्˚), अम्, n. the study of<BR>the Śāstras; (अस्), m. one versed in the scriptures or<BR>well read in sacred works; a student of the Vedas<BR>or one whose conduct is regulated by their precepts;<BR>a Pandit.<BR>—शास्त्रातिक्रम (˚र-अत्˚), अस्, m. trans-<BR>gressing the Śāstras, violation of sacred precepts.<BR>—शास्त्राननुष्ठान (˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. non-<BR>performance of sacred precept, disregard of the<BR>authority of religious books.<BR>—शास्त्रानुष्ठान<BR>(˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. observance of the Śāstras, con-<BR>forming to sacred law or ritual; applying one's self<BR>to books.<BR>—शास्त्रानुष्ठित (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>established or authorized by the Śāstras, obeying or<BR>following sacred institutes.<BR>—शास्त्रानुसार (˚र-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. conformity to the Śāstras, following<BR>sacred ordinances.<BR>—शास्त्राभिज्ञ (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, learned in sacred works, versed in the Śās-<BR>tras.<BR>—शास्त्रार्थ (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m. the object or<BR>purport of a book, the meaning of a sacred precept,<BR>a precept or direction of the Śāstras or of any parti-<BR>cular Śāstra, a scriptural statement or dogma.<BR>—शास्-<BR>त्रोक्त (˚र-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, declared or enjoined<BR>by the Śāstras, declared in works of sacred authority,<BR>said in a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रित
शास्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, treated according to the<BR>Śāstras.<BR>—शास्त्रितार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, m. a scien-<BR>tifically treated subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिन्
शास्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having or following sacred<BR>works, versed in the Śāstras, skilled in books; (ई),<BR>m. a teacher of sacred science; a learned man, one<BR>who has studied the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रीय
शास्त्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, scriptural, authorized by or<BR>conformable to sacred precept, agreeable to sacred<BR>institutes, legal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्य|शास्यः
शास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be governed or regulated,<BR>to be ordained or prescribed by law; to be corrected;<BR>punishable, deserving chastisement or punishment,<BR>corrigible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट|शिष्टः
शिष्ट, शिष्य, &c. See under 2. शिष्ट, p. 1009.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास|शासः
शास शास, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. शस्), Ved.<BR>‘destroyer,’ epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाह
शाह शाह, N. of a country (belonging to<BR>Kaśmīra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाहि
शाहि, इस्, m., N. of a dynasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि 1. शि (closely connected with rt. शो),<BR>cl. 5. P. A. शिनोति, शिनुते (Ved. also cl. 3.<BR>A. शिशीते), शिशाय, शिश्ये, शेष्यति, -ते, अशैषीत्,<BR>अशेष्ट, शेतुम्, to sharpen, whet; to make sharp<BR>or thin, attenuate; to excite; to be sharp; to be<BR>attentive: Caus. शाययति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशीशयत्:<BR>Desid. शिशीषति, -ते: Intens. शेशीयते, शेशयीति,<BR>शेशेति; [cf. Gr. κί-ω, κί-νυ-μαι, κἰνέ-ω; Lat. ci-o,<BR>ci-e-o, ci-tu-s, excito, incito; Lith. koja.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
2. शि, इस्, m. an epithet of Śiva; auspiciousness,<BR>good fortune; peace, composure, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित|शितं
शित, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. शात, fr. rt. शो], sharpened,<BR>whetted; attenuated, thin, emaciated, wasted, de-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">Page1004-b+ 74</a>]<BR>clined; weak, feeble.<BR>—शित-ता, f. or शित-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. sharpness.<BR>—शित-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, sharp-edged.<BR>—शित-शर, अस्, m. a sharp arrow.<BR>—शित-शरा-<BR>भीत (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded or encom-<BR>passed with sharp arrows.<BR>—शित-सूक, अस्, m. ‘sharp-<BR>bearded,’ barley; wheat.<BR>—शिताग्र (˚त-अग्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, sharp-pointed; (अस्), m. a thorn.<BR>—शितास्त्र-भृत्<BR>(˚त-अस्˚), त्, m. bearing sharp weapons.<BR>—शितेषु (˚त-<BR>इषु), उस्, m. a sharp arrow.<BR>—शितोदा, f. = शीतोदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित्वा
शित्वा, ind. having sharpened, having whetted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशान
शिशान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sharpening, making<BR>sharp, (Sāy. = तीक्ष्णी-कुर्वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि 3. शि, (in grammar) a technical term<BR>for the case-ending इ, substituted for जस् and शस् in<BR>neuters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशपा
शिंशपा शिंशपा or (according to some)<BR>शिंशिपा, f. the tree Dalbergia Sisu; the Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशुमार
शिंशुमार शिंशुमार, अस्, m., Ved. a por-<BR>poise (= शिशु-मार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंह्
शिंह् शिंह् = rt. शिङ्घ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंहाण
शिंहाण, शिंहाणक, = शिङ्घाण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्कु|शिक्कुः
शिक्कु शिक्कु, उस्, उस्, उ, idle, lazy, following<BR>no business or profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्थ|शिक्थं
शिक्थ शिक्थ or शिक्थक, अम्, n. bee's<BR>wax, (also written सिक्थक, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्य|शिक्यं
शिक्य शिक्य, अम्, आ, n. f. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. V. 16. fr. शि substituted for rt. स्रंस्, cf.<BR>शिच्), a kind of loop or swing made of rope and<BR>suspended from either end of a pole or yoke to<BR>receive a load; the burden or load so carried; a sort<BR>of hanging-shelf suspended by strings; the strings of<BR>a balance.<BR>—शिक्याधार (˚या-आध्˚), अस्, m. ‘loop-<BR>holder,’ the hook or eye at each end of a pole or<BR>beam for holding the above looped cord or for hold-<BR>ing the strings of a balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यित|शिक्यितं
शिक्यित, अस्, आ, अम्, placed or carried in the above<BR>loop, suspended in a swing or loop made of cord, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्वन्
शिक्वन् शिक्वन् (perhaps connected with<BR>शिक्य above), Ved. a rope, cord, (Sāy. शिक्वभिः =<BR>रज्जुभिः, Ṛg-veda I. 141, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्वस्
शिक्वस् शिक्वस् (connected with rt. 1. शक्),<BR>Ved. mighty, powerful, able, (Sāy. शिक्वसः = शक्-<BR>ताः, Ṛg-veda V. 52, 16; शिक्वसे = शक्ताय, Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 92, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्
शिक्ष् शिक्ष् (properly Desid. of rt. 1. शक्,<BR>q. v., but regarded by some as a separate rt.), cl. 1. A.<BR>शिक्षते, Aor. अशिक्षिष्ट, शिक्षितुम्, to learn,<BR>acquire knowledge; to teach (Ved.); to give (P.,<BR>Ved., see rt. 1. शक्): Pass. शिक्ष्यते, Aor. अशिक्षि:<BR>Caus. शिक्षयति, -ते, Aor. अशिशिक्षत्, -त, to teach,<BR>&c., (see rt. 1. शक्, p. 985.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षक|शिक्षकः
शिक्षक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, a learner; a teacher,<BR>instructor, (in this sense fr. Caus.); one who knows<BR>Śikṣā or the science of euphony, (see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षण|शिक्षणं
शिक्षण, अम्, n. the act of learning, acquiring<BR>knowledge; teaching, instruction (fr. Caus.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षणीय
शिक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be learnt; to be taught<BR>(fr. Caus.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षत्
शिक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. teaching, instructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षमाण|शिक्षमाणः
शिक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. learning; (अस्),<BR>m. a learner, pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षयितृ
शिक्षयितृ, ता, m. (fr. Caus.), an instructor,<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षयित्वा
शिक्षयित्वा, ind. having taught, having instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा, f. desire of being able to effect anything,<BR>wish to prevail (Kirāt. XV. 37); learning, study,<BR>the acquisition of knowledge; teaching, instruction,<BR>training, discipline; the science which teaches proper<BR>pronunciation and especially the laws of euphony<BR>peculiar to the Veda, (one of the six Vedāṅgas; see<BR>वेदाङ्ग); modesty, humility, diffidence; giving,<BR>bestowing (Ved., see rt. 1. शक्); the plant Bignonia<BR>Indica.<BR>—शिक्षा-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, instruction-caus-<BR>ing, instruction-giving; (अस्), m. a teacher, instructor;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">Page1004-c+ 78</a>]<BR>epithet of Vyāsa.<BR>—शिक्षा-गुरु, उस्, m. a religious<BR>preceptor, teacher.<BR>—शिक्षा-नर, अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>chief or foremost in liberality; epithet of Indra,<BR>(Sāy. = दानस्य नेता.)<BR>—शिक्षा-शक्ति, इस्, f.<BR>‘power of learning,’ dexterity, skill.<BR>—शिक्षा-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a section in the Kātantra treating of<BR>the pronunciation of letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाण
शिक्षाण, अस्, आ, अम्, learning, acquiring knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, learnt, studied; instructed,<BR>taught (with acc., e. g. शिक्षितो नृत्यम्, instructed<BR>in dancing); disciplined, exercised, trained, tamed,<BR>tame; docile; skilful, clever, conversant; modest, diffi-<BR>dent.<BR>—शिक्षिताक्षर (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, m. one who is<BR>taught letters or literature, a pupil, scholar.<BR>—शिक्षि-<BR>तायुध (˚त-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षितव्य
शिक्षितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be learnt; to be in-<BR>structed or taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित्वा
शिक्षित्वा, ind. having learnt; having instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षिन्
शिक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, learning; instructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षु
शिक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of learning, one who<BR>wishes to learn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्य
शिक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be learnt; to be trained<BR>or taught, teachable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्यमाण
शिक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being learnt; being<BR>taught; (अस्), m. a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिख
शिख शिख, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a serpent<BR>priest; [cf. अनु-शिख.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखक|शिखकः
शिखक, अस्, m. (according to Śabda-k. = लेख-<BR>क), a writer, scribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्ड|शिखंड|शिखंडः|शिखण्डः
शिखण्ड शिखण्ड, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>शिखा, q. v.), a tuft or lock of hair left on the crown<BR>or sides of the head at tonsure; any crest or plume<BR>or tuft; the tail of a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डक|शिखंडक|शिखंडकः|शिखण्डकः
शिखण्डक, अस्, m. a tuft or lock of hair left<BR>on the crown of the head at tonsure; three or five<BR>locks left on the side of the head (especially in men<BR>of the military class, = काक-पक्ष); a curl or<BR>ringlet; any crest or tuft; a peacock's tail, (in this<BR>sense अम्, n. according to Śabda-k.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिक|शिखंडिक|शिखंडिकः|शिखण्डिकः
शिखण्डिक, अस्, m. a cock; (आ), f. a tuft or lock<BR>of hair on the crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डित
शिखण्डित, अम्, n. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिन्|शिखंडिन्
शिखण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crested, tufted; (ई), m. a pea-<BR>cock; a peacock's tail; a cock; an arrow; a kind of<BR>yellow jasmine; the plant Abrus Precatorius; N. of<BR>Viṣṇu; of a Ṛṣi or Muni (one of the seven stars<BR>of the Great Bear, cf. चित्र-शिखण्डिन्); N. of a son of<BR>Drupada (enemy of Bhīṣma and born as a female);<BR>of a mountain; (इनी), f. a pea-hen; a kind of jasmine<BR>(= यूथिका); the shrub Abrus Precatorius; N. of the<BR>daughter of Drupada (afterwards changed to a male, see<BR>above); N. of two Apsarases (daughters of Kaśyapa and<BR>regarded as the authoresses of Ṛg-veda IX. 104).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाण्डक|शिखाण्डकः
शिखाण्डक, अस्, m. a tuft or lock of hair on the<BR>top or side of the head (= शिखण्डक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखर|शिखरं|शिखरः
शिखर शिखर. See p. 1005, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखलोहित|शिखलोहितः
शिखलोहित शिखलोहित, अस्, m. a plant<BR>(commonly called कुकुर-मुडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखा
शिखा शिखा, f. (according to Uṇādi-s. V.<BR>24. fr. rt. 1. शी; probably connected with rt. 1. शि),<BR>a sharp end, point, spike, peak, pinnacle, projection,<BR>top, summit, end or point (in general); the end or<BR>point of a garment; a crest, top-knot, tuft, plume,<BR>lock of hair on the crown of the head; a peacock's<BR>crest or comb; a pointed flame, flame (in general);<BR>the point or tip of the foot; a ray of light; a fibrous<BR>root, root (in general); a branch which takes root,<BR>any branch; the head or chief of anything, principal<BR>thing, acme; a kind of metre; a particular plant<BR>(= लाङ्गलिकी); the fever or excitement of love;<BR>[cf. Hib. sigh, ‘a hill.’]<BR>—शिखा-कन्द, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of onion or turnip (= गृञ्जन).<BR>—शिखा-जट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who wears a lock of hair in a knot<BR>on the top of the head.<BR>—शिखा-तरु, उस्, m.<BR>‘flame-tree,’ a lamp-stand, candlestick.<BR>—शिखा-<BR>दामन्, अ, n. a garland at the top of the head.<BR>—शिखा-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, having a sharp end or<BR>point, pointed, crested, having a top-knot; (अस्), m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-a" target="_blank">Page1005-a+ 81</a>]<BR>a peacock; epithet of a particular Jaina or Buddhist<BR>deified saint (= मञ्जु-घोष).<BR>—शिखाधर-ज,<BR>‘peacock-produced,’ a peacock's feather.<BR>—शिखा-<BR>धार, अस्, m. ‘crest-wearer,’ a peacock.<BR>—शिखा-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. a crest-gem, jewel worn on the head.<BR>—शिखा-मूल, अम्, n. ‘tuft-root,’ any root having<BR>a tuft of leaves; a carrot; a turnip.<BR>—१. शिखा-वत्,<BR>ind. like a crest.<BR>—२. शिखा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>a point, pointed, wearing a crest, crested; possessing<BR>flame, flaming; (आन्), m. epithet of fire; a lamp;<BR>the personified descending node; a particular plant<BR>or tree (= चित्रक); (अती), f. a kind of plant, cock's<BR>comb; another plant (= मूर्वा).<BR>—शिखा-वर,<BR>अस्, m. the jack fruit tree, Artocarpus Integrifolia (=<BR>पनस).<BR>—शिखा-वल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a point,<BR>pointed, having a crest, crested; (अस्), m. a peacock;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of plant, cock's comb, Celosia Cristata.<BR>—शिखा-वृक्ष, अस्, m. ‘flame-tree,’ a lamp-stand,<BR>candlestick.<BR>—शिखा-वृद्धि, इस्, f. ‘crest-interest,’<BR>a kind of usurious interest increasing daily, (see<BR>वृद्ध्य्-आजीव.)<BR>—शिखा-सूत्र, अम्, n. the lock of<BR>hair on the head and the sacred thread (regarded as the<BR>distinguishing marks of the Brāhmanical caste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1004-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखर|शिखरं|शिखरः
शिखर, अस्, अम्, m. n. point, peak, top, summit,<BR>end, pinnacle, spire, turret; the peak or summit of a<BR>mountain; the top of a tree; the edge or point of<BR>a sword; erection of the hair of the body, bristling<BR>of the hair; the armpit; a particular position of<BR>the fingers or hands; a ruby-like gem (of a bright<BR>red colour said to resemble ripe pomegranate seed);<BR>the bud of the Arabian jasmine; N. of a weapon;<BR>(आ), f. a plant from the fibres of which bow-strings<BR>are made, Sanseviera Roxburghiana (= मूर्वा).<BR>—शिखर-निचय, अस्, m. a collection of mountain<BR>peaks.<BR>—शिखर-वासिनी, f. ‘dwelling on a peak (of<BR>the Himālaya),’ epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिन्
शिखरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, pointed, peaked, crested,<BR>tufted; resembling the buds of the Arabian jasmine;<BR>(ई), m. a mountain; a hill-fort, stronghold; a tree;<BR>the plant Achyranthes Aspera (= अपामार्ग); the<BR>lapwing; (इणी), f. an eminent or excellent woman,<BR>a kind of Atyaṣṭi metre, four times ˘¯¯¯¯¯˘˘<BR>˘˘˘¯¯˘˘˘¯; a line of hair extending across<BR>the navel; a dish of curds and sugar with spices; a<BR>kind of vine; the plant Sanseviera (= मूर्वा); Arabian<BR>jasmine; N. of various other plants (= वन्दाक; =<BR>कुन्दुरुक; = यावनाल).<BR>—शिखरि-सम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, equal to a mountain, mountain-like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखालु|शिखालुः
शिखालु, उस्, m. a peacock's crest; cock's comb,<BR>Celosia Cristata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिन्
शिखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, pointed, crested, peaked, having<BR>a tuft or lock of hair on the top of the head; proud;<BR>(ई), m. a peacock; a cock; an arrow; a tree; fire; a<BR>symbolical expression for the number three (from<BR>the three fires); a lamp; a bull; a horse; a moun-<BR>tain; a Brāhman; a religious mendicant; epithet<BR>of Ketu, the personified descending node; a par-<BR>ticular tree (= चित्रक); various other plants, =<BR>अज-लोमन्; = मेथिका; = सितावर; (इनी), f. a<BR>pea-hen; cock's comb, Celosia Cristata.<BR>—शिखि-<BR>कण्ठ or शिखि-ग्रीव, अम्, n. blue vitriol or sul-<BR>phate of copper (said to be so called because coloured<BR>like a peacock's neck).<BR>—शिखि-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR>—शिखि-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘fire-marked,’<BR>smoke; ‘peacock-marked,’ epithet of Kārttikeya<BR>[cf. शिखि-वाहन].<BR>—शिखिध्वज-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—शिखि-पिच्छ or शिखि-पुच्छ,<BR>अम्, n. a peacock's tail.<BR>—शिखि-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘pea-<BR>cock-loved,’ a tree (= लघु-बदर).<BR>—शिखि-मण्-<BR>डल, अस्, m. Cratæva Roxburghii (= वरुण).<BR>—शि-<BR>खि-मोदा, f. ‘peacock's joy,’ a plant (= अज-मोदा).<BR>—शिखि-यूप, अस्, m. an antelope (= श्री-कारिन्).<BR>—शिखि-वर्धक, अस्, m. ‘peacock-nourisher,’ a<BR>pumpkin, gourd.<BR>—शिखि-वासस्, N. of a mythical<BR>mountain, (Viṣṇu-Purāṇa II. 2.)<BR>—शिखि-वाहन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a peacock for his vehicle,’ epithet of<BR>Kārttikeya, (this god being represented riding on<BR>a peacock.)<BR>—शिखि-व्रत, अम्, n. a particular<BR>religious observance.<BR>—शिखि-शिखा, f. a peacock's<BR>crest; ‘fire-peak,’ a flame.<BR>—शिखि-शेखर, अम्, n. a<BR>peacock's crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रु|शिग्रुः
शिग्रु शिग्रु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. शि),<BR>a kind of tree, Hyperanthera Moringa (the root of<BR>which is used like horse-radish, see शोभाञ्जन); a<BR>pot-herb in general; (अवस्), m. pl., N. of a people<BR>(Ved.).<BR>—शिग्रु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, growing on or pro-<BR>duced by the Moringa; (अम्), n. the seed of the<BR>Moringa.<BR>—शिग्रु-मूल, अम्, n. the pungent root<BR>of the Moringa.<BR>—शिग्रु-वीज, अम्, n. the seed of<BR>the Moringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुक
शिग्रुक, अस्, m. = शिग्रु, a particular plant or<BR>pot-herb, (Manu VI. 14.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्ख्|शिंख्
शिङ्ख् शिङ्ख्, cl. 1. P. शिङ्खति, &c., to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्गाम्बिका
शिङ्गाम्बिका शिङ्गाम्बिका, f. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घ्|शिंघ्
शिङ्घ् शिङ्घ् (sometimes written शिंह्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. P. शिङ्घति, शिशिङ्घ,<BR>शिङ्घितुम्, to perceive by the nose, smell; [cf. उप-<BR>शिङ्घ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाण|शिंघाण|शिङ्घाणं|शिंघाणः|शिङ्घाणः
शिङ्घाण, अस्, m. (also written शिंहाण, सिंहाण),<BR>froth, foam; phlegm; a kind of sauce or gruel (=<BR>पिच्छिल?); the sperm of an alligator, = नक्र-<BR>रेतस्; (अम्), n. the mucus of the nose; rust of<BR>iron; a glass vessel (= काच-पात्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाणक|शिंघाणक|शिंघाणकं|शिंघाणकः|शिङ्घाणकः
शिङ्घाणक, अस्, m. phlegm; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>the mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घित|शिंघित|शिङ्घितं
शिङ्घित, अस्, आ, अम्, perceived by the nose,<BR>smelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घिन्
शिङ्घिन्, ई, इनी, इ, smelling; [cf. सिङ्घिनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिच्
शिच् शिच्, क्, f. (= शिक्य, q. v.), the string<BR>or cord of a pole or yoke for carrying burdens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिजार
शिजार शिजार, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्ज्|शिंज्
शिञ्ज् शिञ्ज्, cl. 2. A. शिङ्क्ते (according<BR>to Vopa-deva also cl. 1. 10. A. शिञ्जते,<BR>शिञ्जयते), शिशिञ्जे, शिञ्जितुम्, to tinkle, rattle,<BR>jingle; to snort, roar, bellow (Ved.); to whisper<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्ज|शिंज|शिंजः|शिञ्जः
शिञ्ज, अस्, आ, m. f. tinkle, jingle, a tinkling or<BR>jingling sound, (especially) the tinkling sound of<BR>silver ornaments on the ancles or wrist, rattle,<BR>rattling sound; (आ), f. a bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जञ्जिका|शिंजंजिका
शिञ्जञ्जिका, f. a chain worn round the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जत्
शिञ्जत्, अन्, अती, अत्, tinkling, jingling, sounding.<BR>—शिञ्जद्-वलय-सुभग, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasant<BR>with tinkling bracelets or zones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जान
शिञ्जान, अस्, आ, अम्, tinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जार
शिञ्जार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sounding, uttering<BR>praise, (Sāy. = शब्दयत्, स्तुवत्, Ṛg-veda VIII. 5,<BR>25.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जित|शिंजित|शिञ्जितं
शिञ्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, tinkled, tinkling; (अम्), n.<BR>tinkling, rattling; the tinkling of metallic ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जिन्
शिञ्जिन्, ई, इनी, इ, tinkling, making a tinkling<BR>sound; (इनी), f. a bow-string; tinkling rings worn<BR>round the toes or feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिट्
शिट् शिट् (also written सिट्), cl. 1. P. शे-<BR>टति, &c., to value little, disregard, despise,<BR>treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिण्डाकी
शिण्डाकी शिण्डाकी, f. a particular edible<BR>substance made with rice and mustard and said to<BR>possess stomachic properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित्
शित् 2. शित्, त्, त्, त्, (in grammar) having श्<BR>as an indicatory letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित|शितं
शित शित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शि or rt. शो),<BR>sharpened, &c. See under rt. 1. शि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितद्रु|शितद्रुः
शितद्रु शित-द्रु, उस्, f. = शत-द्रु, the river<BR>Sutlej.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितामन्
शितामन् शितामन्, अ, n. (probably con-<BR>nected with शित or शिति fr. rt. 1. शि), Ved. a parti-<BR>cular part of a sacrificial victim, (according to Yāska,<BR>the fore-foot; according to others, the shoulder-blade,<BR>the liver, &c. See Nirukta IV. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिति|शितिः
शिति शिति, इस्, ई, इ (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 121. fr. rt. शत्; according to others fr. rt. 1. शि),<BR>white [cf. सित]; black, dark-blue; (इस्), m. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">Page1005-c+ 77</a>]<BR>Bhojpattra or birch tree (= भूर्ज).<BR>—शिति-कण्ठ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a white throat; having a black<BR>throat, dark-necked [cf. नील-कण्ठ]; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva (= श्री-कण्ठ); a gallinule; a<BR>peacock.<BR>—शितिकण्ठ-दीक्षित, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N. (= श्री-कण्ठ-दीक्षित).<BR>—शिति-चार, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of pot-herb (apparently Marsilea Dentata).<BR>—शिति-<BR>च्छद, अस्, m. ‘white-feathered,’ a goose; [cf.<BR>सित-च्छद.]<BR>—शिति-पक्ष, अस्, m. ‘white-winged,’<BR>a goose; [cf. सित-पक्ष.]<BR>—शिति-पाद्, पात्, पदी<BR>or पात्, पत्, Ved. having white feet, white-footed;<BR>black-footed.<BR>—शिति-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>white-backed, having a white back; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a serpent-priest (fabled to have acted as Maitrā-<BR>varuṇa at a sacrifice).<BR>—शिति-रत्न, अम्, n. ‘blue-<BR>gem,’ a sapphire.<BR>—शिति-सारक, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>black essence,’ a sort of ebony (= तिन्दु, q. v.; this<BR>plant yields a strong black resin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिर
शिथिर शिथिर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्रथ्),<BR>Ved. = शिथिल, relaxed, loose, &c.; outstretched,<BR>extended, (Sāy. = दानार्थम् प्रसारित, Ṛg-veda<BR>VII. 45, 2); (अम्), n. anything relaxed or undone<BR>(as a bond, fetter, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिल|शिथिलं
शिथिल, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 54.<BR>fr. श्लथ् for rt. श्रथ्), loose, loosened, slackened,<BR>relaxed, untied, unfastened, undone, lax, flaccid,<BR>flabby, not rigid or compact; dishevelled (as hair);<BR>dissolved; decayed; languid, inert, weak, unnerved,<BR>feeble; ineffective, unenergetic; not strict, not carefully<BR>or strictly observed, loosely performed; loosely retained<BR>or possessed, abandoned, shaken off; (अम्), n. a<BR>loose fastening; looseness, laxity, slowness; a parti-<BR>cular kind of separation or combination of the terms<BR>or members of a logical series.<BR>—शिथिल-ता, f. or<BR>शिथिल-त्व, अम्, n. looseness, laxity, relaxedness,<BR>relaxation; the being unfastened, a state of disso-<BR>lution, want of energy, languor.<BR>—शिथिल-प्र-<BR>यत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, (one) whose efforts are relaxed.<BR>—शिथिल-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, relaxed in strength,<BR>weakened, relaxed.<BR>—शिथिल-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, hav-<BR>ing impaired wealth; shining with diminished rays.<BR>—शिथिल-शक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, impaired in strength or<BR>power.<BR>—शिथिली-करण, अम्, n. the act of loosen-<BR>ing, unfastening; impairing, weakening, reducing,<BR>—शिथिली-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make loose, loosen, unfasten; to relax,<BR>slacken; to make languid, weaken, enfeeble, impair;<BR>to remit, dismiss, give up, abandon.<BR>—शिथिली-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, made loose, loosened, unfastened, un-<BR>bound, slackened; let loose; impaired, weakened,<BR>reduced.<BR>—शिथिली-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवि-<BR>तुम्, to become loosened or slackened, be relaxed,<BR>to slacken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलय
शिथिलय, Nom. P. शिथिलयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>loosen, make loose, relax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलित
शिथिलित, अस्, आ, अम्, loosed, let go; relaxed,<BR>loosened; dissolved, made soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनि|शिनिः
शिनि शिनि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 51. fr. rt. 1. शी), N. of a son of Sumitra; of a<BR>descendant of Garga (a chief of the Kṣatriya tribe);<BR>a man belonging to a particular class of Kṣatriyas;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl., N. of a class of Kṣatriyas; [cf.<BR>शैन्य.]<BR>—शिनि-बाहु, N. of a river.<BR>—शिनेर्-<BR>नप्तृ, ता, m. ‘grandson of Śini,’ N. of Sātyaki<BR>(one of the Pāṇḍu chiefs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपविष्ट|शिपविष्टः
शिपविष्ट शिप-विष्ट for शिपि-विष्ट below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपाटक
शिपाटक शिपाटक, अस्, m., N. of a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपि|शिपिः
शिपि शिपि, इस्, m. (perhaps connected with<BR>rt. 1. शि), a ray of light; (इस्), f. skin, leather.<BR>—शिपि-<BR>विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose rays are displayed,<BR>pervaded by rays; bald-headed (= खलति); leprous;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; a bald man;<BR>a man naturally without prepuce; a leper; [cf. शिप-<BR>विष्ट, शिविपिष्ट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्र|शिप्रः
शिप्र शिप्र, अस्, m., N. of a lake on the<BR>high land of the Himālaya; (अम्), n., Ved. a cheek,<BR>jaw, (अयः-शिप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, iron-jawed, having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">Page1006-a+ 75</a>]<BR>jaws of iron; having an iron visor); the chin; the<BR>nose; a visor or helmet; (ए), n. du. the two jaws;<BR>(आ), f. a helmet, head-dress, turban; a visor, (Sāy.<BR>शिप्रा = उष्णीष-मयी); N. of a river issuing from<BR>the Śipra lake.<BR>—शिप्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having<BR>large or handsome jaws, (Sāy. = शोभन-हनु,<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 17, 2); having a handsome chin,<BR>handsome-chinned; [cf. सु-शिप्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1005-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्रक
शिप्रक, अस्, m., N. of the first king of the<BR>Āndhras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्रिन्
शिप्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. having a (beautiful) cheek<BR>or nose, handsome; having a handsome chin (said<BR>of Indra); (इणी), f. = शिप्र; (according to modern<BR>scholars) a draught imbibed by the mouth or jaws.<BR>—शिप्रिणी-वत्, आन्, m., Ved. epithet of Indra (=<BR>शिप्र-वत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफ|शिफः
शिफ शिफ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. शी),<BR>= शिफा below, which is the more usual form; (आ),<BR>f. a fibrous root or root in general; the root of a<BR>water-lily; a lash or stroke with a whip; spikenard<BR>(= मांसिका); turmeric; a sort of dill or fennel (=<BR>शत-पुष्पा); a mother; a river; a particular<BR>river (Ved.).<BR>—शिफा-कन्द, अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>root of a water-lily.<BR>—शिफा-धर, अस्, m. ‘pos-<BR>sessing a fibrous root,’ a branch.<BR>—शिफा-रुह, अस्,<BR>m. ‘root-growing,’ the Indian fig-tree; [cf. न्यग्-<BR>रोध.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाक|शिफाकः
शिफाक, अस्, m. the root of a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबि|शिबिः
शिबि शिबि, इस्, m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi<BR>(having the patronymic Auśīnara and author of Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 179, 1; cf. शिवि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिमिक
शिमिक शिमिक, N. of a district in Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिमी
शिमी शिमी, f., Ved. power, strength, (Sāy.<BR>= शक्ति, Ṛg-veda 1. 151, 1); a sacrificial rite,<BR>ceremony (= कर्म, Naigh. II. 7).<BR>—शिमी-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of power, full of energy<BR>or strength, strong, vigorous, energetic; granting<BR>desires, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 155, 2.<BR>शिमीवतोः = इष्ट-प्रदानादि-कर्मवतोः or प्र-<BR>हरणादि-कर्मवतोः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिमृडी
शिमृडी शिमृडी, f. a kind of shrub (=<BR>बल्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्ब|शिंबः|शिम्बः
शिम्ब शिम्ब, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. शि),<BR>a sort of large shrub, = चक्र-मर्दक; (आ), f. a<BR>pod, legume, (also written सिम्बा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बल
शिम्बल, अम्, n., Ved. the flower of the Śalmalī<BR>tree, (Sāy. = शल्मली-कुसुम, Ṛg-veda III. 53, 22.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बि|शिम्बिः
शिम्बि, इस्, f. a pod, legume [cf. सिम्बि]; a kind<BR>of grass (= एरका).<BR>—शिम्बि-पर्णी or शिम्बि-पर्-<BR>णिका, f. a sort of kidney-bean, Phaseolus Trilobus<BR>(= मुद्ग-पर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बिक|शिम्बिकः
शिम्बिक, अस्, m. a sort of pulse or kidney-bean,<BR>= कृष्ण-मुद्ग; (आ), f. a pod, legume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बी|शिंबी
शिम्बी, f. a pod, legume; a sort of kidney-bean;<BR>a kind of plant (= कपि-कच्छु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बाता
शिम्बाता शिम्बाता, m. du., Ved. mentioned<BR>in Naigh. III. 6. together with शत-रा and शात-<BR>पन्ता among the सुख-नामानि, see Ṛg-veda X.<BR>105, 5; [cf. शातपन्ता.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्यु
शिम्यु शिम्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. arousing, ex-<BR>citing, (Sāy. = बोधमान, Ṛg-veda VII. 18, 5);<BR>(उस्), m. an evil demon, Rākṣasa, (according to<BR>Sāy. = शमयितृ = बध-कारिन्, ‘a destroyer,’<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 100, 18.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिर्
शिर् शिर्, ईर्, ईर्, ईर् (fr. rt. शॄ, cf. गिर् fr. rt.<BR>1. गॄ), hurting, injuring, wounding; [cf. शशीश-<BR>शिशु-शीः, Kirāt. XV. 5.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिर|शिरं|शिरः
शिर शिर. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्
शिरस् शिरस्, अस्, n. (originally शरस् = क-<BR>रस्; according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 193. fr. rt. श्रि), the<BR>head; the skull; the top of a tree; the head or top<BR>of anything, highest part, (जानु-शिरस्, the knee-<BR>pan); highest point, pinnacle, acme; the fore part,<BR>front; the van of an army; chief, principal; [cf.<BR>Zend śara, śāranh; Gr. κάρα, κάρ, κάρη-νο-ν,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-b" target="_blank">Page1006-b+ 79</a>]<BR>κρανίο-ν, κέρας; Lat. cere-bru-m, cere-bru-m, cer-vix, cra-<BR>nium, perhaps calva; Goth. hvair-n-ei, haurn;<BR>Old Germ. hirni, horn; Angl. Sax. hœrnes; Lith.<BR>karczei, szerai; Hib. ceann.]<BR>—शिरः-कपालिन्,<BR>ई, m. an ascetic or religious mendicant who carries<BR>about a human skull (as a symbol of abandoning all<BR>worldly desires).<BR>—शिरः-पीडा, f. ‘head-pain,’ head-<BR>ache.<BR>—शिरः-प्रणाम, अस्, m. bowing or bending<BR>the head.<BR>—शिरः-प्रावरण, अम्, n. ‘head-cover-<BR>ing,’ a head-dress, turban.<BR>—शिरः-फल, अस्, m.<BR>‘having fruit on the top,’ the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—शि-<BR>रः-शूल, अम्, n. head-ache, sharp pain in the head.<BR>—शिरः-श्रेणि, इस्, m. f. a line of heads, number of<BR>heads.<BR>—शिरः-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being on the head.<BR>—शिरः-स्नात, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has bathed his<BR>head.<BR>—शिरश्-छेद, अस्, m. or शिरश्-छेदन, अम्,<BR>n. cutting off the head, decapitation.<BR>—शिरसि-ज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘head-produced,’ the hair of the head.<BR>—शिरसिज-<BR>पाश, अस्, m. a tuft or quantity of hair.<BR>—शिरसि-रुह्,<BR>ट्, or शिरसि-रुह, अस्, m. ‘head-growing,’ the hair of<BR>the head.<BR>—शिरस्-तस्, ind. from the head.<BR>—शिरस्-<BR>तापिन्, ई, m. an elephant.<BR>—शिरस्-त्र or शिरस्-<BR>त्राण, अम्, n. ‘head-protector,’ a helmet; a cap,<BR>turban, head-dress.<BR>—शिरस्-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>on the head, being on the summit, at the top, &c.;<BR>(अस्), m. a chief, leader.<BR>—शिरो-गृह, अम्, n. top<BR>room, a room on the top of the house, upper cham-<BR>ber, a turret.<BR>—शिरो-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘head-seizure,’<BR>disease or affection of the head.<BR>—शिरो-ग्रीव, अम्,<BR>n. the head and neck.<BR>—शिरो-धरा, f. or शिरो-धि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘head-supporting,’ the neck.<BR>—शिरो-भू-<BR>षण, अम्, n. an ornament for the head.<BR>—शिरो-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. ‘crest-jewel,’ a gem worn in a head-<BR>ornament or any jewel worn on the head; a title of<BR>respect conferred on Pandits; N. of the author of<BR>the Dīdhiti commentary (so called after its author<BR>Raghunātha-śiromaṇi-bhaṭṭācārya).<BR>—शिरो-मर्-<BR>मन्, आ, m. a hog.<BR>—शिरो-मालिन्, ई, m. ‘garlanded<BR>with skulls,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शिरो-रत्न, अम्, n.<BR>‘crest-gem,’ a jewel worn on the head.<BR>—शिरो-रुजा,<BR>f. ‘head-pain,’ any pain or ache in the head; a kind<BR>of tree (= सप्त-पर्ण, the leaves of which are<BR>used as a remedy for head-ache).<BR>—शिरो-रुह्, ट्, or<BR>शिरो-रुह, अस्, m. ‘head-growing,’ the hair of the<BR>head, hair.<BR>—शिरो-रोग, अस्, m. ‘head-sickness,’ any<BR>pain or disease of the head.<BR>—शिरो-ऽर्ति (˚रस्-अर्˚),<BR>इस्, f. ‘head-pain,’ pain in the head, head-ache, &c.<BR>—शिरो-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being at the head, being<BR>on the top or summit; (ई), m. a chief, any one at<BR>the head of affairs, the general of an army.<BR>—शिरो-<BR>वल्ली, f. the crest or comb of a peacock, (said to be<BR>also read शिरो-वन्दि.)<BR>—शिरो-वृत्त, अम्, n. pepper.<BR>—शिरोवृत्त-फल, अस्, m. a kind of Achyranthes<BR>Aspera (= रक्तापामार्ग).<BR>—शिरो-वेष्ट, अस्, m.<BR>or शिरो-वेष्टन, अम्, n. ‘head-cincture,’ ‘head-<BR>covering,’ a head-dress, turban, cap.<BR>—शिरो-ऽस्थि<BR>(˚रस्-अस्˚), इ, n. ‘head-bone,’ the skull.<BR>—शिरो-<BR>हारिन्, ई, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिर|शिरं|शिरः
शिर, अस्, m. the head, (according to some अम्, n.);<BR>the root of the pepper plant, (according to some<BR>अम्, n.); a bed, couch (= शय्या); a large serpent.<BR>—शिर-ज, अस्, m. ‘head-produced,’ the hair of the<BR>head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्क|शिरस्कं
शिरस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the head, being<BR>on the head; (अम्), n. a helmet; a cap, turban,<BR>&c.; (आ), f. a palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्य|शिरस्यः
शिरस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the head, being<BR>on the head; (अस्), m. clean or unentangled hair<BR>(= शीर्षण्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरा
शिरा शिरा, f. (probably another form of<BR>शिला, col. 3), any tubular vessel of the body, a nerve,<BR>tendon, fibre, gut, vein, blood-vessel, artery (=<BR>धमनि).<BR>—शिरा-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the elephant or<BR>wood-apple, Feronia Elephantum (= कपित्थ); a<BR>kind of tree (= हिन्ताल).<BR>—शिरा-वृत्त, अम्, n.<BR>lead (= सीसक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिराल|शिरालं
शिराल, अस्, आ, अम्, veiny, tendinous, sinewy,<BR>skinny, full of tendons or veins; (अम्), n. the acid<BR>fruit of the Averrhoa Carambola (= कर्म-रङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरालक|शिरालकः
शिरालक, अस्, m. the plant Vitis Quadrangularis<BR>(= अस्थि-भङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरि|शिरिः
शिरि शिरि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 142. fr. rt. शॄ), a murderer, killer; a sword; an<BR>arrow; a locust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरिणा
शिरिणा, f., Ved. night, (Sāy. शीर्यते ऽस्याम् भु-<BR>तानीति शिरिणा रात्रिः, Ṛg-veda II. 10, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरीष|शिरीषः
शिरीष, अस्, m. a kind of tree, Acacia Sirisa;<BR>(अम्), n. the flower of this tree.<BR>—शिरीष-पत्-<BR>त्रिका, f. a white kind of the plant Kiṇihī, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरिम्बिठ
शिरिम्बिठ शिरिम्बिठ, अस्, m., N. of a Vedic<BR>Ṛṣi (having the patronymic Bhāradvāja and author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 155).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्
शिल् शिल् (also written सिल्), cl. 6. P.<BR>शिलति, &c., to glean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल|शिलं|शिलः
शिल, अस्, अम्, m. n. gleaning, gathering stalks or<BR>ears of corn, (according to Kullūka on Manu X.<BR>112. शिल = अनेक-धान्योन्नयन, i. e. gleaning<BR>more than one ear of corn at a time, opposed to<BR>उञ्छ = एकैक-धान्यादि-गुडकोच्चयन.)<BR>—शि-<BR>लोञ्छ (˚ल-उञ्˚), अस्, m. gleaning ears of corn;<BR>following irregular occupation.<BR>—शिलोञ्छ-वृत्ति,<BR>इस्, f. subsistence by gleaning; unusual or irregular<BR>occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिला
शिला शिला, f. (probably connected with<BR>rt. 1. शि or rt. शो), a stone, rock; a grindstone or<BR>any flat stone on which substances are ground; the<BR>lower timber of a door; a beam or stone placed<BR>across the top of a pillar, the top or capital of a<BR>column; a vein, tendon, (for शिरा, q. v.); red<BR>arsenic; camphor; [cf. Lat. silex; Hib. clach,<BR>cloch.]<BR>—शिल-गर्भ-ज, अस्, m. (शिल for शिला), a<BR>particular plant (= पाषाण-भेदन).<BR>—शिला-<BR>कर्णी, f. the olibanum tree, Boswellia Thurifera.<BR>—शिला-कुट्टक, अस्, m. a stone-cutter's chisel or<BR>hatchet.<BR>—शिला-कुसुम, अम्, n. benzoin or storax,<BR>(see शिला-ज.)<BR>—शिला-घन, अस्, आ, अम्, firm or<BR>hard as a stone or rock.<BR>—शिला-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘rock-<BR>born,’ produced in a mountain or rock, fossil, mineral;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of resin or bitumen; benzoin, storax<BR>or styrax; petroleum; any fossil production; iron.<BR>—शिला-जतु, उ, n. ‘stone-lac,’ bitumen; red chalk.<BR>—शिला-जित्, त्, f. ‘rock-conquering,’ bitumen.<BR>—शि-<BR>लाञ्जनी (˚ला-अञ्˚), f. a particular plant or shrub (=<BR>कालाञ्जनी).<BR>—शिलाटक (˚ला-अट्˚), अस्, m. a room<BR>on the top of a house (= अट्ट); a hole; a fence,<BR>enclosure.<BR>—शिला-तल, अम्, n. the surface of a rock<BR>or stone.<BR>—शिलात्मज (˚ला-आत्˚), अम्, n. ‘rock-<BR>born,’ iron.<BR>—शिलात्मिका (˚ला-आत्˚), f. a crucible.<BR>—शिला-त्वच्, क्, f. = शिला-वल्का.<BR>—शिला-दद्रु, उस्,<BR>m. ‘rock-eruption,’ bitumen.<BR>—शिला-धातु, उस्, m.<BR>‘rock-mineral,’ chalk; red chalk; a white fossil<BR>substance; an aluminous earth of a white or yellowish<BR>colour (considered to be a sort of chalk).<BR>—शिला-<BR>पट्ट, अस्, m. a flat stone for grinding condiments<BR>&c.; a slab used as a seat, a rocky seat.<BR>—शिला-<BR>पट्टक, अस्, m. a rocky seat.<BR>—शिला-पुत्र or शिला-<BR>पुत्रक, अस्, m. (पुत्र being used as a diminutive),<BR>a roller for grinding condiments &c., a small flat<BR>stone for pounding or grinding.<BR>—शिला-पुष्प, अम्,<BR>n. ‘rock-flower,’ storax or benzoin.<BR>—शिला-पेष,<BR>अस्, m. grinding with a stone.<BR>—शिला-प्रतिकृति, इस्,<BR>f. an image or statue of stone.<BR>—शिला-फलक, अम्,<BR>n. a layer or table of rock, a stone slab.<BR>—शिला-<BR>भव, अम्, n. ‘rock-produced,’ storax or benzoin.<BR>—शिला-भेद, अस्, m. the plant Plectranthus Scu-<BR>tellarioides (= पाषाण-भेद); a stone-cutter's<BR>chisel.<BR>—शिला-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of stone,<BR>rocky, stony.<BR>—शिलारम्भा (˚ला-आर्˚), f. the wild<BR>plantain (= काष्ठ-कदली).<BR>—शिला-रस, अस्, m.<BR>‘rock-exudation,’ olibanum, benzoin, incense.<BR>—शिला-<BR>वल्कल, अस्, अम्, m. n. or शिला-वल्का, f. ‘rock-<BR>bark,’ a kind of moss or lichen (especially a kind<BR>used as a medicinal substance and said to be of cool-<BR>ing and lithonthriptic properties; it is commonly<BR>called Śilābāk).<BR>—शिला-वितान, अस्, अम्, m. n. a<BR>covering or expanse of stones, i. e. a shower of<BR>stones.<BR>—शिला-वृष्टि, इस्, f. ‘stone-rain,’ hail.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">Page1007-a+ 76</a>]<BR>—शिला-वेश्मन्, अ, n. ‘rock-abode,’ a cavern, grotto,<BR>rocky recess.<BR>—शिला-व्याधि, इस्, m. ‘rock-disease,’<BR>bitumen.<BR>—शिला-शित, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpened on a<BR>grindstone.<BR>—शिलासन (˚ला-अस्˚ or -आस्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>stone bench or seat; benzoin or storax.<BR>—शिला-सार,<BR>अम्, n. ‘rock-essence,’ iron.<BR>—शिलाह्व (˚ला-आह्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ‘stone-named,’ bitumen, red chalk.<BR>—शिली-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, converted into a rock, made hard.<BR>—शिलोच्चय (˚ला-उच्˚), अस्, m. ‘rock-accumulation,’<BR>a mountain; a high mountain.<BR>—शिलोत्थ (˚ला-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, growing upon rocks, produced from rocks<BR>or stone; (अम्), n. benzoin, storax.<BR>—शिलोद्भव<BR>(˚ला-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced from stone or on rock;<BR>(अम्), n. a superior sort of sandal-wood (either the<BR>white or yellowish sort); benzoin.<BR>—शिलोरस्क<BR>(˚ला-उर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, rock-chested, having a chest as<BR>hard as a rock (said of the Himālaya mountain).<BR>—शिलौकस् (˚ला-ओक्˚), आस्, m. ‘dwelling in rocks,’<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1006-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलि|शिलिः
शिलि, इस्, f. the lower timber of a door; (इस्), m.<BR>the birch tree (= भूर्ज-पत्त्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिली
शिली, f. the lower timber of a door; the stone or<BR>beam at the top of a pillar; a small earth-worm; a<BR>spike, dart; an arrow.<BR>—शिली-मुख, अस्, m. an<BR>arrow; a bee; a fool, blockhead; war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलेय|शिलेयं
शिलेय, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from rock; like a<BR>stone or rock, as hard as a rock, rocky, stony; (अम्),<BR>n. benzoin; bitumen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाद
शिलाद शिलाद, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलालिन्
शिलालिन् शिलालिन्, ई, or शिलालि, इस्, m., N. of<BR>the supposed author of certain Naṭa-sūtras or rules<BR>for actors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलिन्द|शिलिंद|शिलिंदः|शिलिन्दः
शिलिन्द शिलिन्द, अस्, m. a kind of fish;<BR>[cf. शिलीन्ध्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीन्ध्र|शिलींध्र|शिलीन्ध्रं|शिलींध्रः|शिलीन्ध्रः
शिलीन्ध्र शिलीन्ध्र, अम्, n. a mushroom,<BR>fungus; the flower of the plantain tree; hail, = त्रि-<BR>पुट; (अस्), m. a sort of tree; a kind of fish, =<BR>चित्र-फलक; (ई), f. earth, clay; a small earth-<BR>worm; a sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीन्ध्रक|शिलींध्रक|शिलीन्ध्रकं
शिलीन्ध्रक, अम्, n. a mushroom (especially one<BR>growing out of cow-dung); a fungus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीपद|शिलीपदः
शिलीपद शिलीपद, अस्, m. (= श्लीपद, q. v.),<BR>enlarged or swelled leg, elephantiasis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलूष
शिलूष शिलूष, अस्, m. a proper N., (said<BR>to have been an early teacher of the art of acting;<BR>cf. शैलूष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोञ्छ|शिलोञ्छः
शिलोञ्छ शिलोञ्छ. See under शिल, p. 1006.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्गु
शिल्गु शिल्गु, उस्, m. = सुख (Naigh. III. 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्प|शिल्पं
शिल्प शिल्प, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 28. fr. rt. शील्), an art, any manual or mechanical<BR>or fine art, (sixty-four such arts, sometimes called<BR>वाह्य-कला, ‘external or practical arts,’ are enume-<BR>rated, e. g. carpentering, architecture, jewellery, far-<BR>riery, acting, dancing, music, medicine, poetry, &c.;<BR>and sixty-four अभ्यन्तर-कला, ‘secret arts,’ e. g.<BR>kissing, embracing, and various other arts of coquetry);<BR>skill in any art, ingenuity, contrivance, skill (in<BR>general); any act, work (enumerated among the<BR>कर्म-नामानि in Naigh. II. 1); ceremonial act,<BR>rite, ceremony, (in this sense apparently also अस्,<BR>m.); form, shape (enumerated among the रूप-<BR>नामानि in Naigh. III. 7, cf. सु-शिल्प); a particular<BR>kind of Śastra or hymn (of a highly artificial cha-<BR>racter); creation, procreation; a sort of spoon or<BR>ladle used at sacrifices for throwing the clarified butter<BR>into the fire; (अस्), m., N. of a teacher; (ई), f. a<BR>female artisan or mechanic (regarded by Śāktas as<BR>one of the eight Akulas).<BR>—शिल्प-कर = शिल्प-<BR>कार.<BR>—शिल्प-कर्मन्, अ, n. or शिल्प-क्रिया, f.<BR>manual labour, handicraft.<BR>—शिल्प-कार, अस्, or<BR>शिल्प-कारिन्, ई, m. an artisan, workman, mechanic.<BR>—शिल्प-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, practising any me-<BR>chanical art, versed in an art; (अस्), m. an artisan.<BR>—शिल्प-विद्या, f. the science of mechanics, me-<BR>chanical knowledge, skill in art, mechanical or<BR>manual skill.<BR>—शिल्प-शाल, अम्, आ, n. f. a work-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-b" target="_blank">Page1007-b+ 80</a>]<BR>shop, workroom, manufactory.<BR>—शिल्प-शास्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a book on any mechanical or fine art (as archi-<BR>tecture &c.), a scientific treatise; the whole collection<BR>of treatises on mechanical arts, mechanics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पक|शिल्पकं
शिल्पक, अम्, n. a sort of drama, one exhibiting<BR>magical and mystical rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिक
शिल्पिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, manual, mechanical;<BR>(अम्), n. any handicraft or mechanical art; a sort of<BR>drama, = शिल्पक; (आ), f. = शिल्पिनी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिन्
शिल्पिन्, ई, इनी, इ, belonging or relating to any<BR>mechanical art, mechanical; (ई), m. an artificer,<BR>artist, artisan; (इनी), f. a kind of herb or grass<BR>(called Lahānasipī in Hindī; it is used medicinally,<BR>and described as sweet, cooling, and bearing seeds of<BR>tonic and restorative properties; it is otherwise de-<BR>scribed as a drug, = कोल-दल).<BR>—शिल्पि-शाल, अम्,<BR>आ, n. f. a workshop, a manufactory.<BR>—शिल्पि-शास्त्र<BR>= शिल्प-शास्त्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्हन
शिल्हन शिल्हन. See शिह्लन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिव|शिवं|शिवः
शिव शिव, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 153. fr. rt. 1. शी; more probably to be connected<BR>with rt. श्वि and शवस्, see शिश्वि), auspicious, pro-<BR>pitious, prosperous, happy, fortunate, lucky, increas-<BR>ing, thriving, right; (अस्), m., N. of the third god<BR>of the Hindū Tri-mūrti, (in the later mythology<BR>regarded as ‘the destroyer,’ and with Brahmā, ‘the<BR>creator,’ and Viṣṇu, ‘the preserver,’ constituting<BR>the well known Hindū triad of divine manifestations;<BR>although the name Śiva is not found applied to any<BR>god in the Veda, the worship of the destroying and<BR>reproducing principle under this name was rapidly<BR>developed in the Purāṇas and epic poems, and be-<BR>came very general in later times, the worshippers of<BR>Śiva or Śaivas assigning to him the first place in the<BR>triad and by identifying him with the principles of<BR>creation and reproduction as well as that of destruc-<BR>tion, constituting him the one Supreme Being who<BR>is supposed to comprehend all the powers and forces<BR>of nature and whose formidable character makes him<BR>the first object of propitiation and adoration; in the<BR>Śiva-Purāṇa he is addressed as Brahmā, Viṣṇu,<BR>Indra, Varuṇa, the Sun, Moon, Earth, Fire, Water,<BR>Air, Ether, &c., while even in the Viṣṇu and other<BR>Purāṇas not specially devoted to his praise, he is<BR>mentioned with the greatest reverence and awe;<BR>according to one view the name Śiva belonged<BR>originally to the principal god of the aboriginal<BR>tribes of India, and being subsequently adopted<BR>together with the Liṅga or symbol of reproduction<BR>into the Pantheon of the Āryans, was then identified<BR>with their own deity Rudra, who occupies a con-<BR>spicuous position in the Veda as god of storms; but<BR>according to a more likely supposition the adjective<BR>शिव, ‘auspicious,’ being at first only used as an<BR>euphemistic epithet to propitiate the lord of tempests,<BR>passed afterwards into his name, and was ultimately<BR>adopted as the principal name of the god of destruc-<BR>tion, [see रुद्र]; according to Viṣṇu-Purāṇa I. 8.<BR>there are eight principal manifestations of Śiva, viz.<BR>Rudra, Bhava, Śarva, Iśāna, Paśu-pati, Bhīma, Ugra,<BR>Mahā-deva, which again are visibly represented under<BR>eight Tanus or material forms, viz. the Sun, Water,<BR>Earth, Air, Fire, Ether, the officiating Brahman,<BR>and the Moon, Śiva being supposed to uphold the<BR>universe by means of these forms; as presiding over<BR>reproduction, which follows destruction, his symbol<BR>is the Liṅga or Phallus, under which form he is<BR>generally worshipped at the present day; as god of<BR>justice or punishment, which character he shares with<BR>the gods Yama and Varuṇa, he is represented as<BR>riding on a white bull, the god Dharma, it is said,<BR>having taken this form and requested Śiva to accept<BR>him as his vehicle; his own colour is sometimes<BR>depicted as black in his character of destroyer of the<BR>world, when he is called Kāla or Time; again, one<BR>of his representations is as Ardha-nārī, ‘half-female,’<BR>the other half being male to symbolize the unity of<BR>the generative principle, his name being then Ardha-<BR>nārīśa, ‘the half-female lord;’ he has sometimes five<BR>faces, whence his name Pāñcānana; he has also three<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-c" target="_blank">Page1007-c+ 81</a>]<BR>eyes, one of which is in his forehead, and which are<BR>thought to denote his view of the three divisions of<BR>time, past, present, and future, while a moon's<BR>crescent, round or above the central eye, marks the<BR>measure of time by months, a serpent round his<BR>neck the measure of time by years, and a second<BR>necklace of skulls with numerous other serpents about<BR>his person, the perpetual revolution of ages, and the<BR>successive extinction and generation of the races of<BR>mankind: his hair is thickly matted together, and<BR>gathered above his forehead into a coil, so as to<BR>project like a horn; on the top of it he bears the<BR>Ganges, the rush of which river in its descent form<BR>heaven he intercepted by his head that the earth<BR>might not be crushed by the weight of the falling<BR>stream; his throat is dark-blue from the stain of the<BR>deadly poison which would have destroyed the world<BR>had it not been swallowed by him on its production<BR>at the churning of the ocean by the gods for the<BR>nectar of immortality: he is sometimes represented<BR>clothed in a deer-skin, sometimes in a tiger-skin, or<BR>he appears sitting on a tiger-skin or holding a deer<BR>in one of his hands; in explanation of this a legend<BR>is told that Śiva, having once visited a forest in the<BR>form of a religious mendicant, the wives of the<BR>Ṛṣis residing there fell in love with his great<BR>beauty, which the Ṛṣis perceiving resented; in<BR>order, therefore, to overpower him, they first dug a<BR>pit, and by magical arts caused a tiger to rush out of<BR>it, which he slew, and taking its skin wore it as a<BR>garment; they next caused a deer to spring out upon<BR>him, which he took up in his left hand and ever<BR>afterwards retained there; they then produced a red-<BR>hot iron, but this too he took up and kept in his<BR>hand as a weapon: sometimes, again, he appears<BR>wearing an elephant's skin which belonged to an<BR>Asura named Gaya, who acquired such power that<BR>he conquered the gods and would have destroyed the<BR>Munis had they not fled to Benares and taken<BR>refuge in a temple of Śiva, who then destroyed the<BR>Asura and, ripping up his body, stripped off the hide<BR>which he afterwards cast over his shoulders for a<BR>cloak: Śiva holds a त्रिशूल or three-pronged trident<BR>[also called Pināka] in his hand to denote, as some<BR>think, his combination of the three attributes of<BR>Creator, Destroyer, and Regenerator; his other<BR>weapons are a bow called Ajakava or Ajagava, a<BR>thunderbolt, an axe, a kind of staff with transverse<BR>pieces surmounted by a skull called Khaṭvāṅga, and<BR>another nondescript weapon called Khiṅkira; he also<BR>carries a kind of rattle or drum, shaped like an hour-<BR>glass, called Ḍamaru, and a Pāśa or noose for binding<BR>incorrigible offenders: his attendants or servants are<BR>called Pramatha; they are sometimes regarded as<BR>demons or supernatural beings of various kinds, and<BR>form a complete host; some of his more personal<BR>attendants or chamberlains have special names, such<BR>as Nandi or Nandin, Bhṛṅgin, Taṇḍu, the latter<BR>being the original teacher of dancing &c., whence<BR>Śiva is called Naṭeśvara, ‘the lord of dancers,’ and is<BR>himself described as नाट्य-प्रिय, fond of dancing:<BR>his principal wife Durgā, otherwise called Pārvatī,<BR>Umā, Gaurī, Bhavānī, Satī, &c., is the chief object<BR>of worship with the Śāktas and Tāntrikas, see शक्ति,<BR>शाक्त, तन्त्र: his sons are Gaṇeśa and Kārttikeya:<BR>he destroyed several Asuras or demons, such as Pura,<BR>Tripura, Andhaka, Ruru; he also scorched the god<BR>of love, Kāma-deva, to ashes by a glance from his<BR>central eye, that deity having attempted to inflame<BR>him with passion for Pārvatī whilst he was engaged<BR>in severe penance; he is said to have cut off one of<BR>the heads of the god Brahmā, that god having ori-<BR>ginally possessed five heads, one of which is fabled<BR>to have addressed Śiva on a particular occasion in a<BR>disrespectful manner, cf. ब्रह्म-मूर्ध-भृत्;<BR>he also decapitated Dakṣa and replaced his head by<BR>that of a ram, because that sage, who was his father-<BR>in-law, omitted to invite him and his wife Satī to a<BR>great sacrifice at which all the other gods were<BR>present, see दक्षाध्वर-ध्वंश-कृत्; in the<BR>exercise of his function of Universal Destroyer he<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1008-a" target="_blank">Page1008-a+ 81</a>]<BR>destroys, at the end of every Kalpa, not only all<BR>created beings, but even Brahmā, Viṣṇu, and the<BR>other gods, whose bones and skulls he wears as gar-<BR>lands; moreover, at the end of one of the early<BR>Kalpas he is fabled to have burnt them up by a flash<BR>from his central eye, and afterwards to have rubbed<BR>their ashes upon his body, whence the use of ashes<BR>is considered of great importance in his worship,<BR>while the use of the Rudrākṣa berries or beads<BR>originated, it is said, from the legend that Śiva, on<BR>his way to destroy the three cities, called Tri-pura,<BR>let fall some tears of rage which became converted<BR>into these beads: his residence is Kailāsa, one of the<BR>loftiest northern peaks of the Himālaya, which is<BR>also the paradise of Kuvera: he has strictly no in-<BR>carnations like those of Viṣṇu, though Vīra-bhadra<BR>and the eight Bhairavas are sometimes regarded as<BR>forms of him, sometimes as his sons, see वीर-भ-<BR>द्र, भैरव; he is especially worshipped at Be-<BR>nares and has even more names than Viṣṇu, one<BR>thousand and eight being specified in the sixty-ninth<BR>chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa and in the seventeenth<BR>chapter of the Anuśāsana-parvan of the Mahā-bhā-<BR>rata, some of the most common being Mahā-deva,<BR>Śambhu, Śaṅkara, Īśa, Īśvara, Maheśvara, Hara,<BR>Rudra); the phallic emblem of Śiva, the male<BR>genital organ, penis; a god (= देव, according to<BR>Śabda-k.); an auspicious planetary conjunction; the<BR>twentieth of the astronomical periods called Yogas,<BR>(see योग); epithet of a particular month; the<BR>Veda; final emancipation (= मोक्ष); a pillar or<BR>post to which cattle are tied; a kind of drug and<BR>perfume (= बालुक or वालुक); a particular plant<BR>or drug (= पुण्डरीक); the black Dhustūra or<BR>thorn-apple; bdellium; quicksilver; N. of a scribe;<BR>(औ), m. du. Śiva and his wife; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a class of deities; (आ), f. the wife of Śiva (Durgā,<BR>Pārvatī, &c.); final emancipation (= मुक्ति); N.<BR>of the wife of Aṅgiras; of the mother of the twenty-<BR>second Jina; of a river; a jackal; the Śamī tree;<BR>yellow Myrobalan (= हरीतकी); Emblic Myrobalan<BR>(= आमलकी); the tree Flacourtia Cataphracta (=<BR>तामलकी); Dūrvā grass; turmeric; a kind of yellow<BR>pigment, = गो-रोचना; (अम्), n. bliss, prosperity,<BR>happiness, well-being, auspiciousness, pleasure; final<BR>emancipation or beatitude; water; rock-salt; sea-salt;<BR>white or refined borax.<BR>—शिव-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing<BR>happiness or prosperity, making happy, auspicious,<BR>propitious; (अस्), m. (with Jainas) one of the twenty-<BR>four Arhats of the past Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR>—शिव-क-<BR>वच, अम्, n. ‘Śiva's amulet,’ N. of a chapter in<BR>the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—शिव-काञ्ची, f., N. of a city<BR>(said to have been founded by Śaṅkara; cf. विष्णु-<BR>काञ्ची).<BR>—शिव-कान्ती-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—शिव-कामदुघा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—शिव-कारिणी, f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—शिव-किङ्-<BR>कर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—शिव-कीर्तन, अस्, m.<BR>‘Śiva-praiser,’ epithet of Bhṛṅgi or Bhṛṅgarīṭa,<BR>one of Śiva's attendants; N. of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of praising or celebrating Śiva.<BR>—शिव-कुण्ड, N. of a place.<BR>—शिव-कोष, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a dictionary of synonyms of trees and<BR>medicinal plants by Śiva-datta.<BR>—शिव-गङ्गा-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—शिव-गण, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—शिवगण-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—शिव-<BR>गति, इस्, इस्, इ, having a prosperous course, pros-<BR>perous, auspicious, happy; worshipping Śiva; (इस्),<BR>m. one of the twenty-four Arhats of the past Ut-sar-<BR>piṇī (with Jainas).<BR>—शिव-गीता, f. ‘Śiva's song,’ N.<BR>of a part of the Padma-Purāṇa (propounding the<BR>doctrines of the Śaivas; it is regarded as a Vedānta<BR>treatise, and attributed to Veda-vyāsa).<BR>—शिव-गुरु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of Śaṅkarācārya's father.<BR>—शिव-घर्म-<BR>ज, अस्, m. ‘born from the perspiration of Śiva,’<BR>epithet of the planet Mars.<BR>—शिवङ्-कर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, causing happiness or prosperity, auspicious, pro-<BR>pitious.<BR>—शिव-चक्र, अम्, n. epithet of a particular<BR>mystical circle.<BR>—शिव-चतुर्दशी, f. the fourteenth<BR>day of the dark half of the month Māgha kept as a<BR>festival in honour of Śiva.<BR>—शिवचतुर्दशी-व्रत,<BR>अम्, n. a particular religious observance kept on the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1008-b" target="_blank">Page1008-b+ 81</a>]<BR>above-mentioned day.<BR>—शिव-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing what is fortunate or propitious, worshipping<BR>Śiva; (आ), f. a female devotee of the Śaiva sect.<BR>—शिव-ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of what is fortu-<BR>nate or propitious; a book giving rules for ascertain-<BR>ing auspicious moments or lucky and unlucky seasons.<BR>—शिव-तत्त्व-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a work by<BR>Apyaya-dīkṣita.<BR>—शिव-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra work.<BR>—शिव-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most pros-<BR>perous, very fortunate.<BR>—शिव-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more<BR>auspicious or propitious, very prosperous or fortunate;<BR>very complacent.<BR>—शिव-ताति, इस्, इस्, इ (Pāṇini IV.<BR>4, 143, 144), causing good fortune, conferring hap-<BR>piness, propitious; (इस्), f. propitiousness, benevo-<BR>lence, auspiciousness.<BR>—शिव-तातिक, अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>शिव-ताति above.<BR>—शिव-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—शिव-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, given by Śiva; pre-<BR>sented to Śiva; (अस्), m., N. of the author of the Śiva-<BR>koṣa; of a scribe; (अम्), n. the discus of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शिव-दारु, उ, n. the tree Pinus Deodaru (=<BR>देव-दारु).<BR>—शिव-दास, अस्, m. ‘Śiva's servant,’<BR>N. of the author of the Jātaka-muktāvalī; of the<BR>reputed author of the Kathārṇava.<BR>—शिव-दास-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—शिव-दूतिका, f., N.<BR>of one of the Mātṛs attending on Śiva.<BR>—शिव-<BR>दूती, f. ‘Śiva's messenger,’ epithet of Durgā; of a<BR>Yogiṇī.<BR>—शिव-दूती-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra<BR>work.<BR>—शिव-दृष्टि, इस्, f., N. of a work by So-<BR>mānanda-nātha.<BR>—शिव-द्रुम, अस्, m. ‘Śiva's tree,’<BR>the Vilva, (commonly called Bel.)<BR>—शिव-द्विष्टा,<BR>f. ‘hated by Śiva,’ the Ketaka tree, (see केतक.)<BR>—शिव-धनुर्-वेद, अस्, m., N. of a work ascribed<BR>to Vyāsa.<BR>—सिव-धरम and शिव-धर्मोत्तर<BR>(˚म-उत्˚), N. of two works.<BR>—शिव-धर्मोप-<BR>पुराण (˚म-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>—शिव-धातु, उस्, m. ‘Śiva's essence,’ quicksilver;<BR>‘Śiva's mineral,’ milk-stone, opal or chalcedony,<BR>(according to Śabda-k. = गो-दन्त.)<BR>—शिव-नाभि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘Śiva's navel,’ a particular form of Śiva-<BR>liṅga, (see लिङ्ग.)<BR>—शिव-नारायण, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a god; of a modern author.<BR>—शिव-पुर,<BR>अम्, n. or शिव-पुरी, ‘Śiva's city,’ N. of the<BR>city Benares (especially sacred to Śiva).<BR>—शिव-पु-<BR>राण, अम्, n., N. of one of the eighteen Purāṇas<BR>(devoted to the praise of Śiva; it is thought by some<BR>to be identical with the Vāyu-Purāṇa).<BR>—शिव-पूजा,<BR>f. worship or adoration of Śiva.<BR>—शिव-प्रादुर्-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the manifestation of Śiva.<BR>—शिव-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, dear to or esteemed by Śiva;<BR>(अस्), m. the tree Sesbana Grandiflora (= वक);<BR>the thorn-apple (= धुस्तूर); crystal; (आ), f. the<BR>goddess Durgā; (अम्), n. the seeds of the Rudrākṣa<BR>or Elæocarpus.<BR>—शिव-भक्त, अस्, m. a worshipper<BR>of Śiva, a Śaiva.<BR>—शिव-भक्ति-सिद्धि, इस्, f. ‘per-<BR>formance of the worship of Śiva,’ N. of a devotional<BR>work; [cf. शिव-शक्ति-सिद्धि.]<BR>—शिव-भट्ट, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—शिव-मल्लक, अस्, m. the Arjuna<BR>tree; (इका), f. the tree Sesbana Grandiflora (= व-<BR>सुक).<BR>—शिव-मल्ली, f. the Sesbana Grandiflora.<BR>—शिव-माहात्म्य-खण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a book<BR>of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—शिव-रस, अस्, m. the<BR>water of boiled rice or pulse three days old (under-<BR>going spontaneous fermentation).<BR>—शिव-रहस्य,<BR>अम्, n. ‘secret doctrine of Śiva,’ N. of a part of the<BR>Skanda-Purāṇa; of a compilation from the Tantras<BR>on the divinity and worship of Śiva.<BR>—शिव-राज-<BR>धानी, f. ‘Śiva's capital,’ N. of the city Kāśī or<BR>Benares (especially sacred to Śiva).<BR>—शिव-रात्रि, इस्,<BR>f. ‘Śiva's night,’ N. of a celebrated and very popular<BR>festival in honour of Śiva (kept on the fourteenth<BR>of the dark half of the month Māgha or January-<BR>February; a rigorous fast and extraordinary cere-<BR>monies are observed during the day and night,<BR>and Śiva is worshipped under the type of the<BR>Liṅga; cf. शिव-चतुर्दशी).<BR>—शिवरात्रि-माहात्-<BR>म्य, अम्, n. the greatness or glory of the Śiva-rātri<BR>festival.<BR>—शिव-राम, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor;<BR>of the author of the Kṛtya-cintāmaṇi, the Śrāddha-<BR>cintāmaṇi, the Su-bodhinī, and a commentary on<BR>the Karma-pradīpa.<BR>—शिव-राम-गिर, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—शिव-रूप, अम्, n. the form or image<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1008-c" target="_blank">Page1008-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of Śiva; (अस्, आ, अम्), having the form of Śiva.<BR>—शिव-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. Śiva's genital organ or Śiva<BR>worshipped in the form of a phallus; a temple or<BR>spot dedicated to the worship of the Liṅga, (see<BR>लिङ्ग.)<BR>—शिव-लिङ्गिन्, ई, m. a worshipper of the<BR>Liṅga or one who carries this symbol on his person.<BR>—शिव-लोक, अस्, m. the world or paradise of Śiva,<BR>Kailāsa.<BR>—शिव-वल्लभ, अस्, आ, अम्, loved or<BR>esteemed by Śiva; (अस्), m. the mango tree;<BR>gigantic swallow-wort; (आ), f. the goddess Pārvatī;<BR>the Indian white rose (= शत-पत्त्री).<BR>—शिव-वल्-<BR>लिका, f. a particular plant (= लिङ्गिनी).<BR>—शिव-वल्ली,<BR>f. a particular plant (= लिङ्गिनी); a particular thorny<BR>tree (= श्री-वल्ली).<BR>—शिव-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘Śiva's<BR>vehicle,’ a bull.<BR>—शिव-वीज, अम्, n. ‘Śiva's semen,’<BR>quicksilver.<BR>—शिव-शक्ति, इस्, f. attachment or de-<BR>votion to Śiva; (इस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—शिव-शक्ति-<BR>सिद्धि, इस्, f., N. of a work by Harṣa, (also called<BR>शिव-भक्ति-सिद्धि.)<BR>—शिव-शर्मन्, आ, m., N.<BR>of a priest.<BR>—शिव-शासन, अम्, n. ‘Śiva's ordi-<BR>nance,’ N. of a law-book.<BR>—शिव-शेखर, अस्, m.<BR>Śiva's crest; Śiva's head; the plant Sesbana Grandi-<BR>flora; the thorn-apple; the moon.<BR>—शिव-संहिता,<BR>f., N. of a short treatise on the duties of a Yogin.<BR>—शिव-सङ्कल्प, अस्, m. ‘having an auspicious<BR>resolve,’ N. of a hymn (forming part of the thirty-<BR>fourth book of the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā; cf. Manu<BR>XI. 250).<BR>—शिव-सङ्कल्पोपनिषद् (˚प-उप्˚),<BR>त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—शिव-सर्वस्व, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—शिव-सहस्र-नामन्, अ, n., N. of<BR>a description of one thousand epithets illustrating the<BR>attributes of Śiva.<BR>—शिव-सायुज्य, अम्, n. absorp-<BR>tion into or identification with Śiva, final emanci-<BR>pation.<BR>—शिव-सुन्दरी, f. epithet of Durgā.<BR>—शिव-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of the aphorisms of the Śaiva<BR>philosophy (attributed to the god Śiva); N. of the<BR>fourteen Sūtras with which Pāṇini opens his gram-<BR>mar (said to have been communicated to him by<BR>Śiva).<BR>—शिवसूत्र-विमर्शिनी, f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on the philosophical Śiva-sūtras, (also called<BR>शिव-सूत्र-विवृति); of a commentary on the four-<BR>teen grammatical aphorisms of Śiva (treated as sym-<BR>bolizing the dogmas of the Vedānta).<BR>—शिव-स्कन्-<BR>ध, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—शिव-स्व, अम्, n.<BR>‘Śiva's property,’ anything that has been offered to<BR>Śiva.<BR>—शिव-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a poet; of an<BR>author.<BR>—शिवाक्ष (˚व-अक्˚), अम्, n. the seed of<BR>the Elæocarpus, (see रुद्राक्ष.)<BR>—शिवाख्य (˚व-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, called happy, termed lucky.<BR>—शि-<BR>वाटिका (˚व-अट्˚?), f. a kind of grass (= वंश-पत्-<BR>त्री).<BR>—शिवात्मक (˚व-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, consist-<BR>ing of the essence of Śiva; (अम्), n. rock-salt.<BR>—शिवादेशक (˚व-आद्˚), अस्, m. a fortune-teller.<BR>—शिवानन्द (˚व-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘Śiva's joy,’ N. of<BR>a scribe.<BR>—शिवापीड (˚व or ˚वा-आप्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>chaplet of Śiva or Durgā; Sesbana Grandiflora (=<BR>वक).<BR>—१. शिवाप्रिय (˚व-अप्˚ or ˚वा-अप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, disliked by Śiva or by Durgā.<BR>—२. शिवा-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, beloved by Durgā; (अस्), m. a goat.<BR>—शि-<BR>वा-फला, f. the Śamī tree.<BR>—शिवा-बलि, इस्, m. an<BR>offering to Durgā made at night and consisting chiefly<BR>of flesh.<BR>—शिवाराति (˚व or ˚वा-अर्˚), इस्, m. an<BR>enemy of Śiva or Durgā; ‘jackal's enemy,’ a dog.<BR>—शिवा-रुत, अम्, n. the howling of a jackal.<BR>—शि-<BR>वार्चन-चन्द्रिका (˚व-अर्˚), f., N. of a work.<BR>—शिवालय (˚व-आल्˚), अस्, m. the residence of Śiva,<BR>Śiva's abode; red Tulasī or basil; (अम्), n. any<BR>temple or shrine dedicated to Śiva (generally con-<BR>taining a Liṅga); a cemetery, place where dead<BR>bodies are burnt or buried; N. of a place.<BR>—शिवा-<BR>स्मृति, इस्, f. ‘Durgā-memorial,’ the plant Sesbana<BR>Ægyptiaca (= जयन्ती).<BR>—शिवाह्लाद (˚व-आह्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘Śiva's joy,’ the tree Sesbana Grandiflora.<BR>—शिवाह्व (˚व-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, called or named<BR>after Śiva; (आ), f. a species of creeper (= रुद्र-<BR>जटा).<BR>—शिवेतर (˚व-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘other than<BR>auspicious,’ inauspicious, unhappy, unlucky.<BR>—शि-<BR>वेष्ट (˚व-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, loved by Śiva; (अस्),<BR>m. Sesbana Grandiflora; (आ), f. Dūrvā grass.<BR>—शिवो-<BR>पनिषद् (˚व-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad (sup-<BR>posed to have been the work on which the Śiva-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">Page1009-a+ 76</a>]<BR>sūtras were founded).<BR>—शिवोपपुराण (˚व-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवक|शिवकः
शिवक, अस्, m. a pillar or post to which cattle are<BR>tethered or to which cows are tied (when milked);<BR>a scratching-post (for cattle to rub against).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवानी
शिवानी, f. the wife of Śiva (i. e. Durgā); the<BR>plant Sesbana Ægyptiaca (= जयन्ती; or, according<BR>to others, Celtis Orientalis).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवालु|शिवालुः
शिवालु, उस्, m. a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविय
शिविय, Nom. P. शिवीयति, -यितुम्, to treat any<BR>one (acc.) like Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवि|शिविः
शिवि शिवि, इस्, m. a beast of prey, noxious<BR>animal; the birch tree (= भूर्ज); N. of a king<BR>(son of Uśīnara; the story of his rescuing Agni in<BR>the form of a pigeon from Indra in the form of a<BR>hawk by the offering of an equal portion of his own<BR>flesh, weighed in a balance, is told in the Vahni-<BR>Purāṇa and Mahā-bhārata, see below); N. of a<BR>country; (अयस्), m. pl., N. of a people or race.<BR>—शिवि-चरित or शिवि-चरित्र, अम्, n. ‘the story<BR>of Śivi,’ N. of an episode of the Mahā-bhārata; see<BR>Vana-parvan 13275-13300; the same story of the<BR>hawk and the pigeon is told of Uśīnara in Vana-<BR>parvan 10560-10596.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविका
शिविका शिविका, f. a palanquin, palkee,<BR>litter; a bier; a stage erected for exhibitions; a<BR>proper N.<BR>—शिविका-दान, अम्, n. the gift of a<BR>litter, &c.; N. of a chapter of the Vahni-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवीरथ|शिवीरथः
शिवी-रथ, अस्, m. a palanquin, litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविपिष्ट|शिविपिष्टः
शिविपिष्ट शिविपिष्ट for शिपि-विष्ट, अस्, m.<BR>epithet of Śiva, &c. See शिपि, p. 1005.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविर|शिविरं
शिविर शिविर, अम्, n. (said in Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>54. to be fr. rt. 1. शी), a camp; a royal camp, royal<BR>residence; an intrenchment for the protection of an<BR>army; a sort of grain; (अस्), m., N. of a tribe (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशयिषा
शिशयिषा शिशयिषा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt.<BR>1. शी), desire to lie down, wish to sleep, drowsiness,<BR>sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशयिषु
शिशयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to lie down, sleepy,<BR>drowsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशान
शिशान शिशान. See under rt. 1. शि, p. 1004.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिर|शिशिरः
शिशिर शिशिर, अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. I. 54. fr. rt. शश्; probably connected with<BR>rt. शॄ or rt. शो), cool, chilly, cold, frigid, freezing;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of the seventh month of the year (ac-<BR>cording to one reckoning); N. of a mountain; of a<BR>teacher of the Ṛg-veda (a pupil or descendant of Śā-<BR>kalya Veda-mitra); (अस्, अम्), m. n. hoar frost, dew,<BR>coolness, cold; the cool or dewy season (comprising<BR>two months, Māgha and Phālguna, or from about<BR>the middle of January to that of March, see ऋतु).<BR>—शिशिर-काल, अस्, m. the dewy season.<BR>—शि-<BR>शिर-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying frost; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Agni or fire.<BR>—शिशिर-तर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>more cool, very refreshing.<BR>—शिशिर-मथित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, pinched by cold.<BR>—शिशिरर्तु (˚र-ऋतु),<BR>उस्, m. the dewy season.<BR>—शिशिरांशु (˚र-अं˚), उस्,<BR>m. ‘having cold rays,’ the moon.<BR>—शिशिरांशु-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the state of having cold rays.<BR>—शिशिरी-भू,<BR>cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become cool.<BR>—शिशिरो-<BR>ष्ण-वर्ष (˚र-उष्˚), आस्, f. pl. the dewy, hot,<BR>and rainy seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशु|शिशुः
शिशु शिशु, उस्, m. (a reduplicated form of<BR>1. शु for rt. श्वि; according to Uṇādi-s. I. 21. fr. rt.<BR>शो; Ved. शिश्वः = शिशवः, शिश्वा = शिशुना), a<BR>child, infant; the young of any animal (as a calf,<BR>puppy, &c.); a boy under eight years of age; a lad<BR>under sixteen; a pupil, scholar; N. of a descendant<BR>of Aṅgiras (author of Ṛg-veda IX. 112).<BR>—शिशु-<BR>काल, अस्, m. childhood.<BR>—शिशु-क्रन्द, अस्, m. or<BR>शिशु-क्रन्दन, अम्, n. the weeping of a child<BR>or infant.<BR>—शिशु-क्रन्दीय, अस्, m., scil. ग्रन्थ,<BR>a book treating of infantile complaints or (perhaps) a<BR>book suitable for naughty children, (Pān. IV. 3, 88.)<BR>—शिशु-गन्धा, f. double jasmine.<BR>—शिशु-चान्द्रा-<BR>यण, अम्, n. the lunar penance of children, (eating<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">Page1009-b+ 79</a>]<BR>four mouthfuls at sunrise and four mouthfuls at sun-<BR>set for a month, Manu XI. 219.)<BR>—शिशु-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. or शिशु-ता, f. childhood, boyhood, the period up<BR>to eight years of age; pupilage, the period before<BR>sixteen.<BR>—शिशु-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the<BR>place of a child, not far from or almost a child.<BR>—शिशु-नाग, अस्, m. a young elephant; a kind of<BR>Rākṣasa or demon; N. of a king of Magadhā (the<BR>founder of a dynasty).<BR>—शिशु-पाल, अस्, m. ‘child-<BR>cherisher,’ N. of the king of the Cedis inhabiting a<BR>country in central India, probably the same as Bun-<BR>delkhand, (see चेदि; he was son of Dama-ghoṣa,<BR>and is also called Su-nītha; his impiety in opposing<BR>the worship of Kṛṣṇa is described in the Sabhā-<BR>parvan of the Mahā-bhārata; when Yudhi-ṣṭhira<BR>was about to perform a Rājasūya sacrifice, numerous<BR>princes attended, and Bhīṣma proposed that especial<BR>honour should be paid to Kṛṣṇa, who was also<BR>present, but Śiśu-pāla objected, and after denouncing<BR>Kṛṣṇa as a contemptible person challenged him to<BR>fight, whereupon Kṛṣṇa struck off his head with<BR>his discus; the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa identifies this impious<BR>monarch with the demons Hiraṇya-kaśipu and Rā-<BR>vaṇa; his death forms the subject of Māgha's cele-<BR>brated poem called Śiśupāla-vadha.)<BR>—शिशुपालक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, protecting or cherishing children; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a king (= शिशु-पाल); the plant Nauclea<BR>Cordifolia.<BR>—शिशुपाल-बध or शिशुपाल-वध,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the slaying of Śiśu-pāla,’ N. of a part of<BR>the Mahā-bhārata (see below) and of an epic poem<BR>by Māgha on the subject of Śiśu-pāla's death by the<BR>hand of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—शिशुपाल-बध-पर्वन्, अ,<BR>n., N. of a section of the Mahā-bhārata (contained<BR>in the Sabhā-parvan 1418 — 1627, see above).<BR>—शि-<BR>शुपाल-हन्, आ, m. ‘destroyer of Śiśu-pāla,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—शिशु-भाव, अस्, m. the state of<BR>childhood, infancy.<BR>—शिशु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>infantine, childish, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 140, 10. शिशुमतीर् = शैशववतीर् ज्वालाः.)<BR>—शिशु-मार, अस्, m. ‘child-killing,’ the Gangetic<BR>porpoise, Delphinus Gangeticus; ‘the heavenly por-<BR>poise,’ a form of Viṣṇu (described as a collection<BR>of the stars and planets); N. or a form of Viṣṇu.<BR>—शिशुमार-शिरस्, अस्, n. the dolphin's head, a<BR>part of the heavens studded with stars, the north-<BR>east point.<BR>—शिशु-वाहक or शिशु-वाह्यक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘child-carrier,’ a wild goat.<BR>—शिशु-हत्या, f.<BR>child-murder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक|शिशुकः
शिशुक, अस्, m. a child; the young of any animal;<BR>a porpoise; a fish resembling a porpoise; a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशूल
शिशूल, अस्, m., Ved. a child or a young animal,<BR>(Sāy. = शिशु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्वन्
शिश्वन् in सं-शिश्वन्, q. v.; (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda I. 65, 5. शिश्वा may either = तनू-<BR>कृतः, ‘attenuated,’ as if fr. rt. शो, or = शिशुना,<BR>inst. c. of शिशु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्वायै
शिश्वायै in Ṛg-veda X. 95, 13 = शिवे, i. e. कल्-<BR>याणे समुपस्थिते सति (according to Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्वि
शिश्वि, इस्, इस्, इ, swelling, increasing, thriving, &c.,<BR>in सु-शिश्वि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्न|शिश्नं|शिश्नः
शिश्न शिश्न, अस्, m. (according to Yāska<BR>fr. rt. श्नथ्; according to others fr. rt. शश्), the<BR>male generative organ, (also अम्, n. in Ved.); (अम्),<BR>n., Ved. a tail; thread steeped in rice-water, (said<BR>by Sāy. to be fr. rt. स्ना, Ṛg-veda I. 105, 8.)<BR>—शिश्न-देव, अस्, m. ‘having the generative organ<BR>for a god’ or ‘sporting with that organ,’ a lustful or<BR>unchaste man, (Sāy. शिश्नेन दीव्यन्ति क्रीडन्ति<BR>इति शिश्न-देवाः अब्रह्मचर्याः इत्य् अर्थः); a<BR>tailed or priapic demon.<BR>—शिश्नोदर-परायण<BR>(˚न-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, addicted to lust and gluttony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्रियाण
शिश्रियाण शिश्रियाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्रि),<BR>Ved. seeking refuge, taking refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्विदान|शिश्विदानः
शिश्विदान शिश्विदान, अस्, आ, अम् (according<BR>to Uṇādi-s. II. 93. fr. rt. श्वित्, ‘to be white,’ with<BR>substitution of द् for त् and elision of the desiderative<BR>affix स्), ‘being pure,’ innocent, virtuous (= शुक्ल-<BR>कर्मन्); guilty, sinful, wicked (= कृष्ण-कर्-<BR>मन् according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्
शिष् 1. शिष्, cl. 1. P. शेषति, शिशेष,<BR>शेक्ष्यति, अशिक्षत्, शेष्टुम्, to hurt,<BR>injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्
शिष् 2. शिष्, cl. 7. P. शिनष्टि, शिशेष,<BR>शेक्ष्यति, अशिषत्, शेष्टुम्, to leave,<BR>leave remaining; to distinguish from others, indi-<BR>vidualize; (according to some also) cl. 1. P. शेषति,<BR>&c., to leave a residue, allow to remain, spare:<BR>Pass. शिष्यते, (for शिष्यते, Pass. of rt. 1. शास्, see<BR>p. 1003), to be left remaining, remain; Caus. (or cl.<BR>10) शेषयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशीशिषत्, to cause to<BR>remain, leave, allow to remain, spare: Desid. शि-<BR>क्षति: Intens. शेशिष्यते, शेशेष्टि; [cf. Lat.<BR>quœso, quœro, quœstor, perhaps cura; Goth. qvis-<BR>teins, qvistjan, fra-qvisteins, fra-qvistjan, fra-<BR>qvistnan, us-qvistjan (based on a noun qvist = शिष्टि,<BR>in the sense of ‘leaving, abandoning’), us-haista.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट|शिष्टः
1. शिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, left, remaining, residual,<BR>anything that remains or is left.<BR>—१. शिष्ट-ता, f. or<BR>शिष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. the being left, the being residual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट|शिष्टः
शिष्ट 2. शिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शास्),<BR>ordered, commanded; disciplined, well regulated,<BR>educated, trained; tamed, obedient, docile; orderly,<BR>correct, learned, wise, good; select, (perhaps refer-<BR>rible to 1. शिष्ट); eminent, excellent, superior, prin-<BR>cipal, chief; (अस्), m. a chief; a courtier, counsellor.<BR> — 2. शिष्ट-ता, f. or शिष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. docility;<BR>good behaviour, urbanity, civility.<BR>—शिष्ट-सभा,<BR>f. an assembly of chiefs, council of state.<BR>—शिष्ट-<BR>सभाचार (˚भा-आच्˚), अस्, m. history or tradition of<BR>eminent persons.<BR>—शिष्ट-सम्मत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>approved or loved by the learned, (Manu III. 39.)<BR>—शिष्टाचरण (˚ट-आच्˚), अम्, n. the conduct or<BR>procedure of the virtuous, practice of the good, gen-<BR>tlemanly behaviour.<BR>—शिष्टाचार (˚ट-आच्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the practice or traditional usages of the virtuous; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), well-behaved; the approved conduct of the<BR>wise and good, good manners, gentlemanly conduct,<BR>proper behaviour.<BR>—शिष्टाचार-विरुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>opposed to the practice of the virtuous.<BR>—शिष्टा-<BR>चाराविरुद्ध (˚र-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not opposed<BR>to the practice of the virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टि|शिष्टिः
शिष्टि, इस्, f. ruling, governing, commanding; an<BR>order, command; correction, punishment, chastise-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट्वा
शिष्ट्वा, ind. having governed or regulated or<BR>trained; having ordered or decreed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्य|शिष्यः
शिष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taught, docile [cf. अ-श्˚];<BR>(अस्), m. a scholar, pupil, disciple, (कु-शिष्य, a bad<BR>or wicked pupil); passion, anger; violence.<BR>—शिष्य-<BR>ता, f. or शिष्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state or character<BR>of a pupil, pupilage, instruction.<BR>—शिष्य-परम्-<BR>परा, f. a series or succession of pupils or disciples.<BR>—शिष्य-पुत्र, अस्, m. a pupil equal to a son.<BR>—शिष्य-प्रदेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be delivered or<BR>imparted to pupils.<BR>—शिष्य-शिष्टि, इस्, f. chastise-<BR>ment or correction of a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्यमाण
शिष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being ruled or controlled;<BR>being instructed or trained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिह्ल|शिह्लः
शिह्ल शिह्ल or शिह्लक, अस्, m. (also written<BR>सिह्ल, q. v.), olibanum, benzoin, Indian incense (=<BR>शिला-रस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिह्लन
शिह्लन, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Śānti-<BR>śataka, (sometimes written शिल्हन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी 1. शी (perhaps connected with rt.<BR>शद्), cl. 2. A. शेते (1st du. शेवहे, 3rd du.<BR>शयाते, 1st pl. शेमहे, 3rd pl. शेरते, Ved. cl. 1.<BR>शयते, but शये = शेते, Ṛg-veda III. 55, 4, cf. Pāṇ.<BR>VII. 1, 41; Ved. and ep. also P. in some tenses),<BR>Impf. अशेत (P. अशयत्, Ved. 2nd du. P. अशायतम्,<BR>3rd du. A. अशयाताम्, 3rd pl. अशेरत), Pot. श-<BR>यीत (ep. शयेत्), Impv. शेताम् (2nd sing. शेष्व,<BR>1st du. शयावहै, 3rd pl. शेरताम्), शिश्ये, श-<BR>यिष्यते (ep. शेष्यति), अशयिष्ट, शयितुम् (Ved.<BR>Inf. शयध्यै), to lie, lie down, lie on the ground,<BR>recline; to rest, repose; to sleep: Pass. शय्यते,<BR>Aor. अशायि: Caus. शाययति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>lie down, put down, throw down; to throw, put;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">Page1010-a+ 79</a>]<BR>to allow to rest: Desid. शिशयिषते: Intens. शा-<BR>शय्यते, शेशयीति, शेशेति; [cf. Gr. κεῖ-μαι (κεῖσαι<BR>= शेषे, κεῖται = शेते); κοί-τη, κοι-μά-ω, κῶ-μο-ς,<BR>κῶμα, κώ-μη: Lat. qui-e-s, qui-e-sc-o, civi-s:<BR>Goth. hai-m-s, he-thyô, haithi, heiwa, ‘house,’ in<BR>comp. heiva-franja: Old Island. hei-mr, ‘house:’<BR>Old Germ. haim, heim, hī-wī, hi-wo, ‘husband;’<BR>hiwa, ‘wife;’ hijan, hiwjan, ‘to marry;’ hīrāt:<BR>Mod. Germ. Heirath: Angl. Sax. ham, hœman:<BR>Lith. sze†tra, ‘a tent;’ kie†ma, ‘a village.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनीय|शयनीयं
शयनीय, शयित, &c. See p. 994, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायक|शायकः
शायक. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्यान
शिश्यान, अस्, आ, अम्, lying, reclining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
2. शी, ईस्, f. sleep, repose; tranquillity, devotion,<BR>complete absorption in religious worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीक्
शीक् शीक् (also written सीक्, and per-<BR>haps connected with rt. 1. सिच्), cl. 1.<BR>A. शीकते, शिशीके, शीकिष्यते, अशीकिष्ट, शीकितुम्,<BR>to sprinkle, wet, moisten; to go gently, move; cl.<BR>1. 10. P. शिकति, शीकयति, to bear ill or impatiently,<BR>be angry; to bear patiently, be patient; to touch<BR>(= rt. चीक्); to speak (cl. 10); to shine (cl. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकर|शीकरं|शीकरः
शीकर, अस्, m. thin or drizzling rain, drizzle,<BR>spray, mist, rain driven by wind; a drop of rain or<BR>water, (also written सीकर); (अम्), n. the resin of<BR>the Sarala pine or the tree itself.<BR>—शीकरौघ<BR>(˚र-ओघ), अस्, आ, अम्, abounding with mist, having<BR>much spray or thin rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिकरिन्
शिकरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, sprinkling, drizzling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र|शीघ्रं
शीघ्र शीघ्र, अस्, आ, अम् (etymology doubt-<BR>ful), quick, speedy; (अस्), m. (in astronomy) con-<BR>junction; (according to others) parallax; N. of a<BR>king; (आ), f., N. of a river; a particular plant, =<BR>दन्ती; (अम्), ind. quickly, rapidly, swiftly; [cf. Gr.<BR>κιχάνω; Angl. Sax. higian.]<BR>—शिघ्र-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. (in astronomy) the calculation of the conjunc-<BR>tion (of a planet).<BR>—शिघ्र-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting<BR>speedily or expeditiously.<BR>—शिघ्र-कृत्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be done quickly, what must be done quickly.<BR>—शिघ्र-केन्द्र, अम्, n. (in astronomy) the dis-<BR>tance from the conjunction (of a planet), commuta-<BR>tion.<BR>—शिघ्र-कोपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, quickly angry, irri-<BR>table.<BR>—शीघ्र-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going quickly; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—शिघ्र-गन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or<BR>शीघ्र-गमन, अस्, आ, अम्, going quickly.<BR>—शी-<BR>घ्र-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going or moving quickly,<BR>swift, expeditious.<BR>—शीघ्र-चेतन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having quick intellect, very sagacious; (अस्), m. a<BR>dog.<BR>—शीघ्र-जन्मन्, आ, m. ‘having quick birth,’<BR>the plant Cæsalpinia Bonducella; another plant (=<BR>करञ्ज).<BR>—शीघ्र-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more quick,<BR>very swift; (अम्), ind. as swiftly as possible.<BR>—शी-<BR>घ्र-ता, f. or शीघ्र-त्व, अम्, n. quickness, speed,<BR>rapidity.<BR>—शीघ्र-परिधि, इस्, m. (in astronomy)<BR>the epicycle of a conjunction.<BR>—शीघ्र-पुष्प, अस्,<BR>m. ‘quick-flowering,’ a kind of plant (= अगस्त्य).<BR>—शीघ्र-फल, अम्, n. (in astronomy) the equation<BR>of a conjunction.<BR>—शीघ्र-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, quick-<BR>witted, having quick apprehension, acute, sharp.<BR>—शी-<BR>घ्र-यान, अम्, n. rapid motion.<BR>—शिघ्र-लङ्-<BR>घन, अस्, आ, अम्, springing or jumping quickly,<BR>moving rapidly.<BR>—शिघ्र-वेग, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a rapid course, impetuous.<BR>—शीघ्र-वेधिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘quickly piercing (the mark),’ a good archer.<BR>—शी-<BR>घ्र-श्रोतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having a rapid current (said<BR>of a river)<BR>—शीघ्रोच्च (˚र-उच्˚), अस्, m. ‘the apex of<BR>the swiftest motion,’ a conjunction (in astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिघ्राय
शिघ्राय, Nom. A. शीघ्रायते, -यितुम्, to be-<BR>come quick or rapid; to hasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रायमाण
शीघ्रायमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming quick,<BR>going rapidly, hastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रिन्
शीघ्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speedy, one who is quick or<BR>expeditious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रिय|शीघ्रियः
शीघ्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, quick, fleet; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva; of Viṣṇu; the fighting of cats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रीय|शीघ्रीयं
शीघ्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, quick, speedy, rapid, swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र्य|शीघ्र्यं
शीघ्र्य, अम्, n. quickness, speed, rapidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्
शीत् शीत्, ind. [cf. सीत्], a sound made by<BR>drawing in the breath to express any sudden thrill of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-b" target="_blank">Page1010-b+ 80</a>]<BR>pleasure or pain (but especially pleasurable sensations<BR>during sexual enjoyments, = रति-काल-ध्वनि).<BR>—शीत्-कार, अस्, m. making the above sound शीत्;<BR>a frown.<BR>—शित्-कृत, अम्, n. the sound शीत्, a sound<BR>made by drawing in the breath to express pleasurable<BR>sensations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत|शीतं|शीतः
शीत शीत, अस्, आ, अम् (according to some fr.<BR>rt. श्यै or fr. rt. 1. शी; according to others an<BR>old pass. part. fr. rt. शो), cold, chilly, frigid; dull, apa-<BR>thetic, stupid, sluggish, sleepy, (in this sense connected<BR>with rt. 1. शी); idle, lazy, stupid; decocted, boiled;<BR>(अम्), n. cold, coldness; cold weather, the cold<BR>season; water; bark or cinnamon, = त्वच; (अस्),<BR>m. a small tree, Cordia Myxa; a kind of ratan,<BR>Calamus Fasciculatus; the plant Marsilea Quadrifolia;<BR>the Nimb tree; another plant (= पर्पट); cam-<BR>phor; (आ), f. a furrow; N. of the wife of Rāma,<BR>(in these last two tenses more usually written सीता,<BR>q. v.; but derived according to Uṇādi-s. III. 90. fr.<BR>rt. 1. शी.)<BR>—शीत-काल, अस्, m. the cold season,<BR>winter.<BR>—शीतकालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the<BR>cold season, produced in winter, wintry.<BR>—शीत-<BR>कुम्भ, अस्, m. the fragrant oleander, = कर-<BR>वीर; (ई), f. an aquatic plant; [cf. शीतला.]<BR>—शीत-<BR>कृच्छ्र, अस्, m. a particular religious penance (con-<BR>sisting in drinking cold water for three days, cold<BR>milk for three days, cold ghee for three days, and<BR>eating air or fasting for three days).<BR>—शीत-क्षार,<BR>अम्, n. refined borax.<BR>—शीत-गन्ध, अम्, n. ‘hav-<BR>ing cool fragrance,’ white sandal.<BR>—शीत-गु, उस्, m.<BR>‘having cold rays,’ the moon.<BR>—शित-चम्पक, अस्,<BR>m. a lamp; a mirror; pleasing, satisfying (?).<BR>—शित-<BR>ज्वर, अस्, m. a cold fever, ague.<BR>—शीत-ता, f. or<BR>शीत-त्व, अम्, n. coldness, cold.<BR>—शीत-दीधिति, इस्,<BR>m. ‘cold-rayed,’ the moon.<BR>—शित-पर्णी, f. ‘cool-<BR>leaved,’ the plant Cleome Pentaphylla; another plant<BR>(= अर्क).<BR>—शीत-पल्लव, अस्, m. ‘cool-blossomed,’<BR>a kind of plant, Ardisea Solanacea; (आ), f. another<BR>plant (= भूमि-जम्बु).<BR>—शीत-पाकिनी, f. a kind<BR>of medicinal root (= काकोली); another plant (=<BR>महा-समङ्गा).<BR>—शित-पाकी, f. a medicinal root<BR>(= काकोली); the plant Sida Cordifolia; another plant<BR>(= गुञ्जा).<BR>—शीत-पित्त, अम्, n. increase of bile or<BR>phlegm caused by cold.<BR>—शित-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘cool-<BR>flowered,’ the Śirīṣa tree; (आ), f. a kind of plant, =<BR>अति-बला; (अम्), n. a fragrant grass, Cyperus Ro-<BR>tundus.<BR>—शीत-पुष्पक, अस्, m. a kind of plant,<BR>= अर्क; (अम्), n. storax or benzoin.<BR>—शीत-पू-<BR>तना, f. epithet of a particular Graha or disease of<BR>children, (see ग्रह, पूतना.)<BR>—शित-प्रभ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having cool radiance,’ camphor.<BR>—शित-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, m. ‘fond of cold,’ a plant (= पर्पट).<BR>—शीत-<BR>फल, अस्, m. ‘having cool fruit,’ the tree Ficus Glo-<BR>merata; another tree (= शेलु).<BR>—शीत-बला, f. a kind<BR>of plant (= महा-समङ्गा).<BR>—शीत-भानु, उस्, m.<BR>‘cool-rayed,’ the moon.<BR>—शीत-भीरु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>afraid of cold; (उस्), m. Arabian jasmine, Jasminum<BR>Zambac.<BR>—शित-भोजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, eating cold viands.<BR>—शीत-मञ्जरी, f. a particular plant (= शेफाली).<BR>—शीत-मयूख, अस्, or शीत-मरीचि, इस्, m. ‘cool-<BR>rayed,’ the moon; camphor.<BR>—शित-मूलक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a cool root; (अम्), n. the root of the<BR>Uśīra.<BR>—शीत-रम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasant in cold<BR>weather; (अस्), m. a lamp.<BR>—शीत-रश्मि, इस्, m.<BR>‘cool-rayed,’ the moon; camphor.<BR>—शीत-रुच्, क्, or<BR>शीत-रुचि, इस्, m. ‘having cool light,’ the moon.<BR>—शीत-वल्क, अस्, आ, अम्, having cool bark; (अस्),<BR>m. the Udumbara tree.<BR>—शीत-वीर्यक, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing cold seed,’ the fig-tree (= प्लक्ष).<BR>—शीत-<BR>शिव, अस्, आ, m. f. a kind of fennel (= मधुरिका,<BR>मिश्रेया); the Śamī tree; (अम्), n. a sort of resin,<BR>storax or benzoin; rock-salt.<BR>—शित-शूक, अस्, m.<BR>‘having cold awns or beards,’ barley.<BR>—शीत-श्पर्श,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, cool to the touch or feeling, cooling, re-<BR>freshing, pleasant.<BR>—शीत-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing<BR>or enduring cold; (अस्), m. the Pīlu tree (growing in<BR>the Himālaya mountains); (आ), f. a small tree. Vitex<BR>Negundo; another plant (= वासन्ती).<BR>—शीत-हर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, removing cold.<BR>—शीतांशु (˚त-अं˚), उस्, m.<BR>‘cool-rayed,’ the moon; camphor.<BR>—शितांशु-ता, f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">Page1010-c+ 79</a>]<BR>coldness of ray, chilliness.<BR>—शीतांशु-तैल, अम्, n.<BR>camphor oil, camphor liniment^1.<BR>—शिताकुल (˚त-<BR>आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, benumbed with cold, frozen.<BR>—शी-<BR>ताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, cold-bodied, having<BR>cold limbs; (अस्), m. a kind of fever (supposed to<BR>arise from a vitiated state of one of the humors of<BR>the body); (ई), f. a particular plant (= हंस-पदी).<BR>—शीताद (˚त-अद), अस्, m. scorbutic affection or<BR>otherwise diseased state of the gums.<BR>—शीताद्रि (˚त-<BR>अद्˚), इस्, m. the snowy mountains, the Himālayas.<BR>—शीताबला (˚ता-अब्˚), a kind of plant (= महा-<BR>समङ्गा).<BR>—शीतार्त (˚त-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pained<BR>or pinched with cold, suffering from cold, chilled,<BR>shivering, cold.<BR>—शीताश्मन् (˚त-अश्˚), आ, m. a cold<BR>stone; the moon-gem, crystal.<BR>—शीती-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>cold state, coldness, cold, coolness; composure; final<BR>emancipation.<BR>—शीती-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c.,<BR>to be or become cold.<BR>—शीतोत्तम (˚त-उत्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘the best of cold things,’ water.<BR>—शीतोद (˚त-<BR>उद), ‘having cool water,’ N. of a lake; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a river.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतक|शीतकः
शीतक, अस्, m. cold weather, the cold season,<BR>winter; a lazy or dilatory man, a dull person; a<BR>happy or contented man, one without cares or<BR>anxieties (= सु-स्थित); the plant Marsilea Den-<BR>tata; a scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतल|शीतलं|शीतलः
शीतल, अस्, आ, अम्, cool, cold, frigid, chilly; (अस्),<BR>m. the moon; the plant Marsilea Quadrifolia; a<BR>particular Jina or Arhat, (the tenth of the twenty-<BR>four Tīrthakāras); a religious ceremony observed<BR>upon the sun's entering Aries; the small tree Cordia<BR>Myxa; the Campaka tree; a sort of camphor; tur-<BR>pentine or the resin of Shorea Robusta; (आ), f.<BR>small-pox (= मसूरिका); the goddess presiding<BR>over or inflicting small-pox; a kind of aquatic plant<BR>(perhaps the Phrynium Dichotymum, from the split<BR>stems of which a cool mat is made; = शीत-कुम्भी,<BR>शुक्ल-पुष्पा); other plants, = कुटुम्बिनी; = आरा-<BR>म-शीतला; = बालुका; (ई), f. a kind of aquatic<BR>plant, see above; small-pox; (अम्), n. cold, cold-<BR>ness, coolness, cold weather; the cold season; green<BR>sulphate of iron (= पुष्प-कासीस); benzoin or<BR>storax; sandal, white sandal; a lotus; a pearl; the<BR>root of the Andropogon Muricatus.<BR>—शीतल-च्छद,<BR>अस्, m. a white leaf; (अस्, आ, अम्), having white<BR>leaves; (अस्), m. the Campaka tree.<BR>—शितल-जल,<BR>अम्, n. cold water; a lotus.<BR>—शीतल-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, more cool, colder.<BR>—शीतल-ता, f. or शीतल-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. coldness, coolness, frigidity, chilliness; in-<BR>sensibility, apathy (= जड-ता).<BR>—शीतल-प्रद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, giving or producing coolness; (अस्), m.<BR>sandal.<BR>—शीतल-प्रसाद, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—शी-<BR>तल-वात, अस्, m. a cool breeze, cold wind.<BR>—शीतल-<BR>वातक, अस्, आ, अम्, having cool breezes; (अस्), m.<BR>the plant Marsilea Quadrifolia (= अशन-पर्णी).<BR>—शीतल-षष्ठी, f. or शीतला-षष्ठी, the sixth<BR>of the light half of the month Māgha (when only<BR>cold food is eaten).<BR>—शीतला-पूजा, f. worship of the<BR>goddess Śītalā (a festival on the eighth day of the<BR>second half of the month Phālguna).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलक|शीतलकं|शीतलकः
शीतलक, अस्, m. a kind of plant, = मरुवक;<BR>(अम्), n. a white lotus (= सितोत्पल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतालु|शीतालुः
शीतालु, उस्, उस्, उ, suffering from cold, shivering<BR>with cold, chilled, cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतिका
शीतिका, f., Ved. coldness, cold.<BR>—शीतिका-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. possessing coldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्य|शीत्यं
शीत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cooled or chilled;<BR>ploughed, tilled, (in this sense more usually सीत्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्कार|शीत्कारः
शीत्कार शीत्-कार, शित्-कृत. See शीत्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधु|शीधुः
शीधु शीधु, उस्, उ, m. n. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 38. fr. rt. 1. शी, but also written सीधु),<BR>a spirit distilled from molasses, any intoxicating<BR>liquor, rum; wine.<BR>—शीधु-गन्ध, अस्, m. ‘smell-<BR>ing of spirits,’ the Vakula tree, Mimusops Elengi.<BR>—शीधु-प, अस्, ई, अम्, drinking spirits, a drinker<BR>of spirits, dram-drinker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीन|शीनं|शीनः
शीन शीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्यै, cf. शीत),<BR>congealed, thick (as oil or butter); (अस्), m. a fool,<BR>blockhead; a large snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीपाल
शीपाल शीपाल, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of plant,<BR>(Sāy. = शैवाल, Ṛg-veda X. 68, 5; cf. शेपाल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीफालिका
शीफालिका शीफालिका, f. the plant Nyctan-<BR>thes Tristis, (also written शेफालि, शेफालिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्
शीभ् शीभ्, cl. 1. A. शीभते, शिशीभे, शी-<BR>भितुम्, to boast: Caus. शीभयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अशिशीभत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिभ्य
शिभ्य, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva; a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभम्
शीभम् शीभम्, ind., Ved. quickly, speedily<BR>(= क्षिप्रम्, Naigh. II. 15).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभव|शीभवः
शीभव शीभव, अस्, m. thin rain (= शीकर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीम
शीम शीम in सु-शीम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीयमान
शीयमान शीयमान. See rt. शद्, p. 991.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्
शीर् शीर्. See शिर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर|शीरः
शीर 1. शीर, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 13. fr. rt. 1. शी), a large snake, the boa constrictor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीरिन्
शीरिन्, ई, m. a kind of plant (= हरिद्-गर्भ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर|शीरः
शीर 2. शीर, अस्, आ, अम् (according to some<BR>fr. rt. 1. शि or fr. rt. 2. श्री, ‘to cook’), Ved. piercing,<BR>burning; an epithet of Agni, (according to Nirukta<BR>IV. 14. fr. rt. 1. शी, and explained by अनुशयिन् or<BR>वासिन्, which Sāy. interprets to mean ‘sleeping or<BR>lying in the sacrifices.’)<BR>—शीर-शोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved.<BR>having burning or piercing splendor, gleaming like<BR>lightning, (Sāy. = शयन-स्वभाव-रोचिष्क, ‘he<BR>whose brilliance has the character of lying or sleep-<BR>ing,’ or अशन-शील-ज्वाल, ‘he whose flame has the<BR>character of pervading.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ण|शीर्णं
शीर्ण शीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. शॄ), withered,<BR>shriveled, shrunk, dry, sere, decayed, rotten; thin,<BR>wasted, emaciated, small, slender, broken off, shivered,<BR>shattered, injured; (अम्), n. a sort of perfume (=<BR>स्थौणेयक).<BR>—शीर्ण-ता, f. ‘having a shriveled<BR>or slender stem,’ or शीर्ण-त्व, अम्, n. the state of<BR>being withered or decayed, a withered condition,<BR>emaciation.<BR>—शीर्ण-नाला, f. the plant Hemionites<BR>Cordifolia (= शीर्ण-माला).<BR>—शीर्ण-पत्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>a withered leaf; (अस्, आ, अम्), having withered or<BR>shriveled leaves; (अस्), m. the tree Pterospermum<BR>Acerifolium; a kind of Lodhra (= पट्टिका-लोध्र);<BR>the Nimb tree.<BR>—शीर्ण-पर्ण, अम्, n. a withered<BR>leaf; (अस्, आ, अम्), having withered or shriveled<BR>leaves; (अस्), m. the Nimb tree.<BR>—शीर्ण-पाद,<BR>अस्, m. a thin foot; ‘having shriveled feet,’ epithet<BR>of Yama (said to have become so in consequence of<BR>his mother's curse).<BR>—शीर्ण-पुष्पिका, f. a kind<BR>of fennel, Anethum Sowa.<BR>—शीर्ण-माल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a withered garland; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>plant (= शीर्ण-नाला).<BR>—शीर्ण-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having withered roots, withered at the root.<BR>—शीर्ण-<BR>वृन्त, अम्, n. ‘slender-stalked,’ a water-melon.<BR>—शीर्णाङ्घ्रि (˚ण-अङ्˚), इस्, m. ‘having shriveled<BR>feet,’ epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्यमाण
शीर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being broken or shattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्त
शीर्त शीर्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्रि), Ved.<BR>served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्वि|शीर्व्वि|शीर्व्विः
शीर्वि शीर्वि, इस्, इस्, इ (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 54. fr. rt. शॄ), destructive, hurtful, injurious,<BR>mischievous, malignant; savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ष|शीर्षं
शीर्ष शीर्ष, अम्, n. (an abbreviated form<BR>of शीर्षन्, col. 2), the head, skull; black Agallochum<BR>or aloe wood (= कृष्णागुरु); [cf. probably Lat.<BR>collum; Old Germ. and Angl. Sax. hals.]<BR>—शीर्-<BR>ष-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, striking the head; beheading,<BR>decapitating.<BR>—शीर्ष-च्छेद, अस्, m. or शीर्ष-<BR>च्छेदन, अम्, n. the act of cutting off the head,<BR>decapitating, decapitation.<BR>—शीर्षच्छेदिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, deserving decapitation.<BR>—शीर्ष-च्छेदिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, cutting off the head, decapitating.<BR>—शीर्ष-<BR>च्छेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be beheaded, meriting death<BR>by decapitation.<BR>—शीर्ष-रक्ष, अम्, n. ‘head-<BR>protector,’ a helmet.<BR>—शीर्ष-शोक, अस्, m. pain in<BR>the head.<BR>—शीर्षामय (˚ष-आम्˚), अस्, m. disease<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">Page1011-b+ 80</a>]<BR>or morbid affection of the head.<BR>—शीर्षावशेषी-<BR>कृ (˚ष-अव्˚), cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to leave<BR>only the head undestroyed.<BR>—शीर्षोदय (˚ष-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘head-rising’ or ‘rising in front,’ epi-<BR>thet of the zodiacal signs Gemini, Leo, Virgo, Libra,<BR>Scorpio, Aquarius, and Pisces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षक|शीर्षकं|शीर्षकः
शीर्षक, अम्, n. the head, skull; a helmet; a<BR>cap, hat; judgment, award, verdict, sentence, result<BR>of judicial investigation; (अस्), m., N. of Rāhu (the<BR>personified ascending node).<BR>—शीर्षक-स्थ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, being in or on the head, staying on the<BR>head; abiding by an award or verdict, submitting<BR>to the penalty imposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षक्ति
शीर्षक्ति, इस्, f. (probably fr. शीर् = शीर्ष + सक्ति),<BR>Ved. a pain or affection in the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षण्य|शीर्षण्यः
शीर्षण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the head<BR>(Ved.); (अम्), n. a helmet; a cap; a rope fastened<BR>to a horse's head, head-rope, halter (Ved.); (अस्), m.<BR>clean and unentangled hair; [cf. शिरस्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षन्
शीर्षन्, अ, n. (connected with शिरस्, but not<BR>declined in the later language except in acc. pl. and<BR>remaining cases, where it may be optionally substi-<BR>tuted for शिरस्; it is also used in some comps., e. g.<BR>सहस्र-श्˚), the head; any eminent or illustrious<BR>person (Ved., e. g. शीर्ष्णे-शीर्ष्णे = श्रेष्ठाय<BR>श्रेष्ठाय, to every eminent person, Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>18, 24).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील्
शील् शील् (perhaps to be regarded as a<BR>Nom. fr. शील below), cl. 1. P. शीलति,<BR>शिशील, शीलिष्यति, शीलितुम्, to meditate, contem-<BR>plate, intend; to serve, worship, honour; to act, do,<BR>practise, make; cl. 10. P. or Caus. शीलयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अशिशीलत्, to honour, worship; to do, make,<BR>practise repeatedly, exercise, engage in; to act or<BR>practise excessively, exceed; to put on, wear, pos-<BR>sess; to visit, frequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील|शीलः
शील, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 38. fr. rt.<BR>1. शी; according to others fr. rt. 2. शिष्), disposition,<BR>inclination, character, nature, natural disposition,<BR>quality, tendency, custom, habit, usage, (in all these<BR>senses said to be also अस्, m.); practice, behaviour,<BR>conduct, (said to be also अस्, m.); good disposition<BR>or character, good nature, amiability, good conduct,<BR>moral practice, piety; virtue, morality, steadiness;<BR>form, shape, beauty; (in all the preceding senses<BR>often used at the end of adj. comps., e. g. दान-<BR>शील, अस्, आ, अम्, disposed to give, cf. अभिवादन-<BR>श्˚, गुण-श्˚, मांस-श्˚, पुण्य-श्˚, मृगया-श्˚,<BR>कु-श्˚, सु-श्˚, वि-श्˚); (अस्), m. a large snake, (in this<BR>sense fr. rt. 1. शी); (आ), f., N. of the wife of the<BR>Muni Kauṇḍinya; [cf. Slav. sila, ‘strength, power.’]<BR>—शील-ज्ञान-निधि, इस्, m. a treasury of virtue and<BR>knowledge.<BR>—शील-तट, अस्, आ, अम्, having virtue<BR>for a bank or shore (said figuratively of a river).<BR>—शील-तस्, ind. according to character, by natural<BR>disposition; in regard to the character.<BR>—शील-ता, f.<BR>or शील-त्व, अम्, n. disposition, inclination; quality;<BR>conversancy, practice.<BR>—शील-धारिन्, ई, m. ‘virtue-<BR>holder,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शील-निधि, इस्, m. a<BR>treasure of virtue.<BR>—शील-पारमिता, f. one of the<BR>six perfections (with Buddhists).<BR>—शील-भट्टारिका,<BR>f., N. of a female poet.<BR>—शील-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessed of good qualities, of a good or amiable<BR>disposition, well-conducted.<BR>—शील-वृत्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well-conducted, moral, steady, uniformly, well-<BR>behaved.<BR>—शील-वृत्ति, इस्, f. practice of virtue,<BR>good behaviour, virtue.<BR>—शील-सम्पन्न, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, endowed with good nature or conduct, well-<BR>disposed, of proper conduct or disposition, well-con-<BR>ducted.<BR>—शीलादित्य (˚ल-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Vikramāditya (= प्रताप-शील).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलन|शीलनं
शीलन, अम्, n. repeated practice, habitual per-<BR>formance, constant study (of the Śāstras &c.), ex-<BR>cessive performance or exercise; wearing, putting on,<BR>possessing; serving, honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलयत्
शीलयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, worshipping, honouring;<BR>practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलित|शीलितं
शीलित, अस्, आ, अम्, practised, exercised, skilled in,<BR>conversant with; endowed with, possessed of; visited,<BR>frequented; (अम्), n. practice, conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवन्
शीवन् शीवन्, आ, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 113. fr. rt. 1. शी), a large snake, the boa con-<BR>strictor; (अरी), f. an iguana (= गोधा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवल|शीवलं
शीवल शीवल, अम्, n. the aquatic plant<BR>Vallisneria Octandra [cf. शेवल, शैवल]; benzoin<BR>or storax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीहर
शीहर शीहर, अस्, m., N. of a scribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शु
शु 1. शु, a form assumed by rt. श्वि, cf.<BR>rt. शव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शु
शु 2. शु, ind. (perhaps connected with सु or<BR>with आशु), well, right, brilliantly, elegantly; quickly<BR>(= क्षिप्रम्, Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 33, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकम्
शुकम्, ind. quickly, swiftly (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंशुमार|शुंशुमारः
शुंशुमार शुंशुमार, अस्, m. a porpoise,<BR>(more usually written शिशु-मार, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्
शुक् शुक्, cl. 1. P. शोकति, शोकितुम्, to go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक|शुकं|शुकः
शुक शुक, अस्, m. (said in Uṇādi-s. III.<BR>42. to be fr. rt. 1. शुभ्, the final of the root being<BR>rejected), a parrot; the Śirīṣa tree; a plant (com-<BR>monly called Śeyālkāṃṭā); N. of a son of Vyāsa<BR>(narrator of the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa to king Parīkṣit,<BR>see भागवत-पुराण); N. of the minister of<BR>Rāvaṇa; (ई), f. a female parrot; N. of a daughter<BR>or, as some say, wife of Kaśyapa (represented as the<BR>mother of parrots, Viṣṇu-Purāṇa I. 21); (अम्), n.<BR>cloth, clothes; the end or hem of a garment; a<BR>helmet, turban; a particular drug and perfume (=<BR>ग्रन्थि-पर्ण, commonly called Gāṃṭhiālā); the<BR>plant Bignonia Indica.<BR>—शुक-कर्णी, see Pāṇini<BR>IV. 1, 64.<BR>—शुक-च्छद, अम्, n. ‘resembling a<BR>parrot's wing,’ a fragrant root and perfume (= ग्रन्-<BR>थि-पर्ण).<BR>—शुक-जिह्वा, f. a parrot's tongue; a<BR>plant (commonly called Śuyā-ṭhoṃṭī or parrot's beak).<BR>—शुक-तरु, उस्, m. the Śirīṣa tree, Acacia Si-<BR>rīṣa.<BR>—शुक-तुण्ड, अस्, m. ‘parrot's beak,’ a par-<BR>ticular position of the hands.<BR>—शुक-देव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the son of Vyāsa, (see शुक above.)<BR>—शुक-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. the Śirīṣa tree.<BR>—शुक-नामा, f.<BR>‘parrot-named,’ a kind of plant (= शुक-जिह्वा).<BR>—शुक-नाशन, अस्, m. ‘parrot-destroying,’ a par-<BR>ticular plant (= दद्रु-घ्न).<BR>—शुक-नास, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a nose like a parrot's beak, having an<BR>aquiline nose; (अस्), m. the tree Bignonia Indica;<BR>another tree, Sesbana Grandiflora.<BR>—शुक-नासिका, f.<BR>a parrot's nose; a nose like that of a parrot; an<BR>aquiline nose.<BR>—शुक-पिण्डि, इस्, f., see शूक-पिण्डि.<BR>—शुक-पितामह, अस्, m. ‘the grandfather of<BR>Śuka,’ epithet of the sage Parāśara (father of Vyāsa).<BR>—शुक-पुच्छ, अस्, m. a parrot's tail; ‘coloured<BR>like a parrot's tail,’ sulphur.<BR>—शुक-पुच्छक, अम्,<BR>n. ‘parrot-tailed,’ a particular perfume, (see शुक<BR>above.)<BR>—शुक-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘parrot-flowered,’<BR>the Śirīṣa tree; (अम्), n. a kind of perfume, (see<BR>above.)<BR>—शुक-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, dear to parrots;<BR>(अस्), m. the Śirīṣa tree; (आ), f. the rose-apple,<BR>Eugenia Jambu.<BR>—शुक-वत्, ind. like a parrot.<BR>—शुक-वर्ह, अम्, n. a sort of perfume, (see<BR>शुक.)<BR>—शुक-वल्लभ, अस्, आ, अम्, beloved by<BR>parrots; (अस्), m. the pomegranate.<BR>—शुक-वाह,<BR>अस्, m. ‘parrot-borne,’ epithet of Kāma-deva (whose<BR>vehicle is a parrot).<BR>—शुक-शारिक, अम्, n. a parrot<BR>and a Maina bird.<BR>—शुक-शिम्बा or शुक-शिम्बि, see<BR>शूक-शिम्बा.<BR>—शुक-संहिता, f., N. of a particular<BR>Tantra composition.<BR>—शुक-सप्तति, इस्, f., N. of<BR>seventy stories related by a parrot.<BR>—शुकाख्या (˚क-<BR>आख्˚), f. ‘parrot-named,’ a kind of plant (= शुक-<BR>नामा).<BR>—शुकादन (˚क-अद्˚), अम्, n. parrot's<BR>food; (अस्), m. the pomegranate.<BR>—शुकानना (˚क-<BR>आन्˚), f. ‘parrot-beaked,’ a kind of plant (= शुक-<BR>नामा).<BR>—शुकानुशासन (˚क-अन्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>an episode extracted from the Śānti-parvan of the<BR>Mahā-bhārata, 1. 12046 &c.<BR>—शुकाष्टक (˚क-<BR>अष्˚), अम्, n., N. of eight stanzas on the Vedānta<BR>doctrine (attributed to Śuka, the son of Vyāsa).<BR>—शुकोत्पत्ति (˚क-उत्˚), इस्, f. ‘the birth of Śuka,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-a" target="_blank">Page1012-a+ 79</a>]<BR>N. of part of the Śānti-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata<BR>(beginning chapter 325, I. 12158; the story is also<BR>related in a chapter of the Vahni-Purāṇa, called Pra-<BR>jāpati-sarga).<BR>—शुकोदर (˚क-उद्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>belly of a parrot; a kind of tree (= तालीश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकी
शुकी, f. See under शुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त|शुक्तं
शुक्त शुक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (in some senses fr.<BR>rt. 3. शुच्, in others perhaps fr. rt. 1. शुच्), bright,<BR>pure, clean; harsh, hard; sour, acid, (perhaps con-<BR>nected with rt. शुच्य्); united, joined (= श्लिष्ट);<BR>lonely, deserted, = निर्-जन; (अम्), n. flesh; sour<BR>gruel (= काञ्जिक); vinegar or a kind of acid liquid<BR>(prepared from roots and fruits by first steeping them<BR>in oil and salt, then drying them, and afterwards<BR>leaving them in water to undergo acetous fermenta-<BR>tion; in this sense probably connected with rt. शुच्य्),<BR>any sour sauce; crabbed or harsh speech; (आ), f. a<BR>sort of sorrel (= चुक्रिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तक|शुक्तकं
शुक्तक, अम्, n. sour eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ति|शुक्तिः
शुक्ति, इस्, f. a pearl-oyster or oyster-shell, (eight<BR>different sources of pearls are enumerated by Malli-<BR>nātha, viz. clouds, elephants, fish, serpents, bamboos,<BR>conch-shells, boars, and oyster-shells, Kirāt. XII. 40);<BR>a small shell, muscle, cockle; a conch-shell; a por-<BR>tion of the skull (used as a cup &c.); a sort of per-<BR>fume (in appearance like dried shell-fish, = नखी);<BR>a curl or feather on a horse's neck or breast; a weight<BR>of two Karṣas or four Tolas (= अष्टमिका); he-<BR>morrhoids (= अर्शो-रोग); a disease of the cornea<BR>(= शुक्ल).<BR>—शुक्ति-ज, अम्, n. ‘oyster-born,’ a<BR>pearl.<BR>—शुक्ति-पुट, अम्, n. a pearl-oyster shell.<BR>—शुक्ति-पेशी, f. ‘pearl-envelope,’ a pearl-oyster<BR>shell.<BR>—शुक्ति-मत्, आन्, m. one of the seven prin-<BR>cipal mountains or mountainous ranges of India, (see<BR>कुलाचल, p. 240, col. 3); (अती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—शुक्ति-वधू, ऊस्, f. mother of pearl or the pearl-<BR>oyster (which produces the pearl).<BR>—शुक्ति-वीज, अम्,<BR>n. ‘oyster-seed,’ a pearl.<BR>—शुक्ति-स्पर्श, अस्, m.<BR>dusky spots on a pearl (diminishing its value).<BR>—शुक्त्य्-उद्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘sprung from or<BR>produced in a pearl-oyster,’ epithet of a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिका
शुक्तिका, f. a pearl-oyster; a sort of sorrel (=<BR>चुक्रिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्र|शुक्रं|शुक्रः
शुक्र शुक्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. शुच्; con-<BR>nected with शुक्ल), bright, resplendent (Ved.); white,<BR>pure (Ved.); (अस्), m. the planet Venus or its regent<BR>(regarded as the son of Bhṛgu and preceptor of the<BR>Daityas); the month Jyeṣṭha (May-June); N. of<BR>Agni or fire; of a son of Vasiṣṭha; a kind of ग्रह<BR>or Soma cup; a kind of mystical formula, (भूर्,<BR>भुवः, स्वर् are said to be the three Śukras); a<BR>kind of plant, = चित्रक; (अम्), n. semen virile,<BR>seed of animals, sperm; male and female energy;<BR>the essence of anything; water (Ved. = उदक ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. I. 12); a morbid affection of the<BR>iris (change of colour &c. accompanied by imperfect<BR>vision, = शुक्ल); a particular Vedic metre.<BR>—शुक्र-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing or producing semen, sper-<BR>matic; (अस्), m. the marrow of the bones.<BR>—शुक्र-<BR>चार, अस्, m. the course of the planet Venus.<BR>—शु-<BR>क्र-पिश्, Ved. having a bright or pure form (=<BR>शुक्र-पेशस्, Nirukta VIII. 11; cf. विश्व-पिश्).<BR>—शुक्र-पूत-पा, आस्, m., Ved. one who drinks<BR>bright and purified Soma.<BR>—शुक्र-भुज्, क्, m.<BR>‘seed-eater,’ a peacock.<BR>—शुक्र-भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ,<BR>semen-produced; (ऊस्), m. ‘semen-site,’ the marrow<BR>of the bones.<BR>—शुक्र-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing bright lustre or colour.<BR>—शुक्र-वर्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. bright-coloured, resplendent.<BR>—शुक्र-<BR>वार, अस्, m. ‘Venus' day,’ Friday.<BR>—शुक्र-वासस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having a bright or white robe,<BR>clad in white, (Sāy. = श्वेत-वसन or निर्मल-<BR>दीप्ति, Ṛg-veda I. 113, 7.)<BR>—शुक्र-शिष्य, अस्, m.<BR>‘pupil of Śukra,’ a demon, Asura, Daitya, enemy of<BR>the gods, (see above.)<BR>—शुक्र-शोच, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. brightly shining, (Sāy. = ज्वल-दीप्त.)<BR>—शु-<BR>क्र-शोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having bright colour, having<BR>resplendent lustre or majesty.<BR>—शुक्राङ्ग (˚र-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘having a brilliant body,’ a peacock;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-b" target="_blank">Page1012-b+ 80</a>]<BR>[cf. शुक्लाङ्ग.]<BR>—शुक्राचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the regent of the planet Venus and preceptor of<BR>the Daityas.<BR>—शुक्रेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), N. of a<BR>Liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रल
शुक्रल, अस्, आ, अम्, spermatic, seminal, augment-<BR>ing the seminal secretion; (आ), f. a kind of fragrant<BR>grass (= उच्चटा; considered by some to be a sort<BR>of Cyperus, by others Zedoary).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रिय|शुक्रियः
शुक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Śukra, sacred<BR>to Śukra; seminal, spermatic; (अम्), n. epithet of a<BR>part of the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā (chapters 36-40).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ल|शुक्लं|शुक्लः
शुक्ल शुक्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. 3. शुच्; connected<BR>with शुक्र), light, bright, white, of a white colour,<BR>pure, unsullied; (अस्), m. a white colour; the twenty-<BR>fourth of the astronomical Yogas; epithet of the thirty-<BR>seventh (or third) year of Jupiter's cycle of sixty years;<BR>the light half of a month from new to full moon or<BR>any lunar day in it; epithet of Śiva; (अम्), n. silver;<BR>a disease of the cornea or white part of the eye<BR>(opacity, albugo); fresh butter; sour gruel; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of Sarasvatī; clayed or candied sugar; a kind of<BR>root (= काकोली); a kind of plant (= विदरी); another<BR>plant (= स्नुही).<BR>—शुक्ल-कण्ठक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a white throat; (अस्), m. a kind of gallinule<BR>or water-hen.<BR>—शुक्ल-कन्द, अस्, m. a white bulb;<BR>a kind of plant, = महिष-कन्द; (आ), f. the<BR>plant Aconitum Ferox.<BR>—शुक्ल-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>pure in action or conduct, guileless, innocent, virtuous.<BR>—शुक्ल-कुष्ठ, अम्, n. white skin-disease, leprosy.<BR>—शुक्ल-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, white-haired, gray-haired.<BR>—शुक्ल-क्षीर, अस्, आ, अम्, having white milk or<BR>juice; (ई), f. a kind of root (= काकोली).<BR>—शुक्ल-<BR>क्षेत्र, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—शुक्ल-ता, f. or<BR>शुक्ल-त्व, अम्, n. whiteness.<BR>—शुक्ल-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—शुक्ल-दशन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having white teeth, white-toothed.<BR>—शुक्ल-दुग्ध,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having white milk or juice,’ a kind of<BR>aquatic plant (= शृङ्गाटक).<BR>—शुक्ल-धातु, उस्,<BR>m. a white mineral, chalk.<BR>—शुक्ल-पक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>the light half of a month, the fifteen days of the<BR>moon's increase, the period from new to full moon;<BR>the innocent side of the two contending sides or<BR>parties.<BR>—शुक्लपक्षीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to<BR>the light half of the month.<BR>—शुक्ल-पुष्प, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having white flowers; (अस्), m., N. of various<BR>plants, a white variety of amaranth; a species of<BR>jasmine, Jasminum Pubescens; other plants, = छत्-<BR>त्रक; = मरुवक; (आ), f. a kind of aquatic<BR>plant (= शीत-कुम्भी); a species of Nāga-dantī or<BR>sunflower; (ई), f. a species of sunflower.<BR>—शुक्ल-<BR>पृष्ठक, अस्, m. ‘white-backed,’ a small tree,<BR>Vitex Nigundo.<BR>—शुक्ल-बल, अस्, m. a white Bala<BR>or Bala-deva (according to the Jainas; nine of these<BR>personages are enumerated, corresponding to the nine<BR>Kṛṣṇas or black Vāsudevas, see बल, बल-देव).<BR>—शुक्ल-मण्डल, अम्, n. a white circle or globe;<BR>the cornea or white of the eye.<BR>—शुक्ल-माल्यानु-<BR>लेपन (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a white gar-<BR>land and unguents (i. e. wearing a white garland and<BR>anointed with unguents).<BR>—शुक्ल-रोहित, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of white Rohita tree; a kind of bright-looking<BR>Rohita fish.<BR>—शुक्ल-वर्ग, अस्, m. a class of white<BR>objects (as the conch-shell, pearl-oyster, and cowrie).<BR>—शुक्ल-वस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a white robe,<BR>dressed in white.<BR>—शुक्ल-वायस, अस्, m. a white<BR>crow; a crane<BR>—शुक्ल-वृत्ति, इस्, f. pure employ-<BR>ment or subsistence; maintenance derived by a<BR>Brāhman from other Brāhmans only.<BR>—शुक्लाङ्ग<BR>(˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having a white or brilliant<BR>body or limbs; (अस्), m. a peacock; (ई), f. a particular<BR>plant (= शेफालिका).<BR>—शुक्लापाङ्ग (˚ल-अप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘having white eye-corners,’ a peacock.<BR>—शुक्ला-<BR>भिजातीय (˚ल-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of a pure race.<BR>—शुक्लाम्बर-धर (˚ल-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wear-<BR>ing or arrayed in white garments.<BR>—शुक्लाम्ल (˚ल-<BR>अम्˚), अम्, n. a sort of sorrel (= अम्ल-शाक).<BR>—शु-<BR>क्लार्मन् (˚ल-अर्˚), अ, n. a particular disease of<BR>the eyes.<BR>—शुक्ली-करण, अम्, n. making white,<BR>whitening.<BR>—शुक्ली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>make white, whiten.<BR>—शुक्ली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">Page1012-c+ 79</a>]<BR>white, whitened.<BR>—शुक्लोपल (˚ल-उप्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>white stone; (आ), f. clayed or candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लक|शुक्लकः
शुक्लक, अस्, आ, अम्, of a white colour, white;<BR>(अस्), m. a white colour; the light fortnight or time<BR>from new moon to full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लल
शुक्लल, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to Śabda-k.) white,<BR>whitening; (आ), f. a kind of fragrant grass (= उच्-<BR>चटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लायन
शुक्लायन, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लिमन्
शुक्लिमन्, आ, m. whiteness, brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्वन्
शुक्वन् शुक्वन् (fr. rt. 3. शुच्) in सु-शुक्वन्,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्षि|शुक्षिः
शुक्षि शुक्षि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 155. fr. rt. शुष्), air, wind; fire, light, lustre<BR>(= तेजस्); = चित्रम् (according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्ग|शुंग|शुंगः|शुङ्गः
शुङ्ग शुङ्ग, अस्, m. (etymology doubtful),<BR>the Indian fig-tree (= वट); the hog-plum (=<BR>आम्रातक); the awn of corn; N. of a dynasty of<BR>kings; (आ), f. the sheath or calyx of a young bud;<BR>the waved-leaf fig; the awn of barley &c., a bristle.<BR>—शुङ्गा-कर्मन्, अ, n. a form of the Saṃskāra or<BR>rite called Puṃ-savana, (see under 2. पुंस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्गिन्|शुंगिन्
शुङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a sheath or calyx; awned,<BR>furnished with an awn; (ई), m. the Indian fig-tree<BR>(= वट); the waved-leaf fig-tree (= प्लक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच् 1. शुच्, cl. 1. P. शोचति (ep. also A.<BR>-ते), शुशोच, शोचिष्यति, अशोचीत्, शोचितुम्<BR>(or शोक्तुम्, Vopa-deva VIII. 79, 80), to be grieved<BR>or sorrowful, be afflicted; to bewail, grieve for (with<BR>acc.); to regret, repent; to be absorbed in deep<BR>meditation: Caus. शोचयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशूशु-<BR>चत्, to afflict, grieve, make sorrowful; to be sor-<BR>rowful; to bewail: Desid. शुशुचिषति, शुशोचि-<BR>षति: Intens. शोशुच्यते, शोशोक्ति; [cf. Goth.<BR>hiufan; Angl. Sax. heaf, heofian; Old Germ.<BR>huvo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
2. शुच्, क्, f. sorrow, grief, distress, regret; calamity,<BR>affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचा
शुचा, f. sorrow, grief, distress; affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचित
1. शुचित, अस्, आ, अम्, grieved, sad, lamenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोक|शोकः
शोक, अस्, m. sorrow, grief, sadness, anguish, afflic-<BR>tion, distress, mourning, lamentation; (ई), f., Ved.<BR>night (= रात्रि, Naigh. I. 7).<BR>—शोक-कर्षित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, harassed by sorrow, agonized with grief.<BR>—शोक-चर्चा, f. ‘sorrow-repetition,’ indulgence in<BR>grief.<BR>—शोक-च्छिद्, त्, त्, त्, sorrow-removing, allaying<BR>grief, consoling.<BR>—शोक-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, sorrow-born,<BR>produced by sorrow.<BR>—शोक-दुःख-समन्वित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, affected by sorrow and pain.<BR>—शोक-<BR>नाश, अस्, m. ‘sorrow-destroying,’ the Aśoka tree.<BR>—शोक-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, sorrow-destroying, a<BR>remover of grief.<BR>—शोक-निहत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck<BR>down or overcome with grief, afflicted.<BR>—शोक-<BR>पङ्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. a slough of sorrow (i. e. grief<BR>compared to a quagmire).<BR>—शोक-परायण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, wholly given up to grief.<BR>—शोक-परिप्लुत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, overwhelmed with sorrow.<BR>—शोक-<BR>भङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘sorrow-break,’ dissipation or re-<BR>moval of sorrow.<BR>—शोक-भार, अस्, m. a weight or<BR>burden of sorrow.<BR>—शोक-मूर्छित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>stupified with sorrow, swooning with grief.<BR>—शोक-<BR>रुग्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, broken down with sorrow, in<BR>great distress, care-worn.<BR>—शोक-लालस, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>entirely given up to sorrow, abandoned to grief.<BR>—शोक-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, full of grief, sorrowful.<BR>—शोक-विनाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroying or removing<BR>sorrow.<BR>—शोक-विवर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, increasing<BR>sorrow.<BR>—शोक-संविग्न-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the heart distracted with grief.<BR>—शोक-सन्-<BR>तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, inflamed or consumed by sorrow.<BR>—शोक-सन्तप्त-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>mind is consumed by sorrow.<BR>—शोक-सागर, अस्,<BR>m. a sea of trouble, ocean of grief.<BR>—शोक-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. any circumstance or occasion of sorrow.<BR>—शोक-हारी, f. a kind of plant (= वन-वर्व-<BR>रिका).<BR>—शोकाकुल (˚क-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, over-<BR>whelmed or overcome with sorrow.<BR>—शोकाग्नि (˚क-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, or शोकानल (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m. the fire<BR>of sorrow, torment of grief, deep distress, violent<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">Page1013-a+ 80</a>]<BR>grief.<BR>—शोकाग्नि-सन्तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, inflamed or<BR>consumed by the fire of sorrow, tormented with<BR>violent grief.<BR>—शोकातिसार (˚क-अत्˚), अस्, m. dysen-<BR>tery or diarrhœa produced by grief.<BR>—शोकान्वित<BR>(˚क-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, filled with grief.<BR>—शोकाप-<BR>नुद (˚क-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, removing or alleviating<BR>sorrow, consoling.<BR>—शोकापनोद (˚क-अप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>removal of sorrow, dispelling grief; a teacher of holy<BR>wisdom.<BR>—शोकापह (˚क-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>stroying or removing sorrow.<BR>—शोकापहर्तृ (˚क-<BR>अप्˚), ता, त्री, तृ, taking away or removing sorrow,<BR>allaying or dissipating grief.<BR>—शोकाराति-भय-त्राण<BR>(˚क-अर्˚), अम्, n. protection or a protector from<BR>danger, enemies, and sorrow.<BR>—शोकारि (˚क-अरि),<BR>इस्, m. ‘grief-enemy,’ the Kadamba tree, Nauclea<BR>Kadamba.<BR>—शोकार्त (˚क-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted<BR>with sorrow, sorrow-stricken.<BR>—शोकाविष्ट (˚क-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, filled with grief, full of sorrow.<BR>—शोकैकमय (˚क-एक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, consisting<BR>of sorrow only.<BR>—शोकोत्पादन (˚क-उत्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, causing sorrow, producing grief, afflicting.<BR>—शो-<BR>कोद्भव (˚क-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, arising from sor-<BR>row, caused by grief.<BR>—शोकोन्मथित-चित्तात्मन्<BR>(˚क-उन्˚, ˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having the thoughts and<BR>mind agitated by sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1012-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकिन्
शोकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sorrowful, full of grief, sad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचक
शोचक, अस्, इका, अम्, afflictive, distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचत्
शोचत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sorrowing, grieving, lament-<BR>ing, bewailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचन|शोचनं
शोचन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, sorrowing, lamenting, sor-<BR>rowful; causing or producing sorrow, afflicting, griev-<BR>ing; (अम्), n. sorrow, grief, grieving, mourning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचनीय
शोचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be grieved or lamented;<BR>lamentable, deplorable, mournful.<BR>—शोचनीय-ता, f.<BR>the state of being condoled with or grieved for;<BR>lamentableness, deplorableness, mournfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचमान
शोचमान, अस्, आ, अम्, grieving, sorrowing, mourning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचयत्
1. शोचयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing grief or sorrow,<BR>distressing, afflicting, grieving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचित
शोचित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to grieve, made sad,<BR>saddened; afflicted; sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचितव्य
शोचितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be grieved or mourned,<BR>lamentable, deplorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचित्वा
शोचित्वा, ind. having grieved or mourned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्य
1. शोच्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. शोच्य see col. 2), to<BR>be lamented or bewailed, to be mourned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच् 3. शुच्, cl. 4. P. A. शुच्यति, -ते (Ved.<BR>also cl. 1. शोचति, -ते, and in some forms<BR>apparently cl. 6. शुचति), शुशोच, शुशुचे, शोचिष्यति,<BR>-ते, अशुचत् or अशोचीत्, अशोचिष्ट, शोचितुम् (Ved. Inf.<BR>शुचध्यै, other Vedic forms शोचा = शोचस्व, शु-<BR>शुग्धि = प्रकाशय, शुशुचित = दीप्यताम्, Ṛg-<BR>veda II. 2, 10), to shine, be bright or radiant; to brighten,<BR>illuminate; to burn, consume; to become clean or<BR>pure, be pure; to yield moisture, be wet; to decay,<BR>become fetid, stink: Caus. शोचयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>brighten, illuminate; to make pure, purify: Desid.<BR>शुशुचिषति, -ते, or शुशोचिषति, -ते: Intens. शोशुच्-<BR>यते, शोशोक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त|शुक्तं
शुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्. See p. 1012, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
4. शुच्, क्, f., Ved. brightness, lustre, radiance, (शुचा-<BR>शुचा, with reiterated lustre, Ṛg-veda III. 4, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचत्
शुचत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. shining, pure.<BR>—शु-<BR>चद्-रथ, अस्, m., Ved. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचन्ति
शुचन्ति, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a person under the<BR>especial protection of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचमान
शुचमान, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to modern<BR>scholars) observed, seen of men; shining, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 23, 8, and Nirukta X. 41<BR>= दीप्यमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचि|शुचिः
शुचि, इस्, इस्, इ, bright, resplendent, clear, clean,<BR>cleansed, purified, pure; white; virtuous, holy, in-<BR>nocent, unsullied, undefiled, pious; correct, honest,<BR>upright, true, trusty, faithful, correct, accurate, free<BR>from fault or error, guileless, gentle; (इस्), m. white<BR>(the colour); purity, purification (by ablution &c.);<BR>innocence, virtue, goodness; correctness, accuracy;<BR>acquittal; a pure man; a Brāhman; a faithful<BR>minister, true friend; N. of fire or of a particular<BR>fire (described as son of Antardhāna and brother of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">Page1013-b+ 80</a>]<BR>the fires called Pavamāna and Pāvaka); N. of a son<BR>of Agni; oblation to fire at the first feeding of an<BR>infant; the sun; the moon; the planet Venus or its<BR>regent [cf. शुक्र]; the hot season (i. e. the months<BR>Jyeṣṭha and Āṣāḍha); love, passion (= शृङ्गार-<BR>रस); the condition of a religious student; a par-<BR>ticular plant (= चित्रक); N. of Śiva; of a son of<BR>Bhṛgu; of a son of Śata-dyumna; of a son of<BR>Andhaka; of a son of Vipra; of the Indra of the<BR>fourteenth Manv-antara; (इस्), f., N. of a daughter<BR>of Tāmrā, wife of Kaśyapa (regarded as the parent<BR>of water-fowl).<BR>—शुचि-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. hav-<BR>ing a pure birth, pure-born.<BR>—शुचि-ता, f. or शुचि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. purity, brightness, cleanness, virtue,<BR>holiness, innocence.<BR>—शुचि-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>having bright teeth.<BR>—शुचि-द्रव्य, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—शुचि-द्रुम, अस्, m. ‘pure-tree,’ the sacred<BR>fig-tree (= अश्वत्थ).<BR>—शुचि-प्रणी, ईस्, f. ‘leading<BR>to purity,’ sipping water, rinsing the mouth, &c.<BR>—शुचि-बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having a brilliant<BR>relation (said of Soma as being related to fire).<BR>—शुचि-भ्राजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having a bright<BR>radiance, shining brightly.<BR>—शुचि-मणि, इस्, m.<BR>‘pure-jewel,’ crystal; a jewel worn on the head.<BR>—शुचि-मल्लिका, f. Arabian jasmine (= नव-मल्-<BR>लिका).<BR>—शुचि-मुखी, f. the plant Sanseviera Zeyla-<BR>nica.<BR>—शुचि-रोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, having pure or white<BR>light; (इस्), m. the moon.<BR>—शुचि-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, having pure splendor.<BR>—शुचि-वर्चाय, Nom. A.<BR>-वर्चायते, -यितुम्, to have pure splendor.<BR>—शुचि-<BR>वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, externally pure.<BR>—शुचि-व्रत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, whose acts are pure or holy, pious,<BR>virtuous; having pure sacrifices.<BR>—शुचि-श्रवस्, आस्,<BR>m. ‘having bright renown,’ N. of a Prajā-pati.<BR>—शुचि-स्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘smiling with white<BR>(teeth),’ smiling pleasantly, accompanied with a<BR>sweet smile.<BR>—शुची-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c.,<BR>to become pure, to purify one's self.<BR>—शुच्य्-उप-<BR>चार, अस्, आ, अम्, performing holy actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचित
2. शुचित, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed, purified, pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिस्
शुचिस्, इस्, n. = शोचिस्, light, lustre, radiance, &c.<BR>—शुचिष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, bright, radiant; (आन्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Kardama; epithet of Agni, (शु-<BR>चिष्मः, voc. c. in Ṛg-veda VI. 6, 4 = दीप्तिमन्,<BR>‘O resplendent being,’ i. e. Agni); (अती), f., N. of the<BR>mother of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचीय
शुचीय, Nom. A. शुचीयते, -यितुम्, to become<BR>pure or white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुक्वन
शुशुक्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining excessively,<BR>very brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुक्वनि
शुशुक्वनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. resplendent, shining,<BR>(Sāy. = दीपन-शील, Ṛg-veda VIII. 23, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुक्वस्
शुशुक्वस्, वान्, m., Ved. one who has purified or<BR>brightened, an illuminator, (Sāy. = शोचयिता, सर्-<BR>वस्य प्रकाशयिता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुचान
शुशुचान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining, bright, bril-<BR>liant, (Sāy. = दीप्यमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच
शोच, shining &c., in शुक्र-शोच, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचयत्
2. शोचयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to shine, bright-<BR>ening, illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिष्ठ
शोचिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining very much,<BR>most brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिस्
शोचिस्, इस्, n. light, lustre, radiance; a flame, blast<BR>of fire.<BR>—शोचिष्-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having (rays<BR>of) light for hair, having flaming locks; epithet of<BR>the sun; of Agni; (अस्), m. fire or its deity.<BR>—शो-<BR>चिष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of lustre,<BR>effulgent, radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्य
2. शोच्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. शोच्य see col. 1), to<BR>be cleansed; requiring purification, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्यक
शोच्यक, अस्, m. one who requires purifying, a<BR>low man, vile or base person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्य्
शुच्य् शुच्य् (also written चुच्य्), cl. 1. P.<BR>शुच्यति, शुशुच्य, शुच्यितुम्, to express<BR>or squeeze out juice, distil; to perform ablution (in<BR>the sense अभिषव, which some interpret to mean<BR>‘religious bathing’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीर|शुटीरः
शुटीर शुटीर (apparently not in use), a<BR>hero; [cf. शौटीर.]<BR>—शुटीर-ता, f. or शुटीर-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीर्य|शुटीर्यं|शुटीर्य्य|शुटीर्य्यं
शुटीर्य, अम्, n. valour, heroism; [cf. शौटीर्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुठ्
शुठ् शुठ् [cf. rts. शुण्ठ्, 4. शठ्], cl. 1. P.<BR>शोठति, शोठितुम्, to limp, be lame, go<BR>lame; to be impeded or obstructed; to resist; cl.<BR>10. P. शोठयति, -यितुम्, to be lazy or idle; to<BR>be dull or slow; [cf. Gr. κωλός..]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोठ|शोठः
शोठ, अस्, आ, अम्, foolish; idle, lazy; wicked,<BR>low; (अस्), m. a fool, blockhead; a sluggard, idler;<BR>a rogue, cheat, villain, criminal, sinner; a low man,<BR>one of a degraded tribe or occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठ्|शुंठ्
शुण्ठ् शुण्ठ्, cl. 1. P. शुण्ठति, शुण्ठितुम्,<BR>to limp, be lame [cf. rt. शुठ् above]; to<BR>dry, grow dry, be or become dry; cl. 10. P. शुण्ठ-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to dry, become dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठाचार्य
शुण्ठाचार्य, अस्, m., N. of a chief priest of Śiva<BR>(in the Dhūrta-nartaka).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठि|शुंठि|शुंठिः|शुण्ठिः
शुण्ठि, इस्, or शुण्ठी, f. dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठ्य|शुंठ्य
शुण्ठ्य, अम्, n. dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ड्|शुंड्
शुण्ड् शुण्ड्, cl. 1. P. शुण्डति, &c., to<BR>break; to disturb, harass, vex, torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ड|शुंड|शुंडः|शुण्डः
शुण्ड, अस्, m. (probably connected with the pre-<BR>ceding rt.), the juice exuding from the temples of an<BR>elephant in rut; an elephant's trunk; (आ), f. spirituous<BR>liquor; a place where spirituous liquor is sold, a<BR>tavern; an elephant's proboscis or trunk; the stalk<BR>of the lotus; a harlot, prostitute, bawd; a particular<BR>animal (perhaps a water-elephant or hippopotamus).<BR>—शुण्ड-रोह, अस्, m. a kind of grass (= भू-<BR>तृण).<BR>—शुण्डा-पान, अम्, n. a place where spirits<BR>are drunk or sold, a tavern, dram-shop.<BR>—शुण्डा-<BR>रोचनी, f. a species of plant (= रोचनिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डक|शुंडक|शुंडकः|शुण्डकः
शुण्डक, अस्, m. a distiller or seller of spirituous<BR>liquors; a military flute or fife (= युद्ध-वेणु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डार|शुंडार|शुंडारः|शुण्डारः
शुण्डार, अस्, m. a distiller, vintner; an elephant's<BR>trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डाल|शुंडाल|शुंडालः|शुण्डालः
शुण्डाल, अस्, m. ‘possessing a proboscis or trunk,’<BR>an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिका|शुंडिका
शुण्डिका, f. spirituous liquor, &c. (= शुण्डा above);<BR>the uvula or soft palate; a swelling or enlargement<BR>of any gland; [cf. गल-श्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिन्|शुंडिन्
शुण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing spirituous liquor;<BR>having a proboscis; (ई), m. a distiller, preparer and<BR>seller of spirituous liquors; an elephant.<BR>—शुण्डि-<BR>मूषिका, f. the musk-rat or shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डी
शुण्डी, f. a swelling or enlargement of any gland<BR>[cf. कण्ठ-श्˚, गल-श्˚]; the plant Heliotropium<BR>Indicum (= हस्ति-शुण्डी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रि|शुतुद्रिः
शुतुद्रि शुतु-द्रि, इस्, f. (according to Sāy.<BR>fr. शु = क्षिप्रम् + तु = तुन्ना with rt. द्रु), the<BR>Śatadru or Sutlej river. See शत-द्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्री
शुतु-द्री, f., Ved. = शुतु-द्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रु|शुतुद्रुः
शुतु-द्रु, उस्, or शुतु-द्रू, ऊस्, f. = शुतु-द्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुध्
शुध् शुध् (thought by some to be for<BR>an original श्वध्), cl. 4. P. (ep. also A.)<BR>शुध्यति (-ते), शुशोध, शोत्स्यति, अशुधत्, शोद्-<BR>धुम्, to be or become pure, be purified, be cleared,<BR>be cleansed or washed, be made clear: Pass. शुध्-<BR>यते, Aor. अशोधि: Caus. शोधयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अशूशुधत्, to make pure, purify, wash or clear off,<BR>cleanse, purge, refine, filter; to correct; to acquit;<BR>to make clear, explain; to examine, investigate:<BR>Desid. शुशुत्सति: Intens. शोशुध्यते, शोशोद्धि;<BR>[cf. Gr. καθ-αρό-ς, καθαίρ-ω, κάθαρσις, Κασταλία;<BR>Lat. cas-tu-s for cad-tu-s; Old Germ. heitar;<BR>Slav. cistu; Hib. cuidh, ‘clean, pure.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्ध|शुद्धं|शुद्धः
शुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, pure, clean, purified, cleansed;<BR>white, bright; stainless, innocent, guileless, simple,<BR>genuine, true, fair, honest; correct, faultless, blame-<BR>less; cleared, acquitted; simple, mere, only, alone;<BR>simple, unmixed (said of a note or sound in music);<BR>(in phil.) very, unequalled (= द्वितीय-रहित); non-<BR>nasal (said of letters); whetted, sharp (as an arrow);<BR>authorised, admitted; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva; (अम्),<BR>n. anything pure; pure spirit; rock-salt; black<BR>pepper.<BR>—शुद्ध-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, of pure prac-<BR>tices, acting virtuously, holy.<BR>—शुद्ध-कोटि, इस्, f.<BR>‘upright side,’ one of the sides of a right-angled<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-a" target="_blank">Page1014-a+ 81</a>]<BR>triangle.<BR>—शुद्ध-चैतन्य, अम्, n. pure intelli-<BR>gence (the basis of the divine and individual intelli-<BR>gence according to the Vedānta).<BR>—शुद्ध-जङ्घ,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having clean legs or thighs,’ an ass.<BR>—शुद्-<BR>ध-ता, f. or शुद्ध-त्व, अम्, n. purity, cleanness,<BR>correctness, faultlessness, &c.<BR>—शुद्ध-दत्, अन्,<BR>अती, अत्, white-toothed, having handsome teeth.<BR>—शुद्ध-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, pure-minded, having a<BR>pure understanding.<BR>—शुद्ध-बध, अस्, m. simple<BR>putting to death, killing in any ordinary way; (ac-<BR>cording to Rāghavānanda on Manu IX. 279 =<BR>शिरश्-छेद, beheading.)<BR>—शुद्ध-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>a state of purity, being pure; (अस्, आ, अम्), having a<BR>pure mind or disposition, pure-minded.<BR>—शुद्ध-<BR>मति, इस्, इस्, इ, pure-minded, free from guile, sincere,<BR>honest; intelligent; (इस्), m. one of the twenty-four<BR>Jinas of the past age.<BR>—शुद्ध-मांस, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of condiment or strong seasoning made with<BR>pieces of meat, Asa Fetida, turmeric, &c.<BR>—शुद्-<BR>ध-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, pure-coloured, of a good<BR>caste, &c.; having pure or non-nasal letters.<BR>—शुद्-<BR>ध-वल्लिका, f. a kind of plant, Menispermum Gla-<BR>brum; another plant (= गुडूची).<BR>—शुद्ध-वासस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, dressed in clean garments, having pure<BR>vesture.<BR>—शुद्धात्मन् (˚ध-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, pure-<BR>minded; (आ), m. the pure soul or spirit; epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—शुद्धानन्द (˚ध-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘pure-<BR>joy,’ N. of a preceptor.<BR>—शुद्धानुमान (˚ध-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘correct inference,’ a figure of rhetoric.<BR>—शुद्धान्त (˚ध-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘pure or sacred<BR>interior,’ the private or women's apartments (espe-<BR>cially in the palace of a king), a harem, seraglio; a<BR>king's wife or concubine; (आ), f. a king's wife, queen.<BR>—शुद्धान्त-चारिन्, ई, m. an attendant or servant of<BR>the private apartments.<BR>—शुद्धान्त-पालक, अस्, m.<BR>‘seraglio-guardian,’ a guard of the private or women's<BR>apartments, attendant on women, eunuch.<BR>—शुद्-<BR>धान्त-युज्, क्, f. (?), change of mode or key in<BR>music.<BR>—शुद्धापह्नुति (˚ध-अप्˚), इस्, f. ‘pure<BR>denial or turning off,’ a particular figure of rhetoric,<BR>(denial of any quality or property for the sake of<BR>applying some other, e. g. this is not the moon, it<BR>is a lotus of the heavenly Ganges.)<BR>—शुद्धोदन<BR>(˚ध-ओद्˚), अस्, m. ‘pure-food,’ N. of a king of Kapila-<BR>vastu (said to have belonged to the race of Ikṣvāku;<BR>he was father of the great Buddha Śākya-muni, see<BR>बुद्ध).<BR>—शुद्धोदन-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of Śud-<BR>dhodana,’ epithet of Śākya (the great Buddha or<BR>founder of the Buddhist religion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1013-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धि|शुद्धिः
शुद्धि, इस्, f. purity, cleanness, holiness, freedom<BR>from defilement; purification, expiation, cleansing;<BR>a particular expiatory and purificatory rite (described<BR>as a kind of Śrāddha performed at the cost of a<BR>person who needs purification from some defilement,<BR>when a stated number of Brāhmans are fed); clear-<BR>ing, clearance, innocence (established by ordeal or<BR>trial), acquittal; clearing (of expences), paying off<BR>arrears; quittance; retaliation; rectification, correc-<BR>tion, correctness, accuracy, truth, certainty; subtrac-<BR>tion; N. of Durgā; of one of the Śaktis of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Dākṣāyaṇī as worshipped at Kapāla-mocana.<BR>—शुद्धि-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing purity, purify-<BR>ing, correcting.<BR>—शुद्धि-कौमुदी, f., N. of a work<BR>on purificatory rites by Govindānanda.<BR>—शुद्धि-<BR>चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a treatise on the observances of<BR>mourning and the purificatory rites thereto belong-<BR>ing.<BR>—शुद्धि-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—शुद्धि-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a work on purifi-<BR>cation (being part of Raghu-nandana's Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—शुद्धि-दीपिका, f., N. of a work by Śrī-nivāsa<BR>on the position of stars considered favourable for<BR>marriages, journeys, &c.<BR>—शुद्धि-निरूपण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the seventh chapter of the Yoga-vāsiṣṭha-<BR>sāra.<BR>—शुद्धि-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a sheet or paper of<BR>corrections, errata list; a certificate of purification by<BR>penance.<BR>—शुद्धि-प्रदीप and शुद्धि-मयू-<BR>ख, अस्, m., N. of two works.<BR>—शुद्धि-भृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, possessing purity, free from soil, clean, clear;<BR>pure, virtuous.<BR>—शुद्धि-रत्नाकर(˚न-आक्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a work.<BR>—शुद्धि-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a work by Rudra-dhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्ध्वा
शुद्ध्वा, ind. having purified, having cleared, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोत्स्यत्
शोत्स्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to cleanse or<BR>purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोद्धव्य
शोद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cleansed or purified;<BR>to be corrected, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोध|शोधः
शोध, अस्, m. purification, cleansing; correction;<BR>payment; retaliation.<BR>—शोध-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a<BR>sheet or paper of corrections; [cf. शुद्धि-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधक|शोधकः
शोधक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, purificatory, cleans-<BR>ing, cleaning, purgative; corrective; (अस्), m. a<BR>purifier, refiner; a corrector (in arithmetic or algebra),<BR>the subtrahend, the quantity to be subtracted from a<BR>number to render it capable of yielding an exact<BR>square root; (अम्), n. a particular kind of earth (=<BR>कङ्कुष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधन|शोधनं|शोधनः
शोधन, अस्, ई, अम्, cleaning, purifying, cleansing,<BR>refining, purgative; (अम्), n. the act of cleaning,<BR>cleansing, purifying, refining; clearance, correction,<BR>freeing from faults, clearing away errors, removing<BR>or eradicating anything prejudicial or erroneous;<BR>precise determination; the cleansing of a sore or<BR>wound; the refining of metals, a sort of refining<BR>practised for chemical or medicinal purposes, (exposing<BR>metals to heat and then sprinkling them with the<BR>urine of cows, &c.); payment, clearance or discharge<BR>of a debt, quittance, paying off arrears, acquittance;<BR>expiation; retaliation, punishment; (in arithmetic)<BR>subtraction; excrement, feces, ordure; green vitriol;<BR>(अस्), m. the lime (= निम्बूक); a kind of गण्डूष,<BR>q. v. (swallowing or rinsing the mouth ?); (ई), f. a<BR>broom, brush; a kind of plant (= ताम्र-वल्ली);<BR>another plant (= नीली).<BR>—शोधनी-वीज, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of plant (= जय-पाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधनक|शोधनकः
शोधनक, अस्, m., N. of an officer in an assize<BR>court, (Mṛc-chakaṭikā, Act 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधनीय|शोधनीयः
शोधनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cleansed or purified;<BR>to be corrected; to be refined; to be cleared off or<BR>discharged; to be paid off or liquidated (as a debt);<BR>payable, due; to be subtracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधयत्
शोधयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, making clean, purifying,<BR>cleansing, purging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधयित्वा
शोधयित्वा, ind. having cleared or purified, &c.;<BR>having paid or discharged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधित|शोधितं
शोधित, अस्, आ, अम्, cleaned, cleansed; purified,<BR>purged; refined; strained, filtered; corrected; ex-<BR>cused; cleared off, discharged, paid off, liquidated;<BR>acquitted, absolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधिन्
शोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, purifying, clearing; requiting,<BR>settling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोध्य|शोध्यः
शोध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be purified or cleansed, to<BR>be cleaned or refined; to be cleared off or discharged;<BR>payable; due; to be subtracted; (अस्), m. an accused<BR>person, one to be cleared or tried; (अम्), n. a con-<BR>stant number to be subtracted in some astronomical<BR>computations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्
शुन् शुन्, cl. 6. P. शुनति, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन|शुनः
शुन शुन, अस्, आ, अम् (probably fr. rt. श्वि),<BR>white, pure, bright (Ved.; cf. श्वेत); causing pros-<BR>perity or happiness, auspicious (Ved.); (अम्), ind.<BR>happily, auspiciously (Ved.; Sāy. = सुखम्); (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Vāyu (Ved.); a dog, (fr. श्वन्.)<BR>—शुन-<BR>होत्र, अस्, m., N. of the author of the hymns Ṛg-<BR>veda VI. 33, 34 (having the patronymic Bhārad-<BR>vāja).<BR>—शुनासीरीय or शुनासीर्य, अम्, n. a par-<BR>ticular sacrificial oblation (said to be offered in the<BR>thirteenth month or Mala-māsa, and probably in<BR>honour of Śuna and Sīra).<BR>—शुना-सीरौ, m. du.,<BR>Ved. Śuna and Sīra, N. of two Vedic gods (addressed<BR>in Ṛg-veda IV. 57, and identified by Yāska with<BR>Vāyu and Āditya; according to other authorities<BR>Indra and Vāyu or Indra and Sūrya are meant; but<BR>according to another view Sīra may perhaps denote<BR>‘a ploughshare,’ and Śuna some part of a plough).<BR>—शुनेषित (˚ना-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (probably)<BR>borne along or carried by dogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनःपुच्छ
शुनः-पुच्छ, अस्, m. (properly fr. शुनः, gen.<BR>c. of श्वन् + पुच्छ), ‘dog-tailed,’ N. of one of the<BR>three sons of Ṛcīka (or according to the Aitareya-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">Page1014-c+ 78</a>]<BR>Brāhmaṇa the eldest of the three sons of Ajīgarta);<BR>N. of the author of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनःशेप|शुनःशेपः
शुनः-शेप or शुनः-शेफ, अस्, m. (शुनः,<BR>gen. c. of श्वन्), ‘dog-tailed,’ N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi<BR>(having the patronymic Ājigarti, as son of Ajigarta<BR>or Ajīgarta, and regarded as the author of the hymns<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 24-30, IX. 3; according to a legend<BR>told in the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa VII. 13-18, king<BR>Hariścandra, whose priest was Viśvā-mitra, being<BR>childless, made a vow that on obtaining a son he<BR>would sacrifice him to the god Varuṇa; a son was<BR>then born to him named Rohita, but Hariścandra<BR>put off on various pretexts the fulfilment of his vow,<BR>and when he at length consented to perform it, his<BR>son declined being sacrificed, and retiring to the<BR>forest passed six years there until he met a poor<BR>Brāhman Ṛṣi named Ajīgarta, who had three sons,<BR>the second of whom, Śunaḥ-śepha, was purchased by<BR>Rohita for a hundred cows to serve as a substitute<BR>for himself; Varuṇa having accepted him as a ransom,<BR>he was about to be sacrificed, Viśvā-mitra being Hotṛ<BR>priest, when he saved himself by reciting verses in<BR>praise of various deities, and was received into the<BR>family of Viśvā-mitra as one of his sons under the<BR>name of Deva-rāta, q. v.: the legend is different in<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa, which makes Ambarīṣa, king of<BR>Ayodhyā, perform a sacrifice, the victim of which is<BR>stolen by Indra; this king is described as wandering<BR>over the earth in search of either the real victim or<BR>a substitute until he meets with a Brāhman named<BR>Ṛcīka, from whom he purchases his middle son,<BR>Śunaḥ-śepha, who is about to be sacrificed, when<BR>Viśvā-mitra saves him by teaching him a prayer to<BR>Agni and two hymns to Indra and Viṣṇu; see<BR>Rāmāyaṇa I. 61, 62); (अम्), n. the genital organ<BR>of a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनक|शुनकः
शुनक, अस्, m. a young dog; a dog; N. of a<BR>descendant of Bhṛgu; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a family;<BR>[cf. शौनक.]<BR>—शुनक-चञ्चुका, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= क्षुद्र-चञ्चु).<BR>—शुनक-चिल्ली, f. a kind<BR>of pot-herb (= श्वान-चिल्लिका).<BR>—शुनक-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. the son of Śunaka, i. e. Śaunaka, (also applied<BR>to Gṛtsamada, who is elsewhere described as the<BR>father of Śunaka.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनाशीर|शुनाशीरः
शुनाशीर or शुनासीर, अस्, m., N. of Indra, (also<BR>written सुनासीर, q. v., cf. शुना-सीरौ under शुन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनि|शुनिः
शुनि, इस्, m. (fr. श्वन्), a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनी
शुनी, f. a female dog, bitch, (see under श्वन्);<BR>a kind of gourd (= कुष्माण्डी).<BR>—शुनिन्-धम,<BR>see Vopa-deva XXVI. 54.<BR>—शुनिन्-धय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (शुनि for शुनी), sucking a bitch, suckled by a<BR>bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनीर|शुनीरः
शुनीर, अस्, m. a number of female dogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनोलाङ्गूल
शुनो-लाङ्गूल, अस्, m. (fr. शुनः, gen. c. of<BR>श्वन् + लाङ्गूल), N. of the youngest of the three<BR>sons of Ṛcīka (or of the three sons of Ajīgarta,<BR>according to the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa; cf. शुनः-<BR>पुच्छ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्य|शुन्यं
1. शुन्य, अम्, n. (for 2. शुन्य see below), a<BR>number of dogs or female dogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्|शुंध्
शुन्ध् शुन्ध् (connected with rt. शुध्);<BR>cl. 1. P. A. शुन्धति, -ते, शुशुन्ध,<BR>शुशुन्धे, शुन्धितुम्, to purify, make clean or pure,<BR>cleanse (P., according to some also A.); to be or be-<BR>come pure, be purified, be cleansed (A.); cl. 10. P.<BR>(according to some also A.) शुन्धयति (-ते), -यि-<BR>तुम्, to purify, cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्धावत्
शुन्धा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (thought by some to be<BR>fr. a lost Nom. शुन्ध्य, meaning ‘to desire purifi-<BR>cation’), Ved. ‘possessed of desire for purification,’<BR>sacred, holy, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्यु|शुंध्युः|शुन्ध्युः
शुन्ध्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. ‘desirous of purifica-<BR>tion,’ purifying; pure, bright; (उस्), m., N. of Agni<BR>or fire, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 124, 4, an<BR>Āditya or a kind of water-fowl); (उस्), f. a mare,<BR>(the chariot of the Sun is said to be drawn by seven<BR>mares); [cf. perhaps Lat. castus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्य|शुन्यं
शुन्य 2. शुन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (more usually<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-a" target="_blank">Page1015-a+ 79</a>]<BR>written शून्य, q. v.; for 1. शुन्य see p. 1014,<BR>col. 3), empty, void; (अम्), n. a cypher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुप्
शुप् शुप्, (in grammar) a technical term<BR>for the affix उ, the characteristic sign of the eighth<BR>class of verbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुफाहिल
शुफाहिल शुफाहिल, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
शुभ् 1. शुभ् (perhaps for an original<BR>श्वभ्, cf. rts. शुध्, शुम्भ्), cl. 1. A.<BR>शोभते (rarely cl. 6. P. शुभति or cl. 1. P. शो-<BR>भति, but this latter is referred to rt. 3. शुभ्), शु-<BR>शोभ, शुशुभे, शोभिष्यति, -ते, अशुभत्, अशो-<BR>भिष्ट, शोभितुम् (Ved. Inf. शोभसे, शुभम्,<BR>शुभे, see 2. शुभ्), to shine, be splendid; to be<BR>beautiful, look beautiful or handsome, appear to ad-<BR>vantage; to be gay or happy; to be victorious,<BR>triumph over: Caus. शोभयति, -ते (Ved. also शु-<BR>भयति), -यितुम्, Aor. अशूशुभत्, to cause to<BR>shine, ornament, decorate: to adorn one's self (A.);<BR>to shine (?): Desid. शुशोभिषते, -ति, or शुशुभि-<BR>षते, -ति: Intens. शोशुभ्यते, शोशोब्धि, to shine<BR>intensely; [cf. Gr. κομψός, κομ-μός, κομέω; Old<BR>Germ. sūbar, ‘pure;’ Mod. Germ. sauber; Lith.<BR>źibbu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
2. शुभ्, प्, f., Ved. splendor, beauty, brilliancy,<BR>glory; happiness; victory, triumph, (शुभे, for<BR>victory or conquest); an ornament; an auspicious<BR>offering; a brilliant place of sacrifice, (Sāy. = शो-<BR>भन देव-यजन, Ṛg-veda I. 23, 11); water<BR>or a brilliant chariot (= उदक or रथ, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 167, 6, &c.).<BR>—शुभं-या, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>causing happiness, bestowing blessings, benevolent<BR>(said of the wind; Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 3, 6. ex-<BR>plains शुभं-ये by शुभस्य प्रापयित्रे, con-<BR>necting या with rt. 1. या in the sense of प्रापणे).<BR>—शुभं-यावन्, आ, &c., Ved. going to splendor<BR>or happiness (said of the Maruts, Sāy. = शोभन-<BR>गति, शोभनं गन्ता; cf. ऋण-यावन्).<BR>—शु-<BR>भस्-पति, इस्, m. lord or preserver of splendor,<BR>(Sāy. = शोभनस्य कर्मणः पालकः); (ई), m.<BR>du., Ved. epithet of the two Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ|शुभं|शुभः
शुभ, अस्, आ, अम्, bright, shining, splendid, hand-<BR>some, beautiful; auspicious, fortunate, lucky, happy,<BR>well, right, good, virtuous, eminent, distinguished;<BR>learned, versed in the Vedas; (अस्), m. the twenty-<BR>third of the astronomical Yogas; a city in the sky,<BR>(see व्योमचारि-पुर; said to be also fem. and<BR>neut.); (आ), f. light, lustre; beauty; desire; N. of<BR>a female friend and companion of the goddess Umā;<BR>an assembly of the gods; bamboo-manna; white<BR>Dūrvā grass; the Śamī tree; the yellow pigment<BR>गो-रोचना; a particular plant, = प्रियङ्गु; (अम्),<BR>n. anything bright or beautiful, auspiciousness; hap-<BR>piness, hail, welfare, good fortune, good; an orna-<BR>ment; water, rain, (Sāy. = अलङ्कार or उदक,<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 82, 5); a fragrant wood (= पद्म-<BR>काष्ठ); [cf. Pers. خوب khūb.]<BR>—शुभ-कर,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing welfare, producing good,<BR>propitious, &c.<BR>—शुभ-कर्मन्, अ, n. a good or<BR>virtuous act, auspicious action; reputable occupation<BR>or employment.<BR>—शुभ-कृत्, त्, m. epithet of the<BR>thirty-sixth or tenth year of Jupiter's cycle of sixty<BR>years.<BR>—शुभ-क्षण, अस्, अम्, m. n. an auspicious<BR>or lucky moment.<BR>—शुभ-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going<BR>well or beautifully, graceful, elegant; propitious, for-<BR>tunate.<BR>—शुभ-गन्धक, अस्, आ, अम्, good-<BR>scented; (अम्), n. gum-myrrh.<BR>—शुभ-ग्रह, अस्,<BR>m. an auspicious planet, lucky star (such as Jupiter,<BR>Venus, Mercury, and the moon when more than half<BR>full).<BR>—शुभग्रहोदय (˚ह-उद्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>rising of an auspicious planet.<BR>—शुभङ्-कर, अस्,<BR>आ or ई, अम्, conferring happiness or fortune; auspicious,<BR>propitious; (ई), f. Pārvatī.<BR>—शुभ-जानि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>having a beautiful wife.<BR>—शुभ-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>granting happiness, propitious, auspicious; (अस्), m.<BR>the sacred fig-tree (= अश्वत्थ).<BR>—शुभ-दन्ती, f.<BR>a woman with good teeth; the female elephant of<BR>Puṣpa-danta or of the north-west quarter, (also read<BR>शुभ्र-दन्ती.)<BR>—शुभ-दृष्टि, इस्, f. an auspicious<BR>look or aspect.<BR>—शुभ-धर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-b" target="_blank">Page1015-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—शुभ-नामा, f. epithet of the fifth lunar night.<BR>—शुभ-पत्त्रिका, f. ‘having auspicious leaves,’ a<BR>kind of shrub (= शाल-पर्णी).<BR>—शुभ-फल, अम्,<BR>n. auspicious result, good or happy consequence.<BR>—शुभम्-भावुक, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘disposed to be<BR>bright,’ resplendent, decorated, ornamented.<BR>—शुभ-<BR>योग, अस्, m. a particular astronomical Yoga, (see<BR>शुभ.)<BR>—शुभ-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>an auspicious sign or symptom; marked or charac-<BR>terized by felicity.<BR>—शुभ-लग्न, अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>rising of an auspicious constellation, a lucky moment.<BR>—शुभ-वार्त्ता, f. good news.<BR>—शुभ-वासन,<BR>अस्, m. auspicious perfuming; perfume for the mouth.<BR>—शुभ-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular religious<BR>observance (kept on the twelfth day in one of the<BR>halves of the month Kārttika).<BR>—शुभ-शंसिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, indicative of good luck.<BR>—शुभ-शील, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well-disposed, having a good disposition.<BR>—शु-<BR>भ-संयुत, अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with prosperity<BR>or happiness, blissful.<BR>—शुभ-सप्तमी-व्रत, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a particular religious observance.<BR>—शुभ-<BR>सूचनी, f. ‘indicating good,’ N. of a female deity<BR>worshipped by women in times of calamity, (she is<BR>also called Su-vacanī.)<BR>—शुभ-स्थली, f. any<BR>auspicious place, a room or hall in which sacrifices are<BR>offered.<BR>—शुभाक्ष (˚भ-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘auspicious-<BR>eyed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शुभागम (˚भ-आग्˚),<BR>अम्, n. epithet of certain Tantra works regarded as<BR>especially orthodox.<BR>—शुभाङ्ग (˚भ-अङ्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, handsome-limbed, beautifully formed, handsome,<BR>elegant; (अस्), m., N. of a lexicographer; of another<BR>person; (ई), f. a handsome woman; N. of Rati<BR>(wife of the god of love); of the wife of Kuvera<BR>(god of wealth).<BR>—शुभाचार (˚भ-आच्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, pure in practices or observances, virtuous; (आ),<BR>f. epithet of a female attendant on Umā; [cf. शु-<BR>भा.]<BR>—शुभाञ्जन (˚भ-अञ्˚), अस्, m. the tree<BR>Hyperanthera Moringa, (see शोभाञ्जन.)<BR>—शु-<BR>भानन (˚भ-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, handsome-faced,<BR>good-looking; (आ), f. a handsome woman.<BR>—शु-<BR>भानन्दा (˚भ-आन्˚), f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—शु-<BR>भान्वित (˚भ-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with<BR>prosperity or good fortune, happy, prosperous.<BR>—शु-<BR>भापाङ्गा (˚भ-अप्˚), f. ‘a woman who has beauti-<BR>ful eye-corners,’ a beautiful woman.<BR>—शुभाशुभ<BR>(˚भ-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, prosperous and unfortunate,<BR>good and evil; (अम्), n. good and evil, good and<BR>bad fortune, weal and woe.<BR>—शुभाशुभ-लक्-<BR>षण, अम्, n. a mark or sign of good or bad<BR>fortune, a good or evil omen.<BR>—शुभेतर (˚भ-<BR>इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, other than auspicious, unlucky, in-<BR>auspicious; evil, bad.<BR>—शुभोदर्क (˚भ-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having prosperous results or happy con-<BR>sequences; causing happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंया
शुभं-या, शुभं-यावन्. See under 2. शुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंयु|शुभंयुः
शुभंयु, उस्, उस्, उ, happy, fortunate, pros-<BR>perous, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभान
शुभान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining bright, brilliant;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. (according to some) epithet of the<BR>Maruts, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 165, 3.<BR>शुभानैः = शोभमानैर् वचनैः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभिका
शुभिका, f., Ved. a garland formed of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्र|शुभ्रं|शुभ्रः
शुभ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, radiant, bright;<BR>white; (अस्), m. white (the colour); sandal; (अम्),<BR>n. silver; talc; green vitriol; rock or fossil salt;<BR>(आ), f. the Ganges; crystal; bamboo-manna; [cf.<BR>Old Germ. sūbar; Mod Germ. sauber, ‘clean;’<BR>Angl. Sax. syfr.]<BR>—शुभ्र-कृत्, त्, m. the thirty-<BR>sixth year of Jupiter's cycle; [cf. शुभ-कृत्.]<BR>—शुभ्र-खादि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having shining<BR>rings, having bright weapons (said of the Maruts;<BR>Sāy. = शोभनायुध or शोभन-हविष्क, Ṛg-<BR>veda VIII. 20, 4).<BR>—शुभ्र-ता, f. or शुभ्र-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. whiteness.<BR>—शुभ्र-दन्ती, f. the female<BR>elephant of Puṣpa-danta, the elephant of the north-<BR>west quarter, (see शुभ-दन्ती.)<BR>—शुभ्र-रश्मि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘white-rayed,’ the moon.<BR>—शुभ्र-शस्तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining very much, (according to<BR>some either for शुभ्र-शस्त-तम or for शुभ्र-<BR>शस्-तम.)<BR>—शुभ्रांशु (˚र-अं˚), उस्, m. ‘white-<BR>rayed,’ the moon; camphor.<BR>—शुभ्रालु (˚र-आलु),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">Page1015-c+ 78</a>]<BR>उस्, m. a white esculent root; a particular plant<BR>with a tuberous root (= महिष-कन्द).<BR>—शु-<BR>भ्रा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing radiance,<BR>shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रि|शुभ्रिः
शुभ्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, shining bright (Ved., Sāy. = शो-<BR>भन); (इस्), m. an epithet of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रिका
शुभ्रिका, f., see Vopa-deva IV. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभ
शोभ, अस्, आ, अम्, bright, brilliant, handsome;<BR>(आ), f. light, lustre, radiance, splendor, sheen, bril-<BR>liancy; beauty, elegance, grace, comeliness; dis-<BR>tinguished merit; turmeric; the yellow pigment<BR>गो-रोचना; a species of the Kṛti metre.<BR>—शोभ-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing lustre, beautifying; (त्), m. the<BR>thirty-seventh (or sixth) year of Jupiter's cycle of<BR>sixty years [cf. शुभ-कृत्]; the marking-nut<BR>plant.<BR>—शोभा-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing lustre,<BR>beautifying.<BR>—शोभाञ्जन (˚भा-अञ्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>tree Hyperanthera Moringa (commonly called Śa-<BR>jinā; it is much valued for its various properties;<BR>the legumes, blossoms, and leaves are esculent;<BR>the root of the young tree is used as a substitute for<BR>horse-radish as well as a stimulant in medicine, and<BR>the expressed oil of the seeds is said to relieve<BR>arthritic pains; it has a great many synonyms; cf.<BR>शिग्रु, नील-शिग्रु, काक्षीवक, जन-प्रिय, च-<BR>क्षुष्य, &c.).<BR>—शोभा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, full of<BR>lustre or beauty; beautiful.<BR>—शोभा-वती, f., N. of<BR>a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभथ
शोभथ, Ved. splendor, (used only in the inst.<BR>c. शोभथा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभन|शोभनं|शोभनः
शोभन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, adorning, causing to<BR>look beautiful, shining, splendid; beautiful, hand-<BR>some, (sometimes used ironically); richly dressed or<BR>ornamented; propitious, auspicious; virtuous, de-<BR>corous, good, moral; (अस्), m. a burnt offering for<BR>auspicious results; epithet of Śiva; epithet of the<BR>eleventh year of Jupiter's cycle; a planet; the fifth<BR>of the astronomical Yogas; (आ), f. turmeric; the<BR>yellow pigment गो-रोचना; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>adorning or causing to look beautiful; the being<BR>bright or handsome, brilliance, sheen; a lotus.<BR>—शोभन-वाह, अस्, आ, अम्, having splendid car-<BR>riers or horses.<BR>—शोभनाचरित (˚न-आच्˚), अम्, n.<BR>virtuous practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभनक|शोभनकः
शोभनक, अस्, m. the tree Hyperanthera Mo-<BR>ringa (= शोभाञ्जन above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभनीय
शोभनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be beautified or adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभमान
शोभमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, looking beauti-<BR>ful or handsome, splendid, fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभयत्
शोभयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to shine, orna-<BR>menting, decorating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभस्
शोभस्, अस्, n., Ved. splendor, beauty, (the dat.<BR>c. शोभसे is used as a Ved. Inf.; Sāy. = शोभनार्-<BR>थम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभित
शोभित, अस्, आ, अम्, beautiful, adorned, decorated,<BR>trimmed, made splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभिन्
शोभिन्, ई, इनी, इ, shining, brilliant, beautiful,<BR>handsome, distinguished, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभिष्ठ
शोभिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most brilliant, very<BR>handsome or beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
शुभ् 3. शुभ् (sometimes written शुन्भ्<BR>or शुम्भ् = rts. सुभ्, सुन्भ्, सुम्भ्),<BR>cl. 1. P. शोभति, शुन्भति, &c., to shine [cf. rt.<BR>1. शुभ्]; to speak; to strike, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ्|शुंभ्
शुम्भ् शुम्भ्, cl. 6. P. A. शुम्भति,<BR>-ते, शुशुम्भ, शुम्भिष्यति, शुम्-<BR>भितुम्, Ved. to shine, be brilliant; to decorate;<BR>cl. 1. P. शुम्भति, &c., to shine; to speak; to<BR>strike, injure, kill, (in these senses = rts. 3. शुभ्,<BR>सुभ्, सुम्भ्): Caus. A., Ved. शुभयते, -यितुम्,<BR>to decorate one's self, to shine; [cf. probably Gr.<BR>κομψός.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भन
शुम्भन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. shining, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भमान
शुम्भमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. decorating, adorn-<BR>ing; handsome, beautiful, (Sāy. = शोभमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भान
शुम्भान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. decorating, illumi-<BR>nating, (Sāy. = शोभयत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भित
शुम्भित. See ब्रह्म-शुम्भित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ|शुंभ|शुंभः|शुम्भः
शुम्भ शुम्भ, अस्, m., N. of an Asura or<BR>demon slain by Durgā, (he was son of Gaveṣṭhin<BR>and grandson of Prahlāda.)<BR>—शुम्भ-घातिनी or<BR>शुम्भ-मर्दिनी, f. ‘Śumbha-killing,’ an epithet<BR>of Durgā.<BR>—शुम्भ-पुर, अम्, ई, n. f. ‘the city<BR>of the Asura Śumbha,’ a town and district, (the<BR>modern Sambhalpūr in the district of Gondwāna;<BR>it is also called Eka-cakra and Hari-gṛha.)<BR>—शुम्-<BR>भ-बध or शुम्भ-वध, अस्, m. ‘killing of<BR>Śumbha,’ N. of the tenth chapter of the Devī-<BR>māhātmya of the Mārkaṇḍeya-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुर
शुर शुर, अस्, m. (for शूर, q. v.), a hero;<BR>a lion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुरुध्
शुरुध् शुरुध्, धस्, f. pl., Ved. gifts,<BR>treasures, riches; waters, water, (Sāy. = आपः, Ṛg-<BR>veda IV. 23, 8); preventers or alleviators of pain or<BR>sorrow, (Sāy. = शुचेर् दुःखस्य प्रतिरोद्धारः<BR>or शोकस्य रोधयितृ); herbs or other remedies<BR>used to allay pain; exhilarating drinks (according to<BR>some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क्
शुल्क् शुल्क्, cl. 10. P. शुल्कयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to pay, give; to gain, acquire; to<BR>abandon, leave, forsake; to create (सर्जने); to<BR>narrate, tell; [cf. rt. श्वल्क्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क|शुल्कं|शुल्कः
शुल्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. toll, tax, duty, customs<BR>(especially money levied at ferries, passes, and roads);<BR>a sum of money, price, (Sāy. = मूल्य); property,<BR>wealth, (Sāy. = धन); gain, profit; money ad-<BR>vanced to ratify a bargain; money given to the<BR>parents of the bride (originally as purchase-price); a<BR>present made by a bridegroom to his bride; nuptial<BR>present; a marriage-settlement or dower; a wife's<BR>perquisites or private property (such as the profits of<BR>household labour, domestic utensils, milch cattle,<BR>ornaments, servants, &c.).<BR>—शुल्क-खण्डन, अम्,<BR>n. defrauding the revenue.<BR>—शुल्क-ग्राहक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, or शुल्क-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, receiving a<BR>toll or duty.<BR>—शुल्क-द, अस्, m. the giver of a<BR>nuptial present, an affianced suitor.<BR>—शुल्क-मो-<BR>षण, अम्, n. stealing or defrauding the revenue.<BR>—शुल्क-शाला, f. a custom-house; [cf. शौल्क-<BR>शालिक.]<BR>—शुल्क-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, having (merely)<BR>the name of a nuptial gratuity.<BR>—शुल्क-स्थान, अम्,<BR>n. a toll-office, custom-house (Manu VIII. 400);<BR>any object of taxation or duty.<BR>—शुल्क-हानि, इस्,<BR>f. loss or forfeiture of wages or dower, &c.<BR>—शुल्का-<BR>भिधान (˚क-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, = शुल्क-सञ्ज्ञ.<BR>—शुल्कावाप्त (˚क-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, obtained as a<BR>dowry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्किक
शुल्किक शुल्किक, अस्, m., N. of a country<BR>or district; [cf. शौल्किकेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्ल|शुल्लं
शुल्ल शुल्ल, अम्, n. (for शुल्व), a cord, rope,<BR>string; copper (= ताम्र; cf. शुल्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व्
शुल्व् शुल्व् (also written शुल्ब्), cl. 10. P.<BR>शुल्वयति, -यितुम्, to send away, dis-<BR>miss; to measure; to create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व|शुल्वं
शुल्व or शुल्ब, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 95. fr. rt. 1. शुच्), a rope, cord, string, (said to<BR>be also अस्, m., आ or ई, f.); copper, a copper vessel;<BR>a sacrificial observance; institute, law, custom; a<BR>quantity of water; (आनि), n. pl., N. of a Pariśiṣṭa<BR>of the Yajur-veda; [cf. शुल्विक.]<BR>—शुल्व-ज, अम्,<BR>n. brass.<BR>—शुल्व-दीपिका, f., N. of a work.<BR>—शुल्व-<BR>परिशिष्ट and शुल्व-वार्त्तिक and शुल्व-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of works.<BR>—शुल्वारि (˚व-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of copper,’ sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्विक
शुल्विक, आनि, n. pl., N. of a Pariśiṣṭa of the<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुक्वस्
शुशुक्वस् शुशुक्वस्. See under rt. 3. शुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुक्षणि
शुशुक्षणि शुशुक्षणि in आ-शुशुक्षणि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुमा
शुशुमा शुशुमा, f., N. of the wife of Śukra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुलूकयातु
शुशुलूकयातु शुशुलूक-यातु, उस्, m., Ved. a<BR>demon in the shape of an owlet, (according to Sāy.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">Page1016-b+ 79</a>]<BR>on Ṛg-veda VII. 104, 22. शुशूलूक = शिशूलूक,<BR>a small owl; cf. उलूक-यातु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रुवस्
शुश्रुवस् शुश्रुवस्. See under rt. 1. श्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रू
शुश्रू शुश्रू, ऊस्, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. 1. श्रु),<BR>‘one who waits on a child,’ a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषक|शुश्रूषकः
शुश्रूषक, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of hearing,<BR>attentive, obedient, attending or waiting on; (अस्),<BR>m. an attendant, servant (comprehending five de-<BR>scriptions of persons, viz. a pupil, a religious pupil, a<BR>hired servant, an officer, and a slave).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषण|शुश्रूषणं
शुश्रूषण, अम्, n. obedience; dutiful homage,<BR>close and assiduous attendance, service, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषा
शुश्रूषा, f. desire or wish to hear, desire to<BR>obey, obedience; service (said to be of five kinds,<BR>see शुश्रूषक); obsequiousness, reverence; say-<BR>ing, speaking, telling.<BR>—शुश्रूषा-पर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>diligent or attentive in service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषित्वा
शुश्रूषित्वा, ind. having attended or waited upon<BR>(as a slave upon his master, Manu XI. 110).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषु
शुश्रूषु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of hearing or obey-<BR>ing, obedient, attentive, serving, attending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्
शुष् शुष् (thought to be for सुष्, which<BR>again was probably for an original सुस्),<BR>cl. 4. P. शुष्यति (ep. also A. -ते), शुशोष, शोक्ष्-<BR>यति, अशुषत्, शोष्टुम्, to dry, become dry, dry<BR>up; to wither, become withered; to languish, be-<BR>come emaciated; to be afflicted: Caus. शोषयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अशूशुषत्, to make dry, dry up,<BR>wither, parch; to emaciate; to destroy; to extinguish:<BR>Desid. शुशुक्षति: Intens. शोशुष्यते, शोशोष्टि;<BR>[cf. Zend hushka: Gr. σαυαρός, σαυσαρισμός,<BR>σαυκός (= शुष्क), σαυχμός, αὐχμός, σαχνός,<BR>αὔω, αὖος, αὐστηρός: Lat. siccus: Goth. siuk,<BR>sauht: Old Germ. siuh, siuchi, siuhjan, suht:<BR>Angl. Sax. seoc, seac, sioc, sic, suht: Slav. such,<BR>‘dry:’ Lith. sausa-s: Hib. seacadh, ‘parched,<BR>frozen;’ sioc, ‘frost;’ sican.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष|शुषः
शुष, अस्, ई, m. f. drying, drying up; a hole in<BR>the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषत्
शुषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. drying up, absorbing<BR>(moisture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषि|शुषिः
शुषि, इस्, f. drying; a hole, chasm; the hollow<BR>or groove in the fang of a snake; [cf. Gr. κυσό-ς,<BR>κυσ-θό-ς; Lat. cun-nu-s; Lith. kuszy-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिर|शुषिरं|शुषिरः
शुषिर, अस्, आ, अम्, full of holes or crevices<BR>(caused by drying), perforated, bored, pierced, full<BR>of interstices or spaces; (अम्), n. a hole, vacuity,<BR>chasm; the atmosphere; a wind-instrument; (अस्),<BR>m. fire; a rat, mouse; (आ), f. a river; a sort of per-<BR>fume (commonly called Nalī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिल|शुषिलः
शुषिल, अस्, m. ‘the dryer,’ air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्क|शुष्कः
शुष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, dried, dried up, dry; shriveled,<BR>withered, emaciated, shrunk up; groundless, cause-<BR>less; unproductive, fruitless, unprofitable; offensive;<BR>(अम्), n., Ved. anything dry, dry wood (for lighting<BR>fire by attrition).<BR>—शुष्क-कलह, अस्, m. vain or<BR>useless wrangling, a quarrel about trifles.<BR>—शुष्क-<BR>ता, f. or शुष्क-त्व, अम्, n. dryness.<BR>—शुष्क-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. a dry or withered leaf; a dried pot-<BR>herb.<BR>—शुष्क-पर्ण, अम्, n. a dry or withered<BR>leaf.<BR>—शुष्क-फल, अम्, n. dry fruit.<BR>—शुष्क-<BR>मत्स्य, अस्, m. a dried fish.<BR>—शुष्क-मांस,<BR>अम्, n. dry flesh, dry meat.<BR>—शुष्क-रेवती, f.<BR>epithet of a particular Mātrikā or goddess presiding<BR>over a kind of disease; [cf. रेवती, पूतना.]<BR>—शुष्क-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, dried up.<BR>—शुष्क-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m. a dry tree; a particular plant or<BR>shrub (= धव).<BR>—शुष्क-वैर, अम्, n. ground-<BR>less enmity.<BR>—शुष्क-व्रण, अस्, m. a dried up<BR>wound, cicatrized sore, scar.<BR>—शुष्क-स्रोत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the stream dried up.<BR>—शुष्काङ्ग (˚क-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having shriveled limbs, emaciated,<BR>withered; (अस्), m. a particular plant or shrub, =<BR>धव; (ई), f. a lizard, chameleon.<BR>—शुष्कान्न<BR>(˚क-अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘dry food,’ rice in the husk.<BR>—शुष्कार्द्र (˚क-आर्˚), अम्, n. dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कल|शुष्कलं|शुष्कलः
शुष्कल, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, m. f. n. dry flesh;<BR>flesh; one who eats flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्ण|शुष्णः
शुष्ण, अस्, m. the sun; fire; N. of a demon of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">Page1016-c+ 78</a>]<BR>drought (represented in the Ṛg-veda as being over-<BR>come by Indra); (अम्), n., Ved. strength, (enume-<BR>rated among the बल-नामानि in Naigh. II. 9.)<BR>—शुष्ण-हत्य, अम्, n., Ved. the slaughter of<BR>Śuṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्म|शुष्मं|शुष्मः
शुष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, strong, powerful (Ved.);<BR>(अस्), m. power, strength, vigour (Ved.); the sun;<BR>fire, flame, light; air, wind; a bird; (अम्), n.<BR>strength, prowess (= बल, Naigh. II. 9); light,<BR>lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मन्
शुष्मन्, आ, m. fire; a particular plant, = चि-<BR>त्रक; (अ), n. light, lustre; strength, prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मिण
शुष्मिण, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Śivis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मिन्
शुष्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, powerful, strong; fiery, mettle-<BR>some; (इणस्), m. pl., N. of a caste living in Kuśa-<BR>dvīpa (corresponding to the Kṣatriyas).<BR>—शुष्-<BR>मिन्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most powerful, very<BR>mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्यत्
शुष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, becoming dry, drying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्यमाण
शुष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being dry or dried up,<BR>languishing, thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोष|शोषः
शोष, अस्, m. drying up, exsiccation, dryness;<BR>pulmonary consumption; emaciation; intumescence,<BR>(for शोथ.)<BR>—शोष-सम्भव, अम्, n. the root<BR>of long pepper.<BR>—शोषापहा (˚ष-अप्˚), f. ‘re-<BR>moving consumption,’ a kind of plant (= क्लीत-<BR>नक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषक
शोषक, अस्, इका, अम्, drying up, exsiccating,<BR>absorbing, absorbent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषण|शोषणं|शोषणः
शोषण, अस्, ई, अम्, drying up, draining; causing<BR>to fade; (अस्), m. one of the arrows of Kāma-deva<BR>(god of love); the plant Bignonia Indica; (अम्), n.<BR>the act of drying up; absorption; exhaustion; suck-<BR>ing up, suction; dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषणीय
शोषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be dried up or absorbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषयितव्य
शोषयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be dried up, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषयित्वा
शोषयित्वा, ind. having dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषित|शोषितः
शोषित, अस्, आ, अम्, dried, dried up, desiccated,<BR>absorbed, sucked up, exhausted, drained, emptied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषिन्
शोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, drying up (often at the end of<BR>comps.); (इणी), f. ether, one of the five Dhāraṇās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूक|शूकं|शूकः
शूक शूक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt. शो),<BR>the awn of barley, &c.; a bristle, spicule; the bristle<BR>or sharp hair of insects, &c.; compassion, clemency,<BR>tenderness; a kind of venomous insect or lizard<BR>(produced in stagnant water); a sort of water-leech (?);<BR>a kind of moss or weed growing on stagnant water<BR>(= जल-श्˚); a particular remedy in which the Śūka<BR>is used; (आ), f. cowach.<BR>—शूक-कीट or शूक-<BR>कीटक, अस्, m. a kind of caterpillar covered with<BR>bristles or hairs.<BR>—शूक-तृण, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>grass.<BR>—शूक-धान्य, अम्, n. any awned or bearded<BR>grain (as barley &c.).<BR>—शूक-पिण्डि, इस्, or शूक-<BR>पिण्डी, f. cowach (= कपि-कच्छु).<BR>—शूक-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, awned, bearded; (अती), f. cowach.<BR>—शूक-शिम्बा, f. or शुक-शिम्बि, इस्, or शूक-<BR>शिम्बिका or शूक-शिम्बी, f. cowach, (also spelt<BR>शुक-शिम्बा, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकक|शूककः
शूकक, अस्, m. barley or a bearded kind of wheat<BR>resembling barley; the sentiment of compassion or<BR>tenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकिन्
शूकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, awned, bearded (as corn, grain,<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकर|शूकरः
शूकर शूकर, अस्, m. (said to be connected<BR>with शूक, or fr. शू, an imitative sound, + कर; cf.<BR>सूकर), a hog, pig; N. of a Naraka; (ई), f. a<BR>sow; a kind of moss, Lycopodium Imbricatum; [cf.<BR>Gr. αῦς, ὗς; Old Germ. sū; Mod. Germ. sau.]<BR>—शूकर-कन्द, अस्, m. ‘hog's root,’ a kind of<BR>bulbous plant (= वाराही-कन्द).<BR>—शूकर-दंष्-<BR>ट्र, अस्, m. a hog's tusk; N. of a kind of disease,<BR>(prolapsus ani.)<BR>—शूकर-पादिका, f. a kind of plant<BR>(= कोल-शिम्बी).<BR>—शूकराक्रान्ता (˚र-आक्˚), f. a<BR>kind of moss (= वराह-क्रान्ता).<BR>—शूकरेष्ट<BR>(˚र-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, liked by hogs or swine; (अस्),<BR>m. a kind of grass (= कसेरु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकल|शूकलः
शूकल शूकल, अस्, m. a restive horse; [cf.<BR>शूलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकापुट्ट
शूकापुट्ट शूकापुट्ट or (according to Śabda-<BR>k.) शूकापूट्ट, अस्, m. a particular gem, (perhaps)<BR>a kind of amber (= तृण-मणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकुल
शूकुल शूकुल, अस्, m. (?), a fish in general;<BR>a kind of fish; a fragrant grass, Cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकृत
शूकृत शू-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. making<BR>the sound शू or शूत्, snorting (said of a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूक्ष्म|शूक्ष्मं|शूक्ष्मः
शूक्ष्म शूक्ष्म, incorrect for सूक्ष्म, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूघन
शूघन शूघन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. going<BR>quickly, (Sāy. शूघनासः = आशु-गन्त्र्यः, Ṛg-<BR>veda IV. 58, 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूतिपर्ण|शूतिपर्णः
शूतिपर्ण शूति-पर्ण, अस्, m. (the meaning<BR>of शूति is doubtful), a kind of tree (= आरग्-बध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्र|शूद्रः
शूद्र शूद्र, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 19. fr. rt. 1. शुच्, to be afflicted, &c.), a man of<BR>the fourth or servile tribe (whose only business, ac-<BR>cording to Manu I. 91, was to serve the three higher<BR>castes; in Ṛg-veda X. 90, 12. the Śūdra is said to<BR>have been born from the feet of Puruṣa; in Manu<BR>I. 87. he is fabled to have sprung from the same<BR>part of the body of Brahmā; केवल-शूद्र, a pure<BR>Śūdra); (आ), f. a woman of the Śūdra tribe; (ई), f.<BR>the wife of a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्र-कन्या, f. a Śūdra<BR>girl.<BR>—शूद्र-कृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be done by a<BR>Śūdra, proper for a Śūdra; (अम्), n. the duty of<BR>a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्रकृत्य-विचार-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a part of Raghu-nandana's Smṛti-tattva (illustrat-<BR>ing the duties of Śūdras at the anniversaries of the<BR>death of parents and at other ceremonies).<BR>—शूद्र-<BR>ता, f. or शूद्र-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition<BR>of a Śūdra or slave; servility.<BR>—शूद्र-धर्म,<BR>अस्, m. the duty of a Śūdra (i. e. the service of the<BR>three higher castes).<BR>—शूद्रधर्म-तत्त्व, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the nature of a Śūdra's duties,’ N. of a work by<BR>Kamalākara.<BR>—शूद्र-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, dear to a<BR>Śūdra, liked by Śūdras; (अस्), m. an onion (= प-<BR>लाण्डु).<BR>—शूद्र-प्रेष्य, अस्, m. a man of one of<BR>the three superior castes who has become a servant<BR>to a Śūdra; (अम्), n. the being servant to a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्र-भिक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, (anything) begged<BR>or received as alms from a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्र-भू-<BR>यिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabited mostly by Śūdras,<BR>abounding with Śūdras.<BR>—शूद्र-याजक, अस्, m.<BR>one who sacrifices for a Śūdra, the conductor of a<BR>sacrifice for a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्रयाजक-प्रायश्चित्त,<BR>अम्, n. the penance incurred by sacrificing for a<BR>Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्र-योनि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born of a ser-<BR>vile womb, of plebeian origin.<BR>—शूद्र-राज्य, अम्,<BR>n. a country of which a Śūdra is king.<BR>—शूद्र-<BR>वर्ग, अस्, m. the Śūdra or servile class.<BR>—शूद्र-<BR>वर्जम्, ind. except Śūdras.<BR>—शूद्र-वृत्ति, इस्, f.<BR>the occupation or mode of life of a Śūdra (i. e. ser-<BR>vitude to the higher castes).<BR>—शूद्र-शासन, अम्,<BR>n. an edict or grant addressed to Śūdras.<BR>—शूद्र-<BR>संस्कार, अस्, m. any purificatory rite relating to<BR>Śūdras.<BR>—शूद्र-सेवन, अम्, n. attendance on a<BR>Śūdra master, the being in the service of a man of<BR>the servile class, (Manu XI. 70.)<BR>—शूद्र-हत्या, f.<BR>the killing of a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्र-हन्, आ, m. one<BR>who kills a Śūdra, the slayer of a Śūdra.<BR>—शू-<BR>द्रान्न (˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. food belonging to a<BR>Śūdra; [cf. शूद्रोदक below.]<BR>—शूद्रा-परिण-<BR>यन, अम्, n. the marrying a Śūdra female.<BR>—शू-<BR>द्रा-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of a Śūdra woman, (the<BR>father being either a Śūdra or a man of a different<BR>caste.)<BR>—शूद्रा-भार्य, अस्, m. one who has a<BR>Śūdra woman for his wife, the husband of a Śūdra<BR>woman.<BR>—शूद्रार्ता (˚र-आर्˚), f. a kind of plant<BR>(= प्रियङ्गु).<BR>—शूद्रा-वेदन, अम्, n. the mar-<BR>rying a Śūdra woman.<BR>—शूद्रा-वेदिन्, ई, m. marry-<BR>ing a Śūdra woman, a man of one of the three<BR>higher classes who has married a Śūdra wife.<BR>—शू-<BR>द्राशौच (˚र-अश्˚), अम्, n. the impurity of a<BR>Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्रा-सुत, अस्, m. = शूद्रा-पुत्र.<BR>—शू-<BR>द्राह्निक (˚र-आह्˚), अम्, n. the daily ceremonies<BR>of a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्री-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c.,<BR>to become a Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्रोदक (˚र-उद्˚), अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">Page1017-b+ 77</a>]<BR>n. water that has been polluted by the touch of a<BR>Śūdra.<BR>—शूद्रोदक-पान-प्रायश्चित्त, अम्, n. a<BR>penance for drinking water given by a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रक|शूद्रकः
शूद्रक, अस्, m., N. of the first Āndhra king,<BR>(variously written Sindhuka, Śiśuka, and Śūraka);<BR>of a king (the author of the drama called Mṛc-<BR>chakaṭikā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्राणी
शूद्राणी, f. the wife of a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून|शूनः
शून शून, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्वि, q. v.),<BR>swelled, swollen, increased, grown, prospered; mor-<BR>bidly swollen; empty, vacant (Ved., Sāy. = शून्य);<BR>(अम्), n., Ved. swelling, increase, (Sāy. = सम्-ऋद्-<BR>धि, Ṛg-veda III. 33, 13); emptiness, poverty, (Sāy.<BR>= शून्य, दारिद्र्य, Ṛg-veda II. 27, 17); an in-<BR>correct pronunciation (in Vedic phonetics).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूनवत्
शून-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूना
शूना शूना, f. (= सूना, q. v.), the uvula<BR>or soft palate; a slaughter-house, any place where<BR>animals are killed or are liable to be destroyed, (five<BR>of these are enumerated, viz. a fire-place, a grind-<BR>stone, a broom, a mortar, and a water-pot; cf.<BR>पञ्च-सूना.)<BR>—शूना-चक्र-ध्वज-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, one who keeps a slaughter-house, one who has<BR>an oil-press, and one who exhibits a vintner's sign,<BR>(Manu IV. 84.)<BR>—शूना-दोष, see सूना-दोष.<BR>—शूना-वत्, आन्, m. one who keeps a slaughter-<BR>house, a butcher.<BR>—शूना-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in<BR>or brought from a slaughter-house or any place where<BR>animals are destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्य|शून्यं|शून्यः
शून्य शून्य, अस्, आ, अम् (probably connected<BR>with शून above, fr. rt. श्वि), empty, void, hollow;<BR>vacant, barren, non-existent; utterly destitute or de-<BR>prived of, without (with inst.); ruined; nonsensical, un-<BR>meaning; guileless, unsuspicious; indifferent; lonely,<BR>private, desert, desolate, (शून्ये or शून्यम्, ind. in<BR>a lonely place, secretly); bare, naked; (अम्), n. a<BR>void, vacuum, blank; space, heaven, ether, the sky,<BR>atmosphere; a dot, spot; a cypher; naught, vacuity,<BR>nonentity, (one of the principles of Bauddha meta-<BR>physics); N. of Brahma; (आ), f. a hollow reed; a<BR>barren woman; the prickly pear; [cf. Gr. κενός,<BR>κενεός; Æol. κέννος.]<BR>—शून्य-गेह, अम्, n. an<BR>empty house.<BR>—शून्य-ता, f. or शून्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. emptiness, voidness, vacuity, non-existence, un-<BR>reality, the false or illusory nature of all existence.<BR>—शून्य-पदवी, f. ‘empty path,’ the road or<BR>passage of the soul, (see महा-पथ, मुद्रा-<BR>मार्ग.)<BR>—शून्य-मध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>hollow centre, empty inside; (अस्), m. a hollow reed.<BR>—शून्य-वत्, ind. like a cypher, annihilated or vanished<BR>as it were.<BR>—शून्य-वाद, अस्, m. the doctrine of the<BR>non-existence of anything.<BR>—शून्य-वादिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘affirmer of non-existence,’ an atheist; a Buddhist.<BR>—शून्य-स्थान, अम्, n. an empty place.<BR>—शून्य-<BR>हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, empty-handed.<BR>—शून्य-हृ-<BR>दय, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘empty-hearted,’ unsuspecting,<BR>unsuspicious; absent in mind.<BR>—शून्याकृति (˚य-<BR>आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, ‘empty-formed,’ having a vacant<BR>appearance or aspect.<BR>—शून्यागार-कृतालय (˚य-<BR>आग्˚, ˚त-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, making an abode in de-<BR>serted houses.<BR>—शून्यालय (˚य-आल्˚), अस्, m. an<BR>empty or deserted house, (sleeping in such a house<BR>is forbidden.)<BR>—शून्यी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make empty, leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूपकार|शूपकारः
शूपकार शूप-कार, अस्, m. (for सूप-कार,<BR>q. v.), one who lives by cooking for Śūdras (= शूद्र-<BR>पाकोपजीविन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूयमान
शूयमान शूयमान. See under rt. श्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्
शूर् शूर् (also written सूर्, q. v.), cl. 4. A.<BR>शूर्यते, शुशूरे, शूरितुम्, to hurt, in-<BR>jure, kill; to be firm or motionless, stand fast, be<BR>fixed; to make firm or immovable; to be senseless;<BR>cl. 10. A. शूरयते, -यितुम्, Aor. अशुशूरत्, to be<BR>valiant or powerful, act the hero; to make great<BR>effort or exertion, (in these senses rather a Nom. fr.<BR>शूर below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शूर, अस्, m. (probably connected with शवस्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">Page1017-c+ 80</a>]<BR>a hero, warrior, champion, valiant man, great or<BR>mighty man; a lion; a boar; the sun; N. of<BR>Yādava, the grandfather of Kṛṣṇa; the Śāl tree,<BR>Shorea Robusta; N. of certain other plants or trees,<BR>= चित्रक; = लकुच; = मसूर; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a tribe inhabiting Bhārata-varṣa; [cf. Zend<BR>śūra; Gr. κῦρ-ος, κυρό-ω, κύριος, κοίρανος, κοῦρος<BR>κόρος.]<BR>—शूर-कीट, अस्, m. ‘warrior-insect,’ an in-<BR>ferior hero.<BR>—शूर-ग्राम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>a multitude of heroes.<BR>—शूर-तर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. more heroic, very valiant.<BR>—शूर-ता, f. or<BR>शूर-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition of a hero,<BR>heroism, prowess, valour, bravery.<BR>—शूर-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the second of the twenty-four Arhats of<BR>the future Utsarpiṇī.<BR>—शूर-पुत्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having heroes as sons; (आ), f., Ved. epithet of Aditi.<BR>—शूर-पुर, अम्, n. ‘hero-town,’ N. of a town.<BR>—शूर-मठ, अस्, अम्, m. n. the college or<BR>monastery of Śūra.<BR>—शूर-मान, अम्, n. thinking<BR>one's self a hero, arrogance, vaunting.<BR>—शूर-मा-<BR>निन्, ई, m. one who thinks himself a hero, a boaster,<BR>braggart.<BR>—शूरम्-मन्य, अस्, m. one who thinks<BR>himself a hero, a boaster.<BR>—शूर-वर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of several kings.<BR>—शूर-वीर, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—शूर-श्लोक, अस्, m. a kind of arti-<BR>ficial verse; [cf. वीर-विरुद.]<BR>—शूर-साति, इस्,<BR>f., Ved. conflict of heroes, battle, war, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 31, 6. शूर-साता =<BR>शूरैः सम्भजनीये युद्धे.)<BR>—शूर-सेन, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the country about Mathurā; of a king (of<BR>Mathurā and ruler of the Yadus); (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of the people inhabiting the above country.<BR>—शूर-<BR>सेनक, आस्, m. pl., N. of the people and country<BR>about Mathurā.<BR>—शूरसेन-ज, अस्, m. one born in<BR>Śūra-sena, an inhabitant of Śūra-sena.<BR>—शूरार्थ<BR>(˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, useful for or suited to heroes,<BR>for the sake of warriors.<BR>—शूरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of Śūra,’ the tutelary deity of Śūra (or the<BR>statue of a deity); a temple built by Śūra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरक
शूरक, अस्, m., N. of a king (= शूद्रक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरण|शूरणः
शूरण, अस्, आ, अम्, high-spirited (Ved., said of<BR>horses; Sāy. = विक्रम-शील, Ṛg-veda I. 163, 10);<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of esculent root, Arum Campanu-<BR>latum; the plant Bignonia Indica.<BR>—शूरणोद्भुज<BR>(˚ण-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘feeding on Arum Campanu-<BR>latum,’ a kind of yellow bird (= हरिद्राङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्ण
शूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्त
शूर्त शूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (probably)<BR>eager, quick, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 174,<BR>6. शूर्ताः = क्षिप्राः or = क्षिप्ताः, वर्जिताः; in<BR>Naigh. II. 15. शूर्ताः is enumerated among the<BR>क्षिप्र-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्
शूर्प् शूर्प् (perhaps rather a Nom. fr.<BR>शूर्प below), cl. 10. P. शूर्पयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to measure, mete out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प|शूर्पं|शूर्पः|शूर्प्प
शूर्प, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according to Uṇādi-s. III.<BR>26. fr. rt. शॄ; also written सूर्प), a winnowing<BR>basket or a kind of wicker receptacle which, when<BR>shaken about, serves as a fan for winnowing corn;<BR>(अस्), m. a measure of two Droṇas; (ई), f. a small<BR>winnowing basket or fan; a toy for children; N. of<BR>the sister of Rāvaṇa, (see शूर्प-णखा.)<BR>—शूर्प-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m. ‘having ears like winnowing fans,’<BR>an elephant.<BR>—शूर्प-णखा, f. or शूर्प-णखी, f.<BR>‘having finger-nails like winnowing fans,’ N. of the<BR>sister of the Daitya Rāvaṇa, (she fell in love with<BR>Rāma and, being rejected by him, attacked Sītā, but<BR>was beaten off and mutilated by Lakṣmaṇa; in<BR>revenge she incited her brother to carry off Sītā.)<BR>—शूर्प-निष्पाव, अस्, m. a basket-full of win-<BR>nowed corn.<BR>—शूर्प-पर्णी, f. a sort of bean,<BR>Phaseolus Trilobus.<BR>—शूर्प-वात, अस्, m. the wind<BR>raised by shaking a winnowing basket.<BR>—शूर्प-<BR>श्रुति, इस्, m. ‘having ears like winnowing fans,’<BR>an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्पक|शूर्पकः|शूर्प्पक
शूर्पक, अस्, m., N. of a demon (an enemy of<BR>Kāma-deva).<BR>—शूर्पकाराति or शूर्पकारि (˚क-<BR>अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘enemy of Śūrpaka,’ epithet of Kāma<BR>(god of love).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्पी
शूर्पी, f. See above under शूर्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्पारक
शूर्पारक शूर्पारक, N. of a mythical<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्म|शूर्मः|शूर्म्म|शूर्म्मः
शूर्म शूर्म, अस्, m. an iron image; an anvil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्मि|शूर्मिः|शूर्म्मि|शूर्म्मिः
शूर्मि, इस्, m. f. or शूर्मिका or शूर्मी, f. =<BR>शूर्म above; [cf. सूर्मि, स्युर्मि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्
शूल् शूल् (rather a Nom. fr. शूल below),<BR>cl. 1. P. शूलति, शुशूल, शूलितुम्, to be<BR>ill; to disorder, make sick, disease; to pierce, transfix,<BR>impale; to cry, make a loud noise; to collect (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल|शूलं|शूलः
शूल, अस्, अम्, m. n. any sharp or acute pain;<BR>pain in the stomach, colic; rheumatism, gout; any<BR>sharp or pointed weapon, a pike, dart, spear, lance,<BR>spike; the trident of Śiva; a sharp iron pin or spit<BR>(on which meat is roasted); a stake for impaling<BR>criminals; a banner, ensign; the ninth astronomical<BR>Yoga; death, dying; (आ), f. a stake for impaling<BR>criminals; a harlot, prostitute; [cf. Slav. sūliza.]<BR>—शूल-गव, a kind of animal sacrifice.<BR>—शूल-<BR>ग्रन्थि, इस्, f. ‘having sharp knots,’ a kind of Dūrvā<BR>grass (= माला-दूर्वा).<BR>—शूल-घातन, अम्, n.<BR>‘pain-destroying,’ iron rust or filings.<BR>—शूल-घ्न,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, removing or allaying sharp pain, sedative,<BR>anodyne; (अस्), m. a kind of plant (= तुम्बुरु).<BR>—शूल-द्विष्, ट्, m. ‘enemy to colic,’ Asa Fetida.<BR>—शूल-धन्वन्, आ, m. ‘having a trident for a<BR>bow,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शूल-धर, अस्, m. ‘spear-<BR>holder, trident-holder,’ epithet of Śiva; (आ), f.<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—शूल-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, spear-<BR>holding, lance-bearing, trident-holding; (इणी), f.<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—शूल-धृक्, m. (see धृक्,<BR>p. 459), ‘trident-bearing,’ epithet of Śiva; (क्), f.<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—शूल-नाशन, अम्, n. ‘remov-<BR>ing pain in the stomach,’ white sochal salt.<BR>—शूल-<BR>पत्त्री, f. a kind of grass (= शूली).<BR>—शूल-पाणि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘trident-handed,’ epithet of Śiva (regarded<BR>as the king of the Bhūtas); N. of the author of the<BR>Prāyaścitta-viveka and of the Tithi-dvaidha-prakaraṇa<BR>and of the Yājñavalkya-ṭīkā.<BR>—शूल-पाणिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, holding or bearing a lance or spear.<BR>—शूल-भृत्,<BR>त्, m. ‘spear-holder,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शूल-<BR>भेद, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—शूल-मुद्गर-<BR>हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having a lance and mace in hand,<BR>armed with a lance and club.<BR>—शूल-वेदना, f.<BR>sharp or acute pain.<BR>—शूल-शत्रु, उस्, m. ‘hostile<BR>to colic,’ the castor-oil plant, Ricinus Communis.<BR>—शूल-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed on a stake, impaled.<BR>—शूल-हन्त्री, f. ‘colic-removing,’ a kind of barley<BR>(= यवानी).<BR>—शूल-हस्त, अस्, m. ‘lance-handed,’<BR>a man armed with a lance, lancer, pikeman.<BR>—शूल-<BR>हृत्, त्, m. ‘removing colic,’ Asa Fetida.<BR>—शूला-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to roast on a spit.<BR>—शूलाकृत (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, roasted on a<BR>spit, &c.; (अम्), n. roasted meat.<BR>—शूलाग्र (˚ल-<BR>अग्˚), अम्, n. the point of a pike or stake, &c.<BR>—शूलेश्वरी-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—शू-<BR>लोत्खा (˚ल-उत्˚), f. the medicinal plant Serratula<BR>Anthelmintica.<BR>—शूलोद्यत-कर (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, with uplifted spear in hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलक|शूलकः
शूलक, अस्, m. a restive or unbroken horse;<BR>[cf. शूकल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिक|शूलिकं|शूलिकः
शूलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a spear or any sharp<BR>instrument; roasted on a spit; (अस्), m. a hare;<BR>(अम्), n. roast meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन्
शूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering sharp pain, suffering<BR>from colic; armed with a spear or pike, carrying a<BR>lance or stake; (ई), m. a spearman, pikeman, lancer;<BR>epithet of Śiva (as holding a trident); a hare; N.<BR>of a Muni; (इनी), f. epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन|शूलिनः
शूलिन, अस्, m. the Indian fig-tree (= भाण्डीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूली
शूली, f. a kind of grass (= मधु-लता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्य|शूल्यं
शूल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, roasted on a spit; deserving<BR>impalement; (अम्), n. roasted meat.<BR>—शूल्य-पाक,<BR>अस्, m. any meat or other substance roasted on a spit.<BR>—शूल्य-मांस, अम्, n. roast meat, meat cooked<BR>on a spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूशुजान
शूशुजान शूशुजान, अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Sāy. = शोशुचान, दीप्यमान, Ṛg-veda X. 34, 6;<BR>cf. शुशुचान, p. 1013), Ved. glowing, resplen-<BR>dent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूशुवस्
शूशुवस् शूशुवस्, वान्, m. (fr. rt. श्वि), Ved.<BR>one who has increased, increasing; large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूशुवान
शूशुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. growing in size, in-<BR>creasing in strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूष्
शूष् शूष् (also written सूष्), cl. 1. P.<BR>शूषति, शुशूष, शूषितुम्, to bring<BR>forth; to beget, propagate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूष|शूषः
शूष शूष, अम्, n. (perhaps connected<BR>with rt. श्वि), Ved. strength, (according to Naigh. II.<BR>9, Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 154, 3 = बल; cf. शुष्म;<BR>in Naigh. III. 6 = सुख); (अस्), m., N. of a pre-<BR>ceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूषणि
शूषणि, in Ṛg-veda X. 93, 1. probably fr. a<BR>base शूषन्; regarded by some as a kind of Ved.<BR>Inf. fr. rt. श्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृकाल|शृकालः
शृकाल शृकाल, अस्, m. (for शृगाल below),<BR>a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगाल|शृगालः
शृगाल शृगाल, अस्, m. (etymology doubt-<BR>ful, but cf. Gr. κραγέτης; perhaps connected with<BR>rt. शॄ; sometimes written सृगाल), a jackal; a<BR>rogue, cheat; a coward, poltroon; an ill-natured or<BR>harsh-speaking man; N. of a demon; epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; (ई), f. a female jackal; a fox; flight, re-<BR>treat; a kind of plant (= कोकिलाक्ष); another<BR>plant (= विदारी).<BR>—शृगाल-कण्टक, अस्, m.<BR>‘jackal's thorn,’ a kind of plant, Zizyphus Scandens.<BR>—शृगाल-कोलि, इस्, m. a sort of jujube.<BR>—शृगाल-<BR>घण्टी, f. a particular plant (= कोकिलाक्ष).<BR>—शृ-<BR>गाल-जम्बु, उस्, or शृगाल-जम्बू, ऊस्, f. a kind<BR>of cucumber, Cucumis Madraspatanus; the fruit of<BR>the jujube.<BR>—शृगाल-जाति, इस्, f. birth (in a future<BR>life) as a jackal.<BR>—शृगाल-योनि, इस्, m. f. the womb<BR>of a jackal; the being born in a future birth as a<BR>jackal.<BR>—शृगाल-रूप, अस्, m. ‘jackal-formed,’ epi-<BR>thet of Śiva.<BR>—शृगाल-विन्ना, f. a kind of plant<BR>(= पृश्नि-पर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालिका
शृगालिका, f. a female jackal; a fox; running<BR>away, flight, retreat; a kind of plant (= भूमि-<BR>कुष्माण्ड); a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खल|शृंखल|शृंखलं|शृंखलः|शृङ्खलः
शृङ्खल शृङ्खल, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. (ety-<BR>mology doubtful; perhaps connected with शिञ्जा, ‘a<BR>tinkling sound’), an iron chain; any chain or fetter;<BR>a belt or chain worn round the waist for ornament,<BR>&c.; an iron chain for confining the feet of an<BR>elephant; a measuring chain.<BR>—शृङ्खल-ता, f. or<BR>शृङ्खल-त्व, अम्, n. the being chained together;<BR>restraint; concatenation, connection, order; a series.<BR>—शृङ्खला-बन्ध or शृङ्खला-बन्धन,<BR>अम्, n. confining by chains or fetters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलक|शृंखलक|शृंखलकः|शृङ्खलकः
शृङ्खलक, अस्, m. a chain; a young camel or<BR>other young animal with wooden rings or clogs on<BR>his feet (to prevent his straying); any camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलित|शृंखलित|शृङ्खलितः
शृङ्खलित, अस्, आ, अम्, chained, fettered, bound,<BR>confined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खली
शृङ्खली, f. a kind of plant (= कोकिलाक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्ग|शृंग|शृंगं|शृङ्गं|शृङ्गः
शृङ्ग शृङ्ग, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 125. fr. rt. शॄ with affix ग, a nasal being inserted;<BR>according to some perhaps contracted fr. शिरङ्-ग,<BR>‘head-going’), a horn; the top or summit of a<BR>mountain, a peak, crag; the summit of a building,<BR>pinnacle, turret; any peak or point or projection or<BR>lofty object; a cusp or horn of the moon; height,<BR>elevation, dignity, lordship, mastership, supremacy,<BR>sovereignty; the rising or bursting forth of desire,<BR>excess of love or passion; anything sharp or fine-<BR>pointed; a fountain or artificial spout of water; any<BR>horn-like vessel or instrument; a buffalo's horn or<BR>other horn used for blowing; a lotus; a mark, token,<BR>sign; (अस्), m. a medicinal plant and root (= जी-<BR>वक); N. of a Ṛṣi or Muni (of whom, in some<BR>parts of India, on occasions of drought, earthen<BR>images are said to be made and supplicated for rain);<BR>[cf. Gr. κέρας; Lat. cornu; Goth. haurn; Angl.<BR>Sax. horn.]<BR>—शृङ्ग-कन्द, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>plant (= शृङ्गाटक).<BR>—शृङ्ग-गिरि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—शृङ्ग-ग्राहिका, f. (in logic) dis-<BR>tribution, taking singly and severally all the parti-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">Page1018-c+ 81</a>]<BR>culars included under a general term or all the indi-<BR>viduals composing a body.<BR>—शृङ्ग-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>horn-produced, made from horn; produced on<BR>mountain-peaks; (अस्), m. an arrow, shaft; (अम्), n.<BR>the aloe wood or tree (= अ-गुरु).<BR>—शृङ्ग-पुर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—शृङ्ग-प्रहारिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, horn-striking, butting or fighting with the horns.<BR>—शृङ्ग-प्रिय, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शृङ्ग-<BR>मूल, अस्, m. a kind of plant (= शृङ्गाटक).<BR>—शृङ्ग-मोहिन्, ई, m. the Campaka tree.<BR>—शृङ्ग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having peaks, peaked;<BR>(आन्), m. a mountain; epithet of a mythical moun-<BR>tain forming one of the boundaries of the earth.<BR>—शृङ्ग-वृष्, ट्, m., Ved. epithet of the Sun;<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi (said to have been the father of Indra;<BR>शृङ्ग-वृषो नपात्, the offspring of Śṛṅga-vṛṣ,<BR>i. e. Indra).<BR>—शृङ्ग-वेर, अम्, n. ginger (undried<BR>or dry); N. of a town (= गुह-चण्डाल-पुर).<BR>—शृङ्ग-वेरक, अम्, n. ginger.<BR>—शृङ्गवेरा-<BR>भ-मूलक (˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘having a root<BR>like that of ginger,’ a kind of grass (= एरका).<BR>—शृङ्ग-शत, अम्, n. a hundred peaks.<BR>—शृङ्-<BR>गाग्र-प्रहरणाभिमुख (˚ग-अग्˚, ˚ण-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, advancing towards or making a charge<BR>with the weapons of the points of the horns; ready<BR>to strike with the points of the horns.<BR>—शृङ्गान्-<BR>तर (˚ग-अन्˚), अम्, n. the space or interval be-<BR>tween the horns (of a cow &c.).<BR>—शृङ्गीश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ (˚गी-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—शृङ्गोच्-<BR>छ्राय (˚ग-उच्˚), अस्, m. a lofty peak.<BR>—शृङ्गोन्-<BR>नति (˚ग-उन्˚), इस्, f. elevation of a horn, the rising<BR>(of the moon?; cf. शीर्षोदय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गक|शृंगक|शृंगकं|शृंगकः|शृङ्गकः
शृङ्गक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a horn; anything<BR>pointed; a cusp or horn of the moon; (अस्), m. a<BR>medicinal root, (commonly called Jīvaka.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गला
शृङ्गला, f. a particular plant (= अज-शृङ्गी,<BR>‘goat's horn’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाट|शृंगाट|शृङ्गाटं|शृंगाटः|शृङ्गाटः
शृङ्गाट, अम्, n. a place where four roads meet;<BR>(अस्), m. the aquatic plant Trapa Bispinosa; the<BR>shrub Ruellia or Barleria Longifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाटक|शृंगाटक|शृङ्गाटकं|शृंगाटकः|शृङ्गाटकः
शृङ्गाटक, अम्, n. a place where four roads<BR>meet; a kind of pastry or dish of minced meat, &c.<BR>(called Samūsā in Hindī); a door; (अस्), m. the<BR>aquatic plant Trapa Bispinosa; a mountain having<BR>three peaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गार|शृंगार|शृङ्गारं|शृंगारः|शृङ्गारः
शृङ्गार, अस्, m. (probably connected with शृङ्ग<BR>in the sense of ‘rising of desire;’ according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. III. 136. fr. rt. शॄ with affix आर, a nasal<BR>and ग् being inserted), love, sexual passion, erotic sen-<BR>timent; sexual union, coition; a dress suitable for<BR>amorous purposes, an elegant dress; a mark or marks<BR>with red-lead on an elephant's head and trunk by<BR>way of ornament; any mark; N. of the father of<BR>Jaya-ratha; (अम्), n. cloves; red-lead; fragrant<BR>powder for the dress or person; undried ginger;<BR>Agallochum.<BR>—शृङ्गार-चेष्टा, f. love-gesture, any<BR>outward action indicating love.<BR>—शृङ्गार-तिलक,<BR>अम्, n., N. of an erotic poem by Rudra-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—शृङ्गार-भाषित, अम्, n. a love story.<BR>—शृङ्-<BR>गार-भूषण, अम्, n. red-lead.<BR>—शृङ्गार-<BR>मण्डप, N. of a temple.<BR>—शृङ्गार-योनि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘love-source,’ epithet of Kāma, god of love.<BR>—शृङ्गार-रस, अस्, m. the erotic sentiment.<BR>—शृङ्गाररसाष्टक (˚स-अष्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>eight stanzas by Kālidāsa on the erotic sentiment.<BR>—शृङ्गार-वती, f., N. of a town; of a queen.<BR>—शृङ्गार-विधि, इस्, m. a dress suitable for<BR>amorous interviews.<BR>—शृङ्गार-वेश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dressed suitably for amorous enterprises.<BR>—शृङ्गार-<BR>शत or शृङ्गार-शतक, अम्, n. ‘a hundred verses<BR>on love,’ N. of the second book of Bhartṛ-hari's<BR>poem.<BR>—शृङ्गार-सहाय, अस्, m. an assistant in<BR>affairs of love, confidant of a dramatic hero.<BR>—शृङ्-<BR>गारैक-रस (˚र-एक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, whose sole<BR>feeling is love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारक|शृङ्गारकं|शृंगारकः|शृङ्गारकः
शृङ्गारक, अस्, आ, अम्, horned, having a horn<BR>or crest; (अस्), m. love, &c. = शृङ्गार; (अम्), n.<BR>red-lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारित|शृंगारित
शृङ्गारित, अस्, आ, अम्, affected by love, impas-<BR>sioned; stained with red-lead, reddened; adorned,<BR>decorated, embellished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारिन्|शृंगारिन्
शृङ्गारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, feeling love or amorous pas-<BR>sion; full of love, amorous, enamoured, impassioned;<BR>relating to love; stained with red-lead; (ई), m. an<BR>impassioned lover; an elephant; dress, decoration;<BR>the Areca or betel-nut tree; a ruby (= माणिक्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गि|शृंगि|शृंगिः|शृङ्गिः
शृङ्गि, इस्, f. a species of Silurus or sheat-fish;<BR>(इस्), m. gold for ornaments, (said to be also शृङ्गि,<BR>n.; cf. शृङ्गी.)<BR>—शृङ्गि-कनक, अम्, n. gold used<BR>for ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिक|शृंगिक|शृंगिकं|शृङ्गिकं
शृङ्गिक, अम्, n. a sort of poison; (आ), f. a kind<BR>of Betula or birch tree (= प्रति-विषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिण|शृंगिण|शृंगिणः|शृङ्गिणः
शृङ्गिण, अस्, आ, अम्, horned; (अस्), m. a ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिन्|शृंगिन्
शृङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, horned; crested, peaked; (ई),<BR>m. a mountain; N. of a mythical mountain forming<BR>one of the boundaries of the earth, (Viṣṇu-Purāṇa<BR>II. 2); an elephant; a tree; N. of a son of Gautama;<BR>epithet of Śiva; (इणी), f. a cow; Arabian jasmine or<BR>another species; heart-pea; the plant Kaṭukī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गी|शृंगी
शृङ्गी, f. a kind of gold used for making orna-<BR>ments; a sort of Silurus or sheat-fish; a particular<BR>medicinal root shaped like a bull's horn (= ऋष-<BR>भ); a kind of poison; a kind of Betula; N. of<BR>various other plants and trees (= अति-विषा; = कर्-<BR>कट-शृङ्गी; = प्लक्ष; = वट).<BR>—शृङ्गी-क-<BR>नक, अम्, n. a kind of gold used for ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गेरिपुर
शृङ्गेरि-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गेरीमठ
शृङ्गेरी-मठ, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृणि|शृणिः
शृणि शृणि, इस्, f. (said to be fr. rt. शॄ), the<BR>hook for goading an elephant, (also written सृणि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृण्वत्
शृण्वत् शृण्वत्. See under rt. 1. श्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृत|शृतं
शृत शृत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्रा), boiled,<BR>(used especially with reference to water, milk, and<BR>ghee); cooked, dressed; [cf. श्राण, श्रपित.]<BR>—शृत-पा, आस्, आस्, अम् (see 2. and 4. पा), Ved. a<BR>drinker or appropriator of an oblation, (Sāy. = क्षी-<BR>रादेर् हविषः पातृ, Ṛg-veda VII. 18, 16.)<BR>—शृत-पाक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a well-<BR>performed cooking, cooked or dressed fit for the<BR>gods, (Sāy. = देव-योग्य-पाकोपेत, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>162, 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृध्
शृध् शृध्, cl. 1. A. (also P. in Fut.,<BR>Aor., Cond.) शर्धते, शशृधे, शर्-<BR>धिष्यते (and शर्त्स्यति), अशृधत्, &c., शर्धि-<BR>तुम्, to break wind downwards; cl. 1. P. A. शर्-<BR>धति, -ते, to moisten, become moist or wet; cl.<BR>10. P. शर्धयति, to insult (by breaking wind<BR>against or by voiding excrement), mock at, ridicule;<BR>to strive, make effort, (in this sense also cl. 1. P.<BR>according to some): Caus. शर्धयति, -यितुम्:<BR>Desid. शिशर्धिषते, शिशृत्सति: Intens. शरीशृ-<BR>ध्यते, शरीशर्द्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ध|शर्द्धः|शर्धः
शर्ध, शर्धन. See p. 995, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृद्ध
शृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, expelled from the body (as<BR>wind); moistened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृद्ध्वा
शृद्ध्वा, ind. having expelled wind from the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृधु|शृधुः
शृधु, उस्, m. f. (according to Śabda-k. only<BR>m.), the anus; = बुद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृधू
शृधू, ऊस्, m. f. (according to Śabda-k. only<BR>m.), the anus; = कुत्सित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृध्या
शृध्या, f., Ved. effort, success, (Sāy. = उत्साह-<BR>नीयं कर्म, Ṛg-veda II. 12, 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शॄ
शॄ शॄ, cl. 9. P. शृणाति, शशार (3rd pl.<BR>शशरुः and शश्रुः, Pāṇ. VII. 4, 12),<BR>शरिष्यति or शरीष्यति, अशारीत्, शरितुम्, शरी-<BR>तुम् (Ved. Inf. शरीतोस्), to injure, hurt, wound, kill,<BR>destroy; to tear or split in pieces, break, tear asunder:<BR>Pass. शीर्यते (ep. also -ति), to be injured; to be<BR>broken or torn or shattered, be split to pieces; to<BR>wither, moulder, decay, waste away: Caus. शार-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशीशरत्: Desid. शिशरिषति<BR>or शिशरीषति or शिशीर्षति: Intens. शेशीर्यते,<BR>शाशर्ति; [cf. Zend śūra: Gr. κείρω, κορ-μός,<BR>κέρμα, κουρά, κουρεύ-ς, κεραΐζω, κέρασ, κεραός,<BR>κλάω, κλῆρος, κολαβός, (probably) κορύνη: Lat.<BR>cur-tu-s (Sabin. curi-s); cornu, cervus; clava,<BR>quiris, (probably) in-columis: Goth. hair-u-s, ‘a<BR>sword;’ haurn: Old Norse hior: Old Sax. her-u:<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">Page1019-b+ 73</a>]<BR>Angl. Sax. hyrt; horn; heorot, heort: Slav.<BR>kor-a.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ण|शीर्णं
शीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, withered, &c. See s. v.,<BR>p. 1011, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृणान
शृणान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hurting, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखर|शेखरं|शेखरः
शेखर शेखर, अस्, m. (fr. शिखर; the<BR>more usual form would be शैखर), a crest, chap-<BR>let, diadem, crown, tuft, garland of flowers worn on<BR>the top of the head; a peak, summit; the chief or<BR>head of anything (generally at the end of comps.);<BR>a particular Dhruva or recurring stanza of a song,<BR>(another kind is called लघु-शेखर); a proper<BR>N.; (अम्), n. cloves; the root of the Hyperanthera<BR>Moringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखरित
शेखरित, अस्, आ, अम्, crested, tufted, topped,<BR>peaked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखरी
शेखरी, f. a particular parasitical plant (= वन्दा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेणवी
शेणवी शेणवी or शेणा, f. (doubtful), under-<BR>standing, mind, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेप|शेपः
शेप शेप, अस्, m. or शेपस्, अस्, n. (perhaps<BR>connected with rt. 3. शप्, see Nirukta III. 21; ac-<BR>cording to Uṇādi-s. IV. 200. fr. rt. 1. शी), the penis<BR>or male organ; a testicle; a tail.<BR>—शेप-हर्षण,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, exciting the male organ, see Atharva-veda<BR>Prātiśākhya II. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफ|शेफः
शेफ, अस्, m. (also written सेफ), or शेफस्,<BR>अस्, n. the male organ, penis; a testicle; a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपान
शेपान शेपान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. शप्),<BR>Ved. one who has sworn, bound by oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपाल|शेपालः
शेपाल शेपाल, अस्, m. the aquatic plant<BR>Vallisneria (= शेवाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालि|शेफालिः
शेफालि शेफालि, इस्, f. a kind of plant,<BR>Nyctanthes Arbor Tristis; another plant (= निर्-<BR>गुण्टी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालिका
शेफालिका or शेफाली, f. = शेफालि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेमुषी
शेमुषी शेमुषी, f. (probably fem. of the<BR>perf. part. of rt. 1. शम्), understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेल्
शेल् शेल् (also written सेल्), cl. 1. P. शे-<BR>लति, Caus. Aor. अशिशेलत्, to go, move<BR>about; to shake, tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेलाय
शेलाय, Nom. P. शेलायति, -यितुम्, (meaning<BR>doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेलु|शेलुः
शेलु शेलु, उस्, m. a kind of plant or small<BR>tree, Cordia Myxa; a kind of fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव्
शेव् शेव् (another form of rt. सेव्), cl. 1.<BR>A. शेवते, &c., to worship, serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव|शेवः
शेव शेव, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 152, 154. fr. rt. 1. शी, but more probably con-<BR>nected with rt. श्वि and शवस्, cf. शिव), causing<BR>happiness, propitious, affectionate (Ved., Sāy. = सु-<BR>ख-कर); (अस्), m. a snake; height, elevation;<BR>happiness; treasure, wealth; an epithet of Agni (as<BR>being the source of happiness, Sāy. = सुख-कर);<BR>of Soma; the male organ, = शेप; (अम्), n. happi-<BR>ness; (अम्), ind. hail, homage, an exclamation or<BR>salutation addressed to the deities; (अम्, आ), n. f.<BR>the male organ, penis (= शेप).<BR>—शेव-धि, इस्, m.<BR>(also written सेव-धि), ‘wealth-receptacle,’ one of<BR>the nine treasures of Kuvera, divine treasure, any<BR>valuable treasure; [cf. नि-धि.]<BR>—शेवधि-पा, आस्,<BR>m., Ved. a lord of treasures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवृध्
शे-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. conferring happiness, (Sāy.<BR>शे-वृधः = शेवस्य, सुखस्य वर्धयितारः,<BR>Ṛg-veda V. 87, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवृध
शे-वृध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. increasing or con-<BR>tributing to felicity, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 16, 2.<BR>appears to derive शे-वृध fr. 2. शम् and rt.<BR>वृध्); (अम्), n. happiness (enumerated among the<BR>सुख-नामानि in Naigh. III. 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव्य
शेव्य, अस्, m., Ved. a giver of happiness, (Sāy.<BR>= साधुः सुख-कर्ता, Ṛg-veda I. 156, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवल|शेवलं
शेवल शेवल, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. शी, cf. शैवल), the aquatic plant Vallisneria<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">Page1019-c+ 79</a>]<BR>Octandra [cf. शेपाल]; the green moss-like sub-<BR>stance growing on the surface of stagnant water,<BR>duck-weed, (said to be also अस्, m.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवलिनी
शेवलिनी, f. ‘having Śevala,’ a river; [cf. शैवलिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवाल|शेवालं
शेवाल, अम्, n. = शेवल above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवाली
शेवाली, f. a kind of plant (= आकाश-मांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवृध्
शेवृध् शे-वृध्, शे-वृध. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्यित
शेश्यित शेश्यित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of<BR>rt. 1. शी, Pāṇ. I. 2, 19), fast asleep, sleeping much.<BR>—शेश्यित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has slept<BR>soundly, sleeping much or soundly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्वीयमान
शेश्वीयमान शेश्वीयमान. See under rt. श्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेष|शेषं|शेषः
शेष शेष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. शिष्), re-<BR>maining, other, all the other; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>remainder, leavings, rest, residue, surplus, balance;<BR>the being spared or left, escape, salvation, reprieve,<BR>respite; anything rejected, anything left or left out<BR>or omitted or left to be supplied; anything left out<BR>or omitted to be said, (इति शेषः, ‘so it was intended<BR>to be said,’ a phrase used by commentators in sup-<BR>plying any word or words necessary to elucidate the<BR>text); (अस्), m. result, issue, effect, conclusion, end,<BR>termination; finish, destruction, death, killing; N.<BR>of a celebrated mythological thousand-headed serpent<BR>regarded as the emblem of eternity (whence he is<BR>also called An-anta, ‘the infinite;’ in the Viṣṇu-<BR>Purāṇa he and the serpents Vāsuki and Takṣaka<BR>are described as sons of Kadru, but in one place<BR>Śeṣa alone is called king of the Nāgas or snakes<BR>inhabiting Pātāla, while elsewhere Vāsuki also is<BR>described as king of the Nāgas and Takṣaka of the<BR>serpents; the thousand-headed Śeṣa is sometimes<BR>represented as forming the couch and canopy of<BR>Viṣṇu whilst sleeping during the intervals of creation,<BR>sometimes as bearing the entire world on one of his<BR>heads, sometimes as supporting the seven Pātālas;<BR>he is said to have taught astronomy to Garga; ac-<BR>cording to some legends he became incarnate in<BR>Bala-rāma, see बल-राम); N. of Bala-rāma, (see<BR>above); N. of one of the Prajā-patis; of a Muni;<BR>(अम्), n. the remnants of food; remains of an<BR>offering, &c.; (आ), f. the remains of flowers or other<BR>offerings made to an idol and afterwards distributed<BR>amongst the worshippers and attendants; (ए), ind.<BR>in the end, at last, finally, lastly; in other cases, in<BR>the case of a less amount.<BR>—शेष-करण, अम्, n.<BR>the doing what remains to be done.<BR>—शेष-काल,<BR>अस्, m. the time of end or death.<BR>—शेष-कृष्ण, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the drama called Kaṃsa-vadha.<BR>—शेष-जाति, इस्, f. assimilation of residue; reduc-<BR>tion of fractions of residues or successive fractional<BR>remainders.<BR>—शेष-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being<BR>a remainder, (शेषत्वेन, by the remainder, in<BR>every other case); all that is left, residue; aid,<BR>succouring others, regard or consideration for others<BR>(= उपकारित्व, पारार्थ्य).<BR>—शेष-नाग, अस्,<BR>m. the serpent Śeṣa, (see above); N. of the<BR>mythical author of the Paramārtha-sāra.<BR>—शे-<BR>ष-भाग, अस्, m. the last or remaining part.<BR>—शेष-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, one who eats leavings.<BR>—शेष-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being the remainder,<BR>being left.<BR>—शेष-भोजन, अम्, n. the eating of<BR>leavings, eating the rest of food after feeding the<BR>family guests, &c.<BR>—शेष-रक्षण, अम्, n. ‘end-<BR>protection,’ taking care that an undertaking is brought<BR>to a conclusion.<BR>—शेष-रात्रि, इस्, f. the last watch<BR>of the night.<BR>—शेष-राम-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a commentator on the Naiṣadīya-carita.<BR>—शेष-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, characterized by an effect or result,<BR>(sometimes applied in logic to a posteriori reason-<BR>ing.)<BR>—शेष-शरीर, अम्, n. the remainder of the<BR>body, i. e. all the other parts of the body.<BR>—शे-<BR>षान्न (˚ष-अन्˚), अम्, n. leavings of a meal, &c.<BR>—शेषार्या (˚ष-आर्˚), f., N. of a metrical intro-<BR>duction to the Vedānta by Śeṣa-nāga.<BR>—शेषा-<BR>वचयन (˚ष-अव्˚), अम्, n. gathering up rem-<BR>nants, collecting what remains.<BR>—शेषावस्था (˚ष-<BR>अव्˚), f. the last state or condition of life, old age.<BR>—शेषाहि (˚ष-अहि), इस्, m. the serpent Śeṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषस्
शेषस्, अस्, n., Ved. offspring (= अपत्य, Naigh.<BR>II. 2; cf. वरुण-श्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शै
शै शै, cl. 1. P. शायति, &c. = rt. श्रा, to<BR>cook; (according to some also A. शायते, in<BR>the sense) to go; [cf. rt. श्यै.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्य|शैक्यः
शैक्य शैक्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. शिक्य), sus-<BR>pended in the loop or swing of a porter's yoke;<BR>pointed, spiked, (for शैख्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्ष|शैक्षः
शैक्ष शैक्ष, अस्, m. (fr. शिक्षा), a young<BR>Brāhman studying with his preceptor, a youthful<BR>student just commencing the study of the Vedas (=<BR>प्राथमकल्पिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्षिक|शैक्षिकः
शैक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>Śikṣā or the science of euphony; (अस्), m. one<BR>skilled in the above science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्ष्य|शैक्ष्यं
शैक्ष्य, अम्, n. learning, skill.<BR>—शैक्ष्य-<BR>गुण-क्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing skill, cleverness<BR>and dexterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैख|शैखः
शैख शैख, अस्, m. (doubtful), the off-<BR>spring of an outcast Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखरिक|शैखरिकः
शैखरिक शैखरिक, अस्, m. (fr. शेखर),<BR>the plant Achyranthes Aspera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखरेय|शैखरेयः
शैखरेय, अस्, m. = शैखरिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखावत्य
शैखावत्य शैखावत्य, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैख्य
शैख्य शैख्य, अस्, &c. (fr. शिखा), pointed,<BR>spiked; [cf. शैक्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैग्रव
शैग्रव शैग्रव, अस्, m. (fr. शिग्रु), a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैघ्र
शैघ्र शैघ्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शीघ्र), relating<BR>to a conjunction (in astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैघ्र्य|शैघ्र्यं
शैघ्र्य, अम्, n. quickness, rapidity; (अस्, आ or<BR>-री, अम्), relating to a conjunction (in astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैत्य|शैत्यं
शैत्य शैत्य, अम्, n. (fr. शीत), coldness, fri-<BR>gidity, cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैत्यायन
शैत्यायन, अस्, m., N. of a Vedic grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैथिल्य|शैथिल्यं
शैथिल्य शैथिल्य, अम्, n. (fr. शिथिल),<BR>looseness, laxity; flaccidity, slackness, remissness;<BR>dilatoriness, inattention, weakness, cowardice, small-<BR>ness; relaxation of rule or connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैनेय|शैनेयः
शैनेय शैनेय, अस्, m. (fr. शिनि), N. of Sāt-<BR>yaki, the charioteer of Kṛṣṇa (represented as having<BR>destroyed a number of Dasyus, Mahā-bh. Droṇa-p.<BR>4748); (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Śini (a<BR>branch of the Yādavas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैन्य
शैन्य, आस्, m. pl. the descendants of Śini (who be-<BR>came Brāhmans, though originally of Kṣattriya race).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैरिक
शैरिक शैरिक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैरीयक|शैरीयकः
शैरीयक शैरीयक, अस्, m. a kind of shrub,<BR>blue Barleria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैरेयक
शैरेयक, अस्, m. = शैरीयक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैरीषि
शैरीषि शैरीषि, इस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>the Vedic Ṛṣi Su-vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल|शैलं|शैलः
शैल शैल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शिला), craggy,<BR>rocky, stony, mountainous; (अस्), m. a rock, crag,<BR>mountain, hill; a dike; (अम्), n. benzoin or storax;<BR>bitumen; a sort of collyrium, = रसाञ्जन, तार्-<BR>क्ष्य-शैल; (ई), f., see below.<BR>—शैल-कटक,<BR>अस्, m. the brow of a hill, slope of a mountain.<BR>—शैल-कुञ्ज, अस्, m. a mountain-thicket.<BR>—शैल-<BR>गन्ध, अम्, n. a kind of sandal (= शावर-चन्-<BR>दन).<BR>—शैल-गर्भाह्वा (˚भ-आह्˚), f. a kind<BR>of medicinal substance (= शिला-वल्का).<BR>—शैल-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, produced in or on mountains or rocks,<BR>&c.; (आ), f. epithet of Durgā; a kind of plant, =<BR>सिंह-पिप्पली; another plant, = गज-पिप्पली;<BR>(अम्), n. a fragrant resinous substance, benzoin or<BR>storax; bitumen.<BR>—शैल-जन, अस्, m. one who<BR>inhabits mountains, a mountaineer.<BR>—शैल-तस्, ind.<BR>from a mountain; than a mountain.<BR>—शैल-धन्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">Page1020-b+ 78</a>]<BR>वन्, आ, m. ‘rock-bowed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—शैल-<BR>धर, अस्, m. ‘mountain-holder,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa,<BR>(see गो-वर्धन.)<BR>—शैल-निर्यास, अस्, m. ‘rock-<BR>exudation,’ storax, benzoin.<BR>—शैल-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘mountain-lord,’ the Himālaya mountain.<BR>—शैल-<BR>पत्त्र, अस्, m. the Vilva tree.<BR>—शैल-पुत्री, f. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—शैल-भित्ति, इस्, f. a stone-cutter's chisel<BR>or axe, an instrument for dividing or cutting stones.<BR>—शैल-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, rocky, made of stone,<BR>consisting of stones.<BR>—शैल-रन्ध्र, अम्, n.<BR>‘rocky hollow,’ a cavern, cave.<BR>—शैल-राज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘king of mountains,’ epithet of the Himālaya;<BR>of Indra-kīla.<BR>—शैलराज-सुता, f. ‘daughter of<BR>Himālaya,’ epithet of Durgā.<BR>—शैल-रुग्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, crushed by mountains.<BR>—शैल-वनोपपन्न<BR>(˚न-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of mountains and<BR>woods.<BR>—शैल-वल्कला, f. a kind of medicinal<BR>substance (= शिला-वल्का).<BR>—शैल-वास, अस्, m. a<BR>mountain-habitation.<BR>—शैल-वीज, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>stony seeds,’ the marking-nut plant.<BR>—शैल-शिख-<BR>र, अम्, n. the crest or peak of a mountain.<BR>—शैल-<BR>शिखा, f. ‘mountain-top,’ a kind of metre.<BR>—शैल-<BR>शिविर, अम्, n. ‘rock-camp,’ the ocean.<BR>—शैल-<BR>शृङ्ग, अम्, n. a mountain-peak.<BR>—शैल-सार, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the strength of a mountain, as strong<BR>as a mountain, hard, firm as a rock.<BR>—शैल-सुता,<BR>f. ‘daughter of the mountain,’ epithet of Umā or<BR>Pārvatī, daughter of Himavat.<BR>—शैलसुता-चरण-<BR>राग-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, produced by the colour of<BR>the feet of Pārvatī.<BR>—शैलांश or शैलांश-<BR>देश (˚ल-अं˚), अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR>—शैला-<BR>ख्य (˚ल-आख्˚), अम्, n. a fragrant resinous sub-<BR>stance; benzoin.<BR>—शैलाग्र (˚ल-अग्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>peak of a mountain.<BR>—शैलाङ्ग or शैलाङ्ग-देश<BR>(˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR>—शैला-ज, अम्,<BR>n. (शैला for शैल), = शैल-ज, q. v.<BR>—शैलाट (˚ल-<BR>अट), अस्, m. a mountaineer, savage, barbarian; a<BR>lion; (an attendant on) an idol; crystal.<BR>—शै-<BR>लाधिप (˚ल-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘king of mountains,’<BR>epithet of the Himālaya.<BR>—शैलेन्द्र (˚ल-इन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘prince of mountains,’ epithet of the Himālaya.<BR>—शैलेन्द्र-स्थ, अस्, m. the Bhojpatra tree (=<BR>भूर्ज).<BR>—शैलेश-लिङ्ग, अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—शैलोदा (˚ल-उद्˚), f., N. of a river.<BR>—शैलोद्-<BR>भवा (˚ल-उद्˚), f. a kind of plant, a small species<BR>of पाषाण-भेदिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलक|शैलकं
शैलक, अम्, n. benzoin or storax; bitumen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलादि|शैलादिः
शैलादि, इस्, m., N. of Nandin (the attendant<BR>of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलावत्य
शैलावत्य, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैली
शैली, f. a short explanatory rule, concise explana-<BR>tion of a grammatical aphorism; a special or parti-<BR>cular interpretation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलेय|शैलेयं|शैलेयः
शैलेय, अस्, ई, अम्, produced in the mountains,<BR>&c., mountainous; produced from rocks; rocky,<BR>stony, mountain-like, hard; (अम्), n. a fragrant<BR>resin; benzoin or storax; a vegetable perfume (=<BR>मुरा); a kind of plant (= ताल-पर्णी); rock-salt;<BR>(अस्), m. a lion; a bee; (ई), f., N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—शैलेय-गन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, fragrant with benzoin<BR>or with the bituminous exudation of rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलेयिक
शैलेयिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to benzoin or storax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल्य|शैल्यं
शैल्य, अस्, -ली, अम्, rocky, stony, hard; (अम्),<BR>n. rockiness, stoniness, hardness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलाद
शैलाद शैलाद, अस्, m. (fr. शिलाद), a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलाल
शैलाल शैलाल, अम्, n. (fr. शिलालि, q. v.),<BR>the principles of acting, (this word seems to have<BR>been formed to account for the derivation of शैला-<BR>लिन् below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलालि
शैलालि, इस्, m. a proper N., (Śatapatha-Br. XIII.<BR>5, 3, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलालिन्
शैलालिन्, ई, m. an actor, dancer; (इनस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a school.<BR>—शैलालि-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलिक्य|शैलिक्यः
शैलिक्य शैलिक्य, अस्, m. (etymology doubt-<BR>ful), an impostor, hypocrite, pretended devotee (=<BR>सर्वलिङ्गिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूष|शैलूषः
शैलूष शैलूष, अस्, m. (said to be fr. शि-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">Page1020-c+ 79</a>]<BR>लूष, q. v.), an actor, public dancer, tumbler, &c.;<BR>a band-master, leader of a band, one who beats time<BR>at a concert (= ताल-धारक); a rogue, cheat; the<BR>Vilva tree, Ægle Marmelos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूषक
शैलूषक, अस्, m. = शैलूष above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूषि
शैलूषि, इस्, m. a patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi<BR>Kulmala-barhiṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूषिक|शैलूषिकः
शैलूषिक, अस्, m. one who follows the profession<BR>of an actor, &c. (= नट-वृत्त्य्-अन्वेषिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूषिकी
शैलूषिकी, f. a woman of the actor caste, an<BR>actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव|शैवं|शैवः
शैव शैव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शिव), relating or<BR>belonging to the god Śiva; (अस्), m. ‘a worshipper<BR>or follower of Śiva,’ N. of one of the three great<BR>divisions of modern Hindū sects, (the other two<BR>being the Vaiṣṇavas and Śāktas, see वैष्णव,<BR>शाक्त; the Śaivas believe in the superiority of Śiva<BR>to the other gods of the Tri-mūrti, and identify him<BR>with the Supreme Being as the destroying principle<BR>as well as source and essence of the whole universe;<BR>the temples dedicated to him in his popular symbol<BR>of the Liṅga [see शिव] are very numerous every-<BR>where, but the doctrines of the Śaivas as represented<BR>by their great teachers, such as Śaṅkara, are too<BR>philosophical for the majority of the people, who are<BR>more attracted by Viṣṇu, especially in his forms<BR>of Kṛṣṇa and Rāma: various divisions of Śaiva<BR>sects have prevailed at different times, the earlier<BR>divisions being those of the Raudras who have<BR>the Tri-śūla or trident marked on their foreheads,<BR>the Ugras who have the Ḍamaru or drum on their<BR>arms, the Bhāktas who have the Liṅga on their<BR>foreheads, the Jaṅgamas who have that symbol on<BR>their heads, and the Pāśupatas who have it marked<BR>on other parts of their bodies; the more modern<BR>divisions being the Daṇḍins or mendicant staff-<BR>bearers, including the Daś-nāmī-daṇḍins [cf. शङ्क-<BR>राचार्य], the Yogins who cultivate absorption into<BR>Śiva by suppression of breathing, fixing of the eyes,<BR>and eighty-four different attitudes, the Jaṅgamas or<BR>Liṅgavats, the Parama-haṃsas, the Aghorins, the<BR>Ūrdhva-bāhus, the Ākāśa-mukhins, and many others);<BR>a particular religious rite in honour of Durgā (con-<BR>sisting of devout meditation and prostration of the<BR>body); the thorn-apple; another plant or tree, =<BR>वसुक; (ई), f., N. of the goddess Manasā; (अम्),<BR>n. the Śiva-Purāṇa; the aquatic plant Vallisneria<BR>Octandra (= शैवाल).<BR>—शैव-गव, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a Gotra or family.<BR>—शैव-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tantra work.<BR>—शैव-ता, f. devotion to Śiva,<BR>worship of or belief in Śiva.<BR>—शैव-पुराण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Purāṇa, (see शिव-पुराण.)<BR>—शैव-<BR>वायवीय-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—शैव-<BR>सर्वस्व, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—शैव-सिद्धान्त-<BR>शेखर, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—शैवागम (˚व-<BR>आग्˚), N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव्य|शैव्यः
शैव्य, अस्, -वी, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>Śiva, &c.; of or belonging to the Śivis, (in this sense<BR>fr. शिवि); (अस्), m., N. of one of the four horses of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa [cf. सु-ग्रीव]; of a king and cham-<BR>pion in the Pāṇḍava army; a tribe of the Śivis, (in<BR>this sense fr. शिवि); (आ), f., N. of a river; of the wife<BR>of Hariścandra; of the wife of Śata-dhanu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवल|शैवलं|शैवलः
शैवल शैवल, अस्, m. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. IV. 38. fr. rt. 1. शी), a kind of aquatic plant,<BR>Vallisneria (or Blyxa) Octandra; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people, (also written शैवाल); (अम्), n. a kind<BR>of fragrant wood used in medicine (= पद्म-काष्-<BR>ठ); [cf. शेवाल, शैवाल, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवलिन्
शैवलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing the plant Śaivala;<BR>(इनी), f. a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवाल|शैवालं
शैवाल, अम्, n. the aquatic plant Vallisneria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवालक
शैवालक, अम्, n., at the end of a comp. = शै-<BR>वाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशव|शैशवं
शैशव शैशव, अम्, n. (fr. शिशु), childhood,<BR>infancy, pupilage, the period under age (i. e. under<BR>sixteen); N. of a portion of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशुनाग
शैशुनाग, आस्, m. pl. (fr. शिशु-नाग), N. of a<BR>dynasty founded by Śiśu-nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिर|शैशिरः
शैशिर शैशिर, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the<BR>Śiśira or dewy season; composed by Śaiśira; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a mountain; of a founder of a supposed<BR>separate Śākhā of the Ṛg-veda; of a dark kind of<BR>Caṭaka bird.<BR>—शैशिर-शाखा, f., N. of a Śākhā of<BR>the Ṛg-veda (perhaps only a subdivision of the<BR>Śākala).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिरि
शैशिरि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher of the White<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिरीय
शैशिरीय, N. of one of the seven Śākala texts.<BR>—शैशिरीय-शाखा, f. a subordinate branch of the<BR>Śākala-śākhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिरेय
शैशिरेय, अस्, m., N. of a teacher of the Ṛg-<BR>veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैषिक
शैषिक शैषिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a re-<BR>mainder, belonging to the end or termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैष्योपाध्यायिका
शैष्योपाध्यायिका शैष्योपाध्यायिका, f. (fr.<BR>शिष्य + उपाध्याय), instruction of youth, tuition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शो
शो शो (closely connected with rt. 1. शि,<BR>q. v.; according to some the original form<BR>was perhaps अश्; cf. अश्र, अश्रि, अश्मन्, &c.), cl.<BR>4. P. श्यति, शशौ, शास्यति, अशात् or अशासीत्, (Ved.<BR>also cl. 3. P. शिशाति), शातुम्, to sharpen, whet; to<BR>pare, attenuate, make thin or small; Pass. शायते:<BR>Caus. शाययति: Desid. शिशासति: Intens. शाशायते;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἀκή, ἀκμή, .ακρος, ἀκόνη, ἄκων, ἀκωκή,<BR>ἀκρέμων, ἀκριβήςσ, ὄκρις, ἄκανος, ἄκανθα, ἄκορνα,<BR>ὀξύς (i. e. ὀκ+τυ), ὄξος, ἄχωρ, ἄχορον, ἄχερδος,<BR>αἰχμή, κῶνος: Lat. acies, acus, acer, acidus,<BR>aculeus, catus (= शात), cos, cautes, citus (= शित),<BR>cuneus, cacu-men, (probably also) cio, cieo: Goth.<BR>aqvizi, ahana, hvotjan: probably Old Germ. hvez-<BR>jan: Angl. Sax. hvetan: Iceland. hvetia: Lith.<BR>as-trus, as-mu: Slav. os-tr: Hib. geur, gear,<BR>‘sharp;’ geire, ‘sharpness;’ geirim, ‘I whet, grease.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात|शातं|शातः
शात, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpened, &c. See s. v., p. 1000.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित|शितं
शित, अस्, आ, अम्. See under rt. 1. शि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यत्
श्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sharpening, whetting; paring,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोंस्
शोंस् शोंस्, a form assumed by rt. शंस् in<BR>certain sacrificial formularies. See rt. शंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोक|शोकः
शोक शोक, शोचन, &c. See under rt. 1.<BR>शुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच
शोच शोच, शोचिस्, &c. See under rt. 3. शुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोटीर्य|शोटीर्यं|शोटीर्य्य|शोटीर्य्यं
शोटीर्य शोटीर्य, अम्, n. valour, heroism;<BR>[cf. शुटीरता, शुटीर्य, शौटीर्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोठ|शोठः
शोठ शोठ. See rt. शुठ्, p. 1013, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण्
शोण् शोण् (perhaps to be regarded as a<BR>Nom. fr. शोण below), cl. 1. P. शोणति,<BR>शुशोण, शोणितुम्, to be or become red; to go,<BR>move, approach: Caus. शोणयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अशुशोणत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण|शोणं|शोणः
शोण, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (thought by some to be fr.<BR>स-वर्ण), coloured like the red lotus, red, crimson,<BR>of a crimson or chesnut colour; red in the face (from<BR>passion &c.); brown, bay; yellow; (अस्), m. the<BR>colour of the red lotus, red, crimson (the colour);<BR>fire or the god of fire; a sort of red sugar-cane; a<BR>chesnut or bay horse; a particular ocean; the river<BR>Śoṇa or Sone (sometimes written शोणा, f.; it rises<BR>in Gondwana in the district of Nagpore, on the<BR>table-land of Amara-kaṇṭaka, four or five miles east<BR>of the source of the Narma-dā or Nerbudda, and<BR>running first northerly and then easterly for five<BR>hundred miles falls into the Ganges above Pāṭali-<BR>putra or Patna); the plant Bignonia Indica; a proper<BR>N.; (अम्), n. blood; red-lead, minium; [cf. Slav.<BR>sini.]<BR>—शोण-झिण्टिका, f. a kind of red Barleria.<BR>—शोण-झिण्टी, f., N. of two plants (= कुरुवक,<BR>कण्टकिनी).<BR>—शोण-नद, N. of a river.<BR>—शोण-<BR>पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘red-leaved,’ a red kind of hogweed.<BR>—शोण-पद्मक, अम्, n. a red lotus.<BR>—शोण-<BR>पुष्पक, अस्, m. ‘red-flowered,’ the Kovidāra tree.<BR>—शोण-पुष्पी, f. ‘red-flowered,’ a kind of plant<BR>(= सिन्दूर-पुष्पी).<BR>—शोण-रत्न, अम्, n. a red<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">Page1021-b+ 74</a>]<BR>gem; a ruby.<BR>—शोण-सङ्गम, अस्, m. ‘Śoṇa-con-<BR>fluence,’ N. of a place.<BR>—शोणाम्बु (˚ण-अम्˚), उस्,<BR>m. ‘having crimson waters or having waters of<BR>blood,’ N. of one of the seven clouds at the destruc-<BR>tion of the world.<BR>—शोणाश्मन् (˚ण-अश्˚), आ, m. a<BR>red stone; a ruby.<BR>—शोणोपल (˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a red stone; a ruby.<BR>—शोणोल्लीढ (˚ण-उल्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, sharpened or polished on a whetstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणक|शोणकः
शोणक, अस्, m. the plant Bignonia or Calosanthes<BR>Indica, (this plant has many synonyms; cf. कुटन्-<BR>नट, नट, मण्डूक-पर्ण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणाक|शोणाकः
शोणाक, अस्, m. = शोणक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणित|शोणितं
शोणित, अस्, आ, अम्, red, crimson, purple; (अम्),<BR>n. blood; saffron.<BR>—शोणित-चन्दन, अम्, n. red<BR>sandal.<BR>—शोणित-प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking blood;<BR>blood-sucking.<BR>—शोणित-पारणा, f. ‘breakfast of<BR>blood,’ a meal of flesh-meat.<BR>—शोणित-पुर, अम्,<BR>n. the city of the Asura Vāṇa (= वाण-पुर).<BR>—शोणित-वर्णन, अम्, n. description of the nature<BR>and properties of blood.<BR>—शोणित-वर्णनीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, treating of the above.<BR>—शोणित-विन्दु-वर्षिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, showering drops of blood.<BR>—शोणित-स्नात,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bathed in blood.<BR>—शोणितादिग्ध (˚त-<BR>आद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blood-stained.<BR>—शोणितार्शिन् (˚त-<BR>अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, suffering from piles attended with<BR>excretions of blood.<BR>—शोणिताह्वय (˚त-आह्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘blood-named,’ saffron.<BR>—शोणितोक्षित (˚त-उक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, blood-stained, sprinkled with blood.<BR>—शोणितोत्पल (˚त-उत्˚), अम्, n. a red lotus.<BR>—शो-<BR>णितोपल (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, m. ‘blood-stone,’ a ruby,<BR>(according to some also अम्, n.)<BR>—शोणितौघ<BR>(˚त-ओघ), अस्, m. a torrent or stream of blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणिमन्
शोणिमन्, आ, m. redness, the quality of being red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथ|शोथः
शोथ शोथ, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 4. fr. rt. शु, ‘to go;’ evidently connected with<BR>rt. श्वि), swelling, intumescence, tumefaction from<BR>disease, dropsy.<BR>—शोथ-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying<BR>or removing swellings, discutient; (ई), f. hogweed,<BR>Boerhavia Diffusa; a kind of shrub (= शाल-पर्णी).<BR>—शोथ-जित्, त्, त्, त्, overcoming or removing swell-<BR>ings, discutient; (त्), f. hogweed; the marking-nut<BR>plant.<BR>—शोथ-जिह्म, अस्, m. hogweed.<BR>—शोथ-<BR>रोग, अस्, m. ‘swelling disease,’ dropsy.<BR>—शोथ-<BR>रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, suffering from dropsy, dropsical.<BR>—शोथ-हृत्, त्, त्, त्, removing swellings, discutient;<BR>(त्), m. the marking-nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथक|शोथकः
शोथक, अस्, m. = शोथ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोध|शोधः
शोध शोध, शोधक, शोधन, शोधित,<BR>&c. See under rt. शुध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोपारीपाक
शोपारीपाक शोपारी-पाक, a particular me-<BR>dicinal decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोफ|शोफः
शोफ शोफ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. श्वि; cf. शोथ),<BR>intumescence, morbid swelling, tumefaction, bloated-<BR>ness, flabbiness.<BR>—शोफ-घ्नी, f. a kind of shrub<BR>(= शाल-पर्णी); a kind of red hogweed.<BR>—शोफ-<BR>नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, removing swellings; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of tree (= नील).<BR>—शोफ-हृत्, त्, त्, त्, re-<BR>moving swellings; (त्), m. the marking-nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभ
शोभ शोभ, शोभन, शोभित, &c. See<BR>under rt. 1. शुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोली
शोली शोली, f. wild turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोशुचत्
शोशुचत् शोशुचत्, अत्, अती, अत् (fr. Intens.<BR>of rt. 3. शुच्), Ved. shining very brightly, very<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोशुचान
शोशुचान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining very brightly,<BR>very radiant, resplendent; [cf. शुशुचान.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोशुच्यमान
शोशुच्यमान शोशुच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>Intens. of rt. 1. शुच्), sorrowing intensely, grieving<BR>deeply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोशुभ्यमान
शोशुभ्यमान शोशुभ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>Intens. of rt. 1. शुभ्), shining very much, very<BR>brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोष|शोषः
शोष शोष, शोषन, शोषित, &c. See<BR>under rt. शुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोस्
शोस् शोस् (?), ind. a particle of reproach<BR>or contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक|शौकं
शौक शौक, अम्, n. (fr. शुक), a flock of<BR>parrots; (fr. शोक?), sorrowfulness, (according to<BR>Śabda-k. = स्त्रीणां करणम्, for करुणम्?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौकर|शौकरं
शौकर शौकर or शौकरव, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a particular Tīrtha (described in a chapter of the<BR>Vārāha-Purāṇa called Jambūkopākhyāna).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्त|शौक्तं
शौक्त शौक्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शुक्त), acid,<BR>acetic, acetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तिक
1. शौक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, acid, acetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तिक
शौक्तिक 2. शौक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शुक्ति),<BR>relating to a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तिकेय|शौक्तिकेयं
शौक्तिकेय, अम्, n. a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तेय|शौक्तेयं
शौक्तेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a pearl; (अम्),<BR>n. a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्र
शौक्र शौक्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शुक्र), seminal,<BR>relating to sperm, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्लिकेय|शौक्लिकेयः
शौक्लिकेय शौक्लिकेय, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>poison, (probably for शौल्किकेय, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्ल्य|शौक्ल्यं
शौक्ल्य शौक्ल्य, अम्, n. (fr. शुक्ल), white-<BR>ness, clearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौङ्ग
शौङ्ग शौङ्ग, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौङ्गीपुत्र
शौङ्गी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौङ्गेय|शौङ्गेयः
शौङ्गेय शौङ्गेय, अस्, m. (doubtful), epi-<BR>thet of Garuḍa or a black-winged enemy of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौच|शौचं
शौच शौच, अम्, n. (fr. शुचि), purification<BR>from personal defilement (especially from defilement<BR>caused by the death of a relation &c.); evacuation of<BR>excrement; freedom from defilement, purity, cleanness;<BR>honesty; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—शौच-कल्प, अस्,<BR>m. mode of purification, purificatory rite.<BR>—शौच-<BR>कूप, अस्, m. ‘cleansing-pit,’ a privy.<BR>—शौच-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. purity.<BR>—शौच-विधि, इस्, m. rule of purifi-<BR>cation (after defilement by the death of a relation<BR>&c.), directions for cleansing the person.<BR>—शौचा-<BR>चार (˚च-आच्˚), अस्, m. a purificatory rite, rule of<BR>purification established by immemorial custom, mode<BR>of cleansing the person by ablution &c. (after voiding<BR>excrement or contracting any defilement).<BR>—शौचेप्सु<BR>(˚च-ईप्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, wishing or intending to obtain<BR>purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचिक|शौचिकः
शौचिक, अस्, m. a cleanser, cleaner; a particular<BR>mixed caste (the son of a Śauṇḍika and a Kaivarta<BR>woman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचिवृक्षि
शौचिवृक्षि, इस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचेय|शौचेयः
शौचेय, अस्, m. a washerman; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचद्रथ
शौचद्रथ शौचद्रथ, अस्, m., Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic of a descendant of Śucad-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौट्
शौट् शौट् (also written शौड्), cl. 1. P.<BR>शौटति, शुशौट, शौटितुम्, to be proud<BR>or haughty: Caus. शौटयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशु-<BR>शौटत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर|शौटीरः
शौटीर, अस्, आ, अम्, proud, haughty; (अस्), m. a<BR>hero; a proud or haughty man (but of low tribe or<BR>occupation); an upstart; one who abandons the<BR>world, an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर्य|शौटीर्यं|शौटीर्य्य|शौटीर्य्यं
शौटीर्य, अम्, n. pride, arrogance; heroism,<BR>prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौड्
शौड् शौड् (= rt. शौट्), cl. 1. P. शौडति,<BR>&c., to be proud or haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौड
शौड, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डर्य|शौंडर्य|शौण्डर्य्य
शौण्डर्य, अम्, n. pride, arrogance; [cf. शौ-<BR>टीर्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डीर|शौंडीर|शौण्डीरः
शौण्डीर, अस्, आ, अम्, proud, haughty; elevated,<BR>looking upwards; (also written शौण्डिर, शौडीर.)<BR>—शौण्डीर-ता, f. haughtiness, pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्ड|शौंड|शौण्डः
शौण्ड शौण्ड, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शुण्डा), fond of<BR>spirituous liquor, addicted to drinking; drunk, in-<BR>toxicated; (ई), f. long pepper; another sort (=<BR>चव्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिक|शौंडिक|शौंडिकः|शौण्डिकः
शौण्डिक, अस्, m. a distiller and vender of spirituous<BR>liquors, vintner; a particular mixed caste (the son<BR>of a Kaivarta and a Gāndhika woman); (ई), f. a<BR>female vintner or keeper of a tavern or dram shop<BR>(regarded as one of the eight Akulas according to<BR>the Śāktas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिकेय|शौंडिकेय|शौंडिकेयः|शौण्डिकेयः
शौण्डिकेय, अस्, m. a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिन्|शौंडिन्
शौण्डिन्, ई, m. = शौण्डिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डीक
शौण्डीक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्धाक्षर
शौद्धाक्षर शौद्धाक्षर, अस्, m., scil. सन्-<BR>धि, epithet of a particular Sandhi, (viz. the insertion<BR>of श् before चन्द्र, e. g. पुरु-श्-चन्द्र; of ष् be-<BR>fore कृ, e. g. परि-ष्-कृण्वन्, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्धोदनि|शौद्धोदनिः
शौद्धोदनि शौद्धोदनि, इस्, m. (fr. शुद्धो-<BR>दन), ‘son of Śuddhodana,’ a patronymic of the<BR>great Buddha (founder of the Buddhist religion, see<BR>बुद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्र|शौद्रः
शौद्र शौद्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शूद्र), servile,<BR>relating or belonging to the Śūdra or lowest tribe;<BR>(अस्), m. the son of a man of either of the first three<BR>classes by a Śūdra woman, (the last of the twelve<BR>kinds of sons acknowledged in the ancient Hindū<BR>law.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौधिका
शौधिका शौधिका, f. a variety of panic,<BR>(Panicum Italicum, = रक्त-कङ्गु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौन|शौनं
शौन शौन, अम्, n. (fr. शूना), meat kept<BR>at a slaughter-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनिक|शौनिकः
शौनिक, अस्, m. a butcher, poulterer, vender of<BR>the flesh of beasts or birds; chase, hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनक|शौनकः
शौनक शौनक, अस्, m., N. of the reputed<BR>author of the Ṛg-veda Prātiśākhya and of certain<BR>Kalpa-sūtras and various other Vedic compositions<BR>and works on law, (he is described as the teacher of<BR>Kātyāyana and especially of Āśvalāyana; he is said<BR>to have united the Bāṣkala and Śākala Śākhās,<BR>and is sometimes identified with the Vedic Ṛṣi<BR>Gṛtsa-mada; but according to the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa,<BR>Śaunaka was a son of Gṛtsa-mada, and originated<BR>the system of four castes; the various legends about<BR>him are very confused.)<BR>—शौनक-कल्प-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of certain Kalpa-sūtras (ascribed to<BR>Śaunaka and supposed to have been destroyed by<BR>the author).<BR>—शौनक-गृह्य-सूत्र, अम्, n. the<BR>Gṛhya-sūtras of the Ṛg-veda ascribed to Śaunaka.<BR>—शौनकानुक्रमणी (˚क-अन्˚), f. an Anukra-<BR>maṇī or Vedic index ascribed to Śaunaka.<BR>—शौन-<BR>कारण्यक (˚क-आर्˚), अम्, n. an Āraṇyaka ascribed<BR>to Śaunaka (probably identified with the Aitareyā-<BR>raṇyaka).<BR>—शौनकोपनिषद् (˚क-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of<BR>an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनकिन्
शौनकिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the pupils or followers of<BR>Śaunaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनकीपुत्र
शौनकी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनकीय
शौनकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or composed<BR>by Śaunaka or the Śaunakīyas, (शौनकीय-च-<BR>तुराध्यायिका, ‘Śaunaka's treatise in four chapters,’<BR>i. e. the Atharva-veda Prātiśākhya); (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the pupils or school of Śaunaka.<BR>—शौनकीय-च-<BR>तुराध्यायिका, f., N. of the above Prātiśākhya.<BR>—शौनकीय-चरण, N. of a Caraṇa (probably<BR>founded by the author of the Śākala-prātiśākhya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनहोत्र
शौनहोत्र शौनहोत्र, अस्, m. the son of<BR>Śuna-hotra and grandson of Bharad-vāja; epithet of<BR>the Vedic Ṛṣi Gṛtsa-mada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभ|शौभं|शौभः
शौभ शौभ, अस्, m. (fr. शुभ), a god, di-<BR>vinity; the Areca or betel-nut tree (= गुवाक);<BR>(अम्), n. the city of Hariścandra (fabled to be sus-<BR>pended in the air, see हरि-श्-चन्द्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभनेय|शौभनेयः
शौभनेय शौभनेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शोभना),<BR>sprung from a handsome mother; relating to any-<BR>thing handsome or brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभाञ्जन|शौभांजन|शौभांजनः|शौभाञ्जनः
शौभाञ्जन शौभाञ्जन, अस्, m. (fr. शोभाञ्-<BR>जन, q. v.), the tree Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभिक|शौभिकः
शौभिक शौभिक, अस्, m. (probably con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">Page1022-b+ 73</a>]<BR>nected with शुभ), a juggler, conjurer (= इन्द्र-<BR>जालिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभ्रेय|शौभ्रेयः
शौभ्रेय शौभ्रेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or be-<BR>longing to anything white or shining (e. g. to silver,<BR>talc, sandal, &c.); (अस्), m. ‘son of Śubhrā,’ a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर
शौर शौर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शूर), relating to<BR>a hero, heroic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौरदेव्यः|शौरदेव्य
शौरदेव्यः, in Ṛg-veda VIII. 70, 15. appa-<BR>rently acc. pl. of शौरदेवी, qualifying गाः, ‘cows,’<BR>and explained by Sāy. thus, दीव्यन्ति क्रीडन्त इति<BR>देवा योद्धारः शूराश्-च ते देवाश्-च शूर-देवाः,<BR>तेषां हितं शौरदेवं युद्धं तत्-सम्-<BR>बन्धिन्यो गाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौरसेन
शौरसेन, अम्, n. (fr. शूर-सेन), the language<BR>spoken by the people of Śūra-sena; (ई), f. a Prākṛt<BR>dialect supposed to have been spoken at Mathurā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौरि|शौरिः
शौरि, इस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; of Bala-<BR>rāma (as descended from Śūra); the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्य|शौर्यं|शौर्य्य|शौर्य्यं
शौर्य, अम्, n. heroism, valour, prowess, might;<BR>the heroic branch of the dramatic art, representation<BR>of war and supernatural events on the stage (= आर-<BR>भटी).<BR>—शौर्योपार्जित (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ac-<BR>quired by valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्प|शौर्पः|शौर्प्प
शौर्प शौर्प, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शूर्प), measured<BR>by a winnowing basket &c., belonging to a winnow-<BR>ing fan &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्पणाय्य
शौर्पणाय्य, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्पिक|शौर्पिकः
शौर्पिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = शौर्प above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्क|शौल्कं|शौल्कः
शौल्क शौल्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शुल्क), relating<BR>to tolls or customs or taxes, levied (as a tax &c.); (अस्),<BR>m. a superintendant of tolls or customs, a custom-<BR>house officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्कशालिक
शौल्कशालिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शुल्क-शाला), of or<BR>belonging to a custom-house, derived from a custom-<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्कायनि
शौल्कायनि, इस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्किक|शौल्किकः
शौल्किक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to taxes or tolls;<BR>(अस्), m. a superintendant of tolls or customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्किकेय|शौल्किकेयः
शौल्किकेय शौल्किकेय, अस्, m. (fr. शुल्किक),<BR>a kind of poison (said to be produced in a country<BR>called Śulkika; according to some the venom of a<BR>kind of snake).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्फ|शौल्फं
शौल्फ शौल्फ, अम्, n. a kind of vegetable<BR>(commonly called Śulphā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्विक|शौल्विकः
शौल्विक शौल्विक, अस्, m. (fr. शुल्व), a cop-<BR>persmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौव|शौवं
शौव शौव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. श्वन्), relating<BR>or belonging to dogs, canine; (अस्), m., N. of a par-<BR>ticular Udgītha; (अम्), n. a pack or number of<BR>dogs; the nature or state of a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवन|शौवनं
शौवन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to canine nature;<BR>having the qualities of a dog; (अम्), n. the nature of<BR>a dog; the progeny of a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवापद|शौवापदं
शौवापद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. श्वा-पद), relating to<BR>a wild beast or beast of prey, ferocious, savage, wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवस्तिक|शौवस्तिकं
शौवस्तिक शौवस्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. श्वस्),<BR>of or belonging to to-morrow, lasting till to-morrow,<BR>ephemeral.<BR>—शौवस्तिक-त्व, अम्, n. the lasting or<BR>enduring till to-morrow, ephemeralness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौष्कल|शौष्कलः
शौष्कल शौष्कल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शुष्कली),<BR>eating fish and flesh; (अस्), m. an habitual eater of<BR>meat; a vender of flesh, dealer in flesh or dried<BR>meat; (अम्), n. the price of dried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चम्
श्चम् श्चम्, for rt. चम्, to consume, (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 104, 2.<BR>श्चम्नन् = भक्षयन्तु, but also referrible to rt.<BR>1. शम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुत्
श्चुत् 1. श्चुत् or 1. श्च्युत् (perhaps fr. a<BR>noun formed fr. an original rt. श्च्यु; cf.<BR>rts. 1. च्यु, 2. च्युत्), cl. 1. P. श्चोतति or श्च्योतति,<BR>चुश्चोत or चुश्च्योत, अश्चुतत्, अश्चोतीत्, &c., श्चोतितुम्<BR>or श्च्योतितुम्, to ooze, trickle, flow, exude, drop,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">Page1022-c+ 77</a>]<BR>distil; to sprinkle, scatter, diffuse, shed, pour out;<BR>Pass. श्चुत्यते, Aor. अश्चोति, &c.: Caus. श्चोतयति,<BR>&c.; [cf. Goth. skevjan, skura; Angl. Sax. scur.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुत्
2. श्चुत् or 2. श्च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, distilling, sprinkling,<BR>shedding, (at the end of comps., e. g. जल-श्˚, shed-<BR>ding or sprinkling water.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुतित
श्चुतित or श्च्युतित, अस्, आ, अम्, oozed, exuded,<BR>issued, sprinkled, shed; oozing, dropping, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुतित्वा
श्चुतित्वा, ind. having oozed, having exuded or<BR>flowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चोत|श्चोतः
श्चोत or श्च्योत, अस्, m. oozing, trickling out,<BR>sprinkling, aspersion, pouring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चोतत्
श्चोतत् or श्च्योतत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, oozing, trickling,<BR>flowing; shedding.<BR>—श्च्योतन्-मयूख, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>diffusing light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चोतन|श्चोतनं
श्चोतन, अम्, n. the act of oozing, flowing; ex-<BR>udation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नथ्
श्नथ् श्नथ्, cl. 1. P. श्नथति (2nd sing.<BR>Impv. Ved. श्नथिहि), शश्नाथ, अश्न-<BR>थीत् (श्नथिष्टम्, ‘you two have destroyed,’ Ṛg-<BR>veda VII. 99, 5), श्नथितुम्, Ved. to strike, injure,<BR>hurt, destroy, slay, kill: Caus. श्नथयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अशिश्नथत् (अशिश्नत् = हिनस्ति, Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>28, 3), to do violence, kill; Desid. शिश्नथिषति:<BR>Intens. शाश्नथ्यते, शाश्नत्ति; [cf. Goth. snithan,<BR>‘to cut;’ Old Germ. snîdu; Angl. Sax. snidhan;<BR>Hib. slethe, ‘cutting, striking.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नथयत्
श्नथयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. injuring, destroy-<BR>ing, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नथित
श्नथित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hurt, wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नथितृ
श्नथितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who slays or<BR>kills, a smiter; killing, destroying, destructive, deadly,<BR>fatal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नम्
श्नम् श्नम्, (in grammar) a technical term<BR>for the verbal affix न, the characteristic sign of the<BR>seventh class of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ना
श्ना श्ना, (in grammar) a technical term for<BR>the affix ना, the characteristic sign of the ninth class<BR>of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नु
श्नु श्नु, (in grammar) a technical term for<BR>the affix नु, the characteristic sign of the fifth class<BR>of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मन्
श्मन् श्मन्, अ, n. (according to some ind.),<BR>the face, mouth; the body (according to Nirukta<BR>III. 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशा
श्मशा श्मशा, f., Ved. the channel of a<BR>river, (Sāy. = कुल्या); the brim or rim or edge of<BR>(the Soma) vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशान|श्मशानं
श्मशान श्मशान, अम्, n. (according to Ni-<BR>rukta III. 5. fr. श्म for श्मन् = शरीर + शान =<BR>शयन; or fr. श्म = शरीरम् + शृणाति or शम्-<BR>नाति; according to others = अश्म-शयन), ‘a place<BR>of repose for bodies, place for destroying bodies,’ a<BR>cemetery, sepulchre, burning or burial-ground, (पारे-<BR>श्मशानम्, beyond the cemetery); = ब्रह्म-रन्-<BR>ध्र, q. v.<BR>—श्मशान-काली, f., N. of a female evil<BR>spirit or form of Durgā (= कालिका).<BR>—श्मशान-<BR>गोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, frequenting burning-grounds,<BR>employed in places for burning the dead, (Manu<BR>XI. 39.)<BR>—श्मशान-निवासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in<BR>burial-grounds, a ghost, spectre.<BR>—श्मशान-भाज्,<BR>क्, m. ‘inhabiting burial-grounds,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—श्मशान-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, abiding in burial-<BR>grounds or cemeteries, a ghost, spectre.<BR>—श्मशान-<BR>वाट, अस्, m. a cemetery-enclosure, burying-ground.<BR>—श्मशान-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in cemeteries,<BR>a ghost, spectre; (ई), m. epithet of Śiva; (इनी), f.<BR>epithet of Kālī or Durgā.<BR>—श्मशान-वेश्मन्, आ,<BR>m. ‘inhabiting cemeteries,’ epithet of Śiva or Mahā-<BR>deva; a ghost.<BR>—श्मशान-वैराग्य, अम्, n. mo-<BR>mentary despondency or abandonment of worldly<BR>desire at the sight of a cemetery.<BR>—श्मशान-शूल,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. an impaling stake in a cemetery.<BR>—श्मशान-साधन, अम्, n. magical rites per-<BR>formed in a cemetery to obtain control over evil spirits.<BR>—श्मशानाग्नि (˚न-अग्˚), इस्, m. the fire of a<BR>burning-ground.<BR>—श्मशानालय (˚न-आल्˚), अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">Page1023-a+ 75</a>]<BR>‘cemetery-house,’ a cemetery.<BR>—श्मशानालय-<BR>वासिनी (˚न-आल्˚), f. ‘inhabiting cemeteries,’ epithet<BR>of Kālī or Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रु
श्मश्रु श्मश्रु, उ, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>V. 28. and Nirukta III. 5. fr. श्मन्, ‘the face,’ +<BR>rt. श्रि), ‘growing on the face,’ the beard.<BR>—श्म-<BR>श्रु-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose beard has grown.<BR>—श्मश्रु-प्रवृद्धि, इस्, f. the growth of a beard.<BR>—श्मश्रु-मुखी, f. ‘beard-faced,’ a woman with<BR>a beard (= पालि, पाली).<BR>—श्मश्रु-वर्धक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘a beard-cutter,’ a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुल
श्मश्रुल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a beard, bearded,<BR>one who lets his beard grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रूयमाण
श्मश्रूयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being as if bearded,<BR>having something like a beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मसि
श्मसि श्मसि, Ved. for उश्मसि, fr. rt. वश्,<BR>q. v., (Sāy. = कामयामहे, we desire, Ṛg-veda II.<BR>31, 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मील्
श्मील् श्मील् (also written स्मील्; cf. rt.<BR>मील्), cl. 1. P. श्मीलति, श्मीलितुम्,<BR>to wink, contract the eyelids; to twinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलन|श्मीलनं
श्मीलन, अम्, n. winking; twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलित|श्मीलितं
श्मीलित, अस्, आ, अम्, winked, blinked; (अम्), n. a<BR>wink, winking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मे
श्मे श्मे, ind. an abbreviation for पार्थु-<BR>रश्मे, (see पार्थुरश्म.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यत्
श्यत् श्यत्. See under rt. शो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यन्
श्यन् श्यन्, (in grammar) a technical term<BR>for the syllable य or characteristic sign of the fourth<BR>class of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यान|श्यानः
श्यान श्यान, &c. See under rt. श्यै, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यापर्ण
श्यापर्ण श्यापर्ण, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>family; (अस्, आ, अम्), belonging to the Śyāparṇa<BR>family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यापर्णीय
श्यापर्णीय, अस्, m. a man belonging to the<BR>Śyāparṇa race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यापर्णेय
श्यापर्णेय, see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. VI. 2, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याम|श्यामः
श्याम श्याम, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>श्यै or connected with rt. श्वि; cf. श्येत, श्वेत),<BR>black or dark-coloured, dark-blue, dark-brown,<BR>brown; dark-green, green; dark, shady, dusky;<BR>(अस्), m. black, brown, green (the colour); a cloud;<BR>the Kokila or Indian cuckoo; a sacred fig-tree at<BR>Prayāga or Allahabad; a kind of plant (= वृद्-<BR>ध-दारक); epithet of various other trees and<BR>plants (= पीलु; = श्यामाक; = दमनक; = गन्-<BR>ध-तृण); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a Vedic Caraṇa, (a<BR>subdivision^1 of the Maitrāyaṇīyas); the thorn-apple,<BR>Datura Metel; N. of a son of Śūra; (आ), f. night;<BR>shade, shadow; a dark woman; a woman who has<BR>not borne children; another kind of woman (de-<BR>scribed as from eight to sixteen years of age, resem-<BR>bling in complexion the blossom of the Priyaṅgu or<BR>in shape its slender stalk); a form of Durgā (much<BR>worshipped by the Tāntrikas); a cow; a small sing-<BR>ing bird with black plumage (commonly called<BR>Śāmā, Turdus Macrourus); the female of the Indian<BR>cuckoo; a kind of plant (= प्रियङ्गु); turmeric;<BR>the sacred basil; the climbing-plant Ichnocarpus or<BR>Echites Frutescens (= शारिवा); indigo (= नीलिका);<BR>a kind of dark creeper (= कृष्ण-शारिवा); epithet<BR>of various other plants and shrubs (= कृष्णा; =<BR>वागुजी; = गुडूची; = गुग्गुलु; = सोम-लता; =<BR>कृष्ण-त्रिवृता; = गुन्द्रा; = कस्तूरी; = वट-<BR>पत्त्री; = वन्दा; = नील-पुनर्णवा; = नील-<BR>दूर्वा; = पिप्पली; = शिंशपा; = श्यामाक); epi-<BR>thet of the river Yamunā or Jumnā; the seed of<BR>the lotus, = पद्म-वीज; (अम्), n. black pepper;<BR>sea-salt; [cf. Gr. κύανο-ς; Lith. sze†mas; Hib.<BR>ciar, ‘dark-brown, black.’]<BR>—श्याम-कण्ठ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘black-throated, blue-throated,’ a peacock; a<BR>kind of small bird; an epithet of Śiva; [cf. नील-<BR>कण्ठ.]<BR>—श्याम-कन्दा, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>अति-विषा).<BR>—श्याम-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, black-<BR>eared; (अस्), m. a horse suitable for a horse-sacrifice.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">Page1023-b+ 79</a>]<BR>—श्याम-काण्डा, f. a kind of Dūrvā grass (=<BR>गण्ड-दूर्वा).<BR>—श्याम-ग्रन्थि, इस्, f. = श्याम-<BR>काण्डा.<BR>—श्याम-ता, f. or श्याम-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>blackness, brownness, darkness.<BR>—श्याम-देव, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—श्याम-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘black-<BR>leaved,’ the Tamāla tree.<BR>—श्याम-भास्, आस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, of a brilliant black, glossy black.<BR>—श्याम-लता,<BR>f. the climbing-plant Ichnocarpus or Echites Fru-<BR>tescens.<BR>—श्याम-शवल, औ, m. du. Yama's two<BR>watch-dogs, (see शवल.)<BR>—श्याम-सुन्दर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘dark and beautiful,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—श्या-<BR>माङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, black-bodied, dark-<BR>bodied, black; (अस्), m. the planet Mercury or its<BR>regent.<BR>—श्यामा-पूजा, f. the worship of Śyāmā or<BR>Durgā (on the new moon of the month Kārttika).<BR>—श्यामाम्ली (˚म-अम्˚), f. a kind of shrub (= नी-<BR>लाम्ली).<BR>—श्यामा-रहस्य, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—श्यामी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make black<BR>or dark-coloured.<BR>—श्यामी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति,<BR>&c., to become black or dark-blue.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामक|श्यामकं|श्यामकः
श्यामक, अस्, m. a kind of edible grain, (Panicum<BR>Frumentaceum or Colonum); a gramineous plant;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of grass (= रोहिष-तृण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामल|श्यामलः
श्यामल, अस्, आ, अम्, blackish, black, dark-blue,<BR>brownish, dusky; (अस्), m. black (the colour); black<BR>pepper; the sacred fig-tree; a large bee; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of Durgā or Pārvatī; epithet of various plants<BR>(= अश्व-गन्धा; = कट-भी; = जम्बु; = कस्-<BR>तूरी).<BR>—श्यामल-चूडा, f. a kind of shrub (=<BR>गुञ्जा).<BR>—श्यामलेक्षु (˚ल-इक्˚), उस्, m. a sort of<BR>dark sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामलिका
श्यामलिका, f. the indigo plant (= नीली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाक|श्यामाकः
श्यामाक, अस्, m. = श्यामक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाय
श्यामाय, Nom. A. श्यामायते, -यितुम्, to be-<BR>come black or dark-blue or green, to prove impure<BR>(as gold).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामायनि
श्यामायनि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher of the Yajur-<BR>veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामायनीय
श्यामायनीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Vedic Caraṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामायमान
श्यामायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, growing dark or<BR>dusk, becoming dusky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामिका
श्यामिका, f. blackness, impurity, alloy (of metals<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामित
श्यामित, अस्, आ, अम्, blackened, turned or be-<BR>come black; darkened, discoloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याव|श्यावः
श्याव, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (connected with श्याम),<BR>brown, bay, of a brown or dark-brown colour, dark,<BR>dusky, livid; drawn by bay horses (said of chariots,<BR>Ved.); (अस्), m. brown (the colour); a proper N.;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the horses of the Sun; (ई), f., Ved.<BR>night (= रात्रि, Naigh. I. 7); [cf. Russ. sivyĭ,<BR>‘dark-grey.’]<BR>—श्याव-तैल, अस्, m. ‘having dark-<BR>brown oil,’ the mango tree.<BR>—श्याव-दत्, अन्, अती,<BR>अत्, or श्याव-दन्त or श्याव-दन्तक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has naturally brown or discoloured teeth,<BR>brown-toothed, black-toothed; (according to some<BR>the latter two words may mean ‘having a little tooth<BR>growing between or over the two front teeth.’)<BR>—श्यावाश्व (˚व-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘having brown or<BR>bay horses,’ N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi, (an Ātreya and<BR>author of several hymns in the fifth, eighth, and<BR>ninth Maṇḍalas of the Ṛg-veda.)<BR>—श्यावाश्वि, इस्,<BR>m. a patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Andhīgu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यावक
श्यावक, अस्, आ, अम्, brown, bay; (अस्), m., Ved.,<BR>N. of a person under the especial protection of Indra;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the horses of the Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याल|श्यालः
श्याल श्याल, अस्, m. (also written स्याल),<BR>a wife's brother, brother-in-law; a proper N.; (ई),<BR>f. a wife's sister; [cf. Gr. ἀέλιοι, εἰλιόνες.]<BR>—श्याल-<BR>नामन्, आ, &c., called after the name of a brother-<BR>in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालक|श्यालकः
श्यालक, अस्, m. a wife's brother; a poor or<BR>miserable brother-in-law; (अकी), f. a wife's sister;<BR>sister-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालिका
श्यालिका, f. a wife's sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याव|श्यावः
श्याव श्याव. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येत|श्येतः
श्येत श्येत, अस्, ता or श्येनी, अम् (probably<BR>connected with श्वेत), white, of a white colour;<BR>(अस्), m. white (the colour).<BR>—श्येत-कोलक, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">Page1023-c+ 77</a>]<BR>m. the Saphara fish, Cyprinus Saphore (commonly<BR>called Puṃṭī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येन|श्येनः
श्येन, अस्, m. white (the colour); whiteness,<BR>paleness; a hawk, falcon, bird of prey; ‘hawk-like<BR>conduct,’ violence; a horse (Ved.); a particular sacri-<BR>ficial ceremony or imprecatory rite; N. of a Vedic<BR>Ṛṣi (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 188); (ई),<BR>f. white, (see above under श्येत); a female hawk;<BR>N. of a daughter of Kaśyapa (regarded as the mother<BR>of hawks); a woman (described as resembling a<BR>lily-leaf); a species of the Tṛṣṭubh metre.<BR>—श्येन-<BR>कपोतीय, अम्, n. the story of the hawk and<BR>pigeon; [cf. शिवि.]<BR>—श्येन-करण, अम्, n. or<BR>श्येन-करणिका, f. acting like a hawk (i. e. rashly<BR>or desperately); burning on a separate funeral pile.<BR>—श्येन-घण्टा, f. a kind of plant (= दन्ती).<BR>—श्येन-चित्, त्, m. a hawk-feeder, hawk-keeper,<BR>falconer; a receptacle shaped like a hawk (for sacri-<BR>ficial fire &c.)<BR>—श्येन-जित्, त्, m. a proper N.<BR>—श्येनजिद्-आख्यान, अम्, n., N. of an episode in<BR>the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—श्येन-जीविन्, ई, m. one who<BR>lives by selling or training hawks, a falconer.<BR>—श्ये-<BR>न-पत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. going like a hawk or<BR>going as fast as a horse.<BR>—श्येनोपदेश (˚न-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. recommendation or injunction to women to<BR>burn on a separate funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनिका
श्येनिका, f. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैत
श्यैत, आस्, m. pl., N. of a family; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैनम्पाता|श्यैनंपाता
श्यैनम्पाता, f. (fr. श्येन + पात), hawking,<BR>hunting, the chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यै
श्यै श्यै, cl. 1. A. श्यायते, शश्ये, श्यास्-<BR>यते, अश्यास्त, श्यातुम्, to go, move; to<BR>coagulate, be congealed, freeze; to dry up, wither:<BR>Pass. श्यायते: Caus. श्यापयति, -यितुम्: Desid.<BR>शिश्यासते: Intens. शाश्यायते, शाश्येति, शाश्याति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत|शीतं|शीतः
शीत, अस्, आ, अम्. See p. 1010, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीन|शीनं|शीनः
शीन, अस्, आ, अम्. See p. 1010, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यान|श्यानः
श्यान, अस्, आ, अम्, gone; coagulated, congealed;<BR>viscous, thick, sticky, adhesive (as clarified butter);<BR>shrunk up, shrunk; (अम्), n. smoke.<BR>—श्यान-<BR>पुलिन, अस्, आ, अम्, having shrunk or dry sand-<BR>banks (as a river in the hot season).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्योणाक|श्योणाकः
श्योणाक श्योणाक or श्योनाक, अस्, m. (said<BR>to be fr. rt. श्यै), the plant Bignonia or Calosanthes<BR>Indica, (see शोणक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रङ्क्|श्रंक्
श्रङ्क् श्रङ्क् (also written श्लङ्क्, स्रङ्क्),<BR>cl. 1. A. श्रङ्कते, शश्रङ्के, श्रङ्कि-<BR>तुम्, to go, move, creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रङ्ग्|श्रंग्
श्रङ्ग् श्रङ्ग् (also written श्लङ्ग्, श्वङ्ग्,<BR>स्वङ्ग्), cl. 1. P. श्रङ्गति, &c., to go,<BR>move; to shake (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रण्
श्रण् श्रण्, cl. 1. P. श्रणति, &c., cl. 10.<BR>P. (or Caus.) श्राणयति, श्रणयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अशिश्रणत् and अशश्राणत्, to give,<BR>grant, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रत्
श्रत् श्रत्, ind. (a kind of prefix combined<BR>or compounded with rt. 1. धा, and in the Veda<BR>with rt. 1. कृ, and generally implying) faith, trust,<BR>belief, (enumerated among the सत्य-नामानि in<BR>Naigh. III. 10; Sāy. श्रत् = सत्यानि, Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>75, 2; cf. Lat. cred in cred-o.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधत्
श्रद्-दधत्, अत्, अती, अत्, having faith; trusting,<BR>believing; respecting, venerating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधान|श्रद्दधानः
श्रद्-दधान, अस्, आ, अम्, having faith, &c. (=<BR>श्रद्-दधत्); a believer.<BR>—श्रद्दधान-ता, f.<BR>faith, (Manu VII. 86.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्ध
श्रद्-ध, अस्, आ, अम्, having faith, believing in,<BR>trusting; (आ), f. faith, belief, trust, confidence, (said<BR>to be also अम्, n.); belief in the Śāstras or divine<BR>revelation; calmness or composure of mind; inti-<BR>macy; respect, reverence; hope, wish, vehement<BR>desire, the longing of a pregnant woman; purity,<BR>(the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 151. is attributed to Śraddhā<BR>Kāmāyanī.)<BR>—श्रद्धा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done<BR>with faith.<BR>—श्रद्धा-जाड्य, अम्, n. blind or obsti-<BR>nate adherence to one's faith.<BR>—श्रद्धा-देव, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">Page1024-a+ 78</a>]<BR>m., Ved. epithet of Manu; [cf. श्राद्ध-देव.]<BR>—श्रद्धान्वित (˚धा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, endowed<BR>with faith, faithful, believing.<BR>—श्रद्धा-मनस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having a faithful mind, faithful-<BR>hearted.<BR>—श्रद्धा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, full of faith,<BR>believing.<BR>—श्रद्धा-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>faith, believing.<BR>—श्रद्धा-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>prived of faith, distrusting, disbelieving.<BR>—श्रद्धा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having faith, trusting, believing.<BR>—श्रद्धा-विरहित, अस्, आ, अम्, void of faith,<BR>destitute of belief.<BR>—श्रद्धा-समन्वित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, = श्रद्धान्वित above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धा
श्रद्-धा (cf. perhaps cred-o for cred-do), cl. 3.<BR>P. A. -दधाति, -धत्ते, -धातुम्, to place con-<BR>fidence in, have faith in, trust, believe, (श्रद्धातुम्<BR>अर्हः, worthy to be believed, trustworthy); to<BR>respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धातृ
श्रद्-धातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who believes, a<BR>believer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धालु|श्रद्धालुः
श्रद्धालु, उस्, उस्, उ, disposed to trust, faithful,<BR>believing; desirous, wishing; (उस्), f. a pregnant<BR>woman longing for anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धेय
श्रद्-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be trusted, reliable,<BR>worthy of confidence.<BR>—श्रद्धेय-ता, f. trust-<BR>worthiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथ्
श्रथ् श्रथ् or श्रन्थ् (connected with<BR>rt. श्लथ्, of which it appears to be an<BR>older form; cf. also rt. ग्रथ्), cl. 1. 9. 10. P. श्र-<BR>थति, श्रन्थति, श्रथ्नाति (Ved. also A. श्रथ्-<BR>नीते), श्राथयति, श्रन्थयति, शश्रन्थ (or श-<BR>श्राथ, 3rd pl. शश्रन्थुः or श्रेथुः, Pāṇ. I. 2, 6),<BR>श्रन्थिष्यति, अश्रन्थीत् (Ved. forms शिश्रथत्,<BR>शिश्रथस्, शिश्रथन्तु, श्रथ्नास्), श्रथितुम्,<BR>श्रन्थितुम्, श्राथयितुम्, to untie, loosen, let loose,<BR>discharge, liberate, set free, release, remove; to<BR>hurt, injure, destroy, kill, (usually cl. 9. or श्र-<BR>थति for श्नथति, cf. rt. श्नथ्); to bind, tie,<BR>connect, arrange [cf. rt. ग्रथ्]; to strive eagerly,<BR>endeavour, use exertion, (in this sense only cl.<BR>10); to delight repeatedly, amuse; cl. 1. 9. A.<BR>श्रन्थते, श्रथ्नीते (in neut. sense or Pass. refl.),<BR>to be loosened or dissolved or untied, to be loose;<BR>to be weak; to be shallow; cl. 10. P. A. श्रथ-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, to loosen, release (Ved.); to<BR>relax efforts; to be loose or relaxed, be weak<BR>or infirm: Caus. श्रन्थयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अशश्रन्थत्, -त, to cause to loosen, release, &c.;<BR>[cf. Gr. κλώθω, κάλαθος; Lat. crates, rete, res-tis<BR>(for ret-tis); Goth. af-hlathan; Old Germ. hla-<BR>dan, hlast; Angl. Sax. hladan, hlœst.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथन|श्रथनं
श्रथन, अम्, n. the act of untying, loosening;<BR>destroying, killing; tying, stringing, binding, con-<BR>necting; making effort, exertion; delighting repeat-<BR>edly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथित्वा
श्रथित्वा, ind. having loosened, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथ्नान
श्रथ्नान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. loosening, untying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ|श्रंथ|श्रंथः|श्रन्थः
श्रन्थ, अस्, m. loosening, liberating; looseness,<BR>flaccidity; tying, binding, stringing together; N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थन|श्रंथन|श्रंथनं|श्रन्थनं
श्रन्थन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of loosening,<BR>untying; tying, binding, stringing together (flowers<BR>&c.); killing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थित|श्रंथित|श्रन्थितः
श्रन्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, loosed, let loose; strung,<BR>connected, bound together; hurt, injured, killed;<BR>overcome, overpowered; delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थित्वा
श्रन्थित्वा, ind. having loosened, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्ध
श्रद्ध श्रद्-ध, श्रद्-धा, &c. See under<BR>श्रत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपण|श्रपणं|श्रपणः
श्रपण श्रपण, श्रपित, &c. See cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्
श्रम् श्रम्, cl. 4. P. श्राम्यति (sometimes<BR>also A. -ते), शश्राम, अश्रमत् or<BR>अश्रमीत्, श्रमितुम्, to make effort, exert one's<BR>self, take pains; to perform acts of penance or<BR>austerity, mortify the body; to be wearied or fatigued;<BR>to be distressed or pained: Pass. श्रम्यते, Aor.<BR>अश्रमि: Caus. श्रमयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशिश्र-<BR>मत्; [cf. perhaps Angl. Sax. hearm; Old Germ.<BR>ramen, ramjan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम|श्रमः
श्रम, अस्, m. exertion, labour, toil, taking pains;<BR>penance, austerity, mortification of the body; hard<BR>study, (श्रमं कृ, to make exertion, study);<BR>exercise, military exercise, drill; weariness, fatigue;<BR>distress, pain.<BR>—श्रम-कर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, worn<BR>out by toil; weighed down with fatigue.<BR>—श्रम-<BR>जल, अम्, n. ‘toil-water,’ perspiration.<BR>—श्रम-<BR>मोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, bewildered by exertion, para-<BR>lysed or stupefied by fatigue.<BR>—श्रम-साध्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, to be accomplished by labour.<BR>—श्रम-<BR>सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished by labour or exer-<BR>tion.<BR>—श्रम-स्थान, अम्, n. ‘labour-place,’ a place<BR>for work or exercise, workshop, drilling-place.<BR>—श्र-<BR>माम्बु (˚म-अम्˚), उ, n. ‘toil-water,’ perspiration;<BR>[cf. श्रम-जल.]<BR>—श्रमार्त (˚म-आर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, overcome with fatigue, wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमण|श्रमणः
श्रमण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, making effort or exertion,<BR>toiling, labouring; following a low or menial busi-<BR>ness; base, vile, bad; (अस्), m. one who performs<BR>acts of penance and austerity, an ascetic, devotee,<BR>one who restrains his passions and mortifies his body;<BR>a religious mendicant; a Buddhist ascetic; a beggar;<BR>(आ, ई), f. a woman of low caste or business; a female<BR>mendicant, (कुमार-श्रमणा, a female mendicant<BR>even in girlhood); a handsome woman; Bengal<BR>madder (= मञ्जिष्ठा); another plant (= मुण्-<BR>डीरी); Indian spikenard (= जटा-मांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणाय
श्रमणाय, Nom. A. श्रमणायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>become a Śramaṇa, become a beggar, be reduced to<BR>beggary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमयु
श्रमयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. weary, overcome with<BR>fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमिन्
श्रमिन्, ई, इणी, इ, making great efforts, laborious,<BR>diligent; undergoing fatigue or weariness; wearying,<BR>tiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्त|श्रांत|श्रान्तः
श्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, wearied, fatigued, tired, ex-<BR>hausted, distressed; calmed, tranquil; (अस्), m. one<BR>whose passions are subdued, an ascetic.<BR>—श्रान्त-<BR>संवाहन, अस्, आ, अम्, soothing a weary person<BR>(by rubbing or shampooing his limbs); relieving<BR>or tending the wearied (by offering a seat &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्ति|श्रांति|श्रांतिः|श्रान्तिः
श्रान्ति, इस्, f. fatigue, weariness, exhaustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम|श्रामः
श्राम, अस्, m. a temporary shed (= मण्डप);<BR>a month; time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्भ्|श्रंभ्
श्रम्भ् श्रम्भ् (also written स्रम्भ्; ge-<BR>nerally found with the prefix वि, see वि-<BR>श्रम्भ्, p. 943), cl. 1. A. श्रम्भते, शश्रम्भे,<BR>श्रम्भिष्यते, श्रम्भितुम्, to be careless or inat-<BR>tentive, be negligent, neglect; to err, do wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रय|श्रयः
श्रय श्रय, श्रयण, &c. See p. 1025, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रव|श्रवः
श्रव श्रव, श्रवक, श्रवण, &c. See<BR>p. 1027, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रा
श्रा श्रा or श्रै (also written स्रै, cf. शै;<BR>connected with rt. 2. श्री), cl. 2. 4. P. श्राति,<BR>श्रायति (or cl. 1. if fr. the form श्रै), शश्रौ,<BR>श्रास्यति, अश्रासीत्, श्रातुम्, to boil, seethe, cook,<BR>dress, mature, ripen; to sweat: Pass. श्रायते, Aor.<BR>अश्रायि: Caus. श्रपयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अशि-<BR>श्रपत्, to cause to boil or cook, to boil; to render<BR>mature or ripe; श्रापयति, -यितुम्, to make hot,<BR>heat; to cause to sweat, (according to Vopa-deva<BR>XXI. 16. श्रापयति = प्रशस्यम् आचष्टे): Pass.<BR>of Caus. श्रप्यते or श्राप्यते, Aor. अश्रापि or<BR>अश्रपि: Desid. शिश्रासति: Intens. शाश्रायते, शा-<BR>श्राति, शाश्रेति; [cf. Gr. κρίβανος, κρίβανον,<BR>κλίβανος, κριβάνη, κράμβος, καρπός, κάρψω,<BR>κάρδοπος , (probably) κραῦρος, (perhaps also) κέραμος,<BR>κέρνον, (according to some also perhaps) ἄρτος for<BR>κάρτος or κράτος, κάγχρυς for κάρχρυς; περκάζω:<BR>Lat. cremare, carbo, (probably) calere, cinis; cu-<BR>līna: Goth. hauri, hlaif-s: Old Germ. rifi (=<BR>Mod. Germ. reif), herpist: Angl. Sax. heordh,<BR>hlaf, hœrefœst, hœrfest, ripe: Lith. is-sirpstu:<BR>Hib. cramhaim, ‘I concoct, digest.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृत|शृतं
शृत, अस्, आ, अम्, boiled, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपण|श्रपणं|श्रपणः
श्रपण, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of causing to boil<BR>or boiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपणीय
श्रपणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपयत्
श्रपयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to boil, boiling,<BR>cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपयितव्य
श्रपयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपयित्वा
श्रपयित्वा, ind. having caused to be boiled or<BR>dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपित|श्रपितं
श्रपित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be boiled; boiled<BR>(said to be applied to anything except water, milk,<BR>or ghee, cf. शृत); seethed, sodden; (आ), f. rice-<BR>gruel; (अम्), n. boiled meat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राण|श्राणं
श्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, boiled (said to be applied to<BR>anything except water, milk, or ghee), stewed, cooked,<BR>prepared, dressed [cf. शृत, 2. श्रित]; moist, wet;<BR>(आ), f. rice-gruel; (अम्), n. boiled meat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रात
श्रात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = श्राण above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्ध|श्राद्धं
श्राद्ध श्राद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. श्रद्-धा,<BR>see श्रद्-ध), faithful, believing; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a kind of funeral rite or ceremony in honour of<BR>the departed spirits of dead relatives observed with<BR>great, strictness at various fixed periods and on oc-<BR>casions of rejoicing as well as mourning, (these cere-<BR>monies are of three principal kinds, 1. Nitya, i. e.<BR>general and constant, in honour of the Pitṛs or<BR>deceased ancestors and progenitors collectively [also<BR>called पार्वण, अष्टक, q. q. v. v.], when three<BR>Piṇḍas or balls of meal [see पिण्ड] and water are<BR>offered to three paternal ancestors and three maternal<BR>forefathers [see पितृ]: 2. Naimittika, i. e. occasional<BR>and special, as, for instance, in behalf of a parent or<BR>some one relative recently deceased [called also<BR>एकोद्दिष्ट, q. v.]; the object being twofold, viz.<BR>first, the re-embodying of his soul in some kind of<BR>form after burning his corpse; secondly, the raising<BR>him from the regions of the atmosphere, where he<BR>would otherwise roam among demons and evil<BR>spirits, to a particular heaven above, where he is, as<BR>it were, deified among the shades of departed kins-<BR>men; the offering of the funeral Piṇḍa or ball of<BR>meal is in this case the office of the nearest male<BR>kinsman, and confers the title to any property that<BR>may be inherited: 3. Kāmya, i. e. voluntary and<BR>performed apparently by way of supererogation for<BR>the greater benefit of deceased ancestors or for ob-<BR>taining increase of religious merit, &c.: other Śrād-<BR>dha ceremonies and oblations appear to have more<BR>reference to the living than the dead, and to be<BR>performed either for the sake of पुष्टि and वृद्धि,<BR>‘increase of prosperity,’ &c., or as thank-offerings on<BR>various joyful occasions, such as the birth of a son,<BR>when gifts and food are offered to the living relations<BR>and assisting Brāhmans present: there is also an<BR>important Śrāddha, called Daiva, in honour of the<BR>Viśva-devas or Viśve Devāḥ, ‘deities collectively’<BR>[see विश्व]: the Śrāddha to a recently deceased<BR>relative should be offered on the day after mourning<BR>expires, and at intervals during twelve successive<BR>months, and afterwards on all anniversaries of his<BR>death; that to the Pitṛs collectively should take<BR>place on the dark fortnight of a lunation as well as<BR>at various other seasons, different names being given<BR>to the various Śrāddhas according to the times and<BR>objects of their performance, see अष्टक, एकादशी,<BR>मासिक, अन्व्-आहार्य, दश-पिण्ड-श्राद्ध, प्रेत-<BR>श्राद्ध, सपिण्डन, महालय, वृद्धि-श्राद्-<BR>ध, शुद्धि, नान्दी-मुख); gifts or offerings at<BR>a Śrāddha.<BR>—श्राद्ध-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, or श्राद्-<BR>ध-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who performs a Śrād-<BR>dha, the offerer of an obsequial oblation.<BR>—श्राद्ध-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. a Śrāddha rite, a funeral ceremony.<BR>—श्राद्ध-कल्प, अस्, m., N. of a Pariśiṣṭa of the<BR>Yajur-veda (ascribed to Kātyāyana).<BR>—श्राद्ध-<BR>कल्प-भाष्य, अम्, n. a commentary on the<BR>Śrāddha-kalpa (ascribed to Gobhila).<BR>—श्राद्ध-<BR>कल्प-लता, f., N. of a work by Nanda-paṇḍita.<BR>—श्राद्ध-कृत्, त्, m. the performer of a funeral<BR>rite.<BR>—श्राद्ध-क्रिया, f. a Śrāddha ceremony,<BR>funeral rite.<BR>—श्राद्ध-चन्द्रिका, f. ‘Śrāddha-<BR>elucidation,’ N. of a work.<BR>—श्राद्ध-चिन्तामणि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘Śrāddha-gem,’ N. of a work by Śiva-rāma on<BR>funeral rites.<BR>—श्राद्ध-तत्त्व, अम्, n. ‘Śrāddha-<BR>truth,’ N. of two portions of Raghu-nandana's Smṛti-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">Page1025-a+ 75</a>]<BR>tattva (called respectively the Chandoga-śrāddha-<BR>tattva and the Yajurvedi-śrāddha-tattva).<BR>—श्राद्ध-<BR>तत्त्व-टीका, f., N. of a commentary by Kāśi-rāma<BR>on the Chandoga-śrāddha-tattva.<BR>—श्राद्ध-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. faithfulness; the being a Śrāddha.<BR>—श्राद्-<BR>ध-द, अस्, m. the offerer of a Śrāddha.<BR>—श्राद्-<BR>ध-दिन, अस्, अम्, m. n. the day of a Śrāddha, the<BR>anniversary of the death of a near relative.<BR>—श्राद्-<BR>ध-दीप-कलिका, f., N. of a work.<BR>—श्राद्ध-<BR>दीपिका, f. ‘Śrāddha-elucidation,’ N. of a work.<BR>—श्राद्ध-देव, अस्, m. any god presiding over<BR>funeral rites; a Viśva-deva; Yama (lord of the<BR>dead); Manu Vaivasvata (brother of Yama; in a<BR>former mundane age he was Manu Satya-vrata).<BR>—श्राद्ध-देवता, f. any deity presiding over<BR>obsequial rites; a Viśva-deva; a Pitṛ or progenitor;<BR>Yama.<BR>—श्राद्ध-पङ्क्ति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—श्राद्ध-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work by Nīla-<BR>kaṇṭha.<BR>—श्राद्ध-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—श्राद्ध-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, or श्राद्ध-भोक्तृ, ता,<BR>त्री, तृ, eating food prepared at a Śrāddha, a de-<BR>ceased ancestor.<BR>—श्राद्ध-मयूख, अस्, m.<BR>‘Śrāddha-light,’ N. of a part of Nīla-kaṇṭha's Bha-<BR>gavad-bhāskara.<BR>—श्राद्ध-विवेक, अस्, m. ‘Śrād-<BR>dha-investigation,’ N. of a work.<BR>—श्राद्ध-शाक,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of pot-herb (= काल-शाक).<BR>—श्राद्-<BR>ध-शिष्ट, अम्, n. what remains at a Śrāddha, food<BR>that has been presented to the Pitṛs.<BR>—श्राद्ध-<BR>सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘Śrāddha-compilation,’ N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—श्राद्ध-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of certain<BR>aphorisms by Kātyāyana on the rites to be per-<BR>formed at anniversaries of the death of near relatives.<BR>—श्राद्ध-स्तवक, अस्, m. a chapter on Śrāddhas.<BR>—श्राद्धोपयोगिन् (˚ध-उप्˚), ई, इनी, इ, service-<BR>able or appropriate for Śrāddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिक|श्राद्धिकः
श्राद्धिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a Śrāddha or<BR>obsequial rite; the recipient of an obsequial obla-<BR>tion; (अम्), n. a present given at a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिन्
श्राद्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a Śrāddha, any object<BR>or receiver of a funeral oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धीय
श्राद्धीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>funeral ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्त|श्रांत|श्रान्तः
श्रान्त श्रान्त, श्राम, &c. See under rt.<BR>श्रम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम्
श्राम् श्राम् (also written ग्राम्, see ग्रा-<BR>मय; perhaps rather a Nom.), cl. 10. P.<BR>श्रामयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशश्रामत्, to call, sum-<BR>mon, invite; to counsel, consult in private, advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रामणेर|श्रामणेरः
श्रामणेर श्रामणेर, अस्, m. (fr. श्रमण),<BR>a follower or disciple of a Jaina or Buddhist mendi-<BR>cant, a novice, lay-brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राय|श्रायः
श्राय श्राय, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रायस|श्रायसः
श्रायस श्रायस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. श्रेयस्), pro-<BR>duced in or on the best, &c.; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव|श्रावः
श्राव श्राव, श्रावक, श्रावण, &c. See<BR>p. 1027, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावन्ती
श्रावन्ती श्रावन्ती. See श्रावस्ती below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावस्त
श्रावस्त श्रावस्त, अस्, m. (fr. श्रवस्), N. of<BR>a king, (also written श्रावस्तक and शावस्त); (ई),<BR>f., N. of a city situated north of the Ganges and<BR>founded by king Śrāvasta, (it was the capital of<BR>Kośala, and said to have been the place where the<BR>merchant Anātha-piṇḍāda gave Buddha a building<BR>for his residence and the delivery of his lectures; it<BR>is less correctly written श्रावन्ती, and is identified<BR>with Dharma-pattana, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रि
श्रि श्रि (some of the forms of this rt.,<BR>such as the Perf., Caus., &c., are identical with<BR>those of rt. 1. श्री), cl. 1. P. A. श्रयति, -ते, शिश्राय<BR>(3rd du. शिश्रियतुस्, 3rd pl. शिश्रियुस्), शिश्रिये (3rd<BR>du. शिश्रियाते), श्रयिष्यति, -ते, अशिश्रियत्, -त<BR>(Ved. forms अश्रेत्, अशिश्रेत्), श्रयितुम् (Ved. Inf.<BR>श्रियसे), to go to, approach, go near to, resort or<BR>have recourse to, fly to (for refuge), approach for<BR>protection, seek; to go into, enter; to cling to, lean<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">Page1025-b+ 76</a>]<BR>on, depend on, rest on; to honour, serve, worship,<BR>devote or addict one's self to, be devoted; to serve,<BR>help, assist; to use, employ, make use of; to obtain,<BR>possess, receive, (Sāy. श्रीणीषे = श्रयसि or पचसि,<BR>Ṛg-veda V. 6, 9; cf. rt. श्री); to undergo; to<BR>abide or dwell in (with loc.): Pass. श्रीयते, Aor.<BR>अश्रायि: Caus. श्राययति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशिश्रयत्:<BR>Desid. शिश्रयिषति, -ते, and शिश्रीषति, -ते: Intens.<BR>शेश्रीयते, शेश्रयीति, शेश्रेति; [cf. Gr. κλίνω, κλιτύς,<BR>κλισία: Lat. clî-no, in-clino, clīvus, (perhaps)<BR>clemens: Old Germ. hlei-tara, ‘a ladder;’ hlinian,<BR>hlinôn, hlinen, ‘to lean upon;’ obahlinên, ‘to<BR>excel;’ fora-hlinên; hlîta, ‘a declivity;’ scrîtan,<BR>‘to step;’ ga-scrîtan, scrit: Angl. Sax. hlynian,<BR>hlidh, hlœ-dre, hlœ-der, hold, hal: Goth. hlains,<BR>hlei-thra, hlija, hulth, (perhaps) hail: Lith. kle†-<BR>tis, a room in the uppermost part of a house; kle-<BR>joyu, ‘to roam through;’ klystu fr. klydtu, kly-<BR>deju: Slav. klje-tj: Old Island. scrid, ‘a step.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्रिवस्
शिश्रिवस्, वान्, युषी, वत्, one who has gone to<BR>or approached, &c., (Pāṇ. VII. 2, 67.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रय|श्रयः
श्रय, अस्, m. approaching for protection, asylum,<BR>refuge, protection; [cf. उच्-छ्रय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयण|श्रयणं
श्रयण, अम्, n. the act of going to or approach-<BR>ing (especially for protection), asylum, refuge, pro-<BR>tection, shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयणीय
श्रयणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be had recourse to, to<BR>be depended on; to be sheltered or protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयमाण
श्रयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, going to, entering;<BR>having recourse to, &c.; being near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयितव्य
श्रयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = श्रयणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयित्वा
श्रयित्वा, ind. having gone to or approached (for<BR>refuge &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयिन्
श्रयिन् in सं-श्रयिन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राय|श्रायः
श्राय, अस्, m. taking refuge, refuge, reliance,<BR>shelter, protection; [cf. उच्-छ्राय]; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>sacred or belonging to the goddess Śrī, (in this sense<BR>fr. 2. श्री.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रायत्
श्रायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, having recourse, taking<BR>refuge, &c., (श्रायन्तः = सम्-आश्रिताः, Nirukta<BR>VI. 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित्
श्रित्, त्, त्, त् (at the end of comps.), going to, ap-<BR>proaching (especially for protection), having recourse<BR>to, clinging to; reaching to, rising to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित|श्रितः
1. श्रित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see col. 3), gone to, ap-<BR>proached, had recourse to, fled for refuge, approached<BR>for protection, entered, clung to, rested on, founded<BR>on, placed on; resting or sitting on, attached or con-<BR>tiguous to, connected with, joined with; subservient,<BR>subordinate, auxiliary; protected; served, honoured,<BR>cherished, worshipped, sustained, covered with, over-<BR>spread; contained; obtained, having, possessing, as-<BR>sembled, collected.<BR>—श्रित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one<BR>who has had recourse to or taken refuge with; one<BR>who has served, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिति|श्रितिः
श्रिति, इस्, f. going to, approach, recourse, enter-<BR>ing; [cf. उच्-छ्रिति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीयमाण
श्रीयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being resorted to, being<BR>approached for protection, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियपुत्र
श्रियपुत्र श्रिय-पुत्र, अस्, m. a kind of bird,<BR>(incorrect for प्रिय-पुत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियस्
श्रियस् श्रियस्, श्रिया. See p. 1026, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिष्
श्रिष् 1. श्रिष् (= rt. 1. श्लिष्), cl. 1. P. श्रे-<BR>षति, शिश्रेष, श्रेषितुम्, to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिष्
श्रिष् 2. श्रिष् (probably an older form<BR>of rt. 2. श्लिष्), cl. 1. P. श्रेषति, &c.,<BR>to join, fix, infix, impress, (Sāy. श्रेषाम = श्लेष-<BR>येम or श्राययेम, ‘may we infix,’ Ṛg-veda IV.<BR>43, 1; मा श्रेषत् = आश्लिष्टम् मा भूत्, ‘let it<BR>not be left on the ground,’ I. 162, 11.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री 1. श्री (connected with rt. श्रा), cl. 9.<BR>P. A. श्रीणाति, श्रीणीते, शिश्राय, शिश्रिये,<BR>श्रेष्यति, -ते, अश्रैषीत्, अश्रेष्ट, श्रेतुम्, to cook,<BR>dress, mature, prepare, (Sāy. श्रीणीषे = श्रयसि or प-<BR>चसि, Ṛg-veda V. 6, 9; cf. rt. श्रि); to mix, mingle:<BR>Caus. श्राययति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशिश्रयत्: Desid. शि-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-c" target="_blank">Page1025-c+ 80</a>]<BR>श्रीषति, -ते: Intens. शेश्रीयते, शेश्रयीति, शेश्रेति;<BR>[cf. probably Gr. κίρνημι, κεράω, κεράννυμι, κικράω;<BR>Lat. pin-cerna.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित|श्रितः
2. श्रित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see col. 2), Ved. = श्रीत<BR>below or श्राण under rt. श्रा; [cf. शृत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीणत्
श्रीणत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. mixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीणा
श्रीणा, f., Ved. night, (a various reading for शिरिणा<BR>in Naigh. I. 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीत
श्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, cooked; dressed, prepared,<BR>mixed (said of the Soma juice, Sāy. = पय-आदिभिः<BR>श्रयण-द्रव्यैर् मिश्रितः or संस्कृतः, Ṛg-<BR>veda VIII. 2, 28).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री 2. श्री, ईस्, f. (thought to be either fr.<BR>rt. श्रि or to be connected with rts. 1. श्री, श्रै, श्रा,<BR>‘to mature,’ cf. Lat. Ceres), prosperity, well-being,<BR>wealth, happiness, good fortune, success, thriving or<BR>flourishing condition, riches, plenty; high rank,<BR>dignity, elevation, sacredness, majesty, royalty, glory,<BR>fame, renown; state, the insignia of royalty; beauty,<BR>grace, loveliness, splendor, light, lustre; the twelfth<BR>digit of the moon; Prosperity or Fortune or Beauty<BR>personified; N. of Lakṣmī as goddess of prosperity<BR>or beauty (wife of Viṣṇu, see लक्ष्मी); N. of<BR>Sarasvatī, goddess of speech and learning (wife of<BR>Brahmā, cf. श्री-पञ्चमी); any virtue or excel-<BR>lence; decoration, ornament, dress; intellect, under-<BR>standing; superhuman power; the three objects of<BR>life collectively, (viz. virtue, pleasure, and wealth, cf.<BR>त्रि-वर्ग); N. of the mother of the Arhat Kunthu<BR>(according to the Jainas); the Sarala tree, Pinus<BR>Longifolia; the Vilva tree; a lotus; cloves, = ल-<BR>वङ्ग; a kind of drug, = वृद्धि; (ईस्), m., N. of<BR>one of the six Rāgas or musical modes (according<BR>to some the fifth, according to others the third or<BR>first in order). The word Śrī is frequently used as<BR>an honorific prefix to the names of deities [e. g.<BR>Śrī-Durgā, Śrī-Rāma], and may be repeated twice,<BR>thrice, or even four and five times to express excessive<BR>veneration [e. g. Śrī-śrī-śrī-Durgā]; it is also used<BR>as a respectful prefix to the names of eminent persons<BR>[e. g. Śrī-Jayadeva] as well as of celebrated works<BR>[e. g. Śrī-Bhāgavata] and sacred objects, and is often<BR>placed at the beginning or back of letters, manu-<BR>scripts, important documents, &c.<BR>—श्रियम्-मन्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fancying one's self Śrī; confiding in one's<BR>beauty or wealth; arrogant, conceited, proud, (also<BR>written श्रि-मन्य according to some.)<BR>—श्रिया-<BR>दित्य, अस्, m. (श्रिया for श्री + आद्˚), a proper N.<BR>—श्रियानकुल, N. of a place.<BR>—श्रिया-वासिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘dwelling with Śrī,’ epithet of Śiva, (according<BR>to the commentator श्रिया सह वसतीति.)<BR>—श्रि-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, m. ‘holy or eloquent throat,’ epithet<BR>of Śiva; of Bhava-bhūti (the author of the Mālatī-<BR>Mādhava, &c.); N. of a medical author; of an arid<BR>district north-west of Dehli; (ई), f., N. of a treatise<BR>on the Śaiva doctrines (also called Śrī-kaṇṭhīya-saṃ-<BR>hitā).<BR>—श्रीकण्ठ-दीक्षित, अस्, m., N. of a com-<BR>mentator.<BR>—श्रीकण्ठ-पद-लाञ्छन, अस्, m.<BR>‘marked by the name Śrī-kaṇṭha,’ epithet of the<BR>poet Bhava-bhūti.<BR>—श्रीकण्ठ-शिव, अस्, m. epithet<BR>of Śambhū-nātha.<BR>—श्रीकण्ठ-सख, अस्, m.<BR>‘friend of Śiva,’ epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—श्रीकण्ठ-<BR>स्तव, अस्, m. ‘praise of the district of Śrī-kaṇṭha,’<BR>N. of a poem.<BR>—श्री-कन्दा, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>बन्ध्या-कर्कोटकी).<BR>—श्री-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>causing prosperity, giving good fortune; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; of the author of a law-book; of<BR>another person; (अम्), n. the red lotus.<BR>—श्री-क-<BR>रण, अस्, m. ‘making the word Śrī,’ a pen.<BR>—श्री-<BR>कराचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a philosophical<BR>writer.<BR>—श्री-कान्त, अस्, m. ‘beloved by Śrī,’ epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu; N. of the preceptor of Hari-nātha.<BR>—श्री-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring prosperity or<BR>happiness.<BR>—श्री-कार, अस्, m. the word Śrī written<BR>at the top of a book or letter, &c.<BR>—श्री-कारिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘causing increase,’ a kind of antelope (= कुरङ्ग;<BR>the flesh of this animal is considered highly nutritious;<BR>some make the word श्री-कारी, f.).<BR>—श्री-कुल, N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—श्री-क्रम, N. of a work.<BR>—श्री-खण्ड,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. sandal-wood.<BR>—श्री-गणेश, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-a" target="_blank">Page1026-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the divine Gaṇeśa.<BR>—श्री-गदित, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>Upa-rūpaka or minor drama (described as a compo-<BR>sition in one act, dedicated chiefly to the goddess<BR>Śrī).<BR>—श्री-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘Fortune-womb,’ epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu; a sword.<BR>—श्री-ग्रह, अस्, m. a trough<BR>or place for watering birds (= शकुनी-प्रपा).<BR>—श्री-ग्राम, अस्, m. ‘village of Fortune,’ N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—श्री-ग्रामर, अस्, m. epithet of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—श्री-घन, अम्, n. coagulated milk, sour curds;<BR>(अस्), m. a Buddha, Bauddha saint.<BR>—श्री-चक्र,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of magical circle used in the worship<BR>of Tripura-sundarī (= त्रिपुर-सुन्दर्याः पूजा-<BR>यन्त्र-विशेषः); an astrological division of the<BR>body (said to represent the uterine or pubic<BR>region); a wheel of Indra's car; the circle of the<BR>earth, globe.<BR>—श्री-ज, अस्, m. ‘born from Śrī,’<BR>epithet of Kāma (god of love).<BR>—श्री-ताल, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of palm tree (= लक्ष्मी-ताल, = मृदु-<BR>च्छद).<BR>—श्री-द, अस्, आ, अम्, bestowing wealth or<BR>prosperity, &c.; (अस्), m. epithet of Kuvera (god of<BR>riches).<BR>—श्री-दत्त, अस्, m. ‘Fortune-given,’ N. of<BR>the author of the Ācārādarśa and the Samaya-pra-<BR>dīpa.<BR>—श्री-दयित, अस्, m. ‘husband of Śrī,’ epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—श्री-धर, अस्, m. a kind of Śāla-<BR>grāma, q. v.; epithet of Viṣṇu; of an Arhat of<BR>the past Utsarpiṇī (according to the Jainas); N. of<BR>a commentator on the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa [cf. श्री-<BR>धर-स्वामिन्]; of an astronomer; of a poet.<BR>—श्रीधर-मालव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—श्री-<BR>धर-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Smṛty-artha-sāra and the following commentaries,<BR>the Ātma-prakāśa, the Bhāgavata-bhāvārtha-dīpikā,<BR>and the Subodhinī.<BR>—श्रीधराचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—श्री-धरोल, N. of a town.<BR>—श्री-<BR>नगर, अम्, n. ‘city of Fortune,’ N. of two towns<BR>(one situated in the district of Caunpore, the other<BR>in Bundelcund).<BR>—श्री-नन्दन, अस्, m. ‘son of<BR>Śrī,’ epithet of Kāma-deva (god of love).<BR>—श्री-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—श्रीनाथ-शर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of the author of the Ācāra-candrikā, a com-<BR>mentary on the Tithi-dvaidha-prakaraṇa, and the<BR>Sāra-mañjarī commentary.<BR>—श्री-निकेतन, अस्, m.<BR>‘dwelling with Śrī,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—श्री-निवास,<BR>अस्, m. ‘dwelling with Śrī,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; N.<BR>of the author of the Śuddhi-dīpikā.<BR>—श्री-पञ्-<BR>चमी, f. the fifth of the light half of Māgha, (a<BR>festival in honour of Sarasvatī, goddess of learning,<BR>when books and implements of writing are wor-<BR>shipped.)<BR>—श्रीपञ्चमी-व्रत, अम्, n. the above<BR>religious observance.<BR>—श्री-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>fortune,’ a king, prince; epithet of Viṣṇu (as<BR>husband of Śrī); N. of the author of the Jyotiṣa-<BR>ratna-mālā and of the Vyavahāra-nirṇaya.<BR>—श्रीपति-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Kā-tantra-<BR>pariśiṣṭa.<BR>—श्रीपति-समुच्चय, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—श्री-पत्तन, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—श्री-<BR>पथ, अस्, m. a royal road, highway.<BR>—श्री-पर्ण,<BR>अम्, n. a lotus; the tree Premna Spinosa (the wood<BR>of which produces fire by attrition); (ई), f. the Premna<BR>Spinosa; the shrub Gmelina Arborea; the medicinal<BR>plant Kaṭphala; the silk-cotton tree; the aquatic<BR>plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—श्री-पर्णिका, f. a kind of<BR>medicinal shrub (= कट्-फल, commonly called<BR>Kāyaphal).<BR>—श्री-पर्वत, अस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain or range of mountains; of a Liṅga.<BR>—श्री-पा,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, preserving fortune.<BR>—श्री-पिष्ट, अस्,<BR>m. the resin of the pine tree, turpentine (prepared<BR>by pounding the wood of the Śrī or Sarala tree),<BR>—श्री-पुट, अस्, m. a kind of metre.<BR>—श्री-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. ‘son of Śrī,’ epithet of Kāma (god of love);<BR>a horse; [cf. श्री-भ्रातृ.]<BR>—श्री-पुर, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a town.<BR>—श्री-पुष्प, अम्, n. cloves; a parti-<BR>cular fragrant wood (= पद्म-काष्ठ).<BR>—श्री-<BR>फल, अम्, n. the Vilva tree or fruit; another tree<BR>(= राजादनी); (आ), f. the indigo plant; (another<BR>plant (= क्षुद्र-कारवेल्ली); (ई), f. the indigo<BR>plant, Emblic Myrobalan.<BR>—श्री-फलिका, f. a kind<BR>of plant (= क्षुद्र-कारवेल्ली); another plant (=<BR>महा-नीली).<BR>—श्री-बलि, N. of a village.<BR>—श्री-भ-<BR>ड, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—श्री-भद्र, अस्, m. the<BR>fragrant grass Cyperus Rotundus.<BR>—श्री-भागवत,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-b" target="_blank">Page1026-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, n. ‘the sacred Bhāgavata,’ epithet of the cele-<BR>brated Bhāgavata-Puraṇa (said to contain 18,000<BR>verses, see भागवत).<BR>—श्री-भाष्य, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a commentary by Rāmānuja on the Brahma-sūtra.<BR>—श्री-भ्रातृ, ता, m. ‘brother of Lakṣmī,’ the<BR>moon; a horse, (the moon and the horse Uccaiḥ-<BR>śravas, q. v., being recovered with Lakṣmī at the<BR>churning of the ocean.)<BR>—श्री-मङ्गल, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR>—श्री-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of<BR>fortune, fortunate, prosperous, thriving; wealthy,<BR>opulent; beautiful, pleasing; famous, illustrious;<BR>(आन्), m. epithet of Viṣṇu (as husband of Śrī); of<BR>Kuvera (the god of wealth); of Śiva; a title applied<BR>to any exalted or venerable person; a kind of tree<BR>(commonly called Tila or Tilaka); the Aśvattha<BR>fig-tree; (अती), f. a title applied to women; N. of<BR>the mother of Mādhavācārya.<BR>—श्री-मति, इस्, f., N.<BR>of Rādhā.<BR>—श्रीमत्-ता, f. prosperity, thriving con-<BR>dition, beauty.<BR>—श्री-मद, अस्, m. the intoxication<BR>produced by prosperity.<BR>—श्रीमद्-दत्तोपनिषद्<BR>(˚त-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad; [cf. दत्तोप-<BR>निषद्.]<BR>—श्री-मलापहा (˚ल-अप्˚), f. a kind of<BR>shrub (= धूम्र-पत्त्रा).<BR>—श्री-मस्तक, अस्, m.<BR>Lakṣmī's head; garlic.<BR>—श्री-माल, N. of a dis-<BR>trict; of a town (said to have been built by Viśva-<BR>karman).<BR>—श्रीमाल-खण्ड, N. of a book of<BR>the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—श्रीमाल-माहात्म्य^1, अम्, n.<BR>‘greatness of Śrī-māla,’ N. of a part of the Skanda-<BR>Purāṇa (containing fifty-four chapters descriptive of<BR>the origin, sanctity, and Tīrthas of Śrī-māla).<BR>—श्री-<BR>मुख, अम्, n. a beautiful face; (अस्), m. epithet<BR>of the seventh (or forty-first) year of Jupiter's cycle<BR>of sixty years; the word Śrī written on the back of<BR>a letter.<BR>—श्री-मुद्रा, f. a particular mark made<BR>on the forehead &c. by the worshippers of Viṣṇu.<BR>—श्री-मुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, stealing beauty.<BR>—श्री-मूर्ति,<BR>इस्, f. ‘sacred or divine image,’ an image of Viṣṇu;<BR>any idol.<BR>—श्री-युक्त or श्री-युत, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘en-<BR>dowed with Śrī,’ happy, fortunate; wealthy, opulent;<BR>famous, illustrious, (prefixed as an honorific title to<BR>the names of men, and in the common language<BR>written श्री-युत्.)<BR>—श्री-रङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘holy Raṅga,’<BR>N. of Viṣṇu; (according to some) of Śiva; (ac-<BR>cording to others) of an ancient king who founded<BR>the city of Seringapatam.<BR>—श्रीरङ्ग-पत्तन, अम्,<BR>n. ‘Viṣṇu's city,’ the city of Seringapatam (situated<BR>in Mysore on an island in the channel of the Kā-<BR>verī, said to have been founded by an ancient king<BR>who called it after himself or by a devotee who<BR>dedicated it to Viṣṇu).<BR>—श्री-रस, अस्, m. ‘juice<BR>of the Śarala tree,’ turpentine; resin.<BR>—श्री-राग,<BR>अस्, m. the fifth (or according to some, third or first)<BR>of the Rāgas or personified musical modes, (see श्री.)<BR>—श्री-राम, अस्, m. the divine Rāma, i. e. Rāma-<BR>candra (whose name in this form is used as a saluta-<BR>tion by those who worship Viṣṇu in this Avatāra).<BR>—श्रीराम-नवमी, f. the ninth of the light<BR>half of the month Caitra, observed as a festival in<BR>honour of the birthday of Rāma-candra (when cere-<BR>monies are said to be performed with the Śāla-grāma<BR>and Tulasī leaves).<BR>—श्रीराम-पद्धति, इस्, f., N.<BR>of a work on the proper mode of worshipping Rāma<BR>(attributed to Rāmānuja).<BR>—श्री-लक्ष्मण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, characterized by Śrī.<BR>—श्री-लता, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= महा-ज्योतिष्मती).<BR>—श्री-वत्स, अस्, m.<BR>‘the favourite of the goddess of fortune,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; a particular mark or curl of hair on the<BR>breast of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (said to be white and<BR>represented in pictures by a symbol resembling a<BR>cruciform flower); the emblem of the tenth Jina<BR>(or Viṣṇu's mark so used); a hole made through<BR>a wall by a housebreaker; epithet of the eighth<BR>astronomical Yoga.<BR>—श्रीवत्सकिन्, ई, m. a horse<BR>having a curl of hair on his breast (resembling that<BR>of Viṣṇu).<BR>—श्रीवत्स-धारिन्, ई, m. or श्रीवत्स-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. ‘wearing the Śrī-vatsa mark,’ epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—श्रीवत्स-लक्ष्मन्, आ, or श्रीवत्स-<BR>लाञ्छन or श्रीवत्साङ्क (˚स-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>the Śrī-vatsa mark,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—श्री-वर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the Jaina-taraṅgiṇī<BR>(which is said to be a continuation of the Rāja-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">Page1026-c+ 79</a>]<BR>taraṅgiṇī up to the year A. D. 1477).<BR>—श्री-वराह,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the divine boar,’ epithet of Viṣṇu (in his<BR>boar-incarnation).<BR>—श्री-वर्धन, अस्, m. epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—श्री-वल्लभ, अस्, m. a favourite of for-<BR>tune.<BR>—श्री-वल्ली, f. a kind of plant (= कण्ट-वल्ली).<BR>—श्री-वाटी, f. a kind of plant (= नाग-वल्ली).<BR>—श्री-वारक, अस्, m. a kind of pot-herb (= सिता-<BR>वर).<BR>—श्री-वास, अस्, m. ‘dwelling with Śrī,’<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; a lotus; turpentine.<BR>—श्री-वासस्, आस्, m. = श्री-वास, turpentine.<BR>—श्री-<BR>विजय-प्रशस्ति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—श्री-विद्या,<BR>f. exalted science; a form of Durgā (= महा-वि-<BR>द्या-विशेषः or त्रिपुर-सुन्दरी).<BR>—श्री-विशाल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in good fortune.<BR>—श्री-वृक्-<BR>ष, अस्, m. the sacred fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa; the<BR>Vilva tree; a ring or curl of hair on the chest and<BR>forehead of a horse; [cf. श्रीवत्सकिन्.]<BR>—श्री-वृक्-<BR>षक, अस्, m. a curl or lock of hair on the chest of<BR>a horse, (perhaps for श्री-वत्सक.)<BR>—श्रीवृक्ष-<BR>नवमी-व्रत, अम्, n. epithet of a particular re-<BR>ligious observance.<BR>—श्री-वेष्ट, अस्, m. ‘Śarala-<BR>exudation,’ turpentine; resin.<BR>—श्री-वैष्णव, अस्,<BR>m. a member of the Vaiṣṇava sect (especially a<BR>follower of Rāmānuja).<BR>—श्रीश (श्री-ईश), अस्, m.<BR>‘husband of Śrī,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; of Rāma-<BR>candra, (his wife Sītā being regarded as an incarna-<BR>tion of Śrī or Lakṣmī.)<BR>—श्री-शल्मली-भाण्ड-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—श्री-शुक-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—श्री-शैल, अस्, m. ‘Śrī's<BR>mountain,’ N. of a mountain.<BR>—श्री-सञ्ज्ञ, अम्, n.<BR>‘called after Śrī,’ cloves (the various names of Śrī are<BR>applied to this spice).<BR>—श्री-सरस्वती, त्यौ, f. du.<BR>Lakṣmī and Sarasvatī.<BR>—श्री-सहोदर, अस्, m.<BR>‘brother of Śrī,’ the moon (so called from having<BR>been produced with Śrī and other objects at the<BR>churning of the ocean).<BR>—श्री-सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Vedic hymn.<BR>—श्री-स्रज, अम्, n., see Vopa-deva<BR>VI. 7.<BR>—श्री-हरि, इस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu, (श्री-हरेर्<BR>उत्थानम्, N. of a festival on the fourteenth day of<BR>the month Kārttika.)<BR>—श्री-हस्तिनी, f. the sunflower,<BR>Heliotropium Indicum (so called as held in the hand<BR>of Śrī or Lakṣmī).<BR>—श्र्य्-आह्व, अम्, n. ‘having<BR>the name of Śrī,’ a lotus, (the goddess Śrī or Lak-<BR>ṣmī is said to have appeared first from within this<BR>flower and thence derives many of her names.)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161213. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 316-318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियस्
श्रियस्, Ved. happiness, prosperity; ornament, deco-<BR>ration, (Sāy. श्रियसे = श्रिये, Ṛg-veda V. 59, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिया
श्रिया, f., Ved. (for 2. श्री), the wife of Viṣṇu,<BR>(thought by some to be a doubtful form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीक
श्रीक = 2. श्री (at the end of adj. comps., e. g.<BR>पुण्य-श्रीक, possessing pure majesty; cf. निःश्रीक,<BR>विगत-श्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रील|श्रीलः
श्रील, अस्, आ, अम्, prosperous, fortunate; rich,<BR>wealthy; famous, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीत
श्रीत श्रीत. See p. 1025, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीषवायण
श्रीषवायण श्रीषवायण, N. of a part of<BR>the Romaka-siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
श्रु 1. श्रु (regarded by native gram-<BR>marians as an irregular rt. of cl. 1), cl. 5. P.<BR>शृणोति (ep. also A. शृणुते, 1st du. P. शृणुवस्<BR>or शृण्वस्), Impv. श्रिणोतु (2nd sing. शृणु Ved.,<BR>शृणुहि, शृणुधी, Pāṇ. VI. 4, 102, and श्रुधि,<BR>as if cl. 2), शुश्राव (2nd sing. शुश्रोथ, 1st du.<BR>शुश्रुव, 1st pl. शुश्रुम), अश्रौषीत्, (Ved. forms<BR>श्रोषन् = शृण्वन्ति, श्रोषन्तु = शृण्वन्तु,<BR>शृण्विषे, शृणोतु, शृणवत्, श्रवत्, शुश्रवत्),<BR>श्रोतुम्, to hear, listen to (with acc.), give ear<BR>to (with acc. or gen.); to be attentive, be obedient,<BR>obey; to go (according to Vopa-deva): Pass. श्रू-<BR>यते (शृण्वे = श्रूयते, Ṛg-veda I. 74, 7; शृण्-<BR>विरे = श्रूयन्ते, Ṛg-veda I. 15, 8), Aor. अश्रावि, to<BR>be heard; to be celebrated or renowned (Ved.);<BR>to be called (Ved.): Caus. श्रावयति, -ते, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अशिश्रवत्, -त, or अशुश्रवत्, -त, to cause<BR>any one to hear anything (with two acc.), tell, nar-<BR>rate, relate: Pass. of Caus. श्राव्यते: Desid. of<BR>Caus. शिश्रावयिषति, -ते, or (according to some)<BR>शुश्रावयिषति, -ते: Desid. शुश्रूषते, to desire to<BR>hear or listen to; to attend to, obey, be obedient to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">Page1027-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(with acc.); to wait upon, tend, serve: Intens.<BR>शोश्रूयते, शोश्रवीति, शोश्रोति; [cf. Gr. κλύ-ω,<BR>κλῦ-θι (= श्रुधि), κλυ-τό-ς (= श्रुत), κλέ-ος,<BR>κλε-ί-ω, κλέ-ο-μαι, κλε-ιν-ό-ς, κλει-τό-ς,<BR>ἀ-κρο-ά-ομαι, (perhaps also) κλαίω, κλαύσω, καλέω for<BR>κλαϝέω: Lat. clu-o, clu-e-o, cli-ens, in-clu-tu-s,<BR>clamo, (probably also) aus-cul-to, laudo for<BR>claus-do: Goth. hliu-ma, hrotheigs, (perhaps)<BR>hausja for hlausja: Old Germ. hlū-t (= श्रुत<BR>= Mod. Germ. Laut); hlūti, ‘a sound;’ hlūtian,<BR>‘to sound;’ hliu-munt (= Mod. Germ. Leumund),<BR>hlio-tar; hlo-s-en, hloson, hlosian, losen, ‘to<BR>hear;’ hōrin; hlamon: Old Sax. hlus-t; hlāmon,<BR>‘to sound:’ Angl. Sax. hlud, hlyd, hlowan, hlyn,<BR>hlyrian (?), hliosa, hlyst, hlystan: Eng. listen:<BR>Slav. slu-ti, slov-o, ‘a word;’ slava, ‘fame:’ Lith.<BR>szlove, ‘honour;’ klau-s-au, ‘I hear;’ slowiju, ‘I<BR>praise, celebrate;’ perhaps klabu, ‘to speak:’ Russ.<BR>slusaju, ‘I listen;’ slav-i-tj, ‘to celebrate;’ slovo,<BR>‘a word, speech:’ Hib. cluinim, ‘I hear;’ cluas,<BR>‘ear;’ clos, ‘hearing, report;’ cloisim, cluisim,<BR>‘I hear.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रुवस्
शुश्रुवस्, आन्, उषी, अत्, one who has heard, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृण्वत्
शृण्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, hearing, listening to, hearken-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रव|श्रवः
1. श्रव, अस्, m. (for 2. श्रव see p. 1028, col. 2),<BR>the ear; the hypothenuse of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवक
श्रवक, अस्, m. one who hears, a hearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवण|श्रवणं|श्रवणः
1. श्रवण, अम्, n. the act of hearing; that which<BR>is heard, i. e. Śruti or the Veda, (इति श्रवणात्, since<BR>it is so said in the Veda, because of or according to<BR>such a Vedic text); studying; (according to the<BR>Vedānta-sāra) the determining by means of the six<BR>Liṅgas the import of the whole Vedānta in regard<BR>to the Real and only existing Being; fame, glory;<BR>wealth; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the ear; the hypothenuse<BR>of a triangle; (अस्, आ), m. f., N. of one of the lunar<BR>asterisms (placed either twenty-second or twenty-third<BR>in the common list, and presided over by Viṣṇu,<BR>whence it is represented by three footsteps contain-<BR>ing three stars, अ, α, β, and γ Aquilæ; cf. त्रि-विक्रम);<BR>(अस्), m. a sort of disease, = श्रोण; (आ), f. a species<BR>of plant, = मुण्डीरिका; (अस्, आ, अम्), produced in<BR>or under Śravaṇā.<BR>—श्रवण-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a preceptor.<BR>—श्रवण-द्वादशी, f. a particular<BR>Tithi or lunar day (when certain religious ceremonies<BR>of great efficacy are observed; it is said to fall on<BR>the twelfth of the light half of Bhādra, when that<BR>month is connected with the asterism Śravaṇā).<BR>—श्र-<BR>वण-पथ, अस्, m. ‘hearing-path,’ the ear.<BR>—श्र-<BR>वण-परुष, अस्, आ, अम्, hard or cruel to the ear,<BR>hard to be listened to.<BR>—श्रवण-पालि, इस्, f. the<BR>tip of the ear.<BR>—श्रवण-विधि, इस्, m. a method or<BR>rule of hearing or studying.<BR>—श्रवण-विधि-विचार,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a treatise on the study of the Upani-<BR>shads.<BR>—श्रवण-विषय-प्रापिन्, reaching the<BR>range of the ear.<BR>—श्रवण-शीर्षिका, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= श्रावणी).<BR>—श्रवणाधिकारिन् (˚ण-<BR>अध्˚), ई, m. ‘one who rules or influences the ears<BR>(of others),’ a speaker, addresser.<BR>—श्रवणेन्द्रिय<BR>(˚ण-इन्˚), अम्, n. the organ of hearing, the ear.<BR>—श्रवणोत्पल (˚ण-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘ear-lotus,’ a<BR>lotus fastened in the ear (as an ornament).<BR>—श्र-<BR>वणोदर (˚ण-उद्˚), अम्, n. the hollow of the<BR>outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणस्य
श्रवणस्य, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणिकाव्रत
श्रवणिका-व्रत, अम्, n. epithet of a particular<BR>religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणीय
श्रवणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be heard, &c.; to be<BR>celebrated, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवयत्
श्रवयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. making famous or<BR>celebrated, celebrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्
श्रवस्, अस्, n. the ear; fame, renown, glory [cf.<BR>Gr. κλέος]; wealth; a hymn, eulogy; anything<BR>deserving praise, a praiseworthy action, (in the latter<BR>senses chiefly Ved.); food, (Sāy. = अन्न.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्य|श्रवस्यं
1. श्रवस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worthy of praise,<BR>praiseworthy, to be celebrated, (Sāy. = श्रवणीय);<BR>(अम्), n. anything praiseworthy, fame, glory, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्य|श्रवस्यं
2. श्रवस्य, Nom. P. श्रवस्यति, &c., to desire<BR>fame or glory; to desire a sacrifice or oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्या
श्रवस्या, f., Ved. desire of fame or glory; desire<BR>of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्यु
श्रवस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desirous of fame or<BR>that which deserves praise, eager for glory, desiring<BR>wealth or treasures; desirous of food or of an obla-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवाप्य|श्रवाप्यः
श्रवाप्य, अस्, m. an animal fit for sacrifice, sacri-<BR>ficial animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवाय्य|श्रवाय्यः
श्रवाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be praised, noto-<BR>rious, well-known, (Sāy. = श्रवणीय); (अस्), m. an<BR>animal fit for sacrifice; [cf. श्रवाप्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठ
श्रविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, most famous; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a lunar asterism (placed twenty-fourth in the com-<BR>mon list; it is also called Dhaniṣṭhā, q. v., and<BR>corresponds to the four principal stars in the head of<BR>the Dolphin); (अस्, आ, अम्), produced in or under<BR>Śraviṣṭhā.<BR>—श्रविष्ठा-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born under<BR>Śraviṣṭhā; (अस्), m. the planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठक
श्रविष्ठक, अस्, m., N. of a Muni, (see श्र-<BR>विष्ठ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रव्य|श्रव्यः
श्रव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be heard, worthy of being<BR>listened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव|श्रावः
1. श्राव, अस्, m. hearing, listening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावक|श्रावकः
श्रावक, अस्, इका, अम्, hearing, a hearer; (अस्),<BR>m. a pupil, disciple; a particular class of Buddhist<BR>saints or ascetics, (properly one who by adhering to<BR>the teaching of the Buddha and practising the four<BR>great truths becomes eventually qualified to be ranked<BR>as an Arhat and to be addressed as Āyuṣ-mat;<BR>eighty of the disciples of the great Buddha are called<BR>Mahā-śrāvakas or Great Śrāvakas); a Bauddha or<BR>Buddhist votary (in general); a heretic; a crow.<BR>—श्रावक-व्रत, N. of a Jaina treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावण|श्रावणः
श्रावण, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the ear or hearing,<BR>audible; belonging to or produced under the asterism<BR>Śravaṇā; (अस्), m. the month Śrāvaṇa (July-August);<BR>a heretic, impostor [cf. श्रावक]; N. of a Muni;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of causing to be heard; knowledge<BR>derived from hearing; (आ), f. a kind of plant (com-<BR>monly called Kaṭukī); (ई), f. the day of full moon<BR>in the month Śrāvaṇa; N. of one of the domestic<BR>sacrifices; a species of plant (= भिक्षु).<BR>—श्रा-<BR>वण-कृष्ण-चतुर्थी, f. the fourth day in the<BR>dark half of the month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>—श्रावण-द्वा-<BR>दशी, f. the twelfth day of Śrāvaṇa.<BR>—श्रावणद्वा-<BR>दशी-व्रत, अम्, n. a religious observance on the<BR>above day.<BR>—श्रावण-विधि, इस्, m., N. of a Pari-<BR>śiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—श्रावण-शुक्ल-चतुर्थी,<BR>f. the fourth day in the light half of the month<BR>Śrāvaṇa.<BR>—श्रावण-शुक्ल-तृतीया, the third day in<BR>the light half of the month Śrāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणिक|श्रावणिकः
श्रावणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or produced in<BR>the month Śrāvaṇa; (अस्), m. the month Śrāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणीय
श्रावणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be caused to be heard,<BR>to be declared or pronounced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावयत्
श्रावयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to be heard,<BR>making famous, conferring honour.<BR>—श्रावयत्-<BR>पति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. causing the mighty to hear, i. e.<BR>gaining the ear of the mighty gods; (Sāy.) conferring<BR>honour on fathers, making ancestors celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावयितव्य
श्रावयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made to be heard,<BR>to be declared or made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावयित्वा
श्रावयित्वा, ind. having caused to hear, having<BR>made to be heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावष्ठीय
श्रावष्ठीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging<BR>to the asterism Śravaṇā or (according to some) to<BR>Śraviṣṭhā, produced in or under this asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावित
श्रावित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be heard, spoken,<BR>told, related, narrated, read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राविन्
श्राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, hearing, a hearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव्य
श्राव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be caused to be heard, to<BR>be told or related or read; to be heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत|श्रुतं|श्रुतः
श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, heard, listened to; reported,<BR>heard of; ascertained, understood; called; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of an enemy of Indra (Ved.); of a son of Dharma;<BR>of a son of Bhagīratha; of a son of Upagu; of a<BR>son of Kṛṣṇa; (अम्), n. the object of hearing;<BR>that which was heard from the beginning, the Veda,<BR>revelation, sacred knowledge, holy writ, &c.<BR>—श्रुत-<BR>ऋषि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. one by whom the Ṛṣis have<BR>been heard, (Sāy. = श्रुता ऋषयो येन; cf. श्रु-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-c" target="_blank">Page1027-c+ 81</a>]<BR>तर्षि.)<BR>—श्रुत-कक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a Vedic<BR>Ṛṣi (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda VIII. 81).<BR>—श्रुत-कर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a son of Saha-deva.<BR>—श्रुत-कीर्त्ति, इस्, f. ‘Veda-renown,’ fame of divine<BR>science; (इस्, इस्, इ), having renowned fame, cele-<BR>brated, famous; (इस्), m. epithet of various persons;<BR>a divine sage; a generous man, benefactor, donor;<BR>(इस्), f. a river; N. of the wife of Śatru-ghna; of<BR>other women.<BR>—श्रुत-केवलिन्, इनस्, m. pl. epithet<BR>of a class of Jaina Arhats (of whom six are enume-<BR>rated).<BR>—श्रुतञ्-जय, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—श्रु-<BR>त-देवा, f., N. of a daughter of Śūra and wife of<BR>Vṛddha-śarman.<BR>—श्रुत-देवी, f. ‘goddess of learn-<BR>ing,’ epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR>—श्रुत-धर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, recollecting or remembering what has been<BR>heard, having or observing the Vedas; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a poet; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people (inhabiting<BR>a division of Plaksha-dvīpa).<BR>—श्रुत-प्रकास, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, renowned for knowledge of the Vedas.<BR>—श्रुत-बन्धु, उस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>several hymns in the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—श्रुत-बोध, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a treatise on the most common Sanskrit<BR>metres by a certain Kālidāsa.<BR>—श्रुतर्षि (˚त-<BR>ऋषि), इस्, m. a kind of secondary Ṛṣi, one by<BR>whom the Vedic Ṛṣis have been heard; the son of<BR>a Ṛṣi; a Ṛṣi of a particular order (as the author<BR>of the Su-śruta).<BR>—१. श्रुत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one<BR>who has heard, hearing.<BR>—२. श्रुत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessing or knowing the Veda, instructed in sacred<BR>learning, pious; (आन्), m., N. of a king.<BR>—श्रुत-<BR>विद्, त्, m. ‘knowing sacred revelation,’ N. of an<BR>Ātreya (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda V. 62).<BR>—श्रुत-शील, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—श्रुत-श्रवस्,<BR>आस्, m., N. of a king; (आस्), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Śūra.<BR>—श्रुतश्रवो-ऽनुज (˚वस्-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘born<BR>after Śruta-śravas,’ the planet Saturn (said to be one<BR>of the sons of Sūrya).<BR>—श्रुत-श्रोणी, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= द्रवन्ती).<BR>—श्रुत-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Parīkṣit.<BR>—श्रुत-सोम, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Bhīma.<BR>—श्रुतादान (˚त-आद्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘Veda-acceptation,’ citing the Vedas.<BR>—श्रुताध्य-<BR>यन-सम्पन्न (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, well read<BR>in sacred science, conversant with the Vedas.<BR>—श्रु-<BR>तान्वित (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, acquainted with or<BR>conforming to the Vedas.<BR>—श्रुता-मघ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having renowned treasures.<BR>—श्रुतायु or<BR>श्रुतायुस् (˚त-आय्˚), उस्, m., N. of a king of the<BR>solar race descended from Kuśa, son of Rāma; of a<BR>son of Purū-ravas; of another king:<BR>—श्रुतार्थ<BR>(˚त-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘heard-matter,’ any matter ascer-<BR>tained by hearing, a fact verbally or orally communi-<BR>cated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतर्य
श्रुतर्य, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a man (protected<BR>by the Aśvins).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतर्वन्
श्रुतर्वन्, आ, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुति|श्रुतिः
श्रुति, इस्, f. ‘audition,’ hearing; an ear; anything<BR>heard, sound, oral account, report, rumour, intelli-<BR>gence, news; that which was heard or revealed from<BR>the beginning, revelation, the Veda (i. e. sound<BR>eternally heard and so differing from स्मृति or what<BR>is only remembered and handed down by human<BR>authors, see Manu II. 10; properly applied to works<BR>considered to have been revealed by a deity, and<BR>therefore only to the Mantra and Brāhmaṇa portion<BR>of the Vedas, but often applied also to the Upaniṣads<BR>and other Vedic works); any Vedic or sacred text,<BR>(इति श्रुतेः, according to or because of such a श्रुति<BR>or Vedic text); the hearing of a sound, a sound;<BR>the diagonal of a tetragon or hypothenuse of a<BR>triangle; (in music) a particular division of the<BR>octave, a quarter tone or interval, (twenty-two of<BR>these are enumerated, four constituting a major tone,<BR>three a minor, and two a semitone; they are said<BR>to be personified as nymphs); the constellation Śra-<BR>vaṇā.<BR>—श्रुति-कट, अस्, m. penance, expiation; a<BR>snake; (according to Śabda-k.) = प्राञ्चल्लोह.<BR>—श्रुति-कटु, उस्, उस्, उ, harsh to the ear, unme-<BR>lodious; (उस्), m. a harsh or unmelodious sound,<BR>cacophony (a fault in rhetoric).<BR>—श्रुति-कथित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, mentioned in the Veda, taught or prescribed<BR>by the Vedas.<BR>—श्रुति-कीर्त्ति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">Page1028-a+ 80</a>]<BR>—श्रुति-चोदन, अम्, n. ‘Veda-precept,’ holy pre-<BR>cept or injunction, the doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>—श्रुति-<BR>जीविका, f. a law-book or code of laws.<BR>—श्रुति-तत्-<BR>पर, अस्, आ, अम्, intent on hearing; intent on<BR>studying the Veda.<BR>—श्रुति-द्वैध, अम्, n. dis-<BR>agreement or contradiction of any two passages in<BR>the Vedas or of two Vedas.<BR>—श्रुति-धर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ascertaining or perceiving by the ear, hearing;<BR>holding or observing the Vedas; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>poet; [cf. श्रुत-धर.]<BR>—श्रुति-निदर्शन, अम्,<BR>n. the evidence of revelation, testimony of the Veda.<BR>—श्रुति-प्रसादन, अस्, ई, अम्, gratifying the ear,<BR>grateful to the ear.<BR>—श्रुति-प्रामाण्यतस्, ind. on<BR>the authority of the Veda, with the sanction of the<BR>Veda.<BR>—श्रुति-मण्डल, अम्, n. ‘ear-circle,’ the<BR>outer ear.<BR>—श्रुति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of ears,<BR>capable of hearing.<BR>—श्रुति-मूल, अम्, n. the root of<BR>the ear; the text of the Vedas.<BR>—श्रुति-मूलक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, founded on the Veda, springing from the<BR>Veda.<BR>—श्रुति-मृग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sought by<BR>hearing or by the Vedas (not by sight).<BR>—श्रुति-वर्-<BR>जित, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of hearing, deaf; ignorant<BR>or unread in the Vedas.<BR>—श्रुति-विप्रतिपन्न, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, dissenting from revelation, disregarding the<BR>doctrine of the Veda.<BR>—श्रुति-विषय, अस्, m. the<BR>object of hearing (i. e. sound, see विषय); subject-<BR>matter or doctrine of the Veda, any sacred matter or<BR>ordinance; (अस्, आ, अम्), conversant with sacred<BR>matters, familiar with the Veda.<BR>—श्रुति-विषय-<BR>गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘having the quality [sound] which<BR>is the object of hearing or which is perceptible by<BR>the ear,’ epithet of ether.<BR>—श्रुति-वेध, अस्, m. the<BR>piercing or boring of the ear.<BR>—श्रुति-स्फोटा, f. a<BR>kind of creeper (= कर्ण-स्फोटा).<BR>—श्रुति-स्मृति,<BR>ई, f. du. the Veda and legal tradition, the Veda<BR>and institutes of law.<BR>—श्रुति-स्मृति-विरुद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, opposed to the Vedas and to tra-<BR>dition or law.<BR>—श्रुति-स्मृति-विहित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>enjoined by the Vedas and the law.<BR>—श्रुति-स्मृत्य्-<BR>उदित, अस्, आ, अम्, declared or enjoined by the Veda<BR>and law.<BR>—श्रुत्य्-अनुप्रास, अस्, m. repetition of<BR>sound, alliteration.<BR>—श्रुत्य्-उक्त or श्रुत्य्-उदित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, said or enjoined by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिन्
श्रुतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hearing; obeying, observing;<BR>having or possessing the Veda, following the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुती
श्रुती, f. = श्रुति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्कर्ण
श्रुत्-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who has hearing<BR>ears, quick-hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्य
श्रुत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be heard, famous,<BR>glorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्वा
श्रुत्वा, ind. having heard or listened to, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुश्रुतवत्
श्रुश्रुतवत्, आन्, अती, अत् (doubtful; said to be a<BR>reduplicated form), one who has heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्ट
श्रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to some)<BR>heard, handed down, (श्रुष्टे, according to tradition<BR>or ordinance.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्टि|श्रुष्टिः
श्रुष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. hearing, listening to, audience;<BR>help, assistance; a boon; prosperity, happiness,<BR>abundance, (Sāy. = यज्ञ-फल-रूपं सुखम्,<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 69, 4.)<BR>—श्रुष्टि-गु, उस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of one of the Vālakhilya hymns.<BR>—श्रुष्टि-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing happiness, pros-<BR>perous, happy, (Sāy. = सुख-वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्टी
श्रुष्टी, ind. (according to some an old inst. or<BR>dat. for श्रुष्ट्यै), Ved. having heard, having<BR>listened to, (Sāy. = श्रुत्वा, Ṛg-veda VIII. 23, 14);<BR>‘as soon as heard,’ readily, quickly, in a moment,<BR>(Sāy. = क्षिप्रम्; in Ṛg-veda II. 3, 9. श्रुष्टी is<BR>regarded as a nom. c. masc. and explained by क्षि-<BR>प्र-गुणः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्टीवन्
श्रुष्टी-वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. possessing happiness,<BR>granting prosperity, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 45, 2. ex-<BR>plains श्रुष्टीवानः by श्रुष्टिः फलस्य दानं<BR>तद्-भाजः; in Ṛg-veda I. 119, 1. श्रुष्टीवानम्<BR>= क्षिप्रं सम्भजमानम् or सुखवन्तम्;<BR>श्रुष्टीवरीः = सुखवत्यः, Ṛg-veda X. 30, 11);<BR>listening to, helping (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रूयमाण
श्रूयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being heard, heard.<BR>—श्रूयमाण-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition<BR>of being heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतव्य|श्रोतव्यं
श्रोतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be heard or listened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतस्
1. श्रोतस्, अस्, n. the ear; an organ of sense; the<BR>trunk of an elephant (as his special organ).<BR>—श्रोत-<BR>आपन्न, अस्, m., N. of one of the four orders of<BR>Buddhist Āryas.<BR>—श्रोतो-रन्ध्र, अम्, n. an aper-<BR>ture of the proboscis, a nostril.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतु
श्रोतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. hearing, a hearer; re-<BR>nowned.<BR>—श्रोतु-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having re-<BR>nowned wealth or gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतृ
श्रोतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who hears, hearing, a<BR>hearer; (ता), m. a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्र|श्रोत्रं
श्रोत्र, अम्, n. the organ of hearing, ear; con-<BR>versancy with the Veda or sacred revelation; the<BR>Veda; [cf. Angl. Sax. hleodhor.]<BR>—श्रोत्र-पदा-<BR>नुग, अस्, आ, अम्, agreeable to the ear.<BR>—श्रोत्र-<BR>पेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be imbibed by the ear, i. e. to<BR>be heard respectfully.<BR>—श्रोत्र-भिद्, त्, त्, त्, splitting<BR>the ears.<BR>—श्रोत्र-मूल, अम्, n. the root of the<BR>ear.<BR>—श्रोत्र-सुख, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding agreeably,<BR>melodious, musical.<BR>—श्रोत्रादि (˚र-आदि), इ, n.<BR>‘the ear and the other senses,’ i. e. the five senses,<BR>(see इन्द्रिय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रिय|श्रोत्रियः
श्रोत्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, learned in the Veda, con-<BR>versant with sacred revelation, teachable, docile, well-<BR>behaved; (अस्), m. a Brāhman versed in the study<BR>of the Vedas, a theologian, divine; a Brāhman fol-<BR>lowing a particular branch or school of the Vedas.<BR>—श्रोत्रिय-ता, f. conversancy with the Vedas, the<BR>being a learned Brāhman.<BR>—श्रोत्रिय-स्व, अम्, n.<BR>the property of a learned Brāhman, (Manu VIII.<BR>149.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोमत
श्रोमत (according to Sāy. to be connected with<BR>rt. 1. श्रु), Ved. fame, renown, (Sāy. श्रोमताय =<BR>कीर्त्तिमत्त्वाय, Ṛg-veda I. 182, 7; श्रोमतेभिः<BR>= श्रोतव्यैर् यशोभिः, Ṛg-veda VI. 19, 10; श्रो-<BR>मतेन = श्रवणीयेन पुंस्त्वेन, Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>66, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोषमाण
श्रोषमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hearing, listening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत|श्रौतं|श्रौतः
श्रौत, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the ear or hearing;<BR>relating or belonging to the Veda, prescribed by the<BR>Vedas, founded on the Vedas; sacrificial; (अम्), n.<BR>any observance ordained by the Vedas; preservation<BR>of the sacred fire; the three sacred fires collectively,<BR>(viz. गार्हपत्य, आहवनीय, and दक्षिण); (ई),<BR>f. comparison expressed by a particle (?).<BR>—श्रौत-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. a Vedic rite.<BR>—श्रौत-पद्धति, इस्,<BR>f., N. of a work, (probably belonging to the Sāma-<BR>veda.)<BR>—श्रौत-प्रायश्चित्त, अम्, n., N. of a Pari-<BR>śiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—श्रौत-श्रव, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—श्रौत-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of certain<BR>Sūtras or Sūtra works based on Śruti or the Veda,<BR>see सूत्र, (ascribed to various authors, such as Āśva-<BR>lāyana, Kātyāyana, Śāṅkhāyana, &c.)<BR>—श्रौत-<BR>स्मार्त-क्रिया, f. any act conformable to law and<BR>the Veda.<BR>—श्रौत-स्मार्त-धर्म, अस्, m. a duty<BR>enjoined by law and the Veda.<BR>—श्रौत-होम-प-<BR>रिशिष्ट, अम्, n. a Pari-śiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतर्ष
श्रौतर्ष, अस्, m. a patronymic from Śrutarṣi,<BR>a son of Śrutarṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत्र|श्रौत्रं
श्रौत्र, अम्, n. the ear; that which relates to<BR>the ear or hearing; conversancy with the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौषट्
श्रौषट्, ind. ‘may he, i. e. the god, hear us!’<BR>an exclamation used in making an offering with fire<BR>to the gods or departed spirits; [cf. वौषट्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
श्रु 2. श्रु (a less correct reading for rt.<BR>स्रु, q. v.), cl. 1. P. श्रवति, &c., to flow,<BR>go, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रव|श्रवः
2. श्रव, अस्, m. (for स्रव, q. v.), flowing,<BR>oozing, dripping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवण|श्रवणं|श्रवणः
2. श्रवण, अम्, n. (for स्रवण, q. v.), the act<BR>of flowing, dripping, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव|श्रावः
2. श्राव, अस्, m. (for स्राव, q. v.), flowing, oozing,<BR>dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुव|श्रुवः
श्रुव, अस्, m. (for स्रुव, q. v.), a sacrificial ladle,<BR>(according to some अम्, n.); a sacrifice, oblation;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of creeper or shrub (= मूर्वा).<BR>—श्रुवा-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the Vikaṅkata tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतस्
2. श्रोतस्, अस्, n. (for स्रोतस्, q. v.), the current of<BR>a stream.<BR>—श्रोतो-ऽञ्जन, अम्, n. antimony, (for<BR>स्रोतो-ऽञ्जन, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुग्वारु|श्रुग्वारुः
श्रुग्वारु श्रुग्वारु, उस्, m. the plant Fla-<BR>courtia Sapida (= विकङ्कत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुघ्निका
श्रुघ्निका श्रुघ्निका, f. impure carbonate of<BR>soda, natron, alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्
श्रुष् श्रुष्, a form in Ved. assumed by rt.<BR>1. श्रु (q. v.) in certain tenses and derivatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्ट
श्रुष्ट, श्रुष्टि, श्रुष्टी, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रू
श्रू श्रू, ऊस्, according to Vopa-deva XXVI.<BR>75. connected with a rt. श्रिव् for स्रिव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेक्
श्रेक् श्रेक्, another form of rt. स्रेक्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेटी
श्रेटी श्रेटी, f. (perhaps connected with<BR>श्रेणी, cf. श्रेधी), a particular numerical notation or<BR>progression of figures in arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणि|श्रेणिः
श्रेणि श्रेणि, इस्, m. f. or श्रेणी, f. (according<BR>to Uṇādi-s. IV. 51. fr. rt. श्रि), a line, row, range;<BR>a troop, multitude, number, quantity; a corporation<BR>or company of artisans following the same business,<BR>a guild or company of traders dealing in the same<BR>articles; a bucket, baling vessel.<BR>—श्रेणि-दत् (?) , अन्,<BR>m. according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X. 20, 3. श्रेणि-<BR>दन् = अभीष्ट-फल-समूह-प्रदः or शत्रु-<BR>भ्यो ज्वाल-पङ्क्ति-प्रदः.<BR>—श्रेणि-मत्, आन्, m.<BR>the commander or master of a company, chief of a<BR>corporate body or guild.<BR>—श्रेणि-शस्, ind. in rows<BR>or lines; in troops or flocks.<BR>—श्रेणी-धर्म, आस्,<BR>m. pl. the customs of trades or guilds, (Manu VIII.<BR>41.)<BR>—श्रेणी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्,<BR>to arrange in line or in regular order, to be or be-<BR>come a heap.<BR>—श्रेणी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, arranged in<BR>rows, formed in lines; become or made a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणिक|श्रेणिकः
श्रेणिक, अस्, m., N. of one of the kings of Ma-<BR>gadhā (said to have been contemporary with and<BR>patron of Śākya-siṃha); (आ), f. a tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेधी
श्रेधी श्रेधी, f. [cf. श्रेटी, श्रेणी], any set or<BR>succession of distinct things; (in arithmetic) pro-<BR>gression; sequence.<BR>—श्रेधी-फल, अम्, n. the<BR>sum of a progression.<BR>—श्रेधी-व्यवहार, अस्, m.<BR>the ascertainment or determination of progressions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्
श्रेयस् श्रेयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (considered as<BR>compar. of either श्री-मत् or प्रशस्य), better,<BR>more excellent, superior, preferable; best, excellent,<BR>most excellent; more fortunate, very fortunate, more<BR>prosperous, very prosperous; most beloved; (अस्), ind.<BR>well, most excellent, rather, (श्रेयस् — न, rather —<BR>than); (अस्), n. virtue, moral merit; an act leading<BR>to the chief temporal good; good fortune, auspicious-<BR>ness, prosperity, bliss, final happiness or beatitude;<BR>(आन्), m., N. of the eleventh Arhat, (see below);<BR>epithet of the second Muhūrta; N. of the third<BR>month (according to a particular reckoning); (असी),<BR>f. a plant resembling pepper, Pothos Officinalis; the<BR>shrub Cissampelos Hexandra; yellow myrobalan;<BR>other plants (= पाठा; = रास्ना).<BR>—श्रेयः-परि-<BR>श्राम, अस्, आ, अम्, toiling after final emancipation.<BR>—श्रेयस्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, making better or su-<BR>perior; effecting happiness, ensuring felicity, con-<BR>ferring future felicity; auspicious, propitious.<BR>—श्रे-<BR>यस्-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring final felicity, &c.<BR>—श्रेयस्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, very much better.<BR>—श्रेयस्-त्व, अम्, n. betterness, superiority; final<BR>felicity, &c.<BR>—श्रेयो-ऽर्थिन् (˚यस्-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>desirous of the good (of others), wishing well; seek-<BR>ing happiness, desirous of felicity, seeking merit in<BR>the performance of religious rites &c., ambitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस
श्रेयस at the end of a comp., e. g. निः-श्रेयस,<BR>श्वः-श्रेयस, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयसितरा
श्रेयसितरा or श्रेयसीतरा, f. a more excellent<BR>woman, (Pāṇ. VI. 3, 45.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयांश
श्रेयांश, अस्, m., N. of the eleventh Arhat of<BR>the present Avasarpiṇī, (also written श्रेयांस.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठ|श्रेष्ठं|श्रेष्ठः
श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, best (with gen. or loc., e. g.<BR>तेषाम् or तेषु श्रेष्ठः, best of them), excel-<BR>lent, most excellent, very eminent or illustrious, pre-<BR>eminent, highest in rank, higher in rank; most<BR>prosperous; oldest, senior; (अस्), m. a Brāhman; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">Page1029-a+ 73</a>]<BR>king; an epithet of Viṣṇu; of Kuvera; (आ), f. an<BR>excellent woman; a kind of shrub (= स्थल-पद्-<BR>मिनी); a root, = मेदा; (अम्), n. cow's milk.<BR>—श्रेष्ठ-काष्ठ, अम्, n. the main pillar of<BR>a house.<BR>—श्रेष्ठ-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, the very<BR>best, most excellent.<BR>—श्रेष्ठ-ता, f. or श्रेष्-<BR>ठ-त्व, अम्, n. betterness, superiority, eminence,<BR>excellence.<BR>—श्रेष्ठ-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, possessing the<BR>best.<BR>—श्रेष्ठ-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, pre-eminent in<BR>speech, eloquent.<BR>—श्रेष्ठ-शोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved.<BR>having the best splendor.<BR>—श्रेष्ठाम्ल (˚ठ-<BR>अम्˚), अम्, n. the fruit of the tamarind.<BR>—श्रेष्ठा-<BR>श्रम (˚ठ-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘best order,’ one who<BR>is in the best order, a householder (considered to<BR>belong to the best of the four orders as supporting<BR>the other three).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठिन्
श्रेष्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ, best, chief; (ई), m. an artist<BR>eminent by birth, the head or chief of a company<BR>following the same trade, a president or foreman of<BR>a guild or corporation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रैष्ठ्य|श्रैष्ठ्यं
श्रैष्ठ्य, अम्, n. superiority, preference, super-<BR>excellence, pre-eminence, superlativeness.<BR>—श्रैष्-<BR>ठ्य-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रै
श्रै श्रै, another form of rt. श्रा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण्
श्रोण् श्रोण् (also written श्लोण्), cl. 1. P.<BR>श्रोणति, श्रोणितुम्, to collect, accumu-<BR>late, heap together; to go, move (according to Yāska).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण|श्रोणः
श्रोण श्रोण, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. III. 6. apparently fr. rt. 1. or 2. श्रु), lame, a<BR>cripple; dressed, cooked, matured, (in this sense<BR>probably for श्राण); (अस्), m. a kind of disease<BR>[cf. 1. श्रवण]; (आ), f. rice-gruel [cf. श्राण]; the<BR>constellation Śravaṇā, (contracted fr. श्रवणा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणि|श्रोणिः
श्रोणि, इस्, f. m. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 51. fr.<BR>rt. 1. or 2. श्रु), the hip and loins, buttocks; a<BR>road, way; [cf. Gr. κλόνι-ς, κλόνιο-ν, κλονιστήρ,<BR>Lat. clûnis, clunaclum; Lith. szlauni-s; Hib.<BR>slias, ‘the thigh, the loins.’]<BR>—श्रोणि-तट, अस्, m.<BR>the slope of the hips, (see तट.)<BR>—श्रोणि-फल or<BR>श्रोणि-फलक, अम्, n. the hip and loins or the<BR>hip only; the hip-bone (os ilium).<BR>—श्रोणि-वर्जम्,<BR>ind. except the hips.<BR>—श्रोणि-विम्ब, अम्, n. a<BR>waist-band.<BR>—श्रोणि-सूत्र, अम्, n. a string worn<BR>round the loins; a sword-belt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणी
श्रोणी, f. = श्रोणि above; N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतोञ्जन
श्रोतोञ्जन श्रोतो-ऽञ्जन. See under 2. श्रो-<BR>तस्, p. 1028.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्र|श्रोत्रं
श्रोत्र श्रोत्र, श्रौत, &c. See p. 1028.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोमत
श्रोमत श्रोमत, श्रोषमाण, &c. See<BR>p. 1028, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौषट्
श्रौषट् श्रौषट्. See p. 1028, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौष्टिन्
श्रौष्टिन् श्रौष्टिन्, ई, m. (fr. श्रुष्टी = क्षि-<BR>प्र), Ved. having speed, quick, rapid, (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 48, 2. श्रौष्टी = क्षि-<BR>प्र-गाम्य् अश्वः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्र्याह्व|श्र्याह्वं
श्र्याह्व श्र्य्-आह्व. See under 2. श्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्ण|श्लक्ष्णं
श्लक्ष्ण श्लक्ष्ण अस्, आ, अम् (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. III. 19. fr. rt. श्लिष्), small, fine, thin,<BR>minute, slender, delicate; smooth, even, plain,<BR>polished; beautiful, pleasing, charming, soft, gentle,<BR>mild, amiable; honest, sincere, candid.<BR>—श्लक्ष्ण-<BR>त्वच्, क्, m. smooth bark; (क्), m. ‘having a smooth<BR>bark,’ a kind of plant (= अश्मन्तक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णक|श्लक्ष्णकं
श्लक्ष्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, smooth, even; beautiful,<BR>pleasing; (अम्), n. the fruit of the Areca Catechu,<BR>the Areca nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णय
श्लक्ष्णय, Nom. P. श्लक्ष्णयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make thin or small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लङ्क्|श्लंक्
श्लङ्क् श्लङ्क् (= rt. श्रङ्क्, q. v.), cl. 1. A.<BR>श्लङ्कते, शश्लङ्के, श्लङ्कितुम्, to go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लङ्ग्|श्लंग्
श्लङ्ग् श्लङ्ग् (= rt. श्रङ्ग्), cl. 1. P. श्लङ्-<BR>गति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ्
श्लथ् श्लथ् (apparently a later form of<BR>rt. श्रथ्, q. v.), cl. 1. 10. P. श्लथति,<BR>&c., श्लथयति, -यितुम्, to be loose or relaxed or<BR>flaccid, be unfastened; to be weak; to hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ
श्लथ, अस्, आ, अम्, relaxed, loose, flaccid; untied,<BR>unfastened; dishevelled (as hair).<BR>—श्लथ-बन्-<BR>धन, अस्, ई, अम्, having the muscles relaxed.<BR>—श्लथ-लम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hanging loosely.<BR>—श्ल-<BR>थोद्यम (˚थ-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, relaxing one's<BR>efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथत्
श्लथत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being loose or relaxed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लवण
श्लवण श्लवण, अस्, m. = श्रवण; [cf.<BR>श्लोण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाख्
श्लाख् श्लाख् (= rt. शाख्), cl. 1. P. श्ला-<BR>खति, श्लाखितुम्, to pervade, pene-<BR>trate, embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्
श्लाघ् श्लाघ्, cl. 1. A. श्लाघते (ep. also<BR>P. -ति), शश्लाघे, अश्लाघिष्ट, श्लाघि-<BR>तुम्, to flatter, coax, wheedle (with dat.); to praise,<BR>commend, applaud, celebrate, eulogise; to be proud<BR>of, boast of (with inst.): Pass. श्लाघ्यते, Aor.<BR>अश्लाघि, to be praised or celebrated or magnified:<BR>Caus. श्लाघयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अशश्लाघत्, to<BR>approve, praise, celebrate, congratulate; [cf. Gr. κρή-<BR>γυον, probably κόλαξ: Hib. sleigh, ‘adoration;’<BR>sleachd, ‘adoration;’ sleachdaim, ‘I adore.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघन|श्लाघनं
श्लाघन, अम्, n. the act of flattering, praising, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघनीय
श्लाघनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, praise-<BR>worthy, laudable, commendable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघमान
श्लाघमान, अस्, आ, अम्, flattering, praising; con-<BR>gratulating one's self, rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघयित्वा
श्लाघयित्वा, ind. having praised or applauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघा
श्लाघा, f. flattery, praise, commendation, pane-<BR>gyric, eulogium; boasting; service, obedience; wish,<BR>desire.<BR>—श्लाघा-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, meriting praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघित
श्लाघित, अस्, आ, अम्, flattered, praised, commended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघित्वा
श्लाघित्वा, ind. having flattered, having praised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघिन्
श्लाघिन्, ई, इनी, इ, flattering, praising, commend-<BR>ing; desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्य|श्लाघ्यः
श्लाघ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised or commended,<BR>praiseworthy, entitled to praise or veneration, venera-<BR>ble, respectable, honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्यमान
श्लाघ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being praised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिकु|श्लिकुः
श्लिकु श्लिकु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 33. fr. rt. 2. श्लिष्), a servant, slave, dependant;<BR>a profligate or low person, libertine, debauchee; (उ),<BR>n. astronomy, astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्
श्लिष् 1. श्लिष् (= rt. 1. श्रिष्), cl. 1. P.<BR>श्लेषति, शिश्लेष, श्लेषितुम्, to burn,<BR>consume by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष|श्लेषः
1. श्लेष, अस्, m. burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्
श्लिष् 2. श्लिष्, cl. 4. P. श्लिष्यति (ep.<BR>also A. -ते), शिश्लेष, श्लेक्ष्यति,<BR>अश्लिक्षत् (in the sense of ‘to embrace’), अश्लि-<BR>षत् (and according to some also अश्लैक्षीत् in<BR>other senses), श्लेष्टुम्, to adhere, cling to, be<BR>united or connected with; to embrace; to unite,<BR>tie, join, connect: Pass. श्लिष्यते, Aor. अश्लेषि, to<BR>be joined or connected; to be implied or intimated;<BR>cl. 10. P. or Caus. श्लेषयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशि-<BR>श्लिषत्, to cause to embrace; to embrace, connect:<BR>Desid. शिश्लिक्षति: Intens. शेश्लिष्यते, शेश्लेष्टि;<BR>[cf. Gr. κλη-ΐς, κλείς, κλει-δός, κλεί-ω: Lat.<BR>clāvi-s, clau-d-o: Old Germ. sliuz-u: Slav. klju-<BR>ci, ‘a key;’ kljucati se, ‘to agree:’ Hib. crios, ‘a<BR>belt, girdle.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिषा
श्लिषा, f. clinging, embracing, an embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्ट|श्लिष्टः
श्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, clung to, adhered to; touched<BR>by; leaning on; embraced; connected so as to be sus-<BR>ceptible of a double interpretation, (applied to a figure<BR>of speech by which two objects are closely connected<BR>and epithets applied to both in common), implied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्टि|श्लिष्टिः
श्लिष्टि, इस्, f. adherence, connection; embrace;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a son of Dhruva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्ट्वा
श्लिष्ट्वा, ind. having clung or adhered, having<BR>embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्यत्
श्लिष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, clinging to, adhering to,<BR>being in close contact with; embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्यमाण
श्लिष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being embraced, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष|श्लेषः
2. श्लेष, अस्, m. adhering or clinging to; em-<BR>bracing, an embrace; union, junction, contact, prox-<BR>imity; association, society, presence; a figure of<BR>rhetoric, connection of words so as to admit of a<BR>double meaning, verbal equivocation, paronomasia,<BR>pun, irony, implied meaning.<BR>—श्लेष-भित्तिक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, resting on or adhering to a wall, (said to mean<BR>simply ‘resting on.’)<BR>—श्लेषार्थ (˚ष-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a meaning other than the literal one, a second<BR>sense hidden in the obvious one, implied meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषण
श्लेषण, अम्, n. the act of adhering, embracing,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषणीय
श्लेषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be embraced, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषिन्
श्लेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, adhering, clinging to, embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मक|श्लेष्मकः
श्लेष्मक, अस्, m. phlegm, the watery or phleg-<BR>matic humor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मण|श्लेष्मणः
श्लेष्मण, अस्, आ, अम्, phlegmatic; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of plant (= तर्पणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मन्
श्लेष्मन्, आ, m. phlegm, rheum, the phlegmatic<BR>humor, (one of the three humors of the body; see<BR>धातु.)<BR>—श्लेष्म-घ्न, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, removing<BR>phlegm; (आ), f. Arabian jasmine; a kind of tree<BR>(= केतक); (ई), f. Arabian jasmine; hogweed;<BR>another plant (= ज्योतिष्मती); the three spices (=<BR>त्रि-कटु).<BR>—श्लेष्म-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced or<BR>proceeding from phlegm.<BR>—श्लेष्म-धातु, उस्, m.<BR>the phlegmatic humor.<BR>—श्लेष्म-ह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>removing phlegm; (अस्), m. a medicinal plant (=<BR>कट्-फल).<BR>—श्लेष्मातिसार (˚म-अत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>dysentery or diarrhœa produced by vitiated phlegm.<BR>—श्लेष्मान्तक (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘destroying<BR>phlegm,’ a kind of plant (= पिच्छिल, बहु-वार).<BR>—श्लेष्माश्रु (˚म-अश्˚), उ, n. a tear consisting<BR>of phlegmatic humor.<BR>—श्लेष्मौजस् (˚म-ओज्˚),<BR>अस्, n. the phlegmatic humor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मल|श्लेष्मलः
श्लेष्मल, अस्, आ, अम्, phlegmatic, abounding or<BR>affected with phlegm, &c.; (अस्), m. the plant Cordia<BR>Myxa or Latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मात|श्लेष्मातः
श्लेष्मात, अस्, m. a kind of tree, = श्लेष्मातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मातक|श्लेष्मातकः
श्लेष्मातक, अस्, m. the tree Cordia Myxa.<BR>—श्ले-<BR>ष्मातक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of Cordia Myxa.<BR>—श्लेष्मातक-वन, अम्, n. ‘forest of Śleṣmā-<BR>taka trees,’ N. of a forest about Go-karṇa (where<BR>Śiva is said to have been concealed in the form of a<BR>stag).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लैष्मिक
श्लैष्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>phlegm, phlegmatic; producing phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपद|श्लीपदं
श्लीपद श्लीपद, अम्, n. (thought by some<BR>to be fr. rt. 2. श्लिष् + पद), morbid enlargement<BR>of the leg, swelled leg, elephantiasis.<BR>—श्लीपद-प्र-<BR>भव, अस्, m. ‘source of elephantiasis,’ the Mango<BR>tree.<BR>—श्लीपदापह (˚द-अप्˚), अस्, m. ‘removing or<BR>curing elephantiasis,’ a kind of tree (= पुत्र-जीव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदिन्
श्लीपदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a swelled leg, club-<BR>footed; (ई), m. a club-footed man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लील|श्लीलः
श्लील श्लील, अस्, आ, अम् (for श्रील), prosperous,<BR>fortunate, affluent, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लु
श्लु श्लु, one of the three technical terms for<BR>grammatical elision classed with लुक्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक्
श्लोक् श्लोक् (probably rather a Nom. fr.<BR>श्लोक below), cl. 1. A. श्लोकते, श्लोकि-<BR>तुम्, to versify, compose or make verses, hymn or<BR>praise in verse; to be put together or composed; to<BR>acquire; to relinquish, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक|श्लोकः
श्लोक, अस्, m. (probably connected with rt. 1.<BR>श्रु; according to Rāmāyaṇa I. 2, 33. fr. शोक,<BR>‘sorrow,’ the first Śloka having resulted from the<BR>involuntary expression of Vālmīki's grief at be-<BR>holding a bird killed by a fowler), praising or<BR>hymning in verse, a hymn of praise; an object of<BR>praise; celebrity, renown, fame, reputation; a par-<BR>ticular kind of common epic metre (also called Anu-<BR>ṣṭubh, consisting of four Pādas or quarter verses of<BR>eight syllables each, or two lines of sixteen syllables<BR>each; the following is the usual scheme applicable<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">Page1030-a+ 74</a>]<BR>to both lines ....˘˘˘. | ....˘¯˘. , the<BR>mark. denoting either long or short, and the sixth<BR>syllable being either short or long, but if short, then<BR>requiring the seventh to be short also, and if long,<BR>then long); any verse or stanza; a proverb, saying;<BR>= वाच् (Naigh. I. 11).<BR>—श्लोक-ता, f. or श्लोक-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. versification; celebrity in verse.<BR>—श्लोक-<BR>द्वय, अम्, n. a couple of Ślokas, two verses.<BR>—श्लोक-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, composed in Ślokas.<BR>—श्लोक-मात्र, अम्, n. a single Śloka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकय
श्लोकय, Nom. P. श्लोकयति, -यितुम्, to celebrate<BR>in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकिन्
श्लोकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having hymns of praise,<BR>receiving praise, praised, lauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक्य
श्लोक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in hymns of praise, be-<BR>longing to Ślokas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोण्
श्लोण् श्लोण् (also written श्रोण्), cl. 1. P.<BR>श्लोणति, श्लोणितुम्, to accumulate, col-<BR>lect, assemble, heap together: Caus. श्लोणयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अशुश्लोणत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोण|श्लोणः
श्लोण श्लोण, अस्, m. (= श्रोण; cf. अ-श्लोण),<BR>a lame man, cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वघ्निन्
श्वघ्निन् श्वघ्निन्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वङ्क्|श्वंक्
श्वङ्क् श्वङ्क् (also written स्वङ्क्), cl. 1.<BR>A. श्वङ्कते, शश्वङ्के, श्वङ्कितुम्, to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वङ्ग्
श्वङ्ग् श्वङ्ग् (also written श्रङ्ग्, स्वङ्ग्,<BR>&c.; cf. rt. श्वङ्क्), cl. 1. P. श्वङ्गति,<BR>श्वङ्गितुम्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वच्
श्वच् श्वच् or श्वञ्च् (= rts. शञ्च्, श्वज्),<BR>cl. 1. A. श्वचते, श्वञ्चते, &c., (Ved.<BR>form श्वञ्चयः, Ṛg-veda X. 138, 2; शश्वचै,<BR>see s. v.), to go, move; to gape, open, be opened,<BR>be split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वज्
श्वज् श्वज् or श्वञ्ज् (= rts. श्वच्, शञ्च्), cl. 1.<BR>A. श्वजते, श्वञ्जते, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वञ्च्|श्वंच्
श्वञ्च् श्वञ्च्. See above under rt. श्वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वठ्
श्वठ् 1. श्वठ् (= rt. 2. शठ्), cl. 10. P.<BR>श्वठयति, -यितुम्, to speak ill; (ac-<BR>cording to some) to speak well or correctly; to be<BR>accurate or true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वठ्
श्वठ् 2. श्वठ् or श्वण्ठ् (= rts. 3. शठ्,<BR>स्वठ्, सठ्), cl. 10. P. श्वाठयति, श्वण्-<BR>ठयति, &c., -यितुम्, to finish, accomplish, adorn;<BR>to leave unfinished or unornamented; to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वन्
श्वन् श्वन्, आ, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>158. fr. rt. श्वि, perhaps fr. a participial base श्वन्त्;<BR>Nom. sing. du. pl. श्वा, श्वानौ, श्वानस्; Acc. श्वा-<BR>नम्, श्वानौ, शुनस्; Inst. शुना, श्वभ्याम्, &c.,<BR>Gram. 155. a), a dog, hound, cur; (शुनी), f. a female<BR>dog, bitch. श्वन् becomes श्वा for श्व in some com-<BR>pounds, see below; [cf. Zend śpâ; Gr. κύ-ων,<BR>κυνός (= शुनस्), ἁλ-κυών; Lat. can-i-s (for cvan-<BR>i-s), catulus; Goth. hun-d-s; Lith. nom. szu§,<BR>gen. szuns; Hib. nom. cu, gen. and pl. coin; Russ.<BR>sobaka (for shaka); Pers. sag.]<BR>—श्व-किष्किन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, Ved. (according to some) having the tail of<BR>a dog, (Sāy. connects किष्किन् with किष्कु, ‘a staff,<BR>thunderbolt,’ Atharva-veda VIII. 6, 6.)<BR>—श्व-क्री-<BR>डिन्, ई, m. one who sports with dogs, a dog-feeder<BR>or trainer, a breeder of sporting dogs.<BR>—श्व-गण,<BR>अस्, m. a pack or collection of dogs.<BR>—श्वगणिक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘one who has to do with packs of dogs,’ a<BR>hunter; (अस्, ई), m. f. a dog-feeder; one who is drawn<BR>by dogs.<BR>—श्व-गणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having packs of<BR>hounds.<BR>—श्व-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘dog-seizure,’ epithet<BR>of a particular disease or the deity presiding over<BR>it.<BR>—श्व-घ्नी, see under श्व-हन्.<BR>—श्व-चाण्-<BR>डाल, अम्, n. a dog and an outcast.<BR>—श्व-चिल्ली, f.<BR>a kind of pot-herb (= शुनक-चिल्ली).<BR>—श्व-जा-<BR>घनी, f. a dog's thigh, the haunch of a dog, (Manu<BR>X. 108.)<BR>—श्व-दंष्ट्रक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>plant (= गो-क्षुर).<BR>—श्व-दंष्ट्रा, f. a dog's<BR>tooth; a kind of plant (= गो-क्षुर).<BR>—श्व-धूर्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-b" target="_blank">Page1030-b+ 80</a>]<BR>त, अस्, m. ‘dog-rogue,’ a jackal.<BR>—श्व-नर, अस्,<BR>m. a dog-like fellow, low fellow, currish or snappish<BR>fellow.<BR>—श्व-निश, अम्, आ, n. f. ‘dog-night,’ a night<BR>on which dogs bark and howl.<BR>—श्व-पच्, क्, or श्व-<BR>पच, अस्, आ, m. f. ‘dog-cooking,’ a man or woman<BR>of a low and degraded caste, (see श्व-पाक); a<BR>public executioner; a dog-feeder, dog-keeper; (ई), f.<BR>a form of one of the Śaktis of Śiva.<BR>—श्व-पद,<BR>अम्, n. a dog's foot; a mark like a dog's foot to be<BR>branded on the forehead of a thief.<BR>—श्व-पाक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘dog-cooking,’ a man of a degraded and outcast<BR>tribe (described as son of an Ugra woman by a<BR>Kṣatriya, and classed with the Caṇḍāla, q. v.; he<BR>is required to live outside towns, to eat his food in<BR>broken vessels, to wear the clothes of the dead, and<BR>to be excluded from all intercourse with other tribes;<BR>he can possess no other property than asses and dogs,<BR>and his only office is to act as public executioner or<BR>to carry out the bodies of those who die without<BR>kindred); (ई), f. a woman of the above low or out-<BR>cast tribe.<BR>—श्व-फल, अम्, n. the lime or common<BR>citron.<BR>—श्व-फल्क, अस्, m., N. of the son of<BR>Pṛśni (or according to others of Vṛṣṇi; he was<BR>husband of Gāndinī, by whom he had a son named<BR>Akrūra).<BR>—श्व-भीरु, उस्, m. ‘dog-fearing,’ a jackal.<BR>—श्व-भोजन, अस्, m. ‘having dogs for food,’ N.<BR>of a Naraka.<BR>—श्व-यातु, उस्, m., Ved. a demon in<BR>the shape of a dog.<BR>—श्व-यूथ्य, अम्, n. a number or<BR>pack of dogs.<BR>—श्व-रूप-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wearing<BR>or having the form of a dog.<BR>—१. श्व-वत्, आन्, m.<BR>possessing or keeping a dog, a dog-feeder, dog-<BR>trainer.<BR>—२. श्व-वत्, ind. like a dog, cur-like.<BR>—श्व-वृत्ति, इस्, f. the life of a dog; condition of<BR>a dog; service, servitude (which a Brāhman ought<BR>not to engage in).<BR>—श्व-व्याघ्र, अस्, m. a beast<BR>of prey, a tiger; the hunting leopard or Chīta.<BR>—श्व-सुत, अस्, m. the plant Conyza Aspera.<BR>—श्व-<BR>स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, touched by a dog, defiled.<BR>—श्व-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, killed by a dog, killed by<BR>dogs.<BR>—श्व-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, Ved. one who kills<BR>with dogs; (आ), m. a hunter; (घ्नी), f. the wife<BR>of a hunter.<BR>—श्वा-कर्ण, अस्, m. a dog's ear.<BR>—श्वा-दन्त, अस्, m. (श्वा for श्व), a dog's tooth.<BR>—श्वा-पद, अस्, m. a beast of prey, wild beast; a<BR>tiger; (अस्, ई, अम्), relating or belonging to a wild<BR>beast, ferocious, savage, (in this sense properly an<BR>adj. fr. श्वा-पद, and therefore to be written<BR>without a hyphen.)<BR>—श्वापद-सेवित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>frequented or infested by wild beasts.<BR>—श्वापदा-<BR>चरित (˚द-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, overrun or infested by<BR>wild beasts.<BR>—श्वापदानुसरण (˚द-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the pursuit or chase after a wild animal.<BR>—श्वा-<BR>पुच्छ, अस्, अम्, m. n. a dog's tail.<BR>—श्वाविच्-<BR>छरण, अम्, n. (i. e. श्वा-विध्, see below, + शर-<BR>ण), the lair or resting-place of a porcupine, (a<BR>porcupine's hole has always two or more entrances.)<BR>—श्वा-विध्, त्, m. (श्वा for श्व), a porcupine, hedge-<BR>hog.<BR>—श्वाश्व (श्व-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘having a dog<BR>for a horse,’ epithet of Bhairava (or Śiva in a ter-<BR>rific form, sometimes represented as mounted on<BR>a dog).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्व|श्वः
श्व at the end of comps. = श्वन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वघ्निन्
श्वघ्निन्, ई, m. (according to some श्व is for<BR>स्व, and the word is thought to mean ‘one who<BR>destroys his own,’ others connect it with श्व-हन्),<BR>Ved. a gamester, (Sāy. = देवन-शील.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वागणिक|श्वागणिकः
श्वागणिक, अस्, m. (fr. श्व-गण), one who has<BR>to do with packs of dogs, a hunter; (अस्, ई), m. f.<BR>one who lives by feeding or keeping dogs, a dog-<BR>keeper; one who is drawn by dogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वान|श्वानः
श्वान, अस्, m. a dog; the wind, (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 161, 13. श्वानम् = अन्तरिक्षे<BR>श्वसन्तं वायुम्); (ई), f. a female dog, bitch.<BR>—श्वान-चिल्लिका, f. a kind of pot-herb.<BR>—श्वान-<BR>निद्रा, f. a dog's sleep; light slumber.<BR>—श्वान-<BR>वैखरी, f. ‘dog's speech,’ a term for angry snarling<BR>on trifling occasions.<BR>—श्वानोच्छिष्ट (˚न-उच्˚),<BR>अम्, n. anything left by a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र्
श्वभ्र् श्वभ्र् [cf. rt. श्वर्त्], cl. 10. P. श्व-<BR>भ्रयति, -यितुम्, to go, move; to live<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">Page1030-c+ 75</a>]<BR>in misery (in a hole?); to break, pierce, bore, make<BR>a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र|श्वभ्रं
श्वभ्र, अम्, n. a hole, gap, chasm; a den.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयथु|श्वयथुः
श्वयथु श्वयथु, श्वयीचि. See under rt.<BR>श्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वर्त्|श्वर्त्त्
श्वर्त् श्वर्त् (also written स्वर्त्; cf. rt.<BR>श्वभ्र्), cl. 10. P. श्वर्तयति, &c., -यि-<BR>तुम्, to go, move; to live in misery or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्
श्वल् श्वल् or श्वल्ल्, cl. 1. P. श्वलति or<BR>श्वल्लति, शश्वाल or शश्वल्ल, श्वलितुम्<BR>or श्वल्लितुम्, to go quickly, run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्क्
श्वल्क् श्वल्क् [cf. rt. शुल्क्], cl. 10. P. श्वल्-<BR>कयति, -यितुम्, to tell, narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्ल्
श्वल्ल् श्वल्ल् = rt. श्वल् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर|श्वशुरः
श्वशुर श्वशुर, अस्, m. (perhaps for original<BR>स्व-शुर, see शुर; in Uṇādi-s. I. 45. said to be<BR>fr. rt. 1. अश् with शु for आशु prefixed), a father-in-<BR>law, a wife's or husband's father; one to be treated<BR>as a father-in-law, a venerable man; a proper N.;<BR>(औ), m. du. a father and mother-in-law; [cf. Zend<BR>qaśura; Gr. ἑκυρό-ς for σϝεκυρό-ς; Lat. socer<BR>for svecer; Goth. svaihra; Old Germ. svehur;<BR>Angl. Sax. sweger, sweor; Slav. svekru; Lith.<BR>szeszura-s; Cambro-Brit. cwegrwn.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुरक|श्वशुरकः
श्वशुरक, अस्, m. a father-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर्य|श्वशुर्यः|श्वशुर्य्य|श्वशुर्य्यः
श्वशुर्य, अस्, m. a brother-in-law, wife's brother,<BR>husband's brother; a husband's younger brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वश्रू
श्वश्रू, ऊस्, f. a mother-in-law; [cf. Gr. ἔκυρα;<BR>Lat. socrus; Goth. svaihrô; Old Germ. suigar;<BR>Cambro-Brit. çwegyr; Slav. svekruvi or svekry;<BR>perhaps Lith. u§szwe†.]<BR>—श्वश्रू-श्वशुर, औ, m.<BR>du. mother and father-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
श्वस् 1. श्वस्, cl. 2. P. श्वसिति, (also ap-<BR>parently cl. 1. P. A. श्वसति, -ते, in certain<BR>forms and according to a various reading in Naigh.<BR>II. 19), Impf. अश्वसीत् or अश्वसत् (Pāṇ. VII. 3, 98,<BR>99, cf. rt. 1. रुद्), Pot. श्वसेत् (cl. 1), Impv. श्व-<BR>सितु (or श्वसतु, 2nd pl. A. श्वसध्वम्), श-<BR>श्वास, श्वसिष्यति, अश्वसीत्, श्वसितुम्, to breathe,<BR>respire, draw breath, live, pant, puff, sigh; to hiss,<BR>snort; to strike, kill, (enumerated among the वध-<BR>कर्माणः in Naigh. II. 19): Caus. श्वासयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अशिश्वसत्, to cause to breathe easily,<BR>to refresh: Desid. शिश्वसिषति: Intens. शाश्वस्यते,<BR>शाश्वस्ति, to breathe frequently, pant; [cf. Lat. queri,<BR>ques-tus; Angl. Sax. hweosan, perhaps hysian,<BR>hyst, gist.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसत्
श्वसत्, अन्, अती (ep. also अन्ती), अत्, breathing,<BR>sighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसथ
श्वसथ, Ved. breathing; hissing; snorting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसन|श्वसनं|श्वसनः
श्वसन, अस्, m. air, wind; epithet of a demon<BR>of drought vanquished by Indra [cf. शुष्ण]; the<BR>thorny plant Vangueria Spinosa; (अम्), n. breathing,<BR>respiration, breath; sighing.<BR>—श्वसनासन (˚न-<BR>अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘air-eater, breath-eater,’ a snake, serpent.<BR>—श्वसनेश्वर (˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘breath-lord,’<BR>the tree Pentaptera Arjuna.<BR>—श्वसनोत्सुक (˚न-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘eager for air’ or ‘fond of hissing,’ a<BR>snake.<BR>—श्वसनोर्मि (˚न-ऊर्˚), इस्, m. f. a wave<BR>or gust of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसमान
श्वसमान, अस्, आ, अम्, breathing; panting,<BR>snorting, hissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसित|श्वसितं
श्वसित, अस्, आ, अम्, breathed, sighed; breathing,<BR>sighing; (अम्), n. breathing, breath, respiration,<BR>sighing, a sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसीवत्|श्वसीवन्त्
श्वसी-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of breath,<BR>vivifying, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 140, 10.<BR>श्वसीवान् = श्वसन-वान् ज्वालाभिश् चेष्टा-वान्<BR>प्राणन-वान् वा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसुन|श्वसुनः
श्वसुन, अस्, m. a kind of plant (= क्षत-<BR>घ्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वास|श्वासः
श्वास, अस्, m. breathing, breath, inspiration, re-<BR>spiration; sighing, a sigh; air, wind; affection of<BR>the breath, hard breathing, asthma.<BR>—श्वास-कास,<BR>अस्, m. ‘breath-cough,’ asthma.<BR>—श्वास-कुठार, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">Page1031-a+ 75</a>]<BR>m. a particular drug used as a remedy for asthma.<BR>—श्वास-ता, f. breathing, respiration, aspiration.<BR>—श्वास-प्रश्वास-धारण, अम्, n. suppression or<BR>suspension of inspiration and expiration (= प्राणा-<BR>याम, q. v.).<BR>—श्वास-रोध, अस्, m. an obstruction<BR>of the breath.<BR>—श्वास-हिक्का, f. a kind of hiccough.<BR>—श्वास-हेति, इस्, f. ‘cure for hard breathing,’ sleepi-<BR>ness, sleep.<BR>—श्वासारि (˚स-अरि), इस्, m. ‘breath-<BR>enemy,’ a kind of plant (= पुष्कर-मूल).<BR>—श्वा-<BR>सोच्छ्वास (˚स-उच्˚), औ, m. du. inspiration and ex-<BR>piration, respiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासित
श्वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to breathe, refreshed,<BR>invigorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासिन्
श्वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, breathing, respiring; (ई), m.<BR>air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
श्वस् 2. श्वस्, ind. (according to some con-<BR>nected with a lost rt. श्वि in श्वित्, ‘to be white,’<BR>and originally denoting ‘the morrow's dawn’), to-<BR>morrow; future, (at the beginning of a comp.);<BR>future happiness or fortune, (apparently used in this<BR>sense at the beginning of certain comps.); a particle<BR>implying auspiciousness; [cf. Lat. cras.]<BR>—श्वः-<BR>श्रेयस, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘happy in the future,’ happy,<BR>prosperous; (अम्), n. happiness, prosperity; Brahma,<BR>the Supreme Spirit; (अम्), ind. happy, well, right.<BR>—श्वः-सुत्या, f., Ved. to-morrow's preparation of<BR>the Soma.<BR>—श्वो-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being to-morrow;<BR>(ए), ind. on its being to-morrow.<BR>—श्वो-वसीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘happy for all future time,’ auspicious, fortunate;<BR>(अम्), n. happiness.<BR>—श्वो-वसीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्,<BR>fortunate, prosperous, auspicious.<BR>—श्वो-वसीयस,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fortunate, auspicious; (अम्), n. auspicious-<BR>ness, good fortune.<BR>—श्वो-वस्यस, अम्, n., Ved.,<BR>N. of Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्तन|श्वस्तनं
श्वस्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the morrow,<BR>what will be to-morrow, future; (अम्), n. the future<BR>[cf. Lat. crastinus]; (ई), f., scil. विभक्ति, a gram-<BR>matical term for the personal terminations of the first<BR>future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्त्य|श्वस्त्यं
श्वस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the morrow,<BR>what will be to-morrow, future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वागणिक|श्वागणिकः
श्वागणिक श्वागणिक. See p. 1030, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वात्र
श्वात्र 1. श्वात्र, अस्, आ, अम् (probably fr. rt.<BR>श्वि; cf. शवस्, शिव), Ved. increasing, powerful,<BR>strong, flourishing, blooming (according to some);<BR>quick, swift, (Sāy. = क्षिप्र-धर्मक, Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 46, 7); (अम्), ind. quickly, (Sāy. = क्षिप्रम्);<BR>(अम्), n. prosperity, riches, wealth.<BR>—श्वात्र-भाज्, क्,<BR>क्, क्, Ved. wealth-associated, endowed with riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वात्र
2. श्वात्र, Nom. P. श्वात्रति, &c., Ved. to go,<BR>hasten, (enumerated among the गति-कर्माणः in<BR>Naigh. II. 14.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वात्र्य
श्वात्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing prosperity or<BR>happiness, (Sāy. = सुखावह); going quickly, (Sāy.<BR>= क्षिप्र-गमनार्ह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वान|श्वानः
श्वान श्वान, &c. See p. 1030, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वान्त
श्वान्त श्वान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wearied;<BR>placid, (Sāy. = श्रान्त or शान्त, Ṛg-veda I. 145,<BR>4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वापद|श्वापदः
श्वापद श्वा-पद, श्वा-विध्, &c. See under<BR>श्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाशुरि
श्वाशुरि श्वाशुरि, इस्, m. (fr. श्वशुर), a<BR>patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वि
श्वि श्वि (this rt. assumes the form शु,<BR>q. v., in some of its tenses and derivatives;<BR>cf. rt. शव्), cl. 1. P. श्वयति, शुशाव or शिश्वाय<BR>(2nd sing. शुशविथ or शिश्वयिथ, 3rd du. शुशु-<BR>वतुस् or शिश्वियतुस्), श्वयिष्यति, अश्वयीत् or<BR>अश्वत् or अशिश्वियत्, Prec. शूयात्, श्वयितुम्, to<BR>swell, increase, grow; to thrive; to appear (Ved.,<BR>see वि-श्वि, referred by some to rt. श्वित्); to go, ap-<BR>proach: Pass. शूयते, Aor. अश्वायि: Caus. श्वाय-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अशूशवत् or अशिश्वयत्, (accord-<BR>ing to others also अशीशवत्): Desid. of Caus. शुशा-<BR>वयिषति or शिश्वाययिषति, to cause to swell or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">Page1031-b+ 79</a>]<BR>grow or be prosperous: Desid. शिश्वयिषति: Intens.<BR>शेश्वीयते, शोशूयते, शेश्वयीति, शेश्वेति, to swell<BR>much; [cf. Gr. κυ-έ-ω, κύ-ος, κῦ-μα, κύ-η-μα,<BR>κύ-αρ, κύ-τ-ος, κοῖ-λο-ς, κοιλ-ία, καυλό-ς, κύ-λο-ν,<BR>ἐγ-κισσάω, κίσσα, κύαμος, κύαθος, κῶνος, κηκίς,<BR>κίκυς, (probably also) κίων, κίω, κινέω, perhaps also<BR>κό-μη (for κύ-μη): Lat. in-ci-ens, cu-mu-lu-s,<BR>cavu-s, cau-li-s, cau-lœ, cœlu-m, ciliu-m, super-<BR>cili-um, cuneus, crescere; coma: Goth. us-hul-<BR>on, hul-undi: Old Germ. hol, (according to some)<BR>wī-t, ‘wide’ (= श्वित): Angl. Sax. hol: Hib. cin-<BR>neas, cinneachdin, ‘growth, increase.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूति|शूतिः
शूति, इस्, f. swelling, increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून|शूनः
शून, अस्, आ, अम्, swollen, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूयमन
शूयमन, अस्, आ, अम्, being swollen, swelling,<BR>enlarging, expanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्वीयमान
शेश्वीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. swelling or in-<BR>creasing excessively, enlarging, expanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वय|श्वयः
श्वय, अस्, m. swelling, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयथु|श्वयथुः
श्वयथु, उस्, m. swelling, intumescence.<BR>—श्वय-<BR>थु-चिकित्सा, f. the cure or treatment of swellings, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयन|श्वयनं
श्वयन, अम्, n. swelling, intumescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयित्वा
श्वयित्वा, ind. having swelled or increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयीचि|श्वयीचिः
श्वयीचि, इस्, f. sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्विक्न
श्विक्न श्विक्न, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race; [cf.<BR>श्वैक्न.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्
श्वित् श्वित् (perhaps a kind of Nom.<BR>based on a lost rt. श्वि, cf. Zend śpi-<BR>तम, &c.), cl. 1. A. श्वेतते (Ved. also P. -ति),<BR>शिश्विते, श्वेतिष्यते, अश्वेतिष्ट, अश्वितत्, श्वेतितुम्,<BR>to be or become white, (according to Vopa-deva<BR>XXI. 15. श्वेतयति = श्वेताश्वम् आचष्टे); [cf.<BR>Lith. swe†ciu for swetiu, ‘I shine;’ Inf. swe†sti for<BR>swe†t-ti, (perhaps also) swe†ta-s, ‘the world;’ kaiciu<BR>for kaitiu, kaitinu, ‘I make hot;’ kais-tu for<BR>kait-tu, ‘I become warm;’ kaitau: Slav. svit-a-ti,<BR>‘to become light;’ swjet, ‘light, the world.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित
श्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, white; (अम्), n. whiteness<BR>(according to Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वितान
श्वितान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being white, white-<BR>coloured, (Sāy. = श्वेतमान, श्वेत-वर्ण, Ṛg-<BR>veda VI. 6, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्विति|श्वितिः
श्विति, whiteness, a white colour (according to<BR>Sāy.).<BR>—श्वित्य्-अञ्च्, अङ्, -तीची, अक्, Ved. going to<BR>whiteness, becoming white, white-coloured, fair-com-<BR>plexioned, white, (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 83, 8.<BR>श्वित्यञ्चः = श्वितं श्वैत्यं नैर्मल्यम् अञ्-<BR>चन्तो गच्छन्तः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्त
श्वित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, see Pāṇ. VII. 2, 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्न
श्वित्न, white (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I.<BR>100, 18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्न्य
श्वित्न्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. white, white-coloured,<BR>fair-complexioned (said of the winds or Maruts ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 100, 18; but accord-<BR>ing to some more probably referring to the fair-<BR>coloured worshippers of Indra as opposed to the<BR>darker aborigines of India).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्य
श्वित्य, अस्, आ, अम्, white, white-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्र|श्वित्रं
श्वित्र, अम्, n. morbid whiteness of the skin,<BR>white leprosy, vitiligo; = अन्तरिक्ष (Ved., cf.<BR>श्वैत्रेय); (आ), f. a proper N.<BR>—श्वित्र-घ्नी, f.<BR>‘removing whiteness of the skin,’ the plant Tragia<BR>Involucrata (= पीत-पर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्रिन्
श्वित्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, affected with whiteness of the<BR>skin or leprosy, leprous; (ई), m. a leper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्र्य
श्वित्र्य, अस्, m., Ved. a son of Śvitrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेत|श्वेतं|श्वेतः
श्वेत, अस्, आ or श्वेनी, अम्, white, dressed in<BR>white; (अस्), m. white (the colour); the planet Venus<BR>or its regent Śukra; the sixth range of mountains<BR>dividing the known continent, the white mountains<BR>separating the Varṣas of Hiraṇmaya and Ramyaka;<BR>one of the minor Dvīpas or divisions of the world,<BR>(see श्वेत-द्वीप); a white cloud; cumin seed; a<BR>conch-shell; N. of a particular Avatāra of Śiva; of<BR>a manifestation of Viṣṇu in his Varāha incarnation<BR>(worshipped in a particular part of India); N. of one<BR>of Śiva's pupils; (अस्, आ), m. f. a small white shell,<BR>cowri; (आ), f. one of the tongues of Fire; a kind of<BR>grass, Andropogon Aciculatum; a kind of plant (=<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-c" target="_blank">Page1031-c+ 81</a>]<BR>काष्ठ-पाटला); Aconitum Ferox; various other<BR>plants (= अपराजिता; = श्वेत-वृहती; = श्वेत-<BR>कण्टकारी; = पाषाण-भेदिन्; = शिला-वल्कला;<BR>= छूरिका-पत्त्री); hogweed; white Dūrvā grass;<BR>bamboo-manna; crystal; clayed or candied sugar;<BR>a mystical term for the letter स्; (अम्), n. silver;<BR>(श्वेत वैदार्व or वैदार्व्य or वैदर्व्य is<BR>according to some ‘a serpent demon,’ others give<BR>श्वैत-वैदारव as signifying ‘a particular deity<BR>connected with the sun’); [cf. Goth. hveit-s, ‘white;’<BR>(perhaps) hvaitei, ‘wheat:’ Old Germ. huiz, wīz:<BR>Old Sax., Angl. Sax., Old Norse hvīt: Lith.<BR>kwe†ty-s, ‘wheat.’]<BR>—श्वेत-कण्टकारी, f. a species<BR>of plant (= प्रियङ्-करी).<BR>—श्वेत-कन्दा, f. ‘hav-<BR>ing a white bulb,’ the plant Aconitum Ferox.<BR>—श्वेत-<BR>कमल, अम्, n. a white lotus.<BR>—श्वेत-काकीय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, belonging or relating to a white crow.<BR>—श्वेत-किणिही, f. a species of Kiṇihī with white<BR>blossoms.<BR>—श्वेत-कुञ्जर, अस्, m. ‘white elephant,’<BR>Indra's elephant Airāvata.<BR>—श्वेत-कुश, अस्, m.<BR>white Kuśa grass (= पुण्य-तृण).<BR>—श्वेत-कुष्-<BR>ठ, अम्, n. white leprosy.<BR>—श्वेत-केतु, उस्, m. a<BR>Bauddha or Jaina saint; epithet of the descending<BR>node; N. of a Brāhman; of a sage (son of Uddā-<BR>laka).<BR>—श्वेत-केश, अस्, m. white hair; a variety of<BR>the Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR>—श्वेत-कोल, अस्, m.<BR>‘having a white or glittering breast,’ the Śaphara<BR>fish.<BR>—श्वेत-खदिर, अस्, m. a white variety of the<BR>Khadira tree.<BR>—श्वेत-गङ्गा, f. ‘the white Ganges,’<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—श्वेत-गज, अस्, m. a white elephant;<BR>the elephant of Indra.<BR>—श्वेत-गरुत्, त्, or श्वेत-ग-<BR>रुत, अस्, m. ‘white-winged,’ a goose.<BR>—श्वेत-गुञ्जा, f.<BR>a kind of plant (= भिरिण्टिका).<BR>—श्वेत-घोषा,<BR>f. a white Ghoṣā plant.<BR>—श्वेत-चन्दन, अम्,<BR>n. white sandal.<BR>—श्वेत-चिल्लिका or श्वेत-चिल्ली, f.<BR>a kind of pot-herb.<BR>—श्वेत-च्छत्त्र, अम्, n. a<BR>white umbrella; (अस्, आ, अम्), having a white um-<BR>brella.<BR>—श्वेत-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘white-winged’ or<BR>‘white-leaved,’ a goose; a kind of basil, Ocymum<BR>Album.<BR>—श्वेत-जीरक, अस्, m. white cumin.<BR>—श्वे-<BR>त-टङ्कक or -टङ्कण, अम्, n. white or refined<BR>borax.<BR>—श्वेत-ता, f. whiteness.<BR>—श्वेत-दूर्वा, f.<BR>white Dūrvā grass.<BR>—श्वेत-द्विप, अस्, m. a white<BR>elephant; Indra's elephant.<BR>—श्वेत-द्वीप, अस्, m.<BR>‘the white island,’ N. of one of the eighteen minor<BR>Dvīpas or divisions of the known continent, (also<BR>termed Candra-dvīpa, see चन्द्र; identified by<BR>some with Vaikuṇṭha, q. v., and by others supposed<BR>to be Britain); N. of a place near Kāśi.<BR>—श्वेत-<BR>धातु, उस्, m. a white mineral; chalk; the milk-<BR>stone, opal or chalcedony.<BR>—श्वेत-धामन्, आ, m.<BR>‘having white lustre,’ the moon; camphor; cuttle-<BR>fish bone.<BR>—श्वेत-नील, अस्, आ, अम्, white and black,<BR>(अस्), m. a cloud.<BR>—श्वेत-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a white<BR>feather; (अस्), m. ‘white-feathered,’ a goose.<BR>—श्वे-<BR>तपत्त्र-रथ, अस्, m. ‘whose vehicle is a goose,’<BR>epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—श्वेत-पद्म, अम्, n. the<BR>white lotus.<BR>—श्वेत-पर्णा, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>वारि-पर्णी).<BR>—श्वेत-पर्णास, अस्, m. white basil.<BR>—श्वेत-पर्वत, अस्, m. ‘white-mountain,’ N. of<BR>a mountain.<BR>—श्वेत-पाटला, f. the white trumpet-<BR>flower, Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—श्वेत-पिङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>‘white and tawny,’ a lion.<BR>—श्वेत-पिङ्गल, अस्, m.<BR>‘white and tawny,’ a lion; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—श्वेत-<BR>पिङ्गलक, अस्, m. a lion.<BR>—श्वेत-पिण्डीतक, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of plant (= महा-पिण्डीतरु).<BR>—श्वेत-<BR>पुनर्नवा, f. the white-flowered hogweed.<BR>—श्वेत-<BR>पुष्प, अम्, n. a white flower; (अस्), m. ‘having<BR>white flowers,’ the plant Vitex Trifolia, = सिन्धु-<BR>वार; (आ), f. a Ghoṣā with white flowers; another<BR>plant (= नाग-दन्ती); colocynth.<BR>—श्वेत-पुष्-<BR>पक, अस्, इका, अम्, having white flowers; (अस्), m.<BR>the plant Nerium Odorum (the white variety);<BR>(इका), f. a kind of plant (= पुत्र-दात्री); another<BR>plant (= महा-शणपुष्पिका).<BR>—श्वेत-प्रसू-<BR>नक, अस्, आ, अम्, having white flowers; (अस्), m.<BR>the tree Tapia Cratæva.<BR>—श्वेत-बला, f. the white<BR>Balā, a kind of plant.<BR>—श्वेत-भण्डा, f. the plant<BR>Clitoria Ternatea.<BR>—श्वेत-भिक्षु, उस्, m. a kind of<BR>mendicant.<BR>—श्वेत-मन्दारक, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of tree (= पृथ्वी-कुरवक).<BR>—श्वेत-मरिच,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">Page1032-a+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, n. white pepper; the seed of the Hyperanthera<BR>Moriṅga.<BR>—श्वेत-माधव-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—श्वेत-माल, अस्, m. ‘having white wreaths,’<BR>a cloud; smoke.<BR>—श्वेत-यावरी, f., Ved. ‘clear-<BR>flowing,’ N. of a river.<BR>—श्वेत-रक्त, अस्, m.<BR>‘whitish-red,’ pale-red, rosy, pink (the colour).<BR>—श्वेत-रञ्जन, अम्, n. ‘white-coloured,’ lead.<BR>—श्वेत-रथ, अस्, m. a white chariot; ‘having a<BR>white car,’ the planet Venus.<BR>—श्वेत-राजी, f. a kind<BR>of creeper (= चचेण्डा).<BR>—श्वेत-रास्ना, f. the white<BR>Rāsnā plant.<BR>—श्वेत-रोचिस्, इस्, m. ‘having white<BR>light,’ the moon.<BR>—श्वेत-रोमन्, अ, n. white hair.<BR>—श्वेत-रोमाङ्क (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a spot of<BR>white hair.<BR>—श्वेत-रोहित, अस्, m. ‘white and red,’<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa; a kind of tree (= लक्ष्मी-<BR>वत्).<BR>—श्वेत-लोध्र, अस्, m. a white Lodhra tree.<BR>—श्वेत-लोहित, अस्, m., N. of a Muni (a pupil of<BR>Śiva).<BR>—श्वेत-वचा, f. white orris root (= अति-<BR>विषा).<BR>—श्वेत-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, white-coloured.<BR>—श्वेत-वल्कल, अस्, m. white bark; ‘white-<BR>barked,’ the glomerous fig-tree, Ficus Glomerata.<BR>—श्वेत-वाजिन्, ई, m. a white horse; ‘having white<BR>horses,’ the moon; epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—श्वेत-वा-<BR>सस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having white clothes; (आस्), m.<BR>‘clad in white,’ an ascetic wearing white garments.<BR>—श्वेत-वाह्, वाट्, श्वेतौही or -वाही, वाट्, borne<BR>on white horses; (ट्), m. epithet of Indra; (-तौही<BR>or -वाही), f. the wife of Indra.<BR>—श्वेत-वाह, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having white horses,’ epithet of Arjuna; of<BR>Indra.<BR>—श्वेत-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘having white<BR>horses,’ epithet of the moon; of Arjuna; N. of a<BR>king, (see भद्राश्व); a marine monster (= म-<BR>कर).<BR>—श्वेत-वाहिन्, ई, m. ‘borne by white horses,’<BR>epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—श्वेत-वुह्ना, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= वन-तिक्ता).<BR>—श्वेत-वृक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>‘white tree,’ the Varuṇa tree.<BR>—श्वेत-वृहती, f. a<BR>kind of white Vārtāki or egg-plant.<BR>—श्वेत-शर-<BR>पुङ्खा, f. a kind of shrub.<BR>—श्वेत-शिंशपा, f.<BR>the white Śiṃśapā tree.<BR>—श्वेत-शिख, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Muni.<BR>—श्वेत-शिग्रु, उस्, m. the white Śigru<BR>tree.<BR>—श्वेत-शुङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having white awns;<BR>(अस्), m. barley.<BR>—श्वेत-शूरण, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>plant (= वन-शूरण).<BR>—श्वेत-शृङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>‘having white awns,’ barley.<BR>—श्वेत-सर्प, अस्,<BR>m. a white snake; the tree Tapia Cratæva.<BR>—श्वेत-<BR>सार, अस्, m. the tree Mimosa Catechu.<BR>—श्वेत-<BR>सुरसा, f. a white variety of the Nyctanthes Arbor<BR>Tristis.<BR>—श्वेत-स्पन्दा, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>अपराजिता).<BR>—श्वेत-हय, अस्, m. a white horse;<BR>the horse of Indra; ‘having white horses,’ epithet<BR>of Arjuna.<BR>—श्वेत-हस्तिन्, ई, m. a white elephant;<BR>Airāvata (the elephant of Indra).<BR>—श्वेता-त्रिवृत्, त्,<BR>f. the white Trivṛt plant.<BR>—श्वेतात्रेय (˚त-आत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—श्वेतानुकाश (˚त-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. possessing a white light; white and<BR>shining.<BR>—श्वेताम्बर (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>white garments,’ an order of ascetics among the<BR>Jainas.<BR>—श्वेताम्लि (˚त-अम्˚), इस्, f. a kind of shrub<BR>(= अम्लिका).<BR>—श्वेतारण्य-तीर्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—श्वेतावर (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>kind of vegetable (= सितावर).<BR>—श्वेताश्वतर<BR>(˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—श्वेताश्वतर-<BR>शाखा, f., N. of a Śākhā of the Yajur-veda.<BR>—श्वे-<BR>ताश्वतर-शाखिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the followers of<BR>the Śvetāśvatara-śākhā.<BR>—श्वेताश्वतरोपनिषद्<BR>(˚र-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—श्वेतास्य<BR>(˚त-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘white-faced,’ N. of a Muni.<BR>—श्वे-<BR>ताह्वा (˚त-आह्˚), f. a kind of plant (= शुक्ल-पाटला).<BR>—श्वेतेक्षु (˚त-इक्˚), उस्, m. ‘white sugar-cane,’<BR>a species of sugar-cane (= पाण्डुरेक्षु).<BR>—श्वेतो-<BR>दर (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, m. a white belly; ‘white-<BR>bellied,’ epithet of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतक|श्वेतकं|श्वेतकः
श्वेतक, अस्, m. a cowri; (अम्), n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतना
श्वेतना, f., Ved. ‘the whitener,’ epithet of Uṣas<BR>or dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतयत्
श्वेतयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, making white, whitening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतित
श्वेतित, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) whitened, see Pāṇ.<BR>VII. 2, 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेती
श्वेती, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतौही
श्वेतौही, f. the wife of Indra; [cf. श्वेत-वाह्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेत्या
श्वेत्या, f., Ved. the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेत्र|श्वेत्रं
श्वेत्र, अम्, n. white leprosy (= श्वित्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैतवैदारव
श्वैत-वैदारव. See under श्वेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्य|श्वैत्यं
श्वैत्य, अम्, n. whiteness; white leprosy; viti-<BR>ligo; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्र|श्वैत्रं
श्वैत्र, अम्, n. white leprosy; vitiligo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्रेय
श्वैत्रेय, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. produced in the<BR>atmosphere; (अस्), m. = श्वित्र्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्र्य|श्वैत्र्यं
श्वैत्र्य, अम्, n. leprosy, whiteness of the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्विन्द्|श्विंद्
श्विन्द् श्विन्द् (connected with rt. श्वित्),<BR>cl. 1. A. श्विन्दते, शिश्विन्दे, श्विन्दिष्-<BR>यते, श्विन्दितुम्, to be white, become white; to be<BR>cold (according to some); [cf. probably Gr. κυδνός,<BR>κυδρός, κῦδος; Goth. hveits, hvaitei; Old Germ.<BR>hwiz, hwaizi, hiza, haiz; Angl. Sax. hvit, hvœte.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेनी
श्वेनी श्वेनी, fem. of श्वेत, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैक्न
श्वैक्न श्वैक्न, अस्, m. (fr. श्विक्न), a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वोभूत
श्वोभूत श्वो-भूत, श्वो-वसीयस. See under<BR>2. श्वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष|षः
ष 1. ष, the thirty-first consonant of the<BR>Nāgarī alphabet and second of the three sibilants; it<BR>belongs to the cerebral class, and in sound corresponds<BR>to sh in the English word shun. (Many roots which<BR>begin with the dental स् are written in native gram-<BR>mars and in the Dhātu-pāṭha with ष्, to show that<BR>the dental स् is liable to be cerebralized after certain<BR>prepositions.)<BR>—ष-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound<BR>ष.<BR>—ष-त्व, अम्, n. the state of the letter ष,<BR>the cerebral sibilant, the substitution of ष् for स्.<BR>—षत्व-णत्व, अम्, n. the substitution of ष् for<BR>स् and of ण् for न् in grammatical derivatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष|षः
ष 2. ष, अस्, आ, अम्, best, excellent; wise,<BR>learned; (अस्), m. loss, destruction; loss of know-<BR>ledge; end, term; rest, remainder; eternal happi-<BR>ness, final emancipation, (in some of the preceding<BR>senses said to be fr. rt. सो); heaven, paradise; sleep;<BR>a learned man, teacher; a nipple; (according to<BR>Śabda-k.) = कच; = मानव; = सर्व; = गर्भ-<BR>विमोचन [cf. षू]; (अम्), n. the embryo; patience,<BR>endurance (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षग्
षग् षग्, षघ्, षच्, &c. See सग्,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्
