सं-वीक्ष्य, ind. having looked at or into, hav-<BR>ing searched for; having perceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीत|संवीतं
संवीत सं-वीत. See under सं-व्ये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृ
संवृ सं-वृ or सं-वॄ, cl. 5. 9. 1. P. A.<BR>-वृणोति, -वृणुते, -वृणाति, -वृणीते, -वरति, -ते,<BR>-वरितुम्, -वरीतुम् (ep. also -वर्तुम्), to cover<BR>over, cover, enclose, hide, conceal; to secure; to keep<BR>together, close, shut up, compress, contract; to put<BR>or place together, arrange, put in order; to keep or<BR>ward off, avert, restrain, keep back, stop; to refuse,<BR>reject; to select, choose: Caus. -वारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cover; to restrain; to keep back, ward off, avert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर|संवरं|संवरः
सं-वर, अस्, m. (sometimes written and con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">Page1038-c+ 79</a>]<BR>founded with सम्बर), covering; comprehending,<BR>comprehension, collection; closing, contraction, com-<BR>pression; a causeway, dam, mound, bridge; a kind<BR>of deer (= शम्बर); a sort of fish (= शम्बर);<BR>N. of a demon, = शम्बर; (अम्), n. covering, con-<BR>cealment; restraint, self-control, forbearance; a parti-<BR>cular religious observance (with Buddhists); water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवरण|संवरणं
सं-वरण, अम्, n. the act of covering or<BR>screening, concealing, enclosing, concealment; a<BR>secret; a disguise, pretext; the act of closing, shut-<BR>ting; an enclosure; a sanctuary, house, (in Ṛg-veda<BR>IX. 107, 9. according to Sāy. संवरणानि = सम्-<BR>भजनीयानि रस-रूपाण्य् अन्नानि; according to<BR>some, used as an epithet of rivers enclosed in beds);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of the author of the hymns Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 33, 34 (having the patronymic Prājāpatya); N.<BR>of a king mentioned in the Mahā-bhārata, (the<BR>father of Kuru.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवार|संवारः
सं-वार, अस्, m. covering, concealing, closing<BR>up; compression or contraction of the throat &c.<BR>(in pronunciation), obtuse articulation (opposed to<BR>वि-वार or acute articulation, and regarded as one of<BR>the Vāhya-prayatnas); diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवार्य
1. सं-वार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be covered or con-<BR>cealed; to be secured, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवार्य
2. सं-वार्य, ind. having kept off, having warded<BR>off or averted, having repelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवुवूर्षु
सं-वुवूर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to cover or<BR>conceal or disguise, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृण्वत्
सं-वृण्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, hiding, concealing;<BR>compressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृण्वान
सं-वृण्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, concealing, hiding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत|संवृतः
सं-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, covered up, covered, en-<BR>closed, enveloped, surrounded; concealed, hidden,<BR>kept secret, secured; retired, secluded; closed, shut,<BR>shut up, secured, put away, kept in safety; contracted,<BR>compressed (as the throat &c.); restrained, sup-<BR>pressed; sequestered, confiscated; filled with, full of;<BR>furnished or attended with, accompanied by; (अम्),<BR>n. a secret place; (in grammar) a particular mode<BR>of pronunciation, (one of the Ābhyantara-prayatnas.)<BR>—संवृत-संवार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who con-<BR>ceals what ought to be concealed, securing what ought<BR>to be secured.<BR>—संवृताकार (˚त-आक्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who conceals all signs of feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृति|संवृतिः
सं-वृति, इस्, f. covering up, concealment, com-<BR>pression, suppression; secret purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्य
सं-वृत्य, ind. having concealed; having closed<BR>or compressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृंह्
संवृंह् सं-वृंह् (see rt. वृंह्, also written<BR>बृंह्), cl. 1. P. -वृंहति, -वृंहितुम्, to join<BR>firmly together (Ved.): Caus. -वृंहयति (Ved.<BR>-वर्हयति), &c., to cause to be joined together, to<BR>unite (Ved.); to make strong, strengthen, invigorate;<BR>to incite, stimulate, encourage, animate, urge, (Sāy.<BR>सं-वर्हय = उत्साहय, Ṛg-veda VII. 31, 12.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृज्
संवृज् 1. सं-वृज्, cl. 7. P. A. -वृणक्ति,<BR>वृङ्क्ते, -वर्जितुम्, Ved. to bend or attract or<BR>appropriate to one's self, carry off, despoil; to devour,<BR>consume, (Sāy. = खादति): Desid. -विवृक्षते, to<BR>wish to appropriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्ग|संवर्गः
सं-वर्ग, अस्, m., Ved. plunder, spoils, (Sāy.<BR>= सम्यग् वृष्टेर् वर्जयिता, discharger of rain,<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 43, 5); (perhaps) food, (Sāy. संवर्-<BR>गम् = शत्रुभ्यः सहाच्छिद्यमानम्, Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 75, 12); epithet of Agni (‘the consumer’).<BR>—संवर्ग-जित्, त्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्ग्य
सं-वर्ग्य, अस्, m., N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्जन|संवर्जनं
सं-वर्जन, अम्, n. the act of bending or appro-<BR>priating to one's self; devouring, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृक्त
सं-वृक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, consumed, devoured, de-<BR>stroyed.<BR>—संवृक्त-धृष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one<BR>who has cut off or destroyed valiant (enemies; Sāy.<BR>सञ्छिन्ना धर्षण-शीला शत्रवो येन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृज्
2. सं-वृज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. one who carries off, a<BR>spoiler; one who consumes or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृज्य
सं-वृज्य, ind. = सं-हृत्य, having carried<BR>off, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्
संवृत् सं-वृत्, cl. 1. A. -वर्तते, &c.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">Page1039-a+ 79</a>]<BR>-वर्तितुम्, to turn towards, go towards, approach;<BR>to go against, attack, assault (with acc.); to come<BR>together, meet together, be united, meet in sexual<BR>embrace; to come round, come to pass, happen,<BR>take place, be produced, be fulfilled, be accomplished;<BR>to fall to the lot (of any one); to be, become, exist:<BR>Caus. -वर्तयति, -यितुम्, to cause to turn or re-<BR>volve, cause to proceed or go on; to cast, throw; to<BR>carry on, accomplish, fulfil, roll together, roll up,<BR>fold up, wrap up, envelop; to crumple up; to crush,<BR>destroy, dash to pieces: Desid. P. -विवृत्सति, to wish<BR>to be sexually united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त|संवर्तः|संवर्त्त|संवर्त्तः
सं-वर्त, अस्, m. turning towards; coming to<BR>pass, being, becoming; rolling up, crumpling up,<BR>destruction; the periodical destruction or dissolution<BR>of the universe; a cloud; a particular kind of cloud<BR>(abounding in water and so distinct from the Ā-varta<BR>which has no water, cf. द्रोण, पुष्कलावर्तक);<BR>N. of one of the seven clouds at the dissolution of the<BR>universe [cf. भीम-नाद]; a collection, multitude;<BR>a year; the tree Terminalia Bellerica; N. of a Muni<BR>and legislator [cf. वृहत्-स्˚]; of an Āṅgirasa (author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 172); (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तक|संवर्तकः|संवर्त्तक|संवर्त्तकः
सं-वर्तक, अस्, m. the fire that is to roll every-<BR>thing together and destroy the world at the period of<BR>universal dissolution; submarine fire; a kind of cloud,<BR>(see above, cf. मातङ्ग); N. of Bala-rāma, (other-<BR>wise called Bala-deva, elder brother of Kṛṣṇa); the<BR>plough of Bala-rāma.<BR>—संवर्तकाग्नि (˚क-अग्˚),<BR>इस्, m. the world-destroying fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तकिन्|संवर्त्तकिन्
संवर्तकिन्, ई, m., N. of Bala-rāma, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तमान
सं-वर्तमान, अस्, आ, अम्, turning towards,<BR>going towards, approaching; coming or meeting to-<BR>gether, having sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तयत्
सं-वर्तयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, crushing, destroying,<BR>dashing to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तयित्वा
सं-वर्तयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having per-<BR>formed, having fulfilled, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्ति|संवर्तिः|संवर्त्ति|संवर्त्तिः
सं-वर्ति, इस्, f. = संवर्तिका below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तिका|संवर्त्तिका
संवर्तिका, f. the new leaf of a water-lily, the<BR>petal or leaf near the filament (= केशर-समी-<BR>पस्थ-दल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तित
सं-वर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, rolled up, wrapped up,<BR>enveloped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्त|संवृत्तः
सं-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, become, arisen, happened,<BR>taken place, fulfilled, accomplished, past, gone; fur-<BR>nished with (for सं-वृत); covered (for सं-<BR>वृत); (अस्), m., N. of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्ति|संवृत्तिः
सं-वृत्ति, इस्, f. being, existing, becoming, hap-<BR>pening, fulfilment, accomplishment; covering, con-<BR>cealing (for सं-वृति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृध्
संवृध् सं-वृध्, cl. 1. P. A. -वर्धति, -ते<BR>(see rt. 1. वृध्), -वर्धितुम्, to grow to perfection<BR>or completion, grow up, increase; to fulfil, satisfy,<BR>grant (P.): Caus. -वर्धयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>grow or increase, augment, enlarge; to plant; to<BR>bring up, rear, raise, cherish, foster, nourish, fatten,<BR>feed, nurse; to cause to prosper, make prosperous or<BR>happy; to present with (with inst.); to fulfil, satisfy,<BR>grant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धक|संवर्द्धकः
सं-वर्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, causing complete<BR>growth or increase, augmenting, prospering; an in-<BR>creaser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धन|संवर्द्धनं|संवर्धनं
सं-वर्धन, अम्, n. the act of augmenting or<BR>increasing, prospering, cherishing, encouraging; com-<BR>plete growth, prospering, thriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धनीय
सं-वर्धनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be increased or<BR>augmented, to be fostered or encouraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धयत्
सं-वर्धयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to grow<BR>up or increase, enlarging, increasing, much increased,<BR>magnifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धित|संवर्द्धितः
सं-वर्धित, अस्, आ, अम्, brought to complete<BR>growth, brought up, reared, raised, cherished, pro-<BR>tected, encouraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृद्ध
सं-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, full grown, completely<BR>grown, grown up, grown tall or high, increased,<BR>augmented, enlarged, large, big; flourishing, bloom-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृष्
संवृष् सं-वृष्, cl. 1. P. -वर्षति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to rain upon, shower down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्षण
सं-वर्षण, अम्, n. raining, showering down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृह्
संवृह् सं-वृह्, cl. 6. P. -वृहति, &c. (see<BR>rt. 1. वृह्), -वर्हितुम्, -वर्ढुम्, Ved. to draw<BR>out or extract together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवे
संवे सं-वे, cl. 1. P. A. -वयति, -ते, -वातुम्,<BR>Ved. to weave together, interweave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवयत्
सं-वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, weaving together, in-<BR>terweaving in concert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत
सम्-उत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. woven or sewn to-<BR>gether, (तर्द्म-समुत, having the holes sewn<BR>together or fastened together with pins.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेग|संवेगः
संवेग सं-वेग. See under सं-विज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेद|संवेदः
संवेद सं-वेद. See under 1. सं-विद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेप्
संवेप् सं-वेप्, cl. 1. A. -वेपते, &c., to<BR>tremble, shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेपमान
सं-वेपमान, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, shaking<BR>(from cold &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेष्ट्
संवेष्ट् सं-वेष्ट्, cl. 1. A. -वेष्टते, &c., to<BR>be surrounded: Caus. -वेष्टयति, -यितुम्, to sur-<BR>round, envelop, encompass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेष्टमान
सं-वेष्टमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being surrounded<BR>or enveloped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यच्
संव्यच् सं-व्यच्, cl. 6. P. -विचति, -व्यचि-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to surround, encompass, envelop; to roll<BR>together, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 63, 1.<BR>सम्-अविव्यक् = सह विचति, सं-वेष्टयति); to<BR>pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यवसो
संव्यवसो सं-व्य्-अव-सो (-वि-अव-), cl. 4. P.<BR>-स्यति, -सातुम्, to decide upon, decree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यवहार|संव्यवहारः
संव्यवहार सं-व्यवहार, अस्, m. dealing<BR>together, mutual traffic or business, intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यूढ
संव्यूढ सं-व्यूढ, अस्, आ, अम् (see 2. व्य्-<BR>ऊढ), combined together, mixed, united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यूह|संव्यूहः
सं-व्यूह, अस्, m. combination, mixture, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्ये
संव्ये सं-व्ये, cl. 1. P. A. -व्ययति, -ते,<BR>-व्यातुम्, to cover over, overlay, clothe, put on<BR>clothes; to invest, surround, enclose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविव्यान
सं-विव्यान, अस्, आ, अम् (perf. part. A.), Ved.<BR>fully surrounded or invested with, endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीत|संवीतं
सं-वीत, अस्, आ, अम्, covered over, coated over,<BR>overlaid; clothed; adorned; invested, surrounded,<BR>enclosed, encompassed, shut in; overwhelmed.<BR>—सं-<BR>वीताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having the body<BR>covered, properly clothed, (according to Kullūka =<BR>आच्छादित-देह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यान|संव्यानं
सं-व्यान, अम्, n. the act of covering over, a<BR>covering; cloth, clothes, garment, vestment, vesture;<BR>an upper garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशकला
संशकला संशकला, ind. (doubtful), kill-<BR>ing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशङ्क्
संशङ्क् सं-शङ्क्, cl. 1. A. -शङ्कते, -शङ्कि-<BR>तुम्, to be very suspicious of, suspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशद्
संशद् सं-शद्, Caus. -शातयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to fall down, throw down, break to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशप्तक|संशप्तकः
संशप्तक सं-शप्तक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. शप्<BR>with सम्), a soldier sworn never to recede from a<BR>fight and stationed to prevent the flight of others;<BR>a picked warrior, a brother in arms; a conspirator<BR>bound by an oath to kill another; N. of a kind of<BR>soldier or guard belonging to Nārāyaṇī (mentioned<BR>in the Mahā-bhārata).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशब्द|संशब्दः
संशब्द सं-शब्द, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शब्द् with<BR>सम्), mention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशब्दन|संशब्दनं
सं-शब्दन, अम्, n. making a sound, calling<BR>out; praising, eulogizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशब्द्य
सं-शब्द्य, ind. (see rt. शब्द्), having called<BR>out, having said or spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशम्
संशम् सं-शम्, cl. 4. P. -शाम्यति, -शमि-<BR>तुम्, to become calm or pacified, be allayed, be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">Page1039-c+ 76</a>]<BR>extinguished: Caus. -शमयति, -यितुम्, to miti-<BR>gate, calm, allay; to settle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशमन
सं-शमन in पाप-श्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशान्त
सं-शान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय|संशयः
संशय सं-शय, सं-शयितृ. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशरण|संशरणं
संशरण सं-शरण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. शॄ with<BR>सम्), commencement of a combat, charge, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशास्
संशास् सं-शास्, cl. 2. P. -शास्ति, -शासितुम्,<BR>Ved. to sanctify, purify, make perfect, (Sāy. सं-<BR>शिशाधि = संस्कुरु, Ṛg-veda VII. 104, 19.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशि
संशि सं-शि (closely connected with सं-<BR>शो), cl. 5. P. A. -शिनोति, -शिनुते, (Ved. also cl. 3. A.)<BR>-शिशीते, -शेतुम्, to sharpen up or well, excite, incite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशित|संशितं
1. सं-शित, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see under सं-शो),<BR>sharpened up, aroused, excited; [cf. यज्ञ-स्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशिशान
सं-शिशान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sharpening well or<BR>thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशिश्रीषु
संशिश्रीषु सं-शिश्रीषु. See under सं-<BR>श्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशिश्वन्
संशिश्वन् सं-शिश्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. having<BR>young ones, (Sāy. सं-शिश्वरीः = सं-शिश्वर्यः<BR>सङ्गच्छमाना गावः, Ṛg-veda VIII. 69, 11.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशी
संशी सं-शी, cl. 2. A. -शेते, -शयितुम्, to<BR>lie down for rest or repose, sleep, grow languid, be-<BR>come feeble; to waver, be uncertain or irresolute or<BR>doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय|संशयः
सं-शय, अस्, m. uncertainty, irresolution, doubt,<BR>scruple, misgiving, suspicion, (frequently in the phrase<BR>न संशयः, there is no doubt, to be sure); diffi-<BR>culty, danger, risk, peril; dispute, question; possibility.<BR>—संशय-च्छेद, अस्, m. the solution of doubt.<BR>—संशय-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in uncertainty,<BR>uncertain, doubtful,<BR>—संशयात्मक (˚य-आत्˚), अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, consisting of doubt, made up of uncertainties.<BR>—संशयात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having a doubt-<BR>ful or irresolute mind; (आ), m. a sceptic.<BR>—संशया-<BR>पन्न (˚य-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, beset with doubt, hesi-<BR>tating, irresolute; doubtful, uncertain, dubious.<BR>—सं-<BR>शयापन्न-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, having the mind<BR>beset with doubts, of an irresolute or hesitating dis-<BR>position.<BR>—संशयोपेत (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessed of uncertainty, subject to doubt, doubtful,<BR>dubious, uncertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयान|संशयानः
सं-शयान, अस्, आ, अम्, feeling uncertain or<BR>irresolute, wavering, doubting, dubious, sceptical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयालु|संशयालुः
सं-शयालु, उस्, उस्, उ, disposed to doubt, irreso-<BR>lute, doubting, dubious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयित
सं-शयित, अस्, आ, अम्, uncertain, dubious,<BR>doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयितृ
सं-शयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who hesitates or<BR>wavers, a doubter, sceptic; dubious, doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयिन्
सं-शयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, doubtful, dubious, uncertain,<BR>questionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय्य
सं-शय्य, ind. having doubted or wavered, being<BR>in doubt, deliberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुध्
संशुध् सं-शुध्, cl. 4. P. -शुध्यति, -शोद्-<BR>धुम्, to become completely pure or purified: Caus.<BR>-शोधयति, -यितुम्, to purify or cleanse thoroughly,<BR>clear; to clear (expenses), pay off; to correct, rectify;<BR>to examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्ध
सं-शुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, completely purified or<BR>cleansed, pure, clean; refined, polished; expiated;<BR>acquitted (of crime or debt).<BR>—संशुद्ध-किल्वि-<BR>ष, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose offences are expiated,<BR>purified from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्धि|संशुद्धिः
सं-शुद्धि, इस्, f. thorough purification; cleansing<BR>or cleaning (the body); purity, cleanness; clearance;<BR>acquittal, acquittance; correction, rectification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोधन|संशोधनं
सं-शोधन, अम्, n. the act of purifying<BR>thoroughly, purification, cleaning, cleansing; refin-<BR>ing, clearing; paying off, correcting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोधित|संशोधितं
सं-शोधित, अस्, आ, अम्, completely cleansed or<BR>purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोध्य
1. सं-शोध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be purified, to be<BR>cleared or acquitted; to be paid off; to be corrected<BR>or rectified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोध्य
2. सं-शोध्य, ind. having cleansed; having<BR>cleared (a road).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुभ्
संशुभ् सं-शुभ्, Caus. -शोभयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to decorate, adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुष्
संशुष् सं-शुष्, cl. 4. P. -शुष्यति, -शोष्-<BR>टुम्, to be completely dried or dried up: Caus.<BR>-शोषयति, -यितुम्, to make dry, dry up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुष्क|संशुष्कं
सं-शुष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, completely dried, dry;<BR>withered, sere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोषित
सं-शोषित, अस्, आ, अम्, made thoroughly dry,<BR>dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशून
संशून सं-शून. See under सं-श्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशो
संशो सं-शो (closely connected with सं-<BR>शि), cl. 3. P. -शिशाति, -शातुम्, Ved. to sharpen<BR>thoroughly, sharpen up, excite, raise, produce; to<BR>finish off, effect, complete, supply, (Sāy. सं-शिशातु<BR>= सम्यक् तीक्ष्णी-करोतु = प्रयच्छतु, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 111, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशित|संशितं
2. सं-शित, अस्, आ, अम्, thoroughly finished<BR>or completed, finished off, effected, accomplished;<BR>established, decided, determined, certified, certain,<BR>well-ascertained; completing, effecting, diligent in<BR>accomplishing.<BR>—संशित-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has finished or accomplished a vow, faithful to<BR>a vow or obligation.<BR>—संशितात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, one whose mind or spirit is thoroughly matured<BR>or disciplined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्चत्
संश्चत् संश्-चत्, त्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 85. fr. rt. 1. चि with सम्; more probably fr. rt.<BR>चत्; cf. सञ्चत्, सं-श्वत्), deceit, trick, illusion,<BR>juggling; (त्), m. a juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्चाय
संश्चाय, Nom. A. संश्चायते, -यितुम्, to con-<BR>jure, juggle; to be cheated or deceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्यान|संश्यानः
संश्यान सं-श्यान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्यै<BR>with सम्), contracted, drawn together, shrunk up,<BR>congealed, frozen; collapsed; rolled up, gathered up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्राव
संश्राव सं-श्राव, अस्, m. (for सं-स्राव),<BR>flowing or pouring out, sprinkling, aspersion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रि
संश्रि सं-श्रि, cl. 1. P. A. -श्रयति, -ते,<BR>-श्रयितुम्, to go towards or have recourse to, betake<BR>one's self or flee for refuge or succour, seek protec-<BR>tion with, seek; to lean on, rest on, depend on;<BR>to attain, obtain; to unite with; to approach for<BR>sexual intercourse; to serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशिश्रीषु
सं-शिश्रीषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to have recourse<BR>to, desiring to adhere to or depend upon; wishing<BR>to serve, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रय|संश्रयः
सं-श्रय, अस्, m. the having recourse to, betak-<BR>ing one's self to [cf. कलि-श्˚], fleeing for refuge or<BR>protection, seeking shelter or succour; refuge, shelter,<BR>asylum, protection, patronage, favour; a resting-<BR>place, dwelling-place; seeking alliance, leaguing to-<BR>gether for mutual protection (one of the six Guṇas<BR>of a military prince mentioned in Manu VII. 160),<BR>league; an aim, object; N. of a Prajā-pati.<BR>—सं-<BR>श्रय-कारित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused by alliance (Manu<BR>VII. 176).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रयिन्
सं-श्रयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having recourse to, seeking<BR>refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रित|संश्रितः
सं-श्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone or fled to for refuge;<BR>come for protection or an asylum; taken under<BR>protection, sheltered, secured, protected, supported;<BR>united, joined; (अस्), m. a dependant, servant, fol-<BR>lower.<BR>—संश्रितानुराग (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>affection of dependants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रित्य
सं-श्रित्य, ind. having fled to for refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रु
संश्रु सं-श्रु, cl. 5. P. A. -शृणोति, -शृ-<BR>णुते, -श्रोतुम्, to hear well (P.); to listen well or<BR>attentively, be attentive (A. without acc. c. follow-<BR>ing); to promise: Caus. -श्रावयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to hear, cause to be heard; to narrate, report,<BR>recite, tell, proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रव|संश्रवः
सं-श्रव, अस्, m. hearing or listening atten-<BR>tively; promise, assent, agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रवण|संश्रवणं
सं-श्रवण, अम्, n. the act of hearing; the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रुत|संश्रुतः
सं-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, well heard; promised,<BR>agreed, assented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रुत्य
सं-श्रुत्य, ind. having heard or listened atten-<BR>tively, having promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लिष्
संश्लिष् सं-श्लिष्, cl. 4. P. -श्लिष्यति, -श्लेष्-<BR>टुम्, to clasp or press together, join together, em-<BR>brace: Caus. -श्लेषयति, -यितुम्, to join or connect<BR>together, unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लिष्ट|संश्लिष्टः
सं-श्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, clasped or pressed toge-<BR>ther, embraced, joined, united; adjoining, touching,<BR>close together; endowed; possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लिष्य
सं-श्लिष्य, ind. having clasped or embraced,<BR>having joined together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेष|संश्लेषः
सं-श्लेष, अस्, m. embrace, embracing; union,<BR>connection, junction, association, contact.<BR>—सं-<BR>श्लेष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing union or contact,<BR>joined, united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषण|संश्लेषणं
सं-श्लेषण, अम्, n. the act of clasping or<BR>pressing together; means of binding together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषित
सं-श्लेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, joined together, united,<BR>attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषिन्
सं-श्लेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, clasping, embracing, joining<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्वत्
संश्वत् सं-श्वत्, त्, n. = संश्-चत्, deceit,<BR>illusion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्वि
संश्वि सं-श्वि, cl. 1. P. -श्वयति, -श्वयितुम्,<BR>to swell up, swell greatly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशून
सं-शून, अस्, आ, अम्, much swelled, swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसञ्ज्|संसंज्
संसञ्ज् सं-सञ्ज्, Pass. -सज्यते, -सज्जते<BR>(see rt. 2. सञ्ज्), to adhere or cling together, stick<BR>close, be attached or connected together, adhere or<BR>cling to; to be entwined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्त|संसक्तः
सं-सक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, adhered or stuck together,<BR>joined or attached or linked together, sticking close<BR>to, adhering to, attached or tied to; fastened; re-<BR>strained; closely connected; close, near, adjoining,<BR>contiguous; intent on; possessing, endowed with,<BR>affected by.<BR>—संसक्त-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having<BR>the mind attached or fastened.<BR>—संसक्त-युग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, attached to a yoke, harnessed, yoked.<BR>—संसक्त-वदनाश्वास (˚न-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>with breath adhering to the mouth, with suppressed<BR>breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्ति|संसक्तिः
सं-सक्ति, इस्, f. close adherence, sticking close<BR>together, intimate union or junction; close connec-<BR>tion or contact, proximity; tying or fastening toge-<BR>ther; intercourse, intimacy, acquaintance; addiction<BR>or devotion to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसज्जमान
सं-सज्जमान, अस्, आ, अम्, adhering or sticking<BR>close together; being prepared or ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसद्
संसद् 1. सं-सद्, cl. 1. 6. P. -सीदति (Ved.<BR>and ep. also A. -ते), -सत्तुम्, to sit down together,<BR>sit along with, sit down; to sink down, be afflicted,<BR>be in distress; to pine away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसद्
2. सं-सद्, त्, त्, त्, one who sits together, one<BR>who sits at or takes part in a sacrifice; (त्), f. an as-<BR>sembly, meeting, congress, session; a court of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसाद|संसादः
सं-साद, अस्, m. a sitting down together, meet-<BR>ing, assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसीदत्
सं-सीदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sitting down together,<BR>sinking down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसरण|संसरणं
संसरण सं-सरण. See under सं-सृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्ग|संसर्गः
संसर्ग सं-सर्ग, सं-सर्जन, &c. See<BR>under 1. सं-सृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्प|संसर्पः
संसर्प सं-सर्प, &c. See under सं-<BR>सृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसव
संसव सं-सव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. सु with<BR>सम्), a confusion of libations, an irregular or sinful<BR>sacrifice (so regarded when two Brāhmans perform<BR>the Soma sacrifice on the same spot and at the same<BR>time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसाध्
संसाध् सं-साध्, Caus. -साधयति, -ते,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to be completely finished; to ac-<BR>complish or perform thoroughly, complete; to finish<BR>off; to settle; to destroy, kill, extinguish; to cause<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">Page1040-c+ 77</a>]<BR>to be settled or paid; to regain; to obtain; to be<BR>successful (A.): Pass. of Caus. -साध्यते, to be com-<BR>pletely accomplished; to be thoroughly provided or<BR>furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसाधयत्
सं-साधयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, accomplishing, &c.;<BR>obtaining, receiving, taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसाध्य
सं-साध्य, ind. having accomplished or per-<BR>formed thoroughly; having destroyed or killed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसार|संसारः
संसार सं-सार, &c. See under सं-सृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिच्
संसिच् 1. सं-सिच्, cl. 6. P. A. -सिञ्चति, -ते,<BR>-सेक्तुम्, to sprinkle over, sprinkle thoroughly, water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिक्त
सं-सिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well sprinkled or moistened,<BR>watered.<BR>—संसिक्त-रेणु, उस्, उस्, उ, having the<BR>dust laid or well watered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिच्
2. सं-सिच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. one who sprinkles,<BR>sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिच्य
सं-सिच्य, ind. having sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेक|संसेकः
सं-सेक, अस्, m. sprinkling over, moistening,<BR>watering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिध्
संसिध् सं-सिध्, cl. 4. P. -सिध्यति, -सेद्-<BR>धुम्, to be accomplished or performed thoroughly,<BR>to be made perfect; to be made happy, attain<BR>beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्ध
सं-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fully done or accom-<BR>plished, made perfect, perfected; one who has at-<BR>tained beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्धि|संसिद्धिः
सं-सिद्धि, इस्, f. complete accomplishment, per-<BR>fection, completion, complete attainment, beati-<BR>tude, final emancipation; nature, natural disposition,<BR>natural state or quality; a passionate or intoxicated<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसुदा
संसुदा सं-सुदा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. altogether<BR>munificent, one who gives very liberally, (Sāy. =<BR>सम्यक् सुष्ठु दातृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसुप्त
संसुप्त सं-सुप्त. See under सं-स्वप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूच्
संसूच् सं-सूच्, cl. 10. P. -सूचयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to indicate or show plainly, prove, imply, argue; to<BR>inform, tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूचन|संसूचनं
सं-सूचन, अम्, n. the act of indicating or show-<BR>ing plainly, proving; telling, informing; reproving,<BR>reproaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूचित
सं-सूचित, अस्, आ, अम्, plainly indicated; in-<BR>formed, told, apprised; reproved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृ
संसृ सं-सृ, cl. 1. P. -सरति, -सर्तुम्, to<BR>go towards, approach, attain, obtain; to go round,<BR>revolve, pass through a succession of states: Caus.<BR>-सारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to go round or revolve<BR>or pass through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसरण|संसरणं
सं-सरण, अम्, n. going, proceeding, moving<BR>or going round in a circuit, revolving, revolution,<BR>passing through a succession of states, birth and re-<BR>birth of living beings, the world; going well or<BR>unobstructedly, the unresisted march of troops; the<BR>commencement of war or battle; a highway, prin-<BR>cipal road; a resting-place for passengers near the<BR>gates of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसार|संसारः
सं-सार, अस्, m. course, passage, passing through<BR>a succession of states, course or circuit of mundane<BR>existence, transmigration, metempsychosis, the world,<BR>secular life, worldly illusion.<BR>—संसार-गमन,<BR>अम्, n. passing from one state of existence to another<BR>or from one body to another, transmigration, metem-<BR>psychosis.<BR>—संसार-गुरु, उस्, m. ‘the Guru of<BR>the world,’ epithet of Kāma (god of love).<BR>—सं-<BR>सार-मण्डल, अम्, n. the circle of the world.<BR>—संसार-मार्ग, अस्, m. the road of the world,<BR>the course or stage of mundane affairs, the world;<BR>the vulva.<BR>—संसार-मोक्षण, अस्, ई, अम्, libe-<BR>rating or emancipating from worldly existence;<BR>(अम्), n. emancipation from the world.<BR>—सं-<BR>सार-समुद्र or संसार-सागर, अस्, m. the<BR>ocean-like world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारिन्
संसारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, passing through (successive<BR>existences), transmigratory, worldly, mundane, secu-<BR>lar, mixing with society, engaged in worldly or secular<BR>occupations; (ई), m. a living or sentient being,<BR>human being, animal, creature, embodied spirit.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">Page1041-a+ 80</a>]<BR>—संसार्य्-आत्मन्, आ, m. (perhaps rather two separate<BR>words), the transmigratory soul, the soul passing through<BR>various mundane states, (opposed to परमात्मन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृति|संसृतिः
सं-सृति, इस्, f. course, current, flow, stream,<BR>revolution; course of mundane existence, transmi-<BR>gration; the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृत्य
सं-सृत्य, ind. having gone to or approached,<BR>having obtained; having passed onwards or through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृज्
संसृज् 1. सं-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति, -स्रष्-<BR>टुम्, to let loose together; to mix together, commin-<BR>gle, conjoin, connect, unite; to endow with, bestow<BR>upon; to cover with, anoint with (Ved.); to create:<BR>Pass. -सृज्यते, to be commingled or mixed, come<BR>together; to meet with (with inst.); to converse<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्ग|संसर्गः
सं-सर्ग, अस्, m. mixture or union together,<BR>commixture, conjunction, close or intimate union,<BR>close contact, touch, proximity, approximation, asso-<BR>ciation, society, (पापिष्ठ-स्˚, the society of very<BR>low people); intercourse, sexual attachment or con-<BR>nection, copulation, coition; acquaintance, familiarity;<BR>intimate relation (= सम्-अवाय), co-existence.<BR>—संसर्ग-तस्, ind. through union or connection,<BR>in consequence of intercourse or familiarity.<BR>—सं-<BR>सर्ग-दोष, अस्, m. the fault or evil consequences<BR>of society (with bad people).<BR>—संसर्ग-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, = सं-सृष्ट, mixed, joined with.<BR>—सं-<BR>सर्गाभव (˚ग-अभ्˚), अस्, m. (in the Nyāya<BR>phil.) a particular form of the category of non-<BR>existence (said to be of three kinds, prior, incidental<BR>and final, or absence of birth, destruction of present<BR>being and necessary cessation of existence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गिन्
संसर्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, commingling, commingled,<BR>united or mixed with, in contact with, connected;<BR>associated, keeping company, familiar, friendly, ac-<BR>quainted, an acquaintance; (ई), m. an associate,<BR>companion.<BR>—संसर्गि-ता, f. or संसर्गि-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. association, combination, fellowship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्जन|संसर्जनं|संसर्ज्जन
सं-सर्जन, अम्, n. the act of letting loose<BR>together, commingling; discharging, voiding, aban-<BR>doning, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिसृक्षु
सं-सिसृक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to mix together<BR>or unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृज्
2. सं-सृज्, Ved. commingling, collision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृज्यमान
सं-सृज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being joined or<BR>united together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्ट|संसृष्टः
सं-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, commingled, mixed to-<BR>gether, connected, conjoined, united; composed;<BR>associated or connected together (as partners &c.);<BR>reunited, rejoined; involved in; clothed in clean<BR>garments, cleanly dressed; created.<BR>—संसृष्ट-<BR>जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. conquering combatants.<BR>—संसृ-<BR>ष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. commixture, union, association; re-<BR>union; (in law) voluntary reunion or co-residence<BR>of kinsmen (as of father and son or of brothers with<BR>each other, after partition of property).<BR>—संसृष्ट-<BR>रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed in form or kind, adulterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टि|संसृष्टिः
सं-सृष्टि, इस्, f. union, combination, combin-<BR>ing, uniting; association, intercourse, co-partnership;<BR>living together in one family; collection, collecting,<BR>assembling; (in rhetoric) the aggregation or combin-<BR>ing of a number of metaphors in one passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टिन्
संसृष्टिन्, ई, m. a reunited kinsman (applied<BR>in Hindū law to persons of the same family who,<BR>after having made a partition, again live together,<BR>annulling the partition previously made); a co-<BR>partner, co-parcener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्रष्टृ
सं-स्रष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, Ved. one who mixes<BR>together or commingles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृप्
संसृप् सं-सृप्, cl. 1. P. -सर्पति, &c., to<BR>creep together, creep along with; to flow; to glide,<BR>move, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्प|संसर्पः
सं-सर्प, अस्, m. creeping along, gliding, flow-<BR>ing gently; any equable or gentle motion; the<BR>intercalary month occurring in a year in which there<BR>falls a Kṣaya-māsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पण|संसर्पणं
सं-सर्पण, अम्, n. the act of creeping along,<BR>sneaking; an unexpected attack, surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पत्
सं-सर्पत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, creeping or gliding<BR>along, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पिन्
सं-सर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, creeping along or over,<BR>winding, gliding, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेक|संसेकः
संसेक सं-सेक. See under 1. सं-सिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेव्
संसेव् सं-सेव्, cl. 1. A. -सेवते, &c., to<BR>attend on, wait on, serve; to worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवन
सं-सेवन, अम्, n. waiting on, attending on,<BR>serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवा
सं-सेवा, f. service, attendance, reverence, wor-<BR>ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवित
सं-सेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, waited on, attended on,<BR>served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृ
संस्कृ सं-स्-कृ (for सङ्-कृ, स् being inserted<BR>as in उप-स्-कृ, परि-ष्-कृ; cf. सङ्-कृ), cl. 8.<BR>P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते; Impv. संस्-करोतु (2nd sing.<BR>संस्-कुरु); Perf. सञ्-चस्कार (2nd sing. सञ्-च-<BR>स्करिथ, 1st pl. सञ्-चस्करिम, 3rd pl. सञ्-च-<BR>स्करुः); Aor. A. सम्-अस्कृत; Prec. P. संस्-<BR>क्रियात्, A. संस्-कृषीष्ट, -कर्तुम्, to put to-<BR>gether, construct, compose, form well or thoroughly,<BR>make perfect, elaborate, refine, polish, educate; to<BR>fabricate artificially; to form grammatically or accu-<BR>rately; to make ready, prepare, arrange; to cook,<BR>dress (food); to form or arrange according to sacred<BR>precept, consecrate, sanctify, dedicate, hallow, devote<BR>to sacred uses; to invest (with the sacrificial thread);<BR>to purify, cleanse; to decorate, embellish, ornament;<BR>to heap together, bring together, collect: Pass. -क्रि-<BR>यते, to be well put together or prepared, &c.; to<BR>be consecrated: Caus. -कारयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to form or construct well; to cause to prepare or<BR>arrange; to make, render (with two acc.); to cause<BR>to consecrate: Desid. सञ्-चिष्कीर्षति: Intens.<BR>सञ्-चेष्क्रीयते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कर्तृ|संस्कर्त्तृ
संस्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who makes perfect<BR>or polishes, one who prepares or dresses or cooks;<BR>one who consecrates, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कार|संस्कारः
संस्-कार, अस्, m. forming well or thoroughly,<BR>making perfect, perfecting, completing, finishing,<BR>polishing, refining, perfection, refinement, education,<BR>accomplishment; forming in the mind, conception,<BR>idea, notion; impression, form, mould; impression<BR>on the mind or memory; the power of memory,<BR>faculty of recollection, self-reproductive quality (one<BR>of the twenty-four qualities enumerated in the Vai-<BR>śeṣika branch of the Nyāya phil.); any faculty,<BR>capacity, instinct; operation, influence; preparation,<BR>making ready, preparation of food, &c., cooking,<BR>dressing, compounding; decoration, embellishment,<BR>ornament, elegance; making sacred, hallowing, con-<BR>secration, dedication; consecration of a king, &c.;<BR>making pure, purification, purity; a sanctifying or<BR>purificatory rite or essential ceremony (enjoined on<BR>all the first three or twice-born classes; the following<BR>are the twelve purificatory rites given in Manu II. 27,<BR>but of these ten only are enjoined according to some<BR>authorities, the tenth and eleventh being omitted:<BR>1. गर्भाधान, ‘embryo-reception,’ on the first<BR>sigh of conception, sometimes on a woman's attain-<BR>ing maturity: 2. पुं-सवन, ‘male-production,’<BR>on the first signs of vitality in the embryo: 3. सी-<BR>मन्तोन्नयन, ‘parting the hair’ of a pregnant<BR>woman in the fourth, sixth, or eighth month of her<BR>first pregnancy: 4. जात-कर्मन्, ‘birth-ceremony,’<BR>i. e. giving the infant butter out of a golden spoon<BR>before cutting the navel-string: 5. नाम-कर्मन्<BR>or नाम-करण, ‘naming-rite’ on the tenth or<BR>twelfth day after birth: 6. निष्क्रमण, ‘taking<BR>out’ the child when three months old to see the sun<BR>or, according to some, to look at the moon: 7. अन्-<BR>न-प्राशन, ‘feeding with boiled rice’ in the sixth<BR>month after birth: 8. चूडा-कर्मन् or चूडा-क-<BR>रण, ‘tonsure-rite,’ i. e. shaving the head all but<BR>the चूडा or one lock in the first or third year after<BR>birth: 9. उप-नय or उप-नयन, ‘investiture’<BR>with the sacrificial thread, see उप-नय; this is<BR>the most important of all the Saṃskāras: 10. के-<BR>शान्त, ‘cutting off the hair:’ 11. सम्-आवर्तन,<BR>‘returning,’ a rite performed on the student's return<BR>home after completing his studies: 12. विवाह,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">Page1041-c+ 79</a>]<BR>‘marriage:’ other Saṃskāras are mentioned as peculiar<BR>to various parts of India, e. g. अन्-अवलोभन, per-<BR>formed by a pregnant woman to prevent disappointment<BR>or miscarriage; विष्णु-बलि, an offering to Viṣṇu<BR>on the seventh month of pregnancy; स्वर्गारोहण,<BR>सूर्य-विलोकन, कर्ण-वेध, q. q. v. v.); any<BR>rite or ceremony; funeral obsequies; a polishing<BR>stone.<BR>—संस्कार-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by<BR>purificatory rites.<BR>—संस्कार-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of<BR>part of Raghu-nandana's Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—संस्कार-<BR>पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, rendered pure by sacred rites,<BR>purified by refinement.<BR>—संस्कार-भास्कर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a work on the Saṃskāras by Saṅkara.<BR>—संस्कार-रहित or संस्कार-वर्जित = संस्का-<BR>र-हीन below.<BR>—संस्कार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possess-<BR>ing refinement, cultivated.<BR>—संस्कारवत्-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the being possessed of refinement.<BR>—संस्कार-<BR>विधि, इस्, m. the rules of Saṃskāra, the law concern-<BR>ing purificatory rites.<BR>—संस्कार-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>destitute of purificatory rites; (अस्), m. a man of<BR>one of the three classes who has not been invested<BR>with the sacred thread or received the other purifica-<BR>tory ceremonies (in consequence of which neglect he<BR>becomes a Vrātya or outcast).<BR>—संस्काराधिकारिन्<BR>(˚र-अध्˚), ई, इणी, इ, one who has a right to receive<BR>or observe all the purificatory ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारक
संस्कारक, अस्, आ, अम्, consecrating, purifying,<BR>purificatory; serving as an article of cooking or for<BR>preparing any article of food or for dressing it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कार्य
संस्कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be finished or perfected;<BR>to be consecrated or initiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत|संस्कृतं|संस्कृतः
संस्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, carefully or accurately<BR>formed, artificially made or constructed or fabricated,<BR>elaborated, highly wrought, artificial, refined, polished,<BR>cultivated, perfected, completed, finished; made<BR>ready, prepared, cooked, dressed, compounded; con-<BR>secrated, sanctified, hallowed, initiated; married,<BR>(अ-संस्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, unmarried); cleansed,<BR>cleaned, purified; decorated, embellished, orna-<BR>mented; excellent, best; (अस्), m. a word formed<BR>according to accurate rules, a regular derivative; a<BR>man of one of the three classes who has received<BR>all the purificatory rites; a learned man; (अम्), n.<BR>language formed by accurate grammatical rules, re-<BR>fined or polished or highly wrought speech, the<BR>Sanskrit language; an offering, oblation, sacrifice<BR>(Ved.); a sacred usage or custom.<BR>—संस्कृतात्-<BR>मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, m. one who has received the puri-<BR>ficatory rites; a sage.<BR>—संस्कृतोक्ति (˚त-उक्˚), इस्,<BR>f. refined or polished language; a Sanskrit word or<BR>expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृतवत्
संस्कृत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has perfected<BR>or elaborated or polished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृति|संस्कृतिः
संस्-कृति, इस्, f. = संस्-कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत्य
संस्-कृत्य, ind. having perfected, having polished<BR>or adorned, &c.; having prepared or dressed, having<BR>cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत्रिम
संस्-कृत्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, perfected, polished;<BR>fabricated, made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्क्रिया
संस्-क्रिया, f. any purificatory rite (= संस्-कार<BR>above); funeral ceremonies or obsequies (burning<BR>the dead, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्त्
संस्त् संस्त् = rt. सस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भ्|संस्तंभ्
संस्तम्भ् सं-स्तम्भ्, cl. 5. 9. P. -स्तभ्-<BR>नोति, -स्तभ्नाति, -स्तब्धुम्, to support, prop up;<BR>to confirm, establish, corroborate; to stop, restrain:<BR>Caus. -स्तम्भयति, -यितुम्, to prop up, stay, sup-<BR>port; to confirm, strengthen, encourage; to stop;<BR>to make immovable or rigid, stupefy, paralyze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तब्ध
सं-स्तब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, supported, confirmed,<BR>corroborated; stopped, stayed, made firm or rigid,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तभ्य|संस्तभ्यं
सं-स्तभ्य, ind. having supported, having con-<BR>firmed or established; having made firm or stable<BR>or rigid, &c.; having supported or composed the<BR>mind firmly (in affliction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भ|संस्तंभ|संस्तंभः|संस्तम्भः
सं-स्तम्भ, अस्, m. support, supporting, prop;<BR>confirming, establishing, fixing, making firm; stop,<BR>stay; paralysis, muscular rigidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भनीय
सं-स्तम्भनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be propped; to<BR>be made firm; to be stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भयितृ
सं-स्तम्भयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who supports<BR>or props up, a supporter; one who stops or restrains,<BR>a restrainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भयित्वा
सं-स्तम्भयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having<BR>propped or confirmed or encouraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भित
सं-स्तम्भित, अस्, आ, अम्, propped, supported;<BR>stopped; stupefied, paralyzed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तर|संस्तरः
संस्तर सं-स्तर. See under सं-स्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तु
संस्तु सं-स्तु, cl. 2. P. A. -स्तौति, -स्तवीति,<BR>-स्तुते, -स्तुवीते, -स्तोतुम्, to praise or hymn together,<BR>praise in chorus; to praise properly or well; to<BR>celebrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तव|संस्तवः
सं-स्तव, अस्, m. praise; association together,<BR>agreeing together, acquaintance, intimacy (= परि-<BR>चय).<BR>—संस्तव-स्थिर, अस्, आ, अम्, firm through<BR>acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तवान|संस्तवानः
सं-स्तवान, अस्, आ, अम्, praising properly; talk-<BR>ing fluently and well, eloquent; (अस्), m. a singer,<BR>chanter (= उद्-गातृ); joy (= हर्ष, according to<BR>some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्ताव|संस्तावः
सं-स्ताव, अस्, m. hymning in chorus, repetition<BR>of hymns by a number of Brāhmans; the place<BR>occupied at a sacrifice by the Brāhmans reciting<BR>hymns and prayers; praise, celebration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुत|संस्तुतः
सं-स्तुत, अस्, आ, अम्, praised or hymned together;<BR>praised well or properly; lauded, hymned, eulogized;<BR>agreeing together, intimate, acquainted, known.<BR>—संस्तुत-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, for the most part<BR>lauded or hymned together, usually associated in<BR>hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुति|संस्तुतिः
सं-स्तुति, इस्, f. praise in chorus, hymning to-<BR>gether; praise, celebration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तूयमान
सं-स्तूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being praised or<BR>celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तृ
संस्तृ सं-स्तृ, cl. 5. 9. P. A. -स्तृणोति,<BR>-स्तृणुते, -स्तृणाति, -स्तृणीते, -स्तर्तुम्, -स्तरितुम्,<BR>-स्तरीतुम्, to spread out, spread, extend; to strew<BR>over, cover, cover over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तर|संस्तरः
सं-स्तर, अस्, m. a bed, couch; a bed made of<BR>leaves, &c.; a sacrifice (or perhaps rather the ritual<BR>arrangements for a sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तरण
सं-स्तरण, अम्, n. the act of strewing or<BR>covering over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तार|संस्तारः
सं-स्तार, अस्, m. spreading out, extension.<BR>—सं-<BR>स्तार-पङ्क्ति, इस्, f. a particular metre, (the first and<BR>fourth Pādas containing twelve syllables each, and<BR>the second and third eight each; cf. विष्टार-प्˚,<BR>प्रस्तार-प्˚, आस्तार-प्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तिर
सं-स्तिर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. entirely covered,<BR>hidden, concealed, (opposed to वि-ष्टिर, displayed,<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 140, 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तीर्ण
सं-स्तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, spread over, covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तीर्य
सं-स्तीर्य, ind. having spread; having covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्त्याय|संस्त्यायः
संस्त्याय सं-स्त्याय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्त्यै<BR>with सम्), assemblage, collection, heap, multitude,<BR>number; spreading, expansion, diffusion; vicinity,<BR>proximity; a habitation, house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्था
संस्था सं-स्था, cl. 1. A. -तिष्ठते (ep.<BR>also P. -तिष्ठति), -स्थातुम्, to stand or stay close<BR>together, abide or remain or live together; to agree,<BR>conform; to stand firmly; to stand or remain on;<BR>to exist, live, be; to stand still, stop; to be com-<BR>pleted; to die, perish: Caus. -स्थापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to stand firmly, to settle, establish or fix<BR>firmly; to place; to collect or compose (the mind);<BR>to cause to stand still, stop, restrain; to cause to<BR>cease or die, kill; to place in subjection, subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थ|संस्थः
सं-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or staying or being<BR>together, living together, staying with, associated,<BR>domesticated; staying, abiding, dwelling, living;<BR>lasting; stopping still, stationary, fixed; ended,<BR>perished, dead; (अस्), m. a dweller, resident, inha-<BR>bitant; a fellow-countryman, neighbour; a spy,<BR>secret emissary; (आ), f. an assembly, assemblage;<BR>state or condition of being, situation, time of life,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">Page1042-b+ 78</a>]<BR>&c.; occupation, business, profession; continuance<BR>in the right way, correct conduct; stop, stay; end,<BR>completion; loss, destruction, destruction of the world<BR>(= प्रलय, said to be of four kinds, viz. नैमित्-<BR>तिक, प्राकृतिक, नित्य, आत्यन्तिक); death, dying;<BR>manifestation, appearance; resemblance, likeness;<BR>form; a form or kind of Soma sacrifice [cf. यज्ञ-<BR>स्˚, पाक-स्˚, हविर्-यज्ञ-स्˚, सोम-स्˚]; a royal ordi-<BR>nance; (अम्), n., Ved. a battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थान|संस्थानं
सं-स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, standing together; agree-<BR>ing, resembling, like; (अम्), n. the act of standing<BR>or being together; a collection, aggregation, heap,<BR>quantity; the aggregation of primitive atoms, primary<BR>formation; conformation, configuration; form, figure,<BR>shape, construction; a common place of abode, vici-<BR>nity, neighbourhood; a place where four roads meet;<BR>any place, station; position, situation; a spot, mark,<BR>sign; standing still, stopping, dying, death.<BR>—सं-<BR>स्थान-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going in various forms (of<BR>gods or demons); moving in various stations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापक
सं-स्थापक, अस्, इका, अम्, fixing firmly, settling,<BR>establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापन|संस्थापनं
सं-स्थापन, अम्, n. the act of placing together,<BR>collecting; fixing firmly, placing, fixing; confirming,<BR>establishing, establishment; restraining; a statute,<BR>regulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापनीय
सं-स्थापनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be established or<BR>settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापित
सं-स्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to stand together,<BR>heaped up, accumulated; established, fixed, placed,<BR>deposited; stopped, restrained, controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थाप्य
सं-स्थाप्य, ind. having made to stand firmly,<BR>having fixed, having confirmed, having established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थास्नु
सं-स्थास्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, firmly fixed, stationary,<BR>immovable; lasting, durable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थित|संस्थितः
सं-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or being together,<BR>lying or situated close at hand, contiguous, near;<BR>brought together, collected, heaped, covered; agree-<BR>ing, like, resembling; standing firm, settled, fixed,<BR>established; staying, abiding; residing, being in or<BR>at; placed in or on; standing still, stationary; stopped,<BR>concluded, completed, ended, finished; dead, deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थिति|संस्थितिः
सं-स्थिति, इस्, f. staying or abiding or being to-<BR>gether; collection, accumulation, heap; standing or<BR>staying with, residing or living with or near; con-<BR>tiguity, nearness, connection; standing firm; duration,<BR>continuance; being, abiding, abode, situation, station,<BR>state, condition (of life); standing still or stationary,<BR>stoppage; restraint; death, dying; destruction of<BR>the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृश्
संस्पृश् 1. सं-स्पृश्, cl. 6. P. -स्पृशति,<BR>-स्पर्ष्टुम्, -स्प्रष्टुम्, to come into close con-<BR>tact, to touch, lay hold of; to reach; to perceive;<BR>to sprinkle (with water &c.): Caus. -स्पर्शयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to touch; to sprinkle over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्श|संस्पर्शः
सं-स्पर्श, अस्, m. close or mutual contact, touch,<BR>touching, conjunction, mixture, laying hold of; per-<BR>ception, sense; the being touched, being affected;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of fragrant plant or perfume (= जनी).<BR>—संस्पर्श-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by contact<BR>or sensible perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृश्
2. सं-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, touching, coming into con-<BR>tact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृशत्
सं-स्पृशत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, touching, laying<BR>hold of; striking together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृश्य
सं-स्पृश्य, ind. having touched; having rubbed<BR>or chafed; having reached; extending to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृष्ट
सं-स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, touched, brought into<BR>contact; mixed, combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फाल|संस्फालः
संस्फाल सं-स्फाल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्फल्<BR>with सम्), a ram (= मेष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फुट|संस्फुटः
संस्फुट सं-स्फुट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. स्फुट्<BR>with सम्), bursting open, blossomed, blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फोट|संस्फोटः
सं-स्फोट, अस्, m. war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फोटि|संस्फोटिः
सं-स्फोटि, इस्, m. = सं-स्फोट above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फेट|संस्फेटः
संस्फेट सं-स्फेट, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्फिट् with<BR>सम्), war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मि
संस्मि सं-स्मि, cl. 1. A. -स्मयते, -स्मेतुम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">Page1042-c+ 77</a>]<BR>to laugh at, deride: Desid. -सिस्मयिषते, to wish<BR>to laugh at or deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिस्मयिषमाण
सं-सिस्मयिषमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to<BR>ridicule, desirous of laughing at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृ
संस्मृ सं-स्मृ, cl. 1. P. -स्मरति, -स्मर्तुम्,<BR>to remember fully, recollect (with acc. or gen.);<BR>Caus. -स्मारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to remember,<BR>remind of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मरण|संस्मरणं
सं-स्मरण, अम्, n. the act of remembering,<BR>calling to mind, recollecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मरत्
सं-स्मरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, fully remembering,<BR>recollecting well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मर्तव्य
सं-स्मर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be remembered;<BR>to be thought upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मार्य
सं-स्मार्य, ind. having caused to remember,<BR>having reminded of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृत
सं-स्मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, remembered, recollected,<BR>called to mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृति|संस्मृतिः
सं-स्मृति, इस्, f. remembering, remembrance,<BR>recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृत्य
सं-स्मृत्य, ind. having remembered or called<BR>to mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्रव|संस्रवः
संस्रव सं-स्रव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्रु with<BR>सम्), flowing, oozing out; that which flows, a<BR>stream; anything flowing off or remaining; the<BR>droppings or remains of a libation; a kind of offer-<BR>ing or libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्राव|संस्रावः
सं-स्राव, अस्, m. flowing, oozing out; a kind<BR>of offering or libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्रष्टृ
संस्रष्टृ सं-स्रष्टृ. See under सं-सृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्वप्
संस्वप् सं-स्वप्, cl. 2. P. -स्वपिति, &c., to<BR>sleep soundly, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसुप्त
सं-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, soundly asleep, fast asleep,<BR>asleep, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्वृ
संस्वृ सं-स्वृ, cl. 1. A. -स्वरते, -स्वर्तुम्,<BR>-स्वरितुम्, to hymn, praise (Ved.); to pain, afflict,<BR>torment, cause pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहन्
संहन् सं-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -हन्तुम्,<BR>to strike together, join or unite closely, put together,<BR>close (the hands &c.), shut; to contract, diminish;<BR>to bring together, heap, accumulate, collect; to fight<BR>together, clash; to strike, kill, destroy completely:<BR>Caus. -घातयति, -यितुम्, to strike together, kill,<BR>destroy utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह
सं-ह = सं-हत below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहत|संहतः
सं-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck together, closely<BR>joined or united, closed, shut; well knit or com-<BR>pacted together, firmly united, compact, close, firm,<BR>solid; closely allied; combined, joined, connected,<BR>acting or making effort together, keeping together;<BR>collected, assembled, accumulated; struck, hurt,<BR>wounded, killed.<BR>—संहत-जानु, उस्, उस्, उ, or<BR>संहत-जानुक, अस्, ई, अम्, knock-kneed.<BR>—सं-<BR>हत-तल, अस्, m. the two hands joined with the<BR>open palms brought together.<BR>—संहत-ता, f. or<BR>संहत-त्व, अम्, n. compactness, close combina-<BR>tion; close contact or approximation, conjunction;<BR>union, agreement.<BR>—संहत-भ्रू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ,<BR>knitting the brows.<BR>—संहत-स्तनी, f. (a woman)<BR>whose breasts are very close to each other.<BR>—सं-<BR>हताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहति|संहतिः
सं-हति, इस्, f. the state of being brought into<BR>close contact, firm or close combination, firm union<BR>or alliance, junction, joint effort, agreement, com-<BR>pactness, firmness, solidity, bulk, mass, assemblage,<BR>collection, heap, number, host, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहत्य
सं-हत्य, ind. having struck together, having<BR>closed or joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहनन|संहननं
सं-हनन, अस्, ई, अम्, striking together; kill-<BR>ing, destroying, a destroyer, conqueror; (अम्), n.<BR>the act of striking together, compactness, inflexi-<BR>bility; strength, muscularity; rubbing the limbs;<BR>the body (as having the limbs well compacted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहनु
सं-हनु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. destructive, deadly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घ|संघ|संघः|सङ्घः
सङ्-घ, अस्, m. close contact or combination;<BR>any collection or assemblage, heap, multitude, quantity,<BR>crowd, host, band, number, group, flock, shoal; any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">Page1043-a+ 75</a>]<BR>number of people or inhabitants living together.<BR>—सङ्घ-गुप्त, अस्, m. a proper N., (also read<BR>सिंह-गुप्त.)<BR>—सङ्घ-चारिन्, ई, m. ‘going in<BR>shoals,’ a fish.<BR>—सङ्घ-जीविन्, ई, m. ‘living by<BR>multitudes of people,’ a hired labourer, porter, cooly.<BR>—सङ्घ-तल, अस्, m. the two hands joined with<BR>the open palms brought together.<BR>—सङ्घ-पुष्पी,<BR>f. a particular plant (= धातकी).<BR>—सङ्घ-वृत्ति,<BR>इस्, f. a state of close combination.<BR>—सङ्घवृत्ति-<BR>ता, f. combined action.<BR>—सङ्घ-शस्, ind. collec-<BR>tively, all together; by troops, in flocks, in shoals,<BR>in companies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घात|संघात|संघातः|सङ्घातः
सङ्-घात, अस्, m. close combination, union,<BR>association, connection, confederacy; a collection,<BR>quantity, assemblage, multitude, heap, cluster, band;<BR>a collection of mucus, phlegm [cf. सङ्-घाणक];<BR>composition of words, formation of compounds;<BR>striking, killing, hurting; a particular gait or mode<BR>of walking (in the drama); N. of a division of the<BR>infernal regions; [cf. सं-हात.]<BR>—सङ्घात-क-<BR>ठिन, अस्, आ, अम्, compactly or solidly hard, hard<BR>from solidity or compactness.<BR>—सङ्घात-पत्त्रिका,<BR>f. a sort of fennel (= शत-पुष्पा).<BR>—सङ्घात-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having close union, possessing a heap<BR>or multitude, closely compacted or combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहरण|संहरणं
संहरण सं-हरण. See under सं-हृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्ष|संहर्षः
संहर्ष 1. सं-हर्ष, अस्, m. (for सङ्-घर्-<BR>ष, q. v.; for 2. see under सं-हृष्), rubbing,<BR>grinding, trituration; envy, emulation; air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहवन|संहवनं
संहवन सं-हवन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. हु with<BR>सम्), the act of sacrificing or offering oblations toge-<BR>ther; sacrificing in a proper manner; a quadrangle,<BR>group of four houses; [cf. सञ्-जवन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहा
संहा सं-हा, cl. 3. A. -जिहीते, &c., to go<BR>together, proceed; to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जिहान|संजिहान
सञ्-जिहान, अस्, आ, अम्, going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहात|संहातः
संहात संहात, अस्, m. (probably for सङ्-<BR>घात, q. v.), one of the twenty-one hells (mentioned<BR>in Manu IV. 89).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहार|संहारः
संहार सं-हार. See under सं-हृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहि
संहि सं-हि, cl. 5. P. -हिनोति, &c., to send<BR>forth, utter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहित|संहितः
संहित सं-हित. See under सन्-धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहूति|संहूतिः
संहूति सं-हूति. See under सं-ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृ
संहृ सं-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते, -हर्-<BR>तुम्, to bring or draw together; to contract, abridge,<BR>compress; to close, clench (the fists &c.); to crush<BR>together, crumple up, destroy, annihilate, (opposed<BR>to सृज्); to bring together, collect, accumulate; to<BR>draw together, unite, bind by obligations; to draw<BR>aside (a curtain &c.), withdraw, withhold, hold back,<BR>take back; to restrain, suppress, curb; to lay hold<BR>of, seize, subtract, take: Pass. -ह्रियते, to be drawn<BR>together, be contracted or abridged; to be destroyed;<BR>to be finished or concluded; to be restrained, &c.:<BR>Desid. -जिहीर्षति, to wish to draw together or<BR>destroy or annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर
सं-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, drawing together, bringing<BR>together; contracting; destroying, &c.<BR>—संह-<BR>राख्य (˚र-आख्˚), अस्, m. ‘called Saṃhara,’ the<BR>fire Pāvaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहरण|संहरणं
सं-हरण, अम्, n. the act of drawing or bring-<BR>ing together; contracting; crumpling together, de-<BR>stroying, destruction, ruin; collecting, accumulating;<BR>withdrawing; restraining, checking; seizing, taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्तृ
सं-हर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who draws together<BR>or contracts, &c.; destroying, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहार|संहारः
सं-हार, अस्, m. drawing together, contraction,<BR>abridgement, comprehensive description, abbrevia-<BR>tion, compression; a fault in pronunciation, (opposed<BR>to वि-हार); close, end, conclusion, (काव्य-सं-<BR>हार, अस्, m. ‘the close of a poem,’ epithet of the<BR>benediction at the conclusion of a drama); destruc-<BR>tion, loss; the periodical destruction of the universe<BR>at the end of a Kalpa; collection, assemblage, accu-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">Page1043-b+ 75</a>]<BR>mulation; withdrawing, withholding, restraining,<BR>suppressing; a charm or spell for restraining magical<BR>weapons or bringing them back after discharging<BR>them; seizing, laying hold of, taking [cf. वेणी-स्˚];<BR>a division of the infernal regions; practice, skill.<BR>—संहार-भैरव, अस्, m. one of the eight<BR>forms of Bhairava, q. v.<BR>—संहार-मुद्रा, f., N.<BR>of a particular posture in the Tantra worship (=<BR>विसर्जन-मुद्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहारक
सं-हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, drawing together,<BR>compressing, closing; destructive, ruinous; a de-<BR>stroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहार्य
सं-हार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be drawn together or<BR>contracted, to be abridged; to be destroyed, &c.;<BR>to be restrained or curbed or suppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृत|संहृतः
सं-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn together; contracted,<BR>compressed, abridged; closed; destroyed, scattered;<BR>collected, assembled; withdrawn, withheld; restrained,<BR>curbed; seized, laid hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृति|संहृतिः
सं-हृति, इस्, f. contraction, compression, abridge-<BR>ment; destruction, loss, disappearance; collection;<BR>restraint; taking, seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृत्य
सं-हृत्य, ind. having drawn together or con-<BR>tracted, having abridged; having closed or clenched<BR>(the fist); having destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृष्
संहृष् सं-हृष्, cl. 4. P. -हृष्यति, -हर्-<BR>षितुम्, to bristle, stand erect (as the hair of the<BR>body from joy or fright); to thrill with delight, be<BR>glad, rejoice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्ष|संहर्षः
2. सं-हर्ष, अस्, m. bristling or erection of the<BR>hair of the body (either from rapture or terror),<BR>thrill of delight, joy, pleasure; ardour, emulation,<BR>(perhaps for सङ्-घर्ष); air, wind; trituration,<BR>rubbing together, (for सङ्-घर्ष.)<BR>—संहर्ष-<BR>योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing joy, enraptured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृष्ट
सं-हृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, thrilled, enraptured,<BR>rejoiced, delighted, glad; bristling, shuddering; fired<BR>with ardour or emulation.<BR>—संहृष्ट-रोमन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, or संहृष्ट-रोमाङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the hair of the body bristling (with joy<BR>or fright), thrilling with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहोत्र
संहोत्र सं-होत्र, Ved. = समीचीन-यज्ञ,<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 86, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्राद|संह्रादः
संह्राद सं-ह्राद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. ह्रद् with<BR>सम्), a loud noise, uproar, sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रादिन्
सं-ह्रादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding together, making<BR>a noise, tumultuous, noisy.<BR>—संह्रादि-कण्ठ,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a sounding throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्री
संह्री सं-ह्री, cl. 3. P. -जिह्रेति, &c., to be<BR>quite ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रीण
सं-ह्रीण, अस्, आ, अम्, altogether ashamed; bash-<BR>ful, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्लाद
संह्लाद सं-ह्लाद, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Hiraṇya-kaśipu (and brother of Pra-hlāda, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्वे
संह्वे सं-ह्वे, cl. 1. A. -ह्वयते, -ह्वातुम्<BR>(Ved. Inf. -ह्वयितवै), to call out loudly, shout<BR>together; to call out, tell, relate, make known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहूति|संहूतिः
सं-हूति, इस्, f. shouting or calling out together,<BR>general shout or clamour, exclamation, tumultuous<BR>exultation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक|सकः
सक सक, अस्, m. (a diminutive fr. स, the<BR>base of nom. sing. of तद्), he, that man; (आ), f.<BR>she, (Ṛg-veda I. 191, 11.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकट|सकटः
सकट स-कट, अस्, आ, अम्, bad, vile; (अस्),<BR>m. the small tree Trophis Aspera (= शाखोट).<BR>—सकटान्न (˚ट-अन्˚), अम्, n. impure food (ac-<BR>cording to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकण्टक|सकंटक|सकण्टकः
सकण्टक स-कण्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>thorns, thorny, prickly; troublesome, perilous; (अस्),<BR>m. the aquatic plant Vallisneria (= शैवाल); a kind<BR>of Karañja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकपटम्
सकपटम् स-कपटम्, ind. with fraud or<BR>dissimulation, fraudulently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकमल
सकमल स-कमल, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>lotuses, abounding in lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकम्प|सकंप
सकम्प स-कम्प, अस्, आ, अम्, having tremor,<BR>tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकम्पन|सकंपन
स-कम्पन, अस्, आ, अम्, having tremor, trem-<BR>bling; accompanied with earthquakes; (according<BR>to Nīla-kaṇṭha) = स-विद्युत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर
सकर 1. स-कर, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कर),<BR>having hands; possessing a trunk (as an elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर
सकर 2. स-कर, अस्, आ, अम् (see 2. कर),<BR>having rays, full of rays; having or bearing tax,<BR>bringing in toll, liable to pay taxes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकरुण|सकरुणः
सकरुण स-करुण, अस्, आ, अम्, having pity,<BR>tender, compassionate; (अम्), ind. compassionately,<BR>tenderly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्ण|सकर्णः
सकर्ण स-कर्ण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having<BR>ears; hearing, listening; accompanied by Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्तृक
सकर्तृक स-कर्तृक, अस्, आ, अम्, having an<BR>agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्मक|सकर्म्मक|सकर्म्मकः
स-कर्मक, अस्, m. having or performing any<BR>act; (in grammar) ‘having an object,’ the transitive<BR>or active verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्मन्|सकर्म्मन्
स-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, performing any act or rite;<BR>following similar business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकारण
स-कारण, अस्, आ, अम्, having a cause, originating<BR>from a cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल|सकलं
सकल 1. स-कल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. स and<BR>कला), together with parts or portions; all, whole,<BR>entire; (अम्), n. everything; the whole; [cf. Lith.<BR>cźiela-s; Russ. zielyï; Slav. ziel; Pol. saly, salki;<BR>perhaps Goth. hail-s; Old Norse heil; Angl. Sax.<BR>hal.]<BR>—सकल-सिद्धि-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving all<BR>perfection.<BR>—१. सकल-हंस-गण, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing entire or unbroken flocks of geese.<BR>—सकलार्-<BR>थ-शास्त्र-सार (˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, containing the<BR>essence of precepts about all things.<BR>—सकलेन्दु<BR>(˚ल-इन्˚), उस्, m. the full moon.<BR>—सकलेन्दु-मुख,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, having a face like the full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल|सकलं
सकल 2. स-कल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a soft<BR>or low sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलङ्क
सकलङ्क स-कलङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>spots or stains, stained, contaminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलत्र
सकलत्र स-कलत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied<BR>by a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलह
सकलह स-कलह, अस्, आ, अम्, having quar-<BR>rels, quarrelsome, quarrelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलहंसगण
सकलहंसगण 2. स-कलहंस-गण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having flocks of Kala-haṃsas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल्प|सकल्पः
सकल्प स-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>ritual or ceremonial part of the Veda, along with the<BR>ritual, (Manu II. 140); having rites or ceremonies;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकवच
सकवच स-कवच, अस्, आ, अम्, having armour<BR>or mail, clad in armour, mailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाकोल|सकाकोलः
सकाकोल स-काकोल, अस्, m. one of the<BR>twenty-one hells (mentioned in Manu IV. 89).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकातर
सकातर स-कातर, अस्, आ, अम्, cowardly,<BR>dastardly; (अम्), ind. with cowardice, in a cowardly<BR>manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाम|सकामः
सकाम स-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, having love or<BR>affection, full of love, loving, a lover; one who has<BR>obtained his wish, contented, satisfied, humoured,<BR>gratified; (अम्), ind. with pleasure; contentedly,<BR>assuredly, indeed.<BR>—सकामारि (˚म-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of lovers,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकार
सकार स-कार. See under 1. स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकार्मुक
सकार्मुक स-कार्मुक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>bow, armed with a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाल
सकाल स-काल, अस्, आ, अम्, seasonable; (अम्),<BR>ind. seasonably, betimes, early in the morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाली
सकाली सकाली, f., N. of a place.<BR>—सकाली-<BR>समुद्र, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाश|सकाशः
सकाश स-काश, अस्, आ, अम्, having appear-<BR>ance or visibility, visible, present, near; (अस्), m.<BR>presence, propinquity, vicinity, nearness; (अम्, ए),<BR>ind. in the presence of, near; (आत्), ind. from the<BR>presence of, from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकिरीटकौस्तुभ
सकिरीटकौस्तुभ स-किरीट-कौस्तुभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a diadem and breast-jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुक्षि
सकुक्षि स-कुक्षि, इस्, इस्, इ, having the same<BR>womb, born from the same mother (as a brother or<BR>other relation of whole blood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुण्डल
सकुण्डल स-कुण्डल, अस्, आ, अम्, having ear-<BR>rings, decorated with ear-rings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुरुण्ड|सकुरुण्डः
सकुरुण्ड सकुरुण्ड, अस्, m. yellow Ama-<BR>ranth or Barleria (= साकुरुण्ड, कुरुण्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल|सकुलः
सकुल स-कुल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a family;<BR>belonging to a noble family, &c.; belonging to the<BR>same family; (अस्), m. a kinsman; (अस्, ई), m. f.<BR>a sort of fish (= शकुल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल्य|सकुल्यः
सकुल्य, अस्, m. one of the same family and<BR>name (= स-गोत्र); a distant relation, remote kins-<BR>man (said to be one who shares a divided oblation,<BR>e. g. the grandson's grandson or even other descendants<BR>as far as three degrees or more from him; sometimes<BR>extended to the tenth descendant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृच्छ्र
सकृच्छ्र स-कृच्छ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>trouble or distress, attended with pain, painful, dis-<BR>tressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्
सकृत् 1. स-कृत्, ind. (connected with rt.<BR>1. कृ), once, on one occasion only [cf. अ-स्˚]; at<BR>one time; at once, together; together with, with;<BR>always; [with the former part of this word cf. Lat.<BR>se, si, sim, of the words se-mel, si-mul, sim-plex,<BR>and Gr. ἁ of ἁ-πλοῦς; with the latter part cf. Lith.<BR>kartas.]<BR>—सकृत्-प्रज, अस्, m. ‘having offspring<BR>once,’ a crow.<BR>—सकृत्-प्रयोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved.<BR>being employed only once.<BR>—सकृत्-प्रसूतिका, f.<BR>one who has borne one child; (a cow) that has<BR>calved once.<BR>—सकृत्-फला, f. ‘bearing fruit once,’<BR>the plantain tree (= कदली).<BR>—सकृत्-सू, ऊस्, f.,<BR>Ved. one who bears a child only once.<BR>—सकृद्-<BR>आगामिन्, ई, m., N. of one of the four orders of Bud-<BR>dhist Āryas.<BR>—सकृद्-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘having only<BR>one conception,’ a mule, = खेसर; (आ), f. a woman<BR>who is pregnant only once.<BR>—सकृद्-वीर, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of plant (= एक-वीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्
सकृत् 2. सकृत्, त्, m. (more usually written<BR>शकृत्, q. v.), excrement, feces, ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृप
सकृप स-कृप, अस्, आ, अम्, having pity, com-<BR>passionate; with Kṛpa, accompanied by Kṛpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृपण
स-कृपण, अस्, आ, अम्, pitiable, miserable,<BR>wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकेश
सकेश स-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, having hair,<BR>hairy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकैतव|सकैतवः
सकैतव स-कैतव, अस्, आ, अम्, having fraud,<BR>fraudulent; (अस्), m. a deceiver, cheat, impostor;<BR>(अम्), ind. fraudulently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकोप
सकोप स-कोप, अस्, आ, अम्, enraged, full of<BR>anger, angry, displeased; (अम्), ind. with anger,<BR>angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकौतुक
सकौतुक स-कौतुक, अस्, आ, अम्, full of ex-<BR>pectation, eagerly expectant; (अम्), ind. expectantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्त|सक्तः
सक्त सक्त, सक्ति. See under rt. सञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तु|सक्तुः
सक्तु सक्तु, उस्, उ, m. n. (also written शक्तु,<BR>q. v.; according to Uṇādi-s. I. 70. fr. rt. सच्; ac-<BR>cording to some only masc. pl.), the flour of barley<BR>(fried before ground); barley-meal.<BR>—सक्तु-प्रस्-<BR>थ, अस्, अम्, m. n. a Prastha or particular measure<BR>of flour.<BR>—सक्तुप्रस्थीय, अम्, n., N. of an episode<BR>in the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—सक्तु-फला or सक्तु-<BR>फली, f. ‘having fruit resembling flour,’ the Śamī<BR>tree, Mimosa Suma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुक|सक्तुकः
सक्तुक, अस्, m. = सक्तु above; a species of<BR>poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुल
सक्तुल, अस्, आ, अम्, containing flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थि
सक्थि सक्थि, इ, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 154. fr. rt. सञ्ज्, because the body ‘is attached<BR>to’ or ‘rests on’ the thigh; according to Yāska fr.<BR>rt. सच्; the base of some cases is सक्थन्, see<BR>below; in Ṛg-veda X. 86, 16. सक्थ्या = सक्थिनी,<BR>n. du., occurs), the thigh; a bone; the pole or shafts<BR>of a cart; a part of the frame of a cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थ
सक्थ at the end of a comp. = सक्थि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थन्
सक्थन्, a form of base substituted for सक्थि<BR>above, in the weakest cases (e. g. inst. sing. सक्थ्ना,<BR>dat. सक्थ्ने, abl. gen. सक्थ्नस्, loc. सक्थ्नि<BR>or सक्थनि, gen. pl. सक्थ्नाम्, Ved. acc. pl. सक्-<BR>थानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्म
सक्म सक्म, सक्म्य. See under rt. सच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्रिय
सक्रिय स-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, having action,<BR>active, mutable, movable, migratory; one who ob-<BR>serves his religious duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्रोध
सक्रोध स-क्रोध, अस्, आ, अम्, full of anger,<BR>angry; (अम्), ind. with anger, angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्ष्
सक्ष् सक्ष्. See rt. सच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्षण
सक्षण स-क्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>leisure moment, being at leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्षणि
सक्षणि सक्षणि, इस्, इस्, इ (according to<BR>some fr. rt. क्षन्, perhaps fr. rt. 1. सह्; according<BR>to Sāy. fr. rt. सच्), Ved. overpowering, destroying;<BR>honouring, obeying; to be honoured; (Sāy. = स-<BR>चमान, Ṛg-veda VIII. 70, 8; = सचनीय-शील,<BR>VIII. 22, 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्षत्रम्
सक्षत्रम् स-क्षत्रम्, ind. suitably to the<BR>state of a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्षित्
सक्षित् स-क्षित्, त्, त्, त् (see 2. क्षित्), Ved.<BR>dwelling along with, associated together, going to-<BR>gether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखड्ग
सखड्ग स-खड्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, armed with a<BR>sword, sword in hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखि
सखि सखि, आ, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 136. fr. स for समान + rt. ख्या; according<BR>to others fr. 4. स and rt. 2. क्षि, and meaning<BR>‘living together’), a friend, (किं-स्˚, a bad friend);<BR>an associate, companion; [cf. Lat. socius.]<BR>—सखि-<BR>ता, f. or सखि-त्व, अम्, n. friendship, intimacy.<BR>—सखि-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has been<BR>formerly a friend; (अम्), n. the being formerly a<BR>friend.<BR>—सखि-वत्, ind. like a friend, as a friend.<BR>—सखि-विग्रह, अस्, m. war of friends, civil war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सख
सख, अस्, m. a friend, (frequently used at the<BR>end of comps. for सखि above; cf. नर-स्˚, व-<BR>सन्त-स्˚); the tree Mimosa Catechu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखी
सखी, f. a female friend or companion, a woman's<BR>confidante, (कु-सखी, a bad female friend.)<BR>—स-<BR>खी-कदम्बक, अम्, n. a number of female friends.<BR>—सखी-गण, अस्, m. a number of female friends.<BR>—सखीगण-समावृत, अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded<BR>by a company of female friends.<BR>—सखी-जन, अस्,<BR>m. a female friend, confidante.<BR>—सखी-सहित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, attended by female friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखीय
सखीय, Nom. P. सखीयति, &c., to wish for a<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखीयत्
सखीयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. desiring friends,<BR>desirous of friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सख्य|सख्यं|सख्यः
सख्य, अम्, n. friendship, intimacy; equality;<BR>(अस्), m. a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखेद
सखेद स-खेद, अस्, आ, अम्, having grief or<BR>sorrow; (अम्), ind. with grief, sorrowfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखेलम्
सखेलम् स-खेलम्, ind. with a gentle<BR>motion, moving gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्
सग् सग्, cl. 1. P. सगति, ससाग, असगीत्,<BR>सगितुम्, to cover: Caus. सगयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cause to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगजारोह
सगजारोह स-गजारोह, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by an elephant-rider, attended by men riding<BR>on elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगण|सगणः
सगण स-गण, अस्, आ, अम्, having troops or<BR>flocks, accompanied by a troop, attended by a body<BR>of followers; attended or accompanied by (with<BR>inst.); (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगद्गदम्
सगद्गदम् स-गद्गदम्, ind. with stammer-<BR>ing, in a faltering voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगन्ध|सगंध|सगन्धः
सगन्ध स-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>smell, odoriferous, fragrant, sweet-smelling; (अस्),<BR>m. a relation, kinsman, co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगन्धर्व
सगन्धर्व स-गन्धर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, together<BR>with the Gandharvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर|सगरः
सगर स-गर, अस्, आ, अम्, having poison,<BR>poisonous; (अस्), m. the ocean, sea (Ved., enumerated<BR>among the अन्तरिक्ष-नामानि in Naigh. I. 3;<BR>also अम्, n.); N. of a king of the solar race,<BR>sovereign of Ayodhyā (son of Bāhu; he is said to<BR>have been called Sagara, as born together with a<BR>poison given to his mother by the other wife of his<BR>father; he was father of Asamañja by Keśinī and<BR>of sixty thousand sons by Sumati; the latter were<BR>turned into a heap of ashes by the sage Kapila, see<BR>भगीरथ, and their funeral ceremonies could<BR>only be performed by the waters of Gaṅgā to be<BR>brought from heaven for the purpose of purifying<BR>their remains; this was finally accomplished by the<BR>devotion of Bhagīratha, q. v., who having led the<BR>river to the sea, called it Sāgara in honour of his<BR>ancestor: Sagara is described as having subdued the<BR>Śakas, Yavanas, and other barbarous tribes, and de-<BR>prived them of their social and religious position);<BR>N. of a particular Arhat.<BR>—सगरोपाख्यान (˚र-<BR>उप्˚), अम्, n. ‘the story of Sagara,’ N. of the fifteenth<BR>chapter of the Svarga-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ|सगर्भः
सगर्भ स-गर्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, pregnant; (अस्),<BR>m. ‘having the same womb,’ a brother by the same<BR>father and mother, a brother of whole blood (= स-<BR>होदर; cf. Gr. ἀδελφός (आ), f. a pregnant<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ्य|सगर्भ्यः
सगर्भ्य, अस्, m. a brother of whole blood,<BR>one by the same father and mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्व|सगर्व्व
सगर्व स-गर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, proud; joyful,<BR>glad, elated; (अम्), ind. haughtily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगुडशृङ्गक
सगुडशृङ्गक स-गुडशृङ्गक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>furnished with cupolas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगुण
सगुण स-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, having properties<BR>or qualities, &c.; possessing good qualities or attri-<BR>butes, virtuous; worldly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगूढम्
सगूढम् स-गूढम्, ind. secretly, privately,<BR>privily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगोत्र|सगोत्रं|सगोत्रः
सगोत्र स-गोत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, being of the<BR>same family or kin, related; (अस्), m. a kinsman of<BR>the same family; one sprung from a common an-<BR>cestor; one connected by funeral oblations of food<BR>and water; a distant kinsman; (अम्), n. a family,<BR>race, lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्धि|सग्धिः
सग्धि स-ग्धि, इस्, f. (contracted fr. सह-<BR>जग्धि, see जग्धि), eating together; (इस्, इस्, इ,),<BR>Ved. eating together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्मन्
सग्मन् सग्मन्, enumerated among the<BR>सङ्ग्राम-नामानि in Naigh. II. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सघ्
सघ् सघ्, cl. 5. P. सघ्नोति, ससाघ,<BR>सघिष्यति, असघीत् or असाघीत्, सघि-<BR>तुम्, to strike, hurt, injure, kill; to receive, accept;<BR>to support, bear [cf. rt. 1. सह्]: Caus. साघयति,<BR>-यितुम्, Aor. असीषघत् or असीसघत्: Desid.<BR>सिसघिषति: Intens. सासघ्यते, सासग्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सघन
सघन स-घन, अस्, आ, अम्, having density<BR>or solidity, dense, solid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क
सङ्क सङ्-क, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Sāy.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">Page1045-a+ 75</a>]<BR>fr. rt. कै with सम्; but according to Yāska, Nir.<BR>IX. 14, either fr. rt. सच् or fr. सङ्-कॄ), sounding<BR>together, shouting; having assembled warriors; (in<BR>Naigh. II. 17. सङ्काः is enumerated among the<BR>सङ्ग्राम-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कट|संकट|सङ्कटः
सङ्कट सङ्-कट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. सम् + कट,<BR>q. v.), ‘having the hips close together,’ contracted,<BR>narrow, strait; impassable, impervious; crowded;<BR>(अस्), m. a proper N.; (आ), f. a particular goddess<BR>worshipped at Benares; a particular Yoginī, (seven<BR>others are named, viz. Maṅgalā, Piṅgalā, Dhanyā,<BR>Bhrāmarī, Bhadrikā, Ulkā, Siddhi); (अम्), n. a<BR>narrow passage, strait, defile, pass; a strait, difficulty,<BR>trouble, (प्राण-सङ्कट, risk of life.)<BR>—सङ्क-<BR>टाक्ष (˚ट-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, ‘having contracted<BR>eyes,’ winking, leering; (अस्), m. the tree Grislea<BR>Tomentosa (= धव).<BR>—सङ्कटापन्न (˚ट-<BR>आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, beset with difficulties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथ्|संकथ्
सङ्कथ् सङ्-कथ् (सम्-कथ्), cl. 10. P. -क-<BR>थयति, -यितुम्, to relate or narrate fully, tell, com-<BR>municate, inform; to explain; to speak about or of<BR>(with acc.); to converse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथन|संकथन|संकथनं|सङ्कथनं
सङ्-कथन, अम्, n. the act of narrating fully,<BR>narration, relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथा|संकथा
सङ्-कथा, f. conversation, discourse, talking to-<BR>gether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथित|संकथित
सङ्-कथित, अस्, आ, अम्, related, narrated, com-<BR>municated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथ्यमान
सङ्-कथ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being told or related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कन्|संकन्
सङ्कन् सङ्-कन् (सम्-कन्, cf. 2. का, rt. कै),<BR>cl. 1. P. -कनति, &c. (apparently only used in the<BR>participle below), Ved. to be satisfied or pleased, &c.;<BR>[cf. rt. चक्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चकान|संचकान
सञ्-चकान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. satisfied with,<BR>pleased; praised, glorified, (Sāy. = स्तूयमान, as if<BR>fr. rt. कै with सम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कम्प्|संकम्प्
सङ्कम्प् सङ्-कम्प् (सम्-कम्प्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-कम्पते, -कम्पितुम्, to shake about, quake,<BR>tremble: Caus. -कम्पयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>shake or tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कर|संकर|संकरः|सङ्करः
