सङ्ख्या सङ्-ख्या (सम्-ख्या), cl. 2. P. (in<BR>some tenses also A., see rt. ख्या, p. 277), -ख्याति,<BR>-ख्यातुम्, to appear along with, be connected with<BR>(Ved.); to reckon or count up, sum up, enumerate,<BR>calculate; Caus. -ख्यापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>be looked at or observed (Ved.); to cause to reckon<BR>up, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्य|संख्य|संख्यं|सङ्ख्यं
सङ्-ख्य, अम्, n. conflict, battle, war, (in Naigh.<BR>II. 17. enumerated among the सङ्ग्राम-नामानि);<BR>(अस्), m. a proper N.; (आ), f. reckoning up, num-<BR>bering, numeration, calculation; an account, sum; a<BR>number, numeral; deliberation, reasoning, reflection;<BR>reason, intellect, understanding; manner; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), = सङ्ख्येय, to be reckoned up or counted.<BR>—सङ्ख्य-ता, f. or सङ्ख्य-त्व, अम्, n. nume-<BR>rableness, numeration.<BR>—सङ्ख्या-तस्, ind. from a<BR>number.<BR>—सङ्ख्यातिग (˚या-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘going beyond numeration,’ innumerable.<BR>—सङ्-<BR>ख्या-मात्र, अम्, n. the amount of; mere nume-<BR>ration.<BR>—सङ्ख्या-योग, see under योग. — 1. सङ्-<BR>ख्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having number, possessed of<BR>number, numbered; possessing reason or intellect,<BR>intelligent, discriminating; (आन्), m. a learned<BR>Brāhman, Paṇḍit, teacher.<BR>—२. सङ्ख्या-वत्, ind.<BR>like number.<BR>—सङ्ख्या-वाचक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">Page1047-b+ 79</a>]<BR>expressive of number; (अस्), m. a numeral.<BR>—सङ्-<BR>ख्या-समापन, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यक|संख्यक
सङ्ख्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, numbering, amounting<BR>to, composed of a certain number, (at the end of<BR>comps., e. g. सहस्र-सङ्ख्यक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>amounting to a thousand.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यात|संख्यात|सङ्ख्यातं
सङ्-ख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, reckoned up, enumerated,<BR>calculated; numbered, counted; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>riddle or enigma; (अम्), n. number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यान|संख्यान|संख्यानं|सङ्ख्यानं
सङ्-ख्यान, अम्, n. the act of reckoning up,<BR>numbering, numeration, calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्याय
सङ्-ख्याय, ind. having reckoned up, having<BR>counted or numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्येय|संख्येय|सङ्ख्येयं
सङ्-ख्येय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be reckoned or<BR>counted up, numerable, calculable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग|संग|संगः|सङ्गः
सङ्ग सङ्-ग, सङ्-गथ, &c. See below<BR>and under rt. 1. सञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गणिका|संगणिका
सङ्गणिका सङ्गणिका, f. (fr. rt. गण् with<BR>सम्), incomparable or unequalled discourse (=<BR>अप्रतिरूप-कथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गम्|संगम्
सङ्गम् सङ्-गम् (सम्-गम्), cl. 1. A. -गच्-<BR>छते (Pāṇ. I. 3, 29; but with an object P. -गच्छति;<BR>in Hari-vaṃśa 14, 787. सम-गच्छतु occurs for<BR>सङ्-गच्छतु, Perf. -जग्मे; Ved. forms &c.<BR>-गमेमहि, -गमामहै, -अजग्मिरन्, -अगत,<BR>-अगन्महि, -अगस्महि or -अगंस्महि, -ग्मि-<BR>षीय, -गसीष्ट or -गंसीष्ट, -गंस्यते, &c.,<BR>see rt. 1. गम्, cf. Pāṇ. I. 2, 13, VII. 2. 58), -गन्-<BR>तुम्, to go together, come together, assemble, meet,<BR>encounter (either in a friendly or hostile manner),<BR>come into collision; to meet with, to ally or connect<BR>one's self with; to have sexual intercourse with; to<BR>meet harmoniously, harmonize, agree, be suitable or<BR>fit, correspond; to become contracted, shrink up; to<BR>go away, depart, die; to go to, attain (with acc.);<BR>to go to, visit (P.): Caus. -गमयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to go together, bring together, connect or unite<BR>with, endow or present with (with inst. of person and<BR>acc. of thing); to connect, combine; to lead any one<BR>to anything (with two acc.); to deliver or hand over<BR>to another (with loc.), transfer, bestow, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग|संग|संगः|सङ्गः
1. सङ्-ग, अस्, m. (for 2. सङ्ग see under rt.<BR>1. सञ्ज्), coming together, concurrence, meeting,<BR>encountering, conflict, war, battle, (in Naigh. II. 17.<BR>सङ्गे is enumerated among the सङ्ग्राम-नामा-<BR>नि); uniting, union, association, contact, touch, co-<BR>herence; intercourse, keeping company, intimacy,<BR>friendship, love; the confluence of rivers.<BR>—१. सङ्ग-<BR>विच्युति, इस्, f. dissolution of union, disunion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गत्|संगत्
सङ्-गत्, see Vopa-deva XXVI. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गत|संगत|सङ्गतं
सङ्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, come together, convened,<BR>met, encountered; joined, conjoined, united, associ-<BR>ated; united in wedlock; sexually united; assembled,<BR>collected, accumulated, mixed; fitted together, ap-<BR>posite, proper, seasonable, appropriate, applicable,<BR>adapted to, fitted for; in conjunction (as planets);<BR>contracted, shrunk up; (अस्), m., N. of a king<BR>(belonging to the Maurya dynasty); (अम्), n. com-<BR>ing together, union, meeting; alliance, association,<BR>intercourse, connection; friendship, acquaintance.<BR>—सङ्गत-गात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having contracted<BR>or shriveled limbs.<BR>—सङ्गत-सन्धि, इस्, m. a<BR>peace concluded after friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गति|संगति|संगतिः|सङ्गतिः
सङ्-गति, इस्, f. coming together, meeting, inter-<BR>view, union, junction, conjunction, mixture; associa-<BR>tion, intercourse, society; sexual intercourse; adapta-<BR>tion, fitness, appropriateness, applicability; going to,<BR>visiting, frequenting; meeting or coming to pass<BR>accidentally, chance, accident, (सङ्गत्या, by chance,<BR>haply); going to, visiting, frequenting; becoming<BR>acquainted, knowledge, questioning for further in-<BR>formation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

