सञ्छाद्यमान
सञ्-छाद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being entirely<BR>covered over or concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छद्|संछद्
सञ्छद् 2. सञ्-छद् or सञ्-छन्द् (सम्-छ्˚;<BR>see rt. 3. छद्), Caus. -छदयति, -छन्दयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to gratify with anything (inst.), present, offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छन्द्यमान
सञ्-छन्द्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being presented<BR>or offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छिद्|संछिद्
सञ्छिद् सञ्-छिद् (सम्-छ्˚), cl. 7. P. A.<BR>-छिनत्ति, -छिन्त्ते, -छेत्तुम्, to cut to pieces; to<BR>cut off, hack off, chop off; to cut through, penetrate,<BR>pierce, split; to cut away, destroy, remove, resolve<BR>(a doubt &c.); to decide, settle, answer (a question<BR>&c.): Pass. -छिद्यते, to be cut to pieces; to be<BR>cut off, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छिद्य
सञ्-छिद्य, ind. having cut to pieces; having<BR>cut away, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छिद्यत्
सञ्-छिद्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, mutually cutting off<BR>or cutting to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छिद्यमान
सञ्-छिद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being cut to pieces,<BR>being hacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छिन्न|संछिन्न
सञ्-छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, cut to pieces, cut off;<BR>dissipated, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्|संज्
सञ्ज् 1. सञ्ज् (= rts. सञ्च्, 1. सज्ज्), cl. 1.<BR>P. सञ्जति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्|संज्
सञ्ज् 2. सञ्ज् (sometimes written सज्ज्,<BR>which appears to be a form of the rt.<BR>developed out of सज्जते, ep. for Pass. सज्यते), cl.<BR>1. P. सजति (ep. also सज्जति), ससञ्ज (ep. also<BR>ससज्ज), सङ्क्ष्यति, असाङ्क्षीत्, सङ्क्तुम्, to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">Page1051-a+ 76</a>]<BR>cling or adhere to, stick; to fasten: Pass. सज्यते<BR>(ep. also सज्जते), to be attached, become attached<BR>or connected, adhere, cling, stick: Caus. सञ्जयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अससञ्जत्, to cause to stick or cling<BR>to; to cause to be connected or have intercourse<BR>with: Desid. सिसङ्क्षति: Intens. सासज्यते, सा-<BR>सङ्क्ति; [cf. Gr. σάττω, σαγή, σάγμα, σακτός,<BR>σάκτωρ, (probably) σάκκος, σάκτας.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्त|सक्तः
सक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, clung, stuck or attached to,<BR>joined or connected with, in contact with, near at<BR>hand, impending; addicted or devoted to, fond of,<BR>intent on; diligent, attentive; belonging or related<BR>to, concerning; hindered, impeded, (अ-सक्तम्, ind.<BR>uninterruptedly.)<BR>—सक्त-वैर, अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>stant in enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्ति|सक्तिः
सक्ति, इस्, f. clinging to, attachment, contact,<BR>union, junction, cohesion, addiction to, devotion.<BR>—सक्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having attachment,<BR>attached or addicted to, fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग|संग|संगः|सङ्गः
2. सङ्ग, अस्, m. (for 1. सङ्-ग see under सङ्-<BR>गम्), clinging to, adhering to, attachment, addiction<BR>or devotion to, fondness, propensity for, worldly or<BR>selfish attachment, affection, desire, wish, cupidity.<BR>—सङ्ग-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, free from attachment,<BR>indifferent, unworldly, stoical.<BR>—सङ्ग-वर्जित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, free from worldly attachments or affections,<BR>unwordly.<BR>—२. सङ्ग-विच्युति, इस्, f. separation from<BR>wordly affection, dissolution of wordly attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गिन्|संगिन्
2. सङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ (for 1. see under सङ्-गम्),<BR>full of attachment or devotion, attached, devoted,<BR>addicted to, fond of, intent on, connected with; full<BR>of affection or desire, desirous; libidinous, lustful;<BR>continuous, uninterrupted, (Kirāt. XIV. 59.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जन|संजन
सञ्जन, अम्, n. the act of clinging, adhering,<BR>sticking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जतर
सञ्जतर सञ्जतर, अम्, n., N. of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जन्|संजन्
सञ्जन् सञ्-जन् (सम्-ज्˚), cl. 4. A. -जायते,<BR>-जनितुम्, to be born or produced together with;<BR>to be born, arise, grow, be produced, come into<BR>existence, take place, appear, happen; to become,<BR>be; to elapse, pass (as time); to bring forth: Caus.<BR>-जनयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be born, bring forth,<BR>generate, beget, produce, create, cause, form, make.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज|संज|संजः|सञ्जः
सञ्-ज, अस्, m. ‘universal producer,’ epithet of<BR>Brahmā; of Śiva; (आ), f. a she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जनन|संजनन
सञ्-जनन, अम्, n. the act of begetting, causing,<BR>producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जनयत्
सञ्-जनयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, begetting, producing,<BR>causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जनित|संजनित
सञ्-जनित, अस्, आ, अम्, produced, caused, created.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जात|संजात
सञ्-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born, produced, grown, ap-<BR>peared, arisen, become, aroused (often at the begin-<BR>ning of comps. in the sense ‘becoming,’ ‘growing,’<BR>‘grown’); elapsed, passed (as time).<BR>—सञ्जात-<BR>कोप, अस्, आ, अम्, growing angry, becoming enraged.<BR>—सञ्जात-कौतुक, अस्, आ, अम्, having the curiosity<BR>roused, becoming curious.<BR>—सञ्जात-निर्वेद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, grown despondent.<BR>—सञ्जात-विश्रम्भ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having confidence excited, becoming confi-<BR>dent.<BR>—सञ्जातेर्ष्य (˚त-ईर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, becom-<BR>ing envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जप्|संजप्
सञ्जप् सञ्-जप् (सम्-ज्˚), cl. 1. P. -जपति,<BR>-जपितुम्, to whisper or talk about, speak about, tell<BR>of, report, communicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

