सट|सटं
सट सट, अम्, आ, n. f. (= जटा, शटा; ac-<BR>cording to some also अस्, m.), an ascetic's matted or<BR>clotted hair, the hair collected into a loose braid and<BR>twisted forwards upon the forehead, a braid of hair<BR>(in general); the mane (of a lion &c.); the bristles<BR>(of a boar); a crest, (in these last three senses usually<BR>आ, f.)<BR>—सटाङ्क (˚टा-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘mane-marked,’<BR>a lion.<BR>—सटा-पाटल, अस्, m. the red mane (of a<BR>lion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटङ्कार|सटंकार
