सण्डिश सण्डिश, अस्, m. (= सन्-दंश), a<BR>pair of tongs or nippers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्डी
सण्डी सण्-डी (सम्-डी), cl. 1. 4. A. -डयते,<BR>-डीयते, -डयितुम्, to fly together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्डीन|संडीन|संडीनं|सण्डीनं
सण्-डीन, अम्, n. flying together, one of the<BR>modes of flight attributed to birds; alighting from a<BR>flight, perching (as a bird).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्|सन्त्|संत्
सत् सत्, अन्, अती, अत् (Pres. part. of rt. 1. अस्),<BR>being, existing; real, essential, true; good, virtuous;<BR>right, proper; excellent, best; handsome, beautiful;<BR>venerable, respectable; wise, learned; firm, steady;<BR>(ई), f. a virtuous wife, &c., (see p. 1053); (सत्), n.<BR>that which really is, entity or existence, essence, the<BR>true being, the really existent, the self-existent or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1052-b" target="_blank">Page1052-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Universal Spirit, Brahma; that which is good or real<BR>or true, reality, truth; water, (in Naigh. 1. 12. सत्<BR>is enumerated among the उदक-नामानि; cf. स-<BR>तीन); (सत्), ind. well, rightly, fitly; [cf. Gr. ὤν<BR>(Ion. ἐών for ἐσών); Lat. sens, sent-is, in prœ-sens,<BR>ab-sens; Lith. Nom. m. esañs, f. esanti.]<BR>—सच्-<BR>चरित or सच्-चरित्र, अम्, n. good conduct, good<BR>behaviour; (अस्, आ, अम्), well-conducted, well-behaved,<BR>virtuous, honest, upright.<BR>—सच्चरित-मीमांसा, f.,<BR>N. of a work by Vidyā-nivāsa-bhaṭṭācārya.<BR>—सच्-<BR>चित्, त्, n. ‘existence and thought,’ epithet of Brahma<BR>or the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—सच्-चिद्-अंश, अस्, m. a<BR>portion of existence and thought.<BR>—सच्-चिद्-आत्मन्,<BR>आ, m. the soul which consists of entity (or essence)<BR>and thought.<BR>—सच्-चिद्-आनन्द, अम्, n. ‘existence<BR>(or entity), thought (or knowledge), and joy,’ epithet<BR>of Brahma or the Supreme Spirit; of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सच्-<BR>चिद्-आनन्द-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of existence,<BR>thought, and joy.<BR>—सच्चिदानन्द-स्तोत्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a hymn addressed to Gaṇeśa (extracted from the<BR>Sanatkumāra-saṃhitā).<BR>—सच्-छील (सत्-शी˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of a virtuous disposition, benevolent.<BR>—सच्-<BR>छूद्र (सत्-शू˚), अस्, m. a good Śūdra, a Śūdra<BR>who has gone through the ceremonies customary in<BR>some places even for men of the lower caste.<BR>—२. सज्-<BR>जन, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. सज्जन see under rt. 2. सज्ज्,<BR>p. 1049), well-born, of good family, respectable,<BR>reputable, virtuous, good; (अस्), m. a good man,<BR>virtuous man; a proper N.<BR>—सज्जन-गर्हित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, despised by the virtuous.<BR>—सज्जन-वल्-<BR>लभ, ‘friend of the good,’ N. of a work.<BR>—सज्-<BR>जनेष्ट (˚न-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, desired or chosen<BR>by the good.<BR>—सज्जनैकवसति (˚न-एक्˚), इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, residing only in the good.<BR>—सती-ता, &c., see<BR>under सती, p. 1055.<BR>—सत्-कदम्ब, अस्, m. ‘good<BR>Kadamba,’ a species of Kadamba, (Nauclea Cordi-<BR>folia.)<BR>—सत्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, acting well; treat-<BR>ing well or kindly; (ता), m. epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सत्-कर्मन्, अ, n. a good or virtuous act, pious<BR>deed; virtue, piety; hospitality; funeral obsequies;<BR>expiation.<BR>—सत्-कवि-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—सत्-काञ्चनार, अस्, m. ‘good mountain ebony,’<BR>a sort of ebony (= रक्त-काञ्चन).<BR>—सत्-काण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. a hawk, kite.<BR>—सत्-कार, अस्, m. kind action,<BR>kind treatment, hospitable treatment or reception,<BR>hospitality; reverence, respect; care, attention; a<BR>meal; a festival, religious observance.<BR>—सत्कारार्ह<BR>(˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of hospitable treatment.<BR>—सत्-कुल, अम्, n. a good family, noble family.<BR>—सत्-कुलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a good<BR>family, born of a noble family, well-born, nobly<BR>descended.<BR>—सत्कुलोद्भव (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sprung from a noble family.<BR>—सत्-कृ, cl. 8. P. A.<BR>-करोति, -कुरुते, &c., to do well or rightly, treat<BR>well or kindly, treat with respect, receive hospitably,<BR>welcome; to honour, worship; to adorn: Caus.<BR>-कारयति, &c., -यितुम्, to cause to be treated with<BR>respect or reverence, show reverence, pay respect.<BR>—सत्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done well, acted rightly or<BR>properly; treated with respect or hospitality; respected,<BR>revered, honoured; worshipped, adored, welcomed,<BR>saluted; entertained; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva;<BR>(अम्), n. virtue; respect; hospitality.<BR>—सत्-कृति,<BR>इस्, f. doing good, acting properly, virtue, morality;<BR>treating with respect, hospitality.<BR>—सत्-कृत्य, ind.<BR>having treated with respect, &c., having hospitably<BR>entertained.<BR>—सत्-क्रिया, f. a good action, virtuous<BR>action, doing good, charity, virtue; respectful treat-<BR>ment, salutation, welcome, courtesy, worship, homage,<BR>hospitality; any purificatory ceremony; funeral or<BR>obsequial ceremonies.<BR>—सत्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>good or right; most virtuous; excellent, best; very<BR>venerable or respectable.<BR>—सत्-ता, f. existence, entity,<BR>being, reality; a particular Jāti (in phil.); goodness,<BR>excellence, see सत्-त्व below.<BR>—सत्ता-मात्र, अम्,<BR>n. mere entity or existence.<BR>—सत्ता-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>endowed with existence, possessing reality.<BR>—सत्ता-<BR>वाप्य (˚ता-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, included in (the notion<BR>of) existence.<BR>—सत्-त्व, अम्, n. being, existence,<BR>(ईश्वर-सत्त्व, the existence of a Supreme Being),<BR>entity, essence, nature, true essence, life, the principle<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1052-c" target="_blank">Page1052-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of being, breath, spirit, mind, sense, consciousness;<BR>an embryo; substance, thing, wealth; elementary<BR>substance (as earth, air, fire, &c.); anything of which<BR>a property may be predicated; any living or sentient<BR>being, animal, beast, evil being, demon, spirit, ghost,<BR>goblin, monster, (in these senses also अस्, m.); a<BR>substantive, noun; goodness, virtue, excellence; truth,<BR>certainty, reality; strength, energy, vigour, power,<BR>courage, self-command, sound sense, good sense,<BR>wisdom; the quality of purity or goodness (regarded<BR>in philosophy as the highest of the three Guṇas<BR>which are supposed to constitute the external world,<BR>the other two being रजस् and तमस्, see गुण;<BR>the quality of सत्त्व renders a person in whom it<BR>predominates chaste, true, honest, wise, &c., and a<BR>thing pure, clean, &c.); any natural property, quality,<BR>characteristic, disposition; (अस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—सत्त्व-कषाय, अस्, m. one of the<BR>signs of decay (with Buddhists, see कषाय).<BR>—सत्-<BR>त्व-गुण, अस्, m. the quality of purity or goodness,<BR>(see above.)<BR>—सत्त्वगुणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having the<BR>above quality predominant.<BR>—सत्त्व-ता, f. purity,<BR>goodness, the existence of the Sattva-guṇa.<BR>—सत्त्व-<BR>प्रधान, अस्, आ, अम्, having the quality of good-<BR>ness predominant.<BR>—सत्त्वम्-एजय, अस्, आ, अम्, ter-<BR>rifying living beings, making animals tremble.<BR>—सत्-<BR>त्व-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, endowed with life, living,<BR>existent, a living being; endowed with or possessed<BR>of the true essence; endowed with strength, mag-<BR>nanimous, endowed with the quality of goodness,<BR>pure, virtuous.<BR>—सत्त्व-विप्लव, अस्, m. loss of con-<BR>sciousness.<BR>—सत्त्व-विहित, अस्, आ, अम्, effected or<BR>caused by nature, natural; caused by goodness;<BR>virtuous, upright.<BR>—सत्त्व-वृत्ति, इस्, f. the con-<BR>dition or quality of goodness, &c.<BR>—सत्त्व-शील, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of a virtuous disposition, disposed to what is<BR>right and good.<BR>—सत्त्व-संशुद्धि, इस्, f. purity<BR>of nature or disposition.<BR>—सत्त्व-समाविष्ट, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, filled or thoroughly penetrated by the<BR>quality of goodness.<BR>—सत्त्व-सम्पन्न, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, endowed with the quality of goodness, good,<BR>excellent; equable, even-minded.<BR>—सत्त्व-सम्-<BR>प्लव, अस्, m. universal destruction of beings; loss<BR>of vigour.<BR>—सत्त्व-सार, अस्, m. essence of strength;<BR>a most powerful person.<BR>—सत्त्व-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being in the nature (of anything); inherent in<BR>animals; animate; being in the quality of good-<BR>ness, excellent, holy, pure.<BR>—सत्त्वानुरूप (˚व-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, according to nature, in conformity<BR>with natural character.<BR>—सत्त्वोत्साह (˚व-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. natural energy; (औ), m. du. courage and energy.<BR>—सत्त्वोत्साह-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, endowed with<BR>courage and energy.<BR>—सत्त्वोद्रिक्त (˚व-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one in whom the quality of goodness pre-<BR>dominates.<BR>—सत्त्वोद्रेक (˚व-उद्˚), अस्, m. excess<BR>or predominance of the quality of goodness, super-<BR>abundance of energy or wisdom.<BR>—सत्-पति, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a good lord; the lord of the good, lord of real<BR>men, lord of heroes; epithet of Indra.<BR>—सत्-पत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. the new leaf of a water-lily.<BR>—सत्-पथ,<BR>अस्, m. a good road; good course of life, correct or<BR>virtuous conduct; orthodox doctrine.<BR>—सत्-परि-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, m. acceptance (of gifts) from a proper<BR>person.<BR>—सत्-पशु, उस्, m. a good or suitable animal,<BR>a victim fit for a sacrifice.<BR>—सत्-पात्र, अम्, n. a<BR>proper object of presents or honours, a worthy or<BR>virtuous person.<BR>—सत्पात्र-वर्ष, अस्, m. raining<BR>down or bestowing favours on worthy objects, judi-<BR>cious liberality.<BR>—सत्पात्र-वर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, bounti-<BR>ful to worthy objects.<BR>—सत्-पुत्र, अस्, m. a virtuous<BR>son; a son who performs all the prescribed rites in<BR>honour of his ancestors.<BR>—सत्-पुरुष, अस्, m. a<BR>good or virtuous man, worthy man.<BR>—सत्-पुष्प,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having good flowers.<BR>—सत्-प्रतिपक्ष,<BR>अस्, m. (in logic) a counterbalanced reason or one<BR>along with which there exists another equally good<BR>on the opposite side (as sound is eternal because it<BR>is audible, sound is non-eternal because it is a pro-<BR>duct); contrariety of argument, existence of oppo-<BR>site premises proving the existence or non-existence<BR>of a thing.<BR>—सत्प्रतिपक्षि-ता, f. the condition of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-a" target="_blank">Page1053-a+ 81</a>]<BR>containing two opposite sets of premises.<BR>—सत्प्र-<BR>तिपक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, containing opposite reasons or<BR>arguments.<BR>—सत्-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having good<BR>fruit; (अस्), m. the pomegranate or any tree produc-<BR>ing good fruit.<BR>—सत्-फलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, producing<BR>good fruits.<BR>—सत्-संसर्ग, अस्, m. association<BR>with the good, the society of the good.<BR>—सत्-सङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. association with the good.<BR>—सत्-सन्निधान,<BR>अम्, n. the proximity of the good, association or in-<BR>tercourse with the good or wise.<BR>—सत्-समागम,<BR>अस्, m. association with the good.<BR>—सत्-सम्प्र-<BR>योग, अस्, m. right application.<BR>—सत्-सहाय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having good or virtuous friends.<BR>—सत्-सार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having good sap or essence; (अस्), m. a<BR>kind of tree; a painter; a poet.<BR>—सत्-सुखानु-<BR>भव (˚ख-अन्˚), अस्, m. fruition of real happiness;<BR>N. of a short treatise on Vedānta subjects by Icchā-<BR>rāma-svāmin.<BR>—सद्-अञ्जन, अम्, n. good colly-<BR>rium; calx of brass.<BR>—सद्-अश्व, अस्, m. a good<BR>horse; ‘having a good horse,’ N. of a son of Sa-<BR>mara.<BR>—सद्-अश्व-वत्, ind. like a good horse.<BR>—सद्-असत्, अन्, अती, अत्, being and not being,<BR>existent and non-existent, real and unreal, true and<BR>false, perceptible and non-perceptible; good and bad,<BR>virtuous and wicked; (अती), n. du. existence and<BR>non-existence, entity and non-entity, truth and false-<BR>hood, good and evil.<BR>—सद्-असद्-आत्मक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, having the nature of entity and non-entity,<BR>consisting of existent and non-existent, real and un-<BR>real, existing everywhere essentially though not ob-<BR>viously.<BR>—सद्-असद्-विवेक, अस्, m. discrimination<BR>between true and false or between good and bad.<BR>—सद्-असद्-व्यक्ति-हेतु, उस्, m. the cause of the<BR>discrimination between good and bad or between<BR>true and false.<BR>—सद्-अस्थि-माला, f. ‘good necklace<BR>of bones,’ N. of a commentary by Vaidya-nātha on<BR>the Laghu-śabdendu-śekhara.<BR>—सद्-आचार, अस्, m.<BR>moral or virtuous conduct, good manners, approved<BR>usage, traditionary observance, immemorial custom<BR>(especially as preserved in the land lying between<BR>the Sarasvatī and Dṛṣadvatī rivers, Manu II. 18).<BR>—सदाचार-चन्द्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘moon-<BR>rise of good manners,’ N. of a work.<BR>—सदाचार-<BR>प्रकरण, अम्, n., N. of a short treatise on the<BR>duties of ascetics by Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—सदाचार-वत्,<BR>आन्, m. one who has or observes approved usages.<BR>—सद्-आत्मन्, आ, आ, अ, being of a good essence or<BR>nature, good, virtuous.<BR>—१. सद्-आश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(for 2. सदाश्रित see under सदा), having recourse<BR>or attaching one's self to the virtuous, belonging to the<BR>good, virtuous.<BR>—सद्-उत्तर, अम्, n. a proper answer,<BR>good reply.<BR>—सद्-गति, इस्, f. good or happy state,<BR>felicity, fortune, good conduct.<BR>—सद्-गुण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having good qualities, good, pure, virtuous,<BR>excellent, eminent.<BR>—सद्-धन, अम्, n. good<BR>wealth, property.<BR>—सद्धेतु, उस्, m. (i. e. सत्-हे˚),<BR>the existence of cause and effect.<BR>—सद्-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. the quality of being, actual existence, reality,<BR>being, entity; the quality of goodness; good nature<BR>or disposition; goodness, amiability, kindly feeling.<BR>—सद्भाव-श्री, ईस्, f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—सद्-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being good, who or what is real or true.<BR>—सद्-युवती, f. a good young woman, virtuous<BR>maiden.<BR>—सद्-वंश, अस्, आ, अम्, of a good family<BR>or race, of high birth.<BR>—सद्-वचस्, अस्, n. agree-<BR>able speech.<BR>—सद्-वती, f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Pulastya and wife of Agni.<BR>—सद्-वसथ, अस्, m.<BR>a village.<BR>—सद्-वस्तु, उ, n. an excellent work.<BR>—सद्-वादित, अस्, आ, अम्, well-spoken.<BR>—सद्-<BR>विगर्हित, अस्, आ, अम्, censured by the good,<BR>blamed by the benevolent.<BR>—सद्-विद्या, f. good<BR>learning.<BR>—सद्-वियोग, अस्, m. separation from the<BR>good.<BR>—सद्-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well-behaved, well-<BR>conducted, amiable; virtuous, moral; well-rounded,<BR>beautifully circular; (अम्), n. good conduct, virtuous<BR>conduct, amiable character or disposition.<BR>—सद्-<BR>वृत्तान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having good or beautiful<BR>stories.<BR>—सद्-वृत्ति, इस्, f. good course of conduct,<BR>good state.<BR>—सद्वृत्ति-भाज्, क्, क्, क् or सद्वृत्ति-<BR>विशिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing good habits, having<BR>a good character.<BR>—सन्-निमित्त, अम्, n. a good<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">Page1053-b+ 81</a>]<BR>cause; the cause of the good, (सन्-निमित्ते, in a<BR>good cause; for the sake of the good.)<BR>—सन्-नि-<BR>सर्ग, अस्, m. good nature, kindness.<BR>—सन्-मा-<BR>तुर, अस्, m. ‘having a good mother,’ the son of a<BR>virtuous mother.<BR>—सन्-मात्र, अस्, m. ‘consisting<BR>of mere existence,’ epithet of Ātman.<BR>—सन्-मान,<BR>अम्, n. respect for the good; the respect or esteem<BR>of the good.<BR>—सन्-मार्ग, अस्, m. a virtuous<BR>way, good or virtuous conduct.<BR>—सन्मार्गालोकन<BR>(˚ग-आल्˚), अम्, n. the seeing or following of good<BR>paths (of morality &c.).<BR>—सन्-मित्र, अम्, n. a<BR>good friend, real or faithful friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सती
सती, f. (fem. of सत्), a virtuous wife (especially<BR>applied in later use to the Suttee or faithful wife who<BR>burns herself with her husband's corpse); a female<BR>ascetic; N. of the goddess Durgā or Umā (some-<BR>times described as Truth personified or as daughter<BR>of Dakṣa and wife of Bhava [Śiva], and sometimes<BR>represented as putting an end to herself by Yoga, or<BR>at a later period destroying herself on the funeral<BR>pyre of her husband; also represented as one of<BR>the wives of Aṅgiras); N. of the mother of Nāgeśa;<BR>a fragrant earth (commonly called Surāt earth); a<BR>species of the Prati-ṣṭhā metre.<BR>—सती-ता, f. or<BR>सती-त्व, अम्, n. virtuousness, purity, chastity, fidelity<BR>(especially as evinced by ascending the husband's<BR>funeral pile).<BR>—सती-देह-त्याग, अस्, m. ‘Satī's aban-<BR>donment of the body,’ N. of the forty-third chapter of<BR>the Gaṇeśa-khaṇḍa of the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—सती-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of a virtuous woman.<BR>—सतीश्वर-लिङ्ग (˚ती-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—सती-सरस्, अस्, n., N. of a lake in Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीक
सतीक, अम्, n., Ved. water (= उदक, Naigh. I. 12).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीन|सतीनः
सतीन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. real, essential, mighty,<BR>powerful; (अस्), m. a bamboo; pease, pulse or a<BR>particular kind of it, (see सतील); (अम्), n., Ved.<BR>water (= उदक, Naigh. 1. 12; Sāy. सतीन =<BR>वृष्ट्य्-उदक, cf. सत्).<BR>—सतीन-कङ्कत, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. a kind of venomous aquatic animal.<BR>—स-<BR>तीन-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved., (Sāy.) eager to (shed)<BR>rain-water.<BR>—सतीन-सत्वन्, आ, m., Ved. ‘having<BR>real or mighty power,’ epithet of Indra; (Sāy.) a<BR>sender of water (= उदकस्य सादयितृ, गम-<BR>यितृ, Ṛg-veda I. 100, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीनक|सतीनकः
सतीनक, अस्, m. pease or pulse, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतील|सतीलः
सतील, अस्, m. a bamboo; air, wind; (अस्, आ), m.<BR>f. pease, pulse or a particular kind (called Teorā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीलक|सतीलकः
सतीलक, अस्, m. pease; [cf. सातीलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्य|सत्यं|सत्यः
सत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, true, real, genuine, sincere,<BR>honest, truthful, faithful, pure, virtuous, good, (सत्-<BR>यं कृ, to make true, make good, ratify, fulfil);<BR>fulfilled, realized; (अस्), m. the uppermost of the<BR>seven Lokas or worlds (the abode of Brahmā and<BR>heaven of truth, see लोक); the Aśvattha tree; epithet<BR>of Rāma-candra; of Viṣṇu; of a deity presiding<BR>over the Nāndī-mukha Śrāddha; N. of the author<BR>of the Horā-śāstra; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>deities; (आ), f. truth, sincerity, veracity; epithet of<BR>Sītā (wife of Rāma); of Satya-vatī (mother of<BR>Vyāsa); = सत्य-भामा, col. 3; N. of the goddess<BR>Durgā; (अम्), n. truth; sincerity, reality, goodness,<BR>the quality of goodness or purity, knowledge; demon-<BR>strated truth or conclusion, dogma; a solemn asseve-<BR>ration, promise, oath; water (= उदक, Naigh. 1.<BR>12); the first of the four Yugas or ages (i. e. the<BR>best or golden age as the age of general virtue and<BR>purity, comprising 1,728,000 years of men; it is<BR>also called कृत, q. v.); (अम्), ind. truly, indeed,<BR>verily, necessarily, (Sāy. = अवश्यम्); yes; a par-<BR>ticle of asseveration and interrogation; [cf. Gr.<BR>ἐτεός.]<BR>—सत्य-कर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king.<BR>—सत्य-काम, अस्, m. a lover of truth; a proper<BR>N.<BR>—सत्य-कारुण्य-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing<BR>truth and tenderness and the Veda.<BR>—सत्य-केतु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—सत्यङ्-कार, अस्, m. making<BR>true or good, ratification of a contract or bargain;<BR>something given in advance as an earnest or security<BR>for the performance of a contract, earnest-money,<BR>pledge.<BR>—सत्यङ्कार-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, given or<BR>deposited in order to ratify a bargain.<BR>—सत्य-जित्,<BR>त्, m. ‘truth-conqueror’ or ‘truly conquering,’ N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-c" target="_blank">Page1053-c+ 81</a>]<BR>a king.<BR>—सत्य-तपस्, आस्, m. ‘practising true<BR>penance,’ N. of a Muni (who was once a hunter,<BR>but after performing severe austerities obtained as a<BR>boon from Durvāsas that he should become a great<BR>sage and saint).<BR>—सत्य-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most<BR>true, quite true.<BR>—सत्य-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more<BR>true, very true.<BR>—सत्य-ता, f. or सत्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. trueness, truth, sincerity, veracity.<BR>—सत्य-दर्-<BR>शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, truth-seeing, foreseeing truth, truth-<BR>discerning.<BR>—सत्य-देव, अस्, आ, अम्, shining through<BR>truth.<BR>—सत्य-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, rich in truth,<BR>virtuous, sincere.<BR>—सत्य-धर्म, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—सत्य-धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. practising the<BR>duty of truth; ruling by fixed ordinances.<BR>—सत्य-<BR>धर्म-परायण, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to truth<BR>and virtue.<BR>—सत्य-धृत, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Puṣpa-vat.<BR>—सत्य-धृति, इस्, इस्, इ, holding fast to<BR>truth, strictly truthful; (इस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi (author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 185; he has the patro-<BR>nymic Vāruṇi); of a son of Śatānanda; of several<BR>other persons.<BR>—सत्य-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘truth-ban-<BR>nered,’ N. of a king.<BR>—सत्य-ध्वृत्, त्, त्, त्, destroy-<BR>ing or perverting truth.<BR>—सत्य-नामन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>having a true name.<BR>—सत्य-नारायण, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a particular divinity (called सत्य-पीर् in Bengālī).<BR>—सत्य-नेत्र, अस्, m. ‘true-eyed,’ N. of a son of<BR>Atri.<BR>—सत्य-पराक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, having real<BR>valour, truly brave.<BR>—सत्य-पुर, अम्, n. the world<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सत्य-पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, purified by<BR>truth (as a speech &c.).<BR>—सत्य-प्रतिज्ञ or सत्य-<BR>प्रतिश्रव, अस्, आ, अम्, true or faithful to a promise.<BR>—सत्य-प्रतिष्ठान, अस्, आ, अम्, having truth<BR>for a foundation, grounded in truth.<BR>—सत्य-फल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having good fruit,’ the Vilva tree.<BR>—सत्य-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound by truth, adhering to the<BR>truth, truthful.<BR>—सत्य-भामा, f. ‘having true<BR>lustre,’ N. of the daughter of Satrā-jit and one of<BR>the eight wives of Kṛṣṇa, (she is described as<BR>having promoted the quarrels of the Yādavas.)<BR>—सत्य-भारत, अस्, m., N. of the poet Vyāsa.<BR>—सत्य-भेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, a truth-breaker, breaking<BR>a promise.<BR>—सत्य-मन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>or repeating true prayers, praying effectually.<BR>—सत्-<BR>यम्-उग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having very invigorating or<BR>exciting qualities, (Ṛg-veda IX. 113, 5.)<BR>—सत्य-यज्,<BR>ट्, ट्, ट्, sincerely worshipping, sacrificing in truth.<BR>—सत्य-यज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—सत्य-<BR>युग, अम्, n. the first of the four Yugas or ages.<BR>—सत्य-युगाद्या (˚ग-आद्˚), f. the third day of<BR>the light half of Vaiśākha (on which the commence-<BR>ment of the Kṛta-yuga is celebrated).<BR>—सत्य-यौ-<BR>वन, अस्, m., N. of a particular Vidyā-dhara.<BR>—सत्-<BR>य-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to truth, honest, sincere;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a prince (son of Satya-vrata); epithet<BR>of Vyāsa.<BR>—सत्य-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Vidarbha.<BR>—सत्य-रथि, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—सत्य-राधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. one who grants<BR>real or true gifts.<BR>—सत्य-लोक, अस्, m., N. of one of<BR>the seven worlds, (see सत्य above.)<BR>—सत्य-वक्तृ,<BR>ता, त्री, तृ, a speaker of truth.<BR>—सत्य-वचन,<BR>अम्, n. truth-speaking, veracity, admitting the truth.<BR>—सत्यवचनार्थम् (˚न-अर्˚), ind. for the sake<BR>of speaking the truth.<BR>—सत्य-वचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>truth-speaking, veracious; (आस्), m. a Ṛṣi, saint,<BR>seer; (अस्), n. veracity, truth.<BR>—सत्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessing or practising truth, veracious, true; con-<BR>taining the word सत्य (said of a hymn); (आन्), m.,<BR>N. of a king (husband of Sāvitrī); (अती), f., N. of<BR>the wife of Parāśara and mother of Vyāsa; of a<BR>daughter of Gādhi and wife of Ṛcīka (fabled to have<BR>become the Kauśikī river); N. of the wife of Nā-<BR>rada; epithet of Acchodā.<BR>—सत्यवती-सुत, अस्,<BR>m. ‘son of Satyavatī,’ epithet of the poet Vyāsa.<BR>—सत्य-वद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, true-speaking, veracious;<BR>(अम्), n. truth.<BR>—सत्य-वाक्य, अम्, n. true-speak-<BR>ing, veracity, truth.<BR>—सत्य-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, truth-<BR>speaking, veracious, sincere; (क्), m. a Ṛṣi, saint;<BR>N. of a son of Cākṣuṣa; a crow.<BR>—सत्यवादि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. veracity, truthfulness.<BR>—सत्य-वादिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, speaking truth, veracious; (इनी), f., N. of<BR>a goddess.<BR>—सत्य-वाह, अस्, m., N. of a descendant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">Page1054-a+ 79</a>]<BR>of Bharad-vāja.<BR>—सत्य-विक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing real valour, truly valiant.<BR>—सत्य-वृत्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, practising truth, honest or upright in conduct.<BR>—सत्य-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, true to a vow or promise,<BR>adhering to truth, veracious, honest, sincere; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a king, (the twenty-fifth of the solar<BR>dynasty in the second age); N. of Manu Vaivasvata;<BR>of the author of a Dharma-śāstra; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a race inhabiting Śāka-dvīpa.<BR>—सत्य-व्रत-<BR>परायण, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to truth and religious<BR>observances.<BR>—सत्य-शवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having<BR>real strength, possessing true vigour, truly vigorous.<BR>—सत्य-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>hymns Ṛg-veda V. 79, 80 (having the patronymic<BR>Ātreya); of a teacher of the Ṛg-veda; of a son of<BR>Mārkaṇḍeya.<BR>—सत्य-श्रवसी, f., Ved. ‘possessed<BR>of real wealth or renown,’ epithet of Uṣas.<BR>—सत्य-<BR>श्रावण, अम्, n. the speaking or taking of an oath.<BR>—सत्य-श्री, ईस्, m., N. of a teacher of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—सत्य-सङ्काश, अस्, आ, अम्, like the truth, likely,<BR>probable, plausible.<BR>—सत्य-सङ्गर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>true to an agreement or promise, veracious, faithful;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Kuvera (god of wealth).<BR>—सत्य-<BR>सन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, true to an agreement or com-<BR>pact, faithful to an engagement; faithful, veracious;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Bharata (younger brother of<BR>Rāma); of Rāma-candra; of king Janam-ejaya;<BR>(आ), f. epithet of Draupadī (wife of the Pāṇḍu<BR>princes).<BR>—सत्य-सन्निभ, अस्, आ, अम्, like the<BR>truth, likely, probable, plausible.<BR>—सत्य-सव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. really generating; possessing true energy<BR>(epithet of Savitṛ); observing truth, (Sāy. = सत्या-<BR>नुज्ञ, Ṛg-veda V. 82, 7.)<BR>—सत्य-साक्षिन्, ई, m.<BR>a genuine or trustworthy witness.<BR>—सत्य-हित, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a teacher of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—सत्या-कृति,<BR>इस्, f. ratification of a bargain.<BR>—सत्याग्नि (˚य-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, m., N. of the Muni Agastya.<BR>—सत्याङ्ग<BR>(˚य-अङ्˚), आस्, m. pl., N. of a mythical race inha-<BR>biting Plaksha-dvīpa.<BR>—सत्यात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, having a true soul, true-hearted, true; (आ), m. a<BR>virtuous and upright man.<BR>—सत्यानुरक्त (˚य-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, attached to truth, upright, true.<BR>—सत्यानृत (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, true and false,<BR>containing truth and falsehood; (अम्), n. practice<BR>of truth and falsehood, commerce, trade, traffic.<BR>—सत्याभिधान (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, truth-<BR>speaking.<BR>—सत्याभिध्यायिन् (˚य-अभ्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, truth-meditating, meditating upon truth.<BR>—सत्या-<BR>भिसन्ध or सत्याभिसन्धान, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>सत्याभिसन्धिन् (˚य-अभ्˚), ई, इनी, इ, faithful to<BR>a promise or agreement.<BR>—सत्योत्कर्ष (˚य-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. eminence or excellence in truth; true excel-<BR>lence.<BR>—सत्योदक (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>truth for water, flowing with truth.<BR>—सत्योद्य (˚य-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, speaking the truth.<BR>—सत्योपया-<BR>चन (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, true to a request,<BR>granting or fulfilling a prayer or petition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यक|सत्यकं
सत्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, = सत्य, true, real, veracious,<BR>&c.; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Śini; (अम्), n. rati-<BR>fication (of a contract or bargain &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापन|सत्यापनं
सत्यापन, अम्, आ, n. f. (fr. सत्यापय below),<BR>speaking or observing the truth; ratification (of a<BR>bargain &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापय
सत्यापय, Nom. P. सत्यापयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>speak the truth; to ratify (a bargain or contract).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वन्
सत्वन्, आ, m. (according to Sāy. to be connected<BR>in some senses with rts. सद्, सन्), Ved. = सत्-त्व,<BR>entity, existence, being; a living being; reality,<BR>power, strength; a strong or valiant man, hero,<BR>warrior, (Sāy. = शत्रूणं सादयितृ धनानां<BR>वा सनितृ, Ṛg-veda VI. 45, 22); (आनस्), m. pl. a<BR>class of spirits attendant on Parameśvara, (Sāy. =<BR>परमेश्वरस्य भूत-गणा अतिशयेन बल-<BR>पराक्रमाः, Ṛg-veda I. 64, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत|सतः
सत सत, a kind of sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतःपङ्क्ति
सतःपङ्क्ति सतः-पङ्क्ति. See सतस्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत|सततं
सतत स-तत, अस्, आ, अम् (= सन्-तत, see<BR>सन्-तन्), constant, lasting, incessant, perpetual,<BR>eternal, continual, uninterrupted; (अम्), n. incessantly,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">Page1054-b+ 68</a>]<BR>eternally, perpetually, uninterruptedly, continually,<BR>always.<BR>—सतत-ग, अस्, m. or सतत-गति, इस्, m.<BR>‘continually moving,’ the wind.<BR>—सतत-ज्वर, अस्,<BR>m. a constant fever, one not intermitting.<BR>—स-<BR>तत-यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, continually moving or going,<BR>always tending to decay, (Manu I. 50.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत्त्व|सतत्त्वं
सतत्त्व स-तत्त्व, अम्, n. natural property,<BR>nature; (अस्, आ, अम्), having or knowing the real<BR>truth; containing the words तद्, ‘this,’ and त्व,<BR>‘thou.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतर्क|सतर्कः
सतर्क स-तर्क, अस्, आ, अम्, having argument<BR>or reasoning, skilled in speculation; cautious, con-<BR>siderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतर्ष
सतर्ष स-तर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having thirst,<BR>thirsty; (अम्), ind. with thirst, thirstily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतल
सतल स-तल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a bottom;<BR>[cf. अ-तल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतलत्र
सतलत्र स-तलत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having leather<BR>guards (used in archery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतस्
सतस् सतस्, ind. (according to some fr.<BR>सत्; according to others fr. स = सह, सम; usually<BR>occurring at the beginning of comps.), = तिरस् (ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. III. 29; cf. Nirukta III. 20).<BR>—सतः-पङ्क्ति, इस्, f. a kind of metre consisting<BR>of two Pādas of eight syllables and two Pādas of<BR>twelve syllables.<BR>—सतो-बृहती, f. a kind of metre<BR>the even Pādas of which consist of eight syllables and<BR>the uneven of twelve.<BR>—सतो-महत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. truly great, greater than everything that exists,<BR>(Sāy. सतो-महान्तः = सर्वस्माद् विद्यमानात्<BR>पृथिव्याम् अपि ये महान्तस्, Ṛg-veda VIII. 30,<BR>1.)<BR>—सतो-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. thoroughly brave or<BR>valiant, (Sāy. = प्राप्त-वीर्य, Ṛg-veda VI. 75, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतानन्द|सतानन्दः
सतानन्द सतानन्द, अस्, m. (for शतानन्द,<BR>p. 990, col. 3), N. of the sage Gautama; of the<BR>son of Gautama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सताह
सताह सताह, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सति|सतिः
सति 1. सति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. सो; for 2. सति see<BR>under rt. सन्), end, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सती
सती सती, सती-त्व. See p. 1053, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीन|सतीनः
सतीन सतीन. See p. 1053, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ|सतीर्थः
सतीर्थ स-तीर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, having sacred<BR>bathing-places; having the same bathing-place;<BR>(अस्), m. a pupil of the same spiritual preceptor,<BR>fellow religious student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ्य|सतीर्थ्यः
सतीर्थ्य, अस्, m. a fellow religious student, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतुष|सतुषं
सतुष स-तुष, अस्, आ, अम्, having husk or<BR>chaff; (अम्), n. grain with the husk remaining on it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतृणम्
सतृणम् स-तृणम्, ind. with grass, grass<BR>and all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतृष्
सतृष् स-तृष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, or स-तृष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having thirst, thirsty, desirous, greedy, longing<BR>after, cupidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतृष्ण
स-तृष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, thirsty; (अम्), ind. with<BR>thirst, thirstily; with desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतेर|सतेरः
सतेर सतेर, अस्, m. husk, chaff (= तुष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र्
सत्र् सत्र्, cl. 10. A. सत्रयते, सत्राप-<BR>यते, -यितुम्, to fulfil, accomplish; (ac-<BR>cording to others) to extend; to connect, fasten<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र सत्र or सत्त्र. See under rt. 1. सद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रप
सत्रप स-त्रप, अस्, आ, अम्, having shame<BR>or modesty, ashamed, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रा
सत्रा सत्रा, ind. (fr. स + त्रा; cf. 2. स-<BR>ध्रि), with, together with, (Sāy. = सह); all toge-<BR>ther, all at once; always, ever, continually, (Sāy. =<BR>सन्ततम्, सर्वदा); truly, (in Naigh. III. 10.<BR>सत्रा is enumerated among the सत्य-नामानि);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">Page1054-c+ 76</a>]<BR>great, many, abundant, (Sāy. = महत्, बहु, प्र-<BR>भूतम्.)<BR>—सत्रा-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. always conquer-<BR>ing; conqueror of the great; (त्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Nighna and father of Satya-bhāmā, (he was father-in-<BR>law of Kṛṣṇa and was killed by Śata-dhanvan);<BR>N. of Pratardana.<BR>—सत्राञ्च् (˚रा-अञ्च्), आङ्, आची, आक्<BR>[cf. सध्र्य्-अञ्च्], going with, associated, united;<BR>perfect.<BR>—सत्रा-दावन्, आ, m., Ved. always granting,<BR>giving all at once, (Sāy. = सह प्रदातृ); epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR>—सत्रा-सह् or सत्रा-साह्, साट्, ट्, ट्, Ved.<BR>always overcoming or conquering; conquering the<BR>great; conquering many.<BR>—सत्रा-हन्, आ, m. always<BR>destroying, destroyer of mighty foes, (Sāy. = मह-<BR>तां शत्रूणाम् हन्तृ); epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रम्
सत्रम्, ind. with, together with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रासम्
सत्रासम् स-त्रासम्, ind. with terror or fear,<BR>in a fright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रिजातक|सत्रिजातकं
सत्रिजातक स-त्रि-जातक, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>dish consisting of meat fried with three sorts of<BR>spices, (it is then soaked and dried and again dressed<BR>with ghee and condiments.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्व
सत्व सत्व, अम्, n. See सत्-त्व under सत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वच
सत्वच स-त्वच, अस्, आ, अम्, having skin or<BR>bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वत्|सत्वन्त्
सत्वत् सत्वत्, N. of a people inhabiting<BR>the south of India; [cf. सात्वत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वन्
सत्वन् सत्वन्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वर|सत्वरं
सत्वर स-त्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, having haste or<BR>speed, expeditious, quick; (अम्), ind. quickly, swiftly,<BR>hastily, suddenly.<BR>—सत्वर-ता, f. or सत्वर-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. quickness, hastiness, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सथूत्कार|सथूत्कारः
सथूत्कार स-थूत्-कार, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied with the sound थूत् or the sound made in<BR>spitting or sputtering, sputtered; (अम्), n. sputtering<BR>(in speech), speech accompanied with sputtering;<BR>[cf. अम्बू-कृत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्
सद् 1. सद् [cf. rt. शद्], cl. 1. P. (or ac-<BR>cording to some cl. 6. P.) सीदति (ep. also<BR>A. -ते), ससाद (2nd sing. सेदिथ or ससत्थ,<BR>3rd pl. सेदुस्), सत्स्यति, असदत् (Vedic forms, cl. 2.<BR>सत्सि, cl. 1. सदतु, सदताम्), सत्तुम् (Ved. Inf.<BR>सदे), to sink down, lie down, lie, recline; to sit,<BR>sit down, settle down, rest, settle; to be seated,<BR>reside, remain, live, be; to sink into despondency,<BR>be dejected or low-spirited; to become wearied,<BR>faint away, pine away; to sink into distress; to waste<BR>away, perish, decay, be destroyed; to be impeded;<BR>to go: Pass. सद्यते, Aor. असादि: Caus. सादयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. असीषदत्, to cause to sink or sit<BR>down, throw down, cast down, place down, place, put;<BR>to weary out, wear out, exhaust, harass, afflict; to cause<BR>to perish, destroy: Desid. सिषत्सति: Intens. सा-<BR>सद्यते, सासत्ति, to sit or lie down in an indecent<BR>posture; [cf. Gr. ὁδός, οὐδός, ἔδεθλον, ἕδ-ος, ἕζομαι,<BR>ἱδρόω: Lat. solum, sedeo, sido, probably also de-<BR>sidero, sella (for sed-la): Goth. sat, ‘to sit;’ satja,<BR>‘to place;’ sinths, sitan, sitls: Old Germ. saz,<BR>‘to sit;’ sezin, ‘to place;’ senal, satul: Angl. Sax.<BR>in-sidhian, on-settan, sittan, sadl, sadel: Lith.<BR>se†d-mi, ‘to place;’ sodiun, ‘to plant:’ Slav. sjadū,<BR>sad-i-ti: Hib. suidhim, suidhinghaim, ‘I set, I<BR>plant;’ saidhe, saidhiste, ‘a seat.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त
सत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = सन्न, (नि-षत्त = नि-<BR>षण्ण, Ṛg-veda 1. 68, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ति|सत्तिः
सत्ति, इस्, f. sitting down, sitting; [cf. नि-षत्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्तृ
सत्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, sitting down, sitting; one who<BR>sits or resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्र
सत्त्र, अम्, n. a long sacrifice or sacrificial session<BR>(lasting, according to some, from 13 to 100 days);<BR>a sacrifice (in general); an oblation, offering, gift;<BR>giving alms or charity, liberality, munificence; wealth;<BR>a residence, house; a place of refuge, asylum, hiding-<BR>place, covert; covering, clothing, concealing; fraud,<BR>roguery, cheating; a wood, forest; a tank, pond.<BR>—सत्त्र-परिवेषण, अम्, n. a distribution of<BR>food or other gifts at a sacrifice.<BR>—सत्त्र-वर्धन,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">Page1055-a+ 80</a>]<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, increasing or promoting sacrifice.<BR>—सत्-<BR>त्र-शाला, f. a large hall or room where food and<BR>alms are given away to Brāhmans or mendicants,<BR>&c., an alms-house.<BR>—सत्त्रापश्रय (˚र-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a place of refuge, asylum.<BR>—सत्त्रायण<BR>(˚र-अय्˚), अम्, n. a long course of sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्राय
सत्त्राय, Nom. A. सत्त्रायते, &c., to perform<BR>a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रि
सत्त्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, conquering, a conqueror; (इस्),<BR>m. a cloud; an elephant; [cf. शद्रि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रिन्
सत्त्रिन्, ई, m. a liberal householder who constantly<BR>performs sacrifices and distributes gifts or alms; a<BR>priest superintending or performing a sacrifice; an<BR>ambassador or agent residing in a foreign country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वा
सत्त्वा, ind. having sunk down, sitting, resting,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र = सत्त्र, p. 1054, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्
2. सद्, त्, त्, त्, one who sits or settles down,<BR>sitting, dwelling, residing (often at the end of comps.,<BR>see नाक-स्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद|सदः
सद, अस्, m. [cf. शद], the fruit of trees; N.<BR>of one of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra's sons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदन|सदनं
सदन, अम्, n. sinking or settling down, sitting,<BR>a seat; a dwelling, residence, house, palace; the<BR>abode of sacrifice, sacrificial hall; the abode of Yama;<BR>perishing, decaying; exhaustion; water (= उदक,<BR>Naigh. 1. 12).<BR>—सदना-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sitting<BR>on a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदन्य
सदन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, of or belonging to a house,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्
सदस्, अस्, n. a seat, residence, abode, dwelling;<BR>an assembly, meeting, (also आस्, f. according to some,<BR>and आस्, m. according to others; सदसः पतिः,<BR>‘lord of the assembly,’ epithet of Agni); (असी), n.<BR>du, Ved. heaven and earth (= द्यावा-पृथिवी,<BR>Naigh. III. 30); [cf. Gr. ἕδος.]<BR>—सदस्-पती, m.<BR>du., Ved. ‘lords of the assembly,’ epithet of Indra<BR>and Agni.<BR>—सदो-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to the<BR>assembly, being in the assembly.<BR>—सदो-गृह, अम्,<BR>n. ‘assembly-house,’ the court of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्य|सदस्यः
सदस्य, अस्, m. any person present at or belong-<BR>ing to an assembly, an assessor, spectator, member<BR>of an assembly, councillor; any one present or assist-<BR>ing at a sacrifice, a superintending priest or Ṛtvij,<BR>(his duties, according to the Kauṣītakins, are to<BR>superintend the whole sacrifice and correct mistakes;<BR>cf. विधि-दर्शिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मन्
सद्मन्, आ, m. an abode, dwelling (Ved.); (अ),<BR>n. a seat; a house, dwelling, palace; a temple; an<BR>altar; a place, station; conflict, (in Naigh. II. 17.<BR>enumerated among the सङ्ग्राम-नामानि); water<BR>(= उदक, Naigh. I. 12); (अनी), n. du., Ved. heaven<BR>and earth (= द्यावा-पृथिवी, Naigh. III. 30); (आ,<BR>आ, अ), Ved. sitting, seated, (in Ṛg-veda I. 173, 1.<BR>according to Sāy. सद्मानम् = सीदन्तम्.)<BR>—सद्-<BR>म-चिति, इस्, f. a collection of houses.<BR>—सद्म-बर्-<BR>हिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having sacred grass for its abode<BR>or place of sprinkling.<BR>—सद्म-मखस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. (according to Sāy. मखस् = महस्), hav-<BR>ing light for a seat or abode, radiant, (Sāy. = प्राप्त-<BR>तेजस्क, Ṛg-veda 1. 18, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्रु
सद्रु, उस्, उस्, उ [cf. शद्रु], resting, staying;<BR>going, moving; [cf. probably Gr. ἱδρυ in ἱδρύνω..]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न|सन्नः
सन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk down; lying down;<BR>seated, resting; settled down; still, motionless;<BR>sunk, low (in tone, accent, &c.); depressed, low (in<BR>spirits), desponding, dispirited, spiritless, weak, feeble,<BR>diminished; wasted away, exhausted, decayed, perished,<BR>destroyed, spoiled, lost; stunted, shrunk, contracted;<BR>oppressed; lying near, adjacent; gone, departed;<BR>(अस्), m. the Piyāla tree; (अम्), n. little, a small<BR>quantity.<BR>—सन्न-कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>contracted throat, having a feeble or broken utter-<BR>ance, with a choking voice, scarcely able to articulate,<BR>choking, choked.<BR>—सन्न-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more<BR>depressed, very weak or feeble; (in grammar)<BR>lower (in tone or accent), more depressed than the<BR>ordinary accentless tone (= अनुदात्त-तर).<BR>—सन्-<BR>न-मुसल, अम्, n. a motionless pestle; (ए), ind. at<BR>the time when the pestle lies motionless, (Manu VI.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">Page1055-b+ 76</a>]<BR>56.)<BR>—सन्न-हर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose joy<BR>has departed, depressed in spirits, desponding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नक|सन्नकः
सन्नक, अस्, आ, अम्, low, dwarfish; (अस्), m. the<BR>Piyāla tree.<BR>—सन्नक-द्रु, उस्, m. the Piyāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद|सादः
साद, अस्, m. sinking or settling down, sinking,<BR>exhaustion, weariness, lassitude; perishing, decay;<BR>suffering, pain; purity, clearness, cleanness [cf. प्र-<BR>सन्न, प्र-साद]; going, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादक
सादक, अस्, इका, अम्, exhausting, wearying, de-<BR>stroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादत्
सादत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. sitting down (= सीदत्).<BR>—सादद्-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. sitting in the interior,<BR>sitting on the hearth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादन|सादनं
सादन, अम्, n. causing to sink, wearying, ex-<BR>hausting; destroying, dispelling; sinking, sitting,<BR>settling; a seat, house, dwelling, palace; (ई), f. the<BR>plant Helleborus Niger; exhaustion, decay.<BR>—सा-<BR>दन-स्पृश् = गृहादि-प्रद, Ṛg-veda IX. 72, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादन्य
सादन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = सदन्य, belonging<BR>to a house, &c., skilful in domestic affairs, (Sāy. =<BR>गृह-कार्य-कुशल, Ṛg-veda I. 91, 20.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयत्
सादयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to sink down,<BR>wearying, wearing out, exhausting; destroying;<BR>expelling, removing; extracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयितव्य
सादयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be destroyed, de-<BR>structible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयित्वा
सादयित्वा, ind. having caused to sink or sit down;<BR>having put or placed down; having destroyed; hav-<BR>ing removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयिष्यत्
सादयिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादि|सादिः
सादि, इस्, m. a charioteer; a warrior; a dispirited<BR>or melancholy person; air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादित|सादितः
सादित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), made to sink<BR>down, depressed, exhausted, harassed; dispirited,<BR>wearied, distressed; wasted, decayed; destroyed, ex-<BR>terminated; broken; made to go, drawn, dragged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sitting down, settling down; (fr.<BR>the Caus.) exhausting, wearying, destroying; (ई), m.<BR>a horseman, cavalier; any one seated or riding on an<BR>elephant; any one seated or mounted on a car or<BR>chariot; a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासद्यमान
सासद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting or lying down<BR>in an indecent posture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीदत्
सीदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sinking, desponding, pining,<BR>grieving, sorrowing; decaying, perishing; distressed,<BR>pained; going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीदमान
सीदमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sinking down, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेदिवस्
सेदिवस्, वान्, -दुषी, वत्, one who has sat down<BR>or sunk down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशक|सदंशकः
सदंशक स-दंशक, अस्, आ, अम्, having teeth;<BR>having a sharp sting; (अस्), m. ‘having nippers,’ a crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशवदन|सदंशवदनः
स-दंश-वदन, अस्, m. ‘having a face with a<BR>sharp bill,’ a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदक्षिण
सदक्षिण स-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>presents, accompanied by gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदन्दि|सदंदि
सदन्दि सदन्दि, इस्, m., Ved. (perhaps)<BR>‘continuous, uninterrupted,’ epithet of a kind of<BR>Takman or fever, (Atharva-veda V. 22, 13, XIX.<BR>39, 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदम्
सदम् सदम्. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदय
सदय स-दय, अस्, आ, अम्, merciful, com-<BR>passionate, benevolent; (अम्), ind. kindly; gently,<BR>softly.<BR>—सदय-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>compassionate heart, tender-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदर
सदर स-दर, अस्, आ, अम्, fearful, afraid,<BR>timorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदर्प
सदर्प स-दर्प, अस्, आ, अम्, having pride;<BR>haughty; (अम्), ind. haughtily, arrogantly, proudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदश
सदश स-दश, अस्, आ, अम् (see दशा), having<BR>a fringe, fringed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदा
सदा सदा, ind. (fr. 5. स + दा), always, at<BR>all times, continually, perpetually, ever.<BR>—सदा-कल-<BR>वह, अस्, आ, अम्, flowing at all seasons, (opposed to<BR>प्रावृट्-काल-वह).<BR>—सदा-कान्ता, f., N. of a<BR>river; [cf. सदा-नीरा.]<BR>—सदा-गति, इस्, m. ‘ever-<BR>going,’ air, wind; the Universal Spirit; the sun;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">Page1055-c+ 76</a>]<BR>everlasting happiness, final emancipation.<BR>—सदा-<BR>तोया, f. ‘always (wanting) water,’ the plant Mimosa<BR>Octandra; the Karatoyā river (= सदा-नीरा).<BR>—१. स-<BR>दा-दान, अम्, n. ‘always giving,’ liberality, munifi-<BR>cence.<BR>—२. सदा-दान, अस्, m. (see 2. दान),<BR>‘always exuding ichor,’ epithet of Airāvata (the<BR>elephant of Indra); of Gaṇeśa; an elephant in rut.<BR>—सदानन्द (˚दा-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, always happy;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Śiva; N. of the author of the<BR>Vedānta-sāra.<BR>—सदा-नर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, always<BR>dancing; (अस्), m. a kind of bird, the wagtail.<BR>—सदा-नीर-वहा or सदा-नीरा, f. ‘always bear-<BR>ing or possessing water,’ epithet of the Karatoyā<BR>river, (see कर-तोया.)<BR>—सदा-न्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. always crying out, (Sāy. = सदा नोनुव,<BR>सर्वदाक्रोश-कारिन्, Ṛg-veda X. 155, 1, see<BR>Nirukta VI. 30.)<BR>—सदा-पुष्प, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>always in flower, ever-flowering; (अस्), m. the cocoa-<BR>nut; (ई), f. a variety of the gigantic swallow-wort<BR>(= रक्तार्क).<BR>—सदा-पृण, अस्, m. ‘always mu-<BR>nificent,’ N. of a Ṛṣi (having the patronymic<BR>Ātreya and author of the hymn Ṛg-veda V. 45).<BR>—सदा-प्रसून, अस्, m. ‘always in flower,’ N. of<BR>various plants (= रोहितक; = अर्क; = कुन्द).<BR>—सदा-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, always bearing fruit;<BR>(अस्), m. the cocoa-nut tree; the glomerous fig-tree;<BR>the jack, Artocarpus Integrifolia; the Vilva tree;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of mallow; a kind of egg-plant.<BR>—सदा-भद्रा, f. ‘always auspicious,’ a kind of<BR>shrub, Gmelina Arborea.<BR>—सदा-भव्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, always present; attentive.<BR>—सदा-मद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ever-furious.<BR>—सदामर्ष (˚दा-अम्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, always impatient, very impatient, petulant.<BR>—सदा-योगिन्, ई, m. ‘always practising abstract<BR>contemplation,’ epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—स-<BR>दा-वृध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. always increasing or<BR>prospering, ever-growing.<BR>—सदा-शिव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>always happy or prosperous; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Śiva; a proper N.<BR>—सदाशिव-संहिता, f., N. of<BR>part of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—२. सदाश्रित (˚दा-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. सद्-आश्रित see under सत्),<BR>always resorting to; always dependant on.<BR>—सदा-<BR>स, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (see rt. 1. सन्), always honour-<BR>ing or giving, (Sāy. = सर्वदा भजमान or अन्-<BR>नस्य दातृ, Ṛg-veda IV. 16, 21.)<BR>—सदा-सह् or<BR>सदा-साह्, साट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. always conquering.<BR>—स-<BR>दोत्सव (˚दा-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ever-festive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदम्
सदम्, ind., Ved. always, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातन|सदातनः
सदातन, अस्, ई, अम्, incessant, continual, per-<BR>petual, eternal; (अस्), m. epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—स-<BR>दातन-त्व, अम्, n. eternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाचार|सदाचारः
सदाचार सद्-आचार. See under सत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदान
सदान 1. स-दान, अस्, आ, अम्, having gifts,<BR>with gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदान
सदान 2. स-दान, अस्, आ, अम्, having ichor<BR>(exuding from the temples), being in rut (as an<BR>elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदार
सदार स-दार, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by<BR>a wife, together with a wife.<BR>—सदार-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, accompanied by wife and son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदिश्
सदिश् स-दिश्, क्, क्, क्, together with the<BR>quarters (of the sky).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदीनम्
सदीनम् स-दीनम्, ind. lamentably, misera-<BR>bly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश्
सदृश् स-दृश्, क्, क्, क् (see 2. दृश्, p. 428,<BR>col. 3), having the same look or appearance, like,<BR>similar, same; fit, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्ष|सदृक्षः
स-दृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, like, resembling, similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश|सदृशः
स-दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, like, resembling, same, similar,<BR>of the same rank; conformable, fit, proper, right,<BR>suitable; worthy.<BR>—सदृश-ता, f. or सदृश-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. likeness, similarity, sameness.<BR>—सदृश-<BR>स्पन्दन, अम्, n. any regular or even throbbing<BR>motion (= नि-स्पन्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृष्टिक्षेपम्
सदृष्टिक्षेपम् स-दृष्टि-क्षेपम्, ind. with<BR>a glance of the eye, with a sidelong glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेवासुरराक्षस
सदेवासुरराक्षस स-देवासुर-राक्षस (˚व-<BR>अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by gods, Asuras, and<BR>Rākṣasas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेवीक
सदेवीक स-देवीक, अस्, आ, अम्, along with<BR>or accompanied by a queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेश|सदेशः
सदेश स-देश, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing a<BR>country; of the same country or place; neighbour-<BR>ing, proximate, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदोष
सदोष स-दोष, अस्, आ, अम्, having faults,<BR>faulty, defective; improper, wrong; liable to objec-<BR>tions, objectionable.<BR>—सदोष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>containing anything defective.<BR>—सदोष-विकाश,<BR>अस्, m. a defective exhibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भाव|सद्भावः
सद्भाव सद्-भाव. See under सत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मन्
सद्मन् सद्मन्. See p. 1055, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्
सद्यस् स-द्यस्, ind. (fr. 4. स + द्यस् for दि-<BR>वस्, fr. 3. दिव्, q. v.), to-day, this very day, now,<BR>instantly, at the moment, in an instant, momenta-<BR>rily; presently, forthwith, immediately, on a sudden;<BR>quickly, promptly; recently.<BR>—सद्य-ऊति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. quickly aiding or assisting; quickly going, (Sāy.<BR>= सद्यो-गमन.)<BR>—सद्यः-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>done at the moment, done promptly or quickly; (अम्),<BR>n. a name, appellation.<BR>—सद्यः-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>quickly falling or dropping, frail.<BR>—सद्यः-प्रक्षा-<BR>लक, अस्, m. one who cleans corn immediately for<BR>use (without storing it).<BR>—सद्यः-प्राणकर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, quickly inspiriting or invigorating.<BR>—सद्यः-<BR>प्राणहर, अस्, आ, अम्, quickly destroying vigour,<BR>debilitating.<BR>—सद्यः-शुद्धि, इस्, f. = सद्यः-<BR>शौच.<BR>—सद्यः-शोथा, f. ‘quickly swelling,’<BR>cowach, Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR>—सद्यः-शौच,<BR>अम्, n. present or immediate purity or purification.<BR>—सद्यस्-काल, अस्, m. present time.<BR>—सद्यस्-<BR>कालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the present time,<BR>recent, modern, new.<BR>—सद्यस्-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>just heated.<BR>—सद्यो-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. quickly<BR>going, swift-moving.<BR>—सद्यो-जात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>newly born, born in a moment; (अस्), m. a calf;<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सद्यो-भाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, existing<BR>or becoming born in a moment, newly born; (ई),<BR>m. a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्क|सद्यस्कः
सद्यस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the present day,<BR>immediate, present, quick, prompt; new, recent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्रु
सद्रु सद्रु. See p. 1055, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वन्द्व
सद्वन्द्व स-द्वन्द्व, अस्, आ, अम्, quarrelsome,<BR>strifeful, contentious, fond of strife or litigation, dis-<BR>agreeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वसथ|सद्वसथः
सद्वसथ सद्-वसथ. See p. 1053, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध
सध स-ध, ind. (probably for स-धा),<BR>Ved. = 2. सह, with, together with, (Pāṇ. VI. 3,<BR>96.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधमा
सध-मा, आस्, m., Ved. a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधमाद
सध-माद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having intoxi-<BR>cation or joy together, exulting or rejoicing toge-<BR>ther; intoxicating together; (अस्), m. a companion,<BR>friend; a feast, festival (= सह-मदन); a sacri-<BR>fice; (अम्), ind. so as to exult or become intoxicated<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधमाद्य
सध-माद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. intoxicating or<BR>rendering glad together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधस्तुति
सध-स्तुति, इस्, f., Ved. united praise; (इ), ind.<BR>along with praise, (Sāy. = स्तुत्या सहितम्, Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 18, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधस्तुत्य
सध-स्तुत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be praised<BR>together; (अम्), n. praising together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधस्थ
सध-स्थ, अम्, n., Ved. a place where persons<BR>stand together, place of meeting, a spot, place; a<BR>seat; an abode, region, world, sphere, firmament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधन
सधन स-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>riches, wealthy, rich, opulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधनु
सधनु स-धनु, उस्, उस्, उ, or स-धनुस्, उस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">Page1056-b+ 74</a>]<BR>उस्, उस्, having a bow, armed with a bow, with bow<BR>(in hand).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मन्|सधर्म्मन्
सधर्मन् स-धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, or स-धर्म,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having similar duties, having the same<BR>or similar properties; of the same sect or caste;<BR>performing like duties; resembling, equal, like.<BR>—स-धर्मचारिणी, f. a wife who assists (her<BR>husband) in the performance of religious duties, a<BR>virtuous wife, one wedded with the proper rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मिन्|सधर्म्मिन्
सधर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, observing the same customs<BR>or laws; (इणी), f. a wife wedded according to the<BR>proper ritual; a legal or virtuous wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधवा
सधवा स-धवा, f. a woman having a<BR>husband, a wife whose husband is living; [cf. वि-<BR>धवा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधि|सधिः
सधि स-धि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. धा with स),<BR>N. of Agni or fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधिस्
सधिस् सधिस्, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 114. fr. rt. 1. सह्), an ox, bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधूम्र
सधूम्र स-धूम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, dusky, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधे
सधे स-धे, a various reading for स्वधे,<BR>enumerated among the द्यावा-पृथिवी-नामधे-<BR>यानि in Naigh. III. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधैर्यम्
सधैर्यम् स-धैर्यम्, ind. with firmness,<BR>with gravity; firmly, gravely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्रि
सध्रि 1. सध्रि, इस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 114 (having the patro-<BR>nymic Vairūpa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्रि
सध्रि 2. सध्रि [cf. स-त्रा], a form sub-<BR>stituted for 2. सह, with, together with, (Pāṇ. VI.<BR>3, 95.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्री
सध्री, scil. नद्यः, Ved. the rivers going or flow-<BR>ing together, (Sāy. = सध्रीचीनाः, Ṛg-veda II. 13,<BR>2, the अञ्च् of सध्र्य्-अञ्च् being dropped.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्रीचीन
सध्रीचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, going or coming with,<BR>accompanying, associated; [cf. प्रतीचीन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्र्यञ्च्|सध्र्यंच्
सध्र्य्-अञ्च्, अङ्, -रीची, अक् [cf. सत्राञ्च्], going<BR>with, accompanying, associated; a companion; (ईची),<BR>f. a woman's companion or female friend, a confi-<BR>dante; (अक्), ind. together with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्वंस
सध्वंस स-ध्वंस, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda VIII. 8 (having the patro-<BR>nymic Kāṇva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्वज
सध्वज स-ध्वज, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>banner, bannered, with a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्
सन् 1. सन्, cl. 1. P., 8. P. A. सनति,<BR>सनोति, सनुते (Ved. सनिष्णत = सम्-<BR>भजन्ते, Ṛg-veda 1. 131, 5), ससान, सनितुम्,<BR>to love, like, worship, honour; to obtain through<BR>love or worship, obtain, acquire, gain; to receive<BR>graciously; to honour with gifts, give, bestow, dis-<BR>pense, distribute: Pass. सन्यते or सायते (Pāṇ. VI.<BR>4, 43), to be loved, &c.: Caus. सानयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. असीषणत्: Desid. सिसनिषति, सिषासति, to<BR>be eager to worship or honour; to wish to obtain,<BR>desire, strive for; to wish to bestow or give: Intens.<BR>संसन्यते, सासायते, संसन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स|सं|सः
5. स, अस्, आ, अम्, giving, bestowing, &c. (at the<BR>end of comps., cf. सदा-स).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सति|सतिः
2. सति, इस्, f. (for 1. सति see s. v.), giving, a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन|सनः
1. सन, अस्, m. the flapping of an elephant's ears;<BR>the plant Ghaṇṭā-pāṭali; the tree Pentaptera To-<BR>mentosa; (अम्), n., Ved. food, (Sāy. सनानि = अन्-<BR>नानि, Ṛg-veda I. 95, 10.)<BR>—सन-पर्णी, f. the<BR>plant Marsilea Quadrifolia, (also written असन-<BR>पर्णी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्
1. सनत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. bestowing, granting.<BR>—सनत्-कुमार, see under 2. सनत्.<BR>—सनद्-<BR>रयि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. granting wealth.<BR>—सनद्-वाज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. granting food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनस्
1. सनस्, अस्, n. (doubtful), excrement, ordure;<BR>Śiva's trident (?); crystal (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनि|सनिः
सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. giving, a giver, (Sāy. सनि<BR>= धनस्य दातृ; cf. सहस्र-स्˚); (इस्), m.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">Page1056-c+ 80</a>]<BR>Ved. obtaining, acquisition, pursuit; giving, dona-<BR>tion; service, worship; (इस्), m. f. request, solicitation,<BR>respectful entreaty (addressed to a spiritual preceptor,<BR>&c.); quarter, region, point of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनित|सनितः
सनित, अस्, आ, अम्, granted; gained, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनितृ
सनितृ, ता, m., Ved. one who grants anything<BR>(with acc. or gen.; Sāy. = सम्भजन-शील); a<BR>benefactor; a husband, (Sāy. = भर्तृ, Ṛg-veda<BR>III. 31, 2; see Nirukta III. 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनित्र
सनित्र, अम्, n., Ved. an instrument or means<BR>of honouring, (Ṛg-veda IX. 97, 29.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनित्व
सनित्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be honoured or loved,<BR>(Sāy. = सम्भजनीय, Ṛg-veda VIII. 81, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठ
सनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most liberal or boun-<BR>tiful, very munificent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्य
सनिष्य, Nom. P. सनिष्यति, Ved. to wish to<BR>give; to wish for or desire gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्यत्
सनिष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. desiring to bestow;<BR>wishing for riches, desirous of wealth, (Sāy. = धनम्<BR>इच्छत् or लप्स्यमान, Ṛg-veda VII. 100, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्यु
सनिष्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. wishing to give, de-<BR>sirous of giving; desirous to honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनी
सनी, f. a respectful request (= सनि above); a<BR>quarter or point of the compass; the flapping of an<BR>elephant's ears (= 1. सन); light, lustre; epithet<BR>of Gaurī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनुत्री
सनुत्री, f. (probably fem. of a form सनुतृ),<BR>Ved. a giver or dispenser (of light to the whole<BR>world), epithet of Uṣas, (Sāy. सनुत्री = सर्वं<BR>जगत् सम्भजन्ती or दात्री प्रकाशस्य, Ṛg-veda<BR>1. 123, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनेरु
सनेरु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. honouring, worshipping,<BR>&c., (Sāy. = सम्भक्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ति|संति|संतिः|सन्तिः
1. सन्ति, इस्, f. (for 2. सन्ति see s. v.), giving, a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्य|संत्य
सन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be honoured or wor-<BR>shipped, adorable; to be possessed, (Sāy. = भजन-<BR>शील, सम्भजनीय); giving, a giver, a giver of<BR>rewards, (Sāy. = फलस्य दातृ, Ṛg-veda 1. 45,<BR>9); (अस्), m. epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्यस्
सन्यस्, apparently only used in dat. c. सन्यसे<BR>= सम्भजनाय, ‘for the honouring,’ (according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 31, 19. fr. rts. 1. सन् and<BR>यस्, perhaps a kind of Ved. Inf.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषासत्
सिषासत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. desirous of giving,<BR>eager to bestow benefits, (Sāy. = सम्भक्तुम् इच्-<BR>छत्, Ṛg-veda I. 123, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्
सन् 2. सन्, (in grammar) a technical term<BR>for the syllable स or sign of the desiderative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन|सनः
सन 2. सन, a Vedic word meaning ‘old,’<BR>‘ancient,’ occurring in the form सना, neut. pl. =<BR>सनानि = सनातनानि, सदातनानि, Ṛg-veda III.<BR>1, 20, 1. 174, 8; see also सना, सनात्, &c.; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of one of the seven sons of Brahmā; [cf.<BR>Lat. senex; Goth. sins, sineigs.]<BR>—सन-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, or सन-जा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. born or pro-<BR>duced of old, ancient.<BR>—सन-वित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>long since obtained.<BR>—सन-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. famous of old; always celebrated; (अस्), m. a<BR>proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनक|सनकः
सनक, अस्, m., N. of one of the four sons of<BR>Brahmā (described as one of the councillors or com-<BR>panions of Viṣṇu and as inhabiting the Janar-loka;<BR>some accounts assign to Brahmā seven mind-born<BR>sons); N. of an inspired legislator; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>Ved. epithet of the Asuras (represented in the Ṛg-<BR>veda as slain by Indra).<BR>—सनक-संहिता, f., N. of<BR>a Tantra work, (one of the Śubhāgamas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्
2. सनत्, त्, m. (according to some properly neut.<BR>of 2. सन above), N. of Brahmā; (त्), ind. always,<BR>ever, perpetually.<BR>—सनत्-कुमार, अस्, m. ‘son of<BR>Brahmā,’ or, according to some, ‘always a youth,’<BR>N. of one of the four sons of Brahmā and oldest of<BR>the progenitors of mankind (= वैधात्र; other<BR>lists give seven sons); N. of one of the twelve Sār-<BR>vabhaumas or emperors of India according to the<BR>Jainas; N. for any sanctified person who retains<BR>throughout life the purity of youth.<BR>—सनत्कु-<BR>मार-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—स-<BR>नत्कुमार-संहिता, f., N. of a part of the Skanda-<BR>Purāṇa; of a Tantra work (regarded as one of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">Page1057-a+ 74</a>]<BR>Śubhāgamas).<BR>—सनत्कुमरीय, N. of a Tantra<BR>work.<BR>—सनत्कुमारोपपुराण (˚र-उप्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>—सनत्-सुजात, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the second of the seven mind-born sons of<BR>Brahmā.<BR>—सनत्सुजातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to<BR>Sanat-sujāta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनय
सनय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. old, ancient (= पु-<BR>राण, Nirukta IV. 19).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनस्
2. सनस् = 2. सन, p. 1056.<BR>—सनो-जा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, Ved. = सन-ज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सना
सना, ind. (properly an old inst. fr. 2. सन,<BR>p. 1056), always, eternally, perpetually; [cf. Angl.<BR>Sax. sin, especially at the beginning of comps.; Old<BR>Germ. sin; Goth. sin in sin-teins.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनात्
सनात्, ind. (properly abl. fr. 2. सन), Ved.<BR>‘from ancient times,’ of old, always, eternally, per-<BR>petually, ever, (न सनात्, never.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनातन|सनातनः
सनातन, अस्, ई, अम्, eternal, continual, perpetual;<BR>firm, fixed, permanent; primeval, ancient; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of Brahmā; of one of<BR>Brahmā's sons; of one of Rudra's sons; of a teacher<BR>of the Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa; a guest of the Manes,<BR>one who must always be fed whenever he attends<BR>Śrāddhas or obsequial ceremonies; (ई), f., N. of<BR>the goddess Lakṣmī; of Durgā; of Sarasvatī; [cf.<BR>Goth. sinteins, sinteino.]<BR>—सनातन-तम, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the most eternal, most ancient,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—सनातन-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of an author<BR>of a commentary on the Megha-dūta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाय
सनाय, Nom. A. सनायते, Ved. to act like an<BR>immortal being, be eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनग
सनग सनग, अस्, m., N. of a teacher of<BR>the Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनन्द|सनन्दः
सनन्द स-नन्द, अस्, m. ‘joy-possessing,’<BR>N. of one of the four sons of Brahmā (inhabiting<BR>Janar-loka; see लोक); one of the sons of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनन्दन|सनन्दनः
स-नन्दन, अस्, m., N. of one of the mind-<BR>engendered sons of Brahmā (said to have preceded<BR>Kapila in teaching the Sāṅkhya phil.); of a pupil<BR>of Śaṅkarācārya and author of the Pañca-pādikā;<BR>of a commentator.<BR>—सनन्दन-संहिता, f., N. of<BR>a Tantra work, (one of the Śubhāgamas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनरद्विप
सनरद्विप स-नर-द्विप, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by men and elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनलदानलद
सनलदानलद स-नलदानल-द (˚द-अन्˚,<BR>cf. 3. द), अस्, आ, अम्, having the Nalada (i. e. An-<BR>dropogon Muricatus or Uśīra plant) and appeasing<BR>heat, (Kirāt. V. 25.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनसूत्र|सनसूत्रं
सनसूत्र सन-सूत्र, अम्, n. (= शण-सूत्र),<BR>hempen cord or string, packthread; a net made of<BR>hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाकवनित
सनाकवनित स-नाक-वनित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having celestial women or Apsarases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथ
सनाथ स-नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a master<BR>or protector; having a lord or husband; occupied<BR>by, possessed by; endowed with, possessed of, pos-<BR>sessing, having; (आ), f. a woman whose husband is<BR>living.<BR>—सनाथ-ता, f. the state of having a pro-<BR>tector or husband.<BR>—सनाथी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to make to possess a master or protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभि|सनाभिः
सनाभि स-नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ, connected by<BR>the same navel or womb, uterine, nearly related,<BR>kindred; like, resembling; affectionate; having<BR>even or evenly formed naves (Ved.); (इस्), m. a<BR>near kinsman, uterine brother, one of the same<BR>family name; a relation or kinsman as far as the<BR>seventh degree (= स-पिण्ड, q. v.); (अयस्), f. pl.<BR>‘the sisters,’ epithet of the fingers, (enumerated<BR>among the अङ्गुलि-नामानि in Naigh. II. 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभ्य|सनाभ्यः
स-नाभ्य, अस्, m. a relation as far as the seventh<BR>degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनामक|सनामकः
सनामक स-नामक, अस्, इका, अम्, having<BR>the same name; (अस्), m. the tree Hyperanthera<BR>Moringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनामन्
स-नामन्, आ, आ, or -म्नी, अ, having the same<BR>name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनारु
सनारु सनारु, उस्, m., N. of a teacher of<BR>the Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिःश्वासम्
सनिःश्वासम् स-निःश्वासम्, ind. with a sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनियम
सनियम स-नियम, अस्, आ, अम्, performing<BR>or observing religious ceremonies, engaged in religious<BR>observances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिर्घात
सनिर्घात स-निर्घात, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by a hurricane or whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिर्घृण
सनिर्घृण स-निर्घृण, अस्, आ, अम्, merciless,<BR>cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिर्वेदम्
सनिर्वेदम् स-निर्वेदम्, ind. in a modest<BR>manner, with humility, humbly; despairingly; with<BR>indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठीव|सनिष्ठीवं
सनिष्ठीव स-निष्ठीव, अम्, n. sputtered<BR>speech, speech accompanied with sputtering or emis-<BR>sion of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठेव|सनिष्ठेवं
स-निष्ठेव, अम्, n. = स-निष्ठीव above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीड|सनीडः
सनीड स-नीड, अस्, आ, अम्, having a nest or<BR>abode; having or occupying the same nest or abode,<BR>dwelling together; near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीळ
स-नीऌअ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = स-नीड above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीय
सनीय सनीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनुतर्
सनुतर् सनुतर्, ind. (thought by some to<BR>be fr. सानु + तः), Ved. from behind, behind the<BR>back, in concealment, secretly, clandestinely, (enume-<BR>rated in Naigh. III. 25. among the निर्णीतान्तर्-<BR>हित-नामधेयानि); far away, far off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनुत्य
सनुत्य, अस्, m., Ved. one who lies in ambush<BR>(as a thief; Sāy. अन्तर्हिते देशे भवश् चोरः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनेमि
सनेमि स-नेमि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. ‘having the<BR>halves,’ complete, entire, whole, (see नेम); having<BR>equal or even fellies, i. e. revolving with even<BR>motion, (Sāy. समान-नेम्य् एकप्रकार-वहिर्-<BR>वलयम् अक्षीण-नेमि, Ṛg-veda I. 164, 14);<BR>(इ), ind. wholly, entirely; enumerated among the<BR>पुराण-नामानि in Naigh. III. 27; = क्षिप्रम्,<BR>(Nirukta XII. 44.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनोजा
सनोजा सनो-जा. See under 2. सनस्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त|संत|संतः|सन्तः
सन्त सन्त, अस्, m. the two hands opened<BR>and the palms joined (= संहत-तल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तक्ष्|संतक्ष्
सन्तक्ष् सन्-तक्ष् (सम्-त्˚), cl. 1. P. -तक्-<BR>षति, -तक्षितुम्, -तष्टुम्, to cut out, form,<BR>fashion by cutting; to construct, compose (hymns<BR>&c., Ved.); to cut through, cut to pieces, wound;<BR>to hurt by words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तक्षण|संतक्षणं
सन्-तक्षण, अम्, n. cutting language, sarcasm,<BR>scoff, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तक्ष्य
सन्-तक्ष्य, ind. having cut out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तष्ट
सन्-तष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, cut out, formed, cut<BR>through, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तड्|संतड्
सन्तड् सन्-तड् (सम्-त्˚), cl. 10. P. -ताड-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to strike effectually, strike or hit hard,<BR>hit (with an arrow &c.); to beat or play a musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ताड्य|संताड्य
सन्-ताड्य, ind. having struck or hit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तन्|संतन्
सन्तन् सन्-तन् (सम्-त्˚), cl. 8. P. A. -तनोति,<BR>-तनुते, -तनितुम्, to stretch or extend along,<BR>stretch over, cover with, cover over; to join or<BR>connect together, make continuous; to effect, accom-<BR>plish; to exhibit, display, evince; to be connected<BR>or combined with (Ved.); Caus. -तानयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to extend, cause to accomplish, cause to be<BR>finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तत|संतत|सन्ततं
सन्-तत, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. स-तत], stretched<BR>along, extended along, stretched or spread over,<BR>covered over, connected together, sewn or woven<BR>together, extended; continued, continuous, uninter-<BR>rupted, regular, continual, lasting, eternal; much,<BR>many; (अम्), ind. constantly, continually, eternally,<BR>always.<BR>—सन्तत-ज्वर, अस्, m. continuous fever.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">Page1057-c+ 80</a>]<BR>—सन्तत-वर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, raining continuously.<BR>—सन्तत-वेपथु, उस्, उस्, उ, trembling all over.<BR>—सन्ततापद् (˚त-आप्˚), त्, त्, त्, one whose mis-<BR>fortunes are continuous.<BR>—सन्तताभ्यास (˚त-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, m. habitual practice, regular study or<BR>repetition (of the Vedas &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तति|संतति|संततिः|सन्ततिः
सन्-तति, इस्, f. stretching or extending along,<BR>stretching or spreading over, extent, expanse, con-<BR>tinuity; a continuous line, row, range; uninterrupted<BR>succession, descent; lineage, race, progeny, offspring;<BR>a son; a daughter; a number of people, multitude;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a son of Alarka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ततेयु|संततेयु
सन्ततेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तनि|संतनि
सन्-तनि, इस्, m., Ved. extension; continuous stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तन्वत्
सन्-तन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, extending along, covering<BR>over, covering with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तान|संतान|संतानं|संतानः|सन्तानः
सन्-तान, अस्, अम्, m. n. extending, extension,<BR>expansion, spreading; the being spread or increased,<BR>continuance, continuous succession, lineage, race,<BR>family; progeny, offspring; a son or daughter; one<BR>of the five trees of Indra's paradise.<BR>—सन्तान-<BR>सन्धि, इस्, m. peace cemented by family alliance<BR>(by giving a daughter in marriage, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तानक|संतानक|संतानकः
सन्तानक, अस्, इका, अम्, stretching, spreading,<BR>who or what spreads; (अस्), m. one of the trees of<BR>Indra's heaven, the Kalpa tree or its flower; (इका),<BR>f. froth, foam; cream, coagulated milk, custard; a cob-<BR>web; the blade of a knife or sword.<BR>—सन्तानका-<BR>कीर्ण (˚क-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, strewn with celestial<BR>flowers, &c. (from the Kalpa tree).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तप्|संतप्
सन्तप् सन्-तप् (सम्-तप्), cl. 1. P. -तपति,<BR>-तप्तुम्, to heat thoroughly, make red hot, cause<BR>to glow, inflame; to scorch, parch, dry up; to pain<BR>by heat, torture: Pass. -तप्यते (ep. P. -ति), to be<BR>well heated, to become hot, suffer great pain or<BR>torment; to undergo penance; to be penitent,<BR>repent: Caus. -तापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be<BR>heated, to make very hot, heat, scorch, burn, inflame,<BR>set on fire; to foment; to burn up, consume; to<BR>pain by heat, torment, torture, distress, harass; (with<BR>आत्मानम्) to torture or torment one's self, harass<BR>the body by penance: Pass. of Caus. -ताप्यते, to<BR>be made very hot, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तपन|संतपन|संतपनं
सन्-तपन, अम्, n. the act of inflaming or tor-<BR>menting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तप्त|संतप्त|सन्तप्तः
सन्-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly heated or inflamed,<BR>red hot, glowing; melted, burnt up, scorched, dried<BR>up, inflamed with passion, &c.; suffering great pain<BR>or anguish, tormented, distressed, afflicted, wearied,<BR>fatigued.<BR>—सन्तप्त-चामीकर, अम्, n. glowing or<BR>molten gold.<BR>—सन्तप्त-रजत, अम्, n. molten<BR>silver.<BR>—सन्तप्त-वक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, oppressed<BR>in the chest or breathing, short-breathed.<BR>—सन्-<BR>तप्त-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, feeling great anguish of<BR>heart.<BR>—सन्तप्तायस् (˚त-अय्˚), अस्, n. heated iron,<BR>red hot iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तप्य
सन्-तप्य, ind. having undergone penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तप्यमान|संतप्यमान
सन्-तप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being inflamed, being<BR>tormented or distressed.<BR>—सन्तप्यमान-मनस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, one whose mind is in a state of torture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ताप|संताप|संतापः|सन्तापः
सन्-ताप, अस्, m. great heat, burning heat; in-<BR>flammation, fire; affliction, pain, anguish, distress;<BR>passion; remorse, resentment, penance, penitence,<BR>repentance.<BR>—सन्ताप-हर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, re-<BR>moving heat, cooling; consolatory, consoling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापन|संतापन|संतापनः|सन्तापनः
सन्-तापन, अस्, ई, अम्, burning up, scorching,<BR>inflaming; (अम्), n. the act of burning, scorching;<BR>paining, affliction; exciting passion; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of one of the arrows of Kāma-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापयित्वा
सन्-तापयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having burnt<BR>up or inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापित|संतापित|सन्तापितः
सन्-तापित, अस्, आ, अम्, made very hot, burnt up,<BR>scorched; inflamed, consumed; tormented, pained,<BR>harassed, distressed, afflicted, wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ताप्य|संताप्य
सन्-ताप्य, ind. having caused to be heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तम्|संतम्
सन्तम् सन्-तम् (सम्-त्˚), cl. 4. P. -ताम्-<BR>यति, -तमितुम्, to be distressed, pine away, become<BR>exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तमक|संतमक|संतमकः
सन्-तमक, अस्, m. oppression or distress (in<BR>breathing &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तमस्|संतमस्
सन्-तमस्, अस्, n. great darkness, universal dark-<BR>ness or obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तमस|संतमस|सन्तमसं
सन्-तमस, अस्, आ, अम्, darkened, clouded;<BR>(अम्), n. overspreading or universal darkness; great<BR>darkness or delusion of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्क्|संतर्क्
