सन्तीर्य|संतीर्य
सन्-तीर्य, ind. having crossed over, having passed<BR>through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्य|संत्य
सन्त्य सन्त्य. See p. 1056, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यज्|संत्यज्
सन्त्यज् सन्-त्यज् (सम्-त्यज्), cl. 1. P. -त्य-<BR>जति, -त्यक्तुम्, to relinquish altogether, abandon,<BR>leave, desert; to leave (a place), depart from, avoid,<BR>shun; to give up, resign, renounce, deliver up; to<BR>leave alone, take no notice of, disregard, omit:<BR>Caus. -त्याजयति, -यितुम्, to cause to abandon; to<BR>deprive or rob a person of anything (with two acc.);<BR>to cause a person (acc.) to be delivered up by any<BR>one (inst.), rescue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यक्त|संत्यक्त
सन्-त्यक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, completely deserted, left,<BR>abandoned, renounced, resigned, robbed, deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यजत्
सन्-त्यजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, relinquishing, abandon-<BR>ing, deserting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यजन|संत्यजन|संत्यजनं
सन्-त्यजन, अम्, n. the act of deserting, leaving,<BR>abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यज्य|संत्यज्य
सन्-त्यज्य, ind. having abandoned or given up<BR>entirely, having discarded or renounced; having<BR>avoided; having left alone, having taken no notice of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रस्|संत्रस्
सन्त्रस् सन्-त्रस् (सम्-त्रस्), cl. 1. 4. P.<BR>-त्रसति, -त्रस्यति, -त्रसितुम्, to tremble all over,<BR>start with fear, be afraid, be terrified or frightened:<BR>Caus. -त्रासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to tremble,<BR>frighten, terrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रस्त|संत्रस्त
सन्-त्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling with fear,<BR>afraid, scared, frightened, alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रास|संत्रास|संत्रासः
सन्-त्रास, अस्, m. great trembling, terror, fear,<BR>alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रासित|संत्रासित
सन्-त्रासित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to tremble, terri-<BR>fied, frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रै|संत्रै
सन्त्रै सन्-त्रै (सम्-त्˚), cl. 1. A. -त्रायते,<BR>-त्रातुम्, to protect well or effectually, preserve,<BR>defend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्वर्|संत्वर्
सन्त्वर् सन्-त्वर् (सम्-त्˚), cl. 1. A. -त्वरते,<BR>-त्वरितुम्, to hurry, make great haste, hasten: Caus.<BR>-त्वरयति, -यितुम्, to cause to hurry, cause to<BR>hasten, urge on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्वरमाण
