सन्दशत्
सन्-दशत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, biting together, biting,<BR>pressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दश्य
सन्-दश्य, ind. having bitten; having pressed<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दष्ट|संदष्ट
सन्-दष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, bitten, compressed, pressed<BR>closely together, nipped, pinched; (अम्), n. a parti-<BR>cular fault in pronunciation (arising from keeping the<BR>teeth too close together).<BR>—सन्दष्ट-कुसुम-<BR>शयन, अस्, आ, अम्, indenting (by pressure of the<BR>limbs) a couch of flowers.<BR>—सन्दष्ट-ता, f. a<BR>particular incorrect pronunciation of nasalized vowels,<BR>(see सन्-दष्ट.)<BR>—सन्दष्ट-दन्तच्छद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, biting the lips.<BR>—सन्दष्टौष्ठ (˚ट-<BR>ओष्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, biting or compressing the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दद्
