सन्दहत्
सन्-दहत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, burning up, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दह्यमान
सन्-दह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being burnt, burn-<BR>ing, glowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दाह|संदाह|संदाहः|सन्दाहः
सन्-दाह, अस्, m. burning up, consuming; in-<BR>flammation of the mouth and lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दा|संदा
सन्दा 1. सन्-दा (सम्-दा, see rt. 1. दा), cl.<BR>3. P. A. -ददाति, -दत्ते, -दातुम्, to give together,<BR>present; to hold or keep together; (according to<BR>some) to meet together, (Sāy. सन्-ददे = सम्-<BR>बध्नाति, Ṛg-veda IV. 44, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दा|संदा
सन्दा 2. सन्-दा (सम्-दा, see rt. 3. दा), cl.<BR>2. 4. P. -दाति, -द्यति, -दातुम्, to cut together; to<BR>cut, divide, clip, cut off, pare; to reap, gather toge-<BR>ther.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दान|संदान|संदानं|सन्दानं|संदानः|सन्दानः
1. सन्-दान, अम्, n. the act of cutting or divid-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. that part of an elephant's temples whence<BR>the fluid called Mada issues; [cf. 2. दान.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दित|संदित|सन्दितः
1. सन्-दित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut off, cut; tired, weary,<BR>(Sāy. = सम्यक् खण्डित, दूर-गमनेन श्रान्-<BR>त, Ṛg-veda 1. 25, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दा|संदा
सन्दा 3. सन्-दा (सम्-दा, see rt. 4. दा), cl.<BR>4. P. -द्यति, -दातुम्, Ved. to bind together, fasten<BR>together, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दान|संदान|संदानं|सन्दानं|संदानः|सन्दानः
2. सन्-दान, अम्, n. a rope, cord (especially for<BR>tying cattle); a head-rope, halter, (Sāy. = शिरो-बन्-<BR>धन, Ṛg-veda 1. 162, 16.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दानिका|संदानिका
सन्-दानिका, f. a kind of tree (= अरि-खदिर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दानित|संदानित|सन्दानितः
सन्दानित, अस्, आ, अम्, bound together, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दानिनी|संदानिनी
सन्दानिनी, f. a cow-house; [cf. सन्-धानिनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दाय|संदाय|संदायः
सन्-दाय, ind. having bound together, having tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दित|संदित|सन्दितः
2. सन्-दित, अस्, आ, अम्, bound or fastened toge-<BR>ther, bound, tied; detained, caught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दामितक|संदामितक
सन्दामितक सन्दामितक, अम्, n. (doubtful),<BR>a poem of three stanzas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दाव|संदाव|संदावः|सन्दावः
सन्दाव सन्-दाव, अस्, m. (probably for सन्-<BR>द्राव), flight, retreat, running away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दित|संदित|सन्दितः
सन्दित 1. and 2. सन्-दित. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिश्|संदिश्
सन्दिश् सन्-दिश् (सम्-दिश्), cl. 6. P. -दिशति,<BR>-देष्टुम्, to point out, appoint; to assign, destine<BR>for; to commission, depute, direct, give an order or<BR>message to any one (sometimes with two acc.); to<BR>pronounce, state, communicate intelligence, report,<BR>send any one (acc.) with a message to another<BR>(dat.); to order, command, declare: Caus. -देश-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to point out or declare or<BR>communicate; to invite or ask to speak about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिशत्
सन्-दिशत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, pointing out,<BR>assigning; informing, telling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिश्य|संदिश्य
सन्-दिश्य, ind. having pointed out, having as-<BR>signed, having instructed or directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिष्ट|संदिष्ट|सन्दिष्टं|संदिष्टः
सन्-दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, pointed out, assigned,<BR>indicated, directed; communicated, told, related (as<BR>tidings or a message); promised, engaged, agreed;<BR>(अम्), n. news, tidings, information.<BR>—सन्दिष्टार्-<BR>थ (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्, m. one who communicates infor-<BR>mation or news, a messenger, royal messenger,<BR>herald, pursuivant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देश|संदेश|संदेशः|सन्देशः
सन्-देश, अस्, m. communication of intelligence,<BR>information, tidings, news; a message, commission,<BR>command, direction; a particular kind of sweetmeat<BR>or savoury mixture.<BR>—सन्देश-वाच्, क्, f. communi-<BR>cation of intelligence, news, tidings.<BR>—सन्देश-हर<BR>or सन्देश-हारक, अस्, m. a news-bringer, message-<BR>bearer, messenger, courier; an envoy, ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशक|संदेशकं
सन्-देशक, अम्, n. information, news, tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशित|संदेशित
सन्-देशित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to point out, made<BR>to declare, asked to speak about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देष्टव्य|संदेष्टव्य
सन्-देष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pointed out or<BR>indicated, to be enjoined; to be communicated;<BR>(अम्), n. an injunction, direction, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिह्|संदिह्
सन्दिह् 1. सन्-दिह् (सम्-दिह्), cl. 2. P. A. -देग्-<BR>धि, -दिग्धे, -देग्धुम्, to smear over, besmear,<BR>anoint, plaster over, cover over, obliterate; to heap<BR>together: Pass. -दिह्यते, to be plastered or smeared<BR>over; to become indistinct or doubtful; to be uncertain<BR>or dubious: Caus. -देहयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to make<BR>indistinct or uncertain, confuse, perplex; to be doubt-<BR>ful or uncertain (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्ध|संदिग्ध|सन्दिग्धः
सन्-दिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, besmeared, smeared<BR>over, covered, confused, indistinct, obscure, unintel-<BR>ligible; doubted, questioned, dubious, doubtful; en-<BR>tertaining doubt, unsettled, despairing; uncertain,<BR>unsafe, dangerous riskful.<BR>—सन्दिग्ध-ता, f. or<BR>सन्दिग्ध-त्व, अम्, n. uncertainty, hesitation, in-<BR>distinctness.<BR>—सन्दिग्ध-निश्चय, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who hesitates to hold a firm opinion; one who is<BR>confident in a doubtful matter.<BR>—सन्दिग्ध-बुद्धि<BR>or सन्दिग्ध-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, having a doubtful<BR>mind, sceptical, doubtful about the use of religious<BR>observances.<BR>—सन्दिग्ध-लेख्य, अम्, n. a writing<BR>or document of doubtful meaning or authority.<BR>—सन्दिग्धाक्षर (˚ध-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing indistinct utterance.<BR>—सन्दिग्धार्थ (˚ध-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">Page1059-b+ 76</a>]<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m. doubtful meaning, dubious interpreta-<BR>tion; a disputed debt; (अस्, आ, अम्), having doubtful<BR>meaning, dubious in sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिह्|संदिह्
2. सन्-दिह्, धिक्, f., Ved. smearing over, covering<BR>over; a heap, accumulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिहान|सन्दिहानः
सन्-दिहान, अस्, आ, अम्, doubtful, dubious, un-<BR>certain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिह्य
सन्-दिह्य, ind. having smeared over, being in<BR>doubt, being subject to doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिह्यमान
सन्-दिह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being or becoming<BR>doubtful, uncertain, obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देघ|संदेघ
सन्-देघ, अस्, m., Ved. = सन्-देह below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देह|संदेह|संदेहः|सन्देहः
सन्-देह, अस्, m. doubt, uncertainty, suspense;<BR>risk, danger.<BR>—सन्देह-गन्ध, अस्, m. the<BR>(slightest) shade of a doubt.<BR>—सन्देह-दोला-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being in the swing or perplexity of<BR>doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देहय
सन्-देहय, Nom. P. -देहयति, &c., to render<BR>doubtful or uncertain, make dubious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देहयान|संदेहयान
सन्-देहयान, अस्, आ, अम्, being in doubt or<BR>uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देहिन्|संदेहिन्
सन्देहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, doubtful, dubious; doubting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दी|संदी
सन्दी 1. सन्-दी (सम्-दी, see rt. 2. दी), cl.<BR>3. P. (Ved. Impv. 2nd sing. -दीदिहि or -दिदीहि), to<BR>shine together; to make very bright or manifest,<BR>(Sāy. = सम्यक् प्रकाशयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दी|संदी
सन्दी 2. सन्-दी f. (perhaps connected with<BR>3. सन्-दा), a small bedstead or cot (= खट्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीक्ष्
सन्दीक्ष् सन्-दीक्ष् (सम्-द्˚), cl. 1. A. -दीक्-<BR>षते, -दीक्षितुम्, to consecrate one's self together<BR>or along with, be initiated with others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीक्षित|संदीक्षित
सन्-दीक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, consecrated together,<BR>initiated along with others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीप्|संदीप्
सन्दीप् सन्-दीप् (सम्-दीप्), cl. 4. A. (ep. also<BR>P.) -दीप्यते (-ति), -दीपितुम्, to blaze up, flame;<BR>burn or shine very brightly, glow: Caus. -दीपयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to set on fire, light up, kindle, inflame,<BR>illumine; to inflame with anger; to fire, animate,<BR>excite, inspirit, encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीपन|संदीपनः
सन्-दीपन, अस्, ई, अम्, lighting up, kindling,<BR>inflaming, inspiriting, encouraging, (कामाग्नि-स्˚,<BR>kindling the fire of love, exciting sexual desire);<BR>(अम्), n. the act of lighting up, inflaming, inflam-<BR>mation, kindling (of wrath &c.), encouragement;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of one of the arrows of Kāma-deva<BR>(god of love).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीपित|संदीपित
सन्-दीपित, अस्, आ, अम्, lighted up, kindled, in-<BR>flamed, excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीप्त|संदीप्त
सन्-दीप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, inflamed, flaming, burning,<BR>being on fire.<BR>—सन्दीप्त-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing inflamed or flashing eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीप्य|संदीप्य|सन्दीप्यः
सन्-दीप्य, अस्, m. the plant Celosia Cristata (=<BR>मयूर-शिखा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीप्यत्
सन्-दीप्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, flaming up, burning,<BR>shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दुष्|संदुष्
सन्दुष् सन्-दुष् (सम्-द्˚), cl. 4. P. -दुष्-<BR>यति, -दोष्टुम्, to be or become utterly corrupt,<BR>be defiled or polluted, become unclean: Caus. -दू-<BR>षयति, -यितुम्, to corrupt, defile, pollute, stain,<BR>spoil; to revile, abuse, censure, libel, expose to shame<BR>or infamy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दुष्ट|संदुष्ट
सन्-दुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, polluted, defiled, unclean;<BR>very depraved, wicked, bad; ill-disposed, ill-affected<BR>towards (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दूषण|संदूषणं
सन्-दूषण, अम्, n. the act of vitiating or cor-<BR>rupting, defiling, any vice which causes infamy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दूषित|संदूषित
सन्-दूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, utterly corrupted, vitiated,<BR>defiled, stained, made unclean; made or grown<BR>worse (as a disease); exposed to shame, reviled,<BR>abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दूष्य
सन्-दूष्य, ind. having entirely spoiled or cor-<BR>rupted, having vitiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दुह्|संदुह्
सन्दुह् सन्-दुह् (सम्-दुह्), cl. 2. P. A. -दोग्-<BR>धि, -दुग्धे, &c. (see rt. 2. दुह्), to milk at the<BR>same time, milk together; to milk out, suck: Caus.<BR>-दोहयति, -यितुम्, to cause to milk, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दुग्ध|संदुग्ध
सन्-दुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, milked at the same<BR>time, milked together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दोह|संदोह|संदोहः|सन्दोहः
सन्-दोह, अस्, m. ‘the whole of a quantity of<BR>drawn milk,’ any quantity, multitude, mass, assem-<BR>blage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दोह्य|संदोह्य
सन्-दोह्य, ind. having caused to milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृभ्|संदृभ्
सन्दृभ् सन्-दृभ् (सम्-द्˚), cl. 6. P. -दृ-<BR>भति, -दर्भितुम्, to string or bind together; to<BR>connect, arrange, compose; to collect or bind into<BR>a bunch or tuft, weave into a garland, interweave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्भ|संदर्भ|संदर्भः|सन्दर्भः
सन्-दर्भ, अस्, m. stringing or connecting toge-<BR>ther (especially into a wreath or chaplet), weaving,<BR>interweaving, arranging; collecting, uniting, mixture;<BR>regular connection, coherence, continuity, composi-<BR>tion; construction.<BR>—सन्दर्भ-विरुद्ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, contrary to order or consistency, incoherent,<BR>unconnected.<BR>—सन्दर्भ-शुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>clearly arranged, coherent, connected.<BR>—सन्दर्भ-<BR>शुद्धि, इस्, f. clearness of connection or arrange-<BR>ment (as of the parts of a composition or narrative),<BR>regular coherence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृब्ध|संदृब्ध
सन्-दृब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, strung together, inter-<BR>woven, bound or collected into a tuft or bunch;<BR>arranged, composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृश्|संदृश्
सन्दृश् 1. सन्-दृश् (सम्-द्˚), cl. 1. P. सम्पश्-<BR>यति (ep. also A. -ते), सन्द्रष्टुम्, to see together<BR>or at the same time; to look at steadfastly, see well,<BR>gaze at, see, behold, view, perceive, become aware<BR>of, recognise; to review; to regard, consider, reflect<BR>upon; to calculate, enumerate; to overlook, wink<BR>at, allow to happen; to look about (A. if without<BR>an object, Pāṇ. 1. 3, 29, Vārtt. 2): Pass. -दृश्यते,<BR>to be seen at the same time, appear together; to<BR>look like, resemble, be similar, be equal; to be<BR>observed, become visible, appear: Caus. -दर्शयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to see well, make manifest, show,<BR>display; to represent; to show one's self to any one<BR>(acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शन|संदर्शन|संदर्शनं|सन्दर्शनं
सन्-दर्शन, अम्, n. the act of looking stead-<BR>fastly, gazing, looking, viewing, beholding, seeing,<BR>sight, vision, seeing one another, meeting, appear-<BR>ance, presence; regard, consideration, reflection;<BR>the act of causing to see, showing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शयत्
सन्-दर्शयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to see, show-<BR>ing, pointing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शित|संदर्शित
सन्-दर्शित, अस्, आ, अम्, shown, pointed out;<BR>displayed, manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्श्य
सन्-दर्श्य, ind. having made to appear, having<BR>shown, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिदर्शयिषु|संदिदर्शयिषु
सन्-दिदर्शयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to show,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृश्|संदृश्
2. सन्-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. one who sees well or<BR>thoroughly, (Sāy. सम्यक् पश्यति यः); (क्), f.<BR>sight, vision; a glance, look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृश्य|संदृश्य
सन्-दृश्य, ind. having looked at, having beheld,<BR>&c.; having considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृश्यमान
सन्-दृश्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being seen well or<BR>thoroughly, being looked at, being foreseen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृष्ट|संदृष्ट
सन्-दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, seen, beheld, (पाप-<BR>सन्दृष्ट, having an evil aspect); foreseen, antici-<BR>pated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृष्टि|संदृष्टि
सन्-दृष्टि, इस्, f. complete sight, full view; a<BR>sight, glance, look, aspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पश्यत्
सम्-पश्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, looking at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पश्यमान
सम्-पश्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देह|संदेह|संदेहः|सन्देहः
सन्देह सन्-देह. See under 1. सन्-दिह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दो|संदो
सन्दो सन्-दो (सम्-दो) = 2. सन्-दा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दोह|संदोह|संदोहः|सन्दोहः
सन्दोह सन्-दोह. See under सन्-दुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्द्युत्
सन्द्युत् सन्-द्युत् (सम्-द्˚), cl. 1. A. -द्योतते,<BR>-द्योतितुम्, to shine together with, shine along with,<BR>rival in shining; to shine forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्द्रु|संद्रु
सन्द्रु सन्-द्रु (सम्-द्रु), cl. 1. P. -द्रवति,<BR>-द्रोतुम्, to run together; to run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्द्राव|संद्राव|संद्रावः|सन्द्रावः
सन्-द्राव, अस्, m. running together, running<BR>away, flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धन्व्|संधन्व्
सन्धन्व् सन्-धन्व् (सम्-ध्˚), cl. 1. A.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-a" target="_blank">Page1060-a+ 80</a>]<BR>-धन्वते, &c., to flow towards, be directed towards,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda III. 31, 1. according to Sāy. सन्-द-<BR>धन्वे = आत्मानं सन्धत्ते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धा
सन्धा सन्-धा (सम्-धा), cl. 3. P. A. -द-<BR>धाति, -धत्ते (ep. -दधामहे = -दध्महे),<BR>-धातुम् (ep. -धितुम्), to place or hold together,<BR>join together, unite, combine, connect, fasten toge-<BR>ther; to repair, restore, mend, heal; to make good,<BR>atone for, redress; to put together, compose, com-<BR>pound, make, construct, prepare, mix; to draw toge-<BR>ther, contract, close up, close; to bring together,<BR>collect; to bring together or unite in friendship,<BR>reconcile; to make a compact or agreement, con-<BR>clude a league or alliance, come to terms, make<BR>peace with (with inst. or sometimes with acc.); to be<BR>associated or allied with (A.); to come near, approach;<BR>to fix or compose the mind or thoughts, (see under<BR>rt. 1. धा); to put or lay down by the side of, put<BR>or lay on, fix on (e. g. शरं धनुषि सन्-<BR>दधाति or सन्-धत्ते, he fixes an arrow on a<BR>bow; sometimes धनुर् शरेण सन्-धा, to con-<BR>nect a bow with an arrow); to aim at, direct towards;<BR>to take hold of, grasp, support, sustain; to render<BR>aid, assist; to take hold of with the mind, compre-<BR>hend, conceive; to hold, possess, have; to perform,<BR>do; to grant, yield; to inflict; to be a match for,<BR>hold out against (A.); to employ, make use of<BR>(with inst.): Pass. -धीयते, to be joined together,<BR>be connected, unite one's self with, become recon-<BR>ciled, &c.; to become possessed of (with inst.):<BR>Desid. -धित्सति, to wish to place or join together,<BR>desire to unite or repair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहित|संहितः
सं-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. 1. धा with सम्),<BR>put together, placed together, conjoined, combined,<BR>joined, connected, united, attached, agreed, agreeing<BR>with, conformable to, in accordance with, (धर्म-<BR>स्˚, in accordance with justice); referring to, relating<BR>to; collected, assembled; compiled; placed, fixed;<BR>endowed with, provided, furnished, equipped, pos-<BR>sessed of, accompanied by, abounding in; caused by;<BR>(आ), f. conjunction, combination, connection, union;<BR>a collection, compilation, compendium; any metho-<BR>dical or arranged collection of texts or verses; the<BR>real continuous hymnical text of the Veda as formed<BR>out of the Padas or separate words (see पद) by<BR>proper phonetic changes according to various schools,<BR>(the Prātiśākhyas teaching how these Padas must<BR>change in order to become the Saṃhitā; hence the<BR>term Saṃhitā is applied to that portion of the Veda<BR>which contains the collection of Mantras or hymns<BR>thus formed, collected, and arranged according to<BR>particular Śākhās or schools [cf. शाखा]; the number<BR>of Vedas being four, and the Yajur-veda having two<BR>branches, it follows that there must be at least five<BR>Saṃhitās of the Veda, viz. the Ṛk-s˚, Taittirīya-s˚,<BR>Vājasaneyi-s˚, Sāma-s˚, Atharva-s˚; for the division<BR>of the Saṃhitā of the Śākala school of the Ṛg-veda,<BR>which is the only Śākhā of this Veda preserved, see<BR>मण्डल; Vyāsa is said to have compiled a Saṃ-<BR>hitā of the Purāṇas, the substance of which is sup-<BR>posed to be represented by the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa); a<BR>compilation or compendium of laws, code, digest;<BR>(in grammar) the junction or combination of letters<BR>according to euphonic rules (= सन्धि, but some-<BR>times considered rather as the state preparatory to<BR>the actual junction than the junction itself); the<BR>Being who holds together and supports the universe,<BR>(a term applied to the Supreme Being, according to<BR>some); N. of an astrological work; [cf. वृहत्-स्˚.]<BR>—संहित-पुष्पिका, f. a particular plant (= मि-<BR>श्रेया).<BR>—संहिता-पाठ, अस्, m. the continuous<BR>text of the Veda (as formed out of the Pada-pāṭha).<BR>—संहिता-प्रदीप, अस्, m. ‘light of the Saṃhitā,’<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—संहिता-वत्, ind. as in the Saṃ-<BR>hitā text.<BR>—संहितेषु (˚त-इषु), उस्, उस्, उ, one<BR>who has fitted or placed an arrow on a bow-string.<BR>—संहितोपनिषद (˚ता-उप्˚) or संहितोपनि-<BR>षद्-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N. of a Brāhmaṇa (of<BR>the Sāma-veda).<BR>—संहितोरु (˚त-ऊरु), उस्, उस् or<BR>ऊस्, उ, having the thighs joined (through obesity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दधान
सन्-दधान, अस्, आ, अम्, placing or holding<BR>together; being at peace with, making peace, being<BR>reconciled; fixing in or on; holding, possessing, having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध|संध
सन्-ध, अस्, आ, अम्, holding together; joined,<BR>united, closely blended; placing in or on; possessing;<BR>(आ), f. junction, intimate union, association, identi-<BR>fication; alliance, compact, stipulation, agreement,<BR>assent, promise; twilight (as joining night and<BR>morning or day and evening; cf. सन्ध्या); fixation,<BR>steadiness, fixedness; steady continuance in any state;<BR>state, condition; a boundary, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धय|संधय
सन्धय, Nom. P. -धयति, -यितुम्, to join<BR>together, reconcile; to fasten on, (see सन्-धित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धातव्य|संधातव्य
सन्-धातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed or held<BR>together, to be united or connected, to be allied<BR>with, to be reconciled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धातृ|संधातृ
सन्-धातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who puts together<BR>or joins, a joiner, uniter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धान|संधान|संधानं|सन्धानं
1. सन्-धान, अम्, n. the act of placing or holding<BR>together, joining, junction, uniting, tying or binding<BR>together, intimate union, combining, combination,<BR>repairing, restoration; composing, compounding,<BR>mixing, preparation; drawing together, contraction<BR>(as of the skin by astringents &c.); bringing toge-<BR>ther, alliance, league, association, companionship,<BR>peace; the act of fixing an arrow on a bow-string;<BR>directing, taking aim; direction; advertence, atten-<BR>tion; sustaining, supporting, reception, receiving;<BR>spirituous liquor; a preparation of pickles &c. (made<BR>from the Vilva and other fruits); mixed or bell-<BR>metal (= सौराष्ट्र); a kind of relish eaten to<BR>excite thirst; sour rice-gruel; (अम्, ई), n. f. distil-<BR>lation, distilling; the manufacture of fermented or<BR>spirituous liquors; (ई), f. a braziery, foundery, place<BR>where metals are wrought or stored.<BR>—सन्धान-<BR>करण, अस्, ई, अम्, causing union or combination,<BR>who or what re-unites or heals or reconciles; uniting,<BR>connecting; (अम्), n. the act of combining or unit-<BR>ing; healing; allying, making peace.<BR>—सन्धान-<BR>कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, = सन्धान-करण above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धान|संधान|संधानं|सन्धानं
2. सन्-धान, अस्, आ, अम् (ep. for सन्-दधान),<BR>placing together, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानिका|संधानिका
सन्धानिका, f. a kind of pickle or sauce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानित|संधानित|सन्धानितः
सन्धानित, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. 1. सन्-धान), joined,<BR>united, strung together; bound, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानिन्|संधानिन्
सन्धानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, tying or binding together;<BR>clever in taking aim, shrewd; (इनी), f. a cow-house<BR>(= गो-गृह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानी|संधानी
सन्-धानी, f. See under 1. सन्-धान above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धाय|संधाय
सन्-धाय, ind. having placed together, having<BR>joined or united; having repaired; having formed<BR>an alliance or made peace; having fixed an arrow<BR>on a bow-string, having taken aim, shooting at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धि|संधि|संधिः|सन्धिः
सन्-धि, इस्, m. placing or holding together, con-<BR>junction, junction, connection, combination, union,<BR>contact; composition, construction, structure; distil-<BR>lation; compact, agreement, alliance, league, reconcili-<BR>ation, peace, making a treaty of peace, negotiating alli-<BR>ances, (one of the six Guṇas or courses of action<BR>recommended to kings, see गुण; many kinds of<BR>treaty are enumerated, e. g. अदृष्ट-पुरुषः<BR>सन्धिः, an alliance concluded without the inter-<BR>vention of an agent; उच्छिन्नः सन्धिः, a treaty<BR>purchased by the cession of fertile territories; काञ्-<BR>चनः सन्धिः, ‘golden alliance,’ an alliance which<BR>lasts throughout the lifetime of the parties, each of<BR>whom pursues the same object, see also कपाल-स्˚,<BR>सन्तान-स्˚); euphonic junction of final and initial<BR>letters in grammar, (every sentence in Sanskrit being<BR>regarded as a euphonic chain, the links being syl-<BR>lables rather than words, and a break in the chain<BR>denoting the end of a sentence, commonly called<BR>‘a Virāma or stop;’ this Sandhi or euphonic coa-<BR>lition is applied both to the final and initial letters<BR>of separate Padas or finished words in a sentence<BR>and to the final letters of Dhātus or roots, and Prāti-<BR>padikas or nominal bases when combined with ter-<BR>minations and affixes to form such words); a con-<BR>necting link (as of a perpendicular in mensuration);<BR>a joint, articulation (of the body &c.); juncture,<BR>critical juncture, opportune moment; division, sepa-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">Page1060-c+ 81</a>]<BR>ration; breaking, dividing; a breach, chasm, mine,<BR>hole, opening or cavity made in a wall or underneath<BR>a building by a housebreaker or enemy &c.; the<BR>vagina or vulva (in anatomy); a division in a<BR>drama (e. g. critical junctures, changes of situa-<BR>tion &c. considered as breaks though contributing<BR>to the connection of the whole); a fold; an interval,<BR>pause, rest; a period at the expiration of each Yuga<BR>or age (equivalent to one sixth of its duration and<BR>intervening before the commencement of the next;<BR>occurring also at the end of each Manv-antara and<BR>Kalpa).<BR>—सन्धि-कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in the<BR>art of making treaties or forming alliances.<BR>—सन्-<BR>धि-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. ‘joint-knot,’ a synovial gland<BR>connecting and lubricating a joint.<BR>—सन्धि-चौर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘hole-thief,’ one who enters a house by<BR>undermining it, a housebreaker.<BR>—सन्धि-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced by Sandhi; (अम्), n. spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>—सन्धि-जीवक, अस्, m. one who lives by<BR>dishonest means (especially by making matches or<BR>as a go-between).<BR>—सन्धि-तस्, ind. from an alli-<BR>ance.<BR>—सन्धि-दूषण, अम्, n. the violation of<BR>a treaty or alliance.<BR>—सन्धि-पूजा, f., N. of the<BR>third period in the great autumnal Durgā-pūjā.<BR>—सन्धि-प्रबन्धन, अम्, n. (in anatomy) the<BR>ligament of a joint.<BR>—सन्धि-बन्ध, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Kæmpferia Rotunda.<BR>—सन्धि-बन्धन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘joint-binding,’ a ligament, tendon, nerve.<BR>—सन्धि-भङ्ग, अस्, m. joint-fracture, dislocation<BR>of a joint.<BR>—सन्धि-मति, इस्, m., N. of the minister<BR>of Jayendra, king of Kaśmīra.<BR>—सन्धि-मुक्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘joint-loosened,’ dislocated.<BR>—सन्धि-मुक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. ‘joint-loosening,’ dislocation of a joint.<BR>—सन्-<BR>धि-रन्ध्रका, f. a hole or breach in a wall.<BR>—सन्धि-विग्रह, औ, m. du. peace and war.<BR>—सन्धि-विग्रहक, अस्, m. one who has the<BR>charge of peace and war, a chief minister.<BR>—सन्धि-<BR>विग्रहाधिकार (˚ह-अध्˚), अस्, m. superintend-<BR>ence of peace and war, war-ministry.<BR>—सन्धि-<BR>विग्रहाधिकारिन्, ई, m. superintendent of peace and<BR>war, a chief political minister.<BR>—सन्धि-विचक्षण,<BR>अस्, m. one skilled in peace-making, an able nego-<BR>tiator of treaties.<BR>—सन्धि-विद्, त्, त्, त्, skilled in<BR>alliances; (त्), m. a negotiator of treaties, a minister.<BR>—सन्धि-वेला, f. ‘a connecting period, time of<BR>junction,’ any period or time which connects parts<BR>of the day or night or fortnight (e. g. morning,<BR>noon, evening, new moon, the first or thirteenth day<BR>of the fortnight, full moon, &c.).<BR>—सन्धि-सितासित-<BR>रोग (˚त-अस्˚), अस्, m. a kind of disease.<BR>—सन्धि-<BR>स्तोत्र, अम्, n., N. of a particular hymn.<BR>—सन्धि-<BR>हारक, अस्, m. a housebreaker, (see सन्धि-<BR>चौर.)<BR>—सन्ध्य्-अक्षर, अम्, n. a compound<BR>vowel, diphthong, N. of the diphthongs ए, ऐ, ओ,<BR>औ; [cf. समानाक्षर.]<BR>—सन्ध्य्-अध्याय, अस्,<BR>m. an Adhyāya or chapter on Sandhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिक|संधिक|संधिकः
सन्धिक, अस्, m. a kind of fever (said to be<BR>caused by a vitiated state of the three humors of<BR>the body); (आ), f. distillation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिग|संधिग
सन्धिग, a kind of disease, (probably for सन्-<BR>धिक.)<BR>—सन्धिग-चिकित्सा, f. the treatment or<BR>cure of Sandhiga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धित|संधित|सन्धितः
सन्धित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. सन्धय), joined or<BR>fastened together, united, strung, bound, tied; recon-<BR>ciled, allied; fixed, fitted, prepared, mixed together;<BR>pickled; (अम्), n. pickles, acid preparations, spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>—सन्धितेषु (˚त-इषु), उस्, उस्, उ, having an<BR>arrow fitted on a bow-string; [cf. संहितेषु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धितव्य|संधितव्य
सन्धितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = सन्-धेय below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धित्सु|संधित्सु
सन्-धित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to make peace or<BR>form an alliance with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिनी|संधिनी
सन्धिनी, f. a cow with calf, one which has just<BR>taken the bull; a cow milked unseasonably.<BR>—सन्-<BR>धिनी-क्षीर, अम्, n. the milk of a cow in heat,<BR>(prohibited as an article of food.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिला|संधिला
सन्धिला, f. a breach or hole made in a wall; a<BR>chasm, mine, pit; spirituous liquor; a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धीयमान
सन्-धीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being joined toge-<BR>ther by the rules of Sandhi, (as words in the Saṃhitā<BR>text of the Vedas, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धेय|संधेय
सन्-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be joined or united, &c.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">Page1061-a+ 78</a>]<BR>to be connected or allied, &c.; to be reconciled; to<BR>be made peace with; to be aimed at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्य|संध्य
सन्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, of or belonging to Sandhi,<BR>relating to euphonic conjunction, joined together by<BR>Sandhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्या|संध्या
1. सन्ध्या, f. (for 2. see under सन्-ध्यै), hold-<BR>ing or joining together, union, conjunction, connec-<BR>tion; joint, division; boundary, limit; twilight (a<BR>period consisting of two Daṇḍas connecting day and<BR>night), morning or evening twilight, evening, dusk;<BR>early morning, day-break; Twilight personified as<BR>daughter of Brahmā and wife of Śiva; the period<BR>which precedes a Yuga or age of the world (see युग);<BR>any one of the three divisions of the day, (forenoon,<BR>noon, and afternoon); morning or evening or mid-<BR>day prayer (or any religious exercise, such as abstrac-<BR>tion, meditation, repetition of Mantras, sipping<BR>water, &c., performed at the three divisions of the<BR>day); promise, agreement, assent; a kind of jasmine<BR>(according to some); N. of a river.<BR>—सन्ध्यांश<BR>(˚या-अं˚), अस्, m. ‘portion of twilight,’ the period<BR>at the end of each Yuga, (see युग.)<BR>—सन्ध्यांशु<BR>(˚या-अं˚), उस्, m. ‘twilight-ray,’ twilight.<BR>—सन्ध्या-<BR>काल, अस्, m. twilight-period, (a term applied to the<BR>intervals of a Yuga, see युग); evening.<BR>—सन्ध्या-<BR>चल (˚या-अच्˚), अस्, m. ‘twilight-mountain,’ N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—सन्ध्या-त्रय, अम्, n. the three<BR>divisions or periods of the day (i. e. forenoon, noon,<BR>and afternoon).<BR>—सन्ध्या-त्व, अम्, n. the state of<BR>twilight; the time of twilight (period for devotional<BR>exercises).<BR>—सन्ध्या-नाटिन्, ई, m. ‘dancing at<BR>evening twilight,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सन्ध्या-पा-<BR>त्र, अम्, n. a vessel used for pouring out water in<BR>performing the Sandhyā ceremonies.<BR>—सन्ध्या-<BR>पुष्पी, f. a kind of jasmine; nutmeg (= जाति or<BR>जाती).<BR>—सन्ध्या-बल, अस्, m. ‘strong in twilight,’<BR>a demon, imp, Rākṣasa.<BR>—सन्ध्या-बलि, इस्, m.<BR>‘receiving twilight-oblations,’ a clay or stone image<BR>of the bull of Śiva (usually standing in the temples<BR>of that deity).<BR>—सन्ध्याभ्र (˚या-अभ्˚), अम्, n.<BR>an evening cloud; a sort of red chalk (= सुवर्ण-<BR>गैरिक).<BR>—सन्ध्या-मङ्गल, अम्, n. an evening<BR>solemnity or religious service.<BR>—सन्ध्या-राग, अम्,<BR>n. ‘having the colour of twilight,’ red-lead.<BR>—सन्-<BR>ध्याराम (˚या-आर्˚), अस्, m. ‘delighting in San-<BR>dhyā,’ epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—सन्ध्या-वन्दन,<BR>अम्, n. morning and evening adoration or prayer.<BR>—सन्ध्या-विधि, इस्, m. a Sandhyā rite, (see<BR>above.)<BR>—सन्ध्या-शङ्ख, अस्, m. the evening<BR>conch, the conch which sounds the evening hour.<BR>—सन्ध्या-समय, अस्, m. twilight-period, even-<BR>ing; a portion of each Yuga, (see युग.)<BR>—सन्-<BR>ध्योपनिषद् (˚य-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad<BR>belonging to the Atharva-veda.<BR>—सन्ध्योपासन<BR>(˚या-उप्˚), अम्, n. worship performed at the Sandhyās,<BR>(see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धारण|संधारण|संधारणं
सन्धारण सन्-धारण, &c. See under<BR>सन्-धृ, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धाव्|संधाव्
सन्धाव् 1. सन्-धाव् (सम्-ध्˚), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-धावति, -ते, -धावितुम्, to run together; to run<BR>up to violently, assail, attack; to run to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धाव्|संधाव्
सन्धाव् 2. सन्-धाव् (सम्-ध्˚), cl. 1. A.<BR>-धावते, -धावितुम्, Ved. to rub one's self, wash<BR>one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धाव्य
सन्-धाव्य, ind. having washed one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्ष्|संधुक्ष्
सन्धुक्ष् सन्-धुक्ष् (सम्-ध्˚), cl. 1. A.<BR>-धुक्षते, -धुक्षितुम्, to kindle; to animate,<BR>revive: Caus. -धुक्षयति, -यितुम्, to set on fire,<BR>light up, inflame, animate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्षण|संधुक्षणं
सन्-धुक्षण, अम्, n. kindling, inflaming, in-<BR>flammation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्षयत्
सन्-धुक्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, setting on fire,<BR>kindling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्षित|संधुक्षित
सन्-धुक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, kindled, inflamed,<BR>lighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्ष्यमाण
सन्-धुक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being kindled<BR>or lighted up; being increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धू|संधू
सन्धू सन्-धू (सम्-धू), cl. 5. P. A. -धू-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">Page1061-b+ 76</a>]<BR>नोति, -धूनुते (also -धुनोति, -धुनुते, see rt.<BR>1. धू), -धोतुम्, -धवितुम्, to scatter or distri-<BR>bute liberally, bestow; to seize or carry off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धृ|संधृ
सन्धृ सन्-धृ (सम्-धृ), cl. 10. P. A.<BR>-धारयति, -ते (Impf. ep. सम्-अधारम् = -अधा-<BR>रयम्), -यितुम्, to hold together; to hold up,<BR>support, sustain, preserve, maintain; to hold back,<BR>restrain; to hold, have, possess; to hold, bear, carry;<BR>to hold, observe, keep; to hold or fix the mind<BR>(मनस्) on anything (loc.); to keep in the mind<BR>or memory, remember; to bear, suffer, endure, to<BR>hold out, remain alive, survive, exist: Pass. -धार्-<BR>यते, to be held together or supported, be held up,<BR>&c.; to be maintained or governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धारण|संधारण|संधारणं
सन्-धारण, अम्, आ, n. f. holding together,<BR>holding in, restraining, observing, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धारयत्
सन्-धारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, holding or possessing<BR>completely; keeping in mind, remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धारयमाण
सन्-धारयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, holding together,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धारयाण
सन्-धारयाण, अस्, आ, अम्, holding together,<BR>supporting, &c.; keeping back, restraining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धार्य|संधार्य|सन्धार्य्य
सन्-धार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be held or observed<BR>or followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धार्यमाण
सन्-धार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being held toge-<BR>ther, being held or maintained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धृत|संधृत
सन्-धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, held together, compacted;<BR>closely connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धृष्
सन्धृष् सन्-धृष् (सम्-ध्˚), cl. 1. P. -धर्-<BR>षति, &c., to injure greatly, destroy: Caus. -धर्ष-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to violate, ravish; to disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धर्षित|संधर्षित
सन्-धर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly injured, violated,<BR>disgraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्मा|संध्मा
सन्ध्मा सन्-ध्मा (सम्-ध्˚), cl. 1. P. -ध-<BR>मति, -ध्मातुम्, to blow together; to melt toge-<BR>ther; to proclaim aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यै|संध्यै
सन्ध्यै सन्-ध्यै (सम्-ध्˚), cl. 1. P. -ध्या-<BR>यति, -ध्यातुम्, to reflect on, think about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्या|संध्या
2. सन्-ध्या, f. (for 1. see col. 1), reflection, medi-<BR>tation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यातृ
सन्-ध्यातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who reflects or<BR>thinks about; one who binds, (Manu VIII. 342;<BR>probably for सन्-दातृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न|सन्नः
सन्न सन्न, सन्नक. See under rt. 1. सद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नद्|संनद्
सन्नद् सन्-नद् (सम्-नद्), cl. 1. P. -नदति,<BR>-नदितुम्, to cry aloud, roar: Caus. -नादयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to resound, fill with noise or cries;<BR>to cry aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाद|संनाद|संनादः
सन्-नाद, अस्, m. shouting together, a confused<BR>or tumultuous noise, uproar, din, clamour; a voice,<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नादयत्
सन्-नादयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, making to sound,<BR>causing a clamour or uproar, making to resound or<BR>ring with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नादित|संनादित
सन्-नादित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to resound, filled<BR>with noise or cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नद्ध|संनद्ध|सन्नद्धः
सन्नद्ध सन्-नद्ध. See under सन्-नह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नम्|संनम्
सन्नम् सन्-नम् (सम्-नम्), cl. 1. P. A. -न-<BR>मति, -ते, -नन्तुम्, to bend together, bend down,<BR>bow down before, bow to; to bow down in sub-<BR>mission, submit to, comply with, obey, be obedient<BR>(A.); to bend in the right direction, make straight,<BR>bring into order, direct, make ready, accomplish; to<BR>be accomplished: Caus. -नामयति, -नमयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to bend, cause to bow or curve, cause to<BR>sink; to make crooked, bend together, contract;<BR>to bend in a particular direction, make right, make<BR>ready, prepare for a particular object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नत|संनत
सन्-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, bent together, bowed down,<BR>bent, curved, stooping; bent down through sorrow,<BR>dispirited, downcast; deepened; contracted.<BR>—सन्-<BR>नत-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more deepened, deeper.<BR>—सन्नत-भ्रू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, bending or contracting<BR>the brow, frowning.<BR>—सन्नताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having the body bent, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नति|संनति|संनतिः|सन्नतिः
सन्-नति, इस्, f. bowing down, reverential salutation,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">Page1061-c+ 75</a>]<BR>obeisance; reverence, humility; Humility (personified<BR>as daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma); sound,<BR>noise.<BR>—सन्नति-मत्, आन्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नमत्
सन्-नमत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bending down, bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नममान
सन्-नममान, अस्, आ, अम्, bending together,<BR>bending in the right direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नमित
सन्-नमित, अस्, आ, अम्, bent together, bent.<BR>—सन्नमितोभयांस (˚त-उभय-अं˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having both shoulders bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नम्य
सन्-नम्य, ind. having bent together, having<BR>bowed down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाम
सन्-नाम, अस्, m. bowing down before any one,<BR>worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नमस्य|संनमस्य
सन्नमस्य सन्-नमस्य (सम्-न्˚), Nom. P.<BR>-नमस्यति, -यितुम्, to show respect or honour, to<BR>worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नय|संनय|संनयः|सन्नयः
सन्नय सन्-नय. See under सन्-नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नर्द्|संनर्द्
सन्नर्द् सन्-नर्द् (सम्-न्˚), cl. 1. P. -नर्दति<BR>(ep. also A. -ते), &c., to roar aloud, bellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नर्दमान
सन्-नर्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, roaring aloud, bel-<BR>lowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नश्|संनश्
सन्नश् 1. सन्-नश् (सम्-नश्, see rt. 1. नश्),<BR>cl. 1. P. A. -नशति, -ते, &c. (according to some<BR>Ved. Inf. सन्-नशे), Ved. to reach, attain, (Sāy. न<BR>सन्-नशे = न सम्यग्-आपनीयः, i. e. परैर्<BR>अ-प्रधृष्यः, not to be overcome by others,<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 3, 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नश्|संनश्
सन्नश् 2. सन्-नश् (सम्-नश्), cl. 4. P. -नश्-<BR>यति, -नशितुम्, -नंष्टुम्, to disappear entirely,<BR>perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नष्ट|संनष्ट
सन्-नष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely disappeared,<BR>utterly perished, ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नस्|संनस्
सन्नस् सन्-नस् (सम्-नस्), cl. 1. A. -नसते,<BR>&c., Ved. to come together, meet together, assemble,<BR>approach, be united, (in Ṛg-veda II. 16, 8. accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. नसीमहि = व्याप्येमहि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नह्|संनह्
सन्नह् सन्-नह् (सम्-नह्), cl. 4. P. A. -नह्-<BR>यति, -ते, -नद्धुम्, to bind or tie together, bind<BR>over, bind or fasten on, to put or gird on, clothe<BR>with, furnish with; to put anything on one's self,<BR>accoutre one's self, dress or arm one's self with (A.<BR>with acc.; सन्नह्यध्वम् चारूणि दंशनानि,<BR>put ye on your beautiful armour); to prepare for<BR>doing anything (with inf.): Pass. -नह्यते, to be<BR>fastened on, &c.; to be harnessed: Caus. -नाहयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to gird or bind on, cause to clothe<BR>or dress one's self in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नद्ध|संनद्ध|सन्नद्धः
सन्-नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound or fastened or<BR>tied together, bound round, girded round, girded on,<BR>fastened on, girt, bound (in general), dressed or clad<BR>in, armed, mailed, accoutred; harnessed; arranged,<BR>arrayed, prepared, provided, ready for battle, pre-<BR>pared or ready (in general); provided with destruc-<BR>tive weapons, murderous, felonious; provided with<BR>charms, &c.; well provided or furnished with any-<BR>thing; closely attached or connected, in close con-<BR>tact with, contiguous, bordering, near.<BR>—सन्नद्ध-<BR>कवच, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has girded on his<BR>armour, clad in mail or accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नहन|संनहनं
सन्-नहन, अम्, n. the act of arming, preparing,<BR>making one's self ready, preparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नह्य|संनह्य
सन्-नह्य, ind. having girded on, having bound<BR>or fastened on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नह्यत्
सन्-नह्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, binding, fastening,<BR>girding on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नह्यमान
सन्-नह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being girt with,<BR>being clothed in; being accoutred or harnessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाह|संनाह|संनाहः|सन्नाहः
सन्-नाह, अस्, m. girding on armour, arming for<BR>battle; accoutrements, armour, mail, a coat of mail<BR>(made of iron or thick quilted cotton).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाह्य|संनाह्य|संनाह्यः|सन्नाह्यः
सन्नाह्य, अस्, m. a war elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकाश्|संनिकाश्
सन्निकाश् सन्-नि-काश् (सम्-), Caus. -काश-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to make quite clear, manifest, reveal;<BR>to make known, announce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकीर्ण|संनिकीर्ण
सन्निकीर्ण सन्-निकीर्ण. See सन्-नि-कॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकृष्|संनिकृष्
सन्निकृष् सन्-नि-कृष् (सम्-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-कर्षति, &c., to draw together, draw near, attract,<BR>contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकर्ष|संनिकर्ष|संनिकर्षः|सन्निकर्षः
सन्-निकर्ष, अस्, m. bringing or drawing near,<BR>nearness, proximity, vicinity, presence; connection,<BR>relation; connection of an Indriya or organ of sense<BR>with its Viṣaya or object, (this is the source of<BR>Jñāna according to the Nyāya phil., and is of two<BR>kinds, 1. Laukika, which is sixfold, and 2. A-laukika,<BR>which is threefold.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकर्षण|संनिकर्षण|संनिकर्षणं|सन्निकर्षणं
सन्-निकर्षण, अम्, n. the act of drawing toge-<BR>ther, bringing near, approaching near, approximating,<BR>approximation, proximity, vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकृष्ट|संनिकृष्ट|सन्निकृष्टः
सन्-निकृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn together, drawn<BR>near, brought near, contiguous, proximate, approxi-<BR>mate, near, adjacent, close; (अम्), ind. near, close<BR>to; (अम्), n. proximity, vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकॄ
सन्निकॄ सन्-नि-कॄ (सम्-), cl. 6. P. -किरति,<BR>&c., to scatter along, strew about; to stretch out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकीर्ण|संनिकीर्ण
सन्-निकीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, scattered along; stretched<BR>out at full length, lying; flung, thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निक्षार|संनिक्षार
सन्निक्षार सन्-निक्षार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. क्षर्<BR>with नि and सम्), the Piyāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निक्षिप्|संनिक्षिप्
सन्निक्षिप् सन्-नि-क्षिप् (सम्-), cl. 6. P.<BR>-क्षिपति, -क्षेप्तुम्, to throw down, put or lay<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निगम्|संनिगम्
सन्निगम् सन्-नि-गम् (सम्-), cl. 1. P. -गच्-<BR>छति, -गन्तुम्, to go or come together with, unite<BR>with any one (inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निग्रह्|संनिग्रह्
सन्निग्रह् सन्-नि-ग्रह् (सम्-), cl. 9. P. A.<BR>-गृह्णाति, -गृह्णीते, &c., -ग्रहीतुम्, to hold or<BR>keep down, keep under, overpower, subdue; to hold<BR>or keep back, keep in, restrain, suppress, obstruct;<BR>to lay hold of, seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निगृह्य
सन्-निगृह्य, ind. having held or kept in, sup-<BR>pressing; overpowering, vanquishing, discomfiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निघृष्|संनिघृष्
सन्निघृष् सन्-नि-घृष् (सम्-), cl. 1. P.<BR>-घर्षति, -घर्षितुम्, to rub or pound down<BR>together, mix together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निचि
सन्निचि सन्-नि-चि (सम्-), cl. 5. P. A. -चिनोति,<BR>-चिनुते, -चेतुम्, to pile or heap up together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निचय|संनिचय|संनिचयः
सन्-निचय, अस्, m. piling or heaping together, a<BR>collection; (अस्, आ, अम्), heaped together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निचित|संनिचित
सन्-निचित, अस्, आ, अम्, heaped together, collected;<BR>congested, constipated, stagnated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निदृश्
सन्निदृश् सन्-नि-दृश् (सम्-), Caus. -दर्श-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to be observed, bring into<BR>view, show, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निदर्शित|संनिदर्शित
सन्-निदर्शित, अस्, आ, अम्, brought into view,<BR>shown, pointed out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधा|संनिधा
सन्निधा सन्-नि-धा (सम्-), cl. 3. P. A. -द-<BR>धाति, -धत्ते, -धातुम्, to put or place down near<BR>together, put in the same place, to place or put down<BR>near; to deposit; to put into; to place or fix upon,<BR>direct towards, (दृष्टिम् सन्निधा, to fix the eyes<BR>upon; मनः or हृदयं सन्निधा, to fix or<BR>direct the mind or thoughts, see rt. 1. धा); to<BR>place together, collect, pile up; to deliver over,<BR>assign; to look at closely, inspect, observe: Pass.<BR>-धीयते, to be put together in the same place, to<BR>be placed near, to be near, to be present: Caus.<BR>-धापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be put down near<BR>or close at hand, to bring near: Pass. of Caus. -धाप्-<BR>यते, to appear or become manifested in the presence<BR>of (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निध|संनिध|सन्निधं
सन्-निध, अम्, n. juxta-position, proximity, vici-<BR>nity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधातृ|संनिधातृ
सन्-निधातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what places<BR>near, one who brings near or introduces; depositing,<BR>placing in deposit; receiving in charge; (ता), m. a<BR>receiver of stolen goods; an officer who introduces<BR>people at court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधान|संनिधान|संनिधानं|सन्निधानं
सन्-निधान, अम्, n. placing down together,<BR>juxta-position, proximity, nearness, vicinity, neigh-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">Page1062-b+ 77</a>]<BR>bourhood, presence, appearance, perceptibility; plac-<BR>ing down, depositing; a receptacle; receiving, taking<BR>charge of; (ए), ind. in the vicinity or presence of,<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधाप्य
सन्-निधाप्य, ind. having caused to be placed<BR>near, having brought near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधाय
सन्-निधाय, ind. having placed near together,<BR>having placed near at hand; having piled up or col-<BR>lected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधि|संनिधि|संनिधिः|सन्निधिः
सन्-निधि, इस्, m. placing near; juxta-position,<BR>proximity, approximation, nearness, vicinity, presence,<BR>appearance, visibility, perceptibility; receiving, taking<BR>charge of.<BR>—सन्निधि-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being near,<BR>neighbouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निहित|संनिहित|सन्निहितं
सन्-निहित, अस्, आ, अम्, placed near together,<BR>near, contiguous, proximate; close at hand, present;<BR>deposited, fixed, laid up [cf. हृदय-स्˚]; prepared,<BR>ready; staying, being.<BR>—सन्निहितापाय (˚त-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having loss or destruction near at hand,<BR>transient, transitory, fleeting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निनी|संनिनी
सन्निनी सन्-नि-नी (सम्-), cl. 1. P. A. -न-<BR>यति, -ते, -नेतुम्, Ved. to bring together, pour toge-<BR>ther, mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निनीय
सन्-निनीय, ind. having poured together, having<BR>mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपत्|संनिपत्
सन्निपत् सन्-नि-पत् (सम्-), cl. 1. P. -प-<BR>तति, -पतितुम्, to fly down, alight, descend, fall<BR>down; to perish, be destroyed; to fall together,<BR>come together, meet; to present one's self, arrive,<BR>appear: Caus. -पातयति, -यितुम्, to cause to fall<BR>down, throw down, shoot down or off, discharge;<BR>to cause to come together, convoke, bring together,<BR>collect, unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपतित|संनिपतित|सन्निपतितः
सन्-निपतित, अस्, आ, अम्, flown down, descended,<BR>alighted; fallen together, met together, come toge-<BR>ther; assembled, collected, mixed, blended; arrived,<BR>come near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपत्य|संनिपत्य
सन्-निपत्य, ind. having flown down, alighting,<BR>descending; having flocked together, having come<BR>together, having met; having come near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपात|संनिपात|संनिपातः|सन्निपातः
सन्-निपात, अस्, m. flying down, alighting, de-<BR>scending, falling down; a kind of musical time or<BR>measure (= ताल-भेद); falling together, meeting;<BR>contact, union, junction, collision, collection, assem-<BR>blage, multitude; mixture, miscellaneous collection;<BR>coming near, arrival; combined derangement of the<BR>three humors producing fever and dangerous illness.<BR>—सन्निपात-कलिका, f., N. of a treatise on the<BR>cure of fevers arising from a vitiated state of the<BR>three humors.<BR>—सन्निपात-ज्वर, अस्, m. a dan-<BR>gerous fever resulting from morbid condition of the<BR>three humors, (one of the eight kinds of fevers.)<BR>—सन्निपात-नुद्, त्, m. ‘removing the above<BR>fever,’ N. of a kind of tree (= नेपाल-निम्ब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपातक|संनिपातक|संनिपातकः
सन्निपातक, अस्, m. combined disorder of the<BR>three humors (wind, bile, and phlegm) or a dangerous<BR>fever resulting from such disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपातित|संनिपातित
सन्निपातित, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or shot down,<BR>shot off, discharged; brought together, assembled,<BR>called together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपात्य|संनिपात्य
सन्-निपात्य, ind. having caused to come together,<BR>having collected or brought together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबन्ध्
सन्निबन्ध् सन्-नि-बन्ध् (सम्-). See rt.<BR>बन्ध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबद्ध|संनिबद्ध|सन्निबद्धः
सन्-निबद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, firmly bound on, firmly<BR>tied, fettered, closely connected with or attached to,<BR>engrossed in; planted or covered with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबन्ध|संनिबन्ध|सन्निबंध|संनिबंधः|संनिबन्धः
सन्-निबन्ध, अस्, m. binding firmly, tying;<BR>attachment, connection, consequence; effectiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबन्धन|संनिबन्धन|सन्निबन्धनं
सन्-निबन्धन, अम्, n. the act of binding or<BR>tying firmly, binding fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबुध्|संनिबुध्
सन्निबुध् सन्-नि-बुध् (सम्-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-बोधति, -ते, &c., to perceive thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निभ|संनिभ|सन्निभः
सन्निभ सन्-निभ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. भा<BR>with नि and सम्), like, similar, resembling, (at the<BR>end of comps., e. g. मेघ-स्˚, resembling a cloud.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निभृ
सन्निभृ सन्-नि-भृ (सम्-). See rt. भृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निभृत|संनिभृत
सन्-निभृत, अस्, आ, अम्, kept secret, concealed,<BR>hidden; discreet, prudent, modest, unassuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमज्ज्|संनिमज्ज्
सन्निमज्ज् सन्-नि-मज्ज् (सम्-), cl. 6. P. -मज्-<BR>जति, &c., to sink quite under, sink down, be im-<BR>mersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमग्न|संनिमग्न
सन्-निमग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk under, submerged,<BR>immersed; sleeping, asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमज्जत्
सन्-निमज्जत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, sinking down<BR>into, sinking under.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमन्त्र्|संनिमन्त्र्
सन्निमन्त्र् सन्-नि-मन्त्र् (सम्-), cl. 10. P. A.<BR>-मन्त्रयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमित्त|संनिमित्त
सन्निमित्त सन्-निमित्त. See under सत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमील्|संनिमील्
सन्निमील् सन्-नि-मील्, cl. 1. P. -मीलति, &c.,<BR>to close completely, shut (the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियम्|संनियम्
सन्नियम् सन्-नि-यम् (सम्-), cl. 1. P. -यच्-<BR>छति (ep. also A. -ते), -यन्तुम्, to hold together,<BR>hold tight, keep back, restrain, keep in check, subdue,<BR>suppress; to annihilate, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियत|संनियत
सन्-नियत, अस्, आ, अम्, restrained, controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियन्तृ
सन्-नियन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a restrainer, suppress-<BR>ing, one who chastises, chastising, a chastiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियम्य
सन्-नियम्य, ind. having restrained or controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियुज्|संनियुज्
सन्नियुज् सन्-नि-युज् (सम्-), cl. 7. P. A.<BR>-युनक्ति, -युङ्क्ते, -योक्तुम्, to connect with, attach<BR>to, place in or on; to appoint, commission, employ,<BR>depute; to enjoin, order: Caus. -योजयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to place in or on, appoint to (with acc.), entrust<BR>with; to enjoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियुक्त|संनियुक्त
सन्-नियुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, attached to, connected<BR>with; appointed, employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियोग|संनियोग|संनियोगः
सन्-नियोग, अस्, m. connection or union with,<BR>attachment, application to (any pursuit &c.); appoint-<BR>ment, employment (in any office), commission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियोजित|संनियोजित
सन्-नियोजित, अस्, आ, अम्, appointed, entrusted<BR>with, commissioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरुध्|संनिरुध्
सन्निरुध् सन्-नि-रुध् (सम्-), cl. 7. P. A.<BR>-रुणद्धि, -रुन्द्धे, -रोद्धुम्, to keep back,<BR>hold firm, keep in, suppress, restrain, hinder, check,<BR>stop; to shut in, confine; to shut, close, lock up;<BR>to block up, crowd, fill: Pass. -रुध्यते, to be<BR>kept back or restrained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरुद्ध|संनिरुद्ध
सन्-निरुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, obstructed, hindered,<BR>checked, stopped, blocked up, choked, shut, closed,<BR>crowded, filled, covered over.<BR>—सन्निरुद्ध-<BR>गुद, अस्, आ, अम्, having an obstruction of the<BR>lower intestine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरुध्य
सन्-निरुध्य, ind. having suppressed or re-<BR>strained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरोध|संनिरोध|संनिरोधः
सन्-निरोध, अस्, m. obstruction, hindrance, check,<BR>suppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निर्गम्|संनिर्गम्
सन्निर्गम् सन्-निर्-गम् (सम्-), cl. 1. P. -गच्-<BR>छति, -गन्तुम्, to go out together, go away, depart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निर्मथ्|संनिर्मथ्
सन्निर्मथ् सन्-निर्-मथ् or सन्-निर्-मन्थ्<BR>(सम्-), cl. 1. 9. P. -मथति, -मन्थति, -मथ्-<BR>नाति, &c., to churn out, stir or shake about together,<BR>crush together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निर्मा
सन्निर्मा सन्-निर्-मा (सम्-), cl. 2. P. -माति,<BR>&c. (see rt. 3. मा), Ved. to construct, compose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निर्मित|संनिर्मित
सन्-निर्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. constructed, com-<BR>posed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निर्वप्|संनिर्वप्
सन्निर्वप् सन्-निर्-वप् (सम्-), cl. 1. P. A. -व-<BR>पति, -ते, &c., to scatter about, distribute, dispense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निली|संनिली
सन्निली सन्-नि-ली (सम्-), cl. 4. A. -लीयते,<BR>-लेतुम्, -लातुम्, to settle down, alight, settle; to<BR>cower down, hide or conceal one's self, disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवप्|संनिवप्
सन्निवप् सन्-नि-वप् (सम्-), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-वपति, -ते, &c., to throw together, heap together,<BR>heap up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवस्|संनिवस्
सन्निवस् 1. सन्-नि-वस् (सम्-, see rt. 5. वस्),<BR>cl. 2. A. -वस्ते, &c., to clothe with, put on (clothes<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवस्|संनिवस्
सन्निवस् 2. सन्-नि-वस् (सम्-, see rt. 6. वस्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">Page1063-a+ 76</a>]<BR>cl. 1. P. -वसति, &c., to dwell together, live with;<BR>to live in, inhabit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निविद्|संनिविद्
सन्निविद् सन्-नि-विद् (सम्-), Caus. -वेद-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to know, make known,<BR>announce, inform, tell; to offer, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निविश्|संनिविश्
सन्निविश् सन्-नि-विश् (सम्-), cl. 6. A. (also<BR>P.) -विशते (-ति), -वेष्टुम्, to enter into together;<BR>to enter into deeply; to sit down together; to have<BR>intercourse or intimate connection with; to enter;<BR>to sit down, encamp: Caus. -वेशयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to enter or sit down together; to unite, join,<BR>collect; to cause to enter, introduce, insert, install;<BR>to fix or fasten in; to cause to sit or lie or settle<BR>down, put or place down, cause to encamp, pitch a<BR>camp; to found (a town &c.); to put on, place on,<BR>impose, consign, commit; to fix the thoughts or<BR>mind on anything; to contemplate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निविष्ट|संनिविष्ट|सन्निविष्टः
सन्-निविष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, entered together, met<BR>together, assembled, collected; entered deeply into;<BR>absorbed or engrossed in; stationed in, abiding in,<BR>resting in; inserted in, sticking in, depending on;<BR>stationed near, contiguous, neighbouring, near, pre-<BR>sent, at hand; seated, encamped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवेश|संनिवेश|संनिवेशः|सन्निवेशः
सन्-निवेश, अस्, m. entering together, thorough<BR>or deep entrance into (any pursuit &c.), ardent<BR>attachment to; assembling, assemblage, collection,<BR>multitude; union, junction, contact; proximity, vici-<BR>nity, neighbourhood; station, seat, encampment,<BR>place, situation, position, posture; an open space<BR>near a town (where people assemble for recreation),<BR>a sort of play-ground in or near a town; causing to<BR>enter together, putting together, construction, fabrica-<BR>tion, preparation; form, figure; the collective form of<BR>an asterism; causing to enter, putting in, insertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवेशित|संनिवेशित
सन्-निवेशित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to enter in, intro-<BR>duced, inserted; made to settle, located, lodged,<BR>stationed, encamped; put down; consigned, com-<BR>mitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवेश्य|संनिवेश्य
सन्-निवेश्य, ind. having caused to enter or per-<BR>vade, having introduced, having made to encamp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृ|संनिवृ
सन्निवृ सन्-नि-वृ (सम्-), Caus. -वारयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to keep off, keep back, restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृत्|संनिवृत्
सन्निवृत् सन्-नि-वृत् (सम्-), cl. 1. A. -वर्-<BR>तते (in some tenses also P., see rt. 1. वृत्), -वर्ति-<BR>तुम्, to turn back, turn round, return together,<BR>return, retire; to desist from (with abl.), leave off,<BR>cease, stop; to pass away: Caus. -वर्तयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to return or turn back, send back; to divert,<BR>avert, keep off, hinder, preclude; to cause to cease,<BR>suppress, stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवर्तित|संनिवर्तित
सन्-निवर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to return, sent<BR>back, sent away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवर्त्य
सन्-निवर्त्य, ind. having caused to turn back,<BR>having diverted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृत्त|संनिवृत्त
सन्-निवृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, turned back, come back,<BR>returned, coming back; desisted, stopped, ceased;<BR>ceasing, forbearing; withdrawing. shrinking from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृत्ति|संनिवृत्ति|संनिवृत्तिः|सन्निवृत्तिः
सन्-निवृत्ति, इस्, f. turning back, returning, com-<BR>ing back; desisting from, forsaking, avoiding; for-<BR>bearance, restraint, complete abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निशम्|संनिशम्
सन्निशम् सन्-नि-शम् (सम्-), cl. 4. P. -शाम्-<BR>यति, -शमितुम्, to hear, perceive: Caus. -शामयति,<BR>&c., to cause to hear, summon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निशम्य
सन्-निशम्य, ind. having heard or perceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निषद्|संनिषद्
सन्निषद् सन्-नि-षद् (सम्-नि-सद्), cl. 1. 6.<BR>P. -षीदति, -षत्तुम्, to sink down; to sit down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निषण्ण|संनिषण्ण
सन्-निषण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, seated down, settled<BR>down, seated; halted, stationary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निसूद्
सन्निसूद् सन्-नि-सूद् (सम्-), Caus. -सूदयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to kill or destroy utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निसृज्
सन्निसृज् सन्-नि-सृज् (सम्-), cl. 6. P. -सृ-<BR>जति, -स्रष्टुम्, to deliver up, deliver over, entrust,<BR>commit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निसृष्ट|संनिसृष्ट
सन्-निसृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, delivered up or over,<BR>entrusted, committed, handed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नी|संनी
सन्नी सन्-नी (सम्-), cl. 1. P. A. -नयति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">Page1063-b+ 77</a>]<BR>ते, -नेतुम्, to lead together, bring together, collect;<BR>to connect, unite; to mix together, mingle, mix; to<BR>arrange; to lead or direct towards, lead, bring; to<BR>guide, direct, govern; to obtain, procure; to bring<BR>back, return, restore, give back, pay; to endow with<BR>(with inst., Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नय|संनय|संनयः|सन्नयः
सन्-नय, अस्, m. a collection, multitude, number,<BR>quantity; the rear of an army, rear-guard; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>Ved. bringing together, collecting, aggregating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नयत्
सन्-नयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bringing together;<BR>leading to, directing towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाय्य|संनाय्य
सन्-नाय्य, अम्, n. (for सान्नाय्य, q. v.), any<BR>substance to be mixed with clarified butter &c. and<BR>offered as a burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नीय
सन्-नीय, ind. having led or brought together;<BR>having mixed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नु|संनु
सन्नु सन्-नु (सम्-), cl. 2. P. -नौति, &c.<BR>(Ved. cl. 1. A. -नवते, &c.), to roar or sound toge-<BR>ther, bellow, bleat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नुद्|संनुद्
सन्नुद् सन्-नुद् (सम्-), cl. 6. P. A. -नुदति,<BR>-ते, -नोत्तुम्, to impel or bring together: Caus.<BR>-नोदयति, -यितुम्, to impel or bring together, col-<BR>lect, bring near; to procure, find; to push or urge<BR>on, impel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नृत्|संनृत्
सन्नृत् सन्-नृत् (सम्-), cl. 4. P. -नृत्यति,<BR>-नर्तितुम्, Ved. to dance together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यस्|संन्यस्
सन्न्यस् सन्-न्य्-अस् (सम्-नि-अस्), cl. 4. P.<BR>-अस्यति (sometimes also cl. 1. P. -असति), -असितुम्,<BR>to throw down together, place or put together, lay<BR>together; to put or lay upon; to put down, lay<BR>down, deposit; to give over to, consign, entrust,<BR>deliver over; to lay aside, give up, resign; to resign<BR>the world, become an ascetic or Sannyāsin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यसन|संन्यसन|संन्यसनं
सन्-न्यसन, अम्, n. the act of placing or laying<BR>down, depositing, delivering over, entrusting to;<BR>resigning, resignation, relinquishment, abandonment<BR>of the world, renunciation of temporal concerns,<BR>abdication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यस्त|संन्यस्त|सन्न्यस्तः
सन्-न्यस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown down, laid down,<BR>placed down; encamped; deposited, entrusted, de-<BR>livered over, consigned; laid aside; relinquished,<BR>discarded, abandoned, deserted.<BR>—सन्न्यस्त-देह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has given up his body.<BR>—सन्-<BR>न्यस्त-शस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has laid aside<BR>his weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यस्य
सन्-न्यस्य, ind. having put down or deposited,<BR>having consigned or delivered; having put off, having<BR>laid aside; having given up or resigned, having left<BR>or abandoned, having abandoned the world, having<BR>become an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यास|संन्यास|संन्यासः|सन्न्यासः
सन्-न्यास, अस्, m. deposit, trust; stake, wager;<BR>relinquishment, resignation, abandonment, profession<BR>of asceticism, abandonment of the world; giving up<BR>the body, sudden death; Indian spikenard.<BR>—सन्-<BR>न्यास-ग्रहण, अम्, n. assuming or practising<BR>asceticism.<BR>—सन्न्यास-ग्रहण-पद्धति, इस्, f.,<BR>N. of a short treatise on the duties of ascetics by<BR>Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—सन्न्यास-धर्म, अस्, m. the<BR>duty of giving up worldly concerns, asceticism.<BR>—सन्न्यास-धर्म-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>short treatise on the duties of ascetics.<BR>—सन्न्यासो-<BR>पनिषद् (˚स-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad<BR>belonging to the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यासिक
सन्-न्यासिक in वेद-स्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यासिन्|संन्यासिन्
सन्न्यासिन्, ई, m. one who lays down or deposits;<BR>one who abandons or resigns, an ascetic, devotee<BR>(especially one who retires from worldly concerns<BR>and is no longer bound to read the Mantras and<BR>perform sacrifices, but only to read the Āraṇyakas or<BR>Upaniṣads); a Brāhman of the fourth order or<BR>Āśrama, religious mendicant.<BR>—सन्न्यासि-ता, f. or<BR>सन्न्यासि-त्व, अम्, n. abandonment of worldly con-<BR>cerns, retirement from the world.<BR>—सन्न्यासि-दर्-<BR>शन, अम्, n., N. of the forty-ninth chapter of the<BR>Pātāla-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मातुर|सन्मातुरः
सन्मातुर सन्-मातुर, सन्-मान. See under<BR>सत्, p. 1053, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मार्ग
सन्मार्ग सन्-मार्ग, सन्-मित्र, &c. See<BR>under सत्, p. 1053, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्
सप् सप् (probably connected with rt.<BR>सच् and सपर्य), cl. 1. P. सपति, स-<BR>साप, सपितुम्, Ved. to worship, honour, serve,<BR>follow, (in Naigh. III. 5. सपति is placed among<BR>the परिचरण-कर्माणः, and in Naigh. III. 14.<BR>among the अर्चति-कर्माणः); to conform to; to<BR>join or unite together, connect (= समवाये); to<BR>obtain, (Sāy. = प्राप्); to touch, sip, (Sāy. सपन्त<BR>= स्पृशन्ति, Ṛg-veda V. 3, 4); to perform, do,<BR>(Sāy. = कृ): Caus. सपयति, -यितुम्, to follow,<BR>worship, (Ved. सीषपन्त = परिचरणं कुर्-<BR>वन्तु); [cf. Gr. σέβομαι, σέβας, σεμνός, ἔπομαι;<BR>Goth. siponeis, ‘a pupil.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्
सपत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, honouring, worshipping, fol-<BR>lowing; obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्य
सपर्य (probably fr. a lost noun सपस् = Gr. σέβας,<BR>cf. सबस्), Nom. P. सपर्यति, -यितुम्, Ved.<BR>to worship, adore, honour, serve, (in Naigh. III. 5.<BR>सपर्यति is enumerated among the परिचरण-<BR>कर्माणः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्यत्
सपर्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. worshipping, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्या|सपर्य्या
सपर्या, f. worship, adoration, reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्यु
सपर्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. serving, honouring,<BR>adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप
सप सप, अस्, m., Ved. (probably) the<BR>organ of generation; [cf. शेप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपक्ष|सपक्षः
सपक्ष स-पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having wings,<BR>winged; having a side or party; being on the same<BR>side, belonging to the same party; containing the<BR>major term or subject; (अस्), m. a partisan, follower,<BR>adherent; (in logic) an instance on the same side<BR>(e. g. the common illustration of ‘the culinary<BR>hearth’), a similar instance or one in which the<BR>major term is found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपताक
सपताक स-पताक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>banner, with a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्तन
सपत्तन स-पत्तन, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>towns or cities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्त्रलेख
सपत्त्रलेख स-पत्त्रलेख, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>fragrant pigments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्त्राकृ
सपत्त्राकृ स-पत्त्रा-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to wound with an arrow or other feathered<BR>weapon in such a way that the feathers enter the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्त्राकरण
सपत्त्रा-करण, अम्, n. wounding so that the<BR>feathered part of an arrow enters the body, causing<BR>excessive pain, worrying any one to death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्त्राकृत
सपत्त्रा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to some<BR>also सपत्त्र-कृत), severely wounded or pained,<BR>excessively afflicted; (अस्), m. a deer or other animal<BR>severely wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्त्राकृति
सपत्त्रा-कृति, इस्, f. great agony or affliction;<BR>excessive pain or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्न|सपत्नः
सपत्न स-पत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, (said by some<BR>to be fr. स-पत्नी below, but regarded by others as<BR>a separate word and connected with rt. सप् above, in<BR>the sense of ‘following,’ ‘persecuting’), hostile; (अस्),<BR>m. an enemy, adversary, rival.<BR>—सपत्न-ता, f.<BR>enmity, rivalry.<BR>—सपत्न-हन्, आ, -घ्नी, अ, Ved.<BR>killing enemies, destroying rivals.<BR>—सपत्नारि (˚न-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. a sort of bamboo, Bambusa Spinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नी
स-पत्नी, f. a woman who has the same husband<BR>with another woman (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 35) or whose<BR>husband has other wives, a fellow wife, rival wife,<BR>cotemporary wife, rival mistress.<BR>—सपत्नी-तस्,<BR>ind. from a rival wife.<BR>—सपत्नी-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of a woman whose husband has other wives.<BR>—सपत्नी-दुहितृ, ता, f. the daughter of a rival<BR>wife.<BR>—सपत्नी-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of a rival<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नीक
स-पत्नीक, अस्, m. accompanied with a wife,<BR>along with a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपदि
सपदि स-पदि, ind. at the same instant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">Page1064-a+ 68</a>]<BR>instantly, in a moment, at the moment, immediately;<BR>quickly, swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपद्म
सपद्म स-पद्म, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with<BR>lotuses, having lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपन्नग
सपन्नग स-पन्नग, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished<BR>with serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपराक्रम
सपराक्रम स-पराक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>valour, valiant, brave, bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरिकर
सपरिकर स-परिकर, अस्, आ, अम्, attended<BR>by a retinue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरिच्छद
सपरिच्छद स-परिच्छद, अस्, आ, अम्, attended<BR>by a train, provided with necessaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरिजन
सपरिजन स-परिजन, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>attendants, accompanied by followers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरितोष
सपरितोष स-परितोष, अस्, आ, अम्, feeling<BR>satisfaction, much pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरिवार
सपरिवार स-परिवार, अस्, आ, अम्, attended<BR>by a retinue, having a multitude of dependants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरिवाह
सपरिवाह स-परिवाह, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>an overflow, overflowing, brimful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरिशेष
सपरिशेष स-परिशेष, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a remainder, with the remainder, with the rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपरिषत्क
सपरिषत्क स-परिषत्क, अस्, m. a teacher<BR>surrounded by a college of his own disciples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्य
सपर्य सपर्य. See under rt. सप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्वतवनद्रुम
सपर्वतवनद्रुम स-पर्वत-वन-द्रुम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, with mountains, forests, and trees.<BR>—स-<BR>पर्वत-वनार्णव (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessing mountains, forests, and seas (said of the<BR>earth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपलाश
सपलाश स-पलाश, अस्, आ, अम्, together<BR>with a Palāśa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपल्लव
सपल्लव स-पल्लव, अस्, आ, अम्, together<BR>with shoots, having branches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपवित्रक
सपवित्रक स-पवित्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>taining sacrificial grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपाद|सपादः
सपाद स-पाद, अस्, आ, अम्, having feet;<BR>having a fourth part, with a quarter, increased by<BR>one fourth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपादपीठ|सपादपीठं
स-पादपीठ, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with a foot-<BR>stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपादुक
सपादुक स-पादुक, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing<BR>shoes, wearing sandals; with shoes or sandals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्ड|सपिंड|सपिंडः|सपिण्डः
सपिण्ड स-पिण्ड, अस्, m. ‘having the same<BR>Piṇḍa,’ a kinsman connected by the offering of the<BR>funeral cake to the Manes of certain relations (viz.<BR>father, grandfather, great-grandfather, &c., including<BR>the direct descendants of four persons, or, according to<BR>others, seven persons in an ascending and descending<BR>line: the following are therefore called Sapiṇḍas —<BR>son, son's son, and son's grandson; widow, daughter,<BR>and daughter's son; father, mother, brother, brother's<BR>son, brother's grandson; father's daughter's son;<BR>father's brother's son and grandson; paternal grand-<BR>father's daughter's son; paternal grandfather; paternal<BR>grandmother, paternal grandfather's brother, brother's<BR>son and grandson; great grandfather's daughter's<BR>son).<BR>—सपिण्ड-ता, f. the condition of being a Sa-<BR>piṇḍa.<BR>—सपिण्डी-करण, अम्, n. investing a person<BR>with the rights of a Sapiṇḍa or kinsman (as described<BR>above); performing the Śrāddha to deceased relatives<BR>called Sapiṇḍas (at the end of a full year after the<BR>death of a relative).<BR>—सपिण्डी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>invested with the relationship of Sapiṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्डन
सपिण्डन, अम्, n. = सपिण्डी-करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपित्व
सपित्व स-पित्व, according to Sāy. सपित्वम्<BR>= सह-प्राप्तव्यं स्थानम्, ‘a place to be ob-<BR>tained together,’ (Ṛg-veda 1. 109, 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिशाच
सपिशाच स-पिशाच, अस्, आ, अम्, together<BR>with or accompanied by the Piśācas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीड
सपीड स-पीड, अस्, आ, अम्, suffering pain or<BR>anguish, painful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीतक|सपीतकः
सपीतक स-पीतक, अस्, m. a kind of plant<BR>(= राज-कोषातकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीतिका
स-पीतिका, f. a kind of creeper (= हस्ति-घोषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीति|सपीतिः
सपीति स-पीति, इस्, f. compotation, drinking<BR>together, drinking in company; (इस्, इस्, इ), Ved. one<BR>who drinks together, a boon-companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुत्र
सपुत्र स-पुत्र or स-पुत्रक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a son, accompanied by a son.<BR>—स-पुत्र-<BR>दार, अस्, आ, अम्, with son and wife, accompanied<BR>by son and wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुत्रिन्
स-पुत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, together with sons, accom-<BR>panied by sons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुरोहित
सपुरोहित स-पुरोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by a family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुष्प
सपुष्प स-पुष्प, अस्, आ, अम्, having flowers,<BR>blooming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुष्पबलि
स-पुष्प-बलि, इस्, इस्, इ, filled with offerings of<BR>flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपौर
सपौर स-पौर, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied<BR>by citizens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तन्
सप्तन् सप्तन्, अ, m. f. n. pl. (in Uṇādi-s. 1.<BR>156. said to be fr. rt. सप्, ‘to connect, join’),<BR>seven, (a favourite number with the Hindūs, and<BR>regarded as a sacred number; hence mention is<BR>made of seven Mātṛs, seven streams, seven oceans,<BR>seven cities [Ṛg-veda 1. 63, 7], seven divisions of<BR>the world, seven Ṛṣis, seven Vipras [Ṛg-veda 1.<BR>62, 4], seven Ādityas, seven Dānavas, seven horses<BR>of the Sun, seven flames or tongues of fire, seven<BR>Yonīs of fire, seven Samidhs, seven tones, seven<BR>sacrificial rites, seven Maryādās, thrice seven Padāni<BR>or mystical steps by which heaven is obtained [Ṛg-<BR>veda 1. 72, 6], thrice seven cows, &c.); [cf. Zend<BR>हप्त; Gr. ἑπτά; Lat. septem; Goth. sibun;<BR>Angl. Sax. seofon; Lith. septyni, septynios; Slav.<BR>sedmij; Hib. seacht; Cambro-Brit. saith; Armor.<BR>seiz.]<BR>—सप्त-ऋषि, अयस्, m. pl. ‘the seven Ṛṣis,’<BR>epithet of the authors of the hymn Ṛg-veda IX. 107.<BR>—सप्त-कोण, अस्, आ, अम्, septangular, heptagonal.<BR>—सप्त-गङ्गम्, ind. the place of the seven streams<BR>of the Gaṅgā, (Pāṇ. II. 1, 20; cf. पञ्च-नद.)<BR>—सप्त-गु, उस्, m., N. of an Āṅgirasa (author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 47).<BR>—सप्त-गोदावरम्,<BR>ind. the place of the seven streams of the Godā-<BR>varī.<BR>—सप्त-ग्रही, f. the meeting of the seven<BR>planets under one sign.<BR>—सप्त-चक्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having seven wheels, (according to Śaṅkara = सर्-<BR>पण-चक्र.)<BR>—सप्तचत्वारिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>47th.<BR>—सप्त-चत्वारिंशत्, त्, f., 47.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>च्छद, अस्, m. ‘having seven leaves,’ a kind of tree<BR>[cf. सप्त-पर्ण]; (आ), f. a species of plant (=<BR>मद-गन्ध).<BR>—सप्त-जानि or सप्त-जामि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. (probably) having seven brothers or<BR>sisters.<BR>—सप्त-जिह्व, अस्, m. ‘seven-tongued,’ epi-<BR>thet of Agni or fire, (the seven tongues of fire have<BR>all names, e. g. काली, कराली, मनो-जवा, सु-लोहिता,<BR>सु-धूम्र-वर्णा, उग्रा or स्फुलिङ्गिनी, प्र-<BR>दीप्ता, and these names vary according to the parti-<BR>cular rite in which fire is used, see हिरण्या, सु-<BR>वर्णा, सु-प्रभा, &c.)<BR>—सप्त-ज्वाल, अस्, m.<BR>‘seven-flamed,’ epithet of Agni or fire.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>तन्तु, उस्, m. ‘having seven performers,’ a sacrifice,<BR>offering, oblation, (Sāy. = सप्त तनितारः, i. e.<BR>कर्मणां विस्तारयितारो यस्य.)<BR>—सप्तत्रिंश,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 37th.<BR>—सप्त-त्रिंशत्, त्, f., 37.<BR>—सप्तदश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 17th; having 17<BR>properties or attributes (said of a कुल or family);<BR>(अस्), m., scil. स्तोम, epithet of a particular Stoma;<BR>N. of a collection of hymns (said to have been<BR>created from Brahmā's western mouth).<BR>—सप्त-<BR>दशन्, अ, m. f. n. pl., 17.<BR>—सप्त-दीधिति, इस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-c" target="_blank">Page1064-c+ 81</a>]<BR>‘having seven rays of light,’ epithet of Agni.<BR>—सप्त-द्वारावकीर्ण (˚र-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>fined within seven gates (i. e. according to Kullūka,<BR>confined to the five organs of sense, the mind and<BR>the intellect, or restricted to this world and the three<BR>above and the three below it, Manu VI. 48).<BR>—सप्त-द्वीप, आस्, m. pl. the seven divisions of<BR>the terrestrial world, see द्वीप; (आ), f. ‘having or<BR>consisting of seven Dvīpas,’ epithet of the earth.<BR>—सप्तद्वीप-पति, इस्, m. the lord of the seven<BR>Dvīpas.<BR>—सप्त-द्वीप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing<BR>or consisting of seven Dvīpas.<BR>—सप्त-धातु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, consisting of seven elements, sevenfold, con-<BR>taining seven; (अवस्), m. pl. the seven constituent<BR>elements of the body (viz. chyle, blood, flesh, fat,<BR>bone, marrow, and semen).<BR>—सप्त-धातुक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, = सप्त-धातु.<BR>—सप्त-धारा-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a place.<BR>—सप्तनवत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 97th.<BR>—सप्त-नवति, इस्, f., 97.<BR>—सप्तनवति-तम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 97th.<BR>—सप्त-नाडी-चक्र, अम्, n.<BR>an astrological diagram supposed to foretell rain, (it<BR>consists of seven serpentine lines marked with the<BR>names of the Nakṣatras and planets.)<BR>—सप्त-ना-<BR>मन्, आ, आ, अ, having seven names.<BR>—सप्त-नामा,<BR>f. a kind of plant (= आदित्य-भक्ता).<BR>—सप्तपञ्-<BR>चाश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 57th.<BR>—सप्त-पञ्चाशत्, त्, f.,<BR>57.<BR>—सप्त-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘seven-leaved,’ a kind<BR>of plant (-मुद्गर).<BR>—सप्त-पद, अस्, आ, or ई,<BR>अम्, having seven steps, containing seven Padas; (ई),<BR>f. the seven steps at marriage.<BR>—सप्त-पदार्थी, f., N.<BR>of a treatise on Kaṇāda's seven Vaiśeṣika categories.<BR>—सप्तपदी-गमन, अम्, n. the walking together<BR>round the nuptial fire in seven steps, (see साप्त-<BR>पदीन.)<BR>—सप्त-पर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, seven-leaved;<BR>(अस्), m. the tree Alstonia or Echites Scholaris; (ई),<BR>f. the sensitive plant; (अम्), n. a sort of sweetmeat<BR>(made of grapes, pomegranates, dates, with sugar,<BR>spices, honey, and ghee).<BR>—सप्त-पाताल, अम्, n.<BR>the seven Pātālas or regions under the earth, (see<BR>पाताल, the names Ni-tala and Gabhasti-mat are<BR>sometimes substituted for Rasā-tala and Talātala.)<BR>—सप्त-पुत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having seven sons, hav-<BR>ing seven children.<BR>—सप्त-पुत्र-सू, ऊस्, f. the<BR>mother of seven sons or children.<BR>—सप्त-प्रकृति,<BR>अयस्, f. pl. the seven constituent parts of a kingdom<BR>(viz. the king, his ministers, ally, territory, fortress,<BR>army, and treasury, see प्रकृति).<BR>—सप्त-बुद्ध-<BR>स्तोत्र, अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>बुध्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having seven bottoms or<BR>foundations.<BR>—सप्त-भद्र, अस्, m. the Śirīṣa<BR>tree.<BR>—सप्त-भूमिक or सप्त-भौम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having seven stories, seven stories high.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>मृत्तिका, आस्, f. pl. seven earths collected from seven<BR>places and used in certain solemn rites.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>योजनी, f. a distance or extent of seven Yojanas.<BR>—सप्त-रक्त, अम्, n. the seven red-coloured<BR>parts of the body (viz. the palms of the hands, soles<BR>of the feet, nails, corners of the eyes, tongue, palate,<BR>and lips).<BR>—सप्त-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. seven-<BR>rayed, having seven rays; (इस्), m. epithet of Agni.<BR>—सप्त-रात्र, अम्, n. a period of seven nights.<BR>—सप्त-रात्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, lasting seven nights.<BR>—सप्त-राशिक, अम्, n. the rule of proportion<BR>with seven terms.<BR>—सप्तर्षि (˚त-ऋषि), अयस्,<BR>m. pl. ‘the seven Ṛṣis,’ the constellation Ursa<BR>Major, (the seven stars of which are supposed to be<BR>the seven great Ṛṣis, viz. Marīci, Atri, Aṅgiras,<BR>Pulastya, Pulaha, Kratu, and Vasiṣṭha.)<BR>—सप्तर्-<BR>षि-मत, अम्, n., N. of a work on law.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>वध्रि, इस्, m., N. of an Ātreya (author of the<BR>hymns Ṛg-veda V. 78, &c.).<BR>—सप्त-वरूथ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having seven protecting ledges (said of a<BR>carriage, see वरूथ).<BR>—सप्तविंश, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>the 27th; consisting of or containing 27.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>विंशक, अस्, ई, अम्, the 27th.<BR>—सप्त-विंशति, इस्, f.,<BR>27.<BR>—सप्त-विदारु, a particular kind of tree, (not<BR>ascertained.)<BR>—सप्त-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, sevenfold.<BR>—सप्त-शत, अम्, n., 700; 107; (ई), f. the aggre-<BR>gate of 700; a collection of 700 verses.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>शतिका, f. the aggregate of 700.<BR>—सप्त-शलाक,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of astrological diagram marked with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">Page1065-a+ 81</a>]<BR>twice seven lines crossing each other at right angles,<BR>(it is used for indicating auspicious days for mar-<BR>riages.)<BR>—सप्त-शिव, आस्, f. pl., Ved. ‘being seven<BR>auspicious ones,’ epithet of the seven Mātṛs; (आ), f.<BR>a kind of plant (= नाग-वल्ली).<BR>—सप्त-षष्ट,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 67th.<BR>—सप्त-षष्टि, इस्, f., 67.<BR>—सप्तषष्टि-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 67th.<BR>—सप्-<BR>त-सङ्ख्याक, अस्, आ, अम्, seven in number, amount-<BR>ing to seven.<BR>—सप्त-सप्तक, अम्, n. ‘seven times<BR>seven,’ forty-nine.<BR>—सप्तसप्तक-वेत्तृ, ता, m.<BR>one who knows seven times seven sciences.<BR>—सप्त-<BR>सप्तत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 77th.<BR>—सप्त-सप्तति, इस्,<BR>f., 77.<BR>—सप्तसप्तति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 77th.<BR>—सप्त-सप्ति, इस्, m. ‘having seven horses,’ epi-<BR>thet of the Sun.<BR>—सप्त-सागर or सप्त-सागरक,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of very valuable gift (compared to<BR>seven oceans).<BR>—सप्तसागर-प्रादानिका, f., N.<BR>of a chapter of the Matsya-Purāṇa.<BR>—सप्त-सू, ऊस्,<BR>f. the mother of seven children (= सुत-वस्करा).<BR>—सप्त-स्वसृ, सा, सा, सृ, Ved. having seven<BR>sisters.<BR>—सप्त-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having seven<BR>hands; measuring seven cubits.<BR>—सप्त-होतृ, ता,<BR>&c., (probably) having seven Hotṛs; [cf. चतुर्-<BR>होतृ, दश-होतृ.]<BR>—सप्त-हौत्र, N. of a treatise<BR>on ritual.<BR>—सप्तांशु (˚त-अं˚), उस्, उस्, उ, having<BR>seven rays.<BR>—सप्तांशु-पुङ्गव, अस्, m. ‘eminent<BR>with seven rays of light,’ the planet Saturn.<BR>—सप्-<BR>ताक्षर (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, containing seven<BR>syllables; (अस्), m. a word or a Pāda which contains<BR>seven syllables.<BR>—सप्ताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, consisting of seven members or parts or con-<BR>stituent elements, (epithet of a kingdom, see सप्त-<BR>प्रकृति.)<BR>—सप्तात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, m. ‘having<BR>seven forms or essences,’ epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—सप्-<BR>तार्चिस् (˚त-अर्˚), इस्, इस्, इस्, seven-flamed, having<BR>seven flames or tongues; of inauspicious aspect, evil-<BR>eyed; (इस्), m. epithet of Agni or fire; of the planet<BR>Saturn; a particular plant (= चित्रक).<BR>—सप्ताशीत<BR>(˚त-अश्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, the 87th.<BR>—सप्ताशीति (˚त-<BR>अश्˚), इस्, f., 87.<BR>—सप्ताशीति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>87th.<BR>—सप्ताश्र (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, septangular;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a heptagon, (also spelt सप्तास्र,<BR>see 1. अश्र.)<BR>—सप्ताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>seven horses,’ epithet of the Sun, (the seven horses<BR>are supposed to symbolize the seven days of the week.)<BR>—सप्ताश्व-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘borne by seven horses,’<BR>epithet of the Sun.<BR>—सप्तास्य (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. seven-mouthed, having seven mouths.<BR>—सप्ताह (˚त-अह), अम्, n. seven days, a week.<BR>—सप्तोत्तर (˚त-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a sur-<BR>plus or excess of seven (e. g. सप्तोत्तरं शतम्,<BR>a hundred + seven or 107.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्त
सप्त, अस्, ई, अम्, (according to Śabda-k.) = सप्-<BR>तम, the seventh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तक|सप्तकः
सप्तक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, containing seven, seven;<BR>the seventh; (अम्), n. a collection of seven (as of seven<BR>stanzas or verses); (ई), f. a woman's girdle, zone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तत
सप्तत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 70th (only used when<BR>other numerals precede, see एक-स्˚, द्वा-स्˚, त्रि-स्˚,<BR>&c., cf. Pāṇ. V. 2, 58.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तति|सप्ततिः
सप्तति, इस्, f., 70; N. of a work, = साङ्ख्य-<BR>कारिका; (ई), f. du. two seventies; (-अयस्), f. pl.<BR>many seventies.<BR>—सप्तति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>70th; [cf. एक-स्˚.]<BR>—सप्तति-सम्बन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>a collection of 70 tales.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तथ
सप्तथ, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. the seventh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तधा
सप्तधा, ind. in seven ways, sevenfold; in seven<BR>parts or pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तम|सप्तमः
सप्तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the seventh; (ई), f. the<BR>seventh case, i. e. the locative; the seventh Tithi or<BR>lunar day of the fortnight, (in the light fortnight<BR>there is a festival in honour of the seventh digit of<BR>the moon on this day; it often occurs at the end<BR>of comps., e. g. गङ्गा-सप्तमी, the seventh day in<BR>the light half of the month Vaiśākha; जयन्ती-<BR>सप्तमी, the seventh day in the light half of the<BR>month Māgha); [cf. Zend haptatha; Gr. ἕβδομος;<BR>Lat. septimus; Lith. sekma-s for sepma-s; Slav.<BR>sedmyĭ; Old Germ. sibunto(n); Hib. seachtmad.]<BR>—सप्तम-कला, f. the seventh digit of the moon.<BR>—सप्तमी-प्रतिरूपक, अस्, इका, अम्, resembling<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">Page1065-b+ 69</a>]<BR>in form a locative case.<BR>—सप्तमी-व्रत, अम्, n. a<BR>religious observance to be performed on the seventh<BR>day of a month.<BR>—सप्तमी-समास, अस्, m. a Tat-<BR>puruṣa compound of which the first member is sup-<BR>posed to be a locative case.<BR>—सप्तमी-स्नपन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘bathing on the seventh day,’ a particular<BR>religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तला
सप्तला, f., N. of several plants, double jasmine<BR>(= नव-मालिका); other plants (= चर्म-कशा;<BR>= गुञ्जा; = पाटला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तिन्
सप्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having or containing seven (syl-<BR>lables &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ति|सप्तिः
सप्ति सप्ति, इस्, m. (probably fr. rt. सप्, ‘to<BR>join’), a yoke (of horses); a horse; a yoke-fellow;<BR>N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 79 (hav-<BR>ing the patronymic Vājambhara).<BR>—सप्ती-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत् (Ved. for सप्ति-वत्), possessed of horses,<BR>having splendid horses, (Sāy. = प्रशस्ताश्व.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्त्य
सप्त्य सप्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 41, 4 = सर्पणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रणय
सप्रणय स-प्रणय, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>affection, affectionate, friendly; (अम्), ind. affection-<BR>ately, kindly; confidently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रणव
सप्रणव स-प्रणव, अस्, आ, अम्, together<BR>with the Praṇava or sacred syllable ॐ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रणामम्
सप्रणामम् स-प्रणामम्, ind. with a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रतिबन्ध
सप्रतिबन्ध स-प्रतिबन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, at-<BR>tended with obstacles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रत्यय
सप्रत्यय स-प्रत्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>confidence, reposing confidence in (with loc.); cer-<BR>tain, secure, sure, (सप्रत्यया वृत्तिः, sure means<BR>of subsistence); having an affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रत्याशम्
सप्रत्याशम् स-प्रत्याशम्, ind. hopefully,<BR>expectantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रथ
सप्रथ स-प्रथ, अस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 181, 2 (with patronymic Bhāradvāja).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रथस्
सप्रथस् स-प्रथस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having<BR>breadth, broadly diffused, extensive, far-famed,<BR>glorious, mighty; (आस्), m. epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—स-<BR>प्रथस्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, very extensive, very large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रभ
सप्रभ स-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>splendor, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रमाण
सप्रमाण स-प्रमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>proof or evidence, authentic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रयोगनिवर्तन
सप्रयोगनिवर्तन स-प्रयोग-निवर्तन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, along with the (secret for) using and restrain-<BR>ing; (see the next.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रयोगरहस्य
स-प्रयोग-रहस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>secret spells for (their) use (said of magical weapons<BR>which are not wielded manually but invoked or<BR>meditated upon, and are useless to one unacquainted<BR>with the mode of invoking them).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रश्रयम्
सप्रश्रयम् स-प्रश्रयम्, ind. with affection<BR>or courtesy, affectionately, respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रसाद
सप्रसाद स-प्रसाद, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied<BR>with favour or kindness, propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रस्वेद
सप्रस्वेद स-प्रस्वेद, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>perspiration, perspiring, sweating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्राण
सप्राण स-प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, having breath<BR>or life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रेम
सप्रेम स-प्रेम, अस्, आ, अम्, having love,<BR>full of love or affection, loving, affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रेष्य
सप्रेष्य स-प्रेष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by<BR>servants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्सरस्
सप्सरस् स-प्सरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having<BR>the same form or beauty, (Sāy. = समान-रूप or<BR>हिंसक, Ṛg-veda 1. 168, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफर|सफरः
सफर सफर, अस्, m. (also written श-<BR>फर, q. v.), a small glistening fish (Cyprinus<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">Page1065-c+ 70</a>]<BR>Sophore, said to be a sort of carp and commonly<BR>called Puṃṭī); (ई), f. the above fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफल|सफलं
सफल स-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing fruit,<BR>fruitful, productive, profitable, yielding profit; ful-<BR>filled, rewarded, blessed.<BR>—सफल-प्रार्थन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has attained his desire.<BR>—सफलो-<BR>दय (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘auspicious-rising,’ epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबधूक
सबधूक स-बधूक. See स-वधूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबन्धु|सबंधु|सबन्धुः
सबन्धु स-बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, possessed of<BR>a friend, befriended; being of the same family;<BR>closely connected or united; (उस्), m. a kinsman,<BR>relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबर्दुघ
सबर्दुघ सबर्-दुघ, सबर्-धु. See under<BR>सबस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबल|सबलः
सबल स-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, powerful, strong;<BR>accompanied by a force or army.<BR>—स-बलानुग<BR>(˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, with an army and followers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबलि|सबलिः
सबलि स-बलि, इस्, इस्, इ, endowed with<BR>royal revenue; accompanied by the Bali offering;<BR>(इस्), m. evening twilight (this being the proper<BR>hour for offering food to spirits, &c.; see बलि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबस्
सबस् सबस् (changeable into सबर् before<BR>soft consonants; cf. सपस् under rt. सप्), Ved.<BR>water, heavenly food, nectar, (Sāy. = उदक, पयस्,<BR>अमृत; cf. Gr. σέβας, ‘worship’ or ‘the object of<BR>worship.’)<BR>—सबर्-दुघ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. yielding<BR>or granting heavenly food or water, dispensing water.<BR>—सबर्-दुह्, -धुक्, क्, क्, Ved. yielding nectar.<BR>—सबर्-धु, Ved. = सबर्-दुह् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबहुमानम्
सबहुमानम् स-बहुमानम्, ind. with great<BR>honour or reverence, very respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाध्
सबाध् स-बाध्, त्, m., Ved. an oppressor,<BR>destroyer, one who is oppressed; a sacrificer who is<BR>disturbed by enemies, (Sāy. = शत्रुभिर् बाधितो<BR>यजमानः, Ṛg-veda I. 64, 8; = बाधा-सहित,<BR>Ṛg-veda IV. 17, 18); a priest, (in Naigh. III. 18.<BR>सबाधः is enumerated among the ऋत्विङ्-ना-<BR>मानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाध|सबाधः
स-बाध, अस्, आ, अम्, painful, hurtful; extor-<BR>tionate, oppressive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाधस्
स-बाधस्, Ved. according to Sāy. स-बाधसस्<BR>= दारिद्र-निमित्त-बाध-सहितस्य, having the<BR>suffering caused by poverty, Ṛg-veda V. 10, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबान्धव
सबान्धव स-बान्धव, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>kindred, connected, related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबालवृद्ध
सबालवृद्ध स-बाल-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, with<BR>children and old men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबीभत्सम्
सबीभत्सम् स-बीभत्सम्, ind. with abhor-<BR>rence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मक
सब्रह्मक स-ब्रह्मक, अस्, आ, अम्, together<BR>with Brahmā, together with (the world of) Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचर्य|सब्रह्मचर्यं|सब्रह्मचर्य्य
सब्रह्मचर्य स-ब्रह्मचर्य, अम्, n. fellow-<BR>studentship, studying together or being disciples of<BR>the same teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचारिन्
स-ब्रह्मचारिन्, ई, m. a fellow-student, one<BR>engaged in the same studies and observing the same<BR>austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभक्तिकम्
सभक्तिकम् स-भक्तिकम्, ind. respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभद्रमुस्त
सभद्रमुस्त स-भद्रमुस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, full<BR>of Cyperus Rotundus, (also read सु-भ्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभय
सभय स-भय, अस्, आ, अम्, fearful, appre-<BR>hensive; (अम्), ind. with fear, timidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभरस्
सभरस् स-भरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. bearing<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभर्तृका|सभर्त्तृका
सभर्तृका स-भर्तृका, f. ‘having a hus-<BR>band,’ a woman whose husband is alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभा
सभा सभा, f. (said to be fr. rt. 1. भा<BR>with स, because people, सह भान्ति, ‘appear<BR>together’ at a place of meeting), an assembly, con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">Page1066-a+ 77</a>]<BR>gregation, meeting, company, society, good society;<BR>Society (personified as a daughter of Prajā-pati); a<BR>council, council-chamber, hall; a court of justice;<BR>a court, palace [cf. राज-स्˚]; a public audience,<BR>levee; a gaming room, gambling house; any<BR>house or large room or frequented place.<BR>—सभा-<BR>चातुर्य, अम्, n. politeness in society.<BR>—सभाचार<BR>(˚भा-आच्˚), अस्, m. the customs or usages of society,<BR>court-manners.<BR>—सभा-धैर्य, अम्, n. boldness in<BR>company.<BR>—सभा-नर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—स-<BR>भा-नायक, अस्, or सभा-पति, इस्, m. the president<BR>of an assembly, chairman; the keeper of a gaming<BR>house.<BR>—सभा-पर्वन्, अ, n., N. of the second book<BR>of the Mahā-bhārata (which describes the holding of<BR>a great assembly at Hastināpura and the gambling<BR>between Yudhi-ṣṭhira and Śakuni, in which the<BR>former staked and lost all his possessions, including<BR>his territory and his wife Draupadī).<BR>—सभा-पूजा,<BR>f. respect or reverence paid to the audience (in the<BR>prelude of a drama).<BR>—सभा-मण्डन, अम्, n. the<BR>adorning or arranging of an assembly-room.<BR>—सभा-<BR>वशकर, अस्, ई, अम्, controlling or influencing an<BR>assembly.<BR>—सभा-सद्, त्, m. one who sits at an<BR>assembly, a member of any society or company,<BR>an assistant at an assembly or meeting; (in law) an<BR>assessor, one who sits in a court of justice, a judge.<BR>—सभा-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who restrains<BR>or rules an assembly.<BR>—सभा-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a king.<BR>—सभास्तार (˚भा-आस्˚), अस्, m. an assistant<BR>at an assembly, one of a society or company.<BR>—सभा-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being at an assembly or court; (अस्),<BR>m. one who sits in an assembly; a courtier.<BR>—स-<BR>भोचित (˚भा-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, fit for an assembly,<BR>fit for good society; (अस्), m. a learned Brāhman,<BR>any learned or educated person.<BR>—सभोद्देश (˚भा-<BR>उद्˚), the neighbourhood of any place of meeting;<BR>the precincts of a house, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभिक|सभिकः
सभिक, अस्, m. the keeper of a gaming house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभीक|सभीकः
सभीक, अस्, m. = सभिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभेय
सभेय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to an assembly,<BR>skilled in council, shining in society.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्य|सभ्यः
सभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to an<BR>assembly, fit for an assembly; suitable to good<BR>society; fit for a court; polite; refined, civilized,<BR>(अ-सभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not met with in good society,<BR>not used in the best society, unrefined, indecorous);<BR>trusted, confidential, faithful; (अस्), m. an assistant<BR>at an assembly; an assessor; a person of honourable<BR>parentage; N. of one of the five sacred fires; the<BR>keeper of a gaming house; the servant of a keeper<BR>of a gaming house; [cf. Old Germ. sibba, sibbi,<BR>sibbo, ga-sibbo, ga-sibbot; Goth. trasti-sibja,<BR>ga-sibjon, un-sibja; Angl. Sax. sib, sibbe, ge-sib.]<BR>—सभ्य-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most worthy of an<BR>assembly, very senatorial or oratorical, very polite or<BR>refined; (अस्), m. a very polite or refined person, an<BR>ornament of society.<BR>—सभ्य-ता, f. or सभ्य-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. politeness, refinement, good breeding.<BR>—स-<BR>भ्येतर (˚य-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘contrary to good<BR>society,’ vulgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाज्
सभाज् सभाज्, cl. 10. P. सभाजयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अससभाजत्, to serve,<BR>honour, worship; to salute; to please, gratify, satisfy,<BR>exhilarate; to beautify; to show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजन|सभाजनं
सभाजन, अम्, n. service, honour, courtesy,<BR>politeness, civility in receiving or taking leave of a<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजित
सभाजित, अस्, आ, अम्, served, honoured, treated<BR>with courtesy, gratified, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभार्य
सभार्य स-भार्य or स-भार्यक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, with a wife, having a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभावन|सभावनः
सभावन स-भावन, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभासद्
सभासद् सभा-सद्. See under सभा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभीति
सभीति स-भीति, इस्, इस्, इ, having fear, fear-<BR>ful, timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभीम
सभीम स-भीम, अस्, आ, अम्, together with<BR>Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभृकुटीमुख
सभृकुटीमुख स-भृकुटी-मुख, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a frowning face, frowning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभृत्य
सभृत्य स-भृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by<BR>servants, with (the assistance of) servants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्रातृ
सभ्रातृ स-भ्रातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, with a brother,<BR>attended by brethren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्रातृक
स-भ्रातृक, अस्, आ, अम्, = स-भ्रातृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्रूभङ्ग
सभ्रूभङ्ग स-भ्रूभङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, with a<BR>frown, frowning, knitting the brows; (अम्), ind.<BR>frowningly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
सम् 1. सम् (= rt. स्तम्), cl. 1. P. स-<BR>मति, ससाम, समितुम्, to be confused<BR>or agitated or disturbed; (according to some) to be<BR>undisturbed, not to be agitated [cf. rt. 1. शम्]; cl.<BR>10. P. समयति, -यितुम्, to be agitated or dis-<BR>turbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
सम् 2. सम् [cf. 5. स, सम; by some con-<BR>nected with 4. स], ind. (as a preposition or prefix<BR>to verbs and verbal derivatives opposed to 1. वि,<BR>q. v., and like Gr. σύν, Lat. con, expressing) with,<BR>together with, along with, together (e. g. सं-युज्,<BR>to join together; सञ्-चि, to gather together; सन्-<BR>धा, to place together; सन्-धि, placing together);<BR>when prefixed to some roots and verbal derivatives<BR>सम् intensifies the idea contained in the simple rt.,<BR>and may often be translated by ‘much,’ ‘greatly,’<BR>‘thoroughly,’ ‘quite,’ ‘very,’ ‘well,’ (see सन्-तप्,<BR>सन्-तुष्, &c.); it may also express ‘completeness,’<BR>‘perfection,’ ‘beauty,’ &c., (see सम्-उच्छेद, सन्-<BR>तमस्, &c.); it is not unfrequently prefixed to<BR>nouns in the sense of सम, ‘same,’ ‘like,’ ‘similar,’<BR>(see सम, cf. सम्-अर्थ); in the Veda it may be<BR>used as a separable preposition with inst. (e. g. असृ-<BR>जद् मधुना सम् मधूनि, Ṛg-veda X. 54, 6);<BR>[cf. according to some, Gr. σύν, ξύν; perhaps Lat.<BR>cum; Old Russ. sen; Slav. sū, su.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम|समः
सम 1. सम, अस्, आ, अम् (probably connected<BR>with 5. स and 2. सम्; declined like the prono-<BR>minal सर्व except in meanings like ‘even,’ ‘equal,’<BR>&c., e. g. समस्मै, to all, to every one, Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 51, 6), even, level, flat, plain; same, equal,<BR>(समं कृ, to make equal, balance; to pay);<BR>like, similar, like to (with inst., e. g. मया सम,<BR>like to me); a match for, acting in the same way or<BR>with equal justice towards every one; indifferent,<BR>impartial, fair; free from emotion, unaffected by<BR>passion, unmoved; straight; upright, honest, just,<BR>temperate, good, virtuous; fit, convenient, suitable;<BR>not eminent, ordinary, common, low, mean, equally<BR>distant from extremes; all, every one (= सर्व<BR>and so declined, see above); full, complete; whole,<BR>entire; (अस्), m., N. of certain zodiacal signs (espe-<BR>cially Vṛṣa, Karkaṭa, Kanyā, Vṛścika, Makara,<BR>Mīna); a mode of measuring time in music (de-<BR>scribed as a simultaneous movement of the hands<BR>or feet of a singer with the time of the music);<BR>a kind of straight line placed over a numerical figure<BR>to mark the process of extracting the square root;<BR>(आ), f. a year; see p. 1067, col. 1; (अम्), n. anything<BR>even or level, a level plain; (in rhetoric) a particular<BR>figure, sameness of objects compared to one another;<BR>(in geometry) a mean proportional segment (de-<BR>scribed as a fourth proportional to the two perpen-<BR>diculars and the link or segment, and used for solving<BR>certain problems in a trapezium); (अम्), ind. equally;<BR>similarly; like; ceteris paribus; on a level with, in<BR>the same way; conformably to; entirely; with,<BR>along with, together with (used as a preposition<BR>governing the inst.); sometimes used for the pre-<BR>position सम्, cf. सम-चोदित, सम-रञ्जित, and<BR>सम-गच्छतु under सङ्-गम्); [cf. Zend hama:<BR>Gr. ἅμα, ὁμό-ς, ὁμοῦ, ὁμό-θεν, ὁμό-σε, ὁμο-ῖο-ς,<BR>ὁμοί-ι-ος, ὁμαλό-ς, μία, μέν: Lat. sim-ia (?), si-<BR>mili-s, simul, simul-tas, simul-ā-re, semel, sem-<BR>per, singuli: Old Lat. simītu: Goth. sama, sama-<BR>frathjis, sam-ana, samath, sums, sum: Old<BR>Germ. sama, saman, zi-samane (= Mod. Germ.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-c" target="_blank">Page1066-c+ 81</a>]<BR>zusammen), samet: Angl. Sax. same (sam in<BR>comp.), somne, samne, sum: Slav. samu: Hib.<BR>samhuil, ‘like;’ samhladh, ‘resemblance;’ sam-<BR>hlain, ‘I compare, resemble.’]<BR>—सम-कन्या, f. a<BR>suitable maiden, a girl fit to be married.<BR>—सम-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, अम्, m. n. an equi-diagonal tetragon.<BR>—सम-काल, अस्, m. the same time, the same<BR>moment; (अम्), ind. simultaneously.<BR>—सम-कोल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having an even breast,’ a serpent, snake.<BR>—सम-कोष्ठ-मिति, इस्, f. the measure of like<BR>compartments, area or superficial contents of any<BR>figure.<BR>—सम-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. (in astronomy)<BR>‘having an even or complete figure,’ epithet of a<BR>particular division or arrangement of the Nakṣatras.<BR>—सम-खात, अस्, m. (in geometry) an equal<BR>excavation or cavity, a cavity having the figure of a<BR>regular solid with equal sides, a parallelopipedon,<BR>cylinder.<BR>—सम-गन्धक, अस्, m. any com-<BR>pounded perfume, incense, olibanum.<BR>—सम-गन्-<BR>धिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having equal or similar fragrance;<BR>(अम्), n. the fragrant root of the Uśīra.<BR>—सम-<BR>चतुरश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, equally quadrangular, square;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. an equilateral tetragon.<BR>—सम-<BR>चतुर्भुज, अस्, आ, अम्, equally four-sided; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. an equilateral tetragon or rhombus.<BR>—सम-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, even-minded, even-tem-<BR>pered, equanimous, equable; indifferent; having the<BR>thoughts directed to the same subject.<BR>—समचित्त-<BR>ता, f. or समचित्त-त्व, अम्, n. even-mindedness,<BR>equanimity, indifference.<BR>—सम-चोदित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>= सञ्-चोदित, driven, impelled, shot off.<BR>—सम-<BR>च्छेदन, अस्, आ, अम्, having like divisions or deno-<BR>minators.<BR>—सम-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, equal in kind,<BR>homogeneous.<BR>—सम-ज्ञा, f. fame, reputation; [cf.<BR>सम्-अज्या.]<BR>—सम-ता, f. or सम-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>evenness, sameness, equality, similarity; identity;<BR>equanimity; fairness, impartiality, justness, upright-<BR>ness, perfectness, commonness.<BR>—सम-त्रय, अम्, n.<BR>an equal triad, equal quantity of three ingredients, (ac-<BR>cording to Śabda-k. हरीतकी-नागर-गुडम्.)<BR>—स-<BR>म-त्रिभुज, अस्, आ, अम्, having three sides equal;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a tetragon containing three sides equal;<BR>an equilateral triangle.<BR>—सम-त्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, equally<BR>bright or lovely.<BR>—सम-दन्त, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>having even teeth.<BR>—सम-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>तुल्य-दर्शन, regarding with equal or indifferent<BR>eyes.<BR>—सम-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, viewing or regarding<BR>equally, looking at both sides impartially, impartial.<BR>—सम-दुःख, अस्, आ, अम्, sympathising with,<BR>feeling for another's woe.<BR>—सम-दुःख-सुख,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the same grief and joy, sympathis-<BR>ing in sorrow and joy.<BR>—सम-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, looking<BR>on all alike, regarding all alike, impartial; equable.<BR>—सम-दृष्टि, इस्, f. the act of looking at equally<BR>or impartially; (इस्, इस्, इ), looking on all equally,<BR>regarding all alike.<BR>—सम-द्युति, इस्, इस्, इ, equal<BR>in radiance.<BR>—सम-द्वादशाश्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. an<BR>equilateral dodecagon or dodecahedron.<BR>—सम-<BR>द्वि-द्विभुज, अस्, अम्, m. n. a rhomboid consisting<BR>of two pairs of equal sides.<BR>—सम-द्विभुज, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a rhomboid having tow sides equal.<BR>—सम-धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, equal or equivalent to.<BR>—सम-पद, अस्, m. ‘holding the feet even,’ a<BR>particular posture in sexual intercourse; (अम्), n. an<BR>attitude in shooting.<BR>—सम-पाद, अम्, n. standing<BR>with feet even, a particular posture with archers.<BR>—सम-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having equal splendor.<BR>—सम-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, looking on all things<BR>alike, calm, indifferent, philosophical, stoical; (इस्),<BR>m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—सम-भाग, अस्, m. an equal<BR>share.<BR>—सम-भाव, अस्, ई, अम्, of like nature or<BR>property; (अस्), m. sameness, equability.<BR>—सम-<BR>भूमि, इस्, f. even or level ground.<BR>—सम-मण्-<BR>डल, अम्, n. ‘even-circle,’ the prime vertical line<BR>(in astronomy).<BR>—सम-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, of like<BR>origin, proceeding from the same cause.<BR>—सम-<BR>मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, of the same size or measure.<BR>—सम-मिति, इस्, f. mean measure.<BR>—सम-रंहस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, having equal impetuosity or speed.<BR>—स-<BR>म-रज्जु, उस्, f. mean rope or line, mean soundings.<BR>—सम-रञ्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, = सं-रञ्जित, tinged,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-a" target="_blank">Page1067-a+ 81</a>]<BR>coloured, dyed.<BR>—सम-रभ, अस्, m. ‘equal-<BR>clasping,’ a kind of coitus.<BR>—सम-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of the same form.<BR>—सम-रूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, for-<BR>merly in the possession of an honest man, (see<BR>रूप्य.)<BR>—सम-रेख, अस्, आ, अम्, straight-lined,<BR>straight.<BR>—सम-लम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, having equal<BR>perpendiculars; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a trapezoid.<BR>—स-<BR>म-लोष्ट-काञ्चन, अस्, आ, अम्, one to whom a<BR>clod and piece of gold are all the same.<BR>—सम-व-<BR>यस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, of equal age.<BR>—सम-वर्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of the same colour or caste, &c.; (अस्),<BR>m. community of caste, &c.<BR>—सम-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, being equal, being of a fair or impartial dispo-<BR>sition; (ई), m. Yama, the ruler of Tartarus.<BR>—सम-<BR>विभाग, अस्, m. a division of property amongst sons<BR>in equal shares.<BR>—सम-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, equal in<BR>strength.<BR>—सम-वृत्त, अम्, n. = सम-मण्डल<BR>above.<BR>—सम-वृत्ति, इस्, f. even state or temper,<BR>equanimity; (इस्, इस्, इ), of an equal or even temper,<BR>equable, fair, moderate.<BR>—सम-वेध, अस्, m.<BR>mean depth.<BR>—सम-शोधन, अम्, n. equal sub-<BR>traction; subtraction of the same quantity on both<BR>sides of an equation.<BR>—सम-सङ्ख्यात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, equal in number.<BR>—सम-सन्धि, इस्, m. equal<BR>alliance, peace on equal terms.<BR>—सम-सन्धित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, allied on equal terms, bound or con-<BR>nected equally.<BR>—सम-सुप्ति, इस्, f. universal sleep<BR>(i. e. the end of a Kalpa and destruction of the<BR>universe).<BR>—सम-सूत्र-ग or सम-सूत्र-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, (in astronomy) situated on the same<BR>diameter.<BR>—सम-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being level or<BR>even, equal, level, uniform; like, similar.<BR>—सम-<BR>स्थल, अम्, ई, n. f. even or level ground; (ई), f. the<BR>Doab or country between the Ganges and Jumnā<BR>rivers (= अन्तर्-वेदि).<BR>—समस्थली-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, made into level ground, levelled, filled up (as a<BR>marsh or river).<BR>—सम-स्पर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the same contact, equal in touch, having the same<BR>effect of contact, equally defiling.<BR>—सम-स्वर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the same or a similar sound.<BR>—स-<BR>मांश (˚म-अं˚), अस्, m. an equal portion or share;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), entitled to an equal portion or share.<BR>—समांश-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking an equal por-<BR>tion, sharing equally, a co-heir.<BR>—समांशिक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, or समांशिन् (˚म-अं˚), ई, इनी, इ, entitled<BR>to an equal share, a co-heir.<BR>—समाकार (˚म-आक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of like form, like in appearance, similar,<BR>like.<BR>—समाक्षर-पद-क्रम (˚म-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, containing a succession of Padas or metrical<BR>feet of the same number of syllables.<BR>—१. समाचार<BR>(˚म-आच्˚), अस्, m. (for 2. सम्-आचार see p. 1072,<BR>col. 2), equal or similar conduct; upright or virtuous<BR>conduct, proper practice; (अस्, आ, अम्), equal or<BR>similar in practice or in virtuous conduct.<BR>—समार्-<BR>थिन् (˚म-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, seeking or desiring<BR>equality; seeking peace.<BR>—समी-करण, अम्, n.<BR>the act of making even or equal, equalising, levelling;<BR>assimilation, digestion; (in arithmetic) the reducing<BR>of fractions to a common denominator, equation.<BR>—समी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, &c., to<BR>make even or equal, equalise.<BR>—समी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, equalised; levelled, equipoised, balanced; done<BR>in the same manner, imitated; summed up, added.<BR>—समी-क्रिया, f. the act of equalising; (in arith-<BR>metic) equation.<BR>—समी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति,<BR>&c., to be or become equal, be equalised.<BR>—समी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, equalised, equipoised; identified.<BR>—समोदक (˚म-उद्˚), अम्, n. a mixture of half<BR>buttermilk and half water.<BR>—समोपमा (˚म-उप्˚),<BR>f. (in rhetoric) comparison expressed by the adjective<BR>सम in composition with the substantive to which<BR>the object of the comparison is likened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समया
समया, ind. See under सम्-इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समा
1. समा, f. (sometimes आस्, pl.; for 2. समा see<BR>s. v.), a year; a day (according to some).<BR>—समां-<BR>समीना, f. a cow bearing a calf every year.<BR>—समा-<BR>निचय, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has a store (of pro-<BR>visions) sufficient for a year.<BR>—समान्त (˚मा-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the end of a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीय|समीयः
1. समीय, Nom. A. समीयते, &c., to be treated<BR>equally or in the same manner as (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीय|समीयः
2. समीय, अस्, आ, अम्, similar, like, of like<BR>origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीयमान
1. समीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being treated in the<BR>same manner as. (For 2. see under 1. सम्-इ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम|समः
सम 2. स-म, अस्, आ, अम् (i. e. स + मा),<BR>‘together with Lakṣmī,’ happy, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्त
समक्त समक्त. See under सम्-अञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्न|समक्नः
समक्न समक्न. See under सम्-अञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्ष|समक्षं
समक्ष सम्-अक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, being before<BR>the eyes or in sight, visible, being in presence of;<BR>(अम्), ind. before the eyes, in sight of, visibly, in<BR>presence of.<BR>—समक्ष-ता, f. visibility.<BR>—सम्-<BR>अक्ष-दर्शन, अम्, n. the act of seeing with the<BR>eyes, ocular evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समग्र|समग्रः
समग्र सम्-अग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, all, entire, whole,<BR>full, complete.<BR>—समग्र-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessing the whole of one's property.<BR>—समग्र-<BR>सम्पद्, त्, त्, त्, having complete happiness, blessed<BR>with every happiness.<BR>—समग्रेन्दु (˚र-इन्˚), उस्,<BR>m. the full moon.<BR>—समग्रेन्दु-निभानन (˚भ-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a face like the full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समङ्ग
समङ्ग सम्-अङ्ग, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समङ्गल
समङ्गल स-मङ्गल, अस्, आ, अम्, endowed<BR>with happiness, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समङ्गा|समंगा
समङ्गा सम्-अङ्गा, f. Bengal madder (=<BR>मञ्जिष्ठा); a sort of fern, Lycopodium Imbri-<BR>catum; the sensitive plant (= लज्जालु); other plants<BR>(= वराह-क्रान्ता; = बाला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समच्
समच् सम्-अच् or सम्-अञ्च् (see rts. अच्, 1. अञ्च्,<BR>cf. सम्-अञ्ज् below), cl. 1. P. A. -अचति, -अञ्चति,<BR>-ते, -अञ्चितुम्, to bend together; to go together:<BR>Pass. -अच्यते, to be combined or united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्न|समक्नः
सम्-अक्न, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. सम्-अञ्च्), bent toge-<BR>ther; going or moving together or simultaneously,<BR>going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समच्य
सम्-अच्य, ind. having bent together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्
समज् सम्-अज्, cl. 1. P. -अजति, -अजितुम्, to<BR>bring or collect together, (Sāy. = सं-योजयति); to<BR>bring into conflict; to meet (for battle; Sāy. = सङ्-<BR>गच्छते, Ṛg-veda 1. 100, 11); to subdue, over-<BR>come; to animate, incite, (Sāy. = सम्-प्रेरयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज|समजं|समजः
समज, अस्, m. a multitude of beasts or animals;<BR>a number of fools; (अम्), n. a forest, wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्या
सम्-अज्या, f. a meeting, assembly; fame, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज|समाजः
सम्-आज, अस्, m. a meeting [cf. द्यूत-स्˚, प्रेक्-<BR>षा-स्˚], assembly, congregation, congress; a society,<BR>company, association, club; a convivial meeting,<BR>party; a collection, quantity, multitude, number<BR>(applied to any collection of articles except of beasts);<BR>an elephant.<BR>—समाज-सन्निवेश, अस्, m. a building<BR>or place suitable for an assembly, assembly-room,<BR>meeting-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजिक|समाजिकः
समाजिक, अस्, m. a member of an assembly or<BR>congregation; a spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समञ्ज्
समञ्ज् सम्-अञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. A. -अनक्ति, -अङ्क्ते,<BR>अञ्जितुम् or -अङ्क्तुम्, to smear over, anoint, be-<BR>sprinkle; to beautify, decorate, adorn (Ved.); to<BR>honour (Ved.); to join together (Sāy. = एकी-कृ),<BR>connect, unite; to put together, compose; to utter<BR>forth, (Sāy. = सम्यग् व्यक्तं कृ); to consume,<BR>devour (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्त
सम्-अक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, joined together; put toge-<BR>ther, composed, combined, (also referrible to सम्-अच्<BR>above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समञ्जस|समंजस|समञ्जसं|समञ्जसः
सम्-अञ्जस, अस्, आ, अम्, proper, right, fit; correct,<BR>accurate, true, consistent; virtuous, just, good; sound,<BR>healthy; exercised, practised, experienced; (अम्), n.<BR>propriety, fitness, truth, accuracy, consistency, correct<BR>evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समण्ठ|समण्ठः
समण्ठ समण्ठ, अस्, m. a kind of pot-herb<BR>(described as a sort of cucumber, = गण्डीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्
समत् सम्-अत्, cl. 1. P. -अतति, -अतितुम्, to<BR>resort to, approach, visit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रम्
समतिक्रम् सम्-अति-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रा-<BR>मति, -क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to go or pass by en-<BR>tirely, go completely beyond, go or pass completely<BR>through, cross over, step over, step out of; to trans-<BR>gress, neglect, disregard, lose; to surpass, excel, exceed;<BR>to pass by, elapse (as time); to let pass by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रम|समतिक्रमः
सम्-अतिक्रम, अस्, m. going entirely over or<BR>beyond; deviating from, transgressing, omission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रम्य
सम्-अतिक्रम्य, ind. having entirely gone by,<BR>having wholly passed over, (द्वौ मासौ समति-<BR>क्रम्य, having allowed two months to elapse, after<BR>two months); having neglected or omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रान्त
सम्-अतिक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, gone entirely over or<BR>beyond; transgressed; surpassed, exceeded; passed<BR>by, elapsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिया
समतिया सम्-अति-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -यातुम्,<BR>to go completely beyond, pass by or away, elapse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिरिक्त|समतिरिक्तं
समतिरिक्त सम्-अतिरिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt.<BR>रिच् with अति and सम्), excessively redundant or<BR>abundant, exceeding, excessive, much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिवह्
समतिवह् सम्-अति-वह्, Caus. -वाहयति,<BR>&c., to cause to be spent, to pass, spend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिवृत्
समतिवृत् सम्-अति-वृत्, cl. 1. A. -वर्तते, &c.<BR>(see rt. 1. वृत्), to pass by; to escape from, avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समती
समती सम्-अती (-अति-इ), cl. 2. P. -अत्येति,<BR>&c., to go or pass by entirely, pass completely be-<BR>yond; to go through, cross over; to go by, avoid;<BR>to surpass, excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतीत
सम्-अतीत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone or passed by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतीत्य
सम्-अतीत्य, ind. having completely gone or passed<BR>by, having passed through; having avoided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्सर
समत्सर स-मत्सर, अस्, आ, अम्, having envy<BR>or jealousy, envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समद्
समद् 1. सम्-अद्, cl. 2. P. -अत्ति, -अत्तुम्, to<BR>eat completely up, entirely devour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समद्
समद् 2. समद्, त्, f. (in the Pada स-मद्;<BR>according to Yāska either fr. 1. सम्-अद् above or<BR>सम्-मद्), Ved. a battle, contest, fight, (in Naigh.<BR>II. 17. समत्सु is enumerated among the सङ्-<BR>ग्राम-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समद
समद स-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, intoxicated; ex-<BR>hilarated, delighted; furious, mad with rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिक|समधिकः
समधिक सम्-अधिक, अस्, आ, अम्, exceedingly<BR>abundant, very abundant, exceeding, excessive, plen-<BR>tiful; (अम्), ind. exceedingly, excessively.<BR>—सम्-<BR>अधिक-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more abundant, exceed-<BR>ing, excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिकृत्
समधिकृत् सम्-अधि-कृत्, cl. 6. P. -कृन्तति,<BR>-कर्तितुम्, to cut up in addition, cut up completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिकृत्य
सम्-अधिकृत्य, ind. having completely cut up,<BR>having cut in pieces, having cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगम्
समधिगम् सम्-अधि-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to go towards together, go well up to,<BR>come quite near, approach; to come into possession<BR>of, acquire, obtain; to go completely over, surpass;<BR>to go over, study, read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगत
सम्-अधिगत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone quite near to,<BR>approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगमन|समधिगमनं
सम्-अधिगमन, अम्, n. the act of going quite<BR>near to; surpassing, overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगम्य
सम्-अधिगम्य, ind. having completely attained<BR>to; having obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिरुह्
समधिरुह् सम्-अधि-रुह्, cl. 1. P. -रोहति,<BR>&c., to rise up, mount, ascend; to rise up to, be<BR>convinced of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिश्रि
समधिश्रि सम्-अधि-श्रि, cl. 1. P. A. -श्र-<BR>यति, -ते, -श्रयितुम्, to proceed or advance towards,<BR>approach, go up to; to attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिश्रित्य
सम्-अधिश्रित्य, ind. having proceeded or ad-<BR>vanced towards; having approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिष्ठा
समधिष्ठा सम्-अधि-ष्ठा (-स्था), cl. 1. P.<BR>A. -तिष्ठति, -ते, -ष्ठातुम्, to stand over, preside<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">Page1068-a+ 72</a>]<BR>over, superintend, administer, protect; to mount<BR>upon, ascend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिष्ठाय
सम्-अधिष्ठाय, ind. having presided over;<BR>having mounted upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधी
समधी सम्-अधी (-अधि-इ), cl. 2. A. -अधीते,<BR>to go over, read through, study thoroughly, peruse,<BR>investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधीत
सम्-अधीत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone over, read through,<BR>studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समध्यास्
समध्यास् सम्-अध्य्-आस् (-अधि-आस्), cl. 2. A.<BR>-आस्ते, -आसितुम्, to sit on together, occupy (a seat)<BR>along with; to dwell in, inhabit: Desid. -आसिसिषते,<BR>to wish to occupy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समध्व
समध्व सम्-अध्व, अस्, आ, अम्, being on the<BR>same road, travelling in company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्
समन् सम्-अन्, cl. 2. P. -अनिति, -अनितुम्,<BR>Ved. to breathe again, come to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान|समानं|समानः
1. सम्-आन (for 2. समान see s. v.), one of the<BR>five vital airs (that which circulates about the navel<BR>and is considered essential to digestion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन
समन समन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. सम् or<BR>connected with 2. सम्), Ved. a battle, fighting, (in<BR>Naigh. II. 17. enumerated among the सङ्ग्राम-<BR>नामानि, cf. सम्-अर), rivalry; coming or going<BR>together, meeting, union, collection; a marriage,<BR>marriage ceremony; a sacrifice, (Sāy. = यज्ञ); (अस्),<BR>m. zeal; a diligent man (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समना
समना, ind. Ved. in battle, (Sāy. = समने);<BR>(according to others समना is an old inst. = सम्-<BR>आनया fr. 2. समान, see Nirukta X. 5. and Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda VIII. 41, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्य
समन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. warlike, martial,<BR>military.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनन्तरम्
समनन्तरम् सम्-अनन्तरम्, ind. immedi-<BR>ately after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनस्
समनस् स-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, of the same<BR>mind, unanimous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनीक
समनीक सम्-अनीक, अम्, n., Ved. war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुकम्प्
समनुकम्प् सम्-अनु-कम्प्, cl. 1. A. -कम्-<BR>पते, -कम्पितुम्, to sympathise with, have pity on,<BR>pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुकम्प्य
सम्-अनुकम्प्य, ind. having sympathised with,<BR>having pitied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुकॢप्
समनुकॢप् सम्-अनु-कॢप्, Caus. -कल्पयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to make any one (acc.) attain any state or<BR>condition (loc.), convert into, cause to become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुक्रम्
समनुक्रम् सम्-अनु-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रा-<BR>मति, -क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to go or pass through<BR>completely, to go through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुक्रम्य
सम्-अनुक्रम्य, ind. having passed or gone<BR>through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुगम्
समनुगम् सम्-अनु-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to go after, follow, pursue; to penetrate,<BR>pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुगत
सम्-अनुगत, अस्, आ, अम्, followed, pursued;<BR>penetrated, pervaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुगा
समनुगा सम्-अनु-गा, cl. 3. P. -जिगाति, -गातुम्,<BR>to go after together; to go well after, follow quite<BR>closely, follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुग्रह्
समनुग्रह् सम्-अनु-ग्रह्, cl. 9. P. A. -गृह्-<BR>णाति, -गृह्णीते, -ग्रहीतुम्, to collect or gather<BR>together, arrange or put in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुगृह्य
सम्-अनुगृह्य, ind. having arranged in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुचिन्त्
समनुचिन्त् सम्-अनु-चिन्त्, cl. 10. P. -चिन्त-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to reflect deeply about, meditate on,<BR>think upon, remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुजन्
समनुजन् सम्-अनु-जन्, cl. 4. A. -जायते,<BR>-जनितुम्, to be born similar to or resembling (with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञा
समनुज्ञा सम्-अनु-ज्ञा, cl. 9. P. A. -जानाति,<BR>जानीते, -ज्ञातुम्, to permit or allow or consent to<BR>fully, wholly acquiesce in; to approve, admit, grant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">Page1068-b+ 70</a>]<BR>authorize, empower; to pardon, forgive, excuse; to<BR>grant leave of absence, allow to go away, dismiss;<BR>to favour: Caus. -ज्ञापयति, -यितुम्, to ask leave,<BR>beg permission; to ask for, request; to take leave<BR>of (with acc.), bid adieu; to greet, salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञात
सम्-अनुज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely assented or<BR>agreed to, permitted, allowed; authorized; allowed<BR>to go away, dismissed; favoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञान|समनुज्ञानं
सम्-अनुज्ञान, अम्, n. entire assent, concurrence,<BR>permission; (अस्, आ, अम्), entirely acquiesced in,<BR>permitted, allowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञाप्य
सम्-अनुज्ञाप्य, ind. having granted full permis-<BR>sion, having fully allowed, having asked leave, having<BR>requested permission; having taken leave of; having<BR>saluted respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञाय
सम्-अनुज्ञाय, ind. having entirely approved or<BR>consented to; having acquiesced in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुतप्
समनुतप् सम्-अनु-तप्, Pass. -तप्यते, to<BR>suffer great subsequent pain, be very penitent, repent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुदिश्
समनुदिश् सम्-अनु-दिश्, cl. 6. P. -दिशति,<BR>-देष्टुम्, to assign, apportion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुदृश्
समनुदृश् सम्-अनु-दृश्, cl. 1. P. -पश्यति,<BR>-द्रष्टुम्, to look well after; to look on, regard<BR>as, consider, observe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुद्रु
समनुद्रु सम्-अनु-द्रु, cl. 1. P. -द्रवति (ep.<BR>also A. -ते), -द्रोतुम्, to run after together; to run<BR>well after, follow, pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुधाव्
समनुधाव् सम्-अनु-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धा-<BR>वति, -ते, -धावितुम्, to run after together; to run<BR>well after, pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुध्यै
समनुध्यै सम्-अनु-ध्यै, cl. 1. P. -ध्या-<BR>यति, -ध्यातुम्, to reflect upon, think of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुपद्
समनुपद् सम्-अनु-पद्, cl. 4. A. -पद्यते,<BR>-पत्तुम्, to enter into, enter upon, attain to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुप्रछ्
समनुप्रछ् सम्-अनु-प्रछ्, cl. 6. P. -पृच्-<BR>छति, -प्रष्टुम्, to ask about, ask after, inquire<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुप्राप्
समनुप्राप् सम्-अनु-प्राप् (-प्र-आप्), cl. 5. P.<BR>-प्राप्नोति, -प्राप्तुम्, to attain, reach, arrive at; to<BR>obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुप्राप्त
सम्-अनुप्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, arrived at, reached,<BR>attained; obtained, assumed; entirely covered or<BR>overspread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुप्राप्य
सम्-अनुप्राप्य, ind. having reached or arrived at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुभू
समनुभू सम्-अनु-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति,<BR>&c., to enjoy together, feel, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुमन्
समनुमन् सम्-अनु-मन्, cl. 4. A. -मन्यते,<BR>&c., to assent, allow, consent; to recognise as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुमत
सम्-अनुमत, अस्, आ, अम्, assented to, agreed<BR>upon; (अम्), n. consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुया
समनुया सम्-अनु-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -यातुम्,<BR>to go after, follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुयात
सम्-अनुयात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone after, followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुयुज्
समनुयुज् सम्-अनु-युज्, cl. 7. P. A. -युनक्ति,<BR>-युङ्क्ते, -योक्तुम्, to inquire after, ask about; to<BR>appoint, order, enjoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुयुज्य
सम्-अनुयुज्य, ind. inquiring about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुवर्ण्
समनुवर्ण् सम्-अनु-वर्ण्, cl. 10. P. -वर्ण-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to depict, describe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुवर्णित
सम्-अनुवर्णित, अस्, आ, अम्, described, delineated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुवस्
समनुवस् सम्-अनु-वस् (see rt. 6. वस्), cl. 1.<BR>P. -वसति, -वस्तुम्, to abide by, follow, conform to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुविद्
समनुविद् सम्-अनु-विद्, Caus. -वेदयति,<BR>-ते, &c., to cause to know or remember, remind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुवृत्
समनुवृत् सम्-अनु-वृत्, cl. 1. A. -वर्तते,<BR>&c., to follow after, pursue; to obey; to ensue:<BR>Caus. -वर्तयति, -यितुम्, to cause to take place or<BR>happen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुव्रज्
समनुव्रज् सम्-अनु-व्रज्, cl. 1. P. -व्रजति,<BR>-व्रजितुम्, to go after, follow, pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुव्रत
समनुव्रत सम्-अनुव्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely<BR>devoted to, ardently attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुशास्
समनुशास् सम्-अनु-शास्, cl. 2. P. -शास्ति,<BR>-शासितुम्, to rule or regulate well, govern, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त|समंत|समन्तः
समन्त सम्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, being on every<BR>side or part, universal, complete, whole, entire, all;<BR>(अस्), m. limit, boundary, term, end; (अम्), ind. to<BR>the very end, on all sides, wholly, altogether; (आत्),<BR>ind. from every side, on every side, from every part,<BR>all round, completely.<BR>—समन्त-तस्, ind. all round,<BR>on every side, altogether, wholly.<BR>—समन्त-दुग्-<BR>धा, f. the milk hedge-plant (= स्नुही).<BR>—समन्त-<BR>पञ्चक, अम्, n. the district Kuru-kṣetra, q. v. (said<BR>to have been once bordered by five lakes filled by<BR>Paraśu-rāma with the blood of the slaughtered Kṣatri-<BR>yas).<BR>—समन्त-भद्र, अस्, m. ‘wholly auspicious,’<BR>a Buddha or Jina.<BR>—समन्त-भुज्, क्, m. ‘all-<BR>devouring,’ epithet of Agni or fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त्रक
समन्त्रक स-मन्त्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>charms or spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त्रिक
समन्त्रिक स-मन्त्रिक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मन्-<BR>त्रिन् with 5. स, q. v.), together with or accompanied<BR>by counsellors (said of a king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त्रित्व
समन्त्रि-त्व, अम्, n. counsel on the same side,<BR>assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्धकार
समन्धकार सम्-अन्धकार, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>great or universal darkness; [cf. सन्-तमस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्धकारीकृत
समन्धकारी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made dark on<BR>all sides, (Kirāt. XIV. 39.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्मथ
समन्मथ स-मन्मथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>love, filled with love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्य
समन्य समन्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्यु|समन्युः
समन्यु स-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, having the<BR>same splendor (Ved.); feeling the same energy or<BR>anger, (Sāy. = समान-वयस्क or समान-क्रोध,<BR>Ṛg-veda II. 34, 3); feeling anger or resentment,<BR>angry, fierce, enraged; filled with sorrow, sorrowful;<BR>(उस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वागम्
समन्वागम् सम्-अन्व्-आ-गम् (-अनु-आ-), cl. 1.<BR>P. -गच्छति, -गन्तुम्, to go together after, follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वागत
सम्-अन्वागत, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by, accom-<BR>panied by, furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वारभ्
समन्वारभ् सम्-अन्व्-आ-रभ्, cl. 1. A. -र-<BR>भते, &c., to take hold of or clasp together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वारब्ध
सम्-अन्वारब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, taken hold of<BR>together, grasping together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वारुह्
समन्वारुह् सम्-अन्व्-आ-रुह् (-अनु-आ-), cl. 1.<BR>P. -रोहति, -रोढुम्, to ascend after (as a wife<BR>ascends the funeral pile after her husband).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वि
समन्वि सम्-अन्व्-इ (-अनु-इ), cl. 2. P. -एति,<BR>-एतुम्, to go together after, follow; to infer or ensue<BR>as a consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वय|समन्वयः
सम्-अन्वय, अस्, m. regular succession or order,<BR>connected sequence or consequence, conjunction,<BR>mutual connection; [cf. अन्व्-अय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वित|समन्वितः
सम्-अन्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, connected or associated<BR>with; completely possessed of, fully endowed with,<BR>possessing, full of, affected by; [cf. अन्व्-इत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्विष्
समन्विष् सम्-अन्व्-इष् (-अनु-इष्), cl. 6. P.<BR>-इच्छति, &c., to search through, seek about every-<BR>where.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्विष्य
सम्-अन्विष्य, ind. having searched through, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वीक्ष्
समन्वीक्ष् सम्-अन्व्-ईक्ष् (-अनु-ईक्ष्), cl. 1.<BR>A. -ईक्षते, -ईक्षितुम्, to look towards, look or<BR>gaze after; to keep looking at, keep in view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वीक्ष्य
सम्-अन्वीक्ष्य, ind. having looked towards or<BR>kept in view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपध्यै
समपध्यै सम्-अप-ध्यै, cl. 1. P. -ध्यायति,<BR>-ध्यातुम्, to think ill or badly of, meditate evil or<BR>injury against, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपवृज्
समपवृज् सम्-अप-वृज्, Caus. -वर्जयति,<BR>&c., to deliver over, present with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपवर्जित
सम्-अपवर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, given up; delivered<BR>over, given, presented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपवृत्
समपवृत् सम्-अप-वृत्, Caus. -वर्तयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to roll away, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपिधा
समपिधा सम्-अपि-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, to cover completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपिधाय
सम्-अपिधाय, ind. having completely covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपिरुह्
समपिरुह् सम्-अपि-रुह्, cl. 1. P. -रोहति,<BR>&c., to grow together, grow over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपोह्
