समवलोकयत्
सम्-अवलोकयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, looking at, in-<BR>specting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समववृत्
समववृत् सम्-अव-वृत्, Caus. -वर्तयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to turn towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवशिष्
समवशिष् सम्-अव-शिष्, Pass. of Caus.<BR>-शेष्यते, to be left, to remain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवशेषित
सम्-अवशेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, left, spared, remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवश्यान
समवश्यान सम्-अवश्यान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>श्यै with अव and सम्), gone away, wasted, de-<BR>stroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवसद्
समवसद् सम्-अव-सद्, cl. 1. 6. P. -सीदति,<BR>-सत्तुम्, to sink down, pine or waste away, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवसन्न
सम्-अवसन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk down, de-<BR>pressed, dispirited, sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवसृज्
समवसृज् सम्-अव-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति,<BR>-स्रष्टुम्, to let go, cast or hurl down upon; to<BR>abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवसर्ग्य
सम्-अवसर्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be let go, to be<BR>abandoned, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्कन्द्
समवस्कन्द् सम्-अव-स्कन्द्, Caus. -स्कन्द-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to assail, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्तम्भ्
समवस्तम्भ् सम्-अव-स्तम्भ्, cl. 5. 9. P.<BR>-स्तभ्नोति, -स्तभ्नाति, -स्तम्भितुम्, to support,<BR>confirm, encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्था
समवस्था 1. सम्-अव-स्था, cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-तिष्ठति, -ते, -स्थातुम्, to stand firmly, stand still,<BR>stand ready: Caus. -स्थापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>stand firm or still, stop; to establish, found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्था
2. सम्-अवस्था, f. firm or fixed state or condition;<BR>similar condition or state; state or condition (in<BR>general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्थापित
सम्-अवस्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to stand<BR>firmly, set up; fully established, founded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्थित
सम्-अवस्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or remaining<BR>firm, remaining fixed; staunch, steady; standing<BR>ready or prepared, ready; being in any place or<BR>position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवहित
समवहित सम्-अवहित, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt.<BR>धा with अव and सम्), closely connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाकार
समवाकार सम्-अवाकार, अस्, m. probably<BR>incorrect for सम्-अवकार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाप्
समवाप् सम्-अवाप् (-अव-आप्), cl. 5. P. A.<BR>-आप्नोति, -आप्नुते, &c., to meet with, attain, reach,<BR>gain, obtain, incur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाप्त
सम्-अवाप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, obtained, attained.<BR>—समवाप्त-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>obtained his desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाप्ति|समवाप्तिः
सम्-अवाप्ति, इस्, f. attainment, obtaining, getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाप्य
सम्-अवाप्य, ind. having attained, having gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवार्ज्
समवार्ज् सम्-अवार्ज् (-अव-अर्ज्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-अवार्जति, &c., Ved. to leave together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवे
समवे सम्-अवे (-अव-इ), cl. 2. P. -अवैति,<BR>-अवैतुम्, to come together, meet together, blend<BR>or mix together, assemble together, be connected or<BR>united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाय|समवायः
सम्-अवाय, अस्, m. coming or meeting together,<BR>conjunction, close combination or union, mixing<BR>together, cohesion, connection; a collection, aggre-<BR>gate, meeting, concourse, congress, assemblage, mul-<BR>titude, quantity; complete or intimate union, con-<BR>stant and inseparable connection or cohesion, inse-<BR>parable existence or inherence of one thing in another,<BR>intimate or material relation (e. g. the relation which<BR>exists between a whole and its parts; between cloth<BR>and the yarn composing it; between a genus or<BR>species and its individuals; between an action or<BR>quality and its subject; between particularity and the<BR>eternal substances of ether, time, space, soul, &c.;<BR>this is one of the seven categories or Padārthas of<BR>the Vaiśeṣika system or school of Nyāya philosophy<BR>founded by Kaṇāda).<BR>—समवाय-तस्, ind. in con-<BR>sequence of constant and intimate connection or rela-<BR>tion.<BR>—समवाय-सम्बन्ध, अस्, m. intimate and<BR>constant connection, inseparable relation (as described<BR>above), connection by inseparable inherence or co-<BR>hesion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायिन्
समवायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, closely and intimately con-<BR>nected or united, aggregated; multitudinous; (इ), n.<BR>intimate and inseparable cause (as clay of pottery,<BR>thread of cloth, &c.).<BR>—समवायि-कारण, अम्, n.<BR>inseparable cause or connection, cause of constant<BR>inherence or cohesion, material cause, substantial<BR>cause, (in the Vedānta phil. उपादान-कारण is<BR>more commonly used.)<BR>—समवायि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>intimate connection or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेत|समवेतः
सम्-अवेत, अस्, आ, अम्, come together, met toge-<BR>ther, met, closely united, mixed, mingled, blended,<BR>collected, assembled, intimately connected with or<BR>related to, intimately united or inherent; con-<BR>tained or comprised or included in a larger number,<BR>contained or comprised in anything.<BR>—समवेत-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of being intimately related or<BR>connected.<BR>—समवेतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>containing a meaning, significant, instructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेत्य
सम्-अवेत्य, ind. having come together, having<BR>assembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेक्ष्
समवेक्ष् सम्-अवेक्ष् (-अव-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-अवेक्षते, &c., to look at, behold, observe, view,<BR>look about, look round; to perceive; to consider,<BR>regard, notice; to concern one's self about; to reflect<BR>or ponder on; to acknowledge: Caus. -अवेक्ष-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to look at or consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेक्षित
सम्-अवेक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, observed, considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेक्ष्य
सम्-अवेक्ष्य, ind. having viewed, having con-<BR>sidered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समश्
समश् 1. सम्-अश् (see rt. 1. अश्), cl. 5. P. A.<BR>-अश्नोति, -अश्नुते, &c., to pervade or penetrate<BR>thoroughly, extend through; to obtain, gain, attain;<BR>to meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समश्नुवान|समश्नुवानः
सम्-अश्नुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, completely pervading,<BR>extending throughout, spreading over; obtaining,<BR>experiencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्टि|समष्टिः
सम्-अष्टि, इस्, f. (in the Vedānta phil.) collective<BR>pervasion, a collective aggregate or one which is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">Page1071-b+ 78</a>]<BR>viewed as consisting of one thing or as constituted<BR>of parts of which each is consubstantially the same<BR>with the whole, totality; [cf. व्य्-अष्टि.]<BR>—सम्-<BR>अष्ट्य्-अभिप्राय, अस्, m. the regarding a group of<BR>objects collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समश्
समश् 2. सम्-अश्, cl. 9. P. -अश्नाति, -अशितुम्,<BR>to eat together, consume; to taste, enjoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समशन
सम्-अशन, अम्, n. the act of eating together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समशनीय
सम्-अशनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be eaten together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्ठिल|समष्ठिलः
समष्ठिल सम्-अष्ठिल, अस्, m. (see अष्ठि),<BR>a kind of shrub (= कोकाग्र, आम्र-गन्धक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्ठिला
सम्-अष्ठिला, f. a kind of pot-herb or cucumber<BR>(= गण्डीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्ठीला
सम्-अष्ठीला, f. = सम्-अष्ठिला above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्
समस् 1. सम्-अस्, cl. 2. P. -अस्ति, to be, exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्
समस् 2. सम्-अस्, cl. 4. P. -अस्यति, -असितुम्<BR>(Ved. Inf. सम्-आसम्), to throw or bring together,<BR>join together, combine, compound, mix, mingle,<BR>connect: Pass. -अस्यते, to be thrown together or<BR>combined, to be compounded; (in grammar) to be<BR>compounded, form a compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन|समसनं
सम्-असन, अम्, n. the act of throwing together,<BR>aggregation, combination, conjunction, compound-<BR>ing, composition, formation of compound words;<BR>contracting, contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्त|समस्तं
सम्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown together, combined,<BR>connected, united, compounded, compound; inherent<BR>in or pervading the whole of anything; all, the<BR>whole, entire, complete [cf. यावत्-स्˚]; contracted,<BR>abbreviated, condensed, concise, succinct, abridged.<BR>—समस्त-बल, अम्, n. a whole army, entire force.<BR>—समस्त-लोक, अस्, m. the whole world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्य
1. सम्-अस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thrown or brought<BR>together, to be collected together, to be compounded<BR>or combined; to be made entire or complete; (आ),<BR>f. part of a stanza given to another person to be<BR>completed; the giving this to any one and requiring<BR>him (as a proof of his skill) to complete it.<BR>—सम्-<BR>अस्या-पूरण, अम्, n. the filling up or completing<BR>a Samasyā, (see above.)<BR>—समस्यार्था (˚य-अर्˚),<BR>f. part of a stanza to be completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्य
2. सम्-अस्य, ind. having thrown or put together,<BR>having duly collected or arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्यमान
सम्-अस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being combined,<BR>being compounded, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास|समासः
1. सम्-आस, अस्, m. (for 2. see under 2. सम्-आस्),<BR>throwing or bringing together, aggregation, collec-<BR>tion, conjunction, combination, connection, union,<BR>compounding, composition; composition of words,<BR>a compound word (of which there are six kinds,<BR>according to native grammarians, viz. Dvandva,<BR>Bahu-vrīhi, Karma-dhāraya, Tat-puruṣa, Dvigu,<BR>and Avyaya or Avyayī-bhava, an improper com-<BR>pound is called अस्थान-समास); euphonic combi-<BR>nation (= सन्धि); composition of differences, unit-<BR>ing enemies, reconciliation; an aggregate, collection,<BR>assemblage; a collection of parts, whole, totality,<BR>summary; contraction, abbreviation, condensation,<BR>abridgement; succinctness, conciseness; (एन), ind.<BR>summarily, with conciseness, succinctly.<BR>—समास-<BR>तस्, ind. in a summary manner, succinctly, concisely,<BR>briefly.<BR>—समास-पाद, अस्, m., N. of a section of<BR>the Kātantra grammar on the subject of compound<BR>words; of a section on the same subject in the<BR>Saṅkṣipta-sāra.<BR>—समास-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>sisting chiefly of compound words.<BR>—समास-ब-<BR>हुल, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in compounds (as a<BR>poetical style).<BR>—समास-भावना, f. (in mathema-<BR>tics) composition effected by addition or by the sum<BR>of the products.<BR>—समास-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possess-<BR>ing compounds, compounded; contracted, abridged;<BR>(आन्), m. the Toon tree (= तुन्न).<BR>—समास-<BR>सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, called a compound.<BR>—समा-<BR>साङ्ग (˚स-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a member or part of a<BR>compound word.<BR>—समासान्त (˚स-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>(in grammar) a Taddhita affix added at the end of<BR>a compound and belonging to the whole compound.<BR>—समासाध्याहार (˚स-अध्˚), अस्, m. the act of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">Page1071-c+ 72</a>]<BR>supplying an ellipsis in a compound, &c.<BR>—समा-<BR>सार्थ (˚स-अर्˚), अस्, m. the sense of a compound;<BR>(आ), f. part of a stanza proposed as a trial of skill to<BR>be completed (= समस्या).<BR>—समासोक्ति (˚स-उक्˚),<BR>इस्, f. a compound metaphor, protracted metaphor<BR>(in rhetoric).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासित
समासित, अस्, आ, अम्, formed into a collection,<BR>assembled, aggregated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थ|समस्थः
समस्थ सम-स्थ. See p. 1067, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समह्
समह् सम्-अह्, cl. 1. P. -अहति, to join or<BR>connect with, (but according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 48, 5. सम्-अनाह = सन्-दधते, as if fr.<BR>सन्-नह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समह
समह स-मह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. accompanied<BR>with honour, honoured by all; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Indra, (Sāy. = समान-पूज, सर्वैः पूज्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समहीधर
समहीधर स-महीधर, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>mountains, mountainous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समह्या
समह्या समह्या, f. (perhaps for सम-ज्ञा,<BR>q. v.), fame, reputation; [cf. सम्-अज्या.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समा
समा 2. समा (for 1. see p. 1067, col. 1),<BR>ind. (apparently an old inst. and connected with<BR>2. सम्, see समि; cf. अमा, p. 74, सचा, p. 1049),<BR>with, together with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकर्णय
समाकर्णय सम्-आ-कर्णय, cl. 10. P. -कर्-<BR>णयति, -यितुम्, to give ear to, listen to, hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकर्ण्य
सम्-आकर्ण्य, ind. having listened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकाङ्क्ष्
समाकाङ्क्ष् सम्-आ-काङ्क्ष्, cl. 1. P. -काङ्क्-<BR>षति, &c., to long for, hope for, desire, wish for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुल
समाकुल सम्-आकुल, अस्, आ, अम्, crowded<BR>together, crowded, thronged, crammed, filled with;<BR>greatly agitated or confounded, bewildered, troubled,<BR>flurried, confused.<BR>—समाकुल-ता, f. or समाकुल-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. great agitation or confusion, great bewil-<BR>derment or trouble of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकृ
समाकृ सम्-आ-कृ, cl. 5. 8. P. A. -कृणोति,<BR>कृणुते, -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, Ved. to bring<BR>together, unite; to collect together; to make ready,<BR>prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुर्वाण
सम्-आकुर्वाण, अस्, आ, अम्, bringing together, mak-<BR>ing ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकृत
सम्-आकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought or collected toge-<BR>ther.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकृष्
समाकृष् सम्-आ-कृष्, cl. 1. P. -कर्षति,<BR>-कर्ष्टुम्, -क्रष्टुम्, to draw together; to draw<BR>towards, attract; to draw away or out, extract, take<BR>out: Caus. -कर्षयति, -यितुम्, to draw away,<BR>carry off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकर्षिन्
सम्-आकर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, drawing together;<BR>attracting; spreading or extending far, diffusing<BR>fragrance; (ई), m. a scent spreading afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकृष्ट
सम्-आकृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn together;<BR>attracted; drawn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकृष्य
सम्-आकृष्य, ind. having drawn towards or<BR>attracted; having drawn away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकॄ
समाकॄ सम्-आ-कॄ, cl. 6. P. -किरति, -करि-<BR>तुम्, -करीतुम्, to scatter over, pour over, strew<BR>over, cover or fill with anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकीर्ण
सम्-आकीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, strewn over, bestrewed,<BR>completely covered, overspread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रन्द्
समाक्रन्द् सम्-आ-क्रन्द्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रन्-<BR>दति, -ते, &c., to cry out together, cry or lament<BR>piteously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रम्
समाक्रम् सम्-आ-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रा-<BR>मति, -क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to tread upon, step<BR>upon; to press or bear down upon (with acc.); to<BR>overrun, attack, assail, invade, seize upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रान्त
सम्-आक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, trod upon; pressed or<BR>borne down (by a burden &c.); attacked, assailed,<BR>seized upon, possessed; overcome; overrun, per-<BR>vaded, overspread; surmounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रीड्
समाक्रीड् सम्-आ-क्रीड्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रीडति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">Page1072-a+ 75</a>]<BR>ते, -क्रीडितुम्, to play or sport along with<BR>(another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रुश्
समाक्रुश् सम्-आ-क्रुश्, cl. 1. P. -क्रोशति,<BR>-क्रोष्टुम्, to join in reviling any one, call out<BR>abusively at, scold at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रुष्ट
सम्-आक्रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, reviled, abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्लिद्
समाक्लिद् सम्-आ-क्लिद्, cl. 4. P. -क्लिद्यति,<BR>&c., to be well moistened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्लिन्न
सम्-आक्लिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, well moistened, well<BR>wetted; suffused with tears, affected by pity or com-<BR>passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्षिप्
समाक्षिप् सम्-आ-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. A. -क्षि-<BR>पति, -ते, -क्षेप्तुम्, to throw together, heap or<BR>pile up; to thrust or throw away violently, hurl; to<BR>drive way, expel, to throw down; to tear off; to<BR>destroy; to insult, mock, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्षिप्त
सम्-आक्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or heaped<BR>together; thrown or cast off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्षिप्य
सम्-आक्षिप्य, ind. having thrown or cast off;<BR>having torn off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्या
समाख्या 1. सम्-आ-ख्या, cl. 2. P. -ख्याति,<BR>-ख्यातुम्, to reckon up, count up, calculate, enu-<BR>merate; to sum up, add together; to relate fully,<BR>report, communicate, tell; to declare, proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्या
2. सम्-आख्या, f. report, fame, reputation, cele-<BR>brity; name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्यात
सम्-आख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, reckoned up, enume-<BR>rated, summed up; completely or fully related; de-<BR>clared, proclaimed; famed, celebrated, well known,<BR>public, notorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्याय
सम्-आख्याय, ind. having related, having told,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागम्
समागम् सम्-आ-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to come together (either in a friendly or<BR>hostile manner), meet, encounter; become united or<BR>allied with (with inst. or with inst. and सह); to<BR>enter into an alliance; to come together sexually,<BR>have intercourse with; to come together (as heavenly<BR>bodies in conjunction or occultation); to come to,<BR>come near, approach, arrive; to come back, return;<BR>to meet with, come upon, find: Caus. -गमयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to come together, bring together,<BR>unite one thing or person (acc.) with another (inst.<BR>or loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागत|समागतः
सम्-आगत, अस्, आ, अम्, come together, met,<BR>encountered, joined in close conflict, united, joined;<BR>met together, assembled; being in conjunction (as<BR>the heavenly bodies); come to, approached, arrived;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of riddle or enigma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागति|समागतिः
सम्-आगति, इस्, f. coming together; encountering,<BR>meeting; union, joining; approach, arrival, similar<BR>condition or progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागत्य
सम्-आगत्य, ind. = सम्-आगम्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागम|समागमः
सम्-आगम, अस्, m. coming together, encounter,<BR>meeting, union, junction, coalition, assembling; asso-<BR>ciation, acquaintance, intercourse, society, company;<BR>an assembly; (in astronomy) conjunction, the occul-<BR>tation of a heavenly body by another; approach,<BR>arrival.<BR>—समागम-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, causing union.<BR>—समागम-प्रार्थना, f. the desire of associ-<BR>ation.<BR>—समागम-मनोरथ, अस्, m. desire of<BR>union.<BR>—समागमोपाय (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m. means<BR>of union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागमन
सम्-आगमन, अम्, n. the act of coming toge-<BR>ther, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागम्य
सम्-आगम्य, ind. having come together, having<BR>met, having joined in conflict, having gone to meet;<BR>having coalesced; having approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागल्
समागल् सम्-आ-गल्, cl. 1. P. -गलति, -ग-<BR>लितुम्, to fall together, fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागलित
सम्-आगलित, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen down, fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाग्रह्
समाग्रह् सम्-आ-ग्रह्, cl. 9. P. A. -गृह्णाति,<BR>गृह्णीते (Ved. -गृभ्णाति, &c.), -ग्रहीतुम्, to<BR>seize together or at once, lay hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघात|समाघातः
समाघात सम्-आघात. See सम्-आ-हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघ्रा
समाघ्रा सम्-आ-घ्रा, cl. 1. P. -जिघ्रति,<BR>-घ्रातुम्, to smell at, smell; to kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघ्राय
सम्-आघ्राय, ind. having smelt at; having kissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचक्ष्
समाचक्ष् सम्-आ-चक्ष्, cl. 2. A. -चष्टे, &c.<BR>(see rt. चक्ष्), to relate fully, tell, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचम्
समाचम् सम्-आ-चम्, cl. 1. P. -चमति (but<BR>-चामति with आ, see आ-चम्, cf. Pāṇ. VII. 3, 75),<BR>to sip water (as a religious act forming part of the<BR>ceremony of ablution).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचम्य
सम्-आचम्य, ind. having sipped water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचर्
समाचर् सम्-आ-चर्, cl. 1. P. A. -चरति,<BR>-ते, &c., to proceed; to practise, perform thoroughly,<BR>do, act, accomplish; to conduct one's self, behave;<BR>to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचर
सम्-आचर, अस्, ई, अम्, who or what proceeds or<BR>practises; practising, observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरण|समाचरणं
सम्-आचरण, अम्, n. the act of proceeding,<BR>practising, performing, observing, behaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरत्
सम्-आचरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, proceeding, practising,<BR>behaving, following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरित
सम्-आचरित, अस्, आ, अम्, practised, performed,<BR>done, committed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचार|समाचारः
2. सम्-आचार, अस्, m. (for 1. समाचार see<BR>p. 1067, col. 1), proceeding, going; performance,<BR>practice, conduct, behaviour, usage, way; proper<BR>practice or behaviour; doings, news, report, infor-<BR>mation, intelligence, tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचीर्ण
सम्-आचीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, performed, done, prac-<BR>tised, committed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचि
समाचि सम्-आ-चि, cl. 5. P. A. -चिनोति, -चि-<BR>नुते, -चेतुम्, to heap up together, accumulate; to<BR>load or cover with; to fill up (cavities in a road &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचयन|समाचयनं
सम्-आचयन, अम्, n. the act of heaping up<BR>together, accumulation, aggregation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचित
सम्-आचित, अस्, आ, अम्, heaped together, covered<BR>with, overspread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचीर्ण
समाचीर्ण सम्-आचीर्ण. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाच्छद्
समाच्छद् सम्-आ-च्छद्, cl. 10. P. -च्छाद-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cover completely with, overspread,<BR>conceal, veil, cloud; to stupefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाच्छन्न
सम्-आच्छन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, completely covered<BR>with, concealed; involved in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाच्छाद्य
सम्-आच्छाद्य, ind. having covered with, having<BR>overspread, having clouded, having stupefied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाच्छिद्
समाच्छिद् सम्-आ-च्छिद्, cl. 7. P. A. -च्छि-<BR>नत्ति, -च्छिन्त्ते, -च्छेत्तुम्, to cut off; to tear<BR>away, snatch away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाच्छिद्य
सम्-आच्छिद्य, ind. having cut off; having snatched<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज|समाजः
समाज समाज, &c. See under सम्-अज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजुष्
समाजुष् सम्-आ-जुष्, cl. 6. P. A. -जुषति,<BR>-ते (Prec. -जुष्यात्), &c., to have a liking for, be<BR>inclined towards, resolve upon (with dat.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजुहूषमाण
समाजुहूषमाण सम्-आजुहूषमाण. See<BR>सम्-आ-ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञा
समाज्ञा 1. सम्-आ-ज्ञा, cl. 9. P. A. -जानाति,<BR>जानीते, -ज्ञातुम्, to know or understand thoroughly,<BR>become acquainted with, learn, ascertain, perceive,<BR>observe; to acknowledge, recognise: Caus. -ज्ञाप-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, to order, command, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञप्त
सम्-आज्ञप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ordered, commanded,<BR>directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञा
2. सम्-आज्ञा, f. reputation, fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञात
सम्-आज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, known, ascertained, ac-<BR>knowledged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञाय
सम्-आज्ञाय, ind. having known, having learnt<BR>or ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समातन्
समातन् सम्-आ-तन्, cl. 8. P. A. -तनोति,<BR>-तनुते, -तनितुम्, to extend, spread; to effect,<BR>cause, produce, procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समातत
सम्-आतत, अस्, आ, अम्, extended, stretched, strung<BR>(as a bow); excessive, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समातन्वत्
सम्-आतन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, extending; producing,<BR>procuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समातृचक्रवाल
समातृचक्रवाल स-मातृ-चक्रवाल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, attended by the whole circle of divine Mātṛs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादा
समादा सम्-आ-दा, cl. 3. P. A. -ददाति,<BR>-दत्ते, -दातुम्, to give, bestow, present; to give<BR>back, restore; to take or receive fully or entirely;<BR>to take together, take away with, take away, take<BR>off; to take hold of, seize; to take up; to appre-<BR>hend, perceive, comprehend; to take, receive, ac-<BR>cept; to collect; to undertake, begin, (वचनं<BR>सम्-आदा, to begin a speech); to take to heart,<BR>reflect on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादत्त
सम्-आदत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, taken away, taken hold<BR>of, seized, received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाददान
सम्-आददान, अस्, आ, अम्, taking away, taking<BR>hold of, receiving, taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादान|समादानं
सम्-आदान, अम्, n. the act of taking or receiving<BR>fully or entirely; receiving suitable donations; the<BR>daily observances of the Jaina sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादाय
सम्-आदाय, ind. having wholly taken, having taken<BR>away, having taken or seized, having accepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादेय
सम्-आदेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or received,<BR>acceptable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादिश्
समादिश् सम्-आ-दिश्, cl. 6. P. -दिशति, -देष्-<BR>टुम्, to assign, allot; to point out, indicate, declare,<BR>announce, communicate, inform; to foretell, fore-<BR>show; to appoint, name, commission, charge, de-<BR>pute, delegate; to direct, advise, order, command;<BR>to determine: Caus. -देशयति, -यितुम्, to order,<BR>command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादिश्य
सम्-आदिश्य, ind. having assigned, having indi-<BR>cated, having directed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादिष्ट
सम्-आदिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, assigned, indicated,<BR>directed, commanded, enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादेश|समादेशः
सम्-आदेश, अस्, m. direction, advice, order, com-<BR>mand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादृ
समादृ सम्-आ-दृ, cl. 6. A. -द्रियते, &c.,<BR>to respect greatly; to be greatly respected or<BR>honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादर
सम्-आदर, अस्, m. great respect, veneration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादरणीय
सम्-आदरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be greatly re-<BR>spected or venerated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादृत
सम्-आदृत, अस्, आ, अम्, very respectful, showing<BR>great regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाद्रु
समाद्रु सम्-आ-द्रु, cl. 1. P. -द्रवति (ep.<BR>also A. -ते), -द्रोतुम्, to run towards together, run<BR>towards; to rush against, rush at, attack (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधा
समाधा 1. सम्-आ-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, to place or put or hold together,<BR>fix together, compose, collect, unite, join, reconcile,<BR>compose differences; to adjust, set right, make right,<BR>settle, solve a difficulty, reply to an objection (e. g.<BR>समाधत्ते, he settles a question, he answers an<BR>objection, he clears up a doubt or difficulty); to<BR>dispose, put in order, arrange, repair, redress; to put<BR>or place to, put or place on (e. g. इध्मं समा-<BR>धत्ते, he puts on fuel; वासः समाधत्ते, he<BR>puts on a garment); to lay or place upon, apply,<BR>impose; to deliver over, intrust, commit to, appoint<BR>to; to impose a burden, load; to compose or collect<BR>the thoughts, pay great attention, apply or fix in-<BR>tently (e. g. दृष्टिं समाधा, to fix the sight;<BR>चित्तम् or चेतः or मनः or मतिं समाधा,<BR>to fix the mind upon, with loc.); to devote one's<BR>self to, give one's self up to (generally A.); to<BR>assume, take to one's self, take upon one's self;<BR>to conceive (in the womb); to produce, effect,<BR>cause, make, accomplish, complete; to put down as<BR>settled (A.), establish, declare: Pass. -धीयते, to be<BR>placed together or adjusted or arranged; to be recon-<BR>ciled, &c.: Desid. -धित्सति, to wish to put together,<BR>desire to collect or compose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधा
2. सम्-आधा, आस्, m. putting together, adjusting,<BR>settling, reconciling, clearing up difficulties, &c.;<BR>completion, accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधान|समाधानं
सम्-आधान, अम्, n. the act of putting together<BR>or collecting or composing; fixing the mind in<BR>abstract contemplation (as on the true nature of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">Page1073-a+ 79</a>]<BR>spirit), religious meditation, profound absorption or<BR>contemplation (in general); intentness, attention,<BR>eagerness; clearing up a doubt, answering an objec-<BR>tion, replying to the Pūrva-pakṣa (in logic); agree-<BR>ing, promising; declaring, declaration (in the drama),<BR>a leading incident (described as one which unexpect-<BR>edly gives rise to the whole plot).<BR>—समाधान-<BR>मात्र, अम्, n. mere contemplation, only religious<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधाय
सम्-आधाय, ind. having put together, having<BR>steadily composed or collected or adjusted, &c.; hav-<BR>ing fixed (the mind or thoughts) upon, being en-<BR>gaged in religious meditation, being intent upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधि|समाधिः
सम्-आधि, इस्, m. putting together; collecting or<BR>composing the mind, fixing the thoughts, intentness,<BR>attentiveness, intent contemplation, profound or ab-<BR>stract meditation (especially on the true nature of<BR>spirit &c.), perfect absorption of thought into the<BR>one object of meditation (i. e. the Supreme Spirit;<BR>this is the eighth and last stage of Yoga); intense<BR>absorption or contemplation (in general); silence;<BR>devotion; a religious vow or self-imposed restraint;<BR>composing differences, making up quarrels, recon-<BR>cilement; agreement, assent, promise, engagement;<BR>making good; requital, retaliation; support, uphold-<BR>ing; continuance; completion, accomplishment, con-<BR>clusion, demonstrated conclusion; attempting impos-<BR>sibilities; perseverance in extreme difficulties; col-<BR>lecting or laying up grain in times of dearth; the<BR>joint of the neck; a tomb, grave; a Jaina saint of<BR>the future age; a particular figure of rhetoric (de-<BR>scribed as the coincidence of two events accidentally<BR>connected and expressed by a common verb, e. g.<BR>सा जगाम अस्तं च भानुमान्, she went away<BR>and the sun to its setting).<BR>—समाधि-भङ्ग, अस्,<BR>m. the breaking or interruption of meditation.<BR>—स-<BR>माधि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, engaged in meditation,<BR>absorbed in contemplation; making a promise, an-<BR>nouncing assent or permission.<BR>—समाधि-योग, अस्,<BR>m. application or employment of religious medita-<BR>tion, the efficacy of contemplation.<BR>—समाधि-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, abiding in contemplation, absorbed in<BR>devout meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिन्
समाधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, absorbed in contemplation,<BR>meditating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहित|समाहितः
सम्-आहित, अस्, आ, अम्, placed together, put or<BR>fixed together, held together, composed, collected,<BR>compiled, accumulated, assembled; comprehended;<BR>united, joined, reconciled, adjusted, made up (as a<BR>quarrel), set right, put in order, settled, disposed,<BR>arranged, repaired; concluded, inferred, demonstrated;<BR>agreed upon, assented to; promised; placed or put<BR>on, imposed, applied; deposited, entrusted, delivered<BR>over; composed or collected (as the thoughts), fixed<BR>(in abstract meditation), intently absorbed, very<BR>intent on or attentive, abstracted; steadfast, firm,<BR>cool, calm; made, effected, accomplished, finished,<BR>completed; (अस्), m. a pure or holy man; (अम्), n.<BR>great attention or intentness, description of great<BR>intentness (as a figure of rhetoric).<BR>—समाहित-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the mind fixed in con-<BR>templation, absorbed in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधाव्
समाधाव् सम्-आ-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति,<BR>-ते, &c., to run together towards, rush towards, run<BR>near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधू
समाधू सम्-आ-धू, cl. 5. P. A. -धूनोति,<BR>-धूनुते, -धुनोति, -धुनुते, &c., to shake off,<BR>drive away, dispel, disperse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधूत
सम्-आधूत, अस्, आ, अम्, driven away, dispersed,<BR>scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाध्मा
समाध्मा सम्-आ-ध्मा, cl. 1. P. -धमति,<BR>-ध्मातुम्, to blow into (a horn &c.); to inflate; to<BR>cause (musical instruments) to sound forth together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाध्मात
सम्-आध्मात, अस्, आ, अम्, blown into; made to<BR>sound forth together; swelled up, puffed up, swollen,<BR>inflated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाध्यै
समाध्यै सम्-आ-ध्यै, cl. 1. P. -ध्यायति,<BR>-ध्यातुम्, to meditate deeply upon, reflect upon,<BR>be lost in thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान|समानं|समानः
समान 2. समान, अस्, आ (Ved. also ई), अम्<BR>(according to some fr. स + मान, as if the original<BR>meaning were ‘having the same measure,’ according<BR>to others connected with 1. सम; in Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 87, 4. समानस्मात्, abl. c. = समस्मात् = सर्-<BR>वेषाम् साधारणात्, see 1. सम; for 1. सम्-आन<BR>see under सम्-अन्), same, alike, similar, equal (with<BR>inst., e. g. तेन समान, equal to him), uniform, one;<BR>common to all, common, general; good, virtuous;<BR>honoured; (अम्), ind. equally with (with inst.); (अस्),<BR>m. an equal, friend; any letter which corresponds to<BR>another (e. g. a long to its short vowel, a hard guttural<BR>to its soft), a letter having the same place or organ of<BR>utterance; (ई), f. a kind of metre.<BR>—समान-काल<BR>or समान-कालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, synchronous, occur-<BR>ring or produced at the same time.<BR>—समान-गोत्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being of the same family (= स-गोत्र,<BR>q. v.).<BR>—समान-जन, अस्, m. a person of the same<BR>family or race.<BR>—समान-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, having<BR>a common birth or origin, of equal age.<BR>—समान-<BR>जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, or समान-जातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>longing to the same kind or species, of a common<BR>tribe or caste, of the same sort.<BR>—समान-ता, f. or<BR>समान-त्व, अम्, n. sameness, equality, likeness;<BR>community of kind or quality.<BR>—समान-तेजस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, of equal splendor, equal in glory.<BR>—समान-<BR>दुःख, अस्, आ, अम्, having the same griefs, sympa-<BR>thising.<BR>—समान-बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. of the<BR>same family.<BR>—समान-मान, अस्, आ, अम्, receiving<BR>equal honour, equally respected.<BR>—समान-यम,<BR>अस्, m. the same pitch of voice.<BR>—समान-योग-<BR>क्षेम, अस्, आ, अम्, having the same value.<BR>—स-<BR>मान-योजन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the same<BR>yoking, harnessed for both alike (said of the chariot<BR>of the Aśvins).<BR>—समान-रुचि, इस्, इस्, इ, having the<BR>same tastes, taking pleasure in similar objects.<BR>—स-<BR>मानरुचि-ता, f. the having similar tastes.<BR>—समान-<BR>रूपा, f. a kind of riddle or enigma.<BR>—समान-<BR>वयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or समान-वयस्क, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of the same age.<BR>—समान-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>of equal splendor.<BR>—समान-शब्दा, f. a kind of<BR>riddle or enigma.<BR>—समान-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a<BR>similar disposition or temper.<BR>—समानाक्षर<BR>(˚न-अक्˚), ‘a monophthong,’ N. of the vowels अ, आ,<BR>इ, ई, उ, ऊ, ऋ, ॠ, ऌ (as opposed to the सन्ध्य्-<BR>अक्षर or diphthongs).<BR>—समानाधिकरण<BR>(˚न-अध्˚), अम्, n. common or same government;<BR>same location, same predicament; a predicament<BR>including several things or persons, common or<BR>generic property, common substratum; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>being in the same subject or category, being in the<BR>same predicament, having the same location or<BR>sphere; having a common substratum (in the Vaiśe-<BR>shika phil.); agreeing together in the same case,<BR>&c., being in the same government, (see अधि-<BR>करण.)<BR>—समानाधिकार (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>similar office, like rule or government; generic<BR>character.<BR>—समानार्थ or समानार्थक (˚न-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the same meaning, syno-<BR>nymous.<BR>—समानार्थ-प्रयोजन (˚न-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a common object and purpose,<BR>caused by common interests.<BR>—समानालङ्कार<BR>(˚न-अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wearing the same ornaments.<BR>—समानोदक (˚न-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘having com-<BR>mon water-oblations,’ a kinsman connected by the<BR>offering of water to the departed spirits of common<BR>ancestors, (this relationship is said to extend to the<BR>fourteenth degree, the first seven being both Sapiṇḍas<BR>and Samānodakas, while the remaining seven are<BR>Samānodakas only.)<BR>—समानोदर्य (˚न-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. born from the same womb, a brother of<BR>whole blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानय
समानय, Nom. P. समानयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make equal or similar, equalise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयत्
1. समानयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (for 2. see col. 3),<BR>equalising, making equal or like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानिका
समानिका, f. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानी
समानी सम्-आ-नी, cl. 1. P. A. -नयति, -ते,<BR>-नेतुम्, to lead or conduct together, unite, bring<BR>together, join together, collect, assemble; to lead<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">Page1073-c+ 78</a>]<BR>any one to another, unite one person (acc.) with<BR>another (inst. or inst. with सह); to lead towards,<BR>bring near; to bring on; to pour one liquid into<BR>another; to bring or offer an oblation: Caus. -ना-<BR>ययति, -यितुम्, to cause to be brought together,<BR>cause to bring together, cause to be brought near,<BR>call together, convoke, assemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयत्
2. सम्-आनयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bringing together,<BR>leading towards, bringing near, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयन|समानयनं
सम्-आनयन, अम्, n. the act of bringing together,<BR>collecting, leading towards, conducting, bringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानाय्य
सम्-आनाय्य, ind. (fr. the Caus.), having caused<BR>to be brought together, having convoked or called<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानीत
सम्-आनीत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought together, col-<BR>lected, assembled, led towards or near, conducted,<BR>conveyed, brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानीय
सम्-आनीय, ind. having brought together, having<BR>led near, having brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान्त|समान्तः
समान्त समान्त. See 1. समा, p. 1067.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्
समाप् सम्-आप्, cl. 5. P. -आप्नोति, -आप्तुम्,<BR>to obtain completely, gain; to accomplish, fulfil; to<BR>reach: Caus. -आपयति, -यितुम्, to cause to gain or<BR>obtain completely, cause to reach or attain entirely;<BR>to cause to fulfil, accomplish, bring to an end, finish,<BR>complete, conclude: Desid. of Caus. -आपिपयिषति,<BR>to wish to cause to complete, try to accomplish:<BR>Desid. -ईप्सति, to wish to obtain or reach, wish to<BR>accomplish, wish for, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप|समापः
सम्-आप, अस्, m. sacrificing, offering oblations to<BR>the gods (= देव-यजन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापक|समापकः
सम्-आपक, अस्, इका, अम्, accomplishing, com-<BR>pleting, fulfilling, finishing; bringing to an end;<BR>killing; (इका), f. a verb or any part of speech used as<BR>a verb to complete a sentence.<BR>—समापक-क्रिया,<BR>f. a finishing act, finishing stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन|समापनं
सम्-आपन, अम्, n. the act of causing to obtain<BR>or gain completely, accomplishing, conclusion, com-<BR>pletion; acquisition, gain; killing, destroying; a<BR>section, chapter, division; profound meditation;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), completing, concluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापनीय
सम्-आपनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be accomplished or<BR>completed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापित|समापितं
सम्-आपित, अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished, finished,<BR>concluded, done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापिपयिषु
सम्-आपिपयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to cause to<BR>complete, desirous of accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्त|समाप्तः
सम्-आप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, concluded, completed,<BR>finished, ended, done; clever.<BR>—समाप्त-प्राय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, nearly finished.<BR>—समाप्त-भूयिष्ठ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, nearly completed or ended, having the<BR>greater part finished.<BR>—समाप्त-शिक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has completed his studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्ताल|समाप्तालः
समाप्ताल, अस्, m. (doubtful), a lord, master,<BR>(according to Śabda-k. = पति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्ति|समाप्तिः
सम्-आप्ति, इस्, f. complete acquisition, accomplish-<BR>ment, completion, perfection, conclusion, finish, end;<BR>reconciling differences, putting an end to disputes.<BR>—समाप्ति-साधन, अम्, n. means of accom-<BR>plishment or completion.<BR>—समाप्त्य्-अर्था, f. part<BR>of a stanza given as a trial of skill to be completed;<BR>[cf. समस्यार्था.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तिक|समाप्तिकः
समाप्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, concluding, completing,<BR>final, finite; one who has finished the whole; (अस्),<BR>m. one who has completed a course of holy study;<BR>a finisher, ender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्य|समाप्यं
1. सम्-आप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = सम्-आपनीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्य|समाप्यं
2. सम्-आप्य, ind. having obtained completely,<BR>having completed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीप्सित
सम्-ईप्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished for, longed for,<BR>desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापत्
समापत् सम्-आ-पत्, cl. 1. P. -पतति, -पति-<BR>तुम्, to fly together towards; to rush fully upon,<BR>fall upon, assail, assault, attack; to come together,<BR>be united sexually with (with inst.); to come to,<BR>attain to, obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापतत्
सम्-आपतत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, rushing upon, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापद्
समापद् सम्-आ-पद्, cl. 4. A. -पद्यते,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">Page1074-a+ 75</a>]<BR>पत्तुम्, to fall upon, assail, attack; to fall into any<BR>state or condition, attain to, undergo; to begin; to<BR>come together, come about, come to pass, occur,<BR>take place, appear; to be finished or completed:<BR>Caus. -पादयति, &c., to cause to come to pass; to<BR>bring about, complete, accomplish; to restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापत्ति|समापत्तिः
सम्-आपत्ति, इस्, f. coming together, meeting, en-<BR>countering; restoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन्न|समापन्नं
सम्-आपन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, attained, obtained,<BR>gained; occurred, come, arrived, happened; finished,<BR>completed, accomplished, concluded, done; perfect,<BR>proficient (in any science &c.); furnished or endowed<BR>with; distressed, afflicted; killed; [cf. व्य्-आपन्न.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापादन|समापादनं
सम्-आपादन, अम्, n. the act of bringing about,<BR>accomplishing, &c.; restoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापाद्य|समापाद्यं
सम्-आपाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought about, to<BR>be restored; (अम्), n. the change of Visarga to स् or<BR>ष् (= उपा-चरित); the change to ष् (in Vedic<BR>phonetics, = ष-त्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापा
समापा सम्-आ-पा, cl. 1. P. -पिबति, -पिवति,<BR>पातुम्, to drink entirely up, drink up, absorb; to<BR>drink in, imbibe, suck in; to suck out, drain, im-<BR>poverish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापिबत्
सम्-आपिबत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, drinking up, absorbing;<BR>drinking in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापू
समापू सम्-आ-पू, cl. 9. P. A. -पुनाति, -पु-<BR>नीते, &c., to purify thoroughly, purge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापॄ
समापॄ सम्-आ-पॄ, Pass. -पूर्यते, to be-<BR>come completely full, be quite filled: Caus. -पूर-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to make quite full; to fill out; to<BR>draw or bend (a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापूर्ण
सम्-आपूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, completely full, well<BR>filled; complete, entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्यै
समाप्यै सम्-आ-प्यै, cl. 1. A. -प्यायते,<BR>-प्यातुम्, -प्यायितुम्, to grow, increase: Caus.<BR>-प्याययति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause to increase or<BR>grow, nourish, invigorate; to refresh, reanimate,<BR>animate, enliven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्यायित
सम्-आप्यायित, अस्, आ, अम्, nourished, invigorated,<BR>refreshed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्लु
समाप्लु सम्-आ-प्लु, cl. 1. A. -प्लवते, -प्लो-<BR>तुम्, to bathe or immerse together; to overflow,<BR>inundate, overwhelm, overspread; to jump or spring<BR>upon, rush upon; to come into violent collision with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्लुत
सम्-आप्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, bathed, bathing in;<BR>drowned, well drenched, flooded, inundated, over-<BR>whelmed; overflowing or suffused with moisture;<BR>overflowing, filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्लुत्य
सम्-आप्लुत्य, ind. having bathed together; inun-<BR>dating; rushing together, coming into collision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाबन्ध्
समाबन्ध् सम्-आ-बन्ध्, cl. 9. P. -बध्नाति,<BR>-बन्द्धुम्, to bind on, fasten on firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाबध्य
सम्-आबध्य, ind. having bound or fastened on<BR>firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभा
समाभा सम्-आ-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति, -भातुम्,<BR>to appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभाष्
समाभाष् सम्-आ-भाष्, cl. 1. A. -भाषते,<BR>-भाषितुम्, to talk together, converse with, converse<BR>together, address, speak to; to speak about, com-<BR>municate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभाषण|समाभाषणं
सम्-आभाषण, अम्, n. the act of conversing<BR>with, speaking to or addressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभाष्य
सम्-आभाष्य, ind. having talked or conversed<BR>together, having spoken to, having addressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभुज्
समाभुज् सम्-आ-भुज्, cl. 7. P. A. -भुनक्ति,<BR>-भुङ्क्ते, to enjoy or possess entirely or completely;<BR>to rule over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभृ
समाभृ सम्-आ-भृ, cl. 1. P. A. -भरति,<BR>-ते, -भर्तुम्, Ved. to bring together; to produce,<BR>procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभृत
सम्-आभृत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought together, pro-<BR>cured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समामन्त्र्
समामन्त्र् सम्-आ-मन्त्र्, cl. 10. A. -मन्त्र-<BR>यते, -यितुम्, to address, accost; to invoke, summon;<BR>to bid farewell to any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समामन्त्रय
सम्-आमन्त्रय, ind. having addressed; having<BR>bid farewell to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्ना
समाम्ना सम्-आ-म्ना, cl. 1. P. -मनति, -म्ना-<BR>तुम्, to repeat or mention together; to hand down;<BR>to repeat memoriter or by tradition (especially to<BR>repeat or hand down traditionally collections of words<BR>or sacred texts); to enumerate; to prescribe: Pass.<BR>-म्नायते, to be handed down, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नात
सम्-आम्नात, अस्, आ, अम्, repeated or mentioned<BR>together; repeated traditionally, handed down by<BR>memory or tradition; recited, enumerated; pre-<BR>scribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नान|समाम्नानं
सम्-आम्नान, अम्, n. repetition, mention, hand-<BR>ing down or repeating traditionally; enumeration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नाय|समाम्नायः
सम्-आम्नाय, अस्, m. repetition or mention toge-<BR>ther, traditional repetition or mention (especially of<BR>sacred texts &c.); a traditional collection (of words<BR>&c.); tradition or repetition or mention (in general);<BR>enumeration, reading, recitation (= पठन); tota-<BR>lity, aggregate; epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाय|समायः
समाय सम्-आय. See under 1. सम्-इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायत्
समायत् सम्-आ-यत्, cl. 1. A. -यतते, -य-<BR>तितुम्, to attach one's self to, be devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायत्त
सम्-आ-यत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to, resting or<BR>depending on (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायम्
समायम् सम्-आ-यम्, cl. 1. P. A. -यच्छति,<BR>-ते, &c., to draw together, contract; to draw out,<BR>extend; to draw, pull, stretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायत
सम्-आयत, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn out, lengthened,<BR>extended, long (e. g. द्वि-योजन-समायत, two<BR>Yojanas long).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायस्त
समायस्त सम्-आ-यस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. यस्<BR>with आ and सम्), distressed, troubled, oppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाया
समाया सम्-आ-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -यातुम्, to<BR>come together; to come to, approach, arrive at,<BR>reach, attain, obtain, meet with; to go to any state<BR>(with acc.; see rt. 1. या); to pass away, elapse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायात्
सम्-आयात्, आन्, आती or आन्ती, आत्, coming towards,<BR>approaching, arriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायात
सम्-आयात, अस्, आ, अम्, come together, come to,<BR>arrived at, reached, attained, arrived, come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुज्
समायुज् सम्-आ-युज्, cl. 7. P. A. -युनक्ति,<BR>-युङ्क्ते, -योक्तुम्, to join or fasten together, unite<BR>with; to join, connect, prepare, make ready; to<BR>provide, furnish, supply; to meet together, encounter;<BR>to enjoin, charge, entrust, appoint; to surround:<BR>Caus. -योजयति, -यितुम्, to join together, connect,<BR>fit together; to furnish or supply with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुक्त
सम्-आयुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, joined, connected, united;<BR>attached; touched; intent on, devoted to; pre-<BR>pared, made ready; well furnished or endowed with;<BR>supplied, provided; enjoined, charged, appointed;<BR>met together, encountered, brought into contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायोग|समायोगः
सम्-आयोग, अस्, m. conjunction, connection, union,<BR>junction, preparation, fitting (an arrow to a bow),<BR>aiming; association; assemblage, multitude, heap;<BR>cause, origin, motive, object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुत
समायुत सम्-आयुत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. यु<BR>with आ and सम्), joined together, connected or<BR>united with, attached to; furnished or endowed<BR>with, possessed of, adorned with; brought together,<BR>collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारत
समारत सम्-आरत, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. रम्<BR>with आ and सम्), ceased from, left off, desisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारभ्
समारभ् सम्-आ-रभ्, cl. 1. A. -रभते,<BR>-रब्धुम्, to take in hand, undertake, begin, com-<BR>mence, try; to try to propitiate: Pass. -रभ्यते,<BR>to be undertaken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारब्ध
सम्-आरब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, taken in hand, under-<BR>taken, begun, commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारभ्य
सम्-आरभ्य, ind. having undertaken; having<BR>commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारम्भ|समारंभ|समारंभः|समारम्भः
सम्-आरम्भ, अस्, m. undertaking, enterprise,<BR>commencement, beginning; using; anointing the<BR>body, an unguent (= सम्-आलम्भ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारम्भण
सम्-आरम्भण, अम्, n. taking in hand, under-<BR>taking; anointing (= सम्-आलम्भन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाराण
समाराण सम्-आराण. See under सम्-ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाराध्
समाराध् सम्-आ-राध्, Caus. -राधयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to conciliate, propitiate, make favour-<BR>able, gratify, satisfy, serve; to win.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाराधन|समाराधनं
सम्-आराधन, अम्, n. the act of conciliating,<BR>gratifying, conciliation, propitiation; winning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुज्
समारुज् सम्-आ-रुज्, cl. 6. P. -रुजति, -रोक्-<BR>तुम्, to break to pieces, break down, break off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुज्य
सम्-आरुज्य, ind. having broken off, having<BR>broken to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुध्
समारुध् सम्-आ-रुध्, cl. 7. P. A. -रुणद्धि,<BR>-रुन्द्धे, -रोद्धुम्, to block up, obstruct, stop up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुध्य
सम्-आरुध्य, ind. having blocked up or ob-<BR>structed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुह्
समारुह् सम्-आ-रुह्, cl. 1. P. -रोहति, -रो-<BR>ढुम्, to ascend or mount on, ride on; to ascend<BR>or rise to (with acc. or sometimes loc.); to go to,<BR>enter upon, undertake, begin, engage in, attain to:<BR>Caus. -रोहयति, -ते, -रोपयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to mount upon or ascend; to cause to rise up, lift<BR>up, raise; to string (a bow); to put or place or<BR>deposit upon or in (with loc. or acc.); to plant; to<BR>deliver over to (with loc.), hand over; to ascribe,<BR>attribute; to display, put forth, exhibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुरुक्षु
सम्-आरुरुक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुध्य
सम्-आरुध्य, ind. having ascended, having mounted<BR>upon, having surmounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारूढ
सम्-आरूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, ascended, mounted, gone<BR>up; grown over, healed; agreed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपण|समारोपणं
सम्-आरोपण, अम्, n. the act of causing to ascend,<BR>placing or fixing in or on, depositing, delivering over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपित
सम्-आरोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to mount or<BR>ascend; strung (as a bow); placed in or on, de-<BR>posited, planted, lodged; delivered over; put forth,<BR>displayed.<BR>—समारोपित-कार्मुक, अस्, m. a strung<BR>bow; one who has strung a bow.<BR>—समारोपित-<BR>भार, अस्, आ, अम्, one on whom a burden has been<BR>placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोप्य
सम्-आरोप्य, ind. having caused to ascend, having<BR>raised; having placed or deposited in or on; having<BR>delivered over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोह|समारोहः
सम्-आरोह, अस्, m. ascending, mounting, going<BR>up; riding upon; agreeing upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोहण
सम्-आरोहण, अम्, n. the act of mounting or<BR>ascending, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोह्य
सम्-आरोह्य, ind. having put or placed on or<BR>deposited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालक्ष्
समालक्ष् सम्-आ-लक्ष्, cl. 10. P. A. -लक्-<BR>षयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to look at attentively, behold,<BR>see, perceive, view, observe, regard, consider, watch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालक्ष्य
सम्-आलक्ष्य, ind. having looked at or con-<BR>sidered well, perceiving, regarding, contemplating,<BR>watching for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालग्न
समालग्न सम्-आ-लग्न, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>लग् with आ and सम्), sticking or adhering together,<BR>closely clasped or united together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालप्
समालप् सम्-आ-लप्, cl. 1. P. -लपति, &c.,<BR>to converse together; to speak to, address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालभ्
समालभ् सम्-आ-लभ्, cl. 1. A. -लभते,<BR>-लब्धुम्, to take hold of, seize, grasp; to stroke,<BR>handle; to touch, rub, anoint, smear over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालब्ध
सम्-आलब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, taken hold of, grasped,<BR>handled, touched; rubbed, anointed, smeared (with<BR>unguents &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भ|समालंभ|समालंभः|समालम्भः
सम्-आलम्भ, अस्, m. taking hold of, seizing,<BR>seizing a victim (for sacrifice); rubbing, smearing<BR>the body with unguents or coloured perfumes (as<BR>saffron &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भन|समालंभन|समालंभनं|समालम्भनं
सम्-आलम्भन, अम्, n. the act of taking hold<BR>of, seizing; anointing or smearing the body (with<BR>perfumes &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्ब्|समालंब्
समालम्ब् सम्-आ-लम्ब्, cl. 1. A. -लम्बते,<BR>-लम्बितुम्, to hang on to (any one), hold on to,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">Page1075-a+ 73</a>]<BR>cling to, grasp, lay hold of, seize; to lean or rest<BR>upon, be supported by, depend upon, trust to, devote<BR>one's self to, give one's self up to; to assume, maintain;<BR>to settle down or abide in: Caus. -लम्बयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to hang or rest or depend, suspend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्बन|समालंबनं
सम्-आलम्बन, अम्, n. the act of clinging to,<BR>laying hold of, leaning or resting on, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्बित
सम्-आलम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, suspended; clung to;<BR>rested on, supported, upheld, maintained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्बिन्|समालंबिन्
सम्-आलम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, clinging to, laying hold,<BR>&c.; (ई), m. a particular grass (= भूतृण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्ब्य
सम्-आलम्ब्य, ind. having suspended; having<BR>clung to; having maintained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालिख्
समालिख् सम्-आ-लिख्, cl. 6. P. -लिखति,<BR>&c., to scratch down, mark down, mark out, write<BR>down, delineate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालिङ्ग्
समालिङ्ग् सम्-आ-लिङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. A. -लिङ्गति,<BR>-ते, &c., to embrace closely, clasp or hold in a firm<BR>embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालिङ्ग्य
सम्-आलिङ्ग्य, ind. having embraced closely; hav-<BR>ing clasped firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालिप्
समालिप् सम्-आ-लिप्, cl. 6. P. A. -लिम्पति,<BR>-ते, -लेप्तुम्, to anoint all over; to anoint one's self<BR>(A.): Caus. -लेपयति, -यितुम्, to anoint or smear<BR>over, anoint well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालिप्त
सम्-आलिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well anointed or smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाली
समाली स-माली, f. (fr. 5. स + माला, q. v.),<BR>a collection of flowers, nosegay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालुड्
समालुड् सम्-आ-लुड्, Caus. -लोडयति, &c., to<BR>stir or mix together, stir up, agitate, disturb, confuse;<BR>to rummage, investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालोड्य
सम्-आलोड्य, ind. having stirred or mixed toge-<BR>ther; having rummaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालोक्
समालोक् सम्-आ-लोक्, cl. 1. A., 10. P. -लो-<BR>कते, -लोकयति, &c., to look at attentively, inspect,<BR>view, observe, regard, perceive, consider; to look<BR>about, look around; to acknowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालोक
सम्-आलोक, अस्, m. looking at or considering well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालोक्य
सम्-आलोक्य, ind. having looked at or observed<BR>thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालोच्
समालोच् सम्-आ-लोच्, cl. 1. A. -लोचते, &c.,<BR>to look at attentively, consider well or thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालोच्य
सम्-आलोच्य, ind. having looked at or considered<BR>well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावद्
समावद् सम्-आ-वद्, cl. 1. P. A. -वदति,<BR>-ते, &c., to speak with certainty, tell fully; to speak<BR>to, tell, say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावप्
समावप् सम्-आ-वप्, cl. 1. P. A. -वपति,<BR>-ते, &c., to sow or scatter together, mix up together,<BR>throw in together: Caus. -वापयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to be sown or scattered in together or at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावाप्य
सम्-आवाप्य, ind. (fr. the Caus.), having caused<BR>to be sown or scattered in together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावर्तन|समावर्तनं|समावर्त्तन|समावर्त्तनं
समावर्तन सम्-आवर्तन. See सम्-आ-वृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावलोक्य
समावलोक्य सम्-आवलोक्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>लोक् with अव, आ, and सम्), to be perceived or observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावस्
समावस् सम्-आ-वस्, cl. 1. P. -वसति, -वस्-<BR>तुम्, to dwell in, inhabit, settle in (with acc.); to<BR>encamp, lodge, halt; to resort to: Caus. -वासयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to dwell or settle or halt; to pitch<BR>a camp, encamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावास|समावासः
सम्-आवास, अस्, m. a dwelling-place, residence,<BR>abode, halting-place, encampment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावासित
सम्-आवासित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to dwell or settle,<BR>lodged, encamped; sojourned.<BR>—समावासित-क-<BR>टक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has pitched a camp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावह्
समावह् सम्-आ-वह्, cl. 1. P. A. -वहति,<BR>-ते, &c., to bear or bring together, bring or convey<BR>towards; to procure means of subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावाय|समावायः
समावाय सम्-आवाय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 5. इ with<BR>अव, आ, and सम्), association; integral or inseparable<BR>connection, (see सम्-अवाय); aggregation, totality;<BR>a multitude, number, heap, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविग्न
समाविग्न सम्-आविग्न, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>1. विज् with आ and सम्), agitated, terrified, trembling<BR>greatly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविद्
समाविद् सम्-आ-विद्, Caus. -वेदयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cause to know thoroughly, inform; to tell,<BR>announce, report fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेद्य
1. सम्-आवेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be told or commu-<BR>nicated fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेद्य
2. सम्-आवेद्य, ind. having announced or reported<BR>fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविश्
समाविश् सम्-आ-विश्, cl. 6. P. -विशति, -वेष्-<BR>टुम्, to enter together or at once, enter into, go<BR>towards, approach, betake one's self to; to enter<BR>thoroughly, take possession of, occupy, penetrate,<BR>pervade, engross, fill; to overcome, seize upon; to<BR>sit down, settle down, sit down in or on, take up an<BR>abode; to go or fall into any state or condition; to<BR>apply one's self to, undertake: Caus. -वेशयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cause to enter together or thoroughly; to<BR>cause to enter in, insert; to conduct, lead or bring<BR>into; to contain; to place or fix in or on, direct<BR>towards; to impose; to deliver over or consign to<BR>(with acc. and loc.); to cause to sit down, cause to<BR>settle down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविश्य
सम्-आविश्य, ind. having entered together, having<BR>entered thoroughly or entirely, having penetrated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविष्ट
सम्-आविष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, entered together, entered<BR>entirely or thoroughly, completely occupied or pos-<BR>sessed, penetrated, pervaded, filled, seized, overcome,<BR>absorbed, engrossed (as by any feeling, passion, &c.);<BR>possessed by (an evil spirit), possessed of, endowed<BR>with, well instructed in; seated, settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेश|समावेशः
सम्-आवेश, अस्, m. entering together, coming<BR>together, abiding together, meeting, association, co-<BR>inherence; entrance, penetration, complete possession;<BR>possession by evil spirits, &c.; affection, passion,<BR>emotion; (in grammar) applying together, employ-<BR>ing a term with a common applicability, common<BR>applicability of a term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेशित|समावेशितः
सम्-आवेशित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to enter together,<BR>brought together, caused to enter, inserted, made to<BR>penetrate, brought in or into; placed, fixed, absorbed,<BR>engrossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेश्य
सम्-आवेश्य, ind. having made to enter, having<BR>fixed or placed (in any place), having made to settle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृ
समावृ सम्-आ-वृ, cl. 5. P. A. -वृणोति, -वृ-<BR>णुते, &c., to cover all over, cover completely, en-<BR>velop, encompass, enclose, surround; to conceal,<BR>hide; to shut out, shut, close; to obstruct, impede,<BR>hinder, stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत|समावृतः
सम्-आवृत, अस्, आ, अम्, covered all over, com-<BR>pletely covered, enveloped, encompassed, surrounded,<BR>enclosed, beset, filled up; overspread; screened,<BR>veiled, concealed, hidden; protected, guarded; shut<BR>out, excluded, shut, closed, stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्य
सम्-आवृत्य, ind. having completely covered<BR>over, having enclosed or surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृज्
समावृज् सम्-आ-वृज्, cl. 1. P. -वर्जति, cl.<BR>7. P. A. -वृणक्ति, -वृङ्क्ते, &c., to bend or turn<BR>down; to bend or turn to one's own use, appropriate<BR>(Ved., A.): Caus. -वर्जयति, -यितुम्, to bend down,<BR>incline, lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावर्जित
सम्-आवर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, bent down, inclined,<BR>turned down, lowered.<BR>—समावर्जित-केतु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, one who has lowered his standard.<BR>—समावर्-<BR>जित-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having the eyes bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्
समावृत् सम्-आ-वृत्, cl. 1. A. -वर्तते, -वर्-<BR>तितुम्, to turn or advance towards, approach, come;<BR>to come together, assemble; to turn back, come<BR>back, return (said especially of a Brahma-cārin or<BR>religious student who returns home after completing<BR>his studies with a preceptor); to turn out well, suc-<BR>ceed; to come to an end, be concluded or completed:<BR>Caus. -वर्तयति, -यितुम्, to cause to turn back,<BR>cause to return home, dismiss; to put an end to,<BR>annihilate, (Sāy. सम्-आवर्तयन्ति = नाशयन्ति,<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 79, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावर्तन|समावर्तनं|समावर्त्तन|समावर्त्तनं
सम्-आवर्तन, अम्, n. the act of turning back,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">Page1075-c+ 75</a>]<BR>returning; a pupil's return home after finishing his<BR>religious studies; the ceremony performed on the<BR>above occasion, (see संस्-कार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्त|समावृत्तः
सम्-आवृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, come together, assem-<BR>bled, returned; completed, ended, concluded; (अस्),<BR>m. a pupil who has returned home after completing<BR>his studies.<BR>—समावृत्त-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has completed a religious vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्तक|समावृत्तकः
सम्-आवृत्तक, अस्, m. a pupil who has returned<BR>home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्ति|समावृत्तिः
सम्-आवृत्ति, इस्, f. turning back, returning, return;<BR>completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावे
समावे सम्-आ-वे, cl. 1. P. A. -वयति, -ते,<BR>&c., Ved. to weave together, interweave; to string<BR>together (Ved., A.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाव्यध्
समाव्यध् सम्-आ-व्यध्, cl. 4. P. -विध्यति,<BR>-व्यद्धुम्, to move or shake about, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविद्ध
सम्-आविद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken about, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाशंस्
समाशंस् सम्-आ-शंस्, cl. 1. A. -शंसते, &c.,<BR>to wish for, long for, hope for, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाशङ्कित
समाशङ्कित सम्-आशङ्कित, अस्, आ, अम् [cf.<BR>आ-शङ्क्], very fearful or apprehensive; doubted,<BR>doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रि
समाश्रि सम्-आ-श्रि, cl. 1. P. A. -श्रयति,<BR>-ते, -श्रयितुम्, to go to or have recourse to together<BR>(especially for protection), fly to for refuge, seek<BR>refuge with, resort to, approach, enter, occupy; to<BR>attain to, obtain, assume; to seek, follow, practise;<BR>to rest on, depend on, lean on, trust to, confide in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रय|समाश्रयः
सम्-आश्रय, अस्, m. going together to any one<BR>for support or shelter, seeking protection; support,<BR>protection; a refuge, place of refuge, place of resort<BR>or shelter, resting-place, dwelling-place, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रित|समाश्रितः
सम्-आश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, fled to for refuge, resorted<BR>to, protected, defended, cherished; going to for<BR>protection, resorting to; rested on; depending on,<BR>supported by; assuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रित्य
सम्-आश्रित्य, ind. having resorted to for protection<BR>or support; having followed or practised or engaged<BR>in; resting on, depending upon, trusting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रु
समाश्रु सम्-आ-श्रु, cl. 5. P. A. -शृणोति,<BR>-शृणुते, &c., to promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्लिष्
समाश्लिष् सम्-आ-श्लिष्, cl. 4. P. -श्लिष्यति,<BR>-श्लेष्टुम्, to embrace closely or firmly, to join<BR>together, bring near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्लिष्ट
सम्-आश्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, closely embraced, closely<BR>or firmly attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्लिष्य
सम्-आश्लिष्य, ind. having closely embraced, hav-<BR>ing intwined together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्लेष|समाश्लेषः
सम्-आश्लेष, अस्, m. a close or firm embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वस्
समाश्वस् सम्-आ-श्वस्, cl. 2. P. -श्वसिति (also<BR>cl. 1. P. -श्वसति, see rt. 1. श्वस्), &c., to breathe<BR>again, take or recover breath, revive, recover, take<BR>courage, (समाश्वसिहि, 2nd sing. Impv. take courage),<BR>regain confidence; to trust or confide in (with loc.):<BR>Caus. -श्वासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to revive, re-<BR>animate, encourage, refresh, cheer, comfort, console,<BR>calm, make confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वस्त
सम्-आश्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, recovered, revived, re-<BR>animated, encouraged, comforted, consoled; trusting,<BR>confiding, full of confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वस्य
सम्-आश्वस्य, ind. having taken confidence, gain-<BR>ing courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वास|समाश्वासः
सम्-आश्वास, अस्, m. recovering breath, relief,<BR>comfort, consolation, encouragement; trust, belief,<BR>confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वासन|समाश्वासनं
सम्-आश्वासन, अम्, n. the act of causing to take<BR>breath, encouraging, reviving, cheering, comforting,<BR>consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वासित
सम्-आश्वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, reanimated, revived,<BR>refreshed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वास्य
सम्-आश्वास्य, ind. having reanimated or encou-<BR>raged or refreshed, having cheered or comforted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्
समास् 1. समास्, m. (doubtful, except as<BR>nom. pl. of 1. समा, q. v.), a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्
समास् 2. सम्-आस्, cl. 2. A. -आस्ते, &c. (see<BR>rt. 4. आस्), to sit together; to sit along with, assemble<BR>or meet around (with acc. or with inst.); to sit toge-<BR>ther in council, hold a council; to be a match for,<BR>cope with (with acc.); to sit down, be seated; to<BR>join in adhering to or following; to adhere to,<BR>observe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास|समासः
2. सम्-आस, अस्, m. (in the Nyāya phil.) proper abid-<BR>ing or connection. (For 1. see under 2. सम्-अस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासीन
सम्-आसीन, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting together, seated<BR>together, sitting down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्या
सम्-आस्या, f. (doubtful), sitting together, colloquy,<BR>interview.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासञ्ज्|समासंज्
समासञ्ज् सम्-आ-सञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. -सजति, -सज्-<BR>जति, &c. (see rt. 2. सञ्ज्), to fasten or stick toge-<BR>ther, to join or attach or fix to; to fix or place on,<BR>impose, place down on, resign or deliver over to<BR>(with loc.): Pass. -सज्यते, -सज्जते, to cling or<BR>adhere closely together, to cling or stick to, become<BR>attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्त|समासक्तः
सम्-आसक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fastened or joined toge-<BR>ther, attached, united, combined, comprehended;<BR>attached to, fixed on (with loc.); reached, attained;<BR>affected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्ति|समासक्तिः
सम्-आसक्ति, इस्, f. sticking or adhering closely<BR>together, union; attachment, affection; compre-<BR>hension, inclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासङ्ग|समासंगः
सम्-आसङ्ग, अस्, m. adhering together, attach-<BR>ment, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासजत्
सम्-आसजत् or (according to some) सम्-आसज्जत्,<BR>अन्, अन्ती, अत्, joining or connecting with; attaching,<BR>adhering to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासज्य
सम्-आसज्य, ind. having attached together, having<BR>fixed or placed on, having delivered over or con-<BR>signed to (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासञ्जन|समासंजन|समासंजनं|समासञ्जनं
सम्-आसञ्जन, अम्, n. (according to some also<BR>written सम्-आसज्जन), the act of attaching or unit-<BR>ing together, joining, union; connection, combina-<BR>tion, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासद्
समासद् सम्-आ-सद्, cl. 1. 10. P. -सीदति,<BR>सादयति, &c. (see rt. 1. सद्), to go to or approach<BR>together, go towards; to go against, encounter, assail,<BR>attack; to attain, obtain, meet with, find, recover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासन्न|समासन्नं
सम्-आसन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, approached, attained,<BR>obtained; met with, found; near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासादन|समासादनं
सम्-आसादन, अम्, n. the act of approaching,<BR>meeting with, attaining, obtaining, finding; effecting,<BR>accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासादित|समासादितः
सम्-आसादित, अस्, आ, अम्, approached; assailed,<BR>encountered; met with, attained, obtained; accom-<BR>plished, effected, finished, performed, done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासाद्य|समासाद्यं
1. सम्-आसाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, attainable, obtainable,<BR>procurable, to be effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासाद्य|समासाद्यं
2. सम्-आसाद्य, ind. having encountered; having<BR>met with or obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासृज्
समासृज् सम्-आ-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति,<BR>-स्रष्टुम्, to let go or abandon completely, resign,<BR>deliver over, consign; to place or put down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासर्जन|समासर्जनं
सम्-आसर्जन, अम्, n. the act of resigning or<BR>abandoning completely, delivering over, abandon-<BR>ment, consignment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासृज्य
सम्-आसृज्य, ind. having resigned or consigned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासृष्ट
सम्-आसृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, abandoned, delivered<BR>over, made over, consigned, given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेव्
समासेव् सम्-आ-सेव्, cl. 1. A. -सेवते, &c.,<BR>to practise or perform assiduously; to pursue, follow,<BR>addict one's self to; to enjoy; to employ; to serve,<BR>honour, gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेवन
सम्-आसेवन, अम्, n. the act of practising, follow-<BR>ing, addicting one's self to, employing, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेवित
सम्-आसेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, practised, followed, em-<BR>ployed, served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेव्य
सम्-आसेव्य, ind. having practised, having em-<BR>ployed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्कन्द्
समास्कन्द् सम्-आ-स्कन्द्, cl. 1. P. -स्कन्दति,<BR>-स्कन्तुम्, to assail, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्तृ
समास्तृ सम्-आ-स्तृ, cl. 5. or सम्-आ-स्तॄ, cl.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">Page1076-b+ 77</a>]<BR>9. P. A. -स्तृणोति, -स्तृणुते, -स्तृणाति, -स्तृणीते, &c.,<BR>to spread entirely over, cover over; to extinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्था
समास्था सम्-आ-स्था, cl. 1. P. A. -तिष्ठति,<BR>-ते, -स्थातुम्, to undergo, undertake, practise, per-<BR>form, engage in; to employ, use, apply, exert:<BR>Caus. -स्थापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be performed<BR>or practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्थ
सम्-आस्थ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. सम् + आस्था), being<BR>in a prosperous condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्थाप्य
सम्-आस्थाप्य, ind. having caused to be performed;<BR>having duly observed, paying proper regard to; having<BR>placed one's self on a seat, having sat down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्थाय
सम्-आस्थाय, ind. having practised or engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्थित
सम्-आस्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, undergone, engaged in,<BR>practised; having recourse to; seated together,<BR>seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहन्
समाहन् सम्-आ-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -हन्-<BR>तुम्, to strike together; to unite, join; to strike<BR>violently, strike down completely, strike, beat, slay,<BR>kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघात|समाघातः
सम्-आघात, अस्, m. striking together, uniting;<BR>striking down, beating, killing; conflict, war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहत
सम्-आहत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck together; com-<BR>pletely struck down, well beaten, wounded, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहत्य
सम्-आहत्य, ind. having struck down; having<BR>struck or killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहित|समाहितः
समाहित सम्-आहित. See under सम्-आ-धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहूत
समाहूत सम्-आहूत, सम्-आहूय. See below<BR>under सम्-आ-ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृ
समाहृ सम्-आ-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते,<BR>-हर्तुम्, to bring together, combine, collect, accu-<BR>mulate, assemble, compile; to draw together, con-<BR>tract, abridge; to crush together, destroy, annihilate;<BR>to bring back, restore; to offer up, offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहरण|समाहरणं
सम्-आहरण, अम्, n. the act of bringing toge-<BR>ther, collecting, collection, accumulation, uniting,<BR>combination, composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहरत्
सम्-आहरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bringing together,<BR>collecting, contracting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहर्तृ
सम्-आहर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who collects toge-<BR>ther or accumulates, a collector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहार|समाहारः
सम्-आहार, अस्, m. collection, accumulation, ag-<BR>gregation, assemblage, union by association; con-<BR>traction, abridgement; composition of words (in<BR>grammar); conjunction of words or sentences (as by<BR>the particle ‘and’); epithet of a particular subdivision<BR>of Dvandva and Dvigu compounds, (applied to the<BR>former when the last part of the compound is in<BR>the neuter gender, e. g. अहि-नकुलम्, the snake<BR>and the ichneumon; to the latter when the com-<BR>pound expresses an aggregate, e. g. त्रि-लोकी, the<BR>aggregate of three worlds); a combination of two<BR>letters of the alphabet into a syllable (= प्रत्य्-<BR>आहार, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृत|समाहृतः
सम्-आहृत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought together, col-<BR>lected, accumulated, assembled, combined, compiled;<BR>abundant, much; contracted, abridged; accepted,<BR>received, taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृति|समाहृतिः
सम्-आहृति, इस्, f. collection, compilation, abridge-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वे
समाह्वे सम्-आ-ह्वे, cl. 1. P. A. -ह्वयति,<BR>-ते, -ह्वातुम्, to call together, convoke; to call<BR>upon, invoke, summon, challenge, provoke to battle;<BR>to invite; to call, name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजुहूषमाण
सम्-आजुहूषमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, challenging<BR>(e. g. समराय, to battle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहूत
सम्-आहूत, अस्, आ, अम्, collected together, con-<BR>voked, invited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहूय
सम्-आहूय, ind. having called together, having<BR>summoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्व|समाह्वः
सम्-आह्व, अस्, ई, m. f. calling out, mutual calling,<BR>challenge; defiance; (आ), f. appellation, name; a<BR>kind of plant (= गो-जिह्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वय|समाह्वयः
सम्-आह्वय, अस्, m. calling out, challenging;<BR>single combat, war, battle; setting animals to fight<BR>for sport, a match with fighting-cocks, &c., betting<BR>or gambling with living creatures (as distinguished<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">Page1076-c+ 80</a>]<BR>from gaming with dice or other inanimate objects,<BR>see द्यूत); an appellation, name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वान|समाह्वानं
सम्-आह्वान, अम्, n. calling together, calling,<BR>convoking, summoning, provocation, challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समि
समि 1. सम्-इ (see rt. 5. इ), cl. 2. P. -एति,<BR>-एतुम्, to go or come together, meet together,<BR>assemble; to meet or be united with (with acc. or<BR>inst. or dat.); to meet any one (inst.) in hostile<BR>encounter; to come together or be united sexually;<BR>to be joined or united together (generally); to go<BR>or come to, arrive at, approach, visit, enter, reach,<BR>attain; to enter upon, commence; to lead to; to<BR>agree with, harmonize with (with inst.): Pass. -ईयते,<BR>to be united; to be resorted to or frequented by; to<BR>be agreed upon: Intens., Ved. -ईयते, to go repeat-<BR>edly, traverse frequently; to present one's self, be<BR>manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समय|समयः
सम्-अय, अस्, m. coming together, convention,<BR>coming to a mutual understanding, agreement, com-<BR>pact, covenant, treaty, contract, bargain, engage-<BR>ment, appointment; stipulation, condition; oath;<BR>concurrence of circumstances, juncture, fit or proper<BR>time, right moment, opportunity, occasion, season, time,<BR>emergency, exigency; leisure; conventional rule or<BR>usage, established custom, law, rule, regulation, regu-<BR>lar observance, religious obligation; order, direction,<BR>precept, instruction, affirmation, declaration; sign,<BR>hint, indication; coming to an end, conclusion, ter-<BR>mination; limit, boundary; demonstrated conclusion;<BR>end of trouble or distress; success, prosperity; poetī-<BR>cal idiom or conventionality (in rhetoric); (एन),<BR>ind. according to agreement, on condition, con-<BR>ditionally.<BR>—समय-कार, अस्, m. making an<BR>agreement or appointment or engagement, fixing a<BR>time.<BR>—समय-क्रिया, f. making an agreement or<BR>compact.<BR>—समय-परिरक्षण, अम्, n. the<BR>observance of a compact or agreement.<BR>—समय-<BR>प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—समय-प्र-<BR>दीप, अस्, m., N. of a work by Śrī-datta.<BR>—समय-<BR>भेद, अस्, m. breaking an agreement.<BR>—समय-<BR>भेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, a promise-breaker, breaking an<BR>agreement, violating an engagement.<BR>—समय-<BR>व्यभिचार, अस्, m. transgression or violation of a<BR>compact, breaking an agreement.<BR>—समय-व्य-<BR>भिचारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, transgressing a compact, violating<BR>an engagement.<BR>—समय-सेतु-वारित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>restrained by the barrier of the rules of decorum.<BR>—समयाचार (˚य-आच्˚), अस्, m. conventional<BR>practice or usage; [cf. सामयाचारिक.]<BR>—समया-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—समया-<BR>ध्युषित (˚य-अध्˚), अम्, n. a time at which<BR>neither stars nor sun are visible.<BR>—समयानुवर्तिन्<BR>(˚य-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, following established rules, ob-<BR>servant of duties.<BR>—समयानुसारेण (˚य-अन्˚),<BR>ind. according to the occasion, suitably to the time<BR>or season.<BR>—समयोचित (˚य-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>suited to the occasion or time, suitable to an emer-<BR>gency, seasonable, timely, opportune; (अम्), ind.<BR>suitably to the occasion, as the occasion demands.<BR>—समयोद्द्योत (˚य-उद्˚), N. of a work by<BR>Hemādri.<BR>—समयोल्लङ्घित-त्व (˚य-उल्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the overleaping or violating of contracts or agree-<BR>ments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समया
समया, ind. at a fixed or appointed time; duly,<BR>seasonably, in due time or season; (in the following<BR>senses probably an old inst. of सम), within, in<BR>the middle, in the midst, betwixt, between, within;<BR>near (with acc.); [cf. Gr. ὁμῇ, ὁμοῦ, ὁμῶς; Lat.<BR>simul.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाय|समायः
सम्-आय, अस्, m. coming towards, arriving at,<BR>arrival, visiting, a visit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित्
सम्-इत्, त्, f. conflict, war, battle.<BR>—समित्-पाणि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित
सम्-इत, अस्, आ, अम्, come together, met; col-<BR>lected, assembled; united with, conjoined, connected;<BR>coming into contact, contiguous, parallel; promised,<BR>agreed, assented to; finished, completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिति|समितिः
1. सम्-इति, इस्, f. coming together, meeting, assem-<BR>bling, union, association; Association or Society (per-<BR>sonified as a daughter of Prajā-pati); an assembly,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">Page1077-a+ 75</a>]<BR>company; encounter, hostile meeting, war, battle,<BR>(enumerated among the सङ्ग्राम-नामानि in<BR>Naigh. II. 17); sameness, likeness, equality, (in<BR>this and the following sense probably to be con-<BR>nected with 1. सम); moderation, (एषण-स-<BR>मिति, moderation in desires); one of the five Jaina<BR>rules of life, irreproachable conduct as an ascetic [cf.<BR>भाषा-स्˚].<BR>—समितिञ्-जय, अस्, आ, अम्, conquering<BR>or eminent in an assembly.<BR>—समिति-शोभन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, conspicuous in fight or battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिथ|समिथः
सम्-इथ, अस्, अम्, m. n. war, battle (= सङ्-<BR>ग्राम, Naigh. II. 17); fire; offering oblations<BR>with fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीयमान
2. सम्-ईयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being come together,<BR>being united with; being treated equally, (in this<BR>sense probably for 1. समीयमान, see p. 1067.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीयिवस्
सम्-ईयिवस्, आन्, -युषी, अत्, one who has met or<BR>encountered; one who has gone to or arrived at<BR>or resorted to; one who has attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समि
समि 2. समि, apparently an old loc. con-<BR>nected with 2. सम्. See सम्य्-अञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिक|समिकं
समिक समिक, अम्, n. (see समीक), a pike,<BR>javelin, dart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिङ्ग्
समिङ्ग् सम्-इङ्ग्, Caus. -इङ्गयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Ved. to cause to move or throb, agitate, shake about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिता
समिता समिता, f. [cf. समीद], wheat-flour;<BR>[cf. Gr. σεμίδαλις; Lat. simila, similago.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिति|समितिः
समिति 2. सम्-इति, ind. a sacred verse be-<BR>ginning with सम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित्र
समित्र स-मित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by a<BR>friend, along with a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिनक्ष्
समिनक्ष् सम्-इनक्ष् (see इनक्ष्), -इनक्-<BR>षति, Ved. to wish to obtain, strive to reach, be<BR>desirous of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्ध्|समिंध्
समिन्ध् सम्-इन्ध्, cl. 7. A. -इन्द्धे or<BR>-इन्धे, &c., to light up, kindle, ignite; to glorify;<BR>to kindle (figuratively), inflame, excite; to take<BR>fire: Pass. -इध्यते, to be kindled, take fire, break<BR>out into flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिद्ध|समिद्धः
सम्-इद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, lighted up, kindled, ignited,<BR>set alight, set on fire.<BR>—समिद्ध-दर्प, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, inflamed with pride.<BR>—समिद्ध-शरण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, (a town &c.) which has its houses set on<BR>fire.<BR>—समिद्ध-होम, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>oblation kindled.<BR>—समिद्धार्चिस् (˚ध-अर्˚), इस्,<BR>n. a blazing flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध्
सम्-इध्, त्, f. fuel, wood, a log of wood, fire-<BR>wood, grass &c. employed as fuel, (seven Samidhs,<BR>or sometimes three times seven, are mentioned, as<BR>well as seven Yonis, seven flames, &c.); a division<BR>of a stanza, (Ved., Sāy. = पाद.)<BR>—समिद्-आधान,<BR>अम्, n. the placing on of wood or fuel (for the obla-<BR>tion to fire).<BR>—समिद्-धोम, अस्, m. (i. e. समिध्-<BR>होम), an oblation of fuel (to fire).<BR>—समिद्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having fuel, supplied with fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध|समिधः
सम्-इध, अस्, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिधान
सम्-इधान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. kindled, lighted<BR>(= सम्-इध्यमान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध्य
1. सम्-इध्य, ind. having kindled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध्य
2. समिध्य, Nom. P. समिध्यति, &c., to wish<BR>for fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध्यमान
सम्-इध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being kindled or<BR>ignited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्धन|समिंधनं|समिन्धनं
सम्-इन्धन, अम्, n. the act of kindling; fuel,<BR>fire-wood; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्धान
सम्-इन्धान, अस्, आ, अम्, kindling, inflaming;<BR>augmenting, prospering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समेद्धृ
सम्-एद्धृ, धा, m., Ved. one who kindles,<BR>kindling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्व्
समिन्व् सम्-इन्व्, cl. 6. P. -इन्वति, -इन्वितुम्,<BR>Ved. to impart, bestow; to spread through, (Sāy.<BR>समिन्वतु = व्याप्नोतु = प्रापयतु, Ṛg-veda IV.<BR>53, 7); to restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिर|समिरः
समिर सम्-इर, अस्, m. = सम्-ईर, wind,<BR>air, (see सम्-ईर्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिष्ट
समिष्ट सम्-इष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. सं-यज्),<BR>sacrificed together, sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक|समीकं
समीक समीक, अम्, n. (perhaps connected<BR>with सम्य्-अञ्च्), war, battle, (in Naigh. II. 17. स-<BR>मीके is enumerated among the सङ्ग्राम-नामानि);<BR>a pike, dart; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीकरण|समीकरणं
समीकरण समी-करण, समी-कृ, &c. See<BR>p. 1067, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष्
समीक्ष् सम्-ईक्ष्, cl. 1. A. -ईक्षते, -ईक्षि-<BR>तुम्, to look at or inspect thoroughly, investigate<BR>closely, view, perceive, see; to look about for, look<BR>around; search for; to look towards, look to; to<BR>consider well, inquire into, investigate, examine,<BR>contemplate, reflect upon: Caus. P. A. -ईक्षयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to cause to look at or perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष|समीक्षं|समीक्षः
सम्-ईक्ष, अम्, n. complete investigation; the<BR>Sāṅkhya system of philosophy; (आ), f. thorough or<BR>close inspection; looking well at, consideration, (अ-<BR>समीक्षम्, inconsiderately); investigation, search;<BR>the Mīmāṃsā system of philosophy or any work<BR>examining Vedic ritual and explaining the modes of<BR>sacrifice; understanding, intellect; effort; essential<BR>nature or truth (= तत्त्व, q. v.); any essential princi-<BR>ple (according to the Sāṅkhya system of philosophy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्षण|समीक्षणं
सम्-ईक्षण, अम्, n. the act of looking at or<BR>inspecting thoroughly; looking about for, search,<BR>close investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्षमाण
सम्-ईक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, looking at or con-<BR>sidering attentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्षित
सम्-ईक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, well looked at; per-<BR>ceived, considered, investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष्य
1. सम्-ईक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be looked at or<BR>considered; to be investigated (in phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष्य
2. सम्-ईक्ष्य, ind. having well looked at or<BR>considered, having reflected.<BR>—समीक्ष्य-कारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, acting after due deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष्यमाण
सम्-ईक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being looked at<BR>or well considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीच|समीचः
समीच समीच, अस्, m. (fr. सम्य्-अञ्च्), the<BR>ocean; (ई), f. a female deer, doe; praise, eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचक|समीचकः
समीचक, अस्, m. sexual union, copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचीन|समीचीनं
समीचीन. See under सम्य्-अञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीद|समीदः
समीद समीद, अस्, m. fine wheat-flour;<BR>[cf. समिता.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीन|समीनः
समीन समीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. समा), yearly,<BR>annual, relating to a year; hired for a year; after a<BR>year, a year hence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीनिका
समीनिका, f. a cow calving every year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीप|समीपः
समीप समीप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. सम्-आप्), near,<BR>contiguous, proximate, adjacent, close by, at hand;<BR>(अम्), n. proximity, vicinity; (ए), ind. in the<BR>vicinity, in the presence of, towards.<BR>—समीप-ग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, going near.<BR>—समीप-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>produced near, growing near.<BR>—समीप-तस्, ind. in<BR>the vicinity of, in the presence of, near, before.<BR>—समीप-ता, f. or समीप-त्व, अम्, n. nearness,<BR>contiguity, proximity.<BR>—समीप-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>or समीप-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being or situated near,<BR>living near, adjoining, neighbouring.<BR>—समीपोप-<BR>गत (˚प-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, approached near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीभू
समीभू समी-भू, &c. See p. 1067, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीय|समीयः
समीय समीय, &c. See p. 1067.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीयिवस्
समीयिवस् सम्-ईयिवस्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीर्
समीर् सम्-ईर्, Caus. P. A. -ईरयति, -ते,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to move about, agitate; to move,<BR>stir up, excite, rouse; to lift up, raise up, revive; to<BR>send forth, emit, utter (a sound &c.); to throw,<BR>cast; to bring about, accomplish; to confer, bestow,<BR>endow with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीर|समीरः
सम्-ईर, अस्, m. air, wind; the Samī tree; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीरण|समीरणः
सम्-ईरण, अस्, m. breeze, wind, air; the breath;<BR>a traveller; the plant Maruvaka; (अम्), n. the act<BR>of sending forth or emitting, throwing.<BR>—समीरण-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">Page1077-c+ 75</a>]<BR>सहाय, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by the wind,<BR>fanned by the breeze (as a forest fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीरित
सम्-ईरित, अस्, आ, अम्, stirred, moved, roused,<BR>sent forth, emitted, uttered; cast, tossed, thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीर्ण
सम्-ईर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, moved about, moved, &c.;<BR>[cf. सम्-ऋ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीष्
समीष् सम्-ईष्, cl. 1. A. -ईषते, Ved. to<BR>become extended or lengthened out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीषित
सम्-ईषित, अस्, आ, अम्, extended, stretched out,<BR>lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीह्
समीह् सम्-ईह्, cl. 1. A. -ईहते, -ईहितुम्, to<BR>strive after (with acc.), endeavour to gain, long after,<BR>desire to accomplish, wish for, desire, hope for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीहा
सम्-ईहा, f. striving after, longing for, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीहित
सम्-ईहित, अस्, आ, अम्, longed or wished for,<BR>desired; undertaken; (अम्), n. great effort to obtain<BR>anything, desire, longing, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुक्ष्
समुक्ष् 1. सम्-उक्ष् (see rt. 1. उक्ष्), cl. 6. P.<BR>-उक्षति, -उक्षितुम्, to sprinkle well or thoroughly,<BR>wet; to besprinkle, strew, scatter or pour over, pour<BR>out; to confer, endow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुक्षण|समुक्षणं
सम्-उक्षण, अम्, n. the act of sprinkling or<BR>pouring over, shedding, effusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुक्षित
1. सम्-उक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, besprinkled, scattered,<BR>strewed, covered; poured out, effused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुक्ष्
समुक्ष् 2. सम्-उक्ष्. See rt. 2. उक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुक्षित
1. सम्-उक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. strengthened,<BR>augmented, exalted, (Sāy. = वर्धित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुख|समुखः
समुख स-मुख, अस्, आ, अम्, talkative, lo-<BR>quacious, eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्
समुच् सम्-उच्, cl. 4. P. -उच्यति (Perf.<BR>-उवोच), -उचितुम्, Ved. to delight in (with inst.);<BR>to like to combine or blend with, (Sāy. = सम्-उच्यसि<BR>= सङ्गच्छसि, Ṛg-veda V. 81, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुचित|समुचितः
सम्-उचित, अस्, आ, अम्, liked; well suited, suit-<BR>able, fit, right, proper; appropriate, worthy; accus-<BR>tomed, used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चर्
समुच्चर् सम्-उच्-चर् (-उद्-चर्), cl. 1. P. -च-<BR>रति, -चरितुम्, to go out together; to go up, be<BR>borne upwards, ascend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चर|समुच्चरः
सम्-उच्चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going or coming forth<BR>together; going upwards, ascending, flying upwards;<BR>traversing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चरत्
सम्-उच्चरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going or coming out<BR>together; rising upwards together, ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चल्
समुच्चल् सम्-उच्-चल् (-उद्-चल्), cl. 1. P. -च-<BR>लति, -चलितुम्, to set out together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चि
समुच्चि सम्-उच्-चि (-उद्-चि), cl. 5. P. A. -चि-<BR>नोति, -चिनुते, -चेतुम्, to heap up together, aggregate,<BR>collect together, gather, collect; to arrange, array in<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चय|समुच्चयः
सम्-उच्चय, अस्, m. collection, assemblage, ag-<BR>gregation, accumulation, multitude, mass, aggregate;<BR>conjunction of words or sentences (as by the particle<BR>‘and,’ &c., see सम्-आहार); the gathering together<BR>of two or more things independent of each other (but<BR>associated in idea with reference to some common<BR>action).<BR>—समुच्चयालङ्कार (˚य-अल्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>rhetorical ornament of conjunction, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चयित्वा
सम्-उच्चयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having col-<BR>lected, having picked up and placed in a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चित
सम्-उच्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, collected or aggregated<BR>together, regularly arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चित्य
सम्-उच्चित्य, ind. having collected or gathered<BR>together, having arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चीय
सम्-उच्चीय (anom. ind. part.), having arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चीयमान
सम्-उच्चीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being aggregated<BR>or conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छद्
समुच्छद् सम्-उच्-छद् (-उद्-छद्), cl. 10. P.<BR>-छादयति, -यितुम्, to uncover (the body &c.),<BR>put off (a garment), undress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छिद्
