समुत्पिञ्जलक|समुत्पिञ्जलकः
सम्-उत्पिञ्जलक, अस्, m. excessive confusion or<BR>disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पिपतिषु
समुत्पिपतिषु सम्-उत्पिपतिषु. See सम्-<BR>उत्-पत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पिष्
समुत्पिष् सम्-उत्पिष्, cl. 7. P. -पिनष्टि, &c.,<BR>to crush or squeeze together; to grind to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पिष्ट
सम्-उत्पिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, crushed or squeezed<BR>together; greatly crushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पीडन
समुत्पीडन सम्-उत्पीडन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. पीड्<BR>with उद् and सम्), the act of pressing together, com-<BR>pression, pressing; great pressure or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पॄ
समुत्पॄ सम्-उत्-पॄ, Caus. -पारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Ved. to spread out, stretch out, stretch forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्प्लु
समुत्प्लु सम्-उत्-प्लु (-उद्-प्˚), cl. 1. A. -प्ल-<BR>वते, -प्लोतुम्, to jump or leap up together, spring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्प्लुत्य
सम्-उत्प्लुत्य, ind. having jumped or leaped up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सद्
समुत्सद् सम्-उत्-सद्, Caus. P. -सादयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to destroy utterly, overturn, overthrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सव|समुत्सवः
समुत्सव सम्-उत्सव, अस्, m. a great festival<BR>or festivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सह्
समुत्सह् सम्-उत्-सह्, Caus. P. -साहयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to encourage or exhort together, animate,<BR>incite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्साह्य
सम्-उत्साह्य, ind. having encouraged or exhorted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सुक|समुत्सुकः
समुत्सुक सम्-उत्सुक, अस्, आ, अम्, very un-<BR>easy or anxious, very agitated, anxiously desirous,<BR>longing for (an absent person), eager for, fond of,<BR>attached to; regretting, missing, grieving for, sor-<BR>rowful.<BR>—समुत्सुक-त्व, अम्, n. sorrow, regret,<BR>longing desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सुकय
सम्-उत्सुकय, Nom. P. -उत्सुकयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to long for, cause to be fond of, make<BR>attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सृ
समुत्सृ सम्-उत्-सृ (-उद्-सृ), Caus. P. -सार-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">Page1079-a+ 79</a>]<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to move away, drive away;<BR>to give away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सारण|समुत्सारणं
सम्-उत्सारण, अम्, n. the act of expelling or<BR>driving to a distance, driving away; pursuing, hunt-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सृज्
समुत्सृज् सम्-उत्-सृज् (-उद्-स्˚), cl. 6. P. -सृ-<BR>जति, -स्रष्टुम्, to pour out or shed forth together,<BR>pour out, shed; to send forth, give forth, cast forth,<BR>let go, let loose, dismiss; to leave or abandon or lay<BR>aside completely; to put off; to lose; to place or<BR>put down, throw forth or away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सर्ग|समुत्सर्गः
सम्-उत्सर्ग, अस्, m. pouring out or shedding<BR>forth together, casting or giving forth, giving away;<BR>leaving, abandoning; evacuation (of the bowels or<BR>bladder), feculent discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सृजत्
सम्-उत्सृजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, letting loose, letting go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सृज्य
सम्-उत्सृज्य, ind. having wholly abandoned or<BR>given up, having cast away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सृष्ट
सम्-उत्सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, altogether poured or<BR>shed forth, cast forth, given away; let loose, wholly<BR>given up or abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सृप्
समुत्सृप् सम्-उत्-सृप् (-उद्-स्˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-सर्पति, &c., to glide or soar upwards together; to<BR>go upwards, ascend, rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सेध|समुत्सेधः
समुत्सेध सम्-उत्सेध, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. सिध्<BR>with उद् and सम्), elevation, height; swelling up,<BR>intumescence, fatness, thickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्
समुद् सम्-उद् or सम्-उन्द्, cl. 7. P. -उनत्ति,<BR>-उन्दितुम्, to moisten thoroughly, sprinkle all over,<BR>water, wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्य
2. सम्-उद्य, ind. (for 1. see p. 1037, col. 1),<BR>having sprinkled all over, having moistened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्र|समुद्रः
1. सम्-उद्र, अस्, m. [cf. उद्र, अन्-उद्र], the<BR>waters above the firmament, the aerial ocean or sky<BR>(Ved.; in Naigh. 1. 3. enumerated among the अन्-<BR>तरिक्ष-नामानि); a collection of water, sea, ocean,<BR>(seven seas are enumerated in Viṣṇu-Purāṇa II. 4,<BR>viz. the sea of Lavaṇa, ‘salt-water;’ Ikṣu, ‘sugar-<BR>cane juice or syrup;’ Surā, ‘wine;’ Ghṛta, ‘clarified<BR>butter;’ Dadhi, ‘curds;’ Dugdha, ‘milk;’ Jala,<BR>‘fresh water’); a symbolical expression for the num-<BR>ber four (the number of oceans being only four,<BR>according to one reckoning); the Ocean (personified<BR>and represented as the king of rivers); epithet of<BR>Śiva; a kind of metre; N. of a place; of a work;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. having a collection of water,<BR>watery, flowing; (आ), f. the plant called zedoary<BR>(= सटी); the Śamī tree.<BR>—समुद्र-कफ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘sea-foam,’ cuttle-fish bone.<BR>—समुद्र-कान्ता,<BR>f. ‘sea-beloved,’ a river.<BR>—समुद्र-कुक्षि, इस्, f.<BR>the shore of the ocean.<BR>—समुद्र-ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ocean-going, sea-faring; flowing towards the ocean;<BR>(अस्), m. a sea-farer, seaman; sea-trader; (आ), f. a<BR>river.<BR>—समुद्र-गमन, अम्, n. going or voyag-<BR>ing by sea; sea-roving.<BR>—समुद्र-गामिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, sea-going, sea-faring.<BR>—समुद्र-गुप्त, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king of the Gupta dynasty.<BR>—समुद्र-<BR>गृह, अम्, n. a sort of summer-house built in the<BR>midst of water (= जल-यन्त्र-गृह, q. v.).<BR>—स-<BR>मुद्र-चुलुक, अस्, m. ‘holding a mouthful of the<BR>ocean,’ epithet of the sage Agastya (fabled to have<BR>drunk up the ocean).<BR>—समुद्र-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sea-born, produced in the sea.<BR>—समुद्र-तट, अम्,<BR>n. the sea-coast.<BR>—समुद्र-तीर, अम्, n. the sea-<BR>shore.<BR>—समुद्र-दयिता, f. ‘sea-beloved,’ a river.<BR>—समुद्र-नवनीत, अम्, n. ‘ocean-butter,’ nectar<BR>or ambrosia (= अ-मृत); the moon (as produced<BR>or recovered at the churning of the ocean).<BR>—स-<BR>मुद्र-नेमि, इस्, इस्, इ, encircled or surrounded by<BR>the ocean.<BR>—समुद्र-फल, अम्, n. ‘sea-fruit,’ a<BR>particular drug or medicament.<BR>—समुद्र-फेन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘sea-foam,’ cuttle-fish bone; [cf. फेन.]<BR>—समुद्र-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the ocean,<BR>produced from or in the sea.<BR>—समुद्र-मेखला,<BR>f. ‘sea-girdled,’ the earth.<BR>—समुद्र-यात्रा, f. a sea-<BR>voyage.<BR>—समुद्र-यान, अम्, n. a sea-voyage; a<BR>vessel, ship, boat.<BR>—समुद्र-यायिन्, ई, m. a sea-farer,<BR>mariner, sailor, navigator, sea-trader.<BR>—समुद्र-<BR>योषित्, त्, f. ‘sea-wife,’ a river.<BR>—समुद्र-रशना<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">Page1079-b+ 77</a>]<BR>or समुद्र-रसना, f. ‘sea-girdled,’ the earth.<BR>—समुद्र-लवण, अम्, n. sea-salt.<BR>—समुद्र-<BR>वर्णन, अम्, n. ‘description of the ocean,’ N. of<BR>the sixty-eighth chapter of the Sundara-kāṇḍa of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—समुद्र-वसना, f. ‘sea-clothed,’<BR>the earth.<BR>—समुद्र-वह्नि, इस्, m. submarine fire.<BR>—समुद्र-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. ‘sea-clothed,’<BR>enveloped by the ocean, surrounded by the sea.<BR>—समुद्र-विजय, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>the twenty-second Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī.<BR>—समुद्र-वेला, f. the ocean-tide; an ocean-wave,<BR>wave of the sea.<BR>—समुद्र-व्यचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. extensive or expanded as the ocean.<BR>—समु-<BR>द्र-शोष, अस्, m. the creeping-plant Convolvulus<BR>Argenteus.<BR>—समुद्र-सुभगा, f. ‘ocean-favourite,’<BR>the Ganges.<BR>—समुद्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—समुद्र-स्नान, अम्, n. ablution in the sea.<BR>—समुद्रान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. the sea-shore;<BR>nutmeg; (आ), f. the shrub Alhagi Maurorum (=<BR>दुर्-आलभा); the cotton plant; the plant Trigo-<BR>nella Corniculata; another plant (= यवास).<BR>—स-<BR>मुद्राम्बरा (˚र-अम्˚), f. ‘sea-clothed,’ the earth.<BR>—समुद्राम्भस् (˚र-अम्˚), अस्, n. sea-water.<BR>—समुद्रारु (˚र-अरु or -आरु), उस्, m. a croco-<BR>dile, shark; a large fabulous fish (= तिमिङ्-गिल);<BR>Rāma's bridge or the ridge of rocks between India<BR>and Ceylon.<BR>—समुद्रार्थ (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. tending to the sea.<BR>—समुद्रोपप्लुत (˚र-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, inundated or submerged by the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रिय|समुद्रियः
समुद्रिय or समुद्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging<BR>to or generated in the firmament, aerial, (in Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 65, 13. the form समुद्रियः, acc. pl. fem., occurs);<BR>marine, oceanic, maritime, living in the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्र्य
समुद्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = समुद्रिय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्दन|समुंदन|समुंदनं|समुन्दनं
सम्-उन्दन, अम्, n. the act of thoroughly moist-<BR>ening or sprinkling; moisture, damp, wetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्न|समुन्नं
सम्-उन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, well moistened or sprin-<BR>kled, thoroughly wetted or watered, very wet or<BR>moist, moistened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदक्त|समुदक्तं
समुदक्त सम्-उदक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अञ्च्<BR>with उद् and सम्), lifted up, raised up, thrown up,<BR>drawn up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदागम्
समुदागम् सम्-उद्-आ-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्-<BR>छति, -गन्तुम्, to arrive at full or complete know-<BR>ledge, understand perfectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदागत
सम्-उदागत, अस्, आ, अम्, completely known or<BR>understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदागम|समुदागमः
सम्-उदागम, अस्, m. full or complete knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाचर्
समुदाचर् सम्-उद्-आ-चर्, cl. 1. P. A. -च-<BR>रति, -ते, &c., to move or travel about (e. g. रथेन,<BR>in a chariot); to practise, perform, accomplish, do;<BR>to act towards, treat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाचरत्
सम्-उदाचरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, practising; acting<BR>towards, treating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाचार|समुदाचारः
सम्-उदाचार, अस्, m. proper or right practice or<BR>usage; intention, purpose, design, motive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदावह्
समुदावह् सम्-उद्-आ-वह्, cl. 1. P. A. -व-<BR>हति, -ते, &c., to lead or conduct out, draw out,<BR>carry out; to carry away, carry off; to conduct<BR>home, marry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाहृ
समुदाहृ सम्-उद्-आ-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति,<BR>-ते, &c., to utter together; to pronounce, declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाहरण|समुदाहरणं
सम्-उदाहरण, अम्, n. the act of uttering, de-<BR>claring, pronouncing; illustrating, illustration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाहृत
सम्-उदाहृत, अस्, आ, अम्, declared, uttered; pro-<BR>nounced, said, spoken, mentioned, recorded; illus-<BR>trated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदि
समुदि सम्-उद्-इ, cl. 2. P. -एति, -एतुम्, to go<BR>upwards or rise together; to go up, ascend, rise; to<BR>rise up together or prepare for battle; to come toge-<BR>ther, collect together in great numbers; to come<BR>into the possession (of any one).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदय|समुदयं|समुदयः
सम्-उदय, अस्, m. going upwards, rise, ascent,<BR>rising (of the sun &c.); coming together, collection,<BR>multitude, number, heap, quantity; totality, the<BR>whole; revenue; combination, mixture, blending<BR>together; effort, exertion, perseverance; war,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">Page1079-c+ 76</a>]<BR>battle; the rear or reserve of an army; a day;<BR>(अम्), n. the rising of a planet, &c.; an auspicious<BR>moment (= लग्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाय|समुदायः
सम्-उदाय, अस्, m. rise, ascent; a collection, mul-<BR>titude, quantity, number, heap, mass, aggregate,<BR>whole, totality; a word of more than one syllable;<BR>war, battle; the rear or reserve of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदित|समुदितः
2. सम्-उदित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see under सं-<BR>वद्), gone up, risen, ascended, rising upwards, lofty,<BR>elevated; arisen, produced, occasioned, excited; come<BR>together, collected, gathered together, aggregated,<BR>united, assembled; possessed of, furnished with, en-<BR>dowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्यत्|समुद्यन्त्
सम्-उद्यत्, अन्, अती, अत्, ascending, rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीक्ष्
समुदीक्ष् सम्-उद्-ईक्ष्, cl. 1. A. -ईक्षते,<BR>-ईक्षितुम्, to look up at; to look at attentively,<BR>perceive, observe; to look well up to, confide in,<BR>trust in; to respect, honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीक्ष्य
सम्-उदीक्ष्य, ind. having looked up at, having<BR>looked at or observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीर्
समुदीर् सम्-उद्-ईर्, cl. 2. A. ईर्ते, &c., to<BR>move upwards; to move about, be agitated, be<BR>greatly moved or excited: Caus. -ईरयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to move upwards, raise; to cause to move<BR>about, agitate, excite, incite, stimulate; to throw;<BR>to raise the voice, speak, utter, declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीरण|समुदीरणं
सम्-उदीरण, अम्, n. the act of raising the voice,<BR>uttering, declaring, speaking, pronouncing; repeat-<BR>ing, reciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीरित
सम्-उदीरित, अस्, आ, अम्, set in motion, caused<BR>to move, agitated, excited; uttered, said, spoken,<BR>declared, recited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीर्ण
सम्-उदीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly moved or agi-<BR>tated, excited.<BR>—समुदीर्ण-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>agitated or excited in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीष्
समुदीष् सम्-उद्-ईष्, cl. 1. P. A. -ईषति,<BR>-ते, &c., Ved. to rise well upwards, mount quite<BR>upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग|समुद्गः
समुद्ग 1. स-मुद्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>cover or lid; having beans, filled with beans; (अस्),<BR>m. a covered box or casket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गक|समुद्गकः
1. स-मुद्गक, अस्, m. a covered box, casket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गम्
समुद्गम् सम्-उद्-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to go up or rise together; to rise up,<BR>ascend; to come forth, break forth, issue, exude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग|समुद्गः
2. सम्-उद्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going up or rising toge-<BR>ther, rising, ascending; entirely pervading; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of artificial stanza, (see below.)<BR>—समुद्ग-<BR>यमक, अम्, n. (in rhetoric) artificially combining<BR>words so as to make different parts of a stanza cor-<BR>respond in sound but with different senses, (see<BR>यमक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गक|समुद्गकः
2. समुद्गक, अस्, m. a kind of artificial stanza<BR>(each half of which corresponds exactly in sound,<BR>though the meanings of the words are different,<BR>those of one half being respectively adjectives to those<BR>of the other; an example occurs in Kirātārjunīya<BR>XV. 16).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गत
सम्-उद्गत, अस्, आ, अम्, risen up together, risen,<BR>ascended, arisen; rising; breaking forth, issuing,<BR>exuding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गम|समुद्गमः
सम्-उद्गम, अस्, m. rising, ascent, arising;<BR>issuing; birth, production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गॄ
समुद्गॄ सम्-उद्-गॄ. See rt. 2. गॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गीर्ण|समुद्गीर्णः
सम्-उद्गीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, vomited forth (as food<BR>&c.), ejected; raised up, lifted up; raised (as the<BR>voice), uttered, exclaimed, (in these senses perhaps<BR>to be connected with rt. 1. गॄ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गै
समुद्गै सम्-उद्-गै. See rt. गै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गीत|समुद्गीतं
सम्-उद्गीत, अस्, आ, अम्, sung out loud, chanted<BR>loudly; (अम्), n. a loud song, chant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग्रन्थ्
समुद्ग्रन्थ् सम्-उद्-ग्रन्थ्, cl. 9. P. -ग्रथ्-<BR>नाति, &c., to bind up together; to tie or fasten up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग्रथ्य
सम्-उद्ग्रथ्य, ind. having bound up together,<BR>having tied up (as the hair &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग्रह्
समुद्ग्रह् सम्-उद्-ग्रह्, cl. 9. P. A. -गृह्णाति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">Page1080-a+ 74</a>]<BR>-गृह्णीते, &c., to raise up together; to raise or lift<BR>up; to take hold of, lay hold of, seize on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गृह्य
सम्-उद्गृह्य, ind. having raised up, having<BR>taken hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्दिश्
समुद्दिश् सम्-उद्-दिश्, cl. 6. P. -दिशति,<BR>-देष्टुम्, to point out or indicate fully, mention at<BR>full, state, declare, communicate; to designate as,<BR>name; to refer to, relate to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्दिश्य
सम्-उद्दिश्य, ind. having fully pointed out; re-<BR>lating or referring to, with reference or regard to<BR>(with acc.); aiming at, in behalf of, on account of,<BR>in honour of, in remembrance of; for; against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्दिष्ट
सम्-उद्दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fully pointed out or<BR>declared or indicated, shown, explained; enumerated,<BR>particularised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्देश|समुद्देशः
सम्-उद्देश, अस्, m. fully pointing out or indicat-<BR>ing, accurate or complete description; explanation,<BR>enumeration, particularising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्दॄ
समुद्दॄ सम्-उद्-दॄ, Pass. -दीर्यते, to be com-<BR>pletely rent or torn in pieces, to burst asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्द्युत्
समुद्द्युत् सम्-उद्-द्युत्, cl. 1. A. -द्योतते,<BR>&c., to blaze up, shine very brilliantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्द्रु
समुद्द्रु सम्-उद्-द्रु, cl. 1. P. -द्रवति, -द्रो-<BR>तुम्, to run forth together, escape together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धन्
समुद्धन् सम्-उद्-धन् (-उद्-हन्). See rt.<BR>हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धत|समुद्धतः
सम्-उद्धत, अस्, आ, अम्, raised well up, com-<BR>pletely lifted up, upraised, uplifted, elevated, risen,<BR>excited, drawn up, upheld; puffed up with pride,<BR>proud, arrogant, overbearing; impudent, rude; ill-<BR>mannered, ill-behaved.<BR>—समुद्धत-लाङ्गूल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, (an animal) whose tail is raised or<BR>cocked up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धस्त
समुद्धस्त सम्-उद्-धस्त (-उद्-हस्त), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, wiped off with the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धू
समुद्धू सम्-उद्-धू, cl. 5. P. A. -धूनोति,<BR>-धूनुते, &c. (see rt. 1. धू), to shake up, toss<BR>up, rouse up, raise; to shake about, disturb, agitate,<BR>move hither and thither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धूत
सम्-उद्धूत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken about, agitated,<BR>driven hither and thither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धूय
सम्-उद्धूय, ind. having shaken up, having<BR>raised up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धृ
समुद्धृ सम्-उद्-धृ (-उद्-हृ), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-उद्धरति, -ते, -धर्तुम्, to raise well up, lift<BR>completely up, elevate, erect; to extol, honour; to<BR>take or pick up; to take quite out, draw well out,<BR>take out, extract; to extricate; to root out, extirpate,<BR>exterminate, destroy utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धरण|समुद्धरणं
सम्-उद्धरण, अम्, n. the act of raising well<BR>up, drawing up, upraising, lifting; picking up;<BR>drawing out, lifting out; complete extraction, extri-<BR>cation, deliverance; eradication, pulling up by the<BR>roots, extirpation; taking out from (as a part or<BR>share); food thrown up (from the stomach), vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धरत्
सम्-उद्धरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, raising up; picking<BR>up; drawing out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धर्तृ|समुद्धर्त्तृ
सम्-उद्धर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who lifts up or<BR>raises or extricates; (ता), m. a raiser up; deliverer,<BR>redeemer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धृत|समुद्धृतं
सम्-उद्धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, well raised or drawn<BR>up or uplifted; picked up; completely drawn out or<BR>extracted; lifted out, extricated; thrown up, vomited;<BR>taken away, removed; taken out from (as a share),<BR>deducted; set apart, divided; seized, possessed of;<BR>ill-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ध्वंस्
समुद्ध्वंस् सम्-उद्-ध्वंस्. See rt. ध्वंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ध्वस्त
सम्-उद्ध्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, completely overspread,<BR>sprinkled or covered with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

