सम्प्राद्रवत्|संप्राद्रवन्त्
सम्-प्राद्रवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, running away<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्|संप्राप्
सम्प्राप् सम्-प्राप् (-प्र-आप्), cl. 5. P. -प्रा-<BR>प्नोति, -प्राप्तुम्, to reach or attain fully to, reach,<BR>arrive at; to meet with, light upon, come to; to<BR>obtain or acquire thoroughly, gain; Caus. -प्राप-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to attain or obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्त|संप्राप्त|सम्प्राप्तः
सम्-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well reached or attained,<BR>arrived, found, met with; completely obtained, got,<BR>caught hold of; effected, accomplished; become.<BR>—सम्प्राप्त-यौवन, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>fully attained youth or manhood, come of age.<BR>—सम्प्राप्त-विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has ac-<BR>quired all knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्ति|संप्राप्ति|संप्राप्तिः|सम्प्राप्तिः
सम्-प्राप्ति, इस्, f. attainment, obtaining, getting,<BR>acquisition; gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्य
1. सम्-प्राप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be fully attained<BR>to, attainable, obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्य
2. सम्-प्राप्य, ind. having attained to or ob-<BR>tained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रार्थ्
सम्प्रार्थ् सम्-प्रार्थ् (-प्र-अर्थ्), cl. 10. P. A.<BR>-प्रार्थयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to ask for earnestly, pray<BR>for, beg, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रार्थित
सम्-प्रार्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, asked for, begged,<BR>requested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राव्
सम्प्राव् सम्-प्राव् (-प्र-अव्), cl. 1. P. -प्रा-<BR>वति, &c., Ved. to assist together, join in assisting,<BR>aid, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्री|संप्री
सम्प्री सम्-प्री, cl. 4. A. -प्रीयते, &c., to be<BR>completely satisfied or contented, to be greatly<BR>pleased with, delight in (with inst.): Caus. -प्रीणयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to make completely happy or pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रिय|संप्रिय
सम्-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, very dear or beloved;<BR>mutually dear, loving each other.<BR>—सम्प्रिय-ता,<BR>f. dearness, the being very dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीणित
सम्-प्रीणित, अस्, आ, अम्, made completely happy,<BR>thoroughly satisfied, well pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीत|संप्रीत
सम्-प्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, completely satisfied or<BR>pleased, delighted, well pleased.<BR>—सम्प्रीत-मानस,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, delighted in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीति|संप्रीति|संप्रीतिः
सम्-प्रीति, इस्, f. attachment, affection; friendly<BR>assent; delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीयमाण
सम्प्रीयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being greatly pleased,<BR>rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रे
सम्प्रे सम्-प्रे (-प्र-इ), cl. 2. P. -प्रैति, &c.,<BR>to go forth together, flow together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयत्
2. सम्-प्रयत्, अन्, अती, अत् (for 1. सम्-प्र-यत् see<BR>p. 1087, col. 1), flowing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्ष्|संप्रेक्ष्
सम्प्रेक्ष् सम्-प्रेक्ष् (-प्र-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-प्रेक्षते, &c., to look well at, observe carefully,<BR>behold, become aware of, perceive; to look well<BR>into, consider carefully, reflect on, examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्षण|संप्रेक्षण|संप्रेक्षणं
सम्-प्रेक्षण, अम्, n. the act of looking well<BR>at, observing, viewing, beholding, seeing; looking<BR>thoroughly into, deliberating about, considering, in-<BR>vestigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्षमाण
सम्-प्रेक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, fully beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्षित
सम्-प्रेक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, well looked at or seen,<BR>beheld; well looked into, considered, investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्ष्य
सम्-प्रेक्ष्य, ind. having looked carefully at,<BR>having observed or noticed; having looked well into,<BR>having considered or examined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेर्|संप्रेर्
सम्प्रेर् सम्-प्रेर् (-प्र-ईर्, see rt. ईर्), cl. 2.<BR>A. -प्रेर्ते, &c., to come forth together, rise to-<BR>gether; Caus. -प्रेरयति, -यितुम्, to drive or push<BR>forwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेर्ण
सम्-प्रेर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, risen up together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेर्य
सम्-प्रेर्य, ind. having pushed forwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेष्|संप्रेष्
सम्प्रेष् सम्-प्रेष् (-प्र-इष्, see rt. 1. इष्),<BR>cl. 4. P. -प्रेष्यति, -प्रेषितुम्, to throw, fling,<BR>cast; (in Vedic ritual) to summon, invite [cf. 2.<BR>प्रेष्]: Caus. -प्रेषयति, -यितुम्, to send forth<BR>together, send away, dispatch, send, dismiss; to send<BR>a message to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेषण
सम्-प्रेषण, अम्, n. the act of sending forth<BR>together, sending away, dispatching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेषित
सम्-प्रेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, sent forth, ordered;<BR>dismissed, sent away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेष्य
सम्-प्रेष्य, ind. having sent away or dispatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रैष|संप्रैष|संप्रैषः|सम्प्रैषः
सम्-प्रैष, अस्, m. sending away, dismissing;<BR>direction, order, command, precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्त|संप्रोक्त
सम्प्रोक्त सम्-प्रोक्त. See under सम्-प्र-<BR>वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्ष्
सम्प्रोक्ष् सम्-प्रोक्ष् (-प्र-उक्ष्), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>-प्रोक्षति, -ते, &c., to sprinkle well over, sprinkle<BR>on; to consecrate by sprinkling; to be sprinkled<BR>over (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्षण|संप्रोक्षण|संप्रोक्षणं
सम्-प्रोक्षण, अम्, n. the act of sprinkling well<BR>over, consecration (of a temple &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्षित
सम्-प्रोक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, well sprinkled or<BR>wetted (especially with holy water), consecrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्ष्य
सम्-प्रोक्ष्य, ind. having besprinkled; having<BR>sprinkled one's self well over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोर्णु
सम्प्रोर्णु सम्-प्रोर्णु (-प्र-ऊर्˚), cl. 2. P. A.<BR>-प्रोर्णोति or -प्रोर्णौति, -प्रोर्णुते, &c., to cover<BR>all over, cover completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्लु|संप्लु
सम्प्लु सम्-प्लु, cl. 1. A. -प्लवते, -प्लोतुम्,<BR>to flow together; to float about; to fluctuate: Caus.<BR>-प्लावयति, -यितुम्, to inundate, flood over, sub-<BR>merge, overwhelm; to cause to float about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्लव|संप्लव|संप्लवः
सम्-प्लव, अस्, m. submersion, inundation; flood;<BR>surging, surge; splashing or tumbling about in water;<BR>falling into ruins, ruin; subversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्लवमान
सम्-प्लवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, flowing together,<BR>floating about, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्लुत|संप्लुत
सम्-प्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, flooded, overspread, over-<BR>cast.<BR>—सम्प्लुतोदक (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, flooded<BR>with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फल|संफल
सम्फल सम्-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, see Vopa-<BR>deva IV. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फाल|संफाल|संफालः|सम्फालः
सम्फाल सम्-फाल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. फल् or<BR>rt. स्फल् with सम्), a ram, sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फुल्ल|संफुल्ल|सम्फुल्लः
सम्फुल्ल सम्-फुल्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. फल्<BR>with सम्), full-blown, blossomed, fully opened (as<BR>a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फेट|संफेट|संफेटः
सम्फेट सम्फेट, अस्, m. (perhaps fr. फेट्,<BR>q. v., with सम्), mutual encounter of persons en-<BR>raged or agitated, angry and tumultuous conflict (as<BR>a particular division of dramatic action; described in<BR>the Sāhitya-darpaṇa, and illustrated by the encounter<BR>of Mādhava and Aghora-ghaṇṭa in the Mālatī-<BR>mādhava).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब्|संब्
सम्ब् सम्ब् [cf. rts. सर्ब्, शम्ब्, साम्ब्], cl.<BR>1. P. सम्बति, &c., to go, creep; cl. 10.<BR>P. सम्बयति, -यितुम्, to collect, accumulate, con-<BR>nect, join together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब|संब|संबं|सम्बं
सम्ब, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. सम्ब् above),<BR>water [cf. सम्बर]; twice ploughing, the second<BR>ploughing of a field [cf. शम्ब].<BR>—सम्बा-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. -करोति, &c., to plough twice.<BR>—सम्बा-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, twice ploughed [cf. शम्बा-कृत].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बंह्
सम्बंह् सम्-बंह्, cl. 10. P. or Caus. (or Nom.<BR>of बहुल) -बंहयति, -यितुम्, to make firm or<BR>prosperous, establish firmly, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बत्
सम्बत् सम्-बत्, ind. (according to Śabda-k.)<BR>= सं-वत्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्ध्|संबंध्|संबन्ध्
सम्बन्ध् सम्-बन्ध्, cl. 9. P. -बध्नाति, &c.,<BR>to bind together, fasten or tie together, bind or fix<BR>on, attach, connect, to construct, form: Pass. -बध्-<BR>यते, to be bound together, to be attached or con-<BR>nected, belong to; to be furnished or supplied with:<BR>Caus. -बन्धयति, -यितुम्, to cause to bind toge-<BR>ther; to make to bind on or attach or connect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बद्ध|संबद्ध|सम्बद्धः
सम्-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound or tied together,<BR>connected; connected in sense, having meaning;<BR>fastened together; closed, shut; bound on, fastened<BR>or fixed on, attached; connected with, belonging to,<BR>related, inherent, endowed with, possessing, possessed<BR>of authority, empowered.<BR>—सम्बद्ध-दर्प, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having feelings of pride formed (in the heart).<BR>—सम्बद्ध-सैन्यौघ (˚य-ओघ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the main body of troops concentrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बध्नत्
सम्-बध्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, binding together, at-<BR>taching, forming (fruit as a plant &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बध्यमान
सम्-बध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being bound toge-<BR>ther or connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्ध|संबन्ध|संबंध|संबन्धः|सम्बन्धः
सम्-बन्ध, अस्, m. binding together, joining<BR>together, union, association, connection (sometimes<BR>at the end of comps. in the sense ‘connected,’ &c.,<BR>cf. सु-स्˚); connection by marriage [cf. स्त्री-स्˚];<BR>relationship, relation, (in phil. said to be of<BR>three kinds, 1. समवाय, ‘intimate relation,’ as<BR>between a whole and its parts; 2. संयोग, ‘con-<BR>junction,’ as between a pot and the ground; 3.<BR>स्वरूप, ‘the nature of a thing,’ as between an<BR>object and the knowledge of it, which last is also<BR>called विषयता-सम्बन्ध), inherence; a rela-<BR>tion, kinsman, relative, (कु-सम्बन्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>wicked relation); binding, restraining, restraint; (in<BR>grammar) the possessive case (but see कारक); the<BR>application of authority to prove a theological doc-<BR>trine; fitness, propriety; prosperity, success; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), able, capable; fit, right, proper.<BR>—सम्बन्ध-<BR>तत्त्व, अम्, n. and सम्बन्ध-विवेक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of two works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्धक|संबन्धक|संबंधक|संबन्धकः
सम्बन्धक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to, concern-<BR>ing; fit, suitable; (अस्), m. connection by birth or<BR>marriage; a relation, friend; (scil. सन्धि), a kind<BR>of alliance proceeding from relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्धिन्|संबन्धिन्|संबंधिन्
सम्बन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, connected with, belong-<BR>ing to, relating or related to, referring to, adjunct,<BR>inherent; possessing good qualities; (ई), m. a rela-<BR>tion or connection (by marriage), relative, kinsman.<BR>—सम्बन्धि-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, divided or shared<BR>by relatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बर|संबर|सम्बरं|संबरः|सम्बरः
सम्बर सम्बर, अस्, m. (apparently mixed<BR>up and confounded with the words सं-वर, शं-<BR>वर, शम्बर, but in some senses said to be fr. rt.<BR>सम्ब्), a bridge, dam, causeway, (probably for सं-<BR>वर); a kind of deer; a sort of fish; a particular<BR>mountain; a kind of dramatic entertainment; N. of<BR>a demon or Daitya, (see शम्बर); N. of a Jaina<BR>Arhat of the future period; N. of a district and lake<BR>in Rājputāna (where the salt called गड-लवण is<BR>found; sometimes written सं-वर); (ई), f. the plant<BR>Asparagus Racemosus (= शता-वरी); the aquatic<BR>plant Salvinia Cucullata; (अम्), n. restraint, self-<BR>control; a religious observance with Buddhists;<BR>water, (in the preceding senses probably for सं-<BR>वर, but cf. शम्बर.)<BR>—सम्बरारि (˚र-अरि),<BR>इस्, m. ‘enemy of Sambara,’ epithet of Kāma-deva.<BR>—सम्बरोद्भव (˚र-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘produced in<BR>Sambara,’ a kind of salt (= गड-लवण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बर्य
सम्बर्य (said to be connected with सम्बर<BR>above), Nom. P. सम्बर्यति, -यितुम्, to bring<BR>together [cf. rt. सम्ब्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बल|संबल|संबलं|संबलः
सम्बल, अस्, अम्, m. n. [cf. शम्बल], provender,<BR>stock of provisions for a journey; (अम्), n. water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाकृ
सम्बाकृ सम्बा-कृ. See सम्ब, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाध्|संबाध्
सम्बाध् सम्-बाध्, cl. 1. A. -बाधते, &c., to<BR>press together, compress, contract; to press heavily on;<BR>to bind firmly together; to oppress, afflict, torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाध|संबाध|संबाधः|सम्बाधः
सम्-बाध, अस्, m. pressing together, compres-<BR>sion, contraction, pressing on, pressure, thronging,<BR>blocking up, the being thronged; difficulty, obstruc-<BR>tion, (sometimes at the end of comps. in the senses,<BR>‘narrow,’ ‘contracted,’ ‘confined,’ ‘blocked up,’<BR>‘crowded,’ ‘completely covered or strewn,’ ‘ob-<BR>structed;’ cf. हस्त्य्-अश्व-रथ-स्˚, शर-स्˚); the<BR>female organ of generation; the road to Naraka or<BR>hell; fear, dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाधक|संबाधक
सम्-बाधक, अस्, आ, अम्, pressing together, com-<BR>pressing, contracting; pressing upon, thronging,<BR>crowding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाधन|संबाधन|संबाधनं|सम्बाधनं
सम्-बाधन, अम्, n. the act of pressing to-<BR>gether or compressing; thronging, obstructing, op-<BR>posing; a barrier, gate; the female organ, (according<BR>to Śabda-k. = मदनस्य द्वार); a door-keeper;<BR>the point of a stake or spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुध्|संबुध्
सम्बुध् सम्-बुध्, cl. 1. P. A., 4. A. -बोधति,<BR>-ते, -बुध्यते (ep. also P. -ति), &c., to perceive or<BR>understand thoroughly, have perfect knowledge of;<BR>to perceive, notice, observe, know; to wake up:<BR>Caus. -बोधयति, -यितुम्, to cause to know, inform,<BR>instruct, advise; exhort, admonish; to explain; to<BR>make attentive, cause to wake up, rouse; to call to;<BR>to cause to agree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुद्ध|संबुद्ध|संबुद्धः|सम्बुद्धः
सम्-बुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, well perceived, perfectly<BR>known or understood; thoroughly awake; exces-<BR>sively wise, prudent, clever; (अस्), m. a Buddha or<BR>Jaina deified sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुद्धि|संबुद्धि|संबुद्धिः|सम्बुद्धिः
सम्-बुद्धि, इस्, f. perfect knowledge or per-<BR>ception; calling to; the vocative case (= सम्-<BR>बोधन); an epithet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुध्य
सम्-बुध्य, ind. awaking, waking up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुध्यमान
सम्-बुध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being quite aware.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोध|संबोध|संबोधः|सम्बोधः
सम्-बोध, अस्, m. explaining, instructing, in-<BR>forming; throwing, sending; loss, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोधन|संबोधन|संबोधनं|सम्बोधनं
सम्-बोधन, अम्, n. the act of causing to know<BR>thoroughly, informing, instructing, explanation, call-<BR>ing to, addressing; the vocative case (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोधयित्वा
सम्-बोधयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having caused<BR>to be informed, having instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोधित
सम्-बोधित, अस्, आ, अम्, fully warned, duly apprised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोधितवत्
सम्-बोधितवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has duly<BR>warned or apprised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोध्य|संबोध्य
सम्-बोध्य, ind. having explained, having made<BR>an excuse or apology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बृह्|संबृह्
सम्बृह् सम्-बृह् or सम्-बृंह्. See सं-<BR>वृंह्, p. 1038.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब्रू
सम्ब्रू सम्-ब्रू, cl. 2. P. A. -ब्रवीति, -ब्रूते,<BR>&c. (see rt. ब्रू, p. 694), to speak with, converse<BR>with; to talk together, agree; to say anything to<BR>any one (with two acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भक्ष्|संभक्ष्
सम्भक्ष् सम्-भक्ष्, cl. 10. P. -भक्षयति,<BR>&c., to eat together, eat up, devour, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भक्ष|संभक्ष|संभक्षः
सम्-भक्ष, अस्, m. eating together, food in<BR>common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भक्ष्य
सम्-भक्ष्य, ind. having eaten up, having con-<BR>sumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भक्ष्यमाण
सम्-भक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being consumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भज्|संभज्
सम्भज् सम्-भज्, cl. 1. P. A. -भजति, -ते,<BR>-भक्तुम्, to distribute completely, apportion, allot,<BR>dispense, divide, share, cause to participate in; to<BR>bestow, grant; to favour, serve, help; to share in,<BR>possess, enjoy (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भक्त|संभक्त
सम्-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, distributed, divided,<BR>shared; participating or sharing in, enjoying, pos-<BR>sessing; devoted to, faithful to, faithfully attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भक्ति|संभक्ति|संभक्तिः
सम्-भक्ति, इस्, f. sharing in, possessing, enjoy-<BR>ing; participating, causing to participate, distributing;<BR>favouring, honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भक्तृ
सम्-भक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who shares or par-<BR>ticipates, one who enjoys or possesses, sharing in,<BR>possessing, one who distributes or grants, one who<BR>favours or honours or worships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भजन|संभजन
सम्-भजन, अम्, n. causing to share in, dis-<BR>tributing, favouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भजनीय
सम्-भजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be shared in or<BR>enjoyed, to be liked; to be favoured or honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भञ्ज्|संभञ्ज्
सम्भञ्ज् सम्-भञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. -भनक्ति, &c.,<BR>to break to pieces, shatter, shiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भग्न|संभग्न|संभग्नः
सम्-भग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, broken to pieces, ṣat-<BR>tered; dispersed, scattered, defeated; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>Śiva (= सम्यक्-सेवित, as if fr. सम्-भज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भर|संभर
सम्भर सम्-भर. See under सम्-भृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भर्त्स्
सम्भर्त्स् सम्-भर्त्स्, cl. 10. P. A. -भर्त्स-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, to censure greatly, abuse, reproach,<BR>find fault with, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भर्त्सित|संभर्त्सित
सम्-भर्त्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, much censured, abused,<BR>reviled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भल्
सम्भल् सम्-भल्, cl. 10. P. A. -भालयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to observe well, perceive, hear, see,<BR>behold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भल|संभल
सम्भल सम्भल, अस्, m. (for सम्-भर),<BR>Ved. one who brings together, one who arranges a<BR>marriage, a match-maker; a suitor, wooer; a pro-<BR>curer, pimp; (ई), f. a procuress, bawd, (also written<BR>शम्भली.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भव|संभव|संभवः|सम्भवः
सम्भव सम्-भव, &c. See under सम्-भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भा|संभा
सम्भा सम्-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति, -बभौ,<BR>-भातुम्, to shine fully or brightly, be very bright;<BR>to shine forth, be visible, be conspicuous; to ap-<BR>pear, seem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाण्डय
सम्भाण्डय सम्-भाण्डय (fr. भाण्ड with<BR>सम्), Nom. A. -भाण्डयते, -यितुम्, to collect<BR>vessels or utensils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाण्ड्य
सम्-भाण्ड्य, ind. having collected utensils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाव्य|संभाव्य
सम्भाव्य सम्-भाव्य. See p. 1090.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाष्|संभाष्
सम्भाष् सम्-भाष्, cl. 1. A. -भाषते, &c.,<BR>to speak together, converse with; to address, speak<BR>to (with acc.); to greet, salute; to agree together,<BR>consent; to talk over, persuade (with acc.); to have<BR>sexual intercourse with; to speak, say, recite; Caus.<BR>-भाषयति, -यितुम्, to converse with (with inst.);<BR>to address (with acc.); to persuade, prevail upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाष|संभाषः
सम्-भाष, अस्, m. conversation [cf. स्नेह-स्˚];<BR>(आ), f. conversation, discourse; greeting; criminal<BR>connection; contract, agreement; war-cry, watch-<BR>word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषण|संभाषण|संभाषणं|सम्भाषणं
सम्-भाषण, अम्, n. conversation, discourse;<BR>sexual intercourse; war-cry, watch-word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषत्
सम्-भाषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, speaking together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषमाण
सम्-भाषमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking or con-<BR>versing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषित|संभाषित
सम्-भाषित, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken to, addressed;<BR>said, spoken; (अम्), n. conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषित्वा
सम्-भाषित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having con-<BR>versed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाष्य|संभाष्य
1. सम्भाष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be conversed with,<BR>fit to be talked in, (असम्भाष्ये देशे, in a place<BR>unfit for conversation, Manu VIII. 55.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाष्य|संभाष्य
2. सम्-भाष्य, ind. having addressed in suitable<BR>language; addressing, accosting; having recited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भिद्|संभिद्
सम्भिद् सम्-भिद्, cl. 7. P. A. -भिनत्ति,<BR>-भिन्त्ते, &c., to break to pieces, split or break<BR>completely asunder, pierce; to bring into contact,<BR>combine, join, mingle, associate with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भिन्न|संभिन्न|संभिन्नः|सम्भिन्नः
सम्-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, completely broken or<BR>divided; shaken, agitated; brought into contact or<BR>collision, combined or united with; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सम्भिन्न-मर्याद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has broken through barriers or bounds.<BR>—सम्भिन्न-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>abandoned good conduct.<BR>—सम्भिन्न-सर्वाङ्ग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has contracted or compressed<BR>the whole body (as a tortoise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भेद|संभेद|संभेदः|सम्भेदः
सम्-भेद, अस्, m. breaking to pieces, splitting,<BR>bursting; union, junction, mixture; the confluence<BR>of two rivers, the junction of a river with the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भेदन|संभेदन
सम्-भेदन, अम्, n. the act of breaking up;<BR>bringing into contact or collision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भीत|संभीत
सम्भीत सम्-भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly alarmed,<BR>afraid of (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुज्|संभुज्
सम्भुज् 1. सम्-भुज्. See rt. 1. भुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुग्न
सम्-भुग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, completely bent or curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुज्|संभुज्
सम्भुज् 2. सम्-भुज्, cl. 7. P. A. -भुनक्ति,<BR>-भुङ्क्ते, -भोक्तुम्, to enjoy together, eat together;<BR>to enjoy thoroughly, eat; to enjoy carnally; to serve,<BR>be of service to (Ved.): Pass. -भुज्यते, to be en-<BR>joyed together, to be enjoyed: Caus. -भोजयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to enjoy, cause to eat; to feed with<BR>(with acc. and instr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुक्त|संभुक्त
सम्-भुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well enjoyed; eaten;<BR>made use of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुज
सम्-भुज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. universally enjoyed,<BR>(Sāy. = सन्तत-भुज or सम्-भुजम् = सम्यक्<BR>भोगाय, Ṛg-veda II. 1, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुञ्जत्
सम्-भुञ्जत्, अन्, अती, अत्, enjoying, &c.; being<BR>of service to (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोग|संभोग|संभोगः|सम्भोगः
सम्-भोग, अस्, m. complete enjoyment, pleasure,<BR>delight; sensual enjoyment; carnal enjoyment, sexual<BR>union; a particular subdivision of the Śṛṅgāra Rasa or<BR>sentiment of love (described as successful love leading<BR>to union); employment, use; a sensualist, libertine;<BR>a Jaina or Buddhist edict (= शासन).<BR>—सम्भोग-<BR>क्षम, अस्, आ, अम्, suitable for enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोगिन्|संभोगिन्
सम्भोगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, enjoying, addicted to sensual<BR>enjoyment, sensual; employing, using; (ई), m. a<BR>sensualist, libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोजक|संभोजक|संभोजकः
सम्-भोजक, अस्, m. an eater, taster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोजन|संभोजन|संभोजनं
सम्-भोजन, अम्, n. the act of enjoying or eat-<BR>ing; feeding; eating together, a meal taken in<BR>company, a dinner party; (अस्, ई, अम्), eating to-<BR>gether; [cf. सह-भोजन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोज्य|संभोज्य
सम्-भोज्य, ind. having caused to enjoy or eat;<BR>having fed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुर्
सम्भुर् सम्-भुर्. See rt. भुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जर्भुराण|संजर्भुराण
सञ्-जर्भुराण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens.), moving<BR>about rapidly; seizing, taking, (Sāy. = गृह्णत्, Ṛg-<BR>veda V. 44, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भू|संभू
सम्भू सम्-भू, cl. 1. P. A. -भवति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to be together, be united with, be joined with, have<BR>intercourse with (with inst. or sometimes with acc.),<BR>be united sexually with; to meet with; to be born<BR>or produced, be engendered, be formed, arise, spring<BR>up, proceed, ensue, accrue; to take place, happen,<BR>take effect; to be, become, exist, be found, occur;<BR>to be composed of, to be adequate for (with inf.), be<BR>competent to (with inf.), be able; to be fitting or<BR>compatible or consistent; to be possible; to be capable<BR>of holding; to be capable of existing in, be contained<BR>in; to be numbered among (Ved.): Caus. -भावयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to be together, cause to be united<BR>or meet together; to bring together; to cause to be<BR>born or produced, cause to be or exist, produce, effect,<BR>accomplish, make; to manifest, exhibit; to think<BR>about, think, imagine, fancy, suppose, consider, be-<BR>lieve; to imply, suggest a possibility, suppose anything<BR>possible in any one (with loc. or gen.), believe any<BR>one capable of; to think highly of, honour, esteem,<BR>do honour to, pay one's respects to, salute, greet; to<BR>receive or accept with honour or favour; to honour<BR>or gratify with, present with (with inst.), bestow; to<BR>regard or consider as (with two acc.); to expect:<BR>Pass. of Caus. -भाव्यते, to be produced or effected;<BR>to be possible; to be honoured or esteemed; to be<BR>received with favour; to be supposed or imagined<BR>or proved capable of, &c.; to be thought fitting or<BR>consistent: Desid. -बुभूषति, to wish to be pro-<BR>duced, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भव|संभव|संभवः|सम्भवः
सम्-भव, अस्, m. birth, being, production, ex-<BR>istence, arising, springing up; origin, cause, motive;<BR>uniting together, combination, mixing, union; com-<BR>patibility, consistency, appropriateness, adaptation,<BR>adequacy; capacity, ability, possibility; agreement,<BR>conformity (especially of the receptacle to the thing<BR>received); equivalence (regarded as one of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">Page1090-a+ 79</a>]<BR>Pramāṇas or means of certain knowledge in phil.,<BR>it may be illustrated by the equivalence known to<BR>exist between one shilling and twelve pence); ac-<BR>quaintance, intimacy; loss, destruction; N. of the<BR>third Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī, (also read<BR>शम्-भव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भवत्
सम्-भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being, existing, arising,<BR>springing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भव्य|संभव्य|संभव्यः|सम्भव्यः
सम्-भव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be produced together,<BR>to be capable, &c.; (अस्), m. the wood-apple, Feronia<BR>Elephantum (= कपित्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावन|संभावन|संभावनं|सम्भावनं
सम्-भावन, अम्, आ, n. f. compatibility, fitness,<BR>suitableness, adequacy, competency, ability; possi-<BR>bility; (in logic) doubt; (in grammar) the sense of<BR>the potential mood; considering, reflecting, supposi-<BR>tion, idea, fancy, imagination, thought; regard,<BR>esteem; worship, honour, affection, love; paying<BR>honour, salutation, greeting; celebrity, fame; a par-<BR>ticular Alaṅkāra or figure in rhetoric (described by<BR>some as the use of the verb in the imperative or<BR>potential mood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावनीय|संभावनीय
सम्-भावनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured or<BR>greeted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावयितव्य|संभावयितव्य
सम्-भावयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावित|संभावित|सम्भावितः
सम्-भावित, अस्, आ, अम्, suited, fitted, adequate,<BR>capable, suited to, fit for, possible; perceived, thought<BR>about, thought of, considered, supposed, conjectured,<BR>imagined, reflected; thought highly of, esteemed,<BR>honoured, honourable; satisfied.<BR>—सम्भावित-तर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, more honoured or esteemed, more con-<BR>fided in.<BR>—सम्भावितात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ,<BR>noble-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाव्य|संभाव्य
1. सम्-भाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be adapted, to be<BR>made fit; suitable, capable; to be supposed capable,<BR>to be supposed, supposable, imaginable, probable; to<BR>be honoured, &c.; (अम्), n. adequacy, competency,<BR>fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाव्य|संभाव्य
2. सम्-भाव्य, ind. having honoured or done<BR>honour to, having adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भु|संभु|सम्भुः
सम्-भु, उस्, m. one who is born or produced<BR>(= सम्भवति यः); a parent, progenitor; a species<BR>of the Ati-dhṛti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूत|संभूत|सम्भूतः
सम्-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being together, combined<BR>with; become, born, produced, arisen, accrued, pro-<BR>ceeded from, formed of, composed; capable, ade-<BR>quate, equal; (अस्), m., N. of a king.<BR>—सम्भूत-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the being combined or united with<BR>(e. g. पञ्चसु भूतेषु, with the five elements).<BR>—सम्भूत-विजय, अस्, m. (according to some)<BR>N. of a particular Jaina Arhat (= श्रुत-केवलिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूति|संभूति|संभूतिः
सम्-भूति, इस्, f. the being together, combina-<BR>tion; suitability, fitness; Fitness (personified as a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Marīci); birth, ori-<BR>gin, production; power.<BR>—सम्भूति-विजय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of the six Śruta-kevalins (with Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूय|संभूय
सम्-भूय, ind. being together, being united or<BR>combined with, (सम्भूय समुत्थानम्, en-<BR>gaging in business after joining partnership, associa-<BR>tion in trade, partnership; sometimes written as a<BR>compound word.)<BR>—सम्भूय-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>acting in concert or in company, a coadjutor, co-<BR>partner, colleague.<BR>—सम्भूय-गमन or सम्-<BR>भूय-यान, अम्, n. going in company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूयस्य
सम्भूयस्य (said to be fr. a form सम्-भूयस्),<BR>Nom. P. सम्भूयस्यति, &c., to be born again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूष्
सम्भूष् सम्-भूष्, cl. 1. P. -भूषति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to procure or provide anything (acc.) for any one<BR>(loc.); to obtain, (भूष् being regarded by Sāy. as a<BR>form of rt. 1. भू); to adorn, (Sāy. = अलङ्-कृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृ|संभृ
सम्भृ सम्-भृ, cl. 1. 3. P. A. -भरति, -ते,<BR>-बिभर्ति, -बिभृते, &c., to bring together, collect,<BR>unite, concentrate, place together, compose; to pre-<BR>pare, make ready, procure (materials or ingredients<BR>of any kind, especially for a sacrifice); to offer, pre-<BR>sent; to support or maintain well, nourish; to effect;<BR>accomplish: Caus. -भारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>bring together or prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भर|संभर
सम्-भर, अस्, m., Ved. one who brings together,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">Page1090-b+ 76</a>]<BR>a supporter, bestower, (Sāy. = सम्भर्तृ, धारक,<BR>Ṛg-veda IV. 17, 11.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भार|संभार|संभारः|सम्भारः
सम्-भार, अस्, m. bringing together, collecting,<BR>preparing, preparation, equipment, provision, ap-<BR>paratus, materials, necessaries, constituent part, in-<BR>gredient, requisite, assemblage of things required for<BR>any purpose; multitude, number, quantity, heap, ful-<BR>ness, completeness; wealth; maintaining or support-<BR>ing well, maintenance, support, nourishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भार्य|संभार्य|सम्भार्य्य
सम्-भार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be maintained or<BR>nourished, a dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृत|संभृत|सम्भृतः
सम्-भृत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought together, col-<BR>lected, assembled, accumulated, concentrated, com-<BR>posed, prepared, got ready, equipped, fitted out,<BR>provided, stored, laden, filled, covered, furnished,<BR>endowed, possessed of; full, complete, compact;<BR>brought, placed, deposited, offered (as an oblation);<BR>acquired, obtained, gained; produced, caused; well<BR>maintained or nourished; carried, borne.<BR>—सम्-<BR>भृत-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one who has accom-<BR>plished holy acts (said of Indra; Sāy. = सम्पादित-<BR>कर्मन् or सम्पादित-प्रज्ञ, Ṛg-veda 1. 52, 8).<BR>—सम्भृत-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, one whose beauty is<BR>enhanced, richly stored.<BR>—सम्भृत-सम्भार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has brought together all re-<BR>quisite materials or provided all requisites.<BR>—सम्-<BR>भृतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>accumulated wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृति|संभृति|संभृतिः|सम्भृतिः
सम्-भृति, इस्, f. collection; equipment, prepara-<BR>tion, provision; plenitude, fulness; complete main-<BR>tenance, support, nourishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृत्य|संभृत्य
1. सम्-भृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be maintained or<BR>nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृत्य|संभृत्य
2. सम्-भृत्य, ind. having brought together,<BR>having nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रियमाण
सम्-भ्रियमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being collected;<BR>being nourished, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रंश्
सम्भ्रंश् सम्-भ्रंश् or सम्-भ्रश्, cl. 4. P. A.<BR>-भ्रश्यति, -ते, &c., to fall quite away, glide off,<BR>slip away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रज्ज्
सम्भ्रज्ज् सम्-भ्रज्ज्. See rt. 1. भ्रज्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृष्ट
सम्-भृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, thoroughly parched,<BR>dried, dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रम्|संभ्रम्
सम्भ्रम् सम्-भ्रम्, cl. 1. 4. P. -भ्रमति,<BR>-भ्राम्यति, &c., to roam or wander all about, go<BR>quite astray; to whirl about, be greatly confused, be<BR>perplexed or puzzled: Caus. -भ्रमयति, -भ्राम-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to lead astray, perplex, bewilder:<BR>Pass. of Caus. -भ्राम्यते, &c., to be led astray,<BR>be bewildered, be at a loss, be perplexed about<BR>(with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रम|संभ्रम|संभ्रमः|सम्भ्रमः
सम्-भ्रम, अस्, m. moving about, moving or<BR>going round, turning round, whirling about, re-<BR>volving, haste, hurry; flurry, confusion, agitation;<BR>uproar, tumult; fear, terror, alarm; error, mistake,<BR>ignorance; bustling activity, zeal; respect, reverence;<BR>epithet of a class of beings attending on Śiva.<BR>—सम्-<BR>भ्रम-ज्वलित, अस्, आ, अम्, excited by flurry.<BR>—सम्भ्रम-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, possessing bewilder-<BR>ment, embarrassed, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रान्त|संभ्रांत|संभ्रान्त
सम्-भ्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, whirled about; flurried,<BR>confused, perplexed, troubled, bewildered, stirred up,<BR>agitated, excited.<BR>—सम्भ्रान्त-जन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one whose people are bewildered.<BR>—सम्भ्रान्त-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, bewildered in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्राज्
सम्भ्राज् सम्-भ्राज्, cl. 1. A. -भ्राजते, &c.<BR>(see rt. 1. भ्राज्), to shine brightly, glitter, gleam,<BR>sparkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्राजत्|संभ्राजन्त्
सम्-भ्राजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shining brightly,<BR>glittering, sparkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मज्ज्
सम्मज्ज् सम्-मज्ज्, cl. 6. P. -मज्जति, &c.,<BR>to sink together, sink down, to be wholly submerged<BR>or immersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मग्न|संमग्न
सम्-मग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk down; immersed;<BR>overwhelmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मथ्
सम्मथ् सम्-मथ् or सम्-मन्थ्, cl. 1. 9. P.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">Page1090-c+ 76</a>]<BR>-मथति, -मन्थति, -मथ्नाति, &c., to bruise<BR>or pound together, crush to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मथित
सम्-मथित, अस्, आ, अम्, bruised, pounded,<BR>crushed to pieces, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मद्|संमद्
सम्मद् सम्-मद्, cl. 4. P. -माद्यति (Ved.<BR>also cl. 1. P. A. -मदति, -मन्दति, -ते), -मदितुम्,<BR>to be completely drunk or intoxicated; to be very<BR>glad, be greatly pleased with, rejoice at, rejoice:<BR>Caus. -मादयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to make intoxicated;<BR>to make cheerful, put in good spirits, exhilarate; to<BR>be completely intoxicated (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मत्त|संमत्त
सम्-मत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, completely intoxicated,<BR>greatly exhilarated or excited, intoxicated with love,<BR>enraptured; rutting, in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मद|संमद|संमदः|सम्मदः
सम्-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly exhilarated, happy,<BR>glad; (अस्), m. exhilaration, happiness, joy, pleasure;<BR>N. of the king of the fish (in Viṣṇu-Purāṇa IV. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्माद|संमाद|संमादः|सम्मादः
सम्-माद, अस्, m. great exhilaration, intoxica-<BR>tion, frenzy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मन्|संमन्
सम्मन् सम्-मन्, cl. 4. A. (ep. also P.)<BR>-मन्यते (-ति), -मन्तुम्, to think together, be of<BR>the same mind, agree, consent to, assent to, approve,<BR>sanction, authorise, permit, allow, recognise; to<BR>think highly of, esteem, value, honour; to think,<BR>suppose, imagine; to consider or regard as, to have<BR>in the mind, intend, contemplate, resolve: Caus.<BR>-मानयति, -यितुम्, to honour, reverence, respect;<BR>to consider, regard; to assure of; to instruct, teach,<BR>(Pāṇ. 1. 3, 36.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मत|संमत
सम्-मत, अस्, आ, अम्, agreed, consented or as-<BR>sented to, concurred in, approved; conformable,<BR>corresponding, like, resembling, attached, liked, be-<BR>loved; thought highly of, esteemed, highly honoured,<BR>valued; thought, supposed, considered, regarded;<BR>(अम्), n. assent, consent, approval, acquiescence, con-<BR>currence; opinion, impression, (सम्मते सार्थ-<BR>वाहस्य, under the impression of its being a com-<BR>pany of travellers.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मति|संमति|संमतिः|सम्मतिः
सम्-मति, इस्, f. sameness of opinion, agreement,<BR>consent, assent, approval, approbation; wish, desire;<BR>esteem, respect, homage; regard, affection, love;<BR>self-knowledge; order, command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मतीय|संमतीय
सम्मतीय, N. of one of the four divisions of the<BR>Vaibhāṣika system of Buddhism (whose founder is said<BR>to have been Upāli, a disciple of the great Buddha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान|संमान|संमानः|सम्मानः
1. सम्-मान, अस्, m. (according to some also<BR>अम्, n.), honour, respect, homage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मानन|संमानन|संमाननं
सम्-मानन, अम्, n. the act of honouring, wor-<BR>ship, homage; instruction, teaching, (Pāṇ. 1. 3, 36.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मानित|संमानित|सम्मानितः
सम्-मानित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured, treated with<BR>reverence or respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान्य|संमान्य
सम्-मान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured, honour-<BR>able, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मन्त्र्|संमंत्र्|संमन्त्र्
सम्मन्त्र् सम्-मन्त्र्, cl. 10. A. -मन्त्रयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to consult together, take counsel with (with<BR>inst.), hold a council, deliberate, advise, express an<BR>opinion; to salute, greet, address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मन्त्रणीय|संमन्त्रणीय
सम्-मन्त्रणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be consulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मन्त्रयित्वा
सम्-मन्त्रयित्वा (anom. ind. part.), having con-<BR>sulted together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मन्त्र्य
सम्-मन्त्र्य, ind. having consulted together;<BR>having saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्द|संमर्दः|सम्मर्द्द|सम्मर्द्दः
सम्मर्द सम्-मर्द, सम्-मर्दिन्, &c. See<BR>under सम्-मृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्शिन्|संमर्शिन्
सम्मर्शिन् सम्-मर्शिन्. See under सम्-मृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मा|संमा
सम्मा 1. सम्-मा (see rt. 3. मा), cl. 2. P.,<BR>3. 4. A. -माति, -मिमीते (2nd sing. Impv. P., Ved.<BR>-मिमीहि), -मायते, -मातुम्, to measure out, mea-<BR>sure; to make of the same measure, make equal,<BR>make to correspond, equalize (in size, number,<BR>quantity, &c.); to compare; to mete out, appor-<BR>tion, distribute, grant, bestow (Ved.); to be of the<BR>same capacity with, be contained in (with loc.):<BR>Pass. -मीयते, to be of the same measure; to be<BR>contained in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मा|संमा
2. सम्-मा, f. a kind of Vedic metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान|संमान|संमानः|सम्मानः
2. सम्-मान, अम्, n. the act of measuring out,<BR>equalizing, comparing; measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मित|संमित|संमितं|सम्मितः
सम्-मित, अस्, आ, अम्, measured out, measured,<BR>meted; of the same measure, of equal measure or<BR>extent, commensurate, conformable, corresponding,<BR>equal, same, like, resembling, similar, as large as, as<BR>long as (e. g. तुलया स्˚, equal in weight; समरे स्˚,<BR>equal in battle; पाप-स्˚, equal in crime; नगर-स्˚,<BR>as large as a city; योजनायुत-स्˚, ten thousand<BR>Yojanas long); reaching to (e. g. ललाट-स्˚, reaching<BR>to the forehead); equalized, adapted; furnished or<BR>provided with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिति|संमिति|संमितिः
सम्-मिति, इस्, f. measuring out, measuring, com-<BR>paring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मातुर|संमातुर
सम्मातुर सम्-मातुर, अस्, m. (for सन्-<BR>मातुर, q. v.), the son of a virtuous mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मातृ|संमातृ
सम्मातृ सम्-मातृ, ता, &c., having the<BR>same mother, twin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान|संमान|संमानः|सम्मानः
सम्मान 1. and 2. सम्-मान. See above<BR>and p. 1090, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्ज्
सम्मार्ज् सम्-मार्ज्. See सम्-मृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जक|संमार्जक|संमार्जकः|सम्मार्ज्जकः
सम्-मार्जक, सम्-मार्जन, &c. See under<BR>सम्-मृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मि
सम्मि सम्-मि (see rt. 1. मि), cl. 5. P. A. -मि-<BR>नोति, -मिनुते, &c., Ved. to fasten at the same time,<BR>fasten together, fix, erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिक्ष्
सम्मिक्ष् सम्-मिक्ष् or सम्-मिमिक्ष् (by<BR>some regarded as a Desid. form of सम्-मिह्, see<BR>मिक्ष्, p. 777), -मिमिक्षति, &c., to mix together,<BR>mingle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मित|संमित|संमितं|सम्मितः
सम्मित सम्-मित. See under 1. सम्-मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिल्|संमिल्
सम्मिल् सम्-मिल्, cl. 6. P. A. -मिलति, -ते,<BR>&c., to meet together, assemble together, be present,<BR>associate with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिलित
सम्-मिलित, अस्, आ, अम्, met together, assembled,<BR>collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिल्य
सम्-मिल्य, ind. having assembled or met toge-<BR>ther.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मेलन|संमेलनं
सम्-मेलन, अम्, n. the act of meeting together,<BR>assembling, union; mixing with, mixture, blending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिश्र्|संमिश्र्
सम्मिश्र् सम्-मिश्र्. See rt. मिश्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिश्र|संमिश्र|सम्मिश्रः
सम्-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, commingled, mixed<BR>together, mixed, mingled, blended, joined, con-<BR>nected, furnished or endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिश्रण|संमिश्रण
सम्-मिश्रण, अम्, n. the act of commingling<BR>or mixing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिश्रित|संमिश्रित
सम्-मिश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed together, mingled,<BR>intermixed with (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिश्ल|संमिश्लः
सम्-मिश्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, = सम्-मिश्र above; (अस्),<BR>m. ‘universal mingler,’ epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिह्
सम्मिह् सम्-मिह्, apparently cl. 3. A. (see<BR>Ṛg-veda 1. 48, 16, where the form मिमिक्ष्व<BR>occurs), Ved. to sprinkle with, shower down upon:<BR>Desid. -मिमिक्षति, to wish to mix; to mingle,<BR>unite one's self; [cf. सम्-मिक्ष् above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मील्|संमील्
सम्मील् सम्-मील्, cl. 1. P. -मीलति, &c., to<BR>close up (as a flower &c.); to shut the eyes: Caus.<BR>-मीलयति, -यितुम्, to cause to close up, close, shut;<BR>to close the eyes; to make insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मीलन|संमीलन|संमीलनं
सम्-मीलन, अम्, n. the closing up (of a flower<BR>&c.), covering up, enveloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मील्य|संमील्य
सम्-मील्य, ind., Ved. having closed up, having<BR>covered over, having enveloped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुख|संमुख|सम्मुखः
सम्मुख सम्-मुख, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, facing,<BR>fronting, being in front of, being face to face, oppo-<BR>site; confronting, meeting, encountering; looking<BR>towards, directed towards; propitious; (अम्), ind.<BR>before the face, in front of.<BR>—सम्मुख-वर्तिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, being before the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुखिन्|संमुखिन्
सम्मुखिन्, ई, m. a looking-glass, mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुखीन|संमुखीन|सम्मुखीनः
सम्मुखीन, अस्, आ, अम्, facing, being in face<BR>of, face to face, confronting, before, in front, op-<BR>posite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुच्|संमुच्
सम्मुच् सम्-मुच्, cl. 6. P. A. -मुञ्चति, -ते,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">Page1091-b+ 79</a>]<BR>मोक्तुम्, to let loose together, pour out, discharge,<BR>shed: Caus. -मोचयति, -यितुम्, to release, free,<BR>set free, liberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोचित
सम्-मोचित, अस्, आ, अम्, set free, liberated, released,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुर्छ्
सम्मुर्छ् सम्-मुर्छ्, cl. 1. P. -मूर्छति, &c.,<BR>to congeal into a fixed form, acquire density or con-<BR>sistency, become dense, thicken, coagulate; to be-<BR>come stupid or senseless, become stupefied or insen-<BR>sible; to acquire firmness or strength, grow stronger<BR>or more intense, increase, expand, become powerful:<BR>Caus. -मूर्छयति, -यितुम्, to cause to assume form<BR>or consistency, form, fashion; to stupefy, cause to<BR>faint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्छ|संमूर्छ
सम्-मूर्छ, (perhaps) thickening, augmenting,<BR>increase, expansion, spreading.<BR>—सम्मूर्छ-ज,<BR>अस्, m. grass or any gramineous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्छत्
सम्-मूर्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, becoming more<BR>intense, increasing, spreading, pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्छन|सम्मूर्च्छनं|संमूर्छन|संमूर्छनं
सम्-मूर्छन, अम्, n. the act of congealing or<BR>becoming dense; stupefaction, insensibility, fainting<BR>away; increasing or spreading in all directions,<BR>universal pervasion, entire permeation, expansion,<BR>co-extension; height, elevation.<BR>—सम्मूर्छनोद्-<BR>भव (˚न-उद्˚), अस्, m. a fish or other aquatic<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्छित|संमूर्छित
सम्-मूर्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, coagulated, congealed,<BR>thickened; stupefied, senseless, unconscious; inten-<BR>sified, increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुह्|संमुह्
सम्मुह् सम्-मुह्, cl. 4. P. -मुह्यति, &c.,<BR>to become quite stupefied or unconscious; to be<BR>bewildered or disturbed or confounded; to become<BR>unconscious: Caus. -मोहयति, -यितुम्, to stupefy,<BR>make unconscious, confound, bewilder, perplex, in-<BR>fatuate, lead astray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुग्ध|संमुग्ध
सम्-मुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied, astounded;<BR>bewildered, fascinated; beautiful; (अम्), ind. in a<BR>fascinating manner; furtively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूढ|संमूढ|सम्मूढः
सम्-मूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, completely stupefied,<BR>astounded; unconscious, senseless; bewildered, be-<BR>guiled; infatuated, foolish, ignorant; disordered,<BR>deranged; heaped, accumulated; produced rapidly;<BR>broken; (आ), f. a kind of riddle or enigma.<BR>—सम्-<BR>मूढ-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or सम्मूढ-हृदय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bewildered or infatuated in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोह|संमोह|संमोहः
सम्-मोह, अस्, m. stupefaction, bewilderment,<BR>confusion, insensibility, fainting away, swoon; in-<BR>fatuation, ignorance, folly, illusion of mind; fasci-<BR>nation, beguilement; tumult, battle, (enumerated<BR>among the सङ्ग्राम-नामानि in Naigh. II. 17;<BR>cf. समोह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोहन|संमोहन|संमोहनं|संमोहनः
सम्-मोहन, अस्, ई, अम्, stupefying, bewitching,<BR>fascinating; (अम्), n. fascinating, fascination.<BR>—सम्-<BR>मोहन-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोहयत्
सम्-मोहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, stupefying, infatuat-<BR>ing, bewildering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोहित
सम्-मोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied, bewildered,<BR>infatuated, beguiled, fascinated; enraptured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोह्य
सम्-मोह्य, ind. having fascinated or stupefied,<BR>having bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृज्|संमृज्
सम्मृज् सम्-मृज् or सम्-मार्ज् (see rts.<BR>1. मृज्, मार्ज्), cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि (sometimes<BR>cl. 1. -मार्जति, also cl. 10. P. -मार्जयति, -यितुम्),<BR>&c., to sweep together; to sweep clean, scour; to<BR>rub or wipe off, clean, cleanse, sweep, purify, wash,<BR>strain, filter; to take away, remove; to stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जक|संमार्जक|संमार्जकः|सम्मार्ज्जकः
सम्-मार्जक, अस्, m. a sweeper, purifier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जत्
सम्-मार्जत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, sweeping,<BR>cleansing, scouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जन|संमार्जन|संमार्जनं|सम्मार्ज्जनं
सम्-मार्जन, अम्, n. the act of sweeping or<BR>cleansing thoroughly; cleaning, scouring, purifying,<BR>brushing; the anointing (of images &c.); (ई), f. a<BR>broom, brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जित
सम्-मार्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, well swept or scoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्ज्य
सम्-मार्ज्य, ind. having swept clean, having<BR>scoured, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृज्यमान
सम्-मृज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being swept or<BR>cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृष्ट|संमृष्ट|सम्मृष्टः
सम्-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, well swept or scoured,<BR>cleaned, cleansed; strained, filtered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृण्
सम्मृण् सम्-मृण्, cl. 6. P. -मृणति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to kill, slay, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृत|संमृत
सम्मृत सम्-मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, quite dead,<BR>deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृद्|संमृद्
सम्मृद् सम्-मृद्, cl. 9. 1. P. -मृद्नाति,<BR>-मर्दति, &c., to press or squeeze together, rub or<BR>grind to pieces, bruise, crush, trample upon, defeat:<BR>Caus. -मर्दयति, &c., to cause to be rubbed toge-<BR>ther, &c., crush, pound, bruise; to rub; to clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्द|संमर्दः|सम्मर्द्द|सम्मर्द्दः
सम्-मर्द, अस्, m. pressing or rubbing together,<BR>friction; thronging, trampling or treading on; war,<BR>battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्दयान
सम्-मर्दयान, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbing or dashing<BR>to pieces, shattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्दित
सम्-मर्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, thoroughly bruised,<BR>crushed, pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्दिन्|संमर्दिन्|सम्मर्द्दिन्
सम्-मर्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, pressing thoroughly,<BR>rubbing, crushing, trampling upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्द्य
सम्-मर्द्य, ind. having pounded or bruised;<BR>having rubbed or cleaned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृश्
सम्मृश् सम्-मृश्, cl. 6. P. A. -मृशति, -ते,<BR>&c., to take hold of, seize, touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्शिन्|संमर्शिन्
सम्-मर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, inquiring into, deliberating<BR>about, discriminating, judicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मेलन|संमेलनं
सम्मेलन सम्-मेलन. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोक्ष्
सम्मोक्ष् सम्-मोक्ष्, cl. 10. P. -मोक्षयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to set quite free, liberate, let loose, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोद|संमोद|संमोदः|सम्मोदः
सम्मोद सम्-मोद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मुद्<BR>with सम्), great rejoicing, delight, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोह|संमोह|संमोहः
सम्मोह सम्-मोह. See under सम्-मुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्म्यक्ष्
सम्म्यक्ष् सम्-म्यक्ष्, cl. 1. P. -म्यक्षति,<BR>&c. (see rt. म्यक्ष्), Ved. to be held together or<BR>united; to be joined with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्म्रक्ष्
सम्म्रक्ष् सम्-म्रक्ष्, cl. 1. P. -म्रक्षति,<BR>&c. (see rt. म्रक्ष्), to rub on or in, anoint, em-<BR>brocate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्म्रक्षित
सम्-म्रक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed in, anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यञ्च्|सम्यंच्
सम्यञ्च् सम्य्-अञ्च् or सम्य्-अच्, अङ्, ईची, अक्<BR>(fr. an old loc. 2. समि + अञ्च्, see समि; cf.<BR>तिरि fr. तिरस् in तिर्य्-अञ्च्), going along with or<BR>together, going with, accompanying; uniform, same,<BR>identical; all, entire, whole, complete; correct, accu-<BR>rate, proper, true, right; pleasant, agreeable; (अक्),<BR>ind. at the same time, with, together; wholly, com-<BR>pletely, entirely, comprehensively, thoroughly, fully,<BR>accurately, correctly, truly, properly, fitly, in right<BR>manner, honourably; well, duly; distinctly, clearly.<BR>—सम्यक्-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make true, perform well.<BR>—सम्यक्-चारित्र,<BR>अम्, n. ‘correct conduct,’ one of the three excellent<BR>things (according to the Jainas, see रत्न-त्रय).<BR>—सम्यक्-त्व, अम्, n. completeness, correctness, ac-<BR>curacy, propriety, (क्षायिक-स्˚, that state of perfection<BR>in which material existence is destroyed.)<BR>—सम्यक्-<BR>पाठ, अस्, m. correct recitation or pronunciation.<BR>—सम्यक्-प्रयोग, अस्, m. fitting or proper use<BR>or employment, due practice; (एण), ind. by the<BR>use of proper means.<BR>—सम्यक्-प्रवृत्ति, इस्, f.<BR>the right or proper direction (of the organs).<BR>—सम्-<BR>यग्-उक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, properly or accurately said, of<BR>equal weight or authority.<BR>—सम्यग्-गमन, अम्,<BR>n. the act of going with, accompanying.<BR>—सम्यग्-<BR>गोप्तृ, ता, m. a true protector or guardian.<BR>—सम्-<BR>यग्-ज्ञान, अम्, n. ‘complete knowledge,’ one of<BR>the three jewels or excellent things (according to<BR>the Jainas, see रत्न-त्रय).<BR>—सम्यग्-दण्डन,<BR>अम्, n. the act of punishing properly or justly;<BR>punishing legally.<BR>—सम्यग्-दर्शन, अम्, n. ‘com-<BR>plete vision, accurate perception,’ one of the three<BR>jewels or excellent things (according to the Jainas,<BR>see रत्न-त्रय); (with अव्रत), epithet of the<BR>fourth of the fourteen stages leading to final emanci-<BR>pation (according to the belief of the Jainas).<BR>—सम्-<BR>यग्-वर्तमान, अस्, आ, अम्, continuing in the proper<BR>discharge of duty, &c.<BR>—सम्यग्-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">Page1092-a+ 71</a>]<BR>properly conducted; wholly confiding in.<BR>—सम्यग्-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. steady or complete practice, regular<BR>discharge of prescribed duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचीन|समीचीनं
समीचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, tending in a common<BR>direction, going with or in company with, agreeing<BR>with, concordant, consistent, convenient, fit, proper,<BR>correct, true, just, right; (अम्), n. propriety, fitness,<BR>truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्राज्
सम्राज् सम्-राज्, ट्, m. (fr. सं-राज्, Pāṇ.<BR>VIII. 3, 25), a sovereign lord, paramount sovereign,<BR>one who rules over other princes and has performed<BR>the Rājasūya sacrifice; (ट्), f. a kind of Vedic metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्राजत्
सम्-राजत्, अन्, m., Ved. = सम्-राज्, (see सं-<BR>राज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्राज्ञी
सम्राज्ञी, f., Ved. a woman who takes prece-<BR>dence, a mistress, superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सय्
सय् सय्, cl. 1. A. सयते, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सय
सय स-य, अस्, आ, अम्, with the letter य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयक्ष्मन्
सयक्ष्मन् स-यक्ष्मन्, आ, आ, अ, having or<BR>subject to consumption, consumptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयत्न
सयत्न स-यत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, making efforts,<BR>taking pains, endeavouring, persevering; active, busy;<BR>(अम्), ind. with effort, vigorously, assiduously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयन
सयन सयन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. सि), the act<BR>of binding, fastening; [cf. प्र-स्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयन्त्र
सयन्त्र स-यन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, with machines.<BR>—स-यन्त्र-जल-शैल, अस्, आ, अम्, having engines<BR>and water and a rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयावक
सयावक स-यावक, अस्, आ (according to<BR>some इका), अम्, dyed or coloured with lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयावन्
सयावन् स-यावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. going<BR>along with, attendant, attending, associated with<BR>(with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयुज्
सयुज् स-युज्, क्, m., Ved. a companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयुग्वन्
स-युग्वन्, आ, आ or अरी, अ, Ved. associated with,<BR>attending on, attendant; (आ), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयुज्य
स-युज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, closely united with.<BR>—स-<BR>युज्य-ता, f. intimate union or junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयुधिष्ठिर
सयुधिष्ठिर स-युधिष्ठिर, अस्, आ, अम्, with<BR>or accompanied by Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयूथ्य|सयूथ्यः
सयूथ्य स-यूथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to<BR>the same herd or tribe; (अस्), m. one of the same<BR>tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयोग|सयोगः
सयोग स-योग, अम्, n. (scil. गुण-स्थान),<BR>epithet of the last but one of the fourteen stages<BR>leading to final emancipation (according to the belief<BR>of the Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयोनि|सयोनिः
सयोनि स-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, having the same<BR>womb, uterine; closely related to; closely united<BR>with the womb; (इस्), m. ‘being from the same<BR>womb,’ a brother; a pair of nippers for cutting<BR>betel-nut; N. of Indra (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयोषण
सयोषण स-योषण, अस्, आ, अम्, attended<BR>by women, along with the women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर|सरं|सरः
सर सर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. सृ, cf. सल<BR>under rt. सल्), going, moving, proceeding (often at<BR>the end of comps., cf. पुरः-स्˚); cathartic, purga-<BR>tive; (अस्), m. going, motion; an arrow [cf. शर];<BR>the coagulum of curds or milk, cream, (in this sense<BR>cf. according to some, Gr. ὀρό-ς, ὀῤῤός, οὐρό-ς;<BR>Lat. seru-m; Lith. suri-s; Slav. syru); salt (pro-<BR>bably as coming from water, cf. सल, सरिर, स-<BR>लिल); a waterfall; (आ), f. going, motion, move-<BR>ment; a cascade, waterfall; the plant Pæderia<BR>Fetida; (ई), f. a cascade; (अम्), n. a lake, pool;<BR>water.<BR>—सर-ज, अम्, n. ‘produced from cream,’<BR>fresh butter.<BR>—सर-पत्त्रिका, f. the new leaf of a<BR>lotus.<BR>—सर-वती, f., N. of the river Vitastā.<BR>—स-<BR>रोत्सव (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘delighting in water,’ the<BR>Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरक|सरकं|सरकः
सरक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, going, moving, pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">Page1092-b+ 81</a>]<BR>ceeding; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a continuous line of road,<BR>spirituous liquor (especially that distilled from sugar),<BR>rum; drinking spirits; a drinking vessel, goblet;<BR>distribution of spirituous liquor; (अम्), n. going; a<BR>lake, pond, pool; heaven, sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट्
सरट्, ट्, m. air, wind; a cloud; a bee; a lizard,<BR>chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट|सरटः
सरट, अस्, m. wind; a kind of lizard or cha-<BR>meleon; [cf. शरट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटि|सरटिः
सरटि, इस्, m. air, wind; a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटु|सरटुः
सरटु, उस्, m. a lizard, chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण|सरणं
सरण, अस्, आ, अम्, going, moving, proceeding,<BR>flowing, who or what goes or moves; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of going, flowing, proceeding; iron rust or filings;<BR>(आ), f. the creeping plant Pæderia Fetida; a sort of<BR>convolvulus (= त्रि-वृता, commonly called Tëori).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरणि|सरणिः
सरणि, इस्, f. a road, path, way [cf. 2. शरणि];<BR>a straight or continuous line; the creeping plant<BR>Pæderia Fetida; a disease of the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरणी
सरणी, f. = सरणि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्ड|सरंड|सरंडः|सरण्डः
सरण्ड, अस्, m. a bird; a lizard; a rogue, cheat;<BR>a dissolute man; a sort of ornament; [cf. शरण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्य|सरण्यं
सरण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone; [cf. 2. शरण्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्यत्
सरण्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing to go; wishing<BR>to go everywhere, all-pervading, (Sāy. = सर्वत्र<BR>गमनम् इच्छत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्यु|सरण्युः
सरण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, (probably) fleet, impetuous<BR>(Ved.); (उस्), m., N. of Yama, (Sāy. = सरण-<BR>शील); of the son of Varuṇa, (in Ṛg-veda X. 61,<BR>24. said to have the form of a horse; the<BR>plural of this word is in other places applied to<BR>certain beings called Saraṇyus, who seem to be iden-<BR>tified in Ṛg-veda III. 32, 5. with the Maruts, and<BR>in I. 62, 4. with the Aṅgirasas, who are described by<BR>Sāy. as seven in number); air, wind; a cloud;<BR>water; spring (= वसन्त); fire (= अग्नि); [cf.<BR>Gr. ἐριννύς.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्यू
सरण्यू, ऊस्, f., Ved. ‘the fleet-running one,’ N.<BR>of a daughter of Tvaṣṭṛ, (in Ṛg-veda X. 17, 2.<BR>represented as wife of Vivasvat or the Sun and<BR>mother of the two Aśvins, and according to another<BR>legend, mother of the twins Yama and Yamī; ac-<BR>cording to Yāska XII. 10, Saraṇyū is a personifica-<BR>tion of the Night, and the first twins she bore were<BR>Madhyama and Mādhyamikā Vāc; she then made<BR>Sa-varṇā, q. v., take her place as wife of the Sun,<BR>and herself ran away in the form of a mare, but<BR>being pursued and embraced by the Sun in the form<BR>of a horse, then gave birth to the two Aśvins or<BR>‘horsemen,’ her substitute Sa-varṇā giving birth to<BR>Manu); epithet of the Dawn (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्
1. सरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going, flowing, proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्
2. सरत्, त्, m. a thread; [cf. सरित्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरपसस्
सरपसस्, pl., Ved. (in the Pada-pāṭha sepa-<BR>rated into सर अपसः), the flowing waters, (Sāy.<BR>= सरणम् अपः कर्म यासां ताः, those waters<BR>whose act is flowing, Ṛg-veda II. 13, 12.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरमा
सरमा, f. (probably fr. rt. सृ), ‘the runner,’<BR>N. of the dog of Indra (represented in Ṛg-veda X.<BR>14, 10. as the mother of the four-eyed brindled dogs<BR>of Yama, and called in Mahā-bhārata Ādi-p. 671.<BR>देव-शुनी; in the Ṛg-veda this dog is said to<BR>have gone in search of and recovered the cows stolen<BR>by the Paṇis; according to some modern scholars<BR>Saramā may be one of the names of उषस्, ‘Dawn,’<BR>the cows representing the rays of the sun stolen by<BR>the night; the name Saramā is also thought to cor-<BR>respond with Helena; and Sārameya, q. v., is regarded<BR>as connected with Hermes, Saramā being by some<BR>identified with the Wind, as conductor of the souls<BR>of the departed; Saramā Deva-śunī is said to be the<BR>authoress of part of Ṛg-veda X. 108); a female<BR>dog, bitch; N. of the wife of Vibhīṣaṇa (Rāvaṇa's<BR>brother); of a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of<BR>Kaśyapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयु|सरयुः
सरयु, उस्, m. air, wind; (उस्), f., N. of a well-<BR>known river (commonly called by the various names<BR>Surjoo, Surju, Sirjoo, Seryu; it is a tributary of the<BR>Ghogra [see घर्घर] on which stands the<BR>ancient city of Ayodhyā or Oude, cf. Rāmāyaṇa I.<BR>5, 6; in Ṛg-veda X. 64, 9, X. 75, 5. it is men-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-c" target="_blank">Page1092-c+ 81</a>]<BR>tioned along with the other well-known rivers Saras-<BR>vatī, Sindhu, Gaṅgā, Yamunā, and Śutu-dri).<BR>—स-<BR>रयु-तट, अस्, अम्, m. n. the bank of the Sarayu;<BR>N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयू
सरयू, ऊस्, f., N. of a river (= सरयु above).<BR>—सरयू-वन, अम्, n. a forest on the river Sarayū.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरल|सरलः
सरल, अस्, आ, अम्, straight, not crooked, direct,<BR>right, honest, sincere, candid, artless, simple, upright<BR>[cf. शरल]; (अस्), m. a species of pine tree, Pinus<BR>Longifolia; a kind of bird, Pavo Bicalcarata; a<BR>Buddha; fire; (आ), f. a kind of convolvulus (= त्रि-<BR>पुटा); N. of a river.<BR>—सरल-काष्ठ, अम्, n.<BR>the wood of the pine.<BR>—सरल-द्रव, अस्, m. the<BR>exudation of the Sarala pine; a fragrant resin.<BR>—स-<BR>रल-यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going in a straight line;<BR>upright, honest; (इनी), f. a plant with an upright stem.<BR>—सरल-स्कन्ध-सङ्घट्ट-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>originating in the friction of the trunks of pines.<BR>—सरलाङ्ग (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, m. the exudation of<BR>the Sarala pine, resin, turpentine.<BR>—सरला-भाष्य,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Bhāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरव्य|सरव्यं
सरव्य, अम्, n. (fr. सर, an arrow), a mark for<BR>shooting at, target, butt; [cf. शरव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्
सरस्, अस्, n. (originally perhaps ‘flowing water’),<BR>water; a lake, large sheet of water, pond, pool; any<BR>piece of water in which the lotus grows, (in Naigh.<BR>1. 12. enumerated among the उदक-नामानि, and<BR>in 1. 11. among the वाङ्-नामानि); [cf. Old Norse<BR>sir, sœr, sior; Angl. Sax. sirendœ.]<BR>—सरः-<BR>काक, अस्, m. ‘water-crow,’ a gander; (ई), f. a<BR>goose.<BR>—सरसि-ज, अम्, n. ‘pond-born,’ a lotus.<BR>—सरसि-रुह, अम्, n. ‘growing in a pond,’ a<BR>lotus.<BR>—सरसिरुह-जन्मन्, आ, m. ‘born from<BR>a lotus,’ epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—सरसी-रुह, अम्, n.<BR>‘pool-growing,’ a lotus.<BR>—सरस्-तीर, अम्, n. the<BR>bank of a lake or pond.<BR>—सरस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>‘having water,’ watery, fluid, juicy, sapid; elegant;<BR>sentimental; (आन्), m. the ocean; a male river; N.<BR>of a river-god, (in Ṛg-veda VII. 96, 4-6. assigned<BR>as a consort to Sarasvatī, see below); N. of Vāyu,<BR>(according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 95, 3 =<BR>मध्य-स्थानो वयुः); a buffalo; (अती), f., N.<BR>of the goddess of speech and learning, (in the later<BR>mythology regarded as the wife or female energy of<BR>the god Brahmā or first deity of the Hindū triad<BR>[see ब्रह्मन्], and sometimes identified with Vāc,<BR>q. v., and invoked as a kind of muse or patroness of<BR>science and inventress of the Sanskrit language and<BR>letters; in the earliest mythology she was probably<BR>a river-deity, her name signifying ‘watery;’ according<BR>to Yāska [Nirukta II. 23] she was regarded both as<BR>a river and as a goddess; probably this river was to<BR>the earlier Hindūs what the Ganges [said to be only<BR>twice named in the Ṛg-veda] was to the later;<BR>sacrifices were doubtless performed on its banks, and<BR>its sanctity imparted a sacred character to the district<BR>lying between its waters and those of the Dṛṣad-<BR>vatī [see Manu II. 17]; hence the river Sarasvatī<BR>was not only personified as a river-goddess, but her<BR>assistance was invoked at the sacrifices performed<BR>near her flowing waters and her influence held to<BR>be necessary for inspiring the Ṛṣis who composed<BR>the sacrificial hymns with eloquence and wisdom; in<BR>Ṛg-veda II. 41, 16. she is called the best of mothers,<BR>of rivers, and of goddesses; in other places she is<BR>described as bestowing wealth, fertility, and offspring,<BR>as moving along a golden path, as destroying Vṛtra,<BR>as associated with the Aśvins, and even as the wife<BR>of Indra; in Ṛg-veda VI. 61, 10-12, VII. 36, 6.<BR>she is called the mother of rivers, and is said to be<BR>sevenfold or to have seven sisters; in Mahā-bhārata,<BR>Śalya-parvan 2189, seven Sarasvatīs are also men-<BR>tioned, viz. Su-prabhā, Kāñcanākṣī, Viśālā, Mano-<BR>ramā, Ogha-vatī, Su-reṇu, and Vimalodakā; in the<BR>Śānti-parvan 12920, Sarasvatī is called the mother<BR>of the Vedas, which is also elsewhere said of Vāc,<BR>though Vāc in the earlier mythology is regarded as<BR>a separate deity; according to later legends the<BR>goddess Sarasvatī was persuaded to descend from<BR>heaven and confer her invention of language and<BR>letters on the human race by the sage Bharata,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-a" target="_blank">Page1093-a+ 81</a>]<BR>whence one of her names is Bhāratī; she is some-<BR>times represented as assuming the form of a Haṃsa<BR>or swan, and is also called Mahā-śvetā or Mahā-<BR>śuklā from her extreme whiteness); N. of a cele-<BR>brated river (held very sacred by the Hindūs and in<BR>the earlier mythology mixed up with the goddess<BR>[see above]; it corresponds with the modern Sur-<BR>sooty, which rises in the mountains bounding the<BR>north-east part of the province of Delhi, and running<BR>in a south-westerly direction becomes lost in the<BR>sands of the great desert; this river formerly marked<BR>one of the boundaries of the region called Ārya-deśa,<BR>and of a particularly sacred district called in Manu<BR>II. 17. Brahmāvarta; in Ṛg-veda VII. 95, 2. it is<BR>represented as flowing into the sea, although later<BR>legends make it disappear underground and join the<BR>Ganges and Jumnā at Allahabad, see त्रि-वेणी, प्र-<BR>याग); a river (in general); speech, voice, eloquence,<BR>literary composition; a cow (= गो); N. of Durgā;<BR>an excellent woman; N. of the wife of a Manu;<BR>of the wife of Maṇḍana (see मण्डन-मिश्र); a<BR>female divinity peculiar to the Buddhists or Jainas;<BR>the moon-plant Asclepias Acida (= सोम-लता, ब्राह्-<BR>मी); N. of another plant (= ज्योतिष्-मती); N.<BR>of a celebrated grammarian, (in this and the follow-<BR>ing senses masc.); N. of various learned men.<BR>—सरस्वती-कण्ठाभरण (˚ठ-आभ्˚), N. of<BR>a work on the art of poetry by Bhoja-deva.<BR>—स-<BR>रस्वती-कुटुम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—सरस्वती-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सरस्वती-पू-<BR>जन, अम्, n. or सरस्वती-पूजा, f. the worship of<BR>Sarasvatī (observed on the fifth of the light half<BR>of the month Māgha, on which day books and im-<BR>plements are held sacred and not allowed to be used).<BR>—सरस्वती-प्रयोग, अस्, m. a kind of mystical<BR>rite peculiar to the Tāntrikas.<BR>—सरस्वती-मन्त्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a hymn to Sarasvatī.<BR>—सरस्वती-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular religious observance.<BR>—सरस्वती-सरस्, अस्, n., N. of a sacred lake.<BR>—सरस्वती-सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>hymn.<BR>—सरस्वती-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of particular<BR>grammatical aphorisms.<BR>—सरस्वती-स्तव, अस्, m.<BR>or सरस्वती-स्तोत्र, अम्, n., N. of a hymn.<BR>—सरो-<BR>ज, अम्, n. ‘lake-born,’ a lotus; (अस्), m. a prosodial<BR>foot containing six long syllables (according to some).<BR>—सरो-जन्मन्, अ, n. ‘lake-born,’ a lotus.<BR>—सरो-<BR>जल, अम्, n. the water of a pond or lake.<BR>—सरोजिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, having lotuses; (ई), m. epithet of Brahmā;<BR>(इनी), f. a pond abounding in lotuses; a multitude<BR>of lotuses; a lotus.<BR>—सरो-रक्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>guardian of a pool.<BR>—सरो-रुह्, ट्, or सरो-रुह,<BR>अम्, n. ‘pond-growing,’ a lotus.<BR>—सरोरुहासन<BR>(˚ह-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘sitting on a lotus,’ epithet of<BR>Brahmā (as having appeared first from the interior<BR>of a lotus springing from the navel of Viṣṇu in<BR>order to create the world).<BR>—सरो-रुहिणी, f. ‘pond-<BR>growing,’ a lotus.<BR>—सरो-वर, अस्, m. a lake, large<BR>pond, any piece of water deep enough for the lotus<BR>to grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
1. सरस, अम्, n. (for 2. see col. 2), a tank,<BR>pond, lake, (also a substitute for सरस् at the end of a<BR>comp.); alchemy; (आ), f. a sort of white convolvulus<BR>(= श्वेत-त्रिवृता).<BR>—सरस-वाणी, f. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिक|सरसिकः
सरसिक or सरसीक, अस्, m. the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसी
सरसी, f. a lake, large pond or sheet of water;<BR>N. of a species of metre.<BR>—सरसी-रुह, अम्, n.<BR>‘pond-growing,’ a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरि|सरिः
सरि, इस्, m. a cascade, waterfall; [cf. सर, सरी.]<BR>—सरि-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिका
सरिका, f. the act of going or proceeding; a<BR>woman going or moving [cf. सरक]; a particular<BR>drug (= हिङ्गु-पत्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्
सरित्, त्, f. a stream, river; a thread, string; a<BR>particular species of metre.<BR>—सरितां-वरा, f. ‘best<BR>of rivers,’ the Ganges.<BR>—सरितान्-नाथ, अस्, or<BR>सरिताम्-पति or सरित्-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of rivers,’<BR>the ocean.<BR>—सरित्-वत्, आन्, m. ‘possessed of rivers,’<BR>the ocean.<BR>—सरित्-सुत, अस्, m. ‘river-son,’ epithet<BR>of Bhīṣma (son of Gaṅgā).<BR>—सरिद्-भर्तृ, ता, m.<BR>‘river-lord,’ the ocean; a symbolical term for the<BR>number four, (see 1. सम्-उद्र, p. 1079).<BR>—सरिद्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">Page1093-b+ 70</a>]<BR>वधू, ऊस्, f. ‘river-woman,’ a woman-like river.<BR>—सरिद्-वरा, f. ‘best of rivers,’ the Ganges.<BR>—सरिन्-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘river-lord,’ the ocean.<BR>—सरिन्-मरु-वनाश्रय (˚न-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>protected by a wood, desert, and river.<BR>—सरिन्-<BR>मुख, अम्, n. the source of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिन्
सरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. going, moving, one who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिमन्
सरिमन् or सरीमन्, आ, m. going, moving, pro-<BR>ceeding; air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिर
सरिर, अम्, n., Ved. = सलिल, water, the ocean,<BR>(enumerated among the बहु-नामानि in Naigh.<BR>III. 1); the universe (= लोक, लोक-त्रय, according<BR>to Mahīdhara on Vājasaneyi-s. XV. 52, XVII. 87).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित|सरितः
सरित, अम्, n. = सलिल, water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्म|सर्मः|सर्म्म
सर्म, अस्, m. going, running; sky; heaven;<BR>[cf. Gr. ὁρμή.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरक्तगौर
सरक्तगौर स-रक्त-गौर, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>of a red and whitish colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरघा
सरघा सरघा, f. (said to be fr. सर, ‘a<BR>goer,’ and rt. हन्), a bee, (apparently also अम्, n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरङ्ग|सरंग|सरंगः|सरङ्गः
सरङ्ग स-रङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having colour;<BR>having a nasal sound; (अस्), m. a quadruped; a bird;<BR>[cf. सारङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरङ्गक
सरङ्गक सरङ्गक, a species of the Atiśak-<BR>varī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजत्|सरजन्त्
सरजत् स-रजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. rt. रञ्ज्<BR>with स for सह), Ved. colouring or tinging at the<BR>same time, (Sāy. = सह-रजत्, Ṛg-veda X. 115, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजस्
सरजस् स-रजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having dust or<BR>dirt or impurity; (आस्), f. a woman during menstru-<BR>ation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजस
स-रजस, अस्, आ, अम्, having dirt or impurity of<BR>any kind; (अम्), ind., see Vopa-deva VI. 60.<BR>—स-<BR>रजस-ता, f. dirtiness, dustiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजस्क
स-रजस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, = स-रजस above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटक
सरटक सरटक, अस्, m., N. of a mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण|सरणं
सरण सरण, &c. See p. 1092, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्यु|सरण्युः
सरण्यु, &c. See p. 1092, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्नि|सरत्निः
सरत्नि सरत्नि, इस्, m. f. a kind of cubit mea-<BR>sure (= रत्नि); a short cubit (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरथ|सरथः
सरथ स-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a car or<BR>chariot, possessing a carriage; riding in the same<BR>car; (अस्), m. a warrior or Kṣatriya (as riding in<BR>a chariot).<BR>—स-रथ-पादात, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by or along with chariots and infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरद्वत्
सरद्वत् सरद्-वत् = शरद्-वत्, p. 994.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभ
सरभ सरभ, a species of the Atiśakvarī<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभक
सरभक, (probably) a kind of animal or insect;<BR>[cf. शरभ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभस
सरभस स-रभस, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>speed or impetuosity, impetuous, speedy, quick;<BR>agitated, passionate; delighted; (अम्), ind. im-<BR>petuously, with great speed, hurriedly, hastily, pas-<BR>sionately, delightedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरमा
सरमा सरमा. See p. 1092, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरशन
सरशन स-रशन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>girdle, girdled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरषट्ट
सरषट्ट सरषट्ट, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
सरस 2. स-रस, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see<BR>col. 1), tasty, juicy, succulent, sapid; fresh, new;<BR>beautiful, charming, excellent; agreeable; expressive<BR>of poetical sentiment, (see रस); impassioned, enrap-<BR>tured; (अम्), ind. with rapture.<BR>—सरसाङ्गयष्टि<BR>(˚स-अङ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, one whose delicate body is wet<BR>with perspiration, (see under 2. यष्टि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसम्प्रत|सरसंप्रत|सरसम्प्रतं
सरसम्प्रत सरसम्प्रत, अम्, n. a sort of<BR>Euphorbia (= त्रि-कण्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरहस्य
सरहस्य स-रहस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>anything secret or mystical, magical, mystical; having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">Page1093-c+ 67</a>]<BR>the secret or mystical doctrine (of the Upaniṣads,<BR>see Manu. II. 140); along with the Upaniṣads or<BR>esoteric part of Vedic teaching.<BR>—स-रहस्य-व्रत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, possessing mystical spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराग
सराग स-राग, अस्, आ, अम्, having colour,<BR>coloured, tinted; having passion, passionate, impas-<BR>sioned.<BR>—सराग-ता, f. the being coloured with red.<BR>—सराग-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, red-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराजक
सराजक स-राजक, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>a king; along with the king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराट
सराट सराट, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराति
सराति स-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. accompanied<BR>with presents or wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराव|सरावः
सराव सराव, अस्, m. (for शराव, q. v.),<BR>a lid, cover; a shallow cup, saucer, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराष्ट्र
सराष्ट्र स-राष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing a<BR>kingdom; along with the kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराष्ट्रक
स-राष्ट्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, = स-राष्ट्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराहु
सराहु स-राहु, उस्, उस्, उ, possessed or held<BR>by Rāhu, q. v.; eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरि|सरिः
सरि सरि, सरित्, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिर
सरिर सरिर, सरिल. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिषप|सरिषपः
सरिषप सरिषप, अस्, m. = सर्षप, mus-<BR>tard, Sinapis Dichotoma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरीसृप|सरीसृपः
सरीसृप सरीसृप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. सृप्), crawling, creeping; (अस्), m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरु|सरुः
सरु सरु, उस्, उस्, उ (probably to be con-<BR>nected with rt. सृ, cf. rt. त्सर्), minute, thin, fine,<BR>small; (उस्), m. = त्सरु, the hilt or handle of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरुज्
सरुज् स-रुज्, क्, क्, क्, or स-रुज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>suffering pain or sickness, sick, ill, diseased; [cf. per-<BR>haps Goth. saurga.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोग
स-रोग, अस्, आ, अम्, affected with disease, sick,<BR>diseased.<BR>—सरोग-ता, f. or सरोग-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>sickliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोगिन्
सरोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, diseased, sick.<BR>—सरोगि-ता, f.<BR>sickliness, sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरुष्
सरुष् स-रुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, feeling anger, angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूप|सरूपः
सरूप स-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, of the same<BR>shape, like, similar, resembling, having shape, shaped,<BR>formed.<BR>—सरूप-ता, f. or सरूप-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>identity of form, likeness, resemblance, assimilation<BR>to the deity, (one of the four states into which<BR>मुक्ति, q. v., is distinguished.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरेफ
सरेफ स-रेफ, अस्, आ, अम्, together with<BR>the letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोग
सरोग सरोग, &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोज|सरोजं|सरोजः
सरोज सरो-ज, सरोजिन्, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोत्सव|सरोत्सवः
सरोत्सव सरोत्सव. See under सर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोध|सरोधः
सरोध स-रोध, अस्, आ, अम्, having hin-<BR>drance or obstruction or opposition; having destruc-<BR>tion or loss; (अस्), m. obstruction, opposition (ac-<BR>cording to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोम
सरोम स-रोम, अस्, आ, अम्, having hair,<BR>hairy.<BR>—स-रोम-कण्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, having hair<BR>bristling with ecstasy.<BR>—स-रोम-विक्रिय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, thrilling with ecstasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोष
सरोष स-रोष, अस्, आ, अम्, full of anger,<BR>angry, wrathful; (अम्), ind. with anger, angrily.<BR>—सरोष-रागोपहत (˚ग-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>suffused with a flush of anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्क|सर्कः
सर्क सर्क, अस्, m. (according to Śabda-k.),<BR>wind, air, (probably fr. rt. सृ); the mind; N. of<BR>Prajā-pati, (perhaps for सर्ग below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ग|सर्गः
सर्ग सर्ग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. सृज्), letting<BR>go, relinquishment, abandonment; loss of conscious-<BR>ness, fainting (= मोह); voiding (as excrement<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">Page1094-a+ 80</a>]<BR>&c.); letting loose; creation, the creation of the<BR>world, (in Bhāgavata-Purāṇa III. 10, 13, &c. nine<BR>different creations are enumerated, viz. 1. Mahat or<BR>intellect; 2. Aham or personality; 3. Tan-mātra,<BR>the subtile, with the five grosser elements [see तन्-<BR>मात्र]; 4. Indriya or organs; 5. Vaikārika or<BR>Deva-sarga, which also comprises Manas or mind;<BR>6. Tamas or darkness; 7. Tasthuṣāṃ Sarga or<BR>creation of stationary creatures, such as tress, plants,<BR>&c., which are said to be उत्-स्रोतस्, having the flow<BR>or current of life upwards, cf. ऊर्ध्व-स्रोतस्;<BR>8. Tiraścāṃ Sarga or creation of animals, cf. तिर्यक्-<BR>स्रोतस्; 9. Nṛṇāṃ Sarga or creation of men, which<BR>is said to be अर्वाक्-स्रोतस्, q. v.); nature, the<BR>universe; natural property, disposition, tendency;<BR>onset, advance, motion, rush; a troop of horses let<BR>loose (Ved.); a horse, (Sāy. = अश्व); effort, reso-<BR>lution, determination, resolve, will, perseverance;<BR>a chapter, book, section, canto; assent, agreement;<BR>ascertainment, certainty; epithet of Śiva; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., Ved. a stream of water (= उदक, Naigh. I.<BR>12).<BR>—सर्ग-क्रम, अस्, m. the order of creation.<BR>—सर्ग-तक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. set in motion,<BR>(Sāy. = गमने प्रवृत्त.)<BR>—सर्ग-प्रतक्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. urged on to impetuous motion, (Sāy.<BR>= विसर्जनेन प्रगमित.)<BR>—सर्ग-बन्ध, अस्,<BR>m. ‘chapter-composition,’ a Mahā-kāvya or great<BR>poem; any work or book comprising several sections<BR>or chapters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज|सर्जः|सर्ज्ज|सर्ज्जः
सर्ज, अस्, m. the Śāl tree, Shorea Robusta (=<BR>शाल); another tree (= पीत-शाल); the resinous<BR>exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR>—सर्ज-गन्धा, f. a<BR>particular plant (= रास्ना).<BR>—सर्ज-निर्यासक, अस्,<BR>or सर्ज-मणि, इस्, or सर्ज-रस, अस्, m. the resi-<BR>nous exudation of the Śāl tree; resin (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जक|सर्जकः|सर्ज्जक|सर्ज्जकः
सर्जक, अस्, m. the Śāl tree; another tree (=<BR>पीत-शाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जन|सर्जनं|सर्ज्जन|सर्ज्जनं
सर्जन, अम्, n. the act of letting go or letting<BR>loose, abandonment, quitting; voiding (excrement<BR>&c.); the reserve or rear of an army; the act of<BR>creating, creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जि|सर्जिः|सर्ज्जि|सर्ज्जिः
सर्जि, इस्, f. natron, (see below.)<BR>—सर्जि-क्षार,<BR>अस्, m. = सर्जि, (also written स्वर्जि-क्षार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जिका|सर्ज्जिका
सर्जिका, f. natron, impure alkali or carbonate of<BR>soda (used in India instead of soap for cleaning linen<BR>&c.).<BR>—सर्जिका-क्षार, अस्, m. natron, (also written<BR>स्वर्जिका-क्षार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जी|सर्ज्जी
सर्जी, f. = सर्जि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्|सर्ज्ज्
सर्ज् सर्ज् [cf. rt. 1. अर्ज्], cl. 1. P. सर्जति,<BR>सर्जितुम्, to earn by labour, acquire, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जू|सर्ज्जू
सर्जू, ऊस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. I. 82. said to be fr. rt.<BR>सर्ज् above, but probably to be connected with rt.<BR>1. सृज्, cf. सर्ज above), a merchant, trader; (ऊस्),<BR>f. lightning; a necklace; going, following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प|सर्पः
सर्प सर्प, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सृप्), a creeping<BR>or serpentine or tortuous motion, creeping, moving<BR>gently, gliding, sliding, twining; going, flowing; a<BR>snake, serpent; a particular tree (= नाग-केशर);<BR>a particular tribe of Mlecchas or barbarians who<BR>were formerly Kṣatriyas (mentioned in the twenty-<BR>fourth chapter of the Hari-vaṃśa, and described as<BR>wearing beards); N. of a particular Rudra; (ई), f. a<BR>female snake; N. of the wife of a Rudra; [cf. Gr.<BR>ἑρπ-ετό-ν; Lat. serpens.]<BR>—सर्प-ऋषि, इस्, m.<BR>‘serpent-Ṛṣi,’ epithet of Arbuda Kādraveya.<BR>—सर्-<BR>प-कङ्कालिका or सर्प-कङ्काली, f. ‘serpent's ske-<BR>leton,’ N. of a particular medicinal plant and antidote<BR>(= विष-नाशिनी).<BR>—सर्प-गन्धा, f. a particular<BR>plant (species not known).<BR>—सर्प-घातिनी, f. a<BR>variety of the Sarpa-kaṅkālī plant.<BR>—सर्प-चीर-<BR>निवासन, अस्, m. ‘clothed in a serpent's skin,’<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्प-च्छत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘serpent-<BR>umbrella,’ a mushroom.<BR>—सर्प-तृण, अस्, m. a<BR>mungoose or ichneumon.<BR>—सर्प-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of a snake.<BR>—सर्पत्व-सम्भावना, f.<BR>imagination of being a snake, mistaking for a snake.<BR>—सर्प-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m. a snake's fang; a kind<BR>of plant, = दन्ती; (आ), f. the shrub Tragia Involu-<BR>crata.<BR>—सर्प-दंष्ट्रिका, f. a kind of shrub (=<BR>अज-शृङ्गी).<BR>—सर्प-दण्डा, f. a kind of plant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-b" target="_blank">Page1094-b+ 81</a>]<BR>= सैंहली; (ई), f. another plant (= गो-रक्षी).<BR>—सर्प-दन्ती, f. a species of sunflower (= नाग-<BR>दन्ती).<BR>—सर्प-दमनी, f. a kind of medicinal<BR>plant (= बन्ध्या-कर्कोटकी).<BR>—सर्प-धारक,<BR>अस्, m. a snake-catcher, snake-charmer.<BR>—सर्प-<BR>नामा, f. a variety of the Sarpa-kaṅkālī plant.<BR>—सर्प-पुष्पी, f. a species of sunflower (= नाग-<BR>दन्ती).<BR>—सर्प-फण-ज, अस्, m. ‘produced in a<BR>snake's hood,’ the snake-stone (a gem or pearl said<BR>to be found in a snake's head and to resemble the<BR>berry of the Abrus Precatorius).<BR>—सर्प-बलि, इस्,<BR>m. an offering of rice to serpents.<BR>—सर्प-भुज्, क्,<BR>m. ‘snake-eater,’ a peacock; a crane; a large snake.<BR>—सर्प-मणि, इस्, m. ‘snake-gem,’ the snake-<BR>stone, a kind of carbuncle (said to be found in a<BR>snake's head and to have the power of expelling<BR>poison).<BR>—सर्प-माला, f. a variety of the Sarpa-<BR>kaṅkālī plant.<BR>—सर्प-राज, अस्, m. ‘serpent-king,’<BR>epithet of Vāsuki (sovereign of the serpent-race in-<BR>habiting Pātāla).<BR>—सर्प-लता, f. = नाग-वल्ली.<BR>—सर्प-विद्, त्, m. one who understands serpents,<BR>a serpent-charmer.<BR>—सर्प-विद्या, f. serpent-science,<BR>a particular Veda; the charming of serpents.<BR>—सर्-<BR>प-विष-प्रतिषेध, अस्, m. the keeping off or<BR>expelling of snake-poison.<BR>—सर्प-वेद, N. of a<BR>work on serpents or their influence.<BR>—सर्प-व्यापा-<BR>दन, अम्, n. the killing of serpents; being killed by<BR>a snake.<BR>—सर्प-शिरस्, आस्, m. (scil. हस्त), ‘ser-<BR>pent-headed,’ epithet of a particular position of the<BR>hands.<BR>—सर्प-सत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘serpent-sacrifice,’ a<BR>particular sacrifice for the destruction of serpents.<BR>—सर्प-सत्त्रिन्, ई, m. ‘performer of a snake-<BR>sacrifice,’ epithet of king Janam-ejaya (son of Parī-<BR>kṣit; a legend relates that in order to revenge the<BR>death of his father, who was killed by the bite of a<BR>snake, he compelled, by means of Mantras, the whole<BR>serpent-race to be present at a sacrifice, where they<BR>were all destroyed except a few of the chiefs).<BR>—सर्प-सहा, f. a variety of the plant Sarpa-<BR>kaṅkālī.<BR>—सर्प-सात्, ind. to a snake or serpent.<BR>—सर्प-हन्, आ, m. ‘snake-killer,’ an ichneumon,<BR>mungoose.<BR>—सर्पाक्ष (˚प-अक्˚), अम्, n. ‘ser-<BR>pent-eye,’ the seed of the Elæocarpus; (ई), f. the<BR>plant Sarpa-kaṅkālī; another plant (= गन्ध-<BR>नाकुली); another plant (= नाडी-कलापक).<BR>—सर्-<BR>पाख्य (˚प-आख्˚), अस्, m. ‘serpent-named,’ a kind<BR>of Mahiṣa-kanda, q. v.; the plant Mesua Ferrea<BR>(= नाग-केशर).<BR>—सर्पाङ्गी (˚प-अङ्˚), f. ‘ser-<BR>pent-limbed,’ a variety of the plant Sarpa-kaṅkālī;<BR>another plant.<BR>—सर्पादनी (˚प-अद्˚), f. a parti-<BR>cular plant (= नाकुली).<BR>—सर्पाराति (˚प-अर्˚) or<BR>सर्पारि (˚प-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of snakes,’ an<BR>ichneumon; a peacock; the bird Garuḍa.<BR>—सर्पा-<BR>वलि (˚प-आव्˚), इस्, f. a row of serpents.<BR>—सर्पा-<BR>वास (˚प-आव्˚), अस्, m. the abode of a serpent;<BR>(अम्), n. the Sandal tree or wood.<BR>—सर्पाशन<BR>(˚प-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘snake-eater,’ a peacock.<BR>—सर्-<BR>पीष्ट (˚पी-इष्˚), अम्, n. ‘liked by female snakes,’<BR>the Sandal tree or wood.<BR>—सर्पेश्वर (˚प-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘lord of serpents,’ epithet of Vāsuki (sovereign<BR>of the serpent-race).<BR>—सर्पेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सर्पेष्ट (˚प-इष्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘serpent-loved,’ the Sandal tree or wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पण|सर्पणं|सर्प्पण
सर्पण, अम्, n. the act of creeping or gliding;<BR>going tortuously; the flight of an arrow nearly<BR>parallel with the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पत्|सर्प्पत्
सर्पत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, gliding, creeping, sliding,<BR>slipping, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिन्
सर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going gently or tortuously,<BR>creeping, gliding, winding, sliding, slipping, twin-<BR>ing, moving; (इणी), f. a female serpent; a small<BR>medicinal shrub (= भुज-गी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिस्
सर्पिस्, इस्, n. clarified butter, ghee, (in Naigh. I.<BR>12. enumerated among the उदक-नामानि.)<BR>—सर्-<BR>पिर्-आसुति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. sacrificed or worshipped<BR>with butter; (इस्), m. epithet of Agni.<BR>—सर्पिष्-<BR>कुण्डिका, f. a butter-jar.<BR>—सर्पिष्-टर, more com-<BR>pletely clarified butter, more or most excellent ghee.<BR>—सर्पिष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of ghee,<BR>seasoned with clarified butter.<BR>—सर्पिष्-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, containing ghee, dressed with butter.<BR>—सर्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-c" target="_blank">Page1094-c+ 78</a>]<BR>पिस्-समुद्र, अस्, m. the sea of clarified butter (one<BR>of the seven seas, see 1. सम्-उद्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्|सर्ब्ब्
सर्ब् सर्ब् (also written सम्ब्), cl. 1. P.<BR>सर्बति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्म|सर्मः|सर्म्म
सर्म सर्म. See under सर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्|सर्व्व्
सर्व् सर्व् (= rt. शर्व्), cl. 1. P. सर्वति,<BR>&c., to hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व|सर्वः|सर्व्व|सर्व्वः
सर्व सर्व, अस्, आ, अम् (in Uṇādi-s. 1. 153.<BR>said to be fr. rt. सृ, ‘to go,’ ‘pervade,’ this rt.<BR>having also, according to some, the meaning ‘to be<BR>strong or whole,’ cf. सार; according to others fr.<BR>सत्र for सत्रा, q. v., व being affixed; dat. sing.<BR>सर्वस्मै, nom. pl. सर्वे, &c., this declension<BR>being the model for a whole series of pronominals,<BR>see Gram. 237), all, every; whole, entire, universal,<BR>complete; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; of Viṣṇu;<BR>of a Muni, (सर्वम् is enumerated among the<BR>उदक-नामानि in Naigh. 1. 12); [cf. Gr. ὅλ-ο-ς,<BR>ὁλο-ό-ς, οὖλ-ο-ς: Osk. sol-lu-s (for sol-vu-s),<BR>‘whole, sound:’ Lat. sar-c-ire, sal-vu-s, sal-u-s,<BR>sal-u-ber, sol-u-m, sol-i-du-s, sol-ari, sol-amen,<BR>soll-ennis, ‘yearly;’ soll-ers: (perhaps also) Goth.<BR>alls: Hib. uile, ‘all, every, whole.’]<BR>—सर्वं-<BR>सह, अस्, आ, अम्, all-sustaining, all-bearing; patient,<BR>enduring; (आ), f. the earth.<BR>—सर्व-कर, अस्, m.<BR>‘maker of all,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-कर्तृ, ता,<BR>m. ‘maker or creator of all,’ epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—सर्व-कर्मन्, अ, n. every act; (आ), m. one<BR>who performs all acts; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>कर्मीण, अस्, आ, अम्, performing every act; per-<BR>vading every action, &c.<BR>—सर्व-काम, अस्, m.<BR>every wish; epithet of Śiva; N. of a king.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>काम-द, अस्, m. ‘granting all desires,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-काम-वर, अस्, m. ‘best of all ob-<BR>jects of desire,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-काम-<BR>समृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, amply stocked with all<BR>desired objects, fulfilling every desire.<BR>—सर्व-का-<BR>मिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having every pleasure, having all<BR>desired objects, fulfilling all wishes.<BR>—सर्व-काम्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, to be wished for by every one, having<BR>everything one can wish.<BR>—सर्व-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>making or doing all things; (ई), m. the maker of<BR>all things.<BR>—सर्व-काल, अम्, ind. for all seasons, at<BR>all times.<BR>—सर्व-काल-प्रसाद, अस्, m. ‘pro-<BR>pitious at all seasons,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>कालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to all times or seasons,<BR>perpetual.<BR>—सर्व-केशिन्, ई, m. a dancer, actor, (per-<BR>haps for सर्व-वेशिन्, q. v.)<BR>—सर्व-क्षत्रिय-<BR>मर्दन, अस्, m. the destroyer of all the Kṣatriyas<BR>or men of the military tribe.<BR>—सर्व-क्षार, अस्,<BR>m. ‘universal alkali,’ impure carbonate of soda or<BR>potash, natron (used as a soap for cleaning clothes;<BR>= महा-क्षार).<BR>—सर्व-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going<BR>everywhere, all-pervading, ubiquitous; (अस्), m.<BR>spirit, soul; epithet of Śiva; of Brahmā; N. of a<BR>son of Paurṇamāsa; of a son of Bhīma; (अम्), n.<BR>water; (आ), f. the Priyaṅgu plant.<BR>—सर्व-गण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having all kinds or classes, of every<BR>kind.<BR>—सर्व-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, going everywhere,<BR>universally diffused, all-pervading, omnipresent.<BR>—सर्-<BR>वगत-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of going every-<BR>where, omnipresence.<BR>—सर्व-गन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>‘having all perfumes,’ a class of four aromatic sub-<BR>stances (viz. Kakkola, Lavaṅga or cloves, Aguru or<BR>agallochum, and Sihlaka or olibanum); any perfume.<BR>—सर्व-गन्ध-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, conveying all<BR>perfumes or scents.<BR>—सर्व-गुण-सम्पन्न, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, endued with every excellence, gifted with<BR>every good quality.<BR>—सर्व-गुणोपेत (˚ण-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with every good quality.<BR>—सर्व-गुह्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made up of all<BR>mysteries.<BR>—सर्व-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. or सर्व-ग्रन्-<BR>थिक, अम्, n. ‘all-knotted,’ the root of long pepper.<BR>—सर्व-ग्रास, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowing or engulfing<BR>all.<BR>—सर्वङ्-कष, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘all-grazing,’ all-<BR>pervading, everywhere diffused or extended; (अस्),<BR>m. ‘all-injuring,’ a rogue, wicked man; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a commentary by Malli-nātha on the Śiśupāla-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1095-a" target="_blank">Page1095-a+ 81</a>]<BR>vadha.<BR>—सर्व-चर्मीण, अस्, आ, अम्, made of every<BR>kind of skin or leather.<BR>—सर्व-चारिन्, ई, m. ‘all-<BR>pervading,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-जगत्, त्, f. the<BR>whole world, the universe.<BR>—सर्व-जनीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, belonging or relating to all men, fit for all.<BR>—सर्व-जया, f. ‘all-conquering,’ a particular reli-<BR>gious observance performed by women in the month<BR>Mārga-śīrṣa; a particular plant.<BR>—सर्व-जित्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>all-conquering, all-subduing, irresistible; all-surpass-<BR>ing, excellent, incomparable; (त्), m. a proper N.;<BR>epithet of the twenty-first (or fifty-fifth) year of<BR>Jupiter's cycle of sixty years.<BR>—सर्व-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, all-knowing, omniscient, all-wise; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Śiva; N. of a Muni; a Jina or Buddha<BR>deified sage; (आ), f. epithet of Durgā.<BR>—सर्वज्ञ-<BR>ता, f. or सर्वज्ञ-त्व, अम्, n. omniscience.<BR>—सर्-<BR>वज्ञ-नारायण, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—सर्-<BR>वज्ञ-वासुदेव, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>ज्ञातृ-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of one who is<BR>omniscient.<BR>—सर्व-ज्ञान, अम्, n. all-knowledge.<BR>—सर्वज्ञान-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—सर्व-ज्ञान-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made up of or<BR>containing all knowledge.<BR>—सर्व-ज्ञान-विद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>acquainted with all knowledge.<BR>—सर्व-तनू, ऊस्,<BR>m., Ved. one who is born again with his whole body.<BR>—सर्व-तन्त्र, अस्, m. one who has studied all the<BR>Tantras; (अस्, आ, अम्), universally acknowledged,<BR>admitted by all schools (as a philosophical principle).<BR>—सर्वतन्त्र-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m. a dogma admitted<BR>by all schools, (opposed to प्रतितन्त्र-सिद्धान्त,<BR>a dogma peculiar to some school or a controverted<BR>dogma, such as the Mīmāṃsaka doctrine of the eternity<BR>of sound.)<BR>—सर्व-तस्, see p. 1096, col. 3.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>ताता, ind., Ved. everywhere, (Sāy. = सर्वत्र); at<BR>the sacrifice, (Sāy. = सर्व-तातौ = यज्ञे, Ṛg-veda<BR>IV. 26, 3; see the next.)<BR>—सर्व-ताति, इस्, f. (see<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 4, 142), Ved. all prosperity, complete hap-<BR>piness or health; soundness, wholeness; [cf. Gr.<BR>ὁλό-της; in some passages ताति is connected by Sāy.<BR>with 2. तति, p. 361, and is said to mean either<BR>‘the extension of all enjoyments’ or simply ‘sacri-<BR>fice.’]<BR>—सर्व-तापन, अस्, ई, अम्, all-inflaming;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Kāma (god of love).<BR>—सर्व-<BR>तिक्ता, f. a particular plant (= काक-माची).<BR>—सर्व-<BR>तूर्य-निनादिन्, ई, m. ‘playing all instruments,’<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-तेजस्, अस्, n. all splendor.<BR>—सर्वतेजो-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of all splendor; con-<BR>taining all power.<BR>—सर्व-द, अस्, m. ‘all-giving,’<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-दमन, अस्, ई, अम्, all-<BR>subduing, all-taming, irresistible; (अस्), m. epithet<BR>of Bharata (son of Śakuntalā).<BR>—सर्व-दर्शन-<BR>सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘compendium of all the Darśanas,’<BR>N. of a treatise on the various systems of philosophy<BR>(not including the Vedānta) by Mādhavācārya and<BR>his brother Sāyaṇa.<BR>—सर्व-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, all-<BR>seeing; (ई), m. a Buddha.<BR>—सर्व-दान, अम्, n.<BR>the gift of everything.<BR>—सर्व-दानाधिक (˚न-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, better than every gift.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>दास, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—सर्व-दिग्-विजय,<BR>अस्, m. conquest of all regions, universal conquest.<BR>—सर्व-दुःख-क्षय, अस्, m. destruction of all<BR>pain, final emancipation from all existence, beatitude.<BR>—सर्व-देवत, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to all the<BR>deities.<BR>—सर्व-देव-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of all<BR>deities, comprising all the gods; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-देव-मुख, अस्, m. ‘mouth of all<BR>the gods,’ epithet of Agni or fire (Agni being the<BR>medium of oblations to the gods).<BR>—सर्व-देश्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being in all places.<BR>—सर्व-दैवत्य<BR>= सार्वदैवत्य.<BR>—सर्व-धन, अम्, n. all one's<BR>wealth or property; (in arithmetic) a sum total, sum<BR>of a series, total of a sum in progression.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>धर, ‘all-containing,’ N. of a work on medicine<BR>by Karatha.<BR>—सर्व-धर्म-प्रकाश, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a work on law by Śaṅkara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>धर्म-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing all duties, one who<BR>knows the duties of all tribes and castes.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>धा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. all-containing, all-yielding.<BR>—सर्व-धारिन्, ई, m. ‘all-holder,’ epithet of Śiva;<BR>epithet of the twenty-second (or according to others<BR>fifty-sixth) year of Jupiter's cycle of sixty years.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1095-b" target="_blank">Page1095-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—सर्व-धारी, f. the twenty-second year of the<BR>cycle (according to some; cf. सर्व-धारिन्).<BR>—सर्व-धुरावह (˚र-आव्˚), अस्, m. an ox fit<BR>for any sort of draught or carriage.<BR>—सर्व-धु-<BR>रीण, अस्, m. an ox or other animal fit for any kind<BR>of carriage or draught.<BR>—सर्वनाम-ता, f. the<BR>being a pronoun or pronominal.<BR>—सर्व-नामन्,<BR>अ, n. (in grammar) N. of a class of words beginning<BR>with सर्व, (these comprise the real pronouns and<BR>a series of pronominal adjectives, such as उभय,<BR>विश्व, एकतर, &c.)<BR>—सर्वनाम-स्थान, अम्,<BR>n. (in Pāṇini's grammar) a N. for the Aṅga cases<BR>collectively (i. e. the nom. sing. du. pl., acc. sing. du.<BR>of masc. and fem. nouns, and the nom. acc. pl. of<BR>neuters; these are called by some ‘the strong cases;’<BR>see Pāṇ. 1. 1, 42, 43; the voc. as following the nom.<BR>may be included under this name).<BR>—सर्व-नाश,<BR>अस्, m. total destruction, destruction of all.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>नाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, all-destroying.<BR>—सर्वन्-दम,<BR>अस्, m. ‘all-subduing,’ N. of Bharata.<BR>—सर्व-प-<BR>थ, अस्, m. every road or way, every direction.<BR>—सर्व-पथीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to every<BR>road or way, going in every direction.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>पशु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—१. सर्व-पा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, drinking everything; (आस्), f. the wife of the<BR>Daitya Bali.<BR>—२. सर्व-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, all-preserv-<BR>ing.<BR>—सर्व-पाप-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, removing all<BR>sin.<BR>—सर्व-पार्श्व-मुख, अस्, m. ‘having a<BR>face on all sides,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-पावन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘all-purifying,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>पूजित, अस्, m. ‘worshipped by all,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, full of everything.<BR>—सर्व-पूर्ण-त्व, अम्, n. entire fulness or com-<BR>pleteness, complete preparation or provision.<BR>—सर्-<BR>व-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, dear to all, universally beloved;<BR>generally friendly, loving all.<BR>—सर्व-बन्ध-वि-<BR>मोचन, अस्, m. ‘delivering from every bond,’ epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-भक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, eating all<BR>kinds of food, omnivorous; (आ), f. a female goat.<BR>—सर्व-भक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, all-devouring (as<BR>fire); eating all thing; all-devouring, omnivorous.<BR>—सर्व-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, sharing in everything.<BR>—सर्व-भाव, अस्, m. whole being or nature,<BR>(सर्व-भावेन, with one's whole being, with all<BR>one's thoughts.)<BR>—सर्व-भाव-कर, अस्, m. ‘causer<BR>of all being,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-भावन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘all-creating,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-भूत,<BR>आनि, n. pl. all beings, all created things, all the<BR>elements.<BR>—सर्वभूत-कृत्, त्, m. n. the maker of<BR>all things; the cause of all elements or beings.<BR>—सर्वभूत-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, containing all<BR>living beings or existences, comprising or compre-<BR>hending all elementary matter; (अस्), m. the supreme<BR>pervading spirit.<BR>—सर्व-भूत-स्थ or सर्व-<BR>भूत-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, present in all elements or<BR>beings.<BR>—सर्व-भूत-हर, अस्, m. epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-भूत-हित, अम्, n. the welfare of<BR>all created beings; (अस्, आ, अम्), serviceable to all<BR>creatures.<BR>—सर्वभूतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, m.<BR>‘soul of all beings,’ epithet of the universal or all-<BR>pervading spirit; epithet of Śiva; (आ, आ, अ), having<BR>the nature of all beings, containing all beings.<BR>—सर्वभूतात्म-मेधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having a<BR>knowledge of the essence or nature of all creatures.<BR>—सर्वभूतेप्सित (˚त-ईप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, desired<BR>by all beings.<BR>—सर्व-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, all-sustaining,<BR>cherishing or supporting all.<BR>—सर्व-भोगिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, enjoying all.<BR>—सर्व-भोगीण, अस्, आ, अम्, good<BR>or beneficial for all, to be enjoyed or possessed by<BR>all.<BR>—सर्व-मङ्गला, f. ‘all-auspicious,’ an epithet<BR>of the goddess Durgā; N. of a work.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or consisting of all, all-<BR>containing, general, universal, comprehensive of all.<BR>—सर्व-मही, f. the whole earth.<BR>—सर्व-मात्रा,<BR>f. epithet of a kind of metre.<BR>—सर्व-मूल्य, अम्,<BR>n. ‘price of all things,’ a cowry; any small coin.<BR>—सर्व-मूषक, अस्, m. ‘all-stealing,’ time.<BR>—सर्व-मेध, अस्, m. a universal sacrifice, sacri-<BR>fice for universal success.<BR>—सर्व-मेध्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. perfect purity.<BR>—सर्व-यमक, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of Yamaka, q. v.<BR>—सर्व-योगिन्, ई, m. epithet of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1095-c" target="_blank">Page1095-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-रक्षण-कवच, अम्, n. an all-<BR>preserving amulet or charm.<BR>—सर्व-रक्षिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, all-protecting; preserving from all (harm).<BR>—सर्व-रत्न, अस्, m. ‘having all gems,’ N. of a<BR>minister of king Yudhi-ṣṭhira; (आ), f., N. of one of<BR>the female personifications of musical tones or modes.<BR>—सर्व-रत्न-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made up of all<BR>kinds of jewels.<BR>—सर्व-रत्न-समन्वित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, possessing all gems or precious things.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>रस, अस्, m. the resinous exudation of the Śāl tree,<BR>resin; saltness, salt, saline flavour or taste; a sort<BR>of musical instrument, a kind of lute; a scholar,<BR>learned man.<BR>—सर्वरसोत्तम (˚स-उत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘the best of all flavours,’ the saline flavour, saltness,<BR>salt.<BR>—सर्व-रात्र, अस्, m. the whole night.<BR>—सर्-<BR>व-रूप-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, assuming all forms.<BR>—सर्वर्तु (˚व-ऋतु), उस्, m. every season.<BR>—सर्-<BR>वर्तुक (˚व-ऋत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, adapted to every<BR>season, habitable in every season.<BR>—सर्वर्तु-<BR>परिवर्त, अस्, m. ‘revolution of all the sea-<BR>sons,’ a year.<BR>—सर्वर्तु-फल, अम्, n. the fruit<BR>of all the seasons.<BR>—सर्व-लक्षण-लक्षित, अस्,<BR>m. ‘characterized by all marks,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-लालस, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>लिङ्गिन्, ई, m. ‘having all the external marks,’ a<BR>heretic, impostor (especially one who, not belonging<BR>to the orthodox faith, wears the dress and assumes<BR>the character of an ascetic).<BR>—सर्व-लोक, अस्, m. the<BR>universe.<BR>—सर्व-लोक-कृत्, त्, m. ‘Universe-maker,’<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-लोक-पितामह, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>great forefather of all creatures,’ epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—सर्वलोक-प्रजापति, इस्, m. ‘father of the Uni-<BR>verse,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वलोक-भयङ्कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, formidable to the whole world.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>लोक-विद्, त्, त्, त्, acquainted with all worlds.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>लोह, अस्, m. an iron arrow.<BR>—सर्व-वर्णिका, f. or<BR>(according to some) सर्व-वर्तिका, f. the tree Gme-<BR>lina Arborea.<BR>—सर्व-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of the<BR>author of the Kā-tantra Sūtras.<BR>—सर्व-वल्लभ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, dear to all; (आ), f. an unchaste woman.<BR>—सर्व-वात-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, able to bear every<BR>wind (said of a ship).<BR>—सर्व-वादि-सम्मत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, approved by all disputants, universally ad-<BR>mitted.<BR>—सर्व-वास, अस्, or सर्व-वासिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘all-abiding,’ Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-विख्यात, अस्, m. ‘cele-<BR>brated by all,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-विग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. ‘all-shaped,’ Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-विद्, त्, त्, त्, all-<BR>knowing, omniscient, all-wise; (त्), m. the Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>—सर्व-विभूति, इस्, f. dominion over all.<BR>—सर्व-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. all-heroic, contain-<BR>ing all heroes; possessing numerous male descendants.<BR>—सर्व-वेद, अस्, आ, अम्, having all knowledge;<BR>(अस्), m. a Brāhman who has read the four Vedas.<BR>—सर्व-वेदस्, आस्, m. a man who gives away all<BR>his acquisitions or property to the priests employed<BR>by him at particular sacrifices.<BR>—सर्व-वेदिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, all-knowing, omniscient.<BR>—सर्व-वेशिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘having all dresses or disguises,’ an actor, dancer.<BR>—सर्व-वैनाशिक, अस्, m. ‘all-annihilating,’ epi-<BR>thet of a class of Buddhists who argue total an-<BR>nihilation.<BR>—सर्व-व्यापि-त्व, अम्, n. universality.<BR>—सर्व-व्यापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, all-pervading, universal,<BR>ubiquitous; embracing all particulars; (ई), m. epi-<BR>thet of Rudra.<BR>—सर्व-शक्, क्, क्, क्, all-powerful,<BR>omnipotent.<BR>—सर्व-शङ्का, f. suspicion of every-<BR>body.<BR>—सर्वशस्, see p. 1096, col. 3.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>शान्ति-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, ‘causing universal peace or tranquil-<BR>lity,’ epithet of Bharata (sovereign of all India and son<BR>of Śakuntalā).<BR>—सर्व-शास्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing<BR>every science.<BR>—सर्व-शास्त्र-प्रवेतृ, ता, m. ‘cha-<BR>rioteer of all the sciences,’ one who is well acquainted<BR>with all the sciences.<BR>—सर्व-शास्त्र-विद्, त्, त्, त्, or<BR>सर्व-शास्त्र-विशारद, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in all the<BR>sciences.<BR>—सर्व-शुभङ्-कर, अस्, m. ‘beautifying<BR>everything,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-शून्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, empty of everything, completely empty.<BR>—सर्व-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, anything remaining out<BR>of a whole.<BR>—सर्व-शोक-विनाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, re-<BR>moving all sorrow or griefs.<BR>—सर्व-श्राव्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, audible to all.<BR>—सर्व-संसर्ग-लवण, अम्,<BR>n. a particular kind of salt or salt soil (mixing with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-a" target="_blank">Page1096-a+ 81</a>]<BR>everything).<BR>—सर्व-सङ्गत, अस्, आ, अम्, united<BR>with all, met with universally; (अस्), m. a sort of<BR>quick-growing rice (= षष्टिका).<BR>—सर्व-सङ्ग-<BR>परित्याग, अस्, m. abandonment of all wordly<BR>affections or connections.<BR>—सर्व-सङ्गा, f. ‘all-<BR>uniting,’ N. of a river.<BR>—सर्व-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>a general or universal collection; any collection.<BR>—सर्व-सन्नहन, अम्, n. or सर्व-सन्नह-<BR>नार्थक (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, m. a complete armament;<BR>the arming or assembling of a complete army (con-<BR>sisting of elephants, chariots, horse and foot), a<BR>complete armament.<BR>—सर्व-सन्नाह, अस्, m. a<BR>complete armament (see above); the universally-per-<BR>vading spirit.<BR>—सर्व-सम-ता, f. sameness or<BR>identity with all things; equality towards all, equal<BR>regard for all, equanimity.<BR>—सर्व-सस्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, bearing all kinds of corn, (also written सर्व-<BR>शस्य.)<BR>—सर्व-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, all-enduring, all-<BR>bearing, very patient; (अस्), m. bdellium; (आ), f.<BR>the earth.<BR>—सर्व-साक्षिन्, ई, m. ‘all-witnessing,’<BR>epithet of the Supreme Being; of Wind; of Fire.<BR>—सर्व-साधन, अस्, m. ‘all-accomplishing,’ Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-साधारण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, common to<BR>all.<BR>—सर्व-साधु, ind. in all respects good or<BR>well.<BR>—सर्व-साधु-निषेवित, अस्, m. ‘honoured<BR>by all good people,’ Śiva.<BR>—सर्व-सामान्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, common to all.<BR>—सर्व-सारोपनिषद्<BR>(˚र-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>सिद्धार्थ (˚ध-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having every<BR>object attained, having every wish gratified, quite<BR>happy.<BR>—सर्व-सिद्धि, इस्, f. accomplishment of<BR>every object, universal success; (इस्), m. the Vilva<BR>tree.<BR>—सर्व-सेन, अस्, m., Ved. the lord of the<BR>whole host.<BR>—सर्व-स्व, अम्, n. the whole of a<BR>person's property or possessions; whole substance or<BR>essence of anything.<BR>—सर्व-स्व-दण्ड, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fined in all possessions; (अम्), n. confiscation<BR>of the whole of a property.<BR>—सर्वस्व-हरण,<BR>अम्, n. or सर्वस्व-हार, अस्, m. the seizure or<BR>confiscation of the whole of any one's property.<BR>—सर्व-स्वामि-गुणोपेत (˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>endowed with all the excellences of a master.<BR>—सर्व-स्वामिन्, ई, m. the owner or master of all;<BR>a universal monarch.<BR>—सर्वस्विन्, ई, m. a kind of<BR>mixed caste (the result of intermarriage between<BR>a woman of the Gopa or cowherd caste with a<BR>Nāpita or barber).<BR>—सर्व-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘seizing<BR>all,’ an epithet of death.<BR>—सर्व-हरण, अम्, n.<BR>or सर्व-हार, अस्, m. seizing of the whole, total<BR>confiscation.<BR>—सर्व-हरि, इस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 96, (having the patronymic<BR>Aindra.)<BR>—सर्व-हायस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having all<BR>strength or vigour.<BR>—सर्व-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, useful<BR>or beneficial to all; (अम्), n. black pepper.<BR>—सर्व-<BR>हुत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. (perhaps) all-sacrificing or sacrificing<BR>all at once.<BR>—सर्वागमोपनिषद् (˚व-आगम-<BR>उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—सर्वाङ्ग (˚व-<BR>अङ्˚), अम्, n. the whole body (from head to foot);<BR>all the Aṅgas or Vedāṅgas (see वेदाङ्ग) collec-<BR>tively; (अस्, आ, अम्), having all members, perfect in<BR>limb; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वाङ्ग-रूप,<BR>अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वाङ्ग-सुन्दर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, beautiful in every member, completely beau-<BR>tiful.<BR>—सर्वाङ्ग-सुन्दर-रस, अस्, m. ‘whose<BR>essence is good for all the limbs,’ epithet of a par-<BR>ticular drug or medicament.<BR>—सर्वाङ्गीण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, spread over all the limbs, thrilling through the<BR>whole body or throughout the body, generally dif-<BR>fusive, pervading; relating or belonging to the<BR>Aṅgas or Vedāṅgas collectively, (see वेदाङ्ग.)<BR>—सर्वातिथि-व्रत (˚व-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, devoted<BR>to all guests, hospitable.<BR>—सर्वातोद्य-परिग्रह<BR>(˚व-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘comprehending every musical in-<BR>strument,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वात्मक (˚व-आत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, all-containing, all-pervading.<BR>—सर्वात्-<BR>मत्व-दर्शन, अम्, n. the doctrine of the one-<BR>ness of everything with Spirit.<BR>—सर्वात्मन् (˚व-<BR>आत्˚), आ, m. the universal soul, the Supreme Spirit;<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वात्म-भूति, इस्, f. all beings<BR>collectively.<BR>—सर्वा-दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, like to<BR>all.<BR>—सर्वाधिकरण (˚व-अध्˚), आणि, n. pl. all<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-b" target="_blank">Page1096-b+ 81</a>]<BR>occasions; (एषु), ind. on all occasions.<BR>—सर्वा-<BR>धिकार (˚व-अध्˚), अस्, m. general superintendence.<BR>—सर्वाधिकारिन्, ई, or सर्वाध्यक्ष (˚व-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a general superintendent.<BR>—सर्वाधिक्य<BR>(˚व-आध्˚), अम्, n. superiority to all.<BR>—सर्वा-<BR>नवद्याङ्ग (˚व-अनवद्य-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having altogether blameless or faultless limbs.<BR>—सर्वानुकारिन् (˚व-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, all-imitating;<BR>(इणी), f. a kind of shrub (= शाल-पर्णी).<BR>—सर्वा-<BR>नुक्रम (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. a general index (show-<BR>ing the successive contents of any book); = सर्वा-<BR>नुक्रमणी below.<BR>—सर्वानुक्रमणिका (˚व-<BR>अन्˚), f., N. of Kātyāyana's index to the Ṛg-veda;<BR>of an index to the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā by the same<BR>author.<BR>—सर्वानुक्रमणी (˚व-अन्˚), f., N. of a<BR>general index to the Veda by Kātyāyana (a pupil of<BR>Śaunaka).<BR>—सर्वानुक्रमणी-वृत्ति, इस्, f. a com-<BR>mentary by Ṣaḍ-guru-śiṣya on the above.<BR>—सर्-<BR>वानुभूति (˚व-अन्˚), इस्, f. universal experience;<BR>‘all-perceiving,’ epithet of one of the twenty-four<BR>Arhats of the past Ut-sarpiṇī; also of one of the future<BR>Ut-sarpiṇī; a white variety of the Tri-vṛt plant.<BR>—सर्वानुमति (˚व-अन्˚), इस्, f. the consent of<BR>all.<BR>—सर्वान्तर्यामिन् (˚व-अन्˚), ई, m. ‘ruling or<BR>pervading all hearts,’ epithet of the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—सर्वान्न-भक्षक (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>सर्वान्न-भोजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or सर्वान्नीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>eating all sorts of food (whether clean or otherwise).<BR>—सर्वाभरण-भूषित (˚व-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>adorned with all ornaments.<BR>—सर्वाभिसन्धिन्<BR>(˚व-अभ्˚), ई m. ‘all-censuring,’ a cynic, calum-<BR>niator, reviler.<BR>—सर्वाभिसार (˚व-अभ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>an attack with a complete army (of elephants, chariots,<BR>horse and foot), assembling a complete armament.<BR>—सर्वायस (˚व-अय्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, entirely made<BR>of iron.<BR>—सर्वायुध (˚व-आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘armed<BR>with every weapon,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वायुधो-<BR>पेत (˚व-आयुध-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessing all<BR>weapons, stored with all sorts of arms.<BR>—सर्वार्थ<BR>(˚व-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having all objects or aims;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of the twenty-ninth Muhūrta; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. all matters, (सर्वार्थेषु, in all matters, in<BR>all the subjects contained in any particular work);<BR>all objects; (अम्), ind. for the sake of all.<BR>—सर्-<BR>वार्थ-कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, skilful in all matters.<BR>—सर्वार्थ-चिन्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, a superintendent<BR>or manager of all affairs, (according to Kullūka =<BR>कार्य-द्रष्टा नगराधिपतिः.)<BR>—सर्वार्थ-ता,<BR>f. the state of possessing all objects.<BR>—सर्वार्थ-<BR>साधिका, f. ‘effecting all objects,’ epithet of Durgā.<BR>—सर्वार्थ-सिद्ध, अस्, m. ‘one by whom all<BR>objects are effected,’ epithet of the great Buddha (or<BR>Śākya-muni, the founder of the Buddhist religion;<BR>according to some he was so called because his<BR>parents' wishes were all fulfilled by his birth).<BR>—सर्वार्थानुसाधिनी (˚थ-अन्˚), f. ‘effecting all<BR>objects,’ epithet of Durgā.<BR>—सर्वावसर (˚व-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘universal leisure,’ midnight.<BR>—सर्वावस्था<BR>(˚व-अव्˚), f. every condition, (सर्वावस्थासु, at all<BR>periods.)<BR>—सर्वाशय (˚व-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘refuge of<BR>all,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वाशिन् (˚व-अश्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>eating all things.<BR>—सर्वाश्रमिन् (˚व-आश्˚), ई, इणी,<BR>इ, belonging to every order of life.<BR>—सर्वाश्रय<BR>(˚व-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, giving shelter or protection<BR>to all; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सर्वास्ति-वाद<BR>(˚व-अस्˚), अस्, m. or सर्वास्ति-वादिन् (˚व-अस्˚), ई,<BR>m. ‘one who asserts the reality of all existence,’<BR>epithet of one of the four divisions of the Vaibhā-<BR>shika system of Buddhism (said to have been founded<BR>by Rāhula, son of the great Buddha).<BR>—सर्वास्त्र<BR>(˚व-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having all weapons; (आ), f.<BR>epithet of one of the sixteen Jaina Vidyā-devīs or<BR>goddesses of learning.<BR>—सर्वास्त्र-महाज्वाला, one<BR>of the Vidyā-devīs described above.<BR>—सर्वास्त्र-<BR>विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing or skilled in all weapons.<BR>—सर्-<BR>वाह्न (˚व-अह्˚), अस्, m. the whole day, (also spelt सर्-<BR>वाह्ण.)<BR>—सर्वेन्द्रिय-सम्भव (˚व-इन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, arising from every sense.<BR>—सर्वेश (˚व-ईश),<BR>अस्, m. ‘lord of all,’ the Supreme Being; a universal<BR>monarch.<BR>—सर्वेश्वर (˚व-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>all,’ a universal monarch, paramount lord; epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">Page1096-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of Śiva; a proper N.<BR>—सर्वोत्तम (˚व-उत्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, best of all, supremely good.<BR>—सर्वोपकारिन्<BR>(˚व-उप्˚), ई, इणी, इ, assisting all; (इणी), f., N. of a<BR>commentary on the Tattvas of the Sāṅkhya phil.<BR>—सर्वोपध (˚व-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having any<BR>penultimate letter.<BR>—सर्वोपनिषद् (˚व-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—सर्वोपाधि (˚व-उप्˚), इस्,<BR>m. a general attribute.<BR>—सर्वौघ (˚व-ओघ),<BR>अस्, m. great speed or impetuosity; the assembling<BR>of a complete army (consisting of elephants, chariots,<BR>horse and foot).<BR>—सर्वौषधि (˚व-ओष्˚), इस्,<BR>m. or सर्वौषधि-गण or सर्वौषधि-<BR>वर्ग, अस्, m. a class of certain medicinal herbs<BR>or drugs (such as Murā, Campaka, Jaṭā-māṃsī,<BR>Haridrā or turmeric, Vacā or orris root, Śaileya or<BR>benzoin, Śaṭī or zedoary, Kuṣṭha or Costus Spe-<BR>ciosus, Karpūra or camphor, Candana or sandal,<BR>Musta or Cyperus, &c.).<BR>—सर्वौषधि-रस, अस्,<BR>m. the juice or infusion of all the above herbs<BR>(especially of those used at a royal inauguration).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वक|सर्व्वक|सर्व्वकः
सर्वक, अस्, आ, अम्, all, every, whole, entire,<BR>universal; (ए), ind. everywhere, universally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतस्|सर्व्वतस्
सर्व-तस्, ind. from every quarter, from every<BR>side, from all parts, from everybody; in every di-<BR>rection; on all sides, every way, all round, every-<BR>where; wholly, entirely.<BR>—सर्वतः-शुभा, f.<BR>‘wholly auspicious,’ the plant Priyaṅgu.<BR>—सर्वतो-<BR>दिक्क, अस्, आ, अम् (see 2. दिश्), diffused over all<BR>quarters, extending in every direction.<BR>—सर्वतो-<BR>दिशम् or सर्वतो-दिशस्, ind. to every quarter (of<BR>the world), in every direction.<BR>—सर्वतो-भद्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, everywhere or on every side good, in<BR>every direction or towards every quarter auspicious;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a temple or palace of a square form<BR>and having an entrance opposite to every point of<BR>the compass; (अस्), m. the car of Viṣṇu; a bam-<BR>boo; a form of military array; a square mystical<BR>diagram (painted on a cloth with various colours, and<BR>used on particular occasions to cover a sort of altar<BR>erected to Viṣṇu); a kind of charade in which the<BR>same word answers several questions; a particular<BR>kind of artificial verse (so contrived that the same<BR>meanings and syllables occur, whether the line be<BR>read backwards or forwards, or in various other direc-<BR>tions; an example occurs in Kirāt. XV. 25); the<BR>Nimba tree; N. of a forest; (आ), f. the tree Gmelina<BR>Arborea (= गम्भारी); an actress, the wife of an<BR>actor or dancer; a sort of yam, Dioscorea; (अम्), n.<BR>a mystical diagram of a square shape but enclosing<BR>a circle (this diagram is regarded as sacred, and em-<BR>ployed on the occasion of the letting loose of a bull,<BR>the completion of a vow or other religious observ-<BR>ance; it may perhaps be identical with that de-<BR>scribed above); another square diagram employed<BR>for astrological purposes or to foretel good and bad<BR>fortune.<BR>—सर्वतो-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, facing every<BR>quarter (of the compass), turned everywhere, going<BR>everywhere; complete, unrestrained, unlimited, bound-<BR>less; (अस्), m. soul, spirit; epithet of Śiva (as repre-<BR>sented with five faces); of Brahmā (as represented with<BR>four faces); of Agni or Fire; a Brāhman; the heaven<BR>of Indra or Svarga; (अम्), n. water; sky, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्र|सर्व्वत्र
सर्वत्र, ind. everywhere, in all places; always,<BR>at all times.<BR>—सर्वत्र-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going every-<BR>where, all-pervading; (अस्), m. air, wind.<BR>—सर्वत्र-<BR>गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going everywhere; (ई), m. air,<BR>wind.<BR>—सर्वत्राप्रतिघ (˚र-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not kept back from (penetrating) everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वथा|सर्व्वथा
सर्वथा, ind. in all ways, by all means; at all,<BR>(न सर्वथा, not at all), altogether, entirely, wholly,<BR>completely, mostly, assuredly, certainly; exceed-<BR>ingly; at all times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वदा|सर्व्वदा
सर्वदा, ind. always, at all times, at every time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वद्र्यञ्च्|सर्वद्र्यंच्
सर्वद्र्यञ्च्, अङ्, -द्रीची, अक् (fr. सर्व with अद्रि<BR>substituted for the final + rt. अञ्च्), honouring all<BR>(= सर्वस्य पूजक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वशस्|सर्व्वशस्
सर्वशस्, ind. wholly, altogether, completely,<BR>entirely, universally; everywhere; on all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वाणी|सर्व्वाणी
सर्वाणी, f., N. of Durgā (wife of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्विका
सर्विका, f. according to Vopa-deva IV. 6. a dimi-<BR>nutive of सर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वीय|सर्व्वीय|सर्व्वीयः
सर्वीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to all,<BR>suitable or fit for all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वरी|सर्व्वरी
सर्वरी सर्वरी, f. (for शर्वरी), night.<BR>—सर्वरी-कर, अस्, m. ‘night-maker,’ the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वला|सर्व्वला
सर्वला सर्वला, f. (for शर्वला, p. 995,<BR>col. 3), an iron club or crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वली|सर्व्वली
सर्वली, f. = सर्वला above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षप|सर्षपः
सर्षप सर्षप, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. III.<BR>141. said to be fr. rt. सृ), mustard or mustard-seed,<BR>Sinapis Dichotoma; a kind of poison; a small<BR>measure of weight or a mustard-seed so considered;<BR>(ई), f. a kind of small bird (said to be a species of<BR>wagtail, = खञ्जनिका).<BR>—सर्षप-तैल, अम्, n.<BR>mustard-oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षिगण
सर्षिगण सर्षि-गण (स-ऋषि-), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having or attended by a host of Ṛṣis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षिमरुद्गण
सर्षि-मरुद्-गण, अस्, आ, अम्, with a host of<BR>Ṛṣis and Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षीका
सर्षीका सर्षीका, f. a particular kind of<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्
सल् सल् (connected with rt. सृ), cl. 1.<BR>P. सलति, ससाल, सलितुम्, to go, move;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἅλλ-ο-μαι, ἅλμα; Lat. salio; Lith. selu,<BR>‘to creep;’ Slav. sl-a-ti, ‘to send;’ Hib. silim, ‘I<BR>drop, distil, spit.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल|सलं
सल, अम्, n. [cf. सर], water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिल|सलिलं
सलिल, अम्, n. [cf. the older form सरिर, p. 1093,<BR>col. 2], water; (in the Sāṅkhya phil.) a technical<BR>term for one of the four kinds of अध्यात्मिका तुष्टि<BR>or internal acquiescence, (the other three being<BR>अम्भस्, ओघ, and वृष्टि; cf. सु-पारा); a kind<BR>of metre; [cf. Gr. σάλος, ἅλς; Lat. salum, sal,<BR>saliva; Slav. sol, ‘salt.’]<BR>—सलिल-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>a particular funeral rite (= सलिल-क्रिया).<BR>—सलिल-<BR>कुन्तल, अस्, m. ‘water-hair,’ the aquatic plant Val-<BR>lisneria Octandra.<BR>—सलिल-क्रिया, f. ‘water-rite,’ the<BR>funeral rite of washing a corpse.<BR>—सलिल-ज, अम्,<BR>n. ‘water-born,’ a lotus.<BR>—सलिल-निधि, इस्, m.<BR>‘water-receptacle,’ the ocean.<BR>—सलिल-पूर-वत्,<BR>ind. like a large quantity of water.<BR>—सलिल-रय,<BR>अस्, m. ‘water-flow,’ a current, stream.<BR>—सलिल-<BR>राशि, इस्, m. ‘water-heap,’ any piece of water.<BR>—सलिल-स्थल-चर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, frequenting<BR>water and land, amphibious.<BR>—सलिलार्थिन् (˚ल-अर्˚),<BR>ई, इनी, इ, wishing for water, thirsty.<BR>—सलिलाशय<BR>(˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, m. a receptacle or reservoir of water,<BR>tank, lake.<BR>—सलिलिले-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, moving about<BR>in the water.<BR>—सलिलेन्धन (˚ल-इन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘water-kindling,’ submarine fire.<BR>—सलिले-शय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, resting or lying in water.<BR>—सलिलोच्चय<BR>(˚ल-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a mass or collection of<BR>water.<BR>—सलिलोपप्लव (˚ल-उप्˚), अस्, m. a flood<BR>of water, inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलक्ष
सलक्ष स-लक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having a lac<BR>or a hundred thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलक्षण
सलक्षण स-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>same marks, of the same species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलक्ष्मन्
सलक्ष्मन् स-लक्ष्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having<BR>the same marks or characteristics, related, a relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलज्ज|सलज्जः
सलज्ज स-लज्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, feeling shame<BR>or modesty, bashful, modest, ashamed; (अम्), ind.<BR>bashfully, modestly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सललितम्
सललितम् स-ललितम्, ind. with sport,<BR>wantonly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सललूक
सललूक सललूक, अस्, m. (probably fr. rt.<BR>सल्; according to Sāy. for सररूक, fr. rt. सृ),<BR>Ved. (probably) an unstable or wavering person;<BR>a wicked person, sinner, (Sāy. = सरण-शील or<BR>संलुब्ध or पापक; see Nirukta VI. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलवक
सलवक स-लवक. See लवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलाजकुसुम
सलाजकुसुम स-लाज-कुसुम, अस्, आ, अम्, ac-<BR>companied with sprinkled grain and flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलील|सलीलः
सलील स-लील, अस्, आ, अम्, playful, wanton,<BR>sportive; (अम्), ind. playfully, sportingly; affec-<BR>tionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलेश
सलेश स-लेश, अस्, आ, अम्, having parts or<BR>portions, with every part, entire; (अम्), ind. with<BR>every particle, entirely, wholly (= 1. स-कलम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलोक
सलोक स-लोक, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the<BR>same world.<BR>—सलोक-ता, f. the being in the same<BR>world or sphere, residence in the same heaven with<BR>any particular deity (one of the four states into<BR>which Mukti or final beatitude is distinguished).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्लकी
सल्लकी सल्लकी, f. (= शल्लकी), the gum<BR>olibanum tree, Boswellia Thurifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्व
सल्व सल्व, आस्, m. pl., Ved., N. of a peo-<BR>ple; [cf. शल्व.]<BR>—सल्व-देश, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव|सवं|सवः
सव 1. सव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. सु), pressing<BR>out or extracting the Soma juice; a libation, obla-<BR>tion, sacrifice; N. of the fifth book of the Śata-<BR>patha-Brāhmaṇa; (अम्), n. sprinkling or pouring<BR>out the juice of the Soma plant; making libations;<BR>water; the juice or honey of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवन|सवनं
1. सवन, अम्, n. the act of extracting or pouring<BR>out the juice of the Soma plant; a libation; a sacri-<BR>fice or oblation (in general); drinking the Soma<BR>juice; bathing (as a religious exercise or as prepara-<BR>tory to a sacrifice; generally performed three times<BR>a day, viz. morning, mid-day, and evening; cf. त्रि-<BR>षवण); any purificatory ablution; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a son of Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—सवन-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>a sacrificial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवनीय
सवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the Savana (see<BR>above); to be offered or poured out; to be distilled;<BR>sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव|सवं|सवः
सव 2. सव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 4. सु), a gene-<BR>rator; the sun; the moon; offspring, progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवन|सवनं
2. सवन, अम्, n. the act of bearing children,<BR>bringing forth young, generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृ
सवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, generating, vivifying, pro-<BR>ducing, causing, effecting; (ता), m. a generator,<BR>vivifier; the sun, (in the Veda sometimes identified<BR>with and sometimes distinguished from Sūrya, q. v.;<BR>according to Sāy. the sun before rising is called<BR>Savitṛ, and after rising till its setting Sūrya; many<BR>hymns of the Ṛg-veda are devoted to the praise of<BR>Savitṛ, e. g. 1. 35, II. 38, III. 62, 10-12, IV. 53,<BR>54, V. 81, 82, &c.; he is described as ‘golden-<BR>eyed,’ ‘golden-handed,’ ‘golden-armed,’ ‘golden-<BR>tongued,’ ‘yellow-haired,’ &c., the waters and the<BR>winds are said to obey him, and the other gods are<BR>described as following his lead and bowing to his<BR>authority; he is also, like Agni, called Apāṃ napāt,<BR>‘son of the waters,’ and is even worshipped as a<BR>‘lord of all creatures,’ supporting the world and de-<BR>livering his votaries from sin; the celebrated verse<BR>called गायत्री and सावित्री, q. q. v. v., is addressed to<BR>him); epithet of Indra; of Śiva; N. of one of the<BR>twenty-eight Vyāsas; a particular plant or tree<BR>(= अर्क); (त्री), f. a mother; a cow.<BR>—सवितृ-<BR>दैवत, अस्, m. ‘having the sun for a deity,’ the<BR>constellation Hastā or the thirteenth of the lunar<BR>asterisms (so called because the sun is the ruling<BR>deity of this asterism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृल|सवितृलः
सवितृल, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the sun, solar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्र|सवित्रं
सवित्र, अम्, n. a cause of generation, instrument<BR>of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्रिय|सवित्रियः
सवित्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>the sun, solar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्री
सवित्री, f., see under सवितृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवीमन्
सवीमन्, आ, m., Ved. production, generation,<BR>vivifying power, favouring aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवज्रसङ्घात|सवज्रसंघात
सवज्रसङ्घात स-वज्र-सङ्घात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>with the stroke of a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवत्स
सवत्स स-वत्स, अस्, आ, अम्, together with<BR>a calf, having a calf; having descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवधूक
सवधूक स-वधूक, अस्, m. along with a<BR>wife, a man with his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवपुष
सवपुष स-वपुष, अस्, ई, अम्, having a body<BR>or form, embodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवयस्
सवयस् स-वयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, being of the<BR>same age, coeval, cotemporary; (आस्), m. a coeval,<BR>cotemporary, friend of the same age; (आस्), f. a<BR>woman's female friend or confidante.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर|सवरः
सवर सवर, अस्, m. (= शवर), water;<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवरूथ
सवरूथ स-वरूथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>protecting ledge, (see वरूथ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्ण|सवर्णः
सवर्ण स-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, being of the<BR>same colour; being of like appearance, like, resem-<BR>bling; of the same tribe or class; belonging to the<BR>same class of letters (i. e. uttered by the same organs<BR>of speech); of the same kind, homogeneous; (आ),<BR>f., N. of the woman substituted by Saraṇyū for<BR>herself as a wife of the Sun, (she is said to have<BR>given birth to Manu, and is called in later legends<BR>Chāyā; see सरण्यू); N. of a daughter of the<BR>Ocean, and wife of Prācīna-varhis.<BR>—सवर्णास-<BR>वर्ण-विवाह (˚ण-अस्˚), अस्, m. the marriage of<BR>people of the same and of different castes.<BR>—सवर्-<BR>णोपायिन् (˚णा-उप्˚), ई, m. one who approaches a<BR>woman of the same caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्णिलिङ्गिन्
स-वर्णि-लिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing the marks of<BR>a religious student, disguised as a Brahma-cārin, (see<BR>वर्णिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्मन्
सवर्मन् स-वर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, having armour,<BR>along with armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवल
सवल सवल, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Puṣkara (son of Priya-vrata; also written सवन).<BR>—सवलाश्व (˚ल-अश्˚), आस्, m. pl. (perhaps for श-<BR>वलाश्व), epithet of the thousand sons of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवहा
सवहा स-वहा, f. the plant Tri-vṛt; [cf.<BR>सु-वहा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवाचस्
सवाचस् स-वाचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or स-वाचस,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having words or conversation, conversing<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवाणधि
सवाणधि स-वाणधि, इस्, इस्, इ, together with<BR>a quiver, bearing a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवालखिल्य
सवालखिल्य स-वालखिल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to-<BR>gether with the Vālakhilya hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवाष्पस्तम्भम्
सवाष्पस्तम्भम् स-वाष्प-स्तम्भम्, ind.<BR>with suppression of tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवास
सवास 1. स-वास, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. वास),<BR>scented, perfumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवास
सवास 2. स-वास, अस्, आ, अम् (see 2. वास),<BR>having a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवासस्
सवासस् स-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस् [cf. 3. वास],<BR>clothed, dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्प
सविकल्प स-विकल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, admitting<BR>of an alternative or option, optional; admitting of<BR>ambiguity or doubt, doubtful; having distinction,<BR>distinguishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्पक
स-विकल्पक, अस्, आ, अम्, = स-विकल्प above;<BR>recognising distinctions (e. g. those of subject and<BR>object in the Vedānta phil; opposed to निर्-वि-<BR>कल्पक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकाश|सविकाशः
सविकाश स-विकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>expansion, expanded, extended, extensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविग्रह
सविग्रह स-विग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, having body<BR>or form, embodied; having meaning or import,<BR>meaning, importing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितर्कम्
सवितर्कम् स-वितर्कम्, ind. with reasoning<BR>or thought, thoughtfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृ
सवितृ सवितृ. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविदिश्
सविदिश् स-विदिश्, क्, क्, क्, along with the<BR>intermediate quarters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविद्य
सविद्य स-विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having learn-<BR>ing, learned, wise, versed in science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविद्युत्स्तनित
सविद्युत्स्तनित स-विद्युत्-स्तनित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>accompanied with lightning and thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविध|सविधः
सविध स-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of the same<BR>kind or sort; near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविनय
सविनय स-विनय, अस्, आ, अम्, having good<BR>behaviour or propriety, well-conducted, well-behaved,<BR>modest; (अम्), n. modestly, humbly, respectfully,<BR>graciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविभास
सविभास स-विभास, अस्, m. ‘having great<BR>lustre,’ epithet of one of the seven suns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविभ्रम
सविभ्रम स-विभ्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, employing<BR>amorous or coquettish glances, coquettish, wanton;<BR>(अम्), ind. coquettishly, playfully, with amorous<BR>action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविमर्शम्
सविमर्शम् स-विमर्शम्, ind. thoughtfully,<BR>with consideration or deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविलास
सविलास स-विलास, अस्, आ, अम्, acting co-<BR>quettishly, sportive, playful, wanton, amorous; (अम्),<BR>ind. playfully, coquettishly, with expressive looks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेष
सविशेष स-विशेष, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>distinguishing or characteristic qualities; peculiar,<BR>singular, extraordinary; excellent, superior; having<BR>discrimination, discriminating; (अम्), ind. in a special<BR>or peculiar manner, especially, singularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषक
स-विशेषक, अस्, इका, अम्, having distinguishing<BR>properties or peculiar qualities; discriminated; (अम्),<BR>n. any distinguishing peculiarity or characteristic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषण
स-विशेषण, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing distinctions<BR>or peculiarities; distinguished, marked, characterized,<BR>individualized by peculiar marks or properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषतस्
