सव्य|सव्यः
सव्य सव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. IV. 109. fr. rt. सू; perhaps for an original<BR>स्कव्य), left, left hand; south, southern; reverse,<BR>contrary, backward; (अस्), m., N. of an Āṅgirasa<BR>(author of the hymns Ṛg-veda 1. 51-57); an epi-<BR>thet of Viṣṇu; [cf. Gr. σκαιό-ςμ σκαιό-τη-ς, σκαιο-<BR>σύνη (probably also σκαῦρο-ς); Lat. scœvu-s, scœ-<BR>vitas, scœvola (perhaps also scauru-s, sinister);<BR>Slav. sui.]<BR>—सव्य-तस्, ind. from the left side; on<BR>the left side, on the left hand; in a reverse way.<BR>—सव्य-ष्ठृ, ठा, m. = सव्ये-ष्ठृ.<BR>—सव्य-<BR>साचिन्, ई, m. (see साचिन्), ‘drawing a bow with the<BR>left hand as well as the right,’ epithet of Arjuna;<BR>any person who can use both hands alike.<BR>—सव्या-<BR>पसव्य (˚य-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, left and right, re-<BR>verse and direct, wrong and right.<BR>—सव्येतर<BR>(˚य-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘other than left,’ right.<BR>—सव्ये-<BR>ष्ठ, अस्, or सव्ये-ष्ठृ, ठा, m. ‘standing on<BR>the left,’ a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

