सस्
सस् सस् (= rts. 2. शस्, शंस्त्, संस्त्), cl. 2.<BR>P. सस्ति (apparently also cl. 3. P. ससस्ति),<BR>ससास, ससिष्यति, अससीत् or असासीत्, ससितुम्, to<BR>sleep: Caus. सासयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असीषसत्:<BR>Desid. सिससिषति: Intens. सासयते, सासस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्
ससत्, अन्, अती, अत्, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस
सस सस, अम्, n. food (= अन्न, Naigh. II.<BR>7); (अस्), m., N. of an Ātreya, (author of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda V. 21.)<BR>—सस-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>possessed of food, feeding on sacrificial food, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 87, 2. ससवान् either<BR>= अन्नवान् or as if fr. rt. 1. सन् = सम्भक्तवान्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंशय
ससंशय स-संशय, अस्, आ, अम्, doubtful,<BR>uncertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंहार
ससंहार स-संहार, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>means of restraint, (said of magical weapons which<BR>can only be restrained by repeating certain Mantras.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससखि
ससखि स-सखि, ind. similar to a friend,<BR>(Pāṇ. II. 1, 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससचिव
ससचिव स-सचिव, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied<BR>or attended by ministers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससञ्ज्ञ|ससंज्ञ
ससञ्ज्ञ स-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, having sense,<BR>sensible, conscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्त्व
ससत्त्व स-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>energy or vigour; (आ), f. containing an embryo, a<BR>pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससन|ससनं
ससन ससन, अम्, n. (= शसन, शमन),<BR>immolation, slaughtering a victim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससन्देह|ससंदेह|ससंदेहः
ससन्देह स-सन्देह, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>doubt or hesitation, (applied to a kind of indirect<BR>praise in rhetoric.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससन्ध्य|ससंध्य
ससन्ध्य स-सन्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>period called Sandhyā, (see युग); relating to<BR>evening, vespertine.<BR>—स-सन्ध्यांश (˚या-अं˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, with the period called Sandhyāṃśa, (see<BR>युग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससम्पद
ससम्पद स-सम्पद, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>happiness or prosperity, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससम्भ्रम|ससंभ्रम
ससम्भ्रम स-सम्भ्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, filled<BR>with confusion or bewilderment, bewildered, flurried,<BR>agitated; (अम्), ind. with confusion or perplexity,<BR>hurriedly, hastily; in fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससर्प
ससर्प स-सर्प, अस्, आ, अम्, having serpents,<BR>infested by serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससर्परी
ससर्परी ससर्परी, ईस्, f. (fr. rt. सृप्), Ved.<BR>gliding everywhere (said of Vāc, the daughter of<BR>Sūrya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससवस्
ससवस् ससवस्, आन्, m., Ved. one who<BR>possesses, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 34, 8.<BR>fr. rt. 1. सन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससहाय
ससहाय स-सहाय, अस्, आ, अम्, along with<BR>associates, having companions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससाध्वस
ससाध्वस स-साध्वस, अस्, आ, अम्, filled with<BR>terror, terrified, frightened, alarmed; timid; (अम्),<BR>ind. in fear, timidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससार
ससार स-सार, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>strength or energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससारवाण
स-सार-वाण, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing both strength<BR>and sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससीमन्
ससीमन् स-सीमन्, आ, आ, अ, having the<BR>same boundary, conterminous, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससुत
ससुत स-सुत, अस्, आ, अम्, having a son,<BR>with sons, with children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससुत्वन्
ससुत्वन् स-सुत्वन्, आ, &c., accompanied<BR>by Soma-offering priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससुरचापम्
ससुरचापम् स-सुरचापम्, ind. with Indra's<BR>bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससुहृज्जन
ससुहृज्जन स-सुहृज्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, attended<BR>by friendly people, along with kinsfolk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससूत
ससूत स-सूत, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by a<BR>charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससेन
ससेन स-सेन, अस्, आ, अम्, having an army,<BR>commanding an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससैन्य
ससैन्य स-सैन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having an<BR>army, along with an army, attended by guards.<BR>—स-सैन्य-बल-वाहन, अस्, आ, अम्, with guards,<BR>armies, and equipages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससौष्ठव
ससौष्ठव स-सौष्ठव, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>excellence, excellent; with lightness or fleetness,<BR>quick, fleet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्ज्
सस्ज् सस्ज् = rt. 2. सञ्ज्, p. 1050.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्तर
सस्तर स-स्तर, अस्, m. ‘having a strewing,’<BR>a bed of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्त्रीक
सस्त्रीक स-स्त्रीक, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by<BR>a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्थाणुजङ्गम
सस्थाणुजङ्गम स-स्थाणु-जङ्गम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>along with immovables and movables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्थान
सस्थान स-स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, (= समान-<BR>स्थान, Vopa-deva VI. 98), having the same position,<BR>having the same class, corresponding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्थावन्
सस्थावन् स-स्थावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. stand-<BR>ing or fixed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्नि
सस्नि सस्नि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. 1. सन्; accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. fr. rt. स्ना with 5. स), Ved. granting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">Page1099-b+ 73</a>]<BR>offering, generous; eager to gain or win or acquire;<BR>pure, holy, (Sāy. = शुद्ध, Ṛg-veda II. 18, 1);<BR>becoming lulled, (according to Sāy. = सन्निरुद्ध,<BR>and in this sense said to be fr. rt. सस्, Ṛg-veda III.<BR>15, 5; according to Nirukta V. 1. सस्नि = सं-<BR>स्नात = मेघ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्नेह
सस्नेह स-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing affec-<BR>tion, affectionate; (अम्), ind. affectionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्पृह
सस्पृह स-स्पृह, अस्, आ, अम्, filled with<BR>desire or longing, wishing for, desirous; (अम्), ind.<BR>wistfully, with passionate longing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्मित|सस्मितः
सस्मित स-स्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied<BR>with smiles, smiling, laughing; (अम्), ind. with a<BR>smile, smilingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्य|सस्यं
सस्य 1. सस्य, अम्, n. (for 1. शस्य, q. v.;<BR>in Uṇādi-s. IV. 109. said to be fr. rt. सस्), a good<BR>quality, excellence, merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यक|सस्यकः
1. सस्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of good qualities;<BR>(अस्), m. a sort of precious stone (coloured like the<BR>inner fruit of a cocoa-nut; perhaps an opal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्य|सस्यं
सस्य 2. सस्य, अम्, n. (for 2. शस्य, q. v.;<BR>said to be fr. rt. सस्), corn, grain; fruit; a weapon;<BR>[cf. perhaps Gr. εἴα, ἤϊον.]<BR>—सस्य-क्रेणी, f. buying<BR>grain.<BR>—सस्य-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, yielding corn,<BR>fertile.<BR>—सस्य-प्रवृद्धि, इस्, f. the growth of<BR>corn.<BR>—सस्य-मारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, corn-destroying,<BR>destructive of grain; (ई), m. a kind of rat or large<BR>mouse.<BR>—सस्य-संवर, अस्, m. the Śāl tree,<BR>Shorea Robusta.<BR>—सस्य-संवरण, अस्, m. the<BR>Aśva-karṇa tree.<BR>—सस्याद् (˚य-अद्), त्, त्, त्, eating<BR>grain or fruit, granivorous.<BR>—सस्येष्टि (˚य-इष्˚),<BR>इस्, f. sacrifice offered on the ripening of new grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यक|सस्यकः
2. सस्यक, अस्, m. a weapon, sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यद्
सस्यद् स-स्यद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. flowing toge-<BR>ther, (Sāy. = सह-स्यन्दमान, as an epithet of<BR>‘the waters,’ Ṛg-veda X. 113, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्र
सस्र सस्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. सृ), Ved.<BR>going, flowing, rapid, swift (said of rivers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससृवस्
ससृवस्, वान्, -रुषी, वत्, Ved. one who has<BR>gone, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्रि
सस्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, going, who or what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्रुत्
सस्रुत् सस्रुत्, त्, त्, त् (fr. rt. स्रु with 5. स<BR>or a reduplicated form), Ved. flowing or going toge-<BR>ther; flowing, (Sāy. = सह प्रवर्तमान and<BR>सरण-शील); (त्), f. a flowing stream, river (=<BR>नदी, Naigh. I. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वध
सस्वध स-स्वध, आस्, m. pl. (fr. स्वधा<BR>with स), having the Sva-dhā or food offered to<BR>deceased ancestors; epithet of a particular class of<BR>Pitṛs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वर्
सस्वर् सस्वर्, ind. secretly; secret, (Sāy.<BR>= अन्तर्हित; in Naigh. III. 25. enumerated among<BR>the निर्णीतान्तर्हित-नामधेयानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वेद
सस्वेद स-स्वेद, अस्, आ, अम्, moist with<BR>sweat; perspiring, exuding; (आ), f. a girl who has<BR>been recently deflowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्
सह् 1. सह् (perhaps for स-वह्, cf. सोढ<BR>for स-ऊढ), cl. 1. A. सहते (sometimes<BR>also P. -ति), सेहे, ससाह, सहिष्यते, असहिष्ट,<BR>सहितुम् or सोढुम् (Ved. साह्याम for सह्याम,<BR>Atharva-veda IV. 32, 1; सासहः = ससहः = अभि-<BR>भवसि, Vājasaneyi-s. XV. 40), to bear, bear patiently,<BR>suffer, endure, be patient; to allow; to be strong or<BR>able to bear up against or resist, overpower, over-<BR>come, conquer, defeat; to stop, keep back, suppress;<BR>to be able (with inf.); cl. 10. or Caus. साहयति,<BR>यितुम्, to cause to bear, make bearable, Aor. असी-<BR>सहत्: Desid. of Caus. सिसाहयिषति (Pāṇ. VIII.<BR>3, 62): Desid. सिसहिषते, to wish to bear: Intens.<BR>सासह्यते, सासोढि, to resist, defeat; [cf. Gr. ἔχ-ω<BR>for ἕχ-ω (i.e. (σ)έχ-ω), ἕξω, ἑχείης, ἐξῆς, ἔχ-ο-μαι,<BR>ἔ-σχο-ν, σχή-σω, ἔ-σχη-κα, σχέ-σι-ς, σχή-μα,<BR>σχο-λή, σχε-δόν, ἴσχ-ω (probably for σι-σεχ-ω),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">Page1099-c+ 81</a>]<BR>ἰσχανάω, ἐχ-υρό-ς, ὀχ-υρό-ς; according to some<BR>also Lat. sag-ax, sagus, sagio.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्
2. सह्, साट्, ट्, ट्, bearing, enduring, &c. (frequently<BR>at the end of comps., cf. वने-षह्, सत्रा-सह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
1. सह, अस्, आ, अम्, patient, enduring, suffering,<BR>bearing; able; (अस्), m. the month Mārga-śīrṣa,<BR>(see सहस्); epithet of Śiva; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>strength, power; (आ), f. the earth; N. of a division<BR>of the world (according to the Buddhists); the aloe<BR>plant or flower; a sort of bean (= मुद्ग-पर्णी);<BR>the perfume or drug Nakha; the plant Daṇḍot-<BR>pala; a sort of white Barleria; the ichneumon plant<BR>(= रास्ना); a kind of medicinal moon-plant; other<BR>plants, = सर्प-कङ्काली; = तरणी; (अम्), n. the<BR>salt called Pāṃśava.<BR>—१. सह-त्व, अम्, n. or सह-<BR>ता, f. sufferance, endurance, capacity for enduring.<BR>—सह-रक्ष, अस्, m. ‘preserving strength,’ epi-<BR>thet of the son of the Fire called Pavamāna.<BR>—सहा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing strength, strong,<BR>powerful.<BR>—सहा-वन्, Ved. = सहा-वत्, (Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 178, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहक
सहक, अस्, आ, अम्, enduring, bearing, patient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहन|सहनं|सहनः
सहन, अस्, आ, अम्, patient, enduring; (अम्), n.<BR>patience, endurance, forbearance, bearing, enduring.<BR>—सहन-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a patient disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहनीय
सहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne or endured,<BR>tolerable, endurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहन्त्य
सहन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. capable of overcom-<BR>ing or conquering (said of Agni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमान
1. सहमान, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. सह-मान see<BR>p. 1100, col. 2), bearing, enduring; overpowering,<BR>conquering, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्
सहस्, अस्, n. strength, force, power (= बल,<BR>Naigh. II. 9); overpowering, overcoming, conquer-<BR>ing, victory; light; water (= उदक, Naigh. I. 12);<BR>(आस्), m. the month Mārga-śīrṣa or Agrahāyaṇa<BR>(November-December); the winter season; (स-<BR>हसा), ind. with great force or precipitation, pre-<BR>cipitately, quickly, inconsiderately, on a sudden, at<BR>once; along with (= सह); [cf. Goth. sigis; Angl.<BR>Sax. sigor, sige.]<BR>—सहसस्-पुत्र, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>‘son of strength,’ epithet of Agni; of Brahmaṇas-<BR>pati.<BR>—सहसा-दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, suddenly beheld,<BR>seen quickly; (अस्), m. an adopted son.<BR>—सहसा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. powerful, mighty, (Sāy. =<BR>बल-वत्.)<BR>—सहस्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pro-<BR>duced by strength or force; made strong or powerful,<BR>strengthened; (अस्), m. epithet of Agni; of Indra.<BR>—सहस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing power, power-<BR>ful; (अत्), ind. powerfully, mightily (Ved.).<BR>—सहो-<BR>जा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. produced by power.<BR>—सहो-दा,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. strength-bestowing.<BR>—सहो-बल,<BR>अम्, n. great force or violence, cruelty.<BR>—सहो-<BR>भरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. strength-supporting, strength-<BR>nourishing.<BR>—सहो-वन्, Ved. = सहस्-वत्.<BR>—सहो-<BR>वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. increasing strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसान|सहसानः
सहसान, अस्, आ, अम्, patient, enduring; over-<BR>powering; (अस्), m. a peacock; sacrifice, oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसिन्
सहसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. powerful, strong, mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्य|सहस्यः
सहस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to strength, strong,<BR>vigorous (Ved.); coming from strength, being the<BR>offspring of might (Ved.); (अस्), m. the month<BR>Pauṣa (December-January).<BR>—सहस्य-चन्द्र,<BR>अस्, m. the wintry moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहा
सहा, सहा-वत्. See under 1. सह above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित|सहितः
1. सहित, अस्, आ, अम्, borne, endured, supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहितृ
सहितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a bearer, bearing, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित्र|सहित्रं
सहित्र, अम्, n. patience, endurance, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णु|सहिष्णुः
सहिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, able to support, capable of<BR>enduring, disposed to bear, patient, enduring, re-<BR>signed; (उस्), m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—सहिष्णु-ता,<BR>f. or सहिष्णु-त्व, अम्, n. ability to bear or sup-<BR>port; patience, resignation, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहीयस्
सहीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. fr. सोढृ), Ved.<BR>stronger, very strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहुरि|सहुरिः
सहुरि, इस्, इस्, इ, patient, enduring (Ved.); con-<BR>quering, victorious (Ved.); (इस्), m. epithet of Agni<BR>(Ved.); the sun; (इस्), f. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोर|सहोरः
सहोर, अस्, आ, अम्, good, excellent; (अस्), m. a<BR>saint, a pure or pious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्य|सह्यं|सह्यः
सह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne or endured,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">Page1100-a+ 80</a>]<BR>endurable, sufferable, tolerable; able to bear, adequate<BR>to, equal to; powerful, strong; sweet, agreeable;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of one of the seven principal ranges of<BR>mountains in India, (see कुलाचल); of the moun-<BR>tainous district on the north-west side of the Penin-<BR>sula (near Poonah; the Go-dāvarī river rises in this<BR>district); (अम्), n. health, convalescence; adequacy;<BR>assistance; [cf. according to some, Gr. σάο-ς, σα-ώ-τερο-ς,<BR>σῶο-ς, σῶς, σω-τήρ, σῶ-κο-ς, σώ-ζ-ω; per-<BR>haps Lat. sa-nu-s; Old Germ. ga-sunt; Angl. Sax.<BR>sund.]<BR>—सह्य-पर्वत, अस्, or सह्य-महीभृत्,<BR>त्, or सह्याद्रि, इस्, m. the Sahya range of moun-<BR>tains.<BR>—सह्याद्रि-खण्ड, N. of a section of the<BR>Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1099-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्यस्
सह्यस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. = सहीयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्यु
सह्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. conquering, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साढ
साढ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. overcome, conquered;<BR>[cf. अ-षाढ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साळ्हृ
साऌहृ, ऌहा, m., Ved. one who overcomes or<BR>conquers, a conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासहान
सासहान, अस्, आ, अम् (for ससहान), Ved. over-<BR>coming, conquering, oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासहि
सासहि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. the Intens.), able to bear much;<BR>overpowering, conquering, victorious (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासह्वस्
सासह्वस्, आन्, &c. (for ससह्वस्), Ved. one who<BR>has overcome, overcoming, conquering, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहन|साहनं
साहन, साहय, साहस, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वस्
साह्वस्, आन्, m. (in the Pada text सह्वस्), Ved. one<BR>who overcomes or subdues, mighty, (Sāy. = शत्रून्<BR>अभिभावुकः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीक्षत्
सीक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. a Vedic Desid.), Ved.<BR>desiring to overcome, anxious to conquer, (Sāy. =<BR>सोढुम्, i. e. अभिभवितुम् इच्छत्, Ṛg-veda VI.<BR>14, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढ|सोढः
सोढ, सोढृ, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्
सह् 3. सह् (connected with rt. सुह्), cl.<BR>4. P. सह्यति, ससाह, &c., to satisfy, de-<BR>light; to be pleased; to bear, endure; [cf. rt.<BR>1. सह्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
सह 2. सह, ind. (perhaps fr. 4. स or<BR>5. स + धा, which in Ved. may become ध, see<BR>स-ध), with, along with, together, together with<BR>(often used as a preposition governing the inst. case,<BR>but generally placed after the governed word; fre-<BR>quently also as a prefix in comp.; according to<BR>native lexicographers the following words express the<BR>senses which 2. सह may convey, साकल्यम्, विद्-<BR>यमानम्, सादृश्यम्, यौगपद्यम्, समृद्-<BR>धिः, सम्बन्धः, सामर्थ्यम्); [cf. probably<BR>Lat. soda-lis.] — 1. सह-कार, अस्, m. (for 2. स-<BR>हकार see p. 1101), acting with, co-operation; a<BR>sort of fragrant Mango tree.<BR>—सहकार-भञ्जिका,<BR>f. a sort of game.<BR>—सहकारि-ता, f. or सहकारि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. co-operation, assistance.<BR>—सह-कारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, or सह-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, one who acts toge-<BR>ther or co-operates with another, an assistant, coad-<BR>jutor, associate, co-operating, working together, assist-<BR>ing.<BR>—सह-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, co-operated with,<BR>assisted, aided.<BR>—सह-कृत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, co-<BR>operating, assisting; a coadjutor.<BR>—सह-गत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, gone with, accompanied, associated, going<BR>with.<BR>—सह-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति, -गन्तुम्,<BR>to go with, accompany.<BR>—सह-गमन, अम्, n. the<BR>act of going with or accompanying; a woman's<BR>going with her deceased husband (i. e. burning her-<BR>self with his dead body).<BR>—सह-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>going with, accompanying; (इनी), f. a woman who<BR>goes with her deceased husband (i. e. burns herself<BR>with his body).<BR>—सह-गोपास्, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>accompanied by a protector.<BR>—सह-ग्रह्, cl. 9. P.<BR>A. -गृह्णाति, -गृह्णीते, -ग्रहीतुम्, to take along<BR>with, carry off with.<BR>—सह-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going<BR>with, accompanying, associating with; (अस्), m. a<BR>companion, follower; a friend; a surety; the shrub<BR>Barleria Cristata, yellow and blue Barleria; (ई), f.<BR>a female companion, female friend, confidante; a<BR>wife; yellow Barleria.<BR>—सह-चरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्,<BR>going with, accompanying, attending.<BR>—सह-च-<BR>रित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone with; going with, accom-<BR>panying, attending, associating with.<BR>—सह-चार,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-b" target="_blank">Page1100-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. going together; harmony, agreement; the<BR>accompanyment of the middle term by the major;<BR>right course, (opposed to व्य्-अभिचार.)<BR>—सह-<BR>चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going along with, a companion,<BR>friend, attendant.<BR>—सह-च्छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. along with metre.<BR>—सह-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born<BR>or produced together, born from the same mother,<BR>connate, congenital, innate, inherent, naturally be-<BR>longing to, natural, co-existent; (अस्), m, a brother<BR>of whole blood; the natural state or disposition;<BR>epithet of the third astrological mansion; a proper<BR>N.<BR>—सह-जग्धि, इस्, f. eating together.<BR>—सह-<BR>जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, = सह-ज above; (आ), f., N. of<BR>an Aspsaras.<BR>—सह-जन्या, f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—सहज-मित्र, अस्, m. a natural friend, one<BR>friendly by birth (as a sister's son, cousin, &c.).<BR>—सहज-वत्सल, अस्, आ, अम्, having innate fond-<BR>ness, naturally fond.<BR>—सहज-शत्रु, उस्, m. = स-<BR>हजारि.<BR>—सह-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born together,<BR>born from the same mother, twin-born.<BR>—सहजा-<BR>धिनाथ (˚ज-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—स-<BR>हजारि (˚ज-अरि), इस्, m. a natural enemy, one hostile<BR>by birth (as the son of the same father by another<BR>mother, the son of a paternal uncle, &c.).<BR>—सह-<BR>जेतर (˚ज-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, other than natural, not<BR>innate, not inherent, not congenital, accidental.<BR>—सहजेन्द्र (˚ज-इन्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—सहजोदासीन (˚ज-उद्˚), अस्, m. a born neutral,<BR>one who is naturally neither an enemy nor a friend,<BR>a common acquaintance, a friend unconnected by<BR>birth.<BR>—२. सह-ता, f. or सह-त्व, अम्, n. associ-<BR>ation, connection, union.<BR>—सह-दार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>along with a wife, married.<BR>—सह-देव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi (having the patronymic Vār-<BR>ṣāgira, q. v.); of the youngest of the five Pāṇḍava<BR>princes (son of Mādrī and reputed son of Pāṇḍu,<BR>but really of the Aśvins, and twin-brother of Nakula,<BR>see माद्री); of a person renowned as a swordsman;<BR>of a son of Sṛñjaya; of a son of Harṣa-vardhana;<BR>of a son of Su-dāsa; of a son of Jarā-sandha; of a<BR>son of Divākara; (आ), f. a kind of Balā plant; the<BR>twining shrub Echites Frutescens; the plant Daṇ-<BR>ḍotpala; another plant (= शरिवा); the mother of<BR>an Arhat; N. of a daughter of Devaka; (ई), f. the<BR>wife of Saha-deva; a sort of Balā plant; a yellow<BR>Daṇḍotpala; the shrub Priyaṅgu; another plant<BR>(= सर्पाक्षी).<BR>—सहदेवी-गण, अस्, m. a collec-<BR>tion of herbs used in certain rites of ablution at the<BR>consecration of an idol, &c.<BR>—सह-द्रोण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, along with Droṇa, accompanied by Droṇa.<BR>—सह-धर्म, अस्, m. community of duty or<BR>law, common usage or characteristic.<BR>—सह-धर्-<BR>म-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, one following the same law<BR>or duties.<BR>—सह-धर्मचारिन्, ई, m. a helper in<BR>the fulfilment of duties, a husband; (इणी), f. a<BR>woman who aids in fulfilling duties, helpmate, legiti-<BR>mate wife.<BR>—सह-धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, following<BR>the same duties or customs; possessing similar pro-<BR>perties; (इणी), f. a lawful or legitimate wife.<BR>—स-<BR>ह-नर्तन, अम्, n. the act of dancing together.<BR>—सह-पत्नी, f., Ved. (a woman) along with her<BR>husband.<BR>—सह-पथिन्, -पन्थास्, -पथी, m. f.<BR>going by the same road, a companion on a journey,<BR>fellow-traveller.<BR>—सह-पांशु-किल, अस्, m. ‘one<BR>who has played with another in the sand,’ a friend<BR>from childhood, cotemporary.<BR>—सह-पान or सह-<BR>पानक, अम्, n. drinking together.<BR>—सह-पिण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. a kinsman, (see स-पिण्ड.)<BR>—सह-पुत्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, along with a son, accompanied by a son.<BR>—सह-<BR>पूर्वाह्णम्, ind. like the forenoon, (Vopa-deva VI.<BR>61.)<BR>—सह-भार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, along with a wife,<BR>accompanied by a wife.<BR>—सह-भाविन्, ई, m. being<BR>together, a friend, companion, adherent, partisan.<BR>—सह-भोजन, अम्, n. eating together, eating in<BR>company; joint possession.<BR>—सह-भ्रातृ, ता, त्री,<BR>तृ, along with a brother, accompanied by a brother<BR>or brothers.<BR>—सह-मरण, अम्, n. dying toge-<BR>ther, concremation, a widow's burning herself with<BR>the corpse of her husband.<BR>—२. सह-मान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (for 1. see under rt. 1. सह्), possessing pride,<BR>full of arrogance.<BR>—सह-मारीच, अस्, आ, अम्, ac-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-c" target="_blank">Page1100-c+ 81</a>]<BR>companied by Mārīca.<BR>—१. सह-मूर, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>(मूर = मूढ), Ved. infatuated, bewildered, con-<BR>fused.<BR>—२. सह-मूर, अस्, आ, अम्, along with the<BR>root, (Sāy. = मूलेन सहित, Ṛg-veda X. 87, 19.)<BR>—सह-मृता, f. a woman who has burnt herself<BR>on the funeral pile of her husband.<BR>—सह-यायिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, going along with, going together, accom-<BR>panying.<BR>—सह-युध्वन्, आ, &c., fighting together,<BR>fighting in company, a brother-in-arms.<BR>—सह-<BR>रक्षस्, one of the three kinds of sacrificial fire<BR>(viz. that which receives the offerings to the Rāk-<BR>ṣasas).<BR>—सह-रसा, f. a sort of bean (= मुद्ग-<BR>पर्णी).<BR>—सह-लक्ष्मण, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—सह-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>being together, keeping company.<BR>—सह-वसति,<BR>इस्, f. dwelling together.<BR>—सह-वसु, उस्, m., Ved.<BR>‘having wealth,’ N. of an Asura (an enemy of<BR>Indra).<BR>—सह-वह् or सह-वाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. draw-<BR>ing together (said of horses).<BR>—सह-वास, अस्, m.<BR>one who lives with another, a fellow-lodger; dwell-<BR>ing together.<BR>—सह-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living together.<BR>—सह-वाहन, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by an<BR>army; with vehicles.<BR>—सह-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>accompanied with heroes, together with sons or<BR>progeny.<BR>—सह-शेय्य, अम्, n., Ved. the lying<BR>together with.<BR>—सह-स्तोम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. along<BR>with hymns.<BR>—सहा-चर, अस्, m. (for सह-चर),<BR>yellow Barleria.<BR>—सहाध्ययन (˚ह-अध्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a reading together, fellowship in study.<BR>—सहा-<BR>ध्यायिन् (˚ह-अध्˚), ई, m. a fellow student, fellow<BR>disciple, condisciple.<BR>—सहानुज (˚ह-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, along with a younger brother.<BR>—सहापत्य<BR>(˚ह-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, along with offspring.<BR>—सहा-<BR>पवाद (˚ह-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, containing contradic-<BR>tions, disagreeing.<BR>—सहामात्य (˚ह-अम्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having councillors, attended by ministers.<BR>—स-<BR>हाय, सहायक, &c., see below.<BR>—सहारोग्य<BR>(˚ह-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessing freedom from<BR>disease, healthful.<BR>—सहार्थ (˚ह-अर्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>common object; (अस्, आ, अम्), having the same<BR>object, having the same meaning, synonymous.<BR>—सहार्थ-नाश, अस्, आ, अम्, one who is the<BR>same in profit and loss.<BR>—सहासन (˚ह-आस्˚), अम्,<BR>n. sitting on the same seat.<BR>—सहेति (˚ह-इति), इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, along with the particle इति, followed by इति.<BR>—सहेतिकरण or सहेतिकार, अम्, n., scil. पद,<BR>a word followed by the particle इति; [cf. सेतिक-<BR>रण.]<BR>—सहोक्ति (˚ह-उक्˚), इस्, f. speaking at the<BR>same time; a figure of rhetoric (either employing<BR>a word in a double meaning, or connecting different<BR>ideas by using the word सह).<BR>—सहोटज (˚ह-<BR>उट्˚), अस्, m. a cabin or hut made of leaves, (sometimes<BR>erected on the funeral pile of an ascetic and burnt<BR>with the body).<BR>—१. सहोढ (˚ह-ऊढ), अस्, m.<BR>(for 2. स-होढ see p. 1102), the son of a woman<BR>pregnant at marriage.<BR>—सहोढ-ज, अस्, m. the son<BR>of a woman pregnant at marriage.<BR>—सहोदय<BR>(˚ह-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, together with the following<BR>(words, letters, &c.).<BR>—सहोदर (˚ह-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘co-uterine,’ a brother of whole blood; [cf. सोदर.]<BR>—सहोदित (˚ह-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, said together,<BR>declared comprehensively or collectively.<BR>—सहोप-<BR>ध (˚ह-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, along with a penultimate<BR>letter.<BR>—सहोपमा (˚ह-उप्˚), f. ‘comparison by<BR>the word सह,’ a particular figure of speech which<BR>by coupling two objects implies their similarity.<BR>—सहोरु (˚ह-ऊरु), उस्, ऊस्, उ, along with thighs,<BR>having thighs.<BR>—सहोषित (˚ह-उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dwelling or abiding together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाय|सहायः
सहाय, अस्, m. (i. e. सह-अय), one who goes<BR>along with (another), a companion, follower, adhe-<BR>rent, ally; a helper, patron; epithet of Śiva; the<BR>ruddy goose; a sort of drug or perfume (= घण्टा-<BR>पाटली).<BR>—सहाय-करण, अम्, n. the act of ren-<BR>dering assistance, aiding.<BR>—सहाय-ता, f. or सहाय-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. companionship, union, association,<BR>friendship, assistance, help; a number of companions,<BR>company of associates or followers.<BR>—सहाय-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having a companion, accompanied, be-<BR>friended, assisted.<BR>—सहायार्थिन् (˚य-अर्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, seeking a companion, desirous of an ally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायक
सहायक, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by (at the<BR>end of an adj. comp., e. g. नारायण-स्˚, accompa-<BR>nied by Nārāyaṇa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहावत्|सहावन्त्
सहा-वत्. See under 1. सह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित|सहितः
2. सहित, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 3. see col. 3), accompa-<BR>nied or attended by, associated or connected with, in<BR>company with, with (with inst. or at the end of<BR>comps.), possessed of; (अम्), ind. with, along with,<BR>together with.<BR>—सहित-कुम्भक, अस्, m. epithet<BR>of a particular mode of suppressing the breath, (see<BR>प्राणायाम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहंसपात
सहंसपात स-हंस-पात, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied with flights of swans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकार|सहकारः
सहकार 2. स-हकार, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. सह-<BR>कार see under 2. सह), having the sound ह, i. e.<BR>the sound used in calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहण्डुक|सहण्डुकं
सहण्डुक सहण्डुक, अम्, n. a particular<BR>kind of condiment prepared with meat &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहम
सहम सहम, अम्, n. (fr. Arabic सह्म्),<BR>good or evil luck arising from the influence of the<BR>stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहय
सहय स-हय, अस्, आ, अम्, having horses,<BR>along with horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहरि|सहरिः
सहरि स-हरि, ind. resembling Hari or<BR>Viṣṇu; (इस्), m. the sun; a bull (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहर्ष|सहर्षः
सहर्ष स-हर्ष, अस्, m. joyfulness, envy,<BR>emulation; pleasure, delight; (अम्), ind. joyfully,<BR>cheerfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहलनीय
सहलनीय स-हलनीय, अस्, m. (probably)<BR>a plough-mate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्त
सहस्त स-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, dexterous or<BR>skilled in handling weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्र|सहस्रं
सहस्र सहस्र, अम्, n. (perhaps connected<BR>with सहस्; cf. Pers. hazār), a thousand (used in<BR>the sing. with a plur. noun, e. g. सहस्रम् पितरः<BR>or सहस्रम् पितॄणाम्, a thousand ancestors; and<BR>used with other numerals thus, एकाधिकं सहस्रम्<BR>or एक-सहस्रम्, a thousand + one, 1001; द्व्य्-<BR>अधिकं सहस्रम्, a thousand + two, 1002;<BR>एकादशाधिकं सहस्रम् or एकादशं सह-<BR>स्रम् or एकादश-सहस्रम्, a thousand + eleven<BR>or a thousand having eleven, 1011; विन्शत्य्-अधि-<BR>कं सहस्रम् or विन्शं सहस्रम्, a thousand<BR>+ twenty, 1020); any very large number (enume-<BR>rated among the बहु-नामानि in Naigh. III. 1;<BR>cf. सहस्र-किरण &c. below); (ए), n. du. two<BR>thousand (= द्वे सहस्रे, द्वि-सहस्रम्); (आणि),<BR>n. pl. thousands (e. g. त्रीणि सहस्राणि or त्रि-<BR>सहस्राणि, three thousand); (अस्, ई, अम्), thousandth,<BR>(but सहस्र-तम is the better form, cf. Pāṇ. V.<BR>2, 57.)<BR>—सहस्र-काण्डा, f. ‘many-jointed,’ white<BR>Dūrvā grass.<BR>—सहस्र-किरण, अस्, m. ‘thousand-<BR>rayed,’ the sun.<BR>—सहस्र-कृत्वस्, ind. a thousand<BR>times, many times.<BR>—सहस्र-केतु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. thousand-bannered, having many banners.<BR>—सहस्र-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, possessing a thousand<BR>cows.<BR>—सहस्र-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, a thousandfold.<BR>—सहस्र-घ्नि, Ved. smiting thousands, (Atharva-<BR>veda XI. 2, 12.)<BR>—सहस्र-चरण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>thousand-footed.<BR>—सहस्र-जित्, त्, त्, त्, conquering<BR>a thousand (Ved.); (त्), m., N. of a son of Yadu;<BR>of a son of Bhajamāna.<BR>—सहस्र-तम, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>thousandth, the thousandth.<BR>—सहस्र-द, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, giving thousands, liberal; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सहस्र-दंष्ट्र, अस्, or सहस्र-दंष्-<BR>ट्रिन्, ई, m. ‘thousand-toothed,’ a sort of sheat fish,<BR>Silurus Pelorius.<BR>—सहस्र-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a thousand rewards.<BR>—सहस्र-दा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, Ved. giving a thousand, very liberal.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>दातु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. thousandfold.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>दावन्, आ, m., Ved. a giver of thousands.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>दृश्, क्, m. ‘thousand-eyed,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—सहस्र-दोस्, स्, m. ‘having a thousand arms,’<BR>epithet of Arjuna Kārtavīrya.<BR>—सहस्र-द्वार, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, thousand-gated.<BR>—सहस्र-धा, ind. in a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-b" target="_blank">Page1101-b+ 81</a>]<BR>thousand ways, thousandfold, in a thousand parts or<BR>portions.<BR>—सहस्र-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘thou-<BR>sand-streamed,’ flowing in a thousand streams; hav-<BR>ing a thousand edges; (अस्), m. the discus of Viṣṇu;<BR>(आ), f. a stream of water for the ablution of an idol<BR>conveyed through a vessel pierced with a multitude<BR>of little holes like a shower-bath.<BR>—सहस्र-न-<BR>यन, अस्, m. ‘thousand-eyed,’ an epithet of Indra;<BR>[cf. सहस्राक्ष.]<BR>—सहस्र-नामन्, अ, n. the<BR>thousand names (of Viṣṇu, Śiva, or any deity);<BR>(आ, &c.), thousand-named, having a thousand names.<BR>—सहस्रनाम-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. ‘hymn of a thou-<BR>sand names,’ N. of a Tantra hymn.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>निर्णिज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. having a thousand ornaments<BR>(said of the car of the Aśvins).<BR>—सहस्र-नीथ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praised in a thousand hymns;<BR>skilled in a thousand sciences.<BR>—सहस्र-नेत्र, अस्,<BR>m. ‘thousand-eyed,’ epithet of Indra.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>पति, इस्, m. lord of a thousand towns, governor of<BR>a district.<BR>—सहस्र-पत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘having a thou-<BR>sand leaves,’ a lotus.<BR>—सहस्रपत्त्राभरण<BR>(˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having lotus ornaments,<BR>decorated with lotuses.<BR>—सहस्र-पाजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. having infinite splendor or might, glittering a<BR>thousandfold.<BR>—सहस्र-पाद्, -पात्, -पदी, -पात्,<BR>thousand-footed, milliped; (त्), m. epithet of Pu-<BR>rusha (as described in the Puruṣa-sūkta, q. v.); of<BR>Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of Brahmā.<BR>—सहस्र-पाद, अस्,<BR>m. ‘thousand-footed’ or ‘thousand-rayed,’ the sun;<BR>Viṣṇu; a sort of duck (= कारण्डव).<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>पोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. nourishing a thousand.<BR>—स-<BR>हस्र-प्रधन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who has<BR>experienced a thousand battles.<BR>—सहस्र-बल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—सहस्र-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, having<BR>a thousand arms; (उस्), m. epithet of Śiva; of the<BR>Asura Vāṇa.<BR>—सहस्र-भर्णस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. a<BR>thousandfold; having unlimited food; [cf. भर्णस्.]<BR>—सहस्र-भुज, अस्, m. ‘having a thousand arms,’<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; (आ), f. epithet of Durgā.<BR>—स-<BR>हस्र-भृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a thousand<BR>points, thousand-edged.<BR>—सहस्र-मन्यु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. filled with unbounded passion, filled with<BR>infinite splendor.<BR>—सहस्र-मरीचि, इस्, m. ‘thou-<BR>sand-rayed,’ epithet of the sun.<BR>—सहस्र-मीढ<BR>or सहस्र-मीऌह, अस्, आ, अम् (see मीढ, p. 780,<BR>col. 1), Ved. possessing or yielding a thousand trea-<BR>sures; (अम्), n. a battle.<BR>—सहस्र-मुष्क, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having a thousand testicles (said of Indra,<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 46, 3); having many flames (said of<BR>Agni; Sāy. = बहु-तेजस्क, Ṛg-veda VIII. 19, 32).<BR>—सहस्र-मूर्ध, अस्, m. ‘thousand-headed,’<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सहस्र-मूर्धन्, आ, m.<BR>‘thousand-headed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>मूली, f. ‘having a thousand roots,’ a kind of plant<BR>(= द्रवन्ती).<BR>—सहस्र-मौलि, इस्, m. ‘thousand-<BR>crested,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सहस्र-यज्ञ-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सहस्र-याज्, ट्, m. one<BR>who sacrifices a thousand victims.<BR>—सहस्र-युग,<BR>अम्, n. a period of a thousand ages.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>रश्मि, इस्, m. ‘thousand-rayed,’ the sun.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>रेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. containing inexhaustible seed.<BR>—सहस्र-रोमन्, अ, n. ‘having a thousand hairs,’<BR>a blanket.<BR>—सहस्र-वदन, अस्, m. ‘thousand-<BR>faced,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सहस्र-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. having infinite splendor or power.<BR>—स-<BR>हस्र-वर्तनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a thousand<BR>paths.<BR>—सहस्र-वर्तनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a thou-<BR>sand wheels.<BR>—सहस्र-वल्श, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having a thousand branches, thousand-branched.<BR>—सहस्र-वाज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. possessing infinite<BR>strength.<BR>—सहस्र-वीर्या, f. a kind of Dūrvā or<BR>bent grass, Panicum Dactylon; another plant (=<BR>महा-शतावरी).<BR>—सहस्र-वेध, अम्, n. sorrel;<BR>a kind of sour gruel.<BR>—सहस्र-वेधिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘thousand-piercer,’ a sort of cane, Calamus Fascicu-<BR>latus, = कस्तूरी; (इ), n. Asa Fœtida.<BR>—सहस्र-<BR>शत-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by hundreds<BR>of thousands of sacrificial fees.<BR>—सहस्र-शस्, ind. by<BR>thousands, in a thousand ways, thousandfold.<BR>—स-<BR>हस्र-शिखर, अस्, m. ‘thousand-peaked,’ the<BR>Vindhya mountain.<BR>—सहस्र-शीर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-c" target="_blank">Page1101-c+ 78</a>]<BR>or सहस्र-शीर्षन्, आ, आ, अ, thousand-headed, hav-<BR>ing a thousand heads.<BR>—सहस्र-शृङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>thousand-horned, having a thousand horns.<BR>—स-<BR>हस्र-श्रवण, अस्, m. ‘having a thousand ears,’<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सहस्र-सङ्ख्या, f. the sum of<BR>a thousand.<BR>—सहस्र-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. giving or<BR>bestowing a thousand.<BR>—सहस्र-सम्मित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, measuring or numbering a thousand, a thousand<BR>in number.<BR>—सहस्र-सव, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>thousand libations.<BR>—सहस्र-सा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>granting a thousand, bringing a thousand (treasures).<BR>—सहस्र-सातम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving thou-<BR>sands.<BR>—सहस्र-स्तुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a<BR>thousand tufts or curls of hair.<BR>—सहस्र-स्थूण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. supported by a thousand columns.<BR>—सहस्र-हर्य्-अश्व, अस्, m. ‘having a thousand<BR>bay horses,’ the car of Indra.<BR>—सहस्र-हस्त, अस्,<BR>m. ‘thousand-handed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सह-<BR>स्रांशु (˚र-अं˚), उस्, m. ‘thousand-rayed,’ the<BR>sun.<BR>—सहस्रांशु-ज, अस्, m. ‘sun-born,’ epithet of<BR>Saturn.<BR>—सहस्राक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, ‘thou-<BR>sand-eyed,’ all-perceiving, all-inspecting, vigilant, all-<BR>powerful; (अस्), m. an epithet of Indra (so called,<BR>according to one legend, in consequence of the curse<BR>of the sage Gautama, who, detecting him in the<BR>desire to seduce his wife Ahalyā, covered him with<BR>a thousand marks resembling the female organ, which<BR>he afterwards changed to eyes; a different legend is<BR>related in Rāmāyaṇa 1. 48); epithet of Puruṣa (in<BR>the Puruṣa-sūkta, q. v.); of Viṣṇu; epithet of Fire<BR>and Rudra (as identified with Fire in the Upani-<BR>shads); of Śiva; N. of a place; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>goddess.<BR>—सहस्राचार (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m. a sort of<BR>yellow Barleria, Barleria Prionitis; [cf. सह-चर.]<BR>—सहस्राधिपति (˚र-अध्˚), इस्, m. the governor<BR>of a thousand villages, chief of a district.<BR>—सहस्रा-<BR>नन (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘thousand-faced,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—सहस्रानीक (˚र-अन्˚) or सहस्राणीक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king (son of Śatānīka, q. v.).<BR>—स-<BR>हस्रापसस् (˚र-अप्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having a<BR>thousand forms or shapes.<BR>—सहस्रा-मघ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम् (for सहस्र-मघ), Ved. having thousands<BR>of gifts, giving thousands, (Sāy. = बहु-धन.)<BR>—सहस्रार (˚र-अर), अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘having a<BR>thousand lines or divisions,’ a kind of receptacle said<BR>to be found in the top of the head and to resemble<BR>a lotus reversed, (it is fabled to be the seat of the<BR>soul.)<BR>—सहस्रार्घ (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. equi-<BR>valent to a thousand.<BR>—सहस्रार्चिस् (˚र-अर्˚), इस्,<BR>m. ‘thousand-rayed,’ the sun.<BR>—सहस्रावर (˚र-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. a fine below a thousand or from five<BR>hundred to a thousand Paṇas.<BR>—सहस्रावर्तक-<BR>तीर्थ (˚र-आव्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सह-<BR>स्राश्व (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘having a thousand<BR>horses,’ N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

