सहोढ|सहोढः
सहोढ 2. स-होढ, अस्, m. (for 1. सहोढ<BR>see p. 1100, col. 3), ‘having stolen goods,’ a thief<BR>caught with stolen property upon him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोदर|सहोदरः
सहोदर सहोदर. See p. 1100, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोर|सहोरः
सहोर सहोर. See p. 1099, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सा
सा 1. सा, f. (nom. fem. of the pronoun<BR>तद्, see 4. स), she; N. of Lakṣmī; of Gaurī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सा
सा 2. सा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (fr. rt. 1. सन्), Ved.<BR>giving, bestowing, granting (at the end of a comp.,<BR>e. g. सहस्र-सा, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
1. सात, अस्, आ, अम्, given, bestowed; (अम्), n.,<BR>Ved. a gift, present, wealth, riches, (Sāy. सातानि =<BR>धनानि, Ṛg-veda II. 24, 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साति|सातिः
1. साति, इस्, f. gaining, obtaining, acquisition, (Sāy.<BR>सातये = लाभाय); gift, giving, dispensing; honour-<BR>ing, helping, help; wealth [cf. 2. सति, 1. सन्ति];<BR>(इस्), m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानसि|सानसिः
सानसि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. granting, giving; enjoyable,<BR>full of enjoyment, (Sāy. = सम्भजनीय); (इस्), m.<BR>gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सा
सा 3. सा = rt. सो, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
2. सात, अस्, आ, अम्, (regarded as an irregular part.<BR>fr. rt. सो), destroyed. (For 3. सात see p. 1104,<BR>col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साति|सातिः
2. साति, इस्, f. end, conclusion; cessation; destruc-<BR>tion; sharp pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयमन
सांयमन सांयमन, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>यमन), relating to restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयात्रिक|सांयात्रिकः
सांयात्रिक सांयात्रिक, अस्, m. (fr. सं-<BR>यात्रा), a voyaging merchant, one who trades by<BR>sea, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयुगीन|सांयुगीनः
सांयुगीन सांयुगीन, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>युग), relating to war or battle; warlike, martial,<BR>skilled in war; (अस्), m. a soldier skilled in war,<BR>great warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांराविण|सांराविणं
सांराविण सांराविण, अम्, n. (fr. सं-राव or<BR>सं-राविन्), general acclamation or calling out of a<BR>number of people together, a general shout, crying<BR>or complaining aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सर|सांवत्सरः
सांवत्सर सांवत्सर, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>वत्सर), yearly, annual, perennial, lasting or occupy-<BR>ing a year; (अस्), m. an astrologer; an almanac-<BR>maker.<BR>—सांवत्सर-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a chapter<BR>of Bhaṭṭotpala's commentary on the Bṛhat-saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरक
सांवत्सरक or सांवत्सरिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>yearly, annual, relating to a year, produced in a year,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">Page1102-b+ 70</a>]<BR>&c.; (अस्), m. an astrologer.<BR>—सांवत्सरिक-<BR>श्राद्ध, अम्, n. an annual funeral ceremony in<BR>honour of deceased ancestors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरीय
सांवत्सरीय, अस्, ई, अम्, = सांवत्सर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवरण
सांवरण सांवरण, अस्, m. ‘son of Saṃ-<BR>varaṇa,’ a patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवादिक|सांवादिकः
सांवादिक सांवादिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>वाद), colloquial, controversial, causing discussion;<BR>(अस्), m. a disputant, controversialist, logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवृत्तिक
सांवृत्तिक सांवृत्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>वृत्ति), phenomenal, illusory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांशयिक|सांशयिकः
सांशयिक सांशयिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सं-<BR>शय), dubious, doubtful; in doubt, uncertain, ir-<BR>resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसारिक
सांसारिक सांसारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>सार), worldly, belonging to the world, mundane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धिक
सांसिद्धिक सांसिद्धिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>सिद्धि), effected naturally, belonging to nature,<BR>natural, native, innate; absolute, existing absolutely;<BR>effected by supernatural means (as spells).<BR>—सां-<BR>सिद्धिक-द्रव, अस्, m. natural (as opposed to<BR>generated) fluidity, (it belongs to water only.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्थानिक|सांस्थानिकः
सांस्थानिक सांस्थानिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सं-<BR>स्थान), relating or belonging to a common place<BR>of abode; (अस्), m. an inhabitant or native of the<BR>same place; fellow-countryman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्राविण|सांस्राविणं
सांस्राविण सांस्राविण, अम्, n. (fr. सं-<BR>स्राव or सं-स्राविन्), a general stream or flow (of<BR>water &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांहननिक
सांहननिक सांहननिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-<BR>हनन), relating to the body, bodily, corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांहित
सांहित सांहित, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. संहिता), re-<BR>lating to the Saṃhitā, found in the Saṃhitā text;<BR>(ई), f., N. of an Upaniṣad (= तैत्तिरीयोपनिषद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक|साकं
साक साक, अम्, n. (for शाक, q. v.), a vege-<BR>table, herb, pot-herb.<BR>—साक-मेध, आस्, m. pl., Ved.<BR>the Sāka sacrifice (observed on the full moon of<BR>Kārttika and following day).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकच्
साकच् साकच् (स-अक्˚), having the Taddhita<BR>affix अकच् (in grammar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकम्
साकम् साकम्, ind. (probably fr. स + rt. 1.<BR>अञ्च्, see साचि), with, together with (with inst.), at<BR>the same time.<BR>—साकं-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being<BR>born together.<BR>—साकं-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. joined<BR>together.<BR>—साकं-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. increasing<BR>along with or at the same time.<BR>—साकम्-उक्ष्,<BR>Ved. sprinkling at the same time.<BR>—साकम्-प्र-<BR>स्थाय्य, a particular kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल
साकल साकल, अम्, n., N. of a town in the<BR>Pañjāb (also read शाकल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल्य|साकल्यं
साकल्य साकल्य, अम्, n. (fr. सकल), to-<BR>tality, entireness, completeness, the whole, entire,<BR>all; (एन), ind. completely.<BR>—साकल्य-वचन, अम्,<BR>n. a complete perusal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकाङ्क्ष|साकांक्ष
साकाङ्क्ष साकाङ्क्ष (स-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a wish or desire, wishing, desirous; having<BR>significance; (अम्), ind. with longing desire, wish-<BR>fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकार|साकारः
साकार साकार (स-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>form, having any shape or definite figure.<BR>—साकार-<BR>सिद्धि, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकुरुण्ड|साकुरुण्डः
साकुरुण्ड साकुरुण्ड, अस्, m. yellow Ama-<BR>ranth or Barleria (= कुरुण्ड, सकुरुण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकुल
साकुल साकुल (स-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, per-<BR>plexed, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूत
साकूत साकूत (स-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>significance or meaning, intentional; significant;<BR>amorous, wanton; (अम्), ind. intentionally, signi-<BR>ficantly, impressively; attentively.<BR>—साकूत-स्मित,<BR>अम्, n. a meaning smile, amorous smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेत|साकेतं
साकेत साकेत, अम्, n., N. of the city Ayo-<BR>dhyā or ancient Oude; (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants<BR>of Sāketa or Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेतक|साकेतकः
साकेतक, अस्, m. an inhabitant of Sāketa; (अम्),<BR>n. = साकेत above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्तुक|साक्तुकं|साक्तुकः
साक्तुक साक्तुक, अस्, m. (fr. सक्तु), barley;<BR>(अम्), n. a quantity of fried barley or barley-meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष
साक्ष 1. साक्ष (स-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (see 2.<BR>अक्ष) , having the seeds of which rosaries are made,<BR>having a rosary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष
साक्ष 2. साक्ष (स-अक्˚), having eyes, (see<BR>4. अक्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्
साक्षात्, ind. (properly abl. c. of the above), be-<BR>fore the eyes, in sight of, in presence of, before;<BR>eye to eye, visibly, evidently, openly, manifestly;<BR>visibly present, visibly manifested as, like; with one's<BR>own eyes.<BR>—साक्षात्-करण, अम्, n. or साक्षात्-<BR>कार, अस्, m. causing to be visibly present; making<BR>evident to the senses; intuitive perception, actual feel-<BR>ing.<BR>—साक्षात्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make<BR>evident to the senses, place clearly before the mind.<BR>—साक्षात्कृत-धर्मन्, आ, m. one who has a<BR>real or intuitive perception of duty.<BR>—साक्षाद्-<BR>धर्म, अस्, m. the personified incarnation of law<BR>or justice; Justice himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिक
साक्षिक, in अ-स्˚, लोक-स्˚, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिन्
साक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, observing, witnessing, seeing;<BR>attesting, testifying, giving evidence; (ई), m. an<BR>observer; an eye-witness; any witness (in law).<BR>—साक्षि-ता, f. or साक्षि-त्व, अम्, n. the office of<BR>a witness, evidence, testimony, attestation.<BR>—साक्षि-<BR>द्वैध, अम्, n. discrepancy between witnesses,<BR>contradictory evidence.<BR>—साक्षि-परीक्षा, f. or<BR>साक्षि-परीक्षण, अम्, n. examination of a wit-<BR>ness.<BR>—साक्षि-प्रत्यय, अस्, m. the evidence or<BR>testimony of witnesses.<BR>—साक्षि-प्रश्न, अस्, m.<BR>interrogating witnesses, examination of witnesses.<BR>—साक्षिप्रश्न-विधान, अम्, n. the rule or law<BR>about examining witnessess.<BR>—साक्षि-भावित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, proved by an eye-witness, established by testi-<BR>mony.<BR>—साक्षि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having or re-<BR>quiring evidence.<BR>—साक्षि-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>defined or proved by testimony.<BR>—साक्षि-वत्, ind.<BR>like a witness.<BR>—साक्ष्य्-अभाव, अस्, m. absence or<BR>want of witnesses, absence of testimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षीकृ
साक्षी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to call to<BR>witness, cause to attest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षीकृत्य
साक्षी-कृत्य, ind. having called to witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्य|साक्ष्यं
साक्ष्य, अम्, n. testimony, evidence, attestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षत
साक्षत साक्षत (स-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>interrupted; possessing grain; (अम्), ind. uninter-<BR>ruptedly.<BR>—साक्षत-पात्र-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing a cup of grain in the hand, holding a vessel full<BR>of parched grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षर|साक्षरं
साक्षर साक्षर (स-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>syllables or letters; containing syllables, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षेप
साक्षेप साक्षेप (स-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>veying reproach or irony, taunting; (अम्), ind. with<BR>contumely, reproachfully, reproachingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साखिदत्तेय
