साखोट
साखोट साखोट for शाखोट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागर|सागरः
सागर सागर, अस्, m. (fr. सगर), the<BR>ocean (said to have been named Sāgara by Bha-<BR>gīratha after his ancestor king Sagara, see the<BR>legend under स-गर; another legend asserts that<BR>the bed of the ocean was dug by the sons of Sagara;<BR>according to various authorities three or four or seven<BR>oceans are enumerated, see 1. सम्-उद्र); a symboli-<BR>cal term for the number four; a sort of deer; N. of<BR>a place; of an author; of a work.<BR>—सागर-ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, going to the ocean; (आ), f. epithet of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">Page1103-a+ 74</a>]<BR>Ganges; a river, stream.<BR>—सागर-गामिनी, f. ‘ocean-<BR>going,’ a river.<BR>—सागरगा-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of<BR>the Ganges,’ epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR>—सागरङ्-गम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, flowing to the ocean.<BR>—सागर-दत्त,<BR>अस्, m. ‘Ocean-given,’ a proper N.<BR>—सागर-धीर-<BR>चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, whose mind is as firm or as deep<BR>as the ocean.<BR>—सागर-नेमि, इस्, f. ‘ocean-encircled,’<BR>the earth.<BR>—सागर-पर्यन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, bounded<BR>by the sea.<BR>—सागर-प्लवन, अम्, n. navigat-<BR>ing the ocean, leaping across the sea.<BR>—सागर-मे-<BR>खल, अस्, आ, अम्, girdled by the ocean, sea-girt;<BR>(आ), f. the earth.<BR>—सागर-वत्, ind. like the ocean.<BR>—सागरानुकूल (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, situated on<BR>the sea-coast.<BR>—सागरान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ending at the sea, bounded by the ocean, sea-girt.<BR>—सागराम्बरा (˚र-अम्˚), f. ‘ocean-clothed,’ the<BR>earth.<BR>—सागरालय (˚र-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘ocean-dwell-<BR>ing,’ epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—सागरेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सागरोत्थ (˚र-उत्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘produced in the sea,’ sea-salt.<BR>—सागरोद्गार (˚र-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. the swelling or heaving of the sea.<BR>—सागरोद्धूत-निःस्वन (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>raising a sound like the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्नि
साग्नि साग्नि (स-अग्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having fire;<BR>taking the sacred fire; (ई), ind. along with fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्निक|साग्निकः
साग्निक, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing or maintaining a<BR>fire; associated with Agni; (अस्), m. a householder<BR>who maintains a sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्र
साग्र साग्र (स-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, with a sur-<BR>plus, more than; (अम्), ind., Ved. for a longer<BR>period, for a whole life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कर्य|सांकर्य|सांकर्यं|साङ्कर्य्य
साङ्कर्य साङ्कर्य, अम्, n. (fr. सङ्-कर),<BR>mixing or blending together confusedly, confusion,<BR>mixture.<BR>—साङ्कर्य-वाद, अस्, m., N. of a short<BR>Nyāya treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कल|सांकल|साङ्कलं
साङ्कल साङ्कल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सङ्-कल),<BR>effected or produced by addition, accumulated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्काश्य|सांकाश्य|सांकाश्यं
साङ्काश्य साङ्काश्य, N. of the country of<BR>king Kuśa-dhvaja (brother of Janaka); (आ), f., N.<BR>of Kuśa-dhvaja's capital, (Rāmāyaṇa 1. 70, 3.)<BR>—साङ्काश्य-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of Sāṅkāśya,’<BR>epithet of Kuśa-dhvaja, (see सीता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कुर|सांकुर
साङ्कुर साङ्कुर (स-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessing shoots or buds, budding, in bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कृति|सांकृति|साङ्कृतिः
साङ्कृति साङ्कृति, इस्, m., N. of a sage (son<BR>of Viśvā-mitra, and founder of the Vaiyāghrapadya<BR>family).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कृत्य|सांकृत्य
साङ्कृत्य, अस्, m., N. of a Muni; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a family or race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्केतिक|सांकेतिक
साङ्केतिक साङ्केतिक (fr. सङ्केत), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>conventional; indicatory, symbolical, expressed by<BR>signs or tokens or marks, consisting of signs, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्क्षेपिक|सांक्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिकः
साङ्क्षेपिक साङ्क्षेपिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सङ्-<BR>क्षेप), throwing together, abridging; abridged,<BR>contracted, concise, summary, short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ख्य|सांख्य|सांख्यं|सांख्यः|साङ्ख्यः
साङ्ख्य साङ्ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. सङ्-ख्या),<BR>relating to number or calculation, reckoning up, cal-<BR>culating, enumerating, deliberating, reasoning; ra-<BR>tional, discriminative; (अस्, अम्), m. n., N. of one<BR>of the three great divisions of Hindū philosophy,<BR>(ascribed to the sage Kapila, q. v., and so called as<BR>‘reckoning up’ or ‘enumerating’ twenty-five Tat-<BR>tvas or true principles, its object being to effect the<BR>final liberation of the twenty-fifth Tattva [Puruṣa,<BR>the Soul] from the fetters of the phenomenal crea-<BR>tion by conveying the correct knowledge of the<BR>twenty-four other Tattvas, and rightly discriminating<BR>the Soul from them; these twenty-four principles<BR>are divided into eight Prakṛtis or Producers and six-<BR>teen Vikāras or Productions; the eight Producers<BR>start from a Mūla-prakṛti or original Producer<BR>[variously called Pradhāna, ‘chief one;’ A-vyakta,<BR>‘unevolved;’ Brahman, ‘supreme;’ Māyā, ‘power<BR>of illusion;’ Bahu-dhānaka, ‘much-containing’],<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-b" target="_blank">Page1103-b+ 81</a>]<BR>which is emphatically the Prakṛti, ‘First-producer,’ or<BR>‘Originant,’ being a kind of primordial germ whence<BR>all the twenty-three remaining Tattvas are evolved;<BR>its first production is the 2nd Tattva, viz. Buddhi,<BR>Intellect [sometimes called महत् from its being<BR>the great source of the two other internal organs<BR>or instruments, Ahaṅkāra and Manas, which are<BR>both modifications of it]; 3rd in order comes Ahaṅ-<BR>kāra, ‘the I-making’ principle or sense of indi-<BR>viduality; 4th come the five Tan-mātras or subtile<BR>elementary particles out of which the five grosser<BR>elements are evolved; the preceding eight principles<BR>constitute the Producers, [all but the first being of<BR>course in one sense also Productions]; then follow,<BR>as proceeding from the Tan-mātras, the five Sthūla-<BR>bhūtas or grosser elements [also called Mahā-bhūta],<BR>viz. a. आकाश, space or ether, having the Guṇa or<BR>property of sound [शब्द], which is the Viṣaya<BR>or object of apprehension for the corresponding<BR>Indriya or organ, the Ear; b. वायु, air, having the<BR>Guṇa or property of tangibility or touch [स्पर्श],<BR>which is the Viṣaya for the Skin; c. तेजस् or<BR>ज्योतिस्, fire or light, having the property of form or<BR>colour [रूप], which is the Viṣaya for the Eye;<BR>d. आपस्, water, having the property of savour or<BR>taste [रस], which is the Viṣaya for the Tongue;<BR>e. पृथिवी or भूमि, earth, having the property of<BR>odour or smell [गन्ध], which is the Viṣaya for<BR>the Nose, [see गुण]; each of these elements after<BR>the first having also the Guṇa or Guṇas of the pre-<BR>ceding besides its own, and these Guṇas being some-<BR>times identified with the Tan-mātras; then follow<BR>the eleven organs, produced like the Tan-mātras from<BR>the 3rd Tattva Ahaṅkāra, forming with them a<BR>class of sixteen [षोडशकः]; these eleven organs<BR>are the five above-named Buddhīndriyāṇi or organs<BR>of sense, viz. ear, skin, eye, tongue, nose; the five<BR>Karmendriyāṇi or organs of action, viz. larynx, hand,<BR>foot, arms, and organ of generation; and an eleventh<BR>organ called Manas, commonly translated ‘mind,’<BR>which stands between both sets of Indriyas as an in-<BR>ternal organ of perception and action, or of cogni-<BR>tion and volition, [see मनस्]: the twenty-fifth<BR>Tattva, Puruṣa or Soul, is to be wholly distinguished<BR>from the twenty-four just enumerated; it is neither<BR>a Producer nor Production; it is altogether passive,<BR>and simply a looker-on, having nothing whatever to<BR>do with the acts of creation, which it only contem-<BR>plates, uniting itself with unintelligent Prakṛti, as<BR>a lame man mounted on a blind man's shoulders,<BR>for the sake of observing and enjoying the acts of<BR>this Prakṛti, who herself cannot see or observe any-<BR>thing; without that union no creation can take<BR>place any more than can the birth of a child without<BR>the union of male and female; this view of creation<BR>implies the eternal existence of innumerable separate<BR>individual souls, each soul by its junction with Pra-<BR>kṛti causing the creation of its own phenomenal<BR>world, which world, however, has an existence of<BR>its own independent of all connection with the par-<BR>ticular Puruṣa to which it is joined; moreover, each<BR>soul is invested in the first place with a subtile body<BR>[लिङ्ग-शरीर or सूक्ष्म-शरीर] composed of<BR>Buddhi, Ahaṅkāra, the five Tan-mātras, and the<BR>eleven organs, and afterwards with a grosser body<BR>formed of the five elements; the former accompany-<BR>ing the soul through all its transmigrations, while the<BR>latter perishes; this system also teaches that Prakṛti<BR>and its products may be regarded as made up of<BR>three ingredients in a state of equipoise, viz. Sattva,<BR>Rajas, and Tamas, Goodness, Passion, and Darkness,<BR>commonly called Guṇas, but rather substances than<BR>qualities, and more correctly translated ‘fetters,’ be-<BR>cause they are like a triple-stranded rope [see<BR>गुण] which binds and confines the soul: the Sāṅ-<BR>khya system agrees with the Vedānta in being<BR>synthetical, and so differing from the Analytical<BR>Nyāya; its great point of divergence from the<BR>Vedānta is in maintaining two principles which the<BR>Vedānta denies, [see वेदान्त]; it is said to be<BR>atheistical as ignoring all notice of a Supreme Soul,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-c" target="_blank">Page1103-c+ 80</a>]<BR>whose existence is, however, established by the Yoga<BR>branch of the Sāṅkhya proper, [see योग]: the<BR>vague outlines of the system before its crystallization<BR>into a distinct school of dualism are propounded in<BR>the first Book of Manu: its more fully developed<BR>doctrines are contained in the Sāṅkhya-sūtras ascribed<BR>to Kapila, in the Tattva-samāsa, or Summary of<BR>Principles, ascribed to the same author, in the<BR>Sāṅkhya-kārikā [see below], and the numerous<BR>commentaries on these works, some of which are<BR>enumerated below: the Buddhist system and that<BR>of bishop Berkeley in Europe have many points of<BR>connection with the Sāṅkhya, but the modern phi-<BR>losophers of India pay far more attention to the<BR>Nyāya and Vedānta); a follower of the Sāṅkhya<BR>system of philosophy; a patronymic of the Vedic<BR>Ṛṣi Atri; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-कारिका, f.,<BR>N. of a collection of memorial verses or stanzas by<BR>Īśvara-kṛṣṇa in which a summary of the Sāṅkhya<BR>system is given.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-कारिका-भाष्य, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a commentary by Gauḍa-pāda on the<BR>Sāṅkhya-kārikā.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-कौमुदी, f. = साङ्-<BR>ख्य-तत्त्व-कौमुदी; N. of another commentary<BR>by Rāma-kṛṣṇa-bhaṭṭācārya on the Sāṅkhya-<BR>kārikā.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-क्रम-दीपिका, f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on the Tattva-samāsa.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-चन्-<BR>द्रिका, f., N. of a commentary on the Sāṅkhya-<BR>kārikā by Nārāyaṇa-tīrtha.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-तत्त्व-कौ-<BR>मुदी, f., N. of a commentary on the Sāṅkhya-<BR>kārikā by Vācaspati-miśra.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-तत्त्व-प्र-<BR>दीप, अस्, m., N. of a brief exposition of the Sāṅkhya<BR>system by Kavi-rāja-yati.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-तत्त्व-विलास,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentary by Raghunātha-tarka-<BR>vāgīśa-bhaṭṭācārya on the Sāṅkhya-tattva-kaumudī.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-प्रवचन, अम्, n. ‘exposition or in-<BR>terpretation of the Sāṅkhya system,’ N. given by<BR>the commentator Vijñāna-bhikṣu to the six books<BR>containing the Sūtras of the Sāṅkhya system of<BR>philosophy ascribed to Kapila; N. of the Yoga-sūtras<BR>(ascribed to Patañjali, see योग-सूत्र; the title<BR>Sāṅkhya-pravacana appears to be more properly ap-<BR>plied to this division of the Sāṅkhya).<BR>—साङ्ख्य-<BR>प्रवचन-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a commentary<BR>on the Sāṅkhya-sūtra by Vijñāna-bhikṣu.<BR>—साङ्-<BR>ख्य-प्रसाद, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-<BR>भाष्य, अम्, n. = साङ्ख्य-प्रवचन-भाष्य.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-भिक्षु, उस्, m. a particular kind of<BR>mendicant.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-मुख्य, अस्, m. epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-योग, अस्, m. ‘application of the<BR>Sāṅkhya doctrine to the knowledge of spirit,’ N. of<BR>the second chapter of the Bhagavad-gītā, (perhaps so<BR>named as setting forth both the Sāṅkhya and Yoga<BR>doctrines in regard to the soul; according to Śabda-<BR>k. = ज्ञान-योग or ब्रह्म-विद्या.)<BR>—साङ्ख्य-<BR>योग-प्रवर्तिन्, ई, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-<BR>वृत्ति-प्रकाश, अस्, m. = साङ्ख्य-तत्त्व-विलास.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-वृत्ति-सार, अस्, m., N. of a commen-<BR>tary on the Sāṅkhya-sūtra by Mahā-deva Sarasvatī.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the Sāṅkhya doctrine<BR>or system of philosophy; any treatise upon it.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-सार or साङ्ख्य-सार-विवेक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a work by Vijñāna-bhikṣu.<BR>—साङ्ख्य-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, N. of six books of aphorisms of the<BR>Sāṅkhya philosophy ascribed to Kapila, (the number<BR>of aphorisms is said to be 526.)<BR>—साङ्ख्य-सूत्र-<BR>विवरण, अम्, n., N. of a commentary on the Tat-<BR>tva-samāsa.<BR>—साङ्ख्यार्थ-तत्त्व-प्रदीपिका (˚य-<BR>अर्˚), f., N. of a brief exposition of the Sāṅkhya<BR>system by Bhaṭṭa-keśava.<BR>—साङ्ख्यार्थ-सङ्ख्या-<BR>यिक (˚य-अर्˚) = साङ्ख्य-तत्त्व-विलास.<BR>—साङ्-<BR>ख्यालङ्कार (˚य-अल्˚), अस्, m. = साङ्ख्य-क्रम-<BR>दीपिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ख्यायन|सांख्यायन
साङ्ख्यायन, अस्, m. (probably for शाङ्ख्या-<BR>यन), N. of a Muni; of the author of certain<BR>Gṛhya-sūtras, &c.<BR>—साङ्ख्यायन-सूत्र, अम्, n.<BR>the Sūtras of Sāṅkhyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग|सांग
साङ्ग साङ्ग (स-अङ्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having<BR>members or subdivisions; comprising every sub-<BR>ordinate part, complete in every part, finished; to-<BR>gether with the Aṅgas of the Veda, (see वेदाङ्ग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गोपाङ्ग
साङ्गोपाङ्ग (˚ग-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, along with the<BR>Aṅgas and Upāṅgas, (see वेदाङ्ग, उपाङ्ग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गज
साङ्गज साङ्गज (स-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, toge-<BR>ther with hair, covered with hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गतिक|सांगतिक|सांगतिकः
साङ्गतिक साङ्गतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सङ्-<BR>गति), relating or belonging to union or association,<BR>relating to society, social, associating; (अस्), m. a<BR>visitor, guest, new comer; one who comes to transact<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गम|सांगम|सांगमः|साङ्गमः
साङ्गम साङ्गम, अस्, m. (fr. सङ्-गम),<BR>coming together, union, meeting, encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गमन|सांगमन
साङ्गमन, अस्, m. See under अन्-अश्नत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गारक
साङ्गारक साङ्गारक (स-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attended by the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गुष्ठम्
साङ्गुष्ठम् साङ्गुष्ठम् (स-अङ्˚), ind. toge-<BR>ther with the thumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग्रामिक|सांग्रामिक|सांग्रामिकः|साङ्ग्रामिकः
साङ्ग्रामिक साङ्ग्रामिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सङ्ग्रा-<BR>म), relating to war; warlike, martial; (अस्), m. a<BR>commander, general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्घातिक|सांघातिकः
साङ्घातिक साङ्घातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सङ्-<BR>घात), utterly destructive, causing complete destruc-<BR>tion, very deadly, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्मुखी
साङ्मुखी साङ्मुखी, f. (according to Śab-<BR>da-k.), N. of a particular Tithi, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साच्
साच् साच् (fr. rt. सच्), Ved. in अपत्य-साच्,<BR>नृ-षाच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिन्
साचिन् in सव्य-स्˚, q. v. (perhaps connected with<BR>साचि below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचि
साचि साचि, ind. (probably loc. c. of a word<BR>formed fr. स + rt. 1. अञ्च्, see 2. अञ्च्), crookedly,<BR>awry, in a sidelong manner, obliquely, bent on one<BR>side.<BR>—साचि-वाटिका, f. the white-flowered hogweed.<BR>—साचि-विलोकित, अम्, n. a side-long glance.<BR>—साचि-<BR>स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or placed unevenly;<BR>standing across.<BR>—साची-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c.,<BR>to make crooked, bend or turn aside.<BR>—साची-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, made crooked; bent, inclined, seen<BR>crookedly or tortuously, distorted, misrepresented;<BR>(अम्), n. distortion or perversion of mind, prejudice.<BR>—साची-गुण, N. of a place or district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिव्य|साचिव्यं
साचिव्य साचिव्य, अम्, n. (fr. सचिव), com-<BR>panionship, friendship, fellowship; the office of a<BR>counsellor, ministership, ministry, administration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचीवित्
साचीवित् साचीवित्, ind. (in Naigh. II. 15.<BR>enumerated among the क्षिप्र-नामानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साजात्य|साजात्यं
साजात्य साजात्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-जाति), com-<BR>munity of genus, homogeneousness, sameness of class<BR>or caste or tribe, equality of kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साञ्चारिक|सांचारिक
साञ्चारिक साञ्चारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सञ्-<BR>चार), moving about, setting in motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साञ्चि
साञ्चि साञ्चि (incorrect for सञ्-चिति), N. of<BR>the ninth book of the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साञ्जन|सांजनः|साञ्जनः
साञ्जन साञ्जन (स-अञ्ज्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>pigment; (अस्), m. a lizard, chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साट्
साट् साट्, cl. 10. P. साटयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make visible or manifest, show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साटोप
साटोप साटोप (स-आट्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>swelling, swollen, puffed up; puffed up with pride,<BR>proud, haughty, consequential; (अम्), ind. arrogantly,<BR>proudly, consequentially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साट्टहास
साट्टहास साट्टहास (स-अट्˚), अम्, ind. with<BR>loud laughter, with a horse-laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साड्भूत
साड्भूत साड्-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, taking the<BR>form साट् or साड्, (said of 2. सह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साढ
साढ साढ. See under rt. 1. सह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात् 1. सात्, a Taddhita affix which when<BR>put after a word denotes a total change of anything<BR>into the thing expressed by that word, (see भस्म-<BR>सात्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात् 2. सात्, a Sautra rt. meaning ‘to give<BR>pleasure.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
3. सात्, त्, n. (according to some), N. of Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
3. सात, अम्, n. pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातय|सातयः
सातय, अस्, आ, अम्, causing or affording pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातला
सातला, f., N. of a plant (= चर्म-कषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
सात 1. and 2. सात, &c. See p. 1102, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातत्य|सातत्यं
सातत्य सातत्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-तत), con-<BR>tinuity, constancy; (एन), ind. with continuity, eter-<BR>nally, perpetually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातवाहन|सातवाहनः
सातवाहन सात-वाहन, अस्, m., N. of king<BR>Śāli-vāhana, (fabled to have been discovered, when<BR>a child, riding on a Gandharva called Sāta, who,<BR>according to one legend, was changed into a lion;<BR>but see शालि-वाहन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साति|सातिः
साति 1. and 2. साति. See p. 1102, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिरेक
सातिरेक सातिरेक (स-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing excess, increased, more extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिशय
सातिशय सातिशय (स-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ex-<BR>cessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिसार|सातिसारः
सातिसार सातिसार (स-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, af-<BR>flicted with dysentery, dysenteric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीन|सातीनः
सातीन सातीन, अस्, m. (fr. सतीन, q. v.),<BR>pease, pulse, Pisum Sativum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीलक|सातीलकः
सातीलक, अस्, m. (fr. सतीलक), pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातोबार्हत
सातोबार्हत सातोबार्हत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सतो-<BR>बृहती), relating or belonging to the Sato-bṛhatī<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्रिक
सात्त्रिक सात्त्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सत्त्र), be-<BR>longing to a sacrifice, sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्विक|सात्त्विकः
सात्त्विक सात्त्विक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सत्-त्व),<BR>real, substantial, essential, natural, genuine, true,<BR>honest, sincere, good, virtuous, excellent, amiable,<BR>vigorous, energetic, pure (without the least admixture<BR>of passion); internal, pertaining to the internal feel-<BR>ings; endowed with the Sattva Guṇa, (i. e. purity or<BR>goodness, see गुण, सत्-त्व); belonging to or pro-<BR>ceeding from this Guṇa; (अस्), m. natural indication<BR>of feeling or emotion, (constituting a class of Bhāvas<BR>which hold a middle place between the Sthāyi-<BR>bhāvas and Vyabhicāri-bhāvas in poetry and the<BR>drama; they are described as eight particular states<BR>of body and mind, viz. स्तम्भ, inability to move;<BR>स्वेद, perspiration; रोमाञ्च, horripilation; स्वर-<BR>विकार, change of voice; वेपथु, tremor; वर्ण-<BR>विकार, change of colour; अश्रु, tears; and प्रलय,<BR>mental absorption); a Brāhman; epithet of Brahmā;<BR>of the eighth creation by Prajā-pati; (ई), f., N. of<BR>Durgā; a particular kind of पूजा practised by the<BR>worshippers of Durgā; scil. तुष्टि, epithet of one of<BR>the five kinds of external acquiescence (in the Sāṅ-<BR>khya phil.; cf. सु-पारा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्मन्
सात्मन् सात्मन् (स-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having a<BR>soul; united to the Supreme Soul.<BR>—सात्म-ता, f.<BR>absorption into the essence (of Brahman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्म्य|सात्म्यं|सात्म्यः
सात्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, agreeable to the nature or<BR>natural constitution, wholesome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यकि|सात्यकिः
सात्यकि सात्यकि, इस्, m. (fr. सत्यक), pa-<BR>tronymic of a warrior in the Pāṇḍu army who acted<BR>as the charioteer of Kṛṣṇa (he was son of Satyaka<BR>and belonged to the Vṛṣṇi family).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यमुग्रि
सात्यमुग्रि सात्यमुग्रि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher<BR>of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यमुग्र्य
सात्यमुग्र्य, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school or Śākhā<BR>of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्ययज्ञि
सात्ययज्ञि सात्ययज्ञि, इस्, m. (fr. सत्य-<BR>यज्ञ), a patronymic of Soma-śuṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवत|सात्यवतः
सात्यवत सात्यवत, अस्, m. (fr. सत्य-वती,<BR>q. v.), a metronymic of the sage Vyāsa, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवतेय|सात्यवतेयः
सात्यवतेय, अस्, m. = सात्यवत above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यहव्य
सात्यहव्य सात्यहव्य, अस्, m. ‘son of Satya-<BR>havya,’ N. of a descendant of Vasiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्राजित
सात्राजित सात्राजित, अस्, m. (fr. सत्रा-जित्),<BR>a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्रासह
सात्रासह सात्रासह, अस्, m. (fr. सत्रा-सह्),<BR>a patronymic of Śona (a king of the Pāñcālas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्रासाह
सात्रासाह for सात्रासह in Atharva-veda V. 13, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत्|सात्वन्त्
सात्वत् सात्वत्, आन्, m. [cf. सत्वत्], a man of<BR>the Yādava tribe, (see Bhāgavata-Purāṇa VIII. 5,<BR>13); a follower, worshipper (of Kṛṣṇa, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत|सात्वतः
सात्वत सात्वत, अस्, m. (probably fr. सात्वत्<BR>or fr. सत्वत्), N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; of Bala-deva;<BR>the son of an outcaste Vaiśya; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people inhabiting a district in central India (said to be<BR>the descendants of outcaste Vaiśyas; cf. सत्वत्); (ई),<BR>f., scil. वृत्ति, one of the four great divisions of dra-<BR>matic style or action (described as abounding in dis-<BR>plays of bravery, generosity, honesty, and cheerful-<BR>ness, containing little love, and characterized by the<BR>marvellous; four kinds of Sātvatī are enumerated,<BR>viz. Utthāpaka, Saṅghātya, Saṃlāpa, and Parivar-<BR>taka); N. of the mother of Śiśu-pāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्विक
सात्विक सात्विक. See सात्त्विक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद|सादः
साद साद, सादन, सादयत्, &c. See under<BR>rt. 1. सद्, p. 1055, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादर
सादर सादर (स-आद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>or paying respect, respectful; impassioned; (अम्),<BR>ind. respectfully, considerately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादि|सादिः
सादि सादि, सादित, सादिन्, &c. See p. 1055,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादृश्य|सादृश्यं
सादृश्य सादृश्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-दृश), like-<BR>ness, resemblance, similarity; a likeness, portrait.<BR>—सादृश्य-वाद, अस्, m. ‘disputation about Sādṛ-<BR>śya,’ N. of a philosophical treatise by Mahā-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यन्त|साद्यंत
साद्यन्त साद्य्-अन्त (स-आद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing beginning and end, complete, entire; (अम्), ind.<BR>from beginning to end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यष्क्र
साद्यष्क्र साद्यष्क्र, अस्, m., Ved. N. of a<BR>particular Kratu or sacrificial ceremony^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यःक्र
साद्यःक्र, अस्, m. Ved. = साद्यष्क्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क|साद्यस्कः
साद्यस्क साद्यस्क, अस्, ई, अम् (probably for<BR>सद्यस्क, q. v.), quick, instantaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् साध् (connected with rt. 3. सिध्),<BR>cl. 5. P. साध्नोति (Ved. also cl. 1. सा-<BR>धति), ससाध, सात्स्यति, असात्सीत्, साद्धुम् (also<BR>साधितुम्), to complete, finish, accomplish; to con-<BR>quer; cl. 4. P. साध्यति, &c., to be completed or<BR>accomplished: Caus. (identical with the Caus. of rt.<BR>3. सिध्), साधयति, -यितुम्: Aor. असीषधत्<BR>(Ved. [प्र-] सीषधाति = प्रसाधयतु, Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 49, 8); to accomplish, effect, perform, do, com-<BR>plete, conclude, perfect, make perfect, bring to per-<BR>fection, bring to an end or conclusion, settle, secure;<BR>to substantiate, prove; to enforce settlement, recover<BR>(a debt); to obtain; to subdue, overcome, conquer;<BR>to destroy, kill; to learn, understand; to set out,<BR>depart, go away, proceed, go, (used for rt. गम् in<BR>dramatic language, according to the Sāhitya-darpaṇa);<BR>to fly, flee: Desid. of Caus. सिषाधयिषति, to<BR>desire to accomplish: Desid. सिषात्सति: Intens. सा-<BR>साध्यते, सासाद्धि; [cf. Gr. ἔθ-ος, ἦθ-ος, ἠθεῖο-ς,<BR>εἴ-ωθ-α, ἐθ-ίζ-ω: Goth. sid-u-s, ‘a habit;’ sidôn,<BR>‘to contrive, perform;’ probably sandjan, sêlis,<BR>‘good;’ un-sêlis: Angl. Sax. sendan: Old Germ.<BR>sit-u, ‘a habit;’ sâlig, ‘happy;’ sâlida.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधक|साधकः
साधक, अस्, अका or इका, अम्, effective, accom-<BR>plishing, fulfilling, completing, perfecting, finishing;<BR>effecting by magic, magical; an efficient or skilful<BR>person, adept; aiding, helping, an assistant; (अका),<BR>f. epithet of Durgā; (इका), f. a skilful or efficient<BR>woman; [cf. साधिका, s. v.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधत्
साधत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, accomplishing, completing,<BR>effecting.<BR>—साधद्-इष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. fulfilling<BR>the objects of sacrifices (said of Agni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन|साधनं
साधन, अस्, ई, अम्, effecting; a perfecter; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of the author of Ṛg-veda X. 157; (अम्), n. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">Page1105-a+ 81</a>]<BR>act of accomplishing, effecting, performing; settling;<BR>accomplishment, completion, complete attainment of<BR>any object; a means of accomplishing or effecting,<BR>means of obtaining, means or expedient (in general);<BR>efficient cause, source, cause (in general); an instru-<BR>ment, agent; the instrumental case (in grammar);<BR>a bodily organ; the penis; an udder; an implement,<BR>utensil, apparatus; matter, materials, ingredient, sub-<BR>stance; a medicinal preparation, drug, medicine; a<BR>component part of an army, any military apparatus,<BR>force, army; aid, assistance, an assistant; substanti-<BR>ation, proof, establishment of the truth, demonstra-<BR>tion; a reason or premise leading to a conclusion,<BR>middle term or Hetu in a syllogism (= व्याप्य,<BR>q. v.); accomplishing anything by magic or incanta-<BR>tions, magic; enforcement of payment or settlement<BR>(of a debt), compelling the delivery of anything,<BR>infliction of a fine (in law); good works, penance,<BR>self-mortification, the observance of moral and cere-<BR>monial duties, attainment of beatitude; wealth;<BR>advantage, profit; friendship; the act of subduing,<BR>overcoming; subduing by charms, stupefying, fasci-<BR>nating; conciliating, propitiating, worshipping; kill-<BR>ing, destroying; killing metals, depriving them by<BR>oxydation &c. of their metallic properties (especially<BR>said of mercury); burning on the funeral pile, ob-<BR>sequies; setting out, proceeding, going; going<BR>quickly; going after, following.<BR>—साधन-क्रिया, f.<BR>(in Pāṇini) an action connected with a Kāraka; a finite<BR>verb; a Kṛd-anta affix.<BR>—साधन-चतुष्टय,<BR>अम्, n. four kinds of proof (in phil.).<BR>—साधन-<BR>ता, f. or साधन-त्व, अम्, n. being a means of<BR>attaining (e. g. धर्मस्य तत्त्व-ज्ञानादि-साध-<BR>नत्वे किम् मानम्, what proof is there of merit<BR>being the means of attaining to the knowledge of<BR>the truth?); the state of perfection.<BR>—साधन-<BR>निर्देश, अस्, m. the production of proof (in law);<BR>the indication of premises leading to a conclusion.<BR>—साधन-पञ्चक, अम्, n., N. of five stanzas<BR>giving rules for the attainment of Pra-śānti or qui-<BR>escence.<BR>—साधन-पत्त्र, अम्, n. any written<BR>document used as evidence or proof.<BR>—साधन-<BR>रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having the form of an instrument,<BR>having the form or character of a means or expe-<BR>dient.<BR>—साधनार्ह (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy<BR>of being accomplished.<BR>—साधनाव्यापक (˚न-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (in logic) not invariably attending<BR>on the proof.<BR>—साधनाव्यापक-ता, f. or सा-<BR>धनाव्यापक-त्व, अम्, n. non-invariable attend-<BR>ance on the proof or on what is brought forward<BR>in proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधना
साधना, f. accomplishment, completion; pro-<BR>pitiation, worship, adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनीय
साधनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be accomplished or<BR>effected; to be proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन्त|साधंत|साधंतः|साधन्तः
साधन्त, अस्, m. a beggar, mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधयत्
साधयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, accomplishing, effecting;<BR>perfecting, purifying; substantiating, proving; en-<BR>forcing payment, recovering (a debt &c.), subduing;<BR>conciliating; waiting upon, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधित|साधितः
साधित, अस्, आ, अम्, effected, completed, finished,<BR>achieved, accomplished, succeeded; settled, fulfilled;<BR>substantiated, proved; made good, settled (as a<BR>debt), discharged, recovered; obtained; fined;<BR>amerced, punished by fine, made to pay; awarded<BR>(as a punishment or fine); subdued, mastered;<BR>enabled to effect or obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिमन्
साधिमन्, आ, m. perfection, goodness, excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठ
साधिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, (superl. of साधु), best,<BR>most excellent; very fit, most proper or right;<BR>hardest, very hard or firm, (in these senses regarded<BR>as an irregular superl. of वाढ, cf. साधय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधीयस्
साधीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of साधु), better,<BR>more excellent; more right, more proper; very right<BR>or proper; very handsome; harder, firmer, very hard<BR>or firm, (in these last senses regarded as a compar.<BR>of वाढ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु, उस्, उस् or -वी, उ, perfect, excellent, good,<BR>eminent; virtuous, honourable, pious, righteous,<BR>faithful, pure; correct, pure, classical (as a language<BR>&c.); fit, proper, right; kind, beautiful, pleasing;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-b" target="_blank">Page1105-b+ 81</a>]<BR>well-born, noble, of honourable or respectable descent;<BR>(उस्), m. a good or honest man, a saint, sage; a<BR>Jina or deified Jaina saint; a merchant; a money-<BR>lender, usurer; (according to some) a derivative or<BR>inflected noun; (वी), f. a chaste or virtuous woman;<BR>a saintly woman; a faithful wife; a particular root,<BR>= मेदा; (उ), ind. well; well done! good! indeed;<BR>enough, away with! (with inst.)<BR>—साधु-कर्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, Ved. doing kind actions, beneficent.<BR>—साधु-<BR>कीर्त्ति, इस्, m. ‘having a good reputation,’ a proper N.<BR>—साधु-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, resorted to by the good,<BR>respectable, virtuous.<BR>—साधु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, well-<BR>born, of noble family or descent.<BR>—साधु-जन, अस्,<BR>m. a good person, good people.<BR>—साधु-तस्, ind. from<BR>a good man.<BR>—साधु-ता, f. or साधु-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>goodness, excellence, correctness.<BR>—साधु-देविन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, Ved. skilfully playing.<BR>—साधु-द्वितीय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a merchant as second, accompanied<BR>by a merchant.<BR>—साधु-धी, ईस्, f. a good under-<BR>standing; good disposition; (ईस्, ईस्, इ), having a<BR>good understanding, wise, well-disposed; (ईस्), f. a<BR>wife's mother, husband's mother, mother-in-law.<BR>—साधु-पुष्प, अम्, n. a beautiful flower; the<BR>shrub Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR>—साधु-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>good nature, goodness, kindness.<BR>—साधु-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, good.<BR>—साधु-मत, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>thought of, highly prized, praised.<BR>—साधुम्-<BR>मन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, thinking one's self good or<BR>virtuous.<BR>—साधु-रत्न-सूरि, इस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of a commentary on the Nava-tattva.<BR>—सा-<BR>धु-वत्, ind. as if good, as if correct.<BR>—साधु-<BR>वाद, अस्, m. a cry of ‘good!’<BR>—साधु-वाह, अस्, m.<BR>a good horse, well-trained horse.<BR>—साधु-वाहिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘carrying well,’ a good horse, well-trained horse;<BR>(ई, इनी, इ), having good horses.<BR>—साधु-वृक्ष,<BR>अस्, m. a good tree; the Kadamba tree; another<BR>tree (= वरुण).<BR>—साधु-वृत्त, अम्, n. good<BR>conduct, virtue, piety; (अस्, आ, अम्), well-conducted,<BR>upright; (अस्), m. a well-conducted person, a virtuous<BR>or honest man.<BR>—साधु-वृत्ति, इस्, f. good pro-<BR>fession or means of living; good exposition, excel-<BR>lent commentary; good or excellent practice, the<BR>moral and ritual observances of the Hindūs; (इस्, इस्,<BR>इ), well-conducted, well-behaved, virtuous.<BR>—साधु-<BR>शब्द, अस्, m. a cry of ‘good!’<BR>—साधु-शील, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well-disposed, virtuously inclined; virtuous<BR>righteous.<BR>—साधुशील-त्व, अम्, n. good disposition,<BR>virtuous inclination.<BR>—साधु-संसर्ग, अस्, m.<BR>association with the good.<BR>—साधु-समाचार, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well-behaved.<BR>—साधु-सम्मत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, approved by the good.<BR>—साधूक्त (˚धु-उक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, said or declared by the good.<BR>—साध्व्-<BR>अनिन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, unblamed or unreproached by<BR>the good, of irreproachable character.<BR>—साध्व्-<BR>अलङ्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, beautifully adorned.<BR>—साध्व्-<BR>आचार, अस्, आ, अम्, well-conducted, of virtuous con-<BR>duct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुक|साधुकः
साधुक, अस्, m., N. of a low or degraded tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुया
साधुया, ind., Ved. kindly, properly, amicably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्य|साध्यः
साध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be accomplished or effected;<BR>to be formed; practicable, feasible, attainable; to<BR>be proved or demonstrated; to be substantiated or<BR>made good; to be inferred or concluded (in logic);<BR>to be subdued or mastered, subduable, to be con-<BR>quered, conquerable; to be killed or destroyed; to<BR>be cured, curable; (अस्), m. a particular celestial<BR>being, (see below); a deity (in general); the twenty-<BR>second astronomical Yoga; a particular Mantra; N.<BR>of a Muni; (आस्), m. pl. ‘the perfect or pure ones,’<BR>N. of a class of celestial beings belonging to the<BR>गण-देवता, q. v., sometimes mentioned in the<BR>Veda, (see Ṛg-veda X. 90, 16; in the Śatapatha-<BR>Brāhmaṇa their world is said to be situated above<BR>the sphere of the gods; according to Yāska [Nirukta<BR>XII. 41] they are the gods whose locality is the<BR>sky, i. e. the Bhuvar-loka or middle region between<BR>the earth and sun; in Manu 1. 22. the Sādhyas are<BR>described as created after the gods with natures<BR>exquisitely refined, and in III. 195. they are said to<BR>be children of the Soma-sads, who are described as<BR>sons of Virāj; in the Purāṇas they are regarded as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-c" target="_blank">Page1105-c+ 79</a>]<BR>sons of Sādhyā, and their number is variously given<BR>as twelve or seventeen; but in the later mythology<BR>the Sādhyas seem rather to be superseded by the<BR>Siddhas, see सिद्ध; their names are sometimes<BR>given as follows, Manas, Mantṛ, Prāṇa, Nara, Pāna,<BR>Vinirbhaya, Naya, Daṃsa, Nārāyaṇa, Vṛṣa, Prabhu);<BR>(आ), f., N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of<BR>Dharma (regarded as the mother of the Sādhyas);<BR>(अम्), n. accomplishment, perfection; an object to<BR>be accomplished (in law), the thing to be proved or<BR>established by proof, the matter in debate; (in<BR>logic) the major term in a syllogism, the subject of<BR>a proposition.<BR>—साध्य-ता, f. the state of being<BR>able to be accomplished or effected, practicableness,<BR>feasibility; conquerableness; curableness.<BR>—साध्य-<BR>तावच्छेदक (˚ता-अव्˚), अम्, n. the characteristic<BR>or distinguishing property of the thing to be proved<BR>or of the major term.<BR>—साध्य-पक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>the side of the thing to be proved, the plaint in a<BR>lawsuit.<BR>—साध्यर्षि (˚य-ऋषि), इस्, m. epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—साध्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, comprehending<BR>the point to be proved; (आन्), m. the party on whom<BR>the burden of proof in a lawsuit rests; (अत्), n.<BR>that which contains the Sādhya or major term (i. e.<BR>the पक्ष and its सपक्ष).<BR>—साध्य-व्यापक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, (in logic) invariably attending on what<BR>is to be proved.<BR>—साध्यव्यापक-ता, f. invariable<BR>attendance on what is to be proved or the property<BR>to be established.<BR>—साध्य-समत्व, अम्, n. same-<BR>ness with the point to be proved, (साध्य-सम-<BR>त्वात्, because it is in the same condition with what<BR>is to be proved.)<BR>—साध्य-साधन, अम्, n. the<BR>means of establishing what is to be established (e. g.<BR>a Hetu or reason), effecting what may be or is to be<BR>done, &c.<BR>—साध्य-सिद्धि, इस्, f. the effecting<BR>of what has to be done; the establishing of what<BR>has to be established or proved; the success of an<BR>undertaking, accomplishment, completion, fulfilment;<BR>proof, conclusion.<BR>—साध्यसिद्धि-पाद, अस्, m.<BR>the fourth stage or division of a suit at law, judg-<BR>ment, decision.<BR>—साध्याभाव (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>absence of the thing to be proved; absence of the<BR>subject of a proposition; impossibility of cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यमान
साध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being effected, being<BR>in course of accomplishment; being subjected to,<BR>capable of proof, in course of proof; being proceeded<BR>against (at law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वी
साध्वी, f. See under साधु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधय
साधय साधय (according to Vopa-deva<BR>XXI. 16. fr. वाढ), Nom. P. साधयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to make hard or firm; [cf. साधिष्ठ, साधीयस्,<BR>col. 1.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्म्य|साधर्म्यं
साधर्म्य साधर्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-धर्म),<BR>community or equality of duty or office; community<BR>of properties, sameness of nature, common character,<BR>likeness; the being of the same religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण|साधारणः
साधारण साधारण, अस्, आ or ई (generally ई),<BR>अम् (fr. स-धारण), belonging or applicable to<BR>many, common to many, general, universal, com-<BR>mon, joint; spreading everywhere (applied to ‘the<BR>atmosphere’ or ‘sky’ or ‘ether’ according to Śab-<BR>da-k. on Naigh. 1. 4); (in logic) belonging to more<BR>than the one instance alleged; equal, like, similar;<BR>generic; (अस्), m., N. of the forty-fourth (or eigh-<BR>teenth) year of Jupiter's cycle of sixty years; (अम्),<BR>n. a common rule or precept or one generally appli-<BR>cable; a generic property, a character common to<BR>all the individuals of a species or to all the species<BR>of a genus, &c.; (ई), f. a twig of bamboo (perhaps<BR>used as a bolt); a key (= कुञ्चिका, Śabda-k.).<BR>—सा-<BR>धारण-त्व, अम्, n. commonness, community,<BR>universality, common right, joint interest, general<BR>law.<BR>—साधारण-देश, अस्, m. common land; a<BR>wild marshy country.<BR>—साधारण-धन, अम्, n.<BR>joint or common property.<BR>—साधारण-धर्म,<BR>अस्, m. common or universal duty, conduct or duty<BR>binding on all castes and orders alike (as humanity<BR>&c.).<BR>—साधारण-पक्ष, अस्, n. common side or<BR>party, middle side, the mean (between two extremes).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">Page1106-a+ 69</a>]<BR>—साधारण-स्त्री, f. a common woman, prostitute,<BR>harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण्य|साधारण्यं
साधारण्य, अम्, n. commonness, universality;<BR>= कुञ्चिका [cf. साधारणी].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिका
साधिका साधिका, f. (स-अध्˚), very deep<BR>or profound sleep (= सु-षुप्ति; by some referred<BR>to साधक, p. 1104, col. 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिक्षेप
साधिक्षेप साधिक्षेप (स-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having or showing contempt, taunting, ironical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिदैव
साधिदैव साधिदैव (स-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(united or identified) with supreme divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिभूत
साधिभूत साधिभूत (स-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(identified or one) with the Being who enters into<BR>all material objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधियज्ञ
साधियज्ञ साधियज्ञ (स-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one with the Being who presides over sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठ
साधिष्ठ साधिष्ठ, साधीयस्. See p. 1105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठान
साधिष्ठान साधिष्ठान (स-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a solid basis, possessing a firm foundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु साधु, &c. See under rt. साध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधृत|साधृतं
साधृत साधृत (स-आध्˚), अम्, n. ‘what is<BR>held together,’ a stall, shop; an umbrella, parasol; a<BR>flock of peacocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्य|साध्यः
साध्य साध्य. See p. 1105, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वस|साध्वसं
साध्वस साध्वस, अम्, n. (probably fr. स<BR>+ ध्वण्स), fear, terror; perturbation; torpor;<BR>[cf. स-स्˚.]<BR>—साध्वस-विप्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, over-<BR>whelmed with consternation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानत्कुमार
सानत्कुमार सानत्कुमार, अम्, n. (fr. सनत्-<BR>कुमार), N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानन्द|सानंद|सानन्दः
सानन्द सानन्द (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessed of joy, happy, delighted, enjoying happiness,<BR>endowed with happiness; (अम्), ind. joyfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानन्दूर|सानन्दूरः
सानन्दूर सानन्दूर, अस्, m., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सानन्दूर-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. ‘the glory of<BR>स्˚,’ N. of a chapter in the Vārāha-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानल|सानलः
सानल सानल (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>taining fire; (अस्), m. the resinous exudation of the<BR>Śāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानसि|सानसिः
सानसि सानसि. See under 2. सा, p. 1102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानिका
सानिका सानिका, f. (probably fr. rt. 1. सन्),<BR>a flute, pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयिका
सानेयिका, f. a flute, pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयी
सानेयी, f. a flute, pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानु|सानुः
सानु सानु, उस्, उ, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. सन्, Uṇādi-s. I. 3; all the cases except the Nom.<BR>Voc. sing. du. pl., Acc. sing. du. are optionally formed<BR>fr. a base स्नु; in Ṛg-veda IV. 45, 1. सानैर् =<BR>सानौ), level ground on the top or edge of a moun-<BR>tain, table-land; a summit, ridge, (अन्तः-सानु, ind.<BR>among the summits or ridges, Kirāt. V. 36); an<BR>elevation, elevated spot, (Sāy. = समुच्छ्रित-प्र-<BR>देश); any surface, point, end, top; a precipice; a<BR>shoot, sprout; a forest, wood; a road; a gale of<BR>wind; a sage, learned man; the sun.<BR>—१. सानु-ज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘produced on table-land,’ the plant Prapauṇ-<BR>ḍarīka; (अम्), n. a kind of tree or plant (= तुम्-<BR>बुरु).<BR>—सानु-मत्, आन्, m. ‘having table-land or<BR>a summit,’ a mountain; (अती), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुक
सानुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. elevated, lofty; arrogant,<BR>(Sāy. = सम्-उच्छ्रित, Ṛg-veda II. 23, 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुकम्प|सानुकंप
सानुकम्प सानुकम्प (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>full of pity, sympathising, kind; (अम्), ind. kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुक्रोश
सानुक्रोश सानुक्रोश (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>full of compassion, compassionate, tender, kind;<BR>(अम्), ind. compassionately, affectionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुग
सानुग सानुग (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>attendants or followers, with attendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुज|सानुजं|सानुजः
सानुज 2. सानुज (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (for<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">Page1106-b+ 70</a>]<BR>1. सानु-ज see under सानु), accompanied by a<BR>younger brother, along with a younger brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुनय
सानुनय सानुनय (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing courtesy, courteous, civil, kind, willing; (अम्),<BR>ind. courteously, civilly, kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुनास्यम्
सानुनास्यम् सानुनास्यम् (स-अन्˚), ind. with<BR>a nasal sound, in a nasal tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुप्लव
सानुप्लव सानुप्लव (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ac-<BR>companied by followers or attendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुबन्ध|सानुबंध
सानुबन्ध सानुबन्ध (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing connection or continuity, uninterrupted,<BR>continuous (= अ-विच्छिन्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुमान
सानुमान सानुमान (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (in<BR>phil.) dependent on or associated with inference,<BR>(opposed to निर्-अनुमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुयात्र
सानुयात्र सानुयात्र (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attended by followers, with a retinue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुराग
सानुराग सानुराग (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attached, passionate, impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुशय
सानुशय सानुशय (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, filled<BR>with remorse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुस्वार
सानुस्वार सानुस्वार (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the nasal mark Anu-svāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयी
सानेयी सानेयी, सानेयिका. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तःस्थ
सान्तःस्थ सान्तःस्थ (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having semivowels, along with semivowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तपन|सांतपन|सांतपनं|सान्तपनं
सान्तपन सान्तपन, अम्, n. (fr. सन्-त-<BR>पन), ‘tormenting,’ a sort of severe penance<BR>(mentioned in Manu XI. 124. and described in XI.<BR>212, see the description under महा-स्˚, p. 761).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तर|सांतर|सान्तरं
सान्तर सान्तर (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessing intervals or interstices; not close or compact,<BR>open in texture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तराल
सान्तराल (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having an in-<BR>terval, separated by intervals, distinct from, apart;<BR>together with the intermediate or mixed (castes;<BR>see Manu II. 18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तर्हासम्
सान्तर्हासम् सान्तर्हासम् (स-अन्˚), ind. with<BR>an inward or suppressed laugh, smilingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तानिक|सांतानिक|सान्तानिकः
सान्तानिक सान्तानिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सन्-<BR>तान), stretching, extending, spreading (as a tree);<BR>relating to offspring or descendants, &c.; belonging<BR>or relating to the heavenly tree Santāna, made of<BR>Santāna flowers; (अस्), m. a Brāhman intending to<BR>marry for the sake of issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व्|सांत्व्
सान्त्व् सान्त्व्. See rt. शान्त्व्, p. 1000.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व|सांत्व|सान्त्वं|सांत्वः|सान्त्वः
सान्त्व, सान्त्वन, सान्त्वित, &c. See under rt.<BR>शान्त्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्दीपनि|सांदीपनि|सांदीपनिः|सान्दीपनिः
सान्दीपनि सान्दीपनि, इस्, m. (fr. सन्-दी-<BR>पन), N. of a Muni, (according to Viṣṇu-Purāṇa<BR>V. 21. he was the tutor of Kṛṣṇa and Bala-rāma,<BR>and requested as his preceptor's fee that his son, sup-<BR>posed to be drowned in the sea but kept under the<BR>waters by the demon Pañca-jana, should be restored<BR>to him; Kṛṣṇa plunged into the sea, killed the<BR>demon, and brought back the boy to his father;<BR>see पञ्च-जन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्दृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिकं|सान्दृष्टिकं
सान्दृष्टिक सान्दृष्टिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सन्-<BR>दृष्टि), visible or perceptible at the same time,<BR>relating to present perception; (अम्), n. present<BR>perception of a result, immediate consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्र|सांद्र|सान्द्रं|सान्द्रः
सान्द्र सान्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, (said to be fr. 5. स<BR>+ rt. अन्द्, ‘to bind’), thick, close, compact (but<BR>having interstices); clustered together, collected;<BR>coarse, gross; strong, stout, robust; much, abundant;<BR>excessive, vehement, intense; unctuous, oily; viscid;<BR>smooth, soft, bland; pleasing, agreeable; (अस्), m. a<BR>thicket, wood; a heap, cluster; [cf. probably Gr.<BR>ἁδρός.]<BR>—सान्द्र-कुतूहल, अस्, आ, अम्, having in-<BR>tense curiosity, excited deeply by curiosity.<BR>—सान्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">Page1106-c+ 70</a>]<BR>द्र-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more vehement, increased.<BR>—सान्द्र-ता, f. or सान्द्र-त्व, अम्, n. thickness,<BR>coarseness; viscidity.<BR>—सान्द्र-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing thick clustering flowers,’ a kind of tree (= विभी-<BR>तक).<BR>—सान्द्र-स्निग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, thick and<BR>unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्धिक|सांधिक|सांधिकः|सान्धिकः
सान्धिक सान्धिक, अस्, m. (fr. सन्-धा or<BR>सन्धिका), a distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्धिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिकः
सान्धिविग्रहिक सान्धिविग्रहिक, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>सन्धि-विग्रह), one who has to do with peace and<BR>war, a minister who decides upon peace and war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्धिवेल|सांधिवेल|सान्धिवेलं
सान्धिवेल सान्धिवेल, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सन्धि-<BR>वेला), belonging to or occurring at a Sandhi-velā, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्ध्य|सांध्य|सान्ध्यः
सान्ध्य सान्ध्य, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सन्ध्या),<BR>relating to the evening twilight; relating to the<BR>morning twilight or dawn.<BR>—सान्ध्य-कुसुमा, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= त्रि-सन्धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नहनिक|सांनहनिक|सांनहनिकः|सान्नहनिकः
सान्नहनिक सान्नहनिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सन्-<BR>नहन), bearing or putting on armour; calling to<BR>arms, sounding (as an alarm); (अस्), m. an armour-<BR>bearer, shield-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नाय्य|सांनाय्य|सान्नाय्यं|सांनाय्यः
सान्नाय्य सान्नाय्य, अम्, n. (fr. सन्-नी, q. v.,<BR>cf. सन्-नाय), any substance mixed with clarified<BR>butter &c., and offered as a burnt offering or obla-<BR>tion; a particular offering of the Agni-hotṛs (said<BR>to consist of milk drawn on the evening of the new<BR>moon, then mixed on the next day with other milk<BR>and offered with clarified butter).<BR>—सान्नाय्य-प्रा-<BR>यश्चित्त, अम्, n. a particular penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निध्य|सांनिध्य|सांनिध्यं|सान्निध्यं
सान्निध्य सान्निध्य, अम्, n. (fr. सन्-निध),<BR>nearness, vicinity, proximity; presence, attendance.<BR>—सान्निध्य-तस्, ind. from the proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निपातिक|सांनिपातिक|सान्निपातिकः
सान्निपातिक सान्निपातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सन्-<BR>निपात), miscellaneous, promiscuous, complicated;<BR>having a combined or complicated state of derange-<BR>ment of the three humors (applied to dangerous<BR>illness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्न्यासिक|सांन्यासिक|सांन्यासिकः|सान्न्यासिकः
सान्न्यासिक सान्न्यासिक, अस्, m. (fr. सन्-<BR>न्यास), a Brāhman of the fourth or mendicant<BR>order, a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्यपुत्र
सान्यपुत्र सान्य-पुत्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्वय
सान्वय सान्वय (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, along<BR>with family or descendants; with all the race or family;<BR>in regular order or succession; related to, of kin to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापगम
सापगम सापगम (स-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attended with departures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न
सापत्न सापत्न, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. स-पत्नी),<BR>born from a rival wife, belonging to fellow-wives;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the children of different wives of the<BR>same husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न्य|सापत्न्यं|सापत्न्यः
सापत्न्य, अस्, m. the son of a rival wife; an<BR>enemy, adversary, rival; (अम्), n. the state or con-<BR>dition of a rival wife or fellow-wife; enmity, rivalry,<BR>ambition, (in these senses to be connected with स-<BR>पत्न.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्य|सापत्यः
सापत्य सापत्य (स-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessing offspring, having progeny; attended by one's<BR>children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापदेशम्
सापदेशम् सापदेशम् (स-अप्˚), ind. under<BR>a pretext or pretence; intentionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापमान
सापमान सापमान (स-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>with contempt, contemptuous; (अम्), ind. contemp-<BR>tuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापराध
सापराध सापराध (स-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having faults, faulty, offending, criminal, guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापिण्ड्य|सापिंड्य|सापिंड्यं|सापिण्ड्यं
सापिण्ड्य सापिण्ड्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-पिण्ड),<BR>connection by presenting obsequial offerings to the<BR>same Manes, consanguinity, kindred, kin.<BR>—सा-<BR>पिण्ड्य-दीपिका and सापिण्ड्य-मीमांसा, f., N. of<BR>two works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापेक्ष
सापेक्ष सापेक्ष (स-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>regard or respect to, dependent on.<BR>—सापेक्ष-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. dependence on; need, necessity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपद
साप्तपद साप्तपद, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सप्त-<BR>पद), belonging to seven steps, produced by or<BR>depending on seven steps; (अम्), n. = साप्तपदीन<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदीन|साप्तपदीनं
साप्तपदीन, अम्, n. the state of seven steps,<BR>circumambulation of the nuptial fire by the bride<BR>and bridegroom in seven steps, or advance of the<BR>bride to meet the bridegroom in seven steps; friend-<BR>ship easily contracted (i. e. formed with any one<BR>with whom seven paces are walked, or, according to<BR>others, contracted after the utterance of only seven<BR>words), intimacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपौरुष
साप्तपौरुष साप्तपौरुष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>सप्त-पुरुष), extending to or comprising seven<BR>generations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तमिक
साप्तमिक साप्तमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सप्तमी),<BR>belonging or relating to the seventh case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तिक
साप्तिक साप्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सप्तन्), re-<BR>lating to seven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्य
साप्य साप्य, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्सरोगण
साप्सरोगण साप्सरो-गण (स-अप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, attended by a number of Apsarases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साफल्य|साफल्यं
साफल्य साफल्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-फल), pro-<BR>ductiveness, fruitfulness; profit, advantage; success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साब्दी
साब्दी साब्दी, f. a sort of grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिकाम
साभिकाम साभिकाम (स-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing love or affection, loving, affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिप्राय
साभिप्राय साभिप्राय (स-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having an aim or purpose, persevering, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिमान
साभिमान साभिमान (स-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>full of pride, haughty, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिलाष
साभिलाष साभिलाष (स-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>full of desire, eager; (अम्), ind. wishfully, eagerly,<BR>passionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्यसूय
साभ्यसूय साभ्यसूय (स-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>full of envy, envious, malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्र
साभ्र साभ्र (स-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>clouds, covered with clouds, overcast, cloudy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्रमती
साभ्रमती साभ्रमती, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्
साम् साम् (perhaps rather a Nominal<BR>verb fr. सामन्, col. 2; cf. rts. शम्,<BR>शन्त्व्, with which साम् is doubtless connected), cl. 10.<BR>P. सामयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अससामत् and असीष-<BR>मत्, to conciliate, appease, pacify, tranquillize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक 1. सामक, अम्, n. (fr. 1. सम), the<BR>principal of a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक 2. सामक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. सो, perhaps for शामक, fr. rt. शो), a whetstone<BR>(especially one for sharpening spindles &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग|सामगः
सामग साम-ग, साम-ज, &c. See under<BR>सामन्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्री
सामग्री सामग्री, f. (fr. सम्-अग्र), a collec-<BR>tion or assemblage of implements or materials, ap-<BR>paratus, baggage, goods and chattels, furniture, effects.<BR>—सामग्री-वाद, अस्, m., N. of a treatise by Hari-<BR>rāma; of a short treatise on the Nyāya philosophy<BR>by Raghu-deva-bhaṭṭācārya.<BR>—सामग्री-विचार, अस्,<BR>m., N. of two short treatises on the Nyāya phi-<BR>losophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्र्य|सामग्र्यं
सामग्र्य, अम्, n. entireness, wholeness, totality,<BR>the whole, completeness, perfection; train, retinue;<BR>collection or assemblage of implements, instruments,<BR>utensils, apparatus; stock, effects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामञ्जस्य|सामंजस्य|सामंजस्यं|सामञ्जस्यं
सामञ्जस्य सामञ्जस्य, अम्, n. (fr. सम्-<BR>अञ्जस), fitness, propriety, consistency, accordance,<BR>correctness, accuracy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्
सामन् सामन्, अ, n. (probably to be con-<BR>nected with rt. शम्, see शामन्, cf. rt. साम्, col. 1;<BR>in Uṇādi-s. IV. 152. said to be fr. rt. 1. सो, as ‘destroy-<BR>ing sin,’ and in this agreeing with Sāyaṇa's derivation<BR>of छन्दस्, fr. rt. 1. छद्, as ‘covering sin;’ by<BR>some connected with 2. सम् and 1. सम, and sup-<BR>posed to mean originally ‘composition,’ ‘stringing<BR>together in metrical song;’ by Yāska, Nirukta VII.<BR>12, apparently connected with सम्मित), calming,<BR>tranquillizing, soothing; reconciling, conciliating, ap-<BR>peasing; conciliation, speaking kindly, kindness;<BR>gentleness, mildness; negotiation (one of the four<BR>Upāyas or means of success against an enemy, the<BR>other three being दान, भेद, and दण्ड, q. q. v. v.);<BR>peaceable or conciliatory behaviour; a particular kind<BR>of sacred text or verse (intended to be chanted,<BR>and forming with ऋच्, यजुस्, छन्दस्, one of the<BR>four different kinds of Vedic composition mentioned<BR>first in the Puruṣa-sūkta, Ṛg-veda X. 90, 9; see<BR>मन्त्र, वेद); a metrical hymn or song of praise,<BR>(Sāy. = स्तोत्र); N. of one of the three principal<BR>Vedas, (see साम-वेद below); (म्ना), ind. in a<BR>conciliatory manner, willingly, voluntarily; (म्नी), f.,<BR>see p. 1108, col. 1.<BR>—साम-ग, अस्, m. a Brāhman<BR>who chants or recites the Sāma-veda; (ई), f. the wife<BR>of a Sāma-veda Brāhman; [cf. Vopa-deva XXVI. 46.]<BR>—साम-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—साम-<BR>ग-वृषोत्सर्ग-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a part of<BR>the Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—साम-गा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. a<BR>chanter of Sāman verses.<BR>—साम-गायक, अस्, m.<BR>a chanter of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-गायन, अस्,<BR>m. a chanter of the Sāma-veda; an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—साम-ज or साम-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, arising<BR>from conciliation, produced by gentleness of conduct<BR>or kindness; produced by the Sāma-veda; (अस्), m.<BR>an elephant.<BR>—साम-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—साम-ध्वनि, इस्, m. the sound of the chanting<BR>of the Sāma-veda, (see Manu IV. 123.)<BR>—साम-<BR>परिशिष्ट, अम्, n. a Pariśiṣṭa belonging to the<BR>Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n. a Brāh-<BR>maṇa of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>one who brings or offers Sāman verses, (Sāy. = उद्गा-<BR>तृ, Ṛg-veda VII. 33, 14.)<BR>—साम-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>born from the Sāma-veda; (इस्), m. Brahmā (as source<BR>of the Veda); an elephant [cf. साम-ज].<BR>—साम-<BR>रथन्तर, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman, (said to have<BR>been created from Brahmā's first mouth.)<BR>—साम-<BR>राज, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Dāma-carita<BR>and Dhūrta-nartaka.<BR>—साम-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Sārasvata (afterwards changed into a female).<BR>—साम-वाद, अस्, m. a kind word, conciliatory<BR>speech.<BR>—साम-विधान-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Brāhmaṇa belonging to the Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-<BR>विधि, इस्, m. = साम-विधान-ब्राह्मण.<BR>—साम-<BR>विप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. skilled in Sāmans or hymns.<BR>—साम-वेद, अस्, m., N. of one of the three prin-<BR>cipal Vedas (see वेद), or of the collective body of<BR>sacred Mantras which constitute this Veda, (although<BR>the word सामन् is thought to be connected with rt.<BR>शम्, and सोम is fr. another rt. [3. सु], yet there<BR>is a clear connection between this Veda and the<BR>Soma ritual or moon-plant ceremonies; the princi-<BR>pal part of its Mantras being specially arranged for<BR>chanting by the Udgātṛ priests at such ceremonies,<BR>[e. g. the Jyotiṣṭoma and its various stages of<BR>Agniṣṭoma, Ukthya, &c.]; nevertheless it is really<BR>a mere reproduction of parts of the Ṛg-veda trans-<BR>posed and scattered about piecemeal, only 78 verses<BR>in the whole Sāma-veda being, it is said, untraceable<BR>to the present recension of the Ṛk: the Saṃhitā of<BR>the Sāma-veda consists of two parts; the first, called<BR>Ārcika [or Pūrvārcika or Chando-grantha], contains<BR>585 verses disjoined from their proper sequence in<BR>the Ṛg-veda and arranged in 59 Daśatis or decades,<BR>which again are subdivided into Prapāṭhakas and<BR>Ardha-prapāṭhakas; the second, called Staubhika [or<BR>Uttarārcika or Uttarā-grantha], contains 1225 verses,<BR>also chiefly from the Ṛk-saṃhitā, but less disjointed<BR>than in the first part, and arranged in nine Prapāṭhakas<BR>with Ardha-prapāṭhakas, mostly, however, grouped<BR>in triplets, the first verse of which is also in the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-c" target="_blank">Page1107-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Ārcika, and thus appears twice in the Saṃhitā; this<BR>verse is called the Yoni or womb, being, as it were,<BR>a kind of parent of the two following verses, called<BR>Uttarā, which are required to adapt themselves to<BR>all the modulations and modifications observed in<BR>the intoning of this leading verse; directions for<BR>these modulations being carefully laid down in the<BR>Gānas or manuals for chanting, two of which, viz.<BR>the Veya-gāna and Āraṇya-gāna, are a directory for<BR>the Ārcika portion, and two, viz. the Ūha-gāna and<BR>Ūhya-gāna, for the Staubhika, the supposed efficacy<BR>of the hymns depending greatly on the right appli-<BR>cation of these directions for their utterance; it has<BR>been calculated that out of the aggregate of 1549<BR>distinct verses remaining in the two divisions of the<BR>Sāma-veda Saṃhitā after subtracting the repeated<BR>verses, 190 are from the 1st Maṇḍala of the Ṛk,<BR>9 from the 2nd, 40 from the 3rd, 23 from the 4th,<BR>53 from the 5th, 77 from the 6th, 75 from the 7th,<BR>355 from the 8th, 9 from the Vālakhilyas, 545<BR>from the 9th, 95 from the 10th; there being also<BR>12 verses from the Atharva-veda, and 4 from the<BR>Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā or white Yajur-veda; it will be<BR>observed that more verses are taken from the ninth<BR>than from any other Maṇḍala of the Ṛk, the whole<BR>of the 114 hymns of this ninth Maṇḍala being<BR>especially devoted to the praise of the Soma plant,<BR>and thence called Pāvamānyaḥ or ‘purificational,’<BR>this plant being there not only personified as a<BR>deity but described as primeval, immortal, all-pervad-<BR>ing, all-powerful, lord of gods, and indeed the Su-<BR>preme Being himself; it is remarkable that although<BR>in Manu I. 23. the Sāma-veda is described as drawn<BR>forth from the sun, yet in IV. 123, 124. its sound<BR>is said to possess a kind of impurity, which, however,<BR>Kullūka explains to be merely a semblance of im-<BR>purity, the reason given for this defect being that<BR>whereas the Ṛg-veda has the gods for its objects<BR>and the Yajur-has men, the Sāma- has special refer-<BR>ence to the Pitṛs or deceased ancestors [this relation-<BR>ship implying, perhaps, a connection between the<BR>Soma plant and the moon, as this plant was collected<BR>by moonlight, and in the later mythology was<BR>sometimes identified with the moon, the supposed<BR>residence of the Pitṛs]; this Veda is said to possess<BR>eight Brāhmaṇas, viz. the Prauḍha or large Brāh-<BR>maṇa [= Pañca-viṃśa], the Ṣaḍviṃśa, the Sāma-<BR>vidhi or Sāma-vidhāna, the Ārṣeya, the Devatā-<BR>dhyāya, the Vaṃśa, the Saṃhitopaniṣad, and the<BR>Upaniṣad [sic], which last is probably the same as<BR>the Chāndogyopaniṣad of the Sāma-veda regarded<BR>as a Brāhmaṇa, see छन्दोग-ब्राह्मण, ब्राह्-<BR>मण.)<BR>—सामवेद-च्छला, f., N. of a short work<BR>(giving certain musical directions in the form of<BR>modulations and intonations of letters or syllables for<BR>the chanting of the Sāma-veda; the work contains<BR>seven chapters, viz. वेय-च्छला, आरणा-च्˚, ऊह-च्˚,<BR>ऊह्य-च्˚, गान-च्˚, उत्तरोतर-पद-च्˚, and स्तो-<BR>भ-च्˚).<BR>—सामवेद-संहिता, f. the Saṃhitā of<BR>the Sāma-veda.<BR>—सामवेदार्थ-प्रकाश (˚द-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of Sāyaṇa's commentary on the<BR>Tāṇḍya-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—साम-वेदिन्, ई, m. a Brāhman<BR>who studies the Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-वेदीय, अस्, m.<BR>one having to do with the Sāma-veda, a Chandoga<BR>priest.<BR>—साम-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Yājñavalkya.<BR>—साम-श्राद्ध-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a part of the Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—साम-संहिता, f.<BR>the collection of texts constituting the Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-सङ्ख्या, f., N. of a Pariśiṣṭa connected<BR>with the Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-सङ्गायक, अस्, m. a<BR>chanter of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—साम-सिद्धि, इस्, f. the<BR>art of accomplishing something in a peaceable way.<BR>—साम-सूत्र, अम्, n. a Sūtra work belonging to<BR>the Sāma-veda, (ten such works are enumerated.)<BR>—सामङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚), अम्, n. an Aṅga or the Sāma-<BR>veda.<BR>—सामोद्भव (˚म-उद्˚), अस्, m. an elephant;<BR>[cf. साम-ज.]<BR>—सामोन्मुख (˚म-उन्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, eager for conciliation, wishing to conciliate.<BR>—सामोपचार or सामोपाय (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>mild remedy, moderate measure, gentle means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम
साम, अस्, आ, अम्, in प्रति-साम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging to the Sāma-<BR>veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन
1. सामन, अस्, ई, अम्, conciliatory, peaceable, con-<BR>tented, (in Ṛg-veda X. 85, 11. सामनौ = सामा-<BR>नौ); (ई), f. a rope for tying cattle (according to<BR>Śabda-k.; cf. साम्नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्य|सामन्यः
सामन्य, अस्, m. a Brāhman conversant with the<BR>Sāma-veda; one skilful in chanting the verses of that<BR>Veda, (Sāy. = साम-गान-कुशल, Ṛg-veda IX. 96,<BR>22.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्नी
साम्नी, f. a sort of metre (one of the classes occur-<BR>ring in the Sāma-veda); a rope for tying cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन
सामन 2. सामन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = समान,<BR>level, even.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्त|सामंत|सामन्तः
सामन्त सामन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सम्-अन्त),<BR>bordering, bounding, limiting, neighbouring; uni-<BR>versal; (अस्), m. a neighbour; a neighbouring king;<BR>a feudatory or tributary prince, the chief of a dis-<BR>trict (paying tribute to a lord paramount); a leader,<BR>general, captain, champion; (अम्), n. a neighbour-<BR>hood.<BR>—सामन्त-चक्र, अम्, n. a circle of neigh-<BR>bouring princes.<BR>—सामन्त-प्रत्यय, अस्, m. the<BR>evidence or testimony of near neighbours.<BR>—सामन्त-<BR>वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling on the borders, bordering,<BR>neighbouring, a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामय
सामय सामय (स-आम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, suffer-<BR>ing from sickness, sick, diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयाचारिक
सामयाचारिक सामयाचारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>समयाचार), relating to conventional practice or<BR>usage.<BR>—सामयाचारिक-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of certain<BR>Sūtras, sometimes called Dharma-sūtras, which treat<BR>of customs and rites sanctioned by the common<BR>agreement and practice of virtuous men, and which<BR>afterwards, with the Gṛhya-sūtras, grew into the<BR>Dharma-śāstras or law-books, (see सूत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिक|सामयिकः
सामयिक सामयिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सम्-अय),<BR>conventional, customary, conformable to agreement,<BR>agreed upon, stipulated, precise, exact; periodical;<BR>seasonable, punctual, observing time or season; tem-<BR>porary.<BR>—सामयिकाभाव (˚क-अभ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>temporary non-existence (as that of a water-pot which<BR>has been removed from its place to be again restored<BR>to it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर
सामर सामर (स-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>with the immortals, accompanied by the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामराधिप
सामराधिप (स-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, together with<BR>the lord of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामरिक
सामरिक सामरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सम्-अर),<BR>belonging to war or battle, martial, warlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्थ्य|सामर्थ्यं
सामर्थ्य सामर्थ्य, अम्, n. (fr. सम्-अर्थ),<BR>sameness of aim or object, sameness or oneness of<BR>meaning or signification; adequacy, fitness, the being<BR>adequate, capacity, the being entitled; force, power,<BR>ability, energy, fortitude, strength; wealth; interest,<BR>advantage; sense or force of words, signification,<BR>mutual relation of words; (आत्), ind. through the<BR>power of, on the strength of, by reason of, on ac-<BR>count of.<BR>—सामर्थ्य-बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing power as the bond of union, cemented by or<BR>contingent on power or fitness.<BR>—सामर्थ्य-हीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of strength, strengthless, weak,<BR>feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्ष
सामर्ष सामर्ष (स-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, full of<BR>impatience or anger, enraged, wrathful; (अम्), ind.<BR>angrily.<BR>—सामर्ष-ता, f. angry impatience, wrath.<BR>—सामर्ष-हासम्, ind. with an ironical smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवश
सामवश साम-वश, अस्, m. (in Vedic gram-<BR>mar) a kind of irregular lengthening of certain short<BR>vowels before consonants (when required by the<BR>metre).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवायिक|सामवायिकः
सामवायिक सामवायिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सम्-<BR>अवाय), belonging to an assembly or association,<BR>collective; relating to close or intimate connection;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">Page1108-b+ 76</a>]<BR>(अस्), m. a minister or counsellor; the chief of a<BR>company or corporation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामाजिक|सामाजिकः
सामाजिक सामाजिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. समाज),<BR>relating or belonging to an assembly or multitude;<BR>(अस्), m. an assistant or spectator at an assembly or<BR>meeting, member of an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामात्य
सामात्य सामात्य (स-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ac-<BR>companied by ministers or counsellors.<BR>—सामात्य-<BR>प्रमुख, अस्, आ, अम्, with the chief ministers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानाधिकरण्य|सामानाधिकरण्यं
सामानाधिकरण्य सामानाधिकरण्य, अम्,<BR>n. (fr. समानाधिकरण), the being in समाना-<BR>धिकरण, q. v.; the being in the same predica-<BR>ment; common office or function or government,<BR>common agreement or relationship (see अधि-क-<BR>रण), the condition of relating to the same object<BR>or residing in the same subject, the being a receptacle<BR>or substratum of common properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्य|सामान्यं
सामान्य सामान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. 2. समान),<BR>common, general, universal, generic, equal; entire,<BR>whole; vulgar, ordinary, common-place, insignifi-<BR>cant, low; (अम्), n. community, generality, uni-<BR>versality; totality, entireness; common or generic<BR>property, specific property; kind, sort; public affairs<BR>or business; equanimity; identity; (in rhetoric) the<BR>connection of different objects by common proper-<BR>ties; (आ), f. a common female, courtezan, harlot.<BR>—सामान्य-ज्ञान, अम्, n. the perception of com-<BR>mon or generic property.<BR>—सामान्य-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, more common; very common-place or insigni-<BR>ficant.<BR>—सामान्य-तस्, ind. generally, commonly,<BR>ordinarily, usually.<BR>—सामान्यतो-दृष्ट, अम्, n.<BR>(in logic) a particular kind of inference, that of which<BR>the ground is neither the relation of cause to effect<BR>nor of effect to cause, (according to the Sāṅkhya and<BR>Nyāya systems it furnishes evidence of things trans-<BR>cending the senses [अतीन्द्रिय-विषय], such as<BR>the paths of the heavenly bodies [सूर्यादि-गति], the<BR>existence of air, ether, soul, space, time, and the<BR>internal organ.)<BR>—सामान्य-पक्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>general side, the middle part, mean (between two<BR>extremes).<BR>—सामान्य-पदार्थ (˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the category Generality.<BR>—सामान्य-प्रतिपत्ति-<BR>पूर्वम्, ind. after an equal elevation, after elevating<BR>to a common rank.<BR>—सामान्य-लक्षण, अम्, n.<BR>a generic definition or sign, a definition comprising<BR>many individuals, a specific characteristic; (आ), f.<BR>one of the three A-laukika or transcendental percep-<BR>tions or Sannikarṣas (in the Nyāya phil., described as<BR>आश्रय-ज्ञापक-सामान्य-ज्ञान; see सन्-निकर्-<BR>ष).<BR>—सामान्य-वनिता, f. a common woman,<BR>prostitute.<BR>—सामान्य-शासन, अम्, n. a general<BR>edict or enactment.<BR>—सामान्य-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a<BR>general rule (in grammar = उत्-सर्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामासिक
सामासिक सामासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. 1. सम्-<BR>आस), belonging or relating to a Samāsa or com-<BR>pound word, &c., (see 1. सम्-आस); compounded,<BR>composite; comprehensive, collective, comprising the<BR>whole; condensed, concise, succinct, brief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामि
सामि सामि, ind. (said to be a form of the<BR>old inst. साम्या of साम्य; cf. आदि for आद्य), half<BR>(often used in comp. like the English सेमि-; cf.<BR>अ-सामि); blamably; [cf. Gr. ἡμι-, ἥμι-συ-ς; Lat.<BR>semi-, semi-s; Old Germ. sâmi- in sâmi-quek,<BR>‘half-alive;’ Angl. Sax. sâm- in sâm-boren, ‘half-<BR>born, abortive,’ sâm-worht; Eng. semi-.]<BR>—सामि-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made half, halved, divided.<BR>—सा-<BR>मि-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, half-drunk.<BR>—सामि-भुक्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, half-eaten, semi-devoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिधेन्य
सामिधेन्य सामिधेन्य, अस्, m. (fr. सम्-इन्ध्<BR>or सम्-इध्), a particular Mantra or mystical prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिधेनी
सामिधेनी, f. a particular prayer or verse recited<BR>whilst the sacrificial fire is being kindled or on add-<BR>ing fuel to it (= धाय्या); fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीची
सामीची सामीची, f. praise, panegyric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीप्य|सामीप्यं|सामीप्यः
सामीप्य सामीप्य, अम्, n. (fr. समीप), near-<BR>ness, vicinity, proximity, contiguity, nearness to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">Page1108-c+ 73</a>]<BR>deity (as one of the four or five states or grades of<BR>beatitude); (अस्), m. a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुदायिक
सामुदायिक सामुदायिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सम्-<BR>उदाय), belonging to a multitude or assemblage,<BR>collective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्र|सामुद्रं|सामुद्रः
सामुद्र 1. सामुद्र, अम्, n. (fr. 1. स-मुद्र),<BR>an impression or mark on the body, spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रक|सामुद्रकं|सामुद्रकः
1. सामुद्रक, अम्, n., N. of a work describing<BR>the various marks on the bodies of men and women,<BR>(so called, according to one account, because com-<BR>posed by Samudra; see 2. सामुद्र below.)<BR>—सामु-<BR>द्रक-विद्या, f. the art of interpreting the marks<BR>of the body, palmistry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिक|सामुद्रिकः
1. सामुद्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to marks on the<BR>body, (सामुद्रिका गुनाः, qualities denoted by<BR>marks on the body); connected with good or bad<BR>fortune supposed to be indicated by marks or spots<BR>on the body; (अस्), m. an interpreter or describer of<BR>marks or spots on the body; a fortune-teller; (अम्),<BR>n. palmistry, N. of a work on this subject; [cf.<BR>1. सामुद्रक above.]<BR>—सामुद्रिकाचार्य (˚क-<BR>आच्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्र|सामुद्रं|सामुद्रः
सामुद्र 2. सामुद्र, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. 2. सम्-<BR>उद्र), oceanic, marine, sea-born; declared or re-<BR>lated by Samudra; (अस्), m. a mariner, voyager,<BR>sailor; (ई), f., N. of the daughter of Samudra and<BR>wife of Prācīna-barhis; (अम्), n. sea-salt; a cuttle-<BR>fish bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रक|सामुद्रकं|सामुद्रकः
2. सामुद्रक, अम्, n. sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रि
सामुद्रि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिक|सामुद्रिकः
2. सामुद्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the sea or<BR>ocean, oceanic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोद
सामोद सामोद, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. स-आम्˚), joy-<BR>ful, pleased; possessing fragrance, fragrant, odori-<BR>ferous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोद्भव|सामोद्भवः
सामोद्भव सामोद्भव, &c. See under सा-<BR>मन्, p. 1107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्नी
साम्नी साम्नी. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्पराय|सांपराय|सांपरायः
साम्पराय साम्पराय, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सम्-<BR>पराय), relating to war or battle, warlike; relating<BR>to the other world or a future state, belonging to the<BR>future; (अस्, अम्), m. n. contention, conflict; the<BR>future, future life; means of attaining a future world;<BR>inquiry into the future; investigation (in general);<BR>uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्परायिक|सांपरायिक|साम्परायिकं|सांपरायिकः
साम्परायिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to war, military,<BR>strategic; warlike; calamitous; relating to the other<BR>world or a future state, belonging to future time,<BR>future; (अस्), m. a war-chariot; (अम्), n. war, battle.<BR>—साम्परायिक-कल्प, अस्, m. military form, strategic<BR>array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्पश्य
साम्पश्य साम्पश्य, अस्, &c. (fr. rt. 1. पश्<BR>with सम्), Ved. causing mutual looks (of love),<BR>forcing mutual glances (of affection; said of a herb<BR>used in charms or philters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रतम्|सांप्रतम्
साम्प्रतम् साम्प्रतम्, ind. (fr. सम्-प्रति),<BR>now, at this time; seasonably, fitly, properly; [cf. अ-स्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रतिक|सांप्रतिक
साम्प्रतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the present<BR>time, present (not future), suitable to the present<BR>occasion, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रदायिक|सांप्रदायिक
साम्प्रदायिक साम्प्रदायिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>सम्-प्रदाय), traditional, belonging to traditional<BR>doctrine, handed down by tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रयोगिक|सांप्रयोगिक
साम्प्रयोगिक साम्प्रयोगिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr.<BR>सम्-प्रयोग), relating to sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्ब्
साम्ब् साम्ब् (= rt. सम्ब्), cl. 10. P. साम्-<BR>बयति, -यितुम्, to accumulate, collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्ब|सांब|सांबः|साम्बः
साम्ब साम्ब (स-अम्˚), अस्, m. attended by<BR>Ambā (said of Śiva).<BR>—सांब-शिव, अस्, m. Śiva<BR>along with Ambā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बन्धिक|सांबंधिक|सांबन्धिक
साम्बन्धिक साम्बन्धिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सम्-<BR>बन्ध), belonging to or proceeding from relation-<BR>ship; (अम्), n. (probably) alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बर|सांबरं|साम्बरं
साम्बर 1. साम्बर, अम्, n. (fr. सम्बर,<BR>q. v.), a kind of salt (= गड-लवण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बर|सांबरं|साम्बरं
साम्बर 2. साम्बर (स-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing clothes, clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बरी|सांबरी
साम्बरी साम्बरी, f. (also written शाम्बरी,<BR>q. v.), a female juggler, sorceress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बवती
साम्बवती साम्बवती, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बेश्वर
साम्बेश्वर (˚ब-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>idol or of a temple built by Sāmbavatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्भवी|सांभवी
साम्भवी साम्भवी, f. (fr. सम्-भव), pos-<BR>sibility, probability; the red Lodhra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्भस्|सांभस्
साम्भस् साम्भस् (स-अम्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, hav-<BR>ing water, containing water, watery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्मद|सांमद
साम्मद साम्मद, अस्, m. (fr. सम्-मद), a<BR>patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Matsya (the author<BR>of a hymn in the Ṛg-veda, according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्मातुर|सांमातुर|साम्मातुरः
साम्मातुर साम्मातुर, अस्, m. (fr. सम्-<BR>मातृ), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्मुख्य|सांमुख्य|सांमुख्यं
साम्मुख्य साम्मुख्य, अम्, n. (fr. सम्-मुख),<BR>the state of being present face to face or in front,<BR>presence, favour, countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्य|साम्यं
साम्य साम्य, अम्, n. (fr. 1. सम), even-<BR>ness, equality, parity, sameness, equipoise; likeness,<BR>similarity; harmony; equability; impartiality, indif-<BR>ference.<BR>—साम्य-ता, f. or साम्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>equality, sameness.<BR>—साम्य-बोधक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>expressive of similarity.<BR>—साम्यावस्था (˚य-अव्˚),<BR>f. equal state, equipoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राज्य|साम्राज्यं
साम्राज्य साम्राज्य, अम्, n. (fr. सम्-राज्),<BR>complete or universal sovereignty, empire, dominion;<BR>(अस्), m. the descendant of a king or Kṣatriya.<BR>—साम्राज्य-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, one who exercises im-<BR>perial sway, obtaining complete sovereignty.<BR>—सा-<BR>म्राज्य-दीक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, consecrated to universal<BR>empire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राणिकर्दम|साम्राणिकर्द्दमं
साम्राणिकर्दम साम्राणि-कर्दम, अम्, n. (ac-<BR>cording to Śabda-k.) a kind of perfume or mixture<BR>of fragrant substances (= जवादि-नामक-गन्ध-<BR>द्रव्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राणिज|साम्राणिजं
साम्राणि-ज, अम्, n. a kind of tree (= महा-<BR>पारेवत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साय|सायं|सायः
साय साय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. सो, cf. अव-सो,<BR>1. अव-साय, दिवसावसान), end, close, termina-<BR>tion; the close of day, evening; an arrow; (अम्),<BR>ind. the evening; Evening personified as a son of<BR>Puṣpārṇa and Prabhā [cf. प्रातर्, मध्यन्-<BR>दिन]; in the evening; (ए), ind. in the evening,<BR>at the close of day; [cf. according to some, Lat.<BR>serus, but recent authorities refer serus to rt. सृ.]<BR>—सायं-सन्ध्या, f. the evening twilight; the<BR>goddess to be worshipped at the evening twilight<BR>or the time at which she is worshipped.<BR>—सायं-<BR>सन्ध्या-देवता, f. ‘the deity of the evening twi-<BR>light,’ epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR>—सायङ्-काल, अस्, m.<BR>evening, eventide.<BR>—सायङ्कालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>longing to evening, vespertine.<BR>—सायङ्-गृह, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—सायन्-धृति, इस्, f. the even-<BR>ing Homa or oblation.<BR>—सायन्-निवास, अस्, m.<BR>evening abode, evening resting-place.<BR>—साय-मण्-<BR>डन, अम्, n. ‘evening-ornament,’ sunset.<BR>—सायम्-<BR>अधिवास, अस्, m. ‘evening-decoration,’ N. of the<BR>ceremony of decorating an image of Durgā on the<BR>fifth day of the month Āśvina.<BR>—सायाह्न (˚य-<BR>अह्˚), अस्, m. the evening, eventide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायक|सायकः
सायक, अस्, इका, अम्, Ved. destroying; (अस्), m.<BR>an arrow [cf. 2. शायक]; a sword, any weapon, a<BR>thunderbolt, (enumerated among the वज्र-नामानि<BR>in Naigh. II. 20); (इका), f. the being or standing<BR>in regular order, = क्रम-स्थिति; (अम्), n., Ved.<BR>an arrow.<BR>—सायक-पुङ्खा, f. the feathered end<BR>of an arrow.<BR>—सायक-प्रणुत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, driven<BR>away by arrows, put to flight by arrows.<BR>—सायक-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायकायन
सायकायन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायन्तन|सायंतन|सायन्तनः
सायन्तन, अस्, ई, अम् [cf. चिरन्तन], belonging<BR>to evening, vespertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायम्प्रातिक|सायंप्रातिक
सायम्प्रातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सायम्-प्रातर्;<BR>cf. पौनःपुनिक), belonging to evening and<BR>morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायण|सायणः
सायण सायण or सायणाचार्य (˚ण-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a learned Brāhman (thought to have<BR>flourished about A. D. 1370, and celebrated as a<BR>well-known commentator on the Ṛg-veda, Śata-<BR>patha-Brāhmaṇa, Tāṇḍya-Brāhmaṇa, and other<BR>works; he was associated in many of his writings<BR>with his elder brother Mādhava, also called Vidyā-<BR>raṇya, who became prime minister to two kings,<BR>Bukka-rāya and Harihara, after having aided them<BR>to found a new capital, called Vijaya-nagara, in the<BR>native kingdom of Karnāṭa about A. D. 1344).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायणीय
सायणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or composed<BR>by Sāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायन|सायनं
सायन सायन (स-अय्˚), अम्, n. the longi-<BR>tude of a planet reckoned from the vernal equi-<BR>noctial point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायवस
सायवस सायवस, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायिन्
सायिन् सायिन्, ई, m. (according to some)<BR>a horseman (= अश्वारोह; cf. सादिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुज्य|सायुज्यं
सायुज्य सायुज्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-युज्), inti-<BR>mate union, identification, absorption (especially into<BR>the divine essence; this is one of the four or five<BR>grades or states into which Mukti is distinguished;<BR>cf. ब्रह्म-स्˚); similarity, likeness; [cf. राज-स्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुध
सायुध सायुध (स-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>weapons, armed.<BR>—सायुध-प्रग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>holding weapons in the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्
सार् सार् = rt. शार्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार|सारं|सारः
सार सार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सृ, ‘to go,<BR>pervade,’ apparently involving in some of its deriva-<BR>tives a meaning ‘to be strong, to be whole or<BR>entire,’ cf. सर्व), essence, substance; the substantial<BR>or essential part of anything; the best or choicest<BR>part; the quintessence; the heart; the matter (of a<BR>book, speech, &c.; also अम्, n., according to some);<BR>real meaning, main point, real truth, (also अम्, n.);<BR>marrow; pith; the sap of trees and plants, (also<BR>अम्, n.); cream, curds; nectar; the matter formed<BR>in a boil or ulcer, pus; strength, power, vigour,<BR>force, courage, prowess, valour, heroism; firmness,<BR>hardness; worth, excellence, highest degree of per-<BR>fection; wealth, goods, riches; a compendium, sum-<BR>mary, epitome; impure carbonate of soda; sickness,<BR>disease [cf. सारण ]; air, wind; (अस्, ई), m. f. a<BR>chess-man, piece at chess or backgammon [cf. शार,<BR>शारि]; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= कृष्ण-त्रिवृता);<BR>Dūrvā grass; Kuśa grass; (ई), f. a kind of bird (=<BR>सारिका); a kind of plant, = सप्तला; (अम्), n.<BR>pith; sap; water; fresh butter; wealth; propriety,<BR>fitness; steel; a wood, thicket, = विपिन; (in rhe-<BR>toric) a climax; (अस्, आ, अम्), essential, substantial;<BR>vigorous, strong, hard; excellent; good, sound,<BR>best; real, true, genuine; sound (as an argument),<BR>thoroughly proved; [cf. Lat. serum.]<BR>—सार-खदि-<BR>र, अस्, m. ‘hard Khadira,’ a kind of Acacia Catechu<BR>(= दुष्-खदिर).<BR>—सार-गन्ध, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing the perfection of scent,’ sandal-wood.<BR>—सार-<BR>गीता, f., N. of a short work on Yoga.<BR>—सार-ग्रा-<BR>हिन्, ई, इणी, इ, extracting the essence or best part of<BR>anything.<BR>—सार-ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘strong-necked,’ epi-<BR>thet of Śiva.<BR>—सार-ज, अम्, n. ‘produced from<BR>cream,’ fresh butter; [cf. सर-ज.]<BR>—सार-तरु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘pith tree, sap tree,’ the plantain tree (=<BR>कदल, q. v.; so called as containing no hard wood<BR>in the stem).<BR>—सार-तस्, ind. essentially, from<BR>strength, by or with vigour, vigorously, according<BR>to wealth, with regard to riches.<BR>—सार-ता, f. or<BR>सार-त्व, अम्, n. essence, substance; strength;<BR>highest degree.<BR>—सार-दा, f. ‘force-giver,’ epithet<BR>of Sarasvatī (goddess of speech); of Durgā.<BR>—सार-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. ‘hard. tree,’ the Khadira tree.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">Page1109-c+ 80</a>]<BR>—सार-पादप, अस्, m. a particular plant or tree,<BR>(probably = धामनी.)<BR>—सार-फल्गुत्व, अम्, n.<BR>substance and emptiness, importance and insignifi-<BR>cance.<BR>—सार-भङ्ग, अस्, अम्, m. n. destruction or<BR>loss of vigour; (अस्, आ, अम्), deprived of substance<BR>or strength.<BR>—सार-भट्टारक, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR>—सार-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a natural vessel (as<BR>the bag or skin containing the musk of the musk-<BR>deer); a bale of goods; implements.<BR>—सार-भुज्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, eating the essence or best part of anything.<BR>—सार-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a commentary by Śrī-<BR>nātha-śarman on the Pariśiṣṭa-prakāśa.<BR>—सार-<BR>मिति, इस्, m. ‘truth-measuring, truth-determining,’<BR>the Veda.<BR>—सार-मूषिका, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>देव-दाली).<BR>—सार-योग, अस्, m. possession of the<BR>essence or substance of anything.<BR>—सार-लहरी, f.,<BR>N. of a grammatical work by Kavi-candra.<BR>—सार-<BR>लोह, अम्, n. ‘the essence of iron,’ steel.<BR>—सार-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having substance, substantial; hav-<BR>ing pith or sap; fertile.<BR>—सारवत्-ता, f. substanti-<BR>ality, hardness, force, strength.<BR>—सार-वर्जित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘devoid of substance,’ pithless, sapless.<BR>—सार-<BR>सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. concentration of essence; N. of a<BR>philosophical work by Varada-rāja; of a work on<BR>the proper seasons for performing ceremonies or for<BR>commencing other undertakings.<BR>—सार-समुच्-<BR>चय, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—सार-सिद्धान्त-<BR>कौमुदी, f., N. of a work by Varada-rāja-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—सारापराध-तस् (˚र-अप्˚), ind. in accordance<BR>with proved offences or crimes.<BR>—सारावली (˚र-<BR>आव्˚), f., N. of a work [cf. स्मृति-स्˚]; of a work<BR>on astronomy.<BR>—सारासार (˚र-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>substantial and unsubstantial, valuable and worthless,<BR>real and vain; (अम्), n. substance and emptiness;<BR>strength and weakness; worth and worthlessness.<BR>—सारासार-ता, f. the state of being substantial and<BR>unsubstantial or of having strong or weak points, &c.<BR>—सारासार-विचार, अस्, m. the considering or<BR>weighing of strong and weak points.<BR>—सारी-कृ, cl.<BR>8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make hard.<BR>—सारोद्-<BR>धार (˚र-उद्˚), N. of a work on music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारक|सारकः
सारक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. Caus. of rt. सृ), causing<BR>to go; cathartic, laxative; (अस्), m. a particular<BR>plant (= जय-पाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण|सारणं|सारणः
सारण, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. Caus. of rt. सृ), caus-<BR>ing to go or flow; (अस्), m. dysentery, diarrhœa<BR>[cf. अति-सार]; the hog-plum, Spondias Mangifera;<BR>another plant (= भद्र-बला); N. of one of Rā-<BR>vaṇa's ministers (sent as ambassador to Rāma);<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणा
सारणा, f. a particular process to which mineral<BR>substances (especially quicksilver) are subjected, (two<BR>others are given, called ऋतु-स्˚ and प्रति-स्˚.)<BR>—सा-<BR>रणा-त्रय, अम्, n. the three Sāraṇā processes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणि|सारणिः
सारणि, इस्, f. a canal, drain, channel, water-pipe;<BR>a small river; the plant Pæderia Fetida; [cf. सा-<BR>रणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिक|सारणिकः
सारणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सरणि), travelling,<BR>wayfaring, journeying; (अस्), m. a traveller, way-<BR>farer.<BR>—सारणिक-घ्न, अस्, m. ‘killing travellers,’<BR>a robber, highwayman, murderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिका
सारणिका, f., N. of a short treatise on astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणी
सारणी, f. = सारणि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारि|सारिः
सारि, इस्, f. a chess-man, &c. (= सार, सारी).<BR>—सारि-<BR>फलक, अस्, m. a chess-board, draught-board; a<BR>table for playing chess or backgammon; [cf. शारि-<BR>फ्˚.]<BR>—सारिम्-एजय, अस्, m., N. of a chieftain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिका
सारिका, f. a kind of bird (= शारिका, श्यामा);<BR>N. of a Rākṣasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिन्
सारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going, resorting to, &c. (gene-<BR>rally at the end of a comp., e. g. ओकः-सारिन्, going<BR>home); having the essence or substance of; (इणी), f.,<BR>N. of various plants (= सह-देवी; = कार्पासी; =<BR>दुर्-आलभा; = कपिल-शिंशपा; = प्र-सारिणी; =<BR>रक्त-पुनर्नवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिवा
सारिवा, f. a kind of plant (= शारिवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारी
सारी, f. See under सार, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारघ|सारघं
सारघ सारघ, अम्, n. (fr. सरघा), honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारङ्ग|सारंग|सारङ्गः
सारङ्ग सारङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम्, (probably fr.<BR>अ-रङ्ग, ‘having colour, &c.;’ but cf. शार,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">Page1110-a+ 74</a>]<BR>शारङ्ग; according to Uṇādi-s. I. 121. fr. rt. सृ),<BR>of a variegated colour, variegated, spotted [cf. कृष्-<BR>ण-स्˚, लोहित-स्˚]; (अस्), m. a variegated colour;<BR>the spotted antelope; a deer; a lion; an elephant;<BR>the Cātaka bird, Cuculus Melanoleucus; the Indian<BR>cuckoo; a kind of large crane, Ardea Sarunga; a<BR>peacock; the Rāja-haṃsa; a large bee; a cloud;<BR>a tree; an umbrella, parasol; a garment, cloth,<BR>cloths; hair; a lotus; a flower; a conch-shell; a<BR>sort of musical instrument; an ornament, jewel;<BR>gold; a bow; epithet of Śiva; of Kāma-deva;<BR>sandal; camphor; the earth; night; light; (ई), f.<BR>a kind of spotted doe or antelope; a sort of violin.<BR>—सारङ्ग-देव, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—सारङ्ग-<BR>रङ्ग-दा, f., N. of a commentary on the Kṛṣṇa-<BR>karṇāmṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारङ्गिक|सारंगिक|सारंगिकः|सारङ्गिकः
सारङ्गिक, अस्, m. a bird-catcher, fowler, hunter,<BR>deer-catcher, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण|सारणं|सारणः
सारण सारण, &c. See under सार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण्ड|सारंड|सारंडः|सारण्डः
सारण्ड सारण्ड, अस्, m. = सर्पाण्ड, a<BR>snake's egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण्यक
सारण्यक सारण्यक (स-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing the Āraṇyakas, together with the Āraṇyakas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथि|सारथिः
सारथि सारथि, इस्, m. (fr. स-रथ), the<BR>son of a Sa-ratha (see स-रथ); a charioteer, driver<BR>of a car, coachman, (forming a mixed caste, com-<BR>monly called Sārthī, and supposed to have sprung<BR>from a Kṣatriya father and Brāhman mother); the<BR>ocean (= 1. सम्-उद्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथिन्
सारथिन्, ई, m., Ved. a charioteer, (Atharva-veda<BR>XV. 2, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथ्य|सारथ्यं
सारथ्य, अम्, n. the office of a charioteer, coach-<BR>manship, charioteering, driving; conveyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारमेय|सारमेयः
सारमेय सारमेय, अस्, m. (fr. सरम,<BR>q. v.), a dog; (औ), m. du. the two children of<BR>Saramā, i. e. the two four-eyed brindled watch-dogs<BR>of Yama (conjectured by some to have been origin-<BR>ally Indra and Agni); (ई), f. a female dog, bitch;<BR>[cf. probably Gr. Ἑρμείας.]<BR>—सारमेय-वाक्य,<BR>अम्, n. ‘Sārameya's speech,’ N. of the fifty-sixth<BR>chapter of the Uttara-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारयत्
सारयत् सारयत्, &c. See under rt. सृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारल्य|सारल्यं
सारल्य सारल्य, अम्, n. straightness, recti-<BR>tude, sincerity, uprightness, honesty, artlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारव|सारवः
सारव सारव, अस्, ई, अम्, (anomalously fr.<BR>सरयु), being on or belonging to the Sarayu river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारशन|सारशनं
सारशन सारशन, अम्, n. (fr. स-रशन),<BR>a woman's zone or girdle (said to be formed of<BR>twenty-five strings); a military belt or girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारसन|सारसनं
सारसन = सारशन above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस|सारसं|सारसः
सारस सारस, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सरस्), relating<BR>or belonging to a lake or pond, coming from a<BR>lake; (अस्), m. the Indian or Siberian crane, Ardea<BR>Sibirica; a bird in general [cf. राज-स्˚]; the moon;<BR>(अम्), n. a lotus; a woman's zone or girdle; [cf.<BR>सारशन.]<BR>—सारस-द्वितीय, अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by a Sārasa or Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारसी
सारसी, f. a female Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस्वत|सारस्वतः
सारस्वत सारस्वत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सरस्-<BR>वती), relating or belonging to the river Sarasvatī;<BR>relating to the goddess Sarasvatī; being in the form<BR>of Sarasvatī; eloquent, learned; belonging to the<BR>Sārasvata country; (अस्), m., N. of the country<BR>about the Sarasvatī river (i. e. the north-west part<BR>of the province of Delhi including part of the<BR>Pañjāb); N. of a Muni or saint (fabled to have<BR>sprung from the personified Sarasvatī river); N. of<BR>a particular tribe of Brāhmans (so called as coming<BR>from the above country or as supposed to be de-<BR>scended from the above Muni; they are said to be<BR>subdivided into ten classes, and to be often cultivators<BR>of literature); a staff of the Vilva tree; a particular<BR>ceremonial used in the worship of Sarasvatī; = सारस्-<BR>वत-प्रक्रिया below; (आस्), m. pl. the people of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">Page1110-b+ 72</a>]<BR>Sārasvata country; (ई), f., scil. प्रक्रिया = सारस्-<BR>वत-प्रक्रिया.<BR>—सारस्वत-कल्प, अस्, m. the<BR>ceremonial used in the worship of Sarasvatī.<BR>—सा-<BR>रस्वत-कोष and सारस्वत-तन्त्र, N. of two<BR>works.<BR>—सारस्वत-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सारस्वत-प्रक्रिया, f., N. of a grammatical<BR>work by Anubhūti-svarūpācārya.<BR>—सारस्वत-व्रत,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a particular religious observance in<BR>honour of Sarasvatī.<BR>—सारस्वतालङ्कार (˚त-अल्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—सारस्वतोत्सव (˚त-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the festival in honour of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस्वत्य
सारस्वत्य, अस्, &c., belonging to the Sārasvata<BR>family or tribe, (सारस्वत्यो गणः, the descendants<BR>or family of Sārasvata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साराल|सारालः
साराल साराल, अस्, m. sesamum (= तिल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारि|सारिः
सारि सारि, सारिन्, &c. See p. 1109, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिसृक्त
सारिसृक्त सारिसृक्त, अस्, m. (probably ano-<BR>mal. fr. the Intens. of rt. 1. सृज्), N. of the author<BR>of Ṛg-veda X. 142, 5, 6 (having the patronymic<BR>Śāṅga).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारु
सारु सारु (doubtful), a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारुन्धतीक
सारुन्धतीक सारुन्धतीक (स-अर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, together with Arundhatī, accompanied by Arun-<BR>dhatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारूप्य|सारूप्यं
सारूप्य सारूप्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-रूप), same-<BR>ness or similarity of form, conformity, resemblance;<BR>assimilation to or conformity with the deity (one of<BR>the states or grades of Mukti, = सरूप-ता, q. v.);<BR>(in the drama) surprise at seeing an object or its<BR>likeness previously seen elsewhere.<BR>—सारूप्य-तस्,<BR>ind. in consequence of similarity of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारोप
सारोप सारोप (स-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, super-<BR>imponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारोष्ट्रिक|सारोष्ट्रिकः
सारोष्ट्रिक सारोष्ट्रिक, अस्, m. (corrupted<BR>fr. सौराष्ट्रिक, q. v.), a kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारोह
सारोह सारोह (स-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>elevation, rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्क
सार्क सार्क (स-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, with the<BR>sun, sunny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्गल
सार्गल सार्गल (स-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a bar or obstacle, barred, impeded, prevented,<BR>(Raghu-v. I. 79.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ञ्जय
सार्ञ्जय सार्ञ्जय, अस्, m. (fr. सृञ्जय), Ved.<BR>the son of Sṛñjaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थ|सार्थः
सार्थ सार्थ (स-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having an<BR>object; having meaning, full of meaning or purport,<BR>significant, important; serving a purpose, useful, ser-<BR>viceable; of like meaning or purport; having pro-<BR>perty, opulent, wealthy; (अस्), m. a wealthy man; a<BR>company of traders, caravan; a multitude of similar<BR>animals; a troop; a collection or multitude (in<BR>general); one of a company of pilgrims.<BR>—सार्थ-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or reared in a caravan.<BR>—सार्-<BR>थ-भ्रंश-समुद्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, arising from<BR>the loss of a caravan.<BR>—सार्थ-मण्डल, अम्, n. the<BR>circle or collected body of a caravan.<BR>—सार्थ-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having a meaning or purpose, signifi-<BR>cant, intending; having a numerous company.<BR>—सार्-<BR>थ-वाह, the leader or conductor of a caravan, a<BR>merchant, trader.<BR>—सार्थवाह-वचस्, अस्, n. the<BR>speech or proclamation of the captain of a caravan.<BR>—सार्थ-हन्, हा, घ्नी, ह, ‘caravan-destroyer,’<BR>a robber who attacks a caravan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थक|सार्थकः
सार्थक (स-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having meaning,<BR>full of meaning, important; serviceable, useful, ad-<BR>vantageous.<BR>—सार्थक-ता, f. the being adapted to<BR>any purpose, serviceableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थिक|सार्थिकः
सार्थिक, अस्, m. a merchant, trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्र|सार्द्रं
सार्द्र सार्द्र (स-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wet, moist,<BR>damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ध|सार्द्धं
सार्ध सार्ध (स-अर्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, joined with<BR>a half, plus one half, increased by one half, having a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">Page1110-c+ 78</a>]<BR>half over (e. g. द्वे शते सार्धे, two hundred toge-<BR>ther with a half, i. e. two hundred and fifty, Manu<BR>VIII. 138; used chiefly in comps., see below);<BR>(अम्), ind. with, along with, together with (with<BR>inst.).<BR>—सारध-शत, अम्, n. ‘a hundred + a half,’<BR>150.<BR>—सार्ध-संवत्सर, अस्, m. a year and a<BR>half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्धमात्र
सार्धमात्र (स-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>half Mātrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्प|सार्पः|सार्प्प
सार्प सार्प, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to snakes or<BR>serpents; (अस्), m., N. of the Nakṣatra Āśleṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पराज्ञी
सार्पराज्ञी, f., N. of the authoress of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्प्य|सार्प्यः
सार्प्य, अस्, -पी, अम्, relating to a snake; (अस्,<BR>पी), m. f., N. of the Nakṣatra Āśleṣā (over which<BR>the serpents are said to preside).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष|सार्पिषः
सार्पिष सार्पिष, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्पिस्), con-<BR>taining clarified butter, cooked with ghee, dressed<BR>with clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष्क|सार्पिष्कं
सार्पिष्क, अस्, ई, अम्, = सार्पिष above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व|सार्वः|सार्व्व|सार्व्वः
सार्व सार्व, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्व), relating<BR>to all, general, universal; fit for all; (अस्), m. a<BR>Buddha; a Jina or Jaina deified saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकामिक|सार्व्वकामिक
सार्वकामिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्व-काम), ful-<BR>filling all desires, gratifying every wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकाल
सार्वकाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-काल), taking<BR>place at all times, suitable for all seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकालिक|सार्व्वकालिक
सार्वकालिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-काल), belong-<BR>ing to all times, suited to all seasons, everlasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वगुणिक
सार्वगुणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-गुण), endued<BR>with every good quality or excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिकः
सार्वजनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-जन), relating<BR>or belonging or suited to all men, universal, public.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनीन|सार्व्वजनीन|सार्व्वजनीनः
सार्वजनीन, अस्, ई, अम्, = सार्वजनिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वज्ञ्य
सार्वज्ञ्य, अम्, n. (fr. सर्व-ज्ञ), omniscience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वत्रिक|सार्व्वत्रिक
सार्वत्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्वत्र), belonging<BR>to every place, general, suited to all places or cir-<BR>cumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वदैवत्य|सार्व्वदैवत्य
सार्वदैवत्य, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्व + देवता),<BR>presided over by or sacred to all the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वधातुक|सार्व्वधातुक
सार्वधातुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-धातु),<BR>applicable to the whole of a radical term or to the<BR>complete form of the verbal base after the conju-<BR>gational characteristics or Vikaraṇas are affixed, i. e.<BR>to the four conjugational or special tenses, &c. (see<BR>below; cf. आर्धधातुक); (अम्), n., N. of the<BR>verbal terminations of the four conjugational or<BR>special tenses (present, imperfect, potential, and<BR>imperative) and of all the root affixes (such as शानच्<BR>and शतृ) which have a servile or indicatory श्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौतिक|सार्व्वभौतिक
सार्वभौतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-भूत),<BR>belonging or relating to all elements or beings, &c.;<BR>comprising all animated beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौम|सार्वभौमः|सार्व्वभौम|सार्व्वभौमः
सार्वभौम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-भूमि),<BR>relating to or consisting of the whole earth, com-<BR>prising the whole world, known throughout the<BR>world; (अस्), m. an emperor, universal monarch;<BR>N. of the elephant of Kuvera (regent of the north);<BR>N. of a king; of a poet.<BR>—सार्वभौम-भट्टा-<BR>चार्य, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिकः
सार्वलौकिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-लोक), pre-<BR>vailing throughout the whole world, common to all<BR>the world, known by every one, universal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववर्णिक|सार्व्ववर्णिक
सार्ववर्णिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्व-वर्ण), of<BR>every kind or sort; belonging or relating to every<BR>tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववर्मिक
सार्ववर्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्व-वर्मन्),<BR>composed or written by Sarva-varman; (अम्), n. any<BR>thing written by Sarva-varman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वविभक्तिक|सार्व्वविभक्तिक
सार्वविभक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सर्व-विभक्ति),<BR>applicable or belonging to all the cases of a noun, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववेदस|सार्ववेदसः|सार्व्ववेदस
सार्ववेदस, अस्, m. (fr. सर्व-वेदस्, q. v.), one<BR>who gives away all his wealth at a sacred rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववेद्य|सार्व्ववेद्य|सार्व्ववेद्यः
सार्ववेद्य, अस्, m. (fr. सर्व-वेद), a Brāhman<BR>conversant with all the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्षप|सार्षपः
सार्षप सार्षप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्षप),<BR>made of mustard; (अम्), n. mustard oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टि
सार्ष्टि सार्ष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ (perhaps fr. स + आ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">Page1111-a+ 73</a>]<BR>+ ऋष्टि; cf. ऋष्व), possessing the same rank or<BR>condition or station, having the same power or sub-<BR>limity; (अयस्), m. pl., N. of a Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टिता
सार्ष्टि-ता, f. equality in rank or condition, equality<BR>in power, &c. (according to Kullūka on Manu IV.<BR>232 = समान-गति-ता, तुल्य-ता; in a passage of<BR>the Mahā-nārāyaṇa Upaniṣad, Sāy. explains सार्ष्टि-<BR>ता by समानैश्वर्य-त्व, which is said to mean<BR>here equality with the Supreme Being in power and<BR>all the divine attributes; it is regarded as the fourth<BR>grade or division of Mukti or final beatitude).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्ट्य|सार्ष्ट्यं
सार्ष्ट्य, अम्, n. the fourth state of Mukti, = सार्-<BR>ष्टि-ता above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल|सालः
साल साल, अस्, m. (= शाल, q. v.), the Śāl<BR>tree or its resin; any tree; a fence or wall surround-<BR>ing a building; any wall; a kind of fish, Ophio-<BR>cephalus Wrahl; (आ), f. a house (more usually written<BR>शाला).<BR>—साल-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a sacred place;<BR>the Śāla-grāma stone, (see शाल-ग्राम.)<BR>—साल-<BR>ग्राम-क्षेत्र, अम्, n., N. of a district.<BR>—साल-<BR>ज्य, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—साल-निर्यास, see<BR>शाल-निर्यास.<BR>—साल-पर्णी, see शाल-पर्णी.<BR>—साल-पुष्प, अम्, n. a flower of the Sāl tree;<BR>the shrub Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR>—साल-भञ्जिका, see<BR>शाल-भञ्जिका.<BR>—साल-रस, अस्, m. the resin of<BR>the Sāl or Śāl tree.<BR>—साल-वाहन, incorrect for<BR>शालि-वाहन.<BR>—साल-वेष्ट, see शाल-वेष्ट.<BR>—सा-<BR>ल-शृङ्ग, अम्, n. ‘wall-pinnacle,’ the coping of a<BR>wall.<BR>—साल-सार, see शाल-सार.<BR>—साला-करी, f.<BR>(according to some) ‘house-worker,’ a female cap-<BR>tive (especially one won in battle).<BR>—साला-वृक, अस्,<BR>m. (see शाला-वृक), a dog; a jackal; a hyena; a<BR>wolf; a wolf-like or cruel man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालन|सालनः
सालन, अस्, m. the resin of the Sāl or Śāl tree;<BR>resin (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालार|सालारं
सालार, अम्, n. a pin or peg projecting from a<BR>wall, a bracket, shelf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालकि
सालकि सालकि, इस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालङ्ग|सालङ्गः
सालङ्ग सालङ्ग, अस्, m. a kind of Rāga or<BR>musical mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालम्ब
सालम्ब सालम्ब (स-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a support or prop, supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालम्बन
सालम्बन (स-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, = सालम्ब above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालस
सालस सालस (स-अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>languor, languid, languishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालातुरीय|सालातुरीयः
सालातुरीय सालातुरीय, अस्, m. (for शालातु-<BR>रीय, q. v.), N. of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालिमञ्जरि
सालिमञ्जरि सालिमञ्जरि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालूर|सालूरः
सालूर सालूर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. सल्),<BR>a frog (= शालूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालेय|सालेयं|सालेयः
सालेय सालेय, अस्, m. a sort of fennel or<BR>dill (= शालेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्य|सालोक्यं
सालोक्य सालोक्य, अम्, n. (fr. स-लोक), the<BR>being in the same sphere or world (with another),<BR>residence in the same heaven with any particular<BR>deity (= सलोक-ता, q. v.).<BR>—सालोक्य-ता, f. = सालोक्य<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्व|साल्वः
साल्व साल्व, अस्, m., N. of a demon-king<BR>who was slain by Viṣṇu, (according to the Śabda-k.<BR>he was king of the country of Saubha); N. of a<BR>country (more usually written शाल्व); (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the inhabitants of Sālva; (अस्, ई, अम्), belonging to<BR>the country Sālva.<BR>—साल्व-हन्, आ, m. ‘slayer of<BR>Sālva,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्विक|साल्विकः
साल्विक साल्विक, अस्, m. (probably a cor-<BR>ruption of सारिका, q. v.), the Sārikā bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साळ्हृ
साळ्हृ साऌहृ. See under rt. 1. सह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साव|सावः
साव साव, अस्, m. (fr. 1. सव), a libation,<BR>in प्रातः-साव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावन|सावनं|सावनः
सावन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. सवन), relating to or<BR>comprising the three Savanas; (अस्), m. an institutor<BR>of a sacrifice or employer of priests at a sacrifice<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">Page1111-b+ 71</a>]<BR>(= यजमान); the conclusion of a sacrifice or the<BR>ceremonies by which it is terminated; N. of Varuṇa;<BR>a month of thirty solar days; a particular kind of<BR>day; a natural or civil day from sunrise to sunset; a<BR>particular kind of year (as distinguished from the<BR>solar year); a particular ceremony performed during<BR>the Sāvana month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावक|सावकः
सावक सावक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.<BR>of rt. 4. सु), generative, productive, causing birth,<BR>&c., obstetric, parturient; the young of any animal<BR>(in this sense for शावक); (इका), f. a midwife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावकाश
सावकाश सावकाश (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing leisure, at leisure; (अम्), ind. leisurely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावग्रह
सावग्रह सावग्रह (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing the grammatical mark called Ava-graha, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावज्ञ
सावज्ञ सावज्ञ (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, feeling<BR>contempt, despising, disdainful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावद्य|सावद्यं
सावद्य सावद्य (स-अव्˚), अम्, n., scil. ऐश्वर्-<BR>य, one of the three kinds of power attainable by<BR>an ascetic, (the other two are called निर्-अवद्य and<BR>सूक्ष्म.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधान|सावधानः
सावधान सावधान (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having or bestowing attention, attentive, heedful,<BR>careful, cautious; diligent; (अम्), ind. cautiously.<BR>—सावधान-ता, f. attention, carefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधानीकृ
सावधानी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make<BR>careful, caution, put on one's guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधानीकृत
सावधानी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, cautioned, apprized,<BR>made aware.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधारण
सावधारण सावधारण (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(in argumentative writings) having a limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधि
सावधि सावधि (स-अव्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, together<BR>with a limit or termination, having a bound or limit,<BR>limited (in time), finite, defined, circumscribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावन्तमिश्र
सावन्तमिश्र सावन्त-मिश्र, अस्, m. a pro-<BR>per N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावयव
सावयव सावयव (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, com-<BR>posed of parts (in the Vaiśeṣika phil. said of all<BR>things except the eternal substances).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर|सावरः
सावर सावर, अस्, m. (= शावर), fault, of-<BR>fence; sin, wickedness, crime; the Lodhra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावरण
सावरण सावरण (स-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing concealment or secrecy, clandestine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण|सावर्णः
सावर्ण सावर्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स-वर्ण), re-<BR>lating or belonging to one of the same colour or<BR>tribe or caste; (अस्), m. (fr. स-वर्णा), a metronymic<BR>of the eighth Manu, (see below.)<BR>—सावर्ण-लक्-<BR>ष्य, अम्, n. ‘mark of sameness of colour or caste,’<BR>the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णि|सावर्णिः
सावर्णि, इस्, m. a metronymic of the eighth Manu<BR>(son of the Sun by Sa-varṇā, q. v., and therefore<BR>younger brother of the seventh Manu or Vaivasvata;<BR>the succeeding Manus to the twelfth, or according<BR>to other authorities to the fourteenth, inclusive are<BR>also called Sāvarṇi; cf. दक्ष-स्˚, ब्रह्म-स्˚,<BR>धर्म-स्˚); (अयस्), m. pl., N. of a Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णिक
सावर्णिक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Sāvarṇi, ar-<BR>ranged by Sāvarṇi (said of a Saṃhitā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण्य|सावर्ण्यं
सावर्ण्य, अम्, n. sameness or similarity of colour;<BR>identity of caste or class; the Manv-antara presided<BR>over by the eighth Manu (in this sense fr. सावर्णि);<BR>(अस्), m., Ved. the eighth Manu (= सावर्णि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावलम्ब
सावलम्ब सावलम्ब (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a support or prop, supported, leaning for sup-<BR>port (on the arm of another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावलेप
सावलेप सावलेप (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, full<BR>of pride, proud; (अम्), ind. insolently, arrogantly,<BR>haughtily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेष
सावशेष सावशेष (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing a remainder, leaving a residue or remainder, re-<BR>maining; imperfect, incomplete, unfinished.<BR>—सा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">Page1111-c+ 74</a>]<BR>वशेष-बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, having bonds still<BR>remaining, still bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावष्टम्भ|सावष्टंभ
सावष्टम्भ सावष्टम्भ (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing self-dependence, full of self-confidence;<BR>(अम्), ind. resolutely, courageously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावहेल
सावहेल सावहेल (स-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dis-<BR>dainful, disdaining, despising; (अम्), ind. disdain-<BR>fully, contemptuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्र|सावित्रं|सावित्रः
सावित्र सावित्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सवितृ), re-<BR>lating or belonging to the sun; descended from the<BR>sun, belonging to the solar dynasty; accompanied by<BR>the Gāyatrī (or sacred verse described below); (अस्),<BR>m. the sun; an embryo or fetus; a Brāhman; N.<BR>of Śiva; of Karṇa (as child of the Sun); of a Vasu,<BR>q. v.; of the tenth Kalpa (according to the Vāyu-<BR>Purāṇa); of one of the Nakṣatras or lunar aste-<BR>risms; (ई), f. a beam or ray of light, a cluster of solar<BR>rays; N. of a celebrated verse of the Ṛg-veda (III.<BR>62, 10. regarded as the most sacred verse of the<BR>Veda, and called Sāvitrī as addressed to the sun; it<BR>is repeated by every Brāhman at his morning and<BR>evening devotions, and is also called गायत्री, see<BR>under गायत्र, p. 288); N. of a wife of Brahmā<BR>(sometimes regarded as the above verse or prayer<BR>deified and represented as mystical mother of the<BR>first three twice-born classes; sometimes identified<BR>with the daughter of Savitṛ by his wife Pṛśni); the<BR>ceremony of investiture with the sacred thread, (see<BR>उप-नय, p. 164, col. 3); a kind of metre; epithet<BR>of Sūryā (daughter of Savitṛ); of Umā (wife of<BR>Śiva); of a daughter of Dakṣa (wife of Dharma);<BR>of the wife of Kaśyapa; of the wife of Satya-vat<BR>(king of Śālva; she was daughter of Aśva-pati, king<BR>of Madra); (अम्), n. the sacred sacrificial thread<BR>worn only by Brāhmans and members of the first<BR>three classes, (see यज्ञोपवीत; it was called Sā-<BR>vitra because the repetition of the Gāyatrī forms<BR>part of the ceremony of investiture.)<BR>—सावित्री-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सावित्री-पतित or सावित्री-<BR>परिभ्रष्ट, अस्, m. ‘fallen from the Sāvitrī,’ a<BR>man of one of the first three classes not invested at<BR>the proper time with the sacrificial cord.<BR>—सावित्री-<BR>महानाम्य, (according to some) the ceremony of<BR>investiture accompanied by repetition of the Gāyatrī.<BR>—सावित्री-व्रत, अम्, n. a particular fast (kept by<BR>Hindū women on the fourteenth day of the second half<BR>of the month Vaiśākha, or of the dark half of Jyaiṣṭha,<BR>to preserve them from widowhood).<BR>—सावित्री-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n. the sacred cord or thread worn by men of<BR>the three twice-born classes, (see above.)<BR>—सावित्र्य्-<BR>अवरजा, f. the younger daughter of Sāvitrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविष्कार
साविष्कार साविष्कार (स-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having manifestation, manifest; showing off or<BR>making an exhibition of any power or talent, proud,<BR>haughty, arrogant (= साहङ्कार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावेतस
सावेतस सावेतस, अस्, m., a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशंस
साशंस साशंस (स-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, full of<BR>desire or strong passion, desirous, hopeful; (अम्),<BR>ind. wishfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशङ्क|साशंक
साशङ्क साशङ्क (स-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, feeling<BR>fear, apprehensive, disheartened, afraid.<BR>—साशङ्क-ता,<BR>f. the state of being afraid or apprehensive, fear, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशन
साशन साशन (स-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>food, consisting of nourishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशनार
साशनार साशनार, अस्, m., N. of a parti-<BR>cular Agra-hāra or royal grant to Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशयन्दक|साशयंदक|साशयंदकः|साशयन्दकः
साशयन्दक साशयन्दक, अस्, m. a small<BR>house-lizard (= ज्येष्ठी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशूक|साशूकः
साशूक साशूक, अस्, m. a blanket (= कम्-<BR>बल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्चर्य|साश्चर्य्य
साश्चर्य साश्चर्य (स-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, won-<BR>derful, marvellous, astonishing; (अम्), ind. with<BR>astonishment, with surprise.<BR>—साश्चर्य-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, wonderful, full of marvels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्र
