सासार
सासार सासार (स-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>showers, rainy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासि
सासि सासि (स-असि), इस्, इस्, इ, having a<BR>sword, armed with a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासुसू
सासुसू सासु-सू (स-अस्˚), ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, having<BR>arrows, (see Kirāt. XV. 5, where, according to Malli-<BR>nātha, असु-सू = वाण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासूय
सासूय सासूय (स-असूया), अस्, आ, अम्, envious,<BR>disdainful, scornful; (अम्), ind. disdainfully, scorn-<BR>fully, angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्थिताम्रार्ध
सास्थिताम्रार्ध सास्थि-ताम्रार्ध, अम्, n. (fr.<BR>स + अस्थि + ताम्र + अर्ध), a kind of amalgam of<BR>zinc and copper, bell-metal (= कांस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्ना
सास्ना सास्ना, f. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 15. said<BR>to be fr. rt. सस्), the dewlap of an ox (= गो-गल-<BR>कम्बल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्र
सास्र 1. सास्र (स-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम् (for<BR>1. साश्र, q. v.), having angles or corners, cornered,<BR>angular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्र
सास्र 2. सास्र (स-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम् (for<BR>2. साश्र, q. v.), weeping, in tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्वादन
सास्वादन सास्वादन (स-आस्˚), अम्, n., scil.<BR>स्थान, one of the steps towards supreme happiness<BR>(according to the Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहङ्कार|साहंकार
साहङ्कार साहङ्कार (स-अह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having egotism or arrogance, proud, arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहचर्य|साहचर्यं|साहचर्य्य|साहचर्य्यं
साहचर्य साहचर्य, अम्, n. (fr. सह-चर),<BR>companionship, fellowship, company, association,<BR>society.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहञ्जि
साहञ्जि साहञ्जि, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहदेव
साहदेव साहदेव, आस्, m. pl. (fr. सह-देव),<BR>the descendants of Saha-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहदेव्य
साहदेव्य, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic of Somaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहन|साहनं
साहन साहन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus. of rt.<BR>1. सह्), the act of causing or enabling to bear;<BR>sufferance, endurance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहय|साहयः
साहय, अस्, आ, अम्, causing or enabling to endure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस|साहसं|साहसः
साहस साहस, अम्, n. (in Manu VIII. 138.<BR>also अस्, m.; fr. सहस्), violence, force, rapine,<BR>robbery, rape, felony, suicide; any act of aggression<BR>or oppression or hatred; cruelty; punishment, chas-<BR>tisement, fine (regarded as of three kinds, the<BR>highest being called Uttama; half of that, Madh-<BR>yama; and half of that, Adhama; see उत्तम-स्˚,<BR>मध्यम-स्˚); boldness, daring, courage, fool-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">Page1112-b+ 75</a>]<BR>hardiness, rashness, temerity, inconsiderate hastiness’<BR>impetuosity; a particular sacred fire in which an<BR>oblation is made (in this sense अस्, m.), or the obla-<BR>tion itself (according to some).<BR>—साहसाङ्क (˚स-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘marked or characterized by daring,’<BR>epithet of king Vikramāditya; of a poet; of a lexi-<BR>cographer.<BR>—साहसाध्यवसायिन् (˚स-अध्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, acting with inconsiderate haste.<BR>—साहसैक-<BR>रसिक (˚स-एक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, one whose only feeling<BR>or passion is cruelty, wholly intent on violence,<BR>brutal, ferocious.<BR>—साहसैकान्त-रसानुवर्तिन्<BR>(˚स-एक्˚, ˚स-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, one who follows or<BR>yields to the one passion of cruelty or rashness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिक|साहसिकः
साहसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, using great force or violence,<BR>violent, perpetrated with violence, cruel, brutal, fero-<BR>cious, felonious, rapacious; bold, daring, impetuous,<BR>rash; punitive, castigatory; (अस्), m. a robber, free-<BR>booter.<BR>—साहसिक-ता, f. cruelty, ferocity, impetu-<BR>osity, temerity, boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिन्
साहसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, violent, ferocious; foolhardy,<BR>bold, daring, impetuous, rash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्र|साहस्रं|साहस्रः
साहस्र साहस्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सहस्र),<BR>relating or belonging to a thousand; consisting of a<BR>thousand; bought with a thousand; paid per thou-<BR>sand (as interest, duty); a thousandfold, a thousand<BR>times better; (अस्), m. an army or detachment con-<BR>sisting of a thousand men; (अम्), n. the aggregate<BR>of a thousand; an aggregate of many thousands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहायक|साहायकं
साहायक साहायक, अम्, n. (fr. सहाय),<BR>assistance, fellowship, association; a number of asso-<BR>ciates or companions; auxiliary troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्य|साहाय्यं
साहाय्य, अम्, n. friendship, fellowship, alliance,<BR>confederation; help, succour; helping another in<BR>danger (regarded as a branch of dramatic action).<BR>—साहाय्यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. the use or ad-<BR>vantage of assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहिड
साहिड साहिड, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहिती
साहिती साहिती, f. (fr. 2. सहित) = साहित्य<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहित्य|साहित्यं
साहित्य, अम्, n. association, connection, combi-<BR>nation, union, society, fellowship; literary compo-<BR>sition, rhetorical composition, rhetoric, poetry; (ac-<BR>cording to some) a collection of materials or means<BR>or rules for the production or performance of any-<BR>thing.<BR>—साहित्य-दर्पण, अम्, n. ‘mirror of com-<BR>position,’ N. of a treatise on rhetorical composition by<BR>Viśva-nātha-kavi-rāja (a kind of Ars Poetica, giving<BR>rules and canons of literary composition, especially<BR>dramatic).<BR>—साहित्य-मीमांसा, f., N. of a work on<BR>rhetorical composition.<BR>—साहित्य-शास्त्र, अम्, n. any<BR>rhetorical treatise (i. e. any work explaining and<BR>applying the figures of rhetoric, setting forth the<BR>various passions and affections, and giving rules for<BR>dramatic or poetical composition).<BR>—साहित्य-सर्-<BR>वस्व, अम्, n., N. of a commentary by Māheśvara<BR>on the Kāvyālaṅkāra-vṛtti.<BR>—साहित्य-सुधा-स-<BR>मुद्र, अस्, m., N. of a work on medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्य|साह्यं
साह्य, अम्, n. (fr. 2. सह), conjunction, union,<BR>society, association, companionship.<BR>—साह्य-कृत्,<BR>त्, m. a companion, associate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहिदेव
साहिदेव साहिदेव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहिवीचि
साहिवीचि साहि-वीचि (स-अह्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, hav-<BR>ing waves of serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहुडियान
साहुडियान साहुडियान, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the author Śūla-pāṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वय|साह्वयः
साह्वय साह्वय (स-आह्˚), अस्, m. gambling<BR>with fighting animals, setting animals to fight for<BR>sport, &c. (= सम्-आह्वय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वस्
साह्वस् साह्वस्. See p. 1100, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सि
सि सि, cl. 5. 9. P. A. सिनोति, सिनुते, सि-<BR>नाति, सिनीते, सिषाय, सिष्ये, सेष्यति, -ते,<BR>असैषीत्, असेष्ट, सेतुम्, to bind, tie, fasten; to<BR>ensnare: Caus. साययति, -यितुम्, Aor. असीषयत्:<BR>Desid. सिसीषति, -ते: Intens. सेषीयते, सेषयीति,<BR>सेषेति; [cf. Zend hi-ta, ‘bound:’ Gr. σει-ρά,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-c" target="_blank">Page1112-c+ 80</a>]<BR>ἱ-μά-ς, ἱ-μον-ιά, ἱμάσσ-ω, ἱμάσ-θλη: Old Germ.<BR>sei-l, sei-d, ‘a noose;’ sai-to: Goth. in-sailjan:<BR>Old Sax. si-mo, ‘a bond:’ Angl. Sax. sal, sœl,<BR>sœlan, sieran, syrwan: Slav. si-lo, se-ti, si-tije:<BR>Lett. see-t, ‘to bind;’ sai-te, ‘a bond, rope.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
1. सित, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see p. 1113, col. 2; for<BR>3. see under rt. 1. सो), bound, tied, fastened; sur-<BR>rounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिति|सितिः
1. सिति, इस्, f. binding, fastening; [cf. 1. प्र-सिति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतु|सेतुः
सेतु, सेतृ, सेत्र, &c. See under सेतु, p. 1134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंसपा
सिंसपा सिंसपा, f. = शिंशपा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंह|सिंहः
सिंह सिंह, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. V. 62. said<BR>to be fr. rt. 1. सिच्, with ह substituted for the final and<BR>a nasal inserted; according to others fr. सिह्, a weakened<BR>form of rt. 1. सह्, with insertion of nasal), a lion; the<BR>sign of the zodiac Leo or the Lagna of that sign (see<BR>लग्न); a hero or any eminent person, (often used<BR>at the end of comps. to express excellence or emi-<BR>nence of any kind, cf. पुरुष-स्˚, राज-स्˚); the<BR>symbol or emblem of the twenty-fourth Arhat of<BR>the present Ava-sarpiṇī; a particular plant (= रक्त-<BR>शिग्रु); N. of a king (father of Sāhideva); (आ), f. a<BR>particular grass or plant, = नाडी; (ई), f. a lioness, &c.,<BR>see p. 1113, col. 1.<BR>—सिंह-कारक, अस्, m. a creator<BR>of lions.<BR>—सिंह-केलि, इस्, m., N. of a celebrated<BR>Bodhi-sattva (= Mañju-ghoṣa).<BR>—सिंह-केशर or<BR>सिंह-केसर, अस्, m. a lion's mane; the plant<BR>Mimusops Elengi; a kind of Modaka or sweetmeat.<BR>—सिंह-ग, अस्, m. ‘lion-going,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सिंह-गुप्त, अस्, m. = सङ्घ-गुप्त, q. v.<BR>—सिंह-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, lion-necked.<BR>—सिंह-<BR>घोष, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—सिंह-तल, अस्, m.<BR>(probably for संह-तल, q. v.), the open hands<BR>joined.<BR>—सिंह-तुण्ड, अस्, m. ‘lion-faced,’ a kind<BR>of fish; a particular plant (= सेहुण्ड).<BR>—सिंह-<BR>दंष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, lion-tusked, having the teeth<BR>of a lion; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सिंह-दत्त,<BR>अस्, m. ‘lion-given,’ N. of a poet.<BR>—सिंह-दर्प,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a lion's pride, proud as a lion.<BR>—सिंह-द्वार, अम्, n. a principal gate, chief gate,<BR>any gate or entrance.<BR>—सिंह-ध्वनि, इस्, m. the<BR>roar of a lion; a sound like the roar of a lion; a<BR>war-cry.<BR>—सिंह-नर्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, roaring like a<BR>lion.<BR>—सिंह-नाद, अस्, m. a lion's roar; a war-cry,<BR>war-whoop; a species of the Ati-jagatī metre (=<BR>कल-हंस); ‘roaring like a lion,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सिंह-नादक, अस्, m. the roar of a lion; a war-<BR>cry; (इका), f. a particular prickly plant (= दुर्-<BR>आलभा).<BR>—सिंह-पर्णी, f. ‘lion-leaved,’ the plant<BR>Justicia Ganderussa (= वासक).<BR>—सिंह-पिप्पली,<BR>f. a kind of plant (= सैंहली).<BR>—सिंह-पुच्छिका,<BR>f. ‘lion-tailed,’ a particular plant (= चित्र-पर्णिका).<BR>—सिंह-पुच्छी, f. the plant Citra-parṇikā; other<BR>plants (= पृश्नि-पर्णी; = माष-पर्णी).<BR>—सिंह-<BR>पुष्पी, f. a kind of plant (= पृश्नि-पर्णी).<BR>—सिंह-प्रगर्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, roaring like a<BR>lion.<BR>—सिंह-प्रगर्जित, अम्, n. the roaring or<BR>roar of a lion.<BR>—सिंह-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work mentioned in the Kuṇḍa-kaumudī.<BR>—सिंह-<BR>बाहु, उस्, m., N. of the father of Vijaya (the founder<BR>of the first Buddhist dynasty in Ceylon).<BR>—सिंह-<BR>मुखी, f. a kind of plant (= वासक).<BR>—सिंह-<BR>याना, f. or सिंह-रथा, f. ‘having a lion as a<BR>vehicle,’ N. of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—सिंह-रव,<BR>अस्, m. the cry or roar of a lion.<BR>—सिंहर्षभ<BR>(˚ह-ऋष्˚), अस्, m. a noble or fierce lion.<BR>—सिंह-<BR>लग्न, अम्, n. the Lagna of the sign Leo, (see<BR>लग्न.)<BR>—सिंह-लम्ब, N. of a place.<BR>—सिंह-<BR>लील, अस्, m. a particular kind of sexual union.<BR>—सिंह-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘having a lion for a<BR>vehicle,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सिंह-वाहिनी, f. ‘borne<BR>on a lion,’ epithet of Durgā.<BR>—सिंह-विक्रम, अस्,<BR>m. = विक्रम-सिंह.<BR>—सिंह-विक्रान्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, valiant as a lion; (अस्), m. a horse.<BR>—सिंह-<BR>विक्रान्त-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, or सिंह-विक्रान्त-गामिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, having a gait as bold as a lion's.<BR>—सिंह-<BR>विक्रीडित, अम्, n. ‘lion's play,’ a kind of metre.<BR>—सिंह-विन्ना, f. a kind of plant (= माष-पर्णी).<BR>—सिंह-व्याघ्र-निषेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabited<BR>by lions and tigers.<BR>—सिंह-शाव, अस्, or सिंह-शिशु,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">Page1113-a+ 77</a>]<BR>उस्, m. a lion's whelp or cub.<BR>—सिंह-संहनन,<BR>अम्, n. the killing or destroying of a lion; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), lion-shaped, well-shaped, handsome; strong as a<BR>lion.<BR>—सिंह-स्कन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘lion-shouldered,’<BR>having the shoulders of a lion.<BR>—सिंह-स्थ, अस्, m.<BR>‘being in the lion,’ epithet of the planet Jupiter<BR>when in the constellation Leo.<BR>—सिंहाढ्य (˚ह-<BR>आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in lions.<BR>—सिंहाव-<BR>लोकन (˚ह-अव्˚), अम्, n. a lion's look (applied to<BR>the habit of constantly pausing and looking back).<BR>—सिंहासन (˚ह-आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘lion-seat,’ a throne<BR>(said to be so called as supported by golden lions);<BR>(अस्), m. a particular kind of sexual union.<BR>—सिंहा-<BR>सन-चक्र, अम्, n., N. of three astrological dia-<BR>grams shaped like a man and marked with the<BR>twenty-seven Nakṣatras.<BR>—सिंहासन-द्वात्रिंशत्,<BR>त्, or सिंहासनद्वात्रिंशत्-पुत्त्रिका-वार्त्ता, f., N.<BR>of a work consisting of thirty-two stories in praise of<BR>Vikramāditya (= विक्रम-चरित).<BR>—सिंहासन-<BR>भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from a throne, dethroned.<BR>—सिंहासन-रण, अस्, अम्, m. n. a strife or struggle<BR>for the throne.<BR>—सिंहासन-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting<BR>on a throne.<BR>—सिंहास्य (˚ह-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, lion-<BR>faced; (अस्), m. a kind of plant (= वासक); a par-<BR>ticular position of the hands.<BR>—सिंहोद्धता (˚ह-<BR>उद्˚), f. a kind of metre.<BR>—सिंहोन्नता (˚ह-उन्˚),<BR>f. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहल|सिंहलं|सिंहलः
सिंहल, अम्, n. tin; brass; bark, rind; Cassia<BR>bark; (अम्, आ), n. f. the island or country of Ceylon,<BR>(perhaps so called as abounding in lions); (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the people of Ceylon.<BR>—सिंहल-द्वीप, अस्, m. the<BR>island of Ceylon.<BR>—सिंहल-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>or dwelling in Ceylon; (आ), f. a kind of plant (=<BR>सर्प-दण्डा, सैंहली).<BR>—सिंहला-स्थान, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of plam tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहलक|सिंहलकं
सिंहलक, अम्, n. the island of Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाय
सिंहाय, Nom. A. सिंहायते, -यितुम्, to be or<BR>become like a lion, act like a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिका
सिंहिका, f., N. of the mother of Rāhu, (she was<BR>one of the thirteen daughters of Dakṣa and wife of<BR>Kaśyapa); N. of a daughter of Kaśyapa (wife of<BR>Vipracitti).<BR>—सिंहिका-सूनु, उस्, m. ‘son of Siṃ-<BR>hikā,’ epithet of Rāhu or the Ascending Node per-<BR>sonified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिकेय
सिंहिकेय, अस्, m. ‘son of Siṃhikā,’ epithet of<BR>Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंही
सिंही, f. a lioness; N. of the mother of Rāhu;<BR>of various plants (= वार्ताकी; = कण्टकारी; = वा-<BR>सक; = बृहती; = मुद्ग-पर्णी).<BR>—सिंही-लता,<BR>f. a kind of plant (= बृहती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाण|सिंहाणं
सिंहाण सिंहाण, अम्, n. (probably for<BR>शिङ्घाण; also written सिङ्घाण), rust of iron;<BR>the mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाणक|सिंहाणकं|सिंहाणकः
सिंहाणक, अस्, अम्, m. n. = सिंहाण above, (also<BR>written सिङ्घाणक, शिङ्घाणक, सङ्घाणक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहान|सिंहानं
सिंहान, अम्, n. = सिंहाण above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्
सिक् सिक्, a Sautra rt. meaning ‘to<BR>scatter about, sprinkle;’ [cf. rts. 1. सिच्,<BR>सीक्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकत
सिकत, आस्, m. pl. (said to be fr. the Sautra rt.<BR>above; probably fr. rt. 1. सिच्), sand; N. of certain<BR>Ṛṣis, (part of the hymn Ṛg-veda IX. 86. is attri-<BR>buted to Sikatāḥ); (आ), f. sandy soil; sand; gravel<BR>or stone (the disease).<BR>—सिकता-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of sand, full of sand, sandy; (अम्), n. a<BR>sand-bank; an island with sandy shores.<BR>—सिकता-<BR>रेणु, उस्, m. a grain of sand.<BR>—सिकता-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessed of sand, abounding in sand, sandy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतिल|सिकतिलः
सिकतिल, अस्, आ, अम्, sandy (as a soil, country, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त|सिक्तः
सिक्त सिक्त, सिक्थ, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्ष्य|सिक्ष्यः
सिक्ष्य सिक्ष्य, अस्, m. crystal, glass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्गापिदि
सिङ्गापिदि सिङ्गापिदि, इस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घण|सिंघण|सिंघणं|सिङ्घणं
सिङ्घण सिङ्घण or सिङ्घाण, अम्, n. (pro-<BR>bably for शिङ्घण, शिङ्घाण, fr. rt. शिङ्घ्, q. v.;<BR>also written सिंहाण; cf. सङ्घाणक), the mucus<BR>of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घाणक|सिंघाणकं|सिङ्घाणकं
सिङ्घाणक, अम्, n. = सिङ्घाण above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घिणी|सिंघिणी
सिङ्घिणी, f. the nose, (see शिङ्घिन्, p. 1005,<BR>col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्
सिच् 1. सिच्, cl. 6. P. A. सिञ्चति, -ते,<BR>सिषेच, सिषिचे, सेक्ष्यति, -ते, असिचत्,<BR>असिचत or असिक्त, सेक्तुम्, to sprinkle, scatter in<BR>small drops; to besprinkle, soak, moisten, water<BR>(plants &c.); to pour out, discharge, emit, shed,<BR>effuse; to pour in; to impregnate: Pass. सिच्यते,<BR>Aor. असेचि, to be sprinkled, &c.: Caus. सेचयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. असीषिचत् or (according to some) असी-<BR>सिचत्, to cause to sprinkle: Desid. सिसिक्षति, -ते:<BR>Intens. सेसिच्यते, सेसेक्ति; [cf. Gr. ἰκ-μά(δ)-ς,<BR>ἰκμα-λέο-ς, ἰκμαίν-ω, ἰκμα-ῖο-ς, στίλη, σίκυς: Lat. stilla<BR>(for stic-la): Old Germ. sîh-u, seich, ‘urine;’<BR>seihjan, seo, gi-sich: Goth. (probably) saivs:<BR>Lith. sunk-iu, séki-s, sek-ti.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त|सिक्तः
सिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled, besprinkled, bespat-<BR>tered, watered; wetted, moistened, soaked, wet;<BR>poured out, effused; impregnated, engendered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्ति|सिक्तिः
सिक्ति, इस्, f. sprinkling; effusion; emission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त्वा
सिक्त्वा, ind. having sprinkled, having poured out<BR>or effused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थ|सिक्थं|सिक्थः
सिक्थ, अस्, m. boiled rice; a lump of boiled rice<BR>or a mouthful of boiled rice kneaded into a ball;<BR>(अम्), n. bee's-wax; indigo (= नीली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थक|सिक्थकं
सिक्थक, अम्, n. bee's-wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्
2. सिच्, क्, f. clothes; the skirt of a dress, (Sāy. =<BR>वस्त्र-प्रान्त); (औ), f. du., Ved. (according to<BR>some) the two wings (of an army); heaven and<BR>earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिचय|सिचयः
सिचय, अस्, m. a robe, raiment, cloth, clothes;<BR>old or ragged raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्यमान
सिच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being sprinkled; being<BR>poured out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्चत्
सिञ्चत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, sprinkling, wetting,<BR>scattering water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक|सेकः
सेक, अस्, m. sprinkling, besprinkling, moistening,<BR>watering (of plants &c.); aspersion; pouring out,<BR>effusion, emission; seminal effusion, impregnation;<BR>that which is poured out, a libation, offering; semi-<BR>nal fluid; a drop of anything.<BR>—सेक-पात्र, अम्, n.<BR>a vessel for pouring out or holding water; a watering-<BR>pot, baling-vessel, bucket.<BR>—सेकान्त (˚क-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the end or conclusion of the process of watering<BR>(plants &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकिम|सेकिमं
सेकिम, अम्, n. a radish (= मूलक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्तव्य
सेक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sprinkled or poured<BR>out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्तृ
सेक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, sprinkling, who or what<BR>sprinkles or impregnates; (ता), m. a sprinkler; a<BR>water-carrier; a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्त्र|सेक्त्रं
सेक्त्र, अम्, n. a vessel for holding or pouring<BR>out water, a watering-pot, bucket, baling-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचक|सेचकः
सेचक, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkling, a sprinkler; (अस्),<BR>m. a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचन|सेचनं
सेचन, अम्, n. the act of sprinkling or watering,<BR>aspersion, effusion, pouring; dripping, oozing out;<BR>(अम्, ई), n. f. a bucket, baling-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचनीय
सेचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sprinkled or watered,<BR>to be poured out or effused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेच्य
सेच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sprinkled; to be moist-<BR>ened, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्चिता|सिंचिता
सिञ्चिता सिञ्चिता, f. long pepper (= पिप्पली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्जा|सिंजा
सिञ्जा सिञ्जा, f. (for शिञ्जा, q. v.), the jingling<BR>sound of metallic ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्जित|सिंजित|सिंजितं
सिञ्जित, अम्, n. tinkling (= शिञ्जित, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्जिनी
सिञ्जिनी, f. = शिञ्जिनी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिट्
सिट् सिट् (= rts. शिट्, षिट्), cl. 1. P. सेटति,<BR>&c., to disregard, despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
सित 2. सित, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (thought by<BR>some to be fr. 2. असित, q. v.; apparently connected<BR>with शिति, p. 1005, cf. श्वित, श्वेत, p. 1031, and<BR>see सिन; for 1. see under rt. सि, for 3. see under<BR>rt. 1. सो), white; (अस्), m. the colour white; the<BR>light half of the month from new to full moon; the<BR>planet Venus or its regent, = शुक्र; (आ), f. candied<BR>sugar, sugar; moonlight; a handsome woman;<BR>spirituous liquor; white Dūrvā grass; Arabian jas-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-c" target="_blank">Page1113-c+ 81</a>]<BR>mine; a sort of Clitoria; a kind of Aparājitā plant<BR>(growing on mountains); various other plants or<BR>trees, = श्वेत-कण्टकारी; = वाकुची; = विदारी; =<BR>कुटुम्बिनी; = पिङ्गा; = त्रायमाणा; = तेजनी;<BR>(अम्), n. silver; sandal; a radish (= मूलक).<BR>—सित-कण्टा or सित-कण्टारिका, f. a kind of plant<BR>(= श्वेत-कण्टकारी).<BR>—सित-कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>white-throated, having a white neck; (अस्), m. a<BR>gallinule.<BR>—सित-कर, अस्, m. ‘white-rayed,’ the<BR>moon; camphor.<BR>—सित-कर्णी, f. a kind of plant<BR>(= वासक).<BR>—सित-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, pure in deeds<BR>or actions.<BR>—सित-कुञ्जर, अस्, m. a white elephant;<BR>N. of Indra's elephant; ‘having a white elephant,’<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>—सित-गुञ्जा, f. a kind of plant<BR>(= श्वेत-गुञ्जा).<BR>—सित-चिह्न, अस्, m. ‘white-<BR>marked,’ a sort of fish (= बालुका-गड).<BR>—सित-<BR>च्छत्त्र, अम्, n. a white umbrella (especially as one<BR>of the emblems of royalty); (आ or ई), f. a sort of<BR>fennel (= शत-पुष्पा).<BR>—सित-च्छत्रित, अस्, m.<BR>having a white umbrella, possessed of all the insignia<BR>of royalty, (according to the Scholiast on Naiṣadha<BR>I. 1. = श्वेतातपत्री-कृत, made into a white um-<BR>brella.)<BR>—सित-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘white-feathered,’<BR>a goose; (आ), f. white Dūrvā grass.<BR>—सित-तुरग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘white-horsed,’ epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—सित-<BR>दर्भ, अस्, m. white Kuśa grass.<BR>—सित-दीधिति,<BR>इस्, m. ‘white-rayed,’ the moon.<BR>—सित-दीप्य, अस्,<BR>m. white cumin.<BR>—सित-दूर्वा, f. white Dūrvā<BR>grass.<BR>—सित-द्रु, उस्, m. ‘white tree,’ a species of<BR>Moraṭa plant.<BR>—सित-धातु, उस्, m. a white mineral;<BR>chalk.<BR>—सित-पक्ष, अस्, m. a white wing; the<BR>light half of a lunar month; ‘white-winged,’ a<BR>goose; [cf. धवल-पक्ष.]<BR>—सित-पर्णी, f.<BR>‘white-leafed,’ a kind of plant (= अर्क-पुष्पिका).<BR>—सित-पाटलिका, f. the white Pāṭalā tree.<BR>—सित-<BR>पुङ्खा, f. the white Śara-puṅkhā plant.<BR>—सित-<BR>पुष्प, अस्, m. the Tagara tree; a kind of grass<BR>(= काश); a kind of tree, = श्वेत-रोहित; (आ), f.<BR>Arabian jasmine; (ई), f. a kind of white Aparājitā<BR>plant; (अम्), n. a sort of grass, Cyperus Rotundus.<BR>—सित-मणि, इस्, m. a white precious stone, a<BR>crystal.<BR>—सितमणि-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of<BR>crystals or jewels, made of crystal.<BR>—सित-मरिच,<BR>अम्, n. white pepper.<BR>—सित-माष, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of bean (= राज-माष).<BR>—सित-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>white and red.<BR>—सित-रञ्जन, अस्, m. ‘white-<BR>tinged,’ yellow (the colour).<BR>—सित-रश्मि, इस्, m.<BR>‘white-rayed,’ the moon.<BR>—सित-वर्षाभू, ऊस्, m.<BR>a kind of plant (= पुनर्-णवा).<BR>—सित-वाजिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘having white horses,’ epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—सित-<BR>शर्करा, f. candied sugar.<BR>—सित-शायका, f. the<BR>white Śara-puṅkhā plant.<BR>—सित-शिंशपा, f. the<BR>white Śiṃśapā tree.<BR>—सित-शिम्बिक, अस्, m. ‘white-<BR>awned,’ wheat, (also read शिति-शिम्बिक.)<BR>—सित-<BR>शिव, अम्, n. rock-salt, (also read शित-शिव, सित-<BR>सिव, शीत-शिव, शीत-सिव.)<BR>—सित-शूक, अस्, m.<BR>‘white-awned,’ barley; [cf. शित-शूक.]<BR>—सित-शू-<BR>रण, अस्, m. the plant Vana-śūraṇa.<BR>—सित-श्म-<BR>श्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, having a white beard, silvery-<BR>bearded.<BR>—सित-सप्ति, इस्, m. ‘having white horses,’<BR>epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—सित-सर्षप, अस्, m. white<BR>mustard.<BR>—सित-सार or सित-सारक, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>white pith,’ the Śāliñca plant.<BR>—सित-सिंही, f. the<BR>white Kaṇṭakārī plant.<BR>—सित-सिन्धु, उस्, f. ‘white<BR>river,’ the Ganges.<BR>—सित-सिव, see सित-शिव.<BR>—सि-<BR>तांशु (˚त-अं˚), उस्, m. ‘white-rayed,’ the moon;<BR>camphor.<BR>—सितांशुक (˚त-अं˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dressed<BR>in a white mantle or garment.<BR>—सितांशु-तैल, अम्,<BR>n. camphor oil or ointment.<BR>—सिता-खण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of clayed or refined sugar (said to be<BR>prepared from honey).<BR>—सिताग्र (˚त-अग्˚), अस्, m.<BR>= शिताग्र, a thorn.<BR>—सिताङ्क (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘white-marked,’ the Bālukā-gaḍa fish.<BR>—सिताङ्ग<BR>(˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, m. the Śveta-rohita tree.<BR>—सिताङ्ग-<BR>राग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a white cosmetic or deco-<BR>ration for the limbs or body.<BR>—सिताजाजी (˚त-अज्˚),<BR>f. white cumin.<BR>—सितातप-वारण (˚त-आत्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a white umbrella (especially as a symbol of<BR>royalty).<BR>—सितादि (˚त-आदि?), इस्, m. treacle, mo-<BR>lasses (= गुड).<BR>—सितानन (˚त-आन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>white-faced; (अस्), m. epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—सिता-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">Page1114-a+ 78</a>]<BR>पाङ्ग (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, m. ‘having white eye-corners,’<BR>a peacock.<BR>—सिताब्ज (˚त-अब्˚), अम्, n. a white<BR>lotus.<BR>—सिताभ (˚त-आभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘white-looking,’<BR>camphor; (आ), f. = तक्राह्वा (according to Śabda-k.).<BR>—सिताभ्र (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. or सिता-<BR>भ्रक, अम्, n. (see अभ्र), camphor; (incorrectly<BR>written शिताभ्र.)<BR>—सिताम्बर (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, clothed in white garments; (अस्), m. an ascetic<BR>wearing white garments.<BR>—सिताम्बुज (˚त-अम्˚)<BR>or सिताम्भोज (˚त-अम्˚), अम्, n. a white lotus.<BR>—सितार्जक (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, m. white basil.<BR>—सिता-<BR>लक (˚त-अल्˚), अस्, m. the white Mandāraka tree.<BR>—सिता-लता, f. white Dūrvā grass.<BR>—सितालि (˚त-आलि),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, having white lines.<BR>—सितालि-कटभी,<BR>f. the white Kiṇihī tree.<BR>—सितालिका (˚त-आल्˚), f.<BR>‘white-lined,’ a cockle.<BR>—सितावर (˚त- or ˚ता-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a species of culinary plant (commonly called<BR>Susunī, = मेधा-कृत्); (ई), f. the plant Vākucī.<BR>—सिताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘having white horses,’<BR>epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—सितासित (˚त-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>white and black; (अस्), m., N. of Bala-rāma; (औ),<BR>m. du. Venus and Saturn.<BR>—सिताह्वय (˚त-आह्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the white Śigru tree; the Śveta-rohita tree.<BR>—सितेक्षु (˚त-इक्˚), उस्, m. white sugar-cane.<BR>—सितेतर (˚त-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, other than white,<BR>black; (अस्), m. a kind of dark-coloured rice; a<BR>kind of pulse (= कुलत्थ).<BR>—सितेतर-गति, इस्, m.<BR>‘having a black course,’ epithet of fire; [cf. कृष्ण-<BR>वर्त्मन्.]<BR>—सितोत्पल (˚त-उत्˚), अम्, n. a white<BR>water-lily.<BR>—सितोदर (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘white-<BR>bellied,’ epithet of the god Kuvera (who is described<BR>as deformed and whitened by a leprous taint).<BR>—सि-<BR>तोद्भव (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced from<BR>sugar; (अम्), n. white sandal.<BR>—सितोपल (˚त-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘white stone,’ crystal; (आ), f. refined or<BR>candied sugar; (अम्), n. chalk (or a similar substance<BR>considered as a variety).<BR>—सितोष्ण-वारण (˚त-<BR>उष्˚), अम्, n. ‘white heat-repeller,’ a white um-<BR>brella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिति|सितिः
2. सिति, इस्, इस्, इ (connected with शिति, p. 1005;<BR>for 1. see p. 1112, col. 3; for 3. see under rt. 1. सो),<BR>white; black.<BR>—सिति-कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>white throat; dark-necked; (अस्), m. Śiva; [cf.<BR>शिति-कण्ठ.]<BR>—सिति-वार, अस्, m. a kind of culinary<BR>plant (= सु-निषण्णक).<BR>—सिति-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>clad in black; (आस्), m. epithet of Bala-rāma (=<BR>नीलाम्बर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिमन्
सितिमन्, आ, m. whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्ध|सिद्धं|सिद्धः
सिद्ध, सिद्ध, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिली
सिद्धिली सिद्धिली, f. (according to some)<BR>a small ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्
सिध् 1. सिध् (according to Vopa-deva<BR>VIII. 41. the स् of this rt. is not changed<BR>to ष् after prepositions; cf. परि-सिध्), cl. 1. P.<BR>सेधति, सिषेध, सेधिष्यति, असेधीत्, सेधि-<BR>तुम्, to go, (in Naigh. II. 14. सेधति is enume-<BR>rated among the गति-कर्माणः); to go towards,<BR>reach, strike, hit (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेध|सेधः
1. सेध, अस्, m. going, reaching [cf. उत्-स्˚]; a tail<BR>(according to some; cf. गो-ष्˚); (आ), f. a porcupine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधत्
सेधत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधन
1. सेधन, अम्, n. the act of going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधित्वा
1. सेधित्वा, ind. having gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्
सिध् 2. सिध् (this rt. allows the change<BR>of स् to ष् after prepositions, cf. प्रति-<BR>षिध्), cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) सेधति (-ते), सि-<BR>षेध, सेत्स्यति or सेधिष्यति, असैत्सीत् or असे-<BR>धीत्, सेद्धुम् or सेधितुम्, to drive off, ward off,<BR>keep off, restrain, hinder; to interdict; to ordain,<BR>instruct; to turn out well or auspiciously: Caus.<BR>सेधयति, -यितुम्: Desid. of Caus. सिषेधयि-<BR>षति: Desid. सिसेधिषति, सिसिधिषति, सिषित्-<BR>सति: Intens. सेषिध्यते, सेषेद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेद्धव्य
सेद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be kept off, to be pre-<BR>vented, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेध|सेधः
2. सेध, अस्, m. restraint, restraining, hindering;<BR>[cf. नि-षेध under नि-षिध्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधक
सेधक, अस्, आ, अम्, driving off, preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधन
2. सेधन, अम्, n. the act of restraining or keep-<BR>ing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधनीय
सेधनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, = सेद्धव्य, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्
सिध् 3. सिध् (connected with rt. साध्),<BR>cl. 4. P. सिध्यति (ep. also A. -ते), सि-<BR>षेध, सेत्स्यति, असिधत्, सेद्धुम्, to be accom-<BR>plished, be fulfilled, be effected; to be successful,<BR>succeed; to be settled or established; to be valid;<BR>to be proved or demonstrated; to be thoroughly<BR>prepared or cooked; to attain an object, hit an aim,<BR>fall true (with loc., e. g. इषुः सिध्यति लक्ष्ये,<BR>the arrow falls true on the mark): Pass. सिध्यते,<BR>Aor. असेधि, to be completed or concluded, &c.:<BR>Caus. सेधयति, with reference to sacred things;<BR>साधयति, -यितुम्, with reference to secular things,<BR>(Pāṇ. VI. 1, 49; see rt. साध्); to accomplish,<BR>complete, effect, settle, perform: Desid. सिषित्सति:<BR>Intens. सेषिध्यते, सेषेद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्ध|सिद्धं|सिद्धः
सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished, effected, com-<BR>pleted, finished, perfected, fulfilled, performed, ob-<BR>tained, acquired, gained; succeeded, successful;<BR>settled, established, substantiated, demonstrated,<BR>proved; valid (as a rule of grammar or in law);<BR>admitted to be true or right; adjudicated, decided,<BR>terminated (as a lawsuit); paid, liquidated, settled<BR>(as a debt); ready (as money); thoroughly pre-<BR>pared, concocted, compounded (as drugs &c.);<BR>cooked, dressed; matured, ripened, ripe; subjugated,<BR>subdued, brought into subjection (by magical power);<BR>thoroughly skilled or versed (in magical arts &c.);<BR>perfected or sanctified (by penance, austerities, &c.);<BR>emancipated, beatified; endowed with supernatural<BR>powers or faculties, (of these eight are usually enu-<BR>merated, see under सिद्धि below; but twenty-six<BR>others are sometimes added, e. g. दूर-श्रवण,<BR>सर्वज्ञ-त्व, मनोयायि-त्व, वह्नि-स्तम्भ, &c.,<BR>see under स्तम्भ); sacred, holy, pious, divine,<BR>immortal, eternal; well-known, eminent, celebrated;<BR>illustrious, shining, splendid; (अस्), m. a semi-divine<BR>being supposed to be of great purity and holiness,<BR>and said to be specially characterized by the eight<BR>supernatural faculties (of which अणिमन् is the first;<BR>see under सिद्धि; according to some the Siddhas<BR>inhabit, together with the Munis &c., the Bhuvar-<BR>loka or middle region between the earth and the<BR>sun; according to the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa eighty-eight<BR>thousand of them occupy the regions of the sky<BR>north of the sun and south of the seven Ṛṣis;<BR>they are regarded as immortal, but only in the sense<BR>of living to the end of a Kalpa; in the later mytho-<BR>logy they appear to be sometimes confused with the<BR>Sādhyas, whose place they seem occasionally to take,<BR>see साध्य); an inspired sage or seer (as Vyāsa and<BR>others); any holy or sanctified personage or great<BR>saint (especially one who by austere practices has<BR>attained some or all of the five states of beatitude,<BR>see सलोक-ता, सरूप-ता, सामीप्य, सायुज्य,<BR>सार्ष्टि-ता); an adept in magical or mystical arts,<BR>one who by the performance of certain mystical rites<BR>has acquired superhuman powers, (see above and<BR>under सिद्धि); a lawsuit, judicial trial (= व्यव-<BR>हार); a kind of dark Dhustūra or thorn-apple;<BR>another plant or a sort of hard sugar (= गुड); N.<BR>of the twenty-first of the astronomical Yogas; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f. a medicinal plant or<BR>root (= ऋद्धि); N. of one of the eight Yoginīs,<BR>(see under योगिन्); (अम्), n. sea-salt.<BR>—सिद्ध-<BR>कामेश्वरी, f. one of the five forms of Kāmākhyā<BR>or Durgā.<BR>—सिद्ध-केरल, अम्, n. ‘the perfect<BR>Kerala,’ N. of a district.<BR>—सिद्ध-क्षेत्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a place.<BR>—सिद्ध-गङ्गा, f. the divine or<BR>heavenly Ganges (= मन्दाकिनी).<BR>—सिद्ध-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a particular kind of madness or seizure<BR>(produced by supernatural agency).<BR>—सिद्ध-जल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘cooked water,’ the fermented water of<BR>boiled rice or sour rice-gruel.<BR>—सिद्ध-ता, f. or<BR>सिद्ध-त्व, अम्, n. perfection, completion; the<BR>establishment or validity of a rule or doctrine.<BR>—सिद्ध-देव, अस्, m. ‘perfected deity,’ epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—सिद्ध-धातु, उस्, m. ‘perfected mineral,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-c" target="_blank">Page1114-c+ 81</a>]<BR>quicksilver.<BR>—सिद्ध-धामन्, अ, n. the abode of<BR>the Siddhas.<BR>—सिद्ध-पक्ष, अस्, m. the established<BR>or logical side of an argument.<BR>—सिद्ध-पीठ, अस्,<BR>m. a most sacred station or shrine; a place sacred<BR>to Durgā.<BR>—सिद्ध-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a mythical<BR>city said to be located in the southern or lower<BR>regions of the earth.<BR>—सिद्ध-पुरुष, अस्, m. a<BR>perfect or completely sanctified personage; a sage, seer;<BR>an adept in mystical rites.<BR>—सिद्ध-पुष्प, अस्, m.<BR>‘having perfect flowers,’ the Kara-vīra plant.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>ध-प्रयोजन, अस्, m. white mustard.<BR>—सिद्ध-<BR>प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, almost accomplished, nearly com-<BR>pleted, almost finished.<BR>—सिद्ध-भूमि, इस्, f. the<BR>region inhabited by Siddhas.<BR>—सिद्ध-मनोरम,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the second day of the civil month<BR>(कर्म-मास).<BR>—सिद्ध-मन्त्र, अस्, m. a parti-<BR>cular Mantra of great efficacy.<BR>—सिद्ध-मोदक,<BR>अस्, m. a particular kind of candied sugar prepared<BR>from the Tavarāja plant.<BR>—सिद्ध-यात्रिक, अस्, m.<BR>a pilgrim who seeks the region of the Siddhas.<BR>—सिद्ध-योगिन्, ई, m. epithet of Śiva; (इनी), f.,<BR>N. of a particular Yoginī; of the goddess Manasā.<BR>—सिद्ध-योगेश्वर-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra work.<BR>—सिद्ध-रस, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>perfected metallic fluids, mineral, metallic; (अस्), m.<BR>‘perfected mineral,’ quicksilver; skilled in the science<BR>of metals, an alchemist.<BR>—सिद्ध-रुद्रेश्वर-तीर्थ<BR>(˚र-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सिद्ध-वट,<BR>N. of a place.<BR>—सिद्ध-वटी, f., N. of a tutelary<BR>goddess.<BR>—सिद्ध-विद्या, f. the worship of Durgā<BR>under a particular form.<BR>—सिद्ध-सङ्कल्प, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who has accomplished his wishes.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>ध-सङ्घ, अस्, m. a company of Siddhas, assem-<BR>blage of saints.<BR>—सिद्ध-सलिल, अम्, n. ‘cooked<BR>water,’ sour rice-gruel.<BR>—सिद्ध-साधक, अस्, m.<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सिद्ध-साधन, अस्, m. white<BR>mustard; (अम्), n. the performance of magical or<BR>mystical rites (for the acquisition of supernatural<BR>powers, &c.); the materials employed in mystical<BR>or chemical processes.<BR>—सिद्ध-साधन-दोष,<BR>अस्, m. the error of labouring to establish what is<BR>already proved.<BR>—सिद्ध-साध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, who<BR>or what has effected what was to be done; effected,<BR>accomplished, proved; (अस्), m. a particular Mantra;<BR>(अम्), n. demonstrated proof or conclusion.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>ध-सारस्वत, N. of a work.<BR>—सिद्धसारस्वत-<BR>दीपिका, f., N. of a commentary by Padmanābha on<BR>the Bhuvaneśvarī-stotra.<BR>—सिद्ध-सिद्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>particular Mantra.<BR>—सिद्ध-सिन्धु, उस्, f. ‘divine<BR>river,’ epithet of the Ganges.<BR>—सिद्ध-सुसिद्ध,<BR>अस्, m. a particular Mantra.<BR>—सिद्ध-सेन, अस्, m.<BR>‘having a divine or perfect army,’ epithet of Kārtti-<BR>keya (god of war); of an astronomer.<BR>—सिद्ध-<BR>सेन-दिवाकर, अस्, m., N. of a son of Sarva-jña<BR>and pupil of Vṛddha-vāda-sūri (said to have induced<BR>Vikramāditya to tolerate the Jaina religion).<BR>—सिद्-<BR>ध-सेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured or worshipped<BR>by Siddhas; (अस्), m. epithet of a form of Bhairava<BR>or Śiva (= वटुक-भैरव).<BR>—सिद्ध-स्थाली,<BR>f. the boiler or pot of a seer (fabled as a vessel<BR>bestowed by a holy personage, and gifted with the<BR>property of overflowing with any kind of food at<BR>the wish of the possessor).<BR>—सिद्धान्त (˚ध-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. established end [cf. राद्धान्त];<BR>demonstrated conclusion of an argument, the esta-<BR>blished line of reasoning or view of any question,<BR>the true logical conclusion (following on the refuta-<BR>tion of the पूर्व-पक्ष or first objection), esta-<BR>blished truth, proved fact, settled opinion or doc-<BR>trine, dogma, axiom, received or admitted truth<BR>(regarded as of four kinds, viz. सर्व-तन्त्र-स्˚,<BR>प्रति-तन्त्र-स्˚, अधिकरण-स्˚, अभ्युपगम-<BR>स्˚, q. q. v. v.); any fixed or established text-book<BR>resting on conclusive arguments, (often used at the<BR>end of comps. to denote certain received treatises<BR>by high authorities on astronomy, mathematics, and<BR>other sciences; nine astronomical works being espe-<BR>cially so designated, viz. the Brahma-s˚, Sūrya-s˚,<BR>Soma-s˚, Vṛhaspati-s˚, Garaga-s˚, Nārada-s˚, Parā-<BR>śara-s˚, Pulastya-s˚, Vasiṣṭha-s˚; five principal astro-<BR>nomical Siddhāntas are enumerated by others, viz.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-a" target="_blank">Page1115-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Pauliśa-s˚, Romaka-s˚, Vāsiṣṭha-s˚, Śaura-s˚, and<BR>Paitāmaha-s˚.)<BR>—सिद्धान्त-कोटि, इस्, f. the point in<BR>an argument which is regarded as a logical conclu-<BR>sion.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-कौमुदी, f., N. of a celebrated<BR>grammar by Bhaṭṭoji-dīkṣita (intended to furnish<BR>a practical arrangement of Pāṇini's Sūtras with a<BR>commentary).<BR>—सिद्धान्त-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a work by Madana-pāla.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-चन्द्रिका,<BR>f. a commentary on the Sarasvatī-sūtra by Rāma-<BR>candrāśrama; another on the Śāstra-dīpikā by<BR>Rāma-kṛṣṇa-bhaṭṭa; N. of Rāma-saṃyamin's Ve-<BR>dānta precepts.<BR>—सिद्धान्तचन्द्रिका-टीका, f. a<BR>commentary by Gaṅgādhara-yati on Rāma-saṃya-<BR>min's work.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-चन्द्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a commentary by Kṛṣṇa-dhūrjaṭi-dīkṣita<BR>on the Tarka-saṅgraha.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-चिन्तामणि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a work on astronomy.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-<BR>तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a work on the principles of<BR>the Vaiśeṣika doctrines, (also called Padārtha-viveka.)<BR>—सिद्धान्ततत्त्व-बिन्दु, a commentary by Ma-<BR>dhu-sūdana-sarasvatī on Śaṅkarācārya's Daśa-ślokī.<BR>—सिद्धान्ततत्त्वबिन्दु-सन्दीपन or बिन्दु-<BR>सन्दीपन, अम्, n. a commentary by Puruṣottama<BR>Sarasvatī on the preceding.<BR>—सिद्धान्ततत्त्व-सर्-<BR>वस्व, अम्, n. a commentary on the Siddhānta-<BR>tattva by Gopīnātha-maunin.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-दीपिका,<BR>f. a commentary on the Siddhānta-muktāvalī by<BR>Nānā-dīkṣita.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-पक्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>logically correct side of an argument.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-<BR>बिन्दु = सिद्धान्ततत्त्व-बिन्दु, q. v.<BR>—सिद्धान्-<BR>तबिन्दु-व्याख्या, f. a commentary by Nārāyaṇa-<BR>yati on the preceding.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-मुक्तावली, f.<BR>‘string of pearls of dogmatic precepts,’ N. of a com-<BR>mentary by Viśva-nātha Pañcānana Bhaṭṭācārya<BR>Tarkālaṅkāra on the Bhāṣā-pariccheda (a text-<BR>book of the Nyāya, also called मुक्तावली); of a<BR>metrical Vedānta treatise with a prose interpretation<BR>by Prakāśānanda; of a metrical exposition of the<BR>theory of Vallabhācārya.<BR>—सिद्धान्तमुक्तावली-<BR>प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a commentary on the Sid-<BR>dhānta-muktāvalī.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-रत्न, N. of a<BR>summary of the Vedānta system by Nimbārka (=<BR>दश-श्लोकी).<BR>—सिद्धान्त-रहस्य, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a work on astronomy.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-लेश, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a metrical work by Apya-dīkṣita on the<BR>Vedānta and other systems of philosophy.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>धान्त-वागीश, अस्, m., N. of the preceptor of<BR>Rāghavendra.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-शिरोमणि, N. of an<BR>astronomical work by Bhāskara.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-सङ्-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of an epitome of Vijñāneśvara's<BR>Mitākṣarā.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-सन्दर्भ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an astronomical work.<BR>—सिद्धान्त-सुन्दर,<BR>N. of a work on astronomy by Jñāna-rāja.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>धान्त-सूक्ति-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a metrical abridg-<BR>ment of the Siddhānta-leśa by Gaṅgā-dhara-sarasvatī.<BR>—सिद्धान्ताचार (˚त-आच्˚), अस्, m. a perfect rule<BR>of action (with the Tāntrikas); one who practises<BR>this rule (said to consist in purity, quietism, and<BR>complete mental absorption in Durgā).<BR>—सिद्धान्-<BR>तित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. सिद्धान्त), logically demon-<BR>strated or proved, established as true.<BR>—सिद्धान्तिन्,<BR>ई, m. one who establishes or proves his conclusions;<BR>one learned in scientific text-books; a follower of<BR>the Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR>—सिद्धान्न (˚ध-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. dressed food, cooked victuals.<BR>—सिद्धापगा<BR>(˚ध-अप्˚), f. ‘divine river,’ epithet of the Ganges.<BR>—सिद्धारि (˚ध-अरि), इस्, m. a particular Mantra.<BR>—सिद्धार्थ (˚ध-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>accomplished an aim or object, successful, prosperous;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of the great Buddha (or Śākya-<BR>muni, founder of the Buddhist religion); N. of the<BR>father of the last and most celebrated Arhat of the<BR>present Ava-sarpiṇī; epithet of Śiva; white mustard;<BR>(आ), f., N. of the mother of the fourth of the<BR>twenty-four Arhats.<BR>—सिद्धार्थक, अम्, n. white<BR>mustard.<BR>—सिद्धार्थ-कारिन्, ई, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सिद्धार्थिन् (˚ध-अर्˚), ई, m., N. of the fifty-<BR>third (or twenty-seventh) year of Jupiter's cycle of<BR>sixty years.<BR>—सिद्धाश्रम (˚ध-आश्˚), N. of a<BR>hermitage in the Himālaya (where Viṣṇu performed<BR>penance before his dwarf incarnation).<BR>—सिद्धा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">Page1115-b+ 81</a>]<BR>श्रम-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सिद्धा-<BR>सन (˚ध-आस्˚), अम्, n. a particular posture in<BR>religious meditation (described as placing the left<BR>heel under the body and the right heel in front of<BR>it, fixing the sight between the eyebrows, and medi-<BR>tating upon the syllable ॐ).<BR>—सिद्धेश्वर-तन्त्र<BR>(˚ध-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>धेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>धेश्वरी (˚ध-ईश्˚), f., N. of a particular goddess.<BR>—सिद्धौघ (˚ध-ओघ), अस्, m., N. of a par-<BR>ticular class of Gurus worshipped or revered by the<BR>Tāntrikas, (their names are said to be Nārada,<BR>Kāśyapa, Śambhu, Bhārgava, Kula-kauśika.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धक|सिद्धकः
सिद्धक, अस्, m. a kind of tree (= सिन्धु-<BR>वार); the Śāl tree; a species of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धा
सिद्धा. See under सिद्ध, p. 1114, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धायिका
सिद्धायिका, f., N. of one of the twenty-four<BR>goddesses, called Śāsana-devatās, who execute the<BR>commands of the twenty-four Arhats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धि|सिद्धिः
सिद्धि, इस्, f. accomplishment, fulfilment, com-<BR>pletion, perfection, complete attainment (of any<BR>object), performance; success, prosperity, well-being;<BR>settlement, establishment, substantiation, demonstra-<BR>tion, proof, indisputable conclusion; validity (of a<BR>rule or law); certainty, truth, accuracy, correctness;<BR>decision, adjudication, determination (of a lawsuit);<BR>payment, liquidation (of a debt), acquittance; the<BR>solution of a problem; preparation, cooking, matur-<BR>ing, maturity; readiness; complete knowledge;<BR>complete perfection or sanctification (by penance<BR>&c.); final emancipation, supreme felicity, beati-<BR>tude; the acquisition of supernatural powers by<BR>magical means or the supernatural faculty so ac-<BR>quired, (eight are usually enumerated, e. g. अणिमन्,<BR>महिमन्, लघिमन्, गरिमन्, प्राप्ति, प्रा-<BR>काम्य, ईशि-त्व, वशि-त्व, q. q. v. v., to which is<BR>sometimes added कामावसायि-त्व and many others,<BR>e. g. सिद्धिः खेचरी, the magical power of flying<BR>through the air; रसोल्लास, q. v., वि-शोका, q. v., see<BR>also under सिद्ध, p. 1114); any marvellous skill or<BR>capability; a magical shoe or slipper (supposed to<BR>have the power of conveying the wearer wherever<BR>he likes); good effect or result, use, advantage; un-<BR>derstanding, intellect; concealment, vanishing, mak-<BR>ing one's self invisible; a particular Yoga (either the<BR>sixteenth of the astronomical periods or the nine-<BR>teenth of the twenty-eight astrological Yogas); a<BR>kind of medicinal root (= ऋद्धि); Perfection (per-<BR>sonified as a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of<BR>Dharma); N. of a Yoginī; of Durgā; of Śiva, (in<BR>this sense masc.)<BR>—सिद्धि-कारण, अम्, n. a cause<BR>of beatitude, means of obtaining felicity.<BR>—सिद्धि-<BR>चामुण्डा-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सिद्धि-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, conferring felicity or beatitude; (अस्),<BR>m. epithet of a form of Bhairava or Śiva (= वटुक-<BR>भैरव).<BR>—सिद्धि-दात्री, f. ‘giver of perfection,’<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—सिद्धि-भैरव, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tantra work.<BR>—सिद्धि-योग, अस्, m. a parti-<BR>cular auspicious conjunction of the planets.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>धि-योगिनी, f. a kind of Yoginī.<BR>—सिद्धि-लाभ,<BR>अस्, m. acquirement of success or perfection.<BR>—सिद्-<BR>धि-सोपान, ‘ladder of success,’ N. of a work.<BR>—सिद्धि-स्थान, अम्, n. ‘place of felicity,’ N. of<BR>any sacred spot where final beatitude is obtained by<BR>religious worship (such as particular places on the<BR>Ganges or Sarasvatī).<BR>—सिद्ध्य्-अर्थम्, ind. for<BR>the sake of accomplishing or obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्ध्वा
सिद्ध्वा, ind. having accomplished or effected,<BR>having completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिधित्वा
सिधित्वा, ind. (according to some) = सिद्ध्वा<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्म|सिध्मं
सिध्म, अम्, or सिध्मन्, अ, n. a blotch, pustule,<BR>scab; pock-mark, leprous spot; leprosy or a kind of<BR>leprosy (one of the seven kinds).<BR>—सिध्म-पुष्-<BR>पिका, f. a particular kind of cutaneous disease or<BR>leprosy.<BR>—सिध्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, scabby, pock-<BR>marked, covered with pustules or blotches; leprous,<BR>tainted with leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मल|सिध्मलः
सिध्मल, अस्, आ, अम्, = सिध्म-वत्; (आ), f. a<BR>scab, blotch, leprous spot; a sort of leprosy; dried<BR>fish, salt fish (= मत्स्य-विकृति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मा
सिध्मा, f. a blotch, scab, leprous spot; leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्य|सिध्यः
सिध्य, अस्, m. ‘auspicious,’ N. of the asterism<BR>Puṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्र|सिध्रः
सिध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. obtaining, effecting,<BR>(Sāy. = साधक); perfect, good; protecting; (अस्),<BR>m. a pious or virtuous man; a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रका
सिध्रका, f. a kind of plant or tree.<BR>—सिध्रका-<BR>वण, अम्, n. ‘Sidhrakā-grove,’ N. of one of the<BR>celestial gardens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधित्वा
2. सेधित्वा, ind. (according to some) = सिद्ध्वा,<BR>col. 2; [cf. 1. सेधित्वा under rt. 1. सिध्. ]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन|सिनं|सिनः
सिन सिन, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 2. fr. rt. सि, ‘to bind;’ see also Nirukta V. 5),<BR>‘a quantity of anything bound or collected together,’<BR>a lump of food, &c., mouthful; (अम्), n. the body;<BR>food (Ved.; Sāy. = अन्न); (अस्, ई, अम्), white,<BR>white-coloured (according to Śabda-k.); blind with<BR>one eye, one-eyed, = काण; (ई), f. white, (perhaps<BR>an old fem. of 2. सित; cf. श्येनी under श्येन.)<BR>—सिन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनीवाली
सिनीवाली, f. (said to be connected with सिनी,<BR>‘white;’ but in Nirukta XI. 31. सिनी is connected<BR>with rt. सि and वाली with rt. वल्, ‘to surround,’ or<BR>with बाल, ‘young;’ the real meaning may be ‘a<BR>white ring’), the day preceding that of new moon<BR>or the day on which the moon rises with a thin<BR>crescent of light scarcely visible; N. of a Vedic god-<BR>dess; of the goddess Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुक|सिंदुक|सिंदुकः|सिन्दुकः
सिन्दुक सिन्दुक, अस्, m. (probably fr. rt.<BR>स्यन्द्, see below), the small tree or shrub Vitex<BR>Negundo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुवार|सिंदुवार|सिंदुवारः|सिन्दुवारः
सिन्दु-वार, अस्, m. (probably for स्यन्द-वार,<BR>the plant being used medicinally to prevent flow<BR>of the humors and laxity), = सिन्दुक above; [cf.<BR>सिन्धु-वार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूर|सिंदूर|सिन्दूरं|सिंदूरः|सिन्दूरः
सिन्दूर सिन्दूर, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. I. 69.<BR>said to be fr. rt. स्यन्द्), a sort of tree; (ई), f., N.<BR>of a plant (= रोचनी); the plant Grislea Tomentosa<BR>(= धातकी); the plant Lythrum Fruticosum; red<BR>cloth or clothes; (अम्), n. red lead, minium, ver-<BR>milion; = राज-लेख (according to some).<BR>—सिन्-<BR>दूर-कारण, अम्, n. ‘origin of minium,’ lead.<BR>—सिन्दूर-तिलक, अस्, m. ‘marked with red lead,’<BR>an elephant; (आ), f. a woman whose forehead is<BR>marked with red lead (and therefore whose husband<BR>is living).<BR>—सिन्दूर-निर्गम, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>137th chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa or second part<BR>of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—सिन्दूर-पुष्पी, f. a kind<BR>of plant (= वीर-पुष्पी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरिका|सिंदूरिका
सिन्दूरिका, f. red lead, minium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरित|सिंदूरित
सिन्दूरित, अस्, आ, अम्, reddened, made red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धु|सिंधु|सिंधुः|सिन्धुः
सिन्धु सिन्धु, उस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rt. स्यन्द्, ‘to flow’), the ocean, sea, (कृपा-<BR>सिन्धु, ‘ocean of mercy,’ a term for an exceedingly<BR>merciful person); N. of Varuṇa (as god of the<BR>ocean); the river Indus; the Indus personified (as<BR>one of the male rivers, cf. नद); the country<BR>around the Indus (commonly called Sindh); the water<BR>into which the Soma drops; water ejected from the<BR>mouth or from an elephant's trunk (= वमथु);<BR>the juice that exudes from an elephant's temples; an<BR>elephant; a particular Rāga or musical mode (re-<BR>garded as son of the Rāga Mālakauśa); the tree<BR>Vitex Negundo [cf. सिन्दुक]; white or refined<BR>borax, = श्वेत-टङ्कण; (अवस्), m. pl. the in-<BR>habitants of Sindh; (उस्), f. the river Sindhu, (Ni-<BR>rukta IX. 26); a river or stream of water in general.<BR>—सिन्धु-कफ, अस्, m. ‘sea-foam,’ cuttle-fish<BR>bone.<BR>—सिन्धु-कर, अम्, n. a kind of white borax<BR>(= श्वेत-टङ्कण).<BR>—सिन्धु-क्षित्, त्, m., N. of<BR>the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 75 (having the<BR>patronymic Praiyamedha).<BR>—सिन्धु-खेल, अस्, m.<BR>‘sported or flowed over by the Indus,’ the country<BR>Sindh.<BR>—सिन्धु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, ocean-born, sea-<BR>born, marine; river-born, aquatic; born or produced<BR>in the country Sindh; (आ), f. epithet of the goddess<BR>Lakṣmī (as produced at the churning of the ocean);<BR>(अम्), n. rock-salt.<BR>—सिन्धु-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>ocean-born, sea-born; produced in Sindh; (आ), m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">Page1116-a+ 76</a>]<BR>the moon; (अ), n. rock-salt.<BR>—सिन्धु-डा, f., N.<BR>of the wife of the Rāga Mālava.<BR>—सिन्धु-देश, अस्,<BR>m. the country of Sindh.<BR>—सिन्धु-द्वीप, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king; of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 9 (having the patronymic Āmbarīṣa).<BR>—सिन्धु-<BR>नद, N. of a river.<BR>—सिन्धु-नन्दन, अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of the ocean,’ the moon (fabled to have been one<BR>of the fourteen precious things recovered at the churn-<BR>ing of the ocean, see मन्दर, p. 746).<BR>—सिन्धु-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of rivers,’ the ocean.<BR>—सिन्धु-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of Sindh,’ epithet of Jayad-ratha.<BR>—सिन्धु-पार-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced<BR>on the further bank of the Indus.<BR>—सिन्धु-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. ‘son of the ocean,’ the moon; a sort of<BR>ebony.<BR>—सिन्धु-पुलिन्द, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—सिन्धु-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘sea-flower,’ a<BR>conch-shell.<BR>—सिन्धु-मध्य, N. of a district.<BR>—सिन्धु-मन्थ, अस्, m. the churning of the<BR>ocean, (see मन्दर, p. 746); ‘ocean churning-<BR>stick,’ a mountain (according to some).<BR>—सिन्धु-<BR>मन्थ-ज, अम्, n. rock-salt.<BR>—सिन्धु-मातृ, ता,<BR>त्री, तृ, Ved. having the sea as mother (said of the<BR>Soma, also of the Maruts and of the Aśvins); (ता), f.<BR>‘mother of streams,’ epithet of the river Sarasvatī<BR>(Ved.).<BR>—सिन्धु-मुख, अम्, n. the mouth of a<BR>river.<BR>—सिन्धु-मुखागत (˚ख-आग्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, arrived at the mouth of a river.<BR>—सिन्धु-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘king of Sindh,’ epithet of Jayad-<BR>ratha.<BR>—सिन्धु-लवण, अम्, n. ‘Sindh-salt,’ rock-<BR>salt.<BR>—सिन्धु-वार, अस्, m. a good horse or one<BR>of a particularly good breed (brought probably from<BR>Sindh or the borders of Persia); the small tree Vitex<BR>Negundo (= सिन्दु-वार).<BR>—सिन्धु-वारक, अस्,<BR>m. Vitex Negundo, (see above.)<BR>—सिन्धु-वारित,<BR>अस्, m. Vitex Negundo, (see above.)<BR>—सिन्धु-वासिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, living in Sindh, an inhabitant of Sindh.<BR>—सिन्धु-वाहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. bringing streams<BR>of water.<BR>—सिन्धु-वेषण, अस्, m. the tree Gme-<BR>lina Arborea.<BR>—सिन्धु-शयन, अस्, m. ‘ocean-<BR>reclining,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सिन्धु-सङ्गम,<BR>अस्, m. ‘sea-confluence,’ the mouth of a river or its<BR>point of junction with the sea.<BR>—सिन्धु-समुद्र-<BR>सङ्गम, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—सिन्धु-सूनु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘son of Sindhu,’ N. of the Asura Jalan-dhara.<BR>—सिन्धु-सौवीर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people (the<BR>people of Sindh and western Rājputāna, according<BR>to some).<BR>—सिन्धूत्थ (˚धु-उत्˚) or सिन्धूद्-<BR>भव (˚धु-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘Sindh-produced,’ rock-<BR>salt (= सैन्धव).<BR>—सिन्धूपल (˚धु-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ‘Sindh-stone,’ rock-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुक|सिंधुक|सिंधुकः|सिन्धुकः
सिन्धुक, अस्, आ, अम्, marine; born or produced<BR>in Sindh; (अस्), m. the tree Vitex Negundo [cf. सिन्-<BR>दुक]; N. of a king (= शूद्रक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुर|सिंधुर|सिंधुरः|सिन्धुरः
सिन्धुर, अस्, m. an elephant; [cf. सिन्धु.]<BR>—सिन्धुर-द्वेषिन्, ई, m. ‘elephant-hater,’ a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुल
सिन्धुल, अस्, m., N. of the father of Bhoja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्व्
