सिपाहण
सिपाहण सिपाहण, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिप्र|सिप्रं|सिप्रः
सिप्र सिप्र, अस्, m. sweat, perspiration,<BR>heat; the moon; (आ), f. a woman's zone; a female<BR>buffalo; N. of a river near Ujjayinī [cf. शिप्रा];<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a lake [cf. शिप्र].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिभ्
सिभ् सिभ् or सिम्भ् = rt. सृभ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्
सिम् सिम्, ind. (in Vedic grammar) a tech-<BR>nical term for the eight simple vowels (viz. अ, आ, इ,<BR>ई, उ, ऊ, ऋ, ॠ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम|सिमः
सिम सिम, अस्, आ, अम्, (in Uṇādi-s. I. 143.<BR>said to be fr. rt. सि; probably connected with<BR>1. सम; सिमस्मात्, abl. c. = सर्वस्मात्, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 95, 7; सिमस्मै, dat. c. everywhere, Ṛg-<BR>veda 1. 115, 4), all, every, whole, entire; (अस्), m.,<BR>Ved. ‘the best, most excellent,’ epithet of Indra,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda VIII. 4, 1. सिमा, voc. c. = सिम =<BR>श्रेष्ठेन्द्र); (आ), f., Ved. a cord, band, (accord-<BR>ing to some अस्, m.; cf. सीमा.)<BR>—सिमा-त्व, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. the state of a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिमिसिमाय
सिमिसिमाय सिमिसिमाय (fr. an imitative<BR>sound), Nom. P. सिमिसिमायति, &c., to tremble,<BR>quiver, be convulsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्बा|सिंबा
सिम्बा सिम्बा, f. (also written शिम्बा, q. v.),<BR>a pod, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्बि|सिम्बिः
सिम्बि, इस्, f. a pod (= शिम्बि).<BR>—सिम्बि-जा, f.<BR>‘pod-born,’ any pulse or grain growing in pods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्बी|सिंबी
सिम्बी, f. = शिम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्भ्
सिम्भ् सिम्भ्. See rt. सिभ्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिर|सिरः
सिर सिर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. सि; but<BR>cf. शिर, शिरा, p. 1006), the root of long pepper;<BR>(आ), f. any tubular vessel of the body, a nerve, vein,<BR>artery, tendon, &c. (see शिरा); a stream, water (Ved.,<BR>Sāy. सिरासु = सरण-शीलास्व् अप्सु, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>121, 11; in Naigh. I. 12. सिरा is enumerated among<BR>the उदक-नामानि; cf. सीरा); a bucket, a baling-<BR>vessel.<BR>—सिरा-जाल, अस्, m. a network or plexus of<BR>vessels or veins, an enlargement of the vessels of<BR>the eye.<BR>—सिरा-मोक्ष, अस्, m. ‘lossing the veins,’<BR>venesection.<BR>—सिरा-व्यध, अस्, m. or सिरा-व्य-<BR>धन, अम्, n. ‘piercing the veins,’ venesection.<BR>—सिरा-हर्ष, अस्, m. thrill of the nerves; a flow of<BR>discoloured tears (according to some).<BR>—सिरोत्पात<BR>(˚रा-उत्˚), अस्, m. disease or morbid affection of the<BR>veins, &c.; redness and inflammation of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिल्
सिल् सिल्. See rt. शिल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिलक
सिलक सिलक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिलिक
सिलिक सिलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to<BR>Sāy.) compact, symmetrical (= संसृत, सङ्गत).<BR>—सिलिक-मध्यम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having com-<BR>pact or symmetrical waists (= संसृत-मध्यम<BR>or शीर्ष-मध्यम, Nirukta IV. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिल्लकी
सिल्लकी सिल्लकी, f. (= सल्लकी, शल्लकी), the<BR>gum olibanum tree, Boswellia Thurifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिव्
सिव् सिव् [cf. rt. सि], cl. 4. P. सीव्यति (in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 25, 3. वि-सीमहि = विशे-<BR>षेण बध्नीमः is referred by Sāy. either to rt.<BR>सिव् with वि or to rt. सि with वि), सिषेव, सेविष्यति,<BR>असेवीत्, सेवितुम्, to sew, darn, stitch; to stitch toge-<BR>ther, unite, join: Pass. सीव्यते, Aor. असेवि, to be<BR>sewn: Caus. सेवयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असीषिवत्:<BR>Desid. सिसेविषति or सिस्यूषति: Intens. सेषीव्-<BR>यते; [cf. Gr. κασ-σύ-ω (κα-τύ-ω), κάσ-σῦ-μα<BR>(κάτ-τυ-μα), καττύ-ς, probably ὑμήν and Ὑμήν: Lat.<BR>su-o, su-tu-s, su-tor, su-tura, su-tela, su-b-ula,<BR>Con-sus, Con-sualia: Goth. siu-ja, ἐπιῤῤάπτω:<BR>Old Germ. siud, sou-m, ‘a hem;’ sui-la: Mod.<BR>Germ. seam: Angl. Sax. seam: Engl. seam: Old<BR>Norse saumr: Slav. siv-a (Inf. si-ti): Lith. siuv-ù<BR>(Inf. siú-ti), siú-ta-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीवन|सीवनं
सीवन, अम्, n. sewing, stitching; a seam, suture;<BR>(ई), f. a needle; the frenum of the prepuce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीव्यत्
सीव्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sewing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन|सेवनं
सेवन. See under 2. सेवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित्वा
सेवित्वा, ind. having sewn or stitched; having<BR>joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूत|स्यूतः
स्यूत, स्यूति, स्यूत्वा, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिवर|सिवरः
सिवर सिवर, अस्, m. (according to some)<BR>an elephant (= हस्तिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसङ्ग्रामयिषु|सिसंग्रामयिषु
सिसङ्ग्रामयिषु सिसङ्ग्रामयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ<BR>(fr. Desid. of rt. सङ्ग्राम्), wishing or intending to<BR>make war, eager or desirous to fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषा
सिषाधयिषा सिषाधयिषा, f. (fr. Desid.<BR>of Caus. of rt. साध् or rt. 3. सिध्), wish to effect or<BR>accomplish; desire to establish or prove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषु
सिषाधयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous to accomplish<BR>or effect; seeking to prove or demonstrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषासत्
सिषासत् सिषासत्. See rt. 1. सन्, p. 1056.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषासु
सिषासु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desirous of obtaining,<BR>eager for wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिष्णु
सिष्णु सिष्णु, उस्, m. (according to Sāy. fr.<BR>an assumed Vedic rt. सिष् = rt. सिच्; according to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">Page1116-c+ 75</a>]<BR>others fr. rt. सि), Ved. sprinkled (with Soma), receiv-<BR>ing libations, (Sāy. = सोमेनासिच्यमान, Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 19, 31.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिष्मियाण
सिष्मियाण सिष्मियाण, अस्, आ, अम्, (Perf.<BR>part. A. of rt. स्मि), one who has smiled, smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिष्विदान
सिष्विदान सिष्विदान, अस्, आ, अम्, (Perf. part.<BR>A. of rt. स्विद्), Ved. one who has perspired, sweating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षा
सिसृक्षा सिसृक्षा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. 1. सृज्),<BR>wish or purpose to create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षु
सिसृक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing or purposing to<BR>create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिस्रत्
सिस्रत् सिस्रत्. See under rt. सृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिहुण्ड|सिहुंड|सिहुंडः|सिहुण्डः
सिहुण्ड सिहुण्ड, अस्, m. the milk-hedge<BR>plant, Euphorbia Antiquorum (= स्नुही).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्ल|सिह्लः
सिह्ल सिह्ल, अस्, m. (= शिह्ल), olibanum,<BR>benzoin, Indian incense.<BR>—सिह्ल-भूमिका, f. the<BR>olibanum tree, Boswellia Serrata or Thurifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्लक|सिह्लकः
सिह्लक, अस्, m. = सिह्ल; (ई), f. = the olibanum<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीक्
सीक् सीक् (also written शीक्, q. v.), cl. 1.<BR>A. सीकते, &c., to sprinkle, scatter in<BR>drops, (in which sense the form सीक् seems preferable<BR>to शीक्, cf. rts. सिक्, 1. सिच्); to go, move; cl. 1. 10.<BR>P. सीकति, सीकयति, &c., to be impatient; to be<BR>patient; to touch, &c. (see rt. शीक्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीकर|सीकरः
सीकर, अस्, m. drizzling rain, drizzle, mist, &c.;<BR>(see शीकर, but the form सीकर seems preferable.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीक्षत्
सीक्षत् सीक्षत्. See p. 1100, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्
सीत् सीत्, ind. a sound made by drawing<BR>in the breath (to express sighing, shivering with cold,<BR>murmuring, sexual enjoyment, &c.; cf. शीत्).<BR>—सीत्-<BR>कार, अम्, n. making or uttering the above sound<BR>सीत्.<BR>—सीत्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make the<BR>sound सीत्.<BR>—सीत्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made or uttered as<BR>the above sound; (अम्), n. the inarticulate sound सीत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीता
सीता सीता, f. (probably fr. rt. सि, ‘to bind,’<BR>cf. सीमन्, ‘a boundary’), a furrow, the track or<BR>line of a ploughshare [cf. सीर]; agriculture; a<BR>Furrow or Husbandry personified (and apparently<BR>once worshipped as a kind of goddess resembling<BR>Pomona; in Ṛg-veda IV. 57, 6, Sītā is invoked as<BR>a deity presiding over agriculture or the fruits of the<BR>earth, and appears to be associated with Indra, whence<BR>some describe her as a wife of Indra; in Vājasaneyi-s.<BR>XII. 69 — 72, Sītā the Furrow is again personified and<BR>addressed, four furrows being required to be drawn<BR>at the ceremony when these stanzas are recited); N.<BR>of the wife of Rāma-candra (daughter of Janaka,<BR>king of Mithilā, capital of Videha, who was other-<BR>wise called Sīra-dhvaja; she was named Sītā because<BR>fabled to have sprung from a furrow made by Janaka<BR>while ploughing the ground to prepare it for a sacri-<BR>fice instituted by him to obtain progeny, whence<BR>her epithet A-yoni-jā, ‘not womb-born;’ her other<BR>common names, Maithilī and Vaidehī, are from the<BR>place of her birth; according to one legend she was<BR>Veda-vatī, q. v., in the Kṛta age; according to others<BR>she was an incarnation of Lakṣmī and of Umā;<BR>the story of Rāma's bending the bow, which was to be<BR>the condition of the gift of Sītā, is told in Rāmāyaṇa<BR>I. 67; Sītā's younger sister Ūrmilā was at the same<BR>time given to Lakṣmaṇa, and two nieces of Ja-<BR>naka, daughters of his brother king Kuśa-dhvaja, to<BR>Bharata and Śatru-ghna); N. of Lakṣmī; of Durgā<BR>or Umā; of a female poet; of the eastern branch<BR>of the four fabulous branches of the heavenly Ganges<BR>(into which it is supposed to divide after falling on<BR>mount Meru; this branch is fabled to flow into the<BR>Varṣa or Dvīpa, called Bhadrāśva, q. v.); spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>—सीता-द्रव्य, आणि, n. pl. implements of<BR>husbandry.<BR>—सीता-पति or सीतायाः-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘husband of Sītā,’ epithet of the hero Rāma-candra.<BR>—सीता-फल, अस्, m. ‘Sītā's fruit,’ the custard apple<BR>tree, Annona Squamosa; (अम्), n. its fruit.<BR>—सीता-<BR>हरण, अम्, n. the carrying off of Sītā.<BR>—सीताहार<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">Page1117-a+ 76</a>]<BR>(˚ता-आह्˚), अस्, m. ‘Sītā's food,’ a kind of plant,<BR>Lycopodium Phlegmaria.<BR>—सीतोर्मिले (˚ता-ऊर्˚), f.<BR>du. Sītā and Ūrmilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्य|सीत्यं
सीत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, measured out by furrows,<BR>ploughed, tilled [cf. शीत्य]; (अम्), n. rice, corn, grain;<BR>[cf. probably Gr. σῖτος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतीनक|सीतीनकः
सीतीनक सीतीनक, अस्, m. = सतीनक, pease,<BR>pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतीलक|सीतीलकः
सीतीलक = सीतीनक above; [cf. सतीलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्कार|सीत्कारः
सीत्कार सीत्-कार, सीत्-कृत. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीदत्
सीदत् सीदत्, सीदमान. See under rt.<BR>1. सद्, p. 1055, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीद्य|सीद्यं
सीद्य, अम्, n. slothfulness, idleness, indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधु|सीधुः
सीधु सीधु, उस्, m. = शीधु (q. v.), spirit<BR>distilled from molasses, rum (or any similar spirit).<BR>—सीधु-गन्ध, अस्, m. ‘having the smell of<BR>rum,’ the plant or tree Mimusops Elengi (= वकुल).<BR>—सीधु-प, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, drinking spirits.<BR>—सीधु-पुष्प, अस्, m. the Kadamba tree; the<BR>Vakula tree; (ई), f. the Dhātakī plant.<BR>—सीधु-<BR>रस, अस्, m. ‘having spirit-like juice,’ the Mango<BR>tree.<BR>—सीधु-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, m. the Vakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीध्र|सीध्रं
सीध्र सीध्र, अम्, n. (according to some)<BR>the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीप|सीपः
सीप सीप, अस्, m. a sacrificial vessel in the<BR>shape of a boat (for making libations).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीम्
सीम् सीम्, ind., Ved. a particle laying stress<BR>on a preceding word (= इद्); everywhere, on all<BR>sides (= सर्वतस्, Ṛg-veda II. 28, 4, IV. 56, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्
सीमन् सीमन्, आ, f. (according to some also<BR>m., but only f. according to Amara and Vopa-deva<BR>IV. 3; according to others also n. in Ved.; in<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 150. said to be fr. rt. सि; in some<BR>senses perhaps connected with rt. सिव्), a boundary,<BR>border, bound, limit, margin, frontier; a mound or<BR>ridge or anything serving to mark the boundary of<BR>a field, village, &c.; a mark, landmark (in general);<BR>a bank, shore, coast; the horizon; a suture (of the<BR>skull &c.; cf. सीवन); the bounds of morality or<BR>decorum, keeping within bounds, rectitude; a field;<BR>the nape of the neck; the scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमतस्
सीमतस्, Ved. from a boundary or horizon, (ac-<BR>cording to Nirukta I. 7. = सीम्नस् or सीमा-तस्;<BR>according to others an abl. c. fr. a base सीमत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्त|सीमंत|सीमंतः|सीमन्तः
सीमन्त, अस्, m. (for सीमान्त, i. e. सीमन् or<BR>सीमा + अन्त), a boundary-line, (see सीमान्त under<BR>सीमा); a separation or parting of the hair on<BR>each side of the head so as to leave a line; a land-<BR>mark; N. of a son of king Bhadra-sena; of a poet;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. the head (according to some).<BR>—सी-<BR>मन्त-करण, अम्, n. the act or ceremony of part-<BR>ing the hair.<BR>—सीमन्तोन्नयन (˚त-उन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘arranging the parting of the hair,’ N. of one of<BR>the twelve Saṃskāras or purificatory rites, (it is ob-<BR>served by women in the fourth, sixth, or eighth<BR>month of their pregnancy; see under संस्-कार,<BR>p. 1041.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तक|सीमंतक|सीमन्तकं|सीमंतकः|सीमन्तकः
सीमन्तक, अस्, m., N. of a particular kind of<BR>infernal being or inhabitant of hell; (अम्), n. red<BR>lead (with which a mark is sometimes made along<BR>the division of the hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तय
सीमन्तय, Nom. P. सीमन्तयति, &c., to mark<BR>by a line, part (as hair &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तित|सीमंतित
सीमन्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, marked by a line, parted<BR>(as hair &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तिनी|सीमंतिनी
सीमन्तिनी, f. ‘having hair-parting,’ a woman;<BR>N. of a daughter of king Citra-varman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्त्यमान
सीमन्त्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being parted or<BR>divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमा
सीमा, f. a boundary, bound, border, limit, &c.<BR>(= सीमन् above).<BR>—सीमाज्ञान (˚मा-अज्˚), अम्, n.<BR>ignorance of boundaries.<BR>—सीमाधिप (˚मा-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a neighbouring king.<BR>—सीमा-निश्चय, अस्,<BR>m. a legal decision with respect to landmarks and<BR>boundaries.<BR>—सीमान्त (˚मा-अन्˚), अस्, m. a boun-<BR>dary-line, frontier-line, border, boundary.<BR>—सी-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">Page1117-b+ 73</a>]<BR>मान्त-पूजन, अम्, n. the act of honouring a<BR>village boundary, &c.<BR>—सीमा-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. a boun-<BR>dary-mark, landmark.<BR>—सीमा-वाद, अस्, m. a dispute<BR>about boundaries.<BR>—सीमा-विनिर्णय, अस्, m. the<BR>(legal) decision of disputed questions about boun-<BR>daries and landmarks.<BR>—सीमा-विवाद, अस्, m. liti-<BR>gation about boundaries.<BR>—सीमा-विवाद-धर्म,<BR>अस्, m. the law respecting disputes about boundaries.<BR>—सीमा-वृक्ष, अस्, m. ‘boundary-tree,’ a tree<BR>serving as a boundary-mark.<BR>—सीमा-सन्धि, इस्, m.<BR>‘boundary-junction,’ the meeting of two boundaries.<BR>—सीमा-सेतु-विनिर्णय, अस्, m. (legal) decision<BR>about boundaries and barriers.<BR>—सीमोल्लङ्घन<BR>(˚मा-उल्˚), अम्, n. the leaping over or transgressing<BR>boundaries, passing a frontier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमिक|सीमिकः
सीमिक सीमिक, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. II. 43.<BR>said to be fr. rt. स्यम्), a kind of tree; an ant-hill<BR>(= स्यमीक); an ant or similar small insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमीक
सीमीक, अस्, m. a kind of tree; [cf. सीमिक above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीर|सीरः
सीर सीर, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. II. 25. said<BR>to be fr. rt. सि; cf. सीता), a plough; the sun; N. of<BR>a Vedic god, (see शुना-सीरौ); the Arka plant;<BR>(अम्), n., Ved. a plough.<BR>—सीर-देव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a grammarian.<BR>—सीर-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘plough-<BR>bannered,’ N. of Janaka (father of Sītā, q. v.).<BR>—सीर-<BR>पाणि, इस्, m. ‘plough-handed,’ epithet of Bala-rāma<BR>(as armed with a weapon like a plough-share).<BR>—सीर-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. ‘plough-bearer,’ Bala-rāma; [cf. हल-<BR>भृत्.]<BR>—सीर-योग, अस्, m. the yoking of cattle to<BR>a plough or a team so yoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरक|सीरकः
सीरक, अस्, m. a plough; the sun; a porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरा
सीरा, आस्, f. pl., Ved. streams, waters, rivers, (Sāy.<BR>= नदीः, Ṛg-veda I. 174, 9; in Naigh. I. 13. enu-<BR>merated among the नदी-नामानि; cf. सिरा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरिन्
सीरिन्, ई, m. ‘having or holding a plough,’ epithet<BR>of Bala-rāma, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरज
सीरज सीरज, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीलन्ध|सीलंध|सीलन्धः
सीलन्ध सीलन्ध, अस्, m. a kind of fish<BR>(commonly called Silindā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीलमा
सीलमा सीलमा, f., Ved. (probably) a plant.<BR>—सीलमा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having plants,<BR>abounding in plants (said of the river Sindhu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीवन|सीवनं
सीवन सीवन. See p. 1116, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीषत्
सीषत् सीषत्, अन्, अती, अत् (probably fr. rt.<BR>1. सन्), Ved. giving, granting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीस|सीसं
सीस सीस, अम्, n. (etymology doubtful),<BR>lead.<BR>—सीस-पत्त्र or सीस-पत्त्रक, अम्, n. lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसक
सिसक, अम्, n. lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीसताण
सीसताण सीसताण, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीसर
सीसर सीसर, अस्, m., N. of the husband<BR>of Saramā (according to one legend).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीहुण्ड|सीहुंड|सीहुंडः|सीहुण्डः
सीहुण्ड सीहुण्ड, अस्, m. = सेहुण्ड, the milk-<BR>hedge plant, Euphorbia Antiquorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु 1. सु, cl. 1. P. A. सवति, सवते, &c.,<BR>to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु 2. सु, cl. 1. 2. P. सवति, सौति, सुषाव,<BR>&c., to possess power or supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु 3. सु, cl. 5. P. A. सुनोति (1st du. सु-<BR>नुवस् or सुन्वस्, 1st pl. सुनुमस् or सुन्-<BR>मस्), सुनुते, सुषाव, सुषुवे, सोष्यति, -ते,<BR>असावीत् or असौषीत्, असोष्ट or असविष्ट, सोतुम्<BR>(Ved. Inf. सोतवे), to pour out, sprinkle, make a<BR>libation (especially of the Soma juice); to press out<BR>juice (especially from the Soma plant), to extract<BR>or prepare the Soma juice or any other juice, to<BR>distil (wine, spirits, &c.); to churn; to perform a<BR>sacrifice (especially with the Soma); to bathe [cf.<BR>1. सवन, सूत्या]: Pass. सूयते, Aor. असावि (Ved.<BR>Pass. 3rd sing. सुन्वे, 3rd pl. सुन्विरे = सुता ब-<BR>भूवुः): Caus. सावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असूष-<BR>वत् (according to some असीषवत्): Desid. of Caus.<BR>सुषावयिषति: Desid. सुसूषति: Intens. सोषू-<BR>यते; [cf. Gr. ὕ-ω, ὑ-ε-τό-ς; Umbr. savitu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्
1. सुत्, त्, त्, त्, extracting juice, pouring out, sprinkling,<BR>making libations, (see प्र-सुत्, मधु-षुत्); (त्),<BR>m. = स्तोतृ, (Naigh. III. 16.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत|सुतः
1. सुत, अस्, आ, अम्, poured out; extracted or<BR>expressed (as Soma juice); (अस्, अम्), m. n., Ved.<BR>the expressed Soma juice, a Soma libation, (in Naigh.<BR>II. 7. enumerated among the अन्न-नामानि.)<BR> — 1. सुत-प, अस्, m. (for 2. सु-तप see p. 1120,<BR>col. 1), a drinker of the Soma juice; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a class of deities.<BR>—सुत-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>a drinker of libations, (Sāy. = हुत-शिष्ट-सोम-<BR>पीत-यजमान, Ṛg-veda I. 155, 2); drinking the<BR>effused Soma juice (said of Indra).<BR>—सुत-पावन्, आ,<BR>अरी, अ, Ved. drinking the effused Soma juice.<BR>—सु-<BR>तम्-भर, अस्, m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi.<BR>—१. सुत-<BR>वत्, आन्, m. possessed of Soma juice, a drinker of<BR>Soma juice; an offerer of a libation.<BR>—सुत-सोम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. possessing effused Soma, (Sāy. =<BR>अभिषुतेन सोमेनोपेतः, Ṛg-veda I. 2, 2.)<BR>—सुता-वत्, Ved. = 1. सुत-वत् above.<BR>—सुते-कर,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. (Sāy.) one who makes a Soma libation.<BR>—सुते-गृभ्, प्, प्, प्, or सुते-गृभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. received at the effusion (said of Soma; Sāy. =<BR>अभिषुतेन रसेन गृहीतः, Ṛg-veda V. 44, 5).<BR>—सुते-मनस्, आस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुति|सुतिः
सुति, इस्, f. extracting or pouring out the Soma<BR>juice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्या
1. सुत्या, f. Soma pressing, Soma preparation [cf.<BR>अद्य-स्˚, श्वः-स्˚]; sacrificial ablution, (see सूत्या<BR>below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्वन्
सुत्वन्, आ, m. an offerer of Soma juice; a drinker<BR>of Soma; a student who has performed his ablutions<BR>(subsequent or preparatory to a sacrifice); a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्वत्|सुन्वन्त्
सुन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, pouring out libations, offering<BR>sacrifice, sacrificing; (अन्), m. an offerer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्वान
सुन्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. offering libations;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of Su-mantu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुवाण
सुषुवाण, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has poured out<BR>libations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्वयत्
सुष्वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (according to some<BR>fr. a Nominal base सुष्वय, to which सुष्व-<BR>यन्त, Ṛg-veda VII. 36, 6, may possibly also be<BR>referred; but according to Sāy. derived fr. rt. अय्<BR>with a reduplicated form of सु prefixed), Ved. pour-<BR>ing out libations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्वाण
सुष्वाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pouring out libations,<BR>being poured forth, (Sāy. सुष्वाणेभिस् = सुन्वद्-<BR>भिर् यजमानैः, Ṛg-veda IV. 29, 2; = सूय-<BR>मान, IX. 101, 11; सुष्वाणः = यजमानेभ्यः<BR>कामान् प्रेरयन्, as if fr. rt. 1. सू, Ṛg-veda IX.<BR>6, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्वि
सुष्वि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. pouring out libations, offer-<BR>ing sacrifices, (Sāy. सुष्विम् = सोमानाम् अभिषो-<BR>तारम्, Ṛg-veda I. 61, 15; सुष्वये = सोमं<BR>सुन्वते, Ṛg-veda IV. 25, 7.)<BR>—सुष्वि-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. making more libations, one who offers<BR>frequent sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्वान
सुस्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, = सुष्वाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूति|सूतिः
1. सूति, इस्, f. (for 2. see p. 1118, col. 1), a place<BR>where Soma juice is poured out or extracted (=<BR>सोमाभिषव-भूमि, according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्या
सूत्या, f. drinking the Soma juice at a sacrifice;<BR>religious bathing, ablution preparatory or subsequent<BR>to a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूम|सूमं|सूमः
सूम, अस्, m. milk; water; sky, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोतव्य
सोतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be poured out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोतृ
1. सोतृ, ता, त्री, तृ (for 2. see p. 1118, col. 2),<BR>Ved. one who presses out the Soma plant, one who<BR>pours out libations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्व
सोत्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = सोतव्य, to be poured<BR>out or offered, (Sāy. अभिषोतव्य, Ṛg-veda X.<BR>160, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोम|सोमं|सोमः
सोम. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु 4. सु (= rt. 3. सू, p. 1130, but by<BR>some identified with rt. 3. सु, col. 2, the<BR>act of pouring out the Soma juice being compared<BR>to that of generation); cl. 1. 2. P. सवति, सौति,<BR>सुषाव, सोष्यति, असौषीत् or (according to some)<BR>असावीत्, cl. 2. A. सूते (1st sing. सुवे), Impf. असूत<BR>(1st sing. असुवि, 1st du. असूवहि), Pot. सुवीत,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">Page1118-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Impv. सूताम् (1st sing. सुवै, 1st du. सुवावहै,<BR>1st pl. सुवामहै), cl. 4. A. सूयते, सुषुवे,<BR>सोष्यते or सविष्यते, असोष्ट or असविष्ट, (in<BR>Atharva-veda XIV. 1, 33. the form सुवाति occurs,<BR>which might also be referred to rt. 1. सू), Inf. सोतुम्,<BR>सवितुम्, to beget, procreate, engender, generate; to<BR>bring forth a child, give birth to, bear, produce, yield;<BR>to confer, bestow (Ved.); to gain, acquire (Ved.); to ac-<BR>cept, (Sāy. साविषत् = अनुजानातु, Ṛg-veda I. 164,<BR>26): Pass. सूयते, Aor. असावि, to be begotten; to be<BR>brought forth: Caus. सावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असू-<BR>षवत्, (according to some असीषवत्): Desid. of<BR>Caus. सुषावयिषति: Desid. सुसूषति, -ते: In-<BR>tens. सोषूयते, सोषवीति, सोषोति; [cf. Zend<BR>hunu, ‘a son;’ Gr. υἱός, ὑατέρα = Lat. uterus; Goth.<BR>su-nu-s; Slav. sy-nu; Lith. su-nu-s, ‘a son.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्
2. सुत्, त्, त्, त्, begetting, generating, engendering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत|सुतः
2. सुत, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see p. 1117), begotten,<BR>brought forth; (अस्), m. a son; a child, offspring;<BR>a king; N. of the fifth sign or astrological house;<BR>(आ), f. a daughter; the plant Dur-ālabhā, q. v.<BR>—सु-<BR>तङ्-गम, अस्, m. ‘son-obtaining,’ the father of a<BR>son.<BR>—सुत-जीवक, अस्, m. a kind of tree (= पु-<BR>त्र-जीव).<BR>—सुत-निर्विशेषम्, ind. exactly as a<BR>child, not differently from a son.<BR>—सुत-पादिका, f.<BR>a particular plant (= हंस-पदी).<BR>—२. सुत-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत् (for 1. see p. 1117), having children;<BR>(आन्), m. the father of a son.<BR>—सुत-वस्करा, f. the<BR>mother of seven children.<BR>—सुत-श्रेणी, f. the plant<BR>Salvinia Cucullata.<BR>—सुत-स्नेह, अस्, m. ‘love for a<BR>son,’ paternal affection.<BR>—सुत-हिबुक-योग, अस्, m.<BR>junction of the fifth and fourth signs or astrological<BR>houses (said to be suitable for marriages).<BR>—सुतात्म-<BR>ज (˚त-आत्˚ or ˚ता-आत्˚), अस्, m. a grandson (either a<BR>son's son or a daughter's son); (आ), f. a grand-<BR>daughter (either a son's daughter or a daughter's<BR>daughter).<BR>—सुतार्थिन् (˚त-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, desirous<BR>of offspring.<BR>—सुतोत्पत्ति (˚त-उत्˚), इस्, f. birth of<BR>a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिन्
सुतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having or possessing a child, hav-<BR>ing children; (ई), m. a father; (इनी), f. a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुती
सुती, ईस्, m. f. (abl. gen. sing. सुत्युस्), one who<BR>wishes for a son; one who treats like a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतीय
सुतीय, Nom. P. सुतीयति, &c., to desire a son;<BR>to treat like a son (e. g. सुतीयति शिष्यम्, he treats<BR>the pupil like a son); to wish for a daughter, (in this<BR>case for सुता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्या
2. सुत्या, f. bringing forth a child, parturition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
सू, ऊस्, f. child-bearing, &c. See 4. सू, p. 1130,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत|सूतः
1. सूत, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see p. 1130, col. 2), born,<BR>engendered, produced; the sun [cf. सूर]; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. quicksilver, mercury; (आ), f. a woman who has<BR>given birth to a child or one recently delivered.<BR>—सूत-महोदधि, N. of a work on medicine.<BR>—सूत-राज्, ट्, m. quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतक|सूतकं|सूतकः
सूतक, अम्, n. birth, production; impurity from<BR>child-birth or miscarriage; (अस्, अम्), m. n. quick-<BR>silver, mercury; (अका), f. a woman recently de-<BR>livered; [cf. सूतिका below.]<BR>—सूतका-गृह, अम्,<BR>n. a part of a house appropriated to a woman in<BR>child-birth; a lying-in chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूति|सूतिः
2. सूति, इस्, f. (for 1. see p. 1117, col. 3; for 3. see<BR>p. 1131), birth, production, delivery, child-bearing,<BR>parturition, bringing forth; offspring, progeny.<BR>—सूति-<BR>गृह, अम्, n. the lying-in chamber, (also written<BR>सूती-गृह.)<BR>—सूति-मास or सूती-मास, अस्, m. the<BR>month of delivery, the last month of gestation or<BR>pregnancy (= वैजनन).<BR>—सूत्य्-आशौच, अम्, n.<BR>impurity caused by child-birth (continuing for ten<BR>days in the case of regular parturition, and in the<BR>case of a miscarriage for a period of days equal to<BR>the number of months elapsed since conception).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिका
सूतिका, f. a woman who has recently given birth<BR>to a child, a lying-in woman.<BR>—सूतिकागार (˚का-<BR>आग्˚) or सूतिका-गृह or सूतिका-गेह or सूतिका-<BR>भवन, अम्, n. or सूतिकावास (˚का-आव्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a room or part of a house appropriated to a woman<BR>at child-birth, a lying-in chamber.<BR>—सूतिका-रोग,<BR>अस्, m. puerperal sickness, fever or sickness of any<BR>kind supervening on child-birth.<BR>—सूतिका-षष्ठी,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-b" target="_blank">Page1118-b+ 80</a>]<BR>f. a particular goddess worshipped on the sixth day<BR>after child-birth.<BR>—सूतिकाषष्ठी-पूजा, f. the wor-<BR>ship of the above goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून|सूनं|सूनः
सून, अस्, आ, अम्, born, produced; blown, blos-<BR>somed, budded (as a flower); empty, vacant, (in this<BR>sense probably for शून and शून्य); (आ), f. a<BR>daughter, (for सूना, a slaughter-house, &c., see s. v.);<BR>(अम्), n. bringing forth, parturition; a bud, blossom,<BR>flower; [cf. प्र-सून.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनवत्
सूनवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has borne or pro-<BR>duced; having budded or blossomed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनु|सूनुः
सूनु, उस्, m. a son; a child, offspring; a daughter's<BR>son; a younger brother; the sun; N. of the author<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 176 (having the patro-<BR>nymic Ārbhava); (उस्, ऊस्), f. a daughter; [cf. Zend<BR>hunu; Gr. υἱός; Goth. sunus, ‘a son;’ Angl. Sax.<BR>sunu; Mod. Germ. sohn, &c.; see col. 1.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूवन्
सूवन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. bearing children, generat-<BR>ing, producing; [cf. बहु-सूवरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोतृ
2. सोतृ, ता, त्री, तृ (for 1. see p. 1117, col. 3),<BR>engendering, generating, bringing forth children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु 5. सु, ind. (thought by some to be a<BR>shortened form of वसु, q. v.; opposed to<BR>दुस्, q. v., and corresponding to Gr. εὖ; in the Veda<BR>liable to become षु, see Ṛg-veda I. 36, 13, I. 112,<BR>1, Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 107; and to lengthen a preceding<BR>vowel, see Pāṇ. VI. 3, 134; also becoming सू in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 10, 11, &c.; cf. सुकम्), an enhancing<BR>particle frequently used as a prefix implying ‘good,<BR>well, excellent, excellently, beautiful, beautifully,<BR>honourable, worthy of respect or reverence, excessive,<BR>excessively, exceedingly, much, very; readily, easily,<BR>willingly, quickly’ (Ved., Sāy. = सुष्ठु, and in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 112, 1, &c. used separately to qualify a<BR>verb); according to native authorities this prefix may<BR>also imply अनु-मति, ‘assent;’ सम्-ऋद्धि, ‘pros-<BR>perity;’ कृच्छ्र, ‘distress;’ [cf. Gr. εὖ: Cambro-<BR>Brit. hu, hy, he: Armor. he: Hib. so, soailce, ‘a<BR>good fashion, good manners;’ sucridh, ‘easy,’ = सु-<BR>कृत.]<BR>—सु-ऊति, इस्, f., Ved. good protection, kind<BR>assistance or favour.<BR>—सु-कक्ष, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the hymn Ṛg-veda VIII. 81, 82 (having<BR>the patronymic Āṅgirasa).<BR>—सु-कण्टका, f. ‘hav-<BR>ing good thorns,’ the Aloe plant, Aloe Indica.<BR>—सु-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a musician.<BR>—सु-कण्डु, उस्,<BR>m. ‘much-scratching,’ the itch.<BR>—सु-कन्द, अस्, m.<BR>‘having a good bulb,’ an onion; a yam; the esculent<BR>root Arum Campanulatum; a sort of grass, Scirpus<BR>Kysoor; other bulbous plants (= वाराही-कन्द; =<BR>धरणी-कन्द).<BR>—सु-कन्दक, अस्, m. an onion.<BR>—सु-कन्दिन्, ई, m. Arum Campanulatum.<BR>—सु-<BR>कन्यक or सु-कन्याक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>beautiful maiden, (Vopa-deva VII. 23.)<BR>—सु-कन्या,<BR>f. a beautiful girl; N. of a daughter of Śaryāti (and<BR>wife of the Ṛṣi Cyavana).<BR>—सु-कपर्द, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having beautiful braided hair.<BR>—सु-कर, अस्, आ,<BR>or ई, अम्, easy to be done, practicable, feasible,<BR>attainable; easy to be managed, doing well; (आ), f.<BR>a tractable cow; (अम्), n. doing good, charity, be-<BR>nevolence.<BR>—सुकर-सन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, easily joined<BR>or united.<BR>—सु-कर्णक, अस्, इका, अम्, having<BR>beautiful ears; (अस्), m. a particular tree, = हस्ति-<BR>कन्द; (इका), f. the plant Salvinia Cucullata.<BR>—सु-<BR>कर्णी, f. the colocynth.<BR>—सु-कर्म, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a class of deities.<BR>—सु-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, one<BR>whose deeds are righteous or virtuous, performing<BR>good works; doing what is right, acting virtuously,<BR>virtuous, good; active, diligent; (आ), m. epithet of<BR>Viśva-karman (the artist or architect of the gods);<BR>the seventh of the twenty-seven astronomical Yogas,<BR>(see योग); N. of a teacher of the Sāma-veda;<BR>(आणस्), m. pl., N. of a class of deities.<BR>—सु-कल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, (said to be fr. rt. 1. कल्, to sound forth),<BR>one who has a great reputation for liberality both<BR>in giving and using.<BR>—सु-कवि, इस्, m. a good or<BR>excellent poet.<BR>—सुकवि-ता, f. the state of a good<BR>poet, excellent poetical talent.<BR>—सु-काण्ड, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a good stem or stalk; well-jointed;<BR>(अस्), m. the Kāravella plant.<BR>—सु-काण्डिका, f. the<BR>Kāṇḍīra creeper.<BR>—सु-काण्डिन्, having good stems<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-c" target="_blank">Page1118-c+ 81</a>]<BR>or stalks; beautifully jointed; (ई), m. a bee.<BR>—सु-<BR>कान्ति, इस्, m., N. of a son of Pulaha.<BR>—सु-काम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having good desires; (आ), f. the Trāya-<BR>māṇā plant.<BR>—सु-कालिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a class<BR>of Pitṛs (regarded as the sons of Vasiṣṭha and<BR>the especial Pitṛs of Śūdras).<BR>—सु-कालुका, f. the<BR>Ḍoḍī shrub.<BR>—सु-काष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having good<BR>wood; (आ), f. the Kaṭvī plant, the Kāṣṭha-kadalī,<BR>q. v.<BR>—सु-काष्ठक, अस्, आ, अम्, having good<BR>wood; (अम्), n. the Deva-dāru pine.<BR>—सु-किं-<BR>शुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having beautiful Kiṃśuka<BR>wood (said of a carriage either from being made of<BR>this wood or from resembling in colour the flowers<BR>of the Kiṃśuka tree, Ṛg-veda X. 85, 20; perhaps<BR>to be translated ‘bright-coloured’).<BR>—सु-कीर्त्ति, इस्,<BR>f. good report, celebration; epithet of a particular<BR>hymn; (इस्), m., N. of the author of Ṛg-veda X.<BR>131 (having the patronymic Kākṣīvata).<BR>—सु-कुच,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, handsome-breasted, having beautiful breasts.<BR>—सु-कुन्दक, अस्, m. an onion; [cf. सु-कन्दक.]<BR>—सु-कुन्दन, अस्, m. the Varvara plant.<BR>—सु-<BR>कुमार, अस्, m. a beautiful youth; (अस्, आ or ई, अम्),<BR>beautifully young or youthful, very soft or tender,<BR>delicate, smooth; (अस्), m. a variety of the sugar-<BR>cane (= पुण्ड्र); the Śyāmāka grain; a sort of<BR>mustard (= क्षव); the wild Campaka; N. of a<BR>Daitya; of the father of Satya-ketu; (आ), f. double<BR>jasmine; great-flowered jasmine; the plantain; another<BR>plant (= पृक्का); N. of a river; (ई), f. the Nava-<BR>mālikā jasmine.<BR>—सु-कुमारक, अस्, m. a beautiful<BR>youth; rice, = शालि; (अम्), n. the Tamāla-pattra,<BR>q. v.<BR>—सुकुमार-तनु-त्वच्, क्, क्, क्, having very<BR>soft and delicate skin.<BR>—सुकुमार-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, much more delicate.<BR>—सुकुमार-नख-त्वच्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, having very delicate nails and skin.<BR>—सुकु-<BR>माराङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having very soft<BR>limbs.<BR>—सु-कुरीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a beau-<BR>tiful head-dress.<BR>—सु-कुल, अम्, n. a good or virtuous<BR>family; (अस्, आ, अम्), of good family; well-born.<BR>—सु-कुल-स्त्री, ईस्, f. a woman of good family, a<BR>respectable woman.<BR>—सु-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, doing good,<BR>benevolent; virtuous, pious; wise, learned; fortunate,<BR>well-fated; performing splendid sacrifices, making<BR>good offerings; (त्), m. a skilful worker, epithet of<BR>Tvaṣṭṛ.<BR>—सु-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done well or pro-<BR>perly; well made, well constructed; treated with<BR>kindness, befriended, assisted; virtuous, pious; for-<BR>tunate, auspicious; (अम्), n. any good or virtuous<BR>act, kindness, bounty, friendliness, aid; virtue, moral<BR>merit; fortune, auspiciousness; reward, recompense.<BR>—सुकृतावास (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, constituting a<BR>well-made residence, well provided with accommoda-<BR>tion.<BR>—सु-कृति, इस्, f. well-doing; acting in a friendly<BR>or kind manner, kindness; virtue; the practice of<BR>religious austerities; (इस्), m., N. of a son of Pṛthu.<BR>—सु-कृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, acting well or kindly; vir-<BR>tuous, pious, good; benevolent; wise, learned;<BR>fortunate, lucky.<BR>—सुकृतोच्छ्रय (˚त-उच्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made very high, very lofty.<BR>—सुकृतोदीरण<BR>(˚त-उद्˚), अम्, n. the proclaiming or blazoning<BR>abroad of good actions.<BR>—सुकृत्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. more beneficent.<BR>—सु-कृत्या, f., Ved. good<BR>sacrificing, a splendid sacrificial offering.<BR>—सु-केतु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of a son of Nandi-vardhana; of a son<BR>of Su-nītha.<BR>—सु-केश, अस्, आ, or ई (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 54),<BR>अम्, having beautiful hair; (अस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Vidyut-keśa; (ई), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—सु-केशन्,<BR>m. (apparently) a proper N. (in conjunction with<BR>Bhāradvāja).<BR>—सु-केशर or सु-केसर, अस्, m. the<BR>citron; (अम्), n. a kind of metre.<BR>—सुकेशान्त<BR>(˚श-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having beautiful locks of hair<BR>or ringlets.<BR>—सु-केशि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Vidyut-<BR>keśin.<BR>—सु-केशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, = सु-केश; (ई), m. =<BR>सु-केशि.<BR>—सु-कोली, f. a medicinal root (= क्षीर-<BR>काकोली).<BR>—सु-कोशक, अस्, m. the Kośāmra plant.<BR>—सु-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. well-sacrificing, doing<BR>good acts or very wise, (Sāy. = शोभन-कर्मन् or<BR>शोभन-प्रज्ञ); (उस्), m. an epithet of Agni;<BR>of Mitra and Varuṇa; of Savitṛ; of Soma; of<BR>Indra.<BR>—सुक्रतूयया, ind. from a desire to sacrifice<BR>well or to do good, (Sāy. शोभन-कर्मेच्छया,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1119-a" target="_blank">Page1119-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 160, 4.)<BR>—सु-क्रिया, f. a good action,<BR>good work, moral or religious observance.<BR>—सु-<BR>क्रुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, very angry.<BR>—सु-क्षत्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a good dominion, mighty,<BR>strong, powerful; (अस्), m., N. of a king.<BR>—सु-<BR>क्षय, अस्, m. a beautiful house, (Sāy. = शोभन<BR>यज्ञ-गृह, Ṛg-veda X. 23, 4.)<BR>—सु-क्षिति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. having good dwellings, granting good<BR>dwellings.<BR>—सु-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. an excellent field.<BR>—सु-क्षेत्रिया, ind., Ved. desire for good fields or<BR>with such desire, (Sāy. = सुक्षेत्रेच्छा, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 97, 2; cf. सु-गातुया.)<BR>—सु-क्षेमन्, अ, n.,<BR>Ved. water, (in Naigh. I. 12. enumerated among<BR>the उदक-नामानि.)<BR>—सु-ख, &c., see सुख,<BR>s. v.<BR>—सु-खादि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. wearing beautiful<BR>rings (said of the Maruts; cf. खादि-हस्त).<BR>—सु-<BR>ख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, very renowned, celebrated,<BR>famous.<BR>—सु-ख्याति, इस्, f. good report, fame, cele-<BR>brity.<BR>—सु-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going well or gracefully,<BR>graceful, elegant; easy of access, easily passed, (op-<BR>posed to दुर्-ग); easily understood, intelligible;<BR>(अम्), n. happiness; feces, ordure.<BR>—सु-गण्, ण्, ण्,<BR>ण्, counting well or easily, a ready reckoner; easily<BR>calculated.<BR>—सु-गणित, अस्, आ, अम्, easily or accu-<BR>rately calculated.<BR>—सु-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, well-gone,<BR>going well, passed, gone; well-bestowed; (अस्), m.<BR>the Buddha or a particular Buddha.<BR>—सु-गति, इस्, m.<BR>a good or happy condition; N. of an Arhat.<BR>—सु-<BR>गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, sweet-smelling, odoriferous,<BR>fragrant; (अस्), m. fragrance, odour, perfume; sul-<BR>phur; the red Śigru tree; = चणक; = भू-तृन;<BR>a trader, dealer; (आ), f. the ichneumon plant (=<BR>रास्ना); zedoary, Curcuma Zerumbet; a fragrant<BR>grass; a sort of lime; sacred basil; various plants<BR>and trees (including several kinds of jasmine, =<BR>बन्ध्या-कर्कोटकी; = रुद्र-जटा; = शत-पुष्-<BR>पा; = नाकुली; नव-मालिका; स्वर्ण-यूथिका;<BR>पृक्का; गङ्गा-पत्त्री; सल्लकी; माधवी;<BR>अनन्ता; मातुलुङ्गा); N. of a goddess; of an<BR>Apsaras; (अम्), n. small cumin seed; a fragrant<BR>grass (= कत्-तृण, p. 199); the blue lotus; sandal;<BR>the Granthi-parṇa plant.<BR>—सुगन्धक, अस्, m. the<BR>red Tulasī; sulphur; the orange; a sort of gourd,<BR>Momordica Mixta.<BR>—सुगन्ध-ता, f. fragrance,<BR>perfume.<BR>—सुगन्ध-तैल-निर्यास, अम्, n. a par-<BR>ticular perfume made with roses, &c.<BR>—सुगन्ध-<BR>पत्त्रा, f. the plant Rudra-jaṭā.<BR>—सुगन्ध-भू-<BR>तृण, अम्, n. a kind of fragrant grass.<BR>—सुगन्ध-<BR>मूला, f. ‘having a fragrant root,’ the ichneumon<BR>plant (= स्थल-पद्मिनी).<BR>—सुगन्धादित्य (˚ध-<BR>आद्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—सुगन्धामलक<BR>(˚ध-आम्˚), अम्, n. a kind of mixture of various<BR>herbs.<BR>—सु-गन्धार, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-गन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, very sweet-smelling or<BR>fragrant, redolent with perfumes; virtuous, pious;<BR>(इस्), m. a perfume, fragrance; the supreme Being<BR>(= परमात्मन्); a sort of sweet-smelling Mango;<BR>(इ), n. a drug and perfume (= एलबालुक); the<BR>root of long pepper; a kind of fragrant grass (both<BR>Cyperus Rotundus and Scirpus Kysoor); coriander<BR>seed (= गन्ध-तृण; = पिप्पली-मूल).<BR>—सु-<BR>गन्धिक, अस्, m. ‘having a sweet or strong smell,’<BR>incense; sulphur; a sort of large rice; (अम्), n. the<BR>white lotus (= पुष्कर-मूल; = गौर-सुवर्ण;<BR>= उशीर).<BR>—सुगन्धि-कुसुम, अम्, n. a fragrant<BR>flower; (अस्), m. a sort of yellow oleander; (आ), f.<BR>the plant Trigonella Corniculata.<BR>—सुगन्धि-ता,<BR>f. fragrance, agreeable scent, perfume.<BR>—सुगन्धि-<BR>तेजन, Ved. a kind of fragrant grass.<BR>—सुगन्धि-<BR>त्रिफला, f. nutmeg; areca nut; cloves.<BR>—सु-गन्-<BR>धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, very fragrant or sweet-smelling;<BR>(इनी), f. the fragrant plant Ārāma-śītalā.<BR>—सुगन्-<BR>धि-मूल, अम्, n. the root of Uśīra; (आ), f. the<BR>ichneumon plant.<BR>—सुगन्धि-मूषिका, f. the musk<BR>rat or shrew.<BR>—सुगन्धेश (˚धा-ईश), अस्, m. a<BR>statue of the tutelary deity of Su-gandhā.<BR>—सु-गन्-<BR>मन्, see Vopa-deva XXVI. 68.<BR>—सु-गभस्ति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. beautiful-handed, skilful-handed (said of<BR>Tvaṣṭṛ).<BR>—सु-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be tra-<BR>versed or travelled over, easy of access or approach,<BR>accessible; easy, practicable; plain, intelligible; [cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1119-b" target="_blank">Page1119-b+ 81</a>]<BR>दुर्-गम.]<BR>—सु-गम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = सु-गम,<BR>col. 1.<BR>—सु-गव or सु-गव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having fine cows, abounding in cattle.<BR>—सु-गहन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very thick or close, very impervious;<BR>(आ), f. an enclosure round a place of sacrifice to<BR>exclude profane access (= कुम्बा).<BR>—सुगहना-<BR>वृति (˚न-आव्˚), इस्, f. a sacred enclosure, (see above.)<BR>—सु-गातुया, ind., Ved. with a desire for good<BR>roads, (Sāy. = शोभन-मार्गेच्छया, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>97, 2.)<BR>—सु-गात्र, अम्, n. a fine figure, graceful<BR>person; (अस्, आ, अम्), handsome-limbed, having a<BR>good figure, graceful.<BR>—सु-गाध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>easily fordable.<BR>—सु-गीति, इस्, f. good singing; a kind<BR>of metre.<BR>—सु-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. = सु-गव above.<BR>—सु-गुणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, very rich in virtues, very<BR>virtuous or excellent.<BR>—सु-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>hidden or concealed, very secret; (अम्), ind. very<BR>secretly, privily.<BR>—सुगुप्त-लेख, अस्, m. a very<BR>private letter or one written in cipher.<BR>—सु-गुप्ति,<BR>इस्, f. good protection, secrecy.<BR>—सुगुप्ती-कृ, cl. 8. P.<BR>-करोति, -कर्तुम्, to guard well.<BR>—सु-गुल्फ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having beautiful ancles, (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 54.)<BR>—सु-<BR>गूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, well concealed, very secret.<BR>—सु-गृह, अस्, ई, अम्, having a beautiful abode;<BR>(अस्), m. the taylor-bird, Sylvia Sutoria.<BR>—सु-गृहीत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, held fast or firmly, seized, grasped; taken<BR>or applied properly or auspiciously.<BR>—सुगृहीत-ना-<BR>मन्, आ, m. ‘one whose name is invoked auspiciously,’<BR>epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira and of others who are in-<BR>voked early in the morning to secure good luck.<BR>—सुगृहीताभिध (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>an auspicious name.<BR>—सु-गोपा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing good protectors, well protected.<BR>—सुगोपा-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the best guardians, protected<BR>most effectually.<BR>—सु-ग्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. easy to<BR>be obtained or acquired, (Sāy. = सुष्ठु गन्तव्य);<BR>yielding happiness, (in Naigh. III. 6. सुग्म्यम्<BR>is enumerated among the सुख-नामानि.)<BR>—सु-<BR>ग्रथित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well fastened.<BR>—सु-ग्रन्-<BR>थि, इस्, इस्, इ, well knotted; having beautiful joints;<BR>(इस्), m. a kind of plant (= चोरक).<BR>—सु-ग्रास,<BR>अस्, m. a dainty morsel, tidbit, bonne bouche.<BR>—सु-<BR>ग्राह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be taken, easily appre-<BR>hensible, easy to be laid hold of, &c.<BR>—सु-ग्रीव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, handsome-necked, having a beautiful neck;<BR>(अस्), m. a swan or Rāja-haṃsa; a hero; a sort of<BR>weapon; N. of a monkey-king (who, with his<BR>army of monkeys headed by Hanumat, assisted<BR>Rāma-candra in conquering Rāvaṇa and recovering<BR>Sītā; he was fabled to be son of the Sun, and was<BR>re-established by Rāma in the throne of Kiṣkindhya,<BR>which had been usurped by his brother Bāli or Bālin,<BR>see किष्किन्ध्य); N. of one of the four horses of<BR>Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu [cf. मेघ-पुष्प, वलाहक,<BR>शैव्य]; N. of Śiva; of Indra; of a particular moun-<BR>tain; of a particular Nāga or serpent of Pātāla; of<BR>the father of the ninth Jina or Arhat of the present<BR>age; of an Asura or demon; the countenance of a<BR>friend (?); a piece of water (?); (ई), f., N. of a<BR>daughter or (according to others) wife of Kaśyapa<BR>(regarded as the parent of horses, camels, and asses;<BR>she is usually held to be the daughter of Kaśyapa<BR>and Tāmrā).<BR>—सुग्रीवेश (˚व-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the monkey-king Su-grīva,’ Rāma.<BR>—सु-ग्ल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, (rt. ग्लै), very weary.<BR>—सु-घटित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well joined or united, well contrived or devised,<BR>well arranged or managed.<BR>—सु-घोर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very fearful or terrible, terrific, hideous.<BR>—सु-घोष,<BR>अस्, m. a pleasant sound or cry.<BR>—सुघोष-ग्राम,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—सु-चक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having beautiful wheels.<BR>—सु-चक्षुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्,<BR>having good eyes, seeing well; (उस्), m. a dis-<BR>cerning or wise man, a learned man; the glo-<BR>merous fig-tree.<BR>—सु-चञ्चुका, f. a kind of vege-<BR>table (= महा-चञ्चु).<BR>—सु-चतुर, अस्, आ, अम्, see<BR>Vopa-deva VI. 29.<BR>—सु-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king of Vaiśālī; of another person.<BR>—सु-चरित,<BR>अम्, n. good conduct; (अस्, आ, अम्), well conducted,<BR>well behaved; well managed; (आ), f. a well conducted<BR>or faithful wife.<BR>—सुचरित-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>performing religious obligations.<BR>—सु-चरित्र, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1119-c" target="_blank">Page1119-c+ 81</a>]<BR>n. good conduct, a good or virtuous course of life;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), well conducted; (आ), f. a virtuous or<BR>faithful wife.<BR>—सु-चर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, having beautiful<BR>skin or bark; (आ), m. the Bhūrja tree.<BR>—सु-चारु,<BR>उस्, उस् or वी, उ, very lovely or beautiful, pleasing,<BR>delightful; (उस्), m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—सु-<BR>चारु-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a delightful sound,<BR>melodious, harmonious, mellifluous.<BR>—सु-चित्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, very variegated or spotted; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a king; (आ), f. a kind of gourd (= चिर्भिटा).<BR>—सु-चित्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, very variegated; (अस्),<BR>m. a kingfisher; a kind of speckled snake (= चित्र-<BR>सर्प).<BR>—सुचित्र-वीजा, f. ‘having variegated seed,’<BR>a kind of plant (= विडङ्गा).<BR>—सु-चिन्तन, अम्,<BR>n. the act of thinking well, deliberate consideration.<BR>—सु-चिन्ता, f. deep thought, due reflection or con-<BR>sideration.<BR>—सु-चिन्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, well thought<BR>about, well considered or weighed, well imagined,<BR>well pondered upon, well conceived.<BR>—सु-चिरम्,<BR>ind. for a very long time, very long, a good while;<BR>(आय), ind. for a very long time.<BR>—सुचिरायुस् (˚र-<BR>अय्˚), उस्, m. ‘having a very long life,’ a god, divinity.<BR>—सु-चुटी, f. ‘cutting well or easily,’ a pair of<BR>nippers or tongs.<BR>—सु-चेती-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>good minded or well disposed.<BR>—सु-चेतु, Ved. good<BR>feeling, benevolence, kindness, favour, graciousness,<BR>(generally in inst. c. सु-चेतुना, which may, how-<BR>ever, be referred to सु-चेतुन below.)<BR>—सु-चेतुन,<BR>Ved. well disposed, favourable, gracious, auspicious,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda IX. 65, 30. सु-चेतुनम् = सु-ज्ञानम्,<BR>according to Sāy.)<BR>—सु-चेलक, अस्, m. fine cloth,<BR>cloth.<BR>—सु-च्छत्त्र, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva; (आ), f.<BR>the river Śata-dru or Sutlej.<BR>—सु-च्छर्दिष्-टम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a most delightful dwelling,<BR>very blissful.<BR>—सु-च्छर्दिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having<BR>a beautiful abode.<BR>—सु-जङ्घ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>beautiful leg.<BR>—सु-जन, अस्, m. a good or virtuous<BR>man, benevolent man; a gentleman; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>virtuous, good, respectable; kind, benevolent; N. of<BR>Indra's charioteer.<BR>—सुजन-ता, f. goodness, virtue,<BR>kindness, benevolence; bravery; a number of good<BR>men or respectable persons.<BR>—सुजन-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>goodness, kindness.<BR>—सु-जनिमन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>having noble birth, of exalted birth.<BR>—सुजनेतर-<BR>मैत्री (˚न-इत्˚), f. the friendship of a bad man.<BR>—सु-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, of noble or respectable birth;<BR>lawfully begotten, legitimate.<BR>—सु-जम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. handsome-jawed, (Sāy. = सु-दंष्ट्र.)<BR>—सु-<BR>जम्भन्, आ, आ, अ, having good jaws.<BR>—सु-जल, अम्,<BR>n. good water; a lotus; (अस्, आ, अम्), having good or<BR>sweet water.<BR>—सु-जल्प, अस्, m. good speech; a<BR>particular kind of discourse (described as sincere,<BR>earnest, humble, full of meaning and vivacity).<BR>—सु-<BR>जवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, quick, swift.<BR>—सु-जात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well born, of high birth; well grown, tall; well<BR>produced, well made, beautiful; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>plant (= तुवरी).<BR>—सुजात-ता, f. the being well<BR>born, nobility.<BR>—सुजाताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having well-formed limbs.<BR>—सु-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, of a<BR>good tribe or species; of a good race or caste; (इस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Vīti-hotra.<BR>—सुजातीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, = सु-जाति above.<BR>—सु-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>beautiful-tongued, bright-tongued, having bright<BR>flames (said of Agni).<BR>—सु-जीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>digested; decayed, worn out.<BR>—सु-जीव, अस्, m. good<BR>or easy life.<BR>—सु-जीवन्ती, f. a kind of plant (= स्वर्-<BR>ण-जीवन्ती).<BR>—सु-जीवित, अस्, आ, अम्, lived well or<BR>to some purpose; (अम्), n. a lucky or happy life.<BR>—सु-जुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well satisfied, fully<BR>propitiated.<BR>—सु-जूर्णि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. very quick or<BR>active; very old, worn out, (Sāy. = शोभन-जव,<BR>सुष्ठु जीर्ण, i. e. पुराण, Ṛg-veda IV. 6, 3);<BR>glowing brightly [cf. rt. जूर्व्, and see Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 63, 4].<BR>—सु-ज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, well known,<BR>easily known.<BR>—सु-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—सु-ज्यैष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having much<BR>pre-eminence, bringing much prosperity (said of a<BR>son).<BR>—सु-ज्योतिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, having a beautiful light,<BR>well lighted.<BR>—सु-तनु, उस्, f. a beautiful body;<BR>(उस्, उस् or वी, उ), having a beautiful body; very<BR>thin, very slender or delicate; emaciated; (उस् or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1120-a" target="_blank">Page1120-a+ 81</a>]<BR>वी), f. a woman; N. of a daughter of Ugra-sena.<BR>—सुतनु-ता, f. great thinness or delicacy.<BR>—सु-<BR>तन्त्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, having good strings, well-stringed,<BR>sounding well, melodious.<BR>—२. सु-तप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(for 1. सुत-प see under 1. सुत), practising great<BR>penance, very austere.<BR>—सु-तपस्, अस्, n. severe<BR>penance; (आस्, आस्, अस्), one who practises great or<BR>severe penance; having great heat; (आस्), m. an<BR>ascetic, devotee, anchorite, hermit; the sun; N. of<BR>the father of Bali; of the son of Pariplava; of a son<BR>of Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—सु-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, much heated,<BR>very hot.<BR>—सु-तमाम्, ind. most excellently, best.<BR>—सु-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. easy to be crossed.<BR>—सु-तराम्, ind. better, more excellently; more;<BR>excessively; exceedingly; consequently; (न स्˚, very<BR>badly; मा स्˚, in no way, by no means.)<BR>—सु-तर्-<BR>कारी, f. a kind of gourd (= देव-दाली).<BR>—सु-तर्-<BR>दन, अस्, m. the Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>—सु-तर्-<BR>मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. easily carrying across (said of a<BR>boat; Sāy. = सुष्ठु तारयितृ, Ṛg-veda VIII. 42,<BR>3).<BR>—सु-तल, अम्, n. ‘immense depth,’ one of the<BR>seven divisions of the lower regions or regions under<BR>the earth peopled by the Nāgas, (according to<BR>some the sixth in order, but see पाताल, p. 563);<BR>the base or foundation of a large building.<BR>—सु-<BR>तष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well-fashioned.<BR>—सुताम्-<BR>रोष्ठ (˚र-ओष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, very ruddy-lipped.<BR>—सु-तार, अस्, m. ‘well-crossing,’ ‘well-delivering,’<BR>N. of a Muni; (आ), f., scil. तुष्टि, one of the nine<BR>kinds of acquiescence (in the Sāṅkhya phil.; cf. सु-<BR>पारा); scil. सिद्धि, one of the eight kinds of<BR>Perfection (in the Sāṅkhya phil.); N. of a daughter<BR>of Śva-phalka.<BR>—सु-तारक, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>beautiful stars; (आ), f. ‘good-accomplisher,’ N. of<BR>one of the twenty-four goddesses who execute<BR>the commands of the twenty-four Arhats.<BR>—सु-<BR>तिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, very bitter or pungent; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of bitter medicinal plant, = पर्पट; (आ),<BR>f. a species of gourd (= कोषातकी).<BR>—सु-तिक्तक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘very bitter,’ a kind of gentian, Gentiana<BR>Cherayta; the coral tree.<BR>—सु-तीक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very sharp; very pungent; acutely painful; (अस्), m.<BR>the Śigru tree or a white species of it; N. of a<BR>Muni.<BR>—सुतीक्ष्ण-दशन, अस्, m. ‘very sharp-<BR>toothed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सुतीक्ष्णाग्र (˚ण-अग्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very sharp-pointed.<BR>—सु-तीर्थ, अस्, m.<BR>a good preceptor (opposed to कु-तीर्थ); epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सु-तुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having good off-<BR>spring.<BR>—सु-तुङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, very lofty or tall;<BR>(अस्), m. the cocoa-nut tree; a particular culmination<BR>or high position (of the planets &c.).<BR>—सु-तुष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, easily satisfied.<BR>—सु-तुस्, ऊस्, ऊस्, ऊस् (inst.<BR>pl. सु-तूर्भिस्), well-sounding.<BR>—सु-तेजन, अस्, m.<BR>a particular tree (= धन्वन्).<BR>—सु-तेजस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, very sharp or sharp-edged; very bright, splendid;<BR>very mighty or potent; (आस्), m., N. of one of the<BR>Arhats of the past age; a worshipper of the sun.<BR>—सु-तेजित, अस्, आ, अम्, well-sharpened, very sharp.<BR>—सु-तैला, f. the plant Mahā-jyotiṣmatī, q. v.<BR>—सु-त्रातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. a good protector or<BR>preserver, well protecting or saving.<BR>—सु-त्रामन्, आ,<BR>m. ‘good protector,’ N. of Indra [cf. सूत्रामन्];<BR>(आ), f. ‘excellent protectress,’ epithet of Pṛthivī.<BR>—सु-दंशित, अस्, आ, अम्, well bitten; well armed<BR>[cf. परि-दंशित]; pressed very close together,<BR>crowded into close proximity.<BR>—सु-दंसस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. accomplishing mighty or splendid actions,<BR>energetic, active, powerful; [cf. पुरु-दंसस्.]<BR>—सु-<BR>दक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, very capable or clever; (Ved.)<BR>having great energy, very strong.<BR>—सु-दक्षिण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very sincere or upright, very liberal in<BR>sacrificial gifts; (अस्), m., N. of a king of Vidarbha;<BR>(आ), f., N. of the wife of Dilīpa.<BR>—सु-दग्धिका, f.<BR>a kind of plant (= दग्धा).<BR>—सु-दण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>the ratan cane (= वेत्र).<BR>—सु-दण्डिका, f. the Go-<BR>rakṣī plant.<BR>—सु-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, having hand-<BR>some teeth.<BR>—सु-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well or properly<BR>given; [cf. सूत्त, s. v.]<BR>—सु-दत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>granting well or liberally (= कल्याण-दान, Nir-<BR>ukta VI. 14).<BR>—सु-दन्त, अस्, m. a good tooth;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), having good teeth; (अस्), m. an actor,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1120-b" target="_blank">Page1120-b+ 80</a>]<BR>dancer; (ई), f. the female elephant of the north-<BR>west quarter.<BR>—सु-दम, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be<BR>subdued.<BR>—सु-दयित, अस्, आ, अम्, much beloved,<BR>very dear.<BR>—सु-दर्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, having good<BR>Darbha or Kuśa grass; (आ), f. a kind of grass or<BR>sugar-cane (= इक्षु-दर्भा).<BR>—सु-दर्श, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, easily seen.<BR>—सु-दर्शन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, good<BR>looking, beautiful, handsome; easily seen; (अस्), m.<BR>the discus of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (in this sense also<BR>अम्, n.); a vulture; epithet of Śiva; N. of Mount<BR>Meru; of a son of Dadhīci; of a son of Dhruva-<BR>sandhi; of the father of the eighteenth Arhat of the<BR>present Avasarpiṇī; of one of the nine Jaina Śukla-<BR>balas or Bala-devas [cf. शुक्ल-बल]; of a poet; the<BR>rose-apple, Eugenia Jambu; (ई, अम्), f. n., N. of<BR>Indra's city Amarāvatī; (आ), f. a handsome woman;<BR>a woman; an order, command; a particular drug or<BR>medicinal plant; the plant Cocculus Cordifolius or<BR>Menispermum Glabrum; (अम्), n., N. of Jambu-<BR>dvīpa.<BR>—सुदर्शन-चूर्ण, अम्, n. ‘beautiful<BR>powder,’ a particular medicinal compound used in<BR>fevers.<BR>—सुदर्शन-द्वीप, अम्, n. Jambu-dvīpa.<BR>—सुदर्शन-संहिता, f., N. of a work (from<BR>which the Hanūmat-paddhati and Hanūmat-kavaca<BR>are chiefly extracted).<BR>—सु-दल, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>good leaves;’ a kind of plant, = क्षीर-मोरटा;<BR>(आ), f. other plants (= शाल-पर्णी; = तरुणी).<BR>—सु-<BR>दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, very bountiful, munificent.<BR>—सु-<BR>दानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. giving well or liberally, mak-<BR>ing beautiful presents, bounteous, giving plentiful<BR>rain; offering sacrifices.<BR>—सु-दान्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well-subdued, well-restrained, very self-controlled;<BR>(अस्), m. a follower of Śākya-muni (q. v.), a Buddhist.<BR>—सुदान्त-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a medical author.<BR>—सु-दामन्, आ, आ, अ, giving well, one who gives<BR>liberally; (आ), m. a cloud; the sea; a mountain;<BR>N. of Indra's elephant Airāvata; of a particular<BR>Go-pa or cowherd; of a poor Brāhman (who came<BR>to Dvārakā to ask Kṛṣṇa's aid, and was raised to<BR>wealth by him); N. of a particular mountain [cf.<BR>सौदामनी]; of a river.<BR>—सु-दामा, f., N. of a<BR>river in the north of India (mentioned in Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa II. 71, 1).<BR>—सु-दाय, अस्, m. a good gift,<BR>auspicious gift; a special gift given on particular<BR>solemn occasions (e. g. a gift to a student at his in-<BR>vestiture with the sacred thread or Yajñopavīta, a<BR>nuptial present, &c.); one who makes the above<BR>present (e. g. a mother, father, husband, &c.).<BR>—सु-<BR>दारु, उस्, m. ‘having good timber,’ N. of a part of<BR>the Vindhya mountains called Pāripātra, q. v.; [cf.<BR>कुलाचल.]<BR>—सु-दारुण, अस्, आ, अम्, very cruel,<BR>very dreadful or terrible.<BR>—सु-दावन्, आ, m., Ved. a<BR>giver of good, a benefactor.<BR>—सु-दास्, आस्, m., Ved. a<BR>liberal man, liberal sacrificer; N. of a king at whose<BR>court both Vasiṣṭha and Viśvā-mitra appear to have<BR>acted as family priests, (Sudās Paijavana is regarded<BR>as the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 133.)<BR>—सु-<BR>दास, अस्, m., N. of a king; [cf. सु-दास्.]<BR>—सु-<BR>दास्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more liberal, very liberal.<BR>—सु-दिन, अम्, n. a fine day, auspicious day,<BR>happy day; fine weather.<BR>—सुदिन-त्व, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. state of fine weather, an auspicious time.<BR>—सु-<BR>दिनाय, Nom. A. सुदिनायते, to be fine weather.<BR>—सुदिनाह (˚न-अह), अम्, n. a day of fine wea-<BR>ther, a fine day.<BR>—सु-दिव्, -द्यौस्, -द्यौस्, -द्यु,<BR>Ved. having a good sky, having good days.<BR>—सु-<BR>दीति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. shining beautifully, = सु-दीदिति<BR>below; (इस्), m., N. of an Āṅgirasa (author of a<BR>hymn in the Ṛg-veda).<BR>—सु-दीदिति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>shining beautifully.<BR>—सु-दीर्घ, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>long (in time or space), very extended; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of cucumber (= चीनाकर्कटी).<BR>—सुदीर्घ-<BR>घर्मा, f. the plant Marsilia Quadrifolia.<BR>—सु-<BR>दीर्घ-फलिका, f. ‘having very long fruit;’ a kind<BR>of egg-plant.<BR>—सु-दुःख, अम्, n. great pain;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), very painful; (अम्), ind. very sorrow-<BR>fully.<BR>—सु-दुःखित, अस्, आ, अम्, much grieved,<BR>greatly afflicted.<BR>—सु-दुःसह, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>difficult to be borne or endured.<BR>—सु-दुघ, अस्, आ,<BR>चार, अस्, आ, अम्, very ill-conducted, very badly be-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1120-c" target="_blank">Page1120-c+ 81</a>]<BR>haved or wicked; (अस्), m. a profligate.<BR>—सु-दुरा-<BR>रुह, अस्, आ, अम्, very hard to be ascended, inacces-<BR>sible.<BR>—सु-दुरावर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, very difficult to<BR>be dissuaded.<BR>—सु-दुर्गम, अस्, आ, अम्, very diffi-<BR>cult to traverse or cross, very difficult to sail over.<BR>—सु-दुर्जय, अस्, आ, अम्, very difficult to be over-<BR>come or conquered.<BR>—सु-दुर्दर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>difficult to be beheld or observed.<BR>—सु-दुर्बुद्धि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, very foolish.<BR>—सु-दुर्लभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very difficult to be attained, quite unattainable, very<BR>scarce or rare.<BR>—सु-दुश्चर, अस्, आ, अम्, very diffi-<BR>cult to be performed or attained; very arduous or<BR>painful.<BR>—सु-दुष्कर, अस्, ई, अम्, very difficult to<BR>be done, most arduous.<BR>—सु-दुष्ख, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very painful, very unpleasant; (अम्), ind. very pain-<BR>fully, very sorrowfully.<BR>—सु-दुष्खित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>much pained or grieved.<BR>—सु-दुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very bad, very wicked or depraved, much cor-<BR>rupted or spoiled.<BR>—सु-दुस्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>difficult to be passed or crossed; [cf. दुस्-तर.]<BR>—सु-दुस्त्यज, अस्, आ, अम्, very difficult to be<BR>abandoned or quitted.<BR>—सु-दूर, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>distant; (अम्), ind. for a very long distance; in a<BR>very high degree; (आत्), ind. from afar.<BR>—सुदूर-<BR>पराहत, अस्, आ, अम्, driven back to a great dis-<BR>tance.<BR>—सु-दृढ, अस्, आ, अम्, very firm or hard;<BR>(अम्), ind. very firmly.<BR>—सुदृढ-व्रत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very rigid or strict in vows.<BR>—सु-दृश्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>having beautiful eyes, very beautiful; (क्), f. a pretty<BR>woman.<BR>—सु-दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. looking beauti-<BR>fully, having a beautiful appearance (said of Uṣas).<BR>—सु-दृशीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. looking beautiful,<BR>handsome.<BR>—सुदृशीक-सन्दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing a handsome or beautiful appearance; (क्), f. epi-<BR>thet of Uṣas.<BR>—सु-दृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, clearly<BR>visible.<BR>—सु-दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, easily seen, easy to<BR>be seen; looked at earnestly.<BR>—सु-देव, अस्, m. a<BR>favourable or propitious deity; N. of a Brāhman;<BR>(ई), f. a proper N.<BR>—सु-देष्ण, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Kṛṣṇa; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of the wife of Virāṭa; of the wife of Bali.<BR>—सु-<BR>दोहन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. easy to be milked.<BR>—सु-<BR>द्युत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. shining brightly.<BR>—सु-द्युम्न,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very bright; (अस्), m., N. of a king; of<BR>a son of Manu Vaivasvata (supposed to have been<BR>born a female, under the name of Iḍā, q. v., and<BR>afterwards changed into a male through the favour<BR>of Mitra and Varuṇa).<BR>—सु-द्रविणस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. having splendid riches or treasures (said of<BR>Agni).<BR>—सु-द्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having beautiful<BR>wood.<BR>—सु-द्विजानन (˚ज-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing a mouth containing beautiful teeth.<BR>—सु-धन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very rich; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—सु-<BR>धनुस्, उस्, m., N. of a son of Kuru.<BR>—सु-धन्-<BR>वन्, आ, आ, अ, having an excellent bow; (आ), m. a<BR>good archer, bowman; N. of Viśva-karman, q. v.;<BR>of a king; the son of an outcast Vaiśya (but see<BR>below).<BR>—सुधन्वाचार्य, अस्, m. (by some sepa-<BR>rated into two words, see सु-धन्वन् and चार्य),<BR>the son of an outcast Vaiśya by a woman of the<BR>same class, (Manu X. 23.)<BR>—सु-धर्म, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of the ten disciples of the celebrated Jaina<BR>teacher and Arhat Mahā-vīra, q. v., (the line of Jaina<BR>ascetics is said to be traced up to him in regular suc-<BR>cession, the other ten disciples of Mahā-vīra having<BR>left no successors); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>deities; (आ, ई), f. an assembly or council of the gods.<BR>—सु-धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, keeping well to duty, at-<BR>tentive to duties; (आ), m. a council or assembly of<BR>the gods; the hall or palace of Indra (given to Ugra-<BR>sena by Kṛṣṇa); a man attentive to the proper<BR>maintenance of his family; N. of a son of king<BR>Bhadra-sena; of a Kṣatriya.<BR>—सु-धर्ष or सु-<BR>धर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) easy to be laid<BR>hold of, easy of attainment or approach; [cf. दुर्-<BR>धर्ष.]<BR>—सु-धा, see p. 1127.<BR>—सु-धाम, N.<BR>of a mountain; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of deities.<BR>—सु-धामन्, आ, m., N. of a Muni; of a Loka-pāla.<BR>—सु-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. streaming beautifully.<BR>—सु-धित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well or properly placed,<BR>well-ordered, perfect, secure; well-disposed, kind,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1121-a" target="_blank">Page1121-a+ 81</a>]<BR>good, benevolent; prosperous, happy; well held, well<BR>a ned, well thrown (said of weapons).<BR>—सु-धिति,<BR>इस्, m. f. an axe (more correctly written स्व-धिति,<BR>q. v.).<BR>—सु-धी, ईस्, f. a good understanding, good<BR>sense, intelligence; (ईस्, ईस्, इ), having a good under-<BR>standing, wise, clever, sensible; (ईस्), m. a wise or<BR>clever or intelligent man; a Pandit, teacher.<BR>—सु-<BR>धीर, अस्, आ, अम्, very firm or resolute; very con-<BR>siderate or wise.<BR>—सु-धुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. carry-<BR>ing a burden well (said of a horse).<BR>—सु-धूम्य,<BR>अस्, m. a particular fragrant substance (= स्वादु).<BR>—सु-धूम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, very purple.<BR>—सुधूम्र-<BR>वर्णा, f. ‘of a deep purple colour,’ epithet of one<BR>of the seven tongues of fire.<BR>—सु-धृति, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—सुध्य्-उपास्य (written सुद्ध्य्-<BR>उपास्य), अस्, m. ‘he who is to be worshipped by the<BR>intelligent,’ epithet of the Deity; (अस्), m. a particu-<BR>lar kind of royal palace (of which twelve sorts are<BR>enumerated); a particular attendant on Kṛṣṇa;<BR>(आ), f. a woman; N. of the goddess Umā; of one<BR>of Umā's female companions; the plant Aristolochia<BR>Indica; a sort of pigment, = गो-रोचना; (अम्), n.<BR>the club of Bala-rāma.<BR>—सु-नक्षत्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king; (आ), f., N. of the second night of the civil<BR>month (कर्म-मास).<BR>—सु-नन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, pleas-<BR>ing well, delighting.<BR>—सुनन्दा-सहित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attended by Su-nandā.<BR>—सु-नन्दिनी, f. a species of<BR>the Ati-jagatī metre (= मञ्जु-भाषिणी).<BR>—सु-<BR>नय, अस्, m. good conduct; good policy [cf. दुर्-<BR>नय]; N. of a son of Ṛta; of a son of Pariplava;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—सु-नयन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having beautiful eyes; (अस्), m. a deer; (आ), f.<BR>a woman.<BR>—सु-नस, अस्, आ, अम्, handsome-nosed;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—सु-नाभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a beautiful navel, having a good nave or centre;<BR>(अस्), m. a mountain; the mountain Maināka, q. v.;<BR>N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a son of Garuḍa.<BR>—सु-नाम-द्वादशी, f. a particular religious ob-<BR>servance performed on the twelfth day of the twelfth<BR>month.<BR>—सु-नामन्, आ, -म्नी, अ, well named; (आ),<BR>m., N. of a son of Ugra-sena, of a chief of the Śūra-<BR>senas (represented as destroyed in battle together<BR>with his whole army by Kṛṣṇa).<BR>—सु-नालक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, having a beautiful stalk or stem; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of tree (= वक-पुष्प).<BR>—सु-नासा, f. a hand-<BR>some nose.<BR>—सु-नासाक्ष-भ्रुव (˚सा-अक्ष्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, endowed with handsome nose, eyes, and eye-<BR>brows.<BR>—सु-नासिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a handsome<BR>nose; having a good point or projection; (आ), f. a<BR>particular plant (= काक-नासा).<BR>—सु-नासीर, see s. v.<BR>—सु-निग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, well controlled, easily<BR>restrained.<BR>—सु-निद्रा, f. sound sleep.<BR>—सु-निधा<BR>(inst. of सु-निध for सु-निधा according to Sāy.),<BR>Ved. with careful putting down, with great care,<BR>(Sāy. = शोभनेन निधानेन, Ṛg-veda III. 29,<BR>12.)<BR>—सु-निनद, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding agreeably<BR>or pleasantly.<BR>—सु-निभृत, अस्, आ, अम्, very lonely<BR>or private; (अम्), ind. very secretly or closely, very<BR>narrowly, very privately.<BR>—सु-निरज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. altogether easy to be attained, (Sāy. = सुखेन<BR>निःशेषम् प्राप्य, Ṛg-veda I. 10, 7.)<BR>—सु-<BR>निरूपित, अस्, आ, अम्, well observed or inspected,<BR>well examined, well seen into.<BR>—सु-निर्णिक्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, thoroughly cleansed, well washed off.<BR>—सु-<BR>निर्मथा (according to Sāy. inst. case fr. सु-निर्-<BR>मथ्), Ved. with auspicious attrition (= शोभनेन<BR>मन्थनेन, Ṛg-veda III. 29, 12).<BR>—सु-निर्यासा,<BR>f. ‘having good exudation or resin,’ the plant Jiṅginī,<BR>q. v.<BR>—सु-निशित, अस्, आ, अम्, very sharp.<BR>—सु-निश्-<BR>चल, अस्, m. ‘very unchangeable,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-निश्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, well ascertained or de-<BR>termined, resolved; commended, approved; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a particular Buddha.<BR>—सु-निषण्ण or<BR>सु-निषण्णक, अम्, n. the pot-herb Marsilea<BR>Quadrifolia.<BR>—सु-निष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>beautiful ornaments.<BR>—सु-निष्टप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well heated or burnished.<BR>—सु-नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, well-<BR>conducted, well-behaved; politic; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>king; (अम्), n. good conduct or behaviour; good<BR>policy, prudence.<BR>—सु-नीति, इस्, f. good conduct or<BR>behaviour, good manners, propriety, good policy; N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1121-b" target="_blank">Page1121-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of the mother of Dhruva; (इस्, इस्, इ), well-conducted.<BR>—सु-नीथ, अस्, आ, अम्, well-disposed, well-conducted,<BR>righteous, virtuous, moral, good; (अस्), m. a good<BR>leader (Ved.); a Brāhman; N. of a king; of Śiśu-<BR>pāla, king of Cedi; (आ), f., N. of the first-born<BR>daughter of Mṛtyu or death (wife of Aṅga).<BR>—सु-<BR>नील, अस्, आ, अम्, very black or blue, dark; (अस्), m.<BR>the pomegranate tree; (अम्), n. the root of the<BR>Andropogon Muricatus; (आ), f. common flax (=<BR>अलसी); other plants (= विष्णु-क्रान्ता; = जरती-<BR>तृण).<BR>—सु-नीलक, अस्, m. ‘very blue,’ a kind of<BR>blue Bhṛṅga-rāja bird; a blue gem (perhaps an<BR>emerald or sapphire); a kind of tree (= नीलासन).<BR>—सु-नृशंस, अस्, आ, अम्, very mischievous or in-<BR>jurious, very cruel.<BR>—सु-नृशंस-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, doing<BR>very malicious things, malicious.<BR>—सु-नेत्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, beautiful-eyed; (आ), f., scil. तुष्टि, one of the<BR>nine kinds of acquiescence (according to the Sāṅkhya<BR>phil.; cf. सु-पार).<BR>—सु-नौ, औस्, औस्, उ, having<BR>good ships; (उ), n. water (according to Śabda-k.).<BR>—सु-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, well cooked or matured,<BR>thoroughly ripe; (अस्), m. a sort of fragrant Mango.<BR>—सु-पत्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having beautiful leaves;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of plant (= आदित्य-पत्त्र); a sort<BR>of grass, = पल्लिवाह; (आ), f. various plants, = रु-<BR>द्र-जटा; = शतावरी; = पालक्या; = शमी; =<BR>शाल-पर्णी; (अम्), n. the leaf of the Laurus Cassia.<BR>—सु-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. the Śigru tree; (इका), f.<BR>= जतुका.<BR>—सु-पत्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, well feathered.<BR>—सु-पत्नी, f. (a woman) having a good husband;<BR>[cf. स-पत्नी.]<BR>—सु-पथ, अस्, m. a good road;<BR>good course or way; good conduct; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having a good road, having beautiful paths; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a brother of Śaśi-kalā.<BR>—सु-पथिन्, -पन्-<BR>थास्, m. a good road; (-पन्थास्, -पथी, -पथि),<BR>having good roads.<BR>—सुपथिन्-तर, अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>better road.<BR>—सु-पथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, very whole-<BR>some; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= श्वेत-चिल्ली).<BR>—सु-<BR>पद्म, अस्, आ, अम्, having beautiful lotuses; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a grammar by Padma-nābha-datta; (आ), f.<BR>orris root.<BR>—सु-पप्तनी, m. du. (in the Pada text<BR>सु-पप्तनि), easily descending, quickly alighting,<BR>(according to Sāy. सु-पप्तनि = शोभन-पतनम्<BR>यथा भवति or सु-पतनौ, Ṛg-veda I. 182, 5.)<BR>—सु-परिक्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, sorely distressed,<BR>grievously pained.<BR>—सु-परिच्छन्न, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well surrounded or furnished with requisites.<BR>—सु-<BR>परिश्रान्त-वाह, अस्, आ, अम्, having very wearied<BR>horses.<BR>—सु-परीक्षण, अम्, n. the art of examin-<BR>ing or trying well, thorough examination.<BR>—सु-प-<BR>रीक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, well examined, well tried,<BR>thoroughly investigated.<BR>—सु-पर्ण, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्,<BR>well-winged, having good or beautiful wings; having<BR>beautiful leaves; (अस्), m. a ray of the sun, solar ray,<BR>(in Naigh. I. 5. सु-पर्णाः is enumerated among the<BR>रश्मि-नामानि, and in I. 14. among the अश्व-ना-<BR>मानि); N. of Garuḍa, q. v.; a class of bird-like beings<BR>of a semi-divine character; any supernatural bird; a<BR>cock; the tree Cassia Fistula; N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi;<BR>(आ, ई), f. a number of lotuses or a pool abound-<BR>ing with them; (ई), f. the mother of the bird Ga-<BR>ruḍa; (Ved.) ‘the beautiful-winged one,’ the sky<BR>(= द्यौस्, sometimes identified with Vāc and re-<BR>garded as the mother of metres; see सौपर्णेय).<BR>—सु-पर्णक, अस्, इका, अम्, having good wings;<BR>having beautiful leaves; (अस्), m. Garuḍa or any bird<BR>of supernatural character; the tree Cassia Fistula;<BR>the tree Echites Scholaris; (इका), f. various plants,<BR>&c. (= स्वर्ण-जीवन्ती; = पलाशी; = शाल-पर्णी;<BR>= रेणुका; = वाकुची).<BR>—सुपर्ण-केतु, उस्, m.<BR>‘having Garuḍa for a symbol,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सुपर्ण-यातु, उस्, m., Ved. a demon in the<BR>shape of a Su-parṇa.<BR>—सुपर्ण-वात, अस्, m. the wind<BR>agitated by the wings of Garuḍa.<BR>—सुपर्णाख्य<BR>(˚ण-आख्˚), अस्, m. the plant Nāga-keśara.<BR>—सुपर्-<BR>णी-तनय, अस्, m. ‘son of Su-parṇī,’ Garuḍa.<BR>—सु-<BR>पर्णेय, अस्, m. a son of Su-parṇī.<BR>—सु-पर्यव-<BR>सित, अस्, आ, अम्, quite finished or concluded, well-<BR>nigh accomplished.<BR>—सु-पर्याप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>extensive, very spacious or comprehensive; well filled<BR>or fitted out (as a palace with various offices and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1121-c" target="_blank">Page1121-c+ 81</a>]<BR>buildings).<BR>—सु-पर्वन्, आ, आ, अ, well jointed, hav-<BR>ing many joints or knots; (आ), m. a bamboo; an<BR>arrow; a god, deity; a special lunar day (in which<BR>religious ceremonies are performed, as the full and<BR>new moon, and the eighth and fourteenth days of<BR>each fortnight); smoke; (आ), f. white Dūrvā grass.<BR>—सु-पलायित, अस्, आ, अम्, completely fled or run<BR>away; well or skilfully retreated; (अम्), n. a total<BR>rout or retreat; a good or skilful retreat.<BR>—सु-पलाश,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having many leaves, abounding in<BR>leaves, leafy.<BR>—सु-पाक्य, अम्, n. a particular medi-<BR>cinal salt (= विड्-लवण).<BR>—सु-पाञ्चालक, see Vopa-<BR>deva VII. 2, VII. 18.<BR>—सु-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. beau-<BR>tiful-handed, skilful-handed, dexterous.<BR>—सु-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. a good or suitable vessel, proper receptacle;<BR>a fit or competent person, an able man, any one well<BR>fitted for an office.<BR>—सु-पाद्, -पात्, -पात् or -पदी,<BR>पात्, having good or handsome feet.<BR>—सु-पान, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well or easily drunk, easy to be drunk.<BR>—सु-<BR>पार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well crossing, easy to be<BR>crossed; (आ), f., scil. तुष्टि (in the Sāṅkhya phil.),<BR>one of the nine kinds of acquiescence and five kinds<BR>of external acquiescence (the other four being सु-<BR>तारा, सु-नेत्रा, सु-मरीचिका, and अनुत्तमा or<BR>सात्त्विकी; cf. सलिल).<BR>—सु-पार्श्व, अस्, m. the waved-<BR>leaf fig-tree (= प्लक्ष); N. of a minister of Rā-<BR>vaṇa; of a fabulous bird (son of Sampāti, mentioned<BR>in Rāmāyaṇa IV. 59); of the seventh Arhat of the<BR>present Ava-sarpiṇī; of a son of Śrutāyus; of a son<BR>of Dṛḍha-nemi; of a place.<BR>—सुपार्श्वक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the third Arhat of the future Utsarpiṇī; a kind<BR>of veined-leaf fig (= गर्दभाण्ड).<BR>—सुपार्श्वोरु<BR>(˚व-ऊरु), उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ, having fine ribs and<BR>thighs.<BR>—सु-पिङ्गला, f. a kind of plant (= जीवन्ती);<BR>another plant (= ज्योतिष्मती).<BR>—सु-पिप्पल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having fine fruit, (Sāy. = सु-फल, Ṛg-<BR>veda VII. 101, 5.)<BR>—सु-पिश्, Ved. beautifully varie-<BR>gated or decorated, having fine ornaments, well-<BR>formed, having beautiful limbs, graceful; [cf. विश्व-<BR>पिश्.]<BR>—सु-पिस्, ईस्, ईस्, ईस् (inst. pl. सु-पीर्भीस्), well<BR>going, well walking.<BR>—सु-पीडन, अम्, n. the act of<BR>pressing or pinching pleasantly, rubbing and knead-<BR>ing the limbs.<BR>—सु-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, well pressed.<BR>—सु-पीत, अस्, m., N. of the fifth Muhūrta; (अम्), n.<BR>a carrot (= गर्जर, see 2. पीत).<BR>—सु-पीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very stout or big.<BR>—सु-पीवन्, आ, &c., drinking<BR>well (according to Śabda-k.).<BR>—सु-पुंसी, f. (a woman)<BR>having a good husband.<BR>—सु-पुट, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of bulbous plant (= कोल-कन्द); another plant<BR>(= विष्णु-कन्द).<BR>—सु-पुत्र, अस्, m. an excellent<BR>son.<BR>—सु-पुत्रिका, f. = जतुका (according to Śab-<BR>da-k.).<BR>—सु-पुरु-हूति, इस्, इस्, इ, very much invoked.<BR>—सु-पुष्करा, f. a particular plant (= स्थल-<BR>पद्मिनी).<BR>—सु-पुष्कल, अस्, आ, अम्, very copious.<BR>—सु-पुष्प, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having beautiful<BR>flowers; (अस्), m. the coral tree; the Śirīṣa tree;<BR>other plants, &c., = रक्त-पुष्पक; = हरि-द्रु;<BR>= राज-तरुणी; (ई), f. the plantain tree; a sort of<BR>fennel (= मिश्रेया); the white Clitoria Ternatea<BR>(= अ-पराजिता); other plants, &c., = जीर्ण-फञ्जी;<BR>= शत-पुष्पी; = द्रोण-पुष्पी; (अम्), n. cloves;<BR>various plants, &c. (= आहुल्य; = प्रपौण्डरीक;<BR>= तूल); the menstrual excretion.<BR>—सु-पुष्पिका,<BR>f. a kind of tree or plant (= पाटला).<BR>—सु-पुष्पित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, blooming beautifully, in full flower; hav-<BR>ing the hair bristling or thrilling (with internal plea-<BR>sure).<BR>—सु-पूजित, अस्, आ, अम्, much honoured.<BR>—सु-पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well purified.<BR>—सु-<BR>पूर, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be filled; well filling; a<BR>sort of lime or citron (= वीज-पूर).<BR>—सुपारक,<BR>अस्, m. the Vaka-puṣpa tree.<BR>—सु-पूर्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well filled.<BR>—सु-पेशस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. beauti-<BR>ful in form, handsome.<BR>—सु-प्रकाश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. very visible, manifest, apparent; public.<BR>—सु-<BR>प्रकेत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very wise; beautifully<BR>shining.<BR>—सु-प्रच्छन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, well con-<BR>cealed, very secret or private.<BR>—सु-प्रजस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, having good offspring.<BR>—सु-प्रणीति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. skilfully guiding, wisely directing.<BR>—सु-<BR>प्रतर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. easily crossing over;<BR>far-shooting.<BR>—सु-प्रतर्क, अस्, m. a sound judg-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1122-a" target="_blank">Page1122-a+ 81</a>]<BR>ment, good understanding or intellect.<BR>—सु-प्र-<BR>तिचक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. beautiful to look at<BR>or behold.<BR>—सु-प्रतिच्छन्नम्, ind. in a very<BR>secret manner.<BR>—सु-प्रतिभा, f. spirituous liquor<BR>(= मदिरा).<BR>—सु-प्रतिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, stand-<BR>ing well; very celebrated, very glorious, famous; (आ),<BR>f. good position, good reputation, fame, celebrity;<BR>the establishment or erection (of a temple, idol,<BR>&c.); installation, consecration; a species of metre<BR>containing four lines of five syllables each; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a month.<BR>—सु-प्रतिष्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>set up or established or fixed, well situated or placed;<BR>consecrated; celebrated; (अस्), m. the Uḍumbara<BR>tree.<BR>—सु-प्रतिष्णात, अस्, आ, अम्, well bathed;<BR>thoroughly purified or cleared; well versed in; well<BR>investigated, clearly ascertained.<BR>—सुप्रतिष्णात-<BR>सूत्र, अस्, m. a Brāhman well versed in the Sūtras,<BR>one who is well skilled in repeating or has clearly<BR>ascertained the (meaning of the) Sūtras.<BR>—सु-प्र-<BR>तीक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a beautiful shape or form,<BR>well made, handsome; handsome-faced (Ved.); hav-<BR>ing a beautiful trunk, strong as an elephant's trunk;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Kāma-deva; of Śiva; of the ele-<BR>phant of the north-east quarter.<BR>—सु-प्रतीत, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—सु-प्रतूर्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>easily overpowering; (Sāy.) inflicting much injury.<BR>—सु-प्रदोह, अस्, आ, अम्, easily milked, easy to<BR>be milked.<BR>—सु-प्रधृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to<BR>be injured, easily overpowered.<BR>—सु-प्रपाण, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. a pond &c. easy for drinking, a good<BR>drinking place, a good tank.<BR>—सु-प्रबुद्ध, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king (father of Māyā-devī, mother of<BR>Buddha).<BR>—सु-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, very bright or<BR>splendid, brilliant, glorious; (अस्), m., N. of one of<BR>the nine Śukla-balas of the Jainas; of a king; (आ),<BR>f. one of the seven tongues of Fire; N. of a river<BR>(sometimes regarded as one of the seven Sarasvatīs);<BR>the Vākucī plant.<BR>—सुप्रभ-पुर, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a town.<BR>—सु-प्रभात, अस्, आ, अम्, well dawned,<BR>well shone forth, well illumined or enlightened; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a particular river; (अम्), n. an auspicious<BR>dawn or day-break, beautiful morning; the earliest<BR>dawn; (ए), ind. at earliest break of day.<BR>—सु-प्र-<BR>यस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having much food or sacrifice,<BR>abounding in oblations (said of Agni); food-bestow-<BR>ing, (in Ṛg-veda VII. 39, 2. सु-प्रया बर्हिस् =<BR>शोभनान्नेन युक्तम् बर्हिस्, according to Sāy.;<BR>by others regarded as from a base सु-प्रया, see<BR>Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-s. XXXIII. 44.)<BR>—सु-<BR>प्रयुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well joined or applied, well<BR>attached; well managed; closely connected.<BR>—सु-<BR>प्रयुक्त-शर, अस्, m. one who fits an arrow skil-<BR>fully on a bow, a good marksman, skilful archer.<BR>—सु-प्रयोग, अस्, m. good application, good ma-<BR>nagement; dexterity, expertness; close contact; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR>—सुप्रयोग-विशिख, अस्, m.<BR>= सुप्रयुक्त-शर above.<BR>—सु-प्रलम्भ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, easy of attainment.<BR>—सु-प्रलाप, अस्, m.<BR>good speaking, discoursing well, eloquence.<BR>—सु-<BR>प्रवाचन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having much speech<BR>or eloquence, worthy of much praise.<BR>—सु-प्रवृद्-<BR>ध, अस्, आ, अम्, full-grown; a proper N.<BR>—सु-<BR>प्रसन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, well pleased, very gracious or<BR>favourable; (अस्), m., N. of Kuvera.<BR>—सुप्रसन्-<BR>नक, अस्, m. a kind of plant (= कृष्णार्जक).<BR>—सु-प्रसरा, f. a kind of creeper (= प्र-सारिणी).<BR>—सु-प्रसाद, अस्, m. extreme graciousness or kind-<BR>ness, great propitiousness; (अस्, आ, अम्), very gracious<BR>or kind, auspicious; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—सुप्र-<BR>सादक, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) easily propitiated,<BR>very placable.<BR>—सु-प्राञ्च्, -प्राङ्, -प्राची, -प्राक्,<BR>Ved. easily going in front, proceeding well or quietly.<BR>—सु-प्रात, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably for सु-प्रभात,<BR>q. v.), dawning finely.<BR>—सु-प्रातर्, ind. fine dawn<BR>or morning.<BR>—सु-प्राप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easily obtain-<BR>able.<BR>—सु-प्रायण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be ap-<BR>proached easily, easily accessible.<BR>—सुप्रायण-त-<BR>म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most accessible; very delicate<BR>or tender (said of the बर्हिस् or sacred grass; Sāy.<BR>= मृदु-तम, Ṛg-veda VI. 63, 3).<BR>—सु-प्रावी,<BR>ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. well protected; well protecting, a care-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1122-b" target="_blank">Page1122-b+ 81</a>]<BR>ful protector, (Sāy. = सुष्ठु प्रकर्षेण रक्-<BR>षितृ, Ṛg-veda I. 60, 1.)<BR>—सु-प्राव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. to be well protected, especially worthy of pro-<BR>tection, (Sāy. = सुष्ठु प्रकर्षेण रक्षणीय,<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 34, 4.)<BR>—सु-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>dear, greatly beloved, much loved or liked, agreeable,<BR>pleasant; (अस्), m. (in prosody) a foot of two short<BR>syllables, a pyrrhic; (आ), f. a lovely or charming<BR>woman, a favourite wife; N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—सु-<BR>प्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, well pleased, much delighted, very<BR>happy, well cared for, favoured, cherished; very<BR>kind, very gracious or friendly.<BR>—सु-प्रैतृ, ता,<BR>त्री, तृ, Ved. one who goes well.<BR>—सु-प्सरस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, Ved. handsome in form.<BR>—सुप्सरस्-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most handsome in form (said of<BR>Vāyu).<BR>—सु-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing good or<BR>much fruit, very fruitful, very fertile, very profitable;<BR>(अस्), m. the wood-apple tree, Feronia Elephantum<BR>(= कपित्थ); the pomegranate; the jujube; a sort<BR>of bean, Phaseolus Mungo; the Karṇikāra tree;<BR>(आ), f. colocynth; a pumpkin, gourd; the plantain;<BR>a kind of brown grape; another plant (= काश्मरी).<BR>—सु-फेन, अम्, n. ‘good foam,’ a cuttle-fish<BR>bone.<BR>—सु-बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, well bound or<BR>secured, having a good binding; (अस्), m. sesamum.<BR>—सु-बन्धन-विमोचन, अस्, m. ‘good deliverer<BR>from bonds,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-बन्धु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, having good connections or friends; (उस्), m. a<BR>good friend; N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi having the patro-<BR>nymic Gaupāyana or Laupāyana and author of<BR>several hymns in the Ṛg-veda; N. of a merchant;<BR>of the author of the Vāsava-dattā.<BR>—सु-बल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘very powerful,’ epithet of Śiva; N. of<BR>a king of Gāndhāra.<BR>—सुबल-पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of Subala,’ epithet of Śakuni; [cf. सौबल.]<BR>—सु-<BR>बहु, उस्, वी, उ, very much, very many, very nume-<BR>rous.<BR>—सु-बहु-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who is deeply<BR>versed in the Veda, a very profound divine or theo-<BR>logian.<BR>—सु-बान्धव, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-बालक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kauśika.<BR>—सु-<BR>बालधि, इस्, इस्, इ, fine-tailed.<BR>—सु-बाला-ग्राम, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a village.<BR>—सु-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, handsome-<BR>armed; having mighty arms, strong-armed; (उस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra and king of Cedi;<BR>of a son of Śatru-ghna and king of Mathurā; (उस्),<BR>f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—सु-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, of good<BR>understanding, wise, clever, intelligent, shrewd.<BR>—सु-<BR>बोध, अस्, आ, अम्, easy of apprehension; easily<BR>understood, easily taught; (अस्), m. making well<BR>known, good information or knowledge; awakening<BR>or waking up well; (आ), f., N. of a commentary on<BR>the Mugdha-bodha; of a commentary on the Megha-<BR>dūta by Bharata-sena; of a commentary on the Śiśu-<BR>pāla-vadha by Bharata-sena.<BR>—सु-बोधनी, f., N.<BR>of a commentary on the Kṛṣṇa-karṇāmṛta; of<BR>another on the Bhagavad-gītā; of another on the<BR>Śruta-bodha by Manohara-śarman.<BR>—सु-बोधिनी, f.,<BR>N. of a commentary on Vijñāneśvara's Mitākṣarā<BR>by Viśveśvara; of another on the Bhagavad-gītā by<BR>Śrī-dhara-svāmin; of a short treatise on ritual by<BR>Śiva-rāma.<BR>—सु-ब्रह्मण्य, अस्, m., N. of Kārtti-<BR>keya; one of the sixteen priests employed at a solemn<BR>sacrifice; N. of a district; (आ), f. a particular recita-<BR>tion of certain Mantras.<BR>—सु-ब्रह्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>having or receiving excellent prayers, receiving or<BR>uttering beautiful hymns; very pious.<BR>—सुब्रह्म-<BR>वासुदेव, अस्, m. (according to Śabda-k.), epithet of<BR>the son of Vasudeva in the form of Brahman (i. e. of<BR>Kṛṣṇa identified with the Creator).<BR>—सु-भग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, possessing good fortune, very fortunate<BR>or prosperous, happy, blessed, auspicious, highly fa-<BR>voured; beautiful, lovely, charming, pretty; beloved,<BR>liked, amiable; illustrious; (अस्), m. borax; the Aśoka<BR>tree; the Campaka tree; red Amaranth; (आ), f. a<BR>woman beloved by her husband; a favourite wife;<BR>an honoured or honourable mother; a kind of wild<BR>jasmine; turmeric; holy basil; various other plants,<BR>&c., = कैवर्ती; = शाल-पर्णी; = नील-दूर्वा; =<BR>प्रियङ्गु; = कस्तूरी; = सुवर्ण-कदली; (अम्),<BR>n. good fortune.<BR>—सुभगङ्-करण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>making prosperous.<BR>—सुभग-त्व, अम्, n. prosperity.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1122-c" target="_blank">Page1122-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—सुभग-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fancying or consider-<BR>ing one's self fortunate or pleasing.<BR>—सुभगम्-<BR>भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, or सुभगम्-भावुक, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, becoming happy or prosperous or pleasing.<BR>—सुभगम्-मन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, thinking one's self<BR>fortunate or pleasing, fancying one's self a favourite;<BR>vain, a self-flatterer.<BR>—सुभगम्मन्य-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. the state of supposing one's self pleasing or a<BR>favourite, self-conceit, vanity.<BR>—सुभगा-सुत, अस्,<BR>m. the son of a favourite or much-loved wife; the<BR>son of an honoured or honourable mother.<BR>—सुभ-<BR>गोदय (˚ग-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘rise of prosperity,’ N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—सु-भङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking easily;<BR>(अस्), m. the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—सु-भट, अस्, m. a great<BR>warrior, champion; N. of the author of the Dūtāṅ-<BR>gada.<BR>—सु-भट्ट, अस्, m. a very learned man; a<BR>distinguished warrior (in this sense probably for सु-<BR>भट, q. v.).<BR>—सु-भद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, very pro-<BR>pitious or auspicious, very happy or fortunate; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Viṣṇu; of a particular king; (आ), f., N.<BR>of the sister of Kṛṣṇa and wife of Arjuna, (she was<BR>forcibly seized and carried off by Arjuna from Dvā-<BR>rakā after obtaining Kṛṣṇa's leave, as described in<BR>Mahā-bh. Ādi-parvan, chap. 219, 220; her image<BR>is carried in procession with those of Jagan-nātha and<BR>Bala-rāma at the Ratha-yātrā); the creeper Echites<BR>Frutescens; a particular plant (= घृत-मण्डा);<BR>another plant (= काश्मरी).<BR>—सुभद्रक, अस्, m.<BR>a car or vehicle of a god or for carrying the image of<BR>a god in procession (also अम्, n. according to some);<BR>the Vilva tree; a species of the Ati-śakkarī metre<BR>(according to some).<BR>—सुभद्राणी, f. a kind of<BR>medicinal plant (= त्रायमाणा).<BR>—सुभद्रा-ह-<BR>रण-पर्वन्, अ, n. ‘the section relating to the<BR>seizure of Subhadrā,’ see above under सु-भद्रा.<BR>—सु-भद्रिका, f., Ved. the wicked Su-bhadrā; a<BR>particular metre.<BR>—सुभद्रेश (˚रा-ईश), अस्, m.<BR>‘husband of Su-bhadrā,’ epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—सु-भर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bearing well, well burdened; easy to be<BR>borne.<BR>—सु-भसत्तरा, f., Ved. = अतिशयेन सु-<BR>भगा, Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X. 86, 6.<BR>—सु-भानु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of the seventeenth (or fifty-first) year of<BR>Jupiter's cycle of sixty years.<BR>—सु-भाषित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, spoken well or eloquently; speaking or dis-<BR>coursing well, eloquent; (अस्), m. a particular Buddha<BR>or Bauddha sage; (अम्), n. a fine speech, eloquence.<BR>—सुभाषित-रसास्वाद-जात-रोमाञ्च-कञ्चुक<BR>(˚स-आस्˚, ˚म-अञ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having (as it were) a<BR>coat of mail consisting of bristling hairs produced by<BR>tasting the flavour of delightful words.<BR>—सु-भास,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—सु-भिक्ष, अम्, n. good<BR>alms, successful begging; abundance of food (espe-<BR>cially that given as alms), an abundant supply of<BR>provisions, plenty [cf. दुर्-भिक्ष]; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having good food or an abundant supply of pro-<BR>visions; (आ), f. the tree Grislea Tomentosa.<BR>—सु-<BR>भिषक्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. healing best, curing<BR>most effectually, a most excellent physician.<BR>—सु-<BR>भिषज्, क्, क्, क्, healing well, a good physician.<BR>—सु-भीरक, अस्, m. the Palāśa tree, Butea Fron-<BR>dosa.<BR>—सु-भू, ऊस्, f. a good or illustrious birth, (in<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 66, 3. सु-भ्वे, ‘for an illustrious<BR>birth,’ is explained by Sāy. to mean नृणां सम्यक्<BR>भवनाय, ‘entirely for the benefit of men’); (ऊस्,<BR>ऊस्, उ), Ved. (सुभ्वः, nom. pl. masc., Ṛg-veda<BR>VII. 67, 8), being good or excellent; having an ex-<BR>cellent birth; beautiful, excellent; (भ्वस्), pl. (=<BR>नद्यः, Ṛg-veda I. 52, 4; = स्तोतारः, I. 52, 1).<BR>—सु-भूतिक, अस्, m. the Vilva tree.<BR>—सु-भूम,<BR>अस्, m., N. of Kārtavīrya (as the eighth Jaina<BR>Cakra-vartin or universal emperor).<BR>—सु-भूमि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a son of Ugra-sena.<BR>—सु-भृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well borne or maintained, well cherished<BR>or protected.<BR>—सु-भृश, अस्, आ, अम्, very much,<BR>exceeding; (अम्), ind. very much, exceedingly.<BR>—सु-भेषज, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—सु-भै-<BR>रव, अस्, ई, अम्, very fearful, terrific.<BR>—सु-भो-<BR>गीन, अस्, आ, अम्, very fit to be enjoyed, very<BR>desirable.<BR>—सु-भ्राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, shining brightly.<BR>—सु-भ्रातृ, ता, m. a good brother.<BR>—सु-भ्रु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, = सु-भ्रू.<BR>—सु-भ्रू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ (acc. sing.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1123-a" target="_blank">Page1123-a+ 81</a>]<BR>-भ्रुवम्, dat. -भ्रुवे or -भ्रुवै, abl. -भ्रुवस्<BR>or -भ्रुवास्, gen. pl. -भ्रुवाम् or -भ्रूणाम्, voc.<BR>sing. -भ्रूस् or -भ्रु, the latter form of voc. occur-<BR>ring once in the Bhaṭṭi-kāvya), lovely-browed, having<BR>beautiful eyebrows; (ऊस्), f. a woman.<BR>—सु-भ्रू-<BR>नासाक्षि-केशान्त (˚सा-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>handsome brows, nose, eyes, and hair.<BR>—सु-मख,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in sacrifices; much adored;<BR>(Sāy.) = शोभन-यज्ञ, having worthy oblations or<BR>sacrifices.<BR>—सु-मङ्गल, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, very<BR>auspicious, bringing good fortune; abounding in<BR>sacrifices; (आ), f., N. of a river in the district of<BR>Kāmākhyā; a kind of medicinal root (= काकोली);<BR>N. of one of the mothers of the twenty-four Arhats<BR>(according to some); (ई), f., Ved. a woman who<BR>brings good luck.<BR>—सु-मत्, सुमद्-अंशु, &c., see<BR>p. 1128.<BR>—सु-मत, अस्, आ, अम्, well or kindly dis-<BR>posed, friendly.<BR>—सु-मति, इस्, f. a good mind or dis-<BR>position, benevolence, kindness, friendship; favour<BR>of the gods, favour, blessing, gift; a hymn, prayer,<BR>desire, wish; (इस्, इस्, इ), very wise; (इस्), m., N. of a<BR>son of Ranti-bhāra; of a son of Bharata; of a son<BR>of Janam-ejaya; of a son of Sūta and teacher of the<BR>Purāṇas; of several other persons; the fifth Arhat of<BR>the present era; one of the Arhats of the past era;<BR>(इस्), f., N. of the wife of Sagara (mother of 60,000<BR>sons); of the wife of Viṣṇu-yaśas and mother of<BR>Kalki, q. v.<BR>—सुमती-वृध्, त्, त्, त् (for सुमति-<BR>वृध्), Ved. augmenting blessings, increasing favour.<BR>—सु-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, very drunk, mad or impas-<BR>sioned.<BR>—सु-मदन, अस्, m. ‘greatly delighting,’<BR>the Mango tree.<BR>—सुमदात्मजा (˚द-आत्˚), f.<BR>‘daughter of intoxication or passion,’ an Apsaras or<BR>courtezan of Indra's heaven.<BR>—सु-मद्रम्, ind.<BR>excessive prosperity of the Madras, (Pāṇ. II. 1, 6.)<BR>—सु-मधुर, अस्, आ, अम्, very sweet or saccha-<BR>rine, very sweet or pleasing, very gentle or soothing;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of pot-herb, = जीव-शाक; (अम्), n.<BR>very soothing or gentle speech, &c.; (अम्), ind.<BR>very sweetly.<BR>—सु-मध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>beautiful waist, slender-waisted.<BR>—सु-मध्यम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, slender-waisted; (आ), f. a graceful woman.<BR>—सु-मन, अस्, आ, अम्, very charming, beautiful,<BR>handsome; (अस्), m. wheat; the thorn-apple; (आ),<BR>f. great-flowered jasmine.<BR>—सुमनः-पत्त्रिका, f.<BR>(probably) the outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR>—सुम-<BR>नः-फल, अस्, m. elephant or wood-apple, Feronia<BR>Elephantum; (अम्), n. nutmeg.<BR>—सु-मनस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, good-minded, well-disposed, benevolent,<BR>happy; well pleased, satisfied; (आस्), m. a god,<BR>divinity; a learned man or teacher; a student of the<BR>Vedas, &c.; wheat; the Nimb tree; other plants<BR>(= पूति-करञ्ज; = महा-करञ्ज); N. of a son<BR>of Uru; of a son of Hary-aśva; (असस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a class of deities; (आस्, अस्), f. n. a flower; (असस्),<BR>f. pl. (with a singular meaning), a flower; (आस्), f.<BR>great-flowered jasmine; other plants (= मालती; =<BR>शत-पत्त्री).<BR>—सु-मनस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being in good spirits, cheerful, being of a cheerful<BR>disposition; regarding with favour.<BR>—सु-मना, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= जाती-पुष्प).<BR>—सु-मनाय, Nom.<BR>A. -मनायते, &c., to become happy.<BR>—सुमनी-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make of good mind,<BR>make well-disposed.<BR>—सुमनी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भ-<BR>वति, &c., to be of good mind.<BR>—सुमनो-भर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, possessing or ornamented with flowers.<BR>—सुमनो-रजस्, अस्, n. the pollen of a flower.<BR>—सु-मनोहर, अस्, आ, अम्, or सु-मनोहरण,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, very captivating or agreeable, very charm-<BR>ing or pleasing, beautiful.<BR>—सु-मन्तु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>advising well; very faulty, very blamable; (उस्), m.<BR>excellent praise (Ved.); a good adviser; N. of a<BR>Muni (and lawyer, said to have been a pupil of<BR>Veda-vyāsa and to have been taught by him the<BR>Atharva-veda, originally handed down by tradition<BR>from Brahmā); N. of a king; of a son of Jahnu (or,<BR>according to some, of Purū-ravas).<BR>—सु-मन्त्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the elder brother of Kalki, q. v.; of the<BR>charioteer and minister of king Daśa-ratha, (see<BR>Rāmāyaṇa II. 14, 30); of a preceptor.<BR>—सु-मन्-<BR>त्रज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, well versed in sacred texts.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1123-b" target="_blank">Page1123-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—सु-मन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, well or wisely coun-<BR>selled, well advised, wisely planned.<BR>—सु-मन्दधी,<BR>ईस्, ईस्, इ, very dull of understanding.<BR>—सु-मन्द-<BR>बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, very dull-witted; much disheart-<BR>ened.<BR>—सु-मन्दभाज्, क्, क्, क्, very unfortunate.<BR>—सु-मन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having good under-<BR>standing, very wise or intelligent.<BR>—सु-मरीचिका, f.,<BR>scil. तुष्टि, epithet of one of the five kinds of<BR>external acquiescence (in the Sāṅkhya phil.; cf.<BR>सु-पारा).<BR>—सु-मर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be<BR>borne.<BR>—सु-महत्, आन्, अती, अत्, very great, very<BR>large or abundant; (अत्), ind. very greatly, mightily.<BR>—सु-महस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. beautifully shining.<BR>—सु-महा-कक्ष, अस्, m. a very great gate; a<BR>large court-yard.<BR>—सु-महा-तपस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, one<BR>who has practised very great religious austerities,<BR>very pious.<BR>—सु-महात्मन्, आ, आ, अ, most magna-<BR>nimous.<BR>—सु-महात्यय (˚हा-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>causing very great evil or destruction, very per-<BR>nicious.<BR>—सु-महा-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, of very<BR>great strength, very strong or powerful.<BR>—सु-<BR>महा-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, having very long arms, very<BR>powerful.<BR>—सु-महा-स्वन, अस्, m. ‘very loud-<BR>sounding,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-माय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abounding in illusions, very wise.<BR>—सु-मार्दव,<BR>अम्, n. beautiful softness.<BR>—सु-मालि, इस्, इस्, इ, well-<BR>garlanded.<BR>—सु-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, well-garlanded; (ई),<BR>m., N. of a son of Veda-māli.<BR>—सु-माल्य, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Mahā-padma or Nanda.<BR>—सु-मित्र,<BR>अस्, m. ‘good friend,’ N. of the father of the twentieth<BR>Arhat of the present era; of the author of Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 105 (having the patronymic Kautsa); of the<BR>author of Ṛg-veda X. 69, 70 (having the patronymic<BR>Vādhryaśva); N. of a son of Vṛṣṇi; of a descendant<BR>of Vṛhad-bala (last of the race of Ikṣvāku); (आ),<BR>f., N. of one of the wives of Daśa-ratha (mother of<BR>Lakṣmaṇa and Śatru-ghna); of the mother of Mār-<BR>kaṇḍeya.<BR>—सुमित्र-भू, ऊस्, m., N. of Sagara (as<BR>one of the Jaina Cakra-vartins); of the twentieth<BR>Arhat of the present era.<BR>—सुमित्रा-भू, ऊस्, or<BR>सुमित्रा-तनय, अस्, m., N. of Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—सु-<BR>मीऌह, अस्, m., Ved. a proper N.<BR>—सु-मुख, अम्,<BR>n. a good or beautiful mouth; a handsome face;<BR>(अस्, आ or ई, अम्), having a good or beautiful mouth,<BR>(according to Vopa-deva the fem. is आ when used in<BR>a metaphorical sense, e. g. सुमुखा शाला, a hall with<BR>a good entrance); handsome-faced, lovely; pleas-<BR>ing, agreeable; (अस्), m. a learned man or teacher;<BR>N. of a Muni; of Garuḍa; of the son of Garuḍa;<BR>of Gaṇeśa; of Śiva; of one of the serpents of<BR>Pātāla; a kind of pot-herb; other plants, = सितार्-<BR>जक; = वन-वर्वरिका; = वर्वर; (आ, ई), f. a<BR>handsome woman; a mirror; (ई), f. a species of the<BR>Tri-ṣṭubh metre; (अम्), n. the mark or scratch of<BR>a finger-nail.<BR>—सुमुख-सू, ऊस्, m. ‘the father of<BR>Sumukha,’ epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—सु-मुष्टि, इस्, m.<BR>a kind of shrub (= विष-मुष्टि).<BR>—सु-मू, ऊस्,<BR>ऊस्, उ, binding well.<BR>—सु-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a good root; (अस्), m. the white Śigru tree; (आ), f.<BR>a kind of plant (= शाल-पर्णी; = पृश्नि-पर्णी).<BR>—सु-मूलक, अम्, n. a carrot.<BR>—सु-मृडीक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. making very happy; very bountiful.<BR>—सु-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, well rubbed or purified,<BR>well brushed, very smooth or glossy, very fine.<BR>—सु-<BR>मृष्ट-पुष्पाढ्य (˚प-आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abounding in bright flowers.<BR>—सुमृष्ट-वेष,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, dressed in well-brushed clothes.<BR>—सु-<BR>मेक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) well-formed, of<BR>a beautiful shape, (Sāy. सु-मेक = सु-रूप, Ṛg-<BR>veda III. 6, 10; = सु-दीप्त, shining beautifully,<BR>Ṛg-veda IV. 6, 3; सु-मेके = शोभन-कर्माणौ<BR>or शोभन-मेहने, well acting or well nourishing,<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 146, 3.)<BR>—सु-मेखल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing a good girdle, well girdled; (अस्), m. the<BR>Muñja grass (which forms the Brāhmanical girdle).<BR>—सु-मेधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having a good under-<BR>standing, sensible, intelligent; (आस्), m. a wise man;<BR>N. of a Muni; of a son of Veda-mitra; (आस्), f.<BR>heart-pea.<BR>—सु-मेरु, उस्, m. the sacred mountain<BR>Meru, q. v.; N. of Śiva; (उस्, उस्, उ), very exalted,<BR>excellent.<BR>—सु-यत, अस्, आ, अम्, well restrained or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1123-c" target="_blank">Page1123-c+ 81</a>]<BR>governed.<BR>—सु-यन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, well curbed<BR>or governed, well restrained or bound, well regu-<BR>lated; one who governs his passions completely.<BR>—सुयन्त्रित-त्व, अम्, n. the being well or firmly<BR>restrained or bound.<BR>—सु-यभ्या, f., Ved. to be<BR>well embraced (sexually).<BR>—सु-यम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. well restraining; well traversing, (Sāy. = शो-<BR>भन-नियमन, i. e. सञ्चारिन्, Ṛg-veda I. 180,<BR>1.)<BR>—सु-यवस, अम्, n. beautiful grass, good pas-<BR>turage; (अस्, आ, अम्), having good pasturage, abound-<BR>ing in grass; (अस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—सु-यवसिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, having excellent grass, abounding in pasture.<BR>—सु-यश, अस्, आ, अम्, = सु-यशस् below; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a wife of Parīkṣit.<BR>—सु-यशस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>very famous or renowned; (आस्), m., N. of a king<BR>(belonging to the Maurya dynasty).<BR>—सु-यामुन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu; of a king of Kośāmbī, (also<BR>called Vatsa); a palace; a mountain; a kind of<BR>cloud.<BR>—सु-याशु-तरा, f., Ved. (a female) who<BR>has excessive sexual embraces, (Ṛg-veda X. 86, 6.)<BR>—सु-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, well joined, harmoniously<BR>combined; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-युक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. good appliance or contrivance.<BR>—सु-युज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, Ved. well joined, well yoked.<BR>—सु-युत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well accompanied by, well furnished or provided<BR>with.<BR>—सु-युद्ध, अम्, n. a well-fought war or<BR>battle.<BR>—सु-योग, अस्, m. a favourable juncture, good<BR>opportunity.<BR>—सु-योधन, अस्, m. ‘fighting well,’<BR>epithet of Dur-yodhana, q. v.<BR>—सु-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well coloured, deeply dyed; deep red, crimson;<BR>strongly affected or impassioned; well or kindly<BR>affected.<BR>—सु-रक्तक, अस्, m. a sort of red or<BR>golden chalk; a kind of Mango tree (apparently one<BR>bearing a small red fruit).<BR>—सु-रक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>‘good-protector,’ N. of a Muni.<BR>—सु-रक्षण,<BR>अम्, n. careful protection, protecting or preserving<BR>well.<BR>—सु-रक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, well preserved or<BR>protected, carefully guarded.<BR>—सु-रक्ष्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, easy to be preserved.<BR>—सु-रङ्ग, अस्, m. a<BR>good colour, good dye; ‘bright-coloured,’ the orange;<BR>a hole cut in a house; (आ), f. a hole cut in a<BR>wall for the purpose of breaking into a house, &c.,<BR>(probably for सु-रुङ्गा, q. v.); a kind of fragrant<BR>grass; crystal; (ई), f. a kind of plant (= काक-नाशा);<BR>a kind of red Śobhāñjana; (अम्), n. red sanders;<BR>vermilion.<BR>—सुरङ्ग-द, अम्, n. ‘yielding a good<BR>colour,’ red sanders.<BR>—सुरङ्ग-धातु, उस्, m. red<BR>chalk.<BR>—सुरङ्ग-युज्, क्, m. a house-breaker, (see<BR>सु-रङ्ग.)<BR>—सु-रङ्गिका, f. the Mūrvā plant.<BR>—सु-<BR>रजः-फल, अस्, m. the jack-fruit tree.<BR>—सु-<BR>रजनी, f. night.<BR>—सु-रजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, very dusty.<BR>—सु-रजाय, Nom. A. सुरजायते, &c., to become<BR>very dusty.<BR>—सु-रञ्जन, अस्, m. the betel-nut tree<BR>Areca Faufel or Catechu.<BR>—सु-रण, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>a pleasant sound, (Sāy. = शोभन-गीतादि-ध्वनि,<BR>the sound of pleasant hymns, or सु-रमणीयम्,<BR>ind. very pleasantly); pleasure, enjoyment (according<BR>to some); (अस्, आ, अम्), giving forth pleasant sounds<BR>(said of Agni or fire).<BR>—सु-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, much<BR>sported or dallied, playful; much enjoyed; com-<BR>passionate, tender; (अम्), n. great delight or enjoy-<BR>ment; amorous pleasure, the union of the sexes, sexual<BR>intercourse, coition.<BR>—सुरत-ताली, f. a female mes-<BR>senger, go-between; a chaplet, garland for the head.<BR>—सुरत-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m. addiction to amorous<BR>pleasures.<BR>—सुरत-प्रसङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, devoted or<BR>addicted to amorous pleasures.<BR>—सुरत-विशेष, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of sexual intercourse.<BR>—सु-रति, इस्, f. great<BR>enjoyment or delight.<BR>—सुरति-मिश्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of the author of the Alaṅkāra-mālā.<BR>—सु-रथ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king of the lunar race; of a son of<BR>Jahnu; of a son of Caitra; of a son of Adhiratha.<BR>—सुरथ-विजय, अस्, m., N. of the seventy-ninth<BR>chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—सु-रभि, सुरभित, &c., see p. 1129.<BR>—सु-<BR>रस, अस्, आ, अम्, well flavoured, juicy, sapid, savoury;<BR>sweet; elegant (as a composition); (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of plant (= सिन्धु-वार); a particular resin, =<BR>मोच-रस; (आ, अम्), f. n. sacred basil; (आ), f., N.<BR>of Durgā; of the mother of the Nāgas; of a daughter<BR>of Dakṣa and wife of Kaśyapa; of an Apsaras; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1124-a" target="_blank">Page1124-a+ 81</a>]<BR>kind of plant (= रासना); other plants (= मिश्रेया;<BR>= ब्राह्मी; = महा-शतावरी); a species of the Ati-<BR>dhṛti metre; N. of a river; (अम्), n. gum-myrrh,<BR>Cassia bark; fragrant grass.<BR>—सुरसाष्ट (˚स-अष्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a class of eight plants (viz. Nirguṇṭī, Tulasī,<BR>Brāhmī, Vṛhatī, Kaṇṭa-kārikā, Punar-ṇavā, &c.).<BR>—सु-राजक, अस्, m. a kind of plant (= भृङ्ग-<BR>राज).<BR>—सु-राजन्, आ, m. a good king; a divinity.<BR>—सु-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. rich in gifts, (Sāy. = सु-<BR>दान.)<BR>—सु-रात्रि, इस्, f. a fine night.<BR>—सु-राधस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having beautiful gifts; granting<BR>good things, very rich; having great power; (आस्),<BR>m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi (having the patronymic<BR>Vārṣāgira, q. v.).<BR>—सु-राष्ट्र, अम्, n. (sometimes<BR>also आ, f.), ‘good country,’ N. of a country on the<BR>western side of India, (commonly called Surat.)<BR>—सु-<BR>राष्ट्र-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced in Surat;<BR>(अस्), m. a sort of pulse (= कृष्ण-मुद्ग); a sort<BR>of poison; (आ), f. a sort of fragrant earth; (अम्), n.<BR>the fragrant earth Tuvarī.<BR>—सुराष्ट्र-ब्रह्म, अस्,<BR>m. a Brāhman of Su-rāṣṭra, (Pāṇ. V. 4, 104.)<BR>—सु-रुक्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining beautifully.<BR>—सु-रुच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. brightly shining.<BR>—सु-रुचि,<BR>इस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—सु-रुज, अस्, आ, अम्, very sick,<BR>unwell.<BR>—सु-रूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing well up or<BR>out, very prominent or projecting.<BR>—सु-रूप, अस्, आ,<BR>or ई, अम्, well-formed, handsome; wise, learned;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Śiva; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class<BR>of deities; (आ), f. the shrub Śāla-parṇī; (अम्), n. =<BR>तूल.<BR>—सुरूप-कृत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. accomplish-<BR>ing excellent actions.<BR>—सु-रूहक, अस्, m. ‘easily<BR>mounted,’ a horse resembling an ass (= गर्दभा-<BR>भाश्व).<BR>—सु-रेक्णस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having<BR>beautiful property, rich in possessions.<BR>—सु-रेणु,<BR>उस्, m. a sort of atom, (also उ, n., according to some,<BR>cf. त्रस-रेणु, हेम-रेणु); (उस्), f. ‘having beau-<BR>tiful sand,’ N. of a river, (sometimes regarded as<BR>one of the seven Sarasvatīs.) — 1. सु-रेभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, (for 2. सुरेभ see p. 1129, col. 2), fine-<BR>sounding, fine-voiced, (Kirāt. XV. 16); (अम्), n.<BR>tin.<BR>—सु-रेवट, अस्, m. a species of small Areca<BR>tree (= राम-पूग).<BR>—सु-रै, रास्, रास्, रि, very<BR>rich; (रास्), m. f. an opulent person.<BR>—सु-रोचिस्, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—सु-लक्षण, अम्,<BR>n. the act of observing or examining carefully, looking<BR>well into, ascertaining, determining; a good mark<BR>or characteristic, auspicious mark; (अस्, आ, अम्), hav-<BR>ing beautiful or auspicious marks, having an auspicious<BR>name, fortunate; (आ), f., N. of one of Durgā's female<BR>companions; epithet of one of Kṛṣṇa's wives.<BR>—सु-<BR>लक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, well examined, well determined<BR>or ascertained.<BR>—सु-लङ्घित, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has been caused to fast properly, (see rt. लङ्घ्.)<BR>—सु-लभ, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be obtained or<BR>effected, easy of acquisition or attainment, easy of<BR>access, attainable, feasible, easy; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>shrub (= माष-पर्णी); N. of a female mendicant.<BR>—सुलभावकाश (˚भ-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, easily<BR>gaining room or admission.<BR>—सु-ललाट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a beautiful forehead.<BR>—सु-ललित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sporting gracefully; greatly pleased or happy; very<BR>delicate or dainty; (अम्), ind. very sportively or<BR>wantonly, with delight, easily.<BR>—सु-लाभिका, f. =<BR>शोभन-लाभा (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X.<BR>86, 7).<BR>—सु-लू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, one who cuts well.<BR>—सु-<BR>लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, fine-eyed, having beautiful eyes;<BR>(अस्), m. a deer; epithet of Duryodhana (according<BR>to some); N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; (आ), f. a<BR>handsome woman; N. of the wife of king Mādhava.<BR>—सु-लोम, अस्, आ, अम्, fine-haired, having beautiful<BR>hair or down; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= ताम्र-<BR>वल्ली); another plant (= मांस-च्छदा).<BR>—सु-<BR>लोमन्, आ, आ, अ, = सु-लोम.<BR>—सु-लोमश, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having good hair or down, very hairy or downy;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of plant (= काक-जङ्घा).<BR>—सु-लो-<BR>हक, अम्, n. ‘good metal,’ brass.<BR>—सु-लोहित, अस्,<BR>m. a beautiful red colour; (अस्, आ or -हिनी, अम्),<BR>very red; (आ), f. epithet of one of the seven tongues<BR>of fire.<BR>—सु-वक्त्र, अम्, n. a good mouth or face;<BR>correct utterance or intonation; (अस्, आ, अम्), hand-<BR>some-mouthed; handsome-faced; (अस्), m. epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1124-b" target="_blank">Page1124-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of Śiva; a kind of plant (= वन-वर्वरी).<BR>—सु-<BR>वक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having a handsome breast.<BR>—सु-वचन, अम्, n. the act of speaking well,<BR>good speech, eloquence; (ई), f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—सु-वचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, speaking much or well,<BR>discoursing eloquently.<BR>—सु-वचस्या, f., Ved. sweet<BR>praise, an excellent hymn.<BR>—सु-वज्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having an excellent thunderbolt.<BR>—सु-वदन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a beautiful face, beautiful; (आ), f.<BR>a particular metre.<BR>—सु-वयस्, आस्, m. (probably)<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>—सु-वरत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing good thongs.<BR>—सु-वरूथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a good protecting ledge (said of a chariot; see व-<BR>रूथ).<BR>—१. सु-वर्ग, अस्, m., Ved. having good<BR>society, (but see 2. सुवर्-ग, स्वर्ग.)<BR>—सु-वर्-<BR>चक, अस्, m. natron, alkali; N. of an ancient sage.<BR>—सु-वर्चल, अस्, m., N. of a country; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a wife of the Sun; of a wife of Rudra;<BR>linseed, Linum Usitatissimum; other plants (=<BR>सूर्य-मुखी; = आदित्य-भक्ता; = ब्राह्मी.) — सु-<BR>वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, very bright, very glorious; (आस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—सु-वर्चस,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having great splendor; (अस्), m. epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—सु-वर्चसिन्, ई, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-<BR>वर्चिक, अस्, आ, m. f. natron, alkali.<BR>—सु-वर्चिन्, ई, m.<BR>natron.<BR>—सु-वर्ण, &c., see p. 1129.<BR>—सु-वर्मन्,<BR>आ, m. ‘having good armour,’ N. of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra.<BR>—सु-वल्लि, इस्, or सु-वल्ली, f. the shrub<BR>Serratula Anthelmintica (= सोम-राजी).<BR>—सु-वस्,<BR>अस्, अस्, अस्, covering or clothing well.<BR>—सु-वसन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well dressed, elegantly attired.<BR>—सु-वसन्त, अस्, m. a beautiful vernal season;<BR>the day of full moon in the month Caitra; a festival<BR>in honour of Kāma-deva celebrated in that month.<BR>—सु-वसन्तक, अस्, m. a kind of large creeper,<BR>Gærtnera Racemosa; a festival in honour of Kāma-<BR>deva in the month Caitra.<BR>—सु-वह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bearing well, conveying pleasantly; patient, enduring;<BR>easy to be borne; (आ), f. the plant Nyctanthes<BR>Tristis; the shrub Mimosa Octandra; the plant<BR>Rāsnā; the shrub Cissus Pedata; the gum olibanum<BR>tree, Boswellia Thurifera; the plant Tri-vṛt or Con-<BR>volvulus Turpethum; other plants (= रुद्र-जटा;<BR>= हंस-पदी; = गन्ध-नाकुली; = मुसली; =<BR>नील-सिन्धुवार); a Vīṇā or lute.<BR>—सु-वाच्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, Ved. speaking well; sounding beautifully; making<BR>a loud noise; (क्), m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—सु-वाच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be read.<BR>—सु-<BR>वामा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—सु-वार्, र्, र्, र्, having<BR>beautiful water.<BR>—सु-वार्त्ता, f. good news.<BR>—१. सु-<BR>वास, अस्, m. an agreeable perfume.<BR>—२. सु-वास, अस्,<BR>m. a pleasant dwelling.<BR>—३. सु-वास, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well clad; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-वासस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, Ved. having beautiful garments, well dressed.<BR>—सु-वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, well scented or perfumed.<BR>—सु-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in a comfortable or<BR>respectable abode; (इनी), f. a woman married or single<BR>who resides in her father's house; a term of courtesy<BR>for a respectable woman whose husband is alive.<BR>—सु-वास्तु, N. of a river.<BR>—सु-वाहन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Muni.<BR>—सु-विक्रम, अस्, m. prowess,<BR>valour.<BR>—सु-विक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, very valiant or<BR>heroic, bold, chivalrous; (अस्), m. a hero; (अम्), n.<BR>heroism.<BR>—सु-विचक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, very clever,<BR>well discerning, sensible, proficient, skilful.<BR>—सु-<BR>विचार, अस्, m. good or deliberate consideration; a<BR>proper N.<BR>—सु-विचारित, अस्, आ, अम्, well weighed,<BR>deliberately considered.<BR>—सु-विचार्य, ind. having<BR>well deliberated, having carefully investigated or dis-<BR>cussed.<BR>—सुविचार्य-कारिन्, ई, इणि, इ, acting after<BR>due deliberation, discreet.<BR>—सु-विज्ञान, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very wise.<BR>—सु-विज्ञेय, अस्, m. ‘easily discernible,’<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-वित्त, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—सु-वित्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly scared, terrified,<BR>affrighted.<BR>—सु-विद्, त्, m. a learned man; (त्), f. a<BR>shrewd or clever woman.<BR>—सु-विद, अस्, m. an<BR>attendant on the women's apartments; [cf. सौ-<BR>विद.]<BR>—सु-विदत्, त्, m. a king.<BR>—सु-विदत्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well-disposed, gracious; having good pos-<BR>sessions, (Sāy. = सु-प्रतिज्ञ or सु-धन, Ṛg-<BR>veda II. 9, 6; according to Yāska = कल्याण-विद्य,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1124-c" target="_blank">Page1124-c+ 81</a>]<BR>cf. दुर्-विदत्र); related, of kin, a kinsman, &c.;<BR>(अम्), n. wealth, riches, property, (Sāy. = धन);<BR>a household, family.<BR>—सु-विदत्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. well-disposed, gracious, worthy of knowledge<BR>or wealth, (Sāy. = ज्ञानार्ह or धनार्ह, Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 17, 4.)<BR>—सु-विदल्ल, अम्, n. the women's<BR>apartments; (आ), f. a married woman.<BR>—सु-विदित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well known or understood.<BR>—सु-विदीर्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, much torn or split, greatly expanded.<BR>—सु-विद्युत्, त्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—सु-विध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of a good kind, in a good or easy way;<BR>(अम्), ind. easily.<BR>—सु-विधि, इस्, m. a good rule or<BR>ordinance; the ninth Arhat of the present age (with<BR>Jainas).<BR>—सु-विनीत, अस्, आ, अम्, well trained, pro-<BR>perly behaved, very modest; (आ), f. a tractable cow.<BR>—सु-विपुल, अस्, आ, अम्, very great, very spacious,<BR>very ample or roomy; very loud.<BR>—सु-विभक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well divided, well proportioned.<BR>—सु-<BR>विभक्त-गात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, having well divided or<BR>symmetrical limbs.<BR>—सु-विभात, अस्, आ, अम्, shin-<BR>ing splendidly, very bright.<BR>—सु-विभीषण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, very frightful.<BR>—सु-विभु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—सु-विलय, अस्, आ, अम्, easily fusible, lique-<BR>fying.<BR>—सु-विवृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very extensive<BR>or extended, everywhere abundant.<BR>—सु-विश्रब्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very confident.<BR>—सु-विश्वस्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very confiding; very trusty, confidential.<BR>—सु-<BR>विषण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, very sorrowful.<BR>—सु-विस्तरम्,<BR>ind. very diffusely or fully, at length.<BR>—सु-विस्तीर्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well spread or laid out; very broad.<BR>—सु-विस्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, very astonished.<BR>—सु-<BR>विहित, अस्, आ, अम्, well placed or deposited; well<BR>furnished or appointed, well provided, well arranged,<BR>well supplied; well done, well performed.<BR>—सु-वीज,<BR>अम्, n. good seed; (अस्, आ, अम्), having good seed;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Śiva; the poppy (= खस्खस).<BR>—सु-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having many heroes;<BR>having excellent offspring; (अस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Śiva; of a son of Kṣemya; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—सु-वीरक, अम्, n. a collyrium prepared<BR>from the Amomum Anthorhizon (= सौवीराञ्जन).<BR>—सु-वीराम्ल (˚र-अम्˚), अम्, n. sour rice-gruel.<BR>—सु-वीर्य, अम्, n. great vigour, heroism; abun-<BR>dance of heroes; (अस्, आ, अम्), having great vigour<BR>or power; of heroic strength; having good essence<BR>or seed; (आ), f. wild cotton; (अम्), n. the fruit of<BR>the jujube.<BR>—सु-वृक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. well trimmed,<BR>having excellent purity; (इस्), f. a pure offering; a<BR>hymn of praise, hymn.<BR>—सु-वृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. easy<BR>rolling, well turning; well built (said of a chariot;<BR>Sāy. = शोभन-वर्तन or सु-चक्र, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>111, 1).<BR>—सु-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, virtuous, good;<BR>well rounded, beautifully globular or round; a kind<BR>of plant, = शूरण; (आ), f. a kind of plant (=<BR>शत-पत्त्री); a sort of grape (= काकली-द्राक्षा);<BR>a particular metre.<BR>—सु-वृत्ति, इस्, f. a good way of<BR>living.<BR>—सु-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, full-grown; (अस्),<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—सु-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, or सु-वृध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. well increasing, full-grown.<BR>—सु-वृश्च्,<BR>वृट्, ट्, ट्, cutting well, (Vopa-deva III. 148.)<BR>—सु-<BR>वृष्ट, अम्, n. beautiful rain.<BR>—सु-वेगा, f. a kind<BR>of plant (= महा-ज्योतिष्मती).<BR>—सु-वेदन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. easy to be found.<BR>—सु-वेदस्, आस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 147<BR>(having the patronymic Śairīṣi).<BR>—सु-वेम, अस्, m.<BR>a good loom.<BR>—सु-वेल, अस्, आ, अम्, bowed or stoop-<BR>ing greatly; humble, quiet; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>mountain (= त्रि-कूट).<BR>—सु-वेश or सु-वेष, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well dressed, well clad; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>sugar-cane (= श्वेतेक्षु).<BR>—सु-वेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, well<BR>dressed, well ornamented or decorated.<BR>—सु-व्यक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very plain, manifest; (अम्), ind. very<BR>evidently or clearly, most distinctly.<BR>—सु-व्यस्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, greatly dispersed, much scattered, strag-<BR>gling (said of an army).<BR>—सु-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>strict in observing a religious vow or obligation,<BR>strictly religious or virtuous; (अस्), m. a religious<BR>student; N. of a king; of the twentieth Arhat of<BR>the present Avasarpiṇī, (also called Muni-suvrata);<BR>of the eleventh Arhat of the future Utsarpiṇī; (आ),<BR>f. a virtuous wife; a cow easily milked or one of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1125-a" target="_blank">Page1125-a+ 81</a>]<BR>tractable disposition; N. of the mother of the<BR>fifteenth Jina of the present age.<BR>—सु-शंस, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having praise, enjoying good report, well spoken<BR>of, praiseworthy, glorious.<BR>—सु-शक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>capable of being easily done.<BR>—सु-शक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. displaying great prowess.<BR>—सु-शमी, m., Ved.<BR>one who does mighty deeds; sacrificing well; (ई),<BR>ind. for the sake of an auspicious rite (= सु-कर्म-<BR>त्वाय, Ṛg-veda V. 87, 9).<BR>—सु-शरण, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n., Ved. a good protector, a noble refuge.<BR>—सु-<BR>शर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, well destroying (enemies); pro-<BR>tecting well, sheltering; enjoying great happiness or<BR>prosperity, very happy; (आ), m., N. of a king; of a<BR>wicked Brāhman.<BR>—सु-शल्य, अस्, m. the Khadira<BR>tree.<BR>—सु-शवी, f. the gourd Momordica Charantia;<BR>a sort of black cumin, Nigella Indica (= कृष्ण-<BR>जीरक).<BR>—सु-शस्ति, इस्, f., Ved. a beautiful hymn,<BR>hymn of praise.<BR>—सु-शाक, अस्, m. ‘good herb,’ epi-<BR>thet of various plants, = चञ्चु; = भिण्डा; = तण्-<BR>डुलीय; (अम्), n. undried ginger.<BR>—सु-शान्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, very placid; (आ), f., N. of the wife of king<BR>Śaśi-dhvaja.<BR>—सुशान्त-तोय, अस्, आ, अम्, having very<BR>placid water.<BR>—सु-शान्ति, इस्, m., N. of the Indra of<BR>the third Manv-antara; of a king.<BR>—सु-शारद, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a preceptor; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-शासन,<BR>अम्, n. good government.<BR>—सु-शासित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well-governed or regulated, kept under good discipline.<BR>—सु-शिक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, well trained or taught, dis-<BR>ciplined.<BR>—सु-शिख, अस्, आ, अम्, having beautiful<BR>points or crests; (अस्), m. ‘possessing beautiful flames,’<BR>N. of Agni or fire; (आ), f. a peacock's crest; cock's<BR>comb.<BR>—सु-शिप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, or सु-शिप्रिन्, ई, इणि,<BR>इ, Ved. having a handsome chin; having beautiful<BR>cheeks.<BR>—सु-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having a fine head.<BR>—सु-शिश्वि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. much enlarged, (Sāy. =<BR>सुष्ठु प्रवर्धित, Ṛg-veda I. 65, 2.)<BR>—सु-<BR>शिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, governing well; (अस्), m. a faith-<BR>ful minister or counsellor.<BR>—सु-शीत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very cold or cooling; (अस्), m. a kind of dwarf<BR>Plaksha tree; (आ), f. a particular plant, = शत-पत्-<BR>त्री; (अम्), n. great coldness; a kind of fragrant<BR>yellow sandal-wood.<BR>—सु-शीतल, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>cold or cooling, frigid, freezing; (अम्), n. a sort of<BR>fragrant grass (= गन्ध-तृण).<BR>—सु-शीम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, easy to be attained, (according to a commentator<BR>= सु-प्राप; cf. दुः-शीम); well-disposed (for सु-<BR>शील, according to some); cold, frigid [cf. सु-षीम];<BR>(अस्), m. cold, coldness.<BR>—सु-शील, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well-disposed, good tempered, having an amiable<BR>disposition; well conducted, well made, well shaped;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of king Cola; (आ), f. epithet of<BR>Yama's wife; of one of Kṛṣṇa's eight wives; of a<BR>daughter of Hari-svāmin.<BR>—सुशील-ता, f. or सुशील-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. excellence of temper or disposition, good<BR>morals, natural amiability.<BR>—सु-शीविका, f. a kind of<BR>bulbous root or plant (= वाराही-कन्द).<BR>—सु-शुक्-<BR>वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. shining brightly, brilliant.<BR>—सु-शेव, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing good fortune,<BR>blessed; granting prosperity, auspicious, propitious,<BR>favourable.<BR>—सु-शोक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining<BR>brightly, (said of Agni; Sāy. = शोभन-दीप्ति, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 70, 1.)<BR>—सु-श्चन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, (for सु-<BR>चन्द्र), beautifully shining.<BR>—सु-श्रवस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. abounding in glory, famous; prosperous;<BR>having good oblations; (आस्), m., N. of a Prajā-pati;<BR>of a preceptor.<BR>—सु-श्राव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, distinctly<BR>audible; pleasing to the ear.<BR>—सु-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved.<BR>abounding in good fortune or prosperity.<BR>—सु-श्रीक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, possessing good fortune or great pros-<BR>perity, greatly blessed or happy; (आ), f. the gum<BR>olibanum tree.<BR>—सु-श्रुण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very<BR>famous, (Sāy. = सु-प्रसिद्ध.)<BR>—सु-श्रुत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. hearing well; having a good reputation, (Sāy.<BR>= सु-श्रवस्.)<BR>—सु-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, well heard;<BR>versed in the Vedas; (अस्), m., N. of a king; of an<BR>author of a system of medicine (son of Viśvā-mitra<BR>and descendant of Dhanvan-tari; his work with<BR>that of Caraka, another older medical authority, is<BR>held in great esteem, and consists of six books); (अम्),<BR>n. ‘may it be well heard!’ an exclamation used at<BR>a Śrāddha; [cf. श्रौषट्.]<BR>—सुश्रुत-संहिता, f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1125-b" target="_blank">Page1125-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Su-śruta's system of medicine.<BR>—सु-श्रोणि, इस्, इस्, or ई,<BR>इ, having beautiful hips, καλλίπυγος; (इस्), f., N.<BR>of a goddess.<BR>—सु-श्रोतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. well or<BR>altogether hearing, (Sāy. = संयक् श्रोतृ, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 122, 6.)<BR>—सु-श्लक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, very smooth.<BR>—सु-श्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, closely united or adhering.<BR>—सु-श्लेष, अस्, m. close or intimate union; a<BR>close embrace.<BR>—सु-षंसद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. having<BR>a good meeting; [cf. सु-संसद्.]<BR>—सु-षखि, खा,<BR>m., Ved. a good friend.<BR>—सु-षण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. easy to be acquired; to be liberally distributed.<BR>—सु-षणन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having beautiful<BR>gifts; liberally distributed.<BR>—सु-षद्मन्, आ, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—सु-षम, अस्, आ, अम्, very even, very<BR>beautiful or handsome, very pleasing; same, all; (आ),<BR>f. exquisite beauty; a particular Jaina division of<BR>time, (the second Ara or spoke of a time-wheel con-<BR>taining six such divisions; it is supposed to be a<BR>period in which steady happiness is enjoyed by man-<BR>kind; sometimes written सु-खमा.)<BR>—सु-षमिध्,<BR>त्, m., Ved. ‘lighting or igniting well,’ epithet of<BR>Agni.<BR>—सु-षमिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, beautifully kin-<BR>dled or lighted.<BR>—सु-षवी, f. a sort of gourd, Mo-<BR>mordica Charantia (or a small species); black cumin,<BR>Nigella Indica; cumin-seed; [cf. सु-शवी.]<BR>—सु-<BR>षह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having excellent strength.<BR>—सु-षाढ, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-षामन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, having good conciliation, sweet or kindly<BR>spoken; N. of a king, (Ṛg-veda VIII. 26, 2.)<BR>—सु-षारथि, इस्, m., Ved. a good charioteer.<BR>—सु-षीम, अस्, आ, अम्, cold, frigid; pleasant,<BR>agreeable; (अस्), m. cold; a sort of snake; the Can-<BR>dra-kānta or moon gem.<BR>—सु-षुत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. beautifully pressed (said of Soma).<BR>—सु-षुप्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fast asleep; (अम्), n. deep or profound<BR>sleep.<BR>—सुषुप्त-वत्, ind. like one who is fast<BR>asleep.<BR>—सु-षुप्ति, इस्, f. deep sleep, profound re-<BR>pose; (in phil.) entire insensibility (or spiritual<BR>ignorance (= सत्त्व-प्रधानम् अज्ञानम् and,<BR>according to Śabda-k., equivalent to कारण-शरीर<BR>and आनन्द-मय-कोष, q. q. v. v.).<BR>—सु-षुमत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. very beautiful.<BR>—सु-षुम्ण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. rich in pleasure or happiness, highly<BR>blessed; (अस्), m., N. of one of the seven prin-<BR>cipal rays of the sun (supposed to supply heat to<BR>the moon); (आ), f. a particular artery or vessel<BR>of the body lying between the vessels called इडा<BR>and पिङ्गला, and supposed to be one of the pas-<BR>sages for the breath or spirit, (see ब्रह्म-रन्-<BR>ध्र.)<BR>—सु-षूतम, अस्, आ, अम्, (i. e. सु-सूतम<BR>= सु-सुततम), = अतिशयेन सु-सुत, (Vājasa-<BR>neyi-s. VI. 30.)<BR>—सु-षेण, अस्, m. (i. e. सु + सेना),<BR>‘having beautiful clusters,’ the Kara-marda tree; a<BR>cane or reed, the ratan; ‘having a good army,’ epi-<BR>thet of Viṣṇu; N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of<BR>a son of Vasu-deva; of a son of Vṛṣṇi-mat; of a<BR>son of Kṛṣṇa; of a monkey-chief, son of Varuṇa, (see<BR>हनु-मत्); (ई), f. the plant Convolvulus Turpe-<BR>thum (= त्रि-वृत्).<BR>—सु-षेणिका, f. a kind of dark<BR>Tri-vṛt or Convolvulus Turpethum.<BR>—सु-षोमा, f.,<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—सु-ष्टुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well<BR>praised.<BR>—सु-ष्टुति, इस्, f. a beautiful hymn, excellent<BR>praise; (इस्, इस्, इ), having a beautiful hymn,<BR>—सु-<BR>ष्टुभ्, प्, प्, प्, Ved. praising well, lauding, extol-<BR>ling.<BR>—सु-संयत, अस्, आ, अम्, well restrained, well<BR>composed.<BR>—सु-संरब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, very angry,<BR>greatly enraged or agitated.<BR>—सु-संवीत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well clothed or dressed.<BR>—सु-संवृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well covered or veiled, well wrapped up.<BR>—सु-<BR>संशित, अस्, आ, अम्, very sharp.<BR>—सु-संसद्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, Ved. having a good company or assembly.<BR>—सु-<BR>संस्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, well perfected or completed,<BR>well polished, highly finished; highly seasoned, well-<BR>cooked.<BR>—सुसंस्कृतोपस्कर (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who carefully polishes or cleanses the house-<BR>hold utensils.<BR>—सु-संस्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, well situ-<BR>ated; standing firmly, doing well; well brought<BR>together, circumscribed.<BR>—सु-संहत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well compacted, well knit together.<BR>—सु-संहित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well united.<BR>—सुसंहित-प्रमाण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having well united principals or chiefs.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1125-c" target="_blank">Page1125-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—सु-सक्थ, सु-सक्थि, see Vopa-deva VI. 25.<BR>—सु-सङ्काश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a beautiful<BR>appearance, fair, handsome.<BR>—सु-सङ्क्षेप, अस्, m.<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-सङ्गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>kept or preserved; well abridged.<BR>—सु-सत्कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well or hospitably received, highly honoured,<BR>treated with great hospitality.<BR>—सु-सत्या, f., N. of<BR>the wife of king Janaka.<BR>—सु-सदृश, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>very like.<BR>—सु-सनितृ, ता, m. a liberal giver,<BR>generous benefactor.<BR>—सु-सन्त्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>greatly alarmed.<BR>—सु-सन्दृश्, क्, क्, क्, having a<BR>pleasing aspect, agreeable to look at.<BR>—सु-सन्धि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—सु-सन्धित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>well reconciled.<BR>—सु-सन्नत, अस्, आ, अम्, well di-<BR>rected (said of an arrow).<BR>—सु-समाहित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very intent or attentive, having the mind intently<BR>fixed or absorbed on a subject or object.<BR>—सु-समिद्-<BR>ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. thoroughly well kindled, well<BR>lighted (said of Agni).<BR>—सु-समुब्ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. much contracted or shriveled up, much<BR>shrunk.<BR>—सु-समृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very pros-<BR>perous; quite perfect.<BR>—सु-सम्पद्, त्, f. good for-<BR>tune, prosperity.<BR>—सु-सम्पिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, much<BR>crushed or shattered.<BR>—सु-सम्बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>joined.<BR>—सु-सम्भ्रम, अस्, m. great haste, confusion;<BR>great respect or reverence.<BR>—सु-सम्भ्रान्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, greatly bewildered.<BR>—सु-सम्मत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>much honoured, highly approved.<BR>—सु-सम्मृष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well rubbed, well cleaned (said of<BR>horses).<BR>—सु-सरण, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-<BR>सर्तू, ऊस्, f., Ved., N. of a river.<BR>—सु-सर्व, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. quite complete.<BR>—सु-सवी, f. = सु-षवी-<BR>—सु-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be borne or suf-<BR>fered; bearing or enduring well; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—सु-सामन्, अ, n. good negotiation.<BR>—सु-<BR>सार, अस्, m. good essence, good sap, good sub-<BR>stance; competence; (अस्, आ, अम्), having good es-<BR>sence or sap; (अस्), m. the red-flowering Khadira,<BR>Mimosa Catechu.<BR>—सु-सार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, hav-<BR>ing good essence or substance; (अत्), n. crystal.<BR>—सु-सिकता, f. good sand; gravel; sugar.<BR>—सु-<BR>सिद्धार्थ (˚ध-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>object is completely effected, completely supplied<BR>with.<BR>—सु-सीमा, f. a good boundary; good con-<BR>duct; N. of the mother of the sixth Arhat.<BR>—सु-<BR>सुखम्, ind. very happily.<BR>—सु-सूक्ष्म, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very subtle or minute, very small, very delicate.<BR>—सु-सेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, well served, much addicted<BR>to.<BR>—सु-स्त्री, f. a good wife.<BR>—सु-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well situated, being well or in good condition,<BR>in health, healthy, faring well, prosperous, well off,<BR>in good circumstances, happy.<BR>—सुस्थ-ता, f. or<BR>सुस्थ-त्व, अम्, n. the being well or well-established,<BR>health, welfare, happiness, good or easy circum-<BR>stances.<BR>—सुस्थय, Nom. P. सुस्थयति, &c., to<BR>establish or settle well.<BR>—सुस्थयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्,<BR>settling well, setting at rest, appeasing.<BR>—सुस्था-<BR>वती, f., N. of a particular scale in music.<BR>—सु-स्थित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well-established, being well or in good<BR>condition, in good health; living well or happily.<BR>—सुस्थित-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, being in a happy<BR>frame of mind, contented.<BR>—सुस्थितम्-मन्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, fancying one's self prosperous or well off.<BR>—सु-स्थिति, इस्, f. a good condition, good circum-<BR>stances or position, well-being, welfare; health, con-<BR>valescence.<BR>—सु-स्थिर, अस्, आ, अम्, very firm or<BR>steady, stable; resolute, cool.<BR>—सु-स्ना (perhaps more<BR>properly written सुस्ना), a kind of pulse, Lathyrus<BR>Sativus.<BR>—सु-स्नात, अस्, आ, अम्, well bathed (some-<BR>times used as a benedictory term addressed to a per-<BR>son about to bathe); one who has duly performed<BR>his ablutions, a student who has performed his ablu-<BR>tions in preparation for or after a sacrifice.<BR>—सु-<BR>स्निग्ध-गम्भीर, अस्, आ, अम्, very soft and deep-<BR>toned.<BR>—सु-स्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasantly smiling;<BR>(आ), f. a woman with a pleasing or smiling counte-<BR>nance.<BR>—सु-स्वप्न, अस्, m. a good or lucky<BR>dream; ‘having good dreams,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सु-स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, well-sounding, harmonious,<BR>melodious; having a loud voice, loud; (अम्), ind.<BR>in a loud voice.<BR>—सु-स्वरु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. going<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1126-a" target="_blank">Page1126-a+ 81</a>]<BR>well; well praised, (Sāy. = शोभन-गमन or शो-<BR>भन-स्तुतिक, Ṛg-veda V. 44, 5.)<BR>—सु-स्वान्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a good or happy mind, well-dis-<BR>posed.<BR>—सु-हन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. easy to be killed,<BR>to be killed gloriously.<BR>—सु-हन्तु, Ved. ‘killing<BR>easily,’ a thunderbolt, (Sāy. सु-हन्तु = सुहन्तुना<BR>वज्रेन, Ṛg-veda VII. 19, 4.)<BR>—सु-हव, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. well or easily invoked, to be well invoked.<BR>—सु-हविस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having or offering beau-<BR>tiful oblations, devout, pious.<BR>—सु-हसानन (˚स-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a cheerful smiling face.<BR>—सु-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having beautiful or<BR>skilful hands, skilful-handed, clever; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—सु-हस्तिन्, ई, m. (also<BR>written सु-हस्ति according to some), one of the Jaina<BR>saints called Daśa-pūrvins; [cf. महा-गिरि, वज्र.]<BR>—सु-हस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having beautiful<BR>hands; skilful-handed, clever, skilful, (in Ṛg-veda I.<BR>64, 1. सु-हस्त्य = कृताञ्जलि, having folded hands);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X.<BR>41 (having the patronymic Ghauṣeya).<BR>—सु-हार्द्,<BR>m., Ved. = सु-हृद्, a friend, (see Atharva-veda III. 28,<BR>5, 6; VI. 120, 3.)<BR>—सु-हिंस्, हिन्, न्, न्, one who<BR>strikes well.<BR>—सु-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, very fit or suit-<BR>able; salutary, beneficial, good; very friendly, affec-<BR>tionate; satiated, satisfied; (आ), f. one of the tongues<BR>of Agni or fire.<BR>—सु-हिरण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing beautiful gold, abounding in gold.<BR>—सुहृच्-<BR>छोक-विवर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, augmenting the grief<BR>of a friend.<BR>—सुहृज्-जन, अस्, m. a friendly person,<BR>friend.<BR>—सुहृत्-कुल, अम्, n. a company or family<BR>of friends.<BR>—सुहृत्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, very friendly<BR>or cordial, kind, affectionate.<BR>—सुहृत्-ता, f. or सु-<BR>हृत्-त्व, अम्, n. friendship, friendliness, affection.<BR>—सुहृत्-त्याग, अस्, m. the desertion of a friend.<BR>—सु-हृद्, त्, त्, त्, having a kind heart, cordial,<BR>friendly, affectionate, loving; (त्), m. a friend, (किं-<BR>सुहृद्, a bad friend); an ally; N. of the fourth<BR>Lagna, (see लग्न.)<BR>—सु-हृद, a friend, (see the<BR>next.)<BR>—सुहृद-द्रुह्, -ध्रुक् or -ध्रुट्, injuring<BR>a friend, one who smites a friend secretly.<BR>—सु-<BR>हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, good-hearted, well-disposed,<BR>affectionate.<BR>—सुहृद्-बल, अम्, n. the army of an<BR>ally.<BR>—सुहृद्-भेद, अस्, m. the separation of<BR>friends; N. of the second book of the Hitopadeśa.<BR>—सुहृद्-वध, अस्, m. killing a friend, (Manu<BR>XI. 56.)<BR>—सुहृद्-वाक्य, अम्, n. the speech of a<BR>friend; a friend's advice.<BR>—सुहृल्-लिङ्गधर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the mere appearance of a friend.<BR>—सु-<BR>होतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. abounding in priests; (ता),<BR>m., N. of one of the five sons of Vitatha.<BR>—सु-<BR>होत्र, अस्, m., N. of the author of the hymns Ṛg-<BR>veda VI. 31, 32 (having the patronymic Bhārad-<BR>vāja); N. of a son of king Vṛhad-ishu of the lunar<BR>race; of a son of Kāñcana; of a son of Bhumanyu;<BR>of several other persons; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a sect of<BR>fire-worshippers.<BR>—सूक्त (सु-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>spoken, well or properly said; (आ), f. a kind of bird,<BR>the Śārikā, q. v.; (अम्), n. a Vedic metrical prayer<BR>or hymn, (the Sūkta is properly a whole hymn as<BR>distinguished from a Ṛc or single verse of a Vedic<BR>hymn, the term Mantra, q. v., being still more com-<BR>prehensive; but many other words are loosely used<BR>for hymns of the Veda, e. g. अर्क, उक्थ, ऋच्, गिर्,<BR>धी, नीथ, नि-विद्, मति, स्तोत्र, स्तोम, वाच्, वचस्,<BR>&c.)<BR>—सूक्तदर्शि-त्व, अम्, n. the seeing or com-<BR>posing of Vedic hymns, the being a seer or Ṛṣi.<BR>—सूक्त-दर्शिन्, ई, m. or सूक्त-द्रष्टृ, टा, m.<BR>a hymn-seer, the author of a Sūkta or Vedic hymn,<BR>a Ṛṣi (to whom a Sūkta is revealed).<BR>—सूक्त-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, one who has a hymn or hymns (of<BR>the Veda addressed to his honour).<BR>—सूक्त-वाक,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. praise-speaking, a hymn; a particular<BR>ceremony.<BR>—सूक्त-वाच्, क्, f. a word of praise,<BR>praise, hymn.<BR>—सूक्तासि (˚त-असि), इस्, m. the<BR>sword of pleasant speech.<BR>—सूक्ति (सु-उक्˚), इस्, f.<BR>good speech, friendly speech.<BR>—सूक्ति-सहस्र,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—सूत्तर (सु-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very superior; well towards the north, northern.<BR>—सूत्थान (सु-उत्˚), अम्, n. good effort or exer-<BR>tion, active effort; (अस्, आ, अम्), making good effort,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1126-b" target="_blank">Page1126-b+ 81</a>]<BR>clever.<BR>—सू-नृत, see s. v.<BR>—सून्मद or सून्माद<BR>(सु-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, quite mad.<BR>—सूपतीर्थ (सु-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having good steps for bathing.<BR>—सूपवञ्चन (सु-उप्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. easily<BR>deceiving.<BR>—सूपसदन (सु-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>easy to be approached.<BR>—सूपस्कर (सु-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with good instruments.<BR>—सू-<BR>पस्थ (सु-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. granting good<BR>help, rich in help.<BR>—सूपायन (सु-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having easy approach, easy of access.<BR>—सू-<BR>भर्व, see s. v.<BR>—सू-यवस, अम्, n., Ved. = सु-<BR>यवस, a good pasture; (अस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Ajīgarta.<BR>—सूयवसाद् (˚स-अद्), त्, त्, त्, Ved. eat-<BR>ing abundance of grass or fodder.<BR>—सू-यवसिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, Ved. having good pasturage.<BR>—१. सूर्मि (सु-<BR>ऊर्˚), इस्, इस्, इ (for 2. सूर्मि, see s. v.), Ved. having<BR>mightly waves, billowy, surging.<BR>—स्व्-अक्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>or ई, अम्, handsome-eyed; having good or keen<BR>organs, acute; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—स्व्-<BR>अग्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a good fire.<BR>—स्व्-अङ्ग, अम्,<BR>n. a good or handsome limb; (अस्, ई, अम्), hand-<BR>some-limbed, well-shaped, handsome.<BR>—स्व्-अङ्गुरि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. handsome-fingered.<BR>—स्व्-अच्छ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, very transparent or clear, pellucid, crystalline;<BR>white; pure, stainless; healthy, sound, convalescent;<BR>(अस्), m. crystal; (आ), f. white Dūrvā grass; (अम्),<BR>n. a pearl; pure chalk, &c. (= विमलोपरस).<BR>—स्व्-<BR>अच्छक, अस्, इका, अम्, = स्व्-अच्छ above.<BR>—स्वच्-<BR>छ-ता, f. or स्वच्छ-त्व, अम्, n. great transparency<BR>or purity.<BR>—स्वच्छ-द्रव्य, अम्, n. the crystalline<BR>humour.<BR>—स्वच्छ-पत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘transparent<BR>leaf,’ talc.<BR>—स्वच्छ-बालुक, अम्, n. pure chalk, &c.<BR>(= विमलोपरस).<BR>—स्वच्छ-मणि, इस्, m. ‘clear-<BR>gem,’ crystal.<BR>—स्व्-अञ्च्, अङ्, &c., Ved. going well,<BR>gracefully moving, stepping well (said of horses),<BR>swift, rapid, (in Nirukta V. 7. स्व्-अञ्चाः occurs.) — 1. स्व्-<BR>अदित, अस्, आ, अम्, well eaten, (see 2. स्वदित.)<BR>—स्व्-<BR>अधिष्ठान, अस्, आ, अम्, having a solid foundation<BR>or framework (said of a chariot &c.).<BR>—स्व्-अधीत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well read, well versed in or conversant<BR>with.<BR>—स्व्-अध्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, quite uninjured;<BR>having beautiful sacrifices, propitious for sacrifice<BR>(Ved.).<BR>—स्व्-अनीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having beauti-<BR>ful lustre, very radiant (said of Agni).<BR>—स्व्-अनुगुप्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well guarded, well secured, well hidden.<BR>—स्व्-अनुरूप, अस्, आ, अम्, well suited.<BR>—स्व्-अनु-<BR>ष्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, well observed, duly practised or<BR>performed.<BR>—स्व्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having a good end,<BR>terminating well.<BR>—१. स्व्-अप्, see Vopa-deva III. 168, (for<BR>rt. 2. स्वप् see s. v.)<BR>—स्व्-अपत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having many descendants, prolific.<BR>—स्व्-अपराद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very faulty.<BR>—स्व्-अपस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. ac-<BR>complishing excellent works, skilful, energetic.<BR>—स्व-<BR>पस्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most skilful.<BR>—स्व्-अपस्या,<BR>f., Ved. desire of performing a good work, wish to do<BR>good.<BR>—स्व्-अपिवात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. easy to be gained<BR>or obtained, (see rt. 2. वत्.)<BR>—स्व्-अभिष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>having good protection, (Sāy. = शोभनाभ्येषण-<BR>वत् or शोभनाभिगमन, Ṛg-veda I. 51, 2.)<BR>—स्व्-अभीशु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having beautiful reins<BR>or bridles.<BR>—स्व्-अरङ्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well<BR>ordered, well arranged.<BR>—स्व्-अरित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having good oars, well rowed.<BR>—स्व्-अर्क, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. flashing beautifully; rich in praise, resounding<BR>with beautiful songs.<BR>—स्व्-अलक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, alto-<BR>gether unseen, not thoroughly observed.<BR>—स्व्-अलङ्-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, well adorned, highly decorated.<BR>—स्व्-<BR>अलङ्कृत्य, ind. having well adorned.<BR>—स्व्-अल्प,<BR>स्वल्पक, see s. v., p. 1161.<BR>—स्व्-अवस्, अस्, n., Ved.<BR>good protection; (आस्, आस्, अस्), well protecting, affording<BR>favourable assistance.<BR>—स्व्-अवेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, well<BR>considered; well cared for.<BR>—स्व्-अश्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>possessing excellent horses; (अस्), m., Ved., N. of a<BR>king (said to have been the father of Sūrya, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 61, 15).<BR>—स्वश्वयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desiring beau-<BR>tiful horses, fond of good horses, (Sāy. = कल्याणम्<BR>अश्वम् इच्छन्, Ṛg-veda VIII. 45, 7.)<BR>—स्व्-अश्व्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. consisting of beautiful horses.<BR>—स्व्-<BR>असितायत-लोचन (˚त-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having very<BR>black and long eyes.<BR>—स्व्-अस्ति, स्वस्तिक, &c., see<BR>s. v.<BR>—स्व्-आकार, अस्, आ, अम्, well formed, well<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1126-c" target="_blank">Page1126-c+ 79</a>]<BR>shaped, handsome.<BR>—१. स्व्-आगत, अम्, n. (for 2.<BR>स्वागत see s. v.), welcome, salutation; (आ), f. a species<BR>of the Triṣṭubh metre.<BR>—स्वागत-वचन, अम्, n.<BR>the uttering of welcome, the word welcome.<BR>—स्व्-<BR>आगती-कृत्य, ind. having made into a welcome,<BR>giving (to a cry) the sound of ‘welcome.’<BR>—स्व्-<BR>आचार, अस्, आ, अम्, well-behaved.<BR>—स्व्-आजीव्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, yielding an easy subsistence.<BR>—स्व्-आदान, अम्,<BR>n. the act of taking anything justly or properly,<BR>(Manu VIII. 172.)<BR>—स्व्-आधी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. well-<BR>minded [cf. दुर्-आधी]; thoughtful, contemplative,<BR>meditating, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X. 61, 7.<BR>स्व्-आध्यण् = सु-ध्यानाः or सु-कर्माणः.)<BR>—स्व्-<BR>आपि, इस्, m., Ved. a good ally or relation, (perhaps for<BR>स्व-आपि.)<BR>—स्व्-आभास, अस्, आ, अम्, very illustrious or<BR>splendid, (Kirāt. XV. 22.)<BR>—स्व्-आभू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved.<BR>being well or beautifully present, being happily near<BR>at hand.<BR>—स्व्-आयस, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. made of good<BR>iron.<BR>—स्व्-आयुज्, see s. v.<BR>—स्व्-आयुध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having good weapons.<BR>—स्व्-आराधित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, well or easily propitiated, made very propitious.<BR>—स्व्-आराध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be propitiated.<BR>—स्व्-आशित, अस्, आ, अम्, well fed, well eaten.<BR>—स्व्-<BR>आशिस्, ईस्, &c., Ved. having beautiful prayers.<BR>—स्व्-<BR>आ-श्लिष्, cl. 4. P. -श्लिष्यति, &c., to embrace firmly<BR>or closely, (Manu XI. 103.)<BR>—स्व्-आसीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sitting at ease, comfortably seated.<BR>—स्व्-आस्तीर्ण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, well spread.<BR>—स्व्-आहार, अस्, m. good food;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), easy to be brought or procured.<BR>—१. स्व्-<BR>आहुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well honoured (by offerings<BR>&c.).<BR>—२. स्व्-आहुत, अस्, आ, अम्, (see rt. ह्वे), well or<BR>properly invoked.<BR>—स्व्-इध्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>bright-faced, bright-edged (said of a hatchet; Sāy.<BR>= सु-दीप्तास्य or सूर्य-किरणैः सु-दीप्त, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 121, 7).<BR>—स्व्-इषु, उस्, उस्, उ, having ex-<BR>cellent arrows.<BR>—स्व्-इष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, well or pro-<BR>perly sacrificed, completely sacrificed.<BR>—स्विष्ट-कृत्,<BR>त्, m. ‘causing good sacrifice,’ a form of Fire, (Manu<BR>III. 86); epithet of particular sacred texts.<BR>—स्व्-<BR>औपश, अस्, आ, अम् (औपश = ओपश), Ved. having<BR>beautiful locks of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकम्
सुकम्, ind. = 5. सु, (Naigh. III. 12.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्ठु
सुष्ठु, ind. (fr. सु + स्थु fr. rt. 1. स्था; accord-<BR>ing to some ष्ठु = स्तु is merely an affix), well, excel-<BR>lently, beautifully; much, very, exceedingly; truly.<BR>—सुष्ठु-वह् or सुष्ठु-वाह्, -वाट्, ट्, ट्, Ved.<BR>carrying well, bearing along rapidly (said of horses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्
सुख् सुख् (perhaps to be regarded as a<BR>Nominal fr. सुख below), cl. 10. 4. P.<BR>सुखयति, सुख्यति, &c., to make happy, please,<BR>delight, rejoice, comfort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख|सुखं
सुख, अम्, n. (said to be fr. 5. सु + 3. ख, q. v.,<BR>cf. दुःख), happiness, pleasure, delight, joy, com-<BR>fort; prosperity; ease, alleviation; easiness; heaven,<BR>paradise; water (in Naigh. I. 12. enumerated among<BR>the उदक-नामानि); epithet of the fourth astro-<BR>logical house; the drug or medicinal root called<BR>Vṛddhi; (अस्, आ, अम्), happy, joyful, delighted;<BR>agreeable, sweet; virtuous, pious; easy, practicable;<BR>meet, suitable; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Dharma;<BR>(आ), f. the capital of Varuṇa; (अम्), ind. happily,<BR>joyfully; well, (सुखम् आस्ताम् भवान्, may your<BR>honour be well! farewell!); placidly; willingly, rather<BR>(followed by न पुनर्); comfortably; easily;<BR>(एन), ind. with pleasure, pleasantly, joyfully; easily;<BR>[cf. Hib. sogh, ‘prosperity, ease, pleasure.’]<BR>—सुख-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing happiness or pleasure;<BR>doing anything easily, done easily.<BR>—सुख-कार =<BR>सुख-कर above.<BR>—सुख-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, or सुख-<BR>गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going easily.<BR>—सुख-ग्राह्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, easy to be grasped; easy to be comprehended<BR>or understood.<BR>—सुखग्राह्य-निबन्धन, अम्,<BR>n. a composition or construction easy to be compre-<BR>hended, easily intelligible language.<BR>—सुखङ्-कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, causing happiness or pleasure; (ई), f. the<BR>plant Jīvantī.<BR>—सुख-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going or<BR>moving easily; (अस्), m. a particular Grāma.<BR>—सु-<BR>ख-चार, अस्, m. ‘going easily,’ a good horse.<BR>—सुख-च्छेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be cut; easily<BR>destroyed.<BR>—सुख-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born or pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-a" target="_blank">Page1127-a+ 81</a>]<BR>duced easily; conscious of pleasure, feeling pleasure,<BR>happy.<BR>—सुख-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most happy, very<BR>pleasant or agreeable.<BR>—सुख-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving<BR>or affording pleasure, &c.; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; a particular kind of musical time or measure;<BR>(आ), f. the river Ganges; a courtezan of Indra's<BR>heaven (= स्वर्ग-वेश्या); the Śamī tree; (अम्), n.<BR>the seat of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सुख-दुःख, ए, n. du.<BR>pleasure and pain.<BR>—सुखदुःखात्मक (˚ख-<BR>आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, consisting of pleasure and pain.<BR>—सुख-दोह्या, f. a cow easily milked; [cf.<BR>सुख-सन्दुह्या.]<BR>—सुख-पुण्याह-घोष,<BR>अस्, m. the proclamation of a happy holiday.<BR>—सुखप्रतिबन्धि-ता, f. the prevention or inter-<BR>ruption of happiness.<BR>—सुख-प्रतिबन्धिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, obstructing or interrupting happiness.<BR>—सु-<BR>ख-प्रतीक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, looking for or expecting<BR>happiness, hoping for pleasure.<BR>—सुख-प्रबो-<BR>धक, अस्, इका, अम्, easy to understand.<BR>—सुख-<BR>प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has attained happiness.<BR>—सुख-प्राप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easily attainable.<BR>—सुख-बोध, अस्, m. perception or sensation of<BR>pleasure; easy teaching, easy knowledge.<BR>—सुख-<BR>भाग, अस्, m. a happy lot or portion, good fortune.<BR>—सुखभागिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a happy lot or<BR>portion, happy, prosperous.<BR>—सुख-भाज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>possessing or enjoying happiness; embracing a loved<BR>object (= इष्ट-परिष्वङ्ग).<BR>—सुख-भेद्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, easily broken or disunited, fragile,<BR>brittle.<BR>—सुख-भोग, अस्, m. the enjoyment of<BR>pleasure.<BR>—सुख-भोगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, enjoying pleasure.<BR>—सुख-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of happiness,<BR>full of joy or pleasure.<BR>—सुख-मोदा, f. the gum<BR>olibanum tree.<BR>—सुख-राज, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—सुख-रात्रि, इस्, or सुख-रात्रिका, f. a particular<BR>night of new moon (when there is a festival in honour<BR>of Lakṣmī, celebrated with lighted lamps); a night<BR>when a wife may be legally approached; [cf.<BR>Manu III. 47.]<BR>—सुख-लक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, easy<BR>to be seen or known, easily recognised.<BR>—सुख-<BR>लिप्सा, f. desire of attaining pleasure or happiness.<BR>—सुख-लेश, अस्, m. a little pleasure, (see लेश.)<BR>—सुख-वर्चक, अस्, or सुख-वर्चस्, आस्, m.<BR>‘having a pleasant lustre,’ natron, alkali.<BR>—सुख-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m. a proper N.<BR>—सुख-वास, अस्, m.<BR>a water-melon.<BR>—सुख-वासन, अस्, m. ‘pleasantly-<BR>perfuming,’ a perfume for the mouth.<BR>—सुख-<BR>वेदन, अम्, n. the consciousness of pleasure.<BR>—सु-<BR>ख-शयन, अम्, n. pleasant sleep, sleeping well.<BR>—सुख-शोभार्थम्, ind. for the sake of comfort<BR>and honour.<BR>—सुख-श्रव, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>sweet sound, sweetly sounding.<BR>—सुख-श्रुति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, agreeable or pleasant to the ear.<BR>—सुख-सं-<BR>वित्ति, इस्, f. consciousness of happiness, enjoyment<BR>or experience of happiness.<BR>—सुख-सङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>attachment to pleasure.<BR>—सुख-सङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>attached to pleasure.<BR>—सुख-सञ्ज्ञा, f. the term<BR>‘ease.’<BR>—सुख-सन्दुह्या or सुख-सन्दोह्या, f.<BR>‘easily milked,’ a tractable and gentle cow; [cf.<BR>सुख-दोह्या, दुःख-दोह्या.]<BR>—सुख-सागर,<BR>अस्, m. an ocean of pleasure.<BR>—सुख-साधन, अम्,<BR>n. a means of obtaining pleasure.<BR>—सुख-साध्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be accomplished or attained; easy<BR>to be cured; easy to be conquered or subdued.<BR>—सुख-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sweetly sleeping, com-<BR>fortably asleep.<BR>—सुख-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, living<BR>happily, happy.<BR>—सुख-स्पर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, agree-<BR>able to the touch, pleasant to the feelings, gratifying.<BR>—सुखा-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make happy,<BR>gladden, please.<BR>—सुखाजात (˚ख-आज्˚), अस्, m.<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सुखात्मक (˚ख-आत्˚), अस्, इका,<BR>अम्, consisting of pleasure.<BR>—सुखाद्-अपेत or<BR>सुखापेत (˚ख-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, a little removed<BR>from or deprived of pleasure, (see Pāṇ. II. 1, 38.)<BR>—सुखाधार (˚ख-आध्˚), अस्, m. a receptacle<BR>of pleasure or delight; ‘pleasure-location,’ Indra's<BR>heaven, paradise.<BR>—सुखानन्द (˚ख-आन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the joy of happiness.<BR>—सुखानुभव (˚ख-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘perception of pleasure,’ anticipation or<BR>consciousness of pleasure.<BR>—सुखान्त (˚ख-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ending in happiness; friendly; subver-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-b" target="_blank">Page1127-b+ 81</a>]<BR>sive of happiness.<BR>—सुखान्वित (˚ख-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, attended with happiness, happy.<BR>—सुखापन्न<BR>(˚ख-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has attained or<BR>gained happiness.<BR>—सुखाप्लव (˚ख-आप्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, convenient for bathing.<BR>—सुखाभियोज्य<BR>(˚ख-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, easily assailable.<BR>—सुखा-<BR>भिलाष (˚ख-अभ्˚), अस्, m. longing for pleasure,<BR>desire of pleasure.<BR>—सुखायत (˚ख-आय्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘easily restrained or guided,’ a well-trained horse.<BR>—सुखायन (˚ख-आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘going easily or<BR>pleasantly,’ a good horse.<BR>—सुखारोहण (˚ख-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of easy ascent.<BR>—सुखारोहण-<BR>सोपान, अस्, आ, अम्, having stairs of easy ascent.<BR>—सुखार्त (˚ख-ऋत), अस्, आ, अम् (see Gram. 38.<BR>द्), affected by joy.<BR>—सुखार्थम् (˚ख-अर्˚), ind.<BR>for the sake of ease or happiness, &c.<BR>—सुखार्थिन्<BR>(˚ख-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, seeking or wishing for happi-<BR>ness.<BR>—सुखार्ह (˚ख-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deserving<BR>of happiness.<BR>—सुखालोक (˚ख-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pleasant-looking, charming.<BR>—सुखावगाह (˚ख-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, easy to penetrate, easily seen<BR>through.<BR>—सुखावती-देव, आस्, m. pl., N. of par-<BR>ticular deities.<BR>—सुखावती-व्यूह, N. of a Buddhist<BR>work.<BR>—सुखावतीश्वर (˚ती-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a parti-<BR>cular Buddha.<BR>—सुखावह (˚ख-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bringing or conferring pleasure, delighting, pleasing.<BR>—सुखाश (˚ख-आश), अस्, m. eating with pleasure;<BR>pleasant food; N. of Varuṇa; a cucumber, Cucumis<BR>Sativus.<BR>—सुखाशक (˚ख-आश्˚), अस्, m. a cucum-<BR>ber.<BR>—सुखाशय (˚ख-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, aiming<BR>at or expecting pleasure; feeling happy.<BR>—सुखा-<BR>सक्त (˚ख-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘devoted to happiness,’<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सुखासीन (˚ख-आस्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, seated or sitting at ease, comfortably seated.<BR>—सुखास्पर्श (˚ख-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, = सुख-<BR>स्पर्श.<BR>—सुखास्वाद (˚ख-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pleasantly flavoured; delightful, agreeable; (अस्),<BR>m. pleasant flavour; enjoyment.<BR>—सुखाहर<BR>(˚ख-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bringing or conferring<BR>pleasure, agreeable, delightful.<BR>—सुखाहार (˚ख-<BR>आह्˚), अम्, n. ease and food.<BR>—सुखेच्छा (˚ख-<BR>इच्˚), f. hope or desire of happiness.<BR>—सुखेतर<BR>(˚ख-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, other than happy, unhappy,<BR>unfortunate.<BR>—सुखेप्सु (˚ख-ईप्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, de-<BR>sirous of ease.<BR>—सुखैकायतन (˚ख-एक-आय्˚),<BR>अम्, n. sole abode of joy.<BR>—सुखैषिन् (˚ख-<BR>एष्˚), ई, इणी, इ, one who seeks happiness, desiring<BR>happiness; seeking another's happiness, wishing well<BR>to.<BR>—सुखोच्छेद्य (˚ख-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>cut up or destroyed with ease, to be exterminated<BR>easily.<BR>—सुखोत्सव (˚ख-उत्˚), अस्, m. a pleasure-<BR>festival, merry-making, jubilee, occasion of joy; a<BR>husband.<BR>—सुखोदक (˚ख-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘pleasant<BR>water,’ warm water.<BR>—सुखोदय (˚ख-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, following or resulting from pleasure; (अस्),<BR>m. realization or occurrence of pleasure.<BR>—सुखो-<BR>दर्क (˚ख-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘having happiness<BR>as a consequence,’ leading to or resulting in happi-<BR>ness or pleasure, causing happiness.<BR>—सुखोद्य<BR>(˚ख-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, to be uttered easily or<BR>agreeably.<BR>—सुखोपविष्ट (˚ख-उप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, seated comfortably or at ease.<BR>—सुखोपसर्प्य<BR>(˚ख-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, to be approached easily,<BR>easy of access.<BR>—सुखोर्जिक (˚ख-ऊर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>natron (= सर्जिका-क्षार).<BR>—सुखोषित (˚ख-<BR>उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pleasantly lodged.<BR>—सुखोष्ण<BR>(˚ख-उष्˚), अम्, n. warm water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाय
सुखाय, Nom. A. सुखायते, &c., to be happy<BR>or pleased; to be glad; to rejoice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखित
सुखित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, delighted, comforted,<BR>happy; (अम्), n. happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखिन्
सुखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing happiness or pleasure,<BR>happy, joyful, pleasant, comfortable, easy; (ई), m. a<BR>religious ascetic.<BR>—सुखि-ता, f. happiness.<BR>—सुखि-<BR>स्वभाव, अस्, m. a happy or contented disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखी
सुखी, ईस्, m. f. one who loves pleasure, (see Vopa-<BR>deva III. 61.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखीबल
सुखीबल or सुखीवल, अस्, m., N. of a king,<BR>(also read सुखीनल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्य
1. सुख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to pleasure,<BR>pleasurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्य
2. सुख्य, Nom. P. सुख्यति, -यितुम्, to render<BR>happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखङ्घुण|सुखंघुण|सुखंघुणः|सुखङ्घुणः
सुखङ्घुण सुखङ्घुण, अस्, m. (perhaps fr.<BR>सुखम् + घुण, ‘easily brandished’), a kind of<BR>staff with a skull at the top considered as a weapon<BR>of Śiva (= खट्वाङ्ग, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

