सुह्म
सुह्म सुह्म, अस्, m., N. of a son of Bali and<BR>Su-deṣṇā; of a district in the west of Bengal;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
सू 1. सू, cl. 6. P. सुवति, सुषाव, सवि-<BR>ष्यति, असावीत्, सवितुम्, to excite, incite,<BR>impel, send, throw; to discharge; to remit (debts<BR>&c.): Caus. सावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असूषवत्, to<BR>excite, hasten on: Desid. सुसूषति: Intens. सो-<BR>षूयते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
2. सू, ऊस्, f. impelling, sending, dispatching, throw-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक|सूकः
सूक, अस्, m. an arrow; air, wind; a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत|सूतः
2. सूत, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see p. 1118), impelled,<BR>sent, dispatched; gone, departed; drank (a doubtful<BR>sense perhaps referrible to rt. 3. सु); (अस्), m. a<BR>charioteer, driver; a man of a mixed caste (the son<BR>of a Kṣatriya father and Brāhman mother; his oc-<BR>cupation is managing horses and driving cars); a<BR>bard, encomiast; a carpenter [cf. सूत्र-धार];<BR>N. of a pupil of Vyāsa (to whose teaching the Iti-<BR>hāsas and Purāṇas are said to have been entrusted<BR>by his preceptor), a teacher of the Purāṇas; (ई), f.<BR>the wife of a Sūta; a female bard.<BR>—सूत-ज or<BR>सूत-तनय, अस्, m. the son of a charioteer; epi-<BR>thet of Karṇa, q. v.<BR>—सूत-त्व, अम्, n. the business<BR>of a charioteer.<BR>—सूत-नन्दन, अस्, m. a charioteer's<BR>joy; the son of a charioteer.<BR>—सूत-पुत्र or सूत-<BR>पुत्रक, अस्, m. a charioteer's son; epithet of<BR>Karṇa, q. v.<BR>—सूत-व्यसनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering<BR>from the unskilfulness of a charioteer.<BR>—सूत-सं-<BR>हिता, f., N. of part of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूती
सूती. See under 2. सूत above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
सू 3. सू = rt. 4. सु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
4. सू, ऊस्, f. child-bearing, parturition [cf. षू];<BR>(ऊस्, ऊस्, उ), bringing forth, bearing, producing (often<BR>in comps., cf. वीर-सू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
सू 5. सू, ind., Ved. = 5. सु, well, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूकर|सूकरः
सूकर सूकर, अस्, m. (probably fr. सू +<BR>कर, ‘making the noise सू;’ = शूकर, q. v.), a<BR>hog, pig; a sort of deer (the hog-deer); a potter;<BR>(ई), f. a sow; a sort of moss, Lycopodium Imbrica-<BR>tum; [cf. Gr. σῦς, ὖς; Lat. sus; Angl. Sax. suga;<BR>Old Germ. sū; Mod. Germ. sau.]<BR>—सूकर-<BR>कन्द, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्त|सूक्तं
सूक्त सूक्त. See p. 1126, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्तक
सूक्तक सूक्तक (incorrect for शुक्तक, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्षण
सूक्षण सूक्षण, अम्, n. (for सूर्क्षण,<BR>q. v.), disregard, disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्म|सूक्ष्मं|सूक्ष्मः
सूक्ष्म सूक्ष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 176. fr. rt. सूच्, cf. सूचि, col. 3; thought<BR>by some to be a contraction of 5. सु + क्षाम),<BR>subtile, minute, atomic; little, small; thin, fine, at-<BR>tenuated, delicate, exquisite, refined; nice; sharp,<BR>acute; subtle, crafty, artful, sly, ingenious; exact,<BR>precise, accurate, correct; (अस्), m. an atom; the<BR>Kataka or clearing-nut plant; epithet of Śiva; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of jasmine, Jasminum Auriculatum; a par-<BR>ticular perfume (described as a substance in small<BR>grains, = एलवालु); small cardamoms; = करुणी; =<BR>बालुका; (अम्), n. the subtile all-pervading spirit,<BR>the Supreme Soul; subtlety, minuteness; one of the<BR>three kinds of power attainable by an ascetic, (see<BR>सावद्य); slyness, craft, ingenuity; fraud, cheat-<BR>ing; fine thread, &c.; a particular figure of rhetoric<BR>(described as the delicate or subtle expression of an<BR>intended act).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-कृष्ण-फला, f. a par-<BR>ticular plant (= मध्यम-जम्बु-वृक्ष).<BR>—सू-<BR>क्ष्म-जातक, N. of a work by Varāha-mihira (=<BR>स्वल्प-जातक).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-तण्डुल, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing small seeds,’ the poppy; (आ), f. long pepper; a<BR>sort of grass, Andropogon Muricatus.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-ता,<BR>f. or सूक्ष्म-त्व, अम्, n. minuteness, subtilty or<BR>subtlety, fineness.<BR>—सूक्ष्मदर्शि-ता, f. quick-<BR>sightedness, acuteness, wisdom.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-दर्शिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, or सूक्ष्म-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, sharp-sighted,<BR>eagle-eyed; of acute discernment; acute, quick, in-<BR>telligent.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-दारु, उ, n. a thin plank of<BR>wood, a board.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-देह, अस्, अम्, m. n. =<BR>सूक्ष्म-शरीर, q. v.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-पत्त्र, अस्, m.<BR>‘small-leaved,’ coriander seed; a kind of wild cumin;<BR>a sort of mustard (= देव-सर्षप); a sort of red<BR>sugar-cane; the gum-arabic tree, Mimosa Arabica;<BR>other plants and trees (according to Śabda-k. =<BR>लघु-बदर; = सुर-पर्ण; = वन-वर्वरी;<BR>= कुक्कुट-द्रु; = वावल).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-पत्त्रिका,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-c" target="_blank">Page1130-c+ 80</a>]<BR>f. ‘small-leaved,’ epithet of various plants and trees<BR>(= शत-पुष्पा; = शतावरी; = लघु-ब्राह्मी; =<BR>क्षुद्रोपोदकी; = दुर्-आलभा; = आकाश-मांसी).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-पर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, small-leaved, hav-<BR>ing sharp leaves; (आ), f., N. of two plants, = जीर्ण-<BR>फञ्जी; = डोडी; (ई), f. a kind of basil (= राम-<BR>दूती).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-पिप्पली, f. wild pepper.<BR>—सू-<BR>क्ष्म-पुष्प, अस्, ई, अम्, small-flowered, having<BR>small blossoms; (ई), f. a kind of plant (= यव-<BR>तिक्ता).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having small<BR>fruit; (अस्), m. the plant Cordia Myxa; (आ), f. the<BR>plant Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-बदरी, f.<BR>a kind of jujube (= भू-बदरी).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-बुद्-<BR>धि, इस्, f. sharp wit, acute intellect, mental acumen;<BR>(इस्, इस्, इ), sharp-witted, acute, shrewd, intelligent.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-भूत, आनि, n. pl. the subtle elements<BR>(= तन्-मात्र).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-मक्षिक, अस्, आ, m. f.<BR>a small fly, musquito, gnat.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-मान, अम्,<BR>n. minute or exact measurement, precise computa-<BR>tion.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a small<BR>root; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= जयन्ती).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-<BR>वल्ली, f. a medicinal plant (= ताम्र-वल्ली).<BR>—सू-<BR>क्ष्म-वस्त्र or सूक्ष्म-वस्त्रक, अम्, n. fine<BR>cloth.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-वीज, अस्, m. ‘having small seeds,’<BR>the poppy.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-शरीर, अम्, n. (in phil.) the<BR>subtile body which is invested by and the archetype<BR>or pattern of the grosser material frame, = लिङ्ग-<BR>शरीर, q. v.; (आणि), n. pl. the six subtile principles<BR>from which the grosser elements are evolved (viz.<BR>Ahaṅkāra and the five Tan-mātras, see Manu I. 17;<BR>according to other systems seventeen subtile princi-<BR>ples exist of the five organs of sense, five organs of<BR>action, five elements, Buddhi and Manas).<BR>—सू-<BR>क्ष्म-शर्करा, f. small gravel, sand.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-<BR>शाख, अस्, m. ‘having small branches,’ a kind of<BR>plant (= जाल-वर्वूर).<BR>—सूक्ष्म-शालि, इस्, m. a<BR>kind of fine rice.<BR>—सूक्ष्म-षट्चरण, अस्, m.<BR>‘small insect,’ a sort of tick or louse (said to breed<BR>at the roots of the eye-lashes).<BR>—सूक्ष्मात्मन्<BR>(˚म-आत्˚), आ, m. ‘subtile-soul,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सूक्ष्मी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make thin<BR>or fine, subtilize, refine.<BR>—सूक्ष्मी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, subtilized, made thin or minute.<BR>—सूक्ष्मी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become subtile or fine, minute.<BR>—सूक्ष्मैला (˚म-एला), f. small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्
सूच् सूच् (thought by some to be pro-<BR>perly a Nom. fr. सूचि), cl. 10. P. सूच-<BR>यति, असुसूचत्, सूचयितुम्, to pierce; to point out,<BR>indicate, show, prove, make manifest; to betray, re-<BR>veal, inform against, inform; to indicate by gesture,<BR>gesticulate, communicate by signs, declare, relate,<BR>tell; to trace out, ascertain, spy out, espy: Pass.<BR>सूच्यते, Aor. असूचि: Intens. सोसूच्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच|सूचः
सूच, अस्, m. a pointed shoot or blade of Kuśa<BR>grass [cf. सूक्ष्म]; (आ), f. piercing; making signs;<BR>gesticulation; spying out, sight, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचक|सूचकः
सूचक, अस्, इका, अम्, indicative, indicating, prov-<BR>ing, making manifest; betraying, informing; (अस्),<BR>m. a piercer; a needle, any implement for perforat-<BR>ing or sewing; a pointer out; an informer, tale-<BR>bearer, traducer, spy; a narrator, teacher, instructor;<BR>the manager or chief actor of a company; a Buddha;<BR>a Siddha; a villain, scoundrel; a demon, imp; a<BR>dog; a crow; a cat; a kind of fine rice.<BR>—सूचक-<BR>वाक्य, अम्, n. the information given by an in-<BR>former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचन|सूचनं
सूचन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of piercing or per-<BR>forating, perforation; pointing out, indicating, indi-<BR>cation, intimation; informing against, traducing,<BR>betraying; indicating by signs or gesture, gesticula-<BR>tion; hinting, hint; information, informing; teach-<BR>ing, showing, describing; spying out, espying, see-<BR>ing; villainy, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचनीय
सूचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pointed out or indi-<BR>cated, to be made known or communicated, to be<BR>informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचि|सूचिः
सूचि, इस्, or सूची, f. piercing, perforating [cf. सू-<BR>क्ष्म]; a needle; the point of a blade of grass,<BR>point of a bud, sharp point of anything; a kind of<BR>military array (according to Kullūka on Manu VII.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">Page1131-a+ 78</a>]<BR>187. placing the sharpest and most active soldiers in<BR>front), a sharp file or column; a triangle formed by<BR>the sides of a trapezium produced till they meet; a<BR>cone, pyramid; indication by gesture, making signs,<BR>gesticulation; a particular mode of gesticulating or<BR>dancing; dramatic action; an index, table of con-<BR>tents, catalogue, (see सूची-पत्त्र); (in astronomy)<BR>the earth's disc in computing eclipses (or corrected<BR>diameter of the earth).<BR>—सूचि-खात, अस्, m. a sharp<BR>pyramid or pyramidal excavation, an excavation of<BR>a conical form, a pyramid, cone.<BR>—सूचि-ता, f. needle-<BR>work.<BR>—सूचि-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. ‘having pointed<BR>leaves,’ the pot-herb Marsilea Quadrifolia (= सिता-<BR>वर).<BR>—सूचि-पुष्प, अस्, m. the Ketaka tree,<BR>Pandanus Odoratissimus.<BR>—सूचि-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>divided into needles, split or bursting open at the<BR>points of the buds.<BR>—सूचि-रोमन्, आ, m. ‘having<BR>needle-like or sharp bristles,’ a hog.<BR>—सूचि-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having a needle; having a pointed beak,<BR>&c., pointed; (आन्), m. epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—सूचि-<BR>वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, needle-faced; having a pointed<BR>mouth or beak; (अस्), m. the mungoose; a mus-<BR>quito.<BR>—सूचि-शालि, इस्, m. a kind of fine rice.<BR>—सूची-<BR>कटाह-न्याय, अस्, m. the rule of the needle and<BR>the boiler, (a phrase used to denote that when two<BR>matters, one easy and the other more difficult and<BR>important, require to be done at once, the more<BR>simple should be despatched first.)<BR>—सूची-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. needle-work.<BR>—सूची-दल, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>pot-herb (= सितावर).<BR>—सूची-पत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘in-<BR>dicatory-leaf,’ an index, table of contents, catalogue;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), having pointed leaves; (आ), f. a kind<BR>of Dūrvā grass (= गण्ड-दूर्वा).<BR>—सूची-पुष्प,<BR>अस्, m. = सूचि-पुष्प.<BR>—सूची-भेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>to be pierced or penetrated by a needle; gross,<BR>thick, dense; palpable, tangible.<BR>—सूची-मुख, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, needle-mouthed, having a pointed beak or<BR>proboscis, pointed; (अस्), m. a bird; white Kuśa<BR>grass; a particular position of the hands; (ई), f. a<BR>female bird; (अम्), n. a diamond.<BR>—सूची-रोमन्,<BR>आ, m. a hog.<BR>—सूच्य्-अग्र, अम्, n. the point of a<BR>needle; (अस्, आ, अम्), needle-pointed, having a<BR>needle-like point, acuminated; pointed.<BR>—सूच्य्-<BR>अग्र-स्थूलक, अस्, m. a sort of grass, Saccharum<BR>Cylindricum.<BR>—सूच्य्-आस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, needle-faced,<BR>having a pointed beak or mouth; (अस्), m. a rat; a<BR>particular position of the hands.<BR>—सूच्य्-आह्व, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of pot-herb (= सितावर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिक|सूचिकः
सूचिक, अस्, m. any one who lives by his needle,<BR>a tailor, &c. [cf. सौचिक]; (आ), f. an elephant's<BR>trunk or proboscis; a needle [cf. सूचक, p. 1130].<BR>—सूचिका-धर, अस्, m. ‘having a trunk,’ an ele-<BR>phant.<BR>—सूचिकाभरण (˚का-आभ्˚?), अम्, n. a<BR>particular drug or medicament, (apparently used as<BR>a remedy for the bite of a serpent.)<BR>—सूचिका-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having a pointed mouth or head;<BR>having a needle-shaped point or end; (अम्), n. a<BR>shell, the conch shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचित|सूचितः
सूचित, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced, perforated; pointed<BR>out, indicated, intimated, hinted; made known, in-<BR>dicated by signs or gestures, communicated, told,<BR>revealed; ascertained, known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचितव्य
सूचितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = सूच्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिन्
सूचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, piercing, perforating; pointing<BR>out, indicating; informing against, informing; spying<BR>out; (ई), m. a spy, informer; (इनी), f. a needle;<BR>night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूची
सूची, f. a needle; an index, &c. See सूचि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्य
सूच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be indicated or pointed out,<BR>to be made known, communicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्
सूत् सूत्, ind. an imitative sound.<BR>—सूत्-<BR>कार, अस्, अम्, m. n. making the sound सूत् or any<BR>sound expressive of impatience or aversion; snorting,<BR>snoring; roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत|सूतः
सूत सूत, &c. See p. 1118, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूति|सूतिः
सूति 3. सूति, इस्, f. (for स्यूति, fr. rt. सिव्;<BR>for 1. सूति see p. 1117, col. 3; for 2. see p. 1118),<BR>sewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्त
सूत्त सूत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (contracted fr. सु-<BR>दत्त, q. v.), well given, entirely given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्तर
सूत्तर सूत्तर. See p. 1126, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्थान|सूत्थानः
सूत्थान सूत्थान. See p. 1126, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्पर|सूत्परं
