सूत्र्
सूत्र् सूत्र् (probably to be regarded as a<BR>Nom. fr. सूत्र below; see सूत्रय,<BR>col. 3), cl. 10. P. सूत्रयति, सूत्रापयति, &c., to<BR>tie, bind, thread, string; to unbind, relax: Intens.<BR>सोसूत्र्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्र|सूत्रं
सूत्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. सिव्, ‘to sew;’ but said to<BR>be connected with rt. सूत्र् above), a thread, string,<BR>line, cord; fibre, wire; a collection of threads; the<BR>sacred thread or cord worn by the first three classes,<BR>(see यज्ञोपवीत, p. 804); the string or wire of a<BR>puppet or doll; a short rule or precept, axiom,<BR>aphorism (in morals, religion, or science; इति सू-<BR>त्रेण, according to such an aphorism); a short and<BR>technical sentence or metrical line used as a memorial<BR>rule to aid in the acquirement of any system (and<BR>hence generally expressed in brief and obscure and<BR>sometimes symbolical language, intelligible only to<BR>those who possess the key to its interpretation, this<BR>key being sometimes given in separate Sūtras called<BR>Paribhāṣās, and the right understanding of a whole<BR>series or chain of rules depending on a knowledge of<BR>the Adhikāra or heading-rule and its influence [अनु-<BR>वृत्ति] on those that follow; these short sentences<BR>and aphoristic rules, the use of which constitutes a<BR>most curious feature in the literary history of the<BR>Hindūs, appear to have been often mere aids to the<BR>memory of teachers — mere hints to guide lecturers in<BR>their oral explications; they were also especially<BR>useful in this way to the priests who had the<BR>management of a complicated ritual); any work or<BR>manual consisting of strings or long lines of the<BR>above aphoristic rules and sentences hanging toge-<BR>ther like threads, (though the term सूत्र may<BR>possibly indicate not so much a line or series of<BR>rules as rules written on leaves which were kept<BR>together by strings; these Sūtra works form a sort<BR>of groundwork or foundation of teaching, not only<BR>in all religious ritual, but in philosophy, in grammar,<BR>and in the collateral subjects of accent, euphony,<BR>etymology, and prosody: thus in religion and ritual<BR>there are first the Śrauta-sūtras, and among them<BR>principally the Kalpa-sūtras, founded directly on<BR>Śruti, q. v., and treating especially of ritual; they<BR>form a kind of rubric or directory to Vedic cere-<BR>monial, or in other words, a complete systema-<BR>tized guide to the rambling discursive Brāhmaṇa as<BR>distinct from the Mantra portion of the Veda [see<BR>ब्राह्मण], giving concise rules for the perform-<BR>ance of every kind of sacrifice; there are Sūtras of<BR>this kind by Āśvalāyana and Śāṅkhāyana for the<BR>Ṛg-veda; by Kātyāyana for the White Yajur-veda;<BR>by Āpastamba, Baudhāyana, and the Mānavas for<BR>the Black Yajur-veda; by Lāṭyāyana, Drāhyāyaṇa,<BR>Maśaka, and Gobhila for the Sāma-veda; and by<BR>Kuśika for the Atharva-veda; there are also two<BR>other kinds of Sūtras connected with ceremonial,<BR>viz. the Grihya-sūtras and Sāmayācārika or Dharma-<BR>sūtras [often by the same authors, with special refer-<BR>ence also to each separate Veda, and even placed by<BR>some, like the Kalpa, under the head of Sūtras<BR>founded on Śruti], which are really ‘rules for domestic<BR>ceremonies and conventional customs,’ and are some-<BR>times called collectively Smārta-sūtras [as founded<BR>on स्मृति or ‘tradition,’ see स्मार्त]; these led to<BR>the later Dharma-śāstras or ‘law-books’ attributed<BR>to Manu, Yājñavalkya, Parāśara, &c., the names of<BR>the authors of the Sūtras and of the law-books being<BR>often identical; in philosophy each system has its<BR>regular text-book of aphorisms written in Sūtras by<BR>its supposed founder, see वेदान्त-सूत्र, न्याय-स्˚,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-c" target="_blank">Page1131-c+ 81</a>]<BR>साङ्ख्य-स्˚, मीमांसा-स्˚, वैशेषिक-स्˚, योग-स्˚;<BR>in Vyākaraṇa or grammar there are the celebrated<BR>Sūtras of Pāṇini in eight books, which are the<BR>groundwork of a vast grammatical literature, besides<BR>the Uṇādi-sūtras on certain affixes; in Vedic accent<BR>and phonetics there are the Prātiśākhyas [see प्राति-<BR>शाख्य] and the Phiṭ-sūtras of Śāntanava; in<BR>etymology there are strings of Vedic words, and<BR>in prosody there are the Sūtras of Piṅgala-nāga on<BR>Chandas, including both Vedic and non-Vedic<BR>metres, and the Nidāna-sūtra on the metres of the<BR>Sāma-veda and Vedic metres generally: it should be<BR>borne in mind that the mixture of Ślokas in some<BR>of the Prātiśākhyas and in some more recent Sūtra<BR>works, though depriving them of the brevity strictly<BR>necessary to constitute Sūtras, does not prevent their<BR>being regarded as collections of aphoristic and me-<BR>morial rules: with regard to grammatical Sūtras it is<BR>necessary to remember that all connecting words<BR>used as prepositions, however necessary to the sense,<BR>are omitted; thus, a word in the genitive case re-<BR>quires स्थाने, ‘instead of,’ to be supplied; a word in<BR>the ablative requires परम्, ‘after;’ a word in the<BR>instrumental requires सह, ‘together with;’ a word<BR>in the locative, though sometimes to be translated<BR>in the ordinary way by prefixing ‘in,’ may often be<BR>used as a locative absolute, and परे must then be<BR>supplied, the sense being ‘on such an affix or word<BR>coming after or following;’ the word वा is equivalent<BR>to ‘optionally’ or ‘alternative’); any rule, law, canon,<BR>decree (in law &c.).<BR>—सूत्र-कण्ठ, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing Sūtras in the throat or mouth ready to be<BR>repeated,’ a Brāhman; ‘having lines on the throat,’<BR>a pigeon, dove; a wagtail.<BR>—सूत्र-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>‘rule-work,’ carpentry.<BR>—सूत्र-कार, अस्, m. the<BR>author or composer of Sūtras.<BR>—सूत्र-कृत्, त्, m.<BR>‘Sūtra-maker,’ the author of an aphorism or set of<BR>aphorisms.<BR>—सूत्र-कोण or सूत्र-कोणक, अस्, m.<BR>a small drum shaped like an hour-glass and struck<BR>by a string and button (= डमरु).<BR>—सूत्र-<BR>गण्डिका, f. a kind of stick used by weavers in<BR>spinning threads.<BR>—सूत्र-ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, hold-<BR>ing a thread.<BR>—सूत्र-ग्राह, अस्, ई, अम्, taking a<BR>thread.<BR>—सूत्र-चरण, N. of a class of Caraṇas or<BR>Vedic schools who introduced various Sūtra works.<BR>—सूत्र-तन्तु, उस्, m. a thread, string, line.<BR>—सू-<BR>त्र-तर्कुटी, f. a distaff, spindle.<BR>—सूत्र-धर,<BR>अस्, m. = सूत्र-धार.<BR>—सूत्र-धार, अस्, m. ‘rule-<BR>holder, thread-holder,’ a stage-manager, a director or<BR>principal actor who arranges the plot of a drama<BR>and takes a leading part in the prelude; a carpenter;<BR>the author of a set of rules or aphorisms; epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>—सूत्र-पिटक, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>three collections of Buddhist writings (viz. those<BR>which prescribe rules for the laity, see त्रि-पिटक).<BR>—सूत्र-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘thread-flowered,’ the<BR>cotton plant.<BR>—सूत्र-भिद्, त्, m. ‘thread-cutter,’ a<BR>tailor.<BR>—सूत्र-भृत्, त्, m. = सूत्र-धार.<BR>—सू-<BR>त्र-मध्य-भू, ऊस्, f. ‘born amid threads or<BR>fibres,’ the resin or Shorea Robusta; incense.<BR>—सू-<BR>त्र-यन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘thread-machine,’ a shuttle; a<BR>weaver's loom.<BR>—सूत्र-विद्, त्, m. ‘a Sūtra-knower,’<BR>one versed in Sūtras.<BR>—सूत्र-वीणा, f. a kind of lute<BR>(= लाबुकी).<BR>—सूत्र-वेष्टन, अम्, n. a weaver's<BR>shuttle; the act of weaving.<BR>—सूत्रात्मन् (˚र-आत्˚),<BR>आ, आ, अ, having the nature of a string or thread;<BR>(आ), m. ‘soul-thread,’ intellect having for its site the<BR>collective totality of subtile bodies; the soul.<BR>—सू-<BR>त्राली (˚र-आली), f. a string of beads &c. worn round<BR>the neck, necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रण|सूत्रणं
सूत्रण, अम्, n. the act of stringing together, ar-<BR>ranging, putting in order; arranging in aphorisms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रय
सूत्रय, Nom. P. सूत्रयति, सूत्रयाम्-आस,<BR>सूत्रयितुम्, to make a Sūtra or aphorism, arrange<BR>in the form of an aphorism, prescribe or declare in<BR>a Sūtra or aphorism, propound an aphorism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रला
सूत्रला, f. a spindle, distaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिका
सूत्रिका, f. a kind of dish or cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रित
सूत्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, strung, arranged, methodized;<BR>ruled, directed or declared in a Sūtra; prescribed or<BR>enjoined in an aphorism, delivered in axioms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिन्
सूत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having threads or lines, having<BR>rules; (ई), m. a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रामन्
सूत्रामन् सूत्रामन्, आ, m. = सु-त्रामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूद्
सूद् 1. सूद्, cl. 1. A. सूदते, सुषूदे, सूदि-<BR>तुम्, to strike, hurt, wound, kill, destroy;<BR>to effuse, pour out; to distil, flow; to eject (accord-<BR>ing to some); to deposit (according to some); cl.<BR>10. or Caus. सूदयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असूषुदत्, to<BR>strike, wound, kill, massacre; to incite, excite, urge<BR>on, animate, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda V. 5, 2.<BR>सुषूदयति = सुष्ठु प्रेरयति; सूदयन्तु =<BR>कर्मसु प्रेरयन्तु, Ṛg-veda IV. 40, 1); to<BR>cook, dress, season, prepare, purify; to preserve,<BR>(Sāy. सूदयन्तु = रक्षन्तु, Ṛg-veda IV. 39, 1);<BR>to pour out, effuse; to eject; to assent, agree, pro-<BR>mise: Desid. सुसूदिषते: Intens. सोसूद्यते, सो-<BR>सूत्ति; [cf. Gr. συδ in παν-συδίῃ, πασ-συδί; Lett.<BR>saudêt, ‘to destroy.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूद्
2. सूद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. flowing, distilling, pouring<BR>forth, dropping, (in हव्य-सूद्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूद|सूदः
सूद, अस्, m. destroying, destruction, massacre; a<BR>destructive weapon, (Sāy. = हिंसकं शस्त्रम्,<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 61, 2); pouring out, distilling, (Sāy.<BR>= क्षारयितृ, Ṛg-veda IX. 97, 44); a well, spring,<BR>(in Naigh. III. 25. enumerated among the कूप-<BR>नामानि); cooking, a cook [cf. सूप]; sauce, soup,<BR>seasoning; anything seasoned, a made dish; split<BR>pease; mud, mire; sin, fault (= पाप); the<BR>Lodhra tree; = सारथ्य, q. v.; N. of a country in<BR>Kaśmīra.<BR>—सूद-कर्मन्, अ, n. cook's work, cook-<BR>ing.<BR>—सूद-शाला, f. ‘cooking-room,’ a kitchen.<BR>—सूदाध्यक्ष (˚द-अध्˚), अस्, m. a superin-<BR>tendent of cooking, overseer of the kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदन|सूदनं
सूदन, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying, destructive, a<BR>destroyer; dear, beloved; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>destroying, destruction, killing; the act of assenting<BR>to or promising (= अङ्गी-करण); the act of<BR>ejecting or throwing away (= निःक्षेपण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदयित्नु
सूदयित्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. inciting, urging on,<BR>animating, exciting, (Sāy. = प्रेरयितृ, Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 64, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदित
सूदित, अस्, आ, अम्, wounded, destroyed, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदितृ
सूदितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, destroying, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून|सूनं|सूनः
सून सून, सूनु. See p. 1118, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनर
सूनर सूनर, अस्, m. (probably for सु-<BR>नर), Ved. a good or excellent man, (Sāy. =<BR>शोभन-मनुष्य, Ṛg-veda V. 34, 7); ‘a good<BR>leader,’ epithet of Soma, (Sāy. = सुष्ठु रात्रीणां<BR>नेता, Ṛg-veda VIII. 29, 1); (ई), f., Ved. a good or<BR>well-married or happy woman; epithet of the Dawn,<BR>(Sāy. = जनानां सुष्ठु नेत्री, Ṛg-veda VII. 81,<BR>1); (अस्, ई, अम्), well-disposed, friendly (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूना
सूना सूना, f. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 13. said to<BR>be fr. rt. 3. सु), any place where animals are killed<BR>or sacrificed; any place or utensil in a house where<BR>animals are liable to be accidentally destroyed, (of<BR>five kinds, see शूना, पञ्च-सूना); a slaughter-<BR>house; killing, hurting, injuring [cf. सूदन]; the<BR>sale of flesh or meat; the uvula or soft palate, (in<BR>this and the next sense perhaps connected with<BR>शून); inflammation of the glands of the neck<BR>(commonly called mumps); a zone, girdle (according<BR>to some); a ray (according to some); a river (ac-<BR>cording to some).<BR>—सूना-दोष, अस्, m. the guilt<BR>incurred by destroying animals in any of the five<BR>Sūnās, (see above; cf. Manu III. 71.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनिन्
सूनिन्, ई, m. one who keeps a slaughter-house, a<BR>butcher, flesh-seller, one who causes the death of<BR>animals, a hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनृत|सूनृतं
सूनृत सूनृत, अस्, आ, अम्, (thought to be<BR>fr. 5. सु and rt. 1. नृत्), Ved. movable, quick,<BR>active, brisk, lively, cheerful, kind, agreeable,<BR>pleasant and at the same time true, (सूनृता वाच्<BR>or गिर्, ‘cheerful words,’ or, according to some, ‘kind<BR>yet sincere language,’ is one of the four things with<BR>which even the poorest man is expected to greet a<BR>guest, Manu III. 101; the sense ‘true’ may have<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">Page1132-b+ 76</a>]<BR>arisen from some fancied connection with ऋत,<BR>q. v.); fortunate, auspicious; dear, beloved; (आ), f.<BR>true and agreeable speech, (Sāy. = प्रिय-हित-वाच्);<BR>the goddess of true speech (= वाग्-देवता, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 40, 3, and invoked as a goddess in X. 141, 2);<BR>excellent song; N. of Uṣas, (Naigh. I. 8); food<BR>(= अन्न, Naigh. II. 7); N. of a wife of Uttāna-<BR>pāda; (अम्), n. true and agreeable speech, pleasant<BR>discourse; auspiciousness.<BR>—सूनृत-वाच्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>truth-speaking, speaking politely and truthfully.<BR>—सू-<BR>नृता-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a pleasant or<BR>friendly voice, having excellent songs; (अती), f., N.<BR>of Uṣas, (Naigh. I. 8.)<BR>—सूनृता-वन्, आ, अरी, अ,<BR>Ved. having a pleasant voice; (अरी), f. epithet of<BR>Uṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून्मद|सून्मदः
सून्मद सून्मद. See p. 1126, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूप|सूपः
सूप सूप, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 26. said<BR>to be fr. rt. 3. सु, ‘to distil;’ cf. सूद), sauce, con-<BR>diment; soup, broth; split pease; a cook; one who<BR>lives by cooking for Śūdras (शूद्र-पाकोपजीविन्);<BR>a vessel, pot, pan; an arrow; [cf. Old Germ. suf,<BR>sufan, saufjan; Old Norse sup; Angl. Sax. su-<BR>pan.]<BR>—सूप-कार, अस्, m. ‘sauce-maker,’ a cook.<BR>—सूप-धूपन or सूप-धूपक, अम्, n. ‘scent-<BR>ing sauce,’ Asa Fetida.<BR>—सूप-पर्णी, f. a sort of<BR>bean (= मुद्ग-पर्णी).<BR>—सूप-प्रति, ind. a little<BR>sauce or soup, (Pāṇ. II. 1, 9.)<BR>—सूप-श्रेष्ठ,<BR>अस्, m. ‘best of sauces,’ a sort of bean.<BR>—सूपाङ्ग<BR>(˚प-अङ्˚), अम्, n. ‘sauce-ingredient,’ Asa Fetida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपस्कर
सूपस्कर सूपस्कर, सूपस्थ. See p. 1126,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूभर्व
सूभर्व सू-भर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (for सु-<BR>भर्व; see rt. भर्व्), well-fed, having good food<BR>or pasturage, (Sāy. = शोभन-भक्ष, Ṛg-veda X.<BR>94, 3; = शोभन-चरण, Ṛg-veda X. 102, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूम|सूमं|सूमः
सूम सूम, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>144. said to be fr. rt. 4. सु or 3. सू), the sky,<BR>heaven; milk; water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूमय
सूमय सू-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, (for सु-मय),<BR>Ved. abounding in happiness, very successful, (Sāy.<BR>= सु-सुख.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूयवस
सूयवस सू-यवस, &c. See p. 1126, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्
सूर् सूर् = rt. शूर्, cl. 4. A. सूर्यते, &c.,<BR>to hurt, kill; to be firm; to make firm,<BR>&c., (see rt. शूर्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरण|सूरणः
सूरण, अस्, m. = शूरण, the esculent root Arum<BR>Campanulatum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्ण
सूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, hurt, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर|सूरः
सूर सूर, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. II. 24. said<BR>to be fr. rt. 4. सु or 3. सू, but probably connected<BR>with 2. स्वर्, originally सुवर्, from which a form<BR>सूर् appears to have been derived, see Ṛg-veda VI.<BR>49, 3), the sun; N. of the father of the seventeenth<BR>Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī; the swallow-wort,<BR>Calotropis Gigantea (= अर्क); the Soma; a wise or<BR>learned man, teacher; a hero, king, (in these senses<BR>probably for शूर, q. v.); (ई), f., N. of Kuntī (as<BR>married to the Sun before her marriage with Pāṇḍu);<BR>black mustard, = राज-सर्षप; [cf. Lat. sol; Goth.<BR>sunna, ‘the sun;’ Lith. saule.]<BR>—सूर-चक्षस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. sun-eyed; radiant as the sun.<BR>—सूर-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—सूर-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of the Sun,’ N. of Saturn; [cf.<BR>सौरी.]<BR>—सूर-सूत, अस्, m. ‘charioteer of the Sun,’<BR>N. of Aruṇa (or the Dawn personified).<BR>—सूरा-<BR>पगा (˚र-अप्˚), f. ‘river of the gods,’ epithet of<BR>the Ganges.<BR>—सूरासन-देश (˚र-आस्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरि|सूरिः
सूरि, इस्, m. the sun; a learned man, sage; a<BR>priest; a worshipper, praiser, (Sāy. = स्तोतृ); a title<BR>commonly given to Jaina teachers; N. of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>a kind of plant (= भुजङ्ग-घातिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरिन्
सूरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wise, learned; (ई), m. a wise or<BR>learned man, scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरी
सूरी, f., N. of the wife of Sūrya, (see under सूर<BR>above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य|सूर्यः|सूर्य्य|सूर्य्यः
सूर्य, अस्, m. (perhaps originally सुवर्-य, or<BR>according to some, सवर्-य, सवर् being for स-<BR>वन्, cf. the etymology of सूर, col. 2; according<BR>to Vopa-deva fr. rt. सृ), the Sun or its deity, (the<BR>name Sūrya being generally distinguished in the<BR>Veda from Savitṛ, q. v., and Āditya, q. v., as be-<BR>longing to a distinct god; from some passages, how-<BR>ever, it would appear that these names are intended<BR>to be interchangeable as representing various forms<BR>of one and the same divine personality; in the later<BR>mythology Sūrya as Savitṛ is reckoned as one of the<BR>twelve Ādityas or emblems of the Sun in the twelve<BR>months of the year; by Yāska, Nirukta VII. 5, he<BR>is regarded as one of the original Vedic triad, his<BR>place being in the sky, while that of Agni is on the<BR>earth, and that of Indra is in the atmosphere; many<BR>hymns or parts of hymns in the Ṛg-veda are in<BR>praise of Sūrya, e. g. I. 50, I. 115, IV. 13, VII. 60,<BR>X. 37, X. 170; sometimes he is called son of<BR>Dyaus, sometimes of Aditi; in one passage Uṣas,<BR>the Dawn, is his wife, in another he is styled the<BR>child of the Dawns; he moves through the sky in<BR>a chariot drawn by seven ruddy horses or mares<BR>[see सप्ताश्व, हरित्, हरिद्-अश्व, शुन्ध्यु]; he<BR>is described as the eye of Mitra and Varuṇa, and<BR>sometimes of Agni; he is all-seeing, ever beholding<BR>the good and bad deeds of mortals, the preserver of<BR>all things stationary and moving; in other passages<BR>he is represented as holding a somewhat secondary<BR>position, being made to shine or have his path pre-<BR>pared for him by Mitra and Varuṇa, by Aryaman,<BR>by Indra, by the Dawns, and others; the long hymn,<BR>Atharva-veda XIII. 2, is entirely in his praise;<BR>there is another addressed to the Sun, called Bhānu,<BR>in Mahā-bhārata, Vana-parvan 166, &c.; and in the<BR>Yuddha-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa [VI. 106, Bombay<BR>edit.], Rāma, when about to do battle with Rāvaṇa,<BR>is told by Agastya to repeat a hymn, called Āditya-<BR>hṛdaya, to the Sun, there called Vivasvat, and iden-<BR>tified with Āditya, Savitṛ, Sūrya, Pūṣan, and in<BR>fact with Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Śiva, and all the other<BR>gods; in the later mythology the seven-horsed<BR>chariot of Sūrya is said to be driven by Aruṇa or the<BR>Dawn as its charioteer, who is represented without<BR>legs; the Sun, whether named Sūrya or Vivasvat,<BR>has several wives, see सूर्या below, and cf. स-वर्णा,<BR>see also छाया, सञ्-ज्ञा, अश्विनी; by Sañjñā he had<BR>two children, Yama and Yamunā, q. q. v. v.; by<BR>Aśvinī, the two Aśvins; by Kuntī, before her mar-<BR>riage with Pāṇḍu, he had Karṇa, q. v.; and he is<BR>also supposed to be the father of Manu Vaivasvata,<BR>and to be the progenitor of one of the two great<BR>lines of Hindū kings [see सूर्य-वंश below];<BR>seven Sūryas are sometimes mentioned, which are<BR>probably the seven planets, the Sun being regarded<BR>as a planet by Hindū astronomers; ninety-four<BR>synonyms of Sūrya are commonly given, and his<BR>epithets are almost innumerable; at the end of a<BR>Kalpa he is called Kāla-sūrya); a symbolical expres-<BR>sion for the number twelve (in allusion to the sun in<BR>the twelve signs of the zodiac); the swallow-wort<BR>(either Calotropis or Asclepias Gigantea, = अर्क);<BR>N. of the son of Bali; of a Dānava; of an astro-<BR>nomer (= सूर्य-दास); epithet of Śiva; (आ), f. the<BR>wife of Sūrya or the Sun, (also called Sañjñā, q. v.);<BR>the daughter of Sūrya or the Sun, (see Ṛg-veda I.<BR>116, 17; also described as daughter of Savitṛ and<BR>wife of the Aśvins, and in other places as married<BR>to Soma; in Ṛg-veda I. 119, 2. she is called<BR>Ūrjānī, and in VI. 55, 4, VI. 58, 4. the sister of<BR>Pūṣan, q. v., who is described as loving her, and<BR>receiving her as a gift from the gods; according to<BR>some she represents a weak manifestation of the<BR>Sun; Sūryā Sāvitrī is regarded as the authoress of<BR>the Sūryā-sūkta, Ṛg-veda X. 85; in Naigh. I. 11.<BR>Sūryā is enumerated among the वाङ्-नामानि); the<BR>hymn about the marriage of Sūryā (= सूर्या-सूक्त,<BR>q. v.); a new bride; a drug; the colocynth or<BR>bitter gourd; [cf. Gr. ἥλιος; Lat. sol; Goth.<BR>sunna, sunno, sanil; Angl. Sax. sunna, sunne,<BR>sun.]<BR>—सूर्य-कमल, अम्, n. the sunflower,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-a" target="_blank">Page1133-a+ 81</a>]<BR>heliotrope.<BR>—सूर्य-कान्त, अस्, m. ‘sun-loved,’ the<BR>sun-stone, sun-gem, sun-crystal (a kind of crystal<BR>cool to the touch and supposed to possess fabulous<BR>properties because like a glass lens it gave out heat<BR>when exposed to the rays of the sun; there is a<BR>fellow-stone in connection with the moon called<BR>चन्द्र-कान्त, q. v.); crystal (= स्फटिक); the<BR>flowering shrub Hibiscus Phœniceus.<BR>—सूर्य-कान्ति,<BR>इस्, f. sun-light, sun-shine; a particular flower (pro-<BR>bably the China rose); the flower of sesamum (ac-<BR>cording to some).<BR>—सूर्य-काल, अस्, m. ‘sun-time,’<BR>day-time, day.<BR>—सूर्य-कालानल-चक्र (˚ल-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a kind of astrological diagram for indicating<BR>good and bad fortune.<BR>—सूर्य-गङ्गा-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सूर्य-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘sun-<BR>planet,’ the sun; ‘sun-seizure,’ an eclipse of the sun;<BR>‘sun-seizer,’ epithet of Rāhu and Ketu, q. q. v. v.;<BR>the bottom of a water-jar.<BR>—सूर्य-ग्रहण, अम्,<BR>n. ‘sun-seizure,’ a solar eclipse.<BR>—सूर्य-ज, अस्, m.<BR>‘sun-born,’ epithet of the monkey Sugriva; of the hero<BR>Karṇa; of the planet Saturn; (आ), f. the river Yamunā<BR>(also called Aṃśu-matī, q. v.).<BR>—सूर्य-तनय, अस्,<BR>m. ‘son of the Sun,’ epithet of the planet Saturn; of<BR>Karṇa; of Sugrīva; (आ), f. ‘daughter of the Sun;’<BR>the river Yamunā.<BR>—सूर्य-तेजस्, अस्, n. the radiance<BR>or heat of the sun.<BR>—सूर्य-त्वच्, क्, क्, क्, or सूर्य-<BR>त्वच, अस्, आ, अम्, having skin as bright or as clear<BR>as the sun.<BR>—सूर्य-दास, अस्, m., N. of an astro-<BR>nomer of the sixteenth century (author of the Rāma-<BR>kṛṣṇa-kāvya); of a son of Śiva-dāsa.<BR>—सूर्य-<BR>ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘sun-bannered,’ N. of a king.<BR>—सूर्-<BR>य-नक्षत्र, अम्, n. ‘sun-asterism,’ that Nak-<BR>ṣatra (of the twenty-seven) in which the sun hap-<BR>pens to be.<BR>—सूर्य-नगर, ‘city of the Sun,’ N.<BR>of the capital of Cashmere (commonly called Siri-<BR>nagar or Seri-nagar).<BR>—सूर्य-नारायण, अस्, m. the<BR>Sun personified; a proper N.<BR>—सूर्य-पत्त्र, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Calotropis Gigantea.<BR>—सूर्य-पर्वन्,<BR>अ, n. a solar festival (on the days of the solstices,<BR>equinoxes, eclipses, &c.).<BR>—सूर्य-पुत्र, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of Karṇa; of Sugrīva; of Varuṇa; of the planet<BR>Saturn, (see शनि); of Yama; (ई), f. ‘daughter of<BR>the Sun,’ lightning; the river Yamunā.<BR>—सूर्य-<BR>पुर, अम्, n. ‘city of the Sun,’ N. of a city.<BR>—सूर्य-<BR>प्रज्ञप्ति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—सूर्य-प्रभ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king of Śākala (son of Candra-<BR>prabha).<BR>—सूर्य-प्रभव, अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from<BR>the Sun.<BR>—सूर्य-फणि-चक्र, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>astrological diagram for indicating auspicious and in-<BR>auspicious moments for doing anything.<BR>—सूर्य-<BR>भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, worshipping the sun, one who<BR>worships the sun; (अस्), m. a particular tree (= बन्-<BR>धूक-पुष्प).<BR>—सूर्य-भक्तक, अस्, m. a sun-<BR>worshipper; the tree Bandhūka-puṣpa.<BR>—सूर्य-भा,<BR>आस्, &c., bright as the sun.<BR>—सूर्य-मणि, इस्, m. the<BR>sun-stone, or sun-gem, (see सूर्य-कान्त); the shrub<BR>Hibiscus Phœniceus.<BR>—सूर्यमणि-वृक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>the flowering shrub Hibiscus Phœniceus (= पुष्प-<BR>रक्त).<BR>—सूर्य-मण्डल, अम्, n. the orb or disk<BR>of the sun.<BR>—सूर्य-मुखी, f. the plant Helianthus<BR>Annuus.<BR>—सूर्य-यन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘sun-machine,’<BR>a representation of the sun, instrument used in<BR>worshipping the Sun (or in taking solar observa-<BR>tions).<BR>—सूर्य-रश्मि, इस्, m. a ray of the sun, sun-<BR>beam; (इस्, इस्, इ), having the rays of Sūrya; (इस्), m.<BR>epithet of Savitṛ.<BR>—सूर्य-लता, f. the plant Cleome<BR>Viscosa or another (= अर्क-भक्ता).<BR>—सूर्य-लोक,<BR>अस्, m. the world or heaven of the sun (a region or<BR>space supposed to exist round the sun, constituting<BR>a heaven of which the sun is regent).<BR>—सूर्य-<BR>वंश, अस्, m. the family or race of the sun, the<BR>solar race of kings (i. e. the royal dynasty of Rāma-<BR>candra, king of Ayodhyā, hero of the Rāmāyaṇa,<BR>who was descended from Ikṣvāku, son of Vaivas-<BR>vata Manu, son of the Sun; many Rājput tribes still<BR>claim to belong to this race; it is one of the two<BR>great lines of kings, the other being called ‘lunar,’<BR>see चन्द्र-वंश).<BR>—सूर्य-वन, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a forest in Kuru-kṣetra.<BR>—सूर्य-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>resplendent as the sea; (आस्), m. a proper N.<BR>—सूर्-<BR>य-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, sun-coloured, bright as the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">Page1133-b+ 78</a>]<BR>sun.<BR>—सूर्य-वल्ली, f. the plant Arka-puṣpikā (or,<BR>according to some, Cleome Pentaphylla).<BR>—सूर्य-<BR>विम्ब, अस्, अम्, m. n. the disk of the sun.<BR>—सूर्य-<BR>विम्ब-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सूर्य-वि-<BR>लोकन, अम्, n. the ceremony of taking a child out<BR>to see the sun when four months old.<BR>—सूर्य-श-<BR>तक, अम्, n., N. of a short poem by Mayūra (=<BR>मयूर-शतक).<BR>—सूर्य-शोभा, f. sun-shine.<BR>—सूर्-<BR>य-सङ्क्रम, अस्, m. the passage of the sun from<BR>one sign to another.<BR>—सूर्य-सङ्क्रान्ति, इस्, f. the<BR>sun's entrance into a new sign.<BR>—सूर्य-सञ्ज्ञ, अम्,<BR>n. saffron.<BR>—सूर्य-सम, अस्, आ, अम्, equal to or<BR>resembling the sun.<BR>—सूर्य-सारथि, इस्, m. the<BR>charioteer of the Sun, i. e. Aruṇa (the Dawn per-<BR>sonified).<BR>—सूर्य-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m. a celebrated<BR>astronomical text-book (said to be a direct revelation<BR>from the Sun, and thought by some to be the same<BR>as the Saura-s˚ or one of the five earlier works on<BR>which was founded the Pañca-siddhāntikā of Varāha-<BR>mihira, who lived about the beginning of the sixth<BR>century of our era; the Sūrya-s˚ has been printed with<BR>Raṅga-nātha's commentary, the Gūḍhārtha-prakā-<BR>śaka).<BR>—सूर्यसिद्धान्त-टीका, f. a commentary on<BR>the Sūrya-siddhānta.<BR>—सूर्य-स्तवन, अम्, n. ‘praise<BR>of the Sun,’ N. of the 107th chapter of the Mārkaṇ-<BR>ḍeya-Purāṇa.<BR>—सूर्य-स्तुति, इस्, f. a hymn to the sun.<BR>—सूर्य-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. a hymn to the sun (attri-<BR>buted to Śāmba).<BR>—सूर्य-हृदय, अम्, n. ‘heart<BR>of the sun,’ a hymn to the sun of great efficacy (also<BR>called Āditya-h˚, see under सूर्य).<BR>—सूर्या-चन्-<BR>द्रमसौ, m. du. the sun and moon.<BR>—सूर्यातप<BR>(˚य-आत्˚), अस्, m. the heat or glare of the sun, sun-<BR>shine.<BR>—सूर्यातप-च्छिन्न-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, hav-<BR>ing the sight dazzled by the sun's glare.<BR>—सूर्यात-<BR>प-परिक्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, darted upon or over-<BR>spread by the rays of the sun.<BR>—सूर्या-मासा, m. du.,<BR>Ved. the sun and moon.<BR>—सूर्यार्घ्य (˚य-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the presentation of an offering to the<BR>sun.<BR>—सूर्यालोक (˚य-आल्˚), अस्, m. sun-shine.<BR>—सूर्यावर्त (˚य-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘turning to the<BR>sun,’ the plant Cleome Viscosa; a kind of sun-<BR>flower, Helianthus Indicus; (आ), f. a kind of plant<BR>(= अर्क-भक्ता).<BR>—सूर्या-विवाह, अस्, m. the<BR>marriage of Sūryā (as described in Ṛg-veda X. 85).<BR>—सूर्यावेक्षण (˚य-अव्˚), अम्, n. the act of<BR>looking at the sun.<BR>—सूर्याश्मन् (˚य-अश्˚), आ, m.<BR>the sun-stone or sun-gem, (see सूर्य-कान्त.)<BR>—सूर्-<BR>याश्व (˚य-अश्˚), अस्, m. a horse of the sun (=<BR>हरित्, q. v.).<BR>—सूर्या-सूक्त, अम्, n. the hymn Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 85 (giving an account of the marriage of<BR>Sūryā; this hymn is also given with some variations<BR>in Atharva-veda XIV. 1).<BR>—सूर्यास्त (˚य-अस्˚),<BR>अम्, n. sun-set.<BR>—सूर्याह्व (˚य-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>named after the sun; (अस्), m. gigantic swallow-wort;<BR>(अम्), n. copper.<BR>—सूर्येन्दु-सङ्गम (˚य-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘conjunction of sun and moon,’ the day of<BR>new moon (= अमा-वास्या).<BR>—सूर्योढ (˚य-ऊढ),<BR>अस्, m. an evening guest (one who arrives after sun-<BR>set).<BR>—सूर्योत्थान (˚य-उत्˚), अम्, n. sun-rise, the<BR>rising of the sun.<BR>—सूर्योदय (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>sun-rise.<BR>—सूर्योपासक (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m. a sun-<BR>worshipper.<BR>—सूर्योपासना, f. the worship of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यक
सूर्यक, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्याणी
सूर्याणी, f. = सूर्या, the wife of the god Sūrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरत|सूरतः
सूरत सूरत, अस्, आ, अम्, (for सु-रत), well<BR>disposed towards, compassionate, tender; tranquil,<BR>calm; (आ), f. a tractable cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्
सूर्क्ष् सूर्क्ष्, cl. 1. P. सूर्क्षति, सुषूर्-<BR>क्ष (or सुसूर्क्ष according to some),<BR>सूर्क्षितुम्, to respect, regard, treat with reverence;<BR>to disregard, disrespect, slight, neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्षण|सूर्क्षणं
सूर्क्षण, अम्, n. disrespect, contumely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य|सूर्क्ष्यः
सूर्क्ष्य, अस्, m. a kind of bean, Phaseolus Ra-<BR>diatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य्
सूर्क्ष्य् सूर्क्ष्य्, cl. 1. P. सूर्क्ष्यति, सु-<BR>सूर्क्ष्य, सूर्क्ष्यितुम्, to despise, dis-<BR>respect; to envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्त
सूर्त सूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = सृत, moving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">Page1133-c+ 78</a>]<BR>going, (Sāy. = सरण-सहित); near (said of Rajas<BR>or ‘the atmosphere;’ cf. अ-स्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्प|सूर्पः|सूर्प्प
सूर्प सूर्प, अस्, अम्, m. n. = शूर्प, a win-<BR>nowing-basket; a measure of two Droṇas; another<BR>measure (= कुम्भ); [cf. probably Old Germ.<BR>swarb, swerban; Goth. svairban.]<BR>—सूर्प-नखा,<BR>f., see शूर्प-नखा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्मि|सूर्मिः|सूर्म्मि
सूर्मि 2. सूर्मि, इस्, f. (= शूर्मि, q. v.; for 1.<BR>सूर्मि see p. 1126, col. 2), an iron or metal image;<BR>the pillar of a house; brightness, a flame (Ved.; in<BR>this sense probably connected with सूर and सूर्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्मी|सूर्म्मी
सूर्मी, f. = 2. सूर्मि above; (Ved.) brightness, ra-<BR>diance (in this sense probably connected with सूर<BR>and सूर्य; सूर्म्या = ज्वालया, Ṛg-veda VII. 1, 3;<BR>according to Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-s. XVII. 76.<BR>सूर्मी = समित्-काष्ठ, ‘kindled wood,’ or it may<BR>mean ‘an iron post’ or ‘a burning post,’ and there-<BR>fore figuratively ‘a flame’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्म्य
सूर्म्य, (probably) the fire that will consume<BR>everything at the dissolution of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य|सूर्यः|सूर्य्य|सूर्य्यः
सूर्य सूर्य. See p. 1132, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूष्
सूष् सूष् (= rt. शूष्, q. v.), cl. 1. P. सू-<BR>षति, &c., to bring forth, bear; to beget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूषणा
सूषणा, f. (perhaps fr. an old Desid. of rt. 3. सू,<BR>without reduplication), ‘one desiring to bring forth,’<BR>a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूषा
सूषा, f., Ved. = सूषणा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूष्यन्ती|सूष्यंती
सूष्यन्ती, f. (a woman) desiring to bring forth,<BR>one who is parturient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृ
सृ सृ [cf. rt. सल्], cl. 1. P. सरति (Ved.<BR>also cl. 3. P. सिसर्ति, सिसर्षि = प्रापय,<BR>Ṛg-veda III. 32, 5), ससार (1st du. ससृव, 1st<BR>pl. ससृम), सरिष्यति, असार्षीत् or असरत्, Prec.<BR>स्रियात्, सर्तुम् (Ved. Inf. सर्तवे, सर्तवै), to go,<BR>move, proceed; to approach; to go fast, run; to flow;<BR>to blow (as the wind): Pass. स्रियते, Aor. असारि, to<BR>be gone, &c.: Caus. सारयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असी-<BR>सरत्, to cause to go, move; to extend; to push,<BR>strike, to push away, remove: Desid. सिसीर्षति (ac-<BR>cording to some सुसूर्षति): Intens. सेस्रीयते,<BR>सर्सर्ति, (Ved. सर्सृते); [cf. Zend har; Gr.<BR>ὁρ-μή, ὁρμά-ω, ἀφ-ορμή, ὁρμη-τήριο-ν, σάλος,<BR>σάλα, σαλεύω, (according to some also) ἅρμα, ἁρμός,<BR>ὅρμος, ἕρμα; Lat. salio, salto (probably also serere);<BR>Angl. Sax. saltian, serian.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर|सरं|सरः
सर, सरस्, &c., see p. 1092.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारयत्
सारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to go, putting in<BR>the proper place, fixing, adjusting, replacing; causing<BR>to go away, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारयित्वा
सारयित्वा, ind. having caused to move or vibrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिस्रत्
सिस्रत्, अत्, अती, अत्, Ved. going, rapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक|सृकः
सृक, अस्, m. air, wind; an arrow; a thunderbolt<BR>(= वज्र, Naigh. II. 20); a lotus (= कैरव,<BR>पद्म).<BR>—सृका-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, probably holding<BR>an arrow.<BR>—सृका-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having an<BR>arrow in the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृग|सृगः
सृग, अस्, m. a short javelin or arrow thrown with<BR>the hand or shot through a tube (= भिन्दपाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणि|सृणिः
सृणि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 104, IV.<BR>49. fr. rt. सृ above), an enemy; the moon; (इस्), f.<BR>a hook used to drive an elephant (also written शृणि,<BR>q. v.); a weapon (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणिका
सृणिका, f. saliva, spittle, slaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणी
सृणी, f. = सृणि, a hook for driving an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणीका
सृणीका, f. = सृणिका, saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृण्य
सृण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, skilful in weapons or arms,<BR>(according to Sāy. = आयुध-कुशल, and connected<BR>with सृणि above, Ṛg-veda IV. 20, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत्
सृत्, त्, त्, त्, going, running, &c.; [cf. स्व-स्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत|सृतः
सृत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, proceeded, flowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृति|सृतिः
सृति, इस्, f. a road, path, way; gliding, going,<BR>proceeding; (according to some) hurting, injuring<BR>(perhaps to be connected with rt. सॄ = rt. शॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत्वन्
सृत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. one who goes or creeps<BR>or moves, (Sāy. = सरण-शील); (आ), m. epithet of<BR>Prajā-pati; = विसर्प; = वृद्धि, (these meanings<BR>are made fem. by Śabda-k.); (अरी), f. a stream,<BR>river; a mother (according to Śabda-k, = माता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत्वर|सृत्वरः
सृत्वर, अस्, ई, अम्, going, moving, creeping,<BR>proceeding, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत्वा
सृत्वा, ind. having gone or proceeded, having ap-<BR>proached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृदर|सृदरः
सृदर, अस्, m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृदाकु|सृदाकुः
सृदाकु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 78.<BR>fr. rt. सृ above); fire; air, wind; a deer (= मृ-<BR>ग); Indra's thunderbolt; the disk or orb of the<BR>sun; (उस्), f. a river, stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृमर|सृमरः
सृमर, अस्, आ, अम्, going, going well or quickly;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of animal; (according to some) a<BR>young deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृकण्डु|सृकंडु|सृकण्डुः
सृकण्डु सृ-कण्डु, उस्, f. (see कण्डु), the<BR>itch, itching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृकाल|सृकालः
सृकाल सृकाल, अस्, m. (= शृकाल), a jackal;<BR>[cf. सृगाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्क|सृक्कं
सृक्क सृक्क, अम्, n. (probably fr. rt. 1. सृज्<BR>below; according to Sāy. फेनस्य स्रष्टृ, ‘the<BR>emitter of saliva’), the corner of the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्कणी
सृक्कणी, f. (according to Śabda-k.) the corner of<BR>the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्कन्
सृक्कन्, अ, n. the corner of the mouth; (अणी),<BR>n. du. the two corners of the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्किणी
सृक्किणी, f. = सृक्कणी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्किन्
सृक्किन्, इ, n. the corner of the mouth; (इणी), n.<BR>du. the two corners of the mouth, (but according to<BR>Śabda-k. the crude form is सृक्कि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्व|सृक्वं
सृक्व, अम्, n. = सृक्क above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्वणी
सृक्वणी, f. (according to Śabda-k.) = सृक्कणी<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्वन्
सृक्वन्, अ, n. = सृक्कन् above, (in Ṛg-veda I.<BR>164, 28. and Atharva-veda IX. 10, 6. the form सृ-<BR>क्वाणम्, acc. masc., occurs; this is by some trans-<BR>lated ‘the mouth,’ but according to Sāy. ‘the corner<BR>of the mouth;’ according to Yāska, Nirukta XI. 42,<BR>= सरण); (अणी), n. du. the two corners of the<BR>mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्विणी
सृक्विणी, f. (according to Śabda-k.) = सृक्कणी<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्विन्
सृक्विन्, इ, n. = सृक्किन् above; (इणी), n. du. the<BR>two corners of the mouth (according to Śabda-k.<BR>the crude form is सृक्वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्कृ
सृक्कृ सृक्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make<BR>the inarticulate sound सृक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृगाल|सृगालः
सृगाल सृगाल, अस्, m. (= शृगाल), a jackal;<BR>a particular Daitya or demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृङ्का|सृंका
सृङ्का सृङ्का, f. a kind of garland made of<BR>jewels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्
सृज् 1. सृज् (connected with rt. सृ), cl. 6.<BR>P. सृजति (Ved. and ep. also A. -ते), स-<BR>सर्ज (2nd sing. ससर्जिथ or सस्रष्ठ, 1st pl.<BR>A. Ved. ससृज्महे or ससृग्महे), स्रक्ष्यति,<BR>अस्राक्षीत्, cl. 4. A. सृज्यते, ससृजे, &c., (Ved.<BR>forms असृग्रम्, अस्रिग्रन् or असृग्रन्, अससृ-<BR>ग्रम्, Ṛg-veda X. 31, 3), स्रष्टुम्, to let go, let<BR>loose; to emit, send forth, let flow, pour out, shed,<BR>effuse; to let off, throw, cast; to create, produce,<BR>make; to procreate, beget; to put on, place on,<BR>apply; to send away, abandon, leave, quit; to be let<BR>loose or sent forth (cl. 4. A.): Pass. सृज्यते, Aor.<BR>असर्जि, to be made or created; to be left or aban-<BR>doned: Caus. सर्जयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अससर्जत्<BR>or असीसृजत्, to cause to let loose, let go, create, &c.:<BR>Desid. सिसृक्षति, -ते: Intens. सरीसृज्यते, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ग|सर्गः
सर्ग, सर्ज, सर्जन, &c., see pp. 1093, 1094.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससृजान
ससृजान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being let loose, let go,<BR>(Sāy. = सृज्यमान, Ṛg-veda VII. 8, 2); created.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्
2. सृज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, creating, a creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृजत्
सृजत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, shedding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृजमान
सृजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. creating, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृजय
सृजय, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृजान
सृजान, अस्, आ, अम्, let go, poured out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृजिकाक्षार|सृजिकाक्षारः
सृजिका-क्षार, अस्, m. = सर्जिका-क्षार, natron,<BR>alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्य
सृज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be let go or emitted; to<BR>be created, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्यमान
सृज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being let go, being let<BR>loose; being made or created.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्ट|सृष्टं
सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, let go, let loose; poured out,<BR>emitted; given away; created, made; ascertained;<BR>sent away, abandoned, deserted, left; joined, at-<BR>tached, connected; ornamented, adorned; abundant,<BR>much, many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्टवत्
सृष्टवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has let go or<BR>created or made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्टि|सृष्टिः
सृष्टि, इस्, f. letting go, letting loose, emission;<BR>giving away, gift; creation, procreation, creating;<BR>the creation of the world, (मनोरथ-स्˚, mental<BR>creation, fiction of the imagination); nature, natural<BR>property or disposition; the existence of properties<BR>or qualities; the absence of properties.<BR>—सृष्टि-<BR>कर्तृ, ता, m. a creator, maker.<BR>—सृष्टि-खण्ड,<BR>N. of the first book of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—सृष्टि-<BR>प्रदा, f. ‘causing procreation,’ a particular shrub<BR>(= गर्भ-दात्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्ट्वा
सृष्ट्वा, ind. having let go; having created;<BR>having abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृञ्जय|सृंजय
सृञ्जय सृञ्जय, अस्, m., N. of a son of Deva-<BR>vāta (Ved.); N. of several kings; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people (said to have been allies of the Pañcālas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृञ्जरी
सृञ्जरी सृञ्जरी, f., N. of a wife of Bhaja-<BR>māna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्
सृप् सृप् (connected with rt. सृ), cl. 1.<BR>P. सर्पति (ep. also A. -ते), ससर्प (1st<BR>du. ससृपिव), सर्प्स्यति or स्रप्स्यति, असृपत्,<BR>असार्प्सीत् or अस्राप्सीत्, सर्प्तुम् or स्रप्तुम्, to<BR>creep, crawl; to go, move: Pass. सृप्यते, Aor.<BR>असर्पि: Caus. सर्पयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असीसृपत्<BR>or अससर्पत्, to cause to creep, cause to go, &c.:<BR>Desid. सिसृप्सति: Intens. सरीसृप्यते, सरीसर्प्ति;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἕρπ-ω, ἑρπ-ύζ-ω, ἑρπ-ετό-ν, ἕρπ-η(τ)-ς,<BR>Σαρπηδών, (according to some also) ῥέπ-ω, &c.: Lat.<BR>serp-o, serp-en(t)-s, serp-ula, Pro-serp-ina (?),<BR>rep-o (probably for srep-o): Old Germ. slich, ‘to<BR>creep;’ (according to some also) slif for silf, ‘to<BR>glide;’ Mod. Germ. schleife: Angl. Sax. slipan:<BR>Lith. slenkiu, ‘to creep;’ reptoju, ‘to creep with<BR>hands and feet:’ Hib. sleagaim, ‘to sneak.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प|सर्पः
सर्प, &c. See p. 1094.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्त
सृप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, crept, crawled; gone, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्ति
सृप्ति, इस्, f. creeping, crawling; going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्त्वा
सृप्त्वा, ind. having crept or crawled; having<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्र|सृप्रः
सृप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, creeping, going, proceeding,<BR>gliding, (Sāy. = सर्पण-शील, प्रसृत); (अस्), m.<BR>the moon.<BR>—सृप्र-करस्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one<BR>whose hands are extended or mighty, (Sāy. = प्र-<BR>सृत-बाहु.)<BR>—सृप्र-दानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. con-<BR>stantly giving, (Sāy. = अविच्छेदेन धनानि प्र-<BR>यच्छत्, Ṛg-veda I. 96, 3); (perhaps according to<BR>some) possessed of flowing rain.<BR>—सृप्र-भोजस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. conferring extended enjoyment.<BR>—सृप्र-वन्धुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to<BR>some) having a wide fore part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाट|सृपाटः
सृपाट सृपाट, अस्, m. a kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाटिका
सृपाटिका, f. the beak of a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाटी
सृपाटी, f. a kind of measure; (according to<BR>Śabda-k.) = रक्त-धारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृबिन्द
सृबिन्द सृबिन्द, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>demon (an enemy of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृभ्
सृभ् सृभ् or सृम्भ्, cl. 1. P. सर्भति,<BR>सृम्भति, &c., to kill, slay, injure; [cf.<BR>rt. सिभ्, स्रिभ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सॄ
सॄ सॄ [cf. rts. शॄ, स्वॄ], cl. 9. P. सृणाति,<BR>&c., to hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीर्ण
सीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to Śabda-k.) hurt,<BR>injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीर्णि|सीर्णिः
सीर्णि, इस्, f. (according to Śabda-k.) injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्
सेक् सेक् (= rt. स्रेक्), cl. 1. A. सेकते, &c.,<BR>to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक|सेकः
सेक सेक, सेक्तृ, &c. See p. 1113, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचक|सेचकः
सेचक सेचक, सेचन, &c. See p. 1113,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेटु|सेटुः
सेटु सेटु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. सिट्), a<BR>water-melon; a kind of cucumber, Cucumis Ma-<BR>draspatanus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतिकरण
सेतिकरण सेति-करण (स-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the word इति, followed by इति (as in the Pada<BR>text of the Ṛg-veda; cf. सहेतिकरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतिका
सेतिका सेतिका, f., N. of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतु|सेतुः
सेतु सेतु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>70. fr. rt. सि, ‘to bind’), a ridge of earth, mound, bank,<BR>causeway, dike, dam, any raised piece of ground<BR>separating fields (serving as a boundary or as a pas-<BR>sage during inundations); a landmark; a bridge; a<BR>pass, defile, mountain road or track; a boundary,<BR>limit; a barrier or obstruction of any kind; an estab-<BR>lished institution, fixed rule or law; epithet of the<BR>Praṇava or sacred syllable Om (which is said to be<BR>मन्त्राणां सेतुः); the tree Cratæva Roxburghii<BR>or Tapia Cratæva (= वरण, वरुण); N. of a<BR>king; of a place.<BR>—सेतु-खण्ड, N. of a book of<BR>the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—सेतु-बन्ध, अस्, m. the<BR>forming of a causeway or bridge; the ridge of rocks<BR>extending from the south extremity of the Coro-<BR>mandel coast towards the island of Ceylon (supposed<BR>to have been formed by Hanumat as a bridge for<BR>the passage of Rāma's forces against Rāvaṇa); any<BR>causeway, bridge, dike, &c.; N. of a poem.<BR>—सेतु-<BR>भेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, breaking down barriers; removing<BR>obstructions; (ई), m. the medicinal plant Dantī, q. v.<BR>—सेतु-मङ्गल-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra<BR>work.<BR>—सेतु-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the tree Cratæva Rox-<BR>burghii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतव्य
सेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bound, to be fastened<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुक|सेतुकः
सेतुक, अस्, m. a bank, causeway, bridge, pass;<BR>the tree Cratæva Roxburghii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतृ
सेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who binds, binding, fasten-<BR>ing; that which binds, a bond, fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेत्र|सेत्रं
सेत्र, अम्, n. a bond, ligament, fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरु|सेरुः
सेरु, उस्, उस्, उ, binding, tying, fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेदिवस्
सेदिवस् सेदिवस्. See p. 1055, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेध|सेधः
सेध सेध, &c. See rt. 1. सिध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन
सेन सेन (स-इन), अस्, आ, अम्, having a lord,<BR>possessing a master or leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनक
सेनक सेनक, अस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेना
सेना सेना, f. (in Uṇādi-s. III. 10. said to<BR>be fr. rt. सि, ‘to bind;’ according to some fr. सेन<BR>above), an army, armament, armed force; an Army<BR>personified as the wife of Kārttikeya; N. of the<BR>mother of the third Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī.<BR>—सेन-जित्, त्, m. (for सेना-जित्), a proper N.<BR>—सेना-<BR>कल्प, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—सेनाग्र (˚ना-अग्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the front or van of an army.<BR>—सेनाग्र-ग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘going at the front of an army,’ the leader of<BR>an army, general.<BR>—सेनाङ्ग (˚ना-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>component part of an army (supposed to be con-<BR>stituted of four divisions, viz. elephants, chariots,<BR>cavalry, and infantry).<BR>—सेना-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going<BR>with or accompanying an army; (अस्), m. a soldier;<BR>a suttler, camp-follower.<BR>—सेना-जू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved.<BR>inciting an army, outstripping a host.<BR>—सेना-नि-<BR>वेश, अस्, m. the camp of an army.<BR>—सेना-नी, ईस्,<BR>m. (acc. सेनान्यम्, loc. सेनान्याम्, see Gram. 126.<BR>द्), the leader of an army, commander, general; N.<BR>of Kārttikeya (god of war); epithet of a die<BR>(the head of a host of dice); N. of one of the<BR>eleven Rudras (according to some); of a son of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—सेना-पति, इस्, m. ‘army-chief,’<BR>a general; N. of Kārttikeya; of Śiva.<BR>—सेना-<BR>पति-त्व, अम्, n. generalship.<BR>—सेना-परिच्छद्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, surrounded by an army.<BR>—सेना-पुर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a city.<BR>—सेना-पृष्ठ, अम्, n. the rear of an<BR>army.<BR>—सेना-भङ्ग, अस्, m. the breaking of an<BR>army, rout, disorderly flight.<BR>—सेना-मुख, अम्, n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">Page1135-a+ 73</a>]<BR>a division or battalion of an army, a company con-<BR>sisting of three Pattis (or three elephants, three<BR>chariots, nine horse and fifteen foot; see पत्ति); a<BR>mound or covered way in front of a city gate.<BR>—सेना-<BR>योग, अस्, m. the equipment of an army.<BR>—सेना-<BR>रक्ष, अस्, m. ‘army-protector,’ a guard, sentinel.<BR>—सेना-विन्दु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनय
सेनय, Nom. P. सेनयति, &c. See अभि-षे-<BR>णय, p. 68, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्य
सेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to an army, re-<BR>sembling an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनापत्य|सैनापत्यं
सैनापत्य, अम्, n. (fr. सेना-पति), the office of<BR>a general, command of an army, generalship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनिक|सैनिकः
सैनिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to an<BR>army, military, martial, drawn up in martial array;<BR>(अस्), m. an army-man, soldier; a guard, sentinel;<BR>a body of forces in array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्य|सैन्यं|सैन्यः
सैन्य, अस्, m. a soldier, one under arms, one<BR>drawn up in martial array; a guard, sentinel; (अम्),<BR>n. an army.<BR>—सैन्य-पृष्ठ, अम्, n. the rear of<BR>an army.<BR>—सैन्याधिपति (˚य-अध्˚), इस्, or सै-<BR>न्याध्यक्ष (˚य-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘army-overseer,’<BR>a general, commander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्र
सेन्द्र सेन्द्र (स-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, accom-<BR>panied by Indra, together with Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रगण
सेन्द्रगण (स-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, together with<BR>the troops of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रचाप
सेन्द्रचाप (स-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, along with the<BR>bow of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रायुधतडित्
सेन्द्रायुध-तडित् (˚र-आय्˚), त्, त्, त्, with a rain-<BR>bow and lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रायुधपुरोगम
सेन्द्रायुध-पुरोगम, अस्, आ, अम्, preceded<BR>by the rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रिय
सेन्द्रिय सेन्द्रिय (स-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>organs of sense, with the organs of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेफ|सेफः
सेफ सेफ, अस्, m. (= शेफ, q. v.), the penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेमन्ती|सेमंती
सेमन्ती सेमन्ती, f. the Indian white rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेमन्तिका
सेमन्तिका, f. = सेमन्ती (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेराह|सेराहः
सेराह सेराह, अस्, m. a horse of a milk-<BR>white colour (= पीयूष-वर्णाश्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरु|सेरुः
सेरु सेरु. See under सेतु, p. 1134, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेर्ष्य
सेर्ष्य सेर्ष्य (स-ईर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, full of envy<BR>or jealousy; (अम्), ind. enviously, with jealousy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल्
सेल् सेल्, cl. 1. P. सेलति, &c. = rt. शेल्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेलु|सेलुः
सेलु सेलु, उस्, m. the tree Cordia Myxa<BR>(see शेलु); N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल्हार
सेल्हार सेल्हार, अस्, m., N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्
सेव् सेव् (thought to be connected with<BR>rt. सप्), cl. 1. A. सेवते (sometimes also<BR>P. सेवति), सिषेवे, सेविष्यते, असेविष्ट, सेवितुम्,<BR>to follow, go after, seek, pursue; to wait upon, serve,<BR>honour, obey, worship, gratify; to love, attend to,<BR>devote or apply one's self to, cultivate, study, prac-<BR>tise, perform, do; to use, enjoy; to enjoy (sexually);<BR>to frequent, dwell in, inhabit; to watch over, protect,<BR>guard: Pass. सेव्यते, to be followed or served, &c.:<BR>Caus. सेवयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असिषेवत्, to serve,<BR>honour, worship: Desid. सिसेविषते, -ति: Intens.<BR>सेषेव्यते; [cf. Gr. σέβομαι; perhaps Goth. sai-<BR>vala, ‘soul;’ Old Germ. sela.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
1. सेवक, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see col. 2), serv-<BR>ing, waiting or attending upon, worshipping; prac-<BR>tising; servile, dependent; (अस्), m. a servant, at-<BR>tendant; a worshipper, votary.<BR>—सेवकोत्तम (˚क-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, आ, m. f. best of servants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन|सेवनं
1. सेवन, अम्, n. (for 2. see col. 2), the act of<BR>following, serving, service; devotion or addiction to,<BR>being fond of, fondness for, using, practising, adopt-<BR>ing, enjoying; carnal enjoyment; frequenting, dwell-<BR>ing in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवनीय
1. सेवनीय, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see col. 2), to<BR>be followed; to be practised; to be served or waited<BR>on, to be honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवमान
सेवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, following, pursuing, serv-<BR>ing, attending on; practising, being addicted to, using,<BR>employing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवा
सेवा, f. service, attendance, servitude; worship,<BR>homage; devotion or addiction to; use, practice,<BR>employment; resorting to, frequenting.<BR>—सेवा-काकु,<BR>उस्, f. change of voice in service (i. e. sometimes<BR>speaking loudly, sometimes softly, sometimes angrily,<BR>sometimes sorrowfully).<BR>—सेवा-धर्म, अस्, m. the<BR>duty or rule of service; the functions or obligations<BR>of service.<BR>—सेवा-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, maintaining service,<BR>doing service, serving.<BR>—सेवावलम्ब (˚वा-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, depending on the service of another.<BR>—सेवा-व्यवहार, अस्, m. the practice of service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवि
सेवि, n. (according to Śabda-k.) the jujube (=<BR>बदर); an apple (in this sense probably fr. Per-<BR>sian सेब्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविका
सेविका, f. a kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित|सेवितः
सेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, followed, pursued; served, at-<BR>tended on, obeyed, honoured, worshipped, adored;<BR>protected, preserved; practised, used; infested or<BR>frequented by; (अम्), n. the jujube (= बदर);<BR>an apple (= सेवि).<BR>—सेवित-मन्मथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>addicted to love or amorous enjoyments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवितव्य
सेवितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = 1. सेवनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवितृ
सेवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, serving, worshipping; a ser-<BR>vant, attendant, worshipper; addicted or devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविन्
सेविन्, ई, इनी, इ, following, pursuing, serving, obey-<BR>ing, honouring; practising, using; dwelling in, fre-<BR>quenting; (ई), m. a servant.<BR>—सेवि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>service, obedience, devotion; the state of one who<BR>dwells in or inhabits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्य|सेव्यं|सेव्यः
सेव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be served or obeyed, to be<BR>worshipped or honoured, honourable; to be prac-<BR>tised, to be used or employed or enjoyed; to be<BR>taken care of or guarded; (अस्), m. the Aśvattha tree;<BR>the Hijjala plant; (आ), f. the parasitical plant Vandā;<BR>(अम्), n. the root of Andropogon Muricatus.<BR>—से-<BR>व्य-ता, f. or सेव्य-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of<BR>being worthy of honour, honourableness, rank, emi-<BR>nence, worth.<BR>—सेव्य-सेवक, औ, m. du. served<BR>and server, master and servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यमान
सेव्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being served or waited<BR>on, being attended on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
सेवक 2. सेवक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सिव्; for 1.<BR>सेवक see col. 1), one that sews, a sewer; a sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन|सेवनं
2. सेवन, अम्, n. (for 1. see col. 1), the act of<BR>sewing, darning, stitching (= सीवन); a sack; (ई),<BR>f. a needle; a seam; (in anatomy) a suture or pecu-<BR>liar seam-like union of parts (of which there are<BR>seven in the body, viz. the five sutures of the cranium,<BR>the frenum of the tongue, and that of the glans<BR>penis).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवनीय
2. सेवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see col. 1), to be<BR>sewn or stitched together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवकालु|सेवकालुः
सेवकालु सेवकालु, उस्, m. a kind of plant<BR>(= निशा-भङ्गा, commonly called Dugdhapeyā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवती
सेवती सेवती, f. the Indian white rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवधि|सेवधिः
सेवधि सेव-धि, इस्, m. (for शेव-धि, q. v.),<BR>one of the nine treasures of Kuvera, a divine trea-<BR>sure; a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेष्मीयाण
सेष्मीयाण सेष्मीयाण, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the<BR>Intens. of rt. स्मि), Ved. (according to some) smiling<BR>much, continuing to smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेश्वरसाङ्ख्य|सेश्वरसांख्य
सेश्वरसाङ्ख्य सेश्वर-साङ्ख्य (स-इश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the theistical branch of the Sāṅkhya school of<BR>philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेहान
सेहान सेहान, अस्, आ, अम्, (Perf. part. A. fr.<BR>rt. 1. सह्), one who has overcome, overcoming, con-<BR>quering, (Sāy. = अभि-भवत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेहुण्ड
सेहुण्ड सेहुण्ड, अस्, m. a kind of Euphorbia<BR>(= सीहुण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सै
सै सै [cf. rts. 3. सा, 1. सो], cl. 1. P. सायति,<BR>ससौ, सातुम्, to waste away, decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंह|सैंहः
सैंह सैंह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सिंह), belonging<BR>to lions, leonine, lion-like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिक|सैंहिकः
सैंहिक, अस्, ई, अम्, lion-like, leonine; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of Rāhu or the personified ascending node (=<BR>सैंहिकेय below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिकेय|सैंहिकेयः
सैंहिकेय, अस्, m. (fr. सिंहिका, q. v.), a metro-<BR>nymic of Rāhu, q. v.; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>Dānavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहल
सैंहल सैंहल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सिंहल), be-<BR>longing to Ceylon; produced or growing in Ceylon;<BR>(ई), f. a kind of plant (= सिंह-पिप्पली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकत|सैकतं|सैकतः
सैकत सैकत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सिकता), sandy,<BR>gravelly, having sandy soil; (अम्), n. a sand-bank;<BR>an island with sandy shores; any bank or shore.<BR>—सैकत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing sand-banks.<BR>—सैकतेष्ट (˚त-इष्˚), अम्, n. ‘loved by sandy<BR>soil,’ ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिक|सैकतिकं|सैकतिकः
सैकतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>sand-banks; fluctuating, living in doubt and error,<BR>= सन्देह-जीविन्; (अस्), m. a religious mendi-<BR>cant; an ascetic; (अम्), n. a thread worn round the<BR>wrist or neck to secure good fortune (= मङ्गल-<BR>सूत्र); = मातृ-यात्रा (according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैतव
सैतव सैतव, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैतवाहिनी
सैतवाहिनी सैतवाहिनी, f. (fr. सित + वा-<BR>हिनी), N. of the river Bāhu-dā, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैद्धान्तिक|सैद्धांतिक|सैद्धान्तिकः
सैद्धान्तिक सैद्धान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सिद्-<BR>धान्त), belonging or relating to a dogma or estab-<BR>lished truth; one who knows the real truth; relating<BR>to an astronomical text-book or to any scientific text-<BR>book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनापत्य|सैनापत्यं
सैनापत्य सैनापत्य, सैनिक. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धव|सैंधव|सैन्धवं|सैन्धवः
सैन्धव सैन्धव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सिन्धु), pro-<BR>duced or born in Sindh or in the country near the<BR>Indus; belonging to the Indus; river-born; belong-<BR>ing to the sea, oceanic, marine, aquatic; (अस्), m. a<BR>horse (particular one bred in Sindh); N. of a Muni;<BR>of a family; of a country; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a kind<BR>of rock-salt (found in the country near the Indus);<BR>(ई), f., N. of one of the Rāgiṇīs or personified<BR>musical scales; (अम्), n. (in dramatic literature) a<BR>kind of song in Prākṛt words accompanied with<BR>music expressive of disappointment in the keeping<BR>of an assignation; (आस्), m. pl. the people inhabit-<BR>ing Sindh or the country near the Indus.<BR>—सैन्-<BR>धव-घन, अस्, m. a lump of salt.<BR>—सैन्धव-<BR>शिला, f. ‘Sindh-rock,’ a kind of rock or fossil-salt.<BR>—सैन्धवारण्य (˚व-अर्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>jungly district of Sindhu or the Indus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धवक|सैंधवक|सैन्धवकः
सैन्धवक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating<BR>to the Saindhavas; (अस्), m. a miserable inhabitant<BR>of Sindhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धवायन
सैन्धवायन, अस्, m., N. of a teacher of the<BR>Atharva-veda; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a family (supposed<BR>to have been descended from Viśvā-mitra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धी|सैंधी
सैन्धी सैन्धी, f. (according to Śabda-k.)<BR>spirituous liquor (especially that prepared from the<BR>fermented juice of the palm).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्य|सैन्यं|सैन्यः
सैन्य सैन्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैमन्तिक|सैमंतिक|सैमंतिकं|सैमन्तिकं
सैमन्तिक सैमन्तिक, अम्, n. (fr. सीमन्त),<BR>red-lead (so called because used to make a mark<BR>along the parting of the hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरन्ध्र|सैरंध्र|सैरंध्रः|सैरन्ध्रः
सैरन्ध्र सैरन्-ध्र, अस्, m. (probably fr. an<BR>unused word सीरन्-ध्र, derived fr. सीर, ‘a plough,’<BR>+ ध्र for धर, ‘holding,’ cf. मही-ध्र, अं-<BR>स-ध्री), a kind of menial or domestic servant (em-<BR>ployed to dress his master, and, though not a slave,<BR>required to perform various servile offices; he is<BR>employed also in the chase, and constitutes a kind of<BR>mixed tribe or caste, being originally the offspring<BR>of a Dasyu and an Ayogava female; see Manu X.<BR>32); any menial servant or attendant; (ई), f. a maid-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">Page1136-a+ 72</a>]<BR>servant or female attendant in the women's apart-<BR>ments (= भुजिष्या), a woman of the mixed tribe<BR>described above; an independent female artizan<BR>working in another person's house; epithet of Drau-<BR>padī, wife of the Pāṇḍava princes, (when these five<BR>princes entered the service of king Virāṭa in various<BR>disguises, Draupadī became servant-maid and needle-<BR>woman in the same king's household; see Mahā-bh.<BR>Virāṭa-parvan 77.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिन्ध्र|सैरिंध्र|सैरिंध्रः|सैरिन्ध्रः
सैरिन्ध्र for सैरन्-ध्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिन्ध्री|सैरिंध्री
सैरिन्ध्री for सैरन्-ध्री above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरावत्|सैरावन्त्
सैरावत् सैरा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (according to<BR>Sāy. connected with इरा, ‘food;’ according to others<BR>perhaps connected with सीर), Ved. having plenty<BR>of provisions (said of a ship).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिक|सैरिकः
सैरिक सैरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सीर), relating<BR>or belonging to a plough; having furrows; (अस्), m.<BR>a plough-ox; a ploughman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरीय|सैरीयः
सैरीय or सैरीयक, अस्, m. ‘turned up by the<BR>plough,’ the plant Barleria Cristata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरेय|सैरेयः
सैरेय or सैरेयक, अस्, m. = सैरीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिन्ध्र|सैरिंध्र|सैरिंध्रः|सैरिन्ध्रः
सैरिन्ध्र सैरिन्ध्र. See under सैरन्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिभ|सैरिभः
सैरिभ सैरिभ, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with सीर), a buffalo; Indra's heaven, Svarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैर्य
सैर्य सैर्य, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैवाल|सैवालं
सैवाल सैवाल, अम्, n. (= शैवाल), the<BR>aquatic plant Vallisneria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैसक
सैसक सैसक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सीस), leaden, of<BR>lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सो
सो 1. सो (usually found with preposi-<BR>tions, see अव-सो, व्य्-अव-सो, अध्य्-अव-सो,<BR>पर्य्-अव-सो, &c.), cl. 4. P. स्यति, ससौ (2nd sing.<BR>ससिथ or ससाथ, 1st du. ससिव), सास्यति, असात्<BR>or असासीत्, Prec. सेयात्, सातुम्, to destroy, kill; to<BR>bring to an end, finish, complete: Pass. सीयते, Aor.<BR>असायि: Caus. साययति (or, according to some, सा-<BR>पयति), &c.: Desid. सिषासति: Intens. सेषीयते,<BR>सासाति, सासेति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साय|सायं|सायः
साय, अस्, m. end, close, &c. See p. 1109, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
3. सित, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see under rt. सि; for 2.<BR>see p. 1113, col. 2), destroyed, brought to an end,<BR>finished, completed, concluded; ascertained, known;<BR>(अस्), m. an arrow (probably for शित, cf. सायक,<BR>शायक).<BR>—सिताग्र (˚त-अग्˚), अस्, m. = शिताग्र, a<BR>thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिति|सितिः
3. सिति, इस्, f. destruction; [cf. 2. प्र-सिति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेय
सेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be destroyed; to be com-<BR>pleted or effected; (अम्), n. completion, effecting;<BR>[cf. शत-स्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सो
2. सो, सोस्, f., N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढ|सोढः
सोढ सोढ, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. 1. सह्), borne,<BR>suffered, endured; patient, enduring; (अस्), m. a<BR>proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढवत्
सोढवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has borne or en-<BR>dured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढाय
सोढाय, Nom. A. सोढायते, &c., to bear, en-<BR>dure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढृ
सोढृ, ढा, ढ्री, ढृ, a bearer, one who bears<BR>or suffers, patient, enduring; able, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोतृ
सोतृ सोतृ. See p. 1117, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्कण्ठ|सोत्कंठ|सोत्कण्ठः
सोत्कण्ठ सोत्कण्ठ (स-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ar-<BR>dently longing, impatiently eager; regretful; bewail-<BR>ing, sorrowing; (अम्), ind. with ardent or eager<BR>longing; regretfully, sorrowfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्कम्प
