सोभ्य
सोभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in or belonging<BR>to Sobha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोभरि
सोभरि सोभरि, इस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the hymns Ṛg-veda VIII. 19 — 22, &c. (having the<BR>patronymic Kāṇva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोभाञ्जन|सोभाञ्जनः
सोभाञ्जन सोभाञ्जन, अस्, m. (= शोभाञ्-<BR>जन), the tree Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोम|सोमं|सोमः
सोम सोम, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 139. fr. rt. 3. सु, ‘to distil or extract or sprinkle,’<BR>but connected by some with rt. 4. सु, ‘to generate,’<BR>the act of expressing the Soma juice being compared<BR>to the act of begetting), a particular climbing plant,<BR>Sarcostema Viminalis or Asclepias Acida (said to grow<BR>abundantly on the mountains of India and Persia;<BR>this celebrated plant, sometimes called ‘the moon-<BR>plant’ and perhaps a kind of milk-weed, was for-<BR>merly a most important ingredient in sacrificial offer-<BR>ings, and is perpetually alluded to in Vedic literature<BR>as well as in the Persian Avesta; it was collected by<BR>moon-light on certain mountains [in Ṛg-veda X. 34,<BR>1. the mountain Mūja-vat is mentioned], stripped of<BR>its numerous leaves, and then carried to the place of<BR>sacrifice; the stalks having been there crushed be-<BR>tween stones by the priests were sprinkled with<BR>water and placed on a sieve or strainer for purifica-<BR>tion [see पावमान], whence, after further pressure,<BR>the acid juice trickled into a vessel called Droṇa;<BR>after which it was mixed with clarified butter, flour,<BR>&c., made to ferment, and then offered in libations<BR>to the gods or drunk by the Brāhmans, by both of<BR>whom its exhilarating or intoxicating qualities were<BR>supposed to be highly prized; it is sometimes de-<BR>scribed as having been brought from the sky by a<BR>Śyena or falcon, and guarded by the Gandharvas;<BR>sometimes as having been brought by the Gāyatrī in<BR>the form of a bird, or by the daughter of the Sun,<BR>from a spot where it had been nourished by the<BR>rain-god Parjanya, who is represented in Ṛg-veda<BR>IX. 82, 3. as its father, the god Soma being else-<BR>where described as rejoicing in the society of the<BR>waters; all the 114 hymns of the ninth Maṇḍala of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1137-a" target="_blank">Page1137-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the Ṛg-veda, besides many others throughout this<BR>Veda and the whole Sāma-veda, are devoted to the<BR>praise of this plant, the use of which seems now to<BR>be little known, though in some parts of India<BR>Soma sacrifices are still offered; for the connection<BR>between the Soma ceremonies and the Sāma-veda<BR>see साम-वेद; this Veda distinguishes two kinds<BR>of Soma, one said to be green and the other yellow,<BR>but the golden-coloured is described as most cele-<BR>brated; the more modern Su-śruta, q. v., on the<BR>other hand, distinguishes twenty-four varieties of the<BR>Soma plant); the intoxicating and invigorating juice<BR>of the above plant (which, in the Vedic period, was<BR>regarded as a kind of Amṛta or nectar, conferring<BR>eternal life and vigour on the drinkers of it, whether<BR>gods or men, and was offered to the gods to pro-<BR>pitiate them and make them accede to the petitions<BR>of their worshippers, see above); the above plant or<BR>its juice personified (and constantly deified in the Veda,<BR>and in its character of a god represented as primeval,<BR>all-powerful, all-pervading, healing all diseases, lord of<BR>all other gods, and identified with the very supreme<BR>Being himself; this worship of Soma by the Hindūs<BR>of the Vedic age is thought to possess great<BR>community of character with that of Dionysus and<BR>Bacchus by the Greeks and Romans; Soma is<BR>regarded as the author of Ṛg-veda X. 124, 1, 5 — 9);<BR>nectar, the beverage of the gods; water; the moon<BR>or its deity (to whom the name Soma, which first<BR>belonged to the plant only, came to be applied in<BR>Post-vedic mythology, traces of this application being<BR>also observable in Ṛg-veda X. 85, in Atharva-veda<BR>XI. 6, 7, and in several passages of the Śatapatha-<BR>Brāhmaṇa; in the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa I. 22, Brahmā is<BR>said to have appointed Soma or the moon to be the<BR>‘monarch of planets, of plants, of sacrifices, and<BR>penances,’ and one of the names of the moon is<BR>Oṣadhi-pati or Oṣadhīśa, ‘lord of herbs;’ again,<BR>at the churning of the ocean, as described in the<BR>Purāṇas, after all sorts of medicinal plants and heal-<BR>ing herbs &c. are thrown in, three of the precious<BR>things said to be produced are Soma, ‘the moon,’<BR>Amṛta, ‘nectar,’ and Surā, ‘spirituous liquor,’ and<BR>in other legends this nectar is said to be preserved in<BR>the body of the moon; in Manu V. 96, Soma is<BR>called one of the eight Loka-pālas or guardians of<BR>the world); a ray of light (= दीधिति, according<BR>to Śabda-k.); air, wind; camphor; a particular<BR>drug of supposed magical properties; a particular<BR>mountain or mountainous range, (according to some)<BR>the mountains of the moon; a particular class of<BR>Pitṛs, (probably for सोम-पा); N. of a monkey<BR>chief; of Kuvera; of Yama; of one of the Vasus,<BR>(see वसु); of Śiva; of the author of a law-book;<BR>of the author of the Rāga-vibodha; (आ), f., N. of<BR>an Apsaras; (अम्), n. rice-water, rice-gruel; heaven,<BR>sky, ether.<BR>—सोम-कवि, इस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—सोम-कान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, moon-beloved; lovely<BR>as the moon; (अस्), m. the moon-gem, moon-stone<BR>(= चन्द्र-कान्त, q. v.); N. of a king of Saurāṣṭra.<BR>—सोम-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. delighting in Soma.<BR>—सोम-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra.<BR>—सोम-क्षय, अस्, m. disappearance of<BR>the moon, new moon.<BR>—सोम-गर्भ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सोम-गिरि, इस्, m. ‘moon-mountain,’<BR>N. of a mythical mountain.<BR>—सोम-गोपा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, having Soma as protector.<BR>—सोम-ग्रह, अस्,<BR>m. a vessel for taking up the Soma.<BR>—सोम-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, moon-produced, moon-born; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of the planet Mercury or Budha; (अम्), n.<BR>milk.<BR>—सोम-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place of pil-<BR>grimage in the west of India (= प्रभास, q. v.).<BR>—सोम-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a king of Vaiśālī;<BR>(आ), f., N. of the wife of Yajña-soma.<BR>—सोम-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Kathā-sarit-<BR>sāgara.<BR>—सोम-दैवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having Soma<BR>as a deity, presided over by Soma.<BR>—सोम-धान,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. holding or containing Soma (as a<BR>bowl).<BR>—सोम-धारा, f. ‘Soma-holding,’ the sky,<BR>heaven.<BR>—सोम-नन्दीश्वर (˚दि-ईश्˚), N. of a<BR>Liṅga.<BR>—सोम-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘Soma's lord, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1137-b" target="_blank">Page1137-b+ 81</a>]<BR>divinity set up by Soma,’ N. of a celebrated Liṅga,<BR>i. e. columnar emblem of Śiva or of the place or<BR>temple where it was set up, (this temple was<BR>established in the town described below, and was<BR>one of the twelve celebrated Liṅga temples which<BR>in various parts of India are held in especial venera-<BR>tion; the legend relates that the god Soma or the<BR>moon propitiated Śiva by performing great austerities<BR>on the spot, whereupon Śiva granted him a boon,<BR>and Soma in return set up a Liṅga on the place<BR>where he had done penance; the temple built there<BR>was so famed for its splendor and enormous wealth<BR>that it attracted the celebrated Mahmūd of Ghaznī,<BR>A. D. 1024, who, under pretext of destroying its<BR>idols, carried off its treasures along with its renowned<BR>gates); N. of several persons.<BR>—सोमनाथ-तीर्थ,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—सोमनाथ-पत्तन, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a town on the western coast of India (com-<BR>monly called Somnath Pattan in the peninsula of<BR>Kattywar and province of Guzerat; it was celebrated<BR>for the temple of Śiva above described).<BR>—सोम-<BR>प, अस्, m. one who drinks the Soma juice (especially<BR>at a sacrifice); a Soma sacrificer; a class of Pitṛs,<BR>(see सोम-पा.)<BR>—सोम-पति, इस्, m., Ved. ‘lord of<BR>Soma,’ epithet of Indra.<BR>—सोम-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a<BR>sort of grass, Saccharum Cylindricum.<BR>—सोम-पर्-<BR>वन्, अ, n., Ved. the time for preparing the Soma.<BR>—सोम-पा, आस्, m. (acc. pl. सोम-पस्, dat. sing.<BR>सोम-पे, see Gram. 108. अ), a drinker of Soma<BR>juice (especially at a sacrifice); a Soma sacrificer;<BR>the performer of a sacrifice; a Pitṛ of a particular<BR>class (said to be especially the progenitors of the<BR>Brāhmans).<BR>—सोमपा-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>drinking much Soma, very fond of Soma.<BR>—सोम-<BR>पान, अम्, n. the drinking of the Soma juice.<BR>—सोम-पाल, अस्, m. a preserver of Soma, (pro-<BR>bably) a provider or seller of the Soma plant; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. epithet of the Gandharvas (as keeping especial<BR>guard over the Soma).<BR>—सोम-पावन्, आ, m., Ved.<BR>a Soma drinker.<BR>—सोम-पीति, इस्, f. drinking Soma,<BR>a draught of Soma; a Soma sacrifice.<BR>—सोम-पीतिन्,<BR>ई, m. a drinker of the Soma juice.<BR>—सोम-पीथ,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. a draught of Soma; [cf. गो-पीथ.]<BR>—सोम-पीथिन्, ई, m. a Soma drinker.<BR>—सोम-<BR>पीविन्, ई, m. (doubtful), a Soma drinker.<BR>—सोम-पु-<BR>त्र, अस्, m. ‘son of the moon,’ the planet Mercury.<BR>—सोम-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. touching Soma,<BR>sprinkling Soma, (Sāy. = सोम-स्प्रष्टृ, सोमाभि-<BR>षव-कर्तृ, Ṛg-veda VIII. 63, 2.)<BR>—सोम-पेय,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. a sacrifice in which Soma is drunk,<BR>a Soma libation.<BR>—सोम-प्रतीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having Soma at the head.<BR>—सोम-प्रभा, f., N. of<BR>a female.<BR>—सोम-प्रयोग, अस्, m., N. of a treatise.<BR>—सोम-प्रवाक, अस्, m. ‘Soma-sacrifice-an-<BR>nouncer,’ a person commissioned to engage Śrotriyas<BR>or sacrificial priests for a Soma sacrifice.<BR>—सोम-<BR>बन्धु, उस्, m. ‘friend of the moon,’ the white<BR>esculent water-lily (as expanding at night).<BR>—सोम-<BR>भव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—सोम-भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ,<BR>Soma-born, belonging to the family of the moon;<BR>(ऊस्), m. ‘son of Soma,’ epithet of Budha (regent of<BR>the planet Mercury and supposed founder of the<BR>lunar dynasty); one of the persons called Vāsudevas<BR>by the Jainas.<BR>—सोम-यज्ञ, अस्, m. a Soma sacri-<BR>fice, an offering or libation of the juice of the acid<BR>Asclepias.<BR>—सोम-याग, अस्, m. a great triennial<BR>sacrifice in which the Soma juice is drunk.<BR>—सोम-<BR>याजिन्, ई, m. a Soma-yāga sacrificer (who also drinks<BR>the Soma juice at the ceremony).<BR>—सोम-योगिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, being in conjunction with the moon.<BR>—सोम-<BR>योनि, इस्, m. a sort of yellow and very fragrant<BR>sandal.<BR>—सोम-रस, अस्, m. the juice of the Soma<BR>plant.<BR>—सोम-राजकि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a Gotra.<BR>—सोम-राजन्, आ, -ज्ञी, अ, having the Soma plant<BR>as king, (Atharva-veda VIII. 1, 17); (आ), m., N. of<BR>a Muni.<BR>—सोम-राजिका, f. = सोम-राजिन् below.<BR>—सोम-राजिन्, ई, m. the medicinal plant Serratula<BR>or Vernonia Anthelmintica.<BR>—सोम-राजी, f. = सोम-<BR>राजिन् above; a particular metre consisting of six<BR>syllables.<BR>—सोम-राष्ट्र, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—सोम-रोग, अस्, m. a particular disease incident<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1137-c" target="_blank">Page1137-c+ 81</a>]<BR>to women.<BR>—सोम-रौद्र, अम्, n., N. of a sacred<BR>text; [cf. सोमा-रौद्र.]<BR>—सोम-लता, f. the<BR>moon-plant Sarcostema Viminalis, (see सोम, col. 1);<BR>N. of the river Godāvarī.<BR>—सोम-लतिका, f. a par-<BR>ticular shrub (= गुडूची).<BR>—सोम-वंश, अस्, m.<BR>‘the family or race of the moon,’ the lunar dynasty<BR>or line of kings supposed to be descended from<BR>Soma, ‘the moon,’ and his son Budha, (in this line<BR>came Puru, Yadu, Dushyanta, Kṛṣṇa, Bharata,<BR>Kuru, Dhṛta-rāṣṭra, and Pāṇḍu, see चन्द्र-<BR>वंश; it was one of the two great lines of ancient<BR>Hindū kings, the other being called Solar, see सूर्य-<BR>वंश); N. of Yudhi-ṣṭhira (as belonging to this<BR>line).<BR>—सोम-वंशिन्, ई, m. a prince or king of the<BR>lunar dynasty.<BR>—१. सोम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>Soma (said of the Himālaya district), having Soma<BR>juice; having the moon, lunar.<BR>—२. सोम-वत्, ind.<BR>like the moon.<BR>—सोम-वल्क, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>white Khadira, Mimosa Catechu; a medicinal plant<BR>(commonly called Kāyaphal, = कट्-फल); the<BR>plant Karañja; another kind (= रीठा-करञ्ज).<BR>—सोम-वल्लरि, इस्, or सोम-वल्लरी, f. the moon-<BR>plant Sarcostema Viminalis; a kind of vegetable<BR>(= ब्रह्मी).<BR>—सोम-वल्लिका, f. the moon-plant;<BR>the plant Vernonia Anthelmintica.<BR>—सोम-वल्ली,<BR>f. the moon-plant, (see सोम above); the shrub<BR>Cocculus Cordifolius (= यज्ञ-वल्ली); the medicinal<BR>plant Vernonia Anthelmintica; other plants (=<BR>ब्राह्मी; = पाताल-गरुडी; = सु-दर्शना).<BR>—सो-<BR>म-वह्नि-प्रकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, bright as the fire<BR>of the moon.<BR>—सोम-वामिन्, ई, m. ‘Soma-vomiter,’<BR>a priest who has drunk so much Soma juice that he<BR>is obliged to vomit it out of his mouth.<BR>—सोम-<BR>वार, अस्, m. ‘moon-day,’ Monday.<BR>—सोमवार-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n. a kind of religious observance per-<BR>formed in the evening and consisting of the worship<BR>of Śiva and Durgā preceded by fasting every Mon-<BR>day.<BR>—सोम-विक्रयिन्, ई, m. a vendor of Soma<BR>juice.<BR>—सोम-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the medicinal plant<BR>Kaṭ-phala; the white Khadira; Vernonia Anthel-<BR>mintica.<BR>—सोम-शकला, f. ‘resembling a portion<BR>of the moon,’ a kind of cucumber (= शशाण्डुली).<BR>—सोम-शम्भु, उस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—सोम-<BR>शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king (belonging to the<BR>Maurya dynasty); of a Muni; of a merchant.<BR>—सोम-शुष्म, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—सो-<BR>म-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of a merchant.<BR>—सोम-<BR>संस्था, f., N. of the fifth division of the Jyo-<BR>tiṣṭoma sacrifice, (seven Soma-saṃsthās are enume-<BR>rated, viz. Agni-ṣṭoma, Aty-agniṣṭoma, Ukthya,<BR>Ṣoḍaśin, Ati-rātra, Vāja-peya, and Aptor-yāma.)<BR>—सोम-सञ्ज्ञ, अम्, n. ‘Soma-named,’ camphor.<BR>—सोम-सद्, त्, m. a Pitṛ of a peculiar class (de-<BR>scribed as progenitor of the celestial beings called<BR>Sādhyas, Manu III. 195).<BR>—सोम-सार, अस्, m.<BR>the white Khadira tree.<BR>—सोम-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m.<BR>‘the Soma doctrine,’ N. of a particular astronomical<BR>text-book; a particular Tantra doctrine or system of<BR>philosophy followed by a sect of Śaivas and regarded<BR>as unorthodox, (it is personified in the Third Act of<BR>the Prabodha-candrodaya); one who holds the above<BR>system of doctrines; a particular Buddha.<BR>—सोम-<BR>सिद्धान्तिन्, ई, m. one who knows the Soma-sid-<BR>dhānta; a follower of the above sect of the Śaivas,<BR>a rationalist of the above school.<BR>—सोम-सिन्धु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘ocean of Soma,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—सोम-<BR>सुत्, त्, m. a Soma-distiller, Soma-sprinkler, a priest<BR>who offers the Soma juice at a sacrifice.<BR>—सोम-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of the moon,’ epithet of Budha,<BR>q. v.; (आ), f. ‘daughter of the moon,’ the river<BR>Narma-dā or Nerbudda.<BR>—सोमसुत्-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, possessing offerers of Soma juice (said of a her-<BR>mitage, a sacrifice, &c.).<BR>—सोम-सुत्वन्, आ, m., Ved.<BR>one who offers Soma libations.<BR>—सोम-सुन्दर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—सोम-सूक्त, अम्,<BR>n. a hymn in honour of Soma.<BR>—सोम-सूत्र, अम्,<BR>n. a channel for conveying water from a Śiva-liṅga<BR>or a kind of receptacle to receive the water with<BR>which the idol has been bathed.<BR>—सोमसूत्र-प्र-<BR>दक्षिणा, f. circumambulation around Śiva's idol<BR>in such a way as that the Soma-sūtra shall not be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">Page1138-a+ 76</a>]<BR>crossed.<BR>—सोम-सूर्य-प्रकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, bright<BR>as the sun and moon.<BR>—सोम-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king of Campaka-pura.<BR>—सोमाख्य (˚म-आख्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the red lotus.<BR>—सोमातिपूत (˚म-अत्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, excessively purified by the Soma juice (which,<BR>if drunk in excess, is supposed to pass through the<BR>nose, ears, and other apertures of the body).<BR>—सो-<BR>मानन्द (˚म-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—सोमानन्द-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—सोमा-पूषणा, m. du., Ved. Soma and Pūṣan.<BR>—सोमाभ (˚म-आभ), अस्, आ, अम्, like the moon;<BR>(आ), f. epithet of Candrāvalī, q. v.<BR>—सोमाभिषव<BR>(˚म-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the distilling or extracting of<BR>Soma juice.<BR>—सोमा-रुद्र-सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Vedic hymn, (see the next.)<BR>—सोमा-रौद्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the four Vedic texts beginning with or<BR>containing the word Somā-rudrā, (these occur in<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 74, 1 — 4; cf. Atharva-veda VII. 42,<BR>Manu XI. 254.)<BR>—सोमार्क-प्रतिसङ्काश (˚म-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, resembling the sun and moon.<BR>—सोमाह (˚म-अह्˚), अस्, m. ‘moon-day,’ Monday.<BR>—सोमाहुति (˚म-आह्˚), इस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>the hymns Ṛg-veda II. 4-7 (having the patronymic<BR>Bhārgava).<BR>—सोमेश्वर (˚म-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘Soma's<BR>lord, the divinity set up by Soma,’ N. of a celebrated<BR>representation of Śiva (supposed to have been set<BR>up by Soma at Benares) or of the place where it<BR>was established, (see सोम-नाथ); of an author;<BR>of a poet; of the author of a work on music; of the<BR>author of the Nyāya-sudhā commentary; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a Liṅga at Benares.<BR>—सोमोत्पत्ति (˚म-उत्˚),<BR>इस्, f. the production or origin of Soma; N. of a<BR>Pariśiṣṭa of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—सोमोद्भव (˚म-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, moon-produced, sprung from the<BR>moon; (आ), f. the river Narma-dā or modern Ner-<BR>budda (so called either as supposed to be descended<BR>from the moon or as the source of celestial nectar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमक
सोमक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Saha-deva and<BR>grandfather of Drupada; of a particular Bharaṭaka or<BR>mendicant; (आस्), m. pl. the family of Drupada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमन्
सोमन्, आ, m. the moon; a Soma sacrificer, an<BR>offerer of libations (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमाल|सोमालः
सोमाल, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to some a Prākṛt<BR>corruption for सु-कुमार; cf. कोमल), resembling<BR>the moon, soft, bland, placid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमिन्
सोमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, offering Soma, performing the<BR>Soma sacrifice; (ई), m. a performer of a Soma sacri-<BR>fice; (इनी), f. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोम्य
सोम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of Soma; offering<BR>Soma; shaped like Soma; resembling the moon,<BR>soft, good, amiable, (सोम्य, voc. c. ‘my good Sir,’<BR>used in addressing; cf. सौम्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिक
सौमिक, सौम्य. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमिल
सोमिल सोमिल, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमिलक
सोमिलक सोमिलक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोराष्ट्रिक
सोराष्ट्रिक सोराष्ट्रिक, अस्, m. = सौराष्-<BR>ट्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोलङ्क
सोलङ्क सोलङ्क, अस्, m., N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्कालातावपोथिक
सोल्कालातावपोथिक सोल्कालातावपोथिक<BR>(स-उल्का-अलात-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, with machines<BR>for hurling down fire-brands and lighted darts (on<BR>an enemy; these machines appear to have been a<BR>kind of catapult or ballista).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठ|सोल्लुंठ|सोल्लुंठः|सोल्लुण्ठः
सोल्लुण्ठ सोल्लुण्ठ (स-उल्˚), अस्, m. irony,<BR>sarcasm, ridicule.<BR>—सोल्लुण्ठ-वचन, अम्, n. or<BR>सोल्लुण्ठोक्ति (˚ठ-उक्˚), इस्, f. an ironical expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठन|सोल्लुंठन|सोल्लुंठनं|सोल्लुण्ठनं
सोल्लुण्ठन, अम्, n. apparent praise and covert<BR>censure, irony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोष्मन्
सोष्मन् सोष्मन् (स-उष्˚ or स-ऊष्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, having heat, warm; (in grammar) having aspi-<BR>ration, aspirated (said of the aspirated letters ख्, घ्,<BR>छ्, झ्, ठ्, ढ्, थ्, ध्, फ्, भ्, also of the sibilants<BR>and the letter ह्); (आ), m. an aspirated letter, aspi-<BR>rate.<BR>—सोष्म-ता, f. the state or condition of being<BR>aspirated, aspiration.<BR>—सोष्म-वत्, आन्, m. ‘having<BR>an aspirate,’ an aspirated word or syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोहम्
सोऽहम् सोऽहम्, nom. sing. m. I myself,<BR>(see तद्, p. 360.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोहलग्राम
सोहलग्राम सोहल-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर|सौकरः
सौकर सौकर, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सूकर), be-<BR>longing or relating to a hog, hoggish, swinish; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a district.<BR>—सौकर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकरकतीर्थ
सौकरक-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकरिक|सौकरिकः
सौकरिक, अस्, m. a hunter; N. of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर्य|सौकर्यं|सौकर्य्य|सौकर्य्यं
1. सौकर्य, अम्, n. hoggishness, swinishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकरायण
सौकरायण सौकरायण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>teacher of the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर्य|सौकर्यं|सौकर्य्य|सौकर्य्यं
सौकर्य 2. सौकर्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-कर),<BR>easiness of performance, practicability, feasibility,<BR>facility; adroitness; easy and extempore preparation<BR>of food or medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकुमार्य|सौकुमार्यं|सौकुमार्य्य
सौकुमार्य सौकुमार्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-कु-<BR>मार), youthfulness, tenderness, delicacy; softness,<BR>fineness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकृत्य
सौकृत्य सौकृत्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-कृत),<BR>strictness in performing religious acts, piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौक्ष्म्य|सौक्ष्म्यं
सौक्ष्म्य सौक्ष्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. सूक्ष्म),<BR>minuteness, fineness, subtilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौक्ष्मक|सौक्ष्मकः
सौक्ष्मक, अस्, m. a kind of small animal or<BR>insect, (perhaps) a grub or maggot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखशायनिक|सौखशायनिकः
सौखशायनिक सौखशायनिक, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>सुख-शयन), one who asks another whether he<BR>has slept well; [cf. सौस्नातिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखशायिक|सौखशायिकः
सौखशायिक, अस्, m. (fr. सुख-शायिन्), = the<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखसुप्तिक|सौखसुप्तिकः
सौखसुप्तिक सौखसुप्तिक, अस्, m. (fr. सुख-<BR>सुप्ति), one who asks another whether he has slept<BR>well; a bard or minstrel whose duty is to waken<BR>kings in the morning with music and song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौख्य|सौख्यं
सौख्य सौख्य, अम्, n. (fr. सुख), pleasure,<BR>happiness, felicity, enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखिक|सौखिकः
सौखिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to pleasure, pleasur-<BR>able, sensual, pleasure-seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखीय
सौखीय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to pleasure or<BR>enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगत|सौगतः
सौगत सौगत, अस्, m. (fr. सु-गत), a fol-<BR>lower of Su-gata, q. v.; a Buddhist, (the Buddhists<BR>are said to be divided into four classes or schools,<BR>viz. Mādhyamikas, Yogācāras, Sautrāntikas, and<BR>Vaibhāṣikas); N. of a son of Daśa-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगतिक|सौगतिकः
सौगतिक, अस्, m. a Buddhist; a Buddhist or<BR>Brāhman mendicant; an atheist, heretic, unbeliever;<BR>(अम्), n. unbelief, scepticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध|सौगंध|सौगन्धं|सौगन्धः
सौगन्ध सौगन्ध, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सु-गन्-<BR>ध), possessing a fragrant odour, sweet-scented,<BR>fragrant; (अम्), n. sweet-scentedness, fragrance; a<BR>particular fragrant grass (= कत्-तृण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धिक|सौगंधिक|सौगन्धिकं|सौगन्धिकः
सौगन्धिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, sweet-scented,<BR>fragrant; (अस्), m. a dealer in perfumes; sulphur;<BR>N. of a mountain; (आ), f. a kind of lotus; (अम्),<BR>n. the white water-lily, the blue lotus; a kind of<BR>fragrant grass (= कत्-तृण); a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध्य|सौगंध्य|सौगंध्यं|सौगन्ध्यं
सौगन्ध्य, अम्, n. sweetness of odour, fra-<BR>grance, perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगम्य|सौगम्यं
सौगम्य सौगम्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-गम),<BR>easiness of access, easiness of attainment, facility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचि|सौचिः
सौचि सौचि, इस्, m. (fr. सूचि; cf. सूचिक),<BR>one who lives by his needle, a tailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचिक|सौचिकः
सौचिक, अस्, m. = सौचि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचीक
सौचीक सौचीक, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>the Vedic Ṛṣi Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजन्य|सौजन्यं
सौजन्य सौजन्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-जन),<BR>goodness, generosity, kindness, compassion, bene-<BR>volence, clemency; friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजात
सौजात सौजात, अस्, m. (fr. सु-जात), N. of<BR>a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौण्डी|सौंडी
सौण्डी सौण्डी, f. long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौति|सौतिः
सौति सौति, इस्, m. (fr. 2. सूत), N. of<BR>Karṇa, (so called from having been brought up by<BR>the charioteer [सूत] Adhi-ratha, see कर्ण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्य|सौत्यं
1. सौत्य, अम्, n. the office of a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्य|सौत्यं
सौत्य 2. सौत्य, अस्, &c. (fr. सुत्या), relating<BR>to Soma-pressing, sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्र|सौत्रः
सौत्र सौत्र, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सूत्र), belong-<BR>ing to a thread or string, having a thread, &c.;<BR>belonging to a Sūtra, mentioned or declared in<BR>Sūtras, according to rule or precept, preceptive, for-<BR>mulary; (अस्), m. a Brāhman; an artificial root<BR>occurring in grammatical Sūtras only and not capable<BR>of conversion into a verb, but used to form deriva-<BR>tive nouns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रान्तिक|सौत्रांतिक
सौत्रान्तिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of one of the four<BR>great schools or systems of Buddhism, (see सौगत;<BR>they are said to admit the authority of the Buddhist<BR>Sūtras but not of the Abhi-dharma.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रामणी
सौत्रामणी सौत्रामणी, f. (probably fr. सु-<BR>त्रामन्), a particular sacrifice (one of the seven<BR>Havir-yajñas; it is described as a substitute for the<BR>Soma sacrifice, spirituous liquors and milk being<BR>taken instead of Soma, and both liquids placed in the<BR>Soma vessels; animals are also immolated, one to<BR>the Aśvins, one to Sarasvatī, one to Indra, and<BR>one to Bṛhaspati; in Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa XII. 8,<BR>3, 31. it is said that every one who is consecrated<BR>by the Sautrāmaṇī enters among the gods and is<BR>born in the next world [सर्व-तनूः] with his<BR>entire body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदर्य|सौदर्यं
सौदर्य सौदर्य, अम्, n. (fr. सोदर), bro-<BR>therhood; (अस्, आ, अम्), having brotherhood with<BR>(at the end of a comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामनी
सौदामनी सौदामनी, f. (fr. सु-दामन्),<BR>lightning or a particular kind of lightning; N. of<BR>an Apsaras of Indra's heaven; of part of the Su-<BR>dāman mountain (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामिनी
सौदामिनी, f. a particular kind of lightning;<BR>lightning (in general); N. of an Apsaras of Indra's<BR>heaven; N. of a city or country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदाम्नी
सौदाम्नी, f. = सौदामनी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदायिक|सौदायिकं
सौदायिक सौदायिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सु-दाय),<BR>that which is given to a woman at her marriage by<BR>her father or mother or any relative and which there-<BR>fore becomes her own property; relating to such a<BR>present; (अम्), n. a nuptial gift or present (as de-<BR>scribed above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदास|सौदासः
सौदास सौदास, अस्, m. (fr. सु-दास), N. of<BR>a king of the solar race (a descendant of Ikṣvāku<BR>and Sagara in the thirteenth generation, son of king<BR>Su-dāsa, and also called Mitra-saha and Kalmāṣa-<BR>pāda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौध|सौधः
सौध सौध, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सुधा), relating<BR>or belonging to nectar, having nectar; having plaster;<BR>plastered, stuccoed; (अस्), m. a kind of plant, =<BR>दुग्ध-पाषाण; (अम्), n. a plastered or white-<BR>washed mansion; any great mansion or house; a<BR>palace, (also अस्, m. according to some); silver;<BR>opal (according to some).<BR>—सौध-कार, अस्, m. a<BR>plasterer, whitewasher; the builder or maker of a<BR>palace.<BR>—सौध-वास, अस्, m. a palatial dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधन्य
सौधन्य सौधन्य, अस्, &c. (probably fr.<BR>सु-धन), epithet of certain Dharmāḥ or laws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधन्वन|सौधन्वनः
सौधन्वन सौधन्वन, अस्, m. (fr. सु-धन्-<BR>वन्), a son or descendant of Su-dhanvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधातकि
सौधातकि सौधातकि, इस्, m. (fr. सु-धातृ),<BR>a patronymic, (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 97); N. of a hermit<BR>(pupil of Vālmīki).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधार|सौधारः
सौधार सौधार, अस्, m. (according to<BR>some) one of the fourteen parts or divisions of a<BR>drama, (a doubtful word.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधाल|सौधालं
सौधाल सौधाल, अम्, n. (probably to be<BR>connected with सौध, p. 1138), a temple of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन|सौनः
सौन सौन, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सूना), belonging<BR>or relating to a slaughter-house or to butchery, &c.;<BR>(अम्), n. butcher's meat; [cf. शौन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनधर्म्य
सौनधर्म्य, अम्, n. ‘the law or rule of<BR>butchery,’ a state of deadly hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनिक|सौनिकः
सौनिक, अस्, m. a butcher, vender of the flesh of<BR>beasts or birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्द|सौनंद|सौनंदं|सौनन्दं
सौनन्द सौनन्द, अम्, n. the club of Bala-<BR>rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्दिन्|सौनंदिन्
सौनन्दिन्, ई, m. ‘having Saunanda,’ epithet of<BR>Bala-rāma, (see p. 675.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन्दर्य|सौंदर्य|सौंदर्यं|सौन्दर्य्य|सौन्दर्य्यं
सौन्दर्य सौन्दर्य, अम्, n. (fr. सुन्दर),<BR>beauty, loveliness, handsomeness, gracefulness, ele-<BR>gance.<BR>—सौन्दर्य-लहरी, f., N. of a mystical<BR>poem ascribed to Śaṅkarācārya (= आनन्द-लहरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपन्थ्य
सौपन्थ्य सौपन्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. सु-<BR>पथ, according to some), connected with a good<BR>road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्ण|सौपर्णं
सौपर्ण सौपर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सु-पर्ण or<BR>सु-पर्णी, q. v.), belonging or relating to Su-parṇa<BR>or Su-parṇī; (अम्), n. dry ginger; the emerald; N. of<BR>a Vedic story which relates the transformation of the<BR>metres into birds that they might fetch the Soma from<BR>heaven; (ई), f. a kind of creeper (= पाताल-गरुडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्णेय|सौपर्णेयः
सौपर्णेय, अस्, m. a metronymic of Garuḍa; (ई),<BR>f. a female descendant of Su-parṇa; (आस्), pl. epithet<BR>of the metres (regarded as children of Su-parṇī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिक|सौप्तिकं
सौप्तिक सौप्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सुप्त), con-<BR>nected with or relating to sleep, somnolent, som-<BR>niferous, &c.; (अम्), n. a nocturnal combat; a night-<BR>attack, attack on sleeping men.<BR>—सौप्तिक-पर्वन्,<BR>अ, n., N. of the tenth book of the Mahā-bhārata<BR>(in which is described how the three surviving Kuru<BR>warriors, Aśvatthāman, Kṛta-varman, and Kṛpa,<BR>after the destruction of their army, determined on<BR>attacking the camp of the Pāṇḍavas by night and<BR>murdering them while asleep; this they accordingly<BR>did, Aśvatthāman entering the camp stealthily and,<BR>with the assistance of the god Śiva, slaughtering<BR>thousands, while the two others stood at the gate<BR>and killed all who attempted to escape; the whole<BR>Pāṇḍava army was thus destroyed, except the five<BR>Pāṇḍu princes themselves, with Kṛṣṇa and Sātyaki,<BR>who were stationed at some distance from the camp;<BR>a messenger having escaped conveyed the news to<BR>Yudhi-ṣṭhira, who, with his brothers and Draupadī,<BR>then returned to the camp and bewailed their<BR>slaughtered kindred).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबल|सौबलः
सौबल सौबल, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Śakuni (as son of Su-bala, king of Gāndhāra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबली
सौबली, f. a patronymic of Gāndhārī (daughter<BR>of Su-bala and wife of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबलेयी
सौबलेयी, f., N. of Gāndhārī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ|सौभं
सौभ सौभ, अम्, n. (for शौभ), N. of<BR>Hari-ścandra's city (suspended in mid-air); N. of a<BR>town of the Śālvas; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—सौभ-पति, इस्, or सौभ-राज, अस्, m. the king<BR>of Saubha or of the Saubhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभकि
सौभकि सौभकि, इस्, m., N. of Drupada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभग|सौभगं
सौभग सौभग, अम्, n. (fr. सु-भग),<BR>good luck, happiness; prosperity, riches, wealth.<BR>—सौभग-त्व, अम्, n. a state of prosperity, hap-<BR>piness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्य|सौभाग्यं
सौभाग्य, अम्, n. auspiciousness, good fortune,<BR>fortunateness, good luck; blessedness; beauty, grace,<BR>charm; the happy and auspicious state of wife-hood<BR>(as opposed to widowhood); affection, favour; con-<BR>gratulations, good wishes; the fourth of the astor-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">Page1139-b+ 71</a>]<BR>nomical Yogas; red lead; borax (टङ्कण).<BR>—सौ-<BR>भाग्य-काण्ड, N. of part of the Atharva-veda.<BR>—सौभाग्य-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m. a particular drug<BR>or medicine compounded of various medicaments.<BR>—सौभाग्य-चिह्न, अम्, n. any mark of good<BR>fortune or blessedness; any sign or token of the<BR>blessed state of wife-hood (e. g. red pigment on the<BR>forehead, the marriage string, &c.).<BR>—सौभाग्य-<BR>तन्तु, उस्, m. the marriage string (which is cast<BR>round the neck of the bride by the bridegroom at<BR>the wedding and worn till widowhood).<BR>—सौ-<BR>भाग्य-तृतीया, f. the third day of the light half of<BR>the month Bhādra.<BR>—सौभाग्य-देवता, f. an<BR>auspicious or tutelary deity.<BR>—सौभाग्य-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessing good fortune or blessedness,<BR>auspicious, fortunate; (अती), f. a married and un-<BR>widowed woman.<BR>—सौभाग्यवत्-ता, f. or सौ-<BR>भाग्यवत्-त्व, अम्, n. auspiciousness, prosperity.<BR>—सौभाग्य-वायन, अम्, n. auspicious offerings<BR>of sweetmeats, &c.<BR>—सौभाग्य-सुन्दरी-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्र|सौभद्रः
सौभद्र सौभद्र, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सु-भद्रा),<BR>belonging or relating to Su-bhadrā, q. v.; (अस्), m.<BR>‘son of Su-bhadrā,’ epithet of Abhimanyu; (अम्),<BR>n., scil. युद्ध, the war occasioned by the carrying<BR>off of Su-bhadrā, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्रेय|सौभद्रेयः
सौभद्रेय, अस्, m. a metronymic of Abhi-<BR>manyu; Beleric Myrobalan (= विभीतक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभर
सौभर सौभर, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Kuśika (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 127).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभरि|सौभरिः
सौभरि सौभरि, इस्, m., N. of a Muni<BR>(married to the fifty daughters of Māndhātṛ and<BR>father of 150 sons).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभरी
सौभरी सौभरी, f. (fr. सोभरि), Ved. a<BR>verse composed by Sobhari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभागिनेय|सौभागिनेयः
सौभागिनेय 1. सौभागिनेय, अस्, m. (fr. सु-<BR>भगा), the son of a favourite wife or of an<BR>honoured mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभागिनेय|सौभागिनेयः
सौभागिनेय 2. सौभागिनेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>सु-भागिनेय), belonging or relating to a good<BR>sister's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्य|सौभाग्यं
सौभाग्य सौभाग्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाञ्जन|सौभाञ्जनः
सौभाञ्जन सौभाञ्जन, अस्, m. = सोभाञ्-<BR>जन, शोभाञ्जन, the tree Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभिक|सौभिकः
सौभिक सौभिक, अस्, m. (for शौभिक), a<BR>juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ्रात्र|सौभ्रात्रं
सौभ्रात्र सौभ्रात्र, अम्, n. (fr. सु-भ्रातृ),<BR>good brotherhood, fraternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमदत्ति
सौमदत्ति सौमदत्ति, इस्, m. (fr. सोम-<BR>दत्त), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस
सौमनस सौमनस, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. सु-<BR>मनस्), agreeable to the feelings, pleasing; relating<BR>to flowers, floral, flowery; (अस्), m., N. of the eighth<BR>day of the civil month (= कर्म-मास); (आ), f. the<BR>outer skin of the nutmeg, = जाती-पत्त्री; (ई), f., N.<BR>of the fifth night of the civil month; (अम्), n.<BR>benevolence, kindness; pleasure, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्य|सौमनस्यं
सौमनस्य, अम्, n. satisfaction of mind, agree-<BR>ableness, enjoyment; a particular offering of flowers<BR>with holy texts placed in the hands of the priest at<BR>a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्यायनी
सौमनस्यायनी, f. the blossom of the Mālatī<BR>or great-flowering jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमायन|सौमायनः
सौमायन सौमायन, अस्, m. (fr. सोम), a<BR>patronymic of Budha; [cf. सौम्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिक
सौमिक सौमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सोम), per-<BR>formed with Soma juice (said of an oblation or<BR>sacrifice), relating to the Soma juice; relating to<BR>Soma or the moon, lunar; (ई), f. a particular sacrifice<BR>performed on the day of full moon (= दीक्षणी-<BR>येष्टि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्र|सौमित्रः
सौमित्र सौमित्र, अस्, m. (fr. सु-मित्रा), a<BR>metronymic of Lakṣmaṇa the younger brother of<BR>Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्रि|सौमित्रिः
सौमित्रि, इस्, m. = सौमित्र above; N. of a<BR>teacher of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिल्ल|सौमिल्लः
सौमिल्ल सौमिल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a dramatic<BR>writer (mentioned in the Mālavikāgnimitra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेचक|सौमेचकं
सौमेचक सौमेचक, अम्, n. (probably fr.<BR>सु-मेचक), gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेधिक|सौमेधिकः
सौमेधिक सौमेधिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 5. सु +<BR>मेधा), possessing supernatural knowledge or wis-<BR>dom; (अस्), m. a sage, seer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेरुक|सौमेरुकं
सौमेरुक सौमेरुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सु-मेरु),<BR>belonging to or coming from Su-meru; (अम्), n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्य|सौम्यः
सौम्य सौम्य, अस्, आ or मी, अम् (fr. सोम),<BR>belonging or relating to Soma or to the moon,<BR>sacred to Soma; having the nature or properties<BR>of Soma; resembling the moon; handsome, pleas-<BR>ing, good, mild, gentle, soft, benign, placid, (सौम्य,<BR>voc. c. ‘O gentle Sir,’ ‘O good Sir,’ used in address-<BR>ing another); auspicious; (अस्), m., N. of Budha or<BR>the planet Mercury (son of Soma); N. of the Vedic<BR>Ṛṣi Budha; a Brāhman (or the proper epithet by<BR>which he should be addressed, see Manu II. 125);<BR>N. of one of the nine Khaṇḍas or divisions of the earth<BR>or of Bharata-varṣa; epithet of the forty-third (or<BR>seventeenth) year of Jupiter's cycle of sixty years;<BR>epithet of certain signs of the zodiac (viz. Taurus,<BR>Cancer, Virgo, Scorpio, Capricornus); the Uḍumbara<BR>fig-tree; the Saumya penance, (see सौम्य-कृच्-<BR>छ्र); (in anatomy) the blood before it becomes<BR>red, serum; the gastric juice; = भास्वर (according<BR>to Śabda-k.); (आस्), m. pl., N. of the five stars in<BR>Orion's head, (also called इल्वल, q. v.); N. of a<BR>class of Pitṛs, (Manu III. 199); (आ), f., N. of<BR>Durgā; a particular metre; the moon-plant, (see<BR>सोम); various other plants, = मल्लिका; = शटी; =<BR>शाल-पर्णी; = गुञ्जा; = महिष-वल्ली; = महा-<BR>ज्योतिष्मती; = रुद्र-जटा; = महेन्द्र-वारुणी;<BR>(अम्), n., scil. अद्भुत, a particular kind of omen<BR>or prodigy (occurring in the Diva or sky).<BR>—सौम्य-<BR>कृच्छ्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind of religious penance<BR>(described as subsisting for five days, severally, on<BR>sesamum, the water of boiled rice, butter-milk<BR>mixed with water, water, and parched grain, and<BR>fasting on the sixth day).<BR>—सौम्य-गन्धी, f. the<BR>Indian white rose.<BR>—सौम्य-ग्रह, अस्, m. an<BR>auspicious or benign planet (such as Mercury, Ju-<BR>piter, Venus, and the full moon).<BR>—सौम्य-ता, f.<BR>or सौम्य-त्व, अम्, n. gentleness, mildness, be-<BR>nignity, placidity; benevolence; beauty.<BR>—सौम्य-<BR>धातु, उस्, m. (according to Śabda-k. f.), the<BR>phlegmatic humor, phlegm.<BR>—सौम्य-नामन्, आ,<BR>म्नी, अ, having a soft or agreeable name (or one<BR>easily pronounced; see Manu III. 10).<BR>—सौम्य-<BR>वपुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, of an agreeable form.<BR>—सौम्य-<BR>वार, अस्, m. ‘Mercury's day,’ Wednesday.<BR>—सौम्यो-<BR>पचार (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m. a mild or gentle remedy,<BR>mild measure or means of cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौयवस
सौयवस सौयवस, अस्, m. a son of Su-<BR>yavasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौयवसि
सौयवसि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौयामि
सौयामि सौयामि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर|सौरः
सौर सौर, अस्, ई, अम् (in some senses fr.<BR>सूर, in others fr. सुर), belonging or relating to<BR>the sun, solar; sacred to Sūrya or the sun; celestial,<BR>divine; relating to spirituous liquor; (अस्), m. a<BR>worshipper of the sun; the planet Saturn [cf. सूर-<BR>सुत]; a solar month (consisting of thirty risings<BR>and settings of the sun or the period during which<BR>the sun is in one sign of the zodiac); a representation<BR>of a solar zodiacal sign used at marriage ceremonies;<BR>a solar day; N. of a Guru; the Tumburu plant;<BR>(ई), f. the wife of the sun; (अम्), n., N. of a col-<BR>lection of hymns addressed to Sūrya (extracted from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">Page1140-a+ 76</a>]<BR>the Ṛg-veda).<BR>—सौर-ज, अस्, m. ‘sun-born,’ the<BR>Tumburu plant.<BR>—सौर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—सौर-दिवस, अस्, m.<BR>a solar day.<BR>—सौर-नक्त, अम्, n. a particular reli-<BR>gious observance (accompanied with ceremonial ablu-<BR>tions, worship of the sun, &c.).<BR>—सौर-भुवन,<BR>अम्, n. = सूर्य-लोक, q. v.<BR>—सौर-मास, अस्, m.<BR>a solar month.<BR>—सौर-संवत्सर, अस्, m. a solar<BR>year.<BR>—सौर-संहिता, f., N. of part of the Skanda-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—सौर-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m., N. of one of<BR>five ancient astronomical Siddhāntas or text-books,<BR>(see सिद्धान्त, cf. सूर्य-स्˚.)<BR>—सौर-सूक्त, अम्,<BR>n. a hymn addressed to Sūrya.<BR>—सौरोपपुराण<BR>(˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरक
सौरक, N. of a town founded by Surendra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसैन्धव|सौरसैंधव|सौरसैन्धवः
सौरसैन्धव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सुर-सिन्धु),<BR>belonging to the river Ganges, Gangetic; related to<BR>the Ganges (applicable as an epithet to Bhīṣma);<BR>(अस्), m. a horse of the Sun (in this sense com-<BR>pounded of सौर and सैन्धव, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरि|सौरिः
सौरि, इस्, m., N. of the planet Saturn (as son of<BR>the Sun); the tree Asana (q. v.); the plant Āditya-<BR>bhaktā (q. v.).<BR>—सौरि-रत्न, अम्, n. a particular<BR>gem (sapphire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरिक|सौरिकः
सौरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, celestial; spirituous, vinous; any-<BR>thing (such as money) due for spirits; (अस्), m. Saturn;<BR>heaven, paradise; a vender of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरी
सौरी, f. See above under सौर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरीय|सौरीयं
सौरीय, अस्, ई, अम्, solar, belonging or suitable to<BR>the sun (= सूर्याय हित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरेय|सौरेयः
सौरेय or सौरेयक, अस्, m. the white Barleria<BR>(a shrub bearing white flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर्य|सौर्य्य
सौर्य, अस्, ई, अम्, of or belonging to the sun,<BR>solar; (अस्), m. a patronymic of several Vedic Ṛṣis<BR>(authors of hymns in the Ṛg-veda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर्यायणि
सौर्यायणि, इस्, or सौर्यायणिन्, ई, m. a de-<BR>scendant of Saurya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरथ|सौरथः
सौरथ सौरथ, अस्, m. (fr. सु-रथ), a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ|सौरभं
सौरभ सौरभ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सु-रभि),<BR>fragrant; (अस्), m. a proper N.; (ई), f. a cow; a<BR>daughter of the cow Su-rabhi; (अम्), n. fragrance;<BR>saffron; N. of a commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभक
सौरभक, अम्, n. a particular metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेय|सौरभेयः
सौरभेय, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>Su-rabhi; (अस्), m. an ox; (ई), f. a cow; the daughter<BR>of Su-rabhi.<BR>—सौरभेय-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ्य|सौरभ्यं|सौरभ्यः
सौरभ्य, अम्, n. fragrance, sweet-scentedness,<BR>odour; pleasingness, agreeableness, beauty; good cha-<BR>racter, good reputation, fame; (अस्), m., N. of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरस|सौरसः
सौरस सौरस, अस्, m., N. of a Vihāra<BR>founded by king Surendra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेन
सौरसेन सौरसेन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>or district; (ई), f., scil. भाषा, the language spoken<BR>in the above district; [cf. शौरसेनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेय|सौरसेयः
सौरसेय सौरसेय, अस्, m. (fr. सु-रसा), ‘off-<BR>spring of Su-rasā,’ epithet of Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरस्य|सौरस्यं
सौरस्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-रस), well-flavoured-<BR>ness, tastiness, savoriness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराज्य|सौराज्यं
सौराज्य सौराज्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-राज), good<BR>government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्र|सौराष्ट्रः
सौराष्ट्र सौराष्ट्र, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. सु-<BR>राष्ट्र), belonging or relating to the district of<BR>Surāt; (अस्), m. the district of Surāt; the resin of<BR>the plant Boswellia Thurifera; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people inhabiting part of Bhārata-varṣa; (आ), f.<BR>a sort of fragrant earth, = तुवरी; (ई), f. a sort of<BR>fragrant earth found in Surāt; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>amalgam of zinc and copper, bell-metal, brass.<BR>—सौ-<BR>राष्ट्र-देश, अस्, m. the country of Surāt.<BR>—सौ-<BR>राष्ट्र-मृत्तिका, f. Surāt earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रक|सौराष्ट्रकं|सौराष्ट्रकः
सौराष्ट्रक, अम्, n. a sort of white or bell-<BR>metal; a kind of amalgam of five metals (= पञ्च-<BR>लोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रिक|सौराष्ट्रिकं
सौराष्ट्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the dis-<BR>trict of Surāt; (अम्), n. a sort of poison, (according<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">Page1140-b+ 68</a>]<BR>to some, of a kind of snake; according to others, a<BR>vegetable or mineral.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौलभ
सौलभ सौलभ, आनि, n. pl. (fr. सु-लभ),<BR>N. of particular Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौलभ्य|सौलभ्यं
सौलभ्य, अम्, n. easiness of acquisition or at-<BR>tainment; feasibility, facility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौल्विक|सौल्विकः
सौल्विक सौल्विक, अस्, m. (for शौल्विक), a<BR>copper-smith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौव|सौवं
सौव 1. सौव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्व), relating<BR>to self or to one's own property; (अम्), n. an order,<BR>edict (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवग्रामिक|सौवग्रामिकं
सौवग्रामिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्व-ग्राम), be-<BR>longing or relating to one's own village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौव|सौवं
सौव 2. सौव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. स्वर्), belong-<BR>ing to heaven, being in heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर|सौवरं
सौवर सौवर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्वर), relat-<BR>ing to sound or to a note in music, produced or<BR>existing in a note; treating of accents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्चल|सौवर्च्चल|सौवर्च्चलं
सौवर्चल सौवर्चल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सु-वर्-<BR>चल or सु-वर्चला), belonging to Su-varcala or Su-<BR>varcalā, coming from the country called Su-varcala;<BR>(अम्), n. sochal salt (prepared by fusing fossil salt<BR>with myrobalan); natron, alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्ण|सौवर्णं|सौवर्णः
सौवर्ण सौवर्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सु-वर्ण),<BR>made or consisting of gold, golden; weighing a Su-<BR>varṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्णभेदिनी
सौवर्णभेदिनी, f. the plant Priyaṅgu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्णिक|सौवर्णिकः
सौवर्णिक, weighing a Su-varṇa (at the end of<BR>a comp., e. g. चतुः-स्˚, weighing four Su-varṇas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवल्य
सौवल्य सौवल्य, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>(also read सौशल्य, सौशुल्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवश्व
सौवश्व सौवश्व, अस्, m. (fr. स्व्-अश्व), a<BR>descendant of Sv-aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवश्वि
सौवश्वि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Sv-aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवश्व्य
सौवश्व्य, अस्, m., Ved. the son of Sv-aśva; [cf.<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 1, 171.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवस्तिक|सौवस्तिकः
सौवस्तिक सौवस्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्वस्ति),<BR>benedictive, salutatory; (अस्), m. a family Brāhman<BR>or priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवाध्यायिक
सौवाध्यायिक सौवाध्यायिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>स्वाध्याय), belonging or relating to sacred study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवास्तव|सौवास्तवः
सौवास्तव सौवास्तव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सु +<BR>वास्तु), having a good site, pleasantly situated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविद|सौविदः
सौविद सौविद, अस्, m. (fr. सु-विद), a guard<BR>or attendant on the women's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविदल्ल|सौविदल्लः
सौविदल्ल सौविदल्ल or सौविदल्लक, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. सु-विदल्ल), = सौविद above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविष्टकृत
सौविष्टकृत सौविष्टकृत, अस्, ई, अम्, dedi-<BR>cated or relating to Agni Sviṣṭa-kṛt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीर|सौवीरं|सौवीरः
सौवीर सौवीर, अम्, n. (fr. सु-वीर), the<BR>fruit of the jujube; antimony; sour gruel; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a district of country in the west of India con-<BR>nected with the country along the Indus (perhaps<BR>the district now inhabited by the Suirs); (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the people of Su-vīra; N. of a people inhabiting<BR>part of Bhārata-varṣa.<BR>—सौवीर-राज, अस्, m. a<BR>king of Sauvīra.<BR>—सौवीर-सार, अम्, n. antimony.<BR>—सौवीराञ्जन (˚र-अञ्˚), अम्, n. a kind of anti-<BR>mony or collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीरक|सौवीरकं|सौवीरकः
सौवीरक, अस्, ई, अम्, of or belonging to Sauvīra;<BR>(अस्), m. an inhabitant of Sauvīra; a miserable Sau-<BR>vīra; N. of Jayad-ratha; the jujube tree; (अम्), n.<BR>sour barley-gruel, sour wheat-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीर्य|सौवीर्यं|सौवीर्य्य
सौवीर्य, अम्, n. great heroism or fortitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौशील्य|सौशील्यं
सौशील्य सौशील्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-शील), ex-<BR>cellence of disposition, good morals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौश्रवस|सौश्रवसं
सौश्रवस सौश्रवस, अम्, n. (fr. सु-श्रवस्),<BR>celebrity, renown; (अस्), m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौश्रुत
सौश्रुत सौश्रुत, आस्, m. pl. (fr. सु-श्रुत),<BR>N. of a family descended from Viśvā-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौषद्मन
सौषद्मन सौषद्मन, अस्, m. (fr. सु-षद्-<BR>मन्), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौष्ठव|सौष्ठवं
सौष्ठव सौष्ठव, अम्, n. (fr. सु-ष्ठु), ex-<BR>cellence, superior goodness or beauty, extreme skil-<BR>fulness, cleverness; excess (of anything); lightness,<BR>suppleness, fleetness, a particular division of dramatic<BR>composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौस्नातिक|सौस्नातिकः
सौस्नातिक सौस्नातिक, अस्, m. (fr. सु-स्नात),<BR>one who asks whether an ablution has been success-<BR>ful or auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द|सौहार्दः|सौहार्द्द|सौहार्द्दं|सौहार्द्दः
सौहार्द सौहार्द, अम्, n. (fr. सु-हृद्), good-<BR>heartedness, affection, friendship, friendliness; (अस्),<BR>m. the son of a friend.<BR>—सौहार्द-निधि, इस्, m.<BR>‘treasury of friendship,’ epithet of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द्य|सौहार्द्यं
सौहार्द्य, अम्, n. friendship, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद|सौहृदं
सौहृद, अम्, n. friendship, (कु-सौहृद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who is a bad friend); (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृदय|सौहृदयं
सौहृदय, अम्, n. (fr. सु-हृदय), cordial<BR>affection; friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद्य|सौहृद्यं
सौहृद्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-हृद्), friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहित्य|सौहित्यं
सौहित्य सौहित्य, अम्, n. (fr. सु-हित), sa-<BR>tiety, satisfaction; fulness, completion; kindness,<BR>friendliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहोत्र
सौहोत्र सौहोत्र, अस्, m. (fr. सु-होत्र), a<BR>patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Aja-mīḍha; of Puru-<BR>mīḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द्|स्कंद्
स्कन्द् 1. स्कन्द् = rt. स्कुन्द्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द्|स्कंद्
स्कन्द् 2. स्कन्द् (also written स्कन्ध्), cl.<BR>10. P. स्कन्दयति, स्कन्दायति, &c., to<BR>collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द्|स्कंद्
स्कन्द् 3. स्कन्द् (connected with rt. स्कुन्द्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. P. स्कन्दति (also A. -ते),<BR>चस्कन्द (2nd sing. चस्कन्दिथ or चस्कन्त्थ),<BR>स्कन्त्स्यति, अस्कदत् or अस्कान्त्सीत्, स्कन्त्तुम्, to<BR>leap, jump, spring; to jump or spring upwards, rise,<BR>mount, ascend; to raise (A., but in this sense re-<BR>garded as a form of rt. स्कुन्द्); to jump down-<BR>wards, drop, fall; to leap out, shoot out, burst out,<BR>drop out, be poured out, be spilled, ooze; to go,<BR>move, approach; to fall away; to perish (A.); to<BR>become dry: Pass. स्कद्यते, Perf. चस्कदे or च-<BR>स्कन्दे, Aor. अस्कन्दि: Caus. स्कन्दयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अचस्कन्दत्, to pour out, effuse, shed, spill,<BR>emit (seminal fluid); to omit, neglect; Desid. चि-<BR>स्कन्त्सति: Intens. चनीस्कद्यते, चनीस्कन्ति; [cf.<BR>Gr. σκάνδ-αλο-ν, σκανδάλη-θρο-ν, σχαστήρ, per-<BR>haps σκαίρω, σκάζω; Lat. scand-o, de-scend-o, (ac-<BR>cording to some also) scateo; Hib. skeinnead,<BR>‘eruption, gushing forth.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्त्तृ
स्कन्त्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who leaps, &c.; [cf.<BR>वि-ष्कन्त्तृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्त्त्वा
स्कन्त्त्वा, ind. having jumped, &c.; having de-<BR>scended or fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द|स्कंद|स्कंदः|स्कन्दः
स्कन्द, अस्, m. leaping; flowing; quicksilver;<BR>N. of Kārttikeya (son of Śiva and god of war, see<BR>कार्त्तिकेय); epithet of Śiva; a king, prince; the<BR>body; the bank of a river; a clever or learned man<BR>[cf. स्कन्ध]; a kind of disease (attacking children).<BR>—स्कन्द-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Gupta<BR>dynasty.<BR>—स्कन्द-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of one of<BR>the eighteen Purāṇas, (see स्कान्द-पुराण.)<BR>—स्कन्-<BR>द-मातृ, ता, f. the mother of Skanda, i. e. Durgā.<BR>—स्कन्द-षष्ठी, f. a festival in honour of<BR>Kārttikeya on the sixth day of the month Caitra.<BR>—स्कन्द-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a commentator<BR>(mentioned by Mādhavācārya; cf. स्कान्द-भा-<BR>ष्य).<BR>—स्कन्दांशक (˚द-अं˚), अस्, m. quick-<BR>silver.<BR>—स्कन्देश्वर-तीर्थ (˚द-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR>—स्कन्दोपनिषद् (˚द-उप्˚), त्, f., N.<BR>of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दक|स्कंदक|स्कंदकः|स्कन्दकः
स्कन्दक, अस्, m. one who leaps or springs; a<BR>soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दन|स्कंदन|स्कंदनं|स्कन्दनं
स्कन्दन, अम्, n. emission, effusion; purging,<BR>looseness; going, moving; drying up; the suppres-<BR>sion of bleeding by cold applications.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दनीय
स्कन्दनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be emitted, to be<BR>poured out or effused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दयत्
स्कन्दयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, emitting, effusing, pour-<BR>ing out, shedding; neglecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दित
स्कन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, emitted, effused, shed;<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दिन्
स्कन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, leaping, jumping; bursting<BR>out; effusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्न|स्कन्नं
स्कन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen, fallen down, descended;<BR>oozed out, trickled down; emitted, sprinkled; gone;<BR>dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दिलाचार्य
स्कन्दिलाचार्य स्कन्दिलाचार्य (˚ल-आच्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्ध्|स्कंध्
स्कन्ध् स्कन्ध् (= rt. 2. स्कन्द्), cl. 10. P.<BR>स्कन्धयति, &c., to collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्ध|स्कंध|स्कंधः|स्कन्धः
स्कन्ध स्कन्ध, अस्, m. (according to Uṇā-<BR>di-s. IV. 206. fr. rt. 3. स्कन्द्, ‘to rise’), the shoulder,<BR>upper part of the back or the region from the neck<BR>to the shoulder-joint (in men and animals); the<BR>body; the stem or trunk of a tree (especially that<BR>part of the stem where the branches begin); a large<BR>branch or bough; a branch or department of human<BR>knowledge (five of which are enumerated); a sec-<BR>tion, chapter, division of a book; a division of an<BR>army, form of military array; war, battle; a body of<BR>men &c., troop, multitude, quantity, (see करि-स्क्˚,<BR>नर-स्क्˚, तुरङ्ग-स्क्˚); the five objects of sense,<BR>(see विषय); the elements of being or the five<BR>forms of mundane consciousness (according to the<BR>Buddhist philosophy); the regalia or other articles<BR>used at the coronation of a king (as a jar filled with<BR>holy water, a parasol, a chowri, &c.); a king, prince;<BR>a sage, wise man, seer, teacher; equality of height<BR>in the humps of a pair of draught oxen; a road,<BR>path, way; an engagement, agreement; a sort of<BR>metre; a heron; N. of a poet; = भद्रादि (accord-<BR>ing to Śabda-k.); (आ), f. a branch; a creeper; [cf.<BR>perhaps Gr. σπάθη: Lat. scapula: Angl. Sax. scul-<BR>dor, sculder, scoldr: Old Germ. scultra, sculdra,<BR>scultarra: Armor. skoaz: Cambro-Brit. ysgwyz;<BR>perhaps Hib. guala for sguada or sguana.]<BR>—स्कन्-<BR>ध-चाप, अस्, m. ‘shoulder-bow,’ a sort of yoke or<BR>pole made of bamboo with a sling attached to either end<BR>for carrying burdens (= शिक्य).<BR>—स्कन्ध-ज, अस्, m.<BR>a tree growing from a principal stem (such as the gum<BR>olibanum tree &c.).<BR>—स्कन्ध-तरु, अस्, m. the cocoa-<BR>nut tree.<BR>—स्कन्ध-देश, अस्, m. ‘shoulder-region,’<BR>the shoulder; the part about the shoulders or withers of<BR>an elephant where the driver sits.<BR>—स्कन्ध-परि-<BR>निर्वाण, अम्, n. the annihilation of the elements<BR>of being (with Buddhists).<BR>—स्कन्ध-फल, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having fruit at the top,’ the cocoa-nut tree; the<BR>Vilva; the glomerous fig-tree.<BR>—स्कन्ध-बन्ध-<BR>ना, f. a sort of fennel, Anethum Panmorium.<BR>—स्कन्-<BR>ध-मल्लक, अस्, m. a heron.<BR>—स्कन्ध-रुह, अस्,<BR>m. ‘branch-growing,’ the Indian fig-tree.<BR>—स्कन्ध-<BR>वाह or स्कन्ध-वाहक, अस्, m. ‘carrying on the<BR>shoulders,’ an ox trained to carry burdens, pack-bullock.<BR>—स्कन्ध-शाखा, f. a principal branch, the forked<BR>branch which issues from the upper stem of a tree.<BR>—स्कन्ध-शृङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘branch-horned,’ a buf-<BR>falo.<BR>—स्कन्ध-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. every shoulder.<BR>—स्कन्धाग्नि (˚ध-अग्˚), इस्, or स्कन्धानल<BR>(˚ध-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘trunk-conflagration,’ the trunk<BR>of a tree or any large piece of timber set on fire by<BR>attrition &c.<BR>—स्कन्धावार (˚ध-आव्˚), अस्, m.<BR>an army or a division of it attached to the person of<BR>a king; a royal capital, royal residence; a camp.<BR>—स्कन्धोपनेय (˚ध-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>carried on the shoulders; (अस्), m. a form of peace-<BR>offering in which fruit or grain is presented as a<BR>mark of submission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धक
स्कन्धक, अम्, n. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्|स्कंधस्
स्कन्धस्, अस्, n. the shoulder; the trunk of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">Page1141-b+ 78</a>]<BR>tree.<BR>—स्कन्धो-ग्रीवी, f. a kind of metre (the first,<BR>third, and fourth Pādas of which consist of eight<BR>syllables each, and the second of twelve syllables, =<BR>न्यङ्कु-सारिणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिक|स्कंधिक|स्कंधिकः|स्कन्धिकः
स्कन्धिक, अस्, m. an ox trained to carry burdens<BR>(= स्कन्ध-वाह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिन्|स्कंधिन्
स्कन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having shoulders, having<BR>branches, having a branched stem; (ई), m. a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्ध्य
स्कन्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the shoulders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्न|स्कन्नं
स्कन्न स्कन्न. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भ्|स्कंभ्
स्कम्भ् स्कम्भ् or स्कभ् (probably a mere<BR>phonetic variety of rt. स्तम्भ्, q. v.;<BR>in native lists written स्कन्भ्), cl. 1. A. स्कम्भते,<BR>चस्कम्भे, &c.; cl. 5. 9. P. स्कभ्नोति, स्कभ्नाति,<BR>&c., स्कम्भितुम्, to make firm, establish, to sup-<BR>port, prop up (Ved.); to create; to stop, hinder,<BR>impede, restrain, block, obstruct: Caus. स्कभयति<BR>or स्कम्भयति (Ved. also स्कभायति), &c., to<BR>establish, support; [cf. according to some, Gr. σκῆπτρον,<BR>σκήπτω, σκίμπτω; Lat. scabellum, scam-<BR>num; Goth. ga-skapjan, ga-skafts; Angl. Sax.<BR>scapen, sceapan, sceaft; Old Germ. scafan, sca-<BR>fon, scoppon, ‘to stop.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कब्ध
स्कब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, propped, supported; stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कभित
स्कभित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. supported, fixed, fast-<BR>ened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कभीयस्
स्कभीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. supporting more,<BR>supporting firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भ|स्कंभ|स्कंभः|स्कम्भः
स्कम्भ, अस्, m. support, prop, fulcrum; ‘the sup-<BR>porter, propper,’ N. of a Vedic deity, (he is identified<BR>in Atharva-veda X. 7. with the supreme Being him-<BR>self, and is there represented, like Puruṣa, as co-<BR>extensive with the universe, and comprehending<BR>every existing thing in his members; the gods and<BR>all other entities, and even such abstract conceptions<BR>as faith, truth, &c., standing to him in the relation<BR>of branches to a tree; in X. 8. he is described as a<BR>sort of universal fulcrum as well as a universally dif-<BR>fused essence, the sky and the earth being said to<BR>be supported by him, and ‘all which has soul, which<BR>breathes, which winks’ being identified with him;<BR>he is even called ज्येष्ठम् ब्रह्म, which some<BR>think may mean not only the highest divine essence,<BR>but a kind of preæval Veda, of which the existing<BR>Vedas are merely branches.)<BR>—स्कम्भ-देष्ण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. whose gifts are firm, stable in giving<BR>(said of the Maruts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भन|स्कंभन|स्कंभनं
स्कम्भन, अम्, n. the act of supporting, a sup-<BR>port, prop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कान्द|स्कांद|स्कान्दं
स्कान्द स्कान्द, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्कन्द), relat-<BR>ing to Skanda or Kārttikeya; relating to Śiva; (अम्),<BR>n. the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—स्कान्द-पुराण, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of one of the eighteen Purāṇas (also called<BR>स्कन्द-पुराण; it is supposed to be lost or only<BR>to exist in fragments, the most celebrated of which is<BR>the Kāśī-khaṇḍa, which gives a description of the<BR>temples or Liṅgas of Śiva near Benares, with direc-<BR>tions for worshipping that god, and various legends<BR>chiefly intended to glorify Kāśī and exalt the sanctity<BR>of its shrines).<BR>—स्कान्द-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कु
स्कु स्कु, cl. 5. 9. P. A. स्कुनोति, स्कुनाति,<BR>स्कुनुते, स्कुनीते, चुस्काव, चुस्कुवे, स्को-<BR>ष्यति, -ते, अस्कौषीत्, अस्कोष्ट, स्कोतुम्, to go by<BR>leaps, jump; to raise, lift; to cover, overspread; to<BR>approach: Caus. स्कावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अचुस्क-<BR>वत्: Desid. चुस्कूषति, -ते: Intens. चोस्कूयते<BR>(Ved. चोष्कूयते), चोस्कोति; [cf. Gr. σκευ-ή, σκεῦ-ος,<BR>σκευά-ζ-ω, σκῦ-το-ς, κύ-τ-ος, ἐπι-σκύ-νιο-ν:<BR>Lat. ob-scu-ru-s, scu-tu-m, cu-ti-s, corium, cavere,<BR>cautus, causa: probably Angl. Sax. scuva, scoh,<BR>sceo, scunian, scawian, sceawian: Goth. skoh:<BR>Old Germ. scur, skiuhan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष्कूयमाण
चोष्कूयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bestowing, giv-<BR>ing, (Sāy. = प्रयच्छत्, Ṛg-veda I. 33, 3, = द-<BR>दत्, Nirukta VI. 22.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुन्द्|स्कुंद्
स्कुन्द् स्कुन्द् (connected with rt. 3. स्कन्द्,<BR>q. v.; cf. rt. स्कु), cl. 1. A. स्कुन्दते,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">Page1141-c+ 76</a>]<BR>चस्कुन्दे, &c., स्कुन्दितुम्, to jump, go by leaps<BR>or jumps; to raise, lift, (see rt. 3. स्कन्द्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुम्भ्|स्कुंभ्
स्कुम्भ् स्कुम्भ् (connected with^1 rt. स्कम्भ्;<BR>in native lists regarded as a Sautra rt.<BR>and written स्कुन्भ्), cl. 5. 9. P. स्कुभ्नोति, स्कुभ्-<BR>नाति, &c., to hold, stop, hinder.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कोटिका
स्कोटिका स्कोटिका, f. a kind of bird (pro-<BR>bably a sort of wagtail, = खञ्जनिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खद्
स्खद् स्खद् [cf. rt. क्षद्], cl. 1. A. स्ख-<BR>दते, चस्खदे, स्खदितुम्, to cut, cut<BR>or tear to pieces; to destroy; to hurt, injure, kill;<BR>to rout, defeat; to harass, fatigue, exhaust; to make<BR>firm; to be firm: Caus. स्खदयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अचिस्खदत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खदन|स्खदनं
स्खदन, अम्, n. cutting or tearing to pieces;<BR>the act of hurting or killing, injury; harassing, de-<BR>feating, discomfiting; firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खल्
स्खल् स्खल् (connected with rts. छल्,<BR>स्फल्), cl. 1. P. स्खलति, चस्खाल,<BR>स्खलिष्यति, अस्खालीत्, स्खलितुम्, to stumble,<BR>tumble, fall, fall down, trip, slip; to totter, waver;<BR>to fall or deviate from the right course; to make<BR>mistakes, blunder, err, fail; to make mistakes in<BR>speaking, stammer, falter, stutter, hesitate; to drop,<BR>drip, trickle; to go, move; disappear; to gather,<BR>collect: Pass. स्खल्यते, Perf. चस्खले (Kirāt.<BR>XVIII. 6), Aor. अस्खालि: Caus. स्खलयति or<BR>स्खालयति, &c., to cause to stumble, trip up; [cf.<BR>Lat. scelus, culpa; Goth. skula, skulan; Angl.<BR>Sax. sceal, sculan, scyld.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलत्
स्खलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, stumbling, tripping; blun-<BR>dering; stuttering; dropping, trickling.<BR>—स्खलद्-<BR>वाक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, making mistakes in speaking,<BR>stammering, faltering, blundering.<BR>—स्खलन्-मति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, erring in judgment, weak-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलन|स्खलनं
स्खलन, अम्, n. the act of stumbling, slipping,<BR>tripping, falling, tottering; falling or deviating from<BR>the right course; blundering, an error, mistake,<BR>blunder; blundering in speech or pronunciation;<BR>dropping, dripping, trickling, effusion, emission;<BR>dashing or clashing together, shock, collision; mutual<BR>striking or rubbing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलित|स्खलितं
स्खलित, अस्, आ, अम्, stumbled, slipped, tripped,<BR>fallen; dropped down; shaking, fluctuating, waver-<BR>ing, tottering, unsteady; erring; stuttering, stammer-<BR>ing, faltering, hesitating; intoxicated, drunk; agi-<BR>tated, disturbed; dropped, effused, emitted; trickling<BR>down; interrupted, stopped, obstructed; confounded;<BR>gone; (अम्), n. tumbling, falling; deviation from<BR>the right course; blunder, fault, error, sin; deceit,<BR>treachery; circumvention, stratagem (in war).<BR>—स्ख-<BR>लित-सुभगम्, ind. slipping or tripping along plea-<BR>santly, dashing or flowing along in a charming manner<BR>(said of a stream).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलित्वा
स्खलित्वा, ind. having stumbled; having slipped<BR>or tripped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खुड्
स्खुड् स्खुड् (= rts. स्थुड्, थुड्), cl. 6. P.<BR>स्खुडति, to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तक्
स्तक् स्तक्, cl. 1. P. स्तकति, तस्ताक, स्त-<BR>कितुम्, to resist; to strike against, repel:<BR>Caus. स्तकयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अतिष्टकत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्
स्तन् स्तन्, cl. 1. P. स्तनति, तस्तान, स्त-<BR>नितुम्, to sound, make a sound, resound,<BR>reverberate; to groan, breathe hard, sigh; cl. 10. P.<BR>स्तनयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अतस्तनत्, to thunder:<BR>Caus. स्तनयति (or स्तानयति according to some),<BR>-यितुम्, Aor. अतिष्टनत् (or अतिस्तनत् according<BR>to some), to cause to resound: Desid. तिस्तनिषति:<BR>Intens, तंस्तन्यते, तंस्तन्ति; [cf. Gr. στέν-ω,<BR>στενάχ-ω, στόνο-ς, στένο-μαι, στείνομαι, στενό-ς,<BR>στεινό-ς, στεῖνος, Στέν-τωρ: Lat. tono, tonitru:<BR>Old Norse stynija, styn: Old Germ. stunôd, ‘a<BR>sigh;’ thonar, donar, ‘thunder:’ Old Sax. thunar:<BR>Angl. Sax. thunor: Lith. sten-e-ti: Slav. sten-a-ti,<BR>‘to groan.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन|स्तनः
स्तन, अस्, m. the breast of a woman, (probably<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">Page1142-a+ 79</a>]<BR>so called from the noise made in breathing); the<BR>nipple of the breast; an udder or dug or breast of<BR>any female animal, (at the end of an adj. comp. the<BR>fem. may end in आ or ई, according to Vopa-deva IV.<BR>17, but the more usual form is in ई.)<BR>—स्तन-<BR>कलश, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘goblet-like breast,’ a<BR>woman's breast.<BR>—स्तन-कुट्मल, अम्, n. ‘breast-<BR>bud,’ a woman's breast.<BR>—स्तन-तट, अस्, m. the<BR>slope of the breasts, (see तट.)<BR>—स्तनन्-धम,<BR>अस्, आ, m. f. = स्तनन्-धय below.<BR>—स्तनन्-<BR>धय, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, breast-sucking, sucking at<BR>the breast; (अस्, आ), m. f. an infant; a suckling.<BR>—स्तन-प, अस्, आ, अम्, or स्तन-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>or स्तन-पायक, अस्, इका, अम्, or स्तन-पायिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, breast-sucking, sucking the breast or udder;<BR>an infant at the breast, suckling.<BR>—स्तन-पान, अम्,<BR>n. the drinking or sucking of the breast.<BR>—स्तन-<BR>भर, अस्, m. ‘breast-possessing,’ a man with a<BR>breast like a woman's.<BR>—स्तन-भव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being on the breast; (अस्), m. a particular posture<BR>in sexual union.<BR>—स्तन-मण्डल, अम्, n. ‘breast-<BR>orb,’ a woman's breast.<BR>—स्तन-मध्य or स्तन-<BR>मुख, अस्, m. ‘breast-point,’ a nipple.<BR>—स्तन-<BR>वृन्त, अस्, m. ‘breast-stalk,’ a nipple.<BR>—स्तन-<BR>शिखा, f. ‘breast-point,’ a nipple.<BR>—स्तनांशुक<BR>(˚न-अं˚), अम्, n. ‘breast-mantle,’ a cloth covering<BR>the bosom.<BR>—स्तनाग्र (˚न-अग्˚), अस्, m. ‘breast-<BR>point,’ a nipple.<BR>—स्तनाङ्ग-राग (˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>paint or pigment on the breasts (of women).<BR>—स्त-<BR>नान्तर (˚न-अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘breast-interval,’ the<BR>heart (as situated under the centre bone of the<BR>sternum); a mark on the breast (supposed to indi-<BR>cate future widowhood).<BR>—स्तना-भुज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. feeding or nourishing with the udder (said of<BR>cows).<BR>—स्तनाभोग (˚न-आभ्˚), अस्, m. fulness or<BR>swelling of the breast, the expanding of the bosom<BR>of a young woman; the circumference or orb of the<BR>breast; a man with large breasts like those of a<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनथ|स्तनथः
स्तनथ, अस्, m., Ved. thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनन|स्तननं
स्तनन, अम्, n. sounding, sound, noise; the<BR>rumbling of clouds; groaning; breathing hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनयत्
स्तनयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, thundering.<BR>—स्तनयद्-<BR>अमास्, m. pl. (see अमा, p. 74, col. 3), Ved. roaring<BR>together, sounding in concert (said of the Maruts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनयित्नु|स्तनयित्नुः
स्तनयित्नु, उस्, m. thundering, thunder, the mut-<BR>tering of clouds; a cloud; lightning; sickness;<BR>death; a kind of grass (= मुस्तक).<BR>—स्तनयित्नु-<BR>घोष, अस्, आ, अम्, loud as thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनित|स्तनितं
स्तनित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, sounding; thun-<BR>dering; (अम्), n. the rattling of thunder, rumbling<BR>of thunder-clouds; thunder, noise; the noise of<BR>clapping the hands.<BR>—स्तनित-फल, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Vikaṇṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्य|स्तन्यं
स्तन्य, अम्, n. (fr. स्तन), ‘that which is to be<BR>drawn from the breast,’ mother's milk, milk.<BR>—स्त-<BR>न्य-त्याग, अस्, m. leaving off the mother's milk,<BR>weaning.<BR>—स्तन्य-त्याग-मात्रक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>only just weaned.<BR>—स्तन्य-पायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or<BR>स्तन्य-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, sucking or feeding on milk,<BR>sucking at the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्ध|स्तब्धः
स्तब्ध स्तब्ध, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभ|स्तभः
स्तभ स्तभ, अस्, m. a goat; a ram; [cf.<BR>स्तुभ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्
स्तम् स्तम् (= rt. 1. सम्), cl. 1. P. स्तमति,<BR>तस्ताम, स्तमितु, to be confused or<BR>agitated; (according to some) not to be confused,<BR>see rt. 1. सम्; cl. 10. P. स्तमयति, to be agitated,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्ब|स्तंब|स्तंबः|स्तम्बः
स्तम्ब स्तम्ब, अस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. IV. 96.<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. स्था; probably connected with<BR>स्तम्भ, q. v.), a clump of grass, &c.; a sheaf of<BR>corn; any clump or bunch or cluster; a bush,<BR>thicket; a shrub or plant having no decided stem<BR>(such as the Jhiṇṭī or Barleria); the post to which<BR>an elephant is tied; any post or pillar, (in this and<BR>the next sense probably for स्तम्भ, but said by<BR>some to be neut.); stupefaction, insensibility; a<BR>mountain; [cf. Angl. Sax. stapel.]<BR>—स्तम्ब-करि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">Page1142-b+ 80</a>]<BR>इस्, m. ‘forming clusters,’ corn, rice.<BR>—स्तम्ब-कार,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, making a clump, forming a cluster.<BR>—स्तम्ब-घन, अस्, m. ‘clump-destroyer,’ a small<BR>hoe for weeding or eradicating clumps of grass, &c.;<BR>a sickle for cutting corn; a basket for holding the<BR>heads of wild rice, &c.<BR>—स्तम्ब-घात = स्तम्ब-<BR>घ्न below.<BR>—स्तम्ब-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, clump-<BR>destroying, weed-destroying; (अस्), m. a hoe or<BR>sickle.<BR>—स्तम्ब-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, growing on a<BR>clump or bush; growing on a post.<BR>—स्तम्ब-पुर्,<BR>ऊर्, f., N. of the city Tāmalipta, q. v.<BR>—स्तम्ब-<BR>मित्र, अस्, m., N. of the author of Ṛg-veda X.<BR>142, 7, 8 (having the patronymic Śārṅga).<BR>—स्तम्-<BR>ब-हन् or स्तम्ब-हनन, अम्, ई, n. f. ‘clump-<BR>destroyer,’ a hoe for eradicating weeds; a sickle for<BR>cutting corn.<BR>—स्तम्बे-रम, अस्, m. ‘delighting<BR>in clumps of high grass,’ an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ्|स्तंभ्
स्तम्भ् स्तम्भ् or स्तभ् (connected with<BR>rt. स्कम्भ्, q. v.; in native lists written<BR>स्तन्भ्), cl. 5. 9. P. स्तभ्नोति, स्तभ्नाति, (2nd<BR>sing. Impv. स्तभान), तस्तम्भ, अस्तम्भीत् or<BR>अस्तभत्, स्तम्भितुम् (originally perhaps ‘to<BR>stamp’), to fix firmly, make firm, make stiff or im-<BR>movable; to paralyze, stupefy; to prop, support, prop<BR>up, sustain; to create (Ved.); to stop, arrest, suppress,<BR>oppose, hinder; cl. 1. A. स्तम्भते, तस्तम्भे (ac-<BR>cording to some also टष्टम्भे, ष्टम्भते), &c.,<BR>to become fixed or immovable, to become senseless<BR>or insensible, become stiff or rigid: Pass. स्तभ्यते,<BR>Aor. अस्तम्भि: Caus. स्तम्भयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अतस्तम्भत्, to fix, make firm or immovable, to<BR>make stiff or rigid, stupefy, paralyze, stun; to prop,<BR>support; stop, arrest, bring to a stand, suppress, re-<BR>strain: Desid. तिस्तम्भिषति: Intens. तास्तभ्यते;<BR>[cf. Gr. στέμφ-υλο-ν, ἀ-στεμφ-ής, στέμβ-ω,<BR>στεμβ-άζω, στοβέ-ω, στοβάζ-ω, στείβ-ω; Lat. stupeo,<BR>stipes; Old Germ. stamph, stamphon, stab;<BR>Mod. Germ. stampfen; Old Norse stofn.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्ध|स्तब्धः
स्तब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed, firm, stiff, rigid, hard,<BR>immovable, motionless, numb, paralyzed, senseless,<BR>stupid, dull, insensible, indifferent; stopped, brought<BR>to a stand, blocked up; obstinate, stubborn, hard-<BR>hearted; coarse; [cf. Old Germ. stīf; Mod. Germ.<BR>steif; Engl. stiff.]<BR>—स्तब्ध-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>‘stiff-eared,’ having the ears fixed, pricking up the<BR>ears.<BR>—स्तब्ध-ता, f. or स्तब्ध-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>fixedness, rigidity, immobility, steadiness, stupor,<BR>stubbornness.<BR>—स्तब्ध-रोमन्, आ, m. ‘stiff-<BR>bristled,’ a boar, hog.<BR>—स्तब्ध-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having fixed or unwinking eyes (applied as an epi-<BR>thet to the gods who are supposed to be known by<BR>this characteristic).<BR>—स्तब्धी-करण, अम्, n. the<BR>act of making stiff, stiffening, making rigid, para-<BR>lyzing.<BR>—स्तब्धी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made stiff,<BR>stiffened, rigid, paralyzed.<BR>—स्तब्धी-कृत्य, ind.<BR>having stiffened or made rigid.<BR>—स्तब्धी-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. the becoming stiffened or rigid, torpidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धि|स्तब्धिः
स्तब्धि, इस्, f. fixedness, hardness, rigidity, firm-<BR>ness, immobility, stupor, numbness, obstinacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्ध्वा
स्तब्ध्वा, ind. = स्तम्भित्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभित
स्तभित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = स्तब्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभु
स्तभु, n. = स्तम्भन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभूय
स्तभूय (fr. स्तभु), Nom. A. स्तभूयते,<BR>&c., Ved. to desire to support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभूयमान
स्तभूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desiring to<BR>support, upholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभ्यमान
स्तभ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being made firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ|स्तंभ|स्तंभः|स्तम्भः
स्तम्भ, अस्, m. fixedness, stiffness, rigidity;<BR>immobility, a prop, support, fulcrum; a pillar,<BR>column, post; a stem, stock, trunk; insensibility,<BR>stupor, stupefaction (from fear, joy, grief, &c.);<BR>numbness, paralysis, torpor; stupidity, coldness, want<BR>of feeling or excitability; stoppage, obstruction, hin-<BR>drance; suppression; a particular faculty acquired by<BR>magical means, the supernatural suppression or ar-<BR>resting of any feeling or force (as of hunger, thirst,<BR>or the forces of fire, water, &c.; this is one of the<BR>षट्-कर्मन् described as taught in the Tantras,<BR>see p. 1032, col. 3; many varieties of Stambha are<BR>enumerated, e. g. जल-स्त्˚, वह्नि-स्त्˚, वायु-स्त्˚,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">Page1142-c+ 75</a>]<BR>क्षुत्-स्त्˚, पिपासा-स्त्˚, निद्रा-स्त्˚, and in the case of<BR>the first of these one effect of this faculty is to enable<BR>a person to walk on the waters); N. of a Ṛṣi;<BR>[cf. Angl. Sax. steb.]<BR>—स्तम्भ-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>causing obstruction; causing stiffness, paralyzing;<BR>(अस्), m. a fence, railing, &c.<BR>—स्तम्भ-कारण,<BR>अम्, n. cause of obstruction or impediment.<BR>—स्तम्-<BR>भ-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—स्तम्भ-पूजा,<BR>f. worship of the posts of the temporary pavilions<BR>erected for marriages or other festive occasions.<BR>—स्तम्भी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become<BR>a post.<BR>—स्तम्भोत्कीर्ण (˚भ-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>carved out of a post of wood (as a statue).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भक
स्तम्भक, अस्, इका, अम्, fixing, propping, stop-<BR>ping, restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकिन्|स्तंभकिन्
स्तम्भकिन्, ई, m. a kind of musical instrument<BR>covered with leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भन|स्तंभन|स्तंभनं|स्तम्भनं|स्तम्भनः
स्तम्भन, अम्, n. the act of fixing firmly,<BR>making stiff or hard or rigid, making like a post,<BR>(रम्भा-स्तम्भन, the turning of the nymph<BR>Rambhā into a pillar by the curse of Viśvā-mitra, see<BR>Rāmāyaṇa I. 64); paralyzing, stupefying, stunning,<BR>benumbing; propping or supporting, holding up-<BR>right; stopping, making immovable, hindering,<BR>arresting, bringing to a stand, suppression, obstruc-<BR>tion; stopping of hemorrhage, staunching the flow<BR>of blood; anything employed as a styptic or astrin-<BR>gent; a particular magical act or faculty, suppression<BR>of any of the bodily feelings or forces of nature by<BR>supernatural means, (see under स्तम्भ; जल-<BR>स्तम्भन = जल-स्तम्भ); (अस्, ई, अम्), fixing<BR>immovably, paralyzing, supporting, stopping; (अस्),<BR>m. ‘the paralyzer,’ epithet of one of the five arrows<BR>of Kāma-deva, (the names of the other four are<BR>Unmādana, Śoṣaṇa, Tāpana, and Sammohana.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भनीय
स्तम्भनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be fixed firmly; to<BR>be propped; to be stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भित|स्तंभित|स्तम्भितः
स्तम्भित, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed firmly; stiffened,<BR>benumbed, paralyzed, stupefied, senseless; propped<BR>up, supported; stopped, brought to a standstill, sup-<BR>pressed; staunched; restrained, constrained.<BR>—स्तम्-<BR>भित-रम्भ, अम्, n., N. of a particular Troṭaka<BR>or drama; [cf. रम्भा-स्तम्भन above.]<BR>—स्तम्-<BR>भित-वाष्प-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, suppressing the flow<BR>of tears.<BR>—स्तम्भिताश्रु (˚त-अश्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, one<BR>who has suppressed his tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भित्वा
स्तम्भित्वा, ind. having fixed, having stopped,<BR>having suppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भिन्|स्तंभिन्
स्तम्भिन्, ई, इनी, इ, supporting; stopping, re-<BR>straining; (इनी), f. one of the five Dhāraṇās or<BR>elements (= earth, see भ्रमणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तर|स्तरः
स्तर स्तर, स्तरण, स्तरिमन्, &c. See<BR>p. 1144, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तव|स्तवः
स्तव स्तव, स्तवक, &c. See p. 1143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवरक|स्तवरकः
स्तवरक स्तवरक, अस्, m. (doubtful), a<BR>fence, railing (= आवरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तामु
स्तामु स्तामु, उस्, m. (= स्तोतृ, Naigh. III.<BR>16), Ved. a praiser, worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताव|स्तावः
स्ताव स्ताव. See p. 1143, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ति
स्ति स्ति, स्ति-पा. See under rt. स्त्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिघ्
स्तिघ् स्तिघ्, cl. 5. A. स्तिघ्नुते, तिष्-<BR>टिघे, अस्तेघिष्ट, स्तेघितुम्, to as-<BR>cend; to assail: Caus. स्तेघयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अतिष्टिघत्: Desid. तिस्तिघिषते or तिस्तेघिषते:<BR>Intens. तेष्टिघ्यते, तेष्टेग्धि; [cf. Gr. στείχ-ω,<BR>ἔ-στιχ-ον, στίχο-ς, στοῖχο-ς, στιχάο-μαι: Goth.<BR>steig-a, staig-a, ‘a path:’ Old Germ. steg-a, ‘an<BR>ascent, path:’ Mod. Germ. steig-en, ‘to rise:’ Slav.<BR>stiz-a, ‘a path:’ Lith. staig-ù-s, ‘quick;’ staigiō-s,<BR>‘to hasten:’ Hib. staighre, ‘a step, stair.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिप्
स्तिप् स्तिप् (also written स्तेप्), cl. 1. A.<BR>स्तेपते, तिष्टिपे, &c., to ooze, drip,<BR>drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिभि|स्तिभिः
स्तिभि स्तिभि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 121. fr. rt. स्तम्भ्), an obstacle, obstruction;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">Page1143-a+ 78</a>]<BR>the ocean; a cluster, clump, bunch (= फल-स्त-<BR>वक; cf. स्तम्ब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिम्भि|स्तिम्भिः
स्तिम्भि, इस्, m. = स्तिभि above (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिम्
स्तिम् स्तिम् or स्तीम् (connected with rt.<BR>तिम्), cl. 4. P. स्तिम्यति, स्तीम्यति,<BR>तिष्टेम, तिष्टीम, &c., to be or become wet or<BR>moist; to become fixed or immovable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमित|स्तिमितः
स्तिमित, अस्, आ, अम्, [cf. तिमित], wet, moist;<BR>still, motionless, unmoved, steady, fixed, rigid (as<BR>the eye), immovable, benumbed; tender, soft;<BR>gratified, pleased; (अम्), n. moisture.<BR>—स्तिमित-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. steadiness, fixedness, stillness, absence of<BR>motion, absorption.<BR>—स्तिमित-वायु, उस्, m. still air.<BR>—स्तिमित-समाधि-शुचि, इस्, इस्, इ, pure with steady<BR>meditation.<BR>—स्तिमितायताक्ष (˚त-आय्˚, ˚त-अक्˚),<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, one who keeps his large eyes fixed or<BR>still.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेम|स्तेमः
स्तेम, अस्, m. wetness, moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीम्
स्तीम् स्तीम् = rt. स्तिम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीर्वि|स्तीर्विः|स्तीर्व्वि|स्तीर्व्विः
स्तीर्वि स्तीर्वि, इस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 54. fr. rt. 1. स्तृ), an officiating priest at a sacri-<BR>fice (especially an Adhvaryu versed in the Yajur-veda);<BR>grass (= तृण-जाति); sky, atmosphere (= नभस्);<BR>water (= पयस्); blood (= रुधिर); Indra (=<BR>शक्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तु
स्तु स्तु, cl. 2. P. A. स्तौति or स्तवीति (1st<BR>du. स्तुवस् or स्तुवीवस्, 3rd pl. स्तुवन्ति),<BR>स्तुते or स्तुवीते, Impf. अस्तौत् or अस्तवीत् (1st sing.<BR>अस्तवम्), Impv. स्तौतु or स्तवीतु (2nd sing.<BR>स्तुहि or स्तुवीहि), Perf. तुष्टाव (2nd sing. तुष्-<BR>टोथ, 1st du. तुष्टुव, 1st pl. तुष्टुम), तुष्-<BR>टुवे, स्तोष्यति, -ते, अस्तावीत्, अस्तोष्ट, स्तोतुम् or<BR>(according to Vopa-deva also) स्तवितुम् (Ved. Inf.<BR>स्तुषे, स्तवध्यै), to praise, laud, eulogize, glorify,<BR>extol, celebrate; to hymn, praise or celebrate in song,<BR>worship by hymns; cl. 1. A. स्तवते (Ved. स्तवे),<BR>to be praised (Ved.): Pass. स्तूयते, &c., Aor.<BR>अस्तावि, to be praised, &c.: Caus. स्तावयति, Aor.<BR>अतुष्टवत्: Desid. तुष्टूषति, -ते: Intens.<BR>तोष्टूयते, तोष्टोति; [cf. perhaps Gr. στό-μα,<BR>Æol. στύ-μα: Goth. staua, ‘a judge;’ stauja,<BR>‘to judge.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तव|स्तवः
स्तव, अस्, m. praising, celebrating, hymning;<BR>praise, eulogium, panegyric.<BR>—स्तव-राज, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a particular mystical prayer or incantation.<BR>—स्तवावलि, इस्, or स्तवावली (˚व-आव्˚), f., N. of<BR>a work by Kavi-candra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवक|स्तवकः
स्तवक, अस्, इका, अम्, praising, eulogising; (अस्),<BR>m. a panegyrist, praiser; praise, eulogium; a cluster<BR>of blossoms, bunch of flowers, nosegay, tuft, (in<BR>these senses said to be fr. rt. 1. स्था according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 96); N. of the chapters in the Kusu-<BR>māñjali; a quantity, multitude; [cf. स्तोम.]<BR>—स्त-<BR>वकाचित (˚क-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, covered with blos-<BR>soms, in blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवकित
स्तवकित, अस्, आ, अम्, full of blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवथ
स्तवथ, अस्, m., Ved. praise, (Sāy. = स्तोत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवन|स्तवनं
स्तवन, अम्, n. praising, praise; a hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवनीय
स्तवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, praiseworthy,<BR>laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवमान
स्तवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, lauding, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवान्
स्तवान्, nom. c. masc., Ved. being praised or<BR>lauded, (Sāy. = स्तूयमान, Ṛg-veda VI. 24, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवान
स्तवान, अस्, आ, अम्, being praised, being lauded<BR>or glorified, (Sāy. = स्तूयमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवितव्य
स्तवितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवितृ
स्तवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a praiser, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवेय्य|स्तवेय्यः
स्तवेय्य (according to some) = स्तुवेय्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताव|स्तावः
स्ताव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praising, one who praises,<BR>a praiser; (अस्), m. praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तावक|स्तावकः
स्तावक, अस्, m. a praiser, panegyrist, eulogiser,<BR>flatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताविन्
स्ताविन्, ई, इनी, इ, praising, hymning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताव्य
स्ताव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be praised, praise-<BR>worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्
स्तुत्, त्, त्, त् (at the end of comps.), praising, cele-<BR>brating, (see देव-स्त्˚, यथा-स्त्˚, छन्दः-स्त्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत|स्तुतः
स्तुत, अस्, आ, अम्, praised, eulogised, hymned,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">Page1143-b+ 77</a>]<BR>glorified; flattered; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—स्तुत-<BR>स्वामि-क्षेत्र, अम्, n., N. of a sacred place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुति|स्तुतिः
स्तुति, इस्, f. praise, eulogy, commendation, adula-<BR>tion, flattery; N. of Durgā.<BR>—स्तुति-गीत, अम्, n. a<BR>song of praise, panegyric.<BR>—स्तुति-पद, अम्, n. an<BR>object of praise.<BR>—स्तुति-पर्यवसायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>concluding or ending in praise (said of ironical<BR>निन्दा or censure).<BR>—स्तुति-पाठक, अस्, m. ‘praise-<BR>reciter,’ a panegyrist, encomiast, bard, herald (espe-<BR>cially one who accompanies a chief or an army, =<BR>वन्दिन्, q. v.).<BR>—स्तुति-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of<BR>praise or adulation.<BR>—स्तुति-वाद, अस्, m. a laudatory<BR>speech, panegyric.<BR>—स्तुति-व्रत, अस्, m. ‘one whose<BR>duty is praise,’ a bard, &c., (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्य|स्तुत्यः
स्तुत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, laudable, praise-<BR>worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्वा
स्तुत्वा, ind. having praised, having glorified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुवत्
स्तुवत्, अन्, अती, अत्, praising, glorifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुवान
स्तुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, praising, glorifying; being<BR>praised or celebrated, (Sāy. = स्तूयमान, Ṛg-veda<BR>VII. 96, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुवेय्य|स्तुवेय्यः
स्तुवेय्य, अस्, m., Ved., N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुषेय्य
स्तुषेय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. excellent, praise-<BR>worthy, (Sāy. = स्तोतव्य, Ṛg-veda X. 120, 6);<BR>(अम्), n. excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूयमान
स्तूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being praised or lauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतव्य
स्तोतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, deserving<BR>praise, laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतृ
स्तोतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, praising, a praiser, panegyrist,<BR>flatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्र|स्तोत्रं
स्तोत्र, अम्, n. praise, eulogium, a hymn of praise,<BR>ode.<BR>—स्तोत्रार्ह (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रिय|स्तोत्रियः
स्तोत्रिय, अस्, m. a kind of verse (used in parti-<BR>cular ceremonies along with the अनु-रूप, q. v.);<BR>(आ), f. a kind of verse (= स्तोत्रीया below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रीया
स्तोत्रीया, f. a particular kind of verse consisting<BR>of eighty syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम|स्तोमः
स्तोम, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 139. fr.<BR>rt. स्तु), praise, eulogium, a hymn, (see सूक्त);<BR>sacrifice, oblation; a Soma libation; a heap, collec-<BR>tion, assemblage, number, multitude, quantity, mass<BR>[cf. स्तवक, col. 1]; (अम्), n. the head; riches;<BR>wealth; grain, corn; an iron-pointed stick or staff<BR>or one bound with iron; (अस्, आ, अम्), crooked,<BR>bent (according to some).<BR>—स्तोम-तष्ट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. composed by poets, (Sāy. = स्तोम-का-<BR>रिभिः कृत.)<BR>—स्तोम-वाहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. per-<BR>forming or offering hymns of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोमय
स्तोमय (referred in native lists to a rt. स्तोम्,<BR>but rather to be regarded as a Nom. fr. स्तोम above),<BR>Nom. or cl. 10. P. स्तोमयति, अतुस्तोमत्, स्तोम-<BR>यितुम्, to praise, laud, hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्य
स्तोम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, praiseworthy,<BR>laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुक|स्तुकः
स्तुक स्तुक, अस्, m. (probably another form<BR>of स्तुप, but cf. स्तवक), a collection of hair, knot<BR>or braid of hair, (Sāy. = केश-सङ्घात); (आ), f. a<BR>knot or braid of hair (= केश-वेणी; cf. पृथु-<BR>ष्ठुक, सहस्र-स्˚); a curl of hair, bunch of curly<BR>hair between the horns of a bull; (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda IX. 97, 17. स्तुका = अपत्य; cf. तोक);<BR>a hip, thigh, (according to some = जघन.)<BR>—स्तुका-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. possessing bunches of<BR>hair, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 74, 13.<BR>स्तुकाविनः = ऊर्णायवः.)<BR>—स्तुका-सर्गम्, ind.<BR>after the form of a curl or knot of hair (= स्तुका<BR>यथा सृज्यते तथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुच्
स्तुच् स्तुच्, cl. 1. A. स्तोचते, तुष्टुचे,<BR>स्तोचितुम्, to be bright or pellucid; to<BR>be propitious or pleased: Caus. स्तोचयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अतुष्टुचत्: Desid. तुस्तुचिषते or तुस्तो-<BR>चिषते: Intens. तोष्टुच्यते, तोष्टोक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुनक|स्तुनकः
स्तुनक स्तुनक, अस्, m. a goat (= छाग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुप
स्तुप स्तुप, अस्, m. [cf. स्तूप], Ved. a knot<BR>of hair, top-knot; the collection of curly hair be-<BR>tween the horns of a bull; the horns of a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ्
स्तुभ् 1. स्तुभ् (connected in some senses<BR>with rt. स्तम्भ्, and in these senses also<BR>identical with rt. स्तुम्भ् below, and perhaps ori-<BR>ginally ‘to stamp’), cl. 1. A. स्तोभते, तुष्टुभे,<BR>स्तोभितुम्, to stop, suppress; to paralyze, stupefy;<BR>to be stupefied; cl. 1. P. स्तोभति, to praise, (in<BR>this sense probably connected with and developed<BR>out of rt. स्तु); to celebrate, worship (Ved., in<BR>Naigh. III. 14. स्तोभति is enumerated among the<BR>अर्चति-कर्माणः): Caus. स्तोभयति, &c., to<BR>praise (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ्
2. स्तुभ्, प्, m., Ved. one who stops, (perhaps<BR>the words त्रि-ष्टुभ् and अनु-ष्टुभ् are to be<BR>referred to this sense, the metre requiring regular<BR>stoppages or pauses); one who praises, a worshipper<BR>(= स्तोतृ, Naigh. III. 16).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ्वन्
स्तुभ्वन्, आ, m., Ved. one who praises, a praiser,<BR>(Sāy. = स्तोतृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभ|स्तोभं|स्तोभः
स्तोभ, अस्, m. stopping, obstructing; a stop,<BR>pause; disrespect, contumely; hymn, praise; a<BR>division of the Sāma-veda, (see साम-वेद, p. 1107);<BR>an insertion, anything inserted.<BR>—स्तोभ-च्छला, f.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Sāma-veda-cchalā, q. v.<BR>—स्तोभ-प्रकृति, इस्, f., N. of part of the Sāma-<BR>veda.<BR>—स्तोभानुसंहार (˚भ-अन्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a short treatise on Śikṣā (one of the Pariśiṣṭas<BR>of the Sāma-veda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभनसंहार
स्तोभन-संहार = स्तोभानुसंहार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौभिक|स्तौभिकं
स्तौभिक, अम्, n., N. of the second portion of<BR>the Saṃhitā of the Sāma-veda, (see साम-वेद,<BR>p. 1107.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ|स्तुभः
स्तुभ स्तुभ, अस्, m. a goat (= छाग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुम्भ्|स्तुंभ्
स्तुम्भ् स्तुम्भ् (connected with rt. स्तम्भ्,<BR>and in some senses indentical with rt.<BR>1. स्तुभ् above; in native lists written स्तुन्भ्), cl.<BR>5. 9. P. स्तुभ्नोति, स्तुभ्नाति, to stop; to stupefy; to<BR>expel; [cf. Gr. στύφ-ω, στυφελός, στυμνός,<BR>στυφεδανός, τυφεδανός, probably also τυφός,<BR>τυφώδης; perhaps Old Germ. stumph, stumbal; Angl.<BR>Sax. stypel, dumb; Goth. dumb.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुवेय्य|स्तुवेय्यः
स्तुवेय्य स्तुवेय्य, स्तुषेय्य. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप्
स्तूप् स्तूप् (probably derived fr. स्तूप<BR>below), cl. 4. 10. P. स्तूप्यति, स्तूप-<BR>यति, &c., to heap up, pile, collect; to erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप|स्तूपः
स्तूप, अस्, m. (according to Sāy. fr. rt. स्त्यै;<BR>according to Uṇādi-s. III. 25. fr. rt. स्तु), a heap or<BR>pile of earth, any heap or pile or mound; a Buddhist<BR>monument (commonly called Tope; it is a kind of<BR>Tumulus erected over sacred relics of the great<BR>Buddha or on spots consecrated as the scenes of<BR>his acts); a funeral pile; a heap of rays, accumu-<BR>lated rays (Ved., according to Sāy. स्तूपैः = तप्तै<BR>रश्मिभिः, Ṛg-veda VII. 2, 1); (according to<BR>Śabda-k.) = निष्प्रयोजन; = बल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौपिक|स्तौपिकं
स्तौपिक, अम्, n. a kind of small broom carried<BR>by a Buddhist or Jaina ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ 1. स्तृ, cl. 5. or स्तॄ, cl. 9. P. A. स्तृ-<BR>णोति, स्तृणुते, स्तृणाति, स्तृणीते, तस्तार<BR>(1st du. तस्तरिव), तस्तरे, स्तरिष्यति or स्त-<BR>रीष्यति, -ते (if in cl. 9), अस्तार्षीत् (according to<BR>some also अस्तारीत्), अस्तृत, अस्तरिष्ट or अस्त-<BR>रीष्ट, अस्तीर्ष्ट (if in cl. 9, Pāṇ. VII. 2, 42);<BR>Prec. स्तर्यात्, स्तीर्यात्, स्तृषीष्ट, स्तरिषीष्ट<BR>or स्तरीषीष्ट, स्तीर्षीष्ट (if in cl. 9, Pāṇ.<BR>VII. 2, 42), स्तर्तुम् or स्तरितुम् or स्तरीतुम्<BR>(Ved. Inf. स्तर्तवै), to spread, spread out, expand,<BR>diffuse; to spread about, strew, scatter; to spread on<BR>or over; to cover, clothe; to kill, (in Naigh. II. 19.<BR>स्तृणाति is enumerated among the वध-कर्मा-<BR>णः): Pass. cl. 5. स्तर्यते, cl. 9. स्तीर्यते, Aor.<BR>अस्तारि, to be spread, &c.: Caus. स्तारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अतस्तरत्, to spread; to cover: Desid. तिस्तीर्-<BR>षति, -ते, or तिस्तरिषति, -ते, or तिस्तरीषति, -ते:<BR>Intens. तास्तर्यते, तेस्तीर्यते, तास्तर्ति; [cf. Zend<BR>śtar, śtair-is: Gr. στόρ-νυ-μι, στορέννυ-μι,<BR>στρώννυ-μι, στρῶ-μα, στρω-μνή, στρα-τό-ς: Lat.<BR>ster-n-o, stra-tu-s, stra-men, stra-mentu-m,<BR>toru-s: Goth. strau-ja: Old Germ. strao, betti-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">Page1144-a+ 73</a>]<BR>strewi, ‘lectisternium:’ Slav. stre-ti, ‘to extend;’<BR>po-stla-ti, ‘to strew;’ po-stel-ja, ‘a bed:’ Lith.<BR>stra-je, ‘a bed of straw.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिस्तिराण
तिस्तिराण, अस्, आ, अम् (Perf. part. A.), Ved. one<BR>who has spread, spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तर|स्तरः
स्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, spreading, extending, covering,<BR>&c.; (अस्), m. anything spread, a layer, stratum; a<BR>bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरण|स्तरणं
स्तरण, अम्, n. the act of spreading, strewing,<BR>scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरणीय
स्तरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spread; to be<BR>strewn or scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरिमन्
स्तरिमन्, आ, m. ‘that which is spread,’ a bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरी
स्तरी, ईस्, f. smoke, vapour; a heifer; a barren cow<BR>(acc. c. स्तर्यम्, Ṛg-veda I. 118, 20; in this sense<BR>probably connected with स्थिर, q. v.); [cf. Gr. στεῖρα<BR>(for στερια); Lat. sterilis; Goth. stairo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरीमन्
स्तरीमन्, आ, m. = स्तरिमन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीर्ण
स्तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, spread, covered, strewn; pre-<BR>pared; [cf. Gr. στέρ-νο-ν.]<BR>—स्तीर्ण-बर्हिस्, इस्, इस्,<BR>इस्, Ved. one who has spread Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
2. स्तृ, spreading, covering, clothing, (Sāy. = आच्-<BR>छादक, Ṛg-veda I. 87, 1); a star, (Ṛg-veda II.<BR>2, 5. स्तृभिः = नक्षत्रैः, ‘a star;’ cf. तार,<BR>‘light-strewer, light-scatterer;’ in this sense thought<BR>by some to be for अस्तृ, fr. rt. 2. अस् + तृ; cf. Gr.<BR>ἀστήρ, τεῖρος, Æol. τέῤῤος; Lat. stella; Goth.<BR>stairno; Angl. Sax. steorra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृणत्
स्तृणत्, अन्, अती, अत्, covering, strewing, spread-<BR>ing over or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृणान
स्तृणान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. spreading, strewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृत
स्तृत, अस्, आ, अम्, spread, spread out; [cf. वि-<BR>स्तृत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृति|स्तृतिः
स्तृति, इस्, f. spreading, stretching out, expansion;<BR>covering, clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ 3. स्तृ (= rt. स्पृ, q. v.), cl. 5. P. स्तृ-<BR>णोति, &c., to please, gratify, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृक्ष्
स्तृक्ष् स्तृक्ष्, cl. 1. P. स्तृक्षति, तस्तृ-<BR>क्ष, &c., to go: Intens. तरीष्टृक्ष्-<BR>यते, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृह्
स्तृह् स्तृह् or स्तॄह् (connected with rt.<BR>तृह्, q. v.), cl. 6. P. स्तृहति, स्तॄहति, त-<BR>स्तर्ह, स्तर्हितुम् or स्तर्ढुम्, to strike, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄ
स्तॄ स्तॄ. See rt. 1. स्तृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄह्
स्तॄह् स्तॄह्. See rt. स्तृह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन्
स्तेन् स्तेन् (more properly regarded as a<BR>Nom. fr. स्तेन below; cf. rt. स्तै), cl. 10.<BR>P. स्तेनयति, अतिस्तेनत्, &c., to steal, rob; [cf. Gr.<BR>στερέω; Goth. stil-an, ‘to steal;’ Angl. Sax. stelan,<BR>stal, stalian, stalu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन|स्तेनं|स्तेनः
स्तेन, अस्, m. (perhaps to be connected with a<BR>form स्ते derived fr. स्ति for rt. स्तै; cf. स्त्येन fr.<BR>rt. स्त्यै), a thief, robber; (अम्), n. thieving, steal-<BR>ing.<BR>—स्तेन-निग्रह, अस्, m. the restraining or<BR>punishing of thieves; suppression of theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेय|स्तेयं
स्तेय, अम्, n. [cf. rt. स्तै], theft, robbery; any-<BR>thing stolen or liable to be stolen; anything clandes-<BR>tine or private.<BR>—स्तेय-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. one who<BR>commits a theft, a thief, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयिन्
स्तेयिन्, ई, m. a thief, robber; a goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन|स्तैनं
स्तैन, अम्, n. theft, robbery, thievery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन्य|स्तैन्यं|स्तैन्यः
स्तैन्य, अम्, n. theft, thievery, robbery; (अस्),<BR>m. a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौन
स्तौन, अस्, m., Ved. a thief, robber, (Sāy. = स्तेन,<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 66, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेप्
स्तेप् स्तेप्, cl. 1. A. स्तेपते, &c., to ooze,<BR>&c. (= rt. स्तिप्, q. v.); cl. 10. P. स्तेप-<BR>यति, &c., to send, throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेम|स्तेमः
स्तेम स्तेम. See under rt. स्तिम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेय|स्तेयं
स्तेय स्तेय, स्तैन. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तै
स्तै स्तै, cl. 1. P. स्तायति, &c., to put on,<BR>adorn (= rt. स्नै); (probably also) to steal,<BR>do anything stealthily (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तायत्
स्तायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. stealing, acting stealthily,<BR>(Atharva-veda IV. 16, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैमित्य|स्तैमित्यं
स्तैमित्य स्तैमित्य, अम्, n. (fr. स्तिमित), fixed-<BR>ness, rigidity, immobility, numbness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोक|स्तोकः
स्तोक स्तोक, अस्, आ, अम्, little, small, short;<BR>few; low; (अस्), m. a small portion, drop (of water,<BR>ghee, &c.); the Cātaka bird; (अम्), ind. a little;<BR>less; [cf. Lith. stokoju, ‘I want.’]<BR>—स्तोक-काय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, little-bodied, small, diminutive.<BR>—स्तोक-<BR>नम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, a little bent down, slightly de-<BR>pressed.<BR>—स्तोक-शस्, ind. sparingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकक|स्तोककः
स्तोकक, अस्, m. the Cātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतव्य
स्तोतव्य स्तोतव्य, स्तोतृ, स्तोत्र. See p. 1143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभ|स्तोभं|स्तोभः
स्तोभ स्तोभ, &c. See under rt. 1. स्तुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्
स्तोम् स्तोम्. See स्तोमय, p. 1143,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम|स्तोमः
स्तोम स्तोम. See p. 1143, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौपिक|स्तौपिकं
स्तौपिक स्तौपिक. See स्तूप, p. 1143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौभिक|स्तौभिकं
स्तौभिक स्तौभिक. See under rt. 1. स्तुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौल
स्तौल स्तौल, अस्, आ, अम्, (for स्थौल fr. स्थू-<BR>ल), Ved. stout, robust, powerful, (Sāy. = स्थूल,<BR>प्रवृद्ध, Ṛg-veda VI. 44, 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यान|स्त्यानं|स्त्यानः
स्त्यान स्त्यान, स्त्येन. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यै
स्त्यै स्त्यै (also written ष्ट्यै), cl. 1. P.<BR>स्त्यायति, &c., to be collected into a heap<BR>or mass; to be spread about; to sound; [cf. accord-<BR>ing to some, probably Gr. στενός; Lat. stipare.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ति
स्ति, इस्, m. (according to Sāy. fr. rt. स्त्यै, but cf.<BR>उप-स्ति), Ved. a house, dwelling, abode, (Sāy. =<BR>गृह, Ṛg-veda VII. 19, 11; perhaps also ‘those<BR>who live in the house.’)<BR>—स्ति-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, house-<BR>protecting, (see Ṛg-veda VII. 66, 3; Nirukta VI.<BR>17.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिया
स्तिया, f., Ved. a collected mass; a mass or quantity<BR>of water, (Sāy. = आपः, Ṛg-veda VII. 5, 2; see<BR>Nirukta VI. 17.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यान|स्त्यानं|स्त्यानः
स्त्यान, अस्, आ, अम्, collecting into a mass; thick,<BR>bulky, gross; soft, bland, unctuous, smooth; sound-<BR>ing; (अम्), n. thickness, grossness, massiveness;<BR>unctuousness; nectar; idleness, sloth; echo, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्याय
स्त्याय in सं-स्त्याय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यायन|स्त्यायनं
स्त्यायन, अम्, n. collecting into a mass, aggrega-<BR>tion, crowding together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्येन|स्त्येनः
स्त्येन, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. II. 46. fr.<BR>rt. स्त्यै above), nectar (= अ-मृत); a thief (in<BR>this sense probably for स्तेन, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्री
स्त्री स्त्री, f. (probably a contraction of सो-<BR>त्री, fem. of 2. सोतृ, ‘a bearer of children,’ see<BR>p. 1118, col. 2; but according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 165.<BR>fr. rt. स्त्यै), a woman, female; a wife; the female<BR>of any animal (e. g. शाखामृग-स्त्री, ‘a female<BR>monkey’).<BR>—स्त्री-काम, अस्, m. desire of intercourse<BR>with women; fondness for women; desire of a wife;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), desirous of women, fond of women.<BR>—स्त्री-कार्य, अम्, n. the business of women; at-<BR>tendance on women or the women's apartments.<BR>—स्त्री-कुमार, अम्, n. a woman and child.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>कुसुम, अम्, n. the menstrual excretion in women.<BR>—स्त्री-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done by women.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>क्षीर, अम्, n. mother's milk.<BR>—स्त्री-गवी, f. a<BR>milch cow.<BR>—स्त्री-गुरु, उस्, m. a female Guru or<BR>priestess (who teaches initiatory Mantras).<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>घोष, अस्, m. ‘marked by the sound of women,’<BR>dawn, day-break.<BR>—स्त्री-घ्न, अस्, m. the murderer<BR>of a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-चरित्र, अम्, n. the doings of<BR>women.<BR>—स्त्री-चित्त-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, captivating the<BR>heart of women, pleasing to the female sex; (ई), m.<BR>the tree Śobhāñjana.<BR>—स्त्री-चिह्न, अम्, n. any mark<BR>or characteristic of the female sex; the female organ,<BR>vulva or womb.<BR>—स्त्री-चौर, अस्, m. ‘woman-thief,’<BR>a seducer of women, libertine.<BR>—स्त्री-जननी, f.<BR>‘bearing females,’ the mother of a daughter, a wo-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-c" target="_blank">Page1144-c+ 81</a>]<BR>man who brings forth only daughters.<BR>—स्त्री-जाति, इस्,<BR>f. the female sex.<BR>—स्त्री-जित, अस्, m. ‘wife-subdued,’<BR>a man ruled by his wife, a hen-pecked husband.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>तमा or स्त्रि-तमा, f. a thorough woman, (Pāṇ. VI.<BR>3, 44.)<BR>—स्त्री-तरा or स्त्रि-तरा, f. more thoroughly<BR>a woman, (Pāṇ. VI. 3, 44.)<BR>—स्त्री-ता, f. or स्त्री-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. womanhood, wife-hood; feminineness,<BR>effeminacy.<BR>—स्त्री-धन, अम्, n. ‘woman's wealth,’<BR>a wife's peculiar property or any property belonging<BR>to a woman over which she has independent control<BR>(said to be of six kinds, viz. अध्य्-अग्निक, a gift<BR>upon or in presence of the nuptial fire by a member<BR>of either family; अध्य्-आवाहनिक, that which is<BR>taken from the father's house at the time of the<BR>bridal procession or when the bride is conducted to<BR>her husband's home; आधिवेदनिक, a settlement on<BR>a first wife when her husband contracts a second<BR>marriage; प्रीति-दत्त, a gift of affection; शुल्क, a<BR>kind of dower or money given to a woman to induce<BR>her to go to her husband's house; अन्व्-आधेय, a<BR>gift from her own or husband's family after marriage:<BR>according to others the six kinds are, भर्तृ-दाय,<BR>पितृ-दत्त, मातृ-द्˚, भ्रातृ-द्˚, with the first two<BR>enumerated above: other varieties of woman's pro-<BR>perty are बन्धु-दत्त, q. v., यौतक, q. v., सौ-<BR>दायिक, q. v., पारिणाय्य, q. v., लावण्यार्जित, q. v.,<BR>and पादवन्दनिक, the last being a gift to a wife<BR>from a husband in return for her पाद-वन्दन,<BR>q. v., on her entering his house).<BR>—स्त्री-धर्म, अस्,<BR>m. the duty of a woman or wife; the laws concerning<BR>women; menstruation.<BR>—स्त्रीधर्म-योग, अस्, m.<BR>the application of laws or customs relative to women.<BR>—स्त्री-धर्मिणी, f. a woman during menstruation.<BR>—स्त्री-धव, अस्, m. a woman's husband; a man,<BR>male.<BR>—स्त्री-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘having the mark of a<BR>female,’ the female of any species of animal.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a woman as lord or pro-<BR>tector, protected by a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-नामन्, आ,<BR>म्नी, अ, having a female name.<BR>—स्त्री-निबन्धन,<BR>अम्, n. a woman's peculiar province, domestic duty,<BR>housewifery.<BR>—स्त्री-पण्योपजीविन् (˚य-उप्˚), ई, m.<BR>one who makes a living by keeping women for<BR>prostitution.<BR>—स्त्री-पर, अस्, m. one who is devoted<BR>to women, a woman-lover, libertine.<BR>—स्त्री-पर्वत-<BR>देश, अस्, m., N. of a district.<BR>—स्त्री-पर्वन्, अ, n.,<BR>N. of the eleventh book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>पिशाची, f. a fiend-like wife.<BR>—स्त्री-पुंस्, मान्, m.<BR>a woman who has become a man.<BR>—स्त्री-पुंस, औ,<BR>m. du. wife and husband, man and wife, the union<BR>of man and wife.<BR>—स्त्री-पुंस-लक्षणा, f. a wo-<BR>man who has the characteristic marks of both male<BR>and female, a hermaphrodite.<BR>—स्त्री-पुन्-धर्म,<BR>अस्, m. the law (which regulates the duties) of<BR>man and wife, the mutual duties of husband and<BR>wife or of man and woman.<BR>—स्त्री-पुन्-नपुं-<BR>सक, masculine, feminine, and neuter.<BR>—स्त्री-पूर्व<BR>or स्त्री-पूर्वक or स्त्री-पूर्विक, अस्, m. or स्त्री-<BR>पूर्विन्, ई, m. one who has been a woman for-<BR>merly or in a former birth, (according to Śabda-k.<BR>स्त्री-पूर्व = स्त्री-जित, ruled by a woman.)<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>प्रत्यय, अस्, m. (in grammar) a feminine affix, an<BR>affix used in forming feminines from Prātipadikas.<BR>—स्त्री-प्रमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, having a wife for an<BR>authority, one who is ruled by a wife.<BR>—स्त्री-प्र-<BR>सङ्ग, अस्, m. intercourse with women.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>प्रसू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, bearing females, bringing forth<BR>daughters only.<BR>—स्त्री-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, liked or<BR>loved by women; (अस्), m. the Mango tree.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>बाध्य, अस्, m. one who suffers himself to be dis-<BR>tressed by a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-बुद्धि, इस्, f. the female<BR>understanding.<BR>—स्त्री-भृत्य, आस्, m. pl. women and<BR>servants.<BR>—स्त्री-भोग, अस्, m. enjoyment of women,<BR>sexual intercourse.<BR>—स्त्री-मत्, आन्, m. a wife-pos-<BR>sessor, a married man.<BR>—स्त्री-मन्त्र, अस्, m. a<BR>woman's counsel, female stratagem.<BR>—स्त्री-मुख-<BR>प, अस्, m. ‘drinking the mouth of women,’ the<BR>Aśoka tree (= दोहली).<BR>—स्त्री-यन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘wo-<BR>man-vessel,’ woman regarded as a vessel or machine,<BR>a woman who works like a machine.<BR>—स्त्री-याचित-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. a son obtained through a wife's solicita-<BR>tions.<BR>—स्त्री-रञ्जन, अम्, n. ‘delighting women,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">Page1145-a+ 79</a>]<BR>betel (which with the areca-nut is much chewed by<BR>Hindū women).<BR>—स्त्री-रत्न, अम्, n. a jewel or<BR>gem of a woman, an excellent woman; N. of Lak-<BR>ṣmī.<BR>—स्त्री-राज्य, अम्, n. the kingdom of women<BR>(a country placed by some in the region of Bhotan).<BR>—स्त्री-रोग, अस्, m. any disease incident to women.<BR>—स्त्री-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. the female organ; the feminine<BR>gender.<BR>—स्त्रीलिङ्ग-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being in the<BR>feminine gender, being a feminine.<BR>—स्त्री-वध,<BR>अस्, m. the slaying of a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-वश, अम्, n.<BR>subjection to women, submissiveness to a wife.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>वाक्याङ्कुश-प्रक्षुण्ण (˚य-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>driven or urged on by the goad of women's words.<BR>—स्त्री-विधेय, अस्, आ, अम्, submissive to a wife,<BR>governed by a wife, uxorious.<BR>—स्त्री-वियोग, अस्, m.<BR>separation from a wife.<BR>—स्त्री-विवाह, अस्, m. ‘wo-<BR>man-marriage,’ the act of contracting marriage with<BR>a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded or at-<BR>tended by women.<BR>—स्त्री-संसर्ग, अस्, m. inter-<BR>course with women, female society.<BR>—स्त्री-सं-<BR>स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, having a female shape.<BR>—स्त्री-<BR>सङ्ग, अस्, m. attachment or addiction to women;<BR>intercourse with a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-सङ्ग्रहण, अम्,<BR>n. the act of embracing a woman (improperly),<BR>adultery, seduction.<BR>—स्त्री-सभ, अम्, n. an assembly<BR>of women, collection of females.<BR>—स्त्री-सम्बन्ध,<BR>अस्, m. matrimonial connection with a woman; con-<BR>nection by marriage; relation or reference to women.<BR>—स्त्री-सेवा, f. ‘woman-service,’ addiction to wo-<BR>men.<BR>—स्त्री-स्वभाव, अस्, m. the nature or disposi-<BR>tion of women; a guard of the women's apartments,<BR>eunuch.<BR>—स्त्री-स्वरूप, अस्, आ, अम्, or स्त्री-स्वरूप-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, or स्त्री-स्वरूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having<BR>a woman's shape or figure.<BR>—स्त्री-हत्या, f. the<BR>murder of a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-हन्तृ, ता, m. the mur-<BR>derer of a woman.<BR>—स्त्री-हरण, अम्, n. the carry-<BR>ing off or forcible abduction of a woman; rape.<BR>—स्त्री-हारिन्, ई, m. the carrier off of a woman; one<BR>who commits rape, a ravisher.<BR>—स्त्र्य्-अभिगमन,<BR>अम्, n. the act of approaching a woman, sexual inter-<BR>course.<BR>—स्त्र्य्-आजीव, अस्, m. one who lives by his<BR>wife; one who lives by keeping women for pros-<BR>titution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीक
स्त्रीक = स्त्री (at the end of an adj. comp., e. g.<BR>स-स्त्रीक, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैण|स्त्रैणं|स्त्रैणः
स्त्रैण, अस्, ई, अम्, female, feminine; suited or<BR>belonging to women; being among women; (अम्),<BR>n. womanhood, feminineness; the female sex; the<BR>nature of woman; a multitude of women; sexual<BR>enjoyment (Ved.).<BR>—स्त्रैण-ता, f. or स्त्रैण-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. effeminacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैराजक
स्त्रैराजक, आस्, f. pl. (probably) the women of<BR>Strī-rājya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैषूय
स्त्रैषूय. See Atharva-veda VI. 11, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ|स्थः
स्थ स्थ. See under rt. 1. स्था, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थकर|स्थकरं
स्थकर स्थकर (connected with स्थगर<BR>below), a betel-nut (according to some; cf. स्थगी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग्
स्थग् स्थग्, cl. 1. P. स्थगति, तस्थाग,<BR>अस्थगीत्, &c., to cover, hide, conceal:<BR>Caus. स्थगयति, &c., to cover, veil, hide, make<BR>invisible; [cf. Gr. στέγ-ω, στέγ-η, τέγη, στέγος,<BR>τέγος, στεγ-ανό-ς, στεγ-νό-ς: Lat. teg-o, tec-tu-m,<BR>teg-i-men, teg-ula: Old Norse thek, ‘a roof:’ Old<BR>Germ. dak-jan: Angl. Sax. theccan, thaca: Lith.<BR>steg-iu, ‘I cover;’ stoga-s, ‘a roof.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग|स्थगः
स्थग, अस्, आ, अम्, fraudulent, dishonest, shame-<BR>less, abandoned; (अस्), m. a rogue, cheat; (ई), f. a<BR>betel box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगन|स्थगनं
स्थगन, अम्, n. the act of covering or conceal-<BR>ing, concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगर|स्थगरं|स्थगरः
स्थगर, a kind of plant (= पुत्र-जीवक);<BR>(perhaps) a betel-nut; [cf. स्थगी above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगिका
स्थगिका, f. a courtezan; the office of betel-<BR>bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगित|स्थगितं
स्थगित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered, concealed, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगु|स्थगुः
स्थगु, उस्, m. a hump, an excrescence or pro-<BR>tuberance on the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिल|स्थंडिल|स्थंडिलं|स्थण्डिलं
स्थण्डिल स्थण्डिल, अम्, n. (according to<BR>some connected with rt. स्थल्), a piece of ground<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">Page1145-b+ 79</a>]<BR>(levelled, squared, and prepared for a sacrifice); a<BR>barren field; a heap of clods; a boundary, limit, land-<BR>mark; (अस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—स्थण्डिल-शायिन्,<BR>ई, m. a devotee who sleeps on the bare ground or on<BR>the sacrificial Sthaṇḍila (on account of a religious<BR>vow).<BR>—स्थण्डिल-सितक, अम्, n. an altar.<BR>—स्थण्-<BR>डिले-शय, अस्, m. an ascetic who sleeps on the bare<BR>ground or on the Sthaṇḍila; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलेयु
स्थण्डिलेयु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थन
स्थन स्थन (fr. rt. 1. अस्), Ved. = भवथ,<BR>(Ṛg-veda VIII. 18, 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपति|स्थपतिः
स्थपति स्थ-पति. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुट|स्थपुटः
स्थपुट स्थपुट, अस्, आ, अम्, being in con-<BR>tracted or difficult circumstances; unevenly raised,<BR>elevated and depressed, bent down.<BR>—स्थपुट-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, being in contracted and uneven<BR>places, being on raised places and in hollows.<BR>—स्थपुटी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made uneven, raised<BR>and depressed; (according to one commentator)<BR>covered with grass, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल्
स्थल् स्थल् (connected with rt. 1. स्था),<BR>cl. 1. P. स्थलति, तस्थाल, स्थलिष्-<BR>यति, अस्थालीत्, स्थलितुम्, to stand firm, be firm:<BR>Caus. स्थालयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अतिष्ठलत्, to<BR>cause to stand firm, fix firmly: Desid. of Caus.<BR>तिस्थालयिषति: Desid. तिस्थलिषति: Intens. ता-<BR>स्थल्यते, तास्थल्ति; [cf. Gr. στέλλ-ω, ἔσταλκα,<BR>ἐ-στάλη-ν, στόλο-ς, στάλ-ιξ, στελεό-ν;] Lat. prœ-<BR>stol-o-r, stul-tu-s, stol-i-du-s (?); Old Germ. stil,<BR>stallan, stellan; Lith. stelloju, ‘I appoint.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल|स्थलं
स्थल, अम्, ई, n. f. firm or dry ground, terra<BR>firma, dry land (as opposed to ‘water’); shore,<BR>strand, beach; ground or land (in general), soil;<BR>place, spot, site; field, tract, district; station; (अम्,<BR>आ), n. f. a spot of dry ground artificially raised and<BR>drained; (ई), f. a deity of the soil, local or tutelary<BR>divinity; (अम्), n. a piece of raised ground, mound,<BR>terrace; a topic, case, subject (of a description &c.),<BR>point under discussion; part (of a book); a tent,<BR>house of cloth; [cf. Old Germ. stal, ‘a place;’ stul-<BR>lan, stelza, stolv: Goth. ga-stalds: Angl. Sax.<BR>stal, stœl, stillan, stille: Mod. Germ. stall.]<BR>—स्थल-कन्द, अस्, m. a kind of plant (= अग्रा-<BR>म्य-कन्द).<BR>—स्थल-कमल, अम्, n. or स्थल-<BR>कमलिनी, f. the flowering shrub, Hibiscus Muta-<BR>bilis.<BR>—स्थल-कुमुद, अस्, m. the Kara-vīra plant.<BR>—स्थल-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone or left on dry land.<BR>—स्थल-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, land-going, living on dry<BR>land, not aquatic (opposed to जल-चर).<BR>—स्थल-<BR>च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen or removed from a place or<BR>position.<BR>—स्थल-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, land-born, ter-<BR>restrial, not aquatic.<BR>—स्थल-तस्, ind. from dry<BR>land, from terra firma.<BR>—स्थल-ता, f. the state of<BR>being dry ground.<BR>—स्थल-देवता, f. a local or<BR>rural deity, tutelary god presiding over some par-<BR>ticular spot.<BR>—स्थल-नलिनी, f. = स्थल-पद्मिनी<BR>below.<BR>—स्थल-पद्म, अस्, m. = मानक; (अम्),<BR>n. the shrub Hibiscus Mutabilis; another plant (=<BR>छत्त्र-पत्त्र, तमालक).<BR>—स्थल-पद्मिनी, f.<BR>the shrub Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR>—स्थल-मञ्जरी, f.<BR>the plant Achyranthes Aspera.<BR>—स्थल-मार्ग, अस्,<BR>m. or स्थल-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. a way or road by land,<BR>(स्थल-वर्त्मना, inst. c. by land, as opposed to<BR>जल-मार्गेण, by water.)<BR>—स्थल-विग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>a battle on level ground.<BR>—स्थल-शुद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>purification or clearance of a place from impurity.<BR>—स्थल-शृङ्गाट or स्थल-शृङ्गाटक, अस्, m.<BR>the plant Tribulus Lanuginosus (= गो-क्षुर).<BR>—स्थल-सीमन्, आ, m. a land-mark, boundary.<BR>—स्थल-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or being on<BR>dry ground, being on terra firma, being on shore.<BR>—स्थलान्तर (˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n. another place.<BR>—स्थलारूढ (˚ल-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, alighted on<BR>the ground.<BR>—स्थले-रुह, अस्, आ, अम्, growing on<BR>dry ground; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= गृह-कु-<BR>मारी); another plant (= दग्धा).<BR>—स्थले-शय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping on dry ground; (अस्), m. any<BR>amphibious animal (such as a tortoise, otter, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थली
स्थली, f. dry ground, &c.; see under स्थल<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">Page1145-c+ 79</a>]<BR>above.<BR>—स्थली-देवता, f. a local divinity, deity of<BR>the soil or tutelary deity presiding over some par-<BR>ticular spot (as a field, grove, village, &c.), a kind<BR>of faun or dryad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीय
स्थलीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to dry<BR>ground, terrestrial; belonging to a place, local.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलेयु
स्थलेयु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवि|स्थविः
स्थवि स्थवि, स्थविर, &c. See p. 1146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविष्ठ|स्थविष्ठः
स्थविष्ठ स्थविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, (superl. of<BR>स्थूल), largest, most bulky; very big, very fat or<BR>corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवीयस्
स्थवीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of स्थूल), larger,<BR>bigger, more bulky, fatter, stronger; very fat, very<BR>corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्था
स्था 1. स्था, cl. 1. P. (ep. and in some<BR>special significations also A.) तिष्ठति, -ते<BR>(स्थात् = तिष्ठतु, Ṛg-veda II. 3, 10), तस्थौ<BR>(2nd sing, तस्थिथ or तस्थाथ, 1st du. तस्थिव),<BR>तस्थे, स्थास्यति, -ते, अस्थात् (3rd pl. अस्थुः), अस्-<BR>थित (3rd pl. अस्थिषत), Prec. स्थेयात्, स्था-<BR>सीष्ट, स्थातुम्, to stand (often with inst., e. g.<BR>पादाभ्यां स्था, to stand on the feet; जानुभ्यां<BR>स्था, to stand on the knees, i. e. to kneel); to stand<BR>still, stand firmly; to stay, stop, abide, dwell, remain,<BR>rest, wait; to stop, cease, desist; to rest on, depend<BR>on (sometimes A.); to be in any situation or state<BR>or position; to be, exist, live; to be at hand, be<BR>near or at the side; to abide or continue or be en-<BR>gaged in any act or course of action, practice, per-<BR>form, behave, occupy one's self with, (sometimes with<BR>loc., e. g. शासने स्था, to abide in a command, i. e. to<BR>be obedient; sometimes with inst., e. g. सामादिभिः<BR>स्था, to practice or continue practising conciliation,<BR>&c.; मौन-व्रतेन स्था, to continue observing<BR>a vow of silence; sometimes with ind. part., especially<BR>if a habit or continuous course of action is implied,<BR>e. g. धर्मम् आश्रित्य तिष्ठति, he continues prac-<BR>tising virtue); to stand as a prostitute, give one's<BR>self up to sexual embrace, offer one's self to (A., e. g.<BR>देव-दत्ताय तिष्ठते, she offers herself to Deva-<BR>datta, Pāṇ. 1. 4, 34): Pass. स्थीयते, 2nd fut. स्था-<BR>स्यते or स्थायिष्यते, Aor. अस्थायि, to be stood;<BR>to be stayed or remained or abided, to be fixed<BR>or located, &c. (frequently used impersonally, e. g.<BR>मया स्थीयताम्, let it be abided by me, i. e.<BR>I must abide): Caus. स्थापयति, -ते (sometimes<BR>regarded as a nominal fr. स्थिर), -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अतिष्ठिपत्, -त, to cause to stand; to cause to<BR>stand still or firmly; to fix, settle, establish, set<BR>up, found, institute, erect, build; to place, put, lo-<BR>cate, set, lay; to stop, arrest, restrain, hold in; to<BR>cause to be in any state or position; to cause to<BR>continue, make durable; to cause to live; to give in<BR>marriage; to make (with two acc.); to instruct in<BR>(with two acc.): Desid. तिष्ठासति, -ते: Intens.<BR>तेष्ठीयते, तास्थाति; [cf. Zend hi-stā-mi = Sans.<BR>ति-ष्ठा-मि: Gr. ἵ-στη-μι, ἔ-στη-ν, στά-σι-ς, στα-μίν,<BR>στά-μνο-ς, ἰ-στό-ς, στή-μην, στή-λη, στα-τήρ,<BR>στα-θ-ερό-ς, στα-θ-μό-ς, στῆ-θ-ο-ς, στε-νό-ς; (with<BR>the Caus. may be compared also, according to some)<BR>στέφ-ω (for στεπ-ω), στέμ-μα, στέφ-ος, στέφ-ανο-ς,<BR>στεφ-άνη, τόπ-ο-ς: Lat. st-o, si-st-o, stă-ti-m,<BR>stă-ti-o, Sta-tor, stă-tu-s, stă-tu-o, stă-tua, stā-<BR>men, stă-bu-lu-m, stă-bi-li-s; (also with the Caus.)<BR>stipa-re, stipatores, stipulāri, stapia; (according<BR>to some also) stup-eo, stup-idu-s: Old Germ. stā-m,<BR>stedi, standa, stat: Goth. stan-dan, ‘to stand;’<BR>stath-s, ‘a place;’ stol-s, ‘a stool, throne:’ Angl.<BR>Sax. stan-dan, stand, studu, stund: Slav. sta-ti,<BR>‘to stand:’ Lith. stó-ti, ‘to stand;’ sta-tù-s, ‘stand-<BR>ing;’ statý-ti, ‘to place;’ sto-na-s, ‘a stand, sta-<BR>tion;’ stá-kle-s, ‘a loom:’ Hib. sta-d, ‘stop, delay,<BR>state, condition;’ stadaim, ‘I stand, stop.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्थिवस्
तस्थिवस्, वान्, -थुषी, वत्, one who has stood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ|स्थः
स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing, staying, abiding, being<BR>situated, living, existing (generally found at the end<BR>of comps., e. g. गर्भ-स्˚, जल-स्˚, दूर-स्˚); a<BR>place, spot, ground, = स्थल (according to Śabda-k.).<BR>—स्थ-पति, इस्, m. (probably fr. स्थ + पति, but<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">Page1146-a+ 81</a>]<BR>according to some from the Caus. of rt. 1. स्था),<BR>‘ground-lord,’ a sovereign, chief, king (according to<BR>Kātyāyana's Śrauta-sūtras XXII. 11, 11, &c. a Stha-<BR>pati is a Vaiśya, or even a person of lower caste, who<BR>has celebrated the Go-sava sacrifice after being chosen<BR>king); an architect; a master carpenter or mason,<BR>wheelwright; a charioteer; one who sacrifices to<BR>Vṛhas-pati, a performer of the Vṛhas-pati sacrifice;<BR>a guard or attendant of the women's apartments; N.<BR>of Kuvera; (इस्, इस्, इ), chief, best, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवि|स्थविः
स्थवि, इस्, m. a weaver; heaven (= स्वर्ग); =<BR>जङ्गम (according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविर|स्थविरं|स्थविरः
स्थविर, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed, firm, steady [cf. स्था-<BR>विर]; old, aged, ancient, (सप्तत्या स्थविरः, one<BR>who is seventy years old, see स्थाविर); (अस्), m.<BR>an old man; a beggar; epithet of Brahmā; (आ), f.<BR>an old woman; a kind of plant, = महा-श्रावणी;<BR>(अम्), n. = शैलेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्था
2. स्था, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. standing, stationary, (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X. 88, 4. स्थाः = स्था-<BR>वरं वृक्षादि रूपम्; see also Nirukta V. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणु|स्थाणुः
स्थाणु, उस्, उस्, उ, firm, fixed, steady, stable, im-<BR>movable, motionless; (उस्), m., N. of Śiva; a stake,<BR>post, pile; a peg, pin, pillar; the gnomon of a dial;<BR>a spear, dart; a nest of white ants; the drug or per-<BR>fume called Jīvaka, q. v.; (उस्, उ), m. n. a branchless<BR>trunk or stem, the trunk of a lopped tree or of any<BR>tree, any bare stock or stem.<BR>—स्थाणु-च्छेद, अस्,<BR>m. one who cuts down the trunks of trees, one who<BR>clears away timber, (Manu IX. 44.)<BR>—स्थाणु-तीर्-<BR>थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—स्थाणु-भ्रम, अस्,<BR>m. mistaking anything for a post.<BR>—स्थाणु-वत्,<BR>ind. like a post.<BR>—स्थाणु-वनौकस् (˚न-ओक्˚), आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, inhabiting Śiva's forest.<BR>—स्थाण्व्-ईश्वर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a particular Śiva-liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातव्य|स्थातव्यं
स्थातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stood; to be stayed<BR>or remained; to be fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातुस्
स्थातुस्, n. (according to some modern scholars<BR>an old nom. sing. neut. for the later स्थातृ), Ved.<BR>anything standing or stationary (opposed to चरथ,<BR>see Ṛg-veda I. 58, 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातृ
स्थातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what stands or stays<BR>stationary, standing (frequently opposed to जगत् in<BR>the phrase स्थातुर् जगतश्च, e. g. विश्वस्य स्था-<BR>तुर् जगतश्च गोपाः, the preserver of everything<BR>that stands and moves, Ṛg-veda VII. 60, 2); [cf.<BR>Lat. stator.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थान|स्थानं
स्थान, अम्, n. the act of standing or staying,<BR>stay, continuance, the being fixed or stationary;<BR>state, condition; a stationary state or condition, (one<BR>of the three aims or results of state policy; it is de-<BR>scribed as a kind of neutral or middle state character-<BR>ized by neither loss nor gain, failure nor success);<BR>the act of standing firm so as to resist a charge, firm<BR>or calm bearing of troops, (Manu VII. 190); halt;<BR>the stamina of a kingdom, that which constitutes its<BR>chief strength or by virtue of which it exists, (regarded<BR>as consisting of four parts, viz. army, treasury, city,<BR>and territory, Manu VII. 56); the place of standing<BR>or staying, any place, spot, locality, site, situation,<BR>position, posture, station, post; office, appointment,<BR>rank, dignity, degree; proper or right place; the<BR>place or organ of utterance of any letter (which, ac-<BR>cording to Pāṇini, are eight, viz. कण्ठ, the throat;<BR>तालु, the palate; मूर्धन्, the top of the palate;<BR>दन्त, the teeth; ओष्ठ, the lips; कण्ठ-तालु,<BR>the throat and palate; कण्ठोष्ठ, the throat and<BR>lips; दन्तोष्ठ, the teeth and lips; to which may<BR>be added नासिका, which is the place of utterance for<BR>the true Anusvāra, and उरस्, the chest, which is said<BR>to be the place of Visarga); dwelling-place, abode,<BR>house; country, region, district; a town, city; a par-<BR>ticular place or sphere assigned after death to those<BR>who do their duty or neglect it, (that of virtuous<BR>Brāhmans is called Prājāpatya; of Kṣatriyas, Aindra;<BR>of Vaiśyas, Māruta; of Śūdras, Gāndharva; similarly,<BR>neglectors of duty have places of punishment assigned<BR>to them); a holy place; an altar; an open place in<BR>a town, green, plain, square; part or division of a<BR>book, section, chapter; the part or character of an<BR>actor; interval, opportunity, leisure; an object (e. g.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-b" target="_blank">Page1146-b+ 81</a>]<BR>शुल्क-स्थ्˚, an object of toll, taxation; पूजा-स्थ्˚,<BR>object of honour; कोप-स्थ्˚, object of anger); a<BR>modulation of the voice, note, tone (of which, ac-<BR>cording to the Ṛg-veda-Prātiśākhya, there are three;<BR>see मन्द्र); likeness, resemblance; intimation;<BR>(स्थाने), loc. c. in the right or proper place, pro-<BR>perly, suitably, appropriately, justly, fitly, truly; at<BR>the right or appropriate moment, opportunely; some-<BR>times; in the place of, in the room of, in lieu of,<BR>instead of (with gen.; in Pāṇini's grammar, when<BR>the gen. c. stands alone, the word स्थाने has to be<BR>supplied, thus हन्तेर् जः means that ज is to be sub-<BR>stituted ‘in place of’ हन्, see Pāṇ. I. 1, 49); on<BR>account of, because of; like, resembling, similarly,<BR>as; [cf. δύστηνος (i. e. δυσ-στηνος), ἄ-στηνος,<BR>ἀστήν, ἀσταίνω, δυσταίνω.]<BR>—स्थान-चञ्चला, f.<BR>the plant Ocimum Pilosum (= वर्वरी).<BR>—स्थान-<BR>चिन्तक, अस्, m. an officer who superintends places<BR>of residence or official dwellings or provides quarters<BR>for an army, a kind of quarter-master.<BR>—स्थान-<BR>च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, = स्थान-भ्रष्ट below.<BR>—स्थान-तस्, ind. according to place or station;<BR>in regard to the place or organ of utterance.<BR>—स्था-<BR>न-त्याग, अस्, m. desertion of post, leaving one's<BR>place.<BR>—स्थान-पाल, अस्, m. ‘place-protector,<BR>place-keeper,’ a watchman, sentinel, policeman.<BR>—स्थान-प्रच्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, ejected from a<BR>station or post, removed from an office, &c.<BR>—स्थान-<BR>भूमि, इस्, f. a dwelling-place, mansion.<BR>—स्थान-<BR>भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen or removed from any<BR>place or station, ejected from an office, displaced, out<BR>of place.<BR>—स्थान-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. the greatness<BR>or glory of any place, a kind of divine virtue sup-<BR>posed to be inherent in a sacred spot, and to operate<BR>upon those who visit it.<BR>—स्थान-योग, अस्, m. as-<BR>signment of suitable places, proper mode or place for<BR>preserving articles, (Manu IX. 332.)<BR>—स्थान-रक्-<BR>षक, अस्, m. = स्थान-पाल.<BR>—स्थान-विभाग,<BR>अस्, m. subdivision of a number according to the<BR>places of its figures.<BR>—स्थान-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, abid-<BR>ing in one place, staying at home.<BR>—स्थनाध्य-<BR>क्ष (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m. the superintendent of any<BR>place or post; a local governor; a watchman, police-<BR>officer.<BR>—स्थानान्तर (˚न-अन्˚), अम्, n. another<BR>place.<BR>—स्थानान्तर-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to<BR>another place, gone away.<BR>—स्थानान्य-त्व (˚न-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. difference or diversity of place.<BR>—स्था-<BR>नाभाव (˚न-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the want of a place or<BR>situation.<BR>—स्थानासन (˚न-आस्˚), ए, n. du. stand-<BR>ing and sitting down.<BR>—स्थानासन-विहार-वत्,<BR>आन्, m. (a pupil) occupying the station and seat and<BR>place of religious exercises (of his preceptor, Manu<BR>II. 248).<BR>—स्थानासेध (˚न-आस्˚), अस्, m. confine-<BR>ment to a place, imprisonment, arrest.<BR>—स्थानेश्वर<BR>(˚न-ईश्˚), N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानक|स्थानकं
स्थानक, अम्, n. a position, situation; a par-<BR>ticular point or situation in dramatic action, (पताका-<BR>स्थानक, a striking situation introduced as an episode<BR>into the regular plot of a drama); a city, town; a<BR>basin or trench dug for water at the root of a tree;<BR>froth or a kind of scum on spirits or wine; a mode<BR>of recitation; a division or section of the Taittirīya<BR>branch of the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिक|स्थानिकः
स्थानिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to a place or site,<BR>local; (in grammar) that which takes the place of<BR>anything else or is substituted for it; (अस्), m. any one<BR>holding an official post, a placeman, the governor of a<BR>place, superintendent of a district, manager of a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिन्
स्थानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a place, having fixedness,<BR>placed, abiding, permanent; having a substitute; (ई),<BR>m. (in Pāṇini's grammar) the original form or primitive<BR>element (i. e. that form for which anything is substi-<BR>tuted; the substituted form which takes its place being<BR>called आदेश); that which has a place, that which has<BR>a place in a sentence or is actually expressed.<BR>—स्था-<BR>नि-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being the original or primitive<BR>form.<BR>—स्थानि-वत्, ind. (in grammar) like the<BR>original form or primitive element, (the आदेश or<BR>substituted form is said to be स्थानि-वत् when it is<BR>liable to all the rules which hold good for the primi-<BR>tive.)<BR>—स्थानिवत्-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">Page1146-c+ 81</a>]<BR>like the original form or element.<BR>—स्थान्य्-आश्रय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, depending on the primitive form (said of<BR>a grammatical operation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानीय|स्थानीयं
स्थानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or suitable to any<BR>place, prevailing in any place, local; (अम्), n. a town, city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापक|स्थापकः
स्थापक, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the Caus.), causing to<BR>stand, placing, fixing, establishing, founding, order-<BR>ing, regulating; (अस्), m. the establisher or director<BR>of the stage-business, a kind of stage-manager; the<BR>founder of a temple, erector of an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्य|स्थापत्यः
स्थापत्य, अस्, m. (fr. स्थ-पति), a guard of the<BR>women's apartments; (अम्), n. architecture, building,<BR>erecting.<BR>—स्थापत्य-वेद, अस्, m. ‘the science of<BR>architecture,’ one of the four Upa-vedas, (see उप-<BR>वेद.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापन|स्थापनं
स्थापन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), the act of caus-<BR>ing to stand, placing, fixing, establishing, erecting,<BR>founding, instituting, regulating, directing, appoint-<BR>ing; fixing the thoughts, concentration of the mind,<BR>abstraction; a dwelling, habitation; a ceremony per-<BR>formed when a mother perceives the first signs of<BR>living conception, = पुं-सवन; (आ), f. placing,<BR>fixing, establishing, regulating, arranging (as a drama<BR>&c.), stage-management; (ई), f. a kind of plant (=<BR>पाठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापनीय
स्थापनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed or fixed or<BR>established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापयत्
स्थापयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to stand, fixing,<BR>placing, establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापयित्वा
स्थापयित्वा, ind. having placed or fixed, having<BR>established or erected, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापित|स्थापितं
स्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused or made to stand,<BR>fixed, established, placed, located, deposited; set up,<BR>erected; founded, instituted, endowed, set apart;<BR>placed in any post or situation, appointed; ordered,<BR>regulated, directed, enjoined, ordained, enacted; set-<BR>tled, ascertained, certain; firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापितवत्
स्थापितवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has placed or<BR>fixed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्य|स्थाप्यः
स्थाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed or deposited;<BR>to be fixed or established; (अम्), n. a deposit, pledge<BR>(= निक्षेप).<BR>—स्थाप्यापहरण (˚य-अप्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the stealing or embezzling of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थामन्
स्थामन्, अ, n. strength, power, stamina; fixity,<BR>stability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिन्
स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, standing, staying, being, situ-<BR>ated (often at end of comps., cf. अन्तर-स्थ्˚); abid-<BR>ing, stopping, fixed, stationary, enduring, continuing,<BR>permanent, constant, lasting (as a feeling or state,<BR>see स्थायि-भाव below); steady, firm, unchange-<BR>able, invariable; (इ), n. anything lasting, a permanent<BR>state or condition (opposed to व्य्-अभिचारिन्, q. v.).<BR>—स्थायि-ता, f. or स्थायि-त्व, अम्, n. permanency,<BR>steadiness, fixedness, constancy, invariableness.<BR>—स्था-<BR>यि-भाव, अस्, m. a particular fixed or permanent<BR>condition of mind or body, lasting feeling (as form-<BR>ing a class of feelings or conditions which are fa-<BR>vourite subjects of description in poetical and dramatic<BR>compositions; these Sthāyi-bhāvas are opposed to<BR>the Vyabhicāri-bhāvas, and are said in the Sāhitya-<BR>darpaṇa to be eight in number, viz. 1. रति, love or<BR>desire; 2. हास, mirth; 3. शोक, sorrow; 4. क्रो-<BR>ध, resentment; 5. उत्साह, high-mindedness or<BR>heroism; 6. भय, terror; 7. जुगुप्सा, disgust or<BR>aversion; 8. विस्मय, surprise; to which is some-<BR>times added a ninth, viz. शम, quietism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायुक|स्थायुकः
स्थायुक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, disposed to stay or last,<BR>apt to endure, of a steady nature, abiding, stopping,<BR>stationary, steady, firm; (अस्), m. the overseer of a<BR>village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाल|स्थालं
स्थाल, अम्, n. a plate or dish (generally made of<BR>some metal and used in eating); a cooking-pot,<BR>caldron or any culinary utensil.<BR>—स्थाल-रूप, अम्,<BR>n. the form or representation of a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाली
स्थाली, f. an earthen pot or pan, cooking-pot,<BR>caldron, kettle, boiler; a particular vessel used in the<BR>preparation of Soma; the substitution of a cooked<BR>offering of rice &c. for the offering of meat at the<BR>Māṃsāṣṭakā, q. v.; the trumpet-flower, Bignonia<BR>Suaveolens.<BR>—स्थाली-दरण, अम्, n. the breaking<BR>of a pot.<BR>—स्थाली-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, cooked or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">Page1147-a+ 81</a>]<BR>dressed in a pot, boiled.<BR>—स्थाली-पाक, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a particular religious act performed by a house-<BR>holder, a cooked offering of rice, &c.; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>scil. मन्त्राः, epithet of particular Vedic hymns.<BR>—स्थाली-पुरीष, अम्, n. the sediment or dirt<BR>sticking to a kettle or cooking-pot.<BR>—स्थाली-पु-<BR>लाक, अस्, m. boiled rice in a cooking-pot; an illus-<BR>tration derived from the rule of boiled rice in a pot<BR>(by which all the grains are equally moistened by<BR>the heated water).<BR>—स्थाली-विल, अम्, n. the interior<BR>or hollow of a caldron or cooking-pot.<BR>—स्थाली-<BR>विलीय or स्थाली-विल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit to be boiled<BR>or cooked in a pot.<BR>—स्थाली-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of plant or tree (= नन्दी-वृक्ष, अश्वत्थ-<BR>भेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावन्
स्थावन्, आ, अरी, अ, standing, stable, stationary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावर|स्थावरं|स्थावरः
स्थावर, अस्, आ, अम्, standing still, not moving,<BR>not having the power of motion, not locomotive,<BR>fixed to one spot, fixed, stationary, firm, stable, immov-<BR>able, (opposed to जङ्गम, q. v.); inert, inactive,<BR>slow (said of poison); regular, established; (अस्), m.<BR>a mountain; (अम्), n. any stationary or inanimate<BR>object (as a plant, mineral, &c.; these stationary<BR>objects constituted the seventh creation of Brahmā<BR>or तस्थुषां सर्ग, see under सर्ग; cf. Manu<BR>I. 41); a bow-string; immovable property, real<BR>estate (such as land or houses); a heir-loom, family<BR>possession (such as jewels &c. which have been long<BR>preserved in a family and ought not to be sold).<BR>—स्थावर-ता, f. fixedness, stability, the quality of<BR>being stationary, immobility; the state of a vegetable<BR>or mineral, (Manu XII. 9.)<BR>—स्थावर-जङ्गम,<BR>अम्, n. or आनि, n. pl. things stationary and movable<BR>or inanimate and animate, (Manu I. 41.)<BR>—स्थाव-<BR>रादि (˚र-आदि), n. the poison called Vatsa-nābha,<BR>q. v.<BR>—स्थावरास्थावर (˚र-अस्˚), अम्, n. things<BR>stationary and movable, immovable and movable<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाविर|स्थाविरं
स्थाविर, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. स्थविर), thick, firm<BR>(Ved.); (अम्), n. old age (described as commencing<BR>after seventy in men and after fifty in women, and<BR>ending at ninety, after which period a man is called<BR>वर्षीयस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासक|स्थासकः
स्थासक, अस्, m. perfuming or smearing the body<BR>with fragrant unguents (of sandal &c.); a bubble of<BR>water or any fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासु
स्थासु, उ, n. bodily strength or stamina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नु|स्थास्नुः
स्थास्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, disposed to stand, firm,<BR>stationary, immovable, fixed, stable; durable, per-<BR>manent, eternal; a tree or plant (= वृक्ष; cf.<BR>स्थावर).<BR>—स्थास्नु-ता, f. firmness, stability, dura-<BR>bility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित|स्थितः
स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, stood, stayed, remained,<BR>stopped; standing; standing up, risen; staying,<BR>resting, abiding, (उच्चावचेषु स्थित, abiding in<BR>all things high and low); being, situated, existing,<BR>living; stood still, standing still, desisted, stopped;<BR>fixed, permanent, settled, steady, firm, immovable;<BR>steadfast, determined, resolved, decreed, established;<BR>steady or steadfast in conduct; faithful to a promise<BR>or agreement; upright, virtuous; agreed, engaged,<BR>contracted, promised; being close at hand, ready;<BR>(अम्), n. (in Vedic grammar), scil. पद, a word<BR>standing by itself (i. e. without the particle इति in<BR>the Pada text; opposed to उप-स्थित).<BR>—स्थित-<BR>धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, steady-minded, firm-minded, firm,<BR>unmoved, calm.<BR>—स्थित-पाठ्य, (in the drama)<BR>recitation in Prākṛt by a woman standing.<BR>—स्थित-<BR>प्रज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, firm in judgment or wisdom,<BR>free from fancies or hallucinations, calm, contented.<BR>—स्थित-प्रेमन्, आ, m. ‘firm in affection,’ a firm<BR>or faithful friend.<BR>—स्थितोपस्थित (˚त-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, (a word) with and without the particle इति<BR>(in the Pada text; see स्थित above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितवत्|स्थितवन्त्
स्थितवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has stood or<BR>stayed or abided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिति|स्थितिः
स्थिति, इस्, f. standing, staying, remaining, con-<BR>tinuing, living, residing, abiding; stay, residence;<BR>standing still, stopping, continuance in one state;<BR>remaining stationary, stability, duration, fixedness,<BR>fixity, a firm position; stop, cessation; pause; any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-b" target="_blank">Page1147-b+ 81</a>]<BR>situation, state, position; posture, condition, natural<BR>state, state of a case; good condition, well-doing,<BR>welfare; station, high station, rank, dignity; per-<BR>manence; continuance or steadfastness in the path<BR>of duty, steadiness, correctness of conduct, propriety,<BR>good manners; consistency; establishment of good<BR>order (in a government); settled rule, sure or fixed<BR>decision, ordinance, decree, axiom, maxim; settled<BR>determination; term, limit, boundary; (in philo-<BR>sophy) inertia, resistance to motion; one of the<BR>three states through which the system of created<BR>things and every individual being passes, (these<BR>three states are, 1. उत्पत्ति, arising into being;<BR>2. स्थिति, continuance in life; 3. लय, dissolution);<BR>(in astronomy) duration of an eclipse; (in Vedic<BR>grammar) the standing of a word by itself (i. e.<BR>without the particle इति, see स्थित).<BR>—स्थिति-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessing firmness or stability, firm,<BR>stable; steady (in purpose or conduct), upright,<BR>firm, virtuous.<BR>—स्थिति-स्थापक, अस्, आ, अम्, fixing<BR>in a (former or original) state or condition, capable<BR>of placing in or restoring to a (previous) form or<BR>position, having elastic properties; (अस्), m. (ac-<BR>cording to some also अम्, n.), the capability of<BR>placing in or recovering a (previous) position or<BR>condition, elasticity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित्वा
स्थित्वा, ind. having stood or stayed or stopped,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर|स्थिरः
स्थिर, अस्, आ, अम्, firm, fixed, steady, steadfast;<BR>unfluctuating, permanent, enduring, durable, settled,<BR>lasting; not moving, immovable, still, placid, calm,<BR>quiescent, cool, composed, collected, free from pas-<BR>sion; steadfast or steady in conduct; constant,<BR>faithful, determined; certain, sure, convinced; firm,<BR>hard, solid, strong; (अस्), m. a deity, immortal;<BR>epithet of Śiva; of Kārttikeya; a mountain; a<BR>tree; a bull; final emancipation from existence;<BR>the planet Saturn; a particular plant (= 1. धव);<BR>N. of a particular astronomical Yoga; of certain<BR>zodiacal signs (viz. Taurus, Leo, Scorpio, Aquarius;<BR>so called because any work done under these signs<BR>is supposed to be lasting); (आ), f. a strong-minded<BR>woman; the earth; the shrub Śāla-parṇī; a medi-<BR>cinal root (= काकोली); the silk-cotton tree; [cf. Gr.<BR>στερεό-ς, στεῤῤό-ς, στέρι-φο-ς, στερίφη, στεῖρα,<BR>στήρ-ιγξ, στηρίζ-ω, στελεόν: Lat. steri-li-s, stīr-<BR>ia, stilla, stolidus, stultus: Goth. stairo: Old<BR>Germ. staren, storren, stornen, ga-starken, starh-<BR>jan, &c.: Angl. Sax. starian, starc: Lith. styr-u,<BR>‘to be stiff or benumbed;’ ster-va, ‘a carcass.’]<BR>—स्थिर-कुट्टक, अस्, m. (in algebra) a steady<BR>pulverizer, constant multiplier, common divisor (ap-<BR>plied to a particular kind of common divisor).<BR>—स्थिर-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, having durable per-<BR>fume, strong-scented; (अस्), m. the Campaka tree,<BR>Michelia Champaca; (आ), f. Pandanus Odoratissimus<BR>(= केतकी); the trumpet-flower (= पाटला).<BR>—स्थि-<BR>र-चक्र, अस्, m. a particular Jina or Bodhi-sattva<BR>(= मञ्जु-श्री).<BR>—स्थिर-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, or स्थिर-<BR>चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, firm-minded, firm, resolute, constant,<BR>steady.<BR>—स्थिर-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘firm-leafed,’ the<BR>birch tree (= भूर्ज-पत्त्र).<BR>—स्थिर-च्छाय, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having deep shade,’ a tree which gives shelter to<BR>travellers; any tree.<BR>—स्थिर-जिह्व, अस्, m. ‘firm-<BR>tongued,’ a fish.<BR>—स्थिर-जीविता, f. ‘firm-lived,’ the<BR>silk-cotton tree.<BR>—स्थिर-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more<BR>firm, fixed, stationary; very firm or permanent,<BR>durable, eternal.<BR>—स्थिर-ता, f. or स्थिर-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. firmness, stability, steadiness, steadfastness; moral<BR>firmness, fortitude; fearlessness.<BR>—स्थिर-दंष्ट्र,<BR>अस्, m. ‘strong-toothed,’ a snake; N. of Viṣṇu in<BR>the boar-Avatāra; = ध्वनि (according to Śabda-k.).<BR>—स्थिर-धन्वन्, आ, आ, अ, having or armed with<BR>a strong bow (said of Rudra, Ṛg-veda VII. 46, 1).<BR>—स्थिर-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, firm-minded, resolute, per-<BR>severing.<BR>—स्थिर-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘firm-leafed,’ the<BR>marshy date tree.<BR>—स्थिर-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘firm-<BR>flowered,’ the Campaka tree; the Vakula tree.<BR>—स्थिर-पुष्पिन्, ई, m. ‘strong-flowered,’ the<BR>Tilaka tree.<BR>—स्थिर-प्रतिज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, persist-<BR>ing in an assertion, pertinacious; faithful to a promise.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">Page1147-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—स्थिर-प्रतिबन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, firm in resist-<BR>ance, pertinacious, obstinate.<BR>—स्थिर-प्रतिष्ठा,<BR>f. a firm resting-place, fixed residence.<BR>—स्थिर-<BR>प्रेमन्, आ, आ, अ, firm or steady in affection, a firm<BR>friend.<BR>—स्थिर-प्स्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having con-<BR>stant food; [cf. विश्व-प्स्न्य.]<BR>—स्थिर-फला, f.<BR>‘having firm fruit,’ a kind of gourd (= कुष्-<BR>माण्डी).<BR>—स्थिर-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, steady-minded,<BR>resolute, calm, dispassionate.<BR>—स्थिर-मति, इस्, f. a<BR>firm mind, fixed resolution; (इस्, इस्, इ), firm-minded,<BR>firm, steady, resolute.<BR>—स्थिर-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>firm-minded, resolute, determined, faithful.<BR>—स्थिर-<BR>योनि, इस्, m. ‘having a firm receptacle,’ a large tree<BR>which gives shade and shelter.<BR>—स्थिर-यौवन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, possessing constant youth, ever youthful;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of good or evil genius, a fairy (=<BR>विद्या-धर).<BR>—स्थिर-रङ्गा, f. ‘having a durable<BR>colour,’ indigo; a sort of Curcuma.<BR>—स्थिर-रागा,<BR>f. a kind of Curcuma (= दारु-हरिद्रा).<BR>—स्थिर-<BR>लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, steady-eyed; (one) whose gaze<BR>is fixed.<BR>—स्थिर-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, having fixed or en-<BR>during prosperity.<BR>—स्थिर-सङ्गर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>faithful to an agreement or promise, true, veracious.<BR>—स्थिर-साधनक, अस्, m. the Sindu-vāra tree.<BR>—स्थिर-सार, अस्, m. ‘having firm sap,’ a kind of<BR>tree (= शाक).<BR>—स्थिर-सौहृद, अस्, आ, अम्, firm<BR>in friendship; (अम्), n. firmness in friendship.<BR>—स्थिर-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, remaining firm or<BR>steady, keeping perfectly still (as in meditation).<BR>—स्थिरांह्रिप (˚र-अं˚), अस्, m. ‘durable tree,’<BR>the marshy date tree.<BR>—स्थिरात्मन् (˚र-आत्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, firm-minded, resolute, unmoved, stable, steady.<BR>—स्थिरानुराग (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, constant in<BR>affection or love.<BR>—स्थिरायुस् (˚र-आय्˚), उस्, उस्, उस्,<BR>long-lived, long-lasting; (उस्), m. the silk-cotton<BR>tree, (also स्थिरायु according to some.)<BR>—स्थिरा-<BR>रम्भ (˚र-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, firm in undertakings,<BR>persevering.<BR>—स्थिरी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to<BR>make firm, confirm, strengthen, corroborate; to<BR>bring to a standstill, stop, make fast.<BR>—स्थिरी-भू,<BR>cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become firm or steady;<BR>to become calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरक
स्थिरक, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिराय
स्थिराय, Nom. P. स्थिरायति, &c., to remain<BR>firm or constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुर
स्थुर in अप-ष्ठ्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुरिन्
स्थुरिन्, ई, m. = स्थूरिन् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुल
1. स्थुल in अप-ष्ठ्˚, वि-संष्ठ्˚, q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूर|स्थूरः
स्थूर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = स्थूल, स्थविर,<BR>strong, firm; wide, extended, (Sāy. = विस्तृत, Ṛg-<BR>veda VI. 29, 2); (अस्), m. a bull (Ved.); a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूरिका
स्थूरिका, f. (probably) a barren cow, (according<BR>to some this is the more correct reading for छूरिका<BR>in Manu VIII. 325.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूरिन्
स्थूरिन्, ई, m. (also written स्थुरिन्, cf. स्थौ-<BR>रिन्), a pack-horse, one carrying loads on his back;<BR>a pack-bullock; (इ), n., Ved. a cart drawn by one<BR>bull or draught animal, (Sāy. = एकेन धुर्येण<BR>युक्तम् अनः, Ṛg-veda X. 131, 3); [cf. Zend<BR>staora, ‘a beast of burden:’ Gr. ταῦρο-ς: Lat.<BR>tauru-s: Umbr. turu: Old Germ. stiuri, ‘strong;’<BR>stur, ‘large:’ Goth. stiur: Angl. Sax. steor, stor:<BR>Engl. steer: Slav. turu, ‘a bull:’ Lith. taura-s,<BR>‘a wild ox.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेमन्
स्थेमन्, आ, m. (according to some), firmness,<BR>stability, fixedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेय|स्थेयः
स्थेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed or fixed, to be<BR>settled or determined; (अस्), m. a person chosen to<BR>settle a dispute between two parties, an arbitrator,<BR>umpire, judge; a domestic priest; (आस्), f. pl., scil.<BR>आपः, standing water (i. e. water standing in a pot<BR>used in certain nuptial ceremonies).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेयस्
स्थेयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of स्थिर), more<BR>fixed or firm, firmer; very firm or stable; eternal,<BR>permanent; very resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेष्ठ|स्थेष्ठः
स्थेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, (superl. of स्थिर), most<BR>fixed, very firm or stable, durable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थैर्य|स्थैर्यं|स्थैर्य्य|स्थैर्य्यं
स्थैर्य, अम्, n. (fr. स्थिर), firmness, stability,<BR>fixedness, steadiness; continuance; firmness of mind,<BR>resolution, constancy, calmness; patience; hardness,<BR>solidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थोरिन्
स्थोरिन्, ई, m. a pack-horse or animal carrying<BR>burdens, (see स्थौरिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौर|स्थौरं
स्थौर, अम्, n. (fr. स्थूर = स्थूल), firmness,<BR>strength, power; a sufficient load for a horse or ass;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic of the Vedic Ṛṣi Agni-<BR>yuta or Agni-yūpa (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 116).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौरिन्
स्थौरिन्, ई, m. (see स्थूरिन्, स्थोरिन्, स्थुरिन्),<BR>a horse carrying burdens on his back, a pack-horse;<BR>a strong horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थागर
स्थागर स्थागर, Ved. probably connected<BR>with स्थगर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणु|स्थाणुः
स्थाणु स्थाणु. See p. 1146, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाण्डिल|स्थांडिल|स्थांडिलः|स्थाण्डिलः
स्थाण्डिल स्थाण्डिल, अस्, m. (fr. स्थण्डिल),<BR>a devotee who sleeps on the bare ground or on<BR>ground prepared for a sacrifice (= स्थण्डिल-शायिन्);<BR>a mendicant, religious beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थान|स्थानं
स्थान स्थान, स्थानिन्, &c. See p. 1146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापन|स्थापनं
स्थापन स्थापन, स्थायिन्, &c. See p. 1146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाल|स्थालं
स्थाल स्थाल, &c. See p. 1146, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावर|स्थावरं|स्थावरः
स्थावर स्थावर, &c. See p. 1147, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासु
स्थासु स्थासु, स्थास्नु, &c. See p. 1147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिक|स्थिकः
स्थिक स्थिक, अस्, m. (according to some<BR>fr. rt. 1. स्था), the buttocks (= कटि-प्रोथ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित|स्थितः
स्थित स्थित, स्थिति, &c. See p. 1147, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर्
स्थिर् स्थिर्, cl. 1. P. स्थिरति, &c., (see<BR>Nirukta IX. 11.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर|स्थिरः
स्थिर स्थिर, &c. See p. 1147, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिवि
स्थिवि स्थिवि, see Ṛg-veda X. 68, 3, (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. स्थिविभ्यः apparently = कुसीदे-<BR>भ्यः, but the MS. is doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुड्
स्थुड् स्थुड् = rt. थुड्, cl. 6. P. स्थुडति,<BR>&c., to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुल
स्थुल 2. स्थुल, अम्, n. (perhaps for स्थुड,<BR>fr. rt. स्थुड्, but cf. 1. स्थुल at p. 1147, col. 3),<BR>a sort of long tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूणा
स्थूणा स्थूणा, f. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 15. fr. rt. 1. स्था), the post or pillar of a house;<BR>any post or pillar; an iron image, statue; an anvil;<BR>a disease (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूम|स्थूमः
स्थूम स्थूम, अस्, m. (according to Śabda-k.)<BR>light; the moon; [cf. स्यूम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूर|स्थूरः
स्थूर स्थूर, स्थूरिन्. See p. 1147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल्
स्थूल् स्थूल् (rather a Nom. derived fr.<BR>स्थूल below), cl. 10. A. स्थूलयते<BR>(also P. स्थूलयति according to some), अतुस्थूलत्,<BR>त, to become big or stout, to become bulky, in-<BR>crease, grow fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल|स्थूलं|स्थूलः
स्थूल, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably a later form of<BR>स्थूर for स्थावर, see p. 1147, col. 3), strong,<BR>powerful; stout, bulky, big, huge; fat, corpulent;<BR>great, large, thick; clumsy, coarse, gross, rough,<BR>(opposed to सूक्ष्म); not exact; doltish, stolid,<BR>thick-headed; stupid, dull, ignorant; (अस्), m. the<BR>jack tree; (आ), f. a sort of pepper (= गज-पिप्पली);<BR>a kind of gourd or cucumber (= एर्वारु); large<BR>cardamoms; (अम्), n. a heap, quantity; = कूट<BR>(according to Śabda-k.); a tent, (probably for<BR>2. स्थुल.)<BR>—स्थूल-कङ्गु, उस्, m. a sort of wild<BR>and coarse kidney-bean (= वरक).<BR>—स्थूल-कणा,<BR>f. the plant Nigella Indica.<BR>—स्थूल-कण्टक, अस्, m.<BR>‘large-thorned,’ a kind of plant, = जाल-वर्वूरक;<BR>(इका), f. the silk-cotton tree.<BR>—स्थूल-कण्टा, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= बृहती).<BR>—स्थूल-कन्द, अस्, m.<BR>‘having a large bulb,’ a kind of esculent root or<BR>plant with such a root (= सूरण; = माणक; =<BR>हस्ति-कन्द); a kind of garlic (= रक्त-लशुन).<BR>—स्थूल-काय, अस्, आ, अम्, large-bodied, corpulent.<BR>—स्थूल-काष्ठ-दह्, -धक्, or स्थूल-काष्-<BR>ठाग्नि (˚ठ-अग्˚), इस्, m. the trunk of a tree or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-b" target="_blank">Page1148-b+ 81</a>]<BR>any thick piece of timber on fire.<BR>—स्थूल-क्षेड<BR>or स्थूल-क्ष्वेड, अस्, m. (see क्ष्वेड), an arrow.<BR>—स्थूल-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, thick-necked.<BR>—स्थू-<BR>लङ्-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, making big or large.<BR>—स्थूल-चञ्चु, उस्, m. a kind of culinary plant<BR>(= महा-चञ्चु).<BR>—स्थूल-चाप, अस्, m. (for तूल-<BR>चाप), a large bow-like instrument used in cleaning<BR>cotton.<BR>—स्थूल-जीरक, अस्, m. the plant Nigella<BR>Indica (called Kaloñjī in Hindī).<BR>—स्थूल-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, more bulky, bigger, stouter, very large,<BR>larger.<BR>—स्थूल-ता, f. or स्थूल-त्व, अम्, n. big-<BR>ness, stoutness, bulkiness, coarseness; dulness, stu-<BR>pidity.<BR>—स्थूल-ताल, अस्, m. the marshy date tree<BR>(= हिन्ताल).<BR>—स्थूल-त्वचा, f. ‘thick-barked,’ a<BR>kind of plant (= काश्मरी).<BR>—स्थूल-दण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. a sort of large reed (= देव-नल).<BR>—स्थूल-<BR>दर्भ, अस्, m. a kind of grass, Saccharum Munja.<BR>—स्थूल-दला, f. the plant Aloe Perfoliata.<BR>—स्थू-<BR>ल-देह, अस्, अम्, m. n. = स्थूल-शरीर below.<BR>—स्थूल-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, dull-witted, stupid, ignorant.<BR>—स्थूल-नाल, अस्, m. a kind of large reed (=<BR>देव-नल).<BR>—स्थूल-नास or स्थूल-नासिक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, large-nosed, thick-nosed; (अस्), m. a hog,<BR>boar.<BR>—स्थूल-पट, अस्, अम्, m. n. coarse cloth;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), having coarse cloth or clothes.<BR>—स्थूल-<BR>पट्ट, अस्, m. cotton; (अम्), n. coarse cloth (accord-<BR>ing to some).<BR>—स्थूल-पट्टाक, अस्, m. coarse cloth.<BR>—स्थूल-पाद, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, large-footed, club-<BR>footed, having swelled legs; (अस्), m. an elephant;<BR>a man with elephantiasis.<BR>—स्थूल-पुष्प, अस्, m.<BR>‘large-flowered,’ the tree Æschynomene Grandiflora;<BR>(आ), f. a sort of mountain Clitorea; (ई), f. a kind<BR>of plant (= यव-तिक्ता).<BR>—स्थूल-फल, अम्, n.<BR>the gross result of a calculation or measurement;<BR>(अस्), m. ‘having large fruit,’ the silk-cotton tree;<BR>(आ), f. the Crotolaria (= शण-पुष्पी).<BR>—स्थूल-<BR>बाहू, ऊस्, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—स्थूल-बुद्धि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, dull-witted, dull, stupid.<BR>—स्थूल-भद्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the six Jaina Śruta-kevalins.<BR>—स्थूल-भूत, आनि, n. pl. the five grosser ele-<BR>ments (according to the Sāṅkhya phil., see साङ्ख्य).<BR>—स्थूल-मरिच, अम्, n. a particular fragrant berry<BR>(= कक्कोल).<BR>—स्थूल-मान, अम्, n. gross or<BR>rough measure, rough computation.<BR>—स्थूल-मूल,<BR>अम्, n. a large root; a kind of radish (= चाणक्य-<BR>मूलक).<BR>—स्थूलम्-भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, or<BR>स्थूलम्-भावुक, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming large or<BR>stout.<BR>—स्थूल-लक्ष or स्थूल-लक्ष्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘having large aims or attributes,’ munificent,<BR>liberal, generous; wise, learned; disposed to recol-<BR>lect both benefits and injuries; taking careless aim.<BR>—स्थूललक्ष्य-त्व, अम्, n. munificence, libe-<BR>rality; aiming carelessly.<BR>—स्थूल-वर्त्म-कृत्, त्,<BR>m. a kind of shrub (= ब्राह्मण-यष्टिका).<BR>—स्थूल-वल्कल, अस्, m. ‘thick-barked,’ the red<BR>Lodhra (or Lodh tree, the bark of which is used in<BR>tanning, &c.).<BR>—स्थूल-वृक्ष-फल, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of plant or tree (= स्निग्ध-पिण्डीतक).<BR>—स्थूल-वैदेही, f. a particular plant (= गज-<BR>पिप्पली).<BR>—स्थूल-शङ्खा, f. a woman having a<BR>large vulva.<BR>—स्थूल-शर, अस्, m. a kind of large<BR>reed.<BR>—स्थूल-शरीर, अम्, n. the grosser or material<BR>and perishable body with which a soul clad in its<BR>subtile body is invested, (opposed to सूक्ष्म-<BR>शरीर and लिङ्ग-शरीर, q. q. v. v.); (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>large-bodied, huge.<BR>—स्थूल-शाटक, अस्, अका or<BR>इका, m. f. or स्थूल-शाटि, इस्, m. thick or coarse<BR>cloth.<BR>—स्थूल-शालि, इस्, m. a kind of large rice.<BR>—स्थूल-शिरस्, अस्, n. a large head or summit;<BR>(आस्, आस्, अस्), large-headed.<BR>—स्थूल-शीर्षक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, large-headed; (इका), f. a small ant having<BR>a large head in proportion to its size.<BR>—स्थूल-षट्-<BR>पद, अस्, m. a large bee; wasp.<BR>—स्थूल-ष्ठीवि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of the father of a grammarian.<BR>—स्थूल-<BR>सूक्ष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, mighty and subtile (as God<BR>who sustains the universe and an atom).<BR>—स्थूल-<BR>स्कन्ध, अस्, m. ‘having a thick stem,’ the Lakuca<BR>tree.<BR>—स्थूल-हस्त, अस्, m. a large hand; the<BR>thick trunk of an elephant; (अम्), n. an elephant's<BR>trunk; (अस्, आ, अम्), having large hands.<BR>—स्थू-<BR>लांशा (˚ल-अं˚), f. a kind of Curcuma (= गन्ध-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">Page1148-c+ 75</a>]<BR>पत्त्रा).<BR>—स्थूलान्त्र (˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n. the larger<BR>intestine near the anus.<BR>—स्थूलाम्र (˚ल-आम्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the large Mango tree (= महाराज-चूत).<BR>—स्थूलास्य (˚ल-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, large-faced,<BR>large-mouthed; (अस्), m. a snake.<BR>—स्थूली-करण,<BR>अम्, n. the act of making large or bulky, enlarging,<BR>fattening.<BR>—स्थूली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made large,<BR>enlarged, fattened.<BR>—स्थूली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>come large or thick, become bulky, fattened.<BR>—स्थू-<BR>लैरण्ड (˚ल-एर्˚), अस्, m. the large castor-oil<BR>plant.<BR>—स्थूलैला (˚ल-एला), f. large cardamoms.<BR>—स्थूलोच्चय (˚ल-उच्˚), अस्, m. ‘rough aggre-<BR>gation,’ a large fragment of rock or crag fallen from<BR>a mountain and forming an irregular mound or<BR>hillock; incompleteness, deficiency, defect; the<BR>middle pace of elephants (neither quick nor slow);<BR>an eruption of pimples on the face; a hollow at the<BR>root of an elephant's tusks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलक|स्थूलकः
स्थूलक, अस्, आ, अम्, large, bulky; (अस्), m. a<BR>sort of grass or reed (Saccharum Cylindricum, com-<BR>monly called Ulu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलिन्
स्थूलिन्, ई, m. a camel; [cf. स्थूरिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौल
स्थौल, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, stout, robust (= स्थूल,<BR>Ṛg-veda VI. 44, 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौललक्ष्य
स्थौललक्ष्य, अम्, n. (fr. स्थूल-लक्ष),<BR>the having great aims, munificence, liberality, (Manu<BR>VII. 211.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौलशीर्ष|स्थौलशीर्षं
स्थौलशीर्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. स्थूल-शीर्ष),<BR>having a large head or summit, large-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौलाष्ठीवि
स्थौलाष्ठीवि, इस्, m. (sometimes written स्थौ-<BR>लष्ठीवि), N. of an ancient grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौल्य|स्थौल्यं
स्थौल्य, अम्, n. stoutness, bigness, largeness,<BR>bulk, size, thickness, coarseness, grossness, denseness,<BR>(opposed to सौक्ष्म्य); doltishness, density of<BR>intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेय|स्थेयः
स्थेय स्थेय, स्थेयस्, स्थेष्ठ. See p. 1147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थैर्य|स्थैर्यं|स्थैर्य्य|स्थैर्य्यं
स्थैर्य स्थैर्य. See p. 1147, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौणेय|स्थौणेयं|स्थौणेयः
स्थौणेय स्थौणेय, अम्, n. (said to be fr.<BR>स्थूणा), a sort of perfume (= ग्रन्थि-पर्ण;<BR>commonly called Gāṇṭhiāla).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौणेयक|स्थौणेयकं|स्थौणेयकः
स्थौणेयक, अम्, n. a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौर|स्थौरं
स्थौर स्थौर, स्थौरिन्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपन|स्नपनं
स्नपन स्नपन, स्नपित. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नव|स्नवः
स्नव स्नव. See under rt. 1. स्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नस्
स्नस् स्नस्, cl. 1. 4. P. स्नसति, स्नस्यति,<BR>सस्नास, &c., (according to some) to<BR>eject, eject from the mouth, reject (निरासे); to<BR>inhabit (निवासे, according to others); to eat (?); [cf.<BR>rt. स्नुस्]: Caus. स्नसयति or स्नासयति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नसा
स्नसा स्नसा, f. a tendon, muscle, = स्नाव;<BR>[cf. perhaps, according to some, Old Germ. snor,<BR>snuor.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ना
स्ना स्ना (probably connected with rt.<BR>1. स्नु), cl. 2. P. (ep. also A.) स्नाति (-ते),<BR>Pot. P. स्नायात् (Manu IV. 82; A. anomalous, स्ना-<BR>यीत, Mahā-bh. Vana-p. 7072), सस्नौ, स्नास्यति,<BR>अस्नासीत्, Prec. स्नायात् or स्नेयात्, स्नातुम् (perhaps<BR>originally ‘to float or swim,’ cf. rt. 1. स्नु, 3. नौ,<BR>p. 518), to bathe, perform ablution; to perform the<BR>ceremony of bathing when leaving the house of a<BR>spiritual preceptor: Caus. स्नापयति or स्नप-<BR>यति (with preps. the form स्नापयति is more<BR>correct), to cause to bathe, wash, cleanse, bathe,<BR>wet; to bathe with tears, weep for (?): Desid. सि-<BR>स्नासति: Intens. सास्नायते, सास्नाति, सास्नेति; [cf.<BR>Gr. νά-ω, νᾶ-μα, να-ρό-ς, νη-ρό-ς, νῆ-αο-ς, νίπτω,<BR>νή-χ-ω for ανή-χ-ω; Lat. nâ-re, nâ-s (= Sans. स्नासि),<BR>na-ta-re, na-su-s; Goth. nadr; Angl. Sax. nœd-<BR>dre, nedre; Old Germ. nacho; Hib. snamhaim,<BR>‘I swim.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपन|स्नपनं
स्नपन, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to bathe; used for<BR>bathing (as water &c.); (अम्), n. causing to bathe,<BR>bathing, ablution; washing, sprinkling, wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपित|स्नपितः
स्नपित, अस्, आ, अम्, bathed, washed, sprinkled,<BR>wetted, moistened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात्
स्नात्, आन्, आती or आन्ती, आत्, bathing, performing<BR>ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात|स्नातः
स्नात, अस्, आ, अम्, bathed, washed, purified by ab-<BR>lution, pure; (अस्), m. one whose spiritual instruc-<BR>tion is finished; an initiated householder.<BR>—स्नाता-<BR>नुलिप्त (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who is both bathed<BR>and anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नातक|स्नातकः
स्नातक, अस्, m. a Brāhman who has performed<BR>the ceremony of ablution (cf. आ-प्लव) required on<BR>his finishing his first Āśrama or period of studentship<BR>as a Brahma-cārin (and on becoming initiated into<BR>the second Āśrama or order of a Gṛha-stha, q. v.);<BR>a Brāhman just returned from the house of his pre-<BR>ceptor and become a married man or initiated house-<BR>holder, (three kinds of Snātakas are enumerated,<BR>1. the Vidyā-snātaka or Brahma-cārin, who, at the<BR>end of his period of studentship, has completed a<BR>course of study of the Vedas only; 2. the Vrata-<BR>snātaka, who has completed the prescribed Vratas or<BR>vowed observances, such as fasting, continence, &c.,<BR>without becoming perfect in the Vedas; 3. the Vidyā-<BR>vrata-snātaka or Ubhaya-snātaka, who has com-<BR>pleted both the Vedas and the Vratas; this last is of<BR>course regarded as the highest kind, see Kullūka on<BR>Manu III. 2); a Brāhman who is a Bhikṣu or<BR>asker of alms for any religious object or legitimate<BR>purpose, (nine kinds are enumerated in Manu XI. 1);<BR>any man of the first three classes who is an initiated<BR>householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नातृ
स्नातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who bathes or washes, a<BR>bather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात्व
स्नात्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fit for ablutions, capable<BR>of being used for bathing, (Sāy. स्नात्वाः = स्नानार्-<BR>हाः, Ṛg-veda X. 71, 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात्वा
स्नात्वा (Ved. also स्नात्वी), ind. having bathed or<BR>washed, having performed ablutions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नान|स्नानं
स्नान, अम्, n. bathing, washing, ablution, dipping<BR>in water, wetting, purification by bathing, religious<BR>or ceremonial ablution, bathing in sacred waters<BR>(considered as a daily observance or as an essential<BR>part of some ceremonial); the ceremony of bathing<BR>or anointing an idol; anything used in ablution (e. g.<BR>water, perfumed powder for the body, &c.).<BR>—स्ना-<BR>न-तृण, अम्, n. ‘bathing-grass,’ Kuśa grass.<BR>—स्ना-<BR>न-दीपिका, f., N. of a commentary by Gopī-nātha<BR>on the Snāna-sūtra.<BR>—स्नान-द्रोणी, f. a bathing-tub.<BR>—स्नान-यात्रा, f. ‘bathing procession,’ the festival<BR>held on the day of full moon in the month Jyeṣṭha<BR>(when images of Kṛṣṇa as Jagan-nātha are carried<BR>out and bathed; in Orissa this festival is called<BR>Ratha-yātrā).<BR>—स्नानयात्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, attend-<BR>ing the above procession at the bathing of Jagan-<BR>nātha.<BR>—स्नान-वस्त्र, अम्, n. a cloth put on for<BR>bathing, a bathing-dress, wet cloth.<BR>—स्नान-विधि, इस्,<BR>m. the rules of ablution, proper manner of bathing;<BR>N. of a Pariśiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—स्नान-शील,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fond of bathing, observing or performing<BR>ablution (especially in sacred waters).<BR>—स्नान-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Sūtra work (ascribed to Kātyāyana).<BR>—स्नानसूत्र-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a summary<BR>of a commentary by Hari-jīvana-miśra on the Snāna-<BR>sūtra.<BR>—स्नानागार (˚न-आग्˚), अम्, n. a bath-room.<BR>—स्नानोत्तीर्ण (˚न-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, rising up from<BR>a bath, one who has just completed his ablutions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानीय|स्नानीयं
स्नानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for bathing or ablution,<BR>suitable for bathing; (अम्), n. water or any article<BR>(such as unguents, perfumed powders, &c.) proper<BR>for bathing.<BR>—स्नानीय-वस्त्र, अम्, n. a cloth tied<BR>round the waist for bathing, a bathing dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापक|स्नापकः
स्नापक, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus.), a servant who<BR>bathes his master or attends him while bathing<BR>(bringing water and pouring it over his person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापन|स्नापनं
स्नापन, अम्, n. the act of causing to bathe or<BR>attending a person while bathing, (Manu II. 209.)<BR>—स्नापनोच्छिष्ट-भोजन (˚न-उच्˚), ए, n. du.<BR>the act of bathing another person and eating his<BR>leavings, (Manu II. 209.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापित
स्नापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to bathe, attended on<BR>while bathing, immersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायिन्
स्नायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bathing; (ई), m. a bather, per-<BR>former of ablutions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नास्यत्|स्नास्यन्त्
स्नास्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to bathe or<BR>perform an initiatory ceremonial ablution; (अन्), m.<BR>a religious student about to become a Snātaka, (Manu<BR>II. 245.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायु|स्नायुः
स्नायु स्नायु, उस्, f. (according to some उस्,<BR>m.; said in Uṇādi-s. I. 1. to be fr. rt. स्ना), a sinew,<BR>tendon, muscle (described as वायु-वाहिनी-नाडी, ‘a<BR>tubular vessel conveying vital air’); the string of a<BR>bow; [cf. probably Gr. νεῦρο-ν, νευρ-ά; Lat. ner-<BR>vu-s, nerviœ, nervosus; Old Germ. snar-a, snar-<BR>ahha, snuor, narwa; Old Sax. naru; Lith. nar-<BR>a-s, ner-u.]<BR>—स्नायु-बन्धन, अम्, n. a sinew-<BR>string.<BR>—स्नायु-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of tendons.<BR>—स्नायु-युत, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of tendons,<BR>(Manu VI. 76.)<BR>—स्नायु-रज्जु, उस्, उस्, उ, having<BR>tendons for cords (said of the body).<BR>—स्नाय्व्-अर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. a kind of disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायुक|स्नायुकः
स्नायुक = स्नायु above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नाव|स्नावः
स्नाव, अस्, m. (the form स्नावानि, neut. pl., occurs),<BR>a tendon, muscle; (according to some) the vascular<BR>membrane investing the bones; [cf. probably Old<BR>Germ. senwa; Angl. Sax. sinu, sinw, senw.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नावन्
स्नावन्, आ, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 112. fr.<BR>rt. स्ना), a muscle, sinew (Ved.); = रसिक, a<BR>lover (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्ध|स्निग्धं|स्निग्धः
स्निग्ध स्निग्ध. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निट्
स्निट् स्निट्, cl. 10. P. स्नेटयति, to go; to<BR>love, be in love; [cf. rt. 1. स्निह् below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निह्
स्निह् 1. स्निह्, cl. 4. P. स्निह्यति, सिष्णेह,<BR>स्नेहिष्यति or स्नेक्ष्यति, अस्निहत्,<BR>स्नेहितुम् or स्नेग्धुम् or स्नेढुम्, (probably<BR>originally) to be adhesive or sticky or viscid; to be<BR>bland; to be easily attached; to have affection for,<BR>love, regard; to be fond of (with gen.); to be kind<BR>to or pleased with; cl. 10. P. स्नेहयति, &c., to be<BR>unctuous or greasy: Pass. स्निह्यते, Aor. अस्नेहि:<BR>Caus. स्नेहयति, &c., Aor. असिष्णिहत्, to make<BR>unctuous, anoint, lubricate; to cause to love, &c.; to<BR>dissolve, destroy, kill, slay, (in Naigh. II. 19. स्नेह-<BR>यति and [according to some readings] स्नेहति are<BR>enumerated amongst the वध-कर्माणः): Desid.<BR>सिस्नेहिषति, सिस्निहिषति, सिस्निक्षति: Intens.<BR>सेष्णिह्यते, सेष्णेग्धि or सेष्णेढि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्ध|स्निग्धं|स्निग्धः
स्निग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, oily, oleaginous, unctuous,<BR>greasy, fat, sticky, viscid, cohesive, adhesive; emol-<BR>lient, smooth; glossy, shining, resplendent; moist,<BR>wet; cooling; bland, kind, amiable; attached, lov-<BR>ing, tender, affectionate, friendly, well affected; lovely,<BR>agreeable; coarse, thick, dense; (अस्), m. a friend;<BR>a sort of pine, (see स्निग्ध-दारु below); the red<BR>castor-oil plant; scil. गण्डूष, a particular mode<BR>of rinsing the mouth; (आ), f. marrow, = मेदा;<BR>(अम्), n. oil; bees'-wax; light, lustre; thickness,<BR>coarseness.<BR>—स्निग्ध-जन, अस्, m. an affectionate<BR>or friendly person, a friend.<BR>—स्निग्ध-तण्डुल, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of rice of quick growth (= षष्टिक).<BR>—स्निग्ध-ता, f. or स्निग्ध-त्व, अम्, n. unctuous-<BR>ness, oiliness; blandness; tenderness, kindness, affec-<BR>tion, love.<BR>—स्निग्ध-दारु, उ, n. a sort of pine,<BR>Pinus Longifolia (= सरल); another kind, Pinus<BR>Devadaru.<BR>—स्निग्ध-पत्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>smooth or glossy leaves; (अस्, आ), m. f. the jujube,<BR>Zizyphus Jujuba; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= काश्-<BR>मरी); another kind (= पालक्या).<BR>—स्निग्ध-<BR>पत्त्रक, अस्, m. ‘having smooth leaves,’ a kind of<BR>grass; other plants (= घृत-करञ्ज; = गुच्छ-<BR>करञ्ज).<BR>—स्निग्ध-पिण्डीतक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>Madana tree.<BR>—स्निग्ध-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>unctuous fruit, having glossy fruit; (आ), f. the ich-<BR>neumon plant (= नाकुली).<BR>—स्निग्ध-वर्ण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a glossy or bright colour; having a<BR>soft or agreeable complexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्ध्वा
स्निग्ध्वा or स्निहित्वा, ind. becoming unctuous,<BR>becoming bland or affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निह्
2. स्निह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, or क्, क्, क्, loving, affectionate; one<BR>who loves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नीढ
स्नीढ, अस्, आ, अम्, attached, bland, tender, loving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नीढ्वा
स्नीढ्वा, ind. = स्निग्ध्वा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नीहिति
स्नीहिति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. killing, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नीहिती
स्नीहिती, f., Ved. killing, slaying; malevolent, (Sāy.<BR>= वध-कारिणी, Ṛg-veda I. 74, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेह|स्नेहः
स्नेह, अस्, m. oiliness, unctuousness, fattiness,<BR>greasiness, lubricity, viscidity (as one of the twenty-<BR>four Guṇas of the Vaiśeṣika branch of the Nyāya<BR>phil.); moisture; blandness, tenderness, love, affec-<BR>tion, kindness; filial love or affection; any unctuous<BR>or oleaginous substance, oil, grease, fat, an unguent;<BR>a fluid of the body; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a caste (cor-<BR>responding to the Vaiśyas).<BR>—स्नेह-गुणित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, endowed with love or affection.<BR>—स्नेह-च्छेद,<BR>अस्, m. interruption of friendship, cessation or loss of<BR>regard.<BR>—स्नेह-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, cooked or<BR>dressed with oil.<BR>—स्नेह-पात्र, अम्, n. a worthy<BR>object of affection.<BR>—स्नेह-पूर्वम्, ind. preceded<BR>by affection, affectionately, tenderly, fondly.<BR>—स्नेह-<BR>प्रवृत्ति, इस्, f. ‘course of friendship,’ affection,<BR>love.<BR>—स्नेह-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of oil; (अस्),<BR>m. a lamp.<BR>—स्नेह-भाण्ड, अम्, n. an oil-vessel,<BR>pot of oil.<BR>—स्नेहभाण्ड-जीविन्, ई, m. living by<BR>oil-vessels, an oilman.<BR>—स्नेह-भू, ऊस्, m. phlegm,<BR>rheum, the phlegmatic humor.<BR>—स्नेह-भूमि, इस्,<BR>f. ‘oil-ground, oil-source,’ any substance yielding oil<BR>or grease; any object of affection, one worthy of<BR>love.<BR>—स्नेह-रङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘oil-coloured,’ se-<BR>samum.<BR>—स्नेह-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, unctuous, oily;<BR>possessed of affection, affectionate; (अती), f. = मेदा<BR>(according to Śabda-k.).<BR>—स्नेह-वस्ति, इस्, f. a<BR>clyster or injection of oil, oily enema.<BR>—स्नेह-विद्-<BR>ध, अस्, m. ‘pierced or impregnated with oil,’ a<BR>sort of pine, Pinus Devadaru (according to Śabda-k.<BR>अम्, n.).<BR>—स्नेह-विमर्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed or<BR>anointed with oil.<BR>—स्नेह-वीज, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>oily seeds, causing unctuousness, &c.; (अस्), m. the<BR>Piyāla tree.<BR>—स्नेह-व्यक्ति, इस्, f. manifestation or<BR>display of friendship.<BR>—स्नेह-संयुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>mixed with oil, dressed with ghee, (Manu V. 24.)<BR>—स्नेह-सम्भाष, अस्, m. kind conversation.<BR>—स्नेहाक्त (˚ह-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, anointed with<BR>oil, oiled, greased, lubricated.<BR>—स्नेहानुवृत्ति (˚ह-<BR>अन्˚), इस्, f. continuance of affection, affectionate or<BR>friendly intercourse.<BR>—स्नेहाश (˚ह-आश), अस्, m.<BR>‘oil-consumer,’ a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन्
स्नेहन्, आ, m. a friend; the moon; a kind of<BR>disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन|स्नेहनं
स्नेहन, अस्, ई, अम्, anointing, lubricating; de-<BR>stroying; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva; (अम्), n. the act<BR>of anointing, unction, lubrication, rubbing or smear-<BR>ing with oil or unguents; unctuousness, being or<BR>becoming oily, &c.; an emollient, unguent, lini-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहनीय
स्नेहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be anointed or lubri-<BR>cated; to be loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहयत्
स्नेहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. destroying, killing,<BR>murdering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहित|स्नेहितः
स्नेहित, अस्, आ, अम्, anointed, smeared with oil;<BR>loved, beloved; kind, affectionate; (अस्), m. a loved<BR>one, friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहितव्य
स्नेहितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = स्नेहनीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहिती
स्नेहिती, f., Ved. destroying, killing; [cf. स्नीहिती<BR>above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहित्वा
स्नेहित्वा, ind. = स्निग्ध्वा, स्निहित्वा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहिन्
स्नेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, oily, unctuous, fat; attached, af-<BR>fectionate, friendly; (ई), m. an anointer, smearer;<BR>a painter; a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहु|स्नेहुः
स्नेहु, उस्, m. the moon; a kind of disease; [cf.<BR>स्नेहन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नैग्ध्य|स्नैग्ध्यं
स्नैग्ध्य, अम्, n. (fr. स्निग्ध), unctuousness,<BR>oiliness, smoothness, lubricity, blandness; tenderness,<BR>fondness; affectionateness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु 1. स्नु (probably connected with rt.<BR>स्ना), cl. 2. P. स्नौति, सुष्णाव, स्नविष्-<BR>यति, अस्नावीत्, स्नवितुम्, to drip, trickle, distil, fall<BR>in drops, drop, ooze, run out, leak; to flow, stream;<BR>cl. 2. A. (Pass. reflex.) स्नुते, अस्नोष्ट or अस्ना-<BR>विष्ट: Pass. स्नूयते, स्नोता or स्नाविता, स्नोष्-<BR>यते or स्नाविष्यते, Aor. अस्नावि, to be distilled,<BR>&c.: Caus. स्नावयति, &c., Aor. असुष्णवत्:<BR>Desid. of Caus. सिस्नावयिषति or सुस्नावयिषति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">Page1150-a+ 73</a>]<BR>(according to Vopa-deva): Desid. सुस्नूषति: In-<BR>tens. सोष्णूयते, सोष्णवीति, सोष्णोति; [cf. Gr.<BR>νέ-ω (for σνεϝ-ω), νεύ-σω (for σνεύ-σω), νεῦ-σι-ς,<BR>νευ-σ-τήρ, νά-ω (for σναϝ-ω), ἀένα-ο-ς, νᾶ-μα,<BR>νᾱ-ρό-ς, νη-ρό-ς, Νη-ρ-εύ-ς, Νη-ιά-(δ)-ς; (probably also<BR>ναῦ-ς, ναύ-τη-ς, &c., see under 3. नौ, p. 518):<BR>Goth. snu, ‘to go;’ sniva, snau, snivum (for snu-<BR>um), snaivs, ‘snow:’ Old Germ. sniutan, sniumi,<BR>sneo, snê: Angl. Sax. sniwan, snytan, sneome:<BR>Lith. snega-s (w being changed to g): Slav. snêg:<BR>Hib. snuadhaim, ‘I flow;’ snuadh, ‘blood;’<BR>sneachd, ‘snow.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नव|स्नवः
स्नव, अस्, m. oozing, drizzling, dripping, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नवन
स्नवन, अम्, n. the act of oozing, trickling;<BR>distillation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुत|स्नुतः
स्नुत, अस्, आ, अम्, trickled, distilled, dropped,<BR>trickling, flowing, dropping, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुति
स्नुति, इस्, f. trickling, distilling, oozing, stream,<BR>flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुत्वा
स्नुत्वा, ind. having trickled or oozed or flowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु 2. स्नु, उस्, उ, m. n. (a defective word<BR>optionally substituted for सानु, q. v., in certain cases;<BR>according to some fr. rt. 1. सो), the level summit or<BR>edge of a mountain, table-land; any top, surface;<BR>anything fixed or stationary (as the firmament; Sāy.<BR>= स्थित, Ṛg-veda IV. 28, 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु 3. स्नु, उस्, f. = स्नायु, a sinew, tendon,<BR>muscle.<BR>—स्नु-तस्, ind. from the sinews or muscles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु 4. स्नु, a Kṛd-anta affix to roots form-<BR>ing adjectives expressive of an aptitude to be what is<BR>implied by the root; [cf. स्थास्नु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुच्
स्नुच् स्नुच्, cl. 1. A. स्नोचते, &c., to be<BR>bright or clear (probably for rt. स्तुच्, but<BR>according to Śabda-k., under ष्णुच्, the meaning is<BR>सेचने).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुषा
स्नुषा स्नुषा, f. (said to be fr. rt. 1. स्नु),<BR>a daughter-in-law; the milk-hedge plant (= 2. स्नुह्);<BR>[cf. Gr. νυό-ς; Lat. nuru-s (for snusu-s); Old<BR>Germ. snur; Angl. Sax. snoru; Slav. snochâ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुस्
स्नुस् स्नुस्, cl. 4. P. स्नुस्यति, सुस्नोष,<BR>स्नोसितुम्, to eat; to disappear or become<BR>invisible; to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
स्नुह् 1. स्नुह्, cl. 4. P. स्नुह्यति, सुष्णोह,<BR>स्नोहितुम् or स्नोग्धुम् or स्नोढुम्, to<BR>vomit; = rt. 1. स्निह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
2. स्नुह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, or क्, क्, क्, vomiting, one who<BR>vomits; (क्), f. the milk-hedge plant, Euphorbia<BR>Antiquorum (its milky juice has various medicinal pro-<BR>perties, and is used as an emetic; seventeen synonyms<BR>of this plant are enumerated, cf. सीहुण्ड).<BR>—स्नुक्-<BR>छद, अस्, m. a kind of reed (= क्षीर-कञ्चुकिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहा
स्नुहा, f. the milk-hedge plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहि|स्नुहिः
स्नुहि, इस्, or स्नुही, f. = 2. स्नुह् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेह|स्नेहः
स्नेह स्नेह, स्नेहिन्. See p. 1149, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नै
स्नै स्नै (also written स्तै, q. v.), cl. 1. P.<BR>स्नायति, &c., to dress, wrap round, envelope,<BR>adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नैग्ध्य|स्नैग्ध्यं
स्नैग्ध्य स्नैग्ध्य. See p. 1149, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्द्|स्पंद्
स्पन्द् स्पन्द् (sometimes incorrectly con-<BR>founded with rt. स्यन्द्), cl. 1. A. स्पन्-<BR>दते, पस्पन्दे, अस्पन्दिष्ट, स्पन्दितुम्, to<BR>quiver, throb, tremble, quake, shake, palpitate, beat,<BR>to go, move (= rt. स्यन्द्): Pass. स्पद्यते (accord-<BR>ing to some), Aor. अस्पन्दि: Caus. स्पन्दयति,<BR>Aor. अपस्पन्दत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्द|स्पंद|स्पंदः|स्पन्दः
स्पन्द, अस्, m. throbbing, throb, pulse, tremor,<BR>vibration, motion; [cf. वि-ष्पन्द.]<BR>—स्पन्द-<BR>कारिका, f., N. of a metrical version of the Spanda-<BR>sūtra.<BR>—स्पन्द-शास्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—स्पन्द-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of the aphorisms of<BR>the Śaiva philosophy (= शिव-सूत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दन|स्पंदन|स्पंदनं|स्पन्दनं
स्पन्दन, अम्, n. throbbing, pulsation, palpita-<BR>tion, quivering, (throbbings and quiverings of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">Page1150-b+ 74</a>]<BR>limbs and different parts of the body are supposed by<BR>the Hindūs to indicate good or bad luck; they are<BR>therefore minutely described in certain works);<BR>tremor, vibration, agitation; the quickening of a<BR>child in the womb; rapid motion, going; (according<BR>to some) a car, chariot (Sāy. explains स्पन्दने by<BR>रथस्य गमने सति, Ṛg-veda III. 53, 19); (अस्),<BR>m. a sort of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दमान
स्पन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, throbbing, quivering,<BR>palpitating, beating; going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दित|स्पंदित
स्पन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, throbbed, quivered, agitated,<BR>throbbing, beating; gone; (अम्), n. a pulsation,<BR>throb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दिन्
स्पन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, quivering, throbbing, palpitat-<BR>ing, beating, tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्परितृ
स्परितृ स्परितृ. See स्पर्ष्टृ, p. 1151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्परिश|स्परिशः
स्परिश स्परिश. See p. 1151, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ध्
स्पर्ध् स्पर्ध् (connected with rt. स्पृह्,<BR>q. v.; the older form seems to have been<BR>स्पृध्, q. v.), cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.) स्पर्धते<BR>(-ति), पस्पर्धे, स्पर्धिष्यते, अस्पर्धिष्ट,<BR>स्पर्धितुम्, to contend or compete with, contest,<BR>vie with, emulate, rival, be equal with; to envy; to<BR>challenge, defy, bid defiance to: Pass. स्पर्धते,<BR>Aor. अस्पर्धि: Caus. स्पर्धयति, Aor. अप-<BR>स्पर्धत्, &c.: Desid. पिस्पर्धिषते: Intens. पा-<BR>स्पर्ध्यते, पास्पर्द्धि; [cf. Goth. spauards;<BR>Old Germ. spurt; Angl. Sax. spyrd.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ध
स्पर्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, emulous, envious; (आ), f.<BR>emulation, rivalry, competition, the successive eleva-<BR>tion of rivals; envy, jealousy; defiance; equality<BR>with.<BR>—स्पर्ध-ता, f. rivalry, emulation, envious-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धन|स्पर्धनं
स्पर्धन, अम्, n. competition, emulation; envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धमान
स्पर्धमान, अस्, आ, अम्, vying, emulating, com-<BR>peting, contending with, envying, challenging, de-<BR>fying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धित
स्पर्धित, अस्, आ, अम्, contended with, emulated,<BR>envied; defied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धित्वा
स्पर्धित्वा, ind. having contended or competed<BR>or vied with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धिन्
स्पर्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, rivalling, emulating, compet-<BR>ing; emulous, envious; proud, superb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धिष्यमाण
स्पर्धिष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, about to contend<BR>or compete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पूर्धस्
स्पूर्धस् (probably to be connected with rt.<BR>स्पर्ध्), Ved. envy, (Sāy. स्पूर्धसे = स्पर्ध-<BR>नाय, Ṛg-veda V. 64, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श्
स्पर्श् स्पर्श् (also written स्पश्, see rt. 5.<BR>स्पश्; cf. rt. 1. स्पृश्), cl. 10. A. स्पर्-<BR>शयते, अपस्पर्शत, &c., to take, take hold of,<BR>touch (= rt. 1. स्पृश्); to unite, join, embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श|स्पर्शः
स्पर्श स्पर्श, स्पर्शन, &c. See p. 1151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्
स्पर्ष् स्पर्ष् (= rt. पर्ष्, q. v.), cl. 1. A.<BR>स्पर्षते, &c., to become wet or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
स्पश् 1. स्पश् (= rt. 1. पश्, q. v.), cl. 1.<BR>P. A. स्पशति, -ते, पस्पाश, पस्पशे,<BR>स्पशिष्यति, -ते, अस्पाशीत्, अस्पशिष्ट, स्पशितुम्,<BR>to see, behold, perceive clearly, spy out, espy: Caus.<BR>स्पाशयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अपस्पशत्, to destroy;<BR>Desid. पिस्पशिषति, -ते: Intens. पास्पश्यते, पा-<BR>स्पष्टि; [cf. Zend śpaś; Gr. σκέπ-τ-ο-μαι, σκοπ-ή,<BR>σκοπιά, σκοπ-ό-ς, ἐπι-σκοπος, σκώψ; Lat. spec-i-o,<BR>con-spic-i-o, specula, speculum, spec-to; Old<BR>Germ. speh-o-m, spāh-i, ‘circumspect, prudent.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
2. स्पश्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. seeing, spying out, perceiving;<BR>(ट्), m. one who espies, a spy, messenger, (in the Ṛg-<BR>veda especially applied to the messengers (of Varuṇa);<BR>a guardian, protector, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 59, 1. स्पल् or स्पट् = स्प्रष्टा = होता, a priest;<BR>in Ṛg-veda VIII. 61, 15. स्पट् = सर्वस्य ज्ञाता,<BR>‘omniscient,’ applied to Indra); a ray or rein, (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI. 67, 5. स्पशः =<BR>रश्मयः or चराः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश|स्पशः
स्पश, अस्, m. a spy [cf. Old Germ. spëhon, ‘to<BR>look;’ spëhu, ‘a spy’]; any secret messenger or<BR>emissary; a fight, war, battle; a kind of gladiator<BR>who fights with a savage animal for a reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्ट|स्पष्टं
स्पष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, clearly perceived or discerned,<BR>distinctly visible, distinct, clear, evident, manifest,<BR>plain, apparent, intelligible; true, real; one who sees<BR>clearly; (अम्), ind. clearly, distinctly; openly, boldly,<BR>(न स्पष्टम् उद्वीक्षते, he does not look [at<BR>me] straight in the face.)<BR>—स्पष्ट-गर्भा, f. a<BR>woman evidently pregnant.<BR>—स्पष्ट-तारक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, (the sky) which has its stars distinctly seen<BR>or clearly displayed.<BR>—स्पष्ट-प्रतिपत्ति, इस्, f.<BR>clear perception or ascertainment.<BR>—स्पष्ट-भा-<BR>षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or स्पष्ट-वक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, speak-<BR>ing clearly or distinctly, plain-spoken.<BR>—स्पष्टार्-<BR>थ (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, clear in meaning, obvious,<BR>perspicuous, intelligible.<BR>—स्पष्टी-करण, अम्, n.<BR>the act of making distinct or clear, elucidation.<BR>—स्पष्टी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make dis-<BR>tinct or clear.<BR>—स्पष्टी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>plain or clear, explained, expounded, elucidated, made<BR>manifest, revealed, exposed.<BR>—स्पष्टी-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, become plain or evident.<BR>—स्पष्टेतर (˚ट-<BR>इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, the reverse of clear, indistinct, un-<BR>intelligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टय
स्पष्टय, Nom. P. स्पष्टयति, &c., to make<BR>clear, elucidate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
स्पश् 3. स्पश्, = rt. 3. पश्, ‘to bind,’<BR>q. v. This rt. is said to have the follow-<BR>ing additional meanings — to obstruct, oppose, hinder;<BR>to string together; to touch, undertake, perform,<BR>(Sāy. पस्पशे = स्पृष्टवान् = अनुतिष्ठति, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 22, 19; अस्पष्ट = उपक्रान्तवान्, I. 10,<BR>2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
4. स्पश्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पाशित
स्पाशित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be stopped, hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
स्पश् 5. स्पश् (= rt. स्पर्श्), cl. 10. A.<BR>स्पाशयते, &c., to take, &c. See rt.<BR>स्पर्श्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्ट|स्पष्टं
स्पष्ट स्पष्ट. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पार्ह
स्पार्ह स्पार्ह. See rt. स्पृह्, p. 1151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पूर्धस्
स्पूर्धस् स्पूर्धस्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृ
स्पृ स्पृ (= rts. 3. स्तृ, 1. स्मृ), cl. 5. P.<BR>स्पृणोति, पस्पार, स्पर्तुम्, &c., Ved. to<BR>gratify, grant, confer; to extricate from, deliver from,<BR>preserve from, defend, (स्पर्तम् in निष्पर्तम् =<BR>न्यपारयतम्, ‘you rescued or extricated,’ Ṛg-<BR>veda VII. 71, 5); to live; to fill or bestow abun-<BR>dantly, (Sāy. स्पृणवाम = पूरयाम, Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 44, 10); to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्तृ
स्पर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, delivering or protecting from,<BR>a deliverer; [cf. अव-स्प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृत्
स्पृत्, त्, त्, त्, gratifying with, conferring; delivering<BR>from, (in किल्विष-स्˚, delivering from guilt; लोक-स्˚,<BR>[probably] conferring worlds; cf. धन-स्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृक्का
स्पृक्का स्पृक्का, f. the plant Trigonella Cor-<BR>niculata (= पृक्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृध्
स्पृध् 1. स्पृध्, a Vedic form of rt. स्पर्ध्,<BR>col. 2 (e. g. अस्पृध्रन्, they strove toge-<BR>ther, Ṛg-veda VII. 56, 3; पस्पृध्रे = पस्पृ-<BR>धिरे; पस्पृधाते = मिथः स्पर्धेते, Ṛg-veda<BR>VII. 104, 12).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्पृधान
पस्पृधान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. contending with,<BR>rivaling, a rival, opponent, enemy (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृध्
2. स्पृध्, त्, त्, त्, one who contends or fights; (त्),<BR>f. battle, fight (in Naigh. II. 17. स्पृधः is enume-<BR>rated among the सङ्ग्राम-नामानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृधान
स्पृधान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. contending, vying,<BR>rivaling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृध्य
स्पृध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. vying, emulous, &c.<BR>(in मिथ-स्˚, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
स्पृश् 1. स्पृश् (cf. rt. स्पर्श्), cl. 6. P. (ep.<BR>also A.) स्पृशति (-ते), पस्पर्श (3rd<BR>pl. पस्पृशुः; ep. 3rd sing. A. पस्पृशे, 3rd pl.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">Page1151-a+ 81</a>]<BR>पस्पृशिरे), स्प्रक्ष्यति or स्पर्क्ष्यति, अस्प्रा-<BR>क्षीत् or अस्पार्क्षीत् or अस्पृक्षत्, Prec. स्पृश्यात्,<BR>स्प्रष्टुम् or स्पर्ष्टुम्, to touch, graze; to<BR>handle, take hold of, (अन्योन्यं हस्तौ स्पृश-<BR>तः, they mutually touch hands, i. e. they shake<BR>hands with each other); to cleave to, cling to, come<BR>in contact with; to act upon, affect; to take, re-<BR>ceive, accept (a sacrificial offering &c.); to reach,<BR>attain, obtain, undergo; to wash, sprinkle (e. g.<BR>अद्भिस्, with water, Manu II. 60): Pass. स्पृश्यते,<BR>Aor. अस्पर्शि, to be touched; to be seized or affected<BR>by: Caus. स्पर्शयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अपस्पर्-<BR>शत् or अपस्पृशत् (according to some अपिस्पृशत्),<BR>to cause to touch, make to touch (with two acc.); to<BR>offer, present, give: Desid. पिस्पृक्षति: Intens.<BR>परीस्पृश्यते, परीस्प्रष्टि, परीस्पर्ष्टि, &c.;<BR>[cf. Lat. spargo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्परिश|स्परिशः
स्परिश, अस्, m. touch (= स्पर्श below; Śab-<BR>da-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श|स्पर्शः
स्पर्श, अस्, m. touching, touch, perception by<BR>touch, handling, contact; sexual union; collision, con-<BR>flict, encounter (= सम्-पराय); the quality of tangi-<BR>bility (which is the Viṣaya for the skin; see साङ्-<BR>ख्य); feeling, sensation; anything which touches<BR>or comes in contact, (eleven such Sparśas are enume-<BR>rated, viz. 1. उष्ण, hot; 2. शीत, cold; 3. सुख,<BR>pleasant; 4. दुःख, painful; 5. स्निग्ध, greasy;<BR>6. विशद, clean; 7. खर, hard; 8. मृदु, soft;<BR>9. श्लक्ष्ण, smooth; 10. लघु, light; 11. गुरु,<BR>heavy); who or what affects or acts upon or in-<BR>fluences; affection, morbid affection or influence, any-<BR>thing the contact or influence of which causes pain<BR>or disease, disorder, sickness, fever; air, wind; a<BR>consonant of any of the five classes of Gutturals,<BR>Palatals, Cerebrals, Dentals, and Labials (so called be-<BR>cause the first four are pronounced by the contact of<BR>the tongue with the four places of utterance [see<BR>स्थान, स्पृष्ट], throat, palate, top of palate, and<BR>teeth; the fifth class or labials being formed by contact<BR>of the lips); contact (in astron.); presentation, gift,<BR>donation, offering, (काक-स्पर्श, a particular cere-<BR>mony on the tenth day after a death, putting out a lump<BR>of rice as an offering for the crows); a spy (probably<BR>for स्पश, q. v.); (आ), f. a wanton or unchaste wo-<BR>man.<BR>—स्पर्श-तन्मात्र, अम्, n. the subtile ele-<BR>ment of tangibility, (see साङ्ख्य.)<BR>—स्पर्श-ता,<BR>f. a state of contact, touching.<BR>—स्पर्श-मणि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘touch-stone,’ a kind of stone (supposed to<BR>turn everything it touches to gold), the philo-<BR>sopher's stone.<BR>—स्पर्शमणि-प्रभव, अम्, n.<BR>‘touchstone-production,’ gold.<BR>—स्पर्श-लज्जा, f.<BR>‘shrinking from touch,’ the sensitive plant, Mimosa<BR>Pudica.<BR>—स्पर्श-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having tangi-<BR>bility, palpable; agreeable to the touch, smooth,<BR>soft.<BR>—स्पर्श-वर्ग, अस्, m. a class of consonants,<BR>(see under स्पर्श).<BR>—स्पर्श-वेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to<BR>be known or apprehended by the sense of touch.<BR>—स्पर्श-शुद्धा, f. ‘pure to the touch,’ the plant<BR>Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>—स्पर्श-सुख, अम्, n. the<BR>pleasure of touch.<BR>—स्पर्श-स्नान, अम्, n. ablution<BR>at the ingress of the sun or moon into an eclipse.<BR>—स्पर्श-स्यन्द, अस्, m. a frog (also written<BR>स्पर्श-स्पन्द).<BR>—स्पर्शानन्दा (˚श-आन्˚), f.<BR>‘touch-delighting,’ N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—स्पर्शोदय<BR>(˚श-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a consonant succeed-<BR>ing, followed by a consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शक|स्पर्शकः
स्पर्शक, अस्, आ, अम्, touching, who or what<BR>touches or comes in contact with, a toucher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शन|स्पर्शनं|स्पर्शनः
स्पर्शन, अस्, ई, अम्, touching, handling; affect-<BR>ing, acting upon; (अस्), m. air, wind; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of touching, touch, contact; sensation, sense of<BR>touch, organ of sensation or feeling, sensitive nerve;<BR>gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शनक|स्पर्शनकं
स्पर्शनक, अम्, n. ‘that which touches,’ a term<BR>for the skin (in the Sāṅkhya phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शनीय
स्पर्शनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be touched, percepti-<BR>ble by touch, tangible, sensible, palpable, to be felt,<BR>to be handled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शिन्
स्पर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, touching, handling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्टव्य
स्पर्ष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, tangible, to be felt, to<BR>be handled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्टृ
स्पर्ष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, who or what touches or<BR>affects or acts upon; (टा), m. any agent or affection<BR>causing bodily pain or sickness, morbid heat, (the<BR>word स्परितृ given in Śabda-k. appears to be a<BR>corrupt form of this word; cf. स्परिश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पार्शनप्रत्यक्ष
स्पार्शनप्रत्यक्ष, अम्, n. (fr. स्पर्शन +<BR>प्रत्यक्ष), tactile perception, perception by touch<BR>or feel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
2. स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, a toucher, who or what touches,<BR>touching, piercing (generally in comps.; cf. मर्म-<BR>स्पृश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशत्
स्पृशत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, touching, handling,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशा
स्पृशा, f. a kind of plant (= भुजङ्ग-घातिनी,<BR>commonly called Kankālikā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशी
स्पृशी, f. the prickly nightshade, Solanum Jacquini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्य
स्पृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be touched or felt, tangi-<BR>ble, sensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्यमान
स्पृश्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being touched, being<BR>handled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्ट|स्पृष्टः
स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, touched, felt with the hand,<BR>handled; formed by complete contact of the organs<BR>of utterance (as the consonants of the five classes of<BR>Gutturals, Palatals, Cerebrals, Dentals, and Labials,<BR>except the semivowels which are called ईषत्-स्पृ-<BR>ष्ट, formed by slight contact, and the sibilants and<BR>ह् which are called ईषद्-विवृत, formed by slight<BR>opening); defiled.<BR>—स्पृष्ट-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>merely touched.<BR>—स्पृष्ट-मैथुन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>defiled by sexual intercourse.<BR>—स्पृष्टा-स्पृष्टम्<BR>or स्पृष्टा-स्पृष्टि, ind. mutual touching, touching<BR>one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टि|स्पृष्टिः
स्पृष्टि, इस्, f. touch, touching, feeling, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टिन्
स्पृष्टिन्, ई, इनी, इ (?) , one who has touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्ट्वा
स्पृष्ट्वा, ind. having touched or felt or handled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रष्टव्य
स्प्रष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be touched, tangible,<BR>to be handled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रष्टृ
स्प्रष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, = स्पर्ष्टृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्
स्पृह् स्पृह् (connected with rts. 1. स्पृध्,<BR>स्पर्ध्), cl. 10. P. A. स्पृहयति, -ते,<BR>स्पृहयाम्-आस, स्पृहयाम्-बभूव, अपस्पृहत्,<BR>स्पृहयितुम्, to desire, wish for, long for (with dat.<BR>or gen., e. g. राज्याय न स्पृहये, I do not desire<BR>dominion); to envy (with dat. or gen., e. g. न<BR>तेषां स्पृहयामि, I do not envy them; कुवेराय<BR>स्पृहयति, he envies Kuvera): Pass. स्पृह्यते, to<BR>be desired, &c.; [cf. perhaps Gr. σκέρχομαι; Lat.<BR>spero; Old Germ. spulgen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पार्ह
स्पार्ह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्पृहा), Ved. wished for,<BR>desirable, agreeable, enviable; (अम्), n., Ved. any-<BR>thing enviable or beautiful, (Sāy. स्पार्हा = स्पृह-<BR>णीयानि तेजांसि, Ṛg-veda I. 135, 2.)<BR>—स्पार्ह-रा-<BR>धस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having or bestowing enviable<BR>wealth, (Sāy. = स्पृहणीय-धन, Ṛg-veda IV.<BR>16, 16.)<BR>—स्पार्ह-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>enviable heroes or posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहण|स्पृहणं
स्पृहण, अम्, n. the act of desiring or wishing<BR>for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहणीय|स्पृहणीयं
स्पृहणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be wished or longed<BR>for, desirable, enviable.<BR>—स्पृहणीय-ता, f. or<BR>स्पृहणीय-त्व, अम्, n. desirableness, enviableness.<BR>—स्पृहणीय-शोभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having desirable<BR>beauty, of enviable beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयत्
स्पृहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, longing for, desiring,<BR>envying.<BR>—स्पृहयद्-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. en-<BR>dowed with any form that may be desired, assuming all<BR>shapes, (Sāy. = यादृशं वर्णं यजमानः स्पृ-<BR>हयति तादृश-वर्णोपेतः, Ṛg-veda II. 10, 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयमाण
स्पृहयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring, wishing for,<BR>envying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयाय्य
स्पृहयाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring, desirable, en-<BR>viable, (Sāy. = स्पृहणीय); (अस्), m. epithet of a<BR>particular Nakṣatra, (Uṇādi-s. III. 96.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयालु|स्पृहयालुः
स्पृहयालु, उस्, उस्, उ, disposed to be desirous<BR>or envious of, wishful, desirous, eager for, covetous,<BR>cupidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयित्वा
स्पृहयित्वा, ind. having desired or wished for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहा
स्पृहा, f. desire, eager desire, longing, wish, envy,<BR>covetousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहालु
स्पृहालु (according to some) = स्पृहयालु above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहित
स्पृहित, अस्, आ, अम्, desired, wished for, longed for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्य|स्पृह्यः
स्पृह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be wished for or desired,<BR>desirable; (अस्), m. the wild citron tree (= मातु-<BR>लुङ्गक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्यमाण
स्पृह्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being desired or longed<BR>for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पॄ
स्पॄ स्पॄ (also written स्वॄ, सॄ), cl. 9. P.<BR>स्पृणाति, to hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रष्टृ
स्प्रष्टृ स्प्रष्टृ, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट्
स्फट् स्फट् (thought to be for an original<BR>स्पर्त्; cf. Germ. spalten; Eng. split),<BR>cl. 1. P. स्फटति, &c., to burst, expand, &c. (= rt.<BR>स्फुट्, q. v.): Caus. or cl. 10. P. स्फाटयति, &c.,<BR>to split open, cleave; to kill (= rt. स्फिट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट|स्फटः
स्फट, अस्, आ, m. f. a snake's expanded hood;<BR>(ई), f. alum, (see स्फटिकारि below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिक|स्फटिकः
स्फटिक, अस्, m. crystal, quartz; (आ), f. sulphate<BR>of alumina or alum.<BR>—स्फटिक-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>glittering like crystal, crystalline, transparent.<BR>—स्फ-<BR>टिक-मणि-गृह, अम्, n. a house of crystalline gems,<BR>crystal-abode.<BR>—स्फटिक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made<BR>or consisting of crystal, crystalline.<BR>—स्फटिक-<BR>स्कम्भ, अस्, m. a crystal pillar.<BR>—स्फटिक-हर्-<BR>म्य, अम्, n. a crystal palace.<BR>—स्फटिकाचल (˚क-<BR>अच्˚), अस्, m. ‘crystal-mountain,’ mount Meru.<BR>—स्फटिकात्मन् (˚क-आत्˚), आ, m. crystal.<BR>—स्फ-<BR>टिकाद्रि (˚क-अद्˚), इस्, m. ‘crystal-mountain,’ the<BR>mountain Kailāsa.<BR>—स्फटिकाद्रि-भिद, अस्, m.<BR>‘penetrating Kailāsa,’ camphor.<BR>—स्फटिकाभ्र (˚क-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘crystal-cloud,’ camphor.<BR>—स्फटि-<BR>काश्मन् (˚क-अश्˚), आ, m. ‘crystal-stone,’ crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकारि|स्फटिकारिः
स्फटिकारि, इस्, or स्फटिकारिका or स्फटिकारी,<BR>f. sulphate of alumina or alum (commonly corrupted<BR>into फट्-करी, फट्-कारी, फट्-किरि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकी
स्फटिकी, f. (according to some) alum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटक|स्फाटकं|स्फाटकः
स्फाटक, अस्, m. a drop of water; (अम्), n.<BR>crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटिक|स्फाटिकं
स्फाटिक, अस्, ई, अम्, made of crystal, crystalline;<BR>(अम्), n. crystal.<BR>—स्फाटिकोपल (˚क-उप्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘crystal-stone,’ crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटित
स्फाटित, अस्, आ, अम्, split open, expanded, made<BR>to gape, cleft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटीक|स्फाटीकं
स्फाटीक, अम्, n. crystal, quartz.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फण्ट्|स्फंट्
स्फण्ट् स्फण्ट्, cl. 1. P. स्फण्टति, &c., to<BR>burst, open, expand, &c. (= rt. स्फुट्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 10. P. स्फण्टयति, to jest or joke with<BR>(= rt. स्फण्ड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फण्ड्|स्फंड्
स्फण्ड् स्फण्ड्, cl. 1. P. स्फण्डति, &c.,<BR>cl. 10. P. स्फण्डयति, to jest or joke<BR>with, to laugh at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फर्
स्फर् स्फर् = rt. स्फुर्, and serving as<BR>the form of its Caus. स्फारयति, &c.,<BR>see स्फुर्, वि-स्फुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फरण|स्फरणं
स्फरण, अम्, n. trembling, quivering, throbbing,<BR>vibration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फार|स्फारं|स्फारः
1. स्फार, अस्, m. (for 2. see p. 1152), throbbing,<BR>quivering, vibration; twanging (of a bow-string; cf.<BR>वि-स्फार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फारण|स्फारणं
स्फारण, अम्, n. the act of throbbing, shaking,<BR>trembling; causing to throb or vibrate (fr. the Caus.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फारित
1. स्फारित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 1152), made<BR>to quiver or vibrate [cf. वि-स्फारित]; throbbing;<BR>vibrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फल्
स्फल् स्फल्, cl. 1. P. स्फलति, पस्फाल,<BR>स्फलितुम्, to tremble, quiver, throb,<BR>palpitate, beat (= rt. स्फुल्, q. v.): Caus. स्फाल-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to tremble or shake, &c.;<BR>[cf. Gr. σφάλλ-ω, σφάλ-μα, ἀ-σφαλ-ής, σφαλ-ερός;<BR>Lat. fall-o, fal-sus, falla, fallax, fallac-ia; Old<BR>Germ. fallan; Lith. pula, pulti, ‘to fall.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाल|स्फालः
स्फाल, अस्, m. throbbing, quivering, palpitation,<BR>beat, trembling, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फालन|स्फालनं
स्फालन, अम्, n. the act of palpitating, shaking,<BR>quivering; causing to shake about or move; rubbing,<BR>friction; stroking or patting (a horse &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटक|स्फाटकं|स्फाटकः
स्फाटक स्फाटक, स्फाटिक. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाय्
स्फाय् स्फाय् (thought by some to be<BR>derived from a Pass. of a lost rt. स्पन्,<BR>प् becoming फ् through the influence of initial स्;<BR>but apparently connected in some senses with rts.<BR>स्फर्, स्फुर्), cl. 1. A. स्फायते, पस्फाये, स्फा-<BR>यितुम्, to grow large or fat, become bulky, swell,<BR>expand, increase: Caus. स्फावयति (perhaps ori-<BR>ginally स्फापयति), -यितुम्, Aor. अपिस्फवत्<BR>(Pāṇ. VII. 3, 11), to cause to grow large, enlarge,<BR>augment, increase; [cf. Gr. σπά-ω, σπά-σ-μα, σπα-σ-μό-ς,<BR>ἀ-σπάζομαι, ἀγαπάω (i. e. ἀγαν-σπαω);<BR>Lat. spa-ti-um, patere; Old Germ. spannan, spa-<BR>nan; Angl. Sax. spanan, spinnan; Goth. spin-<BR>nan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फात|स्फातः
स्फात, अस्, आ, अम्, grown big, swollen, enlarged,<BR>increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाति|स्फातिः
स्फाति, इस्, f. swelling, intumescence, increase,<BR>growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फार|स्फारं|स्फारः
2. स्फार, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. II. 13.<BR>fr. rt. स्फाय् above; perhaps also connected with rt.<BR>स्फर् and 1. स्फार), swelling, increase, enlargement<BR>(= वृद्धि); a bubble (in gold &c.); a protuber-<BR>ance [cf. Gr. σφαῖρα] (अस्, आ, अम्), large, increased,<BR>expanded, spreading, great; abundant; loud; (अम्),<BR>n. much, abundance.<BR>—स्फारी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भ-<BR>वति, &c., to become large or swollen, swell out,<BR>expand, spread out; to become manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फारित
2. स्फारित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. स्फार above; but<BR>perhaps also connected with rt. स्फर्), swollen out,<BR>spread out, extended, large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फावयत्
स्फावयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, augmenting, increasing,<BR>enlarging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिर|स्फिरं
स्फिर, अस्, आ, अम्, abundant, much, many, large;<BR>swollen, expanded; vast, capacious, (Sāy. = वृद्-<BR>ध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीत|स्फीतः
स्फीत, अस्, आ, अम्, swollen, enlarged, bulky, fat,<BR>big, large, thick; much, abundant, many, numerous;<BR>successful, prosperous; affected by hereditary disease.<BR>—स्फीत-ता, f. bulkiness, enlargement; prosperity,<BR>successful progress.<BR>—स्फीती-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>&c., to enlarge, augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीति|स्फीतिः
स्फीति, इस्, f. increase, enlargement; prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेयस्
स्फेयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of स्फिर), more<BR>abundant, very much or abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेष्ठ|स्फेष्ठः
स्फेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of स्फिर), most<BR>abundant, very much or abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फार|स्फारं|स्फारः
स्फार स्फार, स्फारण. See p. 1151,<BR>col. 3, and above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाल|स्फालः
स्फाल स्फाल, स्फालन. See p. 1151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिच्
स्फिच् स्फिच्, क्, f. (by some connected with<BR>rt. स्फाय्, ‘to be fat’), a buttock, hip; (औ), f. du.<BR>the buttocks; [cf. Old Germ. spech; Angl. Sax.<BR>spic.]<BR>—स्फिक्-घातनक, अस्, m. a particular plant<BR>or small tree much used in medicine (= कट्-फल,<BR>p. 196, col. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिगी
स्फिगी, f., Ved. the buttock, hip; (this form<BR>स्फिगी seems necessary to account for स्फिग्या =<BR>कट्या, Ṛg-veda III. 32, 11; स्फिग्यम् = कटि-<BR>प्रदेशम्, Ṛg-veda VIII. 4, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिज्
स्फिज्, क्, f. = स्फिच् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्
स्फिट् स्फिट्, cl. 10. P. स्फेटयति, &c.,<BR>to hurt, injure, kill (= rt. स्फिट्ट्); to<BR>despise; to love (according to some); to cover (ac-<BR>cording to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्ट्
स्फिट्ट् स्फिट्ट्, cl. 10. P. स्फिट्टयति, &c.,<BR>to hurt, kill (= rts. स्फिट्, स्फट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिर|स्फिरं
स्फिर स्फिर. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीत|स्फीतः
स्फीत स्फीत, स्फीति. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्
स्फुट् स्फुट् (connected with rts. स्फुर्,<BR>स्फुल्), cl. 6. P. स्फुटति, cl. 1. P. A.<BR>स्फोटति, -ते, पुस्फोट, पुस्फुटे, अस्फुटत्, अस्-<BR>फुटीत्, अस्फोटीत्, स्फुटितुम् (cl. 1. स्फोटितुम्), to<BR>burst or become suddenly rent asunder, burst open,<BR>split open, part asunder, break forth, expand; to<BR>blossom, blow (generally A.); to burst into view, be-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">Page1152-b+ 81</a>]<BR>come manifested or made public, to disperse, run<BR>away; cl. 10. P. स्फुटयति, to burst, crack, break<BR>open; to burst into view: Pass. स्फुट्यते, Aor.<BR>अस्फोटि: Caus. स्फोटयति, to burst or rend sud-<BR>denly, break, split, cleave, tear open, divide; to<BR>disclose, make clear; to hurt, destroy, kill; to<BR>winnow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट|स्फुटः
स्फुट, अस्, आ, अम्, burst, split open, broken,<BR>rent, torn, opened, expanded; open, blossomed,<BR>blown; clearly displayed, clear; plain, distinct, mani-<BR>fest, evident; well known or understood; bright;<BR>white; loud; spread, diffused; (in astronomy) ap-<BR>parent, true; corrected; (आ), f. the expanded hood<BR>of a serpent; (अम्), ind. distinctly, manifestly, evi-<BR>dently, certainly.<BR>—स्फुट-ता, f. openness, mani-<BR>festation; perspicuity; blossoming.<BR>—स्फुट-तार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having stars clearly seen, bright with<BR>stars.<BR>—स्फुट-पौरुष, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>displayed valour or energy.<BR>—स्फुट-फल, अम्,<BR>n. (in geometry) clear or precise result (of any<BR>calculation); distinct or precise area (of a triangle<BR>&c.).<BR>—स्फुट-बन्धनी, f. a kind of plant, heart-<BR>pea (= पारावत-पदी).<BR>—स्फुट-वल्कली, f. the<BR>plant heart-pea.<BR>—स्फुट-सार, अस्, m. (probably)<BR>the true latitude of a star or planet.<BR>—स्फुट-सूर्य-<BR>गति, इस्, f. apparent or true motion of the sun.<BR>—स्फुटार्थ (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a clear<BR>meaning, intelligible, obvious, significant.<BR>—स्फुटी-<BR>करण, अम्, n. the act of displaying clearly, making<BR>distinct; making true or correct, correction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटत्
स्फुटत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, bursting open, part-<BR>ing or bursting asunder, splitting in two; blowing,<BR>blossoming; becoming manifest or clear; evolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटन|स्फुटनं
स्फुटन, अम्, n. the act of breaking or rending<BR>suddenly, bursting, tearing open, disruption, open-<BR>ing, expanding, blossoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटनीय
स्फुटनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken open or<BR>split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटि|स्फुटिः
स्फुटि, इस्, or स्फुटी, f. cracking or chapping of<BR>the skin of the feet, sores or swelling of the feet;<BR>the fruit of the Karkaṭī or a sort of melon, Cucumis<BR>Momordica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटिका
स्फुटिका, f. (probably) a small bit broken off,<BR>little bit or piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटित|स्फुटितः
स्फुटित, अस्, आ, अम्, burst, broken open, split,<BR>cracked; budded, blown, expanded (as a flower);<BR>made clear, manifested, spread out; torn, destroyed;<BR>laughed at (= परि-हसित; cf. rt. स्फुण्ट्).<BR>—स्फु-<BR>टित-चरण, अस्, आ, अम्, having wide feet, splay-<BR>footed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोट|स्फोटः
स्फोट, अस्, m. breaking, splitting open, bursting,<BR>disclosure, (नर्म-स्फोट in dramatic action is ex-<BR>plained to mean भाव-लेशैः सूचितो ऽल्परसः,<BR>i. e. slight disclosures or glimpses of love); a swelling,<BR>boil, tumor; the idea or disclosure which bursts out<BR>or flashes on the mind when a sound is uttered; the<BR>eternal sound in the Pūrva-mīmāṃsā; (आ), f. the<BR>expanded hood of a snake.<BR>—स्फोट-वाद, अस्, m.<BR>a dissertation on the above philosophical Sphoṭa.<BR>—स्फोट-वीजक, अस्, m. ‘having bursting seeds,’<BR>the marking-nut plant (= भल्लातक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटक|स्फोटकः
स्फोटक, अस्, m. one who bursts or splits open;<BR>a swelling, boil, tumor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटन|स्फोटनं|स्फोटनः
स्फोटन, अस्, ई, अम्, breaking or splitting asunder,<BR>opening, making clear, disclosing, manifesting; (अस्),<BR>m. (in Vedic grammar) = व्यञ्जक, separated utter-<BR>ance of a close combination of consonants; (अम्), n.<BR>the act of bursting or rending suddenly, splitting,<BR>cracking; tearing; winnowing grain, &c.; cracking<BR>the finger-joints, snapping the fingers; (in grammar)<BR>the separation of the letters of a double consonant;<BR>(ई), f. an instrument for splitting or cleaving, a<BR>gimlet, boring-tool, auger [cf. आ-स्फोटनी, लास्फो-<BR>टनी].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटायन|स्फोटायनः
स्फोटायन, अस्, m., N. of an ancient gram-<BR>marian, (Pāṇ. VI. 1, 123; he is identified by some<BR>with Kakṣīvat.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटिका
स्फोटिका, f. a kind of bird, a wagtail (= हापु-<BR>त्रिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटित
स्फोटित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), made to<BR>burst open, rent or torn asunder, disclosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्ट्
स्फुट्ट् स्फुट्ट्, cl. 10. P. स्फुट्टयति, &c.,<BR>to despise, disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुड्
स्फुड् स्फुड्, cl. 6. P. स्फुडति, &c., to<BR>cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुण्ट्|स्फुंट्
स्फुण्ट् स्फुण्ट्, cl. 1. P. स्फुण्टति, &c.,<BR>to open, expand, &c. (= rt. स्फुट्);<BR>cl. 10. P. स्फुण्टयति, &c., to jest, joke, laugh at<BR>(= rt. स्फण्ड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुण्ड्|स्फुंड्
स्फुण्ड् स्फुण्ड्, cl. 1. A. स्फुण्डते, &c.,<BR>to open, expand, &c. (= rt. स्फुट्); cl.<BR>10. P. स्फुण्डयति, &c., to jest, &c. (= rt.<BR>स्फण्ड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुत्
स्फुत् स्फुत्, an imitative sound; [cf. फुत्.]<BR>—स्फुत्-कर, अस्, m. ‘making a blowing or<BR>crackling sound,’ fire.<BR>—स्फुत्-कार, अस्, m. making<BR>the noise स्फुत्, crackling, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्
स्फुर् स्फुर् (= rt. स्फर्, which appears<BR>in the Caus. and is probably the older<BR>form, see स्फर्; the rt. स्फुर् is evidently con-<BR>nected with rts. स्फुट्, स्फुल्), cl. 6. P. स्फुरति,<BR>पुस्फोर, स्फुरिष्यति, अस्फुरीत्, Prec. स्फूर्-<BR>यात्, स्फुरितुम्, to tremble, palpitate, throb, vibrate,<BR>thrill, quiver, twitch, become agitated, struggle; to<BR>start, dart, spring, bound; to spring back, rebound;<BR>to spring up, shoot out, break forth, burst out plainly<BR>or visibly, start into view, be evident or manifest,<BR>appear clearly, become displayed or expanded; to<BR>flash, scintillate, twinkle, sparkle, shine, gleam,<BR>glitter; to flash on the mind, rush into the memory;<BR>to go tremulously; to bruise, destroy, (Sāy. स्फुरत्<BR>= स्फुरिष्यति = वाधिष्यति, Ṛg-veda I. 84, 8):<BR>Pass. स्फुर्यते, Aor. अस्फोरि: Caus. स्फोरयति,<BR>स्फारयति (see rt. स्फर्), -यितुम्, Aor. अपु-<BR>स्फुरत्, अपुस्फरत्, to cause to vibrate; to make<BR>to shine or glitter; to cast: Desid. पुस्फुरिषति:<BR>Intens. पोस्फुर्यते, पोस्फोर्ति; [cf. Zend śpar;<BR>Gr. σπαίρ-ω, ἀ-σπαίρ-ω, (probably also) σπείρω,<BR>σπέρμα, σποράς, σφυρόν; (probably) Lat. sperno;<BR>Angl. Sax. spurnan, spura; Lith. spir-ti, spar-<BR>dy-ti.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर|स्फुरः
स्फुर, अस्, m. trembling, throbbing; swelling;<BR>coruscating; a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरण|स्फुरणं
स्फुरण, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of trembling,<BR>throbbing, pulsation, vibration; quivering or throb-<BR>bing of parts of the body (e. g. quivering of the<BR>lips, twitching of the eyes, &c., as indicating good<BR>or bad luck); springing or breaking forth, starting<BR>into view, expansion; flashing, coruscation, scintilla-<BR>tion, twinkling, glittering; flashing on the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरत्
स्फुरत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, trembling, shaking,<BR>quivering, throbbing; starting, darting; springing<BR>up, breaking forth, bursting out plainly or visibly,<BR>becoming clear or manifest; flashing, glittering;<BR>flashing vividly on the mind; swelling, expanding<BR>[cf. स्फुटत्]; going, moving; going tremulously.<BR>—स्फुरद्-अधरोष्ठ (˚र-ओष्˚) or स्फुरद्-<BR>ओष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम्, having quivering lips, (स्फुरद्-<BR>अधरोष्ठम्, ind. with quivering or pouting lips.)<BR>—स्फुरद्-उल्का, f. a shooting meteor, aerolite.<BR>—स्फुरदुल्काकृति (˚का-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having<BR>the form of a shooting meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरित|स्फुरितं
स्फुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, heaving, throb-<BR>bing, thrilling, palpitating; shaken, agitated; flash-<BR>ing, glittering, gleaming, playing, unsteady; swelled,<BR>swollen; (अम्), n. a throb, throbbing, tremor,<BR>quivering or twitching of the eyelids, &c., agitation<BR>or emotion of mind.<BR>—स्फुरित-शतह्रद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having flashing lightning (said of a cloud).<BR>—स्फुरितोत्तराधर (˚त-उत्˚, ˚र-अध्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having trembling upper and under lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्त
स्फूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to some) throbbed,<BR>throbbing; suddenly risen into remembrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ति|स्फूर्तिः|स्फूर्त्ति|स्फूर्त्तिः
स्फूर्ति, इस्, f. throb, palpitation, tremor, trem-<BR>bling, shaking, vibration; spring, bound, start;<BR>breaking forth visibly, becoming evident or apparent,<BR>manifestation, expansion; flashing on the mind or<BR>memory.<BR>—स्फूर्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, throbbing,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">Page1153-a+ 75</a>]<BR>thrilling (with joy or excitement), tremulous, agi-<BR>tated; tender-hearted; (आन्), m. a follower or wor-<BR>shipper of Śiva (= पाशुपत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोरण|स्फोरणं
स्फोरण, अम्, n. throbbing, quivering, &c. =<BR>स्फार (according to Vopa-deva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्छ्
स्फुर्छ् स्फुर्छ् (also written स्वुर्छ्), cl.<BR>1. P. स्फूर्छति, पुस्फूर्छ, स्फूर्-<BR>छितुम्, to spread, extend; to forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्छित
स्फूर्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, spread; forgotten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ण
1. स्फूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, = स्फूर्छित above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्
स्फुर्ज् स्फुर्ज् (probably connected with<BR>rt. स्फुर्), cl. 1. P. स्फूर्जति, पु-<BR>स्फूर्ज, स्फूर्जितुम्, to thunder, make a sound<BR>like a thunder-clap, crash, explode: Pass. स्फूर्ज्-<BR>यते: Caus. स्फूर्जयति: Desid. पुस्फूर्जिषति:<BR>Intens. पोस्फूर्ज्यते, पोस्फूर्क्ति; [cf. Lat. spargo;<BR>Angl. Sax. sprecan, sprœncan, sprengan, sprin-<BR>can, springan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्जक|स्फुर्ज्जक|स्फुर्ज्जकः
स्फुर्जक = स्फूर्जक below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्जथु|स्फुर्जथुः|स्फुर्ज्जथु
स्फुर्जथु = स्फूर्जथु below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज|स्फूर्जः|स्फूर्ज्ज
स्फूर्ज, अस्, m. the crashing sound of a thunder-<BR>clap, thunder; Indra's thunderbolt; sudden burst,<BR>(नर्म-स्फूर्ज, sudden burst of love; in dramatic<BR>action defined to mean सुखारम्भो भयान्तो<BR>नव-सङ्गमः, first union of lovers characterized<BR>by joy in the beginning and some cause of fear in<BR>the end.)<BR>—स्फूर्जा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जक|स्फूर्जकः|स्फूर्ज्जक
स्फूर्जक, अस्, m. a sort of ebony tree, Diospyros<BR>Glutinosa (= तिन्दुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जथु|स्फूर्जथुः|स्फूर्ज्जथु
स्फूर्जथु, उस्, m. a clap of thunder, explosion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जन|स्फूर्जनं|स्फूर्ज्जन
स्फूर्जन, अम्, n. the act of thundering; an<BR>explosion, crash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जयत्
स्फूर्जयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. overwhelming,<BR>crushing, (Sāy. = निष्पिषत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जित
स्फूर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, thundered; [cf. वि-स्फूर्-<BR>जित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ण
2. स्फूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to some) thun-<BR>dered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल्
स्फुल् स्फुल् (connected with rts. स्फुर्,<BR>स्फुट्, स्फल्), cl. 6. P. स्फुलति, पु-<BR>स्फोल, Aor. अस्फुलीत्, स्फुलितुम्, to tremble,<BR>throb, vibrate; to dart forth, appear; to collect; to<BR>slay, kill, (enumerated among the वध-कर्माणः<BR>in Naigh. II. 19): Pass. स्फुल्यते, Aor. अस्फोलि:<BR>Caus. स्फोलयति, &c. (For comparisons see rt.<BR>स्फल्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल|स्फुलं
स्फुल, अम्, n. a tent (= वस्त्र-वेश्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलन|स्फुलनं
स्फुलन, अम्, n. trembling, throbbing, vibration,<BR>palpitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्ग|स्फुलिंग|स्फुलिंगं|स्फुलिंगः|स्फुलिङ्गः
स्फुलिङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. (perhaps to be<BR>connected with स्फुत्, p. 1152), a spark of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्गिन्
स्फुलिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having sparks of fire,<BR>sparkling; (इनी), f., N. of one of the seven tongues<BR>of Agni or fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोलन
स्फोलन, अम्, n. = स्फाल (according to Vopa-<BR>deva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेयस्
स्फेयस् स्फेयस्, स्फेष्ठ. See p. 1152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोट|स्फोटः
स्फोट स्फोट, स्फोटित, &c. See p. 1152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्य|स्फ्यं
स्फ्य स्फ्य, अम्, n. an implement used in<BR>sacrifices (described as a piece of wood shaped like<BR>a sword for stirring the boiled rice, or, according to<BR>some, for trimming the mound used as an altar).<BR>—स्फ्य-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made or marked out<BR>by the स्फ्य.<BR>—स्फ्य-वर्तनि, इस्, m. the furrow<BR>or line made by the स्फ्य (in marking out the<BR>sacrificial ground).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फैयकृत
स्फैयकृत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्फ्य-कृत), re-<BR>lating to anything made by the स्फ्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्बॄ
स्बॄ स्बॄ = rt. स्वॄ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्म
स्म स्म (probably for 2. समा, an old inst.<BR>of 1. सम, and meaning ‘wholly, entirely’), ind. a<BR>particle added to the present tense of verbs or to<BR>present participles (generally giving them a past<BR>signification, e. g. प्रविशन्ति स्म पुरीम्, they<BR>entered the city); a pleonastic particle (often used<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">Page1153-b+ 77</a>]<BR>after मा, see मा स्म under 1. मा; also in the<BR>Veda preceded by अध, q. v., and other particles).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मत्
स्मत् स्मत्, ind. (probably connected with<BR>स्म; according to some an old neut. of 1. सम;<BR>but according to Sāy. a contraction of सुमत्), Ved.<BR>well, excellently, (Sāy. = सु, सुमत्); with, together<BR>with (= 2. सह; cf. Gr. μετά; Mod. Germ. mit);<BR>constantly, always, (Sāy. = नित्यम्.)<BR>—स्मत्-पुरन्-<BR>धि, इस्, m. = स्वर्ग-कुटुम्बी (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 34, 6).<BR>—स्मद्-अभीशु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. having beautiful reins, (Sāy. = शोभन-रज्जु-<BR>युक्त or शोभन-शरीर-कान्ति, Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>25, 24.)<BR>—स्मद्-इष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according<BR>to Sāy.) going well or sent together (= प्रशस्त-<BR>गति or सह-प्रेषित, Ṛg-veda VII. 87, 3).<BR>—स्मद्-<BR>ऊध्नी, f. (see ऊधस्), Ved. (a cow) always giving<BR>milk, (Sāy. = नित्यम् उधसा युक्ता, सर्वदा<BR>पयसः प्रदात्री, Ṛg-veda I. 73, 6; cf. पी-<BR>नोध्नी.)<BR>—स्मद्-दिष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. auspiciously<BR>speaking (said of Indra; Sāy. = भद्र-वाक्य,<BR>Ṛg-veda III. 45, 5); handsome-looking, (Sāy. =<BR>प्रशस्त-दर्शन, Ṛg-veda VI. 63, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मय|स्मयः
स्मय स्मय, स्मयत्, &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर|स्मरः
स्मर स्मर. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त|स्मार्तः|स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त स्मार्त, &c. See p. 1154, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मि
स्मि स्मि, cl. 1. A. स्मयते (ep. also P.<BR>-ति), सिष्मिये, स्मेष्यते, अस्मेष्ट,<BR>स्मेतुम्, to smile, laugh; to expand, bloom (as a<BR>flower): Pass. स्मीयते, Aor. अस्मायि: Caus. स्मा-<BR>ययति, -ते (also स्मापयते in वि-स्मि, q. v.), to<BR>cause to laugh, provoke or excite laughter; (A.) to<BR>laugh at, mock, despise: Desid. सिस्मयिषते:<BR>Intens. सेष्मीयते, (in Mālavikāgnimitra, Act IV,<BR>the Prākṛt सिमिसिमा-अन्ति [see s.v.] is incorrectly<BR>referred to the Intens. of rt. स्मि), सेष्मयीति, सेष्-<BR>मेति; [cf. Gr. μεῖ-δ-ος, μεί-δ-η-μα, μει-δ-ά-ω,<BR>μει-διάω, (perhaps also) σμοιός. μέμφομαι, μῶμος:<BR>Lat. mi-ru-s, ni-miru-m, mira-ri: Old Germ.<BR>smie-l-en, smie-r-en: Eng. smile: Angl. Sax.<BR>smœrc: Slav. sme-ja-ti, po-sme-chu: Lett. smee-t:<BR>Hib. smigeadh, magadh, ‘mocking;’ magamhuil,<BR>‘jeering.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मय|स्मयः
स्मय, अस्, m. smiling at anything, wonder, sur-<BR>prise, astonishment; Wonder (personified as a son<BR>of Dharma); pride, conceit, arrogance.<BR>—स्मय-<BR>नुत्ति, इस्, f. the driving away or pulling down of<BR>pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयत्
स्मयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, smiling, laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयन
स्मयन, अम्, n. the act of smiling, a smile,<BR>gentle laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयनीय
स्मयनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be smiled (used im-<BR>personally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयमान
स्मयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, smiling, gently laugh-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयिन्
स्मयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, smiling, laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मित|स्मितं
स्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, smiled, smiling; expanded,<BR>blown, blossomed; (अम्), n. a smile, gentle laugh.<BR>—स्मित-दृश्, क्, f. ‘having a smiling look,’ a hand-<BR>some woman.<BR>—स्मित-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, preceded by<BR>a smile; (अम्), ind. with a smile, smilingly.<BR>—स्मित-<BR>पूर्वाभिभाषिन् (˚व-अभ्˚), ई, इणी, इ, addressing<BR>with a smile.<BR>—स्मित-शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having smiles,<BR>smiling, laughing.<BR>—स्मित-शोभिन्, ई, इनी, इ, smiling<BR>beautifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मिति|स्मितिः
स्मिति, इस्, f. smiling, a smile, laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मित्वा
स्मित्वा, ind. having smiled or laughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेतव्य
स्मेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be smiled (used imper-<BR>sonally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेर|स्मेरः
स्मेर, अस्, आ, अम्, smiling, laughing; blown,<BR>blooming, opened, expanded (as a flower); proud;<BR>evident, apparent; (अस्), m. (according to some) ap-<BR>pearance, manifestation.<BR>—स्मेर-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>smiling-faced, having a smiling face.<BR>—स्मेर-विष्-<BR>किर, अस्, m. ‘proud bird,’ a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मिट्
स्मिट् स्मिट् (connected with rt. स्मि),<BR>cl. 10. P. स्मेटयति, &c., to slight,<BR>despise; to love; to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मील्
स्मील् स्मील् (= rt. श्मील्, p. 1023; cf. rt.<BR>मील्), cl. 1. P. स्मीलति, &c., to wink,<BR>blink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
स्मृ 1. स्मृ (= rt. स्पृ, q. v.), cl. 5. P.<BR>स्मृणोति, &c., to please, gratify; to protect,<BR>defend; to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
स्मृ 2. स्मृ, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) स्मरति<BR>(-ते), सस्मार (2nd sing. सस्मर्थ, 1st<BR>du. सस्मरिव, 3rd pl. सस्मरुस्), स्मरिष्यति,<BR>अस्मार्षीत्, स्मर्तुम्, to remember (with acc. or<BR>gen., and when joined with 2nd Fut. of another rt.<BR>giving it a past signification, e. g. अमुं स्मरति ह-<BR>निष्यति, he remembers having killed him, Pāṇ. III.<BR>2, 112); to recollect, call to mind, bear in mind,<BR>think of, think upon, be mindful of; to recite men-<BR>tally or call upon the name (of a deity &c.); to re-<BR>cord (in the Smṛti), declare (as Smṛti or law;<BR>स्मरन्ति, they declare in the Smṛti); to desire, long<BR>for (with gen.): Pass. स्मर्यते, Aor. अस्मारि, Prec.<BR>स्मृषीष्ट and स्मरिषीष्ट, to be remembered;<BR>to be recorded; to be mentioned; to be declared (as<BR>a law); to be mentioned in the Smṛti: Caus. स्मार-<BR>यति (or स्मरयति), -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. असस्मरत्,<BR>त, to cause to remember, call to mind, remind; to<BR>give information; to cause to regret, cause to desire<BR>or long for (in the latter sense only स्मरयति):<BR>Desid. सुस्मूर्षते, to wish to recollect: Intens.<BR>सास्मर्यते, सास्मर्ति; [cf. Gr. μέρ-μηρ-α, μέρ-ι-μνα,<BR>μερ-μαίζω, μερμηρ-ίζω, μέρ-μερ-ος, μάρ-τυρ,<BR>μάρ-τυρ-ο-ς, μάρ-τυ-ς, μαρ-τύρ-ιον, μαρτύρ-ο-μαι,<BR>(perhaps also) μέλειν, μέλ-ε-σθαι, μελ-έ-τη, &c.:<BR>Lat. me-mor, memor-ia, memor-ā-re, mor-a, mos,<BR>mor-is: Goth. mêr-j-an, ‘to proclaim;’ meritha,<BR>maurnan: Old Germ. smer-zo, m., smer-za, f.<BR>‘pain;’ smerzan, mâriu, ‘to announce;’ māri,<BR>‘memorable:’ Mod. Germ. Mährchen: Angl. Sax.<BR>mœlan, mal, ge-mœred, mœrdh, mœrsian, mel-<BR>dian, ameldian, murnan, smeortan, ‘to smart:’<BR>Lith. uz-mirs-tu, ‘to forget:’ Hib. smuairean,<BR>‘dejection;’ (perhaps) smalanach, ‘sorrowful;’<BR>muirn, ‘natural affection.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्मूर्षमाण
सुस्मूर्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to re-<BR>member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर|स्मरः
स्मर, अस्, m. remembrance, recollection; loving<BR>recollection, love; Kāma-deva (god of love).<BR>—स्मर-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. amorous action or conduct, any wanton<BR>act, lasciviousness.<BR>—स्मर-कूपक, अस्, m. or स्मर-<BR>कूपिका, f. ‘well of love,’ the female organ.<BR>—स्मर-<BR>गुरु, उस्, m. ‘love-preceptor,’ epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—स्मर-गृह, अम्, n. ‘abode of love,’ the female<BR>organ.<BR>—स्मर-चक्र, अस्, m. a particular kind of<BR>sexual union.<BR>—स्मर-च्छत्र, अम्, n. the clitoris.<BR>—स्मर-दशा, f. a state of love, state of the body<BR>produced by being in love, (ten such states are enu-<BR>merated, e. g. anxious thought, sleeplessness, emacia-<BR>tion, loss of appetite, fainting, &c.)<BR>—स्मर-दायिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, causing or exciting love (= कामोद्दीपक).<BR>—स्मर-दीपिका, f., N. of a work.<BR>—स्मर-ध्व-<BR>ज, अस्, m. ‘love-sign,’ ‘love-emblem,’ the male<BR>organ; a fabulous fish (regarded as the emblem of<BR>Kāma-deva; cf. मकर-ध्वज); a musical in-<BR>strument; (आ), f. a bright moonlight night (accord-<BR>ing to some); (अम्), n. the female organ.<BR>—स्मर-<BR>प्रिया, f. ‘dear to Kāma,’ epithet of Rati (Kāma-<BR>deva's wife).<BR>—स्मर-भासित, अस्, आ, अम्, love-<BR>illuminated, inflamed by love.<BR>—स्मर-मन्दिर,<BR>अम्, n. ‘love-palace,’ the female organ.<BR>—स्मर-<BR>मोह, अस्, m. infatuation of love, passion, love.<BR>—स्मर-मोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, infatuated by love,<BR>overcome by passion.<BR>—स्मर-लेखनी, f. the<BR>Śārikā bird.<BR>—स्मर-वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘love's fa-<BR>vourite,’ epithet of A-niruddha.<BR>—स्मर-वाण-<BR>पङ्क्ति, इस्, f. the five arrows of Kāma-deva collec-<BR>tively (see पञ्च-वाण).<BR>—स्मर-वीथिका, f. ‘love-<BR>shop,’ a prostitute, harlot.<BR>—स्मर-वृद्धि-सञ्-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, m. a particular shrub (= काम-वृद्धि).<BR>—स्मर-शवर, अस्, m. ‘love-barbarian,’ cruel<BR>love.<BR>—स्मर-शासन, अस्, m. ‘chastiser of Kāma-<BR>deva,’ epithet of Śiva (see अन्-अङ्ग).<BR>—स्मर-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">Page1154-a+ 81</a>]<BR>सख, अस्, m. ‘love's friend,’ the moon.<BR>—स्मर-<BR>स्तम्भ, अस्, m. ‘love-column,’ the male organ.<BR>—स्मर-स्मर्य, अस्, m. a donkey, ass (= गर्द-<BR>भ).<BR>—स्मर-हर, अस्, m. ‘love-destroyer,’ epi-<BR>thet of Śiva (see अन्-अङ्ग).<BR>—स्मराकुल or स्म-<BR>राकुलित (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, agitated by love, love-<BR>sick.<BR>—स्मरागार (˚र-आग्˚), अम्, n. ‘love-abode,’<BR>the female organ.<BR>—स्मराङ्कुश (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘love-hook,’ a finger-nail; a lover, lascivious person.<BR>—स्मरातुर (˚र-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, love-sick, pining<BR>with love.<BR>—स्मरान्ध (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>love-blinded, infatuated with passion.<BR>—स्मरारि<BR>(˚र-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of Kāma-deva,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—स्मरार्त (˚र-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, love-sick.<BR>—स्मरासव (˚र-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘love-liquid,’ saliva.<BR>—स्मरोत्सुक (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pining or<BR>languishing with love, love-sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरण|स्मरणं
स्मरण, अम्, n. the act of remembering, re-<BR>membrance, memory, recollecting, recollection, re-<BR>miniscence; tradition, traditional precept, (इति स्मर-<BR>णात्, ‘from its being so mentioned in the Smṛti,’ cf.<BR>स्मृति); mental recitation (of the name of a deity),<BR>calling upon the name of a god; regretting, remem-<BR>bering with regret; thinking upon, anxious thought.<BR>—स्मरण-पदवी, f. ‘road to mere memory,’<BR>death.<BR>—स्मरणानुग्रह (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>favour of remembrance, kind remembrance.<BR>—स्मर-<BR>णापत्य-तर्पक (˚ण-अप्˚), अस्, m. ‘satisfying<BR>memory's offspring,’ a turtle, tortoise.<BR>—स्मरणा-<BR>यौगपद्य (˚ण-अय्˚), अम्, n. the non-simulta-<BR>neousness of recollections.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणीय
स्मरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be remembered, memo-<BR>rable, to be borne in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरत्
स्मरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, remembering, recollecting,<BR>considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्तव्य|स्मर्त्तव्य
स्मर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be remembered, memo-<BR>rable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्तृ
स्मर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who remembers or re-<BR>collects.<BR>—स्मर्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. remembrance, recol-<BR>lection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्यमाण|स्मर्य्यमाण
स्मर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being remembered,<BR>being mentioned in the Smṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार
स्मार, अस्, m. memory, recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारक
स्मारक, अस्, इका, अम्, reminding, putting in<BR>mind, instructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारण|स्मारणं
स्मारण, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), the act of caus-<BR>ing to remember, reminding, calling to mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारम्
स्मारम्, ind. having remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारित
स्मारित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), reminded,<BR>called to mind, recalled to recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारिन्
स्मारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, remembering; reminding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त|स्मार्तः|स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्मृति), relating to memory,<BR>memorial, remembered, coming within the range of<BR>memory; recorded in the Smṛtis, prescribed in the<BR>inspired codes of law, based on Smṛti, q. v.; sanc-<BR>tioned by law, canonical, legal; following the doc-<BR>trine of the law-books; domestic (applied to the<BR>domestic fire which every Brāhman is bound to keep<BR>up); (अस्), m. a Brāhman skilled in jurisprudence<BR>or traditional law (especially one belonging to a sect<BR>founded by Śaṅkarācārya, whose expositions of the<BR>principle of unity, according to the Vedānta doc-<BR>trine, they professedly follow, though holding Śiva<BR>in especial honour; their chief establishment is at<BR>Śṛṅga-giri, but they are said to be found throughout<BR>the south of India); (अम्), n. any act or rite enjoined<BR>by Smṛti or allowed by traditional usage, a legal act.<BR>—स्मार्त-कर्मन्, अ, n. a rite enjoined in the<BR>Smṛtis, one of the less important domestic rites.<BR>—स्मार्त-काल, अस्, m. the period to which memory<BR>may extend (i. e. a century, according to some<BR>lawyers).<BR>—स्मार्त-सूत्र, अम्, n. any Sūtra work<BR>based on Smṛti (opposed to श्रौत-सूत्र or Sūtras<BR>based on श्रुति, see सूत्र).<BR>—स्मार्त-होम-परि-<BR>शिष्ट, अम्, n., N. of a Pariśiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्य
स्मार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be remembered, memo-<BR>rable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत|स्मृतः
स्मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, remembered, recollected, called<BR>to mind; recorded, mentioned, said, declared, termed,<BR>styled, named; enjoined by Smṛti or traditional<BR>law, declared or propounded in the law-books.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-b" target="_blank">Page1154-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—स्मृत-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, only remembered or<BR>thought of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृति|स्मृतिः
स्मृति, इस्, f. remembrance, memory, reminiscence,<BR>recollection, thinking of or upon (any person or<BR>thing), calling to mind; Memory (personified as a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Aṅgiras); what is<BR>remembered, that which is borne in mind from the<BR>beginning, tradition, law; the institutes or body of<BR>traditional or memorial law (as handed down ori-<BR>ginally by Manu, Yājñavalkya, and other great legis-<BR>lators who were supposed to have been inspired, and<BR>to have based their precepts on the Veda and divine<BR>revelation, though the laws they promulgated were<BR>called Smṛti, ‘what is remembered,’ in contradistinc-<BR>tion to Śruti, ‘what is heard or revealed,’ and to<BR>Ācāra, ‘established usage;’ the very essence of Smṛti<BR>being that it was delivered memoriter by human<BR>authors, and not directly revealed, as explained in<BR>Manu II. 10, see श्रुति; in its widest acceptation<BR>Smṛti is said to include the Vedāṅgas, the Sūtras or<BR>aphorisms both श्रौत and गृह्य, the institutes of<BR>Manu and other inspired law-givers, the Itihāsas,<BR>such as the Rāmāyaṇa and Mahā-bhārata, and the<BR>Purāṇas, but the term Smṛti is more usually re-<BR>stricted to the metrical codes of Manu, Yājñavalkya,<BR>Parāśara, &c., see स्मृति-शास्त्र below); any par-<BR>ticular law-book or code of laws; any particular law<BR>or rule of law, canon, legal text (e. g. अनुमिता<BR>स्मृतिः प्रत्यक्षया स्मृत्या बाध्यते, a Smṛti<BR>which is only inferred is set aside by a visibly exist-<BR>ing Smṛti; इति स्मृतेः, according to such a Smṛti<BR>or legal text, according to such a traditional law);<BR>a passage in a work treating of law; pensive or<BR>loving recollection, desire, wish [cf. स्मर]; under-<BR>standing.<BR>—स्मृति-कौमुदी, f. ‘light of law,’ N.<BR>of a legal work by Viśveśvara (composed under the<BR>patronage of king Madana-pāla).<BR>—स्मृति-कौस्तु-<BR>भ, ‘jewel of law,’ N. of a work by Ananta-deva.<BR>—स्मृति-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a legal work.<BR>—स्मृ-<BR>ति-तत्त्व, अम्, n. ‘digest of legal truth,’ N. of a<BR>work by Raghu-nandana.<BR>—स्मृति-दर्पण, ‘mirror<BR>of law,’ N. of a work.<BR>—स्मृति-प्रत्यवमर्श,<BR>अस्, m. retentiveness of memory, accuracy of recollec-<BR>tion.<BR>—स्मृति-प्रबन्ध, अस्, m. a Smṛti com-<BR>position, legal work.<BR>—स्मृति-भ्रंश, अस्, m. loss<BR>or failure of memory.<BR>—स्मृति-मञ्जरी, f., N. of<BR>a legal work.<BR>—स्मृति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a<BR>good memory, remembering, recollecting.<BR>—स्मृति-<BR>महार्णव (˚हा-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘ocean of law,’ N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—स्मृति-रत्नाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘jewel-mine of law,’ N. of a work by Caṇḍeśvara.<BR>—स्मृतिरत्नावली (˚न-आव्˚), f. ‘string of jewels of<BR>law,’ N. of a work by Rāma-nātha.<BR>—स्मृति-रोध,<BR>अस्, m. temporary interruption or obstruction of<BR>memory, failure of memory.<BR>—स्मृति-विभ्रम, अस्,<BR>m. confusion of memory.<BR>—स्मृति-विरुद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, contrary to law, illegal, unjust.<BR>—स्मृति-<BR>विरोध, अस्, m. opposition to law, illegality, im-<BR>propriety; disagreement between two or more codes<BR>of law or legal texts.<BR>—स्मृति-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a law-<BR>book, a code, digest; legal science, (the most cele-<BR>brated law-books are those of Manu, Yājñavalkya<BR>with its commentary the Mitākṣarā, Parāśara, Hā-<BR>rīta, Vyāsa, Vasiṣṭha, Viṣṇu, Vṛhas-pati, Atri, Śaṅ-<BR>kha, Likhita, Uśanas, Aṅgiras, Yama, Āpastamba,<BR>Saṃvarta, Śātātapa, Kātyāyana, Dakṣa, Gautama;<BR>these authors are sometimes classed in three divisions,<BR>under the three heads of सात्त्विक, राजस, and<BR>तामस, according to the tendency of their writings.)<BR>—स्मृति-शील, ए, n. du. traditions and moral prac-<BR>tices.<BR>—स्मृति-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, one of whom only<BR>remembrance remains, a deceased or defunct person;<BR>that of which nothing is left but remembrance.<BR>—स्मृति-शैथिल्य, अम्, n. temporary failure or<BR>loss of memory.<BR>—स्मृति-सङ्ग्रह or स्मृति-<BR>समुच्चय, अस्, m. ‘law-collection,’ N. of two legal<BR>works.<BR>—स्मृति-सम्मत, अस्, आ, अम्, approved by<BR>law.<BR>—स्मृति-सागर and स्मृति-सागर-सङ्-<BR>ग्रह and स्मृति-सागर-सार, N. of various<BR>legal works.<BR>—स्मृति-साध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, capable<BR>of being proved by law.<BR>—स्मृति-सार, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">Page1154-c+ 77</a>]<BR>‘essence of law,’ N. of a work by Deva-yājñika; of<BR>another work by Yādavendra; of another by Hari-<BR>nātha.<BR>—स्मृति-सारावली (˚र-आव्˚), f. ‘line of es-<BR>sence of law,’ N. of a work.<BR>—स्मृति-सिद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, established by law.<BR>—स्मृति-हारिका, f.<BR>‘memory-seizer,’ N. of a daughter of Duḥsahana<BR>(described in the fifty-first chapter of the Mārkaṇ-<BR>ḍeya-Purāṇa as exercising an evil influence on the<BR>memory).<BR>—स्मृति-हेतु, उस्, m. a cause of recollec-<BR>tion, any mental act stirring the memory, impression<BR>on the mind, reflection, association of ideas, recollec-<BR>tion.<BR>—स्मृत्य्-अन्तर, अम्, n. another law-book.<BR>—स्मृत्य्-अपेत, अस्, आ, अम्, departed from memory,<BR>forgotten; inconsistent with Smṛti; illegal, unjust.<BR>—स्मृत्य्-अर्थ-सागर, अस्, m., N. of a work by<BR>Nṛ-siṃha.<BR>—स्मृत्य्-अर्थ-सार, अस्, m. ‘essence of<BR>the meaning of Smṛti,’ N. of a work on Hindū cere-<BR>monies by Śrīdhara-svāmin.<BR>—स्मृत्य्-उक्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, prescribed in the codes of law, enjoined by the<BR>Smṛtis, canonical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतीक
स्मृतीक, अम्, n. water (= उदक, Naigh. I. 12).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेर|स्मेरः
स्मेर स्मेर, स्मेर-मुख. See p. 1153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्य
स्य स्य, अम्, n., Ved. a winnowing basket<BR>(= शूर्प, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यद्
स्यद् स्यद्, स्यद. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द्|स्यंद्
स्यन्द् स्यन्द्, cl. 1. A. (in Fut., Aor., and<BR>Condit. also P., Ved. also P. in other<BR>tenses), स्यन्दते (-ति), सस्यन्दे (Ved. 3rd pl.<BR>Perf. P. सिष्यदुस्, Atharva-veda IX. 2, 20), स्यन्-<BR>दिषते, स्यन्त्स्यते (स्यन्त्स्यति), अस्यन्दिष्ट,<BR>अस्यन्त (अस्यदत्), स्यन्दितुम्, स्यन्त्तुम् or<BR>स्यन्तुम् (Ved. Inf. स्यन्दयध्यै), to trickle,<BR>ooze, drip, drop, distil, flow, ooze out, flow out; to<BR>flow with, pour forth, shed (with acc.); to run, flee<BR>(P.); (according to Naigh. II. 14), to move, rush,<BR>go: Pass. स्यद्यते, Aor. अस्यन्दि: Caus. स्यन्द-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. असिस्यन्दत्, -त: Desid.<BR>सिस्यन्दिषते, सिस्यन्त्सते, सिस्यन्त्सति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यद्
स्यद् in रघु-ष्यद्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यद|स्यदः
स्यद, अस्, m. rapid motion, speed, velocity, rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्तव्य
स्यन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be flowed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्त्त्वा
स्यन्त्त्वा or स्यन्त्वा, ind. having flowed; having<BR>rushed on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द|स्यंद|स्यंदः|स्यन्दः
स्यन्द, अस्, m. trickling; going, moving rapidly;<BR>a car, chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दत्
स्यन्दत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, moving on, rushing im-<BR>petuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दन|स्यंदन|स्यन्दनं|स्यन्दनः
स्यन्दन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, flowing, going quickly;<BR>quick, expeditious, swift; (अस्), m. a war-chariot,<BR>chariot, car; air, wind; the tree Dalbergia Ougei-<BR>nensis (= तिनिश); a particular Arhat of the past era;<BR>(ई), f. saliva; (according to some) the urinary pas-<BR>sage; (अम्), n. the act of trickling, oozing, drop-<BR>ping; rushing, going or flowing swiftly; water.<BR>—स्यन्दन-द्रुम, अस्, m. the tree Dalbergia<BR>Ougeinensis (said to be so called because its wood is<BR>used to make chariot-wheels &c.).<BR>—स्यन्दनारू-<BR>ढ (˚न-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mounted on a chariot or<BR>car.<BR>—स्यन्दनारोह (˚न-आर्˚), अस्, m. a warrior<BR>who fights mounted on a war-chariot.<BR>—स्यन्दना-<BR>लोक-भीत (˚न-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, terrified at the<BR>sight of a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनि|स्यन्दनिः
स्यन्दनि, इस्, m. the tree Dalbergia Ougeinensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनिका|स्यंदनिका
स्यन्दनिका, f. a drop of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनीय
स्यन्दनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be flowed; to be run;<BR>to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दमान
स्यन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, trickling, flowing, mov-<BR>ing rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दितृ
स्यन्दितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who runs or rushes<BR>quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दित्वा
स्यन्दित्वा, ind. having flowed; having rushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दिन्|स्यंदिन्
स्यन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, trickling, oozing, dropping;<BR>flowing, rushing; going, moving; (इनी), f. saliva;<BR>a cow bearing two calves at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द्र
स्यन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rushing, impetuous; (in<BR>Naigh. II. 9. स्यन्द्रासः is enumerated among the<BR>बल-नामानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्न|स्यन्नः
स्यन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, flowed, trickled, dropped;<BR>dropping, trickling, flowing (as water &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यम्
स्यम् स्यम्, cl. 1. P. स्यमति, सस्याम<BR>(3rd pl. सस्यमुस् or स्येमुस्), स्य-<BR>मिष्यति, अस्यमीत्, स्यमितुम्, (according to Vopa-<BR>deva also) cl. 10. P. स्यमयति, &c., to sound, cry<BR>aloud, shout, vociferate; to go, (in Naigh. II. 14.<BR>enumerated among the गति-कर्माणः); cl. 10. A.<BR>स्यामयते (sometimes also P. -ति), to consider,<BR>reflect, think: Caus. स्यमयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>असिस्यमत्, to cause to sound: Desid. सिस्यमिषति:<BR>Intens. सेसिम्यते (Pāṇ. VI. 1, 19), संस्यन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमिक|स्यमिकः
स्यमिक = स्यमीक below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमित्वा
स्यमित्वा, ind. having sounded; having gone, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमीक|स्यमीकः
स्यमीक, अस्, m. a cloud; an ant-hill; a kind of<BR>tree; time; (आ), f. indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यान्त
स्यान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded; gone, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यान्त्वा
स्यान्त्वा, ind. = स्यमित्वा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमन्तक|स्यमंतक|स्यमंतकः|स्यमन्तकः
स्यमन्तक स्यमन्तक, अस्, m. the jewel<BR>worn by Kṛṣṇa (given to Satrā-jit by the Sun and<BR>transferred by him to his brother Prasena, from<BR>whom it was taken by Jāmbavat, and after much<BR>fighting and contention appropriated by Kṛṣṇa;<BR>the whole story is told in Viṣṇu-Purāṇa IV. 13;<BR>the jewel is described as yielding daily eight loads of<BR>gold and preserving from all dangers; it is said to<BR>have been worn by Kṛṣṇa on his wrist, that on<BR>his breast being called Kaustubha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्या
स्या स्या, fem. of the pronoun त्यद् = तद्,<BR>‘he,’ ‘that,’ &c., (nom. c. masc. स्यस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यात्
स्यात् स्यात्, ind. (properly 3rd sing. Pot.<BR>of rt. 1. अस्), it may be, perhaps, perchance, (स्याद्<BR>अस्ति, it may be, perhaps it is; स्यान् नास्ति, it may<BR>not be.)<BR>—स्याद्-वाद, अस्, m. (probably) assertion<BR>of possibility (in phil.).<BR>—स्याद्वाद-मञ्जरी, f.,<BR>N. of a philosophical work classed under the Ārhata-<BR>darśana in the Sarva-darśana-saṅgraha.<BR>—स्याद्वाद-<BR>वादिन्, ई, m., N. of an Arhat.<BR>—स्याद्-वादिन्, ई, m.<BR>one who asserts possibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याल|स्यालः
स्याल स्याल, अस्, m. (according to Yāska<BR>on Nirukta VI. 9. fr. स्य, a winnowing basket, and<BR>ला for लाजा, fried grains, it being the custom for the<BR>bride's brother to scatter fried grains at marriage<BR>ceremonies), the brother of a bride, a wife's brother;<BR>the favourite of a king; a proper N.; (ई), f. a wife's<BR>sister, (also written श्याल); [cf. Gr. ἀέλιοι.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्युम्न
स्युम्न स्युम्न, अम्, n. (a doubtful form,<BR>but probably fr. rt. सिव्; cf. द्युम्न, fr. rt. 2. दिव्,<BR>and see स्यूम below), happiness, joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूत|स्यूतः
स्यूत स्यूत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. सिव्), sewn<BR>with a needle, stitched, woven; sewn or woven toge-<BR>ther, joined, fabricated; pierced, penetrated; (अस्),<BR>m. a bag, sack; coarse canvas bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूति|स्यूतिः
स्यूति, इस्, f. sewing with a needle, stitching, join-<BR>ing together, weaving; needle-work; a bag, sack;<BR>lineage, family, offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूत्वा
स्यूत्वा, ind. having sewed or joined together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यून|स्यूनः
स्यून, अस्, m. a sack, bag of coarse cloth; a ray<BR>of light; the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योत|स्योतः
स्योत, अस्, m. a bag, sack, bag of coarse canvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योन|स्योनः
स्योन, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. स्यूम below], beautiful,<BR>pleasing, favourable, propitious, auspicious; (अस्),<BR>m. a sack, coarse bag; a ray of light; the sun;<BR>(अम्), n. happiness, pleasure (= सुख, Naigh. III.<BR>6).<BR>—स्योन-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. one who causes hap-<BR>piness (to guests), a hospitable person, (Sāy. = अति-<BR>थीनां सुख-कारिन्, Ṛg-veda I. 31, 15.)<BR>—स्योन-<BR>शी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. lying or resting in a happy or<BR>pleasant place (i. e. in a sacrificial chamber; applied<BR>in Ṛg-veda I. 73, 1. to Agni, and according to<BR>Sāy. = गार्हपत्यायतने शयानः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूम|स्यूमं|स्यूमः
स्यूम स्यूम, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>1. 143. fr. rt. सिव्), a ray of light; (अम्), n. a ray<BR>of light; water (according to Śabda-k.); happiness,<BR>pleasure (Ved., cf. सुम्न).<BR>—स्यूम-गभस्ति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. having pleasing or happy rays, (Sāy. =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">Page1155-b+ 76</a>]<BR>सुख-रश्मि or स्यूत-रश्मि, Ṛg-veda VII. 71,<BR>3.)<BR>—स्यूम-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, having happy rays;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi under the protection of the<BR>Aśvins (author of the hymns Ṛg-veda X. 77, 78).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूमक
स्यूमक, अम्, n., Ved. happiness, pleasure (=<BR>सुख, Naigh. III. 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूमन्
स्यूमन्, (according to some) anything woven<BR>or connected, a web, (but according to Sāy. स्यूमना<BR>= स्यूमानि or अनुस्यूतानि or सन्ततानि, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 113, 17.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूमन्यु
स्यूमन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desiring happiness,<BR>(Sāy. = सुखम् इच्छत् or सतत-गामिन्, going<BR>continuously, Ṛg-veda I. 174, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस्
स्रंस् 1. स्रंस् (sometimes written स्रंश्),<BR>cl. 1. A. स्रंसते, सस्रंसे, स्रंसिष्-<BR>यते, अस्रंसिष्ट or अस्रसत् (Pāṇ. I. 3, 91, III.<BR>1, 55), स्रंसितुम्, to fall, fall down, drop, slip,<BR>slip down or off, tumble; to fall asunder; to hang<BR>down; to go (according to Naigh. II. 14): Pass.<BR>स्रस्यते, Aor. अस्रंसि: Caus. स्रंसयति, &c.,<BR>Aor. असस्रंसत्, to cause to fall or slip down;<BR>cause to move, loosen; to move, disturb: Desid.<BR>सिस्रंसिषते: Intens. सनीस्रस्यते, सनीस्रंस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस|स्रंसः
स्रंस, अस्, m. falling, slipping, fracture; [cf.<BR>परुः-स्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसन|स्रंसनं
स्रंसन, अम्, n. the act of falling or causing to<BR>fall, bringing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसमान
स्रंसमान, अस्, आ, अम्, falling, dropping, falling<BR>down, slipping off; fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसित
स्रंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to fall or slip down,<BR>loosened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसित्वा
स्रंसित्वा, ind. having fallen, having slipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिन्
स्रंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling down, slipping down,<BR>hanging down, depending, pendulous; being loos-<BR>ened; (ई), m. the Pīlu tree.<BR>—स्रंसिनी-फल, अस्,<BR>m. the Śirīṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्
स्रस्, त्, त्, त्, falling, dropping (at the end of comps.;<BR>see also वि-स्रस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्त|स्रस्तं
स्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen, dropped, fallen down,<BR>slipped off, fallen from; hanging down; loosened;<BR>let go, relaxed; separated.<BR>—स्रस्त-कर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having trunks hanging down or dangling.<BR>—स्रस्त-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, relaxing the grasp,<BR>letting go the hold.<BR>—स्रस्ताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ<BR>or ई, अम्, having the limbs relaxed; swooning,<BR>fainting.<BR>—स्रस्तोत्तर-पट (˚त-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the upper garment slipped down or loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तर|स्रस्तरः
स्रस्तर, अम्, n. (probably fr. rt. 1. स्रंस्), a<BR>couch or sofa for reclining (placed on the top of a<BR>house or terrace, see Manu II. 204, = शयनार्था-<BR>सनादि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्ति|स्रस्तिः
स्रस्ति, इस्, f. falling, slipping; a slip; loosening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्त्वा
स्रस्त्वा, ind. having fallen, having slipped or<BR>tumbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस्
स्रंस् 2. स्रंस्, a various reading for rt.<BR>श्रम्भ्, q. v. (and said to be used प्र-<BR>मादे or, according to another reading, प्रसादे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंह्
स्रंह् स्रंह् [cf. rt. श्रम्भ्], cl. 1. A.<BR>स्रंहते, &c., to confide, trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रक्व
स्रक्व स्रक्व (= सृक्वन्, q. v.), Ved. the<BR>corner of the mouth, the mouth, jaws; the flame of<BR>fire, (Sāy. = ज्वाला, Ṛg-veda VIII. 72, 15); (आ), f.<BR>the part about the lips, (Sāy. = ओष्ठ-देश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रक्ति|स्रक्तिः
स्रक्ति, (according to some) a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रङ्क्
स्रङ्क् स्रङ्क् = rt. श्रङ्क्, p. 1023, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्
स्रज् स्रज्, क्, f. (fr. rt. 1. सृज्), a chaplet,<BR>wreath of flowers, garland worn on the head; any<BR>garland or string of flowers, (औदकी स्रक्, Ved. a<BR>watery garland, i. e. one woven with water-flowers);<BR>a species of the Ati-śakvarī metre.<BR>—स्रग्-दामन्,<BR>अ, n. the fillet or tie of a garland.<BR>—स्रग्-धर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a garland; (आ), f. a species of<BR>the Prakṛti metre (a stanza of four lines of twenty-<BR>one syllables, each line being divided into three<BR>portions of seven syllables each).<BR>—स्रग्-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessed of garlands, wearing a wreath.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">Page1155-c+ 73</a>]<BR>—स्रग्-विन्, ई, इणी, इ, garlanded, wearing a garland,<BR>bearing a chaplet; (इणी), f., N. of a goddess; a<BR>species of the Jagatī metre (consisting of four times<BR>¯˘¯¯˘¯¯˘¯¯˘¯).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रजय
स्रजय (fr. स्रग्विन्), Nom. P. स्रजयति,<BR>यितुम्, to garland, i. e. furnish with a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रजिष्ठ|स्रजिष्ठः
स्रजिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. fr. स्रग्विन्),<BR>completely covered with garlands, profusely deco-<BR>rated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रजीयस्
स्रजीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. fr. स्रग्विन्),<BR>well covered with garlands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्वा
स्रज्वा स्रज्वा, f. (probably fr. rt. 1. सृज्),<BR>a rope, cord, string (according to Śabda-k. = रज्जु,<BR>q. v.); = तन्तु-पट-सङ्घात; N. of Prajā-pati, (in<BR>this sense given as fem. by Śabda-k.; perhaps fr. a<BR>form स्रज्वन्; cf. यज्वन्, fr. यज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रद्धू
स्रद्धू स्रद्धू, ऊस्, f. (better written श्रद्-<BR>धू and derived fr. rt. शृध्, q. v.), breaking wind<BR>downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रम्भ्|स्रंभ्
स्रम्भ् स्रम्भ् = rt. श्रम्भ्, q. v.; [cf.<BR>वि-स्रम्भ्, विस्रब्ध, वि-स्रम्भ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रव|स्रवः
स्रव स्रव, स्रवण. See p. 1156, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रष्टृ
स्रष्टृ स्रष्टृ, टा, m. (fr. rt. 1. सृज्), a<BR>creator; a maker, author; N. of Brahmā; of Śiva.<BR>—स्रष्टृ-ता, f. or स्रष्टृ-त्व, अम्, n. creator-<BR>ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्
स्रस् स्रस्, स्रस्त, &c. See under rt. 1. स्रंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राक्
स्राक् स्राक्, ind. (probably fr. rt. सृ + अञ्च्;<BR>cf. द्राक्), quickly, speedily, instantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राम
स्राम स्राम, अस्, m. (according to some fr.<BR>rt. स्रु), Ved. a sick man, (Sāy. = व्याधित or वि-<BR>श्लिष्टाङ्ग; cf. अ-स्˚), disease, sickness, (Sāy. =<BR>व्याधि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राव|स्रावः
स्राव स्राव, स्रावक. See p. 1156, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिध्
स्रिध् 1. स्रिध्, cl. 1. P. A. स्रेधति, -ते,<BR>&c., Ved. to assail, injure, ruin, destroy;<BR>to perish; cl. 6. P. A. स्रिधति, -ते, &c., Ved. to<BR>perish, be injured; [cf. Lat. stlis, lis; Old Germ.<BR>stritan, strit; Angl. Sax. stridh.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिध्
2. स्रिध्, त्, f., Ved. injury, distress, suffering, (Sāy.<BR>= दुःख); battle; (त्), m. an enemy, (Sāy. =<BR>शोषयितृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेधत्
स्रेधत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, injuring, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिभ्
स्रिभ् स्रिभ् or स्रिम्भ्, cl. 1. P. स्रेभति,<BR>स्रिम्भति, &c., to hurt, injure, kill (=<BR>rt. सृभ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिम
स्रिम स्रिम, अस्, m., Ved. (probably) a kind<BR>of evil spirit, (Atharva-veda VIII. 6, 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिव्
स्रिव् स्रिव्, cl. 4. P. स्रीव्यति, सिस्रेव,<BR>स्रेवितुम्, to go; to become dry: Caus.<BR>स्रेवयति, -यितुम्, to make dry, dry up: Desid.<BR>सिस्रेविषति, सुस्र्यूषति: Intens. सेस्रीव्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रूत
स्रूत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone; dried, become dry,<BR>(Pāṇ. VI. 4, 20.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रूत्वा
स्रूत्वा, ind. = स्रेवित्वा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेवयत्
स्रेवयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. making dry, drying<BR>up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेवित्वा
स्रेवित्वा, ind. having gone; having become dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रु|स्रुः
स्रु स्रु (incorrectly written श्रु, see rt.<BR>2. श्रु), cl. 1. P. स्रवति (ep. rarely A. -ते),<BR>सुस्राव (1st du. सुस्रुव), स्रोष्यति, असुस्रुवत्,<BR>स्रोतुम् (Ved. Inf. स्रवितवे, स्रवितवै), to flow,<BR>stream, trickle, ooze, drip, drop, distil, exude; to<BR>move, go; to let flow, shed (with acc.); to trickle<BR>away, slip away, waste away, perish; to flow from<BR>(with abl.); to be diffused or spread about, trans-<BR>pire: Caus. स्रावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असुस्रवत् or<BR>असिस्रवत्, to cause to flow, pour out, shed, effuse,<BR>spill: Desid. of Caus. सुस्रावयिषति or सिस्राव-<BR>यिषति: Desid. सुस्रूषति: Intens. सोस्रूयते,<BR>सोस्रोति; [cf. Gr. ῥέ-ω (for σρεϝω), ῥεύ-σω, ἐ-ῤῤύη-ν,<BR>ῥέ-ος, ῥό-ο-ς, ῥεῦ-μα, ῥο-ή, ῥύ-σι-ς, ῥεῦ-σι-ς, ῥυ-τό-ς,<BR>ῥευσ-τό-ς, ῥέ-ε-θρο-ν, ῥύ-αξ, ῥύ-μη,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">Page1156-a+ 80</a>]<BR>ῥυ-θ-μό-ς, Στρύμων: Lat. riv-u-s, Rumo, rumen, Ru-<BR>mina: Old Germ. strou-m, sliu-mo, ‘quickly;’<BR>sliumor, ‘quicker:’ Mod. Germ. schleunig: Lith.<BR>srav-j-u, ‘to flow;’ srov-e: Slav. s-t-ru-ja, o-s-t-<BR>rovu, ‘an island:’ Hib. sruth, ‘stream.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रव|स्रवः
स्रव, अस्, m. flowing, streaming, dropping,<BR>trickling, oozing; a drop; a spring, fountain, torrent;<BR>(आ), f. the Mūrvā plant.<BR>—स्रव-द्रङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>‘moving town,’ a fair, market, bazaar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवक
स्रवक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, flowing, dropping, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवण|स्रवणं
स्रवण, अम्, n. the act of flowing, streaming,<BR>trickling, oozing; sweat, perspiration; urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवत्
स्रवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, flowing, streaming, oozing,<BR>dripping, dropping, distilling; (अन्), m., Ved. a<BR>stream; (अन्ती), f. a stream, river, (in Naigh. I. 13.<BR>स्रवन्त्यः is enumerated among the नदी-ना-<BR>मानि); the region of the spleen (sometimes called<BR>the left hypochondriac region); a particular drug or<BR>medicinal plant.<BR>—स्रवत्-स्वेदजल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>streaming with perspiration, perspiring profusely.<BR>—स्रवद्-गर्भा, f. a woman that miscarries; a<BR>cow miscarrying by accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवन्त
स्रवन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, flowing, dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राव|स्रावः
स्राव, अस्, m. flow, flowing, oozing, dripping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावक|स्रावकं
स्रावक, अस्, इका, अम्, causing to flow, letting<BR>flow, pouring out, shedding, exuding; (अम्), n.<BR>black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावण
स्रावण, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to flow, exuding;<BR>(ई), f. a kind of medicinal plant (= ऋद्धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राविन्
स्राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, flowing, streaming, fluid.<BR>—स्रावि-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, very watery, marshy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत्
स्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, flowing, &c. (at the end of comps.,<BR>see परि-स्रुत्, अमृत-स्रुत्, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत|स्रुतं
स्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, flowed, trickled, flowing, drop-<BR>ping, dripping, fluid; (आ), f. a kind of medicinal<BR>plant (= हिङ्गु-पत्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुति|स्रुतिः
स्रुति, इस्, f. flow, flowing, streaming, oozing,<BR>distilling; exudation, resin; a stream; (Ved.) a<BR>path, by-way, course, road, (Sāy. = मार्ग; in Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 88, 15. द्वे स्रुती अशृणवम् पित्रीणां<BR>देवानाम् उत is translated, ‘I have heard of two<BR>paths, that of the fathers and that of the gods.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुव|स्रुवः
स्रुव, अस्, आ, m. f. [cf. स्रुच्], a wooden ladle<BR>(of a semicircular shape with a double extremity, or<BR>two oval collateral excavations, used to pour ghee on<BR>the sacrificial fire, = 2. जुहू); a Soma ladle, Soma<BR>spoon; (आ), f. the Mūrvā plant; the tree Boswellia<BR>Thurifera.<BR>—स्रुव-हस्त, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—स्रुवा-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the plant or tree Fla-<BR>courtia Sapida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रू
स्रू, ऊस्, f. a sacrificial ladle (= स्रुव above);<BR>a spring, fountain, cascade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोत|स्रोतं|स्रोतः
स्रोत, अस्, m. = स्रोतस् below [cf. शुष्क-स्˚];<BR>(अम्), n. a stream (= स्रोतस् below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्
स्रोतस्, अस्, n. a natural stream of water, current,<BR>flow or course of water; a rapid stream, torrent; a<BR>stream or river or spring (in general); a wave;<BR>water, (in Naigh. I. 12. enumerated among the<BR>उदक-नामानि); the course or current of nutriment<BR>in the body, stream of life, (see ऊर्ध्व-स्˚, तिर्-<BR>यक्-स्˚); an organ of sense; [cf. 1. श्रोतस्.]<BR>—स्रोत-ईश, अस्, m. ‘lord of streams,’ the ocean.<BR>—स्रोतस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing a stream or<BR>current; (अती), f. a river.<BR>—स्रोतस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>having a stream or current; (इनी), f. a river.<BR>—स्रोतो-<BR>जव, अस्, m. rapidity of current.<BR>—स्रोतो-ऽञ्जन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘stream-collyrium,’ antimony (especially as a<BR>collyrium for the eyes, said to be produced in the<BR>river Yamunā, cf. यामुन).<BR>—स्रोतो-वह्, वाट्, f. a<BR>river (= स्रोतो-वहा below).<BR>—स्रोतो-वह, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, flowing like a stream or river; (आ), m. a river<BR>in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्य|स्रोतस्यः
स्रोतस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in a stream (Ved.);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Śiva; a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोत्य
स्रोत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. produced in a stream;<BR>(आ), f., Ved. a stream, current, river, (in Naigh. I.<BR>13. स्रोत्याः is enumerated among the नदी-ना-<BR>मानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्न|स्रुघ्नः
स्रुघ्न स्रुघ्न, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्नी
स्रुघ्नी, f. natron, (see स्रुग्-घ्नी under स्रुच्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रौघ्न|स्रौघ्नः
स्रौघ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, of or belonging to the<BR>country of Srughna, coming from Srughna; suited<BR>to Srughna; abounding in Srughna, abiding or staying<BR>in Srughna; going or leading to Srughna, looking<BR>toward Srughna (as a gate &c.); (अस्), m. an inha-<BR>bitant of Srughna; (अम्), n. the gate leading to<BR>Srughna, (Pāṇ. IV. 3, 86.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्
स्रुच् स्रुच्, क्, f. (connected with rt. स्रु and<BR>by some derived fr. स्रु + अञ्च्, cf. स्रुव, स्रू), a<BR>sort of wooden ladle used for pouring clarified butter<BR>on a sacrificial fire, (it ought to be made of Palāśa<BR>or Khadira wood.)<BR>—स्रुक्-प्रणालिका, f. the spout<BR>of a ladle.<BR>—स्रुग्-घ्नी, f. (probably fr. स्रुच् +<BR>घ्नी; but also spelt स्रुघ्नी), natron, alkali.<BR>—स्रुग्-<BR>दारु, उस्, m. the tree Flacourtia Sapida.<BR>—स्रुग्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having a ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुचय
स्रुचय, Nom. P. स्रुचयति = स्रुग्वन्तम्<BR>आचष्टे or करोति, (see Vopa-deva XXI. 14.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्य
स्रुच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in a sacrificial<BR>ladle, contained in a ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुप
स्रुप स्रुप. See स्तुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेक्
स्रेक् स्रेक् (also written श्रेक्, सेक्, स्वेक्),<BR>cl. 1. A. स्रेकते, सिस्रेके, स्रेकितुम्: Caus.<BR>स्रेकयति, Aor. असिस्रेकत्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रै
स्रै स्रै, cl. 4. P. स्रायति, &c. = rts. श्रै,<BR>श्रा, शै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व 1. स्व, अस्, आ, अम्, own, one's own, my<BR>own, thy own, his own, our own, &c. (according<BR>to the context; and in these senses frequently used<BR>at the beginning of comps.; when declined, स्व is<BR>generally treated as a pronominal, and follows सर्व,<BR>e. g. स्वस्मै dat. c. sing., स्वस्मात् abl. c. sing.,<BR>स्वस्मिन् loc. c. sing., but in abl. loc. sing. Nom.<BR>pl. it optionally follows शिव, e. g. तं स्वयम्-<BR>भूः स्वाद् आस्याद् असृजत्, him, the self-existent,<BR>created from his own mouth, Manu I. 94; when,<BR>however, स्व is used as a substantive, meaning<BR>‘kinsman’ and ‘property,’ it cannot be declined as<BR>a pronominal, but must necessarily follow the de-<BR>clension of शिव, e. g. स्वाः, one's own relations,<BR>प्रभूताः स्वाः, great riches), innate, native, natural,<BR>inherent, proper, peculiar, appropriate; belonging to<BR>one's own family or tribe; (अस्), m. self, one's own<BR>self, self-identity; the soul; N. of Viṣṇu; a kins-<BR>man, relative, relation, (Manu II. 109); (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. property, wealth, riches; (in algebra) plus or<BR>affirmative quantity; [cf. Zend hva, qa: Gr. ἑ, ϝε<BR>(for αϝε), σφέ (οὖ, οἴ, ἕ), ἑ-ό-ς, ὅ-ς, σφ-ό-ς, ἴ-διο-ς:<BR>Lat. se, suu-s: Goth. si-k, ‘self;’ sves, ‘own;’<BR>svesa, ‘property;’ sei-na (for svei-na), sve, svi in<BR>svi-kunths, ‘manifest:’ Old Germ. suâs, ‘own:’<BR>Angl. Sax. sin, swa: Lith. saw, sawa-s, sawa:<BR>Slav. sebje, sebe, svoi, svaja, svœ, svo-bodi, ‘free;’<BR>svo-boda, ‘liberty.’]<BR>—स्व-कम्पन, अस्, m. ‘self-<BR>moving,’ air, wind.<BR>—स्व-कर्म-कृत्, त्, m. doing<BR>one's own business, an independent workman.<BR>—स्व-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. one's own work, own business, own<BR>duty, peculiar or proper business.<BR>—स्व-कर्म-<BR>वश, अस्, आ, अम्, subject to (the consequences of)<BR>one's own acts.<BR>—स्व-कर्म-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>minding one's own business or duty.<BR>—स्व-कामिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, self-loving, selfish.<BR>—स्व-कार्य, अम्, n.<BR>one's own business or duty or function.<BR>—स्व-कार्य-<BR>सह, अस्, आ, अम्, able to do one's duty or effect<BR>one's own business.<BR>—स्व-कुटुम्ब, अम्, n. one's<BR>own household.<BR>—स्व-कुल, अम्, n. one's own<BR>family or race.<BR>—स्व-कुल-क्षय, अस्, m. ‘destroy-<BR>ing its own family,’ a fish.<BR>—स्व-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>self-performed, done or made by one's self.<BR>—स्व-<BR>क्षत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. possessing innate strength,<BR>self-powerful, innately strong.<BR>—स्व-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘gone to one's self,’ passing in one's own mind,<BR>spoken to one's self, apart, aside; (अम्), n. to one's<BR>self, aside (in theatrical language).<BR>—स्व-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, m. own womb; own embryo.<BR>—स्व-गुण-तस्,<BR>ind. from personal merit.<BR>—स्व-गुण-प्रकाशक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, proclaiming one's own merits, boast-<BR>ful.<BR>—स्व-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, self-defended, self-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-c" target="_blank">Page1156-c+ 81</a>]<BR>preserved; (आ), f. cowach; the sensitive plant (=<BR>लज्जालु).<BR>—स्व-गूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sponta-<BR>neously striving, (Sāy. = स्वयम्-उद्यत, Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 68, 4); self-flowing, spontaneously going (said<BR>of rivers; Sāy. = स्वयम् एव गामिन्, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>140, 13).<BR>—स्व-गृह, अम्, n. one's own house;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of bird, Loxia Philippensis.<BR>—स्व-<BR>ग्राम, अस्, m. one's own village.<BR>—स्व-चरण-<BR>पर्षद्, त्, f. a college or community of members<BR>of one's own Caraṇa or sect.<BR>—स्व-च्छन्द, अस्, m.<BR>one's own will, own choice, own fancy; independ-<BR>ence; (अस्, आ, अम्), self-willed, independent, un-<BR>controlled; spontaneous; uncultivated, wild; (अम्),<BR>ind. according to one's own will or choice or fancy,<BR>voluntarily, spontaneously, independently.<BR>—स्व-<BR>च्छन्दक, अस्, आ, अम्, = स्व-च्छन्द above.<BR>—स्वच्छन्द-चारिणी, f. ‘going about at will,’ a<BR>harlot.<BR>—स्वच्छन्द-तस्, ind. voluntarily.<BR>—स्वच्-<BR>छन्द-भैरव, N. of a work.<BR>—स्वच्छन्द-<BR>शाक्तागम (˚त-आग्˚) and स्वच्छन्द-सङ्ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m., N. of two works.<BR>—स्व-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>self-produced, self-born, produced in or by one's<BR>self; (अस्), m. a son; sweat, perspiration; (आ), f.<BR>a daughter; (अम्), n. blood.<BR>—स्व-जन, अस्, m.<BR>one's own people, own kindred, own family or<BR>household; a kinsman, connection.<BR>—स्वजनाय,<BR>Nom. A. स्वजनायते, -यितुम्, to become a relation.<BR>—स्व-जनावृत (˚न-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded<BR>or accompanied by one's own people.<BR>—स्व-जाति,<BR>इस्, f. own cast or tribe, own kind or species.<BR>—स्व-<BR>जातीय or स्व-जात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to one's<BR>own tribe or species.<BR>—स्व-ज्ञाति, इस्, f. one's own<BR>kindred or kin; (इस्), m. a kinsman.<BR>—स्वतः-<BR>प्रमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, self-proved, self-evident.<BR>—स्वतः-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, self-accomplished;<BR>self-proved, self-demonstrated.<BR>—स्व-तन्त्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, self-dependent, self-reliant, independent, free,<BR>self-willed, unrestrained, uncontrolled; no longer<BR>subject to parents, of age, full grown; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a mystical work.<BR>—स्वतन्त्र-ता, f. self-depend-<BR>ence, self-reliance, independence; wilfulness.<BR>—स्व-<BR>तन्त्र-वृत्ति, इस्, f. acting self-reliantly, independent<BR>action.<BR>—स्वतन्त्र-सार, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—स्व-तवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having power in<BR>one's self, having innate or peculiar power, very<BR>strong or powerful (said of the Maruts); having<BR>wealth in one's self, (Sāy. स्व-तवान्, nom. c.<BR>masc. = धन-वान्, Ṛg-veda IV. 2, 6; cf. Pāṇini<BR>VIII. 3, 11, VII. 1, 83); firmly rooted (said of a<BR>mountain).<BR>—स्व-तस्, ind. by one's self, in one's<BR>self, of one's self (applicable to any person, e. g.<BR>by himself, in himself, &c., by itself, in itself, of<BR>itself, &c.); own, peculiar.<BR>—स्वतस्-सिद्ध, see<BR>स्वतः-सिद्ध.<BR>—स्व-ता, f. = स्व-त्व, q. v.<BR>—स्व-<BR>त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, self-preserving; (अस्), m. a blind<BR>man.<BR>—स्व-त्व, अम्, n. ‘selfness,’ self-existence,<BR>independent being or condition; the state of relation<BR>to one's self; own right or property, ownership,<BR>proprietorship, proprietary right.<BR>—स्वत्व-निवृत्ति,<BR>इस्, f. cessation or loss of proprietary right.<BR>—स्वत्व-<BR>बोधन, अम्, n. declaration or proof of ownership.<BR>—स्वत्व-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having proprietary right;<BR>(आन्), m. an owner.<BR>—स्वत्व-व्यभिचारि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. uncertainty of ownership.<BR>—स्वत्व-व्यभिचारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, departing or deviating from ownership.<BR>—स्वत्व-हानि, इस्, f. loss of proprietary right, for-<BR>feiture of title.<BR>—स्वत्व-हेतु, उस्, m. ground or<BR>cause of proprietary right.<BR>—स्वत्वाभाव (˚व-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, m. non-existence of proprietary right.<BR>—स्वत्वावगम (˚व-अव्˚), अस्, m. determination<BR>or ascertainment of ownership.<BR>—स्वत्वास्पद (˚व-<BR>आस्˚), अम्, n. site of ownership, that in which any<BR>one has proprietorship.<BR>—स्वत्वास्पदी-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, become the subject of proprietary right.<BR>—स्व-<BR>त्वोत्पत्ति (˚व-उत्˚), इस्, f. the arising of proprietary<BR>right, origin of ownership.<BR>—स्व-दार, अस्, m. one's<BR>own wife.<BR>—स्वदार-निरत, अस्, आ, अम्, attached<BR>to one's wife, uxorious.<BR>—स्व-दुहितृ, ता, f. one's<BR>own daughter.<BR>—स्व-देश, अस्, m. own country,<BR>native country, home; one's own place, proper<BR>place.<BR>—स्वदेश-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born in one's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1157-a" target="_blank">Page1157-a+ 81</a>]<BR>country, a fellow-countryman, compatriot.<BR>—स्व-<BR>देश-परिधि, इस्, m. circumference of a circle of<BR>longitude in any place that has latitude.<BR>—स्वदेश-<BR>मध्य-परिधि, इस्, m. circumference of the ter-<BR>restrial equator.<BR>—स्व-देह-दान, अम्, n. the gift<BR>of one's own body.<BR>—स्व-धर्म, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>own right, own duty, peculiar duty or occupation,<BR>the duties of one's own class or caste (as defined<BR>in Manu I. 88 — 91), peculiar property, peculiarity.<BR>—स्वधर्म-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of one's<BR>rights, fallen from or neglecting one's duty.<BR>—स्व-<BR>धर्म-त्याग, अस्, m. dereliction or neglect of<BR>one's own duty; abandoning one's religion, apostasy.<BR>—स्वधर्म-स्खलन, अम्, n. falling from or<BR>neglect of one's own duty.<BR>—स्वधर्म-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, abiding in one's peculiar duty.<BR>—स्वधर्मा-<BR>चरण (˚म-आच्˚), अम्, n. the act of practising one's<BR>own duties.<BR>—स्वधर्मानपग (˚म-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, not swerving from one's duties.<BR>—स्वधर्-<BR>मार्थ-विनिश्चय, अस्, m. the knowing or ascer-<BR>taining one's duty and interests.<BR>—स्व-धा, see s.v.<BR>—स्व-नगर, अम्, n. one's own town, native city.<BR>—स्व-नामन्, अ, n. one's own name.<BR>—स्वना-<BR>माङ्क (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, marked with one's<BR>own name, called after one's own name.<BR>—स्व-नाश,<BR>अस्, m. self-destruction.<BR>—स्व-पक्ष, अस्, m. one's<BR>own side, own party; ‘being on one's own side,’ a<BR>friend.<BR>—स्व-पर-मण्डल, अम्, n. one's own<BR>and an enemy's country.<BR>—स्व-पिण्डा, f. a kind of<BR>date tree (= पिण्ड-खर्जूरी).<BR>—स्व-पितृ, ता, m.<BR>one's own father; (तरस्), m. pl. one's ancestors.<BR>—स्व-पुत्र-वत्, ind. like one's own children.<BR>—स्व-पू, see s.v.<BR>—स्व-पोषम्, ind. according<BR>to the nurture or training practised by one's own<BR>kindred.<BR>—स्व-प्रकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, self-resplendent,<BR>self-luminous, self-evident.<BR>—स्व-प्रधान-ता, f.<BR>one's own nature or natural condition.<BR>—स्व-प्र-<BR>भु-ता, f. own power or supremacy, (स्व-प्रभु-<BR>तया, inst. c. by one's own power, arbitrarily.)<BR>—स्व-<BR>प्रयोगात्, ind. through the application of one's own<BR>efforts, by means of one's own exertions.<BR>—स्व-<BR>प्रयोजन-वश, अस्, m. the force of one's own ob-<BR>ject or purpose.<BR>—स्व-बलाश्रय (˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, depending on one's own strength.<BR>—स्व-बान्-<BR>धव, अस्, m. one's own relation.<BR>—स्व-बाहु, उस्,<BR>m. one's own arm.<BR>—स्वबाहु-बल, अम्, n. strength<BR>of one's own arm.<BR>—स्व-ब्राह्मण्या, f. the text<BR>called Sva-brāhmaṇyā (used for invoking Indra in<BR>the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice, Manu IX. 126).<BR>—स्व-<BR>भट, अस्, m. one's own warrior, body-guard.<BR>—स्व-<BR>भाजन, अम्, n. (probably for सभाजन, q. v.),<BR>civility, polite greeting, welcome, adieu.<BR>—स्व-भानु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. self-luminous, self-shining.<BR>—स्व-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. own state, essential or inherent pro-<BR>perty, innate or peculiar disposition, natural state or<BR>constitution, nature; peculiar purpose or aim.<BR>—स्व-<BR>भाव-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by natural disposition,<BR>innate, natural.<BR>—स्वभाव-तस्, ind. from natural<BR>disposition, by nature, naturally.<BR>—स्वभाव-दौर्-<BR>जन्य, अम्, n. natural or innate wickedness.<BR>—स्व-<BR>भाव-द्वेष, अस्, m. natural hatred.<BR>—स्वभाव-<BR>वाद, अस्, m. the doctrine that the universe was pro-<BR>duced and is sustained by the natural and necessary<BR>action of substances according to their inherent pro-<BR>perties.<BR>—स्वभाव-वादिन्, ई, m. one who maintains<BR>the above doctrine.<BR>—स्वभाव-शूर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing natural heroes.<BR>—स्वभाव-सिद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, accomplished by one's own nature, natural,<BR>essential, spontaneous, not acquired.<BR>—स्वभावोक्त<BR>(˚व-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, uttered or said naturally, de-<BR>clared spontaneously.<BR>—स्वभावोक्ति (˚व-उक्˚), इस्,<BR>f. spontaneous declaration, description of natural pe-<BR>culiarities or properties.<BR>—स्व-भू, ऊस्, m. ‘self-ex-<BR>istent,’ N. of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of Brahmā; (ऊस्), f.<BR>one's own land, own country.<BR>—स्वभू-त्याग, अस्,<BR>m. abandonment of one's country, abdication of one's<BR>own territory.<BR>—स्व-भूत्य्-ओजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>whose energy is derived from inherent power.<BR>—स्व-<BR>भूमि, इस्, f. one's own land, own estate; native<BR>country, fatherland.<BR>—स्व-माया, f. own cunning,<BR>own magical art or skill, own art.<BR>—स्व-यत, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1157-b" target="_blank">Page1157-b+ 81</a>]<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. self-guided.<BR>—स्व-यत्न, अस्, m. one's<BR>own exertion, own effort.<BR>—स्व-यशस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. self-famous, deriving renown from one's self,<BR>having peculiar fame.<BR>—स्वयशस्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. more renowned, very famous.<BR>—स्व-यावन्, आ,<BR>&c., Ved. self-moving, (in Ṛg-veda VIII. 25, 12.<BR>the voc. c. स्व-यावन् is applied to Sindhu or the<BR>Ocean; according to Sāy. the nom. c. is स्व-यावान्.)<BR>—स्व-युक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. self-yoked, self-har-<BR>nessed.<BR>—स्व-योनि, इस्, m. f. own womb, one's own<BR>place of birth; (इस्, इस्, इ), nearly related, related on<BR>the mother's side; (इस्), f. a sister or near female<BR>relative.<BR>—स्व-रस, अस्, m. natural or peculiar<BR>flavour; proper taste or sentiment in composition; a<BR>particular kind of astringent juice or decoction; the<BR>sediment of oily substances ground on a stone.<BR>—स्व-राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. self-resplendent, self-lumi-<BR>nous, shining of one's self (said of the Aśvins, Indra,<BR>Mitra, and Varuṇa); (ट्), m. the supreme Being<BR>(Brahman); N. of one of the seven principal rays<BR>of the sun (supposed to supply heat to the planet<BR>Saturn); a kind of metre used in the Vedas (de-<BR>scribed as a stanza of three lines, two containing<BR>eight syllables each, and one ten); a variety of the<BR>same metre containing four lines (probably fem. in<BR>this sense).<BR>—स्व-राज्य, अम्, n., Ved. independent<BR>dominion or sovereignty.<BR>—स्व-राष्ट्र, अम्, n.<BR>one's own country or kingdom; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people (also read सु-राष्ट्र).<BR>—स्व-रुचि, इस्, f.<BR>one's own taste or inclination, own wish; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>following one's own likings or desires, self-willed,<BR>uncontrolled, wilful.<BR>—स्व-रुह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, self-growing,<BR>self-increasing.<BR>—स्व-रूप, अम्, n. one's own form<BR>or shape, natural state or condition, essential pro-<BR>perties; natural character or appearance, true consti-<BR>tution or purpose; peculiar aim; nature; species,<BR>kind, sort; a particular relation (in phil., see under<BR>सम्-बन्ध); (अस्, आ or ई, अम्), having one's own<BR>form or character, having a like nature or character;<BR>similar, like, identical; pleasing, handsome; wise,<BR>learned; (आ), f., N. of a place.<BR>—स्वरूप-गत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, endowed with one's own form or nature,<BR>having a like character.<BR>—स्वरूप-तस्, ind. accord-<BR>ing to one's own form, analogously, similarly, iden-<BR>tically.<BR>—स्वरूप-ता, f. or स्वरूप-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the having a natural form or state; identity of form<BR>or nature; handsomeness.<BR>—स्वरूप-धारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, possessing a natural form or character, having<BR>one's own form.<BR>—स्वरूप-सम्बोधन, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—स्वरूपासिद्धि (˚प-अस्˚), इस्, f. a<BR>form of A-siddhi or fallacious proof (where the nature<BR>or property alleged is not really proved to belong to<BR>the subject).<BR>—स्व-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having one's<BR>own form or character; having essential properties;<BR>identical.<BR>—स्व-रोचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or स्व-रोचिस्, इस्,<BR>इस्, इस्, self-shining.<BR>—स्व-लक्षण, अम्, n. peculiar<BR>characteristic or property.<BR>—स्व-लीन, अस्, m. (per-<BR>haps for स्वर्-लीन), N. of a Dānava (mentioned in<BR>the Vahni-Purāṇa).<BR>—स्व-वंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, belong-<BR>ing to one's own family.<BR>—स्व-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. possessing property, wealthy, opulent, (accord-<BR>ing to some स्ववान् is wrongly separated into स्व-<BR>वान्, and is rather nom. case masc. of स्व्-अवस्, q. v.;<BR>cf. Pāṇ. VII. 1, 83; cf. स्व-तवस्.)<BR>—स्व-वर्ग्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to one's own tribe.<BR>—स्व-<BR>वश, अस्, आ, अम्, subject to one's own will, self-sub-<BR>dued, self-controlled; ruled by one's free will, in-<BR>dependent.<BR>—स्व-वशिनी, f. a kind of metre (con-<BR>sisting of thirty-eight syllables).<BR>—स्व-वहित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, self-impelled, self-moved; alert, active.<BR>—स्व-<BR>वाञ्छा, f. one's own desire, (स्व-वाञ्छया, accord-<BR>ing to one's own wish.)<BR>—स्व-वार्त्त, अम्, n. one's<BR>own condition or welfare.<BR>—स्व-वासिनी, f. a woman<BR>whether married or unmarried who continues to<BR>dwell after maturity in her father's house.<BR>—स्व-<BR>विनाश, अस्, m. self-destruction, suicide.<BR>—स्व-विष-<BR>य, अस्, m. one's own country, own home.<BR>—स्व-<BR>वीज, अम्, n. own seed, own cause; (अस्), m. the<BR>soul.<BR>—स्व-वीर्य-तस्, ind. according to one's power.<BR>—स्व-वृक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. self-cleansing, having<BR>cleansing properties; (इस्), f. a hymn.<BR>—स्व-वृज्, क्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1157-c" target="_blank">Page1157-c+ 81</a>]<BR>क्, क्, Ved. self-cutting, (Sāy. = स्वयं छेत्तृ, Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 38, 5.)<BR>—स्व-वृत्त, अम्, n. one's own<BR>business or occupation.<BR>—स्व-वृत्ति, इस्, f. one's own<BR>peculiar occupation or means of subsistence; (इस्, इस्,<BR>इ), subsisting by one's own exertions.<BR>—स्व-वृष्टि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. rain-appropriating, the appropriator of<BR>rain.<BR>—स्व-शरीर, अम्, n. one's own body, own<BR>person.<BR>—स्व-संवृत, अस्, आ, अम्, self-concealed,<BR>self-covered, self-guarded, self-secured.<BR>—स्व-सं-<BR>स्था, f. self-abiding, self-staying, self-possession, ab-<BR>sorption in one's own self.<BR>—स्व-सदृश, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>like one's self.<BR>—स्व-सर, see s.v.<BR>—स्व-सृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, moving or advancing by one's self, going or<BR>moving at one's own will, moving freely or inde-<BR>pendently.<BR>—स्व-सैन्य, अम्, n. one's own army.<BR>—स्व-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, self-staying, self-abiding,<BR>self-possessed, relying upon one's self, confident, re-<BR>solute, firm, composed; self-sufficient, independent;<BR>contented; well, healthy, comfortable, at ease, in<BR>health; (अम्), ind. composedly.<BR>—स्वस्थ-ता, f.<BR>self-possession, well-being, health.<BR>—स्व-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. one's own place, own home.<BR>—स्वस्थान-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing in or occupying one's own<BR>condition.<BR>—स्व-स्वधास्, m. pl., N. of a particular<BR>class of Manes, (see स्व-धा.)<BR>—स्व-हस्त, अस्, m.<BR>one's own hand; own handwriting, autograph, signa-<BR>ture.<BR>—स्व-हस्त-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen into one's<BR>own hand.<BR>—स्व-हस्तिका, f. (probably) an axe (also<BR>read सु-हस्तिका).<BR>—स्व-हस्तोल्लिखित (˚त-उल्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, drawn or painted by one's own hand.<BR>—स्व-<BR>हित, अस्, आ, अम्, good or advantageous for one's<BR>self; (अम्), n. one's own advantage, own benefit,<BR>own welfare.<BR>—स्व-हितैषिन् (˚त-एष्˚), ई, इणी, इ,<BR>seeking one's own good or advantage.<BR>—स्व-हेतु,<BR>उस्, m. one's own cause, own sake, (स्व-हेतुना, for<BR>one's own sake.)<BR>—स्वाकार (स्व-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or स्वाकृति (स्व-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having one's own<BR>form.<BR>—स्वाक्ष-पाद (स्व-अक्˚), अस्, m. a follower<BR>of the Nyāya system of philosophy, a Naiyāyika.<BR>—स्वाक्षर (स्व-अक्˚), अस्, m. (according to Śab-<BR>da-k.) one's own handwriting or signature.<BR>—२. स्वा-<BR>गत (स्व-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, come of one's self; (for<BR>1. स्व्-आगत see p. 1126.)<BR>—स्वाङ्ग (स्व-अङ्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a limb of the body (Vopa-deva IV. 17); (अस्), m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—स्वाङ्गि, a patronymic from Svāṅga,<BR>(Vopa-deva VII. 1, 4.)<BR>—स्वाधिकार (स्व-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. own office or function, peculiar station.<BR>—स्वा-<BR>धिपत्य (स्व-अध्˚), अम्, n. own supremacy, su-<BR>preme sway, royalty, sovereignty.<BR>—स्वादिष्ठान<BR>(स्व-अध्˚), अम्, n. one of the six Cakras or mys-<BR>tical circles of the body, (see चक्र.)<BR>—स्वाधीन<BR>(स्व-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, self-subject, self-dependent;<BR>independent, uncontrolled; in one's own power or<BR>subjection, dependent on or belonging to one's own<BR>side or party, one's own subject or dependent,<BR>faithful.<BR>—स्वाधीन-कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>prosperity in one's own power.<BR>—स्वाधीन-ता, f. or<BR>स्वाधीन-त्व, अम्, n. self-dependence, independ-<BR>ence; subjection to one's self.<BR>—स्वाधीन-पतिका<BR>or स्वाधीन-भर्तृका, f. a woman who has a hus-<BR>band subject to herself or dependent on herself, an<BR>independent woman.<BR>—स्वाध्याय (स्व-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘going over any subject to one's self,’ self-recit-<BR>ing, self-reading, repeating or rehearsing to one's self,<BR>inaudible reading or muttering of prayers, private<BR>prayer, (especially) repetition or study of the Vedas,<BR>sacred study; perusal of sacred books; the Veda; a<BR>day on which the resumption of sacred study is com-<BR>manded after a suspension of it.<BR>—स्वाध्याय-ब्राह्-<BR>मण, अम्, n., N. of a chapter in the Taittirīyāra-<BR>ṇyaka (ascribed to Kaṭha).<BR>—स्वाध्याय-वत्, आन्,<BR>m. a student of the Vedas.<BR>—स्वाध्यायार्थिन् (˚य-<BR>अर्˚), ई, m. one who seeks a maintenance for him-<BR>self during his studentship, (Manu XI. 1.)<BR>—स्वा-<BR>ध्यायिन्, ई, m. one who recites or repeats to himself,<BR>(especially) a repeater or student of the Vedas; a<BR>tradesman, dealer.<BR>—स्वानुभव (स्व-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. one's own personal experience or observation.<BR>—स्वानुभूति (स्व-अन्˚), इस्, f. one's own experi-<BR>ence; self-enjoyment.<BR>—स्वानुभूत्य्-एक-सार (स्व-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, whose only essence consists in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-a" target="_blank">Page1158-a+ 81</a>]<BR>self-enjoyment.<BR>—स्वानुरूप (स्व-अन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>‘self-conformable,’ natural, innate.<BR>—१. स्वान्त (स्व-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. (for 2. see s. v.), ‘having the end in itself,’<BR>the mind (= मनस्); a cavern.<BR>—स्वान्यदीय-त्व<BR>(स्व-अन्˚), अम्, n. the state of being one's own or<BR>some one else's.<BR>—स्वान्यदीयत्व-सन्देह, अस्, m.<BR>doubt about ‘meum’ and ‘tuum.’<BR>—स्वायत्त (स्व-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, subject to one's self; uncontrolled<BR>by others, one's own master.<BR>—स्वायत्ती-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. -करोति, &c., to make subject to one's self.<BR>—स्वा-<BR>रुह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. = स्व-रुह्.<BR>—स्वार्जित (स्व-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, self-acquired, acquired by one's own<BR>efforts.<BR>—स्वार्थ (स्व-अर्˚), अस्, m. one's own ob-<BR>ject or aim or wish, own advantage or interest, self-<BR>interest; one's own property or substance; own<BR>meaning, inherent or real meaning, true interpreta-<BR>tion, similar meaning, a pleonasm; (according to<BR>Śabda-k.) = लिङ्गार्थ-विशेष; (अस्, आ, अम्), hav-<BR>ing one's own object or aim; self-interested; having<BR>or expressing [its] own inherent or true meaning,<BR>having a natural or literal meaning, having a similar<BR>meaning; pleonastic; (अम्), ind. on one's own ac-<BR>count.<BR>—स्वार्थ-पण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, clever in one's<BR>own affairs.<BR>—स्वार्थ-पर or स्वार्थ-परायण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, intent on one's own object or advantage,<BR>self-interested, selfish.<BR>—स्वार्थपर-ता, f. selfish-<BR>ness.<BR>—स्वार्थ-भ्रंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, injurious to<BR>one's own interests.<BR>—स्वार्थ-लिप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, de-<BR>sirous of gaining one's own object, self-seeking.<BR>—स्वार्थ-विघात, अस्, m. the frustration of one's<BR>object.<BR>—स्वार्थ-सिद्धि, इस्, f. accomplishment of<BR>one's object, attainment of a wish or desire.<BR>—स्वार्-<BR>थानुमान (˚थ-अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘inference for one's<BR>self,’ (in logic) a particular process of induction.<BR>—स्वार्थिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. स्वार्थ), having one's<BR>own object; having [its] own true and natural mean-<BR>ing, having a literal meaning; done with one's own<BR>wealth.<BR>—स्वार्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, pursuing one's own<BR>objects, self-seeking.<BR>—स्वार्थोपपत्ति (˚थ-उप्˚),<BR>इस्, f. the gaining or accomplishing of one's own ob-<BR>ject.<BR>—स्वाश्रित (स्व-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dependent on<BR>one's self.<BR>—स्वी-करण, &c., see col. 3.<BR>—स्वेच्-<BR>छा (स्व-इच्˚), f. one's own wish or will, own inclina-<BR>tion, self-will, wilfulness.<BR>—स्वेच्छाचार (˚छा-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m. acting as one likes, doing what is right in<BR>one's own eyes.<BR>—स्वेच्छा-तस्, ind. according to<BR>one's own will or inclination.<BR>—स्वेच्छाधीन (˚छा-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dependent on one's own will or<BR>inclination.<BR>—स्वेच्छा-मृत्यु, उस्, m. ‘dying at his<BR>own will,’ epithet of Bhīṣma (who had received<BR>from his father the power of fixing the time of his<BR>own death; see Mahā-bhārata, Bhīṣma-parvan 5674).<BR>—स्वेच्छाहार (˚छा-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, eating any-<BR>thing at one's pleasure.<BR>—स्वेच्छाहार-विहार, अस्,<BR>m. feeding and roaming about according to one's in-<BR>clination.<BR>—स्वेदु-हव्य (स्व-इद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>probably = स्व-समृद्ध-हविष्क, (see Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 121, 6, where the word इदु is referred<BR>either to rt. इन्द् or rt. इन्ध्.)<BR>—स्वेष्ट (स्व-इष्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, self-desired, wished for.<BR>—स्वोक्त (स्व-<BR>उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, spoken by one's self, (स्वोक्तम्<BR>आक्षिपति, he corrects his own previous remark.)<BR>—स्वोदय (स्व-उद्˚), अस्, m. the rising of a sign<BR>or any heavenly body at any particular place (de-<BR>termined by adding to or deducting from the लङ्को-<BR>दय or time of rising at Ceylon).<BR>—स्वोपधि (स्व-<BR>उप्˚), इस्, m. self-support; (probably) a fixed star.<BR>—स्वोपार्जित (स्व-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, self-gained,<BR>self-acquired (as wealth &c.).<BR>—स्वौजस् (स्व-ओज्˚),<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, having natural or peculiar energy; (आस्),<BR>m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
2. स्व, Nom. P. स्वति, according to Vopa-deva<BR>XXI. 7. = स्व इवाचरति, he acts like himself, he<BR>acts like his kindred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक|स्वकं|स्वकः
स्वक, अस्, आ, or इका, अम्, own, one's own, proper,<BR>peculiar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीय|स्वकीयः
स्वकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, own, one's own; belonging<BR>to one's self, belonging to one's own family; (आ), f.<BR>one's own wife; [cf. स्वीया.]<BR>—स्वकीय-ता, f. owner-<BR>ship, one's own property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम्, ind. self, myself, himself, herself, itself,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-b" target="_blank">Page1158-b+ 81</a>]<BR>one's self, &c. (applicable to all persons and sometimes<BR>used emphatically with other pronouns, e. g. अहं<BR>स्वयम्, ‘I myself;’ sometimes used alone, e. g.<BR>स्वयं तत् कृतवान्, I or thou or he did that him-<BR>self; स्वयं तत् कृतवती, she did that herself;<BR>स्वयं तत् कुर्वन्ति, they do that themselves);<BR>by one's self, spontaneously, of one's own self, of<BR>one's own accord; [cf. Hib. feiñ, ‘own, self;’ sin,<BR>‘that, there;’ siom, ‘they, them:’ Cambro-Brit. hun,<BR>‘he himself.’]<BR>—स्वयं-वर, अस्, m. ‘self-choice,’<BR>the election of a husband by a princess or daughter<BR>of a Kṣatriya at a public assembly of suitors held<BR>for the purpose; (आ), f. a maiden who thus chooses<BR>her own husband.<BR>—स्वयंवर-कथा, f. the de-<BR>claration of a Svayaṃ-vara.<BR>—स्वयंवर-कृत-<BR>क्षण, आ, f. a maiden who has fixed the moment<BR>for a Svayaṃ-vara (see above).<BR>—स्वयं-वृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, self-chosen, selected by one's self.<BR>—स्वयं-<BR>शीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, self-fallen, dropped spontaneously.<BR>—स्वयं-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—स्व-<BR>यं-हारिका, f. ‘self-seizing,’ N. of a daughter of<BR>Nir-mārṣṭi (who was wife of Duḥsaha; she is de-<BR>scribed in the fifty-first chapter of the Mārkaṇḍeya-<BR>Purāṇa as exercising an evil influence on certain sub-<BR>stances, by abstracting, for example, the colour from<BR>saffron and the thread from cotton).<BR>—स्वयङ्-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, self-formed, self-made, natural, sponta-<BR>neous; self-done, done by one's self; done to or under-<BR>taken for one's self.<BR>—स्वयङ्-गुप्ता, f. ‘self-pre-<BR>served,’ cowach, Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR>—स्वयङ्-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, m. the taking for one's self (without leave).<BR>—स्वयङ्-ग्राह, अस्, आ, अम्, self-choosing, volun-<BR>tary.<BR>—स्वयञ्-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, self-born.<BR>—स्वयन्-<BR>दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, self-given; a child who has given<BR>himself to be adopted by adoptive parents (one of<BR>the twelve kinds of children recognised in law-<BR>books).<BR>—स्वयम्-अर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, self-acquired,<BR>gained by one's own efforts.<BR>—स्वयम्-आगत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, come of one's own accord.<BR>—स्वयम्-उक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. voluntary declaration; (in law) information, de-<BR>position.<BR>—स्वयम्-उपस्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, come<BR>voluntarily or of one's own accord.<BR>—स्वयम्-उपाग-<BR>त, अस्, आ, अम्, come of one's own accord; (अस्), m. a<BR>child who comes and offers himself voluntarily to an<BR>adoptive parent.<BR>—स्वयम्-प्रभ, अस्, m. ‘self-<BR>shining,’ N. of the fourth Arhat of the future Utsarpiṇī;<BR>(आ), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—स्वयम्-भु, उस्, m. ‘self-<BR>existent,’ Brahmā.<BR>—स्वयम्-भुव, अस्, m. ‘self-ex-<BR>isting,’ the first Manu; epithet of Brahmā; of Śiva; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of shrub (= धूम्र-पत्त्रा).<BR>—स्वयम्-<BR>भू, ऊस्, m. ‘self-existing,’ the Self-existent, Brahmā;<BR>Viṣṇu; Śiva; Kāla or time; Kāma-deva; a Jaina<BR>deified sage; N. of the third of the nine black Vāsu-<BR>devas; N. of certain plants (= माष-पर्णी; =<BR>लिङ्गिनी).<BR>—स्वयम्-भूत, अस्, m. ‘self-created,’<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—स्वयम्-भोज, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Yādava chief.<BR>—स्वयम्-मूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>self-curdled, coagulated (said of दधि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयु
स्वयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. possessed of opulence,<BR>wealthy, (Sāy. = धन-वत्, Ṛg-veda III. 45, 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापय
स्वापय (fr. 1. स्व), Nom. P. स्वापयति, &c.,<BR>(Vopa-deva XXI. 16.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिक
स्वामिक = स्वामिन्, at the end of an adj. comp.<BR>(e. g. प्रनष्ट-स्वामिक, whose master or owner<BR>is lost or unknown, i. e. not known whether he be<BR>alive or dead).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिन्
स्वामिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. 1. स्व with affix मिन्), possess-<BR>ing proprietary rights, owning; (ई), m. a proprietor,<BR>owner; a master, lord; a sovereign, king, monarch;<BR>a husband, lover; a spiritual preceptor; a learned<BR>Brāhman, an ascetic or religious man of the highest<BR>order (used as a title at the end of names, e. g.<BR>श्रीधर-स्वामिन्); N. of Kārttikeya; of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Śiva; of the Muni Vātsyāyana; of Garuḍa; of<BR>an Arhat of the past era; of several other persons;<BR>(इनी), f. a mistress, proprietress; (स्वामिन् at the end<BR>of a comp. has frequently the meaning of ‘a temple<BR>or shrine built by,’ ‘a temple in honour of,’ e. g.<BR>धर्म-स्˚, विष्णु-स्˚.)<BR>—स्वामि-कार्त्तिक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the Rāga-mālā.<BR>—स्वामि-कार्त्ति-<BR>केयानुप्रेक्षा (˚य-अन्˚), f., N. of a Jaina work by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">Page1158-c+ 80</a>]<BR>Jaya-candra.<BR>—स्वामि-कार्य, अम्, n. the business of<BR>a king or master.<BR>—स्वामि-कार्यार्थिन् (˚य-अर्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, desirous of or seeking a master's interests.<BR>—स्वामि-जङ्घिन्, ई, m., N. of Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—स्वामि-ता, f. or स्वामि-त्व, अम्, n. ownership,<BR>mastership; lordship, sovereignty, &c.<BR>—स्वामि-पाल,<BR>औ, m. du. the owner and the tender (of cattle, Manu<BR>VIII. 5).<BR>—स्वामि-पाल-विवाद, अस्, m. a dispute be-<BR>tween a master and the servant who tends his cattle.<BR>—स्वामि-भाव, अस्, m. the state or relation of a<BR>lord or owner.<BR>—स्वामि-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, originat-<BR>ing in or derived from a master or lord, depending<BR>on a master or husband.<BR>—स्वामि-वात्सल्य, अम्, n.<BR>affection for a lord or husband.<BR>—स्वामि-सद्-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. existence of a master or owner; amiability of<BR>a master or lord.<BR>—स्वामि-सेवा, f. the service of a<BR>master, respect for a master; reverence for or atten-<BR>tion to a husband.<BR>—स्वाम्य्-अर्थम्, ind. for a<BR>master's sake.<BR>—स्वाम्य्-असम्मत, अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>permitted by a master; one who has not obtained<BR>an owner's permission.<BR>—स्वाम्य्-उपकारक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘serviceable to an owner, benefiting a master,’<BR>a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्य|स्वाम्यं
स्वाम्य, अम्, n. mastership, lordship, ownership;<BR>right or title to property; rule, supremacy, dominion.<BR>—स्वाम्य-कारण, अम्, n. the cause of supremacy<BR>or lordship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाय
स्वाय, Nom. A. स्वायते according to Vopa-deva<BR>XXI. 7. = स्व इवाचरति, he acts like himself, he<BR>acts like his own kindred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विका
स्विका, f. See under स्वक, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विन्
स्विन् in शत-स्विन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरण|स्वीकरणं
स्वी-करण, अम्, n. making one's own, appropria-<BR>tion, adopting, taking, accepting, assenting, agreeing,<BR>assent, promise.<BR>—स्वीकरण-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>whose function is to appropriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरणीय
स्वी-करणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be appropriated; to<BR>be admitted or acknowledged or accepted; to be as-<BR>sumed; to be assented or agreed to; to be pro-<BR>mised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकर्तृ
स्वी-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who appropriates or<BR>accepts or admits, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकार|स्वीकारः
स्वी-कार, अम्, n. making one's own, taking on<BR>one's self, appropriation, adopting, assuming, assump-<BR>tion, claiming, claim; assent, agreement, consent;<BR>promise.<BR>—स्वीकार-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of<BR>assent, not agreed to.<BR>—स्वीकारान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ended or concluded by assent; agreed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकार्य
स्वी-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be admitted, to be as-<BR>sumed (in argument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृ
स्वी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make one's own,<BR>own, win, appropriate, claim; to take upon one's<BR>self; to adopt, admit, assume (in argument); to as-<BR>sent, agree to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृत
स्वी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, appropriated, owned, ac-<BR>cepted, admitted, acknowledged, adopted, claimed,<BR>agreed, assented to, promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृत्य
स्वी-कृत्य, ind. having agreed to or promised;<BR>having satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीय|स्वीयः
स्वीय, अस्, आ, अम्, own, relating or belonging to<BR>one's self, peculiar, characteristic; (आ), f. one's own<BR>wife, a faithful wife, one solely attached to her own<BR>husband; [cf. Gr. ἑός, αφέος, σφός.]<BR>—स्वीयाक्षर<BR>(˚य-अक्˚), अस्, m. one's own handwriting or signa-<BR>ture, autograph, (Śabda-k.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर, अस्, ई, अम् (probably fr. स्व + ईर, going;<BR>see rts. इर्, ईर्), going where one likes, following<BR>one's own fancy, self-willed, wilful, wanton, unre-<BR>strained, refractory; slow, lazy; dependent on will,<BR>voluntary, optional, unimportant; (अम्), n. wilful-<BR>ness; (अम्), ind. with one's own will or assent; of<BR>one's own accord.<BR>—स्वैर-ता, f. wilfulness, inde-<BR>pendence.<BR>—स्वैर-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, acting or liv-<BR>ing as one likes, following one's own inclinations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिन्
स्वैरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going where one likes, self-<BR>willed, wanton, uncontrolled; (इणी), f. a loose or<BR>unchaste woman, an adultress, wanton woman.<BR>—स्वैरि-ता, f. wilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक्क्
स्वक्क् स्वक्क्. See rt. ष्वक्क्, p. 1034,<BR>and Vopa-deva VIII. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक्ष
स्वक्ष स्व्-अक्ष, स्व्-अग्नि, स्व्-अङ्ग. See<BR>p. 1126, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगाकृ
स्वगाकृ स्वगा-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, कु-<BR>रुते, &c., (said to mean) to put in its place, arrange<BR>(perhaps referrible to स्व-ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वङ्क्|स्वंक्
स्वङ्क् स्वङ्क् (= rt. श्वङ्क्), cl. 1. A. स्वङ्-<BR>कते, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वङ्ग्|स्वंग्
स्वङ्ग् स्वङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. स्वङ्गति, &c., to<BR>go, move (= rt. श्रङ्ग्, p. 1023).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं|स्वच्छः
स्वच्छ स्व्-अच्छ, स्वच्छ-ता, &c. See p. 1126,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छंद|स्वच्छन्दः|स्वछन्द
स्वच्छन्द स्व-च्छन्द. See p. 1156, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वञ्च्
स्वञ्च् स्व्-अञ्च्. See p. 1126, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वञ्ज्|स्वंज्
स्वञ्ज् स्वञ्ज् or स्वज् [cf. परि-ष्वञ्ज्], cl.<BR>1. A. स्वजते, सस्वजे, सस्वञ्जे, स्वङ्-<BR>क्ष्यते, अस्वङ्क्त, स्वङ्क्तुम्, &c., to embrace,<BR>clasp, encircle, twist round: Pass. स्वज्यते, Aor.<BR>अस्वञ्जि: Caus. स्वञ्जयति, Aor. असिष्वञ्जत्:<BR>Desid. सिस्वङ्क्षते: Intens. सास्वज्यते, सास्वङ्क्ति;<BR>[cf. perhaps Germ. Schlange, ‘a snake.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक्त
स्वक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, embraced; [cf. परि-ष्वक्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वङ्ग|स्वंग|स्वंगः|स्वङ्गः
स्वङ्ग, अस्, m. embrace; [cf. परि-ष्वङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजमान
स्वजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजित्वा
स्वजित्वा, ind. having embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज्यमान
स्वज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वञ्जन|स्वंजनं
स्वञ्जन, अम्, n. the act of embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वठ्
स्वठ् स्वठ् (= rt. 2. श्वठ्), cl. 10. P.<BR>स्वाठयति, &c., to finish, &c.; to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद्
स्वद् स्वद् or स्वाद् (probably formed from<BR>5. सु + rt. अद्), cl. 1. A. (in Ved. also P.)<BR>स्वदते (Ved. स्वदति), स्वादते, सस्वदे, सस्-<BR>वादे, स्वदितुम्, स्वादितुम्, to taste, relish, eat; to<BR>be sweet or pleasant to the taste, be liked; to please;<BR>to sweeten, make sweet (Ved. P., Sāy. = स्वादू-<BR>कृ): Caus. and cl. 10. P. स्वादयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>असिस्वदत् (Ved. सिष्वदत् = स्वदयतु, स्वादू-<BR>करोतु, Ṛg-veda I. 188, 10), to make to taste; to<BR>taste; to sweeten, make sweet; (according to Vopa-<BR>deva) to cut: Desid. of Caus. सिस्वादयिषति; [cf.<BR>Gr. ἁνο-άν-ω (ἕ-αδ-ο-ν, ἕ-ᾱδ-α), ἥδ-ο-μαι, ἧδ-ος,<BR>ἡδ-ονή, ἡδ-ύ-ς, ἥδυ-μο-σ, ἄσ-μενο-ς, ἑδ-ανό-ς; Lat.<BR>suâ-vi-s (for suâd-vi-s), suâd-e-o, suâd-u-s, su-<BR>âd-a, suâd-êla; Goth. suti-s; Old Germ. suozi,<BR>‘sweet;’ Angl. Sax. svête, swœsend, ‘food;’ Lith.<BR>sald-u-s, ‘sweet;’ Slav. slad-i-ti, slad-u-ku,<BR>‘sweet.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदन|स्वदनं
स्वदन, अम्, n. the act of tasting, licking, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
2. स्वदित, अस्, आ, अम्, tasted, eaten; (अम्), n.<BR>‘may it be well tasted or eaten!’ an exclamation<BR>used at a Śrāddha after presenting the oblation of<BR>food to the Manes, (Manu III. 251, 254; in this<BR>sense probably for स्व्-अदित, see 1. स्व्-अदित, p. 1126;<BR>cf. सु-श्रुत, स्व-धा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद|स्वादः
स्वाद, अस्, m. taste, flavour, savour; tasting, eat-<BR>ing, drinking; liking, relishing, enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादत्
स्वादत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, tasting, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादन|स्वादनं
स्वादन, अम्, n. the act of tasting, eating, drink-<BR>ing; liking, relishing; sweetening, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादनीय
स्वादनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be tasted; tasty, savory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादित|स्वादितः
स्वादित, अस्, आ, अम्, tasted, relished, liked, en-<BR>joyed; sweetened; pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिन्
स्वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, tasting, drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिमन्
स्वादिमन्, आ, m. savoriness, sweetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिष्ठ
स्वादिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, sweetest, very sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादीयस्
स्वादीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, sweeter, very sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादु|स्वादुः
स्वादु, उस्, उस्, or वी, उ, sweet, pleasant to the<BR>taste, savory, tasteful, dainty, delicate; pleasing, agree-<BR>able, desired, lovely, charming, handsome; (उ), ind.<BR>sweetly; (उस्), m. a sweet taste or flavour, sweetness,<BR>relish; treacle, molasses; a medicinal root commonly<BR>called Jīvaka; a particular perfume or fragrant sub-<BR>stance, = गन्ध-धूम-ज, सु-धूम्य; (उस् or<BR>वी), f. = द्राक्षा, a grape; [cf. Gr. ἡδύς; Lat.<BR>suâvis (for suâdvis); Goth. suts, sutizo, ‘sweeter;’<BR>Old Germ. suazi, suozi; Mod. Germ. süss; Angl.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-b" target="_blank">Page1159-b+ 80</a>]<BR>Sax. svet; Eng. sweet.]<BR>—स्वादु-कण्टक, अस्, m.<BR>‘sweet-thorn,’ the plant Flacourtia Sapida; the creeper<BR>Tribulus Lanuginosus; other plants (= वि-कङ्कत;<BR>= गो-क्षुरक; = वि-कण्टक).<BR>—स्वादु-कन्दा,<BR>f. ‘having a sweet root,’ a kind of plant (= वि-दारी).<BR>—स्वादु-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, causing relish, dainty.<BR>—स्वादु-क्षद्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having dainty<BR>food, (Sāy. = स्वाद्व्-अन्न, Ṛg-veda I. 31, 15), pro-<BR>viding delicacies for guests, hospitable.<BR>—स्वादु-<BR>खण्ड, अस्, m. a piece of any sweet substance; raw<BR>sugar, molasses.<BR>—स्वादु-गन्धा, f. a species of<BR>creeper, the dark Convolvulus Paniculatus; other<BR>plants (= भूमि-कुष्माण्ड; = रक्त-शोभाञ्ज-<BR>न).<BR>—स्वादु-धन्वन्, आ, m. ‘having a sweet bow,’<BR>epithet of Kāma-deva (whose bow is said to be made<BR>of sugar-cane).<BR>—स्वादु-पर्णी, f. ‘sweet-leafed,’ a<BR>kind of plant (= दुग्धिका).<BR>—स्वादु-पाका, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= काक-माची).<BR>—स्वादु-पिण्डा, f.<BR>a kind of date tree.<BR>—स्वादु-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing pleasing flowers,’ a kind of plant (= कट-भी).<BR>—स्वादु-फल, अम्, n. ‘sweet fruit,’ the fruit of<BR>the jujube; (आ), f. ‘having sweet fruit,’ the jujube<BR>tree.<BR>—स्वादु-मज्जन्, आ, m. a sort of mountain<BR>Pīlu tree.<BR>—स्वादु-मांसी, f. the root Kākolī, q. v.<BR>—स्वादु-मूल, अम्, n. ‘sweet-root,’ a carrot.<BR>—स्वादु-योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, connected with or pos-<BR>sessing sweetness, sweet.<BR>—स्वादु-रसा, f. ‘having a<BR>sweet flavour,’ the root Kākolī, q. v.; the fruit of the<BR>hog-plum; the plant Śatāvarī; spirituous liquor; a<BR>grape.<BR>—स्वादु-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having pleasant<BR>gifts.<BR>—स्वादु-लता, f. the plant Vidārī.<BR>—स्वादु-<BR>शीत, अस्, आ, अम्, sweet and cool.<BR>—स्वादु-शुद्ध,<BR>अम्, n. ‘sweet and pure,’ rock salt; marine salt.<BR>—स्वादू-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make sweet,<BR>sweeten.<BR>—स्वाद्व्-अन्न, अम्, n. sweet or choice<BR>food, dainties, delicacies; (अस्, आ, अम्), having or<BR>providing delicacies.<BR>—स्वाद्व्-अम्ल, अस्, m. ‘sweet<BR>and sour,’ the pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्मन्
स्वाद्मन्, आ, अ, m. n., Ved. sweetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदेश|स्वदेशः
स्वदेश स्व-देश, स्व-धर्म, &c. See<BR>pp. 1156, 1157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधा
स्वधा स्व-धा or स्वधा, f. (fr. स्व + rt. 1.<BR>धा; but in Uṇādi-s. IV. 174. connected with rt.<BR>स्वद्; cf. स्वदित), Ved. one's own condition or<BR>nature, own peculiarity or individuality; innate or<BR>inherent power or strength, (स्वधया, by one's<BR>own power or strength; Sāy. = स्वकीयेन बलेन,<BR>by one's own nature or determination, spontaneously);<BR>‘self-contained, self-sustained,’ N. of Māyā or Pra-<BR>kṛti (as the source of the phenomenal world; in this<BR>sense Svadhā is sometimes translated ‘Nature,’ as,<BR>for example, in the celebrated hymn Ṛg-veda X.<BR>129. आनीद् अवातं स्वधया तद्, ‘that one, i. e.<BR>the supreme Being breathed calmly along with Na-<BR>ture;’ and in Naigh. III. 30. स्वधे, fem. du., is<BR>enumerated among the द्यावा-पृथिवी-नामधे-<BR>यानि); manner, habit, custom, usage, (अनु स्वधाम्,<BR>according to one's wont or custom, as usual; ac-<BR>cording to one's own determination, according to<BR>pleasure); one's own portion or share; the sacrificial<BR>offering due to each god; the food or oblation<BR>offered to the Pitṛs or spirits of deceased ancestors<BR>(in this sense especially in later Sanskrit); the Śrād-<BR>dha or funeral ceremony itself; the Food or Obla-<BR>tion to the Pitṛs &c. personified (as a daughter of<BR>Dakṣa and wife of the Pitṛs; also represented as a<BR>wife of Aṅgiras, of a Rudra, and of Agni); an ob-<BR>lation or offering or food (in general, = अन्न, Naigh.<BR>II. 7; = उदक, Naigh. I. 12); (स्वधा), ind. an<BR>exclamation or prayer used on presenting an oblation<BR>to the gods or Manes of departed ancestors and pro-<BR>genitors [cf. स्वाहा, श्रौषट्, वौषट्, वषट्],<BR>the highest form of blessing used at a Śrāddha, (स्व-<BR>धास्तु, ‘let there be Svadhā!’ this, according to<BR>Manu III. 252, is the highest benison at a Śrāddha);<BR>[cf. according to some Gr. ἔθ-ος, ἦθ-ος, ἠθεῖο-ς, εἴ-ωθ-α,<BR>ἐθ-ίζ-ω; Lat. suetus; Goth. sidus; Angl.<BR>Sax. sidu, siodo.]<BR>—स्वधा-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, offer-<BR>ing oblations to deceased ancestors or deified pro-<BR>genitors, performing funeral obsequies (Manu IX.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">Page1159-c+ 78</a>]<BR>127); (अस्), m. = स्वधा-कार.<BR>—स्वधा-कार,<BR>अस्, m. pronouncing the exclamation or blessing स्व-<BR>धा; the formula स्वधा.<BR>—स्वधा-निनयन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘Svadhā-performing,’ a sacred text used in<BR>making the oblation to the Pitṛs, (Manu II. 172.)<BR>—स्वधा-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of the Svadhā.<BR>—स्वधा-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘fond of the Svadhā,’<BR>Agni or fire; black sesamum, (तिल or sesamum being<BR>offered to the Manes, Manu III. 267.)<BR>—स्वधा-<BR>भुज्, क्, m. ‘Svadhā-eating,’ a Pitṛ, deceased or<BR>deified ancestor; a deity.<BR>—स्वधा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having natural power, self-controlled, self-reliant, in-<BR>dependent, powerful, (Sāy. स्वधा-वान् = बल-वान्,<BR>Ṛg-veda II. 20, 6; in Ṛg-veda VII. 88, 5. स्व-<BR>धावः, voc. case masc. O self-sustaining one, O self-<BR>dependent God, Sāy. = अन्नवन्); having the Sva-<BR>dhā, rich in oblations; (आन्), m. epithet of Viśva-<BR>karman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधावन्
स्वधावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. abounding in food,<BR>(Sāy. स्वधावरी = अन्नवत्यौ, Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>31, 7); self-reliant, independent (perhaps in this<BR>sense for स्व-धावन्; cf. स्वधा-वत् above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिति|स्वधितिः
स्वधिति स्वधिति, इस्, m. f. (sometimes writ-<BR>ten श्वधिति; fr. स्व + rt. 1. धा), an axe (in<BR>Naigh. II. 20. स्वधितिः is enumerated among the<BR>वज्र-नामानि).<BR>—स्वधिति-हेतिक, अस्, m. ‘axe-<BR>armed,’ a soldier armed with an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिती
स्वधिती, f. an axe.<BR>—स्वधिती-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. possessing or holding an axe, having a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन्
स्वन् स्वन्, cl. 1. P. स्वनति, सस्वान (3rd<BR>pl. सस्वनुस् or स्वेनुस्), स्वनिष्यति,<BR>अस्वनीत् or अस्वानीत्, स्वनितुम्, to sound, make a<BR>noise; to sing: Caus. स्वनयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असि-<BR>स्वनत्, to cause to sound, make to resound; to<BR>sound; to adorn (in this sense also स्वानयति, &c.):<BR>Desid. सिस्वनिषति: Intens. संस्वन्यते, सं-<BR>स्वन्ति; [cf. Lat. son-o; Lith. zwanu, ‘to sound;’<BR>Hib. sian, ‘a voice, sound.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन|स्वनः
स्वन, अस्, m. sound, noise; voice, speech (in<BR>Naigh. I. 11. enumerated among the वाङ्-नामानि).<BR>—स्वन-चक्र, अस्, m. a particular form of sexual<BR>union.<BR>—स्वन-दुह्, see Vopa-deva III. 165.<BR>—स्व-<BR>न-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having sound, sounding, thun-<BR>dering.<BR>—स्वनोत्साह (˚न-उत्˚), अस्, m. a rhinoceros<BR>(= गण्डक; also read शनोत्साह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनत्
स्वनत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sounding, resounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनि|स्वनिः
स्वनि, इस्, m. sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिक
स्वनिक, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding (at the end of a<BR>comp., e. g. पाणि-स्˚, one who claps with the hands).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनित|स्वनितं
स्वनित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, sounding, making<BR>a noise; (अम्), n. the noise of thunder, a thunder-<BR>clap.<BR>—स्वनिताह्वय (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, m. a kind of<BR>pot-herb (= तण्डुलीय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान|स्वानः
स्वान, अस्, m. sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानिन्
स्वानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. noisy, turbulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान्त|स्वांत|स्वान्तं
2. स्वान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. स्वान्त see p. 1158,<BR>col. 1), sounded, making a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनय
स्वनय स्वनय, अस्, m., N. of a king (said<BR>to have given his ten daughters in marriage to the<BR>Ṛṣi Kakṣivat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्
स्वप् 2. स्वप् (for 1. स्व्-अप् see p. 1126),<BR>cl. 2. P. स्वपिति (2nd sing. स्वपिषि, 1st<BR>sing. स्वपिमि, ep. also A. and sometimes even cl.<BR>1. P. A. स्वपति, -ते); Impf. अस्वपीत् or अस्व-<BR>पत् (1st du. अस्वपिव); Pot. स्वप्यात्; Impv. स्व-<BR>पितु (2nd sing. स्वपिहि, 1st sing. स्वपानि); Perf.<BR>सुष्वाप (3rd pl. सुषुपुः), स्वप्स्यति, अस्वाप्सीत्;<BR>Prec. सुप्यात्, स्वप्तुम्, to sleep; to fall asleep; to<BR>lie down to sleep, repose, go to bed; to lie down,<BR>recline; to be dead: Pass. सुप्यते, Aor. अस्वापि:<BR>Caus. स्वापयति, -यितुम्, Aor. असूषुपत् (accord-<BR>ing to some also असिष्वपत्), to cause to sleep,<BR>make sleep, lull to rest; to kill, (Ved. सिष्वपः =<BR>अस्वापयः, पातितवान्, thou didst hurl down, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 121, 11): Pass. of Caus. स्वाप्यते: Desid.<BR>of Caus. सुष्वापयिषति: Desid. सुषुप्सति:<BR>Intens. सोषुप्यते, सास्वप्ति, (according to Vopa-<BR>deva also) सास्वपीति, सोषुपीति, सोषोप्ति; [cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">Page1160-a+ 77</a>]<BR>Zend qap, qaf-na, ‘sleep:’ Gr. ὕπ-νο-ς (for συπ-νο-ς<BR>): Lat. som-nu-s (for sop-nus), sop-or, sop-<BR>i-o (= Caus. स्वापयति): Old Norse svef-n, ‘sleep:’<BR>Old Germ. svebjan: Goth. slêpan: Angl. Sax.<BR>svefian, svefn, slápan: Slav. sŭnŭ, ‘sleep;’ sŭp-<BR>a-ti, ‘to sleep:’ Lith. sap-na-s, ‘a dream:’ Cam-<BR>bro-Brit. hephun: Hib. suain, ‘sleep;’ suaimh-<BR>neach, ‘quiet;’ suaimhnighim, ‘I rest.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्त|सुप्तं|सुप्तः
सुप्त, सुप्ति. See s. v., p. 1128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्त्वा
सुप्त्वा, ind. having slept, having gone to sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुपाण
सुषुपाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sleeping, (Sāy. =<BR>सुप्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्वस्
सुषुप्वस्, आन्, उषी, अत्, one who has slept or<BR>sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्सु
सुषुप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to sleep, sleepy,<BR>drowsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपत्
स्वपत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sleeping, asleep, reposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपन|स्वपनं
स्वपन, अम्, n. the act of sleeping, dreaming,<BR>sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपनीय
स्वपनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be slept, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपितिकर्मन्
स्वपिति-कर्मन्, आ, m. one who lies down to<BR>sleep (= शयन-कर्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्तव्य
स्वप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्तुकाम
स्वप्तु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्तृ
स्वप्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a sleeper, one who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्न|स्वप्नः
स्वप्न, अस्, m. sleep, sleeping; a dream, dream-<BR>ing; sleepiness, sloth, indolence; (आ), f. a dream,<BR>(जाग्रत्-स्वप्नाभ्याम्, inst. du. by alternately wak-<BR>ing and sleeping.)<BR>—स्वप्न-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wish-<BR>ing for sleep.<BR>—स्वप्न-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing or<BR>producing sleep, somniferous, soporific, narcotic;<BR>(त्), n. the pot-herb Marsilea Quadrifolia.<BR>—स्वप्न-<BR>गृह, अम्, n. a sleeping apartment, bed-chamber.<BR>—स्वप्न-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in sleep.<BR>—स्वप्न-दोष, अस्, m. ‘sleep-fault,’ pollutio noc-<BR>turna.<BR>—स्वप्न-धी-गम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, perceptible<BR>by the intellect (only when) in a state of sleep-like<BR>abstraction, (Manu XII. 122.)<BR>—स्वप्न-नंशन,<BR>अस्, m. sleep-destroying, (see Nirukta XII. 28.)<BR>—स्वप्न-निकेतन, अम्, n. a sleeping-room, bed-<BR>chamber.<BR>—स्वप्न-प्रपञ्च, अस्, m. the illusions<BR>of sleep, the world as presented in a dream.<BR>—स्वप्-<BR>न-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, enjoying sleep.<BR>—स्वप्न-वत्,<BR>ind. like a dream.<BR>—स्वप्न-विचार, अस्, m. inter-<BR>pretation of dreams.<BR>—स्वप्न-विचारिन्, ई, m. an<BR>interpreter of dreams.<BR>—स्वप्न-शील, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>disposed to sleep, sleepy, drowsy.<BR>—स्वप्न-सृष्टि,<BR>इस्, f. the creation of dreams or illusions in sleep.<BR>—स्वप्नाध्याय (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘a chapter<BR>on dreams,’ N. of a short work on the interpretation<BR>of dreams, (said to be extracted from the Brahma-<BR>vaivarta-Purāṇa.)<BR>—स्वप्नावस्था (˚न-अव्˚), f.<BR>state of dreaming, (applied to life as a state of<BR>illusion.)<BR>—स्वप्नेश्वर (˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of a commentary on the Śāṇḍilya-sūtra.<BR>—स्वप्नोपम (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>likeness of sleep, resembling a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज्
स्वप्नज्, क्, क्, क्, sleepy, drowsy, sleeping, asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाप|स्वापः
स्वाप, अस्, m. sleep, sleeping; dreaming, a<BR>dream; sleepiness, sloth; paralysis, palsy, loss of<BR>sensation, ignorance; temporary or partial loss of<BR>sensation from pressure on a nerve, numbness, the<BR>sleep of a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापिन्
स्वापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, causing sleep, lulling to sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपिवात
स्वपिवात स्व्-अपिवात. See p. 1126, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपू
स्वपू स्वपू (thought by some to be fr. an<BR>old rt. स्वप्, ‘to tear, pull’), Ved. (according to<BR>some) a beak, bill of a bird, (in Ṛg-veda VII. 56,<BR>3, Sāy. explains स्व-पूभिस् by स्वकीयैः पव-<BR>नैः सञ्चरणैः, by their own pure paths);<BR>[cf. Old Germ. snabul, ‘beak;’ Mod. Germ.<BR>Schnepfe, ‘a snipe;’ Old Norse nef.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वब्दिन्
स्वब्दिन् स्वब्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. (perhaps)<BR>roaring, (Sāy. = शब्दं कुर्वत्, Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>33, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वमेक|स्वमेकः
स्वमेक स्वमेक, अस्, m. (etymology doubt-<BR>ful), a year (= संवत्सर, according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम् स्वयम्, स्वयं-वर, स्वयम्-भू,<BR>&c. See p. 1158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् 1. स्वर्, cl. 10. P. स्वरयति, &c.,<BR>to find fault, blame, censure, reprove (=<BR>rt. सुर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् 2. स्वर्, ind. (probably connected<BR>with rt. 4. सु or 3. सू, and apparently originally<BR>written सुवर्, cf. सूर, सूर्य; but according to<BR>some fr. a lost rt. स्वर् = सुर्, ‘to shine,’ cf. सुर),<BR>the sun (Ved.; according to Sāy. = स्वरण-शील<BR>आदित्य, Ṛg-veda V. 45, 1); heaven, paradise, the<BR>world of the gods, abode of the deities; the heaven<BR>of Indra and temporary abode of the virtuous after<BR>death; the sky, ether; the space above the sun or<BR>between the sun and the polar star, the region of<BR>the planets and constellations; a mystical word<BR>pronounced after ॐ and before the Gāyatrī by<BR>every Brāhman in commencing his daily prayers, (it<BR>is the third of the three Vyāhṛtis, भूर्, भुवः,<BR>स्वर्, and denotes the space of the sky above de-<BR>scribed as distinguished from the earth and atmo-<BR>sphere, see Manu II. 76. and cf. भुवस्, व्य्-आहृति;<BR>the mystical word स्वर् is represented as produced<BR>from the Sāma-veda, just as भूर् and भुवः are<BR>supposed to come from the Ṛg-veda and Yajur-veda<BR>respectively); radiance, splendor; water, (in Naigh.<BR>I. 12. enumerated among the उदक-नामानि); epi-<BR>thet of Śiva; [cf. Zend hvare, ‘the sun;’ qaretha,<BR>qarenanh, ‘splendor:’ Gr. Σείρ-ιο-ς, Σείρ, σειρ-ιά-ω,<BR>σειρ-ία-σι-ς, σείρ-ινο-ς, σέλ-ας, σελ-ήνη:<BR>Lat. ser-enu-s, sol: Goth. sauil, ‘the sun:’ Old<BR>Norse sôl: Lith. saule: Slav. slŭ-nĭce, ‘the sun:’<BR>Hib. speur, ‘the sky;’ (perhaps) soir, ‘the east,<BR>morning.’]<BR>—स्वः-काम्य, Nom. P. -काम्यति, &c.,<BR>to wish for heaven.<BR>—स्वः-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the<BR>lord of heaven.<BR>—स्वर्-आपगा, f. the river of heaven,<BR>the celestial Ganges.<BR>—स्वर्-आरूढ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ascended to heaven.<BR>—स्वर्-आलु, उस्, m. a kind of<BR>root (= वचा).<BR>—स्वर्-गङ्गा, f. the celestial Ganges;<BR>the galaxy.<BR>—स्वर्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to heaven,<BR>dead.<BR>—स्वर्-गति, इस्, f. or स्वर्-गमन, अम्, n.<BR>going to heaven, future felicity; death.<BR>—स्वर्-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘the heavenly mountain,’ Su-meru.<BR>—स्वर्-<BR>जित्, त्, त्, त्, conquering heaven; (त्), m. a proper N.;<BR>N. of a kind of sacrifice, (Manu XI. 74; cf. स्वर्ग-<BR>जित्.)<BR>—स्वर्-णदी, f. the river of heaven, the<BR>celestial Ganges; a kind of shrub (= वृश्चिकाली).<BR>—स्वर्-णर, अस्, m., Ved. the lord of heaven;<BR>one who leads or is led to heaven, a pious or de-<BR>votional man; all-leading, (Sāy. = स्वर्गम् प्रति<BR>नेतृ or नेतव्य or सर्वस्य नेतृ); a sacrifice<BR>(as leading the offerer to heaven).<BR>—स्वर्-दृश्, क्,<BR>क्, क्, Ved. looking heavenwards; (क्), m. epithet<BR>of Indra; of Agni; of Soma.<BR>—स्वर्-नदी, f. =<BR>स्वर्-णदी.<BR>—स्वर्-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the lord of<BR>heaven.<BR>—स्वर्-भानव, अस्, m. a kind of precious<BR>stone (= गो-मेदक).<BR>—स्वर्-भानु, उस्, m., N.<BR>of Rāhu or the personified ascending node (repre-<BR>sented in Ṛg-veda V. 40, 9. as of the Asura race<BR>and as concealing or piercing the sun); N. of a<BR>Dānava (regarded as a son of Kaśyapa or, according<BR>to other authorities, a son of Vipracitti).<BR>—स्वर्-<BR>भानु-सूदन, अस्, m. ‘destroyer of Rāhu,’ the<BR>sun.<BR>—स्वर्-मध्य, अम्, n. the central point of<BR>the sky, zenith.<BR>—स्वर्-मीऌह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>happiness-bestowing, (Sāy. = सुख-सेक्तृ); con-<BR>ferring heaven, (Sāy. स्वर्-मीऌहेषु = स्वर्ग-दे-<BR>शेषु सुखस्य सेचयत्सु, Ṛg-veda I. 130, 8.)<BR>—स्वर्-यात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to heaven, deceased,<BR>dead.<BR>—स्वर्-यातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, going to heaven,<BR>dying.<BR>—स्वर्-लोक, अस्, m. the celestial region,<BR>heaven.<BR>—स्वर्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. full of splen-<BR>dor or happiness, heavenly, celestial, (Sāy. = सुख-<BR>युक्त, Ṛg-veda VI. 22, 3.)<BR>—स्वर्-वधू, ऊस्, f.<BR>‘celestial wife,’ an Apsaras.<BR>—स्वर्-वापी, f. ‘heavenly<BR>lake,’ the Ganges.<BR>—स्वर्-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. obtaining<BR>heaven, possessing heaven (said of the Pitṛs, of<BR>Indra, &c.).<BR>—स्वर्-वेश्या, f. a courtezan of heaven,<BR>nymph, Apsaras (such as Urvaśī &c.).<BR>—स्वर्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-c" target="_blank">Page1160-c+ 78</a>]<BR>वैद्य, अस्, m. ‘physician of heaven,’ either of the<BR>two Aśvins, (see अश्विन्.)<BR>—स्वर्-षा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>Ved. granting heaven; (आस्), m. epithet of Soma;<BR>of the thunderbolt.<BR>—स्वर्-षाति, इस्, f., Ved. the<BR>granting or gaining of heaven, anything which gains<BR>heaven; (इस्, इस्, इ), bestowing or procuring heaven<BR>(and hence applied to ‘war, battle;’ according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X. 99, 3. स्वर्-षाता = स्वर्-<BR>षातौ = स्वर्ग-लाभोपेते; in IX. 88, 2 = स्वर्ग-<BR>लाभ-युक्ते सङ्ग्रामे, cf. वाज-साति).<BR>—स्वस्-<BR>तरु, उस्, m. the tree of paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग|स्वर्गः
स्वर्ग, अस्, m. (according to some for सु-वर्ग),<BR>heaven, Indra's paradise, the residence of beatified<BR>mortals and of the inferior gods (supposed to be<BR>situated on the mountain Meru); N. of a son of<BR>Bhīma.<BR>—स्वर्ग-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of<BR>heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-खण्ड, N. of the third book<BR>of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—स्वर्ग-गत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>gone to heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-गमन, अम्, n. going<BR>to heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going to<BR>heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-गिरि, इस्, m. ‘the heavenly moun-<BR>tain,’ Su-meru.<BR>—स्वर्ग-जित्, त्, त्, त्, winning or<BR>obtaining paradise.<BR>—स्वर्ग-द, अस्, आ, अम्, heaven-<BR>giving, procuring paradise.<BR>—स्वर्ग-द्वार, अम्, n.<BR>heaven's gate, the door of paradise, entrance into<BR>heaven; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—स्वर्ग-पति, इस्, m. the<BR>lord of heaven, Indra.<BR>—स्वर्ग-पर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>intent on heaven, desirous of heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-<BR>भर्तृ, ता, m. the lord of heaven, Indra.<BR>—स्वर्ग-<BR>मार्ग-दिदृक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to see the<BR>road to heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-लोक, अस्, m. the ce-<BR>lestial region, (see स्वर्ग); Indra's heaven, para-<BR>dise.<BR>—स्वर्गलोकेश (˚क-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>celestial world,’ Indra; the body (as enjoying felicity<BR>in the paradise of Indra).<BR>—स्वर्ग-वधू, ऊस्, f. a<BR>woman or nymph of Indra's heaven, Apsaras.<BR>—स्वर्ग-वास, अस्, m. residence in heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, inhabiting heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-श्री, ईस्, f. the glory of heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-<BR>सम्पादन, अस्, ई, अम्, effecting or procuring<BR>heaven, gaining heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-सरित्, त्, f. the<BR>river of heaven.<BR>—स्वर्गसरिद्-वरा, f. ‘best of<BR>heavenly rivers,’ the Ganges.<BR>—स्वर्ग-साधन,<BR>अम्, n. a means of attaining heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-सु-<BR>ख, अम्, n. the joy of heaven.<BR>—स्वर्ग-स्त्री, f. a<BR>woman of paradise, Apsaras.<BR>—स्वर्गापगा (˚ग-<BR>आप्˚), f. the celestial river, the Ganges.<BR>—स्वर्गा-<BR>पवर्ग (˚ग-अप्˚), अस्, m. heaven-like emanci-<BR>pation.<BR>—स्वर्गारूढ (˚ग-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ascended to heaven.<BR>—स्वर्गारोहण (˚ग-आर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the act of ascending to heaven; N. of certain<BR>funeral ceremonies.<BR>—स्वर्गारोहण-पर्वन् or<BR>स्वर्गारोहणिक-पर्वन्, अ, n., N. of the eighteenth<BR>book of the Mahā-bhārata (in which is described the<BR>journey of the five Pāṇḍava princes towards Indra's<BR>heaven in mount Meru).<BR>—स्वर्गेप्सु (˚ग-ईप्˚),<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of obtaining heaven.<BR>—स्वर्-<BR>गौकस् (˚ग-ओक्˚), आस्, m. ‘having an abode in<BR>heaven,’ a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिन्
स्वर्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, belonging to heaven, being in<BR>heaven, heavenly; (ई), m. an inhabitant of heaven,<BR>a god, deity, celestial; (in law) ‘in heaven,’ a dead<BR>person.<BR>—स्वर्गि-गिरि, इस्, m. the celestial moun-<BR>tain, Su-meru.<BR>—स्वर्गि-वधू, ऊस्, f. a celestial<BR>woman, Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गीय
स्वर्गीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>Svarga, heavenly, celestial; conducive to heaven,<BR>leading to heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग्य|स्वर्ग्यः
स्वर्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = स्वर्गीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्य
स्वर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. heavenly, celestial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्यु
स्वर्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. wishing for heaven; de-<BR>siring happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

