हजाज
हजाज हजाज, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हजाजि
हजाजि, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जा|हंजा
हञ्जा हञ्जा, ind. (in the drama) a vocative<BR>particle used in addressing a female attendant or<BR>maid-servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जे|हंजे
हञ्जे, ind. a vocative particle, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जि|हञ्जिः
हञ्जि हञ्जि, इस्, m. a sneeze, sneezing (=<BR>क्षुत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जिका
हञ्जिका हञ्जिका, f. (probably) a kind of<BR>plant (= भार्गी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्
हट् हट्, cl. 1. P. हटति, जहाट, हटितुम्,<BR>to shine, be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हटपर्णि
हटपर्णि हट-पर्णि, n. (according to Śab-<BR>da-k.) the aquatic plant Vallisneria; [cf. हठ-<BR>पर्णी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्ट|हट्टः
हट्ट हट्ट, अस्, m. a market, fair; (ई), f. a<BR>petty market or fair.<BR>—हट्ट-चौरक, अस्, m. a<BR>thief who steals from fairs and markets.<BR>—हट्ट-<BR>विलासिनी, f. ‘dallying in market-places;’ a wanton<BR>woman, prostitute; a sort of perfume (= धमनी);<BR>turmeric (= हरिद्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ्
हठ् हठ्, cl. 1. P. हठति, जहाठ, &c.,<BR>to leap, jump; to be wicked; to treat with<BR>violence, oppress; to bind to a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ|हठः
हठ, अस्, m. violence, force, (हठेन, by force,<BR>forcibly, violently, with precipitation, suddenly), op-<BR>pression; rapine; the aquatic plant Pistia Stratiotes<BR>(= पृश्नी).<BR>—हठ-दीपिका, f., N. of a work, (see<BR>below.)<BR>—हठ-पर्णी, f. the aquatic plant Vallis-<BR>neria Octandra.<BR>—हठ-प्रदीपिका, f. a treatise on<BR>the Haṭha-yoga and asceticism by Ātmārāma.<BR>—ह-<BR>ठ-योग, अस्, m. a particular mode of Yoga or ab-<BR>stract contemplation (forcing the mind to abstain<BR>from external objects; it is treated of in the Haṭha-<BR>pradīpikā, and may be performed in various ways,<BR>such as standing on one leg, holding up the arms,<BR>inhaling smoke with the head inverted, &c.).<BR>—ह-<BR>ठ-विद्या, f. the science or method of forced medita-<BR>tion.<BR>—हठ-सङ्केत-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a treatise<BR>by Sundara-deva on the Haṭha-yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठालु|हठालुः
हठालु, उस्, m. the plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठी
हठी, f. the plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडि|हडिः
हडि हडि, इस्, m. wooden fetters, a kind of<BR>stocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडिक|हडिकः
हडिक हडिक, अस्, m. a servant of the lowest<BR>caste, a sweeper (= मलाकर्षिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डक|हड्डकः
हड्डक, अस्, m. = हडिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डि|हड्डिः
हड्डि, इस्, or हड्डिक, अस्, m. = हडिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्ड|हड्डं
हड्ड हड्ड, अम्, n. a bone.<BR>—हड्ड-ज, अम्,<BR>n. produced from bones, marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डिप|हड्डिपः
हड्डिप हड्डिप, अस्, m. = हडिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डा|हंडा
हण्डा हण्डा, ind. a vocative particle used<BR>in addressing a female of inferior rank; (in the<BR>drama) a form of address used by equals to each other<BR>among those of the lowest class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डे|हंडे
हण्डे, ind. a vocative particle, = हण्डा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डिका|हंडिका
हण्डिका हण्डिका, f. an earthen pot or boiler.<BR>—हण्डिका-सुत, अस्, m. a small earthen pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डी|हंडी
हण्डी, f. = हण्डिका above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत|हतः
हत हत, हतक, &c. See cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हथ|हथः
हथ हथ. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हद्
हद् हद्, cl. 1. A. हदते, जहदे, हत्स्यते,<BR>अहत्त, हत्तुम्, to evacuate, excrete or dis-<BR>charge excrement: Caus. हादयति: Desid. जिहत्-<BR>सते: Intens. जाहद्यते, जाहत्ति; [cf. Zend zad;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">Page1164-b+ 80</a>]<BR>Gr. χέζ-ω (κέ-χοδ-α, χε-σοῦ-μαι), χεσείω, χόδ-ο-ς,<BR>χόδ-ανο-ς; Angl. Sax. scît-e; Old Germ. scîz-u.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हदन|हदनं
हदन, अम्, n. the act of excretion, evacuation<BR>(of excrement or ordure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्न|हन्नं|हन्नः
हन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, passed (as excrement), evacu-<BR>ated, excreted; (अम्), n. excrement, ordure; [cf.<BR>गो-ह्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हद्दा
हद्दा हद्दा, f., (in astronomy) N. of a di-<BR>vision of each zodiacal sign, (thirty such divisions are<BR>specified and distributed variously to each planet;<BR>according to some, a masc. form of this word exists.)<BR>—हद्देश (˚दा-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of a thirtieth<BR>division of a zodiacal sign,’ (probably) an epithet of<BR>the planets (= त्रिंशांश-प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्
हन् 1. हन् (probably for an original<BR>धन्, cf. नि-धन, p. 487; but some<BR>forms are fr. घन्, some fr. घत्, and others are<BR>borrowed fr. rt. वध् or बध्), cl. 2. P. (ep. also<BR>A. in some forms, cf. आ-हन्), हन्ति (3rd du. हतस्,<BR>3rd pl. घ्नन्ति); Impf. अहन् (3rd du. अहताम्,<BR>3rd pl. अघ्नन्); Pot. हन्यात्; Impv. हन्तु (2nd<BR>sing. जहि, 3rd sing. हन्तु, 2nd pl. हत, 3rd pl.<BR>घ्नन्तु; in Naigh. II. 14. a form हन्तात् is given<BR>as one reading); Perf. जघान (2nd sing. जघ-<BR>निथ or जघन्थ, 1st du. जघ्निव, 3rd pl.<BR>जघ्नुस्, ep. A. जघ्निरे); 2nd Fut. हनिष्यति,<BR>Aor. अवधीत् (fr. rt. वध् or बध्, ep. also अहनत्);<BR>Prec. वध्यात्; Cond. अहनिष्यत्, हन्तुम्, (Ved.<BR>forms, Pres. हनति [as if cl. 1], जिघ्नते [cf. rt.<BR>घ्रा]; Perf. जहा = जघान, Nirukta IV. 1; Inf.<BR>हन्तोस्, हन्तवै), to strike, hit, beat; to strike<BR>down, kill, slay, destroy; to wound, hurt, injure,<BR>harass, afflict; to overcome, overthrow, overturn,<BR>conquer; to remove, take away, counteract, cure;<BR>to obstruct, stop, hinder, impede, mar; to go, move,<BR>(in Naigh. II. 14. हनति is enumerated among the<BR>गति-कर्माणह्): Pass. हन्यते, जघ्ने, हन्ता<BR>or घानिता, हनिष्यते or घानिष्यते, अवधि<BR>or अघानि (3rd pl. अघानिषत or अहसत, Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 4, 62), घानिषीष्ट, to be struck, to be killed,<BR>&c.: Caus. घातयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अजीघतत्<BR>(properly a Nom. fr. घात), to cause to be slain or<BR>killed: Desid. जिघांसति, to wish to kill or slay:<BR>Intens. जङ्घन्यते or जेघ्नीयते (in Pāṇ. VII. 4,<BR>31), जङ्घन्ति, (Ved. [नि-]घनिघ्नते, pres. part.<BR>dat. or according to Sāy. = [नि-]हन्ति, Ṛg-veda I.<BR>55, 5); [cf. Gr. ἔ-θαν-ον, θάν-ατος, θείν-ω, θνήακω:<BR>Lat. (fen-d-o), offend-o, defend-o, in-festus: Goth.<BR>dauthus, ‘death:’ Angl. Sax. deád, deadh, dydan,<BR>‘to kill:’ Hib. gonaim, ‘I wound;’ (perhaps also)<BR>gail, ‘slaughter;’ gaillim, ‘I hurt.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घात|घातः
घात, घातयत्, &c. See p. 307.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्न
घ्न, घ्नत्, &c. See p. 310.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्वस्
जघन्वस्, जघ्निवस्. See p. 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घन्यमान
जङ्घन्यमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.),<BR>being repeatedly struck, being greatly wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
4. ह (for 5. ह see under rt. 3. हा), killing, de-<BR>stroying, removing, counteracting (at the end of<BR>comps., cf. विष-ह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत|हतः
हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck, beaten [cf. अ-ह्˚]; struck<BR>down, killed, slain, wounded, hurt, marred, injured,<BR>spoiled, blighted, destroyed, utterly ruined, ex-<BR>tinguished, dimmed, ended, lost; impeded, hindered,<BR>checked; counteracted, neutralized, disappointed,<BR>frustrated; repelled, driven off, avoided; deprived<BR>of, bereft of, freed from, destitute of (especially at the<BR>beginning of comps., see below); miserable, worthless;<BR>(in arithmetic) multiplied; (अम्), n. striking, killing,<BR>hurting; multiplication.<BR>—हत-कण्टक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, freed from thorns; one whose foes are de-<BR>stroyed.<BR>—हत-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, bereft of sense,<BR>perplexed in mind, dispirited, bewildered, confounded.<BR>—हत-जीवित, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of life or hope,<BR>overcome with despair; (अम्), n. despair of life.<BR>—हत-ज्ञान, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of conscious-<BR>ness.<BR>—हतज्योतिर्-निशीथ, अस्, m. a night in which<BR>the stars are extinguished, a starless night.<BR>—हत-<BR>ज्योतिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, having the stars extinguished, star-<BR>less, dark.<BR>—हत-ताप, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from heat,<BR>cooled.<BR>—हत-त्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, dimmed in lustre, de-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">Page1164-c+ 81</a>]<BR>prived of light.<BR>—हत-दैव, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-fated,<BR>ill-starred, luckless.<BR>—हत-द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, one who<BR>has slain his enemy or enemies.<BR>—हत-पितृ, ता,<BR>m. one whose father has been slain.<BR>—हत-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one whose son has been slain.<BR>—हत-प्रभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose power has<BR>been destroyed, bereft of power.<BR>—हत-प्रमाद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, driving away or avoiding negligence, freed<BR>from carelessness.<BR>—हत-प्रवीर, अस्, आ, अम्, whose<BR>choicest warriors are slain.<BR>—हत-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>almost killed.<BR>—हत-बान्धव, अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>prived of relations, destitute of relations.<BR>—हत-<BR>बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, deprived of sense, destitute of sense.<BR>—हत-भाग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-starred, ill-fated.<BR>—हत-मातृ, ता, m. one whose mother has been<BR>slain.<BR>—हत-मूर्ख, अस्, m. an excessive fool, a<BR>blockhead.<BR>—हत-मेधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, perplexed in<BR>mind, deprived of sense or intellect.<BR>—हत-रथ,<BR>अस्, m. a smitten chariot, a chariot of which the<BR>horses and charioteer are slain.<BR>—हत-लक्षण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of good marks, unlucky.<BR>—हत-<BR>विनय, अस्, आ, अम्, lost to a sense of propriety.<BR>—हत-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has lost his<BR>virility or vigour.<BR>—हत-वृषन्, आ, णी, अ, Ved.<BR>(according to Sāy.) one whose obstructor has been<BR>destroyed, (applied to the waters whose obstructor is<BR>said to be Vṛtra, Ṛg-veda IV. 17, 3.)<BR>—हत-<BR>शिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, left remaining out of the slain,<BR>left surviving.<BR>—हत-शिष्ट-जन, अस्, m. a sur-<BR>vivor, (see above.)<BR>—हत-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, re-<BR>maining from among the killed, escaped, survived.<BR>—हत-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, one whose prosperity is<BR>blighted; reduced to penury.<BR>—हत-सम्पद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has lost his property, reduced to<BR>poverty.<BR>—हत-सम्मद, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>pleasures are destroyed or marred.<BR>—हत-सर्व-<BR>योध, अस्, आ, अम्, having all the warriors slain.<BR>—हत-साध्वस, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from fear.<BR>—हत-सूत, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose charioteer is<BR>slain.<BR>—हताधिमन्थ (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, freed<BR>from disease of the eye or from loss of sight.<BR>—हता-<BR>रोह (˚त-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (an elephant &c.) whose<BR>riders are slain.<BR>—हतावशेष (˚त-अव्˚), आस्, m. pl.<BR>those left of the slain.<BR>—हताश (˚त-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one whose hopes are destroyed, bereft of hope, hope-<BR>less, despairing, desponding; weak, powerless; bar-<BR>ren; vile, low, infamous, wicked; cruel, merciless.<BR>—हताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose horse<BR>or horses have been killed.<BR>—हतौजस् (˚त-ओज्˚),<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, one whose vigour is destroyed, bereft of<BR>energy, debilitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतक|हतकः
हतक, अस्, आ, अम्, miserable, ill-bred, bad (in<BR>general); (अस्), m. a low person, coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हति|हतिः
हति, इस्, f. striking, a stroke, blow [cf. हल-ह्˚];<BR>killing, destroying, destruction, removing, &c.; (ac-<BR>cording to Śabda-k.) = अप-कर्ष; = उल्लास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्नु|हत्नुः
हत्नु, उस्, m. a weapon; sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्य
हत्य, अम्, n. killing, slaying; [cf. शम्बर-<BR>ह्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्या
हत्या, f. killing, slaying, slaughter, murder (gene-<BR>rally applied to criminal killing, and chiefly used in<BR>comps.; cf. ब्रह्म-ह्˚, गो-ह्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्वा
हत्वा, ind. having struck or killed, having slain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्वी
हत्वी, ind., Ved. = हत्वा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हथ|हथः
हथ, अस्, m. a stroke, blow; killing, slaughter;<BR>death; a man dejected or in low spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्
2. हन्, हा, घ्नी, m. f. killing, slaying; a killer,<BR>slayer (at the end of comps.; cf. ब्रह्म-हन्,<BR>वृत्र-हन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन|हनः
हन, अस्, m. killing, slaying, a killer, slayer, (see<BR>सु-ह्˚, cf. घन, घनाघन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनन|हननं|हननः
हनन, अम्, n. the act of striking, killing, de-<BR>stroying; wounding, hurting, injuring; (in arith-<BR>metic) multiplication.<BR>—हनन-शील, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of a murderous disposition, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हननीय
हननीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be struck or beaten, to<BR>be killed, worthy of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनिष्यत्
हनिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to kill or<BR>slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनु|हनुः
हनु, उस्, m. f. the jaw (also हनू, ऊस्, f. and<BR>हनु, उ, n., and in the sense ‘jaw,’ thought to be con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">Page1165-a+ 80</a>]<BR>nected with rt. 2. हा, but according to Sāy. so called,<BR>as हनन-साधन, ‘an instrument of destruc-<BR>tion’); (उस्), f. anything which destroys or injures<BR>life; a weapon; death, dying; disease, sickness; a<BR>kind of drug; a wanton woman, prostitute; [cf. Gr.<BR>γένυ-ς, γέν-ειο-ν, γν-άθο-ς, γναθ-μό-ς; Lat. gen-a;<BR>Goth. kinnu-s; Old Germ. kinni; Angl. Sax.<BR>cinn, cyn.]<BR>—हनु-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘jaw-seizure,’<BR>locked jaw.<BR>—हनु-भेद, अस्, m. the gaping or<BR>parting asunder of the jaws.<BR>—हनुमज्-जयन्ती,<BR>f. the day of full moon of the month Caitra (being the<BR>supposed birthday of Hanumat).<BR>—हनु-मत्, आन्, m.<BR>‘having (large) jaws,’ N. of a monkey-chief (one of<BR>the most celebrated of a vast host of semi-divine<BR>apes or monkey-like beings, who, according to Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa I. 16, were created to become the allies of<BR>Rāma-candra in his war with Rāvaṇa; the chiefs of<BR>these Simian armies were supposed to be the progeny<BR>of various gods; thus, Su-grīva, q. v., was son of the<BR>Sun, Bāli of Indra, Tāra of Vṛhas-pati, Gandha-<BR>mādana of Kuvera, Nala of Viśva-karman, Nīla of<BR>Agni, Su-ṣeṇa of Varuṇa, and the celebrated Hanu-<BR>mat of Pavana or Māruta, ‘the Wind;’ their character<BR>corresponds more to that of Genii than animals;<BR>they are all described as capable of supernatural feats,<BR>and Hanumat especially is fabled to have assumed<BR>any form at will, wielded rocks, removed mountains,<BR>mounted the air, seized the clouds, and rivalled<BR>Garuḍa in swiftness of flight; according to other<BR>legends, Hanumat was son of Śiva; his mother's<BR>name was Añjanā, q. v.); a particular sort of monkey,<BR>Simia Sinica.<BR>—हनुमन्-नाटक, अम्, n. the<BR>Hanumat drama (a celebrated drama in fourteen acts,<BR>supposed to have been written about the tenth or<BR>eleventh century of our era, and ascribed to Hanumat<BR>himself, who is said to have engraved it on rocks;<BR>it is emphatically called the Mahā-nāṭaka or great<BR>drama, and is, in fact, the story of the Rāmāyaṇa<BR>dramatized, the monkey-chief Hanumat playing a<BR>very important part in the action of the piece).<BR>—हनु-मूल, अम्, n. the root of the jaw.<BR>—हनु-<BR>स्तम्भ, अस्, m. ‘jaw-stoppage,’ locked jaw.<BR>—हनू-<BR>मत्, आन्, m. = हनु-मत् above; N. of the mythical<BR>author of the Khaṇḍa-praśasti; of the author of the<BR>Hanūman-nāṭaka.<BR>—हनूमत्-कल्प, N. of a work.<BR>—हनूमत्-कवच, अम्, n. ‘Hanūmat's breastplate,’<BR>N. of a hymn addressed to the five-headed Hanūmat,<BR>(this hymn is taken from the Sudarśana-saṃhitā.)<BR>—हनूमत्-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work in five<BR>chapters (describing the rites to be observed in the<BR>worship of Hanūmat; four chapters are said to be<BR>extracted from the Sudarśana-saṃhitā, and the re-<BR>maining one from the Rāmāyaṇa).<BR>—हनूमन्-<BR>नाटक, अम्, n. = हनुमन्-नाटक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनू
हनू, ऊस्, f. See under हनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूष|हनूषः
हनूष, अस्, m. a Rākṣasa, demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तव्य
हन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be struck or killed, de-<BR>serving death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तु|हंतुः|हन्तुः
हन्तु, उस्, m. killing, death; a bull; [cf. सु-ह्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तुमनस्
हन्तु-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (हन्तु for हन्तुम्),<BR>minding to kill, intending to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तृ|हंतृ
हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who strikes or kills, strik-<BR>ing; destroying, removing, counteracting [cf. विष-<BR>ह्˚]; (ता), m. a murderer, slayer; a thief, robber;<BR>(according to some) a particular measure of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्त्व
हन्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be slain, (Sāy. =<BR>हननीय, Ṛg-veda III. 30, 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्मन्
हन्मन्, अ, n., Ved. anything causing death, a<BR>deadly or destructive weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्यमान|हन्यमानः
हन्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being struck or smitten;<BR>being killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानुक|हानुकः
हानुक, अस्, ई, अम्, killing, hurting, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनील|हनीलः
हनील हनील, अस्, m. (according to Śab-<BR>da-k.) a particular tree (= केतकी, also written ह-<BR>लीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्त|हंत
हन्त हन्त, ind. an exclamation of grief,<BR>(equivalent to ‘ah,’ ‘alas’); of pity; of joy; of sur-<BR>prise; of flurry or haste; an exclamation expressive<BR>of good luck or benediction, (see below); an in-<BR>ceptive particle.<BR>—हन्त-कार, अस्, m. the exclama-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">Page1165-b+ 75</a>]<BR>tion Hanta, a particular formula of benediction or salu-<BR>tation (mentioned along with स्वाहा-कार, वषट्-<BR>कार, and स्वधा-कार); rice or other offerings to<BR>be presented to a guest (according to some).<BR>—हन्-<BR>तोक्ति (˚त-उक्˚), इस्, f. ‘saying alas!’ tenderness, com-<BR>passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हपुषा
हपुषा हपुषा, f., N. of a particular sub-<BR>stance forming an article of trade (commonly called<BR>Habush, and said to be of a long form and black<BR>colour, and smelling like raw meat or fish; it is of<BR>two kinds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हबुषा
हबुषा, f. = हपुषा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हबसोर
हबसोर हबसोर, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्
हम् हम्, ind. an exclamation expressive<BR>of anger (= रुषोक्ति); of courtesy or respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हमीआण
हमीआण हमी-आण, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्बा|हंबा
हम्बा हम्बा, f. (onomatopoetic) the lowing<BR>of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्भा|हंभा
हम्भा, f. the lowing or bellowing of cattle.<BR>—हम्भा-रव, अस्, m. the cry Hambhā, lowing<BR>of kine.<BR>—हम्भारव-विराविन्, ई, इणी, इ, making<BR>a lowing or bellowing sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्भायमान
हम्भायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, lowing, bellowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्म्
हम्म् हम्म्, cl. 1. P. हम्मति, जहम्म,<BR>हम्मितुम्, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्मीर
हम्मीर हम्मीर, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Śākam-bharī (patron of Rāghava-deva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय्
हय् हय् [cf. rt. 1. हि, in sense ‘to go’], cl.<BR>1. P. हयति, जहाय, हयिष्यति, अहयीत्,<BR>हयितुम्, to go, move, (in Naigh. II. 14. हयन्तात्<BR>is enumerated among the गति-कर्माणः); to re-<BR>vere, worship; to sound; to be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय|हयः
हय हय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. हि, but connected<BR>with rt. हय् above), a horse; a symbolical expression<BR>for the number seven (that being the number of the<BR>horses of the Sun, see सप्ताश्व); a man of a par-<BR>ticular class; N. of Indra; of a Yādava king; the<BR>Yak or Bos Grunniens; (in prosody) a foot of four<BR>short syllables, proceleusmaticus; (आ), f. = हय-गन्-<BR>धा below; (ई), f. a female horse, mare.<BR>—हय-<BR>कातरा or हय-कातरिका, f. a kind of plant or tree.<BR>—हय-कोविद, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in horses.<BR>—हय-गन्ध, अम्, n. a kind of medicinal salt,<BR>= काच-लवण; (आ), f. the plant Physalis Flexuosa;<BR>another plant (= अज-मोदा).<BR>—हय-गर्दभि, इस्,<BR>m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—हय-ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘horse-<BR>necked,’ N. of a form of Viṣṇu (manifested, accord-<BR>ing to one legend, in order to recover the Veda<BR>carried off by two Daityas called Madhu and Kaiṭa-<BR>bha); N. of a Daitya (called ब्रह्म-वेद-प्र-<BR>हर्तृ, as having seized and carried off the Vedas at<BR>the dissolution of the universe caused by Brahmā's<BR>sleep at the end of the past Kalpa; in order to re-<BR>cover them Viṣṇu became incarnate as the Matsya<BR>or fish, and slew Haya-grīva); N. of a poet; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of Durgā.<BR>—हयग्रीव-हन्, आ, m. ‘slayer of<BR>Haya-grīva,’ Viṣṇu.<BR>—हयङ्-कष, अस्, m. ‘im-<BR>pelling horses,’ a driver, charioteer; epithet of Mātali<BR>(charioteer of Indra).<BR>—हय-ज्ञ, अस्, m. one who<BR>understands the points of a horse, a horse-dealer, groom,<BR>jockey.<BR>—हयज्ञ-ता, f. knowledge of horses and<BR>their management, horsemanship.<BR>—हय-ज्ञान,<BR>अम्, n. knowledge of horses.<BR>—हय-तत्त्व-ज्ञ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, acquainted with the nature of horses.<BR>—हय-द्विषत्, अन्, m. ‘hating horses,’ the buffalo.<BR>—हय-निर्घोष, अस्, m. the noise or clatter of a<BR>horse.<BR>—हय-पुच्छ, अस्, अम्, m. n. a horse's tail;<BR>(ई), f. the plant Māṣa-parṇī, q. v.<BR>—हय-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, m. ‘dear to horses,’ barley; (आ), f. = हय-गन्-<BR>धा above; the Kharjūrī tree.<BR>—हय-मार or<BR>हय-मारक, अस्, m. ‘horse-killer,’ the fragrant<BR>oleander (= कर-वीर).<BR>—हय-मारण, अस्, m.<BR>‘horse-killing,’ the sacred fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa.<BR>—हय-मेध, अस्, m. the horse-sacrifice, (see<BR>अश्व-मेध).<BR>—हयमेध-याज्, ट्, m. one who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">Page1165-c+ 77</a>]<BR>performs the horse-sacrifice.<BR>—हय-रूपिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, Ved. having the shape of a horse.<BR>—हय-लीला-<BR>वती, f., N. of a work (mentioned by Malli-nātha).<BR>—हय-वाहन, अस्, m. epithet of Revanta (son<BR>of the Sun); of Kuvera.<BR>—हय-वाहन-शङ्कर,<BR>अस्, m. red mountain-ebony or a particular tree (=<BR>रक्त-काञ्चन).<BR>—हय-शाला, f. a stable for horses.<BR>—हय-शास्त्र, अम्, n. any treatise on horses, the<BR>art or science of training and managing horses.<BR>—हय-शिरस्, अस्, n. a horse's head; a mythical<BR>monster (described as vomiting forth the fire of<BR>Aurva's wrath, which was cast into the sea); (आस्), f.<BR>‘having a horse's head,’ N. of a daughter of Vṛṣa-<BR>parvan; of a wife of Kratu.<BR>—हय-शीर्ष, अस्, m.<BR>‘having a horse's head,’ a form of Viṣṇu.<BR>—हय-<BR>शीर्ष-पञ्चरात्र, N. of a work.<BR>—हय-सङ्ग्र-<BR>हण, अम्, n. the restraining or curbing of horses,<BR>checking horses.<BR>—हयाध्यक्ष (˚य-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a superintendent of horses, head-groom.<BR>—हया-<BR>नन्द (˚य-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘horse's-joy,’ a kind of<BR>bean, Phaseolus Mungo.<BR>—हयायुर्-वेद (˚य-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, m. the science of medicine applied to<BR>horses, veterinary science.<BR>—हयारि (˚य-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. ‘horse-foe,’ the fragrant oleander, Nerium Odorum.<BR>—हयारूढ (˚य-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mounted on a<BR>horse; (अस्), m. a horseman, rider.<BR>—हयारोह (˚य-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mounted on horseback, a rider; (अस्),<BR>m. horsemanship, riding.<BR>—हयाशना (˚य-अश्˚),<BR>f. ‘horse-food,’ the gum olibanum tree.<BR>—हयेष्ट<BR>(˚य-इष्˚), अस्, m. ‘loved by horses,’ barley.<BR>—ह-<BR>योत्तम (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘best of horses,’ a well-<BR>bred or excellent horse (= आजानेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयन|हयनं|हयनः
हयन, अस्, m. a year [cf. the more usual form<BR>हायन]; (अम्), n. a covered carriage or palanquin,<BR>(also read डयन, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर|हरः
हर हर, हरक, &c. See p. 1175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरण|हरणं
हरण, हरस्, &c. See p. 1175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरमुज
हरमुज हरमुज, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरयाण
हरयाण हरयाण. See under rt. 1. हृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरवे
हरवे हरवे, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरहूरा
हरहूरा हरहूरा, f. (probably for हार-<BR>हूरा, q. v.), a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हराक
हराक हराक, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरि|हरिः
हरि 1. हरि, इस्, इस्, इ (perhaps to be connected<BR>with हिरि and rt. 2. हृ, q. v.; according to some an ab-<BR>breviated form of हरित्, p. 1167; in Uṇādi-s. IV. 118.<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. हृ, p. 1175), green, greenish<BR>yellow, yellow; reddish brown, bay, tawny; (इस्),<BR>m. green (the colour); a yellow or golden colour;<BR>a reddish brown or tawny colour; N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Kṛṣṇa (regarded as identical with Viṣṇu); of<BR>Śiva; of Brahmā; of Indra; of Yama; a man,<BR>people, (in Naigh. II. 3. हरयः is enumerated<BR>among the मनुष्य-नामानि); N. of the Soma<BR>(so called as being हरित-वर्ण, see Nirukta IV.<BR>19); a stone for crushing the Soma (Ved., Sāy.<BR>हरयः = ग्रावाणः, Ṛg-veda III. 44, 1); the<BR>moon; the sun; a ray of light; fire; wind, air; a<BR>horse; a bay horse, horse of Indra, (in Naigh. I.<BR>15. हरी, m. du., is given as ‘the horses of Indra;’<BR>and in Ṛg-veda I. 16, 1; 101, 10, &c., the plurals<BR>हरयः and हरिभिः occur; cf. हरीन्, acc. pl.<BR>‘the horses of Indra,’ in Śakuntalā, Act 1); a lion;<BR>a parrot; the Koïl or Indian cuckoo; a peacock; a<BR>goose; an ape; a frog; a snake; one of the nine<BR>Varṣas or divisions into which the known continent<BR>is divided, (see वर्ष); N. of the poet Bhartṛ-<BR>hari (by which he is usually known); N. of several<BR>other authors; a species of the Aty-aṣṭi metre; [cf.<BR>Zend zairi, ‘yellow;’ zairina, ‘yellowish’ (= ह-<BR>रिण): Gr. χλό-η, χλο-ερό-ς, χλω-ρό-ς, χλό-ο-ς,<BR>χολή: Lat. helus (holus, olus), hel-vu-s, hel-vo-lus,<BR>gilvus: Old Germ. grô-j-u, gruo-j-u, grô-ni:<BR>Angl. Sax. growan, grœn, grene: Slav. zel-ige,<BR>‘vegetables;’ zel-enu, ‘green:’ Lith. zel-iu, ‘to<BR>become green;’ zol-e, ‘grass;’ zal-ie-s, ‘green:’<BR>Hib. glas, ‘green, pale.’]<BR>—हरि-कान्त, अस्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1166-a" target="_blank">Page1166-a+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, beloved by Indra, dear to Indra; beautiful as a<BR>lion.<BR>—हरि-कृष्ण, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—हरि-<BR>केलीय, अस्, m. ‘sported in by Viṣṇu,’ the country<BR>of Bengal; (अस्, आ, अम्), belonging to or dwelling<BR>in Bengal.<BR>—हरि-केश, अस्, m. ‘yellow-haired,’<BR>epithet of Savitṛ (Ved.); N. of one of the seven<BR>principal rays of the sun (supposed to supply heat to<BR>the stars); epithet of Śiva, (according to some so<BR>called as ‘lord of Hari and Brahmā; cf. हरि, 3. क);<BR>N. of a Yakṣa (who propitiated the god Śiva and<BR>was made by him a leader of his troops and a<BR>guardian of fields and fruits; see दण्ड-पाणि).<BR>—हरि-क्रान्ता, f. a kind of plant (= विष्णु-<BR>क्रान्ता).<BR>—हरि-क्षेत्र, N. of a place.<BR>—हरि-<BR>गण, अस्, m. a troop of horses; a proper N.<BR>—हरि-गन्ध, अम्, n. a sort of sandal (= हरि-<BR>चन्दन).<BR>—हरि-गृह, अम्, n. the abode of<BR>Hari; N. of a city and district, (also called Sam-<BR>bhalpūr, = शुम्भ-पुर, एक-चक्र.)<BR>—हरि-<BR>चन्दन, अस्, अम्, m. n. a sort of yellow sandal-<BR>wood or sandal tree (= तैल-पर्णिक, इन्द्र-चन्-<BR>दन, महा-गन्ध); one of the five trees of<BR>paradise (the other four being called Pārijāta, Man-<BR>dāra, Santāna, and Kalpa); (अम्), n. saffron; moon-<BR>light; the filament of a lotus (= पद्म-केशर);<BR>the person of a lover or mistress.<BR>—हरिचन्दना-<BR>स्पद (˚न-आस्˚), अम्, n. the site of yellow sandal-<BR>wood.<BR>—हरि-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a physician<BR>(author of a commentary on the Caraka-tantra).<BR>—हरि-ज, अम्, n. (in astronomy) longitude (said<BR>to = क्षिति-ज).<BR>—हरि-जीवन-मिश्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of the author of the Snāna-sūtra-paddhati.<BR>—हरि-<BR>तुरङ्गम, अस्, m., N. of Indra, (see हर्य्-अश्व.)<BR>—हरितुरङ्गमायुध (˚म-आय्˚), अम्, n.<BR>Indra's thunderbolt.<BR>—हरि-त्रात, अस्, आ, अम्, pro-<BR>tected by Hari.<BR>—हरि-दत्त, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—हरि-दर्भ, see हरिद्-गर्भ.<BR>—हरि-दास,<BR>अस्, m. a slave or worshipper of Viṣṇu; N. of<BR>a king; of the author of a commentary on the<BR>Nyāya-kusumāñjali; of the author of the Le-<BR>khaka-muktāmaṇi.<BR>—हरि-दिन, अम्, n. ‘Hari's<BR>day,’ a particular day sacred to Viṣṇu.<BR>—हरि-<BR>दीक्षित, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—हरि-<BR>दृश्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, see Vopa-deva IV. 13.<BR>—हरि-<BR>देव, अस्, m. the asterism Śravaṇā; a proper N.<BR>—हरि-द्रव, अस्, m. green fluid; (perhaps)<BR>Soma; a powder made from the blossoms of the<BR>Nāga-keśara tree.<BR>—हरि-द्रु, उस्, m. a kind of<BR>Curcuma (= दारु-हरिद्रा, पीत-दारु); a tree (in<BR>general).<BR>—हरि-द्वार, अम्, n. ‘Viṣṇu's gate,’<BR>N. of a celebrated town and Tīrtha or sacred bathing-<BR>place (commonly called Hardvār or Hurdvār; this<BR>is the place where the Ganges finally leaves the<BR>mountainous districts for the level plains of Hin-<BR>dūstān, whence it is sometimes called Gaṅgā-dvāra;<BR>tens of thousands of pilgrims flock to this Tīrtha at<BR>particular seasons and seek priority of ablution in<BR>the sacred stream, the complete purgation from sin<BR>being supposed to depend on seizing the auspicious<BR>moment laid down by astrologers; it is called ‘Hari's<BR>gate,’ as leading to Vaikuṇṭha or Viṣṇu's heaven).<BR>—हरि-धायस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. yellow-rayed,<BR>having golden luminaries, (in Ṛg-veda III. 44, 3,<BR>Sāy. explains हरि-धायसम् by हरितो हरित-<BR>वर्णा धायसो धारका रश्मयो यस्याः.)<BR>—ह-<BR>रि-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Smṛti-<BR>sāra; of the author of the Rāma-vilāsa-kāvya; of<BR>the author of the Kaṇṭhābharaṇa-mārjana and the<BR>Kāvyādarśa-mārjana commentaries.<BR>—हरि-नामन्,<BR>अ, n. the name of Hari or Viṣṇu; (आ), m. the<BR>kidney-bean, Phaseolus Mungo.<BR>—हरि-नायक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of a work on music.<BR>—हरि-नेत्र, अम्, n. the eye of Viṣṇu; a white<BR>lotus; an eye of a greenish colour; (अस्), m. ‘having<BR>greenish eyes,’ an owl.<BR>—हरि-पद, अम्, n. (ac-<BR>cording to some) the vernal equinox.<BR>—हरि-पर्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, green-leaved; (अम्), n. a radish.<BR>—हरि-<BR>प्रबोध, N. of a work.<BR>—हरि-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>liked or loved by Viṣṇu; (अस्), m. the Kadamba<BR>tree; other plants, &c. (= पीत-भृङ्गराज; =<BR>विष्णु-कन्द; = कर-वीर; = बन्धूक); a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1166-b" target="_blank">Page1166-b+ 81</a>]<BR>conch-shell; a mad person; armour (= कञ्चुक);<BR>Śiva; (आ), f. Lakṣmī; the earth; sacred basil (=<BR>तुलसी); the twelfth day of a lunar fortnight; (अम्),<BR>n. a kind of dark sandal-wood; the root Uśīra, q. v.<BR>—हरि-बालुक, अम्, n. ‘yellow sand,’ a kind of<BR>perfume and drug (= एलवालु, q. v.).<BR>—हरि-<BR>बुङ्ग-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—हरि-भक्त,<BR>अस्, m. a worshipper of Viṣṇu.<BR>—हरि-भट्ट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of a work on music.<BR>—हरि-<BR>भद्र, अम्, n. = हरि-बालुक.<BR>—हरि-भाविनी or<BR>हरि-भाविणी, f. a woman who meditates on Viṣṇu.<BR>—हरि-भुज्, क्, m. ‘frog-eater,’ a snake.<BR>—हरि-<BR>मन्थ, अस्, m. the tree Premna Spinosa (the wood<BR>of which by attrition produces flame); the chick-pea<BR>(= चणक); N. of a particular country or district.<BR>—हरि-मन्थक, अस्, m. the chick-pea.<BR>—हरि-<BR>मन्थ-ज, अस्, m. ‘produced in the district Hari-<BR>mantha,’ the chick-pea; a sort of dark kidney-bean.<BR>—हरि-यूपीया, f., Ved., N. of a city or of a river.<BR>—हरि-योग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a yoke of<BR>bay horses, yoked with horses.<BR>—हरि-योजन, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. ‘harnesser of the Hari steeds,’ Indra; [cf.<BR>हारियोजन.]<BR>—हरि-राम, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the Dharmitāvacchedakatā-pratyāsatti-<BR>vicāra, the Navīna-mata-vicāra, the Maṅgala-vāda,<BR>and the Sāmagrī-vāda.<BR>—हरि-राय, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of the Jīcaraṇa-cihna-māhātmya.<BR>—हरि-<BR>लीला, f., N. of Vopa-deva's index to the Bhāgavata-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—हरिलीला-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a com-<BR>mentary by Hemādri on the Hari-līlā.<BR>—हरि-<BR>लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, having dark-green eyes; tawny-<BR>eyed; (अस्), m. a crab; an owl.<BR>—हरि-वंश, अस्,<BR>m. the family of Kṛṣṇa (as identified with Viṣṇu);<BR>N. of a celebrated poem supplementary to the Mahā-<BR>bhārata on the history and adventures of Kṛṣṇa<BR>and his family, (it is usually regarded as part of the<BR>greater epic, though really a comparatively modern<BR>addition to it; the poem consists of no less than<BR>16, 374 verses, comprised in three sections, called<BR>Harivaṃśa-parvan, Viṣṇu-parvan, and Bhaviṣya-<BR>parvan; in the first is contained a description of the<BR>creation of the world and a history of the solar and<BR>lunar races, the second gives a detailed biography<BR>of Kṛṣṇa, and the third an account of the future<BR>condition of the world with the corruptions about to<BR>prevail during the Kali-yuga.)<BR>—हरि-वंश-गोस्वा-<BR>मिन्, ई, m., N. of the author of the Rādhā-rasa-<BR>sudhā-nidhi.<BR>—हरि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>Hari; (आन्), m. ‘possessing bay horses,’ N. of Indra,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda VIII. 40, 9. हरिवः, voc. c., occurs.)<BR>—हरि-वर्पस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having a verdant<BR>form, tinted with green, green-coloured (said of the<BR>earth).<BR>—हरि-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—हरि-वर्ष, अम्, n. one of the nine divisions<BR>of Jambu-dvīpa or the known continent, (the country<BR>between the Niṣadha and Hema-kūṭa mountains,<BR>see वर्ष, p. 893); (अस्), m., N. of a king of<BR>Niṣadha (son of Agnīdhra),<BR>—हरि-वल्लभ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘beloved by Viṣṇu,’ N. of the author of the<BR>Sudhodaya; (आ), f. epithet of Lakṣmī; sacred basil<BR>(= तुलसी); another plant (= जया).<BR>—हरि-वा-<BR>सर, अम्, n. Viṣṇu's day (the eleventh or twelfth<BR>lunar day, or according to some, the first quarter of<BR>the twelfth lunar day).<BR>—हरि-वाहन, अस्, m.<BR>‘Viṣṇu-bearer,’ Garuḍa; ‘having bay horses,’ Indra<BR>[cf. हर्य्-अश्व, हरि-हय].<BR>—हरि-वीज, अस्, m.<BR>‘Viṣṇu's seed,’ yellow orpiment, (see हरिताल.)<BR>—हरि-वृष, अम्, n. a division of the continent,<BR>(see हरि-वर्ष.)<BR>—हरि-शङ्कर, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a scribe; of a place.<BR>—हरि-शयन, अम्, n. the<BR>sleep of Viṣṇu.<BR>—हरि-शर, अस्, m. ‘having Viṣṇu<BR>for an arrow,’ epithet of Śiva, (Viṣṇu having served<BR>Śiva as the shaft which set the cities of Tripura on<BR>fire.)<BR>—हरि-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—हरि-<BR>शिप्र, अस्, m., Ved. ‘ruddy-jawed,’ epithet of Indra.<BR>—हरि-श्चन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम् (see चन्द्र), Ved.<BR>having golden-coloured splendor; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>the twenty-eighth king of the solar dynasty in the<BR>Tretā age, (he was son of Tri-śaṅku, and was cele-<BR>brated for his piety; according to the Mārkaṇḍeya-<BR>Purāṇa, which gives a most interesting legend de-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1166-c" target="_blank">Page1166-c+ 81</a>]<BR>tailing the history of this prince, he gave up his<BR>whole country, sold his wife and son, and finally<BR>himself, to satisfy the demands of Viśvā-mitra, whom<BR>he had provoked by interfering to protect the Sciences<BR>who were becoming mastered by this intensely<BR>austere sage; after enduring incredible sufferings,<BR>Hari-ścandra won the pity of the gods and was<BR>raised with his subjects to heaven; on the other<BR>hand, in the Sabhā-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata,<BR>verse 489 &c., his performance of the Rāja-sūya<BR>sacrifice is stated to have been the cause of his<BR>elevation, and in the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa quite another<BR>legend is told about him, see under शुनः-शेप,<BR>p. 1014: in later legends Hari-ścandra is represented<BR>as insidiously induced by Nārada to relate his actions<BR>with unbecoming pride, whereupon he was degraded<BR>from Svarga, one stage at each sentence, till stopping<BR>in time and doing homage to the gods he was fixed<BR>with his capital in mid-air; his aerial city is popu-<BR>larly believed to be still visible in the skies at parti-<BR>cular times; cf. शौभ); (अम्), n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—हरिश्चन्द्र-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—हरिश्चन्द्र-पुर, अम्, n. the city of Hari-<BR>ścandra (= शौभ, see above).<BR>—हरि-श्मशारु or<BR>हरि-श्मश्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. ruddy-bearded, golden-<BR>bearded, having a yellow beard.<BR>—हरि-श्रम,<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—हरि-श्रवा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—हरि-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. blessed with or abounding<BR>in horses.<BR>—हरि-षाच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. enjoying or par-<BR>taking of Soma, (Sāy. = सोमस्य सम्भक्तृ, Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 94, 12.)<BR>—हरि-षेण, अस्, m. (षेण for<BR>सेन fr. सेना), N. of the tenth of the Jaina Cakra-<BR>vartins.<BR>—हरि-ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम् (ष्ठा for स्था),<BR>Ved. one who stands over horses, a guider of horses,<BR>(Sāy. = हर्योः स्थातृ, Ṛg-veda VI. 17, 2.)<BR>—ह-<BR>रि-सख, अस्, m. ‘friend of Indra,’ a Gandharva.<BR>—हरि-सङ्कीर्तन, अम्, n. the act of pronouncing<BR>or repeating the name of Viṣṇu (supposed to possess<BR>great efficacy).<BR>—हरि-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of Hari,’<BR>N. of Arjuna; of the tenth Cakra-vartin, (also called<BR>Hari-ṣeṇa.)<BR>—हरि-सूक्त, अम्, n. a hymn addressed<BR>to Hari.<BR>—हरि-सूनु, उस्, m. ‘son of Hari,’ N. of<BR>Arjuna.<BR>—हरि-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. and हरि-स्तुति, इस्,<BR>f., N. of two Vedānta hymns (in praise of Viṣṇu).<BR>—हरि-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a priest; of the author<BR>of a commentary on the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—ह-<BR>रि-हय, अस्, m. ‘having bay or gold-coloured<BR>horses,’ epithet of Indra; of the Sun; of Skanda;<BR>of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—हरि-हर, अस्, m. a particular form<BR>of deity consisting of Viṣṇu and Śiva conjoined;<BR>N. of a king; of a poet; of several other persons.<BR>—हरि-हर-कथा, f. the repeating of the names<BR>of Hari and Hara (i. e. of Viṣṇu and Śiva).<BR>—हरि-<BR>हर-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. ‘the sacred place of Viṣṇu and<BR>Śiva conjoined,’ N. of a particular Tīrtha and place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR>—हरि-हर-पुरी, N. of a preceptor.<BR>—हरिहर-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a commen-<BR>tary.<BR>—हरि-हरात्मक (˚र-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>identified with Viṣṇu and Śiva in their united state;<BR>(अस्), m. Garuḍa; the bull of Śiva (= शिव-वृष);<BR>Dakṣa (according to some); (अम्), n. = हरिहर-<BR>क्षेत्र.<BR>—हरि-हेति, इस्, f. the weapon of Viṣṇu,<BR>i. e. the Cakra or discus.<BR>—हरिहेति-हूति, इस्, m. =<BR>चक्र-वाक, a sort of duck.<BR>—हर्य्-अक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>‘green-eyed, brown-eyed,’ a lion; N. of Kuvera;<BR>of Śiva; of a son of Pṛthu.<BR>—हर्य्-अङ्ग, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—हर्य्-अश्व, अस्, m. ‘having bay<BR>horses called Hari,’ N. of Indra; of Śiva; of a son of<BR>Dṛḍhāśva; of several other persons; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of 5000 sons of Dakṣa.<BR>—हर्य्-आत्मन्, आ, m.<BR>epithet of Uttama (one of the twenty-eight Vyāsas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिक|हरिकः
हरिक, अस्, m. a horse of a yellowish or reddish<BR>brown colour (= हालक); a thief, (in this sense<BR>evidently fr. rt. 1. हृ); a gambler with dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिण|हरिणः
हरिण, अस्, ई, अम् (the fem. may equally belong<BR>to हरित, next col.), greenish or yellowish or reddish<BR>white, pale, whitish; (अस्), m. yellowish or reddish<BR>white (the colour); white (the colour); a deer, ante-<BR>lope, fawn, stag (one of five kinds, others being<BR>called ऋष्य, रुरु, पृषत, मृग); a goose; a<BR>minor division of the world; the sun; N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">Page1167-a+ 81</a>]<BR>of Śiva; (ई), f. green (the colour); yellow jasmine;<BR>a female deer, doe; a golden image; one of the<BR>four kinds of women, an excellent woman (= चि-<BR>त्रिणी, corresponding to the kind of man termed<BR>मृग); turmeric (= हरिता); madder (= मञ्-<BR>जिष्ठा); a species of the Aty-aṣṭi metre (= त-<BR>रुणी).<BR>—हरिण-कलङ्क, अस्, m. ‘deer-spotted,’<BR>epithet of the moon.<BR>—हरिण-धामन्, आ, m.<BR>the moon.<BR>—हरिण-नयन, अस्, ई, अम्, deer-<BR>eyed, fawn-eyed, having eyes like a deer.<BR>—हरिण-<BR>नर्तक, अस्, m. a minstrel of Indra's heaven (=<BR>किन्-नर).<BR>—हरिण-प्लुत, अम्, आ, n. f. a kind of<BR>metre (described by some as a stanza having eleven<BR>syllables in every first and third Pāda, and twelve in<BR>every second and fourth; by others two kinds of<BR>metre are given).<BR>—हरिण-लोचन = हरिण-न-<BR>यन.<BR>—हरिण-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, deer-hearted,<BR>faint-hearted, timid.<BR>—हरिणाक्ष (˚ण-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, deer-eyed, fawn-eyed; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Śiva; (ई), f. a woman with beautiful eyes; a kind<BR>of perfume (= हट्ट-विलासिनी).<BR>—हरिणाङ्क (˚ण-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘deer-marked,’ the moon; [cf. ह-<BR>रिण-कलङ्क.]<BR>—हरिणान्तर (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a species of deer (= भार्याटिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणक|हरिणकः
हरिणक, अस्, m. a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाय
हरिणाय, Nom. A. हरिणायते, &c., to become<BR>a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणी
हरिणी, see under हरिण.<BR>—हरिणी-वृत्त, अम्,<BR>n. the Hariṇī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्
हरित्, त्, त्, त् (in Uṇādi-s. I. 99. said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. हृ, perhaps for original हरत्; cf. 1. हरि,<BR>हिरि, हिरण), green, of a green colour; greenish<BR>yellow, yellowish, golden-coloured; (त्), m. green<BR>(the colour); a swift horse; a horse of the Sun, (in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 50, 8. सप्त-हरितः is explained by<BR>Sāy. as ‘the seven horses of the Sun,’ symbolical of<BR>सप्त रश्मयः, ‘the seven rays;’ see also Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 115, 4, where हरितः is explained by ‘the<BR>Sun's horses,’ as well as by रस-हरण-सीलान्<BR>रश्मीन्, ‘the rays which take up the moisture;’ the<BR>seven horses of the Sun are sometimes called mares,<BR>cf. शुन्ध्यु; they probably really symbolize the<BR>seven days of the week); the kidney-bean, Phase-<BR>olus Mungo; a lion; the sun; Viṣṇu; (त्), m. n.<BR>grass; (त्), f. a quarter, region; a point of the com-<BR>pass; turmeric; [cf. according to some, Gr. χάρι-τες,<BR>χόρτος; perhaps Lat. viridi-s (for gviridis);<BR>Goth. gulth, gras; Angl. Sax. gold, grœs.]<BR>—ह-<BR>रित्-पर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, green-leaved, having green<BR>leaves; (अम्), n. a radish; [cf. हरि-पर्ण.]<BR>—ह-<BR>रिद्-अश्व, अस्, m. ‘whose horses are called Harit,’<BR>the sun, (see हरित् above.)<BR>—हरिद्-गर्भ, अस्,<BR>m. a green or yellowish Kuśa grass with broad leaves<BR>(= पृथु-च्छद; also read हरि-दर्भ).<BR>—ह-<BR>रिद्-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, green-coloured, of a yellowish<BR>golden colour.<BR>—हरिन्-मणि, इस्, m. ‘green-gem,’<BR>an emerald.<BR>—हरिन्-मुद्ग, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>kidney-bean (= शारद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित|हरितं|हरितः
हरित, अस्, आ or हरिणी, अम् (connected with<BR>हरिण above; cf. its fem. हरिणी; cf. also 2. भ-<BR>रित with its fem. भरिणी), green, of a green<BR>colour; reddish brown or tawny; grassy, verdant;<BR>dark blue; (अस्), m. green (the colour); a lion; a<BR>kind of grass (= मन्थानक); N. of a son of<BR>Yuvanāśva; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a Gotra; (आ), f.<BR>Dūrvā grass; turmeric; a brown-coloured grape;<BR>other plants, = जयन्ती; = पाची; = नील-दूर्वा;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of perfume (= स्थौणेयक).<BR>—हरित-च्छद, अस्, आ, अम्, green-leaved, having<BR>green leaves.<BR>—हरित-तृण, अम्, n. green grass.<BR>—हरित-पत्त्रिका, f. ‘green-leaved,’ a kind of<BR>creeping plant (= पाची).<BR>—हरित-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>green-coloured.<BR>—हरित-शाक, अस्, m. the Śigru<BR>plant.<BR>—हरिताश्मन् (˚त-अश्˚), अ, n. ‘green-coloured<BR>stone,’ an emerald; a turquoise; sulphate of copper<BR>or blue vitriol.<BR>—हरिताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a son of Su-dyumna.<BR>—हरिती-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>made green, coloured green, made verdant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितक|हरितकं
हरितक, अस्, m. a green vegetable, pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताय
हरिताय, Nom. A. हरितायते, &c., to become<BR>green or verdant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितायत्
हरितायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, becoming green.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताल|हरितालं|हरितालः
हरिताल, अस्, m. a kind of pigeon of a yellowish<BR>green colour; (ई), f. Dūrvā grass; a streak or line<BR>in the sky (= आकाश-रेखा); a sort of creeper (=<BR>खड्ग-पत्त्र); a kind of tree (according to Sāy.);<BR>the fourth day of the light half of the month Bhādra;<BR>(अम्), n. yellow orpiment or sulphuret of arsenic<BR>(described as the seed or seminal energy of Viṣṇu,<BR>= हरेर् वीर्यम्).<BR>—हरिताल-जनक, अस्, m. orpi-<BR>ment-producer (a word employed in modern Sanskrit<BR>to express the metal arsenic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालक|हरितालकं|हरितालकः
हरितालक, अस्, m. a kind of pigeon of a yellowish<BR>green colour; (अम्), n. yellow orpiment; painting<BR>the person, theatrical decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालिका
हरितालिका, f. Dūrvā grass; the fourth day of the<BR>light half of the month Bhādra.<BR>—हरितालिका-व्रत,<BR>अम्, n. a particular religious observance on the above<BR>day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रा
हरिद्रा, f. turmeric; the root of turmeric pow-<BR>dered, (forty-six synonyms of this plant are given.)<BR>—हरिद्राक्त (˚रा-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, smeared or<BR>stained with turmeric.<BR>—हरिद्रा-गणपति, इस्, or<BR>हरिद्रा-गणेश, अस्, m. a particular form of the god<BR>Gaṇesa (in whose honour a Mantra is repeated, ac-<BR>companied with offerings mixed with turmeric).<BR>—हरिद्राङ्ग (˚रा-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘yellow-bodied,’<BR>a kind of yellow bird (= हरिताल).<BR>—हरिद्राभ<BR>(˚रा-आभ), अस्, आ, अम्, resembling turmeric, of a<BR>yellow colour; (अस्), m. the plant Pīta-śāla, q. v.;<BR>zedoary (= कर्पूरक).<BR>—हरिद्रा-राग or हरि-<BR>द्रा-रागक, अस्, आ, अम्, turmeric-coloured; unsteady<BR>in affection or attachment, fickle, capricious (like the<BR>colour of turmeric which does not last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्
1. हरिमन्, आ, m. (for 2. see under rt. 1. हृ),<BR>yellowness; yellowness (of the body), a kind of<BR>disease, (Ṛg-veda I. 50, 11, &c.); paleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिय|हरियः
हरिय, अस्, m. a horse of a yellowish or reddish<BR>colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरीतकी
हरीतकी, f. the yellow Myrobalan tree, Termi-<BR>nalia Chebula, (twenty-eight synonyms and seven<BR>varieties of this are enumerated; a form हरीतक<BR>is also found.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरि|हरिः
हरि 2. हरि, ind. alas!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्त
हरिमन्त हरिमन्त, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>Āṅgirasa (author of the hymn Ṛg-veda IX. 72).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिले
हरिले हरिले, ind. (according to some) a<BR>vocative particle used in addressing a female slave<BR>(in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिष|हरिषः
हरिष हरिष, अस्, m. (a modern form of<BR>हर्ष), joy, happiness (according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरीषा
हरीषा हरीषा, f. a particular kind of<BR>seasoning or condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणु|हरेणुः
हरेणु हरेणु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 1. fr. rt. 1. हृ), pease, pulse; a creeper marking<BR>the boundary of a village; N. of Laṅkā; (उस्), f. a<BR>sort of drug or perfume (= रेणुका, q. v.); a re-<BR>spectable woman; a copper-coloured deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणुक|हरेणुकः
हरेणुक, अस्, m. pease, pulse (= कलाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्तव्य|हर्त्तव्य
हर्तव्य हर्तव्य, हर्तृ, &c. See p. 1175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मन्|हर्म्मन्
हर्मन् हर्मन्, आ, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. हृ),<BR>gaping, yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मित|हर्म्मित|हर्म्मितं
हर्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, yawned; thrown, cast, sent;<BR>burned [cf. घर्म].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मुट|हर्मुटः|हर्म्मुट|हर्म्मुटः
हर्मुट हर्मुट, अस्, m. (according to some)<BR>the sun; a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्य|हर्म्म्यं|हर्म्यं
हर्म्य हर्म्य, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 1. हृ<BR>in the sense of ‘to captivate or charm the mind;’<BR>but more probably to be connected with घर्म),<BR>a hole in the ground for cooking, a kind of pit or<BR>oven for holding fire, fire-place, hearth; a domestic<BR>hearth, home; house, building, palace, mansion,<BR>any large building or residence of a man of wealth,<BR>[cf. Zend zairimya; Lat. formus]; a fiery pit,<BR>place of torment, region of darkness, abode of evil<BR>spirits, abode of the departed, the nether world; (अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">Page1167-c+ 78</a>]<BR>आ, अम्), living in houses.<BR>—हर्म्य-पृष्ठ, अम्,<BR>n. the roof or upper room of a palace.<BR>—हर्म्य-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, living in a palace.<BR>—हर्म्य-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. standing near a hearth or fire-place;<BR>being in a house.<BR>—हर्म्य-स्थल, अम्, n. the<BR>room or chamber of a mansion or palace.<BR>—हर्-<BR>म्याङ्गन (˚य-अङ्˚), अम्, n. the court of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्|हर्य्य्
हर्य् हर्य्, cl. 1. P. हर्यति (sometimes<BR>also A. -ते), जहर्य, हर्यिष्यति, अहर्-<BR>यीत्, हर्यितुम्, Ved. to desire, yearn after, love,<BR>like, be pleased with, (in Naigh. II. 6. enumerated<BR>among the कान्ति-कर्माणः); to worship, pray to;<BR>to take [cf. rt. 1. हृ]; to threaten; to be weary; to<BR>go, (in Naigh. II. 14. enumerated among the गति-<BR>कर्माणः): Caus. हर्ययति, -यितुम्, Aor. अज-<BR>हर्यत्: Desid. जिहर्यिषति: Intens. जाहर्यते,<BR>जाहर्यीति, जाहर्ति; [cf. Gr. χαίρω, χαρ-ά, χάρ-μα,<BR>χάρι-ς, χαρίζομαι, χαρί-εις, γέλως, γελάω: Lat.<BR>gra-tu-s, grat-ia (Osc. her-est, Herentati-s, ‘Ve-<BR>nus:’ Umbr. heriest): Goth. faihu-gair-n-s, ‘ava-<BR>ricious;’ gair-uni, ‘affection;’ gailjan, gôljan:<BR>Old Germ. ger, giri, ‘desirous;’ geri, giri, ‘greedi-<BR>ness;’ gerôn, ‘to desire:’ Angl. Sax. gal, gagol:<BR>Lith. gor-u-ti, gor (?) : Slav. zel-e-ti (?) .]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यत्
हर्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. desiring, liking, lov-<BR>ing, (Sāy. = कामयमान; in Ṛg-veda I. 57, 2.<BR>according to Sāy. हर्यतः = प्रेप्सतः or शोभ-<BR>नः, see the next.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यत|हर्यतः|हर्य्यत|हर्य्यतः
हर्यत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. amiable, beloved, (Sāy.<BR>= स्पृहणीय, Ṛg-veda III. 5, 3); agreeable,<BR>pleasant, delicious (said of Soma); (अस्), m. a horse;<BR>a steed fit for the Aśva-medha sacrifice; N. of the<BR>author of a hymn in the Ṛg-veda, (see प्रागाथ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यमाण
हर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desiring, wishing,<BR>loving, (Sāy. = कामयमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यश्व|हर्यश्वः|हर्य्यश्व|हर्य्यश्वः
हर्यश्व हर्य्-अश्व. See p. 1166, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्ष|हर्षः
हर्ष हर्ष, हर्ष-कर, &c. See p. 1176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षण|हर्षणं|हर्षणः
हर्षण, हर्षित, &c. See p. 1176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षीका
हर्षीका हर्षीका, f. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्
हल् 1. हल्, cl. 1. P. हलति, जहाल, अहा-<BR>लीत्, &c., to plough, make furrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल|हलं|हलः
हल, अम्, n. a plough; ugliness, deformity, =<BR>वैरूप्य; (आ), f. the earth; water; spirituous<BR>liquor, wine.<BR>—हल-धर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, plough-<BR>holding, having a plough; (अस्), m. a ploughman;<BR>epithet of Bala-rāma (as bearing a peculiar weapon<BR>shaped like a ploughshare; cf. सीर-पाणि).<BR>—हल-<BR>भूति, इस्, f. agriculture, husbandry.<BR>—हल-भृत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, plough-holding, possessing a plough; (त्), m.<BR>a ploughman; Bala-rāma; [cf. सीर-भृत्.]<BR>—हल-<BR>भृति, इस्, f. ploughing, agriculture, husbandry;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a Muni (= उप-वर्ष, कृत-कोटि,<BR>अ-याचित).<BR>—हल-मुखी, f. a kind of metre.<BR>—हल-राक्ष, अम्, n. a kind of shrub (=<BR>आहुल्य).<BR>—हल-हति, इस्, f. ‘plough-striking,’<BR>ploughing, furrowing.<BR>—हलायुध (˚ल-आय्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘plough-weaponed,’ Bala-rāma, (see above); N.<BR>of a poet (son of Dhanañ-jaya); of the author of<BR>the Brāhmaṇa-sarvasva; of the author of the Purāṇa-<BR>sarvasva; of the author of the Abhidhāna-ratnamālā<BR>lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलय
हलय, Nom. P. हलयति, &c., to plough (=<BR>हलिं गृह्णाति, Vopa-deva XXI. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाह|हलाहः
हलाह, अस्, m. a horse of a mixed or variegated<BR>colour, (also read हालाह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलि|हलिः
हलि, इस्, m. a large plough, ploughshare (=<BR>जित्या, Vopa-deva XXVI. 20; = वृहद्-धल, q. v.);<BR>a furrow (according to some); agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिन्
हलिन्, ई, m. a ploughman, agriculturist, cultivator;<BR>N. of Bala-rāma; (इनी), f. a number of ploughs;<BR>a kind of plant (= लाङ्गलिकी).<BR>—हलि-प्रिय, अस्,<BR>m. ‘dear to agriculturists,’ the Kadamba tree; (आ),<BR>f. spirituous liquor (= मदिरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हली
हली, f. the plant Kali-kārī, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीषा
हलीषा, f. (probably fr. हल + ईषा), = लाङ्ग-<BR>लीषा, the handle of a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्य|हल्यं
हल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ploughed or tilled,<BR>arable; belonging to or proceeding from ugliness or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">Page1168-a+ 74</a>]<BR>deformity, ugly; (आ), f. a multitude of ploughs;<BR>(अम्), n. a ploughed field, arable land; ugliness; de-<BR>formity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्
हल् 2. हल्, m. n. (in Pāṇini's system) a<BR>technical expression for all the consonants; any con-<BR>sonant.<BR>—हल्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ending in a con-<BR>sonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलद्दी
हलद्दी हलद्दी, f. turmeric (= हरिद्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलहला
हलहला हल-हला (an imitative sound),<BR>halloo, hallooing.<BR>—हलहला-शब्द, अस्, m. shout-<BR>ing Hala-halā, hallooing, shout, outcry, tumult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हला
हला हला, f. a female friend, (see also<BR>हला under हल); (हला), ind. a vocative particle<BR>used in addressing a female friend who is an equal<BR>(in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाहल|हलाहलं|हलाहलः
हलाहल हलाहल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (= हाल-<BR>हल, q. v., sometimes also written हलहल, and<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. हल्), a sort of deadly poison [cf.<BR>कालकूट at p. 226, col. 2]; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>snake (= ब्रह्म-सर्प); a Jaina or Bauddha sage;<BR>a sort of lizard or newt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीन|हलीनः
हलीन हलीन, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>हल्), the Teak tree (= शाक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीमक|हलीमकः
हलीमक 1. हलीमक, अम्, n. (probably con-<BR>nected with 1. हरिमन् at p. 1167, col. 2), a sort<BR>of jaundice, paleness or yellowness of skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलुआण
हलुआण हलुआण or हलूआण, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लक|हल्लकं
हल्लक हल्लक, अम्, n. the red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लन|हल्लनं
हल्लन हल्लन, अम्, n. rolling or tossing<BR>about, rolling about in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीश|हल्लीशं
हल्लीश हल्लीश, अम्, n. one of the eighteen<BR>Upa-rūpakas or minor dramatic entertainments (de-<BR>scribed as a piece in one act, consisting chiefly of<BR>singing and dancing by one male and seven, eight,<BR>or ten female performers), a ballet; a circular dance<BR>(performed by women).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीशक|हल्लीशकः
हल्लीशक, अस्, m. dancing in a ring (as performed<BR>by women).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीष|हल्लीषं
हल्लीष, हल्लीषक, = हल्लीश above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीस
हल्लीस, हल्लीसक, = हल्लीश above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव|हवः
हव 1. हव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. हु), an oblation,<BR>burnt-offering, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवङ्ग
हवङ्ग, अस्, m. (probably हवं + ग), eating<BR>rice and curds from a metal cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवन|हवनं|हवनः
1. हवन, अम्, n. the act of offering an oblation<BR>with fire; an oblation to the gods, burnt-offering,<BR>sacrifice; (ई), f. a hole made in the ground for the<BR>sacrificial fire which is to receive a burnt-oblation.<BR> — 1. हवन-स्यद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hastening to<BR>a sacrifice.<BR>—हवनायुस् (˚न-आय्˚), उस्, m. ‘having<BR>the burnt-offering for its life,’ fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनीय|हवनीयं
हवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be offered with fire, fit<BR>for an oblation or sacrifice, sacrificial; (अम्), n. any-<BR>thing fit for an oblation; clarified butter, ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवित्री
हवित्री, f. a hole made in the ground for holding<BR>the sacred fire for an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्य|हविष्यं
हविष्य, अम्, n. anything fit for an oblation;<BR>clarified butter; wild rice (or any similar wild grain);<BR>rice mixed with ghee; a hymn in praise of oblations<BR>(Ved).<BR>—हविष्य-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, eating clarified<BR>butter; (क्), m. fire.<BR>—हविष्यान्न (˚य-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. food fit to be eaten during certain holy days<BR>(or during the continuance of fasts and other re-<BR>ligious observances); any particularly pure food (as<BR>wheat, cow's milk, &c.).<BR>—हविष्याशिन् (˚य-आश्˚),<BR>ई, इनी, इ, devouring clarified butter, (Manu XI. 218);<BR>(ई), m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्यन्तीय
हविष्यन्तीय. See under हविस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविस्
हविस्, इस्, n. anything offered as an oblation with<BR>fire, clarified butter, ghee; an oblation or burnt-<BR>offering (in general); water, (in Naigh. I. 12. enu-<BR>merated among the उदक-नामानि); epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—हविः-शेष, अस्, m. the residue of an obla-<BR>tion.<BR>—हविर्-अशन, अम्, n. the act of devouring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">Page1168-b+ 79</a>]<BR>clarified butter; (अस्), m. ‘consuming oblations,’ fire.<BR>—हविर्-गन्धा, f. ‘smelling like clarified butter,’<BR>the Śamī tree.<BR>—हविर्-गेह, अम्, n. any house or<BR>chamber in which an oblation is offered, a sacrificial<BR>hall.<BR>—हविर्-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. a giver of obla-<BR>tions, (said of Rudra, Ṛg-veda IV. 3, 7.)<BR>—हविर्-<BR>धान, अम्, n., Ved. ‘ghee-containing,’ an oblation;<BR>(ए), n. du. the two receptacles or vehicles on which<BR>the Soma and other offerings are put; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of the author of the hymns Ṛg-veda X. 11 — 13<BR>(having the patronymic Āṅgi).<BR>—हविर्-भुज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, eating clarified butter; (क्), m. fire; N. of the<BR>Pitṛs of the Kṣatriyas.<BR>—हविर्-भू, ऊस्, f., N. of<BR>the wife of Pulastya.<BR>—हविर्-मथि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>destroying or obstructing oblations, impeding sacrificial<BR>rites.<BR>—हविर्-मन्थ, अस्, m. a kind of plant (= ग-<BR>णिकारी).<BR>—हविर्-यज्ञ, अस्, m. a particular sacrifice,<BR>N. of the first book of the Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa (ac-<BR>cording to the Mādhyandina-śākhā).<BR>—हविर्-यज्ञ-<BR>संस्था, f. a kind of sacrifice, (seven Havir-yajña-<BR>saṃsthās are enumerated, viz. Agny-ādheya, Agni-<BR>hotra, Darśa-pūrṇamāsau, Cāturmāsyāni, Paśu-ban-<BR>dha, Sautrāmaṇī, and Pāka-yajña.)<BR>—हविर्-याजिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘ghee-offerer,’ a priest.<BR>—हविष्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. performing a sacrifice.<BR>—हविष्-पङ्क्ति, इस्,<BR>m., Ved., scil. यज्ञ, a sacrifice consisting of five<BR>oblations.<BR>—हविष्-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the lord of a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—हविष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of<BR>oblations; (अन्तस्), m. pl., N. of a class of Pitṛs (re-<BR>garded as progenitors of Kṣatriyas and as descended<BR>from Aṅgiras; Manu III. 197, 198).<BR>—हविष्य्-<BR>अन्तीय, अम्, n., N. of nineteen Vedic texts begin-<BR>ning हविष्यन्तम्, (Manu XI. 251.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्य|हव्यं
1. हव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit to be offered in oblations,<BR>(Sāy. = होतव्य); (अस्), m., N. of a son of Atri;<BR>(अम्), n. an oblation or offering to the gods (as dis-<BR>tinguished fr. कव्य, q. v.); clarified butter, ghee.<BR>—हव्य-कव्य, अम्, n. oblations both to the gods<BR>and to the spirits of deceased ancestors, (also आनि, n.<BR>pl.)<BR>—हव्य-जुष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. the favour of an<BR>oblation, an acceptable oblation, (Sāy. = हविः-सेवा.)<BR>—हव्य-दाति, इस्, f., Ved. ‘oblation-giving,’ a sacri-<BR>ficial offering; (इस्, इस्, इ), giving sacrificial offerings.<BR>—हव्य-पाक, अस्, m. an oblation (of rice, barley,<BR>&c.) cooked with butter and milk for presentation to<BR>the gods; the vessel in which such an oblation is<BR>prepared.<BR>—हव्य-वाह्, ट्, or हव्य-वाह, अस्, m.<BR>‘oblation-bearer,’ Agni or fire.<BR>—हव्य-वाहन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, bearing oblations, conveying oblations;<BR>(अस्), m. fire; epithet of the ninth Kalpa; N. of a<BR>son of Śuci.<BR>—हव्य-वाहिनी, f. ‘oblation-bearer,’<BR>N. of a goddess.<BR>—हव्य-सूद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. flowing<BR>with oblations, affording oblations (said of cows as<BR>affording milk that yields butter for sacrificial rites).<BR>—हव्याश (˚य-आश) or हव्याशन (˚य-अश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘oblation-eater,’ fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव|हवः
हव 2. हव, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. ह्वे), call-<BR>ing, call; invocation, prayer; order, command;<BR>challenging, defying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवन|हवनं|हवनः
2. हवन, अम्, n. the act of calling, an invoca-<BR>tion; challenging to battle.<BR>—हवन-श्रुत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. listening to an invocation.<BR>—२. हवन-स्यद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hastening to battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवस्
हवस्, अस्, n., Ved. a song of praise, hymn,<BR>prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवीमन्
हवीमन्, आ, m., Ved. invocation; challenging;<BR>battle, (Sāy. = सङ्ग्राम, Ṛg-veda VII. 83, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्य|हव्यं
2. हव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be invoked, (Sāy.<BR>= आह्वातव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवा
हवा हवा or हवाव, ind. (a term imply-<BR>ing) undoubtedly, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्
हस् 1. हस्, cl. 1. P. हसति, जहास, हसि-<BR>ष्यति, अहसीत्, हसितुम्, to laugh, smile;<BR>to laugh at, ridicule (with acc.); to resemble, (see<BR>हसत्): Pass. हस्यते, Aor. अहासि: Caus. हासयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अजीहसत्, to cause to laugh, make laugh,<BR>provoke laughter: Desid. जिहसिषति: Intens. जा-<BR>हस्यते, जाहस्ति, to laugh immoderately; [cf. per-<BR>haps Gr. τω-θεία, τω-θάζω; probably Lat. histrio.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्
2. हस्, Ved. laughter, joy; brightness, brilliance.<BR>—हस्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. causing joy or<BR>prosperity; making bright, (Sāy. = वृद्धेः कर्तृ<BR>or प्रभासक, Ṛg-veda IV. 7, 3.)<BR>—हस्-कार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing brightness or radiance (said<BR>of lightning; Sāy. = दीप्ति-कर, Ṛg-veda I. 23,<BR>12).<BR>—हस्-कृति, इस्, f., Ved. a song of praise; (इस्,<BR>इस्, इ), causing joy, (Sāy. = हास-कारिन् or हर्षस्य<BR>सूचक, Ṛg-veda VIII. 89, 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस|हसः
हस, अस्, m. laughter, laughing, a laugh; de-<BR>rision.<BR>—हसा-मुदौ, m. du., Ved. laughing and<BR>rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसत्
हसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, laughing, smiling; resem-<BR>bling (i. e. smiling like, with acc., Kirāt. VIII. 44);<BR>(अन्ती), f. a portable fire-pan, small furnace, chafing-<BR>dish; Arabian jasmine; a kind of Śākinī, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन|हसनं
हसन, अम्, n. the act of laughing, laughter, a<BR>laugh; (आ), f. laughter; a joke, subject of laughter<BR>or ridicule, (Ṛg-veda IX. 112, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसनी
हसनी, f. a portable fire-place or chafing-dish.<BR>—हसनी-मणि, इस्, m. ‘furnace-jewel,’ fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसनीय
हसनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, laughable; to be ridiculed,<BR>ridiculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन्तिका|हसंतिका
हसन्तिका, f. (fr. हसन्ती), a portable fire-place<BR>or small furnace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसिका
हसिका, f. laughter, derision, jesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसित|हसितं|हसितः
हसित, अस्, आ, अम्, laughed, laughing, smiling;<BR>expanded, blossomed, blown (as a flower); (अम्), n.<BR>laughter, jesting; smiling; the bow of Kāma (god<BR>of love).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसितृ
हसितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who laughs, a laugher,<BR>smiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसित्वा
हसित्वा, ind. having laughed, having smiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्र|हस्रः
हस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, smiling; stupid, ignorant, a<BR>fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास|हासः
हास, अस्, m. laughing, laughter; mirth, merry-<BR>making, joy; derision.<BR>—हास-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>causing laughter, ridiculous; laughing, merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासक|हासकः
हासक, अस्, m. a laugher; one who causes<BR>laughter, a buffoon, merry-andrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासमान
हासमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. laughing, being de-<BR>lighted, (Sāy. = हासं कुर्वत्, हर्ष-युक्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिका
हासिका, f. laughter, mirth, merry-making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिन्
हासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, laughing, smiling, making merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्य|हास्यं|हास्यः
हास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be laughed at, laughable,<BR>ridiculous; (अम्), n. laughter, laughing, mirth (one<BR>of the ten Rasas, see रस), jest, amusement; ridi-<BR>cule, derision.<BR>—हास्य-ता, f. laughableness, ridicu-<BR>lousness.<BR>—हास्य-पदवी, f. ‘road of laughter,’<BR>ridicule, laughter, (हास्य-पदवीं या, to expose<BR>one's self to laughter, incur ridicule.)<BR>—हास्य-रस,<BR>अस्, m. the sentiment of humour, sense of humour,<BR>comic vein, facetiousness (the fifth of the ten Rasas,<BR>see रस).<BR>—हास्यार्णव (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘ocean<BR>of mirth,’ N. of a drama by Jagad-īśvara.<BR>—हास्या-<BR>स्पद (˚य-आस्˚), अम्, n. a laughing-stock, butt for<BR>derision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त|हस्तं|हस्तः
हस्त हस्त, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>III. 86. fr. rt. 1. हस्), the hand; the thirteenth as-<BR>terism, (see below); the fore-arm, cubit; a measure<BR>of length from the elbow to the tip of the middle<BR>finger (= twenty-four Aṅgulas or about eighteen<BR>inches); an elephant's trunk; (in prosody) an ana-<BR>pest; quantity, abundance, mass, (in this sense only<BR>at end of comps. and when compounded with words<BR>signifying ‘hair;’ cf. केश-हस्त); (आ), f. the thir-<BR>teenth lunar asterism (represented by a hand and<BR>containing five stars, identified by some with part of<BR>the constellation Corvus); (अम्), n. a pair of leather<BR>bellows; (ए), ind. in hand, in one's possession; [cf.<BR>Gr. χανδ-άν-ω (ἔ-χαδ-ον, κέ-χανδ-α, χείσομαι);<BR>Lat. pre-hend-o, hed-era (?) ; Goth. bi-git-an,<BR>handu; Angl. Sax. gitan (= Eng. get), hand.]<BR>—हस्त-कमल, अम्, n. a lotus carried in the<BR>hand (thus when Lakṣmī was churned out of the<BR>ocean, she appeared holding a lotus).<BR>—हस्त-कौ-<BR>शल, अम्, n. skilfulness of hand, manual dexterity.<BR>—हस्त-क्रिया, f. any manual performance.<BR>—हस्त-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, come to hand, fallen into one's<BR>possession, procured, gained, obtained, secured.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-a" target="_blank">Page1169-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—हस्त-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—हस्त-<BR>गृह्य, ind., Ved. having taken the hand.<BR>—हस्त-<BR>घ्न, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of arm-guard or shield<BR>(defending the fore-arm from the blows of the bow-<BR>string).<BR>—हस्त-चापल्य, अम्, n. = हस्त-कौशल.<BR>—हस्त-च्छेदन, अम्, n. the amputation of a<BR>hand.<BR>—हस्त-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shaken or<BR>moved with the hand, moved or thrown violently<BR>by means of the hand.<BR>—हस्त-च्युति, इस्, f., Ved.<BR>moving or shaking about with the hand, (according to<BR>Sāy. हस्त-च्युती = हस्त-प्रच्युत्या, हस्त-गत्या,<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 1, 1.)<BR>—हस्त-ज्योडि, इस्, m. a kind of<BR>tree or plant (= कर-ज्योडि).<BR>—हस्त-तल, अम्, n.<BR>the palm of the hand; the tip of an elephant's<BR>trunk.<BR>—हस्त-ताल, अस्, m. clapping the hands<BR>together.<BR>—हस्त-त्रय-सम्मिते, ind. at a distance<BR>of three Hastas.<BR>—हस्त-दोष, अस्, m. a slip of<BR>the hand, mistake committed by the hand.<BR>—हस्त-<BR>धात्री = हस्तामलक.<BR>—हस्त-धारण, अम्, n.<BR>warding off a blow; stopping a blow with the hand.<BR>—हस्त-पादादि (˚द-आदि), the hands and feet<BR>&c., the extremities, the limbs of the body.<BR>—हस्त-<BR>पुच्छ, अम्, n. the lower part of the fore-arm, the<BR>hand below the wrist.<BR>—हस्त-पृष्ठ, अम्, n.<BR>the back of the hand (also called अप-पृष्ठ).<BR>—हस्त-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, reached with the hand,<BR>held in the hand; obtained, secured (= कर-प्राप्त).<BR>—हस्त-मणि, इस्, m. a jewel worn on the wrist.<BR>—हस्त-मात्र, a cubit in length, (see मात्र.)<BR>—हस्त-युगल, अम्, n. the two hands.<BR>—हस्त-<BR>रत्नावली (˚न-आव्˚), f., N. of a work by Rāghava<BR>(treating of the various movements of the hands<BR>&c.).<BR>—हस्त-रेखा, f. a line on the hand.<BR>—हस्त-<BR>लाघव, अम्, n. lightness of hand, manual readiness,<BR>smartness, cleverness, legerdemain.<BR>—हस्त-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having hands, handy, dexterous, clever,<BR>skilful.<BR>—हस्त-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being or remain-<BR>ing in the hand, seized, held, caught hold of.<BR>—हस्त-वारण, अम्, n. restraining the hand (of<BR>another); warding off a blow.<BR>—हस्त-विम्ब, अम्,<BR>n. perfuming or smearing the body with unguents<BR>&c.<BR>—हस्त-संवाहन, अम्, n. rubbing or sham-<BR>pooing with the hands.<BR>—हस्त-सिद्धि, इस्, f. per-<BR>forming or effecting anything with the hand, manual<BR>labour; hire, wages, salary.<BR>—हस्त-सूत्र or हस्त-<BR>सूत्रक, ‘hand-ribbon;’ (अम्), n. a bracelet worn<BR>on the wrist.<BR>—हस्त-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, staying in the<BR>hand, being in hand, held, grasped.<BR>—हस्त-स्थित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being in hand, held.<BR>—हस्ताक्षर (˚त-<BR>अक्˚), अम्, n. one's own sign manual, autograph,<BR>signature, handwriting.<BR>—हस्ताग्र (˚त-अग्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the extremity of the hand, the fingers.<BR>—हस्ता-<BR>ग्र-लग्न (˚त-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘joined hand in<BR>hand,’ married; [cf. पाणि-ग्रह.]<BR>—हस्ताङ्गुलि<BR>(˚त-अङ्˚), इस्, f. ‘hand-finger,’ any finger of the<BR>hand.<BR>—हस्तामलक (˚त-आम्˚), अस्, m., N. of one<BR>of the four principal disciples of Śaṅkarācārya; (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit of Emblic Myrobalan held in the hand;<BR>N. of a short work by Hastāmalaka (containing the<BR>elements of the Vedānta).<BR>—हस्तामलक-भा-<BR>ष्य, अम्, n. a commentary on the above by Śaṅ-<BR>karācārya.<BR>—हस्तावलम्ब (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>supported by the hand of another.<BR>—हस्तावाप<BR>(˚त-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘hand-bracelet,’ a finger-guard,<BR>arm-guard (used by archers, = ज्याघात-वारण).<BR>—हस्ता-हस्ति, ind. hand to hand.<BR>—हस्ते-करण,<BR>अम्, n. ‘taking by the hand,’ marriage (= पाणौ-<BR>करण).<BR>—हस्ते-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to<BR>take in hand, take possession of, make one's own.<BR>—हस्ते-कृत्य, ind. having taken possession of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तक|हस्तकः
हस्तक, अस्, m. a position of the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिक|हस्तिकं
हस्तिक, अस्, n. a multitude or collection of ele-<BR>phants (= गज-त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिन्
हस्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having hands, having a trunk;<BR>(ई), m. an elephant, (four kinds of elephants are<BR>specified, each characterized by particular marks; see<BR>भद्र, मन्द्र, मृग, मिश्र; some give कि-<BR>लिञ्ज-हस्तिन्, a traw elephant, effigy of an elephant<BR>made of grass); N. of a son of king Su-hotra (a prince<BR>of the Lunar race, described in Viṣṇu-Purāṇa IV.<BR>19. as founder of Hastinā-pura); a kind of plant, =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-b" target="_blank">Page1169-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अज-मोदा; (इनी), f. a female elephant; a woman<BR>of a particular class (one of the four into which<BR>females are divided; a woman of this class is de-<BR>scribed as having thick lips, thick hips, thick fingers,<BR>large breasts, dark complexion, and libidinous ap-<BR>petite); a kind of drug and perfume.<BR>—हस्ति-कक्-<BR>ष्य, अस्, m. a lion; a tiger.<BR>—हस्ति-कन्द, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of tree or bulbous plant (described as a sort<BR>of Arum, = गज-कन्द).<BR>—हस्ति-करञ्ज, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of tree (= महा-करञ्ज).<BR>—हस्ति-कर्ण,<BR>अस्, m. ‘elephant-eared,’ the castor-oil tree (also the<BR>red kind); a kind of Palāśa tree; another tree or<BR>bulbous plant (= हस्ति-कन्द); a particular class of<BR>semi-divine beings (forming one of the गण-देवता,<BR>q. v.); N. of a district.<BR>—हस्ति-कर्णक, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of Palāśa tree.<BR>—हस्तिकर्ण-दल, अस्, m.<BR>a sort of Palāśa tree.<BR>—हस्ति-कोलि, इस्, m. a sort of<BR>jujube.<BR>—हस्ति-गिरि, इस्, m. the city and district of<BR>Kāñcī, q. v.<BR>—हस्ति-घट, N. of the seventh book<BR>of the Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—हस्ति-घोषा or<BR>हस्ति-घोषातकी, f. a kind of creeper (= ऐभी,<BR>महा-कोशातकी).<BR>—हस्ति-घ्न, अस्, m. an elephant-<BR>killer; a man.<BR>—हस्ति-चारिन्, ई, m. an elephant-<BR>driver; (इणी), f. a kind of tree (= महा-करञ्ज).<BR>—हस्ति-दन्त, अस्, m. the tusk of an elephant; a<BR>radish; a pin or peg projecting from a wall; (अम्),<BR>n. ivory; a radish.<BR>—हस्ति-दन्तक, अम्, n. a<BR>radish.<BR>—हस्तिदन्त-फला, f. a kind of cucumber<BR>(= एर्वारु).<BR>—हस्ति-द्वयस, अस्, ई, अम् (Gram.<BR>80. XX), as high or as big as an elephant, elephantine.<BR>—हस्ति-नख, अम्, n. ‘elephant's nail,’ a sort of<BR>turret or raised mound of earth or masonry protecting<BR>the access to the gate of a city or fort, (it is described as<BR>furnished with an inner staircase, and affording means<BR>for discharging arrows &c. at an enemy.)<BR>—हस्ति-<BR>प or हस्तिपक, अस्, m. an elephant-driver, ele-<BR>phant-rider; an elephant-keeper.<BR>—हस्ति-पत्त्र,<BR>अस्, m. = हस्ति-कन्द.<BR>—हस्ति-पर्णिका, f. a kind<BR>of plant (= राज-कोशातकी).<BR>—हस्ति-पर्णी, f. a<BR>kind of plant (= मोरटा); a sort of gourd (= कर्-<BR>कटी).<BR>—हस्ति-पाद, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, elephant-<BR>footed.<BR>—हस्ति-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—हस्ति-<BR>पृष्ठक, अम्, n. the back of an elephant.<BR>—हस्ति-मद, अस्, m. the ichor or exudation from<BR>an elephant's temples when in rut.<BR>—हस्ति-मल्ल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of Airāvata (Indra's elephant); of Ga-<BR>ṇeśa; of Śaṅkha (the eighth of the chief Nāgas or<BR>serpents of Pātāla); a heap of ashes; a shower of<BR>dust; frost, cold.<BR>—हस्ति-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, as<BR>great as an elephant.<BR>—हस्ति-यूथ, अम्, n. a herd<BR>of elephants.<BR>—हस्ति-राज, अस्, m. the king or chief<BR>of elephants.<BR>—हस्ति-रोहणक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>tree (= महा-करञ्ज).<BR>—हस्ति-लोध्रक, अस्, m.<BR>the Lodhra tree.<BR>—हस्ति-वध or हस्ति-बध, अस्,<BR>m. the killing of an elephant (especially by a lion,<BR>which incurs the guilt of murder, whilst others carry<BR>off the spoils, such as the tusks and the pearls said to<BR>be found in the head).<BR>—हस्ति-वर्चस, अम्, n. the<BR>magnificence of an elephant.<BR>—हस्ति-वाह, अस्, m.<BR>an elephant-driver; a hook for driving elephants.<BR>—हस्ति-विषाणी, f. the Kadalī tree.<BR>—हस्ति-वै-<BR>द्यक, N. of a work by Vīra-soma.<BR>—हस्ति-शाला,<BR>f. an elephant-stable.<BR>—हस्ति-शुण्ड, अस्, m. or<BR>हस्ति-शुण्डा, f. an elephant's trunk; (आ or ई), f.<BR>the shrub Heliotropium Indicum.<BR>—हस्ति-श्या-<BR>माक, अस्, m. a kind of grain.<BR>—हस्ति-षड्गव,<BR>अम्, n. a yoke or collection of six elephants, (see<BR>षड्-गव.)<BR>—हस्ति-सोमा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—हस्ति-स्नान, अम्, n. the washing of an ele-<BR>phant.<BR>—हस्ति-हस्त, अस्, m. an elephant's trunk.<BR>—हस्ति-हस्त-परामृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, touched<BR>or struck by the trunks of elephants.<BR>—हस्त्य्-अध्य्-<BR>अक्ष, अस्, m. a superintendent or master of ele-<BR>phants.<BR>—हस्त्य्-अश्व-रथ-सम्बाध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>crowded with carriages, horses, and elephants.<BR>—हस्त्य्-आयुर्वेद, अस्, m. a work on the treat-<BR>ment of elephants' diseases.<BR>—हस्त्य्-आरोह, अस्, m.<BR>an elephant-rider, elephant-driver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनपुर|हस्तिनपुरं
हस्तिन-पुर, अम्, n. (fr. हस्तिन् + पुर), the<BR>city of Hastin (= हस्तिना-पुर below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनापुर|हस्तिनापुरं
हस्तिना-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a city founded by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">Page1169-c+ 77</a>]<BR>king Hastin, q. v., (it was situated about fifty-seven<BR>miles north-east of the modern Dillī or Delhi on the<BR>banks of an old channel of the Ganges, and was the<BR>capital of the kings of the Lunar line, as Ayodhyā<BR>was of the Solar dynasty; hence it forms a central<BR>scene of action in the Mahā-bhārata; here Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra reigned when the government was resigned<BR>by his brother Pāṇḍu, and here the five Pāṇḍava<BR>princes were educated along with their cousins the<BR>Kauravas, and here at the conclusion of the great<BR>war between them Yudhi-ṣṭhira was crowned after<BR>a triumphal progress through the streets of the city;<BR>see Śānti-parvan 1386-1410: other names for this<BR>celebrated town are गजाह्वय, नाग-साह्वय,<BR>नागाह्व, हास्तिन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनीपुर|हस्तिनीपुरं
हस्तिनी-पुर, अम्, n. = हस्तिना-पुर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्य|हस्त्यः
हस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the hand, done<BR>with the hand, manual; given with the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्र|हस्रः
हस्र हस्र. See p. 1168, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहल|हहलं
हहल हहल, अम्, n. (= हाहल, see हाल-<BR>हल), a sort of deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहा
हहा हहा, आस्, m. a kind of Gandharva,<BR>q. v.; [cf. 1. हाहा, हुहू.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा 1. हा, ind. an exclamation of pain or<BR>grief or weariness (equivalent to ‘ah!’ ‘alas!’ ‘woe!’<BR>हा हतो ऽस्मि, ah! I am killed! it is all over with<BR>me); an exclamation of joy or surprise (oh! ha!<BR>&c.); an interjection of anger or reproach; [cf.<BR>2. हाहा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा 2. हा (connected with rt. 3. हा), cl. 3.<BR>A. जिहीते (1st sing. जिहे, 3rd du. जिहाते, 2nd<BR>pl. जिहीध्वे, 3rd pl. जिहते), Impf. अजिहीत, Pot.<BR>जिहीत, Impv. जिहीताम्, Perf. जहे, हास्यते, अहास्त,<BR>हातुम्, to go, move, to go to, attain; to give way,<BR>yield [cf. Ṛg-veda I. 37, 7]: Pass. हायते, Aor.<BR>अहायि: Caus. हापयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अजीह-<BR>पत्, -त, to cause to go: Desid. जिहासते: Intens.<BR>जाहायते, जाहाति, जाहेति; [cf. Gr. χα-ίν-ω, χά-σκ-ω,<BR>χάσμα, χά-ος, χή-μη, χάσις, χαλάω; Lat.<BR>hi-sc-o, hi-o, hia-tus; Old Germ. gî-ê-m, gin-ê-m,<BR>gein-o-m; Angl. Sax. ginan, cinan, geonan, gyn-<BR>ian, ganian; Slav. zi-ja-ti, ze-ja-ti, zi-nati, ‘to<BR>gape;’ Lith. zio-j-u, zio-ti-s, ‘a cleft, hole.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहान
जिहान, अस्, आ, अम्, going, &c. See p. 347.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्वा
हात्वा, ind. (Pāṇ. VII. 4, 43), having gone, hav-<BR>ing moved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान|हानं
हान, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, moved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यमान
हास्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being about to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेय|हेयः
1. हेय, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 1170), to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा 3. हा (connected with rt. 2. हा), cl.<BR>3. P. जहाति (1st du. जहीवस् or जहिवस्,<BR>3rd du. जहीतस् or जहितस्, 3rd. pl. जहति, Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 4, 116), Impf. अजहात् (1st du. अजहीव or<BR>अजहिव, 3rd pl. अजहुः), Pot. जह्यात् (Pāṇ. VI.<BR>4, 118), Impv. जहातु (2nd sing. जहीहि or जहिहि<BR>or जहाहि, 3rd pl. जहतु, Pāṇ. VI. 4, 117), Perf.<BR>जहौ (2nd sing. जहिथ or जहाथ, 1st du. ज-<BR>हिव, 2nd pl. जह, 3rd pl. जहुः), हास्यति, अहासीत्,<BR>Prec. हेयात्, हातुम्, to abandon, leave, quit, desert,<BR>forsake, relinquish, dismiss; to resign, forego, let go,<BR>lose; to let fall; to omit, neglect; to avoid, shun;<BR>to remove: Pass. हीयते, Perf. जहे (Kirāt. XII.<BR>12), Aor. अहायि, to be left or deserted, be forsaken;<BR>to be excluded from or deprived or bereft of, to lose<BR>(with inst. or abl., e. g. जहे प्राणैः, he was de-<BR>prived of breath or lost his life; हीयते पति-लोकात्,<BR>she is excluded from the heaven of her husband);<BR>to be destitute of, be deficient in, be wanting in,<BR>fail, decrease; to be lost; to fail (in a lawsuit); to<BR>be left out or omitted or neglected; to become<BR>weary or enfeebled; to be lessened or lowered:<BR>Caus. हापयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अजीहपत्, to cause<BR>to quit or abandon; to drive away, expel; to cause<BR>to lose or want; to neglect, omit, decline; to lose:<BR>Desid. जिहासति, to wish to leave, &c.: Intens. जे-<BR>हीयते, जाहेति, जाहाति; [cf. Gr. χῆ-ρο-ς, χήρα,<BR>χηρεύ-ω, χηρό-ω, χωρίς, χωρίζω, χῆτος, χατέω;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">Page1170-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Lat. habeo (?); Goth. haba, habais, gaidv, giban;<BR>Angl. Sax. gifan, gafol, gœfel, gif; Eng. if.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहत्
जहत्, अत्, अती, अत्, leaving, &c. See p. 343.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
5. ह, (at the end of comps.) abandoning, leaving,<BR>quitting, avoiding; see p. 1163, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
4. हा, f. abandoning, leaving, relinquishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हातव्य|हातव्यं
हातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be abandoned or left,<BR>relinquishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान|हानं
हान, अम्, n. the act of abandoning, relinquish-<BR>ing; escaping; prowess, valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानि|हानिः
हानि, इस्, f. abandonment, relinquishment, neglect,<BR>loss, want, privation, absence; decrease, deficiency,<BR>diminution, detriment, damage.<BR>—हानि-कर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, causing loss, prejudicial, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानीय
हानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, = हातव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापन|हापनं
हापन, अम्, n. the act of causing to quit or<BR>abandon, expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापित
हापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be relinquished;<BR>made to give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायन|हायनं|हायनः
1. हायन, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (for 2. see col. 2),<BR>quitting, leaving; passing away, (in this sense per-<BR>haps to be connected with rt. 2. हा; cf. 2. हायन,<BR>col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायिन्
हायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, leaving, abandoning, neglecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित्वा
1. हित्वा, ind. (for 2. see p. 1171, col. 1), having<BR>left or abandoned, having quitted or renounced, hav-<BR>ing deserted; letting alone, slighting, disregarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित्वाय
हित्वाय, ind., Ved. having abandoned, having<BR>left, having discarded, (Sāy. = हित्वा = परित्यज्य,<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 14, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीत्वा
हीत्वा, ind., Ved. = 1. हित्वा, (Pāṇ. VII. 4, 44.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन|हीनः
हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, left, forsaken, relinquished,<BR>abandoned, quitted, deserted, neglected; excluded,<BR>shut out from (with abl.); deprived of, free from,<BR>devoid of, destitute of, without, bereft of (with inst.,<BR>e. g. प्रानैर् हीनः, bereft of breath or life; or<BR>with abl., e. g. मन्त्रात् or मन्त्रतो हीनः, devoid<BR>of sacred knowledge, Manu III. 65); wasted, dimi-<BR>nished, decayed, enfeebled, feeble; deficient, defec-<BR>tive, faulty, inferior, insufficient; deducted, subtracted,<BR>minus; lower, less, (Manu II. 194); mean, base,<BR>vile, bad, low; (अस्), m. a faulty respondent, insuf-<BR>ficient or defective witness, (five kinds are enume-<BR>rated, viz. अन्य-वादिन्, क्रिया-द्वेषिन्, नोपस्था-<BR>यिन्, निर्-उत्तर, आहूत-प्रपलायिन्); subtraction<BR>(= व्य्-अवकलन).<BR>—हीन-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, or<BR>हीन-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, neglecting or omitting<BR>customary rites or religious acts.<BR>—हीन-कुल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of low family, base-born, plebeian.<BR>—हीन-<BR>कुल-त्व, अम्, n. lowness of birth.<BR>—हीन-कोश,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having an empty treasury.<BR>—हीन-<BR>क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, one who neglects to sacrifice,<BR>(Manu XI. 12.)<BR>—हीन-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, low-born.<BR>—हीन-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, low-born, of low caste, de-<BR>prived of caste, outcaste, degraded, vile.<BR>—हीन-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. defectiveness, deprivation, destitution,<BR>the state of being without, absence of, (generally at<BR>the end of comps., e. g. पुत्र-ह्˚, बुद्धि-ह्˚.)<BR>—हीन-दर्शन-सामर्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute<BR>of the power of seeing, blind.<BR>—हीन-नायक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, having a low or base hero (said of a<BR>drama).<BR>—हीन-यान, अम्, n. ‘the inferior or lesser<BR>vehicle,’ N. of a system of Buddhist teaching, (op-<BR>posed to महा-यान, q. v.)<BR>—हीन-योनि, इस्, m. f.<BR>an inferior womb, low birth or origin.<BR>—हीन-<BR>रोमन्, आ, आ, अ, deprived of hair, bald, (Mahā-bh.<BR>Śānti-p. 13, 229.)<BR>—हीन-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>low caste, outcaste, of inferior rank, belonging to<BR>the lower orders.<BR>—हीन-वाद, अस्, m. defective<BR>statement, insufficient or contradictory evidence, pre-<BR>varication.<BR>—हीन-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, making a de-<BR>fective statement, insufficient or inadmissible (as a<BR>witness, see हीन above); contradictory, prevaricat-<BR>ing; destitute of speech, speechless, dumb; cast in<BR>law.<BR>—हीन-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, deficient in courage.<BR>—हीन-सख्य, अम्, n. making friends with<BR>low people, associating with degraded persons.<BR>—हीन-सन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, destitute of peace or<BR>reconciliation.<BR>—हीन-सेवा, f. attendance on base<BR>people, serving or waiting on low persons.<BR>—ही-<BR>नाङ्ग (˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, deficient in limb,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">Page1170-b+ 71</a>]<BR>crippled, maimed, mutilated, imperfect, defective;<BR>(ई), m. a small ant.<BR>—हीनान्न-वस्त्र-वेष (˚न-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. (a Brahma-cārin) eating less food<BR>(than his preceptor) and wearing an inferior dress,<BR>(Manu II. 194.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनक
हीनक, (at the end of a comp.) = हीन, deprived<BR>of, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनित
हीनित, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to Śabda-k.) sub-<BR>tracted (= व्य्-अवकलित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीयमान
हीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being left or deserted;<BR>being lost; sinking, giving in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेय|हेयः
2. हेय, अस्, आ, अम् (for 3. see p. 1171, col. 2),<BR>to be left or abandoned, to be avoided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाङ्गर|हांगर|हांगरः|हाङ्गरः
हाङ्गर हाङ्गर, अस्, m. a large fish, shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटक|हाटकं
हाटक हाटक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. हट्), golden,<BR>made of gold; (अम्), n. gold; the thorn-apple (=<BR>धुस्तूर).<BR>—हाटक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or<BR>consisting of gold, golden.<BR>—हाटकेश्वर (˚क-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a form of Śiva (worshipped on<BR>the banks of the Godāvarī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्र|हात्रं|हात्रः
हात्र हात्र, अम्, n. (probably fr. rt. 1. हन्,<BR>cf. हान्त्र below), injuring, killing (= प्रम-<BR>थन); death, dying (= मरण); a Rākṣasa,<BR>(in this sense probably masc.); wages, hire, (in this<BR>sense probably fr. rt. 2. हा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान|हानं
हान हान, हानि. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानुक|हानुकः
हानुक हानुक. See p. 1165, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्त्र|हांत्रः|हान्त्रः
हान्त्र हान्त्र, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 159. fr. rt. 1. हन्, cf. हात्र above), death,<BR>dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्द्र|हान्द्रं
हान्द्र, अम्, n. = हान्त्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्दण
हान्दण हान्दण, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापुत्री
