हायन|हायनं|हायनः
हायन 2. हायन, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably<BR>fr. हयन and connected with rt. 1. हि, but cf.<BR>1. हायन at col. 1), a year, (at the end of an<BR>adj. comp. the fem. ends in ई, cf. द्वि-ह्˚); (अस्), m.<BR>a flame, ray; a sort of rice; epithet of Takman (so<BR>called either from this disease lasting the whole year<BR>or because it returns every year).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायस्
हायस् हायस्, अस्, n., Ved. = 2. धायस्,<BR>support, vigour, strength; [cf. सर्व-ह्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार|हारं|हारः
हार हार, हारक. See p. 1175, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

