हारहूर|हारहूरः
हारहूर हारहूर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according<BR>to some only masc.; probably connected with हार-<BR>हारा, see under 1. हार), spirituous liquor, wine;<BR>(आ), f. a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारि|हारिः
हारि हारि. See p. 1175, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिण
हारिण हारिण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. हरिण), be-<BR>longing or relating to deer; (ई), f. a species of the<BR>Aty-aṣṭi metre; (अम्), n. venison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिणिक|हारिणिकः
हारिणिक, अस्, m. a deer-killer, hunter; (ई), f. a<BR>species of the Aty-aṣṭi metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारित|हारितः
हारित 1. हारित, अस्, m. (fr. हरित्; for<BR>2. हारित see under rt. 1. हृ), the colour green; the<BR>Haritāla pigeon; N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the sons or descendants of Harita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारितक|हारितकं|हारितकः
हारितक, अस्, m. [cf. हरितक], a green vege-<BR>table or pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीत|हारीतः
1. हारीत, अस्, m. (for 2. see under rt. 1. हृ), the<BR>Haritāla pigeon; N. of a Muni and writer of a<BR>Dharma-śāstra or law-book; of a poet; of a phy-<BR>sician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीतक|हारीतकः
हारीतक, अस्, m. the Haritāla pigeon; N. of a<BR>son of Viśvā-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्र|हारिद्रः
हारिद्र हारिद्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. हरिद्रा),<BR>stained or dyed with turmeric; turmeric-coloured;<BR>yellow; (अस्), m. a yellow colour; the Kadamba<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">Page1170-c+ 73</a>]<BR>tree; a kind of fever (supposed to arise from a<BR>vitiated state of the three humors of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्रव
