हालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>ploughing or a plough, agricultural; (अस्), m. a<BR>ploughman, ploughboy, agriculturist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिनी
हालिनी, f. a sort of large house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालु|हालुः
हालु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 1. fr. rt.<BR>1. हल्), a tooth (= दन्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालेय
हालेय, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालक|हालकः
हालक हालक, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>हरिक), a horse of a yellowish brown or tawny<BR>colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाह|हालाहः
हालाह, अस्, m. a spotted or piebald horse (accord-<BR>ing to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाव|हावः
हाव हाव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. ह्वे), calling, a<BR>call; any feminine or coquettish gesture tending to<BR>excite amorous sensations, blandishment, dalliance,<BR>the airs and arts of lovers, (in these senses perhaps a<BR>form evolved out of भाव, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हावक|हावकः
हावक, अस्, m. one who calls or summons; (in<BR>nuptial ceremonies) one who summons the bride,<BR>an attendant on the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास|हासः
हास हास, हासक, &c. See p. 1168, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासस्
हासस् हासस्, आस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 220. fr. rt. 3. हा), Ved. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्त
हास्त हास्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. हस्त), formed<BR>by the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिक|हास्तिकं|हास्तिकः
हास्तिक हास्तिक, अस्, r. (fr. हस्तिन्), an<BR>elephant-rider, elephant-driver, &c.; (अम्), n. a<BR>herd or collection of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिन|हास्तिनं
हास्तिन, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>elephants, elephantine, as big as an elephant, huge<BR>(अम्), n. the city of Hastināpura, q. v.<BR>—हास्तिन-<BR>पुर, अम्, n. = हस्तिना-पुर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्य|हास्यं|हास्यः
हास्य हास्य. See p. 1168. col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहल|हाहलं
हाहल हाहल. See p. 1170, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहस्
हाहस् हाहस्, आस्, m. a Gandharva. (See<BR>p. 281, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहा
1. हाहा, आस्, m. (see Gram. 108. ब्), a Gandharva;<BR>a particular high number, ten thousand billions,<BR>(महा-हाहा, a hundred thousand billions.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहा
हाहा 2. हा-हा, ind. (an interjection of<BR>surprise or grief or pain, equivalent to) ah, ah! alas,<BR>alas!<BR>—हाहा-कार, अस्, m. ‘making the exclamation<BR>हाहा,’ a general or great lamentation, or wailing;<BR>sound of grief or pity; the noise or uproar of battle.<BR>—हाहा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made to resound with<BR>the uproar of battle.<BR>—हाहा-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>lamented, bewailed.<BR>—हाहा-रव, अस्, m. the cry<BR>or noise हाहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि 1. हि (connected with rt. हिन्व्, to<BR>which some of the forms in the examples<BR>given below are referred by Sāy.), cl. 5. P. हिनोति<BR>(Ved. also A. हिनुते), जिघाय, हेष्यति, अहै-<BR>षीत्, हेतुम्, to send, send forth, impel, (हिन्वन्ति<BR>= प्रेरयन्ति, Ṛg-veda VIII. 43, 29); to dis-<BR>charge, throw, cast, shoot (as an arrow &c.); to<BR>urge, incite, excite; to further, promote, advance;<BR>to protect, favour, benefit, prosper (Ved.); to please,<BR>gratify, exhilarate, satisfy, (हिन्विरे = प्रीणयन्ति,<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 43, 19); to go, proceed: Pass.<BR>हीयते, Aor. अहायि: Caus. हाययति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अजीहयत्: Desid. of Caus. जिघापयिषति: Desid.<BR>जिघीषति: Intens. जेघीयते, जेघयीति, जेघेति;<BR>[cf. perhaps Gr. κίω; Lat. cieo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय|हयः
हय, हयन. See p. 1165, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित|हितं|हितः
1. हित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 1172), sent,<BR>impelled; gone, proceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिति
हिति, इस्, f. sending, impelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित्वा
2. हित्वा, ind. (for 1. see p. 1170, col. 1), having<BR>sent; having impelled; having gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्व
हिन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. favouring, benefiting,<BR>(Sāy. = प्रीणयितृ, Ṛg-veda VIII. 40, 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्वत्
हिन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. gratifying, pleasing,<BR>(Sāy. हिन्वन् = हिन्वन्तः = प्रीणयन्तः, Ṛg-<BR>veda V. 36, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्वान
हिन्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pleasing, gratifying,<BR>exhilarating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हियान
हियान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. prospering, favouring,<BR>(Sāy. = समृद्धिं गच्छत्, i. e. व्याप्नुवत्,<BR>Ṛg-veda II. 4, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेति|हेतिः
हेति, इस्, m. f. a weapon, missile; stroke, wound,<BR>injury, (Sāy. = हिंसा, Ṛg-veda VI. 75, 14); a ray<BR>of the sun; light, splendor; flame; (इस्), m., N. of<BR>the first Rākṣasa king (father of Vidyut-keśa; repre-<BR>sented as residing in the Sun's chariot in the month<BR>of Caitra or Madhu).<BR>—हेति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessed of weapons, armed with missiles (Ved.);<BR>illuminated by the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतिक
हेतिक = हेति (at the end of a comp., cf. शक्ति-ह्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतु|हेतुः
हेतु, उस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. I. 73. fr. rt.<BR>1. हि), impulse, motive; cause, reason, object, pur-<BR>pose (e. g. अनेन हेतुना, for this reason; मृत्यु-<BR>हेतवे, in order to kill; हेतुर् अलौकिकः, a super-<BR>natural cause); a logical reason, the reason for an<BR>inference (constituting the second Avayava or mem-<BR>ber of the five-membered Nyāya syllogism, e. g.<BR>1. ‘this hill is fiery,’ 2. ‘because it smokes;’ see न्य्-<BR>आय, p. 519; 2. प्रति-ज्ञा, p. 613); any logical deduc-<BR>tion or argument, proof; reasoning, logic (in general);<BR>excuse, sophistry; means, instrument; law, condition;<BR>source, origin; a particular figure of speech, (in the<BR>drama) a brief speech giving a reason; (हेतुना or<BR>हेतौ or हेतोस्), ind. by reason of, because of, on<BR>account of, for the sake of, (generally after a gen. or<BR>at the end of a comp., e. g. मम हेतोः or मद्-<BR>धेतोः, on account of me.)<BR>—हेतु-ता, f. or हेतु-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of being a हेतु or cause,<BR>causation, cause, causativeness, the abstract existence<BR>of cause or motive.<BR>—हेतु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>a reason or cause, proceeding from a cause (as any<BR>effect); having the Hetu (or second Avayava of a<BR>syllogism); accompanied by arguments; controverted<BR>by arguments.<BR>—हेतु-वाद, अस्, m. a statement of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">Page1171-b+ 80</a>]<BR>reasons or argument, assigning a cause, disputation.<BR>—हेतु-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a rationalistic book, (Manu<BR>II. 11); any heretical or sceptical work calling in<BR>question the authority of Śruti.<BR>—हेतु-शास्त्राश्रय<BR>(˚र-आश्˚), अस्, m. reliance on rationalistic treatises.<BR>—हेतु-श्लिष्ट, (in rhetoric) combination of cause,<BR>a method of comparing two objects by using epithets<BR>common to both so as to describe similar results in<BR>each produced by similar causes.<BR>—हेतु-हेतुमद्-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the relation subsisting between cause<BR>and effect.<BR>—हेतूपन्यास (˚तु-उप्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>assignment of reasons or motives, statement of an<BR>argument.<BR>—हेत्व्-अपदेश, the adducing or men-<BR>tioning of the reason (or second member of the<BR>syllogism in logic).<BR>—हेत्व्-आभास, अस्, m. (in logic)<BR>a mere appearance of a reason, fallacious semblance<BR>of an argument, fallacious middle term, fallacy (said<BR>to be of five kinds, viz. व्य्-अभिचार or स-व्य-<BR>भिचार, वि-रुद्ध, अ-सिद्ध, सत्-प्रतिपक्ष,<BR>बाध or बाधित); the bringing forward or stating<BR>of a Hetu (or second member of a syllogism), the<BR>assignment of a reason which can be shown to be<BR>incorrect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुक|हेतुकः
हेतुक, अस्, m. a cause, active cause, instrument<BR>(= हेतु); a logician; (अस्, आ, अम्), causal, instru-<BR>mental, belonging to a motive or cause; causing,<BR>producing (at the end of comps., e. g. विषाद-ह्˚,<BR>causing dejection); N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतृ
हेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. urging on, inciting; (ता),<BR>m. an inciter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेय|हेयः
3. हेय, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. and 2. see pp. 1169,<BR>1170), to be sent or impelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि 2. हि, ind. (probably to be connected<BR>with rt. 1. हि; cf. हेतु), for, because, on<BR>account of (used enclitically so as not to stand first<BR>in a sentence, e. g. प्रमाणं हि भवान्, for your<BR>honour is the authority; तथा हि, for example, for<BR>instance, accordingly); assuredly, certainly; indeed,<BR>surely, (in these senses used emphatically and, accord-<BR>ing to some, also interrogatively; but sometimes to<BR>be treated as redundant and a mere expletive); but;<BR>ah! alas! (said to be also an interjection of envy,<BR>of contempt, of hurry, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्
हिंस् हिंस् (by some regarded as an<BR>anomalous Desid. of rt. 1. हन्), cl. 1. 7.<BR>P. (ep. also A.) हिंसति (-ते), हिनस्ति, जिहिंस,<BR>हिंसिष्यति (ep. A. हिंसिष्यते), अहिंसीत्, हिंसि-<BR>तुम्, to strike, hit, beat; to hurt, harm, wound,<BR>injure; to kill, slay, destroy: Pass. हिंस्यते, Aor.<BR>अहिंसि: Caus. or cl. 10. हिंसयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अजिहिंसत्, to kill, slay: Desid. जिहिंसिषति: Intens.<BR>जेहिंस्यते, जेहिंस्ति; [cf. perhaps Old Germ. geis-<BR>la, ‘a whip;’ Mod. Germ. Geissel.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसक|हिंसकः
हिंसक, अस्, आ, अम्, injurious, noxious, detri-<BR>mental, mischievous, hostile, malignant, ferocious,<BR>savage; an injurer; (अस्), m. any savage or noxious<BR>animal, beast of prey; an enemy; a Brāhman skilled<BR>in the Atharva-veda [cf. हिंसा-कर्मन्, and see<BR>the account of this Veda, p. 964, col. 1].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसत्
हिंसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, hurting, injuring, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसन|हिंसनं
हिंसन, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of hurting, injuring,<BR>injury, detriment; killing; slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसा
हिंसा, f. injuring, injury, mischief, hurt, harm,<BR>wrong (said to be of three kinds, 1. mental or<BR>malice; 2. verbal or abuse; 3. personal or actual<BR>violence); killing, slaying; robbery, spoliation.<BR>—हिंसा-कर्मन्, अ, n. any injurious or hostile act;<BR>magic applied to the ruin or injury of an enemy,<BR>employment of spells and mystical texts (especially<BR>those of the Atharva-veda, see वेद) for injurious<BR>purposes.<BR>—हिंसात्मक (˚सा-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>an injurious nature, naturally hurtful, destructive.<BR>—हिंसा-प्राणिन्, ई, m. a savage or noxious animal.<BR>—हिंसाप्राणि-प्रचुर, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in<BR>noxious animals.<BR>—हिंसा-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, abound-<BR>ing in injury, generally injurious.<BR>—हिंसा-रत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, delighting in mischief.<BR>—हिंसा-रुचि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, taking pleasure in injury, having a taste for<BR>slaughter.<BR>—हिंसारुचि-त्व, अम्, n. the having a<BR>taste for injury or mischief.<BR>—हिंसा-विहार, अस्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">Page1171-c+ 78</a>]<BR>अम्, sporting in mischief, wanton in injuries, roam-<BR>ing about to do harm.<BR>—हिंसा-समुद्भव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, arising from injury (i. e. from the sin of<BR>hurting any living creature).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारु|हिंसारुः
हिंसारु, उस्, m. a destructive animal; a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालु|हिंसालुः
हिंसालु, उस्, उस्, उ, disposed to injure, injurious,<BR>mischievous, hurtful, murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालुक|हिंसालुकः
हिंसालुक, अस्, आ, अम्, disposed to be mischievous,<BR>hurtful; (अस्), m. a mischievous or savage dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसित|हिंसितः
हिंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, injured, hurt; mortally<BR>wounded; (अम्), n. injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसित्वा
हिंसित्वा, ind. having injured, having wronged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसीर|हिंसीरः
हिंसीर, अस्, m. a mischievous wretch, villain,<BR>a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्य
हिंस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, liable to be hurt or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्र|हिंस्रः
हिंस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, injurious, mischievous, hurtful,<BR>noxious, destructive, murderous; formidable, terrible;<BR>cruel, fierce, savage; (अस्), m. any noxious animal;<BR>a beast of prey; a destroyer; N. of Śiva; of Bhīma;<BR>(आ), f. spikenard (= जटा-मांसी); the shrub Abrus<BR>Precatorius; a sort of grass, Coix Barbata; a vein,<BR>nerve.<BR>—हिंस्र-पशु, उस्, m. a noxious animal,<BR>beast of prey.<BR>—हिंस्र-यन्त्र, अम्, n. an imple-<BR>ment for injuring or wounding, a trap; a mystical<BR>text used for injurious purposes.<BR>—हिंस्राहिंस्र<BR>(˚र-अह्˚), अम्, n. noxious and harmless, wicked<BR>and good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रक|हिंस्रकः
हिंस्रक, अस्, m. a savage or noxious animal,<BR>beast of prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्क्
हिक्क् हिक्क्, cl. 1. P. A. हिक्कति, -ते,<BR>जिहिक्क, जिहिक्के, हिक्किष्यति, -ते, अहिक्-<BR>कीत्, अहिक्किष्ट, हिक्कितुम्, to make an indistinct<BR>or inarticulate sound; to hiccough; cl. 10. A. हिक्-<BR>कयते, &c., to injure, kill (= rt. किष्क्, q. v.):<BR>Caus. हिक्कयति, -यितुम्, अजिहिक्कत्: Desid. जि-<BR>हिक्किषति, -ते: Intens. जेहिक्क्यते, जेहिक्कीति,<BR>जेहिक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्का
हिक्का, f. an indistinct or inarticulate sound;<BR>hiccough; [cf. हेक्का.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्कृ
हिङ्कृ हिङ्कृ, cl. 8. 5. P. -करोति, -कृणोति,<BR>&c., to make the sound हिम्; to low (as a cow).<BR>—हिङ्-कार, अस्, m. the sound हिम्; a kind of low<BR>roar; a tiger (as making this sound).<BR>—हिङ्-कृण्-<BR>वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. making the sound हिम्;<BR>roaring (as a tiger); lowing (as of a cow; Sāy. हिङ्-<BR>कृण्वती = वत्सम् प्रति हिङ्कारं कुर्वती, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 164, 27).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गु|हिंगु
हिङ्गु हिङ्गु, उस्, उ, m. n. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. I. 37. fr. हि, substituted for rt. 1. हन्;<BR>according to Śabda-k. only neut.), the plant Asa<BR>Fetida (said to be so called as ‘killing’ or over-<BR>powering all other odours); the substance prepared<BR>from the plant (for household use).<BR>—हिङ्गु-ना-<BR>डिका, f. the resin of a particular plant (= नाडी-<BR>हिङ्गु).<BR>—हिङ्गु-निर्यास, अस्, m. the gummy exu-<BR>dation or concrete juice of Asa Fetida; the Nimba<BR>tree.<BR>—हिङ्गु-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the Iṅgudī tree; (ई),<BR>f. a drug composed of a leaf resembling that of Asa<BR>Fetida; (अम्), n. the leaf of the Asa Fetida plant.<BR>—हिङ्गु-पर्णी, f. a particular plant (= वंश-<BR>पत्त्री).<BR>—हिङ्गु-शिराटिका, f. a kind of plant (=<BR>वंश-पत्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुल|हिंगुल|हिंगुलं|हिंगुलः|हिङ्गुलः
