हिडिम्ब|हिडिंब|हिडिंबः|हिडिम्बः
हिडिम्ब हिडिम्ब, अस्, m. a gigantic Rāk-<BR>ṣasa slain by Bhīma; (आ), f. Hiḍimba's sister (who<BR>changed herself into a beautiful woman and married<BR>Bhīma; he had a son by her named Ghaṭotkaca);<BR>the wife of Hanumat.<BR>—हिडिम्ब-जित्, त्, m. ‘con-<BR>queror of Hiḍimba,’ Bhīma.<BR>—हिडिम्ब-निसूदन,<BR>अस्, or हिडिम्ब-भिद्, त्, m. ‘destroyer of Hiḍimba,’<BR>Bhīma.<BR>—हिडिम्ब-वध or -बध, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>killing of Hiḍimba,’ an episode of the Mahā-bhārata<BR>(Ādi-parvan, section 152 — 156, verse 5927).<BR>—हि-<BR>डिम्बा-पति, इस्, m. ‘husband of Hiḍimbā,’ epi-<BR>thet of Bhīma; of Hanumat.<BR>—हिडिम्बा-रमण,<BR>अस्, m. epithet of Bhīma; of Hanumat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडम्ब
