हिण्डी|हिंडी
हिण्डी, f., N. of Durgā.<BR>—हिण्डी-प्रियतम, अस्,<BR>m. ‘most beloved by Durgā,’ Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डीर|हिंडीर|हिंडीरः|हिण्डीरः
हिण्डीर, अस्, m. cuttle-fish bone (supposed to be<BR>the congealed foam of the sea; = समुद्र-फेन);<BR>a man, male; the egg-plant, Solanum Melongena;<BR>a tonic or stomachic; (अम्), n. the pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित|हितं|हितः
हित 2. हित, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass. part. of<BR>rt. 1. धा; for 1. हित see under rt. 2. हि, p. 1171),<BR>put, placed, laid, imposed [cf. 1. धित]; held, taken,<BR>seized; suitable, proper, fit, worthy, right, advan-<BR>tageous, beneficial, profitable, useful, salutary, whole-<BR>some, agreeing with (often said in a medical sense<BR>of diet, regimen, medicines, &c.); friendly, affec-<BR>tionate, kind, (in these senses hardly distinguishable<BR>fr. 1. हित); (अस्), m. a friend, benefactor; benefit,<BR>profit, service, good, welfare, well-being; (आ), f. a<BR>causeway, dike; (अम्), n. anything suitable or proper,<BR>an advantage.<BR>—हित-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, doing what<BR>is fit or proper, doing a service, performing a kind-<BR>ness, befriending, friendly, favourable; (अस्), m. a<BR>benefactor.<BR>—हित-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing well<BR>to, desirous of benefiting or befriending.<BR>—हित-<BR>काम्या, f. desire for another's welfare, good-will.<BR>—हित-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or हित-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, doing<BR>services, performing kindnesses or benefits, befriend-<BR>ing, useful, beneficial, auspicious.<BR>—हित-प्रणी, ईस्,<BR>m. ‘executing what is advantageous,’ a spy, secret<BR>emissary.<BR>—हित-प्रयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. one who<BR>has offered an oblation of food, &c.<BR>—हित-प्रेप्सु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of effecting another's welfare,<BR>wishing to benefit or befriend.<BR>—हित-बुद्धि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, friendly-minded, well-disposed, wishing well.<BR>—हित-मित्र, अस्, m., Ved. a benevolent friend.<BR>—हित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, friendly, favourable, doing<BR>good, useful.<BR>—हित-वाक्य, अम्, n. friendly advice,<BR>good counsel.<BR>—हित-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking<BR>kindly, giving good counsel or friendly advice; (ई),<BR>m. a friendly counsellor or adviser.<BR>—हित-हरि-<BR>वंश-गोस्वामिन्, ई, m. = हरि-वंश-गोस्वामिन्.<BR>—हितानुकारिन् (˚त-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, acting con-<BR>formably to what is right or kind.<BR>—हितानुबन्-<BR>धिन् (˚त-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, having welfare as a con-<BR>sequence, involving or bringing welfare.<BR>—हितान्-<BR>वेषिन् (˚त-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, seeking another's wel-<BR>fare.<BR>—हिता-भङ्ग, अस्, m. the forcing or breaking<BR>of a dike or causeway, (Manu IX. 274.)<BR>—हितार्-<BR>थिन् (˚त-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, seeking or desiring another's<BR>welfare or advantage.<BR>—हितावली (˚त-आव्˚), f. a<BR>particular plant (= अङ्गार-कुष्ठक).<BR>—हिताहित<BR>(˚त-अह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, good and evil, beneficial and<BR>disadvantageous.<BR>—हितेच्छा (˚त-इच्˚), f. well-wish-<BR>ing, good-will, good wishes.<BR>—हितैषिन् (˚त-एष्˚),<BR>ई, इणी, इ, wishing well, desiring another's welfare,<BR>kindly disposed, benevolent.<BR>—हितोक्ति (˚त-उक्˚), इस्,<BR>f. kind or good advice, salutary instruction, friendly<BR>language.<BR>—हितोपदेश (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, m. friendly<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">Page1172-b+ 76</a>]<BR>advice, salutary instruction; N. of a celebrated and<BR>very popular collection of stories and fables (supposed<BR>to be narrated by a Brāhman named Viṣṇu-śarman<BR>to some young princes, and intermixed with many<BR>admirable didactic sentences and moral precepts ex-<BR>tracted from various sources, the whole being chiefly<BR>founded on the Pañca-tantra, q. v.: the stories illus-<BR>trate four principal subjects, divided into four books,<BR>viz. 1. Mitra-lābha, ‘the acquisition of friends;’<BR>2. Suhṛd-bheda, ‘the separation of friends;’ 3. Vi-<BR>graha, ‘war;’ 4. Sandhi, ‘peace;’ they have been<BR>translated into nearly all the languages of Asia and<BR>Europe, and have served as the substance of many<BR>similar collections, such as the Anvāri Suhailī, Khirad-<BR>afroz, Pilpay's Fables, &c.); N. of a work on medi-<BR>cine; of another work on medicine by Śambhū-<BR>nātha, (also called Vaidyaka-sāra-saṅgraha.)<BR>—हितो-<BR>पदेष्टृ (˚त-उप्˚), ता, m. a friendly instructor,<BR>kind adviser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितक|हितकः
हितक, अस्, m. a child, the young of any animal,<BR>a pupil, &c. (= शिशु, according to Śabda-k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित्वा
3. हित्वा, ind. (for 2. see p. 1171, col. 1), having<BR>put or placed, having made, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्ताल|हिंताल|हिंतालः|हिन्तालः
हिन्ताल हिन्ताल, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>ताल, q. v.), the marshy date tree, a species of palm,<BR>Phœnix or Elate Paludosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दु|हिंदुः|हिन्दुः
हिन्दु हिन्दु, उस्, m. (fr. the Persian هندو),<BR>a Hindu (more properly Hindū).<BR>—हिन्दु-धर्म,<BR>अस्, m. the Hindū religion.<BR>—हिन्दु-स्थान, अम्, n.<BR>the country of the Hindūs, Hindūstān (properly re-<BR>stricted to the upper provinces between Benares and<BR>the river Sutlej).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोल|हिंदोल|हिंदोलः|हिन्दोलः
हिन्दोल हिन्दोल, अस्, m. a swing, swinging<BR>cradle or hammock; an ornamental swing or litter<BR>in which figures of Kṛṣṇa are carried about during<BR>the Swing-festival in the light half of the month<BR>Śrāvaṇa; one of the six Rāgas or personified musical<BR>modes, (see राग, p. 837.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोलक|हिंदोलक|हिंदोलकः|हिन्दोलकः
हिन्दोलक, अस्, m. a swing; a cradle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोलय
हिन्दोलय, Nom. P. हिन्दोलयति, &c., to swing,<BR>rock about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोला|हिंदोला
हिन्दोला, f. a swing (= हिन्दोल above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्व्
हिन्व् हिन्व् (connected with rt. 2. हि; cf.<BR>rt. धिन्व्), cl. 1. P. हिन्वति, जिहिन्व,<BR>हिन्वितुम्, to satisfy, please, exhilarate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्वान
हिन्वान हिन्वान. See under rt. 2. हि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिबुक
हिबुक हिबुक, अम्, n. (= ὑπογείον), epithet<BR>of the fourth Lagna or astrological sign, fourth<BR>house (= पाताल, p. 563).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम|हिमं|हिमः
हिम हिम, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>I. 146. fr. हि substituted for rt. 1. हन्; according<BR>to others from a lost rt. ह्यम्), cold, frigid, frosty,<BR>icy, dewy, any cold substance; (अस्), m. the cold season,<BR>cold, winter (= हेमन्त, p. 1173); the moon;<BR>the Himālaya mountain; the sandal tree; camphor;<BR>(आ), f. the cold season, winter; a year (Ved.); small<BR>cardamoms; a variety of the fragrant grass Cyperus<BR>(= भद्र-मुस्ता, नागर-मुस्ता); a kind of plant<BR>(= पृक्का); a kind of grass (= चणिका); the fra-<BR>grant drug and perfume Reṇukā; (अम्), n. frost,<BR>hoar-frost, ice, snow, dew, cold, coldness, coolness,<BR>(in Ṛg-veda X. 37, 10. हिमा, inst. c. = शैत्येन,<BR>and thought by some to come from a monosyllabic<BR>form हिम्); night, (in Naigh. I. 7. हिमा, inst. c.<BR>is enumerated among the रात्रि-नामानि; cf. हिम्या<BR>under हिम्य); sandal-wood; another fragrant wood<BR>(of cooling properties, = पद्म-काष्ठ); fresh<BR>butter; tin; a pearl; a lotus; [cf. Zend zjao, zim,<BR>zima, ‘winter:’ Gr. χι-ών (χίον-ος), δύσ-χιμο-ς,<BR>χεῖ-μα, χειμάζω, χειμαίνω, χίμεθλο-ν, χειμών,<BR>χειμερινό-ς: Lat. hiem-s, hibernu-s (for himer-<BR>nus): Slav. zima, ‘winter:’ Lith. zema, zemini-s:<BR>Hib. geimhre, geimhrith, geimhreadh, ‘winter;’<BR>gamh, ‘winter, cold.’]<BR>—हिम-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>causing or producing cold, frigorific, cold; (अस्), m.<BR>the moon; camphor.<BR>—हिम-कूट, अस्, m. ‘cold-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-c" target="_blank">Page1172-c+ 81</a>]<BR>summit,’ the winter season.<BR>—हिम-गर्भ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, laden with snow.<BR>—हिम-गिरि, इस्, m. the Himālaya<BR>mountain.<BR>—हिम-गु, उस्, m. ‘cold-rayed,’ epithet<BR>of the moon; [cf. शीत-गु.]<BR>—हिम-गौर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, white as snow.<BR>—हिम-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>by cold; born or produced in the Himālaya mountain;<BR>(अस्), m. the mountain Maināka; (आ), f. ‘daughter<BR>of Himālaya;’ the plant called Zedoary; another<BR>plant (= क्षीरिणी); Pārvatī.<BR>—हिम-ज्झटि, इस्, f.<BR>(ज्झटि for झटि, see rt. झट्), ‘intermixture of cold<BR>dew,’ hoar-frost, mist, fog; [cf. कु-ज्झटि.]<BR>—हिम-<BR>ज्वर, अस्, m. fever with cold paroxysms, ague.<BR>—हिम-तैल, अम्, n. a kind of camphor ointment.<BR>—हिम-दीधिति, इस्, m. ‘having cool rays,’ the<BR>moon.<BR>—हिम-दुग्धा, f. ‘having cool juice,’ a kind<BR>of milky plant or tree (= क्षीरिणी).<BR>—हिम-दुर्-<BR>दिन, अम्, n. cold and bad weather, frosty or snowy<BR>weather, wintry weather.<BR>—हिम-द्युति, इस्, m.<BR>‘having cool radiance,’ the moon.<BR>—हिम-द्रुम,<BR>अस्, m. a sort of large Nimba tree.<BR>—हिम-द्रुह्,<BR>ध्रुक्, m. ‘dew-dispeller,’ the sun.<BR>—हिम-धातु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘having cold minerals,’ the Himālaya moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—हिम-ध्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, withered by cold,<BR>frost-bitten, frost-nipt (as a lotus &c.).<BR>—हिम-<BR>निर्मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from frost.<BR>—हिम-<BR>प्रस्थ, अस्, m. ‘having snowy table-land,’ the<BR>Himālaya mountain.<BR>—हिम-बालुक, अस्, आ, m. f.<BR>camphor.<BR>—हिम-भास्, आस्, m. ‘having cool lustre,’<BR>epithet of the moon.<BR>—हिम-रश्मि, इस्, m. ‘having<BR>cool rays,’ the moon.<BR>—हिमरश्मि-ज, अस्, m.<BR>‘born from the moon,’ epithet of the planet Budha<BR>or Mercury.<BR>—हिमर्तु (˚म-ऋतु), उस्, m. the cold<BR>season.<BR>—हिम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having frost or<BR>snow, snowy, frosty, icy, freezing, snow-clad; (आन्),<BR>m. the Himālaya mountain or the Himālaya per-<BR>sonified, (see हिमालय.)<BR>—हिमवत, at the end of<BR>a comp. = हिम-वत् above.<BR>—हिमवत्-कुक्षि,<BR>इस्, m. a valley of the Himālaya.<BR>—हिमवत्-खण्ड,<BR>N. of a book of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—हिम-<BR>वत्-प्रभव, अस्, आ, अम्, springing from or be-<BR>longing to the Himālaya mountain.<BR>—हिमवत्-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of the Himālaya,’ the moun-<BR>tain Maināka; (आ), f. the Ganges; Pārvatī.<BR>—हिम-<BR>वद्-गिरि, इस्, m. a snowy mountain.<BR>—हिमवद्-<BR>गिरि-संश्रय, अस्, m. ‘taking refuge in the Himā-<BR>laya mountain,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—हिम-विद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘frost-pierced,’ penetrated with frost (as<BR>the west wind in the cold season).<BR>—हिम-शर्करा,<BR>f. a kind of sugar (= यावनाली).<BR>—हिम-शीतल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, very cold or frosty, freezing.<BR>—हिम-शुचि-<BR>भस्म-भूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned with ashes<BR>white as snow.<BR>—हिम-शैल, अस्, m. a snowy moun-<BR>tain, the Himālaya.<BR>—हिमशैल-जा, f. ‘daughter<BR>of Himālaya,’ the goddess Durgā or Pārvatī.<BR>—हिम-<BR>श्रथ, अस्, m. ‘shedding cold,’ the moon.<BR>—हिम-<BR>संहति, इस्, f. a mass of ice or snow.<BR>—हिम-<BR>सरस्, अस्, n. cold water.<BR>—हिम-हान-कृत्, त्, m.<BR>‘causing loss of cold,’ fire.<BR>—हिम-हासक, अस्, m.<BR>‘winter-smiler,’ the marshy date tree.<BR>—हिमांशु<BR>(˚म-अं˚), उस्, m. ‘cool-rayed,’ the moon; camphor.<BR>—हिमांश्व्-अभिख्य, अम्, n. ‘called after the<BR>moon,’ silver.<BR>—हिमागम (˚म-आग्˚), अस्, m. ‘ap-<BR>proach of cold,’ the cold season, winter.<BR>—हिमाद्रि<BR>(˚म-अद्˚), इस्, m. a snowy range of mountains, the<BR>Himālaya mountain (sometimes personified).<BR>—हिमा-<BR>द्रि-जा, f. ‘daughter of Himālaya,’ Pārvatī; a kind of<BR>plant or tree (= क्षीरिणी).<BR>—हिमाद्रि-तनया, f.<BR>‘daughter of Himālaya,’ Durgā.<BR>—हिमाद्रि-तनया-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘husband of the daughter of Himā-<BR>laya,’ Śiva.<BR>—हिमानिल (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. a cold<BR>or frosty wind.<BR>—हिमाब्ज (˚म-अब्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>lotus.<BR>—हिमाभ (˚म-आभ), अस्, आ, अम्, resem-<BR>bling cold, like snow or frost.<BR>—हिमाम्बु (˚म-<BR>अम्˚), उ, n. cold water.<BR>—हिमाराति (˚म-अर्˚), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of cold,’ fire; the sun; a kind of plant (=<BR>चित्रक); another plant (= अर्क).<BR>—हिमारुण<BR>(˚म-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, grey with frost.<BR>—हिमार्त<BR>(˚म-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pinched with cold, suffering from<BR>cold, chilled, frozen.<BR>—हिमार्दित (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, pinched or pained by cold.<BR>—हिमालय (˚म-<BR>आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘abode of snow,’ the Himālaya range of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">Page1173-a+ 79</a>]<BR>mountains (which bounds India on the north and<BR>separates it from Tartary, giving rise to the rivers<BR>Ganges and Indus, and containing the highest eleva-<BR>tions in the world; in mythology personified as the<BR>husband of Menā or Menakā, by whom he had a<BR>son called Maināka, who is also a personified moun-<BR>tain; he was moreover the father of Durgā or Umā,<BR>who became incarnate as Pārvatī, ‘daughter of the<BR>Mountain,’ to captivate Śiva and withdraw him from<BR>a severe penance he had undertaken to perform in<BR>the region of Himālaya; the personified Mountain<BR>is also represented as the father of Gaṅgā, who, as the<BR>personified Ganges, is generally regarded as his eldest<BR>daughter, though sometimes identified with Pārvatī);<BR>the white Khadira tree; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= भू-<BR>म्य्-आमलकी).<BR>—हिमालय-सुता, f. ‘daughter of<BR>Himālaya,’ Umā or Pārvatī.<BR>—हिमा-वती, f. a kind<BR>of Soma or moon-plant (= स्वर्ण-क्षीरी, q. v.).<BR>—हिमाश्रया (˚म-आश्˚), f. ‘depending on cold,’<BR>a kind of plant (= स्वर्ण-जीवन्ती).<BR>—हिमाह्व<BR>(˚म-आह्˚), अस्, m. ‘called after ice,’ camphor.<BR>—हिमाह्वय (˚म-आह्˚), अस्, m. ‘called after ice,’<BR>camphor; (अम्), n. a lotus.<BR>—हिमोत्तरा (˚म-उत्˚), f.<BR>‘following on cold,’ the tawny grape.<BR>—हिमोत्पन्न<BR>(˚म-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced by cold; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of sugar (= यावनाली).<BR>—हिमोद्भवा (˚म-<BR>उद्˚), f. ‘cold-produced,’ the plant called Zedoary<BR>(= शटी).<BR>—हिमोस्र (˚म-उस्˚), अस्, m. ‘cool-<BR>rayed,’ epithet of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमक|हिमकः
हिमक, अस्, m. a kind of tree (= वि-कङ्कत);<BR>N. of a prince or chief of Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवल
हिमवल, अम्, n. (also read हेमवल), a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमा
हिमा, f. See under हिम, p. 1172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमानी
हिमानी, f. great frost, a mass of snow, collection<BR>of ice and snow (= हिम-संहति), snow-drift; a<BR>kind of sugar (= यावनाली).<BR>—हिमानी-विशद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, white as a snow-drift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमिका
हिमिका, f. hoar-frost, cold dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमेलु|हिमेलुः
हिमेलु, उस्, उस्, उ, chilly, suffering from cold,<BR>frozen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम्न|हिम्नः
हिम्न, अस्, m. (see 1. हेमन् and हेम्ना below),<BR>the planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम्य|हिम्यः
हिम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, frosty, snowy, icy, dewy, cold,<BR>frigid, (in Ṛg-veda I. 34, 1. हिम्या, ‘with the night,’<BR>is explained by Sāy. as = हिम-युक्तया रात्र्या,<BR>‘with the frosty night.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्
1. हेमन्, आ, m. (according to Śabda-k. also अ<BR>neut.), winter; cold, the cold season; the planet<BR>Mercury, (see हिम-रश्मि-ज.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्त|हेमंत|हेमंतं|हेमंतः|हेमन्तः
हेमन्त, अस्, अम्, m. n. winter, the cold season<BR>(comprising the two months Agra-hāyaṇa and Pauṣa,<BR>i. e. from middle of November to middle of January).<BR>—हेमन्त-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of winter,’ the<BR>wood-apple tree (= कपित्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्ती|हेमंती
हेमन्ती, f. the winter season, cold season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमवल|हेमवलं
हेमवल, अम्, n. a pearl (= हिमवल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेम्ना
हेम्ना, m. (according to Śabda-k.) the planet<BR>Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरङ्गु|हिरंगुः|हिरङ्गुः
हिरङ्गु हिरङ्गु, उस्, m., N. of Rāhu (the<BR>personified ascending node).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण|हिरणं
हिरण हिरण, अम्, n. (connected with हिरि,<BR>1. हरि, हरित्, q.q. v.v.; but see etymology given<BR>for हिरण्य below), gold; semen; a cowry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरणिन्
हिरणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. golden, (Sāy. = हिरण्य-<BR>वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्मय|हिरण्मयं|हिरण्मयः
हिरण्-मय, अस्, ई, अम् (हिरण् for हिरण),<BR>made of gold, golden; (अस्), m. epithet of Brahmā,<BR>(see हिरण्य-गर्भ); (अम्), n. one of the nine<BR>Varṣas or divisions of the continent (said to be be-<BR>tween the mountainous ranges Śveta and Śṛṅgavat;<BR>see वर्ष, श्वेत).<BR>—हिरण्-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Agnīdhra (king of Śveta-dvīpa).<BR>—हिरण्-<BR>वती, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्य|हिरण्यं
हिरण्य, अम्, n. (according to Uṇādi-s. V. 44.<BR>fr. rt. हर्य् with substitution of हिर), gold (crude<BR>bullion or wrought); any vessel made of gold (e. g.<BR>a golden spoon, Manu II. 29); a golden ornament<BR>(Ved.); any precious metal, silver (crude or wrought);<BR>wealth, property; substance, imperishable matter;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-b" target="_blank">Page1173-b+ 81</a>]<BR>semen virile; a particular measure; a cowry; the<BR>Datura or thorn-apple; (आ), f. one of the seven<BR>tongues of fire.<BR>—हिरण्य-कक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>wearing a golden girdle.<BR>—हिरण्य-कवचोद्भव<BR>(˚च-उद्˚), अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>कशिपु, उस्, m. ‘clothed in gold,’ N. of a king of<BR>the Daityas celebrated for his blasphemous impiety,<BR>(he was son of Kaśyapa and Diti, and had obtained<BR>a boon from Brahmā that he should not be slain by<BR>either god or man or animal; hence he became so<BR>powerful that he usurped the sovereignty of the<BR>three worlds, and appropriated the sacrifices made to<BR>the gods who were compelled by him to fly from<BR>their seats in heaven; when, however, his pious son<BR>Prahlāda praised Viṣṇu, the Daitya exerted all his<BR>power in vain to destroy the boy, and Viṣṇu him-<BR>self appeared out of a pillar [which had been<BR>blasphemously struck by the father, saying, ‘Is the<BR>deity here?’] in the form Nara-siṃha, ‘half man,<BR>half lion,’ and tore Hiraṇya-kaśipu to pieces; this<BR>was Viṣṇu's fourth Avatāra; see प्र-ह्लाद, नर-<BR>सिंह, विष्णु.)<BR>—हिरण्य-कशिपु-हन्, हा, m.<BR>‘slayer of Hiraṇya-kaśipu,’ Viṣṇu.<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>कामधेनु, उस्, f. ‘a golden cow of plenty,’ one<BR>of the sixteen Mahā-dānas, (see महा-दान, तुला-<BR>पुरुष.)<BR>—हिरण्य-केशिन्, ई, m., N. of the author<BR>of certain Kalpa-sūtras.<BR>—हिरण्यकेशि-सूत्र, अम्,<BR>n. the Kalpa-sūtras of Hiraṇya-keśin.<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>केश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. golden-haired, having golden<BR>manes (said of the two horses of Indra).<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>कोष, अस्, m. wrought and unwrought gold and<BR>silver.<BR>—हिरण्य-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of Brahmā<BR>(so called as born from a golden egg supposed to<BR>have been formed out of the seed deposited in the<BR>waters when they were produced as the first creation<BR>of the Self-existent; according to Manu I. 9. this<BR>seed became a golden egg, resplendent as the sun,<BR>in which the Self-existent Brahma was born as<BR>Brahmā, the creator of the worlds, i. e. according<BR>to Kullūka, as, Hiraṇya-garbha, who is therefore re-<BR>garded as a manifestation of the Paramātman or<BR>supreme Soul; in Ṛg-veda X. 121. it is said Hiraṇya-<BR>garbha arose in the beginning; he was the one lord<BR>of existing things; he established the earth and the<BR>sky, &c.); N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 121 (having the patronymic Prājāpatya); N. of<BR>Viṣṇu; (in phil.) the soul invested by the Sūk-<BR>shma-śarīra or subtile body (= सूत्रात्मन्, प्राणात्-<BR>मन्); N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—हिरण्य-चक्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, golden-wheeled.<BR>—हिरण्य-त्वच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>‘golden-skinned,’ having a golden covering, coated<BR>with gold (said of a chariot).<BR>—हिरण्य-त्वच, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having skin bright as gold.<BR>—हिरण्य-द,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, yielding gold, granting gold; (अस्), m.<BR>the ocean; (आ), f. the earth.<BR>—हिरण्य-दत्, अन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. having golden teeth.<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>धनुस्, उस्, m. ‘golden-bowed,’ N. of a king.<BR>—हिरण्य-नाभ, अस्, m. ‘having a golden navel,’<BR>the mountain Maināka; N. of a pupil of Jaimini and<BR>teacher of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—हिरण्य-निर्णिज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, Ved. bright as gold.<BR>—हिरण्य-नेमि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. having golden wheels.<BR>—हिरण्य-पक्ष, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. golden-winged.<BR>—हिरण्य-पाणि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. golden-handed, golden-footed (said of the<BR>horses of the Maruts).<BR>—हिरण्य-पाव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. purifying with gold.<BR>—हिरण्य-पिण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>Ved. a lump of gold.<BR>—हिरण्य-पुर, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a town of the Asuras.<BR>—हिरण्य-पेशस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. having golden lustre.<BR>—हिरण्य-प्रüग,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. a golden fore-part of a chariot-pole,<BR>(Ṛg-veda I. 35, 5.)<BR>—हिरण्य-प्रतिपूर्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, full of gold.<BR>—हिरण्य-बाहु, उस्, m. ‘golden-<BR>armed,’ epithet of Śiva; the river Śoṇa, q. v.<BR>—हिरण्य-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. golden-shaped<BR>(said of Agni).<BR>—हिरण्य-रेतस्, आस्, m. ‘having<BR>golden seed,’ epithet of Agni or fire; of the sun; of<BR>Śiva; a kind of plant or tree (= चित्रक); N. of<BR>a son of Priya-vrata.<BR>—हिरण्य-रोमन्, आ, m.<BR>‘golden-haired,’ N. of a Loka-pāla (son of Marīci);<BR>of a son of Parjanya (regent of the north).<BR>—हिर-<BR>ण्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in gold; (आन्), m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">Page1173-c+ 78</a>]<BR>epithet of Agni; (अती), f. a proper N.<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>वन्धुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a framework of<BR>gold (said of a chariot of Indra and Vāyu).<BR>—हिर-<BR>ण्य-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, golden-coloured; (आ), f. a<BR>river, (in Naigh. I. 13. हिरण्य-वर्णाः is enume-<BR>rated among the नदी-नामानि.)<BR>—हिरण्य-वर्तनि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a golden path.<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m. ‘having golden armour,’ a proper N.<BR>—हिरण्य-वाशीमत्तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most<BR>skilful wielder of the golden spear (said of Pūṣan).<BR>—हिरण्य-वाह, अस्, m. ‘bearing gold,’ the river<BR>Śoṇa, q. v.; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—हिरण्य-विद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. ‘knowing gold,’ possessing or granting gold.<BR>—हिरण्य-विन्दु, उस्, m. fire.<BR>—हिरण्य-शम्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a golden शम्या or yoke.<BR>—हिरण्य-सन्दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. resembling gold,<BR>shining like gold.<BR>—हिरण्य-स्तूप, अस्, m., N. of<BR>an Āṅgirasa (author of Ṛg-veda I. 31 — 35, IX. 4,<BR>69; Arcat Hairaṇyastūpa is the author of Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 149); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a family.<BR>—हिरण्य-<BR>हस्त, अस्, m., Ved. ‘golden-handed,’ epithet of<BR>Savitṛ; N. of a son of Vadhri-matī.<BR>—हिरण्याक्ष<BR>(˚य-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘golden-eyed,’ N. of a celebrated<BR>Daitya, twin brother of Hiraṇya-kaśipu, q. v., (he<BR>was killed by Viṣṇu, in his third Avatāra, in the<BR>form of a Varāha or boar; like his brother, Hiraṇya-<BR>kaśipu, he had obtained a boon from Brahmā, so<BR>that no animal, except a boar, which he had omitted<BR>to mention, could hurt him; he then became very<BR>insolent and seized upon the earth, which he carried<BR>with him into the depths of the ocean, where it<BR>must have perished had not Viṣṇu become in-<BR>carnate as a boar [the symbol of great strength],<BR>and having dived into the abyss, destroyed the<BR>Daitya and lifted up the recovered earth on the<BR>point of his tusks); epithet of Savitṛ (Ved.); N. of<BR>a Muni; of a place; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a family<BR>(supposed to have been descended from Viśvā-mitra).<BR>—हिरण्याङ्ग (˚य-अङ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Muni;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a family.<BR>—हिरण्याभीशु (˚य-<BR>अभ्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having golden reins.<BR>—हिर-<BR>ण्याश्व (˚य-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘a golden horse,’ one of<BR>the sixteen Mahā-dānas, (see महा-दान, तुला-<BR>पुरुष.)<BR>—हिरण्याश्व-रथ, अस्, m. ‘golden-<BR>horsed-chariot,’ one of the sixteen Mahā-dānas, (see<BR>above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यक|हिरण्यकः
हिरण्यक, अस्, m., a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यय
हिरण्यय, अस्, ई, अम्, golden, (in Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>78, 2. हिरण्यया = हिरण्मयानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यया
हिरण्यया, f., Ved. desire for gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्ययु
हिरण्ययु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. fond of gold or trea-<BR>sures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यव|हिरण्यवः
हिरण्यव, अस्, m. a divine treasure, the property<BR>of the gods (= देव-स्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिराधर
हिराधर हिराधर, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरि
हिरि हिरि (see rt. 2. हृ), apparently a Vedic<BR>form of हरि, q. v.<BR>—हिरि-शिप्र, अस्, m., Ved. epi-<BR>thet of Agni, (explained by Sāy. as हरण-शील-<BR>हनु, ‘one whose jaws carry away or seize,’ or<BR>दीप्तोष्णीष, ‘having a flaming head-dress,’ Ṛg-<BR>veda II. 2, 5; cf. हृणि.)<BR>—हिरि-श्मश्रु, उस्, m.,<BR>Ved. ‘golden-bearded,’ epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरीमत्|हिरीमन्त्
हिरीमत्, (in Ṛg-veda X. 105, 6. according to<BR>Sāy. हिरीमान् = हरिताश्वः or हरित-वर्णः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरीमश
हिरीमश, (in Ṛg-veda X. 105, 6. according to<BR>Sāy. हिरीमशः = हरित-श्मश्रुः or पृषो-<BR>दरः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरुक्
हिरुक् हिरुक्, ind. concealed, hidden, (in<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 164, 32. = अन्तर्-हित, and in Naigh.<BR>III. 25. enumerated among the निर्णीतान्तर्हित-<BR>नामधेयानि); without, except; in the midst of,<BR>amongst; near; below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्
हिल् हिल् (connected with rt. हेल्, q. v.),<BR>cl. 6. P. हिलति, जिहेल, &c., to sport<BR>amorously, dally, wanton, express amorous inclina-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिलमोचि|हिलमोचिः
हिल-मोचि, इस्, or हिल-मोची or हिलमोचिका, f.<BR>the pot-herb Hingtsha Repens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिलीसमुद्र
हिलीसमुद्र हिली-समुद्र, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्ल|हिल्लः
हिल्ल हिल्ल, अस्, m. a kind of bird (= शरारि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्लोल|हिल्लोलः
हिल्लोल हिल्लोल, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>हिन्दोल, q. v.), a wave, surge; a whim; a particular<BR>form of sexual union; one of the Rāgas or personified<BR>musical modes, (for हिन्दोल, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्लोलय
हिल्लोलय, Nom. P. हिल्लोलयति, &c., to swing<BR>or rock or roll about (= हिन्दोलय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्वला
हिल्वला हिल्वला, आस्, f. pl., N. of five small<BR>stars in the head of the Nakṣatra Mṛga-śiras; [cf.<BR>इल्वलास्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिष्क्
हिष्क् हिष्क्, a various reading for rts.<BR>हिक्क्, किष्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिहि
हिहि हिहि, ind. = हीही, q. v.; [cf. ही below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ही
ही ही, ind. [cf. हीही], an exclamation or<BR>interjection of surprise (ah! ah!); of fatigue or de-<BR>spondence or sorrow (ah! alas!); (said to be also<BR>used in giving a reason or cause, and equivalent to<BR>‘therefore,’ ‘so,’ ‘for,’ ‘because,’ = 2. हि, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीत
हीत हीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = हित (accord-<BR>ing to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन|हीनः
हीन हीन. See p. 1170, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन्ताल|हींताल|हींतालः|हीन्तालः
हीन्ताल हीन्ताल, अस्, m. = हिन्ताल, the<BR>marshy date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीर|हीरं|हीरः
हीर हीर, अस्, m. (connected with हार),<BR>Indra's thunderbolt, a thunderbolt; a diamond, (see<BR>वज्र); a snake; a necklace; a lion; N. of Śiva; of<BR>the father of Harṣa, q. v.; (आ), f. a sort of cockroach;<BR>an ant; N. of the goddess Lakṣmī; of the wife of<BR>Darpa-nārāyaṇa; a kind of plant, = काश्मरी; (अम्),<BR>n. a thunderbolt; a diamond.<BR>—हीर-भट्ट, अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—हीराङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘diamond-<BR>bodied,’ Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरक|हीरकः
हीरक, अस्, m. the diamond (supposed to be pre-<BR>sided over by Śukra or Venus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हील|हीलं
हील हील, अम्, n. (perhaps connected with<BR>rt. हिल्), semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलुक|हीलुकं
हीलुक, अम्, n. a kind of rum or spirit distilled<BR>from molasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीळित
हीळित हीऌइत. See rt. हेल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीही
हीही हीही, ind. (ही, q. v., repeated), ah,<BR>ha! hee, hee! (or similar sounds made in laughing<BR>or giggling).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हु
हु हु (probably connected with rt. 1. धू<BR>= Gr. θύω; in some forms identical with rt.<BR>ह्वे), cl. 3. P. (Ved. also A.) जुहोति (1st du. जुहु-<BR>वस् or जुह्वस्, 3rd pl. जुह्वति); Impf. अजुहोत् (3rd<BR>pl. अजुहवुस्, 3rd pl. A., Ved. अजुह्वत); Impv.<BR>जुहोतु (2nd sing. जुहुधि, Ved. also जुहोधि, and<BR>2nd pl. जुहोत); Perf. जुहाव (identical in form<BR>with Perf. of rt. ह्वे; 1st du. जुहुविव), or जुह-<BR>वाञ्-चकार, होष्यति, अहौषीत्, होतुम्, to offer<BR>or present (an oblation [acc.], especially with fire or<BR>to fire), make an offering to or in honour of any<BR>deity (sometimes with acc. of the deity honoured,<BR>e. g. पावकं or अग्निं जुहुधि, ‘make oblations<BR>to fire,’ but often with dat., e. g. सोमम् इन्द्राय<BR>हु, ‘to offer Soma to Indra’); to pour or cast clarified<BR>butter &c. (acc.) into the sacred fire (loc.); to offer<BR>up anything, worship or honour with offerings or<BR>oblations; to sacrifice, perform a sacrifice; to accept<BR>or appropriate an oblation, (Sāy. = स्वी-कृ, Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 75, 1); to eat, (according to Vopa-deva X. 1.<BR>अदने): Pass. हूयते (identical in form with Pass.<BR>of rt. ह्वे), Aor. अहावि, to be offered (as an oblation<BR>&c.), to be poured forth (in oblation, as clarified<BR>butter &c.), to be sacrificed: Caus. हावयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अजूहवत्, to cause to offer oblations,<BR>make to sacrifice, cause to honour with oblations:<BR>Desid. जुहूषति: Intens. जोहूयते, जोहवीति, जो-<BR>होति; [cf. Gr. χέ-ω (χεύ-σω), χύ-μα, χεῦ-μα,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">Page1174-b+ 76</a>]<BR>χύ-σι-ς, χο-ή, χό-ο-ς, χυ-μό-ς, χυ-λό-ς, χύ-τρα; Lat.<BR>fo-n(t)-s, fu-ti-s, ec-fû-ti-o, re-fû-to, con-fû-to, fu-<BR>nd-o, fû-ti-li-s; Goth. giu-t-a; Angl. Sax. geotan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुह्वत्
जुह्वत्, अत्, अती, अत्. See p. 350, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुह्वान
जुह्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, sacrificing, offering, present-<BR>ing; accepting (an offering, Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत|हुतं|हुतः
1. हुत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see under rt. ह्वे), of-<BR>fered with fire, poured forth (as clarified butter in the<BR>sacred fire), burnt as an oblation, sacrificed; one to<BR>whom an oblation is offered; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Śiva; (अम्), n. an oblation, offering, sacrifice.<BR>—हुत-जातवेदस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, one who has made<BR>an oblation to fire.<BR>—हुतभुक्-प्रिया, f. ‘dear to<BR>Agni,’ the wife of Agni.<BR>—हुत-भुज्, क्, m. ‘obla-<BR>tion-eater,’ Agni or fire; epithet of a particular star.<BR>—हुत-वह, अस्, m. ‘oblation-bearer,’ Agni or<BR>fire.<BR>—हुत-संविक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to<BR>some) one who has sacrificed all his individuality or<BR>blended his own will with the Universal Soul.<BR>—हुत-<BR>होम, अस्, m. a Brāhman who has offered an obla-<BR>tion; (अम्), n. an offered oblation, burnt-offering.<BR>—हुताग्नि (˚त-अग्˚), इस्, m. fire with which an<BR>oblation is made, sacrificial fire.<BR>—हुताश (˚त-आश),<BR>अस्, m. ‘eating the oblation,’ fire or its deity Agni;<BR>fear, alarm, apprehension (= भय, according to<BR>Śabda-k.; perhaps fr. हुत + 1. आ-शा, but this sense<BR>is doubtless modern).<BR>—हुताशन (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘oblation-eating,’ fire or its deity; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—हुताशन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, bearing or holding<BR>consecrated fire (said of an altar &c.).<BR>—हुताशन-<BR>सहाय, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—हुताहुति (˚त-<BR>आह्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having an oblation just offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुति|हुतिः
1. हुति, इस्, f. (for 2. see under rt. ह्वे), offering<BR>oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत्वा
हुत्वा, ind. having offered (as an oblation &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूयमान
1. हूयमान, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see under rt.<BR>ह्वे, p. 1180), being offered in oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुङ्कार|हुंकार|हुङ्कारः
हुङ्कार हुङ्-कार, हुङ्-कृत. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड्
हुड् हुड्, cl. 6. P. हुडति, &c., to collect,<BR>accumulate, heap together (= rt. हुण्ड्); to<BR>dive, sink, be submerged; cl. 1. P. होडति, &c., to<BR>go (= rts. होड्, हूड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड|हुडः
हुड, अस्, m. a ram [cf. स-हुड, हुण्ड]; a<BR>kind of fence or bulwark, a bastion, tower; a bar or<BR>iron stake for keeping out thieves; a club, iron club;<BR>(according to some) a place for voiding excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडु|हुडुः
हुडु, उस्, m. a ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुक्क|हुडुक्कः
हुडुक्क हुडुक्क, अस्, m. a kind of bird,<BR>Gallinula Madraspatana (= दात्यूह); a drunken<BR>man; a small hourglass-shaped drum; a stick or staff<BR>bound with iron; the bar or bolt of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड्डुक
हुड्डुक, another reading for हुडुक्क above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुत्
हुडुत् हुडुत्, त्, n. (according to Śabda-k.)<BR>the noise of a bull (= वृष-शब्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुम्ब|हुडुम्बः
हुडुम्ब हुडुम्ब, अस्, m. a thunder-clap,<BR>(according to Śabda-k. = भ्रष्ट-चिपिट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्ड्|हुंड्
हुण्ड् हुण्ड्, cl. 1. A. हुण्डते, &c., to col-<BR>lect, accumulate; to select, choose, take,<BR>accept (= rt. भुण्ड्, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्ड|हुंड|हुंडः|हुण्डः
हुण्ड, अस्, m. a tiger; a village hog; a block-<BR>head; a demon, imp; a ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्डिका
हुण्डिका हुण्डिका, f. (Pers. هندي), a bill<BR>of exchange, bond; assignment, order (given for the<BR>maintenance of soldiers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्डी
हुण्डी, f. = हुण्डिका above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुम्
हुम् हुम्, ind. (cf. हूम्; an imitative sound<BR>used as a particle) expressive of remembrance,<BR>doubt, interrogation, assent, anger, aversion, reproach,<BR>fear, (see हूम्); a mystical syllable occurring fre-<BR>quently in spells and incantations; (in Vedic ritual)<BR>a sacrificial exclamation used immediately before the<BR>singing of the Pra-stāva or prelude as well as during<BR>the chanting of the Prati-hāra or response.<BR>—हुङ्-<BR>कार, अस्, m. the word or sound हुम्, making the<BR>sound हुम्, uttering a menacing sound; the grunt-<BR>ing or roaring of a boar; any roaring, bellowing;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">Page1174-c+ 72</a>]<BR>the noise or twang (of a bow).<BR>—हुङ्कार-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, filled with groaning or menacing sounds.<BR>—हुङ्कार-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—हुङ्-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, uttered with a mystical sound,<BR>pronounced as an incantation; roared; (अम्), n. an<BR>incantation; the roar or grunt of a wild boar; the<BR>roar (of thunder); any roar.<BR>—हुङ्-कृति, इस्, f. =<BR>हुङ्-कार above.<BR>—हुम्-फड्-अन्त, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>scil. मन्त्राः, incantations ending in the mystical<BR>words हुम् and फट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्छ्
हुर्छ् हुर्छ् (developed out of rt. ह्वृ,<BR>q. v.; cf. ऋछ्, fr. rt. ऋ), cl. 1. P. हूर्छति,<BR>जुहूर्छ, हूर्छितुम्, to be crooked, go crookedly;<BR>to be crooked or dishonest in conduct, deceive; [cf.<BR>Gr. λοξός; (probably) Lat. quercus, ob-liquus;<BR>Goth. vraiqs.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्
हुर्, हूर् (a Kvip formation fr. rt. हुर्छ्; gen.<BR>sing. हुरस्), one who goes crookedly, a deceiver,<BR>dishonest.<BR>—हुरश्-चित्, त्, m. (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 42, 3. हुरस् is from a Kvip formation,<BR>the final छ् being dropped), a deceiver, thief, (in<BR>Naigh. III. 24. = स्तेन, according to Sāy. = कौ-<BR>टिल्यस्य or कौटिल्येन सञ्चेतृ, a collector of<BR>crookedness or one who collects crookedly.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूर्छन|हूर्च्छनं
हूर्छन, अम्, n. the act of going crookedly,<BR>crookedness, craft, dishonesty, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूर्छित
हूर्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone crookedly; deceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूर्ण
हूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, = हूर्छित above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुल्
हुल् हुल्, cl. 1. P. होलति, &c., to go; to<BR>cover, conceal; to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलहुली
हुलहुली हुलहुली, f. inarticulate sounds<BR>made by women on joyful occasions (= मुख-<BR>घण्टा, a sort of Ululatus, though expressive of<BR>happiness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुवान
हुवान हुवान. See under rt. ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुष्कपुर
हुष्कपुर हुष्क-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहु|हुहुः
हुहु हुहु, उस्, or हुहू, ऊस्, m. (probably from<BR>an anomalous Intens. of rt. ह्वे), a kind of Gan-<BR>dharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हू
हू हू, ind. an interjection of calling; of<BR>contempt; of pride; of grief, (oh! ah! alas! &c.)<BR>—हू-रव, अस्, m. ‘making the sound Hū,’ a<BR>jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूङ्कार|हूंकार|हूङ्कारः
हूङ्कार हूङ्-कार, &c. See under हूम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूङ्गरस्थान
हूङ्गरस्थान हूङ्गर-स्थान, N. of a place<BR>(probably Hungary).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूड्
हूड् हूड् [cf. rts. ह्रुड्, हुड्, होड्, हौड्,<BR>ह्रौड्], cl. 1. P. (according to Vopa-deva<BR>also A.) हूडति (-ते), जुहूड, &c., हूडितुम्, to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूण|हूणः
हूण हूण, अस्, m. a barbarian, Hun; N.<BR>of a district; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people (living in<BR>Bhārata-varṣa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूत|हूतं
हूत हूत, हूति, &c. See under rt. ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हून|हूनः
हून हून, अस्, m., N. of a certain barbarous<BR>race (perhaps the Huns); a kind of gold coin current<BR>in the kingdom of Mādra, (commonly called a pagoda<BR>and worth about eight shillings.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूम्
हूम् हूम्, ind. (cf. ॐ, हुम्, an imitative<BR>sound used as a particle) expressive of doubt or<BR>consideration (equivalent to humph! umph! &c.);<BR>of interrogation (hey? indeed? eh?); of assent<BR>(yes, aye, well, exactly, so be it; see ॐ, p. 189);<BR>of anger, menace, aversion, repulse (avaunt! away!<BR>begone! tush! forbear! be silent! hush!); of re-<BR>proach, contempt (fie! shame!); of fear (ah! oh!);<BR>a magical or mystical monosyllable, (see हुम्.)<BR>—हूङ्-कार, अस्, m. the word or sound हूम्<BR>(uttered disrespectfully or menacingly); uttering the<BR>sound हूम्; roaring, grunting.<BR>—हूङ्-कृति, इस्, f.<BR>making the sound हूम्; grunting, groaning; a<BR>sound made in sleeping; disrespect, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूयमान
हूयमान हूयमान. See p. 1174, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूरव|हूरवः
हूरव हू-रव. See under हू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूर्छन|हूर्च्छनं
हूर्छन हूर्छन, हूर्छित. See p. 1174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूहु|हूहुः
हूहु हूहु, उस्, or हूहू, ऊस्, m. = हुहु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृ
हृ 1. हृ (evolved out of rt. भृ, which<BR>in Ved. often has the sense of rt. 1. हृ), cl. 1.<BR>P. A. हरति, -ते, (Ved. भरति), जहार, जह्रे,<BR>(Ved. जभार, जभ्रे), हरिष्यति, -ते, अहार्षीत्,<BR>अहृत, (Ved. also cl. 2. Pres. 1st sing. P. हर्मि,<BR>also cl. 3. P. जिहर्ति; in Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa X. 4,<BR>3, 9. there is a form हरासै, ‘thou may'st have<BR>seized’), हर्तुम्, to bring, convey, carry, fetch; to<BR>carry away, carry off, take away, take off, seize, take<BR>hold of, extricate; to rob, plunder, steal; to strip off,<BR>spoil, despoil, remove, deprive of; to take, acquire, gain,<BR>obtain, hold; to captivate, charm; to accept, receive,<BR>inherit; to throw, cast (an arrow &c.); to offer:<BR>Pass. ह्रियते, Aor. अहारि, to be taken or seized, &c.:<BR>Caus. हारयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अजीहरत्, -त, to<BR>cause to bring or carry or seize (with acc. and inst.<BR>or with a double acc.), cause to take or take hold of;<BR>to give, give away; to permit to be carried off or<BR>plundered; to send: Desid. जिहीर्षति, -ते, to wish<BR>to take or carry off, wish to rob, &c.: Intens.<BR>जेह्रीयते, जर्हरीति, जरिहरीति, जरीहरीति, जर्-<BR>हर्ति, जरिहर्ति, जरीहर्ति; [cf. Zend zar; Gr.<BR>χείρ, εὐ-χερ-ής, χέρ-ης, χράομαι, κίχρημι, (accord-<BR>ing to some also perhaps) αἴρω, αἱρέω (for χαίρω),<BR>ἀγείρω; Old Lat. hir; Lat. heru-s, hera, her-e(d)-s,<BR>(perhaps also) co-hors, (according to some also per-<BR>haps) gero; Goth. geiro, gairon, gairnjan; Angl.<BR>Sax. georu, geornian; Eng. yare.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर|हरः
हर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, bringing, conveying, carry-<BR>ing, taking, seizing; captivating; removing, taking<BR>away, depriving of; dividing; (अस्), m. the act of<BR>carrying, taking, seizing; a seizer; N. of Śiva; of<BR>Agni; of one of the eleven Rudras; an ass; (in<BR>arithmetic) a divisor; the denominator of a fraction,<BR>division; [cf. Lat. hœres.]<BR>—हर-गौरी, f. one of<BR>the forms of Śiva or of Śiva and Pārvatī conjoined (=<BR>अर्ध-नारीश).<BR>—हर-चापारोपण (˚प-आर्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Nāṭaka or drama.<BR>—हर-चूडा-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. ‘Śiva's crest-gem,’ the moon.<BR>—हर-<BR>जित्, त्, m. a proper N.<BR>—हर-तेजस्, अस्, n. Śiva's<BR>energy; quicksilver.<BR>—हर-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of the Pada-mañjarī; of the Mitākṣarā<BR>commentary.<BR>—हरदत्ताचार्य (˚त-आच्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—हर-दास, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—हर-नेत्र, अम्, n. Śiva's eye; the number<BR>three.<BR>—हर-रूप, अस्, m. ‘having the form of<BR>Hara,’ Śiva.<BR>—हर-वीज, अम्, n. ‘Śiva's seed,’<BR>quicksilver.<BR>—हर-शेखरा, f. ‘Śiva's crest,’ the<BR>Ganges.<BR>—हर-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—हराद्रि (˚र-अद्˚), इस्, m. ‘Śiva's mountain,’<BR>the mountain Kailāsa (fabled as the favourite resort<BR>of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरक|हरकः
हरक, अस्, m. a conveyer, taker; a seizer; N.<BR>of Śiva; a thief, rogue, cheat; (in arithmetic) a<BR>divisor; division; a reflecting or judicious person<BR>(according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरण|हरणं
हरण, अस्, m. ‘the taker,’ the hand; (अम्), n.<BR>the act of taking, accepting, receiving; seizing, carry-<BR>ing off or away, removing; stealing; withholding,<BR>annulling, disregarding; a nuptial present (= यौ-<BR>तक); a gift to a student at his initiation; the<BR>arm; semen virile; gold; a shell, cowry (= क-<BR>पर्द); boiling water; (in arithmetic) dividing,<BR>division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरणीय
हरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or accepted,<BR>acceptable; to be taken away or seized; to be<BR>divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरत्
हरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, conveying, taking away,<BR>seizing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरयाण
हरयाण, अस्, m. (according to some) a proper<BR>N., (according to Nirukta V. 15. = हरमाण-यान;<BR>according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 25, 22. = श-<BR>त्रु-जीवितैश्वर्यादि-हरण-शील-यान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरस्
हरस्, अस्, n., Ved. anger, (Sāy. = क्रोध; cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">Page1175-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Naigh. II. 13); flame, heat, warmth, (enumerated<BR>among the ज्वलतो नामधेयानि, Naigh. I. 17);<BR>impetuosity, precipitation; day; water; blood; the<BR>world, (see Nirukta IV. 19.)<BR>—हरस्-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. impetuous, precipitate, (Sāy. = वेग-वत्);<BR>(अती), f., Ved. a river, (in Naigh. I. 13. हरस्व-<BR>त्यः is enumerated among the नदी-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्
2. हरिमन्, आ, m. (for. 1. see p. 1167), time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्त
हर्त, अस्, m. = हर्तृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्तव्य|हर्त्तव्य
हर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or accepted,<BR>to be seized, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्तृ|हर्त्तृ
हर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who brings or conveys,<BR>one who takes or receives, a taker, receiver, seizer;<BR>a robber; taking up, absorbing; (ता), m. the sun<BR>(= सूर्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार|हारं|हारः
1. हार, अस्, ई, अम्, taking, conveying, seizing,<BR>carrying off, who or what takes, &c.; (according to<BR>Śabda-k. fr. 1. हरि), relating or belonging to Hari<BR>or Viṣṇu (= हरि-सम्बन्धीय); (अस्), m. the<BR>act of taking or conveying away, abstraction, seizing,<BR>removing, deprivation; loss, (काल-हार, loss of time,<BR>waste of time); a porter, carrier; war, battle; a<BR>string or garland of pearls, &c., a pearl-necklace, any<BR>necklace; (in prosody) a long syllable; (in arithmetic)<BR>a divisor, a denominator of a fraction; (ई), f. a pearl.<BR>—हार-गुटिका, f. the bead or pearl of a necklace.<BR>—हार-यष्टि, इस्, f. a string of pearls, necklace.<BR>—हार-लता, f., N. of a work.<BR>—हार-हारा, f. a<BR>kind of tawny grape.<BR>—हारावली (˚र-आव्˚), f. a string<BR>of pearls; N. of a lexicon by Puruṣottama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार|हारं|हारः
2. हार, Nom. P. हारति, &c., to act like a string<BR>of pearls, be like a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारक|हारकः
हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, bringing; taking, seizing;<BR>(अस्), m. one who seizes or takes away, a plunderer,<BR>thief; a cheat, rogue; a gambler; a kind of prose<BR>composition; a particular science; the tree Trophis<BR>Aspera; (in arithmetic) a divisor; a string of pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारयिष्यत्
हारयिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to con-<BR>vey or transmit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारा
हारा, f. See Vopa-deva XXVI. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारि|हारिः
हारि, इस्, इस्, इ, captivating, charming, pleasing,<BR>beautiful; (इस्), f. defeat, discomfiture; losing a game<BR>(in gambling); a traveller's progeny (= पथिक-<BR>सन्तान), a caravan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारित|हारितः
2. हारित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. हारित see p. 1170,<BR>col. 2), made or allowed to be taken, caused to be<BR>taken away; presented, offered; suffered to be seized,<BR>made away with, lost, relinquished; captivated, fas-<BR>cinated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिन्
1. हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking, conveying, bringing,<BR>carrying away, seizing, robbing; obtaining, acquir-<BR>ing; a seizer, disturber (with gen., Manu XII. 28);<BR>captivating, charming, delighting; pleasant, agree-<BR>able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिन्
2. हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a necklace, possessing<BR>a necklace or garland of pearls.<BR>—हारि-कण्ठ, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having a necklace on the throat; (अस्), m.<BR>‘having a ring on the throat,’ the Kokila or Indian<BR>cuckoo, Koïl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारियोजन
हारियोजन, अस्, m. (see हरि-योजन), ‘har-<BR>nesser of the Hari steeds,’ Indra; a particular Graha<BR>or portion of an offering taken out of the Āgrayaṇa<BR>libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारी
हारी, f. a pearl, (see हार above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीत|हारीतः
2. हारीत, अस्, m. (for 1. see p. 1170, col. 2), a<BR>thief, cheat, rogue; thieving, cheating, fraud, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्य|हार्यः|हार्य्य|हार्य्यः
हार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken, to be taken<BR>away; (अस्), m. a serpent; the Vibhītaka tree; (in<BR>arithmetic) the dividend (= भाज्य).<BR>—हार्य-पु-<BR>त्र, अस्, m., N. of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्
हृत्, त्, त्, त् (at the end of comps.), taking away,<BR>removing, carrying off, seizing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत|हृतं
हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, taken, taken away, seized;<BR>captivated; accepted; (अम्), n. that which is taken;<BR>a portion, share.<BR>—हृत-चन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the moon taken away; destitute of moon, moon-<BR>less.<BR>—हृत-ज्ञान, अस्, आ, अम्, bereft of knowledge,<BR>void of knowledge.<BR>—हृत-द्रव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>stripped of everything, deprived of one's property.<BR>—हृत-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, spoiled of wealth.<BR>—हृत-प्रसाद, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of calmness.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">Page1175-c+ 79</a>]<BR>—हृत-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of mind,<BR>robbed of one's senses.<BR>—हृत-राज्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>stripped of a kingdom.<BR>—हृत-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>whose dress is taken away, deprived of clothes.<BR>—हृत-सर्वस्व, अस्, आ, अम्, robbed or stripped<BR>of all personal property, entirely ruined.<BR>—हृता-<BR>धिकार (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of an<BR>office, turned out; deprived of one's right.<BR>—हृ-<BR>तोत्तर (˚त-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of an answer,<BR>left without a reply.<BR>—हृतोत्तरीय (˚त-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the upper garments stripped off.<BR>—हृतोरग (˚त-उर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deprived or<BR>devoid of snakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृति|हृतिः
हृति, इस्, f. taking away, seizure, robbing, rob-<BR>bery; destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्वा
हृत्वा, ind. having taken or seized, having ac-<BR>cepted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रियमाण
ह्रियमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being taken or seized;<BR>being captivated or attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृ
हृ 2. हृ or हॄ (referred in native lists<BR>to the Nom. हृणीय below, technically called<BR>हृणीङ्, but connected with rt. 1. ह्री, q. v., and<BR>perhaps better written हॄ), cl. 9. A. हृणीते, &c.,<BR>Ved. originally perhaps ‘to be yellow’ (cf. हरि);<BR>to blush; to be ashamed, (Sāy. लज्जायाम्); to<BR>be angry (रोषायाम्), be displeased, (Sāy. हृणीते<BR>= क्रुध्यति, Ṛg-veda VII. 86, 3; हृणीषे = क्रु-<BR>ध्यसि, Ṛg-veda VII. 104, 14.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणान
हृणान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. angry, irate, displeased,<BR>(Sāy. = हृणीयमान, Ṛg-veda I. 25, 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणि|हृणिः
हृणि, इस्, m., Ved. anger (= क्रोध, Naigh. II.<BR>13); flaming, (in Naigh. I. 17. enumerated among<BR>the ज्वलतो नामधेयानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणिया
हृणिया, f. = हृणीया below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीय
हृणीय, Nom. A. हृणीयते, &c., to be angry;<BR>to be ashamed; [cf. Gr. χολή; Lat. fel, bilis;<BR>Old Germ. galla; Angl. Sax. gealla.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीयमान
हृणीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीया
हृणीया, f. censure, reproach; shame, bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्
हृद् हृद्, त्, n. (abbreviated fr. हर्द्, but<BR>said by some to be connected with rt. 1. हृ;<BR>it is defective in declension, being optionally substi-<BR>tuted for हृदय in all cases except the first five<BR>inflections or Nom. sing. du. pl., Acc. sing. du.; it<BR>is said by some to be also masc.), the heart; the<BR>mind, (हृद्य् अवेदिन्, ‘one who has no knowledge<BR>or capacity of knowledge in the mind,’ applied to<BR>animals), the soul, the faculty or seat of thought<BR>and feeling; the interior of the body, breast, chest,<BR>bosom; the interior or essence of anything; [cf.<BR>Gr. κῆρ, κέαρ, καρδ-ία, κραδ-ίη; Lat. cor (cord-is),<BR>dimin. cor-culum, cordatus, vêcors; Goth. hairt-o;<BR>Old Germ. herza; Mod. Germ. Herz; Angl. Sax.<BR>heorte; Eng. heart; Lith. szird-i-s; Slav. srŭ-<BR>dĭce.]<BR>—हृच्-छय, अस्, आ, अम् (i. e. हृद् + शय),<BR>lying or abiding in the heart; (अस्), m. ‘heart-<BR>dweller,’ epithet of Kāma-deva (god of love), love.<BR>—हृच्छय-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, tormented by love,<BR>love-sick.<BR>—हृच्छय-वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, aug-<BR>menting love.<BR>—हृच्छयाविष्ट-चेतन (˚य-आव्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a heart penetrated by love.<BR>—हृच्-<BR>छूल, अम्, n. (i. e. हृद् + शूल), ‘heart-pang,’ any<BR>acute internal pain, pain in the chest.<BR>—हृच्-छोक,<BR>अस्, m. (i. e. हृद् + शोक), heart-ache; a pang.<BR>—हृत्-<BR>कम्प, अस्, m. heart-throb, tremor of the heart, palpita-<BR>tion.<BR>—हृत्-पिण्ड, अम्, n. ‘heart-mass,’ the heart.<BR>—हृत्-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the heart, seated<BR>in the heart.<BR>—हृत्स्व्-अस्, अस्, अस्, अस्, Ved. throwing<BR>into the heart.<BR>—हृदं-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. giving<BR>the heart; receiving the heart or essence of anything;<BR>receiving affection or kindness.<BR>—हृद्-आवर्त, अस्,<BR>m. a curl or lock of hair on a horse's chest.<BR>—हृदि-<BR>स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, ‘touching or lying in the heart,’ dear,<BR>beloved, cherished.<BR>—हृद्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone<BR>to the heart, seated in the heart or mind, come to<BR>mind, conceived, designed; cherished; (अम्), n.<BR>anything fixed in the mind, design, meaning, intent.<BR>—हृद्-गोल, अस्, m., N. of a mountainous district.<BR>—हृद्गोलीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the above<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">Page1176-a+ 81</a>]<BR>district; (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of the Hṛd-gola<BR>mountains.<BR>—हृद्-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘heart-seizure,’<BR>spasm of the heart.<BR>—हृद्-ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. (accord-<BR>ing to Śabda-k.) a heart-wound, heart-sore (= हृद्-<BR>व्रण).<BR>—हृद्-देश, अस्, m. the region of the<BR>heart.<BR>—हृद्-भेद-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tan-<BR>tra work.<BR>—हृद्-रुज्, क्, f. ‘heart-disease,’ grief.<BR>—हृद्-रोग, अस्, m. heart-disease, heart-ache, heart-<BR>burn; sorrow, grief, anguish; love; the zodiacal<BR>sign Aquarius.<BR>—हृद्रोग-वैरिन्, ई, m. ‘hostile<BR>to heart-burn,’ the tree Pentaptera Arjuna.<BR>—हृद्-<BR>वण्टक, अस्, m. ‘partitioning the heart or chest,’<BR>the stomach.<BR>—हृल्-लास, अस्, m. ‘heart-sport,’<BR>hiccough; heart-disturbance, disquietude, grief.<BR>—हृल्-लेख, अस्, m. ‘heart-impression,’ knowledge,<BR>reasoning; ‘heart-scratch,’ heart-ache, heart-sorrow;<BR>(आ), f. disquietude, anxiety or regret for any absent<BR>object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदय|हृदयं
हृदय, अम्, n. the mind, soul, seat or faculty<BR>of thought and feeling, (चपल-हृदय, fickle-<BR>minded); affection, love; the heart; the interior of<BR>the body, breast, chest, bosom; the interior or centre<BR>or essence of anything; true or divine knowledge;<BR>the Veda; science; [cf. Gr. καρδία, &c.; Hib. croi-<BR>dhe, cridhe, ‘the heart.’]<BR>—हृदय-कम्प, अस्,<BR>m. tremor or throb of the heart, palpitation.<BR>—हृ-<BR>दय-कम्पन, अम्, n. throbbing of the heart;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), heart-stirring, heart-agitating, causing<BR>the heart to throb (with indignation &c.).<BR>—हृ-<BR>दय-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. ‘heart-tie, heart-bond,’ any-<BR>thing which binds the soul.<BR>—हृदय-ग्राहिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, heart-captivating, engaging the affection.<BR>—हृदयङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, going to the heart,<BR>heart-stirring, thrilling, affecting, touching, moving,<BR>dear, beloved; (अम्), n. an apposite or appropriate<BR>speech.<BR>—हृदय-चौर, अस्, m. a heart-robber,<BR>one who steals the heart or affections.<BR>—हृदय-<BR>च्छिद्, त्, त्, त्, heart-breaking, heart-piercing, heart-<BR>rending.<BR>—हृदय-दौर्बल्य, अम्, n. weakness<BR>of heart, faintheartedness.<BR>—हृदय-रज्जु, (in<BR>geometry) a central line, the semidiameter of a circle<BR>in contact with the angles of a trapezium.<BR>—हृदय-<BR>लेख, अस्, m. heart-impression, knowledge; ‘heart-<BR>scratch,’ heart-ache, anxiety, (see हृल्-लेख.)<BR>—हृ-<BR>दय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a heart, tender-hearted,<BR>kind, humane.<BR>—हृदय-विध्, त्, त्, त् (विध् for<BR>व्यध्, see rt. 2. विध्), heart-piercing.<BR>—हृदय-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. disposition or inclination of the heart.<BR>—हृदय-वेधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, heart-piercing, piercing<BR>the vitals (said of an arrow).<BR>—हृदय-शल्य, अम्,<BR>n. a dagger or arrow in the heart, wound in the<BR>heart.<BR>—हृदय-शोक, अस्, m. heart-sorrow, heart-<BR>ache, a pang of grief.<BR>—हृदय-शोषण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>heart-withering.<BR>—हृदय-सन्निहित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>placed or deposited in the heart, fixed or laid up in<BR>the mind.<BR>—हृदय-सम्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, breast-<BR>high, as high as the breast.<BR>—हृदय-साहि, इस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—हृदय-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in<BR>the heart, cherished in the heart.<BR>—हृदय-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. ‘seat of the heart,’ the breast, chest, bosom.<BR>—हृदयात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, m. a heron.<BR>—हृ-<BR>दयामय (˚य-आम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having sick-<BR>ness of heart, heart-sickening.<BR>—हृदयाम्बुज<BR>(˚य-अम्˚), अम्, n. ‘heart-lotus,’ a lotus-like heart.<BR>—हृदयाविध् (˚य-आव्˚), त्, त्, त्, heart-piercing.<BR>—हृदयेश (˚य-ईश) or हृदयेश्वर (˚य-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘heart-lord,’ a husband; (आ), f. ‘heart-<BR>mistress,’ a wife; a mistress.<BR>—हृदयोदङ्क (˚य-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. upheaving or torturing the heart; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), heart heaving, heart-disturbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयालु|हृदयालुः
हृदयालु, उस्, उस्, उ, good-hearted, tender-<BR>hearted, affectionate, friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयावी
हृदयावी, (according to some) Ved. one who<BR>has a heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिक|हृदयिकः
हृदयिक, अस्, आ, अम्, good-hearted, tender-<BR>hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयित्नु
हृदयित्नु. See Vopa-deva XXVI. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिन्
हृदयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, good-hearted, tender-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदीक|हृदीकः
हृदीक, अस्, m., N. of a Yādava king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्य|हृद्यं|हृद्यः
हृद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, hearty, cordial, proceeding<BR>from or produced in the heart; dear to the heart,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">Page1176-b+ 80</a>]<BR>beloved, cherished, desired; affectionate, kind; grate-<BR>ful, pleasant, agreeable; savory; (अस्), m. a Vedic<BR>Mantra employed to effect the subjection or fascina-<BR>tion of an enemy or rival; (आ), f. the medicinal root<BR>called Vṛddhi; (अम्), n. the bank of the Laurus<BR>Cassia.<BR>—हृद्य-गन्ध, अस्, m. the Vilva tree;<BR>(आ), f. great-flowered jasmine; (अम्), n. small<BR>cumin; sochal salt.<BR>—हृद्य-गन्धि, n. small<BR>cumin.<BR>—हृद्य-ता, f. or हृद्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>cordiality, heartiness, agreeableness, delightfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृल्लास|हृल्लासः
हृल्लास हृल्-लास. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्
हृष् हृष् (originally भृष्), cl. 4. 1. P.<BR>हृष्यति, हर्षति (ep. also A. -ते), ज-<BR>हर्ष, हर्षिष्यति, अहृषत्, अहर्षीत्, हर्-<BR>षितुम्, to bristle or become erect (as the hair of<BR>the body); to thrill with rapture, rejoice, exult, be<BR>glad or pleased; to become erect (said of other things<BR>besides the hair); (according to some, also) to speak<BR>or affirm falsely, lie (but in this sense only P.): Pass.<BR>हृष्यते, Aor. अहर्षि: Caus. हर्षयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अजहर्षत् or अजीहृषत्, to make glad,<BR>cause to rejoice; to be glad, rejoice: Desid. जिहर्-<BR>षिषति: Intens. जरीहृष्यते, जर्हर्ष्टि, &c.,<BR>to rejoice very much, be exceedingly elated; [cf. Gr.<BR>φρίσσω, φρίξ, (perhaps also) χέρσος, χήρ; Lat.<BR>horreo, Hersilia; Old Germ. burst; Angl. Sax.<BR>byrst, bristl, forst, frost, frysan, a-grisan, gerst,<BR>gryre.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्ष|हर्षः
हर्ष, अस्, m. bristling, erection (especially of<BR>the hair, but also said of other things); thrilling,<BR>thrill, rapture, delight, glee, joy, pleasure, gladness,<BR>exultation, happiness; Joy (personified as a son of<BR>Dharma); N. of a king of Kaśmīra (celebrated as<BR>a great patron of learning; he was son of Hīra and<BR>was said to be himself a writer and poet, author of<BR>the Khaṇḍana-khaṇḍa-khādya, the Chanda-praśasti,<BR>the Nāgānanda-nāṭaka, the Naiṣadīya-carita, the<BR>Ratnāvalī, &c.); (अस्, आ, अम्), happy, delighted.<BR>—हर्ष-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing delight, grati-<BR>fying, delighting.<BR>—हर्ष-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of a commentary on the Śruta-bodha.<BR>—हर्ष-क्रोध, औ, m. du. joy and anger.<BR>—हर्-<BR>ष-चरित, अम्, n., N. of a poem.<BR>—हर्ष-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, arising from joy.<BR>—हर्ष-जड, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>paralyzed with joy.<BR>—हर्ष-देव, अस्, m. king<BR>Harṣa, (see हर्ष above.)<BR>—हर्ष-युक्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, filled with joy, joyful.<BR>—हर्ष-वर्धन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘joy-promoter,’ N. of a king.<BR>—हर्ष-विवर्-<BR>धन, अस्, ई, अम्, increasing or promoting joy.<BR>—हर्ष-विवृद्ध-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>vigour is increased by happiness.<BR>—हर्ष-विह्वल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, agitated with joy, overjoyed.<BR>—हर्ष-<BR>समन्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, filled with joy.<BR>—हर्ष-<BR>स्वन, अस्, m. a cry of joy, sound of pleasure.<BR>—हर्षान्वित (˚ष-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, full of joy,<BR>happy.<BR>—हर्षाविष्ट (˚ष-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>penetrated or filled with joy.<BR>—हर्षोत्कर्ष<BR>(˚ष-उत्˚), अस्, m. excess of happiness.<BR>—हर्षो-<BR>दय (˚ष-उद्˚), अस्, m. rise of joy, occurrence of<BR>pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षक|हर्षकः
हर्षक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, delighting, gladden-<BR>ing, rejoicing, pleasing, delightful; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>particular mountain; of a king belonging to the<BR>Śaiśunāga dynasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षण|हर्षणं|हर्षणः
हर्षण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing delight, de-<BR>lighting, gladdening, delightful, pleasurable, pleasant;<BR>(अस्), m. who or what delights or rejoices; ‘glad-<BR>dener,’ epithet of one of the five arrows of Kāma-<BR>deva; the fourteenth of the astronomical Yogas; a<BR>morbid affection of the eyes; a deity presiding over<BR>Śrāddhas; a kind of Śrāddha; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>delighting or making glad, pleasing, making happy;<BR>rejoicing, being happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षमाण|हर्षमाणः
हर्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, rejoicing, joyful, cheer-<BR>ful, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षयत्
हर्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to rejoice, glad-<BR>dening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षयित्नु|हर्षयित्नुः
हर्षयित्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, gladdening, causing de-<BR>light, delighting; (उस्), m. a son, child; (उ), n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षाय
हर्षाय, Nom. A. हर्षायते, &c., to be glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षित|हर्षितः
हर्षित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), made glad<BR>or happy, gladdened, delighted, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षिन्
हर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, rejoicing, delighting; (इणी), f.<BR>a particular plant (= वि-जया).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षु
हर्षु, Ved. joy, delight.<BR>—हर्षु-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. delighted, exulting; eager for war,<BR>(Sāy. = हर्ष-युक्त, i. e. सङ्ग्रामोत्सुक, Ṛg-<BR>veda VIII. 16, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षुल|हर्षुलः
हर्षुल, अस्, आ, अम्, disposed to be cheerful or<BR>happy, delighted; (अस्), m. a deer; a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषि|हृषिः
हृषि, (probably) rejoicing; (ई), m. du. Agni<BR>and Soma, (according to Śabda-k. = अग्नी-सोमौ.)<BR>—हृषी-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. full of joy, glad,<BR>happy, (Sāy. = प्राप्त-हर्ष, Ṛg-veda II. 31, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषित|हृषितं
हृषित, अस्, आ, अम्, having the hair bristling or<BR>thrilling (with joy &c.); enraptured, delighted,<BR>pleased; astonished, surprised; erect, fresh (as flowers,<BR>opposed to म्लान); disappointed, deceived; bent,<BR>bowed (= प्र-णत); armed, accoutred (= वर्-<BR>मित).<BR>—हृषित-स्रज्, क्, क्, क्, having a fresh gar-<BR>land (the flowers of which are erect and unfaded).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीक|हृषीकं
हृषीक, अम्, n. any organ of sense (= इन्द्रिय).<BR>—हृषीकेश (˚क-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the organs<BR>of sense,’ Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—हृषीकेश-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्ट|हृष्टः
हृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. हृषित], having the<BR>hair of the body bristling or thrilling (with delight<BR>or rapture), enraptured, delighted, rejoiced, pleased,<BR>glad, joyous, delighted; exulting, laughing, smiling;<BR>astonished, surprised; disappointed, deceived (=<BR>प्रति-हत).<BR>—हृष्ट-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, rejoiced<BR>in heart.<BR>—हृष्ट-पुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, merry and<BR>fat, happy and well-fed.<BR>—हृष्ट-पुष्टाङ्ग (˚ट-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, merry and fat in limb, happy and<BR>well nourished, frisky and fat.<BR>—हृष्ट-मानस,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, rejoiced in mind, glad in heart, happy.<BR>—हृष्ट-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, thrilling with happi-<BR>ness, in a happy or cheerful mood.<BR>—हृष्ट-रोमन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, having the hair of the body bristling or<BR>thrilling (with delight or rapture).<BR>—हृष्ट-वत्,<BR>ind. cheerfully.<BR>—हृष्ट-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>merry-faced, having a cheerful countenance.<BR>—हृ-<BR>ष्ट-सङ्कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased in mind, con-<BR>tented, glad.<BR>—हृष्ट-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, joyous-<BR>hearted, light-hearted, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टि|हृष्टिः
हृष्टि, इस्, f. delight, pleasure, joy, happiness;<BR>pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्ट्वा
हृष्ट्वा, ind. having rejoiced, being delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हे
हे हे, ind. a vocative particle (oh! ho!<BR>&c.); a particle used in vociferating or challenging<BR>(hallo! ho there!); an interjection expressing envy<BR>or ill-will or disapprobation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेक्का
हेक्का हेक्का, f. (fr. rt. हिक्क्), hiccough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ्
हेठ् हेठ् (according to some written हेट्),<BR>cl. 1. A. P. हेठते, हेठति (according to<BR>some हेटति), जिहेठे, हेठितुम्, to be wicked; to<BR>vex, harass, obstruct; to strike, hurt, injure; cl. 9. P.<BR>हेठ्नाति, &c. = rt. हेढ्: Caus. हेठयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अजिहेठत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ|हेठः
हेठ, अस्, m. vexation, harassing; hindering,<BR>preventing, hindrance, obstruction, opposition; in-<BR>jury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेड्
हेड् हेड् or (in the Veda) हेल् or हेऌ (see<BR>rt. हेल्), cl. 1. A. हेडते (Ved. हेलते, हे-<BR>ऌअते), जिहेडे, हेडितुम्, to disregard, slight, neglect;<BR>to be displeased or angry (Ved.; हेऌअते = क्रुध्यति,<BR>Naigh. II. 12); cl. 1. P. हेडति, जिहेड, &c., to<BR>surround, clothe, attire: Pass. हेड्यते, Aor. अहिडि<BR>or अहीडि or अहेडि, to be surrounded or attired:<BR>Caus. हेडयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अजिहेडत्, to cause to<BR>disregard, &c.; हिडयति, -यितुम्, अजीहिडत्, to cause<BR>to surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेड|हेडः
हेड, अस्, m. disregard, slight.<BR>—हेड-ज, अस्, m.<BR>passion, anger, displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडमान
हेडमान, अस्, आ, अम्, disregarding, neglecting,<BR>neglectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडस्
हेडस्, अस्, n., Ved. anger, wrath, (Sāy. = क्रोध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेळस्
हेऌअस्, अस्, n., Ved. = हेडस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडावुक्क|हेडावुक्कः
हेडावुक्क हेडावुक्क, अस्, m. (= हेलावुक्क,<BR>q. v.), a horse-dealer, horse-seller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेढ्
हेढ् हेढ् (also written हेठ्), cl. 9. P.<BR>हेढ्नाति, &c., to be born again; to pro-<BR>duce happiness, cause prosperity; to purify [cf. rts.<BR>खच्, खव्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेति|हेतिः
हेति हेति. See p. 1171, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतु|हेतुः
हेतु. See p. 1171, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्
हेमन् 2. हेमन्, अ, n. (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 144. fr. rt. 1. हि, perhaps connected with 1. हरि-<BR>मन्, ‘yellowness,’ p. 1167; cf. प्र-उग for प्र-<BR>युग; or perhaps connected with हिम, 1. हेमन्<BR>at pp. 1172, 1173), gold; water, (in Naigh. I. 2.<BR>enumerated among the हिरण्य-नामानि, and in I.<BR>12. among the उदक-नामानि); the thorn-apple;<BR>the Keśara flower.<BR>—हेम-कक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a golden girdle; having golden walls.<BR>—हेम-<BR>कन्दल, अस्, m. ‘having golden shoots,’ coral.<BR>—हेम-कर, अस्, m. a gold-worker, gold-<BR>smith; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—हेम-कर्तृ, ता, m. a<BR>goldsmith; a kind of bird.<BR>—हेम-कान्ति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>having a golden lustre; (इस्), f. a kind of Curcuma<BR>(= दारु-हरिद्रा).<BR>—हेम-कार, अस्, m. a gold-<BR>worker, goldsmith.<BR>—हेम-किञ्जल्क, अम्, n. ‘hav-<BR>ing golden filaments,’ the Nāga-keśara flower.<BR>—हे-<BR>म-किरीट-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, garlanded with a diadem<BR>of gold.<BR>—हेम-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a golden jar.<BR>—हेम-कूट, अस्, m. ‘golden-peaked,’ (perhaps<BR>also connected with 1. हेमन् at p. 1173, col. 1),<BR>one of the ranges of mountains dividing the known<BR>continent into nine Varṣas, (supposed to be situated<BR>north of Himālaya and forming with it the boundaries<BR>of the Kinnara or Kimpuruṣa Varṣa, see वर्ष.)<BR>—हेम-केतकी, f. a kind of tree (= स्वर्ण-<BR>केतकी).<BR>—हेम-केलि, इस्, m. ‘golden-sport,’ epithet<BR>of Agni or fire.<BR>—हेम-केश, अस्, m. ‘golden-<BR>haired,’ Śiva.<BR>—हेम-क्षीरी, f. the plant Svarṇa-<BR>kṣīrī, q. v.<BR>—हेम-गन्धिनी, f. the perfume Re-<BR>ṇukā.<BR>—हेम-गौर, अस्, ई, अम्, of a golden yellow<BR>colour; (अस्), m. the Kiṅkirāta tree.<BR>—हेमगौ-<BR>राङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having limbs or a<BR>body of a golden yellow colour.<BR>—हेम-चक्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, golden-wheeled, having wheels of gold.<BR>—हेम-चन्द्र, अस्, m. a golden or golden-<BR>coloured moon; N. of a king of Vaiśālī; of a phi-<BR>losopher; of a celebrated lexicographer and author<BR>(son of Jaya-siṃha-deva, author of the Abhidhāna-<BR>cintāmaṇi lexicon; of the Uṇādi-vṛtti; of a Dhātu-<BR>pāṭha; of the Vibhrama-sūtra; of a Prākṛt gram-<BR>mar; of the Chandaś-cūḍāmaṇi, &c.).<BR>—हेम-<BR>च्छन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with gold; (अम्), n.<BR>a golden covering, golden trappings (of an elephant<BR>&c.).<BR>—हेम-जीवन्ती, f. a kind of plant (= स्वर्ण-<BR>जीवन्ती).<BR>—हेम-ज्वाल, अस्, m. ‘golden-flamed,’<BR>fire.<BR>—हेम-तरु, उस्, m. ‘golden tree,’ the Datura<BR>or thorn-apple.<BR>—हेम-तार, अम्, n. = हेम-सार,<BR>blue vitriol (= तुत्थ).<BR>—हेम-दुग्ध, अस्, m.<BR>‘having golden or yellow juice,’ the glomerous fig-<BR>tree; (आ), f. the plant Svarṇa-kṣīrī; (ई), f. the plant<BR>Svarṇa-kṣīrī; a kind of tree (= यज्ञोडुम्बर).<BR>—हेम-दुग्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, having golden<BR>or yellow juice; (अस्), m. = हेम-दुग्ध above.<BR>—हेम-नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a golden nave or<BR>centre.<BR>—हेम-पर्वत, अस्, m. ‘golden-mountain,’<BR>the mountain Meru.<BR>—हेम-पीठाधिदेवता (˚ठ-<BR>अध्˚), f. the tutelary deity of a golden foot-stool,<BR>(epithet of a monarch's foot.)<BR>—हेम-पुष्प, अस्,<BR>m. ‘bearing golden flowers,’ the Campaka tree; the<BR>Lodhra tree; (ई), f. Bengal madder; other plants,<BR>= स्वर्ण-जीवन्ती, इन्द्र-वारुणी, स्वर्णुली, मु-<BR>षली, कण्टकारी; (अम्), n. the Aśoka flower; the<BR>flower of the China rose.<BR>—हेम-पुष्पक, अस्,<BR>m. the Campaka tree; the Lodhra tree; (इका), f.<BR>the golden or yellow jasmine.<BR>—हेम-फल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having golden fruit; (आ), f. a kind of plantain<BR>(= स्वर्ण-कदली).<BR>—हेम-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made or consisting of gold, golden.<BR>—हेम-माला,<BR>f. a golden garland; ‘golden-garlanded,’ the wife of<BR>Yama.<BR>—हेम-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a golden<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">Page1177-b+ 78</a>]<BR>garland, golden-crowned; (ई), m. the sun.<BR>—हेम-<BR>मृग, अस्, m. a golden deer, (according to a popular<BR>legend, the Rākṣasa Mārīca transformed himself<BR>into a golden deer and so captivated Rāma-candra<BR>and his wife Sītā, that the former left his cottage<BR>in the forest to pursue the beautiful animal; during<BR>his absence the Rākṣasa Rāvaṇa, q. v., disguised as<BR>a mendicant, presented himself before Sītā and<BR>carried her off; the whole story is told in the third<BR>book or Araṇya-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.)<BR>—हेम-<BR>यूथिका, f. the golden or yellow jasmine.<BR>—हेम-<BR>रत्न-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or consisting of gold<BR>and gems.<BR>—हेम-रागिणी, f. ‘gold-coloured,’ tur-<BR>meric.<BR>—हेम-राज, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—हेम-<BR>रेणु, उस्, उ, m. n. ‘golden-dust,’ a sort of atom;<BR>[cf. सु-रेणु, त्रस-र्˚.]<BR>—हेम-लता, f. ‘golden-<BR>creeper,’ a kind of plant (= स्वर्ण-जीवन्ती).<BR>—हे-<BR>म-लम्ब or हेम-लम्बक, अस्, m. epithet of<BR>the fifth (or thirty-first) year of Jupiter's cycle of sixty<BR>years.<BR>—हेम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, golden.<BR>—हेम-<BR>व्याकरण, अम्, n., N. of a work on grammar by<BR>Hema-sūri or Hema-candra.<BR>—हेम-शङ्ख, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having a golden conch,’ Viṣṇu.<BR>—हेम-<BR>शिखा, f. ‘gold-crested,’ the plant Svarṇa-kṣīrī, q. v.<BR>—हेम-शृङ्ग, अम्, n. a golden horn; a golden<BR>peak or summit.<BR>—हेम-शृङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, golden-<BR>horned, golden-peaked.<BR>—हेम-सार, अम्, n. blue<BR>vitriol or sulphate of copper; [cf. हेम-तार.]<BR>—हेम-सूत्र or हेम-सूत्रक, अम्, n. ‘gold-<BR>string,’ a kind of necklace.<BR>—हेम-सूरि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a grammarian (= हेम-चन्द्र).<BR>—हेम-<BR>हस्ति-रथ, अस्, m. ‘golden-elephant-chariot,’ N.<BR>of one of the sixteen Mahā-dānas; [cf. हिरण्याश्व-<BR>रथ.]<BR>—हेमाङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a golden<BR>body; (अस्, आ or ई, अम्), having a golden body,<BR>golden-limbed, golden; (अस्), m. Garuḍa; a lion;<BR>the mountain Su-meru; Brahmā; Viṣṇu; the Cam-<BR>paka tree.<BR>—हेमाङ्ग-द, अस्, m., N. of a Gan-<BR>dharva.<BR>—हेमाढ्य (˚म-आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abounding in gold.<BR>—हेमाद्रि (˚म-अद्˚), इस्, m.<BR>‘golden-mountain,’ (perhaps also connected with<BR>1. हेमन् at p. 1173, col. 1), the mountain Su-<BR>meru; N. of a Kṣatriya king, (according to Śabda-k.<BR>author of the Cintāmaṇi-kāmadhenu-kalpadruma-<BR>smṛti-saṅgraha; also author of the Harilīlā-viveka<BR>and of a commentary on the Aṣṭāṅga-hṛdaya-<BR>saṃhitā, &c.); N. of a work.<BR>—हेमाद्रि-जरण,<BR>अस्, m. the plant Svarṇa-kṣīrī, q. v.<BR>—हेमाम्भोज<BR>(˚म-अम्˚), अम्, n. a golden lotus-flower.<BR>—हे-<BR>माह्व (˚म-आह्˚), अस्, m. ‘called after gold,’ the<BR>wild Campaka tree; the thorn-apple; (आ), f. a kind<BR>of plant (= स्वर्ण-जीवन्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेम|हेमं|हेमः
हेम, अम्, n. (abbreviated fr. 2. हेमन्, col. 1),<BR>gold; (अस्), m. a horse of a dark or brownish colour<BR>[cf. हरिय, p. 1167]; a particular weight of gold<BR>(= माषक); N. of the father of Su-tapas; of a<BR>king; = हेम-चन्द्र, q. v.; (आ), f. a handsome<BR>woman; an Apsaras of Indra's heaven; N. of a<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमक|हेमकं
हेमक, अम्, n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमल|हेमलः
हेमल, अस्, m. a goldsmith; a chameleon, lizard;<BR>the touchstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमवल|हेमवलं
हेमवल, अम्, n. a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेम्य
हेम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, golden, made of gold.<BR>—हे-<BR>म्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having golden trappings,<BR>(Sāy. = सुवर्ण-निर्मित-कक्ष्यावत्, having a<BR>girth made of gold, Ṛg-veda IV. 2, 8.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्त|हेमंत|हेमंतं|हेमंतः|हेमन्तः
हेमन्त हेमन्त. See p. 1173, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमवल|हेमवलं
हेमवल हेमवल. See p. 1173, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेय|हेयः
हेय हेय. See under rts. 2. 3. हा, 1. हि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेर|हेरं
हेर हेर, अम्, n. (perhaps fr. rt. 1. हि, or<BR>connected with rt. 1. हृ), a sort of crown or tiara;<BR>turmeric; demoniacal illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरिक|हेरिकः
हेरिक, अस्, m. [cf. हैरिक], a spy, secret emis-<BR>sary or agent, (said to be also written हेरक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्ब|हेरंब|हेरंबः|हेरम्बः
हेरम्ब हेरम्ब, अस्, m., N. of Gaṇeśa; a<BR>buffalo; a boastful hero (vain of his own valour); a<BR>particular Buddha (= हेरुक).<BR>—हेरम्ब-जननी,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">Page1177-c+ 73</a>]<BR>f. ‘mother of Gaṇeśa,’ Durgā.<BR>—हेरम्ब-मन्त्र,<BR>अस्, m. a particular Mantra (sacred to Gaṇeśa).<BR>—हेरम्ब-हट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a country, (said<BR>to be one of the provinces of the Deccan.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरम्ब
हैरम्ब, अस्, ई, अम्, connected with or belong-<BR>ing to Gaṇeśa; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरुक|हेरुकः
हेरुक हेरुक, अस्, m. an attendant on<BR>Mahā-kāla or Śiva; (with Buddhists) an inferior<BR>Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेल्
हेल् 1. हेल्. See rt. हेड्, p. 1176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेल्
हेल् 2. हेल् or हेऌ (connected with rt.<BR>हिल्) = rt. हेड्, q. v.; cl. 1. A. हेलते, &c.,<BR>to disregard, slight; to be angry, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीळित
हीऌइत, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Sāy. fr. rt. हेड्<BR>or हेऌ), Ved. angry, displeased (= क्रुद्ध, Ṛg-<BR>veda I. 80, 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलञ्ची
हेलञ्ची, f. a kind of pot-herb (= हिल-मोचि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलन|हेलनं
हेलन, अम्, n. the act of disregarding, slighting,<BR>disrespect, contempt [cf. अव-हेलन]; sporting<BR>amorously, wanton dalliance; [cf. rt. हिल्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेला
हेला, f. disrespect, contempt [cf. अव-हेला]; wan-<BR>ton sport, amorous dalliance, manner or gesture of<BR>lovers, play, sport, pastime, pleasure, delight, (हेलया,<BR>inst. c. sportively, out of mere sport or pastime, for<BR>amusement); facility, ease, (हेलया, with the greatest<BR>ease, easily, at once); moonlight; pausing in a note<BR>or shaking as in music.<BR>—हेला-राज, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a commentator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलि|हेलिः
1. हेलि, इस्, f. dalliance, wanton sport, amorous<BR>embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलित
हेलित, अस्, आ, अम्, disregarded, neglected, slighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलावुक्क|हेलावुक्कः
हेलावुक्क हेलावुक्क, अस्, m. (= हेडावुक्क),<BR>a horse-dealer, horse-seller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलि|हेलिः
हेलि 2. हेलि, इस्, m. (probably borrowed fr.<BR>Gr. ἥλιος), the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलु
हेलु हेलु, N. of a village in Kaśmīra.<BR>—हेलु-ग्राम, अस्, m. the village Helu.<BR>—हेलु-<BR>दिण्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (दिण्ण Prākṛt for दत्त), pre-<BR>sented with (the village) Helu, having received Helu<BR>as a present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेळस्
हेळस् हेऌअस्. See हेडस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेष्
हेष् हेष् [cf. rt. ह्रेष्], cl. 1. A. हेषते,<BR>जिहेषे, हेषितुम्, to neigh (as a horse),<BR>whinny; to make any inarticulate sound, bray, roar;<BR>[cf. Gr. γίννος; Lat. hinnio (for hisnio), hin-<BR>nulus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेष|हेषः
हेष, अस्, m. neighing; a neigh, braying, roaring.<BR>—हेष-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. making a neighing<BR>or roaring sound, roaring, (in Ṛg-veda III. 26, 5.<BR>said of lions; according to Sāy. हेष-क्रतवः =<BR>हेषा-रवस्य क्रतुः करणं येषां ते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषस्
हेषस्, Ved. (probably) neighing, braying; sound-<BR>ing, (in Ṛg-veda X. 89. 12. Sāy. explains हेषसा<BR>by शब्द-कारिण्या हेत्या.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषा
हेषा, f. neighing (of horses), whinnying, braying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषाय
हेषाय, Nom. A. हेषायते, -यितुम्, to neigh,<BR>whinny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषित|हेषितं
हेषित, अम्, n. a neigh or any similar inarticulate<BR>sound, neighing, whinnying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषिन्
हेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, neighing; (ई), m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेहे
हेहे हे-हे, ind. (हे, q. v., repeated), a vo-<BR>cative particle (used in addressing, calling, or vocife-<BR>rating).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

है
है है, ind. a vocative particle (used in<BR>calling or vociferating).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैतुक|हैतुकः
हैतुक हैतुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. हेतु), causal,<BR>causative; argumentative, rationalistic; (अस्), m. a<BR>reasoner, arguer, logical reasoner; a follower of the<BR>Mīmāṃsā doctrines; one who requires a reason for<BR>everything, a rationalist, sceptic, causalist, sophist,<BR>heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैतुक्य
हैतुक्य, अम्, n. causality, causativeness, (अ-है-<BR>तुक्य, अम्, n. absence of interested motives.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैम|हैमं|हैमः
हैम 1. हैम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. हेमन्),<BR>wintry, brumal, cold, frigid, freezing; (अम्), n. hoar-<BR>frost, dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन|हैमनं|हैमनः
1. हैमन, अस्, ई, अम्, winterly, cold; growing<BR>in winter, suitable to winter; (अस्), m. the month<BR>Mārgaśīrṣa (= November-December); a kind of<BR>rice which grows in winter, = षष्टिक; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. winter, the cold season, wintry weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन्त|हैमन्तं
हैमन्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. हेमन्त), wintry,<BR>cold; growing in winter, &c.; suitable to winter;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. the winter season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन्तिक|हैमंतिक|हैमन्तिकं
हैमन्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, wintry, cold, growing<BR>in winter; (अम्), n. a kind of rice, (see हैमन<BR>above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमल|हैमलः
हैमल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. हिमल), winter,<BR>the cold season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमवत|हैमवतं|हैमवतः
हैमवत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. हिम-वत्), snowy,<BR>covered with snow; flowing from the snowy moun-<BR>tain; bred in or belonging to the Himālaya moun-<BR>tains; (अस्), m. a sort of poison; (ई), f. epithet of<BR>the goddess Pārvatī; the river Ganges (which rises<BR>in the Himālaya mountains); N. of a wife of Viśvā-<BR>mitra; a kind of drug or perfume (= रेणुका); a<BR>kind of white orris root; common flax (= अतसी);<BR>the plant Svarṇa-kṣīrī; a kind of myrobalan (=<BR>हरीतकी); the tawny grape, (in some of these last<BR>senses probably to be connected with 2. हैम<BR>below); (अम्), n. Bhārata-varṣa or India.<BR>—है-<BR>मवत-वर्ष, अम्, n. India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैम|हैमं|हैमः
हैम 2. हैम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. हेमन्),<BR>golden, made of gold; of a golden yellow colour;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Śiva; the plant Gentiana Che-<BR>rayta; (आ or ई), f. yellow jasmine; (अम्), n. the<BR>lexicon of Hema-candra.<BR>—हैम-कोष, अस्, m.<BR>Hema-candra's lexicon.<BR>—हैम-चित्र-समुत्सेध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, enchased with golden pictures.<BR>—हैम-<BR>मुद्रा or हैम-मुद्रिका, f. a golden coin.<BR>—है-<BR>ममुद्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, having or possessing a golden<BR>coin.<BR>—हैम-वल्कल, अस्, आ, अम्, having bark<BR>garments set with gold, clothed in gold.<BR>—हैमा-<BR>नेकार्थ (˚म-अन्˚), N. of a lexicon.<BR>—हैमी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become golden, turned into gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन|हैमनं|हैमनः
2. हैमन, अस्, ई, अम्, golden, made of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैयङ्गवीन|हैयंगवीन|हैयंगवीनं|हैयङ्गवीनं
हैयङ्गवीन हैयङ्गवीन, अम्, n. (fr. ह्यस्<BR>+ गो with insertion of nasal), clarified butter pre-<BR>pared from yesterday's milking; butter prepared only<BR>a day before it is used, fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरण्यगर्भ
हैरण्यगर्भ हैरण्यगर्भ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>हिरण्य-गर्भ), belonging to Hiraṇya-garbha;<BR>(अस्), m. the offspring of Hiraṇya-garbha (i. e. Manu<BR>Svāyambhuva, son of Brahmā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरण्यवासस्
हैरण्यवासस् हैरंयवासस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (fr.<BR>हिरण्य + वासस्), having a golden dress or covering;<BR>(आस्), m. an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरण्यस्तूप
हैरण्यस्तूप हैरण्यस्तूप, अस्, ई, अम्, be-<BR>longing to Hiraṇya-stūpa, q. v.; (अस्), m. a patro-<BR>nymic, (see हिरण्य-स्तूप.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरम्ब
हैरम्ब हैरम्ब. See under हेरम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरिक|हैरिकः
हैरिक हैरिक, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rt. 1. हृ, cf. हरिक), a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहय|हैहयः
हैहय हैहय, अस्, m. (thought by some<BR>to be connected with हय, a horse), N. of a tribe<BR>of people (said to have been descendants of Yadu;<BR>they are described in the Purāṇas as separated into<BR>five divisions, viz. the Tāla-jaṅghas, Vīti-hotras,<BR>Āvantyas, Tuṇḍikeras, and Jātas; they are said to<BR>have overrun parts of India along with the Śakas or<BR>Scythian tribes); N. of the great grandson of Yadu;<BR>of Arjuna Kārtavīrya (as ninth in descent from<BR>Haihaya or as king of the Haihayas; he is said to<BR>have had a thousand arms; see कार्तवीर्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहेय|हैहेयः
हैहेय, अस्, m. Arjuna Kārtavīrya (= हैहय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हो
हो हो, ind. a vocative particle used in<BR>calling to a person or in challenging (ho! hallo!);<BR>also expressive of surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड्
होड् होड् [cf. rts. हुड्, हूड्], cl. 1. A.<BR>होडते, जुहोडे, &c., to disregard, disrespect<BR>(= rt. हेड्); cl. 1. P. होडति, जुहोड, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड|होडः
होड, अस्, m. a raft, float, boat (= तरान्धु);<BR>a title of a particular class of Kāyasthas; a title of<BR>Śrotriya Brāhmans in Bengal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होडा
होडा होडा, f. (according to the Laghu-<BR>kaumudī), a young girl (in the language of the Vedas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होडृ
होडृ होडृ, आ, m. (said to be fr. rt. हुड्;<BR>cf. हुर् under rt. हुर्छ्), a robber, foot-pad, high-<BR>way-robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होढ|होढं
होढ 1. होढ, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. हुर् under rt.<BR>हुर्छ्], stolen; (अम्), n. stolen goods; [cf. 2. स-<BR>होढ, p. 1102.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होढ|होढं
2. होढ, Nom. A. होढते, होढायते, see Vopa-<BR>deva XXI. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होतृ
होतृ होतृ, ता, त्री, तृ (according to Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 96. fr. rt. हु; according to others in the sense<BR>‘priest,’ fr. rt. ह्वे), sacrificing, offering oblations with<BR>fire, a sacrificer; (ता), m. an offerer of an oblation<BR>or burnt-offering (with fire); a priest who at a<BR>sacrifice invokes the gods or recites the prayers of<BR>the Ṛg-veda, a priest conversant with the Ṛg-veda,<BR>(one of the four kinds of officiating priest, see ऋत्व्-<BR>इज्, p. 181; properly the Hotṛ priest has three<BR>assistants, sometimes called Puruṣas, viz. the Maitrā-<BR>varuṇa, Acchāvāka, and Grāva-stut; to these are<BR>sometimes added three others, making seven Hotṛ<BR>priests in all, viz. the Brāhmaṇācchaṃsin, Agnīdhra<BR>or Agnīdh, and Potṛ, though these last are properly<BR>assigned to the Brahman priest; sometimes the<BR>Neṣṭṛ is substituted for the Grāva-stut); a sacri-<BR>ficing priest (in general); an epithet of Agni or fire,<BR>(in this sense fr. rt. हु); (त्री), f. one of the eight<BR>Mūrtis or Tanus, i. e. material manifestations of Śiva,<BR>(but this may be referred to होत्रिन्, see शिव.)<BR>—होता-<BR>पोतारौ, m. du. (nom. c.) the Hotṛ and Potṛ<BR>priests.<BR>—होतृ-वूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (a rite) in<BR>which a priest has to be chosen.<BR>—होतृ-षदन,<BR>अम्, n. the Hotṛ's seat or place where the Hotṛ sits<BR>at a sacrifice, (said to be near the उत्तर-वेदि.)<BR>—होतृ-संस्था-जप, N. of a liturgical treatise.<BR>—होतॄकार (˚तृ-ॠक्˚ or -ऌक्˚), अस्, m. the mother<BR>of the Hotṛ (according to Vopa-deva, the letters ॠ,<BR>ऌ, and ॡ being employed as mystical formularies<BR>by the Hotṛ, see ॡ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होतृक|होतृकः
होतृक, अस्, m. a minor Hotṛ priest or assistant<BR>of the Hotṛ, (see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्र|होत्रं
होत्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. हु), anything intended or<BR>fit for offering with fire (generally clarified butter);<BR>the clarified butter so offered (= हविस्); a burnt-<BR>offering, oblation with fire, a sacrifice, (in Ṛg-veda<BR>II. 36, 1. होत्र = होतुर् याग.)<BR>—होत्र-वाहन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘bearer of the burnt-offering,’ a proper N.<BR>—होत्राशंसिन् (˚र-आश्˚), ई, m. ‘a repeater of the<BR>Hotṛ verses,’ a particular minor Hotṛ priest, (the<BR>Potṛ, the Neṣṭṛ, and the Āgnīdhra belong to this<BR>class.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रक|होत्रकः
होत्रक, अस्, m., Ved. an inferior Hotṛ priest, (the<BR>Maitrāvaruṇa or Pra-śāstṛ, the Brāhmaṇācchaṃsin,<BR>and the Acchāvāka belong to this class; see हो-<BR>तृक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रा
होत्रा, f. an oblation, sacrifice; praise (= स्तुति);<BR>speech (= वाच्, Naigh. I. 11); N. of a Vedic god-<BR>dess (said to have been the wife of Agni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रिन्
होत्रिन्, ई, m. a sacrificing priest; the priest who<BR>offers the oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्री
होत्री, f. See under होतृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रीय|होत्रीयं|होत्रीयः
होत्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to an oblation,<BR>connected with a burnt-offering, &c.; (अस्), m. the<BR>priest who offers an oblation; (अम्), n. any place or<BR>chamber where oblations are offered, a sacrificial<BR>chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होम|होमः
होम, अस्, m. the act of making an oblation to<BR>the Devas or gods by casting clarified butter into the<BR>fire (accompanied with prayers and invocations; this<BR>is regarded as one of the five Mahā-yajñas and called<BR>Deva-yajña, see महा-यज्ञ, देव-यज्ञ); an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">Page1178-c+ 76</a>]<BR>oblation of clarified butter, oblation with fire, burnt-<BR>offering; a sacrifice, (अयुत-होम, अस्, m. a sacri-<BR>fice of 10,000 burnt-offerings to the planets.)<BR>—हो-<BR>म-कुण्ड, अम्, n. a hole in the ground for receiv-<BR>ing the consecrated fire for an oblation; [cf. अग्नि-<BR>कुण्ड, हवनी.]<BR>—होम-द्रव्य, अम्, n. anything<BR>employed for a Homa-sacrifice or oblation.<BR>—होम-<BR>द्रव्य-परिमाण, N. of a Pari-śiṣṭa of the Sāma-<BR>veda.<BR>—होम-धान, अम्, n. a sacrificial chamber.<BR>—होम-धान्य, अम्, n. sacrificial grain; sesamum<BR>(= तिल).<BR>—होम-धूम, अस्, m. the smoke of a<BR>burnt-offering or sacrificial fire.<BR>—होम-भस्मन्,<BR>अ, n. the ashes of a burnt-offering.<BR>—होम-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, one who has offered an oblation or performed<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—होम-वेला, f. the time for the burnt-<BR>offering.<BR>—होम-शाला, f. a chamber or place for<BR>keeping the sacred fire for oblations.<BR>—होम-स्व-<BR>रोत्तर (˚र-उत्˚), N. of a work.<BR>—होमाग्नि (˚म-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, m. sacrificial fire, the fire for an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमक|होमकः
होमक, अस्, m. the priest who offers the oblation<BR>(= होतृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमन्
होमन्, अ, n. an oblation, &c. (= होम above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमि|होमिः
होमि, इस्, m. clarified butter; fire; water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमिन्
होमिन्, ई, m. the priest who makes the oblation<BR>(of clarified butter &c.); an offerer of any oblation<BR>(e. g. तिल-होमिन्, an offerer of sesamum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमीय
होमीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to an<BR>oblation, fit for an oblation, belonging to a sacrifice.<BR>—होमीय-द्रव्य, अम्, n. anything used for an<BR>oblation (as clarified butter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होम्य|होम्यं
होम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or fit for an<BR>oblation; (अम्), n. clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौतृक|हौतृकः
हौतृक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. होतृ), relating or<BR>belonging to the Hotṛ priest, sacerdotal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौत्न
हौत्न, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 105.<BR>fr. rt. हु), the offerer of an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौत्र|हौत्रं
हौत्र, अम्, n. (fr. होत्र), the office or function<BR>of a Hotṛ priest.<BR>—हौत्र-प्रयोग, N. of a prac-<BR>tical hand-book for the Hotṛ priests.<BR>—हौत्र-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of certain Sūtras by Kātyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौत्रक
हौत्रक, अम्, n., N. of a Pari-śiṣṭa of the<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौत्रिक
हौत्रिक, अम्, n. = हौत्र-सूत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौम्य|हौम्यं
हौम्य, अस्, आ or -मी, अम् (fr. होम), belonging<BR>to or fit for a Homa or oblation; (अम्), n. clarified<BR>butter.<BR>—हौम्य-धान्य, अम्, n. sacrificial grain,<BR>sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होरा
होरा होरा, f. (borrowed fr. Gr. ὥρα), the<BR>rising of a zodiacal sign; part of the duration of a<BR>sign; an hour; a mark, line; a particular scientific<BR>work or science, (probably astrological.)<BR>—होरा-<BR>फल, अम्, n. the result or effect of the rising of a<BR>sign.<BR>—होरा-मकरन्द, N. of an astrological<BR>work.<BR>—होरा-शास्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work by<BR>Satya.<BR>—होरा-सार-सुधानिधि, N. of a work by<BR>Nārāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होरिलसिंह
होरिलसिंह होरिल-सिंह, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलक|होलकः
होलक होलक, अस्, m. chick-pea or pulse<BR>half parched in the pod or fried on a grass fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलसिंह
होलसिंह होल-सिंह, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलाक|होलाकः
होलाक होलाक, अस्, m. a kind of sweating<BR>(practised for the cure of certain diseases).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलाका
होलाका होलाका, f. (perhaps fr. the sound<BR>made in singing), the spring festival held at the ap-<BR>proach of the vernal equinox (commonly called Hūlī<BR>or Holī, and one of the most popular festivals in India;<BR>it is said to be dedicated to Kṛṣṇa and the Gopīs,<BR>and is properly celebrated during the ten days pre-<BR>ceding the full moon of the month Phālguna, q. v.,<BR>but usually only for the last three or four days ending<BR>with the full moon; the chief observances described<BR>are sprinkling one another with red or yellow<BR>powder in sport, addressing passers-by with jokes,<BR>singing songs in praise of the young Kṛṣṇa, and<BR>lighting fires around which rude frolics are practised;<BR>in Marāṭhī the name Holī is said to be applied also<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">Page1179-a+ 73</a>]<BR>to the pile prepared for the fire; in some parts of<BR>India the Holī festival corresponds to or immediately<BR>precedes the Dola-yātrā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होली
होली (or according to some also होलिका, हूली), the<BR>common designation of the Holākā festival or of the<BR>song sung during the festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होहौ
होहौ हो-हौ, ind. a vocative particle (ho!<BR>ho there! hallo!), an interjection used in calling or<BR>challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौ
हौ, ind. a vocative particle, = हो-हौ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौड्
हौड् हौड्, cl. 1. P. हौडति, &c., to go<BR>(= rt. हूड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौतृक|हौतृकः
हौतृक हौतृक, हौत्न, हौत्र. See<BR>p. 1178, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नु
ह्नु ह्नु, cl. 2. A. (Ved. also P.) ह्नुते<BR>(अपि-ह्नुतस् = अपलापं कुरुतः, Ṛg-<BR>veda VIII. 31, 7), जुह्नुवे, ह्नोष्यते, अह्नोष्ट,<BR>ह्नोतुम्, to take away, rob, abstract; to with-<BR>hold, secrete, conceal; to conceal one's self, hide<BR>from any one, dissimulate or deny before any one<BR>(with dat., e. g. देवदत्ताय ह्नुते, he hides from<BR>Devadatta, Pāṇ. I. 4, 34): Pass. ह्नूयते, Aor. अह्-<BR>नावि: Caus. ह्नावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अजुह्नवत्:<BR>Desid. जुह्नूषते: Intens. जोह्नूयते, जोह्नोति;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἀνα-νεύω, νεύω, νυστάζω, νυθός; Lat. ab-<BR>nuo, nuto, gnavus, navo, i-gnavis, se-gnis, niti,<BR>nicto, con-niveo; Goth. hneivan, hnaivs; Old<BR>Germ. hnigan; Angl. Sax. hnivan, hnigan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नव|ह्नवः
ह्नव, अस्, m. secreting, hiding, concealment,<BR>(अपि-ह्नव, अस्, m. a denial, = अपलाप; cf. नि-<BR>ह्नव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नवन|ह्नवनं
ह्नवन, अम्, n. the act of secreting, concealing,<BR>dissimulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नुत
ह्नुत, अस्, आ, अम्, taken away, withheld, secreted,<BR>hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नुति|ह्नुतिः
ह्नुति, इस्, f. abstraction, concealment; denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नुत्वा
ह्नुत्वा, ind. having concealed; having dissimu-<BR>lated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नोतव्य
ह्नोतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be secreted or con-<BR>cealed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्मल्
ह्मल् ह्मल्, cl. 1. P. ह्मलति, जह्माल,<BR>&c., to shake, move; to go: Caus.<BR>ह्मलयति or ह्मालयति (the former when prepo-<BR>sitions are prefixed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्
ह्यस् ह्यस्, ind. (perhaps fr. 5. ह + द्यस्),<BR>yesterday; [cf. Gr. χθές, ἐ-χθές, χθιζό-ς,<BR>χθεσ-ινό-ς; Lat. heri, hes-ternu-s; Goth. gistra-dagis;<BR>Old Germ. gester, ‘yesterday.’]<BR>—ह्यो-भव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, what happened yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्तन|ह्यस्तनं
ह्यस्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, hesternal, belonging to<BR>yesterday, produced or occurred yesterday.<BR>—ह्यस्-<BR>तन-दिन, अम्, n. the day just past, yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्त्य|ह्यस्त्यः
ह्यस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, hesternal, of yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रग्
ह्रग् ह्रग् (also written ह्लग्), cl. 1. P.<BR>ह्रगति, जह्राग, अह्रगीत्, &c., to cover,<BR>hide, conceal: Caus. ह्रगयति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रणिया
ह्रणिया ह्रणिया, f. (= हृणीया at p. 1175,<BR>col. 3), censure, reproach, shame, bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रद्
ह्रद् ह्रद्, an older form of rt. ह्राद्,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रद|ह्रदः
ह्रद, अस्, m. a large or deep piece of water, a<BR>lake, pool; a ray of light.<BR>—ह्रद-ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>‘lake-monster,’ a crocodile, alligator.<BR>—ह्रदान्तर<BR>(˚द-अन्˚), अम्, n. another lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदिनी
ह्रदिनी, f. a river (either as supplying or issuing<BR>from a lake); lightning [cf. ह्रादिनी].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रप्
ह्रप् ह्रप् (= rt. ह्लप्, q. v.), cl. 10. P. ह्रा-<BR>पयति, &c., to speak; to sound, creak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्
ह्रस् ह्रस् [cf. rts. रस्, ह्लस्], cl. 1. P. ह्र-<BR>सति (ep. also A. -ते), जह्रास, ह्रसितुम्,<BR>to sound (in this sense = rt. ह्लस्), to become small,<BR>be diminished or lessened: Caus. ह्रासयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अजिह्रसत्, to make small or less, shorten,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">Page1179-b+ 79</a>]<BR>lessen, decrease, diminish: Desid. जिह्रसिषति:<BR>Intens. जाह्रस्यते, जाह्रस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसित
ह्रसित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded; made little, short-<BR>ened, curtailed, diminished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिमन्
ह्रसिमन्, आ, m. smallness, shortness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिष्ठ|ह्रसिष्ठः
ह्रसिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. fr. ह्रस्व), short-<BR>est, smallest; very short or small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसीयस्
ह्रसीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. fr. ह्रस्व),<BR>shorter, smaller; very small or short; (असी), f. a<BR>variety of the Gāyatrī metre (containing two lines of<BR>six syllables and one line of seven).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्व|ह्रस्वं|ह्रस्वः
ह्रस्व, अस्, आ, अम्, short, small, little, short in<BR>stature, dwarfish; low (as a doorway &c.); prosodi-<BR>ally or metrically short (opposed to दीर्घ; cf.<BR>लघु); (अस्), m. a dwarf; a short vowel, a vowel<BR>containing only one Mātrā; (आ), f. a female dwarf;<BR>a sort of kidney-bean (= मुद्ग-पर्णी); other<BR>plants or trees, = नाग-बला; = भूमि-जम्बू;<BR>(अम्), n. a particular short measure; a kind of<BR>vegetable (= गौर-सुवर्ण); green or black sul-<BR>phate of iron; [cf. Gr. χέρηϊ, χερείων, χείρων,<BR>χείριστος; perhaps Lat. brevis.]<BR>—ह्रस्व-कुश,<BR>अस्, m. short Kuśa grass, white Kuśa grass.<BR>—ह्रस्व-<BR>गर्भ, अस्, m. Kuśa grass.<BR>—ह्रस्व-गवेधुका,<BR>f. the plant Uraria Lagopodioides.<BR>—ह्रस्व-जम्बु,<BR>उस्, m. the small Jambu tree.<BR>—ह्रस्व-तण्डुल,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of rice (= राजान्न).<BR>—ह्रस्व-ता, f.<BR>or ह्रस्व-त्व, अम्, n. shortness.<BR>—ह्रस्व-दर्भ,<BR>अस्, m. short Kuśa grass, white Kuśa grass.<BR>—ह्रस्व-<BR>दा, f. gum olibanum (= शल्लकी).<BR>—ह्रस्व-पत्-<BR>त्रक, अस्, m. ‘having short leaves,’ a sort of<BR>mountain Madhūka or Bassia; (इका), f. a particular<BR>plant or tree (= अश्वत्थी).<BR>—ह्रस्व-पूर्व, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, preceded by a short vowel.<BR>—ह्रस्व-प्लक्ष,<BR>a species of small Plaksha tree (= पुण्ड्र).<BR>—ह्रस्व-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having small fruit or<BR>kernels; (आ), f. the tree Bhūmi-jambū.<BR>—ह्रस्व-<BR>बाहुक, अस्, आ, अम्, short-armed.<BR>—ह्रस्व-मूर्ति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, short in stature, small in figure, dwarfish.<BR>—ह्रस्व-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a small root;<BR>(अस्), m. the red sugar-cane.<BR>—ह्रस्व-रोमन्, आ,<BR>m. ‘having short hair,’ N. of a king.<BR>—ह्रस्व-<BR>शाखाशिफ, अस्, m. ‘having short branch-roots,’ a<BR>small tree, shrub.<BR>—ह्रस्व-सभा, f. a small or<BR>narrow hall.<BR>—ह्रस्वाग्नि (˚व-अग्˚), इस्, m. the<BR>gigantic swallow-wort (= अर्क).<BR>—ह्रस्वाङ्ग (˚व-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, short-bodied, dwarfish; (अस्), m. a<BR>dwarf; the medicinal plant and root called Jīvaka,<BR>q. v.<BR>—ह्रस्वोदय (˚व-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, followed<BR>by a short vowel.<BR>—ह्रस्वोपध (˚व-उप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a short penultimate; preceded by a short<BR>vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वक
ह्रस्वक, अस्, आ, अम्, short, small, &c. = ह्रस्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रास|ह्रासः
ह्रास, अस्, m. sound, noise; shortening, diminu-<BR>tion, abatement, decrease, decline, deterioration, de-<BR>triment; paucity, scarcity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रासक
ह्रासक, अस्, इका, अम्, shortening, diminishing,<BR>decreasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद्
ह्राद् ह्राद् (closely connected with rt.<BR>ह्लाद्; cf. rt. ह्रद्), cl. 1. A. ह्रादते,<BR>जह्रादे, ह्रादितुम्, to sound (as a drum or other<BR>musical instrument); to roar (as water, thunder);<BR>[cf. Zend zrād; Gr. χλάζω, κέ-χλαδα, probably<BR>χάλαζα; Lat. grando, grandinat; Goth. grêtan;<BR>Angl. Sax. grœtan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद|ह्रादः
ह्राद, अस्, m. noise, sound; N. of a son of<BR>Hiraṇya-kaśipu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादिन्
ह्रादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding, making a sound or<BR>noise; (इनी), f. Indra's thunderbolt; lightning;<BR>a river [cf. ह्रदिनी]; the gum olibanum tree (=<BR>शल्लकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादुनि|ह्रादुनिः
ह्रादुनि, (in Ṛg-veda I. 32, 13) a weapon, the<BR>weapon of Vṛtra, a thunderbolt, (Sāy. = अशनि.)<BR>—ह्रादुनी-वृत् or ह्रादुनि-वृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. wield-<BR>ing the thunderbolt, (said of the Maruts; Sāy. ex-<BR>plains ह्रादुनी-वृतः by ह्रादुन्या अशनेः प्र-<BR>वर्तकाः, Ṛg-veda V. 54, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रास|ह्रासः
ह्रास ह्रास. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिणिया
ह्रिणिया ह्रिणिया or ह्रिणीया, f. (= हृणीया<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">Page1179-c+ 73</a>]<BR>at p. 1175, col. 3), reproach, censure; shame,<BR>bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रित|ह्रितः
ह्रित 1. ह्रित, अस्, आ, अम् (for हृत at<BR>p. 1175), taken, conveyed; taken away, seized;<BR>divided, apportioned; (अम्), n. a portion, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिति|ह्रितिः
ह्रिति, इस्, f. (for हृति), taking, conveying;<BR>seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रित|ह्रितः
ह्रित 2. ह्रित, अस्, आ, अम् (for ह्रीत), ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रियमाण
ह्रियमाण ह्रियमाण. See p. 1175, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिवेर|ह्रिवेरं
ह्रिवेर ह्रिवेर, अम्, n. a kind of drug and<BR>perfume (= बाल, बालक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेर|ह्रीवेरं
ह्रीवेर, अम्, n. = ह्रिवेर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री 1. ह्री (connected with rt. 2. हृ or हॄ,<BR>q. v.), cl. 3. P. जिह्रेति (3rd pl. जिह्रियति),<BR>Perf. जिह्राय or जिह्रयाञ्-चकार, ह्रेष्यति,<BR>अह्रैषीत्, ह्रेतुम्, to blush; to be ashamed, be<BR>modest; to be ashamed of (with abl. or gen., e. g.<BR>अन्योन्यस्य जिह्रीमः, we are ashamed of one an-<BR>other, Kirāt. XI. 58): Caus. ह्रेपयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अजिह्रिपत् (according to some अजिह्रीपत्), to put to<BR>shame, make to blush, confound: Desid. जिह्रीषति:<BR>Intens. जेह्रीयते, जेह्रयीति, जेह्रेति; [cf. probably<BR>Old Germ. hriuwan; Angl. Sax. hreowan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
2. ह्री, ईस्, f. shame, bashfulness, modesty; Modesty,<BR>Shame, (personified as daughter of Dakṣa and wife<BR>of Dharma.)<BR>—ह्री-जित, अस्, आ, अम्, overcome by<BR>shame, modest, ashamed.<BR>—ह्री-निरास, अस्, m.<BR>abandonment of shame, shamelessness.<BR>—ह्री-नि-<BR>षेध, अस्, आ, अम्, having shame as a check,<BR>checked by modesty.<BR>—ह्री-निषेव, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>ह्री-निषेविन्, ई, इणी, इ, practising modesty, modest.<BR>—ह्री-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, bashful, modest, ashamed.<BR>—ह्री-यन्त्रणा, f. the constraint or pain of bash-<BR>fulness, torment of shame.<BR>—ह्री-सन्न-कण्ठ,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, having the throat choked by shame,<BR>i. e. having a feeble or broken utterance through<BR>bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीका
ह्रीका, f. shame, bashfulness, modesty, shyness;<BR>timidity, fear, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीकु|ह्रीकुः
ह्रीकु, उस्, उस्, उ, ashamed, bashful, modest, shy,<BR>timid; (उस्), m. lac; tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीण|ह्रीणः
ह्रीण, अस्, आ, अम्, ashamed, modest, bashful, shy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीत|ह्रीतः
ह्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, ashamed, bashful, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपण|ह्रेपणं
ह्रेपण, अम्, n. the act of putting to shame,<BR>excelling, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपयत्
ह्रेपयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, putting to shame, outvy-<BR>ing, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपित
ह्रेपित, अस्, आ, अम्, made ashamed, put to shame;<BR>excelled, surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीछ्|ह्रीच्छ्
ह्रीछ् ह्रीछ् (connected with rt. 1. ह्री),<BR>cl. 1. P. ह्रीच्छति, जिह्रीच्छ, ह्रीच्छितुम्,<BR>to be ashamed or modest, to blush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेल|ह्रीवेलं
ह्रीवेल ह्रीवेल or ह्रीवेलक, अम्, n. (= ह्री-<BR>वेर, q. v.), a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रु
ह्रु ह्रु (a Vedic form of rt. ह्वृ; cf. वि-<BR>ह्रु, अ-विह्रुत), cl. 9. P. ह्रुणाति, &c., to<BR>hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुत्
ह्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. hurting, injuring; (त्), m. an<BR>enemy; [cf. वि-ह्रुत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुत
ह्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, hurt, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुड्
ह्रुड् ह्रुड् or ह्रूड् (= rts. ह्रौड्, हूड्), cl.<BR>1. P. ह्रोडति, ह्रूडति (according to some<BR>also A. -ते), &c., to go; to be drawn up or con-<BR>tracted; to contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुडु
ह्रुडु or ह्रूडु, उस्, m., Ved. ‘drawing up, con-<BR>tracting, convulsing,’ epithet of Takman, (in Atharva-<BR>veda I. 25, 2, 3. interpreted to mean ‘cramp’ or<BR>‘spasm.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रोड
ह्रोड, अस्, m. contraction; [cf. ज्या-ह्रोड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेप्
ह्रेप् ह्रेप्, cl. 1. A. ह्रेपते, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेष्
ह्रेष् ह्रेष् [cf. rt. हेष्], cl. 1. A. ह्रेषते,<BR>जिह्रेषे, ह्रेषितुम्, to neigh (as a horse),<BR>whinny; to creep, go [cf. rt. 1. प्रेष्]: Caus. ह्रेष-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">Page1180-a+ 43</a>]<BR>यति, &c., to make to neigh, to neigh; [cf. Gr.<BR>χρό-μη, χρεμέθω, χρεμίζω: Old Germ. hros; Mod.<BR>Germ. Ross; Angl. Sax. hors.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषा
ह्रेषा, f. neighing (of a horse), whinnying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषित|ह्रेषितं
ह्रेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, neighed; (अम्), n. neigh-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषुक|ह्रेषुकः
ह्रेषुक ह्रेषुक, अस्, m. (according to some)<BR>an instrument for digging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रौड्
ह्रौड् ह्रौड्, cl. 1. P. ह्रौडति, &c., to go<BR>(= rts. ह्रुड्, हूड्, q.q. v.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लग्
ह्लग् ह्लग् (= rt. ह्रग्, q. v.), cl. 1. P. ह्ल-<BR>गति, &c., to cover, hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लप्
ह्लप् ह्लप् (also written ह्रप्; cf. rt.<BR>क्लप्), cl. 10. P. ह्लापयति, &c., to speak;<BR>to sound, creak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लस्
ह्लस् ह्लस् [cf. rt. ह्रस्], cl. 1. P. ह्लसति,<BR>जह्लास, ह्लसितुम्, to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद्
ह्लाद् ह्लाद् (a later form of rt. ह्राद्, q. v.),<BR>cl. 1. A. ह्लादते, जह्लादे, ह्लादितुम्,<BR>(originally ‘to shout with joy, raise joyful cries’), to<BR>rejoice, be glad, be delighted; to sound (as a musical<BR>instrument): Caus. ह्लादयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अजिह्ल-<BR>दत्, to make glad, gladden, exhilarate, delight; [cf.<BR>Gr. κέχλαδα, καχλάζω, perhaps also γῆθος, γηθέω;<BR>Lat. gaudeo; Old Germ. glat; Angl. Sax. glœd,<BR>glad, gladian; Eng. glad; Hib. gairdim, ‘I re-<BR>joice.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लत्ति|ह्लत्तिः
ह्लत्ति, इस्, f. joy, gladness, happiness; [cf. प्र-<BR>ह्लत्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लन्न
ह्लन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, glad, pleased, delighted,<BR>happy; [cf. प्र-ह्लन्न.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लन्नि
ह्लन्नि, इस्, f. joy, gladness, happiness; [cf. प्र-<BR>ह्लन्नि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद|ह्लादः
ह्लाद, अस्, m. pleasure, joy; N. of a son of<BR>Hiraṇya-kaśipu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादक|ह्लादकः
ह्लादक, अस्, इका, अम्, gladdening, rejoicing;<BR>(इका), f. joy, gladness.<BR>—ह्लादिका-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. possessed of joy, joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादन|ह्लादनं
ह्लादन, अम्, n. the act of rejoicing, joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादित
ह्लादित, अस्, आ, अम्, gladdened, delighted, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादिन्
ह्लादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, delighting, gladdening; happy;<BR>(इनी), f. lightning [cf. ह्रादिनी]; Indra's thunder-<BR>bolt; the olibanum tree; N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्ली
ह्ली ह्ली, another form of rt. 1. ह्री, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीक
ह्लीक, अस्, आ, अम्, bashful, modest; (आ), f. shame,<BR>modesty (= ह्रीका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीकु|ह्लीकुः
ह्लीकु, उस्, उस्, उ (= ह्रीकु), ashamed, modest;<BR>(उस्), m. lac (= जतु); tin; [cf. Gr. χαλ-κό-ς; Slav.<BR>zel-e-zo; Lith. gel-e-zi-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लेष्
ह्लेष् ह्लेष्, another form of rt. ह्रेष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लेषा
ह्लेषा, f. = ह्रेषा, neighing, whinnying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वल्
ह्वल् ह्वल् [cf. rt. ह्वृ], cl. 1. P. ह्वलति,<BR>जह्वाल, &c., to move, shake, tremble;<BR>to go: Caus. ह्वलयति, ह्वालयति (the former<BR>when prepositions are prefixed), to cause to tremble;<BR>[cf. Old Germ. wallôn, ‘to walk about;’ Mod.<BR>Germ. wallen, wall-fahrt.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वलत्
ह्वलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, moving, shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वृ
ह्वृ ह्वृ or ह्वॄ (originally ध्वृ, q. v.;<BR>cf. rts. हुर्छ्, ह्रु), cl. 1. P. ह्वरति, जह्-<BR>वार, ह्वरिष्यति, अह्वार्षीत् (Ved. अह्वार्), ह्वर्-<BR>तुम्, cl. 9. P. ह्वृणाति, &c., to be crooked or curved,<BR>go crookedly; to be crooked in conduct, deceive;<BR>to be injured or afflicted; (according to Naigh. II. 8)<BR>to eat: Caus. ह्वारयति, &c., to make crooked,<BR>bend, curve; to hurt, injure: Desid. जुह्वूर्षति:<BR>Intens. जाह्वर्यते, जाह्वर्ति; [cf. Gr. κυπτός,<BR>κύρβεις, ἐρέφω: Lat. curvus, varus: Goth. hvair-<BR>ban: Angl. Sax. hwearfian, hwerfa, hweorfan,<BR>hwealf, hwealfa: Hib. fiar, ‘crooked;’ fiaraim,<BR>‘I incline, bend;’ fiaras, ‘crookedness.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुत्
ह्रुत्, ह्रुत. See under rt. ह्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वरस्
ह्वरस्, अस्, n., Ved. crookedness, deceit, dis-<BR>honesty, fraud, (Sāy. = कौटिल्य, हिंसन; in<BR>Naigh. II. 13. enumerated among the क्रोध-ना-<BR>मानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वार
ह्वार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. dishonest, malicious, (Sāy.<BR>= कुटिल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वार्य|ह्वार्यः
ह्वार्य, अस्, m., Ved. ‘going crookedly,’ (Sāy.) a<BR>snake or an unbroken horse, (in Naigh. I. 14. enu-<BR>merated among the अश्व-नामानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वृत
ह्वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, curved; injured, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वे
ह्वे ह्वे (in some of its forms identical<BR>with rt. हु at p. 1174, and several derivatives<BR>seem to recognize another rt. हु or हू = ह्वे), cl. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">Page1180-c+ 47</a>]<BR>P. A. ह्वयति, -ते, जुहाव (identical in form with Perf.<BR>of rt. हु), जुहुवे (in Ṛg-veda I. 48, 14. जुहूरे<BR>= जुह्विरे), ह्वास्यति, -ते, अह्वत्, अह्वत or अह्-<BR>वास्त, Prec. हूयात्, ह्वासीष्ट (Vedic forms Pres.<BR>1st sing. हवे or हुवे, 3rd sing. हवते, 1st pl.<BR>हवामहे, ह्वामहे, हूमहे, होम, 3rd pl. ह-<BR>वन्ते; Impf. 3rd pl. हवन्त; Pot. 1st pl. हु-<BR>वेम; Perf. 3rd sing. हुवे, (आ)जुह्वे, 3rd pl.<BR>जुहुरे, जुहूरे; Aor. 1st sing. अह्वे, 3rd pl. अहू-<BR>षत), ह्वातुम् (Ved. Inf. हवीतवे, हुवध्यै),<BR>to call; to call to; to call upon, invoke; to chal-<BR>lenge; to name; to seek, ask, pray, beg; to emu-<BR>late, vie with: Pass. हूयते (identical in form with<BR>Pass. of rt. हु), Aor. अह्वायि, &c., to be called, &c.:<BR>Caus. ह्वाययति, -यितुम्, Aor. अजूहवत्: Desid.<BR>of Caus. जुहावयिषति: Desid. जुहूषति, -ते:<BR>Intens. जोहूयते, जोहवीति, जोहोति (Impf. अजोहवीत्,<BR>3rd pl. अजोहवुः, Pres. part. जोहुवत्), to call on,<BR>invoke; [cf. according to some, Gr. βοή, βοάω, pro-<BR>bably ἀΰω, ἰωή; Lat. re-boare, perhaps voveo, vo-<BR>tum; Goth. vôpjan; Old Germ. hweion, hrôfu,<BR>ruafu; Mod. Germ. Rufe; Angl. Sax. hweop,<BR>wepan; Old Icel. hvîa, ‘to neigh;’ Slav. zv-a-ti,<BR>‘to call;’ Hib. guilim, ‘I bewail.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव|हवः
हव, अस्, अम्, m. n. calling. See 2. हव, p. 1168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाव|हावः
हाव, अस्, m. calling, &c. See p. 1170, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत|हुतं|हुतः
2. हुत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 1174, col. 2),<BR>called, summoned, invited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुति|हुतिः
2. हुति = हूति below; [cf. 2. आ-हुति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुवान
हुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being invoked, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. and Mahī-dhara = आहूयमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूत|हूतं
हूत, अस्, आ, अम्, called, summoned, invited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूति|हूतिः
हूति, इस्, f. calling; invocation; calling defiantly,<BR>challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूत्वा
हूत्वा, ind. having called, having challenged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूय
हूय, in देव-ह्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूयमान
2. हूयमान, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see under rt. हु,<BR>p. 1174), being called or invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वयत्
ह्वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, calling out; challenging,<BR>vying with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वातृ
ह्वातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what calls, a caller,<BR>challenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वान|ह्वानं
ह्वान, अम्, n. the act of calling; a cry, noise;<BR>[cf. कु-ह्वान.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वानीय
ह्वानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be called or invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वायिन्
ह्वायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, calling, invoking, challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वेय
ह्वेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be called; to be invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथम्
अ-कथम्, ind. (fr. 3. अ + 1. कथा), even without<BR>telling, without further words, without any dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुल|अकुलः
अ-कुल; add — (अम्), n. epithet of Śiva (with<BR>Tāntrikas; cf. कुल, p. 1183).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुली
अकुली, f., Ved. a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुहक
अ-कुहक, अस्, आ, अम्, not deceiving, free from<BR>deceit, guileless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्नोपन
अ-क्नोपन, अस्, ई, अम्, not moistening, drying.<BR>See क्नोपन, p. 1183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्र|अक्रः
अक्र; add — अस्, m. (according to B. R., probably)<BR>a standard, banner; a wall, fence (= प्राकार ac-<BR>cording to Durga on Nirukta VI. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
2. अक्ष; add — the collar-bone (Ved.); a mesh<BR>(of a net).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षक|अक्षकः
अक्षक; add — (probably) the collar-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधर|अक्षधरः
अक्ष-धर; for ‘see साखोत’ read — see शा-<BR>खोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षन्
अक्षन्, an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्य|अगस्त्यः
अगस्त्य; correct thus — अस्, m. = अगस्ति; and<BR>add — in Raghu-v. XIII. 36. Agastya is said to be<BR>‘the cleanser of water,’ as on the rising of Canopus<BR>turbid waters become clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्राङ्गुलि|अग्रांगुलि
अग्राङ्गुलि; add — the tip of the toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघासक
अ-घासक, अस्, आ, अम्, without food or provisions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोष|अघोषः
अ-घोष; under अस्, m. add — ‘non-sonance,’ ab-<BR>sence of all sound or soft murmur, hard articulation or<BR>effort as applied to the hard consonants and Visarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्नत्|अघ्नन्त्
अ-घ्नत्; for ‘अन्ती’ read अती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कभाज्|अंकभाज्
अङ्क-भाज्; add — close to one's side; in one's<BR>possession, anything which is close or easy of attain-<BR>ment, close at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग|अंग|अंगं|अङ्गं|अङ्गः
अङ्ग; add — anything inferior or secondary, any-<BR>thing immaterial or unessential; (in grammar) also<BR>in Pāṇini's system a term for the base in the strong<BR>cases only, (see पद, 2. भ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गता
अङ्ग-ता, f. or अङ्ग-त्व, अम्, n. a state of sub-<BR>ordination or dependence, the being of secondary<BR>importance, the being immaterial or unessential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकृ|अंगीकृ
अङ्गी-कृ; add — to take or espouse the side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्
अच्; for ‘carved’ read curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्
अच्, a technical term for all the vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छोद्य
अच्छोद्य (˚छ-उद्˚), ind. having spoken to,<BR>(Pāṇ. I. 4, 69.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
1. अज; for ‘(अस्), m. pl.’ read (आस्), m. pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्त
अज्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ending in a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्मध्यस्थ
अज्-मध्य-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being or occupying<BR>a place between two vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जना|अंजना
अञ्जना; add — a kind of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जि|अंजि|अञ्जिः
अञ्जि; add — an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डदल
अण्ड-दल, अम्, n. an egg-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रान्ति|अतिक्रान्तिः
अति-क्रान्ति, इस्, f. transgression, (Kirāt. XIV. 23.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहित|अतिवाहितः
अति-वाहित; read अति-वापिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविपिन
अति-विपिन; add — very impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वविद्
अथर्व-विद्; for ‘Brāhmaṇas’ read Brahmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण
अ-दक्षिण; add — inexperienced, simple-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिति|अदितिः
3. अ-दिति; add — Aditi was daughter of Dakṣa<BR>and wife of Kaśyapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रेश्य
अ-द्रेश्य = अ-दृश्य, invisible, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःक्रिया
अधः-क्रिया, f. = अप-मान, disgrace, humilia-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरकण्ठ|अधरकण्ठः
अधर-कण्ठ; add — the lower part of the<BR>throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरय
अधरय, Nom. P. अधरयति, &c., to make<BR>inferior, put under; to eclipse, excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिनाथ|अधिनाथः
अधि-नाथ; add — a supreme lord, chieftain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुह्
अधि-रुह्; add — to attack, accuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवास|अधिवासः
3. अधि-वास; add — fumigation of a person or<BR>image with incense, &c.; fragrance, perfume; smell,<BR>odour (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविज्ञान
अधि-विज्ञान, अम्, n. the highest knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्री
अधि-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, having great prosperity, highly<BR>prosperous or fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठेय
अधि-ष्ठेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be superintended or<BR>governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिसेनापति
अधि-सेनापति, इस्, m. ‘over-general,’ a com-<BR>mander-in-chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिहस्ति
अधि-हस्ति, ind. on an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतिन्
अधीतिन्; add — occupied with the study of the<BR>Veda. studying the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीन|अधीनः
अधीन; add — resting on, situated in or on, be-<BR>longing to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोनिलय
अधो-निलय, अस्, m. ‘lower abode,’ the lower<BR>regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्हणीय
अध्य्-अर्हणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured<BR>highly, very honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसिति
अध्य्-अवसिति, इस्, f. exertion, effort, &c. (= अध्य्-<BR>अवसान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावाहनिक|अध्यावाहनिकं
अध्य्-आ-वाहनिक; the proper explanation of this<BR>word is given under स्त्री-धन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढ|अध्यूढः
अध्य्-ऊढ, अस्, m.; add — the son of a woman<BR>pregnant before marriage [cf. 1. सहोढ].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढज
अध्यूढ-ज, अस्, m. = अध्य्-ऊढ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्यु|अध्वर्युः|अध्वर्य्यु|अध्वर्य्युः
अध्वर्यु; add — (उस्), f. the wife of an Adhvaryu<BR>priest, (Pāṇ. IV. 1, 66.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलद
अनल-द, अस्, आ, अम् (see 3. द), destroying or<BR>quenching fire, (said of water, Kirāt. V. 25.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवकाश|अनवकाशः
अन्-अवकाश; add — having no other opportunity<BR>for application, inapplicable, (Pāṇ. I. 4, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवकाशत्वात्
अनवकाशत्वात्, abl. c. from the inapplicability<BR>(of a rule), if the (present) rule does not take effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित
अनित; read — अन्-इत, not gone to, not obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीलवाजिन्
अनीलवाजिन्, ई, m. ‘white-horsed,’ epithet of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलन
अनु-कूलन, अम्, n. kindness towards (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रान्त
अनु-क्रान्त; add — mentioned or written down<BR>in the Anukramaṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगण्डिका
अनु-गण्डिका, f. a line of hills or a little hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगायस्
अनु-गायस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, to be hymned, (Sāy. अनु-<BR>गातव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीता
अनु-गीता, f. an after-song; N. of part of the four-<BR>teenth book of the Mahā-bhārata (chaps. 16 — 92).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुणय
अनु-गुणय, Nom. P. -गुणयति, &c., to favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगोदम्
अनु-गोदम्, ind. near the Godāvarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रहीकृत
अनुग्रही-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made into a favour<BR>or benefit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञातृ
अनु-ज्ञातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who assents, giving<BR>leave or permission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षुल
अनु-तर्षुल, अस्, आ, अम्, causing thirst; causing<BR>a desire or longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतिष्ठासु
अनु-तिष्ठासु, उस्, उस्, उ, intending to do or effect<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर्श
अनु-दर्श, अस्, m. remonstrance, expostulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेहम्
अनु-देहम्; add — behind the body, from behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपक्षित
अन्-उपक्षित; add — unexhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=1181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदेश
